window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES=window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES||{};window.LH_GRADE_BUNDLES[10]={"subjects":{"wiskunde":{"id":"wiskunde","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Wiskunde","en":"Mathematics"},"short":{"af":"Wisk","en":"Maths"},"icon":"📐","color":"#2f6df6","intro":{"af":"Graad 10-Wiskunde lê die fondament vir die NSS: algebra, funksies, trigonometrie, meetkunde, finansies, statistiek en waarskynlikheid. Die Novembereksamen bestaan uit twee vraestelle van 100 punte elk (2 uur elk) en dek die hele jaar se werk. Jy mag 'n goedgekeurde wetenskaplike sakrekenaar gebruik, behalwe waar 'n vraag anders sê.","en":"Grade 10 Mathematics lays the foundation for the NSC: algebra, functions, trigonometry, geometry, finance, statistics and probability. The November exam consists of two papers of 100 marks each (2 hours each) and covers the whole year's work. You may use an approved scientific calculator, except where a question says otherwise."},"examTips":[{"af":"Wys ALTYD jou bewerkings. Die memo gee metodepunte vir elke korrekte stap – 'n antwoord sonder bewerkings kan nul kry, selfs al is dit reg.","en":"ALWAYS show your working. The memo gives method marks for every correct step – an answer without working can score zero, even if it is right."},{"af":"Rond af tot twee desimale plekke, tensy die vraag anders sê, en rond eers aan die einde af – nie in die tussenstappe nie.","en":"Round to two decimal places unless the question says otherwise, and only round at the end – not in the middle steps."},{"af":"Leer die spesiale hoeke (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) en die eksponentwette uit jou kop – daar is gewoonlik 'n vraag sonder sakrekenaar.","en":"Know the special angles (0°, 30°, 45°, 60°, 90°) and the exponent laws by heart – there is usually a question without a calculator."},{"af":"Skryf by meetkunde ALTYD 'n rede langs elke bewering, bv. (teenoorst. sye van ||m) of (midpt-stelling). Sonder 'n rede verloor jy die punt.","en":"In geometry ALWAYS write a reason next to every statement, e.g. (opp. sides of ||m) or (midpt theorem). Without a reason you lose the mark."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte: 'n 1-punt-vraag vra een stap, 'n 5-punt-vraag vra 'n volledige metode. Bestee ongeveer 1 minuut per punt.","en":"Look at the marks: a 1-mark question needs one step, a 5-mark question needs a full method. Spend about 1 minute per mark."},{"af":"Kontroleer jou antwoorde waar jy kan: vervang jou x terug in die vergelyking, of kyk of jou grafiek die regte afsnitte het.","en":"Check your answers where you can: substitute your x back into the equation, or check that your graph has the right intercepts."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: Alles Wiskunde Graad 10 (Afrikaans)","en":"Siyavula: Everything Maths Grade 10 (Afrikaans)"},"url":"https://wcedeportal.co.za/eresource/76196","note":{"af":"Gratis, volledige CAPS-handboek met uitgewerkte voorbeelde en oefeninge vir elke hoofstuk.","en":"Free, complete CAPS textbook with worked examples and exercises for every chapter."}},{"title":{"af":"Noordwes Onderwysdepartement: vraestelle en memo's","en":"North West Department of Education: papers and memos"},"url":"https://education.nwpg.gov.za/?page_id=4644","note":{"af":"Provinsiale Graad 10-Novembervraestelle met memorandums – goed vir eksamenoefening.","en":"Provincial Grade 10 November papers with memos – good for exam practice."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Wiskunde-eksamen: twee vraestelle\n\n**Vraestel 1 en Vraestel 2: 100 punte elk, 2 uur elk** (*skatting volgens CAPS en Hoërskool Brits se 2024-afbakening – bevestig met die 2026-afbakening*). 'n Goedgekeurde wetenskaplike sakrekenaar mag gebruik word.\n\n| Vraestel 1 | ±Punte | Vraestel 2 | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Algebra, eksponente, vergelykings en ongelykhede | 30 | Trigonometrie (ook grafieke en 2D) | 40 |\n| Funksies en grafieke | 30 | Euklidiese meetkunde en meting | 30 |\n| Getalpatrone | 15 | Analitiese meetkunde | 15 |\n| Waarskynlikheid | 15 | Statistiek | 15 |\n| Finansies en groei | 10 | | |\n\n### Wat word gevra?\n\n- Faktoriseer, vereenvoudig en los vergelykings op – altyd met volledige bewerkings.\n- Skets grafieke met afsnitte, asimptote en draaipunte; bepaal vergelykings uit gegewe inligting.\n- Meetkunde: bewerings **met redes** en kort bewyse.\n- Woordprobleme in konteks: rente, huurkoop, hoogtehoeke, volumes.\n\n### Wenke vir hierdie vraestelle\n\n1. Begin met die vrae wat jy ken – maar nommer jou antwoorde presies soos die vraestel.\n2. Teken 'n rowwe skets by elke trigonometrie- en analitiese-meetkundevraag.\n3. Skryf formules eers neer, dan die vervanging, dan die antwoord.\n4. Los geen vraag oop nie: 'n korrekte eerste stap kry dikwels al 'n punt.","en":"## Mathematics exam: two papers\n\n**Paper 1 and Paper 2: 100 marks each, 2 hours each** (*estimate based on CAPS and Hoërskool Brits's 2024 scope – confirm with the 2026 scope*). An approved scientific calculator may be used.\n\n| Paper 1 | ±Marks | Paper 2 | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Algebra, exponents, equations and inequalities | 30 | Trigonometry (incl. graphs and 2D) | 40 |\n| Functions and graphs | 30 | Euclidean geometry and measurement | 30 |\n| Number patterns | 15 | Analytical geometry | 15 |\n| Probability | 15 | Statistics | 15 |\n| Finance and growth | 10 | | |\n\n### What is asked?\n\n- Factorise, simplify and solve equations – always with full working.\n- Sketch graphs with intercepts, asymptotes and turning points; determine equations from given information.\n- Geometry: statements **with reasons** and short proofs.\n- Word problems in context: interest, hire purchase, angles of elevation, volumes.\n\n### Tips for these papers\n\n1. Start with the questions you know – but number your answers exactly as in the paper.\n2. Draw a rough sketch for every trigonometry and analytical geometry question.\n3. Write the formula first, then the substitution, then the answer.\n4. Leave no question blank: a correct first step often already earns a mark."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Algebra, eksponente, patrone en trigonometrie","en":"Algebra, exponents, patterns and trigonometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t1-getalle-uitdrukkings","title":{"af":"Getallestelsel en algebraïese uitdrukkings","en":"Number system and algebraic expressions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal reële getalle kan klassifiseer, repeterende desimale getalle as breuke kan skryf, wortelvorme kan skat en afrond, en algebraïese uitdrukkings kan vermenigvuldig en vereenvoudig.","en":"You will be able to classify real numbers, write recurring decimals as fractions, estimate and round off surds, and multiply and simplify algebraic expressions."},"summary":{"af":"## Die reële getallestelsel\n\n| Simbool | Naam | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| N | Natuurlike getalle | {1; 2; 3; …} |\n| N_{0} | Telgetalle | {0; 1; 2; 3; …} |\n| Z | Heelgetalle | {…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} |\n| Q | Rasionale getalle | [[3/4]]; −5; 0,25; 0,333… |\n| Q′ | Irrasionale getalle | π; √2; ∛5; 1,010010001… |\n| R | Reële getalle | al die rasionale én irrasionale getalle |\n\nElke versameling lê binne die volgende een: N ⊂ N_{0} ⊂ Z ⊂ Q ⊂ R. Q en Q′ saam vorm R.\n\n### Rasionaal of irrasionaal?\n\n'n **Rasionale getal** kan geskryf word as [[a/b]], waar a en b heelgetalle is en b ≠ 0. Dit sluit in:\n\n- alle heelgetalle, bv. −7 = [[−7/1]]\n- **eindigende** desimale getalle, bv. 0,125 = [[1/8]]\n- **repeterende** desimale getalle, bv. 0,272727… = [[3/11]]\n\n'n **Irrasionale getal** kan NIE as [[a/b]] geskryf word nie. Die desimale vorm is **nie-eindigend én nie-repeterend**, bv. π = 3,14159… en √2 = 1,41421…\n\nDie vierkantswortel van 'n negatiewe getal, bv. √(−4), is **nie-reëel**. Let wel: ∛(−8) = −2 is wél reëel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** [[22/7]] is rasionaal – dis net 'n benadering van π. π self is irrasionaal. √9 = 3 en √0,25 = 0,5 is ook rasionaal, want die wortel is presies.\n\n## Repeterende desimale getalle na gewone breuke\n\nHerhalende syfers word met 'n kolletjie of strepie bo-oor aangedui. Metode vir 0,363636… (die 36 herhaal):\n\n1. Stel x gelyk aan die getal: x = 0,363636…\n2. Vermenigvuldig met 10, 100, 1 000 … – een nul vir elke syfer in die herhalende blok: 100x = 36,363636…\n3. Trek af sodat die herhalende deel wegval: 100x − x = 36, dus 99x = 36.\n4. Los op en vereenvoudig: x = [[36/99]] = [[4/11]].\n\nAs net 'n deel herhaal, bv. 0,1666…, maak eers twee vergelykings waarin die herhaling direk ná die komma begin: 10x = 1,666… en 100x = 16,666… Trek af: 90x = 15, dus x = [[15/90]] = [[1/6]].\n\n## Wortelvorme skat\n\n'n **Wortelvorm** soos √30 of ∛20 is irrasionaal as die getal onder die wortelteken nie 'n volkome vierkant (of volkome derdemag) is nie. So skat jy tussen watter twee heelgetalle dit lê:\n\n1. Soek die volkome vierkante net onder en net bo die getal: 25 < 30 < 36.\n2. Neem die wortels: 5 < √30 < 6.\n3. 30 is nader aan 25 as aan 36, dus is √30 nader aan 5 (√30 ≈ 5,48).\n\nVir 'n derdemagswortel gebruik jy derdemagte: 8 < 20 < 27, dus 2 < ∛20 < 3. Ken die volkome vierkante tot 15^{2} = 225 en die derdemagte tot 10^{3} = 1 000.\n\n## Afronding\n\nKyk na die syfer **net ná** die laaste plek wat jy hou: 5 of meer → rond op; 4 of minder → los die syfer soos dit is.\n\n- 3,14159 tot twee desimale plekke: 3,14\n- 2,4651 tot twee desimale plekke: 2,47\n- 7,996 tot twee desimale plekke: 8,00 (skryf die nulle!)\n\n> **Wenk:** Rond slegs aan die **einde** van 'n berekening af, en net een keer – nie in stappe nie. Tensy die vraag anders sê, rond af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n## Produkte van algebraïese uitdrukkings\n\n**Gelyksoortige terme** het presies dieselfde veranderlikes en eksponente, bv. 3x^{2} en −5x^{2}. Net hulle kan bymekaargetel of afgetrek word.\n\n**Binomium × trinomium:** vermenigvuldig elke term in die eerste hakie met elke term in die tweede hakie (2 × 3 = 6 produkte) en versamel dan die gelyksoortige terme:\n\n(x + 2)(x^{2} − 3x + 4) = x^{3} − 3x^{2} + 4x + 2x^{2} − 6x + 8 = x^{3} − x^{2} − 2x + 8\n\n### Spesiale produkte – ken hulle uit jou kop\n\n- (a + b)^{2} = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a + b)(a − b) = a^{2} − b^{2} (verskil van twee vierkante)\n- (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} + b^{3} en (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} − b^{3}\n\n> **Algemene fout:** (x + 3)^{2} ≠ x^{2} + 9. Skryf dit uit as (x + 3)(x + 3) = x^{2} + 6x + 9. Die middelterm 2ab word maklik vergeet.\n\n## Vereenvoudig – stap vir stap\n\n1. Maak die hakies oop (gebruik die spesiale produkte waar jy kan).\n2. 'n Minusteken voor 'n hakie verander die teken van **elke** term binne die hakie: −(x^{2} − 9) = −x^{2} + 9.\n3. Versamel gelyksoortige terme en skryf die antwoord in dalende magte van x.","en":"## The real number system\n\n| Symbol | Name | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| N | Natural numbers | {1; 2; 3; …} |\n| N_{0} | Whole numbers | {0; 1; 2; 3; …} |\n| Z | Integers | {…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} |\n| Q | Rational numbers | [[3/4]]; −5; 0.25; 0.333… |\n| Q′ | Irrational numbers | π; √2; ∛5; 1.010010001… |\n| R | Real numbers | all the rational and irrational numbers |\n\nEach set lies inside the next one: N ⊂ N_{0} ⊂ Z ⊂ Q ⊂ R. Q and Q′ together make up R.\n\n### Rational or irrational?\n\nA **rational number** can be written as [[a/b]], where a and b are integers and b ≠ 0. This includes:\n\n- all integers, e.g. −7 = [[−7/1]]\n- **terminating** decimals, e.g. 0.125 = [[1/8]]\n- **recurring** decimals, e.g. 0.272727… = [[3/11]]\n\nAn **irrational number** can NOT be written as [[a/b]]. Its decimal form is **non-terminating and non-recurring**, e.g. π = 3.14159… and √2 = 1.41421…\n\nThe square root of a negative number, e.g. √(−4), is **non-real**. Note: ∛(−8) = −2 IS real.\n\n> **Common mistake:** [[22/7]] is rational – it is only an approximation of π. π itself is irrational. √9 = 3 and √0.25 = 0.5 are also rational, because the root is exact.\n\n## Recurring decimals to common fractions\n\nRecurring digits are shown with a dot or a bar above them. Method for 0.363636… (the 36 repeats):\n\n1. Let x equal the number: x = 0.363636…\n2. Multiply by 10, 100, 1 000 … – one zero for every digit in the repeating block: 100x = 36.363636…\n3. Subtract so that the repeating part falls away: 100x − x = 36, so 99x = 36.\n4. Solve and simplify: x = [[36/99]] = [[4/11]].\n\nIf only part of the decimal repeats, e.g. 0.1666…, first make two equations in which the repetition starts directly after the decimal point: 10x = 1.666… and 100x = 16.666… Subtract: 90x = 15, so x = [[15/90]] = [[1/6]].\n\n## Estimating surds\n\nA **surd** such as √30 or ∛20 is irrational if the number under the root sign is not a perfect square (or perfect cube). To estimate between which two integers it lies:\n\n1. Find the perfect squares just below and just above the number: 25 < 30 < 36.\n2. Take the roots: 5 < √30 < 6.\n3. 30 is closer to 25 than to 36, so √30 is closer to 5 (√30 ≈ 5.48).\n\nFor a cube root, use cubes: 8 < 20 < 27, so 2 < ∛20 < 3. Know the perfect squares up to 15^{2} = 225 and the cubes up to 10^{3} = 1 000.\n\n## Rounding off\n\nLook at the digit **just after** the last place you are keeping: 5 or more → round up; 4 or less → leave the digit as it is.\n\n- 3.14159 to two decimal places: 3.14\n- 2.4651 to two decimal places: 2.47\n- 7.996 to two decimal places: 8.00 (write the zeros!)\n\n> **Tip:** Round off only at the **end** of a calculation, and only once – not in steps. Unless the question says otherwise, round off to two decimal places.\n\n## Products of algebraic expressions\n\n**Like terms** have exactly the same variables and exponents, e.g. 3x^{2} and −5x^{2}. Only like terms can be added or subtracted.\n\n**Binomial × trinomial:** multiply every term in the first bracket by every term in the second bracket (2 × 3 = 6 products), then collect like terms:\n\n(x + 2)(x^{2} − 3x + 4) = x^{3} − 3x^{2} + 4x + 2x^{2} − 6x + 8 = x^{3} − x^{2} − 2x + 8\n\n### Special products – know them by heart\n\n- (a + b)^{2} = a^{2} + 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}\n- (a + b)(a − b) = a^{2} − b^{2} (difference of two squares)\n- (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} + b^{3} and (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}) = a^{3} − b^{3}\n\n> **Common mistake:** (x + 3)^{2} ≠ x^{2} + 9. Write it out as (x + 3)(x + 3) = x^{2} + 6x + 9. The middle term 2ab is easily forgotten.\n\n## Simplifying – step by step\n\n1. Remove the brackets (use the special products where you can).\n2. A minus sign in front of a bracket changes the sign of **every** term inside the bracket: −(x^{2} − 9) = −x^{2} + 9.\n3. Collect like terms and write the answer in descending powers of x."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Rasionale getal","en":"Rational number"},"def":{"af":"'n Getal wat as a/b geskryf kan word, met a en b heelgetalle en b ≠ 0. Heelgetalle, eindigende en repeterende desimale getalle is almal rasionaal.","en":"A number that can be written as a/b, with a and b integers and b ≠ 0. Integers, terminating and recurring decimals are all rational."}},{"term":{"af":"Irrasionale getal","en":"Irrational number"},"def":{"af":"'n Getal wat nie as a/b geskryf kan word nie; die desimale vorm is nie-eindigend en nie-repeterend, bv. π en √2.","en":"A number that cannot be written as a/b; its decimal form is non-terminating and non-recurring, e.g. π and √2."}},{"term":{"af":"Reële getalle (R)","en":"Real numbers (R)"},"def":{"af":"Al die rasionale en irrasionale getalle saam. Die vierkantswortel van 'n negatiewe getal is nie-reëel.","en":"All the rational and irrational numbers together. The square root of a negative number is non-real."}},{"term":{"af":"Repeterende desimale getal","en":"Recurring decimal"},"def":{"af":"'n Desimale getal waarin een of meer syfers eindeloos herhaal, bv. 0,272727…; dit is altyd rasionaal.","en":"A decimal in which one or more digits repeat endlessly, e.g. 0.272727…; it is always rational."}},{"term":{"af":"Wortelvorm","en":"Surd"},"def":{"af":"'n Wortel wat nie presies uitgewerk kan word nie, bv. √5 of ∛10. Dit is irrasionaal.","en":"A root that cannot be worked out exactly, e.g. √5 or ∛10. It is irrational."}},{"term":{"af":"Afronding","en":"Rounding off"},"def":{"af":"Om 'n getal tot 'n sekere aantal desimale plekke te benader: as die volgende syfer 5 of meer is, rond op; 4 of minder, los dit.","en":"Approximating a number to a certain number of decimal places: if the next digit is 5 or more, round up; 4 or less, leave it."}},{"term":{"af":"Binomium en trinomium","en":"Binomial and trinomial"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking met twee terme (tweeterm, bv. x + 3) en een met drie terme (drieterm, bv. x² − 2x + 5).","en":"An expression with two terms (e.g. x + 3) and one with three terms (e.g. x² − 2x + 5)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gelyksoortige terme","en":"Like terms"},"def":{"af":"Terme met presies dieselfde veranderlikes en eksponente, bv. 4x² en −7x². Net hulle kan bymekaargetel of afgetrek word.","en":"Terms with exactly the same variables and exponents, e.g. 4x² and −7x². Only they can be added or subtracted."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesiale produk","en":"Special product"},"def":{"af":"'n Produk met 'n vaste patroon, bv. (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b² en (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b².","en":"A product with a fixed pattern, e.g. (a + b)² = a² + 2ab + b² and (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b²."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Repeterende desimale getal na 'n breuk","en":"Recurring decimal to a fraction"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 0,1555… (net die 5 herhaal) as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm.","en":"Write 0.1555… (only the 5 repeats) as a common fraction in its simplest form."},"steps":[{"af":"Stel x = 0,1555… Die herhalende syfer (5) begin eers by die tweede desimale plek.","en":"Let x = 0.1555… The repeating digit (5) only starts at the second decimal place."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 10 sodat die herhaling direk ná die komma begin: 10x = 1,555…","en":"Multiply by 10 so that the repetition starts directly after the decimal point: 10x = 1.555…"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 100: 100x = 15,555…","en":"Multiply by 100: 100x = 15.555…"},{"af":"Trek af: 100x − 10x = 15,555… − 1,555…, dus 90x = 14","en":"Subtract: 100x − 10x = 15.555… − 1.555…, so 90x = 14"},{"af":"x = [[14/90]] = [[7/45]] (deel teller en noemer deur 2)","en":"x = [[14/90]] = [[7/45]] (divide numerator and denominator by 2)"}],"answer":{"af":"0,1555… = 7/45","en":"0.1555… = 7/45"}},{"title":{"af":"Skat en rond 'n wortelvorm af","en":"Estimate and round off a surd"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Tussen watter twee opeenvolgende heelgetalle lê √52? (b) Is √52 nader aan die kleiner of die groter heelgetal? (c) Gebruik jou sakrekenaar en rond √52 af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"(a) Between which two consecutive integers does √52 lie? (b) Is √52 closer to the smaller or the larger integer? (c) Use your calculator and round √52 off to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Volkome vierkante naby 52: 7^{2} = 49 en 8^{2} = 64, dus 49 < 52 < 64.","en":"Perfect squares near 52: 7^{2} = 49 and 8^{2} = 64, so 49 < 52 < 64."},{"af":"Neem die vierkantswortel van elke deel: √49 < √52 < √64, dus 7 < √52 < 8.","en":"Take the square root of each part: √49 < √52 < √64, so 7 < √52 < 8."},{"af":"52 − 49 = 3 en 64 − 52 = 12. Omdat 52 baie nader aan 49 is, is √52 nader aan 7.","en":"52 − 49 = 3 and 64 − 52 = 12. Because 52 is much closer to 49, √52 is closer to 7."},{"af":"Sakrekenaar: √52 = 7,2111… Die derde desimale syfer is 1 (minder as 5), dus √52 ≈ 7,21.","en":"Calculator: √52 = 7.2111… The third decimal digit is 1 (less than 5), so √52 ≈ 7.21."}],"answer":{"af":"7 < √52 < 8; nader aan 7; √52 ≈ 7,21","en":"7 < √52 < 8; closer to 7; √52 ≈ 7.21"}},{"title":{"af":"Binomium maal trinomium","en":"Binomial times trinomial"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 3)(x² + 4x − 5)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 3)(x² + 4x − 5)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vermenigvuldig 2x met elke term in die tweede hakie: 2x(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x","en":"Multiply 2x by every term in the second bracket: 2x(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig −3 met elke term (pas op vir die tekens): −3(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = −3x^{2} − 12x + 15","en":"Multiply −3 by every term (watch the signs): −3(x^{2} + 4x − 5) = −3x^{2} − 12x + 15"},{"af":"Skryf al ses produkte saam: 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x − 3x^{2} − 12x + 15","en":"Write all six products together: 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} − 10x − 3x^{2} − 12x + 15"},{"af":"Versamel gelyksoortige terme: 8x^{2} − 3x^{2} = 5x^{2} en −10x − 12x = −22x, dus 2x^{3} + 5x^{2} − 22x + 15","en":"Collect like terms: 8x^{2} − 3x^{2} = 5x^{2} and −10x − 12x = −22x, so 2x^{3} + 5x^{2} − 22x + 15"}],"answer":{"af":"2x³ + 5x² − 22x + 15","en":"2x³ + 5x² − 22x + 15"}},{"title":{"af":"Vereenvoudig met spesiale produkte","en":"Simplify using special products"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 5)² − (x + 4)(x − 4)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 5)² − (x + 4)(x − 4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}: (2x − 5)^{2} = (2x)^{2} − 2(2x)(5) + 5^{2} = 4x^{2} − 20x + 25","en":"Use (a − b)^{2} = a^{2} − 2ab + b^{2}: (2x − 5)^{2} = (2x)^{2} − 2(2x)(5) + 5^{2} = 4x^{2} − 20x + 25"},{"af":"Verskil van twee vierkante: (x + 4)(x − 4) = x^{2} − 16","en":"Difference of two squares: (x + 4)(x − 4) = x^{2} − 16"},{"af":"Hou die tweede produk in hakies: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − (x^{2} − 16)","en":"Keep the second product in brackets: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − (x^{2} − 16)"},{"af":"Die minus voor die hakie verander albei tekens: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − x^{2} + 16","en":"The minus in front of the bracket changes both signs: 4x^{2} − 20x + 25 − x^{2} + 16"},{"af":"Versamel gelyksoortige terme: 3x^{2} − 20x + 41","en":"Collect like terms: 3x^{2} − 20x + 41"}],"answer":{"af":"3x² − 20x + 41","en":"3x² − 20x + 41"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende getalle is irrasionaal?","en":"Which of the following numbers is irrational?"},"options":[{"af":"22/7","en":"22/7"},{"af":"√16","en":"√16"},{"af":"π","en":"π"},{"af":"0,333…","en":"0.333…"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"π = 3,14159… is nie-eindigend en nie-repeterend, dus irrasionaal. 22/7 is 'n breuk (net 'n benadering van π), √16 = 4 en 0,333… = 1/3 – al drie is rasionaal.","en":"π = 3.14159… is non-terminating and non-recurring, so it is irrational. 22/7 is a fraction (only an approximation of π), √16 = 4 and 0.333… = 1/3 – all three are rational."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Elke heelgetal is ook 'n rasionale getal.","en":"Every integer is also a rational number."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Enige heelgetal kan as 'n breuk met noemer 1 geskryf word, bv. −5 = −5/1. Daarom lê Z binne Q.","en":"True. Any integer can be written as a fraction with denominator 1, e.g. −5 = −5/1. That is why Z lies inside Q."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke simbool by die regte getalleversameling.","en":"Match each symbol to the correct set of numbers."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"N","en":"N"},"r":{"af":"{1; 2; 3; …} – natuurlike getalle","en":"{1; 2; 3; …} – natural numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"N₀","en":"N₀"},"r":{"af":"{0; 1; 2; 3; …} – telgetalle","en":"{0; 1; 2; 3; …} – whole numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"Z","en":"Z"},"r":{"af":"{…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} – heelgetalle","en":"{…; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; …} – integers"}},{"l":{"af":"Q′","en":"Q′"},"r":{"af":"Getalle wat nie as a/b geskryf kan word nie – irrasionale getalle","en":"Numbers that cannot be written as a/b – irrational numbers"}},{"l":{"af":"R","en":"R"},"r":{"af":"Al die rasionale en irrasionale getalle – reële getalle","en":"All the rational and irrational numbers – real numbers"}}],"explain":{"af":"N begin by 1, N₀ sluit 0 in, Z sluit die negatiewe heelgetalle in, Q′ is die irrasionale getalle en R is alles saam.","en":"N starts at 1, N₀ includes 0, Z includes the negative integers, Q′ is the irrational numbers and R is everything together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is NIE 'n reële getal nie?","en":"Which of the following is NOT a real number?"},"options":[{"af":"−√9","en":"−√9"},{"af":"∛(−8)","en":"∛(−8)"},{"af":"0","en":"0"},{"af":"√(−9)","en":"√(−9)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"√(−9) is nie-reëel: geen reële getal maal homself gee −9 nie. −√9 = −3, ∛(−8) = −2 (want (−2)³ = −8) en 0 is almal reëel.","en":"√(−9) is non-real: no real number times itself gives −9. −√9 = −3, ∛(−8) = −2 (because (−2)³ = −8) and 0 are all real."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Rond 7,2849 af tot twee desimale plekke: ___","en":"Round 7.2849 off to two decimal places: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7,28","7.28"],"en":["7.28","7,28"]},"explain":{"af":"Kyk net na die derde desimale syfer: 4 is minder as 5, dus bly die 8 soos dit is: 7,28. Moenie in stappe afrond nie (7,2849 → 7,285 → 7,29 is verkeerd).","en":"Look only at the third decimal digit: 4 is less than 5, so the 8 stays as it is: 7.28. Do not round in steps (7.2849 → 7.285 → 7.29 is wrong)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7,29","7,285","7,3"],"en":["7.29","7.285","7.3"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tussen watter twee opeenvolgende heelgetalle lê √40?","en":"Between which two consecutive integers does √40 lie?"},"options":[{"af":"20 en 21","en":"20 and 21"},{"af":"6 en 7","en":"6 and 7"},{"af":"4 en 5","en":"4 and 5"},{"af":"36 en 49","en":"36 and 49"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"36 < 40 < 49, dus √36 < √40 < √49, m.a.w. 6 < √40 < 7 (√40 ≈ 6,32). 20 en 21 kom van halveer, nie van 'n wortel nie; 36 en 49 is die vierkante, nie die wortels nie.","en":"36 < 40 < 49, so √36 < √40 < √49, i.e. 6 < √40 < 7 (√40 ≈ 6.32). 20 and 21 come from halving, not from a root; 36 and 49 are the squares, not the roots."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf 0,777… as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm: ___","en":"Write 0.777… as a common fraction in its simplest form: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7/9"],"en":["7/9"]},"explain":{"af":"x = 0,777…; 10x = 7,777…; 10x − x = 7, dus 9x = 7 en x = 7/9.","en":"x = 0.777…; 10x = 7.777…; 10x − x = 7, so 9x = 7 and x = 7/9."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7/10","77/100","7/99"],"en":["7/10","77/100","7/99"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Brei uit: (x − 4)²","en":"Expand: (x − 4)²"},"options":[{"af":"x² − 8x + 16","en":"x² − 8x + 16"},{"af":"x² − 16","en":"x² − 16"},{"af":"x² + 16","en":"x² + 16"},{"af":"x² − 8x − 16","en":"x² − 8x − 16"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b²: x² − 2(x)(4) + 4² = x² − 8x + 16. x² − 16 vergeet die middelterm, en die laaste term is (−4)² = +16, nie −16 nie.","en":"(a − b)² = a² − 2ab + b²: x² − 2(x)(4) + 4² = x² − 8x + 16. x² − 16 forgets the middle term, and the last term is (−4)² = +16, not −16."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"(3x − 2)² = 9x² − 4","en":"(3x − 2)² = 9x² − 4"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. (3x − 2)² = 9x² − 12x + 4. Die middelterm −2(3x)(2) = −12x ontbreek, en (−2)² = +4, nie −4 nie.","en":"False. (3x − 2)² = 9x² − 12x + 4. The middle term −2(3x)(2) = −12x is missing, and (−2)² = +4, not −4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (x − 3)(x² + 2x − 1)","en":"Simplify: (x − 3)(x² + 2x − 1)"},"options":[{"af":"x³ + 3","en":"x³ + 3"},{"af":"x³ − x² − 7x − 3","en":"x³ − x² − 7x − 3"},{"af":"x³ + 5x² + 5x + 3","en":"x³ + 5x² + 5x + 3"},{"af":"x³ − x² − 7x + 3","en":"x³ − x² − 7x + 3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"x(x² + 2x − 1) − 3(x² + 2x − 1) = x³ + 2x² − x − 3x² − 6x + 3 = x³ − x² − 7x + 3. Vermenigvuldig elke term met elke term (nie net die eerste en laaste nie), en onthou (−3)(−1) = +3.","en":"x(x² + 2x − 1) − 3(x² + 2x − 1) = x³ + 2x² − x − 3x² − 6x + 3 = x³ − x² − 7x + 3. Multiply every term by every term (not just the first and last), and remember (−3)(−1) = +3."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf 0,4666… (net die 6 herhaal) as 'n gewone breuk in sy eenvoudigste vorm: ___","en":"Write 0.4666… (only the 6 repeats) as a common fraction in its simplest form: ___"},"answers":{"af":["7/15"],"en":["7/15"]},"explain":{"af":"x = 0,4666…; 10x = 4,666…; 100x = 46,666… Trek af: 100x − 10x = 42, dus 90x = 42 en x = 42/90 = 7/15.","en":"x = 0.4666…; 10x = 4.666…; 100x = 46.666… Subtract: 100x − 10x = 42, so 90x = 42 and x = 42/90 = 7/15."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["46/99","23/50","14/33"],"en":["46/99","23/50","14/33"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2x − 1)² − (x + 3)(x − 3)","en":"Simplify: (2x − 1)² − (x + 3)(x − 3)"},"options":[{"af":"3x² − 4x + 10","en":"3x² − 4x + 10"},{"af":"3x² − 4x − 8","en":"3x² − 4x − 8"},{"af":"3x² − 2x + 10","en":"3x² − 2x + 10"},{"af":"3x² + 10","en":"3x² + 10"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(2x − 1)² = 4x² − 4x + 1 en (x + 3)(x − 3) = x² − 9. Dan 4x² − 4x + 1 − (x² − 9) = 4x² − 4x + 1 − x² + 9 = 3x² − 4x + 10. Die minus voor die hakie maak −9 → +9.","en":"(2x − 1)² = 4x² − 4x + 1 and (x + 3)(x − 3) = x² − 9. Then 4x² − 4x + 1 − (x² − 9) = 4x² − 4x + 1 − x² + 9 = 3x² − 4x + 10. The minus in front of the bracket turns −9 into +9."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As x + 1/x = 5, wat is die waarde van x² + 1/x²? ___","en":"If x + 1/x = 5, what is the value of x² + 1/x²? ___"},"answers":{"af":["23"],"en":["23"]},"explain":{"af":"Kwadreer albei kante: (x + 1/x)² = x² + 2(x)(1/x) + 1/x² = x² + 2 + 1/x². Dus x² + 2 + 1/x² = 25 en x² + 1/x² = 23. (Die middelterm 2ab = 2 is die sleutel.)","en":"Square both sides: (x + 1/x)² = x² + 2(x)(1/x) + 1/x² = x² + 2 + 1/x². So x² + 2 + 1/x² = 25 and x² + 1/x² = 23. (The middle term 2ab = 2 is the key.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["25","27","24"],"en":["25","27","24"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vierkantige stoep by 'n huis in Hartbeespoort het sye van (2x + 3) m. In die middel word 'n vierkantige blombedding met sye van x m uitgesny. Watter uitdrukking gee die oppervlakte van die stoep wat oorbly, in m²?","en":"A square patio at a house in Hartbeespoort has sides of (2x + 3) m. A square flower bed with sides of x m is cut out in the middle. Which expression gives the area of the patio that remains, in m²?"},"options":[{"af":"3x² + 9","en":"3x² + 9"},{"af":"3x² + 6x + 9","en":"3x² + 6x + 9"},{"af":"3x² + 12x + 9","en":"3x² + 12x + 9"},{"af":"x² + 12x + 9","en":"x² + 12x + 9"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Oorblywende oppervlakte = (2x + 3)² − x² = 4x² + 12x + 9 − x² = 3x² + 12x + 9. 3x² + 9 vergeet die middelterm, 3x² + 6x + 9 vergeet om die middelterm te verdubbel, en x² + 12x + 9 skryf (2x)² verkeerd as 2x².","en":"Remaining area = (2x + 3)² − x² = 4x² + 12x + 9 − x² = 3x² + 12x + 9. 3x² + 9 forgets the middle term, 3x² + 6x + 9 forgets to double the middle term, and x² + 12x + 9 wrongly writes (2x)² as 2x²."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-faktorisering","title":{"af":"Faktorisering en algebraïese breuke","en":"Factorisation and algebraic fractions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal enige Graad 10-uitdrukking volledig kan faktoriseer en algebraïese breuke kan vereenvoudig, vermenigvuldig, deel, optel en aftrek – met die regte beperkings.","en":"You will be able to factorise any Grade 10 expression fully and simplify, multiply, divide, add and subtract algebraic fractions – with the correct restrictions."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is faktorisering?\n\nFaktorisering is die omgekeerde van uitbrei: jy skryf 'n uitdrukking as 'n **produk** van faktore. \"Faktoriseer volledig\" beteken dat geen faktor verder gefaktoriseer kan word nie. Kontroleer altyd jou antwoord deur die faktore terug te vermenigvuldig.\n\n### Kontrolelys – werk in hierdie volgorde\n\n1. Haal die **gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF)** uit – altyd eerste!\n2. Tel die terme. **Twee terme:** verskil van twee vierkante, of som/verskil van twee derdemagte. **Drie terme:** drieterm. **Vier terme:** groepering in pare.\n3. Kyk of enige faktor **verder** gefaktoriseer kan word.\n\n## 1. Gemeenskaplike faktor\n\n- 6x^{2}y − 9xy^{2} = 3xy(2x − 3y)\n- **Negatiewe faktor:** −4x − 8 = −4(x + 2). Al die tekens binne die hakie verander.\n- **Binomiese faktor:** a(x − 2) + 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(a + 3)\n- **Omruil van tekens:** 3 − x = −(x − 3), dus 5(x − 3) − y(3 − x) = 5(x − 3) + y(x − 3) = (x − 3)(5 + y)\n\n## 2. Verskil van twee vierkante\n\na^{2} − b^{2} = (a − b)(a + b)\n\n- 9x^{2} − 25 = (3x − 5)(3x + 5)\n- 2x^{2} − 18 = 2(x^{2} − 9) = 2(x − 3)(x + 3)\n- x^{4} − 16 = (x^{2} − 4)(x^{2} + 4) = (x − 2)(x + 2)(x^{2} + 4)\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n **Som** van twee vierkante, soos x^{2} + 9, kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.\n\n## 3. Drieterme ax^{2} + bx + c\n\n**As a = 1:** soek twee getalle met **produk c** en **som b**. Bv. x^{2} − x − 12: produk −12 en som −1 gee −4 en 3, dus (x − 4)(x + 3).\n\n- c positief → albei getalle het dieselfde teken as b.\n- c negatief → die getalle het verskillende tekens; die groter een kry die teken van b.\n\n**As a ≠ 1 (verdeel die middelterm):**\n\n1. Bereken a × c.\n2. Soek twee getalle met produk ac en som b.\n3. Skryf die middelterm as twee terme en groepeer in pare.\n\nBv. 2x^{2} + 7x + 3: ac = 6, en 6 + 1 = 7. Dus 2x^{2} + 6x + x + 3 = 2x(x + 3) + 1(x + 3) = (x + 3)(2x + 1).\n\n'n **Volkome vierkant** is 'n spesiale drieterm: x^{2} − 10x + 25 = (x − 5)^{2}.\n\n## 4. Groepering in pare (vier terme)\n\nGroepeer twee-twee sodat elke paar 'n gemeenskaplike faktor het, en haal dan die binomiese faktor uit:\n\nax − ay + bx − by = a(x − y) + b(x − y) = (x − y)(a + b)\n\nPas op met 'n minus voor die tweede paar: x^{3} − 2x^{2} − 3x + 6 = x^{2}(x − 2) − 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(x^{2} − 3).\n\n## 5. Som en verskil van twee derdemagte\n\n- a^{3} + b^{3} = (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2})\n- a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2})\n\nTekens: **dieselfde – teenoorgesteld – altyd positief**. Die middelterm van die drieterm is ab (nie 2ab nie), en die drieterm kan nooit verder gefaktoriseer word nie. Ken die derdemagte 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729 en 1 000.\n\nBv. 8x^{3} − 27 = (2x)^{3} − 3^{3} = (2x − 3)(4x^{2} + 6x + 9)\n\n## Algebraïese breuke\n\n**Beperkings:** 'n noemer mag nooit 0 wees nie. Stel elke faktor van elke noemer gelyk aan 0 en sluit daardie waardes uit. By deling geld dit ook vir die teller van die breuk waardeur jy deel, want dit word 'n noemer wanneer jy omkeer.\n\n**Vereenvoudig:** faktoriseer teller en noemer volledig en kanselleer gemeenskaplike **faktore**:\n[[x² − 9/x + 3]] = [[(x − 3)(x + 3)/x + 3]] = x − 3, x ≠ −3\n\n- **Vermenigvuldig:** faktoriseer alles, kanselleer, en vermenigvuldig wat oorbly.\n- **Deel:** vermenigvuldig met die omgekeerde (onderstebo) van die tweede breuk.\n- **Tel op of trek af:** faktoriseer die noemers, kry die KGN (kleinste gemene noemer), skryf elke breuk met die KGN as noemer, kombineer die tellers en vereenvoudig.\n\nOnthou: [[x − 2/2 − x]] = −1, want 2 − x = −(x − 2).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** [[x + 3/3]] ≠ x. Jy mag net **faktore** kanselleer, nooit terme nie. 'n Minus voor 'n breuk geld vir die hele teller – sit die teller in hakies.","en":"## What is factorisation?\n\nFactorisation is the reverse of expanding: you write an expression as a **product** of factors. \"Factorise fully\" means that no factor can be factorised any further. Always check your answer by multiplying the factors back out.\n\n### Checklist – work in this order\n\n1. Take out the **common factor (HCF)** – always first!\n2. Count the terms. **Two terms:** difference of two squares, or sum/difference of two cubes. **Three terms:** trinomial. **Four terms:** grouping in pairs.\n3. Check whether any factor can be factorised **further**.\n\n## 1. Common factor\n\n- 6x^{2}y − 9xy^{2} = 3xy(2x − 3y)\n- **Negative factor:** −4x − 8 = −4(x + 2). All the signs inside the bracket change.\n- **Binomial factor:** a(x − 2) + 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(a + 3)\n- **Swapping signs:** 3 − x = −(x − 3), so 5(x − 3) − y(3 − x) = 5(x − 3) + y(x − 3) = (x − 3)(5 + y)\n\n## 2. Difference of two squares\n\na^{2} − b^{2} = (a − b)(a + b)\n\n- 9x^{2} − 25 = (3x − 5)(3x + 5)\n- 2x^{2} − 18 = 2(x^{2} − 9) = 2(x − 3)(x + 3)\n- x^{4} − 16 = (x^{2} − 4)(x^{2} + 4) = (x − 2)(x + 2)(x^{2} + 4)\n\n> **Common mistake:** A **sum** of two squares, such as x^{2} + 9, cannot be factorised.\n\n## 3. Trinomials ax^{2} + bx + c\n\n**If a = 1:** find two numbers with **product c** and **sum b**. E.g. x^{2} − x − 12: product −12 and sum −1 give −4 and 3, so (x − 4)(x + 3).\n\n- c positive → both numbers have the same sign as b.\n- c negative → the numbers have different signs; the bigger one gets the sign of b.\n\n**If a ≠ 1 (split the middle term):**\n\n1. Calculate a × c.\n2. Find two numbers with product ac and sum b.\n3. Write the middle term as two terms and group in pairs.\n\nE.g. 2x^{2} + 7x + 3: ac = 6, and 6 + 1 = 7. So 2x^{2} + 6x + x + 3 = 2x(x + 3) + 1(x + 3) = (x + 3)(2x + 1).\n\nA **perfect square** is a special trinomial: x^{2} − 10x + 25 = (x − 5)^{2}.\n\n## 4. Grouping in pairs (four terms)\n\nGroup two by two so that each pair has a common factor, then take out the binomial factor:\n\nax − ay + bx − by = a(x − y) + b(x − y) = (x − y)(a + b)\n\nWatch out for a minus in front of the second pair: x^{3} − 2x^{2} − 3x + 6 = x^{2}(x − 2) − 3(x − 2) = (x − 2)(x^{2} − 3).\n\n## 5. Sum and difference of two cubes\n\n- a^{3} + b^{3} = (a + b)(a^{2} − ab + b^{2})\n- a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2})\n\nSigns: **same – opposite – always positive**. The middle term of the trinomial is ab (not 2ab), and the trinomial can never be factorised further. Know the cubes 1, 8, 27, 64, 125, 216, 343, 512, 729 and 1 000.\n\nE.g. 8x^{3} − 27 = (2x)^{3} − 3^{3} = (2x − 3)(4x^{2} + 6x + 9)\n\n## Algebraic fractions\n\n**Restrictions:** a denominator may never be 0. Set every factor of every denominator equal to 0 and exclude those values. With division this also applies to the numerator of the fraction you divide by, because it becomes a denominator when you invert.\n\n**Simplify:** factorise numerator and denominator fully and cancel common **factors**:\n[[x² − 9/x + 3]] = [[(x − 3)(x + 3)/x + 3]] = x − 3, x ≠ −3\n\n- **Multiply:** factorise everything, cancel, and multiply what is left.\n- **Divide:** multiply by the reciprocal (upside down) of the second fraction.\n- **Add or subtract:** factorise the denominators, find the LCD (lowest common denominator), write each fraction with the LCD as denominator, combine the numerators and simplify.\n\nRemember: [[x − 2/2 − x]] = −1, because 2 − x = −(x − 2).\n\n> **Common mistake:** [[x + 3/3]] ≠ x. You may only cancel **factors**, never terms. A minus in front of a fraction applies to the whole numerator – put the numerator in brackets."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Faktoriseer","en":"Factorise"},"def":{"af":"Skryf 'n uitdrukking as 'n produk van faktore – die omgekeerde van uitbrei.","en":"Write an expression as a product of factors – the reverse of expanding."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF)","en":"Common factor (HCF)"},"def":{"af":"Die grootste faktor wat in elke term voorkom. Dit word altyd eerste uitgehaal en kan negatief of 'n binomium wees.","en":"The highest factor that appears in every term. It is always taken out first and can be negative or a binomial."}},{"term":{"af":"Verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Difference of two squares"},"def":{"af":"a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b). 'n Som van twee vierkante, a² + b², kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.","en":"a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b). A sum of two squares, a² + b², cannot be factorised."}},{"term":{"af":"Drieterm (trinomium)","en":"Trinomial"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking met drie terme, bv. ax² + bx + c. Soek twee getalle met produk ac en som b.","en":"An expression with three terms, e.g. ax² + bx + c. Find two numbers with product ac and sum b."}},{"term":{"af":"Groepering in pare","en":"Grouping in pairs"},"def":{"af":"Vier terme word twee-twee gegroepeer sodat 'n gemeenskaplike binomiese faktor uitgehaal kan word.","en":"Four terms are grouped two by two so that a common binomial factor can be taken out."}},{"term":{"af":"Som en verskil van twee derdemagte","en":"Sum and difference of two cubes"},"def":{"af":"a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) en a³ − b³ = (a − b)(a² + ab + b²).","en":"a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) and a³ − b³ = (a − b)(a² + ab + b²)."}},{"term":{"af":"Algebraïese breuk","en":"Algebraic fraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Breuk met 'n algebraïese uitdrukking in die teller en/of die noemer, bv. (x + 1)/(x − 3).","en":"A fraction with an algebraic expression in the numerator and/or denominator, e.g. (x + 1)/(x − 3)."}},{"term":{"af":"Beperking","en":"Restriction"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat die veranderlike nie mag aanneem nie, omdat dit 'n noemer gelyk aan 0 maak, bv. x ≠ 3.","en":"A value the variable may not take because it makes a denominator equal to 0, e.g. x ≠ 3."}},{"term":{"af":"KGN","en":"LCD"},"def":{"af":"Die kleinste gemene noemer: die kleinste uitdrukking waarin al die noemers deel. Faktoriseer eers die noemers om dit te kry.","en":"The lowest common denominator: the smallest expression that all the denominators divide into. Factorise the denominators first to find it."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor en verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Common factor and difference of two squares"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 3x³ − 48x","en":"Factorise fully: 3x³ − 48x"},"steps":[{"af":"GGF eerste: 3x is 'n faktor van albei terme, dus 3x^{3} − 48x = 3x(x^{2} − 16)","en":"HCF first: 3x is a factor of both terms, so 3x^{3} − 48x = 3x(x^{2} − 16)"},{"af":"Die hakie x^{2} − 16 = x^{2} − 4^{2} is 'n verskil van twee vierkante.","en":"The bracket x^{2} − 16 = x^{2} − 4^{2} is a difference of two squares."},{"af":"3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x(x − 4)(x + 4)","en":"3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x(x − 4)(x + 4)"},{"af":"Kontroleer: (x − 4)(x + 4) = x^{2} − 16 en 3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x^{3} − 48x ✓","en":"Check: (x − 4)(x + 4) = x^{2} − 16 and 3x(x^{2} − 16) = 3x^{3} − 48x ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"3x(x − 4)(x + 4)","en":"3x(x − 4)(x + 4)"}},{"title":{"af":"Drieterm met a ≠ 1","en":"Trinomial with a ≠ 1"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 6x² − x − 2","en":"Factorise: 6x² − x − 2"},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken a × c = 6 × (−2) = −12","en":"Calculate a × c = 6 × (−2) = −12"},{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk −12 en som −1: −4 en 3","en":"Find two numbers with product −12 and sum −1: −4 and 3"},{"af":"Verdeel die middelterm: 6x^{2} − 4x + 3x − 2","en":"Split the middle term: 6x^{2} − 4x + 3x − 2"},{"af":"Groepeer in pare: 2x(3x − 2) + 1(3x − 2)","en":"Group in pairs: 2x(3x − 2) + 1(3x − 2)"},{"af":"Haal die binomiese faktor uit: (3x − 2)(2x + 1)","en":"Take out the binomial factor: (3x − 2)(2x + 1)"},{"af":"Kontroleer: (3x − 2)(2x + 1) = 6x^{2} + 3x − 4x − 2 = 6x^{2} − x − 2 ✓","en":"Check: (3x − 2)(2x + 1) = 6x^{2} + 3x − 4x − 2 = 6x^{2} − x − 2 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(3x − 2)(2x + 1)","en":"(3x − 2)(2x + 1)"}},{"title":{"af":"Groepering en derdemagte","en":"Grouping and cubes"},"problem":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: (a) x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12 (b) 2y³ − 54","en":"Factorise fully: (a) x³ + 3x² − 4x − 12 (b) 2y³ − 54"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Vier terme, dus groepeer in pare: x^{2}(x + 3) − 4(x + 3)","en":"(a) Four terms, so group in pairs: x^{2}(x + 3) − 4(x + 3)"},{"af":"Haal die binomiese faktor (x + 3) uit: (x + 3)(x^{2} − 4)","en":"Take out the binomial factor (x + 3): (x + 3)(x^{2} − 4)"},{"af":"x^{2} − 4 is 'n verskil van twee vierkante: (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2)","en":"x^{2} − 4 is a difference of two squares: (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2)"},{"af":"(b) GGF eerste: 2y^{3} − 54 = 2(y^{3} − 27)","en":"(b) HCF first: 2y^{3} − 54 = 2(y^{3} − 27)"},{"af":"y^{3} − 27 = y^{3} − 3^{3}. Gebruik a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}): 2(y − 3)(y^{2} + 3y + 9)","en":"y^{3} − 27 = y^{3} − 3^{3}. Use a^{3} − b^{3} = (a − b)(a^{2} + ab + b^{2}): 2(y − 3)(y^{2} + 3y + 9)"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2) (b) 2(y − 3)(y² + 3y + 9)","en":"(a) (x + 3)(x − 2)(x + 2) (b) 2(y − 3)(y² + 3y + 9)"}},{"title":{"af":"Algebraïese breuke aftrek","en":"Subtracting algebraic fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig 3/(x − 2) − 12/(x² − 4) en noem die beperkings.","en":"Simplify 3/(x − 2) − 12/(x² − 4) and state the restrictions."},"steps":[{"af":"Faktoriseer die noemers: [[3/x − 2]] − [[12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]","en":"Factorise the denominators: [[3/x − 2]] − [[12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]"},{"af":"Beperkings: x − 2 ≠ 0 en x + 2 ≠ 0, dus x ≠ 2 en x ≠ −2","en":"Restrictions: x − 2 ≠ 0 and x + 2 ≠ 0, so x ≠ 2 and x ≠ −2"},{"af":"KGN = (x − 2)(x + 2): [[3(x + 2) − 12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]","en":"LCD = (x − 2)(x + 2): [[3(x + 2) − 12/(x − 2)(x + 2)]]"},{"af":"Vereenvoudig die teller: 3x + 6 − 12 = 3x − 6 = 3(x − 2)","en":"Simplify the numerator: 3x + 6 − 12 = 3x − 6 = 3(x − 2)"},{"af":"Kanselleer die gemeenskaplike faktor (x − 2): [[3(x − 2)/(x − 2)(x + 2)]] = [[3/x + 2]]","en":"Cancel the common factor (x − 2): [[3(x − 2)/(x − 2)(x + 2)]] = [[3/x + 2]]"}],"answer":{"af":"3/(x + 2); x ≠ 2 en x ≠ −2","en":"3/(x + 2); x ≠ 2 and x ≠ −2"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is altyd die eerste stap wanneer jy 'n uitdrukking volledig faktoriseer?","en":"What is always the first step when you factorise an expression fully?"},"options":[{"af":"Tel die aantal terme","en":"Count the number of terms"},{"af":"Soek 'n verskil van twee vierkante","en":"Look for a difference of two squares"},{"af":"Maal die hakies uit","en":"Multiply out the brackets"},{"af":"Haal die gemeenskaplike faktor (GGF) uit","en":"Take out the common factor (HCF)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Haal altyd eers die GGF uit – dit maak die res makliker en jy mis nie faktore nie. Daarna tel jy die terme om die volgende metode te kies.","en":"Always take out the HCF first – it makes the rest easier and you won't miss factors. After that you count the terms to choose the next method."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"x² + 25 kan gefaktoriseer word as (x + 5)(x − 5).","en":"x² + 25 can be factorised as (x + 5)(x − 5)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. (x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25. 'n Som van twee vierkante soos x² + 25 kan nie gefaktoriseer word nie.","en":"False. (x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25. A sum of two squares such as x² + 25 cannot be factorised."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke uitdrukking by sy faktorisering.","en":"Match each expression to its factorisation."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"a² − b²","en":"a² − b²"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)(a + b)","en":"(a − b)(a + b)"}},{"l":{"af":"a² − 2ab + b²","en":"a² − 2ab + b²"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)²","en":"(a − b)²"}},{"l":{"af":"a² + 2ab + b²","en":"a² + 2ab + b²"},"r":{"af":"(a + b)²","en":"(a + b)²"}},{"l":{"af":"a³ + b³","en":"a³ + b³"},"r":{"af":"(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)","en":"(a + b)(a² − ab + b²)"}},{"l":{"af":"a³ − b³","en":"a³ − b³"},"r":{"af":"(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)","en":"(a − b)(a² + ab + b²)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ken hierdie vyf patrone uit jou kop. By derdemagte: die binomium het dieselfde teken, die middelterm van die drieterm die teenoorgestelde teken, en die laaste term is altyd positief.","en":"Know these five patterns by heart. For cubes: the binomial has the same sign, the middle term of the trinomial the opposite sign, and the last term is always positive."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 2x² − 18","en":"Factorise fully: 2x² − 18"},"options":[{"af":"2(x − 3)(x + 3)","en":"2(x − 3)(x + 3)"},{"af":"(x − 3)(x + 3)","en":"(x − 3)(x + 3)"},{"af":"2(x − 9)(x + 9)","en":"2(x − 9)(x + 9)"},{"af":"2(x − 3)²","en":"2(x − 3)²"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"GGF eerste: 2(x² − 9). Dan is x² − 9 'n verskil van twee vierkante: 2(x − 3)(x + 3). Moenie die 2 laat val nie, en √9 = 3, nie 9 nie.","en":"HCF first: 2(x² − 9). Then x² − 9 is a difference of two squares: 2(x − 3)(x + 3). Don't drop the 2, and √9 = 3, not 9."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: x² + 5x − 14 = (x + 7)(x − ___)","en":"Complete: x² + 5x − 14 = (x + 7)(x − ___)"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk −14 en som 5: 7 en −2. Kontroleer: (x + 7)(x − 2) = x² − 2x + 7x − 14 = x² + 5x − 14.","en":"Find two numbers with product −14 and sum 5: 7 and −2. Check: (x + 7)(x − 2) = x² − 2x + 7x − 14 = x² + 5x − 14."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7","14","−2"],"en":["7","14","−2"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: x² − 7x + 12","en":"Factorise: x² − 7x + 12"},"options":[{"af":"(x + 3)(x + 4)","en":"(x + 3)(x + 4)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(x − 6)","en":"(x − 2)(x − 6)"},{"af":"(x − 3)(x − 4)","en":"(x − 3)(x − 4)"},{"af":"(x + 3)(x − 4)","en":"(x + 3)(x − 4)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Produk +12 en som −7: −3 en −4. Omdat c positief is, kry albei die teken van b (negatief). (x − 2)(x − 6) gee wel produk 12, maar die som is −8.","en":"Product +12 and sum −7: −3 and −4. Because c is positive, both get the sign of b (negative). (x − 2)(x − 6) does give product 12, but the sum is −8."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vir x ≠ 5 is (x − 5)/(5 − x) = −1.","en":"For x ≠ 5, (x − 5)/(5 − x) = −1."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 5 − x = −(x − 5), dus (x − 5)/(−(x − 5)) = −1.","en":"True. 5 − x = −(x − 5), so (x − 5)/(−(x − 5)) = −1."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 3x² − 5x − 2","en":"Factorise: 3x² − 5x − 2"},"options":[{"af":"(3x − 1)(x + 2)","en":"(3x − 1)(x + 2)"},{"af":"(3x + 1)(x − 2)","en":"(3x + 1)(x − 2)"},{"af":"(3x + 2)(x − 1)","en":"(3x + 2)(x − 1)"},{"af":"(3x − 2)(x + 1)","en":"(3x − 2)(x + 1)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"ac = 3 × (−2) = −6; getalle met produk −6 en som −5: −6 en 1. 3x² − 6x + x − 2 = 3x(x − 2) + 1(x − 2) = (3x + 1)(x − 2). Kontroleer altyd deur uit te maal – (3x − 1)(x + 2) gee +5x.","en":"ac = 3 × (−2) = −6; numbers with product −6 and sum −5: −6 and 1. 3x² − 6x + x − 2 = 3x(x − 2) + 1(x − 2) = (3x + 1)(x − 2). Always check by multiplying out – (3x − 1)(x + 2) gives +5x."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 5(x − 2) − y(2 − x)","en":"Factorise: 5(x − 2) − y(2 − x)"},"options":[{"af":"(x − 2)(5 − y)","en":"(x − 2)(5 − y)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(y − 5)","en":"(x − 2)(y − 5)"},{"af":"5y(x − 2)","en":"5y(x − 2)"},{"af":"(x − 2)(5 + y)","en":"(x − 2)(5 + y)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Skryf 2 − x = −(x − 2): 5(x − 2) − y(−(x − 2)) = 5(x − 2) + y(x − 2) = (x − 2)(5 + y). Minus maal minus word plus – dis waarom (x − 2)(5 − y) verkeerd is.","en":"Write 2 − x = −(x − 2): 5(x − 2) − y(−(x − 2)) = 5(x − 2) + y(x − 2) = (x − 2)(5 + y). Minus times minus becomes plus – that is why (x − 2)(5 − y) is wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi: 27a³ − 8 = (3a − 2)(9a² + ___a + 4)","en":"Complete: 27a³ − 8 = (3a − 2)(9a² + ___a + 4)"},"answers":{"af":["6"],"en":["6"]},"explain":{"af":"27a³ = (3a)³ en 8 = 2³. Die middelterm van die drieterm is (3a)(2) = 6a, met die teenoorgestelde teken van die binomium, dus +6a.","en":"27a³ = (3a)³ and 8 = 2³. The middle term of the trinomial is (3a)(2) = 6a, with the opposite sign to the binomial, so +6a."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−6","12","5"],"en":["−6","12","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Faktoriseer volledig: 8x³ + 27","en":"Factorise fully: 8x³ + 27"},"options":[{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 12x + 9)","en":"(2x + 3)(4x² − 12x + 9)"},{"af":"(2x − 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)","en":"(2x − 3)(4x² + 6x + 9)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"8x³ = (2x)³ en 27 = 3³. a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) gee (2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9). Die middelterm is ab = 6x (nie 2ab = 12x nie) en het 'n negatiewe teken.","en":"8x³ = (2x)³ and 27 = 3³. a³ + b³ = (a + b)(a² − ab + b²) gives (2x + 3)(4x² − 6x + 9). The middle term is ab = 6x (not 2ab = 12x) and has a negative sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig (x ≠ 3): x/(x − 3) + 3/(3 − x) = ___","en":"Simplify (x ≠ 3): x/(x − 3) + 3/(3 − x) = ___"},"answers":{"af":["1"],"en":["1"]},"explain":{"af":"3 − x = −(x − 3), dus 3/(3 − x) = −3/(x − 3). Dan x/(x − 3) − 3/(x − 3) = (x − 3)/(x − 3) = 1.","en":"3 − x = −(x − 3), so 3/(3 − x) = −3/(x − 3). Then x/(x − 3) − 3/(x − 3) = (x − 3)/(x − 3) = 1."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["(x + 3)/(x − 3)","−1","0"],"en":["(x + 3)/(x − 3)","−1","0"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: [(2x² − 8)/(x² + x − 6)] ÷ [(x + 2)/(x + 3)] = ___","en":"Simplify: [(2x² − 8)/(x² + x − 6)] ÷ [(x + 2)/(x + 3)] = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"Faktoriseer: 2x² − 8 = 2(x − 2)(x + 2) en x² + x − 6 = (x + 3)(x − 2). Deel = maal met die omgekeerde: [2(x − 2)(x + 2)]/[(x + 3)(x − 2)] × (x + 3)/(x + 2). Alles kanselleer behalwe 2 (x ≠ −3; 2; −2).","en":"Factorise: 2x² − 8 = 2(x − 2)(x + 2) and x² + x − 6 = (x + 3)(x − 2). Divide = multiply by the reciprocal: [2(x − 2)(x + 2)]/[(x + 3)(x − 2)] × (x + 3)/(x + 2). Everything cancels except 2 (x ≠ −3; 2; −2)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1/2","−2","2/(x + 3)"],"en":["1/2","−2","2/(x + 3)"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is [(x + 1)/(x − 3)] ÷ [(x + 5)/(x − 2)] ongedefinieerd?","en":"For which values of x is [(x + 1)/(x − 3)] ÷ [(x + 5)/(x − 2)] undefined?"},"options":[{"af":"x = 3 en x = 2","en":"x = 3 and x = 2"},{"af":"x = −1, x = 3, x = −5 en x = 2","en":"x = −1, x = 3, x = −5 and x = 2"},{"af":"x = 3, x = 2 en x = −5","en":"x = 3, x = 2 and x = −5"},{"af":"x = −3 en x = −2","en":"x = −3 and x = −2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die noemers x − 3 en x − 2 mag nie 0 wees nie: x ≠ 3 en x ≠ 2. By deling keer jy (x + 5)/(x − 2) om na (x − 2)/(x + 5), dus is x + 5 ook 'n noemer: x ≠ −5. Die teller x + 1 = 0 gee net 'n antwoord van 0, wat wel gedefinieer is.","en":"The denominators x − 3 and x − 2 may not be 0: x ≠ 3 and x ≠ 2. With division you invert (x + 5)/(x − 2) to (x − 2)/(x + 5), so x + 5 is also a denominator: x ≠ −5. The numerator x + 1 = 0 only gives an answer of 0, which is defined."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-eksponente","title":{"af":"Eksponente","en":"Exponents"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eksponentwette (ook nul- en negatiewe eksponente) kan toepas, uitdrukkings met die priemfaktor-metode kan vereenvoudig en eenvoudige eksponensiële vergelykings kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to apply the laws of exponents (including zero and negative exponents), simplify expressions with the prime factor method and solve simple exponential equations."},"summary":{"af":"## Basiese begrippe\n\nIn a^{n} is a die **grondtal** en n die **eksponent**: a^{n} = a × a × … × a (n faktore). Bv. 2^{5} = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32. In Graad 10 is die eksponente heelgetalle: positief, nul of negatief.\n\n## Die eksponentwette\n\nVir a, b ≠ 0 en m, n heelgetalle:\n\n| Wet | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| a^{m} × a^{n} = a^{m+n} | 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7} |\n| a^{m} ÷ a^{n} = a^{m−n} | x^{9} ÷ x^{4} = x^{5} |\n| (a^{m})^{n} = a^{mn} | (x^{3})^{4} = x^{12} |\n| (ab)^{n} = a^{n}b^{n} | (3x)^{2} = 9x^{2} |\n| ([[a/b]])^{n} = [[aⁿ/bⁿ]] | ([[2/3]])^{3} = [[8/27]] |\n| a^{0} = 1 | 7^{0} = 1 |\n| a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]] | 2^{−3} = [[1/8]] |\n\n**Negatiewe eksponent:** a^{−n} beteken \"een gedeel deur a^{n}\" – dit maak die getal **nie** negatief nie. Om 'n negatiewe eksponent positief te maak, skuif jy die faktor oor die breukstreep: [[1/a⁻ⁿ]] = a^{n}, [[x⁻²/y⁻³]] = [[y³/x²]] en ([[a/b]])^{−n} = ([[b/a]])^{n}.\n\n### Hoekom is a^{0} = 1 en a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]]?\n\nVolgens die deelwet is a^{3} ÷ a^{3} = a^{3−3} = a^{0}. Maar enige getal (behalwe 0) gedeel deur homself is 1, dus a^{0} = 1. Net so is a^{2} ÷ a^{5} = a^{2−5} = a^{−3}. As jy dit uitskryf, kanselleer twee a's en bly daar drie a's onder die breukstreep oor: [[1/a³]]. Daarom is a^{−3} = [[1/a³]].\n\n### Stappe om te vereenvoudig\n\n1. Verwyder hakies met die mag-van-'n-produk-wet.\n2. Skryf verskillende grondtalle as priemfaktore.\n3. Versamel magte van dieselfde grondtal: tel die eksponente op by ×, trek af by ÷.\n4. Skryf die finale antwoord met positiewe eksponente.\n\n### Algemene foute\n\n- 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7}, **nie** 4^{7} nie – die grondtal bly dieselfde.\n- 3x^{0} = 3 × 1 = 3, maar (3x)^{0} = 1.\n- −3^{2} = −9, maar (−3)^{2} = 9.\n- Die wette werk net vir **produkte en kwosiënte**, nie vir somme nie: 2^{3} + 2^{4} ≠ 2^{7}, en (a + b)^{2} ≠ a^{2} + b^{2}.\n- 5^{x} + 5^{x} = 2 × 5^{x} (nie 10^{x} of 5^{2x} nie).\n\n## Die priemfaktor-metode\n\nAs die grondtalle verskil, skryf elke grondtal as 'n produk van **priemfaktore** en pas dan die wette op elke priemgetal apart toe.\n\n- 4 = 2^{2}; 8 = 2^{3}; 9 = 3^{2}; 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 27 = 3^{3}; 36 = 2^{2} × 3^{2}\n- 6^{x} = (2 × 3)^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{x}\n- 9^{x+1} = (3^{2})^{x+1} = 3^{2x+2} – vermenigvuldig die **hele** eksponent met 2.\n\nBv. (6^{x} × 4^{x+1}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = (2^{x} × 3^{x} × 2^{2x+2}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = 2^{3x+2−3x} × 3^{x−x} = 2^{2} = 4\n\n## Uitdrukkings met + of −\n\nAs 'n teller of noemer uit terme bestaan, mag jy nie die wette direk gebruik nie. Haal eers 'n gemeenskaplike faktor uit – gewoonlik die mag met die **kleinste** eksponent. Onthou dat 2^{x+2} = 2^{x} × 2^{2}:\n\n(2^{x+2} − 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 2^{x}(2^{2} − 1) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = (3 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 1\n\n## Eksponensiële vergelykings\n\nIn 'n **eksponensiële vergelyking** is die onbekende in die eksponent. Metode:\n\n1. Skryf albei kante as 'n mag van dieselfde (priem)grondtal.\n2. As a^{x} = a^{y} (a > 0, a ≠ 1), dan is x = y – stel die eksponente gelyk.\n3. Los die lineêre vergelyking op en kontroleer deur terug te vervang.\n\n- 2^{x} = 32 → 2^{x} = 2^{5} → x = 5\n- 3^{x+1} = [[1/27]] → 3^{x+1} = 3^{−3} → x + 1 = −3 → x = −4\n- 5^{2x−1} = 125 → 5^{2x−1} = 5^{3} → 2x − 1 = 3 → x = 2\n- 7^{x} = 1 → 7^{x} = 7^{0} → x = 0\n- 2^{x+1} + 2^{x} = 24 → 2^{x}(2 + 1) = 24 → 2^{x} = 8 → x = 3 (haal eers die gemeenskaplike faktor uit)\n\n> **Onthou!** As a > 0, is a^{x} altyd positief. 'n Vergelyking soos 2^{x} = −8 het dus **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Ken die magte van 2 (tot 2^{10} = 1 024), van 3 (tot 3^{5} = 243) en van 5 (tot 5^{4} = 625) uit jou kop – dan sien jy dadelik watter grondtal om te gebruik.","en":"## Basic concepts\n\nIn a^{n}, a is the **base** and n is the **exponent**: a^{n} = a × a × … × a (n factors). E.g. 2^{5} = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32. In Grade 10 the exponents are integers: positive, zero or negative.\n\n## The laws of exponents\n\nFor a, b ≠ 0 and m, n integers:\n\n| Law | Example |\n|---|---|\n| a^{m} × a^{n} = a^{m+n} | 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7} |\n| a^{m} ÷ a^{n} = a^{m−n} | x^{9} ÷ x^{4} = x^{5} |\n| (a^{m})^{n} = a^{mn} | (x^{3})^{4} = x^{12} |\n| (ab)^{n} = a^{n}b^{n} | (3x)^{2} = 9x^{2} |\n| ([[a/b]])^{n} = [[aⁿ/bⁿ]] | ([[2/3]])^{3} = [[8/27]] |\n| a^{0} = 1 | 7^{0} = 1 |\n| a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]] | 2^{−3} = [[1/8]] |\n\n**Negative exponent:** a^{−n} means \"one divided by a^{n}\" – it does **not** make the number negative. To make a negative exponent positive, move the factor across the fraction line: [[1/a⁻ⁿ]] = a^{n}, [[x⁻²/y⁻³]] = [[y³/x²]] and ([[a/b]])^{−n} = ([[b/a]])^{n}.\n\n### Why is a^{0} = 1 and a^{−n} = [[1/aⁿ]]?\n\nBy the division law, a^{3} ÷ a^{3} = a^{3−3} = a^{0}. But any number (except 0) divided by itself is 1, so a^{0} = 1. In the same way, a^{2} ÷ a^{5} = a^{2−5} = a^{−3}. If you write it out, two a's cancel and three a's are left below the fraction line: [[1/a³]]. That is why a^{−3} = [[1/a³]].\n\n### Steps to simplify\n\n1. Remove brackets with the power-of-a-product law.\n2. Write different bases as prime factors.\n3. Collect powers of the same base: add the exponents for ×, subtract for ÷.\n4. Write the final answer with positive exponents.\n\n### Common mistakes\n\n- 2^{3} × 2^{4} = 2^{7}, **not** 4^{7} – the base stays the same.\n- 3x^{0} = 3 × 1 = 3, but (3x)^{0} = 1.\n- −3^{2} = −9, but (−3)^{2} = 9.\n- The laws only work for **products and quotients**, not for sums: 2^{3} + 2^{4} ≠ 2^{7}, and (a + b)^{2} ≠ a^{2} + b^{2}.\n- 5^{x} + 5^{x} = 2 × 5^{x} (not 10^{x} or 5^{2x}).\n\n## The prime factor method\n\nIf the bases are different, write every base as a product of **prime factors** and then apply the laws to each prime separately.\n\n- 4 = 2^{2}; 8 = 2^{3}; 9 = 3^{2}; 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 27 = 3^{3}; 36 = 2^{2} × 3^{2}\n- 6^{x} = (2 × 3)^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{x}\n- 9^{x+1} = (3^{2})^{x+1} = 3^{2x+2} – multiply the **whole** exponent by 2.\n\nE.g. (6^{x} × 4^{x+1}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = (2^{x} × 3^{x} × 2^{2x+2}) ÷ (2^{3x} × 3^{x}) = 2^{3x+2−3x} × 3^{x−x} = 2^{2} = 4\n\n## Expressions with + or −\n\nIf a numerator or denominator consists of terms, you may not use the laws directly. First take out a common factor – usually the power with the **smallest** exponent. Remember that 2^{x+2} = 2^{x} × 2^{2}:\n\n(2^{x+2} − 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 2^{x}(2^{2} − 1) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = (3 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x}) = 1\n\n## Exponential equations\n\nIn an **exponential equation** the unknown is in the exponent. Method:\n\n1. Write both sides as a power of the same (prime) base.\n2. If a^{x} = a^{y} (a > 0, a ≠ 1), then x = y – equate the exponents.\n3. Solve the linear equation and check by substituting back.\n\n- 2^{x} = 32 → 2^{x} = 2^{5} → x = 5\n- 3^{x+1} = [[1/27]] → 3^{x+1} = 3^{−3} → x + 1 = −3 → x = −4\n- 5^{2x−1} = 125 → 5^{2x−1} = 5^{3} → 2x − 1 = 3 → x = 2\n- 7^{x} = 1 → 7^{x} = 7^{0} → x = 0\n- 2^{x+1} + 2^{x} = 24 → 2^{x}(2 + 1) = 24 → 2^{x} = 8 → x = 3 (take out the common factor first)\n\n> **Remember!** If a > 0, a^{x} is always positive. An equation such as 2^{x} = −8 therefore has **no solution**.\n\n> **Tip:** Know the powers of 2 (up to 2^{10} = 1 024), of 3 (up to 3^{5} = 243) and of 5 (up to 5^{4} = 625) by heart – then you immediately see which base to use."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Grondtal","en":"Base"},"def":{"af":"Die getal wat herhaaldelik met homself vermenigvuldig word; in aⁿ is a die grondtal.","en":"The number that is multiplied by itself repeatedly; in aⁿ, a is the base."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponent","en":"Exponent"},"def":{"af":"Die getal bo regs wat aandui hoeveel keer die grondtal as faktor voorkom; in aⁿ is n die eksponent.","en":"The number at the top right that shows how many times the base appears as a factor; in aⁿ, n is the exponent."}},{"term":{"af":"Mag","en":"Power"},"def":{"af":"'n Uitdrukking in die vorm aⁿ, bv. 2⁵ = 32 is die vyfde mag van 2.","en":"An expression of the form aⁿ, e.g. 2⁵ = 32 is the fifth power of 2."}},{"term":{"af":"Nul-eksponent","en":"Zero exponent"},"def":{"af":"Enige grondtal behalwe 0 tot die mag 0 is 1: a⁰ = 1. Let op: 3x⁰ = 3, maar (3x)⁰ = 1.","en":"Any base except 0 to the power 0 is 1: a⁰ = 1. Note: 3x⁰ = 3, but (3x)⁰ = 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Negatiewe eksponent","en":"Negative exponent"},"def":{"af":"a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ. Dit beteken 'een gedeel deur' en maak die getal nie negatief nie, bv. 2⁻³ = 1/8.","en":"a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ. It means 'one divided by' and does not make the number negative, e.g. 2⁻³ = 1/8."}},{"term":{"af":"Priemfaktor-metode","en":"Prime factor method"},"def":{"af":"Skryf elke grondtal as 'n produk van priemfaktore (bv. 12 = 2² × 3) sodat die eksponentwette op elke priemgetal toegepas kan word.","en":"Write every base as a product of prime factors (e.g. 12 = 2² × 3) so that the laws of exponents can be applied to each prime."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële vergelyking","en":"Exponential equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die onbekende in die eksponent is, bv. 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/27. Maak die grondtalle gelyk en stel die eksponente gelyk.","en":"An equation in which the unknown is in the exponent, e.g. 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/27. Make the bases equal and equate the exponents."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vereenvoudig met die eksponentwette","en":"Simplify with the laws of exponents"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig en skryf die antwoord met positiewe eksponente: (2x³y⁻²)³ ÷ (4x⁵y⁻⁴)","en":"Simplify and write the answer with positive exponents: (2x³y⁻²)³ ÷ (4x⁵y⁻⁴)"},"steps":[{"af":"Mag van 'n produk – verhef elke faktor tot die mag 3: (2x^{3}y^{−2})^{3} = 2^{3}x^{9}y^{−6} = 8x^{9}y^{−6}","en":"Power of a product – raise every factor to the power 3: (2x^{3}y^{−2})^{3} = 2^{3}x^{9}y^{−6} = 8x^{9}y^{−6}"},{"af":"Deel nou 8x^{9}y^{−6} ÷ 4x^{5}y^{−4}: deel die koëffisiënte en trek die eksponente van dieselfde grondtal af.","en":"Now divide 8x^{9}y^{−6} ÷ 4x^{5}y^{−4}: divide the coefficients and subtract the exponents of the same base."},{"af":"8 ÷ 4 = 2; x^{9−5} = x^{4}; y^{−6−(−4)} = y^{−6+4} = y^{−2}","en":"8 ÷ 4 = 2; x^{9−5} = x^{4}; y^{−6−(−4)} = y^{−6+4} = y^{−2}"},{"af":"Skryf met 'n positiewe eksponent: 2x^{4}y^{−2} = [[2x⁴/y²]]","en":"Write with a positive exponent: 2x^{4}y^{−2} = [[2x⁴/y²]]"}],"answer":{"af":"2x⁴/y²","en":"2x⁴/y²"}},{"title":{"af":"Die priemfaktor-metode","en":"The prime factor method"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (12ˣ × 9ˣ⁻¹) ÷ (18ˣ × 6ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (12ˣ × 9ˣ⁻¹) ÷ (18ˣ × 6ˣ)"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf elke grondtal in priemfaktore: 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 9 = 3^{2}; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 6 = 2 × 3","en":"Write every base in prime factors: 12 = 2^{2} × 3; 9 = 3^{2}; 18 = 2 × 3^{2}; 6 = 2 × 3"},{"af":"Teller: 12^{x} × 9^{x−1} = 2^{2x} × 3^{x} × 3^{2x−2} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x−2}","en":"Numerator: 12^{x} × 9^{x−1} = 2^{2x} × 3^{x} × 3^{2x−2} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x−2}"},{"af":"Noemer: 18^{x} × 6^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{2x} × 2^{x} × 3^{x} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x}","en":"Denominator: 18^{x} × 6^{x} = 2^{x} × 3^{2x} × 2^{x} × 3^{x} = 2^{2x} × 3^{3x}"},{"af":"Trek die eksponente af: 2^{2x−2x} × 3^{(3x−2)−3x} = 2^{0} × 3^{−2}","en":"Subtract the exponents: 2^{2x−2x} × 3^{(3x−2)−3x} = 2^{0} × 3^{−2}"},{"af":"= 1 × [[1/3²]] = [[1/9]]","en":"= 1 × [[1/3²]] = [[1/9]]"}],"answer":{"af":"1/9","en":"1/9"}},{"title":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike faktor by eksponente","en":"Common factor with exponents"},"problem":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2ˣ⁺³ − 2ˣ⁺¹) ÷ (3 × 2ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (2ˣ⁺³ − 2ˣ⁺¹) ÷ (3 × 2ˣ)"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf elke mag as 2^{x} maal 'n getal: 2^{x+3} = 2^{x} × 2^{3} = 8 × 2^{x} en 2^{x+1} = 2^{x} × 2 = 2 × 2^{x}","en":"Write every power as 2^{x} times a number: 2^{x+3} = 2^{x} × 2^{3} = 8 × 2^{x} and 2^{x+1} = 2^{x} × 2 = 2 × 2^{x}"},{"af":"Haal die gemeenskaplike faktor 2^{x} in die teller uit: 2^{x}(8 − 2) = 6 × 2^{x}","en":"Take out the common factor 2^{x} in the numerator: 2^{x}(8 − 2) = 6 × 2^{x}"},{"af":"Die uitdrukking word (6 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x})","en":"The expression becomes (6 × 2^{x}) ÷ (3 × 2^{x})"},{"af":"Kanselleer die faktor 2^{x}: 6 ÷ 3 = 2","en":"Cancel the factor 2^{x}: 6 ÷ 3 = 2"}],"answer":{"af":"2","en":"2"}},{"title":{"af":"Eksponensiële vergelykings","en":"Exponential equations"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: (a) 2ˣ⁻³ = 1/16 (b) 4ˣ⁺¹ = 8ˣ","en":"Solve for x: (a) 2ˣ⁻³ = 1/16 (b) 4ˣ⁺¹ = 8ˣ"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 16 = 2^{4}, dus [[1/16]] = 2^{−4}. Die vergelyking word 2^{x−3} = 2^{−4}","en":"(a) 16 = 2^{4}, so [[1/16]] = 2^{−4}. The equation becomes 2^{x−3} = 2^{−4}"},{"af":"Stel die eksponente gelyk: x − 3 = −4, dus x = −1","en":"Equate the exponents: x − 3 = −4, so x = −1"},{"af":"(b) Skryf albei kante met grondtal 2: 4^{x+1} = (2^{2})^{x+1} = 2^{2x+2} en 8^{x} = (2^{3})^{x} = 2^{3x}","en":"(b) Write both sides with base 2: 4^{x+1} = (2^{2})^{x+1} = 2^{2x+2} and 8^{x} = (2^{3})^{x} = 2^{3x}"},{"af":"2^{2x+2} = 2^{3x}, dus 2x + 2 = 3x en x = 2","en":"2^{2x+2} = 2^{3x}, so 2x + 2 = 3x and x = 2"},{"af":"Kontroleer (b): 4^{3} = 64 en 8^{2} = 64 ✓","en":"Check (b): 4^{3} = 64 and 8^{2} = 64 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) x = −1 (b) x = 2","en":"(a) x = −1 (b) x = 2"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: 3⁴ × 3⁵","en":"Simplify: 3⁴ × 3⁵"},"options":[{"af":"3²⁰","en":"3²⁰"},{"af":"9⁹","en":"9⁹"},{"af":"3⁹","en":"3⁹"},{"af":"9²⁰","en":"9²⁰"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Met dieselfde grondtal tel jy die eksponente op: 3⁴⁺⁵ = 3⁹. Die grondtal bly 3 – moenie die grondtalle of die eksponente vermenigvuldig nie.","en":"With the same base you add the exponents: 3⁴⁺⁵ = 3⁹. The base stays 3 – do not multiply the bases or the exponents."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"2⁻³ = −8","en":"2⁻³ = −8"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Negatiewe eksponent beteken 'een gedeel deur': 2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8. Die antwoord is positief.","en":"False. A negative exponent means 'one divided by': 2⁻³ = 1/2³ = 1/8. The answer is positive."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke uitdrukking by sy waarde.","en":"Match each expression to its value."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"7⁰","en":"7⁰"},"r":{"af":"1","en":"1"}},{"l":{"af":"2⁻²","en":"2⁻²"},"r":{"af":"1/4","en":"1/4"}},{"l":{"af":"(−3)²","en":"(−3)²"},"r":{"af":"9","en":"9"}},{"l":{"af":"−3²","en":"−3²"},"r":{"af":"−9","en":"−9"}},{"l":{"af":"(1/2)⁻³","en":"(1/2)⁻³"},"r":{"af":"8","en":"8"}}],"explain":{"af":"7⁰ = 1; 2⁻² = 1/2² = 1/4; (−3)² = (−3)(−3) = 9; −3² = −(3²) = −9 omdat net die 3 gekwadreer word; (1/2)⁻³ = 2³ = 8.","en":"7⁰ = 1; 2⁻² = 1/2² = 1/4; (−3)² = (−3)(−3) = 9; −3² = −(3²) = −9 because only the 3 is squared; (1/2)⁻³ = 2³ = 8."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: 3x⁰ + (3x)⁰","en":"Simplify: 3x⁰ + (3x)⁰"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"3x + 1","en":"3x + 1"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 3x⁰ is net die x tot die mag 0: 3 × 1 = 3. In (3x)⁰ is die hele hakie tot die mag 0: 1. Dus 3 + 1 = 4.","en":"In 3x⁰ only the x is to the power 0: 3 × 1 = 3. In (3x)⁰ the whole bracket is to the power 0: 1. So 3 + 1 = 4."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 2ˣ = 64. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 2ˣ = 64. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["6","x = 6"],"en":["6","x = 6"]},"explain":{"af":"64 = 2⁶, dus 2ˣ = 2⁶ en x = 6.","en":"64 = 2⁶, so 2ˣ = 2⁶ and x = 6."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["32","8","5"],"en":["32","8","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (2a³)⁴","en":"Simplify: (2a³)⁴"},"options":[{"af":"8a¹²","en":"8a¹²"},{"af":"2a¹²","en":"2a¹²"},{"af":"16a⁷","en":"16a⁷"},{"af":"16a¹²","en":"16a¹²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"(ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ: 2⁴ × (a³)⁴ = 16a¹². Die 2 moet ook tot die mag 4 verhef word (2⁴ = 16, nie 2 × 4 = 8 nie), en by 'n mag van 'n mag vermenigvuldig jy die eksponente.","en":"(ab)ⁿ = aⁿbⁿ: 2⁴ × (a³)⁴ = 16a¹². The 2 must also be raised to the power 4 (2⁴ = 16, not 2 × 4 = 8), and for a power of a power you multiply the exponents."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 3ˣ⁺² = 81. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 3ˣ⁺² = 81. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2","x = 2"],"en":["2","x = 2"]},"explain":{"af":"81 = 3⁴, dus 3ˣ⁺² = 3⁴. Stel die eksponente gelyk: x + 2 = 4, dus x = 2.","en":"81 = 3⁴, so 3ˣ⁺² = 3⁴. Equate the exponents: x + 2 = 4, so x = 2."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","6","25"],"en":["4","6","25"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig en skryf met positiewe eksponente: (x⁻³y²)/(x²y⁻¹)","en":"Simplify and write with positive exponents: (x⁻³y²)/(x²y⁻¹)"},"options":[{"af":"y³/x⁵","en":"y³/x⁵"},{"af":"x⁵y³","en":"x⁵y³"},{"af":"y/x⁵","en":"y/x⁵"},{"af":"y³/x","en":"y³/x"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Trek die eksponente af: x⁻³⁻² = x⁻⁵ en y²⁻⁽⁻¹⁾ = y³. Dus x⁻⁵y³ = y³/x⁵. Let op: 2 − (−1) = 3, nie 1 nie.","en":"Subtract the exponents: x⁻³⁻² = x⁻⁵ and y²⁻⁽⁻¹⁾ = y³. So x⁻⁵y³ = y³/x⁵. Note: 2 − (−1) = 3, not 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die vergelyking 2ˣ = −8 het geen reële oplossing nie.","en":"The equation 2ˣ = −8 has no real solution."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 2ˣ is altyd positief, watter waarde x ook al het (selfs 2⁻³ = 1/8 is positief). Dit kan dus nooit −8 wees nie.","en":"True. 2ˣ is always positive, whatever the value of x (even 2⁻³ = 1/8 is positive). So it can never be −8."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/9. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 3ˣ⁺¹ = 1/9. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","x = -3","x = −3"],"en":["-3","−3","x = -3","x = −3"]},"explain":{"af":"1/9 = 1/3² = 3⁻², dus x + 1 = −2 en x = −3.","en":"1/9 = 1/3² = 3⁻², so x + 1 = −2 and x = −3."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["-1","1","3"],"en":["-1","1","3"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (6ˣ × 9ˣ⁺¹)/(2ˣ × 27ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (6ˣ × 9ˣ⁺¹)/(2ˣ × 27ˣ)"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"1/9","en":"1/9"},{"af":"3ˣ⁺²","en":"3ˣ⁺²"},{"af":"9","en":"9"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Priemfaktore: 6ˣ = 2ˣ × 3ˣ, 9ˣ⁺¹ = 3²ˣ⁺² en 27ˣ = 3³ˣ. Teller: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ⁺²; noemer: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ. Antwoord: 3² = 9. As jy 9ˣ⁺¹ as 3²ˣ⁺¹ skryf, kry jy 3 – vermenigvuldig die hele eksponent met 2.","en":"Prime factors: 6ˣ = 2ˣ × 3ˣ, 9ˣ⁺¹ = 3²ˣ⁺² and 27ˣ = 3³ˣ. Numerator: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ⁺²; denominator: 2ˣ × 3³ˣ. Answer: 3² = 9. If you write 9ˣ⁺¹ as 3²ˣ⁺¹ you get 3 – multiply the whole exponent by 2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vereenvoudig: (3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ)","en":"Simplify: (3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ)"},"options":[{"af":"9/10","en":"9/10"},{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"3ˣ⁺²/10","en":"3ˣ⁺²/10"},{"af":"10","en":"10"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Haal 3ˣ in die teller uit: 3ˣ(3² + 1) = 10 × 3ˣ. Dan (10 × 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ) = 1. Jy mag nie 3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ as een mag skryf nie, en die tweede term 3ˣ val nie weg nie.","en":"Take out 3ˣ in the numerator: 3ˣ(3² + 1) = 10 × 3ˣ. Then (10 × 3ˣ)/(10 × 3ˣ) = 1. You may not write 3ˣ⁺² + 3ˣ as one power, and the second term 3ˣ does not disappear."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x: 9ˣ⁻¹ = 27ˣ⁻³. x = ___","en":"Solve for x: 9ˣ⁻¹ = 27ˣ⁻³. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["7","x = 7"],"en":["7","x = 7"]},"explain":{"af":"Skryf albei kante as magte van 3: (3²)ˣ⁻¹ = (3³)ˣ⁻³, dus 3²ˣ⁻² = 3³ˣ⁻⁹. Stel gelyk: 2x − 2 = 3x − 9, dus x = 7.","en":"Write both sides as powers of 3: (3²)ˣ⁻¹ = (3³)ˣ⁻³, so 3²ˣ⁻² = 3³ˣ⁻⁹. Equate: 2x − 2 = 3x − 9, so x = 7."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","−7","11"],"en":["2","−7","11"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Video van Hoërskool Brits se wendrie word op WhatsApp gedeel. Die aantal mense wat dit gesien het, verdubbel elke 10 minute. Om 18:00 het 3 mense dit gesien. Hoeveel minute ná 18:00 het 96 mense dit gesien?","en":"A video of Hoërskool Brits's winning try is shared on WhatsApp. The number of people who have seen it doubles every 10 minutes. At 18:00, 3 people had seen it. How many minutes after 18:00 had 96 people seen it?"},"options":[{"af":"50 minute","en":"50 minutes"},{"af":"5 minute","en":"5 minutes"},{"af":"60 minute","en":"60 minutes"},{"af":"320 minute","en":"320 minutes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná n periodes van 10 minute het 3 × 2ⁿ mense dit gesien. 3 × 2ⁿ = 96, dus 2ⁿ = 32 = 2⁵ en n = 5. Vyf periodes × 10 minute = 50 minute. (3 → 6 → 12 → 24 → 48 → 96 is vyf verdubbelings, nie ses nie; en n = 5 is die aantal periodes, nie minute nie.)","en":"After n periods of 10 minutes, 3 × 2ⁿ people have seen it. 3 × 2ⁿ = 96, so 2ⁿ = 32 = 2⁵ and n = 5. Five periods × 10 minutes = 50 minutes. (3 → 6 → 12 → 24 → 48 → 96 is five doublings, not six; and n = 5 is the number of periods, not minutes.)"}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-getalpatrone","title":{"af":"Getalpatrone","en":"Number patterns"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die konstante verskil van 'n lineêre getalpatroon kan vind, die algemene term kan opstel en dit gebruik om enige term of die posisie van 'n term te bereken.","en":"You will be able to find the constant difference of a linear number pattern, set up the general term and use it to calculate any term or the position of a term."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n getalpatroon?\n\n'n **Getalpatroon** (of **ry**) is 'n lys getalle wat 'n vaste reël volg, bv. 3; 7; 11; 15; … Elke getal in die patroon is 'n **term**, en ons skryf kommapunte tussen die terme.\n\n- T_{1} is die eerste term, T_{2} die tweede term, ensovoorts.\n- **n** is die **posisie** van 'n term. n is altyd 'n natuurlike getal: n = 1; 2; 3; …\n- **T_{n}** is die **waarde** van die term in posisie n.\n\n> **Onthou!** n sê *waar* die term staan; T_{n} sê *wat* die term is. In 3; 7; 11; 15 is n = 3 en T_{3} = 11.\n\n## Konstante verskil en lineêre patrone\n\nTrek elke term van die **volgende** term af: d = T_{2} − T_{1} = T_{3} − T_{2} = T_{4} − T_{3}\n\nAs die verskil elke keer dieselfde is, het die patroon 'n **konstante verskil d** en is dit 'n **lineêre patroon**.\n\n| Ry | Verskille | Lineêr? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3; 7; 11; 15; … | 4; 4; 4 | Ja, d = 4 |\n| 20; 17; 14; 11; … | −3; −3; −3 | Ja, d = −3 |\n| 2; 4; 8; 16; … | 2; 4; 8 | Nee, elke term verdubbel |\n| 1; 4; 9; 16; … | 3; 5; 7 | Nee, dit is kwadrate |\n\n- d > 0: die terme word groter (**stygende** patroon).\n- d < 0: die terme word kleiner (**dalende** patroon).\n- d kan ook 'n breuk of desimaal wees: 1; 2,5; 4; 5,5 het d = 1,5.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** d = T_{1} − T_{2} uitwerk. Dit gee die verkeerde teken. Werk altyd *latere term min vorige term*.\n\n## Die algemene term T_{n} = dn + c\n\nElke keer as n met 1 groter word, word d bygetel. Daarom is elke term d keer sy posisie plus 'n vaste getal c:\n\n**T_{n} = dn + c**\n\n1. Bereken d en kontroleer dat dit konstant is.\n2. Vind c: as n = 1, is T_{1} = d + c, dus **c = T_{1} − d**. Dink aan c as die \"nulde term\": die getal wat voor T_{1} sou kom.\n3. Skryf T_{n} = dn + c neer.\n4. Kontroleer met T_{2} of T_{3}.\n\nVir 3; 7; 11; 15; … is d = 4 en c = 3 − 4 = −1, dus T_{n} = 4n − 1. Kontrole: T_{3} = 4(3) − 1 = 11 ✓\n\nJy sal ook die vorm T_{n} = T_{1} + (n − 1)d sien. Dit gee presies dieselfde formule: 3 + (n − 1)(4) = 4n − 1.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** T_{n} = 4n + 3 skryf, m.a.w. die eerste term as c gebruik. Toets dit: 4(1) + 3 = 7, nie 3 nie!\n\n## Gebruik die algemene term\n\n**'n Term vind:** vervang n. Vir T_{n} = 4n − 1 is T_{50} = 4(50) − 1 = 199.\n\n**Die posisie vind:** stel T_{n} gelyk aan die gegewe waarde en los op vir n. Watter term is 143? 4n − 1 = 143, dus 4n = 144 en n = 36. Dit is T_{36}.\n\n**Is 'n getal 'n term?** Los T_{n} = getal op. Die getal is net 'n term as n 'n **natuurlike getal** is. Is 100 'n term? 4n − 1 = 100 gee n = 25,25, dus **nee**.\n\n**Eerste term groter as 'n waarde:** los die ongelykheid op en rond **op** na die volgende natuurlike getal. 4n − 1 > 100 gee n > 25,25, dus n = 26 en T_{26} = 103.\n\n**'n Ontbrekende term:** as a; b; c opeenvolgende terme van 'n lineêre patroon is, is b − a = c − b. Vir 5; x; 17 is x − 5 = 17 − x, dus x = 11.\n\n## Woordprobleme en patrone met figure\n\nIn woordprobleme is n die nommer van die figuur, week, ry of dag, en T_{n} die hoeveelheid (vuurhoutjies, stoele, rand). Skryf die eerste paar terme as 'n ry neer en werk dan soos hierbo.\n\nByvoorbeeld: vierkante van vuurhoutjies in 'n ry. Een vierkant het 4 vuurhoutjies nodig, twee vierkante 7 en drie vierkante 10. Die ry 4; 7; 10; … het d = 3, want elke nuwe vierkant deel een sy met die vorige een. Dus is T_{n} = 3n + 1 en 25 vierkante het 3(25) + 1 = 76 vuurhoutjies nodig.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** dink die patroon is direk eweredig: \"1 vierkant = 4, dus 25 vierkante = 100\". Dit werk net as c = 0.\n\n> **Wenk:** Antwoord altyd in die konteks, bv. \"Patroon 25 het 76 vuurhoutjies nodig\". As n 'n aantal mense, tafels of weke is, moet n 'n natuurlike getal wees.","en":"## What is a number pattern?\n\nA **number pattern** (or **sequence**) is a list of numbers that follows a fixed rule, e.g. 3; 7; 11; 15; … Each number in the pattern is a **term**, and we write semicolons between the terms.\n\n- T_{1} is the first term, T_{2} the second term, and so on.\n- **n** is the **position** of a term. n is always a natural number: n = 1; 2; 3; …\n- **T_{n}** is the **value** of the term in position n.\n\n> **Remember!** n tells you *where* the term is; T_{n} tells you *what* the term is. In 3; 7; 11; 15, n = 3 and T_{3} = 11.\n\n## Constant difference and linear patterns\n\nSubtract each term from the **next** term: d = T_{2} − T_{1} = T_{3} − T_{2} = T_{4} − T_{3}\n\nIf the difference is the same every time, the pattern has a **constant (common) difference d** and it is a **linear pattern**.\n\n| Sequence | Differences | Linear? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3; 7; 11; 15; … | 4; 4; 4 | Yes, d = 4 |\n| 20; 17; 14; 11; … | −3; −3; −3 | Yes, d = −3 |\n| 2; 4; 8; 16; … | 2; 4; 8 | No, each term doubles |\n| 1; 4; 9; 16; … | 3; 5; 7 | No, these are squares |\n\n- d > 0: the terms get bigger (**increasing** pattern).\n- d < 0: the terms get smaller (**decreasing** pattern).\n- d can also be a fraction or decimal: 1; 2.5; 4; 5.5 has d = 1.5.\n\n> **Common mistake:** working out d = T_{1} − T_{2}. That gives the wrong sign. Always use *later term minus previous term*.\n\n## The general term T_{n} = dn + c\n\nEvery time n increases by 1, d is added. That is why every term is d times its position plus a fixed number c:\n\n**T_{n} = dn + c**\n\n1. Calculate d and check that it is constant.\n2. Find c: when n = 1, T_{1} = d + c, so **c = T_{1} − d**. Think of c as the \"zeroth term\": the number that would come before T_{1}.\n3. Write down T_{n} = dn + c.\n4. Check with T_{2} or T_{3}.\n\nFor 3; 7; 11; 15; … d = 4 and c = 3 − 4 = −1, so T_{n} = 4n − 1. Check: T_{3} = 4(3) − 1 = 11 ✓\n\nYou will also see the form T_{n} = T_{1} + (n − 1)d. It gives exactly the same formula: 3 + (n − 1)(4) = 4n − 1.\n\n> **Common mistake:** writing T_{n} = 4n + 3, i.e. using the first term as c. Test it: 4(1) + 3 = 7, not 3!\n\n## Using the general term\n\n**Finding a term:** substitute n. For T_{n} = 4n − 1, T_{50} = 4(50) − 1 = 199.\n\n**Finding the position:** set T_{n} equal to the given value and solve for n. Which term is 143? 4n − 1 = 143, so 4n = 144 and n = 36. It is T_{36}.\n\n**Is a number a term?** Solve T_{n} = number. The number is only a term if n is a **natural number**. Is 100 a term? 4n − 1 = 100 gives n = 25.25, so **no**.\n\n**First term greater than a value:** solve the inequality and round **up** to the next natural number. 4n − 1 > 100 gives n > 25.25, so n = 26 and T_{26} = 103.\n\n**A missing term:** if a; b; c are consecutive terms of a linear pattern, then b − a = c − b. For 5; x; 17, x − 5 = 17 − x, so x = 11.\n\n## Word problems and patterns with figures\n\nIn word problems n is the number of the figure, week, row or day, and T_{n} is the quantity (matches, chairs, rand). Write the first few terms as a sequence and then work as above.\n\nFor example: squares made of matches in a row. One square needs 4 matches, two squares need 7 and three squares need 10. The sequence 4; 7; 10; … has d = 3, because each new square shares one side with the previous one. So T_{n} = 3n + 1 and 25 squares need 3(25) + 1 = 76 matches.\n\n> **Common mistake:** thinking the pattern is directly proportional: \"1 square = 4, so 25 squares = 100\". That only works if c = 0.\n\n> **Tip:** Always answer in context, e.g. \"Pattern 25 needs 76 matches\". If n is a number of people, tables or weeks, n must be a natural number."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Getalpatroon (ry)","en":"Number pattern (sequence)"},"def":{"af":"'n Lys getalle wat 'n vaste reël volg, bv. 3; 7; 11; 15; …","en":"A list of numbers that follows a fixed rule, e.g. 3; 7; 11; 15; …"}},{"term":{"af":"Term","en":"Term"},"def":{"af":"Elke getal in 'n getalpatroon. T₁ is die eerste term, T₂ die tweede, ensovoorts.","en":"Each number in a number pattern. T₁ is the first term, T₂ the second, and so on."}},{"term":{"af":"Posisie (n)","en":"Position (n)"},"def":{"af":"Die plek van 'n term in die ry. n is altyd 'n natuurlike getal: 1; 2; 3; …","en":"The place of a term in the sequence. n is always a natural number: 1; 2; 3; …"}},{"term":{"af":"Konstante verskil (d)","en":"Constant difference (d)"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste getal wat elke keer bygetel word: d = T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂.","en":"The fixed number that is added each time: d = T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre patroon","en":"Linear pattern"},"def":{"af":"'n Patroon met 'n konstante verskil tussen opeenvolgende terme. Die algemene term het die vorm Tₙ = dn + c.","en":"A pattern with a constant difference between consecutive terms. The general term has the form Tₙ = dn + c."}},{"term":{"af":"Algemene term (Tₙ)","en":"General term (Tₙ)"},"def":{"af":"'n Formule in terme van n waarmee jy enige term van die patroon kan bereken, bv. Tₙ = 4n − 1.","en":"A formula in terms of n with which you can calculate any term of the pattern, e.g. Tₙ = 4n − 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Opeenvolgende terme","en":"Consecutive terms"},"def":{"af":"Terme wat direk na mekaar in die ry volg, bv. T₃ en T₄.","en":"Terms that follow directly after each other in the sequence, e.g. T₃ and T₄."}},{"term":{"af":"Stygende en dalende patroon","en":"Increasing and decreasing pattern"},"def":{"af":"Stygend: die terme word groter (d > 0). Dalend: die terme word kleiner (d < 0).","en":"Increasing: the terms get bigger (d > 0). Decreasing: the terms get smaller (d < 0)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die algemene term en T₅₀","en":"The general term and T₅₀"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee die getalpatroon 5; 9; 13; 17; … (a) Bepaal die algemene term Tₙ. (b) Bereken T₅₀.","en":"Given the number pattern 5; 9; 13; 17; … (a) Determine the general term Tₙ. (b) Calculate T₅₀."},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken die verskille: 9 − 5 = 4; 13 − 9 = 4; 17 − 13 = 4. Die konstante verskil is d = 4, dus is die patroon lineêr.","en":"Calculate the differences: 9 − 5 = 4; 13 − 9 = 4; 17 − 13 = 4. The constant difference is d = 4, so the pattern is linear."},{"af":"Vind c: c = T_{1} − d = 5 − 4 = 1","en":"Find c: c = T_{1} − d = 5 − 4 = 1"},{"af":"(a) T_{n} = 4n + 1. Kontrole: T_{2} = 4(2) + 1 = 9 ✓","en":"(a) T_{n} = 4n + 1. Check: T_{2} = 4(2) + 1 = 9 ✓"},{"af":"(b) T_{50} = 4(50) + 1 = 200 + 1 = 201","en":"(b) T_{50} = 4(50) + 1 = 200 + 1 = 201"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = 4n + 1; T₅₀ = 201","en":"Tₙ = 4n + 1; T₅₀ = 201"}},{"title":{"af":"Dalende patroon: vind die posisie","en":"Decreasing pattern: find the position"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee die getalpatroon 23; 17; 11; 5; … Bepaal die algemene term en bepaal watter term gelyk is aan −151.","en":"Given the number pattern 23; 17; 11; 5; … Determine the general term and determine which term is equal to −151."},"steps":[{"af":"d = 17 − 23 = −6 (kontroleer: 11 − 17 = −6 ✓). Die patroon daal, dus is d negatief.","en":"d = 17 − 23 = −6 (check: 11 − 17 = −6 ✓). The pattern decreases, so d is negative."},{"af":"c = T_{1} − d = 23 − (−6) = 29, dus T_{n} = −6n + 29","en":"c = T_{1} − d = 23 − (−6) = 29, so T_{n} = −6n + 29"},{"af":"Stel T_{n} = −151: −6n + 29 = −151","en":"Set T_{n} = −151: −6n + 29 = −151"},{"af":"−6n = −180, dus n = 30","en":"−6n = −180, so n = 30"},{"af":"Kontrole: T_{30} = −6(30) + 29 = −180 + 29 = −151 ✓","en":"Check: T_{30} = −6(30) + 29 = −180 + 29 = −151 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = −6n + 29; −151 is die 30ste term (T₃₀).","en":"Tₙ = −6n + 29; −151 is the 30th term (T₃₀)."}},{"title":{"af":"Is 100 'n term?","en":"Is 100 a term?"},"problem":{"af":"Is 100 'n term van die patroon 4; 11; 18; 25; …? Indien nie, bepaal die eerste term wat groter as 100 is.","en":"Is 100 a term of the pattern 4; 11; 18; 25; …? If not, determine the first term that is greater than 100."},"steps":[{"af":"d = 11 − 4 = 7 en c = 4 − 7 = −3, dus T_{n} = 7n − 3","en":"d = 11 − 4 = 7 and c = 4 − 7 = −3, so T_{n} = 7n − 3"},{"af":"Stel 7n − 3 = 100: 7n = 103, dus n = [[103/7]] ≈ 14,71","en":"Set 7n − 3 = 100: 7n = 103, so n = [[103/7]] ≈ 14.71"},{"af":"n is nie 'n natuurlike getal nie, dus is 100 NIE 'n term nie.","en":"n is not a natural number, so 100 is NOT a term."},{"af":"Vir T_{n} > 100: 7n − 3 > 100, dus n > 14,71. Die kleinste natuurlike getal is n = 15.","en":"For T_{n} > 100: 7n − 3 > 100, so n > 14.71. The smallest natural number is n = 15."},{"af":"T_{15} = 7(15) − 3 = 102. (Kontrole: T_{14} = 95 is nog kleiner as 100.)","en":"T_{15} = 7(15) − 3 = 102. (Check: T_{14} = 95 is still less than 100.)"}],"answer":{"af":"100 is nie 'n term nie; die eerste term groter as 100 is T₁₅ = 102.","en":"100 is not a term; the first term greater than 100 is T₁₅ = 102."}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem: tafels by 'n braai","en":"Word problem: tables at a braai"},"problem":{"af":"By 'n braai by Hartbeespoortdam word vierkantige tafels in 'n lang ry teen mekaar geskuif. Een tafel sit 4 mense, twee tafels sit 6 mense en drie tafels sit 8 mense. (a) Bepaal 'n formule vir die aantal mense wat by n tafels kan sit. (b) Hoeveel mense kan by 25 tafels sit? (c) Hoeveel tafels is nodig vir presies 40 gaste?","en":"At a braai at Hartbeespoort Dam square tables are pushed together in a long row. One table seats 4 people, two tables seat 6 people and three tables seat 8 people. (a) Determine a formula for the number of people who can sit at n tables. (b) How many people can sit at 25 tables? (c) How many tables are needed for exactly 40 guests?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die ry is 4; 6; 8; … met d = 2. Elke ekstra tafel voeg net 2 plekke by, want waar twee tafels raak, kan niemand sit nie.","en":"The sequence is 4; 6; 8; … with d = 2. Each extra table only adds 2 places, because nobody can sit where two tables touch."},{"af":"(a) c = T_{1} − d = 4 − 2 = 2, dus T_{n} = 2n + 2","en":"(a) c = T_{1} − d = 4 − 2 = 2, so T_{n} = 2n + 2"},{"af":"(b) T_{25} = 2(25) + 2 = 52 mense","en":"(b) T_{25} = 2(25) + 2 = 52 people"},{"af":"(c) 2n + 2 = 40, dus 2n = 38 en n = 19 tafels","en":"(c) 2n + 2 = 40, so 2n = 38 and n = 19 tables"},{"af":"Kontrole: 2(19) + 2 = 40 ✓","en":"Check: 2(19) + 2 = 40 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"Tₙ = 2n + 2; 25 tafels sit 52 mense; 40 gaste het 19 tafels nodig.","en":"Tₙ = 2n + 2; 25 tables seat 52 people; 40 guests need 19 tables."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die ry 2; 4; 8; 16; … is 'n lineêre getalpatroon.","en":"The sequence 2; 4; 8; 16; … is a linear number pattern."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die verskille is 2; 4; 8 – nie konstant nie. Elke term word verdubbel, dus is die patroon nie lineêr nie.","en":"False. The differences are 2; 4; 8 – not constant. Each term is doubled, so the pattern is not linear."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die konstante verskil van die ry 7; 12; 17; 22; …?","en":"What is the constant difference of the sequence 7; 12; 17; 22; …?"},"options":[{"af":"−5","en":"−5"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"2","en":"2"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"d = 12 − 7 = 5 (en 17 − 12 = 5). −5 kry jy as jy die vorige term min die volgende term doen, 7 is die eerste term en 2 is c in Tₙ = 5n + 2.","en":"d = 12 − 7 = 5 (and 17 − 12 = 5). You get −5 if you do the previous term minus the next term, 7 is the first term and 2 is c in Tₙ = 5n + 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die volgende term van die ry 31; 27; 23; 19; … neer: ___","en":"Write down the next term of the sequence 31; 27; 23; 19; …: ___"},"answers":{"af":["15","T5 = 15","T₅ = 15"],"en":["15","T5 = 15","T₅ = 15"]},"explain":{"af":"Die konstante verskil is d = 27 − 31 = −4, dus is die volgende term 19 − 4 = 15.","en":"The constant difference is d = 27 − 31 = −4, so the next term is 19 − 4 = 15."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["23","11","16"],"en":["23","11","16"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke simbool in Tₙ = dn + c by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each symbol in Tₙ = dn + c to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"n","en":"n"},"r":{"af":"die posisie van die term (1; 2; 3; …)","en":"the position of the term (1; 2; 3; …)"}},{"l":{"af":"Tₙ","en":"Tₙ"},"r":{"af":"die waarde van die term in posisie n","en":"the value of the term in position n"}},{"l":{"af":"d","en":"d"},"r":{"af":"die konstante verskil, T₂ − T₁","en":"the constant difference, T₂ − T₁"}},{"l":{"af":"c","en":"c"},"r":{"af":"T₁ − d, die \"nulde term\"","en":"T₁ − d, the \"zeroth term\""}}],"explain":{"af":"n is waar die term staan, Tₙ is wat die term is, d word elke keer bygetel en c = T₁ − d.","en":"n is where the term is, Tₙ is what the term is, d is added every time and c = T₁ − d."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die algemene term van die ry 5; 8; 11; 14; …?","en":"What is the general term of the sequence 5; 8; 11; 14; …?"},"options":[{"af":"Tₙ = 3n + 5","en":"Tₙ = 3n + 5"},{"af":"Tₙ = 2n + 3","en":"Tₙ = 2n + 3"},{"af":"Tₙ = 3n − 2","en":"Tₙ = 3n − 2"},{"af":"Tₙ = 3n + 2","en":"Tₙ = 3n + 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"d = 3 en c = T₁ − d = 5 − 3 = 2, dus Tₙ = 3n + 2. Kontrole: T₁ = 3 + 2 = 5 ✓. Tₙ = 3n + 5 gebruik die eerste term as c (dan is T₁ = 8), en 3n − 2 het die teken van c verkeerd.","en":"d = 3 and c = T₁ − d = 5 − 3 = 2, so Tₙ = 3n + 2. Check: T₁ = 3 + 2 = 5 ✓. Tₙ = 3n + 5 uses the first term as c (then T₁ = 8), and 3n − 2 has the wrong sign for c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gegee Tₙ = 4n − 7. Bereken T₂₀ = ___","en":"Given Tₙ = 4n − 7. Calculate T₂₀ = ___"},"answers":{"af":["73","T20 = 73","T₂₀ = 73"],"en":["73","T20 = 73","T₂₀ = 73"]},"explain":{"af":"Vervang n = 20: T₂₀ = 4(20) − 7 = 80 − 7 = 73.","en":"Substitute n = 20: T₂₀ = 4(20) − 7 = 80 − 7 = 73."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["87","52","80"],"en":["87","52","80"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die algemene term van 'n patroon is Tₙ = −3n + 20. Wat is die eerste drie terme?","en":"The general term of a pattern is Tₙ = −3n + 20. What are the first three terms?"},"options":[{"af":"17; 14; 11","en":"17; 14; 11"},{"af":"20; 17; 14","en":"20; 17; 14"},{"af":"23; 26; 29","en":"23; 26; 29"},{"af":"−3; −6; −9","en":"−3; −6; −9"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vervang n = 1; 2; 3: −3(1) + 20 = 17, −3(2) + 20 = 14, −3(3) + 20 = 11. 20; 17; 14 begin by n = 0, maar n begin altyd by 1.","en":"Substitute n = 1; 2; 3: −3(1) + 20 = 17, −3(2) + 20 = 14, −3(3) + 20 = 11. 20; 17; 14 starts at n = 0, but n always starts at 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"100 is 'n term van die ry 2; 9; 16; 23; …","en":"100 is a term of the sequence 2; 9; 16; 23; …"},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. d = 7 en c = 2 − 7 = −5, dus Tₙ = 7n − 5. 7n − 5 = 100 gee 7n = 105 en n = 15 – 'n natuurlike getal. 100 is T₁₅.","en":"True. d = 7 and c = 2 − 7 = −5, so Tₙ = 7n − 5. 7n − 5 = 100 gives 7n = 105 and n = 15 – a natural number. 100 is T₁₅."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter term van die ry 6; 10; 14; 18; … is gelyk aan 126?","en":"Which term of the sequence 6; 10; 14; 18; … is equal to 126?"},"options":[{"af":"T₃₀","en":"T₃₀"},{"af":"T₃₁","en":"T₃₁"},{"af":"T₃₂","en":"T₃₂"},{"af":"T₁₂₄","en":"T₁₂₄"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Tₙ = 4n + 2. Stel 4n + 2 = 126: 4n = 124 en n = 31. T₃₀ kom van Tₙ = 4n + 6 (eerste term as c), T₃₂ van 'n tekenfout in c, en T₁₂₄ as jy vergeet om deur 4 te deel.","en":"Tₙ = 4n + 2. Set 4n + 2 = 126: 4n = 124 and n = 31. T₃₀ comes from Tₙ = 4n + 6 (first term as c), T₃₂ from a sign error in c, and T₁₂₄ if you forget to divide by 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken T₂₅ van die ry −8; −5; −2; 1; …","en":"Calculate T₂₅ of the sequence −8; −5; −2; 1; …"},"options":[{"af":"67","en":"67"},{"af":"−80","en":"−80"},{"af":"64","en":"64"},{"af":"70","en":"70"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"d = −5 − (−8) = 3 en c = −8 − 3 = −11, dus Tₙ = 3n − 11 en T₂₅ = 75 − 11 = 64. 67 gebruik −8 as c, 70 het −8 + 3 = −5 as c, en −80 het d = −3 (verkeerde volgorde van aftrek).","en":"d = −5 − (−8) = 3 and c = −8 − 3 = −11, so Tₙ = 3n − 11 and T₂₅ = 75 − 11 = 64. 67 uses −8 as c, 70 has −8 + 3 = −5 as c, and −80 has d = −3 (subtracting in the wrong order)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die eerste term van die ry 3; 10; 17; 24; … wat groter as 200 is?","en":"What is the first term of the sequence 3; 10; 17; 24; … that is greater than 200?"},"options":[{"af":"199","en":"199"},{"af":"203","en":"203"},{"af":"213","en":"213"},{"af":"206","en":"206"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tₙ = 7n − 4. 7n − 4 > 200 gee n > 29,14, dus n = 30 en T₃₀ = 7(30) − 4 = 206. 199 is T₂₉ (nog kleiner as 200), en 203 = 7 × 29 sonder die c.","en":"Tₙ = 7n − 4. 7n − 4 > 200 gives n > 29.14, so n = 30 and T₃₀ = 7(30) − 4 = 206. 199 is T₂₉ (still less than 200), and 203 = 7 × 29 without the c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"2x + 1; 5x − 2 en 6x + 3 is die eerste drie terme van 'n lineêre getalpatroon. Bepaal x. x = ___","en":"2x + 1; 5x − 2 and 6x + 3 are the first three terms of a linear number pattern. Determine x. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4","x = 4"],"en":["4","x = 4"]},"explain":{"af":"In 'n lineêre patroon is T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂: (5x − 2) − (2x + 1) = (6x + 3) − (5x − 2), dus 3x − 3 = x + 5, 2x = 8 en x = 4. Die terme is 9; 18; 27 met d = 9 ✓.","en":"In a linear pattern T₂ − T₁ = T₃ − T₂: (5x − 2) − (2x + 1) = (6x + 3) − (5x − 2), so 3x − 3 = x + 5, 2x = 8 and x = 4. The terms are 9; 18; 27 with d = 9 ✓."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","3","9"],"en":["1","3","9"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Seshoeke word van vuurhoutjies in 'n ry gebou, en elke nuwe seshoek deel een sy met die vorige een. Patroon 1 (een seshoek) het 6 vuurhoutjies, patroon 2 het 11 en patroon 3 het 16. Hoeveel vuurhoutjies het patroon 40 nodig?","en":"Hexagons are built from matches in a row, and each new hexagon shares one side with the previous one. Pattern 1 (one hexagon) has 6 matches, pattern 2 has 11 and pattern 3 has 16. How many matches does pattern 40 need?"},"options":[{"af":"240","en":"240"},{"af":"201","en":"201"},{"af":"206","en":"206"},{"af":"200","en":"200"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ry 6; 11; 16; … het d = 5 en c = 6 − 5 = 1, dus Tₙ = 5n + 1 en T₄₀ = 201. 240 = 6 × 40 neem aan die patroon is eweredig (maar seshoeke deel sye), en 206 gebruik die eerste term as c.","en":"The sequence 6; 11; 16; … has d = 5 and c = 6 − 5 = 1, so Tₙ = 5n + 1 and T₄₀ = 201. 240 = 6 × 40 assumes the pattern is proportional (but hexagons share sides), and 206 uses the first term as c."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sipho het aan die einde van week 1 R5 in sy spaarpot en sit elke week R4 by. Anja het aan die einde van week 1 R96, maar spandeer elke week R3 aan selfoondata. Aan die einde van watter week het hulle presies ewe veel geld? Week ___","en":"Sipho has R5 in his money box at the end of week 1 and adds R4 every week. Anja has R96 at the end of week 1, but spends R3 on cellphone data every week. At the end of which week do they have exactly the same amount of money? Week ___"},"answers":{"af":["14","week 14","n = 14","T14"],"en":["14","week 14","n = 14","T14"]},"explain":{"af":"Sipho: 5; 9; 13; … dus Tₙ = 4n + 1. Anja: 96; 93; 90; … dus Tₙ = −3n + 99. Stel gelyk: 4n + 1 = −3n + 99, dus 7n = 98 en n = 14. In week 14 het albei R57.","en":"Sipho: 5; 9; 13; … so Tₙ = 4n + 1. Anja: 96; 93; 90; … so Tₙ = −3n + 99. Set equal: 4n + 1 = −3n + 99, so 7n = 98 and n = 14. In week 14 both have R57."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["13","57","98"],"en":["13","57","98"]}}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-vergelykings","title":{"af":"Vergelykings","en":"Equations"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lineêre vergelykings (ook met breuke), kwadratiese vergelykings, letterlike vergelykings en gelyktydige vergelykings kan oplos en dit in woordprobleme kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to solve linear equations (including fractions), quadratic equations, literal equations and simultaneous equations, and use them in word problems."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat beteken \"los op\"?\n\n'n **Vergelyking** sê dat twee uitdrukkings gelyk is, bv. 3x − 4 = 11. Om dit **op te los**, vind jy die waarde(s) van die veranderlike wat die **linkerkant (LK)** gelyk maak aan die **regterkant (RK)**. Die goue reël: **wat jy aan die een kant doen, doen jy ook aan die ander kant.** Kontroleer jou antwoord deur dit in die oorspronklike vergelyking te vervang.\n\n## Lineêre vergelykings\n\nDie hoogste mag van x is 1, dus is daar **een** oplossing.\n\n1. Verwyder hakies. Pas op vir 'n minus voor 'n hakie: −3(x − 1) = −3x + 3.\n2. Verwyder breuke: vermenigvuldig **elke term** aan **albei** kante met die **KGV** van die noemers.\n3. Bring die x-terme na een kant en die getalle na die ander kant.\n4. Deel deur die koëffisiënt van x.\n\nVoorbeeld: [[x/2]] + [[x−1/3]] = 3. Die KGV is 6: 3x + 2(x − 1) = 18, dus 5x − 2 = 18, 5x = 20 en x = 4.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** net die breuke met die KGV vermenigvuldig en die RK vergeet. *Elke* term, ook die getal aan die ander kant, word vermenigvuldig.\n\n**Veranderlike in die noemer:** skryf eers die **beperking** neer, want 'n noemer mag nooit 0 wees nie. Vir [[3/x−2]] = 1 is x ≠ 2. Vermenigvuldig met (x − 2): 3 = x − 2, dus x = 5. As jou antwoord 'n beperkte waarde is, is daar **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n## Kwadratiese vergelykings\n\nDie hoogste mag van x is 2, dus is daar **hoogstens twee** oplossings. Ons los dit op deur te faktoriseer.\n\n1. Skryf in **standaardvorm** ax^{2} + bx + c = 0. Een kant **moet 0** wees.\n2. Faktoriseer: gemene faktor, verskil van twee vierkante of drieterm.\n3. Gebruik die **nulproduk-reël**: as A × B = 0, dan is A = 0 **of** B = 0.\n4. Los elke faktor op.\n\nVoorbeeld: x^{2} − x − 12 = 0, dus (x − 4)(x + 3) = 0 en x = 4 of x = −3.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** x^{2} = 5x deur x deel. Dan verloor jy die oplossing x = 0! Skryf eerder x^{2} − 5x = 0, dus x(x − 5) = 0 en x = 0 of x = 5.\n\n- x^{2} = 9 gee x = **±3** (x = 3 of x = −3), want (−3)^{2} = 9 ook.\n- (x − 2)(x + 1) = 4 beteken **nie** x − 2 = 4 nie. Die nulproduk-reël werk net as die een kant 0 is. Vermenigvuldig uit en maak een kant 0: x^{2} − x − 6 = 0, dus (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 en x = 3 of x = −2.\n\n## Letterlike vergelykings\n\n'n **Letterlike vergelyking** bevat meer as een letter, soos 'n formule. \"Maak a die **onderwerp**\" beteken: kry a alleen aan een kant van die gelykaanteken. Gebruik presies dieselfde stappe as vir 'n gewone vergelyking.\n\n- v = u + at, dus v − u = at en a = [[v−u/t]]\n- As die onderwerp **twee keer** voorkom, bring albei terme na een kant en **haal dit as gemene faktor uit**: ax + 3 = bx + 7, dus ax − bx = 4, x(a − b) = 4 en x = [[4/a−b]] (a ≠ b).\n\n## Gelyktydige vergelykings\n\nTwee vergelykings met twee onbekendes, x en y. Die oplossing is die **paar** (x; y) wat **albei** vergelykings waar maak.\n\n**Vervangingsmetode:** maak een veranderlike die onderwerp van een vergelyking en vervang dit in die ander. Vir y = 2x − 1 en 3x + y = 9: 3x + (2x − 1) = 9, dus 5x = 10, x = 2 en y = 2(2) − 1 = 3.\n\n**Eliminasiemetode:** maak die koëffisiënte van een veranderlike dieselfde (of teenoorgesteld) en trek die vergelykings van mekaar af (of tel hulle op). Vir x + y = 10 en x − y = 4: tel op, 2x = 14, dus x = 7 en y = 3.\n\n**Grafiese idee:** elke lineêre vergelyking is 'n reguit lyn. Die oplossing is die **snypunt** van die twee lyne. Ewewydige lyne (dieselfde gradiënt, ander y-afsnit) sny nooit nie, dus is daar dan **geen oplossing** nie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kontroleer (x; y) in **albei** oorspronklike vergelykings, nie net in die een wat jy laaste gebruik het nie.\n\n## Woordprobleme\n\n1. Definieer die onbekende(s), bv. \"Laat x = die breedte in meter\".\n2. Vertaal die woorde in 'n vergelyking: \"is\" beteken =, \"3 meer as\" beteken + 3, \"twee keer so oud\" beteken × 2.\n3. Los op.\n4. Antwoord in 'n volsin met eenhede en kyk of dit sin maak. 'n Lengte, ouderdom of aantal kan nie negatief wees nie, dus word 'n negatiewe oplossing **verwerp**.\n\nAlgemene tipes: ouderdomme, opeenvolgende getalle (x; x + 1; x + 2), kaartjies en geld (gelyktydige vergelykings), en die oppervlakte van 'n reghoek (gee dikwels 'n kwadratiese vergelyking).","en":"## What does \"solve\" mean?\n\nAn **equation** says that two expressions are equal, e.g. 3x − 4 = 11. To **solve** it, you find the value(s) of the variable that make the **left-hand side (LHS)** equal to the **right-hand side (RHS)**. The golden rule: **whatever you do to one side, you also do to the other side.** Check your answer by substituting it into the original equation.\n\n## Linear equations\n\nThe highest power of x is 1, so there is **one** solution.\n\n1. Remove brackets. Watch out for a minus in front of a bracket: −3(x − 1) = −3x + 3.\n2. Remove fractions: multiply **every term** on **both** sides by the **LCM** of the denominators.\n3. Bring the x-terms to one side and the numbers to the other side.\n4. Divide by the coefficient of x.\n\nExample: [[x/2]] + [[x−1/3]] = 3. The LCM is 6: 3x + 2(x − 1) = 18, so 5x − 2 = 18, 5x = 20 and x = 4.\n\n> **Common mistake:** multiplying only the fractions by the LCM and forgetting the RHS. *Every* term, including the number on the other side, is multiplied.\n\n**Variable in the denominator:** first write down the **restriction**, because a denominator may never be 0. For [[3/x−2]] = 1, x ≠ 2. Multiply by (x − 2): 3 = x − 2, so x = 5. If your answer is a restricted value, there is **no solution**.\n\n## Quadratic equations\n\nThe highest power of x is 2, so there are **at most two** solutions. We solve them by factorising.\n\n1. Write in **standard form** ax^{2} + bx + c = 0. One side **must be 0**.\n2. Factorise: common factor, difference of two squares or trinomial.\n3. Use the **zero product rule**: if A × B = 0, then A = 0 **or** B = 0.\n4. Solve each factor.\n\nExample: x^{2} − x − 12 = 0, so (x − 4)(x + 3) = 0 and x = 4 or x = −3.\n\n> **Common mistake:** dividing x^{2} = 5x by x. Then you lose the solution x = 0! Rather write x^{2} − 5x = 0, so x(x − 5) = 0 and x = 0 or x = 5.\n\n- x^{2} = 9 gives x = **±3** (x = 3 or x = −3), because (−3)^{2} = 9 too.\n- (x − 2)(x + 1) = 4 does **not** mean x − 2 = 4. The zero product rule only works when one side is 0. Multiply out and make one side 0: x^{2} − x − 6 = 0, so (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 and x = 3 or x = −2.\n\n## Literal equations\n\nA **literal equation** contains more than one letter, like a formula. \"Make a the **subject**\" means: get a on its own on one side of the equals sign. Use exactly the same steps as for an ordinary equation.\n\n- v = u + at, so v − u = at and a = [[v−u/t]]\n- If the subject appears **twice**, bring both terms to one side and **take it out as a common factor**: ax + 3 = bx + 7, so ax − bx = 4, x(a − b) = 4 and x = [[4/a−b]] (a ≠ b).\n\n## Simultaneous equations\n\nTwo equations with two unknowns, x and y. The solution is the **pair** (x; y) that makes **both** equations true.\n\n**Substitution method:** make one variable the subject of one equation and substitute it into the other. For y = 2x − 1 and 3x + y = 9: 3x + (2x − 1) = 9, so 5x = 10, x = 2 and y = 2(2) − 1 = 3.\n\n**Elimination method:** make the coefficients of one variable the same (or opposite) and subtract the equations (or add them). For x + y = 10 and x − y = 4: add, 2x = 14, so x = 7 and y = 3.\n\n**Graphical idea:** every linear equation is a straight line. The solution is the **point of intersection** of the two lines. Parallel lines (same gradient, different y-intercept) never intersect, so then there is **no solution**.\n\n> **Tip:** Check (x; y) in **both** original equations, not just in the one you used last.\n\n## Word problems\n\n1. Define the unknown(s), e.g. \"Let x = the width in metres\".\n2. Translate the words into an equation: \"is\" means =, \"3 more than\" means + 3, \"twice as old\" means × 2.\n3. Solve.\n4. Answer in a full sentence with units and check that it makes sense. A length, age or number of items cannot be negative, so a negative solution is **rejected**.\n\nCommon types: ages, consecutive numbers (x; x + 1; x + 2), tickets and money (simultaneous equations), and the area of a rectangle (often gives a quadratic equation)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vergelyking","en":"Equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Wiskundige sin wat sê dat twee uitdrukkings gelyk is, bv. 3x − 4 = 11.","en":"A mathematical sentence that says two expressions are equal, e.g. 3x − 4 = 11."}},{"term":{"af":"Oplossing (wortel)","en":"Solution (root)"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde van die veranderlike wat die LK gelyk maak aan die RK.","en":"A value of the variable that makes the LHS equal to the RHS."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre vergelyking","en":"Linear equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 1 is. Dit het een oplossing.","en":"An equation in which the highest power of the variable is 1. It has one solution."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwadratiese vergelyking","en":"Quadratic equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 2 is, bv. x² − 5x + 6 = 0. Dit het hoogstens twee oplossings.","en":"An equation in which the highest power of the variable is 2, e.g. x² − 5x + 6 = 0. It has at most two solutions."}},{"term":{"af":"Nulproduk-reël","en":"Zero product rule"},"def":{"af":"As A × B = 0, dan is A = 0 of B = 0. Werk net as een kant van die vergelyking 0 is.","en":"If A × B = 0, then A = 0 or B = 0. Only works if one side of the equation is 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking","en":"Literal equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking of formule met meer as een letter, bv. v = u + at.","en":"An equation or formula with more than one letter, e.g. v = u + at."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp van 'n formule","en":"Subject of a formula"},"def":{"af":"Die veranderlike wat alleen aan een kant van die gelykaanteken staan, bv. a in a = (v − u)/t.","en":"The variable that stands alone on one side of the equals sign, e.g. a in a = (v − u)/t."}},{"term":{"af":"Gelyktydige vergelykings","en":"Simultaneous equations"},"def":{"af":"Twee vergelykings met dieselfde twee onbekendes wat terselfdertyd waar moet wees. Die oplossing is 'n paar (x; y).","en":"Two equations with the same two unknowns that must be true at the same time. The solution is a pair (x; y)."}},{"term":{"af":"Beperking","en":"Restriction"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat die veranderlike nie mag hê nie, omdat 'n noemer dan 0 sou wees, bv. x ≠ 2.","en":"A value the variable may not take, because a denominator would then be 0, e.g. x ≠ 2."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lineêre vergelyking met breuke","en":"Linear equation with fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: (x + 2)/3 − (x − 1)/4 = 2","en":"Solve for x: (x + 2)/3 − (x − 1)/4 = 2"},"steps":[{"af":"Die KGV van 3 en 4 is 12. Vermenigvuldig elke term met 12: 12 × [[x+2/3]] − 12 × [[x−1/4]] = 12 × 2","en":"The LCM of 3 and 4 is 12. Multiply every term by 12: 12 × [[x+2/3]] − 12 × [[x−1/4]] = 12 × 2"},{"af":"4(x + 2) − 3(x − 1) = 24","en":"4(x + 2) − 3(x − 1) = 24"},{"af":"Verwyder hakies – pas op vir die minus voor die tweede hakie: 4x + 8 − 3x + 3 = 24","en":"Remove brackets – watch the minus in front of the second bracket: 4x + 8 − 3x + 3 = 24"},{"af":"x + 11 = 24, dus x = 13","en":"x + 11 = 24, so x = 13"},{"af":"Kontrole: LK = [[15/3]] − [[12/4]] = 5 − 3 = 2 = RK ✓","en":"Check: LHS = [[15/3]] − [[12/4]] = 5 − 3 = 2 = RHS ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 13","en":"x = 13"}},{"title":{"af":"Kwadratiese vergelyking deur faktorisering","en":"Quadratic equation by factorisation"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x: 2x² − 5x = 3","en":"Solve for x: 2x² − 5x = 3"},"steps":[{"af":"Maak een kant 0: 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 = 0","en":"Make one side 0: 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer die drieterm: (2x + 1)(x − 3) = 0. Kontrole: 2x^{2} − 6x + x − 3 = 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 ✓","en":"Factorise the trinomial: (2x + 1)(x − 3) = 0. Check: 2x^{2} − 6x + x − 3 = 2x^{2} − 5x − 3 ✓"},{"af":"Nulproduk-reël: 2x + 1 = 0 of x − 3 = 0","en":"Zero product rule: 2x + 1 = 0 or x − 3 = 0"},{"af":"x = −[[1/2]] of x = 3","en":"x = −[[1/2]] or x = 3"}],"answer":{"af":"x = −½ of x = 3","en":"x = −½ or x = 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking: verander die onderwerp","en":"Literal equation: change the subject"},"problem":{"af":"Maak i die onderwerp van die formule A = P(1 + in).","en":"Make i the subject of the formula A = P(1 + in)."},"steps":[{"af":"Vermenigvuldig uit: A = P + Pin","en":"Multiply out: A = P + Pin"},{"af":"Trek P aan albei kante af: A − P = Pin","en":"Subtract P on both sides: A − P = Pin"},{"af":"Deel albei kante deur Pn: i = [[A−P/Pn]]","en":"Divide both sides by Pn: i = [[A−P/Pn]]"},{"af":"Kontrole met getalle: as P = 1 000, n = 2 en i = 0,1, is A = 1 000(1 + 0,2) = 1 200. Dan is A − P = 200 en Pn = 2 000, dus i = [[200/2 000]] = 0,1 ✓","en":"Check with numbers: if P = 1 000, n = 2 and i = 0.1, then A = 1 000(1 + 0.2) = 1 200. Then A − P = 200 and Pn = 2 000, so i = [[200/2 000]] = 0.1 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"i = (A − P)/(Pn)","en":"i = (A − P)/(Pn)"}},{"title":{"af":"Gelyktydige vergelykings: rugbykaartjies","en":"Simultaneous equations: rugby tickets"},"problem":{"af":"By 'n rugbywedstryd op Brits kos 'n kaartjie vir 'n volwassene R x en vir 'n kind R y. Die Botha-gesin betaal R190 vir 3 volwassene- en 2 kinderkaartjies. Die Mokoena-gesin betaal R180 vir 2 volwassene- en 4 kinderkaartjies. Bepaal die prys van elke soort kaartjie.","en":"At a rugby match in Brits a ticket costs R x for an adult and R y for a child. The Botha family pays R190 for 3 adult and 2 child tickets. The Mokoena family pays R180 for 2 adult and 4 child tickets. Determine the price of each type of ticket."},"steps":[{"af":"Stel die vergelykings op: 3x + 2y = 190 … (1) en 2x + 4y = 180 … (2)","en":"Set up the equations: 3x + 2y = 190 … (1) and 2x + 4y = 180 … (2)"},{"af":"Deel (2) deur 2: x + 2y = 90 … (3)","en":"Divide (2) by 2: x + 2y = 90 … (3)"},{"af":"Eliminasie, (1) − (3): 2x = 100, dus x = 50","en":"Elimination, (1) − (3): 2x = 100, so x = 50"},{"af":"Vervang in (3): 50 + 2y = 90, dus 2y = 40 en y = 20","en":"Substitute into (3): 50 + 2y = 90, so 2y = 40 and y = 20"},{"af":"Kontrole in (2): 2(50) + 4(20) = 100 + 80 = 180 ✓. Grafies sou die twee lyne by (50; 20) sny.","en":"Check in (2): 2(50) + 4(20) = 100 + 80 = 180 ✓. Graphically the two lines would intersect at (50; 20)."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Volwassene se kaartjie kos R50 en 'n kind s'n R20.","en":"An adult ticket costs R50 and a child ticket R20."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van x² = 25 is slegs x = 5.","en":"The solution of x² = 25 is only x = 5."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. x² − 25 = 0 gee (x − 5)(x + 5) = 0, dus x = 5 of x = −5, want (−5)² = 25 ook.","en":"False. x² − 25 = 0 gives (x − 5)(x + 5) = 0, so x = 5 or x = −5, because (−5)² = 25 too."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelsel vergelykings het GEEN oplossing nie?","en":"Which system of equations has NO solution?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = −2x + 1","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = −2x + 1"},{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = 2x − 3","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = 2x − 3"},{"af":"y = x en y = −x","en":"y = x and y = −x"},{"af":"y = 3x − 1 en y = x + 3","en":"y = 3x − 1 and y = x + 3"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"y = 2x + 1 en y = 2x − 3 het dieselfde gradiënt (2) maar verskillende y-afsnitte, dus is die lyne ewewydig en sny nooit nie. Lyne met verskillende gradiënte sny altyd presies een keer.","en":"y = 2x + 1 and y = 2x − 3 have the same gradient (2) but different y-intercepts, so the lines are parallel and never intersect. Lines with different gradients always intersect exactly once."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"As (x − 3)(x + 5) = 0, dan is …","en":"If (x − 3)(x + 5) = 0, then …"},"options":[{"af":"x = 3 of x = −5","en":"x = 3 or x = −5"},{"af":"x = −3 of x = 5","en":"x = −3 or x = 5"},{"af":"x = 3 of x = 5","en":"x = 3 or x = 5"},{"af":"x = −15","en":"x = −15"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Nulproduk-reël: x − 3 = 0 of x + 5 = 0, dus x = 3 of x = −5. Die oplossing het die teenoorgestelde teken van die getal in die hakie.","en":"Zero product rule: x − 3 = 0 or x + 5 = 0, so x = 3 or x = −5. The solution has the opposite sign of the number in the bracket."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 5x − 7 = 2x + 8. x = ___","en":"Solve: 5x − 7 = 2x + 8. x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","x = 5"],"en":["5","x = 5"]},"explain":{"af":"5x − 2x = 8 + 7, dus 3x = 15 en x = 5. Kontrole: 25 − 7 = 18 en 10 + 8 = 18 ✓","en":"5x − 2x = 8 + 7, so 3x = 15 and x = 5. Check: 25 − 7 = 18 and 10 + 8 = 18 ✓"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["15","0,33","2,14"],"en":["15","0.33","2.14"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vergelyking by die tipe en metode.","en":"Match each equation to its type and method."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"4(x − 1) = 2x + 6","en":"4(x − 1) = 2x + 6"},"r":{"af":"Lineêr: verwyder hakies en isoleer x","en":"Linear: remove brackets and isolate x"}},{"l":{"af":"x² + 2x − 15 = 0","en":"x² + 2x − 15 = 0"},"r":{"af":"Kwadraties: faktoriseer en gebruik die nulproduk-reël","en":"Quadratic: factorise and use the zero product rule"}},{"l":{"af":"v = u + at (maak a die onderwerp)","en":"v = u + at (make a the subject)"},"r":{"af":"Letterlike vergelyking","en":"Literal equation"}},{"l":{"af":"x + y = 7 en x − y = 1","en":"x + y = 7 and x − y = 1"},"r":{"af":"Gelyktydig: eliminasie of vervanging","en":"Simultaneous: elimination or substitution"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die hoogste mag (1 of 2), die aantal onbekendes en of jy 'n formule herrangskik, bepaal die metode.","en":"The highest power (1 or 2), the number of unknowns and whether you are rearranging a formula determine the method."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: (2x + 1)/3 − (x − 2)/2 = 2","en":"Solve: (2x + 1)/3 − (x − 2)/2 = 2"},"options":[{"af":"x = 16","en":"x = 16"},{"af":"x = −6","en":"x = −6"},{"af":"x = 6","en":"x = 6"},{"af":"x = 4","en":"x = 4"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"KGV = 6: 2(2x + 1) − 3(x − 2) = 12, dus 4x + 2 − 3x + 6 = 12, x + 8 = 12 en x = 4. x = 16 kom van −3(x − 2) = −3x − 6 (tekenfout), en x = −6 as jy vergeet om die RK met 6 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"LCM = 6: 2(2x + 1) − 3(x − 2) = 12, so 4x + 2 − 3x + 6 = 12, x + 8 = 12 and x = 4. x = 16 comes from −3(x − 2) = −3x − 6 (sign error), and x = −6 if you forget to multiply the RHS by 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: x² − 7x + 12 = 0. Die kleinste oplossing is x = ___","en":"Solve: x² − 7x + 12 = 0. The smallest solution is x = ___"},"answers":{"af":["3","x = 3"],"en":["3","x = 3"]},"explain":{"af":"Soek twee getalle met produk 12 en som −7: −3 en −4. (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, dus x = 3 of x = 4. Die kleinste is 3.","en":"Look for two numbers with product 12 and sum −7: −3 and −4. (x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, so x = 3 or x = 4. The smallest is 3."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−3","−4","4"],"en":["−3","−4","4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: x² = 6x","en":"Solve: x² = 6x"},"options":[{"af":"x = 6","en":"x = 6"},{"af":"x = 0 of x = 6","en":"x = 0 or x = 6"},{"af":"x = 0 of x = −6","en":"x = 0 or x = −6"},{"af":"x = ±√6","en":"x = ±√6"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"x² − 6x = 0, dus x(x − 6) = 0 en x = 0 of x = 6. As jy deur x deel, kry jy net x = 6 en verloor jy x = 0.","en":"x² − 6x = 0, so x(x − 6) = 0 and x = 0 or x = 6. If you divide by x you only get x = 6 and lose x = 0."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy y die onderwerp van 4x − 2y = 10 maak, kry jy y = 2x − 5.","en":"If you make y the subject of 4x − 2y = 10, you get y = 2x − 5."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. −2y = 10 − 4x. Deel elke term deur −2: y = −5 + 2x = 2x − 5.","en":"True. −2y = 10 − 4x. Divide every term by −2: y = −5 + 2x = 2x − 5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los gelyktydig op: x + y = 9 en 2x − y = 3","en":"Solve simultaneously: x + y = 9 and 2x − y = 3"},"options":[{"af":"x = 5 en y = 4","en":"x = 5 and y = 4"},{"af":"x = 12 en y = −3","en":"x = 12 and y = −3"},{"af":"x = 4 en y = 5","en":"x = 4 and y = 5"},{"af":"x = 4 en y = −5","en":"x = 4 and y = −5"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Tel die vergelykings op: 3x = 12, dus x = 4. Dan 4 + y = 9, dus y = 5. Kontrole: 2(4) − 5 = 3 ✓. x = 12 vergeet om deur 3 te deel; y = −5 is 'n tekenfout in 8 − y = 3.","en":"Add the equations: 3x = 12, so x = 4. Then 4 + y = 9, so y = 5. Check: 2(4) − 5 = 3 ✓. x = 12 forgets to divide by 3; y = −5 is a sign error in 8 − y = 3."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Maak x die onderwerp van ax − b = cx + d.","en":"Make x the subject of ax − b = cx + d."},"options":[{"af":"x = (b + d)/(a − c)","en":"x = (b + d)/(a − c)"},{"af":"x = (d − b)/(a − c)","en":"x = (d − b)/(a − c)"},{"af":"x = (b + d)/(a + c)","en":"x = (b + d)/(a + c)"},{"af":"x = (b + d)/(c − a)","en":"x = (b + d)/(c − a)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bring die x-terme na links en die res na regs: ax − cx = d + b. Haal x uit as gemene faktor: x(a − c) = b + d, dus x = (b + d)/(a − c). Die ander opsies het 'n tekenfout wanneer 'n term oorgebring word.","en":"Bring the x-terms to the left and the rest to the right: ax − cx = d + b. Take x out as a common factor: x(a − c) = b + d, so x = (b + d)/(a − c). The other options have a sign error when a term is moved across."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die lengte van 'n reghoekige braai-area is 3 m meer as die breedte. Die oppervlakte is 28 m². Hoe breed is die braai-area? ___ m","en":"The length of a rectangular braai area is 3 m more than its width. The area is 28 m². How wide is the braai area? ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["4","4 m","x = 4"],"en":["4","4 m","x = 4"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat die breedte x wees. x(x + 3) = 28, dus x² + 3x − 28 = 0 en (x + 7)(x − 4) = 0. x = −7 word verwerp ('n breedte kan nie negatief wees nie), dus is die breedte 4 m (en die lengte 7 m).","en":"Let the width be x. x(x + 3) = 28, so x² + 3x − 28 = 0 and (x + 7)(x − 4) = 0. x = −7 is rejected (a width cannot be negative), so the width is 4 m (and the length 7 m)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7","−7","25"],"en":["7","−7","25"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Ma is nou drie keer so oud as haar seun. Oor 12 jaar sal sy twee keer so oud as hy wees. Hoe oud is die seun nou? ___ jaar","en":"A mother is now three times as old as her son. In 12 years she will be twice as old as he is. How old is the son now? ___ years"},"answers":{"af":["12","12 jaar"],"en":["12","12 years"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat die seun nou x jaar oud wees; ma is 3x. Oor 12 jaar: 3x + 12 = 2(x + 12), dus 3x + 12 = 2x + 24 en x = 12. Die seun is 12 en ma 36 (oor 12 jaar: 48 = 2 × 24 ✓).","en":"Let the son now be x years old; the mother is 3x. In 12 years: 3x + 12 = 2(x + 12), so 3x + 12 = 2x + 24 and x = 12. The son is 12 and the mother 36 (in 12 years: 48 = 2 × 24 ✓)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["36","24","48"],"en":["36","24","48"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By 'n kerkbasaar op Brits word koeksisters teen R5 elk en pannekoeke teen R8 elk verkoop. Altesaam 120 items word verkoop vir R816. Hoeveel pannekoeke is verkoop?","en":"At a church fête in Brits koeksisters are sold at R5 each and pancakes at R8 each. Altogether 120 items are sold for R816. How many pancakes were sold?"},"options":[{"af":"48","en":"48"},{"af":"60","en":"60"},{"af":"72","en":"72"},{"af":"102","en":"102"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Laat k = koeksisters en p = pannekoeke. k + p = 120 en 5k + 8p = 816. Vervang k = 120 − p: 600 − 5p + 8p = 816, dus 3p = 216 en p = 72 (en k = 48). 48 is die aantal koeksisters, 60 is net 120 ÷ 2, en 102 = 816 ÷ 8 ignoreer die koeksisters.","en":"Let k = koeksisters and p = pancakes. k + p = 120 and 5k + 8p = 816. Substitute k = 120 − p: 600 − 5p + 8p = 816, so 3p = 216 and p = 72 (and k = 48). 48 is the number of koeksisters, 60 is just 120 ÷ 2, and 102 = 816 ÷ 8 ignores the koeksisters."}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-ongelykhede","title":{"af":"Lineêre ongelykhede","en":"Linear inequalities"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lineêre en saamgestelde ongelykhede kan oplos, weet wanneer om die teken om te draai, en die oplossing op 'n getallelyn en in intervalnotasie kan voorstel.","en":"You will be able to solve linear and compound inequalities, know when to reverse the sign, and represent the solution on a number line and in interval notation."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n ongelykheid?\n\n'n **Ongelykheid** vergelyk twee uitdrukkings met een van die simbole hieronder. 'n **Lineêre ongelykheid** het x tot die mag 1, bv. 3x − 2 > 7. Die oplossing is gewoonlik 'n **interval** (oneindig baie getalle), nie net een getal nie.\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis | Woorde in vrae |\n|---|---|---|\n| < | kleiner as | minder as |\n| > | groter as | meer as |\n| ≤ | kleiner as of gelyk aan | hoogstens, nie meer as nie |\n| ≥ | groter as of gelyk aan | minstens, ten minste, nie minder as nie |\n\n## Los 'n lineêre ongelykheid op\n\nWerk presies soos met 'n vergelyking: verwyder hakies en breuke, bring die x-terme na een kant en die getalle na die ander kant, en deel deur die koëffisiënt van x. Daar is net **een** groot verskil:\n\n> **Onthou!** As jy albei kante met 'n **negatiewe** getal **vermenigvuldig of deel**, moet jy die ongelykheidsteken **omdraai**.\n\n**Hoekom?** 2 < 5 is waar. Vermenigvuldig albei kante met −1 en jy kry −2 en −5. Op die getallelyn lê −2 regs van −5, dus is −2 > −5. Die volgorde het omgedraai.\n\n- **Optel of aftrek** (selfs van 'n negatiewe getal): **moenie** omdraai nie. x − 5 > −2 gee x > 3.\n- **Vermenigvuldig of deel met 'n positiewe getal:** **moenie** omdraai nie.\n- **Ruil die twee kante om:** dan draai die teken ook om. 4 > x beteken dieselfde as x < 4.\n\nVoorbeeld: 5 − 2x > 11, dus −2x > 6. Deel deur −2 en draai om: x < −3.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** die teken omdraai net omdat daar 'n negatiewe getal in die ongelykheid staan. Jy draai slegs om as jy met 'n negatiewe getal **vermenigvuldig of deel**.\n\n## Getallelyn\n\n- **Oop kolletjie (○):** die getal is **nie ingesluit** nie (> of <).\n- **Ingekleurde kolletjie (●):** die getal **is ingesluit** (≤ of ≥).\n- Die pyl wys na **regs** vir \"groter as\" en na **links** vir \"kleiner as\". By 'n saamgestelde ongelykheid trek jy 'n dik lyn tussen die twee kolletjies.\n\n## Intervalnotasie\n\n- **Ronde hakie ( ):** die eindpunt is **nie** ingesluit nie (> of <).\n- **Vierkantige hakie [ ]:** die eindpunt **is** ingesluit (≤ of ≥).\n- By ∞ of −∞ staan **altyd** 'n ronde hakie, want oneindig is nie 'n getal wat jy kan bereik nie.\n- Skryf die kleinste getal eerste, met 'n kommapunt tussenin.\n\n| Ongelykheid | Getallelyn | Intervalnotasie |\n|---|---|---|\n| *x* > 3 | ○ by 3, pyl na regs | (3 ; ∞) |\n| *x* ≤ −1 | ● by −1, pyl na links | (−∞ ; −1] |\n| −2 ≤ *x* < 4 | ● by −2, ○ by 4 | [−2 ; 4) |\n| 1 < *x* ≤ 6 | ○ by 1, ● by 6 | (1 ; 6] |\n\n## Saamgestelde ongelykhede\n\n'n **Saamgestelde ongelykheid** soos −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7 het drie dele. Doen elke bewerking aan **al drie** dele:\n\n- Trek 1 af: −4 ≤ 2x < 6\n- Deel deur 2: −2 ≤ x < 3, dus x ∈ [−2 ; 3)\n\nAs jy deur 'n negatiewe getal deel, draai **albei** tekens om en herskryf dan sodat die kleinste getal links staan:\n\n−7 < 5 − 3x ≤ 11 → trek 5 af: −12 < −3x ≤ 6 → deel deur −3: 4 > x ≥ −2 → herskryf: −2 ≤ x < 4, dus x ∈ [−2 ; 4)\n\n> **Algemene fout:** net een van die twee tekens omdraai, of net die middelste deel deur −3 deel. Al drie dele kry dieselfde bewerking en albei tekens draai om.\n\n## Heelgetal-oplossings\n\nAs die vraag sê x ∈ ℤ (heelgetalle) of x ∈ ℕ (natuurlike getalle), lys jy net daardie getalle in die interval. Kyk mooi na die eindpunte: die eindpunt is ingesluit by ≤ en ≥, maar uitgesluit by > en <.\n\nVir −2 ≤ x < 3 en x ∈ ℤ is x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2. Dit is vyf heelgetalle, want 3 is nie ingesluit nie.\n\n## Breuke en woordprobleme\n\n- **Breuke:** vermenigvuldig elke term met die KGV van die noemers. Die KGV is positief, dus bly die teken dieselfde.\n- **Woordprobleme:** definieer die onbekende, kies die regte simbool (minstens → ≥, hoogstens → ≤), los op en **rond logies af**. Met hoogstens R200 vir items van R30 elk is 30x ≤ 200, dus x ≤ 6,67 en jy kan hoogstens **6** koop (rond af). As jy minstens 'n sekere bedrag moet insamel, rond jy **op**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Toets jou antwoord met 'n getal binne die interval (dit moet werk) en een buite die interval (dit moet nie werk nie).","en":"## What is an inequality?\n\nAn **inequality** compares two expressions using one of the symbols below. A **linear inequality** has x to the power 1, e.g. 3x − 2 > 7. The solution is usually an **interval** (infinitely many numbers), not just one number.\n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Words in questions |\n|---|---|---|\n| < | less than | fewer than |\n| > | greater than | more than |\n| ≤ | less than or equal to | at most, not more than |\n| ≥ | greater than or equal to | at least, no less than |\n\n## Solving a linear inequality\n\nWork exactly as with an equation: remove brackets and fractions, bring the x-terms to one side and the numbers to the other side, and divide by the coefficient of x. There is only **one** big difference:\n\n> **Remember!** If you **multiply or divide** both sides by a **negative** number, you must **reverse** the inequality sign.\n\n**Why?** 2 < 5 is true. Multiply both sides by −1 and you get −2 and −5. On the number line −2 lies to the right of −5, so −2 > −5. The order has reversed.\n\n- **Adding or subtracting** (even a negative number): do **not** reverse.\n- **Multiplying or dividing by a positive number:** do **not** reverse.\n- **Swapping the two sides:** the sign also turns around. 4 > x means the same as x < 4.\n\nFor example, x − 5 > −2 gives x > 3 (no reversing). And 5 − 2x > 11 gives −2x > 6. Divide by −2 and reverse: x < −3.\n\n> **Common mistake:** reversing the sign just because there is a negative number in the inequality. You only reverse when you **multiply or divide** by a negative number.\n\n## Number line\n\n- **Open dot (○):** the number is **not included** (> or <).\n- **Closed (shaded) dot (●):** the number **is included** (≤ or ≥).\n- The arrow points **right** for \"greater than\" and **left** for \"less than\". For a compound inequality you draw a thick line between the two dots.\n\n## Interval notation\n\n- **Round bracket ( ):** the endpoint is **not** included (> or <).\n- **Square bracket [ ]:** the endpoint **is** included (≤ or ≥).\n- At ∞ or −∞ there is **always** a round bracket, because infinity is not a number you can reach.\n- Write the smallest number first, with a semicolon in between.\n\n| Inequality | Number line | Interval notation |\n|---|---|---|\n| *x* > 3 | ○ at 3, arrow right | (3 ; ∞) |\n| *x* ≤ −1 | ● at −1, arrow left | (−∞ ; −1] |\n| −2 ≤ *x* < 4 | ● at −2, ○ at 4 | [−2 ; 4) |\n| 1 < *x* ≤ 6 | ○ at 1, ● at 6 | (1 ; 6] |\n\n## Compound inequalities\n\nA **compound inequality** such as −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7 has three parts. Do every operation to **all three** parts:\n\n- Subtract 1: −4 ≤ 2x < 6\n- Divide by 2: −2 ≤ x < 3, so x ∈ [−2 ; 3)\n\nIf you divide by a negative number, reverse **both** signs and then rewrite so that the smallest number is on the left:\n\n−7 < 5 − 3x ≤ 11 → subtract 5: −12 < −3x ≤ 6 → divide by −3: 4 > x ≥ −2 → rewrite: −2 ≤ x < 4, so x ∈ [−2 ; 4)\n\n> **Common mistake:** reversing only one of the two signs, or dividing only the middle part by −3. All three parts get the same operation and both signs reverse.\n\n## Integer solutions\n\nIf the question says x ∈ ℤ (integers) or x ∈ ℕ (natural numbers), you list only those numbers in the interval. Look carefully at the endpoints: the endpoint is included with ≤ and ≥, but excluded with > and <.\n\nFor −2 ≤ x < 3 and x ∈ ℤ, x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2. That is five integers, because 3 is not included.\n\n## Fractions and word problems\n\n- **Fractions:** multiply every term by the LCM of the denominators. The LCM is positive, so the sign stays the same.\n- **Word problems:** define the unknown, choose the correct symbol (at least → ≥, at most → ≤), solve and **round logically**. With at most R200 for items of R30 each, 30x ≤ 200, so x ≤ 6.67 and you can buy at most **6** (round down). If you must raise at least a certain amount, you round **up**.\n\n> **Tip:** Test your answer with a number inside the interval (it must work) and one outside the interval (it must not work)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Ongelykheid","en":"Inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Wiskundige sin wat twee uitdrukkings met <, >, ≤ of ≥ vergelyk.","en":"A mathematical sentence that compares two expressions using <, >, ≤ or ≥."}},{"term":{"af":"Lineêre ongelykheid","en":"Linear inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Ongelykheid waarin die hoogste mag van die veranderlike 1 is, bv. 3x − 2 > 7.","en":"An inequality in which the highest power of the variable is 1, e.g. 3x − 2 > 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde ongelykheid","en":"Compound inequality"},"def":{"af":"'n Ongelykheid met twee ongelykheidstekens en drie dele, bv. −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7.","en":"An inequality with two inequality signs and three parts, e.g. −3 ≤ 2x + 1 < 7."}},{"term":{"af":"Intervalnotasie","en":"Interval notation"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort manier om 'n versameling reële getalle met hakies te skryf, bv. [−2 ; 3). Ronde hakie: nie ingesluit; vierkantige hakie: ingesluit.","en":"A short way of writing a set of real numbers with brackets, e.g. [−2 ; 3). Round bracket: not included; square bracket: included."}},{"term":{"af":"Getallelyn","en":"Number line"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn waarop die oplossing van 'n ongelykheid met kolletjies en 'n pyl of lyn gewys word.","en":"A line on which the solution of an inequality is shown with dots and an arrow or line."}},{"term":{"af":"Oop en ingekleurde kolletjie","en":"Open and closed dot"},"def":{"af":"Oop kolletjie (○): die getal is nie ingesluit nie (< of >). Ingekleurde kolletjie (●): die getal is ingesluit (≤ of ≥).","en":"Open dot (○): the number is not included (< or >). Closed dot (●): the number is included (≤ or ≥)."}},{"term":{"af":"Oneindig (∞)","en":"Infinity (∞)"},"def":{"af":"Wys dat die interval sonder einde aangaan. Kry altyd 'n ronde hakie, bv. (3 ; ∞).","en":"Shows that the interval goes on without end. Always gets a round bracket, e.g. (3 ; ∞)."}},{"term":{"af":"Heelgetalle (ℤ)","en":"Integers (ℤ)"},"def":{"af":"Die getalle …; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; … sonder breuke of desimale.","en":"The numbers …; −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; … without fractions or decimals."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Deel deur 'n negatiewe getal","en":"Dividing by a negative number"},"problem":{"af":"Los op: 3 − 2x ≥ 11. Gee die oplossing in intervalnotasie en beskryf dit op 'n getallelyn.","en":"Solve: 3 − 2x ≥ 11. Give the solution in interval notation and describe it on a number line."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 3 aan albei kante af: −2x ≥ 8","en":"Subtract 3 on both sides: −2x ≥ 8"},{"af":"Deel albei kante deur −2. Ons deel deur 'n negatiewe getal, dus draai die teken om: x ≤ −4","en":"Divide both sides by −2. We are dividing by a negative number, so the sign reverses: x ≤ −4"},{"af":"Intervalnotasie: x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. Die vierkantige hakie wys dat −4 ingesluit is; by −∞ is daar altyd 'n ronde hakie.","en":"Interval notation: x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. The square bracket shows that −4 is included; at −∞ there is always a round bracket."},{"af":"Getallelyn: 'n ingekleurde kolletjie (●) by −4 en 'n pyl na links.","en":"Number line: a closed dot (●) at −4 and an arrow to the left."},{"af":"Kontrole met x = −5: 3 − 2(−5) = 13 en 13 ≥ 11 ✓","en":"Check with x = −5: 3 − 2(−5) = 13 and 13 ≥ 11 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"x ≤ −4, d.w.s. x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]","en":"x ≤ −4, i.e. x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]"}},{"title":{"af":"Ongelykheid met breuke","en":"Inequality with fractions"},"problem":{"af":"Los op: (x − 1)/3 − (x + 2)/2 < 1","en":"Solve: (x − 1)/3 − (x + 2)/2 < 1"},"steps":[{"af":"Die KGV is 6 (positief, dus bly die teken dieselfde): 6 × [[x−1/3]] − 6 × [[x+2/2]] < 6 × 1","en":"The LCM is 6 (positive, so the sign stays the same): 6 × [[x−1/3]] − 6 × [[x+2/2]] < 6 × 1"},{"af":"2(x − 1) − 3(x + 2) < 6","en":"2(x − 1) − 3(x + 2) < 6"},{"af":"2x − 2 − 3x − 6 < 6, dus −x − 8 < 6","en":"2x − 2 − 3x − 6 < 6, so −x − 8 < 6"},{"af":"Tel 8 by: −x < 14","en":"Add 8: −x < 14"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met −1 en draai die teken om: x > −14, dus x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)","en":"Multiply by −1 and reverse the sign: x > −14, so x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)"}],"answer":{"af":"x > −14, d.w.s. x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)","en":"x > −14, i.e. x ∈ (−14 ; ∞)"}},{"title":{"af":"Saamgestelde ongelykheid en heelgetalle","en":"Compound inequality and integers"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Los op: 1 ≤ 7 − 2x < 13 en gee die antwoord in intervalnotasie. (b) Lys die heelgetalle wat aan die ongelykheid voldoen.","en":"(a) Solve: 1 ≤ 7 − 2x < 13 and give the answer in interval notation. (b) List the integers that satisfy the inequality."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 7 van al drie dele af: −6 ≤ −2x < 6","en":"Subtract 7 from all three parts: −6 ≤ −2x < 6"},{"af":"Deel al drie dele deur −2 en draai albei tekens om: 3 ≥ x > −3","en":"Divide all three parts by −2 and reverse both signs: 3 ≥ x > −3"},{"af":"Herskryf met die kleinste getal links: −3 < x ≤ 3, dus x ∈ (−3 ; 3]","en":"Rewrite with the smallest number on the left: −3 < x ≤ 3, so x ∈ (−3 ; 3]"},{"af":"(b) −3 is nie ingesluit nie, maar 3 wel: x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3","en":"(b) −3 is not included, but 3 is: x = −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3"}],"answer":{"af":"x ∈ (−3 ; 3]; heelgetalle: −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3","en":"x ∈ (−3 ; 3]; integers: −2; −1; 0; 1; 2; 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Woordprobleem: hoeveel kan jy koop?","en":"Word problem: how many can you buy?"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho het R350. Hy koop 'n kaartjie vir 'n rugbywedstryd op Loftus in Pretoria vir R89 en wil met die res sakkies biltong teen R27 elk koop. Hoeveel sakkies kan hy hoogstens koop?","en":"Sipho has R350. He buys a ticket for a rugby match at Loftus in Pretoria for R89 and wants to buy packets of biltong at R27 each with the rest. What is the greatest number of packets he can buy?"},"steps":[{"af":"Laat b die aantal sakkies wees. Die totale koste mag hoogstens R350 wees: 89 + 27b ≤ 350","en":"Let b be the number of packets. The total cost may be at most R350: 89 + 27b ≤ 350"},{"af":"Trek 89 af: 27b ≤ 261","en":"Subtract 89: 27b ≤ 261"},{"af":"Deel deur 27 (positief, dus geen omdraai nie): b ≤ 9,67","en":"Divide by 27 (positive, so no reversing): b ≤ 9.67"},{"af":"b moet 'n heelgetal wees, dus rond ons AF: b = 9. Kontrole: 89 + 27(9) = R332 ≤ R350 ✓, maar 89 + 27(10) = R359 is te veel.","en":"b must be a whole number, so we round DOWN: b = 9. Check: 89 + 27(9) = R332 ≤ R350 ✓, but 89 + 27(10) = R359 is too much."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy kan hoogstens 9 sakkies biltong koop.","en":"He can buy at most 9 packets of biltong."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter intervalnotasie stel x ≥ 4 voor?","en":"Which interval notation represents x ≥ 4?"},"options":[{"af":"(4 ; ∞)","en":"(4 ; ∞)"},{"af":"[4 ; ∞)","en":"[4 ; ∞)"},{"af":"[4 ; ∞]","en":"[4 ; ∞]"},{"af":"(−∞ ; 4]","en":"(−∞ ; 4]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"4 is ingesluit (≥), dus 'n vierkantige hakie by 4. By ∞ is daar altyd 'n ronde hakie. (−∞ ; 4] sou x ≤ 4 wees.","en":"4 is included (≥), so a square bracket at 4. At ∞ there is always a round bracket. (−∞ ; 4] would be x ≤ 4."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy albei kante van 'n ongelykheid met −3 vermenigvuldig, moet jy die ongelykheidsteken omdraai.","en":"If you multiply both sides of an inequality by −3, you must reverse the inequality sign."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Vermenigvuldig of deel jy met 'n negatiewe getal, draai die teken om, bv. 2 < 5 maar −6 > −15.","en":"True. When you multiply or divide by a negative number, the sign reverses, e.g. 2 < 5 but −6 > −15."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van 'n ongelykheid word op 'n getallelyn gewys met 'n oop kolletjie by −1 en 'n pyl na regs. Watter ongelykheid is dit?","en":"The solution of an inequality is shown on a number line with an open dot at −1 and an arrow to the right. Which inequality is it?"},"options":[{"af":"x ≥ −1","en":"x ≥ −1"},{"af":"x < −1","en":"x < −1"},{"af":"x ≤ −1","en":"x ≤ −1"},{"af":"x > −1","en":"x > −1"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Oop kolletjie beteken −1 is nie ingesluit nie (> of <), en 'n pyl na regs beteken groter as. Dus x > −1. 'n Ingekleurde kolletjie sou ≥ wees.","en":"An open dot means −1 is not included (> or <), and an arrow to the right means greater than. So x > −1. A closed dot would be ≥."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ongelykheid by die regte intervalnotasie.","en":"Match each inequality to the correct interval notation."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"−2 < x ≤ 5","en":"−2 < x ≤ 5"},"r":{"af":"(−2 ; 5]","en":"(−2 ; 5]"}},{"l":{"af":"−2 ≤ x < 5","en":"−2 ≤ x < 5"},"r":{"af":"[−2 ; 5)","en":"[−2 ; 5)"}},{"l":{"af":"x < 5","en":"x < 5"},"r":{"af":"(−∞ ; 5)","en":"(−∞ ; 5)"}},{"l":{"af":"x ≥ −2","en":"x ≥ −2"},"r":{"af":"[−2 ; ∞)","en":"[−2 ; ∞)"}}],"explain":{"af":"< en > kry ronde hakies, ≤ en ≥ kry vierkantige hakies, en ∞ kry altyd 'n ronde hakie.","en":"< and > get round brackets, ≤ and ≥ get square brackets, and ∞ always gets a round bracket."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: x − 7 > −3","en":"Solve: x − 7 > −3"},"options":[{"af":"x > 4","en":"x > 4"},{"af":"x < 4","en":"x < 4"},{"af":"x > −10","en":"x > −10"},{"af":"x > 10","en":"x > 10"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Tel 7 aan albei kante by: x > −3 + 7 = 4. Jy het nie met 'n negatiewe getal vermenigvuldig of gedeel nie, dus draai die teken NIE om nie.","en":"Add 7 on both sides: x > −3 + 7 = 4. You did not multiply or divide by a negative number, so the sign does NOT reverse."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 2x + 5 ≤ 17. Die grootste waarde wat x kan hê, is ___","en":"Solve: 2x + 5 ≤ 17. The greatest value x can have is ___"},"answers":{"af":["6","x = 6"],"en":["6","x = 6"]},"explain":{"af":"2x ≤ 12, dus x ≤ 6. Omdat dit ≤ is, is 6 self ingesluit, dus is 6 die grootste waarde.","en":"2x ≤ 12, so x ≤ 6. Because it is ≤, 6 itself is included, so 6 is the greatest value."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11","5","12"],"en":["11","5","12"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: 4 − 3x < 10","en":"Solve: 4 − 3x < 10"},"options":[{"af":"x < −2","en":"x < −2"},{"af":"x > 2","en":"x > 2"},{"af":"x > −2","en":"x > −2"},{"af":"x < 2","en":"x < 2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"−3x < 6. Deel deur −3 en draai die teken om: x > −2. x < −2 is die antwoord as jy vergeet om om te draai.","en":"−3x < 6. Divide by −3 and reverse the sign: x > −2. x < −2 is the answer if you forget to reverse."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die oplossing van −2x ≥ 8 is x ∈ [−4 ; ∞).","en":"The solution of −2x ≥ 8 is x ∈ [−4 ; ∞)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Deel deur −2 en draai om: x ≤ −4, dus x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. Die stelling het vergeet om die teken om te draai.","en":"False. Divide by −2 and reverse: x ≤ −4, so x ∈ (−∞ ; −4]. The statement forgot to reverse the sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel heelgetalle voldoen aan −1 < 3x + 2 ≤ 14? ___","en":"How many integers satisfy −1 < 3x + 2 ≤ 14? ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"explain":{"af":"Trek 2 af: −3 < 3x ≤ 12. Deel deur 3: −1 < x ≤ 4. −1 is nie ingesluit nie, 4 wel: 0; 1; 2; 3; 4 – dit is 5 heelgetalle.","en":"Subtract 2: −3 < 3x ≤ 12. Divide by 3: −1 < x ≤ 4. −1 is not included, 4 is: 0; 1; 2; 3; 4 – that is 5 integers."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","6","3"],"en":["4","6","3"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: −4 ≤ 2x − 6 < 8","en":"Solve: −4 ≤ 2x − 6 < 8"},"options":[{"af":"−5 ≤ x < 1","en":"−5 ≤ x < 1"},{"af":"1 < x ≤ 7","en":"1 < x ≤ 7"},{"af":"2 ≤ x < 14","en":"2 ≤ x < 14"},{"af":"1 ≤ x < 7","en":"1 ≤ x < 7"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tel 6 by al drie dele: 2 ≤ 2x < 14. Deel deur 2: 1 ≤ x < 7. −5 ≤ x < 1 trek 6 af in plaas daarvan om by te tel, 2 ≤ x < 14 vergeet om deur 2 te deel, en 1 < x ≤ 7 het die tekens omgeruil.","en":"Add 6 to all three parts: 2 ≤ 2x < 14. Divide by 2: 1 ≤ x < 7. −5 ≤ x < 1 subtracts 6 instead of adding, 2 ≤ x < 14 forgets to divide by 2, and 1 < x ≤ 7 swaps the signs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op: (x + 3)/2 − (x − 1)/5 ≥ 2","en":"Solve: (x + 3)/2 − (x − 1)/5 ≥ 2"},"options":[{"af":"x ≥ 1","en":"x ≥ 1"},{"af":"x ≤ 1","en":"x ≤ 1"},{"af":"x ≥ −5","en":"x ≥ −5"},{"af":"x ≥ 7/3","en":"x ≥ 7/3"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"KGV = 10: 5(x + 3) − 2(x − 1) ≥ 20, dus 5x + 15 − 2x + 2 ≥ 20, 3x ≥ 3 en x ≥ 1. x ≥ 7/3 kom van −2(x − 1) = −2x − 2 (tekenfout), en x ≥ −5 as jy vergeet om die RK met 10 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"LCM = 10: 5(x + 3) − 2(x − 1) ≥ 20, so 5x + 15 − 2x + 2 ≥ 20, 3x ≥ 3 and x ≥ 1. x ≥ 7/3 comes from −2(x − 1) = −2x − 2 (sign error), and x ≥ −5 if you forget to multiply the RHS by 10."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op: 2 < 5 − 3x ≤ 14. Wat is die kleinste heelgetal wat aan die ongelykheid voldoen? ___","en":"Solve: 2 < 5 − 3x ≤ 14. What is the smallest integer that satisfies the inequality? ___"},"answers":{"af":["−3","-3","x = −3","x = -3"],"en":["−3","-3","x = −3","x = -3"]},"explain":{"af":"Trek 5 af: −3 < −3x ≤ 9. Deel deur −3 en draai albei tekens om: 1 > x ≥ −3, dus −3 ≤ x < 1. −3 is ingesluit, dus is die kleinste heelgetal −3.","en":"Subtract 5: −3 < −3x ≤ 9. Divide by −3 and reverse both signs: 1 > x ≥ −3, so −3 ≤ x < 1. −3 is included, so the smallest integer is −3."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−2","1","3"],"en":["−2","1","3"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is 3x − 2 > 7 EN 2x + 1 ≤ 15 albei waar?","en":"For which values of x are 3x − 2 > 7 AND 2x + 1 ≤ 15 both true?"},"options":[{"af":"[3 ; 7)","en":"[3 ; 7)"},{"af":"(3 ; 7]","en":"(3 ; 7]"},{"af":"(3 ; 7)","en":"(3 ; 7)"},{"af":"[3 ; 7]","en":"[3 ; 7]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"3x > 9 gee x > 3 (3 nie ingesluit nie), en 2x ≤ 14 gee x ≤ 7 (7 ingesluit). Albei saam: 3 < x ≤ 7, dus (3 ; 7].","en":"3x > 9 gives x > 3 (3 not included), and 2x ≤ 14 gives x ≤ 7 (7 included). Both together: 3 < x ≤ 7, so (3 ; 7]."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Taxi-eienaar op Brits het elke dag R480 se koste (brandstof en die bestuurder se loon). Elke passasier betaal R26 vir 'n rit Pretoria toe. Wat is die minste aantal passasiers wat hy per dag moet vervoer om 'n wins te maak? ___","en":"A taxi owner in Brits has R480 in costs every day (fuel and the driver's wage). Each passenger pays R26 for a trip to Pretoria. What is the least number of passengers he must transport per day to make a profit? ___"},"answers":{"af":["19","19 passasiers"],"en":["19","19 passengers"]},"explain":{"af":"Wins beteken inkomste > koste: 26p > 480, dus p > 18,46. Passasiers is heelgetalle, dus rond jy OP: 19. Kontrole: 18 × R26 = R468 (verlies), 19 × R26 = R494 (wins).","en":"Profit means income > costs: 26p > 480, so p > 18.46. Passengers are whole numbers, so you round UP: 19. Check: 18 × R26 = R468 (loss), 19 × R26 = R494 (profit)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["18","18,46","20"],"en":["18","18.46","20"]}}}]},{"id":"w10-t1-trigonometrie","title":{"af":"Trigonometrie: verhoudings en spesiale hoeke","en":"Trigonometry: ratios and special angles"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sin, cos, tan en hul resiproke in reghoekige driehoeke en op die Cartesiese vlak kan gebruik, spesiale hoeke sonder 'n sakrekenaar kan uitwerk en eenvoudige trigonometriese vergelykings kan oplos.","en":"You will be able to use sin, cos, tan and their reciprocals in right-angled triangles and on the Cartesian plane, work out special angles without a calculator and solve simple trigonometric equations."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie trigonometriese verhoudings\n\nIn 'n **reghoekige driehoek** benoem ons die sye **relatief tot 'n skerp hoek θ**:\n\n- **Skuinssy:** die sy oorkant die 90°-hoek. Dit is altyd die langste sy en dit verander nooit.\n- **Teenoorstaande sy:** die sy oorkant θ.\n- **Aangrensende sy:** die sy wat aan θ raak en nie die skuinssy is nie.\n\n| Verhouding | Definisie |\n|---|---|\n| sin θ | [[teenoorstaande/skuinssy]] |\n| cos θ | [[aangrensende/skuinssy]] |\n| tan θ | [[teenoorstaande/aangrensende]] |\n\n**Hoekom werk dit?** Alle reghoekige driehoeke met dieselfde hoek θ is **gelykvormig**. Die verhouding tussen twee sye is dus dieselfde, hoe groot die driehoek ook al is: dit hang net van die hoek af.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** As jy na die ander skerp hoek kyk, ruil die teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy om. Benoem die sye altyd opnuut vir die hoek in die vraag.\n\n## Resiproke verhoudings\n\n| Verhouding | Definisie |\n|---|---|\n| cosec θ = [[1/sin θ]] | [[skuinssy/teenoorstaande]] |\n| sec θ = [[1/cos θ]] | [[skuinssy/aangrensende]] |\n| cot θ = [[1/tan θ]] | [[aangrensende/teenoorstaande]] |\n\nOp die sakrekenaar: cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1,56.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** sin^{−1} is **nie** cosec nie. sin^{−1}(0,5) = 30° gee 'n **hoek**; cosec 30° = [[1/sin 30°]] = 2 gee 'n **getal**.\n\n**Notasie:** sin^{2} θ beteken (sin θ)^{2}, en 2 sin θ ≠ sin 2θ. Op die sakrekenaar is 4 sin 20° = 4 × sin 20° = 1,37, maar sin(4 × 20°) = sin 80° = 0,98.\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak seker jou sakrekenaar is in **grade** (DEG of D op die skerm), nie RAD of GRAD nie.\n\n## Verhoudings op die Cartesiese vlak\n\nKies 'n punt P(x; y). Die hoek θ word vanaf die **positiewe x-as antikloksgewys** tot by die lyn OP gemeet. Met r = OP gee Pythagoras r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}. **r is altyd positief.**\n\n- sin θ = [[y/r]]\n- cos θ = [[x/r]]\n- tan θ = [[y/x]]\n\nDie tekens van x en y bepaal die teken van elke verhouding (CAST-diagram):\n\n| Kwadrant | Hoeke | Positief |\n|---|---|---|\n| I | 0° < θ < 90° | **A**lles |\n| II | 90° < θ < 180° | **S**in (en cosec) |\n| III | 180° < θ < 270° | **T**an (en cot) |\n| IV | 270° < θ < 360° | **C**os (en sec) |\n\n**Metode (sonder sakrekenaar):**\n\n1. Maak die verhouding die onderwerp, bv. 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 → sin θ = [[−3/5]].\n2. Bepaal die kwadrant uit die gegewe tekens.\n3. Skets die punt en skryf x, y en r neer met die regte tekens.\n4. Bereken die ontbrekende koördinaat met r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}; die kwadrant bepaal sy teken.\n5. Vervang in die gevraagde uitdrukking.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die minusteken op r te sit. By sin θ = [[−3/5]] hoort die minus by y, want r is altyd positief.\n\n## Spesiale hoeke (sonder 'n sakrekenaar)\n\nLeer twee driehoeke:\n\n- **45°-driehoek:** reghoekig en gelykbenig, met sye 1 en 1 en skuinssy √2.\n- **30°–60°-driehoek:** die helfte van 'n gelyksydige driehoek met sy 2. Die sye is 1 (oorkant 30°), √3 (oorkant 60°) en skuinssy 2.\n\nVir 0° en 90° gebruik jy die punte (1; 0) en (0; 1) met r = 1.\n\n| | 0° | 30° | 45° | 60° | 90° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin | 0 | [[1/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[√3/2]] | 1 |\n| cos | 1 | [[√3/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[1/2]] | 0 |\n| tan | 0 | [[1/√3]] | 1 | √3 | ongedefinieerd |\n\nLet op: [[1/√2]] = [[√2/2]] en [[1/√3]] = [[√3/3]]. tan 90° is ongedefinieerd, want [[y/x]] = [[1/0]].\n\n> **Wenk:** As 'n vraag sê \"sonder 'n sakrekenaar\", vervang elke verhouding met sy breuk of wortel, vereenvoudig en laat die antwoord in wortelvorm, bv. sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]].\n\n## Sye en hoeke in 'n reghoekige driehoek\n\n**'n Sy bereken:**\n\n1. Benoem die sye relatief tot die gegewe hoek.\n2. Kies die verhouding wat die bekende en die onbekende sy bevat.\n3. Stel 'n vergelyking op en los op. Staan die onbekende onder die breukstreep, ruil om: cos 52° = [[8/PR]] → PR = [[8/cos 52°]].\n\n**'n Hoek bereken:**\n\n1. Kies die verhouding met die twee bekende sye.\n2. Gebruik die inverse: θ = sin^{−1}(…), cos^{−1}(…) of tan^{−1}(…).\n3. Rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n## Eenvoudige trigonometriese vergelykings\n\nIn vergelykings noem ons die onbekende hoek gewoonlik x (moenie dit met die x-koördinaat verwar nie). Vir skerp hoeke:\n\n1. Kry die verhouding alleen: 2 sin x = 1,3 → sin x = 0,65.\n2. Gebruik die inverse: x = sin^{−1}(0,65) = 40,54°.\n3. Is die hoek saamgestel, los eers die hele hoek op: tan(x + 10°) = 1 → x + 10° = 45° → x = 35°. Net so: cos 2x = 0,3 → 2x = 72,54° → x = 36,27°.\n4. By cosec, sec of cot draai jy eers om: sec x = 2 → cos x = [[1/2]] → x = 60°.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** By 2 sin x = 1,3 moet jy **eers deur 2 deel** en dan sin^{−1} gebruik. Onthou ook: sin x en cos x lê altyd tussen −1 en 1, dus het sin x = 1,3 **geen oplossing** nie.","en":"## The three trigonometric ratios\n\nIn a **right-angled triangle** we name the sides **relative to an acute angle θ**:\n\n- **Hypotenuse:** the side opposite the 90° angle. It is always the longest side and it never changes.\n- **Opposite side:** the side opposite θ.\n- **Adjacent side:** the side that touches θ and is not the hypotenuse.\n\n| Ratio | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| sin θ | [[opposite/hypotenuse]] |\n| cos θ | [[adjacent/hypotenuse]] |\n| tan θ | [[opposite/adjacent]] |\n\n**Why does it work?** All right-angled triangles with the same angle θ are **similar**. So the ratio of two sides is the same however big the triangle is: it depends only on the angle.\n\n> **Common mistake:** If you look at the other acute angle, the opposite and adjacent sides swap. Always label the sides again for the angle in the question.\n\n## Reciprocal ratios\n\n| Ratio | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| cosec θ = [[1/sin θ]] | [[hypotenuse/opposite]] |\n| sec θ = [[1/cos θ]] | [[hypotenuse/adjacent]] |\n| cot θ = [[1/tan θ]] | [[adjacent/opposite]] |\n\nOn the calculator: cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1.56.\n\n> **Common mistake:** sin^{−1} is **not** cosec. sin^{−1}(0.5) = 30° gives an **angle**; cosec 30° = [[1/sin 30°]] = 2 gives a **number**.\n\n**Notation:** sin^{2} θ means (sin θ)^{2}, and 2 sin θ ≠ sin 2θ. On the calculator 4 sin 20° = 4 × sin 20° = 1.37, but sin(4 × 20°) = sin 80° = 0.98.\n\n> **Tip:** Make sure your calculator is in **degrees** (DEG or D on the screen), not RAD or GRAD.\n\n## Ratios on the Cartesian plane\n\nChoose a point P(x; y). The angle θ is measured **anticlockwise from the positive x-axis** to the line OP. With r = OP, Pythagoras gives r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}. **r is always positive.**\n\n- sin θ = [[y/r]]\n- cos θ = [[x/r]]\n- tan θ = [[y/x]]\n\nThe signs of x and y decide the sign of each ratio (CAST diagram):\n\n| Quadrant | Angles | Positive |\n|---|---|---|\n| I | 0° < θ < 90° | **A**ll |\n| II | 90° < θ < 180° | **S**in (and cosec) |\n| III | 180° < θ < 270° | **T**an (and cot) |\n| IV | 270° < θ < 360° | **C**os (and sec) |\n\n**Method (without a calculator):**\n\n1. Make the ratio the subject, e.g. 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 → sin θ = [[−3/5]].\n2. Decide on the quadrant from the given signs.\n3. Sketch the point and write down x, y and r with the correct signs.\n4. Calculate the missing coordinate with r^{2} = x^{2} + y^{2}; the quadrant decides its sign.\n5. Substitute into the required expression.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Putting the minus sign on r. In sin θ = [[−3/5]] the minus belongs to y, because r is always positive.\n\n## Special angles (without a calculator)\n\nLearn two triangles:\n\n- **45° triangle:** right-angled and isosceles, with sides 1 and 1 and hypotenuse √2.\n- **30°–60° triangle:** half of an equilateral triangle with side 2. The sides are 1 (opposite 30°), √3 (opposite 60°) and hypotenuse 2.\n\nFor 0° and 90° use the points (1; 0) and (0; 1) with r = 1.\n\n| | 0° | 30° | 45° | 60° | 90° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin | 0 | [[1/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[√3/2]] | 1 |\n| cos | 1 | [[√3/2]] | [[1/√2]] | [[1/2]] | 0 |\n| tan | 0 | [[1/√3]] | 1 | √3 | undefined |\n\nNote: [[1/√2]] = [[√2/2]] and [[1/√3]] = [[√3/3]]. tan 90° is undefined, because [[y/x]] = [[1/0]].\n\n> **Tip:** When a question says \"without a calculator\", replace each ratio with its fraction or surd, simplify, and leave the answer in surd form, e.g. sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]].\n\n## Sides and angles in a right-angled triangle\n\n**Finding a side:**\n\n1. Label the sides relative to the given angle.\n2. Choose the ratio that contains the known side and the unknown side.\n3. Set up an equation and solve. If the unknown is in the denominator, swap it over: cos 52° = [[8/PR]] → PR = [[8/cos 52°]].\n\n**Finding an angle:**\n\n1. Choose the ratio with the two known sides.\n2. Use the inverse: θ = sin^{−1}(…), cos^{−1}(…) or tan^{−1}(…).\n3. Round to two decimal places only at the end.\n\n## Simple trigonometric equations\n\nIn equations the unknown angle is usually called x (do not confuse it with the x-coordinate). For acute angles:\n\n1. Get the ratio on its own: 2 sin x = 1.3 → sin x = 0.65.\n2. Use the inverse: x = sin^{−1}(0.65) = 40.54°.\n3. If the angle is compound, first solve for the whole angle: tan(x + 10°) = 1 → x + 10° = 45° → x = 35°. In the same way: cos 2x = 0.3 → 2x = 72.54° → x = 36.27°.\n4. With cosec, sec or cot, invert first: sec x = 2 → cos x = [[1/2]] → x = 60°.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In 2 sin x = 1.3 you must **divide by 2 first** and then use sin^{−1}. Remember too: sin x and cos x always lie between −1 and 1, so sin x = 1.3 has **no solution**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Skuinssy","en":"Hypotenuse"},"def":{"af":"Die langste sy van 'n reghoekige driehoek; dit lê oorkant die 90°-hoek.","en":"The longest side of a right-angled triangle; it lies opposite the 90° angle."}},{"term":{"af":"Teenoorstaande sy","en":"Opposite side"},"def":{"af":"Die sy oorkant die hoek waarmee jy werk.","en":"The side opposite the angle you are working with."}},{"term":{"af":"Aangrensende sy","en":"Adjacent side"},"def":{"af":"Die sy wat aan die hoek raak waarmee jy werk en nie die skuinssy is nie.","en":"The side that touches the angle you are working with and is not the hypotenuse."}},{"term":{"af":"Trigonometriese verhouding","en":"Trigonometric ratio"},"def":{"af":"'n Verhouding tussen twee sye van 'n reghoekige driehoek (sin, cos, tan) wat net van die grootte van die hoek afhang.","en":"A ratio of two sides of a right-angled triangle (sin, cos, tan) that depends only on the size of the angle."}},{"term":{"af":"Resiproke verhoudings","en":"Reciprocal ratios"},"def":{"af":"cosec θ = 1/sin θ, sec θ = 1/cos θ en cot θ = 1/tan θ.","en":"cosec θ = 1/sin θ, sec θ = 1/cos θ and cot θ = 1/tan θ."}},{"term":{"af":"Inverse (sin⁻¹, cos⁻¹, tan⁻¹)","en":"Inverse (sin⁻¹, cos⁻¹, tan⁻¹)"},"def":{"af":"Die sakrekenaarfunksie wat die hoek gee as jy die waarde van die verhouding ken, bv. sin⁻¹(0,5) = 30°.","en":"The calculator function that gives the angle when you know the value of the ratio, e.g. sin⁻¹(0.5) = 30°."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesiale hoeke","en":"Special angles"},"def":{"af":"0°, 30°, 45°, 60° en 90°: hul verhoudings word sonder 'n sakrekenaar uit twee driehoeke bepaal.","en":"0°, 30°, 45°, 60° and 90°: their ratios are found without a calculator from two triangles."}},{"term":{"af":"CAST-diagram","en":"CAST diagram"},"def":{"af":"Wys watter verhoudings in elke kwadrant positief is: I alles, II sin, III tan, IV cos.","en":"Shows which ratios are positive in each quadrant: I all, II sin, III tan, IV cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Wortelvorm","en":"Surd form"},"def":{"af":"'n Eksakte antwoord met 'n wortelteken, bv. √3/2, in plaas van 'n afgeronde desimale getal.","en":"An exact answer with a root sign, e.g. √3/2, instead of a rounded decimal number."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bereken sye in 'n reghoekige driehoek","en":"Calculate sides in a right-angled triangle"},"problem":{"af":"In △PQR is ∠Q = 90°, ∠P = 52° en PQ = 8 cm. Bereken, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: (a) QR (b) PR.","en":"In △PQR, ∠Q = 90°, ∠P = 52° and PQ = 8 cm. Calculate, rounded to two decimal places: (a) QR (b) PR."},"steps":[{"af":"Benoem die sye relatief tot ∠P = 52°: QR is teenoorstaande, PQ = 8 cm is aangrensende en PR is die skuinssy (oorkant ∠Q = 90°).","en":"Label the sides relative to ∠P = 52°: QR is opposite, PQ = 8 cm is adjacent and PR is the hypotenuse (opposite ∠Q = 90°)."},{"af":"(a) Teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy → tan: tan 52° = [[QR/8]]","en":"(a) Opposite and adjacent side → tan: tan 52° = [[QR/8]]"},{"af":"QR = 8 tan 52° = 10,24 cm","en":"QR = 8 tan 52° = 10.24 cm"},{"af":"(b) Aangrensende sy en skuinssy → cos: cos 52° = [[8/PR]]","en":"(b) Adjacent side and hypotenuse → cos: cos 52° = [[8/PR]]"},{"af":"PR staan onder die breukstreep, dus ruil om: PR = [[8/cos 52°]] = 12,99 cm. Kontrole: 12,99 cm is die langste sy, soos 'n skuinssy moet wees.","en":"PR is in the denominator, so swap it over: PR = [[8/cos 52°]] = 12.99 cm. Check: 12.99 cm is the longest side, as a hypotenuse should be."}],"answer":{"af":"QR = 10,24 cm; PR = 12,99 cm","en":"QR = 10.24 cm; PR = 12.99 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Los trigonometriese vergelykings op","en":"Solve trigonometric equations"},"problem":{"af":"Los op vir x, as x 'n skerp hoek is. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke. (a) 2 sin x = 1,3 (b) 4 cos(x + 15°) = 3","en":"Solve for x if x is an acute angle. Round to two decimal places. (a) 2 sin x = 1.3 (b) 4 cos(x + 15°) = 3"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Deel eers deur 2 sodat sin x alleen staan: sin x = 0,65","en":"(a) First divide by 2 so that sin x stands alone: sin x = 0.65"},{"af":"x = sin^{−1}(0,65) = 40,54°","en":"x = sin^{−1}(0.65) = 40.54°"},{"af":"(b) Deel deur 4: cos(x + 15°) = [[3/4]] = 0,75","en":"(b) Divide by 4: cos(x + 15°) = [[3/4]] = 0.75"},{"af":"Los eers die hele hoek op: x + 15° = cos^{−1}(0,75) = 41,41°","en":"First solve for the whole angle: x + 15° = cos^{−1}(0.75) = 41.41°"},{"af":"x = 41,41° − 15° = 26,41°","en":"x = 41.41° − 15° = 26.41°"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) x = 40,54° (b) x = 26,41°","en":"(a) x = 40.54° (b) x = 26.41°"}},{"title":{"af":"Verhoudings op die Cartesiese vlak","en":"Ratios on the Cartesian plane"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee: 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 en tan θ > 0. Bepaal sonder 'n sakrekenaar die waarde van: (a) cos θ (b) tan θ + sec θ","en":"Given: 5 sin θ + 3 = 0 and tan θ > 0. Without a calculator, determine the value of: (a) cos θ (b) tan θ + sec θ"},"steps":[{"af":"sin θ = [[−3/5]] = [[y/r]], dus y = −3 en r = 5 (r is altyd positief).","en":"sin θ = [[−3/5]] = [[y/r]], so y = −3 and r = 5 (r is always positive)."},{"af":"sin θ < 0 en tan θ > 0 geld net in kwadrant III (T in CAST). Daar is x en y albei negatief.","en":"sin θ < 0 and tan θ > 0 only in quadrant III (T in CAST). There x and y are both negative."},{"af":"Pythagoras: x^{2} = r^{2} − y^{2} = 25 − 9 = 16, dus x = −4 (kwadrant III).","en":"Pythagoras: x^{2} = r^{2} − y^{2} = 25 − 9 = 16, so x = −4 (quadrant III)."},{"af":"(a) cos θ = [[x/r]] = [[−4/5]]","en":"(a) cos θ = [[x/r]] = [[−4/5]]"},{"af":"(b) tan θ + sec θ = [[y/x]] + [[r/x]] = [[−3/−4]] + [[5/−4]] = [[3/4]] − [[5/4]] = −[[1/2]]","en":"(b) tan θ + sec θ = [[y/x]] + [[r/x]] = [[−3/−4]] + [[5/−4]] = [[3/4]] − [[5/4]] = −[[1/2]]"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) cos θ = −4/5 (b) tan θ + sec θ = −1/2","en":"(a) cos θ = −4/5 (b) tan θ + sec θ = −1/2"}},{"title":{"af":"Spesiale hoeke sonder 'n sakrekenaar","en":"Special angles without a calculator"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken sonder 'n sakrekenaar: (tan 60° × cos 30°) ÷ sin² 45°","en":"Calculate without a calculator: (tan 60° × cos 30°) ÷ sin² 45°"},"steps":[{"af":"Vervang die spesiale hoeke: tan 60° = √3, cos 30° = [[√3/2]] en sin 45° = [[1/√2]]","en":"Replace the special angles: tan 60° = √3, cos 30° = [[√3/2]] and sin 45° = [[1/√2]]"},{"af":"Teller: √3 × [[√3/2]] = [[3/2]]","en":"Numerator: √3 × [[√3/2]] = [[3/2]]"},{"af":"Noemer: sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]]","en":"Denominator: sin^{2} 45° = ([[1/√2]])^{2} = [[1/2]]"},{"af":"[[3/2]] ÷ [[1/2]] = [[3/2]] × 2 = 3","en":"[[3/2]] ÷ [[1/2]] = [[3/2]] × 2 = 3"}],"answer":{"af":"3","en":"3"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke verhouding by sy definisie in 'n reghoekige driehoek.","en":"Match each ratio to its definition in a right-angled triangle."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"sin θ","en":"sin θ"},"r":{"af":"teenoorstaande / skuinssy","en":"opposite / hypotenuse"}},{"l":{"af":"cos θ","en":"cos θ"},"r":{"af":"aangrensende / skuinssy","en":"adjacent / hypotenuse"}},{"l":{"af":"tan θ","en":"tan θ"},"r":{"af":"teenoorstaande / aangrensende","en":"opposite / adjacent"}},{"l":{"af":"cosec θ","en":"cosec θ"},"r":{"af":"skuinssy / teenoorstaande","en":"hypotenuse / opposite"}}],"explain":{"af":"sin = teenoorstaande/skuinssy, cos = aangrensende/skuinssy en tan = teenoorstaande/aangrensende. cosec is die omgekeerde van sin, dus skuinssy/teenoorstaande.","en":"sin = opposite/hypotenuse, cos = adjacent/hypotenuse and tan = opposite/adjacent. cosec is the reciprocal of sin, so hypotenuse/opposite."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In △ABC is ∠B = 90°. Watter sy is die skuinssy?","en":"In △ABC, ∠B = 90°. Which side is the hypotenuse?"},"options":[{"af":"AB","en":"AB"},{"af":"BC","en":"BC"},{"af":"AC","en":"AC"},{"af":"Dit hang af van watter skerp hoek jy gebruik","en":"It depends on which acute angle you use"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die skuinssy lê oorkant die regte hoek. ∠B = 90°, dus is AC die skuinssy. Die skuinssy verander nooit; net die teenoorstaande en aangrensende sy hang van die hoek af.","en":"The hypotenuse lies opposite the right angle. ∠B = 90°, so AC is the hypotenuse. The hypotenuse never changes; only the opposite and adjacent sides depend on the angle."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om cosec 40° op jou sakrekenaar te bereken, druk jy sin⁻¹ 40.","en":"To calculate cosec 40° on your calculator, you press sin⁻¹ 40."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1,56. sin⁻¹ werk andersom: dit gee 'n hoek as jy 'n verhouding invoer. sin⁻¹ 40 gee selfs 'n fout, want sin lê altyd tussen −1 en 1.","en":"False. cosec 40° = 1 ÷ sin 40° = 1.56. sin⁻¹ works the other way round: it gives an angle when you enter a ratio. sin⁻¹ 40 even gives an error, because sin always lies between −1 and 1."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sonder 'n sakrekenaar: tan 60° = ?","en":"Without a calculator: tan 60° = ?"},"options":[{"af":"1/√3","en":"1/√3"},{"af":"√3/2","en":"√3/2"},{"af":"1/2","en":"1/2"},{"af":"√3","en":"√3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In die 30°–60°-driehoek is die sy oorkant 60° √3 en die aangrensende sy 1, dus tan 60° = √3/1 = √3. 1/√3 is tan 30°, √3/2 is sin 60° en 1/2 is cos 60°.","en":"In the 30°–60° triangle the side opposite 60° is √3 and the adjacent side is 1, so tan 60° = √3/1 = √3. 1/√3 is tan 30°, √3/2 is sin 60° and 1/2 is cos 60°."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In △PQR is ∠Q = 90°, PQ = 5, QR = 12 en PR = 13. Skryf sin P as 'n breuk: sin P = ___","en":"In △PQR, ∠Q = 90°, PQ = 5, QR = 12 and PR = 13. Write sin P as a fraction: sin P = ___"},"answers":{"af":["12/13","sin P = 12/13","sinP=12/13"],"en":["12/13","sin P = 12/13","sinP=12/13"]},"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot ∠P is QR = 12 die teenoorstaande sy en PR = 13 die skuinssy (oorkant ∠Q = 90°). sin P = 12/13. (5/13 sou cos P wees.)","en":"Relative to ∠P, QR = 12 is the opposite side and PR = 13 is the hypotenuse (opposite ∠Q = 90°). sin P = 12/13. (5/13 would be cos P.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5/13","12/5","13/12"],"en":["5/13","12/5","13/12"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken 3 cos 40°, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"Calculate 3 cos 40°, rounded to two decimal places."},"options":[{"af":"2,30","en":"2.30"},{"af":"−0,50","en":"−0.50"},{"af":"0,77","en":"0.77"},{"af":"−2,00","en":"−2.00"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"3 cos 40° = 3 × cos 40° = 3 × 0,766… = 2,30. −0,50 is cos 120° (jy het die hoek met 3 vermenigvuldig), 0,77 is net cos 40°, en −2,00 kry jy as die sakrekenaar in RAD is.","en":"3 cos 40° = 3 × cos 40° = 3 × 0.766… = 2.30. −0.50 is cos 120° (you multiplied the angle by 3), 0.77 is only cos 40°, and −2.00 is what you get with the calculator in RAD."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x (x is skerp), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: 3 cos x = 2,1. x = ___°","en":"Solve for x (x is acute), rounded to two decimal places: 3 cos x = 2.1. x = ___°"},"answers":{"af":["45,57","45.57","45,57°","45.57°","x = 45,57","x = 45.57","x = 45,57°","x = 45.57°","x=45,57","x=45.57","x=45,57°","x=45.57°"],"en":["45,57","45.57","45,57°","45.57°","x = 45,57","x = 45.57","x = 45,57°","x = 45.57°","x=45,57","x=45.57","x=45,57°","x=45.57°"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel eers deur 3: cos x = 0,7. Dan is x = cos⁻¹(0,7) = 45,57°.","en":"First divide by 3: cos x = 0.7. Then x = cos⁻¹(0.7) = 45.57°."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["44,43","34,99","15,19"],"en":["44.43","34.99","15.19"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In △ABC is ∠C = 90°, ∠A = 32° en AB = 15 cm. Bereken BC, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"In △ABC, ∠C = 90°, ∠A = 32° and AB = 15 cm. Calculate BC, rounded to two decimal places."},"options":[{"af":"12,72 cm","en":"12.72 cm"},{"af":"7,95 cm","en":"7.95 cm"},{"af":"28,31 cm","en":"28.31 cm"},{"af":"9,37 cm","en":"9.37 cm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot ∠A is BC die teenoorstaande sy en AB die skuinssy, dus sin 32° = BC/15 en BC = 15 sin 32° = 7,95 cm. 12,72 cm gebruik cos (verkeerde sy), 28,31 cm is 15 ÷ sin 32° (breuk omgekeer) en 9,37 cm gebruik tan.","en":"Relative to ∠A, BC is the opposite side and AB the hypotenuse, so sin 32° = BC/15 and BC = 15 sin 32° = 7.95 cm. 12.72 cm uses cos (wrong side), 28.31 cm is 15 ÷ sin 32° (fraction upside down) and 9.37 cm uses tan."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As tan θ > 0 en cos θ < 0, dan lê θ in die derde kwadrant.","en":"If tan θ > 0 and cos θ < 0, then θ lies in the third quadrant."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. cos θ < 0 in kwadrant II en III. tan θ > 0 in kwadrant I en III. Albei geld net in kwadrant III (T in CAST).","en":"True. cos θ < 0 in quadrants II and III. tan θ > 0 in quadrants I and III. Both hold only in quadrant III (T in CAST)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"O is die oorsprong en P(−5; 12). Die hoek θ word vanaf die positiewe x-as tot by OP gemeet. Wat is cos θ?","en":"O is the origin and P(−5; 12). The angle θ is measured from the positive x-axis to OP. What is cos θ?"},"options":[{"af":"5/13","en":"5/13"},{"af":"−12/13","en":"−12/13"},{"af":"−5/13","en":"−5/13"},{"af":"−5/12","en":"−5/12"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r² = (−5)² + 12² = 169, dus r = 13. cos θ = x/r = −5/13. 5/13 vergeet die teken van x, −12/13 gebruik y in plaas van x, en −5/12 is x/y.","en":"r² = (−5)² + 12² = 169, so r = 13. cos θ = x/r = −5/13. 5/13 forgets the sign of x, −12/13 uses y instead of x, and −5/12 is x/y."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken sonder 'n sakrekenaar: tan² 60° − 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = ___","en":"Calculate without a calculator: tan² 60° − 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = ___"},"answers":{"af":["2"],"en":["2"]},"explain":{"af":"tan² 60° = (√3)² = 3 en 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = 4 × 1/2 × 1/2 = 1. Dus 3 − 1 = 2.","en":"tan² 60° = (√3)² = 3 and 4 sin 30° × cos 60° = 4 × 1/2 × 1/2 = 1. So 3 − 1 = 2."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","−1","4"],"en":["1","−1","4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Los op vir x sonder 'n sakrekenaar, as x 'n skerp hoek is: 2 cos(x − 15°) = √3","en":"Solve for x without a calculator, if x is an acute angle: 2 cos(x − 15°) = √3"},"options":[{"af":"45°","en":"45°"},{"af":"15°","en":"15°"},{"af":"75°","en":"75°"},{"af":"30°","en":"30°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"cos(x − 15°) = √3/2 en cos 30° = √3/2, dus x − 15° = 30° en x = 45°. 30° vergeet om 15° by te tel, 15° trek af in plaas van bytel, en 75° kom van die fout cos 60° = √3/2.","en":"cos(x − 15°) = √3/2 and cos 30° = √3/2, so x − 15° = 30° and x = 45°. 30° forgets to add 15°, 15° subtracts instead of adding, and 75° comes from the mistake cos 60° = √3/2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Los op vir x (2x is 'n skerp hoek), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: sec 2x = 2,5. x = ___°","en":"Solve for x (2x is an acute angle), rounded to two decimal places: sec 2x = 2.5. x = ___°"},"answers":{"af":["33,21","33.21","33,21°","33.21°","x = 33,21","x = 33.21","x = 33,21°","x = 33.21°","x=33,21","x=33.21","x=33,21°","x=33.21°"],"en":["33,21","33.21","33,21°","33.21°","x = 33,21","x = 33.21","x = 33,21°","x = 33.21°","x=33,21","x=33.21","x=33,21°","x=33.21°"]},"explain":{"af":"sec 2x = 2,5 beteken cos 2x = 1 ÷ 2,5 = 0,4. Dan is 2x = cos⁻¹(0,4) = 66,42°, dus x = 33,21°. Moenie cos⁻¹(2,5) probeer nie (dit gee 'n fout), en onthou om aan die einde deur 2 te deel.","en":"sec 2x = 2.5 means cos 2x = 1 ÷ 2.5 = 0.4. Then 2x = cos⁻¹(0.4) = 66.42°, so x = 33.21°. Do not try cos⁻¹(2.5) (it gives an error), and remember to divide by 2 at the end."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["66,42","78,46","11,79"],"en":["66.42","78.46","11.79"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee: 13 sin θ + 5 = 0 en cos θ < 0. Bepaal sonder 'n sakrekenaar die waarde van 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ.","en":"Given: 13 sin θ + 5 = 0 and cos θ < 0. Without a calculator, determine the value of 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ."},"options":[{"af":"17","en":"17"},{"af":"−7","en":"−7"},{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"−17","en":"−17"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"sin θ = −5/13, dus y = −5 en r = 13. sin θ < 0 en cos θ < 0 → kwadrant III, dus x = −12 (x² = 169 − 25 = 144). 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ = 13(−12/13) − 12(−5/−12) = −12 − 5 = −17. Die ander opsies kom van tekenfoute: x positief gee 17, y positief gee −7, en albei positief gee 7.","en":"sin θ = −5/13, so y = −5 and r = 13. sin θ < 0 and cos θ < 0 → quadrant III, so x = −12 (x² = 169 − 25 = 144). 13 cos θ − 12 tan θ = 13(−12/13) − 12(−5/−12) = −12 − 5 = −17. The other options come from sign errors: x positive gives 17, y positive gives −7, and both positive gives 7."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Funksies, trigonometriese grafieke en Euklidiese meetkunde","en":"Functions, trigonometric graphs and Euclidean geometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t2-funksies-lyn-parabool","title":{"af":"Funksies: reguit lyn en parabool","en":"Functions: straight line and parabola"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal reguit lyne en parabole kan skets, hul definisie- en waardeversameling kan gee en hul vergelykings uit gegewe punte kan bepaal.","en":"You will be able to sketch straight lines and parabolas, give their domain and range, and determine their equations from given points."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n funksie?\n\n'n **Funksie** is 'n reël wat elke invoerwaarde (x) aan **presies een** uitvoerwaarde (y) koppel. Ons skryf y = 2x + 1 of f(x) = 2x + 1. Die notasie f(3) beteken: vervang x met 3. Dus f(3) = 2(3) + 1 = 7, en die punt (3; 7) lê op die grafiek.\n\n- **Vertikale-lyn-toets:** 'n grafiek is 'n funksie as elke vertikale lyn dit hoogstens een keer sny. 'n Vertikale lyn x = k is self **nie** 'n funksie nie.\n- **Definisieversameling:** al die x-waardes wat jy mag invul. Lees dit van links na regs op die x-as.\n- **Waardeversameling:** al die y-waardes wat die grafiek bereik. Lees dit van onder na bo op die y-as.\n- **Notasie:** x ∈ ℝ beteken \"x is enige reële getal\". Skryf 'n waardeversameling as 'n ongelykheid (y ≥ −3) of in intervalnotasie (y ∈ [−3; ∞)). 'n Vierkantige hakie sluit die grenswaarde in, 'n ronde hakie sluit dit uit, en ∞ kry altyd 'n ronde hakie.\n\n## Die reguit lyn: y = ax + q\n\nDit is dieselfde as y = mx + c: **a is die gradiënt** en **q is die y-afsnit**.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | lyn styg van links na regs (toenemend) |\n| a < 0 | lyn daal van links na regs (afnemend) |\n| a = 0 | horisontale lyn y = q |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | steiler lyn |\n| q | skuif die lyn q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0) |\n\n- **Gradiënt deur twee punte:** a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]]. Trek bo en onder in dieselfde volgorde af.\n- **y-afsnit:** stel x = 0 → (0; q).\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0 en los x op.\n- Vir 'n skuins lyn is die definisieversameling x ∈ ℝ en die waardeversameling y ∈ ℝ.\n- **Afsnitmetode (dubbel-afsnitmetode):** bereken albei afsnitte, plot hulle en trek 'n reguit lyn deur die twee punte.\n\n## Die parabool: y = ax^{2} + q\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | \"glimlag\" ∪ met 'n **minimum** draaipunt |\n| a < 0 | \"frons\" ∩ met 'n **maksimum** draaipunt |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | smaller (nouer) parabool |\n| a naby 0 | wyer parabool |\n| q | skuif die parabool op of af |\n\n- **Draaipunt:** (0; q). Dit is ook die **y-afsnit**.\n- **Simmetrie-as:** x = 0 (die y-as). Die linker- en regterkant is spieëlbeelde van mekaar.\n- **x-afsnitte:** stel y = 0: ax^{2} + q = 0 → x^{2} = [[−q/a]] → x = ±√([[−q/a]]). Daar is net x-afsnitte as a en q **teenoorgestelde tekens** het (of as q = 0).\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Waardeversameling:** as a > 0 is y ≥ q, d.w.s. y ∈ [q; ∞). As a < 0 is y ≤ q, d.w.s. y ∈ (−∞; q].\n- **Toenemend en afnemend:** vir a > 0 is die parabool afnemend vir x < 0 en toenemend vir x > 0. Vir a < 0 is dit andersom.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die draaipunt is deel van die grafiek, daarom gebruik die waardeversameling van 'n parabool ≥ of ≤ (nie > of <).\n\n## Hoe om 'n grafiek te skets\n\n1. Bepaal die vorm uit die teken van a.\n2. Bereken die y-afsnit (stel x = 0).\n3. Bereken die x-afsnit(te) (stel y = 0).\n4. Vir 'n parabool: skryf die draaipunt en die simmetrie-as neer.\n5. Plot die punte, trek 'n reguit lyn of 'n gladde kurwe, en benoem die afsnitte, die draaipunt en die vergelyking.\n\n## Die vergelyking bepaal\n\n- **Lyn:** bereken a met die gradiëntformule. Vervang dan een punt in y = ax + q om q te kry. Kontroleer met die ander punt.\n- **Parabool:** q is die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt (0; q). Vervang dan nog 'n punt op die grafiek in y = ax^{2} + q en los a op.\n\n## Snypunte en grafieke lees\n\n- Twee grafieke sny waar hul y-waardes gelyk is: stel f(x) = g(x). Vir 'n lyn en 'n parabool kry jy 'n kwadratiese vergelyking: maak een kant nul, faktoriseer en kry dan die y-waardes.\n- f(x) > g(x) vra: waar lê f se grafiek **bo** g s'n? Lees die x-waardes tussen of buite die snypunte af.\n- f(x) ≥ 0 vra: waar lê die grafiek **op of bo** die x-as?\n\n> **Wenk:** Moet nie net 'n getal neerskryf nie. Toon die vergelyking wat jy oplos, want die memo gee punte vir die metode.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Die definisieversameling en die waardeversameling omruil.\n- Die ± vergeet wanneer jy x^{2} = 9 oplos (x = 3 **of** x = −3).\n- By 2y = 4x + 6 vergeet om eers deur 2 te deel: die gradiënt is 2, nie 4 nie.\n- Die y-koördinaat van enige gegewe punt as q gebruik. q is net die y-afsnit, waar x = 0.\n- Koördinate met 'n komma skryf. In Suid-Afrika skryf ons (2; 3).","en":"## What is a function?\n\nA **function** is a rule that links every input value (x) to **exactly one** output value (y). We write y = 2x + 1 or f(x) = 2x + 1. The notation f(3) means: replace x with 3. So f(3) = 2(3) + 1 = 7, and the point (3; 7) lies on the graph.\n\n- **Vertical line test:** a graph is a function if every vertical line cuts it at most once. A vertical line x = k is itself **not** a function.\n- **Domain:** all the x-values you may substitute. Read it from left to right on the x-axis.\n- **Range:** all the y-values the graph reaches. Read it from bottom to top on the y-axis.\n- **Notation:** x ∈ ℝ means \"x is any real number\". Write a range as an inequality (y ≥ −3) or in interval notation (y ∈ [−3; ∞)). A square bracket includes the end value, a round bracket excludes it, and ∞ always gets a round bracket.\n\n## The straight line: y = ax + q\n\nThis is the same as y = mx + c: **a is the gradient** and **q is the y-intercept**.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | line rises from left to right (increasing) |\n| a < 0 | line falls from left to right (decreasing) |\n| a = 0 | horizontal line y = q |\n| larger numerical value of a | steeper line |\n| q | shifts the line q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0) |\n\n- **Gradient through two points:** a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]]. Subtract in the same order at the top and the bottom.\n- **y-intercept:** let x = 0 → (0; q).\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0 and solve for x.\n- For a slanted line the domain is x ∈ ℝ and the range is y ∈ ℝ.\n- **Dual-intercept method:** calculate both intercepts, plot them and draw a straight line through the two points.\n\n## The parabola: y = ax^{2} + q\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | \"smile\" ∪ with a **minimum** turning point |\n| a < 0 | \"frown\" ∩ with a **maximum** turning point |\n| larger numerical value of a | narrower parabola |\n| a close to 0 | wider parabola |\n| q | shifts the parabola up or down |\n\n- **Turning point:** (0; q). This is also the **y-intercept**.\n- **Axis of symmetry:** x = 0 (the y-axis). The left and right sides are mirror images.\n- **x-intercepts:** let y = 0: ax^{2} + q = 0 → x^{2} = [[−q/a]] → x = ±√([[−q/a]]). There are only x-intercepts if a and q have **opposite signs** (or if q = 0).\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Range:** if a > 0 then y ≥ q, i.e. y ∈ [q; ∞). If a < 0 then y ≤ q, i.e. y ∈ (−∞; q].\n- **Increasing and decreasing:** for a > 0 the parabola is decreasing for x < 0 and increasing for x > 0. For a < 0 it is the other way round.\n\n> **Remember!** The turning point is part of the graph, so the range of a parabola uses ≥ or ≤, not > or <.\n\n## How to sketch a graph\n\n1. Decide on the shape from the sign of a.\n2. Calculate the y-intercept (let x = 0).\n3. Calculate the x-intercept(s) (let y = 0).\n4. For a parabola: write down the turning point and the axis of symmetry.\n5. Plot the points, draw a straight line or a smooth curve, and label the intercepts, the turning point and the equation.\n\n## Determining the equation\n\n- **Line:** calculate a with the gradient formula. Then substitute one point into y = ax + q to find q. Check with the other point.\n- **Parabola:** q is the y-coordinate of the turning point (0; q). Then substitute another point on the graph into y = ax^{2} + q and solve for a.\n\n## Points of intersection and reading graphs\n\n- Two graphs intersect where their y-values are equal: set f(x) = g(x). For a line and a parabola you get a quadratic equation: make one side zero, factorise and then find the y-values.\n- f(x) > g(x) asks: where is the graph of f **above** the graph of g? Read off the x-values between or outside the points of intersection.\n- f(x) ≥ 0 asks: where is the graph **on or above** the x-axis?\n\n> **Tip:** Never write down only a number. Show the equation you are solving, because the memo gives marks for the method.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Swapping the domain and the range.\n- Forgetting the ± when you solve x^{2} = 9 (x = 3 **or** x = −3).\n- With 2y = 4x + 6, forgetting to divide by 2 first: the gradient is 2, not 4.\n- Using the y-coordinate of any given point as q. q is only the y-intercept, where x = 0.\n- Writing coordinates with a comma. In South Africa we write (2; 3)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Funksie","en":"Function"},"def":{"af":"'n Reël wat elke invoerwaarde (x) aan presies een uitvoerwaarde (y) koppel.","en":"A rule that links every input value (x) to exactly one output value (y)."}},{"term":{"af":"Definisieversameling","en":"Domain"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van al die x-waardes (invoerwaardes) waarvoor die funksie gedefinieer is.","en":"The set of all x-values (inputs) for which the function is defined."}},{"term":{"af":"Waardeversameling","en":"Range"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van al die y-waardes (uitvoerwaardes) wat die funksie aanneem.","en":"The set of all y-values (outputs) that the function takes on."}},{"term":{"af":"Gradiënt","en":"Gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die steilheid van 'n reguit lyn: die verandering in y gedeel deur die verandering in x. In y = ax + q is dit a.","en":"The steepness of a straight line: the change in y divided by the change in x. In y = ax + q it is a."}},{"term":{"af":"Afsnit","en":"Intercept"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar 'n grafiek 'n as sny. By die y-afsnit is x = 0; by die x-afsnit is y = 0.","en":"The point where a graph cuts an axis. At the y-intercept x = 0; at the x-intercept y = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Parabool","en":"Parabola"},"def":{"af":"Die U-vormige grafiek van 'n kwadratiese funksie soos y = ax² + q.","en":"The U-shaped graph of a quadratic function such as y = ax² + q."}},{"term":{"af":"Draaipunt","en":"Turning point"},"def":{"af":"Die laagste (minimum) of hoogste (maksimum) punt van 'n parabool. Vir y = ax² + q is dit (0; q).","en":"The lowest (minimum) or highest (maximum) point of a parabola. For y = ax² + q it is (0; q)."}},{"term":{"af":"Simmetrie-as","en":"Axis of symmetry"},"def":{"af":"Die vertikale lyn deur die draaipunt wat die parabool in twee spieëlbeelde verdeel. Vir y = ax² + q is dit x = 0.","en":"The vertical line through the turning point that divides the parabola into two mirror images. For y = ax² + q it is x = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Toenemend en afnemend","en":"Increasing and decreasing"},"def":{"af":"'n Grafiek is toenemend waar y groter word soos x groter word (styg na regs), en afnemend waar y kleiner word (daal na regs).","en":"A graph is increasing where y gets bigger as x gets bigger (rises to the right), and decreasing where y gets smaller (falls to the right)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skets 'n reguit lyn met die afsnitmetode","en":"Sketch a straight line with the dual-intercept method"},"problem":{"af":"Skets die grafiek van g(x) = −2x + 4 met die afsnitmetode. Gee die gradiënt, die definisieversameling en die waardeversameling.","en":"Sketch the graph of g(x) = −2x + 4 using the dual-intercept method. Give the gradient, the domain and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"Vorm: a = −2 < 0, dus daal die lyn van links na regs (afnemend). Die gradiënt is −2.","en":"Shape: a = −2 < 0, so the line falls from left to right (decreasing). The gradient is −2."},{"af":"y-afsnit: stel x = 0: g(0) = −2(0) + 4 = 4 → (0; 4)","en":"y-intercept: let x = 0: g(0) = −2(0) + 4 = 4 → (0; 4)"},{"af":"x-afsnit: stel y = 0: 0 = −2x + 4 → 2x = 4 → x = 2 → (2; 0)","en":"x-intercept: let y = 0: 0 = −2x + 4 → 2x = 4 → x = 2 → (2; 0)"},{"af":"Plot (0; 4) en (2; 0), trek 'n reguit lyn deur albei punte en benoem dit g(x) = −2x + 4.","en":"Plot (0; 4) and (2; 0), draw a straight line through both points and label it g(x) = −2x + 4."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ (die lyn gaan oneindig op en af).","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y ∈ ℝ (the line goes on forever up and down)."}],"answer":{"af":"Lyn deur (0; 4) en (2; 0); gradiënt −2; x ∈ ℝ; y ∈ ℝ","en":"Line through (0; 4) and (2; 0); gradient −2; x ∈ ℝ; y ∈ ℝ"}},{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van 'n parabool","en":"Features of a parabola"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 2x² − 8. Bepaal die vorm, die draaipunt, die simmetrie-as, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en waar f afnemend is.","en":"Given f(x) = 2x² − 8. Determine the shape, the turning point, the axis of symmetry, the intercepts, the domain and range, and where f is decreasing."},"steps":[{"af":"a = 2 > 0, dus is die grafiek 'n \"glimlag\" met 'n minimum draaipunt.","en":"a = 2 > 0, so the graph is a \"smile\" with a minimum turning point."},{"af":"q = −8, dus is die draaipunt (0; −8) en die simmetrie-as x = 0. Die y-afsnit is ook (0; −8).","en":"q = −8, so the turning point is (0; −8) and the axis of symmetry is x = 0. The y-intercept is also (0; −8)."},{"af":"x-afsnitte: 2x^{2} − 8 = 0 → 2x^{2} = 8 → x^{2} = 4 → x = ±2. Die punte is (−2; 0) en (2; 0).","en":"x-intercepts: 2x^{2} − 8 = 0 → 2x^{2} = 8 → x^{2} = 4 → x = ±2. The points are (−2; 0) and (2; 0)."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y ≥ −8, d.w.s. y ∈ [−8; ∞).","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y ≥ −8, i.e. y ∈ [−8; ∞)."},{"af":"Die grafiek daal tot by die draaipunt en styg daarna: f is afnemend vir x < 0 (en toenemend vir x > 0).","en":"The graph falls down to the turning point and rises after it: f is decreasing for x < 0 (and increasing for x > 0)."}],"answer":{"af":"Draaipunt (0; −8); x-afsnitte (−2; 0) en (2; 0); y ∈ [−8; ∞); afnemend vir x < 0","en":"Turning point (0; −8); x-intercepts (−2; 0) and (2; 0); y ∈ [−8; ∞); decreasing for x < 0"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyking van 'n lyn deur twee punte","en":"Equation of a line through two points"},"problem":{"af":"'n Reguit lyn h gaan deur die punte (−1; 5) en (3; −3). Bepaal die vergelyking van h in die vorm y = ax + q.","en":"A straight line h passes through the points (−1; 5) and (3; −3). Determine the equation of h in the form y = ax + q."},"steps":[{"af":"Gradiënt: a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] = [[−3 − 5/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2","en":"Gradient: a = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] = [[−3 − 5/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2"},{"af":"Dus is y = −2x + q. Vervang die punt (−1; 5): 5 = −2(−1) + q","en":"So y = −2x + q. Substitute the point (−1; 5): 5 = −2(−1) + q"},{"af":"5 = 2 + q → q = 3","en":"5 = 2 + q → q = 3"},{"af":"Kontroleer met die ander punt (3; −3): −2(3) + 3 = −3 ✓","en":"Check with the other point (3; −3): −2(3) + 3 = −3 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"h(x) = −2x + 3","en":"h(x) = −2x + 3"}},{"title":{"af":"Parabool, lyn en snypunte","en":"Parabola, line and points of intersection"},"problem":{"af":"Die parabool f(x) = ax² + q het 'n draaipunt by (0; −4) en gaan deur die punt (3; 5). Die lyn g(x) = x + 2 sny f by A en B. (a) Bepaal die vergelyking van f. (b) Bepaal die koördinate van A en B. (c) Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) < g(x)?","en":"The parabola f(x) = ax² + q has a turning point at (0; −4) and passes through the point (3; 5). The line g(x) = x + 2 cuts f at A and B. (a) Determine the equation of f. (b) Determine the coordinates of A and B. (c) For which values of x is f(x) < g(x)?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die draaipunt is (0; −4), dus q = −4 en f(x) = ax^{2} − 4.","en":"(a) The turning point is (0; −4), so q = −4 and f(x) = ax^{2} − 4."},{"af":"Vervang (3; 5): 5 = a(3)^{2} − 4 → 9a = 9 → a = 1. Dus f(x) = x^{2} − 4.","en":"Substitute (3; 5): 5 = a(3)^{2} − 4 → 9a = 9 → a = 1. So f(x) = x^{2} − 4."},{"af":"(b) Stel f(x) = g(x): x^{2} − 4 = x + 2 → x^{2} − x − 6 = 0","en":"(b) Set f(x) = g(x): x^{2} − 4 = x + 2 → x^{2} − x − 6 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer: (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 → x = 3 of x = −2","en":"Factorise: (x − 3)(x + 2) = 0 → x = 3 or x = −2"},{"af":"Kry die y-waardes uit die lyn: g(−2) = −2 + 2 = 0 en g(3) = 3 + 2 = 5. Dus A(−2; 0) en B(3; 5).","en":"Find the y-values from the line: g(−2) = −2 + 2 = 0 and g(3) = 3 + 2 = 5. So A(−2; 0) and B(3; 5)."},{"af":"(c) f(x) < g(x) waar die parabool ONDER die lyn lê, dit is tussen die snypunte: −2 < x < 3.","en":"(c) f(x) < g(x) where the parabola lies BELOW the line, which is between the points of intersection: −2 < x < 3."}],"answer":{"af":"f(x) = x² − 4; A(−2; 0) en B(3; 5); −2 < x < 3","en":"f(x) = x² − 4; A(−2; 0) and B(3; 5); −2 < x < 3"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die definisieversameling van 'n funksie?","en":"What is the domain of a function?"},"options":[{"af":"Al die moontlike y-waardes (uitvoerwaardes)","en":"All the possible y-values (outputs)"},{"af":"Al die moontlike x-waardes (invoerwaardes)","en":"All the possible x-values (inputs)"},{"af":"Die punt waar die grafiek die y-as sny","en":"The point where the graph cuts the y-axis"},{"af":"Die hoogste of laagste punt van die grafiek","en":"The highest or lowest point of the graph"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die definisieversameling is al die x-waardes wat jy mag invul. Al die y-waardes vorm die waardeversameling. Moenie die twee omruil nie.","en":"The domain is all the x-values you may substitute. All the y-values form the range. Don't swap the two."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = −4x² + 1 het 'n maksimum draaipunt.","en":"The graph of y = −4x² + 1 has a maximum turning point."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. a = −4 < 0, dus is die parabool 'n \"frons\" (∩) en die draaipunt (0; 1) is die hoogste punt: 'n maksimum.","en":"True. a = −4 < 0, so the parabola is a \"frown\" (∩) and the turning point (0; 1) is the highest point: a maximum."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke beskrywing by die regte effek op die grafiek.","en":"Match each description to the correct effect on the graph."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"a > 0 in y = ax + q","en":"a > 0 in y = ax + q"},"r":{"af":"Die lyn styg van links na regs","en":"The line rises from left to right"}},{"l":{"af":"a < 0 in y = ax² + q","en":"a < 0 in y = ax² + q"},"r":{"af":"Die parabool het 'n maksimum draaipunt","en":"The parabola has a maximum turning point"}},{"l":{"af":"q in y = ax² + q","en":"q in y = ax² + q"},"r":{"af":"Die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt","en":"The y-coordinate of the turning point"}},{"l":{"af":"a = 0 in y = ax + q","en":"a = 0 in y = ax + q"},"r":{"af":"'n Horisontale lyn y = q","en":"A horizontal line y = q"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die teken van a bepaal die rigting (lyn) of vorm (parabool). q skuif die grafiek op of af: by die parabool is (0; q) die draaipunt. As a = 0 verdwyn die x-term en bly y = q oor.","en":"The sign of a decides the direction (line) or shape (parabola). q shifts the graph up or down: for the parabola (0; q) is the turning point. If a = 0 the x-term disappears and y = q remains."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt en die y-afsnit van die lyn 2y = −6x + 8?","en":"What are the gradient and the y-intercept of the line 2y = −6x + 8?"},"options":[{"af":"Gradiënt −6; y-afsnit 8","en":"Gradient −6; y-intercept 8"},{"af":"Gradiënt 3; y-afsnit −4","en":"Gradient 3; y-intercept −4"},{"af":"Gradiënt −3; y-afsnit 8","en":"Gradient −3; y-intercept 8"},{"af":"Gradiënt −3; y-afsnit 4","en":"Gradient −3; y-intercept 4"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Maak eers y die onderwerp: deel elke term deur 2, dan y = −3x + 4. Dus a = −3 en q = 4. Die algemeenste fout is om net een term (of geen term) deur 2 te deel.","en":"First make y the subject: divide every term by 2, then y = −3x + 4. So a = −3 and q = 4. The most common mistake is to divide only one term (or no term) by 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = 2x − 6 sny die x-as by x = ___.","en":"The graph of y = 2x − 6 cuts the x-axis at x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["3","x = 3","x=3","(3; 0)","(3;0)","(3,0)"],"en":["3","x = 3","x=3","(3; 0)","(3;0)","(3,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"By die x-afsnit is y = 0: 0 = 2x − 6 → 2x = 6 → x = 3. Die punt is (3; 0).","en":"At the x-intercept y = 0: 0 = 2x − 6 → 2x = 6 → x = 3. The point is (3; 0)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−3","−6","12"],"en":["−3","−6","12"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van f(x) = −2x² + 5?","en":"What is the range of f(x) = −2x² + 5?"},"options":[{"af":"y ≥ 5","en":"y ≥ 5"},{"af":"y < 5","en":"y < 5"},{"af":"y ≤ 5","en":"y ≤ 5"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ","en":"y ∈ ℝ"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"a = −2 < 0, dus is dit 'n frons met 'n maksimum draaipunt (0; 5). Die hoogste y-waarde is 5 en dit word bereik, dus y ≤ 5, of y ∈ (−∞; 5]. \"y < 5\" laat die draaipunt uit en \"y ≥ 5\" ignoreer die teken van a.","en":"a = −2 < 0, so it is a frown with a maximum turning point (0; 5). The highest y-value is 5 and it is reached, so y ≤ 5, or y ∈ (−∞; 5]. \"y < 5\" leaves out the turning point and \"y ≥ 5\" ignores the sign of a."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 2x² − 50. Die positiewe x-afsnit van f is x = ___.","en":"Given f(x) = 2x² − 50. The positive x-intercept of f is x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["5","x = 5","x=5","(5; 0)","(5;0)","(5,0)"],"en":["5","x = 5","x=5","(5; 0)","(5;0)","(5,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel f(x) = 0: 2x² − 50 = 0 → x² = 25 → x = ±5. Die positiewe afsnit is x = 5. Deel eers deur 2: √50 is verkeerd.","en":"Let f(x) = 0: 2x² − 50 = 0 → x² = 25 → x = ±5. The positive intercept is x = 5. Divide by 2 first: √50 is wrong."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−5","7,07","25"],"en":["−5","7.07","25"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van die lyn deur (−2; 7) en (4; −5)?","en":"What is the gradient of the line through (−2; 7) and (4; −5)?"},"options":[{"af":"−2","en":"−2"},{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"−½","en":"−½"},{"af":"−6","en":"−6"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"a = (−5 − 7)/(4 − (−2)) = −12/6 = −2. As jy die y's en die x's in verskillende volgordes aftrek, kry jy 2. As jy Δx/Δy bereken, kry jy −½. −6 kom van 4 − 2 in plaas van 4 − (−2).","en":"a = (−5 − 7)/(4 − (−2)) = −12/6 = −2. If you subtract the y's and the x's in different orders you get 2. If you calculate Δx/Δy you get −½. −6 comes from 4 − 2 instead of 4 − (−2)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van f(x) = x² + 4 het twee x-afsnitte.","en":"The graph of f(x) = x² + 4 has two x-intercepts."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. x² + 4 = 0 gee x² = −4, en geen reële getal se kwadraat is negatief nie. Die parabool is 'n glimlag met sy minimum draaipunt (0; 4) bo die x-as, dus sny dit nooit die x-as nie. a en q het dieselfde teken.","en":"False. x² + 4 = 0 gives x² = −4, and no real number squared is negative. The parabola is a smile with its minimum turning point (0; 4) above the x-axis, so it never cuts the x-axis. a and q have the same sign."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) = −x² + 4 toenemend?","en":"For which values of x is f(x) = −x² + 4 increasing?"},"options":[{"af":"x > 0","en":"x > 0"},{"af":"x < 0","en":"x < 0"},{"af":"y < 4","en":"y < 4"},{"af":"−2 < x < 2","en":"−2 < x < 2"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"a < 0, dus 'n frons met 'n maksimum by (0; 4). Van links af styg die grafiek tot by die draaipunt, dus is f toenemend vir x < 0 en afnemend vir x > 0. \"y < 4\" gee y-waardes, nie x-waardes nie, en −2 < x < 2 is waar f(x) > 0.","en":"a < 0, so a frown with a maximum at (0; 4). From the left the graph rises up to the turning point, so f is increasing for x < 0 and decreasing for x > 0. \"y < 4\" gives y-values, not x-values, and −2 < x < 2 is where f(x) > 0."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Reguit lyn gaan deur (−1; 5) en (2; −4). Wat is die vergelyking van die lyn?","en":"A straight line passes through (−1; 5) and (2; −4). What is the equation of the line?"},"options":[{"af":"y = −3x + 8","en":"y = −3x + 8"},{"af":"y = 3x + 8","en":"y = 3x + 8"},{"af":"y = −3x + 5","en":"y = −3x + 5"},{"af":"y = −3x + 2","en":"y = −3x + 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"a = (−4 − 5)/(2 − (−1)) = −9/3 = −3. Vervang (−1; 5): 5 = −3(−1) + q → 5 = 3 + q → q = 2. Kontroleer: −3(2) + 2 = −4 ✓. y = −3x + 8 kom van 'n tekenfout met −3 × −1, en y = −3x + 5 gebruik die y-waarde van 'n punt as q, maar q is net die y-afsnit (x = 0).","en":"a = (−4 − 5)/(2 − (−1)) = −9/3 = −3. Substitute (−1; 5): 5 = −3(−1) + q → 5 = 3 + q → q = 2. Check: −3(2) + 2 = −4 ✓. y = −3x + 8 comes from a sign error with −3 × −1, and y = −3x + 5 uses the y-value of a point as q, but q is only the y-intercept (x = 0)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die parabool y = ax² + q het 'n draaipunt by (0; 5) en gaan deur die punt (2; −7). Bepaal a. a = ___","en":"The parabola y = ax² + q has a turning point at (0; 5) and passes through the point (2; −7). Determine a. a = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","a = -3","a=-3","a = −3","a=−3"],"en":["-3","−3","a = -3","a=-3","a = −3","a=−3"]},"explain":{"af":"q = 5 (die y-koördinaat van die draaipunt). Vervang (2; −7): −7 = a(2)² + 5 → 4a = −12 → a = −3. Dit maak sin: die grafiek daal van 5 na −7, dus is dit 'n frons (a < 0).","en":"q = 5 (the y-coordinate of the turning point). Substitute (2; −7): −7 = a(2)² + 5 → 4a = −12 → a = −3. This makes sense: the graph drops from 5 to −7, so it is a frown (a < 0)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","-6","-0,5"],"en":["3","-6","-0.5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = x² − 1 en g(x) = x + 1. By watter punte sny die twee grafieke mekaar?","en":"Given f(x) = x² − 1 and g(x) = x + 1. At which points do the two graphs intersect?"},"options":[{"af":"(−1; 0) en (2; 3)","en":"(−1; 0) and (2; 3)"},{"af":"(1; 2) en (−2; −1)","en":"(1; 2) and (−2; −1)"},{"af":"(−1; 0) en (1; 0)","en":"(−1; 0) and (1; 0)"},{"af":"(0; −1) en (0; 1)","en":"(0; −1) and (0; 1)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Stel f(x) = g(x): x² − 1 = x + 1 → x² − x − 2 = 0 → (x − 2)(x + 1) = 0 → x = 2 of x = −1. Dan is g(2) = 3 en g(−1) = 0. (1; 2) en (−2; −1) kom van 'n tekenfout in die faktore, (−1; 0) en (1; 0) is net f se x-afsnitte, en (0; −1) en (0; 1) is die twee y-afsnitte.","en":"Set f(x) = g(x): x² − 1 = x + 1 → x² − x − 2 = 0 → (x − 2)(x + 1) = 0 → x = 2 or x = −1. Then g(2) = 3 and g(−1) = 0. (1; 2) and (−2; −1) come from a sign error in the factors, (−1; 0) and (1; 0) are only the x-intercepts of f, and (0; −1) and (0; 1) are the two y-intercepts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Boog oor die ingang van 'n vakansieoord by Hartbeespoortdam het die vorm y = −½x² + 8, met x en y in meter en die grond langs die x-as. Hoe wyd is die boog op grondvlak? ___ m","en":"An arch over the entrance of a holiday resort at Hartbeespoort Dam has the shape y = −½x² + 8, with x and y in metres and the ground along the x-axis. How wide is the arch at ground level? ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["8","8 m","8m"],"en":["8","8 m","8m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die boog raak die grond waar y = 0: −½x² + 8 = 0 → x² = 16 → x = ±4. Die boog strek van x = −4 tot x = 4, dus is dit 4 − (−4) = 8 m wyd. (Dit is ook 8 m hoog by die draaipunt (0; 8).)","en":"The arch touches the ground where y = 0: −½x² + 8 = 0 → x² = 16 → x = ±4. The arch stretches from x = −4 to x = 4, so it is 4 − (−4) = 8 m wide. (It is also 8 m high at the turning point (0; 8).)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","16","5,66"],"en":["4","16","5.66"]}}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-funksies-hiperbool-eksponensieel","title":{"af":"Funksies: hiperbool en eksponensiële grafiek","en":"Functions: hyperbola and exponential graph"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hiperbole en eksponensiële grafieke kan skets, hul asimptote, afsnitte en definisie- en waardeversameling kan gee, en hul vergelykings en snypunte kan bepaal.","en":"You will be able to sketch hyperbolas and exponential graphs, give their asymptotes, intercepts, domain and range, and determine their equations and points of intersection."},"summary":{"af":"## Die hiperbool: y = [[a/x]] + q\n\nDie basiese grafiek y = [[1/x]] bestaan uit **twee takke** wat nie aan mekaar raak nie. Jy mag nie deur 0 deel nie, daarom het die grafiek geen punt by x = 0 nie.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant (relatief tot die asimptote); elke tak is afnemend |\n| a < 0 | takke in die 2de en 4de kwadrant; elke tak is toenemend |\n| groter numeriese waarde van a | takke lê verder van die asimptote af |\n| q | skuif die grafiek q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0) |\n\n- **Asimptoot:** 'n lyn waarna die grafiek al hoe nader kom, maar wat dit nooit raak nie. Die hiperbool het 'n **vertikale asimptoot x = 0** (die y-as) en 'n **horisontale asimptoot y = q**. Teken asimptote as stippellyne.\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0.\n- **Waardeversameling:** y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ q.\n- **y-afsnit:** **geen**, want x = 0 word nie toegelaat nie.\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0: [[a/x]] + q = 0 → x = [[−a/q]]. As q = 0 is daar geen x-afsnit nie.\n- **Simmetrie-asse:** y = x + q en y = −x + q. Albei gaan deur (0; q), waar die asimptote mekaar sny.\n\n## Die eksponensiële grafiek: y = a · b^{x} + q\n\nHier is b > 0 en b ≠ 1, en die veranderlike x staan in die **eksponent**. Die getal b is die **grondtal**.\n\n| Waarde | Effek op die grafiek |\n|---|---|\n| b > 1 (met a > 0) | toenemend: eksponensiële groei, bv. y = 2^{x} |\n| b tussen 0 en 1 (met a > 0) | afnemend: eksponensiële verval, bv. y = ([[1/2]])^{x} |\n| a > 0 | grafiek lê bo die asimptoot |\n| a < 0 | grafiek lê onder die asimptoot; dit is 'n spieëlbeeld, dus draai toenemend en afnemend om |\n| q | horisontale asimptoot y = q |\n\n- **Asimptoot:** y = q. Daar is geen vertikale asimptoot nie.\n- **Definisieversameling:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Waardeversameling:** as a > 0 is y > q, d.w.s. y ∈ (q; ∞). As a < 0 is y ∈ (−∞; q). Gebruik ronde hakies, want die asimptoot word nooit bereik nie.\n- **y-afsnit:** stel x = 0. Omdat b^{0} = 1, is die y-afsnit (0; a + q).\n- **x-afsnit:** stel y = 0: a · b^{x} = −q → b^{x} = [[−q/a]]. Skryf albei kante met dieselfde grondtal en stel die eksponente gelyk, bv. 2^{x} = 8 = 2^{3} → x = 3. As [[−q/a]] nul of negatief is, is daar **geen** x-afsnit nie.\n- b^{−x} = ([[1/b]])^{x}, dus is y = 2^{−x} dieselfde grafiek as y = ([[1/2]])^{x}.\n- **Volgorde van bewerkings:** in 3 · 2^{x} bereken jy eers 2^{x} en vermenigvuldig dan met 3. By x = 2 is dit 3 · 4 = 12, nie 6^{2} = 36 nie. En −2^{x} beteken −(2^{x}), nie (−2)^{x} nie.\n\n## Skets: stappe\n\n1. Teken die asimptoot (of asimptote) as stippellyne.\n2. Bereken die afsnitte met die asse.\n3. Bereken nog een of twee punte, bv. by x = 1 en x = −1.\n4. Bepaal die vorm uit die tekens van a (en b) en trek 'n gladde kurwe wat die asimptote nader, maar nooit raak nie.\n5. Benoem die afsnitte, die asimptote en die vergelyking.\n\n## Die vergelyking uit 'n grafiek bepaal\n\n- **Hiperbool y = [[a/x]] + q:** lees q van die horisontale asimptoot af. Vervang dan 'n punt op die grafiek en los a op.\n- **Eksponensieel y = a · b^{x} + q:** lees q van die asimptoot af. Gebruik die y-afsnit (0; a + q) om a te kry, of vervang 'n ander punt om b te kry. b moet positief wees, dus verwerp 'n negatiewe waarde van b.\n\n## Snypunte en grafieke lees\n\n- Stel f(x) = g(x) en los op. Met 'n hiperbool: vermenigvuldig albei kante met x (x ≠ 0) om 'n kwadratiese vergelyking te kry, en faktoriseer.\n- Vervang elke x-waarde terug in die eenvoudigste vergelyking om die y-waarde te kry.\n- f(x) > g(x) vra: waar lê f se grafiek **bo** g s'n? By 'n hiperbool moet jy die asimptoot x = 0 in ag neem: die antwoord bestaan dikwels uit twee intervalle.\n- Om 'n waarde van 'n grafiek af te lees, vervang die x-waarde in die vergelyking, bv. f(2).\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak altyd seker jou antwoord pas by die skets. 'n Punt op 'n hiperbool met a > 0 en q = 0 moet in die 1ste of 3de kwadrant lê.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Sê dat 'n hiperbool 'n y-afsnit het.\n- Vergeet x ≠ 0 in die definisieversameling van 'n hiperbool.\n- Skryf y ≥ q vir 'n eksponensiële grafiek (dit moet y > q wees as a > 0).\n- Verwar a · b^{x} met (ab)^{x}.\n- Neem die asimptoot as y = a in plaas van y = q.\n- Behou 'n negatiewe b, of x = 0, as antwoord, al word dit nie toegelaat nie.","en":"## The hyperbola: y = [[a/x]] + q\n\nThe basic graph y = [[1/x]] consists of **two branches** that do not touch each other. You may not divide by 0, so the graph has no point at x = 0.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| a > 0 | branches in the 1st and 3rd quadrants (relative to the asymptotes); each branch is decreasing |\n| a < 0 | branches in the 2nd and 4th quadrants; each branch is increasing |\n| larger numerical value of a | branches lie further away from the asymptotes |\n| q | shifts the graph q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0) |\n\n- **Asymptote:** a line that the graph gets closer and closer to, but never touches. The hyperbola has a **vertical asymptote x = 0** (the y-axis) and a **horizontal asymptote y = q**. Draw asymptotes as dotted lines.\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0.\n- **Range:** y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ q.\n- **y-intercept:** **none**, because x = 0 is not allowed.\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0: [[a/x]] + q = 0 → x = [[−a/q]]. If q = 0 there is no x-intercept.\n- **Axes of symmetry:** y = x + q and y = −x + q. Both pass through (0; q), where the asymptotes intersect.\n\n## The exponential graph: y = a · b^{x} + q\n\nHere b > 0 and b ≠ 1, and the variable x is in the **exponent**. The number b is the **base**.\n\n| Value | Effect on the graph |\n|---|---|\n| b > 1 (with a > 0) | increasing: exponential growth, e.g. y = 2^{x} |\n| b between 0 and 1 (with a > 0) | decreasing: exponential decay, e.g. y = ([[1/2]])^{x} |\n| a > 0 | graph lies above the asymptote |\n| a < 0 | graph lies below the asymptote; it is a mirror image, so increasing and decreasing swap |\n| q | horizontal asymptote y = q |\n\n- **Asymptote:** y = q. There is no vertical asymptote.\n- **Domain:** x ∈ ℝ.\n- **Range:** if a > 0 then y > q, i.e. y ∈ (q; ∞). If a < 0 then y ∈ (−∞; q). Use round brackets, because the asymptote is never reached.\n- **y-intercept:** let x = 0. Because b^{0} = 1, the y-intercept is (0; a + q).\n- **x-intercept:** let y = 0: a · b^{x} = −q → b^{x} = [[−q/a]]. Write both sides with the same base and set the exponents equal, e.g. 2^{x} = 8 = 2^{3} → x = 3. If [[−q/a]] is zero or negative, there is **no** x-intercept.\n- b^{−x} = ([[1/b]])^{x}, so y = 2^{−x} is the same graph as y = ([[1/2]])^{x}.\n- **Order of operations:** in 3 · 2^{x} you first calculate 2^{x} and then multiply by 3. At x = 2 it is 3 · 4 = 12, not 6^{2} = 36. And −2^{x} means −(2^{x}), not (−2)^{x}.\n\n## Sketching: steps\n\n1. Draw the asymptote (or asymptotes) as dotted lines.\n2. Calculate the intercepts with the axes.\n3. Calculate one or two more points, e.g. at x = 1 and x = −1.\n4. Decide on the shape from the signs of a (and b) and draw a smooth curve that approaches the asymptotes but never touches them.\n5. Label the intercepts, the asymptotes and the equation.\n\n## Determining the equation from a graph\n\n- **Hyperbola y = [[a/x]] + q:** read q from the horizontal asymptote. Then substitute a point on the graph and solve for a.\n- **Exponential y = a · b^{x} + q:** read q from the asymptote. Use the y-intercept (0; a + q) to find a, or substitute another point to find b. b must be positive, so reject a negative value of b.\n\n## Points of intersection and reading graphs\n\n- Set f(x) = g(x) and solve. With a hyperbola: multiply both sides by x (x ≠ 0) to get a quadratic equation, and factorise.\n- Substitute each x-value back into the simplest equation to get the y-value.\n- f(x) > g(x) asks: where is the graph of f **above** the graph of g? With a hyperbola you must take the asymptote x = 0 into account: the answer often consists of two intervals.\n- To read a value from a graph, substitute the x-value into the equation, e.g. f(2).\n\n> **Tip:** Always check that your answer fits the sketch. A point on a hyperbola with a > 0 and q = 0 must lie in the 1st or 3rd quadrant.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Saying that a hyperbola has a y-intercept.\n- Forgetting x ≠ 0 in the domain of a hyperbola.\n- Writing y ≥ q for an exponential graph (it must be y > q if a > 0).\n- Confusing a · b^{x} with (ab)^{x}.\n- Taking the asymptote as y = a instead of y = q.\n- Keeping a negative b, or x = 0, as an answer even though it is not allowed."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hiperbool","en":"Hyperbola"},"def":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a/x + q: twee afsonderlike takke wat twee asimptote nader.","en":"The graph of y = a/x + q: two separate branches that approach two asymptotes."}},{"term":{"af":"Asimptoot","en":"Asymptote"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn waarna 'n grafiek al hoe nader kom, maar wat dit nooit raak nie.","en":"A line that a graph gets closer and closer to, but never touches."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertikale asimptoot","en":"Vertical asymptote"},"def":{"af":"By y = a/x + q is dit die lyn x = 0, want jy kan nie deur 0 deel nie.","en":"For y = a/x + q it is the line x = 0, because you cannot divide by 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Horisontale asimptoot","en":"Horizontal asymptote"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn y = q by y = a/x + q en by y = a · bˣ + q.","en":"The line y = q for y = a/x + q and for y = a · bˣ + q."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële funksie","en":"Exponential function"},"def":{"af":"'n Funksie van die vorm y = a · bˣ + q (b > 0, b ≠ 1) waarin die veranderlike in die eksponent staan.","en":"A function of the form y = a · bˣ + q (b > 0, b ≠ 1) in which the variable is in the exponent."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondtal","en":"Base"},"def":{"af":"Die getal b in y = a · bˣ + q. Dit moet positief wees en mag nie 1 wees nie.","en":"The number b in y = a · bˣ + q. It must be positive and may not be 1."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksponensiële groei en verval","en":"Exponential growth and decay"},"def":{"af":"Groei: die waardes word al vinniger groter (b > 1). Verval: die waardes neem af na die asimptoot toe (b tussen 0 en 1).","en":"Growth: the values increase faster and faster (b > 1). Decay: the values decrease towards the asymptote (b between 0 and 1)."}},{"term":{"af":"Snypunt","en":"Point of intersection"},"def":{"af":"'n Punt wat op albei grafieke lê. Jy vind dit deur f(x) = g(x) op te los.","en":"A point that lies on both graphs. You find it by solving f(x) = g(x)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van 'n hiperbool","en":"Features of a hyperbola"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 6/x − 2. Bepaal die asimptote, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en twee ekstra punte vir die skets.","en":"Given f(x) = 6/x − 2. Determine the asymptotes, the intercepts, the domain and range, and two extra points for the sketch."},"steps":[{"af":"Asimptote: vertikaal x = 0 en horisontaal y = q = −2.","en":"Asymptotes: vertical x = 0 and horizontal y = q = −2."},{"af":"y-afsnit: geen, want x = 0 word nie toegelaat nie.","en":"y-intercept: none, because x = 0 is not allowed."},{"af":"x-afsnit: 0 = [[6/x]] − 2 → [[6/x]] = 2 → 6 = 2x → x = 3. Die punt is (3; 0).","en":"x-intercept: 0 = [[6/x]] − 2 → [[6/x]] = 2 → 6 = 2x → x = 3. The point is (3; 0)."},{"af":"a = 6 > 0, dus lê die takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant relatief tot die asimptote. Ekstra punte: f(1) = 6 − 2 = 4 → (1; 4) en f(−3) = −2 − 2 = −4 → (−3; −4).","en":"a = 6 > 0, so the branches lie in the 1st and 3rd quadrants relative to the asymptotes. Extra points: f(1) = 6 − 2 = 4 → (1; 4) and f(−3) = −2 − 2 = −4 → (−3; −4)."},{"af":"Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −2.","en":"Domain: x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0. Range: y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −2."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptote x = 0 en y = −2; x-afsnit (3; 0); geen y-afsnit; x ≠ 0; y ≠ −2","en":"Asymptotes x = 0 and y = −2; x-intercept (3; 0); no y-intercept; x ≠ 0; y ≠ −2"}},{"title":{"af":"Eksponensiële grafiek met a < 0","en":"Exponential graph with a < 0"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee g(x) = −2ˣ + 4. Bepaal die asimptoot, die afsnitte, die definisie- en waardeversameling, en of g toenemend of afnemend is.","en":"Given g(x) = −2ˣ + 4. Determine the asymptote, the intercepts, the domain and range, and whether g is increasing or decreasing."},"steps":[{"af":"Hier is a = −1, b = 2 en q = 4. Let op: −2^{x} beteken −(2^{x}).","en":"Here a = −1, b = 2 and q = 4. Note: −2^{x} means −(2^{x})."},{"af":"Asimptoot: y = 4.","en":"Asymptote: y = 4."},{"af":"y-afsnit: g(0) = −2^{0} + 4 = −1 + 4 = 3 → (0; 3)","en":"y-intercept: g(0) = −2^{0} + 4 = −1 + 4 = 3 → (0; 3)"},{"af":"x-afsnit: 0 = −2^{x} + 4 → 2^{x} = 4 = 2^{2} → x = 2 → (2; 0)","en":"x-intercept: 0 = −2^{x} + 4 → 2^{x} = 4 = 2^{2} → x = 2 → (2; 0)"},{"af":"a < 0, dus lê die grafiek onder die asimptoot. Definisieversameling: x ∈ ℝ. Waardeversameling: y < 4, d.w.s. y ∈ (−∞; 4).","en":"a < 0, so the graph lies below the asymptote. Domain: x ∈ ℝ. Range: y < 4, i.e. y ∈ (−∞; 4)."},{"af":"b > 1 maar a < 0, dus is die grafiek omgekeer: g is afnemend (dit daal van links na regs).","en":"b > 1 but a < 0, so the graph is flipped: g is decreasing (it falls from left to right)."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptoot y = 4; afsnitte (0; 3) en (2; 0); y ∈ (−∞; 4); afnemend","en":"Asymptote y = 4; intercepts (0; 3) and (2; 0); y ∈ (−∞; 4); decreasing"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelykings uit grafiekkenmerke","en":"Equations from graph features"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Die hiperbool h(x) = a/x + q het 'n horisontale asimptoot y = 3 en gaan deur (2; 1). Bepaal h(x). (b) Die grafiek van k(x) = bˣ + q het 'n asimptoot y = −1 en gaan deur (2; 8). Bepaal k(x).","en":"(a) The hyperbola h(x) = a/x + q has a horizontal asymptote y = 3 and passes through (2; 1). Determine h(x). (b) The graph of k(x) = bˣ + q has an asymptote y = −1 and passes through (2; 8). Determine k(x)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die horisontale asimptoot is y = 3, dus q = 3 en h(x) = [[a/x]] + 3.","en":"(a) The horizontal asymptote is y = 3, so q = 3 and h(x) = [[a/x]] + 3."},{"af":"Vervang (2; 1): 1 = [[a/2]] + 3 → [[a/2]] = −2 → a = −4. Dus h(x) = [[−4/x]] + 3.","en":"Substitute (2; 1): 1 = [[a/2]] + 3 → [[a/2]] = −2 → a = −4. So h(x) = [[−4/x]] + 3."},{"af":"(b) Die asimptoot is y = −1, dus q = −1 en k(x) = b^{x} − 1.","en":"(b) The asymptote is y = −1, so q = −1 and k(x) = b^{x} − 1."},{"af":"Vervang (2; 8): 8 = b^{2} − 1 → b^{2} = 9 → b = 3 of b = −3","en":"Substitute (2; 8): 8 = b^{2} − 1 → b^{2} = 9 → b = 3 or b = −3"},{"af":"Die grondtal moet positief wees, dus b = 3 en k(x) = 3^{x} − 1. Kontroleer: 3^{2} − 1 = 8 ✓","en":"The base must be positive, so b = 3 and k(x) = 3^{x} − 1. Check: 3^{2} − 1 = 8 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"h(x) = −4/x + 3; k(x) = 3ˣ − 1","en":"h(x) = −4/x + 3; k(x) = 3ˣ − 1"}},{"title":{"af":"Snypunte van 'n hiperbool en 'n lyn","en":"Points of intersection of a hyperbola and a line"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 4/x en g(x) = x + 3. (a) Bepaal die koördinate van die snypunte van f en g. (b) Vir watter waardes van x is f(x) > g(x)?","en":"Given f(x) = 4/x and g(x) = x + 3. (a) Determine the coordinates of the points of intersection of f and g. (b) For which values of x is f(x) > g(x)?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Stel f(x) = g(x): [[4/x]] = x + 3","en":"(a) Set f(x) = g(x): [[4/x]] = x + 3"},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met x (x ≠ 0): 4 = x^{2} + 3x → x^{2} + 3x − 4 = 0","en":"Multiply by x (x ≠ 0): 4 = x^{2} + 3x → x^{2} + 3x − 4 = 0"},{"af":"Faktoriseer: (x + 4)(x − 1) = 0 → x = −4 of x = 1","en":"Factorise: (x + 4)(x − 1) = 0 → x = −4 or x = 1"},{"af":"y-waardes uit g: g(−4) = −1 en g(1) = 4. Die snypunte is (−4; −1) en (1; 4).","en":"y-values from g: g(−4) = −1 and g(1) = 4. The points of intersection are (−4; −1) and (1; 4)."},{"af":"(b) Die hiperbool lê bo die lyn links van x = −4, en tussen die asimptoot x = 0 en x = 1. Toets: f(−5) = −0,8 > g(−5) = −2 ✓ en f(0,5) = 8 > g(0,5) = 3,5 ✓","en":"(b) The hyperbola lies above the line to the left of x = −4, and between the asymptote x = 0 and x = 1. Test: f(−5) = −0.8 > g(−5) = −2 ✓ and f(0.5) = 8 > g(0.5) = 3.5 ✓"},{"af":"Antwoord: x < −4 of 0 < x < 1. x = 0 is uitgesluit, want f bestaan nie daar nie.","en":"Answer: x < −4 or 0 < x < 1. x = 0 is excluded, because f does not exist there."}],"answer":{"af":"(−4; −1) en (1; 4); x < −4 of 0 < x < 1","en":"(−4; −1) and (1; 4); x < −4 or 0 < x < 1"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n eksponensiële funksie?","en":"Which one of the following is an exponential function?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 3x²","en":"y = 3x²"},{"af":"y = 3/x","en":"y = 3/x"},{"af":"y = 3 · 2ˣ","en":"y = 3 · 2ˣ"},{"af":"y = 3x + 2","en":"y = 3x + 2"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By 'n eksponensiële funksie staan die veranderlike x in die eksponent: y = a · bˣ + q. y = 3x² is 'n parabool, y = 3/x 'n hiperbool en y = 3x + 2 'n reguit lyn.","en":"In an exponential function the variable x is in the exponent: y = a · bˣ + q. y = 3x² is a parabola, y = 3/x a hyperbola and y = 3x + 2 a straight line."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die waardeversameling van y = 2ˣ + 3 is y ≥ 3.","en":"The range of y = 2ˣ + 3 is y ≥ 3."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. y = 3 is 'n asimptoot: die grafiek kom al hoe nader, maar raak dit nooit. Omdat a > 0 is die waardeversameling y > 3, d.w.s. y ∈ (3; ∞).","en":"False. y = 3 is an asymptote: the graph gets closer and closer but never touches it. Because a > 0 the range is y > 3, i.e. y ∈ (3; ∞)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vergelyking by die beskrywing van sy grafiek.","en":"Match each equation to the description of its graph."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"y = 2ˣ","en":"y = 2ˣ"},"r":{"af":"Toenemend; gaan deur (0; 1)","en":"Increasing; passes through (0; 1)"}},{"l":{"af":"y = (½)ˣ","en":"y = (½)ˣ"},"r":{"af":"Afnemend; gaan deur (0; 1)","en":"Decreasing; passes through (0; 1)"}},{"l":{"af":"y = 2/x","en":"y = 2/x"},"r":{"af":"Takke in die 1ste en 3de kwadrant","en":"Branches in the 1st and 3rd quadrants"}},{"l":{"af":"y = −2/x","en":"y = −2/x"},"r":{"af":"Takke in die 2de en 4de kwadrant","en":"Branches in the 2nd and 4th quadrants"}}],"explain":{"af":"By y = bˣ is die y-afsnit altyd (0; 1), want b⁰ = 1. b > 1 gee groei en b tussen 0 en 1 gee verval. By y = a/x bepaal die teken van a die kwadrante: a > 0 gee 1ste en 3de, a < 0 gee 2de en 4de.","en":"For y = bˣ the y-intercept is always (0; 1), because b⁰ = 1. b > 1 gives growth and b between 0 and 1 gives decay. For y = a/x the sign of a decides the quadrants: a > 0 gives 1st and 3rd, a < 0 gives 2nd and 4th."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die definisieversameling van y = 3/x − 1?","en":"What is the domain of y = 3/x − 1?"},"options":[{"af":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0","en":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ 0"},{"af":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ −1","en":"x ∈ ℝ, x ≠ −1"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −1","en":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ −1"},{"af":"x ∈ ℝ","en":"x ∈ ℝ"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jy mag nie deur 0 deel nie, dus x ≠ 0. Die −1 (dit is q) beïnvloed die waardeversameling (y ≠ −1), nie die definisieversameling nie.","en":"You may not divide by 0, so x ≠ 0. The −1 (that is q) affects the range (y ≠ −1), not the domain."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die asimptote van y = −4/x + 2?","en":"What are the asymptotes of y = −4/x + 2?"},"options":[{"af":"x = 2 en y = 0","en":"x = 2 and y = 0"},{"af":"x = 0 en y = −4","en":"x = 0 and y = −4"},{"af":"x = −4 en y = 2","en":"x = −4 and y = 2"},{"af":"x = 0 en y = 2","en":"x = 0 and y = 2"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By y = a/x + q is die vertikale asimptoot altyd x = 0 en die horisontale asimptoot y = q = 2. Die a-waarde (−4) bepaal net die kwadrante en die vorm, nie die asimptote nie.","en":"For y = a/x + q the vertical asymptote is always x = 0 and the horizontal asymptote is y = q = 2. The a-value (−4) only decides the quadrants and the shape, not the asymptotes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die y-afsnit van y = 3 · 2ˣ − 5 is (0; ___).","en":"The y-intercept of y = 3 · 2ˣ − 5 is (0; ___)."},"answers":{"af":["-2","−2","y = -2","y=-2","y = −2","y=−2","(0;-2)","(0;−2)"],"en":["-2","−2","y = -2","y=-2","y = −2","y=−2","(0;-2)","(0;−2)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel x = 0: 2⁰ = 1, dus y = 3(1) − 5 = −2. Die y-afsnit is (0; −2). Kortpad: die y-afsnit is a + q = 3 + (−5).","en":"Let x = 0: 2⁰ = 1, so y = 3(1) − 5 = −2. The y-intercept is (0; −2). Shortcut: the y-intercept is a + q = 3 + (−5)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","-5","-8"],"en":["1","-5","-8"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hiperbool y = 6/x + 2 sny die x-as by x = ___.","en":"The hyperbola y = 6/x + 2 cuts the x-axis at x = ___."},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","x = -3","x=-3","x = −3","x=−3","(-3;0)","(−3;0)","(-3,0)","(−3,0)"],"en":["-3","−3","x = -3","x=-3","x = −3","x=−3","(-3;0)","(−3;0)","(-3,0)","(−3,0)"]},"explain":{"af":"Stel y = 0: 6/x + 2 = 0 → 6/x = −2 → 6 = −2x → x = −3. Die x-afsnit is (−3; 0).","en":"Let y = 0: 6/x + 2 = 0 → 6/x = −2 → 6 = −2x → x = −3. The x-intercept is (−3; 0)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","-12","2"],"en":["3","-12","2"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = 5 · (0,4)ˣ is afnemend (dalend).","en":"The graph of y = 5 · (0.4)ˣ is decreasing."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die grondtal 0,4 lê tussen 0 en 1 en a = 5 > 0, dus word die y-waardes kleiner soos x groter word: eksponensiële verval.","en":"True. The base 0.4 lies between 0 and 1 and a = 5 > 0, so the y-values get smaller as x gets bigger: exponential decay."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van f(x) = −2 · 3ˣ + 4?","en":"What is the range of f(x) = −2 · 3ˣ + 4?"},"options":[{"af":"y > 4","en":"y > 4"},{"af":"y < 4","en":"y < 4"},{"af":"y ≤ 4","en":"y ≤ 4"},{"af":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ 4","en":"y ∈ ℝ, y ≠ 4"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die asimptoot is y = 4. a = −2 < 0, dus lê die grafiek onder die asimptoot: y < 4. Gebruik < en nie ≤ nie, want die asimptoot word nooit bereik nie. \"y ≠ 4\" is die soort waardeversameling wat 'n hiperbool het.","en":"The asymptote is y = 4. a = −2 < 0, so the graph lies below the asymptote: y < 4. Use < and not ≤, because the asymptote is never reached. \"y ≠ 4\" is the kind of range a hyperbola has."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die x-afsnit van g(x) = 2ˣ − 8?","en":"What is the x-intercept of g(x) = 2ˣ − 8?"},"options":[{"af":"(3; 0)","en":"(3; 0)"},{"af":"(4; 0)","en":"(4; 0)"},{"af":"(0; −7)","en":"(0; −7)"},{"af":"(−3; 0)","en":"(−3; 0)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Stel g(x) = 0: 2ˣ = 8 = 2³, dus x = 3. (4; 0) kom van 8 ÷ 2, maar 2ˣ beteken nie 2 × x nie. (0; −7) is die y-afsnit.","en":"Let g(x) = 0: 2ˣ = 8 = 2³, so x = 3. (4; 0) comes from 8 ÷ 2, but 2ˣ does not mean 2 × x. (0; −7) is the y-intercept."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hiperbool y = a/x + q het 'n horisontale asimptoot y = −1 en gaan deur die punt (2; 3). Wat is die vergelyking van die hiperbool?","en":"The hyperbola y = a/x + q has a horizontal asymptote y = −1 and passes through the point (2; 3). What is the equation of the hyperbola?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 4/x − 1","en":"y = 4/x − 1"},{"af":"y = 8/x + 1","en":"y = 8/x + 1"},{"af":"y = 8/x − 1","en":"y = 8/x − 1"},{"af":"y = 2/x − 1","en":"y = 2/x − 1"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"q = −1. Vervang (2; 3): 3 = a/2 − 1 → a/2 = 4 → a = 8. Dus y = 8/x − 1. y = 4/x − 1 vergeet om met 2 te vermenigvuldig, y = 2/x − 1 deel in plaas daarvan, en y = 8/x + 1 het die verkeerde teken vir q.","en":"q = −1. Substitute (2; 3): 3 = a/2 − 1 → a/2 = 4 → a = 8. So y = 8/x − 1. y = 4/x − 1 forgets to multiply by 2, y = 2/x − 1 divides instead, and y = 8/x + 1 has the wrong sign for q."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = bˣ − 4 gaan deur die punt (2; 21). Bepaal b. b = ___","en":"The graph of y = bˣ − 4 passes through the point (2; 21). Determine b. b = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","b = 5","b=5"],"en":["5","b = 5","b=5"]},"explain":{"af":"21 = b² − 4 → b² = 25 → b = ±5. By 'n eksponensiële funksie moet die grondtal positief wees, dus b = 5 (verwerp −5).","en":"21 = b² − 4 → b² = 25 → b = ±5. In an exponential function the base must be positive, so b = 5 (reject −5)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−5","25","4,12"],"en":["−5","25","4.12"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gegee f(x) = 6/x en g(x) = x + 1. Wat is die snypunte van f en g?","en":"Given f(x) = 6/x and g(x) = x + 1. What are the points of intersection of f and g?"},"options":[{"af":"(−2; −3) en (3; 2)","en":"(−2; −3) and (3; 2)"},{"af":"(2; 3) en (−3; −2)","en":"(2; 3) and (−3; −2)"},{"af":"(0; 1) en (−1; 0)","en":"(0; 1) and (−1; 0)"},{"af":"Slegs (2; 3)","en":"Only (2; 3)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"6/x = x + 1 → 6 = x² + x → x² + x − 6 = 0 → (x + 3)(x − 2) = 0 → x = −3 of x = 2. g(−3) = −2 en g(2) = 3. Die hiperbool het twee takke, dus moenie die negatiewe oplossing weggooi nie. (−2; −3) en (3; 2) kom van 'n tekenfout in die faktore, en (0; 1) en (−1; 0) is net g se afsnitte.","en":"6/x = x + 1 → 6 = x² + x → x² + x − 6 = 0 → (x + 3)(x − 2) = 0 → x = −3 or x = 2. g(−3) = −2 and g(2) = 3. The hyperbola has two branches, so don't throw away the negative solution. (−2; −3) and (3; 2) come from a sign error in the factors, and (0; 1) and (−1; 0) are only the intercepts of g."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die aantal bakterieë in 'n watermonster uit die Hartbeespoortdam word gegee deur N = 200 · 2ᵗ, met t die tyd in ure. Na hoeveel uur is daar 3 200 bakterieë? ___ uur","en":"The number of bacteria in a water sample from Hartbeespoort Dam is given by N = 200 · 2ᵗ, with t the time in hours. After how many hours are there 3 200 bacteria? ___ hours"},"answers":{"af":["4","4 uur","t = 4","t=4","4 h","4h"],"en":["4","4 hours","t = 4","t=4","4 h","4h"]},"explain":{"af":"3 200 = 200 · 2ᵗ → deel albei kante deur 200: 2ᵗ = 16 = 2⁴ → t = 4 uur. Moenie eers 200 · 2 = 400 uitwerk nie: die eksponent behoort net by die 2.","en":"3 200 = 200 · 2ᵗ → divide both sides by 200: 2ᵗ = 16 = 2⁴ → t = 4 hours. Don't work out 200 · 2 = 400 first: the exponent belongs only to the 2."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["16","8","3"],"en":["16","8","3"]}}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-trig-grafieke","title":{"af":"Trigonometriese grafieke","en":"Trigonometric graphs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die grafieke van y = a sin θ + q, y = a cos θ + q en y = a tan θ + q kan skets, hul eienskappe kan neerskryf, a en q uit 'n grafiek kan bepaal en grafieke kan lees.","en":"You will be able to sketch the graphs of y = a sin θ + q, y = a cos θ + q and y = a tan θ + q, write down their properties, determine a and q from a graph and read graphs."},"summary":{"af":"## Die basiese grafieke vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°\n\nLeer hierdie sleutelpunte. Elke skets begin hier.\n\n| θ | 0° | 90° | 180° | 270° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin θ | 0 | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 |\n| cos θ | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 | 1 |\n\n| θ | 0° | 45° | 90° | 135° | 180° | 225° | 270° | 315° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| tan θ | 0 | 1 | ongedefinieerd | −1 | 0 | 1 | ongedefinieerd | −1 | 0 |\n\n| Eienskap | y = sin θ | y = cos θ | y = tan θ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Periode | 360° | 360° | 180° |\n| Amplitude | 1 | 1 | geen |\n| Maksimum | 1 by θ = 90° | 1 by θ = 0° en 360° | geen |\n| Minimum | −1 by θ = 270° | −1 by θ = 180° | geen |\n| Waardeversameling | [−1; 1] | [−1; 1] | y ∈ ℝ |\n| Asimptote | geen | geen | θ = 90° en θ = 270° |\n| Snypunte met die θ-as | 0°, 180°, 360° | 90°, 270° | 0°, 180°, 360° |\n\n- **Periode:** die horisontale lengte van een volledige siklus (een golf) voordat die patroon herhaal.\n- **Amplitude:** die helfte van die verskil tussen die maksimum- en minimumwaarde: amplitude = [[maks − min/2]]. Dit is altyd positief.\n- **Definisieversameling:** in Gr 10 altyd 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. By 90° en 270° is tan θ ongedefinieerd. Daar is **vertikale asimptote** (stippellyne) wat die grafiek nooit raak nie.\n\n## Die effek van a: y = a sin θ, y = a cos θ, y = a tan θ\n\n- Elke y-waarde word met a vermenigvuldig. Die **amplitude word |a|**: y = 3 sin θ wissel tussen −3 en 3.\n- As a < 0, word die grafiek in die x-as **gereflekteer** (onderstebo gedraai). y = −2 cos θ begin dus by (0°; −2).\n- By tan verander a die steilheid: die punt (45°; 1) skuif na (45°; a).\n- a verander **nie** die periode of die asimptote nie.\n\n## Die effek van q: y = a sin θ + q, ens.\n\n- Die hele grafiek skuif **vertikaal** met q eenhede: op as q > 0 en af as q < 0.\n- Die golf beweeg nou op en af om die lyn y = q.\n- Maksimum = q + |a| en minimum = q − |a|, dus is die waardeversameling [q − |a|; q + |a|].\n- q verander **nie** die amplitude, die periode of tan se asimptote nie. Vir y = a tan θ + q bly die waardeversameling y ∈ ℝ.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** By y = 2 cos θ − 1 is die amplitude 2, nie 1 of 3 nie. q skuif die grafiek net op of af.\n\n## Hoe om te skets\n\n1. Identifiseer die basiese grafiek, a en q.\n2. Maak 'n tabel met die sleutelpunte: vermenigvuldig die basiese y-waardes met a en tel dan q by.\n3. Stip die punte en trek 'n gladde kromme. Golwe het ronde draaipunte, nie skerp punte nie.\n4. Benoem die grafiek, die y-afsnit, die draaipunte en die eindpunte. By tan trek jy die asimptote θ = 90° en θ = 270° as stippellyne.\n\nVoorbeeld: y = 2 sin θ + 1 gaan deur (0°; 1), (90°; 3), (180°; 1), (270°; −1) en (360°; 1). Die amplitude is 2 en die waardeversameling [−1; 3].\n\n## Bepaal a en q uit 'n grafiek\n\n**sin en cos:** q = [[maks + min/2]] en |a| = [[maks − min/2]].\n\n- **Teken van a:** As y = a sin θ + q vanaf (0°; q) eers **afgaan**, is a < 0. As y = a cos θ + q by θ = 0° 'n **minimum** het, is a < 0.\n- Of vervang twee punte en los gelyktydig op. Bv. y = a cos θ + q gaan deur (0°; 5) en (180°; 1): a + q = 5 en −a + q = 1, dus q = 3 en a = 2.\n\n**tan:** By θ = 0° is tan θ = 0, dus lê (0°; q) op die grafiek. By θ = 45° is tan θ = 1, dus lê (45°; a + q) op die grafiek.\n\n## Lees van grafieke\n\n- **Snypunte van f en g:** waar f(θ) = g(θ). Bv. y = sin θ en y = cos θ sny by θ = 45° en θ = 225°.\n- **f(θ) > g(θ):** waar die grafiek van f bó dié van g lê. Gebruik streng ongelykhede (die tekens > en <), want by die snypunte is f(θ) = g(θ). Die tekens ≥ en ≤ sluit die snypunte in.\n- **f(θ) × g(θ) < 0:** waar een grafiek bo en die ander onder die θ-as lê (teenoorgestelde tekens).\n- **Toenemend en afnemend:** y = sin θ neem toe vir 0° < θ < 90° en 270° < θ < 360°; y = cos θ neem af vir 0° < θ < 180°.\n- **Aantal oplossings:** Die vergelyking f(θ) = k het soveel oplossings as wat die horisontale lyn y = k die grafiek sny.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skryf 'n waardeversameling as [min; maks] of as min ≤ y ≤ maks. Vierkantige hakies sluit die eindpunte in.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** tan θ het geen amplitude, maksimum of minimum nie. Die punt (45°; 1) is net 'n punt op die kromme, nie 'n draaipunt nie.","en":"## The basic graphs for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°\n\nLearn these key points. Every sketch starts here.\n\n| θ | 0° | 90° | 180° | 270° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sin θ | 0 | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 |\n| cos θ | 1 | 0 | −1 | 0 | 1 |\n\n| θ | 0° | 45° | 90° | 135° | 180° | 225° | 270° | 315° | 360° |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| tan θ | 0 | 1 | undefined | −1 | 0 | 1 | undefined | −1 | 0 |\n\n| Property | y = sin θ | y = cos θ | y = tan θ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Period | 360° | 360° | 180° |\n| Amplitude | 1 | 1 | none |\n| Maximum | 1 at θ = 90° | 1 at θ = 0° and 360° | none |\n| Minimum | −1 at θ = 270° | −1 at θ = 180° | none |\n| Range | [−1; 1] | [−1; 1] | y ∈ ℝ |\n| Asymptotes | none | none | θ = 90° and θ = 270° |\n| Intercepts with the θ-axis | 0°, 180°, 360° | 90°, 270° | 0°, 180°, 360° |\n\n- **Period:** the horizontal length of one complete cycle (one wave) before the pattern repeats.\n- **Amplitude:** half the difference between the maximum and minimum values: amplitude = [[max − min/2]]. It is always positive.\n- **Domain:** in Gr 10 always 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. At 90° and 270° tan θ is undefined. There are **vertical asymptotes** (dotted lines) that the graph never touches.\n\n## The effect of a: y = a sin θ, y = a cos θ, y = a tan θ\n\n- Every y-value is multiplied by a. The **amplitude becomes |a|**: y = 3 sin θ varies between −3 and 3.\n- If a < 0, the graph is **reflected** in the x-axis (turned upside down). So y = −2 cos θ starts at (0°; −2).\n- For tan, a changes the steepness: the point (45°; 1) moves to (45°; a).\n- a does **not** change the period or the asymptotes.\n\n## The effect of q: y = a sin θ + q, etc.\n\n- The whole graph shifts **vertically** by q units: up if q > 0 and down if q < 0.\n- The wave now moves up and down around the line y = q.\n- Maximum = q + |a| and minimum = q − |a|, so the range is [q − |a|; q + |a|].\n- q does **not** change the amplitude, the period or the asymptotes of tan. For y = a tan θ + q the range stays y ∈ ℝ.\n\n> **Common mistake:** For y = 2 cos θ − 1 the amplitude is 2, not 1 or 3. q only moves the graph up or down.\n\n## How to sketch\n\n1. Identify the basic graph, a and q.\n2. Make a table of the key points: multiply the basic y-values by a and then add q.\n3. Plot the points and draw a smooth curve. Waves have rounded turning points, not sharp points.\n4. Label the graph, the y-intercept, the turning points and the end points. For tan, draw the asymptotes θ = 90° and θ = 270° as dotted lines.\n\nExample: y = 2 sin θ + 1 passes through (0°; 1), (90°; 3), (180°; 1), (270°; −1) and (360°; 1). The amplitude is 2 and the range [−1; 3].\n\n## Determining a and q from a graph\n\n**sin and cos:** q = [[max + min/2]] and |a| = [[max − min/2]].\n\n- **Sign of a:** If y = a sin θ + q first goes **down** from (0°; q), then a < 0. If y = a cos θ + q has a **minimum** at θ = 0°, then a < 0.\n- Or substitute two points and solve simultaneously. E.g. y = a cos θ + q passes through (0°; 5) and (180°; 1): a + q = 5 and −a + q = 1, so q = 3 and a = 2.\n\n**tan:** At θ = 0°, tan θ = 0, so (0°; q) lies on the graph. At θ = 45°, tan θ = 1, so (45°; a + q) lies on the graph.\n\n## Reading graphs\n\n- **Points of intersection of f and g:** where f(θ) = g(θ). E.g. y = sin θ and y = cos θ intersect at θ = 45° and θ = 225°.\n- **f(θ) > g(θ):** where the graph of f lies above that of g. Use strict inequalities (the signs > and <), because at the points of intersection f(θ) = g(θ). The signs ≥ and ≤ include the points of intersection.\n- **f(θ) × g(θ) < 0:** where one graph lies above and the other below the θ-axis (opposite signs).\n- **Increasing and decreasing:** y = sin θ increases for 0° < θ < 90° and 270° < θ < 360°; y = cos θ decreases for 0° < θ < 180°.\n- **Number of solutions:** The equation f(θ) = k has as many solutions as the number of times the horizontal line y = k cuts the graph.\n\n> **Tip:** Write a range as [min; max] or as min ≤ y ≤ max. Square brackets include the end points.\n\n> **Common mistake:** tan θ has no amplitude, maximum or minimum. The point (45°; 1) is just a point on the curve, not a turning point."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Periode","en":"Period"},"def":{"af":"Die horisontale lengte van een volledige siklus van die grafiek: 360° vir sin en cos, 180° vir tan.","en":"The horizontal length of one complete cycle of the graph: 360° for sin and cos, 180° for tan."}},{"term":{"af":"Amplitude","en":"Amplitude"},"def":{"af":"Die helfte van die verskil tussen die maksimum- en minimumwaarde van 'n sin- of cos-grafiek; vir y = a sin θ + q is dit |a|.","en":"Half the difference between the maximum and minimum values of a sin or cos graph; for y = a sin θ + q it is |a|."}},{"term":{"af":"Waardeversameling","en":"Range"},"def":{"af":"Al die y-waardes wat die grafiek aanneem, bv. [q − |a|; q + |a|] vir sin en cos.","en":"All the y-values the graph takes on, e.g. [q − |a|; q + |a|] for sin and cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Definisieversameling","en":"Domain"},"def":{"af":"Al die θ-waardes waarvoor die grafiek geskets word; in Gr 10 is dit 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°.","en":"All the θ-values for which the graph is sketched; in Gr 10 it is 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°."}},{"term":{"af":"Asimptoot","en":"Asymptote"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn wat die grafiek nader maar nooit raak nie; y = tan θ het vertikale asimptote by θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"A line that the graph approaches but never touches; y = tan θ has vertical asymptotes at θ = 90° and θ = 270°."}},{"term":{"af":"Maksimum- en minimumwaarde","en":"Maximum and minimum value"},"def":{"af":"Die grootste en kleinste y-waarde van die grafiek: q + |a| en q − |a| vir sin en cos.","en":"The greatest and smallest y-value of the graph: q + |a| and q − |a| for sin and cos."}},{"term":{"af":"Vertikale skuif","en":"Vertical shift"},"def":{"af":"Die effek van q: die hele grafiek skuif q eenhede op (q > 0) of af (q < 0).","en":"The effect of q: the whole graph moves q units up (q > 0) or down (q < 0)."}},{"term":{"af":"Refleksie in die x-as","en":"Reflection in the x-axis"},"def":{"af":"Die effek van a < 0: die grafiek word onderstebo gedraai, sodat maksimums minimums word.","en":"The effect of a < 0: the graph is turned upside down, so maximums become minimums."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van y = a cos θ + q","en":"Properties of y = a cos θ + q"},"problem":{"af":"Beskou f(θ) = 3 cos θ + 1 vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. (a) Bepaal die sleutelpunte vir 'n skets. (b) Skryf die amplitude, periode, maksimum- en minimumwaarde en die waardeversameling neer.","en":"Consider f(θ) = 3 cos θ + 1 for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. (a) Determine the key points for a sketch. (b) Write down the amplitude, period, maximum and minimum value and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"Basiese cos-waardes by θ = 0°; 90°; 180°; 270°; 360° is 1; 0; −1; 0; 1.","en":"Basic cos values at θ = 0°; 90°; 180°; 270°; 360° are 1; 0; −1; 0; 1."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 3 en tel 1 by: 3(1) + 1 = 4; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(−1) + 1 = −2; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(1) + 1 = 4","en":"Multiply by 3 and add 1: 3(1) + 1 = 4; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(−1) + 1 = −2; 3(0) + 1 = 1; 3(1) + 1 = 4"},{"af":"(a) Sleutelpunte: (0°; 4), (90°; 1), (180°; −2), (270°; 1), (360°; 4). Stip hulle en trek 'n gladde kromme.","en":"(a) Key points: (0°; 4), (90°; 1), (180°; −2), (270°; 1), (360°; 4). Plot them and draw a smooth curve."},{"af":"(b) Amplitude = |a| = 3 (kontrole: [[4 − (−2)/2]] = 3). Periode = 360°, want a en q verander nie die periode nie.","en":"(b) Amplitude = |a| = 3 (check: [[4 − (−2)/2]] = 3). Period = 360°, because a and q do not change the period."},{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = 4 by θ = 0° en 360°; minimum = q − |a| = −2 by θ = 180°. Waardeversameling: [−2; 4], of −2 ≤ y ≤ 4.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = 4 at θ = 0° and 360°; minimum = q − |a| = −2 at θ = 180°. Range: [−2; 4], or −2 ≤ y ≤ 4."}],"answer":{"af":"Amplitude 3; periode 360°; maksimum 4; minimum −2; waardeversameling [−2; 4]","en":"Amplitude 3; period 360°; maximum 4; minimum −2; range [−2; 4]"}},{"title":{"af":"Die tan-grafiek met a en q","en":"The tan graph with a and q"},"problem":{"af":"Beskou g(θ) = 2 tan θ − 1 vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Bepaal (a) die vergelykings van die asimptote, (b) die punte by θ = 0°, 45°, 135° en 180°, (c) die periode en die waardeversameling.","en":"Consider g(θ) = 2 tan θ − 1 for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Determine (a) the equations of the asymptotes, (b) the points at θ = 0°, 45°, 135° and 180°, (c) the period and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) a en q skuif nie die asimptote nie: θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"(a) a and q do not move the asymptotes: θ = 90° and θ = 270°."},{"af":"(b) Basiese tan-waardes by 0°; 45°; 135°; 180° is 0; 1; −1; 0.","en":"(b) Basic tan values at 0°; 45°; 135°; 180° are 0; 1; −1; 0."},{"af":"Vermenigvuldig met 2 en trek 1 af: (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1).","en":"Multiply by 2 and subtract 1: (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1)."},{"af":"(c) Periode = 180°: die patroon herhaal elke 180°. Waardeversameling: y ∈ ℝ, want 'n tan-grafiek het geen maksimum of minimum nie.","en":"(c) Period = 180°: the pattern repeats every 180°. Range: y ∈ ℝ, because a tan graph has no maximum or minimum."}],"answer":{"af":"Asimptote θ = 90° en θ = 270°; (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1); periode 180°; y ∈ ℝ","en":"Asymptotes θ = 90° and θ = 270°; (0°; −1), (45°; 1), (135°; −3), (180°; −1); period 180°; y ∈ ℝ"}},{"title":{"af":"Bepaal a en q uit die maksimum en minimum","en":"Determine a and q from the maximum and minimum"},"problem":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a sin θ + q het 'n minimum van −5 by θ = 90° en 'n maksimum van 1 by θ = 270°. Bepaal a en q, en skryf die y-afsnit en die waardeversameling neer.","en":"The graph of y = a sin θ + q has a minimum of −5 at θ = 90° and a maximum of 1 at θ = 270°. Determine a and q, and write down the y-intercept and the range."},"steps":[{"af":"q = [[maks + min/2]] = [[1 + (−5)/2]] = −2","en":"q = [[max + min/2]] = [[1 + (−5)/2]] = −2"},{"af":"|a| = [[maks − min/2]] = [[1 − (−5)/2]] = 3","en":"|a| = [[max − min/2]] = [[1 − (−5)/2]] = 3"},{"af":"'n Gewone sin-grafiek het sy maksimum by 90°. Hierdie een het 'n minimum by 90°, dus is dit gereflekteer: a = −3.","en":"An ordinary sin graph has its maximum at 90°. This one has a minimum at 90°, so it is reflected: a = −3."},{"af":"Kontrole: θ = 90°: y = −3(1) − 2 = −5 ✓ en θ = 270°: y = −3(−1) − 2 = 1 ✓","en":"Check: θ = 90°: y = −3(1) − 2 = −5 ✓ and θ = 270°: y = −3(−1) − 2 = 1 ✓"},{"af":"y-afsnit: by θ = 0° is y = −3(0) − 2 = −2, dus (0°; −2). Waardeversameling: [−5; 1].","en":"y-intercept: at θ = 0°, y = −3(0) − 2 = −2, so (0°; −2). Range: [−5; 1]."}],"answer":{"af":"a = −3 en q = −2, dus y = −3 sin θ − 2; y-afsnit (0°; −2); waardeversameling [−5; 1]","en":"a = −3 and q = −2, so y = −3 sin θ − 2; y-intercept (0°; −2); range [−5; 1]"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees twee grafieke saam","en":"Reading two graphs together"},"problem":{"af":"f(θ) = 2 sin θ en g(θ) = −2 cos θ vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. Die grafieke sny by θ = 135° en θ = 315°. Bepaal: (a) waar f(θ) > g(θ); (b) waar f(θ) × g(θ) < 0; (c) die waardeversameling van h(θ) = g(θ) + 3.","en":"f(θ) = 2 sin θ and g(θ) = −2 cos θ for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°. The graphs intersect at θ = 135° and θ = 315°. Determine: (a) where f(θ) > g(θ); (b) where f(θ) × g(θ) < 0; (c) the range of h(θ) = g(θ) + 3."},"steps":[{"af":"Sleutelpunte. f: (0°; 0), (90°; 2), (180°; 0), (270°; −2), (360°; 0). g is die grafiek van 2 cos θ, gereflekteer in die x-as: (0°; −2), (90°; 0), (180°; 2), (270°; 0), (360°; −2).","en":"Key points. f: (0°; 0), (90°; 2), (180°; 0), (270°; −2), (360°; 0). g is the graph of 2 cos θ, reflected in the x-axis: (0°; −2), (90°; 0), (180°; 2), (270°; 0), (360°; −2)."},{"af":"(a) By θ = 0° is f = 0 en g = −2, dus begin f bó g. Tussen die snypunte 135° en 315° lê g bo f (bv. by 180°: f = 0 en g = 2). Na 315° is f weer bo.","en":"(a) At θ = 0°, f = 0 and g = −2, so f starts above g. Between the intersections 135° and 315°, g lies above f (e.g. at 180°: f = 0 and g = 2). After 315°, f is above again."},{"af":"f(θ) > g(θ) vir 0° ≤ θ < 135° of 315° < θ ≤ 360°","en":"f(θ) > g(θ) for 0° ≤ θ < 135° or 315° < θ ≤ 360°"},{"af":"(b) Die produk is negatief as f en g teenoorgestelde tekens het. f > 0 vir 0° < θ < 180°, en g > 0 vir 90° < θ < 270°.","en":"(b) The product is negative when f and g have opposite signs. f > 0 for 0° < θ < 180°, and g > 0 for 90° < θ < 270°."},{"af":"Teenoorgestelde tekens: 0° < θ < 90° (f positief, g negatief) of 180° < θ < 270° (f negatief, g positief).","en":"Opposite signs: 0° < θ < 90° (f positive, g negative) or 180° < θ < 270° (f negative, g positive)."},{"af":"(c) h(θ) = −2 cos θ + 3: maksimum = 3 + 2 = 5 en minimum = 3 − 2 = 1. Waardeversameling [1; 5].","en":"(c) h(θ) = −2 cos θ + 3: maximum = 3 + 2 = 5 and minimum = 3 − 2 = 1. Range [1; 5]."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0° ≤ θ < 135° of 315° < θ ≤ 360°; (b) 0° < θ < 90° of 180° < θ < 270°; (c) [1; 5]","en":"(a) 0° ≤ θ < 135° or 315° < θ ≤ 360°; (b) 0° < θ < 90° or 180° < θ < 270°; (c) [1; 5]"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die periode van y = tan θ?","en":"What is the period of y = tan θ?"},"options":[{"af":"360°","en":"360°"},{"af":"90°","en":"90°"},{"af":"180°","en":"180°"},{"af":"Dit het geen periode nie","en":"It has no period"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"tan θ herhaal elke 180°: van (0°; 0) tot (180°; 0) is een volledige siklus. 360° is die periode van sin en cos, en 90° is net die afstand van 'n afsnit tot 'n asimptoot.","en":"tan θ repeats every 180°: from (0°; 0) to (180°; 0) is one complete cycle. 360° is the period of sin and cos, and 90° is only the distance from an intercept to an asymptote."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke eienskap by die regte waarde.","en":"Match each property to the correct value."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Amplitude van y = 3 sin θ","en":"Amplitude of y = 3 sin θ"},"r":{"af":"3","en":"3"}},{"l":{"af":"Periode van y = cos θ","en":"Period of y = cos θ"},"r":{"af":"360°","en":"360°"}},{"l":{"af":"Asimptote van y = tan θ","en":"Asymptotes of y = tan θ"},"r":{"af":"θ = 90° en θ = 270°","en":"θ = 90° and θ = 270°"}},{"l":{"af":"Waardeversameling van y = sin θ","en":"Range of y = sin θ"},"r":{"af":"[−1; 1]","en":"[−1; 1]"}}],"explain":{"af":"Amplitude = |a| = 3. sin en cos herhaal elke 360°. tan θ is ongedefinieerd by 90° en 270°. sin θ wissel tussen −1 en 1.","en":"Amplitude = |a| = 3. sin and cos repeat every 360°. tan θ is undefined at 90° and 270°. sin θ varies between −1 and 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = tan θ het 'n amplitude van 1.","en":"The graph of y = tan θ has an amplitude of 1."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. tan θ het geen maksimum of minimum nie (die waardeversameling is ℝ), dus het dit geen amplitude nie. Die punt (45°; 1) is nie 'n draaipunt nie.","en":"False. tan θ has no maximum or minimum (the range is ℝ), so it has no amplitude. The point (45°; 1) is not a turning point."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By watter waarde van θ het y = cos θ sy minimum vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°?","en":"At which value of θ does y = cos θ have its minimum for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°?"},"options":[{"af":"90°","en":"90°"},{"af":"270°","en":"270°"},{"af":"0°","en":"0°"},{"af":"180°","en":"180°"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"cos θ begin by 1 (θ = 0°), sak tot −1 by θ = 180° en klim terug tot 1 by 360°. By 270° het sin θ sy minimum, en by 90° is cos θ = 0.","en":"cos θ starts at 1 (θ = 0°), drops to −1 at θ = 180° and climbs back to 1 at 360°. At 270° sin θ has its minimum, and at 90° cos θ = 0."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die amplitude van y = −4 sin θ + 2? Amplitude = ___","en":"What is the amplitude of y = −4 sin θ + 2? Amplitude = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4"],"en":["4"]},"explain":{"af":"Amplitude = |a| = |−4| = 4. 'n Amplitude is altyd positief, en q = 2 verander dit nie. (Kontrole: maksimum 6, minimum −2, en (6 − (−2)) ÷ 2 = 4.)","en":"Amplitude = |a| = |−4| = 4. An amplitude is always positive, and q = 2 does not change it. (Check: maximum 6, minimum −2, and (6 − (−2)) ÷ 2 = 4.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−4","6","2"],"en":["−4","6","2"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die waardeversameling van y = 3 cos θ − 1?","en":"What is the range of y = 3 cos θ − 1?"},"options":[{"af":"[−3; 3]","en":"[−3; 3]"},{"af":"[−4; 2]","en":"[−4; 2]"},{"af":"[−2; 4]","en":"[−2; 4]"},{"af":"[−2; 2]","en":"[−2; 2]"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = −1 + 3 = 2 en minimum = q − |a| = −1 − 3 = −4, dus [−4; 2]. [−3; 3] ignoreer q, [−2; 4] skuif op in plaas van af, en [−2; 2] verwar a + q met die amplitude.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = −1 + 3 = 2 and minimum = q − |a| = −1 − 3 = −4, so [−4; 2]. [−3; 3] ignores q, [−2; 4] shifts up instead of down, and [−2; 2] confuses a + q with the amplitude."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die maksimumwaarde van y = 2 sin θ + 3? Maksimum = ___","en":"What is the maximum value of y = 2 sin θ + 3? Maximum = ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","y = 5","y=5"],"en":["5","y = 5","y=5"]},"explain":{"af":"Maksimum = q + |a| = 3 + 2 = 5. Dit gebeur by θ = 90°, waar sin θ = 1.","en":"Maximum = q + |a| = 3 + 2 = 5. It happens at θ = 90°, where sin θ = 1."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","2","1"],"en":["3","2","1"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Grafiek vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360° het 'n y-afsnit by (0°; 3), 'n maksimum van 3, 'n minimum van −1 en 'n periode van 360°. Watter vergelyking pas?","en":"A graph for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360° has a y-intercept at (0°; 3), a maximum of 3, a minimum of −1 and a period of 360°. Which equation fits?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 2 sin θ + 1","en":"y = 2 sin θ + 1"},{"af":"y = 3 cos θ","en":"y = 3 cos θ"},{"af":"y = 2 cos θ + 1","en":"y = 2 cos θ + 1"},{"af":"y = 2 cos θ + 3","en":"y = 2 cos θ + 3"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"q = (3 + (−1)) ÷ 2 = 1 en |a| = (3 − (−1)) ÷ 2 = 2. Die maksimum lê op die y-as (θ = 0°), wat by 'n cos-grafiek met a > 0 gebeur. Dus y = 2 cos θ + 1. y = 2 sin θ + 1 gaan deur (0°; 1), y = 3 cos θ het 'n minimum van −3, en y = 2 cos θ + 3 neem q verkeerdelik as die y-afsnit.","en":"q = (3 + (−1)) ÷ 2 = 1 and |a| = (3 − (−1)) ÷ 2 = 2. The maximum lies on the y-axis (θ = 0°), which happens for a cos graph with a > 0. So y = 2 cos θ + 1. y = 2 sin θ + 1 passes through (0°; 1), y = 3 cos θ has a minimum of −3, and y = 2 cos θ + 3 wrongly takes q as the y-intercept."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die asimptote van y = −3 tan θ + 2 is θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"The asymptotes of y = −3 tan θ + 2 are θ = 90° and θ = 270°."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. a rek en reflekteer die grafiek en q skuif dit op of af, maar die asimptote is vertikale lyne. Hulle bly by θ = 90° en θ = 270°.","en":"True. a stretches and reflects the graph and q moves it up or down, but the asymptotes are vertical lines. They stay at θ = 90° and θ = 270°."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a tan θ + q gaan deur (0°; −2) en (45°; 1). Bepaal a en q.","en":"The graph of y = a tan θ + q passes through (0°; −2) and (45°; 1). Determine a and q."},"options":[{"af":"a = 3; q = −2","en":"a = 3; q = −2"},{"af":"a = 1; q = −2","en":"a = 1; q = −2"},{"af":"a = −2; q = 3","en":"a = −2; q = 3"},{"af":"a = −3; q = −2","en":"a = −3; q = −2"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By θ = 0° is tan 0° = 0, dus y = q = −2. By θ = 45° is tan 45° = 1: a(1) − 2 = 1, dus a = 3. Moenie a gelyk stel aan die y-waarde by 45° nie; trek eers q af.","en":"At θ = 0°, tan 0° = 0, so y = q = −2. At θ = 45°, tan 45° = 1: a(1) − 2 = 1, so a = 3. Do not set a equal to the y-value at 45°; subtract q first."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grafiek van y = a cos θ + q gaan deur (0°; −1) en (180°; 5). Wat is die waarde van a? a = ___","en":"The graph of y = a cos θ + q passes through (0°; −1) and (180°; 5). What is the value of a? a = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3","−3","a = -3","a = −3","a=-3","a=−3"],"en":["-3","−3","a = -3","a = −3","a=-3","a=−3"]},"explain":{"af":"θ = 0°: a(1) + q = −1. θ = 180°: a(−1) + q = 5. Trek af: 2a = −6, dus a = −3 (en q = 2). a is negatief, want die grafiek het 'n minimum by θ = 0°.","en":"θ = 0°: a(1) + q = −1. θ = 180°: a(−1) + q = 5. Subtract: 2a = −6, so a = −3 (and q = 2). a is negative, because the graph has a minimum at θ = 0°."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","2","-6"],"en":["3","2","-6"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"f(θ) = sin θ en g(θ) = cos θ sny by θ = 45° en θ = 225° (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). Vir watter waardes van θ is f(θ) > g(θ)?","en":"f(θ) = sin θ and g(θ) = cos θ intersect at θ = 45° and θ = 225° (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). For which values of θ is f(θ) > g(θ)?"},"options":[{"af":"0° ≤ θ < 45° of 225° < θ ≤ 360°","en":"0° ≤ θ < 45° or 225° < θ ≤ 360°"},{"af":"45° ≤ θ ≤ 225°","en":"45° ≤ θ ≤ 225°"},{"af":"90° < θ < 270°","en":"90° < θ < 270°"},{"af":"45° < θ < 225°","en":"45° < θ < 225°"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By θ = 90° is sin θ = 1 en cos θ = 0, dus lê f tussen die snypunte bó g: 45° < θ < 225°. Gebruik streng ongelykhede, want by 45° en 225° is f(θ) = g(θ). Die eerste opsie is waar g bo f lê.","en":"At θ = 90°, sin θ = 1 and cos θ = 0, so between the intersections f lies above g: 45° < θ < 225°. Use strict inequalities, because at 45° and 225° f(θ) = g(θ). The first option is where g lies above f."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir watter waarde van k (k > 0) het die vergelyking 3 sin θ + 1 = k presies een oplossing vir 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°? k = ___","en":"For which value of k (k > 0) does the equation 3 sin θ + 1 = k have exactly one solution for 0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°? k = ___"},"answers":{"af":["4","k = 4","k=4"],"en":["4","k = 4","k=4"]},"explain":{"af":"Die horisontale lyn y = k sny y = 3 sin θ + 1 net een keer by die maksimum (90°; 4) of die minimum (270°; −2). Omdat k > 0, is k = 4. Vir enige k tussen −2 en 4 is daar twee of drie snypunte.","en":"The horizontal line y = k cuts y = 3 sin θ + 1 only once at the maximum (90°; 4) or the minimum (270°; −2). Because k > 0, k = 4. For any k between −2 and 4 there are two or three points of intersection."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−2","3","1"],"en":["−2","3","1"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hoogte h (in meter) bo die grond van 'n sitplek op 'n reuse-wiel (Ferriswiel) by 'n kermis in Pretoria word gegee deur h = −15 cos θ + 17, waar θ die hoek is waardeur die wiel gedraai het (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). Wat is die deursnee van die wiel?","en":"The height h (in metres) above the ground of a seat on a Ferris wheel at a fair in Pretoria is given by h = −15 cos θ + 17, where θ is the angle through which the wheel has turned (0° ≤ θ ≤ 360°). What is the diameter of the wheel?"},"options":[{"af":"15 m","en":"15 m"},{"af":"30 m","en":"30 m"},{"af":"32 m","en":"32 m"},{"af":"17 m","en":"17 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die amplitude is |−15| = 15 m: die sitplek gaan 15 m bo en 15 m onder die as van die wiel. Dit is die radius, dus is die deursnee 2 × 15 = 30 m. (Hoogste punt 17 + 15 = 32 m, laagste punt 17 − 15 = 2 m, en 32 − 2 = 30 m.) 17 m is die hoogte van die as.","en":"The amplitude is |−15| = 15 m: the seat goes 15 m above and 15 m below the axle of the wheel. That is the radius, so the diameter is 2 × 15 = 30 m. (Highest point 17 + 15 = 32 m, lowest point 17 − 15 = 2 m, and 32 − 2 = 30 m.) 17 m is the height of the axle."}}]},{"id":"w10-t2-euklidiese-meetkunde","title":{"af":"Euklidiese meetkunde: vierhoeke en middelpuntstelling","en":"Euclidean geometry: quadrilaterals and midpoint theorem"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die eienskappe van vierhoeke en die middelpuntstelling kan gebruik om hoeke en lengtes te bereken en kort bewyse met korrekte redes te skryf.","en":"You will be able to use the properties of quadrilaterals and the midpoint theorem to calculate angles and lengths and write short proofs with correct reasons."},"summary":{"af":"## Hersiening: lyne, hoeke en driehoeke\n\nIn meetkunde kry elke bewering 'n **rede** tussen hakies. 'n Korrekte antwoord sonder 'n rede kos jou punte.\n\n- Hoeke op 'n reguit lyn tel op tot 180°. *(hoeke op 'n reguit lyn)*\n- Regoorstaande hoeke is gelyk. *(regoorst. ∠e)*\n- Hoeke om 'n punt tel op tot 360°. *(∠e om 'n punt)*\n- As AB || CD: ooreenkomstige hoeke is gelyk *(ooreenk. ∠e; AB || CD)*, verwisselende hoeke is gelyk *(verwiss. ∠e; AB || CD)* en ko-binnehoeke tel op tot 180° *(ko-binne ∠e; AB || CD)*.\n- Die binnehoeke van 'n driehoek tel op tot 180°. *(som ∠e van Δ)*\n- 'n Buitehoek van 'n driehoek is gelyk aan die som van die twee teenoorstaande binnehoeke. *(buite ∠ van Δ)*\n- In 'n gelykbenige driehoek is die hoeke teenoor die gelyke sye gelyk. *(∠e teenoor gelyke sye)*\n- In 'n reghoekige driehoek is skuinssy^{2} = die som van die kwadrate van die ander twee sye. *(Pyth.)*\n- Kongruente driehoeke (≡) bewys jy met SSS, SHS, HHS of 90°, skuinssy, sy.\n- Die binnehoeke van enige vierhoek tel op tot 360°.\n\n## Eienskappe van vierhoeke\n\n| Vierhoek | Sye | Hoeke | Hoeklyne |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig en gelyk | teenoorstaande hoeke gelyk | halveer mekaar |\n| Reghoek | soos 'n parallelogram | al vier hoeke 90° | halveer mekaar en is **ewe lank** |\n| Ruit | al vier sye gelyk; teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | teenoorstaande hoeke gelyk | halveer mekaar **loodreg** en halveer die hoeke van die ruit |\n| Vierkant | al vier sye gelyk; teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | al vier hoeke 90° | ewe lank, halveer mekaar loodreg en halveer die hoeke (45°) |\n| Trapesium | een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig | ko-binnehoeke tussen die ewewydige sye tel op tot 180° | geen spesiale eienskap nie |\n| Vlieër | twee pare **aangrensende** sye gelyk | die twee hoeke tussen die ongelyke sye is gelyk | sny mekaar loodreg; die hoeklyn deur die hoekpunte waar die gelyke sye ontmoet (die simmetrie-as) halveer die ander hoeklyn en die hoeke by sy eindpunte |\n\n**Families:** 'n Vierkant is 'n spesiale reghoek én 'n spesiale ruit, en reghoeke en ruite is spesiale parallelogramme. Alle eienskappe van 'n parallelogram geld dus ook vir 'n reghoek, ruit en vierkant – maar nie andersom nie.\n\nAs jy reeds wéét dit is 'n parallelogram, gebruik jy die redes *(teenoorst. sye van ||m)*, *(teenoorst. ∠e van ||m)* en *(hoekl. van ||m)*. Vir 'n ruit skryf jy *(hoekl. van ruit)* en vir 'n reghoek *(hoekl. van reghoek)*.\n\n## Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n parallelogram is\n\n'n Vierhoek is 'n parallelogram as **enige een** van hierdie vyf toetse waar is:\n\n1. Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig (die definisie). *(teenoorst. sye ||)*\n2. Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is gelyk. *(teenoorst. sye =)*\n3. Albei pare teenoorstaande hoeke is gelyk. *(teenoorst. ∠e =)*\n4. Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar. *(hoekl. halveer mekaar)*\n5. Een paar teenoorstaande sye is gelyk **en** ewewydig. *(een paar teenoorst. sye = en ||)*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig en die ander paar is gelyk\" is NIE 'n toets nie. 'n Gelykbenige trapesium het ook dié eienskap.\n\n**Stappe vir 'n kort bewys:** (1) skryf neer wat gegee is; (2) kies die toets wat by die gegewe inligting pas; (3) skryf elke bewering met sy rede; (4) sluit af met \"∴ ABCD is 'n parallelogram\" en die rede.\n\n## Die middelpuntstelling\n\nIn ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB en E die middelpunt van AC. Dan is:\n\n- DE || BC **en**\n- DE = [[1/2]]BC *(midpt-stelling)*\n\n**Omgekeerde:** As D die middelpunt van AB is en DE || BC (met E op AC), dan is E die middelpunt van AC. *(lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)*\n\n**Waarom dit werk:** Verleng DE tot by F sodat DE = EF. In vierhoek ADCF halveer die hoeklyne AC en DF mekaar by E, dus is ADCF 'n parallelogram. Dan is CF = AD = DB en CF || DB, dus is DBCF 'n parallelogram (een paar teenoorst. sye = en ||). Daarom is DF || BC en DF = BC, en DE = [[1/2]]DF = [[1/2]]BC.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jy die middelpunte van die vier sye van *enige* vierhoek verbind, kry jy 'n parallelogram. Elke sy van die nuwe vierhoek is ewewydig aan een van die oorspronklike hoeklyne en die helfte daarvan lank (midpt-stelling in twee driehoeke).\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Om te sê die hoeklyne van 'n ruit is ewe lank. Dit geld net vir 'n reghoek en 'n vierkant.\n- Om die midpt-stelling te gebruik as net **een** middelpunt gegee is. Dan het jy die omgekeerde nodig, en dit werk net as die lyn ewewydig aan die tweede sy is.\n- Om DE = 2BC te skryf in plaas van BC = 2DE.\n- Om die ewewydige lyne in die rede te vergeet: skryf *(ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)*, nie net *(ooreenk. ∠e)* nie.","en":"## Revision: lines, angles and triangles\n\nIn geometry every statement gets a **reason** in brackets. A correct answer without a reason costs you marks.\n\n- Angles on a straight line add up to 180°. *(∠s on a str line)*\n- Vertically opposite angles are equal. *(vert opp ∠s)*\n- Angles around a point add up to 360°. *(∠s round a pt)*\n- If AB || CD: corresponding angles are equal *(corresp ∠s; AB || CD)*, alternate angles are equal *(alt ∠s; AB || CD)* and co-interior angles add up to 180° *(co-int ∠s; AB || CD)*.\n- The interior angles of a triangle add up to 180°. *(sum of ∠s in Δ)*\n- An exterior angle of a triangle equals the sum of the two opposite interior angles. *(ext ∠ of Δ)*\n- In an isosceles triangle the angles opposite the equal sides are equal. *(∠s opp equal sides)*\n- In a right-angled triangle hypotenuse^{2} = the sum of the squares of the other two sides. *(Pyth)*\n- You prove triangles congruent (≡) with SSS, SAS, AAS or RHS.\n- The interior angles of any quadrilateral add up to 360°.\n\n## Properties of quadrilaterals\n\n| Quadrilateral | Sides | Angles | Diagonals |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | both pairs of opposite sides parallel and equal | opposite angles equal | bisect each other |\n| Rectangle | as for a parallelogram | all four angles 90° | bisect each other and are **equal in length** |\n| Rhombus | all four sides equal; opposite sides parallel | opposite angles equal | bisect each other **at right angles** and bisect the angles of the rhombus |\n| Square | all four sides equal; opposite sides parallel | all four angles 90° | equal, bisect each other at right angles and bisect the angles (45°) |\n| Trapezium | one pair of opposite sides parallel | co-interior angles between the parallel sides add up to 180° | no special property |\n| Kite | two pairs of **adjacent** sides equal | the two angles between the unequal sides are equal | cut at right angles; the diagonal through the vertices where the equal sides meet (the axis of symmetry) bisects the other diagonal and the angles at its ends |\n\n**Families:** A square is a special rectangle and a special rhombus, and rectangles and rhombuses are special parallelograms. So every property of a parallelogram also holds for a rectangle, rhombus and square – but not the other way round.\n\nIf you already know it is a parallelogram, use the reasons *(opp sides of ||m)*, *(opp ∠s of ||m)* and *(diags of ||m)*. For a rhombus write *(diags of rhombus)* and for a rectangle *(diags of rectangle)*.\n\n## Proving that a quadrilateral is a parallelogram\n\nA quadrilateral is a parallelogram if **any one** of these five tests is true:\n\n1. Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel (the definition). *(opp sides ||)*\n2. Both pairs of opposite sides are equal. *(opp sides =)*\n3. Both pairs of opposite angles are equal. *(opp ∠s =)*\n4. The diagonals bisect each other. *(diags bisect each other)*\n5. One pair of opposite sides is equal **and** parallel. *(one pair opp sides = and ||)*\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"One pair of opposite sides is parallel and the other pair is equal\" is NOT a test. An isosceles trapezium also has this property.\n\n**Steps for a short proof:** (1) write down what is given; (2) choose the test that matches the given information; (3) write every statement with its reason; (4) conclude with \"∴ ABCD is a parallelogram\" and the reason.\n\n## The midpoint theorem\n\nIn ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. Then:\n\n- DE || BC **and**\n- DE = [[1/2]]BC *(midpt theorem)*\n\n**Converse:** If D is the midpoint of AB and DE || BC (with E on AC), then E is the midpoint of AC. *(line through midpt || to 2nd side)*\n\n**Why it works:** Extend DE to F so that DE = EF. In quadrilateral ADCF the diagonals AC and DF bisect each other at E, so ADCF is a parallelogram. Then CF = AD = DB and CF || DB, so DBCF is a parallelogram (one pair opp sides = and ||). Therefore DF || BC and DF = BC, and DE = [[1/2]]DF = [[1/2]]BC.\n\n> **Tip:** If you join the midpoints of the four sides of *any* quadrilateral, you get a parallelogram. Each side of the new quadrilateral is parallel to one of the original diagonals and half as long (midpoint theorem in two triangles).\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Saying the diagonals of a rhombus are equal. That is only true for a rectangle and a square.\n- Using the midpoint theorem when only **one** midpoint is given. Then you need the converse, and it only works if the line is parallel to the second side.\n- Writing DE = 2BC instead of BC = 2DE.\n- Leaving the parallel lines out of the reason: write *(corresp ∠s; DE || BC)*, not just *(corresp ∠s)*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Parallelogram","en":"Parallelogram"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig.","en":"A quadrilateral with both pairs of opposite sides parallel."}},{"term":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},"def":{"af":"'n Parallelogram met al vier hoeke 90°; sy hoeklyne is ewe lank.","en":"A parallelogram with all four angles 90°; its diagonals are equal in length."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},"def":{"af":"'n Parallelogram met al vier sye ewe lank; sy hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg.","en":"A parallelogram with all four sides equal; its diagonals bisect each other at right angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},"def":{"af":"'n Reghoek met al vier sye gelyk – dit is ook 'n ruit met 90°-hoeke.","en":"A rectangle with all four sides equal – it is also a rhombus with 90° angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Trapesium","en":"Trapezium"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig.","en":"A quadrilateral with one pair of opposite sides parallel."}},{"term":{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"},"def":{"af":"'n Vierhoek met twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk; sy hoeklyne sny mekaar loodreg.","en":"A quadrilateral with two pairs of adjacent sides equal; its diagonals cut at right angles."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoeklyn","en":"Diagonal"},"def":{"af":"'n Lynstuk wat twee teenoorstaande hoekpunte van 'n vierhoek verbind.","en":"A line segment joining two opposite vertices of a quadrilateral."}},{"term":{"af":"Middelpuntstelling","en":"Midpoint theorem"},"def":{"af":"Die lyn wat die middelpunte van twee sye van 'n driehoek verbind, is ewewydig aan die derde sy en die helfte daarvan lank.","en":"The line joining the midpoints of two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and half as long."}},{"term":{"af":"Omgekeerde van die middelpuntstelling","en":"Converse of the midpoint theorem"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn deur die middelpunt van een sy van 'n driehoek, ewewydig aan 'n tweede sy, halveer die derde sy.","en":"A line through the midpoint of one side of a triangle, parallel to a second side, bisects the third side."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoeke in 'n parallelogram","en":"Angles in a parallelogram"},"problem":{"af":"In parallelogram ABCD is ∠A = 3x + 10° en ∠C = 5x − 30°. Bereken x, ∠A en ∠B.","en":"In parallelogram ABCD, ∠A = 3x + 10° and ∠C = 5x − 30°. Calculate x, ∠A and ∠B."},"steps":[{"af":"∠A = ∠C (teenoorst. ∠e van ||m), dus 3x + 10° = 5x − 30°","en":"∠A = ∠C (opp ∠s of ||m), so 3x + 10° = 5x − 30°"},{"af":"10° + 30° = 5x − 3x, dus 40° = 2x en x = 20°","en":"10° + 30° = 5x − 3x, so 40° = 2x and x = 20°"},{"af":"∠A = 3(20°) + 10° = 70°. Kontroleer: ∠C = 5(20°) − 30° = 70° ✓","en":"∠A = 3(20°) + 10° = 70°. Check: ∠C = 5(20°) − 30° = 70° ✓"},{"af":"∠A + ∠B = 180° (ko-binne ∠e; AD || BC), dus ∠B = 180° − 70° = 110°","en":"∠A + ∠B = 180° (co-int ∠s; AD || BC), so ∠B = 180° − 70° = 110°"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 20°; ∠A = 70°; ∠B = 110°","en":"x = 20°; ∠A = 70°; ∠B = 110°"}},{"title":{"af":"Sylengte van 'n ruit","en":"Side length of a rhombus"},"problem":{"af":"PQRS is 'n ruit. Die hoeklyne PR = 16 cm en QS = 12 cm sny by T. Bereken ∠PTQ, die lengte van PQ en die omtrek van die ruit.","en":"PQRS is a rhombus. The diagonals PR = 16 cm and QS = 12 cm intersect at T. Calculate ∠PTQ, the length of PQ and the perimeter of the rhombus."},"steps":[{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n ruit halveer mekaar loodreg: ∠PTQ = 90°, PT = 8 cm en QT = 6 cm (hoekl. van ruit)","en":"The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other at right angles: ∠PTQ = 90°, PT = 8 cm and QT = 6 cm (diags of rhombus)"},{"af":"In ΔPTQ: PQ^{2} = PT^{2} + QT^{2} = 8^{2} + 6^{2} = 64 + 36 = 100 (Pyth.)","en":"In ΔPTQ: PQ^{2} = PT^{2} + QT^{2} = 8^{2} + 6^{2} = 64 + 36 = 100 (Pyth)"},{"af":"PQ = √100 = 10 cm","en":"PQ = √100 = 10 cm"},{"af":"Al vier sye van 'n ruit is gelyk: omtrek = 4 × 10 = 40 cm","en":"All four sides of a rhombus are equal: perimeter = 4 × 10 = 40 cm"}],"answer":{"af":"∠PTQ = 90°; PQ = 10 cm; omtrek = 40 cm","en":"∠PTQ = 90°; PQ = 10 cm; perimeter = 40 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Middelpuntstelling en die omgekeerde","en":"Midpoint theorem and its converse"},"problem":{"af":"In ΔABC is AB = 14 cm, BC = 18 cm en ∠ABC = 64°. D is die middelpunt van AB en E is die middelpunt van AC. Die lyn deur E ewewydig aan AB sny BC by F. Bereken DE, ∠ADE, BF en EF.","en":"In ΔABC, AB = 14 cm, BC = 18 cm and ∠ABC = 64°. D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. The line through E parallel to AB cuts BC at F. Calculate DE, ∠ADE, BF and EF."},"steps":[{"af":"D en E is middelpunte van AB en AC, dus DE || BC en DE = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm (midpt-stelling)","en":"D and E are the midpoints of AB and AC, so DE || BC and DE = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm (midpt theorem)"},{"af":"∠ADE = ∠ABC = 64° (ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)","en":"∠ADE = ∠ABC = 64° (corresp ∠s; DE || BC)"},{"af":"In ΔCAB is E die middelpunt van AC en EF || AB, dus is F die middelpunt van BC (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)","en":"In ΔCAB, E is the midpoint of AC and EF || AB, so F is the midpoint of BC (line through midpt || to 2nd side)"},{"af":"BF = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm","en":"BF = [[1/2]] × 18 = 9 cm"},{"af":"E en F is nou middelpunte van CA en CB, dus EF = [[1/2]]AB = [[1/2]] × 14 = 7 cm (midpt-stelling)","en":"E and F are now the midpoints of CA and CB, so EF = [[1/2]]AB = [[1/2]] × 14 = 7 cm (midpt theorem)"}],"answer":{"af":"DE = 9 cm; ∠ADE = 64°; BF = 9 cm; EF = 7 cm","en":"DE = 9 cm; ∠ADE = 64°; BF = 9 cm; EF = 7 cm"}},{"title":{"af":"Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n parallelogram is","en":"Prove that a quadrilateral is a parallelogram"},"problem":{"af":"ABCD is 'n parallelogram en sy hoeklyne sny by O. E en F is punte op AC, met E tussen A en O en F tussen O en C, sodat AE = CF. Bewys dat BEDF 'n parallelogram is.","en":"ABCD is a parallelogram and its diagonals intersect at O. E and F are points on AC, with E between A and O and F between O and C, so that AE = CF. Prove that BEDF is a parallelogram."},"steps":[{"af":"AO = OC en BO = OD (hoekl. van ||m)","en":"AO = OC and BO = OD (diags of ||m)"},{"af":"AE = CF (gegee)","en":"AE = CF (given)"},{"af":"EO = AO − AE en OF = OC − CF. Gelyke lengtes minus gelyke lengtes, dus EO = OF","en":"EO = AO − AE and OF = OC − CF. Equal lengths minus equal lengths, so EO = OF"},{"af":"In vierhoek BEDF sny die hoeklyne BD en EF by O, met BO = OD en EO = OF","en":"In quadrilateral BEDF the diagonals BD and EF meet at O, with BO = OD and EO = OF"},{"af":"∴ BEDF is 'n parallelogram (hoekl. halveer mekaar)","en":"∴ BEDF is a parallelogram (diags bisect each other)"}],"answer":{"af":"BEDF is 'n parallelogram, want sy hoeklyne halveer mekaar.","en":"BEDF is a parallelogram, because its diagonals bisect each other."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter eienskap geld vir elke ruit, maar NIE vir elke parallelogram nie?","en":"Which property holds for every rhombus, but NOT for every parallelogram?"},"options":[{"af":"Teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig","en":"Opposite sides are parallel"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar","en":"The diagonals bisect each other"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne sny mekaar loodreg","en":"The diagonals cut each other at right angles"},{"af":"Teenoorstaande hoeke is gelyk","en":"Opposite angles are equal"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die ander drie eienskappe geld vir álle parallelogramme. Net in 'n ruit (en vierkant) sny die hoeklyne mekaar loodreg.","en":"The other three properties hold for all parallelograms. Only in a rhombus (and square) do the diagonals cut at right angles."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vierhoek by 'n eienskap wat dit definieer.","en":"Match each quadrilateral to a property that defines it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},"r":{"af":"Parallelogram met al vier hoeke 90°","en":"Parallelogram with all four angles 90°"}},{"l":{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},"r":{"af":"Parallelogram met al vier sye gelyk","en":"Parallelogram with all four sides equal"}},{"l":{"af":"Trapesium","en":"Trapezium"},"r":{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig","en":"One pair of opposite sides parallel"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"},"r":{"af":"Twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk","en":"Two pairs of adjacent sides equal"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},"r":{"af":"Al vier sye gelyk en al vier hoeke 90°","en":"All four sides equal and all four angles 90°"}}],"explain":{"af":"Let op: 'n vlieër se gelyke sye is aangrensend (langs mekaar), 'n parallelogram s'n is teenoorstaande. 'n Vierkant is reghoek én ruit.","en":"Note: a kite's equal sides are adjacent (next to each other), a parallelogram's are opposite. A square is both a rectangle and a rhombus."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van elke ruit is ewe lank.","en":"The diagonals of every rhombus are equal in length."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Ruit se hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg, maar hulle is net ewe lank as die ruit 'n vierkant is. Ewe lange hoeklyne is 'n eienskap van 'n reghoek.","en":"False. A rhombus's diagonals bisect each other at right angles, but they are only equal if the rhombus is a square. Equal diagonals are a property of a rectangle."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB en E die middelpunt van AC. Watter rede gebruik jy om te sê dat DE || BC?","en":"In ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB and E is the midpoint of AC. Which reason do you use to say that DE || BC?"},"options":[{"af":"(lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy)","en":"(line through midpt || to 2nd side)"},{"af":"(ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC)","en":"(corresp ∠s; DE || BC)"},{"af":"(teenoorst. sye van ||m)","en":"(opp sides of ||m)"},{"af":"(midpt-stelling)","en":"(midpt theorem)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Albei middelpunte is gegee, dus gebruik jy die middelpuntstelling: DE || BC en DE = ½BC. Die omgekeerde gebruik jy net as een middelpunt en 'n ewewydige lyn gegee is. (ooreenk. ∠e; DE || BC) is sirkelredenasie – jy kan nie DE || BC gebruik om DE || BC te bewys nie.","en":"Both midpoints are given, so you use the midpoint theorem: DE || BC and DE = ½BC. You use the converse only when one midpoint and a parallel line are given. (corresp ∠s; DE || BC) is circular – you cannot use DE || BC to prove DE || BC."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In parallelogram ABCD is ∠A = 68°. Dan is ∠B = ___°.","en":"In parallelogram ABCD, ∠A = 68°. Then ∠B = ___°."},"answers":{"af":["112","112°"],"en":["112","112°"]},"explain":{"af":"∠A en ∠B is ko-binnehoeke tussen AD || BC, dus ∠B = 180° − 68° = 112° (ko-binne ∠e; AD || BC). Die hoek teenoor ∠A (∠C) is 68°.","en":"∠A and ∠B are co-interior angles between AD || BC, so ∠B = 180° − 68° = 112° (co-int ∠s; AD || BC). The angle opposite ∠A (∠C) is 68°."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["68","22","292"],"en":["68","22","292"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ΔPQR is S die middelpunt van PQ en T die middelpunt van PR. QR = 15 cm. Dan is ST = ___ cm.","en":"In ΔPQR, S is the midpoint of PQ and T is the midpoint of PR. QR = 15 cm. Then ST = ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["7,5","7.5","7,5 cm","7.5 cm","15/2"],"en":["7.5","7,5","7.5 cm","7,5 cm","15/2"]},"explain":{"af":"ST = ½QR = ½ × 15 = 7,5 cm (midpt-stelling). Moenie verdubbel nie – die lyn tussen die middelpunte is die korter een.","en":"ST = ½QR = ½ × 15 = 7.5 cm (midpt theorem). Do not double – the line between the midpoints is the shorter one."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["30","15","5"],"en":["30","15","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is NIE genoeg om te bewys dat vierhoek ABCD 'n parallelogram is nie?","en":"Which one of the following is NOT enough to prove that quadrilateral ABCD is a parallelogram?"},"options":[{"af":"Albei pare teenoorstaande sye is gelyk","en":"Both pairs of opposite sides are equal"},{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is ewewydig en die ander paar is gelyk","en":"One pair of opposite sides is parallel and the other pair is equal"},{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar","en":"The diagonals bisect each other"},{"af":"Een paar teenoorstaande sye is gelyk en ewewydig","en":"One pair of opposite sides is equal and parallel"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Gelykbenige trapesium het een paar ewewydige sye en die ander paar gelyk, maar dit is nie 'n parallelogram nie. Die ander drie is van die vyf geldige toetse.","en":"An isosceles trapezium has one pair of parallel sides and the other pair equal, but it is not a parallelogram. The other three are among the five valid tests."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In parallelogram PQRS is ∠P = 4x − 15° en ∠R = 2x + 25°. Wat is die grootte van ∠Q?","en":"In parallelogram PQRS, ∠P = 4x − 15° and ∠R = 2x + 25°. What is the size of ∠Q?"},"options":[{"af":"115°","en":"115°"},{"af":"65°","en":"65°"},{"af":"81,67°","en":"81.67°"},{"af":"20°","en":"20°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"∠P = ∠R (teenoorst. ∠e van ||m): 4x − 15° = 2x + 25°, dus 2x = 40° en x = 20°. ∠P = 4(20°) − 15° = 65°. ∠Q = 180° − 65° = 115° (ko-binne ∠e; PS || QR). 65° is ∠P self, 20° is net x, en 81,67° kry jy as jy teenoorstaande hoeke verkeerdelik as supplementêr behandel.","en":"∠P = ∠R (opp ∠s of ||m): 4x − 15° = 2x + 25°, so 2x = 40° and x = 20°. ∠P = 4(20°) − 15° = 65°. ∠Q = 180° − 65° = 115° (co-int ∠s; PS || QR). 65° is ∠P itself, 20° is just x, and 81.67° comes from wrongly treating opposite angles as supplementary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n ruit is 10 cm en 24 cm lank. Die lengte van een sy van die ruit is ___ cm.","en":"The diagonals of a rhombus are 10 cm and 24 cm long. The length of one side of the rhombus is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["13","13 cm"],"en":["13","13 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne halveer mekaar loodreg, dus vorm die halwe hoeklyne (5 cm en 12 cm) 'n reghoekige driehoek met die sy as skuinssy: sy² = 5² + 12² = 169, sy = 13 cm (Pyth.).","en":"The diagonals bisect each other at right angles, so the half-diagonals (5 cm and 12 cm) form a right-angled triangle with the side as hypotenuse: side² = 5² + 12² = 169, side = 13 cm (Pyth)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["26","17","169"],"en":["26","17","169"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"ABCD is 'n vlieër met AB = AD en CB = CD. ∠BAD = 80° en ∠BCD = 50°. Wat is die grootte van ∠ABC?","en":"ABCD is a kite with AB = AD and CB = CD. ∠BAD = 80° and ∠BCD = 50°. What is the size of ∠ABC?"},"options":[{"af":"50°","en":"50°"},{"af":"230°","en":"230°"},{"af":"115°","en":"115°"},{"af":"80°","en":"80°"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In 'n vlieër is die hoeke tussen die ongelyke sye gelyk: ∠ABC = ∠ADC. Die hoeke van 'n vierhoek tel op tot 360°: 2∠ABC = 360° − 80° − 50° = 230°, dus ∠ABC = 115°. 230° vergeet om deur 2 te deel.","en":"In a kite the angles between the unequal sides are equal: ∠ABC = ∠ADC. The angles of a quadrilateral add up to 360°: 2∠ABC = 360° − 80° − 50° = 230°, so ∠ABC = 115°. 230° forgets to divide by 2."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ΔABC is D die middelpunt van AB, en E is 'n punt op AC sodat DE || BC. Dan is E die middelpunt van AC.","en":"In ΔABC, D is the midpoint of AB, and E is a point on AC such that DE || BC. Then E is the midpoint of AC."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is die omgekeerde van die middelpuntstelling: 'n lyn deur die middelpunt van een sy, ewewydig aan 'n tweede sy, halveer die derde sy (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy).","en":"True. This is the converse of the midpoint theorem: a line through the midpoint of one side, parallel to a second side, bisects the third side (line through midpt || to 2nd side)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In ΔKLM is KL = 18 cm en KM = 22 cm. N is die middelpunt van KL, en P lê op KM sodat NP || LM. NP = 8 cm. Die omtrek van trapesium NLMP is ___ cm.","en":"In ΔKLM, KL = 18 cm and KM = 22 cm. N is the midpoint of KL, and P lies on KM such that NP || LM. NP = 8 cm. The perimeter of trapezium NLMP is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["44","44 cm"],"en":["44","44 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"P is die middelpunt van KM (lyn deur midpt. || 2de sy), dus PM = 11 cm. Nou is N en P middelpunte, dus LM = 2 × NP = 16 cm (midpt-stelling). NL = 9 cm. Omtrek = 9 + 16 + 11 + 8 = 44 cm.","en":"P is the midpoint of KM (line through midpt || to 2nd side), so PM = 11 cm. Now N and P are midpoints, so LM = 2 × NP = 16 cm (midpt theorem). NL = 9 cm. Perimeter = 9 + 16 + 11 + 8 = 44 cm."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["36","53","32"],"en":["36","53","32"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"ABCD is 'n reghoek en sy hoeklyne sny by O. ∠OAB = 35°. Wat is die grootte van ∠AOD?","en":"ABCD is a rectangle and its diagonals intersect at O. ∠OAB = 35°. What is the size of ∠AOD?"},"options":[{"af":"70°","en":"70°"},{"af":"110°","en":"110°"},{"af":"35°","en":"35°"},{"af":"55°","en":"55°"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n reghoek is ewe lank en halveer mekaar, dus OA = OB. Dan is ∠OBA = 35° (∠e teenoor gelyke sye) en ∠AOB = 180° − 70° = 110° (som ∠e van Δ). ∠AOD = 180° − 110° = 70° (hoeke op 'n reguit lyn). 110° is ∠AOB, en 55° is ∠OAD.","en":"The diagonals of a rectangle are equal and bisect each other, so OA = OB. Then ∠OBA = 35° (∠s opp equal sides) and ∠AOB = 180° − 70° = 110° (sum of ∠s in Δ). ∠AOD = 180° − 110° = 70° (∠s on a str line). 110° is ∠AOB, and 55° is ∠OAD."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"P, Q, R en S is die middelpunte van die sye AB, BC, CD en DA van vierhoek ABCD. Die hoeklyne is AC = 20 cm en BD = 14 cm. Wat is die omtrek van PQRS?","en":"P, Q, R and S are the midpoints of the sides AB, BC, CD and DA of quadrilateral ABCD. The diagonals are AC = 20 cm and BD = 14 cm. What is the perimeter of PQRS?"},"options":[{"af":"17 cm","en":"17 cm"},{"af":"34 cm","en":"34 cm"},{"af":"48 cm","en":"48 cm"},{"af":"68 cm","en":"68 cm"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In ΔABC: PQ = ½AC = 10 cm, en in ΔADC: SR = ½AC = 10 cm. In ΔABD: PS = ½BD = 7 cm, en in ΔCBD: QR = ½BD = 7 cm (midpt-stelling). Omtrek = 10 + 7 + 10 + 7 = 34 cm. 68 cm vergeet om te halveer, en 48 cm halveer net een hoeklyn.","en":"In ΔABC: PQ = ½AC = 10 cm, and in ΔADC: SR = ½AC = 10 cm. In ΔABD: PS = ½BD = 7 cm, and in ΔCBD: QR = ½BD = 7 cm (midpt theorem). Perimeter = 10 + 7 + 10 + 7 = 34 cm. 68 cm forgets to halve, and 48 cm halves only one diagonal."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Analitiese meetkunde, finansies, statistiek en trigonometrie","en":"Analytical geometry, finance, statistics and trigonometry"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t3-analitiese-meetkunde","title":{"af":"Analitiese meetkunde","en":"Analytical geometry"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal afstand, middelpunt en gradiënt tussen punte kan bereken, die vergelyking van 'n lyn kan bepaal, en met koördinate kan bewys watter soort vierhoek gegee is.","en":"You will be able to calculate the distance, midpoint and gradient between points, determine the equation of a line, and use coordinates to prove what kind of quadrilateral is given."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie basiese formules\n\nVir twee punte A(x_{1}; y_{1}) en B(x_{2}; y_{2}):\n\n| Wat | Formule |\n|---|---|\n| Afstand (lengte van AB) | AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] |\n| Middelpunt M van AB | M([[x_{1} + x_{2}/2]] ; [[y_{1} + y_{2}/2]]) |\n| Gradiënt van AB | m_{AB} = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] |\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak altyd eers 'n rowwe skets van die punte. Dan sien jy gou of jou antwoord sin maak.\n\n### Afstand\n\nDie afstandsformule is net **Pythagoras**: die horisontale verskil en die vertikale verskil is die twee reghoeksye, en AB is die skuinssy. Omdat die verskille gekwadreer word, maak die volgorde van die punte nie saak nie, en 'n afstand is altyd positief. Los die antwoord in wortelvorm (bv. √45 = 3√5) of rond af tot twee desimale plekke, soos die vraag vra.\n\n### Middelpunt\n\nDie middelpunt is die **gemiddeld** van die x-koördinate en die gemiddeld van die y-koördinate. As die middelpunt M en een eindpunt A gegee is, kry jy die ander eindpunt met x_{B} = 2x_{M} − x_{A} en y_{B} = 2y_{M} − y_{A}.\n\n### Gradiënt\n\nDie gradiënt meet hoe steil 'n lyn is: [[verandering in y/verandering in x]].\n\n- m > 0: die lyn styg na regs. m < 0: die lyn daal na regs.\n- Horisontale lyn (y = k): m = 0.\n- Vertikale lyn (x = k): m is **ongedefinieerd**, want jy sal deur 0 moet deel.\n\n## Ewewydige en loodregte lyne\n\n- **Ewewydig (∥):** m_{1} = m_{2}.\n- **Loodreg (⊥):** m_{1} × m_{2} = −1. Die loodregte gradiënt is die **negatiewe resiprook**: draai die breuk om en verander die teken. Bv. m = [[2/3]] → m_{⊥} = −[[3/2]].\n- Uitsondering: 'n horisontale en 'n vertikale lyn is loodreg, al kan jy nie m_{1} × m_{2} bereken nie.\n\n## Saamlynige punte\n\nPunte A, B en C is **saamlynig** as hulle op dieselfde reguit lyn lê. Bewys dit met m_{AB} = m_{BC}. Omdat die twee lynstukke die punt B deel en ewe steil is, vorm hulle een reguit lyn.\n\n## Vergelyking van 'n reguit lyn: y = mx + c\n\n1. Bereken m uit twee punte, of neem dit van 'n ewewydige of loodregte lyn.\n2. Vervang een bekende punt (x; y) in y = mx + c en los c op.\n3. Skryf die vergelyking in die vorm y = mx + c.\n\nJy mag ook y − y_{1} = m(x − x_{1}) gebruik; dit gee dieselfde antwoord.\n\n## Vierhoeke bewys met koördinate\n\n| Vierhoek | Wys dat ... |\n|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | albei pare teenoorstaande sye ewewydig is (gelyke gradiënte), **of** die hoeklyne mekaar halveer (dieselfde middelpunt), **of** een paar teenoorstaande sye gelyk en ewewydig is |\n| Reghoek | dit 'n parallelogram is met een regte hoek (m_{1} × m_{2} = −1), of met gelyke hoeklyne |\n| Ruit | dit 'n parallelogram is met twee aangrensende sye gelyk, of met hoeklyne wat loodreg op mekaar is |\n| Vierkant | dit 'n ruit is met een regte hoek, of 'n reghoek met twee aangrensende sye gelyk |\n| Trapesium | een paar teenoorstaande sye ewewydig is |\n| Vlieër | twee pare aangrensende sye gelyk is |\n\nVir driehoeke: 'n driehoek is **reghoekig** as twee sye loodreg is (of as Pythagoras klop), en **gelykbenig** as twee sye ewe lank is.\n\n> **Onthou!** Gee altyd die rede in woorde, bv. \"AB = BC, dus is die parallelogram 'n ruit\". Die berekening alleen is nie 'n bewys nie.\n\n## Ontbrekende koördinaat\n\nSkryf die gegewe inligting as 'n vergelyking met die onbekende en los dit op:\n\n- **Gegewe gradiënt:** stel [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] gelyk aan die gegewe waarde en kruisvermenigvuldig.\n- **Gegewe afstand:** kwadreer albei kante. Jy kry dikwels **twee** antwoorde (±), en albei kan geldig wees.\n- **Gegewe middelpunt:** stel elke koördinaat se gemiddeld gelyk aan die middelpunt se koördinaat.\n- **Saamlynig, ewewydig of loodreg:** stel die gradiënte gelyk, of stel hul produk gelyk aan −1.\n- **Vierde hoekpunt van 'n parallelogram:** die hoeklyne het dieselfde middelpunt.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Tekenfoute met negatiewe getalle: 3 − (−2) = 5, en (−4)^{2} = 16, nie −16 nie.\n- Die volgorde in die gradiëntformule meng: as jy bo met y_{2} begin, moet jy onder met x_{2} begin.\n- Vergeet om deur 2 te deel by die middelpunt.\n- Vergeet die wortel by die afstand.\n- Dink loodreg beteken net \"verander die teken\". Jy moet die breuk ook omdraai.\n- Wys net dat al die sye gelyk is en noem die vorm 'n vierkant. Kontroleer ook vir 'n regte hoek.","en":"## The three basic formulas\n\nFor two points A(x_{1}; y_{1}) and B(x_{2}; y_{2}):\n\n| What | Formula |\n|---|---|\n| Distance (length of AB) | AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] |\n| Midpoint M of AB | M([[x_{1} + x_{2}/2]] ; [[y_{1} + y_{2}/2]]) |\n| Gradient of AB | m_{AB} = [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] |\n\n> **Tip:** Always make a rough sketch of the points first. Then you quickly see whether your answer makes sense.\n\n### Distance\n\nThe distance formula is just **Pythagoras**: the horizontal difference and the vertical difference are the two shorter sides, and AB is the hypotenuse. Because the differences are squared, the order of the points does not matter, and a distance is always positive. Leave the answer in surd form (e.g. √45 = 3√5) or round off to two decimal places, as the question asks.\n\n### Midpoint\n\nThe midpoint is the **average** of the x-coordinates and the average of the y-coordinates. If the midpoint M and one endpoint A are given, you find the other endpoint with x_{B} = 2x_{M} − x_{A} and y_{B} = 2y_{M} − y_{A}.\n\n### Gradient\n\nThe gradient measures how steep a line is: [[change in y/change in x]].\n\n- m > 0: the line rises to the right. m < 0: the line falls to the right.\n- Horizontal line (y = k): m = 0.\n- Vertical line (x = k): m is **undefined**, because you would have to divide by 0.\n\n## Parallel and perpendicular lines\n\n- **Parallel (∥):** m_{1} = m_{2}.\n- **Perpendicular (⊥):** m_{1} × m_{2} = −1. The perpendicular gradient is the **negative reciprocal**: flip the fraction and change the sign. E.g. m = [[2/3]] → m_{⊥} = −[[3/2]].\n- Exception: a horizontal and a vertical line are perpendicular, even though you cannot calculate m_{1} × m_{2}.\n\n## Collinear points\n\nPoints A, B and C are **collinear** if they lie on the same straight line. Prove it with m_{AB} = m_{BC}. Because the two line segments share the point B and are equally steep, they form one straight line.\n\n## Equation of a straight line: y = mx + c\n\n1. Calculate m from two points, or take it from a parallel or perpendicular line.\n2. Substitute one known point (x; y) into y = mx + c and solve for c.\n3. Write the equation in the form y = mx + c.\n\nYou may also use y − y_{1} = m(x − x_{1}); it gives the same answer.\n\n## Proving quadrilaterals with coordinates\n\n| Quadrilateral | Show that ... |\n|---|---|\n| Parallelogram | both pairs of opposite sides are parallel (equal gradients), **or** the diagonals bisect each other (same midpoint), **or** one pair of opposite sides is equal and parallel |\n| Rectangle | it is a parallelogram with one right angle (m_{1} × m_{2} = −1), or with equal diagonals |\n| Rhombus | it is a parallelogram with two adjacent sides equal, or with diagonals that are perpendicular to each other |\n| Square | it is a rhombus with one right angle, or a rectangle with two adjacent sides equal |\n| Trapezium | one pair of opposite sides is parallel |\n| Kite | two pairs of adjacent sides are equal |\n\nFor triangles: a triangle is **right-angled** if two sides are perpendicular (or if Pythagoras works), and **isosceles** if two sides are equally long.\n\n> **Remember!** Always give the reason in words, e.g. \"AB = BC, so the parallelogram is a rhombus\". The calculation alone is not a proof.\n\n## Missing coordinate\n\nWrite the given information as an equation with the unknown and solve it:\n\n- **Given gradient:** set [[y_{2} − y_{1}/x_{2} − x_{1}]] equal to the given value and cross-multiply.\n- **Given distance:** square both sides. You often get **two** answers (±), and both can be valid.\n- **Given midpoint:** set the average of each coordinate equal to the midpoint's coordinate.\n- **Collinear, parallel or perpendicular:** set the gradients equal, or set their product equal to −1.\n- **Fourth vertex of a parallelogram:** the diagonals have the same midpoint.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Sign errors with negative numbers: 3 − (−2) = 5, and (−4)^{2} = 16, not −16.\n- Mixing up the order in the gradient formula: if you start with y_{2} at the top, you must start with x_{2} at the bottom.\n- Forgetting to divide by 2 for the midpoint.\n- Forgetting the square root for the distance.\n- Thinking perpendicular only means \"change the sign\". You must also flip the fraction.\n- Showing only that all the sides are equal and calling the shape a square. Also check for a right angle."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Afstandsformule","en":"Distance formula"},"def":{"af":"AB = √[(x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²]. Dit gee die lengte van die lynstuk tussen twee punte en is gebaseer op Pythagoras.","en":"AB = √[(x₂ − x₁)² + (y₂ − y₁)²]. It gives the length of the line segment between two points and is based on Pythagoras."}},{"term":{"af":"Middelpunt","en":"Midpoint"},"def":{"af":"Die punt presies halfpad tussen twee punte: M((x₁ + x₂)/2; (y₁ + y₂)/2).","en":"The point exactly halfway between two points: M((x₁ + x₂)/2; (y₁ + y₂)/2)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gradiënt","en":"Gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die steilheid van 'n lyn: m = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁), die verandering in y gedeel deur die verandering in x.","en":"The steepness of a line: m = (y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁), the change in y divided by the change in x."}},{"term":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne","en":"Parallel lines"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat nooit sny nie. Hulle het gelyke gradiënte: m₁ = m₂.","en":"Lines that never meet. They have equal gradients: m₁ = m₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Loodregte lyne","en":"Perpendicular lines"},"def":{"af":"Lyne wat mekaar teen 90° sny. Die produk van hul gradiënte is −1: m₁ × m₂ = −1.","en":"Lines that cut each other at 90°. The product of their gradients is −1: m₁ × m₂ = −1."}},{"term":{"af":"Negatiewe resiprook","en":"Negative reciprocal"},"def":{"af":"Die breuk omgedraai en die teken verander, bv. ⅔ → −3/2. Dit gee die gradiënt van 'n loodregte lyn.","en":"The fraction flipped and the sign changed, e.g. ⅔ → −3/2. It gives the gradient of a perpendicular line."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamlynige punte","en":"Collinear points"},"def":{"af":"Drie of meer punte wat op dieselfde reguit lyn lê, bv. as m_AB = m_BC.","en":"Three or more points that lie on the same straight line, e.g. if m_AB = m_BC."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoeklyn","en":"Diagonal"},"def":{"af":"'n Lynstuk wat twee teenoorstaande hoekpunte van 'n vierhoek verbind. As die hoeklyne mekaar halveer, is die vierhoek 'n parallelogram.","en":"A line segment that joins two opposite vertices of a quadrilateral. If the diagonals bisect each other, the quadrilateral is a parallelogram."}},{"term":{"af":"Ongedefinieerde gradiënt","en":"Undefined gradient"},"def":{"af":"Die gradiënt van 'n vertikale lyn x = k: die verandering in x is 0 en jy kan nie deur 0 deel nie.","en":"The gradient of a vertical line x = k: the change in x is 0 and you cannot divide by 0."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Afstand, middelpunt en gradiënt","en":"Distance, midpoint and gradient"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee A(−2; 5) en B(4; −3). Bereken (a) die lengte van AB, (b) die koördinate van M, die middelpunt van AB, en (c) die gradiënt van AB.","en":"Given A(−2; 5) and B(4; −3). Calculate (a) the length of AB, (b) the coordinates of M, the midpoint of AB, and (c) the gradient of AB."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] = √[(4 − (−2))^{2} + (−3 − 5)^{2}]","en":"(a) AB = √[(x_{2} − x_{1})^{2} + (y_{2} − y_{1})^{2}] = √[(4 − (−2))^{2} + (−3 − 5)^{2}]"},{"af":"= √[6^{2} + (−8)^{2}] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 eenhede","en":"= √[6^{2} + (−8)^{2}] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 units"},{"af":"(b) M = ([[−2 + 4/2]] ; [[5 + (−3)/2]]) = ([[2/2]] ; [[2/2]]) = (1; 1)","en":"(b) M = ([[−2 + 4/2]] ; [[5 + (−3)/2]]) = ([[2/2]] ; [[2/2]]) = (1; 1)"},{"af":"(c) m_{AB} = [[−3 − 5/4 − (−2)]] = [[−8/6]] = −[[4/3]]","en":"(c) m_{AB} = [[−3 − 5/4 − (−2)]] = [[−8/6]] = −[[4/3]]"}],"answer":{"af":"AB = 10 eenhede; M(1; 1); m_AB = −4/3","en":"AB = 10 units; M(1; 1); m_AB = −4/3"}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyking van 'n lyn en 'n loodregte lyn","en":"Equation of a line and a perpendicular line"},"problem":{"af":"Gegee C(−1; 4) en D(3; −4). (a) Bepaal die vergelyking van die lyn CD. (b) Bepaal die vergelyking van die lyn deur E(4; 1) wat loodreg op CD is.","en":"Given C(−1; 4) and D(3; −4). (a) Determine the equation of the line CD. (b) Determine the equation of the line through E(4; 1) that is perpendicular to CD."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) m_{CD} = [[−4 − 4/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2","en":"(a) m_{CD} = [[−4 − 4/3 − (−1)]] = [[−8/4]] = −2"},{"af":"Vervang C(−1; 4) in y = −2x + c: 4 = −2(−1) + c → 4 = 2 + c → c = 2. Dus CD: y = −2x + 2.","en":"Substitute C(−1; 4) into y = −2x + c: 4 = −2(−1) + c → 4 = 2 + c → c = 2. So CD: y = −2x + 2."},{"af":"(b) Loodreg: m × (−2) = −1 → m = [[1/2]] (die negatiewe resiprook van −2).","en":"(b) Perpendicular: m × (−2) = −1 → m = [[1/2]] (the negative reciprocal of −2)."},{"af":"Vervang E(4; 1) in y = [[1/2]]x + c: 1 = [[1/2]](4) + c → 1 = 2 + c → c = −1","en":"Substitute E(4; 1) into y = [[1/2]]x + c: 1 = [[1/2]](4) + c → 1 = 2 + c → c = −1"},{"af":"Die loodregte lyn is y = [[1/2]]x − 1.","en":"The perpendicular line is y = [[1/2]]x − 1."}],"answer":{"af":"CD: y = −2x + 2; loodregte lyn: y = ½x − 1","en":"CD: y = −2x + 2; perpendicular line: y = ½x − 1"}},{"title":{"af":"Bewys dat 'n vierhoek 'n ruit is","en":"Prove that a quadrilateral is a rhombus"},"problem":{"af":"Die hoekpunte van vierhoek ABCD is A(1; 2), B(4; 6), C(9; 6) en D(6; 2). (a) Bewys dat ABCD 'n parallelogram is. (b) Bewys dat ABCD 'n ruit is. (c) Is ABCD 'n vierkant? Gee 'n rede.","en":"The vertices of quadrilateral ABCD are A(1; 2), B(4; 6), C(9; 6) and D(6; 2). (a) Prove that ABCD is a parallelogram. (b) Prove that ABCD is a rhombus. (c) Is ABCD a square? Give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Middelpunt van AC = ([[1 + 9/2]] ; [[2 + 6/2]]) = (5; 4). Middelpunt van BD = ([[4 + 6/2]] ; [[6 + 2/2]]) = (5; 4).","en":"(a) Midpoint of AC = ([[1 + 9/2]] ; [[2 + 6/2]]) = (5; 4). Midpoint of BD = ([[4 + 6/2]] ; [[6 + 2/2]]) = (5; 4)."},{"af":"Die hoeklyne het dieselfde middelpunt, dus halveer hulle mekaar. ABCD is 'n parallelogram.","en":"The diagonals have the same midpoint, so they bisect each other. ABCD is a parallelogram."},{"af":"(b) AB = √[(4 − 1)^{2} + (6 − 2)^{2}] = √(9 + 16) = 5 en BC = √[(9 − 4)^{2} + (6 − 6)^{2}] = √25 = 5","en":"(b) AB = √[(4 − 1)^{2} + (6 − 2)^{2}] = √(9 + 16) = 5 and BC = √[(9 − 4)^{2} + (6 − 6)^{2}] = √25 = 5"},{"af":"ABCD is 'n parallelogram met twee aangrensende sye gelyk (AB = BC), dus is dit 'n ruit.","en":"ABCD is a parallelogram with two adjacent sides equal (AB = BC), so it is a rhombus."},{"af":"(c) m_{AB} = [[6 − 2/4 − 1]] = [[4/3]] en m_{BC} = [[6 − 6/9 − 4]] = 0. Omdat [[4/3]] × 0 = 0 ≠ −1, is ∠ABC nie 90° nie, dus is ABCD nie 'n vierkant nie.","en":"(c) m_{AB} = [[6 − 2/4 − 1]] = [[4/3]] and m_{BC} = [[6 − 6/9 − 4]] = 0. Because [[4/3]] × 0 = 0 ≠ −1, ∠ABC is not 90°, so ABCD is not a square."}],"answer":{"af":"Parallelogram (hoeklyne halveer mekaar); ruit (AB = BC = 5); nie 'n vierkant nie (geen regte hoek)","en":"Parallelogram (diagonals bisect each other); rhombus (AB = BC = 5); not a square (no right angle)"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontbrekende koördinaat: saamlynige punte","en":"Missing coordinate: collinear points"},"problem":{"af":"Op 'n kaart van 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits staan drie besproeiingskrane by A(2; −1), B(5; 3) en C(k; 11). Hulle lê op een reguit pyplyn. Bepaal k en die lengte van die pyplyn AC as een eenheid 10 m is.","en":"On a map of a citrus farm near Brits, three irrigation taps stand at A(2; −1), B(5; 3) and C(k; 11). They lie on one straight pipeline. Determine k and the length of the pipeline AC if one unit is 10 m."},"steps":[{"af":"Die punte is saamlynig, dus m_{AB} = m_{BC}.","en":"The points are collinear, so m_{AB} = m_{BC}."},{"af":"m_{AB} = [[3 − (−1)/5 − 2]] = [[4/3]]","en":"m_{AB} = [[3 − (−1)/5 − 2]] = [[4/3]]"},{"af":"m_{BC} = [[11 − 3/k − 5]] = [[8/k − 5]]. Stel gelyk: [[8/k − 5]] = [[4/3]]","en":"m_{BC} = [[11 − 3/k − 5]] = [[8/k − 5]]. Set equal: [[8/k − 5]] = [[4/3]]"},{"af":"Kruisvermenigvuldig: 4(k − 5) = 24 → k − 5 = 6 → k = 11. Kontroleer: m_{AC} = [[12/9]] = [[4/3]] ✓","en":"Cross-multiply: 4(k − 5) = 24 → k − 5 = 6 → k = 11. Check: m_{AC} = [[12/9]] = [[4/3]] ✓"},{"af":"AC = √[(11 − 2)^{2} + (11 − (−1))^{2}] = √(81 + 144) = √225 = 15 eenhede = 15 × 10 m = 150 m","en":"AC = √[(11 − 2)^{2} + (11 − (−1))^{2}] = √(81 + 144) = √225 = 15 units = 15 × 10 m = 150 m"}],"answer":{"af":"k = 11; AC = 150 m","en":"k = 11; AC = 150 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter formule gee die gradiënt van die lyn deur (x₁; y₁) en (x₂; y₂)?","en":"Which formula gives the gradient of the line through (x₁; y₁) and (x₂; y₂)?"},"options":[{"af":"(x₂ − x₁)/(y₂ − y₁)","en":"(x₂ − x₁)/(y₂ − y₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ + y₁)/(x₂ + x₁)","en":"(y₂ + y₁)/(x₂ + x₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁)","en":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₂ − x₁)"},{"af":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₁ − x₂)","en":"(y₂ − y₁)/(x₁ − x₂)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Gradiënt = verandering in y gedeel deur verandering in x, met dieselfde volgorde bo en onder. Die eerste opsie is omgekeer, die tweede lyk na die middelpuntformule en die laaste meng die volgorde (dit gee die verkeerde teken).","en":"Gradient = change in y divided by change in x, with the same order at the top and the bottom. The first option is upside down, the second looks like the midpoint formula and the last mixes the order (it gives the wrong sign)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As twee lyne loodreg op mekaar is, is hul gradiënte gelyk.","en":"If two lines are perpendicular to each other, their gradients are equal."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Gelyke gradiënte beteken die lyne is ewewydig. Vir loodregte lyne is m₁ × m₂ = −1, bv. 2 en −½.","en":"False. Equal gradients mean the lines are parallel. For perpendicular lines m₁ × m₂ = −1, e.g. 2 and −½."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gradiënt-eienskap by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each gradient property to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"m₁ = m₂","en":"m₁ = m₂"},"r":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne","en":"Parallel lines"}},{"l":{"af":"m₁ × m₂ = −1","en":"m₁ × m₂ = −1"},"r":{"af":"Loodregte lyne","en":"Perpendicular lines"}},{"l":{"af":"m = 0","en":"m = 0"},"r":{"af":"Horisontale lyn","en":"Horizontal line"}},{"l":{"af":"m is ongedefinieerd","en":"m is undefined"},"r":{"af":"Vertikale lyn","en":"Vertical line"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ewewydige lyne is ewe steil. By loodregte lyne is die gradiënte negatiewe resiproke. 'n Horisontale lyn het geen styging nie (m = 0), en by 'n vertikale lyn is die verandering in x nul, dus is m ongedefinieerd.","en":"Parallel lines are equally steep. For perpendicular lines the gradients are negative reciprocals. A horizontal line has no rise (m = 0), and for a vertical line the change in x is zero, so m is undefined."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die middelpunt van A(−3; 7) en B(5; −1)?","en":"What is the midpoint of A(−3; 7) and B(5; −1)?"},"options":[{"af":"(1; 3)","en":"(1; 3)"},{"af":"(4; −4)","en":"(4; −4)"},{"af":"(2; 6)","en":"(2; 6)"},{"af":"(8; −8)","en":"(8; −8)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"M = ((−3 + 5)/2; (7 + (−1))/2) = (2/2; 6/2) = (1; 3). (2; 6) vergeet om deur 2 te deel, (4; −4) trek af in plaas daarvan om bymekaar te tel, en (8; −8) trek af sonder om te halveer.","en":"M = ((−3 + 5)/2; (7 + (−1))/2) = (2/2; 6/2) = (1; 3). (2; 6) forgets to divide by 2, (4; −4) subtracts instead of adding, and (8; −8) subtracts without halving."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op 'n kaart van Brits (eenhede in km) is die taxistaanplek by P(1; −2) en die skool by Q(7; 6). Hoe ver is dit in 'n reguit lyn van P na Q?","en":"On a map of Brits (units in km) the taxi rank is at P(1; −2) and the school is at Q(7; 6). How far is it in a straight line from P to Q?"},"options":[{"af":"√52 ≈ 7,21 km","en":"√52 ≈ 7.21 km"},{"af":"14 km","en":"14 km"},{"af":"100 km","en":"100 km"},{"af":"10 km","en":"10 km"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"PQ = √[(7 − 1)² + (6 − (−2))²] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 km. √52 kom van 6 − 2 in plaas van 6 − (−2), 14 tel net die verskille bymekaar, en 100 vergeet die wortel.","en":"PQ = √[(7 − 1)² + (6 − (−2))²] = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10 km. √52 comes from 6 − 2 instead of 6 − (−2), 14 just adds the differences, and 100 forgets the square root."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van die lyn deur (−1; 4) en (3; −8)?","en":"What is the gradient of the line through (−1; 4) and (3; −8)?"},"options":[{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"−3","en":"−3"},{"af":"−⅓","en":"−⅓"},{"af":"−6","en":"−6"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"m = (−8 − 4)/(3 − (−1)) = −12/4 = −3. Die lyn daal na regs, dus moet m negatief wees. −⅓ is Δx/Δy (omgekeer) en −6 kom van 3 − 1 = 2 in die noemer.","en":"m = (−8 − 4)/(3 − (−1)) = −12/4 = −3. The line falls to the right, so m must be negative. −⅓ is Δx/Δy (upside down) and −6 comes from 3 − 1 = 2 in the denominator."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wat is die gradiënt van 'n lyn wat loodreg is op y = ⅔x − 1? m = ___","en":"What is the gradient of a line that is perpendicular to y = ⅔x − 1? m = ___"},"answers":{"af":["-3/2","−3/2","-1,5","−1,5","m = -3/2","m=-3/2","m = −3/2","m=−3/2","m = -1,5","m=-1,5"],"en":["-3/2","−3/2","-1.5","−1.5","m = -3/2","m=-3/2","m = −3/2","m=−3/2","m = -1.5","m=-1.5"]},"explain":{"af":"Die gegewe lyn se gradiënt is ⅔. Loodreg: ⅔ × m = −1 → m = −3/2 = −1,5. Draai die breuk om EN verander die teken.","en":"The given line's gradient is ⅔. Perpendicular: ⅔ × m = −1 → m = −3/2 = −1.5. Flip the fraction AND change the sign."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3/2","-2/3","2/3"],"en":["3/2","-2/3","2/3"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die punte A(0; 1), B(2; 5) en C(4; 9) is saamlynig.","en":"The points A(0; 1), B(2; 5) and C(4; 9) are collinear."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. m_AB = (5 − 1)/(2 − 0) = 2 en m_BC = (9 − 5)/(4 − 2) = 2. Die gradiënte is gelyk en B is 'n gemeenskaplike punt, dus lê al drie punte op dieselfde lyn.","en":"True. m_AB = (5 − 1)/(2 − 0) = 2 and m_BC = (9 − 5)/(4 − 2) = 2. The gradients are equal and B is a common point, so all three points lie on the same line."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"M(2; −1) is die middelpunt van lynstuk AB, met A(−1; 3). Die y-koördinaat van B is ___.","en":"M(2; −1) is the midpoint of line segment AB, with A(−1; 3). The y-coordinate of B is ___."},"answers":{"af":["-5","−5","y = -5","y=-5","y = −5","y=−5"],"en":["-5","−5","y = -5","y=-5","y = −5","y=−5"]},"explain":{"af":"(3 + y)/2 = −1 → 3 + y = −2 → y = −5. Net so: (−1 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 5, dus B(5; −5). Kortpad: y_B = 2(−1) − 3 = −5.","en":"(3 + y)/2 = −1 → 3 + y = −2 → y = −5. In the same way: (−1 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 5, so B(5; −5). Shortcut: y_B = 2(−1) − 3 = −5."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","-4","5"],"en":["1","-4","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die vergelyking van die lyn deur (2; 1) wat ewewydig is aan y = 3x − 4?","en":"What is the equation of the line through (2; 1) that is parallel to y = 3x − 4?"},"options":[{"af":"y = 3x − 4","en":"y = 3x − 4"},{"af":"y = 3x + 7","en":"y = 3x + 7"},{"af":"y = −3x + 7","en":"y = −3x + 7"},{"af":"y = 3x − 5","en":"y = 3x − 5"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ewewydig, dus m = 3. Vervang (2; 1): 1 = 3(2) + c → c = 1 − 6 = −5. Dus y = 3x − 5. y = 3x − 4 is die gegewe lyn self (dit gaan nie deur (2; 1) nie), y = 3x + 7 het 'n tekenfout by c, en y = −3x + 7 het die verkeerde gradiënt.","en":"Parallel, so m = 3. Substitute (2; 1): 1 = 3(2) + c → c = 1 − 6 = −5. So y = 3x − 5. y = 3x − 4 is the given line itself (it does not pass through (2; 1)), y = 3x + 7 has a sign error in c, and y = −3x + 7 has the wrong gradient."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die afstand tussen P(1; t) en Q(4; 2) is 5 eenhede. Bepaal t.","en":"The distance between P(1; t) and Q(4; 2) is 5 units. Determine t."},"options":[{"af":"t = −2 of t = 6","en":"t = −2 or t = 6"},{"af":"t = 6","en":"t = 6"},{"af":"t = 2 of t = −6","en":"t = 2 or t = −6"},{"af":"t = 7","en":"t = 7"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"(4 − 1)² + (2 − t)² = 25 → 9 + (2 − t)² = 25 → (2 − t)² = 16 → 2 − t = ±4 → t = −2 of t = 6. Albei punte lê 5 eenhede van Q af: een bo en een onder. \"t = 6\" vergeet die negatiewe wortel.","en":"(4 − 1)² + (2 − t)² = 25 → 9 + (2 − t)² = 25 → (2 − t)² = 16 → 2 − t = ±4 → t = −2 or t = 6. Both points lie 5 units from Q: one above and one below. \"t = 6\" forgets the negative root."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die punte A(−1; −3), B(1; 1) en C(4; k) is saamlynig. k = ___","en":"The points A(−1; −3), B(1; 1) and C(4; k) are collinear. k = ___"},"answers":{"af":["7","k = 7","k=7"],"en":["7","k = 7","k=7"]},"explain":{"af":"m_AB = (1 − (−3))/(1 − (−1)) = 4/2 = 2. Stel m_BC = 2: (k − 1)/(4 − 1) = 2 → k − 1 = 6 → k = 7.","en":"m_AB = (1 − (−3))/(1 − (−1)) = 4/2 = 2. Set m_BC = 2: (k − 1)/(4 − 1) = 2 → k − 1 = 6 → k = 7."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["9","5","6"],"en":["9","5","6"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die hoekpunte van vierhoek PQRS is P(−2; 1), Q(1; 4), R(4; 1) en S(1; −2). Wat is die mees spesifieke naam vir PQRS?","en":"The vertices of quadrilateral PQRS are P(−2; 1), Q(1; 4), R(4; 1) and S(1; −2). What is the most specific name for PQRS?"},"options":[{"af":"Ruit","en":"Rhombus"},{"af":"Vierkant","en":"Square"},{"af":"Reghoek","en":"Rectangle"},{"af":"Vlieër","en":"Kite"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Al vier sye is √18 lank (bv. PQ = √(3² + 3²)), dus is PQRS ten minste 'n ruit. m_PQ = 3/3 = 1 en m_QR = −3/3 = −1, en 1 × (−1) = −1, dus is ∠Q = 90°. 'n Ruit met 'n regte hoek is 'n vierkant. (Die hoeklyne PR en QS is ook albei 6 eenhede lank.)","en":"All four sides are √18 long (e.g. PQ = √(3² + 3²)), so PQRS is at least a rhombus. m_PQ = 3/3 = 1 and m_QR = −3/3 = −1, and 1 × (−1) = −1, so ∠Q = 90°. A rhombus with a right angle is a square. (The diagonals PR and QS are also both 6 units long.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"A(−2; 3), B(4; 5) en C(6; −1) is drie hoekpunte van parallelogram ABCD. Bepaal die koördinate van D. D = ___","en":"A(−2; 3), B(4; 5) and C(6; −1) are three vertices of parallelogram ABCD. Determine the coordinates of D. D = ___"},"answers":{"af":["(0; −3)","(0;-3)","(0;−3)","0;-3","0;−3","(0,-3)","(0,−3)","D(0;-3)","D(0;−3)","D(0; −3)"],"en":["(0; −3)","(0;-3)","(0;−3)","0;-3","0;−3","(0,-3)","(0,−3)","D(0;-3)","D(0;−3)","D(0; −3)"]},"explain":{"af":"Die hoeklyne van 'n parallelogram halveer mekaar, dus het AC en BD dieselfde middelpunt. Middelpunt van AC = ((−2 + 6)/2; (3 + (−1))/2) = (2; 1). Vir BD: (4 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 0 en (5 + y)/2 = 1 → y = −3. Dus D(0; −3).","en":"The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other, so AC and BD have the same midpoint. Midpoint of AC = ((−2 + 6)/2; (3 + (−1))/2) = (2; 1). For BD: (4 + x)/2 = 2 → x = 0 and (5 + y)/2 = 1 → y = −3. So D(0; −3)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["(12; 1)","(−4; 9)","(2; 1)"],"en":["(12; 1)","(−4; 9)","(2; 1)"]}}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-finansies","title":{"af":"Finansies en groei","en":"Finance and growth"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal enkelvoudige en saamgestelde rente, huurkoop, inflasie, bevolkingsgroei en wisselkoerse kan bereken en verduidelik watter formule wanneer gebruik word.","en":"You will be able to calculate simple and compound interest, hire purchase, inflation, population growth and exchange rates, and explain which formula to use when."},"summary":{"af":"## Die simbole wat jy moet ken\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| P | **hoofsom**: die beginbedrag wat jy belê of leen |\n| A | **opgehoopte bedrag**: die eindbedrag ná n jaar |\n| i | **rentekoers** per jaar as 'n desimaal: 8% → i = [[8/100]] = 0,08 |\n| n | **tydperk** in jare (of die aantal saamstellingsperiodes) |\n\nDie rente wat jy verdien (of betaal) is **A − P**. Geldbedrae word afgerond tot die naaste sent, dus **twee desimale plekke**, en in Afrikaans so geskryf: R12 345,67.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om i = 8 in plaas van i = 0,08 in te vervang. Deel die persentasie altyd eers deur 100.\n\n## Enkelvoudige rente\n\n**A = P(1 + in)**\n\nDie rente word elke jaar net op die **oorspronklike hoofsom** bereken, so jy kry elke jaar presies dieselfde bedrag rente. Daarom is die groei **lineêr**: die grafiek van A teenoor n is 'n reguit lyn.\n\n- Tyd in maande? Skakel om na jare: 18 maande → n = [[18/12]] = 1,5.\n- Jy kan ook P, i of n bereken: vervang die bekende waardes en los die vergelyking op. Bv. R6 000 groei teen 8% p.j. enkelvoudige rente tot R8 400: 8 400 = 6 000(1 + 0,08n) → 1,4 = 1 + 0,08n → n = 5 jaar.\n\n## Saamgestelde rente\n\n**A = P(1 + i)^{n}**\n\nHier word rente bereken op die hoofsom **plus die rente wat reeds bygetel is**: rente op rente. Die groei is **eksponensieel**: die grafiek is 'n kromme wat al hoe steiler word. Ná die eerste jaar gee saamgestelde rente altyd meer as enkelvoudige rente teen dieselfde koers.\n\nOm die hoofsom te kry as die eindbedrag gegee is (\"Hoeveel moet ek nou belê?\"): **P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}**.\n\n### Saamstellingsperiodes\n\nAs rente meer as een keer per jaar bygetel word, pas jy i **én** n aan:\n\n| Saamgestel | Koers per periode | Aantal periodes |\n|---|---|---|\n| jaarliks | i | n |\n| halfjaarliks | [[i/2]] | 2n |\n| kwartaalliks | [[i/4]] | 4n |\n| maandeliks | [[i/12]] | 12n |\n\nBv. 8% p.j., kwartaalliks saamgestel vir 5 jaar: A = P(1 + [[0,08/4]])^{20}.\n\n> **Wenk:** Tik die hele berekening in een keer op jou sakrekenaar. As jy tussenin afrond (bv. 1,00875 → 1,01), sal jou antwoord verkeerd wees. Rond net die finale antwoord af.\n\n## Huurkoop\n\nMet **huurkoop** neem jy die item nou en betaal dit in maandelikse paaiemente af. Die rente is **enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag** (die balans ná die deposito).\n\n1. Deposito = persentasie × kontantprys.\n2. Uitstaande bedrag: P = kontantprys − deposito.\n3. A = P(1 + in): die totaal wat jy oor die tydperk terugbetaal.\n4. Maandelikse paaiement = A ÷ aantal maande. Tel maandelikse versekering by as dit gegee word.\n5. Totale koste = deposito + A (+ alle versekering).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om rente op die volle kontantprys te bereken, of om te vergeet om die deposito eers af te trek.\n\n## Inflasie\n\n**Inflasie** is die algemene styging in pryse oor tyd. Dit werk presies soos saamgestelde rente: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, waar i die inflasiekoers is. Om 'n vroeëre prys te kry, deel jy: P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}.\n\n## Bevolkingsgroei\n\n'n Bevolking groei ook saamgesteld: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, met P die huidige bevolking en i die groeikoers per jaar. Rond die antwoord af tot 'n **heelgetal**, want daar is nie 0,4 van 'n mens nie.\n\n## Wisselkoerse\n\n'n **Wisselkoers** sê hoeveel een geldeenheid in 'n ander werd is, bv. $1 = R18,40.\n\n- Buitelandse geld → rand: **vermenigvuldig** met die koers: $150 × 18,40 = R2 760,00.\n- Rand → buitelandse geld: **deel** deur die koers: R2 000 ÷ 18,40 = $108,70.\n- Die rand **verswak** as jy meer rand vir een dollar moet betaal (bv. R18,40 → R19,10). Ingevoerde goedere soos selfone en petrol word duurder, maar uitvoerders, soos die sitrusboere by Brits, kry meer rand vir elke dollar.\n- Die rand **versterk** as een dollar minder rand kos. Dan word invoere goedkoper.\n\n> **Onthou!** Gesonde-verstand-toets: een dollar (of euro of pond) is meer werd as een rand, dus moet die getal rand altyd **groter** wees as die getal dollar.\n\n## Stappe vir enige finansiesom\n\n1. Besluit watter tipe dit is: enkelvoudig, saamgesteld, huurkoop, inflasie, bevolking of wisselkoers.\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Skryf P, i en n neer, en pas i en n aan vir die saamstellingsperiode.\n4. Vervang en bereken in een stap.\n5. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke en skryf die eenheid (R, $, € of £).","en":"## The symbols you must know\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| P | **principal**: the starting amount you invest or borrow |\n| A | **accumulated amount**: the final amount after n years |\n| i | **interest rate** per year as a decimal: 8% → i = [[8/100]] = 0.08 |\n| n | **time period** in years (or the number of compounding periods) |\n\nThe interest you earn (or pay) is **A − P**. Money is rounded to the nearest cent, so **two decimal places**, e.g. R12 345.67.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Substituting i = 8 instead of i = 0.08. Always divide the percentage by 100 first.\n\n## Simple interest\n\n**A = P(1 + in)**\n\nInterest is calculated each year only on the **original principal**, so you get exactly the same amount of interest every year. That is why the growth is **linear**: the graph of A against n is a straight line.\n\n- Time in months? Convert to years: 18 months → n = [[18/12]] = 1.5.\n- You can also calculate P, i or n: substitute the known values and solve the equation. E.g. R6 000 grows at 8% p.a. simple interest to R8 400: 8 400 = 6 000(1 + 0.08n) → 1.4 = 1 + 0.08n → n = 5 years.\n\n## Compound interest\n\n**A = P(1 + i)^{n}**\n\nHere interest is calculated on the principal **plus the interest already added**: interest on interest. The growth is **exponential**: the graph is a curve that gets steeper and steeper. After the first year compound interest always gives more than simple interest at the same rate.\n\nTo find the principal when the final amount is given (\"How much must I invest now?\"): **P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}**.\n\n### Compounding periods\n\nIf interest is added more than once a year, adjust **both** i and n:\n\n| Compounded | Rate per period | Number of periods |\n|---|---|---|\n| annually | i | n |\n| half-yearly | [[i/2]] | 2n |\n| quarterly | [[i/4]] | 4n |\n| monthly | [[i/12]] | 12n |\n\nE.g. 8% p.a. compounded quarterly for 5 years: A = P(1 + [[0.08/4]])^{20}.\n\n> **Tip:** Type the whole calculation into your calculator in one go. If you round in between (e.g. 1.00875 → 1.01), your answer will be wrong. Only round the final answer.\n\n## Hire purchase\n\nWith **hire purchase** you take the item now and pay it off in monthly instalments. The interest is **simple interest on the outstanding amount** (the balance after the deposit).\n\n1. Deposit = percentage × cash price.\n2. Outstanding amount: P = cash price − deposit.\n3. A = P(1 + in): the total you pay back over the period.\n4. Monthly instalment = A ÷ number of months. Add monthly insurance if it is given.\n5. Total cost = deposit + A (+ all insurance).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Calculating interest on the full cash price, or forgetting to subtract the deposit first.\n\n## Inflation\n\n**Inflation** is the general rise in prices over time. It works exactly like compound interest: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, where i is the inflation rate. To find an earlier price, divide: P = A ÷ (1 + i)^{n}.\n\n## Population growth\n\nA population also grows in a compound way: A = P(1 + i)^{n}, with P the current population and i the growth rate per year. Round the answer to a **whole number**, because there is no such thing as 0.4 of a person.\n\n## Exchange rates\n\nAn **exchange rate** tells you how much one currency is worth in another, e.g. $1 = R18.40.\n\n- Foreign currency → rand: **multiply** by the rate: $150 × 18.40 = R2 760.00.\n- Rand → foreign currency: **divide** by the rate: R2 000 ÷ 18.40 = $108.70.\n- The rand **weakens** when you have to pay more rand for one dollar (e.g. R18.40 → R19.10). Imported goods such as cellphones and petrol become more expensive, but exporters, such as the citrus farmers near Brits, get more rand for every dollar.\n- The rand **strengthens** when one dollar costs fewer rand. Then imports become cheaper.\n\n> **Remember!** Common-sense check: one dollar (or euro or pound) is worth more than one rand, so the number of rand must always be **bigger** than the number of dollars.\n\n## Steps for any finance question\n\n1. Decide what type it is: simple, compound, hire purchase, inflation, population or exchange rate.\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Write down P, i and n, and adjust i and n for the compounding period.\n4. Substitute and calculate in one step.\n5. Round to two decimal places and write the unit (R, $, € or £)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofsom (P)","en":"Principal (P)"},"def":{"af":"Die beginbedrag wat belê of geleen word.","en":"The starting amount that is invested or borrowed."}},{"term":{"af":"Opgehoopte bedrag (A)","en":"Accumulated amount (A)"},"def":{"af":"Die totale bedrag (hoofsom plus rente) aan die einde van die tydperk.","en":"The total amount (principal plus interest) at the end of the period."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente","en":"Simple interest"},"def":{"af":"Rente wat elke jaar net op die oorspronklike hoofsom bereken word: A = P(1 + in). Die groei is lineêr.","en":"Interest calculated each year only on the original principal: A = P(1 + in). The growth is linear."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde rente","en":"Compound interest"},"def":{"af":"Rente wat op die hoofsom plus die reeds bygetelde rente bereken word: A = P(1 + i)ⁿ. Die groei is eksponensieel.","en":"Interest calculated on the principal plus the interest already added: A = P(1 + i)ⁿ. The growth is exponential."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamstellingsperiode","en":"Compounding period"},"def":{"af":"Hoe gereeld rente bygetel word (jaarliks, halfjaarliks, kwartaalliks of maandeliks). Dit verander die waardes van i en n.","en":"How often interest is added (annually, half-yearly, quarterly or monthly). It changes the values of i and n."}},{"term":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"def":{"af":"Koop op krediet: jy betaal 'n deposito en dan maandelikse paaiemente, met enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag.","en":"Buying on credit: you pay a deposit and then monthly instalments, with simple interest on the outstanding amount."}},{"term":{"af":"Paaiement","en":"Instalment"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste bedrag wat elke maand betaal word om 'n skuld af te betaal.","en":"The fixed amount paid every month to pay off a debt."}},{"term":{"af":"Inflasie","en":"Inflation"},"def":{"af":"Die algemene styging in die pryse van goedere en dienste oor tyd; dit word met saamgestelde groei bereken.","en":"The general rise in the prices of goods and services over time; it is calculated with compound growth."}},{"term":{"af":"Wisselkoers","en":"Exchange rate"},"def":{"af":"Die waarde van een geldeenheid uitgedruk in 'n ander, bv. $1 = R18,40.","en":"The value of one currency expressed in another, e.g. $1 = R18.40."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Enkelvoudige teenoor saamgestelde rente","en":"Simple versus compound interest"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato belê R8 000 vir 5 jaar teen 7,5% p.j. Bereken die opgehoopte bedrag as die rente (a) enkelvoudig is en (b) jaarliks saamgestel word. (c) Hoeveel meer lewer die saamgestelde belegging op?","en":"Lerato invests R8 000 for 5 years at 7.5% p.a. Calculate the accumulated amount if the interest is (a) simple and (b) compounded annually. (c) How much more does the compound investment give?"},"steps":[{"af":"Skryf die waardes neer: P = 8 000; i = [[7,5/100]] = 0,075; n = 5.","en":"Write down the values: P = 8 000; i = [[7.5/100]] = 0.075; n = 5."},{"af":"(a) A = P(1 + in) = 8 000(1 + 0,075 × 5) = 8 000 × 1,375","en":"(a) A = P(1 + in) = 8 000(1 + 0.075 × 5) = 8 000 × 1.375"},{"af":"A = R11 000,00","en":"A = R11 000.00"},{"af":"(b) A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 8 000(1 + 0,075)^{5} = 8 000(1,075)^{5} = R11 485,03 (tik dit in een keer in)","en":"(b) A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 8 000(1 + 0.075)^{5} = 8 000(1.075)^{5} = R11 485.03 (type it in one go)"},{"af":"(c) Verskil = 11 485,03 − 11 000,00 = R485,03","en":"(c) Difference = 11 485.03 − 11 000.00 = R485.03"},{"af":"Saamgestelde rente lewer meer op, want elke jaar word rente ook op die vorige jare se rente verdien.","en":"Compound interest gives more, because each year interest is also earned on the previous years' interest."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R11 000,00  (b) R11 485,03  (c) R485,03 meer","en":"(a) R11 000.00  (b) R11 485.03  (c) R485.03 more"}},{"title":{"af":"Maandeliks saamgestelde rente","en":"Interest compounded monthly"},"problem":{"af":"Johan belê R15 000 in 'n spaarrekening by 'n bank in Pretoria teen 10,5% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Hoeveel is in die rekening ná 4 jaar, en hoeveel rente het hy verdien?","en":"Johan invests R15 000 in a savings account at a bank in Pretoria at 10.5% p.a., compounded monthly. How much is in the account after 4 years, and how much interest did he earn?"},"steps":[{"af":"Maandeliks: deel die koers deur 12 en vermenigvuldig die jare met 12. i = [[0,105/12]] = 0,00875 per maand; n = 4 × 12 = 48 maande.","en":"Monthly: divide the rate by 12 and multiply the years by 12. i = [[0.105/12]] = 0.00875 per month; n = 4 × 12 = 48 months."},{"af":"A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 15 000(1 + [[0,105/12]])^{48}","en":"A = P(1 + i)^{n} = 15 000(1 + [[0.105/12]])^{48}"},{"af":"A = R22 787,76 (moenie 1,00875 afrond voordat jy die mag bereken nie)","en":"A = R22 787.76 (do not round 1.00875 before you work out the power)"},{"af":"Rente = A − P = 22 787,76 − 15 000 = R7 787,76","en":"Interest = A − P = 22 787.76 − 15 000 = R7 787.76"}],"answer":{"af":"A = R22 787,76; rente = R7 787,76","en":"A = R22 787.76; interest = R7 787.76"}},{"title":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"problem":{"af":"Thandi koop 'n yskas met 'n kontantprys van R12 000 op huurkoop by 'n meubelwinkel in Brits. Sy betaal 10% deposito en die balans oor 2 jaar teen 15% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Bereken (a) haar maandelikse paaiement en (b) die totale bedrag wat sy vir die yskas betaal.","en":"Thandi buys a fridge with a cash price of R12 000 on hire purchase at a furniture store in Brits. She pays a 10% deposit and the balance over 2 years at 15% p.a. simple interest. Calculate (a) her monthly instalment and (b) the total amount she pays for the fridge."},"steps":[{"af":"Deposito = 10% × 12 000 = 0,1 × 12 000 = R1 200,00","en":"Deposit = 10% × 12 000 = 0.1 × 12 000 = R1 200.00"},{"af":"Uitstaande bedrag: P = 12 000 − 1 200 = R10 800,00. Die rente word net hierop bereken.","en":"Outstanding amount: P = 12 000 − 1 200 = R10 800.00. Interest is charged only on this."},{"af":"A = P(1 + in) = 10 800(1 + 0,15 × 2) = 10 800 × 1,3 = R14 040,00","en":"A = P(1 + in) = 10 800(1 + 0.15 × 2) = 10 800 × 1.3 = R14 040.00"},{"af":"(a) 2 jaar = 24 maande. Paaiement = 14 040 ÷ 24 = R585,00 per maand","en":"(a) 2 years = 24 months. Instalment = 14 040 ÷ 24 = R585.00 per month"},{"af":"(b) Totaal = deposito + A = 1 200 + 14 040 = R15 240,00. Dit is R3 240,00 meer as die kontantprys.","en":"(b) Total = deposit + A = 1 200 + 14 040 = R15 240.00. That is R3 240.00 more than the cash price."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R585,00 per maand  (b) R15 240,00","en":"(a) R585.00 per month  (b) R15 240.00"}},{"title":{"af":"Wisselkoerse en 'n swakker rand","en":"Exchange rates and a weaker rand"},"problem":{"af":"'n Sitrusboer naby Brits voer lemoene na Europa uit en ontvang €18 000. (a) Hoeveel rand is dit as €1 = R20,15? (b) Die rand verswak na €1 = R20,90. Hoeveel meer rand kry die boer nou vir dieselfde €18 000? (c) Is 'n swakker rand goed of sleg vir 'n gesin wat 'n vakansie in Europa beplan?","en":"A citrus farmer near Brits exports oranges to Europe and receives €18 000. (a) How many rand is that if €1 = R20.15? (b) The rand weakens to €1 = R20.90. How many more rand does the farmer now get for the same €18 000? (c) Is a weaker rand good or bad for a family planning a holiday in Europe?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Euro → rand: vermenigvuldig met die koers. 18 000 × 20,15 = R362 700,00","en":"(a) Euro → rand: multiply by the rate. 18 000 × 20.15 = R362 700.00"},{"af":"(b) Teen die nuwe koers: 18 000 × 20,90 = R376 200,00","en":"(b) At the new rate: 18 000 × 20.90 = R376 200.00"},{"af":"Verskil = 376 200 − 362 700 = R13 500,00 meer vir die boer","en":"Difference = 376 200 − 362 700 = R13 500.00 more for the farmer"},{"af":"(c) Sleg: die rand het verswak, so die gesin moet nou meer rand betaal vir elke euro wat hulle in Europa spandeer. Wat goed is vir uitvoerders, is sleg vir invoerders en reisigers.","en":"(c) Bad: the rand has weakened, so the family must now pay more rand for every euro they spend in Europe. What is good for exporters is bad for importers and travellers."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R362 700,00  (b) R13 500,00 meer  (c) sleg vir die gesin","en":"(a) R362 700.00  (b) R13 500.00 more  (c) bad for the family"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die formule A = P(1 + in) staan P vir …","en":"In the formula A = P(1 + in), P stands for …"},"options":[{"af":"die opgehoopte bedrag ná n jaar","en":"the accumulated amount after n years"},{"af":"die rentekoers per jaar","en":"the interest rate per year"},{"af":"die hoofsom (die beginbedrag)","en":"the principal (the starting amount)"},{"af":"die rente wat verdien is","en":"the interest earned"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"P is die hoofsom: die bedrag waarmee jy begin. A is die eindbedrag, i die rentekoers en die rente self is A − P.","en":"P is the principal: the amount you start with. A is the final amount, i is the interest rate and the interest itself is A − P."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By enkelvoudige rente is die grafiek van die opgehoopte bedrag teenoor die tyd 'n kromme wat al hoe steiler word.","en":"With simple interest the graph of the accumulated amount against time is a curve that gets steeper and steeper."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Enkelvoudige rente gee elke jaar dieselfde bedrag rente, so die groei is lineêr: 'n reguit lyn. Die kromme hoort by saamgestelde rente (eksponensiële groei).","en":"False. Simple interest gives the same amount of interest every year, so the growth is linear: a straight line. The curve belongs to compound interest (exponential growth)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing of formule.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description or formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente","en":"Simple interest"},"r":{"af":"A = P(1 + in)","en":"A = P(1 + in)"}},{"l":{"af":"Saamgestelde rente","en":"Compound interest"},"r":{"af":"A = P(1 + i)ⁿ","en":"A = P(1 + i)ⁿ"}},{"l":{"af":"Huurkoop","en":"Hire purchase"},"r":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente op die balans ná die deposito","en":"Simple interest on the balance after the deposit"}},{"l":{"af":"Inflasie","en":"Inflation"},"r":{"af":"Die algemene styging in pryse oor tyd","en":"The general rise in prices over time"}},{"l":{"af":"Wisselkoers","en":"Exchange rate"},"r":{"af":"Die waarde van een geldeenheid in 'n ander","en":"The value of one currency in another"}}],"explain":{"af":"Enkelvoudige rente: rente net op P (lineêr). Saamgestelde rente: rente op rente (eksponensieel). Huurkoop gebruik enkelvoudige rente op die uitstaande bedrag. Inflasie is prysstyging en word met saamgestelde groei bereken. 'n Wisselkoers skakel tussen geldeenhede om.","en":"Simple interest: interest only on P (linear). Compound interest: interest on interest (exponential). Hire purchase uses simple interest on the outstanding amount. Inflation is rising prices and is calculated with compound growth. An exchange rate converts between currencies."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Belegging verdien 12% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel, vir 3 jaar. Watter waardes van i en n gebruik jy in A = P(1 + i)ⁿ?","en":"An investment earns 12% p.a., compounded monthly, for 3 years. Which values of i and n do you use in A = P(1 + i)ⁿ?"},"options":[{"af":"i = 0,12 en n = 3","en":"i = 0.12 and n = 3"},{"af":"i = 0,01 en n = 36","en":"i = 0.01 and n = 36"},{"af":"i = 0,12 en n = 36","en":"i = 0.12 and n = 36"},{"af":"i = 0,01 en n = 3","en":"i = 0.01 and n = 3"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Maandeliks: i = 0,12 ÷ 12 = 0,01 per maand en n = 3 × 12 = 36 maande. Jy moet albei aanpas; as jy net een verander, is die antwoord verkeerd.","en":"Monthly: i = 0.12 ÷ 12 = 0.01 per month and n = 3 × 12 = 36 months. You must adjust both; if you change only one, the answer is wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sipho belê R4 000 teen 6% p.j. enkelvoudige rente vir 3 jaar. Die opgehoopte bedrag is R___.","en":"Sipho invests R4 000 at 6% p.a. simple interest for 3 years. The accumulated amount is R___."},"answers":{"af":["4 720,00","R4 720,00","R 4 720,00","4 720","R4 720","R 4 720","4720,00","R4720,00","R 4720,00","4720","R4720","R 4720","4 720.00","R4 720.00","R 4 720.00","4720.00","R4720.00","R 4720.00"],"en":["4 720,00","R4 720,00","R 4 720,00","4 720","R4 720","R 4 720","4720,00","R4720,00","R 4720,00","4720","R4720","R 4720","4 720.00","R4 720.00","R 4 720.00","4720.00","R4720.00","R 4720.00"]},"explain":{"af":"A = P(1 + in) = 4 000(1 + 0,06 × 3) = 4 000 × 1,18 = R4 720,00.","en":"A = P(1 + in) = 4 000(1 + 0.06 × 3) = 4 000 × 1.18 = R4 720.00."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["720,00","4 764,06","4 240,00"],"en":["720.00","4 764.06","4 240.00"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"R5 000 word vir 4 jaar belê teen 8% p.j., jaarliks saamgestel. Wat is die opgehoopte bedrag?","en":"R5 000 is invested for 4 years at 8% p.a., compounded annually. What is the accumulated amount?"},"options":[{"af":"R6 600,00","en":"R6 600.00"},{"af":"R1 802,44","en":"R1 802.44"},{"af":"R21 600,00","en":"R21 600.00"},{"af":"R6 802,44","en":"R6 802.44"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"A = 5 000(1,08)⁴ = R6 802,44. R6 600,00 is enkelvoudige rente, R1 802,44 is net die rente, en R21 600,00 kom van 5 000 × 1,08 × 4 (maal 4 in plaas van tot die mag 4).","en":"A = 5 000(1.08)⁴ = R6 802.44. R6 600.00 is simple interest, R1 802.44 is only the interest, and R21 600.00 comes from 5 000 × 1.08 × 4 (times 4 instead of to the power 4)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die wisselkoers verander van $1 = R17,80 na $1 = R18,90. Dit beteken die rand het verswak, en ingevoerde goedere soos selfone word duurder in rand.","en":"The exchange rate changes from $1 = R17.80 to $1 = R18.90. This means the rand has weakened, and imported goods such as cellphones become more expensive in rand."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy moet nou meer rand (R18,90 in plaas van R17,80) vir een dollar betaal, so die rand is swakker en alles wat in dollar gekoop word, kos meer rand.","en":"True. You now have to pay more rand (R18.90 instead of R17.80) for one dollar, so the rand is weaker and everything bought in dollars costs more rand."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die wisselkoers is $1 = R18,40. Hoeveel dollar kry jy vir R5 000? Rond af tot 2 desimale plekke: $___","en":"The exchange rate is $1 = R18.40. How many dollars do you get for R5 000? Round to 2 decimal places: $___"},"answers":{"af":["271,74","$271,74","$ 271,74","271.74","$271.74","$ 271.74"],"en":["271,74","$271,74","$ 271,74","271.74","$271.74","$ 271.74"]},"explain":{"af":"Rand → dollar: deel deur die koers. 5 000 ÷ 18,40 = $271,74. Gesonde-verstand-toets: die getal dollar moet kleiner as die getal rand wees.","en":"Rand → dollar: divide by the rate. 5 000 ÷ 18.40 = $271.74. Common-sense check: the number of dollars must be smaller than the number of rand."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["92 000,00","271,73","2 717,39"],"en":["92 000.00","271.73","2 717.39"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Brood kos vandag R20,00. As die inflasiekoers 6% p.j. bly, wat sal 'n brood oor 5 jaar kos?","en":"A loaf of bread costs R20.00 today. If the inflation rate stays at 6% p.a., what will a loaf cost in 5 years?"},"options":[{"af":"R26,76","en":"R26.76"},{"af":"R26,00","en":"R26.00"},{"af":"R14,68","en":"R14.68"},{"af":"R6,76","en":"R6.76"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Inflasie is saamgestelde groei: A = 20(1,06)⁵ = R26,76. R26,00 is enkelvoudige groei, R14,68 kom van (1 − 0,06) en R6,76 is net die prysstyging.","en":"Inflation is compound growth: A = 20(1.06)⁵ = R26.76. R26.00 is simple growth, R14.68 comes from (1 − 0.06) and R6.76 is only the price increase."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"R10 000 word belê teen 9% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Wat is die waarde van die belegging ná 3 jaar?","en":"R10 000 is invested at 9% p.a., compounded monthly. What is the value of the investment after 3 years?"},"options":[{"af":"R12 950,29","en":"R12 950.29"},{"af":"R10 226,69","en":"R10 226.69"},{"af":"R13 086,45","en":"R13 086.45"},{"af":"R222 512,25","en":"R222 512.25"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"i = 0,09 ÷ 12 = 0,0075 en n = 3 × 12 = 36: A = 10 000(1,0075)³⁶ = R13 086,45. R12 950,29 is jaarliks saamgestel, R10 226,69 gebruik n = 3 en R222 512,25 gebruik i = 0,09 met n = 36.","en":"i = 0.09 ÷ 12 = 0.0075 and n = 3 × 12 = 36: A = 10 000(1.0075)³⁶ = R13 086.45. R12 950.29 is compounded annually, R10 226.69 uses n = 3 and R222 512.25 uses i = 0.09 with n = 36."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Televisie het 'n kontantprys van R8 400. Lindiwe koop dit op huurkoop: sy betaal 10% deposito en die balans oor 2 jaar teen 16% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Daar is ook R25 versekering per maand. Wat is haar totale maandelikse betaling? R___","en":"A television has a cash price of R8 400. Lindiwe buys it on hire purchase: she pays a 10% deposit and the balance over 2 years at 16% p.a. simple interest. There is also R25 insurance per month. What is her total monthly payment? R___"},"answers":{"af":["440,80","R440,80","R 440,80","440,8","R440,8","R 440,8","440.80","R440.80","R 440.80","440.8","R440.8","R 440.8"],"en":["440,80","R440,80","R 440,80","440,8","R440,8","R 440,8","440.80","R440.80","R 440.80","440.8","R440.8","R 440.8"]},"explain":{"af":"Deposito = 0,1 × 8 400 = R840,00. Balans = R7 560,00. A = 7 560(1 + 0,16 × 2) = R9 979,20. Paaiement = 9 979,20 ÷ 24 = R415,80. Plus versekering: 415,80 + 25 = R440,80.","en":"Deposit = 0.1 × 8 400 = R840.00. Balance = R7 560.00. A = 7 560(1 + 0.16 × 2) = R9 979.20. Instalment = 9 979.20 ÷ 24 = R415.80. Plus insurance: 415.80 + 25 = R440.80."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["415,80","487,00","390,40"],"en":["415.80","487.00","390.40"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gestel 'n dorp in Madibeng het 120 000 inwoners en die bevolking groei teen 2,4% p.j. Wat sal die bevolking ná 6 jaar wees (afgerond tot 'n heelgetal)?","en":"Suppose a town in Madibeng has 120 000 inhabitants and the population grows at 2.4% p.a. What will the population be after 6 years (rounded to a whole number)?"},"options":[{"af":"137 280","en":"137 280"},{"af":"138 351","en":"138 351"},{"af":"436 226","en":"436 226"},{"af":"737 280","en":"737 280"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Bevolkingsgroei is saamgesteld: A = 120 000(1,024)⁶ = 138 350,58 ≈ 138 351. 137 280 is enkelvoudige groei, 436 226 gebruik i = 0,24 en 737 280 vermenigvuldig met 6 in plaas van tot die mag 6.","en":"Population growth is compound: A = 120 000(1.024)⁶ = 138 350.58 ≈ 138 351. 137 280 is simple growth, 436 226 uses i = 0.24 and 737 280 multiplies by 6 instead of raising to the power 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Anika wil oor 4 jaar R20 000 hê vir haar eerste motor. Hoeveel moet sy nou belê teen 7% p.j., jaarliks saamgestel? Rond af tot 2 desimale plekke: R___","en":"Anika wants R20 000 in 4 years for her first car. How much must she invest now at 7% p.a., compounded annually? Round to 2 decimal places: R___"},"answers":{"af":["15 257,90","R15 257,90","R 15 257,90","15 257,9","R15 257,9","R 15 257,9","15257,90","R15257,90","R 15257,90","15257,9","R15257,9","R 15257,9","15 257.90","R15 257.90","R 15 257.90","15 257.9","R15 257.9","R 15 257.9","15257.90","R15257.90","R 15257.90","15257.9","R15257.9","R 15257.9"],"en":["15 257,90","R15 257,90","R 15 257,90","15 257,9","R15 257,9","R 15 257,9","15257,90","R15257,90","R 15257,90","15257,9","R15257,9","R 15257,9","15 257.90","R15 257.90","R 15 257.90","15 257.9","R15 257.9","R 15 257.9","15257.90","R15257.90","R 15257.90","15257.9","R15257.9","R 15257.9"]},"explain":{"af":"Hier is A = 20 000 gegee en jy soek P. P = A ÷ (1 + i)ⁿ = 20 000 ÷ (1,07)⁴ = R15 257,90. Kontroleer: 15 257,90 × (1,07)⁴ ≈ 20 000.","en":"Here A = 20 000 is given and you need P. P = A ÷ (1 + i)ⁿ = 20 000 ÷ (1.07)⁴ = R15 257.90. Check: 15 257.90 × (1.07)⁴ ≈ 20 000."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["26 215,92","15 625,00","14 400,00"],"en":["26 215.92","15 625.00","14 400.00"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter wil R12 000 vir 5 jaar belê. Bank A bied 10% p.j. enkelvoudige rente. Bank B bied 9% p.j., maandeliks saamgestel. Watter bank gee die meeste geld ná 5 jaar?","en":"Pieter wants to invest R12 000 for 5 years. Bank A offers 10% p.a. simple interest. Bank B offers 9% p.a., compounded monthly. Which bank gives the most money after 5 years?"},"options":[{"af":"Bank B: R18 788,17 teenoor Bank A se R18 000,00","en":"Bank B: R18 788.17 against Bank A's R18 000.00"},{"af":"Bank A, want 10% is 'n hoër koers as 9%","en":"Bank A, because 10% is a higher rate than 9%"},{"af":"Bank B: R18 463,49 teenoor Bank A se R18 000,00","en":"Bank B: R18 463.49 against Bank A's R18 000.00"},{"af":"Bank A: R18 000,00 teenoor Bank B se R17 400,00","en":"Bank A: R18 000.00 against Bank B's R17 400.00"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bank A: 12 000(1 + 0,10 × 5) = R18 000,00. Bank B: 12 000(1 + 0,09 ÷ 12)⁶⁰ = R18 788,17. Bank B gee R788,17 meer, al is sy koers laer, want maandelikse saamstelling gee rente op rente. R18 463,49 sou jaarlikse saamstelling wees en R17 400,00 enkelvoudige rente teen 9%.","en":"Bank A: 12 000(1 + 0.10 × 5) = R18 000.00. Bank B: 12 000(1 + 0.09 ÷ 12)⁶⁰ = R18 788.17. Bank B gives R788.17 more, even though its rate is lower, because monthly compounding gives interest on interest. R18 463.49 would be annual compounding and R17 400.00 simple interest at 9%."}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-statistiek","title":{"af":"Statistiek","en":"Statistics"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus, kwartiele, IKO en persentiele kan bereken, 'n vyfgetalopsomming en mond-en-snor-diagram kan opstel, en gegroepeerde data kan ontleed.","en":"You will be able to calculate the mean, median, mode, quartiles, IQR and percentiles, set up a five-number summary and box-and-whisker plot, and analyse grouped data."},"summary":{"af":"## Sentrale neiging: gemiddelde, mediaan en modus\n\n**Ongegroepeerde data** is 'n lys van die werklike waardes. Die drie maatstawwe van sentrale neiging beskryf die \"tipiese\" waarde:\n\n| Maatstaf | Hoe om dit te kry |\n|---|---|\n| **Gemiddelde** (x̄) | x̄ = [[som van die waardes/aantal waardes]] = [[Σx/n]] |\n| **Mediaan** | Rangskik die data eers van klein na groot. Die mediaan is die middelste waarde, by posisie [[n + 1/2]]. As n ewe is, is dit die gemiddelde van die twee middelste waardes. |\n| **Modus** | Die waarde wat die meeste voorkom. Data kan twee modusse hê (bimodaal) of geen modus nie. |\n\nAs die gemiddelde gegee is, kry jy die som so: **som = x̄ × n**. Bv. vyf getalle met 'n gemiddelde van 14 het 'n som van 70. So bereken jy 'n ontbrekende waarde of 'n nuwe gemiddelde.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die middelste getal in die lys te kies sonder om die data eers te rangskik.\n\n### Watter maatstaf pas die beste?\n\n- **Gemiddelde:** gebruik al die waardes, maar word maklik deur uitskieters getrek.\n- **Mediaan:** die beste keuse as daar uitskieters is of as die data skeef is, bv. huispryse en salarisse.\n- **Modus:** die enigste keuse vir kategoriese data, bv. die gewildste skoengrootte.\n\n## Verspreiding: omvang, kwartiele en persentiele\n\n- **Omvang** = grootste waarde − kleinste waarde.\n- **Kwartiele** verdeel die gerangskikte data in vier dele met ewe veel waardes. Q_{2} is die mediaan.\n- **Q_{1}** (onderste kwartiel) is die mediaan van die onderste helfte van die data, en **Q_{3}** (boonste kwartiel) is die mediaan van die boonste helfte.\n- As n onewe is, laat jy die mediaan self uit wanneer jy die twee helftes vorm.\n- **Interkwartielomvang (IKO)** = Q_{3} − Q_{1}. Dit is die omvang van die middelste 50% van die data, en uitskieters raak dit nie.\n- **Semi-interkwartielomvang** = [[1/2]](Q_{3} − Q_{1}).\n- **Persentiele** verdeel die data in 100 dele. Die p-de persentiel is die waarde waaronder ongeveer p% van die data lê. Q_{1} is die 25ste, die mediaan die 50ste en Q_{3} die 75ste persentiel.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jou punt op die 90ste persentiel is, het ongeveer 90% van die groep laer as jy gekry. Dit is NIE 'n punt van 90% nie!\n\n## Vyfgetalopsomming en mond-en-snor-diagram\n\nDie **vyfgetalopsomming** is: minimum; Q_{1}; mediaan; Q_{3}; maksimum.\n\nOm 'n **mond-en-snor-diagram** te teken:\n\n1. Teken 'n getallelyn met 'n eweredige skaal van die minimum tot die maksimum.\n2. Teken 'n reghoek (die \"mond\") van Q_{1} tot Q_{3}.\n3. Trek 'n lyn dwarsdeur die mond by die mediaan.\n4. Trek die \"snorre\": van Q_{1} tot by die minimum en van Q_{3} tot by die maksimum.\n\nElke snor en elke helfte van die mond bevat ongeveer 25% van die data. 'n Lang snor of 'n breë deel van die mond wys dat die data daar meer uitgesprei is; 'n smal mond wys dat die middelste 50% dig bymekaar lê.\n\n## Uitskieters\n\n'n **Uitskieter** is 'n waarde wat baie groter of baie kleiner as die res van die data is, bv. 'n tikfout of een baie hoë salaris. Dit trek die gemiddelde en die omvang sterk, maar die mediaan en die IKO skaars. Op 'n mond-en-snor-diagram sien jy dit as 'n baie lang snor. (In graad 11 leer jy 'n formele reël vir uitskieters.)\n\n## Gegroepeerde data\n\nAs data in **klasintervalle** soos 10 ≤ x < 20 gegee word, ken jy nie die presiese waardes nie, dus **beraam** jy.\n\n- **Modale klas:** die klas met die grootste frekwensie.\n- **Klas wat die mediaan bevat:** bereken die posisie [[n + 1/2]], tel die frekwensies van bo af op (kumulatiewe frekwensie) en kyk in watter klas daardie posisie val.\n- **Beraamde gemiddelde:** gebruik die **middelpunt** van elke klas as die waarde vir al die data in daardie klas.\n\n1. Middelpunt = [[ondergrens + bogrens/2]], bv. 10 ≤ x < 20 → 15.\n2. Vermenigvuldig elke middelpunt met sy frekwensie: f × x.\n3. Beraamde gemiddelde = [[Σ(f × x)/Σf]] = [[som van al die f × x/totale frekwensie]].\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om deur die aantal klasse te deel in plaas van deur die totale frekwensie, of om net die middelpunte op te tel sonder om met f te vermenigvuldig.\n\n## Effek van veranderinge op die data\n\n- Tel 'n getal k by elke waarde: die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en kwartiele styg almal met k, maar die omvang en IKO bly dieselfde, want die hele datastel skuif net op.\n- Vermenigvuldig elke waarde met 'n positiewe getal k: al die maatstawwe, ook die omvang en IKO, word met k vermenigvuldig.","en":"## Central tendency: mean, median and mode\n\n**Ungrouped data** is a list of the actual values. The three measures of central tendency describe the \"typical\" value:\n\n| Measure | How to find it |\n|---|---|\n| **Mean** (x̄) | x̄ = [[sum of the values/number of values]] = [[Σx/n]] |\n| **Median** | First arrange the data from smallest to largest. The median is the middle value, at position [[n + 1/2]]. If n is even, it is the mean of the two middle values. |\n| **Mode** | The value that occurs most often. Data can have two modes (bimodal) or no mode. |\n\nIf the mean is given, you find the sum like this: **sum = x̄ × n**. E.g. five numbers with a mean of 14 have a sum of 70. This is how you calculate a missing value or a new mean.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Choosing the middle number in the list without first arranging the data in order.\n\n### Which measure fits best?\n\n- **Mean:** uses all the values, but is easily pulled by outliers.\n- **Median:** the best choice if there are outliers or the data is skewed, e.g. house prices and salaries.\n- **Mode:** the only choice for categorical data, e.g. the most popular shoe size.\n\n## Spread: range, quartiles and percentiles\n\n- **Range** = largest value − smallest value.\n- **Quartiles** divide the ordered data into four parts with equally many values. Q_{2} is the median.\n- **Q_{1}** (lower quartile) is the median of the lower half of the data, and **Q_{3}** (upper quartile) is the median of the upper half.\n- If n is odd, leave out the median itself when you form the two halves.\n- **Interquartile range (IQR)** = Q_{3} − Q_{1}. It is the range of the middle 50% of the data, and outliers do not affect it.\n- **Semi-interquartile range** = [[1/2]](Q_{3} − Q_{1}).\n- **Percentiles** divide the data into 100 parts. The p-th percentile is the value below which about p% of the data lies. Q_{1} is the 25th, the median the 50th and Q_{3} the 75th percentile.\n\n> **Tip:** If your mark is at the 90th percentile, about 90% of the group scored lower than you. It is NOT a mark of 90%!\n\n## Five-number summary and box-and-whisker plot\n\nThe **five-number summary** is: minimum; Q_{1}; median; Q_{3}; maximum.\n\nTo draw a **box-and-whisker plot**:\n\n1. Draw a number line with an even scale from the minimum to the maximum.\n2. Draw a rectangle (the \"box\") from Q_{1} to Q_{3}.\n3. Draw a line across the box at the median.\n4. Draw the \"whiskers\": from Q_{1} to the minimum and from Q_{3} to the maximum.\n\nEach whisker and each half of the box contains about 25% of the data. A long whisker or a wide part of the box shows that the data is more spread out there; a narrow box shows that the middle 50% lies close together.\n\n## Outliers\n\nAn **outlier** is a value that is much bigger or much smaller than the rest of the data, e.g. a typing error or one very high salary. It pulls the mean and the range strongly, but hardly affects the median and the IQR. On a box-and-whisker plot you see it as a very long whisker. (In Grade 11 you learn a formal rule for outliers.)\n\n## Grouped data\n\nIf data is given in **class intervals** such as 10 ≤ x < 20, you do not know the exact values, so you **estimate**.\n\n- **Modal class:** the class with the highest frequency.\n- **Class containing the median:** work out the position [[n + 1/2]], add up the frequencies from the top (cumulative frequency) and see in which class that position falls.\n- **Estimated mean:** use the **midpoint** of each class as the value for all the data in that class.\n\n1. Midpoint = [[lower limit + upper limit/2]], e.g. 10 ≤ x < 20 → 15.\n2. Multiply each midpoint by its frequency: f × x.\n3. Estimated mean = [[Σ(f × x)/Σf]] = [[sum of all the f × x/total frequency]].\n\n> **Common mistake:** Dividing by the number of classes instead of by the total frequency, or just adding the midpoints without multiplying by f.\n\n## Effect of changes to the data\n\n- Add a number k to every value: the mean, median, mode and quartiles all increase by k, but the range and IQR stay the same, because the whole data set just shifts up.\n- Multiply every value by a positive number k: all the measures, including the range and IQR, are multiplied by k."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde (x̄)","en":"Mean (x̄)"},"def":{"af":"Die som van al die waardes gedeel deur die aantal waardes.","en":"The sum of all the values divided by the number of values."}},{"term":{"af":"Mediaan","en":"Median"},"def":{"af":"Die middelste waarde wanneer die data van klein na groot gerangskik is (Q₂, die 50ste persentiel).","en":"The middle value when the data is arranged from smallest to largest (Q₂, the 50th percentile)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwartiele","en":"Quartiles"},"def":{"af":"Die drie waardes Q₁, Q₂ en Q₃ wat gerangskikte data in vier dele met ewe veel waardes verdeel.","en":"The three values Q₁, Q₂ and Q₃ that divide ordered data into four parts with equally many values."}},{"term":{"af":"Interkwartielomvang (IKO)","en":"Interquartile range (IQR)"},"def":{"af":"Q₃ − Q₁: die omvang van die middelste 50% van die data. Die semi-interkwartielomvang is die helfte daarvan.","en":"Q₃ − Q₁: the range of the middle 50% of the data. The semi-interquartile range is half of it."}},{"term":{"af":"Persentiel","en":"Percentile"},"def":{"af":"Die p-de persentiel is die waarde waaronder ongeveer p% van die data lê.","en":"The p-th percentile is the value below which about p% of the data lies."}},{"term":{"af":"Vyfgetalopsomming","en":"Five-number summary"},"def":{"af":"Minimum; Q₁; mediaan; Q₃; maksimum.","en":"Minimum; Q₁; median; Q₃; maximum."}},{"term":{"af":"Mond-en-snor-diagram","en":"Box-and-whisker plot"},"def":{"af":"'n Diagram van die vyfgetalopsomming: 'n mond van Q₁ tot Q₃ met 'n lyn by die mediaan, en snorre tot by die minimum en maksimum.","en":"A diagram of the five-number summary: a box from Q₁ to Q₃ with a line at the median, and whiskers to the minimum and maximum."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitskieter","en":"Outlier"},"def":{"af":"'n Waarde wat baie groter of baie kleiner as die res van die data is; dit beïnvloed die gemiddelde en omvang sterk.","en":"A value that is much bigger or much smaller than the rest of the data; it strongly affects the mean and range."}},{"term":{"af":"Modale klas","en":"Modal class"},"def":{"af":"By gegroepeerde data: die klasinterval met die grootste frekwensie.","en":"For grouped data: the class interval with the highest frequency."}},{"term":{"af":"Beraamde gemiddelde","en":"Estimated mean"},"def":{"af":"Die gemiddelde van gegroepeerde data, bereken met die klasmiddelpunte: Σ(f × x) ÷ Σf.","en":"The mean of grouped data, calculated with the class midpoints: Σ(f × x) ÷ Σf."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en omvang","en":"Mean, median, mode and range"},"problem":{"af":"'n Skool in Brits se o.16-rugbyspan het in 10 wedstryde die volgende punte aangeteken: 24; 17; 31; 12; 24; 38; 9; 24; 15; 26. Bereken die gemiddelde, mediaan, modus en omvang.","en":"A Brits school's U16 rugby team scored the following points in 10 matches: 24, 17, 31, 12, 24, 38, 9, 24, 15, 26. Calculate the mean, median, mode and range."},"steps":[{"af":"Gemiddelde: som = 220 en n = 10, dus x̄ = [[220/10]] = 22 punte.","en":"Mean: sum = 220 and n = 10, so x̄ = [[220/10]] = 22 points."},{"af":"Rangskik eers: 9; 12; 15; 17; 24; 24; 24; 26; 31; 38.","en":"First arrange in order: 9, 12, 15, 17, 24, 24, 24, 26, 31, 38."},{"af":"Mediaan: n = 10 is ewe, dus lê die mediaan tussen die 5de en 6de waardes: [[24 + 24/2]] = 24 punte.","en":"Median: n = 10 is even, so the median lies between the 5th and 6th values: [[24 + 24/2]] = 24 points."},{"af":"Modus: 24 kom drie keer voor, meer as enige ander waarde, dus is die modus 24 punte.","en":"Mode: 24 occurs three times, more than any other value, so the mode is 24 points."},{"af":"Omvang = 38 − 9 = 29 punte.","en":"Range = 38 − 9 = 29 points."}],"answer":{"af":"x̄ = 22; mediaan = 24; modus = 24; omvang = 29","en":"x̄ = 22; median = 24; mode = 24; range = 29"}},{"title":{"af":"Kwartiele, IKO en die vyfgetalopsomming","en":"Quartiles, IQR and the five-number summary"},"problem":{"af":"Die aantal minute wat 15 leerders op 'n Saterdag op sosiale media spandeer, is: 45; 30; 120; 20; 60; 35; 15; 55; 30; 85; 40; 60; 25; 70; 50. (a) Gee die vyfgetalopsomming. (b) Bereken die IKO en die semi-interkwartielomvang. (c) Beskryf die mond-en-snor-diagram en lewer kommentaar.","en":"The number of minutes 15 learners spend on social media on a Saturday is: 45, 30, 120, 20, 60, 35, 15, 55, 30, 85, 40, 60, 25, 70, 50. (a) Give the five-number summary. (b) Calculate the IQR and the semi-interquartile range. (c) Describe the box-and-whisker plot and comment."},"steps":[{"af":"Rangskik: 15; 20; 25; 30; 30; 35; 40; 45; 50; 55; 60; 60; 70; 85; 120. n = 15.","en":"Arrange in order: 15, 20, 25, 30, 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 60, 70, 85, 120. n = 15."},{"af":"Mediaan by posisie [[15 + 1/2]] = 8: die 8ste waarde is 45 min.","en":"Median at position [[15 + 1/2]] = 8: the 8th value is 45 min."},{"af":"Onderste helfte (die 7 waardes vóór die mediaan): 15; 20; 25; 30; 30; 35; 40, dus Q_{1} = 30. Boonste helfte: 50; 55; 60; 60; 70; 85; 120, dus Q_{3} = 60.","en":"Lower half (the 7 values before the median): 15, 20, 25, 30, 30, 35, 40, so Q_{1} = 30. Upper half: 50, 55, 60, 60, 70, 85, 120, so Q_{3} = 60."},{"af":"(a) Vyfgetalopsomming: minimum 15; Q_{1} = 30; mediaan 45; Q_{3} = 60; maksimum 120.","en":"(a) Five-number summary: minimum 15; Q_{1} = 30; median 45; Q_{3} = 60; maximum 120."},{"af":"(b) IKO = Q_{3} − Q_{1} = 60 − 30 = 30 min; semi-interkwartielomvang = [[30/2]] = 15 min.","en":"(b) IQR = Q_{3} − Q_{1} = 60 − 30 = 30 min; semi-interquartile range = [[30/2]] = 15 min."},{"af":"(c) Die mond strek van 30 tot 60 met 'n lyn by 45; die linkersnor gaan tot 15 en die regtersnor tot 120. Die regtersnor (60 tot 120) is baie langer as die linkersnor (15 tot 30), dus lyk 120 na 'n uitskieter.","en":"(c) The box runs from 30 to 60 with a line at 45; the left whisker goes to 15 and the right whisker to 120. The right whisker (60 to 120) is much longer than the left whisker (15 to 30), so 120 looks like an outlier."}],"answer":{"af":"Vyfgetalopsomming: 15; 30; 45; 60; 120. IKO = 30 min; semi-IKO = 15 min.","en":"Five-number summary: 15; 30; 45; 60; 120. IQR = 30 min; semi-IQR = 15 min."}},{"title":{"af":"Gegroepeerde data","en":"Grouped data"},"problem":{"af":"Die afstand (in km) wat 40 werkers van 'n myn naby Brits elke dag werk toe reis: 0 ≤ x < 10: 6 werkers; 10 ≤ x < 20: 12; 20 ≤ x < 30: 11; 30 ≤ x < 40: 8; 40 ≤ x < 50: 3. Bepaal (a) die modale klas, (b) die klas wat die mediaan bevat en (c) die beraamde gemiddelde afstand.","en":"The distance (in km) that 40 workers at a mine near Brits travel to work each day: 0 ≤ x < 10: 6 workers; 10 ≤ x < 20: 12; 20 ≤ x < 30: 11; 30 ≤ x < 40: 8; 40 ≤ x < 50: 3. Determine (a) the modal class, (b) the class containing the median and (c) the estimated mean distance."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die grootste frekwensie is 12, dus is die modale klas 10 ≤ x < 20.","en":"(a) The highest frequency is 12, so the modal class is 10 ≤ x < 20."},{"af":"(b) Mediaan by posisie [[40 + 1/2]] = 20,5. Kumulatiewe frekwensies: 6; 18; 29; 37; 40. Die 20ste en 21ste waardes lê in 20 ≤ x < 30.","en":"(b) Median at position [[40 + 1/2]] = 20.5. Cumulative frequencies: 6, 18, 29, 37, 40. The 20th and 21st values lie in 20 ≤ x < 30."},{"af":"(c) Middelpunte: 5; 15; 25; 35; 45.","en":"(c) Midpoints: 5, 15, 25, 35, 45."},{"af":"f × x: 6 × 5 = 30; 12 × 15 = 180; 11 × 25 = 275; 8 × 35 = 280; 3 × 45 = 135. Σ(f × x) = 900.","en":"f × x: 6 × 5 = 30; 12 × 15 = 180; 11 × 25 = 275; 8 × 35 = 280; 3 × 45 = 135. Σ(f × x) = 900."},{"af":"Beraamde gemiddelde = [[900/40]] = 22,5 km. Dit is 'n beraming, want ons gebruik middelpunte en nie die werklike afstande nie.","en":"Estimated mean = [[900/40]] = 22.5 km. It is an estimate, because we use midpoints and not the actual distances."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 10 ≤ x < 20  (b) 20 ≤ x < 30  (c) 22,5 km","en":"(a) 10 ≤ x < 20  (b) 20 ≤ x < 30  (c) 22.5 km"}},{"title":{"af":"'n Uitskieter en die beste maatstaf","en":"An outlier and the best measure"},"problem":{"af":"'n Klein besigheid in Brits het ses werknemers. Hulle maandelikse salarisse is R8 500; R9 200; R9 200; R10 400; R11 700 en die eienaar s'n is R65 000. (a) Bereken die gemiddelde en die mediaan. (b) Watter maatstaf beskryf die tipiese salaris die beste? Verduidelik.","en":"A small business in Brits has six employees. Their monthly salaries are R8 500, R9 200, R9 200, R10 400, R11 700 and the owner's is R65 000. (a) Calculate the mean and the median. (b) Which measure describes the typical salary best? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Som = 8 500 + 9 200 + 9 200 + 10 400 + 11 700 + 65 000 = R114 000","en":"Sum = 8 500 + 9 200 + 9 200 + 10 400 + 11 700 + 65 000 = R114 000"},{"af":"Gemiddelde = [[114 000/6]] = R19 000","en":"Mean = [[114 000/6]] = R19 000"},{"af":"Die data is reeds gerangskik en n = 6 is ewe, dus is die mediaan die gemiddelde van die 3de en 4de waardes: [[9 200 + 10 400/2]] = R9 800.","en":"The data is already in order and n = 6 is even, so the median is the mean of the 3rd and 4th values: [[9 200 + 10 400/2]] = R9 800."},{"af":"R65 000 is 'n uitskieter. Dit trek die gemiddelde op tot R19 000, meer as wat 5 van die 6 werknemers verdien.","en":"R65 000 is an outlier. It pulls the mean up to R19 000, more than 5 of the 6 employees earn."},{"af":"(b) Die mediaan (R9 800) beskryf die tipiese salaris die beste, want 'n uitskieter beïnvloed die mediaan skaars.","en":"(b) The median (R9 800) describes the typical salary best, because an outlier hardly affects the median."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Gemiddelde = R19 000; mediaan = R9 800  (b) die mediaan","en":"(a) Mean = R19 000; median = R9 800  (b) the median"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter maatstaf is die middelste waarde wanneer die data van klein na groot gerangskik is?","en":"Which measure is the middle value when the data is arranged from smallest to largest?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gemiddelde","en":"The mean"},{"af":"Die modus","en":"The mode"},{"af":"Die mediaan","en":"The median"},{"af":"Die omvang","en":"The range"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mediaan is die middelste waarde van gerangskikte data. Die gemiddelde is die som ÷ n, die modus die waarde wat die meeste voorkom en die omvang is grootste − kleinste.","en":"The median is the middle value of ordered data. The mean is the sum ÷ n, the mode is the value that occurs most often and the range is largest − smallest."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Uitskieter (baie groot of baie klein waarde) beïnvloed die gemiddelde baie meer as die mediaan.","en":"An outlier (a very large or very small value) affects the mean much more than the median."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die gemiddelde gebruik die grootte van elke waarde, so een uiterste waarde trek dit weg. Die mediaan hang net af van die middelste posisie en verander skaars.","en":"True. The mean uses the size of every value, so one extreme value pulls it away. The median only depends on the middle position and hardly changes."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke maatstaf by die regte beskrywing of formule.","en":"Match each measure to the correct description or formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Omvang","en":"Range"},"r":{"af":"Grootste waarde − kleinste waarde","en":"Largest value − smallest value"}},{"l":{"af":"Interkwartielomvang","en":"Interquartile range"},"r":{"af":"Q₃ − Q₁","en":"Q₃ − Q₁"}},{"l":{"af":"Semi-interkwartielomvang","en":"Semi-interquartile range"},"r":{"af":"½(Q₃ − Q₁)","en":"½(Q₃ − Q₁)"}},{"l":{"af":"75ste persentiel","en":"75th percentile"},"r":{"af":"Q₃, die boonste kwartiel","en":"Q₃, the upper quartile"}},{"l":{"af":"Modus","en":"Mode"},"r":{"af":"Die waarde wat die meeste voorkom","en":"The value that occurs most often"}}],"explain":{"af":"Omvang = maks − min. IKO = Q₃ − Q₁ (middelste 50%). Die semi-IKO is die helfte van die IKO. Q₃ is die 75ste persentiel. Die modus is die waarde wat die meeste voorkom.","en":"Range = max − min. IQR = Q₃ − Q₁ (middle 50%). The semi-IQR is half of the IQR. Q₃ is the 75th percentile. The mode is the value that occurs most often."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die gemiddelde van hierdie data: 7; 12; 9; 15; 12; 8; 14. x̄ = ___","en":"Calculate the mean of this data: 7, 12, 9, 15, 12, 8, 14. x̄ = ___"},"answers":{"af":["11","11,0","11.0","x̄ = 11","x̄=11"],"en":["11","11.0","11,0","x̄ = 11","x̄=11"]},"explain":{"af":"Som = 7 + 12 + 9 + 15 + 12 + 8 + 14 = 77 en n = 7, dus x̄ = 77 ÷ 7 = 11.","en":"Sum = 7 + 12 + 9 + 15 + 12 + 8 + 14 = 77 and n = 7, so x̄ = 77 ÷ 7 = 11."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["12","77","9,63"],"en":["12","77","9.63"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die mediaan van 14; 9; 21; 17; 11; 25?","en":"What is the median of 14, 9, 21, 17, 11, 25?"},"options":[{"af":"19","en":"19"},{"af":"15,5","en":"15.5"},{"af":"16,17","en":"16.17"},{"af":"17","en":"17"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rangskik eers: 9; 11; 14; 17; 21; 25. n = 6 is ewe, dus mediaan = (14 + 17) ÷ 2 = 15,5. 19 kom van die middelste twee getalle in die ongerangskikte lys, 16,17 is die gemiddelde en 17 is net een van die twee middelste waardes.","en":"First arrange in order: 9, 11, 14, 17, 21, 25. n = 6 is even, so median = (14 + 17) ÷ 2 = 15.5. 19 comes from the middle two numbers in the unordered list, 16.17 is the mean and 17 is only one of the two middle values."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n graad met 200 leerders lê Lerato se wiskundepunt op die 85ste persentiel. Ongeveer hoeveel leerders het 'n laer punt as sy gekry? ___","en":"In a grade of 200 learners, Lerato's maths mark is at the 85th percentile. About how many learners got a lower mark than she did? ___"},"answers":{"af":["170","170 leerders"],"en":["170","170 learners"]},"explain":{"af":"Die 85ste persentiel beteken ongeveer 85% van die data lê daaronder: 0,85 × 200 = 170 leerders. Dit sê niks oor haar persentasie nie.","en":"The 85th percentile means about 85% of the data lies below it: 0.85 × 200 = 170 learners. It says nothing about her percentage."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["85","30","15"],"en":["85","30","15"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy 5 by elke waarde in 'n datastel tel, neem die omvang ook met 5 toe.","en":"If you add 5 to every value in a data set, the range also increases by 5."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die grootste én kleinste waardes styg albei met 5, so die verskil (omvang) bly dieselfde. Die gemiddelde, mediaan en kwartiele styg wel met 5.","en":"False. The largest and the smallest values both increase by 5, so the difference (range) stays the same. The mean, median and quartiles do increase by 5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bepaal die interkwartielomvang (IKO) van hierdie data: 12; 18; 3; 20; 8; 13; 22; 5; 18; 10; 8.","en":"Determine the interquartile range (IQR) of this data: 12, 18, 3, 20, 8, 13, 22, 5, 18, 10, 8."},"options":[{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"19","en":"19"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Gerangskik: 3; 5; 8; 8; 10; 12; 13; 18; 18; 20; 22 (n = 11). Mediaan = 12 (6de waarde). Onderste helfte 3; 5; 8; 8; 10 gee Q₁ = 8; boonste helfte 13; 18; 18; 20; 22 gee Q₃ = 18. IKO = 18 − 8 = 10. 19 is die omvang, 5 die semi-IKO en 12 die mediaan.","en":"Ordered: 3, 5, 8, 8, 10, 12, 13, 18, 18, 20, 22 (n = 11). Median = 12 (6th value). Lower half 3, 5, 8, 8, 10 gives Q₁ = 8; upper half 13, 18, 18, 20, 22 gives Q₃ = 18. IQR = 18 − 8 = 10. 19 is the range, 5 the semi-IQR and 12 the median."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vyfgetalopsomming van 'n klas se toetspunte is: minimum 12; Q₁ = 18; mediaan 25; Q₃ = 31; maksimum 44. Wat is die semi-interkwartielomvang? ___","en":"The five-number summary of a class's test marks is: minimum 12; Q₁ = 18; median 25; Q₃ = 31; maximum 44. What is the semi-interquartile range? ___"},"answers":{"af":["6,5","6.5","6,50","6.50","13/2"],"en":["6.5","6,5","6.50","6,50","13/2"]},"explain":{"af":"Semi-IKO = ½(Q₃ − Q₁) = ½(31 − 18) = 13 ÷ 2 = 6,5. Moenie vergeet om te halveer nie: 13 is die IKO.","en":"Semi-IQR = ½(Q₃ − Q₁) = ½(31 − 18) = 13 ÷ 2 = 6.5. Do not forget to halve: 13 is the IQR."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["13","32","16"],"en":["13","32","16"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die mobiele data (in GB) wat 40 leerders in Brits in 'n maand gebruik, is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 0 ≤ x < 2: 6; 2 ≤ x < 4: 13; 4 ≤ x < 6: 11; 6 ≤ x < 8: 7; 8 ≤ x < 10: 3. Wat is die modale klas?","en":"The mobile data (in GB) that 40 learners in Brits use in a month is grouped like this (class: frequency): 0 ≤ x < 2: 6; 2 ≤ x < 4: 13; 4 ≤ x < 6: 11; 6 ≤ x < 8: 7; 8 ≤ x < 10: 3. What is the modal class?"},"options":[{"af":"4 ≤ x < 6","en":"4 ≤ x < 6"},{"af":"2 ≤ x < 4","en":"2 ≤ x < 4"},{"af":"13","en":"13"},{"af":"8 ≤ x < 10","en":"8 ≤ x < 10"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die modale klas is die klas met die grootste frekwensie: 13, dus 2 ≤ x < 4. Die antwoord is 'n klas, nie die frekwensie 13 nie. 4 ≤ x < 6 is die klas wat die mediaan bevat, en 8 ≤ x < 10 het net die grootste waardes.","en":"The modal class is the class with the highest frequency: 13, so 2 ≤ x < 4. The answer is a class, not the frequency 13. 4 ≤ x < 6 is the class containing the median, and 8 ≤ x < 10 only has the largest values."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die gemiddelde punt van 30 leerders in 'n toets is 62%. 'n Nuwe leerder skryf die toets later en kry 93%. Wat is die nuwe gemiddelde van al 31 leerders? ___%","en":"The mean mark of 30 learners in a test is 62%. A new learner writes the test later and gets 93%. What is the new mean of all 31 learners? ___%"},"answers":{"af":["63","63%","63,0","63.0"],"en":["63","63%","63.0","63,0"]},"explain":{"af":"Som van die 30 punte = 62 × 30 = 1 860. Nuwe som = 1 860 + 93 = 1 953. Nuwe gemiddelde = 1 953 ÷ 31 = 63%. Jy kan nie net (62 + 93) ÷ 2 doen nie, want 62 verteenwoordig 30 leerders.","en":"Sum of the 30 marks = 62 × 30 = 1 860. New sum = 1 860 + 93 = 1 953. New mean = 1 953 ÷ 31 = 63%. You cannot just work out (62 + 93) ÷ 2, because 62 represents 30 learners."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["77,5","65,1","62"],"en":["77.5","65.1","62"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die massa (in g) van 50 suurlemoene van 'n sitrusplaas by Brits is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 80 ≤ m < 100: 6; 100 ≤ m < 120: 15; 120 ≤ m < 140: 18; 140 ≤ m < 160: 8; 160 ≤ m < 180: 3. Wat is die beraamde gemiddelde massa?","en":"The mass (in g) of 50 lemons from a citrus farm near Brits is grouped like this (class: frequency): 80 ≤ m < 100: 6; 100 ≤ m < 120: 15; 120 ≤ m < 140: 18; 140 ≤ m < 160: 8; 160 ≤ m < 180: 3. What is the estimated mean mass?"},"options":[{"af":"130 g","en":"130 g"},{"af":"1 248 g","en":"1 248 g"},{"af":"134,8 g","en":"134.8 g"},{"af":"124,8 g","en":"124.8 g"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Middelpunte: 90; 110; 130; 150; 170. Σ(f × x) = 6 × 90 + 15 × 110 + 18 × 130 + 8 × 150 + 3 × 170 = 6 240. Beraamde gemiddelde = 6 240 ÷ 50 = 124,8 g. 130 g is net die gemiddelde van die middelpunte, 1 248 g kom van ÷ 5 klasse en 134,8 g gebruik die bogrense in plaas van die middelpunte.","en":"Midpoints: 90, 110, 130, 150, 170. Σ(f × x) = 6 × 90 + 15 × 110 + 18 × 130 + 8 × 150 + 3 × 170 = 6 240. Estimated mean = 6 240 ÷ 50 = 124.8 g. 130 g is just the mean of the midpoints, 1 248 g comes from ÷ 5 classes and 134.8 g uses the upper limits instead of the midpoints."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die wagtyd (in minute) van 45 pendelaars by 'n taxistaanplek in Brits is so gegroepeer (klas: frekwensie): 0 ≤ t < 5: 18; 5 ≤ t < 10: 12; 10 ≤ t < 15: 8; 15 ≤ t < 20: 5; 20 ≤ t < 25: 2. In watter klas lê die mediaan?","en":"The waiting time (in minutes) of 45 commuters at a taxi rank in Brits is grouped like this (class: frequency): 0 ≤ t < 5: 18; 5 ≤ t < 10: 12; 10 ≤ t < 15: 8; 15 ≤ t < 20: 5; 20 ≤ t < 25: 2. In which class does the median lie?"},"options":[{"af":"0 ≤ t < 5","en":"0 ≤ t < 5"},{"af":"10 ≤ t < 15","en":"10 ≤ t < 15"},{"af":"5 ≤ t < 10","en":"5 ≤ t < 10"},{"af":"20 ≤ t < 25","en":"20 ≤ t < 25"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mediaan is die 23ste waarde ((45 + 1) ÷ 2 = 23). Kumulatiewe frekwensies: 18; 30; … Die 19de tot 30ste waardes lê in 5 ≤ t < 10, dus ook die 23ste. 0 ≤ t < 5 is die modale klas, 10 ≤ t < 15 is net die middelste ry van die tabel, en 20 ≤ t < 25 behandel die posisie 23 asof dit 'n wagtyd van 23 minute is.","en":"The median is the 23rd value ((45 + 1) ÷ 2 = 23). Cumulative frequencies: 18, 30, … The 19th to 30th values lie in 5 ≤ t < 10, so the 23rd does too. 0 ≤ t < 5 is the modal class, 10 ≤ t < 15 is just the middle row of the table, and 20 ≤ t < 25 treats the position 23 as if it were a waiting time of 23 minutes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die vyfgetalopsommings van twee graad 10-klasse se wiskundepunte (in %) is: Klas A: minimum 35; Q₁ = 52; mediaan 60; Q₃ = 71; maksimum 88. Klas B: minimum 41; Q₁ = 55; mediaan 63; Q₃ = 68; maksimum 79. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"The five-number summaries of two Grade 10 classes' maths marks (in %) are: Class A: minimum 35; Q₁ = 52; median 60; Q₃ = 71; maximum 88. Class B: minimum 41; Q₁ = 55; median 63; Q₃ = 68; maximum 79. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Klas B het beter en meer konsekwent presteer: sy mediaan is hoër, en sy IKO (13) en omvang (38) is kleiner as dié van Klas A.","en":"Class B performed better and more consistently: its median is higher, and its IQR (13) and range (38) are smaller than those of Class A."},{"af":"Klas A het beter presteer, want sy hoogste punt (88%) is hoër as dié van Klas B.","en":"Class A performed better, because its highest mark (88%) is higher than that of Class B."},{"af":"Ongeveer 75% van die leerders in Klas A het meer as 71% gekry.","en":"About 75% of the learners in Class A scored more than 71%."},{"af":"Die twee klasse se punte is ewe veel versprei, want hulle mediane verskil met net 3.","en":"The two classes' marks are equally spread out, because their medians differ by only 3."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klas A: IKO = 71 − 52 = 19, omvang = 88 − 35 = 53. Klas B: IKO = 68 − 55 = 13, omvang = 79 − 41 = 38, en mediaan 63 > 60. Een hoë punt sê niks oor die hele klas nie; bo Q₃ lê net ongeveer 25% van die data, nie 75% nie; en die mediaan meet die middel, nie die verspreiding nie.","en":"Class A: IQR = 71 − 52 = 19, range = 88 − 35 = 53. Class B: IQR = 68 − 55 = 13, range = 79 − 41 = 38, and median 63 > 60. One high mark says nothing about the whole class; only about 25% of the data lies above Q₃, not 75%; and the median measures the centre, not the spread."}}]},{"id":"w10-t3-trig-2d","title":{"af":"Trigonometrie: probleme in twee dimensies","en":"Trigonometry: problems in two dimensions"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoogte- en dieptehoeke korrek kan gebruik en 2D-probleme met een of twee reghoekige driehoeke in konteks kan oplos, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"You will be able to use angles of elevation and depression correctly and solve 2D problems with one or two right-angled triangles in context, rounded to two decimal places."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoogtehoek en dieptehoek\n\n- Die **hoogtehoek** is die hoek tussen die **horisontaal** en die **siglyn** as jy **op** na 'n voorwerp kyk.\n- Die **dieptehoek** is die hoek tussen die **horisontaal** en die siglyn as jy **af** na 'n voorwerp kyk.\n- Albei word **altyd vanaf die horisontaal** gemeet, nooit vanaf die vertikaal ('n muur of toring) nie.\n\nDie horisontale lyne by die waarnemer en by die voorwerp is ewewydig. Daarom is die **hoogtehoek van A na B gelyk aan die dieptehoek van B na A** (verwisselende hoeke).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die dieptehoek word binne-in die driehoek teen die muur geplaas. Die hoek tussen die siglyn en die vertikale muur is 90° − dieptehoek. Skuif eerder die dieptehoek met verwisselende hoeke na onder, waar dit 'n hoogtehoek binne die driehoek word.\n\n## Metode vir enige 2D-probleem\n\n1. **Skets** 'n netjiese diagram. Merk regte hoeke, horisontale lyne, gegewe lengtes en hoeke, en die onbekende (h, x, d of θ).\n2. Soek 'n **reghoekige driehoek** wat die onbekende bevat en genoeg gegewe inligting het.\n3. Benoem die sye relatief tot die bekende hoek: teenoorstaande, aangrensende en skuinssy.\n4. Kies die verhouding (sin, cos of tan) wat die bekende en die onbekende sy verbind.\n5. Los op. Hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar en rond **eers aan die einde** af tot twee desimale plekke. Skryf die eenheid by.\n6. Kontroleer: die skuinssy is die langste sy, en 'n groter hoek lê oorkant 'n groter sy.\n\nOm 'n **hoek** te bereken, kies jy die verhouding met die twee bekende sye en gebruik sin^{−1}, cos^{−1} of tan^{−1}.\n\n## Algemene situasies\n\n| Situasie | Skuinssy | Hoek en sye |\n|---|---|---|\n| Leer teen 'n muur | die leer | hoek met die grond; hoogte teen die muur = teenoorstaande |\n| Skaduwee | die sonstraal | hoogtehoek van die son; skaduwee = aangrensende |\n| Vlieër | die tou | hoek tussen tou en horisontaal; hoogte = teenoorstaande |\n| Kabelkar | die kabel | hellingshoek; styging = teenoorstaande |\n| Oprit of pad | die skuins oppervlak | hellingshoek; horisontale afstand = aangrensende |\n\n- As 'n hoogtehoek vanaf iemand se **oë** (of hand) gemeet word, tel die **ooghoogte** (of handhoogte) by die berekende hoogte.\n- Maak seker al die lengtes het **dieselfde eenheid** (m of km) voordat jy bereken.\n\n## Probleme met twee driehoeke\n\nBaie eksamenvrae het twee reghoekige driehoeke met 'n **gemeenskaplike sy**. Bereken eers die gemeenskaplike sy in die driehoek waar jy genoeg inligting het, en gebruik dit dan in die tweede driehoek.\n\n**Tipe 1: Van een gebou na 'n ander.** Vanaf die dak van 'n gebou kyk jy op na die bopunt van 'n toring (hoogtehoek α) en af na die voet daarvan (dieptehoek β). 'n Horisontale lyn vanaf die dak verdeel die figuur in twee driehoeke met die afstand d tussen die geboue as gemeenskaplike sy.\n\n- Onderste driehoek: d = [[hoogte van gebou/tan β]]\n- Boonste driehoek: hoogte bo die dak = d × tan α\n- Toring = hoogte van gebou + d × tan α\n\n**Tipe 2: Twee waarnemers aan dieselfde kant, hoogte bekend.** Bereken elke horisontale afstand apart, bv. [[h/tan 25°]] en [[h/tan 40°]], en trek af. Moenie die hoeke van mekaar aftrek nie.\n\n**Tipe 3: Twee waarnemers, hoogte onbekend.** Laat die onbekende afstand x wees en skryf h op twee maniere, bv. h = x tan 50° en h = (x + 20) tan 30°. Stel gelyk, los op vir x en bereken dan h = x tan 50°.\n\n**Tipe 4: Een waarnemer, twee hoogtes.** Kyk jy vanaf dieselfde punt na die onderkant en die bokant van iets (bv. 'n vlagpaal op 'n toring), is die horisontale afstand die gemeenskaplike sy. Bereken albei hoogtes en trek af.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skryf by elke stap watter driehoek jy gebruik, bv. \"In △ABC:\". So kan die nasiener jou werk volg, en jy kry steeds metodepunte al is 'n getal later verkeerd.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om tussenantwoorde af te rond en dan verder te werk. Dit kan die laaste desimaal van jou finale antwoord verander. Stoor tussenantwoorde in die sakrekenaar se geheue.","en":"## Angle of elevation and angle of depression\n\n- The **angle of elevation** is the angle between the **horizontal** and the **line of sight** when you look **up** at an object.\n- The **angle of depression** is the angle between the **horizontal** and the line of sight when you look **down** at an object.\n- Both are **always measured from the horizontal**, never from the vertical (a wall or tower).\n\nThe horizontal lines at the observer and at the object are parallel. That is why the **angle of elevation from A to B equals the angle of depression from B to A** (alternate angles).\n\n> **Common mistake:** The angle of depression is placed inside the triangle against the wall. The angle between the line of sight and the vertical wall is 90° − angle of depression. Rather move the angle of depression down with alternate angles, where it becomes an angle of elevation inside the triangle.\n\n## Method for any 2D problem\n\n1. **Sketch** a neat diagram. Mark right angles, horizontal lines, given lengths and angles, and the unknown (h, x, d or θ).\n2. Find a **right-angled triangle** that contains the unknown and has enough given information.\n3. Label the sides relative to the known angle: opposite, adjacent and hypotenuse.\n4. Choose the ratio (sin, cos or tan) that links the known and the unknown side.\n5. Solve. Keep the full value in the calculator and round to two decimal places **only at the end**. Write the unit.\n6. Check: the hypotenuse is the longest side, and a bigger angle lies opposite a bigger side.\n\nTo calculate an **angle**, choose the ratio with the two known sides and use sin^{−1}, cos^{−1} or tan^{−1}.\n\n## Common situations\n\n| Situation | Hypotenuse | Angle and sides |\n|---|---|---|\n| Ladder against a wall | the ladder | angle with the ground; height up the wall = opposite |\n| Shadow | the sun ray | angle of elevation of the sun; shadow = adjacent |\n| Kite | the string | angle between string and horizontal; height = opposite |\n| Cable car | the cable | angle of inclination; rise = opposite |\n| Ramp or road | the sloping surface | angle of inclination; horizontal distance = adjacent |\n\n- If an angle of elevation is measured from someone's **eyes** (or hand), add the **eye height** (or hand height) to the calculated height.\n- Make sure all lengths are in the **same unit** (m or km) before you calculate.\n\n## Problems with two triangles\n\nMany exam questions have two right-angled triangles with a **common side**. First calculate the common side in the triangle where you have enough information, then use it in the second triangle.\n\n**Type 1: From one building to another.** From the roof of a building you look up to the top of a tower (angle of elevation α) and down to its foot (angle of depression β). A horizontal line from the roof splits the figure into two triangles with the distance d between the buildings as the common side.\n\n- Lower triangle: d = [[height of building/tan β]]\n- Upper triangle: height above the roof = d × tan α\n- Tower = height of building + d × tan α\n\n**Type 2: Two observers on the same side, height known.** Calculate each horizontal distance separately, e.g. [[h/tan 25°]] and [[h/tan 40°]], and subtract. Do not subtract the angles from each other.\n\n**Type 3: Two observers, height unknown.** Let the unknown distance be x and write h in two ways, e.g. h = x tan 50° and h = (x + 20) tan 30°. Set them equal, solve for x and then calculate h = x tan 50°.\n\n**Type 4: One observer, two heights.** If you look from the same point at the bottom and the top of something (e.g. a flagpole on a tower), the horizontal distance is the common side. Calculate both heights and subtract.\n\n> **Tip:** At every step, write which triangle you are using, e.g. \"In △ABC:\". That way the marker can follow your work, and you still earn method marks even if a number goes wrong later.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Rounding intermediate answers and then working on. It can change the last decimal of your final answer. Store intermediate answers in the calculator's memory."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoogtehoek","en":"Angle of elevation"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as 'n waarnemer óp na 'n voorwerp kyk.","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when an observer looks up at an object."}},{"term":{"af":"Dieptehoek","en":"Angle of depression"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as 'n waarnemer áf na 'n voorwerp kyk.","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when an observer looks down at an object."}},{"term":{"af":"Siglyn","en":"Line of sight"},"def":{"af":"Die reguit lyn van die waarnemer se oog na die voorwerp.","en":"The straight line from the observer's eye to the object."}},{"term":{"af":"Horisontaal","en":"Horizontal"},"def":{"af":"'n Plat lyn ewewydig aan gelyk grond of die wateroppervlak; hoogte- en dieptehoeke word daarvandaan gemeet.","en":"A flat line parallel to level ground or the water surface; angles of elevation and depression are measured from it."}},{"term":{"af":"Hellingshoek","en":"Angle of inclination"},"def":{"af":"Die hoek tussen 'n skuins oppervlak (pad, oprit, kabel) en die horisontaal.","en":"The angle between a sloping surface (road, ramp, cable) and the horizontal."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy","en":"Common side"},"def":{"af":"'n Sy wat twee driehoeke deel; bereken dit in die een driehoek en gebruik dit in die ander.","en":"A side shared by two triangles; calculate it in one triangle and use it in the other."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke","en":"Alternate angles"},"def":{"af":"Gelyke hoeke tussen ewewydige lyne; daarom is die dieptehoek van B na A gelyk aan die hoogtehoek van A na B.","en":"Equal angles between parallel lines; that is why the angle of depression from B to A equals the angle of elevation from A to B."}},{"term":{"af":"Ooghoogte","en":"Eye height"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogte van die waarnemer se oë bo die grond; tel dit by die berekende hoogte as die hoek vanaf die oë gemeet is.","en":"The height of the observer's eyes above the ground; add it to the calculated height if the angle was measured from the eyes."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Hoogtehoek met ooghoogte","en":"Angle of elevation with eye height"},"problem":{"af":"Mpho staan op gelyk grond 40 m van die voet van 'n selfoontoring in Brits. Die hoogtehoek vanaf sy oë na die bopunt van die toring is 38°. Sy oë is 1,6 m bo die grond. Bereken die hoogte van die toring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"Mpho stands on level ground 40 m from the foot of a cellphone tower in Brits. The angle of elevation from his eyes to the top of the tower is 38°. His eyes are 1.6 m above the ground. Calculate the height of the tower, rounded to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Skets: trek 'n horisontale lyn van 40 m vanaf Mpho se oë tot by die toring. Die vertikale sy h van die driehoek is die deel van die toring bó sy oë.","en":"Sketch: draw a horizontal line of 40 m from Mpho's eyes to the tower. The vertical side h of the triangle is the part of the tower above his eyes."},{"af":"Relatief tot 38° is h teenoorstaande en 40 m aangrensende, dus tan 38° = [[h/40]]","en":"Relative to 38°, h is opposite and 40 m is adjacent, so tan 38° = [[h/40]]"},{"af":"h = 40 tan 38° = 31,25 m (hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar)","en":"h = 40 tan 38° = 31.25 m (keep the full value in the calculator)"},{"af":"Tel die ooghoogte by: hoogte van toring = 31,25… + 1,6 = 32,85 m","en":"Add the eye height: height of tower = 31.25… + 1.6 = 32.85 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die toring is 32,85 m hoog.","en":"The tower is 32.85 m high."}},{"title":{"af":"Dieptehoek vanaf 'n krans","en":"Angle of depression from a cliff"},"problem":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n 65 m hoë krans langs die Hartbeespoortdam is die dieptehoek na 'n boot op die water 23°. Hoe ver is die boot van die voet van die krans? Rond af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"From the top of a 65 m high cliff next to the Hartbeespoort Dam, the angle of depression to a boat on the water is 23°. How far is the boat from the foot of the cliff? Round to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Die dieptehoek lê by die bopunt, tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn na die boot. Die horisontaal is ewewydig aan die wateroppervlak.","en":"The angle of depression is at the top, between the horizontal and the line of sight to the boat. The horizontal is parallel to the water surface."},{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke: die hoogtehoek vanaf die boot na die bopunt is ook 23°. Dit is die hoek binne die driehoek by die boot.","en":"Alternate angles: the angle of elevation from the boat to the top is also 23°. This is the angle inside the triangle at the boat."},{"af":"Relatief tot 23° by die boot is 65 m teenoorstaande en die afstand d aangrensende: tan 23° = [[65/d]]","en":"Relative to 23° at the boat, 65 m is opposite and the distance d is adjacent: tan 23° = [[65/d]]"},{"af":"d staan onder die breukstreep, dus ruil om: d = [[65/tan 23°]] = 153,13 m","en":"d is in the denominator, so swap it over: d = [[65/tan 23°]] = 153.13 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die boot is 153,13 m van die voet van die krans.","en":"The boat is 153.13 m from the foot of the cliff."}},{"title":{"af":"Twee driehoeke: van een gebou na 'n ander","en":"Two triangles: from one building to another"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato staan op die plat dak van 'n 20 m hoë woonstelblok in Pretoria. Die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van 'n kantoortoring oorkant die straat is 25° en die dieptehoek na die voet van die toring is 35°. Bereken die hoogte van die kantoortoring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke (ignoreer Lerato se lengte).","en":"Lerato stands on the flat roof of a 20 m high block of flats in Pretoria. The angle of elevation to the top of an office tower across the street is 25° and the angle of depression to the foot of the tower is 35°. Calculate the height of the office tower, rounded to two decimal places (ignore Lerato's height)."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 'n horisontale lyn vanaf die dak tot by die toring. Dit verdeel die figuur in twee reghoekige driehoeke met die horisontale afstand d as gemeenskaplike sy.","en":"Draw a horizontal line from the roof to the tower. It splits the figure into two right-angled triangles with the horizontal distance d as the common side."},{"af":"Onderste driehoek (dieptehoek 35°; die teenoorstaande sy is 20 m): tan 35° = [[20/d]], dus d = [[20/tan 35°]] = 28,56 m","en":"Lower triangle (angle of depression 35°; the opposite side is 20 m): tan 35° = [[20/d]], so d = [[20/tan 35°]] = 28.56 m"},{"af":"Boonste driehoek (hoogtehoek 25°): tan 25° = [[x/d]], dus x = d × tan 25° = 13,32 m (gebruik die volle waarde van d)","en":"Upper triangle (angle of elevation 25°): tan 25° = [[x/d]], so x = d × tan 25° = 13.32 m (use the full value of d)"},{"af":"Hoogte van toring = 20 + x = 20 + 13,32 = 33,32 m","en":"Height of tower = 20 + x = 20 + 13.32 = 33.32 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Die kantoortoring is 33,32 m hoog.","en":"The office tower is 33.32 m high."}},{"title":{"af":"Twee waarnemers, hoogte onbekend","en":"Two observers, height unknown"},"problem":{"af":"P en Q lê op gelyk grond in 'n reguit lyn met die voet T van 'n watertoring op 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits. PQ = 20 m en Q is nader aan die toring. Die hoogtehoek na die bopunt B van die toring is 30° vanaf P en 50° vanaf Q. Bereken die hoogte BT, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"P and Q lie on level ground in a straight line with the foot T of a water tower on a citrus farm near Brits. PQ = 20 m and Q is closer to the tower. The angle of elevation to the top B of the tower is 30° from P and 50° from Q. Calculate the height BT, rounded to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"Laat QT = x en BT = h. Dan is PT = x + 20.","en":"Let QT = x and BT = h. Then PT = x + 20."},{"af":"In △BQT: tan 50° = [[h/x]], dus h = x tan 50°","en":"In △BQT: tan 50° = [[h/x]], so h = x tan 50°"},{"af":"In △BPT: tan 30° = [[h/x + 20]], dus h = (x + 20) tan 30°","en":"In △BPT: tan 30° = [[h/x + 20]], so h = (x + 20) tan 30°"},{"af":"Stel gelyk: x tan 50° = x tan 30° + 20 tan 30°, dus x(tan 50° − tan 30°) = 20 tan 30°","en":"Set equal: x tan 50° = x tan 30° + 20 tan 30°, so x(tan 50° − tan 30°) = 20 tan 30°"},{"af":"x = [[20 tan 30°/tan 50° − tan 30°]] = 18,79 m","en":"x = [[20 tan 30°/tan 50° − tan 30°]] = 18.79 m"},{"af":"h = x tan 50° = 18,794… × tan 50° = 22,40 m (gebruik die volle waarde van x)","en":"h = x tan 50° = 18.794… × tan 50° = 22.40 m (use the full value of x)"}],"answer":{"af":"BT = 22,40 m","en":"BT = 22.40 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n hoogtehoek?","en":"What is an angle of elevation?"},"options":[{"af":"Die hoek tussen die vertikaal en die siglyn as jy opkyk","en":"The angle between the vertical and the line of sight when you look up"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as jy afkyk","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when you look down"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die horisontaal en die siglyn as jy opkyk","en":"The angle between the horizontal and the line of sight when you look up"},{"af":"Die hoek tussen die siglyn en die skaduwee van die voorwerp","en":"The angle between the line of sight and the shadow of the object"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Hoogtehoek word altyd vanaf die horisontaal gemeet, met die siglyn bó die horisontaal (jy kyk op). As jy afkyk, is dit 'n dieptehoek. Die vertikaal word nooit as verwysing gebruik nie.","en":"An angle of elevation is always measured from the horizontal, with the line of sight above the horizontal (you look up). When you look down, it is an angle of depression. The vertical is never used as the reference."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die hoogtehoek vanaf 'n boot na die bopunt van 'n krans is gelyk aan die dieptehoek vanaf die bopunt van die krans na die boot.","en":"The angle of elevation from a boat to the top of a cliff equals the angle of depression from the top of the cliff to the boat."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die horisontale lyne by die boot en by die bopunt is ewewydig, dus is die twee hoeke verwisselende hoeke en ewe groot.","en":"True. The horizontal lines at the boat and at the top are parallel, so the two angles are alternate angles and equal."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Hoogtehoek","en":"Angle of elevation"},"r":{"af":"Bo die horisontaal gemeet; jy kyk op","en":"Measured above the horizontal; you look up"}},{"l":{"af":"Dieptehoek","en":"Angle of depression"},"r":{"af":"Onder die horisontaal gemeet; jy kyk af","en":"Measured below the horizontal; you look down"}},{"l":{"af":"Siglyn","en":"Line of sight"},"r":{"af":"Die reguit lyn van die oog na die voorwerp","en":"The straight line from the eye to the object"}},{"l":{"af":"Hellingshoek","en":"Angle of inclination"},"r":{"af":"Die hoek tussen 'n skuins pad of oprit en die horisontaal","en":"The angle between a sloping road or ramp and the horizontal"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hoogte- en dieptehoeke word albei vanaf die horisontaal gemeet: bo (opkyk) of onder (afkyk). Die siglyn is die lyn waarlangs jy kyk, en 'n hellingshoek beskryf hoe steil 'n oppervlak is.","en":"Angles of elevation and depression are both measured from the horizontal: above (look up) or below (look down). The line of sight is the line along which you look, and an angle of inclination describes how steep a surface is."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n gebou is die dieptehoek na 'n motor 40°. Watter hoek maak die siglyn met die vertikale muur van die gebou?","en":"From the top of a building the angle of depression to a car is 40°. What angle does the line of sight make with the vertical wall of the building?"},"options":[{"af":"40°","en":"40°"},{"af":"50°","en":"50°"},{"af":"140°","en":"140°"},{"af":"90°","en":"90°"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die horisontaal en die vertikale muur maak 90° met mekaar. Die siglyn lê 40° onder die horisontaal, dus maak dit 90° − 40° = 50° met die muur. Moenie die 40° teen die muur plaas nie.","en":"The horizontal and the vertical wall make 90° with each other. The line of sight lies 40° below the horizontal, so it makes 90° − 40° = 50° with the wall. Do not place the 40° against the wall."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Leer van 5 m leun teen 'n vertikale muur en maak 'n hoek van 70° met die horisontale grond. Hoe hoog teen die muur reik die leer? Rond af tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"A 5 m ladder leans against a vertical wall and makes an angle of 70° with the horizontal ground. How high up the wall does the ladder reach? Round to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["4,7","4.7","4,70","4.70","4,7 m","4.7 m","4,70 m","4.70 m"],"en":["4,7","4.7","4,70","4.70","4,7 m","4.7 m","4,70 m","4.70 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die leer is die skuinssy en die hoogte lê oorkant die 70°-hoek: sin 70° = h/5, dus h = 5 sin 70° = 4,70 m.","en":"The ladder is the hypotenuse and the height lies opposite the 70° angle: sin 70° = h/5, so h = 5 sin 70° = 4.70 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1,71","13,74","5,32"],"en":["1.71","13.74","5.32"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die son se hoogtehoek is 35°. Hoe lank is die skaduwee van 'n 6 m hoë lamppaal op gelyk grond?","en":"The angle of elevation of the sun is 35°. How long is the shadow of a 6 m high lamp post on level ground?"},"options":[{"af":"4,20 m","en":"4.20 m"},{"af":"10,46 m","en":"10.46 m"},{"af":"8,57 m","en":"8.57 m"},{"af":"4,91 m","en":"4.91 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Relatief tot 35° is die paal (6 m) teenoorstaande en die skaduwee s aangrensende: tan 35° = 6/s, dus s = 6 ÷ tan 35° = 8,57 m. 4,20 m is 6 × tan 35° (omgekeer), 10,46 m is die sonstraal (6 ÷ sin 35°) en 4,91 m gebruik cos.","en":"Relative to 35°, the post (6 m) is opposite and the shadow s is adjacent: tan 35° = 6/s, so s = 6 ÷ tan 35° = 8.57 m. 4.20 m is 6 × tan 35° (upside down), 10.46 m is the sun ray (6 ÷ sin 35°) and 4.91 m uses cos."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Oprit by 'n skool in Madibeng styg 0,8 m oor 'n horisontale afstand van 9,6 m. Bereken die hellingshoek van die oprit, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___°","en":"A ramp at a school in Madibeng rises 0.8 m over a horizontal distance of 9.6 m. Calculate the angle of inclination of the ramp, rounded to two decimal places. ___°"},"answers":{"af":["4,76","4.76","4,76°","4.76°","θ = 4,76","θ = 4.76","θ = 4,76°","θ = 4.76°","θ=4,76","θ=4.76","θ=4,76°","θ=4.76°"],"en":["4,76","4.76","4,76°","4.76°","θ = 4,76","θ = 4.76","θ = 4,76°","θ = 4.76°","θ=4,76","θ=4.76","θ=4,76°","θ=4.76°"]},"explain":{"af":"Die styging (0,8 m) is teenoorstaande en die horisontale afstand (9,6 m) aangrensende: tan θ = 0,8 ÷ 9,6, dus θ = tan⁻¹(0,8 ÷ 9,6) = 4,76°.","en":"The rise (0.8 m) is opposite and the horizontal distance (9.6 m) is adjacent: tan θ = 0.8 ÷ 9.6, so θ = tan⁻¹(0.8 ÷ 9.6) = 4.76°."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4,78","85,24","85,22"],"en":["4.78","85.24","85.22"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vanaf 'n venster 12 m bo die grond is die dieptehoek na 'n taxi op die straat 28°. Hoe ver is die taxi horisontaal van die gebou?","en":"From a window 12 m above the ground the angle of depression to a taxi in the street is 28°. How far is the taxi horizontally from the building?"},"options":[{"af":"6,38 m","en":"6.38 m"},{"af":"25,56 m","en":"25.56 m"},{"af":"13,59 m","en":"13.59 m"},{"af":"22,57 m","en":"22.57 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Verwisselende hoeke: die hoogtehoek vanaf die taxi na die venster is 28°. tan 28° = 12/d, dus d = 12 ÷ tan 28° = 22,57 m. 6,38 m is 12 × tan 28°, 25,56 m is die lengte van die siglyn (12 ÷ sin 28°) en 13,59 m gebruik cos.","en":"Alternate angles: the angle of elevation from the taxi to the window is 28°. tan 28° = 12/d, so d = 12 ÷ tan 28° = 22.57 m. 6.38 m is 12 × tan 28°, 25.56 m is the length of the line of sight (12 ÷ sin 28°) and 13.59 m uses cos."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vir 'n akkurate antwoord moet jy elke tussenantwoord tot twee desimale plekke afrond voordat jy verder bereken.","en":"For an accurate answer you must round every intermediate answer to two decimal places before you calculate further."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Hou die volle waarde in die sakrekenaar (of sy geheue) en rond net die finale antwoord af. Vroeë afronding kan die laaste desimaal van die antwoord verander.","en":"False. Keep the full value in the calculator (or its memory) and round only the final answer. Rounding early can change the last decimal of the answer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho vlieg 'n vlieër op 'n rugbyveld in Brits. Die tou is 50 m lank, styf getrek, en maak 'n hoek van 52° met die horisontaal. Hy hou die tou 1,2 m bo die grond vas. Hoe hoog is die vlieër bo die grond?","en":"Sipho flies a kite on a rugby field in Brits. The string is 50 m long, pulled tight, and makes an angle of 52° with the horizontal. He holds the string 1.2 m above the ground. How high is the kite above the ground?"},"options":[{"af":"40,60 m","en":"40.60 m"},{"af":"39,40 m","en":"39.40 m"},{"af":"31,98 m","en":"31.98 m"},{"af":"65,20 m","en":"65.20 m"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die tou is die skuinssy: hoogte bo sy hand = 50 sin 52° = 39,40 m. Tel die 1,2 m by: 39,40 + 1,2 = 40,60 m. 39,40 m vergeet die hand se hoogte, 31,98 m gebruik cos en 65,20 m gebruik tan.","en":"The string is the hypotenuse: height above his hand = 50 sin 52° = 39.40 m. Add the 1.2 m: 39.40 + 1.2 = 40.60 m. 39.40 m forgets the height of the hand, 31.98 m uses cos and 65.20 m uses tan."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vanaf die bopunt van 'n 15 m hoë gebou is die dieptehoek na die voet van 'n toring oorkant die straat 40° en die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van die toring 30°. Bereken die hoogte van die toring, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"From the top of a 15 m high building the angle of depression to the foot of a tower across the street is 40° and the angle of elevation to the top of the tower is 30°. Calculate the height of the tower, rounded to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["25,32","25.32","25,32 m","25.32 m"],"en":["25,32","25.32","25,32 m","25.32 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Onderste driehoek: d = 15 ÷ tan 40° = 17,88 m. Boonste driehoek: x = d × tan 30° = 10,32 m. Toring = 15 + 10,32 = 25,32 m.","en":"Lower triangle: d = 15 ÷ tan 40° = 17.88 m. Upper triangle: x = d × tan 30° = 10.32 m. Tower = 15 + 10.32 = 25.32 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10,32","22,27","36,80"],"en":["10.32","22.27","36.80"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die skagtoring van 'n myn naby Brits is 60 m hoog. Vanaf punt A op gelyk grond is die hoogtehoek na die bopunt 25°. Thabo stap reguit na die skagtoring tot by B, waar die hoogtehoek 40° is. Hoe ver het hy gestap?","en":"The headgear (shaft tower) of a mine near Brits is 60 m high. From point A on level ground the angle of elevation to the top is 25°. Thabo walks straight towards the headgear to B, where the angle of elevation is 40°. How far did he walk?"},"options":[{"af":"22,37 m","en":"22.37 m"},{"af":"57,17 m","en":"57.17 m"},{"af":"48,63 m","en":"48.63 m"},{"af":"223,92 m","en":"223.92 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy: die hoogte van 60 m. Afstand vanaf A = 60 ÷ tan 25° = 128,670… m en vanaf B = 60 ÷ tan 40° = 71,505… m. AB = 128,670… − 71,505… = 57,17 m (met die afgeronde waardes 128,67 − 71,51 kry jy 57,16 m, wat verkeerd is). 22,37 m gebruik 60 × tan (omgekeer), 48,63 m gebruik sin, en 223,92 m trek die hoeke af (40° − 25° = 15°), wat nie mag nie.","en":"Common side: the height of 60 m. Distance from A = 60 ÷ tan 25° = 128.670… m and from B = 60 ÷ tan 40° = 71.505… m. AB = 128.670… − 71.505… = 57.17 m (with the rounded values 128.67 − 71.51 you get 57.16 m, which is wrong). 22.37 m uses 60 × tan (upside down), 48.63 m uses sin, and 223.92 m subtracts the angles (40° − 25° = 15°), which is not allowed."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Punt A is 50 m van die voet T van 'n toring op gelyk grond. Die hoogtehoek vanaf A na die bopunt van die toring is 32°. Bo-op die toring staan 'n vlagpaal, en die hoogtehoek vanaf A na die bopunt van die vlagpaal is 36°. Bereken die lengte van die vlagpaal, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke. ___ m","en":"Point A is 50 m from the foot T of a tower on level ground. The angle of elevation from A to the top of the tower is 32°. A flagpole stands on top of the tower, and the angle of elevation from A to the top of the flagpole is 36°. Calculate the length of the flagpole, rounded to two decimal places. ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["5,08","5.08","5,08 m","5.08 m"],"en":["5,08","5.08","5,08 m","5.08 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike sy AT = 50 m. Toring + vlagpaal = 50 tan 36° = 36,327… m en toring = 50 tan 32° = 31,243… m. Vlagpaal = 50(tan 36° − tan 32°) = 5,08 m. As jy eers afrond, kry jy 36,33 − 31,24 = 5,09 m, wat verkeerd is. 50 tan 4° = 3,50 m is ook verkeerd: hoeke mag nie afgetrek word nie.","en":"Common side AT = 50 m. Tower + flagpole = 50 tan 36° = 36.327… m and tower = 50 tan 32° = 31.243… m. Flagpole = 50(tan 36° − tan 32°) = 5.08 m. If you round first, you get 36.33 − 31.24 = 5.09 m, which is wrong. 50 tan 4° = 3.50 m is also wrong: angles may not be subtracted."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5,09","3,50","36,33"],"en":["5.09","3.50","36.33"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Uitkyktoring staan op gelyk grond langs die Hartbeespoortdam. Vanaf punt P is die hoogtehoek na die bopunt van die toring 35°. Jy stap 30 m reguit na die toring tot by Q, waar die hoogtehoek 55° is. Wat is die hoogte van die toring?","en":"A lookout tower stands on level ground next to the Hartbeespoort Dam. From point P the angle of elevation to the top of the tower is 35°. You walk 30 m straight towards the tower to Q, where the angle of elevation is 55°. What is the height of the tower?"},"options":[{"af":"42,84 m","en":"42.84 m"},{"af":"21,01 m","en":"21.01 m"},{"af":"10,92 m","en":"10.92 m"},{"af":"41,21 m","en":"41.21 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Laat QT = x. Dan is h = x tan 55° en h = (x + 30) tan 35°. Stel gelyk: x(tan 55° − tan 35°) = 30 tan 35°, dus x = 28,857… m en h = x tan 55° = 41,21 m (gebruik die volle waarde van x). 42,84 m en 21,01 m behandel 30 m asof dit die afstand tot by die toring is, en 10,92 m trek die hoeke af.","en":"Let QT = x. Then h = x tan 55° and h = (x + 30) tan 35°. Set equal: x(tan 55° − tan 35°) = 30 tan 35°, so x = 28.857… m and h = x tan 55° = 41.21 m (use the full value of x). 42.84 m and 21.01 m treat 30 m as if it were the distance to the tower, and 10.92 m subtracts the angles."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Meting en waarskynlikheid","en":"Measurement and probability"},"topics":[{"id":"w10-t4-meting","title":{"af":"Meting: oppervlakte en volume","en":"Measurement: surface area and volume"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die buiteoppervlakte en volume van prismas, silinders, piramides, keëls, sfere en saamgestelde voorwerpe kan bereken, en weet wat gebeur as afmetings met k vermenigvuldig word.","en":"You will be able to calculate the surface area and volume of prisms, cylinders, pyramids, cones, spheres and combined objects, and know what happens when dimensions are multiplied by k."},"summary":{"af":"## Eenhede en omskakelings\n\n- **Lengte:** 1 cm = 10 mm; 1 m = 100 cm\n- **Oppervlakte** (kwadreer die faktor): 1 cm^{2} = 100 mm^{2}; 1 m^{2} = 10 000 cm^{2}\n- **Volume** (kubeer die faktor): 1 cm^{3} = 1 000 mm^{3}; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 000 cm^{3}\n- **Kapasiteit:** 1 cm^{3} = 1 mℓ; **1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ**; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 ℓ = 1 kℓ\n\n> **Onthou!** Maak al die afmetings eers dieselfde eenheid voordat jy in 'n formule vervang. Buiteoppervlakte is in vierkante eenhede (cm^{2}, m^{2}) en volume in kubieke eenhede (cm^{3}, m^{3}).\n\n## Regte prismas en silinders\n\n'n **Regte prisma** het twee kongruente, ewewydige basisse, en sy syvlakke is reghoeke wat loodreg op die basisse staan. 'n **Silinder** werk dieselfde, maar sy basis is 'n sirkel.\n\n- Volume = oppervlakte van die basis × loodregte hoogte (H)\n- Buiteoppervlakte = 2 × oppervlakte van die basis + omtrek van die basis × H\n\n| Voorwerp | Buiteoppervlakte | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reghoekige prisma (l, b, h) | 2(lb + lh + bh) | l × b × h |\n| Kubus (sy s) | 6s^{2} | s^{3} |\n| Driehoekige prisma | 2 × ([[1/2]] × b × h) + (som van die driehoek se sye) × H | [[1/2]] × b × h × H |\n| Silinder (radius r) | 2πr^{2} + 2πrH | πr^{2}H |\n\nBy die driehoekige prisma is b en h die basis en hoogte van die driehoek, en H is die lengte van die prisma.\n\n**Hoekom 2πrH?** As jy die kromme oppervlak van 'n silinder oopsny en platlê, kry jy 'n reghoek. Sy lengte is die omtrek van die sirkel (2πr) en sy breedte is H.\n\n## Piramides, keëls en sfere\n\nDie volume van 'n piramide of keël is presies [[1/3]] van die prisma of silinder met dieselfde basis en loodregte hoogte:\n\n- Volume = [[1/3]] × oppervlakte van die basis × H\n\nVir die buiteoppervlakte gebruik jy die **skuinshoogte** h_{s}: die hoogte van 'n skuins driehoekige vlak van 'n piramide, of die afstand van die punt van 'n keël tot by die rand van sy basis.\n\n| Voorwerp | Buiteoppervlakte | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vierkantige piramide (sy b) | b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} | [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H |\n| Keël (radius r) | πr^{2} + πrh_{s} | [[1/3]]πr^{2}H |\n| Sfeer (radius r) | 4πr^{2} | [[4/3]]πr^{3} |\n| Halfsfeer (radius r) | 2πr^{2} (kromme deel) + πr^{2} (plat deel) | [[2/3]]πr^{3} |\n\n**Skuinshoogte met Pythagoras:**\n\n- Keël: h_{s}^{2} = r^{2} + H^{2}\n- Vierkantige piramide: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2}\n\n> **Algemene fout:** H (loodregte hoogte) en h_{s} (skuinshoogte) word verwar. Volume gebruik altyd H; die skuins vlakke van piramides en keëls gebruik h_{s}.\n\n## Saamgestelde voorwerpe\n\n- **Volume:** tel die volumes van die dele bymekaar (of trek af as 'n deel uitgehol is).\n- **Buiteoppervlakte:** tel net die vlakke wat aan die buitekant sigbaar is. Waar twee dele aan mekaar vas is, val daardie vlakke weg. Vir 'n graansilo (silinder met 'n halfsfeer bo-op) is dit die kromme oppervlak van die silinder + 2πr^{2} van die halfsfeer, plus die vloer πr^{2} net as die vraag dit vra.\n\n## Vermenigvuldig afmetings met 'n faktor k\n\n| Verandering | Volume | Buiteoppervlakte |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Een** afmeting × k (bv. net die hoogte) | × k | verander, maar nie met 'n vaste faktor nie – bereken weer |\n| **Alle** afmetings × k | × k^{3} | × k^{2} |\n\nKyk na die formule om te sien wat gebeur. In V = πr^{2}H staan r **gekwadreer**: as net r verdubbel, word V met 2^{2} = 4 vermenigvuldig. As net H verdubbel, verdubbel V.\n\n**Voorbeeld:** 'n Bal se radius word verdriedubbel. Die nuwe volume is 3^{3} = 27 keer die oorspronklike volume, en die nuwe buiteoppervlakte is 3^{2} = 9 keer die oorspronklike buiteoppervlakte.\n\n## Stappe vir enige vraag\n\n1. Skryf die formule neer.\n2. Maak die eenhede dieselfde en vervang. Gebruik die **radius**, nie die middellyn nie.\n3. Hou π in die sakrekenaar en rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n4. Skryf die eenheid by (cm^{2} of cm^{3}) en skakel om na ℓ as die vraag dit vra.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** die [[1/3]] by piramides en keëls vergeet; die middellyn as radius gebruik; vergeet om cm^{3} na ℓ om te skakel (÷ 1 000); dink dat die volume net verdubbel as alle afmetings verdubbel (dit word 2^{3} = 8 keer groter).","en":"## Units and conversions\n\n- **Length:** 1 cm = 10 mm; 1 m = 100 cm\n- **Area** (square the factor): 1 cm^{2} = 100 mm^{2}; 1 m^{2} = 10 000 cm^{2}\n- **Volume** (cube the factor): 1 cm^{3} = 1 000 mm^{3}; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 000 cm^{3}\n- **Capacity:** 1 cm^{3} = 1 mℓ; **1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ**; 1 m^{3} = 1 000 ℓ = 1 kℓ\n\n> **Remember!** Make all the dimensions the same unit before you substitute into a formula. Surface area is in square units (cm^{2}, m^{2}) and volume in cubic units (cm^{3}, m^{3}).\n\n## Right prisms and cylinders\n\nA **right prism** has two congruent, parallel bases, and its side faces are rectangles perpendicular to the bases. A **cylinder** works the same way, but its base is a circle.\n\n- Volume = area of the base × perpendicular height (H)\n- Surface area = 2 × area of the base + perimeter of the base × H\n\n| Object | Surface area | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rectangular prism (l, b, h) | 2(lb + lh + bh) | l × b × h |\n| Cube (side s) | 6s^{2} | s^{3} |\n| Triangular prism | 2 × ([[1/2]] × b × h) + (sum of the triangle's sides) × H | [[1/2]] × b × h × H |\n| Cylinder (radius r) | 2πr^{2} + 2πrH | πr^{2}H |\n\nFor the triangular prism, b and h are the base and height of the triangle, and H is the length of the prism.\n\n**Why 2πrH?** If you cut open the curved surface of a cylinder and lay it flat, you get a rectangle. Its length is the circumference of the circle (2πr) and its breadth is H.\n\n## Pyramids, cones and spheres\n\nThe volume of a pyramid or cone is exactly [[1/3]] of the prism or cylinder with the same base and perpendicular height:\n\n- Volume = [[1/3]] × area of the base × H\n\nFor the surface area you use the **slant height** h_{s}: the height of a sloping triangular face of a pyramid, or the distance from the tip of a cone to the edge of its base.\n\n| Object | Surface area | Volume |\n|---|---|---|\n| Square pyramid (side b) | b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} | [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H |\n| Cone (radius r) | πr^{2} + πrh_{s} | [[1/3]]πr^{2}H |\n| Sphere (radius r) | 4πr^{2} | [[4/3]]πr^{3} |\n| Hemisphere (radius r) | 2πr^{2} (curved part) + πr^{2} (flat part) | [[2/3]]πr^{3} |\n\n**Slant height with Pythagoras:**\n\n- Cone: h_{s}^{2} = r^{2} + H^{2}\n- Square pyramid: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2}\n\n> **Common mistake:** mixing up H (perpendicular height) and h_{s} (slant height). Volume always uses H; the sloping faces of pyramids and cones use h_{s}.\n\n## Combined objects\n\n- **Volume:** add the volumes of the parts (or subtract if a part is hollowed out).\n- **Surface area:** only add the faces that are visible on the outside. Where two parts are joined, those faces fall away. For a grain silo (cylinder with a hemisphere on top) it is the curved surface of the cylinder + 2πr^{2} of the hemisphere, plus the floor πr^{2} only if the question asks for it.\n\n## Multiplying dimensions by a factor k\n\n| Change | Volume | Surface area |\n|---|---|---|\n| **One** dimension × k (e.g. only the height) | × k | changes, but not by a fixed factor – recalculate |\n| **All** dimensions × k | × k^{3} | × k^{2} |\n\nLook at the formula to see what happens. In V = πr^{2}H, r is **squared**: if only r doubles, V is multiplied by 2^{2} = 4. If only H doubles, V doubles.\n\n**Example:** A ball's radius is tripled. The new volume is 3^{3} = 27 times the original volume, and the new surface area is 3^{2} = 9 times the original surface area.\n\n## Steps for any question\n\n1. Write down the formula.\n2. Make the units the same and substitute. Use the **radius**, not the diameter.\n3. Keep π in the calculator and only round to two decimal places at the end.\n4. Write the unit (cm^{2} or cm^{3}) and convert to ℓ if the question asks for it.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** forgetting the [[1/3]] for pyramids and cones; using the diameter as the radius; forgetting to convert cm^{3} to ℓ (÷ 1 000); thinking the volume only doubles when all dimensions double (it becomes 2^{3} = 8 times bigger)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Regte prisma","en":"Right prism"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met twee kongruente, ewewydige basisse en reghoekige syvlakke wat loodreg op die basisse staan.","en":"An object with two congruent, parallel bases and rectangular side faces perpendicular to the bases."}},{"term":{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte","en":"Surface area"},"def":{"af":"Die som van die oppervlaktes van al die buitevlakke van 'n voorwerp, in vierkante eenhede.","en":"The sum of the areas of all the outer faces of an object, in square units."}},{"term":{"af":"Volume","en":"Volume"},"def":{"af":"Die hoeveelheid ruimte wat 'n voorwerp beslaan, in kubieke eenhede (cm³, m³).","en":"The amount of space an object takes up, in cubic units (cm³, m³)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kapasiteit","en":"Capacity"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel 'n houer kan hou, gemeet in mℓ, ℓ of kℓ; 1 000 cm³ = 1 ℓ.","en":"How much a container can hold, measured in mℓ, ℓ or kℓ; 1 000 cm³ = 1 ℓ."}},{"term":{"af":"Loodregte hoogte (H)","en":"Perpendicular height (H)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand van die basis tot die top, gemeet teen 90° met die basis.","en":"The distance from the base to the top, measured at 90° to the base."}},{"term":{"af":"Skuinshoogte","en":"Slant height"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogte langs die skuins vlak van 'n piramide of keël; dit word vir buiteoppervlakte gebruik.","en":"The height along the sloping face of a pyramid or cone; it is used for surface area."}},{"term":{"af":"Sfeer","en":"Sphere"},"def":{"af":"'n Perfek ronde voorwerp waarvan elke punt op die oppervlak dieselfde afstand (r) van die middelpunt is.","en":"A perfectly round object where every point on the surface is the same distance (r) from the centre."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde voorwerp","en":"Combined object"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp wat uit twee of meer eenvoudige voorwerpe bestaan, bv. 'n silinder met 'n halfsfeer bo-op.","en":"An object made up of two or more simple objects, e.g. a cylinder with a hemisphere on top."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaalfaktor k","en":"Scale factor k"},"def":{"af":"Die getal waarmee afmetings vermenigvuldig word; as alle afmetings × k, word oppervlakte × k² en volume × k³.","en":"The number by which dimensions are multiplied; if all dimensions × k, area becomes × k² and volume × k³."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Silinder: buiteoppervlakte, volume en liter","en":"Cylinder: surface area, volume and litres"},"problem":{"af":"'n Silindriese blik vir ingelegde perskes het 'n radius van 5 cm en 'n hoogte van 12 cm. Bereken (a) die totale buiteoppervlakte, (b) die volume en (c) hoeveel liter die blik hou. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"A cylindrical tin for canned peaches has a radius of 5 cm and a height of 12 cm. Calculate (a) the total surface area, (b) the volume and (c) how many litres the tin holds. Round to two decimal places."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Buiteoppervlakte = 2πr^{2} + 2πrH = 2π(5)^{2} + 2π(5)(12)","en":"(a) Surface area = 2πr^{2} + 2πrH = 2π(5)^{2} + 2π(5)(12)"},{"af":"= 50π + 120π = 170π = 534,07 cm^{2}","en":"= 50π + 120π = 170π = 534.07 cm^{2}"},{"af":"(b) Volume = πr^{2}H = π(5)^{2}(12) = 300π = 942,48 cm^{3}","en":"(b) Volume = πr^{2}H = π(5)^{2}(12) = 300π = 942.48 cm^{3}"},{"af":"(c) 1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ, dus 942,48 ÷ 1 000 = 0,94 ℓ","en":"(c) 1 000 cm^{3} = 1 ℓ, so 942.48 ÷ 1 000 = 0.94 ℓ"}],"answer":{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte = 534,07 cm²; volume = 942,48 cm³ ≈ 0,94 ℓ","en":"Surface area = 534.07 cm²; volume = 942.48 cm³ ≈ 0.94 ℓ"}},{"title":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vierkantige piramide het 'n basis met sye van 10 cm en 'n loodregte hoogte van 12 cm. Bereken die skuinshoogte, die totale buiteoppervlakte en die volume.","en":"A square pyramid has a base with sides of 10 cm and a perpendicular height of 12 cm. Calculate the slant height, the total surface area and the volume."},"steps":[{"af":"Skuinshoogte: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2} = 12^{2} + 5^{2} = 144 + 25 = 169 (Pyth.)","en":"Slant height: h_{s}^{2} = H^{2} + ([[b/2]])^{2} = 12^{2} + 5^{2} = 144 + 25 = 169 (Pyth)"},{"af":"h_{s} = √169 = 13 cm","en":"h_{s} = √169 = 13 cm"},{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte = b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} = 10^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × 10 × 13","en":"Surface area = b^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × b × h_{s} = 10^{2} + 4 × [[1/2]] × 10 × 13"},{"af":"= 100 + 260 = 360 cm^{2}","en":"= 100 + 260 = 360 cm^{2}"},{"af":"Volume = [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H = [[1/3]] × 100 × 12 = 400 cm^{3} (gebruik H, nie h_{s} nie)","en":"Volume = [[1/3]] × b^{2} × H = [[1/3]] × 100 × 12 = 400 cm^{3} (use H, not h_{s})"}],"answer":{"af":"Skuinshoogte = 13 cm; buiteoppervlakte = 360 cm²; volume = 400 cm³","en":"Slant height = 13 cm; surface area = 360 cm²; volume = 400 cm³"}},{"title":{"af":"Saamgestelde voorwerp: 'n graansilo","en":"Combined object: a grain silo"},"problem":{"af":"'n Graansilo op 'n plaas naby Brits bestaan uit 'n silinder met radius 3 m en hoogte 10 m, met 'n halfsfeer (radius 3 m) as dak. Bereken (a) die volume van die silo en (b) die buiteoppervlakte wat geverf moet word (mure en dak, nie die vloer nie).","en":"A grain silo on a farm near Brits consists of a cylinder with radius 3 m and height 10 m, with a hemisphere (radius 3 m) as roof. Calculate (a) the volume of the silo and (b) the outside area that must be painted (walls and roof, not the floor)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Silinder: V = πr^{2}H = π(3)^{2}(10) = 90π","en":"(a) Cylinder: V = πr^{2}H = π(3)^{2}(10) = 90π"},{"af":"Halfsfeer: V = [[2/3]]πr^{3} = [[2/3]]π(3)^{3} = 18π","en":"Hemisphere: V = [[2/3]]πr^{3} = [[2/3]]π(3)^{3} = 18π"},{"af":"Totale volume = 90π + 18π = 108π = 339,29 m^{3}","en":"Total volume = 90π + 18π = 108π = 339.29 m^{3}"},{"af":"(b) Mure (kromme silinder): 2πrH = 2π(3)(10) = 60π. Dak (kromme halfsfeer): 2πr^{2} = 2π(3)^{2} = 18π","en":"(b) Walls (curved cylinder): 2πrH = 2π(3)(10) = 60π. Roof (curved hemisphere): 2πr^{2} = 2π(3)^{2} = 18π"},{"af":"Die sirkel waar die dak op die silinder sit, en die vloer, word nie geverf nie. Oppervlakte = 60π + 18π = 78π = 245,04 m^{2}","en":"The circle where the roof sits on the cylinder, and the floor, are not painted. Area = 60π + 18π = 78π = 245.04 m^{2}"}],"answer":{"af":"Volume = 339,29 m³; oppervlakte om te verf = 245,04 m²","en":"Volume = 339.29 m³; area to paint = 245.04 m²"}},{"title":{"af":"Die effek van 'n skaalfaktor","en":"The effect of a scale factor"},"problem":{"af":"'n Reghoekige doos is 4 cm × 3 cm × 2 cm. (a) Al drie afmetings word met 3 vermenigvuldig. Bereken die nuwe volume en buiteoppervlakte. (b) Wat gebeur as net die hoogte met 3 vermenigvuldig word?","en":"A rectangular box is 4 cm × 3 cm × 2 cm. (a) All three dimensions are multiplied by 3. Calculate the new volume and surface area. (b) What happens if only the height is multiplied by 3?"},"steps":[{"af":"Oorspronklik: V = 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cm^{3}; A = 2(4 × 3 + 4 × 2 + 3 × 2) = 2(12 + 8 + 6) = 52 cm^{2}","en":"Original: V = 4 × 3 × 2 = 24 cm^{3}; A = 2(4 × 3 + 4 × 2 + 3 × 2) = 2(12 + 8 + 6) = 52 cm^{2}"},{"af":"(a) Alle afmetings × 3, dus volume × 3^{3} = 27: V = 24 × 27 = 648 cm^{3}","en":"(a) All dimensions × 3, so volume × 3^{3} = 27: V = 24 × 27 = 648 cm^{3}"},{"af":"Buiteoppervlakte × 3^{2} = 9: A = 52 × 9 = 468 cm^{2}","en":"Surface area × 3^{2} = 9: A = 52 × 9 = 468 cm^{2}"},{"af":"Kontroleer met die nuwe doos 12 × 9 × 6: V = 648 cm^{3} ✓ en A = 2(108 + 72 + 54) = 468 cm^{2} ✓","en":"Check with the new box 12 × 9 × 6: V = 648 cm^{3} ✓ and A = 2(108 + 72 + 54) = 468 cm^{2} ✓"},{"af":"(b) Net die hoogte × 3 (4 × 3 × 6): V = 72 cm^{3} = 3 × 24, maar A = 2(12 + 24 + 18) = 108 cm^{2}, wat nie 'n eenvoudige veelvoud van 52 is nie","en":"(b) Only the height × 3 (4 × 3 × 6): V = 72 cm^{3} = 3 × 24, but A = 2(12 + 24 + 18) = 108 cm^{2}, which is not a simple multiple of 52"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) V = 648 cm³ (× 27); A = 468 cm² (× 9). (b) V = 72 cm³ (× 3); A = 108 cm²","en":"(a) V = 648 cm³ (× 27); A = 468 cm² (× 9). (b) V = 72 cm³ (× 3); A = 108 cm²"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter formule gee die volume van 'n keël met radius r en loodregte hoogte H?","en":"Which formula gives the volume of a cone with radius r and perpendicular height H?"},"options":[{"af":"πr²H","en":"πr²H"},{"af":"⅓πr²H","en":"⅓πr²H"},{"af":"πr² + πr × skuinshoogte","en":"πr² + πr × slant height"},{"af":"(4/3)πr³","en":"(4/3)πr³"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Keël is ⅓ van die silinder met dieselfde basis en hoogte: V = ⅓πr²H. πr²H is die silinder, πr² + πr × skuinshoogte is die keël se buiteoppervlakte, en (4/3)πr³ is 'n sfeer.","en":"A cone is ⅓ of the cylinder with the same base and height: V = ⅓πr²H. πr²H is the cylinder, πr² + πr × slant height is the cone's surface area, and (4/3)πr³ is a sphere."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Houer met 'n volume van 1 000 cm³ hou presies 1 ℓ.","en":"A container with a volume of 1 000 cm³ holds exactly 1 ℓ."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 1 cm³ = 1 mℓ, dus 1 000 cm³ = 1 000 mℓ = 1 ℓ. Om cm³ na ℓ om te skakel, deel jy deur 1 000.","en":"True. 1 cm³ = 1 mℓ, so 1 000 cm³ = 1 000 mℓ = 1 ℓ. To convert cm³ to ℓ, divide by 1 000."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voorwerp by sy volumeformule.","en":"Match each object to its volume formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Silinder","en":"Cylinder"},"r":{"af":"πr²H","en":"πr²H"}},{"l":{"af":"Keël","en":"Cone"},"r":{"af":"⅓πr²H","en":"⅓πr²H"}},{"l":{"af":"Sfeer","en":"Sphere"},"r":{"af":"(4/3)πr³","en":"(4/3)πr³"}},{"l":{"af":"Reghoekige prisma","en":"Rectangular prism"},"r":{"af":"l × b × h","en":"l × b × h"}},{"l":{"af":"Vierkantige piramide","en":"Square pyramid"},"r":{"af":"⅓ × b² × H","en":"⅓ × b² × H"}}],"explain":{"af":"Prismas en silinders: basis × hoogte. Piramides en keëls: ⅓ × basis × hoogte. Sfeer: (4/3)πr³.","en":"Prisms and cylinders: base × height. Pyramids and cones: ⅓ × base × height. Sphere: (4/3)πr³."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As al die afmetings van 'n voorwerp met k vermenigvuldig word, word die volume met ___ vermenigvuldig.","en":"If all the dimensions of an object are multiplied by k, the volume is multiplied by ___."},"answers":{"af":["k³","k^3","k^{3}","k3","k×k×k","k*k*k","kkk"],"en":["k³","k^3","k^{3}","k3","k×k×k","k*k*k","kkk"]},"explain":{"af":"Volume het drie afmetings (lengte × breedte × hoogte), dus word dit met k × k × k = k³ vermenigvuldig. Buiteoppervlakte het twee afmetings en word met k² vermenigvuldig.","en":"Volume has three dimensions (length × breadth × height), so it is multiplied by k × k × k = k³. Surface area has two dimensions and is multiplied by k²."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["k²","k","3k"],"en":["k²","k","3k"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Silinder het 'n radius van 7 cm en 'n hoogte van 10 cm. Die volume is ___ cm³ (rond af tot twee desimale plekke).","en":"A cylinder has a radius of 7 cm and a height of 10 cm. The volume is ___ cm³ (round to two decimal places)."},"answers":{"af":["1539,38","1 539,38","1539.38","1539,38 cm³","1539,38cm3"],"en":["1539.38","1 539.38","1539,38","1539.38 cm³","1539.38cm3"]},"explain":{"af":"V = πr²H = π × 7² × 10 = 490π = 1 539,38 cm³.","en":"V = πr²H = π × 7² × 10 = 490π = 1 539.38 cm³."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["439,82","219,91","6157,52"],"en":["439.82","219.91","6157.52"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bal het 'n middellyn van 12 cm. Wat is die buiteoppervlakte van die bal?","en":"A ball has a diameter of 12 cm. What is the surface area of the ball?"},"options":[{"af":"113,10 cm²","en":"113.10 cm²"},{"af":"904,78 cm²","en":"904.78 cm²"},{"af":"1 809,56 cm²","en":"1 809.56 cm²"},{"af":"452,39 cm²","en":"452.39 cm²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"r = 12 ÷ 2 = 6 cm. Buiteoppervlakte = 4πr² = 4π × 36 = 144π = 452,39 cm². 1 809,56 gebruik die middellyn as radius, 113,10 vergeet die 4, en 904,78 is die volume (4/3)πr³.","en":"r = 12 ÷ 2 = 6 cm. Surface area = 4πr² = 4π × 36 = 144π = 452.39 cm². 1 809.56 uses the diameter as the radius, 113.10 forgets the 4, and 904.78 is the volume (4/3)πr³."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Watertenk op 'n plaas by Hartbeespoortdam het 'n volume van 2,4 m³. Hoeveel liter water hou dit?","en":"A water tank on a farm at Hartbeespoort Dam has a volume of 2.4 m³. How many litres of water does it hold?"},"options":[{"af":"240 ℓ","en":"240 ℓ"},{"af":"2 400 ℓ","en":"2 400 ℓ"},{"af":"24 000 ℓ","en":"24 000 ℓ"},{"af":"2 400 000 ℓ","en":"2 400 000 ℓ"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"1 m³ = 1 000 ℓ, dus 2,4 × 1 000 = 2 400 ℓ. (Of: 2,4 m³ = 2 400 000 cm³, en ÷ 1 000 gee 2 400 ℓ. 2 400 000 vergeet die ÷ 1 000.)","en":"1 m³ = 1 000 ℓ, so 2.4 × 1 000 = 2 400 ℓ. (Or: 2.4 m³ = 2 400 000 cm³, and ÷ 1 000 gives 2 400 ℓ. 2 400 000 forgets the ÷ 1 000.)"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Keël het 'n radius van 3 cm en 'n loodregte hoogte van 4 cm. Die totale buiteoppervlakte is ___ cm² (rond af tot twee desimale plekke).","en":"A cone has a radius of 3 cm and a perpendicular height of 4 cm. The total surface area is ___ cm² (round to two decimal places)."},"answers":{"af":["75,40","75,4","75.40","75.4","75,40 cm²","24π"],"en":["75.40","75.4","75,40","75,4","75.40 cm²","24π"]},"explain":{"af":"Skuinshoogte² = 3² + 4² = 25, dus is die skuinshoogte 5 cm. Buiteoppervlakte = πr² + πr × skuinshoogte = 9π + 15π = 24π = 75,40 cm². Moenie H = 4 in die buiteoppervlakte gebruik nie.","en":"Slant height² = 3² + 4² = 25, so the slant height is 5 cm. Surface area = πr² + πr × slant height = 9π + 15π = 24π = 75.40 cm². Do not use H = 4 in the surface area."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["65,97","47,12","94,25"],"en":["65.97","47.12","94.25"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Driehoekige prisma het 'n reghoekige driehoek as basis met reghoeksye 6 cm en 8 cm (skuinssy 10 cm). Die prisma is 15 cm lank. Wat is die volume?","en":"A triangular prism has a right-angled triangle as base with legs 6 cm and 8 cm (hypotenuse 10 cm). The prism is 15 cm long. What is the volume?"},"options":[{"af":"360 cm³","en":"360 cm³"},{"af":"720 cm³","en":"720 cm³"},{"af":"120 cm³","en":"120 cm³"},{"af":"408 cm³","en":"408 cm³"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"V = oppervlakte van die driehoek × lengte = (½ × 6 × 8) × 15 = 24 × 15 = 360 cm³. 720 vergeet die ½, 120 deel verkeerdelik deur 3 (dis nie 'n piramide nie), en 408 is die buiteoppervlakte se getal.","en":"V = area of the triangle × length = (½ × 6 × 8) × 15 = 24 × 15 = 360 cm³. 720 forgets the ½, 120 wrongly divides by 3 (it is not a pyramid), and 408 is the surface area's number."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy net die radius van 'n silinder verdubbel (die hoogte bly dieselfde), verdubbel die volume ook.","en":"If you double only the radius of a cylinder (the height stays the same), the volume also doubles."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In V = πr²H is r gekwadreer, dus word die volume met 2² = 4 vermenigvuldig. Net as die hoogte verdubbel, verdubbel die volume.","en":"False. In V = πr²H, r is squared, so the volume is multiplied by 2² = 4. Only when the height doubles does the volume double."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Houtmodel van 'n vuurpyl bestaan uit 'n silinder (middellyn 4 cm, hoogte 10 cm) met 'n keël (dieselfde middellyn, loodregte hoogte 3 cm) bo-op. Wat is die totale volume?","en":"A wooden model of a rocket consists of a cylinder (diameter 4 cm, height 10 cm) with a cone (same diameter, perpendicular height 3 cm) on top. What is the total volume?"},"options":[{"af":"125,66 cm³","en":"125.66 cm³"},{"af":"163,36 cm³","en":"163.36 cm³"},{"af":"138,23 cm³","en":"138.23 cm³"},{"af":"552,92 cm³","en":"552.92 cm³"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r = 2 cm. Silinder: π × 2² × 10 = 40π. Keël: ⅓ × π × 2² × 3 = 4π. Totaal = 44π = 138,23 cm³. 163,36 vergeet die ⅓, 125,66 vergeet die keël, en 552,92 gebruik die middellyn as radius.","en":"r = 2 cm. Cylinder: π × 2² × 10 = 40π. Cone: ⅓ × π × 2² × 3 = 4π. Total = 44π = 138.23 cm³. 163.36 forgets the ⅓, 125.66 forgets the cone, and 552.92 uses the diameter as the radius."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kubus het 'n buiteoppervlakte van 54 cm². Elke sy word verdriedubbel. Die nuwe buiteoppervlakte is ___ cm².","en":"A cube has a surface area of 54 cm². Each side is tripled. The new surface area is ___ cm²."},"answers":{"af":["486","486 cm²"],"en":["486","486 cm²"]},"explain":{"af":"Alle afmetings × 3, dus buiteoppervlakte × 3² = 9: 54 × 9 = 486 cm². (Kontroleer: 6s² = 54 gee s = 3; nuwe s = 9; 6 × 81 = 486.)","en":"All dimensions × 3, so surface area × 3² = 9: 54 × 9 = 486 cm². (Check: 6s² = 54 gives s = 3; new s = 9; 6 × 81 = 486.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["162","1458","81"],"en":["162","1458","81"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Halfsfeervormige bak het 'n binneradius van 9 cm. Hoeveel liter hou die bak as dit vol is?","en":"A hemispherical bowl has an inner radius of 9 cm. How many litres does the bowl hold when it is full?"},"options":[{"af":"3,05 ℓ","en":"3.05 ℓ"},{"af":"15,27 ℓ","en":"15.27 ℓ"},{"af":"1 526,81 ℓ","en":"1 526.81 ℓ"},{"af":"1,53 ℓ","en":"1.53 ℓ"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"V = ⅔πr³ = ⅔ × π × 9³ = 486π = 1 526,81 cm³. Deel deur 1 000: 1,53 ℓ. 3,05 ℓ is 'n hele sfeer, 15,27 ℓ deel deur 100 in plaas van 1 000, en 1 526,81 ℓ vergeet om om te skakel.","en":"V = ⅔πr³ = ⅔ × π × 9³ = 486π = 1 526.81 cm³. Divide by 1 000: 1.53 ℓ. 3.05 ℓ is a whole sphere, 15.27 ℓ divides by 100 instead of 1 000, and 1 526.81 ℓ forgets to convert."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Sitrusplaas naby Brits tap lemoensap uit 'n tenk van 500 ℓ in silindriese bottels met 'n binnemiddellyn van 6 cm en 'n hoogte van 15 cm. Hoeveel bottels kan heeltemal vol gemaak word?","en":"A citrus farm near Brits bottles orange juice from a 500 ℓ tank into cylindrical bottles with an inner diameter of 6 cm and a height of 15 cm. How many bottles can be filled completely?"},"options":[{"af":"1","en":"1"},{"af":"294","en":"294"},{"af":"1 178","en":"1 178"},{"af":"1 179","en":"1 179"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"r = 3 cm. Een bottel: V = π × 3² × 15 = 135π = 424,12 cm³. Tenk: 500 ℓ = 500 000 cm³. 500 000 ÷ 424,12 = 1 178,9, dus 1 178 vol bottels – rond áf, want die 1 179ste bottel word nie vol nie. 294 gebruik die middellyn as radius, en 1 vergeet om ℓ na cm³ om te skakel.","en":"r = 3 cm. One bottle: V = π × 3² × 15 = 135π = 424.12 cm³. Tank: 500 ℓ = 500 000 cm³. 500 000 ÷ 424.12 = 1 178.9, so 1 178 full bottles – round down, because the 1 179th bottle will not be full. 294 uses the diameter as the radius, and 1 forgets to convert ℓ to cm³."}}]},{"id":"w10-t4-waarskynlikheid","title":{"af":"Waarskynlikheid","en":"Probability"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal waarskynlikhede en relatiewe frekwensies kan bereken, die optelreël kan gebruik en Venn-diagramme met twee gebeurtenisse kan invul en lees.","en":"You will be able to calculate probabilities and relative frequencies, use the addition rule and fill in and read Venn diagrams with two events."},"summary":{"af":"## Basiese begrippe\n\n- **Eksperiment:** 'n handeling met 'n onsekere uitkoms, bv. om 'n dobbelsteen te gooi.\n- **Uitkoms:** een moontlike resultaat van die eksperiment.\n- **Steekproefruimte (S):** die versameling van álle moontlike uitkomste. n(S) is die aantal uitkomste. Vir een dobbelsteen is S = {1; 2; 3; 4; 5; 6} en n(S) = 6.\n- **Gebeurtenis (E):** 'n deelversameling van S. Bv. E = \"'n ewe getal\" = {2; 4; 6}, dus n(E) = 3.\n\n## Teoretiese waarskynlikheid\n\nAs al die uitkomste ewe waarskynlik is, is\n\nP(E) = [[n(E)/n(S)]]\n\n- 0 ≤ P(E) ≤ 1. P(E) = 0 beteken die gebeurtenis is onmoontlik; P(E) = 1 beteken dit is seker.\n- Jy kan die antwoord as 'n breuk, desimale getal of persentasie skryf: [[3/8]] = 0,375 = 37,5%.\n\n**Twee stappe:** 'n Draaiskyf met twee gelyke dele, rooi (R) en blou (B), word twee keer gedraai. S = {RR; RB; BR; BB}, dus n(S) = 4. RB en BR is **verskillende** uitkomste, daarom is P(een rooi en een blou) = [[2/4]] = [[1/2]], nie [[1/3]] nie.\n\n## Relatiewe frekwensie\n\nAs jy 'n eksperiment werklik uitvoer, bereken jy die **relatiewe frekwensie** (eksperimentele waarskynlikheid):\n\nRelatiewe frekwensie = [[aantal kere wat E plaasvind/totale aantal proewe]]\n\nHoe meer proewe jy doen, hoe nader kom die relatiewe frekwensie aan die teoretiese waarskynlikheid. As 'n muntstuk 50 keer opgegooi word en 28 keer kop land, is die relatiewe frekwensie [[28/50]] = 0,56, terwyl die teoretiese waarskynlikheid 0,5 is.\n\n## Onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse\n\nA en B is **onderling uitsluitend** as hulle nie gelyktydig kan plaasvind nie – hulle het geen gemeenskaplike uitkomste nie. Dan is P(A en B) = 0 en\n\nP(A of B) = P(A) + P(B)\n\nBv. by een dobbelsteen: A = {1; 2} en B = {5; 6}.\n\n## Komplementêre gebeurtenisse\n\nDie komplement van A is \"nie A\" (ook geskryf as A′): al die uitkomste in S wat nie in A is nie. A en nie A is onderling uitsluitend **en** saam vul hulle die hele steekproefruimte. Daarom is\n\nP(nie A) = 1 − P(A)\n\n> **Onthou!** Komplementêre gebeurtenisse is altyd onderling uitsluitend, maar onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse is nie altyd komplementêr nie. {1; 2} en {5; 6} is onderling uitsluitend, maar 3 en 4 val buite albei.\n\n## Die optelreël\n\nVir enige twee gebeurtenisse A en B geld:\n\nP(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B)\n\n- \"A of B\" (A ∪ B) beteken A, of B, of albei.\n- \"A en B\" (A ∩ B) beteken albei gelyktydig.\n- Ons trek P(A en B) af omdat die oorvleueling in P(A) én in P(B) getel is – anders tel ons dit twee keer.\n\nAs drie van die vier waardes gegee is, kan jy die vierde bereken. As jy P(A en B) = 0 kry, is A en B onderling uitsluitend.\n\n## Venn-diagramme met twee gebeurtenisse\n\n'n Reghoek stel S voor, met twee oorvleuelende sirkels A en B binne-in. Daar is vier gebiede:\n\n| Gebied | Betekenis | Aantal |\n|---|---|---|\n| Oorvleueling | A en B | n(A en B) |\n| Slegs A | in A, maar nie in B nie | n(A) − n(A en B) |\n| Slegs B | in B, maar nie in A nie | n(B) − n(A en B) |\n| Buite albei sirkels | nie A nie en nie B nie | n(S) − n(A of B) |\n\n**Stappe om 'n Venn-diagram in te vul:**\n\n1. Begin altyd by die oorvleueling (A en B).\n2. Trek af om \"slegs A\" en \"slegs B\" te kry.\n3. Trek die som van die drie gebiede van n(S) af vir die gebied buite die sirkels.\n4. Kontroleer dat al vier gebiede saam n(S) gee (of 1 as jy met waarskynlikhede werk).\n5. As die oorvleueling onbekend is, noem dit x en stel 'n vergelyking op: som van al vier gebiede = n(S).\n\n'n Waarskynlikheid uit 'n Venn-diagram is P = [[aantal in die gebied/n(S)]].\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Om n(A) in die \"slegs A\"-gebied te skryf in plaas van n(A) − n(A en B).\n- Om die gebied buite albei sirkels te vergeet.\n- Om P(A) + P(B) te gebruik as A en B oorvleuel – dan tel jy die oorvleueling twee keer.\n- Om RB en BR as een uitkoms te tel.\n- 'n Waarskynlikheid groter as 1 of kleiner as 0 is altyd verkeerd – gaan terug en soek die fout.","en":"## Basic concepts\n\n- **Experiment:** an action with an uncertain outcome, e.g. rolling a die.\n- **Outcome:** one possible result of the experiment.\n- **Sample space (S):** the set of all possible outcomes. n(S) is the number of outcomes. For one die S = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6} and n(S) = 6.\n- **Event (E):** a subset of S. E.g. E = \"an even number\" = {2, 4, 6}, so n(E) = 3.\n\n## Theoretical probability\n\nIf all the outcomes are equally likely, then\n\nP(E) = [[n(E)/n(S)]]\n\n- 0 ≤ P(E) ≤ 1. P(E) = 0 means the event is impossible; P(E) = 1 means it is certain.\n- You can write the answer as a fraction, decimal or percentage: [[3/8]] = 0.375 = 37.5%.\n\n**Two steps:** A spinner with two equal parts, red (R) and blue (B), is spun twice. S = {RR, RB, BR, BB}, so n(S) = 4. RB and BR are **different** outcomes, so P(one red and one blue) = [[2/4]] = [[1/2]], not [[1/3]].\n\n## Relative frequency\n\nWhen you actually carry out an experiment, you calculate the **relative frequency** (experimental probability):\n\nRelative frequency = [[number of times E occurs/total number of trials]]\n\nThe more trials you do, the closer the relative frequency gets to the theoretical probability. If a coin is tossed 50 times and lands heads 28 times, the relative frequency is [[28/50]] = 0.56, while the theoretical probability is 0.5.\n\n## Mutually exclusive events\n\nA and B are **mutually exclusive** if they cannot happen at the same time – they have no outcomes in common. Then P(A and B) = 0 and\n\nP(A or B) = P(A) + P(B)\n\nE.g. for one die: A = {1, 2} and B = {5, 6}.\n\n## Complementary events\n\nThe complement of A is \"not A\" (also written A′): all the outcomes in S that are not in A. A and not A are mutually exclusive **and** together they fill the whole sample space. Therefore\n\nP(not A) = 1 − P(A)\n\n> **Remember!** Complementary events are always mutually exclusive, but mutually exclusive events are not always complementary. {1, 2} and {5, 6} are mutually exclusive, but 3 and 4 fall outside both.\n\n## The addition rule\n\nFor any two events A and B:\n\nP(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B)\n\n- \"A or B\" (A ∪ B) means A, or B, or both.\n- \"A and B\" (A ∩ B) means both at the same time.\n- We subtract P(A and B) because the overlap is counted in P(A) and in P(B) – otherwise we count it twice.\n\nIf three of the four values are given, you can calculate the fourth. If you get P(A and B) = 0, A and B are mutually exclusive.\n\n## Venn diagrams with two events\n\nA rectangle represents S, with two overlapping circles A and B inside it. There are four regions:\n\n| Region | Meaning | Number |\n|---|---|---|\n| Overlap | A and B | n(A and B) |\n| Only A | in A, but not in B | n(A) − n(A and B) |\n| Only B | in B, but not in A | n(B) − n(A and B) |\n| Outside both circles | not A and not B | n(S) − n(A or B) |\n\n**Steps to fill in a Venn diagram:**\n\n1. Always start with the overlap (A and B).\n2. Subtract to get \"only A\" and \"only B\".\n3. Subtract the sum of the three regions from n(S) for the region outside the circles.\n4. Check that all four regions together give n(S) (or 1 if you are working with probabilities).\n5. If the overlap is unknown, call it x and set up an equation: sum of all four regions = n(S).\n\nA probability from a Venn diagram is P = [[number in the region/n(S)]].\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Writing n(A) in the \"only A\" region instead of n(A) − n(A and B).\n- Forgetting the region outside both circles.\n- Using P(A) + P(B) when A and B overlap – then you count the overlap twice.\n- Counting RB and BR as one outcome.\n- A probability greater than 1 or less than 0 is always wrong – go back and find the mistake."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Steekproefruimte (S)","en":"Sample space (S)"},"def":{"af":"Die versameling van alle moontlike uitkomste van 'n eksperiment.","en":"The set of all possible outcomes of an experiment."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitkoms","en":"Outcome"},"def":{"af":"Een moontlike resultaat van 'n eksperiment.","en":"One possible result of an experiment."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebeurtenis","en":"Event"},"def":{"af":"'n Deelversameling van die steekproefruimte, bv. 'gooi 'n ewe getal'.","en":"A subset of the sample space, e.g. 'roll an even number'."}},{"term":{"af":"Teoretiese waarskynlikheid","en":"Theoretical probability"},"def":{"af":"P(E) = n(E)/n(S) as al die uitkomste ewe waarskynlik is.","en":"P(E) = n(E)/n(S) when all the outcomes are equally likely."}},{"term":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie","en":"Relative frequency"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal kere wat 'n gebeurtenis in 'n eksperiment plaasvind gedeel deur die totale aantal proewe.","en":"The number of times an event occurs in an experiment divided by the total number of trials."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend","en":"Mutually exclusive"},"def":{"af":"Gebeurtenisse wat nie gelyktydig kan plaasvind nie; P(A en B) = 0.","en":"Events that cannot happen at the same time; P(A and B) = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Komplementêre gebeurtenisse","en":"Complementary events"},"def":{"af":"Twee onderling uitsluitende gebeurtenisse wat saam die hele steekproefruimte vul; P(nie A) = 1 − P(A).","en":"Two mutually exclusive events that together fill the whole sample space; P(not A) = 1 − P(A)."}},{"term":{"af":"Venn-diagram","en":"Venn diagram"},"def":{"af":"'n Reghoek (die steekproefruimte) met sirkels wat gebeurtenisse en hul oorvleueling voorstel.","en":"A rectangle (the sample space) with circles that represent events and their overlap."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Eenvoudige en komplementêre waarskynlikheid","en":"Simple and complementary probability"},"problem":{"af":"'n Krat van 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits bevat 12 lemoene, 5 nartjies en 3 suurlemoene. Een vrug word lukraak uitgehaal. Bereken (a) P(lemoen), (b) P(nie 'n suurlemoen nie) en (c) P(nartjie of suurlemoen).","en":"A crate from a citrus farm near Brits contains 12 oranges, 5 naartjies and 3 lemons. One fruit is taken out at random. Calculate (a) P(orange), (b) P(not a lemon) and (c) P(naartjie or lemon)."},"steps":[{"af":"n(S) = 12 + 5 + 3 = 20","en":"n(S) = 12 + 5 + 3 = 20"},{"af":"(a) P(lemoen) = [[12/20]] = [[3/5]] = 0,6","en":"(a) P(orange) = [[12/20]] = [[3/5]] = 0.6"},{"af":"(b) P(suurlemoen) = [[3/20]], dus P(nie suurlemoen) = 1 − [[3/20]] = [[17/20]] = 0,85 (komplementêre gebeurtenisse)","en":"(b) P(lemon) = [[3/20]], so P(not lemon) = 1 − [[3/20]] = [[17/20]] = 0.85 (complementary events)"},{"af":"(c) 'n Vrug kan nie tegelyk 'n nartjie en 'n suurlemoen wees nie, dus is die gebeurtenisse onderling uitsluitend: P = [[5/20]] + [[3/20]] = [[8/20]] = [[2/5]] = 0,4","en":"(c) A fruit cannot be a naartjie and a lemon at the same time, so the events are mutually exclusive: P = [[5/20]] + [[3/20]] = [[8/20]] = [[2/5]] = 0.4"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,6  (b) 0,85  (c) 0,4","en":"(a) 0.6  (b) 0.85  (c) 0.4"}},{"title":{"af":"Venn-diagram met 'n onbekende","en":"Venn diagram with an unknown"},"problem":{"af":"In 'n klas van 30 leerders in Brits speel 18 rugby (R) en 15 krieket (K). 4 leerders speel geen van die twee nie. Bereken hoeveel albei speel, en bepaal dan P(slegs rugby) en P(R of K).","en":"In a class of 30 learners in Brits, 18 play rugby (R) and 15 play cricket (K). 4 learners play neither. Calculate how many play both, then find P(only rugby) and P(R or K)."},"steps":[{"af":"Laat x = n(R en K). Dan is slegs R = 18 − x, slegs K = 15 − x en buite die sirkels = 4","en":"Let x = n(R and K). Then only R = 18 − x, only K = 15 − x and outside the circles = 4"},{"af":"Al vier gebiede tel op tot 30: (18 − x) + x + (15 − x) + 4 = 30, dus 37 − x = 30 en x = 7","en":"All four regions add up to 30: (18 − x) + x + (15 − x) + 4 = 30, so 37 − x = 30 and x = 7"},{"af":"Gebiede: slegs R = 11, albei = 7, slegs K = 8, geen = 4. Kontroleer: 11 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 30 ✓","en":"Regions: only R = 11, both = 7, only K = 8, neither = 4. Check: 11 + 7 + 8 + 4 = 30 ✓"},{"af":"P(slegs rugby) = [[11/30]]","en":"P(only rugby) = [[11/30]]"},{"af":"P(R of K) = [[11 + 7 + 8/30]] = [[26/30]] = [[13/15]]. Kontroleer met die optelreël: [[18/30]] + [[15/30]] − [[7/30]] = [[26/30]] ✓","en":"P(R or K) = [[11 + 7 + 8/30]] = [[26/30]] = [[13/15]]. Check with the addition rule: [[18/30]] + [[15/30]] − [[7/30]] = [[26/30]] ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"7 leerders speel albei; P(slegs rugby) = 11/30; P(R of K) = 13/15","en":"7 learners play both; P(only rugby) = 11/30; P(R or K) = 13/15"}},{"title":{"af":"Die optelreël","en":"The addition rule"},"problem":{"af":"P(A) = 0,45, P(B) = 0,3 en P(A of B) = 0,6. Bereken (a) P(A en B), (b) of A en B onderling uitsluitend is, (c) P(nie A nie en nie B nie) en (d) P(slegs A).","en":"P(A) = 0.45, P(B) = 0.3 and P(A or B) = 0.6. Calculate (a) P(A and B), (b) whether A and B are mutually exclusive, (c) P(not A and not B) and (d) P(only A)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) P(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B), dus 0,6 = 0,45 + 0,3 − P(A en B)","en":"(a) P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B), so 0.6 = 0.45 + 0.3 − P(A and B)"},{"af":"P(A en B) = 0,75 − 0,6 = 0,15","en":"P(A and B) = 0.75 − 0.6 = 0.15"},{"af":"(b) P(A en B) = 0,15 ≠ 0, dus is A en B NIE onderling uitsluitend nie","en":"(b) P(A and B) = 0.15 ≠ 0, so A and B are NOT mutually exclusive"},{"af":"(c) P(nie A nie en nie B nie) = 1 − P(A of B) = 1 − 0,6 = 0,4","en":"(c) P(not A and not B) = 1 − P(A or B) = 1 − 0.6 = 0.4"},{"af":"(d) P(slegs A) = P(A) − P(A en B) = 0,45 − 0,15 = 0,3","en":"(d) P(only A) = P(A) − P(A and B) = 0.45 − 0.15 = 0.3"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,15  (b) Nee  (c) 0,4  (d) 0,3","en":"(a) 0.15  (b) No  (c) 0.4  (d) 0.3"}},{"title":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie teenoor teoretiese waarskynlikheid","en":"Relative frequency versus theoretical probability"},"problem":{"af":"'n Dobbelsteen word 120 keer gegooi. Die resultate: 1 → 18 keer, 2 → 22, 3 → 17, 4 → 23, 5 → 19, 6 → 21. Bereken die relatiewe frekwensie van (a) 'n 6 en (b) 'n ewe getal, en vergelyk elkeen met die teoretiese waarskynlikheid.","en":"A die is rolled 120 times. The results: 1 → 18 times, 2 → 22, 3 → 17, 4 → 23, 5 → 19, 6 → 21. Calculate the relative frequency of (a) a 6 and (b) an even number, and compare each with the theoretical probability."},"steps":[{"af":"Kontroleer die totaal: 18 + 22 + 17 + 23 + 19 + 21 = 120 ✓","en":"Check the total: 18 + 22 + 17 + 23 + 19 + 21 = 120 ✓"},{"af":"(a) Relatiewe frekwensie van 'n 6 = [[21/120]] = 0,175. Teoreties: P(6) = [[1/6]] ≈ 0,17","en":"(a) Relative frequency of a 6 = [[21/120]] = 0.175. Theoretical: P(6) = [[1/6]] ≈ 0.17"},{"af":"(b) Ewe getalle: 22 + 23 + 21 = 66, dus relatiewe frekwensie = [[66/120]] = 0,55","en":"(b) Even numbers: 22 + 23 + 21 = 66, so relative frequency = [[66/120]] = 0.55"},{"af":"Teoreties: P(ewe) = [[3/6]] = 0,5","en":"Theoretical: P(even) = [[3/6]] = 0.5"},{"af":"Die waardes is naby aan mekaar, maar nie gelyk nie. Met meer gooie sal die relatiewe frekwensies nader aan die teoretiese waarskynlikhede kom.","en":"The values are close, but not equal. With more rolls the relative frequencies will get closer to the theoretical probabilities."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 0,175 teenoor ≈ 0,17  (b) 0,55 teenoor 0,5","en":"(a) 0.175 versus ≈ 0.17  (b) 0.55 versus 0.5"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Draaiskyf met twee gelyke dele, rooi (R) en blou (B), word twee keer gedraai. Wat is die steekproefruimte?","en":"A spinner with two equal parts, red (R) and blue (B), is spun twice. What is the sample space?"},"options":[{"af":"{RR; RB; BB}","en":"{RR, RB, BB}"},{"af":"{R; B}","en":"{R, B}"},{"af":"{RR; RB; BR; BB}","en":"{RR, RB, BR, BB}"},{"af":"{RB; BR}","en":"{RB, BR}"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Eers rooi dan blou (RB) en eers blou dan rooi (BR) is twee verskillende uitkomste, dus is n(S) = 4. {RR; RB; BB} is die klassieke fout wat RB en BR as een tel.","en":"First red then blue (RB) and first blue then red (BR) are two different outcomes, so n(S) = 4. {RR, RB, BB} is the classic mistake that counts RB and BR as one."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die waarskynlikheid van enige gebeurtenis lê tussen 0 en 1 (0 en 1 ingesluit).","en":"The probability of any event lies between 0 and 1 (0 and 1 included)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 0 beteken onmoontlik en 1 beteken seker. 'n Antwoord soos 1,2 of −0,3 wys dat jy 'n fout gemaak het.","en":"True. 0 means impossible and 1 means certain. An answer such as 1.2 or −0.3 shows that you made a mistake."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each term to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Steekproefruimte","en":"Sample space"},"r":{"af":"Die versameling van alle moontlike uitkomste","en":"The set of all possible outcomes"}},{"l":{"af":"Gebeurtenis","en":"Event"},"r":{"af":"'n Deelversameling van die steekproefruimte","en":"A subset of the sample space"}},{"l":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend","en":"Mutually exclusive"},"r":{"af":"Die gebeurtenisse kan nie gelyktydig plaasvind nie","en":"The events cannot happen at the same time"}},{"l":{"af":"Komplementêre gebeurtenisse","en":"Complementary events"},"r":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend, en saam vul hulle die hele steekproefruimte","en":"Mutually exclusive, and together they fill the whole sample space"}},{"l":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie","en":"Relative frequency"},"r":{"af":"Aantal kere wat die gebeurtenis plaasvind ÷ totale aantal proewe","en":"Number of times the event occurs ÷ total number of trials"}}],"explain":{"af":"Let op die verskil: komplementêre gebeurtenisse is onderling uitsluitend én dek saam die hele steekproefruimte.","en":"Note the difference: complementary events are mutually exclusive and together cover the whole sample space."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,35. Dan is P(nie A) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.35. Then P(not A) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,65","0.65","65%","13/20"],"en":["0.65","0,65","65%","13/20"]},"explain":{"af":"A en nie A is komplementêr: P(nie A) = 1 − P(A) = 1 − 0,35 = 0,65.","en":"A and not A are complementary: P(not A) = 1 − P(A) = 1 − 0.35 = 0.65."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,35","1,35","0,75"],"en":["0.35","1.35","0.75"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die letters van die woord MADIBENG word elkeen op 'n kaartjie geskryf, en een kaartjie word lukraak getrek. Wat is die waarskynlikheid dat dit 'n klinker is?","en":"The letters of the word MADIBENG are each written on a card, and one card is drawn at random. What is the probability that it is a vowel?"},"options":[{"af":"5/8","en":"5/8"},{"af":"3/5","en":"3/5"},{"af":"1/8","en":"1/8"},{"af":"3/8","en":"3/8"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"n(S) = 8 letters. Die klinkers is A, I en E, dus n(E) = 3 en P = 3/8. 5/8 is die medeklinkers, en 3/5 vergelyk klinkers met medeklinkers in plaas van met al die letters.","en":"n(S) = 8 letters. The vowels are A, I and E, so n(E) = 3 and P = 3/8. 5/8 is the consonants, and 3/5 compares vowels with consonants instead of with all the letters."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Losskakel by 'n rugbyklub in Madibeng oefen 40 doelskoppe en slaag met 32 daarvan. Die relatiewe frekwensie van 'n suksesvolle doelskop is ___.","en":"A flyhalf at a rugby club in Madibeng practises 40 conversion kicks and succeeds with 32 of them. The relative frequency of a successful kick is ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,8","0,80","0.8","4/5","80%","32/40"],"en":["0.8","0.80","0,8","4/5","80%","32/40"]},"explain":{"af":"Relatiewe frekwensie = aantal suksesse ÷ aantal proewe = 32/40 = 0,8.","en":"Relative frequency = number of successes ÷ number of trials = 32/40 = 0.8."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,2","1,25","0,32"],"en":["0.2","1.25","0.32"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"A en B is onderling uitsluitend, met P(A) = 0,4 en P(B) = 0,35. Wat is P(A of B)?","en":"A and B are mutually exclusive, with P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.35. What is P(A or B)?"},"options":[{"af":"0,14","en":"0.14"},{"af":"0,75","en":"0.75"},{"af":"0,05","en":"0.05"},{"af":"0,25","en":"0.25"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Onderling uitsluitend beteken P(A en B) = 0, dus P(A of B) = 0,4 + 0,35 = 0,75. 0,14 vermenigvuldig, 0,05 trek af, en 0,25 is P(nie A nie en nie B nie).","en":"Mutually exclusive means P(A and B) = 0, so P(A or B) = 0.4 + 0.35 = 0.75. 0.14 multiplies, 0.05 subtracts, and 0.25 is P(not A and not B)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,6, P(B) = 0,25 en P(A en B) = 0,15. Dan is P(A of B) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.6, P(B) = 0.25 and P(A and B) = 0.15. Then P(A or B) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,7","0,70","0.7","7/10","70%"],"en":["0.7","0.70","0,7","7/10","70%"]},"explain":{"af":"P(A of B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A en B) = 0,6 + 0,25 − 0,15 = 0,7. As jy net optel (0,85), tel jy die oorvleueling twee keer.","en":"P(A or B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A and B) = 0.6 + 0.25 − 0.15 = 0.7. If you only add (0.85), you count the overlap twice."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,85","1","0,55"],"en":["0.85","1","0.55"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n Venn-diagram is n(S) = 40, n(A) = 22, n(B) = 15 en n(A en B) = 6. Hoeveel elemente lê buite albei sirkels?","en":"In a Venn diagram, n(S) = 40, n(A) = 22, n(B) = 15 and n(A and B) = 6. How many elements lie outside both circles?"},"options":[{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"3","en":"3"},{"af":"31","en":"31"},{"af":"37","en":"37"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"n(A of B) = 22 + 15 − 6 = 31, dus buite = 40 − 31 = 9. 3 vergeet om die oorvleueling af te trek (40 − 37), en 31 is n(A of B) self.","en":"n(A or B) = 22 + 15 − 6 = 31, so outside = 40 − 31 = 9. 3 forgets to subtract the overlap (40 − 37), and 31 is n(A or B) itself."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,6 en P(B) = 0,5. Dit is moontlik dat A en B onderling uitsluitend is.","en":"P(A) = 0.6 and P(B) = 0.5. It is possible that A and B are mutually exclusive."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. As hulle onderling uitsluitend was, sou P(A of B) = 0,6 + 0,5 = 1,1 wees – groter as 1, wat onmoontlik is. Hulle móét dus oorvleuel, met P(A en B) ≥ 0,1.","en":"False. If they were mutually exclusive, P(A or B) would be 0.6 + 0.5 = 1.1 – greater than 1, which is impossible. So they must overlap, with P(A and B) ≥ 0.1."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"P(A) = 0,52, P(B) = 0,38 en P(A of B) = 0,7. Dan is P(slegs A) = ___.","en":"P(A) = 0.52, P(B) = 0.38 and P(A or B) = 0.7. Then P(only A) = ___."},"answers":{"af":["0,32","0.32","32%","8/25"],"en":["0.32","0,32","32%","8/25"]},"explain":{"af":"Eers die oorvleueling: P(A en B) = 0,52 + 0,38 − 0,7 = 0,2. Dan P(slegs A) = P(A) − P(A en B) = 0,52 − 0,2 = 0,32.","en":"First the overlap: P(A and B) = 0.52 + 0.38 − 0.7 = 0.2. Then P(only A) = P(A) − P(A and B) = 0.52 − 0.2 = 0.32."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,52","0,2","0,18"],"en":["0.52","0.2","0.18"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kaartjies genommer 1 tot 20 lê in 'n sak. Een kaartjie word lukraak getrek. Wat is die waarskynlikheid dat die getal 'n veelvoud van 3 óf 'n veelvoud van 4 is?","en":"Cards numbered 1 to 20 are in a bag. One card is drawn at random. What is the probability that the number is a multiple of 3 or a multiple of 4?"},"options":[{"af":"11/20","en":"11/20"},{"af":"3/10","en":"3/10"},{"af":"1/2","en":"1/2"},{"af":"1/20","en":"1/20"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Veelvoude van 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18 (6). Veelvoude van 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 (5). Albei: 12 (1). P = 6/20 + 5/20 − 1/20 = 10/20 = 1/2. 11/20 tel 12 twee keer.","en":"Multiples of 3: 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18 (6). Multiples of 4: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 (5). Both: 12 (1). P = 6/20 + 5/20 − 1/20 = 10/20 = 1/2. 11/20 counts 12 twice."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n opname onder 50 leerders in Madibeng gebruik 28 netwerk V vir selfoondata, 20 gebruik netwerk M, en 8 gebruik nie een van die twee nie. Hoeveel leerders gebruik albei netwerke?","en":"In a survey of 50 learners in Madibeng, 28 use network V for cellphone data, 20 use network M, and 8 use neither. How many learners use both networks?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"14","en":"14"},{"af":"48","en":"48"},{"af":"6","en":"6"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"n(V of M) = 50 − 8 = 42. Optelreël: 42 = 28 + 20 − n(albei), dus n(albei) = 48 − 42 = 6. 2 ignoreer die 8 wat geen netwerk gebruik nie (50 − 28 − 20), en 48 tel net op.","en":"n(V or M) = 50 − 8 = 42. Addition rule: 42 = 28 + 20 − n(both), so n(both) = 48 − 42 = 6. 2 ignores the 8 who use neither network (50 − 28 − 20), and 48 just adds."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Sak bevat 12 groen balle en 'n aantal geel balle. As een bal lukraak getrek word, is P(groen) = 3/8. Hoeveel geel balle is in die sak?","en":"A bag contains 12 green balls and some yellow balls. If one ball is drawn at random, P(green) = 3/8. How many yellow balls are in the bag?"},"options":[{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"32","en":"32"},{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"4,5","en":"4.5"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"12/n(S) = 3/8, dus 3 × n(S) = 96 en n(S) = 32 balle altesaam. Geel = 32 − 12 = 20. 32 is die totaal, 5 gebruik die breuk se getalle as aantalle (8 − 3), en 4,5 is 12 × 3/8.","en":"12/n(S) = 3/8, so 3 × n(S) = 96 and n(S) = 32 balls in total. Yellow = 32 − 12 = 20. 32 is the total, 5 uses the fraction's numbers as counts (8 − 3), and 4.5 is 12 × 3/8."}}]}]}]},"fisiese-wetenskappe":{"id":"fisiese-wetenskappe","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Fisiese Wetenskappe","en":"Physical Sciences"},"short":{"af":"Fis Wet","en":"Phys Sci"},"icon":"⚛️","color":"#7c3aed","intro":{"af":"Fisiese Wetenskappe bestaan uit Fisika (beweging, golwe, elektrisiteit, energie) en Chemie (materie, die atoom, binding en chemiese reaksies). In November skryf jy twee vraestelle – Vraestel 1 Fisika en Vraestel 2 Chemie – wat die hele jaar se werk dek. Definisies, formules met eenhede en netjiese berekeninge is die sleutel.","en":"Physical Sciences consists of Physics (motion, waves, electricity, energy) and Chemistry (matter, the atom, bonding and chemical reactions). In November you write two papers – Paper 1 Physics and Paper 2 Chemistry – covering the whole year's work. Definitions, formulae with units and neat calculations are the key."},"examTips":[{"af":"Wys ALTYD jou bewerkings: formule → vervanging → antwoord met eenheid. Metodepunte red jou as die finale antwoord verkeerd is.","en":"ALWAYS show your working: formula → substitution → answer with unit. Method marks save you if the final answer is wrong."},{"af":"Kyk na die punte langs elke vraag: dit sê hoeveel stappe of feite die nasiener soek. Bestee ongeveer 1 minuut per punt.","en":"Look at the marks next to each question: they tell you how many steps or facts the marker wants. Spend about 1 minute per mark."},{"af":"Leer die DBE-definisies woord vir woord – die memo soek spesifieke sleutelwoorde, bv. 'verandering in posisie' vir verplasing.","en":"Learn the DBE definitions word for word – the memo looks for specific key words, e.g. 'change in position' for displacement."},{"af":"Skakel eers alle eenhede om na SI (km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹, g → kg, cm³ → dm³) voordat jy in 'n formule vervang.","en":"Convert all units to SI first (km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹, g → kg, cm³ → dm³) before substituting into a formula."},{"af":"Gee by vektore altyd die rigting saam met die grootte, bv. 12 m·s⁻¹ oos of 3 m noord.","en":"For vectors always give the direction with the magnitude, e.g. 12 m·s⁻¹ east or 3 m north."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Siyavula: Alles Wetenskap Graad 10 (Afrikaans)","en":"Siyavula: Everything Science Grade 10 (Afrikaans)"},"url":"https://wcedeportal.co.za/eresource/76266","note":{"af":"Gratis, volledige CAPS-handboek vir Fisiese Wetenskappe met uitgewerkte voorbeelde.","en":"Free, complete CAPS Physical Sciences textbook with worked examples."}},{"title":{"af":"Noordwes Onderwysdepartement: vraestelle en memo's","en":"North West Department of Education: papers and memos"},"url":"https://education.nwpg.gov.za/?page_id=4644","note":{"af":"Provinsiale Graad 10-Novembervraestelle (ook Fisiese Wetenskappe V1 in Afrikaans) met memorandums.","en":"Provincial Grade 10 November papers (incl. Physical Sciences P1 in Afrikaans) with memos."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Fisiese Wetenskappe: twee vraestelle\n\n**Vraestel 1 (Fisika) en Vraestel 2 (Chemie): 100 punte elk, 2 uur elk** volgens die nuutste DBE-riglyne (*sommige skole gebruik nog 150 punte – bevestig met die 2026-afbakening*). Elke vraestel begin met **meervoudige keuse**, gevolg deur gestruktureerde vrae. Jy kry 'n gegewensblad en mag 'n sakrekenaar gebruik.\n\n| Vraestel 1: Fisika | ±Punte | Vraestel 2: Chemie | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Meganika (vektore, beweging, bewegingsvergelykings) | 45 | Materie en materiale (klassifikasie, KMT, atoom, periodieke tabel, binding) | 50 |\n| Golwe, klank en lig | 25 | Chemiese verandering (fisies/chemies, vergelykings, waterige oplossings, molbegrip) | 50 |\n| Elektrisiteit en magnetisme | 30 | | |\n\n### Wenke vir hierdie vraestelle\n\n1. Definisies is maklike punte – leer dit presies.\n2. Skryf by elke berekening die formule, die vervanging en die antwoord **met eenheid**.\n3. Lees grafiekvrae twee keer: vra hulle die gradiënt of die oppervlakte onder die grafiek?\n4. By meervoudige keuse: elimineer eers die duidelik verkeerde opsies.","en":"## Physical Sciences: two papers\n\n**Paper 1 (Physics) and Paper 2 (Chemistry): 100 marks each, 2 hours each** according to the latest DBE guidelines (*some schools still use 150 marks – confirm with the 2026 scope*). Each paper starts with **multiple choice**, followed by structured questions. You get a data sheet and may use a calculator.\n\n| Paper 1: Physics | ±Marks | Paper 2: Chemistry | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mechanics (vectors, motion, equations of motion) | 45 | Matter and materials (classification, KMT, atom, periodic table, bonding) | 50 |\n| Waves, sound and light | 25 | Chemical change (physical/chemical, equations, aqueous solutions, mole concept) | 50 |\n| Electricity and magnetism | 30 | | |\n\n### Tips for these papers\n\n1. Definitions are easy marks – learn them exactly.\n2. For every calculation write the formula, the substitution and the answer **with its unit**.\n3. Read graph questions twice: do they ask for the gradient or the area under the graph?\n4. In multiple choice: first eliminate the clearly wrong options."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Materie en materiale; golwe, klank en lig","en":"Matter and materials; waves, sound and light"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t1-klassifikasie-materie","title":{"af":"Klassifikasie van materie","en":"Classification of matter"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal materie as mengsels of suiwer stowwe kan klassifiseer, name en formules van verbindings kan skryf, stowwe volgens hul eienskappe kan groepeer en die regte skeidingsmetode kan kies.","en":"You will be able to classify matter as mixtures or pure substances, write names and formulae of compounds, group substances by their properties and choose the right separation method."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is materie?\n\n**Materie** is enigiets wat massa het en ruimte (volume) beslaan. Alles om jou – die water in Hartbeespoortdam, die lug, jou rugbybal – is materie en bestaan uit klein deeltjies (atome, molekules of ione). Ons klassifiseer materie volgens sy **samestelling** en sy **eienskappe**.\n\n## Mengsels en suiwer stowwe\n\n| Materie | Soorte | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mengsel | homogeen, heterogeen | lug, soutwater, sand en water |\n| Suiwer stof | element, verbinding | koper (Cu), water (H_{2}O) |\n\n- **Mengsel:** 'n kombinasie van twee of meer stowwe wat nie chemies aan mekaar gebind is nie. Die samestelling kan wissel, elke komponent behou sy eie eienskappe, en die komponente kan met **fisiese metodes** geskei word.\n- **Heterogene mengsel:** nie eenvormig nie; die verskillende komponente kan gesien word, bv. sand en water, olie en water, modderwater uit die Krokodilrivier.\n- **Homogene mengsel:** eenvormig deurgaans; die komponente kan nie gesien word nie, bv. soutwater, lug, koeldrank en **legerings** soos geelkoper (koper + sink) en staal. 'n **Oplossing** is 'n homogene mengsel van 'n opgeloste stof in 'n oplosmiddel.\n- **Suiwer stof:** materie wat nie deur enige fisiese proses in ander soorte materie geskei kan word nie. Dit het 'n vaste samestelling en 'n skerp, vaste smelt- en kookpunt. ('n Mengsel smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied.)\n- **Element:** 'n stof wat nie deur chemiese metodes in eenvoudiger stowwe afgebreek kan word nie. Dit bestaan uit net een soort atoom, bv. Fe, Cu, O_{2}, N_{2}. Daar is 118 elemente op die periodieke tabel.\n- **Verbinding:** 'n stof wat uit twee of meer verskillende elemente bestaan wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is, bv. H_{2}O, NaCl, CO_{2}. Dit kan net met **chemiese metodes** geskei word (bv. elektrolise van water).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** O_{2} is 'n **element** (net suurstofatome), nie 'n verbinding nie. Lug is 'n **mengsel**. Kraanwater is 'n homogene mengsel (opgeloste soute en chloor); net suiwer, gedistilleerde water is 'n verbinding. Moenie Co (kobalt, element) en CO (koolstofmonoksied, verbinding) verwar nie.\n\n## Name en formules\n\n1. Die metaal (positiewe ioon) word eerste genoem: NaCl = natriumchloried.\n2. 'n Enkel nie-metaal-ioon kry die uitgang **-ied**: oksied (O^{2−}), chloried (Cl^{−}), sulfied (S^{2−}).\n3. By twee nie-metale wys voorvoegsels die aantal atome (mono-, di-, tri-, tetra-): CO = koolstofmonoksied, CO_{2} = koolstofdioksied, SO_{3} = swaweltrioksied.\n4. By oorgangsmetale wys 'n Romeinse syfer die lading: Fe_{2}O_{3} = yster(III)oksied, CuSO_{4} = koper(II)sulfaat.\n\n| Ioon | Formule | Ioon | Formule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ammonium | NH_{4}^{+} | karbonaat | CO_{3}^{2−} |\n| hidroksied | OH^{−} | sulfaat | SO_{4}^{2−} |\n| nitraat | NO_{3}^{−} | fosfaat | PO_{4}^{3−} |\n\nAl hierdie -aat-ione bevat suurstof. Let op: hidroksied eindig op -ied, maar is 'n saamgestelde ioon.\n\n**Formule skryf:** balanseer die ladings sodat die totaal nul is. Aluminiumsulfaat: Al^{3+} en SO_{4}^{2−} → 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6, dus Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}. Sit hakies om 'n saamgestelde ioon as daar meer as een is: Ca(OH)_{2}, nie CaOH_{2} nie. Die getal buite die hakie vermenigvuldig alles binne: Ca(NO_{3})_{2} bevat 1 Ca, 2 N en 6 O = 9 atome.\n\nKen ook: NH_{3} (ammoniak), CH_{4} (metaan), HCl (waterstofchloried), H_{2}SO_{4} (swawelsuur), NaOH (natriumhidroksied), CaCO_{3} (kalsiumkarbonaat).\n\n## Metale, nie-metale en metalloïede\n\n- **Metale** (links en in die middel van die periodieke tabel): blink, goeie geleiers van elektrisiteit en hitte, smeebaar (kan plat geslaan word) en rekbaar (kan in drade getrek word). Almal is vaste stowwe by kamertemperatuur, behalwe kwik.\n- **Nie-metale** (regs): meestal dof, swak geleiers (isolators), bros as vaste stof; baie is gasse. Uitsondering: **grafiet** (koolstof) gelei elektrisiteit.\n- **Metalloïede** (langs die trapvormige lyn, bv. B, Si, Ge, As): lyk dikwels blink soos 'n metaal, maar is bros. Hulle is **halfgeleiers** – hul elektriese geleidingsvermoë **neem toe** as die temperatuur styg (by metale neem dit af). Silikon word in rekenaarskyfies en sonpanele gebruik.\n\n## Geleiers, isolators en magnetisme\n\n- **Elektriese geleier:** laat 'n elektriese stroom deur, bv. koper, yster, grafiet, soutwater. **Elektriese isolator:** laat nie stroom deur nie, bv. plastiek, rubber, hout, glas. Daarom is koperdrade met plastiek bedek. Toets: plaas die materiaal in 'n stroombaan met 'n sel en 'n gloeilamp – brand die gloeilamp, is dit 'n geleier.\n- **Termiese geleier:** gelei hitte goed (metale: braairooster, kastrol). **Termiese isolator:** gelei hitte swak (hout, plastiek, wol, lug, polistireen) – daarom het 'n braaitang hout- of plastiekhandvatsels.\n- **Magnetiese materiale** word deur 'n magneet aangetrek: yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt. Die meeste ander metale (koper, aluminium, sink, goud, silwer) is **nie-magneties**.\n\n## Skeidingsmetodes (fisies)\n\n| Metode | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filtrasie | onoplosbare vaste stof uit 'n vloeistof | sand uit water (sand = **residu**, vloeistof = **filtraat**) |\n| Verdamping | opgeloste vaste stof terugkry | sout uit seewater |\n| Distillasie | vloeistof uit 'n oplossing, of vloeistowwe met verskillende kookpunte | suiwer water uit seewater |\n| Kristallisasie | kristalle uit 'n versadigde oplossing | suikerkristalle |\n| Magnetiese skeiding | magnetiese van nie-magnetiese stof | ystervylsels uit swawel |\n| Skeitregter | vloeistowwe wat nie meng nie | olie en water |\n| Papierchromatografie | opgeloste kleurstowwe | kleure in ink |\n\n> **Wenk:** Kies die metode volgens die eienskap wat verskil: deeltjiegrootte, oplosbaarheid, kookpunt of magnetisme.","en":"## What is matter?\n\n**Matter** is anything that has mass and takes up space (volume). Everything around you – the water in Hartbeespoort Dam, the air, your rugby ball – is matter and is made of tiny particles (atoms, molecules or ions). We classify matter according to its **composition** and its **properties**.\n\n## Mixtures and pure substances\n\n| Matter | Kinds | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mixture | homogeneous, heterogeneous | air, salt water, sand and water |\n| Pure substance | element, compound | copper (Cu), water (H_{2}O) |\n\n- **Mixture:** a combination of two or more substances that are not chemically bonded to each other. The composition can vary, each component keeps its own properties, and the components can be separated by **physical methods**.\n- **Heterogeneous mixture:** not uniform; the different components can be seen, e.g. sand and water, oil and water, muddy water from the Crocodile River.\n- **Homogeneous mixture:** uniform throughout; the components cannot be seen, e.g. salt water, air, cool drink and **alloys** such as brass (copper + zinc) and steel. A **solution** is a homogeneous mixture of a solute dissolved in a solvent.\n- **Pure substance:** matter that cannot be separated into other kinds of matter by any physical process. It has a fixed composition and a sharp, fixed melting and boiling point. (A mixture melts over a range of temperatures.)\n- **Element:** a substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means. It consists of only one kind of atom, e.g. Fe, Cu, O_{2}, N_{2}. There are 118 elements on the periodic table.\n- **Compound:** a substance made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded in a fixed ratio, e.g. H_{2}O, NaCl, CO_{2}. It can only be separated by **chemical methods** (e.g. electrolysis of water).\n\n> **Common mistake:** O_{2} is an **element** (only oxygen atoms), not a compound. Air is a **mixture**. Tap water is a homogeneous mixture (dissolved salts and chlorine); only pure, distilled water is a compound. Do not confuse Co (cobalt, element) with CO (carbon monoxide, compound).\n\n## Names and formulae\n\n1. The metal (positive ion) is named first: NaCl = sodium chloride.\n2. A single non-metal ion gets the ending **-ide**: oxide (O^{2−}), chloride (Cl^{−}), sulfide (S^{2−}).\n3. For two non-metals, prefixes show the number of atoms (mono-, di-, tri-, tetra-): CO = carbon monoxide, CO_{2} = carbon dioxide, SO_{3} = sulfur trioxide.\n4. For transition metals, a Roman numeral shows the charge: Fe_{2}O_{3} = iron(III) oxide, CuSO_{4} = copper(II) sulfate.\n\n| Ion | Formula | Ion | Formula |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ammonium | NH_{4}^{+} | carbonate | CO_{3}^{2−} |\n| hydroxide | OH^{−} | sulfate | SO_{4}^{2−} |\n| nitrate | NO_{3}^{−} | phosphate | PO_{4}^{3−} |\n\nAll these -ate ions contain oxygen. Note: hydroxide ends in -ide, but it is a polyatomic ion.\n\n**Writing a formula:** balance the charges so that the total is zero. Aluminium sulfate: Al^{3+} and SO_{4}^{2−} → 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6, so Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}. Put brackets around a polyatomic ion when there is more than one: Ca(OH)_{2}, not CaOH_{2}. The number outside the bracket multiplies everything inside: Ca(NO_{3})_{2} contains 1 Ca, 2 N and 6 O = 9 atoms.\n\nAlso know: NH_{3} (ammonia), CH_{4} (methane), HCl (hydrogen chloride), H_{2}SO_{4} (sulfuric acid), NaOH (sodium hydroxide), CaCO_{3} (calcium carbonate).\n\n## Metals, non-metals and metalloids\n\n- **Metals** (left and middle of the periodic table): shiny, good conductors of electricity and heat, malleable (can be hammered flat) and ductile (can be drawn into wires). All are solids at room temperature, except mercury.\n- **Non-metals** (right): mostly dull, poor conductors (insulators), brittle as solids; many are gases. Exception: **graphite** (carbon) conducts electricity.\n- **Metalloids** (along the staircase line, e.g. B, Si, Ge, As): often look shiny like a metal, but are brittle. They are **semiconductors** – their electrical conductivity **increases** as the temperature rises (in metals it decreases). Silicon is used in computer chips and solar panels.\n\n## Conductors, insulators and magnetism\n\n- **Electrical conductor:** allows an electric current to pass through, e.g. copper, iron, graphite, salt water. **Electrical insulator:** does not allow current through, e.g. plastic, rubber, wood, glass. That is why copper wires are covered in plastic. Test: put the material in a circuit with a cell and a light bulb – if the bulb glows, it is a conductor.\n- **Thermal conductor:** conducts heat well (metals: braai grid, pot). **Thermal insulator:** conducts heat poorly (wood, plastic, wool, air, polystyrene) – that is why braai tongs have wooden or plastic handles.\n- **Magnetic materials** are attracted by a magnet: iron, steel, nickel and cobalt. Most other metals (copper, aluminium, zinc, gold, silver) are **non-magnetic**.\n\n## Separation methods (physical)\n\n| Method | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filtration | insoluble solid from a liquid | sand from water (sand = **residue**, liquid = **filtrate**) |\n| Evaporation | recover a dissolved solid | salt from sea water |\n| Distillation | liquid from a solution, or liquids with different boiling points | pure water from sea water |\n| Crystallisation | crystals from a saturated solution | sugar crystals |\n| Magnetic separation | magnetic from non-magnetic substance | iron filings from sulfur |\n| Separating funnel | liquids that do not mix | oil and water |\n| Paper chromatography | dissolved dyes | colours in ink |\n\n> **Tip:** Choose the method according to the property that differs: particle size, solubility, boiling point or magnetism."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mengsel","en":"Mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Kombinasie van twee of meer stowwe wat nie chemies aan mekaar gebind is nie; dit kan met fisiese metodes geskei word.","en":"A combination of two or more substances that are not chemically bonded to each other; it can be separated by physical methods."}},{"term":{"af":"Heterogene mengsel","en":"Heterogeneous mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel wat nie eenvormig is nie en waarin die verskillende komponente gesien kan word.","en":"A mixture that is not uniform and in which the different components can be seen."}},{"term":{"af":"Homogene mengsel","en":"Homogeneous mixture"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel wat eenvormig is deurgaans en waarin die verskillende komponente nie gesien kan word nie.","en":"A mixture that is uniform throughout and in which the different components cannot be seen."}},{"term":{"af":"Suiwer stof","en":"Pure substance"},"def":{"af":"Materie wat nie deur enige fisiese proses in ander soorte materie geskei kan word nie.","en":"Matter that cannot be separated into other kinds of matter by any physical process."}},{"term":{"af":"Element","en":"Element"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat nie deur chemiese metodes in eenvoudiger stowwe afgebreek kan word nie.","en":"A substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbinding","en":"Compound"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat uit twee of meer verskillende elemente bestaan wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is.","en":"A substance made up of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded in a fixed ratio."}},{"term":{"af":"Metalloïed","en":"Metalloid"},"def":{"af":"'n Element met eienskappe van sowel metale as nie-metale; 'n halfgeleier waarvan die elektriese geleidingsvermoë toeneem as die temperatuur styg.","en":"An element with properties of both metals and non-metals; a semiconductor whose electrical conductivity increases as the temperature rises."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektriese geleier","en":"Electrical conductor"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat 'n elektriese stroom deur hom laat vloei, bv. koper of grafiet.","en":"A substance that allows an electric current to flow through it, e.g. copper or graphite."}},{"term":{"af":"Termiese isolator","en":"Thermal insulator"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat nie toelaat dat hitte maklik deur hom oorgedra word nie, bv. hout, plastiek of lug.","en":"A substance that does not allow heat to be transferred through it easily, e.g. wood, plastic or air."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese materiaal","en":"Magnetic material"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal wat deur 'n magneet aangetrek word, bv. yster, staal, nikkel en kobalt.","en":"A material that is attracted by a magnet, e.g. iron, steel, nickel and cobalt."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer stowwe","en":"Classify substances"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elk van die volgende as 'n element, 'n verbinding, 'n homogene mengsel of 'n heterogene mengsel: (a) koper, (b) gedistilleerde water, (c) lug, (d) geelkoper, (e) modderwater uit die Krokodilrivier, (f) koolstofdioksied.","en":"Classify each of the following as an element, a compound, a homogeneous mixture or a heterogeneous mixture: (a) copper, (b) distilled water, (c) air, (d) brass, (e) muddy water from the Crocodile River, (f) carbon dioxide."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers: is dit een stof met 'n vaste samestelling (suiwer stof), of meer as een stof wat nie chemies gebind is nie (mengsel)?","en":"First ask: is it one substance with a fixed composition (pure substance), or more than one substance that is not chemically bonded (mixture)?"},{"af":"(a) Koper (Cu) bestaan net uit koperatome → **element**. (b) Gedistilleerde water (H_{2}O) en (f) koolstofdioksied (CO_{2}) bestaan elk uit twee elemente wat in 'n vaste verhouding chemies gebind is → **verbindings**.","en":"(a) Copper (Cu) consists only of copper atoms → **element**. (b) Distilled water (H_{2}O) and (f) carbon dioxide (CO_{2}) each consist of two elements chemically bonded in a fixed ratio → **compounds**."},{"af":"(c) Lug is stikstof, suurstof, argon, koolstofdioksied en waterdamp wat nie chemies gebind is nie, en jy kan die komponente nie sien nie → **homogene mengsel**. (d) Geelkoper is 'n legering van koper en sink wat eenvormig deurgaans is → **homogene mengsel**.","en":"(c) Air is nitrogen, oxygen, argon, carbon dioxide and water vapour that are not chemically bonded, and you cannot see the components → **homogeneous mixture**. (d) Brass is an alloy of copper and zinc that is uniform throughout → **homogeneous mixture**."},{"af":"(e) In modderwater sien jy die gronddeeltjies, en hulle sak later uit – dit is nie eenvormig nie → **heterogene mengsel**.","en":"(e) In muddy water you can see the soil particles, and they settle out later – it is not uniform → **heterogeneous mixture**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) element (b) verbinding (c) homogene mengsel (d) homogene mengsel (e) heterogene mengsel (f) verbinding","en":"(a) element (b) compound (c) homogeneous mixture (d) homogeneous mixture (e) heterogeneous mixture (f) compound"}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf formules en name","en":"Write formulae and names"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die chemiese formule van (a) kalsiumnitraat, (b) aluminiumsulfaat en (c) ammoniumkarbonaat. Gee dan (d) die naam van Na₂SO₄.","en":"Write the chemical formula of (a) calcium nitrate, (b) aluminium sulfate and (c) ammonium carbonate. Then give (d) the name of Na₂SO₄."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ione: Ca^{2+} en NO_{3}^{−}. Twee NO_{3}^{−} (totaal −2) balanseer een Ca^{2+} (+2), en die nitraat kry hakies → Ca(NO_{3})_{2}","en":"(a) Ions: Ca^{2+} and NO_{3}^{−}. Two NO_{3}^{−} (total −2) balance one Ca^{2+} (+2), and the nitrate gets brackets → Ca(NO_{3})_{2}"},{"af":"(b) Ione: Al^{3+} en SO_{4}^{2−}. Die KGV van 3 en 2 is 6: 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6 → Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}","en":"(b) Ions: Al^{3+} and SO_{4}^{2−}. The LCM of 3 and 2 is 6: 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6 → Al_{2}(SO_{4})_{3}"},{"af":"(c) Ione: NH_{4}^{+} en CO_{3}^{2−}. Twee NH_{4}^{+} (+2) balanseer een CO_{3}^{2−} (−2) → (NH_{4})_{2}CO_{3}","en":"(c) Ions: NH_{4}^{+} and CO_{3}^{2−}. Two NH_{4}^{+} (+2) balance one CO_{3}^{2−} (−2) → (NH_{4})_{2}CO_{3}"},{"af":"(d) Na_{2}SO_{4} bevat Na^{+} en SO_{4}^{2−}. Noem die metaal eerste en behou die naam van die saamgestelde ioon → natriumsulfaat","en":"(d) Na_{2}SO_{4} contains Na^{+} and SO_{4}^{2−}. Name the metal first and keep the name of the polyatomic ion → sodium sulfate"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ca(NO₃)₂ (b) Al₂(SO₄)₃ (c) (NH₄)₂CO₃ (d) natriumsulfaat","en":"(a) Ca(NO₃)₂ (b) Al₂(SO₄)₃ (c) (NH₄)₂CO₃ (d) sodium sulfate"}},{"title":{"af":"Skei 'n mengsel van drie stowwe","en":"Separate a mixture of three substances"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder mors sand, sout en ystervylsels in een bak. Beskryf, met redes, hoe sy al drie stowwe afsonderlik kan terugkry.","en":"A learner spills sand, salt and iron filings into one bowl. Describe, with reasons, how she can recover all three substances separately."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik 'n **magneet**: ystervylsels is magneties en word uitgetrek. Sand en sout is nie-magneties en bly agter.","en":"Use a **magnet**: iron filings are magnetic and are pulled out. Sand and salt are non-magnetic and stay behind."},{"af":"Gooi water by die sand-en-sout en roer: die sout **los op**, maar die sand los nie op nie.","en":"Add water to the sand and salt and stir: the salt **dissolves**, but the sand does not."},{"af":"**Filtreer** die mengsel: die sand bly as **residu** in die filtreerpapier, en die soutoplossing loop deur as **filtraat**.","en":"**Filter** the mixture: the sand stays behind as the **residue** in the filter paper, and the salt solution runs through as the **filtrate**."},{"af":"**Verdamp** die filtraat in 'n verdampingsbak: die water verdamp en die sout bly agter.","en":"**Evaporate** the filtrate in an evaporating dish: the water evaporates and the salt stays behind."}],"answer":{"af":"Magneet (yster) → oplos in water → filtrasie (sand) → verdamping (sout)","en":"Magnet (iron) → dissolve in water → filtration (sand) → evaporation (salt)"}},{"title":{"af":"Ondersoek: geleiers en isolators","en":"Investigation: conductors and insulators"},"problem":{"af":"Leerders bou 'n stroombaan met 'n sel, 'n gloeilamp en twee krokodilknippies. Hulle plaas ewe lang stawe van koper, yster, glas, hout en grafiet (potloodlood) een vir een tussen die knippies. Die gloeilamp brand by koper, yster en grafiet, maar nie by glas en hout nie. (a) Noem die onafhanklike en afhanklike veranderlike. (b) Klassifiseer die materiale. (c) Watter resultaat is verrassend, en hoekom?","en":"Learners build a circuit with a cell, a light bulb and two crocodile clips. They place rods of equal length made of copper, iron, glass, wood and graphite (pencil lead) one at a time between the clips. The bulb glows for copper, iron and graphite, but not for glass and wood. (a) Name the independent and dependent variable. (b) Classify the materials. (c) Which result is surprising, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die **onafhanklike veranderlike** is wat die leerders self verander: die tipe materiaal. Die **afhanklike veranderlike** is wat hulle waarneem: of die gloeilamp brand (die elektriese geleidingsvermoë). Gekontroleerd: dieselfde sel, gloeilamp en staaflengte.","en":"(a) The **independent variable** is what the learners change themselves: the type of material. The **dependent variable** is what they observe: whether the bulb glows (the electrical conductivity). Controlled: the same cell, bulb and rod length."},{"af":"(b) Gloeilamp brand → stroom vloei → **geleiers**: koper, yster en grafiet. Gloeilamp brand nie → **isolators**: glas en hout.","en":"(b) Bulb glows → current flows → **conductors**: copper, iron and graphite. Bulb does not glow → **insulators**: glass and wood."},{"af":"(c) **Grafiet** is koolstof, 'n nie-metaal, maar dit gelei tog elektrisiteit. Dit is die bekende uitsondering op die reël dat nie-metale isolators is.","en":"(c) **Graphite** is carbon, a non-metal, yet it conducts electricity. It is the well-known exception to the rule that non-metals are insulators."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Onafhanklik: tipe materiaal; afhanklik: of die gloeilamp brand. (b) Geleiers: koper, yster, grafiet; isolators: glas, hout. (c) Grafiet – 'n nie-metaal wat gelei.","en":"(a) Independent: type of material; dependent: whether the bulb glows. (b) Conductors: copper, iron, graphite; insulators: glass, wood. (c) Graphite – a non-metal that conducts."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n heterogene mengsel?","en":"Which one of the following is a heterogeneous mixture?"},"options":[{"af":"Sand en water","en":"Sand and water"},{"af":"Soutwater","en":"Salt water"},{"af":"Lug","en":"Air"},{"af":"Geelkoper","en":"Brass"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In sand en water kan jy die twee komponente sien, en die sand sak uit – dit is nie eenvormig nie. Soutwater, lug en geelkoper (koper + sink) is eenvormig deurgaans: dit is homogene mengsels.","en":"In sand and water you can see the two components, and the sand settles out – it is not uniform. Salt water, air and brass (copper + zinc) are uniform throughout: they are homogeneous mixtures."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Lug is 'n verbinding van stikstof en suurstof.","en":"Air is a compound of nitrogen and oxygen."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Lug is 'n homogene mengsel: die gasse (hoofsaaklik N₂ en O₂, met bietjie Ar, CO₂ en waterdamp) is nie chemies gebind nie, en die samestelling kan wissel.","en":"False. Air is a homogeneous mixture: the gases (mainly N₂ and O₂, with a little Ar, CO₂ and water vapour) are not chemically bonded, and the composition can vary."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ioon CO₃²⁻ word die ___-ioon genoem.","en":"The ion CO₃²⁻ is called the ___ ion."},"answers":{"af":["karbonaat","karbonaatioon","karbonaat-ioon"],"en":["carbonate","carbonate ion","carbonate-ion"]},"explain":{"af":"CO₃²⁻ is die karbonaat-ioon. Dit bevat suurstof, daarom eindig die naam op -aat, bv. kalsiumkarbonaat (CaCO₃, kalksteen).","en":"CO₃²⁻ is the carbonate ion. It contains oxygen, which is why the name ends in -ate, e.g. calcium carbonate (CaCO₃, limestone)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["karbied","karboniet","bikarbonaat"],"en":["carbide","carbonite","bicarbonate"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ioon by sy formule.","en":"Match each ion to its formula."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ammonium","en":"Ammonium"},"r":{"af":"NH₄⁺","en":"NH₄⁺"}},{"l":{"af":"Hidroksied","en":"Hydroxide"},"r":{"af":"OH⁻","en":"OH⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Nitraat","en":"Nitrate"},"r":{"af":"NO₃⁻","en":"NO₃⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Sulfaat","en":"Sulfate"},"r":{"af":"SO₄²⁻","en":"SO₄²⁻"}},{"l":{"af":"Fosfaat","en":"Phosphate"},"r":{"af":"PO₄³⁻","en":"PO₄³⁻"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ammonium NH₄⁺ is die enigste positiewe saamgestelde ioon hier. Hidroksied OH⁻ en nitraat NO₃⁻ het 'n lading van −1, sulfaat SO₄²⁻ −2 en fosfaat PO₄³⁻ −3.","en":"Ammonium NH₄⁺ is the only positive polyatomic ion here. Hydroxide OH⁻ and nitrate NO₃⁻ have a charge of −1, sulfate SO₄²⁻ −2 and phosphate PO₄³⁻ −3."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Grafiet is 'n nie-metaal wat elektrisiteit gelei.","en":"Graphite is a non-metal that conducts electricity."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Grafiet is 'n vorm van koolstof ('n nie-metaal), maar dit gelei elektrisiteit – die bekende uitsondering op die reël dat nie-metale isolators is. Daarom kan potloodlood 'n gloeilamp laat brand.","en":"True. Graphite is a form of carbon (a non-metal), yet it conducts electricity – the well-known exception to the rule that non-metals are insulators. That is why pencil lead can make a bulb glow."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom het 'n braaitang gewoonlik hout- of plastiekhandvatsels?","en":"Why do braai tongs usually have wooden or plastic handles?"},"options":[{"af":"Hout en plastiek is goeie termiese geleiers.","en":"Wood and plastic are good thermal conductors."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is nie-magneties.","en":"Wood and plastic are non-magnetic."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is termiese isolators, so hitte bereik nie maklik jou hand nie.","en":"Wood and plastic are thermal insulators, so heat does not easily reach your hand."},{"af":"Hout en plastiek is elektriese geleiers.","en":"Wood and plastic are electrical conductors."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die metaal van die tang word warm, want metale is goeie termiese geleiers. Hout en plastiek is termiese isolators: hulle gelei hitte swak, so jou hand bly koel. Magnetisme en elektriese geleiding het niks hiermee te doen nie.","en":"The metal of the tongs gets hot, because metals are good thermal conductors. Wood and plastic are thermal insulators: they conduct heat poorly, so your hand stays cool. Magnetism and electrical conduction have nothing to do with it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter metode gebruik jy om suiwer drinkwater uit seewater te kry?","en":"Which method do you use to obtain pure drinking water from sea water?"},"options":[{"af":"Filtrasie","en":"Filtration"},{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},{"af":"Papierchromatografie","en":"Paper chromatography"},{"af":"Distillasie","en":"Distillation"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By distillasie kook jy die seewater; die waterdamp kondenseer in 'n koeler en jy vang suiwer water op, terwyl die sout agterbly. Filtrasie werk nie, want die sout is opgelos en loop deur die filtreerpapier. Verdamping gee jou die sout, maar die water gaan verlore in die lug.","en":"In distillation you boil the sea water; the water vapour condenses in a condenser and you collect pure water, while the salt stays behind. Filtration does not work, because the salt is dissolved and passes through the filter paper. Evaporation gives you the salt, but the water is lost to the air."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die chemiese formule van kalsiumhidroksied: ___","en":"Write the chemical formula of calcium hydroxide: ___"},"answers":{"af":["Ca(OH)2","Ca(OH)₂"],"en":["Ca(OH)2","Ca(OH)₂"]},"explain":{"af":"Ca²⁺ het 'n lading van +2 en OH⁻ 'n lading van −1, dus is twee OH⁻-ione nodig: Ca(OH)₂. Die hakies is nodig – CaOH₂ sou beteken net een O en twee H.","en":"Ca²⁺ has a charge of +2 and OH⁻ a charge of −1, so two OH⁻ ions are needed: Ca(OH)₂. The brackets are necessary – CaOH₂ would mean only one O and two H."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["CaOH","CaOH2","Ca2OH"],"en":["CaOH","CaOH2","Ca2OH"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte formule van aluminiumsulfaat?","en":"What is the correct formula of aluminium sulfate?"},"options":[{"af":"AlSO₄","en":"AlSO₄"},{"af":"Al₂(SO₄)₃","en":"Al₂(SO₄)₃"},{"af":"Al₃(SO₄)₂","en":"Al₃(SO₄)₂"},{"af":"Al₂SO₄","en":"Al₂SO₄"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Al³⁺ en SO₄²⁻: 2 × (+3) = +6 en 3 × (−2) = −6, dus is die totaal nul: Al₂(SO₄)₃. AlSO₄ ignoreer die ladings, Al₃(SO₄)₂ ruil die getalle verkeerd om, en Al₂SO₄ is nie neutraal nie (+6 − 2 = +4).","en":"Al³⁺ and SO₄²⁻: 2 × (+3) = +6 and 3 × (−2) = −6, so the total is zero: Al₂(SO₄)₃. AlSO₄ ignores the charges, Al₃(SO₄)₂ swaps the numbers the wrong way round, and Al₂SO₄ is not neutral (+6 − 2 = +4)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die chemiese naam van Mg(NO₃)₂: ___","en":"Give the chemical name of Mg(NO₃)₂: ___"},"answers":{"af":["magnesiumnitraat","magnesium nitraat","magnesium-nitraat"],"en":["magnesium nitrate","magnesiumnitrate","magnesium-nitrate"]},"explain":{"af":"Die metaal (magnesium, Mg²⁺) word eerste genoem, gevolg deur die naam van die saamgestelde ioon (nitraat, NO₃⁻): magnesiumnitraat. Twee NO₃⁻-ione balanseer die +2-lading.","en":"The metal (magnesium, Mg²⁺) is named first, followed by the name of the polyatomic ion (nitrate, NO₃⁻): magnesium nitrate. Two NO₃⁻ ions balance the +2 charge."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["magnesiumnitriet","magnesiumnitried","mangaannitraat"],"en":["magnesium nitrite","magnesium nitride","manganese nitrate"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel atome in totaal is daar in een formule-eenheid ammoniumkarbonaat, (NH₄)₂CO₃? ___","en":"How many atoms in total are there in one formula unit of ammonium carbonate, (NH₄)₂CO₃? ___"},"answers":{"af":["14","14 atome"],"en":["14","14 atoms"]},"explain":{"af":"Die 2 buite die hakie vermenigvuldig alles binne: 2 N en 2 × 4 = 8 H. Daarby kom 1 C en 3 O. Totaal: 2 + 8 + 1 + 3 = 14 atome. 'n Algemene fout is om net 1 N en 4 H te tel (9 atome).","en":"The 2 outside the bracket multiplies everything inside: 2 N and 2 × 4 = 8 H. Add 1 C and 3 O. Total: 2 + 8 + 1 + 3 = 14 atoms. A common mistake is to count only 1 N and 4 H (9 atoms)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["9","18","4"],"en":["9","18","4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee wit vaste stowwe word stadig verhit. Stof P smelt presies by 801 °C. Stof Q begin by 150 °C smelt en is eers by 180 °C heeltemal gesmelt. Watter gevolgtrekking is korrek?","en":"Two white solids are heated slowly. Substance P melts at exactly 801 °C. Substance Q starts melting at 150 °C and has only melted completely at 180 °C. Which conclusion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"P is 'n mengsel en Q is 'n suiwer stof.","en":"P is a mixture and Q is a pure substance."},{"af":"Albei is suiwer stowwe, want albei smelt.","en":"Both are pure substances, because both melt."},{"af":"Albei is mengsels, want albei is wit vaste stowwe.","en":"Both are mixtures, because both are white solids."},{"af":"P is 'n suiwer stof en Q is 'n mengsel.","en":"P is a pure substance and Q is a mixture."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Suiwer stof het 'n skerp, vaste smeltpunt (P: presies 801 °C – dit is die smeltpunt van suiwer natriumchloried). 'n Mengsel smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied (Q: 150–180 °C). Die kleur sê niks oor suiwerheid nie.","en":"A pure substance has a sharp, fixed melting point (P: exactly 801 °C – the melting point of pure sodium chloride). A mixture melts over a range of temperatures (Q: 150–180 °C). The colour tells you nothing about purity."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Element X is 'n blink, bros vaste stof. Sy elektriese geleidingsvermoë neem toe wanneer dit verhit word. Watter element is X waarskynlik?","en":"Element X is a shiny, brittle solid. Its electrical conductivity increases when it is heated. Which element is X most likely?"},"options":[{"af":"Silikon","en":"Silicon"},{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},{"af":"Swawel","en":"Sulfur"},{"af":"Yster","en":"Iron"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Silikon is 'n metalloïed: dit lyk blink, maar is bros, en as halfgeleier neem sy geleidingsvermoë toe met temperatuur. Koper en yster is metale: smeebaar (nie bros nie), en hul geleidingsvermoë neem áf as hulle warmer word. Swawel is 'n dowwe nie-metaal en 'n isolator.","en":"Silicon is a metalloid: it looks shiny but is brittle, and as a semiconductor its conductivity increases with temperature. Copper and iron are metals: malleable (not brittle), and their conductivity decreases as they get hotter. Sulfur is a dull non-metal and an insulator."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: \"Die kraanwater in ons huis in Brits is 'n suiwer stof, want dit is helder en jy kan niks anders daarin sien nie.\" Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Thabo says: \"The tap water in our house in Brits is a pure substance, because it is clear and you cannot see anything else in it.\" Which statement best evaluates his claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: as jy niks anders kan sien nie, is dit suiwer.","en":"He is right: if you cannot see anything else, it is pure."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: kraanwater bevat opgeloste soute en chloor, dus is dit 'n homogene mengsel.","en":"He is wrong: tap water contains dissolved salts and chlorine, so it is a homogeneous mixture."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: kraanwater is 'n heterogene mengsel, want dit bevat opgeloste stowwe.","en":"He is wrong: tap water is a heterogeneous mixture, because it contains dissolved substances."},{"af":"Hy is reg: water is 'n verbinding, dus is alle water 'n suiwer stof.","en":"He is right: water is a compound, so all water is a pure substance."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Helder beteken net dat die mengsel eenvormig is – opgeloste stowwe is onsigbaar. Kraanwater bevat opgeloste soute (ione) en chloor wat by die suiweringsaanleg bygevoeg word, dus is dit 'n homogene (nie heterogene) mengsel. Net gedistilleerde water is suiwer H₂O.","en":"Clear only means the mixture is uniform – dissolved substances are invisible. Tap water contains dissolved salts (ions) and chlorine added at the purification plant, so it is a homogeneous (not heterogeneous) mixture. Only distilled water is pure H₂O."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-toestande-kmt","title":{"af":"Toestande van materie en die kinetiese molekulêre teorie","en":"States of matter and the kinetic molecular theory"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die drie toestande van materie en faseveranderinge met die kinetiese molekulêre teorie kan verduidelik, verhittings- en afkoelingskurwes kan interpreteer, en diffusie en Brownbeweging kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to explain the three states of matter and phase changes with the kinetic molecular theory, interpret heating and cooling curves, and describe diffusion and Brownian motion."},"summary":{"af":"## Die drie toestande van materie\n\n| | Vaste stof | Vloeistof | Gas |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Vorm en volume | vaste vorm en volume | vaste volume; neem die vorm van die houer aan | geen vaste vorm of volume nie; vul die houer |\n| Rangskikking | dig gepak in 'n reëlmatige patroon | naby mekaar, maar ongeorden | ver uitmekaar, lukraak |\n| Beweging | vibreer om vaste posisies | gly by mekaar verby | beweeg vinnig in alle rigtings |\n| Kragte tussen deeltjies | sterk | swakker | baie swak |\n| Saamdrukbaar? | nee | amper nie | ja, maklik |\n\n## Die kinetiese molekulêre teorie (KMT)\n\nDie KMT verduidelik die eienskappe van materie met die beweging van deeltjies:\n\n1. Materie bestaan uit klein deeltjies (atome, molekules of ione) wat **voortdurend beweeg**.\n2. Daar is **ruimtes** tussen die deeltjies.\n3. Daar is **aantrekkingskragte** tussen die deeltjies; hulle is sterker hoe nader die deeltjies aan mekaar is.\n4. Alle deeltjies het energie. Deeltjies in 'n vaste stof het die minste energie en dié in 'n gas die meeste.\n5. Die **temperatuur** van 'n stof is 'n maatstaf van die **gemiddelde kinetiese energie** van sy deeltjies.\n6. 'n **Faseverandering** kan plaasvind wanneer die energie van die deeltjies verander.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Deeltjies word nie groter as 'n stof verhit word nie – hulle beweeg vinniger en die ruimtes tussen hulle word groter. Deeltjies in 'n vaste stof staan ook nie stil nie; hulle vibreer.\n\n## Faseveranderinge\n\n| Proses | Verandering | Energie |\n|---|---|---|\n| Smelt | vaste stof → vloeistof | geabsorbeer |\n| Verdamping / kook | vloeistof → gas | geabsorbeer |\n| Sublimasie | vaste stof → gas (direk) | geabsorbeer |\n| Vries (stolling) | vloeistof → vaste stof | vrygestel |\n| Kondensasie | gas → vloeistof | vrygestel |\n| Afsetting (resublimasie) | gas → vaste stof (direk) | vrygestel |\n\nVoorbeelde van sublimasie: jodium, droë ys (vaste CO_{2}) en mottebolle. Ryp op die gras is afsetting.\n\n- **Smeltpunt:** die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word. Vir 'n suiwer stof is die **vriespunt** dieselfde temperatuur.\n- **Kookpunt:** die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n gas te word.\n- **Verdamping teenoor kook:** verdamping gebeur by **enige** temperatuur, net aan die **oppervlak** – die vinnigste deeltjies ontsnap. Daarom koel sweet jou af. Kook gebeur by die kookpunt, **deur die hele vloeistof** (borrels vorm).\n- Hoe sterker die kragte tussen die deeltjies, hoe hoër die smelt- en kookpunt.\n\n**Toestand by 'n gegewe temperatuur T:** T laer as die smeltpunt → vaste stof; T tussen die smelt- en kookpunt → vloeistof; T hoër as die kookpunt → gas. Etanol (smeltpunt −114 °C, kookpunt 78 °C) is dus 'n vloeistof by 25 °C.\n\n## Die verhittingskurwe van water (in woorde)\n\nYs by −20 °C word teen 'n konstante tempo verhit, en die temperatuur word teen die tyd geplot:\n\n1. **Skuins lyn (−20 °C → 0 °C):** net ys. Die deeltjies vibreer vinniger; E_{k} en temperatuur styg.\n2. **Eerste plato (horisontaal by 0 °C):** die ys **smelt** – ys en water is saam teenwoordig. Die temperatuur bly konstant, want al die energie word gebruik om die **aantrekkingskragte tussen die deeltjies te oorkom**, nie om E_{k} te verhoog nie.\n3. **Skuins lyn (0 °C → 100 °C):** net vloeibare water; E_{k} styg.\n4. **Tweede plato (horisontaal by 100 °C):** die water **kook** – water en stoom is saam teenwoordig. Hierdie plato is baie **langer** as die eerste, want baie meer energie is nodig om die deeltjies heeltemal van mekaar te skei (gas) as om hulle net los te maak (vloeistof).\n5. **Skuins lyn bo 100 °C:** net stoom.\n\nDie **afkoelingskurwe** is die omgekeerde: plato's by 100 °C (kondensasie) en 0 °C (vries). Op 'n plato bly die temperatuur konstant omdat energie **vrygestel** word terwyl aantrekkingskragte tussen die deeltjies vorm; dit vervang die hitte wat na die omgewing verlore gaan.\n\n> **Onthou!** Op 'n plato is die temperatuur (en dus die gemiddelde E_{k}) konstant, al absorbeer of verloor die stof steeds energie. 'n Mengsel het nie 'n skerp plato nie; dit smelt oor 'n temperatuurgebied.\n\n## Diffusie en Brownbeweging – bewyse dat deeltjies beweeg\n\n- **Diffusie:** die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie. Jy ruik die boerewors op die buurman se braai omdat die geurdeeltjies deur die lug diffundeer. 'n Kaliumpermanganaatkristal in water kleur stadig die hele beker pers. Diffusie is vinniger in gasse as in vloeistowwe, en vinniger by hoër temperature (die deeltjies beweeg vinniger).\n- **Brownbeweging:** die lukrake sigsagbeweging van klein deeltjies (bv. rookdeeltjies in lug of stuifmeeldeeltjies in water) wat veroorsaak word deur botsings met die onsigbare, vinnig bewegende deeltjies van die gas of vloeistof. Robert Brown het dit in 1827 waargeneem.","en":"## The three states of matter\n\n| | Solid | Liquid | Gas |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Shape and volume | fixed shape and volume | fixed volume; takes the shape of the container | no fixed shape or volume; fills the container |\n| Arrangement | closely packed in a regular pattern | close together, but disordered | far apart, random |\n| Movement | vibrate about fixed positions | slide past each other | move fast in all directions |\n| Forces between particles | strong | weaker | very weak |\n| Compressible? | no | hardly | yes, easily |\n\n## The kinetic molecular theory (KMT)\n\nThe KMT explains the properties of matter in terms of the movement of particles:\n\n1. Matter is made up of tiny particles (atoms, molecules or ions) that are **constantly moving**.\n2. There are **spaces** between the particles.\n3. There are **attractive forces** between the particles; they are stronger the closer the particles are to each other.\n4. All particles have energy. Particles in a solid have the least energy and those in a gas the most.\n5. The **temperature** of a substance is a measure of the **average kinetic energy** of its particles.\n6. A **phase change** can take place when the energy of the particles changes.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Particles do not get bigger when a substance is heated – they move faster and the spaces between them get bigger. Particles in a solid are also not standing still; they vibrate.\n\n## Phase changes\n\n| Process | Change | Energy |\n|---|---|---|\n| Melting | solid → liquid | absorbed |\n| Evaporation / boiling | liquid → gas | absorbed |\n| Sublimation | solid → gas (directly) | absorbed |\n| Freezing (solidification) | liquid → solid | released |\n| Condensation | gas → liquid | released |\n| Deposition (resublimation) | gas → solid (directly) | released |\n\nExamples of sublimation: iodine, dry ice (solid CO_{2}) and mothballs. Frost on the grass is deposition.\n\n- **Melting point:** the temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid. For a pure substance the **freezing point** is the same temperature.\n- **Boiling point:** the temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a gas.\n- **Evaporation versus boiling:** evaporation happens at **any** temperature, only at the **surface** – the fastest particles escape. That is why sweat cools you down. Boiling happens at the boiling point, **throughout the liquid** (bubbles form).\n- The stronger the forces between the particles, the higher the melting and boiling point.\n\n**State at a given temperature T:** T below the melting point → solid; T between the melting and boiling point → liquid; T above the boiling point → gas. Ethanol (melting point −114 °C, boiling point 78 °C) is therefore a liquid at 25 °C.\n\n## The heating curve of water (in words)\n\nIce at −20 °C is heated at a constant rate, and the temperature is plotted against time:\n\n1. **Sloping line (−20 °C → 0 °C):** only ice. The particles vibrate faster; E_{k} and temperature rise.\n2. **First plateau (horizontal at 0 °C):** the ice **melts** – ice and water are present together. The temperature stays constant, because all the energy is used to **overcome the attractive forces between the particles**, not to increase E_{k}.\n3. **Sloping line (0 °C → 100 °C):** only liquid water; E_{k} rises.\n4. **Second plateau (horizontal at 100 °C):** the water **boils** – water and steam are present together. This plateau is much **longer** than the first, because much more energy is needed to separate the particles completely (gas) than to just loosen them (liquid).\n5. **Sloping line above 100 °C:** only steam.\n\nThe **cooling curve** is the reverse: plateaus at 100 °C (condensation) and 0 °C (freezing). On a plateau the temperature stays constant because energy is **released** as attractive forces form between the particles; this replaces the heat lost to the surroundings.\n\n> **Remember!** On a plateau the temperature (and therefore the average E_{k}) is constant, even though the substance is still absorbing or losing energy. A mixture does not have a sharp plateau; it melts over a range of temperatures.\n\n## Diffusion and Brownian motion – evidence that particles move\n\n- **Diffusion:** the movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration. You smell the boerewors on the neighbour's braai because the smell particles diffuse through the air. A potassium permanganate crystal in water slowly colours the whole beaker purple. Diffusion is faster in gases than in liquids, and faster at higher temperatures (the particles move faster).\n- **Brownian motion:** the random zigzag movement of small particles (e.g. smoke particles in air or pollen particles in water) caused by collisions with the invisible, fast-moving particles of the gas or liquid. Robert Brown observed it in 1827."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kinetiese molekulêre teorie","en":"Kinetic molecular theory"},"def":{"af":"Die teorie dat materie uit deeltjies bestaan wat voortdurend beweeg, met ruimtes en aantrekkingskragte tussen hulle; die energie van die deeltjies bepaal die toestand van die stof.","en":"The theory that matter consists of particles that are constantly moving, with spaces and attractive forces between them; the energy of the particles determines the state of the substance."}},{"term":{"af":"Temperatuur","en":"Temperature"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies in 'n stof.","en":"A measure of the average kinetic energy of the particles in a substance."}},{"term":{"af":"Smeltpunt","en":"Melting point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word.","en":"The temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Kookpunt","en":"Boiling point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n gas te word.","en":"The temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a gas."}},{"term":{"af":"Vriespunt","en":"Freezing point"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vloeistof van fase verander om 'n vaste stof te word; vir 'n suiwer stof is dit gelyk aan die smeltpunt.","en":"The temperature at which a liquid changes its phase to become a solid; for a pure substance it equals the melting point."}},{"term":{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering van vloeistof na gas; dit vind by enige temperatuur aan die oppervlak van 'n vloeistof plaas.","en":"The phase change from liquid to gas; it takes place at any temperature at the surface of a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering van gas na vloeistof; energie word vrygestel.","en":"The phase change from gas to liquid; energy is released."}},{"term":{"af":"Sublimasie","en":"Sublimation"},"def":{"af":"Die faseverandering waar 'n vaste stof direk in 'n gas verander sonder om eers 'n vloeistof te word.","en":"The phase change in which a solid changes directly into a gas without first becoming a liquid."}},{"term":{"af":"Diffusie","en":"Diffusion"},"def":{"af":"Die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie.","en":"The movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration."}},{"term":{"af":"Brownbeweging","en":"Brownian motion"},"def":{"af":"Die lukrake beweging van klein deeltjies in 'n vloeistof of gas, veroorsaak deur botsings met die vinnig bewegende deeltjies van die vloeistof of gas.","en":"The random movement of small particles in a liquid or gas, caused by collisions with the fast-moving particles of the liquid or gas."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer die verhittingskurwe van water","en":"Interpret the heating curve of water"},"problem":{"af":"Ys by −20 °C word in 'n beker teen 'n konstante tempo verhit totdat dit stoom by 110 °C is. Die temperatuur-teen-tyd-grafiek het vyf dele: AB styg van −20 °C tot 0 °C; BC is horisontaal by 0 °C; CD styg van 0 °C tot 100 °C; DE is horisontaal by 100 °C en baie langer as BC; EF styg van 100 °C tot 110 °C. (a) Watter fases is in BC en in DE teenwoordig? (b) Verduidelik waarom die temperatuur in BC konstant bly hoewel daar steeds verhit word. (c) Wat gebeur met die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies in DE? (d) Waarom is DE langer as BC?","en":"Ice at −20 °C in a beaker is heated at a constant rate until it is steam at 110 °C. The temperature-versus-time graph has five parts: AB rises from −20 °C to 0 °C; BC is horizontal at 0 °C; CD rises from 0 °C to 100 °C; DE is horizontal at 100 °C and much longer than BC; EF rises from 100 °C to 110 °C. (a) Which phases are present in BC and in DE? (b) Explain why the temperature stays constant in BC although heating continues. (c) What happens to the average kinetic energy of the particles in DE? (d) Why is DE longer than BC?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) BC is die smeltplato: **vaste stof (ys) en vloeistof (water)** is saam teenwoordig. DE is die kookplato: **vloeistof (water) en gas (stoom)**.","en":"(a) BC is the melting plateau: **solid (ice) and liquid (water)** are present together. DE is the boiling plateau: **liquid (water) and gas (steam)**."},{"af":"(b) Die energie wat geabsorbeer word, word gebruik om die **aantrekkingskragte tussen die watermolekules te oorkom** (die potensiële energie neem toe), en nie om die kinetiese energie te verhoog nie. Daarom bly die temperatuur by 0 °C.","en":"(b) The energy absorbed is used to **overcome the attractive forces between the water molecules** (the potential energy increases), not to increase the kinetic energy. That is why the temperature stays at 0 °C."},{"af":"(c) Die temperatuur bly 100 °C, en temperatuur is 'n maatstaf van die gemiddelde kinetiese energie – dus bly die gemiddelde E_{k} **konstant**.","en":"(c) The temperature stays at 100 °C, and temperature is a measure of the average kinetic energy – so the average E_{k} stays **constant**."},{"af":"(d) Om 'n vloeistof in 'n gas te verander, moet die deeltjies **heeltemal van mekaar geskei** word. Tydens smelt word hulle net losgemaak sodat hulle by mekaar kan verbygly. Kook vra dus baie meer energie, en teen dieselfde verhittingstempo duur dit langer.","en":"(d) To change a liquid into a gas, the particles must be **separated from each other completely**. During melting they are only loosened so that they can slide past each other. Boiling therefore needs much more energy, and at the same heating rate it takes longer."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) BC: ys + water; DE: water + stoom (b) energie oorkom die aantrekkingskragte (c) bly konstant (d) meer energie nodig om deeltjies heeltemal te skei","en":"(a) BC: ice + water; DE: water + steam (b) energy overcomes the attractive forces (c) stays constant (d) more energy needed to separate particles completely"}},{"title":{"af":"Toestand uit smelt- en kookpunt","en":"State from melting and boiling point"},"problem":{"af":"Vier stowwe het die volgende smelt- en kookpunte. A: −219 °C en −183 °C. B: −39 °C en 357 °C. C: 44 °C en 280 °C. D: 1 538 °C en 2 862 °C. (a) Gee die toestand van elke stof by kamertemperatuur (25 °C). (b) Watter stof het die sterkste kragte tussen sy deeltjies? (c) In watter toestand is C by 100 °C?","en":"Four substances have the following melting and boiling points. A: −219 °C and −183 °C. B: −39 °C and 357 °C. C: 44 °C and 280 °C. D: 1 538 °C and 2 862 °C. (a) Give the state of each substance at room temperature (25 °C). (b) Which substance has the strongest forces between its particles? (c) In which state is C at 100 °C?"},"steps":[{"af":"Reël: T < smeltpunt → vaste stof; smeltpunt < T < kookpunt → vloeistof; T > kookpunt → gas.","en":"Rule: T < melting point → solid; melting point < T < boiling point → liquid; T > boiling point → gas."},{"af":"(a) A: 25 °C > −183 °C → **gas**. B: −39 °C < 25 °C < 357 °C → **vloeistof**. C: 25 °C < 44 °C → **vaste stof**. D: 25 °C < 1 538 °C → **vaste stof**.","en":"(a) A: 25 °C > −183 °C → **gas**. B: −39 °C < 25 °C < 357 °C → **liquid**. C: 25 °C < 44 °C → **solid**. D: 25 °C < 1 538 °C → **solid**."},{"af":"(b) Hoe sterker die kragte tussen die deeltjies, hoe meer energie is nodig om hulle te skei, en hoe hoër die smelt- en kookpunt. D het die hoogste smelt- en kookpunt → **D**.","en":"(b) The stronger the forces between the particles, the more energy is needed to separate them, and the higher the melting and boiling point. D has the highest melting and boiling point → **D**."},{"af":"(c) 44 °C < 100 °C < 280 °C → C is 'n **vloeistof** by 100 °C.","en":"(c) 44 °C < 100 °C < 280 °C → C is a **liquid** at 100 °C."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) A gas, B vloeistof, C vaste stof, D vaste stof (b) D (c) vloeistof","en":"(a) A gas, B liquid, C solid, D solid (b) D (c) liquid"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik diffusie met die KMT","en":"Explain diffusion with the KMT"},"problem":{"af":"Pa braai boerewors in Brits, en binne 'n paar sekondes ruik die buurkinders dit oor die muur. (a) Noem die proses. (b) Verduidelik dit met die kinetiese molekulêre teorie. (c) 'n Leerder laat val 'n kaliumpermanganaatkristal in 'n beker koue water en een in 'n beker warm water. In watter beker versprei die pers kleur vinniger, en hoekom?","en":"Dad is cooking boerewors on the braai in Brits, and within a few seconds the neighbours' children smell it over the wall. (a) Name the process. (b) Explain it with the kinetic molecular theory. (c) A learner drops a potassium permanganate crystal into a beaker of cold water and one into a beaker of hot water. In which beaker does the purple colour spread faster, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Diffusie** – die beweging van deeltjies vanaf 'n gebied met 'n hoë konsentrasie na 'n gebied met 'n lae konsentrasie.","en":"(a) **Diffusion** – the movement of particles from a region of high concentration to a region of low concentration."},{"af":"(b) Volgens die KMT beweeg die geurdeeltjies voortdurend en lukraak, en daar is groot ruimtes tussen die lugdeeltjies. Die geurdeeltjies beweeg dus weg van die braaivleis (hoë konsentrasie) en versprei deur die lug na die buurkinders (lae konsentrasie).","en":"(b) According to the KMT the smell particles move constantly and randomly, and there are large spaces between the air particles. The smell particles therefore move away from the meat (high concentration) and spread through the air to the neighbours' children (low concentration)."},{"af":"(c) In die **warm** water. 'n Hoër temperatuur beteken 'n hoër gemiddelde kinetiese energie, dus beweeg die deeltjies vinniger en diffundeer die kleur vinniger.","en":"(c) In the **hot** water. A higher temperature means a higher average kinetic energy, so the particles move faster and the colour diffuses faster."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Diffusie (b) geurdeeltjies beweeg voortdurend en lukraak van hoë na lae konsentrasie (c) warm water – hoër gemiddelde Eₖ","en":"(a) Diffusion (b) smell particles move constantly and randomly from high to low concentration (c) hot water – higher average Eₖ"}},{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer 'n afkoelingskurwe","en":"Interpret a cooling curve"},"problem":{"af":"Vloeibare stof X by 90 °C word in 'n proefbuis gelaat om af te koel. Die temperatuur daal tot 69 °C, bly 'n ruk lank konstant by 69 °C en daal dan weer tot 40 °C. (a) Wat is die smeltpunt van X? (b) Watter fases is teenwoordig terwyl die temperatuur by 69 °C konstant bly? (c) Verduidelik waarom die temperatuur konstant bly hoewel X hitte aan die omgewing afgee. (d) Is X waarskynlik 'n suiwer stof? Gee 'n rede.","en":"Liquid substance X at 90 °C is left in a test tube to cool. The temperature drops to 69 °C, stays constant at 69 °C for a while and then drops again to 40 °C. (a) What is the melting point of X? (b) Which phases are present while the temperature stays constant at 69 °C? (c) Explain why the temperature stays constant although X gives off heat to the surroundings. (d) Is X probably a pure substance? Give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die plato is by 69 °C. Dit is die vriespunt, en vir 'n suiwer stof is die smeltpunt dieselfde → **69 °C**.","en":"(a) The plateau is at 69 °C. That is the freezing point, and for a pure substance the melting point is the same → **69 °C**."},{"af":"(b) Tydens die plato vries X: **vloeistof en vaste stof** is saam teenwoordig.","en":"(b) During the plateau X freezes: **liquid and solid** are present together."},{"af":"(c) Terwyl X vries, kom die deeltjies nader aan mekaar en vorm aantrekkingskragte. Daarby word **energie vrygestel**, wat die hitte vervang wat na die omgewing verlore gaan – dus bly die gemiddelde kinetiese energie, en dus die temperatuur, konstant.","en":"(c) While X freezes, the particles move closer together and attractive forces form. This **releases energy**, which replaces the heat lost to the surroundings – so the average kinetic energy, and therefore the temperature, stays constant."},{"af":"(d) **Ja**: X vries by een skerp, vaste temperatuur (een plato). 'n Mengsel sou oor 'n temperatuurgebied stol.","en":"(d) **Yes**: X freezes at one sharp, fixed temperature (one plateau). A mixture would solidify over a range of temperatures."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 69 °C (b) vloeistof en vaste stof (c) energie word vrygestel terwyl aantrekkingskragte vorm (d) ja – skerp vriespunt","en":"(a) 69 °C (b) liquid and solid (c) energy is released as attractive forces form (d) yes – sharp freezing point"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter toestand vibreer die deeltjies net om vaste posisies?","en":"In which state do the particles only vibrate about fixed positions?"},"options":[{"af":"Gas","en":"Gas"},{"af":"Vaste stof","en":"Solid"},{"af":"Vloeistof","en":"Liquid"},{"af":"In al drie toestande","en":"In all three states"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 'n vaste stof is die deeltjies dig gepak en sterk aan mekaar gebind, so hulle kan net om vaste posisies vibreer. In 'n vloeistof gly hulle by mekaar verby, en in 'n gas beweeg hulle vinnig in alle rigtings.","en":"In a solid the particles are closely packed and strongly attracted to each other, so they can only vibrate about fixed positions. In a liquid they slide past each other, and in a gas they move fast in all directions."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tydens kondensasie absorbeer 'n stof hitte-energie uit die omgewing.","en":"During condensation a substance absorbs heat energy from the surroundings."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Kondensasie (gas → vloeistof) stel energie vry, want aantrekkingskragte vorm tussen die deeltjies. Smelt, verdamping en sublimasie absorbeer energie.","en":"False. Condensation (gas → liquid) releases energy, because attractive forces form between the particles. Melting, evaporation and sublimation absorb energy."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die temperatuur waarby 'n vaste stof van fase verander om 'n vloeistof te word, word die ___ genoem.","en":"The temperature at which a solid changes its phase to become a liquid is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["smeltpunt","die smeltpunt"],"en":["melting point","the melting point","meltingpoint"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is die definisie van die smeltpunt. Vir 'n suiwer stof is die vriespunt (vloeistof → vaste stof) by dieselfde temperatuur, bv. 0 °C vir water.","en":"This is the definition of the melting point. For a pure substance the freezing point (liquid → solid) is at the same temperature, e.g. 0 °C for water."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kookpunt","sublimasiepunt","kondensasiepunt"],"en":["boiling point","sublimation point","condensation point"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke proses by die faseverandering.","en":"Match each process to the phase change."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Smelt","en":"Melting"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof → vloeistof","en":"solid → liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"Vries","en":"Freezing"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof → vaste stof","en":"liquid → solid"}},{"l":{"af":"Kook","en":"Boiling"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof → gas","en":"liquid → gas"}},{"l":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"r":{"af":"gas → vloeistof","en":"gas → liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"Sublimasie","en":"Sublimation"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof → gas","en":"solid → gas"}}],"explain":{"af":"Smelt en vries is mekaar se omgekeerde, net soos kook en kondensasie. By sublimasie slaan die stof die vloeistoffase oor, bv. droë ys (vaste CO₂).","en":"Melting and freezing are each other's reverse, just like boiling and condensation. In sublimation the substance skips the liquid phase, e.g. dry ice (solid CO₂)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Volgens die kinetiese molekulêre teorie is die temperatuur van 'n stof 'n maatstaf van die …","en":"According to the kinetic molecular theory, the temperature of a substance is a measure of the …"},"options":[{"af":"totale energie van al die deeltjies.","en":"total energy of all the particles."},{"af":"grootte van die deeltjies.","en":"size of the particles."},{"af":"gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies.","en":"average kinetic energy of the particles."},{"af":"kragte tussen die deeltjies.","en":"forces between the particles."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Temperatuur meet die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies. Dit is nie die totale energie nie (dit sluit ook potensiële energie in), en deeltjies word nie groter as die temperatuur styg nie – hulle beweeg net vinniger.","en":"Temperature measures the average kinetic energy of the particles. It is not the total energy (that also includes potential energy), and particles do not get bigger as the temperature rises – they just move faster."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder kyk deur 'n mikroskoop na rookdeeltjies in lug. Die rookdeeltjies beweeg lukraak in 'n sigsagpatroon. Wat bewys hierdie Brownbeweging?","en":"A learner looks at smoke particles in air through a microscope. The smoke particles move randomly in a zigzag pattern. What does this Brownian motion prove?"},"options":[{"af":"Die lugdeeltjies beweeg voortdurend en lukraak en bots teen die rookdeeltjies.","en":"The air particles move constantly and randomly and collide with the smoke particles."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies is lewendig en beweeg uit hulle eie.","en":"The smoke particles are alive and move on their own."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies word groter omdat die lug warm is.","en":"The smoke particles get bigger because the air is warm."},{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies trek mekaar sterk aan.","en":"The smoke particles attract each other strongly."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die rookdeeltjies word van alle kante deur onsigbare, vinnig bewegende lugdeeltjies gestamp. Omdat die botsings lukraak is, skuif die rookdeeltjies in 'n sigsagpatroon. Dit is bewys dat die deeltjies van 'n gas voortdurend beweeg.","en":"The smoke particles are bumped from all sides by invisible, fast-moving air particles. Because the collisions are random, the smoke particles move in a zigzag pattern. This is evidence that the particles of a gas move constantly."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Diffusie vind vinniger plaas by 'n hoër temperatuur.","en":"Diffusion takes place faster at a higher temperature."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. By 'n hoër temperatuur is die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies hoër, dus beweeg hulle vinniger en versprei hulle vinniger – bv. kaliumpermanganaat versprei vinniger in warm water as in koue water.","en":"True. At a higher temperature the average kinetic energy of the particles is higher, so they move faster and spread faster – e.g. potassium permanganate spreads faster in hot water than in cold water."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Terwyl ys smelt, bly die temperatuur by 0 °C, want die energie wat geabsorbeer word, word gebruik om die ___ tussen die deeltjies te oorkom.","en":"While ice melts, the temperature stays at 0 °C, because the energy absorbed is used to overcome the ___ between the particles."},"answers":{"af":["kragte","aantrekkingskragte","intermolekulêre kragte","intermolekulere kragte","aantrekkingskrag"],"en":["forces","attractive forces","intermolecular forces","forces of attraction"]},"explain":{"af":"Op die plato gaan die energie in die oorkoming van die aantrekkingskragte tussen die watermolekules, nie in die verhoging van hul kinetiese energie nie. Daarom bly die temperatuur konstant totdat al die ys gesmelt het.","en":"On the plateau the energy goes into overcoming the attractive forces between the water molecules, not into increasing their kinetic energy. That is why the temperature stays constant until all the ice has melted."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kinetiese energie","temperatuur","botsings"],"en":["kinetic energy","temperature","collisions"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Suiwer asynsuur het 'n smeltpunt van 17 °C en 'n kookpunt van 118 °C. In watter toestand is dit op 'n winteroggend in Brits as die temperatuur 8 °C is?","en":"Pure acetic acid has a melting point of 17 °C and a boiling point of 118 °C. In which state is it on a winter morning in Brits when the temperature is 8 °C?"},"options":[{"af":"Vloeistof","en":"Liquid"},{"af":"Gas","en":"Gas"},{"af":"Vaste stof en vloeistof saam","en":"Solid and liquid together"},{"af":"Vaste stof","en":"Solid"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"8 °C is laer as die smeltpunt (17 °C), dus is die asynsuur 'n vaste stof. By kamertemperatuur (25 °C) sou dit 'n vloeistof wees – moenie outomaties 25 °C gebruik as die vraag 'n ander temperatuur gee nie. Vaste stof en vloeistof is net saam teenwoordig presies by die smeltpunt.","en":"8 °C is below the melting point (17 °C), so the acetic acid is a solid. At room temperature (25 °C) it would be a liquid – do not automatically use 25 °C when the question gives another temperature. Solid and liquid are only present together exactly at the melting point."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Stof het 'n smeltpunt van −23 °C en 'n kookpunt van 77 °C. By 90 °C is die stof 'n ___ (vaste stof, vloeistof of gas).","en":"A substance has a melting point of −23 °C and a boiling point of 77 °C. At 90 °C the substance is a ___ (solid, liquid or gas)."},"answers":{"af":["gas","'n gas","gasvormig"],"en":["gas","a gas","gaseous"]},"explain":{"af":"90 °C is hoër as die kookpunt (77 °C), dus het die stof reeds gekook en is dit 'n gas. Dit sou 'n vloeistof wees tussen −23 °C en 77 °C.","en":"90 °C is above the boiling point (77 °C), so the substance has already boiled and is a gas. It would be a liquid between −23 °C and 77 °C."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vloeistof","vaste stof","plasma"],"en":["liquid","solid","plasma"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Suiwer vaste stof word teen 'n konstante tempo verhit. Die temperatuur styg van 20 °C tot 80 °C, bly dan 5 minute lank konstant by 80 °C en styg daarna weer. Watter stelling oor die 5 minute by 80 °C is korrek?","en":"A pure solid is heated at a constant rate. The temperature rises from 20 °C to 80 °C, then stays constant at 80 °C for 5 minutes and then rises again. Which statement about the 5 minutes at 80 °C is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die stof kook, en die gemiddelde kinetiese energie van die deeltjies neem toe.","en":"The substance boils, and the average kinetic energy of the particles increases."},{"af":"Die stof smelt; die energie oorkom die kragte tussen die deeltjies, en die gemiddelde kinetiese energie bly konstant.","en":"The substance melts; the energy overcomes the forces between the particles, and the average kinetic energy stays constant."},{"af":"Die stof smelt, en die deeltjies word groter.","en":"The substance melts, and the particles get bigger."},{"af":"Geen energie word geabsorbeer nie, want die temperatuur verander nie.","en":"No energy is absorbed, because the temperature does not change."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste plato van 'n vaste stof is die smeltplato (80 °C is die smeltpunt). Die stof absorbeer steeds energie, maar dit word gebruik om die kragte tussen die deeltjies te oorkom. Omdat die temperatuur konstant is, bly die gemiddelde Eₖ konstant. Deeltjies word nooit groter nie.","en":"The first plateau of a solid is the melting plateau (80 °C is the melting point). The substance still absorbs energy, but it is used to overcome the forces between the particles. Because the temperature is constant, the average Eₖ stays constant. Particles never get bigger."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Water word teen 'n konstante tempo van ys tot stoom verhit. Die plato by 100 °C is baie langer as die plato by 0 °C. Wat is die beste verduideliking?","en":"Water is heated at a constant rate from ice to steam. The plateau at 100 °C is much longer than the plateau at 0 °C. What is the best explanation?"},"options":[{"af":"Meer energie is nodig om die deeltjies heeltemal van mekaar te skei (gas) as om hulle net los te maak sodat hulle by mekaar kan verbygly (vloeistof).","en":"More energy is needed to separate the particles completely (gas) than to only loosen them so they can slide past each other (liquid)."},{"af":"100 °C is 'n hoër temperatuur as 0 °C, dus duur dit langer om dit te bereik.","en":"100 °C is a higher temperature than 0 °C, so it takes longer to reach it."},{"af":"Die kinetiese energie van die deeltjies neem tydens kook toe, maar nie tydens smelt nie.","en":"The kinetic energy of the particles increases during boiling, but not during melting."},{"af":"Stoom gelei hitte beter as ys.","en":"Steam conducts heat better than ice."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die lengte van 'n plato wys hoeveel energie die faseverandering nodig het. Om vloeistof in gas te verander, moet al die aantrekkingskragte oorkom word sodat die deeltjies ver uitmekaar kan beweeg; by smelt word hulle net losgemaak. Die tyd om 100 °C te bereik, is die skuins lyn, nie die plato nie, en op albei plato's bly Eₖ konstant.","en":"The length of a plateau shows how much energy the phase change needs. To change liquid into gas, all the attractive forces must be overcome so the particles can move far apart; in melting they are only loosened. The time to reach 100 °C is the sloping line, not the plateau, and on both plateaus Eₖ stays constant."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op 'n koue wintersoggend by Hartbeespoortdam verander waterdamp in die lug direk in ys en vorm ryp op die gras. Hierdie faseverandering is die omgekeerde van ___.","en":"On a cold winter morning at Hartbeespoort Dam, water vapour in the air changes directly into ice and forms frost on the grass. This phase change is the reverse of ___."},"answers":{"af":["sublimasie"],"en":["sublimation"]},"explain":{"af":"Gas → vaste stof sonder 'n vloeistoffase is afsetting (resublimasie), die omgekeerde van sublimasie (vaste stof → gas direk). Dit is nie kondensasie nie, want daar vorm nie eers vloeibare water nie.","en":"Gas → solid without a liquid phase is deposition (resublimation), the reverse of sublimation (solid → gas directly). It is not condensation, because no liquid water forms first."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verdamping","smelting","kondensasie"],"en":["evaporation","melting","condensation"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter sê: \"Water in 'n oop bakkie by kamertemperatuur kan nie verdamp nie, want dit is ver onder die kookpunt van 100 °C.\" Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Pieter says: \"Water in an open bowl at room temperature cannot evaporate, because it is far below the boiling point of 100 °C.\" Which statement best evaluates his claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: water verdamp slegs by 100 °C.","en":"He is right: water only evaporates at 100 °C."},{"af":"Hy is reg: by kamertemperatuur het die waterdeeltjies geen kinetiese energie nie.","en":"He is right: at room temperature the water particles have no kinetic energy."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: verdamping vind by enige temperatuur aan die oppervlak plaas, want sommige deeltjies het genoeg kinetiese energie om te ontsnap; kook vind by die kookpunt deur die hele vloeistof plaas.","en":"He is wrong: evaporation takes place at any temperature at the surface, because some particles have enough kinetic energy to escape; boiling takes place at the boiling point throughout the liquid."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: water verdamp omdat die deeltjies by kamertemperatuur kleiner word.","en":"He is wrong: water evaporates because the particles get smaller at room temperature."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hy verwar verdamping met kook. Die deeltjies het verskillende kinetiese energieë; die vinnigstes aan die oppervlak ontsnap by enige temperatuur – daarom droog wasgoed sonder om te kook. Deeltjies het altyd kinetiese energie en verander nie van grootte nie.","en":"He confuses evaporation with boiling. The particles have different kinetic energies; the fastest ones at the surface escape at any temperature – that is why washing dries without boiling. Particles always have kinetic energy and do not change size."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-atoom","title":{"af":"Die atoom","en":"The atom"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die ontwikkeling van die atoommodel kan beskryf, protone, neutrone en elektrone kan tel, die relatiewe atoommassa uit isotope kan bereken en elektronkonfigurasies tot Z = 20 kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to describe how the atomic model developed, count protons, neutrons and electrons, calculate relative atomic mass from isotopes and write electron configurations up to Z = 20."},"summary":{"af":"## Atoommodelle – hoe ons idee van die atoom ontwikkel het\n\n| Wetenskaplike | Model of ontdekking |\n|---|---|\n| Dalton (1803) | Materie bestaan uit klein, harde, **ondeelbare** atome (soos klein snoekerballe); alle atome van een element is dieselfde. |\n| Thomson (1897) | Ontdek die **elektron**. **Pruimpoedingmodel:** negatiewe elektrone is in 'n positief gelaaide bol versprei. |\n| Rutherford (1911) | **Alfadeeltjie-verstrooiing** (goudfoelie): die atoom is meestal leë ruimte met 'n klein, digte, **positiewe kern** wat byna al die massa bevat; elektrone beweeg om die kern (**kernmodel**). |\n| Bohr (1913) | Elektrone beweeg in **vaste energievlakke** om die kern. 'n Elektron wat energie absorbeer, spring na 'n hoër vlak; as dit terugval, straal die atoom lig met 'n spesifieke energie uit. |\n| Chadwick (1932) | Ontdek die **neutron**, 'n neutrale deeltjie in die kern. |\n\n**Rutherford se waarnemings:** die meeste alfadeeltjies het reguit deurgegaan → die atoom is meestal leë ruimte; party is afgebuig en baie min het teruggebons → 'n klein, digte, positiewe kern stoot die positiewe alfadeeltjies af. As 'n atoom so groot soos Loftus Versfeld was, sou die kern soos 'n ertjie op die middelkol wees.\n\n**Waarom Bohr?** Volgens Rutherford se model sou bewegende elektrone energie verloor en in die kern inspiraal. Vaste energievlakke verklaar waarom atome stabiel is en net sekere kleure lig uitstraal (bv. die geel lig van natriumstraatligte).\n\n## Die deeltjies in 'n atoom\n\n| Deeltjie | Lading | Relatiewe massa | Ligging |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Proton (p^{+}) | +1 | 1 | kern |\n| Neutron (n^{0}) | 0 | 1 | kern |\n| Elektron (e^{−}) | −1 | [[1/1836]] ≈ 0 | energievlakke om die kern |\n\nProtone en neutrone saam heet **nukleone**. 'n Neutrale atoom het ewe veel protone en elektrone.\n\n- **Atoomgetal (Z):** die aantal protone in 'n atoom van 'n element. Z bepaal watter element dit is.\n- **Massagetal (A):** die aantal protone plus neutrone in die kern van 'n atoom.\n- **Neutrone = A − Z.** Notasie: ^{A}_{Z}X, bv. ^{23}_{11}Na het 11 p, 12 n en 11 e.\n- **Ione:** elektrone = Z − lading. Na^{+} het 10 e (een verloor); Cl^{−} het 18 e (een bygekry). Die aantal protone verander nooit.\n\n## Isotope\n\n**Isotope** is atome van dieselfde element met dieselfde aantal protone, maar verskillende getalle neutrone (dus verskillende massagetalle), bv. C-12, C-13 en C-14, of Cl-35 en Cl-37. Isotope het dieselfde elektronkonfigurasie en dus **dieselfde chemiese eienskappe**, maar verskillende massas. Die SAFARI-1-reaktor by Pelindaba naby Hartbeespoortdam maak radio-isotope vir mediese gebruik.\n\n## Relatiewe atoommassa\n\nDie **relatiewe atoommassa** (A_{r}) is die gemiddelde massa van 'n element se atome, met inagneming van al sy isotope en hul persentasie voorkoms, op 'n skaal waarop 'n koolstof-12-atoom 'n massa van presies 12 het. Dit het **geen eenheid** nie.\n\n**A_{r} = (massagetal_{1} × %_{1} + massagetal_{2} × %_{2} + …) ÷ 100**\n\nChloor: 75 % Cl-35 en 25 % Cl-37 → A_{r} = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) ÷ 100 = 35,5.\n\n**Omgekeerd:** as A_{r} gegee is, laat die een isotoop x % wees en die ander (100 − x) %, en los op vir x.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie net die massagetalle optel en deur 2 deel nie – (35 + 37) ÷ 2 = 36 is verkeerd, want die isotope kom nie ewe veel voor nie. A_{r} lê altyd naaste aan die isotoop wat die meeste voorkom.\n\n## Elektronkonfigurasie\n\nElektrone is in **energievlakke** (n = 1, 2, 3, 4) om die kern. Elke vlak het subvlakke met **orbitale**: 'n s-subvlak het een orbitaal en 'n p-subvlak drie. Elke orbitaal hou hoogstens 2 elektrone, dus hou s 2 en p 6 elektrone. Die maksimum per vlak is 2n^{2}: 2, 8, 18. Tot by Z = 20 word in vlak 3 net 3s en 3p (8 elektrone) gevul voordat 4s begin.\n\n**Drie reëls:**\n\n1. **Aufbau-beginsel:** elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie. Volgorde: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s. (4s het 'n laer energie as 3d, daarom kry K en Ca hul laaste elektrone in 4s.)\n2. **Hund se reël:** in 'n p-subvlak beset elektrone eers elke orbitaal enkel voordat hulle paar.\n3. **Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel:** 'n orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en hulle moet teenoorgestelde spin hê (↑↓).\n\n**sp-notasie:** O (Z = 8): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{4}; Na (Z = 11): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{1} = [Ne] 3s^{1}; K (Z = 19): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} 4s^{1}.\n\n**Aufbau-diagram (orbitaalblokdiagram):** elke orbitaal is 'n blokkie en elke elektron 'n pyltjie; die blokkies word van die laagste energie (onder) na die hoogste (bo) gerangskik. Suurstof: 1s [↑↓], 2s [↑↓], 2p [↑↓][↑][↑] – twee **ongepaarde** elektrone.\n\n**Valenselektrone** is die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak; hulle bepaal hoe 'n atoom reageer. Die res is **kernelektrone**. Cl: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{5} → 7 valenselektrone.\n\n**Ione:** Na^{+}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} en Cl^{−}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} – albei het 'n edelgaskonfigurasie.\n\n> **Wenk:** Tel die superskrifte op – die som moet gelyk wees aan die aantal elektrone.","en":"## Atomic models – how our idea of the atom developed\n\n| Scientist | Model or discovery |\n|---|---|\n| Dalton (1803) | Matter consists of tiny, hard, **indivisible** atoms (like tiny snooker balls); all atoms of one element are the same. |\n| Thomson (1897) | Discovered the **electron**. **Plum pudding model:** negative electrons are spread through a positively charged sphere. |\n| Rutherford (1911) | **Alpha particle scattering** (gold foil): the atom is mostly empty space with a small, dense, **positive nucleus** that contains almost all the mass; electrons move around the nucleus (**nuclear model**). |\n| Bohr (1913) | Electrons move in **fixed energy levels** around the nucleus. An electron that absorbs energy jumps to a higher level; when it falls back, the atom emits light of a specific energy. |\n| Chadwick (1932) | Discovered the **neutron**, a neutral particle in the nucleus. |\n\n**Rutherford's observations:** most alpha particles went straight through → the atom is mostly empty space; some were deflected and very few bounced back → a small, dense, positive nucleus repels the positive alpha particles. If an atom were as big as Loftus Versfeld, the nucleus would be like a pea on the centre spot.\n\n**Why Bohr?** According to Rutherford's model, moving electrons would lose energy and spiral into the nucleus. Fixed energy levels explain why atoms are stable and only emit certain colours of light (e.g. the yellow light of sodium street lights).\n\n## The particles in an atom\n\n| Particle | Charge | Relative mass | Location |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Proton (p^{+}) | +1 | 1 | nucleus |\n| Neutron (n^{0}) | 0 | 1 | nucleus |\n| Electron (e^{−}) | −1 | [[1/1836]] ≈ 0 | energy levels around the nucleus |\n\nProtons and neutrons together are called **nucleons**. A neutral atom has equal numbers of protons and electrons.\n\n- **Atomic number (Z):** the number of protons in an atom of an element. Z determines which element it is.\n- **Mass number (A):** the number of protons plus neutrons in the nucleus of an atom.\n- **Neutrons = A − Z.** Notation: ^{A}_{Z}X, e.g. ^{23}_{11}Na has 11 p, 12 n and 11 e.\n- **Ions:** electrons = Z − charge. Na^{+} has 10 e (lost one); Cl^{−} has 18 e (gained one). The number of protons never changes.\n\n## Isotopes\n\n**Isotopes** are atoms of the same element with the same number of protons, but different numbers of neutrons (therefore different mass numbers), e.g. C-12, C-13 and C-14, or Cl-35 and Cl-37. Isotopes have the same electron configuration and therefore **the same chemical properties**, but different masses. The SAFARI-1 reactor at Pelindaba near Hartbeespoort Dam makes radioisotopes for medical use.\n\n## Relative atomic mass\n\nThe **relative atomic mass** (A_{r}) is the average mass of an element's atoms, taking into account all its isotopes and their percentage abundance, on a scale on which a carbon-12 atom has a mass of exactly 12. It has **no unit**.\n\n**A_{r} = (mass number_{1} × %_{1} + mass number_{2} × %_{2} + …) ÷ 100**\n\nChlorine: 75 % Cl-35 and 25 % Cl-37 → A_{r} = (35 × 75 + 37 × 25) ÷ 100 = 35.5.\n\n**In reverse:** if A_{r} is given, let one isotope be x % and the other (100 − x) %, and solve for x.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not just add the mass numbers and divide by 2 – (35 + 37) ÷ 2 = 36 is wrong, because the isotopes are not equally abundant. A_{r} always lies closest to the most abundant isotope.\n\n## Electron configuration\n\nElectrons are in **energy levels** (n = 1, 2, 3, 4) around the nucleus. Each level has sublevels with **orbitals**: an s sublevel has one orbital and a p sublevel three. Each orbital holds at most 2 electrons, so s holds 2 and p holds 6 electrons. The maximum per level is 2n^{2}: 2, 8, 18. Up to Z = 20, only 3s and 3p (8 electrons) are filled in level 3 before 4s starts.\n\n**Three rules:**\n\n1. **Aufbau principle:** electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first. Order: 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p → 4s. (4s has a lower energy than 3d, which is why K and Ca get their last electrons in 4s.)\n2. **Hund's rule:** in a p sublevel, electrons first occupy each orbital singly before they pair up.\n3. **Pauli's exclusion principle:** an orbital can hold at most two electrons, and they must have opposite spins (↑↓).\n\n**sp notation:** O (Z = 8): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{4}; Na (Z = 11): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{1} = [Ne] 3s^{1}; K (Z = 19): 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} 4s^{1}.\n\n**Aufbau diagram (orbital box diagram):** each orbital is a box and each electron an arrow; the boxes are arranged from the lowest energy (bottom) to the highest (top). Oxygen: 1s [↑↓], 2s [↑↓], 2p [↑↓][↑][↑] – two **unpaired** electrons.\n\n**Valence electrons** are the electrons in the outermost energy level; they determine how an atom reacts. The rest are **core electrons**. Cl: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{5} → 7 valence electrons.\n\n**Ions:** Na^{+}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} and Cl^{−}: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{6} – both have a noble gas configuration.\n\n> **Tip:** Add up the superscripts – the sum must equal the number of electrons."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Atoomgetal (Z)","en":"Atomic number (Z)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal protone in 'n atoom van 'n element.","en":"The number of protons in an atom of an element."}},{"term":{"af":"Massagetal (A)","en":"Mass number (A)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal protone en neutrone in die kern van 'n atoom.","en":"The number of protons and neutrons in the nucleus of an atom."}},{"term":{"af":"Isotoop","en":"Isotope"},"def":{"af":"Atome van dieselfde element met dieselfde aantal protone, maar verskillende getalle neutrone.","en":"Atoms of the same element with the same number of protons, but different numbers of neutrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Relatiewe atoommassa","en":"Relative atomic mass"},"def":{"af":"Die gemiddelde massa van 'n element se atome, met inagneming van sy isotope en hul persentasie voorkoms, op 'n skaal waarop koolstof-12 'n massa van 12 het; dit het geen eenheid nie.","en":"The average mass of an element's atoms, taking into account its isotopes and their percentage abundance, on a scale on which carbon-12 has a mass of 12; it has no unit."}},{"term":{"af":"Orbitaal","en":"Orbital"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied om die kern waar 'n elektron waarskynlik gevind word; elke orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat.","en":"A region around the nucleus where an electron is likely to be found; each orbital can hold at most two electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronkonfigurasie","en":"Electron configuration"},"def":{"af":"Die rangskikking van die elektrone van 'n atoom in energievlakke en orbitale, bv. 1s² 2s² 2p⁴.","en":"The arrangement of an atom's electrons in energy levels and orbitals, e.g. 1s² 2s² 2p⁴."}},{"term":{"af":"Valenselektrone","en":"Valence electrons"},"def":{"af":"Die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak van 'n atoom.","en":"The electrons in the outermost energy level of an atom."}},{"term":{"af":"Aufbau-beginsel","en":"Aufbau principle"},"def":{"af":"Elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie voordat hulle orbitale met 'n hoër energie beset.","en":"Electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first before they occupy orbitals of higher energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Hund se reël","en":"Hund's rule"},"def":{"af":"Elektrone beset eers elke orbitaal in 'n subvlak enkel voordat hulle in dieselfde orbitaal paar.","en":"Electrons first occupy each orbital in a sublevel singly before they pair up in the same orbital."}},{"term":{"af":"Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel","en":"Pauli's exclusion principle"},"def":{"af":"'n Orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en die twee elektrone moet teenoorgestelde spin hê.","en":"An orbital can hold at most two electrons, and the two electrons must have opposite spins."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Rutherford se goudfoelie-eksperiment","en":"Rutherford's gold foil experiment"},"problem":{"af":"Rutherford het positief gelaaide alfadeeltjies op 'n baie dun goudfoelie geskiet. (a) Beskryf die waarnemings en wat elkeen oor die atoom bewys. (b) Waarom kon Thomson se pruimpoedingmodel nie die resultate verklaar nie?","en":"Rutherford fired positively charged alpha particles at a very thin gold foil. (a) Describe the observations and what each one shows about the atom. (b) Why could Thomson's plum pudding model not explain the results?"},"steps":[{"af":"Waarneming 1: die meeste alfadeeltjies het **reguit deurgegaan** → die atoom bestaan meestal uit **leë ruimte**.","en":"Observation 1: most alpha particles **went straight through** → the atom consists mostly of **empty space**."},{"af":"Waarneming 2: party is deur groot hoeke **afgebuig** → daar is 'n **positiewe** lading in die middel van die atoom wat die positiewe alfadeeltjies afstoot.","en":"Observation 2: some were **deflected** through large angles → there is a **positive** charge in the centre of the atom that repels the positive alpha particles."},{"af":"Waarneming 3: baie min het **teruggebons** → die positiewe lading en byna al die massa is in 'n baie **klein, digte kern** saamgepak.","en":"Observation 3: very few **bounced back** → the positive charge and almost all the mass are packed into a very **small, dense nucleus**."},{"af":"(b) In Thomson se model is die positiewe lading eweredig oor die hele atoom versprei. Dit sou die alfadeeltjies hoogstens effens afbuig, nooit laat terugbons nie. Rutherford het daarom die **kernmodel** voorgestel: 'n klein positiewe kern met elektrone wat daarom beweeg.","en":"(b) In Thomson's model the positive charge is spread evenly through the whole atom. It would deflect the alpha particles only slightly, never make them bounce back. Rutherford therefore proposed the **nuclear model**: a small positive nucleus with electrons moving around it."}],"answer":{"af":"Die atoom is meestal leë ruimte met 'n klein, digte, positiewe kern wat byna al die massa bevat; elektrone beweeg om die kern.","en":"The atom is mostly empty space with a small, dense, positive nucleus that contains almost all the mass; electrons move around the nucleus."}},{"title":{"af":"Tel protone, neutrone en elektrone","en":"Count protons, neutrons and electrons"},"problem":{"af":"Bepaal die aantal protone, neutrone en elektrone in (a) ²⁷₁₃Al, (b) ²⁷₁₃Al³⁺ en (c) ³²₁₆S²⁻.","en":"Determine the number of protons, neutrons and electrons in (a) ²⁷₁₃Al, (b) ²⁷₁₃Al³⁺ and (c) ³²₁₆S²⁻."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik: protone = Z (onderste getal); neutrone = A − Z (A is die boonste getal); elektrone = Z − lading.","en":"Use: protons = Z (bottom number); neutrons = A − Z (A is the top number); electrons = Z − charge."},{"af":"(a) ^{27}_{13}Al: p = 13; n = 27 − 13 = 14; e = 13 (neutrale atoom).","en":"(a) ^{27}_{13}Al: p = 13; n = 27 − 13 = 14; e = 13 (neutral atom)."},{"af":"(b) Al^{3+}: p = 13; n = 14; e = 13 − 3 = 10 (die atoom het 3 elektrone verloor; die protone bly dieselfde).","en":"(b) Al^{3+}: p = 13; n = 14; e = 13 − 3 = 10 (the atom lost 3 electrons; the protons stay the same)."},{"af":"(c) S^{2−}: p = 16; n = 32 − 16 = 16; e = 16 − (−2) = 16 + 2 = 18 (die atoom het 2 elektrone bygekry).","en":"(c) S^{2−}: p = 16; n = 32 − 16 = 16; e = 16 − (−2) = 16 + 2 = 18 (the atom gained 2 electrons)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 13 p, 14 n, 13 e (b) 13 p, 14 n, 10 e (c) 16 p, 16 n, 18 e","en":"(a) 13 p, 14 n, 13 e (b) 13 p, 14 n, 10 e (c) 16 p, 16 n, 18 e"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa","en":"Calculate the relative atomic mass"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesium kom in die natuur voor as 79 % Mg-24, 10 % Mg-25 en 11 % Mg-26. Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa van magnesium.","en":"Magnesium occurs in nature as 79 % Mg-24, 10 % Mg-25 and 11 % Mg-26. Calculate the relative atomic mass of magnesium."},"steps":[{"af":"Formule: A_{r} = (massagetal_{1} × %_{1} + massagetal_{2} × %_{2} + massagetal_{3} × %_{3}) ÷ 100","en":"Formula: A_{r} = (mass number_{1} × %_{1} + mass number_{2} × %_{2} + mass number_{3} × %_{3}) ÷ 100"},{"af":"Vervang: A_{r} = (24 × 79 + 25 × 10 + 26 × 11) ÷ 100","en":"Substitute: A_{r} = (24 × 79 + 25 × 10 + 26 × 11) ÷ 100"},{"af":"= (1 896 + 250 + 286) ÷ 100 = 2 432 ÷ 100","en":"= (1 896 + 250 + 286) ÷ 100 = 2 432 ÷ 100"},{"af":"A_{r} = 24,32 (geen eenheid nie). Kontrole: die antwoord lê tussen 24 en 26, naaste aan 24, want Mg-24 kom die meeste voor.","en":"A_{r} = 24.32 (no unit). Check: the answer lies between 24 and 26, closest to 24, because Mg-24 is the most abundant."}],"answer":{"af":"Aᵣ(Mg) = 24,32","en":"Aᵣ(Mg) = 24.32"}},{"title":{"af":"Elektronkonfigurasie van fosfor","en":"Electron configuration of phosphorus"},"problem":{"af":"Vir fosfor (Z = 15): (a) skryf die elektronkonfigurasie in sp-notasie, (b) beskryf die Aufbau-diagram (orbitaalblokdiagram), en (c) bepaal die aantal valenselektrone en ongepaarde elektrone.","en":"For phosphorus (Z = 15): (a) write the electron configuration in sp notation, (b) describe the Aufbau diagram (orbital box diagram), and (c) determine the number of valence electrons and unpaired electrons."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Neutrale P-atoom het 15 elektrone. Vul volgens die Aufbau-beginsel in die volgorde 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{3}. Kontrole: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 3 = 15.","en":"(a) A neutral P atom has 15 electrons. Fill according to the Aufbau principle in the order 1s → 2s → 2p → 3s → 3p: 1s^{2} 2s^{2} 2p^{6} 3s^{2} 3p^{3}. Check: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 3 = 15."},{"af":"(b) 1s, 2s en 3s het elk een blokkie met ↑↓; die drie 2p-blokkies is vol: [↑↓][↑↓][↑↓]. Volgens **Hund se reël** kry die drie 3p-blokkies elk een pyltjie: [↑][↑][↑] – die elektrone paar nie voordat elke blokkie een het nie.","en":"(b) 1s, 2s and 3s each have one box with ↑↓; the three 2p boxes are full: [↑↓][↑↓][↑↓]. According to **Hund's rule** the three 3p boxes each get one arrow: [↑][↑][↑] – the electrons do not pair before every box has one."},{"af":"(c) Valenselektrone = elektrone in die buitenste energievlak (n = 3): 3s^{2} 3p^{3} → 2 + 3 = **5**.","en":"(c) Valence electrons = electrons in the outermost energy level (n = 3): 3s^{2} 3p^{3} → 2 + 3 = **5**."},{"af":"Ongepaarde elektrone: die drie enkel elektrone in 3p → **3**. Elke gepaarde blokkie bevat twee pyltjies in teenoorgestelde rigtings (**Pauli**).","en":"Unpaired electrons: the three single electrons in 3p → **3**. Every paired box contains two arrows in opposite directions (**Pauli**)."}],"answer":{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p³; 5 valenselektrone; 3 ongepaarde elektrone","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p³; 5 valence electrons; 3 unpaired electrons"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter wetenskaplike het die neutron in 1932 ontdek?","en":"Which scientist discovered the neutron in 1932?"},"options":[{"af":"Thomson","en":"Thomson"},{"af":"Rutherford","en":"Rutherford"},{"af":"Bohr","en":"Bohr"},{"af":"Chadwick","en":"Chadwick"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Chadwick het in 1932 die neutron ontdek. Thomson het die elektron ontdek, Rutherford die kern, en Bohr het die model met vaste energievlakke voorgestel.","en":"Chadwick discovered the neutron in 1932. Thomson discovered the electron, Rutherford the nucleus, and Bohr proposed the model with fixed energy levels."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens Bohr se model straal 'n atoom lig uit wanneer 'n elektron van 'n hoër na 'n laer energievlak val.","en":"According to Bohr's model, an atom emits light when an electron falls from a higher to a lower energy level."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n Elektron wat energie absorbeer, spring na 'n hoër vlak. As dit terugval, word die verskil in energie as lig uitgestraal – daarom straal elke element net sekere kleure uit.","en":"True. An electron that absorbs energy jumps to a higher level. When it falls back, the difference in energy is emitted as light – that is why each element emits only certain colours."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die atoomgetal (Z) van 'n element is die aantal ___ in 'n atoom van daardie element.","en":"The atomic number (Z) of an element is the number of ___ in an atom of that element."},"answers":{"af":["protone","proton"],"en":["protons","proton"]},"explain":{"af":"Z = die aantal protone. Dit bepaal watter element dit is: elke atoom met 6 protone is koolstof. Die massagetal (A) is protone plus neutrone.","en":"Z = the number of protons. It determines which element it is: every atom with 6 protons is carbon. The mass number (A) is protons plus neutrons."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["neutrone","nukleone","valenselektrone"],"en":["neutrons","nucleons","valence electrons"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke wetenskaplike by sy bydrae tot die atoommodel.","en":"Match each scientist to his contribution to the atomic model."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Dalton","en":"Dalton"},"r":{"af":"Atoom is 'n klein, harde, ondeelbare bol","en":"Atom is a tiny, hard, indivisible sphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Thomson","en":"Thomson"},"r":{"af":"Pruimpoedingmodel: elektrone in 'n positiewe bol","en":"Plum pudding model: electrons in a positive sphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Rutherford","en":"Rutherford"},"r":{"af":"Klein, digte, positiewe kern; meestal leë ruimte","en":"Small, dense, positive nucleus; mostly empty space"}},{"l":{"af":"Bohr","en":"Bohr"},"r":{"af":"Elektrone in vaste energievlakke","en":"Electrons in fixed energy levels"}},{"l":{"af":"Chadwick","en":"Chadwick"},"r":{"af":"Neutrale deeltjie in die kern","en":"Neutral particle in the nucleus"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die volgorde Dalton → Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Chadwick wys hoe elke nuwe eksperiment die vorige model verbeter het.","en":"The order Dalton → Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr → Chadwick shows how each new experiment improved the previous model."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In Rutherford se goudfoelie-eksperiment het die meeste alfadeeltjies reguit deur die foelie beweeg. Wat het hy hieruit afgelei?","en":"In Rutherford's gold foil experiment most alpha particles went straight through the foil. What did he conclude from this?"},"options":[{"af":"Die atoom bestaan meestal uit leë ruimte.","en":"The atom consists mostly of empty space."},{"af":"Die kern is negatief gelaai.","en":"The nucleus is negatively charged."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg in vaste energievlakke.","en":"Electrons move in fixed energy levels."},{"af":"Die atoom is 'n harde, ondeelbare bol.","en":"The atom is a hard, indivisible sphere."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As die meeste deeltjies ongehinderd deurgaan, is daar niks in hul pad nie: die atoom is meestal leë ruimte. Die kern is positief (dit stoot die positiewe alfadeeltjies af), energievlakke is Bohr se idee, en 'n harde bol is Dalton se model.","en":"If most particles pass through unhindered, there is nothing in their way: the atom is mostly empty space. The nucleus is positive (it repels the positive alpha particles), energy levels are Bohr's idea, and a hard sphere is Dalton's model."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Isotope van dieselfde element het verskillende atoomgetalle.","en":"Isotopes of the same element have different atomic numbers."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Isotope het dieselfde aantal protone, dus dieselfde atoomgetal (anders sou dit 'n ander element wees). Hulle verskil net in die aantal neutrone, dus in die massagetal.","en":"False. Isotopes have the same number of protons, therefore the same atomic number (otherwise it would be a different element). They differ only in the number of neutrons, therefore in the mass number."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is Pauli se uitsluitingsbeginsel?","en":"Which statement is Pauli's exclusion principle?"},"options":[{"af":"Elektrone vul eers die orbitale met die laagste energie.","en":"Electrons fill the orbitals with the lowest energy first."},{"af":"'n Orbitaal kan hoogstens twee elektrone bevat, en hulle moet teenoorgestelde spin hê.","en":"An orbital can hold at most two electrons, and they must have opposite spins."},{"af":"Elektrone beset eers elke orbitaal in 'n subvlak enkel voordat hulle paar.","en":"Electrons first occupy each orbital in a sublevel singly before they pair up."},{"af":"Elke energievlak kan hoogstens 8 elektrone bevat.","en":"Each energy level can hold at most 8 electrons."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pauli: hoogstens twee elektrone per orbitaal, met teenoorgestelde spin (↑↓). Die eerste stelling is die Aufbau-beginsel en die derde is Hund se reël. Die laaste is vals: die maksimum per vlak is 2n², bv. 18 vir n = 3.","en":"Pauli: at most two electrons per orbital, with opposite spins (↑↓). The first statement is the Aufbau principle and the third is Hund's rule. The last is false: the maximum per level is 2n², e.g. 18 for n = 3."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel neutrone is daar in 'n atoom van ³⁹₁₉K? ___","en":"How many neutrons are there in an atom of ³⁹₁₉K? ___"},"answers":{"af":["20","20 neutrone"],"en":["20","20 neutrons"]},"explain":{"af":"Neutrone = A − Z = 39 − 19 = 20. Die boonste getal (39) is die massagetal en die onderste (19) die atoomgetal.","en":"Neutrons = A − Z = 39 − 19 = 20. The top number (39) is the mass number and the bottom one (19) the atomic number."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["58","19","39"],"en":["58","19","39"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel elektrone het die oksiedioon, ¹⁶₈O²⁻?","en":"How many electrons does the oxide ion, ¹⁶₈O²⁻, have?"},"options":[{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"16","en":"16"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elektrone = Z − lading = 8 − (−2) = 10. Die suurstofatoom het 2 elektrone bygekry. 6 is as jy die 2 aftrek in plaas van bytel, 8 is die neutrale atoom, en 16 is die massagetal.","en":"Electrons = Z − charge = 8 − (−2) = 10. The oxygen atom gained 2 electrons. 6 is if you subtract the 2 instead of adding it, 8 is the neutral atom, and 16 is the mass number."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die elektronkonfigurasie van kalsium (Z = 20)?","en":"What is the electron configuration of calcium (Z = 20)?"},"options":[{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 3d²","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 3d²"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s¹","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s¹"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁸","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁸"},{"af":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²","en":"1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p⁶ 4s²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ca het 20 elektrone. Ná 3p⁶ (18 elektrone) gaan die laaste twee na 4s, want 4s het 'n laer energie as 3d (Aufbau). 3d² ignoreer dit, 4s¹ het net 19 elektrone (dit is K), en 3p⁸ is onmoontlik – 'n p-subvlak hou hoogstens 6.","en":"Ca has 20 electrons. After 3p⁶ (18 electrons) the last two go into 4s, because 4s has a lower energy than 3d (Aufbau). 3d² ignores this, 4s¹ has only 19 electrons (that is K), and 3p⁸ is impossible – a p sublevel holds at most 6."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gallium bestaan uit 60,1 % Ga-69 en 39,9 % Ga-71. Bereken die relatiewe atoommassa van gallium (twee desimale plekke): ___","en":"Gallium consists of 60.1 % Ga-69 and 39.9 % Ga-71. Calculate the relative atomic mass of gallium (two decimal places): ___"},"answers":{"af":["69,80","69.80","69,8","69.8"],"en":["69.80","69,80","69.8","69,8"]},"explain":{"af":"Aᵣ = (69 × 60,1 + 71 × 39,9) ÷ 100 = (4 146,9 + 2 832,9) ÷ 100 = 6 979,8 ÷ 100 = 69,80. Geen eenheid nie. Die antwoord lê naaste aan 69, want Ga-69 kom die meeste voor.","en":"Aᵣ = (69 × 60.1 + 71 × 39.9) ÷ 100 = (4 146.9 + 2 832.9) ÷ 100 = 6 979.8 ÷ 100 = 69.80. No unit. The answer lies closest to 69, because Ga-69 is the most abundant."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["70,00","70,20","6979,80"],"en":["70.00","70.20","6979.80"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Stikstof (Z = 7) het die konfigurasie 1s² 2s² 2p³. Watter beskrywing van die drie 2p-orbitaalblokkies is korrek?","en":"Nitrogen (Z = 7) has the configuration 1s² 2s² 2p³. Which description of the three 2p orbital boxes is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"[↑↓] [↑] [  ]","en":"[↑↓] [↑] [  ]"},{"af":"[↑↑] [↑] [  ]","en":"[↑↑] [↑] [  ]"},{"af":"[↑] [↑] [↑]","en":"[↑] [↑] [↑]"},{"af":"[↑↓↑] [  ] [  ]","en":"[↑↓↑] [  ] [  ]"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hund se reël: elke 2p-orbitaal kry eers een elektron voordat enige paar, dus [↑] [↑] [↑] – drie ongepaarde elektrone. [↑↓] [↑] [  ] paar te vroeg (oortree Hund), [↑↑] het twee elektrone met dieselfde spin in een orbitaal, en [↑↓↑] het drie elektrone in een orbitaal (albei oortree Pauli).","en":"Hund's rule: each 2p orbital first gets one electron before any pair up, so [↑] [↑] [↑] – three unpaired electrons. [↑↓] [↑] [  ] pairs too early (breaks Hund), [↑↑] has two electrons with the same spin in one orbital, and [↑↓↑] has three electrons in one orbital (both break Pauli)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Chloor het 'n relatiewe atoommassa van 35,5 en bestaan uit net twee isotope, Cl-35 en Cl-37. Bereken die persentasie Cl-35: ___ %","en":"Chlorine has a relative atomic mass of 35.5 and consists of only two isotopes, Cl-35 and Cl-37. Calculate the percentage of Cl-35: ___ %"},"answers":{"af":["75","75 %","75%"],"en":["75","75 %","75%"]},"explain":{"af":"Laat Cl-35 = x % en Cl-37 = (100 − x) %. Dan 35x + 37(100 − x) = 35,5 × 100, dus 3 700 − 2x = 3 550, 2x = 150 en x = 75 %. Kontrole: 35,5 lê nader aan 35, so Cl-35 moet die meeste voorkom.","en":"Let Cl-35 = x % and Cl-37 = (100 − x) %. Then 35x + 37(100 − x) = 35.5 × 100, so 3 700 − 2x = 3 550, 2x = 150 and x = 75 %. Check: 35.5 lies closer to 35, so Cl-35 must be the most abundant."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["25","50","35,5"],"en":["25","50","35.5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder beweer: \"Cl-35 en Cl-37 reageer verskillend met natrium, want hulle het verskillende massas.\" Watter stelling evalueer die bewering die beste?","en":"A learner claims: \"Cl-35 and Cl-37 react differently with sodium, because they have different masses.\" Which statement best evaluates the claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Verkeerd: albei het 17 protone en 17 elektrone met dieselfde elektronkonfigurasie, dus het hulle dieselfde chemiese eienskappe.","en":"Wrong: both have 17 protons and 17 electrons with the same electron configuration, so they have the same chemical properties."},{"af":"Korrek: die swaarder isotoop het meer neutrone en reageer daarom heeltemal anders.","en":"Correct: the heavier isotope has more neutrons and therefore reacts completely differently."},{"af":"Verkeerd: Cl-37 het 2 ekstra elektrone, daarom reageer dit vinniger.","en":"Wrong: Cl-37 has 2 extra electrons, therefore it reacts faster."},{"af":"Korrek: isotope is verskillende elemente en het dus verskillende eienskappe.","en":"Correct: isotopes are different elements and therefore have different properties."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Chemiese eienskappe hang van die elektrone af, veral die valenselektrone. Isotope verskil net in die aantal neutrone (in die kern), dus het Cl-35 en Cl-37 dieselfde 17 elektrone, dieselfde konfigurasie en dieselfde chemiese eienskappe. Hulle is dieselfde element, en Cl-37 het 2 ekstra neutrone, nie elektrone nie.","en":"Chemical properties depend on the electrons, especially the valence electrons. Isotopes differ only in the number of neutrons (in the nucleus), so Cl-35 and Cl-37 have the same 17 electrons, the same configuration and the same chemical properties. They are the same element, and Cl-37 has 2 extra neutrons, not electrons."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-periodieke-tabel-binding","title":{"af":"Periodieke tabel en chemiese binding","en":"Periodic table and chemical bonding"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal tendense in die periodieke tabel met redes kan verduidelik, ione en formules kan skryf, en kovalente, ioniese en metaalbinding met Lewis-diagramme en eienskappe kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to explain trends in the periodic table with reasons, write ions and formulae, and describe covalent, ionic and metallic bonding with Lewis diagrams and properties."},"summary":{"af":"## Die periodieke tabel\n\nDie elemente is volgens **toenemende atoomgetal (Z)** gerangskik.\n\n- **Groep:** 'n vertikale kolom. Elemente in dieselfde groep het dieselfde aantal **valenselektrone** (elektrone in die buitenste energievlak) en daarom soortgelyke chemiese eienskappe.\n- **Periode:** 'n horisontale ry. Die periodenommer is gelyk aan die aantal energievlakke wat elektrone bevat.\n- **Metale** is links en in die middel (die oorgangsmetale, soos die platinum wat naby Brits gemyn word), **nie-metale** is regs, en **metalloïede** (bv. B en Si) lê op die trapvormige lyn tussen hulle.\n\n| Groep | Naam | Valenselektrone | Tipiese ioon |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | alkalimetale | 1 | Na⁺ (+1) |\n| 2 | aardalkalimetale | 2 | Mg²⁺ (+2) |\n| 13 | – | 3 | Al³⁺ (+3) |\n| 15 | – | 5 | N³⁻ (−3) |\n| 16 | – | 6 | O²⁻ (−2) |\n| 17 | halogene | 7 | Cl⁻ (−1) |\n| 18 | edelgasse | 8 (He: 2) | vorm nie ione nie |\n\n> **Wenk:** Vir groepe 13–18 is die aantal valenselektrone = groepnommer − 10. Uit die elektronkonfigurasie: Cl is 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁵, dus 3 energievlakke (periode 3) en 2 + 5 = 7 valenselektrone (groep 17).\n\nGroep 1-metale reageer heftig met water: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂. Hulle word **meer** reaktief laer af in die groep. Die halogene bestaan as diatomiese molekules (F₂, Cl₂) en word **minder** reaktief laer af. Edelgasse het 'n volle buitenste energievlak en is onreaktief.\n\n## Tendense en die redes\n\nTwee idees verklaar al die tendense:\n\n1. **Oor 'n periode (links → regs):** die kernlading (aantal protone) neem toe, maar die elektrone kom in **dieselfde** energievlak by. Die kern trek die buitenste elektrone sterker aan.\n2. **Af in 'n groep:** elke element het 'n **ekstra energievlak**. Die buitenste elektrone is verder van die kern en word deur die binneste elektrone afgeskerm, dus is die aantrekking swakker.\n\n| Eienskap | Definisie | Oor 'n periode → | Af in 'n groep ↓ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Atoomradius | die afstand van die middel van die kern tot by die buitenste elektrone | neem af | neem toe |\n| Eerste ionisasie-energie | die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder | neem toe | neem af |\n| Elektronaffiniteit | die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom of molekuul geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm | neem toe (in die algemeen) | neem af |\n| Elektronegatiwiteit | 'n maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek | neem toe | neem af |\n\nFluoor is die mees elektronegatiewe element (4,0). 'n Lae ionisasie-energie beteken dat die atoom maklik 'n elektron verloor, wat tipies van metale is. Daarom is K meer reaktief as Na.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Die atome word groter oor die periode, want daar is meer elektrone.\" Verkeerd! Die ekstra protone trek dieselfde energievlak nader, dus word die radius **kleiner**.\n\n## Chemiese binding\n\n'n **Chemiese binding** is 'n wedersydse aantrekking tussen twee atome as gevolg van die gelyktydige aantrekking tussen hul kerne en die buitenste elektrone. Atome bind om 'n stabiele **edelgaskonfigurasie** te kry: 8 valenselektrone (die **oktetreël**), of 2 vir H.\n\n### Kovalente binding: nie-metaal + nie-metaal\n\nDie **deel van elektrone** tussen twee atome om 'n molekuul te vorm. Een gedeelde elektronpaar is 'n enkelbinding (H–H), twee is 'n dubbelbinding (O=O) en drie is 'n drievoudige binding (N≡N). 'n Elektronpaar wat nie gedeel word nie, is 'n **alleenpaar** (nie-bindende paar).\n\n### Ioniese binding: metaal + nie-metaal\n\nDie **oordrag van elektrone**: die metaal verloor elektrone en vorm **katione** (positiewe ione); die nie-metaal kry elektrone en vorm **anione** (negatiewe ione). Die teenoorgesteld gelaaide ione trek mekaar elektrostaties aan en vorm 'n **kristalrooster**. Die eenvoudigste verhouding van die ione is 'n **formule-eenheid**, bv. NaCl (die sout op jou braaivleis). 'n Groot verskil in elektronegatiwiteit tussen die atome lei tot elektronoordrag.\n\n**Formules met die kruismetode:** skryf die ione neer, ruil die getalle van die ladings om en vereenvoudig. Die totale lading moet nul wees.\n\n- Mg²⁺ en Cl⁻ → MgCl₂\n- Al³⁺ en O²⁻ → Al₂O₃\n- Ca²⁺ en OH⁻ → Ca(OH)₂ (hakies om 'n saamgestelde ioon)\n\n### Metaalbinding: metaalatome\n\nDie binding tussen positiewe ione en 'n **see van gedelokaliseerde elektrone**. Die metaalatome gee hul valenselektrone af, en dié elektrone beweeg vrylik deur die hele metaal, bv. in die koperdrade van 'n kragkabel.\n\n## Lewis-diagramme (in woorde)\n\n'n Lewis-diagram toon die valenselektrone as kolletjies (of kruisies) om die simbool van die element.\n\n| Stof | Beskrywing van die Lewis-diagram |\n|---|---|\n| H₂O | O in die middel; 2 bindingspare (O–H) en 2 alleenpare op die O |\n| NH₃ | N in die middel; 3 bindingspare en 1 alleenpaar |\n| CH₄ | C in die middel; 4 bindingspare en geen alleenpare nie |\n| CO₂ | O=C=O: 2 dubbelbindings (4 bindingspare); elke O het 2 alleenpare |\n| NaCl | [Na]⁺ sonder kolletjies en [Cl]⁻ met 8 elektrone, elkeen in vierkantige hakies met sy lading |\n\n## Eienskappe\n\n| | Ionies (NaCl) | Kovalent molekulêr (H₂O, CO₂) | Metaal (Cu) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Smelt- en kookpunt | hoog: sterk aantrekking tussen ione oral in die rooster | laag: swak kragte tussen die molekules | meestal hoog |\n| Elektriese geleiding | slegs gesmelt of in water opgelos (die ione kan dan beweeg) | geen: geen vrye gelaaide deeltjies nie | ja, ook as vastestof (vrye elektrone) |\n| Ander | hard maar bros; baie los in water op | dikwels gasse of vloeistowwe by kamertemperatuur | smeebaar, rekbaar, blink (metaalglans), goeie hittegeleiers |\n\nKovalente **netwerkstrukture** (diamant, SiO₂) is anders: hulle is baie hard en het baie hoë smeltpunte.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Wanneer water kook, breek die O–H-bindings **nie**. Slegs die swak kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom.","en":"## The periodic table\n\nThe elements are arranged in order of **increasing atomic number (Z)**.\n\n- **Group:** a vertical column. Elements in the same group have the same number of **valence electrons** (electrons in the outermost energy level) and therefore similar chemical properties.\n- **Period:** a horizontal row. The period number equals the number of energy levels that contain electrons.\n- **Metals** are on the left and in the middle (the transition metals, such as the platinum mined near Brits), **non-metals** are on the right, and **metalloids** (e.g. B and Si) lie on the staircase line between them.\n\n| Group | Name | Valence electrons | Typical ion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | alkali metals | 1 | Na⁺ (+1) |\n| 2 | alkaline earth metals | 2 | Mg²⁺ (+2) |\n| 13 | – | 3 | Al³⁺ (+3) |\n| 15 | – | 5 | N³⁻ (−3) |\n| 16 | – | 6 | O²⁻ (−2) |\n| 17 | halogens | 7 | Cl⁻ (−1) |\n| 18 | noble gases | 8 (He: 2) | do not form ions |\n\n> **Tip:** For groups 13–18 the number of valence electrons = group number − 10. From the electron configuration: Cl is 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁵, so 3 energy levels (period 3) and 2 + 5 = 7 valence electrons (group 17).\n\nGroup 1 metals react vigorously with water: 2Na + 2H₂O → 2NaOH + H₂. They become **more** reactive further down the group. The halogens exist as diatomic molecules (F₂, Cl₂) and become **less** reactive further down. Noble gases have a full outer energy level and are unreactive.\n\n## Trends and the reasons\n\nTwo ideas explain all the trends:\n\n1. **Across a period (left → right):** the nuclear charge (number of protons) increases, but the electrons are added to the **same** energy level. The nucleus attracts the outer electrons more strongly.\n2. **Down a group:** each element has an **extra energy level**. The outer electrons are further from the nucleus and are shielded by the inner electrons, so the attraction is weaker.\n\n| Property | Definition | Across a period → | Down a group ↓ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Atomic radius | the distance from the centre of the nucleus to the outermost electrons | decreases | increases |\n| First ionisation energy | the energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase | increases | decreases |\n| Electron affinity | the energy released when an electron is attached to an atom or molecule to form a negative ion | increases (in general) | decreases |\n| Electronegativity | a measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons | increases | decreases |\n\nFluorine is the most electronegative element (4.0). A low ionisation energy means the atom loses an electron easily, which is typical of metals. That is why K is more reactive than Na.\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"The atoms get bigger across the period because there are more electrons.\" Wrong! The extra protons pull the same energy level closer, so the radius becomes **smaller**.\n\n## Chemical bonding\n\nA **chemical bond** is a mutual attraction between two atoms resulting from the simultaneous attraction between their nuclei and the outer electrons. Atoms bond to obtain a stable **noble gas configuration**: 8 valence electrons (the **octet rule**), or 2 for H.\n\n### Covalent bonding: non-metal + non-metal\n\nThe **sharing of electrons** between two atoms to form a molecule. One shared electron pair is a single bond (H–H), two is a double bond (O=O) and three is a triple bond (N≡N). An electron pair that is not shared is a **lone pair** (non-bonding pair).\n\n### Ionic bonding: metal + non-metal\n\nThe **transfer of electrons**: the metal loses electrons and forms **cations** (positive ions); the non-metal gains electrons and forms **anions** (negative ions). The oppositely charged ions attract each other electrostatically and form a **crystal lattice**. The simplest ratio of the ions is a **formula unit**, e.g. NaCl (the salt on your braai meat). A large difference in electronegativity between the atoms leads to electron transfer.\n\n**Formulae with the criss-cross method:** write down the ions, swap the numbers of the charges and simplify. The total charge must be zero.\n\n- Mg²⁺ and Cl⁻ → MgCl₂\n- Al³⁺ and O²⁻ → Al₂O₃\n- Ca²⁺ and OH⁻ → Ca(OH)₂ (brackets around a compound ion)\n\n### Metallic bonding: metal atoms\n\nThe bond between positive ions and a **sea of delocalised electrons**. The metal atoms give up their valence electrons, and these electrons move freely through the whole metal, e.g. in the copper wires of a power cable.\n\n## Lewis diagrams (in words)\n\nA Lewis diagram shows the valence electrons as dots (or crosses) around the symbol of the element.\n\n| Substance | Description of the Lewis diagram |\n|---|---|\n| H₂O | O in the centre; 2 bonding pairs (O–H) and 2 lone pairs on the O |\n| NH₃ | N in the centre; 3 bonding pairs and 1 lone pair |\n| CH₄ | C in the centre; 4 bonding pairs and no lone pairs |\n| CO₂ | O=C=O: 2 double bonds (4 bonding pairs); each O has 2 lone pairs |\n| NaCl | [Na]⁺ with no dots and [Cl]⁻ with 8 electrons, each in square brackets with its charge |\n\n## Properties\n\n| | Ionic (NaCl) | Covalent molecular (H₂O, CO₂) | Metal (Cu) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Melting and boiling point | high: strong attraction between ions throughout the lattice | low: weak forces between the molecules | mostly high |\n| Electrical conduction | only when molten or dissolved in water (the ions can then move) | none: no free charged particles | yes, also as a solid (free electrons) |\n| Other | hard but brittle; many dissolve in water | often gases or liquids at room temperature | malleable, ductile, shiny (lustre), good conductors of heat |\n\nCovalent **network structures** (diamond, SiO₂) are different: they are very hard and have very high melting points.\n\n> **Common mistake:** When water boils, the O–H bonds do **not** break. Only the weak forces between the molecules are overcome."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Valenselektrone","en":"Valence electrons"},"def":{"af":"Die elektrone in die buitenste energievlak van 'n atoom. Hulle neem deel aan binding.","en":"The electrons in the outermost energy level of an atom. They take part in bonding."}},{"term":{"af":"Atoomradius","en":"Atomic radius"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand van die middel van die kern van 'n atoom tot by sy buitenste elektrone.","en":"The distance from the centre of the nucleus of an atom to its outermost electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Eerste ionisasie-energie","en":"First ionisation energy"},"def":{"af":"Die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder.","en":"The energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronaffiniteit","en":"Electron affinity"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom of molekuul geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm.","en":"The energy released when an electron is attached to an atom or molecule to form a negative ion."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektronegatiwiteit","en":"Electronegativity"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek.","en":"A measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Chemiese binding","en":"Chemical bond"},"def":{"af":"'n Wedersydse aantrekking tussen twee atome as gevolg van die gelyktydige aantrekking tussen hul kerne en die buitenste elektrone.","en":"A mutual attraction between two atoms resulting from the simultaneous attraction between their nuclei and the outer electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Kovalente binding","en":"Covalent bond"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van elektrone tussen twee atome om 'n molekuul te vorm.","en":"The sharing of electrons between two atoms to form a molecule."}},{"term":{"af":"Ioniese binding","en":"Ionic bond"},"def":{"af":"Die oordrag van elektrone om katione (positiewe ione) en anione (negatiewe ione) te vorm wat mekaar elektrostaties aantrek.","en":"The transfer of electrons to form cations (positive ions) and anions (negative ions) that attract each other electrostatically."}},{"term":{"af":"Metaalbinding","en":"Metallic bond"},"def":{"af":"Die binding tussen positiewe ione en 'n see van gedelokaliseerde elektrone.","en":"The bond between positive ions and a sea of delocalised electrons."}},{"term":{"af":"Lewis-diagram","en":"Lewis diagram"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorstelling van 'n atoom, ioon of molekuul waarin die valenselektrone as kolletjies of kruisies om die simbool van die element geteken word.","en":"A representation of an atom, ion or molecule in which the valence electrons are drawn as dots or crosses around the symbol of the element."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van elektronkonfigurasie na groep, periode en ioon","en":"From electron configuration to group, period and ion"},"problem":{"af":"Element X het atoomgetal 16. (a) Skryf die elektronkonfigurasie van X (sp-notasie). (b) In watter periode en groep is X? (c) Hoeveel valenselektrone het X, en watter ioon vorm dit? (d) Is X 'n metaal of 'n nie-metaal?","en":"Element X has atomic number 16. (a) Write the electron configuration of X (sp notation). (b) In which period and group is X? (c) How many valence electrons does X have, and which ion does it form? (d) Is X a metal or a non-metal?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Neutrale atoom met Z = 16 het 16 elektrone: 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴. Kontroleer: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 16.","en":"(a) A neutral atom with Z = 16 has 16 electrons: 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴. Check: 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 + 4 = 16."},{"af":"(b) Die hoogste energievlak is 3, dus is X in periode 3. Die buitenste energievlak (3s²3p⁴) bevat 6 elektrone, dus groep 6 + 10 = 16.","en":"(b) The highest energy level is 3, so X is in period 3. The outer energy level (3s²3p⁴) holds 6 electrons, so group 6 + 10 = 16."},{"af":"(c) X het 6 valenselektrone. Dit is makliker om 2 elektrone te kry as om 6 te verloor, dus vorm X 'n X²⁻-ioon met die edelgaskonfigurasie van Ar.","en":"(c) X has 6 valence electrons. It is easier to gain 2 electrons than to lose 6, so X forms an X²⁻ ion with the noble gas configuration of Ar."},{"af":"(d) X is swael (S). Dit lê regs in die periodieke tabel en kry elektrone, dus is dit 'n nie-metaal.","en":"(d) X is sulfur (S). It lies on the right of the periodic table and gains electrons, so it is a non-metal."}],"answer":{"af":"1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴; periode 3, groep 16; 6 valenselektrone, vorm S²⁻; nie-metaal (swael)","en":"1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p⁴; period 3, group 16; 6 valence electrons, forms S²⁻; non-metal (sulfur)"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik 'n tendens","en":"Explain a trend"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Verduidelik waarom die atoomradius van natrium (Na) groter is as dié van chloor (Cl). (b) Verduidelik waarom kalium (K) heftiger met water reageer as natrium.","en":"(a) Explain why the atomic radius of sodium (Na) is larger than that of chlorine (Cl). (b) Explain why potassium (K) reacts more vigorously with water than sodium."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Na en Cl is albei in periode 3: hul buitenste elektrone is in dieselfde (derde) energievlak.","en":"(a) Na and Cl are both in period 3: their outer electrons are in the same (third) energy level."},{"af":"Cl het 17 protone en Na net 11. Die groter kernlading van Cl trek die buitenste elektrone sterker na die kern, dus is die Cl-atoom kleiner.","en":"Cl has 17 protons and Na only 11. The greater nuclear charge of Cl pulls the outer electrons more strongly towards the nucleus, so the Cl atom is smaller."},{"af":"(b) K (periode 4) het een energievlak meer as Na (periode 3). Sy valenselektron is verder van die kern en word meer deur die binneste elektrone afgeskerm.","en":"(b) K (period 4) has one more energy level than Na (period 3). Its valence electron is further from the nucleus and more shielded by the inner electrons."},{"af":"Die aantrekking op dié elektron is swakker, dus het K 'n laer ionisasie-energie. K verloor sy valenselektron makliker en reageer heftiger.","en":"The attraction on that electron is weaker, so K has a lower ionisation energy. K loses its valence electron more easily and reacts more vigorously."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Dieselfde aantal energievlakke, maar Cl het 'n groter kernlading wat die elektrone nader trek. (b) K se valenselektron is verder van die kern en meer afgeskerm, dus laer ionisasie-energie en hoër reaktiwiteit.","en":"(a) Same number of energy levels, but Cl has a greater nuclear charge that pulls the electrons closer. (b) K's valence electron is further from the nucleus and more shielded, so lower ionisation energy and higher reactivity."}},{"title":{"af":"Ioniese binding en formules","en":"Ionic bonding and formulae"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesium reageer met chloor. (a) Beskryf hoe die ione vorm. (b) Beskryf die Lewis-diagram van die produk in woorde. (c) Skryf die formule van die produk. (d) Gebruik die kruismetode om die formule van aluminiumoksied te skryf.","en":"Magnesium reacts with chlorine. (a) Describe how the ions form. (b) Describe the Lewis diagram of the product in words. (c) Write the formula of the product. (d) Use the criss-cross method to write the formula of aluminium oxide."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Mg (2 valenselektrone) verloor 2 elektrone en word Mg²⁺ met die konfigurasie van Ne. Elke Cl-atoom (7 valenselektrone) kry 1 elektron en word Cl⁻ met die konfigurasie van Ar. Een Mg-atoom gee dus een elektron aan elk van twee Cl-atome.","en":"(a) Mg (2 valence electrons) loses 2 electrons and becomes Mg²⁺ with the configuration of Ne. Each Cl atom (7 valence electrons) gains 1 electron and becomes Cl⁻ with the configuration of Ar. One Mg atom therefore gives one electron to each of two Cl atoms."},{"af":"(b) Lewis-diagram: [Mg]²⁺ sonder valenselektrone in vierkantige hakies, en twee [Cl]⁻-ione, elk met 8 elektrone (7 kolletjies en 1 kruisie van Mg) in vierkantige hakies met die lading.","en":"(b) Lewis diagram: [Mg]²⁺ with no valence electrons in square brackets, and two [Cl]⁻ ions, each with 8 electrons (7 dots and 1 cross from Mg) in square brackets with the charge."},{"af":"(c) Totale lading: (+2) + 2(−1) = 0, dus is die formule MgCl₂.","en":"(c) Total charge: (+2) + 2(−1) = 0, so the formula is MgCl₂."},{"af":"(d) Al³⁺ en O²⁻: ruil die getalle van die ladings om → Al₂O₃. Kontroleer: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = +6 − 6 = 0.","en":"(d) Al³⁺ and O²⁻: swap the numbers of the charges → Al₂O₃. Check: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = +6 − 6 = 0."}],"answer":{"af":"MgCl₂ (magnesiumchloried); Al₂O₃ (aluminiumoksied)","en":"MgCl₂ (magnesium chloride); Al₂O₃ (aluminium oxide)"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die binding uit die eienskappe","en":"Identify the bonding from the properties"},"problem":{"af":"Drie vastestowwe word getoets. A smelt by 801 °C en gelei nie as vastestof nie, maar wel wanneer dit in water opgelos is. B smelt by 1 085 °C, gelei as vastestof en kan in draad uitgetrek word. C smelt reeds by 80 °C en gelei in geen toestand nie. Identifiseer die tipe binding in elke stof en verduidelik telkens.","en":"Three solids are tested. A melts at 801 °C and does not conduct as a solid, but does conduct when dissolved in water. B melts at 1 085 °C, conducts as a solid and can be drawn into a wire. C already melts at 80 °C and does not conduct in any state. Identify the type of bonding in each substance and explain each time."},"steps":[{"af":"A: hoë smeltpunt en gelei slegs in oplossing → ionies. In die vastestof sit die ione vas in die kristalrooster; in oplossing kan die ione vrylik beweeg en lading dra.","en":"A: high melting point and conducts only in solution → ionic. In the solid the ions are fixed in the crystal lattice; in solution the ions can move freely and carry charge."},{"af":"B: gelei as vastestof en is rekbaar → metaalbinding. Die gedelokaliseerde elektrone beweeg vrylik, en die lae positiewe ione kan oor mekaar gly sonder dat die metaal breek.","en":"B: conducts as a solid and is ductile → metallic bonding. The delocalised electrons move freely, and the layers of positive ions can slide over each other without the metal breaking."},{"af":"C: lae smeltpunt en gelei nooit → kovalent (molekulêr). Net swak kragte hou die molekules bymekaar, en daar is geen vrye gelaaide deeltjies nie.","en":"C: low melting point and never conducts → covalent (molecular). Only weak forces hold the molecules together, and there are no free charged particles."}],"answer":{"af":"A: ionies; B: metaalbinding; C: kovalent molekulêr","en":"A: ionic; B: metallic bonding; C: covalent molecular"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke groep in die periodieke tabel by sy naam.","en":"Match each group in the periodic table to its name."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Groep 1","en":"Group 1"},"r":{"af":"Alkalimetale","en":"Alkali metals"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 2","en":"Group 2"},"r":{"af":"Aardalkalimetale","en":"Alkaline earth metals"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 17","en":"Group 17"},"r":{"af":"Halogene","en":"Halogens"}},{"l":{"af":"Groep 18","en":"Group 18"},"r":{"af":"Edelgasse","en":"Noble gases"}}],"explain":{"af":"Groep 1: alkalimetale (1 valenselektron); groep 2: aardalkalimetale (2); groep 17: halogene (7); groep 18: edelgasse (volle buitenste energievlak).","en":"Group 1: alkali metals (1 valence electron); group 2: alkaline earth metals (2); group 17: halogens (7); group 18: noble gases (full outer energy level)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van elektronegatiwiteit?","en":"Which statement is the definition of electronegativity?"},"options":[{"af":"Die energie benodig per mol om die eerste elektron uit 'n atoom in die gasfase te verwyder","en":"The energy needed per mole to remove the first electron from an atom in the gaseous phase"},{"af":"Die energie wat vrygestel word wanneer 'n elektron aan 'n atoom geheg word om 'n negatiewe ioon te vorm","en":"The energy released when an electron is attached to an atom to form a negative ion"},{"af":"'n Maatstaf van die neiging van 'n atoom in 'n molekuul om bindingselektrone aan te trek","en":"A measure of the tendency of an atom in a molecule to attract bonding electrons"},{"af":"Die afstand van die middel van die kern tot by die buitenste elektrone","en":"The distance from the centre of the nucleus to the outermost electrons"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elektronegatiwiteit gaan oor bindingselektrone in 'n molekuul. Die eerste opsie is ionisasie-energie, die tweede elektronaffiniteit en die laaste atoomradius.","en":"Electronegativity is about bonding electrons in a molecule. The first option is ionisation energy, the second electron affinity and the last atomic radius."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Fosfor (P) is in groep 15. Hoeveel valenselektrone het 'n fosforatoom? ___","en":"Phosphorus (P) is in group 15. How many valence electrons does a phosphorus atom have? ___"},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf","5 valenselektrone","5 elektrone"],"en":["5","five","5 valence electrons","5 electrons"]},"explain":{"af":"Vir groepe 13–18: valenselektrone = groepnommer − 10 = 15 − 10 = 5 (konfigurasie 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p³: 2 + 3 = 5).","en":"For groups 13–18: valence electrons = group number − 10 = 15 − 10 = 5 (configuration 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p³: 2 + 3 = 5)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["15","3","2"],"en":["15","3","2"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die atoomradius neem af van links na regs oor 'n periode.","en":"The atomic radius decreases from left to right across a period."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die kernlading neem toe terwyl die elektrone in dieselfde energievlak bykom, dus word die buitenste elektrone nader aan die kern getrek.","en":"True. The nuclear charge increases while the electrons are added to the same energy level, so the outer electrons are pulled closer to the nucleus."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van hierdie elemente het die hoogste eerste ionisasie-energie?","en":"Which of these elements has the highest first ionisation energy?"},"options":[{"af":"K","en":"K"},{"af":"Na","en":"Na"},{"af":"Mg","en":"Mg"},{"af":"Ar","en":"Ar"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ionisasie-energie neem toe oor 'n periode en af in 'n groep. Ar is 'n edelgas heel regs in periode 3 met 'n volle buitenste energievlak. K het die laagste, want dit is laer af in groep 1.","en":"Ionisation energy increases across a period and decreases down a group. Ar is a noble gas on the far right of period 3 with a full outer energy level. K has the lowest, because it is further down group 1."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vaste natriumchloried gelei elektrisiteit, want dit bestaan uit ione.","en":"Solid sodium chloride conducts electricity because it consists of ions."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In die vastestof sit die ione vas in die kristalrooster en kan nie beweeg nie. NaCl gelei slegs wanneer dit gesmelt of in water opgelos is.","en":"False. In the solid the ions are fixed in the crystal lattice and cannot move. NaCl conducts only when it is molten or dissolved in water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stof bestaan uit 'n kristalrooster van positiewe en negatiewe ione?","en":"Which substance consists of a crystal lattice of positive and negative ions?"},"options":[{"af":"KBr","en":"KBr"},{"af":"Cu","en":"Cu"},{"af":"CO₂","en":"CO₂"},{"af":"H₂O","en":"H₂O"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"KBr is 'n metaal (K) plus 'n nie-metaal (Br): ioniese binding. Cu het metaalbinding (positiewe ione in 'n see van elektrone), en CO₂ en H₂O is kovalente molekules.","en":"KBr is a metal (K) plus a non-metal (Br): ionic bonding. Cu has metallic bonding (positive ions in a sea of electrons), and CO₂ and H₂O are covalent molecules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel elektrone het 'n Ca²⁺-ioon? (Atoomgetal van Ca = 20) ___","en":"How many electrons does a Ca²⁺ ion have? (Atomic number of Ca = 20) ___"},"answers":{"af":["18","18 elektrone","agtien"],"en":["18","18 electrons","eighteen"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Ca-atoom het 20 elektrone. Die lading 2+ beteken dat dit 2 elektrone verloor het: 20 − 2 = 18. (22 is die algemene fout: die elektrone bytel.)","en":"A Ca atom has 20 electrons. The 2+ charge means it lost 2 electrons: 20 − 2 = 18. (22 is the common mistake: adding the electrons.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["22","20","40"],"en":["22","20","40"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruik die kruismetode. Die formule van aluminiumoksied is ___.","en":"Use the criss-cross method. The formula of aluminium oxide is ___."},"answers":{"af":["Al₂O₃","Al2O3"],"en":["Al₂O₃","Al2O3"]},"explain":{"af":"Al³⁺ en O²⁻: ruil die getalle van die ladings om → Al₂O₃. Kontroleer: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = 0.","en":"Al³⁺ and O²⁻: swap the numbers of the charges → Al₂O₃. Check: 2(+3) + 3(−2) = 0."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Al₃O₂","AlO","Al₂O"],"en":["Al₃O₂","AlO","Al₂O"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Element X het die elektronkonfigurasie 1s²2s²2p⁶3s². Wat is die formule van die verbinding wat X met chloor vorm?","en":"Element X has the electron configuration 1s²2s²2p⁶3s². What is the formula of the compound that X forms with chlorine?"},"options":[{"af":"XCl","en":"XCl"},{"af":"X₂Cl","en":"X₂Cl"},{"af":"XCl₂","en":"XCl₂"},{"af":"XCl₃","en":"XCl₃"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"X het 2 valenselektrone (3s²), dus vorm dit X²⁺ (dit is Mg). Chloor vorm Cl⁻. Vir 'n totale lading van nul is twee Cl⁻ nodig: XCl₂. X₂Cl is die kruismetode verkeerd om gedoen.","en":"X has 2 valence electrons (3s²), so it forms X²⁺ (it is Mg). Chlorine forms Cl⁻. For a total charge of zero, two Cl⁻ are needed: XCl₂. X₂Cl is the criss-cross method done the wrong way round."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel alleenpare (nie-bindende elektronpare) is daar op die suurstofatoom in die Lewis-diagram van 'n watermolekuul (H₂O)? ___","en":"How many lone pairs (non-bonding electron pairs) are there on the oxygen atom in the Lewis diagram of a water molecule (H₂O)? ___"},"answers":{"af":["2","twee","2 alleenpare"],"en":["2","two","2 lone pairs"]},"explain":{"af":"O het 6 valenselektrone. Twee daarvan word met die twee H-atome gedeel (2 bindingspare), en die oorblywende 4 elektrone vorm 2 alleenpare. Nou het O 'n oktet.","en":"O has 6 valence electrons. Two of them are shared with the two H atoms (2 bonding pairs), and the remaining 4 electrons form 2 lone pairs. O now has an octet."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","6","3"],"en":["4","6","3"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel bindende elektronpare is daar altesaam in die Lewis-diagram van CO₂?","en":"How many bonding electron pairs are there in total in the Lewis diagram of CO₂?"},"options":[{"af":"2","en":"2"},{"af":"4","en":"4"},{"af":"6","en":"6"},{"af":"8","en":"8"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"CO₂ is O=C=O: twee dubbelbindings, elk met 2 gedeelde pare, dus 4 bindende pare. Dit is 8 bindingselektrone, maar die vraag vra na pare. 2 sou wees as jy enkelbindings teken; dan het C nie 'n oktet nie.","en":"CO₂ is O=C=O: two double bonds, each with 2 shared pairs, so 4 bonding pairs. That is 8 bonding electrons, but the question asks for pairs. 2 would be if you drew single bonds; then C would not have an octet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is die atoomradius van kalium (K) groter as dié van natrium (Na)?","en":"Why is the atomic radius of potassium (K) larger than that of sodium (Na)?"},"options":[{"af":"K het meer protone, so die kern stoot die elektrone verder weg","en":"K has more protons, so the nucleus pushes the electrons further away"},{"af":"K het meer neutrone, wat die atoom groter maak","en":"K has more neutrons, which make the atom bigger"},{"af":"K het 'n hoër elektronegatiwiteit as Na","en":"K has a higher electronegativity than Na"},{"af":"K het 'n ekstra energievlak, dus is sy buitenste elektron verder van die kern","en":"K has an extra energy level, so its outer electron is further from the nucleus"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"K is in periode 4 en Na in periode 3. Die ekstra energievlak plaas die valenselektron verder van die kern, en die binneste elektrone skerm dit af. Protone trek elektrone aan (stoot nie), neutrone bepaal nie die grootte nie, en K se elektronegatiwiteit (0,8) is laer as Na s'n (0,9).","en":"K is in period 4 and Na in period 3. The extra energy level places the valence electron further from the nucleus, and the inner electrons shield it. Protons attract electrons (they do not repel them), neutrons do not determine the size, and K's electronegativity (0.8) is lower than Na's (0.9)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Metaan (CH₄) kook by −162 °C. 'n Leerder sê: \"Dit is omdat die C–H-bindings in metaan swak is en maklik breek.\" Watter evaluering van die stelling is korrek?","en":"Methane (CH₄) boils at −162 °C. A learner says: \"This is because the C–H bonds in methane are weak and break easily.\" Which evaluation of the statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Korrek: kovalente bindings is altyd swak","en":"Correct: covalent bonds are always weak"},{"af":"Verkeerd: tydens kook breek die C–H-bindings nie; slegs die swak kragte tussen die metaanmolekules word oorkom","en":"Wrong: during boiling the C–H bonds do not break; only the weak forces between the methane molecules are overcome"},{"af":"Verkeerd: metaan is 'n ioniese stof, en ione trek mekaar swak aan","en":"Wrong: methane is an ionic substance, and ions attract each other weakly"},{"af":"Korrek: tydens kook skei die H-atome van die C-atoom","en":"Correct: during boiling the H atoms separate from the C atom"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gasvormige metaan bestaan steeds uit CH₄-molekules, dus het die C–H-bindings nie gebreek nie. Die lae kookpunt kom van die swak kragte tussen die molekules. Kovalente bindings self is sterk, en C en H is albei nie-metale, dus is metaan kovalent, nie ionies nie.","en":"Gaseous methane still consists of CH₄ molecules, so the C–H bonds did not break. The low boiling point comes from the weak forces between the molecules. Covalent bonds themselves are strong, and C and H are both non-metals, so methane is covalent, not ionic."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-pulse-transversale-golwe","title":{"af":"Pulse en transversale golwe","en":"Pulses and transverse waves"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal pulse en transversale golwe kan beskryf, superposisie kan toepas en golfberekeninge met v = fλ en T = 1/f kan doen.","en":"You will be able to describe pulses and transverse waves, apply superposition and do wave calculations with v = fλ and T = 1/f."},"summary":{"af":"## Pulse\n\n'n **Puls** is 'n enkele versteuring in 'n medium. Swaai die punt van 'n lang tou een keer op en af, en 'n bult beweeg langs die tou. Die **medium** is die stof waardeur die puls beweeg, soos die tou of 'n veer.\n\n'n **Transversale puls** is 'n puls waar die deeltjies van die medium **loodreg** op die bewegingsrigting van die puls beweeg. Die puls beweeg horisontaal, maar elke stukkie tou beweeg net op en af en keer terug na sy **rus- (ewewigs)posisie**. 'n Puls dra **energie** oor, nie die medium self nie. Dink aan die Mexikaanse golf op Loftus: die toeskouers bly by hul sitplekke en staan net op en sit, maar die golf beweeg om die hele pawiljoen.\n\n- **Amplitude:** die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy rus- (ewewigs)posisie. Meet dit vanaf die ewewigsposisie, **nie** van bo tot onder nie.\n- **Pulslengte:** die horisontale lengte van die puls.\n- Die spoed van 'n puls hang slegs af van die **medium** (bv. hoe styf gespan en hoe dik die tou is), nie van die amplitude nie.\n\n## Superposisie en interferensie\n\nAs twee pulse mekaar ontmoet, tel hulle versteurings bymekaar. **Superposisie** is die algebraïese som van die amplitudes van twee pulse wat dieselfde ruimte op dieselfde tyd beset.\n\nKies \"op\" as positief en \"af\" as negatief:\n\n- **Konstruktiewe interferensie:** 'n kruin oorvleuel met 'n kruin (of 'n trog met 'n trog). Die resulterende amplitude is **groter**: 4 cm + 3 cm = 7 cm.\n- **Destruktiewe interferensie:** 'n kruin oorvleuel met 'n trog. Die resulterende amplitude is **kleiner**: 4 cm + (−3 cm) = 1 cm (bo die ewewigsposisie). As die twee amplitudes ewe groot is, is die resultaat nul: volledige destruktiewe interferensie.\n\nNá die ontmoeting beweeg elke puls **onveranderd** verder, met sy oorspronklike vorm, amplitude en rigting.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om by destruktiewe interferensie die groottes bymekaar te tel. Gebruik die tekens: 'n puls onder die ewewigsposisie is negatief.\n\n## Transversale golwe\n\n'n **Golf** is 'n opeenvolging van pulse. 'n **Transversale golf** is 'n golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium **loodreg** op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.\n\n| Begrip | Definisie | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kruin | die hoogste punt op die golf (maksimum positiewe versteuring) | – |\n| Trog | die laagste punt op die golf (maksimum negatiewe versteuring) | – |\n| Amplitude | die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie | m |\n| Golflengte (λ) | die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase, bv. van kruin tot kruin | m |\n| Frekwensie (f) | die aantal golfpulse per sekonde | Hz (= s⁻¹) |\n| Periode (T) | die tyd wat dit neem vir een volledige golfpuls | s |\n\n### Punte in fase en uit fase\n\nPunte **in fase** is op presies dieselfde posisie in die siklus en beweeg in dieselfde rigting, bv. twee kruine of twee trôe. Hulle is 'n heelgetal golflengtes (1λ; 2λ; 3λ …) uitmekaar. Punte wat nie in fase is nie, is **uit fase**. 'n Kruin en die volgende trog is ½λ uitmekaar en is heeltemal uit fase.\n\n## Die formules\n\n- **T = [[1/f]]** en **f = [[1/T]]**: die periode en frekwensie is mekaar se omgekeerdes.\n- **v = fλ**: golfspoed (m·s⁻¹) = frekwensie (Hz) × golflengte (m).\n- Afstand wat die golf aflê: afstand = v × t.\n\n**Hoekom werk v = fλ?** In een periode T beweeg die golf presies een golflengte λ vorentoe, dus v = [[λ/T]] = fλ.\n\n- Die golfspoed hang van die **medium** af. In dieselfde medium bly v konstant: as f verdubbel, halveer λ.\n- Skakel eers om na SI-eenhede: cm → m (÷ 100), kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000).\n\n> **Wenk:** \"20 golwe gaan in 4 s verby\" beteken f = [[20/4]] = 5 Hz. \"Die afstand tussen 'n kruin en die volgende trog is 0,5 m\" beteken λ = 2 × 0,5 = 1 m.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die vertikale afstand van kruin tot trog as die amplitude te gebruik. Die amplitude is die **helfte** daarvan.\n\n## Grafieke in woorde\n\nOp 'n **verplasing-posisie-grafiek** (y-as: versteuring; x-as: afstand in m) lees jy die amplitude vertikaal af en die golflengte horisontaal, van kruin tot kruin. Op 'n **verplasing-tyd-grafiek** (x-as: tyd in s) is die tyd van kruin tot kruin die **periode T**, nie die golflengte nie.\n\n## Stappe vir berekeninge\n\n1. Lys die gegewe waardes en skakel om na SI-eenhede.\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Vervang en bereken.\n4. Gee die antwoord met die eenheid, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.","en":"## Pulses\n\nA **pulse** is a single disturbance in a medium. Flick the end of a long rope up and down once, and a bump travels along the rope. The **medium** is the substance through which the pulse travels, such as the rope or a spring.\n\nA **transverse pulse** is a pulse in which the particles of the medium move **perpendicular** to the direction of motion of the pulse. The pulse travels horizontally, but each piece of rope only moves up and down and returns to its **rest (equilibrium) position**. A pulse transfers **energy**, not the medium itself. Think of the Mexican wave at Loftus: the spectators stay at their seats and only stand up and sit down, but the wave moves around the whole stand.\n\n- **Amplitude:** the maximum disturbance of a particle from its rest (equilibrium) position. Measure it from the equilibrium position, **not** from top to bottom.\n- **Pulse length:** the horizontal length of the pulse.\n- The speed of a pulse depends only on the **medium** (e.g. how tightly stretched and how thick the rope is), not on the amplitude.\n\n## Superposition and interference\n\nWhen two pulses meet, their disturbances add up. **Superposition** is the algebraic sum of the amplitudes of two pulses that occupy the same space at the same time.\n\nChoose \"up\" as positive and \"down\" as negative:\n\n- **Constructive interference:** a crest overlaps with a crest (or a trough with a trough). The resultant amplitude is **larger**: 4 cm + 3 cm = 7 cm.\n- **Destructive interference:** a crest overlaps with a trough. The resultant amplitude is **smaller**: 4 cm + (−3 cm) = 1 cm (above the equilibrium position). If the two amplitudes are equal, the result is zero: complete destructive interference.\n\nAfter meeting, each pulse continues **unchanged**, with its original shape, amplitude and direction.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Adding the sizes in destructive interference. Use the signs: a pulse below the equilibrium position is negative.\n\n## Transverse waves\n\nA **wave** is a succession of pulses. A **transverse wave** is a wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate **perpendicular** to the direction of motion of the wave.\n\n| Concept | Definition | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Crest | the highest point on the wave (maximum positive disturbance) | – |\n| Trough | the lowest point on the wave (maximum negative disturbance) | – |\n| Amplitude | the maximum disturbance of a particle from its equilibrium position | m |\n| Wavelength (λ) | the distance between two successive points in phase, e.g. from crest to crest | m |\n| Frequency (f) | the number of wave pulses per second | Hz (= s⁻¹) |\n| Period (T) | the time taken for one complete wave pulse | s |\n\n### Points in phase and out of phase\n\nPoints **in phase** are at exactly the same position in the cycle and move in the same direction, e.g. two crests or two troughs. They are a whole number of wavelengths (1λ; 2λ; 3λ …) apart. Points that are not in phase are **out of phase**. A crest and the next trough are ½λ apart and are completely out of phase.\n\n## The formulae\n\n- **T = [[1/f]]** and **f = [[1/T]]**: period and frequency are each other's reciprocals.\n- **v = fλ**: wave speed (m·s⁻¹) = frequency (Hz) × wavelength (m).\n- Distance the wave covers: distance = v × t.\n\n**Why does v = fλ work?** In one period T the wave moves forward exactly one wavelength λ, so v = [[λ/T]] = fλ.\n\n- The wave speed depends on the **medium**. In the same medium v stays constant: if f doubles, λ halves.\n- First convert to SI units: cm → m (÷ 100), kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000).\n\n> **Tip:** \"20 waves pass in 4 s\" means f = [[20/4]] = 5 Hz. \"The distance between a crest and the next trough is 0.5 m\" means λ = 2 × 0.5 = 1 m.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Using the vertical distance from crest to trough as the amplitude. The amplitude is **half** of that.\n\n## Graphs in words\n\nOn a **displacement–position graph** (y-axis: disturbance; x-axis: distance in m) you read the amplitude vertically and the wavelength horizontally, from crest to crest. On a **displacement–time graph** (x-axis: time in s) the time from crest to crest is the **period T**, not the wavelength.\n\n## Steps for calculations\n\n1. List the given values and convert to SI units.\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Substitute and calculate.\n4. Give the answer with the unit, rounded to two decimal places."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Puls","en":"Pulse"},"def":{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium.","en":"A single disturbance in a medium."}},{"term":{"af":"Transversale golf","en":"Transverse wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Amplitude","en":"Amplitude"},"def":{"af":"Die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy rus- (ewewigs)posisie.","en":"The maximum disturbance of a particle from its rest (equilibrium) position."}},{"term":{"af":"Superposisie","en":"Superposition"},"def":{"af":"Die algebraïese som van die amplitudes van twee pulse wat dieselfde ruimte op dieselfde tyd beset.","en":"The algebraic sum of the amplitudes of two pulses that occupy the same space at the same time."}},{"term":{"af":"Konstruktiewe interferensie","en":"Constructive interference"},"def":{"af":"Die verskynsel waar die kruin van een golf met die kruin van 'n ander golf oorvleuel om 'n golf met 'n groter amplitude te vorm.","en":"The phenomenon where the crest of one wave overlaps with the crest of another wave to produce a wave of increased amplitude."}},{"term":{"af":"Destruktiewe interferensie","en":"Destructive interference"},"def":{"af":"Die verskynsel waar die kruin van een golf met die trog van 'n ander golf oorvleuel, wat 'n golf met 'n kleiner amplitude tot gevolg het.","en":"The phenomenon where the crest of one wave overlaps with the trough of another wave, resulting in a wave of reduced amplitude."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (λ)","en":"Wavelength (λ)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase. Eenheid: m.","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase. Unit: m."}},{"term":{"af":"Frekwensie (f)","en":"Frequency (f)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde. Eenheid: hertz (Hz).","en":"The number of wave pulses per second. Unit: hertz (Hz)."}},{"term":{"af":"Periode (T)","en":"Period (T)"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd wat dit neem vir een volledige golfpuls. Eenheid: s. T = 1/f.","en":"The time taken for one complete wave pulse. Unit: s. T = 1/f."}},{"term":{"af":"In fase","en":"In phase"},"def":{"af":"Punte wat op dieselfde posisie in die siklus is en in dieselfde rigting beweeg; hulle is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar.","en":"Points at the same position in the cycle moving in the same direction; they are a whole number of wavelengths apart."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Superposisie van twee pulse","en":"Superposition of two pulses"},"problem":{"af":"Twee pulse beweeg op 'n tou na mekaar toe. Puls A het 'n amplitude van 4 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. (a) Puls B het 'n amplitude van 3 cm, ook bo die ewewigsposisie. Wat is die amplitude van die resulterende puls wanneer A en B presies oorvleuel? (b) Herhaal (a) as puls B 3 cm onder die ewewigsposisie is. (c) Beskryf die twee pulse nadat hulle by mekaar verby is.","en":"Two pulses move towards each other on a rope. Pulse A has an amplitude of 4 cm above the equilibrium position. (a) Pulse B has an amplitude of 3 cm, also above the equilibrium position. What is the amplitude of the resultant pulse when A and B overlap exactly? (b) Repeat (a) if pulse B is 3 cm below the equilibrium position. (c) Describe the two pulses after they have passed each other."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies op as positief: A = +4 cm.","en":"Choose up as positive: A = +4 cm."},{"af":"(a) B = +3 cm. Superposisie: (+4) + (+3) = +7 cm. Kruin op kruin: konstruktiewe interferensie.","en":"(a) B = +3 cm. Superposition: (+4) + (+3) = +7 cm. Crest on crest: constructive interference."},{"af":"(b) B = −3 cm. Superposisie: (+4) + (−3) = +1 cm, dus 1 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. Kruin op trog: destruktiewe interferensie.","en":"(b) B = −3 cm. Superposition: (+4) + (−3) = +1 cm, so 1 cm above the equilibrium position. Crest on trough: destructive interference."},{"af":"(c) Ná die ontmoeting beweeg A (4 cm) en B (3 cm) onveranderd verder in hul oorspronklike rigtings.","en":"(c) After meeting, A (4 cm) and B (3 cm) continue unchanged in their original directions."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 7 cm (konstruktief) (b) 1 cm bo die ewewigsposisie (destruktief) (c) Albei pulse beweeg onveranderd verder.","en":"(a) 7 cm (constructive) (b) 1 cm above the equilibrium position (destructive) (c) Both pulses continue unchanged."}},{"title":{"af":"Golflengte, frekwensie, periode en spoed","en":"Wavelength, frequency, period and speed"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo swaai by rugbyoefening 'n lang tou op en af. Die horisontale afstand tussen 'n kruin en die trog langsaan is 0,6 m, en 15 volledige golwe gaan in 6 s by 'n punt verby. Bereken (a) die golflengte, (b) die frekwensie, (c) die periode en (d) die golfspoed.","en":"At rugby practice Thabo swings a long rope up and down. The horizontal distance between a crest and the neighbouring trough is 0.6 m, and 15 complete waves pass a point in 6 s. Calculate (a) the wavelength, (b) the frequency, (c) the period and (d) the wave speed."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Van 'n kruin tot die volgende trog is ½λ, dus λ = 2 × 0,6 = 1,2 m.","en":"(a) From a crest to the next trough is ½λ, so λ = 2 × 0.6 = 1.2 m."},{"af":"(b) f = [[aantal golwe/tyd]] = [[15/6]] = 2,5 Hz","en":"(b) f = [[number of waves/time]] = [[15/6]] = 2.5 Hz"},{"af":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/2,5]] = 0,4 s","en":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/2.5]] = 0.4 s"},{"af":"(d) v = fλ = 2,5 × 1,2 = 3 m·s⁻¹","en":"(d) v = fλ = 2.5 × 1.2 = 3 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":{"af":"λ = 1,2 m; f = 2,5 Hz; T = 0,4 s; v = 3 m·s⁻¹","en":"λ = 1.2 m; f = 2.5 Hz; T = 0.4 s; v = 3 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Lees 'n golf af van 'n grafiek (in woorde)","en":"Read a wave from a graph (in words)"},"problem":{"af":"'n Verplasing-posisie-grafiek van 'n transversale golf op 'n tou word so beskryf: die x-as loop van 0 tot 4,5 m, en presies 3 volledige golwe pas in daardie afstand. Die kruine is 0,2 m bo die ewewigsposisie en die trôe 0,2 m onder die ewewigsposisie. Die bron vibreer teen 4 Hz. Bepaal (a) die amplitude, (b) die golflengte en (c) die golfspoed. (d) Hoe ver beweeg die golf in 3 s?","en":"A displacement–position graph of a transverse wave on a rope is described as follows: the x-axis runs from 0 to 4.5 m, and exactly 3 complete waves fit into that distance. The crests are 0.2 m above the equilibrium position and the troughs 0.2 m below the equilibrium position. The source vibrates at 4 Hz. Determine (a) the amplitude, (b) the wavelength and (c) the wave speed. (d) How far does the wave travel in 3 s?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Amplitude = maksimum versteuring vanaf die ewewigsposisie = 0,2 m (nie 0,4 m van kruin tot trog nie).","en":"(a) Amplitude = maximum disturbance from the equilibrium position = 0.2 m (not 0.4 m from crest to trough)."},{"af":"(b) 3λ = 4,5 m, dus λ = [[4,5/3]] = 1,5 m","en":"(b) 3λ = 4.5 m, so λ = [[4.5/3]] = 1.5 m"},{"af":"(c) v = fλ = 4 × 1,5 = 6 m·s⁻¹","en":"(c) v = fλ = 4 × 1.5 = 6 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(d) afstand = v × t = 6 × 3 = 18 m","en":"(d) distance = v × t = 6 × 3 = 18 m"}],"answer":{"af":"Amplitude = 0,2 m; λ = 1,5 m; v = 6 m·s⁻¹; afstand = 18 m","en":"Amplitude = 0.2 m; λ = 1.5 m; v = 6 m·s⁻¹; distance = 18 m"}},{"title":{"af":"Punte in fase en 'n verandering in frekwensie","en":"Points in phase and a change in frequency"},"problem":{"af":"Op 'n transversale golf met 'n golflengte van 2 m lê punt A op 'n kruin. Punt B is 1 m regs van A, punt C is 2 m regs van A en punt D is 4 m regs van A. (a) Watter punte is in fase met A? (b) Beskryf die posisie van B. (c) Die frekwensie is 1,5 Hz. Die bron se frekwensie word nou verdubbel terwyl die golf in dieselfde tou bly. Bereken die nuwe golflengte.","en":"On a transverse wave with a wavelength of 2 m, point A lies on a crest. Point B is 1 m to the right of A, point C is 2 m to the right of A and point D is 4 m to the right of A. (a) Which points are in phase with A? (b) Describe the position of B. (c) The frequency is 1.5 Hz. The source's frequency is now doubled while the wave stays in the same rope. Calculate the new wavelength."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Punte in fase is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar. C is 2 m = 1λ van A en D is 4 m = 2λ van A, dus is C en D in fase met A (albei op 'n kruin).","en":"(a) Points in phase are a whole number of wavelengths apart. C is 2 m = 1λ from A and D is 4 m = 2λ from A, so C and D are in phase with A (both on a crest)."},{"af":"(b) B is 1 m = ½λ van A, dus lê B op 'n trog en is heeltemal uit fase met A.","en":"(b) B is 1 m = ½λ from A, so B lies on a trough and is completely out of phase with A."},{"af":"(c) Oorspronklike spoed: v = fλ = 1,5 × 2 = 3 m·s⁻¹. Dieselfde medium, dus bly v = 3 m·s⁻¹.","en":"(c) Original speed: v = fλ = 1.5 × 2 = 3 m·s⁻¹. Same medium, so v stays 3 m·s⁻¹."},{"af":"Nuwe f = 2 × 1,5 = 3 Hz, dus λ = [[v/f]] = [[3/3]] = 1 m. Die frekwensie het verdubbel en die golflengte het gehalveer.","en":"New f = 2 × 1.5 = 3 Hz, so λ = [[v/f]] = [[3/3]] = 1 m. The frequency doubled and the wavelength halved."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) C en D (b) B lê op 'n trog en is uit fase met A (c) λ = 1 m","en":"(a) C and D (b) B lies on a trough and is out of phase with A (c) λ = 1 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n puls?","en":"What is a pulse?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Opeenvolging van pulse","en":"A succession of pulses"},{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium","en":"A single disturbance in a medium"},{"af":"Die maksimum versteuring van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie","en":"The maximum disturbance of a particle from its equilibrium position"},{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde","en":"The number of wave pulses per second"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Puls is 'n enkele versteuring in 'n medium. 'n Opeenvolging van pulse is 'n golf; die derde opsie is amplitude en die laaste frekwensie.","en":"A pulse is a single disturbance in a medium. A succession of pulses is a wave; the third option is amplitude and the last is frequency."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte definisie.","en":"Match each concept to the correct definition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kruin","en":"Crest"},"r":{"af":"Die hoogste punt op 'n golf","en":"The highest point on a wave"}},{"l":{"af":"Trog","en":"Trough"},"r":{"af":"Die laagste punt op 'n golf","en":"The lowest point on a wave"}},{"l":{"af":"Golflengte","en":"Wavelength"},"r":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase"}},{"l":{"af":"Periode","en":"Period"},"r":{"af":"Die tyd vir een volledige golfpuls","en":"The time for one complete wave pulse"}},{"l":{"af":"Frekwensie","en":"Frequency"},"r":{"af":"Die aantal golfpulse per sekonde","en":"The number of wave pulses per second"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kruin en trog is die hoogste en laagste punte. Golflengte is 'n afstand (m), periode 'n tyd (s) en frekwensie 'n aantal per sekonde (Hz).","en":"Crest and trough are the highest and lowest points. Wavelength is a distance (m), period a time (s) and frequency a number per second (Hz)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n transversale golf vibreer die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf.","en":"In a transverse wave the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In 'n transversale golf vibreer die deeltjies loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf. Parallel is 'n longitudinale golf.","en":"False. In a transverse wave the particles vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave. Parallel is a longitudinal wave."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid van frekwensie?","en":"What is the SI unit of frequency?"},"options":[{"af":"s","en":"s"},{"af":"m·s⁻¹","en":"m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"m","en":"m"},{"af":"Hz","en":"Hz"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Frekwensie word in hertz gemeet: 1 Hz = 1 s⁻¹ (een golfpuls per sekonde). s is die eenheid van periode, m van golflengte en m·s⁻¹ van golfspoed.","en":"Frequency is measured in hertz: 1 Hz = 1 s⁻¹ (one wave pulse per second). s is the unit of period, m of wavelength and m·s⁻¹ of wave speed."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Nadat twee pulse deur mekaar beweeg het, beweeg elkeen verder met sy oorspronklike vorm en amplitude.","en":"After two pulses have passed through each other, each continues with its original shape and amplitude."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Pulse beïnvloed mekaar net terwyl hulle oorvleuel (superposisie). Daarna beweeg elkeen onveranderd verder.","en":"True. Pulses affect each other only while they overlap (superposition). Afterwards each continues unchanged."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Eskom se wisselstroom het 'n frekwensie van 50 Hz. Die periode is ___ s.","en":"Eskom's alternating current has a frequency of 50 Hz. The period is ___ s."},"answers":{"af":["0,02","0.02","0,02 s","0.02 s","1/50","2 × 10⁻²"],"en":["0.02","0,02","0.02 s","0,02 s","1/50","2 × 10⁻²"]},"explain":{"af":"T = 1/f = 1/50 = 0,02 s.","en":"T = 1/f = 1/50 = 0.02 s."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["50","0,2","2"],"en":["50","0.2","2"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vertikale afstand van die bokant van 'n kruin tot die onderkant van 'n trog is 30 cm. Die amplitude is ___ cm.","en":"The vertical distance from the top of a crest to the bottom of a trough is 30 cm. The amplitude is ___ cm."},"answers":{"af":["15","15 cm","0,15 m","0.15 m"],"en":["15","15 cm","0.15 m","0,15 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Die amplitude word vanaf die ewewigsposisie gemeet, dus is dit die helfte van kruin tot trog: 30 ÷ 2 = 15 cm.","en":"The amplitude is measured from the equilibrium position, so it is half of crest to trough: 30 ÷ 2 = 15 cm."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["30","60","7,5"],"en":["30","60","7.5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Puls P (5 cm bo die ewewigsposisie) en puls Q (2 cm onder die ewewigsposisie) oorvleuel presies. Wat is die resulterende versteuring?","en":"Pulse P (5 cm above the equilibrium position) and pulse Q (2 cm below the equilibrium position) overlap exactly. What is the resultant disturbance?"},"options":[{"af":"7 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"7 cm above the equilibrium position"},{"af":"3 cm onder die ewewigsposisie","en":"3 cm below the equilibrium position"},{"af":"3 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"3 cm above the equilibrium position"},{"af":"2,5 cm bo die ewewigsposisie","en":"2.5 cm above the equilibrium position"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Op is positief: (+5) + (−2) = +3 cm, dus 3 cm bo die ewewigsposisie. Dit is destruktiewe interferensie. 7 cm kry jy as jy die tekens ignoreer.","en":"Up is positive: (+5) + (−2) = +3 cm, so 3 cm above the equilibrium position. This is destructive interference. You get 7 cm if you ignore the signs."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Golf het 'n frekwensie van 4 Hz en 'n golflengte van 0,75 m. Die golfspoed is ___ m·s⁻¹.","en":"A wave has a frequency of 4 Hz and a wavelength of 0.75 m. The wave speed is ___ m·s⁻¹."},"answers":{"af":["3","3,0","3,00","3.0","3 m·s⁻¹","3 m/s","3 m.s-1"],"en":["3","3.0","3.00","3,0","3 m·s⁻¹","3 m/s","3 m.s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"v = fλ = 4 × 0,75 = 3 m·s⁻¹.","en":"v = fλ = 4 × 0.75 = 3 m·s⁻¹."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5,33","0,19","4,75"],"en":["5.33","0.19","4.75"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"20 volledige golwe gaan in 4 s by 'n punt verby, en die golflengte is 0,5 m. Wat is die golfspoed?","en":"20 complete waves pass a point in 4 s, and the wavelength is 0.5 m. What is the wave speed?"},"options":[{"af":"2,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"2.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"10 m·s⁻¹","en":"10 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"0,1 m·s⁻¹","en":"0.1 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"40 m·s⁻¹","en":"40 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"f = 20 ÷ 4 = 5 Hz, dan v = fλ = 5 × 0,5 = 2,5 m·s⁻¹. 10 m·s⁻¹ kry jy as jy 20 as die frekwensie gebruik; 0,1 m·s⁻¹ as jy f = 4 ÷ 20 bereken.","en":"f = 20 ÷ 4 = 5 Hz, then v = fλ = 5 × 0.5 = 2.5 m·s⁻¹. You get 10 m·s⁻¹ if you use 20 as the frequency; 0.1 m·s⁻¹ if you calculate f = 4 ÷ 20."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Golf beweeg teen 6 m·s⁻¹ langs 'n tou en het 'n golflengte van 1,5 m. Die periode is ___ s.","en":"A wave travels at 6 m·s⁻¹ along a rope and has a wavelength of 1.5 m. The period is ___ s."},"answers":{"af":["0,25","0.25","0,25 s","0.25 s","1/4"],"en":["0.25","0,25","0.25 s","0,25 s","1/4"]},"explain":{"af":"f = v/λ = 6 ÷ 1,5 = 4 Hz, dan T = 1/f = 1/4 = 0,25 s.","en":"f = v/λ = 6 ÷ 1.5 = 4 Hz, then T = 1/f = 1/4 = 0.25 s."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","9","0,11"],"en":["4","9","0.11"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Transversale golf het 'n golflengte van 0,8 m. Punt A lê op 'n kruin. Watter punt is in fase met A?","en":"A transverse wave has a wavelength of 0.8 m. Point A lies on a crest. Which point is in phase with A?"},"options":[{"af":"Die punt 0,4 m regs van A","en":"The point 0.4 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 0,2 m regs van A","en":"The point 0.2 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 1,0 m regs van A","en":"The point 1.0 m to the right of A"},{"af":"Die punt 1,6 m regs van A","en":"The point 1.6 m to the right of A"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Punte in fase is 'n heelgetal golflengtes uitmekaar: 1,6 m = 2 × 0,8 m = 2λ, dus is daardie punt ook op 'n kruin. 0,4 m = ½λ is 'n trog (heeltemal uit fase); 0,2 m = ¼λ en 1,0 m = 1¼λ is by die ewewigsposisie.","en":"Points in phase are a whole number of wavelengths apart: 1.6 m = 2 × 0.8 m = 2λ, so that point is also on a crest. 0.4 m = ½λ is a trough (completely out of phase); 0.2 m = ¼λ and 1.0 m = 1¼λ are at the equilibrium position."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Golf beweeg in dieselfde tou, maar die frekwensie van die bron word verdubbel. Wat gebeur met die golfspoed en die golflengte?","en":"A wave travels in the same rope, but the frequency of the source is doubled. What happens to the wave speed and the wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"Die spoed verdubbel; die golflengte bly dieselfde","en":"The speed doubles; the wavelength stays the same"},{"af":"Die spoed bly dieselfde; die golflengte halveer","en":"The speed stays the same; the wavelength halves"},{"af":"Die spoed bly dieselfde; die golflengte verdubbel","en":"The speed stays the same; the wavelength doubles"},{"af":"Die spoed halveer; die golflengte verdubbel","en":"The speed halves; the wavelength doubles"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die golfspoed hang net van die medium af, en die tou bly dieselfde, dus bly v konstant. Uit v = fλ: as f verdubbel, moet λ halveer.","en":"The wave speed depends only on the medium, and the rope stays the same, so v stays constant. From v = fλ: if f doubles, λ must halve."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho sê: \"As ek die tou harder swaai sodat die amplitude groter is, beweeg die golf vinniger.\" Watter evaluering is korrek?","en":"Sipho says: \"If I swing the rope harder so that the amplitude is bigger, the wave travels faster.\" Which evaluation is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: meer energie beteken altyd 'n hoër spoed","en":"He is right: more energy always means a higher speed"},{"af":"Hy is reg: v = fλ, en die amplitude is deel van die golflengte","en":"He is right: v = fλ, and the amplitude is part of the wavelength"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: die spoed hang net van die medium af; 'n groter amplitude dra meer energie oor, maar teen dieselfde spoed","en":"He is wrong: the speed depends only on the medium; a bigger amplitude transfers more energy, but at the same speed"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: 'n groter amplitude maak die golf altyd stadiger","en":"He is wrong: a bigger amplitude always makes the wave slower"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die golfspoed word deur die medium bepaal (hoe styf gespan en hoe dik die tou is). Die amplitude is 'n vertikale versteuring en kom nie in v = fλ voor nie. 'n Groter amplitude beteken net dat meer energie oorgedra word.","en":"The wave speed is determined by the medium (how tightly stretched and how thick the rope is). The amplitude is a vertical disturbance and does not appear in v = fλ. A bigger amplitude only means that more energy is transferred."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-longitudinale-golwe-klank","title":{"af":"Longitudinale golwe en klank","en":"Longitudinal waves and sound"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal longitudinale golwe en klank kan beskryf, toonhoogte en luidheid aan frekwensie en amplitude kan koppel, en berekeninge met v = fλ en eggo's kan doen.","en":"You will be able to describe longitudinal waves and sound, link pitch and loudness to frequency and amplitude, and do calculations with v = fλ and echoes."},"summary":{"af":"## Longitudinale golwe\n\nDruk en trek die punt van 'n slinky-veer heen en weer in die lengte van die veer, en jy sien digte en oop gebiede wat langs die veer beweeg.\n\n'n **Longitudinale golf** is 'n golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium **parallel** aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.\n\n- **Kompressie:** 'n gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is (hoë druk).\n- **Verdunning:** 'n gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is (lae druk).\n- **Golflengte (λ):** die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kompressies (of twee opeenvolgende verdunnings). Van 'n kompressie tot die volgende verdunning is ½λ.\n- **Amplitude:** die maksimum verplasing van 'n deeltjie vanaf sy ewewigsposisie.\n- Frekwensie, periode en golfspoed werk presies soos by transversale golwe: **v = fλ** en **T = [[1/f]]**.\n\n| | Transversale golf | Longitudinale golf |\n|---|---|---|\n| Deeltjies vibreer | loodreg op die golfrigting | parallel aan die golfrigting |\n| \"Hoë\" deel | kruin | kompressie |\n| \"Lae\" deel | trog | verdunning |\n| Voorbeeld | golf op 'n tou | klank; 'n slinky wat gedruk en getrek word |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is 1,2 m, dus λ = [[1,2/5]].\" Verkeerd! Tel die **gapings**: van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is 4λ, dus λ = [[1,2/4]] = 0,3 m.\n\n## Klank\n\nKlank word deur **vibrasies** gemaak: jou stembande, die membraan van 'n luidspreker of 'n kitaarsnaar. Die vibrerende voorwerp druk en trek die lugdeeltjies, sodat kompressies en verdunnings deur die lug beweeg. **Klank is 'n longitudinale, meganiese golf**: dit het 'n **medium** nodig en kan **nie deur 'n vakuum** beweeg nie. Daarom is dit doodstil in die ruimte.\n\n### Die spoed van klank\n\n| Medium | Spoed van klank (ongeveer) |\n|---|---|\n| lug | 340 m·s⁻¹ |\n| water | 1 500 m·s⁻¹ |\n| staal | 5 000 m·s⁻¹ |\n\nKlank beweeg die **vinnigste in vastestowwe** en die stadigste in gasse. In 'n vastestof is die deeltjies naby aan mekaar en sterk aan mekaar gebind, dus word die vibrasie vinnig van deeltjie na deeltjie oorgedra. As daar by 'n myn naby Brits geskiet word, voel jy die skok deur die grond voordat jy die knal deur die lug hoor. In lug beweeg klank ook vinniger as die temperatuur hoër is.\n\n### Toonhoogte, luidheid en kwaliteit\n\n| Eienskap | Hang af van | Betekenis |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Toonhoogte** | frekwensie | hoë frekwensie = hoë (skril) toon; lae frekwensie = lae (diep) toon |\n| **Luidheid** | amplitude | groter amplitude = harder klank (meer energie word oorgedra) |\n| **Kwaliteit (toonkleur)** | die vorm van die golf | dieselfde noot op 'n kitaar en 'n klavier klink verskillend |\n\n'n Taxi se skril toeter het 'n hoër frekwensie as 'n vragmotor se diep toeter. Die gejuig van die skare by 'n rugbywedstryd het 'n groter amplitude as 'n fluistering.\n\n## Menslike gehoor, infraklank en ultraklank\n\n- Mense hoor frekwensies van ongeveer **20 Hz tot 20 000 Hz** (20 kHz). Met ouderdom verloor mense eerste die vermoë om hoë frekwensies te hoor.\n- **Infraklank:** frekwensies laer as 20 Hz (olifante kommunikeer daarmee).\n- **Ultraklank:** klank met frekwensies **hoër as 20 kHz**, te hoog vir mense om te hoor. Vlermuise en dolfyne stuur ultraklank uit en gebruik die eggo's om prooi en hindernisse op te spoor (eggolokasie).\n\n### Gebruike van ultraklank\n\n- **Mediese beelde**, bv. 'n skandering van 'n ongebore baba of van organe. Ultraklankpulse word die liggaam ingestuur; by elke grens tussen verskillende weefsels word 'n deel van die klank teruggekaats. 'n Rekenaar gebruik die tyd en die sterkte van die eggo's om 'n beeld te bou.\n- Ultraklank is 'n meganiese golf en **nie ioniserend nie** (anders as X-strale), daarom is dit veilig vir ongebore babas.\n- Die hoë frekwensie gee 'n **kort golflengte**, sodat klein besonderhede gesien kan word.\n- **Sonar** meet die diepte van die see of vind visskole. Ultraklank word ook gebruik om juwele en instrumente skoon te maak en in fisioterapie.\n\n## Eggo's\n\n'n **Eggo** is 'n weerkaatste klank. Die klank beweeg **na** die voorwerp **en terug**, dus is die afstand na die voorwerp die helfte van die totale afstand wat die klank aflê:\n\n**afstand = [[v × t/2]]**, waar t die tyd is vandat die klank gemaak word totdat die eggo gehoor word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om te vergeet om deur 2 te deel. Die gemete tyd is vir die heen-en-terug-reis.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skakel altyd eers om na SI-eenhede: kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000), cm → m (÷ 100). Die spoed van klank word in die vraag gegee; dit is nie op die gegewensblad nie.","en":"## Longitudinal waves\n\nPush and pull the end of a slinky spring back and forth along the length of the spring, and you see dense and open regions moving along the spring.\n\nA **longitudinal wave** is a wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate **parallel** to the direction of motion of the wave.\n\n- **Compression:** a region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are closest together (high pressure).\n- **Rarefaction:** a region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are furthest apart (low pressure).\n- **Wavelength (λ):** the distance between two successive compressions (or two successive rarefactions). From a compression to the next rarefaction is ½λ.\n- **Amplitude:** the maximum displacement of a particle from its equilibrium position.\n- Frequency, period and wave speed work exactly as for transverse waves: **v = fλ** and **T = [[1/f]]**.\n\n| | Transverse wave | Longitudinal wave |\n|---|---|---|\n| Particles vibrate | perpendicular to the wave direction | parallel to the wave direction |\n| \"High\" part | crest | compression |\n| \"Low\" part | trough | rarefaction |\n| Example | wave on a rope | sound; a slinky pushed and pulled |\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"The distance from the 1st to the 5th compression is 1.2 m, so λ = [[1.2/5]].\" Wrong! Count the **gaps**: from the 1st to the 5th compression is 4λ, so λ = [[1.2/4]] = 0.3 m.\n\n## Sound\n\nSound is made by **vibrations**: your vocal cords, the membrane of a loudspeaker or a guitar string. The vibrating object pushes and pulls the air particles, so that compressions and rarefactions travel through the air. **Sound is a longitudinal, mechanical wave**: it needs a **medium** and **cannot travel through a vacuum**. That is why space is completely silent.\n\n### The speed of sound\n\n| Medium | Speed of sound (approximately) |\n|---|---|\n| air | 340 m·s⁻¹ |\n| water | 1 500 m·s⁻¹ |\n| steel | 5 000 m·s⁻¹ |\n\nSound travels **fastest in solids** and slowest in gases. In a solid the particles are close together and strongly bonded, so the vibration is passed on quickly from particle to particle. When there is blasting at a mine near Brits, you feel the shock through the ground before you hear the bang through the air. In air, sound also travels faster when the temperature is higher.\n\n### Pitch, loudness and quality\n\n| Property | Depends on | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Pitch** | frequency | high frequency = high (shrill) note; low frequency = low (deep) note |\n| **Loudness** | amplitude | bigger amplitude = louder sound (more energy is transferred) |\n| **Quality (timbre)** | the shape of the wave | the same note on a guitar and a piano sounds different |\n\nA taxi's shrill hooter has a higher frequency than a truck's deep hooter. The cheering of the crowd at a rugby match has a bigger amplitude than a whisper.\n\n## Human hearing, infrasound and ultrasound\n\n- Humans hear frequencies from about **20 Hz to 20 000 Hz** (20 kHz). With age, people first lose the ability to hear high frequencies.\n- **Infrasound:** frequencies lower than 20 Hz (elephants communicate with it).\n- **Ultrasound:** sound with frequencies **higher than 20 kHz**, too high for humans to hear. Bats and dolphins send out ultrasound and use the echoes to find prey and obstacles (echolocation).\n\n### Uses of ultrasound\n\n- **Medical imaging**, e.g. a scan of an unborn baby or of organs. Ultrasound pulses are sent into the body; at every boundary between different tissues part of the sound is reflected. A computer uses the time and the strength of the echoes to build an image.\n- Ultrasound is a mechanical wave and **not ionising** (unlike X-rays), which is why it is safe for unborn babies.\n- The high frequency gives a **short wavelength**, so small details can be seen.\n- **Sonar** measures the depth of the sea or finds shoals of fish. Ultrasound is also used to clean jewellery and instruments, and in physiotherapy.\n\n## Echoes\n\nAn **echo** is a reflected sound. The sound travels **to** the object **and back**, so the distance to the object is half of the total distance the sound covers:\n\n**distance = [[v × t/2]]**, where t is the time from when the sound is made until the echo is heard.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Forgetting to divide by 2. The measured time is for the round trip.\n\n> **Tip:** Always convert to SI units first: kHz → Hz (× 1 000), ms → s (÷ 1 000), cm → m (÷ 100). The speed of sound is given in the question; it is not on the data sheet."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Longitudinale golf","en":"Longitudinal wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer.","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Kompressie","en":"Compression"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is (hoë druk).","en":"A region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are closest together (high pressure)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verdunning","en":"Rarefaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in 'n longitudinale golf waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is (lae druk).","en":"A region in a longitudinal wave where the particles are furthest apart (low pressure)."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (longitudinaal)","en":"Wavelength (longitudinal)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kompressies of twee opeenvolgende verdunnings.","en":"The distance between two successive compressions or two successive rarefactions."}},{"term":{"af":"Meganiese golf","en":"Mechanical wave"},"def":{"af":"'n Golf wat 'n medium nodig het om deur te beweeg, bv. klank. Dit kan nie deur 'n vakuum beweeg nie.","en":"A wave that needs a medium to travel through, e.g. sound. It cannot travel through a vacuum."}},{"term":{"af":"Toonhoogte","en":"Pitch"},"def":{"af":"Hoe hoog of laag 'n klank klink. Dit word deur die frekwensie bepaal: hoe hoër die frekwensie, hoe hoër die toonhoogte.","en":"How high or low a sound is. It is determined by the frequency: the higher the frequency, the higher the pitch."}},{"term":{"af":"Luidheid","en":"Loudness"},"def":{"af":"Hoe hard of sag 'n klank is. Dit word deur die amplitude bepaal: hoe groter die amplitude, hoe harder die klank.","en":"How loud or soft a sound is. It is determined by the amplitude: the bigger the amplitude, the louder the sound."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwaliteit (toonkleur)","en":"Quality (timbre)"},"def":{"af":"Die eienskap wat dieselfde noot van verskillende instrumente anders laat klink; dit hang af van die vorm van die golf.","en":"The property that makes the same note from different instruments sound different; it depends on the shape of the wave."}},{"term":{"af":"Ultraklank","en":"Ultrasound"},"def":{"af":"Klank met frekwensies hoër as 20 kHz, bo die menslike gehoorgebied.","en":"Sound with frequencies higher than 20 kHz, above the human hearing range."}},{"term":{"af":"Eggo","en":"Echo"},"def":{"af":"'n Weerkaatste klank. Afstand na die weerkaatsende voorwerp = v × t ÷ 2.","en":"A reflected sound. Distance to the reflecting object = v × t ÷ 2."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Golflengte en spoed op 'n slinky","en":"Wavelength and speed on a slinky"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato druk en trek die punt van 'n slinky-veer heen en weer met 'n frekwensie van 5 Hz. Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 4de kompressie is 90 cm. Bereken (a) die golflengte, (b) die golfspoed en (c) die periode.","en":"Lerato pushes and pulls the end of a slinky spring back and forth with a frequency of 5 Hz. The distance from the 1st to the 4th compression is 90 cm. Calculate (a) the wavelength, (b) the wave speed and (c) the period."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Tel die gapings: van die 1ste tot die 4de kompressie is 3 golflengtes. 3λ = 90 cm = 0,9 m.","en":"(a) Count the gaps: from the 1st to the 4th compression is 3 wavelengths. 3λ = 90 cm = 0.9 m."},{"af":"λ = [[0,9/3]] = 0,3 m","en":"λ = [[0.9/3]] = 0.3 m"},{"af":"(b) v = fλ = 5 × 0,3 = 1,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"(b) v = fλ = 5 × 0.3 = 1.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/5]] = 0,2 s","en":"(c) T = [[1/f]] = [[1/5]] = 0.2 s"}],"answer":{"af":"λ = 0,3 m; v = 1,5 m·s⁻¹; T = 0,2 s","en":"λ = 0.3 m; v = 1.5 m·s⁻¹; T = 0.2 s"}},{"title":{"af":"'n Eggo in die Magaliesberg","en":"An echo in the Magaliesberg"},"problem":{"af":"Jan staan voor 'n krans in die Magaliesberg en klap sy hande. Hy hoor die eggo 1,5 s later. Die spoed van klank in lug is 340 m·s⁻¹. (a) Hoe ver is die krans van Jan af? (b) Jan stap nader totdat die krans 170 m weg is. Hoe lank ná die klap hoor hy nou die eggo?","en":"Jan stands in front of a cliff in the Magaliesberg and claps his hands. He hears the echo 1.5 s later. The speed of sound in air is 340 m·s⁻¹. (a) How far is the cliff from Jan? (b) Jan walks closer until the cliff is 170 m away. How long after the clap does he now hear the echo?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die klank beweeg na die krans en terug, dus afstand = [[v × t/2]].","en":"(a) The sound travels to the cliff and back, so distance = [[v × t/2]]."},{"af":"afstand = [[340 × 1,5/2]] = [[510/2]] = 255 m","en":"distance = [[340 × 1.5/2]] = [[510/2]] = 255 m"},{"af":"(b) Die klank moet heen en terug beweeg: totale afstand = 2 × 170 = 340 m.","en":"(b) The sound must travel there and back: total distance = 2 × 170 = 340 m."},{"af":"t = [[totale afstand/v]] = [[340/340]] = 1 s","en":"t = [[total distance/v]] = [[340/340]] = 1 s"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 255 m (b) 1 s","en":"(a) 255 m (b) 1 s"}},{"title":{"af":"Sonar en die golflengte van ultraklank","en":"Sonar and the wavelength of ultrasound"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vissersboot stuur 'n ultraklankpuls met 'n frekwensie van 50 kHz na die seebodem. Die eggo word 0,8 s later ontvang. Die spoed van klank in seewater is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Bereken (a) die diepte van die see en (b) die golflengte van die ultraklank in die water. (c) Kan die bemanning die puls hoor? Verduidelik.","en":"A fishing boat sends an ultrasound pulse with a frequency of 50 kHz to the sea floor. The echo is received 0.8 s later. The speed of sound in sea water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Calculate (a) the depth of the sea and (b) the wavelength of the ultrasound in the water. (c) Can the crew hear the pulse? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) diepte = [[v × t/2]] = [[1 500 × 0,8/2]] = [[1 200/2]] = 600 m","en":"(a) depth = [[v × t/2]] = [[1 500 × 0.8/2]] = [[1 200/2]] = 600 m"},{"af":"(b) Skakel eers om: f = 50 kHz = 50 × 1 000 = 50 000 Hz.","en":"(b) First convert: f = 50 kHz = 50 × 1 000 = 50 000 Hz."},{"af":"λ = [[v/f]] = [[1 500/50 000]] = 0,03 m (3 cm)","en":"λ = [[v/f]] = [[1 500/50 000]] = 0.03 m (3 cm)"},{"af":"(c) Nee. 50 kHz is hoër as 20 kHz, die boonste grens van menslike gehoor. Dit is ultraklank.","en":"(c) No. 50 kHz is higher than 20 kHz, the upper limit of human hearing. It is ultrasound."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 600 m (b) 0,03 m (c) Nee, 50 kHz is ultraklank (bo 20 kHz).","en":"(a) 600 m (b) 0.03 m (c) No, 50 kHz is ultrasound (above 20 kHz)."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk twee klankgolwe","en":"Compare two sound waves"},"problem":{"af":"Twee klankgolwe word as verplasing-tyd-grafieke op 'n ossilloskoop vertoon. Golf A: amplitude 2 blokkies, 5 volledige golwe in 0,01 s. Golf B: amplitude 1 blokkie, 10 volledige golwe in 0,01 s. (a) Bereken die frekwensie van elke golf. (b) Watter klank is die hardste? (c) Watter klank het die hoogste toonhoogte? (d) Bereken die golflengte van B in lug (spoed van klank = 340 m·s⁻¹).","en":"Two sound waves are shown as displacement–time graphs on an oscilloscope. Wave A: amplitude 2 blocks, 5 complete waves in 0.01 s. Wave B: amplitude 1 block, 10 complete waves in 0.01 s. (a) Calculate the frequency of each wave. (b) Which sound is the loudest? (c) Which sound has the highest pitch? (d) Calculate the wavelength of B in air (speed of sound = 340 m·s⁻¹)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) f_{A} = [[5/0,01]] = 500 Hz en f_{B} = [[10/0,01]] = 1 000 Hz","en":"(a) f_{A} = [[5/0.01]] = 500 Hz and f_{B} = [[10/0.01]] = 1 000 Hz"},{"af":"(b) Luidheid hang van die amplitude af. A het die groter amplitude (2 blokkies teenoor 1), dus is A die hardste.","en":"(b) Loudness depends on the amplitude. A has the bigger amplitude (2 blocks versus 1), so A is the loudest."},{"af":"(c) Toonhoogte hang van die frekwensie af. B het die hoër frekwensie (1 000 Hz), dus het B die hoogste toonhoogte.","en":"(c) Pitch depends on the frequency. B has the higher frequency (1 000 Hz), so B has the highest pitch."},{"af":"(d) λ_{B} = [[v/f]] = [[340/1 000]] = 0,34 m","en":"(d) λ_{B} = [[v/f]] = [[340/1 000]] = 0.34 m"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 500 Hz en 1 000 Hz (b) A (c) B (d) 0,34 m","en":"(a) 500 Hz and 1 000 Hz (b) A (c) B (d) 0.34 m"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n longitudinale golf?","en":"What is a longitudinal wave?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium loodreg op die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate perpendicular to the direction of motion of the wave"},{"af":"'n Enkele versteuring in 'n medium","en":"A single disturbance in a medium"},{"af":"'n Golf waarin die deeltjies van die medium parallel aan die bewegingsrigting van die golf vibreer","en":"A wave in which the particles of the medium vibrate parallel to the direction of motion of the wave"},{"af":"'n Golf wat sonder 'n medium deur 'n vakuum kan beweeg","en":"A wave that can travel through a vacuum without a medium"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In 'n longitudinale golf vibreer die deeltjies parallel aan die golfrigting. Loodreg is 'n transversale golf, en 'n enkele versteuring is 'n puls.","en":"In a longitudinal wave the particles vibrate parallel to the wave direction. Perpendicular is a transverse wave, and a single disturbance is a pulse."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kompressie","en":"Compression"},"r":{"af":"Gebied waar die deeltjies die naaste aan mekaar is","en":"Region where the particles are closest together"}},{"l":{"af":"Verdunning","en":"Rarefaction"},"r":{"af":"Gebied waar die deeltjies die verste van mekaar is","en":"Region where the particles are furthest apart"}},{"l":{"af":"Toonhoogte","en":"Pitch"},"r":{"af":"Word deur die frekwensie bepaal","en":"Determined by the frequency"}},{"l":{"af":"Luidheid","en":"Loudness"},"r":{"af":"Word deur die amplitude bepaal","en":"Determined by the amplitude"}},{"l":{"af":"Ultraklank","en":"Ultrasound"},"r":{"af":"Klank met 'n frekwensie hoër as 20 kHz","en":"Sound with a frequency higher than 20 kHz"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kompressie = deeltjies dig op mekaar (hoë druk); verdunning = deeltjies ver uitmekaar (lae druk). Toonhoogte hang van frekwensie af, luidheid van amplitude, en ultraklank is bo 20 kHz.","en":"Compression = particles packed closely (high pressure); rarefaction = particles far apart (low pressure). Pitch depends on frequency, loudness on amplitude, and ultrasound is above 20 kHz."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Klank kan deur 'n vakuum beweeg.","en":"Sound can travel through a vacuum."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Klank is 'n meganiese golf: dit het deeltjies ('n medium) nodig om die vibrasie oor te dra. In 'n vakuum is daar geen deeltjies nie.","en":"False. Sound is a mechanical wave: it needs particles (a medium) to pass on the vibration. In a vacuum there are no particles."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter medium beweeg klank die vinnigste?","en":"In which medium does sound travel fastest?"},"options":[{"af":"Vakuum","en":"Vacuum"},{"af":"Lug","en":"Air"},{"af":"Water","en":"Water"},{"af":"Staal","en":"Steel"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Klank beweeg die vinnigste in vastestowwe (staal ± 5 000 m·s⁻¹), stadiger in vloeistowwe (water ± 1 500 m·s⁻¹) en die stadigste in gasse (lug ± 340 m·s⁻¹). In 'n vakuum beweeg klank glad nie.","en":"Sound travels fastest in solids (steel ± 5 000 m·s⁻¹), slower in liquids (water ± 1 500 m·s⁻¹) and slowest in gases (air ± 340 m·s⁻¹). In a vacuum sound does not travel at all."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die boonste grens van die menslike gehoorgebied is ongeveer ___ Hz.","en":"The upper limit of the human hearing range is about ___ Hz."},"answers":{"af":["20 000","20000","20 000 Hz","20000 Hz","20 kHz"],"en":["20 000","20000","20 000 Hz","20000 Hz","20 kHz"]},"explain":{"af":"Mense hoor van ongeveer 20 Hz tot 20 000 Hz (20 kHz). Klank bo 20 kHz is ultraklank.","en":"Humans hear from about 20 Hz to 20 000 Hz (20 kHz). Sound above 20 kHz is ultrasound."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2 000","200 000","340"],"en":["2 000","200 000","340"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hoe hoër die frekwensie van 'n klank, hoe hoër is die toonhoogte.","en":"The higher the frequency of a sound, the higher the pitch."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Toonhoogte word deur frekwensie bepaal: 'n taxi se skril toeter het 'n hoër frekwensie as 'n vragmotor se diep toeter.","en":"True. Pitch is determined by frequency: a taxi's shrill hooter has a higher frequency than a truck's deep hooter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder speel dieselfde noot harder op 'n kitaar. Wat verander aan die klankgolf?","en":"A learner plays the same note louder on a guitar. What changes in the sound wave?"},"options":[{"af":"Die frekwensie neem toe","en":"The frequency increases"},{"af":"Die amplitude neem toe, en die frekwensie bly dieselfde","en":"The amplitude increases, and the frequency stays the same"},{"af":"Die golflengte neem af","en":"The wavelength decreases"},{"af":"Die spoed van die klank in die lug neem toe","en":"The speed of the sound in the air increases"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Harder beteken 'n groter amplitude. Dit is dieselfde noot, dus bly die frekwensie (toonhoogte) dieselfde. Die spoed hang van die medium af, en met dieselfde v en f bly λ ook dieselfde.","en":"Louder means a bigger amplitude. It is the same note, so the frequency (pitch) stays the same. The speed depends on the medium, and with the same v and f, λ also stays the same."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Klank met 'n frekwensie van 680 Hz beweeg teen 340 m·s⁻¹ deur lug. Die golflengte is ___ m.","en":"A sound with a frequency of 680 Hz travels through air at 340 m·s⁻¹. The wavelength is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,5","0.5","0,50","0.50","0,5 m","0.5 m","50 cm"],"en":["0.5","0,5","0.50","0,50","0.5 m","0,5 m","50 cm"]},"explain":{"af":"λ = v/f = 340 ÷ 680 = 0,5 m.","en":"λ = v/f = 340 ÷ 680 = 0.5 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","231200","5"],"en":["2","231200","5"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy skree voor 'n krans en hoor die eggo 2 s later. Die spoed van klank is 340 m·s⁻¹. Die krans is ___ m van jou af.","en":"You shout in front of a cliff and hear the echo 2 s later. The speed of sound is 340 m·s⁻¹. The cliff is ___ m away from you."},"answers":{"af":["340","340 m"],"en":["340","340 m"]},"explain":{"af":"afstand = v × t ÷ 2 = 340 × 2 ÷ 2 = 340 m. As jy vergeet om deur 2 te deel, kry jy 680 m: dit is die heen-en-terug-afstand.","en":"distance = v × t ÷ 2 = 340 × 2 ÷ 2 = 340 m. If you forget to divide by 2, you get 680 m: that is the round-trip distance."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["680","170","1360"],"en":["680","170","1360"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die afstand van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie op 'n slinky is 1,2 m. Wat is die golflengte?","en":"The distance from the 1st to the 5th compression on a slinky is 1.2 m. What is the wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"1,20 m","en":"1.20 m"},{"af":"0,60 m","en":"0.60 m"},{"af":"0,30 m","en":"0.30 m"},{"af":"0,24 m","en":"0.24 m"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van die 1ste tot die 5de kompressie is daar 4 gapings, dus 4λ = 1,2 m en λ = 1,2 ÷ 4 = 0,30 m. 0,24 m kry jy as jy deur 5 deel (die kompressies tel in plaas van die gapings).","en":"From the 1st to the 5th compression there are 4 gaps, so 4λ = 1.2 m and λ = 1.2 ÷ 4 = 0.30 m. You get 0.24 m if you divide by 5 (counting the compressions instead of the gaps)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Dolfyn stuur ultraklank met 'n frekwensie van 150 kHz uit. Die spoed van klank in water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Die golflengte is ___ m.","en":"A dolphin sends out ultrasound with a frequency of 150 kHz. The speed of sound in water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. The wavelength is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,01","0.01","0,01 m","0.01 m","1 cm","1 × 10⁻²"],"en":["0.01","0,01","0.01 m","0,01 m","1 cm","1 × 10⁻²"]},"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: 150 kHz = 150 000 Hz. λ = v/f = 1 500 ÷ 150 000 = 0,01 m (1 cm). As jy vergeet om om te skakel, kry jy 10 m.","en":"First convert: 150 kHz = 150 000 Hz. λ = v/f = 1 500 ÷ 150 000 = 0.01 m (1 cm). If you forget to convert, you get 10 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","100","0,1"],"en":["10","100","0.1"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Skip stuur 'n sonarpuls na die seebodem en ontvang die eggo 1,2 s later. Die spoed van klank in seewater is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. Hoe diep is die see?","en":"A ship sends a sonar pulse to the sea floor and receives the echo 1.2 s later. The speed of sound in sea water is 1 500 m·s⁻¹. How deep is the sea?"},"options":[{"af":"1 800 m","en":"1 800 m"},{"af":"900 m","en":"900 m"},{"af":"1 250 m","en":"1 250 m"},{"af":"450 m","en":"450 m"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"diepte = v × t ÷ 2 = 1 500 × 1,2 ÷ 2 = 900 m. 1 800 m is die heen-en-terug-afstand (vergeet om deur 2 te deel), en 1 250 m kom van v ÷ t.","en":"depth = v × t ÷ 2 = 1 500 × 1.2 ÷ 2 = 900 m. 1 800 m is the round-trip distance (forgetting to divide by 2), and 1 250 m comes from v ÷ t."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom beweeg klank vinniger deur staal as deur lug?","en":"Why does sound travel faster through steel than through air?"},"options":[{"af":"Die deeltjies in staal is nader aan mekaar en sterker aan mekaar gebind, dus word die vibrasie vinniger oorgedra","en":"The particles in steel are closer together and more strongly bonded, so the vibration is passed on faster"},{"af":"Klank is 'n transversale golf in staal, en transversale golwe is altyd vinniger","en":"Sound is a transverse wave in steel, and transverse waves are always faster"},{"af":"Klank kry 'n hoër frekwensie in staal, en 'n hoër frekwensie beteken 'n hoër spoed","en":"Sound gets a higher frequency in steel, and a higher frequency means a higher speed"},{"af":"Staal het minder deeltjies wat die klank in die pad staan","en":"Steel has fewer particles that get in the way of the sound"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Klank word van deeltjie na deeltjie oorgedra. In 'n vastestof is die deeltjies dig op mekaar en sterk gebind, dus beweeg die vibrasie vinnig. Klank bly longitudinaal, die frekwensie word deur die bron bepaal, en staal het juis méér deeltjies per volume as lug.","en":"Sound is passed on from particle to particle. In a solid the particles are packed closely and strongly bonded, so the vibration travels quickly. Sound stays longitudinal, the frequency is set by the source, and steel actually has more particles per volume than air."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder sê: \"Ultraklank is veiliger as X-strale vir 'n skandering van 'n ongebore baba, want ultraklank het 'n baie hoër frekwensie as X-strale.\" Watter evaluering is korrek?","en":"A learner says: \"Ultrasound is safer than X-rays for a scan of an unborn baby, because ultrasound has a much higher frequency than X-rays.\" Which evaluation is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Heeltemal korrek: die gevolgtrekking en die rede is albei reg","en":"Completely correct: the conclusion and the reason are both right"},{"af":"Heeltemal verkeerd: ultraklank is ook ioniserende straling en net so gevaarlik soos X-strale","en":"Completely wrong: ultrasound is also ionising radiation and just as dangerous as X-rays"},{"af":"Verkeerd: ultraklank kan nie deur die liggaam beweeg nie, so dit word nie vir skanderings gebruik nie","en":"Wrong: ultrasound cannot travel through the body, so it is not used for scans"},{"af":"Die gevolgtrekking is reg, maar die rede is verkeerd: ultraklank is 'n meganiese golf wat nie ioniserend is nie, terwyl X-strale ioniserende elektromagnetiese straling met 'n baie hoër frekwensie is","en":"The conclusion is right, but the reason is wrong: ultrasound is a mechanical wave that is not ionising, whereas X-rays are ionising electromagnetic radiation with a much higher frequency"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ultraklank word wel vir babaskanderings gebruik omdat dit veilig is, maar nie oor sy frekwensie nie. Dit is klank ('n meganiese golf, frekwensie net bo 20 kHz) en ioniseer nie. X-strale is elektromagnetiese straling met 'n veel hoër frekwensie wat selle kan beskadig.","en":"Ultrasound is indeed used for baby scans because it is safe, but not because of its frequency. It is sound (a mechanical wave, frequency just above 20 kHz) and does not ionise. X-rays are electromagnetic radiation with a much higher frequency that can damage cells."}}]},{"id":"f10-t1-em-straling","title":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese straling","en":"Electromagnetic radiation"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die EM-spektrum in volgorde kan rangskik, gebruike en gevare kan noem, en met c = fλ en E = hf kan reken.","en":"You will be able to arrange the EM spectrum in order, name uses and dangers, and calculate with c = fλ and E = hf."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is elektromagnetiese straling?\n\n**Elektromagnetiese (EM) straling** is energie wat as golwe deur die ruimte beweeg. 'n EM-golf ontstaan wanneer 'n **gelaaide deeltjie versnel**. Die versnellende lading skep 'n ossillerende **elektriese veld**, wat 'n ossillerende **magneetveld** loodreg daarop opwek, wat weer 'n elektriese veld opwek, ensovoorts. Hierdie **wedersyds regenererende velde** is loodreg op mekaar én loodreg op die bewegingsrigting, daarom is EM-golwe **transversale golwe**.\n\n- EM-golwe het **geen medium** nodig nie: sonlig bereik ons deur die vakuum van die ruimte. (Klank kan nie deur 'n vakuum beweeg nie.)\n- Alle EM-golwe beweeg in 'n vakuum teen dieselfde spoed, die **spoed van lig**: c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. In lug is die spoed feitlik dieselfde.\n\n## Golf-deeltjie-dualiteit\n\nEM-straling het 'n **dubbele aard**. Sommige eienskappe word die beste met 'n **golfmodel** verklaar (bv. interferensie en diffraksie), ander die beste met 'n **deeltjiemodel** (bv. die foto-elektriese effek, waar lig elektrone uit 'n metaaloppervlak slaan). Die \"deeltjies\" van EM-straling heet **fotone**.\n\n> **Definisie:** 'n **Foton** is 'n kwantum (pakkie) energie.\n\n## Die EM-spektrum\n\nDie tipes is hier gerangskik van **lae frekwensie, lang golflengte en lae energie** (bo) na **hoë frekwensie, kort golflengte en hoë energie** (onder):\n\n| Tipe | Gebruike | Gevare |\n|---|---|---|\n| Radiogolwe | radio- en TV-uitsendings, tweerigtingradio's | geen bekende gevaar by normale vlakke |\n| Mikrogolwe | mikrogolfoonde, selfone, wi-fi, radar (spoedlokvalle), satelliet-TV | sterk bundels verhit liggaamsweefsel |\n| Infrarooi (IR) | TV-afstandbeheerders, nagsig- en hittekameras, hittelampe | brandwonde by hoë intensiteit |\n| Sigbare lig | sien, fotografie | baie helder lig (bv. die son) beskadig die oë |\n| Ultraviolet (UV) | sterilisering van water en toerusting, opsporing van vals banknote, vitamien D in die vel | sonbrand, velkanker, oogskade (katarakte) |\n| X-strale | beelde van bene, skandering van bagasie by lughawens | beskadig selle en DNS; kanker |\n| Gammastrale | radioterapie (kankerselle doodmaak), sterilisering van mediese toerusting en voedsel | die gevaarlikste: ernstige sel- en DNS-skade, kanker |\n\n**Sigbare lig** strek van ongeveer 700 nm (**rooi**, laagste energie) tot 400 nm (**violet**, hoogste energie): rooi, oranje, geel, groen, blou, indigo, violet.\n\n> **Wenk:** Leer die volgorde radio → mikro → infrarooi → sigbaar → UV → X → gamma uit jou kop. Vrae vra dikwels om 'n lys in volgorde van toenemende frekwensie of afnemende golflengte te rangskik (dit is dieselfde volgorde).\n\n## Formules\n\n**Golfvergelyking:** c = fλ\n- c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}; f in hertz (Hz); λ in meter (m).\n\n**Energie van 'n foton:** E = hf = [[hc/λ]]\n- E in joule (J); h = 6,63 × 10^{−34} J·s (Planck se konstante).\n- E is **direk eweredig** aan f: dubbel die frekwensie → dubbel die energie per foton.\n- E is **omgekeerd eweredig** aan λ: halveer die golflengte → dubbel die energie.\n\n| Eenheid | Omskakeling |\n|---|---|\n| 1 nm (nanometer) | 1 × 10^{−9} m |\n| 1 kHz | 1 × 10^{3} Hz |\n| 1 MHz | 1 × 10^{6} Hz |\n| 1 GHz | 1 × 10^{9} Hz |\n\n### Stappe vir 'n berekening\n1. Skryf die gegewe waardes neer en skakel om na SI-eenhede (nm → m, MHz → Hz).\n2. Skryf die formule neer.\n3. Vervang die waardes.\n4. Bereken en skryf die antwoord met die eenheid, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke (bv. 3,98 × 10^{−19} J).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om nm nie na m om te skakel nie, of om 340 m·s^{−1} (die spoed van klank) vir lig te gebruik. EM-golwe beweeg altyd teen c in 'n vakuum.\n\n## Deurdringingsvermoë en gevaar\n\nHoe **hoër die frekwensie**, hoe **meer energie** dra elke foton, en hoe **groter is die deurdringingsvermoë** van die straling. Neem die menslike liggaam as voorbeeld: dit straal infrarooi uit, dit weerkaats sigbare lig, UV dring net die vel binne, X-strale gaan deur sagte weefsel maar word deur bene geabsorbeer, en gammastrale gaan dwarsdeur; net dik lood of beton keer gammastrale effektief.\n\nDie fotone van **X-strale en gammastrale** (en hoë-energie UV) het genoeg energie om elektrone uit atome te slaan (**ioniserende straling**). **UV, X-strale en gammastrale** kan DNS beskadig, wat mutasies en **kanker** kan veroorsaak. Daarom:\n- smeer sonskerm en dra 'n hoed: Suid-Afrika, ook die Hoëveld rondom Brits, het baie hoë UV-vlakke;\n- staan 'n radiograaf agter 'n loodskerm en dra pasiënte 'n loodvoorskoot.\n\nSelfone (mikrogolwe) en kraglyne (baie lae frekwensie) straal lae-energie straling uit wat nie ioniserend is nie. Daar is geen duidelike bewys dat dit by normale gebruik skadelik is nie, maar navorsing gaan voort.\n\n> **Onthou!** 'n **Helderder** lig stuur **meer fotone** uit, nie fotone met meer energie nie. Die energie van **elke foton** hang net van f (of λ) af. Daarom kan swak UV jou vel verbrand, maar 'n helder rooi lamp nie.","en":"## What is electromagnetic radiation?\n\n**Electromagnetic (EM) radiation** is energy that travels through space as waves. An EM wave is produced when a **charged particle accelerates**. The accelerating charge creates an oscillating **electric field**, which generates an oscillating **magnetic field** perpendicular to it, which in turn generates an electric field, and so on. These **mutually regenerating fields** are perpendicular to each other and perpendicular to the direction of motion, so EM waves are **transverse waves**.\n\n- EM waves need **no medium**: sunlight reaches us through the vacuum of space. (Sound cannot travel through a vacuum.)\n- All EM waves travel at the same speed in a vacuum, the **speed of light**: c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. In air the speed is practically the same.\n\n## Wave–particle duality\n\nEM radiation has a **dual nature**. Some properties are best explained with a **wave model** (e.g. interference and diffraction), others best with a **particle model** (e.g. the photoelectric effect, where light knocks electrons out of a metal surface). The \"particles\" of EM radiation are called **photons**.\n\n> **Definition:** A **photon** is a quantum (packet) of energy.\n\n## The EM spectrum\n\nThe types are arranged here from **low frequency, long wavelength and low energy** (top) to **high frequency, short wavelength and high energy** (bottom):\n\n| Type | Uses | Dangers |\n|---|---|---|\n| Radio waves | radio and TV broadcasts, two-way radios | no known danger at normal levels |\n| Microwaves | microwave ovens, cellphones, wi-fi, radar (speed traps), satellite TV | strong beams heat body tissue |\n| Infrared (IR) | TV remote controls, night-vision and thermal cameras, heat lamps | burns at high intensity |\n| Visible light | seeing, photography | very bright light (e.g. the sun) damages the eyes |\n| Ultraviolet (UV) | sterilising water and equipment, detecting fake banknotes, vitamin D in the skin | sunburn, skin cancer, eye damage (cataracts) |\n| X-rays | images of bones, scanning luggage at airports | damage cells and DNA; cancer |\n| Gamma rays | radiotherapy (killing cancer cells), sterilising medical equipment and food | the most dangerous: serious cell and DNA damage, cancer |\n\n**Visible light** ranges from about 700 nm (**red**, lowest energy) to 400 nm (**violet**, highest energy): red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet.\n\n> **Tip:** Learn the order radio → micro → infrared → visible → UV → X → gamma by heart. Questions often ask you to arrange a list in order of increasing frequency or decreasing wavelength (that is the same order).\n\n## Formulae\n\n**Wave equation:** c = fλ\n- c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}; f in hertz (Hz); λ in metres (m).\n\n**Energy of a photon:** E = hf = [[hc/λ]]\n- E in joules (J); h = 6.63 × 10^{−34} J·s (Planck's constant).\n- E is **directly proportional** to f: double the frequency → double the energy per photon.\n- E is **inversely proportional** to λ: halve the wavelength → double the energy.\n\n| Unit | Conversion |\n|---|---|\n| 1 nm (nanometre) | 1 × 10^{−9} m |\n| 1 kHz | 1 × 10^{3} Hz |\n| 1 MHz | 1 × 10^{6} Hz |\n| 1 GHz | 1 × 10^{9} Hz |\n\n### Steps for a calculation\n1. Write down the given values and convert to SI units (nm → m, MHz → Hz).\n2. Write down the formula.\n3. Substitute the values.\n4. Calculate and write the answer with its unit, rounded to two decimal places (e.g. 3.98 × 10^{−19} J).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Not converting nm to m, or using 340 m·s^{−1} (the speed of sound) for light. EM waves always travel at c in a vacuum.\n\n## Penetrating ability and danger\n\nThe **higher the frequency**, the **more energy** each photon carries, and the **greater the penetrating ability** of the radiation. Take the human body as an example: it emits infrared, it reflects visible light, UV only penetrates the skin, X-rays pass through soft tissue but are absorbed by bones, and gamma rays go right through; only thick lead or concrete stops gamma rays effectively.\n\nThe photons of **X-rays and gamma rays** (and high-energy UV) have enough energy to knock electrons out of atoms (**ionising radiation**). **UV, X-rays and gamma rays** can damage DNA, which can cause mutations and **cancer**. That is why:\n- you wear sunscreen and a hat: South Africa, including the Highveld around Brits, has very high UV levels;\n- a radiographer stands behind a lead screen and patients wear a lead apron.\n\nCellphones (microwaves) and power lines (very low frequency) emit low-energy radiation that is not ionising. There is no clear proof that it is harmful during normal use, but research continues.\n\n> **Remember!** A **brighter** light sends out **more photons**, not photons with more energy. The energy of **each photon** depends only on f (or λ). That is why weak UV can burn your skin, but a bright red lamp cannot."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese straling","en":"Electromagnetic radiation"},"def":{"af":"Energie wat as transversale golwe van wedersyds regenererende, loodregte elektriese en magnetiese velde teen die spoed van lig deur die ruimte beweeg; dit word deur versnellende ladings veroorsaak.","en":"Energy that travels through space at the speed of light as transverse waves of mutually regenerating, perpendicular electric and magnetic fields; it is caused by accelerating charges."}},{"term":{"af":"Foton","en":"Photon"},"def":{"af":"'n Kwantum (pakkie) energie.","en":"A quantum (packet) of energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Golf-deeltjie-dualiteit","en":"Wave–particle duality"},"def":{"af":"EM-straling gedra soms soos 'n golf (bv. interferensie) en soms soos 'n stroom deeltjies, fotone (bv. die foto-elektriese effek).","en":"EM radiation sometimes behaves like a wave (e.g. interference) and sometimes like a stream of particles, photons (e.g. the photoelectric effect)."}},{"term":{"af":"Golflengte (λ)","en":"Wavelength (λ)"},"def":{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende punte in fase, bv. twee opeenvolgende kruine. Eenheid: meter (m).","en":"The distance between two successive points in phase, e.g. two successive crests. Unit: metre (m)."}},{"term":{"af":"Frekwensie (f)","en":"Frequency (f)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal golwe wat per sekonde by 'n punt verbygaan. Eenheid: hertz (Hz).","en":"The number of waves that pass a point per second. Unit: hertz (Hz)."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese spektrum","en":"Electromagnetic spectrum"},"def":{"af":"Al die tipes EM-straling gerangskik volgens frekwensie of golflengte: radiogolwe, mikrogolwe, infrarooi, sigbare lig, UV, X-strale, gammastrale.","en":"All the types of EM radiation arranged according to frequency or wavelength: radio waves, microwaves, infrared, visible light, UV, X-rays, gamma rays."}},{"term":{"af":"Planck se konstante (h)","en":"Planck's constant (h)"},"def":{"af":"Die konstante h = 6,63 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s wat die energie van 'n foton aan sy frekwensie koppel: E = hf.","en":"The constant h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s that links the energy of a photon to its frequency: E = hf."}},{"term":{"af":"Deurdringingsvermoë","en":"Penetrating ability"},"def":{"af":"Hoe goed straling deur materiale kan beweeg; dit neem toe soos die frekwensie (en dus die energie per foton) toeneem.","en":"How well radiation can pass through materials; it increases as the frequency (and therefore the energy per photon) increases."}},{"term":{"af":"Ioniserende straling","en":"Ionising radiation"},"def":{"af":"Straling waarvan die fotone genoeg energie het om elektrone uit atome te slaan, bv. X-strale en gammastrale; dit kan selle en DNS beskadig.","en":"Radiation whose photons have enough energy to knock electrons out of atoms, e.g. X-rays and gamma rays; it can damage cells and DNA."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Frekwensie van 'n afstandbeheerder","en":"Frequency of a remote control"},"problem":{"af":"'n TV-afstandbeheerder stuur infrarooistraling met 'n golflengte van 940 nm uit. Bereken die frekwensie van die straling.","en":"A TV remote control emits infrared radiation with a wavelength of 940 nm. Calculate the frequency of the radiation."},"steps":[{"af":"Gegee: λ = 940 nm = 940 × 10^{−9} m = 9,4 × 10^{−7} m en c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. Skakel altyd eers nm na m om.","en":"Given: λ = 940 nm = 940 × 10^{−9} m = 9.4 × 10^{−7} m and c = 3 × 10^{8} m·s^{−1}. Always convert nm to m first."},{"af":"Formule: c = fλ, dus f = [[c/λ]]","en":"Formula: c = fλ, so f = [[c/λ]]"},{"af":"Vervang: f = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (9,4 × 10^{−7})","en":"Substitute: f = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (9.4 × 10^{−7})"},{"af":"f = 3,19 × 10^{14} Hz","en":"f = 3.19 × 10^{14} Hz"}],"answer":{"af":"f = 3,19 × 10¹⁴ Hz","en":"f = 3.19 × 10¹⁴ Hz"}},{"title":{"af":"Frekwensie en energie van 'n X-straalfoton","en":"Frequency and energy of an X-ray photon"},"problem":{"af":"'n Bundel X-strale het 'n golflengte van 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ m. Bereken (a) die frekwensie en (b) die energie van een X-straalfoton.","en":"A beam of X-rays has a wavelength of 1 × 10⁻¹⁰ m. Calculate (a) the frequency and (b) the energy of one X-ray photon."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) c = fλ, dus f = [[c/λ]] = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10})","en":"(a) c = fλ, so f = [[c/λ]] = (3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10})"},{"af":"f = 3 × 10^{18} Hz","en":"f = 3 × 10^{18} Hz"},{"af":"(b) E = hf = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{18})","en":"(b) E = hf = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{18})"},{"af":"E = 1,99 × 10^{−15} J. Kontrole met E = [[hc/λ]] = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10}) = 1,99 × 10^{−15} J ✔","en":"E = 1.99 × 10^{−15} J. Check with E = [[hc/λ]] = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (1 × 10^{−10}) = 1.99 × 10^{−15} J ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) f = 3 × 10¹⁸ Hz  (b) E = 1,99 × 10⁻¹⁵ J","en":"(a) f = 3 × 10¹⁸ Hz  (b) E = 1.99 × 10⁻¹⁵ J"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom UV jou vel verbrand, maar rooi lig nie","en":"Why UV burns your skin but red light does not"},"problem":{"af":"Bereken die energie van (a) 'n UV-foton met λ = 300 nm en (b) 'n rooi foton met λ = 700 nm. (c) Hoeveel keer meer energie het die UV-foton? (d) Verduidelik waarom jy op 'n somersdag by Hartbeespoortdam sonbrand kry, maar nie langs 'n helder rooi lamp nie.","en":"Calculate the energy of (a) a UV photon with λ = 300 nm and (b) a red photon with λ = 700 nm. (c) How many times more energy does the UV photon have? (d) Explain why you get sunburnt on a summer's day at Hartbeespoort Dam, but not next to a bright red lamp."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) E = [[hc/λ]] = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (300 × 10^{−9}) = 6,63 × 10^{−19} J","en":"(a) E = [[hc/λ]] = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (300 × 10^{−9}) = 6.63 × 10^{−19} J"},{"af":"(b) E = (6,63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (700 × 10^{−9}) = 2,84 × 10^{−19} J","en":"(b) E = (6.63 × 10^{−34})(3 × 10^{8}) ÷ (700 × 10^{−9}) = 2.84 × 10^{−19} J"},{"af":"(c) E is omgekeerd eweredig aan λ: 700 ÷ 300 = 2,33. Die UV-foton het 2,33 keer soveel energie.","en":"(c) E is inversely proportional to λ: 700 ÷ 300 = 2.33. The UV photon has 2.33 times as much energy."},{"af":"(d) Skade aan velselle hang af van die energie van elke foton, nie van hoe helder die lig is nie. Elke UV-foton het genoeg energie om die DNS in velselle te beskadig (sonbrand, velkanker). 'n Helder rooi lamp stuur net meer fotone uit, maar elkeen het te min energie om selle te beskadig.","en":"(d) Damage to skin cells depends on the energy of each photon, not on how bright the light is. Each UV photon has enough energy to damage the DNA in skin cells (sunburn, skin cancer). A bright red lamp only sends out more photons, but each one has too little energy to damage cells."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 6,63 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (b) 2,84 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (c) 2,33 keer  (d) elke UV-foton het genoeg energie om selle te beskadig; helderheid verander net die aantal fotone.","en":"(a) 6.63 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (b) 2.84 × 10⁻¹⁹ J  (c) 2.33 times  (d) each UV photon has enough energy to damage cells; brightness only changes the number of photons."}},{"title":{"af":"Rangskik en verduidelik: die radiograaf se loodskerm","en":"Arrange and explain: the radiographer's lead screen"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Rangskik die volgende in volgorde van toenemende frekwensie: X-strale, mikrogolwe, gammastrale, sigbare lig. (b) Verduidelik waarom 'n radiograaf agter 'n loodskerm staan terwyl sy 'n X-straalfoto neem, al word die pasiënt self aan die X-strale blootgestel.","en":"(a) Arrange the following in order of increasing frequency: X-rays, microwaves, gamma rays, visible light. (b) Explain why a radiographer stands behind a lead screen while she takes an X-ray, even though the patient is exposed to the X-rays."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Van lae na hoë frekwensie: mikrogolwe → sigbare lig → X-strale → gammastrale.","en":"(a) From low to high frequency: microwaves → visible light → X-rays → gamma rays."},{"af":"(b) X-strale het 'n hoë frekwensie, dus volgens E = hf 'n hoë energie per foton en 'n groot deurdringingsvermoë: hulle gaan deur sagte weefsel en kan selle en DNS beskadig (ioniserende straling).","en":"(b) X-rays have a high frequency, so according to E = hf a high energy per photon and a great penetrating ability: they pass through soft tissue and can damage cells and DNA (ionising radiation)."},{"af":"Lood is baie dig en absorbeer X-strale. Die radiograaf neem elke dag baie foto's, so sonder 'n skerm sou haar blootstelling opbou en die risiko vir kanker verhoog.","en":"Lead is very dense and absorbs X-rays. The radiographer takes many X-rays every day, so without a screen her exposure would build up and increase the risk of cancer."},{"af":"Die pasiënt kry net een klein dosis; die voordeel (bv. om 'n gebreekte been te sien) is groter as die klein risiko.","en":"The patient only gets one small dose; the benefit (e.g. seeing a broken bone) is greater than the small risk."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) mikrogolwe, sigbare lig, X-strale, gammastrale. (b) X-strale is hoë-energie, deurdringende, ioniserende straling; lood absorbeer dit en beskerm die radiograaf teen herhaalde blootstelling.","en":"(a) microwaves, visible light, X-rays, gamma rays. (b) X-rays are high-energy, penetrating, ionising radiation; lead absorbs them and protects the radiographer from repeated exposure."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tipe elektromagnetiese straling het die langste golflengte?","en":"Which type of electromagnetic radiation has the longest wavelength?"},"options":[{"af":"Gammastrale","en":"Gamma rays"},{"af":"Ultravioletstraling","en":"Ultraviolet radiation"},{"af":"Radiogolwe","en":"Radio waves"},{"af":"X-strale","en":"X-rays"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Van lang na kort golflengte: radio → mikro → infrarooi → sigbaar → UV → X → gamma. Radiogolwe het die langste golflengte, en dus die laagste frekwensie en energie; gammastrale het die kortste.","en":"From long to short wavelength: radio → micro → infrared → visible → UV → X → gamma. Radio waves have the longest wavelength, and therefore the lowest frequency and energy; gamma rays have the shortest."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Alle tipes elektromagnetiese straling beweeg in 'n vakuum teen dieselfde spoed, 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹.","en":"All types of electromagnetic radiation travel at the same speed in a vacuum, 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Radiogolwe en gammastrale verskil in frekwensie en golflengte, maar in 'n vakuum beweeg alle EM-golwe teen c = 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹. Daarom kan jy c = fλ vir enige tipe gebruik.","en":"True. Radio waves and gamma rays differ in frequency and wavelength, but in a vacuum all EM waves travel at c = 3 × 10⁸ m·s⁻¹. That is why you can use c = fλ for any type."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n foton?","en":"What is a photon?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Negatief gelaaide deeltjie wat om die kern van 'n atoom beweeg","en":"A negatively charged particle that moves around the nucleus of an atom"},{"af":"'n Kwantum (pakkie) energie","en":"A quantum (packet) of energy"},{"af":"Die afstand tussen twee opeenvolgende kruine van 'n golf","en":"The distance between two successive crests of a wave"},{"af":"'n Gebied waar die deeltjies van 'n medium saamgedruk is","en":"A region where the particles of a medium are pressed together"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Foton is 'n kwantum (pakkie) energie: die 'deeltjie' van EM-straling. Die ander opsies beskryf 'n elektron, golflengte en 'n kompressie.","en":"A photon is a quantum (packet) of energy: the 'particle' of EM radiation. The other options describe an electron, wavelength and a compression."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke tipe EM-straling by 'n gebruik daarvan.","en":"Match each type of EM radiation to one of its uses."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Radiogolwe","en":"Radio waves"},"r":{"af":"Radio- en TV-uitsendings","en":"Radio and TV broadcasts"}},{"l":{"af":"Mikrogolwe","en":"Microwaves"},"r":{"af":"Selfoonseine en radar","en":"Cellphone signals and radar"}},{"l":{"af":"Infrarooi","en":"Infrared"},"r":{"af":"TV-afstandbeheerders en nagsigkameras","en":"TV remote controls and night-vision cameras"}},{"l":{"af":"X-strale","en":"X-rays"},"r":{"af":"'n Beeld van 'n gebreekte arm","en":"An image of a broken arm"}},{"l":{"af":"Gammastrale","en":"Gamma rays"},"r":{"af":"Kankerselle doodmaak (radioterapie)","en":"Killing cancer cells (radiotherapy)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Radio en TV gebruik radiogolwe; selfone en radar gebruik mikrogolwe; afstandbeheerders en nagsigkameras gebruik infrarooi; X-strale gaan deur sagte weefsel maar word deur been geabsorbeer; gammastrale het genoeg energie om kankerselle dood te maak.","en":"Radio and TV use radio waves; cellphones and radar use microwaves; remote controls and night-vision cameras use infrared; X-rays pass through soft tissue but are absorbed by bone; gamma rays have enough energy to kill cancer cells."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling beskryf 'n elektromagnetiese golf korrek?","en":"Which statement describes an electromagnetic wave correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is 'n longitudinale golf wat 'n medium soos lug nodig het.","en":"It is a longitudinal wave that needs a medium such as air."},{"af":"Dit bestaan uit 'n elektriese veld en 'n magneetveld wat ewewydig aan die bewegingsrigting ossilleer.","en":"It consists of an electric field and a magnetic field that oscillate parallel to the direction of motion."},{"af":"Dit bestaan net uit 'n ossillerende elektriese veld; die magneetveld bly konstant.","en":"It consists only of an oscillating electric field; the magnetic field stays constant."},{"af":"Dit bestaan uit 'n elektriese veld en 'n magneetveld wat loodreg op mekaar en op die bewegingsrigting ossilleer en mekaar wedersyds opwek.","en":"It consists of an electric field and a magnetic field that oscillate perpendicular to each other and to the direction of motion and mutually regenerate each other."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n EM-golf is 'n transversale golf: die ossillerende elektriese en magnetiese velde wek mekaar op, staan loodreg op mekaar en loodreg op die bewegingsrigting, en het geen medium nodig nie. 'n Longitudinale golf met 'n medium beskryf klank.","en":"An EM wave is a transverse wave: the oscillating electric and magnetic fields generate each other, are perpendicular to each other and to the direction of motion, and need no medium. A longitudinal wave with a medium describes sound."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Elektromagnetiese golwe het, net soos klank, 'n medium nodig om deur te beweeg.","en":"Electromagnetic waves, just like sound, need a medium to travel through."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. EM-golwe kan deur 'n vakuum beweeg: sonlig bereik die aarde deur die leë ruimte. Klank is 'n meganiese golf en het wel 'n medium nodig.","en":"False. EM waves can travel through a vacuum: sunlight reaches Earth through empty space. Sound is a mechanical wave and does need a medium."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is X-strale en gammastrale baie gevaarliker vir mense as radiogolwe?","en":"Why are X-rays and gamma rays much more dangerous to people than radio waves?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het 'n hoër frekwensie, dus dra elke foton meer energie en kan dit selle en DNS beskadig.","en":"They have a higher frequency, so each photon carries more energy and can damage cells and DNA."},{"af":"Hulle beweeg vinniger as radiogolwe en tref die liggaam dus harder.","en":"They travel faster than radio waves and therefore hit the body harder."},{"af":"Hulle het 'n langer golflengte, dus dra elke foton meer energie.","en":"They have a longer wavelength, so each photon carries more energy."},{"af":"Hulle het altyd 'n groter amplitude as radiogolwe.","en":"They always have a larger amplitude than radio waves."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"E = hf: hoë frekwensie beteken hoë energie per foton en groot deurdringingsvermoë. Alle EM-golwe beweeg teen dieselfde spoed c, en X- en gammastrale het 'n KORTER golflengte, nie 'n langer een nie.","en":"E = hf: high frequency means high energy per photon and great penetrating ability. All EM waves travel at the same speed c, and X-rays and gamma rays have a SHORTER wavelength, not a longer one."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Radiostasie saai uit teen 'n frekwensie van 94,2 MHz. Bereken die golflengte van die radiogolwe, afgerond tot twee desimale plekke: λ = ___ m","en":"A radio station broadcasts at a frequency of 94.2 MHz. Calculate the wavelength of the radio waves, rounded to two decimal places: λ = ___ m"},"answers":{"af":["3,18","3,18 m","3.18","3.18 m"],"en":["3,18","3,18 m","3.18","3.18 m"]},"explain":{"af":"94,2 MHz = 94,2 × 10⁶ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (94,2 × 10⁶) = 3,18 m.","en":"94.2 MHz = 94.2 × 10⁶ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (94.2 × 10⁶) = 3.18 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,31","3184,71","3,19"],"en":["0.31","3184.71","3.19"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Mikrogolfoond werk teen 'n frekwensie van 2,45 GHz. Wat is die golflengte van die mikrogolwe?","en":"A microwave oven works at a frequency of 2.45 GHz. What is the wavelength of the microwaves?"},"options":[{"af":"122,45 m","en":"122.45 m"},{"af":"7,35 × 10¹⁷ m","en":"7.35 × 10¹⁷ m"},{"af":"1,39 × 10⁻⁷ m","en":"1.39 × 10⁻⁷ m"},{"af":"0,12 m","en":"0.12 m"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"2,45 GHz = 2,45 × 10⁹ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (2,45 × 10⁹) = 0,12 m. Jy kry 122,45 m as jy giga as 10⁶ (mega) neem, 7,35 × 10¹⁷ m as jy c en f vermenigvuldig, en 1,39 × 10⁻⁷ m as jy die spoed van klank (340 m·s⁻¹) gebruik.","en":"2.45 GHz = 2.45 × 10⁹ Hz. λ = c/f = (3 × 10⁸) ÷ (2.45 × 10⁹) = 0.12 m. You get 122.45 m if you take giga as 10⁶ (mega), 7.35 × 10¹⁷ m if you multiply c and f, and 1.39 × 10⁻⁷ m if you use the speed of sound (340 m·s⁻¹)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die energie van 'n foton groen lig met 'n golflengte van 500 nm. Rond af tot twee desimale plekke: E = ___ × 10⁻¹⁹ J","en":"Calculate the energy of a photon of green light with a wavelength of 500 nm. Round to two decimal places: E = ___ × 10⁻¹⁹ J"},"answers":{"af":["3,98","3.98","3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹","3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","3,98 x 10^-19","3.98 x 10^-19","3.98e-19"],"en":["3,98","3.98","3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹","3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J","3,98 x 10^-19","3.98 x 10^-19","3.98e-19"]},"explain":{"af":"λ = 500 nm = 500 × 10⁻⁹ m = 5 × 10⁻⁷ m. E = hc/λ = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (5 × 10⁻⁷) = 3,98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J.","en":"λ = 500 nm = 500 × 10⁻⁹ m = 5 × 10⁻⁷ m. E = hc/λ = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (5 × 10⁻⁷) = 3.98 × 10⁻¹⁹ J."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,40","39,78","397,80"],"en":["0.40","39.78","397.80"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bereken die energie van 'n X-straalfoton met 'n frekwensie van 4 × 10¹⁸ Hz.","en":"Calculate the energy of an X-ray photon with a frequency of 4 × 10¹⁸ Hz."},"options":[{"af":"8,84 × 10⁻²⁴ J","en":"8.84 × 10⁻²⁴ J"},{"af":"2,65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J","en":"2.65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J"},{"af":"1,66 × 10⁻⁵² J","en":"1.66 × 10⁻⁵² J"},{"af":"7,96 × 10⁻⁷ J","en":"7.96 × 10⁻⁷ J"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"E = hf = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(4 × 10¹⁸) = 2,65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J. As f gegee is, het jy c nie nodig nie: hf/c gee 8,84 × 10⁻²⁴ J, h/f gee 1,66 × 10⁻⁵² J en hcf gee 7,96 × 10⁻⁷ J.","en":"E = hf = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(4 × 10¹⁸) = 2.65 × 10⁻¹⁵ J. When f is given you do not need c: hf/c gives 8.84 × 10⁻²⁴ J, h/f gives 1.66 × 10⁻⁵² J and hcf gives 7.96 × 10⁻⁷ J."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Foton het 'n energie van 3,315 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Bereken die golflengte van die lig in nanometer: λ = ___ nm","en":"A photon has an energy of 3.315 × 10⁻¹⁹ J. Calculate the wavelength of the light in nanometres: λ = ___ nm"},"answers":{"af":["600","600 nm","600,00","600,00 nm","600.00","600.00 nm"],"en":["600","600 nm","600,00","600,00 nm","600.00","600.00 nm"]},"explain":{"af":"E = hc/λ, dus λ = hc/E = (6,63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (3,315 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6 × 10⁻⁷ m. Omskakeling: 6 × 10⁻⁷ m ÷ 10⁻⁹ = 600 nm (oranje lig).","en":"E = hc/λ, so λ = hc/E = (6.63 × 10⁻³⁴)(3 × 10⁸) ÷ (3.315 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 6 × 10⁻⁷ m. Conversion: 6 × 10⁻⁷ m ÷ 10⁻⁹ = 600 nm (orange light)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["60","6000","0,6"],"en":["60","6000","0.6"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Foton A (UV) het 'n golflengte van 200 nm en foton B 'n golflengte van 600 nm. Hoeveel keer groter is die energie van foton A as dié van foton B? ___","en":"Photon A (UV) has a wavelength of 200 nm and photon B a wavelength of 600 nm. How many times greater is the energy of photon A than that of photon B? ___"},"answers":{"af":["3","3 keer","drie","drie keer","3x","3×"],"en":["3","3 times","three","three times","3x","3×"]},"explain":{"af":"E = hc/λ, dus is E omgekeerd eweredig aan λ. λ_B ÷ λ_A = 600 ÷ 200 = 3, dus het foton A 3 keer soveel energie as foton B. Jy hoef nie die energieë self uit te werk nie.","en":"E = hc/λ, so E is inversely proportional to λ. λ_B ÷ λ_A = 600 ÷ 200 = 3, so photon A has 3 times as much energy as photon B. You do not need to work out the energies themselves."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1/3","9","400"],"en":["1/3","9","400"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: “'n Baie helder rooi lamp is gevaarliker vir jou vel as 'n swak UV-lamp, want die helder lig dra meer energie.” Watter stelling evalueer sy bewering die beste?","en":"Thabo says: “A very bright red lamp is more dangerous to your skin than a weak UV lamp, because the bright light carries more energy.” Which statement evaluates his claim best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: helderder lig beteken dat elke foton meer energie het.","en":"He is right: brighter light means that each photon has more energy."},{"af":"Hy is reg: rooi lig het 'n langer golflengte en dus meer energie per foton.","en":"He is right: red light has a longer wavelength and therefore more energy per photon."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: die helder lamp stuur net meer fotone uit; elke UV-foton het meer energie as 'n rooi foton (E = hf) en kan velselle beskadig, al is die UV-lamp swak.","en":"He is wrong: the bright lamp only sends out more photons; each UV photon has more energy than a red photon (E = hf) and can damage skin cells, even if the UV lamp is weak."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd, want rooi lig beweeg stadiger as UV-straling en tref die vel met minder energie.","en":"He is wrong, because red light travels slower than UV radiation and hits the skin with less energy."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Skade aan selle hang af van die energie van elke foton, en dit hang net van die frekwensie af (E = hf). UV het 'n hoër frekwensie as rooi lig. Helderheid bepaal net hoeveel fotone daar is. Alle EM-straling beweeg teen dieselfde spoed, en 'n langer golflengte beteken MINDER energie.","en":"Damage to cells depends on the energy of each photon, and that depends only on the frequency (E = hf). UV has a higher frequency than red light. Brightness only determines how many photons there are. All EM radiation travels at the same speed, and a longer wavelength means LESS energy."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Elektrisiteit en magnetisme; chemiese verandering","en":"Electricity and magnetism; chemical change"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t2-magnetisme","title":{"af":"Magnetisme","en":"Magnetism"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal magneetvelde in woorde kan beskryf, aantrekking en afstoting kan voorspel, en die aarde se magneetveld, die kompas en die magnetosfeer kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to describe magnetic fields in words, predict attraction and repulsion, and explain Earth's magnetic field, the compass and the magnetosphere."},"summary":{"af":"## Magnete en pole\n\n'n **Magneet** is 'n voorwerp met 'n paar teenoorgestelde pole: 'n **noordpool (N)** en 'n **suidpool (S)**. As 'n staafmagneet vrylik aan 'n tou hang, draai sy N-pool na die noorde; daarom word dit ook die *noordsoekende pool* genoem.\n\n- **Gelyke pole stoot mekaar af; ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan.**\n- Pole kom altyd in pare voor. Breek jy 'n magneet middeldeur, kry **elke stuk weer 'n N- en 'n S-pool**. 'n Magneet met net een pool bestaan nie.\n- Die magnetiese krag is 'n **nie-kontakkrag**: magnete werk op mekaar in sonder om te raak. Die krag is die sterkste naby die pole en word swakker hoe verder die magnete van mekaar af is.\n\n> **Wenk:** Net **afstoting** bewys dat 'n voorwerp 'n magneet is. 'n Magneet trek ook gewone, ongemagnetiseerde yster aan, so aantrekking bewys niks.\n\n## Ferromagnetiese materiale en domeine\n\n**Yster, kobalt en nikkel** (en allooie soos staal) is **ferromagneties**: hulle word sterk deur 'n magneet aangetrek en kan self gemagnetiseer word. Koper, aluminium, goud, plastiek en hout is nie ferromagneties nie. Nie alle metale is dus magneties nie!\n\nIn 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal gedra die atome soos klein magnetjies wat in groepies, **magnetiese domeine**, almal in dieselfde rigting wys. In 'n ongemagnetiseerde spyker wys die domeine lukraak in alle rigtings, sodat hul effekte mekaar uitkanselleer. As jy dit magnetiseer (bv. deur dit herhaaldelik in een rigting met 'n magneet te stryk), lyn die domeine op.\n\n- **Sagte yster** magnetiseer en demagnetiseer maklik: goed vir tydelike magnete en elektromagnete.\n- **Staal** behou sy magnetisme: goed vir permanente magnete.\n- Sterk **verhitting** of **hamer en laat val** krap die domeine weer deurmekaar en verswak die magneet.\n\n## Die magneetveld\n\n> **Definisie:** 'n **Magneetveld** is 'n gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.\n\nOns stel die veld voor met **magneetveldlyne**. Jy kan die patroon sien deur **ystervylsels** om 'n magneet te strooi, of deur 'n klein **kompas** (self 'n magneetjie wat vrylik kan draai) van punt tot punt te skuif.\n\nReëls vir magneetveldlyne:\n1. **Rigting:** buite die magneet wys die lyne **van N na S**. Die rigting van die veld by 'n punt is die rigting waarin die **N-pool van 'n kompasnaald** daar wys.\n2. Veldlyne vorm **geslote lusse** (binne die magneet loop hulle van S na N).\n3. Veldlyne **kruis nooit** nie.\n4. Hoe **digter** die lyne, hoe **sterker** die veld. Die veld is die sterkste by die pole.\n\n### Veldpatrone in woorde\n- **Een staafmagneet:** die lyne kom by die N-pool uit, buig in boë aan albei kante van die magneet om en gaan by die S-pool in. Hulle is die digste by die twee pole.\n- **Ongelyke pole na mekaar (N … S):** die lyne loop reguit oor die gaping van N na S, dig en byna ewewydig. Die magnete **trek aan**.\n- **Gelyke pole na mekaar (N … N):** die lyne van albei pole buig weg van mekaar en loop sywaarts uit die gaping. Presies in die middel is 'n **neutrale punt** waar die twee velde mekaar uitkanselleer (veld = 0). Die magnete **stoot af**. By S … S is die patroon dieselfde, maar die pyltjies wys na die pole toe.\n\n## Die aarde se magneetveld\n\nDie aarde gedra asof daar 'n reuse-**staafmagneet** binne-in hom is. Die veld word waarskynlik veroorsaak deur **gesmelte yster wat in die vloeibare buitenste kern beweeg**.\n\n- Die **suidpool van hierdie \"staafmagneet\"** lê naby die **geografiese Noordpool**. Dit trek die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald aan (ongelyke pole trek aan), daarom wys 'n kompas oral op aarde, ook in Brits, noord.\n- Buite die aarde loop die veldlyne dus van die suidelike halfrond na die noordelike halfrond.\n\n| Eienskap | Geografiese Noordpool | Magnetiese noordpool |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wat is dit? | die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak sny (ware noord) | die punt waarheen 'n kompas wys; die veldlyne gaan hier vertikaal die aarde in |\n| Beweeg dit? | nee | ja, stadig oor die jare (tans in die Arktiese gebied) |\n| Magneetpool? | nee | magneties gesproke 'n **suidpool** |\n\nDie hoek tussen ware (geografiese) noord en magnetiese noord is die **magnetiese deklinasie**. In Suid-Afrika wys 'n kompas etlike grade **wes** van ware noord, so 'n stapper in die Magaliesberg moet sy kompaslesing met die deklinasie op die kaart regstel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** \"In die suidelike halfrond wys 'n kompas suid.\" Nee! Die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald wys oral op aarde na magnetiese noord.\n\n## Die magnetosfeer en die sonwind\n\nDie son stuur voortdurend 'n stroom **gelaaide deeltjies** (hoofsaaklik protone en elektrone) die ruimte in: die **sonwind**. Die **magnetosfeer** is die gebied rondom die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers. Dit **buig die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde** en beskerm so lewende organismes en die atmosfeer teen hierdie hoë-energie deeltjies. (Die osoonlaag, nie die magnetosfeer nie, beskerm ons teen UV-straling.)\n\n- Sommige deeltjies word langs die veldlyne na die **pole** gelei. Daar bots hulle met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer, wat dan gekleurde lig uitstraal: die **aurora** (Aurora Borealis of noorderlig in die noorde, Aurora Australis of suiderlig in die suide).\n- Groot uitbarstings op die son veroorsaak **magnetiese storms**. Dit kan satelliete beskadig, GPS en radiokommunikasie ontwrig, transformators in kragnetwerke beskadig en kompaslesings versteur.","en":"## Magnets and poles\n\nA **magnet** is an object with a pair of opposite poles: a **north pole (N)** and a **south pole (S)**. If a bar magnet hangs freely from a string, its N pole turns to the north; that is why it is also called the *north-seeking pole*.\n\n- **Like poles repel; unlike poles attract.**\n- Poles always occur in pairs. If you break a magnet in half, **each piece again has an N and an S pole**. A magnet with only one pole does not exist.\n- The magnetic force is a **non-contact force**: magnets act on each other without touching. The force is strongest near the poles and becomes weaker the further apart the magnets are.\n\n> **Tip:** Only **repulsion** proves that an object is a magnet. A magnet also attracts ordinary, unmagnetised iron, so attraction proves nothing.\n\n## Ferromagnetic materials and domains\n\n**Iron, cobalt and nickel** (and alloys such as steel) are **ferromagnetic**: they are strongly attracted by a magnet and can be magnetised themselves. Copper, aluminium, gold, plastic and wood are not ferromagnetic. So not all metals are magnetic!\n\nIn a ferromagnetic material the atoms behave like tiny magnets that, in groups called **magnetic domains**, all point in the same direction. In an unmagnetised nail the domains point randomly in all directions, so that their effects cancel. When you magnetise it (e.g. by stroking it repeatedly in one direction with a magnet), the domains line up.\n\n- **Soft iron** magnetises and demagnetises easily: good for temporary magnets and electromagnets.\n- **Steel** keeps its magnetism: good for permanent magnets.\n- Strong **heating** or **hammering and dropping** jumbles the domains again and weakens the magnet.\n\n## The magnetic field\n\n> **Definition:** A **magnetic field** is a region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force.\n\nWe represent the field with **magnetic field lines**. You can see the pattern by sprinkling **iron filings** around a magnet, or by moving a small **compass** (itself a tiny magnet that can turn freely) from point to point.\n\nRules for magnetic field lines:\n1. **Direction:** outside the magnet the lines point **from N to S**. The direction of the field at a point is the direction in which the **N pole of a compass needle** points there.\n2. Field lines form **closed loops** (inside the magnet they run from S to N).\n3. Field lines **never cross**.\n4. The **denser** the lines, the **stronger** the field. The field is strongest at the poles.\n\n### Field patterns in words\n- **One bar magnet:** the lines come out at the N pole, curve around in arcs on both sides of the magnet and go in at the S pole. They are densest at the two poles.\n- **Unlike poles facing (N … S):** the lines run straight across the gap from N to S, dense and almost parallel. The magnets **attract**.\n- **Like poles facing (N … N):** the lines from both poles bend away from each other and run sideways out of the gap. Exactly in the middle is a **neutral point** where the two fields cancel (field = 0). The magnets **repel**. For S … S the pattern is the same, but the arrows point towards the poles.\n\n## Earth's magnetic field\n\nEarth behaves as if there were a giant **bar magnet** inside it. The field is probably caused by **molten iron moving in the liquid outer core**.\n\n- The **south pole of this \"bar magnet\"** lies near the **geographic North Pole**. It attracts the N pole of a compass needle (unlike poles attract), which is why a compass points north everywhere on Earth, also in Brits.\n- Outside Earth the field lines therefore run from the southern hemisphere to the northern hemisphere.\n\n| Property | Geographic North Pole | Magnetic north pole |\n|---|---|---|\n| What is it? | the point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface (true north) | the point a compass points to; the field lines go vertically into Earth here |\n| Does it move? | no | yes, slowly over the years (currently in the Arctic region) |\n| Magnetic pole? | no | magnetically speaking a **south pole** |\n\nThe angle between true (geographic) north and magnetic north is the **magnetic declination**. In South Africa a compass points several degrees **west** of true north, so a hiker in the Magaliesberg must correct his compass reading with the declination on the map.\n\n> **Common mistake:** \"In the southern hemisphere a compass points south.\" No! The N pole of a compass needle points to magnetic north everywhere on Earth.\n\n## The magnetosphere and the solar wind\n\nThe sun continuously sends a stream of **charged particles** (mainly protons and electrons) into space: the **solar wind**. The **magnetosphere** is the region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates. It **deflects most of the solar wind around Earth** and so protects living organisms and the atmosphere from these high-energy particles. (The ozone layer, not the magnetosphere, protects us from UV radiation.)\n\n- Some particles are guided along the field lines to the **poles**. There they collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere, which then give off coloured light: the **aurora** (Aurora Borealis or northern lights in the north, Aurora Australis or southern lights in the south).\n- Large eruptions on the sun cause **magnetic storms**. These can damage satellites, disrupt GPS and radio communication, damage transformers in power grids and disturb compass readings."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Magneet","en":"Magnet"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met 'n paar teenoorgestelde pole (noord en suid) wat 'n magneetveld om hom het.","en":"An object with a pair of opposite poles (north and south) that has a magnetic field around it."}},{"term":{"af":"Magneetveld","en":"Magnetic field"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force."}},{"term":{"af":"Magneetveldlyne","en":"Magnetic field lines"},"def":{"af":"Denkbeeldige lyne wat die rigting en sterkte van 'n magneetveld aandui: buite die magneet van N na S, hulle kruis nooit, en hoe digter, hoe sterker die veld.","en":"Imaginary lines that show the direction and strength of a magnetic field: outside the magnet from N to S, they never cross, and the denser they are, the stronger the field."}},{"term":{"af":"Ferromagnetiese materiaal","en":"Ferromagnetic material"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal soos yster, kobalt, nikkel of hul allooie (bv. staal) wat sterk deur 'n magneet aangetrek word en self gemagnetiseer kan word.","en":"A material such as iron, cobalt, nickel or their alloys (e.g. steel) that is strongly attracted by a magnet and can be magnetised itself."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese domein","en":"Magnetic domain"},"def":{"af":"'n Klein gebied in 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal waarin die atoommagnetjies almal in dieselfde rigting wys.","en":"A small region in a ferromagnetic material in which the atomic magnets all point in the same direction."}},{"term":{"af":"Kompas","en":"Compass"},"def":{"af":"'n Klein magneet (naald) wat vrylik kan draai; sy N-pool wys in die rigting van die magneetveld.","en":"A small magnet (needle) that can turn freely; its N pole points in the direction of the magnetic field."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetiese noordpool","en":"Magnetic north pole"},"def":{"af":"Die punt in die Arktiese gebied waarheen 'n kompas wys. Magneties is dit 'n suidpool, en dit lê nie op dieselfde plek as die geografiese Noordpool nie.","en":"The point in the Arctic region to which a compass points. Magnetically it is a south pole, and it does not lie at the same place as the geographic North Pole."}},{"term":{"af":"Geografiese Noordpool","en":"Geographic North Pole"},"def":{"af":"Die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak in die noorde sny (ware noord).","en":"The point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface in the north (true north)."}},{"term":{"af":"Magnetosfeer","en":"Magnetosphere"},"def":{"af":"Die gebied rondom die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers; dit buig die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde.","en":"The region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates; it deflects most of the solar wind around Earth."}},{"term":{"af":"Sonwind","en":"Solar wind"},"def":{"af":"'n Stroom gelaaide deeltjies (hoofsaaklik protone en elektrone) wat voortdurend van die son af uitvloei.","en":"A stream of charged particles (mainly protons and electrons) that continuously flows out from the sun."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Karteer die veld van 'n staafmagneet","en":"Map the field of a bar magnet"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf hoe jy met 'n klein kompas die magneetveld om 'n staafmagneet kan karteer, en beskryf die veldpatroon wat jy kry in woorde.","en":"Describe how you can map the magnetic field around a bar magnet with a small compass, and describe the field pattern you get in words."},"steps":[{"af":"Sit die magneet op 'n vel papier en trek sy buitelyn. Plaas die kompas naby die N-pool en merk die punt waarheen die N-pool van die kompasnaald wys.","en":"Put the magnet on a sheet of paper and trace its outline. Place the compass near the N pole and mark the point to which the N pole of the compass needle points."},{"af":"Skuif die kompas sodat die S-kant van die naald op die merk is, en merk weer waarheen die N-pool wys. Herhaal tot jy by die S-pool uitkom. Verbind die merke met 'n gladde kromme met pyltjies van N na S: dit is een veldlyn.","en":"Move the compass so that the S end of the needle is on the mark, and mark again where the N pole points. Repeat until you reach the S pole. Join the marks with a smooth curve with arrows from N to S: this is one field line."},{"af":"Herhaal vanaf ander beginpunte. Die lyne kom by die N-pool uit, buig in boë aan albei kante van die magneet om en gaan by die S-pool in.","en":"Repeat from other starting points. The lines come out at the N pole, curve around in arcs on both sides of the magnet and go in at the S pole."},{"af":"Die lyne kruis nooit, en hulle is die digste by die pole, waar die veld die sterkste is. By enige punt is die veldrigting die rigting waarin die kompas se N-pool wys.","en":"The lines never cross, and they are densest at the poles, where the field is strongest. At any point the field direction is the direction in which the compass's N pole points."}],"answer":{"af":"Veldlyne loop buite die magneet van N na S, vorm geslote lusse, kruis nooit en is die digste (sterkste veld) by die pole.","en":"Field lines run from N to S outside the magnet, form closed loops, never cross and are densest (strongest field) at the poles."}},{"title":{"af":"Die veld tussen twee magnete","en":"The field between two magnets"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die magneetveld tussen twee staafmagnete wanneer (a) 'n N-pool en 'n S-pool na mekaar wys, en (b) twee N-pole na mekaar wys. Sê in elke geval of die magnete mekaar aantrek of afstoot.","en":"Describe the magnetic field between two bar magnets when (a) an N pole and an S pole face each other, and (b) two N poles face each other. In each case, say whether the magnets attract or repel each other."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) N … S: die veldlyne loop reguit oor die gaping van die N-pool na die S-pool. In die gaping is hulle dig en byna ewewydig, dus is die veld daar sterk en byna eenvormig.","en":"(a) N … S: the field lines run straight across the gap from the N pole to the S pole. In the gap they are dense and almost parallel, so the field there is strong and almost uniform."},{"af":"Ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan, dus trek die magnete aan.","en":"Unlike poles attract each other, so the magnets attract."},{"af":"(b) N … N: die veldlyne kom by albei N-pole uit en buig weg van mekaar, sywaarts uit die gaping. Geen lyn loop van die een N-pool na die ander nie.","en":"(b) N … N: the field lines come out at both N poles and bend away from each other, sideways out of the gap. No line runs from one N pole to the other."},{"af":"Presies in die middel is die twee velde ewe sterk en teenoorgesteld: hulle kanselleer uit, en dit is 'n neutrale punt (veld = 0). Gelyke pole stoot mekaar af, dus stoot die magnete af.","en":"Exactly in the middle the two fields are equally strong and opposite: they cancel, and this is a neutral point (field = 0). Like poles repel each other, so the magnets repel."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Reguit, digte lyne van N na S oor die gaping; aantrekking. (b) Lyne buig weg van mekaar met 'n neutrale punt in die middel; afstoting.","en":"(a) Straight, dense lines from N to S across the gap; attraction. (b) Lines bend away from each other with a neutral point in the middle; repulsion."}},{"title":{"af":"Kompas, magnetiese noord en ware noord","en":"Compass, magnetic north and true north"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik (a) waarom die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald in Brits na die noorde wys, (b) die verskil tussen die geografiese Noordpool en die magnetiese noordpool, en (c) wat 'n stapper in die Magaliesberg moet doen as sy met kaart en kompas ware noord wil volg.","en":"Explain (a) why the N pole of a compass needle in Brits points north, (b) the difference between the geographic North Pole and the magnetic north pole, and (c) what a hiker in the Magaliesberg must do if she wants to follow true north with a map and compass."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die aarde gedra soos 'n reuse-staafmagneet (waarskynlik weens bewegende gesmelte yster in die buitenste kern). Daardie magneet se S-pool lê naby die geografiese Noordpool. Ongelyke pole trek aan, dus word die N-pool van die naald na die noorde getrek, oral op aarde.","en":"(a) Earth behaves like a giant bar magnet (probably due to moving molten iron in the outer core). That magnet's S pole lies near the geographic North Pole. Unlike poles attract, so the N pole of the needle is pulled towards the north, everywhere on Earth."},{"af":"(b) Die geografiese Noordpool is die punt waar die aarde se rotasie-as die oppervlak sny; dit beweeg nie. Die magnetiese noordpool is die punt waarheen kompasse wys en waar die veldlyne vertikaal die aarde ingaan. Dit lê in die Arktiese gebied, nie op dieselfde plek nie, en beweeg stadig.","en":"(b) The geographic North Pole is the point where Earth's axis of rotation cuts the surface; it does not move. The magnetic north pole is the point compasses point to and where the field lines go vertically into Earth. It lies in the Arctic region, not at the same place, and moves slowly."},{"af":"(c) Die hoek tussen ware noord en magnetiese noord is die magnetiese deklinasie. In Suid-Afrika wys 'n kompas etlike grade wes van ware noord, dus moet sy die deklinasie wat op die kaart aangedui is, by haar kompaslesing in berekening bring.","en":"(c) The angle between true north and magnetic north is the magnetic declination. In South Africa a compass points several degrees west of true north, so she must take the declination shown on the map into account in her compass reading."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die aarde se magnetiese S-pool naby geografiese noord trek die naald se N-pool aan. (b) Geografies = rotasie-as, vas; magneties = waar kompasse wys, elders en beweeg. (c) Stel reg vir die deklinasie.","en":"(a) Earth's magnetic S pole near geographic north attracts the needle's N pole. (b) Geographic = axis of rotation, fixed; magnetic = where compasses point, elsewhere and moving. (c) Correct for the declination."}},{"title":{"af":"Sonstorms, die magnetosfeer en aurora's","en":"Solar storms, the magnetosphere and auroras"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens 'n sterk sonstorm word 'n groot wolk gelaaide deeltjies na die aarde geslinger. Verduidelik (a) hoe die magnetosfeer ons beskerm, (b) waarom aurora's hoofsaaklik naby die pole gesien word, en (c) watter skade so 'n magnetiese storm aan tegnologie kan doen.","en":"During a strong solar storm a large cloud of charged particles is flung towards Earth. Explain (a) how the magnetosphere protects us, (b) why auroras are mainly seen near the poles, and (c) what damage such a magnetic storm can do to technology."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die magnetosfeer is die gebied om die aarde waar die aarde se magneetveld oorheers. Gelaaide deeltjies wat deur 'n magneetveld beweeg, word afgebuig, dus word die meeste van die sonwind om die aarde gelei. Dit beskerm lewende organismes en die atmosfeer.","en":"(a) The magnetosphere is the region around Earth where Earth's magnetic field dominates. Charged particles moving through a magnetic field are deflected, so most of the solar wind is guided around Earth. This protects living organisms and the atmosphere."},{"af":"(b) Sommige deeltjies word langs die veldlyne na die pole gelei, waar die lyne die aarde ingaan. Daar bots hulle met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer, wat dan gekleurde lig uitstraal: Aurora Borealis in die noorde en Aurora Australis in die suide.","en":"(b) Some particles are guided along the field lines to the poles, where the lines enter Earth. There they collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere, which then give off coloured light: Aurora Borealis in the north and Aurora Australis in the south."},{"af":"(c) 'n Magnetiese storm kan satelliete beskadig, GPS en radiokommunikasie ontwrig, groot strome in lang kraglyne veroorsaak wat transformators beskadig, en kompaslesings versteur.","en":"(c) A magnetic storm can damage satellites, disrupt GPS and radio communication, cause large currents in long power lines that damage transformers, and disturb compass readings."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die magneetveld buig die gelaaide deeltjies om die aarde. (b) Veldlyne lei deeltjies na die pole, waar hulle met gasatome bots en lig uitstraal. (c) Satelliete, GPS, radio, kragnetwerke en kompasse word geraak.","en":"(a) The magnetic field deflects the charged particles around Earth. (b) Field lines guide particles to the poles, where they collide with gas atoms that give off light. (c) Satellites, GPS, radio, power grids and compasses are affected."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende materiale is ferromagneties?","en":"Which one of the following materials is ferromagnetic?"},"options":[{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},{"af":"Aluminium","en":"Aluminium"},{"af":"Nikkel","en":"Nickel"},{"af":"Glas","en":"Glass"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Yster, kobalt en nikkel (en allooie soos staal) is ferromagneties. Koper en aluminium is metale wat elektrisiteit goed gelei, maar 'n magneet trek hulle nie aan nie: nie alle metale is magneties nie.","en":"Iron, cobalt and nickel (and alloys such as steel) are ferromagnetic. Copper and aluminium are metals that conduct electricity well, but a magnet does not attract them: not all metals are magnetic."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gelyke magneetpole stoot mekaar af en ongelyke magneetpole trek mekaar aan.","en":"Like magnetic poles repel each other and unlike magnetic poles attract each other."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. N en N (of S en S) stoot af; N en S trek aan.","en":"True. N and N (or S and S) repel; N and S attract."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die korrekte definisie van 'n magneetveld?","en":"Which statement is the correct definition of a magnetic field?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force."},{"af":"'n Gebied in die ruimte waar 'n gelaaide voorwerp 'n elektrostatiese krag ondervind.","en":"A region in space where a charged object experiences an electrostatic force."},{"af":"Die krag wat twee magnete op mekaar uitoefen wanneer hulle aan mekaar raak.","en":"The force that two magnets exert on each other when they touch."},{"af":"Die lyne wat van die suidpool na die noordpool om 'n magneet getrek word.","en":"The lines that are drawn from the south pole to the north pole around a magnet."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Magneetveld is 'n gebied in die ruimte waar 'n magneet of ferromagnetiese materiaal 'n (nie-kontak) krag ondervind. Die tweede opsie beskryf 'n elektriese veld; die magnetiese krag werk sonder kontak; en veldlyne wys buite die magneet van N na S.","en":"A magnetic field is a region in space where a magnet or ferromagnetic material experiences a (non-contact) force. The second option describes an electric field; the magnetic force acts without contact; and field lines point from N to S outside the magnet."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Buite 'n staafmagneet wys die magneetveldlyne van die ___ na die suidpool.","en":"Outside a bar magnet the magnetic field lines point from the ___ to the south pole."},"answers":{"af":["noordpool","noord","N","N-pool","N pool","die noordpool","noord-pool"],"en":["north pole","north","N","N pole","N-pole","the north pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Buite die magneet loop die veldlyne van die noordpool na die suidpool (binne die magneet van S na N, sodat hulle geslote lusse vorm).","en":"Outside the magnet the field lines run from the north pole to the south pole (inside the magnet from S to N, so that they form closed loops)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["suidpool","positiewe pool","negatiewe pool"],"en":["south pole","positive pole","negative pole"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sonwind","en":"Solar wind"},"r":{"af":"'n Stroom gelaaide deeltjies wat van die son af uitvloei","en":"A stream of charged particles flowing out from the sun"}},{"l":{"af":"Aurora","en":"Aurora"},"r":{"af":"Gekleurde lig naby die pole wanneer gelaaide deeltjies met gasatome in die boonste atmosfeer bots","en":"Coloured light near the poles when charged particles collide with gas atoms in the upper atmosphere"}},{"l":{"af":"Magnetiese domein","en":"Magnetic domain"},"r":{"af":"'n Klein gebied in 'n ferromagnetiese materiaal waar die atoommagnetjies in dieselfde rigting wys","en":"A small region in a ferromagnetic material where the atomic magnets point in the same direction"}},{"l":{"af":"Kompas","en":"Compass"},"r":{"af":"'n Klein magneet wat vrylik kan draai en in die rigting van die magneetveld wys","en":"A small magnet that can turn freely and points in the direction of the magnetic field"}},{"l":{"af":"Ferromagnetiese materiaal","en":"Ferromagnetic material"},"r":{"af":"'n Stof soos yster wat sterk aangetrek word en gemagnetiseer kan word","en":"A substance such as iron that is strongly attracted and can be magnetised"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die sonwind bestaan uit gelaaide deeltjies van die son; dié wat na die pole gelei word, veroorsaak aurora's. Domeine is groepies opgelynde atoommagnetjies in ferromagnetiese stowwe soos yster. 'n Kompas is 'n vrydraaiende magneetjie.","en":"The solar wind consists of charged particles from the sun; those guided to the poles cause auroras. Domains are groups of lined-up atomic magnets in ferromagnetic substances such as iron. A compass is a freely turning small magnet."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe beskerm die magnetosfeer lewe op aarde?","en":"How does the magnetosphere protect life on Earth?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit absorbeer die meeste van die son se UV-straling.","en":"It absorbs most of the sun's UV radiation."},{"af":"Dit hou die aarde warm deur hitte vas te vang.","en":"It keeps Earth warm by trapping heat."},{"af":"Dit trek meteoriete weg van die aarde af.","en":"It pulls meteorites away from Earth."},{"af":"Dit buig die meeste van die gelaaide deeltjies van die sonwind om die aarde.","en":"It deflects most of the charged particles of the solar wind around Earth."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die aarde se magneetveld buig die gelaaide deeltjies van die sonwind af, sodat die meeste nie die oppervlak bereik nie. Die osoonlaag (nie die magnetosfeer nie) absorbeer UV, en hitte word deur kweekhuisgasse vasgevang.","en":"Earth's magnetic field deflects the charged particles of the solar wind, so most of them do not reach the surface. The ozone layer (not the magnetosphere) absorbs UV, and heat is trapped by greenhouse gases."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar magneetveldlyne ver uitmekaar is, is die magneetveld die sterkste.","en":"Where magnetic field lines are far apart, the magnetic field is strongest."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hoe digter die veldlyne, hoe sterker die veld. Die veld is die sterkste by die pole, waar die lyne die digste is.","en":"False. The denser the field lines, the stronger the field. The field is strongest at the poles, where the lines are densest."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter breek 'n staafmagneet presies in die middel in twee stukke. Wat is waar van die twee stukke?","en":"Pieter breaks a bar magnet exactly in the middle into two pieces. What is true of the two pieces?"},"options":[{"af":"Een stuk het net 'n noordpool en die ander stuk net 'n suidpool.","en":"One piece has only a north pole and the other piece only a south pole."},{"af":"Elke stuk is 'n kleiner magneet met sy eie noordpool en suidpool.","en":"Each piece is a smaller magnet with its own north pole and south pole."},{"af":"Albei stukke verloor hul magnetisme omdat die pole geskei is.","en":"Both pieces lose their magnetism because the poles have been separated."},{"af":"Elke stuk het twee noordpole.","en":"Each piece has two north poles."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pole kom altyd in pare voor. Die domeine in elke stuk wys steeds in dieselfde rigting, dus vorm elke stuk 'n nuwe, kleiner magneet met 'n N- en 'n S-pool.","en":"Poles always occur in pairs. The domains in each piece still point in the same direction, so each piece forms a new, smaller magnet with an N and an S pole."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Staafmagneet lê op 'n tafel met sy N-pool na die ooste en sy S-pool na die weste. 'n Klein kompas word langs die middel van die magneet neergesit. Ignoreer die aarde se magneetveld. Die N-pool van die kompasnaald wys na die ___.","en":"A bar magnet lies on a table with its N pole to the east and its S pole to the west. A small compass is placed next to the middle of the magnet. Ignore Earth's magnetic field. The N pole of the compass needle points to the ___."},"answers":{"af":["weste","wes","die weste","W"],"en":["west","W","the west"]},"explain":{"af":"Buite die magneet loop die veldlyne van N na S. Langs die middel van die magneet loop hulle ewewydig aan die magneet, van die N-kant (ooste) na die S-kant (weste). Die kompas se N-pool wys in die rigting van die veld: na die weste.","en":"Outside the magnet the field lines run from N to S. Next to the middle of the magnet they run parallel to the magnet, from the N end (east) to the S end (west). The compass's N pole points in the direction of the field: to the west."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ooste","noorde","suide"],"en":["east","north","south"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die S-pool van magneet A word naby kant X van magneet B gebring, en die twee stoot mekaar af. Watter pool is kant X? ___","en":"The S pole of magnet A is brought near end X of magnet B, and the two repel each other. Which pole is end X? ___"},"answers":{"af":["suidpool","suid","S","S-pool","S pool","'n suidpool","die suidpool"],"en":["south pole","south","S","S pole","S-pole","a south pole","the south pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Afstoting gebeur net tussen gelyke pole. Kant X stoot 'n S-pool af, dus is X ook 'n suidpool.","en":"Repulsion happens only between like poles. End X repels an S pole, so X is also a south pole."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["noordpool","positiewe pool","negatiewe pool"],"en":["north pole","positive pole","negative pole"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika kry 'n onbekende metaalstaaf. Watter waarneming bewys dat die staaf 'n magneet is?","en":"Anika finds an unknown metal bar. Which observation proves that the bar is a magnet?"},"options":[{"af":"Een kant van die staaf trek die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald aan.","en":"One end of the bar attracts the N pole of a compass needle."},{"af":"Die staaf gelei elektrisiteit.","en":"The bar conducts electricity."},{"af":"Die staaf word deur 'n sterk magneet aangetrek.","en":"The bar is attracted by a strong magnet."},{"af":"Een kant van die staaf stoot die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald af.","en":"One end of the bar repels the N pole of a compass needle."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Aantrekking bewys niks, want 'n magneet trek ook gewone, ongemagnetiseerde yster aan. Afstoting gebeur net tussen gelyke pole van twee magnete, dus bewys dit dat die staaf 'n magneet is. Elektriese geleiding sê niks oor magnetisme nie.","en":"Attraction proves nothing, because a magnet also attracts ordinary, unmagnetised iron. Repulsion happens only between like poles of two magnets, so it proves that the bar is a magnet. Electrical conduction says nothing about magnetism."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese staafmagnete lê in een lyn met hul N-pole 10 cm van mekaar af. Wat is waar by die punt presies in die middel tussen die twee N-pole?","en":"Two identical bar magnets lie in a line with their N poles 10 cm apart. What is true at the point exactly in the middle between the two N poles?"},"options":[{"af":"Die twee magneetvelde kanselleer mekaar uit, dus is die magneetveld daar nul ('n neutrale punt).","en":"The two magnetic fields cancel each other, so the magnetic field there is zero (a neutral point)."},{"af":"Die magneetveld is daar die sterkste, want twee pole wys na mekaar.","en":"The magnetic field is strongest there, because two poles face each other."},{"af":"Die veldlyne loop daar reguit van die een N-pool na die ander N-pool.","en":"The field lines there run straight from one N pole to the other N pole."},{"af":"Die magneetveld wys daar na die linkerkantste magneet toe.","en":"The magnetic field there points towards the magnet on the left."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By die middelpunt wys die veld van die linkermagneet se N-pool na regs (weg van die N-pool) en dié van die regtermagneet na links. Die magnete is identies en die punt is ewe ver, dus is die velde ewe sterk en teenoorgesteld: hulle kanselleer uit. Veldlyne loop nooit van N na N nie.","en":"At the midpoint the field of the left magnet's N pole points to the right (away from the N pole) and that of the right magnet to the left. The magnets are identical and the point is equally far, so the fields are equally strong and opposite: they cancel. Field lines never run from N to N."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die N-pool van 'n kompasnaald wys na die aarde se geografiese Noordpool. As jy die aarde as 'n reuse-staafmagneet beskou, watter pool van daardie staafmagneet lê naby die geografiese Noordpool? ___","en":"The N pole of a compass needle points to Earth's geographic North Pole. If you think of Earth as a giant bar magnet, which pole of that bar magnet lies near the geographic North Pole? ___"},"answers":{"af":["suidpool","suid","S","S-pool","S pool","'n suidpool","die suidpool"],"en":["south pole","south","S","S pole","S-pole","a south pole","the south pole"]},"explain":{"af":"Ongelyke pole trek mekaar aan. Die kompas se N-pool word na die noorde getrek, dus moet daar 'n magnetiese SUIDpool naby die geografiese Noordpool wees. Ons noem die plek 'magnetiese noordpool' omdat dit in die noorde lê, maar magneties gedra dit soos 'n suidpool.","en":"Unlike poles attract each other. The compass's N pole is pulled to the north, so there must be a magnetic SOUTH pole near the geographic North Pole. We call the place 'magnetic north pole' because it lies in the north, but magnetically it behaves like a south pole."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["noordpool","negatiewe pool","positiewe pool"],"en":["north pole","negative pole","positive pole"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato stap in die Magaliesberg en wil met haar kaart presies na ware (geografiese) noord stap. Sy sê: “Ek volg net my kompasnaald; dit wys presies na die geografiese Noordpool.” Watter stelling evalueer haar plan die beste?","en":"Lerato is hiking in the Magaliesberg and wants to walk exactly to true (geographic) north with her map. She says: “I'll just follow my compass needle; it points exactly to the geographic North Pole.” Which statement evaluates her plan best?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy is reg, want die magnetiese noordpool en die geografiese Noordpool is presies dieselfde punt.","en":"She is right, because the magnetic north pole and the geographic North Pole are exactly the same point."},{"af":"Sy is nie heeltemal reg nie: die kompas wys na magnetiese noord, wat nie op dieselfde plek as geografiese noord lê nie, dus moet sy vir die hoek tussen hulle (die deklinasie) regstel.","en":"She is not completely right: the compass points to magnetic north, which is not at the same place as geographic north, so she must correct for the angle between them (the declination)."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd, want in die suidelike halfrond wys 'n kompasnaald se N-pool suid.","en":"She is wrong, because in the southern hemisphere the N pole of a compass needle points south."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd, want 'n kompas wys altyd na die son.","en":"She is wrong, because a compass always points to the sun."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Kompas wys oral op aarde (ook in Suid-Afrika) na magnetiese noord. Die magnetiese noordpool lê egter nie op die geografiese Noordpool nie en beweeg stadig, dus verskil die rigtings met die deklinasiehoek. In Suid-Afrika wys die kompas etlike grade wes van ware noord.","en":"A compass points to magnetic north everywhere on Earth (also in South Africa). However, the magnetic north pole does not lie at the geographic North Pole and moves slowly, so the directions differ by the declination angle. In South Africa the compass points several degrees west of true north."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-elektrostatika","title":{"af":"Elektrostatika","en":"Electrostatics"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe voorwerpe gelaai word, die beginsels van behoud en kwantisering van lading toepas, en ladingsdeling en elektronoordrag tussen sfere bereken.","en":"You will be able to explain how objects become charged, apply the principles of conservation and quantisation of charge, and calculate charge sharing and electron transfer between spheres."},"summary":{"af":"## Twee soorte lading\n\nAlle materie bestaan uit atome met positiewe **protone** (in die kern) en negatiewe **elektrone** (om die kern). 'n **Neutrale** voorwerp het ewe veel protone en elektrone, dus is sy netto lading nul. Daar is **twee soorte lading: positief en negatief**.\n\n- 'n Voorwerp word **negatief** gelaai as dit **elektrone bykry**.\n- 'n Voorwerp word **positief** gelaai as dit **elektrone verloor**.\n- In vaste stowwe beweeg **slegs elektrone**; protone sit vas in die kern.\n- **Gelyke ladings stoot mekaar af; ongelyke ladings trek mekaar aan.** Die elektrostatiese krag is 'n nie-kontakkrag en word sterker hoe nader die ladings aan mekaar is.\n- Lading (Q) word in **coulomb (C)** gemeet. Die lading op een elektron is q_{e} = −1,6 × 10^{−19} C (data-blad). Voorvoegsels: 1 μC = 10^{−6} C; 1 nC = 10^{−9} C; 1 pC = 10^{−12} C.\n\n## Laai deur wrywing\n\nAs twee verskillende isolators teen mekaar gevryf word, word elektrone van die een na die ander oorgedra. Die een wat elektrone bykry, word negatief; die ander een word **ewe veel** positief.\n\n| Wat word gevryf? | Voorwerp word | Lap/materiaal word |\n|---|---|---|\n| glasstaaf met sy | positief (verloor elektrone) | negatief |\n| eboniet- of plastiekstaaf met pels of wol | negatief (kry elektrone by) | positief |\n| ballon teen jou hare | negatief | hare positief |\n\nAlledaags: jy kry 'n skok as jy ná 'n rit in 'n taxi aan die metaaldeur raak (jou klere het teen die sitplek gevryf), en weerlig tydens 'n Hoëveldse donderstorm is 'n reuse-ontlading tussen gelaaide wolke en die grond. As 'n gelaaide voorwerp met die grond verbind word (**aarding**), vloei elektrone na of van die aarde totdat die voorwerp neutraal is.\n\n## Behoud van lading\n\n> **Definisie (beginsel van behoud van lading):** Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses.\n\nLading word nie geskep of vernietig nie, net **oorgedra**. Kry 'n ebonietstaaf −5 nC, dan kry die pels presies +5 nC: die totaal bly 0.\n\n## Kwantisering van lading\n\n> **Definisie (beginsel van kwantisering van lading):** Alle ladings in die heelal bestaan uit 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron, d.w.s. Q = nq_{e}.\n\n- n is die aantal elektrone wat bygekry of verloor is: altyd 'n **heelgetal**. Bereken dit met n = Q ÷ q_{e}.\n- 'n Negatiewe voorwerp het n **oortollige** elektrone; 'n positiewe voorwerp kort n elektrone.\n- 'n Lading van 2,4 × 10^{−19} C is **onmoontlik**: dit sou 1,5 elektrone beteken.\n\n## Identiese sfere wat aan mekaar raak\n\nAs twee **identiese, geleidende** sfere aan mekaar raak, vloei elektrone totdat die lading **eweredig gedeel** is. Ná skeiding het elkeen:\n\n**Q_{nuut} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]]**\n\n### Stappe\n1. Tel die ladings **met hul tekens** bymekaar en deel deur 2.\n2. Bereken die verandering in lading van een sfeer: ΔQ = Q_{nuut} − Q_{begin}.\n3. Skakel om na coulomb (μC → × 10^{−6}; nC → × 10^{−9}).\n4. Aantal elektrone oorgedra: n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}).\n5. Rigting: elektrone vloei **na** die sfeer wat negatiewer word (ΔQ negatief) en **weg van** die sfeer wat positiewer word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om die tekens te ignoreer. +6 μC en −2 μC gee [[6 + (−2)/2]] = +2 μC, nie [[6 + 2/2]] = +4 μC nie. Moenie ook vergeet om μC of nC na C om te skakel voordat jy n bereken nie.\n\n## Polarisasie: waarom 'n gelaaide voorwerp 'n neutrale voorwerp aantrek\n\nBring 'n negatief gelaaide staaf naby (sonder om te raak) 'n neutrale voorwerp:\n\n- **Geleier** (bv. aluminiumfoelie): die vrye elektrone word na die verste kant afgestoot. Die naaste kant word positief en die verste kant negatief: die lading word **geskei**.\n- **Isolator** (bv. papier of 'n muur): die elektrone kan nie deur die stof beweeg nie, maar die elektronwolk van elke molekuul skuif effens weg. Die molekules word **gepolariseer**: hul naaste kant is effens positief.\n\nDie teenoorgestelde lading is **nader** aan die staaf as die gelyke lading, dus is die aantrekking sterker as die afstoting: die neutrale voorwerp word **aangetrek**. Sy netto lading bly nul. Voorbeelde: 'n gelaaide kam tel papiersnippers op; 'n ballon wat teen jou hare gevryf is, kleef teen die muur; 'n gelaaide staaf buig 'n dun straaltjie water uit 'n kraan.\n\n> **Onthou!** Aantrekking bewys nie dat 'n voorwerp gelaai is nie, want dit kan neutraal wees. Net **afstoting** bewys dat albei voorwerpe gelaai is (met dieselfde soort lading).","en":"## Two kinds of charge\n\nAll matter consists of atoms with positive **protons** (in the nucleus) and negative **electrons** (around the nucleus). A **neutral** object has equal numbers of protons and electrons, so its net charge is zero. There are **two kinds of charge: positive and negative**.\n\n- An object becomes **negatively** charged when it **gains electrons**.\n- An object becomes **positively** charged when it **loses electrons**.\n- In solids **only electrons** move; protons are fixed in the nucleus.\n- **Like charges repel; unlike charges attract.** The electrostatic force is a non-contact force and becomes stronger the closer the charges are to each other.\n- Charge (Q) is measured in **coulombs (C)**. The charge on one electron is q_{e} = −1.6 × 10^{−19} C (data sheet). Prefixes: 1 μC = 10^{−6} C; 1 nC = 10^{−9} C; 1 pC = 10^{−12} C.\n\n## Charging by friction\n\nWhen two different insulators are rubbed together, electrons are transferred from one to the other. The one that gains electrons becomes negative; the other one becomes **equally** positive.\n\n| What is rubbed? | Object becomes | Cloth/material becomes |\n|---|---|---|\n| glass rod with silk | positive (loses electrons) | negative |\n| ebonite or plastic rod with fur or wool | negative (gains electrons) | positive |\n| balloon against your hair | negative | hair positive |\n\nEveryday: you get a shock when you touch the metal door after a ride in a taxi (your clothes rubbed against the seat), and lightning during a Highveld thunderstorm is a huge discharge between charged clouds and the ground. When a charged object is connected to the ground (**earthing**), electrons flow to or from the earth until the object is neutral.\n\n## Conservation of charge\n\n> **Definition (principle of conservation of charge):** The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process.\n\nCharge is not created or destroyed, only **transferred**. If an ebonite rod gets −5 nC, the fur gets exactly +5 nC: the total stays 0.\n\n## Quantisation of charge\n\n> **Definition (principle of charge quantisation):** All charges in the universe consist of an integer multiple of the charge on one electron, i.e. Q = nq_{e}.\n\n- n is the number of electrons gained or lost: always an **integer**. Calculate it with n = Q ÷ q_{e}.\n- A negative object has n **excess** electrons; a positive object is short of n electrons.\n- A charge of 2.4 × 10^{−19} C is **impossible**: it would mean 1.5 electrons.\n\n## Identical spheres that touch\n\nWhen two **identical, conducting** spheres touch, electrons flow until the charge is **shared equally**. After separation each has:\n\n**Q_{new} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]]**\n\n### Steps\n1. Add the charges **with their signs** and divide by 2.\n2. Calculate the change in charge of one sphere: ΔQ = Q_{new} − Q_{initial}.\n3. Convert to coulombs (μC → × 10^{−6}; nC → × 10^{−9}).\n4. Number of electrons transferred: n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}).\n5. Direction: electrons flow **to** the sphere that becomes more negative (ΔQ negative) and **away from** the sphere that becomes more positive.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Ignoring the signs. +6 μC and −2 μC give [[6 + (−2)/2]] = +2 μC, not [[6 + 2/2]] = +4 μC. Also do not forget to convert μC or nC to C before you calculate n.\n\n## Polarisation: why a charged object attracts a neutral object\n\nBring a negatively charged rod near (without touching) a neutral object:\n\n- **Conductor** (e.g. aluminium foil): the free electrons are repelled to the far side. The near side becomes positive and the far side negative: the charge is **separated**.\n- **Insulator** (e.g. paper or a wall): the electrons cannot move through the substance, but the electron cloud of each molecule shifts slightly away. The molecules become **polarised**: their near side is slightly positive.\n\nThe opposite charge is **closer** to the rod than the like charge, so the attraction is stronger than the repulsion: the neutral object is **attracted**. Its net charge stays zero. Examples: a charged comb picks up bits of paper; a balloon rubbed against your hair sticks to the wall; a charged rod bends a thin stream of water from a tap.\n\n> **Remember!** Attraction does not prove that an object is charged, because it may be neutral. Only **repulsion** proves that both objects are charged (with the same kind of charge)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Elektriese lading (Q)","en":"Electric charge (Q)"},"def":{"af":"'n Eienskap van deeltjies soos protone (positief) en elektrone (negatief); gelyke ladings stoot af en ongelyke ladings trek aan. Eenheid: coulomb (C).","en":"A property of particles such as protons (positive) and electrons (negative); like charges repel and unlike charges attract. Unit: coulomb (C)."}},{"term":{"af":"Lading op 'n elektron (qₑ)","en":"Charge on an electron (qₑ)"},"def":{"af":"Die kleinste vrye lading: qₑ = −1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.","en":"The smallest free charge: qₑ = −1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C."}},{"term":{"af":"Neutrale voorwerp","en":"Neutral object"},"def":{"af":"'n Voorwerp met ewe veel protone en elektrone, sodat sy netto lading nul is.","en":"An object with equal numbers of protons and electrons, so that its net charge is zero."}},{"term":{"af":"Laai deur wrywing","en":"Charging by friction"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer twee verskillende materiale teen mekaar gevryf word en elektrone van die een na die ander oorgedra word; die een word negatief en die ander ewe veel positief.","en":"When two different materials are rubbed together and electrons are transferred from one to the other; one becomes negative and the other equally positive."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsel van behoud van lading","en":"Principle of conservation of charge"},"def":{"af":"Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses.","en":"The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsel van kwantisering van lading","en":"Principle of charge quantisation"},"def":{"af":"Alle ladings in die heelal bestaan uit 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron, d.w.s. Q = nqₑ.","en":"All charges in the universe consist of an integer multiple of the charge on one electron, i.e. Q = nqₑ."}},{"term":{"af":"Polarisasie","en":"Polarisation"},"def":{"af":"Die skeiding of herrangskikking van lading binne 'n neutrale voorwerp (of molekuul) as gevolg van 'n gelaaide voorwerp naby.","en":"The separation or rearrangement of charge within a neutral object (or molecule) due to a nearby charged object."}},{"term":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone vrylik kan beweeg, bv. koper en aluminium.","en":"A material in which electrons can move freely, e.g. copper and aluminium."}},{"term":{"af":"Isolator","en":"Insulator"},"def":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone nie vrylik kan beweeg nie, bv. plastiek, glas en rubber.","en":"A material in which electrons cannot move freely, e.g. plastic, glass and rubber."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ballon teen jou hare","en":"Balloon against your hair"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho vryf 'n ballon teen sy hare. Die ballon kry 'n lading van −4,8 nC. (a) Watter deeltjies is oorgedra, en in watter rigting? (b) Wat is die lading op sy hare? (c) Hoeveel elektrone is oorgedra?","en":"Sipho rubs a balloon against his hair. The balloon gets a charge of −4.8 nC. (a) Which particles were transferred, and in which direction? (b) What is the charge on his hair? (c) How many electrons were transferred?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die ballon is negatief, dus het dit elektrone bygekry. Elektrone is van die hare na die ballon oorgedra; protone beweeg nie.","en":"(a) The balloon is negative, so it gained electrons. Electrons were transferred from the hair to the balloon; protons do not move."},{"af":"(b) Behoud van lading: voor die vryf was die totale lading 0. Ná die vryf: Q_{ballon} + Q_{hare} = 0, dus Q_{hare} = +4,8 nC.","en":"(b) Conservation of charge: before rubbing the total charge was 0. After rubbing: Q_{balloon} + Q_{hair} = 0, so Q_{hair} = +4.8 nC."},{"af":"(c) Q = nq_{e}, dus n = Q ÷ q_{e} = (−4,8 × 10^{−9}) ÷ (−1,6 × 10^{−19})","en":"(c) Q = nq_{e}, so n = Q ÷ q_{e} = (−4.8 × 10^{−9}) ÷ (−1.6 × 10^{−19})"},{"af":"n = 3 × 10^{10} elektrone","en":"n = 3 × 10^{10} electrons"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Elektrone, van die hare na die ballon. (b) +4,8 nC (c) 3 × 10¹⁰ elektrone","en":"(a) Electrons, from the hair to the balloon. (b) +4.8 nC (c) 3 × 10¹⁰ electrons"}},{"title":{"af":"Twee identiese sfere raak aan mekaar","en":"Two identical spheres touch"},"problem":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere op geïsoleerde staanders dra ladings van Q_A = −3 μC en Q_B = +9 μC. Hulle raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Bereken (a) die nuwe lading op elke sfeer en (b) die aantal elektrone wat oorgedra is, en sê in watter rigting.","en":"Two identical metal spheres on insulated stands carry charges of Q_A = −3 μC and Q_B = +9 μC. They touch and are then separated. Calculate (a) the new charge on each sphere and (b) the number of electrons transferred, and state in which direction."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Q_{nuut} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]] = [[(−3) + 9/2]] = +3 μC op elke sfeer.","en":"(a) Q_{new} = [[Q₁ + Q₂/2]] = [[(−3) + 9/2]] = +3 μC on each sphere."},{"af":"(b) Vir sfeer A: ΔQ = Q_{nuut} − Q_{begin} = +3 − (−3) = +6 μC = 6 × 10^{−6} C. A word positiewer, dus het A elektrone verloor.","en":"(b) For sphere A: ΔQ = Q_{new} − Q_{initial} = +3 − (−3) = +6 μC = 6 × 10^{−6} C. A becomes more positive, so A lost electrons."},{"af":"n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = (6 × 10^{−6}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 3,75 × 10^{13} elektrone","en":"n = |ΔQ| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = (6 × 10^{−6}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 3.75 × 10^{13} electrons"},{"af":"Die elektrone het van A na B beweeg. Kontrole: vir B is ΔQ = +3 − 9 = −6 μC, dus het B presies soveel elektrone bygekry ✔ (behoud van lading).","en":"The electrons moved from A to B. Check: for B, ΔQ = +3 − 9 = −6 μC, so B gained exactly as many electrons ✔ (conservation of charge)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) +3 μC elk  (b) 3,75 × 10¹³ elektrone, van A na B","en":"(a) +3 μC each  (b) 3.75 × 10¹³ electrons, from A to B"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom 'n kam papier optel","en":"Why a comb picks up paper"},"problem":{"af":"Anika trek 'n plastiekkam deur haar droë hare en hou dit naby klein stukkies papier. Die papier spring na die kam, al is die papier neutraal. Verduidelik.","en":"Anika pulls a plastic comb through her dry hair and holds it near small bits of paper. The paper jumps to the comb, even though the paper is neutral. Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"Die kam word deur wrywing gelaai: dit kry elektrone van die hare by en word negatief.","en":"The comb is charged by friction: it gains electrons from the hair and becomes negative."},{"af":"Papier is 'n isolator, dus kan elektrone nie deur die papier beweeg nie. In elke molekuul word die elektronwolk egter effens weg van die kam gestoot: die molekules word gepolariseer. Die kant van die papier naaste aan die kam word effens positief en die verste kant effens negatief.","en":"Paper is an insulator, so electrons cannot move through the paper. In each molecule, however, the electron cloud is pushed slightly away from the comb: the molecules become polarised. The side of the paper nearest the comb becomes slightly positive and the far side slightly negative."},{"af":"Die positiewe kant is nader aan die kam as die negatiewe kant. Die elektrostatiese krag is sterker hoe nader die ladings is, dus is die aantrekking groter as die afstoting.","en":"The positive side is closer to the comb than the negative side. The electrostatic force is stronger the closer the charges are, so the attraction is greater than the repulsion."},{"af":"Die netto krag is aantrekking en die ligte papier spring na die kam. Die papier se netto lading bly nul.","en":"The net force is attraction and the light paper jumps to the comb. The paper's net charge stays zero."}],"answer":{"af":"Die gelaaide kam polariseer die papier; die nabye teenoorgestelde lading word sterker aangetrek as wat die verder gelyke lading afgestoot word, dus word die neutrale papier aangetrek.","en":"The charged comb polarises the paper; the nearby opposite charge is attracted more strongly than the more distant like charge is repelled, so the neutral paper is attracted."}},{"title":{"af":"Is die lading moontlik?","en":"Is the charge possible?"},"problem":{"af":"Watter van die volgende ladings is moontlik? Gee 'n rede. (a) +4,8 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (b) −6,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (c) +2,0 × 10⁻¹⁹ C","en":"Which of the following charges are possible? Give a reason. (a) +4.8 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (b) −6.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C  (c) +2.0 × 10⁻¹⁹ C"},"steps":[{"af":"Volgens die beginsel van kwantisering van lading is Q = nq_{e}, dus moet n = |Q| ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) 'n heelgetal wees.","en":"According to the principle of charge quantisation Q = nq_{e}, so n = |Q| ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) must be an integer."},{"af":"(a) n = (4,8 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 3: moontlik (die voorwerp het 3 elektrone verloor).","en":"(a) n = (4.8 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 3: possible (the object lost 3 electrons)."},{"af":"(b) n = (6,4 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 4: moontlik (4 oortollige elektrone).","en":"(b) n = (6.4 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 4: possible (4 excess electrons)."},{"af":"(c) n = (2,0 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19}) = 1,25: nie 'n heelgetal nie, dus onmoontlik. 'n Voorwerp kan nie 'n deel van 'n elektron bykry of verloor nie.","en":"(c) n = (2.0 × 10^{−19}) ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19}) = 1.25: not an integer, so impossible. An object cannot gain or lose part of an electron."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) en (b) is moontlik (n = 3 en n = 4); (c) is onmoontlik (n = 1,25 is nie 'n heelgetal nie).","en":"(a) and (b) are possible (n = 3 and n = 4); (c) is impossible (n = 1.25 is not an integer)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid van elektriese lading?","en":"What is the SI unit of electric charge?"},"options":[{"af":"Ampère (A)","en":"Ampere (A)"},{"af":"Volt (V)","en":"Volt (V)"},{"af":"Coulomb (C)","en":"Coulomb (C)"},{"af":"Newton (N)","en":"Newton (N)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Lading word in coulomb (C) gemeet. Die ampère is die eenheid van stroom, die volt van potensiaalverskil en die newton van krag.","en":"Charge is measured in coulombs (C). The ampere is the unit of current, the volt of potential difference and the newton of force."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deeltjies word oorgedra wanneer twee voorwerpe deur wrywing gelaai word?","en":"Which particles are transferred when two objects are charged by friction?"},"options":[{"af":"Elektrone","en":"Electrons"},{"af":"Protone","en":"Protons"},{"af":"Neutrone","en":"Neutrons"},{"af":"Atoomkerne","en":"Atomic nuclei"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Slegs elektrone kan van een voorwerp na 'n ander beweeg. Protone en neutrone sit vas in die kern van die atoom.","en":"Only electrons can move from one object to another. Protons and neutrons are fixed in the nucleus of the atom."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp word positief gelaai wanneer dit protone bykry.","en":"An object becomes positively charged when it gains protons."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Protone beweeg nie; 'n voorwerp word positief gelaai wanneer dit elektrone verloor, sodat daar meer protone as elektrone oorbly.","en":"False. Protons do not move; an object becomes positively charged when it loses electrons, so that more protons than electrons remain."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each concept to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Behoud van lading","en":"Conservation of charge"},"r":{"af":"Die netto lading van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant gedurende enige fisiese proses","en":"The net charge of an isolated system remains constant during any physical process"}},{"l":{"af":"Kwantisering van lading","en":"Charge quantisation"},"r":{"af":"Alle ladings is 'n heelgetalveelvoud van die lading op een elektron","en":"All charges are an integer multiple of the charge on one electron"}},{"l":{"af":"Polarisasie","en":"Polarisation"},"r":{"af":"Die skeiding van lading in 'n neutrale voorwerp weens 'n gelaaide voorwerp naby","en":"The separation of charge in a neutral object due to a nearby charged object"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleier","en":"Conductor"},"r":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone vrylik kan beweeg, bv. koper","en":"A material in which electrons can move freely, e.g. copper"}},{"l":{"af":"Isolator","en":"Insulator"},"r":{"af":"'n Materiaal waarin elektrone nie vrylik kan beweeg nie, bv. plastiek","en":"A material in which electrons cannot move freely, e.g. plastic"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die twee beginsels woordeliks: behoud (die totaal bly dieselfde) en kwantisering (Q = nqₑ met n 'n heelgetal). Polarisasie verklaar waarom gelaaide voorwerpe neutrale voorwerpe aantrek.","en":"Learn the two principles word for word: conservation (the total stays the same) and quantisation (Q = nqₑ with n an integer). Polarisation explains why charged objects attract neutral objects."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Ebonietstaaf word met 'n stuk pels gevryf en kry 'n lading van −5 nC. Wat is die lading op die pels daarna? (Geen lading gaan na die omgewing verlore nie.)","en":"An ebonite rod is rubbed with a piece of fur and gets a charge of −5 nC. What is the charge on the fur afterwards? (No charge is lost to the surroundings.)"},"options":[{"af":"0 nC (die pels bly neutraal)","en":"0 nC (the fur stays neutral)"},{"af":"+5 nC","en":"+5 nC"},{"af":"−5 nC","en":"−5 nC"},{"af":"+10 nC","en":"+10 nC"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Behoud van lading: voor die vryf was die totale lading 0, dus moet dit daarna ook 0 wees: −5 nC + Q_pels = 0, dus Q_pels = +5 nC. Die elektrone wat die staaf bygekry het, het van die pels af gekom.","en":"Conservation of charge: before rubbing the total charge was 0, so afterwards it must also be 0: −5 nC + Q_fur = 0, so Q_fur = +5 nC. The electrons the rod gained came from the fur."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Gelaaide ballon kan 'n neutrale muur aantrek.","en":"A charged balloon can attract a neutral wall."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die ballon polariseer die molekules in die muur: die kant naaste aan die ballon kry 'n effense teenoorgestelde lading, en omdat dit nader is, is die aantrekking sterker as die afstoting.","en":"True. The balloon polarises the molecules in the wall: the side nearest the balloon gets a slight opposite charge, and because it is closer, the attraction is stronger than the repulsion."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Negatief gelaaide plastiekstaaf word naby (sonder om te raak) 'n klein, neutrale aluminiumfoeliebal gebring wat aan 'n draad hang. Wat gebeur, en waarom?","en":"A negatively charged plastic rod is brought near (without touching) a small, neutral aluminium-foil ball hanging from a thread. What happens, and why?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bal word afgestoot, want dit word negatief gelaai.","en":"The ball is repelled, because it becomes negatively charged."},{"af":"Niks gebeur nie, want die bal is neutraal.","en":"Nothing happens, because the ball is neutral."},{"af":"Die bal word aangetrek, want protone vloei van die staaf na die bal.","en":"The ball is attracted, because protons flow from the rod to the ball."},{"af":"Die bal word aangetrek: elektrone in die bal word na die verste kant afgestoot, sodat die naaste kant positief is en sterker aangetrek word as wat die verder negatiewe kant afgestoot word.","en":"The ball is attracted: electrons in the ball are repelled to the far side, so the near side is positive and is attracted more strongly than the more distant negative side is repelled."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Aluminium is 'n geleier: die vrye elektrone beweeg weg van die negatiewe staaf. Die lading word geskei (polarisasie), maar die bal bly neutraal. Die nabye positiewe kant word sterker aangetrek as wat die verder negatiewe kant afgestoot word, dus word die bal aangetrek. Protone beweeg nie, en die staaf raak nie die bal nie.","en":"Aluminium is a conductor: the free electrons move away from the negative rod. The charge is separated (polarisation), but the ball stays neutral. The near positive side is attracted more strongly than the more distant negative side is repelled, so the ball is attracted. Protons do not move, and the rod does not touch the ball."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp het 'n lading van −8 × 10⁻¹⁸ C. Hoeveel oortollige elektrone het die voorwerp? ___","en":"An object has a charge of −8 × 10⁻¹⁸ C. How many excess electrons does the object have? ___"},"answers":{"af":["50","50 elektrone","vyftig"],"en":["50","50 electrons","fifty"]},"explain":{"af":"Q = nqₑ, dus n = Q ÷ qₑ = (−8 × 10⁻¹⁸) ÷ (−1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 50 elektrone.","en":"Q = nqₑ, so n = Q ÷ qₑ = (−8 × 10⁻¹⁸) ÷ (−1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 50 electrons."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−50","5","500"],"en":["−50","5","500"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere met ladings van +8 nC en −2 nC raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Wat is die lading op elke sfeer?","en":"Two identical metal spheres with charges of +8 nC and −2 nC touch and are then separated. What is the charge on each sphere?"},"options":[{"af":"+5 nC","en":"+5 nC"},{"af":"+3 nC","en":"+3 nC"},{"af":"+6 nC","en":"+6 nC"},{"af":"−3 nC","en":"−3 nC"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Q_nuut = (Q₁ + Q₂)/2 = (8 + (−2))/2 = +3 nC. +5 nC kry jy as jy die teken van −2 ignoreer, +6 nC as jy vergeet om deur 2 te deel, en −3 nC het die verkeerde teken, want die totale lading (+6 nC) is positief.","en":"Q_new = (Q₁ + Q₂)/2 = (8 + (−2))/2 = +3 nC. You get +5 nC if you ignore the sign of −2, +6 nC if you forget to divide by 2, and −3 nC has the wrong sign, because the total charge (+6 nC) is positive."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Glasstaaf verloor 5 × 10¹⁰ elektrone wanneer dit met sy gevryf word. Wat is die lading op die glasstaaf? Q = ___ × 10⁻⁹ C","en":"A glass rod loses 5 × 10¹⁰ electrons when it is rubbed with silk. What is the charge on the glass rod? Q = ___ × 10⁻⁹ C"},"answers":{"af":["+8","8","+8,00","8,00","+8.00","8.00","+8 × 10⁻⁹","+8 × 10⁻⁹ C","8 × 10⁻⁹ C","+8 nC","8 nC","+8e-9","8e-9"],"en":["+8","8","+8.00","8.00","+8,00","8,00","+8 × 10⁻⁹","+8 × 10⁻⁹ C","8 × 10⁻⁹ C","+8 nC","8 nC","+8e-9","8e-9"]},"explain":{"af":"Die staaf verloor elektrone, dus is sy lading positief. Q = n × 1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = (5 × 10¹⁰)(1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = +8 × 10⁻⁹ C (+8 nC).","en":"The rod loses electrons, so its charge is positive. Q = n × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ = (5 × 10¹⁰)(1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = +8 × 10⁻⁹ C (+8 nC)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−8","+3,125","+0,8"],"en":["−8","+3.125","+0.8"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere, A (−6 nC) en B (+2 nC), raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Hoeveel elektrone is van A na B oorgedra? ___ × 10¹⁰","en":"Two identical metal spheres, A (−6 nC) and B (+2 nC), touch and are then separated. How many electrons were transferred from A to B? ___ × 10¹⁰"},"answers":{"af":["2,5","2.5","2,50","2.50","2,5 × 10¹⁰","2.5 × 10¹⁰","2,5 x 10^10","2.5 x 10^10","2.5e10"],"en":["2.5","2,5","2.50","2,50","2.5 × 10¹⁰","2,5 × 10¹⁰","2.5 x 10^10","2,5 x 10^10","2.5e10"]},"explain":{"af":"Q_nuut = (−6 + 2)/2 = −2 nC. Vir A: ΔQ = −2 − (−6) = +4 nC = 4 × 10⁻⁹ C (A het elektrone verloor). n = (4 × 10⁻⁹) ÷ (1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2,5 × 10¹⁰ elektrone.","en":"Q_new = (−6 + 2)/2 = −2 nC. For A: ΔQ = −2 − (−6) = +4 nC = 4 × 10⁻⁹ C (A lost electrons). n = (4 × 10⁻⁹) ÷ (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.5 × 10¹⁰ electrons."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","1,25","3,75"],"en":["5","1.25","3.75"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Twee identiese metaalsfere, P (+4 μC) en Q (−8 μC), raak aan mekaar en word dan geskei. Watter stelling beskryf die ladingsoordrag korrek?","en":"Two identical metal spheres, P (+4 μC) and Q (−8 μC), touch and are then separated. Which statement describes the charge transfer correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Protone beweeg van P na Q.","en":"Protons move from P to Q."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg van P na Q.","en":"Electrons move from P to Q."},{"af":"Elektrone beweeg van Q na P.","en":"Electrons move from Q to P."},{"af":"Geen lading word oorgedra nie, want die totale lading bly behoue.","en":"No charge is transferred, because the total charge is conserved."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Elkeen kry (4 + (−8))/2 = −2 μC. P verander van +4 μC na −2 μC: dit word negatiewer, dus het P elektrone bygekry, en dié het van Q af gekom. Protone beweeg nie. Behoud van lading beteken die totaal bly −4 μC, nie dat niks beweeg nie.","en":"Each gets (4 + (−8))/2 = −2 μC. P changes from +4 μC to −2 μC: it becomes more negative, so P gained electrons, and they came from Q. Protons do not move. Conservation of charge means the total stays −4 μC, not that nothing moves."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Drie identiese metaalsfere dra ladings van A = +9 nC, B = −3 nC en C = +5 nC. A raak aan B en hulle word geskei. Daarna raak B aan C en hulle word geskei. Wat is die finale lading op C? ___ nC","en":"Three identical metal spheres carry charges of A = +9 nC, B = −3 nC and C = +5 nC. A touches B and they are separated. Then B touches C and they are separated. What is the final charge on C? ___ nC"},"answers":{"af":["+4","+4 nC","4","4 nC","4,00","4,00 nC","4.00","4.00 nC"],"en":["+4","+4 nC","4","4 nC","4,00","4,00 nC","4.00","4.00 nC"]},"explain":{"af":"Stap 1: A en B: (9 + (−3))/2 = +3 nC elk. Stap 2: B (nou +3 nC) en C: (3 + 5)/2 = +4 nC elk. Gebruik altyd B se NUWE lading in die tweede stap.","en":"Step 1: A and B: (9 + (−3))/2 = +3 nC each. Step 2: B (now +3 nC) and C: (3 + 5)/2 = +4 nC each. Always use B's NEW charge in the second step."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["+1","+8","+7"],"en":["+1","+8","+7"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato meet die lading op 'n klein oliedruppel en rapporteer 2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. Watter stelling evalueer haar resultaat die beste?","en":"Lerato measures the charge on a small oil drop and reports 2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C. Which statement evaluates her result best?"},"options":[{"af":"Die resultaat is onmoontlik: (2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹) ÷ (1,6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 1,5, en 'n voorwerp kan nie 'n halwe elektron bykry of verloor nie; die meting moet foutief wees.","en":"The result is impossible: (2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹) ÷ (1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 1.5, and an object cannot gain or lose half an electron; the measurement must be wrong."},{"af":"Die resultaat is moontlik, want lading kan enige waarde hê.","en":"The result is possible, because charge can have any value."},{"af":"Die resultaat is moontlik, want 2,4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C is groter as die lading op een elektron.","en":"The result is possible, because 2.4 × 10⁻¹⁹ C is larger than the charge on one electron."},{"af":"Die resultaat is onmoontlik, want 'n lading moet altyd negatief wees.","en":"The result is impossible, because a charge must always be negative."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Volgens die beginsel van kwantisering van lading is Q = nqₑ met n 'n heelgetal. Hier is n = 1,5, dus kan die lading nie bestaan nie. Lading kan nie enige waarde hê nie, dit kan positief of negatief wees, en om groter as qₑ te wees, is nie genoeg nie: dit moet 'n heelgetalveelvoud wees.","en":"According to the principle of charge quantisation Q = nqₑ with n an integer. Here n = 1.5, so the charge cannot exist. Charge cannot have any value, it can be positive or negative, and being larger than qₑ is not enough: it must be an integer multiple."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-elektriese-stroombane","title":{"af":"Elektriese stroombane","en":"Electric circuits"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal emk, potensiaalverskil, stroom en weerstand kan definieer en die ekwivalente weerstand, strome en spannings in serie-, parallel- en kombinasiestroombane kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to define emf, potential difference, current and resistance, and calculate the equivalent resistance, currents and voltages in series, parallel and combination circuits."},"summary":{"af":"## Potensiaalverskil en emk\n\n- **Potensiaalverskil (V)** is die arbeid verrig (of energie oorgedra) per eenheid positiewe lading wat tussen twee punte beweeg: V = [[W/Q]]. Eenheid: **volt (V)**; 1 V = 1 J·C^{−1}.\n- **Emk (ε)** is die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer **geen stroom** deur die battery vloei nie. Dit is die maksimum energie wat die battery per coulomb lading verskaf.\n- **Terminale potensiaalverskil** is die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van die battery wanneer stroom **wel** vloei. Dit is effens kleiner as die emk, want 'n bietjie energie word binne-in die battery self in hitte omgeskakel.\n\n> **Wenk:** 'n Voltmeter oor die pole van die battery lees die **emk** as die skakelaar **oop** is, en die **terminale potensiaalverskil** as die skakelaar **toe** is.\n\n**Selle in serie:** Die positiewe pool van een sel word aan die negatiewe pool van die volgende gekoppel, en hulle emk'e **tel op**. Drie 1,5 V-selle in 'n flits gee 3 × 1,5 = 4,5 V. Identiese selle in **parallel** gee dieselfde emk as een sel, maar hou langer.\n\n## Stroom\n\n**Stroom (I)** is die tempo van vloei van lading: I = [[Q/Δt]]. Eenheid: **ampère (A)**; 1 A = 1 C·s^{−1}.\n\n- **Konvensionele stroom** vloei in die eksterne stroombaan van die **positiewe** pool na die **negatiewe** pool. Elektrone vloei in die teenoorgestelde rigting.\n- Die aantal elektrone wat verbybeweeg: n = [[Q/e]], met e = 1,6 × 10^{−19} C.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Δt moet in **sekondes** wees: 2 min = 120 s en 1 h = 3 600 s.\n\n## Weerstand\n\n**Weerstand (R)** is die teenstand teen die vloei van elektriese stroom. Dit is die verhouding van die potensiaalverskil oor 'n resistor tot die stroom daardeur: R = [[V/I]]. Eenheid: **ohm (Ω)**; 1 Ω = 1 V·A^{−1}.\n\n**Hoekom is daar weerstand?** Elektrone wat deur 'n metaal beweeg, bots met die metaalatome (positiewe ione) en dra van hulle kinetiese energie aan die atome oor. Daarom word 'n ketel se element warm en gloei 'n gloeilamp se filament.\n\n| Faktor | Effek op die weerstand van 'n metaaldraad |\n|---|---|\n| Langer draad | R neem toe (meer botsings) |\n| Dikker draad (groter deursnee-oppervlakte) | R neem af (meer ruimte vir elektrone) |\n| Hoër temperatuur | R neem toe (atome vibreer meer) |\n| Tipe materiaal | bv. koper het 'n baie laer R as nichroom |\n\n**'n Battery word pap** omdat sy chemiese potensiële energie na elektriese energie omgeskakel word, wat in die resistors na hitte en lig omgeskakel word. As die chemikalieë opgebruik is, kan dit nie meer energie aan die ladings gee nie.\n\n### Ohm se wet\n\n*Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n geleier is direk eweredig aan die stroom in die geleier by konstante temperatuur.* Dus is [[V/I]] = R konstant. 'n Grafiek van V (y-as) teenoor I (x-as) vir 'n ohmiese geleier is 'n reguit lyn deur die oorsprong; die gradiënt is R.\n\n## Meters\n\n- **Ammeter** – meet stroom; word in **serie** gekoppel; het 'n baie **lae** weerstand (ideaal nul), sodat dit die stroom nie verander nie.\n- **Voltmeter** – meet potensiaalverskil; word in **parallel** oor die komponent gekoppel; het 'n baie **hoë** weerstand (ideaal oneindig), sodat feitlik geen stroom daardeur vloei nie.\n\n## Resistors in serie en in parallel\n\n| | Serie (een pad) | Parallel (aparte takke) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stroom | dieselfde deur elke resistor: I_{T} = I_{1} = I_{2} | verdeel: I_{T} = I_{1} + I_{2} + I_{3} |\n| Potensiaalverskil | verdeel: V_{T} = V_{1} + V_{2} + V_{3} | dieselfde oor elke tak: V_{T} = V_{1} = V_{2} |\n| Ekwivalente weerstand | R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} | [[1/Rₚ]] = [[1/R₁]] + [[1/R₂]] + [[1/R₃]] |\n| Bynaam | spanningsverdeler | stroomverdeler |\n\n- In serie kry die **grootste** resistor die **grootste** deel van die potensiaalverskil.\n- In parallel vloei die **grootste** stroom deur die **kleinste** weerstand.\n- Vir **twee** resistors in parallel: R_{p} = [[R₁R₂/R₁ + R₂]] (produk oor som).\n- R_{p} is altyd **kleiner as die kleinste** resistor in die kombinasie. Hoe meer resistors in parallel, hoe kleiner die totale weerstand, want daar is meer paaie vir die stroom – soos 'n dikker draad.\n- Huisbedrading is in parallel: elke toestel kry die volle spanning, en as een lamp uitbrand, werk die res steeds.\n\n## Metode vir 'n kombinasiestroombaan\n\n1. Bereken R_{p} van die parallelle deel.\n2. Totale weerstand: R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p}.\n3. Hoofstroom: I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}.\n4. Potensiaalverskil oor die serie-resistor: V = I_{T} × R. Dan is V_{p} = V_{T} − V_{serie}.\n5. Takstroom: I = V_{p} ÷ R vir elke tak. Kontroleer dat die takstrome optel tot I_{T}.\n\n### Wat gebeur as ...? (battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand)\n\nRedeneer altyd in hierdie volgorde: R_{T} verander → I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} verander → V oor die serie-resistor verander → V oor die parallelle deel verander.\n\n- 'n Resistor word **in parallel bygevoeg** → R_{T} neem af → I_{T} neem toe.\n- 'n Tak word **verwyder** (bv. 'n gloeilamp brand uit) → R_{T} neem toe → I_{T} neem af.\n- 'n Gloeilamp brand helderder as die stroom deur hom (en die potensiaalverskil oor hom) groter is.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** [[1/Rₚ]] nie omkeer na R_{p} nie; parallelle resistors sommer optel; die battery se volle spanning oor een resistor in 'n serie-stroombaan gebruik.","en":"## Potential difference and emf\n\n- **Potential difference (V)** is the work done (or energy transferred) per unit positive charge moving between two points: V = [[W/Q]]. Unit: **volt (V)**; 1 V = 1 J·C^{−1}.\n- **Emf (ε)** is the potential difference across the terminals of a battery when **no current** flows through the battery. It is the maximum energy the battery provides per coulomb of charge.\n- **Terminal potential difference** is the potential difference across the terminals of the battery when current **does** flow. It is slightly less than the emf, because a little energy is converted to heat inside the battery itself.\n\n> **Tip:** A voltmeter across the battery terminals reads the **emf** when the switch is **open**, and the **terminal potential difference** when the switch is **closed**.\n\n**Cells in series:** The positive terminal of one cell is connected to the negative terminal of the next, and their emfs **add up**. Three 1.5 V cells in a torch give 3 × 1.5 = 4.5 V. Identical cells in **parallel** give the same emf as one cell, but last longer.\n\n## Current\n\n**Current (I)** is the rate of flow of charge: I = [[Q/Δt]]. Unit: **ampere (A)**; 1 A = 1 C·s^{−1}.\n\n- **Conventional current** flows in the external circuit from the **positive** terminal to the **negative** terminal. Electrons flow in the opposite direction.\n- The number of electrons passing: n = [[Q/e]], with e = 1.6 × 10^{−19} C.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Δt must be in **seconds**: 2 min = 120 s and 1 h = 3 600 s.\n\n## Resistance\n\n**Resistance (R)** is the opposition to the flow of electric current. It is the ratio of the potential difference across a resistor to the current through it: R = [[V/I]]. Unit: **ohm (Ω)**; 1 Ω = 1 V·A^{−1}.\n\n**Why is there resistance?** Electrons moving through a metal collide with the metal atoms (positive ions) and transfer some of their kinetic energy to the atoms. That is why a kettle's element gets hot and a light bulb's filament glows.\n\n| Factor | Effect on the resistance of a metal wire |\n|---|---|\n| Longer wire | R increases (more collisions) |\n| Thicker wire (larger cross-sectional area) | R decreases (more room for electrons) |\n| Higher temperature | R increases (atoms vibrate more) |\n| Type of material | e.g. copper has a much lower R than nichrome |\n\n**A battery goes flat** because its chemical potential energy is converted to electrical energy, which is converted to heat and light in the resistors. When the chemicals are used up, it can no longer give energy to the charges.\n\n### Ohm's law\n\n*The potential difference across a conductor is directly proportional to the current in the conductor at constant temperature.* So [[V/I]] = R is constant. A graph of V (y-axis) against I (x-axis) for an ohmic conductor is a straight line through the origin; the gradient is R.\n\n## Meters\n\n- **Ammeter** – measures current; connected in **series**; has a very **low** resistance (ideally zero) so that it does not change the current.\n- **Voltmeter** – measures potential difference; connected in **parallel** across the component; has a very **high** resistance (ideally infinite) so that almost no current flows through it.\n\n## Resistors in series and in parallel\n\n| | Series (one path) | Parallel (separate branches) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Current | the same through each resistor: I_{T} = I_{1} = I_{2} | divides: I_{T} = I_{1} + I_{2} + I_{3} |\n| Potential difference | divides: V_{T} = V_{1} + V_{2} + V_{3} | the same across each branch: V_{T} = V_{1} = V_{2} |\n| Equivalent resistance | R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} | [[1/Rₚ]] = [[1/R₁]] + [[1/R₂]] + [[1/R₃]] |\n| Also called | voltage divider | current divider |\n\n- In series the **largest** resistor gets the **largest** share of the potential difference.\n- In parallel the **largest** current flows through the **smallest** resistance.\n- For **two** resistors in parallel: R_{p} = [[R₁R₂/R₁ + R₂]] (product over sum).\n- R_{p} is always **smaller than the smallest** resistor in the combination. The more resistors in parallel, the smaller the total resistance, because there are more paths for the current – like a thicker wire.\n- House wiring is in parallel: every appliance gets the full voltage, and if one lamp blows, the rest still work.\n\n## Method for a combination circuit\n\n1. Calculate R_{p} of the parallel section.\n2. Total resistance: R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p}.\n3. Main current: I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}.\n4. Potential difference across the series resistor: V = I_{T} × R. Then V_{p} = V_{T} − V_{series}.\n5. Branch current: I = V_{p} ÷ R for each branch. Check that the branch currents add up to I_{T}.\n\n### What happens if ...? (battery with negligible internal resistance)\n\nAlways reason in this order: R_{T} changes → I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} changes → V across the series resistor changes → V across the parallel section changes.\n\n- A resistor is **added in parallel** → R_{T} decreases → I_{T} increases.\n- A branch is **removed** (e.g. a bulb blows) → R_{T} increases → I_{T} decreases.\n- A bulb glows brighter when the current through it (and the potential difference across it) is larger.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not inverting [[1/Rₚ]] to get R_{p}; simply adding parallel resistors; using the battery's full voltage across one resistor in a series circuit."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Emk (ε)","en":"Emf (ε)"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer geen stroom deur die battery vloei nie; die maksimum energie wat die battery per coulomb lading verskaf.","en":"The potential difference across the terminals of a battery when no current flows through the battery; the maximum energy the battery provides per coulomb of charge."}},{"term":{"af":"Terminale potensiaalverskil","en":"Terminal potential difference"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van 'n battery wanneer stroom in die stroombaan vloei. Dit is kleiner as die emk.","en":"The potential difference across the terminals of a battery when current flows in the circuit. It is less than the emf."}},{"term":{"af":"Potensiaalverskil (V)","en":"Potential difference (V)"},"def":{"af":"Die arbeid verrig (energie oorgedra) per eenheid positiewe lading tussen twee punte: V = W/Q. Eenheid: volt (V).","en":"The work done (energy transferred) per unit positive charge between two points: V = W/Q. Unit: volt (V)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stroom (I)","en":"Current (I)"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van vloei van lading: I = Q/Δt. Eenheid: ampère (A); 1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹.","en":"The rate of flow of charge: I = Q/Δt. Unit: ampere (A); 1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Weerstand (R)","en":"Resistance (R)"},"def":{"af":"Die teenstand teen die vloei van elektriese stroom; die verhouding R = V/I. Eenheid: ohm (Ω); 1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹.","en":"The opposition to the flow of electric current; the ratio R = V/I. Unit: ohm (Ω); 1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Ohm se wet","en":"Ohm's law"},"def":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n geleier is direk eweredig aan die stroom in die geleier by konstante temperatuur.","en":"The potential difference across a conductor is directly proportional to the current in the conductor at constant temperature."}},{"term":{"af":"Ekwivalente weerstand","en":"Equivalent resistance"},"def":{"af":"Die enkele weerstand wat 'n kombinasie van resistors kan vervang en by dieselfde potensiaalverskil dieselfde stroom sal deurlaat.","en":"The single resistance that can replace a combination of resistors and will allow the same current at the same potential difference."}},{"term":{"af":"Ammeter","en":"Ammeter"},"def":{"af":"'n Instrument wat stroom meet. Dit word in serie gekoppel en het 'n baie lae weerstand.","en":"An instrument that measures current. It is connected in series and has a very low resistance."}},{"term":{"af":"Voltmeter","en":"Voltmeter"},"def":{"af":"'n Instrument wat potensiaalverskil meet. Dit word in parallel oor 'n komponent gekoppel en het 'n baie hoë weerstand.","en":"An instrument that measures potential difference. It is connected in parallel across a component and has a very high resistance."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Lading, stroom en aantal elektrone","en":"Charge, current and number of electrons"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag laai jy jou foon met 'n kragbank. Die kragbank lewer 'n konstante stroom van 2 A vir 30 minute. Bereken (a) die lading wat gevloei het en (b) die aantal elektrone wat gevloei het.","en":"During load-shedding you charge your phone with a power bank. The power bank delivers a constant current of 2 A for 30 minutes. Calculate (a) the charge that flowed and (b) the number of electrons that flowed."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel eers die tyd na sekondes om: Δt = 30 × 60 = 1 800 s.","en":"First convert the time to seconds: Δt = 30 × 60 = 1 800 s."},{"af":"(a) I = [[Q/Δt]], dus Q = IΔt = 2 × 1 800 = 3 600 C.","en":"(a) I = [[Q/Δt]], so Q = IΔt = 2 × 1 800 = 3 600 C."},{"af":"(b) Elke elektron dra 'n lading van 1,6 × 10^{−19} C: n = [[Q/e]] = 3 600 ÷ (1,6 × 10^{−19})","en":"(b) Each electron carries a charge of 1.6 × 10^{−19} C: n = [[Q/e]] = 3 600 ÷ (1.6 × 10^{−19})"},{"af":"n = 2,25 × 10^{22} elektrone","en":"n = 2.25 × 10^{22} electrons"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Q = 3 600 C; (b) n = 2,25 × 10²² elektrone","en":"(a) Q = 3 600 C; (b) n = 2.25 × 10²² electrons"}},{"title":{"af":"Resistors in serie","en":"Resistors in series"},"problem":{"af":"'n Battery met 'n emk van 12 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand is in serie gekoppel met drie resistors van 2 Ω, 4 Ω en 6 Ω. 'n Ammeter is in serie in die stroombaan en 'n voltmeter is oor die 6 Ω-resistor gekoppel. Bereken (a) die ekwivalente weerstand, (b) die ammeterlesing en (c) die voltmeterlesing.","en":"A battery with an emf of 12 V and negligible internal resistance is connected in series with three resistors of 2 Ω, 4 Ω and 6 Ω. An ammeter is in series in the circuit and a voltmeter is connected across the 6 Ω resistor. Calculate (a) the equivalent resistance, (b) the ammeter reading and (c) the voltmeter reading."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) In serie tel weerstande op: R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} = 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 Ω","en":"(a) In series resistances add up: R_{s} = R_{1} + R_{2} + R_{3} = 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 Ω"},{"af":"(b) R = [[V/I]], dus I = V ÷ R = 12 ÷ 12 = 1 A. In serie is die stroom oral dieselfde, so die ammeter lees 1 A.","en":"(b) R = [[V/I]], so I = V ÷ R = 12 ÷ 12 = 1 A. In series the current is the same everywhere, so the ammeter reads 1 A."},{"af":"(c) V = IR = 1 × 6 = 6 V oor die 6 Ω-resistor.","en":"(c) V = IR = 1 × 6 = 6 V across the 6 Ω resistor."},{"af":"Kontroleer: V oor 2 Ω = 2 V en oor 4 Ω = 4 V. 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 V = emk ✓ – 'n serie-stroombaan is 'n spanningsverdeler, en die grootste resistor kry die grootste deel.","en":"Check: V across 2 Ω = 2 V and across 4 Ω = 4 V. 2 + 4 + 6 = 12 V = emf ✓ – a series circuit is a voltage divider, and the largest resistor gets the largest share."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 12 Ω; (b) 1 A; (c) 6 V","en":"(a) 12 Ω; (b) 1 A; (c) 6 V"}},{"title":{"af":"Kombinasiestroombaan","en":"Combination circuit"},"problem":{"af":"'n Battery met 'n emk van 12 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand is gekoppel aan 'n 4 Ω-resistor in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van 'n 6 Ω- en 'n 3 Ω-resistor. Bereken (a) die totale weerstand, (b) die stroom deur die battery, (c) die potensiaalverskil oor die parallelle kombinasie en (d) die stroom deur die 6 Ω-resistor.","en":"A battery with an emf of 12 V and negligible internal resistance is connected to a 4 Ω resistor in series with a parallel combination of a 6 Ω and a 3 Ω resistor. Calculate (a) the total resistance, (b) the current through the battery, (c) the potential difference across the parallel combination and (d) the current through the 6 Ω resistor."},"steps":[{"af":"Parallelle deel eerste (produk oor som): R_{p} = [[6 × 3/6 + 3]] = [[18/9]] = 2 Ω","en":"Parallel section first (product over sum): R_{p} = [[6 × 3/6 + 3]] = [[18/9]] = 2 Ω"},{"af":"(a) R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p} = 4 + 2 = 6 Ω","en":"(a) R_{T} = R_{s} + R_{p} = 4 + 2 = 6 Ω"},{"af":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} = 12 ÷ 6 = 2 A","en":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T} = 12 ÷ 6 = 2 A"},{"af":"(c) V oor die 4 Ω-resistor = I_{T}R = 2 × 4 = 8 V. Dus V_{p} = 12 − 8 = 4 V (of V_{p} = I_{T}R_{p} = 2 × 2 = 4 V).","en":"(c) V across the 4 Ω resistor = I_{T}R = 2 × 4 = 8 V. So V_{p} = 12 − 8 = 4 V (or V_{p} = I_{T}R_{p} = 2 × 2 = 4 V)."},{"af":"(d) I_{6Ω} = V_{p} ÷ R = 4 ÷ 6 = 0,67 A. Kontroleer: I_{3Ω} = 4 ÷ 3 = 1,33 A en 0,67 + 1,33 = 2,00 A = I_{T} ✓","en":"(d) I_{6Ω} = V_{p} ÷ R = 4 ÷ 6 = 0.67 A. Check: I_{3Ω} = 4 ÷ 3 = 1.33 A and 0.67 + 1.33 = 2.00 A = I_{T} ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 6 Ω; (b) 2 A; (c) 4 V; (d) 0,67 A","en":"(a) 6 Ω; (b) 2 A; (c) 4 V; (d) 0.67 A"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik: 'n ekstra gloeilamp in parallel","en":"Explain: an extra bulb in parallel"},"problem":{"af":"Twee identiese gloeilampe is in parallel aan 'n battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand gekoppel. 'n Ammeter is in serie met die battery. 'n Derde identiese gloeilamp word in parallel bygevoeg. Wat gebeur met (a) die totale weerstand, (b) die ammeterlesing en (c) die helderheid van die oorspronklike twee gloeilampe? Verduidelik.","en":"Two identical bulbs are connected in parallel to a battery with negligible internal resistance. An ammeter is in series with the battery. A third identical bulb is added in parallel. What happens to (a) the total resistance, (b) the ammeter reading and (c) the brightness of the original two bulbs? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Ekstra tak gee 'n ekstra pad vir die stroom, dus neem die totale weerstand **af**. As elke gloeilamp 'n weerstand R het, daal R_{p} van [[R/2]] na [[R/3]].","en":"(a) An extra branch gives an extra path for the current, so the total resistance **decreases**. If each bulb has resistance R, R_{p} drops from [[R/2]] to [[R/3]]."},{"af":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}. Die battery se potensiaalverskil bly dieselfde en R_{T} neem af, dus neem die ammeterlesing **toe** (dit word 1,5 keer groter).","en":"(b) I_{T} = V ÷ R_{T}. The battery's potential difference stays the same and R_{T} decreases, so the ammeter reading **increases** (it becomes 1.5 times larger)."},{"af":"(c) Elke gloeilamp is direk oor die battery gekoppel, dus bly die potensiaalverskil oor elkeen V. Die stroom deur elkeen, I = V ÷ R, bly dieselfde, so die helderheid **bly dieselfde**.","en":"(c) Each bulb is connected directly across the battery, so the potential difference across each stays V. The current through each, I = V ÷ R, stays the same, so the brightness **stays the same**."},{"af":"Daarom word huise in parallel bedraad: as jy 'n ekstra lamp aanskakel, word die ander nie dowwer nie – maar die totale stroom uit die battery of omsetter neem toe.","en":"That is why houses are wired in parallel: switching on an extra lamp does not make the others dimmer – but the total current from the battery or inverter increases."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Neem af; (b) neem toe; (c) bly dieselfde","en":"(a) Decreases; (b) increases; (c) stays the same"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van elektriese stroom?","en":"Which statement is the definition of electric current?"},"options":[{"af":"Die arbeid verrig per eenheid positiewe lading","en":"The work done per unit positive charge"},{"af":"Die tempo van vloei van lading","en":"The rate of flow of charge"},{"af":"Die teenstand teen die vloei van lading","en":"The opposition to the flow of charge"},{"af":"Die totale hoeveelheid lading wat deur 'n geleier vloei","en":"The total amount of charge that flows through a conductor"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Stroom is die tempo van vloei van lading: I = Q/Δt. Die eerste opsie beskryf potensiaalverskil, die derde beskryf weerstand en die laaste is net lading (Q) – stroom gaan oor hoeveel lading per sekonde vloei.","en":"Current is the rate of flow of charge: I = Q/Δt. The first option describes potential difference, the third describes resistance and the last is just charge (Q) – current is about how much charge flows per second."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by sy SI-eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to its SI unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Stroom","en":"Current"},"r":{"af":"ampère (A)","en":"ampere (A)"}},{"l":{"af":"Potensiaalverskil","en":"Potential difference"},"r":{"af":"volt (V)","en":"volt (V)"}},{"l":{"af":"Weerstand","en":"Resistance"},"r":{"af":"ohm (Ω)","en":"ohm (Ω)"}},{"l":{"af":"Lading","en":"Charge"},"r":{"af":"coulomb (C)","en":"coulomb (C)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Stroom: ampère (1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹); potensiaalverskil: volt (1 V = 1 J·C⁻¹); weerstand: ohm (1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹); lading: coulomb.","en":"Current: ampere (1 A = 1 C·s⁻¹); potential difference: volt (1 V = 1 J·C⁻¹); resistance: ohm (1 Ω = 1 V·A⁻¹); charge: coulomb."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om die stroom deur 'n resistor te meet, word 'n ammeter in parallel met die resistor gekoppel.","en":"To measure the current through a resistor, an ammeter is connected in parallel with the resistor."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Ammeter word in serie gekoppel sodat dieselfde stroom deur die ammeter en die resistor vloei. Die voltmeter is die meter wat in parallel gekoppel word.","en":"False. An ammeter is connected in series so that the same current flows through the ammeter and the resistor. The voltmeter is the meter that is connected in parallel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie verskillende resistors is in serie aan 'n battery gekoppel. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"Three different resistors are connected in series to a battery. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor elke resistor is dieselfde.","en":"The potential difference across each resistor is the same."},{"af":"Die totale weerstand is kleiner as die kleinste resistor.","en":"The total resistance is smaller than the smallest resistor."},{"af":"Die stroom deur elke resistor is dieselfde.","en":"The current through each resistor is the same."},{"af":"Die stroom verdeel tussen die resistors.","en":"The current divides between the resistors."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In serie is daar net een pad, dus is die stroom oral dieselfde. Die potensiaalverskil verdeel (die grootste resistor kry die meeste), en R_s = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ is groter as enige van die resistors. Die ander drie opsies beskryf eienskappe van 'n parallelle stroombaan.","en":"In series there is only one path, so the current is the same everywhere. The potential difference divides (the largest resistor gets the most), and R_s = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ is larger than any of the resistors. The other three options describe properties of a parallel circuit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter verandering sal die weerstand van 'n koperdraad VERLAAG?","en":"Which change will DECREASE the resistance of a copper wire?"},"options":[{"af":"Gebruik 'n dikker draad van dieselfde lengte.","en":"Use a thicker wire of the same length."},{"af":"Gebruik 'n langer draad van dieselfde dikte.","en":"Use a longer wire of the same thickness."},{"af":"Verhit die draad.","en":"Heat the wire."},{"af":"Gebruik 'n dunner draad van dieselfde lengte.","en":"Use a thinner wire of the same length."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Dikker draad het 'n groter deursnee-oppervlakte: daar is meer ruimte vir die elektrone om deur te beweeg, dus neem R af. 'n Langer draad gee meer botsings, en 'n warmer draad se atome vibreer meer – albei verhoog R. 'n Dunner draad verhoog ook R.","en":"A thicker wire has a larger cross-sectional area: there is more room for the electrons to move through, so R decreases. A longer wire gives more collisions, and in a hotter wire the atoms vibrate more – both increase R. A thinner wire also increases R."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wanneer die skakelaar oop is en geen stroom vloei nie, lees 'n voltmeter wat oor die pole van 'n battery gekoppel is, die emk van die battery.","en":"When the switch is open and no current flows, a voltmeter connected across the terminals of a battery reads the emf of the battery."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Emk is per definisie die potensiaalverskil oor die pole van die battery wanneer geen stroom vloei nie. As die skakelaar toe is, lees die voltmeter die terminale potensiaalverskil, wat effens kleiner is.","en":"True. Emf is by definition the potential difference across the terminals of the battery when no current flows. With the switch closed, the voltmeter reads the terminal potential difference, which is slightly less."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n 4 Ω-, 'n 6 Ω- en 'n 10 Ω-resistor word in serie gekoppel. Die ekwivalente weerstand is ___ Ω.","en":"A 4 Ω, a 6 Ω and a 10 Ω resistor are connected in series. The equivalent resistance is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["20","20 Ω","20Ω","20 ohm","20,0","20.0","20,00","20.00"],"en":["20","20 Ω","20Ω","20 ohm","20 ohms","20,0","20.0","20,00","20.00"]},"explain":{"af":"In serie tel die weerstande op: R_s = 4 + 6 + 10 = 20 Ω.","en":"In series the resistances add up: R_s = 4 + 6 + 10 = 20 Ω."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1,94","240","6,67"],"en":["1.94","240","6.67"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Lading van 90 C vloei in 1 minuut deur 'n gloeilamp. Die stroom deur die gloeilamp is ___ A.","en":"A charge of 90 C flows through a bulb in 1 minute. The current through the bulb is ___ A."},"answers":{"af":["1,5","1.5","1,5 A","1.5 A","1,5A","1.5A","1,50","1.50","1,50 A","1.50 A"],"en":["1,5","1.5","1,5 A","1.5 A","1,5A","1.5A","1,50","1.50","1,50 A","1.50 A"]},"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: Δt = 1 min = 60 s. I = Q/Δt = 90 ÷ 60 = 1,5 A. As jy vergeet om na sekondes om te skakel, kry jy die verkeerde antwoord van 90 A.","en":"Convert first: Δt = 1 min = 60 s. I = Q/Δt = 90 ÷ 60 = 1.5 A. If you forget to convert to seconds, you get the wrong answer of 90 A."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["90","5400","0,67"],"en":["90","5400","0.67"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die potensiaalverskil oor 'n resistor is 6 V en die stroom daardeur is 0,4 A. Die weerstand van die resistor is ___ Ω.","en":"The potential difference across a resistor is 6 V and the current through it is 0.4 A. The resistance of the resistor is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["15","15 Ω","15Ω","15 ohm","15,0","15.0","15,00","15.00"],"en":["15","15 Ω","15Ω","15 ohm","15 ohms","15,0","15.0","15,00","15.00"]},"explain":{"af":"R = V/I = 6 ÷ 0,4 = 15 Ω. Moenie V × I (= 2,4) bereken nie – weerstand is spanning gedeel deur stroom.","en":"R = V/I = 6 ÷ 0.4 = 15 Ω. Do not calculate V × I (= 2.4) – resistance is voltage divided by current."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2,4","0,07","6,4"],"en":["2.4","0.07","6.4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n 6 Ω- en 'n 12 Ω-resistor word in parallel gekoppel. Wat is die ekwivalente weerstand?","en":"A 6 Ω and a 12 Ω resistor are connected in parallel. What is the equivalent resistance?"},"options":[{"af":"18 Ω","en":"18 Ω"},{"af":"0,25 Ω","en":"0.25 Ω"},{"af":"9 Ω","en":"9 Ω"},{"af":"4 Ω","en":"4 Ω"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/12 = 2/12 + 1/12 = 3/12, dus Rₚ = 12/3 = 4 Ω (of produk oor som: 72 ÷ 18 = 4 Ω). 18 Ω is die serie-antwoord, 0,25 Ω is 1/Rₚ wat nie omgekeer is nie, en 9 Ω is net die gemiddeld. Kontroleer: Rₚ moet kleiner as 6 Ω wees.","en":"1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/12 = 2/12 + 1/12 = 3/12, so Rₚ = 12/3 = 4 Ω (or product over sum: 72 ÷ 18 = 4 Ω). 18 Ω is the series answer, 0.25 Ω is 1/Rₚ not inverted, and 9 Ω is just the average. Check: Rₚ must be smaller than 6 Ω."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie identiese 1,5 V-selle word in serie aan 'n 9 Ω-resistor gekoppel. Ignoreer die selle se interne weerstand. Wat is die stroom in die stroombaan?","en":"Three identical 1.5 V cells are connected in series to a 9 Ω resistor. Ignore the internal resistance of the cells. What is the current in the circuit?"},"options":[{"af":"0,17 A","en":"0.17 A"},{"af":"0,5 A","en":"0.5 A"},{"af":"2 A","en":"2 A"},{"af":"40,5 A","en":"40.5 A"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Selle in serie: emk = 3 × 1,5 = 4,5 V. I = V ÷ R = 4,5 ÷ 9 = 0,5 A. 0,17 A gebruik net een sel (1,5 ÷ 9), 2 A is R ÷ V (omgekeer) en 40,5 A is V × R.","en":"Cells in series: emf = 3 × 1.5 = 4.5 V. I = V ÷ R = 4.5 ÷ 9 = 0.5 A. 0.17 A uses only one cell (1.5 ÷ 9), 2 A is R ÷ V (inverted) and 40.5 A is V × R."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n 2 Ω-resistor is in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van twee 4 Ω-resistors. Die stroombaan is gekoppel aan 'n battery met 'n emk van 8 V en weglaatbare interne weerstand. 'n Ammeter is in serie met die battery. Wat lees die ammeter?","en":"A 2 Ω resistor is in series with a parallel combination of two 4 Ω resistors. The circuit is connected to a battery with an emf of 8 V and negligible internal resistance. An ammeter is in series with the battery. What does the ammeter read?"},"options":[{"af":"2 A","en":"2 A"},{"af":"0,8 A","en":"0.8 A"},{"af":"4 A","en":"4 A"},{"af":"1 A","en":"1 A"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Rₚ = (4 × 4)/(4 + 4) = 2 Ω; R_T = 2 + 2 = 4 Ω; I = 8 ÷ 4 = 2 A. 0,8 A kry jy as jy al drie resistors in serie optel (8 ÷ 10), 4 A as jy die 2 Ω-serie-resistor vergeet (8 ÷ 2), en 1 A is die stroom in net een van die takke.","en":"Rₚ = (4 × 4)/(4 + 4) = 2 Ω; R_T = 2 + 2 = 4 Ω; I = 8 ÷ 4 = 2 A. You get 0.8 A if you add all three resistors in series (8 ÷ 10), 4 A if you forget the 2 Ω series resistor (8 ÷ 2), and 1 A is the current in just one of the branches."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n 3 Ω-resistor is in serie met 'n parallelle kombinasie van 'n 6 Ω-, 'n 3 Ω- en 'n 2 Ω-resistor. Die ekwivalente weerstand van al vier resistors saam is ___ Ω.","en":"A 3 Ω resistor is in series with a parallel combination of a 6 Ω, a 3 Ω and a 2 Ω resistor. The equivalent resistance of all four resistors together is ___ Ω."},"answers":{"af":["4","4 Ω","4Ω","4 ohm","4,0","4.0","4,00","4.00"],"en":["4","4 Ω","4Ω","4 ohm","4 ohms","4,0","4.0","4,00","4.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Parallel eerste: 1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/3 + 1/2 = 1/6 + 2/6 + 3/6 = 6/6 = 1, dus Rₚ = 1 Ω. Tel dan die serie-resistor by: R = 3 + 1 = 4 Ω. Produk oor som werk net vir twee resistors op 'n slag.","en":"Parallel first: 1/Rₚ = 1/6 + 1/3 + 1/2 = 1/6 + 2/6 + 3/6 = 6/6 = 1, so Rₚ = 1 Ω. Then add the series resistor: R = 3 + 1 = 4 Ω. Product over sum only works for two resistors at a time."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["14","6,27","0,75"],"en":["14","6.27","0.75"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Drie identiese gloeilampe P, Q en R is aan 'n battery met weglaatbare interne weerstand gekoppel. Q en R is in parallel met mekaar, en hierdie parallelle kombinasie is in serie met P. Gloeilamp R brand uit (sy filament breek). Watter stelling beskryf die gevolg korrek?","en":"Three identical bulbs P, Q and R are connected to a battery with negligible internal resistance. Q and R are in parallel with each other, and this parallel combination is in series with P. Bulb R blows (its filament breaks). Which statement correctly describes the result?"},"options":[{"af":"P word helderder en Q word dowwer.","en":"P becomes brighter and Q becomes dimmer."},{"af":"P en Q word albei dowwer.","en":"P and Q both become dimmer."},{"af":"P word dowwer en Q word helderder.","en":"P becomes dimmer and Q becomes brighter."},{"af":"P word dowwer en Q gaan ook uit.","en":"P becomes dimmer and Q also goes out."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sonder R het die parallelle deel net een pad, dus neem sy weerstand toe (van ½R na R) en R_T neem toe (van 1,5R na 2R). I_T = V ÷ R_T neem af, dus word P dowwer en die potensiaalverskil oor P daal (van ⅔V na ½V). Die potensiaalverskil oor Q = V − V_P neem dus toe (van ⅓V na ½V), so Q word helderder. Q gaan nie uit nie – dit is steeds in 'n volledige stroombaan met P.","en":"Without R the parallel section has only one path, so its resistance increases (from ½R to R) and R_T increases (from 1.5R to 2R). I_T = V ÷ R_T decreases, so P becomes dimmer and the potential difference across P drops (from ⅔V to ½V). The potential difference across Q = V − V_P therefore increases (from ⅓V to ½V), so Q becomes brighter. Q does not go out – it is still in a complete circuit with P."}}]},{"id":"f10-t2-fisiese-chemiese-verandering","title":{"af":"Fisiese en chemiese verandering","en":"Physical and chemical change"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal fisiese en chemiese veranderinge op deeltjievlak kan onderskei, die behoudswette en die wet van konstante samestelling kan toepas en chemiese vergelykings met toestandsimbole kan balanseer.","en":"You will be able to distinguish physical and chemical changes at particle level, apply the conservation laws and the law of constant composition, and balance chemical equations with state symbols."},"summary":{"af":"## Fisiese verandering\n\n'n **Fisiese verandering** is 'n verandering waartydens **geen nuwe stowwe** gevorm word nie. Net die toestand, vorm of rangskikking van die deeltjies verander.\n\n- Die **molekules bly heel**: geen bindings binne-in die molekules word gebreek nie. Net die afstand tussen die molekules en hulle rangskikking verander.\n- Die **massa**, die aantal **atome** en die aantal **molekules** bly behoue.\n- Die **energieverandering is klein** – net die kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom.\n- Dit is gewoonlik maklik **omkeerbaar**.\n- Voorbeelde: ys smelt, water verdamp of kondenseer, was smelt, glas breek, 'n mengsel word deur filtrasie of distillasie geskei.\n\n## Chemiese verandering\n\n'n **Chemiese verandering** is 'n verandering waartydens **nuwe stowwe** met nuwe chemiese eienskappe gevorm word.\n\n- **Bindings word gebreek** in die reaktanse en **nuwe bindings word gevorm** in die produkte – die atome word **herrangskik**.\n- Die **massa** en die aantal en soort **atome** bly behoue, maar die aantal **molekules** kan verander.\n- Die **energieverandering is groot**: om bindings te breek kos energie, en wanneer bindings vorm, word energie vrygestel. 'n Reaksie wat energie vrystel (bv. die vuur by 'n braai) is **eksotermies**; een wat energie opneem, is **endotermies**.\n- Dit is gewoonlik moeilik omkeerbaar.\n- Tekens van 'n chemiese reaksie: 'n kleurverandering, gas word gevorm (borrels), 'n presipitaat (vaste stof) vorm, die temperatuur verander, of lig of klank word afgegee.\n- Voorbeelde: hout of gas brand, yster roes, kos verteer, kalksteen ontbind as dit verhit word.\n\n| | Fisiese verandering | Chemiese verandering |\n|---|---|---|\n| Nuwe stowwe? | nee | ja |\n| Molekules | bly heel | word opgebreek; atome herrangskik |\n| Energie | klein verandering | groot verandering |\n| Massa en atome | behoue | behoue |\n| Aantal molekules | behoue | kan verander |\n| Omkeerbaar? | maklik | moeilik |\n\n## Ontbinding en sintese\n\n- **Ontbindingsreaksie:** een verbinding breek op in twee of meer eenvoudiger stowwe. Bv. die elektrolise van water: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g), of waterstofperoksied: 2H_{2}O_{2}(aq) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ) + O_{2}(g).\n- **Sintesereaksie:** twee of meer stowwe verbind om **een** nuwe produk te vorm. Bv. yster en swael word saam verhit: Fe(s) + S(s) → FeS(s); of 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n## Behoud van atome en massa\n\n- **Wet van behoud van massa:** *Die massa van 'n geslote sisteem van stowwe bly konstant, ongeag die prosesse wat binne die sisteem plaasvind.* Tydens 'n reaksie is die totale massa van die reaktanse dus gelyk aan die totale massa van die produkte.\n- **Behoud van atome:** atome word nie geskep of vernietig nie, net herrangskik. Daarom moet elke chemiese vergelyking gebalanseer wees.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** In 'n **oop** houer lyk dit asof massa verander. As staalwol brand, is die produk swaarder (suurstof uit die lug het met die yster verbind). As kalksteen verhit word, word die vaste stof ligter (CO_{2}-gas ontsnap). In 'n geslote sisteem bly die totale massa presies dieselfde.\n\n## Wet van konstante samestelling\n\n*In enige gegewe chemiese verbinding verbind die elemente altyd in dieselfde massaverhouding met mekaar*, ongeag hoe die verbinding berei is of waar dit vandaan kom.\n\n- Water (H_{2}O): H : O = 2 × 1 : 16 = 2 : 16 = **1 : 8** volgens massa.\n- Koolstofdioksied (CO_{2}): C : O = 12 : 32 = **3 : 8**.\n- Waterstofperoksied (H_{2}O_{2}) is 'n *ander* verbinding: H : O = 2 : 32 = 1 : 16.\n\n## Reaksies in woorde en simbole\n\n- **Woordvergelyking:** magnesium + suurstof → magnesiumoksied\n- **Gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking:** 2Mg(s) + O_{2}(g) → 2MgO(s)\n\n**Reaktanse** staan links van die pyl en **produkte** regs. Die **koëffisiënt** (groot getal voor 'n formule) gee die aantal deeltjies; die **onderskrif** (klein getal) is deel van die formule.\n\n**Toestandsimbole:** (s) vaste stof; (ℓ) vloeistof; (g) gas; (aq) waterige oplossing – opgelos in water.\n\n## Stappe om 'n vergelyking te balanseer\n\n1. Skryf die korrekte formules van al die reaktanse en produkte. Onthou die diatomiese elemente: H_{2}, N_{2}, O_{2}, F_{2}, Cl_{2}, Br_{2}, I_{2}.\n2. Tel die atome van elke element aan albei kante.\n3. Balanseer **slegs met koëffisiënte** – verander **nooit** 'n onderskrif nie (H_{2}O → H_{2}O_{2} is 'n heel ander stof!).\n4. Begin met die element wat in die minste formules voorkom en laat H en O vir laaste. Hanteer 'n poliatomiese ioon (bv. SO_{4}) as een eenheid as dit onveranderd aan albei kante voorkom.\n5. Kontroleer elke element en skryf die koëffisiënte in die kleinste heelgetalverhouding.\n\n**Voorbeeld:** CH_{4} + O_{2} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O. C: 1 = 1. H: 4 links, dus 2H_{2}O. O: regs 2 + 2 = 4, dus 2O_{2}. Antwoord: CH_{4}(g) + 2O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n> **Wenk – atome tel met hakies:** 3Ca(NO_{3})_{2} bevat 3 Ca-atome, 3 × 2 = 6 N-atome en 3 × 2 × 3 = 18 O-atome. Die koëffisiënt vermenigvuldig alles in die formule.","en":"## Physical change\n\nA **physical change** is a change in which **no new substances** are formed. Only the state, shape or arrangement of the particles changes.\n\n- The **molecules stay intact**: no bonds inside the molecules are broken. Only the distance between the molecules and their arrangement change.\n- The **mass**, the number of **atoms** and the number of **molecules** are conserved.\n- The **energy change is small** – only the forces between the molecules are overcome.\n- It is usually easily **reversible**.\n- Examples: ice melting, water evaporating or condensing, wax melting, glass breaking, a mixture being separated by filtration or distillation.\n\n## Chemical change\n\nA **chemical change** is a change in which **new substances** with new chemical properties are formed.\n\n- **Bonds are broken** in the reactants and **new bonds are formed** in the products – the atoms are **rearranged**.\n- The **mass** and the number and type of **atoms** are conserved, but the number of **molecules** can change.\n- The **energy change is large**: breaking bonds costs energy, and when bonds form, energy is released. A reaction that releases energy (e.g. the fire at a braai) is **exothermic**; one that absorbs energy is **endothermic**.\n- It is usually difficult to reverse.\n- Signs of a chemical reaction: a colour change, a gas forms (bubbles), a precipitate (solid) forms, the temperature changes, or light or sound is given off.\n- Examples: wood or gas burning, iron rusting, food being digested, limestone decomposing when heated.\n\n| | Physical change | Chemical change |\n|---|---|---|\n| New substances? | no | yes |\n| Molecules | stay intact | are broken up; atoms rearranged |\n| Energy | small change | large change |\n| Mass and atoms | conserved | conserved |\n| Number of molecules | conserved | can change |\n| Reversible? | easily | with difficulty |\n\n## Decomposition and synthesis\n\n- **Decomposition reaction:** one compound breaks up into two or more simpler substances. E.g. the electrolysis of water: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g), or hydrogen peroxide: 2H_{2}O_{2}(aq) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ) + O_{2}(g).\n- **Synthesis reaction:** two or more substances combine to form **one** new product. E.g. iron and sulfur heated together: Fe(s) + S(s) → FeS(s); or 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g) → 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n## Conservation of atoms and mass\n\n- **Law of conservation of mass:** *The mass of a closed system of substances will remain constant, regardless of the processes acting inside the system.* So during a reaction the total mass of the reactants equals the total mass of the products.\n- **Conservation of atoms:** atoms are not created or destroyed, only rearranged. That is why every chemical equation must be balanced.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In an **open** container it looks as if mass changes. When steel wool burns, the product is heavier (oxygen from the air combined with the iron). When limestone is heated, the solid becomes lighter (CO_{2} gas escapes). In a closed system the total mass stays exactly the same.\n\n## Law of constant composition\n\n*In any given chemical compound, the elements always combine in the same proportion by mass with each other*, regardless of how the compound was prepared or where it comes from.\n\n- Water (H_{2}O): H : O = 2 × 1 : 16 = 2 : 16 = **1 : 8** by mass.\n- Carbon dioxide (CO_{2}): C : O = 12 : 32 = **3 : 8**.\n- Hydrogen peroxide (H_{2}O_{2}) is a *different* compound: H : O = 2 : 32 = 1 : 16.\n\n## Reactions in words and symbols\n\n- **Word equation:** magnesium + oxygen → magnesium oxide\n- **Balanced chemical equation:** 2Mg(s) + O_{2}(g) → 2MgO(s)\n\n**Reactants** are on the left of the arrow and **products** on the right. The **coefficient** (large number in front of a formula) gives the number of particles; the **subscript** (small number) is part of the formula.\n\n**State symbols:** (s) solid; (ℓ) liquid; (g) gas; (aq) aqueous solution – dissolved in water.\n\n## Steps to balance an equation\n\n1. Write the correct formulae of all the reactants and products. Remember the diatomic elements: H_{2}, N_{2}, O_{2}, F_{2}, Cl_{2}, Br_{2}, I_{2}.\n2. Count the atoms of each element on both sides.\n3. Balance **only with coefficients** – **never** change a subscript (H_{2}O → H_{2}O_{2} is a completely different substance!).\n4. Start with the element that appears in the fewest formulae and leave H and O for last. Treat a polyatomic ion (e.g. SO_{4}) as one unit if it appears unchanged on both sides.\n5. Check every element and write the coefficients in the smallest whole-number ratio.\n\n**Example:** CH_{4} + O_{2} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O. C: 1 = 1. H: 4 on the left, so 2H_{2}O. O: on the right 2 + 2 = 4, so 2O_{2}. Answer: CH_{4}(g) + 2O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + 2H_{2}O(ℓ).\n\n> **Tip – counting atoms with brackets:** 3Ca(NO_{3})_{2} contains 3 Ca atoms, 3 × 2 = 6 N atoms and 3 × 2 × 3 = 18 O atoms. The coefficient multiplies everything in the formula."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Fisiese verandering","en":"Physical change"},"def":{"af":"'n Verandering waartydens geen nuwe stowwe gevorm word nie; die molekules bly heel en net hulle rangskikking verander.","en":"A change in which no new substances are formed; the molecules stay intact and only their arrangement changes."}},{"term":{"af":"Chemiese verandering","en":"Chemical change"},"def":{"af":"'n Verandering waartydens nuwe stowwe met nuwe eienskappe gevorm word; bindings word gebreek en nuwe bindings word gevorm.","en":"A change in which new substances with new properties are formed; bonds are broken and new bonds are formed."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontbindingsreaksie","en":"Decomposition reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin een verbinding in twee of meer eenvoudiger stowwe opbreek, bv. 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂.","en":"A reaction in which one compound breaks up into two or more simpler substances, e.g. 2H₂O₂ → 2H₂O + O₂."}},{"term":{"af":"Sintesereaksie","en":"Synthesis reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin twee of meer stowwe verbind om een nuwe produk te vorm, bv. Fe + S → FeS.","en":"A reaction in which two or more substances combine to form one new product, e.g. Fe + S → FeS."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van massa","en":"Law of conservation of mass"},"def":{"af":"Die massa van 'n geslote sisteem van stowwe bly konstant, ongeag die prosesse wat binne die sisteem plaasvind.","en":"The mass of a closed system of substances will remain constant, regardless of the processes acting inside the system."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van konstante samestelling","en":"Law of constant composition"},"def":{"af":"In enige gegewe chemiese verbinding verbind die elemente altyd in dieselfde massaverhouding met mekaar.","en":"In any given chemical compound, the elements always combine in the same proportion by mass with each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking","en":"Balanced chemical equation"},"def":{"af":"'n Vergelyking met dieselfde aantal atome van elke element aan die reaktant- en die produkkant.","en":"An equation with the same number of atoms of each element on the reactant side and the product side."}},{"term":{"af":"Koëffisiënt","en":"Coefficient"},"def":{"af":"Die getal voor 'n formule in 'n chemiese vergelyking wat die aantal deeltjies aandui; dit word gebruik om te balanseer.","en":"The number in front of a formula in a chemical equation that shows the number of particles; it is used to balance."}},{"term":{"af":"Eksotermiese reaksie","en":"Exothermic reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie wat energie (hitte) aan die omgewing vrystel, bv. die verbranding van hout.","en":"A reaction that releases energy (heat) to the surroundings, e.g. the burning of wood."}},{"term":{"af":"Endotermiese reaksie","en":"Endothermic reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie wat energie uit die omgewing opneem, bv. die ontbinding van kalksteen wanneer dit verhit word.","en":"A reaction that absorbs energy from the surroundings, e.g. the decomposition of limestone when it is heated."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Fisies of chemies? Verduidelik op deeltjievlak","en":"Physical or chemical? Explain at particle level"},"problem":{"af":"Vergelyk wat met die watermolekules gebeur wanneer (a) water in 'n ketel kook en (b) water deur elektrolise in waterstof en suurstof ontbind word. Verwys na die molekules, die energie en die massa.","en":"Compare what happens to the water molecules when (a) water boils in a kettle and (b) water is decomposed into hydrogen and oxygen by electrolysis. Refer to the molecules, the energy and the mass."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Kook: die watermolekules bly H_{2}O; hulle beweeg net verder uitmekaar (vloeistof → gas). Geen nuwe stof vorm nie, dus is dit 'n **fisiese verandering**.","en":"(a) Boiling: the water molecules stay H_{2}O; they just move further apart (liquid → gas). No new substance forms, so it is a **physical change**."},{"af":"(a) Net die kragte tussen die molekules word oorkom, dus is die energieverandering relatief klein. Die massa en die aantal molekules bly dieselfde.","en":"(a) Only the forces between the molecules are overcome, so the energy change is relatively small. The mass and the number of molecules stay the same."},{"af":"(b) Elektrolise: die bindings binne-in die watermolekules word gebreek en die atome word herrangskik in H_{2}- en O_{2}-molekules: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g). Nuwe stowwe vorm, dus is dit 'n **chemiese verandering** ('n ontbindingsreaksie).","en":"(b) Electrolysis: the bonds inside the water molecules are broken and the atoms are rearranged into H_{2} and O_{2} molecules: 2H_{2}O(ℓ) → 2H_{2}(g) + O_{2}(g). New substances form, so it is a **chemical change** (a decomposition reaction)."},{"af":"(b) Baie elektriese energie is nodig om die bindings te breek – 'n groot energieverandering. Daar is 4 H- en 2 O-atome aan albei kante, dus is die massa behoue, maar 2 molekules word 3 molekules.","en":"(b) A lot of electrical energy is needed to break the bonds – a large energy change. There are 4 H and 2 O atoms on both sides, so mass is conserved, but 2 molecules become 3 molecules."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Fisiese verandering; (b) chemiese verandering (ontbinding)","en":"(a) Physical change; (b) chemical change (decomposition)"}},{"title":{"af":"Balanseer 'n verbrandingsreaksie","en":"Balance a combustion reaction"},"problem":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag kook baie gesinne in Brits op 'n gasstoof. Propaan (C₃H₈) brand in suurstof en vorm koolstofdioksied en waterdamp. Skryf 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking met toestandsimbole.","en":"During load-shedding many families in Brits cook on a gas stove. Propane (C₃H₈) burns in oxygen and forms carbon dioxide and water vapour. Write a balanced equation with state symbols."},"steps":[{"af":"Ongebalanseerd: C_{3}H_{8}(g) + O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(g)","en":"Unbalanced: C_{3}H_{8}(g) + O_{2}(g) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(g)"},{"af":"C: 3 atome links, dus 3CO_{2} regs.","en":"C: 3 atoms on the left, so 3CO_{2} on the right."},{"af":"H: 8 atome links, dus 4H_{2}O regs (4 × 2 = 8).","en":"H: 8 atoms on the left, so 4H_{2}O on the right (4 × 2 = 8)."},{"af":"O laaste: regs is daar 3 × 2 + 4 × 1 = 10 O-atome, dus 5O_{2} links (5 × 2 = 10).","en":"O last: on the right there are 3 × 2 + 4 × 1 = 10 O atoms, so 5O_{2} on the left (5 × 2 = 10)."},{"af":"Kontroleer: C 3 = 3; H 8 = 8; O 10 = 10 ✓","en":"Check: C 3 = 3; H 8 = 8; O 10 = 10 ✓"}],"answer":{"af":"C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(g)","en":"C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(g)"}},{"title":{"af":"Van 'n woordvergelyking na simbole","en":"From a word equation to symbols"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 'n gebalanseerde chemiese vergelyking met toestandsimbole vir: aluminium + suurstof → aluminiumoksied (vaste stof). Watter tipe reaksie is dit?","en":"Write a balanced chemical equation with state symbols for: aluminium + oxygen → aluminium oxide (solid). What type of reaction is this?"},"steps":[{"af":"Formules: aluminium is 'n metaal (Al); suurstofgas is diatomies (O_{2}); aluminiumoksied bestaan uit Al^{3+}- en O^{2−}-ione, dus Al_{2}O_{3}.","en":"Formulae: aluminium is a metal (Al); oxygen gas is diatomic (O_{2}); aluminium oxide consists of Al^{3+} and O^{2−} ions, so Al_{2}O_{3}."},{"af":"Ongebalanseerd: Al(s) + O_{2}(g) → Al_{2}O_{3}(s)","en":"Unbalanced: Al(s) + O_{2}(g) → Al_{2}O_{3}(s)"},{"af":"O: 2 links en 3 regs. Die KGV van 2 en 3 is 6, dus 3O_{2} en 2Al_{2}O_{3}.","en":"O: 2 on the left and 3 on the right. The LCM of 2 and 3 is 6, so 3O_{2} and 2Al_{2}O_{3}."},{"af":"Al: regs is daar nou 2 × 2 = 4 Al-atome, dus 4Al links.","en":"Al: on the right there are now 2 × 2 = 4 Al atoms, so 4Al on the left."},{"af":"Kontroleer: Al 4 = 4; O 6 = 6 ✓. Twee stowwe vorm een produk, dus is dit 'n **sintesereaksie**.","en":"Check: Al 4 = 4; O 6 = 6 ✓. Two substances form one product, so it is a **synthesis reaction**."}],"answer":{"af":"4Al(s) + 3O₂(g) → 2Al₂O₃(s); sintesereaksie","en":"4Al(s) + 3O₂(g) → 2Al₂O₃(s); synthesis reaction"}},{"title":{"af":"Behoud van massa en konstante samestelling","en":"Conservation of mass and constant composition"},"problem":{"af":"Kalk (CaO), wat in die mynbedryf en vir sement gebruik word, word gemaak deur kalksteen sterk te verhit: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g). 'n Leerder verhit 10 g CaCO₃ in 'n oop proefbuis totdat dit volledig ontbind, en 5,6 g vaste stof bly oor. (a) Bereken die massa CO₂ wat gevorm het. (b) Die leerder sê massa het verlore gegaan. Evalueer sy stelling. (c) Watter massa CaO sal 25 g CaCO₃ lewer?","en":"Lime (CaO), which is used in mining and for cement, is made by strongly heating limestone: CaCO₃(s) → CaO(s) + CO₂(g). A learner heats 10 g CaCO₃ in an open test tube until it decomposes completely, and 5.6 g of solid remains. (a) Calculate the mass of CO₂ that formed. (b) The learner says mass was lost. Evaluate his statement. (c) What mass of CaO will 25 g CaCO₃ produce?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Behoud van massa: m(CaCO_{3}) = m(CaO) + m(CO_{2})","en":"(a) Conservation of mass: m(CaCO_{3}) = m(CaO) + m(CO_{2})"},{"af":"m(CO_{2}) = 10 − 5,6 = 4,4 g","en":"m(CO_{2}) = 10 − 5.6 = 4.4 g"},{"af":"(b) Massa het nie verlore gegaan nie: die 4,4 g CO_{2} is 'n gas wat uit die oop proefbuis ontsnap het. In 'n geslote sisteem sou die totale massa 10 g gebly het.","en":"(b) Mass was not lost: the 4.4 g CO_{2} is a gas that escaped from the open test tube. In a closed system the total mass would have stayed 10 g."},{"af":"(c) CaCO_{3} het 'n konstante samestelling, dus lewer dit altyd dieselfde massafraksie CaO: 10 g gee 5,6 g. Vir 25 g: m(CaO) = 25 × [[5,6/10]] = 14 g","en":"(c) CaCO_{3} has a constant composition, so it always produces the same mass fraction of CaO: 10 g gives 5.6 g. For 25 g: m(CaO) = 25 × [[5.6/10]] = 14 g"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 4,4 g CO₂; (b) die CO₂-gas het ontsnap – massa is behoue in 'n geslote sisteem; (c) 14 g CaO","en":"(a) 4.4 g CO₂; (b) the CO₂ gas escaped – mass is conserved in a closed system; (c) 14 g CaO"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n chemiese verandering?","en":"Which one of the following is a chemical change?"},"options":[{"af":"Ys smelt in 'n koelhouer.","en":"Ice melts in a cooler box."},{"af":"Suiker word fyngemaak.","en":"Sugar is crushed."},{"af":"'n Spyker roes buite in die reën.","en":"A nail rusts outside in the rain."},{"af":"Water kook in 'n ketel.","en":"Water boils in a kettle."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Roes is 'n nuwe stof (ysteroksied) wat vorm wanneer yster met suurstof en water reageer. Smelt, fynmaak en kook verander net die toestand of vorm van die stof – geen nuwe stof vorm nie.","en":"Rust is a new substance (iron oxide) that forms when iron reacts with oxygen and water. Melting, crushing and boiling only change the state or shape of the substance – no new substance forms."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke toestandsimbool by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each state symbol to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"(s)","en":"(s)"},"r":{"af":"vaste stof","en":"solid"}},{"l":{"af":"(ℓ)","en":"(ℓ)"},"r":{"af":"vloeistof","en":"liquid"}},{"l":{"af":"(g)","en":"(g)"},"r":{"af":"gas","en":"gas"}},{"l":{"af":"(aq)","en":"(aq)"},"r":{"af":"opgelos in water (waterige oplossing)","en":"dissolved in water (aqueous solution)"}}],"explain":{"af":"(s) = vaste stof, (ℓ) = vloeistof, (g) = gas en (aq) = waterige oplossing. Let op: (ℓ) beteken 'n suiwer vloeistof soos water, terwyl (aq) beteken dat die stof in water opgelos is.","en":"(s) = solid, (ℓ) = liquid, (g) = gas and (aq) = aqueous solution. Note: (ℓ) means a pure liquid such as water, while (aq) means the substance is dissolved in water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die reaksie 2H₂O₂(aq) → 2H₂O(ℓ) + O₂(g) is 'n voorbeeld van ...","en":"The reaction 2H₂O₂(aq) → 2H₂O(ℓ) + O₂(g) is an example of ..."},"options":[{"af":"'n sintesereaksie.","en":"a synthesis reaction."},{"af":"'n ontbindingsreaksie.","en":"a decomposition reaction."},{"af":"'n fisiese verandering.","en":"a physical change."},{"af":"'n presipitasiereaksie.","en":"a precipitation reaction."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Een verbinding (H₂O₂) breek op in twee eenvoudiger stowwe (H₂O en O₂) – dit is ontbinding. By sintese verbind stowwe juis om een produk te vorm. Dit is chemies (nuwe stowwe vorm), en geen onoplosbare vaste stof vorm nie, dus is dit nie presipitasie nie.","en":"One compound (H₂O₂) breaks up into two simpler substances (H₂O and O₂) – that is decomposition. In synthesis, substances combine to form one product. It is chemical (new substances form), and no insoluble solid forms, so it is not precipitation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling beskryf 'n fisiese verandering op deeltjievlak die beste?","en":"Which statement best describes a physical change at particle level?"},"options":[{"af":"Bindings binne-in die molekules word gebreek en nuwe bindings word gevorm.","en":"Bonds inside the molecules are broken and new bonds are formed."},{"af":"Atome word vernietig en nuwe atome word gevorm.","en":"Atoms are destroyed and new atoms are formed."},{"af":"Die aantal molekules verander, maar die massa bly dieselfde.","en":"The number of molecules changes, but the mass stays the same."},{"af":"Die molekules bly heel; net hulle rangskikking en die afstand tussen hulle verander.","en":"The molecules stay intact; only their arrangement and the distance between them change."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By 'n fisiese verandering bly die molekules heel – net die rangskikking en spasiëring verander. Bindings breek en vorm, en die aantal molekules verander, by 'n chemiese verandering. Atome word nooit vernietig of geskep nie.","en":"In a physical change the molecules stay intact – only the arrangement and spacing change. Bonds breaking and forming, and the number of molecules changing, happen in a chemical change. Atoms are never destroyed or created."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tydens 'n chemiese reaksie bly die aantal molekules altyd dieselfde.","en":"During a chemical reaction the number of molecules always stays the same."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die aantal en soort atome bly behoue, maar die aantal molekules kan verander. In 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O word 3 molekules 2 molekules, terwyl daar 4 H- en 2 O-atome aan albei kante is.","en":"False. The number and type of atoms are conserved, but the number of molecules can change. In 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, 3 molecules become 2 molecules, while there are 4 H and 2 O atoms on both sides."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens die wet van konstante samestelling bevat suiwer water altyd waterstof en suurstof in die massaverhouding 1 : 8, ongeag waar die water vandaan kom.","en":"According to the law of constant composition, pure water always contains hydrogen and oxygen in the mass ratio 1 : 8, regardless of where the water comes from."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. H₂O bevat 2 × 1 = 2 g waterstof vir elke 16 g suurstof, dus H : O = 2 : 16 = 1 : 8. Suiwer water uit 'n dam of uit 'n laboratorium het presies dieselfde samestelling.","en":"True. H₂O contains 2 × 1 = 2 g hydrogen for every 16 g oxygen, so H : O = 2 : 16 = 1 : 8. Pure water from a dam or from a laboratory has exactly the same composition."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n kers brand, smelt die was eers, en dan brand die wasdamp in die vlam. Watter stelling is korrek?","en":"When a candle burns, the wax first melts, and then the wax vapour burns in the flame. Which statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die smelt is 'n fisiese verandering en die brand is 'n chemiese verandering.","en":"The melting is a physical change and the burning is a chemical change."},{"af":"Albei is fisiese veranderinge.","en":"Both are physical changes."},{"af":"Albei is chemiese veranderinge.","en":"Both are chemical changes."},{"af":"Die smelt is 'n chemiese verandering en die brand is 'n fisiese verandering.","en":"The melting is a chemical change and the burning is a physical change."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Gesmelte was is steeds was (dieselfde molekules) – 'n fisiese verandering. Wanneer die wasdamp brand, reageer dit met suurstof en vorm nuwe stowwe (CO₂ en H₂O) met 'n groot energievrystelling (hitte en lig) – 'n chemiese verandering.","en":"Melted wax is still wax (the same molecules) – a physical change. When the wax vapour burns, it reacts with oxygen and forms new substances (CO₂ and H₂O) with a large release of energy (heat and light) – a chemical change."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Balanseer die vergelyking vir die vorming van ammoniak: N₂(g) + ___H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g)","en":"Balance the equation for the formation of ammonia: N₂(g) + ___H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g)"},"answers":{"af":["3","3H2","3H₂","drie"],"en":["3","3H2","3H₂","three"]},"explain":{"af":"Regs is daar 2 × 3 = 6 H-atome. Links het elke H₂-molekule 2 H-atome, dus is 3H₂ nodig (3 × 2 = 6). N: 2 = 2 ✓.","en":"On the right there are 2 × 3 = 6 H atoms. On the left each H₂ molecule has 2 H atoms, so 3H₂ is needed (3 × 2 = 6). N: 2 = 2 ✓."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6","2","1,5"],"en":["6","2","1.5"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel suurstofatome word deur 2Al₂(SO₄)₃ voorgestel? ___","en":"How many oxygen atoms are represented by 2Al₂(SO₄)₃? ___"},"answers":{"af":["24","24 atome","24 O-atome","24 O"],"en":["24","24 atoms","24 O atoms","24 O"]},"explain":{"af":"Elke SO₄ het 4 O-atome; die hakie word met 3 vermenigvuldig (12 O per Al₂(SO₄)₃), en die koëffisiënt 2 verdubbel alles: 2 × 3 × 4 = 24.","en":"Each SO₄ has 4 O atoms; the bracket is multiplied by 3 (12 O per Al₂(SO₄)₃), and the coefficient 2 doubles everything: 2 × 3 × 4 = 24."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["12","8","4"],"en":["12","8","4"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer 2,4 g magnesium volledig in suurstof brand, vorm 4,0 g magnesiumoksied. Die massa suurstof wat gereageer het, is ___ g.","en":"When 2.4 g of magnesium burns completely in oxygen, 4.0 g of magnesium oxide forms. The mass of oxygen that reacted is ___ g."},"answers":{"af":["1,6","1.6","1,6 g","1.6 g","1,6g","1.6g","1,60","1.60","1,60 g","1.60 g"],"en":["1,6","1.6","1,6 g","1.6 g","1,6g","1.6g","1,60","1.60","1,60 g","1.60 g"]},"explain":{"af":"Behoud van massa: m(Mg) + m(O₂) = m(MgO), dus m(O₂) = 4,0 − 2,4 = 1,6 g. Die produk is swaarder as die magnesium omdat die suurstof nou deel daarvan is.","en":"Conservation of mass: m(Mg) + m(O₂) = m(MgO), so m(O₂) = 4.0 − 2.4 = 1.6 g. The product is heavier than the magnesium because the oxygen is now part of it."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6,4","4,0","2,4"],"en":["6.4","4.0","2.4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die korrekte, gebalanseerde vergelyking vir magnesium wat in suurstofgas brand?","en":"Which one is the correct, balanced equation for magnesium burning in oxygen gas?"},"options":[{"af":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → MgO(s)"},{"af":"Mg(s) + O(g) → MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O(g) → MgO(s)"},{"af":"2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)","en":"2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)"},{"af":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)","en":"Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO: Mg 2 = 2 en O 2 = 2 ✓. Die eerste opsie het 2 O links en net 1 regs. Die tweede skryf suurstofgas as O, maar suurstofgas is diatomies (O₂). Die laaste het 1 Mg links en 2 regs.","en":"2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO: Mg 2 = 2 and O 2 = 2 ✓. The first option has 2 O on the left and only 1 on the right. The second writes oxygen gas as O, but oxygen gas is diatomic (O₂). The last has 1 Mg on the left and 2 on the right."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n hoogoond word ystererts met koolstofmonoksied gereduseer: _Fe₂O₃ + _CO → _Fe + _CO₂. Watter stel koëffisiënte (in volgorde) balanseer die vergelyking?","en":"In a blast furnace iron ore is reduced with carbon monoxide: _Fe₂O₃ + _CO → _Fe + _CO₂. Which set of coefficients (in order) balances the equation?"},"options":[{"af":"1; 1; 2; 1","en":"1; 1; 2; 1"},{"af":"2; 3; 4; 3","en":"2; 3; 4; 3"},{"af":"1; 3; 2; 2","en":"1; 3; 2; 2"},{"af":"1; 3; 2; 3","en":"1; 3; 2; 3"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂: Fe 2 = 2; C 3 = 3; O 3 + 3 = 6 links en 3 × 2 = 6 regs ✓. Met 1; 1; 2; 1 is O 4 teen 2; met 2; 3; 4; 3 is O 9 teen 6; met 1; 3; 2; 2 is C 3 teen 2.","en":"Fe₂O₃ + 3CO → 2Fe + 3CO₂: Fe 2 = 2; C 3 = 3; O 3 + 3 = 6 on the left and 3 × 2 = 6 on the right ✓. With 1; 1; 2; 1, O is 4 vs 2; with 2; 3; 4; 3, O is 9 vs 6; with 1; 3; 2; 2, C is 3 vs 2."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Suiwer water bevat altyd waterstof en suurstof in die massaverhouding 1 : 8. Hoeveel gram suurstof is in 45 g suiwer water? ___ g","en":"Pure water always contains hydrogen and oxygen in the mass ratio 1 : 8. How many grams of oxygen are in 45 g of pure water? ___ g"},"answers":{"af":["40","40 g","40g","40,0","40.0","40,00","40.00"],"en":["40","40 g","40g","40,0","40.0","40,00","40.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Die verhouding 1 : 8 beteken 9 dele altesaam, waarvan 8 dele suurstof is. m(O) = 45 × 8/9 = 40 g (en m(H) = 5 g). As jy 45 × 8 of 45 ÷ 8 bereken, het jy vergeet dat die totaal 9 dele is.","en":"The ratio 1 : 8 means 9 parts in total, of which 8 parts are oxygen. m(O) = 45 × 8/9 = 40 g (and m(H) = 5 g). If you calculate 45 × 8 or 45 ÷ 8, you forgot that the total is 9 parts."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["360","5,63","5"],"en":["360","5.63","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo weeg 5,0 g staalwol (yster), verbrand dit in 'n oop porseleinbakkie en vind dat die produk swaarder as 5,0 g is. Hy sê dit bewys dat die wet van behoud van massa nie altyd geld nie. Watter evaluering van sy stelling is korrek?","en":"Thabo weighs 5.0 g of steel wool (iron), burns it in an open porcelain dish and finds that the product is heavier than 5.0 g. He says this proves that the law of conservation of mass does not always hold. Which evaluation of his statement is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: suurstof uit die lug het met die yster verbind, en die massa van daardie suurstof is nou deel van die produk.","en":"He is wrong: oxygen from the air combined with the iron, and the mass of that oxygen is now part of the product."},{"af":"Hy is reg: die hitte van die vlam het ekstra massa geskep.","en":"He is right: the heat of the flame created extra mass."},{"af":"Hy is reg: die wet geld net vir fisiese veranderinge.","en":"He is right: the law only applies to physical changes."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: sy skaal moet foutief wees, want die massa moes presies 5,0 g gebly het.","en":"He is wrong: his scale must be faulty, because the mass should have stayed exactly 5.0 g."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die bakkie was oop, dus was dit nie 'n geslote sisteem nie. Yster het met suurstof uit die lug gereageer (Fe + O₂ → ysteroksied), en die massa van die suurstof is bygevoeg. As jy die massa van die suurstof wat gereageer het, saam met die yster tel, is die massa behoue. Massa word nooit deur hitte geskep nie, en die wet geld ook vir chemiese veranderinge.","en":"The dish was open, so it was not a closed system. Iron reacted with oxygen from the air (Fe + O₂ → iron oxide), and the mass of the oxygen was added. If you count the mass of the oxygen that reacted together with the iron, mass is conserved. Mass is never created by heat, and the law also applies to chemical changes."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Chemiese reaksies en meganika","en":"Chemical reactions and mechanics"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t3-waterige-oplossings","title":{"af":"Reaksies in waterige oplossings","en":"Reactions in aqueous solution"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kan verduidelik hoe stowwe in water oplos en gelei, presipitasiereaksies en ioontoetse kan uitvoer en interpreteer, en presipitasie-, suur-basis- en redoksreaksies kan herken.","en":"You will be able to explain how substances dissolve in water and conduct, carry out and interpret precipitation reactions and ion tests, and recognise precipitation, acid–base and redox reactions."},"summary":{"af":"## Water as polêre oplosmiddel\n\n- In 'n watermolekule is suurstof meer **elektronegatief** as waterstof, dus word die gedeelde elektrone nader aan die O-atoom getrek. O kry 'n **gedeeltelike negatiewe lading (δ−)** en elke H 'n **gedeeltelike positiewe lading (δ+)**.\n- Die molekule is **hoekig (gebuig)**, dus kanselleer die ladings nie uit nie: water is 'n **polêre molekule**.\n- Daarom los ioniese en polêre stowwe goed in water op.\n\n## Oplos: dissosiasie en ionisasie\n\n**Dissosiasie** is die proses waartydens 'n ioniese verbinding in ione opbreek.\n\n1. Die δ−-kant (O) van die watermolekules trek die **positiewe ione** aan; die δ+-kant (H) trek die **negatiewe ione** aan.\n2. Die ione word uit die kristalrooster losgetrek.\n3. Elke ioon word deur watermolekules omring (**hidrasie**).\n\n- NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)\n- Na_{2}SO_{4}(s) → 2Na^{+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) – 1 mol Na_{2}SO_{4} lewer 3 mol ione.\n\n**Ionisasie** is die proses waartydens ione tydens 'n chemiese reaksie gevorm word, bv. wanneer 'n kovalente stof met water reageer: HCl(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ) → H_{3}O^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq).\n\nNie alle ioniese verbindings is oplosbaar nie. **Onoplosbaar:** AgCl, AgBr, AgI, BaSO_{4}, BaCO_{3}, CaCO_{3}, PbI_{2}. **Oplosbaar:** alle nitrate en alle natrium-, kalium- en ammoniumsoute.\n\n## Elektroliete en geleidingsvermoë\n\n'n **Elektroliet** is 'n stof wat in water oplos en ione vorm, sodat die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei. Die stroom word deur **bewegende ione** gedra, nie deur elektrone nie.\n\n| Tipe | Ione in oplossing | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sterk elektroliet | dissosieer/ioniseer **volledig** – baie ione | NaCl, CuSO_{4}, HCl |\n| Swak elektroliet | ioniseer **gedeeltelik** – min ione | asynsuur (CH_{3}COOH) in asyn |\n| Nie-elektroliet | **geen** ione nie | suiker (sukrose), etanol |\n\nDie **geleidingsvermoë** van 'n oplossing neem toe met 'n hoër **konsentrasie** ione, 'n sterker elektroliet (**tipe stof**) en 'n hoër **temperatuur**.\n\n> **Onthou:** Gedistilleerde water gelei feitlik nie, want dit bevat byna geen ione nie. Kraanwater en damwater gelei wel, want opgeloste soute vorm ione – daarom is 'n haardroër naby die bad so gevaarlik.\n\n## Presipitasiereaksies\n\n'n **Presipitaat** is 'n onoplosbare vaste stof wat vorm wanneer twee oplossings gemeng word. Die ione ruil maats.\n\n- Volledige vergelyking: AgNO_{3}(aq) + NaCl(aq) → AgCl(s) + NaNO_{3}(aq)\n- Netto ioniese vergelyking: Ag^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq) → AgCl(s)\n- **Toeskouerione** (hier Na^{+} en NO_{3}^{−}) bly opgelos en neem nie aan die reaksie deel nie. Hulle word uit die netto ioniese vergelyking weggelaat.\n\n## Toetse vir anione\n\n| Ioon | Voeg by | Positiewe toets |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cl^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **wit** presipitaat (AgCl) wat nie in die suur oplos nie |\n| Br^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **roomkleurige (liggeel)** presipitaat (AgBr) wat nie oplos nie |\n| I^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **geel** presipitaat (AgI) wat nie oplos nie |\n| SO_{4}^{2−} | BaCl_{2}(aq), dan verdunde HNO_{3} | **wit** presipitaat (BaSO_{4}) wat nie in die suur oplos nie |\n| CO_{3}^{2−} | verdunde suur (HCl of HNO_{3}) | **borrels** CO_{2}-gas wat **helder kalkwater melkerig** maak |\n\n- Ba^{2+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) → BaSO_{4}(s)\n- CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) + 2H^{+}(aq) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ)\n- Karbonate vorm **ook** 'n presipitaat met AgNO_{3} en met BaCl_{2} (bv. wit BaCO_{3}). Daarom voeg ons **salpetersuur** by: 'n karbonaatpresipitaat **los op en borrel** (CO_{2}), maar AgCl, AgBr, AgI en BaSO_{4} los **nie** op nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie HCl by die silwernitraattoets gebruik nie. HCl voeg self Cl^{−}-ione by, dus sal 'n wit AgCl-presipitaat vorm al was daar geen chloried in die monster nie.\n\n## Suur-basis- en redoksreaksies\n\n- **Suur-basis-reaksie:** 'n **proton (H^{+})** word van die suur na die basis oorgedra. Suur + basis → sout + water (**neutralisasie**): HCl(aq) + NaOH(aq) → NaCl(aq) + H_{2}O(ℓ); netto: H^{+}(aq) + OH^{−}(aq) → H_{2}O(ℓ). Suur + karbonaat → sout + water + CO_{2} is ook 'n suur-basis-reaksie. Voorbeelde: 'n teensuurmiddel neutraliseer oortollige maagsuur, en boere strooi landboukalk op suur grond.\n- **Redoksreaksie:** **elektrone** word oorgedra. **Oksidasie** is 'n verlies aan elektrone; **reduksie** is 'n wins aan elektrone. Bv. Zn(s) + Cu^{2+}(aq) → Zn^{2+}(aq) + Cu(s): Zn verloor 2 elektrone (word geoksideer) en Cu^{2+} wen 2 elektrone (word gereduseer). 'n Sinkstrook in blou kopersulfaatoplossing word met rooibruin koper bedek en die blou kleur verbleik.\n\n### Hoe herken jy die reaksietipe?\n\n| Tipe | Wat word oorgedra? | Kenteken |\n|---|---|---|\n| Presipitasie | niks – ione ruil maats | twee oplossings (aq) → onoplosbare vaste stof (s) |\n| Suur-basis | H^{+} (protone) | suur + basis → sout + water |\n| Redoks | elektrone | 'n ongebonde element (lading 0) word 'n ioon, of 'n ioon word 'n element |\n\n> **Wenk:** 'n Vaste stof as produk beteken nie outomaties presipitasie nie. In Zn + CuSO_{4} vorm vaste koper omdat Cu^{2+} elektrone wen – dit is redoks.","en":"## Water as a polar solvent\n\n- In a water molecule oxygen is more **electronegative** than hydrogen, so the shared electrons are pulled closer to the O atom. O gets a **partial negative charge (δ−)** and each H a **partial positive charge (δ+)**.\n- The molecule is **angular (bent)**, so the charges do not cancel out: water is a **polar molecule**.\n- That is why ionic and polar substances dissolve well in water.\n\n## Dissolving: dissociation and ionisation\n\n**Dissociation** is the process in which an ionic compound splits into ions.\n\n1. The δ− side (O) of the water molecules attracts the **positive ions**; the δ+ side (H) attracts the **negative ions**.\n2. The ions are pulled out of the crystal lattice.\n3. Each ion is surrounded by water molecules (**hydration**).\n\n- NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)\n- Na_{2}SO_{4}(s) → 2Na^{+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) – 1 mol Na_{2}SO_{4} gives 3 mol of ions.\n\n**Ionisation** is the process in which ions are formed during a chemical reaction, e.g. when a covalent substance reacts with water: HCl(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ) → H_{3}O^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq).\n\nNot all ionic compounds are soluble. **Insoluble:** AgCl, AgBr, AgI, BaSO_{4}, BaCO_{3}, CaCO_{3}, PbI_{2}. **Soluble:** all nitrates and all sodium, potassium and ammonium salts.\n\n## Electrolytes and conductivity\n\nAn **electrolyte** is a substance that dissolves in water and forms ions, so that the solution conducts electricity. The current is carried by **moving ions**, not by electrons.\n\n| Type | Ions in solution | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Strong electrolyte | dissociates/ionises **completely** – many ions | NaCl, CuSO_{4}, HCl |\n| Weak electrolyte | ionises **partially** – few ions | acetic acid (CH_{3}COOH) in vinegar |\n| Non-electrolyte | **no** ions | sugar (sucrose), ethanol |\n\nThe **conductivity** of a solution increases with a higher **concentration** of ions, a stronger electrolyte (**type of substance**) and a higher **temperature**.\n\n> **Remember:** Distilled water hardly conducts, because it contains almost no ions. Tap water and dam water do conduct, because dissolved salts form ions – that is why a hairdryer near the bath is so dangerous.\n\n## Precipitation reactions\n\nA **precipitate** is an insoluble solid that forms when two solutions are mixed. The ions swap partners.\n\n- Full equation: AgNO_{3}(aq) + NaCl(aq) → AgCl(s) + NaNO_{3}(aq)\n- Net ionic equation: Ag^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq) → AgCl(s)\n- **Spectator ions** (here Na^{+} and NO_{3}^{−}) stay dissolved and do not take part in the reaction. They are left out of the net ionic equation.\n\n## Tests for anions\n\n| Ion | Add | Positive test |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cl^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **white** precipitate (AgCl) that does not dissolve in the acid |\n| Br^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **cream (light yellow)** precipitate (AgBr) that does not dissolve |\n| I^{−} | AgNO_{3}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **yellow** precipitate (AgI) that does not dissolve |\n| SO_{4}^{2−} | BaCl_{2}(aq), then dilute HNO_{3} | **white** precipitate (BaSO_{4}) that does not dissolve in the acid |\n| CO_{3}^{2−} | dilute acid (HCl or HNO_{3}) | **bubbles** of CO_{2} gas that turn **clear limewater milky** |\n\n- Ba^{2+}(aq) + SO_{4}^{2−}(aq) → BaSO_{4}(s)\n- CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) + 2H^{+}(aq) → CO_{2}(g) + H_{2}O(ℓ)\n- Carbonates **also** form a precipitate with AgNO_{3} and with BaCl_{2} (e.g. white BaCO_{3}). That is why we add **nitric acid**: a carbonate precipitate **dissolves and fizzes** (CO_{2}), but AgCl, AgBr, AgI and BaSO_{4} do **not** dissolve.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Do not use HCl in the silver nitrate test. HCl adds Cl^{−} ions itself, so a white AgCl precipitate will form even if there was no chloride in the sample.\n\n## Acid–base and redox reactions\n\n- **Acid–base reaction:** a **proton (H^{+})** is transferred from the acid to the base. Acid + base → salt + water (**neutralisation**): HCl(aq) + NaOH(aq) → NaCl(aq) + H_{2}O(ℓ); net: H^{+}(aq) + OH^{−}(aq) → H_{2}O(ℓ). Acid + carbonate → salt + water + CO_{2} is also an acid–base reaction. Examples: an antacid neutralises excess stomach acid, and farmers spread agricultural lime on acidic soil.\n- **Redox reaction:** **electrons** are transferred. **Oxidation** is a loss of electrons; **reduction** is a gain of electrons. E.g. Zn(s) + Cu^{2+}(aq) → Zn^{2+}(aq) + Cu(s): Zn loses 2 electrons (is oxidised) and Cu^{2+} gains 2 electrons (is reduced). A zinc strip in blue copper sulfate solution becomes coated with red-brown copper and the blue colour fades.\n\n### How do you recognise the reaction type?\n\n| Type | What is transferred? | Clue |\n|---|---|---|\n| Precipitation | nothing – ions swap partners | two solutions (aq) → insoluble solid (s) |\n| Acid–base | H^{+} (protons) | acid + base → salt + water |\n| Redox | electrons | an uncombined element (charge 0) becomes an ion, or an ion becomes an element |\n\n> **Tip:** A solid product does not automatically mean precipitation. In Zn + CuSO_{4} solid copper forms because Cu^{2+} gains electrons – that is redox."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Polêre molekule","en":"Polar molecule"},"def":{"af":"'n Molekule met 'n ongelyke ladingsverspreiding: een kant is gedeeltelik negatief (δ−) en die ander kant gedeeltelik positief (δ+), bv. H₂O.","en":"A molecule with an unequal charge distribution: one side is partially negative (δ−) and the other side partially positive (δ+), e.g. H₂O."}},{"term":{"af":"Dissosiasie","en":"Dissociation"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens 'n ioniese verbinding in ione opbreek, bv. NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq).","en":"The process in which an ionic compound splits into ions, e.g. NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq)."}},{"term":{"af":"Ionisasie","en":"Ionisation"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens ione tydens 'n chemiese reaksie gevorm word, bv. wanneer HCl-gas met water reageer om H₃O⁺ en Cl⁻ te vorm.","en":"The process in which ions are formed during a chemical reaction, e.g. when HCl gas reacts with water to form H₃O⁺ and Cl⁻."}},{"term":{"af":"Hidrasie","en":"Hydration"},"def":{"af":"Die proses waartydens opgeloste ione deur watermolekules omring word.","en":"The process in which dissolved ions are surrounded by water molecules."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektroliet","en":"Electrolyte"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat in water oplos en ione vorm, sodat die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei.","en":"A substance that dissolves in water and forms ions, so that the solution conducts electricity."}},{"term":{"af":"Presipitaat","en":"Precipitate"},"def":{"af":"'n Onoplosbare vaste stof wat vorm wanneer twee oplossings gemeng word.","en":"An insoluble solid that forms when two solutions are mixed."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeskouerione","en":"Spectator ions"},"def":{"af":"Ione wat in die oplossing teenwoordig is maar nie aan die reaksie deelneem nie; hulle word uit die netto ioniese vergelyking weggelaat.","en":"Ions that are present in the solution but do not take part in the reaction; they are left out of the net ionic equation."}},{"term":{"af":"Suur-basis-reaksie","en":"Acid–base reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin protone (H⁺-ione) van 'n suur na 'n basis oorgedra word; suur + basis → sout + water.","en":"A reaction in which protons (H⁺ ions) are transferred from an acid to a base; acid + base → salt + water."}},{"term":{"af":"Redoksreaksie","en":"Redox reaction"},"def":{"af":"'n Reaksie waarin elektrone van een stof na 'n ander oorgedra word.","en":"A reaction in which electrons are transferred from one substance to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Oksidasie en reduksie","en":"Oxidation and reduction"},"def":{"af":"Oksidasie is 'n verlies aan elektrone; reduksie is 'n wins aan elektrone.","en":"Oxidation is a loss of electrons; reduction is a gain of electrons."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Sout los in water op","en":"Salt dissolves in water"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik, met verwysing na die watermolekules, wat gebeur wanneer natriumchloried (tafelsout) in water oplos. Skryf 'n vergelyking en verduidelik waarom die oplossing elektrisiteit gelei, terwyl vaste NaCl dit nie doen nie.","en":"Explain, with reference to the water molecules, what happens when sodium chloride (table salt) dissolves in water. Write an equation and explain why the solution conducts electricity, while solid NaCl does not."},"steps":[{"af":"Water is polêr: die O-atoom is δ− en die H-atome is δ+, en die molekule is hoekig.","en":"Water is polar: the O atom is δ− and the H atoms are δ+, and the molecule is angular."},{"af":"Die δ−-O-kante van watermolekules trek die Na^{+}-ione aan, en die δ+-H-kante trek die Cl^{−}-ione aan. Die ione word uit die kristalrooster getrek – dit is **dissosiasie**.","en":"The δ− O sides of water molecules attract the Na^{+} ions, and the δ+ H sides attract the Cl^{−} ions. The ions are pulled out of the crystal lattice – this is **dissociation**."},{"af":"Elke ioon word deur watermolekules omring (hidrasie): NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)","en":"Each ion is surrounded by water molecules (hydration): NaCl(s) → Na^{+}(aq) + Cl^{−}(aq)"},{"af":"In vaste NaCl sit die ione vas in die rooster en kan nie beweeg nie. In die oplossing beweeg die ione vrylik en dra lading, dus gelei die oplossing – NaCl is 'n sterk elektroliet.","en":"In solid NaCl the ions are fixed in the lattice and cannot move. In the solution the ions move freely and carry charge, so the solution conducts – NaCl is a strong electrolyte."}],"answer":{"af":"Die ione dissosieer en word gehidreer: NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq). Die vrye, bewegende ione gelei die stroom.","en":"The ions dissociate and are hydrated: NaCl(s) → Na⁺(aq) + Cl⁻(aq). The free, moving ions conduct the current."}},{"title":{"af":"Presipitasie en die netto ioniese vergelyking","en":"Precipitation and the net ionic equation"},"problem":{"af":"Wanneer kleurlose lood(II)nitraatoplossing, Pb(NO₃)₂(aq), by kleurlose kaliumjodiedoplossing, KI(aq), gevoeg word, vorm 'n helder geel presipitaat van lood(II)jodied. (a) Skryf 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking met toestandsimbole. (b) Skryf die netto ioniese vergelyking. (c) Noem die toeskouerione.","en":"When colourless lead(II) nitrate solution, Pb(NO₃)₂(aq), is added to colourless potassium iodide solution, KI(aq), a bright yellow precipitate of lead(II) iodide forms. (a) Write a balanced equation with state symbols. (b) Write the net ionic equation. (c) Name the spectator ions."},"steps":[{"af":"Die ione ruil maats: Pb^{2+} verbind met I^{−} tot PbI_{2} (twee I^{−} vir elke Pb^{2+}), en K^{+} bly by NO_{3}^{−} as KNO_{3}.","en":"The ions swap partners: Pb^{2+} combines with I^{−} to form PbI_{2} (two I^{−} for each Pb^{2+}), and K^{+} stays with NO_{3}^{−} as KNO_{3}."},{"af":"(a) Pb(NO_{3})_{2}(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI_{2}(s) + 2KNO_{3}(aq). Kontroleer: Pb 1 = 1; N 2 = 2; O 6 = 6; K 2 = 2; I 2 = 2 ✓","en":"(a) Pb(NO_{3})_{2}(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI_{2}(s) + 2KNO_{3}(aq). Check: Pb 1 = 1; N 2 = 2; O 6 = 6; K 2 = 2; I 2 = 2 ✓"},{"af":"(b) Laat die ione wat onveranderd opgelos bly, weg: Pb^{2+}(aq) + 2I^{−}(aq) → PbI_{2}(s). Lading links: +2 + 2(−1) = 0 = lading regs ✓","en":"(b) Leave out the ions that stay dissolved unchanged: Pb^{2+}(aq) + 2I^{−}(aq) → PbI_{2}(s). Charge on the left: +2 + 2(−1) = 0 = charge on the right ✓"},{"af":"(c) K^{+} en NO_{3}^{−} bly opgelos (alle kalium- en nitraatsoute is oplosbaar) – dit is die toeskouerione.","en":"(c) K^{+} and NO_{3}^{−} stay dissolved (all potassium and nitrate salts are soluble) – they are the spectator ions."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Pb(NO₃)₂(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI₂(s) + 2KNO₃(aq); (b) Pb²⁺(aq) + 2I⁻(aq) → PbI₂(s); (c) K⁺ en NO₃⁻","en":"(a) Pb(NO₃)₂(aq) + 2KI(aq) → PbI₂(s) + 2KNO₃(aq); (b) Pb²⁺(aq) + 2I⁻(aq) → PbI₂(s); (c) K⁺ and NO₃⁻"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer drie onbekende oplossings","en":"Identify three unknown solutions"},"problem":{"af":"Drie bottels sonder etikette bevat NaCl(aq), Na₂SO₄(aq) en Na₂CO₃(aq). Jy het verdunde salpetersuur (HNO₃), bariumchloriedoplossing (BaCl₂(aq)) en silwernitraatoplossing (AgNO₃(aq)). Beskryf hoe jy elke oplossing sal identifiseer.","en":"Three unlabelled bottles contain NaCl(aq), Na₂SO₄(aq) and Na₂CO₃(aq). You have dilute nitric acid (HNO₃), barium chloride solution (BaCl₂(aq)) and silver nitrate solution (AgNO₃(aq)). Describe how you would identify each solution."},"steps":[{"af":"Voeg verdunde HNO_{3} by 'n monster van elke oplossing. Die een wat **borrel** (CO_{2}-gas wat kalkwater melkerig maak), is Na_{2}CO_{3}: CO_{3}^{2−} + 2H^{+} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O","en":"Add dilute HNO_{3} to a sample of each solution. The one that **fizzes** (CO_{2} gas that turns limewater milky) is Na_{2}CO_{3}: CO_{3}^{2−} + 2H^{+} → CO_{2} + H_{2}O"},{"af":"Voeg BaCl_{2}(aq) by nuwe monsters van die oorblywende twee. Die een wat 'n **wit presipitaat** gee wat nie in HNO_{3} oplos nie (BaSO_{4}), is Na_{2}SO_{4}.","en":"Add BaCl_{2}(aq) to fresh samples of the remaining two. The one that gives a **white precipitate** that does not dissolve in HNO_{3} (BaSO_{4}) is Na_{2}SO_{4}."},{"af":"Voeg AgNO_{3}(aq) by die laaste oplossing. 'n **Wit presipitaat** (AgCl) wat nie in verdunde HNO_{3} oplos nie, bevestig NaCl: Ag^{+} + Cl^{−} → AgCl(s)","en":"Add AgNO_{3}(aq) to the last solution. A **white precipitate** (AgCl) that does not dissolve in dilute HNO_{3} confirms NaCl: Ag^{+} + Cl^{−} → AgCl(s)"},{"af":"Hoekom die karbonaat eerste? Karbonaat sou ook 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl_{2} en met AgNO_{3} gee. Deur dit eers met suur uit te skakel, voorkom jy verwarring.","en":"Why the carbonate first? Carbonate would also give a white precipitate with BaCl_{2} and with AgNO_{3}. By ruling it out with acid first, you avoid confusion."}],"answer":{"af":"Borrels met suur → Na₂CO₃; wit presipitaat met BaCl₂ → Na₂SO₄; wit presipitaat met AgNO₃ → NaCl","en":"Fizzing with acid → Na₂CO₃; white precipitate with BaCl₂ → Na₂SO₄; white precipitate with AgNO₃ → NaCl"}},{"title":{"af":"Herken die reaksietipe","en":"Recognise the reaction type"},"problem":{"af":"Identifiseer elke reaksie as presipitasie, suur-basis of redoks, en gee 'n rede. (a) Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g); (b) H₂SO₄(aq) + 2KOH(aq) → K₂SO₄(aq) + 2H₂O(ℓ); (c) CaCl₂(aq) + Na₂CO₃(aq) → CaCO₃(s) + 2NaCl(aq)","en":"Identify each reaction as precipitation, acid–base or redox, and give a reason. (a) Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g); (b) H₂SO₄(aq) + 2KOH(aq) → K₂SO₄(aq) + 2H₂O(ℓ); (c) CaCl₂(aq) + Na₂CO₃(aq) → CaCO₃(s) + 2NaCl(aq)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Mg is 'n ongebonde element (lading 0) wat Mg^{2+} word: Mg → Mg^{2+} + 2e^{−} (oksidasie). H^{+} wen elektrone en word H_{2}: 2H^{+} + 2e^{−} → H_{2} (reduksie). Elektrone word oorgedra → **redoks**.","en":"(a) Mg is an uncombined element (charge 0) that becomes Mg^{2+}: Mg → Mg^{2+} + 2e^{−} (oxidation). H^{+} gains electrons and becomes H_{2}: 2H^{+} + 2e^{−} → H_{2} (reduction). Electrons are transferred → **redox**."},{"af":"(b) 'n Suur (H_{2}SO_{4}) en 'n basis (KOH) vorm 'n sout en water. H^{+} word aan OH^{−} oorgedra: H^{+} + OH^{−} → H_{2}O → **suur-basis** (neutralisasie).","en":"(b) An acid (H_{2}SO_{4}) and a base (KOH) form a salt and water. H^{+} is transferred to OH^{−}: H^{+} + OH^{−} → H_{2}O → **acid–base** (neutralisation)."},{"af":"(c) Twee oplossings word gemeng en die ione ruil maats om die onoplosbare CaCO_{3}(s) te vorm: Ca^{2+}(aq) + CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) → CaCO_{3}(s). Geen elektrone of protone word oorgedra nie → **presipitasie**.","en":"(c) Two solutions are mixed and the ions swap partners to form the insoluble CaCO_{3}(s): Ca^{2+}(aq) + CO_{3}^{2−}(aq) → CaCO_{3}(s). No electrons or protons are transferred → **precipitation**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Redoks; (b) suur-basis; (c) presipitasie","en":"(a) Redox; (b) acid–base; (c) precipitation"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is water 'n polêre molekule?","en":"Why is water a polar molecule?"},"options":[{"af":"Waterstof is meer elektronegatief as suurstof, dus is die H-kante negatief.","en":"Hydrogen is more electronegative than oxygen, so the H sides are negative."},{"af":"Water bestaan uit H⁺- en O²⁻-ione.","en":"Water consists of H⁺ and O²⁻ ions."},{"af":"Suurstof is meer elektronegatief as waterstof en die molekule is hoekig, dus is die O-kant δ− en die H-kante δ+.","en":"Oxygen is more electronegative than hydrogen and the molecule is angular, so the O side is δ− and the H sides are δ+."},{"af":"Die molekule is lineêr en die elektrone word eweredig gedeel.","en":"The molecule is linear and the electrons are shared equally."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Suurstof trek die gedeelde elektrone sterker aan (hoër elektronegatiwiteit), dus is O δ− en H δ+. Omdat die molekule hoekig is, kanselleer hierdie ladings nie uit nie. Water is kovalent – dit bestaan nie uit ione nie.","en":"Oxygen attracts the shared electrons more strongly (higher electronegativity), so O is δ− and H is δ+. Because the molecule is angular, these charges do not cancel out. Water is covalent – it does not consist of ions."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke ioon by sy positiewe toets.","en":"Match each ion to its positive test."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Cl⁻","en":"Cl⁻"},"r":{"af":"Wit presipitaat met AgNO₃(aq) wat nie in HNO₃ oplos nie","en":"White precipitate with AgNO₃(aq) that does not dissolve in HNO₃"}},{"l":{"af":"I⁻","en":"I⁻"},"r":{"af":"Geel presipitaat met AgNO₃(aq)","en":"Yellow precipitate with AgNO₃(aq)"}},{"l":{"af":"SO₄²⁻","en":"SO₄²⁻"},"r":{"af":"Wit presipitaat met BaCl₂(aq) wat nie in HNO₃ oplos nie","en":"White precipitate with BaCl₂(aq) that does not dissolve in HNO₃"}},{"l":{"af":"CO₃²⁻","en":"CO₃²⁻"},"r":{"af":"Borrels met verdunde suur; die gas maak kalkwater melkerig","en":"Bubbles with dilute acid; the gas turns limewater milky"}}],"explain":{"af":"Halogeniede gee presipitate met silwernitraat (AgCl wit, AgBr roomkleurig, AgI geel); sulfaat gee wit BaSO₄ met bariumchloried; karbonaat gee CO₂-gas met suur, en CO₂ maak kalkwater melkerig.","en":"Halides give precipitates with silver nitrate (AgCl white, AgBr cream, AgI yellow); sulfate gives white BaSO₄ with barium chloride; carbonate gives CO₂ gas with acid, and CO₂ turns limewater milky."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gedistilleerde water is 'n goeie geleier van elektrisiteit.","en":"Distilled water is a good conductor of electricity."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gedistilleerde water bevat byna geen ione nie, dus gelei dit feitlik nie. Kraanwater gelei wel, omdat opgeloste soute ione vorm.","en":"False. Distilled water contains almost no ions, so it hardly conducts. Tap water does conduct, because dissolved salts form ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat gebeur wanneer kaliumnitraat (KNO₃) in water oplos?","en":"What happens when potassium nitrate (KNO₃) dissolves in water?"},"options":[{"af":"Die KNO₃-molekules versprei tussen die watermolekules.","en":"The KNO₃ molecules spread out between the water molecules."},{"af":"Die K-, N- en O-atome skei van mekaar.","en":"The K, N and O atoms separate from each other."},{"af":"Die verbinding reageer met water om KOH en HNO₃ te vorm.","en":"The compound reacts with water to form KOH and HNO₃."},{"af":"Die K⁺- en NO₃⁻-ione skei en word deur watermolekules omring.","en":"The K⁺ and NO₃⁻ ions separate and are surrounded by water molecules."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"KNO₃ is 'n ioniese verbinding, dus dissosieer dit: KNO₃(s) → K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq), en die ione word gehidreer. Ioniese verbindings bestaan nie uit molekules nie, die nitraatioon (NO₃⁻) bly as een eenheid bymekaar, en daar vorm geen nuwe stowwe nie.","en":"KNO₃ is an ionic compound, so it dissociates: KNO₃(s) → K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq), and the ions are hydrated. Ionic compounds do not consist of molecules, the nitrate ion (NO₃⁻) stays together as one unit, and no new substances form."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kant van 'n watermolekule word na 'n Cl⁻-ioon in oplossing aangetrek?","en":"Which side of a water molecule is attracted to a Cl⁻ ion in solution?"},"options":[{"af":"Die waterstofkant (δ+)","en":"The hydrogen side (δ+)"},{"af":"Die suurstofkant (δ−)","en":"The oxygen side (δ−)"},{"af":"Albei kante ewe veel","en":"Both sides equally"},{"af":"Geen kant nie, want water is nie-polêr","en":"Neither side, because water is non-polar"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Teenoorgestelde ladings trek mekaar aan: die negatiewe Cl⁻-ioon trek die gedeeltelik positiewe (δ+) H-kant van die watermolekule aan. Die δ−-O-kant word na positiewe ione soos Na⁺ aangetrek.","en":"Opposite charges attract: the negative Cl⁻ ion attracts the partially positive (δ+) H side of the water molecule. The δ− O side is attracted to positive ions such as Na⁺."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suiker (sukrose) los in water op, maar die oplossing gelei nie elektrisiteit nie, omdat suiker nie ione in water vorm nie.","en":"Sugar (sucrose) dissolves in water, but the solution does not conduct electricity, because sugar does not form ions in water."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Suiker is 'n kovalente stof wat as heel molekules oplos – dit dissosieer of ioniseer nie. Sonder vrye ione kan die oplossing nie gelei nie, dus is suiker 'n nie-elektroliet.","en":"True. Sugar is a covalent substance that dissolves as whole molecules – it does not dissociate or ionise. Without free ions the solution cannot conduct, so sugar is a non-electrolyte."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vier oplossings het almal dieselfde konsentrasie en temperatuur. Watter een gelei elektrisiteit die swakste?","en":"Four solutions all have the same concentration and temperature. Which one conducts electricity the worst?"},"options":[{"af":"NaCl(aq)","en":"NaCl(aq)"},{"af":"CH₃COOH(aq) (asynsuur)","en":"CH₃COOH(aq) (acetic acid)"},{"af":"HCl(aq)","en":"HCl(aq)"},{"af":"CuSO₄(aq)","en":"CuSO₄(aq)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Asynsuur is 'n swak elektroliet: dit ioniseer net gedeeltelik, dus is daar die minste ione in oplossing. NaCl en CuSO₄ dissosieer volledig en HCl ioniseer volledig – dit is sterk elektroliete.","en":"Acetic acid is a weak electrolyte: it ionises only partially, so there are the fewest ions in solution. NaCl and CuSO₄ dissociate completely and HCl ionises completely – they are strong electrolytes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Silwernitraatoplossing word by kaliumbromiedoplossing gevoeg. Die chemiese formule van die roomkleurige presipitaat is ___.","en":"Silver nitrate solution is added to potassium bromide solution. The chemical formula of the cream-coloured precipitate is ___."},"answers":{"af":["AgBr","AgBr(s)","silwerbromied"],"en":["AgBr","AgBr(s)","silver bromide"]},"explain":{"af":"Die ione ruil maats: Ag⁺ + Br⁻ → AgBr(s). KNO₃ bly opgelos, want alle kalium- en nitraatsoute is oplosbaar.","en":"The ions swap partners: Ag⁺ + Br⁻ → AgBr(s). KNO₃ stays dissolved, because all potassium and nitrate salts are soluble."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["KNO₃","AgNO₃","KBr"],"en":["KNO₃","AgNO₃","KBr"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1 mol CaCl₂ dissosieer volledig in water. Hoeveel mol ione word gevorm? ___ mol","en":"1 mol of CaCl₂ dissociates completely in water. How many moles of ions are formed? ___ mol"},"answers":{"af":["3","3 mol","drie"],"en":["3","3 mol","three"]},"explain":{"af":"CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + 2Cl⁻(aq): 1 mol Ca²⁺ + 2 mol Cl⁻ = 3 mol ione. Onthou die 2 voor Cl⁻ – die onderskrif in CaCl₂ beteken twee chloriedione.","en":"CaCl₂(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + 2Cl⁻(aq): 1 mol Ca²⁺ + 2 mol Cl⁻ = 3 mol of ions. Remember the 2 in front of Cl⁻ – the subscript in CaCl₂ means two chloride ions."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","1","4"],"en":["2","1","4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die netto ioniese vergelyking vir die reaksie AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)?","en":"What is the net ionic equation for the reaction AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)?"},"options":[{"af":"K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq) → KNO₃(s)","en":"K⁺(aq) + NO₃⁻(aq) → KNO₃(s)"},{"af":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(aq)","en":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(aq)"},{"af":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(s)","en":"Ag⁺(aq) + I⁻(aq) → AgI(s)"},{"af":"AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)","en":"AgNO₃(aq) + KI(aq) → AgI(s) + KNO₃(aq)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Net die ione wat die presipitaat vorm, verskyn in die netto ioniese vergelyking, en die presipitaat kry (s). K⁺ en NO₃⁻ is toeskouerione – KNO₃ is oplosbaar. AgI(aq) is verkeerd, want AgI is 'n onoplosbare vaste stof, en die laaste opsie is die volledige vergelyking, nie die netto ioniese vergelyking nie.","en":"Only the ions that form the precipitate appear in the net ionic equation, and the precipitate gets (s). K⁺ and NO₃⁻ are spectator ions – KNO₃ is soluble. AgI(aq) is wrong, because AgI is an insoluble solid, and the last option is the full equation, not the net ionic equation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die reaksie BaCl₂(aq) + K₂SO₄(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2KCl(aq) is die toeskouerione K⁺ en ___.","en":"In the reaction BaCl₂(aq) + K₂SO₄(aq) → BaSO₄(s) + 2KCl(aq) the spectator ions are K⁺ and ___."},"answers":{"af":["Cl⁻","Cl-","Cl−","Cl","chloried","chloriedioon","chloriedione"],"en":["Cl⁻","Cl-","Cl−","Cl","chloride","chloride ion","chloride ions"]},"explain":{"af":"Ba²⁺ en SO₄²⁻ vorm die presipitaat BaSO₄(s): Ba²⁺(aq) + SO₄²⁻(aq) → BaSO₄(s). K⁺ en Cl⁻ bly opgelos as KCl(aq) en neem nie deel nie – hulle is die toeskouerione.","en":"Ba²⁺ and SO₄²⁻ form the precipitate BaSO₄(s): Ba²⁺(aq) + SO₄²⁻(aq) → BaSO₄(s). K⁺ and Cl⁻ stay dissolved as KCl(aq) and do not take part – they are the spectator ions."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Ba²⁺","SO₄²⁻","BaSO₄"],"en":["Ba²⁺","SO₄²⁻","BaSO₄"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die reaksie Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s) is 'n voorbeeld van ...","en":"The reaction Fe(s) + CuSO₄(aq) → FeSO₄(aq) + Cu(s) is an example of ..."},"options":[{"af":"'n presipitasiereaksie, omdat 'n vaste stof vorm.","en":"a precipitation reaction, because a solid forms."},{"af":"'n redoksreaksie, omdat Fe elektrone verloor en Cu²⁺ elektrone wen.","en":"a redox reaction, because Fe loses electrons and Cu²⁺ gains electrons."},{"af":"'n suur-basis-reaksie, omdat 'n sout vorm.","en":"an acid–base reaction, because a salt forms."},{"af":"'n ontbindingsreaksie, omdat CuSO₄ opbreek.","en":"a decomposition reaction, because CuSO₄ breaks up."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Fe (lading 0) word Fe²⁺: Fe → Fe²⁺ + 2e⁻ (oksidasie). Cu²⁺ word Cu (lading 0): Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu (reduksie). Elektrone word oorgedra, dus is dit redoks. Die vaste koper vorm nie deur ione wat maats ruil nie, en geen protone word oorgedra nie.","en":"Fe (charge 0) becomes Fe²⁺: Fe → Fe²⁺ + 2e⁻ (oxidation). Cu²⁺ becomes Cu (charge 0): Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu (reduction). Electrons are transferred, so it is redox. The solid copper does not form by ions swapping partners, and no protons are transferred."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kleurlose oplossing gee 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl₂(aq). Wanneer verdunde HNO₃ bygevoeg word, los die presipitaat op en borrels vorm. Die oplossing bevat ___-ione.","en":"A colourless solution gives a white precipitate with BaCl₂(aq). When dilute HNO₃ is added, the precipitate dissolves and bubbles form. The solution contains ___ ions."},"answers":{"af":["karbonaat","karbonaatione","karbonaatioon","CO₃²⁻","CO3 2-","CO32-","CO3^2-","CO₃","CO3","carbonate"],"en":["carbonate","carbonate ions","carbonate ion","CO₃²⁻","CO3 2-","CO32-","CO3^2-","CO₃","CO3","karbonaat"]},"explain":{"af":"Sulfaat én karbonaat gee albei 'n wit presipitaat met BaCl₂. BaSO₄ los nie in salpetersuur op nie, maar BaCO₃ los op en vorm CO₂-borrels: BaCO₃(s) + 2H⁺(aq) → Ba²⁺(aq) + CO₂(g) + H₂O(ℓ). Dus is dit karbonaat.","en":"Sulfate and carbonate both give a white precipitate with BaCl₂. BaSO₄ does not dissolve in nitric acid, but BaCO₃ dissolves and forms CO₂ bubbles: BaCO₃(s) + 2H⁺(aq) → Ba²⁺(aq) + CO₂(g) + H₂O(ℓ). So it is carbonate."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sulfaat","chloried","nitraat"],"en":["sulfate","chloride","nitrate"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder toets 'n onbekende oplossing vir chloriedione. Sy voeg AgNO₃(aq) by en kry 'n wit presipitaat. Om seker te maak dat dit nie 'n karbonaat is nie, voeg sy daarna verdunde soutsuur (HCl) in plaas van salpetersuur by. Watter evaluering van haar metode is korrek?","en":"A learner tests an unknown solution for chloride ions. She adds AgNO₃(aq) and gets a white precipitate. To make sure it is not a carbonate, she then adds dilute hydrochloric acid (HCl) instead of nitric acid. Which evaluation of her method is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die metode is geldig, want enige suur sal 'n karbonaatpresipitaat oplos.","en":"The method is valid, because any acid will dissolve a carbonate precipitate."},{"af":"Die metode is ongeldig, want HCl los AgCl op.","en":"The method is invalid, because HCl dissolves AgCl."},{"af":"Die metode is geldig, want HCl is 'n sterker suur en gee duideliker resultate.","en":"The method is valid, because HCl is a stronger acid and gives clearer results."},{"af":"Die metode is ongeldig, want HCl voeg self Cl⁻-ione by, sodat AgCl in elk geval vorm en 'n wit presipitaat niks bewys nie.","en":"The method is invalid, because HCl adds Cl⁻ ions itself, so AgCl forms anyway and a white precipitate proves nothing."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Cl⁻-ione uit die HCl reageer met die oortollige Ag⁺ en vorm wit AgCl, selfs al het die monster geen chloried bevat nie (bv. as dit 'n karbonaat was). Die toets moet met salpetersuur gedoen word, want nitrate is oplosbaar en voeg geen ione by wat 'n presipitaat met Ag⁺ vorm nie. AgCl los nie in HCl op nie.","en":"The Cl⁻ ions from the HCl react with the excess Ag⁺ and form white AgCl, even if the sample contained no chloride (e.g. if it was a carbonate). The test must be done with nitric acid, because nitrates are soluble and add no ions that form a precipitate with Ag⁺. AgCl does not dissolve in HCl."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-molbegrip","title":{"af":"Kwantitatiewe aspekte van chemiese verandering","en":"Quantitative aspects of chemical change"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal met die mol kan reken: massa, aantal deeltjies, gasvolume en konsentrasie omskakel, empiriese formules en kristalwater bepaal en molverhoudings in reaksies gebruik.","en":"You will be able to calculate with the mole: convert between mass, number of particles, gas volume and concentration, determine empirical formulae and water of crystallisation, and use mole ratios in reactions."},"summary":{"af":"## Die mol en Avogadro se getal\n\nChemici kan nie atome een vir een tel nie – hulle is te klein en daar is te veel. Daarom tel ons deeltjies in \"pakke\" van 6,02 × 10²³, net soos eiers in dosyne.\n\n- Die **mol** is die SI-eenheid vir **hoeveelheid stof** (simbool n).\n- **Een mol** van 'n stof is die hoeveelheid stof wat dieselfde aantal deeltjies bevat as wat daar atome in 12 g koolstof-12 is.\n- Daardie getal is **Avogadro se getal**: N_{A} = 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies per mol.\n- Die deeltjies kan atome, molekules of ione wees – sê altyd watter een jy bedoel.\n\n> **Wenk:** As jy elke sekonde een deeltjie tel, sal dit jou ongeveer 1,9 × 10¹⁶ jaar neem om een mol te tel – meer as 'n miljoen keer die ouderdom van die heelal!\n\n## Molêre massa\n\n**Molêre massa (M)** is die massa van een mol van 'n stof, gemeet in g·mol⁻¹. Die relatiewe atoommassa op die periodieke tabel, in gram, is een mol atome: 12 g C en 24 g Mg bevat elk 6,02 × 10²³ atome.\n\nTel die relatiewe atoommassas volgens die formule bymekaar:\n\n- M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CaCO₃) = 40 + 12 + 3(16) = 100 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CuSO₄·5H₂O) = 63,5 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 249,5 g·mol⁻¹\n\nVir molekules (kovalente stowwe) praat ons van **relatiewe molekulêre massa** en vir ioniese verbindings van **relatiewe formulemassa**. Dit het geen eenheid nie. Molêre massa het dieselfde getalwaarde, maar met die eenheid g·mol⁻¹.\n\n## Die formules wat jy moet ken\n\n| Formule | Gebruik | Eenhede |\n|---|---|---|\n| n = [[m/M]] | massa ↔ mol | m in g, M in g·mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[N/N_{A}]] | aantal deeltjies ↔ mol | N_{A} = 6,02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[V/V_{m}]] | gasvolume by STD ↔ mol | V in dm³, V_{m} = 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ |\n| c = [[n/V]] = [[m/MV]] | konsentrasie | c in mol·dm⁻³, V in dm³ |\n\n### Molêre gasvolume\n\nEen mol van **enige gas** beslaan 22,4 dm³ by STD (standaardtemperatuur en -druk: 0 °C of 273 K en 101,3 kPa). Dit geld **net vir gasse** – nie vir vloeistowwe of vaste stowwe nie.\n\n### Konsentrasie\n\n**Konsentrasie** is die hoeveelheid opgeloste stof per kubieke desimeter (liter) oplossing. Die volume moet in dm³ wees: 1 dm³ = 1 L = 1 000 cm³, dus deel cm³ deur 1 000.\n\n## Persentasiesamestelling\n\n% element = [[aantal atome × A_{r}/M van verbinding]] × 100\n\nVoorbeeld: % O in H₂O = [[16/18]] × 100 = 88,89 %.\n\n## Empiriese en molekulêre formule\n\n- **Empiriese formule:** die eenvoudigste positiewe heelgetalverhouding van atome in 'n verbinding.\n- **Molekulêre formule:** die werklike aantal atome van elke soort in 'n molekuul.\n\nGlukose het die molekulêre formule C₆H₁₂O₆ en die empiriese formule CH₂O.\n\n**Metode (van persentasies):**\n\n1. Neem 100 g aan, sodat elke persentasie 'n massa in gram word.\n2. Bereken n = [[m/M]] vir elke element.\n3. Deel almal deur die kleinste n.\n4. Kry jy iets soos 1,5 of 1,33? Vermenigvuldig almal met 2 of 3 tot jy heelgetalle het.\n5. Molekulêre formule: faktor = [[M(molekulêr)/M(empiries)]]; vermenigvuldig elke onderskrif met die faktor.\n\n## Kristalwater\n\nSommige soute bevat watermolekules in hul kristalstruktuur – dit is **kristalwater**. Blou kopersulfaat, CuSO₄·5H₂O, word met verhitting wit, watervrye CuSO₄ as die water verdamp.\n\nOm x in 'n gehidreerde sout (sout·xH₂O) te bepaal:\n\n1. m(water) = m(gehidreerde sout) − m(watervrye sout)\n2. n(watervrye sout) = [[m/M]] en n(H₂O) = [[m/18]]\n3. x = [[n(H₂O)/n(sout)]]\n\n## Stoïgiometrie: berekeninge met molverhoudings\n\nDie koëffisiënte in 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking gee die **molverhouding**, nie die massaverhouding nie. In 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO reageer 2 mol Mg met 1 mol O₂ om 2 mol MgO te vorm.\n\n1. Skryf die gebalanseerde vergelyking.\n2. Skakel die gegewe hoeveelheid om na mol.\n3. Gebruik die molverhouding om die mol van die gevraagde stof te kry.\n4. Skakel om na wat gevra word (massa, gasvolume, aantal deeltjies of konsentrasie).\n\n> **Algemene foute:** cm³ nie na dm³ omgeskakel nie; molekules en atome verwar (1 mol H₂O bevat 3 mol atome); 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ vir 'n vloeistof of vaste stof gebruik; massas in plaas van mol met die molverhouding vermenigvuldig; 1,5 in 'n empiriese formule na 2 afgerond in plaas daarvan om met 2 te vermenigvuldig.","en":"## The mole and Avogadro's number\n\nChemists cannot count atoms one by one – they are too small and there are too many. So we count particles in \"packs\" of 6.02 × 10²³, just like eggs in dozens.\n\n- The **mole** is the SI unit for **amount of substance** (symbol n).\n- **One mole** of a substance is the amount of substance having the same number of particles as there are atoms in 12 g carbon-12.\n- That number is **Avogadro's number**: N_{A} = 6.02 × 10²³ particles per mole.\n- The particles can be atoms, molecules or ions – always say which one you mean.\n\n> **Tip:** If you counted one particle every second, it would take you about 1.9 × 10¹⁶ years to count one mole – more than a million times the age of the universe!\n\n## Molar mass\n\n**Molar mass (M)** is the mass of one mole of a substance, measured in g·mol⁻¹. The relative atomic mass on the periodic table, in grams, is one mole of atoms: 12 g C and 24 g Mg each contain 6.02 × 10²³ atoms.\n\nAdd up the relative atomic masses according to the formula:\n\n- M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CaCO₃) = 40 + 12 + 3(16) = 100 g·mol⁻¹\n- M(CuSO₄·5H₂O) = 63.5 + 32 + 4(16) + 5(18) = 249.5 g·mol⁻¹\n\nFor molecules (covalent substances) we speak of **relative molecular mass** and for ionic compounds of **relative formula mass**. These have no unit. Molar mass has the same numerical value, but with the unit g·mol⁻¹.\n\n## The formulae you must know\n\n| Formula | Use | Units |\n|---|---|---|\n| n = [[m/M]] | mass ↔ moles | m in g, M in g·mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[N/N_{A}]] | number of particles ↔ moles | N_{A} = 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹ |\n| n = [[V/V_{m}]] | gas volume at STP ↔ moles | V in dm³, V_{m} = 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ |\n| c = [[n/V]] = [[m/MV]] | concentration | c in mol·dm⁻³, V in dm³ |\n\n### Molar gas volume\n\nOne mole of **any gas** occupies 22.4 dm³ at STP (standard temperature and pressure: 0 °C or 273 K and 101.3 kPa). This applies **only to gases** – not to liquids or solids.\n\n### Concentration\n\n**Concentration** is the amount of solute per cubic decimetre (litre) of solution. The volume must be in dm³: 1 dm³ = 1 L = 1 000 cm³, so divide cm³ by 1 000.\n\n## Percentage composition\n\n% element = [[number of atoms × A_{r}/M of compound]] × 100\n\nExample: % O in H₂O = [[16/18]] × 100 = 88.89 %.\n\n## Empirical and molecular formula\n\n- **Empirical formula:** the simplest positive integer ratio of atoms present in a compound.\n- **Molecular formula:** the actual number of atoms of each type in a molecule.\n\nGlucose has the molecular formula C₆H₁₂O₆ and the empirical formula CH₂O.\n\n**Method (from percentages):**\n\n1. Assume 100 g, so that each percentage becomes a mass in grams.\n2. Calculate n = [[m/M]] for each element.\n3. Divide all of them by the smallest n.\n4. Do you get something like 1.5 or 1.33? Multiply all of them by 2 or 3 until you have whole numbers.\n5. Molecular formula: factor = [[M(molecular)/M(empirical)]]; multiply every subscript by the factor.\n\n## Water of crystallisation\n\nSome salts contain water molecules in their crystal structure – this is **water of crystallisation**. Blue copper sulfate, CuSO₄·5H₂O, turns into white, anhydrous CuSO₄ when heated as the water evaporates.\n\nTo determine x in a hydrated salt (salt·xH₂O):\n\n1. m(water) = m(hydrated salt) − m(anhydrous salt)\n2. n(anhydrous salt) = [[m/M]] and n(H₂O) = [[m/18]]\n3. x = [[n(H₂O)/n(salt)]]\n\n## Stoichiometry: calculations with mole ratios\n\nThe coefficients in a balanced equation give the **mole ratio**, not the mass ratio. In 2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO, 2 mol Mg reacts with 1 mol O₂ to form 2 mol MgO.\n\n1. Write the balanced equation.\n2. Convert the given quantity to moles.\n3. Use the mole ratio to get the moles of the substance asked for.\n4. Convert to what is asked (mass, gas volume, number of particles or concentration).\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not converting cm³ to dm³; confusing molecules and atoms (1 mol H₂O contains 3 mol atoms); using 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ for a liquid or solid; multiplying masses instead of moles by the mole ratio; rounding 1.5 in an empirical formula to 2 instead of multiplying by 2."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mol","en":"Mole"},"def":{"af":"Die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof. Een mol is die hoeveelheid stof wat dieselfde aantal deeltjies bevat as wat daar atome in 12 g koolstof-12 is.","en":"The SI unit for amount of substance. One mole is the amount of substance having the same number of particles as there are atoms in 12 g carbon-12."}},{"term":{"af":"Avogadro se getal (N_A)","en":"Avogadro's number (N_A)"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal deeltjies in een mol van 'n stof: 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies per mol.","en":"The number of particles in one mole of a substance: 6.02 × 10²³ particles per mole."}},{"term":{"af":"Molêre massa (M)","en":"Molar mass (M)"},"def":{"af":"Die massa van een mol van 'n stof, gemeet in g·mol⁻¹.","en":"The mass of one mole of a substance, measured in g·mol⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Molêre gasvolume (V_m)","en":"Molar gas volume (V_m)"},"def":{"af":"Die volume wat een mol van enige gas beslaan: 22,4 dm³ by STD (0 °C / 273 K en 101,3 kPa).","en":"The volume occupied by one mole of any gas: 22.4 dm³ at STP (0 °C / 273 K and 101.3 kPa)."}},{"term":{"af":"Konsentrasie (c)","en":"Concentration (c)"},"def":{"af":"Die hoeveelheid opgeloste stof per kubieke desimeter (liter) oplossing: c = n/V, in mol·dm⁻³.","en":"The amount of solute per cubic decimetre (litre) of solution: c = n/V, in mol·dm⁻³."}},{"term":{"af":"Persentasiesamestelling","en":"Percentage composition"},"def":{"af":"Die persentasie van die massa van 'n verbinding wat deur elke element bygedra word.","en":"The percentage of the mass of a compound contributed by each element."}},{"term":{"af":"Empiriese formule","en":"Empirical formula"},"def":{"af":"Die eenvoudigste positiewe heelgetalverhouding van atome in 'n verbinding.","en":"The simplest positive integer ratio of atoms present in a compound."}},{"term":{"af":"Molekulêre formule","en":"Molecular formula"},"def":{"af":"Die werklike aantal atome van elke soort in 'n molekuul.","en":"The actual number of atoms of each type in a molecule."}},{"term":{"af":"Kristalwater","en":"Water of crystallisation"},"def":{"af":"Watermolekules wat deel van die kristalstruktuur van 'n sout is, bv. die 5H₂O in CuSO₄·5H₂O.","en":"Water molecules that form part of the crystal structure of a salt, e.g. the 5H₂O in CuSO₄·5H₂O."}},{"term":{"af":"Molverhouding","en":"Mole ratio"},"def":{"af":"Die verhouding waarin stowwe in mol reageer en vorm, gegee deur die koëffisiënte in 'n gebalanseerde vergelyking.","en":"The ratio in moles in which substances react and form, given by the coefficients in a balanced equation."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Van massa na mol, molekules en atome","en":"From mass to moles, molecules and atoms"},"problem":{"af":"Na rugbyoefening drink jy 'n sluk water van 9 g. Bereken (a) die hoeveelheid stof (mol) water, (b) die aantal watermolekules en (c) die totale aantal atome in die sluk.","en":"After rugby practice you drink a sip of water of 9 g. Calculate (a) the amount of substance (moles) of water, (b) the number of water molecules and (c) the total number of atoms in the sip."},"steps":[{"af":"Molêre massa: M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹","en":"Molar mass: M(H₂O) = 2(1) + 16 = 18 g·mol⁻¹"},{"af":"(a) n = [[m/M]] = [[9/18]] = 0,5 mol","en":"(a) n = [[m/M]] = [[9/18]] = 0.5 mol"},{"af":"(b) N = n × N_{A} = 0,5 × 6,02 × 10²³ = 3,01 × 10²³ molekules","en":"(b) N = n × N_{A} = 0.5 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 3.01 × 10²³ molecules"},{"af":"(c) Elke H₂O-molekule bevat 3 atome (2 H + 1 O), dus is die aantal atome = 3 × 3,01 × 10²³ = 9,03 × 10²³ atome","en":"(c) Each H₂O molecule contains 3 atoms (2 H + 1 O), so the number of atoms = 3 × 3.01 × 10²³ = 9.03 × 10²³ atoms"}],"answer":{"af":"n = 0,5 mol; 3,01 × 10²³ molekules; 9,03 × 10²³ atome","en":"n = 0.5 mol; 3.01 × 10²³ molecules; 9.03 × 10²³ atoms"}},{"title":{"af":"Konsentrasie, molverhouding en gasvolume","en":"Concentration, mole ratio and gas volume"},"problem":{"af":"Magnesiumlint reageer met 100 cm³ soutsuur met 'n konsentrasie van 0,5 mol·dm⁻³ volgens: Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g). Al die suur reageer. Bereken (a) die hoeveelheid stof HCl, (b) die volume H₂-gas wat by STD vorm en (c) die massa magnesium wat reageer.","en":"Magnesium ribbon reacts with 100 cm³ of hydrochloric acid with a concentration of 0.5 mol·dm⁻³ according to: Mg(s) + 2HCl(aq) → MgCl₂(aq) + H₂(g). All the acid reacts. Calculate (a) the amount of substance of HCl, (b) the volume of H₂ gas formed at STP and (c) the mass of magnesium that reacts."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel die volume om na dm³: V = [[100/1 000]] = 0,1 dm³","en":"Convert the volume to dm³: V = [[100/1 000]] = 0.1 dm³"},{"af":"(a) n(HCl) = c × V = 0,5 × 0,1 = 0,05 mol","en":"(a) n(HCl) = c × V = 0.5 × 0.1 = 0.05 mol"},{"af":"(b) Molverhouding HCl : H₂ = 2 : 1, dus n(H₂) = [[0,05/2]] = 0,025 mol. V = n × V_{m} = 0,025 × 22,4 = 0,56 dm³","en":"(b) Mole ratio HCl : H₂ = 2 : 1, so n(H₂) = [[0.05/2]] = 0.025 mol. V = n × V_{m} = 0.025 × 22.4 = 0.56 dm³"},{"af":"(c) Molverhouding Mg : HCl = 1 : 2, dus n(Mg) = 0,025 mol. m = n × M = 0,025 × 24 = 0,6 g","en":"(c) Mole ratio Mg : HCl = 1 : 2, so n(Mg) = 0.025 mol. m = n × M = 0.025 × 24 = 0.6 g"}],"answer":{"af":"n(HCl) = 0,05 mol; V(H₂) = 0,56 dm³; m(Mg) = 0,6 g","en":"n(HCl) = 0.05 mol; V(H₂) = 0.56 dm³; m(Mg) = 0.6 g"}},{"title":{"af":"Empiriese en molekulêre formule","en":"Empirical and molecular formula"},"problem":{"af":"Die suiker in druiwe bestaan uit 40 % koolstof, 6,67 % waterstof en 53,33 % suurstof (volgens massa). Die molêre massa is 180 g·mol⁻¹. Bepaal (a) die empiriese formule en (b) die molekulêre formule.","en":"The sugar in grapes consists of 40% carbon, 6.67% hydrogen and 53.33% oxygen (by mass). The molar mass is 180 g·mol⁻¹. Determine (a) the empirical formula and (b) the molecular formula."},"steps":[{"af":"Neem 100 g aan: m(C) = 40 g, m(H) = 6,67 g, m(O) = 53,33 g","en":"Assume 100 g: m(C) = 40 g, m(H) = 6.67 g, m(O) = 53.33 g"},{"af":"n(C) = [[40/12]] = 3,33 mol; n(H) = [[6,67/1]] = 6,67 mol; n(O) = [[53,33/16]] = 3,33 mol","en":"n(C) = [[40/12]] = 3.33 mol; n(H) = [[6.67/1]] = 6.67 mol; n(O) = [[53.33/16]] = 3.33 mol"},{"af":"Deel deur die kleinste (3,33): C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1. (a) Empiriese formule = CH₂O","en":"Divide by the smallest (3.33): C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1. (a) Empirical formula = CH₂O"},{"af":"M(CH₂O) = 12 + 2(1) + 16 = 30 g·mol⁻¹. Faktor = [[180/30]] = 6","en":"M(CH₂O) = 12 + 2(1) + 16 = 30 g·mol⁻¹. Factor = [[180/30]] = 6"},{"af":"(b) Vermenigvuldig elke onderskrif met 6: molekulêre formule = C₆H₁₂O₆ (glukose)","en":"(b) Multiply every subscript by 6: molecular formula = C₆H₁₂O₆ (glucose)"}],"answer":{"af":"Empiriese formule CH₂O; molekulêre formule C₆H₁₂O₆","en":"Empirical formula CH₂O; molecular formula C₆H₁₂O₆"}},{"title":{"af":"Kristalwater in Engelse sout","en":"Water of crystallisation in Epsom salt"},"problem":{"af":"Engelse sout (MgSO₄·xH₂O) word gebruik om seer spiere ná 'n rugbywedstryd in te week. 'n Leerder verhit 4,92 g van die gehidreerde sout totdat al die kristalwater verdamp het. 2,40 g watervrye MgSO₄ bly oor. Bepaal die waarde van x.","en":"Epsom salt (MgSO₄·xH₂O) is used to soak sore muscles after a rugby match. A learner heats 4.92 g of the hydrated salt until all the water of crystallisation has evaporated. 2.40 g of anhydrous MgSO₄ remains. Determine the value of x."},"steps":[{"af":"m(H₂O) = m(gehidreerd) − m(watervry) = 4,92 − 2,40 = 2,52 g","en":"m(H₂O) = m(hydrated) − m(anhydrous) = 4.92 − 2.40 = 2.52 g"},{"af":"M(MgSO₄) = 24 + 32 + 4(16) = 120 g·mol⁻¹, dus n(MgSO₄) = [[2,40/120]] = 0,02 mol","en":"M(MgSO₄) = 24 + 32 + 4(16) = 120 g·mol⁻¹, so n(MgSO₄) = [[2.40/120]] = 0.02 mol"},{"af":"n(H₂O) = [[2,52/18]] = 0,14 mol","en":"n(H₂O) = [[2.52/18]] = 0.14 mol"},{"af":"x = [[n(H₂O)/n(MgSO₄)]] = [[0,14/0,02]] = 7, dus is die formule MgSO₄·7H₂O","en":"x = [[n(H₂O)/n(MgSO₄)]] = [[0.14/0.02]] = 7, so the formula is MgSO₄·7H₂O"}],"answer":{"af":"x = 7 (MgSO₄·7H₂O)","en":"x = 7 (MgSO₄·7H₂O)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof?","en":"What is the SI unit for amount of substance?"},"options":[{"af":"kilogram (kg)","en":"kilogram (kg)"},{"af":"gram per mol (g·mol⁻¹)","en":"gram per mole (g·mol⁻¹)"},{"af":"mol","en":"mole (mol)"},{"af":"kubieke desimeter (dm³)","en":"cubic decimetre (dm³)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mol is die SI-eenheid vir hoeveelheid stof (n). Kilogram is die eenheid van massa, g·mol⁻¹ is die eenheid van molêre massa en dm³ is 'n volume-eenheid.","en":"The mole is the SI unit for amount of substance (n). Kilogram is the unit of mass, g·mol⁻¹ is the unit of molar mass and dm³ is a unit of volume."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by sy eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to its unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Molêre massa","en":"Molar mass"},"r":{"af":"g·mol⁻¹","en":"g·mol⁻¹"}},{"l":{"af":"Konsentrasie","en":"Concentration"},"r":{"af":"mol·dm⁻³","en":"mol·dm⁻³"}},{"l":{"af":"Molêre gasvolume","en":"Molar gas volume"},"r":{"af":"dm³·mol⁻¹","en":"dm³·mol⁻¹"}},{"l":{"af":"Hoeveelheid stof","en":"Amount of substance"},"r":{"af":"mol","en":"mol"}}],"explain":{"af":"Molêre massa is gram per mol (g·mol⁻¹); konsentrasie is mol per dm³ oplossing (mol·dm⁻³); molêre gasvolume is dm³ per mol (dm³·mol⁻¹); hoeveelheid stof word in mol gemeet.","en":"Molar mass is grams per mole (g·mol⁻¹); concentration is moles per dm³ of solution (mol·dm⁻³); molar gas volume is dm³ per mole (dm³·mol⁻¹); amount of substance is measured in moles."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Een mol van enige stof, ook vloeibare water en yster, beslaan 22,4 dm³ by STD.","en":"One mole of any substance, including liquid water and iron, occupies 22.4 dm³ at STP."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. 22,4 dm³·mol⁻¹ geld net vir gasse by STD. In vloeistowwe en vaste stowwe is die deeltjies baie nader aan mekaar: een mol vloeibare water (18 g) beslaan net sowat 18 cm³.","en":"False. 22.4 dm³·mol⁻¹ applies only to gases at STP. In liquids and solids the particles are much closer together: one mole of liquid water (18 g) occupies only about 18 cm³."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bereken die hoeveelheid stof in 11 g koolstofdioksied (CO₂). n = ___ mol","en":"Calculate the amount of substance in 11 g of carbon dioxide (CO₂). n = ___ mol"},"answers":{"af":["0,25","0.25","0,25 mol","0.25 mol","n = 0,25","n = 0.25","n = 0,25 mol","n = 0.25 mol"],"en":["0.25","0,25","0.25 mol","0,25 mol","n = 0.25","n = 0,25","n = 0.25 mol","n = 0,25 mol"]},"explain":{"af":"M(CO₂) = 12 + 2(16) = 44 g·mol⁻¹. n = m/M = 11/44 = 0,25 mol.","en":"M(CO₂) = 12 + 2(16) = 44 g·mol⁻¹. n = m/M = 11/44 = 0.25 mol."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4","484","0,39"],"en":["4","484","0.39"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor 1 mol waterstofgas (H₂) en 1 mol suurstofgas (O₂) is korrek?","en":"Which statement about 1 mol of hydrogen gas (H₂) and 1 mol of oxygen gas (O₂) is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Hulle het dieselfde massa.","en":"They have the same mass."},{"af":"Die O₂ bevat meer molekules, want dit is swaarder.","en":"The O₂ contains more molecules, because it is heavier."},{"af":"Die H₂ bevat meer molekules, want H-atome is kleiner.","en":"The H₂ contains more molecules, because H atoms are smaller."},{"af":"Hulle bevat dieselfde aantal molekules, maar die O₂ het 'n groter massa.","en":"They contain the same number of molecules, but the O₂ has a greater mass."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Een mol van enige stof bevat 6,02 × 10²³ deeltjies, dus is die aantal molekules gelyk. Die massas verskil: M(H₂) = 2 g·mol⁻¹ en M(O₂) = 32 g·mol⁻¹, dus weeg 1 mol O₂ 32 g en 1 mol H₂ net 2 g.","en":"One mole of any substance contains 6.02 × 10²³ particles, so the number of molecules is equal. The masses differ: M(H₂) = 2 g·mol⁻¹ and M(O₂) = 32 g·mol⁻¹, so 1 mol O₂ has a mass of 32 g and 1 mol H₂ only 2 g."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die empiriese formule van glukose (C₆H₁₂O₆) is CH₂O.","en":"The empirical formula of glucose (C₆H₁₂O₆) is CH₂O."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Deel al die onderskrifte deur 6 (die grootste gemene faktor): C₆H₁₂O₆ → CH₂O. Dit is die eenvoudigste heelgetalverhouding C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1.","en":"True. Divide all the subscripts by 6 (the highest common factor): C₆H₁₂O₆ → CH₂O. This is the simplest whole-number ratio C : H : O = 1 : 2 : 1."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ammoniak vir kunsmis word gemaak volgens: N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g). As 2 mol N₂ volledig reageer, vorm ___ mol NH₃.","en":"Ammonia for fertiliser is made according to: N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) → 2NH₃(g). If 2 mol N₂ reacts completely, ___ mol NH₃ forms."},"answers":{"af":["4","4 mol"],"en":["4","4 mol"]},"explain":{"af":"Die molverhouding N₂ : NH₃ = 1 : 2. Dus vorm 2 mol N₂ → 2 × 2 = 4 mol NH₃.","en":"The mole ratio N₂ : NH₃ = 1 : 2. So 2 mol N₂ → 2 × 2 = 4 mol NH₃."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2","1","6"],"en":["2","1","6"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel NH₃-molekules is daar in 3,4 g ammoniak?","en":"How many NH₃ molecules are there in 3.4 g of ammonia?"},"options":[{"af":"1,20 × 10²³","en":"1.20 × 10²³"},{"af":"4,82 × 10²³","en":"4.82 × 10²³"},{"af":"2,05 × 10²⁴","en":"2.05 × 10²⁴"},{"af":"0,20","en":"0.20"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"M(NH₃) = 14 + 3(1) = 17 g·mol⁻¹; n = 3,4/17 = 0,2 mol; N = 0,2 × 6,02 × 10²³ = 1,20 × 10²³ molekules. 4,82 × 10²³ is die aantal atome (4 per molekule), 2,05 × 10²⁴ kom van die massa direk met N_A te vermenigvuldig, en 0,20 is die aantal mol, nie molekules nie.","en":"M(NH₃) = 14 + 3(1) = 17 g·mol⁻¹; n = 3.4/17 = 0.2 mol; N = 0.2 × 6.02 × 10²³ = 1.20 × 10²³ molecules. 4.82 × 10²³ is the number of atoms (4 per molecule), 2.05 × 10²⁴ comes from multiplying the mass directly by N_A, and 0.20 is the number of moles, not molecules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"4 g natriumhidroksied (NaOH) word in water opgelos om 250 cm³ oplossing te maak. Die konsentrasie van die oplossing is ___ mol·dm⁻³.","en":"4 g of sodium hydroxide (NaOH) is dissolved in water to make 250 cm³ of solution. The concentration of the solution is ___ mol·dm⁻³."},"answers":{"af":["0,4","0.4","0,40","0.40","0,4 mol·dm⁻³","0.4 mol·dm⁻³","0,4 mol/dm³","0.4 mol/dm³","0,4 mol.dm-3","0.4 mol.dm-3","0,4 mol/dm3","0.4 mol/dm3"],"en":["0.4","0,4","0.40","0,40","0.4 mol·dm⁻³","0,4 mol·dm⁻³","0.4 mol/dm³","0,4 mol/dm³","0.4 mol.dm-3","0,4 mol.dm-3","0.4 mol/dm3","0,4 mol/dm3"]},"explain":{"af":"M(NaOH) = 23 + 16 + 1 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; n = 4/40 = 0,1 mol. V = 250 cm³ = 0,25 dm³. c = n/V = 0,1/0,25 = 0,4 mol·dm⁻³. As jy vergeet om cm³ na dm³ om te skakel, kry jy die verkeerde 0,0004.","en":"M(NaOH) = 23 + 16 + 1 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; n = 4/40 = 0.1 mol. V = 250 cm³ = 0.25 dm³. c = n/V = 0.1/0.25 = 0.4 mol·dm⁻³. If you forget to convert cm³ to dm³, you get the wrong 0.0004."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0,0004","16","0,025"],"en":["0.0004","16","0.025"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Boere naby Brits gebruik ammoniumnitraat (NH₄NO₃) as kunsmis. Wat is die persentasie stikstof (volgens massa) in NH₄NO₃?","en":"Farmers near Brits use ammonium nitrate (NH₄NO₃) as fertiliser. What is the percentage of nitrogen (by mass) in NH₄NO₃?"},"options":[{"af":"17,5 %","en":"17.5%"},{"af":"60 %","en":"60%"},{"af":"58,33 %","en":"58.33%"},{"af":"35 %","en":"35%"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"M(NH₄NO₃) = 2(14) + 4(1) + 3(16) = 80 g·mol⁻¹. Daar is 2 N-atome: % N = (2 × 14)/80 × 100 = 35 %. 17,5 % tel net een N-atoom, 60 % is die persentasie suurstof, en 58,33 % kom van die O net een keer te tel (28/48).","en":"M(NH₄NO₃) = 2(14) + 4(1) + 3(16) = 80 g·mol⁻¹. There are 2 N atoms: % N = (2 × 14)/80 × 100 = 35%. 17.5% counts only one N atom, 60% is the percentage of oxygen, and 58.33% comes from counting the O only once (28/48)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Magnesium brand met 'n helder wit vlam: 2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s). Watter massa MgO vorm as 6 g Mg volledig reageer?","en":"Magnesium burns with a bright white flame: 2Mg(s) + O₂(g) → 2MgO(s). What mass of MgO forms when 6 g Mg reacts completely?"},"options":[{"af":"5 g","en":"5 g"},{"af":"10 g","en":"10 g"},{"af":"20 g","en":"20 g"},{"af":"6 g","en":"6 g"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"n(Mg) = 6/24 = 0,25 mol. Molverhouding Mg : MgO = 2 : 2 = 1 : 1, dus n(MgO) = 0,25 mol. M(MgO) = 24 + 16 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; m = 0,25 × 40 = 10 g. 5 g en 20 g gebruik die verhouding verkeerd, en 6 g vergeet dat die suurstof ook massa byvoeg.","en":"n(Mg) = 6/24 = 0.25 mol. Mole ratio Mg : MgO = 2 : 2 = 1 : 1, so n(MgO) = 0.25 mol. M(MgO) = 24 + 16 = 40 g·mol⁻¹; m = 0.25 × 40 = 10 g. 5 g and 20 g use the ratio incorrectly, and 6 g forgets that the oxygen also adds mass."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Propaan (C₃H₈) is 'n hoofbestanddeel van die gas in braaigasbottels: C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(ℓ). As 22 g propaan volledig verbrand, watter volume CO₂ vorm by STD? V = ___ dm³","en":"Propane (C₃H₈) is a main component of the gas in braai gas bottles: C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(ℓ). If 22 g of propane burns completely, what volume of CO₂ forms at STP? V = ___ dm³"},"answers":{"af":["33,6","33.6","33,6 dm³","33.6 dm³","33,6 dm3","33.6 dm3","V = 33,6","V = 33.6","V = 33,6 dm³","V = 33.6 dm³"],"en":["33.6","33,6","33.6 dm³","33,6 dm³","33.6 dm3","33,6 dm3","V = 33.6","V = 33,6","V = 33.6 dm³","V = 33,6 dm³"]},"explain":{"af":"M(C₃H₈) = 3(12) + 8(1) = 44 g·mol⁻¹; n = 22/44 = 0,5 mol. Molverhouding C₃H₈ : CO₂ = 1 : 3, dus n(CO₂) = 1,5 mol. V = n × V_m = 1,5 × 22,4 = 33,6 dm³.","en":"M(C₃H₈) = 3(12) + 8(1) = 44 g·mol⁻¹; n = 22/44 = 0.5 mol. Mole ratio C₃H₈ : CO₂ = 1 : 3, so n(CO₂) = 1.5 mol. V = n × V_m = 1.5 × 22.4 = 33.6 dm³."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11,2","492,8","67,2"],"en":["11.2","492.8","67.2"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hematiet is 'n ystererts met 70 % yster en 30 % suurstof (volgens massa). Anel kry die molverhouding Fe : O = 1,25 : 1,875 = 1 : 1,5 en skryf die empiriese formule as FeO₂ (sy rond 1,5 op na 2). Johan skryf Fe₂O₃. Wie is korrek?","en":"Haematite is an iron ore with 70% iron and 30% oxygen (by mass). Anel gets the mole ratio Fe : O = 1.25 : 1.875 = 1 : 1.5 and writes the empirical formula as FeO₂ (she rounds 1.5 up to 2). Johan writes Fe₂O₃. Who is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Anel, want 'n molverhouding word altyd na die naaste heelgetal afgerond.","en":"Anel, because a mole ratio is always rounded to the nearest whole number."},{"af":"Geeneen nie; die formule is FeO, want 1,5 moet na 1 afgerond word.","en":"Neither; the formula is FeO, because 1.5 must be rounded down to 1."},{"af":"Johan, want 'n verhouding van 1 : 1,5 moet met 2 vermenigvuldig word om die heelgetalle 2 : 3 te kry.","en":"Johan, because a ratio of 1 : 1.5 must be multiplied by 2 to get the whole numbers 2 : 3."},{"af":"Albei, want FeO₂ en Fe₂O₃ het dieselfde persentasie yster.","en":"Both, because FeO₂ and Fe₂O₃ have the same percentage of iron."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Johan is korrek. 1,5 is nie naby 'n heelgetal nie, dus mag jy nie afrond nie – vermenigvuldig met 2: 1 : 1,5 → 2 : 3, dus Fe₂O₃. Kontroleer: % Fe in Fe₂O₃ = 112/160 × 100 = 70 %, maar in FeO₂ is dit 56/88 × 100 = 63,64 %, so Anel se formule pas nie by die data nie.","en":"Johan is correct. 1.5 is not close to a whole number, so you may not round – multiply by 2: 1 : 1.5 → 2 : 3, so Fe₂O₃. Check: % Fe in Fe₂O₃ = 112/160 × 100 = 70%, but in FeO₂ it is 56/88 × 100 = 63.64%, so Anel's formula does not fit the data."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder verhit blou kopersulfaat (CuSO₄·xH₂O) om x te bepaal, maar stop te gou: die oorblyfsel is nog effens blou. Hoe beïnvloed dit die berekende waarde van x?","en":"A learner heats blue copper sulfate (CuSO₄·xH₂O) to determine x, but stops too soon: the residue is still slightly blue. How does this affect the calculated value of x?"},"options":[{"af":"x sal te klein wees, want minder water is verwyder as wat werklik in die kristal was.","en":"x will be too small, because less water was removed than was actually in the crystal."},{"af":"x sal te groot wees, want die oorblyfsel is swaarder.","en":"x will be too large, because the residue is heavier."},{"af":"x sal korrek wees, want die molverhouding verander nie.","en":"x will be correct, because the mole ratio does not change."},{"af":"x kan glad nie bereken word nie, want watervrye kopersulfaat is wit.","en":"x cannot be calculated at all, because anhydrous copper sulfate is white."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die blou kleur wys daar is nog kristalwater in die oorblyfsel. Die berekende massa water (gehidreerd − oorblyfsel) is dus te klein, en die 'watervrye' massa is te groot. n(H₂O) is te klein en n(CuSO₄) te groot, dus is x = n(H₂O)/n(CuSO₄) te klein. Verhit tot die oorblyfsel heeltemal wit is en die massa nie meer verander nie.","en":"The blue colour shows there is still water of crystallisation in the residue. The calculated mass of water (hydrated − residue) is therefore too small, and the 'anhydrous' mass is too large. n(H₂O) is too small and n(CuSO₄) too large, so x = n(H₂O)/n(CuSO₄) is too small. Heat until the residue is completely white and the mass no longer changes."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-vektore-beweging","title":{"af":"Vektore, skalare en beweging in een dimensie","en":"Vectors, scalars and motion in one dimension"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal vektore en skalare kan onderskei, resultante kan bepaal en beweging met woorde, berekeninge en x–t-, v–t- en a–t-grafieke kan beskryf.","en":"You will be able to distinguish between vectors and scalars, determine resultants and describe motion with words, calculations and x–t, v–t and a–t graphs."},"summary":{"af":"## Skalare en vektore\n\n- **Skalaar:** 'n fisiese hoeveelheid met slegs grootte. Voorbeelde: massa, tyd, afstand, spoed, energie, temperatuur.\n- **Vektor:** 'n fisiese hoeveelheid met grootte én rigting. Voorbeelde: verplasing, snelheid, versnelling, krag, gewig.\n\n'n Vektor word as 'n pyl geteken: die **lengte** van die pyl stel die grootte voor en die **pylpunt** wys die rigting. Gee 'n vektorantwoord altyd met 'n rigting, bv. 250 m oos of +250 m.\n\n## Resultant van vektore in een dimensie\n\nDie **resultante vektor** is die enkele vektor wat dieselfde effek het as twee of meer vektore saam. Vir vektore op een reguit lyn:\n\n1. Kies 'n positiewe rigting (bv. oos = +, wes = −).\n2. Gee elke vektor die regte teken.\n3. Tel die vektore algebraïes bymekaar.\n4. Gee die grootte én die rigting: + is die positiewe rigting, − die teenoorgestelde rigting.\n\nVektore in dieselfde rigting tel op; vektore in teenoorgestelde rigtings trek van mekaar af. As jy hulle kop-aan-stert teken, loop die resultant van die stert van die eerste pyl na die kop van die laaste pyl.\n\n## Verwysingsraamwerk, posisie, afstand en verplasing\n\n- **Eendimensionele beweging:** beweging langs 'n reguit lyn.\n- **Verwysingsraamwerk:** 'n verwysingspunt (oorsprong) gekombineer met 'n stel rigtings, bv. die Brits-taxistaanplek as 0 m met oos as positief.\n- **Posisie (x):** waar 'n voorwerp relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt is. Posisie kan positief of negatief wees.\n- **Afstand:** die lengte van die pad wat afgelê is. Afstand is 'n skalaar en altyd positief.\n- **Verplasing (Δx):** verandering in posisie: Δx = x_{f} − x_{i}. Dit is 'n vektor wat van die beginposisie na die eindposisie wys.\n\n> **Onthou!** Hardloop jy een rondte van 400 m op die atletiekbaan, is jou afstand 400 m maar jou verplasing **nul**, want jy eindig waar jy begin het.\n\n## Spoed, snelheid en versnelling\n\n| Hoeveelheid | Definisie | Formule | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Gemiddelde spoed (skalaar) | totale afstand gedeel deur totale tyd | [[afstand/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Gemiddelde snelheid (vektor) | tempo van verandering van posisie (totale verplasing gedeel deur totale tyd) | v = [[Δx/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Versnelling (vektor) | tempo van verandering van snelheid | a = [[Δv/Δt]] = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] | m·s⁻² |\n\n- **Oombliklike snelheid:** die verplasing gedeel deur 'n baie klein (infinitesimale) tydinterval – die snelheid op 'n spesifieke oomblik.\n- **Oombliklike spoed:** die grootte van die oombliklike snelheid. 'n Motor se spoedmeter wys oombliklike spoed – dit wys nie die rigting nie.\n- **Omskakeling:** 1 km·h⁻¹ = [[1 000 m/3 600 s]], dus km·h⁻¹ ÷ 3,6 = m·s⁻¹ en m·s⁻¹ × 3,6 = km·h⁻¹.\n\n### Positiewe en negatiewe versnelling\n\nDie teken van a gee net sy **rigting**. Of 'n voorwerp vinniger of stadiger gaan, hang van a én v saam af:\n\n- a en v in **dieselfde** rigting → die spoed neem toe.\n- a en v in **teenoorgestelde** rigtings → die spoed neem af; die voorwerp **vertraag**.\n\n'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken dus nie altyd vertraging nie: 'n motor wat wes (−) ry en al vinniger gaan, het 'n negatiewe snelheid én 'n negatiewe versnelling.\n\n## Beweging in grafieke\n\n| Beweging | x–t-grafiek | v–t-grafiek | a–t-grafiek |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stilstaande voorwerp | horisontale lyn (x konstant) | lyn op die t-as (v = 0) | lyn op die t-as (a = 0) |\n| Konstante snelheid | reguit skuins lyn | horisontale lyn by v ≠ 0 | lyn op die t-as (a = 0) |\n| Konstante versnelling uit rus | kromme wat al steiler word | reguit skuins lyn deur die oorsprong | horisontale lyn by a ≠ 0 |\n\n**Wat jy uit 'n grafiek kry:**\n\n- **Gradiënt van die x–t-grafiek** = snelheid. Hoe steiler, hoe vinniger; 'n lyn wat afwaarts loop, beteken beweging in die negatiewe rigting. By 'n kromme gee die gradiënt van die **raaklyn** die oombliklike snelheid.\n- **Gradiënt van die v–t-grafiek** = versnelling.\n- **Oppervlakte onder die v–t-grafiek** = verplasing. Gebruik reghoeke (l × b), driehoeke (½ × basis × hoogte) en trapesiums. Oppervlakte onder die t-as is 'n negatiewe verplasing.\n- **Oppervlakte onder die a–t-grafiek** = verandering in snelheid (Δv).\n\nOp 'n **tikkerband** (bewegingsdiagram) beteken gelyke spasies tussen die kolletjies konstante snelheid. Spasies wat groter word, beteken die spoed neem toe; spasies wat kleiner word, beteken die voorwerp vertraag.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** afstand en verplasing verwar; die rigting by 'n vektorantwoord vergeet; km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; dink dat a = 0 as v = 0 (by die draaipunt is v = 0, maar a is nie nul nie); die y-waarde van 'n x–t-grafiek as die snelheid lees in plaas van die gradiënt te bereken.","en":"## Scalars and vectors\n\n- **Scalar:** a physical quantity having magnitude only. Examples: mass, time, distance, speed, energy, temperature.\n- **Vector:** a physical quantity having both magnitude and direction. Examples: displacement, velocity, acceleration, force, weight.\n\nA vector is drawn as an arrow: the **length** of the arrow represents the magnitude and the **arrowhead** shows the direction. Always give a vector answer with a direction, e.g. 250 m east or +250 m.\n\n## Resultant of vectors in one dimension\n\nThe **resultant vector** is the single vector having the same effect as two or more vectors together. For vectors on one straight line:\n\n1. Choose a positive direction (e.g. east = +, west = −).\n2. Give each vector the correct sign.\n3. Add the vectors algebraically.\n4. Give the magnitude and the direction: + is the positive direction, − the opposite direction.\n\nVectors in the same direction add up; vectors in opposite directions subtract from each other. If you draw them head-to-tail, the resultant runs from the tail of the first arrow to the head of the last arrow.\n\n## Frame of reference, position, distance and displacement\n\n- **One-dimensional motion:** motion along a straight line.\n- **Frame of reference:** a reference point (origin) combined with a set of directions, e.g. the Brits taxi rank as 0 m with east as positive.\n- **Position (x):** where an object is relative to a reference point. Position can be positive or negative.\n- **Distance:** the length of the path travelled. Distance is a scalar and always positive.\n- **Displacement (Δx):** change in position: Δx = x_{f} − x_{i}. It is a vector pointing from the initial position to the final position.\n\n> **Remember!** If you run one 400 m lap on the athletics track, your distance is 400 m but your displacement is **zero**, because you end where you started.\n\n## Speed, velocity and acceleration\n\n| Quantity | Definition | Formula | Unit |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Average speed (scalar) | total distance divided by total time | [[distance/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Average velocity (vector) | rate of change of position (total displacement divided by total time) | v = [[Δx/Δt]] | m·s⁻¹ |\n| Acceleration (vector) | rate of change of velocity | a = [[Δv/Δt]] = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] | m·s⁻² |\n\n- **Instantaneous velocity:** the displacement divided by a very small (infinitesimal) time interval – the velocity at a specific moment.\n- **Instantaneous speed:** the magnitude of the instantaneous velocity. A car's speedometer shows instantaneous speed – it does not show the direction.\n- **Conversion:** 1 km·h⁻¹ = [[1 000 m/3 600 s]], so km·h⁻¹ ÷ 3.6 = m·s⁻¹ and m·s⁻¹ × 3.6 = km·h⁻¹.\n\n### Positive and negative acceleration\n\nThe sign of a only gives its **direction**. Whether an object goes faster or slower depends on a and v together:\n\n- a and v in the **same** direction → the speed increases.\n- a and v in **opposite** directions → the speed decreases; the object **decelerates**.\n\nSo a negative acceleration does not always mean deceleration: a car driving west (−) and going faster and faster has a negative velocity and a negative acceleration.\n\n## Motion in graphs\n\n| Motion | x–t graph | v–t graph | a–t graph |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Stationary object | horizontal line (x constant) | line on the t-axis (v = 0) | line on the t-axis (a = 0) |\n| Constant velocity | straight sloping line | horizontal line at v ≠ 0 | line on the t-axis (a = 0) |\n| Constant acceleration from rest | curve that gets steeper and steeper | straight sloping line through the origin | horizontal line at a ≠ 0 |\n\n**What you get from a graph:**\n\n- **Gradient of the x–t graph** = velocity. The steeper, the faster; a line running downwards means motion in the negative direction. For a curve, the gradient of the **tangent** gives the instantaneous velocity.\n- **Gradient of the v–t graph** = acceleration.\n- **Area under the v–t graph** = displacement. Use rectangles (l × b), triangles (½ × base × height) and trapeziums. Area below the t-axis is a negative displacement.\n- **Area under the a–t graph** = change in velocity (Δv).\n\nOn a **ticker tape** (motion diagram), equal spaces between the dots mean constant velocity. Spaces that get bigger mean the speed is increasing; spaces that get smaller mean the object is slowing down.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** confusing distance and displacement; forgetting the direction in a vector answer; not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; thinking that a = 0 when v = 0 (at the turning point v = 0, but a is not zero); reading the y-value of an x–t graph as the velocity instead of calculating the gradient."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Skalaar","en":"Scalar"},"def":{"af":"'n Fisiese hoeveelheid met slegs grootte, bv. massa, tyd, afstand en spoed.","en":"A physical quantity having magnitude only, e.g. mass, time, distance and speed."}},{"term":{"af":"Vektor","en":"Vector"},"def":{"af":"'n Fisiese hoeveelheid met grootte én rigting, bv. verplasing, snelheid, versnelling en krag.","en":"A physical quantity having both magnitude and direction, e.g. displacement, velocity, acceleration and force."}},{"term":{"af":"Resultante vektor","en":"Resultant vector"},"def":{"af":"Die enkele vektor wat dieselfde effek het as twee of meer vektore saam.","en":"The single vector having the same effect as two or more vectors together."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwysingsraamwerk","en":"Frame of reference"},"def":{"af":"'n Verwysingspunt (oorsprong) gekombineer met 'n stel rigtings.","en":"A reference point (origin) combined with a set of directions."}},{"term":{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},"def":{"af":"Die lengte van die pad wat afgelê is (skalaar).","en":"The length of the path travelled (scalar)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"},"def":{"af":"Verandering in posisie: Δx = x_f − x_i (vektor).","en":"Change in position: Δx = x_f − x_i (vector)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},"def":{"af":"Die totale afstand afgelê gedeel deur die totale tyd geneem (skalaar).","en":"The total distance travelled divided by the total time taken (scalar)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid","en":"Average velocity"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van verandering van posisie: totale verplasing gedeel deur totale tyd (vektor).","en":"The rate of change of position: total displacement divided by total time (vector)."}},{"term":{"af":"Oombliklike snelheid","en":"Instantaneous velocity"},"def":{"af":"Die verplasing gedeel deur 'n baie klein (infinitesimale) tydinterval; die snelheid op 'n spesifieke oomblik.","en":"The displacement divided by a very small (infinitesimal) time interval; the velocity at a specific moment."}},{"term":{"af":"Versnelling","en":"Acceleration"},"def":{"af":"Die tempo van verandering van snelheid: a = Δv/Δt, in m·s⁻² (vektor).","en":"The rate of change of velocity: a = Δv/Δt, in m·s⁻² (vector)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Afstand, verplasing, spoed en snelheid","en":"Distance, displacement, speed and velocity"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo stap van sy huis in Brits 400 m oos na die kafee en dan 150 m wes na sy vriend se huis, langs dieselfde reguit straat. Die hele staptog duur 5 minute. Bereken (a) die afstand, (b) die verplasing, (c) die gemiddelde spoed en (d) die gemiddelde snelheid.","en":"Thabo walks from his house in Brits 400 m east to the café and then 150 m west to his friend's house, along the same straight street. The whole walk takes 5 minutes. Calculate (a) the distance, (b) the displacement, (c) the average speed and (d) the average velocity."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. (a) Afstand = 400 + 150 = 550 m","en":"Choose east as positive. (a) Distance = 400 + 150 = 550 m"},{"af":"(b) Δx = (+400) + (−150) = +250 m, dus 250 m oos","en":"(b) Δx = (+400) + (−150) = +250 m, so 250 m east"},{"af":"Skakel die tyd om na sekondes: Δt = 5 × 60 = 300 s. (c) Gemiddelde spoed = [[afstand/Δt]] = [[550/300]] = 1,83 m·s⁻¹","en":"Convert the time to seconds: Δt = 5 × 60 = 300 s. (c) Average speed = [[distance/Δt]] = [[550/300]] = 1.83 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(d) Gemiddelde snelheid = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[250/300]] = 0,83 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(d) Average velocity = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[250/300]] = 0.83 m·s⁻¹ east"}],"answer":{"af":"Afstand 550 m; verplasing 250 m oos; gemiddelde spoed 1,83 m·s⁻¹; gemiddelde snelheid 0,83 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"Distance 550 m; displacement 250 m east; average speed 1.83 m·s⁻¹; average velocity 0.83 m·s⁻¹ east"}},{"title":{"af":"Resultant van saamlynige vektore","en":"Resultant of collinear vectors"},"problem":{"af":"By die skool se sportdag trek twee spanne toutrek. Aan die westekant trek Pieter met 350 N en Sipho met 400 N. Aan die oostekant trek Johan met 380 N en Kagiso met 420 N. Al die kragte is langs dieselfde reguit lyn. Bepaal die resultante krag op die tou.","en":"At the school's sports day two teams play tug-of-war. On the west side Pieter pulls with 350 N and Sipho with 400 N. On the east side Johan pulls with 380 N and Kagiso with 420 N. All the forces are along the same straight line. Determine the resultant force on the rope."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Wes-kragte kry 'n negatiewe teken: −350 N en −400 N. Oos-kragte: +380 N en +420 N","en":"Choose east as positive. West forces get a negative sign: −350 N and −400 N. East forces: +380 N and +420 N"},{"af":"F_{R} = (+380) + (+420) + (−350) + (−400)","en":"F_{R} = (+380) + (+420) + (−350) + (−400)"},{"af":"F_{R} = +800 − 750 = +50 N","en":"F_{R} = +800 − 750 = +50 N"},{"af":"Die positiewe teken beteken oos: die resultante krag is 50 N oos, dus trek die oostelike span die sterkste","en":"The positive sign means east: the resultant force is 50 N east, so the eastern team pulls the hardest"}],"answer":{"af":"F_R = 50 N oos","en":"F_R = 50 N east"}},{"title":{"af":"Versnelling en vertraging van 'n taxi","en":"Acceleration and deceleration of a taxi"},"problem":{"af":"'n Minibustaxi trek by 'n robot in Brits weg en bereik 72 km·h⁻¹ in 8 s, terwyl dit in 'n reguit lyn oos ry. By die volgende robot rem die taxi eenvormig van 20 m·s⁻¹ tot stilstand in 4 s. Bereken die versnelling (a) terwyl die taxi wegtrek en (b) terwyl dit rem.","en":"A minibus taxi pulls away at a robot in Brits and reaches 72 km·h⁻¹ in 8 s while driving in a straight line east. At the next robot the taxi brakes uniformly from 20 m·s⁻¹ to a standstill in 4 s. Calculate the acceleration (a) while the taxi pulls away and (b) while it brakes."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Skakel om: v_{f} = 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹","en":"Choose east as positive. Convert: v_{f} = 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(a) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[20 − 0/8]] = 2,5 m·s⁻², dus 2,5 m·s⁻² oos","en":"(a) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[20 − 0/8]] = 2.5 m·s⁻², so 2.5 m·s⁻² east"},{"af":"(b) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[0 − 20/4]] = −5 m·s⁻²","en":"(b) a = [[v_{f} − v_{i}/Δt]] = [[0 − 20/4]] = −5 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"Die negatiewe teken beteken wes. Die versnelling is teenoor die snelheid (oos), dus vertraag die taxi: a = 5 m·s⁻² wes","en":"The negative sign means west. The acceleration is opposite to the velocity (east), so the taxi decelerates: a = 5 m·s⁻² west"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 2,5 m·s⁻² oos; (b) 5 m·s⁻² wes (die taxi vertraag)","en":"(a) 2.5 m·s⁻² east; (b) 5 m·s⁻² west (the taxi decelerates)"}},{"title":{"af":"Gradiënt en oppervlakte van 'n v–t-grafiek","en":"Gradient and area of a v–t graph"},"problem":{"af":"'n Motor ry langs 'n reguit pad na Hartbeespoortdam (oos is positief). Die v–t-grafiek word so beskryf: die snelheid neem eenvormig toe van 0 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot 12 m·s⁻¹ by t = 4 s; dit bly konstant op 12 m·s⁻¹ tot t = 10 s; dan neem dit eenvormig af tot 0 m·s⁻¹ by t = 13 s. Bereken (a) die versnelling in elke deel, (b) die totale verplasing en (c) die gemiddelde snelheid vir die 13 s.","en":"A car drives along a straight road to Hartbeespoort Dam (east is positive). The v–t graph is described as follows: the velocity increases uniformly from 0 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to 12 m·s⁻¹ at t = 4 s; it stays constant at 12 m·s⁻¹ until t = 10 s; then it decreases uniformly to 0 m·s⁻¹ at t = 13 s. Calculate (a) the acceleration in each part, (b) the total displacement and (c) the average velocity for the 13 s."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Versnelling = gradiënt. 0–4 s: a = [[12 − 0/4 − 0]] = 3 m·s⁻² oos; 4–10 s: horisontale lyn, dus a = 0 m·s⁻²; 10–13 s: a = [[0 − 12/13 − 10]] = −4 m·s⁻², dus 4 m·s⁻² wes","en":"(a) Acceleration = gradient. 0–4 s: a = [[12 − 0/4 − 0]] = 3 m·s⁻² east; 4–10 s: horizontal line, so a = 0 m·s⁻²; 10–13 s: a = [[0 − 12/13 − 10]] = −4 m·s⁻², so 4 m·s⁻² west"},{"af":"(b) Verplasing = oppervlakte onder die grafiek: driehoek [[1/2]] × 4 × 12 = 24 m; reghoek 6 × 12 = 72 m; driehoek [[1/2]] × 3 × 12 = 18 m","en":"(b) Displacement = area under the graph: triangle [[1/2]] × 4 × 12 = 24 m; rectangle 6 × 12 = 72 m; triangle [[1/2]] × 3 × 12 = 18 m"},{"af":"Totale Δx = 24 + 72 + 18 = 114 m oos","en":"Total Δx = 24 + 72 + 18 = 114 m east"},{"af":"(c) Gemiddelde snelheid = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[114/13]] = 8,77 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(c) Average velocity = [[Δx/Δt]] = [[114/13]] = 8.77 m·s⁻¹ east"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 3 m·s⁻² oos; 0 m·s⁻²; 4 m·s⁻² wes. (b) 114 m oos. (c) 8,77 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"(a) 3 m·s⁻² east; 0 m·s⁻²; 4 m·s⁻² west. (b) 114 m east. (c) 8.77 m·s⁻¹ east"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n vektorhoeveelheid?","en":"Which one of the following is a vector quantity?"},"options":[{"af":"Massa","en":"Mass"},{"af":"Spoed","en":"Speed"},{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Verplasing het grootte én rigting (bv. 250 m oos), dus is dit 'n vektor. Massa, spoed en afstand het net grootte – hulle is skalare. Spoed is die lokval: snelheid is die vektor, spoed die skalaar.","en":"Displacement has magnitude and direction (e.g. 250 m east), so it is a vector. Mass, speed and distance have magnitude only – they are scalars. Speed is the trap: velocity is the vector, speed the scalar."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte definisie.","en":"Match each term to the correct definition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Afstand","en":"Distance"},"r":{"af":"Die lengte van die pad afgelê","en":"The length of the path travelled"}},{"l":{"af":"Verplasing","en":"Displacement"},"r":{"af":"Verandering in posisie","en":"Change in position"}},{"l":{"af":"Spoed","en":"Speed"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van afstand","en":"Rate of change of distance"}},{"l":{"af":"Snelheid","en":"Velocity"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van posisie","en":"Rate of change of position"}},{"l":{"af":"Versnelling","en":"Acceleration"},"r":{"af":"Tempo van verandering van snelheid","en":"Rate of change of velocity"}}],"explain":{"af":"Afstand en spoed is skalare (pad en tempo langs die pad). Verplasing, snelheid en versnelling is vektore: verplasing is die verandering in posisie, snelheid die tempo waarteen posisie verander, en versnelling die tempo waarteen snelheid verander.","en":"Distance and speed are scalars (path and rate along the path). Displacement, velocity and acceleration are vectors: displacement is the change in position, velocity the rate at which position changes, and acceleration the rate at which velocity changes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Atleet hardloop een volle rondte van 400 m op die skool se atletiekbaan en eindig presies waar sy begin het. Haar verplasing is nul, al het sy 'n afstand van 400 m afgelê.","en":"An athlete runs one full 400 m lap on the school's athletics track and ends exactly where she started. Her displacement is zero, even though she covered a distance of 400 m."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Verplasing is die verandering in posisie: begin- en eindposisie is dieselfde, dus Δx = 0. Afstand is die lengte van die pad, en dit is 400 m.","en":"True. Displacement is the change in position: the initial and final positions are the same, so Δx = 0. Distance is the length of the path, and that is 400 m."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Voorwerp beweeg met 'n konstante snelheid in die positiewe rigting. Watter beskrywing van sy grafieke is korrek?","en":"An object moves with a constant velocity in the positive direction. Which description of its graphs is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek is 'n horisontale lyn.","en":"The x–t graph is a horizontal line."},{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn met 'n konstante positiewe gradiënt.","en":"The x–t graph is a straight line with a constant positive gradient."},{"af":"Die v–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn met 'n positiewe gradiënt.","en":"The v–t graph is a straight line with a positive gradient."},{"af":"Die a–t-grafiek is 'n horisontale lyn bo die t-as.","en":"The a–t graph is a horizontal line above the t-axis."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Konstante snelheid beteken die posisie verander elke sekonde ewe veel, dus is die x–t-grafiek 'n reguit skuins lyn (gradiënt = snelheid). 'n Horisontale x–t-lyn is 'n stilstaande voorwerp. 'n Skuins v–t-lyn en 'n a–t-lyn bo die t-as beskryf konstante versnelling – by konstante snelheid is a = 0.","en":"Constant velocity means the position changes by the same amount every second, so the x–t graph is a straight sloping line (gradient = velocity). A horizontal x–t line is a stationary object. A sloping v–t line and an a–t line above the t-axis describe constant acceleration – at constant velocity a = 0."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die spoedgrens op 'n Suid-Afrikaanse snelweg is 120 km·h⁻¹. Skakel dit om na m·s⁻¹ (rond af tot twee desimale plekke): ___ m·s⁻¹","en":"The speed limit on a South African freeway is 120 km·h⁻¹. Convert it to m·s⁻¹ (round off to two decimal places): ___ m·s⁻¹"},"answers":{"af":["33,33","33,33 m·s⁻¹","33,33 m/s","33,33 m.s-1","33,33 m·s-1","33,33 ms-1","33,33 m s^-1","33.33","33.33 m·s⁻¹","33.33 m/s","33.33 m.s-1","33.33 m·s-1","33.33 ms-1","33.33 m s^-1"],"en":["33.33","33.33 m·s⁻¹","33.33 m/s","33.33 m.s-1","33.33 m·s-1","33.33 ms-1","33.33 m s^-1","33,33","33,33 m·s⁻¹","33,33 m/s","33,33 m.s-1","33,33 m·s-1","33,33 ms-1","33,33 m s^-1"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel deur 3,6: 120 ÷ 3,6 = 33,33 m·s⁻¹. Dit is omdat 1 km = 1 000 m en 1 h = 3 600 s, dus 120 × 1 000 ÷ 3 600 = 33,33 m·s⁻¹.","en":"Divide by 3.6: 120 ÷ 3.6 = 33.33 m·s⁻¹. This is because 1 km = 1 000 m and 1 h = 3 600 s, so 120 × 1 000 ÷ 3 600 = 33.33 m·s⁻¹."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["432,00","2,00","0,03"],"en":["432.00","2.00","0.03"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Negatiewe versnelling beteken altyd dat 'n voorwerp stadiger beweeg.","en":"Negative acceleration always means that an object is slowing down."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Vals. Die teken van a gee net die rigting. 'n Voorwerp vertraag net as a en v in teenoorgestelde rigtings is. 'n Motor wat in die negatiewe rigting ry en al vinniger gaan, het 'n negatiewe versnelling, maar sy spoed neem toe.","en":"False. The sign of a only gives the direction. An object slows down only if a and v are in opposite directions. A car driving in the negative direction and going faster and faster has a negative acceleration, but its speed increases."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi se spoedmeter wys 60 km·h⁻¹. Watter hoeveelheid lees die spoedmeter af?","en":"A taxi's speedometer shows 60 km·h⁻¹. Which quantity does the speedometer read?"},"options":[{"af":"Oombliklike spoed","en":"Instantaneous speed"},{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},{"af":"Oombliklike snelheid","en":"Instantaneous velocity"},{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid","en":"Average velocity"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die spoedmeter wys hoe vinnig die taxi op daardie oomblik ry (oombliklik), maar nie in watter rigting nie. Sonder rigting is dit 'n skalaar: oombliklike spoed, nie snelheid nie. Gemiddelde spoed sou die totale afstand gedeel deur die totale tyd vir die hele rit wees.","en":"The speedometer shows how fast the taxi is moving at that moment (instantaneous), but not in which direction. Without direction it is a scalar: instantaneous speed, not velocity. Average speed would be the total distance divided by the total time for the whole trip."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Fietsryer ry langs 'n reguit pad 12 km noord, dan 5 km suid en dan 3 km noord. Die resultante verplasing is ___ km noord.","en":"A cyclist rides along a straight road 12 km north, then 5 km south and then 3 km north. The resultant displacement is ___ km north."},"answers":{"af":["10","10 km","10 km noord","10 km N"],"en":["10","10 km","10 km north","10 km N"]},"explain":{"af":"Kies noord as positief: Δx = (+12) + (−5) + (+3) = +10 km, dus 10 km noord. Die afstand is 12 + 5 + 3 = 20 km, maar die vraag vra die verplasing.","en":"Choose north as positive: Δx = (+12) + (−5) + (+3) = +10 km, so 10 km north. The distance is 12 + 5 + 3 = 20 km, but the question asks for the displacement."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["20","4","14"],"en":["20","4","14"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Hond op 'n plaas naby Brits hardloop 30 m oos in 6 s, draai om en hardloop 10 m wes in 4 s. Wat is die hond se gemiddelde snelheid vir die hele 10 s?","en":"A dog on a farm near Brits runs 30 m east in 6 s, turns around and runs 10 m west in 4 s. What is the dog's average velocity for the whole 10 s?"},"options":[{"af":"4 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"4 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"3,75 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"3.75 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"2 m·s⁻¹ oos","en":"2 m·s⁻¹ east"},{"af":"2 m·s⁻¹ wes","en":"2 m·s⁻¹ west"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kies oos as positief. Δx = (+30) + (−10) = +20 m; Δt = 6 + 4 = 10 s. v = Δx/Δt = 20/10 = 2 m·s⁻¹ oos. 4 m·s⁻¹ is die gemiddelde spoed (40 m/10 s), 3,75 m·s⁻¹ is die gemiddeld van die twee spoede (5 en 2,5), en wes is die verkeerde rigting.","en":"Choose east as positive. Δx = (+30) + (−10) = +20 m; Δt = 6 + 4 = 10 s. v = Δx/Δt = 20/10 = 2 m·s⁻¹ east. 4 m·s⁻¹ is the average speed (40 m/10 s), 3.75 m·s⁻¹ is the average of the two speeds (5 and 2.5), and west is the wrong direction."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Motor op 'n reguit pad buite Brits versnel eenvormig van 5 m·s⁻¹ tot 25 m·s⁻¹ in 4 s. Die grootte van die versnelling is ___ m·s⁻².","en":"A car on a straight road outside Brits accelerates uniformly from 5 m·s⁻¹ to 25 m·s⁻¹ in 4 s. The magnitude of the acceleration is ___ m·s⁻²."},"answers":{"af":["5","5 m·s⁻²","5 m/s²","5 m/s^2","5 m.s-2","5 m·s-2","5 ms-2","5 m s^-2"],"en":["5","5 m·s⁻²","5 m/s²","5 m/s^2","5 m.s-2","5 m·s-2","5 ms-2","5 m s^-2"]},"explain":{"af":"a = (v_f − v_i)/Δt = (25 − 5)/4 = 20/4 = 5 m·s⁻². 'n Algemene fout is om 25/4 = 6,25 te bereken en die beginsnelheid te vergeet.","en":"a = (v_f − v_i)/Δt = (25 − 5)/4 = 20/4 = 5 m·s⁻². A common mistake is to calculate 25/4 = 6.25 and forget the initial velocity."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6,25","7,5","80"],"en":["6.25","7.5","80"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die x–t-grafiek van 'n taxi is 'n reguit lyn van x = 10 m by t = 0 s tot x = 40 m by t = 6 s. Wat is die taxi se snelheid?","en":"The x–t graph of a taxi is a straight line from x = 10 m at t = 0 s to x = 40 m at t = 6 s. What is the taxi's velocity?"},"options":[{"af":"5 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"5 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"6,67 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"6.67 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"1,67 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"1.67 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"},{"af":"0,2 m·s⁻¹ in die positiewe rigting","en":"0.2 m·s⁻¹ in the positive direction"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Snelheid = gradiënt van die x–t-grafiek = Δx/Δt = (40 − 10)/(6 − 0) = 30/6 = 5 m·s⁻¹. 6,67 kom van 40/6 (die beginposisie vergeet), 1,67 van 10/6, en 0,2 van Δt/Δx (die gradiënt omgekeer).","en":"Velocity = gradient of the x–t graph = Δx/Δt = (40 − 10)/(6 − 0) = 30/6 = 5 m·s⁻¹. 6.67 comes from 40/6 (forgetting the initial position), 1.67 from 10/6, and 0.2 from Δt/Δx (the gradient upside down)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n v–t-grafiek is 'n reguit lyn van 4 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot 16 m·s⁻¹ by t = 6 s (positiewe rigting). Die verplasing in hierdie 6 s is ___ m.","en":"A v–t graph is a straight line from 4 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to 16 m·s⁻¹ at t = 6 s (positive direction). The displacement in these 6 s is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["60","60 m","Δx = 60","Δx = 60 m","+60","+60 m"],"en":["60","60 m","Δx = 60","Δx = 60 m","+60","+60 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Verplasing = oppervlakte onder die v–t-grafiek. Die vorm is 'n trapesium: ½(4 + 16) × 6 = 60 m. Of: reghoek 4 × 6 = 24 m plus driehoek ½ × 6 × 12 = 36 m, saam 60 m. 96 m (16 × 6) of 36 m (net die driehoek) is algemene foute.","en":"Displacement = area under the v–t graph. The shape is a trapezium: ½(4 + 16) × 6 = 60 m. Or: rectangle 4 × 6 = 24 m plus triangle ½ × 6 × 12 = 36 m, together 60 m. 96 m (16 × 6) or 36 m (only the triangle) are common mistakes."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["96","36","24"],"en":["96","36","24"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die v–t-grafiek van 'n motor (oos is positief) is 'n reguit lyn van 20 m·s⁻¹ by t = 0 s tot −10 m·s⁻¹ by t = 7,5 s; dit sny die t-as by t = 5 s. Lerato sê: \"By t = 5 s staan die motor stil, dus is sy versnelling daar nul.\" Evalueer haar stelling.","en":"The v–t graph of a car (east is positive) is a straight line from 20 m·s⁻¹ at t = 0 s to −10 m·s⁻¹ at t = 7.5 s; it cuts the t-axis at t = 5 s. Lerato says: \"At t = 5 s the car is stationary, so its acceleration there is zero.\" Evaluate her statement."},"options":[{"af":"Sy is korrek: as v = 0 is, moet a ook 0 wees.","en":"She is correct: if v = 0, a must also be 0."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd: die gradiënt van die v–t-grafiek is oral −4 m·s⁻², dus is a = 4 m·s⁻² wes, ook by t = 5 s.","en":"She is wrong: the gradient of the v–t graph is −4 m·s⁻² everywhere, so a = 4 m·s⁻² west, also at t = 5 s."},{"af":"Sy is korrek: die grafiek sny die t-as by t = 5 s, en daar is die gradiënt nul.","en":"She is correct: the graph cuts the t-axis at t = 5 s, and there the gradient is zero."},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd: by t = 5 s is a = 4 m·s⁻² oos, want die motor draai om.","en":"She is wrong: at t = 5 s, a = 4 m·s⁻² east, because the car turns around."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Versnelling is die gradiënt, nie die waarde van v nie. Gradiënt = (−10 − 20)/7,5 = −4 m·s⁻², dieselfde oral op die reguit lyn. By t = 5 s is v = 0 (die draaipunt), maar a is steeds 4 m·s⁻² wes. Die motor vertraag terwyl dit oos ry, en versnel dan wes.","en":"Acceleration is the gradient, not the value of v. Gradient = (−10 − 20)/7.5 = −4 m·s⁻², the same everywhere on the straight line. At t = 5 s, v = 0 (the turning point), but a is still 4 m·s⁻² west. The car slows down while driving east, and then speeds up westwards."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi ry van die Brits-taxistaanplek na Hartbeespoort en terug na dieselfde staanplek. Die odometer wys dat die taxi altesaam 50 km gery het, en die rit het 1 h geduur. Leerder 1 sê die gemiddelde snelheid was 50 km·h⁻¹. Leerder 2 sê die gemiddelde snelheid was 0 km·h⁻¹, maar die gemiddelde spoed was 50 km·h⁻¹. Wie is korrek?","en":"A taxi drives from the Brits taxi rank to Hartbeespoort and back to the same rank. The odometer shows that the taxi travelled 50 km in total, and the trip took 1 h. Learner 1 says the average velocity was 50 km·h⁻¹. Learner 2 says the average velocity was 0 km·h⁻¹, but the average speed was 50 km·h⁻¹. Who is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Leerder 1, want spoed en snelheid is dieselfde ding.","en":"Learner 1, because speed and velocity are the same thing."},{"af":"Leerder 1, want die taxi het die hele tyd beweeg.","en":"Learner 1, because the taxi was moving the whole time."},{"af":"Geeneen nie: die gemiddelde snelheid is 25 km·h⁻¹, want die taxi was net 25 km van die staanplek af.","en":"Neither: the average velocity is 25 km·h⁻¹, because the taxi was only 25 km from the rank."},{"af":"Leerder 2, want die verplasing is nul (die taxi eindig waar hy begin het), terwyl die afstand 50 km is.","en":"Learner 2, because the displacement is zero (the taxi ends where it started), while the distance is 50 km."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gemiddelde snelheid = verplasing/tyd = 0 km/1 h = 0 km·h⁻¹, want die begin- en eindposisie is dieselfde. Gemiddelde spoed = afstand/tyd = 50 km/1 h = 50 km·h⁻¹. Leerder 1 verwar spoed (skalaar) met snelheid (vektor), en 25 km is 'n posisie halfpad, nie die verplasing vir die hele rit nie.","en":"Average velocity = displacement/time = 0 km/1 h = 0 km·h⁻¹, because the initial and final positions are the same. Average speed = distance/time = 50 km/1 h = 50 km·h⁻¹. Learner 1 confuses speed (scalar) with velocity (vector), and 25 km is a position halfway, not the displacement for the whole trip."}}]},{"id":"f10-t3-bewegingsvergelykings","title":{"af":"Bewegingsvergelykings","en":"Equations of motion"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die vier bewegingsvergelykings kan kies en gebruik om snelheid, versnelling, verplasing en tyd vir eenvormig versnelde beweging te bereken – ook in probleme met meer as een stadium.","en":"You will be able to choose and use the four equations of motion to calculate velocity, acceleration, displacement and time for uniformly accelerated motion – also in multi-stage problems."},"summary":{"af":"## Wanneer gebruik jy die bewegingsvergelykings?\n\nDie vier bewegingsvergelykings beskryf beweging in 'n reguit lyn met **konstante (eenvormige) versnelling**. As die versnelling verander (bv. 'n taxi wat stop-en-gaan ry), mag jy dit nie oor die hele beweging gebruik nie – breek die beweging dan op in stadiums waarin a konstant is.\n\n| Simbool | Grootheid | SI-eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| v_{i} | beginsnelheid | m·s⁻¹ |\n| v_{f} | eindsnelheid | m·s⁻¹ |\n| a | versnelling | m·s⁻² |\n| Δt | tydsinterval | s |\n| Δx | verplasing | m |\n\n## Die vier vergelykings (gegewensblad)\n\n1. **v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt** – bevat nie Δx nie\n2. **Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2}** – bevat nie v_{f} nie\n3. **v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx** – bevat nie Δt nie\n4. **Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt** – bevat nie a nie (gemiddelde snelheid × tyd)\n\nElke vergelyking bevat vier van die vyf groothede. As jy **drie** ken, kan jy die vierde bereken.\n\n### Hoe kies jy die regte vergelyking?\n\nSkryf die gegewe groothede en die onbekende neer. Soek die grootheid wat **nie gegee is nie en ook nie gevra word nie** – kies dan die vergelyking waarin dié grootheid **ontbreek**. Bv. gegee v_{i}, a en Δx, gevra v_{f}: Δt speel geen rol nie, dus gebruik v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n\n### Versteekte inligting in woorde\n\n- \"begin uit rus\" / \"vertrek van stilstand\" → v_{i} = 0\n- \"kom tot stilstand\" / \"stop\" → v_{f} = 0\n- \"konstante snelheid\" → a = 0 (dan is Δx = vΔt)\n- \"rem\" / \"vertraag\" → a is teenoor die bewegingsrigting (negatief as die bewegingsrigting positief gekies is)\n\n## Tekenkonvensie\n\nSnelheid, versnelling en verplasing is **vektore**. Kies eers 'n positiewe rigting (bv. vorentoe of oos = positief) en hou daarby vir die hele probleem.\n\n- 'n Voorwerp wat **vinniger** word: a en v het **dieselfde** teken.\n- 'n Voorwerp wat **stadiger** word: a en v het **teenoorgestelde** tekens.\n- 'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken **nie altyd** stadiger nie – as die voorwerp in die negatiewe rigting beweeg, word dit vinniger.\n- Gee 'n vektor-antwoord altyd met 'n **rigting**, bv. 12 m·s⁻¹ oos.\n\n## Omskakeling: km·h⁻¹ ↔ m·s⁻¹\n\n1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s, dus:\n\n- km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹: **deel deur 3,6** (72 km·h⁻¹ = 20 m·s⁻¹)\n- m·s⁻¹ → km·h⁻¹: **maal met 3,6** (25 m·s⁻¹ = 90 km·h⁻¹)\n\nSkakel ook cm na m en minute na sekondes om **voordat** jy vervang.\n\n## Probleme met meer as een stadium\n\nAs die beweging verander (bv. 'n taxi trek by 'n robot weg en ry dan teen konstante snelheid), werk elke stadium apart uit:\n\n- Die **eindsnelheid van stadium 1 is die beginsnelheid van stadium 2**.\n- Totale verplasing = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2}.\n\n### Stopafstand by 'n robot\n\n'n Bestuurder sien die robot rooi word, maar reageer nie dadelik nie.\n\n1. **Reaksietyd:** die motor ry nog teen **konstante snelheid**, dus reaksie-afstand = v × reaksietyd.\n2. **Remafstand:** die motor vertraag eenvormig tot v_{f} = 0; gebruik v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n3. **Stopafstand = reaksie-afstand + remafstand.**\n\nMet v_{f} = 0 gee die derde vergelyking remafstand = v_{i}^{2} ÷ (2 × grootte van a). Die remafstand is dus eweredig aan v_{i}^{2}: ry jy **twee keer** so vinnig, is die remafstand **vier keer** so lank.\n\n## Stappe vir enige berekening\n\n1. Kies 'n positiewe rigting.\n2. Lys die gegewe en die onbekende met tekens en SI-eenhede.\n3. Kies die vergelyking (die een sonder die ontbrekende grootheid).\n4. Skryf die formule, vervang en bereken.\n5. Gee die antwoord met eenheid (en rigting vir vektore), afgerond tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; die minusteken van 'n remmende versnelling vergeet; afstand in plaas van verplasing gebruik; in ½aΔt^{2} net Δt kwadreer (nie aΔt nie); by v_{f}^{2} vergeet om die vierkantswortel te trek.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kontroleer jou antwoord met 'n v-t-grafiek in jou kop: die **gradiënt** is die versnelling en die **oppervlakte onder die grafiek** is die verplasing.","en":"## When do you use the equations of motion?\n\nThe four equations of motion describe motion in a straight line with **constant (uniform) acceleration**. If the acceleration changes (e.g. a taxi driving stop-start), you may not use them for the whole motion – split the motion into stages in which a is constant.\n\n| Symbol | Quantity | SI unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| v_{i} | initial velocity | m·s⁻¹ |\n| v_{f} | final velocity | m·s⁻¹ |\n| a | acceleration | m·s⁻² |\n| Δt | time interval | s |\n| Δx | displacement | m |\n\n## The four equations (data sheet)\n\n1. **v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt** – contains no Δx\n2. **Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2}** – contains no v_{f}\n3. **v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx** – contains no Δt\n4. **Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt** – contains no a (average velocity × time)\n\nEach equation contains four of the five quantities. If you know **three**, you can calculate the fourth.\n\n### How do you choose the right equation?\n\nWrite down the given quantities and the unknown. Find the quantity that is **neither given nor asked for** – then choose the equation in which that quantity is **missing**. E.g. given v_{i}, a and Δx, asked v_{f}: Δt plays no role, so use v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n\n### Hidden information in words\n\n- \"starts from rest\" / \"departs from standstill\" → v_{i} = 0\n- \"comes to rest\" / \"stops\" → v_{f} = 0\n- \"constant velocity\" → a = 0 (then Δx = vΔt)\n- \"brakes\" / \"slows down\" → a is opposite to the direction of motion (negative if the direction of motion is chosen as positive)\n\n## Sign convention\n\nVelocity, acceleration and displacement are **vectors**. First choose a positive direction (e.g. forward or east = positive) and stick to it for the whole problem.\n\n- An object that **speeds up**: a and v have the **same** sign.\n- An object that **slows down**: a and v have **opposite** signs.\n- A negative acceleration does **not always** mean slowing down – if the object moves in the negative direction, it speeds up.\n- Always give a vector answer with a **direction**, e.g. 12 m·s⁻¹ east.\n\n## Converting: km·h⁻¹ ↔ m·s⁻¹\n\n1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s, so:\n\n- km·h⁻¹ → m·s⁻¹: **divide by 3.6** (72 km·h⁻¹ = 20 m·s⁻¹)\n- m·s⁻¹ → km·h⁻¹: **multiply by 3.6** (25 m·s⁻¹ = 90 km·h⁻¹)\n\nAlso convert cm to m and minutes to seconds **before** you substitute.\n\n## Multi-stage problems\n\nIf the motion changes (e.g. a taxi pulls away at a robot and then drives at constant velocity), work out each stage separately:\n\n- The **final velocity of stage 1 is the initial velocity of stage 2**.\n- Total displacement = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2}.\n\n### Stopping distance at a robot\n\nA driver sees the robot turn red but does not react immediately.\n\n1. **Reaction time:** the car still moves at **constant velocity**, so reaction distance = v × reaction time.\n2. **Braking distance:** the car slows down uniformly to v_{f} = 0; use v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx.\n3. **Stopping distance = reaction distance + braking distance.**\n\nWith v_{f} = 0 the third equation gives braking distance = v_{i}^{2} ÷ (2 × magnitude of a). The braking distance is therefore proportional to v_{i}^{2}: drive **twice** as fast and the braking distance is **four times** as long.\n\n## Steps for any calculation\n\n1. Choose a positive direction.\n2. List the given and the unknown with signs and SI units.\n3. Choose the equation (the one without the missing quantity).\n4. Write the formula, substitute and calculate.\n5. Give the answer with a unit (and a direction for vectors), rounded to two decimal places.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; forgetting the minus sign of a braking acceleration; using distance instead of displacement; in ½aΔt^{2} squaring only Δt (not aΔt); forgetting to take the square root with v_{f}^{2}.\n\n> **Tip:** Check your answer with a v-t graph in your head: the **gradient** is the acceleration and the **area under the graph** is the displacement."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Verplasing (Δx)","en":"Displacement (Δx)"},"def":{"af":"Verplasing is die verandering in posisie van 'n voorwerp. Dit is 'n vektor: dit het grootte en rigting.","en":"Displacement is the change in position of an object. It is a vector: it has magnitude and direction."}},{"term":{"af":"Snelheid (v)","en":"Velocity (v)"},"def":{"af":"Snelheid is die tempo van verandering van posisie. Dit is 'n vektor, gemeet in m·s⁻¹.","en":"Velocity is the rate of change of position. It is a vector, measured in m·s⁻¹."}},{"term":{"af":"Versnelling (a)","en":"Acceleration (a)"},"def":{"af":"Versnelling is die tempo van verandering van snelheid. Dit is 'n vektor, gemeet in m·s⁻².","en":"Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity. It is a vector, measured in m·s⁻²."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenvormige versnelling","en":"Uniform acceleration"},"def":{"af":"Versnelling wat konstant bly: die snelheid verander elke sekonde met dieselfde hoeveelheid. Slegs dan mag die bewegingsvergelykings gebruik word.","en":"Acceleration that stays constant: the velocity changes by the same amount every second. Only then may the equations of motion be used."}},{"term":{"af":"Beginsnelheid (v_i)","en":"Initial velocity (v_i)"},"def":{"af":"Die snelheid van 'n voorwerp aan die begin van die tydsinterval wat bestudeer word. \"Begin uit rus\" beteken v_i = 0.","en":"The velocity of an object at the start of the time interval being studied. \"Starts from rest\" means v_i = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Eindsnelheid (v_f)","en":"Final velocity (v_f)"},"def":{"af":"Die snelheid van 'n voorwerp aan die einde van die tydsinterval wat bestudeer word. \"Kom tot stilstand\" beteken v_f = 0.","en":"The velocity of an object at the end of the time interval being studied. \"Comes to rest\" means v_f = 0."}},{"term":{"af":"Reaksietyd","en":"Reaction time"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd tussen die oomblik wat 'n bestuurder 'n gevaar sien en die oomblik wat hy begin rem. Die motor beweeg intussen teen konstante snelheid.","en":"The time between the moment a driver sees a hazard and the moment he starts braking. The car moves at constant velocity during this time."}},{"term":{"af":"Stopafstand","en":"Stopping distance"},"def":{"af":"Die totale afstand wat 'n voertuig aflê vandat die bestuurder die gevaar sien totdat dit stilstaan: reaksie-afstand + remafstand.","en":"The total distance a vehicle covers from the moment the driver sees the hazard until it stops: reaction distance + braking distance."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Taxi trek by 'n robot weg","en":"Taxi pulls away at a robot"},"problem":{"af":"'n Taxi staan stil by 'n robot in Brits. Toe die lig groen word, versnel dit eenvormig teen 1,5 m·s⁻² vir 8 s. Bereken (a) die taxi se snelheid na 8 s en (b) die taxi se verplasing in hierdie 8 s.","en":"A taxi is stationary at a robot in Brits. When the light turns green, it accelerates uniformly at 1.5 m·s⁻² for 8 s. Calculate (a) the taxi's velocity after 8 s and (b) the taxi's displacement in these 8 s."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. Gegee: v_{i} = 0 (begin uit rus), a = +1,5 m·s⁻², Δt = 8 s.","en":"Choose the direction of motion as positive. Given: v_{i} = 0 (starts from rest), a = +1.5 m·s⁻², Δt = 8 s."},{"af":"(a) Δx is nie nodig nie, dus: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt = 0 + (1,5)(8) = 12 m·s⁻¹ in die bewegingsrigting","en":"(a) Δx is not needed, so: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt = 0 + (1.5)(8) = 12 m·s⁻¹ in the direction of motion"},{"af":"(b) Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2} = (0)(8) + ½(1,5)(8)^{2} = ½(1,5)(64)","en":"(b) Δx = v_{i}Δt + ½aΔt^{2} = (0)(8) + ½(1.5)(8)^{2} = ½(1.5)(64)"},{"af":"Δx = 48 m in die bewegingsrigting. Kontrole: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(0 + 12)(8) = 48 m ✔","en":"Δx = 48 m in the direction of motion. Check: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(0 + 12)(8) = 48 m ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 12 m·s⁻¹ in die bewegingsrigting (b) 48 m in die bewegingsrigting","en":"(a) 12 m·s⁻¹ in the direction of motion (b) 48 m in the direction of motion"}},{"title":{"af":"Remmende motor met omskakeling van eenhede","en":"Braking car with unit conversion"},"problem":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹ op die R511 naby Hartbeespoortdam. Die bestuurder trap rem en die motor kom eenvormig tot stilstand oor 'n afstand van 40 m. Bereken (a) die versnelling van die motor en (b) hoe lank dit neem om te stop.","en":"A car travels at 72 km·h⁻¹ on the R511 near Hartbeespoort Dam. The driver brakes and the car comes to rest uniformly over a distance of 40 m. Calculate (a) the acceleration of the car and (b) how long it takes to stop."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel eers om: v_{i} = 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. v_{f} = 0 (kom tot stilstand), Δx = +40 m.","en":"Convert first: v_{i} = 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Choose the direction of motion as positive. v_{f} = 0 (comes to rest), Δx = +40 m."},{"af":"(a) Δt is nie gegee nie en word nie gevra nie, dus: v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0^{2} = (20)^{2} + 2a(40)","en":"(a) Δt is not given and not asked for, so: v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0^{2} = (20)^{2} + 2a(40)"},{"af":"0 = 400 + 80a → a = −400 ÷ 80 = −5 m·s⁻², d.w.s. 5 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting","en":"0 = 400 + 80a → a = −400 ÷ 80 = −5 m·s⁻², i.e. 5 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion"},{"af":"(b) v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 0 = 20 + (−5)Δt → 5Δt = 20 → Δt = 4 s","en":"(b) v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 0 = 20 + (−5)Δt → 5Δt = 20 → Δt = 4 s"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) a = −5 m·s⁻² (5 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting) (b) Δt = 4 s","en":"(a) a = −5 m·s⁻² (5 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion) (b) Δt = 4 s"}},{"title":{"af":"Stopafstand met reaksietyd (twee stadiums)","en":"Stopping distance with reaction time (two stages)"},"problem":{"af":"'n Bestuurder ry teen 90 km·h⁻¹ toe hy 'n robot 75 m voor hom rooi sien word. Sy reaksietyd is 0,8 s. Daarna rem hy en die motor vertraag eenvormig teen 6 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Bereken die totale stopafstand en bepaal of die motor voor die stopstreep stilhou.","en":"A driver travels at 90 km·h⁻¹ when he sees a robot 75 m ahead turn red. His reaction time is 0.8 s. Then he brakes and the car slows down uniformly at 6 m·s⁻² until it stops. Calculate the total stopping distance and determine whether the car stops before the stop line."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel om: v = 90 ÷ 3,6 = 25 m·s⁻¹. Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief.","en":"Convert: v = 90 ÷ 3.6 = 25 m·s⁻¹. Choose the direction of motion as positive."},{"af":"Stadium 1 (reaksietyd, konstante snelheid, a = 0): Δx_{1} = vΔt = (25)(0,8) = 20 m","en":"Stage 1 (reaction time, constant velocity, a = 0): Δx_{1} = vΔt = (25)(0.8) = 20 m"},{"af":"Stadium 2 (rem): v_{i} = 25 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 0, a = −6 m·s⁻². v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0 = 625 + 2(−6)Δx_{2} → Δx_{2} = 625 ÷ 12 = 52,08 m","en":"Stage 2 (braking): v_{i} = 25 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 0, a = −6 m·s⁻². v_{f}^{2} = v_{i}^{2} + 2aΔx → 0 = 625 + 2(−6)Δx_{2} → Δx_{2} = 625 ÷ 12 = 52.08 m"},{"af":"Stopafstand = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2} = 20 + 52,08 = 72,08 m. Dit is minder as 75 m, dus stop die motor 75 − 72,08 = 2,92 m voor die stopstreep.","en":"Stopping distance = Δx_{1} + Δx_{2} = 20 + 52.08 = 72.08 m. This is less than 75 m, so the car stops 75 − 72.08 = 2.92 m before the stop line."}],"answer":{"af":"Stopafstand = 72,08 m; die motor stop 2,92 m voor die stopstreep.","en":"Stopping distance = 72.08 m; the car stops 2.92 m before the stop line."}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte vergelyking","en":"Choose the right equation"},"problem":{"af":"'n Fietsryer in die Magaliesberg ry teen 8 m·s⁻¹ en vertraag eenvormig tot 2 m·s⁻¹ in 5 s terwyl hy teen 'n steilte uitry. Bereken (a) die afstand wat hy in hierdie 5 s aflê en (b) sy versnelling. Verduidelik telkens waarom jy die vergelyking gekies het.","en":"A cyclist in the Magaliesberg travels at 8 m·s⁻¹ and slows down uniformly to 2 m·s⁻¹ in 5 s while riding up a steep slope. Calculate (a) the distance he covers in these 5 s and (b) his acceleration. Explain each time why you chose the equation."},"steps":[{"af":"Kies die bewegingsrigting as positief. Gegee: v_{i} = 8 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 2 m·s⁻¹, Δt = 5 s.","en":"Choose the direction of motion as positive. Given: v_{i} = 8 m·s⁻¹, v_{f} = 2 m·s⁻¹, Δt = 5 s."},{"af":"(a) a is nie gegee nie en word nie gevra nie, dus gebruik die vergelyking sonder a: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(8 + 2)(5) = 25 m","en":"(a) a is not given and not asked for, so use the equation without a: Δx = ½(v_{i} + v_{f})Δt = ½(8 + 2)(5) = 25 m"},{"af":"(b) Δx is nie nodig nie, dus gebruik die vergelyking sonder Δx: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 2 = 8 + a(5)","en":"(b) Δx is not needed, so use the equation without Δx: v_{f} = v_{i} + aΔt → 2 = 8 + a(5)"},{"af":"a = (2 − 8) ÷ 5 = −1,2 m·s⁻². Die negatiewe teken wys dat die versnelling teenoor die bewegingsrigting is – die fietsryer vertraag.","en":"a = (2 − 8) ÷ 5 = −1.2 m·s⁻². The negative sign shows that the acceleration is opposite to the direction of motion – the cyclist slows down."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 25 m (b) a = −1,2 m·s⁻² (1,2 m·s⁻² teenoor die bewegingsrigting)","en":"(a) 25 m (b) a = −1.2 m·s⁻² (1.2 m·s⁻² opposite to the direction of motion)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter bewegingsvergelyking bevat NIE die tydsinterval Δt nie?","en":"Which equation of motion does NOT contain the time interval Δt?"},"options":[{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt"},{"af":"Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt²","en":"Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt²"},{"af":"Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt","en":"Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt"},{"af":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx","en":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx is die enigste vergelyking sonder Δt. Gebruik dit wanneer die tyd nie gegee is nie en ook nie gevra word nie.","en":"v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx is the only equation without Δt. Use it when the time is neither given nor asked for."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die bewegingsvergelykings mag slegs gebruik word as die versnelling konstant (eenvormig) is.","en":"The equations of motion may only be used if the acceleration is constant (uniform)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die vergelykings geld net vir eenvormige versnelling. As a verander, breek die beweging op in stadiums waarin a konstant is.","en":"True. The equations only hold for uniform acceleration. If a changes, split the motion into stages in which a is constant."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skakel 54 km·h⁻¹ om na m·s⁻¹: ___ m·s⁻¹","en":"Convert 54 km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹: ___ m·s⁻¹"},"answers":{"af":["15","15 m·s⁻¹","15 m/s","15 m.s-1","15 m s-1","15 ms-1","15 m·s-1"],"en":["15","15 m·s⁻¹","15 m/s","15 m.s-1","15 m s-1","15 ms-1","15 m·s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"Deel deur 3,6: 54 ÷ 3,6 = 15 m·s⁻¹ (want 1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s).","en":"Divide by 3.6: 54 ÷ 3.6 = 15 m·s⁻¹ (because 1 km·h⁻¹ = 1 000 m ÷ 3 600 s)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["194,4","54000","0,9"],"en":["194.4","54000","0.9"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke frase in 'n vraag by die versteekte inligting wat dit gee (bewegingsrigting = positief).","en":"Match each phrase in a question to the hidden information it gives (direction of motion = positive)."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"begin uit rus","en":"starts from rest"},"r":{"af":"v_i = 0","en":"v_i = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"kom tot stilstand","en":"comes to rest"},"r":{"af":"v_f = 0","en":"v_f = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"beweeg teen konstante snelheid","en":"moves at constant velocity"},"r":{"af":"a = 0","en":"a = 0"}},{"l":{"af":"rem eenvormig","en":"brakes uniformly"},"r":{"af":"a is negatief","en":"a is negative"}}],"explain":{"af":"Uit rus → v_i = 0; tot stilstand → v_f = 0; konstante snelheid → geen versnelling nie; rem → a is teenoor die beweging, dus negatief.","en":"From rest → v_i = 0; to rest → v_f = 0; constant velocity → no acceleration; braking → a is opposite to the motion, so negative."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry oos en rem. Oos word as positief gekies. Watter tekens het die snelheid en die versnelling terwyl die motor rem?","en":"A car travels east and brakes. East is chosen as positive. What signs do the velocity and the acceleration have while the car is braking?"},"options":[{"af":"v positief, a positief","en":"v positive, a positive"},{"af":"v negatief, a negatief","en":"v negative, a negative"},{"af":"v positief, a negatief","en":"v positive, a negative"},{"af":"v negatief, a positief","en":"v negative, a positive"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die motor beweeg nog oos, dus is v positief. Dit word stadiger, dus is a teenoor die beweging (wes): negatief. 'n Algemene fout is om te dink die snelheid word ook negatief sodra die motor rem.","en":"The car is still moving east, so v is positive. It is slowing down, so a is opposite to the motion (west): negative. A common mistake is to think the velocity also becomes negative as soon as the car brakes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Negatiewe versnelling beteken altyd dat 'n voorwerp stadiger beweeg.","en":"A negative acceleration always means that an object is slowing down."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die teken wys net die rigting. As 'n voorwerp in die negatiewe rigting beweeg en a ook negatief is, wys v en a in dieselfde rigting en word die voorwerp vinniger.","en":"False. The sign only shows the direction. If an object moves in the negative direction and a is also negative, v and a point the same way and the object speeds up."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Taxi begin uit rus en versnel eenvormig teen 2,5 m·s⁻² vir 4 s. Wat is sy snelheid na 4 s?","en":"A taxi starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 2.5 m·s⁻² for 4 s. What is its velocity after 4 s?"},"options":[{"af":"1,6 m·s⁻¹","en":"1.6 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"10 m·s⁻¹","en":"10 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"6,5 m·s⁻¹","en":"6.5 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"20 m·s⁻¹","en":"20 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt = 0 + (2,5)(4) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Die 20 is die verplasing in meter (½aΔt² = ½(2,5)(16)), nie die snelheid nie.","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt = 0 + (2.5)(4) = 10 m·s⁻¹. The 20 is the displacement in metres (½aΔt² = ½(2.5)(16)), not the velocity."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Fietsryer begin uit rus en versnel eenvormig teen 1,5 m·s⁻² vir 6 s. Sy verplasing in hierdie tyd is ___ m.","en":"A cyclist starts from rest and accelerates uniformly at 1.5 m·s⁻² for 6 s. His displacement in this time is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["27","27 m"],"en":["27","27 m"]},"explain":{"af":"v_f is nie nodig nie: Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt² = 0 + ½(1,5)(6)² = ½(1,5)(36) = 27 m.","en":"v_f is not needed: Δx = v_iΔt + ½aΔt² = 0 + ½(1.5)(6)² = ½(1.5)(36) = 27 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["54","4,5","9"],"en":["54","4.5","9"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 20 m·s⁻¹ en rem eenvormig tot stilstand in 5 s. Wat is sy versnelling? (Neem die bewegingsrigting as positief.)","en":"A car travels at 20 m·s⁻¹ and brakes uniformly to rest in 5 s. What is its acceleration? (Take the direction of motion as positive.)"},"options":[{"af":"4 m·s⁻²","en":"4 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−0,25 m·s⁻²","en":"−0.25 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−100 m·s⁻²","en":"−100 m·s⁻²"},{"af":"−4 m·s⁻²","en":"−4 m·s⁻²"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"v_f = v_i + aΔt → 0 = 20 + a(5) → a = −4 m·s⁻². Die minusteken wys dat die versnelling teenoor die beweging is; +4 m·s⁻² vergeet die teken.","en":"v_f = v_i + aΔt → 0 = 20 + a(5) → a = −4 m·s⁻². The minus sign shows that the acceleration is opposite to the motion; +4 m·s⁻² forgets the sign."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry teen 30 m·s⁻¹ en rem met 'n versnelling van −5 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Die remafstand is ___ m.","en":"A car travels at 30 m·s⁻¹ and brakes to rest with an acceleration of −5 m·s⁻². The braking distance is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["90","90 m"],"en":["90","90 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Δt is nie bekend nie: v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx → 0 = 30² + 2(−5)Δx → 0 = 900 − 10Δx → Δx = 90 m.","en":"Δt is not known: v_f² = v_i² + 2aΔx → 0 = 30² + 2(−5)Δx → 0 = 900 − 10Δx → Δx = 90 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["−90","180","6"],"en":["−90","180","6"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motorfiets versnel eenvormig van 10 m·s⁻¹ tot 30 m·s⁻¹ oor 'n afstand van 100 m. Hoe lank neem dit?","en":"A motorbike accelerates uniformly from 10 m·s⁻¹ to 30 m·s⁻¹ over a distance of 100 m. How long does it take?"},"options":[{"af":"5 s","en":"5 s"},{"af":"2,5 s","en":"2.5 s"},{"af":"10 s","en":"10 s"},{"af":"3,33 s","en":"3.33 s"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"a is onbekend en word nie gevra nie, dus Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt → 100 = ½(10 + 30)Δt = 20Δt → Δt = 5 s. 2,5 s kry jy as jy die ½ vergeet; 10 s as jy die snelhede aftrek in plaas van optel.","en":"a is unknown and not asked for, so Δx = ½(v_i + v_f)Δt → 100 = ½(10 + 30)Δt = 20Δt → Δt = 5 s. You get 2.5 s if you forget the ½; 10 s if you subtract the velocities instead of adding them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Taxi begin uit rus, versnel eenvormig teen 2 m·s⁻² vir 5 s en ry dan 10 s lank teen konstante snelheid. Die totale verplasing is ___ m.","en":"A taxi starts from rest, accelerates uniformly at 2 m·s⁻² for 5 s and then drives at constant velocity for 10 s. The total displacement is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["125","125 m"],"en":["125","125 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Stadium 1: Δx₁ = ½(2)(5)² = 25 m en v_f = 0 + (2)(5) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Stadium 2 (a = 0): Δx₂ = (10)(10) = 100 m. Totaal: 25 + 100 = 125 m.","en":"Stage 1: Δx₁ = ½(2)(5)² = 25 m and v_f = 0 + (2)(5) = 10 m·s⁻¹. Stage 2 (a = 0): Δx₂ = (10)(10) = 100 m. Total: 25 + 100 = 125 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["25","100","225"],"en":["25","100","225"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bestuurder ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹ toe 'n robot 50 m voor hom rooi word. Sy reaksietyd is 0,75 s, en daarna vertraag die motor eenvormig teen 5 m·s⁻² tot stilstand. Stop die motor voor die stopstreep?","en":"A driver travels at 72 km·h⁻¹ when a robot 50 m ahead turns red. His reaction time is 0.75 s, after which the car slows down uniformly at 5 m·s⁻² until it stops. Does the car stop before the stop line?"},"options":[{"af":"Ja – die remafstand is 40 m, dus stop dit 10 m voor die streep.","en":"Yes – the braking distance is 40 m, so it stops 10 m before the line."},{"af":"Ja – die totale stopafstand is net 17 m.","en":"Yes – the total stopping distance is only 17 m."},{"af":"Nee – die totale stopafstand is 55 m, dus stop dit 5 m oor die streep.","en":"No – the total stopping distance is 55 m, so it stops 5 m past the line."},{"af":"Nee – die totale stopafstand is 95 m.","en":"No – the total stopping distance is 95 m."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Reaksie-afstand = (20)(0,75) = 15 m. Remafstand: 0 = 20² + 2(−5)Δx → Δx = 40 m. Stopafstand = 15 + 40 = 55 m > 50 m. 'Ja, 40 m' vergeet die reaksie-afstand; 95 m vergeet die 2 in 2aΔx.","en":"72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. Reaction distance = (20)(0.75) = 15 m. Braking distance: 0 = 20² + 2(−5)Δx → Δx = 40 m. Stopping distance = 15 + 40 = 55 m > 50 m. 'Yes, 40 m' forgets the reaction distance; 95 m forgets the 2 in 2aΔx."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: \"As jy twee keer so vinnig ry, is jou remafstand twee keer so lank (met dieselfde remvertraging).\" Evalueer sy stelling.","en":"Thabo says: \"If you drive twice as fast, your braking distance is twice as long (with the same braking deceleration).\" Evaluate his statement."},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg – die remafstand is direk eweredig aan die spoed.","en":"He is right – the braking distance is directly proportional to the speed."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand word vier keer so lank, want remafstand = v_i² ÷ (2 × grootte van a).","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance becomes four times as long, because braking distance = v_i² ÷ (2 × magnitude of a)."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand bly dieselfde, want die remme is dieselfde.","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance stays the same, because the brakes are the same."},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd – die remafstand halveer, want die motor stop vinniger.","en":"He is wrong – the braking distance halves, because the car stops faster."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Met v_f = 0: 0 = v_i² + 2aΔx, dus is die remafstand eweredig aan v_i². Verdubbel v_i → remafstand × 4. Bv. 20 m·s⁻¹ en a = −5 m·s⁻² gee 40 m; 40 m·s⁻¹ gee 160 m. Daarom is spoed so gevaarlik.","en":"With v_f = 0: 0 = v_i² + 2aΔx, so the braking distance is proportional to v_i². Double v_i → braking distance × 4. E.g. 20 m·s⁻¹ and a = −5 m·s⁻² gives 40 m; 40 m·s⁻¹ gives 160 m. That is why speeding is so dangerous."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Energie en die hidrosfeer","en":"Energy and the hydrosphere"},"topics":[{"id":"f10-t4-energie","title":{"af":"Energie","en":"Energy"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal swaartekragpotensiële, kinetiese en meganiese energie kan bereken en die wet van behoud van meganiese energie kan toepas op vallende voorwerpe, tuimeltreine en slingers.","en":"You will be able to calculate gravitational potential, kinetic and mechanical energy and apply the law of conservation of mechanical energy to falling objects, roller coasters and pendulums."},"summary":{"af":"## Energie\n\n**Energie** is die vermoë om arbeid te verrig. Energie is 'n **skalaar** (dit het geen rigting nie) en word in **joule (J)** gemeet: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻². In hierdie onderwerp werk ons met twee vorme van energie wat saam meganiese energie vorm.\n\n## Swaartekragpotensiële energie (E_{p})\n\n**Definisie:** Swaartekragpotensiële energie (gravitasionele potensiële energie) is die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie in die gravitasieveld relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt.\n\n**E_{p} = mgh**\n\n| Simbool | Betekenis | Eenheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| m | massa | kg |\n| g | gravitasieversnelling = 9,8 m·s⁻² | m·s⁻² |\n| h | hoogte bo die verwysingspunt | m |\n\n- By die verwysingspunt (gewoonlik die grond of die laagste punt) is h = 0, dus E_{p} = 0.\n- E_{p} is eweredig aan h: twee keer so hoog → twee keer soveel E_{p}.\n- 'n Rots bo-op 'n krans in die Magaliesberg het meer E_{p} as dieselfde rots onder by die pad.\n\n## Kinetiese energie (E_{k})\n\n**Definisie:** Kinetiese energie is die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging.\n\n**E_{k} = ½mv^{2}** (m in kg, v in m·s⁻¹)\n\n- E_{k} is eweredig aan m: verdubbel die massa → verdubbel E_{k}.\n- E_{k} is eweredig aan v^{2}: verdubbel die spoed → **vier keer** soveel E_{k}. Daarom is 'n botsing teen 120 km·h⁻¹ soveel erger as een teen 60 km·h⁻¹.\n- 'n Voorwerp in rus het E_{k} = 0.\n\n## Meganiese energie (E_{M})\n\n**Definisie:** Meganiese energie is die som van die swaartekragpotensiële energie en die kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp.\n\n**E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = mgh + ½mv^{2}**\n\n## Behoud van energie\n\n**Wet van behoud van energie:** Energie kan nie geskep of vernietig word nie; dit kan slegs van een vorm na 'n ander omgeskakel word.\n\n**Wet van behoud van meganiese energie:** Die totale meganiese energie van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem bly konstant. 'n Sisteem is geïsoleerd as daar **geen wrywing of lugweerstand** (geen eksterne kragte) is nie.\n\nWat 'n voorwerp aan E_{p} verloor, wen dit aan E_{k} – en andersom:\n\n**E_{M} (begin) = E_{M} (einde)** → mgh_{1} + ½mv_{1}^{2} = mgh_{2} + ½mv_{2}^{2}\n\n### Toepassings\n\n- **Vallende voorwerp** (uit rus, geen lugweerstand): bo is al die energie E_{p}; net voor die grond is al die energie E_{k}. mgh = ½mv^{2} → **v = √(2gh)**. Die massa kanselleer, dus tref 'n swaar en 'n ligte klip die grond met dieselfde spoed.\n- **Tuimeltrein (roller coaster):** die karretjie is die vinnigste by die laagste punt. As dit uit rus begin, kan dit (sonder wrywing) nooit hoër as die beginhoogte kom nie.\n- **Slinger:** by die hoogste punte (die draaipunte) is v = 0, dus E_{k} = 0 en E_{p} maksimum. By die laagste punt is E_{p} minimum (kies dit as h = 0) en E_{k} en die spoed maksimum.\n\n### As daar wel wrywing is\n\nMet wrywing of lugweerstand word meganiese energie **nie** behou nie: 'n deel word na **hitte (termiese energie) en klank** omgeskakel. Die **totale** energie bly steeds behoue: omgeskakelde energie = E_{M} (begin) − E_{M} (einde). Daarom swaai 'n slinger in die werklikheid al laer en stop dit uiteindelik.\n\n## Stappe vir 'n behoud-berekening\n\n1. Kies die verwysingspunt (h = 0) – gewoonlik die laagste punt.\n2. Skryf: E_{M} by die beginpunt = E_{M} by die eindpunt.\n3. Vervang mgh en ½mv^{2} aan albei kante (E_{k} = 0 waar die voorwerp in rus is; E_{p} = 0 by h = 0).\n4. Los op vir die onbekende en gee die eenheid. Rond eers aan die einde af tot twee desimale plekke.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** massa in gram gebruik (deel deur 1 000 om kg te kry); hoogte in cm gebruik (deel deur 100); km·h⁻¹ nie na m·s⁻¹ omgeskakel nie; E_{k} = mv^{2} sonder die ½; die vierkantswortel vergeet as jy v bereken; die beginhoogte gebruik in plaas van die hoogte wat die voorwerp gedaal het.\n\n> **Onthou!** Energie is 'n skalaar – moet nooit 'n rigting by 'n energie-antwoord skryf nie. Gebruik altyd g = 9,8 m·s⁻².","en":"## Energy\n\n**Energy** is the ability to do work. Energy is a **scalar** (it has no direction) and is measured in **joules (J)**: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻². In this topic we work with two forms of energy that together make up mechanical energy.\n\n## Gravitational potential energy (E_{p})\n\n**Definition:** Gravitational potential energy is the energy an object possesses due to its position in the gravitational field relative to a reference point.\n\n**E_{p} = mgh**\n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Unit |\n|---|---|---|\n| m | mass | kg |\n| g | gravitational acceleration = 9.8 m·s⁻² | m·s⁻² |\n| h | height above the reference point | m |\n\n- At the reference point (usually the ground or the lowest point) h = 0, so E_{p} = 0.\n- E_{p} is proportional to h: twice as high → twice as much E_{p}.\n- A rock on top of a cliff in the Magaliesberg has more E_{p} than the same rock down by the road.\n\n## Kinetic energy (E_{k})\n\n**Definition:** Kinetic energy is the energy an object possesses as a result of its motion.\n\n**E_{k} = ½mv^{2}** (m in kg, v in m·s⁻¹)\n\n- E_{k} is proportional to m: double the mass → double E_{k}.\n- E_{k} is proportional to v^{2}: double the speed → **four times** as much E_{k}. That is why a crash at 120 km·h⁻¹ is so much worse than one at 60 km·h⁻¹.\n- An object at rest has E_{k} = 0.\n\n## Mechanical energy (E_{M})\n\n**Definition:** Mechanical energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy and the kinetic energy of an object.\n\n**E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = mgh + ½mv^{2}**\n\n## Conservation of energy\n\n**Law of conservation of energy:** Energy cannot be created or destroyed; it can only be changed from one form into another.\n\n**Law of conservation of mechanical energy:** The total mechanical energy of an isolated system remains constant. A system is isolated if there is **no friction or air resistance** (no external forces).\n\nWhat an object loses in E_{p}, it gains in E_{k} – and vice versa:\n\n**E_{M} (start) = E_{M} (end)** → mgh_{1} + ½mv_{1}^{2} = mgh_{2} + ½mv_{2}^{2}\n\n### Applications\n\n- **Falling object** (from rest, no air resistance): at the top all the energy is E_{p}; just before the ground all the energy is E_{k}. mgh = ½mv^{2} → **v = √(2gh)**. The mass cancels, so a heavy and a light stone hit the ground with the same speed.\n- **Roller coaster:** the cart is fastest at the lowest point. If it starts from rest, it can (without friction) never get higher than its starting height.\n- **Pendulum:** at the highest points (the turning points) v = 0, so E_{k} = 0 and E_{p} is maximum. At the lowest point E_{p} is minimum (choose it as h = 0) and E_{k} and the speed are maximum.\n\n### When there is friction\n\nWith friction or air resistance, mechanical energy is **not** conserved: part of it is converted into **heat (thermal energy) and sound**. The **total** energy is still conserved: energy converted = E_{M} (start) − E_{M} (end). That is why a real pendulum swings lower and lower and eventually stops.\n\n## Steps for a conservation calculation\n\n1. Choose the reference point (h = 0) – usually the lowest point.\n2. Write: E_{M} at the starting point = E_{M} at the end point.\n3. Substitute mgh and ½mv^{2} on both sides (E_{k} = 0 where the object is at rest; E_{p} = 0 at h = 0).\n4. Solve for the unknown and give the unit. Only round off at the end, to two decimal places.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** using mass in grams (divide by 1 000 to get kg); using height in cm (divide by 100); not converting km·h⁻¹ to m·s⁻¹; E_{k} = mv^{2} without the ½; forgetting the square root when you calculate v; using the starting height instead of the height the object has dropped.\n\n> **Remember!** Energy is a scalar – never write a direction with an energy answer. Always use g = 9.8 m·s⁻²."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Energie","en":"Energy"},"def":{"af":"Die vermoë om arbeid te verrig. Energie is 'n skalaar en word in joule (J) gemeet.","en":"The ability to do work. Energy is a scalar and is measured in joules (J)."}},{"term":{"af":"Swaartekragpotensiële energie (E_p)","en":"Gravitational potential energy (E_p)"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie in die gravitasieveld relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt. E_p = mgh.","en":"The energy an object possesses due to its position in the gravitational field relative to a reference point. E_p = mgh."}},{"term":{"af":"Kinetiese energie (E_k)","en":"Kinetic energy (E_k)"},"def":{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging. E_k = ½mv².","en":"The energy an object possesses as a result of its motion. E_k = ½mv²."}},{"term":{"af":"Meganiese energie (E_M)","en":"Mechanical energy (E_M)"},"def":{"af":"Die som van die swaartekragpotensiële energie en die kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp. E_M = E_p + E_k.","en":"The sum of the gravitational potential energy and the kinetic energy of an object. E_M = E_p + E_k."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van energie","en":"Law of conservation of energy"},"def":{"af":"Energie kan nie geskep of vernietig word nie; dit kan slegs van een vorm na 'n ander omgeskakel word.","en":"Energy cannot be created or destroyed; it can only be changed from one form into another."}},{"term":{"af":"Wet van behoud van meganiese energie","en":"Law of conservation of mechanical energy"},"def":{"af":"Die totale meganiese energie van 'n geïsoleerde sisteem (geen wrywing of lugweerstand nie) bly konstant.","en":"The total mechanical energy of an isolated system (no friction or air resistance) remains constant."}},{"term":{"af":"Geïsoleerde sisteem","en":"Isolated system"},"def":{"af":"'n Sisteem waarop geen eksterne kragte soos wrywing of lugweerstand inwerk nie, sodat die meganiese energie behoue bly.","en":"A system on which no external forces such as friction or air resistance act, so that mechanical energy is conserved."}},{"term":{"af":"Verwysingspunt","en":"Reference point"},"def":{"af":"Die gekose posisie waar h = 0 en dus E_p = 0 – gewoonlik die grond of die laagste punt van die beweging.","en":"The chosen position where h = 0 and therefore E_p = 0 – usually the ground or the lowest point of the motion."}},{"term":{"af":"Joule (J)","en":"Joule (J)"},"def":{"af":"Die SI-eenheid van energie: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻².","en":"The SI unit of energy: 1 J = 1 kg·m²·s⁻²."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Potensiële, kinetiese en meganiese energie","en":"Potential, kinetic and mechanical energy"},"problem":{"af":"'n Witkruisarend met 'n massa van 4 kg sweef 50 m bo die grond langs die Magaliesberg teen 'n spoed van 10 m·s⁻¹. Neem die grond as verwysingspunt en bereken die arend se (a) swaartekragpotensiële energie, (b) kinetiese energie en (c) meganiese energie.","en":"A Verreaux's (black) eagle with a mass of 4 kg glides 50 m above the ground along the Magaliesberg at a speed of 10 m·s⁻¹. Take the ground as reference point and calculate the eagle's (a) gravitational potential energy, (b) kinetic energy and (c) mechanical energy."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) E_{p} = mgh = (4)(9,8)(50) = 1 960 J","en":"(a) E_{p} = mgh = (4)(9.8)(50) = 1 960 J"},{"af":"(b) E_{k} = ½mv^{2} = ½(4)(10)^{2} = ½(4)(100) = 200 J – kwadreer net die spoed.","en":"(b) E_{k} = ½mv^{2} = ½(4)(10)^{2} = ½(4)(100) = 200 J – square only the speed."},{"af":"(c) E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = 1 960 + 200 = 2 160 J","en":"(c) E_{M} = E_{p} + E_{k} = 1 960 + 200 = 2 160 J"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 1 960 J (b) 200 J (c) 2 160 J","en":"(a) 1 960 J (b) 200 J (c) 2 160 J"}},{"title":{"af":"Vallende klip","en":"Falling stone"},"problem":{"af":"'n Klip van 200 g word uit rus van 'n brug 20 m bo die water van die Krokodilrivier laat val. Ignoreer lugweerstand. Bereken (a) die klip se meganiese energie bo-op die brug en (b) sy spoed net voordat hy die water tref.","en":"A 200 g stone is dropped from rest from a bridge 20 m above the water of the Crocodile River. Ignore air resistance. Calculate (a) the stone's mechanical energy at the top of the bridge and (b) its speed just before it hits the water."},"steps":[{"af":"Skakel om: m = 200 g = 0,2 kg. Kies die wateroppervlak as verwysingspunt (h = 0).","en":"Convert: m = 200 g = 0.2 kg. Choose the water surface as reference point (h = 0)."},{"af":"(a) Bo is v = 0, dus E_{k} = 0. E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (0,2)(9,8)(20) = 39,2 J","en":"(a) At the top v = 0, so E_{k} = 0. E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (0.2)(9.8)(20) = 39.2 J"},{"af":"(b) Geen lugweerstand nie, dus word E_{M} behou: E_{M} bo = E_{M} onder → 39,2 = 0 + ½(0,2)v^{2}","en":"(b) No air resistance, so E_{M} is conserved: E_{M} top = E_{M} bottom → 39.2 = 0 + ½(0.2)v^{2}"},{"af":"v^{2} = 39,2 ÷ 0,1 = 392 → v = √392 = 19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"v^{2} = 39.2 ÷ 0.1 = 392 → v = √392 = 19.80 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"Kontrole: v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9,8 × 20) = 19,80 m·s⁻¹ – die massa kanselleer.","en":"Check: v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9.8 × 20) = 19.80 m·s⁻¹ – the mass cancels."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 39,2 J (b) 19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"(a) 39.2 J (b) 19.80 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Tuimeltrein","en":"Roller coaster"},"problem":{"af":"'n Tuimeltrein-karretjie met passasiers het 'n totale massa van 600 kg. Dit begin uit rus by punt A, 30 m bo die grond, rol af na punt B (5 m bo die grond) en klim dan na punt C (18 m bo die grond). Ignoreer wrywing. Bereken die spoed by B en by C.","en":"A roller-coaster cart with passengers has a total mass of 600 kg. It starts from rest at point A, 30 m above the ground, rolls down to point B (5 m above the ground) and then climbs to point C (18 m above the ground). Ignore friction. Calculate the speed at B and at C."},"steps":[{"af":"Verwysingspunt: die grond. By A is v = 0, dus E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (600)(9,8)(30) = 176 400 J. Sonder wrywing bly E_{M} oral 176 400 J.","en":"Reference point: the ground. At A v = 0, so E_{M} = E_{p} = mgh = (600)(9.8)(30) = 176 400 J. Without friction E_{M} stays 176 400 J everywhere."},{"af":"By B: E_{p} = (600)(9,8)(5) = 29 400 J, dus E_{k} = E_{M} − E_{p} = 176 400 − 29 400 = 147 000 J","en":"At B: E_{p} = (600)(9.8)(5) = 29 400 J, so E_{k} = E_{M} − E_{p} = 176 400 − 29 400 = 147 000 J"},{"af":"½(600)v_{B}^{2} = 147 000 → v_{B}^{2} = 490 → v_{B} = 22,14 m·s⁻¹","en":"½(600)v_{B}^{2} = 147 000 → v_{B}^{2} = 490 → v_{B} = 22.14 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"By C: E_{p} = (600)(9,8)(18) = 105 840 J, dus E_{k} = 176 400 − 105 840 = 70 560 J","en":"At C: E_{p} = (600)(9.8)(18) = 105 840 J, so E_{k} = 176 400 − 105 840 = 70 560 J"},{"af":"½(600)v_{C}^{2} = 70 560 → v_{C}^{2} = 235,2 → v_{C} = 15,34 m·s⁻¹. (C is hoër as B, dus is die karretjie daar stadiger.)","en":"½(600)v_{C}^{2} = 70 560 → v_{C}^{2} = 235.2 → v_{C} = 15.34 m·s⁻¹. (C is higher than B, so the cart is slower there.)"}],"answer":{"af":"v_{B} = 22,14 m·s⁻¹; v_{C} = 15,34 m·s⁻¹","en":"v_{B} = 22.14 m·s⁻¹; v_{C} = 15.34 m·s⁻¹"}},{"title":{"af":"Slinger","en":"Pendulum"},"problem":{"af":"'n Slinger se gewig (massa 0,5 kg) word opgetrek tot 0,2 m bo sy laagste punt en uit rus gelos. Ignoreer lugweerstand. (a) Waar is die gewig se spoed die grootste? Verduidelik. (b) Bereken die maksimum spoed. (c) In die werklikheid swaai die slinger al laer en stop dit uiteindelik. Verduidelik waarom.","en":"A pendulum bob (mass 0.5 kg) is pulled up to 0.2 m above its lowest point and released from rest. Ignore air resistance. (a) Where is the bob's speed the greatest? Explain. (b) Calculate the maximum speed. (c) In reality the pendulum swings lower and lower and eventually stops. Explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) By die laagste punt. Daar is E_{p} die kleinste (h = 0). Omdat E_{M} konstant bly, is E_{k} – en dus die spoed – daar die grootste.","en":"(a) At the lowest point. There E_{p} is the smallest (h = 0). Because E_{M} stays constant, E_{k} – and therefore the speed – is the greatest there."},{"af":"(b) By die hoogste punt: E_{k} = 0 en E_{p} = mgh = (0,5)(9,8)(0,2) = 0,98 J, dus E_{M} = 0,98 J","en":"(b) At the highest point: E_{k} = 0 and E_{p} = mgh = (0.5)(9.8)(0.2) = 0.98 J, so E_{M} = 0.98 J"},{"af":"By die laagste punt: E_{p} = 0, dus E_{k} = 0,98 J → ½(0,5)v^{2} = 0,98 → v^{2} = 3,92 → v = 1,98 m·s⁻¹","en":"At the lowest point: E_{p} = 0, so E_{k} = 0.98 J → ½(0.5)v^{2} = 0.98 → v^{2} = 3.92 → v = 1.98 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"(c) Lugweerstand (en wrywing by die ophangpunt) werk teen die beweging. 'n Deel van die meganiese energie word na hitte en klank omgeskakel, dus neem E_{M} af en bereik die gewig elke swaai 'n laer hoogte. Die totale energie bly wel behoue.","en":"(c) Air resistance (and friction at the pivot) acts against the motion. Part of the mechanical energy is converted into heat and sound, so E_{M} decreases and the bob reaches a lower height with every swing. The total energy is still conserved."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) By die laagste punt (b) 1,98 m·s⁻¹ (c) Lugweerstand en wrywing skakel meganiese energie na hitte en klank om.","en":"(a) At the lowest point (b) 1.98 m·s⁻¹ (c) Air resistance and friction convert mechanical energy into heat and sound."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is die definisie van kinetiese energie?","en":"Which statement is the definition of kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy posisie relatief tot 'n verwysingspunt.","en":"The energy an object possesses due to its position relative to a reference point."},{"af":"Die som van die swaartekragpotensiële en kinetiese energie van 'n voorwerp.","en":"The sum of the gravitational potential and kinetic energy of an object."},{"af":"Die energie wat 'n voorwerp besit as gevolg van sy beweging.","en":"The energy an object possesses as a result of its motion."},{"af":"Die energie wat in die chemiese bindings van 'n stof gestoor is.","en":"The energy stored in the chemical bonds of a substance."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kinetiese energie is bewegingsenergie. Die eerste opsie is die definisie van swaartekragpotensiële energie en die tweede dié van meganiese energie.","en":"Kinetic energy is energy of motion. The first option is the definition of gravitational potential energy and the second that of mechanical energy."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke grootheid by die regte formule of eenheid.","en":"Match each quantity to the correct formula or unit."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Swaartekragpotensiële energie","en":"Gravitational potential energy"},"r":{"af":"mgh","en":"mgh"}},{"l":{"af":"Kinetiese energie","en":"Kinetic energy"},"r":{"af":"½mv²","en":"½mv²"}},{"l":{"af":"Meganiese energie","en":"Mechanical energy"},"r":{"af":"E_p + E_k","en":"E_p + E_k"}},{"l":{"af":"Eenheid van energie","en":"Unit of energy"},"r":{"af":"joule (J) = kg·m²·s⁻²","en":"joule (J) = kg·m²·s⁻²"}}],"explain":{"af":"E_p = mgh, E_k = ½mv², E_M = E_p + E_k, en alle vorme van energie word in joule gemeet.","en":"E_p = mgh, E_k = ½mv², E_M = E_p + E_k, and all forms of energy are measured in joules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Boks van 5 kg staan op 'n rak 2 m bo die vloer. Sy swaartekragpotensiële energie relatief tot die vloer is ___ J.","en":"A 5 kg box stands on a shelf 2 m above the floor. Its gravitational potential energy relative to the floor is ___ J."},"answers":{"af":["98","98 J","98 joule"],"en":["98","98 J","98 joule"]},"explain":{"af":"E_p = mgh = (5)(9,8)(2) = 98 J.","en":"E_p = mgh = (5)(9.8)(2) = 98 J."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","49","24,5"],"en":["10","49","24.5"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Slinger het sy grootste kinetiese energie by sy hoogste punt.","en":"A pendulum has its greatest kinetic energy at its highest point."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. By die hoogste punt staan die gewig vir 'n oomblik stil: v = 0, dus E_k = 0 en E_p is maksimum. E_k is die grootste by die laagste punt.","en":"False. At the highest point the bob is momentarily at rest: v = 0, so E_k = 0 and E_p is maximum. E_k is greatest at the lowest point."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"As die spoed van 'n motor verdubbel, wat gebeur met sy kinetiese energie?","en":"If the speed of a car doubles, what happens to its kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit verdubbel.","en":"It doubles."},{"af":"Dit word vier keer groter.","en":"It becomes four times greater."},{"af":"Dit halveer.","en":"It halves."},{"af":"Dit bly dieselfde, want die massa het nie verander nie.","en":"It stays the same, because the mass has not changed."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"E_k = ½mv²: die spoed word gekwadreer, dus (2)² = 4. Verdubbel die spoed → vier keer soveel E_k. 'Dit verdubbel' geld vir die massa, nie die spoed nie.","en":"E_k = ½mv²: the speed is squared, so (2)² = 4. Double the speed → four times as much E_k. 'It doubles' applies to the mass, not the speed."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Swaar klip en 'n ligte klip word uit rus van dieselfde hoogte laat val. Sonder lugweerstand tref hulle die grond met dieselfde spoed.","en":"A heavy stone and a light stone are dropped from rest from the same height. Without air resistance they hit the ground with the same speed."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh): die massa kanselleer. Die swaar klip het wel meer E_k, maar dieselfde spoed.","en":"True. mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh): the mass cancels. The heavy stone does have more E_k, but the same speed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor van 1 200 kg ry teen 72 km·h⁻¹. Wat is sy kinetiese energie?","en":"A 1 200 kg car travels at 72 km·h⁻¹. What is its kinetic energy?"},"options":[{"af":"240 000 J","en":"240 000 J"},{"af":"3 110 400 J","en":"3 110 400 J"},{"af":"12 000 J","en":"12 000 J"},{"af":"480 000 J","en":"480 000 J"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: 72 ÷ 3,6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. E_k = ½(1 200)(20)² = 240 000 J. 3 110 400 J gebruik 72 sonder omskakeling, 12 000 J vergeet om te kwadreer en 480 000 J vergeet die ½.","en":"Convert first: 72 ÷ 3.6 = 20 m·s⁻¹. E_k = ½(1 200)(20)² = 240 000 J. 3 110 400 J uses 72 without converting, 12 000 J forgets to square and 480 000 J forgets the ½."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Rugbybal van 450 g word teen 20 m·s⁻¹ geskop. Die bal se kinetiese energie is ___ J.","en":"A 450 g rugby ball is kicked at 20 m·s⁻¹. The ball's kinetic energy is ___ J."},"answers":{"af":["90","90 J","90 joule"],"en":["90","90 J","90 joule"]},"explain":{"af":"m = 450 g = 0,45 kg. E_k = ½mv² = ½(0,45)(20)² = ½(0,45)(400) = 90 J.","en":"m = 450 g = 0.45 kg. E_k = ½mv² = ½(0.45)(20)² = ½(0.45)(400) = 90 J."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["90000","180","4,5"],"en":["90000","180","4.5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kolgans van 2 kg vlieg 10 m bo die grond teen 3 m·s⁻¹. Wat is sy meganiese energie relatief tot die grond?","en":"An Egyptian goose of 2 kg flies 10 m above the ground at 3 m·s⁻¹. What is its mechanical energy relative to the ground?"},"options":[{"af":"196 J","en":"196 J"},{"af":"187 J","en":"187 J"},{"af":"199 J","en":"199 J"},{"af":"205 J","en":"205 J"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"E_p = (2)(9,8)(10) = 196 J en E_k = ½(2)(3)² = 9 J, dus E_M = 196 + 9 = 205 J. 196 J is net E_p; 199 J vergeet om v te kwadreer; 187 J trek af in plaas van optel.","en":"E_p = (2)(9.8)(10) = 196 J and E_k = ½(2)(3)² = 9 J, so E_M = 196 + 9 = 205 J. 196 J is only E_p; 199 J forgets to square v; 187 J subtracts instead of adding."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Klip word uit rus van 'n hoogte van 5 m laat val. Ignoreer lugweerstand. Sy spoed net voordat hy die grond tref, is ___ m·s⁻¹.","en":"A stone is dropped from rest from a height of 5 m. Ignore air resistance. Its speed just before it hits the ground is ___ m·s⁻¹."},"answers":{"af":["9,90","9.90","9,90 m·s⁻¹","9.90 m·s⁻¹","9,90 m/s","9.90 m/s","9,90 m.s-1","9.90 m.s-1","9,90 m s-1","9.90 m s-1","9,90 ms-1","9.90 ms-1","9,90 m·s-1","9.90 m·s-1","9,9","9.9","9,9 m·s⁻¹","9.9 m·s⁻¹","9,9 m/s","9.9 m/s","9,9 m.s-1","9.9 m.s-1","9,9 m s-1","9.9 m s-1","9,9 ms-1","9.9 ms-1","9,9 m·s-1","9.9 m·s-1"],"en":["9,90","9.90","9,90 m·s⁻¹","9.90 m·s⁻¹","9,90 m/s","9.90 m/s","9,90 m.s-1","9.90 m.s-1","9,90 m s-1","9.90 m s-1","9,90 ms-1","9.90 ms-1","9,90 m·s-1","9.90 m·s-1","9,9","9.9","9,9 m·s⁻¹","9.9 m·s⁻¹","9,9 m/s","9.9 m/s","9,9 m.s-1","9.9 m.s-1","9,9 m s-1","9.9 m s-1","9,9 ms-1","9.9 ms-1","9,9 m·s-1","9.9 m·s-1"]},"explain":{"af":"E_M bo = E_M onder: mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9,8 × 5) = √98 = 9,90 m·s⁻¹. Die massa is nie nodig nie.","en":"E_M top = E_M bottom: mgh = ½mv² → v = √(2gh) = √(2 × 9.8 × 5) = √98 = 9.90 m·s⁻¹. The mass is not needed."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7,00","98,00","49,00"],"en":["7.00","98.00","49.00"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Tuimeltrein-karretjie begin uit rus by 'n punt 20 m bo die grond. Wat is sy spoed by 'n punt 8 m bo die grond? Ignoreer wrywing.","en":"A roller-coaster cart starts from rest at a point 20 m above the ground. What is its speed at a point 8 m above the ground? Ignore friction."},"options":[{"af":"12,52 m·s⁻¹","en":"12.52 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"15,34 m·s⁻¹","en":"15.34 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"19,80 m·s⁻¹","en":"19.80 m·s⁻¹"},{"af":"235,2 m·s⁻¹","en":"235.2 m·s⁻¹"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"mgh₁ = mgh₂ + ½mv² → ½v² = g(h₁ − h₂) = 9,8 × 12 → v² = 235,2 → v = 15,34 m·s⁻¹. Die karretjie het 12 m gedaal, nie 8 m of 20 m nie; 235,2 vergeet die vierkantswortel.","en":"mgh₁ = mgh₂ + ½mv² → ½v² = g(h₁ − h₂) = 9.8 × 12 → v² = 235.2 → v = 15.34 m·s⁻¹. The cart dropped 12 m, not 8 m or 20 m; 235.2 forgets the square root."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Blok gly teen 4 m·s⁻¹ oor 'n wrywinglose horisontale oppervlak en dan teen 'n wrywinglose helling op. Die maksimum hoogte wat die blok bereik, is ___ m.","en":"A block slides at 4 m·s⁻¹ across a frictionless horizontal surface and then up a frictionless slope. The maximum height the block reaches is ___ m."},"answers":{"af":["0,82","0.82","0,82 m","0.82 m"],"en":["0,82","0.82","0,82 m","0.82 m"]},"explain":{"af":"Onder: E_k = ½mv²; bo (v = 0): E_p = mgh. ½mv² = mgh → h = v² ÷ 2g = 16 ÷ 19,6 = 0,82 m.","en":"At the bottom: E_k = ½mv²; at the top (v = 0): E_p = mgh. ½mv² = mgh → h = v² ÷ 2g = 16 ÷ 19.6 = 0.82 m."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1,63","0,20","0,41"],"en":["1.63","0.20","0.41"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Slinger word uit rus 0,3 m bo sy laagste punt gelos. Lerato sê die gewig se spoed is die helfte van die maksimum spoed wanneer dit 0,15 m bo die laagste punt is. Johan sê dit is by 0,225 m. Wie is reg?","en":"A pendulum is released from rest 0.3 m above its lowest point. Lerato says the bob's speed is half the maximum speed when it is 0.15 m above the lowest point. Johan says it is at 0.225 m. Who is right?"},"options":[{"af":"Johan – by halwe spoed is E_k net ¼ van die maksimum, dus is ¾ van die energie nog E_p: h = ¾ × 0,3 = 0,225 m.","en":"Johan – at half speed E_k is only ¼ of the maximum, so ¾ of the energy is still E_p: h = ¾ × 0.3 = 0.225 m."},{"af":"Lerato – halwe spoed beteken halwe energie, dus h = ½ × 0,3 = 0,15 m.","en":"Lerato – half speed means half the energy, so h = ½ × 0.3 = 0.15 m."},{"af":"Albei is verkeerd – die hoogte is ¼ × 0,3 = 0,075 m.","en":"Both are wrong – the height is ¼ × 0.3 = 0.075 m."},{"af":"Albei is verkeerd – die hoogte hang van die massa af, wat nie gegee is nie.","en":"Both are wrong – the height depends on the mass, which is not given."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"E_k is eweredig aan v²: (½)² = ¼. By halwe spoed is E_k = ¼E_M, dus E_p = ¾E_M en h = ¾ × 0,3 = 0,225 m. Die massa kanselleer. Lerato neem verkeerdelik aan dat E_k eweredig aan v is.","en":"E_k is proportional to v²: (½)² = ¼. At half speed E_k = ¼E_M, so E_p = ¾E_M and h = ¾ × 0.3 = 0.225 m. The mass cancels. Lerato wrongly assumes that E_k is proportional to v."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder van 60 kg gly uit rus van die bopunt van 'n 4 m hoë waterglybaan af en bereik die onderkant teen 7 m·s⁻¹. Watter gevolgtrekking is korrek?","en":"A 60 kg learner slides from rest from the top of a 4 m high water slide and reaches the bottom at 7 m·s⁻¹. Which conclusion is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Meganiese energie is behou, want E_k onder is gelyk aan E_p bo.","en":"Mechanical energy is conserved, because E_k at the bottom equals E_p at the top."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is nie behou nie: 882 J is deur wrywing vernietig.","en":"Mechanical energy is not conserved: 882 J was destroyed by friction."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is nie behou nie: 882 J is deur wrywing na hitte en klank omgeskakel.","en":"Mechanical energy is not conserved: 882 J was converted into heat and sound by friction."},{"af":"Meganiese energie is behou, want die leerder se massa het nie verander nie.","en":"Mechanical energy is conserved, because the learner's mass did not change."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Bo: E_M = E_p = (60)(9,8)(4) = 2 352 J. Onder: E_M = E_k = ½(60)(7)² = 1 470 J. Die verskil van 882 J is nie 'vernietig' nie (energie kan nie vernietig word nie) – wrywing het dit na hitte en klank omgeskakel.","en":"Top: E_M = E_p = (60)(9.8)(4) = 2 352 J. Bottom: E_M = E_k = ½(60)(7)² = 1 470 J. The difference of 882 J was not 'destroyed' (energy cannot be destroyed) – friction converted it into heat and sound."}}]},{"id":"f10-t4-hidrosfeer","title":{"af":"Die hidrosfeer","en":"The hydrosphere"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die samestelling van die hidrosfeer, sy wisselwerking met ander globale sisteme, die waterkringloop, besoedeling, suiwering en die toetsing van watergehalte kan verduidelik – en waarom waterbewaring in Suid-Afrika so belangrik is.","en":"You will be able to explain the composition of the hydrosphere, its interaction with other global systems, the water cycle, pollution, purification and water-quality testing – and why water conservation is so important in South Africa."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is die hidrosfeer?\n\nDie **hidrosfeer** is al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak, in al drie toestande: oseane en seë, riviere, mere en damme, grondwater (bv. boorgate), ys (gletsers en poolyskappe), waterdamp in die atmosfeer en selfs die water in lewende organismes.\n\n- Ongeveer **97,5 %** van alle water is **soutwater**, meestal in die oseane.\n- Net ongeveer **2,5 %** is **varswater**, en die meeste daarvan is gevries in ys of lê diep onder die grond.\n- **Minder as 1 %** van al die water op aarde is varswater wat ons maklik kan gebruik.\n\n### Hoekom is water so spesiaal?\n\n- Water is 'n **polêre** molekule en los baie stowwe op. Daarom is water in die natuur **nooit suiwer nie** – dit bevat altyd opgeloste ione en gasse.\n- Water het 'n hoë **spesifieke warmtekapasiteit**: die oseane warm stadig op en koel stadig af en reguleer so die aarde se klimaat.\n\n## Wisselwerking met ander globale sisteme\n\n| Sisteem | Wisselwerking met die hidrosfeer |\n|---|---|\n| Atmosfeer (lug) | verdamping en neerslag; O_{2} en CO_{2} los in water op; die beweging van water en energie dryf die weer |\n| Litosfeer (rotse en grond) | water verweer en erodeer rotse; dit los minerale (ione) uit rotse en grond op; grondwater word in rotse gestoor |\n| Biosfeer (lewende dinge) | plante neem water op vir fotosintese en gee waterdamp af (transpirasie); water is 'n habitat; alle selle bevat water |\n\n## Die waterkringloop\n\nDie **son** se energie dryf die kringloop; **swaartekrag** laat reën val en water afloop.\n\n1. **Verdamping:** water uit oseane, damme en riviere word waterdamp.\n2. **Transpirasie:** plante gee waterdamp deur hul blare af.\n3. **Kondensasie:** waterdamp styg, koel af en kondenseer tot druppeltjies wat wolke vorm.\n4. **Neerslag:** water val as reën, hael of sneeu.\n5. **Afloop en infiltrasie:** water vloei oor die oppervlak na riviere en damme, of sypel in die grond in en word **grondwater**.\n\n## Water as hulpbron in Suid-Afrika\n\nSuid-Afrika is 'n **waterskaars** land – een van die 30 droogste lande ter wêreld. Ons gemiddelde reënval is ongeveer 500 mm per jaar, teenoor 'n wêreldgemiddeld van ongeveer 860 mm. **Landbou** (besproeiing) gebruik die meeste water (ongeveer 60 %). Gauteng kry deel van sy water via die Lesotho-Hooglandwaterprojek en die Vaalrivier. Tydens beurtkrag staan pompe stil, wat tot wateronderbrekings lei.\n\n## Besoedeling\n\n| Besoedelstof | Bron | Gevolg |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rioolwater | swak bestuurde rioolwerke | bakterieë (bv. *E. coli*, cholera) → siektes |\n| Kunsmis (nitrate, fosfate) | plase, rioolwater | eutrofikasie |\n| Suur mynwater | ou goud- en steenkoolmyne | lae pH, swaar metale, sulfate |\n| Swaar metale (lood, kwik) | nywerhede | giftig; hoop in voedselkettings op |\n| Plastiek en rommel | mense | versmoor diere, verstop riviere |\n| Warm water (termiese besoedeling) | kragstasies, fabrieke | warm water hou minder suurstof op |\n\n**Eutrofikasie:** te veel voedingstowwe (nitrate en fosfate) → alge en waterplante (bv. waterhiasint) groei explosief → hulle blok sonlig, en wanneer hulle vrek, gebruik **bakterieë** wat die dooie materiaal afbreek die **opgeloste suurstof** op → visse vrek. Hartbeespoortdam is 'n bekende voorbeeld: afvalwater van rioolwerke stroomop in Gauteng bring baie fosfate in die dam.\n\n## Ione in water\n\nWater los ione uit rotse en grond op, bv. Na^{+}, Ca^{2+}, Mg^{2+}, Cl^{−}, SO_{4}^{2−}, HCO_{3}^{−} en NO_{3}^{−}. Klein hoeveelhede is onskadelik; hoë vlakke maak water onveilig.\n\n- **Harde water** bevat baie **Ca^{2+}- en Mg^{2+}-ione**. Dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat **ketelsteen** in ketels en geisers.\n- **Sagte water** bevat min van hierdie ione.\n\n## Watergehalte toets\n\n- **pH:** pH < 7 is suur, pH = 7 is neutraal en pH > 7 is basies. Drinkwater is naby neutraal (ongeveer 6,5–8,5). Meet met universele indikator, pH-papier of 'n pH-meter. Suur mynwater het 'n baie lae pH.\n- **Elektriese geleidingsvermoë:** suiwer (gedistilleerde) water gelei elektrisiteit baie swak. Hoe meer **opgeloste ione**, hoe beter gelei die water. Hoë geleidingsvermoë = baie opgeloste soute (bv. seewater, suur mynwater).\n- **Opgeloste suurstof** (lae vlakke dui op besoedeling), **troebelheid** en **bakterieë** (*E. coli* dui op rioolbesoedeling).\n- **Ione:** silwernitraat gee 'n wit presipitaat met Cl^{−}; bariumchloried gee 'n wit presipitaat met SO_{4}^{2−}.\n\n## Watersuiwering\n\n'n Munisipale suiweringsaanleg suiwer water in stappe:\n\n1. **Siwwing:** groot voorwerpe (takke, plastiek) word uitgesif.\n2. **Koagulasie en flokkulasie:** aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) word bygevoeg sodat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont tot groter vlokke.\n3. **Sedimentasie (besinking):** die vlokke sak na die bodem.\n4. **Filtrasie:** water vloei deur sand- en gruisfilters.\n5. **Disinfeksie (chlorinering):** chloor maak bakterieë en ander mikroörganismes dood.\n\nDie pH word ook aangepas (bv. met kalk). Tuis kan jy water **kook** (minstens 1 minuut) of 'n paar druppels huishoudelike bleikmiddel byvoeg om kieme dood te maak – dit verwyder egter **nie** opgeloste soute of swaar metale nie.\n\n## Waterbewaring\n\n- Herstel lekkende krane en toilette; stort kort in plaas van bad.\n- Vang reënwater in tenks op en hergebruik gryswater in die tuin.\n- Plant inheemse, waterwyse plante en lei water in die koel deel van die dag nat.\n- Boere: drupbesproeiing in plaas van sprinkelbesproeiing.\n- Moenie olie, chemikalieë of medisyne in die drein gooi nie.\n\n> **Onthou!** \"Helder\" beteken nie \"veilig\" nie – bakterieë en opgeloste gifstowwe is onsigbaar.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Chloor verwyder nie vuilheid nie – dit **maak kieme dood**. Vaste deeltjies word deur flokkulasie, sedimentasie en filtrasie verwyder.","en":"## What is the hydrosphere?\n\nThe **hydrosphere** is all the water on, below and above the Earth's surface, in all three states: oceans and seas, rivers, lakes and dams, groundwater (e.g. boreholes), ice (glaciers and polar ice caps), water vapour in the atmosphere and even the water in living organisms.\n\n- About **97.5%** of all water is **salt water**, mostly in the oceans.\n- Only about **2.5%** is **fresh water**, and most of it is frozen as ice or lies deep underground.\n- **Less than 1%** of all the water on Earth is fresh water that we can use easily.\n\n### Why is water so special?\n\n- Water is a **polar** molecule and dissolves many substances. That is why water in nature is **never pure** – it always contains dissolved ions and gases.\n- Water has a high **specific heat capacity**: the oceans warm up and cool down slowly and so regulate the Earth's climate.\n\n## Interaction with other global systems\n\n| System | Interaction with the hydrosphere |\n|---|---|\n| Atmosphere (air) | evaporation and precipitation; O_{2} and CO_{2} dissolve in water; the movement of water and energy drives the weather |\n| Lithosphere (rocks and soil) | water weathers and erodes rocks; it dissolves minerals (ions) from rocks and soil; groundwater is stored in rocks |\n| Biosphere (living things) | plants take up water for photosynthesis and release water vapour (transpiration); water is a habitat; all cells contain water |\n\n## The water cycle\n\nThe **sun's** energy drives the cycle; **gravity** makes rain fall and water run off.\n\n1. **Evaporation:** water from oceans, dams and rivers becomes water vapour.\n2. **Transpiration:** plants release water vapour through their leaves.\n3. **Condensation:** water vapour rises, cools and condenses into droplets that form clouds.\n4. **Precipitation:** water falls as rain, hail or snow.\n5. **Run-off and infiltration:** water flows over the surface to rivers and dams, or seeps into the ground and becomes **groundwater**.\n\n## Water as a resource in South Africa\n\nSouth Africa is a **water-scarce** country – one of the 30 driest countries in the world. Our average rainfall is about 500 mm per year, compared to a world average of about 860 mm. **Agriculture** (irrigation) uses the most water (about 60%). Gauteng gets part of its water via the Lesotho Highlands Water Project and the Vaal River. During load-shedding pumps stop, which leads to water outages.\n\n## Pollution\n\n| Pollutant | Source | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sewage | poorly managed sewage works | bacteria (e.g. *E. coli*, cholera) → disease |\n| Fertiliser (nitrates, phosphates) | farms, sewage | eutrophication |\n| Acid mine drainage | old gold and coal mines | low pH, heavy metals, sulfates |\n| Heavy metals (lead, mercury) | industry | toxic; build up in food chains |\n| Plastic and litter | people | suffocates animals, blocks rivers |\n| Warm water (thermal pollution) | power stations, factories | warm water holds less oxygen |\n\n**Eutrophication:** too many nutrients (nitrates and phosphates) → algae and water plants (e.g. water hyacinth) grow explosively → they block sunlight, and when they die, **bacteria** that break down the dead material use up the **dissolved oxygen** → fish die. Hartbeespoort Dam is a well-known example: waste water from sewage works upstream in Gauteng brings large amounts of phosphates into the dam.\n\n## Ions in water\n\nWater dissolves ions from rocks and soil, e.g. Na^{+}, Ca^{2+}, Mg^{2+}, Cl^{−}, SO_{4}^{2−}, HCO_{3}^{−} and NO_{3}^{−}. Small amounts are harmless; high levels make water unsafe.\n\n- **Hard water** contains many **Ca^{2+} and Mg^{2+} ions**. It does not lather easily with soap and leaves **scale** in kettles and geysers.\n- **Soft water** contains few of these ions.\n\n## Testing water quality\n\n- **pH:** pH < 7 is acidic, pH = 7 is neutral and pH > 7 is basic. Drinking water is close to neutral (about 6.5–8.5). Measure with universal indicator, pH paper or a pH meter. Acid mine drainage has a very low pH.\n- **Electrical conductivity:** pure (distilled) water conducts electricity very poorly. The more **dissolved ions**, the better the water conducts. High conductivity = many dissolved salts (e.g. sea water, acid mine drainage).\n- **Dissolved oxygen** (low levels indicate pollution), **turbidity** and **bacteria** (*E. coli* indicates sewage pollution).\n- **Ions:** silver nitrate gives a white precipitate with Cl^{−}; barium chloride gives a white precipitate with SO_{4}^{2−}.\n\n## Water purification\n\nA municipal purification plant purifies water in steps:\n\n1. **Screening:** large objects (branches, plastic) are sieved out.\n2. **Coagulation and flocculation:** aluminium sulfate (alum) is added so that small suspended particles clump together into larger flocs.\n3. **Sedimentation (settling):** the flocs sink to the bottom.\n4. **Filtration:** water flows through sand and gravel filters.\n5. **Disinfection (chlorination):** chlorine kills bacteria and other micro-organisms.\n\nThe pH is also adjusted (e.g. with lime). At home you can **boil** water (at least 1 minute) or add a few drops of household bleach to kill germs – but this does **not** remove dissolved salts or heavy metals.\n\n## Water conservation\n\n- Fix leaking taps and toilets; take short showers instead of baths.\n- Collect rainwater in tanks and reuse grey water in the garden.\n- Plant indigenous, water-wise plants and water them in the cool part of the day.\n- Farmers: drip irrigation instead of sprinkler irrigation.\n- Do not pour oil, chemicals or medicine down the drain.\n\n> **Remember!** \"Clear\" does not mean \"safe\" – bacteria and dissolved toxins are invisible.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Chlorine does not remove dirt – it **kills germs**. Solid particles are removed by flocculation, sedimentation and filtration."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hidrosfeer","en":"Hydrosphere"},"def":{"af":"Al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak in al drie toestande: oseane, riviere, damme, grondwater, ys, waterdamp en die water in organismes.","en":"All the water on, below and above the Earth's surface in all three states: oceans, rivers, dams, groundwater, ice, water vapour and the water in organisms."}},{"term":{"af":"Waterkringloop","en":"Water cycle"},"def":{"af":"Die deurlopende beweging van water tussen die hidrosfeer, atmosfeer, litosfeer en biosfeer deur verdamping, transpirasie, kondensasie, neerslag, afloop en infiltrasie; aangedryf deur die son se energie.","en":"The continuous movement of water between the hydrosphere, atmosphere, lithosphere and biosphere through evaporation, transpiration, condensation, precipitation, run-off and infiltration; driven by the sun's energy."}},{"term":{"af":"Transpirasie","en":"Transpiration"},"def":{"af":"Die verdamping van water uit die blare van plante na die atmosfeer.","en":"The evaporation of water from the leaves of plants into the atmosphere."}},{"term":{"af":"Grondwater","en":"Groundwater"},"def":{"af":"Water wat in die grond insypel en ondergronds in porieë en krake in rotse gestoor word; dit word deur boorgate onttrek.","en":"Water that seeps into the ground and is stored underground in pores and cracks in rocks; it is extracted through boreholes."}},{"term":{"af":"Eutrofikasie","en":"Eutrophication"},"def":{"af":"Die verryking van water met voedingstowwe (nitrate en fosfate) wat oormatige groei van alge en waterplante veroorsaak; wanneer dit afsterf, gebruik bakterieë die opgeloste suurstof op en visse vrek.","en":"The enrichment of water with nutrients (nitrates and phosphates) that causes excessive growth of algae and water plants; when these die, bacteria use up the dissolved oxygen and fish die."}},{"term":{"af":"Harde water","en":"Hard water"},"def":{"af":"Water met 'n hoë konsentrasie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione; dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat ketelsteen.","en":"Water with a high concentration of Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions; it does not lather easily with soap and leaves scale."}},{"term":{"af":"Suur mynwater","en":"Acid mine drainage"},"def":{"af":"Suur water met 'n lae pH en baie opgeloste swaar metale en sulfate wat uit (ou) myne vloei en riviere besoedel.","en":"Acidic water with a low pH and many dissolved heavy metals and sulfates that flows out of (old) mines and pollutes rivers."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektriese geleidingsvermoë","en":"Electrical conductivity"},"def":{"af":"'n Maatstaf van hoe goed water elektrisiteit gelei; dit neem toe namate die hoeveelheid opgeloste ione toeneem.","en":"A measure of how well water conducts electricity; it increases as the amount of dissolved ions increases."}},{"term":{"af":"pH","en":"pH"},"def":{"af":"'n Skaal (0–14) wat aandui hoe suur of basies 'n oplossing is: onder 7 suur, 7 neutraal, bo 7 basies.","en":"A scale (0–14) that shows how acidic or basic a solution is: below 7 acidic, 7 neutral, above 7 basic."}},{"term":{"af":"Flokkulasie","en":"Flocculation"},"def":{"af":"Die stap in watersuiwering waar 'n chemikalie soos aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) bygevoeg word sodat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont tot vlokke wat kan besink.","en":"The step in water purification where a chemical such as aluminium sulfate (alum) is added so that small suspended particles clump together into flocs that can settle."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die waterkringloop","en":"The water cycle"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf hoe water wat uit Hartbeespoortdam verdamp, weer in die dam kan beland. Noem elke proses in die waterkringloop en die energiebron wat die kringloop dryf.","en":"Describe how water that evaporates from Hartbeespoort Dam can end up in the dam again. Name each process in the water cycle and the energy source that drives the cycle."},"steps":[{"af":"Verdamping: die son se energie verhit die damwater en water op die oppervlak word waterdamp in die atmosfeer. (Plante rondom die dam gee ook waterdamp af deur transpirasie.)","en":"Evaporation: the sun's energy heats the dam water and water at the surface becomes water vapour in the atmosphere. (Plants around the dam also release water vapour through transpiration.)"},{"af":"Kondensasie: die warm, klam lug styg en koel af, en die waterdamp kondenseer tot klein druppeltjies wat wolke vorm.","en":"Condensation: the warm, moist air rises and cools, and the water vapour condenses into tiny droplets that form clouds."},{"af":"Neerslag: die druppels groei, word te swaar en val as reën (of hael) oor die opvanggebied van die dam, bv. in Gauteng.","en":"Precipitation: the droplets grow, become too heavy and fall as rain (or hail) over the dam's catchment area, e.g. in Gauteng."},{"af":"Afloop en infiltrasie: 'n deel van die reënwater vloei oor die oppervlak na strome en die Krokodilrivier, wat in die dam invloei; 'n deel sypel in die grond in en word grondwater.","en":"Run-off and infiltration: part of the rainwater flows over the surface to streams and the Crocodile River, which flows into the dam; part seeps into the ground and becomes groundwater."},{"af":"Die son is die energiebron wat die kringloop dryf; swaartekrag laat die reën val en die water afvloei.","en":"The sun is the energy source that drives the cycle; gravity makes the rain fall and the water run off."}],"answer":{"af":"Verdamping (en transpirasie) → kondensasie → neerslag → afloop (en infiltrasie) terug na die dam; die son dryf die kringloop.","en":"Evaporation (and transpiration) → condensation → precipitation → run-off (and infiltration) back to the dam; the sun drives the cycle."}},{"title":{"af":"Eutrofikasie in Hartbeespoortdam","en":"Eutrophication in Hartbeespoort Dam"},"problem":{"af":"Hartbeespoortdam is dikwels met 'n groen laag alge en waterhiasint bedek, en soms vrek baie visse. Verduidelik stap vir stap hoe besoedeling dit veroorsaak en stel twee maatreëls voor om dit te verminder.","en":"Hartbeespoort Dam is often covered with a green layer of algae and water hyacinth, and sometimes many fish die. Explain step by step how pollution causes this and suggest two measures to reduce it."},"steps":[{"af":"Bron: afvalwater van rioolwerke en kunsmis wat van plase afspoel, bevat baie nitrate en fosfate – voedingstowwe vir plante.","en":"Source: waste water from sewage works and fertiliser washed off farms contain lots of nitrates and phosphates – nutrients for plants."},{"af":"Die oormaat voedingstowwe laat alge en waterplante soos waterhiasint baie vinnig groei. Dit word eutrofikasie genoem.","en":"The excess nutrients make algae and water plants such as water hyacinth grow very fast. This is called eutrophication."},{"af":"Die digte laag blok sonlig, sodat plante onder die oppervlak nie kan fotosintetiseer nie en vrek; later vrek die alge self ook.","en":"The dense layer blocks sunlight, so plants below the surface cannot photosynthesise and die; later the algae themselves die too."},{"af":"Bakterieë breek die dooie plantmateriaal af en gebruik daarvoor die opgeloste suurstof in die water. Die suurstofvlak daal so laag dat visse versmoor en vrek.","en":"Bacteria break down the dead plant material and use the dissolved oxygen in the water to do so. The oxygen level drops so low that fish suffocate and die."},{"af":"Maatreëls: (1) rioolwerke stroomop opgradeer sodat minder fosfate in die riviere beland; (2) kunsmis spaarsamer gebruik en nie naby riviere nie. (Om die waterhiasint uit te haal, help net tydelik – dit behandel die simptoom, nie die oorsaak nie.)","en":"Measures: (1) upgrade sewage works upstream so that fewer phosphates end up in the rivers; (2) use fertiliser sparingly and not close to rivers. (Removing the water hyacinth only helps temporarily – it treats the symptom, not the cause.)"}],"answer":{"af":"Oormaat nitrate en fosfate → eutrofikasie → plante vrek → bakterieë gebruik die suurstof op → visse vrek. Maatreëls: beter rioolsuiwering en minder kunsmisafloop.","en":"Excess nitrates and phosphates → eutrophication → plants die → bacteria use up the oxygen → fish die. Measures: better sewage treatment and less fertiliser run-off."}},{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer watertoetse","en":"Interpret water tests"},"problem":{"af":"Leerders toets drie watermonsters. Monster A (kraanwater): pH 7,4; lae geleidingsvermoë; helder. Monster B (stroompie langs 'n ou goudmyn): pH 3,2; baie hoë geleidingsvermoë; oranjebruin. Monster C (boorgatwater): pH 7,9; hoë geleidingsvermoë; laat ketelsteen in die ketel. (a) Watter monster is waarskynlik deur suur mynwater besoedel? Gee twee redes. (b) Waarom laat monster C ketelsteen? (c) Silwernitraatoplossing word by A gevoeg: 'n wit presipitaat vorm wat nie oplos wanneer verdunde salpetersuur bygevoeg word nie. Wat bewys dit?","en":"Learners test three water samples. Sample A (tap water): pH 7.4; low conductivity; clear. Sample B (stream next to an old gold mine): pH 3.2; very high conductivity; orange-brown. Sample C (borehole water): pH 7.9; high conductivity; leaves scale in the kettle. (a) Which sample is probably polluted by acid mine drainage? Give two reasons. (b) Why does sample C leave scale? (c) Silver nitrate solution is added to A: a white precipitate forms that does not dissolve when dilute nitric acid is added. What does this prove?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Monster B. Rede 1: die pH van 3,2 is baie laag – die water is suur, soos suur mynwater. Rede 2: die baie hoë geleidingsvermoë wys daar is baie opgeloste ione (bv. sulfaat- en metaalione).","en":"(a) Sample B. Reason 1: the pH of 3.2 is very low – the water is acidic, like acid mine drainage. Reason 2: the very high conductivity shows there are many dissolved ions (e.g. sulfate and metal ions)."},{"af":"Die oranjebruin kleur kom van opgeloste ysterverbindings – nog 'n teken van suur mynwater.","en":"The orange-brown colour comes from dissolved iron compounds – another sign of acid mine drainage."},{"af":"(b) Monster C is harde water: dit bevat baie Ca^{2+}- en Mg^{2+}-ione (wat ook die hoë geleidingsvermoë verklaar). Wanneer die water verhit word, slaan kalsium- en magnesiumverbindings as ketelsteen neer.","en":"(b) Sample C is hard water: it contains many Ca^{2+} and Mg^{2+} ions (which also explains the high conductivity). When the water is heated, calcium and magnesium compounds precipitate as scale."},{"af":"(c) 'n Wit presipitaat met silwernitraat wat nie in verdunde salpetersuur oplos nie, is silwerchloried (AgCl). Die kraanwater bevat dus chloriedione (Cl^{−}) – water is nooit suiwer nie.","en":"(c) A white precipitate with silver nitrate that does not dissolve in dilute nitric acid is silver chloride (AgCl). The tap water therefore contains chloride ions (Cl^{−}) – water is never pure."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) B – lae pH en baie hoë geleidingsvermoë (b) harde water met baie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione (c) chloriedione (Cl⁻) is teenwoordig.","en":"(a) B – low pH and very high conductivity (b) hard water with many Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions (c) chloride ions (Cl⁻) are present."}},{"title":{"af":"Watersuiwering","en":"Water purification"},"problem":{"af":"Rou water uit 'n rivier word by 'n munisipale aanleg gesuiwer. (a) Rangskik die stappe filtrasie, chlorinering, siwwing, sedimentasie en flokkulasie in die regte volgorde en gee die doel van elk. (b) Tydens 'n wateronderbreking het 'n gesin net onbehandelde rivierwater. Hoe kan hulle dit veiliger maak om te drink, en wat sal hul metode nie verwyder nie?","en":"Raw river water is purified at a municipal plant. (a) Arrange the steps filtration, chlorination, screening, sedimentation and flocculation in the correct order and give the purpose of each. (b) During a water outage a family only has untreated river water. How can they make it safer to drink, and what will their method not remove?"},"steps":[{"af":"1. Siwwing: groot voorwerpe soos takke, blare en plastiek word met skerms uitgesif.","en":"1. Screening: large objects such as branches, leaves and plastic are sieved out with screens."},{"af":"2. Flokkulasie (en koagulasie): aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) word bygevoeg; klein swewende deeltjies klont saam tot groter vlokke. 3. Sedimentasie: die swaar vlokke sak in groot tenks na die bodem.","en":"2. Flocculation (and coagulation): aluminium sulfate (alum) is added; small suspended particles clump together into larger flocs. 3. Sedimentation: the heavy flocs sink to the bottom in large tanks."},{"af":"4. Filtrasie: die water vloei deur lae sand en gruis wat die oorblywende fyn deeltjies vasvang.","en":"4. Filtration: the water flows through layers of sand and gravel that trap the remaining fine particles."},{"af":"5. Chlorinering: chloor word laaste bygevoeg om bakterieë en ander mikroörganismes dood te maak; 'n bietjie bly in die water sodat dit in die pype veilig bly.","en":"5. Chlorination: chlorine is added last to kill bacteria and other micro-organisms; a little stays in the water so that it remains safe in the pipes."},{"af":"(b) Kook die water (minstens 1 minuut) of voeg 'n paar druppels huishoudelike bleikmiddel by om kieme dood te maak. Dit verwyder nie opgeloste soute, swaar metale of ander chemikalieë nie.","en":"(b) Boil the water (at least 1 minute) or add a few drops of household bleach to kill germs. This does not remove dissolved salts, heavy metals or other chemicals."}],"answer":{"af":"Siwwing → flokkulasie → sedimentasie → filtrasie → chlorinering; kook of bleikmiddel maak kieme dood, maar verwyder nie opgeloste stowwe nie.","en":"Screening → flocculation → sedimentation → filtration → chlorination; boiling or bleach kills germs but does not remove dissolved substances."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter beskrywing pas die beste by die hidrosfeer?","en":"Which description best fits the hydrosphere?"},"options":[{"af":"Net die water in die oseane en seë","en":"Only the water in the oceans and seas"},{"af":"Die laag gasse wat die aarde omring","en":"The layer of gases that surrounds the Earth"},{"af":"Net die varswater in riviere, mere en damme","en":"Only the fresh water in rivers, lakes and dams"},{"af":"Al die water op, onder en bo die aarde se oppervlak – vloeibaar, ys en waterdamp","en":"All the water on, below and above the Earth's surface – liquid, ice and water vapour"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die hidrosfeer sluit ALLE water in: oseane, varswater, grondwater, ys, waterdamp en water in organismes. Die laag gasse is die atmosfeer.","en":"The hydrosphere includes ALL water: oceans, fresh water, groundwater, ice, water vapour and water in organisms. The layer of gases is the atmosphere."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die proses waardeur plante waterdamp deur hul blare aan die atmosfeer afgee, word ___ genoem.","en":"The process by which plants release water vapour through their leaves into the atmosphere is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["transpirasie","transpiration"],"en":["transpiration","transpirasie"]},"explain":{"af":"Transpirasie is die verdamping van water uit plante se blare. Dit verbind die biosfeer met die atmosfeer.","en":"Transpiration is the evaporation of water from plants' leaves. It links the biosphere to the atmosphere."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fotosintese","kondensasie","infiltrasie"],"en":["photosynthesis","condensation","infiltration"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke proses in die waterkringloop by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each process in the water cycle to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Verdamping","en":"Evaporation"},"r":{"af":"Vloeibare water word waterdamp deur die son se energie.","en":"Liquid water becomes water vapour due to the sun's energy."}},{"l":{"af":"Kondensasie","en":"Condensation"},"r":{"af":"Waterdamp koel af en vorm druppeltjies in wolke.","en":"Water vapour cools and forms droplets in clouds."}},{"l":{"af":"Neerslag","en":"Precipitation"},"r":{"af":"Water val as reën, hael of sneeu.","en":"Water falls as rain, hail or snow."}},{"l":{"af":"Infiltrasie","en":"Infiltration"},"r":{"af":"Water sypel in die grond in en word grondwater.","en":"Water seeps into the ground and becomes groundwater."}}],"explain":{"af":"Verdamping: vloeistof → gas; kondensasie: gas → vloeistof (wolke); neerslag: water val uit wolke; infiltrasie: water sypel in die grond in.","en":"Evaporation: liquid → gas; condensation: gas → liquid (clouds); precipitation: water falls from clouds; infiltration: water seeps into the ground."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suiwer (gedistilleerde) water is 'n goeie geleier van elektrisiteit.","en":"Pure (distilled) water is a good conductor of electricity."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gedistilleerde water bevat byna geen ione nie en gelei baie swak. Kraan-, rivier- en seewater gelei omdat daar opgeloste ione in is.","en":"False. Distilled water contains almost no ions and conducts very poorly. Tap, river and sea water conduct because they contain dissolved ions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Reënwater los minerale uit rotse op en dra die ione na 'n rivier. Dit is 'n voorbeeld van wisselwerking tussen die hidrosfeer en die …","en":"Rainwater dissolves minerals from rocks and carries the ions to a river. This is an example of interaction between the hydrosphere and the …"},"options":[{"af":"atmosfeer","en":"atmosphere"},{"af":"litosfeer","en":"lithosphere"},{"af":"biosfeer","en":"biosphere"},{"af":"magnetosfeer","en":"magnetosphere"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Rotse en grond vorm die litosfeer. Water verweer rotse en los minerale (ione) daaruit op – daarom bevat natuurlike water altyd ione.","en":"Rocks and soil make up the lithosphere. Water weathers rocks and dissolves minerals (ions) from them – that is why natural water always contains ions."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Harde water bevat 'n hoë konsentrasie magnesiumione en ___-ione.","en":"Hard water contains a high concentration of magnesium ions and ___ ions."},"answers":{"af":["kalsium","Ca²⁺","Ca2+","Ca","kalsiumione","calcium"],"en":["calcium","Ca²⁺","Ca2+","Ca","calcium ions","kalsium"]},"explain":{"af":"Harde water bevat baie Ca²⁺- en Mg²⁺-ione. Dit vorm moeilik skuim met seep en laat ketelsteen in ketels.","en":"Hard water contains many Ca²⁺ and Mg²⁺ ions. It does not lather easily with soap and leaves scale in kettles."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["natrium","kalium","chloried"],"en":["sodium","potassium","chloride"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die doel daarvan om aluminiumsulfaat (aluin) by 'n watersuiweringsaanleg by te voeg?","en":"What is the purpose of adding aluminium sulfate (alum) at a water purification plant?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit maak bakterieë dood.","en":"It kills bacteria."},{"af":"Dit verwyder opgeloste soute soos NaCl.","en":"It removes dissolved salts such as NaCl."},{"af":"Dit laat klein swewende deeltjies saamklont sodat hulle kan besink.","en":"It makes small suspended particles clump together so that they can settle."},{"af":"Dit maak die water sag deur Ca²⁺-ione te verwyder.","en":"It softens the water by removing Ca²⁺ ions."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Aluin veroorsaak flokkulasie: klein deeltjies klont saam tot vlokke wat in die sedimentasietenks besink. Bakterieë word deur chloor doodgemaak, nie deur aluin nie.","en":"Alum causes flocculation: small particles clump together into flocs that settle in the sedimentation tanks. Bacteria are killed by chlorine, not by alum."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Water wat helder lyk, is altyd veilig om te drink.","en":"Water that looks clear is always safe to drink."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Bakterieë (bv. E. coli), virusse en opgeloste gifstowwe soos swaar metale is onsigbaar. Helder water kan steeds besoedel wees.","en":"False. Bacteria (e.g. E. coli), viruses and dissolved toxins such as heavy metals are invisible. Clear water can still be polluted."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter volgorde word rou water in 'n munisipale aanleg gesuiwer?","en":"In which order is raw water purified at a municipal plant?"},"options":[{"af":"siwwing → flokkulasie → sedimentasie → filtrasie → chlorinering","en":"screening → flocculation → sedimentation → filtration → chlorination"},{"af":"chlorinering → siwwing → filtrasie → flokkulasie → sedimentasie","en":"chlorination → screening → filtration → flocculation → sedimentation"},{"af":"siwwing → filtrasie → flokkulasie → chlorinering → sedimentasie","en":"screening → filtration → flocculation → chlorination → sedimentation"},{"af":"siwwing → sedimentasie → flokkulasie → filtrasie → chlorinering","en":"screening → sedimentation → flocculation → filtration → chlorination"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Eers word groot voorwerpe uitgesif, dan laat aluin deeltjies saamklont (flokkulasie) sodat hulle kan besink (sedimentasie). Filtrasie vang die fyn deeltjies vas, en chloor word laaste bygevoeg om kieme dood te maak. Flokkulasie moet vóór sedimentasie kom.","en":"First large objects are screened out, then alum makes particles clump together (flocculation) so that they can settle (sedimentation). Filtration traps the fine particles, and chlorine is added last to kill germs. Flocculation must come before sedimentation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Watermonster uit 'n stroom by 'n ou myn het 'n pH van 3,5. Die water is ___ (suur, neutraal of basies).","en":"A water sample from a stream near an old mine has a pH of 3.5. The water is ___ (acidic, neutral or basic)."},"answers":{"af":["suur","acidic","suur water"],"en":["acidic","suur","acid"]},"explain":{"af":"pH < 7 is suur. 'n pH van 3,5 is baie suur – tipies van suur mynwater.","en":"pH < 7 is acidic. A pH of 3.5 is very acidic – typical of acid mine drainage."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["basies","neutraal","alkalies"],"en":["basic","neutral","alkaline"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Stort gebruik 10 L water per minuut. Elkeen in 'n gesin van 4 verkort sy daaglikse stort van 10 minute na 4 minute. Hoeveel water spaar die gesin per dag? ___ L","en":"A shower uses 10 L of water per minute. Each person in a family of 4 shortens their daily shower from 10 minutes to 4 minutes. How much water does the family save per day? ___ L"},"answers":{"af":["240","240 L","240 ℓ","240 liter","240 dm³","240 dm3"],"en":["240","240 L","240 ℓ","240 litres","240 liters","240 dm³","240 dm3"]},"explain":{"af":"Elke persoon spaar 10 − 4 = 6 minute × 10 L per minuut = 60 L. Vir 4 mense: 4 × 60 = 240 L per dag (meer as 87 000 L per jaar!).","en":"Each person saves 10 − 4 = 6 minutes × 10 L per minute = 60 L. For 4 people: 4 × 60 = 240 L per day (more than 87 000 L per year!)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["60","160","400"],"en":["60","160","400"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Leerders toets vier watermonsters. Watter monster kom waarskynlik uit 'n stroom wat deur suur mynwater besoedel is?","en":"Learners test four water samples. Which sample most likely comes from a stream polluted by acid mine drainage?"},"options":[{"af":"Monster P: pH 7,2; lae geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample P: pH 7.2; low conductivity"},{"af":"Monster Q: pH 3,1; baie hoë geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample Q: pH 3.1; very high conductivity"},{"af":"Monster R: pH 8,9; matige geleidingsvermoë","en":"Sample R: pH 8.9; moderate conductivity"},{"af":"Monster S: pH 7,0; byna geen geleidingsvermoë nie","en":"Sample S: pH 7.0; almost no conductivity"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Suur mynwater is suur (lae pH) en bevat baie opgeloste ione (sulfate en metaalione), dus het dit 'n hoë geleidingsvermoë. S lyk soos gedistilleerde water; R is basies.","en":"Acid mine drainage is acidic (low pH) and contains many dissolved ions (sulfates and metal ions), so it has a high conductivity. S looks like distilled water; R is basic."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Na 'n algeblom in Hartbeespoortdam vrek baie visse. Wat is die hoofrede?","en":"After an algal bloom in Hartbeespoort Dam many fish die. What is the main reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kunsmis in die water is direk giftig vir die visse.","en":"The fertiliser in the water is directly poisonous to the fish."},{"af":"Die alge gebruik al die koolstofdioksied in die water op.","en":"The algae use up all the carbon dioxide in the water."},{"af":"Die alge maak die water te koud omdat hulle die son blok.","en":"The algae make the water too cold because they block the sun."},{"af":"Bakterieë wat die dooie alge en plante afbreek, gebruik die opgeloste suurstof op.","en":"Bacteria that break down the dead algae and plants use up the dissolved oxygen."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By eutrofikasie vrek die alge en plante later. Bakterieë breek die dooie materiaal af en gebruik daarvoor die opgeloste suurstof, sodat die visse versmoor.","en":"In eutrophication the algae and plants die later. Bacteria break down the dead material and use up the dissolved oxygen to do so, so the fish suffocate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die munisipaliteit wil die eutrofikasie in Hartbeespoortdam op die lang termyn verminder. Watter maatreël sal die doeltreffendste wees?","en":"The municipality wants to reduce the eutrophication in Hartbeespoort Dam in the long term. Which measure will be the most effective?"},"options":[{"af":"Gooi meer chloor in die dam om die alge dood te maak.","en":"Add more chlorine to the dam to kill the algae."},{"af":"Haal die waterhiasint een keer per jaar uit.","en":"Remove the water hyacinth once a year."},{"af":"Gradeer rioolwerke stroomop op en beperk kunsmisafloop sodat minder fosfate en nitrate die dam bereik.","en":"Upgrade sewage works upstream and limit fertiliser run-off so that fewer phosphates and nitrates reach the dam."},{"af":"Bou nog 'n dam stroomaf om die water op te vang.","en":"Build another dam downstream to catch the water."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die oorsaak is te veel voedingstowwe (fosfate en nitrate). Net om die bron aan te pak, los die probleem op die lang termyn op. Chloor sou alle waterlewe skade aandoen, die hiasint uithaal behandel net die simptoom, en 'n dam stroomaf help nie die dam stroomop nie.","en":"The cause is too many nutrients (phosphates and nitrates). Only tackling the source solves the problem in the long term. Chlorine would harm all aquatic life, removing the hyacinth only treats the symptom, and a dam downstream does not help the dam upstream."}}]}]}]},"toerisme":{"id":"toerisme","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Toerisme","en":"Tourism"},"short":{"af":"Toer","en":"Tour"},"icon":"🧳","color":"#0891b2","intro":{"af":"Toerisme in Graad 10 leer jou hoe die toerismebedryf werk: die sektore (vervoer, akkommodasie, kos en drank, aantreklikhede), kaartwerk, tydsones en reisplanne, binnelandse en internasionale toerisme, betaalmetodes en buitelandse valuta, toeriste-aantreklikhede en parke, volhoubare toerisme, bemarking, kultuur- en erfenistoerisme, en kommunikasie en kliëntediens. Die Novembereksamen is een vraestel van 200 punte in 3 uur oor die hele jaar se werk.","en":"Tourism in Grade 10 teaches you how the tourism industry works: the sectors (transport, accommodation, food and beverage, attractions), map work, time zones and itineraries, domestic and international tourism, payment methods and foreign exchange, tourist attractions and parks, sustainable tourism, marketing, culture and heritage tourism, and communication and customer care. The November exam is one paper of 200 marks in 3 hours on the whole year's work."},"examTips":[{"af":"Valuta: kies die regte koers – die bankverkoopkoers as 'n toeris buitelandse valuta koop (rand → buitelands), die bankkoopkoers as hy dit terugverkoop (buitelands → rand). Wys elke stap en rond eers aan die einde af.","en":"Foreign exchange: choose the right rate – the bank selling rate when a tourist buys foreign currency (rand → foreign), the bank buying rate when they sell it back (foreign → rand). Show every step and round only at the end."},{"af":"Tydsones: tel ure by vir plekke oos van Greenwich en trek af vir plekke wes daarvan, en onthou dat Suid-Afrika GMT+2 is.","en":"Time zones: add hours for places east of Greenwich and subtract for places west of it, and remember that South Africa is GMT+2."},{"af":"Kaartwerk: ken die nege provinsies, hul hoofstede, die groot lughawens en die Wêrelderfenisterreine, en oefen om afstandstabelle en reisplanne te lees.","en":"Map work: know the nine provinces, their capitals, the major airports and the World Heritage Sites, and practise reading distance tables and itineraries."},{"af":"Leer die terme presies (bv. toeris, dagbesoeker, eko-toerisme, verantwoordelike toerisme, sterregradering) – Afdeling A beloon presiese terme.","en":"Learn the terms exactly (e.g. tourist, same-day visitor, ecotourism, responsible tourism, star grading) – Section A rewards exact terms."},{"af":"By scenariovrae: verwys na die toeris of besigheid in die scenario en gee praktiese, realistiese voorstelle – een punt per geldige idee.","en":"In scenario questions: refer to the tourist or business in the scenario and give practical, realistic suggestions – one mark per valid idea."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Departement van Basiese Onderwys (DBE)","en":"Department of Basic Education (DBE)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za","note":{"af":"CAPS-dokument vir Toerisme, eksamenriglyne en vorige NSS-vraestelle met memorandums – goed om die vraagstyl te leer ken.","en":"CAPS document for Tourism, exam guidelines and past NSC papers with memos – good for learning the question style."}},{"title":{"af":"Thutong-onderwysportaal","en":"Thutong Education Portal"},"url":"https://www.thutong.doe.gov.za","note":{"af":"Die DBE se gratis onderwysportaal met leer- en hersieningsmateriaal per vak en graad.","en":"The DBE's free education portal with learning and revision material by subject and grade."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Toerisme-eksamen Graad 10\n\n**Een vraestel, 200 punte, 3 uur** volgens die CAPS/DBE-patroon (*skatting – bevestig met Hoërskool Brits se 2026-afbakening*; sommige skole gebruik 'n vraestel van 150 punte). Die vraestel dek **die hele jaar** en het vyf afdelings. Die PAT tel apart.\n\n| Afdeling | Inhoud | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Kort vrae oor alle onderwerpe: meervoudige keuse, terme, kolom-pas | 40 |\n| B | Kaartwerk en toerbeplanning; buitelandse valuta | 30 |\n| C | Toeriste-aantreklikhede; kultuur- en erfenistoerisme; bemarking | 50 |\n| D | Toerismesektore; volhoubare en verantwoordelike toerisme | 50 |\n| E | Binnelandse, streeks- en internasionale toerisme; kommunikasie en kliëntediens | 30 |\n\n### Wat om te verwag\n\n- **Bronne:** kaarte, afstandstabelle, valutatabelle, advertensies, foto's en scenario's.\n- **Berekeninge:** valuta-omskakeling, tydverskille en afstande.\n- **Hoër-orde vrae:** evalueer, stel voor, regverdig – gee 'n rede by elke punt.\n\n### Wenke\n\n1. Begin met Afdeling A – vinnige punte.\n2. 200 punte in 180 minute is minder as 'n minuut per punt: werk vinnig en hou tyd oor vir die berekeninge.\n3. Bring 'n sakrekenaar as jou skool dit toelaat.","en":"## Tourism exam Grade 10\n\n**One paper, 200 marks, 3 hours** following the CAPS/DBE pattern (*estimate – confirm with Hoërskool Brits's 2026 scope*; some schools use a 150-mark paper). The paper covers **the whole year** and has five sections. The PAT counts separately.\n\n| Section | Content | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Short questions on all topics: multiple choice, terms, matching columns | 40 |\n| B | Map work and tour planning; foreign exchange | 30 |\n| C | Tourist attractions; culture and heritage tourism; marketing | 50 |\n| D | Tourism sectors; sustainable and responsible tourism | 50 |\n| E | Domestic, regional and international tourism; communication and customer care | 30 |\n\n### What to expect\n\n- **Sources:** maps, distance tables, exchange-rate tables, adverts, photos and scenarios.\n- **Calculations:** currency conversion, time differences and distances.\n- **Higher-order questions:** evaluate, suggest, justify – give a reason for every point.\n\n### Tips\n\n1. Start with Section A – quick marks.\n2. 200 marks in 180 minutes is less than a minute per mark: work quickly and keep time for the calculations.\n3. Bring a calculator if your school allows it."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Toerismesektore","en":"Tourism sectors"},"topics":[{"id":"toer10-t1-inleiding-toeriste","title":{"af":"Inleiding tot toerisme en tipes toeriste","en":"Introduction to tourism and types of tourists"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal toerisme en sy kernbegrippe kan definieer, toeriste in 'n scenario kan klassifiseer, 'n toeristeprofiel kan opstel en verduidelik hoe die toerismesektore van mekaar afhang.","en":"You will be able to define tourism and its key concepts, classify tourists in a scenario, compile a tourist profile and explain how the tourism sectors depend on each other."},"summary":{"af":"## Die eksamenvraestel\n\nDie Graad 10-Novembervraestel tel **200 punte** en duur **3 uur**. Die eksamen tel 50% van jou jaarpunt; die PAT (praktiese assesseringstaak) en die SGA (skoolgebaseerde assessering) tel elk 25%.\n\n| Afdeling | Onderwerpe | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Kort vrae oor alle onderwerpe | 40 |\n| B | Kaartwerk en toerbeplanning; buitelandse valuta | 30 |\n| C | Toeriste-aantreklikhede; kultuur- en erfenistoerisme; bemarking | 50 |\n| D | Toerismesektore; volhoubare en verantwoordelike toerisme | 50 |\n| E | Binnelandse, streeks- en internasionale toerisme; kommunikasie en kliëntediens | 30 |\n\nHierdie onderwerp val in **Afdeling D** (en kort vrae in Afdeling A).\n\n## Wat is toerisme?\n\nDie **UNWTO** (Wêreldtoerismeorganisasie van die Verenigde Nasies) definieer toerisme as *die aktiwiteite van persone wat reis na en bly op plekke buite hul gewone omgewing, vir nie langer nie as een agtereenvolgende jaar, vir ontspanning, sake en ander doeleindes.*\n\nOnthou die drie sleutels: **buite jou gewone omgewing**, **minder as een jaar aaneen** en **enige doel**.\n\n- **Reisiger:** enigiemand wat tussen plekke beweeg, vir enige rede en enige tydsduur.\n- **Toeris:** 'n besoeker wat **ten minste een nag** op die bestemming oorbly.\n- **Dagbesoeker (ekskursionis):** 'n besoeker wat nie oornag nie en dieselfde dag huis toe gaan.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n Gesin uit Pretoria wat vir die dag Hartbeespoortdam toe ry en saans tuis slaap, is **dagbesoekers**, nie toeriste nie. 'n Myner wat elke dag van Brits af werk toe ry, is 'n **reisiger**, maar glad nie 'n besoeker nie – dit is sy gewone omgewing.\n\n## Vorme van toerisme\n\n| Vorm | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Binnelandse toerisme | Inwoners reis binne hul eie land | 'n Gesin uit Brits hou vakansie in Margate |\n| Streekstoerisme | Reis binne die streek (SAOG/Afrika) | Suid-Afrikaners besoek die Okavango-delta in Botswana |\n| Internasionale toerisme | Reis oor landsgrense, veral van en na lande buite die streek | 'n Duitse paartjie besoek Kaapstad |\n| Inkomende toerisme | Nie-inwoners reis 'n land **in** | Chinese toeriste besoek die Krugerwildtuin |\n| Uitgaande toerisme | Inwoners reis hul land **uit** | 'n Rugbyondersteuner uit Pretoria vlieg na Nieu-Seeland |\n\nEen reis kan twee etikette kry: 'n gesin uit Botswana wat in Pretoria inkopies doen en oorslaap, is vir Suid-Afrika **inkomende streekstoerisme**.\n\n## Redes vir reis\n\nOntspanning of vakansie, sake, besoek aan vriende en familie, gesondheid of mediese behandeling, godsdiens, sport, opvoeding en inkopies.\n\n## Tipes toeriste\n\n| Tipe toeris | Wat hy of sy soek | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| VFR (besoek aan vriende en familie) | Kuier by mense en bly dikwels by hulle | Ouma uit Kimberley kuier met Kersfees in Brits |\n| Ontspanning | Rus en plesier | Strandvakansie in Ballito |\n| Avontuur | Opwinding en fisiese uitdaging | Bungee-sprong by die Bloukransbrug |\n| Sake (MICE) | Werk: vergaderings, aansporings, konferensies, uitstallings | Konferensie in Sandton |\n| Inkopies | Om te koop | Inwoners van Botswana doen inkopies in Pretoria |\n| Gesondheid/medies | Mediese behandeling of spa | 'n Operasie by 'n privaat hospitaal |\n| Eko | Natuur en bewaring, met min impak | Voetslaan in die Magaliesberg |\n| Kultuur | Kultuur, geskiedenis en erfenis | Besoek aan die Lesedi-kultuurdorp |\n| Godsdiens | Geloofsbyeenkomste en pelgrimstogte | Die ZCC-Paasbyeenkoms by Moria |\n| Sport en ontspanning | Neem deel aan of kyk na sport | Hardloop die Comrades-maraton |\n| Opvoedkundig | Leer en studeer | Skooluitstappie na die Wieg van die Mensdom |\n| Spesiale belangstelling (SIT) | 'n Spesifieke stokperdjie | Voëlkykers; sterrekykers in Sutherland |\n| Aansporing | Reis as beloning van die werkgewer | Topverkopers kry 'n reis na Mauritius |\n| Rugsakreisiger/jeug | Goedkoop, avontuurlik en sosiaal | Slaap in slaapsale en reis met 'n klein begroting |\n| Tussenjaar (gap year) | 'n Jaar af tussen skool en studie of werk | Werk en reis 'n jaar lank na matriek |\n\n**MICE** = *Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions* (vergaderings, aansporings, konferensies, uitstallings).\n\n## Behoeftes, voorkeure en verwagtinge\n\n- **Behoeftes:** wat 'n toeris *moet* hê: veiligheid, verblyf, kos, vervoer en inligting.\n- **Voorkeure:** wat hy *verkies*, bv. 'n luukse lodge eerder as 'n kampeerterrein.\n- **Verwagtinge:** wat hy vir sy geld *verwag*: skoon kamers, vriendelike diens, waarde vir geld.\n\n## Toeristeprofiel\n\n'n **Toeristeprofiel** beskryf 'n toeris sodat 'n onderneming die regte produk kan aanbied: **ouderdom, herkoms, begroting, belangstellings, reisstyl** (alleen of in 'n groep, onafhanklik of met 'n pakket), **keuse van akkommodasie en vervoer** en **tipe toeris**.\n\n## Die toerismesektore hang van mekaar af\n\nDie vyf sektore is **akkommodasie, vervoer, kos en drank, aantreklikhede** en **reisorganiseerders** (toeroperateurs en reisagente). Hulle is **interafhanklik**: 'n toeris het hulle almal nodig, en as een sektor faal, ly die ander ook. As vlugte na Kaapstad gekanselleer word, staan hotelkamers leeg, verloor restaurante kliënte en kry aantreklikhede minder besoekers.\n\n> **Wenk:** Gee by 'verduidelik'-vrae altyd 'n **kettingvoorbeeld**: sektor A → sektor B → gevolg vir die toeris.","en":"## The exam paper\n\nThe Grade 10 November paper is worth **200 marks** and lasts **3 hours**. The exam counts 50% of your year mark; the PAT (practical assessment task) and the SBA (school-based assessment) count 25% each.\n\n| Section | Topics | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Short questions on all topics | 40 |\n| B | Map work and tour planning; foreign exchange | 30 |\n| C | Tourism attractions; culture and heritage tourism; marketing | 50 |\n| D | Tourism sectors; sustainable and responsible tourism | 50 |\n| E | Domestic, regional and international tourism; communication and customer care | 30 |\n\nThis topic falls in **Section D** (plus short questions in Section A).\n\n## What is tourism?\n\nThe **UNWTO** (United Nations World Tourism Organization) defines tourism as *the activities of persons travelling to and staying in places outside their usual environment for not more than one consecutive year for leisure, business and other purposes.*\n\nRemember the three keys: **outside your usual environment**, **less than one consecutive year** and **any purpose**.\n\n- **Traveller:** anyone who moves between places, for any reason and for any length of time.\n- **Tourist:** a visitor who stays **at least one night** at the destination.\n- **Same-day visitor (excursionist):** a visitor who does not stay overnight and goes home the same day.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A family from Pretoria who drive to Hartbeespoort Dam for the day and sleep at home that night are **same-day visitors**, not tourists. A miner who drives from Brits to work every day is a **traveller**, but not a visitor at all – that is his usual environment.\n\n## Forms of tourism\n\n| Form | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Domestic tourism | Residents travel within their own country | A family from Brits holidays in Margate |\n| Regional tourism | Travel within the region (SADC/Africa) | South Africans visit the Okavango Delta in Botswana |\n| International tourism | Travel across borders, especially to and from countries outside the region | A German couple visits Cape Town |\n| Inbound tourism | Non-residents travel **into** a country | Chinese tourists visit the Kruger National Park |\n| Outbound tourism | Residents travel **out of** their country | A rugby supporter from Pretoria flies to New Zealand |\n\nOne trip can get two labels: a family from Botswana who shop in Pretoria and stay overnight are **inbound regional tourism** for South Africa.\n\n## Reasons for travel\n\nLeisure or holiday, business, visiting friends and relatives, health or medical treatment, religion, sport, education and shopping.\n\n## Types of tourists\n\n| Type of tourist | What he or she wants | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| VFR (visiting friends and relatives) | Visit people and often stay with them | Grandma from Kimberley visits Brits for Christmas |\n| Leisure | Rest and pleasure | Beach holiday in Ballito |\n| Adventure | Excitement and physical challenge | Bungee jump at the Bloukrans Bridge |\n| Business (MICE) | Work: meetings, incentives, conferences, exhibitions | Conference in Sandton |\n| Shopping | To buy | Residents of Botswana shop in Pretoria |\n| Health/medical | Medical treatment or a spa | An operation at a private hospital |\n| Eco | Nature and conservation, with little impact | Hiking in the Magaliesberg |\n| Cultural | Culture, history and heritage | Visit to Lesedi Cultural Village |\n| Religious | Faith gatherings and pilgrimages | The ZCC Easter gathering at Moria |\n| Sport and recreation | Take part in or watch sport | Run the Comrades Marathon |\n| Educational | Learn and study | School tour to the Cradle of Humankind |\n| Special interest (SIT) | A specific hobby | Birdwatchers; stargazers in Sutherland |\n| Incentive | Travel as a reward from the employer | Top salespeople get a trip to Mauritius |\n| Backpacker/youth | Cheap, adventurous and social | Sleep in dormitories and travel on a small budget |\n| Gap year | A year off between school and study or work | Work and travel for a year after matric |\n\n**MICE** = Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions.\n\n## Needs, preferences and expectations\n\n- **Needs:** what a tourist *must* have: safety, accommodation, food, transport and information.\n- **Preferences:** what he *prefers*, e.g. a luxury lodge rather than a campsite.\n- **Expectations:** what he *expects* for his money: clean rooms, friendly service, value for money.\n\n## Tourist profile\n\nA **tourist profile** describes a tourist so that a business can offer the right product: **age, origin, budget, interests, travel style** (alone or in a group, independent or on a package), **choice of accommodation and transport** and **type of tourist**.\n\n## The tourism sectors depend on each other\n\nThe five sectors are **accommodation, transport, food and beverage, attractions** and **travel organisers** (tour operators and travel agents). They are **interdependent**: a tourist needs all of them, and if one sector fails, the others suffer too. If flights to Cape Town are cancelled, hotel rooms stand empty, restaurants lose customers and attractions get fewer visitors.\n\n> **Tip:** In 'explain' questions always give a **chain example**: sector A → sector B → result for the tourist."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Toerisme","en":"Tourism"},"def":{"af":"Die aktiwiteite van persone wat reis na en bly op plekke buite hul gewone omgewing vir nie langer nie as een agtereenvolgende jaar, vir ontspanning, sake en ander doeleindes (UNWTO).","en":"The activities of persons travelling to and staying in places outside their usual environment for not more than one consecutive year for leisure, business and other purposes (UNWTO)."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeris","en":"Tourist"},"def":{"af":"'n Besoeker wat ten minste een nag op die bestemming oorbly.","en":"A visitor who stays at least one night at the destination."}},{"term":{"af":"Dagbesoeker (ekskursionis)","en":"Same-day visitor (excursionist)"},"def":{"af":"'n Besoeker wat nie oornag nie en dieselfde dag terugkeer huis toe.","en":"A visitor who does not stay overnight and returns home on the same day."}},{"term":{"af":"Reisiger","en":"Traveller"},"def":{"af":"Enigiemand wat tussen twee of meer plekke beweeg, vir enige rede en enige tydsduur.","en":"Anyone who moves between two or more places, for any reason and any length of time."}},{"term":{"af":"Inkomende toerisme","en":"Inbound tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme waar nie-inwoners 'n land binnekom om dit te besoek, bv. Duitse toeriste in Suid-Afrika.","en":"Tourism where non-residents enter a country to visit it, e.g. German tourists in South Africa."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitgaande toerisme","en":"Outbound tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme waar inwoners van 'n land na 'n ander land reis, bv. Suid-Afrikaners wat na Thailand vlieg.","en":"Tourism where residents of a country travel to another country, e.g. South Africans flying to Thailand."}},{"term":{"af":"Binnelandse toerisme","en":"Domestic tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme waar inwoners binne hul eie land reis, bv. 'n gesin uit Brits wat in Kaapstad vakansie hou.","en":"Tourism where residents travel within their own country, e.g. a family from Brits holidaying in Cape Town."}},{"term":{"af":"MICE","en":"MICE"},"def":{"af":"Sake-toerisme vir vergaderings, aansporings, konferensies en uitstallings (Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions).","en":"Business tourism for Meetings, Incentives, Conferences and Exhibitions."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeristeprofiel","en":"Tourist profile"},"def":{"af":"'n Beskrywing van 'n toeris se ouderdom, herkoms, begroting, belangstellings, reisstyl en keuse van akkommodasie en vervoer.","en":"A description of a tourist's age, origin, budget, interests, travel style and choice of accommodation and transport."}},{"term":{"af":"Interafhanklikheid","en":"Interdependence"},"def":{"af":"Die toerismesektore het mekaar nodig: as een sektor swak presteer of faal, word die ander sektore en die toeris se ervaring ook geraak.","en":"The tourism sectors need each other: if one sector performs badly or fails, the other sectors and the tourist's experience are affected too."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer die toeriste in 'n bron","en":"Classify the tourists in a source"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron: *Klaus (58) en Anna (55) van München in Duitsland land by O.R. Tambo-lughawe. Hulle ry na 'n lodge in die Pilanesbergwildtuin, bly vier nagte en gaan elke oggend op 'n wildrit.*\n\n(a) Is hulle toeriste of dagbesoekers? (b) Is dit inkomende of uitgaande toerisme vir Suid-Afrika? (c) Is dit binnelandse, streeks- of internasionale toerisme? (d) Watter tipe toeriste is hulle? Gee 'n rede vir elke antwoord.","en":"Read the source: *Klaus (58) and Anna (55) from Munich in Germany land at O.R. Tambo Airport. They drive to a lodge in the Pilanesberg Game Reserve, stay four nights and go on a game drive every morning.*\n\n(a) Are they tourists or same-day visitors? (b) Is this inbound or outbound tourism for South Africa? (c) Is it domestic, regional or international tourism? (d) What type of tourists are they? Give a reason for each answer."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Hulle bly vier nagte oor, dus is hulle **toeriste** (minstens een nag).","en":"(a) They stay four nights, so they are **tourists** (at least one night)."},{"af":"(b) Hulle is nie inwoners van Suid-Afrika nie en reis die land in, dus **inkomende** toerisme.","en":"(b) They are not residents of South Africa and travel into the country, so **inbound** tourism."},{"af":"(c) Hulle kom van Duitsland, buite die streek (Afrika/SAOG), dus **internasionale** toerisme.","en":"(c) They come from Germany, outside the region (Africa/SADC), so **international** tourism."},{"af":"(d) Wildritte in 'n wildtuin om die natuur te geniet: **ekotoeriste** (en ook **ontspanningstoeriste**).","en":"(d) Game drives in a game reserve to enjoy nature: **eco-tourists** (and also **leisure tourists**)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Toeriste (b) Inkomend (c) Internasionaal (d) Eko- en ontspanningstoeriste","en":"(a) Tourists (b) Inbound (c) International (d) Eco- and leisure tourists"}},{"title":{"af":"Toeris, dagbesoeker of reisiger?","en":"Tourist, same-day visitor or traveller?"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elke persoon as 'n toeris, 'n dagbesoeker of slegs 'n reisiger, en gee 'n rede.\n\n1. Sipho ry van Soweto na die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarbaan en is dieselfde aand tuis.\n2. Mev. Botha vlieg van Kaapstad na Pretoria vir 'n tweedaagse konferensie en slaap in 'n hotel.\n3. Mnr. Naidoo ry elke werksdag van Brits na sy kantoor in Pretoria.\n4. 'n Skoolgroep uit Rustenburg kamp twee nagte in die Magaliesberg.","en":"Classify each person as a tourist, a same-day visitor or only a traveller, and give a reason.\n\n1. Sipho drives from Soweto to the Hartbeespoort Aerial Cableway and is home the same evening.\n2. Mrs Botha flies from Cape Town to Pretoria for a two-day conference and sleeps in a hotel.\n3. Mr Naidoo drives from Brits to his office in Pretoria every working day.\n4. A school group from Rustenburg camps for two nights in the Magaliesberg."},"steps":[{"af":"Persoon 1: dieselfde dag terug en geen oornagverblyf nie, dus 'n **dagbesoeker**.","en":"Person 1: back on the same day with no overnight stay, so a **same-day visitor**."},{"af":"Persoon 2: bly oor in 'n hotel buite haar gewone omgewing, dus 'n **toeris** (sakereisiger, MICE).","en":"Person 2: stays over in a hotel outside her usual environment, so a **tourist** (business tourist, MICE)."},{"af":"Persoon 3: 'n daaglikse rit binne sy gewone omgewing, dus slegs 'n **reisiger** (pendelaar), nie 'n besoeker nie.","en":"Person 3: a daily trip within his usual environment, so only a **traveller** (commuter), not a visitor."},{"af":"Persoon 4: bly twee nagte oor, dus **toeriste** (opvoedkundige en ekotoeriste; binnelandse toerisme).","en":"Person 4: stay two nights, so **tourists** (educational and eco-tourists; domestic tourism)."}],"answer":{"af":"1 Dagbesoeker; 2 Toeris; 3 Reisiger; 4 Toeriste","en":"1 Same-day visitor; 2 Tourist; 3 Traveller; 4 Tourists"}},{"title":{"af":"Stel 'n toeristeprofiel op","en":"Compile a tourist profile"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die e-pos aan 'n toerismekantoor in Hartbeespoort: *'Hallo! Ek is Lerato, 19, van Bloemfontein. Ek neem 'n tussenjaar en wil twee weke lank deur Noordwes en Gauteng reis. My begroting is klein, so ek soek goedkoop slaapplek waar ek ander jongmense kan ontmoet. Ek hou van voetslaan en abseil en wil graag die Wieg van die Mensdom sien. Ek reis per bus.'* Stel 'n toeristeprofiel vir Lerato op.","en":"Read the e-mail to a tourism office in Hartbeespoort: *'Hi! I am Lerato, 19, from Bloemfontein. I am taking a gap year and want to travel through North West and Gauteng for two weeks. My budget is small, so I am looking for cheap places to sleep where I can meet other young people. I like hiking and abseiling and would love to see the Cradle of Humankind. I travel by bus.'* Compile a tourist profile for Lerato."},"steps":[{"af":"Ouderdom en herkoms: 19 jaar, van Bloemfontein (Vrystaat), dus 'n binnelandse toeris.","en":"Age and origin: 19 years old, from Bloemfontein (Free State), so a domestic tourist."},{"af":"Begroting en reisstyl: klein begroting; reis alleen en onafhanklik vir twee weke.","en":"Budget and travel style: small budget; travels alone and independently for two weeks."},{"af":"Belangstellings: voetslaan en abseil (avontuur) en die Wieg van die Mensdom (kultuur, erfenis, opvoedkundig).","en":"Interests: hiking and abseiling (adventure) and the Cradle of Humankind (culture, heritage, educational)."},{"af":"Akkommodasie en vervoer: rugsakreisigersverblyf of 'n jeugherberg; reis per bus.","en":"Accommodation and transport: backpackers or a youth hostel; travels by bus."},{"af":"Tipe toeris: tussenjaar-, rugsak- en avontuurtoeris.","en":"Type of tourist: gap-year, backpacker and adventure tourist."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato: 19, van Bloemfontein, klein begroting, reis onafhanklik; tussenjaar-, rugsak- en avontuurtoeris; slaap in 'n backpackers en reis per bus.","en":"Lerato: 19, from Bloemfontein, small budget, travels independently; gap-year, backpacker and adventure tourist; sleeps in a backpackers and travels by bus."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik die interafhanklikheid van die sektore","en":"Explain the interdependence of the sectors"},"problem":{"af":"'n Groot rugbytoets word op Loftus Versfeld in Pretoria gespeel en duisende ondersteuners kom uit ander provinsies. Verduidelik hoe die vyf toerismesektore van mekaar afhang om die besoek te laat slaag, en wat gebeur as een sektor faal.","en":"A big rugby test is played at Loftus Versfeld in Pretoria and thousands of supporters come from other provinces. Explain how the five tourism sectors depend on each other to make the visit a success, and what happens if one sector fails."},"steps":[{"af":"**Aantreklikheid:** die rugbytoets self is die rede vir die reis.","en":"**Attraction:** the rugby test itself is the reason for the trip."},{"af":"**Vervoer:** lugdienste, busse en die Gautrain bring die ondersteuners na Pretoria en die stadion.","en":"**Transport:** airlines, buses and the Gautrain bring the supporters to Pretoria and the stadium."},{"af":"**Akkommodasie** en **kos en drank:** hotelle en gastehuise huisves die ondersteuners; restaurante en kroeë voed hulle.","en":"**Accommodation** and **food and beverage:** hotels and guest houses house the supporters; restaurants and pubs feed them."},{"af":"**Reisorganiseerders:** toeroperateurs stel pakkette saam (kaartjie + vlug + hotel) en reisagente verkoop dit.","en":"**Travel organisers:** tour operators put packages together (ticket + flight + hotel) and travel agents sell them."},{"af":"As een sektor faal, bv. 'n vlugstaking, kan ondersteuners nie kom nie: hotelle staan leeg, restaurante verloor inkomste en die hele ervaring misluk.","en":"If one sector fails, e.g. a flight strike, supporters cannot come: hotels stand empty, restaurants lose income and the whole experience fails."}],"answer":{"af":"Die sektore is interafhanklik: elkeen lewer 'n deel van die toeris se totale ervaring, en as een faal, ly al die ander.","en":"The sectors are interdependent: each delivers part of the tourist's total experience, and if one fails, all the others suffer."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Volgens die UNWTO-definisie van toerisme mag 'n besoeker nie langer as hoe lank aaneen weg wees nie?","en":"According to the UNWTO definition of tourism, a visitor may not be away for longer than how long consecutively?"},"options":[{"af":"Een maand","en":"One month"},{"af":"Ses maande","en":"Six months"},{"af":"Een jaar","en":"One year"},{"af":"Twee jaar","en":"Two years"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die definisie sê 'vir nie langer nie as een agtereenvolgende jaar'. Wie langer bly, word as 'n inwoner beskou, nie meer as 'n toeris nie.","en":"The definition says 'for not more than one consecutive year'. Someone who stays longer is seen as a resident, no longer a tourist."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Besoeker wat nie oornag nie en dieselfde dag huis toe gaan, is 'n ___.","en":"A visitor who does not stay overnight and goes home on the same day is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["dagbesoeker","ekskursionis","dag besoeker","dagbesoekers"],"en":["same-day visitor","same day visitor","excursionist","day visitor","day tripper"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["toeris","pendelaar","inwoner"],"en":["tourist","commuter","resident"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Dagbesoeker (ekskursionis) slaap nie oor nie. 'n Toeris bly ten minste een nag.","en":"A same-day visitor (excursionist) does not stay overnight. A tourist stays at least one night."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Toeris is 'n besoeker wat ten minste een nag op die bestemming oorbly.","en":"A tourist is a visitor who stays at least one night at the destination."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die oornagverblyf is wat 'n toeris van 'n dagbesoeker onderskei.","en":"True. The overnight stay is what separates a tourist from a same-day visitor."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor staan MICE in sake-toerisme?","en":"What does MICE stand for in business tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions (vergaderings, aansporings, konferensies, uitstallings)","en":"Meetings, Incentives, Conferences, Exhibitions"},{"af":"Markets, Industries, Companies, Employees (markte, nywerhede, maatskappye, werknemers)","en":"Markets, Industries, Companies, Employees"},{"af":"Meetings, Investments, Contracts, Events (vergaderings, beleggings, kontrakte, geleenthede)","en":"Meetings, Investments, Contracts, Events"},{"af":"Media, Internet, Communication, Entertainment (media, internet, kommunikasie, vermaak)","en":"Media, Internet, Communication, Entertainment"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"MICE is die sakemark: vergaderings, aansporingsreise, konferensies en uitstallings. Die ander opsies klink saaklik, maar is nie die CAPS-term nie.","en":"MICE is the business market: meetings, incentive trips, conferences and exhibitions. The other options sound business-like but are not the CAPS term."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer inwoners van Suid-Afrika binne Suid-Afrika reis, is dit ___ toerisme.","en":"When residents of South Africa travel within South Africa, it is ___ tourism."},"answers":{"af":["binnelandse","binnelands","binnelandse toerisme"],"en":["domestic","domestic tourism"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["internasionale","uitgaande","inkomende"],"en":["international","outbound","inbound"]}},"explain":{"af":"Binnelandse toerisme: inwoners reis binne hul eie land. Daar word geen landsgrens oorgesteek nie.","en":"Domestic tourism: residents travel within their own country. No national border is crossed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin uit Polokwane kuier met Kersfees by hul niggies in Brits en slaap by hulle. Watter tipe toeriste is hulle?","en":"A family from Polokwane visits their cousins in Brits for Christmas and sleeps at their house. What type of tourists are they?"},"options":[{"af":"Sakereisigers","en":"Business tourists"},{"af":"VFR-toeriste","en":"VFR tourists"},{"af":"Ekotoeriste","en":"Eco-tourists"},{"af":"Aansporingstoeriste","en":"Incentive tourists"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Hulle reis om familie te besoek en bly by hulle: VFR (besoek aan vriende en familie).","en":"They travel to visit family and stay with them: VFR (visiting friends and relatives)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Maatskappy beloon sy beste verkoopspersoon met 'n gratis reis na Mauritius. Watter tipe toeris is sy? ___","en":"A company rewards its best salesperson with a free trip to Mauritius. What type of tourist is she? ___"},"answers":{"af":["aansporingstoeris","aansporing","aansporings-toeris","incentive","incentive-toeris"],"en":["incentive tourist","incentive","incentive traveller"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["VFR-toeris","godsdienstige toeris","opvoedkundige toeris"],"en":["VFR tourist","religious tourist","educational tourist"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Reis wat die werkgewer as beloning betaal, is aansporingstoerisme (die I in MICE).","en":"A trip paid for by the employer as a reward is incentive tourism (the I in MICE)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van UITGAANDE toerisme vir Suid-Afrika?","en":"Which one is an example of OUTBOUND tourism for South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Britse gesin besoek Kaapstad","en":"A British family visits Cape Town"},{"af":"'n Gesin uit Brits ry Durban toe vir die vakansie","en":"A family from Brits drives to Durban for the holiday"},{"af":"'n Groep uit Zimbabwe doen inkopies in Pretoria","en":"A group from Zimbabwe shops in Pretoria"},{"af":"'n Gesin uit Brits vlieg na Thailand","en":"A family from Brits flies to Thailand"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Uitgaand beteken inwoners van SA reis die land uit. Die Britse gesin en die Zimbabwiese groep is inkomend; die rit na Durban is binnelands.","en":"Outbound means SA residents travel out of the country. The British family and the Zimbabwean group are inbound; the trip to Durban is domestic."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Myner wat elke dag van Brits af na 'n myn in die omgewing ry, is 'n toeris.","en":"A miner who drives from Brits to a mine in the area every day is a tourist."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Hy beweeg binne sy gewone omgewing en slaap elke aand tuis. Hy is 'n reisiger (pendelaar), nie 'n toeris nie.","en":"False. He moves within his usual environment and sleeps at home every night. He is a traveller (commuter), not a tourist."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n BEHOEFTE van 'n toeris eerder as 'n voorkeur?","en":"Which one is a NEED of a tourist rather than a preference?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Kamer met 'n seesig","en":"A room with a sea view"},{"af":"Veilige, betroubare vervoer","en":"Safe, reliable transport"},{"af":"'n Vyfster-spa-oord","en":"A five-star spa resort"},{"af":"'n Restaurant met Italiaanse kos","en":"A restaurant with Italian food"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Veiligheid en vervoer is basiese behoeftes wat elke toeris moet hê. 'n Seesig, 'n spa of Italiaanse kos is voorkeure: lekker, maar nie noodsaaklik nie.","en":"Safety and transport are basic needs that every tourist must have. A sea view, a spa or Italian food are preferences: nice, but not essential."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Pieter reis elke jaar na Sutherland net om deur teleskope na die sterre te kyk – dit is sy stokperdjie. Hy is 'n toeris met spesiale belangstelling, afgekort as ___.","en":"Pieter travels to Sutherland every year just to look at the stars through telescopes – it is his hobby. He is a special-interest tourist, abbreviated as ___."},"answers":{"af":["SIT"],"en":["SIT"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["VFR","MICE","TGCSA"],"en":["VFR","MICE","TGCSA"]}},"explain":{"af":"SIT = special interest tourist: iemand wat reis vir 'n spesifieke stokperdjie of belangstelling, soos sterrekyk of voëlkyk.","en":"SIT = special interest tourist: someone who travels for a specific hobby or interest, such as stargazing or birdwatching."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Mei Ling en haar man van Sjanghai in China bly vyf nagte in 'n lodge by die Krugerwildtuin en gaan op wildritte en voëlkykstaptogte. Watter beskrywing is korrek?","en":"Mei Ling and her husband from Shanghai in China stay five nights in a lodge at the Kruger National Park and go on game drives and birdwatching walks. Which description is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Binnelandse ekotoeriste","en":"Domestic eco-tourists"},{"af":"Uitgaande internasionale ekotoeriste","en":"Outbound international eco-tourists"},{"af":"Inkomende internasionale ekotoeriste","en":"Inbound international eco-tourists"},{"af":"Inkomende streeks-sakereisigers","en":"Inbound regional business tourists"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hulle is nie SA-inwoners nie en kom die land in (inkomend), van buite Afrika (internasionaal), vir die natuur (ekotoeriste).","en":"They are not SA residents and come into the country (inbound), from outside Africa (international), for nature (eco-tourists)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke tipe toeris by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each type of tourist to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Avontuurtoeris","en":"Adventure tourist"},"r":{"af":"Doen 'n bungee-sprong van die Bloukransbrug","en":"Does a bungee jump from the Bloukrans Bridge"}},{"l":{"af":"Godsdienstige toeris","en":"Religious tourist"},"r":{"af":"Woon die ZCC-Paasbyeenkoms by Moria by","en":"Attends the ZCC Easter gathering at Moria"}},{"l":{"af":"Mediese toeris","en":"Medical tourist"},"r":{"af":"Kom vir 'n heupvervanging na 'n privaat hospitaal in Pretoria","en":"Comes to a private hospital in Pretoria for a hip replacement"}},{"l":{"af":"Rugsakreisiger","en":"Backpacker"},"r":{"af":"Slaap in goedkoop slaapsale en reis met 'n klein begroting","en":"Sleeps in cheap dormitories and travels on a small budget"}},{"l":{"af":"Sporttoeris","en":"Sport tourist"},"r":{"af":"Reis na KwaZulu-Natal om die Comrades-maraton te hardloop","en":"Travels to KwaZulu-Natal to run the Comrades Marathon"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kyk na die hoofrede vir die reis: opwinding (avontuur), geloof (godsdiens), behandeling (medies), goedkoop reis (rugsak) en deelname aan sport (sport).","en":"Look at the main reason for the trip: excitement (adventure), faith (religious), treatment (medical), cheap travel (backpacker) and taking part in sport (sport)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling verduidelik die interafhanklikheid van die toerismesektore die beste?","en":"Which statement best explains the interdependence of the tourism sectors?"},"options":[{"af":"Die sektore het mekaar nodig: as een swak diens lewer, ly die toeris se hele ervaring en verloor die ander sektore ook kliënte","en":"The sectors need each other: if one gives poor service, the tourist's whole experience suffers and the other sectors also lose customers"},{"af":"Elke sektor werk onafhanklik en kompeteer net met die ander sektore","en":"Each sector works independently and only competes with the other sectors"},{"af":"Net die vervoersektor is belangrik, want toeriste moet eers reis","en":"Only the transport sector is important, because tourists must travel first"},{"af":"Die regering besluit wat elke sektor mag verkoop","en":"The government decides what each sector may sell"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Interafhanklik beteken die sektore steun op mekaar. 'n Kansellasie in een sektor (bv. vlugte) het 'n kettingreaksie op akkommodasie, restaurante en aantreklikhede.","en":"Interdependent means the sectors rely on each other. A cancellation in one sector (e.g. flights) has a chain reaction on accommodation, restaurants and attractions."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Gesin uit Gaborone in Botswana slaap twee nagte in Pretoria en doen inkopies. Vir Suid-Afrika is dit inkomende ___ toerisme.","en":"A family from Gaborone in Botswana sleeps two nights in Pretoria and goes shopping. For South Africa this is inbound ___ tourism."},"answers":{"af":["streeks","streeks-","streekstoerisme"],"en":["regional","regional tourism"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["binnelandse","uitgaande","plaaslike"],"en":["domestic","outbound","local"]}},"explain":{"af":"Botswana is 'n SAOG-land in ons streek, dus streekstoerisme. Hulle kom SA in, dus inkomend. Een reis kan twee etikette kry.","en":"Botswana is a SADC country in our region, so regional tourism. They come into SA, so inbound. One trip can have two labels."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Johan (20) neem 'n tussenjaar. Hy het 'n klein begroting, hou van avontuur en wil ander jongmense ontmoet. Watter reisplan beveel jy vir hom aan?","en":"Johan (20) is taking a gap year. He has a small budget, likes adventure and wants to meet other young people. Which travel plan do you recommend for him?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Vyfsterhotel in Sandton met 'n private chauffeur","en":"A five-star hotel in Sandton with a private chauffeur"},{"af":"'n Luukse reis op die Blue Train","en":"A luxury trip on the Blue Train"},{"af":"'n Konferensiepakket in Sun City","en":"A conference package at Sun City"},{"af":"'n Rugsakreisigersverblyf in die Magaliesberg met voetslaan en abseil, en reis per bus","en":"A backpackers in the Magaliesberg with hiking and abseiling, and travel by bus"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die backpackers pas by sy hele profiel: goedkoop (klein begroting), avontuurlike aktiwiteite en 'n sosiale plek vol jongmense. Die ander opsies is te duur of vir sakereisigers bedoel.","en":"The backpackers fits his whole profile: cheap (small budget), adventurous activities and a social place full of young people. The other options are too expensive or meant for business tourists."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t1-vervoer","title":{"af":"Vervoermetodes","en":"Modes of transport"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal pad-, lug-, spoor-, water- en buitengewone vervoer kan vergelyk, lughawens aan hul IATA-kodes kan herken en die beste vervoer vir 'n toeris met redes kan aanbeveel.","en":"You will be able to compare road, air, rail, water and extraordinary transport, recognise airports by their IATA codes and recommend the best transport for a tourist with reasons."},"summary":{"af":"## Waarom vervoer saak maak\n\nVervoer is die skakel tussen die toeris se **tuiste (oorsprong)** en die **bestemming**, en dit word ook *by* die bestemming gebruik vir oordragte en toere. Sonder vervoer is daar geen toerisme nie.\n\n## Padvervoer\n\n- **Motor en huurmotor:** buigsaam – jy kies jou eie tyd en roete en kan stop waar jy wil. Goedkoop per persoon vir 'n gesin. Nadele: moegheid, ongelukke, brandstof en tolgeld. Vir 'n huurmotor het jy 'n geldige rybewys en gewoonlik 'n kredietkaart nodig.\n- **Busse en luukse busse (coaches):** langafstandbusse (bv. Intercape) en toerbusse vir groepe. Goedkoop, groot kapasiteit, dikwels met 'n gids. Nadele: stadiger, met 'n vaste roete en rooster.\n- **Minibustaxi's:** die goedkoopste en byna oral beskikbaar. Nadele: veiligheidsrisiko's, oorlading, geen vaste rooster nie en min bagasieruimte.\n- **Motorfietse:** avontuurlik en goedkoop op brandstof, maar gevaarlik, met min bagasieruimte en blootgestel aan die weer.\n\n## Lugvervoer\n\nDie **vinnigste** manier om lang afstande af te lê, maar gewoonlik die duurste.\n\n| Geskeduleerde vlugte | Huurvlugte (chartervlugte) |\n|---|---|\n| Vaste, gepubliseerde rooster | Gehuur vir 'n spesifieke groep of reis |\n| Vlieg selfs al is die vliegtuig nie vol nie | Tyd en roete word by die groep aangepas |\n| Enigiemand kan 'n kaartjie koop | Bv. 'n sportspan of 'n pakketgroep na Mauritius |\n\n| Volledigediens-lugdiens | Laekoste-lugdiens |\n|---|---|\n| Bv. SAA, Airlink | Bv. FlySafair |\n| Maaltyd, ingeboekte bagasie en sitplekkeuse ingesluit | Lae basiese tarief; betaal ekstra vir bagasie, kos en sitplekkeuse |\n| Duurder, meer gemak | Goedkoper, minder gemak |\n\n### Suid-Afrika se belangrikste internasionale lughawens\n\n| Lughawe | Ligging | IATA-kode |\n|---|---|---|\n| O.R. Tambo Internasionaal | Johannesburg, Gauteng | JNB |\n| Kaapstad Internasionaal | Kaapstad, Wes-Kaap | CPT |\n| King Shaka Internasionaal | Durban, KwaZulu-Natal | DUR |\n| Lanseria Internasionaal | Noordwes van Johannesburg (die naaste aan Brits) | HLA |\n| Kruger Mpumalanga Internasionaal | Naby Mbombela, Mpumalanga | MQP |\n| Pilanesberg Internasionaal | Naby Sun City, Noordwes | – |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n IATA-kode het **drie letters** en is nie altyd die stad se gewone afkorting nie: Johannesburg is **JNB** (nie JHB nie), en King Shaka het Durban se ou kode **DUR** behou.\n\n## Spoorvervoer\n\n- **Gautrain:** 'n vinnige pendeltrein tussen **Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton en O.R. Tambo-lughawe**. Vinnig, veilig en betroubaar, en jy vermy verkeersopeenhopings.\n- **Shosholoza Meyl:** langafstand-passasierstreine (PRASA) tussen die groot stede. Goedkoper, met slaapkompartemente, maar stadig.\n- **Luukse treine:** die **Blue Train** (Pretoria–Kaapstad) en **Rovos Rail** (vanuit Pretoria). Hier is die trein self die aantreklikheid: luuks en met pragtige uitsigte, maar baie duur.\n\nVoordele van spoor: groot kapasiteit, ontspannend, mooi uitsigte. Nadele: vaste roete en rooster, en 'n beperkte netwerk.\n\n## Watervervoer\n\n- **Plesierskepe (cruise ships):** drywende hotelle wat verskeie hawens besoek.\n- **Veerbote:** bv. die veerboot vanaf die V&A Waterfront in Kaapstad na **Robbeneiland**.\n- **Jagte** en **kano's**, bv. kanotogte op die Oranjerivier.\n\n## Buitengewone vervoermetodes\n\nKamele, donkiekarre, **warmlugballonne** (bv. oor die Magaliesberg), fietse (bv. fietstoere in Soweto) en **kabelkarre** (die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarbaan en die Tafelberg-kabelkarbaan). Toeriste kies dit vir die **ervaring** – die rit self is die aantreklikheid, nie net 'n manier om van A na B te kom nie.\n\n## Vergelyk vervoermetodes\n\n| Metode | Spoed | Koste | Kapasiteit | Gemak |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Lug | Baie vinnig | Duur | Medium tot groot | Hoog |\n| Motor | Medium | Medium (goedkoop vir 'n gesin) | Klein (4–5) | Buigsaam |\n| Bus | Stadig tot medium | Goedkoop | Groot | Redelik |\n| Minibustaxi | Medium | Goedkoopste | Klein (±15) | Laag |\n| Gautrain | Vinnig | Medium | Groot | Hoog |\n| Luukse trein | Stadig | Baie duur | Klein | Luuks |\n\nVergelyk ook **veiligheid** (lug- en spoorvervoer is die veiligste, padvervoer die riskantste) en **betroubaarheid** (vaste roosters teenoor vertragings en verkeer).\n\n## Kies die beste vervoer\n\nOorweeg die toeris se **begroting, tyd, groepgrootte, afstand, doel van die reis** en **spesiale behoeftes** (rolstoel, klein kinders, baie bagasie).\n\n> **Wenk:** By 'beveel aan'-vrae noem jy die vervoermetode **én** minstens twee redes wat direk by die toeris se profiel pas. Net die naam van die vervoermiddel kry nie al die punte nie.","en":"## Why transport matters\n\nTransport is the link between the tourist's **home (origin)** and the **destination**, and it is also used *at* the destination for transfers and tours. Without transport there is no tourism.\n\n## Road transport\n\n- **Car and car hire:** flexible – you choose your own time and route and can stop where you like. Cheap per person for a family. Disadvantages: tiredness, accidents, fuel and toll fees. To hire a car you need a valid driver's licence and usually a credit card.\n- **Buses and coaches:** long-distance coaches (e.g. Intercape) and tour buses for groups. Cheap, large capacity, often with a guide. Disadvantages: slower, with a fixed route and timetable.\n- **Minibus taxis:** the cheapest and available almost everywhere. Disadvantages: safety risks, overloading, no fixed timetable and little luggage space.\n- **Motorbikes:** adventurous and cheap on fuel, but dangerous, with little luggage space and exposed to the weather.\n\n## Air transport\n\nThe **fastest** way to cover long distances, but usually the most expensive.\n\n| Scheduled flights | Charter flights |\n|---|---|\n| Fixed, published timetable | Hired for a specific group or trip |\n| Fly even if the aircraft is not full | Time and route are adapted to the group |\n| Anyone can buy a ticket | E.g. a sports team or a package group to Mauritius |\n\n| Full-service airline | Low-cost airline |\n|---|---|\n| E.g. SAA, Airlink | E.g. FlySafair |\n| Meal, checked luggage and seat choice included | Low basic fare; pay extra for luggage, food and seat choice |\n| More expensive, more comfort | Cheaper, less comfort |\n\n### South Africa's main international airports\n\n| Airport | Location | IATA code |\n|---|---|---|\n| O.R. Tambo International | Johannesburg, Gauteng | JNB |\n| Cape Town International | Cape Town, Western Cape | CPT |\n| King Shaka International | Durban, KwaZulu-Natal | DUR |\n| Lanseria International | North-west of Johannesburg (closest to Brits) | HLA |\n| Kruger Mpumalanga International | Near Mbombela, Mpumalanga | MQP |\n| Pilanesberg International | Near Sun City, North West | – |\n\n> **Common mistake:** An IATA code has **three letters** and is not always the city's usual abbreviation: Johannesburg is **JNB** (not JHB), and King Shaka kept Durban's old code **DUR**.\n\n## Rail transport\n\n- **Gautrain:** a fast commuter train between **Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton and O.R. Tambo Airport**. Fast, safe and reliable, and you avoid traffic congestion.\n- **Shosholoza Meyl:** long-distance passenger trains (PRASA) between the big cities. Cheaper, with sleeper compartments, but slow.\n- **Luxury trains:** the **Blue Train** (Pretoria–Cape Town) and **Rovos Rail** (from Pretoria). Here the train itself is the attraction: luxurious with beautiful views, but very expensive.\n\nAdvantages of rail: large capacity, relaxing, beautiful views. Disadvantages: fixed route and timetable, and a limited network.\n\n## Water transport\n\n- **Cruise ships:** floating hotels that visit several ports.\n- **Ferries:** e.g. the ferry from the V&A Waterfront in Cape Town to **Robben Island**.\n- **Yachts** and **canoes**, e.g. canoe trips on the Orange River.\n\n## Extraordinary modes of transport\n\nCamels, donkey carts, **hot-air balloons** (e.g. over the Magaliesberg), bicycles (e.g. bicycle tours in Soweto) and **cable cars** (the Hartbeespoort Aerial Cableway and the Table Mountain Aerial Cableway). Tourists choose them for the **experience** – the ride itself is the attraction, not just a way to get from A to B.\n\n## Comparing modes of transport\n\n| Mode | Speed | Cost | Capacity | Comfort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Air | Very fast | Expensive | Medium to large | High |\n| Car | Medium | Medium (cheap for a family) | Small (4–5) | Flexible |\n| Bus | Slow to medium | Cheap | Large | Reasonable |\n| Minibus taxi | Medium | Cheapest | Small (±15) | Low |\n| Gautrain | Fast | Medium | Large | High |\n| Luxury train | Slow | Very expensive | Small | Luxurious |\n\nAlso compare **safety** (air and rail are the safest, road the riskiest) and **reliability** (fixed timetables versus delays and traffic).\n\n## Choosing the best transport\n\nConsider the tourist's **budget, time, group size, distance, purpose of the trip** and **special needs** (wheelchair, small children, lots of luggage).\n\n> **Tip:** In 'recommend' questions name the mode of transport **and** at least two reasons that fit the tourist's profile directly. Only naming the vehicle does not earn all the marks."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Geskeduleerde vlug","en":"Scheduled flight"},"def":{"af":"'n Vlug wat volgens 'n vaste, gepubliseerde rooster vlieg, selfs al is die vliegtuig nie vol nie.","en":"A flight that operates according to a fixed, published timetable, even if the aircraft is not full."}},{"term":{"af":"Huurvlug (chartervlug)","en":"Charter flight"},"def":{"af":"'n Vlug wat vir 'n spesifieke groep of reis gehuur word, met 'n tyd en roete wat by die groep pas.","en":"A flight hired for a specific group or trip, with a time and route that suit the group."}},{"term":{"af":"Volledigediens-lugdiens","en":"Full-service airline"},"def":{"af":"'n Lugdiens wat maaltye, ingeboekte bagasie en sitplekkeuse by die kaartjieprys insluit, bv. SAA.","en":"An airline that includes meals, checked luggage and seat choice in the ticket price, e.g. SAA."}},{"term":{"af":"Laekoste-lugdiens","en":"Low-cost airline"},"def":{"af":"'n Lugdiens met 'n lae basiese tarief waar passasiers ekstra betaal vir bagasie, kos en sitplekkeuse, bv. FlySafair.","en":"An airline with a low basic fare where passengers pay extra for luggage, food and seat choice, e.g. FlySafair."}},{"term":{"af":"IATA-kode","en":"IATA code"},"def":{"af":"'n Kode van drie letters wat die Internasionale Lugvervoervereniging (IATA) aan 'n lughawe toeken, bv. JNB vir O.R. Tambo.","en":"A three-letter code given to an airport by the International Air Transport Association (IATA), e.g. JNB for O.R. Tambo."}},{"term":{"af":"Buitengewone vervoermetode","en":"Extraordinary mode of transport"},"def":{"af":"'n Ongewone vervoermiddel wat toeriste vir die ervaring kies, bv. 'n warmlugballon, kameel, donkiekar of kabelkar.","en":"An unusual means of transport that tourists choose for the experience, e.g. a hot-air balloon, camel, donkey cart or cable car."}},{"term":{"af":"Gautrain","en":"Gautrain"},"def":{"af":"'n Vinnige pendeltreinstelsel in Gauteng wat Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton en O.R. Tambo-lughawe verbind.","en":"A fast commuter rail system in Gauteng that links Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton and O.R. Tambo Airport."}},{"term":{"af":"Huurmotor","en":"Car hire"},"def":{"af":"'n Motor wat 'n toeris vir 'n tydperk huur; dit gee buigsaamheid, maar vereis 'n geldige rybewys en gewoonlik 'n kredietkaart.","en":"A car that a tourist rents for a period; it gives flexibility but requires a valid driver's licence and usually a credit card."}},{"term":{"af":"Kapasiteit","en":"Capacity"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal passasiers wat 'n vervoermiddel op een slag kan vervoer.","en":"The number of passengers that a means of transport can carry at one time."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beveel vervoer aan vir 'n sakereisiger","en":"Recommend transport for a business tourist"},"problem":{"af":"Mnr. Dlamini land om 07:00 op 'n werksdag by O.R. Tambo-lughawe. Hy het 'n vergadering om 09:30 in Hatfield, Pretoria. Hy reis alleen met 'n klein tassie en wil nie in die spitsverkeer vassit nie. Beveel 'n vervoermetode aan en gee drie redes.","en":"Mr Dlamini lands at O.R. Tambo Airport at 07:00 on a working day. He has a meeting at 09:30 in Hatfield, Pretoria. He travels alone with a small suitcase and does not want to get stuck in peak-hour traffic. Recommend a mode of transport and give three reasons."},"steps":[{"af":"Ontleed die profiel: alleen, min bagasie, min tyd, spitsverkeer en 'n bestemming in Pretoria.","en":"Analyse the profile: alone, little luggage, little time, peak-hour traffic and a destination in Pretoria."},{"af":"Aanbeveling: die **Gautrain**, want dit verbind die lughawe met Pretoria en Hatfield.","en":"Recommendation: the **Gautrain**, because it links the airport with Pretoria and Hatfield."},{"af":"Rede 1: dit is **vinnig** en ry op sy eie spoor, so dit vermy die spitsverkeer op die snelweë.","en":"Reason 1: it is **fast** and runs on its own track, so it avoids the peak-hour traffic on the highways."},{"af":"Rede 2: dit is **betroubaar** (vaste rooster), sodat hy betyds by sy vergadering is. Rede 3: dit is **veilig** en gemaklik vir 'n alleenreisiger.","en":"Reason 2: it is **reliable** (fixed timetable), so he will be on time for his meeting. Reason 3: it is **safe** and comfortable for someone travelling alone."},{"af":"Waarom nie die ander nie? 'n Minibustaxi is goedkoper, maar minder veilig en sonder 'n vaste rooster; 'n huurmotor sit in die verkeer vas.","en":"Why not the others? A minibus taxi is cheaper, but less safe and without a fixed timetable; a hired car gets stuck in the traffic."}],"answer":{"af":"Die Gautrain: vinnig, betroubaar en veilig, en dit vermy die spitsverkeer.","en":"The Gautrain: fast, reliable and safe, and it avoids the peak-hour traffic."}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken en vergelyk die koste: motor of vliegtuig?","en":"Calculate and compare the cost: car or aeroplane?"},"problem":{"af":"Die Van der Merwe-gesin (4 persone) uit Brits wil Durban toe gaan. Gebruik die gegewe inligting:\n\n- Afstand een rigting: 650 km\n- Die motor gebruik 8 liter per 100 km; petrol kos R22,00 per liter\n- Tolgeld heen en terug: R600\n- Retoervliegkaartjie: R1 450 per persoon, plus R800 vir vervoer na en van die lughawens\n\nBereken die koste van albei opsies vir 'n retoerreis en beveel een aan.","en":"The Van der Merwe family (4 people) from Brits want to go to Durban. Use the given information:\n\n- Distance one way: 650 km\n- The car uses 8 litres per 100 km; petrol costs R22.00 per litre\n- Toll fees there and back: R600\n- Return air ticket: R1 450 per person, plus R800 for transport to and from the airports\n\nCalculate the cost of both options for a return trip and recommend one."},"steps":[{"af":"Totale afstand: 650 km × 2 = 1 300 km. Brandstof: 1 300 ÷ 100 × 8 = 104 liter.","en":"Total distance: 650 km × 2 = 1 300 km. Fuel: 1 300 ÷ 100 × 8 = 104 litres."},{"af":"Brandstofkoste: 104 × R22,00 = R2 288. Plus tolgeld: R2 288 + R600 = **R2 888** met die motor.","en":"Fuel cost: 104 × R22.00 = R2 288. Plus tolls: R2 288 + R600 = **R2 888** by car."},{"af":"Vlug: R1 450 × 4 = R5 800. Plus lughawevervoer: R5 800 + R800 = **R6 600**.","en":"Flight: R1 450 × 4 = R5 800. Plus airport transport: R5 800 + R800 = **R6 600**."},{"af":"Verskil: R6 600 − R2 888 = R3 712. Die motor is goedkoper vir 'n gesin van vier, en hulle kan meer bagasie saamneem en stop waar hulle wil.","en":"Difference: R6 600 − R2 888 = R3 712. The car is cheaper for a family of four, and they can take more luggage and stop where they like."},{"af":"Die vliegtuig spaar egter baie tyd: kies dit as die gesin min verlof het en die ekstra geld kan bekostig.","en":"The aeroplane does save a lot of time, though: choose it if the family has little leave and can afford the extra money."}],"answer":{"af":"Motor: R2 888; vlug: R6 600. Die motor is R3 712 goedkoper en word aanbeveel vir 'n gesin met 'n begroting.","en":"Car: R2 888; flight: R6 600. The car is R3 712 cheaper and is recommended for a family on a budget."}},{"title":{"af":"Lees 'n reisplan met IATA-kodes","en":"Read an itinerary with IATA codes"},"problem":{"af":"'n Toeris se e-kaartjie wys hierdie roete: **JNB → CPT → DUR → JNB**. Daarna wil sy 'n ekstra vlug vanaf **MQP** bespreek. (a) Noem die lughawe en die stad vir elke kode. (b) Waarom sal sy na MQP reis?","en":"A tourist's e-ticket shows this route: **JNB → CPT → DUR → JNB**. After that she wants to book an extra flight from **MQP**. (a) Name the airport and the city for each code. (b) Why would she travel to MQP?"},"steps":[{"af":"JNB = O.R. Tambo Internasionale Lughawe, Johannesburg (Gauteng).","en":"JNB = O.R. Tambo International Airport, Johannesburg (Gauteng)."},{"af":"CPT = Kaapstad Internasionale Lughawe, Kaapstad (Wes-Kaap).","en":"CPT = Cape Town International Airport, Cape Town (Western Cape)."},{"af":"DUR = King Shaka Internasionale Lughawe, Durban (KwaZulu-Natal).","en":"DUR = King Shaka International Airport, Durban (KwaZulu-Natal)."},{"af":"(b) MQP = Kruger Mpumalanga Internasionale Lughawe naby Mbombela. Sy sal waarskynlik die Krugerwildtuin besoek.","en":"(b) MQP = Kruger Mpumalanga International Airport near Mbombela. She will probably visit the Kruger National Park."}],"answer":{"af":"JNB = O.R. Tambo (Johannesburg); CPT = Kaapstad; DUR = King Shaka (Durban); MQP = Kruger Mpumalanga, vir die Krugerwildtuin.","en":"JNB = O.R. Tambo (Johannesburg); CPT = Cape Town; DUR = King Shaka (Durban); MQP = Kruger Mpumalanga, for the Kruger National Park."}},{"title":{"af":"Buitengewone vervoer: voordele en nadele","en":"Extraordinary transport: advantages and disadvantages"},"problem":{"af":"'n Paartjie vier hul huweliksherdenking met 'n warmlugballonvlug oor die Magaliesberg by sonop. (a) Klassifiseer hierdie vervoermetode. (b) Gee twee redes waarom toeriste dit kies. (c) Gee twee nadele. (d) Noem twee ander voorbeelde van dieselfde soort vervoer.","en":"A couple celebrates their wedding anniversary with a hot-air balloon flight over the Magaliesberg at sunrise. (a) Classify this mode of transport. (b) Give two reasons why tourists choose it. (c) Give two disadvantages. (d) Name two other examples of the same kind of transport."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n **Buitengewone vervoermetode** – dit is meer 'n ervaring as 'n manier om iewers te kom.","en":"(a) An **extraordinary mode of transport** – it is more an experience than a way to get somewhere."},{"af":"(b) Dit is 'n unieke, onvergeetlike ervaring, en die uitsig oor die berge en die Hartbeespoortdam is asemrowend.","en":"(b) It is a unique, unforgettable experience, and the view over the mountains and Hartbeespoort Dam is breathtaking."},{"af":"(c) Dit is duur, dit hang van die weer af (wind of reën kan die vlug kanselleer) en net 'n klein groep kan saamgaan.","en":"(c) It is expensive, it depends on the weather (wind or rain can cancel the flight) and only a small group can go along."},{"af":"(d) Die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarbaan of die Tafelberg-kabelkarbaan, 'n kameelrit, 'n donkiekarrit of 'n fietstoer in Soweto.","en":"(d) The Hartbeespoort Aerial Cableway or the Table Mountain Aerial Cableway, a camel ride, a donkey-cart ride or a bicycle tour in Soweto."}],"answer":{"af":"Buitengewone vervoer: gekies vir die unieke ervaring en uitsig; nadele: duur, weerafhanklik, klein kapasiteit.","en":"Extraordinary transport: chosen for the unique experience and view; disadvantages: expensive, weather-dependent, small capacity."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter trein verbind Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton en O.R. Tambo-lughawe?","en":"Which train links Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton and O.R. Tambo Airport?"},"options":[{"af":"Shosholoza Meyl","en":"Shosholoza Meyl"},{"af":"Gautrain","en":"Gautrain"},{"af":"Blue Train","en":"Blue Train"},{"af":"Rovos Rail","en":"Rovos Rail"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die Gautrain is Gauteng se vinnige pendeltrein. Shosholoza Meyl ry lang afstande, en die Blue Train en Rovos Rail is luukse toeristetreine.","en":"The Gautrain is Gauteng's fast commuter train. Shosholoza Meyl covers long distances, and the Blue Train and Rovos Rail are luxury tourist trains."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die luukse trein wat tussen Pretoria en Kaapstad ry en na sy kleur genoem is, is die ___.","en":"The luxury train that runs between Pretoria and Cape Town and is named after its colour is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["Blue Train","Blou Trein","Bloutrein","die Blue Train"],"en":["Blue Train","the Blue Train"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Gautrain","Rovos Rail","Shosholoza Meyl"],"en":["Gautrain","Rovos Rail","Shosholoza Meyl"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Blue Train ry tussen Pretoria en Kaapstad. Rovos Rail is ook 'n luukse trein uit Pretoria, maar is nie na 'n kleur genoem nie.","en":"The Blue Train runs between Pretoria and Cape Town. Rovos Rail is also a luxury train from Pretoria, but it is not named after a colour."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Huurvlug (chartervlug) vlieg volgens 'n vaste, gepubliseerde rooster, maak nie saak hoeveel passasiers bespreek het nie.","en":"A charter flight flies according to a fixed, published timetable, no matter how many passengers have booked."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit beskryf 'n geskeduleerde vlug. 'n Huurvlug word vir 'n spesifieke groep gehuur, met 'n tyd en roete wat by die groep pas.","en":"False. That describes a scheduled flight. A charter flight is hired for a specific group, with a time and route that suit the group."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van 'n buitengewone vervoermetode?","en":"Which one is an example of an extraordinary mode of transport?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Minibustaxi","en":"A minibus taxi"},{"af":"Die Gautrain","en":"The Gautrain"},{"af":"'n Luukse bus","en":"A luxury coach"},{"af":"'n Warmlugballon oor die Magaliesberg","en":"A hot-air balloon over the Magaliesberg"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Warmlugballon is ongewoon en word vir die ervaring gekies. Die ander drie is gewone, alledaagse vervoermiddele.","en":"A hot-air balloon is unusual and is chosen for the experience. The other three are ordinary, everyday means of transport."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Lugdiens met 'n baie lae basiese tarief, waar jy ekstra betaal vir bagasie, kos en sitplekkeuse, is 'n ___-lugdiens.","en":"An airline with a very low basic fare, where you pay extra for luggage, food and seat choice, is a ___ airline."},"answers":{"af":["laekoste","lae koste","laekoste-lugdiens","goedkoop","budget"],"en":["low-cost","low cost","budget","no-frills","no frills"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["volledigediens","luukse","nasionale"],"en":["full-service","luxury","national"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Laekoste-lugdiens (bv. FlySafair) hou die basiese prys laag en laat jou net betaal vir wat jy ekstra wil hê.","en":"A low-cost airline (e.g. FlySafair) keeps the basic price low and makes you pay only for the extras you want."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n VOORDEEL van 'n minibustaxi vir 'n rugsakreisiger met 'n klein begroting?","en":"Which one is an ADVANTAGE of a minibus taxi for a backpacker on a small budget?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is baie goedkoop en byna oral beskikbaar","en":"It is very cheap and available almost everywhere"},{"af":"Dit het baie bagasieruimte en luukse sitplekke","en":"It has lots of luggage space and luxury seats"},{"af":"Dit ry volgens 'n vaste rooster wat aanlyn gepubliseer word","en":"It runs on a fixed timetable that is published online"},{"af":"Dit is die veiligste vervoermetode in Suid-Afrika","en":"It is the safest mode of transport in South Africa"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Minibustaxi's is die goedkoopste vervoer en ry byna oral. Die ander stellings is juis hul nadele: min bagasieruimte, geen vaste rooster nie en veiligheidsrisiko's.","en":"Minibus taxis are the cheapest transport and go almost everywhere. The other statements are exactly their disadvantages: little luggage space, no fixed timetable and safety risks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Toeriste reis met 'n ___ vanaf die V&A Waterfront in Kaapstad na Robbeneiland.","en":"Tourists travel by ___ from the V&A Waterfront in Cape Town to Robben Island."},"answers":{"af":["veerboot","veerbote","boot","ferry"],"en":["ferry","ferries","boat"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kabelkar","trein","warmlugballon"],"en":["cable car","train","hot-air balloon"]}},"explain":{"af":"Robbeneiland lê in die see, dus is watervervoer nodig: die veerboot vertrek vanaf die V&A Waterfront.","en":"Robben Island lies in the sea, so water transport is needed: the ferry leaves from the V&A Waterfront."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Gautrain is 'n langafstandtrein wat passasiers van Johannesburg na Kaapstad vervoer.","en":"The Gautrain is a long-distance train that carries passengers from Johannesburg to Cape Town."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die Gautrain ry net in Gauteng (Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton, O.R. Tambo). Langafstandtreine soos Shosholoza Meyl en die Blue Train ry na Kaapstad.","en":"False. The Gautrain only runs in Gauteng (Pretoria, Johannesburg, Sandton, O.R. Tambo). Long-distance trains such as Shosholoza Meyl and the Blue Train go to Cape Town."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is gewoonlik by 'n volledigediens-lugdiens ingesluit, maar moet jy by 'n laekoste-lugdiens ekstra voor betaal?","en":"What is usually included by a full-service airline, but must be paid for extra on a low-cost airline?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Sitplek op die vliegtuig","en":"A seat on the aircraft"},{"af":"Die veiligheidsdemonstrasie","en":"The safety demonstration"},{"af":"'n Maaltyd en ingeboekte bagasie","en":"A meal and checked luggage"},{"af":"'n Klein handsak onder die sitplek","en":"A small handbag under the seat"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By 'n laekoste-lugdiens betaal jy ekstra vir kos, ingeboekte bagasie en sitplekkeuse. 'n Sitplek, die veiligheidsdemonstrasie en 'n klein handsak is by elke kaartjie ingesluit.","en":"On a low-cost airline you pay extra for food, checked luggage and seat choice. A seat, the safety demonstration and a small handbag are included with every ticket."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin van vyf met baie bagasie wil van Brits na die Drakensberg reis en langs die pad by padstalletjies stop. Watter vervoer pas die beste?","en":"A family of five with lots of luggage wants to travel from Brits to the Drakensberg and stop at farm stalls along the way. Which transport fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Eie motor of huurmotor","en":"Their own car or a hired car"},{"af":"'n Laekoste-vlug","en":"A low-cost flight"},{"af":"'n Minibustaxi","en":"A minibus taxi"},{"af":"Die Gautrain","en":"The Gautrain"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Motor is buigsaam (stop waar jy wil), het plek vir bagasie en is goedkoop per persoon vir 'n gesin. 'n Vlug laat jou nie by padstalletjies stop nie, en die Gautrain ry net in Gauteng.","en":"A car is flexible (stop where you like), has space for luggage and is cheap per person for a family. A flight does not let you stop at farm stalls, and the Gautrain only runs in Gauteng."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Huurmotor kos R480 per dag. 'n Toeris huur dit vir 4 dae en betaal 'n eenmalige versekeringsfooi van R350. Die totale koste is R___.","en":"A hired car costs R480 per day. A tourist hires it for 4 days and pays a once-off insurance fee of R350. The total cost is R___."},"answers":{"af":["2270","2 270","R2270","R2 270"],"en":["2270","2 270","R2270","R2 270"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1 920","3 320","830"],"en":["1 920","3 320","830"]}},"explain":{"af":"R480 × 4 = R1 920, plus die eenmalige fooi: R1 920 + R350 = R2 270. Die fooi word net een keer bygetel, nie per dag nie.","en":"R480 × 4 = R1 920, plus the once-off fee: R1 920 + R350 = R2 270. The fee is added only once, not per day."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeris in Kaapstad wil so naby moontlik aan die Krugerwildtuin land. Na watter van hierdie lughawens moet sy vlieg?","en":"A tourist in Cape Town wants to land as close as possible to the Kruger National Park. To which of these airports should she fly?"},"options":[{"af":"Lanseria Internasionaal (HLA)","en":"Lanseria International (HLA)"},{"af":"Kruger Mpumalanga Internasionaal (MQP)","en":"Kruger Mpumalanga International (MQP)"},{"af":"King Shaka Internasionaal (DUR)","en":"King Shaka International (DUR)"},{"af":"O.R. Tambo Internasionaal (JNB)","en":"O.R. Tambo International (JNB)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kruger Mpumalanga Internasionaal lê naby Mbombela, die naaste aan die Krugerwildtuin. Van JNB of HLA moet sy nog ure ver ry.","en":"Kruger Mpumalanga International lies near Mbombela, the closest to the Kruger National Park. From JNB or HLA she would still have to drive for hours."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lughawe by sy IATA-kode.","en":"Match each airport to its IATA code."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"O.R. Tambo Internasionaal","en":"O.R. Tambo International"},"r":{"af":"JNB","en":"JNB"}},{"l":{"af":"Kaapstad Internasionaal","en":"Cape Town International"},"r":{"af":"CPT","en":"CPT"}},{"l":{"af":"King Shaka Internasionaal","en":"King Shaka International"},"r":{"af":"DUR","en":"DUR"}},{"l":{"af":"Lanseria Internasionaal","en":"Lanseria International"},"r":{"af":"HLA","en":"HLA"}},{"l":{"af":"Kruger Mpumalanga Internasionaal","en":"Kruger Mpumalanga International"},"r":{"af":"MQP","en":"MQP"}}],"explain":{"af":"JNB is Johannesburg se O.R. Tambo (nie JHB nie), CPT is Kaapstad, DUR is King Shaka in Durban, HLA is Lanseria en MQP is Kruger Mpumalanga.","en":"JNB is Johannesburg's O.R. Tambo (not JHB), CPT is Cape Town, DUR is King Shaka in Durban, HLA is Lanseria and MQP is Kruger Mpumalanga."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kies baie toeriste die Blue Train na Kaapstad, al is 'n vlug vinniger en goedkoper?","en":"Why do many tourists choose the Blue Train to Cape Town, even though a flight is faster and cheaper?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is die enigste manier om van Pretoria na Kaapstad te reis","en":"It is the only way to travel from Pretoria to Cape Town"},{"af":"Luukse treine het geen vaste rooster nie","en":"Luxury trains have no fixed timetable"},{"af":"Dit is die goedkoopste vervoer na Kaapstad","en":"It is the cheapest transport to Cape Town"},{"af":"Die trein self is die aantreklikheid: luukse, uitsigte en 'n unieke ervaring","en":"The train itself is the attraction: luxury, views and a unique experience"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vir hierdie toeriste gaan dit oor die reis self, nie oor spoed of prys nie. Die ander stellings is feitelik verkeerd: daar is vlugte en busse, en die Blue Train is baie duur.","en":"For these tourists it is about the journey itself, not about speed or price. The other statements are factually wrong: there are flights and buses, and the Blue Train is very expensive."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Skoolgroep van 45 leerders gaan op 'n dagtoer na die Wieg van die Mensdom. Die beste enkele voertuig met genoeg kapasiteit vir almal is 'n ___.","en":"A school group of 45 learners goes on a day tour to the Cradle of Humankind. The best single vehicle with enough capacity for everyone is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["bus","toerbus","luukse bus","coach"],"en":["bus","coach","tour bus","luxury coach"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["minibustaxi","huurmotor","helikopter"],"en":["minibus taxi","hired car","helicopter"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Bus het groot kapasiteit en is goedkoop per persoon vir 'n groot groep. 'n Minibustaxi neem net ongeveer 15 passasiers en 'n huurmotor net 4–5.","en":"A bus has a large capacity and is cheap per person for a big group. A minibus taxi takes only about 15 passengers and a hired car only 4–5."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Mev. Venter (72) gebruik 'n rolstoel. Sy en haar man wil vir 'n week van Pretoria na Kaapstad reis, het 'n gemiddelde begroting en wil nie lank onderweg wees nie. Watter aanbeveling met rede is die beste?","en":"Mrs Venter (72) uses a wheelchair. She and her husband want to travel from Pretoria to Cape Town for a week, have an average budget and do not want to be on the road for long. Which recommendation with a reason is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Minibustaxi, want dit is die goedkoopste","en":"A minibus taxi, because it is the cheapest"},{"af":"'n Motorfiets, want dit is avontuurlik en goedkoop op brandstof","en":"A motorbike, because it is adventurous and cheap on fuel"},{"af":"'n Vlug met 'n volledigediens-lugdiens, want dit is die vinnigste en gemaklikste oor 'n lang afstand, met bagasie ingesluit","en":"A flight with a full-service airline, because it is the fastest and most comfortable over a long distance, with luggage included"},{"af":"'n Langafstandbus, want dit het 'n groot kapasiteit","en":"A long-distance coach, because it has a large capacity"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beste aanbeveling pas by AL die behoeftes: 'n lang afstand, min tyd, gemak vir 'n bejaarde rolstoelgebruiker en 'n gemiddelde begroting. Die taxi en motorfiets is ongemaklik en onveilig vir haar, en die bus is baie lank onderweg – 'n groot kapasiteit help hierdie paartjie niks.","en":"The best recommendation fits ALL the needs: a long distance, little time, comfort for an elderly wheelchair user and an average budget. The taxi and motorbike are uncomfortable and unsafe for her, and the bus takes very long – a large capacity does not help this couple at all."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t1-akkommodasie","title":{"af":"Akkommodasie: tipes, terminologie en sterregradering","en":"Accommodation: types, terminology and star grading"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal tipes akkommodasie, kamertipes, maaltydplanne en tariefterme kan verduidelik, die TGCSA-sterregradering kan beskryf en die koste van 'n verblyf kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to explain types of accommodation, room types, meal plans and rate terms, describe TGCSA star grading and calculate the cost of a stay."},"summary":{"af":"## Tipes akkommodasie\n\n| Tipe | Voorbeelde | Fasiliteite en dienste | Geskik vir |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Formele diens | Hotelle, oorde, lodges | 24-uur-ontvangs, restaurant, kamerdiens, daaglikse skoonmaak, swembad, konferensiesale | Sake- en ontspanningstoeriste wat volle diens wil hê |\n| Gasteverblyf | Gastehuise, bed-en-ontbyt (B&B), plattelandse huise | Min kamers, persoonlike diens, ontbyt; die eienaar woon dikwels op die perseel | Paartjies en sakereisigers wat 'n tuiste weg van die huis soek |\n| Selfsorg | Chalets, kothuise, woonstelle, vakansiehuise | Toegeruste kombuis en beddegoed; jy kook self; min of geen dienste | Gesinne en groepe met 'n begroting |\n| Karavaan- en kampeerparke | Staanplekke vir tente en karavane | Ablusieblokke, braaiplekke, kragpunte | Gesinne, buitelewe-liefhebbers, begroting |\n| Rugsakreisigersverblyf/jeugherberge | Backpackers, hostelle | Slaapsale, gedeelde badkamers en kombuis; sosiaal en goedkoop | Rugsakreisigers, jongmense, tussenjaartoeriste |\n\n## Kamertipes\n\n- **Enkelkamer:** een bed vir een persoon.\n- **Dubbelkamer:** **een dubbelbed** vir twee persone.\n- **Tweelingkamer (twin):** **twee enkelbeddens**.\n- **Driepersoonskamer (triple):** vir drie persone.\n- **Gesinskamer:** vir ouers en kinders.\n- **Suite:** 'n slaapkamer met 'n **aparte sitkamer**.\n- **Inmekaarlopende kamers (interleading):** twee kamers met 'n binnedeur tussen hulle – ideaal vir gesinne.\n- **En suite-badkamer:** die badkamer is deel van die kamer.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n Dubbelkamer en 'n tweelingkamer is albei vir twee mense, maar die dubbelkamer het **een** groot bed en die tweelingkamer **twee** enkelbeddens.\n\n## Maaltydplanne\n\n| Plan | Afkorting | Ingesluit |\n|---|---|---|\n| Slegs kamer / selfsorg | RO | Geen maaltye nie |\n| Bed en ontbyt | B&B | Ontbyt |\n| Aandete, bed en ontbyt (halfpension) | DBB / HB | Ontbyt en aandete |\n| Volpension | FB | Ontbyt, middagete en aandete |\n| Alles-ingesluit | AI | Alle maaltye, drankies en dikwels aktiwiteite |\n\n## Tarieweterme en afkortings\n\n- **pp:** per persoon\n- **pppn:** per persoon per nag\n- **pps:** per persoon wat deel (die prys geld as twee mense 'n kamer deel)\n- **Enkeltoeslag (single supplement):** 'n ekstra bedrag wat iemand betaal wat alleen in 'n kamer bly\n- **Standaardtarief (rack rate):** die volle, gepubliseerde tarief sonder afslag\n- **Hoog- of spitsseisoen:** besige tye (skoolvakansies, Desember) met hoër tariewe; **laag- of buiteseisoen:** stil tye met laer tariewe\n- **Inboek en uitboek (check-in/check-out):** die tye waarop jy die kamer kry en dit weer moet ontruim\n- **Nie-opdaag (no-show):** 'n gas wat bespreek, nie kanselleer nie en ook nie opdaag nie\n- **Deposito:** 'n gedeeltelike vooruitbetaling wat die bespreking bevestig\n\n## Tegnologie in die kamer\n\n| Doel | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Vermaak | Slim-TV, Wi-Fi, stroomdienste |\n| Inligting | Die hotel se TV-kanaal of toep |\n| Veiligheid | Sleutelkaarte, kluis in die kamer, rookverklikkers |\n| Gemak | Lugversorging |\n| Werk | Lessenaar, kragpunte, USB-poorte |\n| Omgewingsverantwoordelikheid | Sleutelkaart-energieskakelaar, bewegingsensors, LED-ligte |\n\n## Sterregradering\n\nDie **TGCSA** (Toerismegraderingsraad van Suid-Afrika) val onder **SA Tourism** en ken **1 tot 5 sterre** toe: 1 ster beteken skoon, gemaklik en basies; 5 sterre beteken uitsonderlike luukse en diens. Gradering is **vrywillig** – geen wet dwing 'n onderneming om gegradeer te word nie.\n\n**Prosedure:**\n\n1. Die onderneming doen aansoek en betaal die fooi.\n2. 'n **Assessor** besoek en evalueer die onderneming (kamers, netheid, diens, fasiliteite).\n3. Die sterregradering word toegeken, saam met 'n sertifikaat en 'n **plaket** met die TGCSA-logo.\n4. Die gradering moet **jaarliks hernu** word, met 'n herassessering.\n\n**Voordele:** toeriste weet watter **gehalte** om te verwag; die onderneming kry **bemarking** en 'n mededingende voordeel bo ongegradeerde mededingers; **standaarde** in die bedryf styg, wat Suid-Afrika se beeld as bestemming verbeter.\n\n## Bereken die koste van 'n verblyf\n\n`Totaal = tarief pppn × aantal persone × aantal nagte` – tel dan enige enkeltoeslag by.\n\nBv. R950 pppn × 2 persone × 3 nagte = **R5 700**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Skryf altyd die berekening stap vir stap uit en sit die R-teken by die antwoord. Jy kry punte vir die metode, nie net vir die antwoord nie. Kyk of die tarief **per persoon** of **per kamer** is!","en":"## Types of accommodation\n\n| Type | Examples | Facilities and services | Suitable for |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Formal service | Hotels, resorts, lodges | 24-hour reception, restaurant, room service, daily cleaning, swimming pool, conference rooms | Business and leisure tourists who want full service |\n| Guest accommodation | Guest houses, bed and breakfasts (B&B), country houses | Few rooms, personal service, breakfast; the owner often lives on the premises | Couples and business tourists looking for a home away from home |\n| Self-catering | Chalets, cottages, apartments, holiday homes | Equipped kitchen and bedding; you cook yourself; few or no services | Families and groups on a budget |\n| Caravan and camping parks | Sites for tents and caravans | Ablution blocks, braai areas, power points | Families, outdoor lovers, budget |\n| Backpackers/youth hostels | Backpackers, hostels | Dormitories, shared bathrooms and kitchen; social and cheap | Backpackers, young people, gap-year tourists |\n\n## Room types\n\n- **Single room:** one bed for one person.\n- **Double room:** **one double bed** for two people.\n- **Twin room:** **two single beds**.\n- **Triple room:** for three people.\n- **Family room:** for parents and children.\n- **Suite:** a bedroom with a **separate lounge**.\n- **Interleading rooms:** two rooms with an inside door between them – ideal for families.\n- **En suite bathroom:** the bathroom is part of the room.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A double room and a twin room are both for two people, but the double room has **one** big bed and the twin room **two** single beds.\n\n## Meal plans\n\n| Plan | Abbreviation | Included |\n|---|---|---|\n| Room only / self-catering | RO | No meals |\n| Bed and breakfast | B&B | Breakfast |\n| Dinner, bed and breakfast (half board) | DBB / HB | Breakfast and dinner |\n| Full board | FB | Breakfast, lunch and dinner |\n| All-inclusive | AI | All meals, drinks and often activities |\n\n## Rate terms and abbreviations\n\n- **pp:** per person\n- **pppn:** per person per night\n- **pps:** per person sharing (the price applies when two people share a room)\n- **Single supplement:** an extra amount paid by someone who stays alone in a room\n- **Rack rate:** the full, published rate without discount\n- **High or peak season:** busy times (school holidays, December) with higher rates; **low or off-peak season:** quiet times with lower rates\n- **Check-in and check-out:** the times when you get the room and must vacate it again\n- **No-show:** a guest who books, does not cancel and does not arrive\n- **Deposit:** a partial payment in advance that confirms the booking\n\n## In-room technology\n\n| Purpose | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Entertainment | Smart TV, Wi-Fi, streaming services |\n| Information | The hotel's TV channel or app |\n| Safety | Key cards, in-room safe, smoke detectors |\n| Comfort | Air-conditioning |\n| Work | Desk, plug points, USB ports |\n| Environmental responsibility | Key-card energy switch, motion sensors, LED lights |\n\n## Star grading\n\nThe **TGCSA** (Tourism Grading Council of South Africa) falls under **SA Tourism** and awards **1 to 5 stars**: 1 star means clean, comfortable and basic; 5 stars means exceptional luxury and service. Grading is **voluntary** – no law forces a business to be graded.\n\n**Procedure:**\n\n1. The business applies and pays the fee.\n2. An **assessor** visits and evaluates the business (rooms, cleanliness, service, facilities).\n3. The star grading is awarded, together with a certificate and a **plaque** with the TGCSA logo.\n4. The grading must be **renewed every year**, with a re-assessment.\n\n**Benefits:** tourists know what **quality** to expect; the business gets **marketing** and a competitive advantage over ungraded competitors; **standards** in the industry rise, which improves South Africa's image as a destination.\n\n## Calculating the cost of a stay\n\n`Total = rate pppn × number of people × number of nights` – then add any single supplement.\n\nE.g. R950 pppn × 2 people × 3 nights = **R5 700**.\n\n> **Tip:** Always write out the calculation step by step and put the R sign with the answer. You get marks for the method, not only for the answer. Check whether the rate is **per person** or **per room**!"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Formele diens-akkommodasie","en":"Formal service accommodation"},"def":{"af":"Akkommodasie met volle dienste soos 24-uur-ontvangs, 'n restaurant en kamerdiens, bv. hotelle, oorde en lodges.","en":"Accommodation with full services such as 24-hour reception, a restaurant and room service, e.g. hotels, resorts and lodges."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfsorgakkommodasie","en":"Self-catering accommodation"},"def":{"af":"Akkommodasie met 'n toegeruste kombuis waar gaste self kook, bv. chalets, kothuise en vakansiewoonstelle.","en":"Accommodation with an equipped kitchen where guests cook for themselves, e.g. chalets, cottages and holiday apartments."}},{"term":{"af":"Tweelingkamer","en":"Twin room"},"def":{"af":"'n Kamer met twee enkelbeddens vir twee persone.","en":"A room with two single beds for two people."}},{"term":{"af":"En suite","en":"En suite"},"def":{"af":"Die badkamer is deel van die kamer, sodat die gas dit nie met ander hoef te deel nie.","en":"The bathroom is part of the room, so the guest does not have to share it with others."}},{"term":{"af":"Halfpension (DBB)","en":"Half board (DBB)"},"def":{"af":"'n Maaltydplan wat die kamer, ontbyt en aandete insluit (dinner, bed and breakfast).","en":"A meal plan that includes the room, breakfast and dinner (dinner, bed and breakfast)."}},{"term":{"af":"Volpension","en":"Full board"},"def":{"af":"'n Maaltydplan wat ontbyt, middagete en aandete insluit.","en":"A meal plan that includes breakfast, lunch and dinner."}},{"term":{"af":"pppn","en":"pppn"},"def":{"af":"Per persoon per nag: die tarief wat elke gas vir elke nag betaal.","en":"Per person per night: the rate that each guest pays for each night."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkeltoeslag","en":"Single supplement"},"def":{"af":"'n Ekstra bedrag wat 'n gas betaal wat alleen 'n kamer gebruik wat vir twee bedoel is.","en":"An extra amount paid by a guest who uses a room meant for two people on his or her own."}},{"term":{"af":"Standaardtarief (rack rate)","en":"Rack rate"},"def":{"af":"Die volle, gepubliseerde prys van 'n kamer sonder enige afslag.","en":"The full, published price of a room without any discount."}},{"term":{"af":"TGCSA","en":"TGCSA"},"def":{"af":"Die Toerismegraderingsraad van Suid-Afrika, deel van SA Tourism, wat akkommodasie vrywillig met 1 tot 5 sterre gradeer.","en":"The Tourism Grading Council of South Africa, part of SA Tourism, which voluntarily grades accommodation with 1 to 5 stars."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bereken die koste van 'n verblyf","en":"Calculate the cost of a stay"},"problem":{"af":"Mnr. en mev. Mokoena bespreek 'n dubbelkamer by 'n 3-ster-gastehuis in Hartbeespoort vir 3 nagte. Die tarief is R950 pppn (B&B). (a) Wat beteken pppn en B&B? (b) Bereken die totale koste.","en":"Mr and Mrs Mokoena book a double room at a 3-star guest house in Hartbeespoort for 3 nights. The rate is R950 pppn (B&B). (a) What do pppn and B&B mean? (b) Calculate the total cost."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) pppn = per persoon per nag; B&B = bed en ontbyt (die kamer plus ontbyt).","en":"(a) pppn = per person per night; B&B = bed and breakfast (the room plus breakfast)."},{"af":"(b) Formule: tarief pppn × aantal persone × aantal nagte.","en":"(b) Formula: rate pppn × number of people × number of nights."},{"af":"Vervang: R950 × 2 × 3.","en":"Substitute: R950 × 2 × 3."},{"af":"R950 × 2 = R1 900 per nag; R1 900 × 3 = **R5 700**.","en":"R950 × 2 = R1 900 per night; R1 900 × 3 = **R5 700**."}],"answer":{"af":"Totale koste = R5 700","en":"Total cost = R5 700"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken met 'n enkeltoeslag","en":"Calculate with a single supplement"},"problem":{"af":"Drie kollegas bly 2 nagte by 'n hotel in Sandton vir 'n konferensie. Twee van hulle deel 'n tweelingkamer teen R780 pps per nag. Die derde bly alleen en betaal 'n enkeltoeslag van R350 per nag bo-op die pps-tarief. Bereken die totale koste vir die groep.","en":"Three colleagues stay 2 nights at a hotel in Sandton for a conference. Two of them share a twin room at R780 pps per night. The third stays alone and pays a single supplement of R350 per night on top of the pps rate. Calculate the total cost for the group."},"steps":[{"af":"Die twee wat deel: R780 × 2 persone × 2 nagte = R3 120.","en":"The two who share: R780 × 2 people × 2 nights = R3 120."},{"af":"Die enkelgas betaal per nag: R780 + R350 = R1 130.","en":"The single guest pays per night: R780 + R350 = R1 130."},{"af":"Vir 2 nagte: R1 130 × 2 = R2 260.","en":"For 2 nights: R1 130 × 2 = R2 260."},{"af":"Totaal: R3 120 + R2 260 = **R5 380**.","en":"Total: R3 120 + R2 260 = **R5 380**."}],"answer":{"af":"Totale koste = R5 380","en":"Total cost = R5 380"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies akkommodasie vir 'n toeristeprofiel","en":"Choose accommodation for a tourist profile"},"problem":{"af":"Die Nel-gesin (twee ouers en drie kinders van 6, 9 en 12) wil 'n week by Hartbeespoortdam vakansie hou. Hulle begroting is beperk, hulle wil self kook en braai, en die kinders wil swem. Watter tipe akkommodasie, kamerreëling en maaltydplan beveel jy aan? Gee redes.","en":"The Nel family (two parents and three children aged 6, 9 and 12) want to holiday at Hartbeespoort Dam for a week. Their budget is limited, they want to cook and braai themselves, and the children want to swim. Which type of accommodation, room arrangement and meal plan do you recommend? Give reasons."},"steps":[{"af":"Ontleed die profiel: gesin van vyf, beperkte begroting, wil self kook en braai, 'n hele week, kinders wil swem.","en":"Analyse the profile: family of five, limited budget, want to cook and braai themselves, a whole week, the children want to swim."},{"af":"Tipe: 'n **selfsorgchalet** by 'n vakansieoord – goedkoper as 'n hotel vir vyf mense, en met 'n kombuis en braaiplek.","en":"Type: a **self-catering chalet** at a holiday resort – cheaper than a hotel for five people, and with a kitchen and braai area."},{"af":"Kamerreëling: 'n chalet met twee of drie slaapkamers, of **inmekaarlopende kamers**, sodat die ouers naby die kinders is.","en":"Room arrangement: a chalet with two or three bedrooms, or **interleading rooms**, so that the parents are close to the children."},{"af":"Maaltydplan: **slegs kamer / selfsorg (RO)** – hulle kook self, so hulle betaal nie vir maaltye wat hulle nie gaan eet nie.","en":"Meal plan: **room only / self-catering (RO)** – they cook themselves, so they do not pay for meals they are not going to eat."},{"af":"Kies 'n oord met 'n swembad. 'n Hotel met volpension sou te duur wees, en 'n backpackers is nie vir 'n gesin met jong kinders bedoel nie.","en":"Choose a resort with a swimming pool. A hotel with full board would be too expensive, and a backpackers is not meant for a family with young children."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Selfsorgchalet met 'n swembad by die oord, verskeie slaapkamers en die RO-plan (selfsorg).","en":"A self-catering chalet with a swimming pool at the resort, several bedrooms and the RO plan (self-catering)."}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik TGCSA-gradering","en":"Explain TGCSA grading"},"problem":{"af":"Me. Pretorius open 'n nuwe gastehuis in Brits en wonder of sy by die TGCSA moet aansoek doen. (a) Moet sy, volgens die wet? (b) Beskryf die prosedure. (c) Gee drie voordele van gradering.","en":"Ms Pretorius opens a new guest house in Brits and wonders whether she should apply to the TGCSA. (a) Must she, by law? (b) Describe the procedure. (c) Give three benefits of grading."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Nee – TGCSA-gradering is **vrywillig**, maar dit word sterk aanbeveel.","en":"(a) No – TGCSA grading is **voluntary**, but it is strongly recommended."},{"af":"(b) Sy doen aansoek en betaal die fooi; 'n **assessor** besoek en evalueer die gastehuis.","en":"(b) She applies and pays the fee; an **assessor** visits and evaluates the guest house."},{"af":"Die TGCSA ken 1 tot 5 sterre toe met 'n sertifikaat en plaket, en die gradering word **jaarliks hernu** en herassesseer.","en":"The TGCSA awards 1 to 5 stars with a certificate and plaque, and the grading is **renewed every year** and re-assessed."},{"af":"(c) Voordeel 1: toeriste vertrou die gehalte. Voordeel 2: gratis bemarking en 'n voordeel bo ongegradeerde mededingers. Voordeel 3: dit help haar om hoë standaarde te handhaaf.","en":"(c) Benefit 1: tourists trust the quality. Benefit 2: free marketing and an advantage over ungraded competitors. Benefit 3: it helps her to maintain high standards."}],"answer":{"af":"Vrywillig; aansoek → assessor besoek → sterre toegeken → jaarlikse hernuwing; voordele: gehalte, bemarking, standaarde.","en":"Voluntary; apply → assessor visits → stars awarded → annual renewal; benefits: quality, marketing, standards."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is 'n voorbeeld van selfsorgakkommodasie?","en":"Which of the following is an example of self-catering accommodation?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Vyfsterhotel","en":"A five-star hotel"},{"af":"'n Chalet met 'n toegeruste kombuis","en":"A chalet with an equipped kitchen"},{"af":"'n Bed-en-ontbyt","en":"A bed and breakfast"},{"af":"'n Lodge met volpension","en":"A lodge with full board"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"By selfsorg kook die gaste self, daarom is 'n toegeruste kombuis die kenmerk. 'n Hotel, B&B en lodge met volpension voorsien maaltye.","en":"With self-catering the guests cook for themselves, so an equipped kitchen is the key feature. A hotel, B&B and lodge with full board provide meals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die afkorting pppn beteken per persoon per ___.","en":"The abbreviation pppn means per person per ___."},"answers":{"af":["nag"],"en":["night"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dag","week","maand"],"en":["day","week","month"]}},"explain":{"af":"pppn = per persoon per nag. Akkommodasie word per nag gehef, nie per dag nie.","en":"pppn = per person per night. Accommodation is charged per night, not per day."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"TGCSA-sterregradering is verpligtend vir alle akkommodasie-ondernemings in Suid-Afrika.","en":"TGCSA star grading is compulsory for all accommodation businesses in South Africa."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gradering is vrywillig. Ondernemings doen self aansoek omdat dit hulle bemarking en geloofwaardigheid gee.","en":"False. Grading is voluntary. Businesses apply themselves because it gives them marketing and credibility."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter maaltydplan sluit ontbyt, middagete én aandete in?","en":"Which meal plan includes breakfast, lunch and dinner?"},"options":[{"af":"Bed en ontbyt (B&B)","en":"Bed and breakfast (B&B)"},{"af":"Aandete, bed en ontbyt (DBB)","en":"Dinner, bed and breakfast (DBB)"},{"af":"Volpension (FB)","en":"Full board (FB)"},{"af":"Slegs kamer (RO)","en":"Room only (RO)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Volpension = al drie maaltye. DBB (halfpension) sluit net ontbyt en aandete in; B&B net ontbyt; RO geen maaltye nie.","en":"Full board = all three meals. DBB (half board) includes only breakfast and dinner; B&B only breakfast; RO no meals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kamer met twee enkelbeddens word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A room with two single beds is called a ___ room."},"answers":{"af":["tweelingkamer","tweeling","twin","twin-kamer","twinkamer"],"en":["twin","twin room"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dubbelkamer","enkelkamer","suite"],"en":["double","single","suite"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Tweelingkamer (twin) het twee enkelbeddens. 'n Dubbelkamer het een dubbelbed – albei is vir twee mense.","en":"A twin room has two single beds. A double room has one double bed – both are for two people."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die 'rack rate' (standaardtarief) van 'n hotel?","en":"What is the rack rate of a hotel?"},"options":[{"af":"Die afslagprys vir groepe","en":"The discounted price for groups"},{"af":"Die prys vir 'n kamer sonder 'n badkamer","en":"The price for a room without a bathroom"},{"af":"Die tarief vir kinders onder 12","en":"The rate for children under 12"},{"af":"Die volle, gepubliseerde tarief sonder enige afslag","en":"The full, published rate without any discount"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die rack rate is die volle amptelike prys. Groepe, laagseisoen-gaste of aanlynbesprekings kry dikwels 'n afslag daarop.","en":"The rack rate is the full official price. Groups, low-season guests or online bookings often get a discount on it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die TGCSA ken 'n sterregradering van 1 tot ___ sterre toe.","en":"The TGCSA awards a star grading of 1 to ___ stars."},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","7","10"],"en":["3","7","10"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die TGCSA gradeer van 1 ster (skoon en basies) tot 5 sterre (uitsonderlike luukse).","en":"The TGCSA grades from 1 star (clean and basic) to 5 stars (exceptional luxury)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Gas wat 'n kamer bespreek, nie kanselleer nie en ook nie opdaag nie, word 'n 'no-show' genoem.","en":"A guest who books a room, does not cancel and also does not arrive is called a 'no-show'."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n No-show kos die onderneming geld, daarom vra baie plekke 'n deposito om die bespreking te bevestig.","en":"True. A no-show costs the business money, which is why many places ask for a deposit to confirm the booking."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kamertegnologie dra die meeste by tot omgewingsverantwoordelikheid?","en":"Which in-room technology contributes most to environmental responsibility?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Sleutelkaartskakelaar wat die krag afsit wanneer die gas uitgaan","en":"A key-card switch that turns off the power when the guest goes out"},{"af":"'n Slim-TV met stroomdienste","en":"A smart TV with streaming services"},{"af":"'n Kluis in die kamer","en":"An in-room safe"},{"af":"Ekstra USB-poorte by die lessenaar","en":"Extra USB ports at the desk"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die sleutelkaartskakelaar spaar elektrisiteit, want ligte en lugversorging gaan af as niemand in die kamer is nie. Die TV is vermaak, die kluis veiligheid en die USB-poorte werk.","en":"The key-card switch saves electricity, because lights and air-conditioning go off when nobody is in the room. The TV is entertainment, the safe is safety and the USB ports are for work."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Sakereisiger het een nag naby die Sandton-konferensiesentrum nodig. Hy wil 'n lessenaar, vinnige Wi-Fi en 'n restaurant hê. Watter akkommodasie pas die beste?","en":"A business tourist needs one night near the Sandton Convention Centre. He wants a desk, fast Wi-Fi and a restaurant. Which accommodation fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Karavaanpark buite die stad","en":"A caravan park outside the city"},{"af":"'n Selfsorgkothuis op 'n plaas","en":"A self-catering cottage on a farm"},{"af":"'n Slaapsaal in 'n rugsakreisigersverblyf","en":"A dormitory in a backpackers"},{"af":"'n Stadshotel met formele diens, 'n lessenaar en Wi-Fi","en":"A city hotel with formal service, a desk and Wi-Fi"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Formele diens-hotel in die stad voorsien alles wat hy nodig het: ligging, werkfasiliteite, Wi-Fi en 'n restaurant. Die ander opsies is te ver of het nie die dienste nie.","en":"A formal service hotel in the city provides everything he needs: location, work facilities, Wi-Fi and a restaurant. The other options are too far away or lack the services."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Twee volwassenes bly 4 nagte by 'n gastehuis teen R850 pppn. Die totale koste is R___.","en":"Two adults stay 4 nights at a guest house at R850 pppn. The total cost is R___."},"answers":{"af":["6800","6 800","R6800","R6 800"],"en":["6800","6 800","R6800","R6 800"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3 400","1 700","13 600"],"en":["3 400","1 700","13 600"]}},"explain":{"af":"R850 × 2 persone × 4 nagte = R6 800. R3 400 vergeet die tweede persoon, en R1 700 is net een nag.","en":"R850 × 2 people × 4 nights = R6 800. R3 400 forgets the second person, and R1 700 is only one night."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Mnr. en mev. Pillay wil elke dag die omgewing verken en middagete buite eet, maar wil ontbyt en aandete by die hotel geniet. Watter maaltydplan pas die beste?","en":"Mr and Mrs Pillay want to explore the area every day and eat lunch out, but want to enjoy breakfast and dinner at the hotel. Which meal plan fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"Volpension","en":"Full board"},{"af":"Halfpension (DBB)","en":"Half board (DBB)"},{"af":"Slegs kamer","en":"Room only"},{"af":"Bed en ontbyt","en":"Bed and breakfast"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Halfpension (DBB) sluit presies ontbyt en aandete in. Met volpension betaal hulle vir middagete wat hulle nie eet nie; B&B en RO sluit nie aandete in nie.","en":"Half board (DBB) includes exactly breakfast and dinner. With full board they pay for lunch they will not eat; B&B and RO do not include dinner."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke afkorting by die regte betekenis.","en":"Match each abbreviation to the correct meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"pp","en":"pp"},"r":{"af":"Per persoon","en":"Per person"}},{"l":{"af":"pppn","en":"pppn"},"r":{"af":"Per persoon per nag","en":"Per person per night"}},{"l":{"af":"pps","en":"pps"},"r":{"af":"Per persoon wat deel","en":"Per person sharing"}},{"l":{"af":"B&B","en":"B&B"},"r":{"af":"Bed en ontbyt","en":"Bed and breakfast"}},{"l":{"af":"DBB","en":"DBB"},"r":{"af":"Aandete, bed en ontbyt","en":"Dinner, bed and breakfast"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die afkortings verskyn op elke prysskedule. Let veral op pps: die prys geld net as twee mense die kamer deel.","en":"These abbreviations appear on every rate sheet. Watch out for pps in particular: the price applies only when two people share the room."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Alleenreisiger bespreek 3 nagte teen R1 100 pps met 'n enkeltoeslag van R400 per nag. Hoeveel betaal sy altesaam?","en":"A solo traveller books 3 nights at R1 100 pps with a single supplement of R400 per night. How much does she pay in total?"},"options":[{"af":"R3 300","en":"R3 300"},{"af":"R3 700","en":"R3 700"},{"af":"R4 500","en":"R4 500"},{"af":"R6 600","en":"R6 600"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Per nag: R1 100 + R400 = R1 500; vir 3 nagte: R1 500 × 3 = R4 500. R3 300 vergeet die toeslag, R3 700 tel dit net een keer by, en R6 600 betaal vir twee mense.","en":"Per night: R1 100 + R400 = R1 500; for 3 nights: R1 500 × 3 = R4 500. R3 300 forgets the supplement, R3 700 adds it only once, and R6 600 pays for two people."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voordat die TGCSA sterre aan 'n gastehuis toeken, besoek en evalueer 'n ___ die onderneming.","en":"Before the TGCSA awards stars to a guest house, an ___ visits and evaluates the business."},"answers":{"af":["assessor","beoordelaar","evalueerder","gradeerder"],"en":["assessor","grading assessor","evaluator"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["toeroperateur","reisagent","bestuurder"],"en":["tour operator","travel agent","manager"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n TGCSA-assessor kom kyk na die kamers, netheid, diens en fasiliteite voordat die gradering toegeken word. Dit word jaarliks herhaal.","en":"A TGCSA assessor comes to inspect the rooms, cleanliness, service and facilities before the grading is awarded. This is repeated every year."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter argument is die STERKSTE rede vir 'n nuwe B&B in Brits om by die TGCSA aansoek te doen?","en":"Which argument is the STRONGEST reason for a new B&B in Brits to apply to the TGCSA?"},"options":[{"af":"Gradering verseker toeriste van gehalte en gee die B&B 'n bemarkingsvoordeel bo ongegradeerde mededingers","en":"Grading assures tourists of quality and gives the B&B a marketing advantage over ungraded competitors"},{"af":"Dit word deur die wet vereis","en":"It is required by law"},{"af":"Die regering betaal dan die B&B se lopende uitgawes","en":"The government then pays the B&B's running costs"},{"af":"Die B&B hoef daarna nooit weer geassesseer te word nie","en":"The B&B never has to be assessed again afterwards"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Gradering is vrywillig, so die waarde lê in vertroue en bemarking. Dit word nie deur die wet vereis nie, die regering betaal nie uitgawes nie, en die gradering moet jaarliks hernu word.","en":"Grading is voluntary, so its value lies in trust and marketing. It is not required by law, the government does not pay expenses, and the grading must be renewed every year."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t1-kos-aantreklikhede-struktuur","title":{"af":"Kos en drank, die aantreklikheidsektor en die struktuur van die toerismebedryf","en":"Food and beverage, the attraction sector and the structure of the tourism industry"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kos-en-drank-ondernemings en aantreklikhede kan klassifiseer en die rol van die openbare en privaat sektor en die toerismeverenigings kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to classify food and beverage establishments and attractions and explain the roles of the public and private sectors and the tourism associations."},"summary":{"af":"## Kos-en-drank-ondernemings\n\nDie kos-en-drank-sektor sorg dat toeriste kan eet en drink terwyl hulle reis. Ken die CAPS-tipes, hul kenmerke en watter toeriste hulle lok.\n\n| Onderneming | Kenmerke | Teikentoeriste |\n|---|---|---|\n| Volledige-diens-restaurant | Tafeldiens deur kelners, spyskaart met gange, gemaklike sitplek; duurder | Paartjies, sake- en ontspanningstoeriste |\n| Koffiewinkel | Koffie, koek en ligte etes; ontspanne en vinnig | Dagbesoekers, sakemense tussen afsprake |\n| Kitskos-uitlegpunt | Toonbankdiens, standaard spyskaart, vinnig en goedkoop, wegneemetes | Gesinne, rugsakreisigers, toeriste op pad |\n| Kroeg/pub | Hoofsaaklik drankies, kroegetes, sport op TV | Volwasse ontspannings- en sporttoeriste |\n| Nageregwinkel | Roomys, wafels, koek en ander soetgoed | Gesinne en jongmense |\n| Taverne/shebeen | In townships; plaaslike drankies, kos en musiek | Kulturele toeriste, bv. op 'n township-toer |\n| Straatstalletjie en mark | Plaaslike kos (vetkoek, kota, braaivleis) en kunsvlyt in die buitelug; goedkoop | Kulturele en begrotingstoeriste |\n\n## Die aantreklikheidsektor\n\n'n **Toeriste-aantreklikheid** is 'n plek, gebeurtenis of aktiwiteit wat toeriste na 'n gebied lok. Die subsektore is:\n\n- **Natuurlik** – deur die natuur geskep: die Magaliesberg, Tafelberg, die Krugerwildtuin, die Blyderivierkloof.\n- **Mensgemaak/gebou** – deur mense gebou: Sun City, Gold Reef City, die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarweg en ook Hartbeespoortdam self (dit is 'n mensgemaakte dam!).\n- **Kultureel/erfenis** – geskiedenis en kultuur: Robbeneiland, die Apartheidsmuseum, die Wieg van die Mensdom.\n- **Geleenthede** – vir 'n beperkte tyd: die Comrades-maraton, Aardklop in Potchefstroom.\n- **Vermaak** – teaters, casino's en pretparke.\n- **Sport** – stadions soos Loftus Versfeld, gholfbane en avontuursport.\n\nElke aantreklikheid bied **aktiwiteite** aan (wildritte, staptogte, toere, skouspele) en lok 'n bepaalde **tipe toeris**: 'n wildtuin lok ekotoeriste, 'n museum kulturele toeriste en 'n rugbytoets sporttoeriste.\n\n### Primêr teenoor sekondêr\n\n- **Primêre aantreklikheid:** die **hoofrede** vir die besoek – sonder dit sou die toeris nie gekom het nie (bv. die Krugerwildtuin).\n- **Sekondêre aantreklikheid:** 'n plek wat die toeris besoek **omdat hy in elk geval in die omgewing is** (bv. God's Window op pad Kruger toe).\n\n> **Wenk:** Dieselfde plek kan vir een toeris primêr en vir 'n ander sekondêr wees. Vra altyd: *Hoekom het hierdie toeris die reis onderneem?*\n\n## Die struktuur van die toerismebedryf\n\n### Openbare sektor (die regering)\n\n| Vlak | Rol |\n|---|---|\n| Nasionale **Departement van Toerisme** | Maak toerismebeleid en -wetgewing |\n| Provinsiale toerismeowerhede | Bevorder en ontwikkel toerisme in elke provinsie |\n| Distrik- en plaaslike munisipaliteite (bv. Madibeng) | Toerisme-inligtingskantore en **infrastruktuur**: paaie, padtekens, water, vullisverwydering |\n\n**Verwante departemente:** Binnelandse Sake (paspoorte en visums), die departement verantwoordelik vir die omgewing (parke en bewaring), Vervoer (paaie en lughawens) en die Polisie (veiligheid van toeriste).\n\n**Openbare entiteite (staatsondernemings):**\n\n- **SA Toerisme:** bemark Suid-Afrika plaaslik en in die buiteland; die TGCSA val onder SA Toerisme.\n- **SANParke:** bestuur die nasionale parke.\n- **SAHRA:** beskerm erfenishulpbronne en erfenisterreine.\n- **ACSA:** besit en bedryf die belangrikste lughawens.\n\n### Privaat sektor\n\nBesighede wat **vir wins** toerismeprodukte lewer: akkommodasie, vervoer, aantreklikhede, restaurante, toeroperateurs en reisagente.\n\n- 'n **Toeroperateur** stel 'n **pakket** saam (vervoer + akkommodasie + aktiwiteite) teen een prys.\n- 'n **Reisagent** **verkoop** reisprodukte (pakkette, vlugte, verblyf) aan die publiek en verdien **kommissie**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie die twee omruil nie. Toeroperateur = *saamstel*; reisagent = *verkoop*.\n\n**Plaaslike gemeenskappe** verskaf gidse, kunsvlyt, kultuurervarings en werkers – en hulle moet ook voordeel uit toerisme trek.\n\n### Verenigings\n\n| Akroniem | Funksie |\n|---|---|\n| TBCSA | Toerismebesigheidsraad: die stem van die privaat sektor teenoor die regering |\n| TGCSA | Toerismegraderingsraad: ken 1–5 sterre toe |\n| FTTSA | Fair Trade Tourism: sertifiseer besighede wat billike lone en werksomstandighede bied en die gemeenskap en omgewing respekteer |\n| SATSA | Verteenwoordig toerismediensverskaffers soos inkomende toeroperateurs en vervoer |\n| FEDHASA | Verteenwoordig die gasvryheidsbedryf (hotelle, restaurante) |\n| ASATA | Vereniging van reisagente |\n| SAACI | Konferensie- en byeenkomstebedryf |\n| SAVRALA | Motorhuur- en voertuighuurmaatskappye |\n| SAYTC | Jeugreis en rugsakreisigers |\n\n### Internasionale liggame\n\n- **UNWTO** (die VN se Wêreldtoerismeorganisasie, sedert 2024 ook bekend as UN Tourism): bevorder verantwoordelike, volhoubare toerisme wêreldwyd.\n- **WTTC:** die wêreldwye stem van die privaat reis- en toerismesektor; doen navorsing oor toerisme se ekonomiese impak.\n- **SAOG (SADC):** Suider-Afrikaanse Ontwikkelingsgemeenskap – streeksamewerking, ook in toerisme.\n- **WWF:** Wêreldnatuurfonds – bewaring van die natuur en bedreigde spesies.\n\n> **Onthou!** Openbare sektor = regering: beleid, infrastruktuur en bemarking, nie vir wins nie. Privaat sektor = besighede wat produkte en dienste vir wins lewer. Hulle het mekaar nodig: die munisipaliteit bou die pad, en die privaat lodge lok die toeris.","en":"## Food and beverage establishments\n\nThe food and beverage sector makes sure tourists can eat and drink while they travel. Know the CAPS types, their features and which tourists they attract.\n\n| Establishment | Features | Target tourists |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full-service restaurant | Table service by waiters, menu with courses, comfortable seating; more expensive | Couples, business and leisure tourists |\n| Coffee shop | Coffee, cake and light meals; relaxed and quick | Day visitors, business people between meetings |\n| Fast-food outlet | Counter service, standard menu, fast and cheap, takeaways | Families, backpackers, tourists on the road |\n| Pub/bar | Mainly drinks, pub meals, sport on TV | Adult leisure and sport tourists |\n| Dessert store | Ice cream, waffles, cake and other sweet treats | Families and young people |\n| Tavern/shebeen | In townships; local drinks, food and music | Cultural tourists, e.g. on a township tour |\n| Street stall and market | Local food (vetkoek, kota, braaivleis) and crafts in the open air; cheap | Cultural and budget tourists |\n\n## The attraction sector\n\nA **tourist attraction** is a place, event or activity that draws tourists to an area. The subsectors are:\n\n- **Natural** – created by nature: the Magaliesberg, Table Mountain, the Kruger National Park, the Blyde River Canyon.\n- **Man-made/built** – built by people: Sun City, Gold Reef City, the Hartbeespoort Aerial Cableway and also Hartbeespoort Dam itself (it is a man-made dam!).\n- **Cultural/heritage** – history and culture: Robben Island, the Apartheid Museum, the Cradle of Humankind.\n- **Events** – for a limited time: the Comrades Marathon, Aardklop in Potchefstroom.\n- **Entertainment** – theatres, casinos and theme parks.\n- **Sport** – stadiums such as Loftus Versfeld, golf courses and adventure sport.\n\nEvery attraction offers **activities** (game drives, hikes, tours, shows) and draws a particular **type of tourist**: a game reserve attracts ecotourists, a museum cultural tourists and a rugby test sport tourists.\n\n### Primary versus secondary\n\n- **Primary attraction:** the **main reason** for the visit – without it the tourist would not have come (e.g. the Kruger National Park).\n- **Secondary attraction:** a place the tourist visits **because he is in the area anyway** (e.g. God's Window on the way to Kruger).\n\n> **Tip:** The same place can be primary for one tourist and secondary for another. Always ask: *Why did this tourist make the trip?*\n\n## The structure of the tourism industry\n\n### Public sector (government)\n\n| Level | Role |\n|---|---|\n| National **Department of Tourism** | Makes tourism policy and legislation |\n| Provincial tourism authorities | Promote and develop tourism in each province |\n| District and local municipalities (e.g. Madibeng) | Tourism information offices and **infrastructure**: roads, road signs, water, refuse removal |\n\n**Related departments:** Home Affairs (passports and visas), the department responsible for the environment (parks and conservation), Transport (roads and airports) and the Police (tourist safety).\n\n**Public entities (parastatals):**\n\n- **SA Tourism:** markets South Africa locally and abroad; the TGCSA falls under SA Tourism.\n- **SANParks:** manages the national parks.\n- **SAHRA:** protects heritage resources and heritage sites.\n- **ACSA:** owns and operates the main airports.\n\n### Private sector\n\nBusinesses that provide tourism products **for profit**: accommodation, transport, attractions, restaurants, tour operators and travel agents.\n\n- A **tour operator** assembles a **package** (transport + accommodation + activities) at one price.\n- A **travel agent** **sells** travel products (packages, flights, accommodation) to the public and earns **commission**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don't swap the two. Tour operator = *assembles*; travel agent = *sells*.\n\n**Local communities** provide guides, crafts, cultural experiences and workers – and they must also benefit from tourism.\n\n### Associations\n\n| Acronym | Function |\n|---|---|\n| TBCSA | Tourism Business Council: the voice of the private sector to government |\n| TGCSA | Tourism Grading Council: awards 1–5 stars |\n| FTTSA | Fair Trade Tourism: certifies businesses that pay fair wages, offer fair working conditions and respect the community and environment |\n| SATSA | Represents tourism service providers such as inbound tour operators and transport |\n| FEDHASA | Represents the hospitality industry (hotels, restaurants) |\n| ASATA | Association of travel agents |\n| SAACI | Conference and meetings industry |\n| SAVRALA | Car rental and vehicle leasing companies |\n| SAYTC | Youth travel and backpackers |\n\n### International bodies\n\n- **UNWTO** (the UN World Tourism Organization, since 2024 also known as UN Tourism): promotes responsible, sustainable tourism worldwide.\n- **WTTC:** the global voice of the private travel and tourism sector; researches tourism's economic impact.\n- **SADC:** Southern African Development Community – regional co-operation, also in tourism.\n- **WWF:** World Wide Fund for Nature – conservation of nature and endangered species.\n\n> **Remember!** Public sector = government: policy, infrastructure and marketing, not for profit. Private sector = businesses that provide products and services for profit. They need each other: the municipality builds the road, and the private lodge attracts the tourist."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kos-en-drank-onderneming","en":"Food and beverage establishment"},"def":{"af":"'n Besigheid wat kos en/of drank aan toeriste en ander kliënte verkoop, bv. 'n restaurant, koffiewinkel of shebeen.","en":"A business that sells food and/or drinks to tourists and other customers, e.g. a restaurant, coffee shop or shebeen."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeriste-aantreklikheid","en":"Tourist attraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Plek, gebeurtenis of aktiwiteit wat toeriste na 'n gebied lok.","en":"A place, event or activity that draws tourists to an area."}},{"term":{"af":"Primêre aantreklikheid","en":"Primary attraction"},"def":{"af":"Die hoofrede waarom 'n toeris 'n gebied besoek.","en":"The main reason why a tourist visits an area."}},{"term":{"af":"Sekondêre aantreklikheid","en":"Secondary attraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Aantreklikheid wat die toeris besoek omdat hy in elk geval in die omgewing is.","en":"An attraction the tourist visits because he is in the area anyway."}},{"term":{"af":"Natuurlike aantreklikheid","en":"Natural attraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Aantreklikheid wat deur die natuur geskep is, bv. berge, riviere, wildtuine.","en":"An attraction created by nature, e.g. mountains, rivers, game reserves."}},{"term":{"af":"Mensgemaakte aantreklikheid","en":"Man-made attraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Aantreklikheid wat deur mense gebou is, bv. 'n kabelkarweg, dam of pretpark.","en":"An attraction built by people, e.g. a cableway, dam or theme park."}},{"term":{"af":"Openbare sektor","en":"Public sector"},"def":{"af":"Die regering op nasionale, provinsiale en plaaslike vlak, wat beleid maak en infrastruktuur verskaf – nie vir wins nie.","en":"Government at national, provincial and local level, which makes policy and provides infrastructure – not for profit."}},{"term":{"af":"Privaat sektor","en":"Private sector"},"def":{"af":"Besighede in private besit wat toerismeprodukte en -dienste vir wins lewer.","en":"Privately owned businesses that provide tourism products and services for profit."}},{"term":{"af":"Toeroperateur","en":"Tour operator"},"def":{"af":"'n Besigheid wat vervoer, akkommodasie en aktiwiteite in een reispakket saamstel.","en":"A business that assembles transport, accommodation and activities into one travel package."}},{"term":{"af":"Reisagent","en":"Travel agent"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat reisprodukte aan die publiek verkoop en kommissie daarop verdien.","en":"Someone who sells travel products to the public and earns commission on them."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer aantreklikhede","en":"Classify attractions"},"problem":{"af":"Die Duitse gesin Weber vlieg na Suid-Afrika om die Krugerwildtuin te besoek. Op pad soontoe stop hulle by God's Window en besoek hulle 'n kultuurdorp naby Hazyview. Klassifiseer elke aantreklikheid as primêr of sekondêr, en as natuurlik, mensgemaak of kultureel. Watter tipe toeriste is die Webers?","en":"The German Weber family flies to South Africa to visit the Kruger National Park. On the way there they stop at God's Window and visit a cultural village near Hazyview. Classify each attraction as primary or secondary, and as natural, man-made or cultural. What type of tourists are the Webers?"},"steps":[{"af":"Vra eers: wat is die hoofrede vir die reis? Die Krugerwildtuin – dus is Kruger die **primêre** aantreklikheid. Dit is deur die natuur geskep: **natuurlik**.","en":"First ask: what is the main reason for the trip? The Kruger National Park – so Kruger is the **primary** attraction. It was created by nature: **natural**."},{"af":"God's Window besoek hulle net omdat dit op pad is: **sekondêr**. Dit is 'n natuurlike uitkykpunt oor die platorand: **natuurlik**.","en":"They visit God's Window only because it is on the way: **secondary**. It is a natural viewpoint over the escarpment: **natural**."},{"af":"Die kultuurdorp is ook op pad en wys plaaslike kultuur en tradisies: **sekondêr** en **kultureel/erfenis**.","en":"The cultural village is also on the way and shows local culture and traditions: **secondary** and **cultural/heritage**."},{"af":"Die Webers kom van buite Suid-Afrika en kom vir die natuur en wild: **internasionale (inkomende) eko-/ontspanningstoeriste**.","en":"The Webers come from outside South Africa for nature and wildlife: **international (inbound) eco/leisure tourists**."}],"answer":{"af":"Kruger = primêr, natuurlik; God's Window = sekondêr, natuurlik; kultuurdorp = sekondêr, kultureel. Internasionale eko-/ontspanningstoeriste.","en":"Kruger = primary, natural; God's Window = secondary, natural; cultural village = secondary, cultural. International eco/leisure tourists."}},{"title":{"af":"Openbare of privaat sektor?","en":"Public or private sector?"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer die volgende as openbare of privaat sektor en gee elkeen se rol: (a) die Departement van Toerisme, (b) SANParke, (c) 'n reisagentskap in Brits, (d) die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarweg, (e) die Madibeng-munisipaliteit.","en":"Classify the following as public or private sector and give each one's role: (a) the Department of Tourism, (b) SANParks, (c) a travel agency in Brits, (d) the Hartbeespoort Aerial Cableway, (e) the Madibeng municipality."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elkeen: is dit die regering (of 'n staatsonderneming), of 'n besigheid wat vir wins werk?","en":"Ask for each one: is it government (or a parastatal), or a business that works for profit?"},{"af":"(a) **Openbaar** – nasionale regering: maak toerismebeleid en -wetgewing. (b) **Openbaar** – openbare entiteit: bestuur die nasionale parke.","en":"(a) **Public** – national government: makes tourism policy and legislation. (b) **Public** – public entity: manages the national parks."},{"af":"(c) **Privaat** – verkoop reisprodukte en verdien kommissie. (d) **Privaat** – 'n mensgemaakte aantreklikheid wat kaartjies vir wins verkoop.","en":"(c) **Private** – sells travel products and earns commission. (d) **Private** – a man-made attraction that sells tickets for profit."},{"af":"(e) **Openbaar** – plaaslike regering: toerisme-inligtingskantoor, paaie, padtekens, water en vullisverwydering.","en":"(e) **Public** – local government: tourism information office, roads, road signs, water and refuse removal."}],"answer":{"af":"Openbaar: (a), (b), (e). Privaat: (c), (d).","en":"Public: (a), (b), (e). Private: (c), (d)."}},{"title":{"af":"Toeroperateur teenoor reisagent – bereken die kommissie","en":"Tour operator versus travel agent – calculate the commission"},"problem":{"af":"'n Maatskappy in Pretoria stel 'n 3-dag-pakket saam: kombivervoer, 2 nagte in 'n lodge by Pilanesberg en twee wildritte, teen R4 800 per persoon. 'n Agentskap in Brits verkoop die pakket aan die Botha-gesin van 4 en verdien 10% kommissie. (a) Wie is die toeroperateur en wie die reisagent? (b) Bereken die gesin se totale koste en die agent se kommissie.","en":"A company in Pretoria assembles a 3-day package: minibus transport, 2 nights at a lodge near Pilanesberg and two game drives, at R4 800 per person. An agency in Brits sells the package to the Botha family of 4 and earns 10% commission. (a) Who is the tour operator and who is the travel agent? (b) Calculate the family's total cost and the agent's commission."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die Pretoria-maatskappy **stel die pakket saam** = **toeroperateur**. Die Brits-agentskap **verkoop** dit = **reisagent**.","en":"(a) The Pretoria company **assembles the package** = **tour operator**. The Brits agency **sells** it = **travel agent**."},{"af":"(b) Totale koste = R4 800 × 4 persone = **R19 200**.","en":"(b) Total cost = R4 800 × 4 people = **R19 200**."},{"af":"Kommissie = 10% van R19 200 = 0,10 × R19 200 = **R1 920**.","en":"Commission = 10% of R19 200 = 0.10 × R19 200 = **R1 920**."}],"answer":{"af":"Toeroperateur: Pretoria-maatskappy; reisagent: Brits-agentskap. Totaal R19 200; kommissie R1 920.","en":"Tour operator: Pretoria company; travel agent: Brits agency. Total R19 200; commission R1 920."}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte vereniging","en":"Choose the right association"},"problem":{"af":"Watter vereniging moet elkeen kontak? (a) 'n Gastehuis wat 'n stergradering wil hê. (b) 'n Nuwe motorhuurmaatskappy by Lanseria. (c) 'n Besigheid wat konferensies vir maatskappye reël. (d) 'n Lodge wat wil bewys dat hy sy werkers billik betaal en die gemeenskap bevoordeel.","en":"Which association should each contact? (a) A guest house that wants a star grading. (b) A new car rental company at Lanseria. (c) A business that organises conferences for companies. (d) A lodge that wants to prove that it pays its workers fairly and benefits the community."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Stergradering word deur die **TGCSA** toegeken (onder SA Toerisme).","en":"(a) Star grading is awarded by the **TGCSA** (under SA Tourism)."},{"af":"(b) Motorhuur- en voertuighuurmaatskappye behoort aan **SAVRALA**.","en":"(b) Car rental and vehicle leasing companies belong to **SAVRALA**."},{"af":"(c) Die konferensiebedryf word deur **SAACI** verteenwoordig.","en":"(c) The conference industry is represented by **SAACI**."},{"af":"(d) Billike lone, werksomstandighede en gemeenskapsvoordele = **FTTSA** (Fair Trade Tourism).","en":"(d) Fair wages, working conditions and community benefits = **FTTSA** (Fair Trade Tourism)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) TGCSA (b) SAVRALA (c) SAACI (d) FTTSA","en":"(a) TGCSA (b) SAVRALA (c) SAACI (d) FTTSA"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kos-en-drank-onderneming bied toonbankdiens, 'n standaard spyskaart en vinnige, goedkoop wegneemetes?","en":"Which food and beverage establishment offers counter service, a standard menu and quick, cheap takeaways?"},"options":[{"af":"Volledige-diens-restaurant","en":"Full-service restaurant"},{"af":"Kitskos-uitlegpunt","en":"Fast-food outlet"},{"af":"Koffiewinkel","en":"Coffee shop"},{"af":"Taverne","en":"Tavern"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Toonbankdiens, 'n vaste spyskaart en wegneemetes is kenmerke van 'n kitskos-uitlegpunt. 'n Volledige-diens-restaurant het tafeldiens deur kelners.","en":"Counter service, a fixed menu and takeaways are features of a fast-food outlet. A full-service restaurant has table service by waiters."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n ___ aantreklikheid is die hoofrede waarom 'n toeris 'n gebied besoek.","en":"A ___ attraction is the main reason why a tourist visits an area."},"answers":{"af":["primêre","primêr","primere"],"en":["primary"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sekondêre","natuurlike","mensgemaakte"],"en":["secondary","natural","man-made"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die primêre aantreklikheid is die hoofrede vir die reis. 'n Sekondêre aantreklikheid besoek jy omdat jy in elk geval daar is.","en":"The primary attraction is the main reason for the trip. A secondary attraction is visited because you are there anyway."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Hartbeespoortdam is 'n natuurlike aantreklikheid omdat dit uit water bestaan.","en":"Hartbeespoort Dam is a natural attraction because it consists of water."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Dam is deur mense gebou (die damwal), dus is Hartbeespoortdam 'n mensgemaakte aantreklikheid – al is die water natuurlik.","en":"False. A dam is built by people (the dam wall), so Hartbeespoort Dam is a man-made attraction – even though the water is natural."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter organisasie bemark Suid-Afrika plaaslik en in die buiteland as 'n toeristebestemming?","en":"Which organisation markets South Africa locally and abroad as a tourist destination?"},"options":[{"af":"SANParke","en":"SANParks"},{"af":"SAHRA","en":"SAHRA"},{"af":"ACSA","en":"ACSA"},{"af":"SA Toerisme","en":"SA Tourism"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"SA Toerisme is die openbare entiteit wat Suid-Afrika bemark. SANParke bestuur parke, SAHRA beskerm erfenis en ACSA bedryf lughawens.","en":"SA Tourism is the public entity that markets South Africa. SANParks manages parks, SAHRA protects heritage and ACSA operates airports."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vereniging vir reisagente in Suider-Afrika is ___.","en":"The association for travel agents in Southern Africa is ___."},"answers":{"af":["ASATA"],"en":["ASATA"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["SATSA","SAACI","SAVRALA"],"en":["SATSA","SAACI","SAVRALA"]}},"explain":{"af":"ASATA = Association of Southern African Travel Agents. SATSA verteenwoordig toerismediensverskaffers, SAACI die konferensiebedryf en SAVRALA motorhuur.","en":"ASATA = Association of Southern African Travel Agents. SATSA represents tourism service providers, SAACI the conference industry and SAVRALA car rental."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van 'n mensgemaakte aantreklikheid?","en":"Which one is an example of a man-made attraction?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Magaliesberg","en":"The Magaliesberg"},{"af":"Die Blyderivierkloof","en":"The Blyde River Canyon"},{"af":"Sun City","en":"Sun City"},{"af":"Tafelberg","en":"Table Mountain"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sun City is deur mense gebou. Die Magaliesberg, die Blyderivierkloof en Tafelberg is deur die natuur gevorm.","en":"Sun City was built by people. The Magaliesberg, the Blyde River Canyon and Table Mountain were formed by nature."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin ry na Mpumalanga om die Krugerwildtuin te besoek en stop op pad by God's Window. Vir hierdie gesin is God's Window 'n …","en":"A family drives to Mpumalanga to visit the Kruger National Park and stops at God's Window on the way. For this family God's Window is a …"},"options":[{"af":"sekondêre natuurlike aantreklikheid.","en":"secondary natural attraction."},{"af":"primêre natuurlike aantreklikheid.","en":"primary natural attraction."},{"af":"sekondêre mensgemaakte aantreklikheid.","en":"secondary man-made attraction."},{"af":"primêre kulturele aantreklikheid.","en":"primary cultural attraction."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Kruger is die hoofrede (primêr). God's Window besoek hulle net omdat dit op pad is (sekondêr), en dit is deur die natuur geskep (natuurlik).","en":"Kruger is the main reason (primary). They visit God's Window only because it is on the way (secondary), and it was created by nature (natural)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n ___ stel 'n reispakket saam wat vervoer, akkommodasie en aktiwiteite teen een prys insluit.","en":"A ___ assembles a travel package that includes transport, accommodation and activities at one price."},"answers":{"af":["toeroperateur","toer-operateur","toeroperateurs"],"en":["tour operator","touroperator","tour-operator"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["reisagent","munisipaliteit","toergids"],"en":["travel agent","municipality","tour guide"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die toeroperateur stel die pakket saam; die reisagent verkoop dit aan die publiek.","en":"The tour operator assembles the package; the travel agent sells it to the public."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter regeringsdepartement reik paspoorte en visums aan reisigers uit?","en":"Which government department issues passports and visas to travellers?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Departement van Toerisme","en":"The Department of Tourism"},{"af":"SA Toerisme","en":"SA Tourism"},{"af":"Die Departement van Binnelandse Sake","en":"The Department of Home Affairs"},{"af":"SANParke","en":"SANParks"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Binnelandse Sake is verantwoordelik vir paspoorte en visums. Die Departement van Toerisme maak toerismebeleid, en SA Toerisme bemark die land.","en":"Home Affairs is responsible for passports and visas. The Department of Tourism makes tourism policy, and SA Tourism markets the country."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Reisagent verkoop reisprodukte aan die publiek en verdien gewoonlik kommissie daarop.","en":"A travel agent sells travel products to the public and usually earns commission on them."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die reisagent is die verkoper tussen die verskaffer of toeroperateur en die kliënt, en verdien 'n persentasie (kommissie) op elke verkoping.","en":"True. The travel agent is the seller between the supplier or tour operator and the client, and earns a percentage (commission) on every sale."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vereniging by sy funksie.","en":"Match each association to its function."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"TGCSA","en":"TGCSA"},"r":{"af":"Ken 1–5 sterre aan akkommodasie toe","en":"Awards 1–5 stars to accommodation"}},{"l":{"af":"FEDHASA","en":"FEDHASA"},"r":{"af":"Verteenwoordig die gasvryheidsbedryf (hotelle, restaurante)","en":"Represents the hospitality industry (hotels, restaurants)"}},{"l":{"af":"SAVRALA","en":"SAVRALA"},"r":{"af":"Verteenwoordig motorhuurmaatskappye","en":"Represents car rental companies"}},{"l":{"af":"SAACI","en":"SAACI"},"r":{"af":"Verteenwoordig die konferensiebedryf","en":"Represents the conference industry"}},{"l":{"af":"FTTSA","en":"FTTSA"},"r":{"af":"Sertifiseer billike, verantwoordelike toerismebesighede","en":"Certifies fair, responsible tourism businesses"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die akronieme saam met 'n sleutelwoord: TGCSA = sterre, FEDHASA = gasvryheid, SAVRALA = motorhuur, SAACI = konferensies, FTTSA = billike handel.","en":"Learn the acronyms with a key word: TGCSA = stars, FEDHASA = hospitality, SAVRALA = car rental, SAACI = conferences, FTTSA = fair trade."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Groep toeriste wil in Soweto plaaslike kos eet, na musiek luister en met inwoners kuier. Watter onderneming pas die beste?","en":"A group of tourists wants to eat local food, listen to music and socialise with residents in Soweto. Which establishment fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Kitskos-uitlegpunt by die lughawe","en":"A fast-food outlet at the airport"},{"af":"'n Taverne/shebeen op 'n township-toer","en":"A tavern/shebeen on a township tour"},{"af":"'n Nageregwinkel in 'n winkelsentrum","en":"A dessert store in a shopping centre"},{"af":"'n Koffiewinkel in die middestad","en":"A coffee shop in the city centre"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Taverne of shebeen in die township bied plaaslike kos, drankies en musiek en 'n egte kultuurervaring. Die ander opsies bied nie kontak met die plaaslike gemeenskap nie.","en":"A tavern or shebeen in the township offers local food, drinks and music and an authentic cultural experience. The other options don't offer contact with the local community."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Munisipaliteite verskaf ___ soos paaie, padtekens, water en vullisverwydering, wat toerisme moontlik maak.","en":"Municipalities provide ___ such as roads, road signs, water and refuse removal, which make tourism possible."},"answers":{"af":["infrastruktuur"],"en":["infrastructure"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bemarking","sterregradering","reispakkette"],"en":["marketing","star grading","travel packages"]}},"explain":{"af":"Infrastruktuur is die basiese dienste en strukture wat toeriste en besighede nodig het. Plaaslike regering is daarvoor verantwoordelik.","en":"Infrastructure is the basic services and structures that tourists and businesses need. Local government is responsible for it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling vergelyk die openbare en die privaat sektor korrek?","en":"Which statement compares the public and the private sector correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Die privaat sektor maak toerismewette; die openbare sektor bedryf hotelle vir wins.","en":"The private sector makes tourism laws; the public sector runs hotels for profit."},{"af":"Albei sektore werk net vir wins en het niks met mekaar te doen nie.","en":"Both sectors work only for profit and have nothing to do with each other."},{"af":"Die openbare sektor bestaan net uit reisagente en toeroperateurs.","en":"The public sector consists only of travel agents and tour operators."},{"af":"Die openbare sektor maak beleid en verskaf infrastruktuur; die privaat sektor lewer toerismeprodukte vir wins.","en":"The public sector makes policy and provides infrastructure; the private sector provides tourism products for profit."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die regering (openbaar) skep die raamwerk – wette, beleid, paaie en bemarking. Besighede (privaat) lewer die produkte – verblyf, vervoer, toere – vir wins. Hulle is van mekaar afhanklik.","en":"Government (public) creates the framework – laws, policy, roads and marketing. Businesses (private) provide the products – accommodation, transport, tours – for profit. They depend on each other."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Toeroperateur se pakket kos R4 500 per persoon. 'n Reisagent verkoop dit aan 4 mense en verdien 10% kommissie. Die kommissie is R___.","en":"A tour operator's package costs R4 500 per person. A travel agent sells it to 4 people and earns 10% commission. The commission is R___."},"answers":{"af":["1800","1 800","R1800","R1 800"],"en":["1800","1 800","R1800","R1 800"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["450","18 000","4 500"],"en":["450","18 000","4 500"]}},"explain":{"af":"Totale verkope = R4 500 × 4 = R18 000. Kommissie = 10% × R18 000 = R1 800. R450 is die kommissie op net een persoon.","en":"Total sales = R4 500 × 4 = R18 000. Commission = 10% × R18 000 = R1 800. R450 is the commission on only one person."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Nuwe gastehuis in Hartbeespoort wil (1) 'n stergradering kry en (2) bewys dat hy sy werkers billik behandel en die gemeenskap bevoordeel. By watter twee liggame moet hy aansoek doen?","en":"A new guest house in Hartbeespoort wants (1) to get a star grading and (2) to prove that it treats its workers fairly and benefits the community. To which two bodies should it apply?"},"options":[{"af":"TGCSA en FTTSA","en":"TGCSA and FTTSA"},{"af":"SAACI en SAVRALA","en":"SAACI and SAVRALA"},{"af":"ASATA en SAYTC","en":"ASATA and SAYTC"},{"af":"SAHRA en WWF","en":"SAHRA and WWF"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die TGCSA ken sterre toe; FTTSA sertifiseer billike en verantwoordelike praktyke. Die ander liggame dien konferensies, motorhuur, reisagente, jeugreis, erfenis en bewaring.","en":"The TGCSA awards stars; FTTSA certifies fair and responsible practices. The other bodies serve conferences, car rental, travel agents, youth travel, heritage and conservation."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Kaartwerk, binnelandse toerisme en buitelandse valuta","en":"Map work, domestic tourism and foreign exchange"},"topics":[{"id":"toer10-t2-kaartterminologie-tydsones","title":{"af":"Kaartterminologie, kaarttipes en tydsones","en":"Map terminology, types of maps and time zones"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n kaart se legende, skaal, rigting en ruitverwysings kan gebruik, kaarttipes kan onderskei en plaaslike tye en aankomstye oor tydsones kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to use a map's legend, scale, direction and grid references, tell types of maps apart and calculate local times and arrival times across time zones."},"summary":{"af":"## Kaartterminologie en simbole\n\nKaarte is 'n toerisme-werker se belangrikste gereedskap: jy gebruik dit om roetes te beplan, aantreklikhede te vind en toeriste aanwysings te gee.\n\n- **Legende (sleutel):** die blokkie op die kaart wat verduidelik wat elke **simbool**, kleur en lyn beteken, bv. 'n vliegtuigie vir 'n lughawe, 'n tentjie vir 'n kampterrein of 'n dik rooi lyn vir 'n nasionale pad.\n- **Simbole:** klein tekeninge, letters of kleure wat werklike dinge voorstel. Toerismekaarte gebruik dikwels internasionale simbole sodat buitelanders dit ook verstaan.\n- **Ruitverwysing:** die letters en nommers langs die rande van die kaart verdeel dit in blokke. \"D4\" is die blok waar kolom D en ry 4 kruis. So kry jy vinnig 'n straat of hotel in die register.\n- **Rigting:** gebruik die kompasroos. Die **8 rigtings** is N, NO, O, SO, S, SW, W en NW. Die **16 rigtings** voeg tussenrigtings by: NNO, ONO, OSO, SSO, SSW, WSW, WNW en NNW.\n\n> **Wenk:** By die tussenrigtings kom die naaste hoofrigting eerste: NNO lê tussen N en NO, maar ONO lê tussen O en NO. Lees die vraag mooi: \"die rigting van B *vanaf* A\" beteken jy staan by A en kyk na B.\n\n## Skaal\n\n**Skaal** is die verhouding tussen 'n afstand op die kaart en die werklike afstand op die grond.\n\n| Tipe skaal | Voorbeeld | Hoe gebruik jy dit? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Woordskaal | \"1 cm stel 5 km voor\" | Vermenigvuldig die cm met 5 km |\n| Verhoudingskaal (getalskaal) | 1 : 500 000 | 1 cm op die kaart = 500 000 cm = 5 km |\n| Lynskaal (staafskaal) | 'n gegradeerde lyn: 0 – 10 – 20 km | Meet met 'n liniaal of strokie papier en lees op die lyn af |\n\n`werklike afstand = kaartafstand × skaal`\n\nSkakel dan om: **1 km = 100 000 cm**, dus deel cm deur 100 000 om km te kry.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders vergeet om cm na km om te skakel en skryf 1 850 000 km in plaas van 18,5 km. Vra jouself altyd: is die antwoord realisties?\n\n'n **Grootskaalse** kaart (bv. 1 : 50 000) wys 'n klein gebied met baie detail (strate, geboue). 'n **Kleinskaalse** kaart (bv. 1 : 10 000 000) wys 'n groot gebied, soos die hele land, met min detail.\n\n## Breedte- en lengtegrade\n\n- Die **ewenaar** (0°) verdeel die aarde in die **Noordelike** en **Suidelike Halfrond**. Die **pole** lê op 90° N en 90° S.\n- **Breedtegrade** (parallelle) loop oos–wes, parallel aan die ewenaar. Hulle meet hoe ver noord of suid 'n plek lê (0°–90°).\n- **Lengtegrade** (meridiane) loop van pool tot pool. Hulle meet hoe ver oos of wes 'n plek van die **nulmeridiaan** (Greenwich-meridiaan, 0°, deur Londen) lê (0°–180°). Die nulmeridiaan verdeel die aarde in die **Oostelike** en **Westelike Halfrond**.\n- 'n Ligging word gegee as breedtegraad eers, dan lengtegraad: 26° S, 28° O lê naby Johannesburg. Suid-Afrika lê in die Suidelike én Oostelike Halfrond.\n\n## Tipes kaarte in toerisme\n\n| Kaarttipe | Wat dit wys | Toerisme-gebruik |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pad- en straatkaart | paaie, roetenommers, afstande, strate | selfbestuur-roetes, 'n hotel opspoor |\n| Politieke kaart | grense, lande, provinsies, hoofstede | waar lê 'n land of provinsie? |\n| Fisiese kaart | berge, riviere, hoogte bo seespieël (kleure) | stap- en avontuurbestemmings |\n| Spesialis- (tematiese) kaart | een tema, bv. wynroetes, klimaat, staproetes | spesiale-belangstelling-toeriste |\n| Toerisme-inligtingskaart | aantreklikhede, akkommodasie, restaurante, inligtingskantore | toeriste wat 'n dorp verken |\n\n**Elektroniese kaarte** (GPS, Google Maps, Google Earth):\n- **Voordele:** intydse roetes en verkeersinligting, gesproke aanwysings, wys nabygeleë vulstasies en restaurante, word gereeld bygewerk, satelliet- en straataansigte.\n- **Nadele:** benodig sein, data en battery (beurtkrag!), datakoste, kan jou met slegte of onveilige paaie stuur, lei die bestuurder af. Hou altyd 'n papierkaart of 'n afgelaaide (aflyn) kaart as rugsteun.\n\n## Tydsones\n\n- Die aarde draai **360° in 24 uur**, dus **15° per uur** (1° = 4 minute). Daarom is die wêreld in tydsones verdeel.\n- **UTC** (Gekoördineerde Universele Tyd, vroeër GMT) is die standaardtyd by Greenwich (0°).\n- **SAST** (Suid-Afrikaanse Standaardtyd) = **UTC+2**, gebaseer op die 30° O-lengtegraad. Suid-Afrika het **geen somertyd** nie, dus bly ons die hele jaar UTC+2.\n- Plekke **oos** van jou is **voor** (die son kom eerste daar op); plekke **wes** is **agter**.\n- Baie lande in die noorde gebruik **somertyd**: Londen is UTC+0 in die winter maar UTC+1 in die somer. Gebruik altyd die tydsone wat die vraag gee.\n- **Internasionale Datumlyn** (ongeveer 180°): steek jy dit **weswaarts** oor (bv. van die VSA na Japan), **tel jy 'n dag by**; **ooswaarts** (bv. van Nieu-Seeland na Hawaii) **trek jy 'n dag af**.\n- Toerisme gebruik die **24-uurhorlosie**: 3:30 nm = 15:30. Kom jy verby 24:00, trek 24 af en dit is die volgende dag.\n\n### Stappe vir tydsone-berekeninge\n\n1. Skryf die UTC-tydsones van albei plekke neer.\n2. Tydsverskil = tydsone van bestemming − tydsone van vertrekpunt (+ = voor, − = agter).\n3. Vir 'n vlug: aankomstyd in vertrektyd = vertrektyd + vlugtyd.\n4. Plaaslike aankomstyd = stap 3 + tydsverskil.\n5. Kontroleer of die **datum** verander het.\n\n> **Onthou!** Vertrek JNB 20:00 SAST, 11 uur na Londen (UTC+0): 20:00 + 11 h = 07:00 SAST die volgende dag; Londen is 2 uur agter, dus land jy om 05:00 Londense tyd.","en":"## Map terminology and symbols\n\nTourism workers use maps to plan routes, find attractions and give directions.\n\n- **Legend (key):** the box on the map that explains what each **symbol**, colour and line means, e.g. a small aeroplane for an airport, a tent for a campsite or a thick red line for a national road.\n- **Symbols:** small drawings, letters or colours that represent real things. Tourism maps often use international symbols that foreigners also understand.\n- **Grid reference:** the letters and numbers along the edges of the map divide it into blocks. \"D4\" is the block where column D and row 4 meet; use it to find a street or hotel quickly.\n- **Direction:** use the compass rose. The **8 directions** are N, NE, E, SE, S, SW, W and NW. The **16 directions** add the in-between points: NNE, ENE, ESE, SSE, SSW, WSW, WNW and NNW.\n\n> **Tip:** In the in-between directions the nearest cardinal point comes first: NNE lies between N and NE, but ENE lies between E and NE. Read the question carefully: \"the direction of B *from* A\" means you stand at A and look towards B.\n\n## Scale\n\n**Scale** is the relationship between a distance on the map and the real distance on the ground.\n\n| Type of scale | Example | How do you use it? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Word scale | \"1 cm represents 5 km\" | Multiply the cm by 5 km |\n| Ratio scale (numerical scale) | 1 : 500 000 | 1 cm on the map = 500 000 cm = 5 km |\n| Line scale (bar scale) | a graded line: 0 – 10 – 20 km | Measure with a ruler or strip of paper and read it off the line |\n\n`real distance = map distance × scale`\n\nThen convert: **1 km = 100 000 cm**, so divide cm by 100 000 to get km.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Forgetting to convert cm to km and writing 1 850 000 km instead of 18.5 km. Always ask: is the answer realistic?\n\nA **large-scale** map (e.g. 1 : 50 000) shows a small area in a lot of detail (streets, buildings). A **small-scale** map (e.g. 1 : 10 000 000) shows a big area, such as the whole country, with little detail.\n\n## Latitude and longitude\n\n- The **equator** (0°) divides the Earth into the **Northern** and **Southern Hemispheres**. The **poles** are at 90° N and 90° S.\n- **Lines of latitude** (parallels) run east–west, parallel to the equator. They measure how far north or south a place is (0°–90°).\n- **Lines of longitude** (meridians) run from pole to pole. They measure how far east or west a place is from the **prime meridian** (Greenwich meridian, 0°, through London) (0°–180°). The prime meridian divides the Earth into the **Eastern** and **Western Hemispheres**.\n- A position is given as latitude first, then longitude: 26° S, 28° E lies near Johannesburg. South Africa lies in both the Southern and the Eastern Hemisphere.\n\n## Types of maps in tourism\n\n| Type of map | What it shows | Use in tourism |\n|---|---|---|\n| Road and street map | roads, route numbers, distances, streets | self-drive routes, finding a hotel |\n| Political map | borders, countries, provinces, capitals | where is a country or province? |\n| Physical map | mountains, rivers, height above sea level (colours) | hiking and adventure destinations |\n| Specialist (thematic) map | one theme, e.g. wine routes, climate, hiking trails | special-interest tourists |\n| Tourist-information map | attractions, accommodation, restaurants, information offices | tourists exploring a town |\n\n**Electronic maps** (GPS, Google Maps, Google Earth):\n- **Advantages:** real-time routes and traffic information, spoken directions, show nearby fuel stations and restaurants, updated regularly, satellite and street views.\n- **Disadvantages:** need signal, data and battery (load-shedding!), data costs, may send you along bad or unsafe roads, distract the driver. Always keep a paper map or a downloaded (offline) map as a backup.\n\n## Time zones\n\n- The Earth turns **360° in 24 hours**, so **15° per hour** (1° = 4 minutes). That is why the world is divided into time zones.\n- **UTC** (Coordinated Universal Time, formerly GMT) is the standard time at Greenwich (0°).\n- **SAST** (South African Standard Time) = **UTC+2**, based on the 30° E line of longitude. South Africa has **no daylight saving**, so we stay on UTC+2 all year.\n- Places to the **east** of you are **ahead** (the sun rises there first); places to the **west** are **behind**.\n- Many northern countries use **daylight saving time**: London is UTC+0 in winter but UTC+1 in summer. Always use the time zone the question gives.\n- **International Date Line** (about 180°): cross it **westwards** (e.g. from the USA to Japan) and you **add a day**; **eastwards** (e.g. from New Zealand to Hawaii) and you **subtract a day**.\n- Tourism uses the **24-hour clock**: 3:30 pm = 15:30. If you go past 24:00, subtract 24 and it is the next day.\n\n### Steps for time-zone calculations\n\n1. Write down the UTC time zones of both places.\n2. Time difference = time zone of destination − time zone of departure point (+ = ahead, − = behind).\n3. For a flight: arrival time in departure time = departure time + flight time.\n4. Local arrival time = step 3 + time difference.\n5. Check whether the **date** has changed.\n\n> **Remember!** Depart JNB 20:00 SAST, 11 hours to London (UTC+0): 20:00 + 11 h = 07:00 SAST the next day; London is 2 hours behind, so you land at 05:00 London time."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Legende (sleutel)","en":"Legend (key)"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van 'n kaart wat verduidelik wat elke simbool, kleur en lyn beteken.","en":"The part of a map that explains what each symbol, colour and line means."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaal","en":"Scale"},"def":{"af":"Die verhouding tussen 'n afstand op die kaart en die werklike afstand op die grond; as woordskaal, verhoudingskaal of lynskaal gegee.","en":"The relationship between a distance on the map and the real distance on the ground; given as a word scale, ratio scale or line scale."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruitverwysing","en":"Grid reference"},"def":{"af":"'n Letter-en-nommer-kombinasie (bv. D4) wat die blok op 'n kaart aandui waar 'n plek lê.","en":"A letter-and-number combination (e.g. D4) that shows the block on a map where a place is."}},{"term":{"af":"Ewenaar","en":"Equator"},"def":{"af":"Die 0°-breedtegraad wat die aarde in die Noordelike en Suidelike Halfrond verdeel.","en":"The 0° line of latitude that divides the Earth into the Northern and Southern Hemispheres."}},{"term":{"af":"Breedtegrade","en":"Lines of latitude"},"def":{"af":"Denkbeeldige lyne parallel aan die ewenaar wat aandui hoe ver noord of suid 'n plek lê (0°–90°).","en":"Imaginary lines parallel to the equator that show how far north or south a place is (0°–90°)."}},{"term":{"af":"Lengtegrade (meridiane)","en":"Lines of longitude (meridians)"},"def":{"af":"Denkbeeldige lyne van pool tot pool wat aandui hoe ver oos of wes van Greenwich 'n plek lê (0°–180°).","en":"Imaginary lines from pole to pole that show how far east or west of Greenwich a place is (0°–180°)."}},{"term":{"af":"Nulmeridiaan (Greenwich-meridiaan)","en":"Prime meridian (Greenwich meridian)"},"def":{"af":"Die 0°-lengtegraad deur Greenwich in Londen; dit verdeel die aarde in die Oostelike en Westelike Halfrond.","en":"The 0° line of longitude through Greenwich in London; it divides the Earth into the Eastern and Western Hemispheres."}},{"term":{"af":"Tydsone","en":"Time zone"},"def":{"af":"'n Gebied wat dieselfde standaardtyd gebruik; elke 15° lengte is ongeveer 1 uur verskil.","en":"An area that uses the same standard time; every 15° of longitude is about 1 hour's difference."}},{"term":{"af":"UTC en SAST","en":"UTC and SAST"},"def":{"af":"UTC is die wêreldstandaardtyd by Greenwich; SAST (Suid-Afrikaanse Standaardtyd) is UTC+2, die hele jaar.","en":"UTC is the world standard time at Greenwich; SAST (South African Standard Time) is UTC+2, all year round."}},{"term":{"af":"Internasionale Datumlyn","en":"International Date Line"},"def":{"af":"'n Lyn naby 180° lengte waar die datum verander: weswaarts tel jy 'n dag by, ooswaarts trek jy 'n dag af.","en":"A line near 180° longitude where the date changes: westwards you add a day, eastwards you subtract a day."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Werklike afstand met die skaal","en":"Real distance using the scale"},"problem":{"af":"'n Toergids beplan 'n roete op 'n padkaart met 'n verhoudingskaal van 1 : 250 000. Die afstand tussen twee dorpe op die kaart is 7,4 cm. Bereken die werklike afstand in km.","en":"A tour guide is planning a route on a road map with a ratio scale of 1 : 250 000. The distance between two towns on the map is 7.4 cm. Calculate the real distance in km."},"steps":[{"af":"Formule: werklike afstand = kaartafstand × skaal = 7,4 cm × 250 000","en":"Formula: real distance = map distance × scale = 7.4 cm × 250 000"},{"af":"= 1 850 000 cm op die grond","en":"= 1 850 000 cm on the ground"},{"af":"Skakel om na km: 1 km = 100 000 cm, dus 1 850 000 ÷ 100 000 = 18,5 km","en":"Convert to km: 1 km = 100 000 cm, so 1 850 000 ÷ 100 000 = 18.5 km"},{"af":"Kontroleer met 'n woordskaal: 1 : 250 000 beteken 1 cm stel 2,5 km voor, en 7,4 × 2,5 = 18,5 km ✔","en":"Check with a word scale: 1 : 250 000 means 1 cm represents 2.5 km, and 7.4 × 2.5 = 18.5 km ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"Werklike afstand = 18,5 km","en":"Real distance = 18.5 km"}},{"title":{"af":"Plaaslike tyd in ander stede","en":"Local time in other cities"},"problem":{"af":"Dit is Saterdag 15:00 in Brits (SAST = UTC+2). Hoe laat is dit in (a) Dubai (UTC+4), (b) Tokio (UTC+9) en (c) New York in Januarie (UTC−5)?","en":"It is 15:00 on Saturday in Brits (SAST = UTC+2). What time is it in (a) Dubai (UTC+4), (b) Tokyo (UTC+9) and (c) New York in January (UTC−5)?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dubai: verskil = +4 − (+2) = +2 h. Dubai lê oos, dus voor: 15:00 + 2 h = 17:00","en":"(a) Dubai: difference = +4 − (+2) = +2 h. Dubai lies east, so it is ahead: 15:00 + 2 h = 17:00"},{"af":"(b) Tokio: verskil = +9 − (+2) = +7 h: 15:00 + 7 h = 22:00, steeds Saterdag","en":"(b) Tokyo: difference = +9 − (+2) = +7 h: 15:00 + 7 h = 22:00, still Saturday"},{"af":"(c) New York: verskil = −5 − (+2) = −7 h. New York lê wes, dus agter: 15:00 − 7 h = 08:00","en":"(c) New York: difference = −5 − (+2) = −7 h. New York lies west, so it is behind: 15:00 − 7 h = 08:00"}],"answer":{"af":"Dubai 17:00; Tokio 22:00; New York 08:00 (almal Saterdag)","en":"Dubai 17:00; Tokyo 22:00; New York 08:00 (all Saturday)"}},{"title":{"af":"Aankomstyd van 'n oornagvlug","en":"Arrival time of an overnight flight"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vlug vertrek om 20:00 SAST van O.R. Tambo (JNB) na Londen. Die vlug duur 11 uur. Dit is Januarie, dus is Londen op UTC+0. Bereken die plaaslike aankomstyd in Londen.","en":"A flight leaves O.R. Tambo (JNB) for London at 20:00 SAST. The flight takes 11 hours. It is January, so London is on UTC+0. Calculate the local arrival time in London."},"steps":[{"af":"Aankomstyd in SA-tyd: 20:00 + 11 h = 31:00 → 31 − 24 = 07:00 die volgende dag (SAST)","en":"Arrival time in SA time: 20:00 + 11 h = 31:00 → 31 − 24 = 07:00 the next day (SAST)"},{"af":"Tydsverskil: 0 − (+2) = −2 h; Londen is 2 uur agter Suid-Afrika","en":"Time difference: 0 − (+2) = −2 h; London is 2 hours behind South Africa"},{"af":"Plaaslike aankomstyd: 07:00 − 2 h = 05:00 die volgende oggend","en":"Local arrival time: 07:00 − 2 h = 05:00 the next morning"},{"af":"Let op: in die Britse somer (UTC+1) sou dit 06:00 wees. Gebruik altyd die tydsone wat die vraag gee.","en":"Note: in the British summer (UTC+1) it would be 06:00. Always use the time zone the question gives."}],"answer":{"af":"05:00 Londense tyd, die dag ná vertrek","en":"05:00 London time, the day after departure"}},{"title":{"af":"Weswaarts vlieg: dieselfde dag aankom","en":"Flying west: arriving on the same day"},"problem":{"af":"'n Rugbyspan vlieg Dinsdag om 10:15 SAST van Johannesburg na São Paulo, Brasilië (UTC−3). Die vlug duur 10 uur 30 minute. Op watter dag en plaaslike tyd land hulle?","en":"A rugby team flies from Johannesburg to São Paulo, Brazil (UTC−3) at 10:15 SAST on Tuesday. The flight takes 10 hours 30 minutes. On which day and at what local time do they land?"},"steps":[{"af":"Aankoms in SAST: 10:15 + 10 h 30 min = 20:45 Dinsdag","en":"Arrival in SAST: 10:15 + 10 h 30 min = 20:45 Tuesday"},{"af":"Tydsverskil: −3 − (+2) = −5 h; São Paulo lê wes en is 5 uur agter","en":"Time difference: −3 − (+2) = −5 h; São Paulo lies west and is 5 hours behind"},{"af":"Plaaslike tyd: 20:45 − 5 h = 15:45 Dinsdag","en":"Local time: 20:45 − 5 h = 15:45 Tuesday"},{"af":"Volgens die horlosie land hulle net 5 h 30 min ná vertrek, al het hulle 10 h 30 min gevlieg – want hulle vlieg wes, saam met die son.","en":"By the clock they land only 5 h 30 min after departure, even though they flew for 10 h 30 min – because they fly west, with the sun."}],"answer":{"af":"Dinsdag 15:45 plaaslike tyd in São Paulo","en":"Tuesday 15:45 local time in São Paulo"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lyn is die 0°-breedtegraad?","en":"Which line is the 0° line of latitude?"},"options":[{"af":"Die nulmeridiaan (Greenwich)","en":"The prime meridian (Greenwich)"},{"af":"Die ewenaar","en":"The equator"},{"af":"Die Internasionale Datumlyn","en":"The International Date Line"},{"af":"Die Suidpool","en":"The South Pole"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ewenaar is 0° breedte en verdeel die aarde in die Noordelike en Suidelike Halfrond. Die nulmeridiaan is 0° LENGTE – moenie die twee verwar nie.","en":"The equator is 0° latitude and divides the Earth into the Northern and Southern Hemispheres. The prime meridian is 0° LONGITUDE – don't mix the two up."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deel van 'n kaart verduidelik wat die simbole en kleure beteken?","en":"Which part of a map explains what the symbols and colours mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die skaal","en":"The scale"},{"af":"Die ruitverwysing","en":"The grid reference"},{"af":"Die legende (sleutel)","en":"The legend (key)"},{"af":"Die kompasroos","en":"The compass rose"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die legende of sleutel is die 'woordeboek' van die kaart. Die skaal gee afstand, die ruitverwysing ligging en die kompasroos rigting.","en":"The legend or key is the map's 'dictionary'. The scale gives distance, the grid reference location and the compass rose direction."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suid-Afrika gebruik somertyd: in die somer skuif ons die horlosies een uur vorentoe.","en":"South Africa uses daylight saving: in summer we move the clocks one hour forward."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Suid-Afrika het geen somertyd nie – SAST bly die hele jaar UTC+2. Lande soos die Verenigde Koninkryk gebruik wel somertyd.","en":"False. South Africa has no daylight saving – SAST stays UTC+2 all year. Countries such as the United Kingdom do use daylight saving."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die aarde draai 360° in 24 uur, dus draai dit ___° per uur.","en":"The Earth turns 360° in 24 hours, so it turns ___° per hour."},"answers":{"af":["15","15°","15 grade"],"en":["15","15°","15 degrees"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["24","30","10"],"en":["24","30","10"]}},"explain":{"af":"360° ÷ 24 h = 15° per uur. Daarom is elke tydsone ongeveer 15° lengte breed.","en":"360° ÷ 24 h = 15° per hour. That is why each time zone is about 15° of longitude wide."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Avontuurtoeris wil sien waar die berge, riviere en hoë gebiede in die Drakensberg is. Watter tipe kaart moet hy gebruik?","en":"An adventure tourist wants to see where the mountains, rivers and high areas in the Drakensberg are. Which type of map should he use?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Fisiese kaart","en":"A physical map"},{"af":"'n Politieke kaart","en":"A political map"},{"af":"'n Straatkaart","en":"A street map"},{"af":"'n Toerisme-inligtingskaart van 'n dorp","en":"A tourist-information map of a town"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Fisiese kaart wys die landskap: berge, riviere en hoogte bo seespieël met kleure. 'n Politieke kaart wys grense en hoofstede.","en":"A physical map shows the landscape: mountains, rivers and height above sea level using colours. A political map shows borders and capitals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op 'n kaart met 'n skaal van 1 : 500 000 stel 1 cm ___ km op die grond voor.","en":"On a map with a scale of 1 : 500 000, 1 cm represents ___ km on the ground."},"answers":{"af":["5","5 km"],"en":["5","5 km"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["50","500","0,5"],"en":["50","500","0.5"]}},"explain":{"af":"1 cm = 500 000 cm op die grond. 500 000 ÷ 100 000 = 5 km (1 km = 100 000 cm).","en":"1 cm = 500 000 cm on the ground. 500 000 ÷ 100 000 = 5 km (1 km = 100 000 cm)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter rigting lê presies tussen noord (N) en noordoos (NO)?","en":"Which direction lies exactly between north (N) and north-east (NE)?"},"options":[{"af":"ONO","en":"ENE"},{"af":"NO","en":"NE"},{"af":"NNW","en":"NNW"},{"af":"NNO","en":"NNE"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"NNO (noordnoordoos) lê tussen N en NO – die naaste hoofrigting (N) kom eerste. ONO lê tussen O en NO.","en":"NNE (north-north-east) lies between N and NE – the nearest cardinal point (N) comes first. ENE lies between E and NE."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lyn of term by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each line or term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ewenaar","en":"Equator"},"r":{"af":"0° breedte","en":"0° latitude"}},{"l":{"af":"Nulmeridiaan","en":"Prime meridian"},"r":{"af":"0° lengte, deur Greenwich","en":"0° longitude, through Greenwich"}},{"l":{"af":"Internasionale Datumlyn","en":"International Date Line"},"r":{"af":"Ongeveer 180° lengte","en":"About 180° longitude"}},{"l":{"af":"SAST","en":"SAST"},"r":{"af":"UTC+2, die hele jaar","en":"UTC+2, all year round"}},{"l":{"af":"Die pole","en":"The poles"},"r":{"af":"90° N en 90° S","en":"90° N and 90° S"}}],"explain":{"af":"Breedte word van die ewenaar af gemeet (tot 90° by die pole); lengte van die nulmeridiaan af (tot 180°, waar die Datumlyn naastenby loop). SAST is UTC+2.","en":"Latitude is measured from the equator (up to 90° at the poles); longitude from the prime meridian (up to 180°, roughly where the Date Line runs). SAST is UTC+2."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dit is 14:00 in Brits (UTC+2). Hoe laat is dit in Dubai (UTC+4)?","en":"It is 14:00 in Brits (UTC+2). What time is it in Dubai (UTC+4)?"},"options":[{"af":"12:00","en":"12:00"},{"af":"16:00","en":"16:00"},{"af":"18:00","en":"18:00"},{"af":"14:00","en":"14:00"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Verskil = +4 − (+2) = +2 h. Dubai lê oos, dus voor: 14:00 + 2 h = 16:00. 18:00 is die fout om al 4 uur by te tel.","en":"Difference = +4 − (+2) = +2 h. Dubai lies east, so it is ahead: 14:00 + 2 h = 16:00. 18:00 is the mistake of adding all 4 hours."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Dit is 09:00 in Pretoria (UTC+2). In Londen is dit winter (UTC+0). Hoe laat is dit in Londen? ___","en":"It is 09:00 in Pretoria (UTC+2). It is winter in London (UTC+0). What time is it in London? ___"},"answers":{"af":["07:00","7:00","07h00","7h00","0700","07.00"],"en":["07:00","7:00","07h00","7h00","0700","07.00"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11:00","09:00","08:00"],"en":["11:00","09:00","08:00"]}},"explain":{"af":"Verskil = 0 − (+2) = −2 h. Londen lê wes en is agter: 09:00 − 2 h = 07:00.","en":"Difference = 0 − (+2) = −2 h. London lies west and is behind: 09:00 − 2 h = 07:00."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As jy die Internasionale Datumlyn ooswaarts oorsteek (bv. van Nieu-Seeland na Hawaii), trek jy een dag van die datum af.","en":"If you cross the International Date Line eastwards (e.g. from New Zealand to Hawaii), you subtract one day from the date."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Ooswaarts oor die Datumlyn: trek 'n dag af (Dinsdag word Maandag). Weswaarts: tel 'n dag by.","en":"True. Eastwards across the Date Line: subtract a day (Tuesday becomes Monday). Westwards: add a day."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gebruik die reël 15° = 1 uur. Hoeveel verskil die tyd van 'n plek op 45° W van SAST (gebaseer op 30° O)?","en":"Use the rule 15° = 1 hour. How much does the time at a place on 45° W differ from SAST (based on 30° E)?"},"options":[{"af":"3 uur agter SAST","en":"3 hours behind SAST"},{"af":"3 uur voor SAST","en":"3 hours ahead of SAST"},{"af":"5 uur agter SAST","en":"5 hours behind SAST"},{"af":"5 uur voor SAST","en":"5 hours ahead of SAST"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die plekke lê aan weerskante van Greenwich, dus TEL die grade bymekaar: 45° + 30° = 75°; 75 ÷ 15 = 5 uur. Die plek lê wes, dus agter. '3 uur' is net die verskil met Greenwich.","en":"The places are on opposite sides of Greenwich, so ADD the degrees: 45° + 30° = 75°; 75 ÷ 15 = 5 hours. The place lies west, so it is behind. '3 hours' is only the difference from Greenwich."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Op 'n padkaart met skaal 1 : 250 000 is die afstand tussen twee dorpe 6 cm. Die werklike afstand is ___ km.","en":"On a road map with scale 1 : 250 000 the distance between two towns is 6 cm. The real distance is ___ km."},"answers":{"af":["15","15 km"],"en":["15","15 km"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["150","1 500 000","25"],"en":["150","1 500 000","25"]}},"explain":{"af":"6 × 250 000 = 1 500 000 cm; 1 500 000 ÷ 100 000 = 15 km.","en":"6 × 250 000 = 1 500 000 cm; 1 500 000 ÷ 100 000 = 15 km."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Vlug vertrek om 10:00 SAST uit Johannesburg na Dubai (UTC+4). Die vlug duur 8 uur. Die plaaslike aankomstyd in Dubai is ___.","en":"A flight leaves Johannesburg for Dubai (UTC+4) at 10:00 SAST. The flight takes 8 hours. The local arrival time in Dubai is ___."},"answers":{"af":["20:00","20h00","2000","20.00","8 nm","8nm"],"en":["20:00","20h00","2000","20.00","8 pm","8pm"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["18:00","16:00","22:00"],"en":["18:00","16:00","22:00"]}},"explain":{"af":"10:00 + 8 h = 18:00 SAST. Dubai is 2 uur voor (+4 − 2), dus 18:00 + 2 h = 20:00. 18:00 is die fout om nie om te skakel nie.","en":"10:00 + 8 h = 18:00 SAST. Dubai is 2 hours ahead (+4 − 2), so 18:00 + 2 h = 20:00. 18:00 is the mistake of not converting."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toergroep vertrek Maandag om 11:00 SAST uit Johannesburg na New York (UTC−5). Die vlug duur 16 uur. Wanneer land hulle volgens New York se plaaslike tyd?","en":"A tour group leaves Johannesburg for New York (UTC−5) at 11:00 SAST on Monday. The flight takes 16 hours. When do they land in New York local time?"},"options":[{"af":"Maandag 20:00","en":"Monday 20:00"},{"af":"Dinsdag 03:00","en":"Tuesday 03:00"},{"af":"Dinsdag 10:00","en":"Tuesday 10:00"},{"af":"Maandag 22:00","en":"Monday 22:00"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"11:00 + 16 h = 03:00 Dinsdag (SAST). Verskil = −5 − (+2) = −7 h, dus 03:00 − 7 h = 20:00 Maandag. 'Dinsdag 03:00' is nie omgeskakel nie; 'Maandag 22:00' gebruik −5 in plaas van −7.","en":"11:00 + 16 h = 03:00 Tuesday (SAST). Difference = −5 − (+2) = −7 h, so 03:00 − 7 h = 20:00 Monday. 'Tuesday 03:00' was not converted; 'Monday 22:00' used −5 instead of −7."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin wil met Google Maps deur 'n afgeleë deel van die Karoo ry waar daar min of geen selfoonsein is. Watter raad is die beste?","en":"A family wants to use Google Maps to drive through a remote part of the Karoo with little or no cellphone signal. Which advice is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Vertrou net op die toep; dit laai nuwe kaarte selfs sonder sein of data.","en":"Rely only on the app; it loads new maps even without signal or data."},{"af":"Neem slegs 'n wêreldkaart saam, want dit wys al die lande.","en":"Take only a world map, because it shows all the countries."},{"af":"Ry eerder in die nag, want dan is die sein beter.","en":"Rather drive at night, because the signal is better then."},{"af":"Laai die kaart vooraf af vir aflyngebruik, hou 'n kragbank by en neem 'n papierpadkaart as rugsteun.","en":"Download the map beforehand for offline use, keep a power bank and take a paper road map as a backup."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Elektroniese kaarte het sein, data en battery nodig. 'n Afgelaaide kaart, 'n kragbank en 'n papierkaart oorkom al drie nadele. 'n Wêreldkaart is te kleinskaals, en nagry is onveilig.","en":"Electronic maps need signal, data and battery. A downloaded map, a power bank and a paper map overcome all three disadvantages. A world map is too small-scale, and driving at night is unsafe."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t2-kaarte-sa-wereld","title":{"af":"Die kaart van Suid-Afrika en die wêreldkaart","en":"The map of South Africa and the world map"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal provinsies, hoofstede, nasionale paaie, grensposte, hawens, berge en riviere van SA kan aandui, en kontinente, oseane, eilande en SAOG-lande op die wêreldkaart kan benoem.","en":"You will be able to locate SA's provinces, capitals, national roads, border posts, harbours, mountains and rivers, and name the continents, oceans, islands and SADC countries on the world map."},"summary":{"af":"## Die kaart van Suid-Afrika\n\nIn die eksamen kry jy 'n kaart van Suid-Afrika of die wêreld en moet jy plekke uitwys of benoem. Leer die liggings hier in woorde, en oefen dan op 'n atlas.\n\n### Grense en buurlande\n\n- Suid-Afrika lê aan die suidpunt van Afrika. Die **Atlantiese Oseaan** is aan die **weskus** en die **Indiese Oseaan** aan die **oos- en suidkus**. Hulle ontmoet amptelik by **Kaap Agulhas**, die mees suidelike punt van Afrika.\n- **Ses buurlande:** Namibië (noordwes), Botswana (noord), Zimbabwe (noord, oorkant die Limpoporivier), Mosambiek (noordoos), Eswatini (oos) en Lesotho, wat **heeltemal deur Suid-Afrika omring** word.\n\n### Die nege provinsies en hoofstede\n\n| Provinsie | Hoofstad | Onthou |\n|---|---|---|\n| Oos-Kaap | Bhisho | hawens Gqeberha, Ngqura en Oos-Londen |\n| Vrystaat | Bloemfontein | geregtelike hoofstad van SA |\n| Gauteng | Johannesburg | kleinste provinsie; Pretoria en O.R. Tambo lê hier |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | Pietermaritzburg | Durban-hawe en King Shaka-lughawe |\n| Limpopo | Polokwane | N1 na Beitbridge en Zimbabwe |\n| Mpumalanga | Mbombela | Kruger Nasionale Park; N4 na Mosambiek |\n| Noordwes | Mahikeng | Brits, Hartbeespoortdam, Sun City |\n| Noord-Kaap | Kimberley | grootste provinsie; N7 na Namibië |\n| Wes-Kaap | Kaapstad | wetgewende hoofstad (Parlement) |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Johannesburg is Gauteng se hoofstad, nie Suid-Afrika s'n nie. SA het drie hoofstede: **Pretoria** (uitvoerend/administratief), **Kaapstad** (wetgewend) en **Bloemfontein** (geregtelik).\n\n### Lughawens en hawens\n\n- **Internasionale lughawens:** O.R. Tambo (JNB, Gauteng – die besigste in SA), Kaapstad Internasionaal (CPT) en King Shaka Internasionaal (DUR, noord van Durban). Ander met internasionale status: Lanseria (HLA), Kruger Mpumalanga (MQP) en Pilanesberg Internasionaal naby Sun City.\n- **Hawens:** KwaZulu-Natal – **Durban** (besigste hawe; passasiersskepe) en **Richardsbaai**; Wes-Kaap – **Kaapstad** (passasiersskepe), **Saldanhabaai** en **Mosselbaai**; Oos-Kaap – **Gqeberha**, **Ngqura** en **Oos-Londen**.\n\n### Nasionale paaie\n\n| Pad | Roete |\n|---|---|\n| N1 | Kaapstad – Bloemfontein – Johannesburg – Pretoria – Polokwane – Beitbridge (Zimbabwe) |\n| N2 | Kaapstad – George (Tuinroete) – Gqeberha – Oos-Londen – Durban |\n| N3 | Johannesburg – Harrismith – Pietermaritzburg – Durban |\n| N4 | Botswana-grens (Skilpadshek) – Rustenburg – verby Brits – Pretoria – eMalahleni – Mbombela – Komatipoort (Mosambiek) |\n| N7 | Kaapstad – Springbok – Vioolsdrif (Namibië) |\n\n### Poorte en grensposte\n\n| Grenspos | Buurland | Waar? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Beitbridge | Zimbabwe | N1, Limpopo |\n| Lebombo | Mosambiek | N4 by Komatipoort, Mpumalanga |\n| Oshoek | Eswatini | Mpumalanga, naby Mbabane |\n| Maseru-brug | Lesotho | Vrystaat, naby Ladybrand |\n| Vioolsdrif | Namibië | N7 oor die Oranjerivier, Noord-Kaap |\n| Skilpadshek | Botswana | N4, Noordwes |\n| Kopfontein | Botswana | Noordwes, naaste aan Gaborone |\n| Ramatlabama | Botswana | Noordwes, naby Mahikeng |\n\n### Berge, riviere en damme\n\n- **Drakensberg:** SA se hoogste bergreeks, langs die grens tussen KwaZulu-Natal en Lesotho.\n- **Magaliesberg:** van Pretoria weswaarts verby Hartbeespoort en Brits tot by Rustenburg.\n- **Cederberg** (rotsformasies en rotskuns) en **Swartberg** (Swartbergpas, naby Oudtshoorn): albei in die Wes-Kaap.\n- **Oranjerivier (Gariep):** SA se langste rivier; vloei wes in die Atlantiese Oseaan en vorm deel van die grens met Namibië.\n- **Vaalrivier:** die Oranje se grootste sytak; vorm deel van die Vrystaat se noordgrens.\n- **Limpoporivier:** die noordgrens met Botswana en Zimbabwe; vloei deur Mosambiek in die Indiese Oseaan.\n- **Thukelarivier:** KwaZulu-Natal se grootste rivier; ontspring in die Drakensberg.\n- **Krokodilrivier:** vloei in die **Hartbeespoortdam** naby Brits en later in die Limpopo.\n- **Damme:** **Gariepdam** (Oranjerivier, grootste dam in SA), **Vaaldam** (water vir Gauteng; watersport) en **Hartbeespoortdam** (Noordwes; gewilde naweekbestemming).\n\n## Die wêreldkaart\n\n- **Sewe kontinente:** Afrika, Antarktika, Asië (grootste), Australië/Oseanië (kleinste), Europa, Noord-Amerika en Suid-Amerika.\n- **Oseane:** die **Stille Oseaan** (grootste), **Atlantiese** en **Indiese Oseaan**; ken ook die **Arktiese Oseaan** (Noordelike Yssee) en die **Suidelike Oseaan** om Antarktika.\n- **Eilandgroepe:** Mauritius, die Seychelle en Madagaskar (Afrika se grootste eiland) lê in die **Indiese Oseaan**; die Kanariese Eilande (Spanje) in die **Atlantiese Oseaan** noordwes van Afrika; die Karibiese Eilande (bv. Jamaika) tussen Noord- en Suid-Amerika; Hawaii (VSA) in die **Stille Oseaan**.\n- Die **UNWTO** (sedert 2024 ook **UN Tourism**) deel die wêreld in vyf toerismestreke: **Afrika, die Amerikas, Asië en die Stille Oseaan, Europa en die Midde-Ooste**.\n\n### Die SAOG (SADC)\n\nDie Suider-Afrikaanse Ontwikkelingsgemeenskap het **16 lidlande**; die hoofkantoor is in **Gaborone**.\n\n| Land | Hoofstad | Land | Hoofstad |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Angola | Luanda | Mauritius | Port Louis |\n| Botswana | Gaborone | Mosambiek | Maputo |\n| Komore | Moroni | Namibië | Windhoek |\n| DR Kongo | Kinshasa | Seychelle | Victoria |\n| Eswatini | Mbabane | Suid-Afrika | Pretoria |\n| Lesotho | Maseru | Tanzanië | Dodoma |\n| Madagaskar | Antananarivo | Zambië | Lusaka |\n| Malawi | Lilongwe | Zimbabwe | Harare |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Tanzanië se hoofstad is **Dodoma**, nie Dar es Salaam nie, en Malawi s'n is **Lilongwe**, nie Blantyre nie.","en":"## The map of South Africa\n\nIn the exam you get a map of South Africa or the world and must point out or name places. Learn the positions here in words, then practise on an atlas.\n\n### Borders and neighbouring countries\n\n- South Africa lies at the southern tip of Africa. The **Atlantic Ocean** is on the **west coast** and the **Indian Ocean** on the **east and south coasts**. They officially meet at **Cape Agulhas**, the southernmost point of Africa.\n- **Six neighbours:** Namibia (north-west), Botswana (north), Zimbabwe (north, across the Limpopo River), Mozambique (north-east), Eswatini (east) and Lesotho, which is **completely surrounded by South Africa**.\n\n### The nine provinces and capitals\n\n| Province | Capital | Remember |\n|---|---|---|\n| Eastern Cape | Bhisho | harbours Gqeberha, Ngqura and East London |\n| Free State | Bloemfontein | judicial capital of SA |\n| Gauteng | Johannesburg | smallest province; Pretoria and O.R. Tambo are here |\n| KwaZulu-Natal | Pietermaritzburg | Durban harbour and King Shaka airport |\n| Limpopo | Polokwane | N1 to Beitbridge and Zimbabwe |\n| Mpumalanga | Mbombela | Kruger National Park; N4 to Mozambique |\n| North West | Mahikeng | Brits, Hartbeespoort Dam, Sun City |\n| Northern Cape | Kimberley | largest province; N7 to Namibia |\n| Western Cape | Cape Town | legislative capital (Parliament) |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Johannesburg is the capital of Gauteng, not of South Africa. SA has three capitals: **Pretoria** (executive/administrative), **Cape Town** (legislative) and **Bloemfontein** (judicial).\n\n### Airports and harbours\n\n- **International airports:** O.R. Tambo (JNB, Gauteng – the busiest in SA), Cape Town International (CPT) and King Shaka International (DUR, north of Durban). Others with international status: Lanseria (HLA), Kruger Mpumalanga (MQP) and Pilanesberg International near Sun City.\n- **Harbours:** KwaZulu-Natal – **Durban** (busiest port; cruise ships) and **Richards Bay**; Western Cape – **Cape Town** (cruise ships), **Saldanha Bay** and **Mossel Bay**; Eastern Cape – **Gqeberha**, **Ngqura** and **East London**.\n\n### National roads\n\n| Road | Route |\n|---|---|\n| N1 | Cape Town – Bloemfontein – Johannesburg – Pretoria – Polokwane – Beitbridge (Zimbabwe) |\n| N2 | Cape Town – George (Garden Route) – Gqeberha – East London – Durban |\n| N3 | Johannesburg – Harrismith – Pietermaritzburg – Durban |\n| N4 | Botswana border (Skilpadshek) – Rustenburg – past Brits – Pretoria – eMalahleni – Mbombela – Komatipoort (Mozambique) |\n| N7 | Cape Town – Springbok – Vioolsdrif (Namibia) |\n\n### Gateways and border posts\n\n| Border post | Neighbour | Where? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Beitbridge | Zimbabwe | N1, Limpopo |\n| Lebombo | Mozambique | N4 at Komatipoort, Mpumalanga |\n| Oshoek | Eswatini | Mpumalanga, near Mbabane |\n| Maseru Bridge | Lesotho | Free State, near Ladybrand |\n| Vioolsdrif | Namibia | N7 across the Orange River, Northern Cape |\n| Skilpadshek | Botswana | N4, North West |\n| Kopfontein | Botswana | North West, closest to Gaborone |\n| Ramatlabama | Botswana | North West, near Mahikeng |\n\n### Mountains, rivers and dams\n\n- **Drakensberg:** SA's highest mountain range, along the border between KwaZulu-Natal and Lesotho.\n- **Magaliesberg:** from Pretoria westwards past Hartbeespoort and Brits to Rustenburg.\n- **Cederberg** (rock formations and rock art) and **Swartberg** (Swartberg Pass, near Oudtshoorn): both in the Western Cape.\n- **Orange River (Gariep):** SA's longest river; flows west into the Atlantic Ocean and forms part of the border with Namibia.\n- **Vaal River:** the Orange's largest tributary; forms part of the Free State's northern border.\n- **Limpopo River:** the northern border with Botswana and Zimbabwe; flows through Mozambique into the Indian Ocean.\n- **Thukela River:** KwaZulu-Natal's largest river; rises in the Drakensberg.\n- **Crocodile River:** flows into **Hartbeespoort Dam** near Brits and later into the Limpopo.\n- **Dams:** **Gariep Dam** (Orange River, largest dam in SA), **Vaal Dam** (water for Gauteng; water sports) and **Hartbeespoort Dam** (North West; popular weekend destination).\n\n## The world map\n\n- **Seven continents:** Africa, Antarctica, Asia (largest), Australia/Oceania (smallest), Europe, North America and South America.\n- **Oceans:** the **Pacific Ocean** (largest), the **Atlantic** and the **Indian Ocean**; also know the **Arctic Ocean** and the **Southern Ocean** around Antarctica.\n- **Island groups:** Mauritius, the Seychelles and Madagascar (Africa's largest island) lie in the **Indian Ocean**; the Canary Islands (Spain) in the **Atlantic Ocean** north-west of Africa; the Caribbean islands (e.g. Jamaica) between North and South America; Hawaii (USA) in the **Pacific Ocean**.\n- The **UNWTO** (since 2024 also called **UN Tourism**) divides the world into five tourism regions: **Africa, the Americas, Asia and the Pacific, Europe and the Middle East**.\n\n### SADC\n\nThe Southern African Development Community has **16 member states**; its headquarters are in **Gaborone**.\n\n| Country | Capital | Country | Capital |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Angola | Luanda | Mauritius | Port Louis |\n| Botswana | Gaborone | Mozambique | Maputo |\n| Comoros | Moroni | Namibia | Windhoek |\n| DR Congo | Kinshasa | Seychelles | Victoria |\n| Eswatini | Mbabane | South Africa | Pretoria |\n| Lesotho | Maseru | Tanzania | Dodoma |\n| Madagascar | Antananarivo | Zambia | Lusaka |\n| Malawi | Lilongwe | Zimbabwe | Harare |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Tanzania's capital is **Dodoma**, not Dar es Salaam, and Malawi's is **Lilongwe**, not Blantyre."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Provinsiale hoofstad","en":"Provincial capital"},"def":{"af":"Die stad waar 'n provinsie se regering (wetgewer en premier) gesetel is, bv. Mahikeng vir Noordwes.","en":"The city where a province's government (legislature and premier) is based, e.g. Mahikeng for North West."}},{"term":{"af":"Nasionale pad","en":"National road"},"def":{"af":"'n Hoofpad met 'n N-nommer wat groot stede en grensposte verbind, bv. die N4 verby Brits.","en":"A main road with an N number that links major cities and border posts, e.g. the N4 past Brits."}},{"term":{"af":"Poort / grenspos","en":"Gateway / border post"},"def":{"af":"'n Amptelike punt waar reisigers 'n land binnekom of verlaat en paspoorte en goedere gekontroleer word.","en":"An official point where travellers enter or leave a country and passports and goods are checked."}},{"term":{"af":"Hawe","en":"Harbour"},"def":{"af":"'n Beskutte plek aan die kus waar skepe vrag en passasiers laai en aflaai, bv. Durban.","en":"A sheltered place on the coast where ships load and unload cargo and passengers, e.g. Durban."}},{"term":{"af":"Internasionale lughawe","en":"International airport"},"def":{"af":"'n Lughawe met doeane en immigrasie wat vlugte na en van ander lande hanteer, bv. O.R. Tambo (JNB).","en":"An airport with customs and immigration that handles flights to and from other countries, e.g. O.R. Tambo (JNB)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kontinent","en":"Continent"},"def":{"af":"Een van die sewe groot landmassas van die aarde, bv. Afrika of Asië.","en":"One of the Earth's seven large land masses, e.g. Africa or Asia."}},{"term":{"af":"Oseaan","en":"Ocean"},"def":{"af":"'n Groot soutwatermassa tussen kontinente; die Stille Oseaan is die grootste.","en":"A large body of salt water between continents; the Pacific Ocean is the largest."}},{"term":{"af":"SAOG (SADC)","en":"SADC"},"def":{"af":"Die Suider-Afrikaanse Ontwikkelingsgemeenskap: 16 lidlande wat saamwerk aan ontwikkeling en handel; hoofkantoor in Gaborone.","en":"The Southern African Development Community: 16 member states working together on development and trade; headquarters in Gaborone."}},{"term":{"af":"UNWTO-toerismestreke","en":"UNWTO tourism regions"},"def":{"af":"Die vyf streke waarin die VN se Wêreldtoerisme-organisasie die wêreld verdeel: Afrika, die Amerikas, Asië en die Stille Oseaan, Europa en die Midde-Ooste.","en":"The five regions into which the UN World Tourism Organization divides the world: Africa, the Americas, Asia and the Pacific, Europe and the Middle East."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Roete van Brits na die Kruger en Mosambiek","en":"Route from Brits to the Kruger and Mozambique"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gesin van Brits wil met die motor na die Kruger Nasionale Park ry en daarna met vakansie na Mosambiek gaan. Noem (a) die nasionale pad, (b) die provinsies waardeur hulle ry, (c) die grenspos en (d) Mosambiek se hoofstad.","en":"A family from Brits wants to drive to the Kruger National Park and then go on holiday to Mozambique. Name (a) the national road, (b) the provinces they drive through, (c) the border post and (d) Mozambique's capital."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die N4 loop van Brits oos na Pretoria en verder tot by Komatipoort.","en":"(a) The N4 runs from Brits east to Pretoria and on to Komatipoort."},{"af":"(b) Hulle begin in Noordwes, ry deur Gauteng (Pretoria) en dan Mpumalanga (eMalahleni, Mbombela, Komatipoort).","en":"(b) They start in North West, drive through Gauteng (Pretoria) and then Mpumalanga (eMalahleni, Mbombela, Komatipoort)."},{"af":"(c) Die N4 eindig by die Lebombo-grenspos by Komatipoort – die hoofpoort na Mosambiek.","en":"(c) The N4 ends at the Lebombo border post at Komatipoort – the main gateway to Mozambique."},{"af":"(d) Mosambiek is 'n SAOG-land met Maputo as hoofstad.","en":"(d) Mozambique is a SADC country with Maputo as its capital."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) N4 (b) Noordwes → Gauteng → Mpumalanga (c) Lebombo (d) Maputo","en":"(a) N4 (b) North West → Gauteng → Mpumalanga (c) Lebombo (d) Maputo"}},{"title":{"af":"Van Brits na Gaborone","en":"From Brits to Gaborone"},"problem":{"af":"'n Skoolrugbyspan van Brits speel 'n toernooi in Gaborone. Watter pad en grenspos kan die bus gebruik? Waarom is Gaborone vir die SAOG belangrik?","en":"A school rugby team from Brits is playing a tournament in Gaborone. Which road and border post can the bus use? Why is Gaborone important to SADC?"},"steps":[{"af":"Gaborone is die hoofstad van Botswana. Botswana grens aan Noordwes, en Gaborone lê noordwes van Brits.","en":"Gaborone is the capital of Botswana. Botswana borders North West, and Gaborone lies north-west of Brits."},{"af":"Ry met die N4 wes deur Rustenburg en Zeerust tot by die Skilpadshek-grenspos.","en":"Drive west on the N4 through Rustenburg and Zeerust to the Skilpadshek border post."},{"af":"Alternatief: die Kopfontein-grenspos is die naaste aan Gaborone. Albei is in Noordwes.","en":"Alternative: the Kopfontein border post is closest to Gaborone. Both are in North West."},{"af":"Gaborone is die hoofkantoor van die SAOG, wat 16 lidlande het.","en":"Gaborone is the headquarters of SADC, which has 16 member states."}],"answer":{"af":"N4 na Skilpadshek (of Kopfontein); Gaborone is die SAOG se hoofkantoor","en":"N4 to Skilpadshek (or Kopfontein); Gaborone is SADC's headquarters"}},{"title":{"af":"Kaartwerk in woorde: identifiseer die plek","en":"Map work in words: identify the place"},"problem":{"af":"Identifiseer elke plek: (a) die provinsie in die noordweste van SA wat aan Namibië en Botswana grens, met Kimberley as hoofstad; (b) die oseaan teen Durban se kus; (c) 'n SAOG-eiland in die Indiese Oseaan, oos van Madagaskar, met Port Louis as hoofstad; (d) die rivier wat in die Hartbeespoortdam invloei.","en":"Identify each place: (a) the province in the north-west of SA that borders Namibia and Botswana, with Kimberley as its capital; (b) the ocean along Durban's coast; (c) a SADC island in the Indian Ocean, east of Madagascar, with Port Louis as its capital; (d) the river that flows into Hartbeespoort Dam."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Kimberley is die hoofstad van die Noord-Kaap, SA se grootste provinsie.","en":"(a) Kimberley is the capital of the Northern Cape, SA's largest province."},{"af":"(b) Durban lê aan die ooskus, dus die Indiese Oseaan.","en":"(b) Durban is on the east coast, so the Indian Ocean."},{"af":"(c) Port Louis is die hoofstad van Mauritius.","en":"(c) Port Louis is the capital of Mauritius."},{"af":"(d) Die Krokodilrivier vloei in die Hartbeespoortdam naby Brits.","en":"(d) The Crocodile River flows into Hartbeespoort Dam near Brits."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Noord-Kaap (b) Indiese Oseaan (c) Mauritius (d) Krokodilrivier","en":"(a) Northern Cape (b) Indian Ocean (c) Mauritius (d) Crocodile River"}},{"title":{"af":"Die N3 van die kus na Gauteng","en":"The N3 from the coast to Gauteng"},"problem":{"af":"'n Toeris land by King Shaka Internasionaal en ry met die N3 na Johannesburg. Noem (a) die provinsie waar hy land en sy hoofstad, (b) al die provinsies op die roete, en (c) die bergreeks wat die N3 tussen Ladysmith en Harrismith oorsteek.","en":"A tourist lands at King Shaka International and drives the N3 to Johannesburg. Name (a) the province where he lands and its capital, (b) all the provinces on the route, and (c) the mountain range the N3 crosses between Ladysmith and Harrismith."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) King Shaka lê noord van Durban in KwaZulu-Natal; die hoofstad is Pietermaritzburg, wat ook op die N3 lê.","en":"(a) King Shaka is north of Durban in KwaZulu-Natal; the capital is Pietermaritzburg, which is also on the N3."},{"af":"(b) Die N3 loop van KwaZulu-Natal deur die Vrystaat (Harrismith) na Gauteng.","en":"(b) The N3 runs from KwaZulu-Natal through the Free State (Harrismith) to Gauteng."},{"af":"(c) Tussen Ladysmith en Harrismith klim die pad oor die Drakensberg (Van Reenenpas).","en":"(c) Between Ladysmith and Harrismith the road climbs over the Drakensberg (Van Reenen's Pass)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) KwaZulu-Natal, Pietermaritzburg (b) KZN → Vrystaat → Gauteng (c) Drakensberg","en":"(a) KwaZulu-Natal, Pietermaritzburg (b) KZN → Free State → Gauteng (c) Drakensberg"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hoofstad van Limpopo?","en":"What is the capital of Limpopo?"},"options":[{"af":"Mbombela","en":"Mbombela"},{"af":"Polokwane","en":"Polokwane"},{"af":"Mahikeng","en":"Mahikeng"},{"af":"Kimberley","en":"Kimberley"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Polokwane is Limpopo se hoofstad. Mbombela is Mpumalanga s'n, Mahikeng Noordwes s'n en Kimberley die Noord-Kaap s'n.","en":"Polokwane is the capital of Limpopo. Mbombela is Mpumalanga's, Mahikeng North West's and Kimberley the Northern Cape's."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Brits lê in Noordwes. Die hoofstad van Noordwes is ___.","en":"Brits is in North West. The capital of North West is ___."},"answers":{"af":["Mahikeng","Mafikeng"],"en":["Mahikeng","Mafikeng"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Rustenburg","Potchefstroom","Klerksdorp"],"en":["Rustenburg","Potchefstroom","Klerksdorp"]}},"explain":{"af":"Mahikeng (vroeër Mafikeng) is die hoofstad van Noordwes. Rustenburg is groter, maar nie die hoofstad nie.","en":"Mahikeng (formerly Mafikeng) is the capital of North West. Rustenburg is bigger, but not the capital."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Lesotho word heeltemal deur Suid-Afrika omring.","en":"Lesotho is completely surrounded by South Africa."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Lesotho grens aan die Vrystaat, KwaZulu-Natal en die Oos-Kaap en het geen ander buurland nie.","en":"True. Lesotho borders the Free State, KwaZulu-Natal and the Eastern Cape and has no other neighbour."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter oseaan spoel teen Durban se strande?","en":"Which ocean washes Durban's beaches?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Atlantiese Oseaan","en":"The Atlantic Ocean"},{"af":"Die Stille Oseaan","en":"The Pacific Ocean"},{"af":"Die Indiese Oseaan","en":"The Indian Ocean"},{"af":"Die Suidelike Oseaan","en":"The Southern Ocean"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Durban lê aan die ooskus, aan die Indiese Oseaan. Die Atlantiese Oseaan is aan die weskus (Kaapstad, Saldanhabaai).","en":"Durban is on the east coast, on the Indian Ocean. The Atlantic Ocean is on the west coast (Cape Town, Saldanha Bay)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die nasionale pad wat Johannesburg en Durban verbind, is die ___.","en":"The national road that links Johannesburg and Durban is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["N3"],"en":["N3"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["N1","N2","N4"],"en":["N1","N2","N4"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die N3 loop van Johannesburg deur Harrismith en Pietermaritzburg na Durban. Die N2 loop langs die kus van Kaapstad na Durban.","en":"The N3 runs from Johannesburg through Harrismith and Pietermaritzburg to Durban. The N2 runs along the coast from Cape Town to Durban."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter land is NIE een van Suid-Afrika se buurlande nie?","en":"Which country is NOT one of South Africa's neighbours?"},"options":[{"af":"Zambië","en":"Zambia"},{"af":"Namibië","en":"Namibia"},{"af":"Mosambiek","en":"Mozambique"},{"af":"Eswatini","en":"Eswatini"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"SA se ses buurlande is Namibië, Botswana, Zimbabwe, Mosambiek, Eswatini en Lesotho. Zambië is 'n SAOG-land, maar grens nie aan SA nie.","en":"SA's six neighbours are Namibia, Botswana, Zimbabwe, Mozambique, Eswatini and Lesotho. Zambia is a SADC country, but does not border SA."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke SAOG-land by sy hoofstad.","en":"Match each SADC country to its capital."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Tanzanië","en":"Tanzania"},"r":{"af":"Dodoma","en":"Dodoma"}},{"l":{"af":"Malawi","en":"Malawi"},"r":{"af":"Lilongwe","en":"Lilongwe"}},{"l":{"af":"Mosambiek","en":"Mozambique"},"r":{"af":"Maputo","en":"Maputo"}},{"l":{"af":"Botswana","en":"Botswana"},"r":{"af":"Gaborone","en":"Gaborone"}},{"l":{"af":"Zambië","en":"Zambia"},"r":{"af":"Lusaka","en":"Lusaka"}}],"explain":{"af":"Pasop vir die lokvalle: Tanzanië se hoofstad is Dodoma (nie Dar es Salaam nie) en Malawi s'n is Lilongwe (nie Blantyre nie).","en":"Watch the traps: Tanzania's capital is Dodoma (not Dar es Salaam) and Malawi's is Lilongwe (not Blantyre)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter hawe lê in die Oos-Kaap?","en":"Which harbour is in the Eastern Cape?"},"options":[{"af":"Richardsbaai","en":"Richards Bay"},{"af":"Saldanhabaai","en":"Saldanha Bay"},{"af":"Mosselbaai","en":"Mossel Bay"},{"af":"Ngqura","en":"Ngqura"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ngqura (by Coega, naby Gqeberha) is in die Oos-Kaap, saam met Gqeberha en Oos-Londen. Richardsbaai is in KwaZulu-Natal; Saldanha- en Mosselbaai in die Wes-Kaap.","en":"Ngqura (at Coega, near Gqeberha) is in the Eastern Cape, with Gqeberha and East London. Richards Bay is in KwaZulu-Natal; Saldanha Bay and Mossel Bay are in the Western Cape."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die grootste dam in Suid-Afrika is die ___-dam.","en":"The largest dam in South Africa is the ___ Dam."},"answers":{"af":["Gariep","Gariepdam","Gariep-dam"],"en":["Gariep","Gariep Dam"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Vaal","Hartbeespoort","Kariba"],"en":["Vaal","Hartbeespoort","Kariba"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Gariepdam in die Oranjerivier is SA se grootste dam. Die Karibadam is groter, maar lê tussen Zambië en Zimbabwe.","en":"Gariep Dam on the Orange River is SA's largest dam. Kariba is bigger, but lies between Zambia and Zimbabwe."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is NIE een van die UNWTO se vyf toerismestreke nie?","en":"Which one is NOT one of the UNWTO's five tourism regions?"},"options":[{"af":"Afrika","en":"Africa"},{"af":"Die Amerikas","en":"The Americas"},{"af":"Suider-Afrika","en":"Southern Africa"},{"af":"Asië en die Stille Oseaan","en":"Asia and the Pacific"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die vyf UNWTO-streke is Afrika, die Amerikas, Asië en die Stille Oseaan, Europa en die Midde-Ooste. Suider-Afrika is deel van die streek Afrika.","en":"The five UNWTO regions are Africa, the Americas, Asia and the Pacific, Europe and the Middle East. Southern Africa is part of the Africa region."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Dar es Salaam is die hoofstad van Tanzanië.","en":"Dar es Salaam is the capital of Tanzania."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dar es Salaam is Tanzanië se grootste stad, maar die hoofstad is Dodoma.","en":"False. Dar es Salaam is Tanzania's biggest city, but the capital is Dodoma."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeroperateur in Brits neem 'n groep per bus na Gaborone. Watter grenspos is die beste keuse?","en":"A tour operator in Brits takes a group by bus to Gaborone. Which border post is the best choice?"},"options":[{"af":"Beitbridge","en":"Beitbridge"},{"af":"Skilpadshek","en":"Skilpadshek"},{"af":"Oshoek","en":"Oshoek"},{"af":"Lebombo","en":"Lebombo"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gaborone is in Botswana. Skilpadshek lê op die N4 wes van Brits en is 'n grenspos na Botswana. Beitbridge gaan na Zimbabwe, Oshoek na Eswatini en Lebombo na Mosambiek.","en":"Gaborone is in Botswana. Skilpadshek is on the N4 west of Brits and is a border post into Botswana. Beitbridge leads to Zimbabwe, Oshoek to Eswatini and Lebombo to Mozambique."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die rivier wat in die Hartbeespoortdam naby Brits invloei, is die ___-rivier.","en":"The river that flows into Hartbeespoort Dam near Brits is the ___ River."},"answers":{"af":["Krokodil","Krokodilrivier","Krokodil-rivier"],"en":["Crocodile","Crocodile River"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Vaal","Oranje","Limpopo"],"en":["Vaal","Orange","Limpopo"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die Krokodilrivier vloei in die Hartbeespoortdam en later in die Limpopo. Die Vaalrivier vloei in die Oranje.","en":"The Crocodile River flows into Hartbeespoort Dam and later into the Limpopo. The Vaal River flows into the Orange."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeris wil van Pretoria af ry om die Victoria-waterval in Zimbabwe te besoek. Watter pad en grenspos gebruik hy?","en":"A tourist wants to drive from Pretoria to visit the Victoria Falls in Zimbabwe. Which road and border post does he use?"},"options":[{"af":"Die N1 en Beitbridge","en":"The N1 and Beitbridge"},{"af":"Die N4 en Lebombo","en":"The N4 and Lebombo"},{"af":"Die N3 en Oshoek","en":"The N3 and Oshoek"},{"af":"Die N1 en Skilpadshek","en":"The N1 and Skilpadshek"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die N1 loop van Pretoria deur Polokwane tot by Beitbridge op die Limpoporivier, die hoofpoort na Zimbabwe. Skilpadshek is op die N4 na Botswana.","en":"The N1 runs from Pretoria through Polokwane to Beitbridge on the Limpopo River, the main gateway to Zimbabwe. Skilpadshek is on the N4 to Botswana."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die N4 loop van Pretoria deur Mbombela tot by die ___-grenspos na Mosambiek.","en":"The N4 runs from Pretoria through Mbombela to the ___ border post into Mozambique."},"answers":{"af":["Lebombo"],"en":["Lebombo"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Beitbridge","Oshoek","Ramatlabama"],"en":["Beitbridge","Oshoek","Ramatlabama"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die N4 eindig by Komatipoort by die Lebombo-grenspos. Oshoek is die poort na Eswatini en Ramatlabama na Botswana.","en":"The N4 ends at Komatipoort at the Lebombo border post. Oshoek is the gateway to Eswatini and Ramatlabama to Botswana."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Reisagent in Pretoria moet vir 'n gesin 'n eilandvakansie voorstel. Hulle wil in die Indiese Oseaan bly, 'n kort vlug hê en 'n SAOG-land besoek. Watter bestemming pas die beste?","en":"A travel agent in Pretoria must suggest an island holiday for a family. They want to stay in the Indian Ocean, have a short flight and visit a SADC country. Which destination fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Kanariese Eilande","en":"The Canary Islands"},{"af":"Hawaii","en":"Hawaii"},{"af":"Die Karibiese Eilande","en":"The Caribbean islands"},{"af":"Mauritius","en":"Mauritius"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Mauritius lê in die Indiese Oseaan, oos van Madagaskar, en is 'n SAOG-lid. Die Kanariese Eilande is in die Atlantiese Oseaan (Spanje), Hawaii in die Stille Oseaan (VSA) en die Karibiese Eilande tussen Noord- en Suid-Amerika – almal ver en nie SAOG nie.","en":"Mauritius lies in the Indian Ocean, east of Madagascar, and is a SADC member. The Canary Islands are in the Atlantic (Spain), Hawaii in the Pacific (USA) and the Caribbean islands between North and South America – all far away and not SADC."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t2-afstande-reisplan","title":{"af":"Afstandaanwysers, afstandstabelle en reisplanne","en":"Distance indicators, distance tables and itineraries"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal afstandaanwysers en afstandstabelle kan lees, reistyd en brandstofkoste kan bereken en 'n eenvoudige dag-vir-dag-reisplan kan opstel en nagaan.","en":"You will be able to read distance indicators and distance tables, calculate travel time and fuel cost, and draw up and check a simple day-by-day itinerary."},"summary":{"af":"## Afstandaanwysers op kaarte\n\n- Padkaarte het **afstandaanwysers**: klein getalle langs die pad tussen twee merkers (kolletjies, pyltjies of dorpe). Elke getal gee die afstand in km tussen daardie twee punte. **Tel al die getalle op jou roete bymekaar** vir die totale afstand.\n- Is daar geen aanwysers nie, gebruik die **skaal**: werklike afstand = kaartafstand × skaal.\n- Langs die pad wys **afstandsborde** hoeveel km dit na die volgende dorpe is.\n\n## Afstandstabelle\n\n'n **Afstandstabel** gee die padafstand tussen pare dorpe. Lees die km af waar die **ry** van die een dorp en die **kolom** van die ander dorp kruis. Die tabel is simmetries (Brits → Mbombela = Mbombela → Brits) en die skuinslyn is leeg.\n\n*Voorbeelddata vir oefening (km, afgerond):*\n\n| | Brits | Pretoria | eMalahleni | Mbombela | Komatipoort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Brits** | – | 60 | 170 | 390 | 500 |\n| **Pretoria** | 60 | – | 110 | 330 | 440 |\n| **eMalahleni** | 170 | 110 | – | 220 | 330 |\n| **Mbombela** | 390 | 330 | 220 | – | 110 |\n| **Komatipoort** | 500 | 440 | 330 | 110 | – |\n\n1. Kry die eerste dorp in die linkerkolom.\n2. Beweeg langs die ry tot by die kolom van die tweede dorp.\n3. Vir 'n roete met stilhouplekke: lees elke **skof** apart en **tel die skofte bymekaar**.\n4. Vir 'n heen-en-terug-reis: vermenigvuldig met 2.\n\n> **Wenk:** Gebruik altyd die afstande en pryse wat die vraag gee – nie jou eie of 'n toep se afstande nie.\n\n## Afstand en reistyd\n\n`tyd = afstand ÷ gemiddelde spoed`   `afstand = spoed × tyd`   `spoed = afstand ÷ tyd`\n\n- 480 km ÷ 80 km/h = **6 h**.\n- Skakel desimale ure om na minute: 6,25 h = 6 h + (0,25 × 60) min = **6 h 15 min**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 4,5 h is NIE 4 h 50 min nie, maar 4 h 30 min. 'n Uur het 60 minute, nie 100 nie.\n\n**Suid-Afrikaanse spoedgrense (maksimum):**\n\n| Waar? | Spoedgrens |\n|---|---|\n| Stedelike gebiede (dorpe en stede) | 60 km/h |\n| Openbare paaie buite stedelike gebiede | 100 km/h |\n| Vryweë (snelweë) | 120 km/h |\n\nJou **gemiddelde** spoed is altyd laer as die spoedgrens: verkeer, dorpe, padwerke en verkeersligte maak jou stadiger.\n\n- **Russtoppe:** beplan omtrent **elke 2 uur** 'n russtop teen moegheid.\n- `aankomstyd = vertrektyd + bestuurstyd + tyd vir stoppe`\n\n## Brandstof en koste\n\n`liter = afstand ÷ 100 × verbruik (ℓ/100 km)`   `koste = liter × prys per liter`\n\nVoorbeeld: 600 km teen 8 ℓ/100 km → 600 ÷ 100 × 8 = **48 ℓ**; 48 × R22,00 = **R1 056,00**. Onthou om die terugrit by te tel, en rond geldbedrae af tot **2 desimale** (R1 940,625 → R1 940,63).\n\n## Tydtafels en die 24-uurhorlosie\n\nBus-, trein- en vlugroosters gebruik die **24-uurhorlosie**: 07:30, 13:05, 18:45. Reistyd = aankomstyd − vertrektyd, in ure en minute. Bus vertrek 07:30, kom aan 09:15 → **1 h 45 min** (105 minute).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie tye soos desimale getalle aftrek nie (9,15 − 7,30 = 1,85 is verkeerd). Leen 60 minute, nie 100 nie.\n\n## Reisplanne\n\n'n **Reisplan** (itinerarium) is 'n gedetailleerde, chronologiese **dag-vir-dag**-plan van 'n reis: wat gebeur waar en wanneer. In Graad 10 koppel jy afstand aan reistyd en stel jy 'n eenvoudige reisplan op; volledige reisplanne volg in Graad 11.\n\n**Elemente van 'n reisplan:**\n- datums en dae\n- vertrek- en aankomstye (24-uurhorlosie)\n- roete en vervoer (padnommers, vlugnommers)\n- akkommodasie (naam, adres, in- en uitboektye)\n- maaltye (watter is ingesluit)\n- aktiwiteite en aantreklikhede (met oop- en sluitingstye)\n- kontaknommers (akkommodasie, toergids, noodnommers)\n- koste (per persoon, totaal, wat ingesluit is)\n\n**Beplanningsfaktore:** begroting; beskikbare tyd; belangstellings en behoeftes van die toeriste (ouderdom, spesiale behoeftes); afstande en reistyd; oop- en sluitingstye (bv. parkhekke); veiligheid (moenie in die nag ry nie, russtoppe, voertuig nagaan); weer en seisoen (skoolvakansies is vol – bespreek vroeg).\n\n### Kontroleer 'n reisplan (soek die fout)\n\n1. Is die reistyd realisties vir die afstand? (afstand ÷ tyd mag nie bo die spoedgrens wees nie)\n2. Is die volgorde logies (aankoms ná vertrek, inboek ná aankoms)?\n3. Val elke aktiwiteit binne die oop- en sluitingstye?\n4. Is al die elemente daar (akkommodasie vir elke nag, kontaknommers)?\n5. Pas die dae en datums by mekaar?","en":"## Distance indicators on maps\n\n- Road maps have **distance indicators**: small numbers along the road between two markers (dots, arrows or towns). Each number gives the distance in km between those two points. **Add all the numbers on your route** for the total distance.\n- If there are no indicators, use the **scale**: real distance = map distance × scale.\n- Along the road, **distance signs** show how many km it is to the next towns.\n\n## Distance tables\n\nA **distance table** gives the road distance between pairs of towns. Read the km where the **row** of one town and the **column** of the other town meet. The table is symmetrical (Brits → Mbombela = Mbombela → Brits) and the diagonal is empty.\n\n*Example data for practice (km, rounded):*\n\n| | Brits | Pretoria | eMalahleni | Mbombela | Komatipoort |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Brits** | – | 60 | 170 | 390 | 500 |\n| **Pretoria** | 60 | – | 110 | 330 | 440 |\n| **eMalahleni** | 170 | 110 | – | 220 | 330 |\n| **Mbombela** | 390 | 330 | 220 | – | 110 |\n| **Komatipoort** | 500 | 440 | 330 | 110 | – |\n\n1. Find the first town in the left-hand column.\n2. Move along the row to the column of the second town.\n3. For a route with stops: read each **leg** separately and **add the legs**.\n4. For a return trip: multiply by 2.\n\n> **Tip:** Always use the distances and prices the question gives – not your own or an app's distances.\n\n## Distance and travel time\n\n`time = distance ÷ average speed`   `distance = speed × time`   `speed = distance ÷ time`\n\n- 480 km ÷ 80 km/h = **6 h**.\n- Convert decimal hours to minutes: 6.25 h = 6 h + (0.25 × 60) min = **6 h 15 min**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** 4.5 h is NOT 4 h 50 min, but 4 h 30 min. An hour has 60 minutes, not 100.\n\n**South African speed limits (maximum):**\n\n| Where? | Speed limit |\n|---|---|\n| Urban areas (towns and cities) | 60 km/h |\n| Public roads outside urban areas | 100 km/h |\n| Freeways | 120 km/h |\n\nYour **average** speed is always lower than the speed limit: traffic, towns, roadworks and traffic lights slow you down.\n\n- **Rest stops:** plan a rest stop about **every 2 hours** to prevent fatigue.\n- `arrival time = departure time + driving time + time for stops`\n\n## Fuel and cost\n\n`litres = distance ÷ 100 × consumption (ℓ/100 km)`   `cost = litres × price per litre`\n\nExample: 600 km at 8 ℓ/100 km → 600 ÷ 100 × 8 = **48 ℓ**; 48 × R22.00 = **R1 056.00**. Remember to add the return trip, and round money to **2 decimals** (R1 940.625 → R1 940.63).\n\n## Timetables and the 24-hour clock\n\nBus, train and flight timetables use the **24-hour clock**: 07:30, 13:05, 18:45. Travel time = arrival time − departure time, in hours and minutes. Bus departs 07:30, arrives 09:15 → **1 h 45 min** (105 minutes).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don't subtract times like decimal numbers (9.15 − 7.30 = 1.85 is wrong). Borrow 60 minutes, not 100.\n\n## Itineraries\n\nAn **itinerary** is a detailed, chronological **day-by-day** plan of a trip: what happens where and when. In Grade 10 you link distance to travel time and draw up a simple itinerary; full itineraries follow in Grade 11.\n\n**Elements of an itinerary:**\n- dates and days\n- departure and arrival times (24-hour clock)\n- route and transport (road numbers, flight numbers)\n- accommodation (name, address, check-in and check-out times)\n- meals (which are included)\n- activities and attractions (with opening and closing times)\n- contact numbers (accommodation, tour guide, emergency numbers)\n- costs (per person, total, what is included)\n\n**Planning factors:** budget; time available; interests and needs of the tourists (age, special needs); distances and travel time; opening and closing times (e.g. park gates); safety (don't drive at night, rest stops, check the vehicle); weather and season (school holidays are full – book early).\n\n### Check an itinerary (find the error)\n\n1. Is the travel time realistic for the distance? (distance ÷ time may not be above the speed limit)\n2. Is the order logical (arrival after departure, check-in after arrival)?\n3. Does each activity fall within the opening and closing times?\n4. Are all the elements there (accommodation for every night, contact numbers)?\n5. Do the days and dates match?"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Afstandaanwyser","en":"Distance indicator"},"def":{"af":"'n Getal langs 'n pad op 'n kaart wat die afstand in km tussen twee merkers of dorpe gee.","en":"A number along a road on a map that gives the distance in km between two markers or towns."}},{"term":{"af":"Afstandstabel","en":"Distance table"},"def":{"af":"'n Tabel wat die padafstande tussen pare dorpe gee; lees af waar die ry en kolom kruis.","en":"A table that gives the road distances between pairs of towns; read where the row and column meet."}},{"term":{"af":"Skof","en":"Leg (of a journey)"},"def":{"af":"Een deel van 'n roete tussen twee stilhouplekke; die skofte word bymekaargetel vir die totale afstand.","en":"One part of a route between two stops; the legs are added for the total distance."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},"def":{"af":"Die totale afstand gedeel deur die totale tyd, in km/h; altyd laer as die spoedgrens.","en":"The total distance divided by the total time, in km/h; always lower than the speed limit."}},{"term":{"af":"Reistyd","en":"Travel time"},"def":{"af":"Hoe lank 'n reis duur: afstand ÷ gemiddelde spoed, plus tyd vir russtoppe.","en":"How long a journey takes: distance ÷ average speed, plus time for rest stops."}},{"term":{"af":"Brandstofverbruik","en":"Fuel consumption"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel liter brandstof 'n voertuig per 100 km gebruik (ℓ/100 km).","en":"How many litres of fuel a vehicle uses per 100 km (ℓ/100 km)."}},{"term":{"af":"Tydtafel (rooster)","en":"Timetable"},"def":{"af":"'n Lys van vertrek- en aankomstye van busse, treine of vlugte in die 24-uurformaat.","en":"A list of departure and arrival times of buses, trains or flights in 24-hour format."}},{"term":{"af":"Reisplan (itinerarium)","en":"Itinerary"},"def":{"af":"'n Gedetailleerde dag-vir-dag-plan van 'n reis met tye, vervoer, akkommodasie, maaltye, aktiwiteite, kontaknommers en koste.","en":"A detailed day-by-day plan of a trip with times, transport, accommodation, meals, activities, contact numbers and costs."}},{"term":{"af":"Beplanningsfaktore","en":"Planning factors"},"def":{"af":"Dinge waarmee 'n reisbeplanner rekening hou: begroting, tyd, belangstellings, afstande, oop- en sluitingstye, veiligheid en seisoen.","en":"Things a trip planner takes into account: budget, time, interests, distances, opening and closing times, safety and season."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Afstandstabel en reistyd","en":"Distance table and travel time"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die afstandstabel in die opsomming. 'n Gesin vertrek om 06:00 uit Brits na Komatipoort. Hulle ry teen 'n gemiddelde spoed van 80 km/h en hou twee russtoppe van 20 minute elk. Bereken (a) die afstand, (b) die bestuurstyd en (c) die aankomstyd.","en":"Use the distance table in the summary. A family leaves Brits for Komatipoort at 06:00. They drive at an average speed of 80 km/h and make two rest stops of 20 minutes each. Calculate (a) the distance, (b) the driving time and (c) the arrival time."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ry Brits, kolom Komatipoort: 500 km. (Kontrole met die skofte: 60 + 110 + 220 + 110 = 500 km)","en":"(a) Row Brits, column Komatipoort: 500 km. (Check with the legs: 60 + 110 + 220 + 110 = 500 km)"},{"af":"(b) Tyd = afstand ÷ spoed = 500 ÷ 80 = 6,25 h","en":"(b) Time = distance ÷ speed = 500 ÷ 80 = 6.25 h"},{"af":"Skakel om: 0,25 × 60 = 15 min, dus 6 h 15 min (nie 6 h 25 min nie!)","en":"Convert: 0.25 × 60 = 15 min, so 6 h 15 min (not 6 h 25 min!)"},{"af":"(c) Totale reistyd = 6 h 15 min + 2 × 20 min = 6 h 55 min","en":"(c) Total travel time = 6 h 15 min + 2 × 20 min = 6 h 55 min"},{"af":"Aankomstyd = 06:00 + 6 h 55 min = 12:55","en":"Arrival time = 06:00 + 6 h 55 min = 12:55"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 500 km (b) 6 h 15 min (c) 12:55","en":"(a) 500 km (b) 6 h 15 min (c) 12:55"}},{"title":{"af":"Brandstofkoste van 'n Kruger-vakansie","en":"Fuel cost of a Kruger holiday"},"problem":{"af":"Die gesin ry 500 km na die park, 500 km terug en 150 km in die park self. Hul motor gebruik 7,5 ℓ/100 km en petrol kos R22,50 per liter (gegewe). Bereken die totale brandstofkoste.","en":"The family drives 500 km to the park, 500 km back and 150 km inside the park itself. Their car uses 7.5 ℓ/100 km and petrol costs R22.50 per litre (given). Calculate the total fuel cost."},"steps":[{"af":"Totale afstand = 500 + 500 + 150 = 1 150 km","en":"Total distance = 500 + 500 + 150 = 1 150 km"},{"af":"Liter = afstand ÷ 100 × verbruik = 1 150 ÷ 100 × 7,5 = 86,25 ℓ","en":"Litres = distance ÷ 100 × consumption = 1 150 ÷ 100 × 7.5 = 86.25 ℓ"},{"af":"Koste = liter × prys = 86,25 × R22,50 = R1 940,625","en":"Cost = litres × price = 86.25 × R22.50 = R1 940.625"},{"af":"Rond af tot 2 desimale: R1 940,63","en":"Round to 2 decimals: R1 940.63"}],"answer":{"af":"Brandstofkoste = R1 940,63","en":"Fuel cost = R1 940.63"}},{"title":{"af":"Eenvoudige reisplan: skooltoer na die Wieg van die Mensdom","en":"Simple itinerary: school tour to the Cradle of Humankind"},"problem":{"af":"'n Graad 10-klas van Brits besoek die Wieg van die Mensdom. Gegewe: die afstand van die skool na die besoekersentrums is 54 km; die bus ry gemiddeld 72 km/h; laai neem 15 minute; die bus moet om 09:00 daar wees en vertrek om 13:00 terug. Bereken die vertrektyd en stel 'n eenvoudige reisplan vir die dag op.","en":"A Grade 10 class from Brits visits the Cradle of Humankind. Given: the distance from the school to the visitor centres is 54 km; the bus averages 72 km/h; loading takes 15 minutes; the bus must be there at 09:00 and leaves for home at 13:00. Calculate the departure time and draw up a simple itinerary for the day."},"steps":[{"af":"Reistyd = 54 ÷ 72 = 0,75 h = 45 min","en":"Travel time = 54 ÷ 72 = 0.75 h = 45 min"},{"af":"Werk terug van 09:00: 09:00 − 45 min = 08:15 vertrek; trek nog 15 min vir laai af → leerders by die skool om 08:00","en":"Work back from 09:00: 09:00 − 45 min = 08:15 departure; subtract another 15 min for loading → learners at school at 08:00"},{"af":"Reisplan: 08:00 leerders by die skool; 08:15 bus vertrek; 09:00 aankoms; 09:00–10:00 begeleide toer deur die Sterkfontein-grotte; 10:15–11:45 Maropeng-besoekersentrum; 12:00–12:45 middagete (eie kos)","en":"Itinerary: 08:00 learners at school; 08:15 bus departs; 09:00 arrival; 09:00–10:00 guided tour of the Sterkfontein Caves; 10:15–11:45 Maropeng Visitor Centre; 12:00–12:45 lunch (own food)"},{"af":"13:00 vertrek terug (54 km, 45 min) → 13:45 aankoms by die skool. Voeg die bus-maatskappy en die onderwyser se kontaknommers en die koste per leerder by.","en":"13:00 depart for home (54 km, 45 min) → 13:45 arrival at school. Add the bus company's and the teacher's contact numbers and the cost per learner."}],"answer":{"af":"Bus vertrek 08:15 (leerders 08:00 by die skool); terug by die skool om 13:45","en":"Bus departs 08:15 (learners at school at 08:00); back at school at 13:45"}},{"title":{"af":"Soek die foute in 'n reisplan","en":"Find the errors in an itinerary"},"problem":{"af":"Gegewe: Brits na die Malelane-hek van die Kruger is 450 km; parkhekke sluit om 18:00 en besoekers mag ná sluitingstyd nie in hul eie motors in die park ry nie. Reisplan: **Saterdag 5 Desember** – 08:00 vertrek uit Brits met die N4; 10:30 aankoms by die Malelane-hek; 12:00 inboek by die ruskamp; 19:30 aandrit in eie motor om leeus te soek. **Maandag 6 Desember** – 05:30 oggend-wildrit. Identifiseer drie foute en stel 'n verbetering voor.","en":"Given: Brits to the Malelane Gate of the Kruger is 450 km; park gates close at 18:00 and visitors may not drive in their own cars in the park after closing time. Itinerary: **Saturday 5 December** – 08:00 depart Brits on the N4; 10:30 arrive at Malelane Gate; 12:00 check in at the rest camp; 19:30 evening drive in own car to look for lions. **Monday 6 December** – 05:30 morning game drive. Identify three errors and suggest an improvement."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: 450 km in 2 h 30 min = 450 ÷ 2,5 = 180 km/h – bo die spoedgrens van 120 km/h en onmoontlik.","en":"Error 1: 450 km in 2 h 30 min = 450 ÷ 2.5 = 180 km/h – above the 120 km/h speed limit and impossible."},{"af":"Verbetering: teen 90 km/h is dit 450 ÷ 90 = 5 h; plus 30 min se stoppe. Vertrek 05:30 → aankoms 11:00.","en":"Improvement: at 90 km/h it is 450 ÷ 90 = 5 h; plus 30 min of stops. Depart 05:30 → arrive 11:00."},{"af":"Fout 2: 19:30 is ná die hekke om 18:00 sluit. Bespreek eerder 'n begeleide nagrit met die park se veldwagters.","en":"Error 2: 19:30 is after the gates close at 18:00. Rather book a guided night drive with the park's rangers."},{"af":"Fout 3: die dag ná Saterdag 5 Desember is Sondag 6 Desember, nie Maandag nie.","en":"Error 3: the day after Saturday 5 December is Sunday 6 December, not Monday."}],"answer":{"af":"Onrealistiese reistyd (180 km/h), aandrit ná hekke sluit, verkeerde dag (Sondag 6 Des.)","en":"Unrealistic travel time (180 km/h), evening drive after gates close, wrong day (Sunday 6 Dec.)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n reisplan (itinerarium)?","en":"What is an itinerary?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Lys pryse van al die hotelle in 'n dorp","en":"A list of prices of all the hotels in a town"},{"af":"'n Gedetailleerde dag-vir-dag-plan van 'n reis met tye, vervoer, akkommodasie en aktiwiteite","en":"A detailed day-by-day plan of a trip with times, transport, accommodation and activities"},{"af":"'n Kaart wat die afstande tussen dorpe wys","en":"A map that shows the distances between towns"},{"af":"'n Tabel met wisselkoerse vir buitelandse toeriste","en":"A table of exchange rates for foreign tourists"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Reisplan wys chronologies wat waar en wanneer gebeur, met tye, vervoer, akkommodasie, maaltye, aktiwiteite, kontaknommers en koste.","en":"An itinerary shows chronologically what happens where and when, with times, transport, accommodation, meals, activities, contact numbers and costs."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die maksimum spoedgrens op 'n vrypad (snelweg) in Suid-Afrika is ___ km/h.","en":"The maximum speed limit on a freeway in South Africa is ___ km/h."},"answers":{"af":["120","120 km/h"],"en":["120","120 km/h"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["100","80","140"],"en":["100","80","140"]}},"explain":{"af":"Op vryweë is die grens 120 km/h; op ander openbare paaie buite stedelike gebiede 100 km/h en in stedelike gebiede 60 km/h.","en":"On freeways the limit is 120 km/h; on other public roads outside urban areas 100 km/h and in urban areas 60 km/h."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n afstandstabel lees jy die afstand af waar die ry van een dorp en die kolom van die ander dorp kruis.","en":"In a distance table you read the distance where the row of one town and the column of the other town meet."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die tabel is ook simmetries, dus maak dit nie saak watter dorp jy in die ry kies nie.","en":"True. The table is also symmetrical, so it does not matter which town you choose for the row."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die algemene spoedgrens op openbare paaie buite stedelike gebiede (nie vryweë nie)?","en":"What is the general speed limit on public roads outside urban areas (not freeways)?"},"options":[{"af":"60 km/h","en":"60 km/h"},{"af":"80 km/h","en":"80 km/h"},{"af":"100 km/h","en":"100 km/h"},{"af":"120 km/h","en":"120 km/h"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Buite stedelike gebiede is dit 100 km/h. 60 km/h geld in dorpe en stede, en 120 km/h op vryweë.","en":"Outside urban areas it is 100 km/h. 60 km/h applies in towns and cities, and 120 km/h on freeways."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Bus ry 480 km teen 'n gemiddelde spoed van 80 km/h. Die reis duur ___ uur.","en":"A bus travels 480 km at an average speed of 80 km/h. The journey takes ___ hours."},"answers":{"af":["6","6 h","6 uur","ses"],"en":["6","6 h","6 hours","six"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","7","8"],"en":["5","7","8"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tyd = afstand ÷ spoed = 480 ÷ 80 = 6 uur.","en":"Time = distance ÷ speed = 480 ÷ 80 = 6 hours."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een hoort NIE in 'n reisplan nie?","en":"Which one does NOT belong in an itinerary?"},"options":[{"af":"Vertrek- en aankomstye","en":"Departure and arrival times"},{"af":"Akkommodasie vir elke nag","en":"Accommodation for every night"},{"af":"Kontaknommers vir noodgevalle","en":"Contact numbers for emergencies"},{"af":"Die pryse van hotelle wat die gesin nie bespreek het nie","en":"The prices of hotels the family did not book"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Reisplan bevat net inligting oor die reis self. Hotelle wat nie bespreek is nie, is nie deel van die plan nie.","en":"An itinerary contains only information about the trip itself. Hotels that were not booked are not part of the plan."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe skryf jy kwart voor vier in die middag (3:45 nm) in die 24-uurformaat?","en":"How do you write a quarter to four in the afternoon (3:45 pm) in 24-hour format?"},"options":[{"af":"15:45","en":"15:45"},{"af":"03:45","en":"03:45"},{"af":"13:45","en":"13:45"},{"af":"16:45","en":"16:45"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná 12:00 tel jy 12 by: 3:45 nm + 12 h = 15:45. 03:45 is in die vroeë oggend.","en":"After 12:00 you add 12: 3:45 pm + 12 h = 15:45. 03:45 is early in the morning."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Afstandstabel gee: Brits–Pretoria 60 km, Pretoria–eMalahleni 110 km en eMalahleni–Mbombela 220 km. Hoe ver is dit van Brits na Mbombela langs hierdie roete?","en":"A distance table gives: Brits–Pretoria 60 km, Pretoria–eMalahleni 110 km and eMalahleni–Mbombela 220 km. How far is it from Brits to Mbombela along this route?"},"options":[{"af":"330 km","en":"330 km"},{"af":"220 km","en":"220 km"},{"af":"500 km","en":"500 km"},{"af":"390 km","en":"390 km"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Tel die skofte bymekaar: 60 + 110 + 220 = 390 km. 330 km is die afstand van Pretoria af; 500 km gaan tot by Komatipoort.","en":"Add the legs: 60 + 110 + 220 = 390 km. 330 km is the distance from Pretoria; 500 km goes all the way to Komatipoort."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Afstandstabel","en":"Distance table"},"r":{"af":"Gee die km tussen pare dorpe","en":"Gives the km between pairs of towns"}},{"l":{"af":"Reisplan","en":"Itinerary"},"r":{"af":"Dag-vir-dag-plan met tye, vervoer en akkommodasie","en":"Day-by-day plan with times, transport and accommodation"}},{"l":{"af":"Gemiddelde spoed","en":"Average speed"},"r":{"af":"Afstand ÷ tyd","en":"Distance ÷ time"}},{"l":{"af":"Brandstofverbruik","en":"Fuel consumption"},"r":{"af":"Liter per 100 km","en":"Litres per 100 km"}},{"l":{"af":"Tydtafel (rooster)","en":"Timetable"},"r":{"af":"Lys van vertrek- en aankomstye","en":"List of departure and arrival times"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie terme is die gereedskap van reisbeplanning: afstand (tabel), tyd (spoed en rooster), koste (verbruik) en die finale plan (reisplan).","en":"These terms are the tools of trip planning: distance (table), time (speed and timetable), cost (consumption) and the final plan (itinerary)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"2,5 uur = 2 uur en ___ minute.","en":"2.5 hours = 2 hours and ___ minutes."},"answers":{"af":["30","30 min","30 minute"],"en":["30","30 min","30 minutes"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["50","25","15"],"en":["50","25","15"]}},"explain":{"af":"0,5 h × 60 = 30 min. Die fout '50' kom van die gedagte dat 'n uur 100 minute het.","en":"0.5 h × 60 = 30 min. The mistake '50' comes from thinking an hour has 100 minutes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"4,75 uur is dieselfde as 4 uur en 75 minute.","en":"4.75 hours is the same as 4 hours and 75 minutes."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 0,75 × 60 = 45 minute, dus 4,75 h = 4 h 45 min.","en":"False. 0.75 × 60 = 45 minutes, so 4.75 h = 4 h 45 min."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Motor ry 350 km en gebruik 8 ℓ/100 km. Petrol kos R22,00 per liter. Wat is die brandstofkoste?","en":"A car travels 350 km and uses 8 ℓ/100 km. Petrol costs R22.00 per litre. What is the fuel cost?"},"options":[{"af":"R962,50","en":"R962.50"},{"af":"R616,00","en":"R616.00"},{"af":"R308,00","en":"R308.00"},{"af":"R61 600,00","en":"R61 600.00"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Liter = 350 ÷ 100 × 8 = 28 ℓ; koste = 28 × R22,00 = R616,00. R962,50 kom van 350 ÷ 8, en R61 600 van vergeet om deur 100 te deel.","en":"Litres = 350 ÷ 100 × 8 = 28 ℓ; cost = 28 × R22.00 = R616.00. R962.50 comes from 350 ÷ 8, and R61 600 from forgetting to divide by 100."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Bus vertrek om 07:30 en kom om 09:15 aan. Die rit duur ___ minute.","en":"A bus departs at 07:30 and arrives at 09:15. The trip takes ___ minutes."},"answers":{"af":["105","105 min","105 minute"],"en":["105","105 min","105 minutes"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["185","145","75"],"en":["185","145","75"]}},"explain":{"af":"07:30 tot 09:00 = 90 min, plus 15 min = 105 min (1 h 45 min). '185' kom van 9,15 − 7,30 as desimale.","en":"07:30 to 09:00 = 90 min, plus 15 min = 105 min (1 h 45 min). '185' comes from 9.15 − 7.30 as decimals."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin vertrek om 06:00 uit Brits en ry 500 km teen 'n gemiddelde spoed van 80 km/h. Hulle hou twee russtoppe van 20 minute elk. Hoe laat kom hulle aan?","en":"A family leaves Brits at 06:00 and drives 500 km at an average speed of 80 km/h. They make two rest stops of 20 minutes each. What time do they arrive?"},"options":[{"af":"12:15","en":"12:15"},{"af":"13:05","en":"13:05"},{"af":"12:55","en":"12:55"},{"af":"12:35","en":"12:35"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"500 ÷ 80 = 6,25 h = 6 h 15 min; plus 40 min stoppe = 6 h 55 min; 06:00 + 6 h 55 min = 12:55. 12:15 vergeet die stoppe; 13:05 lees 6,25 h as 6 h 25 min.","en":"500 ÷ 80 = 6.25 h = 6 h 15 min; plus 40 min of stops = 6 h 55 min; 06:00 + 6 h 55 min = 12:55. 12:15 forgets the stops; 13:05 reads 6.25 h as 6 h 25 min."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die gesin ry van Brits na Komatipoort (500 km) en terug. Die motor gebruik 8 ℓ/100 km en petrol kos R22,00 per liter. Die totale brandstofkoste is R___.","en":"The family drives from Brits to Komatipoort (500 km) and back. The car uses 8 ℓ/100 km and petrol costs R22.00 per litre. The total fuel cost is R___."},"answers":{"af":["1760","1 760","1760,00","1 760,00","R1760","R1 760","R1760,00","R1 760,00"],"en":["1760","1 760","1760.00","1 760.00","R1760","R1 760","R1760.00","R1 760.00"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R880","R2 750","R3 520"],"en":["R880","R2 750","R3 520"]}},"explain":{"af":"Heen en terug = 1 000 km; liter = 1 000 ÷ 100 × 8 = 80 ℓ; koste = 80 × R22,00 = R1 760,00. R880 is net die heenrit.","en":"There and back = 1 000 km; litres = 1 000 ÷ 100 × 8 = 80 ℓ; cost = 80 × R22.00 = R1 760.00. R880 is only the trip there."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inskrywing in hierdie dagreisplan is onrealisties?","en":"Which entry in this day itinerary is unrealistic?"},"options":[{"af":"07:00–07:20: ontbyt by die gastehuis","en":"07:00–07:20: breakfast at the guest house"},{"af":"07:30: vertrek na die Pilanesberg, 90 km ver; aankoms 09:00","en":"07:30: depart for the Pilanesberg, 90 km away; arrive 09:00"},{"af":"09:00–12:00: wildrit in die Pilanesberg","en":"09:00–12:00: game drive in the Pilanesberg"},{"af":"12:15: vertrek na 'n gastehuis 300 km ver; aankoms 14:15","en":"12:15: depart for a guest house 300 km away; arrive 14:15"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"300 km in 2 h = 150 km/h – bo die vrypad-grens van 120 km/h. Teen 'n realistiese 100 km/h duur dit 3 h, dus aankoms om 15:15. Die 90 km in 1,5 h is 60 km/h en heeltemal realisties.","en":"300 km in 2 h = 150 km/h – above the freeway limit of 120 km/h. At a realistic 100 km/h it takes 3 h, so arrival at 15:15. The 90 km in 1.5 h is 60 km/h and quite realistic."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t2-binnelandse-toerisme","title":{"af":"Binnelandse, streeks- en internasionale toerisme","en":"Domestic, regional and international tourism"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal binnelandse, streeks- en internasionale reis kan onderskei, die voordele en struikelblokke van binnelandse toerisme kan verduidelik en toerismestatistiek kan interpreteer.","en":"You will be able to distinguish domestic, regional and international travel, explain the benefits and barriers of domestic tourism and interpret tourism statistics."},"summary":{"af":"## Kernbegrippe\n\n| Begrip | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Binnelandse toerisme** | Inwoners van Suid-Afrika wat **binne** Suid-Afrika reis | 'n Gesin van Brits hou vakansie in Durban |\n| **Streekstoerisme** | Reis binne die **streek** (SAOG-lande of Afrika) | 'n Toeris uit Botswana doen inkopies in Pretoria |\n| **Internasionale toerisme** | Reis tussen lande buite die streek | 'n Britse toeris besoek Kaapstad |\n| **Inkomende toerisme** | Buitelanders wat Suid-Afrika **binnekom** | Duitse toeriste in die Krugerwildtuin |\n| **Uitgaande toerisme** | Suid-Afrikaners wat na die **buiteland** reis | 'n Paartjie van Pretoria vlieg na Mauritius |\n\n> **Wenk:** Inkomend en uitgaande hang af van wie se land jy as vertrekpunt gebruik. Vir Suid-Afrika is 'n Brit in Kaapstad *inkomend*.\n\n### Intra- teenoor interprovinsiaal\n\n- **Intraprovinsiale reis:** binne **dieselfde** provinsie, bv. Brits → Pilanesberg (albei in Noordwes).\n- **Interprovinsiale reis:** **tussen** provinsies, bv. Brits → Krugerwildtuin (Mpumalanga).\n\n> **Onthou!** *Intra* = binne (soos 'n intranet binne 'n maatskappy); *inter* = tussen (soos 'n interskole-wedstryd).\n\n## Voordele van binnelandse toerisme\n\n**Ekonomie:**\n- Skep **werk** en inkomste, ook in klein dorpies en plattelandse gebiede.\n- **Vermenigvuldigingseffek:** geld wat 'n toeris spandeer, word weer en weer in die plaaslike ekonomie bestee (die lodge betaal die werker, die werker koop by die plaaslike winkel …).\n- Maak toerisme **minder seisoenaal**: Suid-Afrikaners reis in langnaweke en skoolvakansies, ook wanneer daar min buitelandse toeriste is.\n- Die bedryf is minder afhanklik van buitelandse toeriste.\n\n**Mense:** ontspanning en rus; leer meer van jou eie land en sy kulture; bou **nasionale trots** en eenheid.\n\n**Omgewing:** toegangsgeld na parke en reservate betaal vir **bewaring**; mense leer om die natuur te waardeer.\n\n## Struikelblokke\n\n- **Koste** – verblyf, brandstof en vlugte is duur vir baie gesinne.\n- **Tyd** – te min verlof of werk oor naweke.\n- **Gebrek aan inligting** – mense weet nie van bekostigbare plekke naby hulle nie.\n- **Veiligheid** – vrees vir misdaad en onveilige paaie.\n- **Vervoer** – geen eie motor nie en beperkte openbare vervoer.\n\n## Sho't Left\n\n**Sho't Left** is SA Toerisme se binnelandse veldtog wat Suid-Afrikaners aanmoedig om **bekostigbare kort uitstappies naby die huis** te neem. Ander maniere om plaaslike reis aan te moedig: laagseisoen-spesiale, afbetaalplanne, gesinspakkette met vervoer ingesluit, en bemarking op radio en sosiale media in verskillende tale.\n\n## Seisoene en openbare vakansiedae\n\n- **Hoogseisoen (spitsseisoen):** skoolvakansies (veral Desember–Januarie), Paasfees en langnaweke – vol, duurder en besig.\n- **Laagseisoen (buiteseisoen):** gedurende skoolkwartale – stiller en goedkoper, met spesiale aanbiedinge.\n\n| Vakansiedag | Datum |\n|---|---|\n| Menseregtedag | 21 Maart |\n| Vryheidsdag | 27 April |\n| Werkersdag | 1 Mei |\n| Jeugdag | 16 Junie |\n| Nasionale Vrouedag | 9 Augustus |\n| Erfenisdag | 24 September |\n| Versoeningsdag | 16 Desember |\n\nAs 'n openbare vakansiedag op 'n **Sondag** val, is die **Maandag** daarna 'n vakansiedag. 'n Vakansiedag op 'n Vrydag of Maandag gee 'n **langnaweek** – 'n hoogtepunt vir binnelandse toerisme.\n\n## Statistiek lees en bereken\n\nVolgens Stats SA is **besoeke aan vriende en familie (VFR)** tradisioneel die grootste rede vir binnelandse reise in Suid-Afrika. In die eksamen kry jy 'n tabel of grafiek oor die doel van reise, provinsies, verblyfduur, besteding of seisoene. Gebruik **slegs die gegewe data**.\n\n- `Persentasie = deel ÷ totaal × 100`\n- `Verskil = groter waarde − kleiner waarde`\n- `Persentasieverandering = (nuut − oud) ÷ oud × 100`\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders lees die verkeerde kolom of jaar. Onderstreep die kolomopskrif en die eenheid (duisende? miljoene? rand?) voordat jy bereken.\n\n## Streekstoerisme en die SAOG\n\nDie **Suider-Afrikaanse Ontwikkelingsgemeenskap (SAOG/SADC)** het **16 lidlande** en sy hoofkantoor is in **Gaborone**, Botswana. Streekstoerisme is belangrik omdat die meeste buitelandse besoekers aan Suid-Afrika uit SAOG-lande kom (vir inkopies, sake en familiebesoeke). Samewerking maak reis oor grense makliker en skep oorgrens-bewaringsgebiede, soos die Kgalagadi-oorgrenspark (Suid-Afrika en Botswana).","en":"## Key concepts\n\n| Concept | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Domestic tourism** | Residents of South Africa travelling **within** South Africa | A family from Brits holidays in Durban |\n| **Regional tourism** | Travel within the **region** (SADC countries or Africa) | A tourist from Botswana shops in Pretoria |\n| **International tourism** | Travel between countries outside the region | A British tourist visits Cape Town |\n| **Inbound tourism** | Foreigners **entering** South Africa | German tourists in the Kruger National Park |\n| **Outbound tourism** | South Africans travelling **abroad** | A couple from Pretoria flies to Mauritius |\n\n> **Tip:** Inbound and outbound depend on whose country you use as the starting point. For South Africa a British tourist in Cape Town is *inbound*.\n\n### Intra- versus inter-provincial\n\n- **Intra-provincial travel:** within the **same** province, e.g. Brits → Pilanesberg (both in North West).\n- **Inter-provincial travel:** **between** provinces, e.g. Brits → Kruger National Park (Mpumalanga).\n\n> **Remember!** *Intra* = within (like a company's intranet); *inter* = between (like an inter-schools match).\n\n## Benefits of domestic tourism\n\n**Economy:**\n- Creates **jobs** and income, also in small towns and rural areas.\n- **Multiplier effect:** money a tourist spends is spent again and again in the local economy (the lodge pays the worker, the worker buys at the local shop …).\n- Makes tourism **less seasonal**: South Africans travel on long weekends and in school holidays, also when there are few foreign tourists.\n- The industry is less dependent on foreign tourists.\n\n**People:** relaxation and rest; learning more about your own country and its cultures; building **national pride** and unity.\n\n**Environment:** entrance fees to parks and reserves pay for **conservation**; people learn to value nature.\n\n## Barriers\n\n- **Cost** – accommodation, fuel and flights are expensive for many families.\n- **Time** – too little leave or working on weekends.\n- **Lack of information** – people don't know about affordable places near them.\n- **Safety** – fear of crime and unsafe roads.\n- **Transport** – no own car and limited public transport.\n\n## Sho't Left\n\n**Sho't Left** is SA Tourism's domestic campaign that encourages South Africans to take **affordable short breaks close to home**. Other ways to encourage local travel: off-peak specials, payment plans, family packages with transport included, and marketing on radio and social media in different languages.\n\n## Seasons and public holidays\n\n- **Peak (high) season:** school holidays (especially December–January), Easter and long weekends – full, more expensive and busy.\n- **Off-peak (low) season:** during school terms – quieter and cheaper, with special offers.\n\n| Public holiday | Date |\n|---|---|\n| Human Rights Day | 21 March |\n| Freedom Day | 27 April |\n| Workers' Day | 1 May |\n| Youth Day | 16 June |\n| National Women's Day | 9 August |\n| Heritage Day | 24 September |\n| Day of Reconciliation | 16 December |\n\nIf a public holiday falls on a **Sunday**, the **Monday** after it is a holiday. A holiday on a Friday or Monday gives a **long weekend** – a highlight for domestic tourism.\n\n## Reading and calculating statistics\n\nAccording to Stats SA, **visiting friends and relatives (VFR)** is traditionally the biggest reason for domestic trips in South Africa. In the exam you get a table or graph on the purpose of trips, provinces, length of stay, spending or seasons. Use **only the given data**.\n\n- `Percentage = part ÷ total × 100`\n- `Difference = bigger value − smaller value`\n- `Percentage change = (new − old) ÷ old × 100`\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners read the wrong column or year. Underline the column heading and the unit (thousands? millions? rand?) before you calculate.\n\n## Regional tourism and SADC\n\nThe **Southern African Development Community (SADC)** has **16 member states** and its headquarters is in **Gaborone**, Botswana. Regional tourism matters because most foreign visitors to South Africa come from SADC countries (for shopping, business and visiting family). Co-operation makes cross-border travel easier and creates transfrontier conservation areas, such as the Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park (South Africa and Botswana)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Binnelandse toerisme","en":"Domestic tourism"},"def":{"af":"Inwoners van 'n land wat binne hul eie land reis, bv. Suid-Afrikaners wat in Suid-Afrika reis.","en":"Residents of a country travelling within their own country, e.g. South Africans travelling in South Africa."}},{"term":{"af":"Streekstoerisme","en":"Regional tourism"},"def":{"af":"Reis tussen lande in dieselfde streek, bv. binne die SAOG of Afrika.","en":"Travel between countries in the same region, e.g. within SADC or Africa."}},{"term":{"af":"Internasionale toerisme","en":"International tourism"},"def":{"af":"Reis na 'n ander land buite jou eie streek.","en":"Travel to another country outside your own region."}},{"term":{"af":"Inkomende toerisme","en":"Inbound tourism"},"def":{"af":"Buitelandse toeriste wat 'n land binnekom en besoek.","en":"Foreign tourists entering and visiting a country."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitgaande toerisme","en":"Outbound tourism"},"def":{"af":"Inwoners van 'n land wat na die buiteland reis.","en":"Residents of a country travelling abroad."}},{"term":{"af":"Intraprovinsiale reis","en":"Intra-provincial travel"},"def":{"af":"Reis binne dieselfde provinsie.","en":"Travel within the same province."}},{"term":{"af":"Interprovinsiale reis","en":"Inter-provincial travel"},"def":{"af":"Reis van een provinsie na 'n ander.","en":"Travel from one province to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Vermenigvuldigingseffek","en":"Multiplier effect"},"def":{"af":"Toeriste se besteding word herhaaldelik in die plaaslike ekonomie spandeer en skep so meer inkomste en werk.","en":"Tourist spending is spent again and again in the local economy, creating more income and jobs."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoogseisoen en laagseisoen","en":"Peak and off-peak season"},"def":{"af":"Hoogseisoen: besige tye met hoë pryse (skoolvakansies, langnaweke). Laagseisoen: stil tye met laer pryse.","en":"Peak season: busy times with high prices (school holidays, long weekends). Off-peak season: quiet times with lower prices."}},{"term":{"af":"Sho't Left","en":"Sho't Left"},"def":{"af":"SA Toerisme se veldtog wat Suid-Afrikaners aanmoedig om bekostigbare kort uitstappies naby die huis te neem.","en":"SA Tourism's campaign that encourages South Africans to take affordable short breaks close to home."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer die reis","en":"Classify the trip"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elke reis vanuit Suid-Afrika se oogpunt: (a) 'n Gesin van Brits gaan vir 'n naweek na Pilanesberg. (b) 'n Student van Pretoria besoek haar ouma in Kaapstad. (c) 'n Inwoner van Zimbabwe kom koop klere in Musina. (d) 'n Paartjie van Hartbeespoort vlieg na Mauritius.","en":"Classify each trip from South Africa's point of view: (a) A family from Brits goes to Pilanesberg for a weekend. (b) A student from Pretoria visits her grandmother in Cape Town. (c) A resident of Zimbabwe comes to buy clothes in Musina. (d) A couple from Hartbeespoort flies to Mauritius."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Suid-Afrikaners binne Suid-Afrika = **binnelands**. Brits en Pilanesberg is albei in Noordwes = **intraprovinsiaal**.","en":"(a) South Africans within South Africa = **domestic**. Brits and Pilanesberg are both in North West = **intra-provincial**."},{"af":"(b) **Binnelands** en **interprovinsiaal** (Gauteng → Wes-Kaap). Die doel is VFR (besoek aan familie).","en":"(b) **Domestic** and **inter-provincial** (Gauteng → Western Cape). The purpose is VFR (visiting relatives)."},{"af":"(c) Zimbabwe is 'n SAOG-land, dus **streekstoerisme** en **inkomend** vir Suid-Afrika (doel: inkopies).","en":"(c) Zimbabwe is a SADC country, so **regional tourism** and **inbound** for South Africa (purpose: shopping)."},{"af":"(d) Mauritius is ook 'n SAOG-lid, dus **streekstoerisme** en **uitgaande** vir Suid-Afrika.","en":"(d) Mauritius is also a SADC member, so **regional tourism** and **outbound** for South Africa."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) binnelands, intraprovinsiaal (b) binnelands, interprovinsiaal (c) streeks, inkomend (d) streeks, uitgaande","en":"(a) domestic, intra-provincial (b) domestic, inter-provincial (c) regional, inbound (d) regional, outbound"}},{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer 'n statistiektabel","en":"Interpret a statistics table"},"problem":{"af":"Bron (oefendata, nie werklike statistiek nie): Doel van binnelandse reise in 'n provinsie, in duisende.\n\n| Doel | Reise (duisende) |\n|---|---|\n| VFR | 1 040 |\n| Vakansie/ontspanning | 360 |\n| Godsdienstig | 260 |\n| Sake | 180 |\n| Medies | 80 |\n| Ander | 80 |\n| **Totaal** | **2 000** |\n\n(a) Wat is die algemeenste doel? (b) Watter persentasie van die reise was VFR? (c) Hoeveel meer vakansiereise as sakereise was daar?","en":"Source (practice data, not real statistics): Purpose of domestic trips in a province, in thousands.\n\n| Purpose | Trips (thousands) |\n|---|---|\n| VFR | 1 040 |\n| Holiday/leisure | 360 |\n| Religious | 260 |\n| Business | 180 |\n| Medical | 80 |\n| Other | 80 |\n| **Total** | **2 000** |\n\n(a) What is the most common purpose? (b) What percentage of the trips were VFR? (c) How many more holiday trips than business trips were there?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die grootste getal is 1 040 duisend: **VFR** (besoek aan vriende en familie).","en":"(a) The biggest number is 1 040 thousand: **VFR** (visiting friends and relatives)."},{"af":"(b) Persentasie = deel ÷ totaal × 100 = 1 040 ÷ 2 000 × 100 = **52%**.","en":"(b) Percentage = part ÷ total × 100 = 1 040 ÷ 2 000 × 100 = **52%**."},{"af":"(c) Verskil = 360 − 180 = 180 duisend = **180 000** reise meer. Onthou die eenheid is duisende!","en":"(c) Difference = 360 − 180 = 180 thousand = **180 000** more trips. Remember the unit is thousands!"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) VFR (b) 52% (c) 180 000 meer vakansiereise","en":"(a) VFR (b) 52% (c) 180 000 more holiday trips"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken persentasieverandering","en":"Calculate percentage change"},"problem":{"af":"'n Lodge naby Hartbeespoortdam het in Mei verlede jaar 240 gaste gehad. Hierdie Mei, ná 'n Sho't Left-laagseisoenspesiale, het hy 300 gaste gehad (oefendata). Bereken die persentasieverandering en verduidelik wat dit vir die lodge beteken.","en":"A lodge near Hartbeespoort Dam had 240 guests in May last year. This May, after a Sho't Left off-peak special, it had 300 guests (practice data). Calculate the percentage change and explain what it means for the lodge."},"steps":[{"af":"Formule: persentasieverandering = (nuut − oud) ÷ oud × 100.","en":"Formula: percentage change = (new − old) ÷ old × 100."},{"af":"Vervang: (300 − 240) ÷ 240 × 100 = 60 ÷ 240 × 100.","en":"Substitute: (300 − 240) ÷ 240 × 100 = 60 ÷ 240 × 100."},{"af":"= 0,25 × 100 = **25% toename**. Deel deur die **ou** waarde (240), nie die nuwe nie.","en":"= 0.25 × 100 = **25% increase**. Divide by the **old** value (240), not the new one."},{"af":"Betekenis: die spesiale het meer binnelandse toeriste in die stil seisoen gelok – meer inkomste en werk, en minder seisoenaliteit.","en":"Meaning: the special attracted more domestic tourists in the quiet season – more income and jobs, and less seasonality."}],"answer":{"af":"25% toename","en":"25% increase"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik en stel voor","en":"Explain and suggest"},"problem":{"af":"Thandi (Brits) verdien 'n klein salaris, het nie 'n motor nie en weet nie van bekostigbare vakansieplekke nie. (a) Noem die struikelblokke. (b) Stel drie maniere voor om mense soos Thandi aan te moedig om binnelands te reis.","en":"Thandi (Brits) earns a small salary, has no car and doesn't know about affordable holiday places. (a) Name the barriers. (b) Suggest three ways to encourage people like Thandi to travel domestically."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Lees die bron noukeurig: klein salaris = **koste**; geen motor = **vervoer**; weet nie van plekke nie = **gebrek aan inligting**.","en":"(a) Read the source carefully: small salary = **cost**; no car = **transport**; doesn't know about places = **lack of information**."},{"af":"(b) Koppel elke voorstel aan 'n struikelblok: **laagseisoen-spesiale en afbetaalplanne** (koste).","en":"(b) Link each suggestion to a barrier: **off-peak specials and payment plans** (cost)."},{"af":"**Pakkette met veilige vervoer ingesluit**, bv. 'n bus van Brits na die bestemming (vervoer).","en":"**Packages with safe transport included**, e.g. a bus from Brits to the destination (transport)."},{"af":"**Sho't Left-bemarking** op plaaslike radio, sosiale media en by die toerismekantoor (inligting).","en":"**Sho't Left marketing** on local radio, social media and at the tourism office (information)."}],"answer":{"af":"Struikelblokke: koste, vervoer, gebrek aan inligting. Voorstelle: spesiale/afbetaling, pakkette met vervoer, Sho't Left-bemarking.","en":"Barriers: cost, transport, lack of information. Suggestions: specials/payment plans, packages with transport, Sho't Left marketing."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is binnelandse toerisme?","en":"What is domestic tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Inwoners van Suid-Afrika wat binne Suid-Afrika reis","en":"Residents of South Africa travelling within South Africa"},{"af":"Buitelanders wat Suid-Afrika besoek","en":"Foreigners visiting South Africa"},{"af":"Suid-Afrikaners wat na SAOG-lande reis","en":"South Africans travelling to SADC countries"},{"af":"Reis tussen twee buitelandse lande","en":"Travel between two foreign countries"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Binnelands = binne jou eie land. Buitelanders in Suid-Afrika is inkomende toeriste, en reis na SAOG-lande is streekstoerisme.","en":"Domestic = within your own country. Foreigners in South Africa are inbound tourists, and travel to SADC countries is regional tourism."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoofkantoor van die SAOG is in ___.","en":"The headquarters of SADC is in ___."},"answers":{"af":["Gaborone"],"en":["Gaborone"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Pretoria","Harare","Windhoek"],"en":["Pretoria","Harare","Windhoek"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die SAOG se hoofkantoor is in Gaborone, die hoofstad van Botswana.","en":"SADC's headquarters is in Gaborone, the capital of Botswana."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jeugdag word op 16 Junie gevier.","en":"Youth Day is celebrated on 16 June."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jeugdag is op 16 Junie. Openbare vakansiedae skep langnaweke wat binnelandse toerisme 'n hupstoot gee.","en":"True. Youth Day is on 16 June. Public holidays create long weekends that boost domestic tourism."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter reis is 'n voorbeeld van intraprovinsiale reis?","en":"Which trip is an example of intra-provincial travel?"},"options":[{"af":"Brits na die Krugerwildtuin","en":"Brits to the Kruger National Park"},{"af":"Pretoria na Kaapstad","en":"Pretoria to Cape Town"},{"af":"Brits na Pilanesberg","en":"Brits to Pilanesberg"},{"af":"Johannesburg na Durban","en":"Johannesburg to Durban"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Brits en Pilanesberg is albei in Noordwes – binne dieselfde provinsie. Die ander reise gaan oor provinsiale grense (interprovinsiaal).","en":"Brits and Pilanesberg are both in North West – within the same province. The other trips cross provincial borders (inter-provincial)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die SAOG het ___ lidlande.","en":"SADC has ___ member states."},"answers":{"af":["16","sestien"],"en":["16","sixteen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["15","12","54"],"en":["15","12","54"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die SAOG het 16 lidlande. (54 is die aantal lande in Afrika – 'n algemene verwarring.)","en":"SADC has 16 member states. (54 is the number of countries in Africa – a common confusion.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is volgens Stats SA tradisioneel die grootste rede vir binnelandse reise in Suid-Afrika?","en":"According to Stats SA, what is traditionally the biggest reason for domestic trips in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"Sake","en":"Business"},{"af":"Besoeke aan vriende en familie (VFR)","en":"Visiting friends and relatives (VFR)"},{"af":"Vakansie by die see","en":"Beach holidays"},{"af":"Mediese behandeling","en":"Medical treatment"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"VFR is tradisioneel die grootste rede. Baie Suid-Afrikaners reis byvoorbeeld in Desember en met Paasfees huis toe na familie.","en":"VFR is traditionally the biggest reason. Many South Africans, for example, travel home to family in December and at Easter."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"SA Toerisme se binnelandse veldtog vir bekostigbare kort uitstappies naby die huis heet ___.","en":"SA Tourism's domestic campaign for affordable short breaks close to home is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["Sho't Left","Shot Left","Short Left"],"en":["Sho't Left","Shot Left","Short Left"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Proudly SA","Ubuntu","Big Five"],"en":["Proudly SA","Ubuntu","Big Five"]}},"explain":{"af":"Sho't Left (straattaal vir 'n kort ritjie) moedig Suid-Afrikaners aan om naby die huis te toer.","en":"Sho't Left (street slang for a short trip) encourages South Africans to tour close to home."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op watter datum is Erfenisdag?","en":"On which date is Heritage Day?"},"options":[{"af":"16 Desember","en":"16 December"},{"af":"9 Augustus","en":"9 August"},{"af":"27 April","en":"27 April"},{"af":"24 September","en":"24 September"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Erfenisdag is op 24 September. 16 Desember is Versoeningsdag, 9 Augustus Nasionale Vrouedag en 27 April Vryheidsdag.","en":"Heritage Day is on 24 September. 16 December is the Day of Reconciliation, 9 August National Women's Day and 27 April Freedom Day."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As 'n openbare vakansiedag op 'n Sondag val, is die Maandag daarna 'n openbare vakansiedag.","en":"If a public holiday falls on a Sunday, the Monday after it is a public holiday."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit gee 'n langnaweek, wat baie Suid-Afrikaners gebruik om binnelands te reis.","en":"True. This gives a long weekend, which many South Africans use to travel domestically."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe help binnelandse toerisme om seisoenaliteit in die bedryf te verminder?","en":"How does domestic tourism help to reduce seasonality in the industry?"},"options":[{"af":"Suid-Afrikaners reis ook in langnaweke en skoolvakansies wanneer daar min buitelanders is, sodat besighede meer van die jaar inkomste kry.","en":"South Africans also travel on long weekends and in school holidays when there are few foreigners, so businesses earn income for more of the year."},{"af":"Dit maak pryse in die hoogseisoen nog hoër.","en":"It makes prices in peak season even higher."},{"af":"Dit keer dat buitelandse toeriste in die somer kom.","en":"It stops foreign tourists from coming in summer."},{"af":"Dit beteken dat besighede in die winter kan sluit.","en":"It means businesses can close in winter."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Seisoenaliteit beteken besighede is net in sekere tye besig. Binnelandse toeriste vul die stil tye en hou werk die hele jaar aan die gang.","en":"Seasonality means businesses are busy only at certain times. Domestic tourists fill the quiet times and keep jobs going all year."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas die openbare vakansiedag by die datum.","en":"Match the public holiday to the date."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Menseregtedag","en":"Human Rights Day"},"r":{"af":"21 Maart","en":"21 March"}},{"l":{"af":"Vryheidsdag","en":"Freedom Day"},"r":{"af":"27 April","en":"27 April"}},{"l":{"af":"Werkersdag","en":"Workers' Day"},"r":{"af":"1 Mei","en":"1 May"}},{"l":{"af":"Nasionale Vrouedag","en":"National Women's Day"},"r":{"af":"9 Augustus","en":"9 August"}},{"l":{"af":"Versoeningsdag","en":"Day of Reconciliation"},"r":{"af":"16 Desember","en":"16 December"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die datums in volgorde deur die jaar: 21 Mrt, 27 Apr, 1 Mei, 16 Jun, 9 Aug, 24 Sep, 16 Des.","en":"Learn the dates in order through the year: 21 Mar, 27 Apr, 1 May, 16 Jun, 9 Aug, 24 Sep, 16 Dec."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Toeris uit Botswana wat in Pretoria kom inkopies doen, is 'n voorbeeld van ___ toerisme.","en":"A tourist from Botswana who comes to shop in Pretoria is an example of ___ tourism."},"answers":{"af":["streeks","streeks-","streekstoerisme","inkomende"],"en":["regional","inbound"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["binnelandse","uitgaande","intraprovinsiale"],"en":["domestic","outbound","intra-provincial"]}},"explain":{"af":"Botswana is 'n SAOG-land, dus is dit streekstoerisme – en vir Suid-Afrika is dit inkomend. Dit is nie binnelands nie, want die toeris woon nie in Suid-Afrika nie.","en":"Botswana is a SADC country, so this is regional tourism – and for South Africa it is inbound. It is not domestic, because the tourist doesn't live in South Africa."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n opname (oefendata) was 600 van 1 500 binnelandse reise interprovinsiaal. Watter persentasie van die reise was intraprovinsiaal?","en":"In a survey (practice data) 600 of 1 500 domestic trips were inter-provincial. What percentage of the trips were intra-provincial?"},"options":[{"af":"40%","en":"40%"},{"af":"60%","en":"60%"},{"af":"90%","en":"90%"},{"af":"150%","en":"150%"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Intraprovinsiaal = 1 500 − 600 = 900. 900 ÷ 1 500 × 100 = 60%. 40% is die interprovinsiale reise – lees die vraag mooi.","en":"Intra-provincial = 1 500 − 600 = 900. 900 ÷ 1 500 × 100 = 60%. 40% is the inter-provincial trips – read the question carefully."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bron (oefendata): Provinsie X het 3,2 miljoen binnelandse reise ontvang en Provinsie Y 2,4 miljoen. Provinsie X het ___ miljoen reise meer ontvang.","en":"Source (practice data): Province X received 3.2 million domestic trips and Province Y 2.4 million. Province X received ___ million more trips."},"answers":{"af":["0,8","0.8","0,8 miljoen","800 000"],"en":["0.8","0,8","0.8 million","800 000"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5,6","1,2","0,6"],"en":["5.6","1.2","0.6"]}},"explain":{"af":"Verskil = 3,2 − 2,4 = 0,8 miljoen (800 000). 5,6 miljoen is die som, nie die verskil nie.","en":"Difference = 3.2 − 2.4 = 0.8 million (800 000). 5.6 million is the sum, not the difference."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi verdien min, het nie 'n motor nie en weet nie van bekostigbare plekke naby Brits nie. Watter struikelblokke vir binnelandse toerisme ervaar sy?","en":"Thandi earns little, has no car and doesn't know about affordable places near Brits. Which barriers to domestic tourism does she experience?"},"options":[{"af":"Veiligheid en te min verlof","en":"Safety and too little leave"},{"af":"Taal en visums","en":"Language and visas"},{"af":"Seisoene en die weer","en":"Seasons and the weather"},{"af":"Koste, vervoer en gebrek aan inligting","en":"Cost, transport and lack of information"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Min geld = koste; geen motor = vervoer; weet nie van plekke nie = gebrek aan inligting. Visums is nie nodig vir binnelandse reis nie.","en":"Little money = cost; no car = transport; not knowing about places = lack of information. Visas are not needed for domestic travel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorstel sal die beste help om meer mense soos Thandi aan te moedig om binnelands te reis?","en":"Which suggestion would best help to encourage more people like Thandi to travel domestically?"},"options":[{"af":"Verhoog die pryse in die hoogseisoen","en":"Raise prices in peak season"},{"af":"Bemark Suid-Afrika net in die buiteland","en":"Market South Africa only abroad"},{"af":"Laagseisoen-spesiale en afbetaalplanne, pakkette met vervoer ingesluit en bemarking op plaaslike radio","en":"Off-peak specials and payment plans, packages with transport included and marketing on local radio"},{"af":"Sluit die munisipale toerismekantore","en":"Close the municipal tourism offices"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Hierdie voorstel spreek al drie haar struikelblokke aan: koste (spesiale, afbetaling), vervoer (ingesluit) en inligting (plaaslike bemarking). Die ander opsies maak dit moeiliker.","en":"This suggestion addresses all three of her barriers: cost (specials, payment plans), transport (included) and information (local marketing). The other options make it harder."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t2-betaling-valuta","title":{"af":"Betaalmetodes en buitelandse valuta","en":"Payment methods and foreign exchange"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal betaalmetodes vir toeriste kan vergelyk, verduidelik waarom buitelandse valuta belangrik is vir SA, en bedrae met wisselkoerse en kommissie korrek kan omskakel.","en":"You will be able to compare payment methods for tourists, explain why foreign exchange matters to SA, and correctly convert amounts using exchange rates and commission."},"summary":{"af":"## Betaalmetodes in toerisme\n\nToeriste en toerisme-ondernemings moet **veilig, vinnig en goedkoop** kan betaal. CAPS noem die volgende betaaltegnologie:\n\n| Metode | Hoe dit werk | Voordele | Nadele |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Internet-/aanlynbetaling (EFO/EFT)** | Geld word elektronies van een bankrekening na 'n ander oorgeplaas, bv. 'n deposito vir 'n gastehuis | Enige tyd en van enige plek; jy kry 'n bewys van betaling | Kuberbedrog (vals e-posse en webwerwe); kan 'n dag of twee neem om deur te gaan |\n| **OTM** (outomatiese tellermasjien) | Jy trek kontant met jou kaart en PIN | Kontant byna oral beskikbaar, ook in die buiteland | Bankfooie; risiko van roof en kaartbedrog |\n| **Selfoonbank, toeps en QR-kodes** (bv. SnapScan, Zapper) | Jy skandeer die QR-kode met 'n toep op jou slimfoon | Vinnig, geen kontant of kaart nodig; ideaal vir klein besighede en markstalletjies | Jy het 'n slimfoon, data en battery nodig; nie oral aanvaar nie |\n| **Snelpunt** (kaartmasjien; kontaklose tik) | Die kaart word ingesteek, geswiep of getik | Vinnig en veilig; aanvaar internasionale kaarte | Die besigheid betaal fooie; werk nie sonder netwerk of krag nie (beurtkrag!) |\n| **Debietkaart** | Die geld kom dadelik uit jou eie rekening | Jy spandeer net geld wat jy het | Jy kan nie meer as jou saldo spandeer nie |\n| **Kredietkaart** | Jy leen by die bank en betaal later terug | Wêreldwyd aanvaar; baie motorhuur- en hotelbesighede vereis dit vir 'n deposito | Rente en skuld as jy nie betyds terugbetaal nie |\n| **Tjek** | 'n Geskrewe, getekende opdrag aan jou bank om te betaal | Steeds in CAPS gelys | Stadig en maklik om te vervals; SA-banke aanvaar sedert 2021 nie meer tjeks nie |\n\n**Kriteria om 'n betaalmetode te kies:** veiligheid, koste (fooie en rente), gerief en spoed, en **aanvaarding** (aanvaar die besigheid of die land dit?).\n\n> **Wenk:** Raai 'n toeris aan om 'n kombinasie te gebruik: 'n kaart vir groot bedrae en net 'n klein bedrag kontant vir fooitjies en klein aankope.\n\n## Buitelandse valuta\n\n**Buitelandse valuta** is die geld van 'n ander land. Die **wisselkoers** is die waarde van een valuta uitgedruk in 'n ander, bv. R18,50 = US$1.\n\n### Waarom is buitelandse valuta belangrik vir SA?\n\n- Inkomende toeriste ruil hul dollars, euro en pond vir rand en spandeer dit hier, so SA **verdien buitelandse valuta** – net soos met uitvoere.\n- Die besteding **skep werk** en inkomste (akkommodasie, vervoer, gidse, kunsvlyt) en die regering kry belasting (BTW).\n- Dit help die **betalingsbalans**: meer geld vloei die land in as wat uitvloei.\n- Uitgaande toeriste (Suid-Afrikaners wat oorsee reis) neem geld uit die land uit.\n\n### Valutas, ISO-kodes en simbole\n\n| Land/gebied | Valuta | ISO-kode | Simbool |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Suid-Afrika | rand | ZAR | R |\n| VSA | Amerikaanse dollar | USD | $ |\n| Eurosone (bv. Duitsland) | euro | EUR | € |\n| Verenigde Koninkryk | pond sterling | GBP | £ |\n| Japan | jen | JPY | ¥ |\n| China | yuan (renminbi) | CNY | ¥ |\n| Australië | Australiese dollar | AUD | A$ |\n| Botswana | pula | BWP | P |\n| Namibië | Namibiese dollar | NAD | N$ |\n| Lesotho | loti | LSL | L |\n| Eswatini | lilangeni | SZL | E |\n| Mosambiek | metical | MZN | MT |\n\n> **Onthou!** In die **Gemeenskaplike Monetêre Gebied (GMG)** – Suid-Afrika, Namibië, Lesotho en Eswatini – word die rand aanvaar, en die Namibiese dollar, loti en lilangeni is 1:1 aan die rand gekoppel. Botswana is NIE deel van die GMG nie.\n\n## Omskakelings (voorbeeldkoers R18,50 = US$1)\n\n1. **Rand → buitelandse valuta: deel** deur die koers. R3 700 ÷ 18,50 = **$200,00**\n2. **Buitelandse valuta → rand: vermenigvuldig** met die koers. $150 × 18,50 = **R2 775,00**\n3. **Kommissie** is 'n fooi (gewoonlik 'n persentasie) wat die bank vra: 2% van R5 000 = 0,02 × 5 000 = **R100**. Gewoonlik trek jy dit eers van die randbedrag af en skakel dan die res om – lees die vraag mooi.\n4. Rond geldbedrae af tot **twee desimale plekke**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders vermenigvuldig wanneer hulle rand na dollar omskakel. Toets jou antwoord: met 'n koers groter as 1 kry jy altyd **minder** dollars as die getal rand.\n\n### Uitbreiding: bankverkoopkoers en bankkoopkoers\n\nBanke gee twee koerse. Dink altyd vanuit die **bank** se kant:\n\n| Koers | Wanneer? | Rigting | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bankverkoopkoers** | Die bank **verkoop** buitelandse valuta aan die toeris (voor 'n oorsese reis) | rand → buitelands | R18,80 = US$1 |\n| **Bankkoopkoers** | Die bank **koop** buitelandse valuta by die toeris (inkomende toeris, of jy ná die reis) | buitelands → rand | R18,20 = US$1 |\n\nDie verkoopkoers is altyd **hoër** as die koopkoers; die verskil is die bank se wins.\n\n### Sterk en swak rand\n\n- **Swak rand:** jy betaal *meer* rand vir een eenheid buitelandse valuta (bv. R17,00 → R19,00 per US$1). SA word goedkoper vir buitelanders, dus **meer inkomende** toeriste; oorsese reis word duurder, dus **minder uitgaande** toeriste.\n- **Sterk rand:** jy betaal *minder* rand; die teenoorgestelde gebeur.","en":"## Payment methods in tourism\n\nTourists and tourism businesses need to pay **safely, quickly and cheaply**. CAPS lists the following payment technology:\n\n| Method | How it works | Advantages | Disadvantages |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Internet/online payment (EFT)** | Money is transferred electronically from one bank account to another, e.g. a deposit for a guest house | Any time, from anywhere; you get proof of payment | Cyber fraud (fake e-mails and websites); can take a day or two to clear |\n| **ATM** (automated teller machine) | You draw cash with your card and PIN | Cash available almost everywhere, also abroad | Bank fees; risk of robbery and card fraud |\n| **Cellphone banking, apps and QR codes** (e.g. SnapScan, Zapper) | You scan the QR code with an app on your smartphone | Fast, no cash or card needed; ideal for small businesses and market stalls | You need a smartphone, data and battery; not accepted everywhere |\n| **Speed point** (card machine; contactless tap) | The card is inserted, swiped or tapped | Fast and safe; accepts international cards | The business pays fees; does not work without network or power (load-shedding!) |\n| **Debit card** | The money comes straight out of your own account | You only spend money you have | You cannot spend more than your balance |\n| **Credit card** | You borrow from the bank and pay back later | Accepted worldwide; many car-hire and hotel businesses require it for a deposit | Interest and debt if you don't repay on time |\n| **Cheque** | A written, signed instruction to your bank to pay | Still listed in CAPS | Slow and easy to forge; SA banks have not accepted cheques since 2021 |\n\n**Criteria for choosing a payment method:** safety, cost (fees and interest), convenience and speed, and **acceptance** (does the business or the country accept it?).\n\n> **Tip:** Advise a tourist to use a combination: a card for large amounts and only a small amount of cash for tips and small purchases.\n\n## Foreign exchange\n\n**Foreign exchange (foreign currency)** is the money of another country. The **exchange rate** is the value of one currency expressed in another, e.g. R18.50 = US$1.\n\n### Why is foreign exchange important to SA?\n\n- Inbound tourists exchange their dollars, euros and pounds for rand and spend them here, so SA **earns foreign exchange** – just like with exports.\n- The spending **creates jobs** and income (accommodation, transport, guides, crafts) and the government earns tax (VAT).\n- It helps the **balance of payments**: more money flows into the country than flows out.\n- Outbound tourists (South Africans travelling abroad) take money out of the country.\n\n### Currencies, ISO codes and symbols\n\n| Country/area | Currency | ISO code | Symbol |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| South Africa | rand | ZAR | R |\n| USA | US dollar | USD | $ |\n| Eurozone (e.g. Germany) | euro | EUR | € |\n| United Kingdom | pound sterling | GBP | £ |\n| Japan | yen | JPY | ¥ |\n| China | yuan (renminbi) | CNY | ¥ |\n| Australia | Australian dollar | AUD | A$ |\n| Botswana | pula | BWP | P |\n| Namibia | Namibian dollar | NAD | N$ |\n| Lesotho | loti | LSL | L |\n| Eswatini | lilangeni | SZL | E |\n| Mozambique | metical | MZN | MT |\n\n> **Remember!** In the **Common Monetary Area (CMA)** – South Africa, Namibia, Lesotho and Eswatini – the rand is accepted, and the Namibian dollar, loti and lilangeni are pegged 1:1 to the rand. Botswana is NOT part of the CMA.\n\n## Conversions (example rate R18.50 = US$1)\n\n1. **Rand → foreign currency: divide** by the rate. R3 700 ÷ 18.50 = **$200.00**\n2. **Foreign currency → rand: multiply** by the rate. $150 × 18.50 = **R2 775.00**\n3. **Commission** is a fee (usually a percentage) charged by the bank: 2% of R5 000 = 0.02 × 5 000 = **R100**. Usually you first subtract it from the rand amount and then convert the rest – read the question carefully.\n4. Round money amounts to **two decimal places**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners multiply when converting rand to dollars. Check your answer: with a rate bigger than 1 you always get **fewer** dollars than the number of rand.\n\n### Extension: bank selling rate and bank buying rate\n\nBanks give two rates. Always think from the **bank's** side:\n\n| Rate | When? | Direction | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Bank selling rate** | The bank **sells** foreign currency to the tourist (before a trip abroad) | rand → foreign | R18.80 = US$1 |\n| **Bank buying rate** | The bank **buys** foreign currency from the tourist (inbound tourist, or you after the trip) | foreign → rand | R18.20 = US$1 |\n\nThe selling rate is always **higher** than the buying rate; the difference is the bank's profit.\n\n### Strong and weak rand\n\n- **Weak rand:** you pay *more* rand for one unit of foreign currency (e.g. R17.00 → R19.00 per US$1). SA becomes cheaper for foreigners, so **more inbound** tourists; travelling abroad becomes more expensive, so **fewer outbound** tourists.\n- **Strong rand:** you pay *fewer* rand; the opposite happens."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Buitelandse valuta","en":"Foreign exchange"},"def":{"af":"Die geld (valuta) van 'n ander land wat toeriste koop, verkoop en spandeer.","en":"The money (currency) of another country that tourists buy, sell and spend."}},{"term":{"af":"Wisselkoers","en":"Exchange rate"},"def":{"af":"Die waarde van een valuta uitgedruk in 'n ander valuta, bv. R18,50 = US$1.","en":"The value of one currency expressed in another currency, e.g. R18.50 = US$1."}},{"term":{"af":"Kommissie","en":"Commission"},"def":{"af":"'n Fooi, gewoonlik 'n persentasie van die bedrag, wat 'n bank of wisselkantoor vra om valuta om te ruil.","en":"A fee, usually a percentage of the amount, that a bank or bureau de change charges to exchange currency."}},{"term":{"af":"Bankverkoopkoers","en":"Bank selling rate"},"def":{"af":"Die koers wanneer die bank buitelandse valuta aan 'n toeris verkoop (rand → buitelandse valuta).","en":"The rate used when the bank sells foreign currency to a tourist (rand → foreign currency)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bankkoopkoers","en":"Bank buying rate"},"def":{"af":"Die koers wanneer die bank buitelandse valuta by 'n toeris koop (buitelandse valuta → rand).","en":"The rate used when the bank buys foreign currency from a tourist (foreign currency → rand)."}},{"term":{"af":"Betalingsbalans","en":"Balance of payments"},"def":{"af":"Die rekord van al die geld wat 'n land in- en uitvloei; inkomende toeriste se besteding help dit.","en":"The record of all the money flowing into and out of a country; inbound tourists' spending helps it."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemeenskaplike Monetêre Gebied (GMG)","en":"Common Monetary Area (CMA)"},"def":{"af":"Suid-Afrika, Namibië, Lesotho en Eswatini, waar die rand aanvaar word en die ander valutas 1:1 aan die rand gekoppel is.","en":"South Africa, Namibia, Lesotho and Eswatini, where the rand is accepted and the other currencies are pegged 1:1 to the rand."}},{"term":{"af":"Elektroniese fondsoordrag (EFO/EFT)","en":"Electronic funds transfer (EFT)"},"def":{"af":"Geld wat aanlyn en elektronies van een bankrekening na 'n ander oorgeplaas word.","en":"Money transferred online and electronically from one bank account to another."}},{"term":{"af":"Snelpunt","en":"Speed point"},"def":{"af":"'n Kaartmasjien waar jy met 'n debiet- of kredietkaart betaal deur dit in te steek, te swiep of te tik.","en":"A card machine where you pay with a debit or credit card by inserting, swiping or tapping it."}},{"term":{"af":"Debietkaart en kredietkaart","en":"Debit card and credit card"},"def":{"af":"Debietkaart: die geld kom direk uit jou eie rekening. Kredietkaart: jy leen by die bank en betaal later terug, met rente as jy laat is.","en":"Debit card: the money comes directly from your own account. Credit card: you borrow from the bank and repay later, with interest if you are late."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Omskakel in albei rigtings","en":"Converting both ways"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die voorbeeldkoers R18,50 = US$1 (geen kommissie nie). (a) Hoeveel dollar kry Pieter vir R3 700? (b) 'n Amerikaanse toeris ruil $150 om. Hoeveel rand kry hy? (c) Hoeveel dollar is R1 000 werd?","en":"Use the example rate R18.50 = US$1 (no commission). (a) How many dollars does Pieter get for R3 700? (b) An American tourist exchanges $150. How many rand does he get? (c) How many dollars is R1 000 worth?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Rand → dollar: deel deur die koers. R3 700 ÷ 18,50 = $200,00","en":"(a) Rand → dollars: divide by the rate. R3 700 ÷ 18.50 = $200.00"},{"af":"(b) Dollar → rand: vermenigvuldig met die koers. $150 × 18,50 = R2 775,00","en":"(b) Dollars → rand: multiply by the rate. $150 × 18.50 = R2 775.00"},{"af":"(c) R1 000 ÷ 18,50 = 54,054… → rond af tot twee desimale plekke: $54,05","en":"(c) R1 000 ÷ 18.50 = 54.054… → round to two decimal places: $54.05"},{"af":"Kontroleer: rand → dollar moet 'n kleiner getal gee; dollar → rand 'n groter getal. Albei antwoorde maak sin.","en":"Check: rand → dollars must give a smaller number; dollars → rand a bigger number. Both answers make sense."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) $200,00  (b) R2 775,00  (c) $54,05","en":"(a) $200.00  (b) R2 775.00  (c) $54.05"}},{"title":{"af":"Kommissie aftrek","en":"Deducting commission"},"problem":{"af":"Die Nel-gesin van Hartbeespoort ruil R5 000 vir euro om vir 'n reis na Duitsland. Voorbeeldkoers: R20,00 = €1. Die bank vra 2% kommissie, wat eers van die randbedrag afgetrek word. Hoeveel euro kry hulle?","en":"The Nel family from Hartbeespoort exchanges R5 000 for euros for a trip to Germany. Example rate: R20.00 = €1. The bank charges 2% commission, which is first deducted from the rand amount. How many euros do they get?"},"steps":[{"af":"Bereken die kommissie: 2% × R5 000 = 0,02 × 5 000 = R100,00","en":"Calculate the commission: 2% × R5 000 = 0.02 × 5 000 = R100.00"},{"af":"Trek dit af: R5 000 − R100 = R4 900,00 word omgeskakel","en":"Subtract it: R5 000 − R100 = R4 900.00 is converted"},{"af":"Rand → euro: deel. R4 900 ÷ 20,00 = €245,00","en":"Rand → euros: divide. R4 900 ÷ 20.00 = €245.00"},{"af":"Sonder kommissie sou hulle €250,00 kry – die kommissie kos hulle dus €5,00.","en":"Without commission they would get €250.00 – so the commission costs them €5.00."}],"answer":{"af":"€245,00","en":"€245.00"}},{"title":{"af":"Bankverkoopkoers en bankkoopkoers","en":"Bank selling rate and bank buying rate"},"problem":{"af":"'n Bank se voorbeeldkoerse vir die Britse pond is: bankverkoopkoers R24,60 = £1 en bankkoopkoers R23,40 = £1. (a) Lindiwe koop £400 voor haar reis na Londen. Hoeveel rand betaal sy? (b) Ná die reis verkoop sy haar oorblywende £75 terug aan die bank. Hoeveel rand kry sy? (c) Hoeveel pond sou sy vir R6 000 kon koop?","en":"A bank's example rates for the British pound are: bank selling rate R24.60 = £1 and bank buying rate R23.40 = £1. (a) Lindiwe buys £400 before her trip to London. How many rand does she pay? (b) After the trip she sells her remaining £75 back to the bank. How many rand does she get? (c) How many pounds could she buy for R6 000?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die bank VERKOOP pond aan haar → bankverkoopkoers. £400 × 24,60 = R9 840,00","en":"(a) The bank SELLS pounds to her → bank selling rate. £400 × 24.60 = R9 840.00"},{"af":"(b) Die bank KOOP pond by haar → bankkoopkoers. £75 × 23,40 = R1 755,00","en":"(b) The bank BUYS pounds from her → bank buying rate. £75 × 23.40 = R1 755.00"},{"af":"Die verskil tussen die koerse is R24,60 − R23,40 = R1,20 per pond; op £75 is dit R90,00 – die bank se wins.","en":"The difference between the rates is R24.60 − R23.40 = R1.20 per pound; on £75 that is R90.00 – the bank's profit."},{"af":"(c) Die bank verkoop pond → verkoopkoers. R6 000 ÷ 24,60 = 243,902… → £243,90","en":"(c) The bank sells pounds → selling rate. R6 000 ÷ 24.60 = 243.902… → £243.90"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R9 840,00  (b) R1 755,00  (c) £243,90","en":"(a) R9 840.00  (b) R1 755.00  (c) £243.90"}},{"title":{"af":"Inkomende toeris: koers, kommissie en betaalmetode","en":"Inbound tourist: rate, commission and payment method"},"problem":{"af":"Me. Carter van die VSA land by OR Tambo en ruil $500 vir rand om. Voorbeeldkoerse: bankkoopkoers R18,20 = US$1, bankverkoopkoers R18,80 = US$1; kommissie 1,5% op die randbedrag. (a) Watter koers gebruik die bank? (b) Hoeveel rand kry sy? (c) Sy wil by 'n kunsvlytmark by Hartbeespoortdam inkopies doen. Beveel twee geskikte betaalmetodes aan. (d) Noem twee maniere waarop haar besteding SA bevoordeel.","en":"Ms Carter from the USA lands at OR Tambo and exchanges $500 for rand. Example rates: bank buying rate R18.20 = US$1, bank selling rate R18.80 = US$1; commission 1.5% on the rand amount. (a) Which rate does the bank use? (b) How many rand does she get? (c) She wants to shop at a craft market at Hartbeespoort Dam. Recommend two suitable payment methods. (d) Name two ways in which her spending benefits SA."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die bank KOOP haar dollars → bankkoopkoers (R18,20).","en":"(a) The bank BUYS her dollars → bank buying rate (R18.20)."},{"af":"(b) $500 × 18,20 = R9 100,00. Kommissie: 1,5% × 9 100 = R136,50. Sy kry R9 100,00 − R136,50 = R8 963,50.","en":"(b) $500 × 18.20 = R9 100.00. Commission: 1.5% × 9 100 = R136.50. She gets R9 100.00 − R136.50 = R8 963.50."},{"af":"(c) Klein bedrag kontant in rand (vir stalletjies sonder kaartmasjiene) en haar internasionale kredietkaart by 'n snelpunt (kontaklose tik) – veilig, en sy hoef nie baie kontant te dra nie.","en":"(c) A small amount of cash in rand (for stalls without card machines) and her international credit card at a speed point (contactless tap) – safe, and she does not have to carry much cash."},{"af":"(d) SA verdien buitelandse valuta (dit help die betalingsbalans) en die handwerkers en ander plaaslike besighede verdien inkomste, wat werk skep.","en":"(d) SA earns foreign exchange (it helps the balance of payments) and the crafters and other local businesses earn income, which creates jobs."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Bankkoopkoers  (b) R8 963,50  (c) Kontant in rand en 'n kredietkaart by 'n snelpunt  (d) Buitelandse valuta en werkskepping","en":"(a) Bank buying rate  (b) R8 963.50  (c) Cash in rand and a credit card at a speed point  (d) Foreign exchange and job creation"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ISO-kode vir die Suid-Afrikaanse rand is ___.","en":"The ISO code for the South African rand is ___."},"answers":{"af":["ZAR"],"en":["ZAR"]},"explain":{"af":"ZAR kom van die Nederlandse *Zuid-Afrikaanse Rand*. ZAF is die landkode, nie die valutakode nie.","en":"ZAR comes from the Dutch *Zuid-Afrikaanse Rand*. ZAF is the country code, not the currency code."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["RSA","SAR","ZAF"],"en":["RSA","SAR","ZAF"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Suid-Afrikaanse banke aanvaar sedert 2021 nie meer tjeks nie.","en":"Since 2021 South African banks no longer accept cheques."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Tjeks word nog in CAPS gelys, maar SA-banke het in 2021 opgehou om tjeks te aanvaar omdat hulle stadig is en maklik vervals word.","en":"True. Cheques are still listed in CAPS, but SA banks stopped accepting cheques in 2021 because they are slow and easy to forge."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter betaalmetode gebruik jy as jy met jou slimfoon se toep 'n kode by die kasregister skandeer?","en":"Which payment method do you use when you scan a code at the till with an app on your smartphone?"},"options":[{"af":"'n OTM-onttrekking","en":"An ATM withdrawal"},{"af":"'n Tjek","en":"A cheque"},{"af":"'n QR-kode-betaling (bv. SnapScan of Zapper)","en":"A QR-code payment (e.g. SnapScan or Zapper)"},{"af":"Kontant","en":"Cash"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"QR-kode-toeps soos SnapScan en Zapper laat jou betaal deur die kode te skandeer – geen kontant of kaart nodig nie.","en":"QR-code apps such as SnapScan and Zapper let you pay by scanning the code – no cash or card needed."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die waarde van een valuta uitgedruk in 'n ander valuta, bv. R18,50 = US$1, word die ___ genoem.","en":"The value of one currency expressed in another currency, e.g. R18.50 = US$1, is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["wisselkoers","die wisselkoers"],"en":["exchange rate","the exchange rate","rate of exchange"]},"explain":{"af":"Die wisselkoers sê hoeveel van een valuta jy vir een eenheid van 'n ander valuta kry. Kommissie is die fooi wat die bank vra.","en":"The exchange rate tells you how much of one currency you get for one unit of another. Commission is the fee the bank charges."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kommissie","rentekoers","betalingsbalans"],"en":["commission","interest rate","balance of payments"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke valuta by die regte land.","en":"Match each currency to the correct country."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Pula","en":"Pula"},"r":{"af":"Botswana","en":"Botswana"}},{"l":{"af":"Metical","en":"Metical"},"r":{"af":"Mosambiek","en":"Mozambique"}},{"l":{"af":"Lilangeni","en":"Lilangeni"},"r":{"af":"Eswatini","en":"Eswatini"}},{"l":{"af":"Loti","en":"Loti"},"r":{"af":"Lesotho","en":"Lesotho"}},{"l":{"af":"Pond sterling","en":"Pound sterling"},"r":{"af":"Verenigde Koninkryk","en":"United Kingdom"}}],"explain":{"af":"Pula (BWP) – Botswana; metical (MZN) – Mosambiek; lilangeni (SZL) – Eswatini; loti (LSL) – Lesotho; pond sterling (GBP) – Verenigde Koninkryk.","en":"Pula (BWP) – Botswana; metical (MZN) – Mozambique; lilangeni (SZL) – Eswatini; loti (LSL) – Lesotho; pound sterling (GBP) – United Kingdom."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor 'n debietkaart is korrek?","en":"Which statement about a debit card is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy leen geld by die bank en betaal dit later met rente terug.","en":"You borrow money from the bank and pay it back later with interest."},{"af":"Die geld word dadelik van jou eie bankrekening afgetrek.","en":"The money is immediately deducted from your own bank account."},{"af":"Dit is 'n papiervorm wat jy uitskryf en teken.","en":"It is a paper form that you write out and sign."},{"af":"Dit kan net by 'n OTM gebruik word, nie by 'n snelpunt nie.","en":"It can only be used at an ATM, not at a speed point."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Debietkaart gebruik jou eie geld. Om te leen en later terug te betaal, is 'n kredietkaart; 'n papiervorm is 'n tjek.","en":"A debit card uses your own money. Borrowing and repaying later is a credit card; a paper form is a cheque."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lande vorm die Gemeenskaplike Monetêre Gebied (GMG) waar die rand aanvaar word?","en":"Which countries form the Common Monetary Area (CMA) where the rand is accepted?"},"options":[{"af":"Suid-Afrika, Botswana, Namibië en Lesotho","en":"South Africa, Botswana, Namibia and Lesotho"},{"af":"Suid-Afrika, Zimbabwe, Mosambiek en Eswatini","en":"South Africa, Zimbabwe, Mozambique and Eswatini"},{"af":"Al 16 SAOG-lande","en":"All 16 SADC countries"},{"af":"Suid-Afrika, Namibië, Lesotho en Eswatini","en":"South Africa, Namibia, Lesotho and Eswatini"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die GMG is SA, Namibië, Lesotho en Eswatini. Botswana (pula) is 'n algemene lokval – dit is nie deel van die GMG nie.","en":"The CMA is SA, Namibia, Lesotho and Eswatini. Botswana (pula) is a common trap – it is not part of the CMA."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om rand na Amerikaanse dollar om te skakel, vermenigvuldig jy die randbedrag met die wisselkoers (rand per US$1).","en":"To convert rand to US dollars, you multiply the rand amount by the exchange rate (rand per US$1)."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Rand → buitelandse valuta: **deel** deur die koers. Jy vermenigvuldig net as jy van buitelandse valuta na rand omskakel.","en":"False. Rand → foreign currency: **divide** by the rate. You only multiply when converting from foreign currency to rand."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe bevoordeel die geld wat 'n inkomende toeris uit Duitsland in SA spandeer, die SA-ekonomie?","en":"How does the money that an inbound tourist from Germany spends in SA benefit the SA economy?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit verhoog net die inkomste van die toeris se eie land.","en":"It only increases the income of the tourist's own country."},{"af":"Dit bring buitelandse valuta in, skep werk en help die betalingsbalans.","en":"It brings in foreign exchange, creates jobs and helps the balance of payments."},{"af":"Dit tel as uitgaande toerisme, wat geld uit SA neem.","en":"It counts as outbound tourism, which takes money out of SA."},{"af":"Dit help slegs die lughawe, want toeriste betaal net vir vlugte.","en":"It only helps the airport, because tourists only pay for flights."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Inkomende toeriste se besteding werk soos 'n uitvoer: buitelandse valuta kom in, plaaslike besighede verdien en werk word geskep.","en":"Inbound tourists' spending works like an export: foreign exchange comes in, local businesses earn and jobs are created."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voorbeeldkoers: R18,50 = US$1. Thabo ruil R2 960 om (geen kommissie). Hy kry $___.","en":"Example rate: R18.50 = US$1. Thabo exchanges R2 960 (no commission). He gets $___."},"answers":{"af":["160","160,00","$160","$160,00","US$160"],"en":["160","160.00","$160","$160.00","US$160"]},"explain":{"af":"Rand → dollar: deel. R2 960 ÷ 18,50 = $160,00. As jy vermenigvuldig, kry jy 54 760 – veels te groot.","en":"Rand → dollars: divide. R2 960 ÷ 18.50 = $160.00. If you multiply you get 54 760 – far too big."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["54 760","1 600","16"],"en":["54 760","1 600","16"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voorbeeldkoers: R18,50 = US$1. 'n Amerikaanse toeris ruil $240 om (geen kommissie). Sy kry R___.","en":"Example rate: R18.50 = US$1. An American tourist exchanges $240 (no commission). She gets R___."},"answers":{"af":["4440","4 440","4 440,00","R4 440","R4440"],"en":["4440","4 440","4 440.00","R4 440","R4440"]},"explain":{"af":"Dollar → rand: vermenigvuldig. $240 × 18,50 = R4 440,00.","en":"Dollars → rand: multiply. $240 × 18.50 = R4 440.00."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["12,97","444","4 400"],"en":["12.97","444","4 400"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho koop euro by die bank voordat hy na Frankryk vlieg. Watter koers gebruik die bank?","en":"Sipho buys euros at the bank before he flies to France. Which rate does the bank use?"},"options":[{"af":"Die bankverkoopkoers","en":"The bank selling rate"},{"af":"Die bankkoopkoers","en":"The bank buying rate"},{"af":"Die rentekoers","en":"The interest rate"},{"af":"Die inflasiekoers","en":"The inflation rate"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dink vanuit die bank se kant: die bank VERKOOP euro aan Sipho, dus gebruik dit die bankverkoopkoers (rand → buitelandse valuta).","en":"Think from the bank's side: the bank SELLS euros to Sipho, so it uses the bank selling rate (rand → foreign currency)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voorbeeldkoerse: bankverkoopkoers R24,60 = £1 en bankkoopkoers R23,40 = £1 (geen kommissie). Hoeveel rand betaal Anna om £300 by die bank te koop? R___","en":"Example rates: bank selling rate R24.60 = £1 and bank buying rate R23.40 = £1 (no commission). How many rand does Anna pay to buy £300 from the bank? R___"},"answers":{"af":["7380","7 380","7 380,00","R7 380","R7380"],"en":["7380","7 380","7 380.00","R7 380","R7380"]},"explain":{"af":"Die bank verkoop pond aan Anna → verkoopkoers. £300 × 24,60 = R7 380,00. Met die koopkoers sou jy verkeerdelik R7 020 kry.","en":"The bank sells pounds to Anna → selling rate. £300 × 24.60 = R7 380.00. Using the buying rate you would wrongly get R7 020."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7 020","12,20","738"],"en":["7 020","12.20","738"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die rand verswak van R17,00 tot R19,00 per US$1. Wat is die waarskynlikste gevolg vir toerisme?","en":"The rand weakens from R17.00 to R19.00 per US$1. What is the most likely result for tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Minder Amerikaners besoek SA, want SA word vir hulle duurder.","en":"Fewer Americans visit SA, because SA becomes more expensive for them."},{"af":"Suid-Afrikaners reis meer na die VSA, want dit word goedkoper.","en":"South Africans travel more to the USA, because it becomes cheaper."},{"af":"Meer Amerikaners besoek SA, want hul dollars koop nou meer rand.","en":"More Americans visit SA, because their dollars now buy more rand."},{"af":"Die wisselkoers het geen invloed op toerisme nie.","en":"The exchange rate has no influence on tourism."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Swak rand beteken elke dollar koop meer rand, dus is SA goedkoper vir inkomende toeriste. Vir Suid-Afrikaners word oorsese reis duurder.","en":"A weak rand means every dollar buys more rand, so SA is cheaper for inbound tourists. For South Africans travel abroad becomes more expensive."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voorbeeldkoers: R20,00 = €1. Die bank vra 1,5% kommissie, wat eers van die randbedrag afgetrek word. Hoeveel euro kry 'n toeris vir R6 000?","en":"Example rate: R20.00 = €1. The bank charges 1.5% commission, which is first deducted from the rand amount. How many euros does a tourist get for R6 000?"},"options":[{"af":"€300,00","en":"€300.00"},{"af":"€295,50","en":"€295.50"},{"af":"€304,50","en":"€304.50"},{"af":"€118 200,00","en":"€118 200.00"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Kommissie = 1,5% × 6 000 = R90. R6 000 − R90 = R5 910. R5 910 ÷ 20,00 = €295,50. €300 vergeet die kommissie; €304,50 tel dit by; €118 200 vermenigvuldig verkeerdelik.","en":"Commission = 1.5% × 6 000 = R90. R6 000 − R90 = R5 910. R5 910 ÷ 20.00 = €295.50. €300 forgets the commission; €304.50 adds it; €118 200 wrongly multiplies."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi van Brits reis vir tien dae na Londen. Watter raad oor geld is die beste?","en":"Thandi from Brits is travelling to London for ten days. Which advice about money is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Neem al haar geld in randnote saam en ruil dit by straatverkopers in Londen.","en":"Take all her money in rand notes and exchange it with street vendors in London."},{"af":"Ruil al haar geld vooraf in pond om en dra alles as kontant.","en":"Exchange all her money into pounds beforehand and carry everything as cash."},{"af":"Neem tjeks saam, want dit word oral aanvaar.","en":"Take cheques, because they are accepted everywhere."},{"af":"Gebruik 'n kaart wat internasionaal werk vir die meeste aankope en ruil net 'n klein bedrag pond vooraf vir kontant.","en":"Use a card that works internationally for most purchases and exchange only a small amount of pounds beforehand for cash."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Kombinasie is die veiligste en gerieflikste: 'n kaart is veilig en wyd aanvaar, en 'n bietjie kontant help vir klein uitgawes. Baie kontant kan gesteel word, en tjeks word nie meer aanvaar nie.","en":"A combination is the safest and most convenient: a card is safe and widely accepted, and a little cash helps for small expenses. Lots of cash can be stolen, and cheques are no longer accepted."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Toeriste-aantreklikhede, volhoubare toerisme en bemarking","en":"Tourist attractions, sustainable tourism and marketing"},"topics":[{"id":"toer10-t3-aantreklikhede-provinsies","title":{"af":"Toeriste-aantreklikhede in die nege provinsies en Wêrelderfenisterreine","en":"Tourist attractions in the nine provinces and World Heritage Sites"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die belangrikste aantreklikhede van elke provinsie ken, Wêrelderfenisterreine kan identifiseer en klassifiseer, en aantreklikhede vir 'n toeristeprofiel kan aanbeveel.","en":"You will know the main attractions of each province, be able to identify and classify World Heritage Sites, and recommend attractions for a tourist profile."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n Wêrelderfenisterrein?\n\n'n **Wêrelderfenisterrein** (WET) is 'n plek van **uitsonderlike universele waarde** vir die hele mensdom wat deur **UNESCO** (die VN se Opvoedkundige, Wetenskaplike en Kulturele Organisasie) op die Wêrelderfenislys ingeskryf is. Die land moet die terrein beskerm en bewaar. Die status lok internasionale toeriste, bring geld vir bewaring en skep werk. Daar is drie soorte:\n\n- **Kultureel** – deur mense gemaak of gevorm: geboue, argeologiese en fossielterreine, kultuurlandskappe.\n- **Natuurlik** – uitsonderlike landvorme, geologie of biodiversiteit.\n- **Gemeng** – het albei soorte waarde.\n\n## Suid-Afrika se 12 Wêrelderfenisterreine (sedert 2024)\n\n| Terrein (jaar) | Tipe | Ligging | Bekend vir |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fossiel-hominiedterreine: Wieg van die Mensdom, Taung, Makapan-vallei (1999) | Kultureel | Gauteng, Noordwes, Limpopo | Fossiele van vroeë mense, bv. \"Mrs Ples\" en die Taung-skedel |\n| Robbeneiland (1999) | Kultureel | Wes-Kaap, in Tafelbaai | Tronk waar Nelson Mandela 18 van sy 27 jaar aangehou is; simbool van die oorwinning van demokrasie oor onderdrukking |\n| iSimangaliso-vleilandpark (1999) | Natuurlik | KwaZulu-Natal, noordoostelike kus | St Lucia-meer, vleilande, koraalriwwe, seekoeie, krokodille, seeskilpaaie |\n| Maloti-Drakensbergpark / uKhahlamba (2000) | **Gemeng** | KwaZulu-Natal (en Lesotho) | SA se hoogste berge (natuurlik) én duisende San-rotsskilderye (kultureel) |\n| Mapungubwe-kultuurlandskap (2003) | Kultureel | Limpopo, waar die Limpopo- en Sjasjerivier saamvloei (grens met Botswana en Zimbabwe) | Ou koninkryk; die goue renoster |\n| Kaapse Floristiese Streek se beskermde gebiede (2004) | Natuurlik | Wes-Kaap en Oos-Kaap | Fynbos – baie ryk plantlewe |\n| Vredefortkoepel (2005) | Natuurlik | Vrystaat by Parys (grens met Noordwes) | Die oudste en grootste bekende meteoriet-impakstruktuur op aarde |\n| Richtersveld-kultuur- en botaniese landskap (2007) | Kultureel | Noord-Kaap, verre noordweste | Die Nama se tradisionele, semi-nomadiese veeboerlewe |\n| ǂKhomani-kultuurlandskap (2017) | Kultureel | Noord-Kaap, Kalahari | Die kultuur van die San (ǂKhomani) |\n| Barberton-Makhonjwa-berge (2018) | Natuurlik | Mpumalanga | Van die oudste goed bewaarde rotse op aarde |\n| Nelson Mandela-nalatenskapterreine (2024) | Kultureel | Verskeie provinsies, bv. die Uniegebou en Konstitusieheuwel | Menseregte, bevryding en versoening |\n| Pleistoseen-bewoningsterreine (2024) | Kultureel | Wes-Kaap (Pinnacle Point, Diepkloof) en KwaZulu-Natal (Sibhudu-grot) | Bewyse van vroeë moderne menslike gedrag |\n\n**Totaal: 7 kultureel, 4 natuurlik, 1 gemeng.** Ouer handboeke noem 10 – die twee van 2024 het later bygekom.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die Taung-skedel (Noordwes) en die Wieg van die Mensdom (Gauteng) is deel van **dieselfde** WET: die Fossiel-hominiedterreine.\n\n## CAPS-aantreklikhede per provinsie (* = WET)\n\n| Provinsie | Aantreklikhede |\n|---|---|\n| **Oos-Kaap** | Addo-olifant- Nasionale Park (olifante en die Groot Vyf, naby Gqeberha); Nasionale Kunstefees in Makhanda (Grahamstad) elke winter; kanovaart op die Groot-Visrivier |\n| **Vrystaat** | Vredefortkoepel*; Golden Gate Hoogland Nasionale Park (sandsteenkranse naby Clarens) |\n| **Gauteng** | Wieg van die Mensdom* (Sterkfontein-grotte, Maropeng); Apartheidsmuseum; Gold Reef City (temapark op 'n ou goudmyn); Soweto-erfenis – Vilakazi-straat, waar twee Nobelpryswenners (Mandela en Tutu) gewoon het |\n| **KwaZulu-Natal** | iSimangaliso-vleilandpark*; uKhahlamba-Drakensbergpark* |\n| **Limpopo** | Mapungubwe*; Krugerwildtuin (noordelike deel); Afrika-ivoorroete (kampe wat natuur en plaaslike kultuur wys) |\n| **Mpumalanga** | Panoramaroete: Pelgrimsrus (ou gouddelwersdorp), Blyderivierspoort, God's Window, Bourke's Luck-maalgate; Krugerwildtuin (suidelike deel) |\n| **Noord-Kaap** | Die Groot Gat en Mynmuseum in Kimberley (diamantdelwery); Brullende Sande van die Witsand-natuurreservaat (duine wat \"brul\" as die sand beweeg) |\n| **Noordwes** | Sun City en die Lost City (oord, Valley of Waves, gholf); Lesedi-kultuurdorp; Pilanesberg-wildreservaat (in die krater van 'n uitgedoofde vulkaan; Groot Vyf); Hartbeespoortdam; die Magaliesberg; Taung-skedelterrein* |\n| **Wes-Kaap** | Tafelberg (kabelkar); V&A Waterfront; Robbeneiland*; Kaapse Floristiese Streek* |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die Krugerwildtuin is 'n **nasionale park**, nie 'n Wêrelderfenisterrein nie. Sun City, Gold Reef City en die Apartheidsmuseum is ook nie WET's nie.\n\n## Hoe beantwoord jy die eksamenvrae?\n\n1. **Identifiseer 'n WET uit 'n beskrywing:** soek leidrade – riviere, grense, fossiele, rotskuns, 'n meteoriet, 'n tronk.\n2. **Klassifiseer:** is die waarde deur mense geskep (kultureel), deur die natuur (natuurlik) of albei (gemeng)?\n3. **Beveel aantreklikhede vir 'n toeristeprofiel aan:** lees belangstellings, begroting, tyd en waar die toeris bly. Kies aantreklikhede wat daarby pas, hou die afstande realisties (dieselfde of naburige provinsies) en gee 'n **rede** vir elke keuse.\n4. **Kaart-in-woorde:** onthou die ligging – Mapungubwe in die verre noorde, iSimangaliso aan die noordoostelike kus, die Richtersveld in die verre noordweste, Robbeneiland in Tafelbaai.","en":"## What is a World Heritage Site?\n\nA **World Heritage Site** (WHS) is a place of **outstanding universal value** to all of humanity that has been inscribed on the World Heritage List by **UNESCO** (the UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization). The country must protect and conserve the site. The status attracts international tourists, brings money for conservation and creates jobs. There are three kinds:\n\n- **Cultural** – made or shaped by people: buildings, archaeological and fossil sites, cultural landscapes.\n- **Natural** – outstanding landforms, geology or biodiversity.\n- **Mixed** – has both kinds of value.\n\n## South Africa's 12 World Heritage Sites (since 2024)\n\n| Site (year) | Type | Location | Known for |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Fossil Hominid Sites: Cradle of Humankind, Taung, Makapan Valley (1999) | Cultural | Gauteng, North West, Limpopo | Fossils of early humans, e.g. \"Mrs Ples\" and the Taung Skull |\n| Robben Island (1999) | Cultural | Western Cape, in Table Bay | Prison where Nelson Mandela was held for 18 of his 27 years; symbol of the triumph of democracy over oppression |\n| iSimangaliso Wetland Park (1999) | Natural | KwaZulu-Natal, north-east coast | Lake St Lucia, wetlands, coral reefs, hippos, crocodiles, turtles |\n| Maloti-Drakensberg Park / uKhahlamba (2000) | **Mixed** | KwaZulu-Natal (and Lesotho) | SA's highest mountains (natural) and thousands of San rock paintings (cultural) |\n| Mapungubwe Cultural Landscape (2003) | Cultural | Limpopo, where the Limpopo and Shashe rivers meet (border with Botswana and Zimbabwe) | Ancient kingdom; the golden rhinoceros |\n| Cape Floral Region Protected Areas (2004) | Natural | Western Cape and Eastern Cape | Fynbos – very rich plant life |\n| Vredefort Dome (2005) | Natural | Free State near Parys (border with North West) | The oldest and largest known meteorite impact structure on Earth |\n| Richtersveld Cultural and Botanical Landscape (2007) | Cultural | Northern Cape, far north-west | The Nama people's traditional semi-nomadic herding way of life |\n| ǂKhomani Cultural Landscape (2017) | Cultural | Northern Cape, Kalahari | The culture of the San (ǂKhomani) |\n| Barberton Makhonjwa Mountains (2018) | Natural | Mpumalanga | Some of the oldest well-preserved rocks on Earth |\n| Nelson Mandela Legacy Sites (2024) | Cultural | Several provinces, e.g. the Union Buildings and Constitution Hill | Human rights, liberation and reconciliation |\n| Pleistocene Occupation Sites (2024) | Cultural | Western Cape (Pinnacle Point, Diepkloof) and KwaZulu-Natal (Sibhudu Cave) | Evidence of early modern human behaviour |\n\n**Total: 7 cultural, 4 natural, 1 mixed.** Older textbooks list 10 – the two from 2024 were added later.\n\n> **Remember!** The Taung Skull (North West) and the Cradle of Humankind (Gauteng) are part of the **same** WHS: the Fossil Hominid Sites.\n\n## CAPS attractions per province (* = WHS)\n\n| Province | Attractions |\n|---|---|\n| **Eastern Cape** | Addo Elephant National Park (elephants and the Big Five, near Gqeberha); National Arts Festival in Makhanda (Grahamstown) every winter; canoeing on the Great Fish River |\n| **Free State** | Vredefort Dome*; Golden Gate Highlands National Park (sandstone cliffs near Clarens) |\n| **Gauteng** | Cradle of Humankind* (Sterkfontein Caves, Maropeng); Apartheid Museum; Gold Reef City (theme park on an old gold mine); Soweto heritage – Vilakazi Street, where two Nobel Prize winners (Mandela and Tutu) lived |\n| **KwaZulu-Natal** | iSimangaliso Wetland Park*; uKhahlamba-Drakensberg Park* |\n| **Limpopo** | Mapungubwe*; Kruger National Park (northern part); African Ivory Route (camps showing nature and local culture) |\n| **Mpumalanga** | Panorama Route: Pilgrim's Rest (old gold-rush town), Blyde River Canyon, God's Window, Bourke's Luck Potholes; Kruger National Park (southern part) |\n| **Northern Cape** | The Big Hole and Mine Museum in Kimberley (diamond digging); Roaring Sands of Witsand Nature Reserve (dunes that \"roar\" when the sand moves) |\n| **North West** | Sun City and the Lost City (resort, Valley of Waves, golf); Lesedi Cultural Village; Pilanesberg Game Reserve (in the crater of an extinct volcano; Big Five); Hartbeespoort Dam; the Magaliesberg; Taung Skull site* |\n| **Western Cape** | Table Mountain (cableway); V&A Waterfront; Robben Island*; Cape Floral Region* |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Kruger National Park is a **national park**, not a World Heritage Site. Sun City, Gold Reef City and the Apartheid Museum are not WHSs either.\n\n## How to answer the exam questions\n\n1. **Identify a WHS from a description:** look for clues – rivers, borders, fossils, rock art, a meteorite, a prison.\n2. **Classify:** was the value created by people (cultural), by nature (natural) or both (mixed)?\n3. **Recommend attractions for a tourist profile:** read the interests, budget, time and where the tourist is staying. Choose attractions that fit, keep distances realistic (same or neighbouring provinces) and give a **reason** for each choice.\n4. **Map in words:** remember the locations – Mapungubwe in the far north, iSimangaliso on the north-east coast, the Richtersveld in the far north-west, Robben Island in Table Bay."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Toeriste-aantreklikheid","en":"Tourist attraction"},"def":{"af":"'n Natuurlike of mensgemaakte plek, gebeurtenis of aktiwiteit wat toeriste na 'n bestemming lok.","en":"A natural or man-made place, event or activity that draws tourists to a destination."}},{"term":{"af":"Wêrelderfenisterrein (WET)","en":"World Heritage Site (WHS)"},"def":{"af":"'n Plek van uitsonderlike universele waarde vir die mensdom wat deur UNESCO op die Wêrelderfenislys ingeskryf is.","en":"A place of outstanding universal value to humanity that UNESCO has inscribed on the World Heritage List."}},{"term":{"af":"UNESCO","en":"UNESCO"},"def":{"af":"Die Verenigde Nasies se Opvoedkundige, Wetenskaplike en Kulturele Organisasie, wat terreine tot Wêrelderfenisterreine verklaar.","en":"The United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization, which declares sites World Heritage Sites."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitsonderlike universele waarde","en":"Outstanding universal value"},"def":{"af":"So belangrik dat 'n terrein vir alle mense in die wêreld, nou en in die toekoms, van waarde is.","en":"So important that a site is of value to all people in the world, now and in the future."}},{"term":{"af":"Kulturele Wêrelderfenisterrein","en":"Cultural World Heritage Site"},"def":{"af":"'n Terrein wat deur mense gemaak of gevorm is, bv. Robbeneiland of Mapungubwe.","en":"A site made or shaped by people, e.g. Robben Island or Mapungubwe."}},{"term":{"af":"Natuurlike Wêrelderfenisterrein","en":"Natural World Heritage Site"},"def":{"af":"'n Terrein met uitsonderlike natuurlike landvorme, geologie of biodiversiteit, bv. die Vredefortkoepel.","en":"A site with outstanding natural landforms, geology or biodiversity, e.g. the Vredefort Dome."}},{"term":{"af":"Gemengde Wêrelderfenisterrein","en":"Mixed World Heritage Site"},"def":{"af":"'n Terrein met kulturele én natuurlike waarde; in SA net die Maloti-Drakensbergpark.","en":"A site with both cultural and natural value; in SA only the Maloti-Drakensberg Park."}},{"term":{"af":"Panoramaroete","en":"Panorama Route"},"def":{"af":"'n Toeristeroete in Mpumalanga met Pelgrimsrus, Blyderivierspoort, God's Window en Bourke's Luck-maalgate.","en":"A tourist route in Mpumalanga with Pilgrim's Rest, Blyde River Canyon, God's Window and Bourke's Luck Potholes."}},{"term":{"af":"Fossiel-hominiedterreine","en":"Fossil Hominid Sites"},"def":{"af":"Die WET wat die Wieg van die Mensdom (Gauteng), Taung (Noordwes) en die Makapan-vallei (Limpopo) insluit.","en":"The WHS that includes the Cradle of Humankind (Gauteng), Taung (North West) and the Makapan Valley (Limpopo)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer Wêrelderfenisterreine","en":"Classify World Heritage Sites"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elkeen van die volgende WET's as kultureel, natuurlik of gemeng en gee 'n rede: (a) Robbeneiland (b) die Vredefortkoepel (c) die Maloti-Drakensbergpark (d) die Richtersveld.","en":"Classify each of the following WHSs as cultural, natural or mixed and give a reason: (a) Robben Island (b) the Vredefort Dome (c) the Maloti-Drakensberg Park (d) the Richtersveld."},"steps":[{"af":"Vra by elkeen: kom die waarde van mense, van die natuur, of van albei?","en":"Ask for each one: does the value come from people, from nature, or from both?"},{"af":"(a) Robbeneiland – kultureel: 'n tronk wat die stryd teen apartheid en die oorwinning van demokrasie verteenwoordig.","en":"(a) Robben Island – cultural: a prison that represents the struggle against apartheid and the triumph of democracy."},{"af":"(b) Vredefortkoepel – natuurlik: 'n reuse meteoriet-impakstruktuur, deur die natuur gevorm.","en":"(b) Vredefort Dome – natural: a huge meteorite impact structure formed by nature."},{"af":"(c) Maloti-Drakensberg – gemeng: hoë berge en biodiversiteit (natuurlik) plus San-rotskuns (kultureel).","en":"(c) Maloti-Drakensberg – mixed: high mountains and biodiversity (natural) plus San rock art (cultural)."},{"af":"(d) Richtersveld – kultureel: 'n kultuurlandskap wat die Nama se tradisionele leefwyse bewaar.","en":"(d) Richtersveld – cultural: a cultural landscape that preserves the Nama people's traditional way of life."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Kultureel (b) Natuurlik (c) Gemeng (d) Kultureel","en":"(a) Cultural (b) Natural (c) Mixed (d) Cultural"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die terrein uit 'n beskrywing (kaart-in-woorde)","en":"Identify the site from a description (map in words)"},"problem":{"af":"Identifiseer elke WET en die provinsie: (a) 'Hierdie terrein lê in die verre noorde, waar die Limpopo- en Sjasjerivier saamvloei en drie lande ontmoet. Hier is 'n klein goue renoster gevind.' (b) 'Hierdie vleilandpark strek langs die noordoostelike kus; seeskilpaaie lê hul eiers op die strande.' (c) 'Hierdie koepel naby Parys is gevorm toe 'n meteoriet die aarde getref het.'","en":"Identify each WHS and its province: (a) 'This site lies in the far north, where the Limpopo and Shashe rivers meet and three countries meet. A small golden rhinoceros was found here.' (b) 'This wetland park stretches along the north-east coast; turtles lay their eggs on the beaches.' (c) 'This dome near Parys was formed when a meteorite struck the Earth.'"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Leidrade: Limpopo- en Sjasjerivier, goue renoster → Mapungubwe-kultuurlandskap, Limpopo.","en":"(a) Clues: Limpopo and Shashe rivers, golden rhinoceros → Mapungubwe Cultural Landscape, Limpopo."},{"af":"(b) Leidrade: vleiland, noordoostelike kus, seeskilpaaie → iSimangaliso-vleilandpark, KwaZulu-Natal.","en":"(b) Clues: wetland, north-east coast, turtles → iSimangaliso Wetland Park, KwaZulu-Natal."},{"af":"(c) Leidrade: koepel, Parys, meteoriet → Vredefortkoepel, Vrystaat.","en":"(c) Clues: dome, Parys, meteorite → Vredefort Dome, Free State."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Mapungubwe – Limpopo (b) iSimangaliso – KwaZulu-Natal (c) Vredefortkoepel – Vrystaat","en":"(a) Mapungubwe – Limpopo (b) iSimangaliso – KwaZulu-Natal (c) Vredefort Dome – Free State"}},{"title":{"af":"Beveel aantreklikhede vir 'n toeristeprofiel aan","en":"Recommend attractions for a tourist profile"},"problem":{"af":"Toeristeprofiel: Tom (24) en Emma (23) van Engeland is rugsakreisigers op 'n klein begroting. Hulle bly vyf dae by 'n rugsakherberg in Pretoria, het 'n huurmotor en stel belang in geskiedenis, menslike oorsprong en wild. Beveel drie aantreklikhede aan en gee 'n rede vir elkeen.","en":"Tourist profile: Tom (24) and Emma (23) from England are backpackers on a small budget. They are staying for five days at a backpackers' hostel in Pretoria, have a hired car and are interested in history, human origins and wildlife. Recommend three attractions and give a reason for each."},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die profiel: geskiedenis, menslike oorsprong, wild; klein begroting; vyf dae; basis in Pretoria (Gauteng).","en":"Read the profile: history, human origins, wildlife; small budget; five days; based in Pretoria (Gauteng)."},{"af":"1. Die Wieg van die Mensdom (Gauteng) – menslike oorsprong: Sterkfontein-grotte en Maropeng; 'n WET en maklik met die motor bereikbaar.","en":"1. The Cradle of Humankind (Gauteng) – human origins: Sterkfontein Caves and Maropeng; a WHS and easy to reach by car."},{"af":"2. Die Apartheidsmuseum en Vilakazi-straat in Soweto (Gauteng) – SA se geskiedenis en die stryd vir vryheid, naby hul basis.","en":"2. The Apartheid Museum and Vilakazi Street in Soweto (Gauteng) – SA's history and the struggle for freedom, close to their base."},{"af":"3. Pilanesberg-wildreservaat (Noordwes) – die Groot Vyf; hulle kan self in die huurmotor ry, wat goedkoper is as 'n luukse lodge.","en":"3. Pilanesberg Game Reserve (North West) – the Big Five; they can self-drive in the hired car, which is cheaper than a luxury lodge."}],"answer":{"af":"Wieg van die Mensdom, Apartheidsmuseum/Vilakazi-straat en Pilanesberg – elkeen pas by hul belangstellings, begroting en ligging.","en":"Cradle of Humankind, Apartheid Museum/Vilakazi Street and Pilanesberg – each fits their interests, budget and location."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter organisasie skryf terreine op die Wêrelderfenislys in?","en":"Which organisation inscribes sites on the World Heritage List?"},"options":[{"af":"UNWTO","en":"UNWTO"},{"af":"UNESCO","en":"UNESCO"},{"af":"SANParke","en":"SANParks"},{"af":"SAHRA","en":"SAHRA"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"UNESCO (die VN se Opvoedkundige, Wetenskaplike en Kulturele Organisasie) verklaar Wêrelderfenisterreine. Die UNWTO is die VN se toerisme-organisasie.","en":"UNESCO (the UN Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization) declares World Heritage Sites. The UNWTO is the UN's tourism organisation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Groot Gat en Mynmuseum in Kimberley is in die ___-provinsie.","en":"The Big Hole and Mine Museum in Kimberley is in the ___ province."},"answers":{"af":["Noord-Kaap","Noordkaap"],"en":["Northern Cape"]},"explain":{"af":"Kimberley is die hoofstad van die Noord-Kaap; die Groot Gat is ná die diamantvonds gegrawe.","en":"Kimberley is the capital of the Northern Cape; the Big Hole was dug after the diamond discovery."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Vrystaat","Noordwes","Wes-Kaap"],"en":["Free State","North West","Western Cape"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Vredefortkoepel is 'n natuurlike Wêrelderfenisterrein.","en":"The Vredefort Dome is a natural World Heritage Site."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is 'n meteoriet-impakstruktuur – deur die natuur gevorm, nie deur mense nie.","en":"True. It is a meteorite impact structure – formed by nature, not by people."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke aantreklikheid by die regte provinsie.","en":"Match each attraction to the correct province."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Addo-olifant- Nasionale Park","en":"Addo Elephant National Park"},"r":{"af":"Oos-Kaap","en":"Eastern Cape"}},{"l":{"af":"Golden Gate Hoogland Nasionale Park","en":"Golden Gate Highlands National Park"},"r":{"af":"Vrystaat","en":"Free State"}},{"l":{"af":"God's Window","en":"God's Window"},"r":{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"}},{"l":{"af":"Sun City en die Lost City","en":"Sun City and the Lost City"},"r":{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North West"}},{"l":{"af":"iSimangaliso-vleilandpark","en":"iSimangaliso Wetland Park"},"r":{"af":"KwaZulu-Natal","en":"KwaZulu-Natal"}}],"explain":{"af":"Addo – Oos-Kaap (naby Gqeberha); Golden Gate – Vrystaat (naby Clarens); God's Window – Mpumalanga (Panoramaroete); Sun City – Noordwes; iSimangaliso – KwaZulu-Natal.","en":"Addo – Eastern Cape (near Gqeberha); Golden Gate – Free State (near Clarens); God's Window – Mpumalanga (Panorama Route); Sun City – North West; iSimangaliso – KwaZulu-Natal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel Wêrelderfenisterreine het Suid-Afrika sedert 2024?","en":"How many World Heritage Sites has South Africa had since 2024?"},"options":[{"af":"9","en":"9"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"14","en":"14"},{"af":"12","en":"12"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sedert 2024 het SA 12 WET's (7 kultureel, 4 natuurlik, 1 gemeng). Ouer handboeke noem 10, van voor die twee nuwes in 2024.","en":"Since 2024 SA has 12 WHSs (7 cultural, 4 natural, 1 mixed). Older textbooks list 10, from before the two new ones in 2024."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Suid-Afrika se enigste gemengde Wêrelderfenisterrein is die Maloti-___-park.","en":"South Africa's only mixed World Heritage Site is the Maloti-___ Park."},"answers":{"af":["Drakensberg"],"en":["Drakensberg"]},"explain":{"af":"Die Maloti-Drakensbergpark (uKhahlamba) het hoë berge (natuurlik) én San-rotskuns (kultureel).","en":"The Maloti-Drakensberg Park (uKhahlamba) has high mountains (natural) and San rock art (cultural)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Magaliesberg","Cederberg","Swartberg"],"en":["Magaliesberg","Cederberg","Swartberg"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aantreklikheid is deel van die Panoramaroete in Mpumalanga?","en":"Which attraction is part of the Panorama Route in Mpumalanga?"},"options":[{"af":"Bourke's Luck-maalgate","en":"Bourke's Luck Potholes"},{"af":"Die Groot Gat","en":"The Big Hole"},{"af":"Gold Reef City","en":"Gold Reef City"},{"af":"Lesedi-kultuurdorp","en":"Lesedi Cultural Village"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die Panoramaroete sluit Pelgrimsrus, Blyderivierspoort, God's Window en Bourke's Luck-maalgate in. Die Groot Gat is in Kimberley, Gold Reef City in Johannesburg en Lesedi in Noordwes.","en":"The Panorama Route includes Pilgrim's Rest, Blyde River Canyon, God's Window and Bourke's Luck Potholes. The Big Hole is in Kimberley, Gold Reef City in Johannesburg and Lesedi in North West."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is Robbeneiland 'n kulturele Wêrelderfenisterrein?","en":"Why is Robben Island a cultural World Heritage Site?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het die meeste fynbosspesies in die wêreld.","en":"It has the most fynbos species in the world."},{"af":"Dit is waar die eerste diamant in SA gevind is.","en":"It is where the first diamond in SA was found."},{"af":"Dit simboliseer die oorwinning van demokrasie en vryheid oor onderdrukking; Mandela is 18 jaar daar aangehou.","en":"It symbolises the triumph of democracy and freedom over oppression; Mandela was held there for 18 years."},{"af":"Dit is 'n meteoriet-krater in Tafelbaai.","en":"It is a meteorite crater in Table Bay."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Robbeneiland se waarde kom van mense se geskiedenis – die politieke tronk en die stryd teen apartheid – daarom is dit kultureel.","en":"Robben Island's value comes from human history – the political prison and the struggle against apartheid – so it is cultural."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vilakazi-straat, waar twee Nobelpryswenners (Nelson Mandela en Desmond Tutu) gewoon het, is in ___.","en":"Vilakazi Street, where two Nobel Prize winners (Nelson Mandela and Desmond Tutu) lived, is in ___."},"answers":{"af":["Soweto","Soweto, Johannesburg","Orlando West"],"en":["Soweto","Soweto, Johannesburg","Orlando West"]},"explain":{"af":"Vilakazi-straat is in Orlando-Wes, Soweto (Gauteng) – deel van Soweto se erfenistoerisme.","en":"Vilakazi Street is in Orlando West, Soweto (Gauteng) – part of Soweto's heritage tourism."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Alexandra","Sharpeville","Mamelodi"],"en":["Alexandra","Sharpeville","Mamelodi"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Mapungubwe is 'n natuurlike Wêrelderfenisterrein.","en":"Mapungubwe is a natural World Heritage Site."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Mapungubwe is 'n **kultuurlandskap** – die oorblyfsels van 'n ou koninkryk (bv. die goue renoster), dus kultureel.","en":"False. Mapungubwe is a **cultural landscape** – the remains of an ancient kingdom (e.g. the golden rhinoceros), so it is cultural."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gesin in Brits wil hul kinders (10 en 12) leer oor fossiele en die oorsprong van die mens. Watter aantreklikheid is die beste keuse?","en":"A family in Brits wants to teach their children (10 and 12) about fossils and human origins. Which attraction is the best choice?"},"options":[{"af":"Blyderivierspoort","en":"Blyde River Canyon"},{"af":"Die V&A Waterfront","en":"The V&A Waterfront"},{"af":"Die Wieg van die Mensdom (Maropeng en Sterkfontein)","en":"The Cradle of Humankind (Maropeng and Sterkfontein)"},{"af":"Die Brullende Sande van Witsand","en":"The Roaring Sands of Witsand"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Wieg van die Mensdom gaan oor fossiele en menslike oorsprong en is naby Brits. Die ander pas nie by die belangstelling nie of is baie ver.","en":"The Cradle of Humankind is about fossils and human origins and is close to Brits. The others do not match the interest or are very far away."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hierdie WET lê waar die Limpopo- en Sjasjerivier saamvloei, op die grens met Botswana en Zimbabwe. Dit is ___.","en":"This WHS lies where the Limpopo and Shashe rivers meet, on the border with Botswana and Zimbabwe. It is ___."},"answers":{"af":["Mapungubwe","Mapungubwe-kultuurlandskap"],"en":["Mapungubwe","Mapungubwe Cultural Landscape"]},"explain":{"af":"Mapungubwe lê in die verre noorde van Limpopo by die samevloeiing van die Limpopo en die Sjasje.","en":"Mapungubwe lies in the far north of Limpopo at the confluence of the Limpopo and the Shashe."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Vredefortkoepel","iSimangaliso","Richtersveld"],"en":["Vredefort Dome","iSimangaliso","Richtersveld"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter lys bevat SLEGS kulturele Wêrelderfenisterreine?","en":"Which list contains ONLY cultural World Heritage Sites?"},"options":[{"af":"iSimangaliso, Vredefortkoepel, Robbeneiland","en":"iSimangaliso, Vredefort Dome, Robben Island"},{"af":"Robbeneiland, Mapungubwe, ǂKhomani-kultuurlandskap","en":"Robben Island, Mapungubwe, ǂKhomani Cultural Landscape"},{"af":"Kaapse Floristiese Streek, Barberton-Makhonjwa, Mapungubwe","en":"Cape Floral Region, Barberton Makhonjwa, Mapungubwe"},{"af":"Maloti-Drakensberg, Richtersveld, iSimangaliso","en":"Maloti-Drakensberg, Richtersveld, iSimangaliso"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Robbeneiland, Mapungubwe en ǂKhomani is al drie kultureel. iSimangaliso, Vredefort, die Kaapse Floristiese Streek en Barberton is natuurlik; Maloti-Drakensberg is gemeng.","en":"Robben Island, Mapungubwe and ǂKhomani are all cultural. iSimangaliso, Vredefort, the Cape Floral Region and Barberton are natural; Maloti-Drakensberg is mixed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Brosjure beskryf 'n terrein met 'SA se hoogste pieke, skoon bergstrome en duisende eeue-oue San-rotsskilderye'. Waarom is dit 'n gemengde terrein?","en":"A brochure describes a site with 'SA's highest peaks, clean mountain streams and thousands of centuries-old San rock paintings'. Why is it a mixed site?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat dit in twee provinsies lê.","en":"Because it lies in two provinces."},{"af":"Omdat dit sowel natuurlike waarde (berge, strome) as kulturele waarde (San-rotskuns) het.","en":"Because it has both natural value (mountains, streams) and cultural value (San rock art)."},{"af":"Omdat toeriste dit in die somer en die winter besoek.","en":"Because tourists visit it in summer and in winter."},{"af":"Omdat dit 'n nasionale park en 'n privaat reservaat is.","en":"Because it is a national park and a private reserve."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'Gemeng' beteken dat die terrein BEIDE natuurlike en kulturele waarde het – soos die Maloti-Drakensbergpark.","en":"'Mixed' means the site has BOTH natural and cultural value – like the Maloti-Drakensberg Park."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Fossiel-hominiedterreine strek oor drie provinsies: Gauteng (Wieg van die Mensdom), Noordwes (Taung) en ___ (Makapan-vallei).","en":"The Fossil Hominid Sites stretch across three provinces: Gauteng (Cradle of Humankind), North West (Taung) and ___ (Makapan Valley)."},"answers":{"af":["Limpopo"],"en":["Limpopo"]},"explain":{"af":"Die Makapan-vallei is in Limpopo. Saam met die Wieg van die Mensdom en Taung vorm dit een WET.","en":"The Makapan Valley is in Limpopo. Together with the Cradle of Humankind and Taung it forms one WHS."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Mpumalanga","Vrystaat","KwaZulu-Natal"],"en":["Mpumalanga","Free State","KwaZulu-Natal"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Duitse egpaar land by OR Tambo, huur 'n motor en het tien dae. Hulle wil net natuur, wild en mooi uitsigte sien. Watter roete beveel jy aan?","en":"A German couple lands at OR Tambo, hires a car and has ten days. They only want to see nature, wildlife and beautiful views. Which route do you recommend?"},"options":[{"af":"Apartheidsmuseum → Gold Reef City → die Lost City se casino","en":"Apartheid Museum → Gold Reef City → the Lost City's casino"},{"af":"Robbeneiland → Apartheidsmuseum → Vilakazi-straat","en":"Robben Island → Apartheid Museum → Vilakazi Street"},{"af":"Groot Gat in Kimberley → Nasionale Kunstefees → V&A Waterfront","en":"Big Hole in Kimberley → National Arts Festival → V&A Waterfront"},{"af":"Pilanesberg → Panoramaroete (God's Window, Blyderivierspoort) → Krugerwildtuin","en":"Pilanesberg → Panorama Route (God's Window, Blyde River Canyon) → Kruger National Park"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Pilanesberg, die Panoramaroete en Kruger pas almal by natuur, wild en uitsigte, en lê op 'n logiese roete oos van OR Tambo. Die ander roetes fokus op geskiedenis of vermaak, of is te ver uitmekaar.","en":"Pilanesberg, the Panorama Route and Kruger all match nature, wildlife and views, and lie on a logical route from OR Tambo. The other routes focus on history or entertainment, or are too far apart."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t3-fauna-flora-parke","title":{"af":"Fauna en flora: nasionale parke, oorgrensparke, private wildreservate en botaniese tuine","en":"Fauna and flora: national parks, transfrontier parks, private game reserves and botanical gardens"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal bewaringsbegrippe kan definieer, die voordele van oorgrensparke kan verduidelik, 'n nasionale park met 'n privaat wildreservaat kan vergelyk en sê waarom toeriste botaniese tuine besoek.","en":"You will be able to define conservation concepts, explain the benefits of transfrontier parks, compare a national park with a private game reserve and say why tourists visit botanical gardens."},"summary":{"af":"## Kernbegrippe\n\n- **Omgewing:** alles om ons – die *natuurlike* omgewing (plante, diere, water, landskap), die *fisiese* omgewing (landvorme, klimaat, grond), die *kulturele* omgewing (mense se gewoontes, taal en erfenis) en die *mensgemaakte (geboude)* omgewing (geboue, paaie, dorpe).\n- **Biodiversiteit:** die verskeidenheid van alle lewende organismes – plante, diere en mikro-organismes – in 'n gebied.\n- **Ekosisteem:** 'n gemeenskap van plante en diere wat met mekaar en met hul nie-lewende omgewing (water, grond, lug) in wisselwerking is.\n- **Spesie:** 'n groep organismes wat soortgelyk is en met mekaar kan voortplant.\n- **Fauna** is die diere en **flora** die plante van 'n gebied.\n- **Inheems:** kom natuurlik in 'n gebied voor (nie deur mense ingebring nie), maar kan ook elders voorkom.\n- **Endemies:** kom natuurlik **net** in een spesifieke gebied voor en nêrens anders ter wêreld nie.\n- **Bedreigde spesie:** 'n spesie wat gevaar loop om uit te sterf, bv. die swart renoster weens stropery.\n- **Bewaring:** die beskerming en verstandige bestuur van die natuur sodat toekomstige geslagte dit ook kan geniet.\n- **Die Groot Vyf:** leeu, luiperd, olifant, renoster en buffel – die grootste trekpleister vir wildtoeriste.\n\n> **Onthou!** Fynbos is deel van die **Kaapse Floraryk** – die kleinste van die wêreld se ses floraryke, maar met sowat 9 000 plantspesies, waarvan die meeste endemies is.\n\n## SANParke en nasionale parke\n\n**SANParke** (Suid-Afrikaanse Nasionale Parke) bewaar en bestuur SA se nasionale parke en bevorder **ekotoerisme**.\n\n- **Krugerwildtuin** (Limpopo en Mpumalanga) – die vlagskip: byna 2 miljoen hektaar, die Groot Vyf, ruskampe met chalets en kampeerplekke, wildritte (self of begelei) en bosstaptogte.\n- Ander nasionale parke: Addo-olifant (Oos-Kaap), Tafelberg (Wes-Kaap), Golden Gate Hoogland (Vrystaat), Augrabieswaterval (Noord-Kaap, Oranjerivier), Kgalagadi (Noord-Kaap), Tuinroete (Wes- en Oos-Kaap) en Mapungubwe (Limpopo).\n- **Pilanesberg** (Noordwes, naby Sun City) lê in die krater van 'n uitgedoofde vulkaan en het die Groot Vyf. Dit word deur die Noordwes-parkeraad bestuur, nie deur SANParke nie.\n\n## Oorgrensparke (\"vredesparke\")\n\n'n **Oorgrenspark** (oorgrensbewaringsgebied) is 'n beskermde gebied wat oor die grense van twee of meer lande strek en wat die lande saam bestuur. Sommige heinings tussen die parke word verwyder.\n\n| Oorgrenspark / -bewaringsgebied | Lande |\n|---|---|\n| Kgalagadi-oorgrenspark (Afrika se eerste, 2000) | SA en Botswana |\n| Groot Limpopo-oorgrenspark (sluit Kruger in) | SA, Mosambiek en Zimbabwe |\n| Ai-Ais/Richtersveld-oorgrenspark | SA en Namibië |\n| Maloti-Drakensberg-oorgrensbewaringsgebied | SA en Lesotho |\n| Groter Mapungubwe-oorgrensbewaringsgebied | SA, Botswana en Zimbabwe |\n| Lubombo-oorgrensbewaringsgebied | SA, Mosambiek en Eswatini |\n\n**Voordele van oorgrensparke:**\n\n- Diere kan weer hul ou **trekroetes** oor grense volg; 'n groter gebied bevorder biodiversiteit.\n- Die lande **bemark die gebied saam** as een bestemming, wat meer toeriste lok.\n- **Werk en inkomste** vir plaaslike gemeenskappe.\n- **Vrede en samewerking** tussen lande; hulle deel kennis en koste (bv. teen stropery).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n Oorgrenspark maak nie paspoorte onnodig nie. Toeriste moet steeds deur grensbeheer gaan wanneer hulle van een land na 'n ander ry.\n\n## Luukse privaat wildreservate\n\nCAPS-voorbeelde: **Shamwari** (Oos-Kaap), **Madikwe** (Noordwes – luukse privaat lodges), **Phinda** (KwaZulu-Natal) en **Sabi Sabi** (Mpumalanga, langs die Krugerwildtuin).\n\n| | Nasionale park (bv. Kruger) | Luukse privaat wildreservaat (bv. Sabi Sabi) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Eienaar | Die staat (SANParke) | Privaat eienaars of maatskappye |\n| Koste en teikenmark | Bekostigbaar; gesinne en binnelandse toeriste | Baie duur; welgestelde, dikwels buitelandse toeriste |\n| Akkommodasie | Ruskampe, chalets, kampeerterreine, selfsorg | Luukse suites en lodges, soms met 'n privaat swembad |\n| Wildritte | Self in jou eie motor, of begeleide ritte | Begeleide ritte in oop voertuie met 'n veldgids en spoorsnyer; mag van die pad af ry |\n| Groepgrootte | Baie besoekers | Klein, eksklusiewe groepe |\n| Dienste | Basiese winkels en restaurante | Gourmet-etes, spa, persoonlike diens |\n\n## Nasionale botaniese tuine (SANBI)\n\n'n **Botaniese tuin** is 'n tuin waar plante versamel, gekweek, bewaar en bestudeer word en waar die publiek dit kan geniet. **SANBI** (Suid-Afrikaanse Nasionale Biodiversiteitsinstituut) bestuur die nasionale botaniese tuine.\n\n- **Kirstenbosch** (Kaapstad, teen die hange van Tafelberg, gestig in 1913) – die vlagskip. Dit fokus op inheemse plante en het die boomkruinloopbrug **\"Boomslang\"** en somer-sonsondergangkonserte.\n- **Walter Sisulu NBT** (Roodepoort) – 'n waterval en 'n broeipaar witkruisarende.\n- **Pretoria NBT** – inheemse plante uit die hele land.\n\n**Waarom besoek toeriste botaniese tuine?** Om inheemse en endemiese plante te sien, te stap en te piekniek, konserte by te woon, te leer (skooluitstappies en navorsing), te fotografeer en te ontspan.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kirstenbosch word deur **SANBI** bestuur, nie deur SANParke nie – 'n gewilde strikvraag.","en":"## Key concepts\n\n- **Environment:** everything around us – the *natural* environment (plants, animals, water, landscape), the *physical* environment (landforms, climate, soil), the *cultural* environment (people's customs, language and heritage) and the *man-made (built)* environment (buildings, roads, towns).\n- **Biodiversity:** the variety of all living organisms – plants, animals and micro-organisms – in an area.\n- **Ecosystem:** a community of plants and animals interacting with each other and with their non-living environment (water, soil, air).\n- **Species:** a group of organisms that are similar and can reproduce with each other.\n- **Fauna** are the animals and **flora** the plants of an area.\n- **Indigenous:** occurs naturally in an area (not brought in by people), but may also occur elsewhere.\n- **Endemic:** occurs naturally **only** in one specific area and nowhere else in the world.\n- **Endangered species:** a species at risk of becoming extinct, e.g. the black rhino because of poaching.\n- **Conservation:** protecting and wisely managing nature so that future generations can also enjoy it.\n- **The Big Five:** lion, leopard, elephant, rhinoceros and buffalo – the biggest draw for wildlife tourists.\n\n> **Remember!** Fynbos is part of the **Cape Floral Kingdom** – the smallest of the world's six floral kingdoms, but with about 9 000 plant species, most of them endemic.\n\n## SANParks and national parks\n\n**SANParks** (South African National Parks) conserves and manages SA's national parks and promotes **eco-tourism**.\n\n- **Kruger National Park** (Limpopo and Mpumalanga) – the flagship: nearly 2 million hectares, the Big Five, rest camps with chalets and campsites, game drives (self-drive or guided) and bush walks.\n- Other national parks: Addo Elephant (Eastern Cape), Table Mountain (Western Cape), Golden Gate Highlands (Free State), Augrabies Falls (Northern Cape, Orange River), Kgalagadi (Northern Cape), Garden Route (Western and Eastern Cape) and Mapungubwe (Limpopo).\n- **Pilanesberg** (North West, near Sun City) lies in the crater of an extinct volcano and has the Big Five. It is managed by the North West Parks Board, not by SANParks.\n\n## Transfrontier parks (\"peace parks\")\n\nA **transfrontier park** (transfrontier conservation area) is a protected area that stretches across the borders of two or more countries and that the countries manage together. Some fences between the parks are removed.\n\n| Transfrontier park / conservation area | Countries |\n|---|---|\n| Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park (Africa's first, 2000) | SA and Botswana |\n| Great Limpopo Transfrontier Park (includes Kruger) | SA, Mozambique and Zimbabwe |\n| Ai-Ais/Richtersveld Transfrontier Park | SA and Namibia |\n| Maloti-Drakensberg Transfrontier Conservation Area | SA and Lesotho |\n| Greater Mapungubwe Transfrontier Conservation Area | SA, Botswana and Zimbabwe |\n| Lubombo Transfrontier Conservation Area | SA, Mozambique and Eswatini |\n\n**Benefits of transfrontier parks:**\n\n- Animals can again follow their old **migration routes** across borders; a bigger area promotes biodiversity.\n- The countries **market the area together** as one destination, which attracts more tourists.\n- **Jobs and income** for local communities.\n- **Peace and co-operation** between countries; they share knowledge and costs (e.g. against poaching).\n\n> **Common mistake:** A transfrontier park does not make passports unnecessary. Tourists still have to go through border control when they drive from one country into another.\n\n## Luxury private game reserves\n\nCAPS examples: **Shamwari** (Eastern Cape), **Madikwe** (North West – luxury private lodges), **Phinda** (KwaZulu-Natal) and **Sabi Sabi** (Mpumalanga, next to Kruger National Park).\n\n| | National park (e.g. Kruger) | Luxury private game reserve (e.g. Sabi Sabi) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Owner | The state (SANParks) | Private owners or companies |\n| Cost and target market | Affordable; families and domestic tourists | Very expensive; wealthy, often international tourists |\n| Accommodation | Rest camps, chalets, campsites, self-catering | Luxury suites and lodges, sometimes with a private pool |\n| Game drives | Self-drive in your own car, or guided drives | Guided drives in open vehicles with a ranger and tracker; may drive off-road |\n| Group size | Many visitors | Small, exclusive groups |\n| Services | Basic shops and restaurants | Gourmet meals, spa, personal service |\n\n## National botanical gardens (SANBI)\n\nA **botanical garden** is a garden where plants are collected, grown, conserved and studied, and where the public can enjoy them. **SANBI** (South African National Biodiversity Institute) manages the national botanical gardens.\n\n- **Kirstenbosch** (Cape Town, on the slopes of Table Mountain, founded in 1913) – the flagship. It focuses on indigenous plants and has the tree-canopy walkway **\"Boomslang\"** and summer sunset concerts.\n- **Walter Sisulu NBG** (Roodepoort) – a waterfall and a breeding pair of Verreaux's eagles.\n- **Pretoria NBG** – indigenous plants from the whole country.\n\n**Why do tourists visit botanical gardens?** To see indigenous and endemic plants, to walk and picnic, to attend concerts, to learn (school outings and research), to take photos and to relax.\n\n> **Tip:** Kirstenbosch is managed by **SANBI**, not by SANParks – a popular trick question."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Biodiversiteit","en":"Biodiversity"},"def":{"af":"Die verskeidenheid van alle lewende organismes – plante, diere en mikro-organismes – in 'n gebied.","en":"The variety of all living organisms – plants, animals and micro-organisms – in an area."}},{"term":{"af":"Ekosisteem","en":"Ecosystem"},"def":{"af":"'n Gemeenskap van plante en diere wat met mekaar en met hul nie-lewende omgewing in wisselwerking is.","en":"A community of plants and animals interacting with each other and with their non-living environment."}},{"term":{"af":"Spesie","en":"Species"},"def":{"af":"'n Groep organismes wat soortgelyk is en met mekaar kan voortplant.","en":"A group of organisms that are similar and can reproduce with each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Fauna en flora","en":"Fauna and flora"},"def":{"af":"Fauna is die diere en flora die plante van 'n gebied.","en":"Fauna are the animals and flora the plants of an area."}},{"term":{"af":"Inheems","en":"Indigenous"},"def":{"af":"Kom natuurlik in 'n gebied voor en is nie deur mense ingebring nie; kan ook elders voorkom.","en":"Occurs naturally in an area and was not brought in by people; may also occur elsewhere."}},{"term":{"af":"Endemies","en":"Endemic"},"def":{"af":"Kom natuurlik net in een spesifieke gebied voor en nêrens anders ter wêreld nie.","en":"Occurs naturally only in one specific area and nowhere else in the world."}},{"term":{"af":"Bedreigde spesie","en":"Endangered species"},"def":{"af":"'n Spesie wat gevaar loop om uit te sterf.","en":"A species that is at risk of becoming extinct."}},{"term":{"af":"Bewaring","en":"Conservation"},"def":{"af":"Die beskerming en verstandige bestuur van die natuur sodat toekomstige geslagte dit ook kan geniet.","en":"Protecting and wisely managing nature so that future generations can also enjoy it."}},{"term":{"af":"Oorgrenspark","en":"Transfrontier park"},"def":{"af":"'n Beskermde gebied oor die grense van twee of meer lande wat die lande saam bestuur ('vredespark').","en":"A protected area across the borders of two or more countries that the countries manage together ('peace park')."}},{"term":{"af":"Botaniese tuin","en":"Botanical garden"},"def":{"af":"'n Tuin waar plante versamel, gekweek, bewaar en bestudeer word en wat die publiek kan besoek.","en":"A garden where plants are collected, grown, conserved and studied, and which the public can visit."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk 'n nasionale park met 'n privaat wildreservaat","en":"Compare a national park with a private game reserve"},"problem":{"af":"Die Mokoena-gesin van Brits (twee volwassenes en drie kinders) wil op 'n beperkte begroting die Groot Vyf sien. Mnr. en mev. Rossi van Italië vier hul wittebrood en wil luukse, privaatheid en persoonlike diens. Vergelyk die Krugerwildtuin en Sabi Sabi en beveel vir elkeen 'n bestemming aan.","en":"The Mokoena family from Brits (two adults and three children) wants to see the Big Five on a limited budget. Mr and Mrs Rossi from Italy are on honeymoon and want luxury, privacy and personal service. Compare Kruger National Park and Sabi Sabi and recommend a destination for each."},"steps":[{"af":"Kruger (nasionale park): staatsbesit (SANParke), bekostigbaar, selfsorgchalets en kampeerplekke, eie motor op die paaie.","en":"Kruger (national park): state-owned (SANParks), affordable, self-catering chalets and campsites, own car on the roads."},{"af":"Sabi Sabi (privaat wildreservaat): privaat besit, baie duur, luukse suites, begeleide ritte in oop voertuie, gourmet-etes, spa, klein groepe.","en":"Sabi Sabi (private game reserve): privately owned, very expensive, luxury suites, guided drives in open vehicles, gourmet meals, spa, small groups."},{"af":"Die Mokoenas: Kruger – 'n selfsorgchalet in 'n ruskamp en self ry is goedkoop, en hulle kan steeds die Groot Vyf sien.","en":"The Mokoenas: Kruger – a self-catering chalet in a rest camp and self-drive is cheap, and they can still see the Big Five."},{"af":"Die Rossi's: Sabi Sabi – privaatheid, luukse en persoonlike diens pas by 'n wittebroodspaar met 'n groot begroting.","en":"The Rossis: Sabi Sabi – privacy, luxury and personal service suit a honeymoon couple with a big budget."}],"answer":{"af":"Mokoena-gesin: Krugerwildtuin; die Rossi's: Sabi Sabi.","en":"Mokoena family: Kruger National Park; the Rossis: Sabi Sabi."}},{"title":{"af":"Voordele van oorgrensparke","en":"Benefits of transfrontier parks"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron: 'Sedert die Groot Limpopo-oorgrenspark gestig is, is sommige heinings tussen die Krugerwildtuin en die Limpopo Nasionale Park in Mosambiek verwyder. Olifante beweeg weer oor die grens, en toeriste kan op een reis twee lande besoek.' (a) Watter drie lande deel die Groot Limpopo-oorgrenspark? (b) Noem drie voordele van oorgrensparke.","en":"Read the source: 'Since the Great Limpopo Transfrontier Park was established, some fences between Kruger National Park and the Limpopo National Park in Mozambique have been removed. Elephants are moving across the border again, and tourists can visit two countries on one trip.' (a) Which three countries share the Great Limpopo Transfrontier Park? (b) Name three benefits of transfrontier parks."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Suid-Afrika, Mosambiek en Zimbabwe.","en":"(a) South Africa, Mozambique and Zimbabwe."},{"af":"(b) Voordeel 1 (uit die bron): diere soos olifante kan weer hul ou trekroetes oor die grens volg.","en":"(b) Benefit 1 (from the source): animals such as elephants can again follow their old migration routes across the border."},{"af":"Voordeel 2 (uit die bron): toeriste kan twee lande op een reis besoek – die lande bemark die gebied saam en lok meer toeriste.","en":"Benefit 2 (from the source): tourists can visit two countries on one trip – the countries market the area together and attract more tourists."},{"af":"Voordeel 3: werk en inkomste vir plaaslike gemeenskappe, en vrede en samewerking tussen die lande.","en":"Benefit 3: jobs and income for local communities, and peace and co-operation between the countries."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) SA, Mosambiek, Zimbabwe (b) trekroetes vir diere; gesamentlike bemarking en meer toeriste; werk vir gemeenskappe / samewerking","en":"(a) SA, Mozambique, Zimbabwe (b) migration routes for animals; joint marketing and more tourists; jobs for communities / co-operation"}},{"title":{"af":"Waarom besoek toeriste Kirstenbosch?","en":"Why do tourists visit Kirstenbosch?"},"problem":{"af":"'n Graad 10-klas van Brits gaan op 'n toer na Kaapstad. Hul onderwyser vra: (a) Wie bestuur Kirstenbosch? (b) Gee vier redes waarom toeriste Kirstenbosch besoek. (c) Waarom is fynbos so spesiaal?","en":"A Grade 10 class from Brits is going on a tour to Cape Town. Their teacher asks: (a) Who manages Kirstenbosch? (b) Give four reasons why tourists visit Kirstenbosch. (c) Why is fynbos so special?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) SANBI (Suid-Afrikaanse Nasionale Biodiversiteitsinstituut) – nie SANParke nie.","en":"(a) SANBI (South African National Biodiversity Institute) – not SANParks."},{"af":"(b) Om inheemse plante (bv. fynbos en proteas) te sien; om oor die boomkruinloopbrug 'Boomslang' te stap; om 'n somer-sonsondergangkonsert by te woon; om te leer en te ontspan teen die hange van Tafelberg.","en":"(b) To see indigenous plants (e.g. fynbos and proteas); to walk over the 'Boomslang' tree-canopy walkway; to attend a summer sunset concert; to learn and relax on the slopes of Table Mountain."},{"af":"(c) Fynbos is deel van die Kaapse Floraryk – die kleinste van die ses floraryke, maar met sowat 9 000 spesies, waarvan die meeste endemies is (kom nêrens anders voor nie).","en":"(c) Fynbos is part of the Cape Floral Kingdom – the smallest of the six floral kingdoms, but with about 9 000 species, most of them endemic (found nowhere else)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) SANBI (b) plante, Boomslang, konserte, leer/ontspan (c) baie spesies, meeste endemies","en":"(a) SANBI (b) plants, Boomslang, concerts, learning/relaxing (c) many species, most endemic"}},{"title":{"af":"Pas die begrippe toe","en":"Apply the concepts"},"problem":{"af":"Lees 'n toergids se woorde in 'n wildreservaat in Noordwes: 'Hierdie reservaat is 'n **(a)** – plante, diere, water en grond is van mekaar afhanklik. Hier leef baie verskillende **(b)** soogdiere, onder meer die swart renoster, wat as **(c)** gelys is omdat stropers hom jag. Die bewaarders se taak is **(d)**.' Vul die regte begrippe in.","en":"Read a tour guide's words in a game reserve in North West: 'This reserve is an **(a)** – plants, animals, water and soil depend on each other. Many different **(b)** of mammals live here, including the black rhino, which is listed as **(c)** because poachers hunt it. The rangers' task is **(d)**.' Fill in the correct concepts."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Plante, diere en die nie-lewende omgewing in wisselwerking → ekosisteem.","en":"(a) Plants, animals and the non-living environment interacting → ecosystem."},{"af":"(b) Groepe soortgelyke diere wat met mekaar kan voortplant → spesies.","en":"(b) Groups of similar animals that can reproduce with each other → species."},{"af":"(c) 'n Dier wat gevaar loop om uit te sterf → bedreig ('n bedreigde spesie).","en":"(c) An animal at risk of becoming extinct → endangered (an endangered species)."},{"af":"(d) Om die natuur te beskerm en verstandig te bestuur vir die toekoms → bewaring.","en":"(d) To protect and wisely manage nature for the future → conservation."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) ekosisteem (b) spesies (c) bedreig (d) bewaring","en":"(a) ecosystem (b) species (c) endangered (d) conservation"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter dier is NIE deel van die Groot Vyf nie?","en":"Which animal is NOT part of the Big Five?"},"options":[{"af":"Leeu","en":"Lion"},{"af":"Buffel","en":"Buffalo"},{"af":"Seekoei","en":"Hippopotamus"},{"af":"Luiperd","en":"Leopard"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Groot Vyf is leeu, luiperd, olifant, renoster en buffel. Die seekoei is groot en gevaarlik, maar nie deel van die Groot Vyf nie.","en":"The Big Five are lion, leopard, elephant, rhinoceros and buffalo. The hippo is big and dangerous, but not part of the Big Five."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verskeidenheid van alle lewende organismes – plante, diere en mikro-organismes – in 'n gebied word ___ genoem.","en":"The variety of all living organisms – plants, animals and micro-organisms – in an area is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["biodiversiteit"],"en":["biodiversity","biological diversity"]},"explain":{"af":"Biodiversiteit = bio (lewe) + diversiteit (verskeidenheid). 'n Ekosisteem is die gemeenskap en sy omgewing saam.","en":"Biodiversity = bio (life) + diversity (variety). An ecosystem is the community and its environment together."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ekosisteem","bewaring","habitat"],"en":["ecosystem","conservation","habitat"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Krugerwildtuin lê in die provinsies Limpopo en Mpumalanga.","en":"Kruger National Park lies in the provinces of Limpopo and Mpumalanga."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die noordelike deel is in Limpopo en die suidelike deel in Mpumalanga.","en":"True. The northern part is in Limpopo and the southern part in Mpumalanga."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke oorgrenspark of -bewaringsgebied by die lande wat dit deel.","en":"Match each transfrontier park or conservation area to the countries that share it."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Kgalagadi","en":"Kgalagadi"},"r":{"af":"SA en Botswana","en":"SA and Botswana"}},{"l":{"af":"Groot Limpopo","en":"Great Limpopo"},"r":{"af":"SA, Mosambiek en Zimbabwe","en":"SA, Mozambique and Zimbabwe"}},{"l":{"af":"Ai-Ais/Richtersveld","en":"Ai-Ais/Richtersveld"},"r":{"af":"SA en Namibië","en":"SA and Namibia"}},{"l":{"af":"Maloti-Drakensberg","en":"Maloti-Drakensberg"},"r":{"af":"SA en Lesotho","en":"SA and Lesotho"}},{"l":{"af":"Lubombo","en":"Lubombo"},"r":{"af":"SA, Mosambiek en Eswatini","en":"SA, Mozambique and Eswatini"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kgalagadi – Botswana; Groot Limpopo – Mosambiek en Zimbabwe; Ai-Ais/Richtersveld – Namibië (oor die Oranjerivier); Maloti-Drakensberg – Lesotho; Lubombo – Mosambiek en Eswatini.","en":"Kgalagadi – Botswana; Great Limpopo – Mozambique and Zimbabwe; Ai-Ais/Richtersveld – Namibia (across the Orange River); Maloti-Drakensberg – Lesotho; Lubombo – Mozambique and Eswatini."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken dit as 'n plant 'endemies' is?","en":"What does it mean if a plant is 'endemic'?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is deur mense uit 'n ander land ingebring.","en":"It was brought in by people from another country."},{"af":"Dit groei oral in die wêreld.","en":"It grows everywhere in the world."},{"af":"Dit is reeds uitgesterf.","en":"It is already extinct."},{"af":"Dit kom natuurlik net in een spesifieke gebied voor en nêrens anders nie.","en":"It occurs naturally only in one specific area and nowhere else."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Endemies = net daar en nêrens anders. 'Inheems' beteken dit kom natuurlik voor, maar kan ook elders groei. Ingebringde plante is uitheems.","en":"Endemic = only there and nowhere else. 'Indigenous' means it occurs naturally but may also grow elsewhere. Plants brought in are alien (exotic)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die organisasie wat Suid-Afrika se nasionale parke bewaar en bestuur, is ___.","en":"The organisation that conserves and manages South Africa's national parks is ___."},"answers":{"af":["SANParke","SANParks","Suid-Afrikaanse Nasionale Parke","SA Nasionale Parke"],"en":["SANParks","SANParke","South African National Parks","SA National Parks"]},"explain":{"af":"SANParke bestuur parke soos Kruger, Addo en Kgalagadi. SANBI bestuur die botaniese tuine.","en":"SANParks manages parks such as Kruger, Addo and Kgalagadi. SANBI manages the botanical gardens."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["SANBI","SAHRA","TGCSA"],"en":["SANBI","SAHRA","TGCSA"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter provinsie is die luukse privaat wildreservaat Shamwari?","en":"In which province is the luxury private game reserve Shamwari?"},"options":[{"af":"Oos-Kaap","en":"Eastern Cape"},{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"},{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North West"},{"af":"KwaZulu-Natal","en":"KwaZulu-Natal"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Shamwari – Oos-Kaap; Sabi Sabi – Mpumalanga; Madikwe – Noordwes; Phinda – KwaZulu-Natal.","en":"Shamwari – Eastern Cape; Sabi Sabi – Mpumalanga; Madikwe – North West; Phinda – KwaZulu-Natal."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Kirstenbosch Nasionale Botaniese Tuin word deur SANParke bestuur.","en":"Kirstenbosch National Botanical Garden is managed by SANParks."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die nasionale botaniese tuine, ook Kirstenbosch, word deur SANBI (Suid-Afrikaanse Nasionale Biodiversiteitsinstituut) bestuur.","en":"False. The national botanical gardens, including Kirstenbosch, are managed by SANBI (South African National Biodiversity Institute)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom is fynbos so belangrik vir bewaring en toerisme?","en":"Why is fynbos so important for conservation and tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is die grootste floraryk in die wêreld.","en":"It is the largest floral kingdom in the world."},{"af":"Dit is deel van die Kaapse Floraryk, die kleinste floraryk, met duisende spesies waarvan die meeste endemies is.","en":"It is part of the Cape Floral Kingdom, the smallest floral kingdom, with thousands of species, most of them endemic."},{"af":"Dit groei in alle provinsies van SA ewe veel.","en":"It grows equally in all provinces of SA."},{"af":"Dit is 'n uitheemse plant wat uit Europa ingebring is.","en":"It is an alien plant brought in from Europe."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die Kaapse Floraryk is klein, maar ongelooflik ryk (sowat 9 000 spesies) en die meeste kom nêrens anders voor nie – daarom trek dit toeriste en moet dit bewaar word.","en":"The Cape Floral Kingdom is small but incredibly rich (about 9 000 species) and most are found nowhere else – that is why it draws tourists and must be conserved."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die boomkruinloopbrug 'Boomslang' is 'n gewilde aantreklikheid in die ___ Nasionale Botaniese Tuin.","en":"The 'Boomslang' tree-canopy walkway is a popular attraction in the ___ National Botanical Garden."},"answers":{"af":["Kirstenbosch"],"en":["Kirstenbosch"]},"explain":{"af":"Die Boomslang-loopbrug kronkel deur die boomkruine by Kirstenbosch in Kaapstad.","en":"The Boomslang walkway winds through the treetops at Kirstenbosch in Cape Town."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Walter Sisulu","Pretoria","Pilanesberg"],"en":["Walter Sisulu","Pretoria","Pilanesberg"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeris wil wild in die Krugerwildtuin, die Limpopo Nasionale Park (Mosambiek) en Gonarezhou (Zimbabwe) op een reis sien. Watter oorgrenspark besoek hy?","en":"A tourist wants to see wildlife in Kruger National Park, the Limpopo National Park (Mozambique) and Gonarezhou (Zimbabwe) on one trip. Which transfrontier park is he visiting?"},"options":[{"af":"Kgalagadi-oorgrenspark","en":"Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park"},{"af":"Lubombo-oorgrensbewaringsgebied","en":"Lubombo Transfrontier Conservation Area"},{"af":"Ai-Ais/Richtersveld-oorgrenspark","en":"Ai-Ais/Richtersveld Transfrontier Park"},{"af":"Groot Limpopo-oorgrenspark","en":"Great Limpopo Transfrontier Park"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Groot Limpopo-oorgrenspark verbind Kruger (SA), die Limpopo Nasionale Park (Mosambiek) en Gonarezhou (Zimbabwe).","en":"The Great Limpopo Transfrontier Park links Kruger (SA), the Limpopo National Park (Mozambique) and Gonarezhou (Zimbabwe)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Afrika se eerste oorgrenspark, wat in 2000 deur SA en Botswana gestig is, is die ___-oorgrenspark.","en":"Africa's first transfrontier park, established by SA and Botswana in 2000, is the ___ Transfrontier Park."},"answers":{"af":["Kgalagadi"],"en":["Kgalagadi"]},"explain":{"af":"Die Kgalagadi-oorgrenspark in die Kalahari (Noord-Kaap en Botswana) is in 2000 as Afrika se eerste oorgrenspark geopen.","en":"The Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park in the Kalahari (Northern Cape and Botswana) opened in 2000 as Africa's first transfrontier park."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Groot Limpopo","Lubombo","Mapungubwe"],"en":["Great Limpopo","Lubombo","Mapungubwe"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is NIE 'n voordeel van 'n oorgrenspark nie?","en":"Which statement is NOT a benefit of a transfrontier park?"},"options":[{"af":"Diere kan weer hul ou trekroetes oor grense volg.","en":"Animals can again follow their old migration routes across borders."},{"af":"Dit maak paspoorte en grensbeheer vir toeriste onnodig.","en":"It makes passports and border control unnecessary for tourists."},{"af":"Die lande kan die gebied saam as een bestemming bemark.","en":"The countries can market the area together as one destination."},{"af":"Dit skep werk en inkomste vir plaaslike gemeenskappe.","en":"It creates jobs and income for local communities."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Toeriste moet steeds paspoorte hê en deur grensbeheer gaan. Die ander drie is werklike voordele.","en":"Tourists still need passports and must go through border control. The other three are real benefits."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kenmerk is tipies van 'n luukse privaat wildreservaat eerder as van 'n nasionale park?","en":"Which feature is typical of a luxury private game reserve rather than of a national park?"},"options":[{"af":"Bekostigbare kampeerterreine vir gesinne","en":"Affordable campsites for families"},{"af":"Besoekers ry self in hul eie motors op die paaie","en":"Visitors drive themselves in their own cars on the roads"},{"af":"Ruskampe met selfsorgchalets en 'n winkel","en":"Rest camps with self-catering chalets and a shop"},{"af":"Begeleide wildritte in oop voertuie vir klein groepe, met gourmet-etes ingesluit","en":"Guided game drives in open vehicles for small groups, with gourmet meals included"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Privaat reservate bied eksklusiewe, persoonlike diens: klein groepe, veldgidse, oop voertuie en gourmet-etes. Kampeer, self ry en ruskampe is tipies van nasionale parke.","en":"Private reserves offer exclusive, personal service: small groups, rangers, open vehicles and gourmet meals. Camping, self-drive and rest camps are typical of national parks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As al die renosters in 'n ekosisteem uitgewis word, sal die biodiversiteit van daardie ekosisteem ___.","en":"If all the rhinos in an ecosystem are wiped out, the biodiversity of that ecosystem will ___."},"answers":{"af":["verminder","afneem","daal","minder word"],"en":["decrease","decline","drop","go down","be reduced"]},"explain":{"af":"Elke spesie wat verdwyn, verminder die verskeidenheid van lewe (biodiversiteit). Ander dele van die ekosisteem wat van die spesie afhang, word ook geraak.","en":"Every species that disappears reduces the variety of life (biodiversity). Other parts of the ecosystem that depend on that species are also affected."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vermeerder","dieselfde bly","verdubbel"],"en":["increase","stay the same","double"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Ryk egpaar van Dubai wil vir drie nagte eksklusiewe luukse, 'n spa en privaat wildritte om die Groot Vyf te sien. Watter aanbeveling is die beste?","en":"A wealthy couple from Dubai wants exclusive luxury, a spa and private game drives to see the Big Five for three nights. Which recommendation is best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Kampeerplek in die Kgalagadi-oorgrenspark","en":"A campsite in the Kgalagadi Transfrontier Park"},{"af":"'n Lodge in die Sabi Sabi-privaatwildreservaat","en":"A lodge in the Sabi Sabi private game reserve"},{"af":"'n Dagbesoek aan Kirstenbosch","en":"A day visit to Kirstenbosch"},{"af":"'n Selfsorgchalet in 'n ruskamp in Kruger","en":"A self-catering chalet in a rest camp in Kruger"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Sabi Sabi bied luukse lodges, 'n spa, privaat begeleide ritte en die Groot Vyf – presies wat hulle wil hê. Kampeer en selfsorg is nie luuks nie, en Kirstenbosch het geen wild nie.","en":"Sabi Sabi offers luxury lodges, a spa, private guided drives and the Big Five – exactly what they want. Camping and self-catering are not luxurious, and Kirstenbosch has no game."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t3-volhoubare-toerisme","title":{"af":"Volhoubare en verantwoordelike toerisme en aardverwarming","en":"Sustainable and responsible tourism and global warming"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal volhoubare en verantwoordelike toerisme kan verduidelik, die drie pilare met voorbeelde kan toepas, groen praktyke vir besighede kan voorstel en kan verduidelik hoe aardverwarming toerisme raak.","en":"You will be able to explain sustainable and responsible tourism, apply the three pillars with examples, suggest green practices for businesses and explain how global warming affects tourism."},"summary":{"af":"## Volhoubaarheid en volhoubare toerisme\n\n**Volhoubaarheid** beteken dat ons in vandag se behoeftes voorsien sonder om toekomstige geslagte se vermoë om in húlle behoeftes te voorsien, te benadeel.\n\n**Volhoubare toerisme** voorsien in die behoeftes van vandag se toeriste en gasheergemeenskappe, en beskerm terselfdertyd die omgewing, die kultuur en die plaaslike ekonomie vir die toekoms.\n\n### Die drie pilare (*triple bottom line*)\n\n'n Volhoubare toerisme-onderneming meet sy sukses nie net in geld nie, maar aan drie pilare:\n\n| Pilaar | Wat dit beteken | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Planeet** (omgewing) | Beskerm die natuur en spaar hulpbronne | Herwinning, sonkrag, waterbesparing, 'n inheemse tuin |\n| **Mense** (sosiaal/gemeenskap) | Bevoordeel en respekteer die plaaslike gemeenskap | Plaaslike mense in diens neem en oplei, plaaslike produkte koop, skole en klinieke ondersteun |\n| **Wins** (ekonomies) | Maak 'n regverdige wins wat in die gebied bly | Regverdige lone, wins wat in die gebied herbelê word, 'n besigheid wat lank kan voortbestaan |\n\n> **Wenk:** By 'n bronvraag soek jy eers wat die onderneming *doen*, en vra dan: help dit die omgewing (planeet), die gemeenskap (mense) of die ekonomie (wins)? Haal altyd 'n voorbeeld uit die bron aan. Sommige praktyke pas by meer as een pilaar – verduidelik dan net jou keuse.\n\n## Verantwoordelike toerisme\n\n**Verantwoordelike toerisme** beteken dat toeriste, besighede en gemeenskappe verantwoordelikheid neem vir hul optrede, sodat toerisme beter plekke skep om in te woon én om te besoek.\n\n### Verantwoordelike gedrag van toeriste\n\n- Bly op die gemerkte paadjies en roetes.\n- Moenie rommel strooi nie – neem jou rommel saam.\n- Moenie diere voer of steur nie (bv. bobbejane by piekniekplekke).\n- Moenie plante pluk of klippe en skulpe verwyder nie.\n- Spaar water en elektrisiteit, ook in jou hotelkamer.\n- Respekteer plaaslike kulture: trek gepas aan en vra toestemming voordat jy mense afneem.\n- Koop plaaslike kunsvlyt en produkte, sodat die geld in die gemeenskap bly.\n\n### Negatiewe impakte van toerisme\n\nBesoedeling (lug, water en geraas), rommel, **erosie** (as baie mense van die paadjies afstap), die **steuring van wild**, hoë water- en energieverbruik, en **gekommersialiseerde kultuur** (kultuur word net 'n vertoning vir toeriste en verloor sy betekenis).\n\n### Reëls in natuurlike omgewings\n\nIn parke soos die Pilanesberg-wildtuin bly jy in jou voertuig (behalwe by aangewese plekke), hou jy by die spoedgrens, ry jy net op die paaie, voer jy nie diere nie, raas jy nie en neem jy jou rommel saam.\n\n## Goeie omgewingspraktyke vir besighede\n\n| Area | Praktyke |\n|---|---|\n| Rommelbeheer | Afval skei en herwin, kompos maak, minder plastiek gebruik |\n| Energie | LED-ligte, songeisers, sonpanele, sleutelkaart-skakelaars, bewegingsensors |\n| Water | Laevloei-stortkoppe, handdoek-hergebruikkaartjies, gryswater vir die tuin, reënwatertenks |\n| Ander skaars hulpbronne | Plaaslike en seisoenale kos, minder papier (e-fakture) |\n\n**Voordele vir die besigheid:** laer water- en kragrekeninge, 'n goeie beeld, dit lok \"groen\" toeriste, en dit beskerm die natuur waarvan die besigheid self afhang.\n\n## Aardverwarming\n\nDie **kweekhuiseffek** is 'n natuurlike proses: gasse in die atmosfeer vang van die son se hitte vas en hou die aarde warm genoeg vir lewe. Mense **versterk** hierdie effek deur meer **kweekhuisgasse** vry te stel – veral **koolstofdioksied (CO_{2})** wanneer fossielbrandstowwe (steenkool, petrol, diesel) verbrand word, en **metaan** van vee en vullishope. Meer hitte word vasgevang en die aarde se gemiddelde temperatuur styg. Dit is **aardverwarming**, en dit lei tot **klimaatsverandering**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die kweekhuiseffek self is nie sleg nie – dit is die *versterkte* effek wat aardverwarming veroorsaak. Die gat in die osoonlaag is 'n ander probleem.\n\n### Gevolge vir toerisme\n\n- **Droogtes en watertekorte** – bv. Kaapstad se droogte in 2017–2018 en die \"Day Zero\"-krisis (Dag Nul): hotelle moes streng water spaar en die krisis het sommige toeriste laat wegbly.\n- **Koraalverbleiking** – warmer seewater beskadig koraalriwwe, sodat duikbestemmings (soos Sodwanabaai) minder aantreklik word.\n- **Uiterste weer** – oorstromings, storms, hittegolwe en veldbrande beskadig infrastruktuur en lei tot kansellasies.\n- **Verskuiwende seisoene** – hoog- en laagseisoene, blomseisoene en die trekpatrone van diere verander.\n- **Bedreigde spesies** – plante en diere wat nie kan aanpas nie, verdwyn, en ekotoeriste het minder om te sien.\n\n### Koolstofvoetspoor\n\n'n **Koolstofvoetspoor** is die totale hoeveelheid kweekhuisgasse wat deur 'n persoon, besigheid of aktiwiteit veroorsaak word.\n\n- **Toeriste** kan dit verminder deur minder en direkte vlugte te neem, openbare vervoer (bv. die Gautrain) te gebruik of saam te ry, **koolstofverrekening** te betaal (geld vir projekte soos boomplantery wat net soveel CO_{2} bespaar of opneem), plaaslike kos te eet en energie te spaar.\n- **Besighede** kan sonkrag gebruik, energiedoeltreffende toestelle koop en by plaaslike verskaffers koop.","en":"## Sustainability and sustainable tourism\n\n**Sustainability** means meeting today's needs without harming the ability of future generations to meet *their* needs.\n\n**Sustainable tourism** meets the needs of today's tourists and host communities while protecting the environment, the culture and the local economy for the future.\n\n### The three pillars (triple bottom line)\n\nA sustainable tourism business measures its success not only in money, but against three pillars:\n\n| Pillar | What it means | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Planet** (environment) | Protect nature and save resources | Recycling, solar power, saving water, an indigenous garden |\n| **People** (social/community) | Benefit and respect the local community | Employing and training local people, buying local produce, supporting schools and clinics |\n| **Profit** (economic) | Make a fair profit that stays in the area | Fair wages, profit reinvested in the area, a business that can last |\n\n> **Tip:** In a source question, first find what the business *does*, then ask: does it help the environment (planet), the community (people) or the economy (profit)? Always quote an example from the source. Some practices fit more than one pillar – then simply explain your choice.\n\n## Responsible tourism\n\n**Responsible tourism** means that tourists, businesses and communities take responsibility for their actions, so that tourism creates better places to live in *and* better places to visit.\n\n### Responsible tourist behaviour\n\n- Stay on the marked paths and routes.\n- Don't litter – take your rubbish with you.\n- Don't feed or disturb animals (e.g. baboons at picnic sites).\n- Don't pick plants or remove rocks and shells.\n- Save water and electricity, also in your hotel room.\n- Respect local cultures: dress appropriately and ask permission before photographing people.\n- Buy local crafts and products so that the money stays in the community.\n\n### Negative impacts of tourism\n\nPollution (air, water and noise), litter, **erosion** (when many people leave the paths), **disturbing wildlife**, high water and energy use, and **commercialised culture** (culture becomes just a show for tourists and loses its meaning).\n\n### Rules in natural environments\n\nIn parks such as Pilanesberg Game Reserve you stay in your vehicle (except at designated places), keep to the speed limit, drive only on the roads, don't feed animals, don't make a noise and take your rubbish with you.\n\n## Good environmental practices for businesses\n\n| Area | Practices |\n|---|---|\n| Litter control | Separate and recycle waste, compost, use less plastic |\n| Energy | LED lights, solar geysers, solar panels, key-card switches, motion sensors |\n| Water | Low-flow shower heads, towel-reuse cards, grey water for the garden, rainwater tanks |\n| Other scarce resources | Local and seasonal food, less paper (e-invoices) |\n\n**Benefits for the business:** lower water and electricity bills, a good image, it attracts \"green\" tourists, and it protects the nature the business itself depends on.\n\n## Global warming\n\nThe **greenhouse effect** is a natural process: gases in the atmosphere trap some of the sun's heat and keep the earth warm enough for life. People **intensify** this effect by releasing more **greenhouse gases** – especially **carbon dioxide (CO_{2})** when fossil fuels (coal, petrol, diesel) are burned, and **methane** from livestock and landfills. More heat is trapped and the earth's average temperature rises. This is **global warming**, and it leads to **climate change**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The greenhouse effect itself is not bad – it is the *intensified* effect that causes global warming. The hole in the ozone layer is a different problem.\n\n### Consequences for tourism\n\n- **Droughts and water shortages** – e.g. Cape Town's 2017–2018 drought and the \"Day Zero\" crisis: hotels had to save water strictly and the crisis kept some tourists away.\n- **Coral bleaching** – warmer sea water damages coral reefs, so dive destinations (such as Sodwana Bay) become less attractive.\n- **Extreme weather** – floods, storms, heatwaves and wildfires damage infrastructure and lead to cancellations.\n- **Shifting seasons** – peak and off-peak seasons, flower seasons and animal migration patterns change.\n- **Threatened species** – plants and animals that cannot adapt disappear, and ecotourists have less to see.\n\n### Carbon footprint\n\nA **carbon footprint** is the total amount of greenhouse gases caused by a person, business or activity.\n\n- **Tourists** can reduce it by taking fewer and direct flights, using public transport (e.g. the Gautrain) or sharing lifts, paying for **carbon offsetting** (money for projects such as tree planting that save or absorb the same amount of CO_{2}), eating local food and saving energy.\n- **Businesses** can use solar power, buy energy-efficient appliances and buy from local suppliers."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Volhoubaarheid","en":"Sustainability"},"def":{"af":"Om in vandag se behoeftes te voorsien sonder om toekomstige geslagte se vermoë om in hul eie behoeftes te voorsien, te benadeel.","en":"Meeting today's needs without harming the ability of future generations to meet their own needs."}},{"term":{"af":"Volhoubare toerisme","en":"Sustainable tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme wat in die behoeftes van toeriste en gasheergemeenskappe voorsien en terselfdertyd die omgewing, kultuur en ekonomie vir die toekoms beskerm.","en":"Tourism that meets the needs of tourists and host communities while protecting the environment, culture and economy for the future."}},{"term":{"af":"Drie pilare (planeet, mense, wins)","en":"Three pillars (planet, people, profit)"},"def":{"af":"Die drie areas waaraan 'n volhoubare onderneming sy sukses meet: die omgewing, die gemeenskap en die ekonomie (triple bottom line).","en":"The three areas against which a sustainable business measures its success: the environment, the community and the economy (triple bottom line)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verantwoordelike toerisme","en":"Responsible tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme waar toeriste, besighede en gemeenskappe verantwoordelikheid neem vir hul optrede, sodat plekke beter word om in te woon en te besoek.","en":"Tourism in which tourists, businesses and communities take responsibility for their actions, so that places become better to live in and to visit."}},{"term":{"af":"Kweekhuiseffek","en":"Greenhouse effect"},"def":{"af":"Die natuurlike proses waardeur gasse in die atmosfeer van die son se hitte vasvang en die aarde warm hou.","en":"The natural process by which gases in the atmosphere trap some of the sun's heat and keep the earth warm."}},{"term":{"af":"Kweekhuisgasse","en":"Greenhouse gases"},"def":{"af":"Gasse soos koolstofdioksied (CO₂) en metaan wat hitte in die atmosfeer vasvang.","en":"Gases such as carbon dioxide (CO₂) and methane that trap heat in the atmosphere."}},{"term":{"af":"Aardverwarming","en":"Global warming"},"def":{"af":"Die styging in die aarde se gemiddelde temperatuur omdat mense die kweekhuiseffek versterk.","en":"The rise in the earth's average temperature because people intensify the greenhouse effect."}},{"term":{"af":"Koolstofvoetspoor","en":"Carbon footprint"},"def":{"af":"Die totale hoeveelheid kweekhuisgasse wat deur 'n persoon, besigheid of aktiwiteit veroorsaak word.","en":"The total amount of greenhouse gases caused by a person, business or activity."}},{"term":{"af":"Koolstofverrekening","en":"Carbon offsetting"},"def":{"af":"Om te betaal vir projekte (bv. boomplantery) wat net soveel CO₂ bespaar of opneem as wat jy veroorsaak het.","en":"Paying for projects (e.g. tree planting) that save or absorb as much CO₂ as you caused."}},{"term":{"af":"Gryswater","en":"Grey water"},"def":{"af":"Gebruikte water van storte, baddens en wasbakke wat weer gebruik kan word, bv. om die tuin nat te lei.","en":"Used water from showers, baths and basins that can be reused, e.g. to water the garden."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die drie pilare in 'n bron","en":"The three pillars in a source"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron en beantwoord die vraag.\n\n*Bergwind Eko-lodge in die Magaliesberg kry sy elektrisiteit van sonpanele en skei al sy afval vir herwinning. Twaalf van die vyftien personeellede kom uit die nabygeleë dorpie en is as gidse en kokke opgelei. Die lodge koop sy groente by plaaslike boere, maak 'n gesonde wins en skenk elke jaar 'n deel daarvan aan die plaaslike laerskool.*\n\nIdentifiseer die drie pilare van volhoubare toerisme en gee een voorbeeld van elk uit die bron. (6)","en":"Read the source and answer the question.\n\n*Bergwind Eco-lodge in the Magaliesberg gets its electricity from solar panels and separates all its waste for recycling. Twelve of its fifteen staff members come from the nearby village and were trained as guides and cooks. The lodge buys its vegetables from local farmers, makes a healthy profit and donates part of it to the local primary school every year.*\n\nIdentify the three pillars of sustainable tourism and give one example of each from the source. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die bron en merk elke praktyk wat die lodge doen. Vra dan by elkeen: help dit die omgewing, die gemeenskap of die ekonomie?","en":"Read the source and mark every practice the lodge carries out. Then ask for each one: does it help the environment, the community or the economy?"},{"af":"**Planeet (omgewing):** sonpanele vir elektrisiteit en afval wat vir herwinning geskei word – dit spaar hulpbronne en verminder besoedeling.","en":"**Planet (environment):** solar panels for electricity and waste separated for recycling – this saves resources and reduces pollution."},{"af":"**Mense (gemeenskap):** 12 van die 15 personeellede is plaaslike mense wat as gidse en kokke opgelei is; die lodge ondersteun ook die plaaslike laerskool.","en":"**People (community):** 12 of the 15 staff members are local people trained as guides and cooks; the lodge also supports the local primary school."},{"af":"**Wins (ekonomies):** die lodge maak 'n gesonde wins en die geld bly in die gebied – lone, aankope by plaaslike boere en die skenking aan die skool.","en":"**Profit (economic):** the lodge makes a healthy profit and the money stays in the area – wages, purchases from local farmers and the donation to the school."}],"answer":{"af":"Planeet: sonpanele/herwinning. Mense: plaaslike personeel opgelei/steun die skool. Wins: gesonde wins wat in die gebied bly.","en":"Planet: solar panels/recycling. People: local staff trained/supports the school. Profit: healthy profit that stays in the area."}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die waterbesparing","en":"Calculate the water saving"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gastehuis in Brits vervang sy gewone stortkoppe met laevloei-stortkoppe. 'n Gewone stortkop gebruik 15 liter per minuut en 'n laevloei-stortkop 9 liter per minuut (oefendata). Elke dag stort 20 gaste elk 5 minute.\n\n(a) Hoeveel liter water spaar die gastehuis per dag?\n(b) Hoeveel liter is dit in 'n maand van 30 dae?","en":"A guest house in Brits replaces its ordinary shower heads with low-flow shower heads. An ordinary shower head uses 15 litres per minute and a low-flow shower head 9 litres per minute (practice data). Every day 20 guests each shower for 5 minutes.\n\n(a) How many litres of water does the guest house save per day?\n(b) How many litres is that in a 30-day month?"},"steps":[{"af":"Besparing per minuut: 15 L − 9 L = 6 L","en":"Saving per minute: 15 L − 9 L = 6 L"},{"af":"Besparing per gas (5 minute): 6 L × 5 = 30 L","en":"Saving per guest (5 minutes): 6 L × 5 = 30 L"},{"af":"(a) Besparing per dag (20 gaste): 30 L × 20 = 600 L","en":"(a) Saving per day (20 guests): 30 L × 20 = 600 L"},{"af":"(b) Besparing per maand: 600 L × 30 = 18 000 L. Die gastehuis spaar ook krag, want minder warm water word verhit.","en":"(b) Saving per month: 600 L × 30 = 18 000 L. The guest house also saves electricity, because less hot water is heated."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 600 L per dag  (b) 18 000 L per maand","en":"(a) 600 L per day  (b) 18 000 L per month"}},{"title":{"af":"Groen praktyke vir 'n gastehuis","en":"Green practices for a guest house"},"problem":{"af":"Die eienaar van 'n gastehuis by Hartbeespoortdam wil \"groen\" word. Stel VIER goeie omgewingspraktyke voor (een vir elke area) en noem TWEE voordele vir haar besigheid. (6)","en":"The owner of a guest house at Hartbeespoort Dam wants to go \"green\". Suggest FOUR good environmental practices (one for each area) and name TWO benefits for her business. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Rommelbeheer:** sit aparte houers vir glas, papier, plastiek en blik in en maak kompos van kosafval.","en":"**Litter control:** put out separate bins for glass, paper, plastic and cans and compost food waste."},{"af":"**Energie:** vervang gloeilampe met LED-ligte, installeer 'n songeiser en sleutelkaart-skakelaars in die kamers.","en":"**Energy:** replace bulbs with LED lights, install a solar geyser and key-card switches in the rooms."},{"af":"**Water:** installeer laevloei-stortkoppe, sit handdoek-hergebruikkaartjies in die badkamers en gebruik gryswater of reënwater vir die tuin.","en":"**Water:** install low-flow shower heads, put towel-reuse cards in the bathrooms and use grey water or rainwater for the garden."},{"af":"**Ander hulpbronne:** koop plaaslike, seisoenale kos en stuur e-fakture in plaas van papier.","en":"**Other resources:** buy local, seasonal food and send e-invoices instead of paper."},{"af":"**Voordele:** laer water- en kragrekeninge (meer wins) en 'n goeie, groen beeld wat omgewingsbewuste toeriste lok.","en":"**Benefits:** lower water and electricity bills (more profit) and a good, green image that attracts environmentally aware tourists."}],"answer":{"af":"Bv. herwinning, LED-ligte/songeiser, laevloei-stortkoppe, plaaslike kos; voordele: laer koste en 'n groen beeld wat toeriste lok.","en":"E.g. recycling, LED lights/solar geyser, low-flow shower heads, local food; benefits: lower costs and a green image that attracts tourists."}},{"title":{"af":"Aardverwarming en toerisme","en":"Global warming and tourism"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik hoe aardverwarming toerisme in Suid-Afrika kan raak. Verwys na Kaapstad se \"Day Zero\"-krisis (2017–2018) en noem hoe 'n toeris sy koolstofvoetspoor kan verminder. (6)","en":"Explain how global warming can affect tourism in South Africa. Refer to Cape Town's \"Day Zero\" crisis (2017–2018) and state how a tourist can reduce his carbon footprint. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"Oorsaak: mense verbrand fossielbrandstowwe, wat meer CO₂ vrystel. Dit versterk die kweekhuiseffek en die aarde word warmer.","en":"Cause: people burn fossil fuels, which releases more CO₂. This intensifies the greenhouse effect and the earth becomes warmer."},{"af":"Gevolg: klimaatsverandering bring langer en ergere droogtes. In 2017–2018 het Kaapstad se damme so leeg geraak dat die stad gewaarsku het dat krane kon opdroog (\"Day Zero\").","en":"Effect: climate change brings longer and more severe droughts. In 2017–2018 Cape Town's dams became so low that the city warned the taps could run dry (\"Day Zero\")."},{"af":"Impak op toerisme: hotelle moes waterbeperkings toepas (korter storte, geen baddens nie), en die krisis het sommige toeriste laat wegbly – minder inkomste en werk.","en":"Impact on tourism: hotels had to apply water restrictions (shorter showers, no baths), and the crisis kept some tourists away – less income and fewer jobs."},{"af":"Ander gevolge: koraalverbleiking by duikplekke, uiterste weer wat reise kanselleer, en bedreigde spesies.","en":"Other effects: coral bleaching at dive sites, extreme weather that cancels trips, and threatened species."},{"af":"Koolstofvoetspoor verminder: neem direkte vlugte of gebruik openbare vervoer, ry saam, betaal vir koolstofverrekening, eet plaaslike kos en spaar energie.","en":"Reducing the carbon footprint: take direct flights or use public transport, share lifts, pay for carbon offsetting, eat local food and save energy."}],"answer":{"af":"Aardverwarming → droogtes (Day Zero) → waterbeperkings en minder toeriste; verminder deur openbare vervoer, direkte vlugte, koolstofverrekening en plaaslike kos.","en":"Global warming → droughts (Day Zero) → water restrictions and fewer tourists; reduce by public transport, direct flights, carbon offsetting and local food."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is volhoubare toerisme?","en":"What is sustainable tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Toerisme wat die grootste wins in die kortste moontlike tyd maak","en":"Tourism that makes the biggest profit in the shortest possible time"},{"af":"Toerisme wat net in nasionale parke en natuurreservate plaasvind","en":"Tourism that only takes place in national parks and nature reserves"},{"af":"Toerisme wat in vandag se behoeftes voorsien sonder om toekomstige geslagte te benadeel","en":"Tourism that meets today's needs without harming future generations"},{"af":"Toerisme wat slegs deur die regering bestuur en befonds word","en":"Tourism that is managed and funded only by the government"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Volhoubaarheid gaan oor vandag én die toekoms. Dit is nie net vir natuurgebiede nie – 'n hotel in die stad kan ook volhoubaar wees.","en":"Sustainability is about today and the future. It is not only for natural areas – a hotel in the city can also be sustainable."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die drie pilare van volhoubare toerisme is planeet, mense en ___.","en":"The three pillars of sustainable tourism are planet, people and ___."},"answers":{"af":["wins"],"en":["profit"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["omgewing","bewaring","beplanning"],"en":["environment","conservation","planning"]}},"explain":{"af":"Planeet (omgewing), mense (gemeenskap) en wins (ekonomie). \"Omgewing\" is reeds die planeet-pilaar.","en":"Planet (environment), people (community) and profit (economy). \"Environment\" is already the planet pillar."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die kweekhuiseffek is 'n natuurlike proses wat die aarde warm genoeg vir lewe hou.","en":"The greenhouse effect is a natural process that keeps the earth warm enough for life."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Sonder die kweekhuiseffek sou die aarde te koud vir lewe wees. Die probleem is dat mense die effek versterk.","en":"True. Without the greenhouse effect the earth would be too cold for life. The problem is that people intensify the effect."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kweekhuisgas word veral vrygestel wanneer steenkool en petrol verbrand word?","en":"Which greenhouse gas is mainly released when coal and petrol are burned?"},"options":[{"af":"Suurstof (O₂)","en":"Oxygen (O₂)"},{"af":"Koolstofdioksied (CO₂)","en":"Carbon dioxide (CO₂)"},{"af":"Stikstof (N₂)","en":"Nitrogen (N₂)"},{"af":"Argon (Ar)","en":"Argon (Ar)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Wanneer fossielbrandstowwe verbrand, word koolstofdioksied vrygestel. Suurstof word juis tydens verbranding gebruik, nie vrygestel nie.","en":"When fossil fuels burn, carbon dioxide is released. Oxygen is actually used up during burning, not released."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die totale hoeveelheid kweekhuisgasse wat 'n persoon of aktiwiteit veroorsaak, is sy ___.","en":"The total amount of greenhouse gases caused by a person or activity is their ___."},"answers":{"af":["koolstofvoetspoor","koolstof-voetspoor"],"en":["carbon footprint"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kweekhuiseffek","koolstofverrekening","ekologiese voetspoor"],"en":["greenhouse effect","carbon offset","ecological footprint"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Koolstofvoetspoor meet kweekhuisgasse. Koolstofverrekening is 'n manier om die voetspoor te vergoed, en 'n ekologiese voetspoor meet hoeveel grond en hulpbronne iemand gebruik.","en":"A carbon footprint measures greenhouse gases. Carbon offsetting is a way to compensate for the footprint, and an ecological footprint measures how much land and resources someone uses."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter optrede in 'n nasionale park is verantwoordelike toeristegedrag?","en":"Which action in a national park is responsible tourist behaviour?"},"options":[{"af":"Voer die bobbejane sodat hulle nader kom vir foto's","en":"Feed the baboons so they come closer for photos"},{"af":"Pluk 'n paar veldblomme as aandenking","en":"Pick a few wild flowers as a souvenir"},{"af":"Speel harde musiek by die piekniekplek","en":"Play loud music at the picnic site"},{"af":"Bly op die gemerkte paadjies en neem jou rommel saam","en":"Stay on the marked paths and take your rubbish with you"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Om op die paadjies te bly voorkom erosie, en om jou rommel saam te neem hou die park skoon. Die ander opsies steur diere en beskadig die natuur.","en":"Staying on the paths prevents erosion, and taking your rubbish with you keeps the park clean. The other options disturb animals and damage nature."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruikte water van storte en wasbakke wat weer gebruik word om die tuin nat te lei, word ___ genoem.","en":"Used water from showers and basins that is reused to water the garden is called ___ water."},"answers":{"af":["gryswater","grys water","grys"],"en":["grey","gray","grey water","gray water"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["swartwater","drinkwater","reënwater"],"en":["black","drinking","rain"]}},"explain":{"af":"Gryswater kom van storte, baddens en wasbakke. Swartwater is rioolwater van toilette, en reënwater word van dakke opgevang.","en":"Grey water comes from showers, baths and basins. Black water is sewage from toilets, and rainwater is collected from roofs."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Lodge lei plaaslike jongmense as veldgidse op en help om die dorp se kliniek op te knap. Watter pilaar ondersteun dit hoofsaaklik?","en":"A lodge trains local young people as field guides and helps to renovate the village clinic. Which pillar does this mainly support?"},"options":[{"af":"Mense (sosiaal)","en":"People (social)"},{"af":"Planeet (omgewing)","en":"Planet (environment)"},{"af":"Wins (ekonomies)","en":"Profit (economic)"},{"af":"Geen pilaar nie – dit is net liefdadigheid","en":"No pillar – it is just charity"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Opleiding en die ondersteuning van die kliniek bevoordeel die plaaslike gemeenskap direk – dit is die mense-pilaar.","en":"Training and supporting the clinic benefit the local community directly – that is the people pillar."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die gat in die osoonlaag en aardverwarming is presies dieselfde ding.","en":"The hole in the ozone layer and global warming are exactly the same thing."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Aardverwarming word veroorsaak deur meer kweekhuisgasse wat hitte vasvang. Die osoongat is 'n aparte probleem waardeur meer UV-strale die aarde bereik.","en":"False. Global warming is caused by more greenhouse gases trapping heat. The ozone hole is a separate problem that lets more UV rays reach the earth."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke groen praktyk by die manier waarop dit help.","en":"Match each green practice to the way it helps."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Handdoek-hergebruikkaartjie","en":"Towel-reuse card"},"r":{"af":"Minder wasgoed, dus minder water, energie en waspoeier","en":"Less laundry, so less water, energy and detergent"}},{"l":{"af":"Sleutelkaart-skakelaar","en":"Key-card switch"},"r":{"af":"Die krag in die kamer gaan af wanneer die gas uitstap","en":"The power in the room switches off when the guest leaves"}},{"l":{"af":"Songeiser","en":"Solar geyser"},"r":{"af":"Verhit water met die son se energie","en":"Heats water with the sun's energy"}},{"l":{"af":"Inheemse tuin","en":"Indigenous garden"},"r":{"af":"Plante wat by die plaaslike klimaat aangepas is en minder water nodig het","en":"Plants adapted to the local climate that need less water"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke praktyk spaar 'n hulpbron: wasgoed (water en energie), kamerkrag, energie vir warm water en tuinwater.","en":"Each practice saves a resource: laundry (water and energy), room electricity, energy for hot water and garden water."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Honderde stappers loop van die paadjie af op 'n staproete in die Magaliesberg. Watter negatiewe impak is die waarskynlikste?","en":"Hundreds of hikers walk off the path on a hiking trail in the Magaliesberg. Which negative impact is most likely?"},"options":[{"af":"Koraalverbleiking","en":"Coral bleaching"},{"af":"Gekommersialiseerde kultuur","en":"Commercialised culture"},{"af":"Gronderosie en beskadigde plantegroei","en":"Soil erosion and damaged vegetation"},{"af":"Hoër waterverbruik in hotelle","en":"Higher water use in hotels"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Baie voete vertrap plante en maak die grond los, sodat reën dit wegspoel – erosie. Koraalverbleiking gebeur in die see, nie in die berge nie.","en":"Many feet trample plants and loosen the soil so rain washes it away – erosion. Coral bleaching happens in the sea, not in the mountains."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As 'n toeris betaal vir 'n projek (bv. boomplantery) wat net soveel CO₂ opneem as wat sy vlug veroorsaak het, noem ons dit koolstof___.","en":"If a tourist pays for a project (e.g. tree planting) that absorbs as much CO₂ as his flight caused, we call it carbon ___."},"answers":{"af":["verrekening","koolstofverrekening"],"en":["offsetting","offset","carbon offsetting"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["voetspoor","belasting","handel"],"en":["footprint","tax","trading"]}},"explain":{"af":"Koolstofverrekening \"vergoed\" vir jou uitlatings. Koolstofvoetspoor is die hoeveelheid gasse self, en koolstofbelasting is 'n belasting wat die regering hef.","en":"Carbon offsetting \"compensates\" for your emissions. A carbon footprint is the amount of gases itself, and a carbon tax is a tax charged by government."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gastehuis in Brits wil sy kragrekening verlaag. Watter kombinasie van praktyke is die beste?","en":"A guest house in Brits wants to lower its electricity bill. Which combination of practices is best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Inheemse tuin en reënwatertenks","en":"An indigenous garden and rainwater tanks"},{"af":"Meer herwinningsdromme en 'n komposhoop","en":"More recycling bins and a compost heap"},{"af":"Laat die lugversorgers heeldag aan sodat kamers koel is wanneer gaste terugkom","en":"Leave the air conditioners on all day so rooms are cool when guests return"},{"af":"LED-ligte, 'n songeiser en sleutelkaart-skakelaars in die kamers","en":"LED lights, a solar geyser and key-card switches in the rooms"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"LED-ligte gebruik minder krag, 'n songeiser verhit water met sonkrag en sleutelkaarte skakel krag af in leë kamers. Die tuin en tenks spaar water, en herwinning hanteer afval.","en":"LED lights use less power, a solar geyser heats water with solar energy and key cards switch off power in empty rooms. The garden and tanks save water, and recycling handles waste."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Gewone stortkop gebruik 15 L per minuut en 'n laevloei-stortkop 9 L per minuut. As 12 gaste elk 5 minute stort, spaar die laevloei-stortkoppe ___ liter per dag.","en":"An ordinary shower head uses 15 L per minute and a low-flow shower head 9 L per minute. If 12 guests each shower for 5 minutes, the low-flow shower heads save ___ litres per day."},"answers":{"af":["360","360 L","360 liter"],"en":["360","360 L","360 litres"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["540","900","72"],"en":["540","900","72"]}},"explain":{"af":"(15 − 9) × 5 × 12 = 6 × 60 = 360 L. 900 L is wat gewone stortkoppe gebruik, 540 L wat laevloei-stortkoppe gebruik, en 72 L vergeet die 5 minute.","en":"(15 − 9) × 5 × 12 = 6 × 60 = 360 L. 900 L is what ordinary shower heads use, 540 L what low-flow shower heads use, and 72 L forgets the 5 minutes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bron: *Vroeg in 2018 het Kaapstad gewaarsku dat die krane weens die droogte kon opdroog (\"Day Zero\").* Wat was die waarskynlikste direkte gevolg vir toerisme?","en":"Source: *Early in 2018 Cape Town warned that the taps could run dry because of the drought (\"Day Zero\").* What was the most likely direct effect on tourism?"},"options":[{"af":"Hotelle moes waterbeperkings toepas en sommige toeriste het hul besoeke uitgestel of gekanselleer","en":"Hotels had to apply water restrictions and some tourists postponed or cancelled their visits"},{"af":"Meer toeriste het gekom omdat die strande leër was","en":"More tourists came because the beaches were emptier"},{"af":"Die koraalriwwe by Kaapstad het weens die droogte gebleik","en":"The coral reefs at Cape Town bleached because of the drought"},{"af":"Vlugte na Kaapstad het goedkoper geword omdat vliegtuie water gebruik","en":"Flights to Cape Town became cheaper because aircraft use water"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Watertekort raak hotelle direk (korter storte, geen baddens nie) en maak toeriste huiwerig om te kom. Koraalverbleiking word deur warm seewater veroorsaak, nie deur droogte nie.","en":"A water shortage affects hotels directly (shorter showers, no baths) and makes tourists hesitant to come. Coral bleaching is caused by warm sea water, not by drought."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vier vriende uit Pretoria beplan 'n naweek weg. Watter plan is die volhoubaarste?","en":"Four friends from Pretoria are planning a weekend away. Which plan is the most sustainable?"},"options":[{"af":"Elkeen ry in sy eie motor na Hartbeespoort en hulle eet net by internasionale kitskosketting","en":"Each drives his own car to Hartbeespoort and they eat only at international fast-food chains"},{"af":"Hulle vlieg vir een dag na Kaapstad en terug om die see te sien","en":"They fly to Cape Town and back for one day to see the sea"},{"af":"Hulle ry saam in een motor na Hartbeespoort, bly in 'n plaaslike gastehuis met sonkrag en koop by plaaslike padstalletjies","en":"They share one car to Hartbeespoort, stay at a local guest house with solar power and buy at local farm stalls"},{"af":"Hulle ry saam in een motor, maar voer die ape by die kabelkar en los hul rommel by die dam","en":"They share one car, but feed the monkeys at the cableway and leave their rubbish at the dam"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Saamry verminder die koolstofvoetspoor (planeet), en 'n plaaslike gastehuis en padstalletjies hou geld in die gemeenskap (mense en wins). Die laaste opsie ry saam, maar is onverantwoordelik teenoor die natuur.","en":"Sharing a car reduces the carbon footprint (planet), and a local guest house and farm stalls keep money in the community (people and profit). The last option shares a car but is irresponsible towards nature."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t3-bemarking","title":{"af":"Bemarking","en":"Marketing"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal bemarkingsbegrippe kan definieer, die vyf P's op 'n toerismebesigheid kan toepas, die stappe van marknavorsing kan noem en 'n advertensie kan evalueer.","en":"You will be able to define marketing concepts, apply the five Ps to a tourism business, list the steps of market research and evaluate an advert."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is bemarking?\n\n**Bemarking** is die proses waardeur 'n besigheid uitvind wat kliënte nodig het en wil hê, en dan 'n produk of diens ontwikkel, prys, beskikbaar stel en bevorder om daardie behoeftes winsgewend te bevredig. Bemarking is dus baie meer as net advertensies!\n\n### Die doel van bemarking\n\n- om nuwe kliënte te **lok** en bestaande kliënte te **behou**\n- om kliënte te **inlig** oor produkte, pryse en spesiale aanbiedings\n- om **bewustheid** en 'n goeie **beeld** (handelsmerk) te bou\n- om **verkope** en wins te verhoog\n\n## Belangrike begrippe\n\n| Begrip | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Teikenmark** | Die spesifieke groep kliënte op wie 'n besigheid sy produk en bemarking rig | Gesinne met jong kinders uit Pretoria |\n| **Marksegmentering** | Die verdeling van die mark in kleiner groepe met soortgelyke eienskappe | Volgens ouderdom, inkomste, belangstellings, herkoms |\n| **Markaandeel** | Die persentasie van die totale verkope in 'n mark wat een besigheid het | 15% van al die kamernagte in die dorp |\n| **Nismark** | 'n Klein, gespesialiseerde segment met baie spesifieke behoeftes | Voëlkykers, rolstoelgebruikers |\n| **Mededingende voordeel** | Iets wat jou besigheid beter of aantrekliker as die mededingers maak | Beter diens, laer pryse, beste ligging |\n| **Unieke verkoopspunt (USP)** | 'n Kenmerk wat net jou besigheid bied | Die enigste lodge met sy eie warmlugballon-vertrekpunt |\n\n**Markaandeel bereken:** `markaandeel = eie verkope ÷ totale verkope in die mark × 100`\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders verwar *teikenmark* met *markaandeel*. Die teikenmark is **mense** (wie jy wil bereik); markaandeel is 'n **persentasie** (hoeveel van die mark jy het).\n\n## Die bemarkingsmengsel: die vyf P's\n\nDie **bemarkingsmengsel** is die kombinasie van vyf elemente wat 'n besigheid self beheer om sy teikenmark te bereik. Voorbeeld: 'n gastehuis by Hartbeespoortdam.\n\n1. **Produk** – wat jy verkoop: kamers met en-suite-badkamers, ontbyt, damuitsig, Wi-Fi.\n2. **Prys** – wat die kliënt betaal: R850 pppn, afslag in die laagseisoen, gesinspakkette.\n3. **Plek** – waar en hoe kliënte die produk kry en bespreek: die ligging aan die dam, aanlyn besprekings, reisagente.\n4. **Promosie** – hoe jy kliënte inlig en oorreed: sosiale media, brosjures, 'n webwerf, handelskoue.\n5. **Persone (mense)** – die personeel wat die diens lewer: vriendelike, opgeleide personeel wat gaste se name onthou.\n\n> **Wenk:** In die eksamen moet jy elke P op die **besigheid in die scenario** toepas. 'n Algemene definisie sonder 'n voorbeeld kry nie volpunte nie.\n\n## Marknavorsing\n\n**Marknavorsing** is die stelselmatige insameling en ontleding van inligting oor kliënte, die mark en die mededingers sodat 'n besigheid beter besluite kan neem.\n\n### Stappe van marknavorsing\n\n1. Identifiseer die **probleem of doelwit** (bv. “Hoekom daal ons besprekings in die winter?”).\n2. **Beplan** die navorsing (wie, hoe, wanneer, watter begroting).\n3. **Samel data in** – primêr en sekondêr.\n4. **Ontleed** die data.\n5. **Rapporteer** die bevindinge en **tree op** (neem aksie).\n\n### Primêre en sekondêre data\n\n- **Primêre data:** nuwe inligting wat jy *self eerstehands* insamel – vraelyste, onderhoude, waarneming, terugvoervorms.\n- **Sekondêre data:** inligting wat *reeds bestaan* en deur iemand anders ingesamel is – die internet, statistiek (bv. van Stats SA), verslae, koerante, mededingers se webwerwe.\n\n### Waarna kyk marknavorsing?\n\n- die **potensiële kliënt** (wie is hy en wat wil hy hê?)\n- die **breër teikenmark**\n- die **mededinging** (wat bied en vra die mededingers?)\n\n### Hulpbronne en bestuur\n\n- **Hulpbronne:** die **begroting**; **uitkontraktering** aan navorsingspesialiste; **koöperatiewe navorsingsgroepe** (besighede doen saam navorsing en deel die koste); **individuele navorsing** (die eienaar doen dit self).\n- **Bestuur:** stel **tydsraamwerke**, **teikendatums** en **implementeringsdatums** sodat die navorsing betyds klaar is en die resultate werklik gebruik word.\n\n## Promosie-instrumente en AIDA\n\nPromosie-instrumente sluit in: brosjures, pamflette, webwerwe, sosiale media, advertensies (radio, TV, tydskrifte), mond-tot-mond-reklame en handelskoue (bv. Africa's Travel Indaba in Durban).\n\n'n Goeie advertensie volg die **AIDA**-model:\n\n- **A – Aandag:** 'n opvallende opskrif of foto trek die leser se aandag.\n- **I – Belangstelling:** interessante inligting oor die produk hou die leser se belangstelling.\n- **D – Begeerte:** voordele en 'n spesiale aanbod laat die leser die produk *wil hê*.\n- **A – Aksie:** sê presies wat om te doen (“Bespreek nou!”) en gee kontakbesonderhede.\n\n> **Onthou!** Wanneer jy 'n advertensie evalueer, vra: Is die teikenmark duidelik? Word AIDA gevolg? Is die prys, ligging en kontakbesonderhede gegee? Is die boodskap eerlik en maklik om te lees? Gee altyd 'n rede vir jou oordeel.","en":"## What is marketing?\n\n**Marketing** is the process by which a business finds out what customers need and want, and then develops, prices, distributes and promotes a product or service to satisfy those needs profitably. So marketing is much more than just adverts!\n\n### The purpose of marketing\n\n- to **attract** new customers and **keep** existing customers\n- to **inform** customers about products, prices and special offers\n- to build **awareness** and a good **image** (brand)\n- to increase **sales** and profit\n\n## Important concepts\n\n| Concept | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Target market** | The specific group of customers at whom a business aims its product and marketing | Families with young children from Pretoria |\n| **Market segmentation** | Dividing the market into smaller groups with similar characteristics | By age, income, interests, origin |\n| **Market share** | The percentage of the total sales in a market that one business has | 15% of all the room nights in the town |\n| **Niche market** | A small, specialised segment with very specific needs | Birdwatchers, wheelchair users |\n| **Competitive edge (advantage)** | Something that makes your business better or more attractive than its competitors | Better service, lower prices, best location |\n| **Unique selling point (USP)** | A feature that only your business offers | The only lodge with its own hot-air balloon launch site |\n\n**Calculating market share:** `market share = own sales ÷ total sales in the market × 100`\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners confuse *target market* with *market share*. The target market is **people** (whom you want to reach); market share is a **percentage** (how much of the market you have).\n\n## The marketing mix: the five Ps\n\nThe **marketing mix** is the combination of five elements a business controls to reach its target market. Example: a guest house at Hartbeespoort Dam.\n\n1. **Product** – what you sell: rooms with en suite bathrooms, breakfast, a dam view, Wi-Fi.\n2. **Price** – what the customer pays: R850 pppn, low-season discounts, family packages.\n3. **Place** – where and how customers get and book the product: the location on the dam, online bookings, travel agents.\n4. **Promotion** – how you inform and persuade customers: social media, brochures, a website, trade shows.\n5. **People** – the staff who deliver the service: friendly, trained staff who remember guests' names.\n\n> **Tip:** In the exam you must apply each P to the **business in the scenario**. A general definition without an example does not earn full marks.\n\n## Market research\n\n**Market research** is the systematic collection and analysis of information about customers, the market and competitors so that a business can make better decisions.\n\n### Steps of market research\n\n1. Identify the **problem or objective** (e.g. \"Why do our bookings drop in winter?\").\n2. **Plan** the research (who, how, when, what budget).\n3. **Collect data** – primary and secondary.\n4. **Analyse** the data.\n5. **Report** the findings and **act** on them.\n\n### Primary and secondary data\n\n- **Primary data:** new information you collect *yourself, first-hand* – questionnaires, interviews, observation, feedback forms.\n- **Secondary data:** information that *already exists* and was collected by someone else – the internet, statistics (e.g. from Stats SA), reports, newspapers, competitors' websites.\n\n### What does market research look at?\n\n- the **potential customer** (who is he and what does he want?)\n- the **broader target market**\n- the **competition** (what do competitors offer and charge?)\n\n### Resources and management\n\n- **Resources:** the **budget**; **outsourcing** to research specialists; **co-operative research groups** (businesses research together and share the cost); **individual research** (the owner does it himself).\n- **Management:** set **time frames**, **target dates** and **implementation dates** so that the research is finished on time and the results are actually used.\n\n## Promotion tools and AIDA\n\nPromotion tools include: brochures, flyers, websites, social media, adverts (radio, TV, magazines), word of mouth and trade shows (e.g. Africa's Travel Indaba in Durban).\n\nA good advert follows the **AIDA** model:\n\n- **A – Attention:** an eye-catching headline or photo grabs the reader's attention.\n- **I – Interest:** interesting information about the product holds the reader's interest.\n- **D – Desire:** benefits and a special offer make the reader *want* the product.\n- **A – Action:** tell the reader exactly what to do (\"Book now!\") and give contact details.\n\n> **Remember!** When you evaluate an advert, ask: Is the target market clear? Does it follow AIDA? Are the price, location and contact details given? Is the message honest and easy to read? Always give a reason for your judgement."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bemarking","en":"Marketing"},"def":{"af":"Die proses om kliënte se behoeftes te bepaal en 'n produk of diens te ontwikkel, prys, beskikbaar te stel en te bevorder om daardie behoeftes winsgewend te bevredig.","en":"The process of identifying customers' needs and developing, pricing, distributing and promoting a product or service to satisfy those needs profitably."}},{"term":{"af":"Teikenmark","en":"Target market"},"def":{"af":"Die spesifieke groep kliënte op wie 'n besigheid sy produkte en bemarking rig.","en":"The specific group of customers at whom a business aims its products and marketing."}},{"term":{"af":"Marksegmentering","en":"Market segmentation"},"def":{"af":"Die verdeling van die totale mark in kleiner groepe met soortgelyke eienskappe, bv. ouderdom, inkomste, belangstellings en herkoms.","en":"Dividing the total market into smaller groups with similar characteristics, e.g. age, income, interests and origin."}},{"term":{"af":"Markaandeel","en":"Market share"},"def":{"af":"Die persentasie van die totale verkope in 'n mark wat een besigheid verower het.","en":"The percentage of the total sales in a market that one business has captured."}},{"term":{"af":"Nismark","en":"Niche market"},"def":{"af":"'n Klein, gespesialiseerde marksegment met baie spesifieke behoeftes, bv. voëlkykers.","en":"A small, specialised market segment with very specific needs, e.g. birdwatchers."}},{"term":{"af":"Mededingende voordeel","en":"Competitive edge (advantage)"},"def":{"af":"'n Eienskap wat 'n besigheid beter of aantrekliker as sy mededingers maak, bv. beter diens, 'n beter prys of 'n unieke verkoopspunt.","en":"A quality that makes a business better or more attractive than its competitors, e.g. better service, a better price or a unique selling point."}},{"term":{"af":"Bemarkingsmengsel (vyf P's)","en":"Marketing mix (five Ps)"},"def":{"af":"Die kombinasie van produk, prys, plek, promosie en persone wat 'n besigheid gebruik om sy teikenmark te bereik.","en":"The combination of product, price, place, promotion and people that a business uses to reach its target market."}},{"term":{"af":"Marknavorsing","en":"Market research"},"def":{"af":"Die stelselmatige insameling en ontleding van inligting oor kliënte, die mark en mededingers om beter besluite te neem.","en":"The systematic collection and analysis of information about customers, the market and competitors in order to make better decisions."}},{"term":{"af":"Primêre data","en":"Primary data"},"def":{"af":"Nuwe inligting wat die navorser self eerstehands insamel, bv. met vraelyste, onderhoude, waarneming of terugvoervorms.","en":"New information the researcher collects first-hand, e.g. with questionnaires, interviews, observation or feedback forms."}},{"term":{"af":"Sekondêre data","en":"Secondary data"},"def":{"af":"Bestaande inligting wat reeds deur iemand anders ingesamel is, bv. op die internet, in statistiek en in verslae.","en":"Existing information already collected by someone else, e.g. on the internet, in statistics and in reports."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Pas die vyf P's toe op 'n gastehuis","en":"Apply the five Ps to a guest house"},"problem":{"af":"Die Damsig-gastehuis by Hartbeespoortdam wil jong paartjies uit Pretoria vir naweekwegbreke lok. Pas elkeen van die vyf P's van die bemarkingsmengsel op die gastehuis toe.","en":"The Damsig Guest House at Hartbeespoort Dam wants to attract young couples from Pretoria for weekend breaks. Apply each of the five Ps of the marketing mix to the guest house."},"steps":[{"af":"**Produk:** Romantiese kamers met 'n damuitsig, 'n spa-bad, ontbyt in die bed en 'n sonsondergang-bootrit as ekstra.","en":"**Product:** Romantic rooms with a dam view, a spa bath, breakfast in bed and a sunset boat cruise as an extra."},{"af":"**Prys:** 'n Naweekpakket vir twee (bv. R1 900 per kamer per nag met ontbyt) en 'n afslag as hulle Sondagnag ook bly – mededingend vir die teikenmark se begroting.","en":"**Price:** A weekend package for two (e.g. R1 900 per room per night with breakfast) and a discount if they also stay on Sunday night – competitive for the target market's budget."},{"af":"**Plek:** Net 'n uur se ry van Pretoria af; gaste kan aanlyn op die webwerf of via 'n besprekingsprogram bespreek.","en":"**Place:** Only an hour's drive from Pretoria; guests can book online on the website or through a booking app."},{"af":"**Promosie:** Instagram- en Facebook-plasings met foto's van die sonsondergang, 'n Valentynsdag-aanbod en mond-tot-mond-reklame deur tevrede gaste.","en":"**Promotion:** Instagram and Facebook posts with sunset photos, a Valentine's Day offer and word of mouth from satisfied guests."},{"af":"**Persone:** Vriendelike, opgeleide personeel wat gaste by name groet en spesiale versoeke (bv. 'n verjaardagkoek) reël.","en":"**People:** Friendly, trained staff who greet guests by name and arrange special requests (e.g. a birthday cake)."}],"answer":{"af":"Elke P word op die gastehuis en sy teikenmark (jong paartjies uit Pretoria) toegepas: romantiese produk, mededingende pakketprys, maklike ligging en aanlyn bespreking, sosiale media-promosie en vriendelike personeel.","en":"Each P is applied to the guest house and its target market (young couples from Pretoria): a romantic product, a competitive package price, an easy location and online booking, social media promotion and friendly staff."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed 'n advertensie","en":"Analyse an advert"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die beskrywing van die advertensie: Die opskrif in groot, rooi letters lees “AVONTUUR WAG IN DIE MAGALIESBERG!”. Daar is 'n foto van jong mense wat abseil en bergfiets ry. Die teks sê: “Ziplines, abseil en bergfietsroetes vir alle vlakke. Studente kry 20% afslag met 'n geldige studentekaart. Kampeerterrein met braaiplekke.” Onderaan staan: “Bespreek nou op WhatsApp” met 'n nommer en 'n webwerfadres. (a) Identifiseer die teikenmark. (b) Toon aan hoe die advertensie AIDA volg. (c) Stel een verbetering voor.","en":"Read the description of the advert: The headline in big red letters reads \"ADVENTURE AWAITS IN THE MAGALIESBERG!\". There is a photo of young people abseiling and mountain biking. The text says: \"Ziplines, abseiling and mountain-bike trails for all levels. Students get 20% off with a valid student card. Campsite with braai areas.\" At the bottom it says: \"Book now on WhatsApp\" with a number and a website address. (a) Identify the target market. (b) Show how the advert follows AIDA. (c) Suggest one improvement."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die foto van jong mense, die studenteafslag en die kampeerterrein wys die teikenmark is **jong volwassenes/studente wat avontuur soek en op 'n begroting is**.","en":"(a) The photo of young people, the student discount and the campsite show the target market is **young adults/students looking for adventure on a budget**."},{"af":"(b) **Aandag:** die groot, rooi opskrif en aksiefoto. **Belangstelling:** die lys aktiwiteite vir alle vlakke.","en":"(b) **Attention:** the big red headline and action photo. **Interest:** the list of activities for all levels."},{"af":"**Begeerte:** die 20% studenteafslag en braaiplekke laat hulle dit wil hê. **Aksie:** “Bespreek nou op WhatsApp” met kontakbesonderhede.","en":"**Desire:** the 20% student discount and braai areas make them want it. **Action:** \"Book now on WhatsApp\" with contact details."},{"af":"(c) Verbetering: gee die **pryse** en die presiese **ligging/aanwysings**, en noem **veiligheid** (opgeleide gidse, toerusting) sodat ouers en studente vertroue het.","en":"(c) Improvement: give the **prices** and the exact **location/directions**, and mention **safety** (trained guides, equipment) so that parents and students feel confident."}],"answer":{"af":"Teikenmark: jong avontuursoekers/studente op 'n begroting. Die advertensie volg AIDA volledig. Verbetering: voeg pryse, ligging en veiligheidsinligting by.","en":"Target market: young adventure seekers/students on a budget. The advert follows AIDA fully. Improvement: add prices, location and safety information."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan marknavorsing","en":"Plan market research"},"problem":{"af":"Die eienaar van 'n padstal langs die N4 naby Brits sien dat al hoe minder toeriste stop. Beskryf hoe sy die stappe van marknavorsing kan volg, en gee een voorbeeld elk van primêre en sekondêre data wat sy kan insamel.","en":"The owner of a farm stall on the N4 near Brits notices that fewer and fewer tourists stop. Describe how she can follow the steps of market research, and give one example each of primary and secondary data she can collect."},"steps":[{"af":"**1. Probleem/doelwit:** “Hoekom stop minder toeriste, en wat wil hulle by 'n padstal hê?”","en":"**1. Problem/objective:** \"Why are fewer tourists stopping, and what do they want at a farm stall?\""},{"af":"**2. Beplan:** sy doen **individuele navorsing** met 'n klein begroting en stel 'n tydsraamwerk van vier weke met 'n teikendatum.","en":"**2. Plan:** she does **individual research** on a small budget and sets a time frame of four weeks with a target date."},{"af":"**3. Samel data in:** *Primêr* – 'n kort vraelys vir klante en waarneming van hoeveel motors stop. *Sekondêr* – mededingers se webwerwe en aanlyn resensies, en munisipale toerismestatistiek.","en":"**3. Collect data:** *Primary* – a short questionnaire for customers and observing how many cars stop. *Secondary* – competitors' websites and online reviews, and municipal tourism statistics."},{"af":"**4. Ontleed:** sy vind byvoorbeeld dat kliënte skoon toilette, koffie en plaaslike sitrusprodukte verwag.","en":"**4. Analyse:** she finds, for example, that customers expect clean toilets, coffee and local citrus products."},{"af":"**5. Rapporteer en tree op:** sy verbeter die fasiliteite, voeg 'n koffiehoek by en stel 'n implementeringsdatum vas.","en":"**5. Report and act:** she upgrades the facilities, adds a coffee corner and sets an implementation date."}],"answer":{"af":"Volg die vyf stappe: probleem → beplan → samel data in → ontleed → rapporteer en tree op. Primêr: vraelys/waarneming; sekondêr: mededingers se webwerwe/statistiek.","en":"Follow the five steps: problem → plan → collect data → analyse → report and act. Primary: questionnaire/observation; secondary: competitors' websites/statistics."}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken markaandeel","en":"Calculate market share"},"problem":{"af":"Bron: In 2025 het die drie gastehuise in 'n klein dorp saam 12 500 kamernagte verkoop. Gastehuis A het 1 750, gastehuis B 3 125 en gastehuis C 7 625 kamernagte verkoop. Bereken die markaandeel van elke gastehuis.","en":"Source: In 2025 the three guest houses in a small town together sold 12 500 room nights. Guest house A sold 1 750, guest house B 3 125 and guest house C 7 625 room nights. Calculate the market share of each guest house."},"steps":[{"af":"Formule: markaandeel = eie verkope ÷ totale verkope × 100","en":"Formula: market share = own sales ÷ total sales × 100"},{"af":"A: 1 750 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 14%","en":"A: 1 750 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 14%"},{"af":"B: 3 125 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 25%","en":"B: 3 125 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 25%"},{"af":"C: 7 625 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 61%. Kontrole: 14% + 25% + 61% = 100% ✔","en":"C: 7 625 ÷ 12 500 × 100 = 61%. Check: 14% + 25% + 61% = 100% ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"A = 14%, B = 25%, C = 61%. Gastehuis C het die grootste markaandeel.","en":"A = 14%, B = 25%, C = 61%. Guest house C has the largest market share."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n teikenmark?","en":"What is a target market?"},"options":[{"af":"Al die mense in 'n land wat gereeld reis","en":"All the people in a country who travel regularly"},{"af":"Die spesifieke groep kliënte op wie 'n besigheid sy produk en bemarking rig","en":"The specific group of customers at whom a business aims its product and marketing"},{"af":"Die persentasie van die totale verkope wat 'n besigheid het","en":"The percentage of total sales that a business has"},{"af":"Die plek waar 'n produk verkoop word","en":"The place where a product is sold"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die teikenmark is 'n groep mense wat jy wil bereik. Die persentasie van verkope is markaandeel, en die plek is een van die vyf P's.","en":"The target market is a group of people you want to reach. The percentage of sales is market share, and the place is one of the five Ps."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Primêre data is nuwe inligting wat jy self eerstehands insamel, byvoorbeeld met 'n vraelys.","en":"Primary data is new information you collect yourself first-hand, for example with a questionnaire."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Reg – vraelyste, onderhoude, waarneming en terugvoervorms lewer primêre data. Bestaande inligting is sekondêre data.","en":"Correct – questionnaires, interviews, observation and feedback forms give primary data. Existing information is secondary data."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Produk, prys, plek, promosie en persone saam word die ___ genoem.","en":"Product, price, place, promotion and people together are called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["bemarkingsmengsel","die bemarkingsmengsel","vyf P's","die vyf P's"],"en":["marketing mix","the marketing mix","five Ps","the five Ps","five P's"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bemarkingsplan","marknavorsing","teikenmark"],"en":["marketing plan","market research","target market"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die vyf P's vorm saam die bemarkingsmengsel – die elemente wat 'n besigheid self beheer.","en":"The five Ps together form the marketing mix – the elements a business controls itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is NIE een van die vyf P's van die bemarkingsmengsel nie?","en":"Which one is NOT one of the five Ps of the marketing mix?"},"options":[{"af":"Produk","en":"Product"},{"af":"Promosie","en":"Promotion"},{"af":"Persone","en":"People"},{"af":"Wins","en":"Profit"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die vyf P's is produk, prys, plek, promosie en persone. “Wins” (profit) is een van die drie pilare van volhoubare toerisme – moenie die twee lyste meng nie.","en":"The five Ps are product, price, place, promotion and people. \"Profit\" is one of the three pillars of sustainable tourism – don't mix up the two lists."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die AIDA-model staan die laaste A vir ___.","en":"In the AIDA model the last A stands for ___."},"answers":{"af":["aksie"],"en":["action"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aandag","advertensie","aantrekking"],"en":["attention","advertisement","attraction"]}},"explain":{"af":"AIDA = Aandag, Belangstelling (Interest), Begeerte (Desire), Aksie. Die eerste A is aandag; die laaste A is aksie – die leser moet iets doen, bv. bespreek.","en":"AIDA = Attention, Interest, Desire, Action. The first A is attention; the last A is action – the reader must do something, e.g. book."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n bron van sekondêre data?","en":"Which one is a source of secondary data?"},"options":[{"af":"Onderhoude met gaste by ontvangs","en":"Interviews with guests at reception"},{"af":"Terugvoervorms wat gaste in hul kamers invul","en":"Feedback forms guests complete in their rooms"},{"af":"'n Toerismeverslag van Stats SA","en":"A tourism report from Stats SA"},{"af":"Waarneming van hoeveel besoekers by die hek inkom","en":"Observing how many visitors come in at the gate"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Stats SA-verslag bestaan reeds en is deur iemand anders saamgestel – dus sekondêr. Die ander drie samel jy self eerstehands in (primêr).","en":"A Stats SA report already exists and was compiled by someone else – so it is secondary. You collect the other three yourself first-hand (primary)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Klein, gespesialiseerde marksegment met baie spesifieke behoeftes, soos voëlkykers, is 'n ___.","en":"A small, specialised market segment with very specific needs, such as birdwatchers, is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["nismark","nis-mark","nis mark"],"en":["niche market","niche"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["massamark","markaandeel","bemarkingsmengsel"],"en":["mass market","market share","marketing mix"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Nismark is klein en gespesialiseerd. 'n Massamark is die teenoorgestelde: 'n groot, algemene mark.","en":"A niche market is small and specialised. A mass market is the opposite: a large, general market."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gastehuis in Brits bied 25% afslag op kamers in die laagseisoen (winter). Watter P van die bemarkingsmengsel gebruik hulle?","en":"A guest house in Brits offers 25% off rooms in the low season (winter). Which P of the marketing mix are they using?"},"options":[{"af":"Prys","en":"Price"},{"af":"Plek","en":"Place"},{"af":"Produk","en":"Product"},{"af":"Persone","en":"People"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Afslag verander wat die kliënt betaal – dit is prys. (Die afslag moet wel deur promosie bekend gemaak word, maar die afslag self is 'n prysbesluit.)","en":"A discount changes what the customer pays – that is price. (The discount must be made known through promotion, but the discount itself is a pricing decision.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Lodge in die Magaliesberg is die enigste in die gebied met sy eie warmlugballon-vertrekpunt op die perseel. Hierdie kenmerk is die lodge se ___.","en":"A lodge in the Magaliesberg is the only one in the area with its own hot-air balloon launch site on the property. This feature is the lodge's ___."},"options":[{"af":"markaandeel","en":"market share"},{"af":"teikenmark","en":"target market"},{"af":"unieke verkoopspunt (USP)","en":"unique selling point (USP)"},{"af":"nismark","en":"niche market"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Iets wat net een besigheid bied, is 'n unieke verkoopspunt – dit gee die lodge 'n mededingende voordeel. Markaandeel is 'n persentasie; teikenmark en nismark is groepe kliënte.","en":"Something only one business offers is a unique selling point – it gives the lodge a competitive edge. Market share is a percentage; target market and niche market are groups of customers."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Mond-tot-mond-reklame tel nie as 'n promosie-instrument nie, omdat die besigheid nie daarvoor betaal nie.","en":"Word of mouth does not count as a promotion tool, because the business does not pay for it."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – mond-tot-mond-reklame is een van die kragtigste promosie-instrumente. Tevrede gaste vertel ander, en mense vertrou vriende se aanbevelings. Goeie diens “betaal” daarvoor.","en":"False – word of mouth is one of the most powerful promotion tools. Satisfied guests tell others, and people trust friends' recommendations. Good service \"pays\" for it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bron: Die gastehuise in 'n dorp het saam 6 000 kamernagte verkoop, waarvan Gastehuis X 900 verkoop het. Gastehuis X se markaandeel is ___%.","en":"Source: The guest houses in a town together sold 6 000 room nights, of which Guest House X sold 900. Guest House X's market share is ___%."},"answers":{"af":["15","15%","15 %"],"en":["15","15%","15 %"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6,67","9","85"],"en":["6.67","9","85"]}},"explain":{"af":"Markaandeel = 900 ÷ 6 000 × 100 = 15%. Algemene foute: 6 000 ÷ 900 (= 6,67) of 900 ÷ 100 (= 9).","en":"Market share = 900 ÷ 6 000 × 100 = 15%. Common mistakes: 6 000 ÷ 900 (= 6.67) or 900 ÷ 100 (= 9)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke P van die bemarkingsmengsel by die regte voorbeeld vir 'n gastehuis.","en":"Match each P of the marketing mix to the correct example for a guest house."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Produk","en":"Product"},"r":{"af":"Kamers met en-suite-badkamers en ontbyt","en":"Rooms with en suite bathrooms and breakfast"}},{"l":{"af":"Prys","en":"Price"},"r":{"af":"R850 pppn; die derde nag is gratis","en":"R850 pppn; the third night is free"}},{"l":{"af":"Plek","en":"Place"},"r":{"af":"Aanlyn bespreking op die webwerf en via reisagente","en":"Online booking on the website and through travel agents"}},{"l":{"af":"Promosie","en":"Promotion"},"r":{"af":"Facebook-advertensies en brosjures","en":"Facebook adverts and brochures"}},{"l":{"af":"Persone","en":"People"},"r":{"af":"Vriendelike, goed opgeleide personeel","en":"Friendly, well-trained staff"}}],"explain":{"af":"Produk = wat verkoop word; prys = wat dit kos; plek = waar/hoe dit gekoop of bespreek word; promosie = hoe kliënte ingelig word; persone = wie die diens lewer.","en":"Product = what is sold; price = what it costs; place = where/how it is bought or booked; promotion = how customers are informed; people = who delivers the service."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte volgorde van die stappe van marknavorsing?","en":"What is the correct order of the steps of market research?"},"options":[{"af":"Samel data in → identifiseer die probleem → beplan → ontleed → rapporteer en tree op","en":"Collect data → identify the problem → plan → analyse → report and act"},{"af":"Identifiseer die probleem → beplan → samel data in → ontleed → rapporteer en tree op","en":"Identify the problem → plan → collect data → analyse → report and act"},{"af":"Beplan → identifiseer die probleem → ontleed → samel data in → rapporteer en tree op","en":"Plan → identify the problem → analyse → collect data → report and act"},{"af":"Identifiseer die probleem → samel data in → rapporteer → beplan → ontleed","en":"Identify the problem → collect data → report → plan → analyse"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Jy moet eers weet wát jy wil uitvind (probleem), dan beplan, dan data insamel, dit ontleed en laastens rapporteer en optree. Jy kan nie data ontleed voordat jy dit ingesamel het nie.","en":"You must first know what you want to find out (problem), then plan, then collect data, analyse it and finally report and act. You cannot analyse data before you have collected it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Oom Piet wil weet wat ander gastehuise in Brits vra, en lees daarom hulle pryse op hul webwerwe. Die inligting wat hy so kry, is ___ data.","en":"Oom Piet wants to know what other guest houses in Brits charge, so he reads their prices on their websites. The information he gets this way is ___ data."},"answers":{"af":["sekondêre","sekondêr","sekondere"],"en":["secondary"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["primêre","persoonlike","eerstehandse"],"en":["primary","personal","first-hand"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die pryse bestaan reeds en is deur die mededingers self gepubliseer – oom Piet het dit nie self ingesamel nie. Dit is dus sekondêre data.","en":"The prices already exist and were published by the competitors themselves – Oom Piet did not collect them himself. So it is secondary data."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie vir 'n oord by Hartbeespoortdam sê: “Bring die hele span! Kinders onder 12 bly gratis. Plonsdam, springkasteel en braaipakkette vir die gesin. Spesiale skoolvakansie-aanbod!” Wie is die teikenmark?","en":"An advert for a resort at Hartbeespoort Dam says: \"Bring the whole gang! Kids under 12 stay free. Splash pool, jumping castle and family braai packs. Special school-holiday offer!\" Who is the target market?"},"options":[{"af":"Afgetrede paartjies wat rus en stilte soek","en":"Retired couples looking for rest and quiet"},{"af":"Sakereisigers wat 'n konferensie bywoon","en":"Business travellers attending a conference"},{"af":"Rugsakreisigers op 'n wêreldtoer","en":"Backpackers on a world tour"},{"af":"Gesinne met jong kinders","en":"Families with young children"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gratis verblyf vir kinders, 'n springkasteel, gesinsbraaipakkette en 'n skoolvakansie-aanbod wys duidelik na gesinne met jong kinders. Kyk altyd na die leidrade in die advertensie.","en":"Free stays for kids, a jumping castle, family braai packs and a school-holiday offer clearly point to families with young children. Always look for the clues in the advert."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Nuwe gastehuis in Brits het 'n klein bemarkingsbegroting van R2 000 en wil jong volwassenes uit Pretoria lok. Watter promosie-instrument is die BESTE keuse?","en":"A new guest house in Brits has a small marketing budget of R2 000 and wants to attract young adults from Pretoria. Which promotion tool is the BEST choice?"},"options":[{"af":"Betaalde plasings op sosiale media soos Instagram en Facebook, gerig op Pretoria","en":"Paid posts on social media such as Instagram and Facebook, targeted at Pretoria"},{"af":"'n Volbladadvertensie in 'n nasionale koerant","en":"A full-page advert in a national newspaper"},{"af":"'n Advertensie op nasionale televisie","en":"An advert on national television"},{"af":"Gedrukte brosjures wat net by die Brits-biblioteek uitgedeel word","en":"Printed brochures handed out only at the Brits library"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sosiale media is goedkoop, kan op 'n spesifieke gebied en ouderdomsgroep gerig word, en jong volwassenes gebruik dit baie. TV en nasionale koerante is te duur vir R2 000, en brosjures in Brits bereik nie mense in Pretoria nie.","en":"Social media is cheap, can be targeted at a specific area and age group, and young adults use it a lot. TV and national newspapers are too expensive for R2 000, and brochures in Brits do not reach people in Pretoria."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Kultuur- en erfenistoerisme; kommunikasie en kliëntediens","en":"Culture and heritage tourism; communication and customer care"},"topics":[{"id":"toer10-t4-kultuur-erfenis","title":{"af":"Kultuur- en erfenistoerisme","en":"Culture and heritage tourism"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal kultuur en erfenis kan definieer, tasbare en ontasbare erfenis kan onderskei, erfenisterreine kan klassifiseer en kan verduidelik hoekom ons erfenis moet bewaar.","en":"You will be able to define culture and heritage, distinguish tangible from intangible heritage, classify heritage sites and explain why we must conserve heritage."},"summary":{"af":"## Kultuur\n\n**Kultuur** is die manier van lewe van 'n groep mense – hulle oortuigings, gebruike, taal, kos, kleredrag, musiek, dans, kuns, godsdiens en tradisies. Kultuur word aangeleer en van geslag tot geslag oorgedra, maar dit is **dinamies**: dit verander en groei met die tyd.\n\n### Elemente van kultuur\n\n- taal en storievertelling\n- godsdiens en oortuigings\n- kos en kookkuns (bv. pap en vleis, bobotie, potjiekos)\n- kleredrag\n- musiek en dans\n- kuns en handwerk (bv. kralewerk, mandjies, houtsneewerk)\n- gebruike, rituele en seremonies (bv. troues, inisiasie, oesfeeste)\n- argitektuur (boustyle)\n\n**Kulturele diversiteit** is die verskeidenheid van kulture, tale en gelowe in 'n land. Suid-Afrika word die “reënboognasie” genoem: sedert 2023 het ons **12 amptelike tale** (Suid-Afrikaanse Gebaretaal is bygevoeg). Hierdie diversiteit is self 'n groot toeriste-aantreklikheid.\n\n## Erfenis\n\n**Erfenis** is dit wat ons van vorige geslagte erf, vandag waardeer en aan toekomstige geslagte oordra.\n\n| Soort erfenis | Betekenis | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Natuurlike erfenis** | deur die natuur gevorm | berge, watervalle, grotte (Tafelberg, Sudwala-grotte) |\n| **Kulturele erfenis** | deur mense geskep | monumente, museums, geboue, tale, liedjies |\n| **Tasbare erfenis** | iets wat jy kan sien en aanraak | Voortrekkermonument, rotskuns, kralewerk, historiese geboue |\n| **Ontasbare erfenis** | iets wat jy nie kan aanraak nie; dit leef in mense | taal, volksliedjies, stories, rituele, tradisionele danse, resepte |\n\n> **Wenk:** Vra jouself: “Kan ek dit in 'n museum sit of 'n foto daarvan neem?” Indien ja → tasbaar. 'n Geverfde Ndebele-muur is **tasbaar**, maar die *kennis en vaardigheid* om dit te verf is **ontasbaar**.\n\n**Kultuur- en erfenistoerisme** is reis om ander mense se leefwyse, geskiedenis, kuns en erfenis te beleef – bv. 'n besoek aan 'n kultuurdorp, museum, fees of historiese terrein.\n\n## Hoekom moet ons erfenis bewaar?\n\n- **Identiteit:** dit wys wie ons is en waar ons vandaan kom.\n- **Onderrig:** toekomstige geslagte leer uit die verlede – ook uit pynlike geskiedenis soos apartheid.\n- **Trots en versoening:** mense leer hul eie én ander se kulture waardeer.\n- **Toerisme-inkomste:** toeriste betaal toegangsgeld, koop kunsvlyt en bly oor in die gebied.\n- **Werkskepping:** vir gidse, kunstenaars, kunsvlytverkopers en akkommodasie-ondernemings.\n- As erfenis vernietig word, is dit **vir altyd weg** – dit kan nie vervang word nie.\n\n## Erfenisterreine in Suid-Afrika\n\n**Kulturele erfenisterreine:** monumente, museums, historiese geboue, begraafplase en paleontologiese (fossiel-)terreine, bv. die Voortrekkermonument en Freedom Park (Pretoria), Konstitusieheuwel en die Apartheidsmuseum (Johannesburg) en Robbeneiland (Kaapstad).\n\n**Natuurlike erfenisterreine:** berge, watervalle en grotte, bv. die Sudwala-grotte (Mpumalanga) en Tafelberg (Wes-Kaap).\n\n### Wie beskerm ons erfenis?\n\nDie **Wet op Nasionale Erfenishulpbronne (Wet 25 van 1999)** deel erfenisterreine in drie grade in:\n\n| Graad | Vlak | Verantwoordelike owerheid |\n|---|---|---|\n| Graad I | Nasionale erfenisterrein | **SAHRA** (Suid-Afrikaanse Erfenishulpbronagentskap) |\n| Graad II | Provinsiale erfenisterrein | Provinsiale erfenishulpbron-owerheid |\n| Graad III | Plaaslike erfenisterrein | Munisipaliteit |\n\nVerklaarde nasionale erfenisterreine word met 'n amptelike **erfenisplaat** (kenteken) uitgeken. Die wet bepaal ook dat 'n gebou ouer as 60 jaar nie sonder 'n permit verander of gesloop mag word nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** **SAHRA** verklaar **nasionale** erfenisterreine in Suid-Afrika. **UNESCO** lys **Wêrelderfenisterreine** – dit is 'n ander, internasionale lys.\n\n## Erfenis in Noordwes (ons eie provinsie)\n\n- **Taung-skedelfossielterrein** – waar die skedel van die “Taung-kind” in 1924 gevind is; dit is deel van die Wêrelderfenisterrein Fossiel-hominiedterreine van Suid-Afrika.\n- **Mahikeng** – die provinsiale hoofstad met 'n ryk geskiedenis, bv. die beleg van Mafeking (1899–1900) tydens die Anglo-Boereoorlog.\n- **Lesedi-kultuurdorp** naby Hartbeespoortdam – toeriste beleef die tradisionele wonings, kos, danse en musiek van verskillende Suid-Afrikaanse kulture.\n\n## Erfenisdag, kultuurdorpe en feeste\n\n**Erfenisdag** is op **24 September**, en September is **Erfenismaand**. Mense vier hul kultuur met tradisionele klere, kos en musiek – en baie Suid-Afrikaners braai saam. **Kultuurdorpe** (soos Lesedi) wys toeriste hoe verskillende groepe leef. **Kultuurfeeste** soos Aardklop in Potchefstroom en die Nasionale Kunstefees in Makhanda lok duisende besoekers en bring geld in die gebied in.\n\n> **Onthou!** In die eksamen moet jy terreine kan **klassifiseer**: kultureel of natuurlik? tasbaar of ontasbaar? plaaslik, provinsiaal of nasionaal? Gee altyd 'n rede.","en":"## Culture\n\n**Culture** is the way of life of a group of people – their beliefs, customs, language, food, dress, music, dance, art, religion and traditions. Culture is learnt and passed on from generation to generation, but it is **dynamic**: it changes and grows over time.\n\n### Elements of culture\n\n- language and storytelling\n- religion and beliefs\n- food and cooking (e.g. pap and meat, bobotie, potjiekos)\n- dress\n- music and dance\n- art and crafts (e.g. beadwork, baskets, woodcarving)\n- customs, rituals and ceremonies (e.g. weddings, initiation, harvest festivals)\n- architecture (building styles)\n\n**Cultural diversity** is the variety of cultures, languages and beliefs in a country. South Africa is called the \"rainbow nation\": since 2023 we have **12 official languages** (South African Sign Language was added). This diversity is itself a major tourist attraction.\n\n## Heritage\n\n**Heritage** is what we inherit from previous generations, value today and pass on to future generations.\n\n| Type of heritage | Meaning | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Natural heritage** | formed by nature | mountains, waterfalls, caves (Table Mountain, Sudwala Caves) |\n| **Cultural heritage** | created by people | monuments, museums, buildings, languages, songs |\n| **Tangible heritage** | something you can see and touch | Voortrekker Monument, rock art, beadwork, historical buildings |\n| **Intangible heritage** | something you cannot touch; it lives in people | language, folk songs, stories, rituals, traditional dances, recipes |\n\n> **Tip:** Ask yourself: \"Can I put it in a museum or take a photo of it?\" If yes → tangible. A painted Ndebele wall is **tangible**, but the *knowledge and skill* to paint it is **intangible**.\n\n**Culture and heritage tourism** is travel to experience other people's way of life, history, art and heritage – e.g. a visit to a cultural village, museum, festival or historical site.\n\n## Why must we conserve heritage?\n\n- **Identity:** it shows who we are and where we come from.\n- **Education:** future generations learn from the past – also from painful history such as apartheid.\n- **Pride and reconciliation:** people learn to value their own and others' cultures.\n- **Tourism income:** tourists pay entrance fees, buy crafts and stay over in the area.\n- **Job creation:** for guides, artists, craft sellers and accommodation businesses.\n- If heritage is destroyed, it is **gone forever** – it cannot be replaced.\n\n## Heritage sites in South Africa\n\n**Cultural heritage sites:** monuments, museums, historical buildings, graveyards and palaeontological (fossil) sites, e.g. the Voortrekker Monument and Freedom Park (Pretoria), Constitution Hill and the Apartheid Museum (Johannesburg) and Robben Island (Cape Town).\n\n**Natural heritage sites:** mountains, waterfalls and caves, e.g. the Sudwala Caves (Mpumalanga) and Table Mountain (Western Cape).\n\n### Who protects our heritage?\n\nThe **National Heritage Resources Act (Act 25 of 1999)** divides heritage sites into three grades:\n\n| Grade | Level | Responsible authority |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade I | National heritage site | **SAHRA** (South African Heritage Resources Agency) |\n| Grade II | Provincial heritage site | Provincial heritage resources authority |\n| Grade III | Local heritage site | Municipality |\n\nDeclared national heritage sites are identified by an official **heritage plaque** (badge). The Act also states that a building older than 60 years may not be altered or demolished without a permit.\n\n> **Common mistake:** **SAHRA** declares **national** heritage sites in South Africa. **UNESCO** lists **World Heritage Sites** – that is a different, international list.\n\n## Heritage in the North West (our own province)\n\n- **Taung Skull Fossil Site** – where the skull of the \"Taung Child\" was found in 1924; it is part of the Fossil Hominid Sites of South Africa World Heritage Site.\n- **Mahikeng** – the provincial capital with a rich history, e.g. the Siege of Mafeking (1899–1900) during the Anglo-Boer War.\n- **Lesedi Cultural Village** near Hartbeespoort Dam – tourists experience the traditional homes, food, dances and music of different South African cultures.\n\n## Heritage Day, cultural villages and festivals\n\n**Heritage Day** is on **24 September**, and September is **Heritage Month**. People celebrate their culture with traditional clothes, food and music – and many South Africans braai together. **Cultural villages** (such as Lesedi) show tourists how different groups live. **Cultural festivals** such as Aardklop in Potchefstroom and the National Arts Festival in Makhanda attract thousands of visitors and bring money into the area.\n\n> **Remember!** In the exam you must be able to **classify** sites: cultural or natural? tangible or intangible? local, provincial or national? Always give a reason."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kultuur","en":"Culture"},"def":{"af":"Die manier van lewe van 'n groep mense: hul oortuigings, gebruike, taal, kos, kleredrag, musiek, dans, kuns, godsdiens en tradisies.","en":"The way of life of a group of people: their beliefs, customs, language, food, dress, music, dance, art, religion and traditions."}},{"term":{"af":"Erfenis","en":"Heritage"},"def":{"af":"Dit wat ons van vorige geslagte erf, vandag waardeer en aan toekomstige geslagte oordra – natuurlik en kultureel.","en":"What we inherit from previous generations, value today and pass on to future generations – natural and cultural."}},{"term":{"af":"Tasbare erfenis","en":"Tangible heritage"},"def":{"af":"Fisiese erfenis wat jy kan sien en aanraak, bv. monumente, geboue, rotskuns en voorwerpe.","en":"Physical heritage you can see and touch, e.g. monuments, buildings, rock art and objects."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontasbare erfenis","en":"Intangible heritage"},"def":{"af":"Nie-fisiese erfenis wat in mense voortleef, bv. taal, liedjies, stories, rituele, danse en tradisionele kennis.","en":"Non-physical heritage that lives on in people, e.g. language, songs, stories, rituals, dances and traditional knowledge."}},{"term":{"af":"Kulturele diversiteit","en":"Cultural diversity"},"def":{"af":"Die verskeidenheid van kulture, tale en gelowe in 'n land of gemeenskap.","en":"The variety of cultures, languages and beliefs in a country or community."}},{"term":{"af":"Kultuur- en erfenistoerisme","en":"Culture and heritage tourism"},"def":{"af":"Toerisme waar mense reis om ander se leefwyse, geskiedenis, kuns en erfenisterreine te beleef.","en":"Tourism in which people travel to experience others' way of life, history, art and heritage sites."}},{"term":{"af":"Erfenisterrein","en":"Heritage site"},"def":{"af":"'n Plek van kulturele of natuurlike waarde wat beskerm word sodat toekomstige geslagte dit ook kan geniet.","en":"A place of cultural or natural value that is protected so that future generations can also enjoy it."}},{"term":{"af":"SAHRA","en":"SAHRA"},"def":{"af":"Die Suid-Afrikaanse Erfenishulpbronagentskap, wat nasionale (Graad I-) erfenisterreine verklaar en bestuur.","en":"The South African Heritage Resources Agency, which declares and manages national (Grade I) heritage sites."}},{"term":{"af":"Erfenisdag","en":"Heritage Day"},"def":{"af":"'n Openbare vakansiedag op 24 September waarop Suid-Afrikaners hul kulture en erfenis vier; September is Erfenismaand.","en":"A public holiday on 24 September on which South Africans celebrate their cultures and heritage; September is Heritage Month."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Tasbare of ontasbare erfenis?","en":"Tangible or intangible heritage?"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elkeen as tasbare of ontasbare erfenis en gee 'n rede: (a) die Voortrekkermonument, (b) 'n Setswana-lofsang wat mondelings oorgedra word, (c) 'n kralehalssnoer in 'n museum, (d) ouma se melktertresep wat sy vir haar kleinkinders leer, (e) rotskuns in die Drakensberg, (f) 'n tradisionele dans by Lesedi.","en":"Classify each as tangible or intangible heritage and give a reason: (a) the Voortrekker Monument, (b) a Setswana praise song passed on orally, (c) a beaded necklace in a museum, (d) grandma's milk-tart recipe that she teaches her grandchildren, (e) rock art in the Drakensberg, (f) a traditional dance at Lesedi."},"steps":[{"af":"Toets: kan jy dit aanraak of in 'n museum sit? Dan is dit tasbaar. Leef dit in mense se kennis en optrede? Dan is dit ontasbaar.","en":"Test: can you touch it or put it in a museum? Then it is tangible. Does it live in people's knowledge and actions? Then it is intangible."},{"af":"**Tasbaar:** (a) die monument, (c) die halssnoer en (e) die rotskuns – almal fisiese voorwerpe of strukture.","en":"**Tangible:** (a) the monument, (c) the necklace and (e) the rock art – all physical objects or structures."},{"af":"**Ontasbaar:** (b) die lofsang, (d) die resep (die kennis, nie die tert nie) en (f) die dans – dit word deur mense uitgevoer en oorgedra.","en":"**Intangible:** (b) the praise song, (d) the recipe (the knowledge, not the tart) and (f) the dance – they are performed and passed on by people."}],"answer":{"af":"Tasbaar: a, c, e. Ontasbaar: b, d, f.","en":"Tangible: a, c, e. Intangible: b, d, f."}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: moet die ou stasie gesloop word?","en":"Source question: should the old station be demolished?"},"problem":{"af":"Bron: 'n Munisipaliteit in Noordwes wil 'n 110 jaar oue stasiegebou sloop om 'n parkeerterrein te bou. Inwoners protesteer en sê die gebou is deel van die dorp se geskiedenis. (a) Klassifiseer die gebou. (b) Watter wet beskerm die gebou en wat beteken dit vir die munisipaliteit? (c) Gee drie redes hoekom dit bewaar moet word. (d) Stel 'n toerisme-gebruik vir die gebou voor.","en":"Source: A municipality in the North West wants to demolish a 110-year-old station building to build a parking area. Residents protest and say the building is part of the town's history. (a) Classify the building. (b) Which law protects the building and what does it mean for the municipality? (c) Give three reasons why it should be conserved. (d) Suggest a tourism use for the building."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die gebou is **kulturele, tasbare** erfenis – mense het dit gebou en jy kan dit aanraak.","en":"(a) The building is **cultural, tangible** heritage – people built it and you can touch it."},{"af":"(b) Die **Wet op Nasionale Erfenishulpbronne (Wet 25 van 1999)**. Die gebou is ouer as 60 jaar, dus mag dit nie sonder 'n permit van die provinsiale erfenisowerheid gesloop word nie.","en":"(b) The **National Heritage Resources Act (Act 25 of 1999)**. The building is older than 60 years, so it may not be demolished without a permit from the provincial heritage authority."},{"af":"(c) Dit is deel van die dorp se **identiteit**; leerders kan daaruit **leer**; dit kan **toeriste lok** en **werk skep**. As dit gesloop word, is dit vir altyd weg.","en":"(c) It is part of the town's **identity**; learners can **learn** from it; it can **attract tourists** and **create jobs**. If it is demolished, it is gone forever."},{"af":"(d) Omskep dit in 'n klein spoorwegmuseum met 'n koffiewinkel en 'n kunsvlytmark vir plaaslike kunstenaars.","en":"(d) Turn it into a small railway museum with a coffee shop and a craft market for local artists."}],"answer":{"af":"Kulturele, tasbare erfenis wat deur Wet 25 van 1999 beskerm word; bewaar dit vir identiteit, onderrig, toerisme-inkomste en werke, bv. as 'n museum met 'n koffiewinkel.","en":"Cultural, tangible heritage protected by Act 25 of 1999; conserve it for identity, education, tourism income and jobs, e.g. as a museum with a coffee shop."}},{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer erfenisterreine","en":"Classify heritage sites"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elke terrein as kultureel of natuurlik en noem die provinsie: (a) Sudwala-grotte, (b) Konstitusieheuwel, (c) Taung-skedelfossielterrein, (d) Tafelberg. Verduidelik dan watter owerheid verantwoordelik is vir 'n Graad II-terrein.","en":"Classify each site as cultural or natural and name the province: (a) Sudwala Caves, (b) Constitution Hill, (c) Taung Skull Fossil Site, (d) Table Mountain. Then explain which authority is responsible for a Grade II site."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Sudwala-grotte: **natuurlik** (deur die natuur gevorm) – **Mpumalanga**.","en":"(a) Sudwala Caves: **natural** (formed by nature) – **Mpumalanga**."},{"af":"(b) Konstitusieheuwel: **kultureel** (historiese geboue, voormalige tronk) – **Gauteng**.","en":"(b) Constitution Hill: **cultural** (historical buildings, former prison) – **Gauteng**."},{"af":"(c) Taung-skedelfossielterrein: **kultureel** – 'n paleontologiese terrein wat deel is van 'n kulturele Wêrelderfenisterrein – **Noordwes**.","en":"(c) Taung Skull Fossil Site: **cultural** – a palaeontological site that is part of a cultural World Heritage Site – **North West**."},{"af":"(d) Tafelberg: **natuurlik** – **Wes-Kaap**.","en":"(d) Table Mountain: **natural** – **Western Cape**."},{"af":"'n Graad II-terrein is 'n **provinsiale** erfenisterrein en word deur die **provinsiale erfenishulpbron-owerheid** bestuur (Graad I = SAHRA, Graad III = munisipaliteit).","en":"A Grade II site is a **provincial** heritage site and is managed by the **provincial heritage resources authority** (Grade I = SAHRA, Grade III = municipality)."}],"answer":{"af":"Natuurlik: Sudwala (MP), Tafelberg (WK). Kultureel: Konstitusieheuwel (GP), Taung (NW). Graad II = provinsiale erfenishulpbron-owerheid.","en":"Natural: Sudwala (MP), Table Mountain (WC). Cultural: Constitution Hill (GP), Taung (NW). Grade II = provincial heritage resources authority."}},{"title":{"af":"Die waarde van 'n Erfenisdagfees","en":"The value of a Heritage Day festival"},"problem":{"af":"Die Madibeng-munisipaliteit beplan 'n Erfenisdagfees op 24 September in Brits met tradisionele kos, koorsang, kralewerkstalletjies en 'n potjiekoskompetisie. Verduidelik twee ekonomiese en twee sosiale/kulturele voordele vir die gemeenskap.","en":"Madibeng Municipality plans a Heritage Day festival on 24 September in Brits with traditional food, choir singing, beadwork stalls and a potjiekos competition. Explain two economic and two social/cultural benefits for the community."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ekonomies 1:** Stalletjie-eienaars, kokke en kunsvlytverkopers verdien inkomste uit besoekers.","en":"**Economic 1:** Stall owners, cooks and craft sellers earn income from visitors."},{"af":"**Ekonomies 2:** Besoekers van buite Brits spandeer ook by plaaslike winkels, vulstasies en gastehuise – die vermenigvuldigereffek.","en":"**Economic 2:** Visitors from outside Brits also spend at local shops, filling stations and guest houses – the multiplier effect."},{"af":"**Sosiaal/kultureel 1:** Verskillende kultuurgroepe leer mekaar se kos, musiek en tradisies ken – dit bou begrip en versoening.","en":"**Social/cultural 1:** Different cultural groups get to know each other's food, music and traditions – this builds understanding and reconciliation."},{"af":"**Sosiaal/kultureel 2:** Ontasbare erfenis (liedjies, resepte, kralewerkvaardighede) word aan die jeug oorgedra en bewaar, wat trots en identiteit bou.","en":"**Social/cultural 2:** Intangible heritage (songs, recipes, beadwork skills) is passed on to young people and conserved, which builds pride and identity."}],"answer":{"af":"Ekonomies: inkomste vir plaaslike verkopers en die vermenigvuldigereffek. Sosiaal/kultureel: begrip tussen kulture en die oordra van ontasbare erfenis aan die jeug.","en":"Economic: income for local sellers and the multiplier effect. Social/cultural: understanding between cultures and passing intangible heritage on to young people."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is erfenis?","en":"What is heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"Net die geld en eiendom wat ouers aan hul kinders nalaat","en":"Only the money and property parents leave to their children"},{"af":"Die manier waarop 'n groep mense vandag leef","en":"The way a group of people lives today"},{"af":"Dit wat ons van vorige geslagte erf, waardeer en aan toekomstige geslagte oordra","en":"What we inherit from previous generations, value and pass on to future generations"},{"af":"Slegs natuurlike terreine soos berge en grotte","en":"Only natural sites such as mountains and caves"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Erfenis is wat ons erf en oordra – natuurlik én kultureel, tasbaar én ontasbaar. “Die manier van lewe” is die definisie van kultuur.","en":"Heritage is what we inherit and pass on – natural and cultural, tangible and intangible. \"The way of life\" is the definition of culture."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Erfenisdag word op 24 September gevier.","en":"Heritage Day is celebrated on 24 September."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Reg – Erfenisdag is op 24 September, en die hele September is Erfenismaand.","en":"Correct – Heritage Day is on 24 September, and the whole of September is Heritage Month."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sedert Suid-Afrikaanse Gebaretaal in 2023 bygevoeg is, het Suid-Afrika ___ amptelike tale.","en":"Since South African Sign Language was added in 2023, South Africa has ___ official languages."},"answers":{"af":["12","twaalf"],"en":["12","twelve"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["11","9","13"],"en":["11","9","13"]}},"explain":{"af":"Voor 2023 was daar 11 amptelike tale; met Suid-Afrikaanse Gebaretaal is daar nou 12.","en":"Before 2023 there were 11 official languages; with South African Sign Language there are now 12."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Erfenis wat jy kan sien en aanraak, soos monumente, geboue en voorwerpe, word ___ erfenis genoem.","en":"Heritage you can see and touch, such as monuments, buildings and objects, is called ___ heritage."},"answers":{"af":["tasbare","tasbaar"],"en":["tangible"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ontasbare","natuurlike","lewende"],"en":["intangible","natural","living"]}},"explain":{"af":"Tasbare erfenis is fisies. Ontasbare (of lewende) erfenis, soos taal en liedjies, kan jy nie aanraak nie.","en":"Tangible heritage is physical. Intangible (or living) heritage, such as language and songs, cannot be touched."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is NIE 'n element van kultuur nie?","en":"Which one is NOT an element of culture?"},"options":[{"af":"Taal","en":"Language"},{"af":"Kos en kookkuns","en":"Food and cooking"},{"af":"Kleredrag","en":"Dress"},{"af":"Die klimaat van 'n streek","en":"The climate of a region"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Taal, kos en kleredrag is deel van mense se leefwyse. Die klimaat is 'n natuurlike verskynsel – dit kan kultuur beïnvloed, maar is nie self 'n element van kultuur nie.","en":"Language, food and dress are part of people's way of life. Climate is a natural phenomenon – it can influence culture, but it is not itself an element of culture."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van ontasbare erfenis?","en":"Which one is an example of intangible heritage?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Setswana-volksliedjie wat mondelings van geslag tot geslag oorgedra word","en":"A Setswana folk song passed on orally from generation to generation"},{"af":"Die Voortrekkermonument","en":"The Voortrekker Monument"},{"af":"Rotskuns in die Drakensberg","en":"Rock art in the Drakensberg"},{"af":"'n Ndebele-kralehalssnoer in 'n museum","en":"An Ndebele beaded necklace in a museum"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Liedjie leef in mense se geheue en word gesing – dit kan nie aangeraak word nie. Die monument, rotskuns en halssnoer is fisies en dus tasbaar.","en":"A song lives in people's memory and is sung – it cannot be touched. The monument, rock art and necklace are physical and therefore tangible."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Kultuur verander nooit nie; dit bly presies dieselfde van geslag tot geslag.","en":"Culture never changes; it stays exactly the same from generation to generation."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – kultuur is dinamies. Dit word oorgedra, maar mense pas dit aan met tyd, bv. nuwe musiekstyle, kos en klere.","en":"False – culture is dynamic. It is passed on, but people adapt it over time, e.g. new music styles, food and clothes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n natuurlike erfenisterrein?","en":"Which one of the following is a natural heritage site?"},"options":[{"af":"Konstitusieheuwel","en":"Constitution Hill"},{"af":"Tafelberg","en":"Table Mountain"},{"af":"Die Apartheidsmuseum","en":"The Apartheid Museum"},{"af":"Freedom Park","en":"Freedom Park"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Tafelberg is deur die natuur gevorm. Die ander drie is deur mense geskep – dus kulturele erfenisterreine.","en":"Table Mountain was formed by nature. The other three were created by people – so they are cultural heritage sites."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verskeidenheid van kulture, tale en gelowe in 'n land word ___ genoem.","en":"The variety of cultures, languages and beliefs in a country is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["kulturele diversiteit","kultuurdiversiteit","kulturele verskeidenheid","diversiteit"],"en":["cultural diversity","diversity"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kulturele erfenis","kultuurtoerisme","nasionale identiteit"],"en":["cultural heritage","cultural tourism","national identity"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kulturele diversiteit beskryf die verskeidenheid. Suid-Afrika se diversiteit (die “reënboognasie”) lok baie kultuurtoeriste.","en":"Cultural diversity describes the variety. South Africa's diversity (the \"rainbow nation\") attracts many cultural tourists."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke erfenisterrein by die provinsie waarin dit geleë is.","en":"Match each heritage site to the province in which it is located."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Voortrekkermonument","en":"Voortrekker Monument"},"r":{"af":"Gauteng","en":"Gauteng"}},{"l":{"af":"Sudwala-grotte","en":"Sudwala Caves"},"r":{"af":"Mpumalanga","en":"Mpumalanga"}},{"l":{"af":"Taung-skedelfossielterrein","en":"Taung Skull Fossil Site"},"r":{"af":"Noordwes","en":"North West"}},{"l":{"af":"Robbeneiland","en":"Robben Island"},"r":{"af":"Wes-Kaap","en":"Western Cape"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die Voortrekkermonument is in Pretoria (Gauteng); die Sudwala-grotte naby Mbombela (Mpumalanga); Taung in Noordwes; Robbeneiland voor Kaapstad (Wes-Kaap).","en":"The Voortrekker Monument is in Pretoria (Gauteng); the Sudwala Caves near Mbombela (Mpumalanga); Taung in the North West; Robben Island off Cape Town (Western Cape)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die afkorting van die nasionale agentskap wat Graad I- (nasionale) erfenisterreine in Suid-Afrika verklaar, is ___.","en":"The abbreviation of the national agency that declares Grade I (national) heritage sites in South Africa is ___."},"answers":{"af":["SAHRA"],"en":["SAHRA"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["UNESCO","SANParks","SANBI"],"en":["UNESCO","SANParks","SANBI"]}},"explain":{"af":"SAHRA (Suid-Afrikaanse Erfenishulpbronagentskap) verklaar nasionale erfenisterreine. UNESCO lys Wêrelderfenisterreine; SANParks bestuur nasionale parke; SANBI bestuur botaniese tuine.","en":"SAHRA (South African Heritage Resources Agency) declares national heritage sites. UNESCO lists World Heritage Sites; SANParks manages national parks; SANBI manages botanical gardens."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hans, 'n toeris uit Duitsland, besoek Konstitusieheuwel en die Apartheidsmuseum en luister die aand na 'n koor by 'n kultuurdorp. Watter soort toeris is hy hoofsaaklik?","en":"Hans, a tourist from Germany, visits Constitution Hill and the Apartheid Museum and listens to a choir at a cultural village in the evening. What kind of tourist is he mainly?"},"options":[{"af":"Ekotoeris","en":"Ecotourist"},{"af":"Sakereisiger","en":"Business traveller"},{"af":"Avontuurtoeris","en":"Adventure tourist"},{"af":"Kultuur- en erfenistoeris","en":"Culture and heritage tourist"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Al sy aktiwiteite gaan oor geskiedenis, erfenisterreine en kultuur. Hy is ook 'n internasionale toeris, maar die tipe is kultuur- en erfenistoerisme.","en":"All his activities are about history, heritage sites and culture. He is also an international tourist, but the type is culture and heritage tourism."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Plaaslike erfenisterrein wat deur die munisipaliteit bestuur word, is 'n Graad ___-terrein.","en":"A local heritage site managed by the municipality is a Grade ___ site."},"answers":{"af":["III","3","drie"],"en":["III","3","three"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["I","II","IV"],"en":["I","II","IV"]}},"explain":{"af":"Graad I = nasionaal (SAHRA), Graad II = provinsiaal (provinsiale erfenisowerheid), Graad III = plaaslik (munisipaliteit). Daar is geen Graad IV nie.","en":"Grade I = national (SAHRA), Grade II = provincial (provincial heritage authority), Grade III = local (municipality). There is no Grade IV."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Ndebele-vrou leer haar dogter om die kenmerkende geometriese patrone op hul huis se mure te verf. Watter stelling is KORREK?","en":"An Ndebele woman teaches her daughter to paint the distinctive geometric patterns on the walls of their house. Which statement is CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"Die geverfde mure én die vaardigheid is albei ontasbare erfenis.","en":"The painted walls and the skill are both intangible heritage."},{"af":"Die geverfde mure is natuurlike erfenis en die vaardigheid is tasbare erfenis.","en":"The painted walls are natural heritage and the skill is tangible heritage."},{"af":"Die geverfde mure is tasbare erfenis, maar die kennis en vaardigheid om dit te verf is ontasbare erfenis.","en":"The painted walls are tangible heritage, but the knowledge and skill to paint them is intangible heritage."},{"af":"Dit is nie erfenis nie, want die huis is nie deur SAHRA verklaar nie.","en":"It is not heritage, because the house has not been declared by SAHRA."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die mure kan jy sien en aanraak (tasbaar). Die vaardigheid leef in die mense en word van ma na dogter oorgedra (ontasbaar). Erfenis hoef nie amptelik verklaar te wees om erfenis te wees nie.","en":"You can see and touch the walls (tangible). The skill lives in the people and is passed from mother to daughter (intangible). Heritage does not have to be officially declared to be heritage."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Munisipaliteit wil 'n 120 jaar oue gebou in Mahikeng sloop om 'n parkeerterrein te bou. Watter argument is die STERKSTE rede om die gebou te bewaar?","en":"A municipality wants to demolish a 120-year-old building in Mahikeng to build a parking area. Which argument is the STRONGEST reason to conserve the building?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is deel van die dorp se geskiedenis en identiteit, kan erfenistoeriste lok en werk skep, en sal vir altyd weg wees as dit gesloop word.","en":"It is part of the town's history and identity, can attract heritage tourists and create jobs, and will be gone forever if demolished."},{"af":"Ou geboue is altyd goedkoper om in stand te hou as nuwe geboue.","en":"Old buildings are always cheaper to maintain than new buildings."},{"af":"Die wet sê geen gebou in Suid-Afrika mag ooit gesloop word nie.","en":"The law says no building in South Africa may ever be demolished."},{"af":"Net buitelandse toeriste stel belang in erfenis, dus is dit goed vir die ekonomie.","en":"Only foreign tourists are interested in heritage, so it is good for the economy."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste argument noem identiteit, toerisme-inkomste, werke en die feit dat erfenis onvervangbaar is. Die ander is oordrewe of onwaar: die wet vereis 'n permit vir geboue ouer as 60 jaar, maar verbied nie alle sloping nie.","en":"The first argument mentions identity, tourism income, jobs and the fact that heritage is irreplaceable. The others are exaggerated or untrue: the law requires a permit for buildings older than 60 years, but does not forbid all demolition."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die Taung-skedelfossielterrein trek meer besoekers. Watter voorstel sal die terrein die BESTE beskerm en steeds toerisme-inkomste vir die gemeenskap verdien?","en":"The Taung Skull Fossil Site is attracting more visitors. Which suggestion will BEST protect the site while still earning tourism income for the community?"},"options":[{"af":"Laat besoekers klein stukkies fossielrots as soewenirs saamneem.","en":"Let visitors take small pieces of fossil rock home as souvenirs."},{"af":"Begeleide toere met opgeleide plaaslike gidse, gemerkte paadjies, 'n inligtingsentrum en toegangsgeld wat vir bewaring gebruik word.","en":"Guided tours with trained local guides, marked paths, an information centre and entrance fees used for conservation."},{"af":"Sluit die terrein vir altyd vir alle besoekers.","en":"Close the site to all visitors forever."},{"af":"Bou 'n groot hotel reg bo-op die fossielterrein sodat toeriste naby kan bly.","en":"Build a large hotel right on top of the fossil site so that tourists can stay close by."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Begeleide toere en paadjies beskerm die terrein, gidse kry werk, en toegangsgeld betaal vir bewaring. Soewenirs vernietig die erfenis, 'n hotel bo-op beskadig dit, en om dit te sluit lewer geen inkomste of onderrig nie.","en":"Guided tours and paths protect the site, guides get jobs, and entrance fees pay for conservation. Souvenirs destroy the heritage, a hotel on top damages it, and closing it brings no income or education."}}]},{"id":"toer10-t4-kommunikasie-klientediens","title":{"af":"Kommunikasie en kliëntediens","en":"Communication and customer care"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal geskikte kommunikasietegnologie vir 'n toerismescenario kan kies, telefoon- en e-posetiket kan toepas en die gevolge van swak diens kan verduidelik en aanbevelings kan maak.","en":"You will be able to choose suitable communication technology for a tourism scenario, apply telephone and e-mail etiquette, and explain the consequences of poor service and make recommendations."},"summary":{"af":"## Kommunikasietegnologie in toerismebesighede\n\n| Tegnologie | Funksie in toerisme | Voordeel | Nadeel |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Telefoon en skakelbord | oproepe ontvang en na die regte uitbreiding deurskakel | persoonlik en onmiddellik | oproepe kan gemis word |\n| Selfoon en slimfoon (toepassings, WhatsApp) | kontak met gaste en personeel, ook op die pad | draagbaar, vinnig, goedkoop boodskappe | battery, sein en datakoste; lei aandag af |\n| Rekenaar en skootrekenaar | besprekings, rekeninge, e-pos, rekords | stoor baie inligting; werk vinnig | duur; virusse; benodig elektrisiteit |\n| Tablet | spyskaarte, inklokvorms, gidsinligting | lig en maklik om te dra | kan breek of gesteel word |\n| Internet en Wi-Fi | besprekings, e-pos, sosiale media; gaste verwag dit | wêreldwyd, 24/7 | kuberbedrog; swak sein in afgeleë gebiede |\n| E-pos | formele skriftelike kommunikasie | goedkoop; bewys van wat gesê is; aanhegsels | gemors-e-pos; kan oorgesien word |\n| Tweerigtingradio | veldgidse en sekuriteit praat met mekaar | werk sonder selfoonsein | beperkte afstand; almal hoor die boodskap |\n| Verkoopspuntstelsel (POS) | betalings verwerk, verkope en voorraad aanteken | akkuraat; vinnige rekeninge | duur; stelselonderbrekings |\n| Aanlyn besprekingstelsel | gaste bespreek en betaal self | 24/7 beskikbaar; beskikbaarheid word outomaties bygewerk | dubbele besprekings as dit nie gesinchroniseer is nie |\n| GPS | roetes en posisie vir toervoertuie | vind plekke maklik; spaar tyd | kan verkeerde roetes gee; benodig sein |\n\n> **Wenk:** Tydens **beurtkrag** werk baie tegnologie nie sonder rugsteunkrag (kragopwekker, UPS of sonkrag) nie. Noem dit as 'n nadeel – en gee 'n oplossing.\n\n## Mondelinge kommunikasie\n\nPraat **duidelik**, met 'n vriendelike, beleefde **toon**, en vermy sleng.\n\n### Telefoonetiket\n\n1. Antwoord binne **drie luie**.\n2. Groet en noem die **besigheid se naam** en **jou eie naam**: “Goeiemôre, Damsig-gastehuis, Lerato praat. Hoe kan ek help?”\n3. Luister aandagtig en herhaal belangrike besonderhede (datums, name, getalle).\n4. Neem 'n **boodskap** met die **datum**, **tyd**, **naam van die oproeper**, **terugbelnommer** en die **boodskap** self – en jou eie naam.\n5. Bedank die oproeper en wees beleef tot die einde van die oproep.\n\n### Sake-etiket en lyftaal\n\n- **Vergaderings:** wees betyds, sit jou selfoon op stil en berei voor.\n- **Buitelandse toeriste:** groet formeel en wees bewus van kulturele verskille – nie almal skud hande of maak oogkontak op dieselfde manier nie.\n- **Lyftaal:** glimlag, maak oogkontak en staan regop met 'n oop houding. Moenie jou arms vou of op jou foon kyk terwyl 'n gas praat nie.\n\n## Skriftelike kommunikasie\n\n### E-pos en netiket\n\n- 'n duidelike **onderwerplyn** (bv. “Bevestiging van bespreking: 12–14 Desember”)\n- 'n formele **aanhef** (“Geagte mnr. Smit”)\n- **GEEN HOOFLETTERS** nie – dit lees soos skree\n- geen SMS-taal of emoji's in formele e-posse nie\n- kontroleer **spelling** en grammatika\n- 'n professionele **handtekening** (naam, pos, besigheid, telefoonnommer)\n- **antwoord vinnig**, verkieslik binne 24 uur\n\n### Ander skriftelike kommunikasie\n\n- **Webwerwe:** inligting, foto's en aanlyn besprekings.\n- **SMS-boodskappe:** kort bevestigings en herinneringe.\n- **Sosiale media:** promosie en vinnige antwoorde op vrae.\n- **Vraelyste en terugvoervorms:** meet hoe tevrede kliënte is.\n- **Toerismepadtekens:** in Suid-Afrika is toerismetekens **bruin** met wit simbole en skrif. Hulle wys toeriste die pad na aantreklikhede, akkommodasie en dienste.\n\n## Diensuitnemendheid\n\n**Diensuitnemendheid** is wanneer 'n besigheid kliënte se verwagtinge **konsekwent bereik en oortref** – nie net een keer nie, maar elke keer.\n\n**Waarde vir die besigheid:** herhaalkliënte (gaste wat terugkom); positiewe **mond-tot-mond-reklame** en aanlyn **resensies**; 'n **mededingende voordeel**; meer wins. **Waarde vir die toeris:** waarde vir sy geld, 'n aangename en veilige ervaring en goeie herinneringe.\n\n**Gevolge van swak diens:** klagtes; slegte aanlyn resensies; verlore kliënte en inkomste; 'n beskadigde beeld (reputasie); ontevrede personeel en uiteindelik werksverliese.\n\n### Hoe om swak diens te verbeter\n\n- **Opleiding** in kliëntediens en produkkennis.\n- **Terugvoerstelsels:** terugvoervorms, aanlyn opnames, en lees en beantwoord resensies.\n- **Bemagtig personeel** om self probleme op te los.\n- Erken en beloon goeie diens.\n- Hanteer **klagtes** korrek:\n\n1. **Luister** sonder om te onderbreek.\n2. **Vra opreg om verskoning.**\n3. **Los die probleem op** (of sê presies wat gaan gebeur en wanneer).\n4. **Bedank** die gas dat hy dit onder jou aandag gebring het.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie met 'n ontevrede gas **stry** of jouself verdedig nie. 'n Klagte wat goed hanteer word, kan 'n ontevrede gas in 'n lojale kliënt verander.\n\n> **Onthou!** By 'n gevallestudie: (1) identifiseer die swak diens, (2) noem die gevolge vir die besigheid, (3) gee 'n spesifieke aanbeveling vir elke probleem.","en":"## Communication technology in tourism businesses\n\n| Technology | Function in tourism | Advantage | Disadvantage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Telephone and switchboard | receive calls and put them through to the right extension | personal and immediate | calls can be missed |\n| Cellphone and smartphone (apps, WhatsApp) | contact with guests and staff, also on the road | portable, fast, cheap messages | battery, signal and data costs; distracting |\n| Computer and laptop | bookings, accounts, e-mail, records | stores a lot of information; works fast | expensive; viruses; needs electricity |\n| Tablet | menus, check-in forms, guide information | light and easy to carry | can break or be stolen |\n| Internet and Wi-Fi | bookings, e-mail, social media; guests expect it | worldwide, 24/7 | cyber fraud; weak signal in remote areas |\n| E-mail | formal written communication | cheap; proof of what was said; attachments | spam; can be overlooked |\n| Two-way radio | field guides and security talk to each other | works without cellphone signal | limited range; everyone hears the message |\n| Point-of-sale (POS) system | process payments, record sales and stock | accurate; fast bills | expensive; system outages |\n| Online booking system | guests book and pay themselves | available 24/7; availability updates automatically | double bookings if not synchronised |\n| GPS | routes and position for tour vehicles | finds places easily; saves time | can give wrong routes; needs signal |\n\n> **Tip:** During **load-shedding** much technology does not work without backup power (a generator, UPS or solar power). Mention this as a disadvantage – and give a solution.\n\n## Verbal communication\n\nSpeak **clearly**, in a friendly, polite **tone**, and avoid slang.\n\n### Telephone etiquette\n\n1. Answer within **three rings**.\n2. Greet and give the **company's name** and **your own name**: \"Good morning, Damsig Guest House, Lerato speaking. How can I help?\"\n3. Listen carefully and repeat important details (dates, names, numbers).\n4. Take a **message** with the **date**, **time**, **caller's name**, **call-back number** and the **message** itself – and your own name.\n5. Thank the caller and stay polite until the end of the call.\n\n### Business etiquette and body language\n\n- **Meetings:** be on time, put your cellphone on silent and prepare.\n- **Foreign tourists:** greet formally and be aware of cultural differences – not everyone shakes hands or makes eye contact in the same way.\n- **Body language:** smile, make eye contact and stand up straight with an open posture. Don't fold your arms or look at your phone while a guest is talking.\n\n## Written communication\n\n### E-mail and netiquette\n\n- a clear **subject line** (e.g. \"Booking confirmation: 12–14 December\")\n- a formal **greeting** (\"Dear Mr Smit\")\n- **NO CAPITAL LETTERS** – it reads like shouting\n- no SMS language or emojis in formal e-mails\n- check **spelling** and grammar\n- a professional **signature** (name, position, business, phone number)\n- **reply promptly**, preferably within 24 hours\n\n### Other written communication\n\n- **Websites:** information, photos and online bookings.\n- **SMS messages:** short confirmations and reminders.\n- **Social media:** promotion and quick answers to questions.\n- **Surveys and feedback forms:** measure how satisfied customers are.\n- **Tourism road signs:** in South Africa tourism signs are **brown** with white symbols and lettering. They show tourists the way to attractions, accommodation and services.\n\n## Service excellence\n\n**Service excellence** is when a business **consistently meets and exceeds** customers' expectations – not just once, but every time.\n\n**Value for the business:** repeat customers (guests who come back); positive **word of mouth** and online **reviews**; a **competitive edge**; more profit. **Value for the tourist:** value for money, a pleasant and safe experience and good memories.\n\n**Consequences of poor service:** complaints; bad online reviews; lost customers and income; a damaged image (reputation); unhappy staff and eventually job losses.\n\n### How to improve poor service\n\n- **Training** in customer care and product knowledge.\n- **Feedback systems:** feedback forms, online surveys, and reading and answering reviews.\n- **Empower staff** to solve problems themselves.\n- Recognise and reward good service.\n- Handle **complaints** correctly:\n\n1. **Listen** without interrupting.\n2. **Apologise** sincerely.\n3. **Solve the problem** (or say exactly what will happen and when).\n4. **Thank** the guest for bringing it to your attention.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don't **argue** with an unhappy guest or defend yourself. A complaint that is handled well can turn an unhappy guest into a loyal customer.\n\n> **Remember!** In a case study: (1) identify the poor service, (2) name the consequences for the business, (3) give a specific recommendation for each problem."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kommunikasietegnologie","en":"Communication technology"},"def":{"af":"Toestelle en stelsels (bv. telefone, rekenaars, internet, tweerigtingradio's) wat 'n besigheid gebruik om inligting te stuur en te ontvang.","en":"Devices and systems (e.g. telephones, computers, the internet, two-way radios) that a business uses to send and receive information."}},{"term":{"af":"Mondelinge kommunikasie","en":"Verbal communication"},"def":{"af":"Kommunikasie met gesproke woorde, van aangesig tot aangesig of oor die telefoon.","en":"Communication with spoken words, face to face or over the telephone."}},{"term":{"af":"Skriftelike kommunikasie","en":"Written communication"},"def":{"af":"Kommunikasie met geskrewe woorde, bv. e-posse, SMS'e, webwerwe, sosiale media en terugvoervorms.","en":"Communication with written words, e.g. e-mails, SMSes, websites, social media and feedback forms."}},{"term":{"af":"Telefoonetiket","en":"Telephone etiquette"},"def":{"af":"Die reëls vir professionele telefoongebruik, bv. antwoord binne drie luie, noem die besigheid en jou naam, en neem volledige boodskappe.","en":"The rules for professional telephone use, e.g. answer within three rings, give the business and your name, and take complete messages."}},{"term":{"af":"Netiket","en":"Netiquette"},"def":{"af":"Goeie maniere vir aanlyn en e-poskommunikasie, bv. 'n duidelike onderwerplyn, geen hoofletters nie en 'n professionele handtekening.","en":"Good manners for online and e-mail communication, e.g. a clear subject line, no capital letters and a professional signature."}},{"term":{"af":"Lyftaal","en":"Body language"},"def":{"af":"Nie-verbale kommunikasie deur gesigsuitdrukkings, oogkontak, houding en gebare.","en":"Non-verbal communication through facial expressions, eye contact, posture and gestures."}},{"term":{"af":"Diensuitnemendheid","en":"Service excellence"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n besigheid kliënte se verwagtinge konsekwent bereik en oortref.","en":"When a business consistently meets and exceeds customers' expectations."}},{"term":{"af":"Swak dienslewering","en":"Poor service delivery"},"def":{"af":"Diens wat nie aan kliënte se verwagtinge voldoen nie, bv. lang wagtye, onbeleefde personeel of foute met besprekings.","en":"Service that does not meet customers' expectations, e.g. long waiting times, rude staff or booking errors."}},{"term":{"af":"Mond-tot-mond-reklame","en":"Word of mouth"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer kliënte hul ervaring (goed of sleg) aan ander mense vertel, persoonlik of aanlyn.","en":"When customers tell other people about their experience (good or bad), in person or online."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte kommunikasietegnologie","en":"Choose the right communication technology"},"problem":{"af":"'n Lodge in die Pilanesberg het drie behoeftes: (a) veldgidse op 'n wildrit moet met mekaar kommunikeer waar daar geen selfoonsein is nie, (b) toeriste in Duitsland wil self 'n kamer bespreek en betaal, (c) die restaurant moet betalings vinnig en akkuraat verwerk. Beveel vir elkeen 'n tegnologie aan, met een voordeel en een nadeel.","en":"A lodge in the Pilanesberg has three needs: (a) field guides on a game drive must communicate with each other where there is no cellphone signal, (b) tourists in Germany want to book and pay for a room themselves, (c) the restaurant must process payments quickly and accurately. Recommend a technology for each, with one advantage and one disadvantage."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Tweerigtingradio.** Voordeel: werk sonder selfoonsein, so gidse kan mekaar laat weet waar die diere is. Nadeel: beperkte afstand, en almal op die kanaal hoor die boodskap.","en":"(a) **Two-way radio.** Advantage: works without cellphone signal, so guides can tell each other where the animals are. Disadvantage: limited range, and everyone on the channel hears the message."},{"af":"(b) **Aanlyn besprekingstelsel** op die lodge se webwerf. Voordeel: 24/7 beskikbaar, ongeag die tydsverskil, en die beskikbaarheid word outomaties bygewerk. Nadeel: risiko van kuberbedrog; dit benodig internet en krag.","en":"(b) **Online booking system** on the lodge's website. Advantage: available 24/7, regardless of the time difference, and availability updates automatically. Disadvantage: risk of cyber fraud; it needs internet and power."},{"af":"(c) **Verkoopspuntstelsel (POS)** met 'n kaartmasjien. Voordeel: akkurate rekeninge en verkope en voorraad word outomaties aangeteken. Nadeel: duur om aan te koop, en dit werk nie tydens 'n kragonderbreking sonder rugsteunkrag nie.","en":"(c) **Point-of-sale (POS) system** with a card machine. Advantage: accurate bills, and sales and stock are recorded automatically. Disadvantage: expensive to buy, and it does not work during a power outage without backup power."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Tweerigtingradio, (b) aanlyn besprekingstelsel, (c) POS-stelsel – elk met 'n voordeel en nadeel wat op die scenario van toepassing is.","en":"(a) Two-way radio, (b) online booking system, (c) POS system – each with an advantage and disadvantage that apply to the scenario."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter 'n swak e-pos","en":"Correct a badly written e-mail"},"problem":{"af":"'n Ontvangsdame stuur hierdie e-pos aan 'n gas. Onderwerp: (leeg). Teks: “hallo, JOU BESPREKING IS OK. BETAAL DIE DEPOSITO GOU-GOU OF ONS KANSELLEER!!! thx 😀” Daar is geen handtekening nie. Identifiseer die foute en herskryf die e-pos professioneel.","en":"A receptionist sends this e-mail to a guest. Subject: (blank). Text: \"hi, UR BOOKING IS OK. PAY THE DEPOSIT ASAP OR WE CANCEL!!! thx 😀\" There is no signature. Identify the errors and rewrite the e-mail professionally."},"steps":[{"af":"**Foute:** geen onderwerplyn nie; informele aanhef (“hallo”); HOOFLETTERS (skree); dreigende, onbeleefde toon; SMS-taal (“thx”) en 'n emoji; geen besonderhede (datums, bedrag, sperdatum) nie; geen handtekening nie.","en":"**Errors:** no subject line; informal greeting (\"hi\"); CAPITALS (shouting); threatening, rude tone; SMS language (\"ur\", \"asap\", \"thx\") and an emoji; no details (dates, amount, deadline); no signature."},{"af":"**Onderwerp:** Bevestiging van bespreking en deposito – 12–14 Desember","en":"**Subject:** Booking confirmation and deposit – 12–14 December"},{"af":"**Teks:** “Geagte mev. Mokoena. Dankie vir u bespreking vir 12–14 Desember. Ons bevestig graag 'n dubbelkamer vir twee nagte. Betaal asseblief die deposito van 50% teen 30 November om die bespreking te waarborg; die bankbesonderhede is aangeheg.”","en":"**Text:** \"Dear Mrs Mokoena. Thank you for your booking for 12–14 December. We are pleased to confirm a double room for two nights. Please pay the 50% deposit by 30 November to secure the booking; the banking details are attached.\""},{"af":"**Afsluiting en handtekening:** “Ons sien uit daarna om u te verwelkom. Vriendelike groete, Lerato Dlamini, Ontvangsdame, Damsig-gastehuis, met die gastehuis se telefoonnommer.”","en":"**Closing and signature:** \"We look forward to welcoming you. Kind regards, Lerato Dlamini, Receptionist, Damsig Guest House, with the guest house's phone number.\""}],"answer":{"af":"'n Professionele e-pos het 'n duidelike onderwerplyn, formele aanhef, beleefde toon sonder hoofletters of SMS-taal, al die besonderhede en 'n volledige handtekening.","en":"A professional e-mail has a clear subject line, a formal greeting, a polite tone without capitals or SMS language, all the details and a complete signature."}},{"title":{"af":"Gevallestudie: swak diens by 'n restaurant","en":"Case study: poor service at a restaurant"},"problem":{"af":"Bron: 'n Gesin van vier eet by 'n restaurant by Hartbeespoortdam. Hulle wag 45 minute vir hul kos terwyl die kelner op sy foon is. Die verkeerde bestelling word gebring, en toe die pa kla, stry die bestuurder met hom. (a) Noem drie gevolge vir die restaurant. (b) Gee drie aanbevelings om die diens te verbeter.","en":"Source: A family of four eats at a restaurant at Hartbeespoort Dam. They wait 45 minutes for their food while the waiter is on his phone. The wrong order is brought, and when the father complains, the manager argues with him. (a) Name three consequences for the restaurant. (b) Give three recommendations to improve the service."},"steps":[{"af":"Identifiseer die swak diens: lang wagtyd, kelner op sy foon, verkeerde bestelling, bestuurder stry met die gas.","en":"Identify the poor service: long waiting time, waiter on his phone, wrong order, manager argues with the guest."},{"af":"(a) **Gevolge:** die gesin kom nie terug nie (verlore herhaalkliënte); hulle skryf 'n slegte aanlyn resensie en vertel vriende (negatiewe mond-tot-mond); minder kliënte lei tot minder inkomste en 'n beskadigde reputasie.","en":"(a) **Consequences:** the family does not come back (lost repeat customers); they write a bad online review and tell friends (negative word of mouth); fewer customers lead to less income and a damaged reputation."},{"af":"(b) **Aanbevelings:** lei personeel op in kliëntediens en 'n reël van geen persoonlike fone tydens diens nie; lei die bestuurder op om klagtes te hanteer (luister, vra om verskoning, los op, bedank) – bv. 'n gratis nagereg as vergoeding; stel 'n stelsel in om bestellings te kontroleer en vra gaste om terugvoer.","en":"(b) **Recommendations:** train staff in customer care and a rule of no personal phones during service; train the manager to handle complaints (listen, apologise, solve, thank) – e.g. a free dessert as compensation; introduce a system to check orders and ask guests for feedback."}],"answer":{"af":"Gevolge: verlore kliënte, slegte resensies en negatiewe mond-tot-mond, minder inkomste. Aanbevelings: opleiding, korrekte klagtehantering, 'n bestellingkontrole- en terugvoerstelsel.","en":"Consequences: lost customers, bad reviews and negative word of mouth, less income. Recommendations: training, correct complaint handling, an order-checking and feedback system."}},{"title":{"af":"Neem 'n telefoonboodskap","en":"Take a telephone message"},"problem":{"af":"Op 14 Oktober 2026 om 10:15 skakel mnr. Johan Botha die gastehuis. Hy wil met die bestuurder, me. Naidoo, praat oor 'n groepbespreking vir 30 leerders vir 'n skooltoer na die Wieg van die Mensdom. Sy is in 'n vergadering. Hy vra dat sy hom terugbel op 082 000 1234. Hoe antwoord jy die oproep, en hoe lyk die boodskap?","en":"On 14 October 2026 at 10:15 Mr Johan Botha phones the guest house. He wants to speak to the manager, Ms Naidoo, about a group booking for 30 learners for a school tour to the Cradle of Humankind. She is in a meeting. He asks her to call him back on 082 000 1234. How do you answer the call, and what does the message look like?"},"steps":[{"af":"Antwoord binne drie luie: “Goeiemôre, Damsig-gastehuis, Lerato praat. Hoe kan ek help?”","en":"Answer within three rings: \"Good morning, Damsig Guest House, Lerato speaking. How can I help?\""},{"af":"Verduidelik beleefd dat me. Naidoo in 'n vergadering is en bied aan om 'n boodskap te neem. Herhaal die nommer om seker te maak dit is reg.","en":"Explain politely that Ms Naidoo is in a meeting and offer to take a message. Repeat the number to make sure it is correct."},{"af":"**Boodskap:** Vir: me. Naidoo | Datum: 14/10/2026 | Tyd: 10:15 | Van: mnr. Johan Botha | Terugbelnommer: 082 000 1234 | Boodskap: Wil 'n groepbespreking vir 30 leerders (skooltoer na die Wieg van die Mensdom) bespreek; vra dat u hom terugbel. | Geneem deur: Lerato","en":"**Message:** To: Ms Naidoo | Date: 14/10/2026 | Time: 10:15 | From: Mr Johan Botha | Call-back number: 082 000 1234 | Message: Wants to discuss a group booking for 30 learners (school tour to the Cradle of Humankind); please call him back. | Taken by: Lerato"}],"answer":{"af":"'n Volledige boodskap bevat: vir wie, datum, tyd, naam van die oproeper, terugbelnommer, die boodskap en wie dit geneem het.","en":"A complete message contains: for whom, date, time, caller's name, call-back number, the message and who took it."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Binne hoeveel luie moet jy 'n besigheid se telefoon antwoord?","en":"Within how many rings should you answer a business telephone?"},"options":[{"af":"Tien luie","en":"Ten rings"},{"af":"Ses luie","en":"Six rings"},{"af":"Drie luie","en":"Three rings"},{"af":"Sodra jy klaar is met wat jy doen","en":"As soon as you have finished what you are doing"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Telefoonetiket vereis dat jy binne drie luie antwoord – die oproeper voel dan belangrik en word nie ongeduldig nie.","en":"Telephone etiquette requires you to answer within three rings – the caller then feels important and does not become impatient."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n E-pos wat in HOOFLETTERS geskryf is, lees soos skree.","en":"An e-mail written in CAPITAL LETTERS reads like shouting."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Reg – volgens netiket beteken hoofletters skree. Dit kom onbeleefd en aggressief voor.","en":"Correct – according to netiquette, capitals mean shouting. It comes across as rude and aggressive."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Suid-Afrika is toerismepadtekens ___ met wit simbole en skrif.","en":"In South Africa tourism road signs are ___ with white symbols and lettering."},"answers":{"af":["bruin"],"en":["brown"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["blou","groen","geel"],"en":["blue","green","yellow"]}},"explain":{"af":"Bruin tekens wys toeriste die pad na aantreklikhede, akkommodasie en dienste.","en":"Brown signs show tourists the way to attractions, accommodation and services."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n besigheid kliënte se verwagtinge konsekwent bereik en oortref, word dit ___ genoem.","en":"When a business consistently meets and exceeds customers' expectations, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["diensuitnemendheid"],"en":["service excellence"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["diensverlening","kliëntelojaliteit","mond-tot-mond-reklame"],"en":["service delivery","customer loyalty","word of mouth"]}},"explain":{"af":"Diensuitnemendheid = verwagtinge konsekwent bereik en oortref. Lojaliteit en mond-tot-mond-reklame is die gevolge daarvan.","en":"Service excellence = consistently meeting and exceeding expectations. Loyalty and word of mouth are its results."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tegnologie sal veldgidse op 'n wildrit gebruik om met mekaar te praat waar daar geen selfoonsein is nie?","en":"Which technology will field guides on a game drive use to talk to each other where there is no cellphone signal?"},"options":[{"af":"Tweerigtingradio","en":"Two-way radio"},{"af":"E-pos","en":"E-mail"},{"af":"Skakelbord","en":"Switchboard"},{"af":"Verkoopspuntstelsel (POS)","en":"Point-of-sale (POS) system"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Tweerigtingradio werk sonder selfoonsein. E-pos benodig internet, 'n skakelbord is by die kantoor, en 'n POS-stelsel verwerk betalings.","en":"A two-way radio works without cellphone signal. E-mail needs internet, a switchboard is at the office, and a POS system processes payments."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inligting hoort NIE op 'n telefoonboodskap nie?","en":"Which information does NOT belong on a telephone message?"},"options":[{"af":"Die datum en tyd van die oproep","en":"The date and time of the call"},{"af":"Die oproeper se naam en terugbelnommer","en":"The caller's name and call-back number"},{"af":"Die boodskap self","en":"The message itself"},{"af":"Jou persoonlike mening oor die oproeper","en":"Your personal opinion of the caller"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Boodskap moet feitelik en professioneel wees: datum, tyd, naam, nommer, boodskap en wie dit geneem het. Jou mening hoort nie daar nie.","en":"A message must be factual and professional: date, time, name, number, message and who took it. Your opinion does not belong there."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke kommunikasietegnologie by sy funksie in 'n toerismebesigheid.","en":"Match each communication technology to its function in a tourism business."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Verkoopspuntstelsel (POS)","en":"Point-of-sale (POS) system"},"r":{"af":"Verwerk betalings en teken verkope aan","en":"Processes payments and records sales"}},{"l":{"af":"Aanlyn besprekingstelsel","en":"Online booking system"},"r":{"af":"Laat gaste 24/7 self bespreek en betaal","en":"Lets guests book and pay themselves 24/7"}},{"l":{"af":"GPS","en":"GPS"},"r":{"af":"Wys die roete en posisie van 'n toervoertuig","en":"Shows the route and position of a tour vehicle"}},{"l":{"af":"Skakelbord","en":"Switchboard"},"r":{"af":"Skakel inkomende oproepe na die regte uitbreiding deur","en":"Puts incoming calls through to the right extension"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke tegnologie het 'n spesifieke funksie: POS vir betalings, aanlyn bespreking vir reserverings, GPS vir roetes en die skakelbord vir oproepe.","en":"Each technology has a specific function: POS for payments, online booking for reservations, GPS for routes and the switchboard for calls."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om tyd te spaar, is dit aanvaarbaar om SMS-taal soos “thx” en “pls” in 'n formele e-pos aan 'n gas te gebruik.","en":"To save time, it is acceptable to use SMS language such as \"thx\" and \"pls\" in a formal e-mail to a guest."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – SMS-taal is onprofessioneel en kan verkeerd verstaan word, veral deur buitelandse gaste. Skryf woorde voluit en kontroleer spelling.","en":"False – SMS language is unprofessional and can be misunderstood, especially by foreign guests. Write words out in full and check spelling."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die stappe om 'n klagte te hanteer is: luister, vra om verskoning, ___ en bedank die gas.","en":"The steps to handle a complaint are: listen, apologise, ___ and thank the guest."},"answers":{"af":["los op","los die probleem op","oplos","los dit op"],"en":["solve","solve the problem","resolve","solve it","resolve the problem"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verduidelik","verdedig","vergeet"],"en":["explain","defend","forget"]}},"explain":{"af":"Na die verskoning moet jy die probleem oplos (of sê presies wat gaan gebeur). Moenie jouself verdedig of net verduidelik waarom dit gebeur het nie.","en":"After the apology you must solve the problem (or say exactly what will happen). Don't defend yourself or just explain why it happened."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n voordeel van 'n aanlyn besprekingstelsel vir 'n gastehuis?","en":"What is an advantage of an online booking system for a guest house?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit werk ook sonder elektrisiteit of internet.","en":"It also works without electricity or the internet."},{"af":"Gaste kan 24/7 bespreek, en die beskikbaarheid word outomaties bygewerk.","en":"Guests can book 24/7, and availability is updated automatically."},{"af":"Die gastehuis het glad nie meer personeel nodig nie.","en":"The guest house no longer needs any staff at all."},{"af":"Dit kan nooit gekap of bedrieg word nie.","en":"It can never be hacked or defrauded."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Aanlyn bespreking is altyd oop, selfs as die kantoor gesluit is. Die ander stellings is onwaar: dit benodig krag en internet, personeel is steeds nodig, en kuberbedrog is 'n werklike risiko.","en":"Online booking is always open, even when the office is closed. The other statements are false: it needs power and internet, staff are still needed, and cyber fraud is a real risk."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As 'n ontevrede gas 'n slegte ___ op 'n webwerf soos TripAdvisor of Google skryf, kan duisende moontlike gaste dit lees.","en":"If an unhappy guest writes a bad ___ on a website such as TripAdvisor or Google, thousands of potential guests can read it."},"answers":{"af":["resensie","aanlyn resensie","aanlynresensie","beoordeling","review"],"en":["review","online review"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brosjure","advertensie","faktuur"],"en":["brochure","advert","invoice"]}},"explain":{"af":"Aanlyn resensies is moderne mond-tot-mond-reklame – een slegte resensie kan baie moontlike kliënte afskrik.","en":"Online reviews are modern word of mouth – one bad review can put off many potential customers."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n tevrede gas sy vriende en familie van 'n wonderlike verblyf vertel, is dit ___-reklame.","en":"When a satisfied guest tells his friends and family about a wonderful stay, it is ___ advertising."},"answers":{"af":["mond-tot-mond","mond tot mond","mondtotmond"],"en":["word-of-mouth","word of mouth"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["betaalde","televisie","koerant"],"en":["paid","television","newspaper"]}},"explain":{"af":"Mond-tot-mond-reklame kos die besigheid niks, maar mense vertrou aanbevelings van vriende baie. Dit is een van die groot voordele van diensuitnemendheid.","en":"Word-of-mouth advertising costs the business nothing, but people trust recommendations from friends a lot. It is one of the big benefits of service excellence."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeroperateur in Pretoria wil vinnige opdaterings (bv. 'n veranderde vertrektyd) aan 'n groep van 20 toeriste op 'n bustoer stuur. Watter metode is die BESTE?","en":"A tour operator in Pretoria wants to send quick updates (e.g. a changed departure time) to a group of 20 tourists on a bus tour. Which method is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Brief per pos aan elke toeris","en":"A letter by post to each tourist"},{"af":"'n Advertensie in die plaaslike koerant","en":"An advert in the local newspaper"},{"af":"'n Faks na elke hotel","en":"A fax to each hotel"},{"af":"'n WhatsApp-groep op die toeriste se slimfone","en":"A WhatsApp group on the tourists' smartphones"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n WhatsApp-groep bereik almal onmiddellik en goedkoop, waar hulle ook al is. Pos en faks is te stadig, en 'n koerantadvertensie is nie gerig op die groep nie.","en":"A WhatsApp group reaches everyone immediately and cheaply, wherever they are. Post and fax are too slow, and a newspaper advert is not aimed at the group."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die e-pos: Onderwerp: (leeg). “HI, UR ROOM IS READY. COME B4 2!!!” Geen handtekening nie. Watter beskrywing van die foute is die MEES VOLLEDIG?","en":"Read the e-mail: Subject: (blank). \"HI, UR ROOM IS READY. COME B4 2!!!\" No signature. Which description of the errors is the MOST COMPLETE?"},"options":[{"af":"Geen onderwerplyn nie, hoofletters (skree), SMS-taal, informele aanhef en geen professionele handtekening nie","en":"No subject line, capitals (shouting), SMS language, informal greeting and no professional signature"},{"af":"Die e-pos is te formeel en te lank","en":"The e-mail is too formal and too long"},{"af":"Net die handtekening ontbreek; die res is reg","en":"Only the signature is missing; the rest is correct"},{"af":"Daar is geen foute nie, want dit is kort en duidelik","en":"There are no errors, because it is short and clear"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die e-pos oortree byna elke netiket-reël: geen onderwerp, hoofletters, SMS-taal (“UR”, “B4”), 'n informele aanhef, te veel uitroeptekens en geen handtekening nie.","en":"The e-mail breaks almost every netiquette rule: no subject, capitals, SMS language (\"UR\", \"B4\"), an informal greeting, too many exclamation marks and no signature."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gevallestudie: 'n Gas wag 40 minute by ontvangs omdat die ontvangsdame op haar persoonlike foon gesels, en dan is die kamer nog nie skoongemaak nie. Wat is die MEES WAARSKYNLIKE gevolg vir die gastehuis?","en":"Case study: A guest waits 40 minutes at reception because the receptionist is chatting on her personal phone, and then the room has not been cleaned yet. What is the MOST LIKELY consequence for the guest house?"},"options":[{"af":"Meer herhaalkliënte, want die gas sal sy vriende saambring","en":"More repeat customers, because the guest will bring his friends"},{"af":"Die gastehuis kry outomaties 'n hoër stergradering","en":"The guest house automatically gets a higher star grading"},{"af":"Die gas kom nie terug nie en skryf 'n slegte resensie, sodat die gastehuis kliënte en inkomste verloor","en":"The guest does not come back and writes a bad review, so the guest house loses customers and income"},{"af":"Die gas sal niemand vertel nie, so daar is geen gevolge nie","en":"The guest will tell nobody, so there are no consequences"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Swak diens lei tot verlore kliënte, negatiewe resensies en mond-tot-mond, en dus minder inkomste. Ontevrede gaste vertel gewoonlik méér mense as tevrede gaste.","en":"Poor service leads to lost customers, negative reviews and word of mouth, and therefore less income. Unhappy guests usually tell more people than satisfied guests do."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By 'n restaurant by Hartbeespoortdam ignoreer kelners gereeld klagtes, en die aanlyn resensies word al hoe slegter. Watter aanbeveling is die BESTE om die diens te verbeter?","en":"At a restaurant at Hartbeespoort Dam waiters regularly ignore complaints, and the online reviews are getting worse and worse. Which recommendation is the BEST to improve the service?"},"options":[{"af":"Ontslaan dadelik al die personeel en begin oor.","en":"Fire all the staff immediately and start over."},{"af":"Lei personeel op in kliëntediens en klagtehantering, bemagtig hulle om probleme op te los en stel 'n terugvoerstelsel in.","en":"Train staff in customer care and complaint handling, empower them to solve problems and introduce a feedback system."},{"af":"Verhoog die pryse sodat net ryk kliënte kom.","en":"Raise the prices so that only wealthy customers come."},{"af":"Verwyder die kommentaarkaartjies sodat gaste nie meer kan kla nie.","en":"Remove the comment cards so that guests can no longer complain."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Opleiding, bemagtiging en terugvoer pak die oorsaak van die probleem aan. Om almal te ontslaan is duur en los nie die opleidingsprobleem op nie; hoër pryse verhoog net verwagtinge; sonder terugvoer weet die bestuur nie wat skeef loop nie.","en":"Training, empowerment and feedback tackle the cause of the problem. Firing everyone is expensive and does not solve the training problem; higher prices only raise expectations; without feedback management does not know what is going wrong."}}]}]}]},"gasvryheidstudies":{"id":"gasvryheidstudies","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Gasvryheidstudies","en":"Hospitality Studies"},"short":{"af":"Gasv","en":"Hosp"},"icon":"🍽️","color":"#b45309","intro":{"af":"Gasvryheidstudies in Graad 10 kombineer teorie en praktiese kookwerk: die gasvryheidsektore en loopbane, higiëne en voedselveiligheid, kombuistoerusting en -bedrywighede, vrugte, meelmengsels, eiers, graan en suiwel, voedsel- en drankediens, voeding en spyskaartbeplanning, maalvleis, pasta en slaaie, veiligheid en sekuriteit, en akkommodasie. Die Novembereksamen is een teorievraestel van 200 punte in 3 uur oor die hele jaar se werk; die praktiese werk en die PAT tel apart.","en":"Hospitality Studies in Grade 10 combines theory and practical cooking: the hospitality sectors and careers, hygiene and food safety, kitchen equipment and operations, fruit, flour mixtures, eggs, cereals and dairy, food and beverage service, nutrition and menu planning, minced meat, pasta and salads, safety and security, and accommodation. The November exam is one theory paper of 200 marks in 3 hours on the whole year's work; the practicals and the PAT count separately."},"examTips":[{"af":"Leer kookterme en kookmetodes presies (bv. mise en place, invryfmetode, pocheer, blansjeer, al dente) – Afdeling A vra dikwels net een woord of term.","en":"Learn culinary terms and cooking methods exactly (e.g. mise en place, rubbing-in method, poach, blanch, al dente) – Section A often asks for just one word or term."},{"af":"Voedselveiligheid: ken die gevaarsone (5 °C–60 °C), die soorte besmetting en die HACCP-beginsels, en gee by elke gevaar 'n voorkomingstap.","en":"Food safety: know the danger zone (5 °C–60 °C), the types of contamination and the HACCP principles, and give a prevention step for every hazard."},{"af":"Kosteberekening: wys elke stap – koste van elke bestanddeel, totale koste, koste per porsie, en verkoopprys = koste per porsie ÷ voedselkoste-% × 100.","en":"Costing: show every step – cost of each ingredient, total cost, cost per portion, and selling price = cost per portion ÷ food-cost % × 100."},{"af":"Spyskaartbeplanning: let op kleur, tekstuur, smaak, voedingswaarde en die geleentheid, en pas die spyskaart aan by die gaste se dieetbehoeftes.","en":"Menu planning: pay attention to colour, texture, flavour, nutritional value and the occasion, and adapt the menu to the guests' dietary needs."},{"af":"Ken die tafeldek vir 'n à la carte- en table d'hôte-plek en die volgorde van diens; beskryf of teken netjies en benoem elke item.","en":"Know the cover for à la carte and table d'hôte and the order of service; describe or draw neatly and label every item."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Departement van Basiese Onderwys (DBE)","en":"Department of Basic Education (DBE)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za","note":{"af":"CAPS-dokument vir Gasvryheidstudies, eksamenriglyne en vorige NSS-vraestelle met memorandums – goed om die vraagstyl te leer ken.","en":"CAPS document for Hospitality Studies, exam guidelines and past NSC papers with memos – good for learning the question style."}},{"title":{"af":"Thutong-onderwysportaal","en":"Thutong Education Portal"},"url":"https://www.thutong.doe.gov.za","note":{"af":"Die DBE se gratis onderwysportaal met leer- en hersieningsmateriaal per vak en graad.","en":"The DBE's free education portal with learning and revision material by subject and grade."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Gasvryheidstudies-eksamen Graad 10\n\n**Een teorievraestel, 200 punte, 3 uur** volgens die CAPS/DBE-patroon (*skatting – bevestig met Hoërskool Brits se 2026-afbakening*). Die vraestel dek **die hele jaar**; die praktiese lesse en die PAT tel apart.\n\n| Afdeling | Inhoud | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Kort vrae oor alle onderwerpe: meervoudige keuse, kolom-pas, een woord/term, identifisering | 40 |\n| B | Kombuis- en restaurantbedrywighede; higiëne, veiligheid en sekuriteit | ±40 |\n| C | Voeding en spyskaartbeplanning; voedselsoorte (vrugte, meelmengsels, eiers, graan, suiwel, maalvleis, pasta, slaaie) – die grootste afdeling | ±80 |\n| D | Gasvryheidsektore en loopbane; voedsel- en drankediens | ±40 |\n\n### Wat om te verwag\n\n- **Scenario's** van 'n restaurant, hotel, gastehuis of spysenieringsbesigheid.\n- **Berekeninge:** resepte vergroot of verklein, kosteberekening en verkoopprys.\n- **Beskrywings en diagramme:** tafeldek, kombuisuitleg, die voedselpiramide.\n- **Verduidelik-vrae:** waarom 'n metode werk (bv. waarom skons ligte deeg nodig het), of hoe om 'n probleem te voorkom.\n\n### Wenke\n\n1. Gebruik die korrekte kookterme.\n2. Wys al jou berekeninge met eenhede (g, ml, R).\n3. Hou ±70 minute vir Afdeling C.","en":"## Hospitality Studies exam Grade 10\n\n**One theory paper, 200 marks, 3 hours** following the CAPS/DBE pattern (*estimate – confirm with Hoërskool Brits's 2026 scope*). The paper covers **the whole year**; the practical lessons and the PAT count separately.\n\n| Section | Content | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Short questions on all topics: multiple choice, matching, one word/term, identification | 40 |\n| B | Kitchen and restaurant operations; hygiene, safety and security | ±40 |\n| C | Nutrition and menu planning; food commodities (fruit, flour mixtures, eggs, cereals, dairy, minced meat, pasta, salads) – the biggest section | ±80 |\n| D | Hospitality sectors and careers; food and beverage service | ±40 |\n\n### What to expect\n\n- **Scenarios** from a restaurant, hotel, guest house or catering business.\n- **Calculations:** scaling recipes up or down, costing and selling price.\n- **Descriptions and diagrams:** table setting, kitchen layout, the food pyramid.\n- **Explain questions:** why a method works (e.g. why scones need a light dough), or how to prevent a problem.\n\n### Tips\n\n1. Use the correct culinary terms.\n2. Show all your calculations with units (g, ml, R).\n3. Keep ±70 minutes for Section C."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Gasvryheidsektore, higiëne, kombuisbedrywighede, vrugte en meelmengsels","en":"Hospitality sectors, hygiene, kitchen operations, fruit and flour mixtures"},"topics":[{"id":"gas10-t1-sektore-loopbane","title":{"af":"Die gasvryheidsbedryf: sektore, ondernemings en loopbane","en":"The hospitality industry: sectors, enterprises and careers"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die sektore en tipes ondernemings in die gasvryheidsbedryf kan klassifiseer, franchises en kitskosondernemings kan bespreek en loopbane by hul pligte kan pas.","en":"You will be able to classify the sectors and types of establishments in the hospitality industry, discuss franchises and fast-food enterprises and match careers to their duties."},"summary":{"af":"## Die eksamenvraestel (teorie)\n\nDie Graad 10-teorievraestel tel **200 punte** en duur **3 uur**. (Praktiese werk en die PAT word nie hier gedek nie.)\n\n| Afdeling | Inhoud |\n|---|---|\n| A | Kort vrae oor **alle** onderwerpe (40 punte): meervoudige keuse, pas kolomme, een woord/term, identifisering |\n| B | Kombuis- en restaurantbedrywighede; higiëne, veiligheid en sekuriteit |\n| C | Voeding en spyskaartbeplanning; voedselkommoditeite (die **grootste** afdeling) |\n| D | Gasvryheidsektore en loopbane; voedsel- en drankediens |\n\nHierdie onderwerp val in **Afdeling D**.\n\n## Wat is gasvryheid?\n\n**Gasvryheid** is die voorsiening van **kos, drank, akkommodasie en diens** aan gaste. Die bedryf is nou verbind met **toerisme**: toeriste wat Hartbeespoortdam of die Magaliesberg besoek, het 'n bed, etes en vermaak nodig. Plaaslike mense gebruik egter ook gasvryheid – 'n gesin wat Saterdagaand in Brits uiteet, is nie toeriste nie.\n\nDie **eindprodukte** van die bedryf is **voedsel**, **drank**, **akkommodasie** en **diens/ervaring** (hoe die gas voel wanneer hy weggaan).\n\n## Sektore van die bedryf\n\n- **Akkommodasie:** hotelle, gastehuise, lodges, B&B's.\n- **Voedsel en drank:** restaurante, kafees, kroeë, kitskosplekke.\n- **Konferensies en geleenthede:** konferensiesentrums, troues, funksies.\n- **Vermaak en ontspanning:** casino's en temaparke (bv. Sun City).\n- **Institusionele (nie-kommersiële) spysenering:** hospitale, skole, gevangenisse, ouetehuise, die weermag.\n- **Kontrakspysenering:** 'n spysenieringsmaatskappy word gekontrakteer om etes by 'n ander organisasie te voorsien, bv. 'n myn se kantien.\n- **Reisspysenering:** etes op vliegtuie en treine.\n\n### Kommersieel teenoor nie-kommersieel\n\n| Kommersieel | Nie-kommersieel (gesubsidieer) |\n|---|---|\n| Hoofdoel is **wins** | Hoofdoel is **diens** aan 'n groep mense |\n| Gaste kies self en betaal die volle prys | Etes is deel van 'n diens; die koste word dikwels deur die staat of organisasie gesubsidieer |\n| Bv. hotel, restaurant, casino | Bv. hospitaal, skoolkoshuis, gevangenis |\n\n## Tipes voedsel- en drankondernemings\n\nDeftige (fine-dining) **à la carte-restaurante**, **gesinsrestaurante**, **bistro's**, **koffiewinkels**, **kitskosafsetpunte**, **wegneemplekke**, **kroeë**, **spyseniers** (kos vir funksies) en **kosvoertuie (food trucks)**.\n\n### Kenmerke van kitskosondernemings\n\n- 'n **Beperkte, gestandaardiseerde spyskaart**\n- **Vinnige** toonbank- of deurry-diens (drive-through)\n- **Wegneemverpakking**\n- **Lae pryse** en **eenvormige gehalte** – 'n burger smaak elke keer dieselfde\n- **Halfgeskoolde personeel** wat met **gespesialiseerde toerusting** werk\n\n> **Wenk:** Omdat die spyskaart en metodes gestandaardiseer is, kan personeel vinnig opgelei word. Dit hou arbeidskoste laag.\n\n## Franchises\n\n'n **Franchise** is 'n ooreenkoms waarin die **franchisegewer** (die eienaar van die handelsnaam en stelsel) aan 'n **franchisehouer** (franchisenemer) die reg verkoop om 'n onderneming onder daardie naam te bedryf. Die franchisehouer betaal 'n eenmalige **franchisefooi** aan die begin plus **maandelikse tantieme** (royalties), gewoonlik 'n persentasie van die omset. SA-voorbeelde: **Spur, Wimpy, Steers, Nando's** en **Ocean Basket**.\n\n| Voordele vir die franchisehouer | Nadele vir die franchisehouer |\n|---|---|\n| Bekende handelsnaam – klante ken dit reeds | Hoë koste (fooi + tantieme) |\n| Opleiding en ondersteuning | Min vryheid – jy mag nie jou eie spyskaart opstel nie |\n| Nasionale bemarking | Streng reëls en inspeksies |\n| Grootmaataankope – goedkoper voorraad | 'n Deel van die inkomste gaan na die franchisegewer |\n\n## Entrepreneurskap\n\n'n **Entrepreneur** sien 'n geleentheid raak en begin 'n eie besigheid. Eienskappe: **kreatief**, **bereid om risiko's te neem**, **hardwerkend** en **selfgemotiveerd**. Klein besigheidsidees: 'n **tuisnywerheid** (koeksisters, beskuit), **funksiespysenering** (bv. kos vir 'n rugbyklub se funksie) of 'n **koffiekarretjie**.\n\n## Loopbane\n\n| Loopbaan | Werk |\n|---|---|\n| Sjef/kok | berei kos voor en kook |\n| Banketbakker | koeke, terte en nageregte |\n| Bakker | brood en gebak |\n| Kelner | neem bestellings en bedien gaste |\n| Barista | maak koffiedrankies |\n| Kroegman | meng en bedien drankies |\n| Wynkelner (sommelier) | beveel wyn aan en bedien dit |\n| Ontvangsklerk | ontvang gaste; teken hulle in en uit |\n| Huishoudster | hou kamers en openbare areas skoon |\n| Geleentheidskoördineerder | beplan konferensies, troues en funksies |\n| Spysenier | lewer kos vir funksies |\n| Hotelbestuurder | bestuur die hele hotel |\n\n**Persoonlike eienskappe:** goeie persoonlike higiëne, stiptelik, vriendelik, kan **onder druk** en **ongereelde ure** (aande, naweke, vakansies) werk, goeie spanwerk en eerlikheid.\n\n**Opleiding:** TVET-kolleges, universiteite van tegnologie, sjefskole en **leerlingskappe** deur **CATHSSETA** (die SETA vir kultuur, kuns, toerisme, gasvryheid en sport).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders verwar die **franchisegewer** (verkoop die reg) met die **franchisehouer** (koop die reg en bedryf die winkel).","en":"## The exam paper (theory)\n\nThe Grade 10 theory paper counts **200 marks** and lasts **3 hours**. (Practical work and the PAT are not covered here.)\n\n| Section | Content |\n|---|---|\n| A | Short questions on **all** topics (40 marks): multiple choice, matching columns, one word/term, identification |\n| B | Kitchen and restaurant operations; hygiene, safety and security |\n| C | Nutrition and menu planning; food commodities (the **biggest** section) |\n| D | Hospitality sectors and careers; food and beverage service |\n\nThis topic falls in **Section D**.\n\n## What is hospitality?\n\n**Hospitality** is providing **food, drink, accommodation and service** to guests. The industry is closely linked to **tourism**: tourists who visit Hartbeespoort Dam or the Magaliesberg need a bed, meals and entertainment. But local people also use hospitality – a family eating out in Brits on a Saturday evening are not tourists.\n\nThe **final products** of the industry are **food**, **beverages**, **accommodation** and **service/experience** (how the guest feels when he leaves).\n\n## Sectors of the industry\n\n- **Accommodation:** hotels, guest houses, lodges, B&Bs.\n- **Food and beverage:** restaurants, cafés, bars, fast-food outlets.\n- **Conferencing and events:** conference centres, weddings, functions.\n- **Entertainment and leisure:** casinos and theme parks (e.g. Sun City).\n- **Institutional (non-commercial) catering:** hospitals, schools, prisons, old-age homes, the military.\n- **Contract catering:** a catering company is contracted to provide meals at another organisation, e.g. a mine's canteen.\n- **Travel catering:** meals on aeroplanes and trains.\n\n### Commercial versus non-commercial\n\n| Commercial | Non-commercial (subsidised) |\n|---|---|\n| Main aim is **profit** | Main aim is **service** to a group of people |\n| Guests choose and pay the full price | Meals are part of a service; the cost is often subsidised by the state or organisation |\n| E.g. hotel, restaurant, casino | E.g. hospital, school hostel, prison |\n\n## Types of food and beverage establishments\n\nFine-dining **à la carte restaurants**, **family restaurants**, **bistros**, **coffee shops**, **fast-food outlets**, **take-aways**, **pubs/bars**, **caterers** (food for functions) and **food trucks**.\n\n### Characteristics of fast-food enterprises\n\n- A **limited, standardised menu**\n- **Fast** counter or drive-through service\n- **Take-away packaging**\n- **Low prices** and **consistent quality** – a burger tastes the same every time\n- **Semi-skilled staff** working with **specialised equipment**\n\n> **Tip:** Because the menu and methods are standardised, staff can be trained quickly. This keeps labour costs low.\n\n## Franchises\n\nA **franchise** is an agreement in which the **franchisor** (the owner of the brand name and system) sells a **franchisee** the right to run a business under that name. The franchisee pays a once-off **franchise fee** at the start plus **monthly royalties**, usually a percentage of turnover. SA examples: **Spur, Wimpy, Steers, Nando's** and **Ocean Basket**.\n\n| Advantages for the franchisee | Disadvantages for the franchisee |\n|---|---|\n| Known brand name – customers already know it | High costs (fee + royalties) |\n| Training and support | Little freedom – you may not create your own menu |\n| National marketing | Strict rules and inspections |\n| Bulk buying – cheaper stock | Part of the income goes to the franchisor |\n\n## Entrepreneurship\n\nAn **entrepreneur** spots an opportunity and starts his own business. Qualities: **creative**, **willing to take risks**, **hard-working** and **self-motivated**. Small business ideas: a **home industry** (koeksisters, rusks), **function catering** (e.g. food for a rugby club's function) or a **coffee cart**.\n\n## Careers\n\n| Career | Work |\n|---|---|\n| Chef/cook | prepares and cooks food |\n| Pastry chef | cakes, tarts and desserts |\n| Baker | bread and baked goods |\n| Waiter | takes orders and serves guests |\n| Barista | makes coffee drinks |\n| Bartender | mixes and serves drinks |\n| Sommelier (wine steward) | recommends and serves wine |\n| Receptionist | welcomes guests; checks them in and out |\n| Housekeeper | keeps rooms and public areas clean |\n| Events coordinator | plans conferences, weddings and functions |\n| Caterer | supplies food for functions |\n| Hotel manager | manages the whole hotel |\n\n**Personal qualities:** good personal hygiene, punctual, friendly, able to work **under pressure** and **irregular hours** (evenings, weekends, holidays), good teamwork and honesty.\n\n**Training:** TVET colleges, universities of technology, chef schools and **learnerships** through **CATHSSETA** (the SETA for culture, arts, tourism, hospitality and sport).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners confuse the **franchisor** (sells the right) with the **franchisee** (buys the right and runs the outlet)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Gasvryheid","en":"Hospitality"},"def":{"af":"Die voorsiening van kos, drank, akkommodasie en diens aan gaste.","en":"Providing food, drink, accommodation and service to guests."}},{"term":{"af":"Kommersiële onderneming","en":"Commercial establishment"},"def":{"af":"'n Onderneming wat bedryf word met die doel om wins te maak, bv. 'n hotel of restaurant.","en":"An establishment run with the aim of making a profit, e.g. a hotel or restaurant."}},{"term":{"af":"Nie-kommersiële (institusionele) spysenering","en":"Non-commercial (institutional) catering"},"def":{"af":"Spysenering waar diens, nie wins nie, die hoofdoel is; dikwels gesubsidieer, bv. in hospitale, skole en gevangenisse.","en":"Catering where service, not profit, is the main aim; often subsidised, e.g. in hospitals, schools and prisons."}},{"term":{"af":"Kontrakspysenering","en":"Contract catering"},"def":{"af":"'n Spysenieringsmaatskappy word gekontrakteer om etes by 'n ander organisasie (bv. 'n myn of kantoor) te voorsien.","en":"A catering company is contracted to provide meals at another organisation (e.g. a mine or office)."}},{"term":{"af":"Kitskosonderneming","en":"Fast-food enterprise"},"def":{"af":"'n Onderneming met 'n beperkte, gestandaardiseerde spyskaart, vinnige diens, wegneemverpakking en lae pryse.","en":"An enterprise with a limited, standardised menu, fast service, take-away packaging and low prices."}},{"term":{"af":"Franchisegewer","en":"Franchisor"},"def":{"af":"Die maatskappy wat die handelsnaam en bedryfstelsel besit en die reg verkoop om dit te gebruik.","en":"The company that owns the brand name and operating system and sells the right to use it."}},{"term":{"af":"Franchisehouer","en":"Franchisee"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon wat die reg koop om 'n onderneming onder die franchisegewer se naam en reëls te bedryf.","en":"The person who buys the right to run a business under the franchisor's name and rules."}},{"term":{"af":"Tantieme","en":"Royalties"},"def":{"af":"Die maandelikse bedrag, gewoonlik 'n persentasie van die omset, wat die franchisehouer aan die franchisegewer betaal.","en":"The monthly amount, usually a percentage of turnover, that the franchisee pays the franchisor."}},{"term":{"af":"Entrepreneur","en":"Entrepreneur"},"def":{"af":"Iemand wat 'n geleentheid raaksien, 'n risiko neem en 'n eie besigheid begin.","en":"Someone who spots an opportunity, takes a risk and starts his own business."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer ondernemings","en":"Classify establishments"},"problem":{"af":"Klassifiseer elke onderneming volgens sy **sektor** en sê of dit **kommersieel** of **nie-kommersieel** is:\n\nA. Die kombuis van 'n hospitaal wat etes vir pasiënte maak\nB. 'n Gastehuis by Hartbeespoortdam\nC. 'n Maatskappy wat die kantien by 'n myn naby Brits bedryf\nD. Etes wat aan passasiers op 'n vliegtuig bedien word\nE. 'n Oord met 'n casino en 'n temapark","en":"Classify each establishment by its **sector** and say whether it is **commercial** or **non-commercial**:\n\nA. The kitchen of a hospital that makes meals for patients\nB. A guest house at Hartbeespoort Dam\nC. A company that runs the canteen at a mine near Brits\nD. Meals served to passengers on an aeroplane\nE. A resort with a casino and a theme park"},"steps":[{"af":"A: Die hospitaal se doel is om pasiënte te versorg, nie om wins op etes te maak nie → **institusionele spysenering, nie-kommersieel**.","en":"A: The hospital's aim is to care for patients, not to make a profit on meals → **institutional catering, non-commercial**."},{"af":"B: Gaste betaal vir 'n bed en ontbyt → **akkommodasie, kommersieel**.","en":"B: Guests pay for a bed and breakfast → **accommodation, commercial**."},{"af":"C: Die spysenieringsmaatskappy is gekontrakteer en wil wins maak → **kontrakspysenering, kommersieel**.","en":"C: The catering company is contracted and wants to make a profit → **contract catering, commercial**."},{"af":"D: Kos op vliegtuie en treine → **reisspysenering, kommersieel**.","en":"D: Food on aeroplanes and trains → **travel catering, commercial**."},{"af":"E: Casino's en temaparke → **vermaak en ontspanning, kommersieel**.","en":"E: Casinos and theme parks → **entertainment and leisure, commercial**."}],"answer":{"af":"A: institusioneel/nie-kommersieel; B: akkommodasie; C: kontrakspysenering; D: reisspysenering; E: vermaak en ontspanning (B–E kommersieel)","en":"A: institutional/non-commercial; B: accommodation; C: contract catering; D: travel catering; E: entertainment and leisure (B–E commercial)"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die tantieme van 'n franchise","en":"Calculate a franchise's royalties"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato koop 'n hoenderkitskos-franchise in Brits ('n fiktiewe voorbeeld). Die franchisegewer vra 6 % van die omset as maandelikse tantieme. Haar omset vir Maart is R300 000.\n\n(a) Bereken die tantieme vir Maart.\n(b) Hoeveel sal sy in 'n jaar betaal as die omset elke maand dieselfde bly?\n(c) Noem een voordeel en een nadeel van 'n franchise vir Lerato.","en":"Lerato buys a chicken fast-food franchise in Brits (a fictional example). The franchisor asks 6 % of turnover as monthly royalties. Her turnover for March is R300 000.\n\n(a) Calculate the royalties for March.\n(b) How much will she pay in a year if the turnover stays the same every month?\n(c) Give one advantage and one disadvantage of a franchise for Lerato."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Tantieme = 6 % × omset = 0,06 × R300 000","en":"(a) Royalties = 6 % × turnover = 0.06 × R300 000"},{"af":"= **R18 000** vir Maart","en":"= **R18 000** for March"},{"af":"(b) Per jaar: R18 000 × 12 = **R216 000**","en":"(b) Per year: R18 000 × 12 = **R216 000**"},{"af":"(c) Voordeel: 'n bekende handelsnaam lok klante van die eerste dag af (ook: opleiding, nasionale bemarking, grootmaataankope).","en":"(c) Advantage: a known brand name attracts customers from day one (also: training, national marketing, bulk buying)."},{"af":"Nadeel: hoë koste – sy betaal R216 000 per jaar, selfs as haar wins klein is (ook: min vryheid, streng reëls).","en":"Disadvantage: high costs – she pays R216 000 a year, even if her profit is small (also: little freedom, strict rules)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R18 000 (b) R216 000 (c) bv. bekende handelsnaam; hoë koste","en":"(a) R18 000 (b) R216 000 (c) e.g. known brand name; high costs"}},{"title":{"af":"Wins van 'n tuisnywerheid","en":"Profit of a home industry"},"problem":{"af":"Anja begin 'n tuisnywerheid en bak koeksisters vir die Saterdagmark in Brits. Die bestanddele vir 70 koeksisters kos R210. Sy verkoop elke koeksister vir R5.\n\n(a) Bereken die koste per koeksister.\n(b) Bereken haar wins as sy al 70 verkoop.\n(c) Noem twee eienskappe van 'n entrepreneur wat Anja nodig het.","en":"Anja starts a home industry and bakes koeksisters for the Saturday market in Brits. The ingredients for 70 koeksisters cost R210. She sells each koeksister for R5.\n\n(a) Calculate the cost per koeksister.\n(b) Calculate her profit if she sells all 70.\n(c) Name two qualities of an entrepreneur that Anja needs."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Koste per koeksister = R210 ÷ 70 = **R3**","en":"(a) Cost per koeksister = R210 ÷ 70 = **R3**"},{"af":"(b) Inkomste = 70 × R5 = R350","en":"(b) Income = 70 × R5 = R350"},{"af":"Wins = inkomste − koste = R350 − R210 = **R140**","en":"Profit = income − cost = R350 − R210 = **R140**"},{"af":"(c) Bv. **hardwerkend** (sy bak voor die mark) en **bereid om risiko's te neem** (sy koop bestanddele voordat sy weet of alles sal verkoop). Kreatief en selfgemotiveerd is ook reg.","en":"(c) E.g. **hard-working** (she bakes before the market) and **willing to take risks** (she buys ingredients before she knows whether everything will sell). Creative and self-motivated are also correct."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R3 (b) R140 (c) bv. hardwerkend, bereid om risiko's te neem","en":"(a) R3 (b) R140 (c) e.g. hard-working, willing to take risks"}},{"title":{"af":"Eienskappe van 'n goeie kelner","en":"Qualities of a good waiter"},"problem":{"af":"'n Lodge in die Magaliesberg soek 'n kelner. Noem en verduidelik vier persoonlike eienskappe wat die kelner moet hê.","en":"A lodge in the Magaliesberg is looking for a waiter. Name and explain four personal qualities the waiter must have."},"steps":[{"af":"**Goeie persoonlike higiëne** – hy hanteer kos en borde naby gaste, so 'n skoon uniform, hande en naels is noodsaaklik.","en":"**Good personal hygiene** – he handles food and plates close to guests, so a clean uniform, hands and nails are essential."},{"af":"**Vriendelik en hoflik** – die gas se ervaring is een van die eindprodukte van gasvryheid.","en":"**Friendly and polite** – the guest's experience is one of the final products of hospitality."},{"af":"**Kan onder druk en ongereelde ure werk** – restaurante is die besigste in die aande, naweke en vakansies.","en":"**Can work under pressure and irregular hours** – restaurants are busiest in the evenings, weekends and holidays."},{"af":"**Stiptelik, eerlik en 'n spanspeler** – hy hanteer geld en werk saam met die kombuis om kos betyds te bedien.","en":"**Punctual, honest and a team player** – he handles money and works with the kitchen to serve food on time."}],"answer":{"af":"Enige vier: persoonlike higiëne, vriendelik, werk onder druk/ongereelde ure, stiptelik, eerlik, spanwerk","en":"Any four: personal hygiene, friendly, works under pressure/irregular hours, punctual, honest, teamwork"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is NIE een van die eindprodukte van die gasvryheidsbedryf nie?","en":"Which of the following is NOT one of the final products of the hospitality industry?"},"options":[{"af":"Voedsel en drank","en":"Food and beverages"},{"af":"Akkommodasie","en":"Accommodation"},{"af":"Die vervaardiging van kombuistoerusting","en":"The manufacturing of kitchen equipment"},{"af":"Diens en die gas se ervaring","en":"Service and the guest's experience"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die eindprodukte is voedsel, drank, akkommodasie en diens/ervaring. 'n Fabriek wat stowe maak, verskaf aan die bedryf, maar is nie self deel van gasvryheid nie. Onthou: diens is ook 'n produk!","en":"The final products are food, beverages, accommodation and service/experience. A factory that makes stoves supplies the industry but is not itself part of hospitality. Remember: service is also a product!"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Spysenering in hospitale, skole en gevangenisse, waar wins nie die hoofdoel is nie, word ___ spysenering genoem.","en":"Catering in hospitals, schools and prisons, where profit is not the main aim, is called ___ catering."},"answers":{"af":["institusionele","institusioneel","nie-kommersiële","nie-kommersieel","nie kommersiële"],"en":["institutional","non-commercial","non commercial"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is institusionele of nie-kommersiële spysenering: die doel is diens aan pasiënte, leerders of gevangenes, en die koste word dikwels gesubsidieer.","en":"This is institutional or non-commercial catering: the aim is service to patients, learners or prisoners, and the cost is often subsidised."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kommersiële","reis","vermaak"],"en":["commercial","travel","leisure"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Sun City, met sy casino en temapark, is 'n voorbeeld van die vermaak- en ontspanningsektor.","en":"Sun City, with its casino and theme park, is an example of the entertainment and leisure sector."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Casino's en temaparke val onder vermaak en ontspanning. Sun City het ook hotelle – groot oorde dek dikwels meer as een sektor.","en":"True. Casinos and theme parks fall under entertainment and leisure. Sun City also has hotels – large resorts often cover more than one sector."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter persoon koop die reg om 'n bekende handelsnaam soos Spur te gebruik en bedryf dan self die restaurant?","en":"Which person buys the right to use a well-known brand name such as Spur and then runs the restaurant himself?"},"options":[{"af":"Die franchisegewer","en":"The franchisor"},{"af":"Die franchisehouer","en":"The franchisee"},{"af":"Die spysenier","en":"The caterer"},{"af":"Die hotelbestuurder","en":"The hotel manager"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die franchisehouer koop die reg en bedryf die restaurant. Die franchisegewer is die maatskappy wat die handelsnaam besit en die reg verkoop.","en":"The franchisee buys the right and runs the restaurant. The franchisor is the company that owns the brand name and sells the right."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n deftige restaurant beveel die ___ wyn by die geregte aan en bedien dit.","en":"In a fine-dining restaurant the ___ recommends wine to go with the dishes and serves it."},"answers":{"af":["sommelier","wynkelner","wynbediener"],"en":["sommelier","wine steward","wine waiter"]},"explain":{"af":"Die sommelier (wynkelner) is die wynspesialis. 'n Barista maak koffie en 'n kroegman meng en bedien drankies by die kroeg.","en":"The sommelier (wine steward) is the wine specialist. A barista makes coffee and a bartender mixes and serves drinks at the bar."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["barista","kroegman","kok"],"en":["barista","bartender","cook"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Leerlingskappe in die gasvryheidsbedryf word deur die SETA genaamd ___ gereël.","en":"Learnerships in the hospitality industry are arranged by the SETA called ___."},"answers":{"af":["CATHSSETA"],"en":["CATHSSETA"]},"explain":{"af":"CATHSSETA is die SETA vir kultuur, kuns, toerisme, gasvryheid en sport. Ander opleidingsroetes is TVET-kolleges, universiteite van tegnologie en sjefskole.","en":"CATHSSETA is the SETA for culture, arts, tourism, hospitality and sport. Other training routes are TVET colleges, universities of technology and chef schools."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["MERSETA","SAQA","TGCSA"],"en":["MERSETA","SAQA","TGCSA"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n kenmerk van 'n kitskosonderneming?","en":"Which one is a characteristic of a fast-food enterprise?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Beperkte, gestandaardiseerde spyskaart","en":"A limited, standardised menu"},{"af":"Silwerdiens aan die tafel","en":"Silver service at the table"},{"af":"Hoogs opgeleide sjefs wat elke gereg volgens die gas se wense skep","en":"Highly trained chefs who create every dish to the guest's wishes"},{"af":"'n Lang spyskaart met geregte wat elke dag verander","en":"A long menu with dishes that change every day"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Kitskosplekke het 'n kort, gestandaardiseerde spyskaart sodat kos vinnig en elke keer dieselfde gemaak kan word. Silwerdiens en kos op bestelling hoort by deftige restaurante.","en":"Fast-food outlets have a short, standardised menu so that food can be made quickly and the same every time. Silver service and food cooked to the guest's wishes belong to fine-dining restaurants."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Alle gasvryheidsondernemings se hoofdoel is om wins te maak.","en":"The main aim of all hospitality establishments is to make a profit."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Nie-kommersiële (institusionele) ondernemings soos hospitale, skole en gevangenisse se hoofdoel is diens; hulle etes word dikwels gesubsidieer.","en":"False. Non-commercial (institutional) establishments such as hospitals, schools and prisons have service as their main aim; their meals are often subsidised."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die maandelikse bedrag, gewoonlik 'n persentasie van die omset, wat 'n franchisehouer aan die franchisegewer betaal, word ___ genoem.","en":"The monthly amount, usually a percentage of turnover, that a franchisee pays the franchisor is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["tantieme","tantième","tantiemes","royalties","royalty"],"en":["royalties","royalty","royalty fee","royalty fees"]},"explain":{"af":"Tantieme (royalties) word elke maand betaal. Die franchisefooi is 'n eenmalige bedrag aan die begin van die ooreenkoms.","en":"Royalties are paid every month. The franchise fee is a once-off amount at the start of the agreement."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["franchisefooi","BTW","huur"],"en":["franchise fee","VAT","rent"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Maatskappy kry 'n kontrak om die etes in die kantien van 'n myn naby Brits te voorsien. In watter sektor val dit?","en":"A company gets a contract to provide the meals in the canteen of a mine near Brits. Which sector does this fall in?"},"options":[{"af":"Reisspysenering","en":"Travel catering"},{"af":"Akkommodasie","en":"Accommodation"},{"af":"Vermaak en ontspanning","en":"Entertainment and leisure"},{"af":"Kontrakspysenering","en":"Contract catering"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die spysenieringsmaatskappy is gekontrakteer om by 'n ander organisasie (die myn) etes te voorsien – dit is kontrakspysenering. Reisspysenering is kos op vliegtuie en treine.","en":"The catering company is contracted to provide meals at another organisation (the mine) – this is contract catering. Travel catering is food on aeroplanes and trains."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke loopbaan by die regte werksbeskrywing.","en":"Match each career to the correct job description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Barista","en":"Barista"},"r":{"af":"Maak en bedien koffiedrankies soos cappuccino","en":"Makes and serves coffee drinks such as cappuccino"}},{"l":{"af":"Huishoudster","en":"Housekeeper"},"r":{"af":"Hou gastekamers en openbare areas skoon","en":"Keeps guest rooms and public areas clean"}},{"l":{"af":"Ontvangsklerk","en":"Receptionist"},"r":{"af":"Ontvang gaste en teken hulle in en uit","en":"Welcomes guests and checks them in and out"}},{"l":{"af":"Banketbakker","en":"Pastry chef"},"r":{"af":"Berei koeke, terte en nageregte","en":"Prepares cakes, tarts and desserts"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleentheidskoördineerder","en":"Events coordinator"},"r":{"af":"Beplan konferensies, troues en funksies","en":"Plans conferences, weddings and functions"}}],"explain":{"af":"Barista = koffie; huishoudster = kamers skoon; ontvangsklerk = inteken en uitteken; banketbakker = koeke en nageregte; geleentheidskoördineerder = beplan geleenthede.","en":"Barista = coffee; housekeeper = clean rooms; receptionist = check-in and check-out; pastry chef = cakes and desserts; events coordinator = plans events."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n NADEEL van 'n franchise vir die franchisehouer?","en":"Which one is a DISADVANTAGE of a franchise for the franchisee?"},"options":[{"af":"Klante ken die handelsnaam reeds","en":"Customers already know the brand name"},{"af":"Streng reëls laat min vryheid, bv. jy mag nie jou eie spyskaart opstel nie","en":"Strict rules leave little freedom, e.g. you may not create your own menu"},{"af":"Die franchisegewer bied opleiding en ondersteuning","en":"The franchisor offers training and support"},{"af":"Grootmaataankope maak voorraad goedkoper","en":"Bulk buying makes stock cheaper"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die franchisehouer moet die franchisegewer se reëls volg en het min vryheid. Die ander drie is voordele van 'n franchise.","en":"The franchisee must follow the franchisor's rules and has little freedom. The other three are advantages of a franchise."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi leen R15 000 om 'n koffiekarretjie by 'n mark by Hartbeespoortdam te koop, al weet sy sy kan die geld verloor as die besigheid misluk. Watter eienskap van 'n entrepreneur wys sy hier die duidelikste?","en":"Thandi borrows R15 000 to buy a coffee cart for a market at Hartbeespoort Dam, even though she knows she could lose the money if the business fails. Which quality of an entrepreneur does she show most clearly here?"},"options":[{"af":"Kreatiwiteit","en":"Creativity"},{"af":"Eerlikheid","en":"Honesty"},{"af":"Stiptelikheid","en":"Punctuality"},{"af":"Bereidheid om risiko's te neem","en":"Willingness to take risks"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sy weet sy kan geld verloor en doen dit tog – dit is bereidheid om 'n risiko te neem. Kreatiwiteit sou wees as sy 'n nuwe, oorspronklike idee kry.","en":"She knows she could lose money and does it anyway – this is willingness to take a risk. Creativity would be coming up with a new, original idea."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Franchisehouer se maandelikse omset is R250 000 en die tantieme is 5 % van die omset. Hy betaal R___ tantieme per maand.","en":"A franchisee's monthly turnover is R250 000 and the royalties are 5 % of turnover. He pays R___ in royalties per month."},"answers":{"af":["12500","12 500","R12 500","R12500"],"en":["12500","12 500","R12 500","R12500"]},"explain":{"af":"5 % × R250 000 = 0,05 × 250 000 = R12 500. Pasop: 1 250 is 'n desimale fout en 25 000 is 10 %.","en":"5 % × R250 000 = 0.05 × 250 000 = R12 500. Careful: 1 250 is a decimal error and 25 000 is 10 %."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1 250","125 000","25 000"],"en":["1 250","125 000","25 000"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kan kitskosondernemings met halfgeskoolde personeel werk?","en":"Why can fast-food enterprises work with semi-skilled staff?"},"options":[{"af":"Die spyskaart en metodes is gestandaardiseer en gespesialiseerde toerusting doen baie van die werk, so personeel kan vinnig opgelei word","en":"The menu and methods are standardised and specialised equipment does much of the work, so staff can be trained quickly"},{"af":"Die wet verbied kitskosplekke om sjefs aan te stel","en":"The law forbids fast-food outlets to employ chefs"},{"af":"Kitskosplekke hoef nie aan higiënereëls te voldoen nie","en":"Fast-food outlets do not have to follow hygiene rules"},{"af":"Gaste by kitskosplekke gee nie om oor gehalte nie","en":"Guests at fast-food outlets do not care about quality"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Kort, gestandaardiseerde spyskaart en gespesialiseerde toerusting (bv. braaiers met tydhouers) maak die werk eenvoudig en herhalend. Opleiding is dus vinnig en arbeidskoste bly laag. Kitskosplekke moet wel aan higiënereëls voldoen, en eenvormige gehalte is juis een van hul kenmerke.","en":"A short, standardised menu and specialised equipment (e.g. fryers with timers) make the work simple and repetitive. Training is therefore quick and labour costs stay low. Fast-food outlets must follow hygiene rules, and consistent quality is one of their characteristics."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho het R3 miljoen gespaar en wil 'n restaurant op Hartbeespoort oopmaak, maar hy het geen ondervinding van die bedryf nie. Watter evaluering van sy keuse tussen 'n franchise en 'n onafhanklike restaurant is die beste?","en":"Sipho has saved R3 million and wants to open a restaurant in Hartbeespoort, but he has no experience of the industry. Which evaluation of his choice between a franchise and an independent restaurant is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Onafhanklike restaurant is beter, want hy hou al die wins en kan self besluit – ondervinding is nie belangrik nie","en":"An independent restaurant is better, because he keeps all the profit and can decide for himself – experience is not important"},{"af":"'n Franchise is beter, want 'n franchisehouer betaal geen fooie nie","en":"A franchise is better, because a franchisee pays no fees"},{"af":"'n Franchise is waarskynlik beter: die bekende handelsnaam, opleiding en ondersteuning verminder die risiko vir iemand sonder ondervinding, al betaal hy fooie en tantieme en het hy minder vryheid","en":"A franchise is probably better: the known brand name, training and support reduce the risk for someone without experience, even though he pays fees and royalties and has less freedom"},{"af":"Dit maak nie saak nie – alle restaurante het presies dieselfde risiko","en":"It does not matter – all restaurants carry exactly the same risk"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie evaluering weeg voordele teen nadele op. Sonder ondervinding is die franchisegewer se opleiding, stelsels en bekende naam baie waardevol, en hy het genoeg kapitaal vir die fooie. Die prys is hoë koste en min vryheid. 'n Franchisehouer betaal wel fooie en tantieme.","en":"A good evaluation weighs advantages against disadvantages. Without experience, the franchisor's training, systems and known name are very valuable, and he has enough capital for the fees. The price is high costs and little freedom. A franchisee does pay fees and royalties."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-higiene","title":{"af":"Higiëne: persoonlike en kombuishigiëne, berging, afval en plae","en":"Hygiene: personal and kitchen hygiene, storage, waste and pests"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal higiënereëls op 'n kombuisscenario kan toepas, kos by die regte temperatuur en volgorde kan bêre, en afval en plae reg kan bestuur.","en":"You will be able to apply hygiene rules to a kitchen scenario, store food at the correct temperature and in the correct order, and manage waste and pests correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Persoonlike higiëne\n\n'n **Voedselhanteerder** kan bakterieë van sy liggaam en klere na die kos oordra. Daarom:\n\n- Bad of stort **daagliks** en dra 'n **skoon uniform**: sjefsbaadjie, voorskoot, hoed of haarnet en **toe, glyvaste skoene**.\n- Maak hare **vas en bedek** dit.\n- Hou naels **kort en skoon**, sonder naellak (dit skilfer af in kos).\n- Geen **juweliersware** of sterk parfuum nie – juwele huisves bakterieë en kan in kos val.\n- **Moenie rook, eet of kougom kou** in die voedselarea nie.\n- Bedek snye met 'n **blou waterdigte pleister**. Blou is nie 'n natuurlike kleur van kos nie, so 'n pleister wat in die kos val, word maklik raakgesien.\n- **Rapporteer siekte** (diarree, braking) aan jou toesighouer en moenie kos hanteer nie.\n- Proe kos met 'n **skoon lepel elke keer**.\n\n### Handewas\n\n**Wanneer?** Voor jy begin werk; ná die toilet; ná jy rou vleis of eiers hanteer het; ná afval; ná jy jou gesig, hare of selfoon aangeraak het; ná skoonmaak; en ná jy genies of gehoes het.\n\n**Hoe?**\n1. Maak hande nat met **warm water**.\n2. Gebruik **seep**.\n3. Vryf **minstens 20 sekondes** – ook die duime, naels en tussen die vingers.\n4. Spoel af.\n5. Droog af met 'n **papierhanddoek** (nie aan jou voorskoot nie!).\n\n## Kombuishigiëne\n\n| Term | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| **Skoonmaak** | Sigbare vuil, vet en kosreste verwyder met water en 'n skoonmaakmiddel |\n| **Sanitering** | Mikro-organismes tot 'n **veilige vlak** verminder (met 'n saniteermiddel of baie warm water), bv. op werkoppervlakke wat aan kos raak |\n| **Ontsmetting** | Die meeste skadelike mikro-organismes doodmaak met 'n sterk chemiese middel, bv. in toilette, dreine en vullisdromme |\n\n- **Maak skoon soos jy werk** (clean as you go): mors en vuil toerusting word dadelik skoongemaak.\n- 'n **Skoonmaakrooster** sê **wat**, **wanneer**, **hoe** en **deur wie** skoongemaak word (daagliks, weekliks, maandeliks).\n- **Skottelgoed was:** afskraap → was in warm seepwater → spoel → saniteer → laat **lugdroog**.\n- **Lappe** word gereeld gewas en gesaniteer; gebruik aparte lappe vir verskillende areas.\n\n### Kleurgekodeerde snyplanke\n\n| Kleur | Gebruik |\n|---|---|\n| Rooi | Rou vleis |\n| Blou | Rou vis |\n| Geel | Gaar vleis |\n| Groen | Slaai en vrugte |\n| Bruin | Groente |\n| Wit | Suiwel en bakkery |\n\n**Regulasie R638 (2018)** vereis dat elke voedselperseel 'n **Sertifikaat van Aanvaarbaarheid** van die plaaslike munisipaliteit het voordat dit kos mag hanteer en verkoop.\n\n## Berging en temperatuurbeheer\n\n- **Yskas:** 1–4 °C (onder 5 °C). **Vrieskas:** −18 °C of kouer.\n- **Droë stoorkamer:** koel, droog en goed geventileer, met rakke **van die vloer af**.\n- Bêre **rou vleis onder** gaar en gereed-om-te-eet kos, sodat druppels nie op ander kos val nie.\n- **Bedek, etiketteer en dateer** alle kos.\n- **EIEU (FIFO – eerste in, eerste uit):** ou voorraad word eerste gebruik; nuwe voorraad gaan agter of onder die ou voorraad.\n- **Ontdooi** kos in die **yskas**, nie op die toonbank nie.\n- **Moet nooit** ontdooide rou kos weer vries nie. Bakterieë vermeerder tydens ontdooiing, en vries maak hulle nie dood nie.\n\n## Afvalbestuur\n\n- Gebruik vullisdromme met **deksels en 'n voetpedaal**, uitgevoer met 'n sak. Maak hulle **daagliks** leeg en skoon, en hou hulle weg van kos.\n- Skei **herwinbare materiaal**: glas, papier, plastiek en metaal.\n- Maak **kompos** van groente- en vrugteafval.\n- **Gebruikte kookolie** word in geseëlde houers aan **geregistreerde herwinners** gegee – **nooit** in die drein nie. Dit stol en blokkeer dreine; **vetvalle** vang vet op.\n- Volg die reël **verminder, hergebruik, herwin**.\n\n## Kombuisplae\n\n| Plaag | Tekens |\n|---|---|\n| Kakkerlakke | eierkapsules, dooie insekte, 'n onaangename reuk |\n| Vlieë en miere | insekte op of naby kos en afval |\n| Knaagdiere (rotte, muise) | **uitwerpsels**, **knaagmerke** aan sakke en verpakking |\n| Kalanders | klein kewertjies in meel, rys en graan |\n\n**Voorkoming:** seël krake en gate, sit **vlieëskerms** op, bêre kos in **geseëlde houers**, maak mors dadelik skoon, verwyder afval gereeld en gebruik **professionele plaagbeheer**. Moet **nooit gif naby kos** bêre nie.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om hande aan jou voorskoot af te droog. Dit besmet jou skoon hande dadelik weer.","en":"## Personal hygiene\n\nA **food handler** can transfer bacteria from his body and clothes to food. Therefore:\n\n- Bath or shower **daily** and wear a **clean uniform**: chef's jacket, apron, hat or hairnet and **closed, non-slip shoes**.\n- Tie hair **back and cover** it.\n- Keep nails **short and clean**, without nail polish (it flakes into food).\n- No **jewellery** or strong perfume – jewellery harbours bacteria and can fall into food.\n- **Do not smoke, eat or chew gum** in the food area.\n- Cover cuts with a **blue waterproof plaster**. Blue is not a natural food colour, so a plaster that falls into food is easy to spot.\n- **Report illness** (diarrhoea, vomiting) to your supervisor and do not handle food.\n- Taste food with a **clean spoon every time**.\n\n### Hand washing\n\n**When?** Before you start work; after the toilet; after handling raw meat or eggs; after waste; after touching your face, hair or phone; after cleaning; and after sneezing or coughing.\n\n**How?**\n1. Wet hands with **warm water**.\n2. Use **soap**.\n3. Rub for **at least 20 seconds** – including the thumbs, nails and between the fingers.\n4. Rinse.\n5. Dry with a **paper towel** (not on your apron!).\n\n## Kitchen hygiene\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Cleaning** | Removing visible dirt, grease and food particles with water and a detergent |\n| **Sanitising** | Reducing micro-organisms to a **safe level** (with a sanitiser or very hot water), e.g. on work surfaces that touch food |\n| **Disinfecting** | Killing most harmful micro-organisms with a strong chemical, e.g. in toilets, drains and bins |\n\n- **Clean as you go**: spills and dirty equipment are cleaned immediately.\n- A **cleaning schedule** says **what**, **when**, **how** and **by whom** something is cleaned (daily, weekly, monthly).\n- **Washing dishes:** scrape → wash in hot soapy water → rinse → sanitise → **air-dry**.\n- **Cloths** are washed and sanitised regularly; use separate cloths for different areas.\n\n### Colour-coded cutting boards\n\n| Colour | Use |\n|---|---|\n| Red | Raw meat |\n| Blue | Raw fish |\n| Yellow | Cooked meat |\n| Green | Salad and fruit |\n| Brown | Vegetables |\n| White | Dairy and bakery |\n\n**Regulation R638 (2018)** requires every food premises to have a **Certificate of Acceptability** from the local municipality before it may handle and sell food.\n\n## Storage and temperature control\n\n- **Refrigerator:** 1–4 °C (below 5 °C). **Freezer:** −18 °C or colder.\n- **Dry store:** cool, dry and well ventilated, with shelves **off the floor**.\n- Store **raw meat below** cooked and ready-to-eat food, so that drips cannot fall on other food.\n- **Cover, label and date** all food.\n- **FIFO (first in, first out):** old stock is used first; new stock goes behind or below the old stock.\n- **Thaw** food in the **refrigerator**, not on the counter.\n- **Never** refreeze thawed raw food. Bacteria multiply during thawing, and freezing does not kill them.\n\n## Waste management\n\n- Use bins with **lids and a foot pedal**, lined with a bag. Empty and clean them **daily**, and keep them away from food.\n- Separate **recyclables**: glass, paper, plastic and metal.\n- **Compost** vegetable and fruit waste.\n- **Used cooking oil** is given to **registered recyclers** in sealed containers – **never** down the drain. It solidifies and blocks drains; **grease traps** catch fat.\n- Follow the rule **reduce, reuse, recycle**.\n\n## Kitchen pests\n\n| Pest | Signs |\n|---|---|\n| Cockroaches | egg cases, dead insects, an unpleasant smell |\n| Flies and ants | insects on or near food and waste |\n| Rodents (rats, mice) | **droppings**, **gnaw marks** on bags and packaging |\n| Weevils | tiny beetles in flour, rice and grain |\n\n**Prevention:** seal cracks and holes, fit **fly screens**, store food in **sealed containers**, clean spills immediately, remove waste regularly and use **professional pest control**. **Never** store poison near food.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Drying your hands on your apron. It immediately contaminates your clean hands again."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Persoonlike higiëne","en":"Personal hygiene"},"def":{"af":"Die maniere waarop 'n voedselhanteerder sy liggaam, hare, hande en klere skoon hou sodat hy nie kos besmet nie.","en":"The ways a food handler keeps his body, hair, hands and clothes clean so that he does not contaminate food."}},{"term":{"af":"Skoonmaak","en":"Cleaning"},"def":{"af":"Die verwydering van sigbare vuil, vet en kosreste met water en 'n skoonmaakmiddel.","en":"Removing visible dirt, grease and food particles with water and a detergent."}},{"term":{"af":"Sanitering","en":"Sanitising"},"def":{"af":"Die vermindering van mikro-organismes op 'n oppervlak tot 'n veilige vlak, met 'n saniteermiddel of baie warm water.","en":"Reducing the micro-organisms on a surface to a safe level, with a sanitiser or very hot water."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontsmetting","en":"Disinfecting"},"def":{"af":"Die doodmaak van die meeste skadelike mikro-organismes met 'n sterk chemiese middel, bv. in toilette en dreine.","en":"Killing most harmful micro-organisms with a strong chemical, e.g. in toilets and drains."}},{"term":{"af":"Maak skoon soos jy werk","en":"Clean as you go"},"def":{"af":"Die gewoonte om mors en gebruikte toerusting dadelik skoon te maak eerder as aan die einde van die skof.","en":"The habit of cleaning spills and used equipment immediately rather than at the end of the shift."}},{"term":{"af":"Sertifikaat van Aanvaarbaarheid","en":"Certificate of Acceptability"},"def":{"af":"Die sertifikaat wat Regulasie R638 vir elke voedselperseel vereis, uitgereik deur die plaaslike munisipaliteit.","en":"The certificate that Regulation R638 requires for every food premises, issued by the local municipality."}},{"term":{"af":"EIEU (FIFO)","en":"FIFO"},"def":{"af":"Eerste in, eerste uit: voorraad wat eerste ontvang is, word eerste gebruik.","en":"First in, first out: stock that was received first is used first."}},{"term":{"af":"Afvalbestuur","en":"Waste management"},"def":{"af":"Die veilige versameling, skeiding, herwinning en verwydering van afval in 'n kombuis.","en":"The safe collection, separation, recycling and removal of waste in a kitchen."}},{"term":{"af":"Plae","en":"Pests"},"def":{"af":"Insekte en diere, soos kakkerlakke, vlieë, rotte, muise, miere en kalanders, wat kos besmet en siektes versprei.","en":"Insects and animals, such as cockroaches, flies, rats, mice, ants and weevils, that contaminate food and spread disease."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer higiënefoute","en":"Identify hygiene mistakes"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die scenario en identifiseer **vyf** higiënefoute. Sê telkens wat Pieter moet doen.\n\n> Pieter is 'n kok in 'n restaurant in Brits. Hy kom werk toe in sy tekkies, met sy lang hare los en sy horlosie en ring aan. Hy het 'n sny aan sy vinger wat hy met 'n velkleurige pleister bedek. Hy proe die sous met die lepel waarmee hy roer, en droog sy hande aan sy voorskoot af.","en":"Read the scenario and identify **five** hygiene mistakes. Each time, say what Pieter should do.\n\n> Pieter is a cook in a restaurant in Brits. He arrives at work in his sneakers, with his long hair loose and his watch and ring on. He has a cut on his finger that he covers with a skin-coloured plaster. He tastes the sauce with the spoon he stirs with, and dries his hands on his apron."},"steps":[{"af":"1. **Tekkies** → dra toe, glyvaste skoene wat jou voete teen warm vloeistof en messe beskerm.","en":"1. **Sneakers** → wear closed, non-slip shoes that protect your feet from hot liquids and knives."},{"af":"2. **Lang hare los** → maak dit vas en bedek dit met 'n hoed of haarnet.","en":"2. **Long hair loose** → tie it back and cover it with a hat or hairnet."},{"af":"3. **Horlosie en ring** → haal alle juweliersware af; dit huisves bakterieë en kan in kos val.","en":"3. **Watch and ring** → remove all jewellery; it harbours bacteria and can fall into food."},{"af":"4. **Velkleurige pleister** → gebruik 'n blou waterdigte pleister, wat maklik raakgesien word as dit in die kos val.","en":"4. **Skin-coloured plaster** → use a blue waterproof plaster, which is easy to spot if it falls into the food."},{"af":"5. **Proe met die roerlepel** en **hande aan die voorskoot** → proe elke keer met 'n skoon lepel, en droog hande met 'n papierhanddoek.","en":"5. **Tasting with the stirring spoon** and **hands on the apron** → taste with a clean spoon every time, and dry hands with a paper towel."}],"answer":{"af":"Tekkies, hare los, juweliersware, velkleurige pleister, proe met die roerlepel (of hande aan die voorskoot)","en":"Sneakers, hair loose, jewellery, skin-coloured plaster, tasting with the stirring spoon (or hands on the apron)"}},{"title":{"af":"Pak die yskas reg","en":"Pack the refrigerator correctly"},"problem":{"af":"'n Kok moet die volgende in 'n yskas bêre: **rou hoenderstukke**, **gekookte ham**, **jogurt**, **rou maalvleis** en **slaaiblare**. Sê waar elkeen moet gaan en verduidelik waarom.","en":"A cook must store the following in a refrigerator: **raw chicken pieces**, **cooked ham**, **yoghurt**, **raw mince** and **lettuce**. Say where each one should go and explain why."},"steps":[{"af":"Die yskas moet tussen 1 en 4 °C wees (onder 5 °C). Alle kos word bedek, geëtiketteer en gedateer.","en":"The refrigerator must be between 1 and 4 °C (below 5 °C). All food is covered, labelled and dated."},{"af":"**Boonste rakke:** gereed-om-te-eet kos – die gekookte ham en die jogurt. Dit word nie weer gekook nie, so dit moet die beste beskerm word.","en":"**Top shelves:** ready-to-eat food – the cooked ham and the yoghurt. It will not be cooked again, so it must be protected best."},{"af":"**Groentelaai:** die slaaiblare.","en":"**Vegetable drawer:** the lettuce."},{"af":"**Onderste rak:** die rou hoender en rou maalvleis in bakke met deksels, sodat bloed en vleissap nie op ander kos kan drup nie (kruisbesmetting).","en":"**Bottom shelf:** the raw chicken and raw mince in covered containers, so that blood and meat juices cannot drip onto other food (cross-contamination)."}],"answer":{"af":"Bo: ham en jogurt; laai: slaaiblare; onder: rou hoender en rou maalvleis (bedek)","en":"Top: ham and yoghurt; drawer: lettuce; bottom: raw chicken and raw mince (covered)"}},{"title":{"af":"Pas EIEU (FIFO) toe","en":"Apply FIFO"},"problem":{"af":"In die droë stoorkamer staan twee sakke koekmeelblom: een is op **5 September** en een op **19 September** afgelewer. Vandag (3 Oktober) lewer die verskaffer nog 'n sak af.\n\n(a) Watter sak moet eerste gebruik word?\n(b) Waar moet die nuwe sak gaan?\n(c) Verduidelik waarom EIEU belangrik is.","en":"In the dry store there are two bags of cake flour: one was delivered on **5 September** and one on **19 September**. Today (3 October) the supplier delivers another bag.\n\n(a) Which bag must be used first?\n(b) Where must the new bag go?\n(c) Explain why FIFO is important."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) EIEU = eerste in, eerste uit. Die sak van **5 September** het eerste ingekom, so dit word eerste gebruik.","en":"(a) FIFO = first in, first out. The bag from **5 September** came in first, so it is used first."},{"af":"(b) Die nuwe sak (3 Oktober) word **agter of onder** die ouer sakke geplaas, op 'n rak van die vloer af, met die afleweringsdatum daarop.","en":"(b) The new bag (3 October) is placed **behind or below** the older bags, on a shelf off the floor, with the delivery date on it."},{"af":"(c) Ou voorraad word gebruik voordat dit verval of bederf (bv. kalanders in meel). Dit verminder vermorsing en spaar geld.","en":"(c) Old stock is used before it expires or spoils (e.g. weevils in flour). This reduces waste and saves money."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die sak van 5 September (b) Agter/onder die ou sakke (c) Voorkom bederf en vermorsing","en":"(a) The bag from 5 September (b) Behind/below the old bags (c) Prevents spoilage and waste"}},{"title":{"af":"Afvalbestuur by 'n koffiewinkel","en":"Waste management at a coffee shop"},"problem":{"af":"'n Koffiewinkel by Hartbeespoortdam het baie koffiemoer, leë melkbottels, karton, groenteskille en gebruikte kookolie. Stel **vyf** goeie afvalbestuurspraktyke voor.","en":"A coffee shop at Hartbeespoort Dam has a lot of coffee grounds, empty milk bottles, cardboard, vegetable peels and used cooking oil. Suggest **five** good waste-management practices."},"steps":[{"af":"1. Gebruik vullisdromme met **deksels en voetpedale**, uitgevoer met sakke, wat **daagliks** leeggemaak en skoongemaak word – weg van die kos.","en":"1. Use bins with **lids and foot pedals**, lined with bags, that are emptied and cleaned **daily** – away from the food."},{"af":"2. **Skei herwinbare materiaal:** plastiekbottels, karton/papier, glas en blikke in aparte houers vir herwinning.","en":"2. **Separate recyclables:** plastic bottles, cardboard/paper, glass and tins in separate containers for recycling."},{"af":"3. Maak **kompos** van die koffiemoer en groenteskille.","en":"3. **Compost** the coffee grounds and vegetable peels."},{"af":"4. Gooi **gebruikte kookolie** in geseëlde houers vir 'n **geregistreerde herwinner** – nooit in die drein nie, want dit blokkeer dreine.","en":"4. Put **used cooking oil** in sealed containers for a **registered recycler** – never down the drain, because it blocks drains."},{"af":"5. **Verminder en hergebruik:** koop in grootmaat met minder verpakking en moedig klante aan om hul eie bekers te bring.","en":"5. **Reduce and reuse:** buy in bulk with less packaging and encourage customers to bring their own cups."}],"answer":{"af":"Bv. dromme met deksels, herwinning, kompos, olie na 'n herwinner, verminder en hergebruik","en":"E.g. lidded bins, recycling, compost, oil to a recycler, reduce and reuse"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By watter temperatuur moet 'n yskas in 'n kombuis wees?","en":"At what temperature should a refrigerator in a kitchen be?"},"options":[{"af":"−18 °C of kouer","en":"−18 °C or colder"},{"af":"1–4 °C","en":"1–4 °C"},{"af":"10–15 °C","en":"10–15 °C"},{"af":"20–25 °C","en":"20–25 °C"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Yskas moet tussen 1 en 4 °C wees (onder 5 °C) om bakteriegroei te vertraag. −18 °C of kouer is die temperatuur van 'n vrieskas.","en":"A refrigerator must be between 1 and 4 °C (below 5 °C) to slow down bacterial growth. −18 °C or colder is the temperature of a freezer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Vrieskas moet op ___ °C of kouer wees.","en":"A freezer must be at ___ °C or colder."},"answers":{"af":["-18","−18","minus 18"],"en":["-18","−18","minus 18"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Vrieskas moet op −18 °C of kouer wees. By hierdie temperatuur groei bakterieë nie, maar hulle gaan nie dood nie.","en":"A freezer must be at −18 °C or colder. At this temperature bacteria do not grow, but they do not die."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0","4","−5"],"en":["0","4","−5"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Voedselhanteerders gebruik blou waterdigte pleisters omdat 'n blou pleister maklik raakgesien word as dit in die kos val.","en":"Food handlers use blue waterproof plasters because a blue plaster is easy to spot if it falls into the food."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Blou is nie 'n natuurlike kleur van kos nie, so 'n blou pleister val dadelik op. Waterdig keer ook dat bloed of bakterieë uit die wond by die kos kom.","en":"True. Blue is not a natural food colour, so a blue plaster stands out immediately. Waterproof also stops blood or bacteria from the wound reaching the food."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter plaag kry jy gewoonlik in meel, rys en ander droë graanprodukte?","en":"Which pest is usually found in flour, rice and other dry cereal products?"},"options":[{"af":"Kakkerlakke","en":"Cockroaches"},{"af":"Vlieë","en":"Flies"},{"af":"Kalanders","en":"Weevils"},{"af":"Rotte","en":"Rats"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Kalanders is klein kewertjies wat in meel, rys en graan leef. Bêre droë kos in geseëlde houers en gebruik EIEU sodat dit nie te lank staan nie.","en":"Weevils are tiny beetles that live in flour, rice and grain. Store dry food in sealed containers and use FIFO so that it does not stand for too long."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"EIEU (FIFO) staan vir \"eerste in, eerste ___\".","en":"FIFO stands for \"first in, first ___\"."},"answers":{"af":["uit"],"en":["out"]},"explain":{"af":"Eerste in, eerste uit: die voorraad wat eerste ontvang is, word eerste gebruik.","en":"First in, first out: the stock that was received first is used first."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["in","laaste","terug"],"en":["in","last","back"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe lank moet jy jou hande minstens met seep vryf wanneer jy dit was?","en":"For how long must you rub your hands with soap, at least, when you wash them?"},"options":[{"af":"20 sekondes","en":"20 seconds"},{"af":"3 sekondes","en":"3 seconds"},{"af":"10 sekondes","en":"10 seconds"},{"af":"Net totdat die seep skuim","en":"Only until the soap lathers"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vryf minstens 20 sekondes, ook die duime, naels en tussen die vingers. Korter as dit verwyder nie genoeg bakterieë nie.","en":"Rub for at least 20 seconds, including the thumbs, nails and between the fingers. Shorter than that does not remove enough bacteria."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Volgens Regulasie R638 moet elke voedselperseel 'n Sertifikaat van ___ hê voordat dit kos mag hanteer en verkoop.","en":"According to Regulation R638 every food premises must have a Certificate of ___ before it may handle and sell food."},"answers":{"af":["Aanvaarbaarheid"],"en":["Acceptability"]},"explain":{"af":"R638 (2018) vereis 'n Sertifikaat van Aanvaarbaarheid, uitgereik deur die plaaslike munisipaliteit nadat die perseel geïnspekteer is.","en":"R638 (2018) requires a Certificate of Acceptability, issued by the local municipality after the premises has been inspected."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Registrasie","Bekwaamheid","Higiëne"],"en":["Registration","Competence","Hygiene"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verskil tussen skoonmaak en sanitering?","en":"What is the difference between cleaning and sanitising?"},"options":[{"af":"Daar is geen verskil nie – albei beteken om sigbare vuil af te was","en":"There is no difference – both mean washing off visible dirt"},{"af":"Skoonmaak maak alle bakterieë dood; sanitering verwyder net vuil","en":"Cleaning kills all bacteria; sanitising only removes dirt"},{"af":"Sanitering word net op vloere gedoen en skoonmaak net op toerusting","en":"Sanitising is only done on floors and cleaning only on equipment"},{"af":"Skoonmaak verwyder sigbare vuil en vet; sanitering verminder mikro-organismes tot 'n veilige vlak","en":"Cleaning removes visible dirt and grease; sanitising reduces micro-organisms to a safe level"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Skoonmaak verwyder wat jy kan sien (vuil, vet, kosreste). Sanitering kom daarna en verminder die onsigbare mikro-organismes tot 'n veilige vlak. Jy kan nie 'n vuil oppervlak doeltreffend saniteer nie.","en":"Cleaning removes what you can see (dirt, grease, food particles). Sanitising follows and reduces the invisible micro-organisms to a safe level. You cannot sanitise a dirty surface effectively."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Rou vleis moet op die boonste rak van die yskas gebêre word sodat dit vinnig koud word.","en":"Raw meat must be stored on the top shelf of the refrigerator so that it gets cold quickly."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Rou vleis gaan op die onderste rak, sodat bloed en vleissap nie op gaar of gereed-om-te-eet kos kan drup nie.","en":"False. Raw meat goes on the bottom shelf, so that blood and meat juices cannot drip onto cooked or ready-to-eat food."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke snyplankkleur by die kos waarvoor dit gebruik word.","en":"Match each cutting-board colour to the food it is used for."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Rooi","en":"Red"},"r":{"af":"Rou vleis","en":"Raw meat"}},{"l":{"af":"Blou","en":"Blue"},"r":{"af":"Rou vis","en":"Raw fish"}},{"l":{"af":"Geel","en":"Yellow"},"r":{"af":"Gaar vleis","en":"Cooked meat"}},{"l":{"af":"Groen","en":"Green"},"r":{"af":"Slaai en vrugte","en":"Salad and fruit"}},{"l":{"af":"Bruin","en":"Brown"},"r":{"af":"Groente","en":"Vegetables"}}],"explain":{"af":"Rooi = rou vleis, blou = rou vis, geel = gaar vleis, groen = slaai en vrugte, bruin = groente (wit = suiwel en bakkery). Aparte planke voorkom kruisbesmetting.","en":"Red = raw meat, blue = raw fish, yellow = cooked meat, green = salad and fruit, brown = vegetables (white = dairy and bakery). Separate boards prevent cross-contamination."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die regte volgorde om skottelgoed met die hand te was, is: afskraap → was in warm seepwater → spoel → ___ → lugdroog.","en":"The correct order for washing dishes by hand is: scrape → wash in hot soapy water → rinse → ___ → air-dry."},"answers":{"af":["saniteer","sanitering","ontsmet","ontsmetting"],"en":["sanitise","sanitize","sanitising","sanitizing"]},"explain":{"af":"Ná spoel word skottelgoed gesaniteer (saniteermiddel of baie warm water) en dan laat lugdroog. 'n Droogdoek kan bakterieë terugsit.","en":"After rinsing, dishes are sanitised (sanitiser or very hot water) and then left to air-dry. A drying cloth can put bacteria back."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["afdroog met 'n lap","skrop","inweek"],"en":["dry with a cloth","scrub","soak"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kok sny sy vinger terwyl hy groente voorberei. Die sny is klein en hy kan voortgaan met werk. Wat moet hy doen?","en":"A cook cuts his finger while preparing vegetables. The cut is small and he can carry on working. What should he do?"},"options":[{"af":"Bedek dit met 'n velkleurige pleister sodat gaste dit nie sien nie","en":"Cover it with a skin-coloured plaster so that guests do not see it"},{"af":"Laat dit oop sodat dit vinniger gesond word","en":"Leave it open so that it heals faster"},{"af":"Bedek dit met 'n blou waterdigte pleister en dra 'n handskoen daaroor","en":"Cover it with a blue waterproof plaster and wear a glove over it"},{"af":"Draai 'n skoon vadoek om die vinger","en":"Wrap a clean dishcloth around the finger"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Oop wond bevat bakterieë (soos Staphylococcus). 'n Blou waterdigte pleister keer dat dit by die kos kom, en as dit afval, word dit maklik gesien. 'n Handskoen gee ekstra beskerming.","en":"An open wound contains bacteria (such as Staphylococcus). A blue waterproof plaster keeps them away from the food, and if it falls off it is easily seen. A glove gives extra protection."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe moet 'n restaurant van gebruikte kookolie ontslae raak?","en":"How should a restaurant get rid of used cooking oil?"},"options":[{"af":"Gooi dit in geseëlde houers en gee dit aan 'n geregistreerde herwinner","en":"Put it in sealed containers and give it to a registered recycler"},{"af":"Gooi dit met baie warm water in die drein","en":"Pour it down the drain with lots of hot water"},{"af":"Gooi dit in die gewone vullisdrom saam met die kosafval","en":"Put it in the ordinary bin with the food waste"},{"af":"Gooi dit in die tuin uit","en":"Pour it out in the garden"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Olie stol wanneer dit afkoel en blokkeer dreine, selfs met warm water. Dit besoedel ook grond en water. Geregistreerde herwinners verwerk dit veilig (bv. tot biobrandstof).","en":"Oil solidifies when it cools and blocks drains, even with hot water. It also pollutes soil and water. Registered recyclers process it safely (e.g. into biofuel)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Drie blikke tamaties in die droë stoorkamer is op 3 Maart, 10 Februarie en 24 Februarie afgelewer. Volgens EIEU gebruik jy eerste die blik van ___.","en":"Three tins of tomatoes in the dry store were delivered on 3 March, 10 February and 24 February. According to FIFO you first use the tin from ___."},"answers":{"af":["10 Februarie","10 Feb","10"],"en":["10 February","10 Feb","February 10","10"]},"explain":{"af":"10 Februarie is die oudste afleweringsdatum – eerste in, dus eerste uit. 3 Maart is die nuutste blik en word laaste gebruik.","en":"10 February is the oldest delivery date – first in, so first out. 3 March is the newest tin and is used last."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3 Maart","24 Februarie","Enige een"],"en":["3 March","24 February","Any one"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom mag ontdooide rou hoender nie weer gevries word nie?","en":"Why may thawed raw chicken not be refrozen?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat vries alle bakterieë doodmaak, so 'n tweede keer is onnodig","en":"Because freezing kills all bacteria, so a second time is unnecessary"},{"af":"Omdat die hoender chemies giftig word sodra dit twee keer gevries is","en":"Because the chicken becomes chemically poisonous once it has been frozen twice"},{"af":"Omdat die vrieskas dan te vol raak","en":"Because the freezer then becomes too full"},{"af":"Bakterieë het tydens ontdooiing vermeerder; vries maak hulle nie dood nie, so hulle groei verder wanneer die hoender weer ontdooi","en":"Bacteria multiplied during thawing; freezing does not kill them, so they grow further when the chicken thaws again"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vries stop bakteriegroei net tydelik. Elke keer as die hoender ontdooi, vermeerder die bakterieë verder, so die risiko van voedselvergiftiging word groter (en die gehalte swakker).","en":"Freezing only stops bacterial growth temporarily. Every time the chicken thaws the bacteria multiply further, so the risk of food poisoning increases (and the quality decreases)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Omgewingsgesondheidsbeampte vind rotuitwerpsels in 'n restaurant se droë stoorkamer, meelsakke wat op die vloer staan en 'n oop vullisdrom by die agterdeur. Watter plan van aksie is die beste?","en":"An environmental health officer finds rat droppings in a restaurant's dry store, bags of flour standing on the floor and an open bin at the back door. Which plan of action is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"Sit rottegif tussen die meelsakke sodat die rotte dit vinnig kry","en":"Put rat poison between the flour bags so that the rats find it quickly"},{"af":"Kry professionele plaagbeheer, seël krake, bêre meel in geseëlde houers op rakke van die vloer af en gebruik vullisdromme met deksels wat daagliks leeggemaak word","en":"Get professional pest control, seal cracks, store flour in sealed containers on shelves off the floor and use lidded bins that are emptied daily"},{"af":"Vee net die uitwerpsels op – dan is die probleem opgelos","en":"Just sweep up the droppings – then the problem is solved"},{"af":"Spuit insekgif oor die rakke met kos sodat alle plae doodgaan","en":"Spray insecticide over the shelves with food so that all pests die"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die beste plan pak al die oorsake aan: kos wat rotte kan bereik, toegang deur krake en afval wat hulle lok. Gif mag nooit naby kos wees nie (chemiese besmetting), en net opvee los niks op nie.","en":"The best plan tackles all the causes: food that rats can reach, access through cracks and waste that attracts them. Poison may never be near food (chemical contamination), and just sweeping up solves nothing."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-voedselveiligheid","title":{"af":"Voedselbesmetting, voedselvergiftiging en HACCP-beginsels","en":"Food contamination, food-borne illness and HACCP basics"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal besmetting kan klassifiseer, die gevaarsone en FATTOM kan verduidelik, die bakterie in 'n gevallestudie kan identifiseer en die sewe HACCP-beginsels kan toepas.","en":"You will be able to classify contamination, explain the danger zone and FATTOM, identify the bacterium in a case study and apply the seven HACCP principles."},"summary":{"af":"## Tipes besmetting\n\n**Besmetting** beteken dat iets skadeliks in kos beland.\n\n| Tipe | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **Biologies** | bakterieë, virusse, skimmels, giste, parasiete |\n| **Chemies** | skoonmaakmiddels, plaagdoders (insek- en rottegif) |\n| **Fisies** | hare, glas, metaal (bv. staalwol), pleisters, stukkies verpakking |\n\n**Kruisbesmetting** is die oordrag van bakterieë van **rou** kos na **gaar** of gereed-om-te-eet kos – deur hande, snyplanke, messe, lappe of druppels in die yskas.\n\n**Hoërisiko-voedsel** is klam kos met baie proteïen waarin bakterieë maklik groei: vleis, pluimvee, vis, eiers, suiwelprodukte, **gekookte rys**, sous (gravy) en room. Ongekookte rys is droog en dus nie hoërisiko nie.\n\n## Toestande vir bakteriegroei: FATTOM\n\n| Letter | Faktor | Verduideliking |\n|---|---|---|\n| F | Food (voedsel) | bakterieë verkies klam, proteïenryke kos |\n| A | Acidity (suurgehalte) | hulle groei swak in baie suur kos (asyn, suurlemoensap) |\n| T | Time (tyd) | in ideale toestande verdubbel hulle **ongeveer elke 20 minute** |\n| T | Temperature (temperatuur) | hulle groei die vinnigste in die **gevaarsone** |\n| O | Oxygen (suurstof) | sommige het suurstof nodig; ander, soos *C. botulinum*, groei sonder suurstof |\n| M | Moisture (vog) | hulle het water nodig, daarom is droë kos veiliger |\n\n**Hoe vinnig?** As een bakterie elke 20 minute verdubbel, is daar ná 1 uur 8, ná 2 uur 64 en ná 3 uur 512 bakterieë. Gebruik: getal = begingetal × 2^{aantal verdubbelings}.\n\n### Die gevaarsone en temperatuurreëls\n\n- **Gevaarsone: 5 °C–60 °C** – bakterieë vermeerder hier die vinnigste.\n- Kook kos tot 'n **kerntemperatuur van minstens 75 °C** (meet met 'n sondetermometer in die dikste deel).\n- Hou **warm kos bo 60 °C** en **koue kos onder 5 °C**.\n- **Koel warm kos vinnig af** in vlak houers voordat dit in die yskas gaan.\n\n> **Onthou!** Koue laat bakterieë net **stadiger** groei – dit maak hulle nie dood nie. Hitte maak die meeste bakterieë dood, maar sommige vorm **spore** of **gifstowwe (toksiene)** wat hitte oorleef.\n\n## Voedselvergiftiging\n\n**Simptome:** naarheid, braking, diarree, maagkrampe en koors.\n\n| Bakterie | Tipiese bron | Voorkoming |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Salmonella* | rou pluimvee, eiers | kook deeglik; hou rou en gaar kos apart; was hande |\n| *Staphylococcus aureus* | die mens se neus, keel, snye en sere (bv. 'n sweer) | goeie persoonlike higiëne; bedek snye; moenie kos hanteer as jy siek is nie – sy gifstof word nie deur hitte vernietig nie |\n| *Clostridium perfringens* | groot vleisgeregte wat stadig afkoel (bredies, sous) | koel vinnig af in klein, vlak hoeveelhede; herverhit deeglik |\n| *Clostridium botulinum* | sleg ingemaakte kos, **opgeswelde blikke** | gooi opgeswelde of beskadigde blikke weg sonder om te proe – sy gifstof tas die senuweestelsel aan |\n| *E. coli* | halfgaar maalvleis, fekale besmetting | kook maalvleis deur; was hande ná die toilet |\n| *Listeria* | gereed-om-te-eet verwerkte vleis (polonie), sagte kaas | groei **selfs in die yskas**; hou by vervaldatums en streng higiëne |\n| *Bacillus cereus* | gekookte rys wat lank warm gehou word | koel rys vinnig af; moenie dit lank warm hou nie |\n\nSuid-Afrika se **listeriose-uitbreking van 2017–2018** is aan **polonie** gekoppel – een van die grootste listeriose-uitbrekings wat nog ooit aangeteken is.\n\n## HACCP-beginsels\n\n**HACCP** (Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points – **gevaarontleding en kritieke beheerpunte**) is 'n **voorkomende** voedselveiligheidstelsel: jy identifiseer gevare en beheer hulle **voordat** iets verkeerd loop, eerder as om ná 'n uitbreking te reageer. (Meer besonderhede volg in Gr 11–12.)\n\n**Die 7 beginsels:**\n\n1. Doen 'n **gevaarontleding** – watter biologiese, chemiese of fisiese gevare kan by elke stap voorkom?\n2. Bepaal die **kritieke beheerpunte (KBP's)** – die stappe waar 'n gevaar voorkom of uitgeskakel kan word.\n3. Stel **kritieke perke** vas – bv. 'n kerntemperatuur van minstens 75 °C.\n4. **Moniteer** – meet en kontroleer gereeld, bv. met 'n sondetermometer.\n5. Neem **regstellende aksie** as 'n perk nie gehaal word nie – bv. kook langer.\n6. **Verifieer** dat die stelsel werk – bv. toets of die termometers akkuraat is.\n7. Hou **rekords** – skryf temperature en aksies in 'n logboek.\n\n**Voorbeelde van KBP's:** die temperatuur by **ontvangs** van kos, **kook** (kerntemperatuur), **afkoeling** en **warmhou**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders verwar die **KBP** (die stap, bv. kook) met die **kritieke perk** (die meetbare grens, bv. 75 °C).","en":"## Types of contamination\n\n**Contamination** means that something harmful ends up in food.\n\n| Type | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **Biological** | bacteria, viruses, moulds, yeasts, parasites |\n| **Chemical** | cleaning agents, pesticides (insect and rat poison) |\n| **Physical** | hair, glass, metal (e.g. steel wool), plasters, bits of packaging |\n\n**Cross-contamination** is the transfer of bacteria from **raw** food to **cooked** or ready-to-eat food – via hands, cutting boards, knives, cloths or drips in the refrigerator.\n\n**High-risk foods** are moist, high-protein foods in which bacteria grow easily: meat, poultry, fish, eggs, dairy products, **cooked rice**, gravy and cream. Uncooked rice is dry and therefore not high-risk.\n\n## Conditions for bacterial growth: FATTOM\n\n| Letter | Factor | Explanation |\n|---|---|---|\n| F | Food | bacteria prefer moist, high-protein food |\n| A | Acidity | they grow poorly in very acidic food (vinegar, lemon juice) |\n| T | Time | in ideal conditions they double **about every 20 minutes** |\n| T | Temperature | they grow fastest in the **danger zone** |\n| O | Oxygen | some need oxygen; others, such as *C. botulinum*, grow without oxygen |\n| M | Moisture | they need water, which is why dry food is safer |\n\n**How fast?** If one bacterium doubles every 20 minutes, there are 8 bacteria after 1 hour, 64 after 2 hours and 512 after 3 hours. Use: number = starting number × 2^{number of doublings}.\n\n### The danger zone and temperature rules\n\n- **Danger zone: 5 °C–60 °C** – bacteria multiply fastest here.\n- Cook food to a **core temperature of at least 75 °C** (measure with a probe thermometer in the thickest part).\n- Keep **hot food above 60 °C** and **cold food below 5 °C**.\n- **Cool hot food quickly** in shallow containers before it goes into the refrigerator.\n\n> **Remember!** Cold only makes bacteria grow **more slowly** – it does not kill them. Heat kills most bacteria, but some form **spores** or **toxins** that survive heat.\n\n## Food-borne illness\n\n**Symptoms:** nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, stomach cramps and fever.\n\n| Bacterium | Typical source | Prevention |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Salmonella* | raw poultry, eggs | cook thoroughly; keep raw and cooked food apart; wash hands |\n| *Staphylococcus aureus* | the human nose, throat, cuts and sores (e.g. a boil) | good personal hygiene; cover cuts; do not handle food when ill – its toxin is not destroyed by heat |\n| *Clostridium perfringens* | large meat dishes that cool slowly (stews, gravy) | cool quickly in small, shallow quantities; reheat thoroughly |\n| *Clostridium botulinum* | badly canned food, **bulging tins** | throw away bulging or damaged tins without tasting – its toxin attacks the nervous system |\n| *E. coli* | undercooked mince, faecal contamination | cook mince through; wash hands after the toilet |\n| *Listeria* | ready-to-eat processed meats (polony), soft cheese | grows **even in the refrigerator**; keep to expiry dates and strict hygiene |\n| *Bacillus cereus* | cooked rice kept warm for a long time | cool rice quickly; do not keep it warm for long |\n\nSouth Africa's **2017–2018 listeriosis outbreak** was linked to **polony** – one of the largest listeriosis outbreaks ever recorded.\n\n## HACCP principles\n\n**HACCP** (Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points) is a **preventive** food-safety system: you identify hazards and control them **before** anything goes wrong, rather than reacting after an outbreak. (More detail follows in Gr 11–12.)\n\n**The 7 principles:**\n\n1. Conduct a **hazard analysis** – which biological, chemical or physical hazards can occur at each step?\n2. Determine the **critical control points (CCPs)** – the steps where a hazard can be prevented or eliminated.\n3. Set **critical limits** – e.g. a core temperature of at least 75 °C.\n4. **Monitor** – measure and check regularly, e.g. with a probe thermometer.\n5. Take **corrective action** if a limit is not met – e.g. cook for longer.\n6. **Verify** that the system works – e.g. test whether the thermometers are accurate.\n7. Keep **records** – write temperatures and actions in a log book.\n\n**Examples of CCPs:** the temperature on **receiving** food, **cooking** (core temperature), **cooling** and **hot-holding**.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners confuse the **CCP** (the step, e.g. cooking) with the **critical limit** (the measurable boundary, e.g. 75 °C)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Besmetting","en":"Contamination"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iets skadeliks – biologies, chemies of fisies – in kos beland.","en":"When something harmful – biological, chemical or physical – ends up in food."}},{"term":{"af":"Kruisbesmetting","en":"Cross-contamination"},"def":{"af":"Die oordrag van bakterieë van rou kos na gaar of gereed-om-te-eet kos deur hande, toerusting, lappe of druppels.","en":"The transfer of bacteria from raw food to cooked or ready-to-eat food via hands, equipment, cloths or drips."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoërisiko-voedsel","en":"High-risk food"},"def":{"af":"Klam, proteïenryke kos waarin bakterieë maklik groei, bv. vleis, pluimvee, eiers, suiwel en gekookte rys.","en":"Moist, high-protein food in which bacteria grow easily, e.g. meat, poultry, eggs, dairy and cooked rice."}},{"term":{"af":"Gevaarsone","en":"Danger zone"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuurreeks van 5 °C tot 60 °C waarin bakterieë die vinnigste vermeerder.","en":"The temperature range of 5 °C to 60 °C in which bacteria multiply fastest."}},{"term":{"af":"Kerntemperatuur","en":"Core temperature"},"def":{"af":"Die temperatuur in die middel of dikste deel van kos; dit moet minstens 75 °C wees wanneer kos gaar is.","en":"The temperature in the centre or thickest part of food; it must be at least 75 °C when food is cooked."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselvergiftiging","en":"Food-borne illness (food poisoning)"},"def":{"af":"Siekte wat veroorsaak word deur kos te eet wat met bakterieë of hul gifstowwe besmet is; simptome is naarheid, braking, diarree, maagkrampe en koors.","en":"Illness caused by eating food contaminated with bacteria or their toxins; symptoms are nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, stomach cramps and fever."}},{"term":{"af":"FATTOM","en":"FATTOM"},"def":{"af":"Die ses toestande vir bakteriegroei: voedsel, suurgehalte, tyd, temperatuur, suurstof en vog.","en":"The six conditions for bacterial growth: food, acidity, time, temperature, oxygen and moisture."}},{"term":{"af":"HACCP","en":"HACCP"},"def":{"af":"Gevaarontleding en kritieke beheerpunte: 'n voorkomende voedselveiligheidstelsel met sewe beginsels.","en":"Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points: a preventive food-safety system with seven principles."}},{"term":{"af":"Kritieke beheerpunt (KBP)","en":"Critical control point (CCP)"},"def":{"af":"'n Stap in die voedselproses waar 'n gevaar voorkom, uitgeskakel of tot 'n veilige vlak verminder kan word, bv. kook of afkoeling.","en":"A step in the food process where a hazard can be prevented, eliminated or reduced to a safe level, e.g. cooking or cooling."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer die besmetting","en":"Classify the contamination"},"problem":{"af":"'n Inspekteur besoek 'n kombuis in Brits en kry die volgende. Klassifiseer elkeen as **biologiese**, **chemiese** of **fisiese** besmetting:\n\n(a) 'n Stukkie staalwol in 'n pot bredie\n(b) Bleikmiddel wat op 'n snyplank agtergebly het\n(c) Rou hoender wat op dieselfde plank as die slaai gesny is\n(d) Skimmel op brood\n(e) 'n Pleister in die slaai","en":"An inspector visits a kitchen in Brits and finds the following. Classify each one as **biological**, **chemical** or **physical** contamination:\n\n(a) A bit of steel wool in a pot of stew\n(b) Bleach left behind on a cutting board\n(c) Raw chicken cut on the same board as the salad\n(d) Mould on bread\n(e) A plaster in the salad"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Staalwol is 'n voorwerp wat jy kan sien en voel → **fisies**.","en":"(a) Steel wool is an object you can see and feel → **physical**."},{"af":"(b) Bleikmiddel is 'n skoonmaakmiddel → **chemies**.","en":"(b) Bleach is a cleaning agent → **chemical**."},{"af":"(c) Bakterieë (bv. *Salmonella*) gaan van die rou hoender na die slaai → **biologies**, deur **kruisbesmetting**.","en":"(c) Bacteria (e.g. *Salmonella*) move from the raw chicken to the salad → **biological**, through **cross-contamination**."},{"af":"(d) Skimmel is 'n mikro-organisme → **biologies**.","en":"(d) Mould is a micro-organism → **biological**."},{"af":"(e) 'n Pleister is 'n voorwerp → **fisies** (en dit kan ook bakterieë uit 'n wond dra).","en":"(e) A plaster is an object → **physical** (and it can also carry bacteria from a wound)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) fisies (b) chemies (c) biologies – kruisbesmetting (d) biologies (e) fisies","en":"(a) physical (b) chemical (c) biological – cross-contamination (d) biological (e) physical"}},{"title":{"af":"Gevallestudie: watter bakterie?","en":"Case study: which bacterium?"},"problem":{"af":"> 'n Spysenier maak die dag voor 'n troue op Hartbeespoort 'n groot pot beesvleiskerrie. Sy laat die pot oornag op die stoof afkoel en verhit dit die volgende middag weer. Die aand kry baie gaste maagkrampe en diarree.\n\n(a) Watter bakterie is heel waarskynlik verantwoordelik?\n(b) Verduidelik waarom.\n(c) Hoe moes die spysenier dit voorkom het?","en":"> A caterer makes a large pot of beef curry the day before a wedding in Hartbeespoort. She leaves the pot to cool overnight on the stove and reheats it the next afternoon. That evening many guests get stomach cramps and diarrhoea.\n\n(a) Which bacterium is most likely responsible?\n(b) Explain why.\n(c) How should the caterer have prevented it?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Clostridium perfringens**.","en":"(a) **Clostridium perfringens**."},{"af":"(b) Dit is 'n **groot vleisgereg** wat **stadig afgekoel** het. Die kerrie was urelank in die gevaarsone (5–60 °C). *C. perfringens* se spore oorleef kook, en tydens die stadige afkoeling het die bakterieë baie vinnig vermeerder.","en":"(b) It is a **large meat dish** that **cooled slowly**. The curry was in the danger zone (5–60 °C) for hours. *C. perfringens* spores survive cooking, and during the slow cooling the bacteria multiplied very quickly."},{"af":"(c) Verdeel die kerrie in **vlak houers** sodat dit **vinnig afkoel**, sit dit dan in die yskas (onder 5 °C) en herverhit dit die volgende dag **deeglik** (kern minstens 75 °C).","en":"(c) Divide the curry into **shallow containers** so that it **cools quickly**, then put it in the refrigerator (below 5 °C) and reheat it **thoroughly** the next day (core at least 75 °C)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Clostridium perfringens (b) groot vleisgereg wat stadig afgekoel het (c) vinnig afkoel in vlak houers, verkoel, deeglik herverhit","en":"(a) Clostridium perfringens (b) large meat dish that cooled slowly (c) cool quickly in shallow containers, refrigerate, reheat thoroughly"}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken bakteriegroei","en":"Calculate bacterial growth"},"problem":{"af":"'n Stuk rou hoender met **10 bakterieë** daarop lê **3 uur** lank op die toonbank in 'n warm kombuis (25 °C). Die bakterieë verdubbel elke 20 minute. Hoeveel bakterieë is daar ná 3 uur?","en":"A piece of raw chicken with **10 bacteria** on it lies on the counter in a warm kitchen (25 °C) for **3 hours**. The bacteria double every 20 minutes. How many bacteria are there after 3 hours?"},"steps":[{"af":"25 °C is in die gevaarsone, so die bakterieë groei vinnig.","en":"25 °C is in the danger zone, so the bacteria grow quickly."},{"af":"Aantal verdubbelings: 3 uur = 180 minute; 180 ÷ 20 = **9 verdubbelings**.","en":"Number of doublings: 3 hours = 180 minutes; 180 ÷ 20 = **9 doublings**."},{"af":"Getal = begingetal × 2^{9} = 10 × 512","en":"Number = starting number × 2^{9} = 10 × 512"},{"af":"= **5 120 bakterieë** – meer as 500 keer soveel. Daarom ontdooi en bêre ons hoender in die yskas.","en":"= **5 120 bacteria** – more than 500 times as many. That is why we thaw and store chicken in the refrigerator."}],"answer":{"af":"5 120 bakterieë","en":"5 120 bacteria"}},{"title":{"af":"Pas HACCP toe op gebraaide hoender","en":"Apply HACCP to roast chicken"},"problem":{"af":"'n Lodge in die Magaliesberg bedien gebraaide hoender op 'n buffet. Gebruik HACCP-beginsels 2 tot 7 vir die kookstap.","en":"A lodge in the Magaliesberg serves roast chicken on a buffet. Use HACCP principles 2 to 7 for the cooking step."},"steps":[{"af":"**KBP (beginsel 2):** die kookstap, want dit is die stap waar *Salmonella* in die hoender doodgemaak word.","en":"**CCP (principle 2):** the cooking step, because it is the step where *Salmonella* in the chicken is killed."},{"af":"**Kritieke perk (3):** 'n kerntemperatuur van **minstens 75 °C**.","en":"**Critical limit (3):** a core temperature of **at least 75 °C**."},{"af":"**Monitering (4):** steek 'n skoon sondetermometer in die dikste deel van elke groep hoender.","en":"**Monitoring (4):** insert a clean probe thermometer into the thickest part of each batch of chicken."},{"af":"**Regstellende aksie (5):** as dit onder 75 °C is, kook langer en meet weer. **Verifikasie (6):** die bestuurder toets gereeld of die termometer akkuraat is.","en":"**Corrective action (5):** if it is below 75 °C, cook longer and measure again. **Verification (6):** the manager regularly tests whether the thermometer is accurate."},{"af":"**Rekords (7):** skryf die tyd, temperatuur en enige aksie in die logboek en teken dit.","en":"**Records (7):** write the time, temperature and any action in the log book and sign it."}],"answer":{"af":"KBP = kook; perk = kern ≥ 75 °C; moniteer met 'n sondetermometer; kook langer indien te laag; verifieer die termometer; hou rekords","en":"CCP = cooking; limit = core ≥ 75 °C; monitor with a probe thermometer; cook longer if too low; verify the thermometer; keep records"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van fisiese besmetting?","en":"Which one is an example of physical contamination?"},"options":[{"af":"Salmonella op rou hoender","en":"Salmonella on raw chicken"},{"af":"Bleikmiddel op 'n snyplank","en":"Bleach on a cutting board"},{"af":"'n Haar in die sop","en":"A hair in the soup"},{"af":"Skimmel op brood","en":"Mould on bread"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Fisiese besmetting is 'n voorwerp in die kos, soos 'n haar, glas of 'n pleister. Salmonella en skimmel is biologies; bleikmiddel is chemies.","en":"Physical contamination is an object in the food, such as a hair, glass or a plaster. Salmonella and mould are biological; bleach is chemical."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kos moet tot 'n kerntemperatuur van minstens ___ °C gaargemaak word.","en":"Food must be cooked to a core temperature of at least ___ °C."},"answers":{"af":["75"],"en":["75"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Kerntemperatuur van minstens 75 °C maak die meeste skadelike bakterieë dood. Meet dit met 'n sondetermometer in die dikste deel.","en":"A core temperature of at least 75 °C kills most harmful bacteria. Measure it with a probe thermometer in the thickest part."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["60","50","100"],"en":["60","50","100"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In ideale toestande kan bakterieë ongeveer elke 20 minute verdubbel.","en":"In ideal conditions bacteria can double about every 20 minutes."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Daarom word een bakterie ná net 3 uur in die gevaarsone al 512 bakterieë.","en":"True. That is why one bacterium becomes 512 bacteria after only 3 hours in the danger zone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor staan HACCP?","en":"What does HACCP stand for?"},"options":[{"af":"Gevaarontleding en kritieke beheerpunte","en":"Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points"},{"af":"Higiëne-assessering en kombuisbeheerpunte","en":"Hygiene Assessment and Cooking Control Points"},{"af":"Hoërisiko-ontleding en chemiese beheerprosedures","en":"High-risk Analysis and Chemical Control Procedures"},{"af":"Gesondheidsoudit en kritieke kookprosedures","en":"Health Audit and Critical Cooking Procedures"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"HACCP = Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (gevaarontleding en kritieke beheerpunte) – 'n voorkomende voedselveiligheidstelsel.","en":"HACCP = Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points – a preventive food-safety system."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die gevaarsone begin by ___ °C.","en":"The danger zone starts at ___ °C."},"answers":{"af":["5"],"en":["5"]},"explain":{"af":"Die gevaarsone begin by 5 °C. Daarom moet 'n yskas onder 5 °C (1–4 °C) wees.","en":"The danger zone starts at 5 °C. That is why a refrigerator must be below 5 °C (1–4 °C)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["0","10","−18"],"en":["0","10","−18"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is 'n hoërisiko-voedsel?","en":"Which of the following is a high-risk food?"},"options":[{"af":"Suiker","en":"Sugar"},{"af":"Gekookte rys","en":"Cooked rice"},{"af":"Ongekookte rys","en":"Uncooked rice"},{"af":"Beskuit","en":"Rusks"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gekookte rys is klam en bakterieë (bv. Bacillus cereus) groei maklik daarin. Ongekookte rys, suiker en beskuit is droog, dus nie hoërisiko nie.","en":"Cooked rice is moist and bacteria (e.g. Bacillus cereus) grow easily in it. Uncooked rice, sugar and rusks are dry, so not high-risk."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer bakterieë van rou kos na gaar kos oorgedra word, bv. met 'n mes of snyplank, word dit ___ genoem.","en":"When bacteria are transferred from raw food to cooked food, e.g. by a knife or cutting board, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["kruisbesmetting","kruis-besmetting"],"en":["cross-contamination","cross contamination","crosscontamination"]},"explain":{"af":"Kruisbesmetting is die oordrag van rou na gaar. Voedselvergiftiging is die siekte wat daarna kan volg.","en":"Cross-contamination is the transfer from raw to cooked. Food poisoning is the illness that can follow."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["voedselvergiftiging","fermentasie","bederf"],"en":["food poisoning","fermentation","spoilage"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Listeria kan nie in 'n yskas groei nie.","en":"Listeria cannot grow in a refrigerator."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Listeria is gevaarlik juis omdat dit selfs by yskastemperature stadig groei. Daarom moet gereed-om-te-eet vleis soos polonie binne die vervaldatum gebruik word.","en":"False. Listeria is dangerous precisely because it grows slowly even at refrigerator temperatures. That is why ready-to-eat meat such as polony must be used within the expiry date."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke bakterie by sy tipiese bron.","en":"Match each bacterium to its typical source."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Salmonella","en":"Salmonella"},"r":{"af":"Rou pluimvee en eiers","en":"Raw poultry and eggs"}},{"l":{"af":"Staphylococcus aureus","en":"Staphylococcus aureus"},"r":{"af":"Die mens se neus, keel, snye en sere","en":"The human nose, throat, cuts and sores"}},{"l":{"af":"Clostridium botulinum","en":"Clostridium botulinum"},"r":{"af":"Sleg ingemaakte kos en opgeswelde blikke","en":"Badly canned food and bulging tins"}},{"l":{"af":"Bacillus cereus","en":"Bacillus cereus"},"r":{"af":"Gekookte rys wat lank warm gehou word","en":"Cooked rice kept warm for a long time"}},{"l":{"af":"Listeria","en":"Listeria"},"r":{"af":"Gereed-om-te-eet verwerkte vleis en sagte kaas","en":"Ready-to-eat processed meats and soft cheese"}}],"explain":{"af":"Salmonella – pluimvee en eiers; Staph. aureus – die mens self; C. botulinum – blikkieskos sonder suurstof; B. cereus – rys; Listeria – polonie en sagte kaas.","en":"Salmonella – poultry and eggs; Staph. aureus – the human body; C. botulinum – canned food without oxygen; B. cereus – rice; Listeria – polony and soft cheese."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ingelegde uie in asyn hou baie lank goed. Watter FATTOM-faktor verklaar dit die beste?","en":"Pickled onions in vinegar keep for a very long time. Which FATTOM factor explains this best?"},"options":[{"af":"Tyd","en":"Time"},{"af":"Suurstof","en":"Oxygen"},{"af":"Vog","en":"Moisture"},{"af":"Suurgehalte","en":"Acidity"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Asyn maak die kos baie suur, en bakterieë groei swak in suur kos. Pasop: die A in FATTOM is suurgehalte (acidity), nie suurstof nie.","en":"Vinegar makes the food very acidic, and bacteria grow poorly in acidic food. Careful: the A in FATTOM is acidity, not oxygen."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die veiligste manier om 'n groot pot warm bredie af te koel?","en":"What is the safest way to cool a large pot of hot stew?"},"options":[{"af":"Verdeel dit in vlak houers, koel dit vinnig af en sit dit dan in die yskas","en":"Divide it into shallow containers, cool it quickly and then put it in the refrigerator"},{"af":"Los dit oornag op die stoof sodat dit stadig afkoel","en":"Leave it on the stove overnight so that it cools slowly"},{"af":"Sit die deksel op en los dit tot die volgende dag in die afgeskakelde oond","en":"Put the lid on and leave it in the switched-off oven until the next day"},{"af":"Los dit op die toonbank totdat dit heeltemal koud is, al neem dit die hele middag","en":"Leave it on the counter until it is completely cold, even if it takes all afternoon"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vlak houers laat die hitte vinnig ontsnap, so die bredie spandeer min tyd in die gevaarsone. Stadige afkoeling in 'n groot pot is presies hoe Clostridium perfringens-uitbrekings gebeur.","en":"Shallow containers let the heat escape quickly, so the stew spends little time in the danger zone. Slow cooling in a large pot is exactly how Clostridium perfringens outbreaks happen."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Stuk hoender het 50 bakterieë en lê 2 uur lank by kamertemperatuur. As die bakterieë elke 20 minute verdubbel, is daar ná 2 uur ___ bakterieë.","en":"A piece of chicken has 50 bacteria and lies at room temperature for 2 hours. If the bacteria double every 20 minutes, there are ___ bacteria after 2 hours."},"answers":{"af":["3200","3 200"],"en":["3200","3 200"]},"explain":{"af":"2 uur = 120 min; 120 ÷ 20 = 6 verdubbelings. 50 × 2⁶ = 50 × 64 = 3 200. (300 is 50 × 6 – vermenigvuldig nie met die aantal verdubbelings nie!)","en":"2 hours = 120 min; 120 ÷ 20 = 6 doublings. 50 × 2⁶ = 50 × 64 = 3 200. (300 is 50 × 6 – do not multiply by the number of doublings!)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["300","600","6 400"],"en":["300","600","6 400"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gaste by 'n ontbytbuffet word binne 'n paar uur siek ná hulle eiermayonnaise-toebroodjies geëet het. Die kok wat dit gemaak het, het 'n etterende sweer aan sy hand gehad. Watter bakterie is heel waarskynlik die oorsaak?","en":"Guests at a breakfast buffet get sick within a few hours after eating egg-mayonnaise sandwiches. The cook who made them had a festering boil on his hand. Which bacterium is most likely the cause?"},"options":[{"af":"Clostridium botulinum","en":"Clostridium botulinum"},{"af":"Listeria","en":"Listeria"},{"af":"Bacillus cereus","en":"Bacillus cereus"},{"af":"Staphylococcus aureus","en":"Staphylococcus aureus"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Staphylococcus aureus kom van die mens se neus, keel, snye en sere (soos 'n sweer). Dit word deur hande na kos oorgedra wat nie weer gekook word nie, soos toebroodjies.","en":"Staphylococcus aureus comes from the human nose, throat, cuts and sores (such as a boil). It is transferred by hands to food that is not cooked again, such as sandwiches."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Sjef meet elke uur die temperatuur van die kos in die bain-marie. Hierdie HACCP-beginsel heet ___.","en":"A chef measures the temperature of the food in the bain-marie every hour. This HACCP principle is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["monitering","moniteer","monitor"],"en":["monitoring","monitor"]},"explain":{"af":"Gereelde meting om te kyk of die kritieke perk gehaal word, is monitering (beginsel 4). Verifikasie (beginsel 6) toets of die hele stelsel werk, bv. of die termometer akkuraat is.","en":"Regular measuring to check whether the critical limit is met is monitoring (principle 4). Verification (principle 6) tests whether the whole system works, e.g. whether the thermometer is accurate."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verifikasie","rekordhouding","gevaarontleding"],"en":["verification","record keeping","hazard analysis"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n HACCP-plan vir gebraaide hoender is die kookstap die kritieke beheerpunt. Wat is die kritieke perk?","en":"In a HACCP plan for roast chicken the cooking step is the critical control point. What is the critical limit?"},"options":[{"af":"Meet die temperatuur met 'n sondetermometer","en":"Measure the temperature with a probe thermometer"},{"af":"Kook die hoender langer as die temperatuur te laag is","en":"Cook the chicken longer if the temperature is too low"},{"af":"'n Kerntemperatuur van minstens 75 °C","en":"A core temperature of at least 75 °C"},{"af":"Skryf die temperatuur in 'n logboek","en":"Write the temperature in a log book"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die kritieke perk is die meetbare grens wat gehaal moet word: kern minstens 75 °C. Meet is monitering, langer kook is regstellende aksie en die logboek is rekordhouding.","en":"The critical limit is the measurable boundary that must be met: core at least 75 °C. Measuring is monitoring, cooking longer is corrective action and the log book is record keeping."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi sê: \"As ek die bredie wat oornag op die stoof gestaan het net weer goed warm maak, is dit heeltemal veilig.\" Watter evaluering is korrek?","en":"Thandi says: \"If I just heat up the stew that stood on the stove overnight really well, it is completely safe.\" Which evaluation is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy is reg – hitte maak alle bakterieë en hul gifstowwe dood","en":"She is right – heat kills all bacteria and their toxins"},{"af":"Sy is verkeerd – sommige bakterieë vorm spore of gifstowwe wat herverhitting oorleef, so kos mag nie lank in die gevaarsone staan nie","en":"She is wrong – some bacteria form spores or toxins that survive reheating, so food may not stand in the danger zone for long"},{"af":"Sy is reg, solank sy die bredie daarna in die yskas sit","en":"She is right, as long as she puts the stew in the refrigerator afterwards"},{"af":"Sy is reg, want gaar vleis kan glad nie bederf nie","en":"She is right, because cooked meat cannot spoil at all"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Herverhitting maak baie bakterieë dood, maar nie almal se gevolge nie: die gifstowwe van Staphylococcus aureus en Bacillus cereus word nie deur hitte vernietig nie, en Clostridium perfringens se spore oorleef kook. Die veilige oplossing is om tyd in die gevaarsone te beperk deur vinnig af te koel.","en":"Reheating kills many bacteria, but not all their effects: the toxins of Staphylococcus aureus and Bacillus cereus are not destroyed by heat, and Clostridium perfringens spores survive cooking. The safe solution is to limit time in the danger zone by cooling quickly."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-kombuistoerusting","title":{"af":"Kombuistoerusting, gereedskap en kombuisuitleg","en":"Kitchen equipment, utensils and kitchen layout"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal groot, meganiese en warmhou-toerusting en klein gereedskap kan identifiseer en gebruik, messe veilig kan hanteer, die basiese snitte kan beskryf en 'n goeie kombuisuitleg en werkvloei kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to identify and use large, mechanical and hot-holding equipment and small utensils, handle knives safely, describe the basic cuts and explain a good kitchen layout and work flow."},"summary":{"af":"## Groot toerusting\n\n| Toerusting | Gebruik en kenmerke |\n|---|---|\n| Gas-, elektriese en induksiestowe | 'n Induksiestoof verhit die pan self met 'n magnetiese veld – dit werk net met **magnetiese panne** (bv. gietyster) |\n| Konvensionele oond | Hitte van elemente of vlamme; bo in die oond is dit warmer as onder |\n| Konveksie-oond (waaieroond) | 'n Waaier blaas die warm lug rond: kos gaar **vinniger en egaliger** |\n| Kombi-stoomoond | Kombineer droë hitte en stoom, sodat kos sappig bly |\n| Mikrogolfoond | Vinnige verhitting en ontdooiing; geen metaal nie |\n| Salamander | Oorhoofse rooster om bo-op te verbruin of te gratineer (*au gratin*) |\n| Bakplaat (griddle) | Plat, warm plaat vir eiers, pannekoek en hamburgers |\n| Diepvetbraaier | Kos word in warm olie gaargemaak; termostaat ongeveer 160–190 °C |\n| Kantelbraaipan (bratt pan) | Groot pan wat kan braai, smoor, prut en kook, en kantel om leeg te maak |\n| Yskaste, inloopkoelkamer, vrieskaste | Koel en bevrore berging |\n| Skottelgoedwasser | Was en spoel teen hoë temperature |\n\n**Meganiese toerusting:** die **voedselmenger** het drie aanhegsels – die **garde** (klop room en eierwitte), die **klopper/spaan** (room botter en suiker, meng beslag) en die **deeghaak** (knie brooddeeg). Ook die **voedselverwerker** (kap, sny, rasper), **versapper** (maak sop en smoothies glad), **snymasjien** (eweredige skywe vleis of kaas) en **maalmasjien** (maal vleis).\n\n**Warmhou-toerusting:** in 'n **bain-marie** staan houers met kos in warm water; 'n **chafing dish** hou kos warm op 'n buffet en word met brandstofgel of 'n elektriese element verhit; verder die **warmkas/warmplaat**, **hittelampe** en die **sopketel**.\n\n## Klein toerusting en gereedskap\n\n**Messe:** sjefsmes (kap en sny), skilmes (klein, vir skil en fyn werk), gekartelde broodmes, ontbeningsmes, buigsame fileermes (vis), voorsnymes (gaar vleis), paletmes (versprei en glad stryk) en die slypstaal (hou die lem skerp).\n\n**Gereedskap:** skiller, rasper, garde, spatels, visspaan/eierspaan, opskeplepel, gaatjieslepel, knyptang, sif, **chinois** (fyn keëlvormige sif vir souse), vergiettes (dreineer pasta en groente), maatkoppies en -lepels, skaal, **steekpentermometer** (meet die kerntemperatuur van kos), spuitsak, deegroller en uitdrukkers.\n\n**Kookgerei:** kastrolle, voorraadpot (hoog, vir aftreksel), braaipan, sauteuse (skuins kante, vir roerbraai en souse), wok, oondpan, bakplate, muffinpanne en **gastronorm-houers** (standaardgroottes wat in oonde, yskaste en bain-maries pas).\n\n| Materiaal | Voordele | Nadele |\n|---|---|---|\n| Vlekvrye staal | Sterk, roes nie, reageer nie met kos nie | Gelei hitte swak, tensy dit 'n koper- of aluminiumbasis het |\n| Aluminium | Lig, goedkoop, gelei hitte goed | Duik maklik; reageer met suur kos |\n| Gietyster | Hou hitte goed, egalige hitte, werk op induksie | Baie swaar; roes as dit nie gedroog en geolie word nie |\n| Koper | Beste geleier van hitte | Duur, moet gepoleer word, het 'n voering nodig |\n| Kleefvry | Min vet nodig, maklik om skoon te maak | Krap maklik; gebruik hout of silikoon, nie baie hoë hitte nie |\n\n## Messeveiligheid en basiese snitte\n\n- Gebruik die **klouvanggreep**: vingerpunte ingevou, kneukels lei die mes.\n- Sit 'n **klam lap** onder die snyplank sodat dit nie gly nie.\n- Dra 'n mes met die **punt na onder**, langs jou sy.\n- Moet **nooit** 'n vallende mes probeer vang nie – staan terug.\n- Was messe **apart**; los dit nooit in 'n wasbak vol seepwater nie.\n\n| Snit | Beskrywing |\n|---|---|\n| Julienne | Dun vuurhoutjiestrokies |\n| Batonnet/jardinière | Stafies (dikker as julienne) |\n| Brunoise | Baie fyn blokkies (ongeveer 2–3 mm) |\n| Macédoine | Medium blokkies (ongeveer 5 mm) |\n| Paysanne | Dun skyfies |\n| Chiffonade | Fyn gekerfde blare (bv. basiliekruid, spinasie) |\n| Concassé | Grof gekap (bv. geskilde tamatie) |\n\n## Groot toerusting skoonmaak\n\n1. Skakel af en trek die prop uit (of isoleer die krag of gas).\n2. Laat dit afkoel.\n3. Haal verwyderbare dele uit.\n4. Skraap kosreste af.\n5. Was met warm seepwater of 'n ontvetter.\n6. Spoel af.\n7. Ontsmet.\n8. Droog en sit weer aanmekaar.\n\nVolg altyd die vervaardiger se instruksies. By 'n diepvetbraaier filtreer jy die olie gereeld en vervang dit wanneer dit donker word, rook of sleg ruik.\n\n## Kombuisuitleg en werkvloei\n\n**Eenrigting-werkvloei:** ontvangs → berging → voorbereiding → kook → opdiening → opwas. Kos beweeg net vorentoe, sodat rou en gaar kos, en skoon en vuil items, nie kruis nie – dit voorkom **kruisbesmetting**.\n\n- **Werksentrums:** aparte areas vir spesifieke take (bv. groente, gebak, opwas).\n- **Werksdriehoek:** stoof–wasbak–yskas; kort afstande spaar tyd en energie.\n- **Basiese uitlegte:** reguit lyn (teen een muur), parallel/gang (twee rye oorkant mekaar), L-vorm, U-vorm en eiland.\n- **Ontwerp:** nie-gly, afwasbare vloere; ligkleurige, afwasbare mure; goeie beligting; ventilasie met 'n afsuigkap; 'n aparte handewasbak.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders verwar die **salamander** (verbruin van bo) met die **bain-marie** (hou kos warm in water). Leer elke toestel saam met sy gebruik.","en":"## Large equipment\n\n| Equipment | Use and features |\n|---|---|\n| Gas, electric and induction stoves | An induction stove heats the pan itself with a magnetic field – it only works with **magnetic pans** (e.g. cast iron) |\n| Conventional oven | Heat from elements or flames; the top of the oven is hotter than the bottom |\n| Convection oven (fan oven) | A fan circulates the hot air: food cooks **faster and more evenly** |\n| Combi-steam oven | Combines dry heat and steam so food stays moist |\n| Microwave oven | Fast heating and defrosting; no metal |\n| Salamander | Overhead grill for browning or gratinating the top (*au gratin*) |\n| Griddle | Flat, hot plate for eggs, pancakes and burgers |\n| Deep-fat fryer | Food is cooked in hot oil; thermostat about 160–190 °C |\n| Bratt pan | Large pan that can fry, braise, stew and boil, and tilts to empty |\n| Refrigerators, walk-in cold room, freezers | Cold and frozen storage |\n| Dishwasher | Washes and rinses at high temperatures |\n\n**Mechanical equipment:** the **food mixer** has three attachments – the **whisk** (whips cream and egg whites), the **beater/paddle** (creams butter and sugar, mixes batter) and the **dough hook** (kneads bread dough). Also the **food processor** (chops, slices, grates), **blender/liquidiser** (makes soup and smoothies smooth), **slicer** (even slices of meat or cheese) and **mincer** (minces meat).\n\n**Hot-holding equipment:** in a **bain-marie** containers of food stand in hot water; a **chafing dish** keeps food warm on a buffet and is heated by gel fuel or an electric element; also the **hot cupboard/hot plate**, **heat lamps** and the **soup kettle**.\n\n## Small equipment and utensils\n\n**Knives:** chef's knife (chopping and slicing), paring knife (small, for peeling and fine work), serrated bread knife, boning knife, flexible filleting knife (fish), carving knife (cooked meat), palette knife (spreading and smoothing) and the sharpening steel (keeps the edge sharp).\n\n**Utensils:** peeler, grater, whisk, spatulas, fish slice/egg lifter, ladle, slotted spoon, tongs, sieve, **chinois** (fine cone-shaped sieve for sauces), colander (drains pasta and vegetables), measuring cups and spoons, scale, **probe thermometer** (measures the core temperature of food), piping bag, rolling pin and cutters.\n\n**Cookware:** saucepans, stockpot (tall, for stock), frying pan, sauteuse (sloping sides, for tossing and sauces), wok, roasting tin, baking trays, muffin pans and **gastronorm containers** (standard sizes that fit ovens, fridges and bain-maries).\n\n| Material | Advantages | Disadvantages |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stainless steel | Strong, does not rust, does not react with food | Conducts heat poorly unless it has a copper or aluminium base |\n| Aluminium | Light, cheap, conducts heat well | Dents easily; reacts with acidic food |\n| Cast iron | Holds heat well, even heat, works on induction | Very heavy; rusts if not dried and oiled |\n| Copper | Best conductor of heat | Expensive, must be polished, needs a lining |\n| Non-stick | Little fat needed, easy to clean | Scratches easily; use wood or silicone, not very high heat |\n\n## Knife safety and basic cuts\n\n- Use the **claw grip**: fingertips tucked in, knuckles guide the knife.\n- Put a **damp cloth** under the cutting board so it does not slip.\n- Carry a knife with the **point down**, at your side.\n- **Never** try to catch a falling knife – step back.\n- Wash knives **separately**; never leave them in a sink full of soapy water.\n\n| Cut | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Julienne | Thin matchstick strips |\n| Batonnet/jardinière | Batons (thicker than julienne) |\n| Brunoise | Very fine dice (about 2–3 mm) |\n| Macédoine | Medium dice (about 5 mm) |\n| Paysanne | Thin slices |\n| Chiffonade | Finely shredded leaves (e.g. basil, spinach) |\n| Concassé | Roughly chopped (e.g. peeled tomato) |\n\n## Cleaning large equipment\n\n1. Switch off and unplug (or isolate the power or gas).\n2. Let it cool down.\n3. Remove the removable parts.\n4. Scrape off food remains.\n5. Wash with hot soapy water or a degreaser.\n6. Rinse.\n7. Sanitise.\n8. Dry and reassemble.\n\nAlways follow the manufacturer's instructions. For a deep-fat fryer, filter the oil regularly and replace it when it becomes dark, smokes or smells bad.\n\n## Kitchen layout and work flow\n\n**One-direction work flow:** receiving → storage → preparation → cooking → service → washing up. Food only moves forward, so raw and cooked food, and clean and dirty items, do not cross – this prevents **cross-contamination**.\n\n- **Work centres:** separate areas for specific tasks (e.g. vegetables, pastry, washing up).\n- **Work triangle:** stove–sink–fridge; short distances save time and energy.\n- **Basic layouts:** straight line (against one wall), parallel/galley (two rows opposite each other), L-shape, U-shape and island.\n- **Design:** non-slip, washable floors; light-coloured, washable walls; good lighting; ventilation with an extractor hood; a separate hand-wash basin.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners confuse the **salamander** (browns from above) with the **bain-marie** (keeps food warm in water). Learn each piece of equipment together with its use."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Induksiestoof","en":"Induction stove"},"def":{"af":"'n Stoof wat die pan self met 'n magnetiese veld verhit; dit werk net met panne met 'n magnetiese basis.","en":"A stove that heats the pan itself with a magnetic field; it only works with pans that have a magnetic base."}},{"term":{"af":"Konveksie-oond","en":"Convection oven"},"def":{"af":"'n Oond met 'n waaier wat warm lug rondblaas, sodat kos vinniger en egaliger gaar word.","en":"An oven with a fan that circulates hot air so food cooks faster and more evenly."}},{"term":{"af":"Salamander","en":"Salamander"},"def":{"af":"'n Oorhoofse rooster wat gebruik word om geregte bo-op te verbruin of te gratineer.","en":"An overhead grill used to brown or gratinate the top of dishes."}},{"term":{"af":"Bain-marie","en":"Bain-marie"},"def":{"af":"Warmhou-toerusting waarin houers met kos in warm water staan.","en":"Hot-holding equipment in which containers of food stand in hot water."}},{"term":{"af":"Chinois","en":"Chinois"},"def":{"af":"'n Fyn, keëlvormige sif wat gebruik word om souse en sop glad te sif.","en":"A fine, cone-shaped sieve used to strain sauces and soups smooth."}},{"term":{"af":"Gastronorm-houer","en":"Gastronorm container"},"def":{"af":"'n Houer in 'n standaardgrootte wat in oonde, yskaste en bain-maries pas.","en":"A container in a standard size that fits ovens, fridges and bain-maries."}},{"term":{"af":"Klouvanggreep","en":"Claw grip"},"def":{"af":"Om kos met ingevoude vingerpunte vas te hou sodat die kneukels die mes lei en jy jou nie sny nie.","en":"Holding food with fingertips tucked in so the knuckles guide the knife and you don't cut yourself."}},{"term":{"af":"Brunoise","en":"Brunoise"},"def":{"af":"'n Snit waar groente in baie fyn blokkies (ongeveer 2–3 mm) gesny word.","en":"A cut in which vegetables are cut into very fine dice (about 2–3 mm)."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenrigting-werkvloei","en":"One-direction work flow"},"def":{"af":"Die uitleg waar kos net vorentoe beweeg (ontvangs → berging → voorbereiding → kook → opdiening → opwas) om kruisbesmetting te voorkom.","en":"The layout in which food only moves forward (receiving → storage → preparation → cooking → service → washing up) to prevent cross-contamination."}},{"term":{"af":"Werksdriehoek","en":"Work triangle"},"def":{"af":"Die denkbeeldige driehoek tussen die stoof, die wasbak en die yskas; kort afstande spaar tyd en energie.","en":"The imaginary triangle between the stove, the sink and the fridge; short distances save time and energy."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die toerusting","en":"Identify the equipment"},"problem":{"af":"Identifiseer die toerusting en noem waarvoor dit gebruik word:\n\n(a) 'n Rooster wat hoog teen die muur bo die stoof hang en van bo af hitte gee.\n(b) 'n Bak warm water waarin metaalhouers met kos staan.\n(c) 'n Fyn, keëlvormige sif met 'n handvatsel.","en":"Identify the equipment and state what it is used for:\n\n(a) A grill that hangs high on the wall above the stove and gives heat from above.\n(b) A tray of hot water in which metal containers of food stand.\n(c) A fine, cone-shaped sieve with a handle."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Hitte van bo = **salamander**. Gebruik: om die bokant van geregte te verbruin of te gratineer, bv. 'n groente-au gratin.","en":"(a) Heat from above = **salamander**. Use: to brown or gratinate the top of dishes, e.g. a vegetable au gratin."},{"af":"(b) Houers in warm water = **bain-marie**. Gebruik: om kos warm te hou totdat dit opgedien word, bv. souse en groente op die opdienlyn.","en":"(b) Containers in hot water = **bain-marie**. Use: to keep food warm until it is served, e.g. sauces and vegetables on the service line."},{"af":"(c) Fyn keëlvormige sif = **chinois**. Gebruik: om souse en sop baie glad te sif.","en":"(c) Fine cone-shaped sieve = **chinois**. Use: to strain sauces and soups very smooth."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Salamander – verbruin bo-op  (b) Bain-marie – hou kos warm  (c) Chinois – sif souse glad","en":"(a) Salamander – browns the top  (b) Bain-marie – keeps food warm  (c) Chinois – strains sauces smooth"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak 'n snymasjien skoon","en":"Clean a slicer"},"problem":{"af":"Die kok het die middag ham op die snymasjien gesny. Beskryf in die regte volgorde hoe hy dit veilig en higiënies moet skoonmaak.","en":"The cook sliced ham on the slicer during the afternoon. Describe in the correct order how he must clean it safely and hygienically."},"steps":[{"af":"Veiligheid eerste: skakel die masjien af en **trek die prop uit**, sodat die lem nie per ongeluk kan begin draai nie.","en":"Safety first: switch the machine off and **unplug it**, so the blade cannot start turning by accident."},{"af":"Haal die verwyderbare dele (bv. die skuiwer en die lemskerm) volgens die vervaardiger se instruksies uit en skraap vleisreste versigtig af – weg van die lem af.","en":"Remove the removable parts (e.g. the carriage and blade guard) according to the manufacturer's instructions and carefully scrape off meat remains – away from the blade."},{"af":"Was alle dele met warm seepwater of 'n ontvetter en spoel af.","en":"Wash all parts with hot soapy water or a degreaser and rinse."},{"af":"Ontsmet die dele en die masjien, want dit het met rou of gaar vleis in aanraking gekom.","en":"Sanitise the parts and the machine, because they were in contact with raw or cooked meat."},{"af":"Laat alles droog word, sit die masjien weer aanmekaar en maak seker die lemskerm is op sy plek voordat iemand dit weer gebruik.","en":"Let everything dry, reassemble the machine and make sure the blade guard is in place before anyone uses it again."}],"answer":{"af":"Skakel af en trek prop uit → haal dele uit en skraap → was → spoel → ontsmet → droog → sit aanmekaar.","en":"Switch off and unplug → remove parts and scrape → wash → rinse → sanitise → dry → reassemble."}},{"title":{"af":"Basiese snitte in 'n resep","en":"Basic cuts in a recipe"},"problem":{"af":"'n Resep vir 'n groentesop vra: wortels *julienne*, uie *brunoise*, spinasie *chiffonade* en tamaties *concassé*. Verduidelik hoe jy elke groente sny.","en":"A recipe for a vegetable soup asks for: carrots *julienne*, onions *brunoise*, spinach *chiffonade* and tomatoes *concassé*. Explain how you cut each vegetable."},"steps":[{"af":"**Julienne** (wortels): sny dun skywe en sny dit dan in dun vuurhoutjiestrokies.","en":"**Julienne** (carrots): cut thin slices and then cut them into thin matchstick strips."},{"af":"**Brunoise** (uie): sny die strokies dwars in baie fyn blokkies van ongeveer 2–3 mm.","en":"**Brunoise** (onions): cut the strips across into very fine dice of about 2–3 mm."},{"af":"**Chiffonade** (spinasie): pak die blare op mekaar, rol dit styf op en kerf dit in fyn repies.","en":"**Chiffonade** (spinach): stack the leaves, roll them up tightly and shred them into fine ribbons."},{"af":"**Concassé** (tamaties): skil die tamaties, haal die pitte uit en kap die vleis grof.","en":"**Concassé** (tomatoes): peel the tomatoes, remove the seeds and chop the flesh roughly."},{"af":"Gebruik deurentyd die klouvanggreep en 'n klam lap onder die snyplank.","en":"Use the claw grip throughout and a damp cloth under the cutting board."}],"answer":{"af":"Julienne = vuurhoutjiestrokies; brunoise = baie fyn blokkies; chiffonade = fyn gekerfde blare; concassé = grof gekap.","en":"Julienne = matchstick strips; brunoise = very fine dice; chiffonade = finely shredded leaves; concassé = roughly chopped."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die werkvloei","en":"Improve the work flow"},"problem":{"af":"In 'n skoolkombuis in Brits word vuil borde uit die eetsaal deur die slaaivoorbereidingsarea na die opwasarea gedra. Rou hoender word naby die gaar kos uitgepak. Identifiseer die probleem en stel 'n beter werkvloei voor.","en":"In a school kitchen in Brits dirty plates from the dining hall are carried through the salad preparation area to the washing-up area. Raw chicken is unpacked next to the cooked food. Identify the problem and suggest a better work flow."},"steps":[{"af":"Probleem: vuil en skoon items, en rou en gaar kos, kruis mekaar se paaie. Dit veroorsaak **kruisbesmetting** – bakterieë van vuil borde of rou hoender kan op die slaai of gaar kos beland.","en":"Problem: dirty and clean items, and raw and cooked food, cross each other's paths. This causes **cross-contamination** – bacteria from dirty plates or raw chicken can end up on the salad or cooked food."},{"af":"Oplossing: rangskik die kombuis volgens die **eenrigting-werkvloei**: ontvangs → berging → voorbereiding → kook → opdiening → opwas.","en":"Solution: arrange the kitchen according to the **one-direction work flow**: receiving → storage → preparation → cooking → service → washing up."},{"af":"Skuif die opwasarea naby die eetsaal se deur, sodat vuil borde nooit deur die voorbereidingsarea gaan nie.","en":"Move the washing-up area close to the dining-hall door, so dirty plates never pass through the preparation area."},{"af":"Pak rou hoender by die ontvangsarea uit en berg dit dadelik onder in die yskas; berei rou vleis in 'n aparte werksentrum voor, weg van gaar kos.","en":"Unpack raw chicken at the receiving area and store it immediately at the bottom of the fridge; prepare raw meat in a separate work centre, away from cooked food."}],"answer":{"af":"Probleem: kruisbesmetting. Oplossing: eenrigting-werkvloei, opwasarea by die eetsaal en 'n aparte area vir rou vleis.","en":"Problem: cross-contamination. Solution: one-direction work flow, washing-up area by the dining hall and a separate area for raw meat."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stoof werk slegs met panne wat 'n magnetiese basis het?","en":"Which stove only works with pans that have a magnetic base?"},"options":[{"af":"Gasstoof","en":"Gas stove"},{"af":"Elektriese stoof met soliede plate","en":"Electric stove with solid plates"},{"af":"Induksiestoof","en":"Induction stove"},{"af":"Houtstoof","en":"Wood-burning stove"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Induksiestoof skep 'n magnetiese veld wat die pan self verhit. Panne van gewone aluminium, koper of glas werk nie daarop nie.","en":"An induction stove creates a magnetic field that heats the pan itself. Pans of plain aluminium, copper or glass do not work on it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ___ is 'n oorhoofse rooster wat gebruik word om geregte bo-op te verbruin of te gratineer.","en":"The ___ is an overhead grill used to brown or gratinate the top of dishes."},"answers":{"af":["salamander"],"en":["salamander"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bakplaat","kantelbraaipan","bain-marie"],"en":["griddle","bratt pan","bain-marie"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die salamander gee hitte van bo. 'n Bakplaat is 'n plat plaat waarop jy kos braai, en 'n bain-marie hou kos warm in water.","en":"The salamander gives heat from above. A griddle is a flat plate you cook food on, and a bain-marie keeps food warm in water."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Konveksie-oond gebruik 'n waaier om die warm lug rond te blaas, sodat kos vinniger en egaliger gaar word.","en":"A convection oven uses a fan to circulate the hot air so that food cooks faster and more evenly."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die waaier versprei die hitte deur die hele oond, terwyl 'n konvensionele oond bo warmer as onder is.","en":"True. The fan spreads the heat through the whole oven, while a conventional oven is hotter at the top than at the bottom."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom sit 'n kok 'n klam lap onder sy snyplank?","en":"Why does a cook put a damp cloth under his cutting board?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die plank te ontsmet terwyl hy sny","en":"To sanitise the board while he cuts"},{"af":"Sodat die plank nie gly nie","en":"So that the board does not slip"},{"af":"Om die mes skerp te hou","en":"To keep the knife sharp"},{"af":"Om die kos koel te hou","en":"To keep the food cool"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Plank wat gly, kan veroorsaak dat die mes skuif en jy jou sny. Die lap ontsmet niks nie – ontsmetting gebeur ná die was.","en":"A board that slips can make the knife slide so you cut yourself. The cloth sanitises nothing – sanitising happens after washing."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n ___ staan houers met kos in warm water om die kos warm te hou.","en":"In a ___ containers of food stand in hot water to keep the food warm."},"answers":{"af":["bain-marie","bain marie","bainmarie"],"en":["bain-marie","bain marie","bainmarie"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["salamander","warmkas","hittelamp"],"en":["salamander","hot cupboard","heat lamp"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die bain-marie hou kos warm in 'n warmwaterbad. 'n Warmkas gebruik droë hitte en 'n hittelamp skyn van bo op die kos.","en":"The bain-marie keeps food warm in a hot-water bath. A hot cupboard uses dry heat and a heat lamp shines on the food from above."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aanhegsel van die voedselmenger gebruik jy om brooddeeg te knie?","en":"Which attachment of the food mixer do you use to knead bread dough?"},"options":[{"af":"Die garde","en":"The whisk"},{"af":"Die klopper/spaan","en":"The beater/paddle"},{"af":"Die snylem","en":"The cutting blade"},{"af":"Die deeghaak","en":"The dough hook"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die deeghaak rek en knie die deeg. Die garde klop lug in (room, eierwitte) en die spaan room botter en suiker.","en":"The dough hook stretches and kneads the dough. The whisk beats in air (cream, egg whites) and the paddle creams butter and sugar."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die snit waar groente in dun vuurhoutjiestrokies gesny word, heet ___.","en":"The cut in which vegetables are cut into thin matchstick strips is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["julienne"],"en":["julienne"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brunoise","paysanne","chiffonade"],"en":["brunoise","paysanne","chiffonade"]}},"explain":{"af":"Julienne = dun strokies. Brunoise is baie fyn blokkies, paysanne dun skyfies en chiffonade fyn gekerfde blare.","en":"Julienne = thin strips. Brunoise is very fine dice, paysanne thin slices and chiffonade finely shredded leaves."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter mes is dun en buigsaam en word gebruik om visfilette van die graat af te sny?","en":"Which knife is thin and flexible and is used to cut fish fillets off the bones?"},"options":[{"af":"Fileermes","en":"Filleting knife"},{"af":"Ontbeningsmes","en":"Boning knife"},{"af":"Voorsnymes","en":"Carving knife"},{"af":"Gekartelde broodmes","en":"Serrated bread knife"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die buigsame fileermes buig langs die graat. Die ontbeningsmes is stywer en word vir vleis gebruik; die voorsnymes sny gaar vleis.","en":"The flexible filleting knife bends along the bones. The boning knife is stiffer and is used for meat; the carving knife slices cooked meat."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As 'n mes van die tafel af val, moet jy dit vinnig probeer vang sodat dit nie beskadig word nie.","en":"If a knife falls off the table, you should try to catch it quickly so that it does not get damaged."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Moet nooit 'n vallende mes probeer vang nie – staan terug en laat dit val. 'n Mes kan vervang word, jou hand nie.","en":"False. Never try to catch a falling knife – step back and let it fall. A knife can be replaced, your hand cannot."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke snit by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each cut to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Brunoise","en":"Brunoise"},"r":{"af":"Baie fyn blokkies (ongeveer 2–3 mm)","en":"Very fine dice (about 2–3 mm)"}},{"l":{"af":"Macédoine","en":"Macédoine"},"r":{"af":"Medium blokkies (ongeveer 5 mm)","en":"Medium dice (about 5 mm)"}},{"l":{"af":"Chiffonade","en":"Chiffonade"},"r":{"af":"Fyn gekerfde blare","en":"Finely shredded leaves"}},{"l":{"af":"Concassé","en":"Concassé"},"r":{"af":"Grof gekap, bv. geskilde tamatie","en":"Roughly chopped, e.g. peeled tomato"}}],"explain":{"af":"Onthou die grootte-volgorde van blokkies: brunoise (fynste) → macédoine (medium). Chiffonade is vir blare en concassé is grof gekap.","en":"Remember the size order of dice: brunoise (finest) → macédoine (medium). Chiffonade is for leaves and concassé is roughly chopped."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter materiaal gelei hitte die beste, maar is duur en moet gereeld gepoleer word?","en":"Which material conducts heat best, but is expensive and must be polished regularly?"},"options":[{"af":"Vlekvrye staal","en":"Stainless steel"},{"af":"Gietyster","en":"Cast iron"},{"af":"Koper","en":"Copper"},{"af":"Kleefvry","en":"Non-stick"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Koper is die beste geleier van hitte, maar dit is duur, verkleur en het 'n voering nodig. Vlekvrye staal gelei hitte juis swak.","en":"Copper is the best conductor of heat, but it is expensive, tarnishes and needs a lining. Stainless steel actually conducts heat poorly."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die werksdriehoek verbind die stoof, die wasbak en die ___.","en":"The work triangle connects the stove, the sink and the ___."},"answers":{"af":["yskas","koelkas"],"en":["fridge","refrigerator"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["oond","mikrogolfoond","skottelgoedwasser"],"en":["oven","microwave","dishwasher"]}},"explain":{"af":"Stoof, wasbak en yskas is die drie plekke waar 'n kok die meeste werk. Kort afstande tussen hulle spaar tyd en energie.","en":"Stove, sink and fridge are the three places where a cook works most. Short distances between them save time and energy."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die eerste stap om 'n snymasjien skoon te maak, is om dit af te skakel en die ___ uit te trek.","en":"The first step in cleaning a slicer is to switch it off and pull out the ___."},"answers":{"af":["prop","kragprop"],"en":["plug"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lem","skuiwer","lemskerm"],"en":["blade","carriage","blade guard"]}},"explain":{"af":"Trek altyd eers die prop uit, sodat die masjien nie per ongeluk kan aanskakel nie. Eers daarna haal jy die verwyderbare dele uit.","en":"Always pull out the plug first so the machine cannot switch on by accident. Only then do you remove the removable parts."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte volgorde van die eenrigting-werkvloei in 'n kombuis?","en":"What is the correct order of the one-direction work flow in a kitchen?"},"options":[{"af":"Berging → ontvangs → kook → voorbereiding → opdiening → opwas","en":"Storage → receiving → cooking → preparation → service → washing up"},{"af":"Ontvangs → voorbereiding → berging → kook → opwas → opdiening","en":"Receiving → preparation → storage → cooking → washing up → service"},{"af":"Ontvangs → berging → kook → voorbereiding → opdiening → opwas","en":"Receiving → storage → cooking → preparation → service → washing up"},{"af":"Ontvangs → berging → voorbereiding → kook → opdiening → opwas","en":"Receiving → storage → preparation → cooking → service → washing up"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Kos word ontvang, geberg, voorberei, gekook en opgedien; laastens word die skottelgoed gewas. So beweeg kos net vorentoe.","en":"Food is received, stored, prepared, cooked and served; finally the dishes are washed. This way food only moves forward."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n restaurantkombuis word vuil borde deur die area gedra waar slaaie gemaak word. Wat is die grootste probleem en die beste oplossing?","en":"In a restaurant kitchen dirty plates are carried through the area where salads are made. What is the biggest problem and the best solution?"},"options":[{"af":"Kruisbesmetting; skuif die opwasarea sodat vuil borde nie deur die voorbereidingsarea gaan nie","en":"Cross-contamination; move the washing-up area so dirty plates do not pass through the preparation area"},{"af":"Dit mors net tyd; die kelners moet vinniger loop","en":"It only wastes time; the waiters must walk faster"},{"af":"Daar is geen probleem nie, solank die borde toegemaak is","en":"There is no problem as long as the plates are covered"},{"af":"Die slaaie word te warm; sit 'n ekstra yskas in die voorbereidingsarea","en":"The salads get too warm; put an extra fridge in the preparation area"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vuil en skoon items mag nie kruis nie, want bakterieë kan op kos wat nie gekook word nie (slaai) beland. 'n Eenrigting-werkvloei los dit op.","en":"Dirty and clean items must not cross, because bacteria can land on food that is not cooked (salad). A one-direction work flow solves this."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kok wil 'n steak op 'n induksiestoof seël en dit dan in die oond klaar gaarmaak. Watter pan is die beste keuse?","en":"A cook wants to sear a steak on an induction stove and then finish cooking it in the oven. Which pan is the best choice?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Aluminiumpan sonder 'n magnetiese basis","en":"An aluminium pan without a magnetic base"},{"af":"'n Kleefvry pan met 'n plastiekhandvatsel","en":"A non-stick pan with a plastic handle"},{"af":"'n Gietysterpan","en":"A cast-iron pan"},{"af":"'n Glasbakskottel","en":"A glass baking dish"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Gietyster is magneties (werk op induksie), hou baie hitte vir seël en kan in die oond gaan. Aluminium werk nie op induksie nie, plastiek smelt in die oond en glas is nie vir die stoof nie.","en":"Cast iron is magnetic (works on induction), holds plenty of heat for searing and can go into the oven. Aluminium does not work on induction, plastic melts in the oven and glass is not for the stove."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-kombuisbedrywighede","title":{"af":"Mise en place, meet, resepte, kookterme en kookmetodes","en":"Mise en place, measuring, recipes, culinary terms and cooking methods"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal jou werk vooraf kan beplan, akkuraat kan meet, 'n resep kan skaal en die regte kookmetode vir 'n gereg kan kies.","en":"You will be able to plan your work in advance, measure accurately, scale a recipe and choose the right cooking method for a dish."},"summary":{"af":"## Mise en place\n\n**Mise en place** is Frans vir \"alles op sy plek\". Dit beteken jy berei jou bestanddele, toerusting en werkstasie voor en organiseer dit **voordat** jy begin kook of diens lewer.\n\n- Lees die resep deur en skaal dit indien nodig.\n- Versamel en kontroleer die toerusting; voorverhit die oond en smeer die panne.\n- Weeg en meet al die bestanddele af.\n- Was, skil en sny die groente; berei die garnering voor.\n- Hou jou werkstasie skoon en netjies (\"maak skoon soos jy werk\").\n\n**Hoekom?** Jy spaar tyd, werk met minder stres en maak minder foute. Die kos is betyds klaar, van dieselfde gehalte, en jy werk veiliger.\n\n## Meet akkuraat\n\n- **Droë bestanddele** (meel, suiker): skep dit met 'n lepel in die maatkoppie en maak gelyk met 'n reguit kant, soos die rug van 'n mes. Moenie die koppie stamp of die meel vasdruk nie – **behalwe bruinsuiker**, wat jy wel vasdruk.\n- **Weeg** op 'n skaal is die akkuraatste metode, veral vir bak.\n- **Vloeistowwe:** gebruik 'n maatbeker op 'n plat oppervlak en lees dit op **ooghoogte** af.\n\n| Maat | Metriek |\n|---|---|\n| 1 teelepel (t) | 5 ml |\n| 1 eetlepel (e) | 15 ml |\n| 1 koppie | 250 ml |\n| 1 kilogram (kg) | 1 000 g |\n| 1 liter (ℓ) | 1 000 ml |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n Hooplepel of vasgedrukte meel gee te veel meel – die produk word droog en swaar.\n\n## Die standaardresep\n\n'n Standaardresep bevat die **naam** van die gereg, die **opbrengs** (aantal porsies), die **bestanddele in volgorde van gebruik** met hoeveelhede, 'n **genommerde metode**, die **oondtemperatuur**, die **kooktyd** en die nodige **toerusting**.\n\n### 'n Resep skaal\n\n`Omskakelingsfaktor = vereiste opbrengs ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs`\n\nVermenigvuldig **elke** hoeveelheid met die faktor. 'n Resep is vir 12 porsies en jy het 24 nodig: 24 ÷ 12 = 2, dus verdubbel jy alles. Vir 6 porsies: 6 ÷ 12 = 0,5, dus halveer jy alles.\n\n> **Wenk:** Die oondtemperatuur bly dieselfde. Die kooktyd kan verander as jy 'n groter pan gebruik.\n\n## Kookterme\n\n| Term | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| Al dente | Gaar, maar nog ferm as jy daarin byt (pasta, groente) |\n| Au gratin | Bestrooi met kaas en/of broodkrummels en bo bruin gemaak |\n| Bain-marie | 'n Warmwaterbad om kos saggies te kook of warm te hou |\n| Bedruip (baste) | Skep die vleis se eie vet of sous oor terwyl dit braai |\n| Blansjeer | Dompel kortliks in kookwater en dan dadelik in yswater |\n| Smoor (braise) | Bruin eers in vet, kook dan stadig in min vloeistof met 'n deksel |\n| Coulis | 'n Dun, gladde puree van vrugte of groente |\n| In blokkies sny (dice) | Sny in klein, gelyke blokkies |\n| Invou (fold in) | Meng liggies met 'n metaallepel sodat die lug behoue bly |\n| Garneer | Versier 'n gereg om dit aantrekliker te maak |\n| Marineer | Laat kos in 'n gegeurde, dikwels suur vloeistof lê vir geur en sagtheid |\n| Puree | Kos wat fyngemaak is tot 'n gladde pasta |\n| Reduseer (inkook) | Kook sonder deksel sodat water verdamp: dikker sous, sterker geur |\n| Roux | Gelyke dele botter en meel saam gaargemaak; die basis van witsous |\n| Sauté | Braai vinnig in 'n bietjie warm vet terwyl jy die pan skud |\n| Prut (simmer) | Kook net onder kookpunt; klein borreltjies breek stadig |\n| Klits (whisk) | Klits vinnig om lug in te werk of 'n mengsel glad te maak |\n| Sitrusskil (zest) | Die fyngerasperde, gekleurde buitenste laag van sitrusskil |\n\n## Kookmetodes\n\n**Nat hitte** (kos word in water, vloeistof of stoom gaargemaak):\n\n- **Kook** – in borrelende water by 100 °C (pasta, rys, aartappels).\n- **Prut** – net onder kookpunt (sop, sous); die kos breek nie op nie.\n- **Posjeer** – in vloeistof wat skaars beweeg (eiers, vis, vrugte); sag en laevet.\n- **Stoom** – bo kookwater in die stoom (groente, vis); behou die meeste voedingstowwe, kleur en vorm, maar is stadiger.\n- **Stowe** – klein stukke kos, heeltemal met vloeistof bedek, word stadig gaar (bredie); taai snitte word sag en die voedingstowwe bly in die sous.\n\n**Droë hitte** (warm lug, stralingshitte of warm vet):\n\n- **Bak** – in die oond (brood, koek, skons).\n- **Oondbraai** – groot, sagte snitte vleis, hoender en groente; dit word bruin en geurig.\n- **Rooster** – direkte stralingshitte; vinnig en die vet drup af, maar die kos droog maklik uit.\n- **Vlakbraai, diepvetbraai, sauté en roerbraai** – in warm vet of olie; vinnig, bros en goudbruin, maar meer vet. Roerbraai in 'n wok behou kleur en knapperigheid.\n\n**Kombinasie** (eers droë, dan nat hitte): **smoor** en **potbraai** – vir taai, goedkoper snitte (bors, skenkel); die bindweefsel word stadig sag.\n\n**Mikrogolf:** baie vinnig met min voedingstofverlies, maar die kos word nie bruin of bros nie en verhit ongelyk – roer en laat staan.\n\n## Effek op voedingstowwe\n\nDie **B-vitamiene en vitamien C is wateroplosbaar** en vitamien C word ook deur hitte vernietig. Stoom daarom eerder, gebruik min water, kook kort met 'n deksel en gebruik die kookwater in sop of sous.\n\n> **Onthou!** Nat hitte = water of stoom; droë hitte = lug, straling of vet; kombinasie = albei.","en":"## Mise en place\n\n**Mise en place** is French for \"everything in its place\". It means you prepare and organise your ingredients, equipment and workstation **before** you start cooking or serving.\n\n- Read through the recipe and scale it if necessary.\n- Collect and check the equipment; preheat the oven and grease the pans.\n- Weigh and measure all the ingredients.\n- Wash, peel and cut the vegetables; prepare the garnish.\n- Keep your workstation clean and tidy (\"clean as you go\").\n\n**Why?** You save time, work with less stress and make fewer mistakes. The food is ready on time, of consistent quality, and you work more safely.\n\n## Measuring accurately\n\n- **Dry ingredients** (flour, sugar): spoon them into the measuring cup and level off with a straight edge, such as the back of a knife. Don't tap the cup or pack the flour – **except brown sugar**, which you do pack down.\n- **Weighing** on a scale is the most accurate method, especially for baking.\n- **Liquids:** use a measuring jug on a flat surface and read it at **eye level**.\n\n| Measure | Metric |\n|---|---|\n| 1 teaspoon (tsp) | 5 ml |\n| 1 tablespoon (tbsp) | 15 ml |\n| 1 cup | 250 ml |\n| 1 kilogram (kg) | 1 000 g |\n| 1 litre (ℓ) | 1 000 ml |\n\n> **Common mistake:** A heaped spoon or packed flour gives too much flour – the product becomes dry and heavy.\n\n## The standard recipe\n\nA standard recipe contains the **name** of the dish, the **yield** (number of portions), the **ingredients in order of use** with quantities, a **numbered method**, the **oven temperature**, the **cooking time** and the **equipment** needed.\n\n### Scaling a recipe\n\n`Conversion factor = required yield ÷ original yield`\n\nMultiply **every** quantity by the factor. A recipe serves 12 and you need 24: 24 ÷ 12 = 2, so you double everything. For 6 portions: 6 ÷ 12 = 0.5, so you halve everything.\n\n> **Tip:** The oven temperature stays the same. The cooking time may change if you use a bigger pan.\n\n## Culinary terms\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Al dente | Cooked but still firm to the bite (pasta, vegetables) |\n| Au gratin | Sprinkled with cheese and/or breadcrumbs and browned on top |\n| Bain-marie | A hot-water bath to cook food gently or keep it hot |\n| Baste | Spoon the meat's own fat or juices over it while it roasts |\n| Blanch | Dip briefly in boiling water, then immediately in iced water |\n| Braise | Brown in fat first, then cook slowly in a little liquid with a lid |\n| Coulis | A thin, smooth purée of fruit or vegetables |\n| Dice | Cut into small, even cubes |\n| Fold in | Mix gently with a metal spoon so that the air is kept in |\n| Garnish | Decorate a dish to make it more attractive |\n| Marinate | Leave food in a flavoured, often acidic liquid for flavour and tenderness |\n| Purée | Food blended or mashed to a smooth paste |\n| Reduce | Boil without a lid so water evaporates: a thicker sauce, a stronger flavour |\n| Roux | Equal parts butter and flour cooked together; the base of white sauce |\n| Sauté | Fry quickly in a little hot fat while shaking the pan |\n| Simmer | Cook just below boiling point; small bubbles break slowly |\n| Whisk | Beat quickly to add air or to make a mixture smooth |\n| Zest | The finely grated, coloured outer layer of citrus peel |\n\n## Cooking methods\n\n**Moist heat** (food is cooked in water, liquid or steam):\n\n- **Boiling** – in bubbling water at 100 °C (pasta, rice, potatoes).\n- **Simmering** – just below boiling point (soup, sauce); the food doesn't break up.\n- **Poaching** – in liquid that is barely moving (eggs, fish, fruit); gentle and low-fat.\n- **Steaming** – above boiling water in the steam (vegetables, fish); keeps the most nutrients, colour and shape, but is slower.\n- **Stewing** – small pieces of food, fully covered with liquid, cooked slowly (bredie); tough cuts become tender and the nutrients stay in the sauce.\n\n**Dry heat** (hot air, radiant heat or hot fat):\n\n- **Baking** – in the oven (bread, cake, scones).\n- **Roasting** – large, tender cuts of meat, chicken and vegetables; they brown and develop flavour.\n- **Grilling** – direct radiant heat; fast and the fat drips off, but food dries out easily.\n- **Shallow frying, deep-frying, sautéing and stir-frying** – in hot fat or oil; fast, crisp and golden, but more fat. Stir-frying in a wok keeps colour and crunch.\n\n**Combination** (dry heat first, then moist heat): **braising** and **pot-roasting** – for tough, cheaper cuts (brisket, shin); the connective tissue slowly becomes tender.\n\n**Microwave:** very fast with little nutrient loss, but food doesn't brown or crisp and heats unevenly – stir and let it stand.\n\n## Effect on nutrients\n\nThe **B vitamins and vitamin C are water-soluble**, and vitamin C is also destroyed by heat. So rather steam, use little water, cook briefly with a lid and use the cooking water in soup or sauce.\n\n> **Remember!** Moist heat = water or steam; dry heat = air, radiation or fat; combination = both."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Mise en place","en":"Mise en place"},"def":{"af":"\"Alles op sy plek\": die voorbereiding en organisering van bestanddele, toerusting en die werkstasie voordat jy kook of diens lewer.","en":"\"Everything in its place\": preparing and organising ingredients, equipment and the workstation before cooking or service."}},{"term":{"af":"Standaardresep","en":"Standard recipe"},"def":{"af":"'n Resep in 'n vaste formaat met die naam, opbrengs, bestanddele in volgorde van gebruik, genommerde metode, oondtemperatuur, kooktyd en toerusting.","en":"A recipe in a fixed format with the name, yield, ingredients in order of use, numbered method, oven temperature, cooking time and equipment."}},{"term":{"af":"Opbrengs","en":"Yield"},"def":{"af":"Die hoeveelheid of aantal porsies wat 'n resep lewer.","en":"The quantity or number of portions a recipe produces."}},{"term":{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor","en":"Conversion factor"},"def":{"af":"Vereiste opbrengs ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs; elke hoeveelheid in die resep word daarmee vermenigvuldig.","en":"Required yield ÷ original yield; every quantity in the recipe is multiplied by it."}},{"term":{"af":"Nat hitte","en":"Moist heat"},"def":{"af":"Kookmetodes waar kos in water, 'n ander vloeistof of stoom gaargemaak word, bv. kook, prut, posjeer, stoom en stowe.","en":"Cooking methods where food is cooked in water, another liquid or steam, e.g. boiling, simmering, poaching, steaming and stewing."}},{"term":{"af":"Droë hitte","en":"Dry heat"},"def":{"af":"Kookmetodes met warm lug, stralingshitte of warm vet, bv. bak, oondbraai, rooster en braai in vet.","en":"Cooking methods using hot air, radiant heat or hot fat, e.g. baking, roasting, grilling and frying."}},{"term":{"af":"Kombinasiemetode","en":"Combination method"},"def":{"af":"'n Metode wat droë hitte (bruin maak) en nat hitte (stadig in vloeistof) kombineer, bv. smoor en potbraai.","en":"A method that combines dry heat (browning) and moist heat (slow cooking in liquid), e.g. braising and pot-roasting."}},{"term":{"af":"Al dente","en":"Al dente"},"def":{"af":"Gaar, maar steeds ferm wanneer jy daarin byt; gebruik vir pasta en groente.","en":"Cooked but still firm to the bite; used for pasta and vegetables."}},{"term":{"af":"Roux","en":"Roux"},"def":{"af":"Gelyke dele vet (botter) en meel wat saam gaargemaak word as basis vir witsous.","en":"Equal parts fat (butter) and flour cooked together as the base for white sauce."}},{"term":{"af":"Wateroplosbare vitamiene","en":"Water-soluble vitamins"},"def":{"af":"Die B-vitamiene en vitamien C, wat in die kookwater oplos en verlore gaan; vitamien C word ook deur hitte vernietig.","en":"The B vitamins and vitamin C, which dissolve into cooking water and are lost; vitamin C is also destroyed by heat."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skaal 'n resep","en":"Scale a recipe"},"problem":{"af":"Die pampoensopresep is vir 6 porsies: 600 g pampoen, 2 uie, 1 ℓ hoenderaftreksel, 100 ml room en 10 ml kerriepoeier. Jy moet 15 porsies vir 'n kerkbasaar in Brits maak. Bereken die nuwe hoeveelhede.","en":"The pumpkin soup recipe serves 6: 600 g pumpkin, 2 onions, 1 ℓ chicken stock, 100 ml cream and 10 ml curry powder. You must make 15 portions for a church bazaar in Brits. Calculate the new quantities."},"steps":[{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor = vereiste opbrengs ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs = 15 ÷ 6 = 2,5","en":"Conversion factor = required yield ÷ original yield = 15 ÷ 6 = 2.5"},{"af":"Pampoen: 600 g × 2,5 = 1 500 g (1,5 kg); uie: 2 × 2,5 = 5 uie","en":"Pumpkin: 600 g × 2.5 = 1 500 g (1.5 kg); onions: 2 × 2.5 = 5 onions"},{"af":"Aftreksel: 1 ℓ × 2,5 = 2,5 ℓ; room: 100 ml × 2,5 = 250 ml","en":"Stock: 1 ℓ × 2.5 = 2.5 ℓ; cream: 100 ml × 2.5 = 250 ml"},{"af":"Kerriepoeier: 10 ml × 2,5 = 25 ml. Kontroleer: elke bestanddeel is met dieselfde faktor vermenigvuldig.","en":"Curry powder: 10 ml × 2.5 = 25 ml. Check: every ingredient was multiplied by the same factor."}],"answer":{"af":"1,5 kg pampoen, 5 uie, 2,5 ℓ aftreksel, 250 ml room, 25 ml kerriepoeier","en":"1.5 kg pumpkin, 5 onions, 2.5 ℓ stock, 250 ml cream, 25 ml curry powder"}},{"title":{"af":"Skakel huishoudelike mate om","en":"Convert household measures"},"problem":{"af":"'n Resep vra 3 eetlepels olie, 4 teelepels bakpoeier en 1½ koppies melk. Hoeveel milliliter is elkeen?","en":"A recipe asks for 3 tablespoons of oil, 4 teaspoons of baking powder and 1½ cups of milk. How many millilitres is each?"},"steps":[{"af":"Olie: 1 eetlepel = 15 ml, dus 3 × 15 ml = 45 ml","en":"Oil: 1 tablespoon = 15 ml, so 3 × 15 ml = 45 ml"},{"af":"Bakpoeier: 1 teelepel = 5 ml, dus 4 × 5 ml = 20 ml","en":"Baking powder: 1 teaspoon = 5 ml, so 4 × 5 ml = 20 ml"},{"af":"Melk: 1 koppie = 250 ml, dus 1,5 × 250 ml = 375 ml","en":"Milk: 1 cup = 250 ml, so 1.5 × 250 ml = 375 ml"}],"answer":{"af":"45 ml olie, 20 ml bakpoeier, 375 ml melk","en":"45 ml oil, 20 ml baking powder, 375 ml milk"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies en klassifiseer 'n kookmetode","en":"Choose and classify a cooking method"},"problem":{"af":"'n Restaurant by Hartbeespoortdam moet (a) broccoli, (b) 'n taai stuk beesbors en (c) eiers vir 'n ontbytgereg gaarmaak. Beveel vir elkeen 'n kookmetode aan, klassifiseer dit en gee 'n rede.","en":"A restaurant at Hartbeespoort Dam must cook (a) broccoli, (b) a tough piece of beef brisket and (c) eggs for a breakfast dish. Recommend a cooking method for each, classify it and give a reason."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Broccoli: stoom (nat hitte). Die groente lê nie in die water nie, dus gaan minder vitamien C verlore en dit bly groen en knapperig.","en":"(a) Broccoli: steaming (moist heat). The vegetable doesn't lie in the water, so less vitamin C is lost and it stays green and crisp."},{"af":"(b) Beesbors: smoor (kombinasie). Eers bruin maak vir geur, dan stadig in 'n bietjie vloeistof met 'n deksel sodat die bindweefsel sag word.","en":"(b) Brisket: braising (combination). Brown it first for flavour, then cook slowly in a little liquid with a lid so the connective tissue becomes tender."},{"af":"(c) Eiers: posjeer (nat hitte). Die vloeistof beweeg skaars, so die delikate eier word sag gaar sonder ekstra vet.","en":"(c) Eggs: poaching (moist heat). The liquid barely moves, so the delicate egg cooks gently without extra fat."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Stoom – nat hitte; (b) smoor – kombinasie; (c) posjeer – nat hitte","en":"(a) Steaming – moist heat; (b) braising – combination; (c) poaching – moist heat"}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan jou mise en place","en":"Plan your mise en place"},"problem":{"af":"Jy moet om 12:00 pannekoek vir 20 gaste by 'n rugbydag bedien. Die resep is vir 10 pannekoeke. Beskryf jou mise en place in die regte volgorde.","en":"You must serve pancakes to 20 guests at a rugby day at 12:00. The recipe makes 10 pancakes. Describe your mise en place in the correct order."},"steps":[{"af":"Lees die resep en skaal dit: 20 ÷ 10 = 2, dus verdubbel jy elke bestanddeel.","en":"Read the recipe and scale it: 20 ÷ 10 = 2, so you double every ingredient."},{"af":"Versamel die toerusting: mengbak, klitser, maatbeker, skaal, pan, spatel, borde.","en":"Collect the equipment: mixing bowl, whisk, measuring jug, scale, pan, spatula, plates."},{"af":"Weeg en meet al die bestanddele af en maak die beslag vroeg genoeg sodat dit ongeveer 30 minute kan rus.","en":"Weigh and measure all the ingredients and make the batter early enough so that it can rest for about 30 minutes."},{"af":"Berei die bykosse voor (kaneelsuiker, suurlemoenskyfies), verhit die pan en hou jou werkstasie skoon terwyl jy werk.","en":"Prepare the accompaniments (cinnamon sugar, lemon wedges), heat the pan and keep your workstation clean as you go."}],"answer":{"af":"Skaal → versamel toerusting → weeg en meet → maak en rus die beslag → berei bykosse voor → verhit die pan","en":"Scale → collect equipment → weigh and measure → make and rest the batter → prepare accompaniments → heat the pan"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken die term mise en place?","en":"What does the term mise en place mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Kook stadig met 'n deksel","en":"Cook slowly with a lid"},{"af":"Die hoofgereg van die dag","en":"The main course of the day"},{"af":"Alles op sy plek: berei alles voor voordat jy begin","en":"Everything in its place: prepare everything before you start"},{"af":"Versier die bord voor diens","en":"Decorate the plate before service"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Mise en place is Frans vir \"alles op sy plek\": bestanddele, toerusting en werkstasie word vooraf voorberei. Versier is garneer, en stadig kook met 'n deksel is smoor.","en":"Mise en place is French for \"everything in its place\": ingredients, equipment and the workstation are prepared in advance. Decorating is garnishing, and slow cooking with a lid is braising."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1 eetlepel = ___ ml","en":"1 tablespoon = ___ ml"},"answers":{"af":["15","15 ml"],"en":["15","15 ml"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","10","25"],"en":["5","10","25"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Eetlepel is 15 ml en 'n teelepel is 5 ml, dus is 1 eetlepel = 3 teelepels.","en":"A tablespoon is 15 ml and a teaspoon is 5 ml, so 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Bruinsuiker word in die maatkoppie vasgedruk wanneer jy dit meet.","en":"Brown sugar is packed down into the measuring cup when you measure it."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Bruinsuiker is klam en vorm lugsakkies, daarom druk jy dit vas. Meel en witsuiker druk jy nie vas nie – jy skep en maak gelyk.","en":"True. Brown sugar is moist and forms air pockets, so you pack it down. Flour and white sugar are not packed – you spoon in and level off."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die akkuraatste manier om droë bestanddele vir bak te meet, is om dit op 'n ___ te weeg.","en":"The most accurate way to measure dry ingredients for baking is to weigh them on a ___."},"answers":{"af":["skaal","kombuisskaal","weegskaal"],"en":["scale","kitchen scale","scales"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["maatkoppie","maatlepel","maatbeker"],"en":["measuring cup","measuring spoon","measuring jug"]}},"explain":{"af":"Weeg is die akkuraatste omdat 'n koppie meel se massa verskil na gelang van hoe vas dit gepak is.","en":"Weighing is most accurate because the mass of a cup of flour differs depending on how firmly it is packed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van die volgende is 'n nathitte-kookmetode?","en":"Which one of the following is a moist-heat cooking method?"},"options":[{"af":"Rooster","en":"Grilling"},{"af":"Posjeer","en":"Poaching"},{"af":"Diepvetbraai","en":"Deep-frying"},{"af":"Bak","en":"Baking"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Posjeer gebeur in vloeistof wat skaars beweeg, dus is dit nat hitte. Rooster, diepvetbraai en bak gebruik straling, vet of warm lug – droë hitte.","en":"Poaching happens in liquid that is barely moving, so it is moist heat. Grilling, deep-frying and baking use radiation, fat or hot air – dry heat."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke kookterm by die regte betekenis.","en":"Match each culinary term to its correct meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Al dente","en":"Al dente"},"r":{"af":"Gaar, maar nog ferm as jy daarin byt","en":"Cooked but still firm to the bite"}},{"l":{"af":"Au gratin","en":"Au gratin"},"r":{"af":"Met kaas of krummels bestrooi en bo bruin gemaak","en":"Sprinkled with cheese or crumbs and browned on top"}},{"l":{"af":"Blansjeer","en":"Blanch"},"r":{"af":"Kortliks in kookwater en dan in yswater gedompel","en":"Dipped briefly in boiling water, then in iced water"}},{"l":{"af":"Roux","en":"Roux"},"r":{"af":"Gelyke dele botter en meel saam gaargemaak","en":"Equal parts butter and flour cooked together"}},{"l":{"af":"Reduseer","en":"Reduce"},"r":{"af":"Sonder deksel kook sodat die vloeistof dikker word","en":"Boil without a lid so the liquid becomes thicker"}}],"explain":{"af":"Leer die terme met 'n voorbeeld: pasta al dente, blomkool au gratin, tamaties blansjeer om die skil af te trek, 'n roux vir witsous en 'n sous reduseer vir sterker geur.","en":"Learn the terms with an example: pasta al dente, cauliflower au gratin, blanching tomatoes to peel them, a roux for white sauce and reducing a sauce for a stronger flavour."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe lees jy 'n maatbeker met melk korrek af?","en":"How do you read a measuring jug of milk correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Staan regop en kyk van bo af in die beker","en":"Stand upright and look down into the jug"},{"af":"Hou die beker in jou hand op armlengte","en":"Hold the jug in your hand at arm's length"},{"af":"Kantel die beker effens na jou toe","en":"Tilt the jug slightly towards you"},{"af":"Sit dit op 'n plat oppervlak en lees op ooghoogte","en":"Put it on a flat surface and read at eye level"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Op 'n plat oppervlak is die vloeistof gelyk, en op ooghoogte sien jy die regte merk. Van bo af lyk die vlak verkeerd, en 'n beker in die hand is skuins.","en":"On a flat surface the liquid is level, and at eye level you see the correct mark. From above the level looks wrong, and a jug held in the hand is tilted."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Resep is vir 12 porsies en jy het 36 porsies nodig. Die omskakelingsfaktor is ___.","en":"A recipe serves 12 and you need 36 portions. The conversion factor is ___."},"answers":{"af":["3","×3","x3"],"en":["3","×3","x3"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["24","0,33","48"],"en":["24","0.33","48"]}},"explain":{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor = vereiste ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs = 36 ÷ 12 = 3. Moenie aftrek nie (36 − 12 = 24) en moenie die getalle omruil nie (12 ÷ 36).","en":"Conversion factor = required ÷ original yield = 36 ÷ 12 = 3. Don't subtract (36 − 12 = 24) and don't swap the numbers (12 ÷ 36)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Resep vir 4 mense gebruik 300 g rys. Hoeveel rys het jy vir 10 mense nodig?","en":"A recipe for 4 people uses 300 g rice. How much rice do you need for 10 people?"},"options":[{"af":"750 g","en":"750 g"},{"af":"1 200 g","en":"1 200 g"},{"af":"3 000 g","en":"3 000 g"},{"af":"600 g","en":"600 g"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Faktor = 10 ÷ 4 = 2,5, dus 300 g × 2,5 = 750 g. 3 000 g kom van 300 × 10 – dit vergeet dat die resep reeds vir 4 is.","en":"Factor = 10 ÷ 4 = 2.5, so 300 g × 2.5 = 750 g. 3 000 g comes from 300 × 10 – it forgets that the recipe already serves 4."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Stoom is 'n droëhitte-metode omdat die kos nie in die water lê nie.","en":"Steaming is a dry-heat method because the food doesn't lie in the water."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Stoom is nat hitte: die kos word deur warm waterdamp gaargemaak. Dit is juis die beste nathitte-metode om voedingstowwe te behou.","en":"False. Steaming is moist heat: the food is cooked by hot water vapour. It is in fact the best moist-heat method for keeping nutrients."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter manier om broccoli gaar te maak, behou die meeste vitamien C?","en":"Which way of cooking broccoli keeps the most vitamin C?"},"options":[{"af":"Kook dit lank in baie water sodat dit sag word","en":"Boil it for a long time in plenty of water so that it becomes soft"},{"af":"Voeg koeksoda by die kookwater sodat dit groen bly","en":"Add bicarbonate of soda to the cooking water so that it stays green"},{"af":"Stoom dit kort tot dit net sag is","en":"Steam it briefly until just tender"},{"af":"Sny dit die oggend en laat dit tot middagete in water staan","en":"Cut it in the morning and leave it standing in water until lunch"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vitamien C is wateroplosbaar en word deur hitte vernietig. Kort stoom beperk albei. Koeksoda (alkalies) vernietig vitamien C, en week in water laat dit uitloog.","en":"Vitamin C is water-soluble and destroyed by heat. Brief steaming limits both. Bicarbonate of soda (alkaline) destroys vitamin C, and soaking in water leaches it out."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"3 eetlepels + 2 teelepels = ___ ml","en":"3 tablespoons + 2 teaspoons = ___ ml"},"answers":{"af":["55","55 ml"],"en":["55","55 ml"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["45","75","25"],"en":["45","75","25"]}},"explain":{"af":"3 × 15 ml = 45 ml en 2 × 5 ml = 10 ml, dus 45 + 10 = 55 ml. 45 vergeet die teelepels; 25 gebruik 5 ml vir albei lepels.","en":"3 × 15 ml = 45 ml and 2 × 5 ml = 10 ml, so 45 + 10 = 55 ml. 45 forgets the teaspoons; 25 uses 5 ml for both spoons."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die kok het 'n taai, goedkoop snit soos beesskenkel. Watter metode is die beste?","en":"The chef has a tough, cheap cut such as beef shin. Which method is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Rooster","en":"Grilling"},{"af":"Smoor","en":"Braising"},{"af":"Sauté","en":"Sautéing"},{"af":"Roerbraai","en":"Stir-frying"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Taai snitte het baie bindweefsel wat net sag word met stadige, nat hitte. Smoor (eers bruin, dan stadig in vloeistof) is ideaal. Rooster, sauté en roerbraai is vinnige metodes vir sagte snitte.","en":"Tough cuts have lots of connective tissue that only becomes tender with slow, moist heat. Braising (brown first, then slowly in liquid) is ideal. Grilling, sautéing and stir-frying are quick methods for tender cuts."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi se muffins is droog en swaar. Sy het die maatkoppie in die meelsak gedruk en die meel vasgedruk. Wat het verkeerd gegaan?","en":"Thandi's muffins are dry and heavy. She pushed the measuring cup into the flour bag and packed the flour down. What went wrong?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy het te veel meel gebruik, want vasgedrukte meel weeg meer per koppie","en":"She used too much flour, because packed flour weighs more per cup"},{"af":"Sy het te min meel gebruik, want die koppie was nie vol nie","en":"She used too little flour, because the cup wasn't full"},{"af":"Sy moes die meel eers verhit voordat sy dit meet","en":"She should have heated the flour before measuring it"},{"af":"Sy moes die koppie op ooghoogte gehou het","en":"She should have held the cup at eye level"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vasgedrukte meel pak digter, dus kry jy meer meel in 'n koppie as wat die resep bedoel. Skep die meel met 'n lepel in en maak gelyk. Ooghoogte geld vir vloeistowwe in 'n maatbeker.","en":"Packed flour sits more densely, so you get more flour in a cup than the recipe intends. Spoon the flour in and level off. Eye level applies to liquids in a measuring jug."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Resep vir 8 porsies gebruik 200 g botter. Vir 20 porsies het jy ___ g botter nodig.","en":"A recipe for 8 portions uses 200 g butter. For 20 portions you need ___ g butter."},"answers":{"af":["500","500 g"],"en":["500","500 g"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["4 000","1 600","220"],"en":["4 000","1 600","220"]}},"explain":{"af":"Faktor = 20 ÷ 8 = 2,5, dus 200 g × 2,5 = 500 g. 4 000 g is 200 × 20 en 1 600 g is 200 × 8 – albei gebruik die verkeerde faktor.","en":"Factor = 20 ÷ 8 = 2.5, so 200 g × 2.5 = 500 g. 4 000 g is 200 × 20 and 1 600 g is 200 × 8 – both use the wrong factor."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kok kook ertjies 25 minute in baie water en gooi die water weg. Watter aanbeveling sal die meeste voedingstowwe red?","en":"A cook boils peas for 25 minutes in plenty of water and throws the water away. Which recommendation will save the most nutrients?"},"options":[{"af":"Kook dit nog langer sodat dit sagter en makliker verteerbaar is","en":"Cook them even longer so that they are softer and easier to digest"},{"af":"Gebruik meer water sodat die vitamiene verdun word","en":"Use more water so that the vitamins are diluted"},{"af":"Voeg sout aan die begin by sodat die vitamiene in die ertjies bly","en":"Add salt at the start so that the vitamins stay in the peas"},{"af":"Stoom dit of kook dit kort in min water met 'n deksel en gebruik die kookwater in 'n sous","en":"Steam them or boil them briefly in little water with a lid and use the cooking water in a sauce"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die B-vitamiene en vitamien C los in water op en vitamien C word deur hitte vernietig. Min water, kort kooktyd, 'n deksel en die kookwater hergebruik, beperk die verlies. Meer water en langer kook maak dit erger.","en":"The B vitamins and vitamin C dissolve in water, and vitamin C is destroyed by heat. Little water, a short cooking time, a lid and reusing the cooking water limit the loss. More water and longer cooking make it worse."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-vrugte","title":{"af":"Vrugte","en":"Fruit"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal vrugte kan klassifiseer, hul voedingswaarde en gehaltepunte ken, verbruining kan voorkom en 'n geskikte gaarmaakmetode kan kies.","en":"You will be able to classify fruit, know their nutritional value and quality points, prevent browning and choose a suitable cooking method."},"summary":{"af":"## Klassifikasie van vrugte\n\n| Groep | Kenmerk | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sitrusvrugte | Dik skil met geurige olie, sappige segmente, suur | Lemoene, nartjies, suurlemoene, pomelo's |\n| Steenvrugte | Een harde pit (steen) in die middel | Perskes, appelkose, pruime, mango's, kersies |\n| Kernvrugte | 'n Klokhuis met pitte in die middel | Appels, pere |\n| Bessies | Klein, sag, dikwels baie klein saadjies | Aarbeie, bloubessies, druiwe |\n| Tropiese vrugte | Groei in warm, vogtige streke | Piesangs, pynappels, papajas, lietsjies, koejawels |\n| Meloene | Groot, baie sappig, harde skil | Waatlemoen, spanspek |\n| Gedroogde vrugte | Die meeste water is verwyder | Rosyntjies, droë appelkose |\n\nDie Brits-omgewing is 'n bekende sitrusstreek – in die winter sien jy die boorde vol lemoene en nartjies.\n\n## Voedingswaarde\n\n- **Vitamien C:** sitrus, koejawels en aarbeie. Nodig vir gesonde vel en tandvleis, weerstand teen siektes en die opname van yster. Dit is wateroplosbaar en word deur hitte en suurstof vernietig.\n- **Betakaroteen** (die liggaam maak vitamien A daarvan): oranje en geel vrugte soos mango, papaja, appelkose en spanspek. Vitamien A is goed vir die oë (nagsig) en vel.\n- **Vesel** (sellulose) in die skil en vleis: help met spysvertering en voorkom hardlywigheid. Eet die skil waar moontlik.\n- **Natuurlike suikers** (fruktose) gee energie, en vrugte bevat **baie water**.\n- Vrugte is **laag in vet** (die avokado is 'n uitsondering).\n- Gedroogde vrugte is 'n gekonsentreerde bron van suiker, energie en vesel, maar die meeste vitamien C gaan tydens droging verlore.\n\n## Gehaltepunte by aankoop\n\n- Ferm, met 'n helder kleur wat tipies van die vrug is.\n- Geen kneusplekke, sagte kolle, skimmel of skade aan die skil nie.\n- **Swaar vir sy grootte** – dit beteken dit is sappig.\n- 'n Aangename, vrugtige reuk as dit ryp is.\n- Koop vrugte **in seisoen**: dit is goedkoper, vars en die lekkerste.\n- Koop net soveel as wat jy betyds kan gebruik.\n\n## Berging\n\n- Bêre die meeste **ryp vrugte in die yskas** (in die groentelaai): koue vertraag ryping en bederf.\n- **Piesangs** bly by **kamertemperatuur** – in die yskas word die skil swart.\n- Laat **onryp** vrugte (avokado's, perskes, pere) by kamertemperatuur ryp word.\n- Ryp piesangs en appels gee **etileengas** af, wat ander vrugte vinniger laat ryp word. Bêre hulle apart – of sit 'n harde avokado saam met 'n piesang in 'n papiersak as jy wil hê dit moet vinniger ryp word.\n- **Was vrugte net voor gebruik**, nie voor berging nie – vog veroorsaak skimmel.\n- Verwyder vrot vrugte dadelik; bêre gedroogde vrugte in 'n lugdigte houer op 'n koel, droë plek.\n\n## Ensiematiese verbruining\n\nGesnyde appels, pere, piesangs en avokado's word bruin omdat **ensieme** in die beskadigde selle met die **suurstof** in die lug reageer. Dit lyk onaantreklik en die smaak verander.\n\n**Hoe om dit te voorkom:**\n\n1. **Suur** – sprinkel suurlemoen-, lemoen- of pynappelsap oor; die suur vertraag die ensieme.\n2. **Bedek of dompel onder** – kleefplastiek, of onder water, hou die suurstof weg.\n3. **Suikerstroop** – bedek die vrugte en hou lug weg.\n4. **Blansjeer** – die hitte vernietig die ensieme (bv. voor jy vrugte vries).\n5. Gebruik 'n **vlekvrystaalmes**; 'n koolstofstaal- of ystermes versnel die verbruining.\n6. Sny die vrugte so kort moontlik voor diens en hou dit koud.\n\n## Effek van hitte\n\n- Die **sellulose** in die selwande word sag, sodat die vrugte sag word en kan opbreek.\n- **Vitamien C** gaan verlore (hittegevoelig en wateroplosbaar).\n- Die **kleur** verbleik of verander, en die geur verander.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kook vrugte in **suikerstroop** as jy wil hê dit moet sy vorm behou (geposjeerde pere). Kook dit in water en voeg die suiker aan die einde by as jy 'n puree of appelmoes wil maak – in gewone water trek water in die selle in sodat hulle bars.\n\n## Gaarmaakmetodes en geregte\n\n- **Vars vrugteslaai** – eweredige, happiegrootte stukke; doop appel en piesang in suurlemoensap.\n- **Gestoofde of geposjeerde vrugte** – stadig in suikerstroop, bv. geposjeerde pere.\n- **Gebakte appels** – klokhuis uit, gevul met rosyntjies, bruinsuiker en kaneel.\n- **Geroosterde pynappel** – die suiker karamelliseer en gee 'n ryk geur.\n- **Vrugtepoffertjies** – vrugte in bedekkingsbeslag gedoop en in diep vet gebraai, bv. piesangpoffertjies.\n- **Puree en coulis** – 'n gladde vrugtesous, bv. aarbeicoulis oor roomys.\n- **Smoothies** – vrugte saam met jogurt of melk fyngemaak.\n- **Vrugtesosaties** – stukkies vrugte aan 'n stokkie vir 'n buffet of braai.\n\n## Gebruik op die spyskaart\n\nVrugte word by **ontbyt** (vars vrugte, sap, vrugte met jogurt), as **voorgereg** (spanspek met ham), as **garnering** (suurlemoenskyfies, lemoenwiggies) en in **nageregte** (vrugteslaai, tert, poeding) gebruik.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders sê vrugte word bruin weens bakterieë. Dit is **ensieme en suurstof** – dit is nie bederf nie.","en":"## Classification of fruit\n\n| Group | Characteristic | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Citrus fruit | Thick peel with fragrant oil, juicy segments, acidic | Oranges, naartjies, lemons, grapefruit |\n| Stone fruit (drupes) | One hard pit (stone) in the centre | Peaches, apricots, plums, mangoes, cherries |\n| Pome fruit | A core with pips in the centre | Apples, pears |\n| Berries | Small, soft, often with many tiny seeds | Strawberries, blueberries, grapes |\n| Tropical fruit | Grow in warm, humid regions | Bananas, pineapples, papayas, litchis, guavas |\n| Melons | Large, very juicy, hard rind | Watermelon, spanspek |\n| Dried fruit | Most of the water has been removed | Raisins, dried apricots |\n\nThe Brits area is a well-known citrus region – in winter you see the orchards full of oranges and naartjies.\n\n## Nutritional value\n\n- **Vitamin C:** citrus, guavas and strawberries. Needed for healthy skin and gums, resistance to illness and the absorption of iron. It is water-soluble and destroyed by heat and oxygen.\n- **Beta-carotene** (the body makes vitamin A from it): orange and yellow fruit such as mango, papaya, apricots and spanspek. Vitamin A is good for the eyes (night vision) and skin.\n- **Fibre** (cellulose) in the peel and flesh: helps digestion and prevents constipation. Eat the peel where possible.\n- **Natural sugars** (fructose) give energy, and fruit contains **a lot of water**.\n- Fruit is **low in fat** (the avocado is an exception).\n- Dried fruit is a concentrated source of sugar, energy and fibre, but most of the vitamin C is lost during drying.\n\n## Quality points when buying\n\n- Firm, with a bright colour typical of the fruit.\n- No bruises, soft spots, mould or damage to the skin.\n- **Heavy for its size** – this means it is juicy.\n- A pleasant, fruity smell when ripe.\n- Buy fruit **in season**: it is cheaper, fresh and tastes best.\n- Buy only as much as you can use in time.\n\n## Storage\n\n- Store most **ripe fruit in the fridge** (in the crisper): cold slows down ripening and spoilage.\n- **Bananas** stay at **room temperature** – in the fridge the skin turns black.\n- Let **unripe** fruit (avocados, peaches, pears) ripen at room temperature.\n- Ripe bananas and apples give off **ethylene gas**, which makes other fruit ripen faster. Store them separately – or put a hard avocado in a paper bag with a banana if you want it to ripen faster.\n- **Wash fruit just before use**, not before storage – moisture causes mould.\n- Remove rotten fruit immediately; store dried fruit in an airtight container in a cool, dry place.\n\n## Enzymatic browning\n\nCut apples, pears, bananas and avocados turn brown because **enzymes** in the damaged cells react with **oxygen** in the air. It looks unattractive and the taste changes.\n\n**How to prevent it:**\n\n1. **Acid** – sprinkle lemon, orange or pineapple juice over; the acid slows the enzymes.\n2. **Cover or submerge** – cling wrap, or under water, keeps the oxygen away.\n3. **Sugar syrup** – covers the fruit and keeps air out.\n4. **Blanching** – the heat destroys the enzymes (e.g. before you freeze fruit).\n5. Use a **stainless-steel knife**; a carbon-steel or iron knife speeds up browning.\n6. Cut the fruit as close to service as possible and keep it cold.\n\n## Effect of heat\n\n- The **cellulose** in the cell walls softens, so the fruit becomes soft and may break up.\n- **Vitamin C** is lost (heat-sensitive and water-soluble).\n- The **colour** fades or changes, and the flavour changes.\n\n> **Tip:** Cook fruit in **sugar syrup** if you want it to keep its shape (poached pears). Cook it in water and add the sugar at the end if you want a purée or apple sauce – in plain water, water moves into the cells so that they burst.\n\n## Cooking methods and dishes\n\n- **Fresh fruit salad** – even, bite-size pieces; dip apple and banana in lemon juice.\n- **Stewed or poached fruit** – slowly in sugar syrup, e.g. poached pears.\n- **Baked apples** – cored, filled with raisins, brown sugar and cinnamon.\n- **Grilled pineapple** – the sugar caramelises and gives a rich flavour.\n- **Fruit fritters** – fruit dipped in coating batter and deep-fried, e.g. banana fritters.\n- **Purée and coulis** – a smooth fruit sauce, e.g. strawberry coulis over ice cream.\n- **Smoothies** – fruit blended with yoghurt or milk.\n- **Fruit kebabs** – pieces of fruit on a skewer for a buffet or braai.\n\n## Uses on the menu\n\nFruit is used at **breakfast** (fresh fruit, juice, fruit with yoghurt), as a **starter** (spanspek with ham), as a **garnish** (lemon slices, orange wedges) and in **desserts** (fruit salad, tart, pudding).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners say fruit turns brown because of bacteria. It is **enzymes and oxygen** – it is not spoilage."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sitrusvrugte","en":"Citrus fruit"},"def":{"af":"Suur, sappige vrugte met 'n dik, geurige skil en segmente, bv. lemoene, nartjies en suurlemoene; 'n ryk bron van vitamien C.","en":"Acidic, juicy fruit with a thick, fragrant peel and segments, e.g. oranges, naartjies and lemons; a rich source of vitamin C."}},{"term":{"af":"Steenvrugte","en":"Stone fruit (drupes)"},"def":{"af":"Vrugte met een harde pit (steen) in die middel, bv. perskes, appelkose, pruime en kersies.","en":"Fruit with one hard pit (stone) in the centre, e.g. peaches, apricots, plums and cherries."}},{"term":{"af":"Kernvrugte","en":"Pome fruit"},"def":{"af":"Vrugte met 'n klokhuis met pitte in die middel, bv. appels en pere.","en":"Fruit with a core containing pips in the centre, e.g. apples and pears."}},{"term":{"af":"Ensiematiese verbruining","en":"Enzymatic browning"},"def":{"af":"Die bruin verkleuring van gesnyde vrugte wanneer ensieme in die selle met suurstof in die lug reageer.","en":"The brown discolouration of cut fruit when enzymes in the cells react with oxygen in the air."}},{"term":{"af":"Etileengas","en":"Ethylene gas"},"def":{"af":"'n Natuurlike gas wat ryp vrugte soos piesangs en appels afgee en wat ander vrugte vinniger laat ryp word.","en":"A natural gas given off by ripe fruit such as bananas and apples that makes other fruit ripen faster."}},{"term":{"af":"Betakaroteen","en":"Beta-carotene"},"def":{"af":"Die oranje-geel pigment in vrugte soos mango en papaja wat die liggaam in vitamien A omskakel.","en":"The orange-yellow pigment in fruit such as mango and papaya that the body converts into vitamin A."}},{"term":{"af":"Sellulose","en":"Cellulose"},"def":{"af":"Die vesel in die selwande van vrugte; dit help met spysvertering en word sag wanneer vrugte verhit word.","en":"The fibre in the cell walls of fruit; it aids digestion and softens when fruit is heated."}},{"term":{"af":"In seisoen","en":"In season"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd van die jaar wanneer 'n vrug natuurlik geoes word – dan is dit vars, lekker en goedkoper.","en":"The time of year when a fruit is naturally harvested – then it is fresh, tasty and cheaper."}},{"term":{"af":"Posjeer","en":"Poach"},"def":{"af":"Kook saggies in vloeistof wat skaars beweeg, bv. pere in suikerstroop sodat hulle hul vorm behou.","en":"Cook gently in liquid that is barely moving, e.g. pears in sugar syrup so that they keep their shape."}},{"term":{"af":"Coulis","en":"Coulis"},"def":{"af":"'n Dun, gladde puree of sous van vrugte (of groente), bv. aarbeicoulis by 'n nagereg.","en":"A thin, smooth purée or sauce of fruit (or vegetables), e.g. strawberry coulis with a dessert."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer vrugte by 'n padstal","en":"Classify fruit at a farm stall"},"problem":{"af":"'n Padstal buite Brits verkoop lemoene, perskes, pere, bloubessies, pynappels, waatlemoen, rosyntjies, pruime en nartjies. Klassifiseer elke vrug.","en":"A farm stall outside Brits sells oranges, peaches, pears, blueberries, pineapples, watermelon, raisins, plums and naartjies. Classify each fruit."},"steps":[{"af":"Sitrusvrugte (suur, segmente, geurige skil): lemoene en nartjies.","en":"Citrus fruit (acidic, segments, fragrant peel): oranges and naartjies."},{"af":"Steenvrugte (een harde pit): perskes en pruime. Kernvrugte (klokhuis met pitte): pere.","en":"Stone fruit (one hard pit): peaches and plums. Pome fruit (core with pips): pears."},{"af":"Bessies: bloubessies. Tropiese vrugte: pynappels. Meloene: waatlemoen.","en":"Berries: blueberries. Tropical fruit: pineapples. Melons: watermelon."},{"af":"Gedroogde vrugte (die water is verwyder): rosyntjies – dit is gedroogde druiwe.","en":"Dried fruit (the water has been removed): raisins – they are dried grapes."}],"answer":{"af":"Sitrus: lemoene, nartjies; steen: perskes, pruime; kern: pere; bessies: bloubessies; tropies: pynappels; meloen: waatlemoen; gedroog: rosyntjies","en":"Citrus: oranges, naartjies; stone: peaches, plums; pome: pears; berries: blueberries; tropical: pineapples; melon: watermelon; dried: raisins"}},{"title":{"af":"Voorkom verbruining in 'n vrugteslaai","en":"Prevent browning in a fruit salad"},"problem":{"af":"Jy maak om 10:00 'n vrugteslaai met appels en piesangs vir 'n funksie om 13:00. Verduidelik waarom die vrugte bruin word en gee drie maniere om dit te voorkom, met 'n rede vir elkeen.","en":"At 10:00 you make a fruit salad with apples and bananas for a function at 13:00. Explain why the fruit turns brown and give three ways to prevent it, with a reason for each."},"steps":[{"af":"Oorsaak: wanneer jy die vrugte sny, word die selle beskadig en reageer die ensieme met die suurstof in die lug – ensiematiese verbruining.","en":"Cause: when you cut the fruit the cells are damaged and the enzymes react with the oxygen in the air – enzymatic browning."},{"af":"1. Meng die stukke met suurlemoen- of lemoensap: die suur vertraag die ensieme.","en":"1. Mix the pieces with lemon or orange juice: the acid slows down the enzymes."},{"af":"2. Bedek die bak met kleefplastiek en hou dit in die yskas: dit hou suurstof weg en die koue vertraag die ensieme.","en":"2. Cover the bowl with cling wrap and keep it in the fridge: this keeps oxygen out and the cold slows the enzymes."},{"af":"3. Sny die piesangs laaste, kort voor diens, met 'n vlekvrystaalmes: hulle is minder lank aan lug blootgestel en die metaal versnel nie verbruining nie.","en":"3. Cut the bananas last, shortly before service, with a stainless-steel knife: they are exposed to air for less time and the metal doesn't speed up browning."}],"answer":{"af":"Ensieme + suurstof; voorkom met suur, bedek en koud hou, en laat sny met 'n vlekvrystaalmes","en":"Enzymes + oxygen; prevent with acid, covering and chilling, and late cutting with a stainless-steel knife"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies vrugte vir voedingswaarde","en":"Choose fruit for nutritional value"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo wil in die griepseisoen sy weerstand verhoog en sy oë gesond hou. Hy speel ook rugby en wil gesonde energie hê. Watter vrugte moet hy eet en waarom?","en":"Thabo wants to boost his resistance during flu season and keep his eyes healthy. He also plays rugby and wants healthy energy. Which fruit should he eat and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"Weerstand: vitamien C – kies koejawels, lemoene, nartjies of aarbeie. Eet dit vars, want hitte vernietig vitamien C.","en":"Resistance: vitamin C – choose guavas, oranges, naartjies or strawberries. Eat them fresh, because heat destroys vitamin C."},{"af":"Oë: betakaroteen, wat die liggaam in vitamien A omskakel – kies mango, papaja, appelkose of spanspek.","en":"Eyes: beta-carotene, which the body converts into vitamin A – choose mango, papaya, apricots or spanspek."},{"af":"Energie: die natuurlike suikers in vrugte, bv. 'n piesang of 'n handvol rosyntjies. Die vesel help ook met spysvertering.","en":"Energy: the natural sugars in fruit, e.g. a banana or a handful of raisins. The fibre also aids digestion."}],"answer":{"af":"Vitamien C-vrugte (koejawel, sitrus), betakaroteen-vrugte (mango, papaja) en energievrugte (piesang, rosyntjies)","en":"Vitamin C fruit (guava, citrus), beta-carotene fruit (mango, papaya) and energy fruit (banana, raisins)"}},{"title":{"af":"Geposjeerde pere of appelmoes?","en":"Poached pears or apple sauce?"},"problem":{"af":"Die kok wil (a) heel geposjeerde pere vir 'n nagereg en (b) gladde appelmoes by varkvleis maak. Verduidelik hoe hy die suiker vir elkeen moet gebruik.","en":"The chef wants to make (a) whole poached pears for a dessert and (b) smooth apple sauce to go with pork. Explain how he should use the sugar for each."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Posjeer die pere stadig in suikerstroop. Omdat die stroop ook suiker bevat, trek water nie in die selle in nie en die pere behou hul vorm.","en":"(a) Poach the pears slowly in sugar syrup. Because the syrup also contains sugar, water doesn't move into the cells and the pears keep their shape."},{"af":"(b) Kook die appels in 'n bietjie gewone water: water trek in die selle in, die selle bars en die sellulose word sag, sodat dit maklik glad word.","en":"(b) Cook the apples in a little plain water: water moves into the cells, the cells burst and the cellulose softens, so it easily becomes smooth."},{"af":"Voeg die suiker vir die appelmoes eers aan die einde by, en druk of meng dit fyn tot 'n puree.","en":"Add the sugar for the apple sauce only at the end, and mash or blend it to a purée."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Suikerstroop van die begin af – heel pere; (b) eers water, suiker aan die einde – gladde appelmoes","en":"(a) Sugar syrup from the start – whole pears; (b) water first, sugar at the end – smooth apple sauce"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tot watter groep behoort perskes?","en":"To which group do peaches belong?"},"options":[{"af":"Kernvrugte","en":"Pome fruit"},{"af":"Steenvrugte","en":"Stone fruit"},{"af":"Sitrusvrugte","en":"Citrus fruit"},{"af":"Bessies","en":"Berries"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Perske het een harde pit (steen) in die middel, dus is dit 'n steenvrug. Kernvrugte (appels, pere) het 'n klokhuis met pitte.","en":"A peach has one hard pit (stone) in the centre, so it is a stone fruit. Pome fruit (apples, pears) has a core with pips."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Appels en pere is ___, want hulle het 'n klokhuis met pitte.","en":"Apples and pears are ___ fruit, because they have a core with pips."},"answers":{"af":["kernvrugte","kernvrug"],"en":["pome","pome fruit"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["steenvrugte","sitrusvrugte","bessies"],"en":["stone","citrus","tropical"]}},"explain":{"af":"Kernvrugte het 'n klokhuis met pitte in die middel. Steenvrugte het een harde pit.","en":"Pome fruit has a core with pips in the centre. Stone fruit has one hard pit."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Piesangs moet in die yskas gebêre word sodat hulle langer hou.","en":"Bananas should be stored in the fridge so that they last longer."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Piesangs word by kamertemperatuur gebêre – in die yskas word die skil swart. Die meeste ander ryp vrugte hoort wel in die yskas.","en":"False. Bananas are stored at room temperature – in the fridge the skin turns black. Most other ripe fruit does belong in the fridge."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vrug is die beste bron van vitamien C?","en":"Which fruit is the best source of vitamin C?"},"options":[{"af":"Rosyntjies","en":"Raisins"},{"af":"Waatlemoen","en":"Watermelon"},{"af":"Piesang","en":"Banana"},{"af":"Koejawel","en":"Guava"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Koejawels is een van die rykste bronne van vitamien C, saam met sitrus en aarbeie. Rosyntjies het die meeste vitamien C tydens droging verloor.","en":"Guavas are one of the richest sources of vitamin C, together with citrus and strawberries. Raisins lost most of their vitamin C during drying."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die gas wat ryp piesangs en appels afgee en wat ander vrugte vinniger laat ryp word, is ___.","en":"The gas that ripe bananas and apples give off, which makes other fruit ripen faster, is ___."},"answers":{"af":["etileen","etileengas","etileen-gas","etileen gas"],"en":["ethylene","ethylene gas"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koolstofdioksied","suurstof","stikstof"],"en":["carbon dioxide","oxygen","nitrogen"]}},"explain":{"af":"Etileen is 'n natuurlike rypwordingsgas. Bêre piesangs en appels daarom apart van ander vrugte, tensy jy iets doelbewus wil laat ryp word.","en":"Ethylene is a natural ripening gas. So store bananas and apples separately from other fruit, unless you deliberately want something to ripen."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vrug by die regte groep.","en":"Match each fruit to the correct group."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Nartjie","en":"Naartjie"},"r":{"af":"Sitrusvrug","en":"Citrus fruit"}},{"l":{"af":"Appelkoos","en":"Apricot"},"r":{"af":"Steenvrug","en":"Stone fruit"}},{"l":{"af":"Peer","en":"Pear"},"r":{"af":"Kernvrug","en":"Pome fruit"}},{"l":{"af":"Bloubessie","en":"Blueberry"},"r":{"af":"Bessie","en":"Berry"}},{"l":{"af":"Pynappel","en":"Pineapple"},"r":{"af":"Tropiese vrug","en":"Tropical fruit"}}],"explain":{"af":"Kyk na die binnekant: segmente = sitrus, een harde pit = steenvrug, klokhuis met pitte = kernvrug, klein en sag = bessie, groei in warm, vogtige streke = tropies.","en":"Look at the inside: segments = citrus, one hard pit = stone fruit, core with pips = pome fruit, small and soft = berry, grows in warm, humid regions = tropical."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word 'n gesnyde appel bruin?","en":"Why does a cut apple turn brown?"},"options":[{"af":"Bakterieë begin dadelik die appel bederf","en":"Bacteria immediately start spoiling the apple"},{"af":"Die suiker in die appel karamelliseer","en":"The sugar in the apple caramelises"},{"af":"Ensieme in die vrug reageer met suurstof in die lug","en":"Enzymes in the fruit react with oxygen in the air"},{"af":"Die water in die appel verdamp","en":"The water in the apple evaporates"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Dit is ensiematiese verbruining: ensieme in die beskadigde selle reageer met suurstof. Dit is nie bakteriese bederf nie, en karamellisering het hitte nodig.","en":"This is enzymatic browning: enzymes in the damaged cells react with oxygen. It is not bacterial spoilage, and caramelisation needs heat."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Oranje vrugte soos mango en papaja bevat ___, wat die liggaam in vitamien A omskakel.","en":"Orange fruit such as mango and papaya contain ___, which the body converts into vitamin A."},"answers":{"af":["betakaroteen","beta-karoteen","beta karoteen","karoteen"],"en":["beta-carotene","betacarotene","beta carotene","carotene"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vitamien C","vesel","fruktose"],"en":["vitamin C","fibre","fructose"]}},"explain":{"af":"Betakaroteen is die oranje pigment wat die liggaam in vitamien A omskakel – goed vir die oë en vel.","en":"Beta-carotene is the orange pigment that the body converts into vitamin A – good for the eyes and skin."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gehaltepunt wys dat 'n lemoen sappig is?","en":"Which quality point shows that an orange is juicy?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit het 'n paar sagte kolle","en":"It has a few soft spots"},{"af":"Dit voel lig vir sy grootte","en":"It feels light for its size"},{"af":"Die skil is dof met 'n bietjie skimmel","en":"The peel is dull with a little mould"},{"af":"Dit voel swaar vir sy grootte","en":"It feels heavy for its size"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Vrug wat swaar vir sy grootte is, bevat baie sap. 'n Ligte vrug is dikwels droog, en sagte kolle en skimmel is tekens van swak gehalte.","en":"A fruit that is heavy for its size contains a lot of juice. A light fruit is often dry, and soft spots and mould are signs of poor quality."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Blansjeer voorkom verbruining omdat die hitte die ensieme vernietig.","en":"Blanching prevents browning because the heat destroys the enzymes."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Sonder werkende ensieme kan die reaksie met suurstof nie plaasvind nie. Daarom word vrugte dikwels geblansjeer voordat dit gevries word.","en":"True. Without working enzymes the reaction with oxygen cannot take place. That is why fruit is often blanched before it is frozen."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy maak 'n vrugteslaai vir 'n funksie om 18:00. Wat is die beste manier om die piesangskyfies wit te hou?","en":"You are making a fruit salad for a function at 18:00. What is the best way to keep the banana slices white?"},"options":[{"af":"Sny dit kort voor diens met 'n vlekvrystaalmes en meng dit met suurlemoensap","en":"Cut them shortly before service with a stainless-steel knife and mix them with lemon juice"},{"af":"Sny dit soggens en laat dit onbedek op die toonbank staan","en":"Cut them in the morning and leave them uncovered on the counter"},{"af":"Vries die skyfies sodat hulle hard word","en":"Freeze the slices so that they become hard"},{"af":"Sit die skyfies in 'n aluminiumbak sodat die metaal die ensieme stop","en":"Put the slices in an aluminium bowl so that the metal stops the enzymes"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Laat sny beperk die tyd aan suurstof, die suur vertraag die ensieme en vlekvrystaal versnel nie verbruining nie. Onbedekte skyfies word bruin, bevrore piesang word pap en donker wanneer dit ontdooi, en metaal stop nie die ensieme nie.","en":"Cutting late limits the time exposed to oxygen, the acid slows the enzymes and stainless steel doesn't speed up browning. Uncovered slices turn brown, frozen banana goes mushy and dark when it thaws, and metal does not stop the enzymes."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Dun, gladde vrugtesous, bv. van aarbeie, wat oor 'n nagereg geskep word, is 'n ___.","en":"A thin, smooth fruit sauce, e.g. made from strawberries, that is spooned over a dessert is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["coulis"],"en":["coulis"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["roux","marinade","kompot"],"en":["roux","marinade","compote"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Coulis is 'n gladde puree of sous van vrugte of groente. 'n Roux is botter en meel vir witsous, en kompot is gestoofde vrugte in stukke.","en":"A coulis is a smooth purée or sauce of fruit or vegetables. A roux is butter and flour for white sauce, and compote is stewed fruit in pieces."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato het pere in gewone water gekook en hulle het opgebreek, maar sy wou heel pere hê. Wat is die beste verduideliking?","en":"Lerato cooked pears in plain water and they broke up, but she wanted whole pears. What is the best explanation?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy moes die pere eers met suurlemoensap ingesmeer het","en":"She should have rubbed the pears with lemon juice first"},{"af":"Water het in die selle ingetrek sodat hulle gebars het; sy moes die pere in suikerstroop geposjeer het","en":"Water moved into the cells so that they burst; she should have poached the pears in sugar syrup"},{"af":"Sy het te veel suiker by die water gevoeg","en":"She added too much sugar to the water"},{"af":"Pere is kernvrugte en kan nooit heel gaargemaak word nie","en":"Pears are pome fruit and can never be cooked whole"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In gewone water trek water in die selle in, die selle bars en die vrug word pap. Suikerstroop keer dit, sodat die pere hul vorm behou. Suurlemoensap voorkom net verbruining.","en":"In plain water, water moves into the cells, the cells burst and the fruit turns mushy. Sugar syrup prevents this, so the pears keep their shape. Lemon juice only prevents browning."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hitte maak die ___ in die selwande van vrugte sag, daarom word gestoofde vrugte sag.","en":"Heat softens the ___ in the cell walls of fruit, which is why stewed fruit becomes soft."},"answers":{"af":["sellulose"],"en":["cellulose"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["proteïen","gluten","vet"],"en":["protein","gluten","fat"]}},"explain":{"af":"Sellulose is die vesel in die selwande. Wanneer dit sag word, verloor die vrug sy stewigheid. Gluten is 'n koringproteïen en kom nie in vrugte voor nie.","en":"Cellulose is the fibre in the cell walls. When it softens, the fruit loses its firmness. Gluten is a wheat protein and isn't found in fruit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dis Julie in Brits. Watter vrugte sal die vars, goedkoopste keuse vir 'n gastehuis se ontbytbuffet wees?","en":"It is July in Brits. Which fruit will be the freshest, cheapest choice for a guest house's breakfast buffet?"},"options":[{"af":"Perskes en appelkose","en":"Peaches and apricots"},{"af":"Waatlemoen en lietsjies","en":"Watermelon and litchis"},{"af":"Lemoene en nartjies","en":"Oranges and naartjies"},{"af":"Kersies en pruime","en":"Cherries and plums"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sitrus word in Suid-Afrika in die winter geoes, en Brits lê in 'n sitrusstreek – dus is lemoene en nartjies in Julie in seisoen, vars en goedkoper. Die ander is somervrugte.","en":"Citrus is harvested in winter in South Africa, and Brits lies in a citrus region – so oranges and naartjies are in season, fresh and cheaper in July. The others are summer fruit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter EEN van hierdie bergingspraktyke in 'n gastehuiskombuis is VERKEERD?","en":"Which ONE of these storage practices in a guest-house kitchen is WRONG?"},"options":[{"af":"Bêre gedroogde vrugte in 'n lugdigte houer op 'n koel, droë plek","en":"Store dried fruit in an airtight container in a cool, dry place"},{"af":"Laat harde, onryp avokado's by kamertemperatuur ryp word","en":"Let hard, unripe avocados ripen at room temperature"},{"af":"Hou piesangs by kamertemperatuur buite die yskas","en":"Keep bananas at room temperature outside the fridge"},{"af":"Was die aarbeie sodra hulle afgelewer word en bêre hulle nat in 'n toe bak in die yskas","en":"Wash the strawberries as soon as they are delivered and store them wet in a closed container in the fridge"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vrugte word net voor gebruik gewas: nat aarbeie in 'n toe bak begin gou skimmel. Die ander drie praktyke is korrek.","en":"Fruit is washed just before use: wet strawberries in a closed container soon go mouldy. The other three practices are correct."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t1-meelmengsels-beslag","title":{"af":"Vinnige meelmengsels en beslag: skons, muffins, pannekoek en plaatkoekies","en":"Quick flour mixtures and batters: scones, muffins, pancakes and crumpets"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die invryf- en muffinmetode kan beskryf, die rol van gluten en rysmiddels kan verduidelik en foute in skons, muffins en beslag kan herken en regstel.","en":"You will be able to describe the rubbing-in and muffin methods, explain the role of gluten and raising agents, and recognise and correct faults in scones, muffins and batters."},"summary":{"af":"## Meelsoorte\n\n| Meel | Kenmerk | Gebruik |\n|---|---|---|\n| Koekmeel | Fyn en wit, minder proteïen | Koek, skons, muffins, pannekoek |\n| Bruismeel | Koekmeel met bakpoeier (en sout) bygevoeg | Skons en koeke – moenie ekstra bakpoeier byvoeg tensy die resep dit vra nie |\n| Broodmeel | Meer proteïen, dus meer gluten | Gisbrood |\n| Volkoringmeel | Bevat die semels en kiem: meer vesel | Gesonder, maar 'n swaarder produk wat meer vloeistof absorbeer |\n\n## Gluten\n\n**Gluten** vorm wanneer die **proteïene** in koringmeel met vloeistof gemeng word. Dit is 'n elastiese netwerk wat gas vasvang. **Hoe meer jy meng of knie, hoe meer gluten vorm en hoe taaier word die produk.** Vir brood knie jy baie; vir vinnige meelmengsels (skons, muffins, pannekoek) wil jy min gluten hê – meng dus liggies en kortliks.\n\n## Rysmiddels\n\n'n **Rysmiddel** laat 'n mengsel rys sodat dit lig en luguitig word.\n\n- **Lug** – word ingewerk deur te sif, te klits of in te vryf.\n- **Stoom** – die vloeistof in die mengsel word in 'n warm oond stoom en sit uit (belangrik in beslag).\n- **Bakpoeier** – koeksoda (alkalies) plus 'n suur. Met vloeistof en hitte vorm dit **koolstofdioksied (CO₂)**; die gasborrels laat die mengsel rys en die hitte laat dit om die borrels stol.\n- **Koeksoda** (natriumbikarbonaat) alleen het 'n suur nodig, bv. karringmelk, suurmelk, jogurt of suurlemoensap. **Te veel koeksoda gee 'n seperige smaak en 'n geel kleur.**\n\nHulle heet **vinnige** meelmengsels omdat chemiese rysmiddels dadelik begin werk – jy hoef nie, soos met gis, te wag dat dit rys nie. Bak dit dus kort nadat jy gemeng het, anders ontsnap die CO₂.\n\n## Die invryfmetode (skons)\n\n1. Voorverhit die oond tot **200–220 °C** en berei die bakplaat voor.\n2. **Sif** die meel, bakpoeier en sout – dit werk lug in.\n3. **Vryf koue botter met die vingerpunte** in die meel totdat dit soos **fyn broodkrummels** lyk. Lig die mengsel terwyl jy vryf om lug in te werk.\n4. Maak 'n holte, voeg die vloeistof (eier en melk) by en meng **liggies** met 'n mes tot 'n sagte deeg.\n5. **Knie liggies** – net 'n paar keer.\n6. Rol of druk die deeg ongeveer **2 cm dik** uit.\n7. Druk die snyer **reguit af** – moenie dit **draai** nie, anders rys die skons skeef.\n8. Verf met eierwas of melk en bak in 'n **warm oond** tot goudbruin.\n\n> **Hoekom koue botter en vingerpunte?** Warm botter smelt in die meel en maak die skons vetterig en swaar. Jou vingerpunte is die koelste deel van jou hand.\n\n**'n Goeie skon** is goed gerys, het reguit sye, 'n goudbruin bokant en 'n ligte, sagte tekstuur.\n\n## Die muffinmetode\n\n1. **Meng die droë bestanddele** (gesifte meel, bakpoeier, sout, suiker) in een bak.\n2. **Meng die nat bestanddele** (eier, melk, gesmelte botter of olie) **apart**.\n3. Gooi die nat bestanddele **in een keer** by die droë bestanddele.\n4. Roer **net totdat dit klam is** – 'n klonterige beslag is reg!\n5. Skep in gesmeerde muffinpanne en bak tot goudbruin en 'n toetspen skoon uitkom.\n\n**'n Goeie muffin** het 'n **afgeronde** (nie gepunte) goudbruin bokant, 'n eweredige krummel **sonder tonnels**, en is klam en sag.\n\n## Foute en oorsake\n\n| Fout | Oorsaak |\n|---|---|\n| Tonnels (lang gate), gepunte bokant, taai | **Te veel gemeng** – te veel gluten |\n| Plat en swaar | Te min rysmiddel of 'n oond wat nie warm genoeg is nie |\n| Skeef gerys (skons) | Die snyer is gedraai of die deeg is ongelyk uitgerol |\n| Seperige smaak, geel kleur | Te veel koeksoda |\n\n## Beslag\n\n'n **Beslag** is 'n mengsel van meel en vloeistof (melk, eiers) wat dun genoeg is om te gooi of van 'n lepel af te val.\n\n| Soort | Dikte | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Gietbeslag | Dun, soos room | Pannekoek, crêpes |\n| Druppelbeslag (skepbeslag) | Dikker, val van 'n lepel af | Plaatkoekies, druppelskons |\n| Bedekkingsbeslag | Dik genoeg om kos te bedek | Vis, vrugtepoffertjies |\n\n**Wafels** word van 'n beslag in 'n wafelyster gebak.\n\n### Reëls vir 'n gladde beslag\n\n- **Sif** die meel en sout en maak 'n **holte** in die middel.\n- Voeg die eier en 'n bietjie vloeistof in die holte en klits; voeg die res van die vloeistof **geleidelik** by – so vermy jy klonte.\n- Laat pannekoekbeslag ongeveer **30 minute rus**: die styselkorrels swel en die gluten ontspan, sodat die pannekoek sag en dun is.\n- Gebruik 'n **warm, liggies gesmeerde** pan.\n- Plaatkoekies: skep die beslag in die pan en **draai dit om wanneer die borreltjies bo bars**.\n- Suid-Afrikaanse styl: pannekoek met **kaneelsuiker** en suurlemoensap – gewild by kerkbasaars en rugbydae.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om al die vloeistof op een slag by die meel te gooi. Die meel vorm klonte wat moeilik uitklits.","en":"## Types of flour\n\n| Flour | Characteristic | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cake flour | Fine and white, less protein | Cake, scones, muffins, pancakes |\n| Self-raising flour | Cake flour with baking powder (and salt) added | Scones and cakes – don't add extra baking powder unless the recipe asks for it |\n| Bread flour | More protein, so more gluten | Yeast bread |\n| Whole-wheat flour | Contains the bran and germ: more fibre | Healthier, but a heavier product that absorbs more liquid |\n\n## Gluten\n\n**Gluten** forms when the **proteins** in wheat flour are mixed with liquid. It is an elastic network that traps gas. **The more you mix or knead, the more gluten forms and the tougher the product becomes.** For bread you knead a lot; for quick flour mixtures (scones, muffins, pancakes) you want little gluten – so mix lightly and briefly.\n\n## Raising agents\n\nA **raising agent** makes a mixture rise so that it becomes light and airy.\n\n- **Air** – worked in by sifting, whisking or rubbing in.\n- **Steam** – the liquid in the mixture turns to steam in a hot oven and expands (important in batters).\n- **Baking powder** – bicarbonate of soda (alkaline) plus an acid. With liquid and heat it forms **carbon dioxide (CO₂)**; the gas bubbles make the mixture rise and the heat sets it around the bubbles.\n- **Bicarbonate of soda** on its own needs an acid, e.g. buttermilk, sour milk, yoghurt or lemon juice. **Too much bicarbonate of soda gives a soapy taste and a yellow colour.**\n\nThey are called **quick** flour mixtures because chemical raising agents start working immediately – you don't have to wait for it to rise, as with yeast. So bake soon after mixing, or the CO₂ escapes.\n\n## The rubbing-in method (scones)\n\n1. Preheat the oven to **200–220 °C** and prepare the baking tray.\n2. **Sift** the flour, baking powder and salt – this adds air.\n3. **Rub cold butter into the flour with your fingertips** until it looks like **fine breadcrumbs**. Lift the mixture as you rub to add air.\n4. Make a well, add the liquid (egg and milk) and mix **lightly** with a knife to a soft dough.\n5. **Knead lightly** – just a few times.\n6. Roll or pat the dough out about **2 cm thick**.\n7. Press the cutter **straight down** – don't **twist** it, or the scones rise skew.\n8. Brush with egg wash or milk and bake in a **hot oven** until golden brown.\n\n> **Why cold butter and fingertips?** Warm butter melts into the flour and makes the scones greasy and heavy. Your fingertips are the coolest part of your hand.\n\n**A good scone** is well risen, has straight sides, a golden-brown top and a light, soft texture.\n\n## The muffin method\n\n1. **Mix the dry ingredients** (sifted flour, baking powder, salt, sugar) in one bowl.\n2. **Mix the wet ingredients** (egg, milk, melted butter or oil) **separately**.\n3. Pour the wet ingredients into the dry ingredients **all at once**.\n4. Stir **only until just moistened** – a lumpy batter is correct!\n5. Spoon into greased muffin pans and bake until golden brown and a skewer comes out clean.\n\n**A good muffin** has a **rounded** (not peaked) golden-brown top, an even crumb **without tunnels**, and is moist and tender.\n\n## Faults and causes\n\n| Fault | Cause |\n|---|---|\n| Tunnels (long holes), peaked top, tough | **Overmixing** – too much gluten |\n| Flat and heavy | Too little raising agent or an oven that isn't hot enough |\n| Risen skew (scones) | The cutter was twisted or the dough was rolled unevenly |\n| Soapy taste, yellow colour | Too much bicarbonate of soda |\n\n## Batters\n\nA **batter** is a mixture of flour and liquid (milk, eggs) that is thin enough to pour or to drop from a spoon.\n\n| Type | Thickness | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pouring batter | Thin, like cream | Pancakes, crêpes |\n| Dropping batter | Thicker, drops from a spoon | Crumpets (flapjacks), drop scones |\n| Coating batter | Thick enough to coat food | Fish, fruit fritters |\n\n**Waffles** are cooked from a batter in a waffle iron.\n\n### Rules for a smooth batter\n\n- **Sift** the flour and salt and make a **well** in the centre.\n- Add the egg and a little liquid to the well and whisk; add the rest of the liquid **gradually** – this way you avoid lumps.\n- Let pancake batter **rest for about 30 minutes**: the starch granules swell and the gluten relaxes, so the pancakes are tender and thin.\n- Use a **hot, lightly greased** pan.\n- Crumpets: drop the batter into the pan and **turn them when the bubbles on top burst**.\n- South African style: pancakes with **cinnamon sugar** and lemon juice – popular at church bazaars and rugby days.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Pouring all the liquid onto the flour at once. The flour forms lumps that are hard to whisk out."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Gluten","en":"Gluten"},"def":{"af":"'n Elastiese netwerk wat vorm wanneer die proteïene in koringmeel met vloeistof gemeng word; meer meng gee meer gluten en 'n taaier produk.","en":"An elastic network that forms when the proteins in wheat flour are mixed with liquid; more mixing gives more gluten and a tougher product."}},{"term":{"af":"Rysmiddel","en":"Raising agent"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof of proses (lug, stoom, bakpoeier, koeksoda) wat 'n mengsel laat rys sodat dit lig is.","en":"A substance or process (air, steam, baking powder, bicarbonate of soda) that makes a mixture rise so that it is light."}},{"term":{"af":"Bakpoeier","en":"Baking powder"},"def":{"af":"'n Chemiese rysmiddel van koeksoda en 'n suur wat met vloeistof en hitte koolstofdioksied vorm.","en":"A chemical raising agent of bicarbonate of soda and an acid that forms carbon dioxide with liquid and heat."}},{"term":{"af":"Koeksoda","en":"Bicarbonate of soda"},"def":{"af":"Natriumbikarbonaat; 'n alkaliese rysmiddel wat 'n suur soos karringmelk nodig het. Te veel gee 'n seperige smaak en geel kleur.","en":"Sodium bicarbonate; an alkaline raising agent that needs an acid such as buttermilk. Too much gives a soapy taste and a yellow colour."}},{"term":{"af":"Bruismeel","en":"Self-raising flour"},"def":{"af":"Koekmeel waarby bakpoeier (en sout) reeds gevoeg is.","en":"Cake flour to which baking powder (and salt) has already been added."}},{"term":{"af":"Invryfmetode","en":"Rubbing-in method"},"def":{"af":"Koue botter word met die vingerpunte in die meel gevryf tot dit soos fyn broodkrummels lyk; gebruik vir skons.","en":"Cold butter is rubbed into the flour with the fingertips until it looks like fine breadcrumbs; used for scones."}},{"term":{"af":"Muffinmetode","en":"Muffin method"},"def":{"af":"Die droë en nat bestanddele word apart gemeng, dan saamgevoeg en net geroer totdat dit klam is.","en":"The dry and wet ingredients are mixed separately, then combined and stirred only until just moistened."}},{"term":{"af":"Tonnels","en":"Tunnels"},"def":{"af":"Lang, smal gate in 'n muffin wat ontstaan wanneer die beslag te veel gemeng is.","en":"Long, narrow holes in a muffin that form when the batter has been overmixed."}},{"term":{"af":"Beslag","en":"Batter"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel van meel en vloeistof (melk, eiers) wat dun genoeg is om te gooi of van 'n lepel af te val.","en":"A mixture of flour and liquid (milk, eggs) that is thin enough to pour or drop from a spoon."}},{"term":{"af":"Gietbeslag","en":"Pouring batter"},"def":{"af":"'n Dun beslag, soos room, wat gegooi kan word; gebruik vir pannekoek en crêpes.","en":"A thin batter, like cream, that can be poured; used for pancakes and crêpes."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Beskryf die invryfmetode","en":"Describe the rubbing-in method"},"problem":{"af":"'n Teetuin by Hartbeespoortdam wil kaasskons bedien. Beskryf die invryfmetode in die regte volgorde en gee 'n rede vir twee van die stappe.","en":"A tea garden at Hartbeespoort Dam wants to serve cheese scones. Describe the rubbing-in method in the correct order and give a reason for two of the steps."},"steps":[{"af":"Voorverhit die oond (200–220 °C). Sif die meel, bakpoeier en sout – sif werk lug in.","en":"Preheat the oven (200–220 °C). Sift the flour, baking powder and salt – sifting adds air."},{"af":"Vryf koue botter met die vingerpunte in tot dit soos fyn broodkrummels lyk, en meng die gerasperde kaas in. Rede: koue botter smelt nie, sodat die skons lig en nie vetterig is nie.","en":"Rub in cold butter with the fingertips until it looks like fine breadcrumbs, and mix in the grated cheese. Reason: cold butter doesn't melt, so the scones are light and not greasy."},{"af":"Voeg die eier-en-melkmengsel by, meng liggies tot 'n sagte deeg en knie net 'n paar keer.","en":"Add the egg-and-milk mixture, mix lightly to a soft dough and knead only a few times."},{"af":"Rol ongeveer 2 cm dik uit en druk die snyer reguit af sonder om te draai. Rede: draai seël die kante, sodat die skons skeef rys.","en":"Roll out about 2 cm thick and press the cutter straight down without twisting. Reason: twisting seals the edges, so the scones rise skew."},{"af":"Verf met eierwas en bak in die warm oond tot goudbruin.","en":"Brush with egg wash and bake in the hot oven until golden brown."}],"answer":{"af":"Sif → vryf koue botter in → voeg vloeistof by en meng liggies → knie liggies → rol 2 cm dik → sny reguit af → glasuur → bak warm","en":"Sift → rub in cold butter → add liquid and mix lightly → knead lightly → roll 2 cm thick → cut straight down → glaze → bake hot"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed muffinfoute","en":"Analyse muffin faults"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho se muffins het gepunte bokante, is taai en het lang gate binne. Lindiwe s'n is plat en swaar. Verduidelik die oorsaak van elkeen se probleem en hoe om dit reg te stel.","en":"Sipho's muffins have peaked tops, are tough and have long holes inside. Lindiwe's are flat and heavy. Explain the cause of each problem and how to correct it."},"steps":[{"af":"Sipho: die lang gate is tonnels. Gepunte bokante, taaiheid en tonnels wys dat die beslag te veel gemeng is – te veel gluten het gevorm.","en":"Sipho: the long holes are tunnels. Peaked tops, toughness and tunnels show that the batter was overmixed – too much gluten formed."},{"af":"Regstelling: meng die droë en nat bestanddele apart, voeg saam en roer net totdat dit klam is. 'n Klonterige beslag is reg.","en":"Correction: mix the dry and wet ingredients separately, combine them and stir only until just moistened. A lumpy batter is correct."},{"af":"Lindiwe: plat en swaar dui op te min rysmiddel of 'n oond wat nie warm genoeg was nie.","en":"Lindiwe: flat and heavy points to too little raising agent or an oven that wasn't hot enough."},{"af":"Regstelling: meet die bakpoeier akkuraat, voorverhit die oond en bak die beslag dadelik nadat dit gemeng is.","en":"Correction: measure the baking powder accurately, preheat the oven and bake the batter immediately after mixing."}],"answer":{"af":"Sipho: te veel gemeng; Lindiwe: te min rysmiddel of 'n te koel oond","en":"Sipho: overmixed; Lindiwe: too little raising agent or an oven that was too cool"}},{"title":{"af":"Skaal 'n pannekoekresep","en":"Scale a pancake recipe"},"problem":{"af":"'n Pannekoekresep vir 15 pannekoeke gebruik 250 g koekmeel, 2 ml sout, 2 eiers, 500 ml melk en 15 ml olie. Die skool het 45 pannekoeke vir 'n rugbydag nodig. Bereken die hoeveelhede.","en":"A pancake recipe for 15 pancakes uses 250 g cake flour, 2 ml salt, 2 eggs, 500 ml milk and 15 ml oil. The school needs 45 pancakes for a rugby day. Calculate the quantities."},"steps":[{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor = 45 ÷ 15 = 3","en":"Conversion factor = 45 ÷ 15 = 3"},{"af":"Meel: 250 g × 3 = 750 g; sout: 2 ml × 3 = 6 ml; eiers: 2 × 3 = 6","en":"Flour: 250 g × 3 = 750 g; salt: 2 ml × 3 = 6 ml; eggs: 2 × 3 = 6"},{"af":"Melk: 500 ml × 3 = 1 500 ml (1,5 ℓ); olie: 15 ml × 3 = 45 ml","en":"Milk: 500 ml × 3 = 1 500 ml (1.5 ℓ); oil: 15 ml × 3 = 45 ml"},{"af":"Die rustyd van die beslag bly ongeveer 30 minute – dit hang nie van die hoeveelheid af nie.","en":"The resting time of the batter stays about 30 minutes – it doesn't depend on the quantity."}],"answer":{"af":"750 g meel, 6 ml sout, 6 eiers, 1,5 ℓ melk, 45 ml olie","en":"750 g flour, 6 ml salt, 6 eggs, 1.5 ℓ milk, 45 ml oil"}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die beslag en verduidelik die reëls","en":"Identify the batter and explain the rules"},"problem":{"af":"Noem die soort beslag vir (a) pannekoek, (b) plaatkoekies en (c) die beslag om vis vir vis-en-tjips. Verduidelik dan waarom pannekoekbeslag moet rus.","en":"Name the type of batter for (a) pancakes, (b) crumpets and (c) the batter around fish for fish and chips. Then explain why pancake batter must rest."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Pannekoek: gietbeslag – dun soos room, sodat dit oor die pan versprei.","en":"(a) Pancakes: pouring batter – thin like cream, so that it spreads over the pan."},{"af":"(b) Plaatkoekies: druppelbeslag – dikker, dit val van 'n lepel af en hou sy vorm in die pan.","en":"(b) Crumpets: dropping batter – thicker, it drops from a spoon and keeps its shape in the pan."},{"af":"(c) Vis: bedekkingsbeslag – dik genoeg om aan die vis te kleef en 'n bros laag te vorm.","en":"(c) Fish: coating batter – thick enough to stick to the fish and form a crisp layer."},{"af":"Rus ongeveer 30 minute: die styselkorrels absorbeer vloeistof en swel, en die gluten ontspan – die pannekoek is dan sag en dun.","en":"Rest for about 30 minutes: the starch granules absorb liquid and swell, and the gluten relaxes – the pancakes are then tender and thin."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Gietbeslag; (b) druppelbeslag; (c) bedekkingsbeslag; rus sodat stysel swel en gluten ontspan","en":"(a) Pouring batter; (b) dropping batter; (c) coating batter; rest so that the starch swells and the gluten relaxes"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter metode word gebruik om skons te maak?","en":"Which method is used to make scones?"},"options":[{"af":"Muffinmetode","en":"Muffin method"},{"af":"Roommetode","en":"Creaming method"},{"af":"Invryfmetode","en":"Rubbing-in method"},{"af":"Klitsmetode","en":"Whisking method"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vir skons word koue botter met die vingerpunte in die meel gevryf – die invryfmetode. Die muffinmetode meng nat en droë bestanddele apart.","en":"For scones cold butter is rubbed into the flour with the fingertips – the rubbing-in method. The muffin method mixes wet and dry ingredients separately."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Pannekoekbeslag is 'n ___beslag.","en":"Pancake batter is a ___ batter."},"answers":{"af":["giet","gietbeslag","dun","dun beslag"],"en":["pouring","pouring batter","thin","thin batter"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["druppel","bedekkings","skep"],"en":["dropping","coating","stiff"]}},"explain":{"af":"Pannekoekbeslag is dun soos room en word in die pan gegooi – 'n gietbeslag. Plaatkoekies gebruik 'n druppelbeslag.","en":"Pancake batter is thin like cream and is poured into the pan – a pouring batter. Crumpets use a dropping batter."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Bruismeel bevat reeds bakpoeier.","en":"Self-raising flour already contains baking powder."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Bruismeel is koekmeel met bakpoeier (en sout) bygevoeg, daarom voeg jy nie ekstra bakpoeier by tensy die resep dit vra nie.","en":"True. Self-raising flour is cake flour with baking powder (and salt) added, so you don't add extra baking powder unless the recipe asks for it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gas vorm bakpoeier wanneer dit met vloeistof en hitte reageer?","en":"Which gas does baking powder form when it reacts with liquid and heat?"},"options":[{"af":"Suurstof","en":"Oxygen"},{"af":"Koolstofdioksied","en":"Carbon dioxide"},{"af":"Waterstof","en":"Hydrogen"},{"af":"Stikstof","en":"Nitrogen"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die koeksoda en suur in bakpoeier reageer en vorm koolstofdioksied (CO₂). Die gasborrels laat die mengsel rys.","en":"The bicarbonate of soda and acid in baking powder react and form carbon dioxide (CO₂). The gas bubbles make the mixture rise."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gluten vorm wanneer die ___ in koringmeel met vloeistof gemeng word.","en":"Gluten forms when the ___ in wheat flour are mixed with liquid."},"answers":{"af":["proteïene","proteïen","proteine","proteien"],"en":["proteins","protein"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stysel","vette","suikers"],"en":["starches","fats","sugars"]}},"explain":{"af":"Gluten is 'n proteïennetwerk. Hoe meer jy meng, hoe sterker word dit – goed vir brood, maar sleg vir skons en muffins.","en":"Gluten is a protein network. The more you mix, the stronger it becomes – good for bread, but bad for scones and muffins."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke produk by die regte beslag of metode.","en":"Match each product to the correct batter or method."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Pannekoek","en":"Pancakes"},"r":{"af":"Gietbeslag","en":"Pouring batter"}},{"l":{"af":"Plaatkoekies","en":"Crumpets"},"r":{"af":"Druppelbeslag","en":"Dropping batter"}},{"l":{"af":"Vis vir vis-en-tjips","en":"Fish for fish and chips"},"r":{"af":"Bedekkingsbeslag","en":"Coating batter"}},{"l":{"af":"Skons","en":"Scones"},"r":{"af":"Invryfmetode","en":"Rubbing-in method"}},{"l":{"af":"Muffins","en":"Muffins"},"r":{"af":"Muffinmetode","en":"Muffin method"}}],"explain":{"af":"Dun en gegooi = gietbeslag; van 'n lepel af = druppelbeslag; om kos te bedek = bedekkingsbeslag. Skons word ingevryf en muffins gebruik die muffinmetode.","en":"Thin and poured = pouring batter; from a spoon = dropping batter; to coat food = coating batter. Scones are rubbed in and muffins use the muffin method."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom moet die botter vir skons koud wees en met die vingerpunte ingevryf word?","en":"Why must the butter for scones be cold and rubbed in with the fingertips?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat die botter nie smelt nie; gesmelte botter maak die skons vetterig en swaar","en":"So that the butter doesn't melt; melted butter makes the scones greasy and heavy"},{"af":"Sodat meer gluten vorm en die skons stewiger is","en":"So that more gluten forms and the scones are firmer"},{"af":"Sodat die bakpoeier gouer begin reageer","en":"So that the baking powder starts reacting sooner"},{"af":"Sodat die skons 'n donkerder kors kry","en":"So that the scones get a darker crust"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jou vingerpunte is die koelste deel van jou hand. Koue botter bly in klein stukkies tussen die meel, sodat die skons lig is. Meer gluten sou die skons taai maak.","en":"Your fingertips are the coolest part of your hand. Cold butter stays in small pieces between the flour, so the scones are light. More gluten would make the scones tough."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Druk die skonsnyer reguit af en moenie dit ___ nie, anders rys die skons skeef.","en":"Press the scone cutter straight down and don't ___ it, or the scones will rise skew."},"answers":{"af":["draai"],"en":["twist","turn"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["meelbestrooi","lig","was"],"en":["flour","lift","wash"]}},"explain":{"af":"As jy die snyer draai, word die kante toegedruk en rys die skons ongelyk. 'n Snyer met meel op is juis reg – dit keer dat die deeg vassit.","en":"If you twist the cutter the edges are sealed and the scones rise unevenly. A floured cutter is actually correct – it stops the dough from sticking."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Muffinbeslag moet geklits word totdat dit heeltemal glad is.","en":"Muffin batter should be beaten until it is completely smooth."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Roer net totdat die droë bestanddele klam is – 'n klonterige beslag is reg. Te veel meng gee tonnels, gepunte bokante en taai muffins.","en":"False. Stir only until the dry ingredients are moistened – a lumpy batter is correct. Overmixing gives tunnels, peaked tops and tough muffins."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die regte volgorde vir die muffinmetode?","en":"What is the correct order for the muffin method?"},"options":[{"af":"Room die botter en suiker, klits die eiers by en vou die meel in","en":"Cream the butter and sugar, beat in the eggs and fold in the flour"},{"af":"Vryf koue botter in die meel, voeg melk by en knie liggies","en":"Rub cold butter into the flour, add milk and knead lightly"},{"af":"Meng alles saam en klits drie minute lank tot glad","en":"Mix everything together and beat for three minutes until smooth"},{"af":"Meng die droë bestanddele, meng die nat bestanddele apart, gooi nat by droog en roer net tot klam","en":"Mix the dry ingredients, mix the wet ingredients separately, pour wet into dry and stir only until moistened"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is die muffinmetode. Die eerste opsie is die roommetode vir koeke, die tweede is die invryfmetode vir skons, en die derde sal tonnels veroorsaak.","en":"This is the muffin method. The first option is the creaming method for cakes, the second is the rubbing-in method for scones, and the third would cause tunnels."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Skonsresep vir 12 skons gebruik 480 g koekmeel. Vir 30 skons het jy ___ g koekmeel nodig.","en":"A scone recipe for 12 scones uses 480 g cake flour. For 30 scones you need ___ g cake flour."},"answers":{"af":["1200","1 200","1200 g","1,2 kg","1.2 kg"],"en":["1200","1 200","1200 g","1.2 kg","1,2 kg"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1 440","960","14 400"],"en":["1 440","960","14 400"]}},"explain":{"af":"Faktor = 30 ÷ 12 = 2,5, dus 480 g × 2,5 = 1 200 g. 1 440 g gebruik faktor 3 in plaas van 2,5, en 14 400 g is 480 × 30.","en":"Factor = 30 ÷ 12 = 2.5, so 480 g × 2.5 = 1 200 g. 1 440 g uses a factor of 3 instead of 2.5, and 14 400 g is 480 × 30."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom laat jy pannekoekbeslag ongeveer 30 minute rus?","en":"Why do you let pancake batter rest for about 30 minutes?"},"options":[{"af":"Sodat die bakpoeier al sy CO₂ kan vorm","en":"So that the baking powder can form all its CO₂"},{"af":"Sodat meer gluten vorm en die pannekoek stewiger is","en":"So that more gluten forms and the pancakes are firmer"},{"af":"Sodat die styselkorrels swel en die gluten ontspan, en die pannekoek sag en dun is","en":"So that the starch granules swell and the gluten relaxes, and the pancakes are tender and thin"},{"af":"Sodat die eiers in die beslag kan stol","en":"So that the eggs in the batter can set"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Tydens die rus absorbeer die stysel vloeistof en swel, en die gluten ontspan. Meer gluten sou die pannekoek taai maak, en eiers stol eers met hitte.","en":"While resting, the starch absorbs liquid and swells, and the gluten relaxes. More gluten would make the pancakes tough, and eggs only set with heat."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Muffins het tonnels binne en gepunte bokante. Wat is die waarskynlikste oorsaak?","en":"Muffins have tunnels inside and peaked tops. What is the most likely cause?"},"options":[{"af":"Te min bakpoeier","en":"Too little baking powder"},{"af":"Die beslag is te veel gemeng","en":"The batter was overmixed"},{"af":"Die oond was te koel","en":"The oven was too cool"},{"af":"Die muffinpanne was nie gesmeer nie","en":"The muffin pans were not greased"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Te veel meng ontwikkel gluten wat die gas in lang kanale (tonnels) laat opstoot en die bokant laat punt. Te min bakpoeier of 'n koel oond gee eerder plat, swaar muffins.","en":"Overmixing develops gluten that pushes the gas up in long channels (tunnels) and makes the top peak. Too little baking powder or a cool oven rather gives flat, heavy muffins."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Karringmelkskons proe seperig en is geelerig. Die kok het te veel ___ gebruik.","en":"Buttermilk scones taste soapy and are yellowish. The cook used too much ___."},"answers":{"af":["koeksoda","natriumbikarbonaat","bikarbonaat van soda","soda"],"en":["bicarbonate of soda","bicarb","baking soda","sodium bicarbonate","soda"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koekmeel","botter","suiker"],"en":["cake flour","butter","sugar"]}},"explain":{"af":"Koeksoda is alkalies. As daar meer is as wat die suur in die karringmelk kan neutraliseer, bly 'n seperige smaak en geel kleur oor.","en":"Bicarbonate of soda is alkaline. If there is more than the acid in the buttermilk can neutralise, a soapy taste and yellow colour remain."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho se skons is plat en swaar. Watter verduideliking is die waarskynlikste?","en":"Sipho's scones are flat and heavy. Which explanation is the most likely?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy het koue botter gebruik en die deeg net 'n paar keer liggies geknie","en":"He used cold butter and kneaded the dough lightly only a few times"},{"af":"Hy het die skons met eierwas geverf en die snyer reguit afgedruk","en":"He brushed the scones with egg wash and pressed the cutter straight down"},{"af":"Hy het die deeg ongeveer 2 cm dik uitgerol en dadelik gebak","en":"He rolled the dough about 2 cm thick and baked it immediately"},{"af":"Hy het te min rysmiddel gebruik en die oond was nie warm genoeg nie","en":"He used too little raising agent and the oven wasn't hot enough"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sonder genoeg CO₂ en 'n warm oond om die mengsel vinnig te laat rys en stol, bly skons plat en swaar. Die ander drie opsies beskryf almal korrekte praktyk.","en":"Without enough CO₂ and a hot oven to make the mixture rise and set quickly, scones stay flat and heavy. The other three options all describe correct practice."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder se pannekoekbeslag is vol klonte. Wat is die beste raad?","en":"A learner's pancake batter is full of lumps. What is the best advice?"},"options":[{"af":"Sif die meel, maak 'n holte en voeg die vloeistof geleidelik by terwyl jy klits; druk 'n klonterige beslag deur 'n sif","en":"Sift the flour, make a well and add the liquid gradually while whisking; push a lumpy batter through a sieve"},{"af":"Gooi volgende keer al die melk op een slag by sodat die meel vinniger natword","en":"Next time pour in all the milk at once so that the flour gets wet faster"},{"af":"Voeg nog meel by sodat die klonte verdwyn","en":"Add more flour so that the lumps disappear"},{"af":"Klits die beslag 10 minute kragtig, want meer gluten maak dit gladder","en":"Beat the batter hard for 10 minutes, because more gluten makes it smoother"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Om die vloeistof geleidelik in te werk, keer dat droë meel klonte vorm, en 'n sif red 'n beslag wat reeds klonte het. Meer meel maak meer klonte, en meer gluten maak die pannekoek taai.","en":"Working the liquid in gradually stops dry flour forming lumps, and a sieve rescues a batter that already has lumps. More flour makes more lumps, and more gluten makes the pancakes tough."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Voedsel- en drankediens; eiers, graan en suiwel","en":"Food and beverage service; eggs, cereals and dairy"},"topics":[{"id":"gas10-t2-voedsel-drankediens","title":{"af":"Voedsel- en drankediens: mise en place, tafeldek, diensstyle, tee en koffie","en":"Food and beverage service: mise en place, table setting, service styles, tea and coffee"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n tafel vir 'n spyskaart kan dek, diensstyle kan vergelyk, die diensvolgorde kan toepas en tee en koffie korrek kan maak en bedien.","en":"You will be able to lay a cover for a menu, compare service styles, apply the service sequence and make and serve tea and coffee correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Restauranttoerusting\n\n| Groep | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Breekware | Sybord, hoofgeregbord, visbord, sopbak, nageregbord, koppie en piering |\n| Eetgerei | Hoofgeregmes en -vurk, vismes en -vurk, symes, soplepel, nageregslepel en -vurk, teelepel |\n| Glasware | Waterkelk, wynglas, tumbler, highball-glas |\n| Linne | Tafeldoek, oorlêdoek (slip cloth), servet, diensdoek |\n\nDie **diensstasie** (dientafel) hou ekstra eetgerei, breekware, servette, bestelboekies en rekeningomslae naby die tafels.\n\n## Mise en place in die restaurant\n\nMaak die tafels, stoele en vloer skoon; sit tafeldoeke op en dek die tafels; maak die sout-, peper- en soushouers skoon en vol; vou servette; kontroleer dat die spyskaarte skoon en korrek is; vul die diensstasie aan en poleer die glase. Ken die spesiale geregte van die dag.\n\n## Tafeldek\n\n'n **Tafeldek** (cover) is die plek en items vir een gas.\n\n- **À la carte-tafeldek:** 'n basiese tafeldek. Die eetgerei vir elke gang word gebring **nadat die gas bestel het**.\n- **Table d'hôte-tafeldek:** al die eetgerei vir die **vaste spyskaart** word **vooraf** gedek.\n\n**Reëls:**\n\n- **Vurke links**; **messe** (lem na binne, na die bord) en **lepels regs**.\n- Eetgerei word **van buite na binne** gebruik – die eerste gang se eetgerei lê buite.\n- Die **nageregslepel en -vurk** lê **bo** die tafeldek.\n- Die **sybord** staan **links** met die **symes** daarop.\n- Die **glas** staan bo die **punt van die hoofgeregmes**.\n- Eetgerei lê **1–2 cm** van die tafelrand af, netjies in lyn.\n\n**Buffet:** borde word aan die **begin** van die buffet gestapel; daar is **koue en warm afdelings** (warm kos in warmhouskottels – chafing dishes); elke gereg het sy eie **opskepgerei**; die vloei is in een rigting, en personeel vul aan en sny vleis.\n\n## Diensstyle\n\n| Styl | Hoe dit werk |\n|---|---|\n| Borddiens (Amerikaans) | Kos word in die kombuis opgeskep; bedien en afgeruim van die gas se **regterkant** |\n| Silwerdiens | Die kelner skep met 'n diens-lepel en -vurk van 'n skottel op die gas se bord, van **links** |\n| Gesinsdiens | Skottels word op die tafel gesit en gaste skep vir mekaar |\n| Buffet | Gaste help hulself by 'n uitstallingstafel; personeel vul aan en sny vleis |\n| Selfdiens / kafeteria | Gaste kies by 'n toonbank, dra 'n skinkbord en betaal by die kasregister |\n\nBorddiens is vinnig met eenvormige porsies; silwerdiens is elegant maar stadig en het vaardige kelners nodig; 'n buffet bedien baie gaste vinnig met baie keuse.\n\n## Diensvolgorde\n\n1. Groet die gaste en wys hulle na 'n tafel.\n2. Bied die spyskaart aan.\n3. Neem die drankbestelling.\n4. Neem die kosbestelling.\n5. Bedien die kos.\n6. Kontroleer na 'n paar minute of alles reg is.\n7. Ruim af wanneer **almal** klaar geëet het.\n8. Bied nagereg en koffie aan.\n9. Bied die rekening aan.\n10. Verwerk die betaling.\n11. Bedank die gaste en groet.\n12. Dek die tafel weer.\n\n## Betaling en kliënteverhoudinge\n\nKontroleer of die rekening korrek is en bied dit in 'n **rekeningomslag** aan. Tel kontantkleingeld voor die gas uit. Bring die **kaartmasjien na die tafel**, sodat die kaart nooit die gas se sig verlaat nie. Selfoonbetaling (bv. 'n QR-kode) word ook aanvaar.\n\nWees vriendelik, aandagtig en netjies, en ken die spyskaart. **Klagtes:** luister, vra om verskoning, los die probleem op en bedank die gas. Moenie stry nie; roep die bestuurder as dit nodig is.\n\n## Tee\n\n- **Swart tee** (Ceylon), **Earl Grey** (swart tee met bergamotolie), **groen tee**, **rooibos** (Suid-Afrikaans en **kafeïenvry**) en **kruietee** (bv. kamille, peperment).\n- Warm die teepot voor, gebruik **vars gekookte water** vir swart tee en rooibos, en laat dit **3–5 minute** trek. Groen tee verkies water wat effens afgekoel het.\n\n## Koffie\n\n| Koffie | Beskrywing |\n|---|---|\n| Espresso | 'n Klein, sterk koffie: warm water word onder druk deur fyngemaalde koffie gedruk |\n| Americano | Espresso met warm water bygevoeg |\n| Cappuccino | Espresso, gestoomde melk en 'n dik laag melkskuim |\n| Café latte | Espresso met baie gestoomde melk en 'n dun laag skuim |\n| Filterkoffie | Water drup stadig deur gemaalde koffie in 'n filter |\n| Plunjer (French press) | Grof gemaalde koffie trek in die warm water en die plunjer word afgedruk |\n| Kitskoffie | Koffiekorrels wat in warm water oplos |\n\nGebruik water wat **net van die kookpunt af** is – kookwater brand die koffie en maak dit bitter.\n\n**Diens:** die koppie en piering staan aan die gas se **regterkant** met die **handvatsel na regs** en die teelepel op die piering. Sit melk en suiker op die tafel.\n\n> **Onthou!** Borddiens: bedien en ruim af van regs. Silwerdiens: bedien van links. Drankies: van regs.","en":"## Restaurant equipment\n\n| Group | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Crockery | Side plate, joint (dinner) plate, fish plate, soup bowl, dessert plate, cup and saucer |\n| Cutlery | Joint knife and fork, fish knife and fork, side knife, soup spoon, dessert spoon and fork, teaspoon |\n| Glassware | Water goblet, wine glass, tumbler, highball glass |\n| Linen | Tablecloth, slip cloth, napkin (serviette), service cloth |\n\nThe **service station** (sideboard) keeps extra cutlery, crockery, napkins, order pads and bill folders close to the tables.\n\n## Restaurant mise en place\n\nClean the tables, chairs and floor; put on tablecloths and lay the tables; clean and fill the salt, pepper and sauce containers; fold napkins; check that the menus are clean and correct; stock the service station and polish the glasses. Know the specials of the day.\n\n## Covers\n\nA **cover** is the place and items for one guest.\n\n- **À la carte cover:** a basic cover. The cutlery for each course is brought **after the guest has ordered**.\n- **Table d'hôte cover:** all the cutlery for the **set menu** is laid **in advance**.\n\n**Rules:**\n\n- **Forks on the left**; **knives** (blade facing inwards, towards the plate) and **spoons on the right**.\n- Cutlery is used **from the outside in** – the first course's cutlery lies on the outside.\n- The **dessert spoon and fork** lie **above** the cover.\n- The **side plate** stands on the **left** with the **side knife** on it.\n- The **glass** stands above the **tip of the joint knife**.\n- Cutlery lies **1–2 cm** from the table edge, neatly in line.\n\n**Buffet:** plates are stacked at the **start** of the buffet; there are **hot and cold sections** (hot food in chafing dishes); each dish has its own **serving utensils**; the flow is in one direction, and staff replenish and carve.\n\n## Service styles\n\n| Style | How it works |\n|---|---|\n| Plated (American) | Food is plated in the kitchen; served and cleared from the guest's **right** |\n| Silver service | The waiter serves from a platter onto the guest's plate with a service spoon and fork, from the **left** |\n| Family service | Dishes are placed on the table and guests serve one another |\n| Buffet | Guests help themselves at a display table; staff replenish and carve |\n| Self-service / cafeteria | Guests choose at a counter, carry a tray and pay at the till |\n\nPlated service is fast with uniform portions; silver service is elegant but slow and needs skilled waiters; a buffet serves many guests quickly with lots of choice.\n\n## Service sequence\n\n1. Greet the guests and show them to a table.\n2. Present the menu.\n3. Take the drinks order.\n4. Take the food order.\n5. Serve the food.\n6. Check back after a few minutes that everything is fine.\n7. Clear when **everyone** has finished eating.\n8. Offer dessert and coffee.\n9. Present the bill.\n10. Process the payment.\n11. Thank the guests and say goodbye.\n12. Reset the table.\n\n## Payment and customer relations\n\nCheck that the bill is correct and present it in a **bill folder**. Count cash change out in front of the guest. Bring the **card machine to the table**, so that the card never leaves the guest's sight. Mobile payment (e.g. a QR code) is also accepted.\n\nBe friendly, attentive and neat, and know the menu. **Complaints:** listen, apologise, solve the problem and thank the guest. Don't argue; call the manager if necessary.\n\n## Tea\n\n- **Black tea** (Ceylon), **Earl Grey** (black tea with bergamot oil), **green tea**, **rooibos** (South African and **caffeine-free**) and **herbal tea** (e.g. chamomile, peppermint).\n- Warm the teapot, use **freshly boiled water** for black tea and rooibos, and let it brew for **3–5 minutes**. Green tea prefers water that has cooled slightly.\n\n## Coffee\n\n| Coffee | Description |\n|---|---|\n| Espresso | A small, strong coffee: hot water is forced under pressure through finely ground coffee |\n| Americano | Espresso with hot water added |\n| Cappuccino | Espresso, steamed milk and a thick layer of milk foam |\n| Café latte | Espresso with lots of steamed milk and a thin layer of foam |\n| Filter coffee | Water drips slowly through ground coffee in a filter |\n| Plunger (French press) | Coarsely ground coffee brews in the hot water and the plunger is pressed down |\n| Instant coffee | Coffee granules that dissolve in hot water |\n\nUse water that is **just off the boil** – boiling water burns the coffee and makes it bitter.\n\n**Service:** the cup and saucer stand on the guest's **right** with the **handle to the right** and the teaspoon on the saucer. Put milk and sugar on the table.\n\n> **Remember!** Plated service: serve and clear from the right. Silver service: serve from the left. Drinks: from the right."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Tafeldek","en":"Cover"},"def":{"af":"Die plek en al die items (eetgerei, breekware, glas, servet) wat vir een gas op die tafel gedek word.","en":"The place and all the items (cutlery, crockery, glass, napkin) laid on the table for one guest."}},{"term":{"af":"À la carte-tafeldek","en":"À la carte cover"},"def":{"af":"'n Basiese tafeldek; die eetgerei vir elke gang word gebring nadat die gas bestel het.","en":"A basic cover; the cutlery for each course is brought after the guest has ordered."}},{"term":{"af":"Table d'hôte-tafeldek","en":"Table d'hôte cover"},"def":{"af":"Al die eetgerei vir die vaste spyskaart word vooraf gedek.","en":"All the cutlery for the set menu is laid in advance."}},{"term":{"af":"Breekware","en":"Crockery"},"def":{"af":"Borde, bakke, koppies en pierings wat gebruik word om kos en drank te bedien.","en":"Plates, bowls, cups and saucers used to serve food and drinks."}},{"term":{"af":"Diensstasie","en":"Service station (sideboard)"},"def":{"af":"'n Dientafel naby die eetarea met ekstra eetgerei, breekware, linne en bestelboekies.","en":"A sideboard near the dining area holding extra cutlery, crockery, linen and order pads."}},{"term":{"af":"Borddiens","en":"Plated (American) service"},"def":{"af":"Die kos word in die kombuis op borde opgeskep en van die gas se regterkant bedien en afgeruim.","en":"Food is plated in the kitchen and served and cleared from the guest's right."}},{"term":{"af":"Silwerdiens","en":"Silver service"},"def":{"af":"Die kelner skep die kos met 'n diens-lepel en -vurk van 'n skottel op die gas se bord, van die linkerkant.","en":"The waiter serves the food from a platter onto the guest's plate with a service spoon and fork, from the left."}},{"term":{"af":"Buffet","en":"Buffet"},"def":{"af":"'n Diensstyl waar gaste hulself by 'n uitstallingstafel help terwyl personeel aanvul en vleis sny.","en":"A service style where guests help themselves at a display table while staff replenish and carve."}},{"term":{"af":"Rooibos","en":"Rooibos"},"def":{"af":"'n Suid-Afrikaanse tee wat van nature kafeïenvry is en met vars gekookte water gemaak word.","en":"A South African tea that is naturally caffeine-free and made with freshly boiled water."}},{"term":{"af":"Cappuccino","en":"Cappuccino"},"def":{"af":"Espresso met gestoomde melk en 'n dik laag melkskuim.","en":"Espresso with steamed milk and a thick layer of milk foam."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Dek vir 'n table d'hôte-spyskaart","en":"Lay a cover for a table d'hôte menu"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gastehuis in die Magaliesberg bedien hierdie vaste spyskaart: Groentesop; Gebraaide hoender met groente; Malvapoeding met vla. Lys die tafeldek en sê waar elke item lê.","en":"A guest house in the Magaliesberg serves this set menu: Vegetable soup; Roast chicken with vegetables; Malva pudding with custard. List the cover and say where each item goes."},"steps":[{"af":"Regs, van buite na binne: soplepel (eerste gang, heel buite) en dan die hoofgeregmes met die lem na die bord.","en":"Right, from the outside in: soup spoon (first course, on the outside), then the joint knife with the blade facing the plate."},{"af":"Links: die hoofgeregvurk. Die sybord staan links van die vurk met die symes daarop.","en":"Left: the joint fork. The side plate stands to the left of the fork with the side knife on it."},{"af":"Bo die tafeldek: die nageregslepel en -vurk vir die malvapoeding.","en":"Above the cover: the dessert spoon and fork for the malva pudding."},{"af":"Die servet in die middel van die tafeldek en die waterglas bo die punt van die hoofgeregmes. Alles lê 1–2 cm van die tafelrand.","en":"The napkin in the centre of the cover and the water glass above the tip of the joint knife. Everything lies 1–2 cm from the table edge."}],"answer":{"af":"Soplepel en hoofgeregmes regs; hoofgeregvurk links; sybord en symes links; nageregslepel en -vurk bo; servet in die middel; glas bo die mespunt","en":"Soup spoon and joint knife right; joint fork left; side plate and side knife left; dessert spoon and fork above; napkin in the centre; glass above the knife tip"}},{"title":{"af":"Stel foute in 'n tafeldek reg","en":"Correct the errors in a cover"},"problem":{"af":"'n Nuwe kelner het so gedek: die vurk lê regs van die bord, die mes lê links met die lem na buite, die sybord staan regs, die glas staan bo die vurk en die eetgerei lê 6 cm van die tafelrand af. Identifiseer en verbeter die foute.","en":"A new waiter laid this cover: the fork lies to the right of the plate, the knife lies on the left with the blade facing outwards, the side plate stands on the right, the glass stands above the fork and the cutlery lies 6 cm from the table edge. Identify and correct the errors."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: die vurk moet links lê en die mes regs.","en":"Error 1: the fork must lie on the left and the knife on the right."},{"af":"Fout 2: die mes se lem moet na binne, na die bord toe, wys.","en":"Error 2: the knife's blade must face inwards, towards the plate."},{"af":"Fout 3: die sybord moet links staan, met die symes daarop.","en":"Error 3: the side plate must stand on the left, with the side knife on it."},{"af":"Fout 4: die glas moet bo die punt van die mes staan. Fout 5: die eetgerei moet 1–2 cm van die tafelrand af lê.","en":"Error 4: the glass must stand above the tip of the knife. Error 5: the cutlery must lie 1–2 cm from the table edge."}],"answer":{"af":"Vurk links, mes regs met die lem na binne, sybord links, glas bo die mespunt, eetgerei 1–2 cm van die rand","en":"Fork left, knife right with the blade inwards, side plate left, glass above the knife tip, cutlery 1–2 cm from the edge"}},{"title":{"af":"Plaas die diensstappe in volgorde","en":"Put the service steps in order"},"problem":{"af":"Rangskik hierdie stappe in die regte volgorde: (A) bied die rekening aan, (B) neem die kosbestelling, (C) groet en plaas die gaste, (D) ruim af wanneer almal klaar is, (E) neem die drankbestelling, (F) bedien die kos, (G) bied die spyskaart aan, (H) kontroleer of alles reg is.","en":"Arrange these steps in the correct order: (A) present the bill, (B) take the food order, (C) greet and seat the guests, (D) clear when everyone has finished, (E) take the drinks order, (F) serve the food, (G) present the menu, (H) check back that everything is fine."},"steps":[{"af":"Begin by die gas se aankoms: C (groet en plaas), dan G (spyskaart).","en":"Start with the guest's arrival: C (greet and seat), then G (menu)."},{"af":"Drankies eerste, want dit neem gaste tyd om die spyskaart te lees: E, dan B.","en":"Drinks first, because guests take time to read the menu: E, then B."},{"af":"F (bedien), dan H (kontroleer na 'n paar minute), dan D (ruim af wanneer almal klaar is).","en":"F (serve), then H (check back after a few minutes), then D (clear when everyone has finished)."},{"af":"Laastens A (rekening) – nadat nagereg en koffie aangebied is.","en":"Finally A (bill) – after dessert and coffee have been offered."}],"answer":{"af":"C → G → E → B → F → H → D → A","en":"C → G → E → B → F → H → D → A"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak en bedien 'n cappuccino","en":"Make and serve a cappuccino"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gas in 'n koffiewinkel in Pretoria bestel 'n cappuccino. Verduidelik hoe jy dit maak en bedien, en hoe dit van 'n café latte verskil.","en":"A guest in a coffee shop in Pretoria orders a cappuccino. Explain how you make and serve it, and how it differs from a café latte."},"steps":[{"af":"Trek 'n espresso: warm water wat net van die kookpunt af is, word onder druk deur fyngemaalde koffie gedruk.","en":"Pull an espresso: hot water just off the boil is forced under pressure through finely ground coffee."},{"af":"Stoom die melk met die stoompyp sodat dit warm word en 'n dik, romerige skuim vorm.","en":"Steam the milk with the steam wand so that it becomes hot and forms a thick, creamy foam."},{"af":"Gooi die gestoomde melk by die espresso en skep 'n dik laag skuim bo-op; strooi gerus 'n bietjie kakao of kaneel oor.","en":"Pour the steamed milk into the espresso and spoon a thick layer of foam on top; you may sprinkle a little cocoa or cinnamon over it."},{"af":"Bedien op 'n piering aan die gas se regterkant, met die handvatsel na regs en 'n teelepel op die piering; sit suiker op die tafel.","en":"Serve on a saucer on the guest's right, with the handle to the right and a teaspoon on the saucer; put sugar on the table."},{"af":"Verskil: 'n café latte het meer gestoomde melk en net 'n dun laag skuim.","en":"Difference: a café latte has more steamed milk and only a thin layer of foam."}],"answer":{"af":"Espresso + gestoomde melk + dik skuim, bedien van regs met die handvatsel na regs; 'n latte het meer melk en minder skuim","en":"Espresso + steamed milk + thick foam, served from the right with the handle to the right; a latte has more milk and less foam"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter item is breekware?","en":"Which item is crockery?"},"options":[{"af":"Soplepel","en":"Soup spoon"},{"af":"Waterkelk","en":"Water goblet"},{"af":"Servet","en":"Napkin"},{"af":"Sopbak","en":"Soup bowl"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Breekware is borde, bakke, koppies en pierings. 'n Soplepel is eetgerei, 'n waterkelk is glasware en 'n servet is linne.","en":"Crockery is plates, bowls, cups and saucers. A soup spoon is cutlery, a water goblet is glassware and a napkin is linen."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n tafeldek lê die vurke aan die ___kant van die bord.","en":"In a cover the forks lie on the ___ side of the plate."},"answers":{"af":["linker","linkerkant","links"],"en":["left","left-hand","left hand"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["regter","boonste","onderste"],"en":["right","top","bottom"]}},"explain":{"af":"Vurke lê links; messe en lepels lê regs. Die nageregslepel en -vurk lê bo die tafeldek.","en":"Forks lie on the left; knives and spoons lie on the right. The dessert spoon and fork lie above the cover."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Rooibostee bevat van nature geen kafeïen nie.","en":"Rooibos tea naturally contains no caffeine."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Rooibos is 'n Suid-Afrikaanse tee wat van nature kafeïenvry is – 'n goeie keuse vir gaste wat kafeïen vermy.","en":"True. Rooibos is a South African tea that is naturally caffeine-free – a good choice for guests who avoid caffeine."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Van watter kant van die gas word kos by silwerdiens bedien?","en":"From which side of the guest is food served in silver service?"},"options":[{"af":"Van links","en":"From the left"},{"af":"Van regs","en":"From the right"},{"af":"Van voor af, oor die tafel","en":"From the front, across the table"},{"af":"Die gas skep self","en":"The guest serves himself"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By silwerdiens skep die kelner van 'n skottel af en bedien van die gas se linkerkant. By borddiens word van regs bedien en afgeruim.","en":"In silver service the waiter serves from a platter from the guest's left. In plated service food is served and cleared from the right."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die waterglas staan bo die punt van die ___.","en":"The water glass stands above the tip of the ___."},"answers":{"af":["hoofgeregmes","mes","groot mes","tafelmes"],"en":["joint knife","knife","main knife","dinner knife","main-course knife"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vurk","soplepel","sybord"],"en":["fork","soup spoon","side plate"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die glas staan regs bo, by die punt van die hoofgeregmes, sodat die gas dit maklik met die regterhand kan bereik.","en":"The glass stands at the top right, at the tip of the joint knife, so that the guest can easily reach it with the right hand."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke diensstyl by die beskrywing.","en":"Match each service style to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Borddiens","en":"Plated service"},"r":{"af":"Kos word in die kombuis op borde opgeskep","en":"Food is plated in the kitchen"}},{"l":{"af":"Silwerdiens","en":"Silver service"},"r":{"af":"Die kelner skep van 'n skottel op die gas se bord","en":"The waiter serves from a platter onto the guest's plate"}},{"l":{"af":"Gesinsdiens","en":"Family service"},"r":{"af":"Skottels word op die gaste se tafel gesit","en":"Dishes are placed on the guests' table"}},{"l":{"af":"Buffet","en":"Buffet"},"r":{"af":"Gaste help hulself by 'n uitstallingstafel","en":"Guests help themselves at a display table"}},{"l":{"af":"Kafeteria","en":"Cafeteria"},"r":{"af":"Gaste kies by 'n toonbank, dra 'n skinkbord en betaal by die kas","en":"Guests choose at a counter, carry a tray and pay at the till"}}],"explain":{"af":"Vra jouself: wie skep die kos op en waar? Die kombuis (bord), die kelner (silwer), die gaste aan hul eie tafel (gesin), die gaste by 'n uitstalling (buffet) of by 'n toonbank (kafeteria).","en":"Ask yourself: who serves the food and where? The kitchen (plated), the waiter (silver), the guests at their own table (family), the guests at a display (buffet) or at a counter (cafeteria)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die verskil tussen 'n à la carte- en 'n table d'hôte-tafeldek?","en":"What is the difference between an à la carte and a table d'hôte cover?"},"options":[{"af":"By à la carte word al die eetgerei vooraf gedek; by table d'hôte word dit per bestelling gebring","en":"For à la carte all the cutlery is laid in advance; for table d'hôte it is brought per order"},{"af":"Daar is geen verskil nie; net die spyskaart se prys verskil","en":"There is no difference; only the menu price differs"},{"af":"By table d'hôte word al die eetgerei vir die vaste spyskaart vooraf gedek; by à la carte word dit gebring nadat die gas bestel het","en":"For table d'hôte all the cutlery for the set menu is laid in advance; for à la carte it is brought after the guest has ordered"},{"af":"By table d'hôte word geen glase gedek nie","en":"For table d'hôte no glasses are laid"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By table d'hôte ken jy die vaste spyskaart vooraf, dus kan jy alles dek. By à la carte weet jy nie wat die gas gaan bestel nie, dus dek jy basies en bring die regte eetgerei later.","en":"For table d'hôte you know the set menu in advance, so you can lay everything. For à la carte you don't know what the guest will order, so you lay a basic cover and bring the correct cutlery later."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak swart tee en rooibos met vars, pas ___ water.","en":"Make black tea and rooibos with fresh, freshly ___ water."},"answers":{"af":["gekookte","gekook","kokende"],"en":["boiled","boiling"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lou","koue","afgekoelde"],"en":["cooled","chilled","warmed"]}},"explain":{"af":"Swart tee en rooibos het vars gekookte water nodig om ten volle te trek. Groen tee verkies water wat effens afgekoel het.","en":"Black tea and rooibos need freshly boiled water to brew fully. Green tea prefers water that has cooled slightly."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By borddiens word die borde van die gas se linkerkant afgeruim.","en":"In plated service the plates are cleared from the guest's left."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. By borddiens word van die gas se regterkant bedien én afgeruim. Silwerdiens bedien van links.","en":"False. In plated service food is served and cleared from the guest's right. Silver service serves from the left."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stap kom direk ná \"bedien die kos\" in die diensvolgorde?","en":"Which step comes directly after \"serve the food\" in the service sequence?"},"options":[{"af":"Bied die rekening aan","en":"Present the bill"},{"af":"Kontroleer na 'n paar minute of alles reg is","en":"Check back after a few minutes that everything is fine"},{"af":"Ruim die borde af, al eet sommige gaste nog","en":"Clear the plates, even if some guests are still eating"},{"af":"Neem die drankbestelling","en":"Take the drinks order"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Na die bediening kontroleer jy of die kos reg is, sodat 'n probleem dadelik opgelos kan word. Jy ruim eers af wanneer almal klaar is, en die rekening kom heel aan die einde.","en":"After serving you check back that the food is fine, so that a problem can be solved immediately. You only clear when everyone has finished, and the bill comes right at the end."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die spyskaart is sop, hoofgereg en nagereg. Die eetgerei wat heel buite aan die regterkant lê, is die ___.","en":"The menu is soup, main course and dessert. The cutlery lying furthest out on the right is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["soplepel"],"en":["soup spoon","soupspoon"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoofgeregmes","nageregslepel","teelepel"],"en":["joint knife","dessert spoon","teaspoon"]}},"explain":{"af":"Eetgerei word van buite na binne gebruik. Sop is die eerste gang, dus lê die soplepel heel buite regs, met die hoofgeregmes binne. Die nageregslepel lê bo die tafeldek.","en":"Cutlery is used from the outside in. Soup is the first course, so the soup spoon lies furthest out on the right, with the joint knife inside it. The dessert spoon lies above the cover."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n cappuccino?","en":"What is a cappuccino?"},"options":[{"af":"Espresso met warm water bygevoeg","en":"Espresso with hot water added"},{"af":"Espresso met baie gestoomde melk en 'n dun laag skuim","en":"Espresso with lots of steamed milk and a thin layer of foam"},{"af":"Kitskoffie met warm melk","en":"Instant coffee with hot milk"},{"af":"Espresso, gestoomde melk en 'n dik laag melkskuim","en":"Espresso, steamed milk and a thick layer of milk foam"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Cappuccino het 'n dik laag skuim. Espresso met warm water is 'n americano, en baie melk met 'n dun laag skuim is 'n café latte.","en":"A cappuccino has a thick layer of foam. Espresso with hot water is an americano, and lots of milk with a thin layer of foam is a café latte."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy kontroleer 'n tafeldek. Watter EEN van hierdie is 'n fout?","en":"You are checking a cover. Which ONE of these is an error?"},"options":[{"af":"Die mes se lem wys na buite, weg van die bord","en":"The knife's blade faces outwards, away from the plate"},{"af":"Die waterglas staan bo die punt van die hoofgeregmes","en":"The water glass stands above the tip of the joint knife"},{"af":"Die vurk lê links van die bord","en":"The fork lies to the left of the plate"},{"af":"Die nageregslepel en -vurk lê bo die tafeldek","en":"The dessert spoon and fork lie above the cover"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die mes se lem moet na binne, na die bord toe, wys – dis veiliger en netjieser. Die ander drie is korrekte reëls.","en":"The knife's blade must face inwards, towards the plate – it is safer and neater. The other three are correct rules."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Gas kla. Jy luister, vra om verskoning, los die probleem op en ___ die gas.","en":"A guest complains. You listen, apologise, solve the problem and ___ the guest."},"answers":{"af":["bedank","dank"],"en":["thank"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verwys","ignoreer","kritiseer"],"en":["refer","ignore","blame"]}},"explain":{"af":"Bedank die gas dat hy die probleem genoem het – so kan die restaurant verbeter en die gas voel gerespekteer. Moenie stry nie; roep die bestuurder as dit nodig is.","en":"Thank the guest for raising the problem – this way the restaurant can improve and the guest feels respected. Don't argue; call the manager if necessary."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Skool in Brits hou 'n matriekafskeid vir 200 gaste. Daar is min opgeleide kelners, die gaste wil uit verskeie geregte kies en die begroting is beperk. Watter diensstyl is die beste?","en":"A school in Brits is holding a matric farewell for 200 guests. There are few trained waiters, the guests want to choose from several dishes and the budget is limited. Which service style is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Silwerdiens","en":"Silver service"},{"af":"Buffet","en":"Buffet"},{"af":"Gesinsdiens","en":"Family service"},{"af":"À la carte-borddiens","en":"À la carte plated service"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Buffet bedien baie gaste vinnig, bied baie keuse en het min kelners nodig – net personeel om aan te vul en vleis te sny. Silwerdiens het baie vaardige kelners nodig, gesinsdiens vra skottels met elke gereg op elke tafel, en à la carte vir 200 is stadig en duur.","en":"A buffet serves many guests quickly, offers lots of choice and needs few waiters – only staff to replenish and carve. Silver service needs many skilled waiters, family service needs platters of every dish on every table, and à la carte for 200 is slow and expensive."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gas wil met 'n bankkaart betaal. Wat is die korrekte praktyk?","en":"A guest wants to pay with a bank card. What is the correct practice?"},"options":[{"af":"Neem die kaart na die kasregister agter in die restaurant","en":"Take the card to the till at the back of the restaurant"},{"af":"Vra die gas vir sy PIN sodat jy dit vir hom kan intik","en":"Ask the guest for his PIN so that you can key it in for him"},{"af":"Bring die kaartmasjien na die tafel sodat die kaart nooit die gas se sig verlaat nie","en":"Bring the card machine to the table so that the card never leaves the guest's sight"},{"af":"Bied die rekening aan terwyl die ander gaste nog eet","en":"Present the bill while the other guests are still eating"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die kaart moet altyd in die gas se sig bly en net die gas tik sy PIN in – dit beskerm teen bedrog. Die rekening word eers aangebied wanneer die gaste klaar is en daarvoor vra.","en":"The card must always stay in the guest's sight and only the guest keys in his PIN – this protects against fraud. The bill is only presented when the guests have finished and ask for it."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t2-eiers","title":{"af":"Eiers","en":"Eggs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die struktuur, varsheid, berging, funksies en kookmetodes van eiers kan verduidelik en kookprobleme soos sinerese en die groen ring kan voorkom.","en":"You will be able to explain the structure, freshness, storage, functions and cooking methods of eggs, and prevent cooking problems such as syneresis and the green ring."},"summary":{"af":"## Die struktuur van 'n eier\n\n| Deel | Beskrywing en funksie |\n|---|---|\n| **Dop** | Hoofsaaklik kalsiumkarbonaat. Dit is **poreus** (vol klein porieë), dus kan vog, gasse en reuke in en uit beweeg. 'n Dun beskermlagie (kutikula) help om bakterieë uit te hou. |\n| **Dopvliese** | Twee dun vliese (binne- en buitevlies) teen die binnekant van die dop; nog 'n versperring teen bakterieë. |\n| **Lugsak** | By die **breë punt**, tussen die twee vliese. Hoe ouer die eier, hoe **groter** die lugsak, want vog verdamp deur die porieë en lug kom in. |\n| **Dik eierwit** | Die stewige wit (albumien) om die dooier. 'n Vars eier het baie dik wit. |\n| **Dun eierwit** | Die waterige wit naby die dop. Soos die eier ouer word, word meer van die wit dun. |\n| **Chalazae** | Twee gedraaide \"toutjies\" van eierwit wat die **dooier in die middel hou**. |\n| **Dooier** | Die geel deel, omring deur die **dooiervlies**. Bevat byna al die vet. |\n\n## Voedingswaarde\n\n- **Proteïen van hoë biologiese waarde** (in die wit én die dooier) – vir groei en herstel.\n- **Vet** – byna net in die dooier; die wit is feitlik vetvry.\n- **Vitamiene A, D en B** (veral B2 en B12) en **yster** – hoofsaaklik in die dooier.\n- Eiers bevat **geen vitamien C** nie en baie min koolhidrate. Bedien dit saam met groente, vrugte of brood vir 'n gebalanseerde maaltyd.\n\n## Varsheidstoetse\n\n1. **Watertoets:** Plaas die eier in 'n bak koue water. **Vars:** lê plat op die bodem. **Ouer:** kantel of staan regop. **Oud/bederf:** **dryf** – die lugsak is groot. Gooi dit weg.\n2. **Breektoets:** Breek die eier op 'n plat bord. **Vars:** dik wit wat bymekaar bly en 'n ronde, hoë dooier. **Oud:** waterige wit wat wyd uitloop en 'n plat dooier wat maklik breek.\n3. **Deurligtoets (candling):** Hou die eier voor 'n helder lig. 'n Vars eier het 'n klein lugsak en die dooier is in die middel.\n\n## Berging\n\n- In die **yskas**, in die **karton**, met die **skerp punt na onder** – so bly die lugsak bo en die dooier in die middel.\n- Weg van sterk reuke (uie, vis, kaas), want die poreuse dop neem reuke op.\n- Moenie eiers was voor jy dit bêre nie – dit verwyder die beskermlagie.\n\n## Funksies van eiers in kookkuns\n\n| Funksie | Hoe dit werk | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bind | proteïen stol en hou bestanddele bymekaar | frikkadelle, viskoekies |\n| Bedek (paneer) | eier laat krummels vasklou | gepaneerde hoender of vis |\n| Emulgeer | **lesitien** in die dooier hou olie en suur saam | mayonnaise |\n| Belug/rys | geklitste eier vang lug vas wat met hitte uitsit | sponskoek, meringue |\n| Verdik | proteïen stol met hitte | eiervla (custard), quiche |\n| Glaseer | eierglans gee 'n blink, goue kors | skons, pasteie |\n| Verryk | voeg proteïen, kleur en geur by | brooddeeg, kapokaartappels |\n| Garneer | gekookte eier in skyfies of gekap | slaaie |\n| Verhelder | eierwit stol en vang klein deeltjies vas | consommé (helder sop) |\n\n## Effek van hitte: stolling\n\nEierproteïen **stol (koaguleer)** met hitte: dit verander van vloeibaar na vas, en dit kan nie omgekeer word nie.\n\n- Die **wit** stol by ongeveer **60–65 °C** en die **dooier** by ongeveer **65–70 °C**. Daarom kan 'n eier 'n gestolde wit en 'n lopende dooier hê.\n- **Oorkook** veroorsaak:\n  - 'n **rubberagtige**, taai tekstuur;\n  - **sinerese** – die proteïen trek saam en druk vloeistof uit (die eier \"huil\"), bv. waterige roereiers of vla;\n  - 'n **groengrys ring** om die dooier van hardgekookte eiers: swael uit die wit reageer met **yster** in die dooier en vorm **ystersulfied**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Voorkom die groen ring: moenie langer as nodig kook nie (±8–10 min) en dompel die eiers dadelik in koue water.\n\n## Klits van eierwitte\n\n- 'n Skoon, **vetvrye** bak van glas of vlekvrye staal – vet keer dat skuim vorm. Plastiekbakke hou maklik vet vas.\n- **Geen dooier** nie, want die dooier bevat vet.\n- Eiers op **kamertemperatuur** klits tot 'n groter volume.\n- 'n Bietjie **suur** (suurlemoensap of kremetart) stabiliseer die skuim.\n- **Sagte punte:** die punte buig om. **Stywe punte:** die punte staan regop.\n- Vir **meringue** voeg jy die suiker **geleidelik** by nadat sagte punte gevorm het.\n- **Oorklits** maak die skuim droog en korrelrig, en dit val inmekaar.\n\n## Kookmetodes\n\n- **Gekookte eiers:** sag ongeveer **3–4 min**; hard ongeveer **8–10 min**.\n- **Geposjeerde eier:** stadig prutelende water met 'n bietjie **asyn** (help die wit om vinnig te stol). Breek die eier eers in 'n koppie, laat dit in die water gly, posjeer ±3–4 min en haal uit met 'n gaatjieslepel.\n- **Roereier:** oor **lae hitte**, roer stadig en haal van die hitte af **net voordat** dit gestol is – die oorblywende hitte kook dit klaar.\n- **Gebakte eier:** spieëleier (*sunny side up*, nie omgedraai nie) of *over easy* (omgedraai, die dooier bly sag).\n- **Omelette:** **Franse/gewone omelet** (gevou, sag binne); **Spaanse omelet** (plat, met groente soos aartappel en ui, nie gevou nie); **soufflé-omelet** (styfgeklitste witte word by die dooiers ingevou; klaargemaak onder die salamander).\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Te hoë hitte maak eiers taai en veroorsaak sinerese. Onthou ook: eiers is **hoërisiko-voedsel** (*Salmonella*) – kook dit deeglik vir jong kinders, bejaardes en swanger vroue.","en":"## The structure of an egg\n\n| Part | Description and function |\n|---|---|\n| **Shell** | Mainly calcium carbonate. It is **porous** (full of tiny pores), so moisture, gases and smells can move in and out. A thin protective layer (cuticle) helps keep bacteria out. |\n| **Shell membranes** | Two thin membranes (inner and outer) against the inside of the shell; another barrier against bacteria. |\n| **Air cell** | At the **broad end**, between the two membranes. The older the egg, the **bigger** the air cell, because moisture evaporates through the pores and air enters. |\n| **Thick albumen** | The firm white around the yolk. A fresh egg has a lot of thick white. |\n| **Thin albumen** | The watery white near the shell. As the egg ages, more of the white becomes thin. |\n| **Chalazae** | Two twisted \"cords\" of egg white that **hold the yolk in the centre**. |\n| **Yolk** | The yellow part, surrounded by the **yolk membrane**. Contains almost all the fat. |\n\n## Nutritional value\n\n- **High-biological-value protein** (in both the white and the yolk) – for growth and repair.\n- **Fat** – almost only in the yolk; the white is practically fat-free.\n- **Vitamins A, D and B** (especially B2 and B12) and **iron** – mainly in the yolk.\n- Eggs contain **no vitamin C** and very little carbohydrate. Serve them with vegetables, fruit or bread for a balanced meal.\n\n## Freshness tests\n\n1. **Water test:** Place the egg in a bowl of cold water. **Fresh:** lies flat on the bottom. **Older:** tilts or stands upright. **Old/stale:** **floats** – the air cell is large. Throw it away.\n2. **Break test:** Break the egg onto a flat plate. **Fresh:** thick white that stays together and a round, high yolk. **Old:** watery white that spreads widely and a flat yolk that breaks easily.\n3. **Candling:** Hold the egg in front of a bright light. A fresh egg has a small air cell and the yolk is in the centre.\n\n## Storage\n\n- In the **fridge**, in the **carton**, **pointed end down** – this keeps the air cell at the top and the yolk in the centre.\n- Away from strong smells (onions, fish, cheese), because the porous shell absorbs smells.\n- Don't wash eggs before storing them – it removes the protective layer.\n\n## Functions of eggs in cooking\n\n| Function | How it works | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Binding | protein sets and holds ingredients together | frikkadelle, fish cakes |\n| Coating (crumbing) | egg makes crumbs stick | crumbed chicken or fish |\n| Emulsifying | **lecithin** in the yolk keeps oil and acid together | mayonnaise |\n| Aerating/raising | beaten egg traps air that expands with heat | sponge cake, meringue |\n| Thickening | protein sets with heat | egg custard, quiche |\n| Glazing | egg wash gives a shiny, golden crust | scones, pies |\n| Enriching | adds protein, colour and flavour | bread dough, mashed potatoes |\n| Garnishing | boiled egg sliced or chopped | salads |\n| Clarifying | egg white sets and traps tiny particles | consommé (clear soup) |\n\n## Effect of heat: coagulation\n\nEgg protein **coagulates (sets)** with heat: it changes from liquid to solid, and it cannot be reversed.\n\n- The **white** sets at about **60–65 °C** and the **yolk** at about **65–70 °C**. That is why an egg can have a set white and a runny yolk.\n- **Overcooking** causes:\n  - a **rubbery**, tough texture;\n  - **syneresis** – the protein shrinks and squeezes out liquid (the egg \"weeps\"), e.g. watery scrambled eggs or custard;\n  - a **green-grey ring** around the yolk of hard-boiled eggs: sulphur from the white reacts with **iron** in the yolk to form **iron sulphide**.\n\n> **Tip:** Prevent the green ring: don't cook longer than needed (±8–10 min) and plunge the eggs into cold water immediately.\n\n## Whisking egg whites\n\n- A clean, **grease-free** glass or stainless-steel bowl – fat stops foam from forming. Plastic bowls easily hold on to grease.\n- **No yolk**, because the yolk contains fat.\n- **Room-temperature** eggs whisk to a bigger volume.\n- A little **acid** (lemon juice or cream of tartar) stabilises the foam.\n- **Soft peaks:** the tips fold over. **Stiff peaks:** the tips stand upright.\n- For **meringue**, add the sugar **gradually** once soft peaks have formed.\n- **Overbeating** makes the foam dry and grainy, and it collapses.\n\n## Cooking methods\n\n- **Boiled eggs:** soft about **3–4 min**; hard about **8–10 min**.\n- **Poached egg:** gently simmering water with a little **vinegar** (helps the white set quickly). Break the egg into a cup first, slide it into the water, poach ±3–4 min and lift out with a slotted spoon.\n- **Scrambled egg:** over **low heat**, stir slowly and remove from the heat **just before** it is set – the remaining heat finishes the cooking.\n- **Fried egg:** sunny side up (not turned) or over easy (turned, the yolk stays soft).\n- **Omelettes:** **French/plain omelette** (folded, soft inside); **Spanish omelette** (flat, with vegetables such as potato and onion, not folded); **soufflé omelette** (stiffly beaten whites are folded into the yolks; finished under the salamander).\n\n> **Common mistake:** Too high a heat makes eggs tough and causes syneresis. Also remember: eggs are a **high-risk food** (*Salmonella*) – cook them thoroughly for young children, the elderly and pregnant women."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lugsak","en":"Air cell"},"def":{"af":"Die luggevulde ruimte by die breë punt van die eier tussen die twee dopvliese; dit word groter soos die eier ouer word.","en":"The air-filled space at the broad end of the egg between the two shell membranes; it gets bigger as the egg ages."}},{"term":{"af":"Chalazae","en":"Chalazae"},"def":{"af":"Twee gedraaide toutjies van eierwit wat die dooier in die middel van die eier hou.","en":"Two twisted cords of egg white that hold the yolk in the centre of the egg."}},{"term":{"af":"Albumien (eierwit)","en":"Albumen (egg white)"},"def":{"af":"Die wit van die eier wat uit dik en dun eierwit bestaan en hoofsaaklik water en proteïen bevat.","en":"The white of the egg, made up of thick and thin albumen and consisting mainly of water and protein."}},{"term":{"af":"Poreus","en":"Porous"},"def":{"af":"Vol klein gaatjies (porieë) sodat vog, gasse en reuke deur die eierdop kan beweeg.","en":"Full of tiny holes (pores) so that moisture, gases and smells can pass through the eggshell."}},{"term":{"af":"Stolling (koagulasie)","en":"Coagulation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer proteïen deur hitte (of suur) van vloeibaar na vas verander; dit is onomkeerbaar.","en":"When protein changes from liquid to solid because of heat (or acid); it cannot be reversed."}},{"term":{"af":"Sinerese","en":"Syneresis"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer oorverhitte proteïen saamtrek en vloeistof uitdruk, sodat die gereg 'huil' en waterig word.","en":"When overheated protein shrinks and squeezes out liquid, so that the dish 'weeps' and becomes watery."}},{"term":{"af":"Lesitien","en":"Lecithin"},"def":{"af":"Die emulgeerder in eiergeel wat olie en water/suur saamhou, bv. in mayonnaise.","en":"The emulsifier in egg yolk that holds oil and water/acid together, e.g. in mayonnaise."}},{"term":{"af":"Deurligtoets","en":"Candling"},"def":{"af":"'n Varsheidstoets waar 'n eier voor 'n helder lig gehou word om die grootte van die lugsak en die posisie van die dooier te sien.","en":"A freshness test in which an egg is held in front of a bright light to see the size of the air cell and the position of the yolk."}},{"term":{"af":"Stywe punte","en":"Stiff peaks"},"def":{"af":"Die stadium wanneer geklitste eierwit regop punte vorm wat nie omval nie.","en":"The stage when beaten egg white forms upright peaks that do not fall over."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Interpreteer die watertoets","en":"Interpret the water test"},"problem":{"af":"'n Kok by 'n gastehuis in Hartbeespoort toets drie eiers in 'n bak koue water. Eier A lê plat op die bodem. Eier B staan regop op die bodem. Eier C dryf bo-op. Rangskik die eiers van die varsste tot die oudste en verduidelik waarom die toets werk. Wat moet sy met eier C doen?","en":"A cook at a guest house in Hartbeespoort tests three eggs in a bowl of cold water. Egg A lies flat on the bottom. Egg B stands upright on the bottom. Egg C floats on top. Arrange the eggs from freshest to oldest and explain why the test works. What should she do with egg C?"},"steps":[{"af":"Die dop is poreus: soos 'n eier ouer word, verdamp vog deur die porieë en die lugsak by die breë punt word groter.","en":"The shell is porous: as an egg ages, moisture evaporates through the pores and the air cell at the broad end gets bigger."},{"af":"'n Groter lugsak maak die eier ligter aan die breë kant, dus kantel dit, staan dit regop of dryf dit uiteindelik.","en":"A bigger air cell makes the egg lighter at the broad end, so it tilts, stands upright or eventually floats."},{"af":"Eier A (plat) het die kleinste lugsak → varsste. Eier B (regop) is ouer. Eier C (dryf) het 'n baie groot lugsak → oudste.","en":"Egg A (flat) has the smallest air cell → freshest. Egg B (upright) is older. Egg C (floats) has a very large air cell → oldest."},{"af":"Eier C is oud en waarskynlik bederf, dus moet dit weggegooi word – moenie dit vir gaste gebruik nie.","en":"Egg C is old and probably stale, so it must be thrown away – don't use it for guests."}],"answer":{"af":"A → B → C (varsste tot oudste). Gooi eier C weg.","en":"A → B → C (freshest to oldest). Throw egg C away."}},{"title":{"af":"Die groen ring en rubberagtige eiers","en":"The green ring and rubbery eggs"},"problem":{"af":"Vir 'n slaaibuffet kook 'n leerling die eiers 20 minute lank en laat dit dan in die warm water afkoel. Die wit is rubberagtig en daar is 'n groengrys ring om elke dooier. (a) Verduidelik wat die ring veroorsaak. (b) Gee twee maniere om dit te voorkom.","en":"For a salad buffet a learner boils the eggs for 20 minutes and then leaves them to cool in the hot water. The white is rubbery and there is a green-grey ring around each yolk. (a) Explain what causes the ring. (b) Give two ways to prevent it."},"steps":[{"af":"Oorkook laat die proteïen in die wit te veel stol en saamtrek → 'n rubberagtige tekstuur.","en":"Overcooking makes the protein in the white set and shrink too much → a rubbery texture."},{"af":"(a) Met lang verhitting kom swael uit die eierwit vry. Dit reageer met die yster in die dooier en vorm groengrys ystersulfied op die oppervlak van die dooier.","en":"(a) With long heating, sulphur is released from the egg white. It reacts with the iron in the yolk and forms green-grey iron sulphide on the surface of the yolk."},{"af":"(b) Kook hardgekookte eiers net ±8–10 minute, nie 20 nie.","en":"(b) Boil hard-boiled eggs for only ±8–10 minutes, not 20."},{"af":"(b) Dompel die eiers dadelik in koue water sodat die kookproses stop – moenie dit in die warm water laat staan nie.","en":"(b) Plunge the eggs into cold water immediately so that cooking stops – don't leave them in the hot water."}],"answer":{"af":"Ystersulfied (swael uit die wit + yster uit die dooier) as gevolg van oorkook. Voorkom: kook net 8–10 min en koel dadelik in koue water af.","en":"Iron sulphide (sulphur from the white + iron from the yolk) caused by overcooking. Prevent: boil only 8–10 min and cool immediately in cold water."}},{"title":{"af":"Stappe vir 'n geposjeerde eier","en":"Steps for a poached egg"},"problem":{"af":"Beskryf die metode om 'n perfekte geposjeerde eier vir 'n ontbyt te maak, en verduidelik die rede vir elke belangrike stap.","en":"Describe the method for making a perfect poached egg for breakfast, and explain the reason for each important step."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik 'n baie vars eier: die dik eierwit hou bymekaar en die eier versprei nie in die water nie.","en":"Use a very fresh egg: the thick white holds together and the egg doesn't spread out in the water."},{"af":"Bring water in 'n vlak pan tot 'n stadige prut en voeg 'n bietjie asyn by – die suur help die wit om vinniger te stol. Die water moet nie vinnig kook nie, anders breek die borrels die eier op.","en":"Bring water in a shallow pan to a gentle simmer and add a little vinegar – the acid helps the white set faster. The water must not boil rapidly, otherwise the bubbles break the egg apart."},{"af":"Breek die eier eers in 'n koppie en laat dit saggies in die water gly, sodat die dooier heel bly.","en":"Break the egg into a cup first and slide it gently into the water, so that the yolk stays whole."},{"af":"Posjeer ±3–4 minute tot die wit gestol is en die dooier nog sag is. Haal uit met 'n gaatjieslepel, dreineer op kombuispapier en bedien dadelik.","en":"Poach for ±3–4 minutes until the white is set and the yolk is still soft. Lift out with a slotted spoon, drain on kitchen paper and serve immediately."}],"answer":{"af":"Vars eier → prutelende water met asyn → eier uit 'n koppie ingly → 3–4 min → met 'n gaatjieslepel uithaal en dreineer.","en":"Fresh egg → simmering water with vinegar → slide the egg in from a cup → 3–4 min → lift out with a slotted spoon and drain."}},{"title":{"af":"Skaal en bereken die koste van 'n omeletresep","en":"Scale and cost an omelette recipe"},"problem":{"af":"'n Spaanse omeletresep vir 4 porsies gebruik 6 eiers en 60 ml melk. 'n Gastehuis in Brits moet 30 porsies vir 'n ontbytfunksie maak. 'n Bak van 30 eiers kos R85,00. (a) Bereken die hoeveelheid eiers en melk. (b) Bereken die koste van die eiers.","en":"A Spanish omelette recipe for 4 portions uses 6 eggs and 60 ml milk. A guest house in Brits has to make 30 portions for a breakfast function. A tray of 30 eggs costs R85.00. (a) Calculate the quantity of eggs and milk. (b) Calculate the cost of the eggs."},"steps":[{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor = vereiste opbrengs ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs = 30 ÷ 4 = 7,5","en":"Conversion factor = required yield ÷ original yield = 30 ÷ 4 = 7.5"},{"af":"Eiers: 6 × 7,5 = 45 eiers. Melk: 60 ml × 7,5 = 450 ml.","en":"Eggs: 6 × 7.5 = 45 eggs. Milk: 60 ml × 7.5 = 450 ml."},{"af":"Koste van eiers = hoeveelheid gebruik ÷ aankoophoeveelheid × aankoopprys = 45 ÷ 30 × R85,00","en":"Cost of eggs = quantity used ÷ purchase quantity × purchase price = 45 ÷ 30 × R85.00"},{"af":"= 1,5 × R85,00 = R127,50 (sy moet dus 2 bakke koop).","en":"= 1.5 × R85.00 = R127.50 (so she must buy 2 trays)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 45 eiers en 450 ml melk; (b) R127,50","en":"(a) 45 eggs and 450 ml milk; (b) R127.50"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar in 'n eier is die lugsak?","en":"Where in an egg is the air cell?"},"options":[{"af":"By die skerp punt","en":"At the pointed end"},{"af":"By die breë punt","en":"At the broad end"},{"af":"In die middel van die dooier","en":"In the centre of the yolk"},{"af":"Tussen die dooier en die chalazae","en":"Between the yolk and the chalazae"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die lugsak lê by die breë punt tussen die twee dopvliese. Daarom bêre jy eiers met die skerp punt na onder.","en":"The air cell lies at the broad end between the two shell membranes. That is why you store eggs pointed end down."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die chalazae hou die dooier in die middel van die eier.","en":"The chalazae hold the yolk in the centre of the egg."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar – die chalazae is twee gedraaide toutjies eierwit wat die dooier gesentreer hou.","en":"True – the chalazae are two twisted cords of egg white that keep the yolk centred."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die deel van die eier wat byna al die vet bevat, is die ___.","en":"The part of the egg that contains almost all the fat is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["dooier","eiergeel","die dooier"],"en":["yolk","egg yolk","the yolk"]},"explain":{"af":"Die dooier bevat die vet (en vitamiene A en D en yster); die wit is feitlik vetvry.","en":"The yolk contains the fat (and vitamins A and D and iron); the white is practically fat-free."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["eierwit","dop","lugsak"],"en":["egg white","shell","air cell"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voedingstof kom NIE in eiers voor nie?","en":"Which nutrient is NOT found in eggs?"},"options":[{"af":"Vitamien A","en":"Vitamin A"},{"af":"Yster","en":"Iron"},{"af":"Vitamien C","en":"Vitamin C"},{"af":"Vitamien D","en":"Vitamin D"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Eiers bevat geen vitamien C nie. Hulle bevat wel proteïen, vet, vitamiene A, D en B en yster.","en":"Eggs contain no vitamin C. They do contain protein, fat, vitamins A, D and B, and iron."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tydens die watertoets dryf 'n eier bo-op die water. Wat beteken dit?","en":"During the water test an egg floats on top of the water. What does this mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Die eier is baie vars en ideaal vir posjeer.","en":"The egg is very fresh and ideal for poaching."},{"af":"Die eier het baie dik eierwit.","en":"The egg has a lot of thick white."},{"af":"Die dop is te dik om water deur te laat.","en":"The shell is too thick to let water through."},{"af":"Die eier is oud – die lugsak is groot, dus gooi dit weg.","en":"The egg is old – the air cell is large, so throw it away."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Vars eier lê plat. Soos vog deur die porieë verdamp, word die lugsak groter; 'n eier wat dryf, is oud en moet weggegooi word.","en":"A fresh egg lies flat. As moisture evaporates through the pores the air cell grows; an egg that floats is old and must be thrown away."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die emulgeerder in eiergeel wat mayonnaise bymekaar hou, is ___.","en":"The emulsifier in egg yolk that holds mayonnaise together is ___."},"answers":{"af":["lesitien","lesitine"],"en":["lecithin"]},"explain":{"af":"Lesitien in die dooier hou die olie- en suurdruppels saam sodat die emulsie nie skei nie.","en":"Lecithin in the yolk holds the oil and acid droplets together so that the emulsion doesn't separate."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gluten","albumien","kollageen"],"en":["gluten","albumen","collagen"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom word eiers met die skerp punt na onder gebêre?","en":"Why are eggs stored pointed end down?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit hou die lugsak bo en die dooier in die middel.","en":"It keeps the air cell at the top and the yolk in the centre."},{"af":"Dit keer dat die dop kraak.","en":"It stops the shell from cracking."},{"af":"Dit laat die eier vinniger afkoel.","en":"It makes the egg cool down faster."},{"af":"Dit maak die porieë in die dop toe.","en":"It closes the pores in the shell."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Met die breë punt bo bly die lugsak waar dit hoort en die dooier bly gesentreer, sodat die eier langer vars bly.","en":"With the broad end up, the air cell stays where it belongs and the yolk stays centred, so the egg stays fresh for longer."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Eierwitte klits tot 'n groter volume as daar 'n bietjie dooier in die bak is.","en":"Egg whites whisk to a bigger volume if there is a little yolk in the bowl."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – die dooier bevat vet, en selfs 'n bietjie vet keer dat die witte 'n stewige skuim vorm.","en":"False – the yolk contains fat, and even a little fat stops the whites from forming a firm foam."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke funksie van eiers by die regte gereg.","en":"Match each function of eggs to the correct dish."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Bind","en":"Binding"},"r":{"af":"Frikkadelle","en":"Frikkadelle"}},{"l":{"af":"Emulgeer","en":"Emulsifying"},"r":{"af":"Mayonnaise","en":"Mayonnaise"}},{"l":{"af":"Belug","en":"Aerating"},"r":{"af":"Sponskoek","en":"Sponge cake"}},{"l":{"af":"Glaseer","en":"Glazing"},"r":{"af":"Eierglans op skons","en":"Egg wash on scones"}},{"l":{"af":"Verhelder","en":"Clarifying"},"r":{"af":"Consommé","en":"Consommé"}}],"explain":{"af":"Bind: eier stol en hou die maalvleis bymekaar. Emulgeer: lesitien hou olie en suur saam. Belug: geklitste eier vang lug vas. Glaseer: gee 'n blink kors. Verhelder: eierwit vang deeltjies in helder sop vas.","en":"Binding: egg sets and holds the mince together. Emulsifying: lecithin holds oil and acid together. Aerating: beaten egg traps air. Glazing: gives a shiny crust. Clarifying: egg white traps particles in clear soup."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Roereierresep vir 2 porsies gebruik 3 eiers. Vir 'n ontbyt vir 14 gaste het jy ___ eiers nodig.","en":"A scrambled-egg recipe for 2 portions uses 3 eggs. For a breakfast for 14 guests you need ___ eggs."},"answers":{"af":["21","21 eiers"],"en":["21","21 eggs"]},"explain":{"af":"Faktor = 14 ÷ 2 = 7. Eiers = 3 × 7 = 21. (42 is 14 × 3 – jy het vergeet om eers deur 2 te deel.)","en":"Factor = 14 ÷ 2 = 7. Eggs = 3 × 7 = 21. (42 is 14 × 3 – you forgot to divide by 2 first.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["42","28","17"],"en":["42","28","17"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kan 'n sagtegekookte eier 'n gestolde wit en 'n lopende dooier hê?","en":"Why can a soft-boiled egg have a set white and a runny yolk?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dooier bevat geen proteïen nie.","en":"The yolk contains no protein."},{"af":"Die chalazae isoleer die dooier teen hitte.","en":"The chalazae insulate the yolk against heat."},{"af":"Die dooier stol by 'n effens hoër temperatuur as die wit.","en":"The yolk sets at a slightly higher temperature than the white."},{"af":"Die lugsak hou die hitte weg van die dooier.","en":"The air cell keeps the heat away from the yolk."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die wit stol by ±60–65 °C en die dooier by ±65–70 °C. Met kort kook stol die wit, maar die dooier bly sag.","en":"The white sets at ±60–65 °C and the yolk at ±65–70 °C. With short cooking the white sets but the yolk stays soft."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die groengrys ring om die dooier van 'n oorgekookte eier bestaan uit ___.","en":"The green-grey ring around the yolk of an overcooked egg consists of ___."},"answers":{"af":["ystersulfied","yster-sulfied"],"en":["iron sulphide","iron sulfide"]},"explain":{"af":"Swael uit die wit reageer met yster in die dooier en vorm ystersulfied. Kook korter en koel dadelik in koue water af.","en":"Sulphur from the white reacts with iron in the yolk to form iron sulphide. Cook for less time and cool immediately in cold water."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kalsiumkarbonaat","lesitien","swaeldioksied"],"en":["calcium carbonate","lecithin","sulphur dioxide"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Roereiers wat 'n uur lank in 'n warm chafing dish op 'n buffet staan, word waterig met vloeistof rondom. Wat het gebeur?","en":"Scrambled eggs that stand in a hot chafing dish on a buffet for an hour become watery with liquid around them. What has happened?"},"options":[{"af":"Gelatinering van die stysel in die eiers.","en":"Gelatinisation of the starch in the eggs."},{"af":"Sinerese – die oorverhitte proteïen het saamgetrek en vloeistof uitgedruk.","en":"Syneresis – the overheated protein shrank and squeezed out liquid."},{"af":"Die eiers was te vars toe dit gekook is.","en":"The eggs were too fresh when they were cooked."},{"af":"Emulgering deur die lesitien in die dooier.","en":"Emulsification by the lecithin in the yolk."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Lang verhitting laat eierproteïen te veel stol; dit trek saam en druk water uit (sinerese). Kook roereiers in klein hoeveelhede en vervang dit gereeld op die buffet.","en":"Long heating makes egg protein set too much; it shrinks and squeezes out water (syneresis). Cook scrambled eggs in small batches and replace them often on the buffet."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Bak van 30 eiers kos R81,00. Die 4 eiers wat in een quiche gebruik word, kos R ___.","en":"A tray of 30 eggs costs R81.00. The 4 eggs used in one quiche cost R ___."},"answers":{"af":["R10,80","10,80","10,8","R10,8"],"en":["R10.80","10.80","10.8","R10.8"]},"explain":{"af":"Koste = 4 ÷ 30 × R81,00 = R10,80. (R2,70 is die prys van net een eier.)","en":"Cost = 4 ÷ 30 × R81.00 = R10.80. (R2.70 is the price of only one egg.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R2,70","R20,25","R10,08"],"en":["R2.70","R20.25","R10.08"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lindiwe se eierwitte wil nie styf klits nie. Wat is die mees waarskynlike rede?","en":"Lindiwe's egg whites won't whisk stiffly. What is the most likely reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy het eiers op kamertemperatuur gebruik.","en":"She used room-temperature eggs."},{"af":"Sy het 'n knippie kremetart bygevoeg.","en":"She added a pinch of cream of tartar."},{"af":"Sy het die suiker geleidelik bygevoeg.","en":"She added the sugar gradually."},{"af":"Sy het 'n plastiekbak gebruik waarin daar nog 'n bietjie botter was.","en":"She used a plastic bowl that still had a little butter in it."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vet (botter, dooier of 'n vetterige plastiekbak) keer dat 'n skuim vorm. Kamertemperatuur, kremetart en geleidelike suiker help juis.","en":"Fat (butter, yolk or a greasy plastic bowl) stops a foam from forming. Room temperature, cream of tartar and gradual sugar actually help."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo sê: \"Ek laat die water vinnig kook en gooi 'n bietjie asyn in sodat my geposjeerde eiers hul vorm hou.\" Evalueer sy stelling.","en":"Thabo says: \"I let the water boil rapidly and add a little vinegar so that my poached eggs keep their shape.\" Evaluate his statement."},"options":[{"af":"Gedeeltelik reg: asyn help die wit stol, maar die water moet net prutel – vinnige kook breek die eier op.","en":"Partly right: vinegar helps the white set, but the water must only simmer – rapid boiling breaks the egg up."},{"af":"Heeltemal reg: hoe vinniger die water kook, hoe beter hou die eier sy vorm.","en":"Completely right: the faster the water boils, the better the egg keeps its shape."},{"af":"Verkeerd: asyn laat die eierwit skif en mag nooit gebruik word nie.","en":"Wrong: vinegar makes the egg white curdle and must never be used."},{"af":"Heeltemal reg: die asyn laat die dooier vinniger stol as die wit.","en":"Completely right: the vinegar makes the yolk set faster than the white."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die suur in asyn laat die eierwit vinniger stol, maar die groot borrels van vinnig kokende water skeur die wit uitmekaar. Posjeer altyd in stadig prutelende water.","en":"The acid in vinegar makes the egg white set faster, but the big bubbles of rapidly boiling water tear the white apart. Always poach in gently simmering water."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t2-graan-suiwel","title":{"af":"Graan, rys en suiwelprodukte","en":"Cereals, rice and dairy products"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal graansoorte, die struktuur van 'n graankorrel, gelatinering en dekstrinering, rystipes en -kookmetodes, en die prosessering, tipes en hantering van suiwelprodukte kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to explain types of cereals, the structure of a grain, gelatinisation and dextrinisation, rice types and cooking methods, and the processing, types and handling of dairy products."},"summary":{"af":"## Graan en styselvoedsel\n\nGraan is die sade van grasse. Dit is 'n goedkoop bron van energie (stysel) en die basis van die meeste Suid-Afrikaanse maaltye.\n\n| Graan | Produkte |\n|---|---|\n| Mielies | mieliemeel (super, spesiaal, gesif, ongesif), stampmielies, mielierys, mielievlokkies (cornflakes), springmielies |\n| Koring | koekmeel, broodmeel, bruismeel, volkoringmeel, semolina, couscous |\n| Rys | witrys, bruinrys, voorafgekookte (parboiled) rys |\n| Hawer | hawermout, hawersemels |\n| Sorghum en gars | mabele (sorghummeel vir pap), gars in sop en bredies |\n\n**Supermieliemeel** is die fynste en meeste verfyn (minste semels). **Ongesifte** mieliemeel bevat die meeste semels en kiem, dus die meeste vesel en voedingstowwe.\n\n### Die struktuur van 'n graankorrel\n\n| Deel | Bevat |\n|---|---|\n| **Semels** (buitenste lae) | vesel, B-vitamiene, minerale |\n| **Endosperm** (grootste deel) | stysel en 'n bietjie proteïen – wit meel kom hiervandaan |\n| **Kiem** (die deel wat kan ontkiem) | vet, vitamien E, B-vitamiene |\n\n- **Volgraan** (volkoringmeel, ongesifte mieliemeel, bruinrys, hawermout) bevat al drie dele → meer vesel en voedingstowwe.\n- **Verfynde** graan (koekmeel, witrys, supermieliemeel): die semels en kiem is verwyder → fyner en witter en dit hou langer, maar met minder vesel en vitamiene.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die kiem bevat vet. Daarom word volgraanprodukte vinniger galsterig – bêre dit koel, droog en toegemaak.\n\n## Die effek van hitte op stysel\n\n- **Gelatinering** (nat hitte): styselkorrels absorbeer vloeistof, swel en bars wanneer dit verhit word → die mengsel **verdik**. Voorbeelde: pap, witsous, vla. Roer aanhoudend en meng die stysel eers met 'n bietjie koue vloeistof om **klonte** te voorkom.\n- **Dekstrinering** (droë hitte): stysel breek af in **dekstriene** → **verbruining** en 'n effens soet geur. Voorbeelde: roosterbrood, die kors van brood.\n\n## Pap en ontbytgraan\n\n- **Stywe pap** (dik en stewig), **slap pap** (sag, vir ontbyt), **krummelpap** (droog en krummelrig, lekker met sous by 'n braai) en **hawermoutpap**.\n- Strooi die meel stadig in kookwater terwyl jy roer, of maak dit eers met koue water aan.\n- Kies ontbytgraan met baie vesel en min suiker (bv. hawermout, semelsvlokkies).\n\n## Rys\n\n| Tipe | Eienskappe | Gebruik |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Langgraan** (basmati, jasmyn) | korrels bly los en donsig | by kerrie, as bykos |\n| **Kort-/mediumgraan** (bv. arborio) | sag, klewerig en romerig | risotto, ryspoeding |\n| **Voorafgekookte (parboiled) rys** | voor verwerking gestoom; korrels bly los en behou meer voedingstowwe | groot hoeveelhede, buffette |\n| **Bruinrys** | semels behou; meer vesel; langer kooktyd | gesonde bykos |\n| **Wilde rys** | eintlik die saad van 'n watergras; donker en neutagtig | slaaie, rysmengsels |\n\n**Kookmetodes:**\n\n1. **Absorpsiemetode:** **1 koppie rys : 2 koppies water** (plus sout). Bring tot kookpunt, sit 'n deksel op en prut tot al die water geabsorbeer is.\n2. **Kook en dreineer:** kook in baie water en dreineer as die rys gaar is.\n3. **Stoom:** in 'n stoommandjie of rysstomer.\n4. **Pilaf:** braai die rys en ui eers liggies in botter of olie, voeg warm aftreksel by en kook toegemaak.\n5. **Risotto:** arborio-rys; voeg warm aftreksel **geleidelik** by terwyl jy roer → romerig.\n\n> **Veiligheid:** Die spore van *Bacillus cereus* oorleef kook. Koel gekookte rys vinnig af, bêre dit in die yskas en moenie dit lank warm hou nie.\n\n## Suiwelprodukte\n\n### Prosessering van melk\n\n- **Pasteurisering:** verhit tot **72 °C vir 15 sekondes** en dan vinnig afgekoel. Dit maak skadelike bakterieë dood; die smaak en voedingswaarde bly feitlik dieselfde. Bêre in die yskas.\n- **UHT (langlewe-melk):** verhit tot 'n **baie hoë temperatuur** (bo 135 °C) vir 'n paar sekondes en steriel verpak. Ongeopend hou dit maande lank sonder 'n yskas; ná oopmaak moet dit in die yskas.\n- **Homogenisering:** melk word onder hoë druk deur klein gaatjies gedruk sodat die **vetbolletjies** opgebreek word en die room nie bo-op uitskei nie.\n\n### Tipes\n\n- **Melk:** volroom, laevet, vetvry (afgeroom), karringmelk, maas (gesuurde melk), kondensmelk (water verwyder, suiker bygevoeg), ingedampte melk (water verwyder, onversoet), melkpoeier.\n- **Room** en **jogurt** (melk wat met goeie bakterieë gegis is).\n- **Kaas:** vars – maaskaas (cottage cheese), roomkaas; sag – brie, camembert; semi-hard – gouda, edam; hard – cheddar, parmesaan.\n\n### Voedingswaarde\n\n**Kalsium en fosfor** (sterk bene en tande), **proteïen** van hoë biologiese waarde, en **vitamiene A, D en B2** (riboflavien). Melk bevat min yster en vitamien C.\n\n### Die effek van hitte\n\n| Probleem | Oorsaak | Voorkoming |\n|---|---|---|\n| 'n Vel vorm | proteïen stol bo-op | roer gereeld, sit 'n deksel op |\n| Aanbrand | proteïen en melksuiker sak en brand vas | lae hitte, swaarboompan, dubbelkoker |\n| Oorkook | stoom word onder die vel vasgevang | lae hitte, hou dop |\n| Skif (stremming) | suur (tamatie, suurlemoen), sout, hoë hitte of ou melk | vars melk, lae hitte, voeg suur stadig by |\n| Kaas word rubberagtig, draderig en olierig | oorverhitting | voeg kaas aan die einde oor lae hitte by; rasper dit fyn |\n\n### Berging\n\nBêre suiwel **in die yskas**, toegemaak, **weg van lig** (lig vernietig riboflavien) en **weg van sterk reuke** (melk neem reuke op).","en":"## Cereals and starchy foods\n\nCereals are the seeds of grasses. They are a cheap source of energy (starch) and the basis of most South African meals.\n\n| Cereal | Products |\n|---|---|\n| Maize | mealie meal (super, special, sifted, unsifted), samp, mealie rice, cornflakes, popcorn |\n| Wheat | cake flour, bread flour, self-raising flour, whole-wheat flour, semolina, couscous |\n| Rice | white rice, brown rice, parboiled rice |\n| Oats | rolled oats, oat bran |\n| Sorghum and barley | mabele (sorghum meal for porridge), barley in soups and stews |\n\n**Super mealie meal** is the finest and most refined (least bran). **Unsifted** mealie meal contains the most bran and germ, so the most fibre and nutrients.\n\n### The structure of a cereal grain\n\n| Part | Contains |\n|---|---|\n| **Bran** (outer layers) | fibre, B vitamins, minerals |\n| **Endosperm** (largest part) | starch and some protein – white flour comes from here |\n| **Germ** (the part that can sprout) | fat, vitamin E, B vitamins |\n\n- **Whole-grain** products (whole-wheat flour, unsifted mealie meal, brown rice, rolled oats) contain all three parts → more fibre and nutrients.\n- **Refined** cereals (cake flour, white rice, super mealie meal): the bran and germ are removed → finer and whiter and they keep longer, but with less fibre and fewer vitamins.\n\n> **Remember!** The germ contains fat. That is why whole-grain products go rancid faster – store them cool, dry and covered.\n\n## The effect of heat on starch\n\n- **Gelatinisation** (moist heat): starch granules absorb liquid, swell and burst when heated → the mixture **thickens**. Examples: porridge, white sauce, custard. Stir continuously and first mix the starch with a little cold liquid to prevent **lumps**.\n- **Dextrinisation** (dry heat): starch breaks down into **dextrins** → **browning** and a slightly sweet flavour. Examples: toast, the crust of bread.\n\n## Porridge and breakfast cereals\n\n- **Stiff porridge** (stywe pap, thick and firm), **soft porridge** (slap pap, for breakfast), **crumbly porridge** (krummelpap, dry and crumbly, great with sauce at a braai) and **oats porridge**.\n- Sprinkle the meal slowly into boiling water while stirring, or first mix it with cold water.\n- Choose breakfast cereals high in fibre and low in sugar (e.g. oats, bran flakes).\n\n## Rice\n\n| Type | Characteristics | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Long-grain** (basmati, jasmine) | grains stay separate and fluffy | with curry, as a side dish |\n| **Short-/medium-grain** (e.g. arborio) | soft, sticky and creamy | risotto, rice pudding |\n| **Parboiled rice** | steamed before processing; grains stay separate and keep more nutrients | large quantities, buffets |\n| **Brown rice** | bran kept; more fibre; longer cooking time | healthy side dish |\n| **Wild rice** | actually the seed of a water grass; dark and nutty | salads, rice mixes |\n\n**Cooking methods:**\n\n1. **Absorption method:** **1 cup rice : 2 cups water** (plus salt). Bring to the boil, put a lid on and simmer until all the water has been absorbed.\n2. **Boiling and draining:** boil in plenty of water and drain when the rice is cooked.\n3. **Steaming:** in a steamer basket or rice steamer.\n4. **Pilaf:** first lightly fry the rice and onion in butter or oil, add hot stock and cook covered.\n5. **Risotto:** arborio rice; add hot stock **gradually** while stirring → creamy.\n\n> **Safety:** The spores of *Bacillus cereus* survive cooking. Cool cooked rice quickly, store it in the fridge and don't keep it warm for long.\n\n## Dairy products\n\n### Milk processing\n\n- **Pasteurisation:** heated to **72 °C for 15 seconds**, then cooled quickly. This kills harmful bacteria; the taste and nutritional value stay practically the same. Store in the fridge.\n- **UHT (long-life milk):** heated to a **very high temperature** (above 135 °C) for a few seconds and packed in sterile containers. Unopened it keeps for months without a fridge; once opened it must go in the fridge.\n- **Homogenisation:** milk is forced under high pressure through tiny holes so that the **fat globules** are broken up and the cream doesn't separate on top.\n\n### Types\n\n- **Milk:** full-cream, low-fat, fat-free (skim), buttermilk, maas (soured milk), condensed milk (water removed, sugar added), evaporated milk (water removed, unsweetened), milk powder.\n- **Cream** and **yoghurt** (milk fermented with good bacteria).\n- **Cheese:** fresh – cottage cheese, cream cheese; soft – brie, camembert; semi-hard – gouda, edam; hard – cheddar, parmesan.\n\n### Nutritional value\n\n**Calcium and phosphorus** (strong bones and teeth), high-biological-value **protein**, and **vitamins A, D and B2** (riboflavin). Milk contains little iron and vitamin C.\n\n### The effect of heat\n\n| Problem | Cause | Prevention |\n|---|---|---|\n| A skin forms | protein sets on top | stir often, put a lid on |\n| Scorching | protein and milk sugar sink and burn on | low heat, heavy-based pan, double boiler |\n| Boiling over | steam is trapped under the skin | low heat, watch it |\n| Curdling | acid (tomato, lemon), salt, high heat or old milk | fresh milk, low heat, add acid slowly |\n| Cheese becomes rubbery, stringy and oily | overheating | add cheese at the end over low heat; grate it finely |\n\n### Storage\n\nStore dairy **in the fridge**, covered, **away from light** (light destroys riboflavin) and **away from strong smells** (milk absorbs smells)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Semels","en":"Bran"},"def":{"af":"Die buitenste lae van 'n graankorrel; ryk aan vesel, B-vitamiene en minerale.","en":"The outer layers of a cereal grain; rich in fibre, B vitamins and minerals."}},{"term":{"af":"Endosperm","en":"Endosperm"},"def":{"af":"Die grootste deel van 'n graankorrel; bevat hoofsaaklik stysel en 'n bietjie proteïen. Wit meel word daarvan gemaak.","en":"The largest part of a cereal grain; contains mainly starch and some protein. White flour is made from it."}},{"term":{"af":"Kiem","en":"Germ"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van die graankorrel wat kan ontkiem; bevat vet, vitamien E en B-vitamiene.","en":"The part of the cereal grain that can sprout; contains fat, vitamin E and B vitamins."}},{"term":{"af":"Volgraan","en":"Whole-grain"},"def":{"af":"Graanprodukte wat al drie dele van die korrel (semels, endosperm en kiem) bevat.","en":"Cereal products that contain all three parts of the grain (bran, endosperm and germ)."}},{"term":{"af":"Gelatinering","en":"Gelatinisation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer styselkorrels met nat hitte vloeistof absorbeer, swel en bars, sodat die mengsel verdik.","en":"When starch granules absorb liquid with moist heat, swell and burst, so that the mixture thickens."}},{"term":{"af":"Dekstrinering","en":"Dextrinisation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer stysel met droë hitte in dekstriene afbreek en bruin word, bv. roosterbrood.","en":"When starch breaks down into dextrins with dry heat and turns brown, e.g. toast."}},{"term":{"af":"Absorpsiemetode","en":"Absorption method"},"def":{"af":"'n Metode om rys te kook waar 'n afgemete hoeveelheid water (1 : 2) heeltemal deur die rys opgeneem word.","en":"A method of cooking rice in which a measured amount of water (1 : 2) is completely absorbed by the rice."}},{"term":{"af":"Pasteurisering","en":"Pasteurisation"},"def":{"af":"Melk word tot 72 °C vir 15 sekondes verhit en vinnig afgekoel om skadelike bakterieë dood te maak.","en":"Milk is heated to 72 °C for 15 seconds and cooled quickly to kill harmful bacteria."}},{"term":{"af":"Homogenisering","en":"Homogenisation"},"def":{"af":"Melk word onder druk deur klein gaatjies gedruk om die vetbolletjies op te breek sodat die room nie uitskei nie.","en":"Milk is forced under pressure through tiny holes to break up the fat globules so that the cream doesn't separate."}},{"term":{"af":"Skif (stremming)","en":"Curdling"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer melkproteïen as gevolg van suur, sout of te veel hitte in klonte saamklont en van die vloeistof skei.","en":"When milk protein clumps into lumps and separates from the liquid because of acid, salt or too much heat."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skaal 'n rysresep","en":"Scale a rice recipe"},"problem":{"af":"'n Rysresep (absorpsiemetode) vir 4 porsies gebruik 250 ml rys, 500 ml water en 2,5 ml sout. Die skoolkoshuis in Brits het 30 porsies nodig. Bereken die nuwe hoeveelhede.","en":"A rice recipe (absorption method) for 4 portions uses 250 ml rice, 500 ml water and 2.5 ml salt. The school hostel in Brits needs 30 portions. Calculate the new quantities."},"steps":[{"af":"Omskakelingsfaktor = vereiste opbrengs ÷ oorspronklike opbrengs = 30 ÷ 4 = 7,5","en":"Conversion factor = required yield ÷ original yield = 30 ÷ 4 = 7.5"},{"af":"Rys: 250 ml × 7,5 = 1 875 ml (= 1,875 ℓ)","en":"Rice: 250 ml × 7.5 = 1 875 ml (= 1.875 ℓ)"},{"af":"Water: 500 ml × 7,5 = 3 750 ml (= 3,75 ℓ). Kontroleer: die verhouding bly 1 : 2.","en":"Water: 500 ml × 7.5 = 3 750 ml (= 3.75 ℓ). Check: the ratio stays 1 : 2."},{"af":"Sout: 2,5 ml × 7,5 = 18,75 ml – in die praktyk ± 1 eetlepel (15 ml) plus 'n bietjie minder as 1 teelepel (5 ml).","en":"Salt: 2.5 ml × 7.5 = 18.75 ml – in practice ± 1 tablespoon (15 ml) plus a little less than 1 teaspoon (5 ml)."}],"answer":{"af":"1 875 ml rys, 3 750 ml water en 18,75 ml sout","en":"1 875 ml rice, 3 750 ml water and 18.75 ml salt"}},{"title":{"af":"Gelatinering teenoor dekstrinering","en":"Gelatinisation versus dextrinisation"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik wat met die stysel gebeur wanneer (a) jy mieliepap kook en (b) jy brood rooster. Noem die term vir elke verandering.","en":"Explain what happens to the starch when (a) you cook mealie-meal porridge and (b) you toast bread. Name the term for each change."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Pap word met water (nat hitte) gekook. Die styselkorrels absorbeer water, swel en bars, en die pap verdik.","en":"(a) Porridge is cooked with water (moist heat). The starch granules absorb water, swell and burst, and the porridge thickens."},{"af":"Dit is gelatinering. Roer aanhoudend, anders vorm klonte waar korrels aan mekaar vasklou.","en":"This is gelatinisation. Stir continuously, otherwise lumps form where granules stick together."},{"af":"(b) Roosterbrood word met droë hitte verhit. Die stysel breek af in dekstriene wat bruin is en effens soet proe.","en":"(b) Toast is heated with dry heat. The starch breaks down into dextrins, which are brown and taste slightly sweet."},{"af":"Dit is dekstrinering.","en":"This is dextrinisation."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Gelatinering (nat hitte, verdikking); (b) dekstrinering (droë hitte, verbruining)","en":"(a) Gelatinisation (moist heat, thickening); (b) dextrinisation (dry heat, browning)"}},{"title":{"af":"Wat het met die kaassous verkeerd gegaan?","en":"What went wrong with the cheese sauce?"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter maak kaassous vir makaroni-en-kaas. Hy verhit die melk oor hoë hitte in 'n dun pan sonder om te roer, gooi dan groot stukke kaas in en laat die sous 10 minute kook. Die sous het 'n vel, is onder aangebrand en die kaas is draderig en olierig. Identifiseer drie foute en gee die regstelling vir elkeen.","en":"Pieter makes cheese sauce for macaroni and cheese. He heats the milk over high heat in a thin pan without stirring, then adds big pieces of cheese and lets the sauce boil for 10 minutes. The sauce has a skin, has scorched at the bottom and the cheese is stringy and oily. Identify three mistakes and give the correction for each."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: Hy het nie geroer nie → proteïen het bo-op gestol en 'n vel gevorm. Regstelling: roer gereeld of sit 'n deksel op.","en":"Mistake 1: He did not stir → protein set on top and formed a skin. Correction: stir often or put a lid on."},{"af":"Fout 2: Hoë hitte in 'n dun pan → proteïen en melksuiker het gesak en vasgebrand. Regstelling: lae hitte en 'n swaarboompan of dubbelkoker.","en":"Mistake 2: High heat in a thin pan → protein and milk sugar sank and burnt on. Correction: low heat and a heavy-based pan or double boiler."},{"af":"Fout 3: Hy het die kaas gekook → oorverhitting maak kaas rubberagtig, draderig en olierig. Regstelling: rasper die kaas fyn en roer dit aan die einde oor lae hitte in.","en":"Mistake 3: He boiled the cheese → overheating makes cheese rubbery, stringy and oily. Correction: grate the cheese finely and stir it in at the end over low heat."}],"answer":{"af":"Roer/deksel (vel); lae hitte en swaarboompan (aanbrand); fyn gerasperde kaas aan die einde oor lae hitte (draderig/olierig).","en":"Stir/lid (skin); low heat and heavy-based pan (scorching); finely grated cheese at the end over low heat (stringy/oily)."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk mieliemeelsoorte","en":"Compare types of mealie meal"},"problem":{"af":"'n Winkel in Madibeng verkoop supermieliemeel en ongesifte mieliemeel. Verwys na die struktuur van 'n graankorrel en verduidelik watter een die beter keuse vir gesondheid is en waarom die ander langer hou.","en":"A shop in Madibeng sells super mealie meal and unsifted mealie meal. Refer to the structure of a cereal grain and explain which one is the better choice for health and why the other one keeps longer."},"steps":[{"af":"'n Graankorrel het drie dele: semels (vesel, B-vitamiene, minerale), endosperm (stysel) en kiem (vet, vitamien E, B-vitamiene).","en":"A cereal grain has three parts: bran (fibre, B vitamins, minerals), endosperm (starch) and germ (fat, vitamin E, B vitamins)."},{"af":"Ongesifte mieliemeel bevat meer van die semels en kiem → meer vesel, vitamiene en minerale. Dit is die gesonder keuse.","en":"Unsifted mealie meal contains more of the bran and germ → more fibre, vitamins and minerals. It is the healthier choice."},{"af":"Supermieliemeel is hoofsaaklik endosperm; die vetryke kiem is verwyder, dus word dit nie so maklik galsterig nie en hou dit langer.","en":"Super mealie meal is mainly endosperm; the fat-rich germ has been removed, so it doesn't go rancid as easily and keeps longer."}],"answer":{"af":"Ongesifte mieliemeel is gesonder (semels en kiem); supermieliemeel hou langer (geen vetryke kiem nie).","en":"Unsifted mealie meal is healthier (bran and germ); super mealie meal keeps longer (no fat-rich germ)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deel van 'n graankorrel bevat die meeste vesel?","en":"Which part of a cereal grain contains the most fibre?"},"options":[{"af":"Endosperm","en":"Endosperm"},{"af":"Kiem","en":"Germ"},{"af":"Semels","en":"Bran"},{"af":"Stysel","en":"Starch"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die semels is die buitenste lae van die korrel en bevat die meeste vesel, B-vitamiene en minerale.","en":"The bran is the outer layers of the grain and contains the most fibre, B vitamins and minerals."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wit meel word hoofsaaklik van die ___ van die koringkorrel gemaak.","en":"White flour is made mainly from the ___ of the wheat grain."},"answers":{"af":["endosperm"],"en":["endosperm"]},"explain":{"af":"Wit meel is verfyn: die semels en kiem word verwyder, en net die stysel-ryke endosperm bly oor.","en":"White flour is refined: the bran and germ are removed, and only the starch-rich endosperm remains."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["semels","kiem","dop"],"en":["bran","germ","husk"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gepasteuriseerde melk word tot 72 °C vir 15 sekondes verhit en dan vinnig afgekoel.","en":"Pasteurised milk is heated to 72 °C for 15 seconds and then cooled quickly."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar – dit maak skadelike bakterieë dood sonder om die smaak en voedingswaarde veel te verander.","en":"True – this kills harmful bacteria without changing the taste and nutritional value much."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter van die volgende is 'n harde kaas?","en":"Which of the following is a hard cheese?"},"options":[{"af":"Maaskaas","en":"Cottage cheese"},{"af":"Camembert","en":"Camembert"},{"af":"Gouda","en":"Gouda"},{"af":"Parmesaan","en":"Parmesan"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Parmesaan (en cheddar) is harde kase. Maaskaas is vars, camembert is sag en gouda is semi-hard.","en":"Parmesan (and cheddar) are hard cheeses. Cottage cheese is fresh, camembert is soft and gouda is semi-hard."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is homogenisering?","en":"What is homogenisation?"},"options":[{"af":"Melk word vir 'n paar sekondes bo 135 °C verhit.","en":"Milk is heated above 135 °C for a few seconds."},{"af":"Melk word onder druk deur klein gaatjies gedruk om die vetbolletjies op te breek.","en":"Milk is forced under pressure through tiny holes to break up the fat globules."},{"af":"Water word uit melk verwyder en suiker word bygevoeg.","en":"Water is removed from milk and sugar is added."},{"af":"Goeie bakterieë word by melk gevoeg om dit te laat gis.","en":"Good bacteria are added to milk to make it ferment."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Homogenisering breek die vetbolletjies op sodat die room nie bo-op uitskei nie. Die ander opsies beskryf UHT, kondensmelk en jogurt.","en":"Homogenisation breaks up the fat globules so that the cream doesn't separate on top. The other options describe UHT, condensed milk and yoghurt."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"By die absorpsiemetode gebruik jy 1 koppie rys vir ___ koppies water.","en":"In the absorption method you use 1 cup of rice for ___ cups of water."},"answers":{"af":["2","twee"],"en":["2","two"]},"explain":{"af":"Die verhouding is 1 : 2. Met 'n deksel op word al die water deur die rys geabsorbeer.","en":"The ratio is 1 : 2. With a lid on, all the water is absorbed by the rice."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","3","4"],"en":["1","3","4"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorbeeld toon dekstrinering?","en":"Which example shows dextrinisation?"},"options":[{"af":"Brood word bruin in die rooster.","en":"Bread turns brown in the toaster."},{"af":"Witsous verdik op die stoof.","en":"White sauce thickens on the stove."},{"af":"Mieliepap word dik terwyl dit kook.","en":"Mealie-meal porridge becomes thick while it cooks."},{"af":"Vla verdik wanneer dit verhit word.","en":"Custard thickens when it is heated."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dekstrinering gebeur met droë hitte en veroorsaak verbruining. Die ander drie is voorbeelde van gelatinering (nat hitte, verdikking).","en":"Dextrinisation happens with dry heat and causes browning. The other three are examples of gelatinisation (moist heat, thickening)."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke rystipe by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each type of rice to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Basmati","en":"Basmati"},"r":{"af":"Langgraan; korrels bly los en donsig","en":"Long-grain; grains stay separate and fluffy"}},{"l":{"af":"Arborio","en":"Arborio"},"r":{"af":"Gebruik vir romerige risotto","en":"Used for creamy risotto"}},{"l":{"af":"Bruinrys","en":"Brown rice"},"r":{"af":"Semels behou; meer vesel","en":"Bran kept; more fibre"}},{"l":{"af":"Wilde rys","en":"Wild rice"},"r":{"af":"Eintlik die saad van 'n watergras","en":"Actually the seed of a water grass"}},{"l":{"af":"Voorafgekookte rys","en":"Parboiled rice"},"r":{"af":"Voor verwerking gestoom; korrels bly los","en":"Steamed before processing; grains stay separate"}}],"explain":{"af":"Langgraan (basmati) bly los; kort-/mediumgraan (arborio) is romerig; bruinrys behou die semels; wilde rys is nie ware rys nie; parboiled rys is vooraf gestoom.","en":"Long-grain (basmati) stays separate; short-/medium-grain (arborio) is creamy; brown rice keeps the bran; wild rice is not true rice; parboiled rice is steamed beforehand."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Ongesifte mieliemeel bevat minder vesel as supermieliemeel.","en":"Unsifted mealie meal contains less fibre than super mealie meal."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – ongesifte mieliemeel bevat meer semels en kiem en dus méér vesel. Supermieliemeel is die meeste verfyn.","en":"False – unsifted mealie meal contains more bran and germ and therefore more fibre. Super mealie meal is the most refined."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy verhit melk vir warm sjokolade by 'n koffiewinkel in Brits. Hoe voorkom jy dat 'n vel bo-op vorm?","en":"You are heating milk for hot chocolate at a coffee shop in Brits. How do you prevent a skin from forming on top?"},"options":[{"af":"Voeg 'n bietjie suurlemoensap by.","en":"Add a little lemon juice."},{"af":"Kook die melk vinnig oor hoë hitte.","en":"Boil the milk quickly over high heat."},{"af":"Roer gereeld of sit 'n deksel op die kastrol.","en":"Stir often or put a lid on the saucepan."},{"af":"Voeg 'n knippie sout by.","en":"Add a pinch of salt."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die vel is proteïen wat bo-op stol. Roer of 'n deksel keer dit. Suur en sout laat melk skif, en hoë hitte laat dit aanbrand en oorkook.","en":"The skin is protein that sets on top. Stirring or a lid prevents it. Acid and salt make milk curdle, and high heat makes it scorch and boil over."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Rysresep vir 6 porsies gebruik 375 ml rys. Vir 24 porsies het jy ___ ml rys nodig.","en":"A rice recipe for 6 portions uses 375 ml rice. For 24 portions you need ___ ml rice."},"answers":{"af":["1 500","1500","1 500 ml","1500 ml","1,5 ℓ","1,5 l"],"en":["1 500","1500","1 500 ml","1500 ml","1.5 ℓ","1.5 l"]},"explain":{"af":"Faktor = 24 ÷ 6 = 4. Rys = 375 ml × 4 = 1 500 ml. (9 000 is 375 × 24 – jy het vergeet om deur 6 te deel.)","en":"Factor = 24 ÷ 6 = 4. Rice = 375 ml × 4 = 1 500 ml. (9 000 is 375 × 24 – you forgot to divide by 6.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["750","2 250","9 000"],"en":["750","2 250","9 000"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Volgraanmeel word vinniger galsterig omdat die kiem ___ bevat.","en":"Whole-grain flour goes rancid faster because the germ contains ___."},"answers":{"af":["vet","olie","vette"],"en":["fat","oil","fats"]},"explain":{"af":"Die vet in die kiem oksideer en word galsterig. Verfynde meel (sonder kiem) hou daarom langer.","en":"The fat in the germ oxidises and goes rancid. Refined flour (without germ) therefore keeps longer."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["stysel","vesel","suiker"],"en":["starch","fibre","sugar"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kafee hou 'n groot pot gekookte rys die hele dag op lae hitte op die stoof warm. Wat is die grootste gevaar?","en":"A café keeps a big pot of cooked rice warm on low heat on the stove all day. What is the biggest danger?"},"options":[{"af":"Die rys gelatineer verder en word te dik.","en":"The rice gelatinises further and becomes too thick."},{"af":"Dekstrinering maak die rys bruin.","en":"Dextrinisation turns the rice brown."},{"af":"Die rys verloor al sy stysel.","en":"The rice loses all its starch."},{"af":"Bacillus cereus kan groei en gifstowwe vorm wat voedselvergiftiging veroorsaak.","en":"Bacillus cereus can grow and form toxins that cause food poisoning."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die spore van Bacillus cereus oorleef kook en groei in lou rys. Koel rys vinnig af en hou dit nie lank warm nie.","en":"The spores of Bacillus cereus survive cooking and grow in lukewarm rice. Cool rice quickly and don't keep it warm for long."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir 'n kampeertoer in die Magaliesberg sonder 'n yskas is ___ die beste keuse, want dit hou ongeopend maande lank.","en":"For a camping trip in the Magaliesberg without a fridge, ___ is the best choice, because it keeps for months unopened."},"answers":{"af":["UHT-melk","UHT","langlewe-melk","langlewemelk","langlewe"],"en":["UHT milk","UHT","long-life milk","long-life"]},"explain":{"af":"UHT-melk word bo 135 °C verhit en steriel verpak, dus hou dit sonder 'n yskas tot dit oopgemaak word. Gepasteuriseerde melk moet altyd in die yskas bly.","en":"UHT milk is heated above 135 °C and packed in sterile containers, so it keeps without a fridge until it is opened. Pasteurised milk must always stay in the fridge."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gepasteuriseerde melk","volroommelk","karringmelk"],"en":["pasteurised milk","full-cream milk","buttermilk"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter se kaassous is draderig en olierig. Wat is die mees waarskynlike oorsaak?","en":"Pieter's cheese sauce is stringy and oily. What is the most likely cause?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kaas was te fyn gerasper.","en":"The cheese was grated too finely."},{"af":"Die kaas is oorverhit – hy het die sous laat kook nadat die kaas bygevoeg is.","en":"The cheese was overheated – he let the sauce boil after the cheese was added."},{"af":"Hy het die kaas aan die einde oor lae hitte bygevoeg.","en":"He added the cheese at the end over low heat."},{"af":"Hy het 'n swaarboompan gebruik.","en":"He used a heavy-based pan."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Oorverhitting laat die kaasproteïen saamtrek (draderig) en die vet uitskei (olierig). Die ander drie is juis die korrekte manier van werk.","en":"Overheating makes the cheese protein shrink (stringy) and the fat separate (oily). The other three are actually the correct way of working."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Skoolkoshuis wil die voedingswaarde van ontbyt verbeter sonder om baie meer te spandeer. Watter voorstel is die beste?","en":"A school hostel wants to improve the nutritional value of breakfast without spending much more. Which suggestion is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"Vervang die slap pap van supermieliemeel met hawermout of ongesifte mieliemeel en bedien dit met melk.","en":"Replace the soft porridge made from super mealie meal with oats or unsifted mealie meal and serve it with milk."},{"af":"Vervang volkoringbrood met witbrood omdat dit langer hou.","en":"Replace whole-wheat bread with white bread because it keeps longer."},{"af":"Bedien die pap met ekstra suiker vir meer energie.","en":"Serve the porridge with extra sugar for more energy."},{"af":"Vervang die melk met koffieromer om geld te spaar.","en":"Replace the milk with coffee creamer to save money."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Volgraan gee meer vesel, B-vitamiene en minerale, en melk voeg kalsium en proteïen by – teen min ekstra koste. Witbrood, suiker en koffieromer verlaag die voedingswaarde.","en":"Whole grains give more fibre, B vitamins and minerals, and milk adds calcium and protein – at little extra cost. White bread, sugar and coffee creamer lower the nutritional value."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Voeding, spyskaartbeplanning, maalvleis, pasta en slaaie","en":"Nutrition, menu planning, minced meat, pasta and salads"},"topics":[{"id":"gas10-t3-voeding","title":{"af":"Voeding: voedingstowwe en die voedselpiramide","en":"Nutrition: nutrients and the food pyramid"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die funksies, bronne en tekortsiektes van die voedingstowwe ken, kJ kan bereken en 'n maaltyd teen die voedselpiramide en die dieetriglyne kan evalueer.","en":"You will know the functions, sources and deficiency diseases of the nutrients, be able to calculate kJ and evaluate a meal against the food pyramid and the dietary guidelines."},"summary":{"af":"## Voedingstowwe\n\n**Voedingstowwe** is die stowwe in voedsel wat die liggaam nodig het vir energie, groei en herstel, en om liggaamsprosesse te reguleer. Daar is ses: koolhidrate, proteïene, vette, vitamiene, minerale en water.\n\n### Koolhidrate\n- **Funksie:** die **hoofbron van energie**.\n- **Tipes:** suikers, stysel en **vesel** (sellulose).\n- **Bronne:** mieliepap, brood, rys, aartappels, pasta, vrugte, suiker.\n- **Vesel** word nie verteer nie; dit help met **vertering** en voorkom **hardlywigheid**. Bronne: volgraan, groente, vrugte met skil, droëbone.\n- Te veel: vetsug en tandbederf (suiker).\n\n### Proteïene\n- **Funksie:** **groei en herstel** van selle en weefsel; ook 'n bron van energie. Proteïen is uit **aminosure** opgebou.\n- **Hoë biologiese waarde (HBW)** – bevat al die noodsaaklike aminosure: vleis, hoender, vis, eiers, melk, kaas (en soja).\n- **Lae biologiese waarde (LBW)** – plantbronne: droëbone, lensies, ertjies, neute, graan. Kombineer dit (bv. pap en bone) om al die aminosure te kry.\n- **Kwashiorkor:** tekort aan **proteïen** – opgeswelde maag en bene (water in die weefsel), haar verkleur, velsere.\n- **Marasmus:** tekort aan **energie én proteïen** – die kind is uitgeteer, \"vel en been\".\n\n### Vette\n- **Funksie:** gekonsentreerde energie, **isolasie**, **beskerm organe** en dra die vetoplosbare vitamiene A, D, E en K.\n- **Versadigde vette:** meestal dierlik en vas by kamertemperatuur (botter, varkvet, vet op vleis).\n- **Onversadigde vette:** meestal plantaardig en vloeibaar (sonneblomolie, olyfolie, avokado, neute, vetterige vis).\n- Te veel (veral versadigde vet) → vetsug, hoë cholesterol en hartsiektes.\n\n### Vitamiene\n\n| Vitamien | Funksie | Bronne | Tekort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A (vetoplosbaar) | sig in dowwe lig, gesonde vel | lewer, eiergeel, wortels, patats, donkergroen groente | nagblindheid |\n| D (vetoplosbaar) | help kalsium opneem vir bene en tande | sonlig, vetterige vis, eiergeel | ragitis (sagte, krom bene) |\n| E (vetoplosbaar) | beskerm selle (antioksidant) | plantolies, neute, koringkiem | seldsaam |\n| K (vetoplosbaar) | bloedstolling | groen blaargroente | bloed stol swak |\n| B-groep (wateroplosbaar) | stel energie uit voedsel vry; senuweestelsel | volgraan, vleis, melk, eiers | niasien (B3) → **pellagra**, gekoppel aan diëte van hoofsaaklik mielies |\n| C (wateroplosbaar) | gesonde tandvleis en vel, wondgenesing, weerstand; help yster opneem | sitrus, koejawels, soetrissies, tamaties | **skeurbuik** (bloeiende tandvleis) |\n\n> **Onthou!** Wateroplosbare vitamiene (B en C) word nie in die liggaam gestoor nie – jy het dit elke dag nodig, en dit gaan maklik in kookwater verlore.\n\n### Minerale\n\n| Mineraal | Funksie | Bronne | Tekort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Kalsium | sterk bene en tande | melk, maas, kaas, jogurt, sardiens | swak, bros bene |\n| Yster | vorm hemoglobien in rooibloedselle (dra suurstof) | rooivleis, lewer, donkergroen blaargroente, droëbone | **bloedarmoede (anemie)**: moeg en bleek |\n| Jodium | laat die skildklier reg werk | **gejodeerde sout**, seekos | **kropgeswel** (goiter) |\n\n### Water\nVervoer voedingstowwe, reguleer liggaamstemperatuur, help met vertering en verwyder afval.\n\n## Energiewaarde\n\n| Voedingstof | Energie per gram |\n|---|---|\n| Koolhidrate | 17 kJ |\n| Proteïen | 17 kJ |\n| Vet | 37 kJ |\n\n`Energie (kJ) = (g koolhidrate × 17) + (g proteïen × 17) + (g vet × 37)`\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders gebruik 17 kJ vir alles. Vet gee meer as twee keer soveel energie per gram!\n\n## Die voedselpiramide\n\nVan onder na bo: **styselvoedsel** (eet die meeste) → **groente en vrugte** → **proteïenvoedsel en suiwel** → bo-aan **vette, olies en suiker** (spaarsamig). Drink baie skoon water.\n\n## SA Voedselgebaseerde Dieetriglyne\n\n1. Geniet 'n verskeidenheid voedsel.\n2. Wees aktief.\n3. Maak styselvoedsel deel van die meeste maaltye.\n4. Eet elke dag baie groente en vrugte.\n5. Eet gereeld droëbone, split-ertjies, lensies en soja.\n6. Drink elke dag melk, maas of jogurt.\n7. Vis, hoender, maer vleis of eiers kan daagliks geëet word.\n8. Drink baie skoon, veilige water.\n9. Gebruik vette spaarsamig.\n10. Gebruik suiker spaarsamig.\n11. Gebruik sout spaarsamig.\n\nDie **SA Voedselgids** het **7 voedselgroepe**: styselvoedsel; groente en vrugte; droëbone, split-ertjies, lensies en soja; hoender, vis, vleis en eiers; melk, maas of jogurt; vette en olie; water.\n\n## Beplanning van 'n gebalanseerde maaltyd\n\n- **Bord:** ½ groente en slaai, ¼ stysel, ¼ proteïen.\n- **Tieners** het baie **energie** vir groei en aktiwiteit nodig, **kalsium** vir bene wat nog groei, **yster** (veral meisies, weens menstruasie) en proteïen.\n\n## Spesiale diëte\n\n- **Vegetaries:** lakto-ovo (eet melk en eiers); lakto (melk, geen eiers). **Veganisties:** geen diereprodukte nie – kombineer peulgewasse en graan vir proteïen, en let op yster, kalsium en vitamien B12.\n- **Halaal** (Moslem): geen varkvleis of alkohol nie.\n- **Kosher** (Joods): geen varkvleis of skulpvis nie; vleis en suiwel word nie saam berei of geëet nie.\n- **Diabeties:** beheer suiker en koolhidrate; hoë vesel en gereelde maaltye.\n- **Allergieë en intoleransies:** neute (kan lewensgevaarlike anafilaktiese skok veroorsaak), gluten (seliakie – geen koring, rog of gars nie), laktose (kan melksuiker nie verteer nie – gebruik laktosevrye melk).","en":"## Nutrients\n\n**Nutrients** are the substances in food that the body needs for energy, growth and repair, and to regulate body processes. There are six: carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals and water.\n\n### Carbohydrates\n- **Function:** the **main source of energy**.\n- **Types:** sugars, starch and **fibre** (cellulose).\n- **Sources:** mealie-meal porridge, bread, rice, potatoes, pasta, fruit, sugar.\n- **Fibre** is not digested; it aids **digestion** and prevents **constipation**. Sources: whole grains, vegetables, fruit with the skin, dry beans.\n- Too much: obesity and tooth decay (sugar).\n\n### Proteins\n- **Function:** **growth and repair** of cells and tissue; also a source of energy. Protein is built from **amino acids**.\n- **High biological value (HBV)** – contains all the essential amino acids: meat, chicken, fish, eggs, milk, cheese (and soya).\n- **Low biological value (LBV)** – plant sources: dry beans, lentils, peas, nuts, cereals. Combine them (e.g. pap and beans) to get all the amino acids.\n- **Kwashiorkor:** a lack of **protein** – swollen belly and legs (fluid in the tissue), hair loses colour, skin sores.\n- **Marasmus:** a lack of **energy and protein** – the child is wasted, \"skin and bones\".\n\n### Fats\n- **Function:** concentrated energy, **insulation**, **protect organs** and carry the fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E and K.\n- **Saturated fats:** mostly from animals and solid at room temperature (butter, lard, fat on meat).\n- **Unsaturated fats:** mostly from plants and liquid (sunflower oil, olive oil, avocado, nuts, oily fish).\n- Too much (especially saturated fat) → obesity, high cholesterol and heart disease.\n\n### Vitamins\n\n| Vitamin | Function | Sources | Deficiency |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A (fat-soluble) | vision in dim light, healthy skin | liver, egg yolk, carrots, sweet potatoes, dark-green vegetables | night blindness |\n| D (fat-soluble) | helps absorb calcium for bones and teeth | sunlight, oily fish, egg yolk | rickets (soft, bent bones) |\n| E (fat-soluble) | protects cells (antioxidant) | plant oils, nuts, wheat germ | rare |\n| K (fat-soluble) | blood clotting | green leafy vegetables | blood clots poorly |\n| B group (water-soluble) | releases energy from food; nervous system | whole grains, meat, milk, eggs | niacin (B3) → **pellagra**, linked to maize-heavy diets |\n| C (water-soluble) | healthy gums and skin, wound healing, resistance; helps absorb iron | citrus, guavas, sweet peppers, tomatoes | **scurvy** (bleeding gums) |\n\n> **Remember!** Water-soluble vitamins (B and C) are not stored in the body – you need them every day, and they are easily lost into cooking water.\n\n### Minerals\n\n| Mineral | Function | Sources | Deficiency |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Calcium | strong bones and teeth | milk, maas, cheese, yoghurt, sardines | weak, brittle bones |\n| Iron | forms haemoglobin in red blood cells (carries oxygen) | red meat, liver, dark-green leafy vegetables, dry beans | **anaemia**: tired and pale |\n| Iodine | makes the thyroid gland work properly | **iodised salt**, seafood | **goitre** |\n\n### Water\nTransports nutrients, regulates body temperature, aids digestion and removes waste.\n\n## Energy value\n\n| Nutrient | Energy per gram |\n|---|---|\n| Carbohydrates | 17 kJ |\n| Protein | 17 kJ |\n| Fat | 37 kJ |\n\n`Energy (kJ) = (g carbohydrate × 17) + (g protein × 17) + (g fat × 37)`\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners use 17 kJ for everything. Fat gives more than twice as much energy per gram!\n\n## The food pyramid\n\nFrom bottom to top: **starchy foods** (eat the most) → **vegetables and fruit** → **protein foods and dairy** → at the top **fats, oils and sugar** (sparingly). Drink plenty of clean water.\n\n## SA Food-Based Dietary Guidelines\n\n1. Enjoy a variety of foods.\n2. Be active.\n3. Make starchy foods part of most meals.\n4. Eat plenty of vegetables and fruit every day.\n5. Eat dry beans, split peas, lentils and soya regularly.\n6. Have milk, maas or yoghurt every day.\n7. Fish, chicken, lean meat or eggs can be eaten daily.\n8. Drink lots of clean, safe water.\n9. Use fats sparingly.\n10. Use sugar sparingly.\n11. Use salt sparingly.\n\nThe **SA Food Guide** has **7 food groups**: starchy foods; vegetables and fruit; dry beans, split peas, lentils and soya; chicken, fish, meat and eggs; milk, maas or yoghurt; fats and oil; water.\n\n## Planning a balanced meal\n\n- **Plate:** ½ vegetables and salad, ¼ starch, ¼ protein.\n- **Teenagers** need a lot of **energy** for growth and activity, **calcium** for bones that are still growing, **iron** (especially girls, because of menstruation) and protein.\n\n## Special diets\n\n- **Vegetarian:** lacto-ovo (eats milk and eggs); lacto (milk, no eggs). **Vegan:** no animal products at all – combine legumes and cereals for protein, and watch iron, calcium and vitamin B12.\n- **Halaal** (Muslim): no pork or alcohol.\n- **Kosher** (Jewish): no pork or shellfish; meat and dairy are not prepared or eaten together.\n- **Diabetic:** control sugar and carbohydrates; high fibre and regular meals.\n- **Allergies and intolerances:** nuts (can cause life-threatening anaphylactic shock), gluten (coeliac disease – no wheat, rye or barley), lactose (cannot digest milk sugar – use lactose-free milk)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Voedingstowwe","en":"Nutrients"},"def":{"af":"Stowwe in voedsel wat die liggaam nodig het vir energie, groei en herstel en om liggaamsprosesse te reguleer.","en":"Substances in food that the body needs for energy, growth and repair and to regulate body processes."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoë biologiese waarde (HBW)","en":"High biological value (HBV)"},"def":{"af":"Proteïen wat al die noodsaaklike aminosure bevat, bv. vleis, eiers, melk en soja.","en":"Protein that contains all the essential amino acids, e.g. meat, eggs, milk and soya."}},{"term":{"af":"Vesel (sellulose)","en":"Fibre (cellulose)"},"def":{"af":"Die onverteerbare deel van plantvoedsel wat vertering help en hardlywigheid voorkom.","en":"The indigestible part of plant foods that aids digestion and prevents constipation."}},{"term":{"af":"Kwashiorkor","en":"Kwashiorkor"},"def":{"af":"'n Tekortsiekte as gevolg van te min proteïen; die maag en bene swel op en die hare verkleur.","en":"A deficiency disease caused by too little protein; the belly and legs swell and the hair loses colour."}},{"term":{"af":"Marasmus","en":"Marasmus"},"def":{"af":"'n Tekortsiekte as gevolg van te min energie én proteïen; die liggaam is uitgeteer.","en":"A deficiency disease caused by too little energy and protein; the body is wasted."}},{"term":{"af":"Vetoplosbare vitamiene","en":"Fat-soluble vitamins"},"def":{"af":"Vitamiene A, D, E en K, wat in vet oplos en in die liggaam gestoor kan word.","en":"Vitamins A, D, E and K, which dissolve in fat and can be stored in the body."}},{"term":{"af":"Wateroplosbare vitamiene","en":"Water-soluble vitamins"},"def":{"af":"Die B-groep en vitamien C, wat in water oplos, nie gestoor word nie en maklik in kookwater verlore gaan.","en":"The B group and vitamin C, which dissolve in water, are not stored and are easily lost into cooking water."}},{"term":{"af":"Bloedarmoede (anemie)","en":"Anaemia"},"def":{"af":"'n Toestand as gevolg van ystertekort waarin die bloed te min hemoglobien het; die persoon is moeg en bleek.","en":"A condition caused by iron deficiency in which the blood has too little haemoglobin; the person is tired and pale."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselpiramide","en":"Food pyramid"},"def":{"af":"'n Diagram wat wys hoeveel van elke voedselgroep jy moet eet: styselvoedsel onder (die meeste), vette en suiker bo (die minste).","en":"A diagram that shows how much of each food group to eat: starchy foods at the bottom (the most), fats and sugar at the top (the least)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselgebaseerde dieetriglyne","en":"Food-based dietary guidelines"},"def":{"af":"Eenvoudige, positiewe boodskappe (bv. 'Gebruik sout spaarsamig') wat Suid-Afrikaners help om gesond te eet.","en":"Simple, positive messages (e.g. 'Use salt sparingly') that help South Africans eat healthily."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bereken die energiewaarde","en":"Calculate the energy value"},"problem":{"af":"'n Hoenderburger by 'n kitskosplek in Brits bevat 45 g koolhidrate, 28 g proteïen en 22 g vet. Bereken die energiewaarde in kJ. Watter voedingstof verskaf die meeste energie?","en":"A chicken burger at a fast-food outlet in Brits contains 45 g carbohydrate, 28 g protein and 22 g fat. Calculate the energy value in kJ. Which nutrient provides the most energy?"},"steps":[{"af":"Koolhidrate: 45 g × 17 kJ = 765 kJ","en":"Carbohydrate: 45 g × 17 kJ = 765 kJ"},{"af":"Proteïen: 28 g × 17 kJ = 476 kJ","en":"Protein: 28 g × 17 kJ = 476 kJ"},{"af":"Vet: 22 g × 37 kJ = 814 kJ","en":"Fat: 22 g × 37 kJ = 814 kJ"},{"af":"Totaal = 765 + 476 + 814 = 2 055 kJ. Die vet verskaf die meeste energie (814 kJ), al is daar minder gram vet as koolhidrate.","en":"Total = 765 + 476 + 814 = 2 055 kJ. The fat provides the most energy (814 kJ), even though there are fewer grams of fat than carbohydrate."}],"answer":{"af":"2 055 kJ; vet verskaf die meeste energie.","en":"2 055 kJ; fat provides the most energy."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer 'n maaltyd teen die voedselpiramide","en":"Evaluate a meal against the food pyramid"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder eet vir middagete 'n vetkoek met kaas, 'n pakkie slaptjips en 'n 500 ml-koeldrank. Evalueer die maaltyd teen die voedselpiramide en stel drie verbeterings voor.","en":"A learner eats a vetkoek with cheese, a packet of slap chips and a 500 ml cool drink for lunch. Evaluate the meal against the food pyramid and suggest three improvements."},"steps":[{"af":"Styselvoedsel: vetkoek en slaptjips – albei is gebraai, dus baie vet. Suiwel: kaas (kalsium en proteïen).","en":"Starchy foods: vetkoek and slap chips – both are fried, so very high in fat. Dairy: cheese (calcium and protein)."},{"af":"Bo-aan die piramide: baie vet (gebraaide kos) en baie suiker (koeldrank) – dit moet spaarsamig gebruik word.","en":"Top of the pyramid: a lot of fat (fried food) and a lot of sugar (cool drink) – these should be used sparingly."},{"af":"Wat ontbreek: groente en vrugte (vitamien C, vesel) en byna geen water nie.","en":"What is missing: vegetables and fruit (vitamin C, fibre) and almost no water."},{"af":"Verbeterings: (1) 'n volkoringbroodjie in plaas van vetkoek en tjips; (2) voeg slaai of 'n vrug by; (3) drink water of maas in plaas van koeldrank.","en":"Improvements: (1) a whole-wheat roll instead of vetkoek and chips; (2) add salad or a piece of fruit; (3) drink water or maas instead of a cool drink."}],"answer":{"af":"Onbalans: te veel vet en suiker, geen groente of vrugte. Verbeter met volgraan, groente/vrugte en water of maas.","en":"Unbalanced: too much fat and sugar, no vegetables or fruit. Improve with whole grains, vegetables/fruit and water or maas."}},{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die tekortsiekte","en":"Identify the deficiency disease"},"problem":{"af":"In 'n arm gemeenskap eet 'n gesin byna net mieliepap. Die ma kry 'n donker, skilferige uitslag op haar arms en nek waar die son daarop skyn, en sy het gereeld diarree. Identifiseer die waarskynlike tekortsiekte en stel twee voedselsoorte voor wat sal help.","en":"In a poor community a family eats almost only mealie-meal porridge. The mother develops a dark, scaly rash on her arms and neck where the sun shines on them, and she often has diarrhoea. Identify the likely deficiency disease and suggest two foods that will help."},"steps":[{"af":"'n Dieet van hoofsaaklik mielies is arm aan niasien (vitamien B3).","en":"A diet of mainly maize is poor in niacin (vitamin B3)."},{"af":"'n Velontsteking op plekke wat aan die son blootgestel is, plus diarree, is tipiese tekens van pellagra.","en":"Skin inflammation on sun-exposed areas, plus diarrhoea, are typical signs of pellagra."},{"af":"Voedsel ryk aan niasien: vleis, hoender, vis, eiers, melk, grondboontjies en droëbone. Pap met bone of melk is 'n goedkoop oplossing.","en":"Foods rich in niacin: meat, chicken, fish, eggs, milk, peanuts and dry beans. Pap with beans or milk is a cheap solution."}],"answer":{"af":"Pellagra (niasien-/B3-tekort). Voeg bv. droëbone, grondboontjies, eiers of melk by.","en":"Pellagra (niacin/B3 deficiency). Add e.g. dry beans, peanuts, eggs or milk."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan vir 'n spesiale dieet","en":"Plan for a special diet"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gastehuis in Hartbeespoort ontvang 'n veganistiese gas en 'n halaal-gas. Die kok wil vir albei dieselfde hoofgereg bedien. Sy oorweeg (a) beesvleisbredie met rys, (b) lensie-en-groentekerrie met bruinrys, (c) hoender in roomsous. Watter een is geskik vir albei, en waarom?","en":"A guest house in Hartbeespoort is hosting a vegan guest and a halaal guest. The cook wants to serve the same main course to both. She is considering (a) beef stew with rice, (b) lentil and vegetable curry with brown rice, (c) chicken in cream sauce. Which one suits both, and why?"},"steps":[{"af":"'n Veganis eet geen diereprodukte nie – dus val (a) (beesvleis) en (c) (hoender en room) uit.","en":"A vegan eats no animal products – so (a) (beef) and (c) (chicken and cream) are out."},{"af":"'n Halaal-gas eet geen varkvleis of alkohol nie. Die lensiekerrie bevat geen van die twee nie (gebruik olie, nie varkvet nie, en geen wyn in die kerrie nie).","en":"A halaal guest eats no pork or alcohol. The lentil curry contains neither (use oil, not lard, and no wine in the curry)."},{"af":"Lensies (LBW-proteïen) saam met bruinrys (graan) gee al die aminosure, en die groente gee vitamiene en vesel – 'n gebalanseerde gereg.","en":"Lentils (LBV protein) with brown rice (a cereal) give all the amino acids, and the vegetables give vitamins and fibre – a balanced dish."}],"answer":{"af":"(b) Lensie-en-groentekerrie met bruinrys – geen diereprodukte, geen varkvleis of alkohol, en gebalanseerd.","en":"(b) Lentil and vegetable curry with brown rice – no animal products, no pork or alcohol, and balanced."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hooffunksie van koolhidrate?","en":"What is the main function of carbohydrates?"},"options":[{"af":"Groei en herstel van selle","en":"Growth and repair of cells"},{"af":"Om energie te verskaf","en":"To provide energy"},{"af":"Bloedstolling","en":"Blood clotting"},{"af":"Vorming van hemoglobien","en":"Forming haemoglobin"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Koolhidrate is die liggaam se hoofbron van energie. Groei en herstel is die funksie van proteïene.","en":"Carbohydrates are the body's main source of energy. Growth and repair is the function of proteins."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Tekort aan vitamien C veroorsaak ___.","en":"A lack of vitamin C causes ___."},"answers":{"af":["skeurbuik"],"en":["scurvy"]},"explain":{"af":"Skeurbuik (bloeiende tandvleis, wonde wat swak genees) is die tekortsiekte van vitamien C. Ragitis = vitamien D, pellagra = niasien, nagblindheid = vitamien A.","en":"Scurvy (bleeding gums, wounds that heal poorly) is the vitamin C deficiency disease. Rickets = vitamin D, pellagra = niacin, night blindness = vitamin A."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ragitis","pellagra","nagblindheid"],"en":["rickets","pellagra","night blindness"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vitamiene A, D, E en K is vetoplosbaar.","en":"Vitamins A, D, E and K are fat-soluble."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar – hulle los in vet op en kan in die liggaam gestoor word. Die B-groep en vitamien C is wateroplosbaar.","en":"True – they dissolve in fat and can be stored in the body. The B group and vitamin C are water-soluble."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter toestand word deur 'n tekort aan jodium veroorsaak?","en":"Which condition is caused by a lack of iodine?"},"options":[{"af":"Bloedarmoede","en":"Anaemia"},{"af":"Skeurbuik","en":"Scurvy"},{"af":"Kwashiorkor","en":"Kwashiorkor"},{"af":"Kropgeswel (goiter)","en":"Goitre"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Jodium is nodig vir die skildklier; 'n tekort laat die klier in die nek opswel (kropgeswel). Daarom word sout in SA gejodeer.","en":"Iodine is needed for the thyroid gland; a lack makes the gland in the neck swell (goitre). That is why salt in SA is iodised."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke voedingstof by sy funksie.","en":"Match each nutrient to its function."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Proteïen","en":"Protein"},"r":{"af":"Groei en herstel van selle","en":"Growth and repair of cells"}},{"l":{"af":"Kalsium","en":"Calcium"},"r":{"af":"Sterk bene en tande","en":"Strong bones and teeth"}},{"l":{"af":"Yster","en":"Iron"},"r":{"af":"Vorm hemoglobien wat suurstof dra","en":"Forms haemoglobin that carries oxygen"}},{"l":{"af":"Vesel","en":"Fibre"},"r":{"af":"Voorkom hardlywigheid","en":"Prevents constipation"}},{"l":{"af":"Vitamien D","en":"Vitamin D"},"r":{"af":"Help die liggaam om kalsium op te neem","en":"Helps the body absorb calcium"}}],"explain":{"af":"Proteïen bou en herstel; kalsium vir bene en tande; yster vir hemoglobien; vesel help vertering; vitamien D help met kalsiumopname.","en":"Protein builds and repairs; calcium for bones and teeth; iron for haemoglobin; fibre aids digestion; vitamin D helps calcium absorption."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voedsel bevat proteïen van hoë biologiese waarde (HBW)?","en":"Which food contains protein of high biological value (HBV)?"},"options":[{"af":"Lensies","en":"Lentils"},{"af":"Droëbone","en":"Dry beans"},{"af":"Eiers","en":"Eggs"},{"af":"Grondboontjies","en":"Peanuts"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Eiers (en vleis, vis, melk en soja) bevat al die noodsaaklike aminosure. Lensies, bone en grondboontjies is plantproteïen van lae biologiese waarde.","en":"Eggs (and meat, fish, milk and soya) contain all the essential amino acids. Lentils, beans and peanuts are plant proteins of low biological value."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"1 g vet verskaf ongeveer ___ kJ energie.","en":"1 g of fat provides about ___ kJ of energy."},"answers":{"af":["37","37 kJ"],"en":["37","37 kJ"]},"explain":{"af":"Vet gee 37 kJ per gram – meer as twee keer soveel as koolhidrate en proteïen (17 kJ per gram).","en":"Fat gives 37 kJ per gram – more than twice as much as carbohydrate and protein (17 kJ per gram)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["17","27","9"],"en":["17","27","9"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Van watter voedselgroep moet jy volgens die voedselpiramide die MEESTE eet?","en":"According to the food pyramid, which food group should you eat the MOST of?"},"options":[{"af":"Styselvoedsel","en":"Starchy foods"},{"af":"Vette en olies","en":"Fats and oils"},{"af":"Proteïenvoedsel","en":"Protein foods"},{"af":"Suiwel","en":"Dairy"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Styselvoedsel vorm die basis (onderste laag) van die piramide. Vette, olies en suiker is bo-aan en moet spaarsamig gebruik word.","en":"Starchy foods form the base (bottom layer) of the pyramid. Fats, oils and sugar are at the top and should be used sparingly."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Kwashiorkor word deur 'n tekort aan energie én proteïen veroorsaak, en die kind lyk soos 'vel en been'.","en":"Kwashiorkor is caused by a lack of energy and protein, and the child looks like 'skin and bones'."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – dit beskryf marasmus. By kwashiorkor is daar 'n proteïentekort en die maag en bene swel op weens vog in die weefsel.","en":"False – that describes marasmus. In kwashiorkor there is a protein deficiency and the belly and legs swell because of fluid in the tissue."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Snoepie bevat 20 g koolhidrate, 5 g proteïen en 10 g vet. Die energiewaarde is ___ kJ.","en":"A snack contains 20 g carbohydrate, 5 g protein and 10 g fat. The energy value is ___ kJ."},"answers":{"af":["795","795 kJ"],"en":["795","795 kJ"]},"explain":{"af":"(20 × 17) + (5 × 17) + (10 × 37) = 340 + 85 + 370 = 795 kJ. (595 kry jy as jy 17 vir die vet ook gebruik.)","en":"(20 × 17) + (5 × 17) + (10 × 37) = 340 + 85 + 370 = 795 kJ. (You get 595 if you use 17 for the fat as well.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["595","995","710"],"en":["595","995","710"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter bord volg die reël vir 'n gebalanseerde maaltyd (½ – ¼ – ¼)?","en":"Which plate follows the rule for a balanced meal (½ – ¼ – ¼)?"},"options":[{"af":"½ pap, ¼ wors, ¼ sous","en":"½ pap, ¼ boerewors, ¼ gravy"},{"af":"½ steak, ¼ aartappels, ¼ groente","en":"½ steak, ¼ potatoes, ¼ vegetables"},{"af":"½ pasta, ¼ maalvleis, ¼ kaas","en":"½ pasta, ¼ mince, ¼ cheese"},{"af":"½ groente en slaai, ¼ rys, ¼ hoender","en":"½ vegetables and salad, ¼ rice, ¼ chicken"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die helfte van die bord moet groente en slaai wees, 'n kwart stysel en 'n kwart proteïen.","en":"Half the plate should be vegetables and salad, a quarter starch and a quarter protein."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir 'n halaal-gas moet jy varkvleis en ___ vermy.","en":"For a halaal guest you must avoid pork and ___."},"answers":{"af":["alkohol","drank"],"en":["alcohol"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Halaal-dieet sluit varkvleis en alkohol uit. Hoender, melk en rys is toelaatbaar (die vleis moet halaal geslag wees).","en":"A halaal diet excludes pork and alcohol. Chicken, milk and rice are allowed (the meat must be halaal slaughtered)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoender","melk","rys"],"en":["chicken","milk","rice"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n gebied waar mense hoofsaaklik mieliepap eet, kry baie mense 'n donker, skilferige uitslag op vel wat aan die son blootgestel is, diarree en verwardheid. Watter tekort is die mees waarskynlike?","en":"In an area where people eat mainly mealie-meal porridge, many people develop a dark, scaly rash on sun-exposed skin, diarrhoea and confusion. Which deficiency is most likely?"},"options":[{"af":"Vitamien C – skeurbuik","en":"Vitamin C – scurvy"},{"af":"Niasien (vitamien B3) – pellagra","en":"Niacin (vitamin B3) – pellagra"},{"af":"Jodium – kropgeswel","en":"Iodine – goitre"},{"af":"Vitamien A – nagblindheid","en":"Vitamin A – night blindness"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Pellagra (velontsteking, diarree en verwardheid) word deur 'n niasientekort veroorsaak en word gekoppel aan diëte wat hoofsaaklik uit mielies bestaan.","en":"Pellagra (skin inflammation, diarrhoea and confusion) is caused by a niacin deficiency and is linked to diets that consist mainly of maize."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Veganis eet geen diereprodukte nie. Hy moet veral oppas vir 'n tekort aan vitamien ___, wat byna net in diereprodukte voorkom.","en":"A vegan eats no animal products. He must especially watch out for a lack of vitamin ___, which is found almost only in animal products."},"answers":{"af":["B12","B 12","B-12"],"en":["B12","B 12","B-12"]},"explain":{"af":"Vitamien B12 kom byna net in vleis, vis, eiers en suiwel voor, dus het veganiste verrykte voedsel of 'n aanvulling nodig. Vitamiene C, K en E kom in plantvoedsel voor.","en":"Vitamin B12 is found almost only in meat, fish, eggs and dairy, so vegans need fortified foods or a supplement. Vitamins C, K and E are found in plant foods."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["C","K","E"],"en":["C","K","E"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Koshuis se spyskaart vir een dag is: ontbyt – witbrood met konfyt; middagete – slaptjips en koeldrank; aandete – macaroni en kaas. Watter voedingstowwe is die grootste tekort?","en":"A hostel's menu for one day is: breakfast – white bread with jam; lunch – slap chips and a cool drink; supper – macaroni and cheese. Which nutrients are most lacking?"},"options":[{"af":"Koolhidrate","en":"Carbohydrates"},{"af":"Vet","en":"Fat"},{"af":"Vitamien C en vesel","en":"Vitamin C and fibre"},{"af":"Suiker","en":"Sugar"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die spyskaart is vol stysel, vet en suiker, maar daar is geen groente of vrugte nie – dus kort dit veral vitamien C en vesel. Witbrood en tjips gee ook min vesel.","en":"The menu is full of starch, fat and sugar, but there are no vegetables or fruit – so it lacks especially vitamin C and fibre. White bread and chips also give little fibre."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho (15) speel rugby en voel altyd moeg en lyk bleek. Hy eet byna net pap en witbrood, drink baie koeldrank en eet byna nooit vleis, groente of vrugte nie. Watter advies is die beste?","en":"Sipho (15) plays rugby and always feels tired and looks pale. He eats almost only pap and white bread, drinks a lot of cool drink and almost never eats meat, vegetables or fruit. Which advice is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"Eet elke dag donkergroen blaargroente, bone of maer rooivleis, en 'n sitrusvrug – dit gee yster, en vitamien C help die liggaam om yster op te neem.","en":"Eat dark-green leafy vegetables, beans or lean red meat, and a citrus fruit every day – they give iron, and vitamin C helps the body absorb iron."},{"af":"Drink meer koeldrank vir vinnige energie voor oefening.","en":"Drink more cool drink for quick energy before practice."},{"af":"Eet net meer vleis en sny alle styselvoedsel uit.","en":"Just eat more meat and cut out all starchy foods."},{"af":"Neem vitamien E-pille, want dit genees moegheid.","en":"Take vitamin E pills, because they cure tiredness."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Moegheid en bleekheid dui op bloedarmoede (ystertekort). Blaargroente, bone en rooivleis gee yster, en vitamien C help die liggaam om plantyster op te neem. Koeldrank gee net suiker, en 'n sportman het stysel vir energie nodig.","en":"Tiredness and paleness point to anaemia (iron deficiency). Leafy vegetables, beans and red meat give iron, and vitamin C helps the body absorb plant iron. Cool drink gives only sugar, and a sportsman needs starch for energy."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t3-spyskaartbeplanning","title":{"af":"Spyskaartbeplanning, spyskaarttipes en kosteberekening","en":"Menu planning, menu types and costing"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n gebalanseerde, aantreklike spyskaart kan beplan en skryf, spyskaarttipes kan onderskei en die koste per porsie en verkoopprys van 'n gereg kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to plan and write a balanced, appealing menu, distinguish between menu types and calculate the cost per portion and selling price of a dish."},"summary":{"af":"## Beginsels van spyskaartbeplanning\n\nOorweeg die volgende voordat jy 'n spyskaart opstel:\n\n1. **Teikenmark en kliënte se voorkeure** – ouderdom, kultuur, godsdiens en spesiale diëte (bv. halaal, vegetaries).\n2. **Tipe onderneming en geleentheid** – 'n kitskosplek, 'n deftige restaurant, 'n troue of 'n skoolfunksie.\n3. **Voedingsbalans** – volg die voedselpiramide en die dieetriglyne.\n4. **Sintuiglike aantrekkingskrag** – sorg vir **variasie** in **kleur, tekstuur, geur, vorm, temperatuur** (warm en koud) en **kookmetode**. Moenie herhaal nie: nie 'n roomsop, 'n roomsous én 'n roomnagereg nie.\n5. **Seisoen en beskikbaarheid** – seisoensprodukte is goedkoper, varser en smaakliker (bv. lemoene en nartjies in die winter).\n6. **Koste en begroting** van die onderneming en die kliënt.\n7. **Toerusting en personeel se vaardighede** – kan die kombuis dit maak?\n8. **Tyd** – voorbereidingstyd en hoe vinnig die kos bedien moet word.\n\n## Spyskaarttipes\n\n| | Table d'hôte | À la carte |\n|---|---|---|\n| Prys | **een vaste prys** vir die hele maaltyd | **elke gereg apart** geprys |\n| Keuse | beperk | wyd |\n| Gange | 'n vaste aantal gange | die gas kies self |\n| Tyd | bedien op 'n **vaste tyd** | gaargemaak **na bestelling** |\n| Wagtyd | kort – kos is vooraf voorberei | langer |\n\n- **Siklusspyskaart:** 'n reeks spyskaarte wat ná 'n vaste tydperk (bv. elke drie weke) **herhaal**. Gebruik in hospitale, skole, koshuise en die weermag.\n- **Funksie- of buffetspyskaart:** vooraf ooreengekom vir 'n spesifieke geleentheid en groep, met 'n prys per persoon.\n- **Carte du jour:** die \"spyskaart van die dag\" – geregte wat net vandag beskikbaar is (dagspesiale).\n\n## Gangvolgorde\n\n**Klassiek:** voorgereg (*hors d'oeuvre*) → sop → visgereg → hoofgereg met groente en stysel → nagereg → koffie.\n\n**Vereenvoudigde driegangmaaltyd:** voorgereg (of sop) → hoofgereg → nagereg.\n\n## Reëls vir die skryf van 'n spyskaart\n\n- Die naam van die onderneming of geleentheid en die **datum** bo-aan.\n- Gange in die **korrekte volgorde** en **gesentreer**.\n- **Hoofletters** vir die name van geregte.\n- Bykosse (groente, stysel, souse) word **onder die hoofgereg** geskryf.\n- **Een taal** deurgaans; Franse kookterme korrek gespel (bv. *à la carte*, *crème brûlée*).\n- **Geen herhaling** van bestanddele, kleure of kookmetodes nie.\n\n## Ontbyt, brunch en ligte maaltye\n\n- **Kontinentale ontbyt:** lig, met **geen gaar (warm) geregte** nie: broodrolletjies of croissants, botter, konfyt of heuning, vrugtesap, vrugte of jogurt, tee of koffie.\n- **Engelse (volledige) ontbyt:** ontbytgraan of pap, gaar eiers, spek, worsies, geroosterde tamatie, sampioene, roosterbrood, tee of koffie.\n- **Brunch:** 'n laatoggendmaaltyd wat ontbyt en middagete kombineer (bv. eiers Benedict, quiche, vrugteslaai).\n- **Ligte maaltye:** toebroodjies, slaaie, quiche, sop.\n\n## Kosteberekening\n\n**Stap 1 – Koste van elke bestanddeel wat gebruik is:**\n\n`koste = hoeveelheid gebruik ÷ aankoophoeveelheid × aankoopprys`\n\nDie eenhede moet dieselfde wees (g met g, ml met ml). Bv. 250 g botter uit 'n 500 g-pak van R60: 250 ÷ 500 × R60 = **R30,00**.\n\n**Stap 2 – Totale resepkoste** = die som van al die bestanddele.\n\n**Stap 3 – Koste per porsie** = totale koste ÷ aantal porsies.\n\n**Stap 4 – Verkoopprys** = koste per porsie ÷ voedselkoste-% × 100.\n\n**Stap 5 – Voeg 15% BTW by:** verkoopprys × 1,15.\n\n| Voorbeeld | Berekening | Antwoord |\n|---|---|---|\n| Koste per porsie | R84 ÷ 6 | R14,00 |\n| Verkoopprys (35% voedselkoste) | R14 ÷ 35 × 100 | R40,00 |\n| Met BTW | R40 × 1,15 | R46,00 |\n\nDie **voedselkoste-persentasie** is die deel van die verkoopprys wat aan voedsel bestee word. Die res (hier 65%) moet lone, elektrisiteit, huur en wins dek.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** (1) Eenhede word gemeng (kg en g). (2) Leerders tel net 35% by die koste (R14 × 1,35 = R18,90) – dit is VERKEERD; deel deur die voedselkoste-%. (3) Geld word nie tot twee desimale plekke (sente) afgerond nie. (4) BTW word vergeet.","en":"## Principles of menu planning\n\nConsider the following before you draw up a menu:\n\n1. **Target market and customer preferences** – age, culture, religion and special diets (e.g. halaal, vegetarian).\n2. **Type of establishment and occasion** – a fast-food outlet, a fine-dining restaurant, a wedding or a school function.\n3. **Nutritional balance** – follow the food pyramid and the dietary guidelines.\n4. **Sensory appeal** – provide **variety** in **colour, texture, flavour, shape, temperature** (hot and cold) and **cooking method**. Don't repeat: not a cream soup, a cream sauce and a cream dessert.\n5. **Season and availability** – seasonal produce is cheaper, fresher and tastier (e.g. oranges and naartjies in winter).\n6. **Cost and budget** of the establishment and the customer.\n7. **Equipment and staff skills** – can the kitchen make it?\n8. **Time** – preparation time and how quickly the food must be served.\n\n## Menu types\n\n| | Table d'hôte | À la carte |\n|---|---|---|\n| Price | **one fixed price** for the whole meal | **each dish priced separately** |\n| Choice | limited | wide |\n| Courses | a set number of courses | the guest chooses |\n| Time | served at a **set time** | cooked **to order** |\n| Waiting time | short – food is prepared in advance | longer |\n\n- **Cyclical menu:** a series of menus that **repeats** after a set period (e.g. every three weeks). Used in hospitals, schools, hostels and the military.\n- **Function or buffet menu:** agreed in advance for a specific occasion and group, with a price per person.\n- **Carte du jour:** the \"menu of the day\" – dishes available only today (daily specials).\n\n## Course sequence\n\n**Classical:** starter (*hors d'oeuvre*) → soup → fish course → main course with vegetables and starch → dessert → coffee.\n\n**Simplified three-course meal:** starter (or soup) → main course → dessert.\n\n## Rules for writing a menu\n\n- The name of the establishment or occasion and the **date** at the top.\n- Courses in the **correct order** and **centred**.\n- **Capital letters** for the names of dishes.\n- Accompaniments (vegetables, starch, sauces) are written **under the main dish**.\n- **One language** throughout; French culinary terms spelled correctly (e.g. *à la carte*, *crème brûlée*).\n- **No repetition** of ingredients, colours or cooking methods.\n\n## Breakfast, brunch and light meals\n\n- **Continental breakfast:** light, with **no cooked (hot) dishes**: bread rolls or croissants, butter, jam or honey, fruit juice, fruit or yoghurt, tea or coffee.\n- **English (full) breakfast:** cereal or porridge, cooked eggs, bacon, sausages, grilled tomato, mushrooms, toast, tea or coffee.\n- **Brunch:** a late-morning meal that combines breakfast and lunch (e.g. eggs Benedict, quiche, fruit salad).\n- **Light meals:** sandwiches, salads, quiche, soup.\n\n## Costing\n\n**Step 1 – Cost of each ingredient used:**\n\n`cost = quantity used ÷ purchase quantity × purchase price`\n\nThe units must be the same (g with g, ml with ml). E.g. 250 g butter from a 500 g pack costing R60: 250 ÷ 500 × R60 = **R30.00**.\n\n**Step 2 – Total recipe cost** = the sum of all the ingredients.\n\n**Step 3 – Cost per portion** = total cost ÷ number of portions.\n\n**Step 4 – Selling price** = cost per portion ÷ food-cost % × 100.\n\n**Step 5 – Add 15% VAT:** selling price × 1.15.\n\n| Example | Calculation | Answer |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cost per portion | R84 ÷ 6 | R14.00 |\n| Selling price (35% food cost) | R14 ÷ 35 × 100 | R40.00 |\n| With VAT | R40 × 1.15 | R46.00 |\n\nThe **food-cost percentage** is the part of the selling price that is spent on food. The rest (here 65%) must cover wages, electricity, rent and profit.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** (1) Units are mixed (kg and g). (2) Learners just add 35% to the cost (R14 × 1.35 = R18.90) – this is WRONG; divide by the food-cost %. (3) Money is not rounded to two decimal places (cents). (4) VAT is forgotten."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Table d'hôte","en":"Table d'hôte"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste spyskaart met 'n beperkte keuse en 'n vaste aantal gange teen een vaste prys, bedien op 'n vaste tyd.","en":"A set menu with limited choice and a set number of courses at one fixed price, served at a set time."}},{"term":{"af":"À la carte","en":"À la carte"},"def":{"af":"'n Spyskaart waarop elke gereg apart geprys word en na bestelling gaargemaak word.","en":"A menu on which each dish is priced separately and cooked to order."}},{"term":{"af":"Siklusspyskaart","en":"Cyclical menu"},"def":{"af":"'n Reeks spyskaarte wat ná 'n vaste tydperk herhaal, bv. in hospitale en koshuise.","en":"A series of menus that repeats after a set period, e.g. in hospitals and hostels."}},{"term":{"af":"Carte du jour","en":"Carte du jour"},"def":{"af":"Die spyskaart van die dag: geregte wat net op daardie dag beskikbaar is.","en":"The menu of the day: dishes that are available only on that day."}},{"term":{"af":"Sintuiglike aantrekkingskrag","en":"Sensory appeal"},"def":{"af":"Hoe aantreklik kos vir die sintuie is – variasie in kleur, tekstuur, geur, vorm en temperatuur.","en":"How appealing food is to the senses – variety in colour, texture, flavour, shape and temperature."}},{"term":{"af":"Kontinentale ontbyt","en":"Continental breakfast"},"def":{"af":"'n Ligte ontbyt sonder gaar geregte: broodrolletjies of croissants, konfyt, vrugte, sap en tee of koffie.","en":"A light breakfast without cooked dishes: rolls or croissants, preserves, fruit, juice and tea or coffee."}},{"term":{"af":"Brunch","en":"Brunch"},"def":{"af":"'n Laatoggendmaaltyd wat ontbyt en middagete kombineer.","en":"A late-morning meal that combines breakfast and lunch."}},{"term":{"af":"Koste per porsie","en":"Cost per portion"},"def":{"af":"Die totale resepkoste gedeel deur die aantal porsies wat die resep lewer.","en":"The total recipe cost divided by the number of portions the recipe yields."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselkoste-persentasie","en":"Food-cost percentage"},"def":{"af":"Die persentasie van die verkoopprys wat aan die bestanddele bestee word.","en":"The percentage of the selling price that is spent on the ingredients."}},{"term":{"af":"BTW","en":"VAT"},"def":{"af":"Belasting op toegevoegde waarde – 15% wat in Suid-Afrika by die verkoopprys gevoeg word.","en":"Value-added tax – 15% that is added to the selling price in South Africa."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Volledige kosteberekening","en":"Full costing"},"problem":{"af":"'n Restaurant in Brits maak hoender à la king vir 8 porsies. Bestanddele (gebruik; aankoop): hoenderborsies 1,2 kg uit 'n 2 kg-pak teen R180,00; sampioene 250 g uit 'n 250 g-pak teen R30,00; room 250 ml uit 'n 500 ml-houer teen R44,00; uie 500 g uit 'n 2 kg-sak teen R36,00; botter 50 g uit 'n 500 g-pak teen R70,00; rys 500 g uit 'n 2 kg-pak teen R64,00. Die voedselkoste is 40%. Bereken die koste per porsie en die verkoopprys met BTW.","en":"A restaurant in Brits makes chicken à la king for 8 portions. Ingredients (used; purchased): chicken breasts 1.2 kg from a 2 kg pack at R180.00; mushrooms 250 g from a 250 g pack at R30.00; cream 250 ml from a 500 ml container at R44.00; onions 500 g from a 2 kg bag at R36.00; butter 50 g from a 500 g pack at R70.00; rice 500 g from a 2 kg pack at R64.00. The food cost is 40%. Calculate the cost per portion and the selling price including VAT."},"steps":[{"af":"Koste per bestanddeel (gebruik ÷ aankoop × prys): hoender 1,2 ÷ 2 × R180 = R108,00; sampioene 250 ÷ 250 × R30 = R30,00; room 250 ÷ 500 × R44 = R22,00.","en":"Cost per ingredient (used ÷ purchased × price): chicken 1.2 ÷ 2 × R180 = R108.00; mushrooms 250 ÷ 250 × R30 = R30.00; cream 250 ÷ 500 × R44 = R22.00."},{"af":"Uie 500 ÷ 2 000 × R36 = R9,00 (2 kg = 2 000 g); botter 50 ÷ 500 × R70 = R7,00; rys 500 ÷ 2 000 × R64 = R16,00.","en":"Onions 500 ÷ 2 000 × R36 = R9.00 (2 kg = 2 000 g); butter 50 ÷ 500 × R70 = R7.00; rice 500 ÷ 2 000 × R64 = R16.00."},{"af":"Totale koste = R108 + R30 + R22 + R9 + R7 + R16 = R192,00. Koste per porsie = R192,00 ÷ 8 = R24,00.","en":"Total cost = R108 + R30 + R22 + R9 + R7 + R16 = R192.00. Cost per portion = R192.00 ÷ 8 = R24.00."},{"af":"Verkoopprys = R24,00 ÷ 40 × 100 = R60,00. Met BTW: R60,00 × 1,15 = R69,00.","en":"Selling price = R24.00 ÷ 40 × 100 = R60.00. With VAT: R60.00 × 1.15 = R69.00."}],"answer":{"af":"Koste per porsie R24,00; verkoopprys R60,00 sonder BTW en R69,00 met BTW.","en":"Cost per portion R24.00; selling price R60.00 excluding VAT and R69.00 including VAT."}},{"title":{"af":"Vind die foute in 'n spyskaart","en":"Find the errors in a menu"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder skryf hierdie Sondagmiddagete-spyskaart vir 'n gastehuis in Hartbeespoort (in hierdie volgorde, sonder datum): Sjokolademousse / Roomsop van Sampioene / Gebraaide hoender met Roomsous, Kapokaartappels, Blomkool in Witsous en Rys / Vanieljeroomys. Identifiseer vier beplanningsfoute en stel 'n verbeterde spyskaart voor.","en":"A learner writes this Sunday-lunch menu for a guest house in Hartbeespoort (in this order, without a date): Chocolate Mousse / Cream of Mushroom Soup / Roast Chicken with Cream Sauce, Mashed Potatoes, Cauliflower in White Sauce and Rice / Vanilla Ice Cream. Identify four planning errors and suggest an improved menu."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1 – Volgorde en uitleg: die nagereg (mousse) staan eerste, daar is twee nageregte en geen datum of naam van die gastehuis bo-aan nie.","en":"Error 1 – Order and layout: the dessert (mousse) comes first, there are two desserts and no date or name of the guest house at the top."},{"af":"Fout 2 – Herhaling van bestanddele: room kom in die sop, die sous, die mousse en die roomys voor.","en":"Error 2 – Repetition of ingredients: cream appears in the soup, the sauce, the mousse and the ice cream."},{"af":"Fout 3 – Geen kleurvariasie nie: sop, sous, kapokaartappels, blomkool, witsous en rys is almal wit of roomkleurig. Fout 4 – Twee styselbykosse (kapokaartappels én rys).","en":"Error 3 – No colour variety: soup, sauce, mashed potatoes, cauliflower, white sauce and rice are all white or cream-coloured. Error 4 – Two starch accompaniments (mashed potatoes and rice)."},{"af":"Verbeter: Hartbeespoort Gastehuis, Sondag 15 November 2026 / Tamatie-en-Basiliekumsop / Gebraaide Hoender met Pan-sous, Geroosterde Patats, Groenbone en Wortels / Vars Vrugteslaai met Jogurt.","en":"Improved: Hartbeespoort Guest House, Sunday 15 November 2026 / Tomato and Basil Soup / Roast Chicken with Pan Gravy, Roast Sweet Potatoes, Green Beans and Carrots / Fresh Fruit Salad with Yoghurt."}],"answer":{"af":"Foute: verkeerde volgorde en geen datum, herhaling van room, geen kleurvariasie, twee styselbykosse.","en":"Errors: wrong order and no date, repetition of cream, no colour variety, two starch accompaniments."}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die voedselkoste-persentasie","en":"Calculate the food-cost percentage"},"problem":{"af":"'n Koffiewinkel in die Magaliesberg verkoop 'n hoender-en-avokado-toebroodjie teen R60,00 (sonder BTW). Die bestanddele kos R18,00 per porsie. Bereken (a) die voedselkoste-persentasie en (b) die bruto wins per toebroodjie. (c) Die eienaar wil 'n voedselkoste van 30% hê. Is die prys reg?","en":"A coffee shop in the Magaliesberg sells a chicken and avocado sandwich at R60.00 (excluding VAT). The ingredients cost R18.00 per portion. Calculate (a) the food-cost percentage and (b) the gross profit per sandwich. (c) The owner wants a food cost of 30%. Is the price right?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Voedselkoste-% = koste per porsie ÷ verkoopprys × 100 = R18 ÷ R60 × 100 = 30%","en":"(a) Food-cost % = cost per portion ÷ selling price × 100 = R18 ÷ R60 × 100 = 30%"},{"af":"(b) Bruto wins = verkoopprys − voedselkoste = R60,00 − R18,00 = R42,00 (dit is 70% van die verkoopprys).","en":"(b) Gross profit = selling price − food cost = R60.00 − R18.00 = R42.00 (that is 70% of the selling price)."},{"af":"(c) Kontroleer: R18 ÷ 30 × 100 = R60,00. Ja, die prys gee presies 30% voedselkoste.","en":"(c) Check: R18 ÷ 30 × 100 = R60.00. Yes, the price gives exactly 30% food cost."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 30%; (b) R42,00; (c) Ja, R60,00 is korrek.","en":"(a) 30%; (b) R42.00; (c) Yes, R60.00 is correct."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n kontinentale ontbytspyskaart","en":"Write a continental breakfast menu"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 'n kontinentale ontbytspyskaart vir 'n gastehuis in Brits wat in die wintermaand Julie oop is. Pas die reëls vir spyskaartskryf toe en gebruik seisoensprodukte.","en":"Write a continental breakfast menu for a guest house in Brits that is open in the winter month of July. Apply the menu-writing rules and use seasonal produce."},"steps":[{"af":"Bo-aan: die naam en datum, bv. Brits Gastehuis – Kontinentale Ontbyt – Saterdag 18 Julie 2026.","en":"At the top: the name and date, e.g. Brits Guest House – Continental Breakfast – Saturday 18 July 2026."},{"af":"Drankies en vrugte (gesentreer, hoofletters): Vars Lemoensap / Nartjie-en-Pomelo-skyfies met Jogurt – sitrus is in die winter in seisoen in die Brits-omgewing.","en":"Drinks and fruit (centred, capital letters): Fresh Orange Juice / Naartjie and Grapefruit Segments with Yoghurt – citrus is in season in winter in the Brits area."},{"af":"Gebak: Botter-croissants en Volkoring-broodrolletjies / Botter, Appelkooskonfyt en Heuning.","en":"Baked goods: Butter Croissants and Whole-wheat Rolls / Butter, Apricot Jam and Honey."},{"af":"Warm drankies: Tee, Rooibos of Koffie. Kontroleer: geen gaar geregte (eiers, spek) nie – anders is dit nie meer kontinentaal nie.","en":"Hot drinks: Tea, Rooibos or Coffee. Check: no cooked dishes (eggs, bacon) – otherwise it is no longer continental."}],"answer":{"af":"Naam en datum bo-aan; sap en sitrusvrugte met jogurt; croissants en broodrolletjies met botter, konfyt en heuning; tee, rooibos of koffie – geen gaar geregte nie.","en":"Name and date at the top; juice and citrus fruit with yoghurt; croissants and rolls with butter, jam and honey; tea, rooibos or coffee – no cooked dishes."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter beskrywing pas by 'n table d'hôte-spyskaart?","en":"Which description fits a table d'hôte menu?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Vaste aantal gange teen een vaste prys, met beperkte keuse","en":"A set number of courses at one fixed price, with limited choice"},{"af":"Elke gereg word apart geprys en na bestelling gaargemaak","en":"Each dish is priced separately and cooked to order"},{"af":"Geregte wat net vandag beskikbaar is","en":"Dishes that are available only today"},{"af":"'n Reeks spyskaarte wat elke drie weke herhaal","en":"A series of menus that repeats every three weeks"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Table d'hôte is 'n vaste spyskaart: een prys, 'n vaste aantal gange en beperkte keuse. Die ander beskryf à la carte, carte du jour en 'n siklusspyskaart.","en":"Table d'hôte is a set menu: one price, a set number of courses and limited choice. The others describe à la carte, carte du jour and a cyclical menu."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Kontinentale ontbyt sluit gaar geregte soos gebakte eiers en spek in.","en":"A continental breakfast includes cooked dishes such as fried eggs and bacon."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – 'n kontinentale ontbyt is lig en het geen gaar geregte nie. Eiers en spek hoort by 'n Engelse (volledige) ontbyt.","en":"False – a continental breakfast is light and has no cooked dishes. Eggs and bacon belong to an English (full) breakfast."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Spyskaart waarop elke gereg apart geprys en na bestelling gaargemaak word, is 'n ___-spyskaart.","en":"A menu on which each dish is priced separately and cooked to order is an ___ menu."},"answers":{"af":["à la carte","a la carte","à-la-carte","a-la-carte"],"en":["à la carte","a la carte","à-la-carte","a-la-carte"]},"explain":{"af":"À la carte = 'volgens die kaart': die gas kies elke gereg apart, en dit word na bestelling gaargemaak, dus is die wagtyd langer.","en":"À la carte = 'from the card': the guest chooses each dish separately, and it is cooked to order, so the waiting time is longer."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["table d'hôte","siklus","carte du jour"],"en":["table d'hôte","cyclical","carte du jour"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die korrekte klassieke gangvolgorde?","en":"What is the correct classical course sequence?"},"options":[{"af":"Sop → voorgereg → hoofgereg → vis → nagereg → koffie","en":"Soup → starter → main course → fish → dessert → coffee"},{"af":"Voorgereg → vis → sop → hoofgereg → koffie → nagereg","en":"Starter → fish → soup → main course → coffee → dessert"},{"af":"Voorgereg → sop → vis → hoofgereg → nagereg → koffie","en":"Starter → soup → fish → main course → dessert → coffee"},{"af":"Sop → vis → voorgereg → nagereg → hoofgereg → koffie","en":"Soup → fish → starter → dessert → main course → coffee"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die klassieke volgorde begin met die voorgereg (hors d'oeuvre), dan sop, vis, die hoofgereg en nagereg, en eindig met koffie.","en":"The classical order starts with the starter (hors d'oeuvre), then soup, fish, the main course and dessert, and ends with coffee."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter onderneming sal die meeste baat by 'n siklusspyskaart?","en":"Which establishment will benefit most from a cyclical menu?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Deftige à la carte-restaurant","en":"A fine-dining à la carte restaurant"},{"af":"'n Hospitaal","en":"A hospital"},{"af":"'n Eenmalige troue","en":"A once-off wedding"},{"af":"'n Koffiekar by 'n rugbywedstryd","en":"A coffee cart at a rugby match"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Hospitaal bedien elke dag dieselfde mense; 'n siklusspyskaart gee variasie, maak aankope en beplanning makliker en herhaal na 'n vaste tydperk.","en":"A hospital serves the same people every day; a cyclical menu gives variety, makes purchasing and planning easier and repeats after a set period."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke spyskaarttipe by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each menu type to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Table d'hôte","en":"Table d'hôte"},"r":{"af":"Een vaste prys vir 'n vaste aantal gange","en":"One fixed price for a set number of courses"}},{"l":{"af":"À la carte","en":"À la carte"},"r":{"af":"Elke gereg apart geprys","en":"Each dish priced separately"}},{"l":{"af":"Siklusspyskaart","en":"Cyclical menu"},"r":{"af":"Herhaal ná 'n vaste tydperk","en":"Repeats after a set period"}},{"l":{"af":"Carte du jour","en":"Carte du jour"},"r":{"af":"Spyskaart van die dag","en":"Menu of the day"}},{"l":{"af":"Funksiespyskaart","en":"Function menu"},"r":{"af":"Vooraf gereël vir 'n spesifieke geleentheid","en":"Arranged in advance for a specific occasion"}}],"explain":{"af":"Table d'hôte = vaste prys; à la carte = apart geprys; siklus = herhaal; carte du jour = vandag se spesiale; funksie = vir 'n spesifieke geleentheid.","en":"Table d'hôte = fixed price; à la carte = priced separately; cyclical = repeats; carte du jour = today's specials; function = for a specific occasion."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n 1 kg-pak meel kos R24,00. 'n Resep gebruik 250 g meel. Die koste van die meel is R ___.","en":"A 1 kg pack of flour costs R24.00. A recipe uses 250 g flour. The cost of the flour is R ___."},"answers":{"af":["R6,00","6,00","6","R6"],"en":["R6.00","6.00","6","R6"]},"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers om: 1 kg = 1 000 g. Koste = 250 ÷ 1 000 × R24,00 = R6,00. (R4,00 kry jy as jy 1 000 ÷ 250 bereken.)","en":"Convert first: 1 kg = 1 000 g. Cost = 250 ÷ 1 000 × R24.00 = R6.00. (You get R4.00 if you calculate 1 000 ÷ 250.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R4,00","R2,40","R60,00"],"en":["R4.00","R2.40","R60.00"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Seisoensprodukte is gewoonlik goedkoper, varser en smaakliker.","en":"Seasonal produce is usually cheaper, fresher and tastier."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar – wanneer iets in seisoen is, is daar baie van beskikbaar, dit hoef nie ver vervoer of lank gestoor te word nie, en die prys daal.","en":"True – when something is in season there is plenty available, it doesn't have to be transported far or stored long, and the price drops."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n brunch?","en":"What is a brunch?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Ligte ontbyt sonder gaar geregte","en":"A light breakfast without cooked dishes"},{"af":"'n Vaste driegang-aandete","en":"A set three-course dinner"},{"af":"'n Buffet wat net nageregte bedien","en":"A buffet that serves only desserts"},{"af":"'n Laatoggendmaaltyd wat ontbyt en middagete kombineer","en":"A late-morning meal that combines breakfast and lunch"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Brunch = breakfast + lunch: dit word laat in die oggend bedien en het items van albei maaltye. 'n Ligte ontbyt sonder gaar geregte is 'n kontinentale ontbyt.","en":"Brunch = breakfast + lunch: it is served late in the morning and has items from both meals. A light breakfast without cooked dishes is a continental breakfast."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die totale resepkoste is R126,00 vir 9 porsies. Die koste per porsie is R ___.","en":"The total recipe cost is R126.00 for 9 portions. The cost per portion is R ___."},"answers":{"af":["R14,00","14,00","14","R14"],"en":["R14.00","14.00","14","R14"]},"explain":{"af":"Koste per porsie = totale koste ÷ aantal porsies = R126,00 ÷ 9 = R14,00. (R1 134,00 kry jy as jy vermenigvuldig in plaas van deel.)","en":"Cost per portion = total cost ÷ number of portions = R126.00 ÷ 9 = R14.00. (You get R1 134.00 if you multiply instead of divide.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R12,60","R15,75","R1 134,00"],"en":["R12.60","R15.75","R1 134.00"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die koste per porsie van 'n gereg is R21,00 en die voedselkoste is 35%. Wat is die verkoopprys sonder BTW?","en":"The cost per portion of a dish is R21.00 and the food cost is 35%. What is the selling price excluding VAT?"},"options":[{"af":"R28,35","en":"R28.35"},{"af":"R7,35","en":"R7.35"},{"af":"R60,00","en":"R60.00"},{"af":"R69,00","en":"R69.00"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Verkoopprys = R21,00 ÷ 35 × 100 = R60,00. R28,35 is die algemene fout (R21 × 1,35) en R69,00 sluit reeds BTW in.","en":"Selling price = R21.00 ÷ 35 × 100 = R60.00. R28.35 is the common mistake (R21 × 1.35) and R69.00 already includes VAT."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Gereg se verkoopprys sonder BTW is R80,00. Met 15% BTW is die prys R ___.","en":"A dish's selling price excluding VAT is R80.00. With 15% VAT the price is R ___."},"answers":{"af":["R92,00","92,00","92","R92"],"en":["R92.00","92.00","92","R92"]},"explain":{"af":"R80,00 × 1,15 = R92,00. (R12,00 is net die BTW-bedrag, en R68,00 kry jy as jy die BTW aftrek.)","en":"R80.00 × 1.15 = R92.00. (R12.00 is only the VAT amount, and you get R68.00 if you subtract the VAT.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["R12,00","R68,00","R95,00"],"en":["R12.00","R68.00","R95.00"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die grootste beplanningsfout in hierdie spyskaart? Roomsop van Blomkool / Hoender in Witsous met Rys en Blomkool / Vanieljevla","en":"What is the biggest planning error in this menu? Cream of Cauliflower Soup / Chicken in White Sauce with Rice and Cauliflower / Vanilla Custard"},"options":[{"af":"Die gange is in die verkeerde volgorde.","en":"The courses are in the wrong order."},{"af":"Geen kleurvariasie nie en herhaling – alles is wit of roomkleurig en blomkool kom twee keer voor.","en":"No colour variety and repetition – everything is white or cream-coloured and cauliflower appears twice."},{"af":"Daar is geen nagereg nie.","en":"There is no dessert."},{"af":"Daar is te veel verskillende kleure.","en":"There are too many different colours."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die volgorde (sop → hoofgereg → nagereg) is reg, en vla is 'n nagereg. Die probleem is sintuiglike aantrekkingskrag: alles is bleek en blomkool word herhaal.","en":"The order (soup → main course → dessert) is correct, and custard is a dessert. The problem is sensory appeal: everything is pale and cauliflower is repeated."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Gereg kos R18,00 om te maak en word teen R72,00 (sonder BTW) verkoop. Die voedselkoste-persentasie is ___%.","en":"A dish costs R18.00 to make and is sold at R72.00 (excluding VAT). The food-cost percentage is ___%."},"answers":{"af":["25","25%","25 %"],"en":["25","25%","25 %"]},"explain":{"af":"Voedselkoste-% = R18 ÷ R72 × 100 = 25%. (75% is die deel wat oorbly vir ander koste en wins.)","en":"Food-cost % = R18 ÷ R72 × 100 = 25%. (75% is the part left over for other costs and profit.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["75","4","54"],"en":["75","4","54"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Ontbyt bestaan uit croissants, botter, appelkooskonfyt, lemoensap, jogurt, roereiers en koffie. Watter item verhoed dat dit 'n kontinentale ontbyt is?","en":"A breakfast consists of croissants, butter, apricot jam, orange juice, yoghurt, scrambled eggs and coffee. Which item stops it from being a continental breakfast?"},"options":[{"af":"Croissants","en":"Croissants"},{"af":"Lemoensap","en":"Orange juice"},{"af":"Jogurt","en":"Yoghurt"},{"af":"Roereiers","en":"Scrambled eggs"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Roereiers is 'n gaar (warm) gereg. 'n Kontinentale ontbyt het geen gaar geregte nie; croissants, sap en jogurt pas almal daarby.","en":"Scrambled eggs are a cooked (hot) dish. A continental breakfast has no cooked dishes; croissants, juice and yoghurt all fit."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Wildtuin-lodge in die Magaliesberg moet 'n spyskaart vir 'n troue met 120 gaste beplan. Watter keuse is die beste?","en":"A game lodge in the Magaliesberg has to plan a menu for a wedding with 120 guests. Which choice is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Funksiespyskaart (table d'hôte-styl) met 'n vaste prys per persoon – koste en hoeveelhede is vooraf bekend en almal word gelyktydig bedien.","en":"A function menu (table d'hôte style) with a fixed price per person – cost and quantities are known in advance and everyone is served at the same time."},{"af":"À la carte, want gaste hou daarvan om self te kies.","en":"À la carte, because guests like to choose for themselves."},{"af":"Carte du jour, want dit verander elke dag.","en":"Carte du jour, because it changes every day."},{"af":"'n Siklusspyskaart, want dit herhaal elke drie weke.","en":"A cyclical menu, because it repeats every three weeks."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Vir 120 gaste is à la carte te stadig en onvoorspelbaar (alles na bestelling). 'n Vaste funksiespyskaart laat die kombuis vooraf voorberei, maak kosteberekening en aankope akkuraat en sorg dat almal saam eet.","en":"For 120 guests à la carte is too slow and unpredictable (everything to order). A set function menu lets the kitchen prepare in advance, makes costing and purchasing accurate and ensures everyone eats together."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t3-maalvleis-pasta-slaai","title":{"af":"Maalvleis, worsies, pasta en slaaie","en":"Minced meat, sausages, pasta and salads"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die regte gaarmaakmetode vir vleissnitte kan kies, maalvleis veilig kan hanteer, pasta korrek kan kook en slaaie en slaaisouse kan beplan.","en":"You will be able to choose the right cooking method for meat cuts, handle mince safely, cook pasta correctly and plan salads and dressings."},"summary":{"af":"## Vleis: struktuur en sagtheid\n\nVleis is spierweefsel. Dit bestaan uit **spiervesels** (lang selle vol proteïen en water) wat in bondels deur **bindweefsel** bymekaar gehou word. Bindweefsel bevat twee proteïene:\n\n- **Kollageen** (wit): word sag en verander in **gelatien** as dit stadig met klam hitte gaargemaak word.\n- **Elastien** (geel en rekbaar): word **nie** sag as dit gekook word nie. Sny dit weg, of maak die vleis meganies sag (klop of maal dit).\n\nSpiere wat baie werk (bene, nek, bors) het meer bindweefsel en is dus **taaier**. Spiere wat min werk (langs die ruggraat) is **sag**.\n\n| Snit | Voorbeelde | Beste gaarmaakmetode |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sagte snitte | filet, lendestuk (*sirloin*), kruisskyf (*rump*) | **droë hitte**: rooster, braai, panbraai, oondbraai |\n| Taaier snitte | skenkel, borsstuk, dikrib (*chuck*), nek | **klam, stadige hitte**: stowe, smoor, potbraai |\n\n**Verbruining (Maillard-reaksie):** wanneer die proteïene en suikers op die vleis se oppervlak by hoë temperatuur bruin word, ontstaan nuwe geur- en kleurstowwe. Daarom verbruin ons vleis eers in 'n warm pan voordat ons dit stowe.\n\n### Klassifikasie van rooivleis in Suid-Afrika\n\nElke karkas kry 'n **rolmerk** (voedselveilige ink) wat die **ouderdomsklas** wys:\n\n| Klas | Permanente snytande | Kleur van die rolmerk |\n|---|---|---|\n| A (jongste) | geen | pers |\n| AB | 1–2 | groen |\n| B | 3–6 | bruin |\n| C (oudste) | meer as 6 | rooi |\n\nHoe jonger die dier, hoe sagter die vleis. Die **vetkode** (0–6) wys hoeveel vet daar is: 0 = geen vet, 1 = baie maer, 2 = maer, 3 = medium, 4 = vet, 5 = effens oorvet, 6 = buitensporig oorvet.\n\n## Maalvleis\n\nMaalvleis word van bees-, vark-, lams- of hoendervleis gemaak en is **maer** of **gewoon** (gewone maalvleis het meer vet, krimp meer en gee meer vet af).\n\n**Hoekom is maalvleis 'n hoërisiko-kos?** Bakterieë sit hoofsaaklik op die *oppervlak* van vleis. Wanneer vleis gemaal word, word die bakterieë deur die hele massa versprei, en die groot oppervlakte gee hulle baie plek om te groei.\n\n- Maak dit **deur en deur** gaar: geen pienk binne nie, en 'n kerntemperatuur van **minstens 75 °C**.\n- Bêre dit by **4 °C of kouer** en gebruik dit binne **1–2 dae**, of vries dit.\n- Ontdooi dit in die yskas, nooit op die kombuistoonbank nie.\n\n**Geregte:** bobotie, frikkadelle, hamburgerpatties, spaghetti bolognaise, lasagne en cottage pie (maalvleis onder kapokaartappels). Frikkadelle en patties het 'n **bindmiddel** nodig (eier, broodkrummels) sodat hulle nie uitmekaar val nie.\n\n## Worse\n\n**Boerewors** moet volgens wet minstens **90% vleis** bevat en **nie meer as 30% vet** nie. Dit word tradisioneel met koljander, naeltjies en asyn gegeur. *Vars* (rou) wors moet gaargemaak word; *gesoute of gerookte* worse (bv. Russians en Weense worsies) is reeds verwerk.\n\n> **Wenk:** Braai wors oor **medium** hitte en moenie dit prik nie. Die sappe en vet loop uit en die wors word droog.\n\n## Pasta\n\nPasta word gemaak van **durumkoring-semolina** en water (soms ook eier). **Vars pasta** kook binne 'n paar minute; **droë pasta** hou lank en kook langer (kyk op die pakkie).\n\n| Groep | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Lank | spaghetti, fettuccine, tagliatelle |\n| Kort/buise | penne, macaroni, fusilli, farfalle |\n| Velle | lasagne |\n| Gevul | ravioli, tortellini, cannelloni |\n\n**Reëls vir pasta kook:**\n\n1. Gebruik baie water: ongeveer **1 ℓ per 100 g** pasta.\n2. Bring die water tot 'n **vinnige kookpunt** en voeg sout by.\n3. Voeg die pasta by en **roer** sodat dit nie aan mekaar vassit nie.\n4. Kook tot **al dente** (\"tot by die tand\"): gaar, maar steeds effens ferm as jy daarin byt.\n5. **Dreineer** dadelik en sit saam met die sous voor.\n\nPas die sous by die vorm: dun, lang pasta met ligte, gladde souse; lintpasta (fettuccine) met roomsouse; buise en spirale met dik, stukkerige souse wat in die gaatjies vassit; velle word in lae gebak.\n\n## Slaaie\n\n**Dele van 'n slaai:** die **basis** (onderlaag, bv. slaaiblare), die **liggaam** (hoofbestanddele), die **slaaisous** en die **garnering**.\n\n**Tipes:** eenvoudige (groen) slaai; gemengde (saamgestelde) slaai; **gebonde slaai** (bestanddele met 'n dik sous saamgebind, bv. aartappelslaai en koolslaai); hoofgereg-slaai (met proteïen, bv. hoender); vrugteslaai.\n\n**Reëls:** vars, bros en koud; was die blare en **droog** hulle goed; **skeur** blare met die hand ('n mes beskadig die selle aan die snykant sodat dit bruin word); voeg die slaaisous **net voor opdiening** by; sorg vir kontras in kleur en tekstuur; sny alles in happiegrootte stukke.\n\n> **Hoekom verlep 'n slaai?** Die sout en suur in die slaaisous trek water uit die blaarselle. Nat blare, warmte en ou blare maak dit erger.\n\n## Slaaisouse en emulsies\n\n'n **Emulsie** is 'n mengsel van twee vloeistowwe wat normaalweg nie meng nie (olie en water), waar die een as klein druppeltjies deur die ander versprei is.\n\n- **Vinaigrette (Franse slaaisous):** 3 dele olie : 1 deel asyn of suurlemoensap, plus sout, peper en mosterd. Dit is 'n **tydelike emulsie**: dit skei as dit staan, dus **skud dit voor gebruik**.\n- **Mayonnaise:** eiergeel + olie (**druppel vir druppel** ingeklits) + asyn of suurlemoensap. Dit is 'n **permanente emulsie**, want **lesitien** in die eiergeel is die **emulgeermiddel**. As die olie te vinnig bygevoeg word, **skif** dit. Red dit só: begin met 'n vars eiergeel in 'n skoon bak en klits die geskifte mengsel druppel vir druppel daarby in.\n- **Jogurt- of roomslaaisouse** (bv. vir koolslaai): hou dit altyd in die yskas.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders sê vinaigrette is 'n permanente emulsie. Onthou: sonder 'n sterk emulgeermiddel soos lesitien skei die olie en asyn weer.","en":"## Meat: structure and tenderness\n\nMeat is muscle tissue. It consists of **muscle fibres** (long cells full of protein and water) held together in bundles by **connective tissue**. Connective tissue contains two proteins:\n\n- **Collagen** (white): softens and changes into **gelatine** when cooked slowly with moist heat.\n- **Elastin** (yellow and stretchy): does **not** soften when cooked. Cut it away, or tenderise the meat mechanically (pound or mince it).\n\nMuscles that work hard (legs, neck, breast) have more connective tissue and are therefore **tougher**. Muscles that do little work (along the backbone) are **tender**.\n\n| Cut | Examples | Best cooking method |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tender cuts | fillet, sirloin, rump | **dry heat**: grill, braai, pan-fry, roast |\n| Tougher cuts | shin, brisket, chuck, neck | **moist, slow heat**: stew, braise, pot-roast |\n\n**Browning (Maillard reaction):** when the proteins and sugars on the surface of meat brown at a high temperature, new flavour and colour compounds form. That is why we brown meat in a hot pan before stewing it.\n\n### Classification of red meat in South Africa\n\nEvery carcass gets a **roller mark** (food-safe ink) that shows its **age class**:\n\n| Class | Permanent incisors | Colour of the roller mark |\n|---|---|---|\n| A (youngest) | none | purple |\n| AB | 1–2 | green |\n| B | 3–6 | brown |\n| C (oldest) | more than 6 | red |\n\nThe younger the animal, the more tender the meat. The **fat code** (0–6) shows how much fat there is: 0 = no fat, 1 = very lean, 2 = lean, 3 = medium, 4 = fat, 5 = slightly overfat, 6 = excessively overfat.\n\n## Minced meat\n\nMinced meat is made from beef, pork, lamb or chicken and is **lean** or **regular** (regular mince has more fat, shrinks more and releases more fat).\n\n**Why is mince a high-risk food?** Bacteria are found mainly on the *surface* of meat. When meat is minced, the bacteria are spread through the whole mass, and the large surface area gives them lots of room to grow.\n\n- Cook it **right through**: no pink inside, and a core temperature of **at least 75 °C**.\n- Store it at **4 °C or colder** and use it within **1–2 days**, or freeze it.\n- Thaw it in the fridge, never on the kitchen counter.\n\n**Dishes:** bobotie, frikkadelle (meatballs), burger patties, spaghetti bolognaise, lasagne and cottage pie (mince under mashed potato). Meatballs and patties need a **binding agent** (egg, breadcrumbs) so that they do not fall apart.\n\n## Sausages\n\nBy law, **boerewors** must contain at least **90% meat** and **not more than 30% fat**. It is traditionally flavoured with coriander, cloves and vinegar. *Fresh* (raw) sausage must be cooked; *cured or smoked* sausages (e.g. Russians and Viennas) have already been processed.\n\n> **Tip:** Cook sausage over **medium** heat and do not prick it. The juices and fat run out and the sausage becomes dry.\n\n## Pasta\n\nPasta is made from **durum-wheat semolina** and water (sometimes egg as well). **Fresh pasta** cooks in a few minutes; **dried pasta** keeps for a long time and takes longer to cook (check the packet).\n\n| Group | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Long | spaghetti, fettuccine, tagliatelle |\n| Short/tubes | penne, macaroni, fusilli, farfalle |\n| Sheets | lasagne |\n| Filled | ravioli, tortellini, cannelloni |\n\n**Rules for cooking pasta:**\n\n1. Use plenty of water: about **1 ℓ per 100 g** of pasta.\n2. Bring the water to a **rapid boil** and add salt.\n3. Add the pasta and **stir** so that it does not stick together.\n4. Cook until **al dente** (\"to the tooth\"): cooked, but still slightly firm when you bite it.\n5. **Drain** immediately and serve with the sauce.\n\nMatch the sauce to the shape: thin, long pasta with light, smooth sauces; ribbon pasta (fettuccine) with cream sauces; tubes and spirals with thick, chunky sauces that catch in the holes; sheets are baked in layers.\n\n## Salads\n\n**Parts of a salad:** the **base** (underliner, e.g. lettuce leaves), the **body** (main ingredients), the **dressing** and the **garnish**.\n\n**Types:** simple (green) salad; mixed (composite) salad; **bound salad** (ingredients held together with a thick dressing, e.g. potato salad and coleslaw); main-course salad (with protein, e.g. chicken); fruit salad.\n\n**Rules:** fresh, crisp and cold; wash the leaves and **dry** them well; **tear** leaves by hand (a knife damages the cells along the cut so that it turns brown); add the dressing **just before serving**; provide contrast in colour and texture; cut everything into bite-size pieces.\n\n> **Why does a salad wilt?** The salt and acid in the dressing draw water out of the leaf cells. Wet leaves, warmth and old leaves make it worse.\n\n## Dressings and emulsions\n\nAn **emulsion** is a mixture of two liquids that normally do not mix (oil and water), in which one is spread as tiny droplets through the other.\n\n- **Vinaigrette (French dressing):** 3 parts oil : 1 part vinegar or lemon juice, plus salt, pepper and mustard. It is a **temporary emulsion**: it separates on standing, so **shake it before use**.\n- **Mayonnaise:** egg yolk + oil (whisked in **drop by drop**) + vinegar or lemon juice. It is a **permanent emulsion** because **lecithin** in the egg yolk is the **emulsifier**. If the oil is added too quickly, it **curdles**. Rescue it like this: start with a fresh egg yolk in a clean bowl and whisk the curdled mixture into it drop by drop.\n- **Yoghurt- or cream-based dressings** (e.g. for coleslaw): always keep them in the fridge.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners say vinaigrette is a permanent emulsion. Remember: without a strong emulsifier such as lecithin, the oil and vinegar separate again."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Kollageen","en":"Collagen"},"def":{"af":"Wit bindweefselproteïen wat by stadige, klam hitte sag word en in gelatien verander.","en":"White connective-tissue protein that softens with slow, moist heat and changes into gelatine."}},{"term":{"af":"Elastien","en":"Elastin"},"def":{"af":"Geel, rekbare bindweefsel wat nie sag word as dit gaargemaak word nie; dit moet weggesny of meganies sag gemaak word.","en":"Yellow, stretchy connective tissue that does not soften when cooked; it must be cut away or tenderised mechanically."}},{"term":{"af":"Maillard-reaksie","en":"Maillard reaction"},"def":{"af":"Die verbruining van proteïene en suikers op die oppervlak van kos by hoë temperatuur, wat geur en kleur gee.","en":"The browning of proteins and sugars on the surface of food at a high temperature, which gives flavour and colour."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoërisiko-kos","en":"High-risk food"},"def":{"af":"Kos waarin bakterieë maklik groei, soos maalvleis; dit moet koud gebêre en deeglik gaargemaak word.","en":"Food in which bacteria grow easily, such as mince; it must be stored cold and cooked thoroughly."}},{"term":{"af":"Durumkoring-semolina","en":"Durum-wheat semolina"},"def":{"af":"Grof gemaalde meel van harde durumkoring; die hoofbestanddeel van pasta.","en":"Coarsely ground flour from hard durum wheat; the main ingredient of pasta."}},{"term":{"af":"Al dente","en":"Al dente"},"def":{"af":"Italiaans vir 'tot by die tand': pasta wat gaar is, maar steeds effens ferm is as jy daarin byt.","en":"Italian for 'to the tooth': pasta that is cooked but still slightly firm when you bite it."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebonde slaai","en":"Bound salad"},"def":{"af":"'n Slaai waarvan die bestanddele met 'n dik slaaisous soos mayonnaise saamgebind word, bv. aartappelslaai of koolslaai.","en":"A salad whose ingredients are held together with a thick dressing such as mayonnaise, e.g. potato salad or coleslaw."}},{"term":{"af":"Emulsie","en":"Emulsion"},"def":{"af":"'n Mengsel van twee vloeistowwe wat normaalweg nie meng nie, waar die een as klein druppeltjies deur die ander versprei is.","en":"A mixture of two liquids that normally do not mix, in which one is spread as tiny droplets through the other."}},{"term":{"af":"Emulgeermiddel","en":"Emulsifier"},"def":{"af":"'n Stof wat 'n emulsie stabiel hou sodat dit nie skei nie, bv. lesitien in eiergeel.","en":"A substance that keeps an emulsion stable so that it does not separate, e.g. lecithin in egg yolk."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte gaarmaakmetode","en":"Choose the correct cooking method"},"problem":{"af":"'n Restaurant in Brits ontvang 'n aflewering beesfilet en beesskenkel. (a) Stel 'n gaarmaakmetode vir elke snit voor. (b) Verduidelik waarom elke metode geskik is.","en":"A restaurant in Brits receives a delivery of beef fillet and beef shin. (a) Suggest a cooking method for each cut. (b) Explain why each method is suitable."},"steps":[{"af":"Identifiseer die snitte: filet kom van 'n spier langs die ruggraat wat min werk, dus is dit 'n sagte snit. Skenkel kom van die been, wat baie werk, dus is dit 'n taai snit met baie bindweefsel.","en":"Identify the cuts: fillet comes from a muscle along the backbone that does little work, so it is a tender cut. Shin comes from the leg, which works hard, so it is a tough cut with a lot of connective tissue."},{"af":"Filet: gebruik droë hitte, bv. rooster, braai of panbraai. Dit het min bindweefsel, so kort, vinnige gaarmaak hou dit sag en sappig.","en":"Fillet: use dry heat, e.g. grill, braai or pan-fry. It has little connective tissue, so short, quick cooking keeps it tender and juicy."},{"af":"Skenkel: gebruik klam, stadige hitte, bv. stowe of smoor vir 'n paar uur. Die kollageen in die bindweefsel verander stadig in gelatien, en die vleis word sag.","en":"Shin: use moist, slow heat, e.g. stew or braise for a few hours. The collagen in the connective tissue slowly changes into gelatine and the meat becomes tender."},{"af":"Ekstra punt: verbruin die skenkel eers in 'n warm pan. Die Maillard-reaksie gee ekstra geur en kleur aan die bredie.","en":"Extra point: brown the shin in a hot pan first. The Maillard reaction gives the stew extra flavour and colour."}],"answer":{"af":"Filet → droë hitte (rooster/braai/panbraai); skenkel → klam, stadige hitte (stowe/smoor), omdat die kollageen dan in gelatien verander.","en":"Fillet → dry heat (grill/braai/pan-fry); shin → moist, slow heat (stew/braise), because the collagen then changes into gelatine."}},{"title":{"af":"Pasta vir 'n rugbyspan","en":"Pasta for a rugby team"},"problem":{"af":"Jy kook spaghetti bolognaise vir 'n rugbyspan van 15 spelers. Die resep gebruik 120 g droë spaghetti per persoon. Spaghetti kos R28 vir 'n pak van 500 g. Bereken (a) hoeveel spaghetti jy nodig het, (b) hoeveel water jy nodig het volgens die reël van 1 ℓ per 100 g, en (c) hoeveel pakke jy moet koop en wat dit kos.","en":"You are cooking spaghetti bolognaise for a rugby team of 15 players. The recipe uses 120 g of dried spaghetti per person. Spaghetti costs R28 for a 500 g packet. Calculate (a) how much spaghetti you need, (b) how much water you need using the rule of 1 ℓ per 100 g, and (c) how many packets you must buy and what they cost."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Spaghetti: 15 × 120 g = 1 800 g = 1,8 kg","en":"(a) Spaghetti: 15 × 120 g = 1 800 g = 1.8 kg"},{"af":"(b) Water: 1 800 g ÷ 100 g = 18, dus 18 × 1 ℓ = 18 ℓ. Verdeel dit in die praktyk oor twee of drie groot potte sodat die water vinnig bly kook.","en":"(b) Water: 1 800 g ÷ 100 g = 18, so 18 × 1 ℓ = 18 ℓ. In practice, divide it between two or three large pots so the water keeps boiling rapidly."},{"af":"(c) Pakke: 1 800 g ÷ 500 g = 3,6 pakke. Jy kan nie 'n deel van 'n pak koop nie, dus rond op na 4 pakke.","en":"(c) Packets: 1 800 g ÷ 500 g = 3.6 packets. You cannot buy part of a packet, so round up to 4 packets."},{"af":"Koste: 4 × R28 = R112","en":"Cost: 4 × R28 = R112"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 1,8 kg spaghetti; (b) 18 ℓ water; (c) 4 pakke = R112","en":"(a) 1.8 kg spaghetti; (b) 18 ℓ water; (c) 4 packets = R112"}},{"title":{"af":"Maak 'n vinaigrette","en":"Make a vinaigrette"},"problem":{"af":"Jy moet 360 ml vinaigrette vir 'n buffet maak in die verhouding 3 dele olie : 1 deel asyn. (a) Bereken hoeveel olie en hoeveel asyn jy nodig het. (b) Verduidelik waarom die kelners die vinaigrette moet skud voordat hulle dit oor die slaai gooi.","en":"You must make 360 ml of vinaigrette for a buffet in the ratio 3 parts oil : 1 part vinegar. (a) Calculate how much oil and how much vinegar you need. (b) Explain why the waiters must shake the vinaigrette before they pour it over the salad."},"steps":[{"af":"Totale dele: 3 + 1 = 4 dele","en":"Total parts: 3 + 1 = 4 parts"},{"af":"Een deel: 360 ml ÷ 4 = 90 ml","en":"One part: 360 ml ÷ 4 = 90 ml"},{"af":"Olie: 3 × 90 ml = 270 ml; asyn: 1 × 90 ml = 90 ml. Kontroleer: 270 + 90 = 360 ml ✔","en":"Oil: 3 × 90 ml = 270 ml; vinegar: 1 × 90 ml = 90 ml. Check: 270 + 90 = 360 ml ✔"},{"af":"(b) Vinaigrette is 'n tydelike emulsie: daar is geen sterk emulgeermiddel nie, dus skei die olie en asyn as dit staan. Skud dit net voor gebruik sodat elke porsie olie én asyn kry.","en":"(b) Vinaigrette is a temporary emulsion: there is no strong emulsifier, so the oil and vinegar separate on standing. Shake it just before use so that every portion gets oil and vinegar."}],"answer":{"af":"270 ml olie en 90 ml asyn; skud dit, want dit is 'n tydelike emulsie wat skei.","en":"270 ml oil and 90 ml vinegar; shake it, because it is a temporary emulsion that separates."}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: foute met maalvleis","en":"Source question: mistakes with mince"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die scenario: Pieter koop Vrydagoggend 1 kg maalvleis by die slaghuis in Brits. Hy laat dit twee uur lank in sy warm motor terwyl hy inkopies doen. By die huis sit hy dit in die yskas, en eers die volgende Woensdag maak hy hamburgerpatties daarmee. Die patties is buite mooi bruin, maar binne nog pienk. Identifiseer drie foute en sê wat Pieter moes gedoen het.","en":"Read the scenario: On Friday morning Pieter buys 1 kg of mince at the butchery in Brits. He leaves it in his hot car for two hours while he shops. At home he puts it in the fridge, and only the following Wednesday does he make burger patties with it. The patties are nicely brown outside but still pink inside. Identify three mistakes and say what Pieter should have done."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: Die maalvleis het twee uur in 'n warm motor gelê. Bakterieë vermenigvuldig vinnig in warmte, en maalvleis is 'n hoërisiko-kos. Hy moes dit in 'n koelsak gesit en dadelik in die yskas (4 °C of kouer) gebêre het.","en":"Mistake 1: The mince lay in a hot car for two hours. Bacteria multiply quickly in warmth, and mince is a high-risk food. He should have put it in a cooler bag and refrigerated it (4 °C or colder) straight away."},{"af":"Fout 2: Van Vrydag tot Woensdag is 5 dae – baie langer as die 1–2 dae wat maalvleis in die yskas mag bly. Hy moes dit teen Saterdag gebruik of dadelik gevries het.","en":"Mistake 2: From Friday to Wednesday is 5 days – much longer than the 1–2 days mince may stay in the fridge. He should have used it by Saturday or frozen it straight away."},{"af":"Fout 3: Die patties is binne nog pienk. Omdat die bakterieë deur die hele maalvleis versprei is, moet die kern minstens 75 °C bereik en daar mag geen pienk wees nie. Hy moes dit oor medium hitte langer gaargemaak het.","en":"Mistake 3: The patties are still pink inside. Because the bacteria are spread through all of the mince, the core must reach at least 75 °C and there may be no pink. He should have cooked them longer over medium heat."}],"answer":{"af":"1) Warm motor → hou dit koud; 2) 5 dae in die yskas → gebruik binne 1–2 dae of vries; 3) pienk binne → maak gaar tot geen pienk, kern minstens 75 °C.","en":"1) Hot car → keep it cold; 2) 5 days in the fridge → use within 1–2 days or freeze; 3) pink inside → cook until no pink, core at least 75 °C."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tipe slaai is aartappelslaai?","en":"What type of salad is potato salad?"},"options":[{"af":"Eenvoudige (groen) slaai","en":"Simple (green) salad"},{"af":"Gebonde slaai","en":"Bound salad"},{"af":"Vrugteslaai","en":"Fruit salad"},{"af":"Hoofgereg-slaai","en":"Main-course salad"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Aartappelslaai is 'n gebonde slaai: die stukke aartappel word met 'n dik sous (mayonnaise) saamgebind. Koolslaai is nog 'n voorbeeld.","en":"Potato salad is a bound salad: the pieces of potato are held together with a thick dressing (mayonnaise). Coleslaw is another example."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die slaaiblare wat die bord uitvoer en onder die res van die slaai lê, vorm die ___ van die slaai.","en":"The lettuce leaves that line the plate and lie under the rest of the salad form the ___ of the salad."},"answers":{"af":["basis","onderlaag","basis/onderlaag"],"en":["base","underliner","base/underliner"]},"explain":{"af":"Die basis (onderlaag) lê onder; die liggaam is die hoofbestanddele, en die garnering kom bo-op vir kleur en aantreklikheid.","en":"The base (underliner) lies underneath; the body is the main ingredients, and the garnish goes on top for colour and appeal."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["liggaam","garnering","slaaisous"],"en":["body","garnish","dressing"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Mayonnaise is 'n permanente emulsie omdat die lesitien in eiergeel as emulgeermiddel optree.","en":"Mayonnaise is a permanent emulsion because the lecithin in egg yolk acts as an emulsifier."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Lesitien hou die olie-druppeltjies deur die asyn versprei, daarom skei mayonnaise nie soos 'n vinaigrette nie.","en":"True. Lecithin keeps the oil droplets spread through the vinegar, which is why mayonnaise does not separate like a vinaigrette."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Droë pasta word hoofsaaklik van ___ en water gemaak.","en":"Dried pasta is made mainly from ___ and water."},"answers":{"af":["semolina","durum-semolina","durumsemolina","durumkoring-semolina","griesmeel"],"en":["semolina","durum semolina","durum-wheat semolina","durum wheat semolina"]},"explain":{"af":"Pasta word van durumkoring-semolina gemaak. Durumkoring is 'n harde koring met baie proteïen, en daarom hou pasta sy vorm as dit gekook word.","en":"Pasta is made from durum-wheat semolina. Durum wheat is a hard wheat with a lot of protein, which is why pasta keeps its shape when cooked."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koekmeel","mieliemeel","rogmeel"],"en":["cake flour","maize meal","rye flour"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom word maalvleis as 'n hoërisiko-kos beskou?","en":"Why is mince regarded as a high-risk food?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit bevat altyd meer vet as ander vleis","en":"It always contains more fat than other meat"},{"af":"Dit word van die swakste vleis gemaak","en":"It is made from the poorest-quality meat"},{"af":"Maal versprei bakterieë van die oppervlak deur die hele vleis en vergroot die oppervlakte","en":"Mincing spreads bacteria from the surface through all of the meat and increases the surface area"},{"af":"Dit bevat minder proteïen as 'n steak","en":"It contains less protein than a steak"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Bakterieë sit op die oppervlak van vleis. Met maal kom hulle oral in die vleis, en die groot oppervlakte laat hulle vinnig groei. Daarom moet maalvleis deur en deur gaar wees.","en":"Bacteria sit on the surface of meat. Mincing spreads them all through the meat, and the large surface area lets them grow quickly. That is why mince must be cooked right through."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maalvleis moet so gaargemaak word dat die kerntemperatuur minstens ___ °C bereik.","en":"Mince must be cooked so that the core temperature reaches at least ___ °C."},"answers":{"af":["75","75 °C","75°C"],"en":["75","75 °C","75°C"]},"explain":{"af":"Die kern (middel) van maalvleisgeregte moet minstens 75 °C bereik, en daar mag geen pienk vleis oorbly nie.","en":"The core (centre) of mince dishes must reach at least 75 °C, and no pink meat may remain."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["37","50","60"],"en":["37","50","60"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom word 'n taai snit soos skenkel sag as dit stadig gestowe word?","en":"Why does a tough cut such as shin become tender when it is stewed slowly?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kollageen in die bindweefsel verander in gelatien","en":"The collagen in the connective tissue changes into gelatine"},{"af":"Die elastien smelt en word sag","en":"The elastin melts and becomes soft"},{"af":"Die vet verander in proteïen","en":"The fat changes into protein"},{"af":"Die water maak die spiervesels langer","en":"The water makes the muscle fibres longer"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Stadige, klam hitte verander kollageen in gelatien. Elastien word NIE sag nie – dit is die lokval in hierdie vraag.","en":"Slow, moist heat changes collagen into gelatine. Elastin does NOT soften – that is the trap in this question."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy moet boerewors met 'n vurk prik voordat jy dit braai sodat dit nie bars nie.","en":"You should prick boerewors with a fork before you braai it so that it does not burst."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. As jy wors prik, loop die sappe en vet uit en word die wors droog. Braai dit eerder oor medium hitte sodat dit nie bars nie.","en":"False. If you prick sausage, the juices and fat run out and it becomes dry. Rather cook it over medium heat so that it does not burst."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hoofrede waarom jy 'n vinaigrette moet skud net voordat jy dit oor 'n slaai gooi?","en":"What is the main reason why you must shake a vinaigrette just before you pour it over a salad?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die sout te laat oplos","en":"To make the salt dissolve"},{"af":"Om lug in te klits sodat dit dik word","en":"To whisk in air so that it thickens"},{"af":"Dit is 'n permanente emulsie wat dik word as dit staan","en":"It is a permanent emulsion that thickens on standing"},{"af":"Dit is 'n tydelike emulsie: die olie en asyn skei as dit staan","en":"It is a temporary emulsion: the oil and vinegar separate on standing"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vinaigrette het geen sterk emulgeermiddel nie, dus is dit 'n tydelike emulsie. Skud dit sodat die olie en asyn weer meng.","en":"Vinaigrette has no strong emulsifier, so it is a temporary emulsion. Shake it so that the oil and vinegar mix again."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke pastavorm by die regte groep.","en":"Match each pasta shape to the correct group."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Fettuccine","en":"Fettuccine"},"r":{"af":"Lang pasta","en":"Long pasta"}},{"l":{"af":"Penne","en":"Penne"},"r":{"af":"Kort pasta (buise)","en":"Short pasta (tubes)"}},{"l":{"af":"Lasagne","en":"Lasagne"},"r":{"af":"Velle","en":"Sheets"}},{"l":{"af":"Ravioli","en":"Ravioli"},"r":{"af":"Gevulde pasta","en":"Filled pasta"}}],"explain":{"af":"Fettuccine is lang lintpasta, penne is kort buise, lasagne is plat velle wat in lae gebak word, en ravioli is gevulde pasta.","en":"Fettuccine is long ribbon pasta, penne is short tubes, lasagne is flat sheets baked in layers, and ravioli is filled pasta."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy kook 400 g droë pasta. Volgens die reël van 1 ℓ water per 100 g pasta het jy ___ ℓ water nodig.","en":"You are cooking 400 g of dried pasta. Using the rule of 1 ℓ of water per 100 g of pasta, you need ___ ℓ of water."},"answers":{"af":["4","4 ℓ","4 l","4 liter"],"en":["4","4 ℓ","4 l","4 litres","4 liters"]},"explain":{"af":"400 g ÷ 100 g = 4, dus 4 × 1 ℓ = 4 ℓ water. Baie water hou die kookpunt hoog en keer dat die pasta aan mekaar vassit.","en":"400 g ÷ 100 g = 4, so 4 × 1 ℓ = 4 ℓ of water. Plenty of water keeps it boiling and stops the pasta sticking together."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","2","40"],"en":["1","2","40"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Spyskaart vra vir 'n sagte, geurige beesgereg van borsstuk. Watter gaarmaakmetode is die beste?","en":"A menu calls for a tender, flavourful beef dish made from brisket. Which cooking method is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Vinnig rooster onder 'n warm rooster","en":"Grill quickly under a hot grill"},{"af":"Stadig smoor in 'n toe pot met vloeistof","en":"Braise slowly in a covered pot with liquid"},{"af":"Roerbraai vir 3 minute","en":"Stir-fry for 3 minutes"},{"af":"Panbraai tot medium-rooi","en":"Pan-fry until medium-rare"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Borsstuk is 'n taai snit met baie bindweefsel. Klam, stadige hitte (smoor) verander die kollageen in gelatien. Vinnige, droë hitte maak dit net taaier.","en":"Brisket is a tough cut with a lot of connective tissue. Moist, slow heat (braising) changes the collagen into gelatine. Quick, dry heat only makes it tougher."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Jy maak 'n vinaigrette in die verhouding 3 dele olie : 1 deel asyn. As jy 80 ml asyn gebruik, het jy ___ ml olie nodig.","en":"You make a vinaigrette in the ratio 3 parts oil : 1 part vinegar. If you use 80 ml of vinegar, you need ___ ml of oil."},"answers":{"af":["240","240 ml"],"en":["240","240 ml"]},"explain":{"af":"1 deel = 80 ml, dus olie = 3 × 80 = 240 ml. (320 ml is die totale hoeveelheid slaaisous, nie die olie nie.)","en":"1 part = 80 ml, so oil = 3 × 80 = 240 ml. (320 ml is the total amount of dressing, not the oil.)"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["80","160","320"],"en":["80","160","320"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Beeskarkas het 'n pers rolmerk met vetkode 2. Wat beteken dit?","en":"A beef carcass has a purple roller mark with fat code 2. What does this mean?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Ou dier (klas C) met baie vet","en":"An old animal (class C) with a lot of fat"},{"af":"'n Middeljarige dier (klas B) met geen vet nie","en":"A middle-aged animal (class B) with no fat"},{"af":"'n Jong dier (klas A) met maer vleis","en":"A young animal (class A) with lean meat"},{"af":"'n Jong dier (klas AB) wat buitensporig oorvet is","en":"A young animal (class AB) that is excessively overfat"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Pers = klas A, die jongste (geen permanente snytande nie) en dus die sagste. Vetkode 2 = maer. Klas C is rooi, klas B bruin en klas AB groen.","en":"Purple = class A, the youngest (no permanent incisors) and therefore the most tender. Fat code 2 = lean. Class C is red, class B brown and class AB green."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Groen slaai word om 17:00 met vinaigrette aangemaak en eers om 18:30 bedien. Die blare is pap en verlep. Wat is die hoofrede?","en":"A green salad is dressed with vinaigrette at 17:00 and only served at 18:30. The leaves are limp and wilted. What is the main reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Die sout en suur in die slaaisous het water uit die blare getrek","en":"The salt and acid in the dressing drew water out of the leaves"},{"af":"Die blare is met die hand geskeur in plaas van gesny","en":"The leaves were torn by hand instead of cut"},{"af":"Die slaai is te koud bedien","en":"The salad was served too cold"},{"af":"Die olie in die slaaisous het die blare uitgedroog","en":"The oil in the dressing dried out the leaves"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die slaaisous was 1½ uur lank op die blare. Sout en suur trek water uit die blaarselle, en die blare verlep. Voeg die slaaisous net voor opdiening by. (Skeur is juis die regte metode, en 'n slaai moet koud wees.)","en":"The dressing was on the leaves for 1½ hours. Salt and acid draw water out of the leaf cells and the leaves wilt. Add the dressing just before serving. (Tearing is in fact the correct method, and a salad should be cold.)"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi koop Maandag maalvleis en bêre dit by 4 °C in die yskas. Sy wil Saterdag frikkadelle daarmee maak. Wat is die beste raad?","en":"Thandi buys mince on Monday and stores it at 4 °C in the fridge. She wants to make meatballs with it on Saturday. What is the best advice?"},"options":[{"af":"Gebruik dit Saterdag – kos in die yskas hou 'n week","en":"Use it on Saturday – food in the fridge keeps for a week"},{"af":"Kook dit net langer; hitte maak alle gevare dood","en":"Just cook it longer; heat destroys all dangers"},{"af":"Ruik daaraan: as dit nie sleg ruik nie, is dit veilig","en":"Smell it: if it does not smell bad, it is safe"},{"af":"Dit is te oud – sy moes dit binne 1–2 dae gebruik of gevries het, dus moet sy dit weggooi","en":"It is too old – she should have used it within 1–2 days or frozen it, so she must throw it away"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Maandag tot Saterdag is 5 dae. Bakterieë groei stadig selfs by 4 °C, en sommige bakterieë vorm gifstowwe wat nie deur kook vernietig word nie. Gevaarlike bakterieë ruik ook nie altyd sleg nie. Die veilige besluit is om dit weg te gooi.","en":"Monday to Saturday is 5 days. Bacteria grow slowly even at 4 °C, and some bacteria form toxins that cooking does not destroy. Dangerous bacteria also do not always smell bad. The safe decision is to throw it away."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Veiligheid, sekuriteit en akkommodasie","en":"Safety, security and accommodation"},"topics":[{"id":"gas10-t4-veiligheid-sekuriteit","title":{"af":"Veiligheid, noodhulp en sekuriteit","en":"Safety, first aid and security"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal gevare in 'n kombuis kan raaksien en voorkom, die regte brandblusser kan kies, noodhulp kan toepas en sekuriteitsmaatreëls vir gaste, personeel, voorraad en kontant kan voorstel.","en":"You will be able to identify and prevent hazards in a kitchen, choose the correct fire extinguisher, apply first aid and suggest security measures for guests, staff, stock and cash."},"summary":{"af":"## Die Wet op Beroepsgesondheid en -veiligheid (Wet 85 van 1993)\n\nHierdie Wet beskerm die gesondheid en veiligheid van almal by die werk. Dit plaas pligte op albei kante:\n\n| Werkgewer (artikel 8) | Werknemer (artikel 14) |\n|---|---|\n| Voorsien en onderhou 'n veilige werkplek en veilige toerusting | Sorg vir jou eie en ander se veiligheid en werk saam met die werkgewer |\n| Lei personeel op en gee inligting oor gevare | Volg alle veiligheidsreëls en -prosedures |\n| Voorsien 'n toegeruste noodhulpkissie en beskermende klere waar nodig | Dra die beskermende klere wat voorsien word |\n| Identifiseer gevare en neem stappe om dit te verminder | Rapporteer gevare, onveilige toestande en ongelukke dadelik |\n\n## Ongelukke in die kombuis en restaurant – en hoe om dit te voorkom\n\n| Gevaar | Voorkoming |\n|---|---|\n| **Brandwonde** (droë hitte: oond, warm panne, vlamme) en **skroeiwonde** (stoom en warm vloeistowwe soos kookwater) | Draai pothandvatsels **na binne**; gebruik **droë** oondhandskoene (nat handskoene gelei hitte); lig deksels weg van jou af; moenie potte te vol maak nie |\n| **Snywonde** | Hou messe **skerp** (stomp messe gly); gebruik die **klougreep**; sit 'n klam lap onder die snyplank; los nooit messe in seepwater nie; moenie 'n vallende mes probeer vang nie |\n| **Gly, struikel en val** | Vee storting **dadelik** op; plaas 'n “**nat vloer**”-teken; dra **glyvaste skoene**; hou looppaaie oop |\n| **Elektriese skokke** | Werk met **droë hande**; kontroleer koorde en proppe; geen water naby proppe nie; skakel toestelle af voordat jy dit skoonmaak |\n| **Spierverrekking** | Lig met **gebuigde knieë** en 'n **reguit rug**; hou die vrag naby jou liggaam; kry hulp of gebruik 'n trollie |\n\n**Gebreekte glas of breekware:** moenie dit met kaal hande optel nie. Vee dit met 'n besem en skoppie op (klein stukkies met 'n klam papierhanddoek), draai dit in koerantpapier toe en gooi dit in 'n aparte, gemerkte houer. As glas in 'n opwasbak breek, laat eers die water uitloop. Gooi kos weg wat naby die gebreekte glas was.\n\n## Brandveiligheid\n\nDie **vuurdriehoek**: 'n vuur het **hitte**, **brandstof** en **suurstof** nodig. Verwyder een sy en die vuur gaan dood: koel dit af (hitte weg), versmoor dit (suurstof weg) of neem die brandstof weg (bv. skakel die gas af).\n\n| Blusser | Gebruik op |\n|---|---|\n| Water | **slegs** hout, papier en materiaal |\n| Skuim | vlambare vloeistowwe (bv. petrol) en vaste stowwe |\n| CO₂ (koolstofdioksied) | **elektriese** brande en vlambare vloeistowwe; gelei nie elektrisiteit nie en laat geen residu nie |\n| Droë chemiese poeier (DCP) | veeldoelig: die meeste brande, ook elektriese brande |\n| Nat chemiese blusser en **brandkombers** | brande in **kookolie en vet** |\n\n> **Onthou!** Gooi **nooit water** op 'n olie- of vetbrand nie. Die water sak onder die olie, verander onmiddellik in stoom en skiet die brandende olie oral heen – 'n vuurbal. Skakel die hitte af (as dit veilig is), bedek die pan met 'n deksel of brandkombers en laat dit toe totdat dit afgekoel het.\n\n**Ontruiming:** lui die alarm; volg die ontruimingsplan; gebruik die nooduitgange (nooit die hysbak nie); moenie vir besittings stop nie; gaan na die **versamelpunt**, waar almal getel word. Nooduitgange moet duidelik gemerk, oopgesluit en vry van hindernisse wees.\n\n## Noodhulp\n\n**Noodhulpkissie:** blou pleisters (maklik sigbaar as dit in kos val), verbande, steriele gaas, weggooibare handskoene, antiseptiese middel, brandwondverband en 'n skêr. Kontroleer en vul dit gereeld aan.\n\n| Besering | Wat om te doen |\n|---|---|\n| Brand- of skroeiwond | Koel onder koel lopende water vir **minstens 10 minute**; verwyder ringe; moenie blase oopbreek of botter smeer nie; bedek los met kleefplastiek of 'n skoon verband |\n| Snywond | Trek handskoene aan; druk op die wond om die bloeding te stop; maak skoon; blou pleister **plus** 'n handskoen as jy met kos werk |\n| Neusbloeding | Sit en **leun vorentoe**; knyp die sagte deel van die neus vir ongeveer **10 minute** |\n| Verstikking | Rugslae tussen die skouerblaaie, dan **buikstote** (die Heimlich-maneuver) |\n| Elektriese skok | **Skakel eers die krag af** voordat jy aan die persoon raak |\n| Floutes | Laat die persoon plat lê en **lig die bene** |\n\nKry mediese hulp by ernstige beserings: skakel **10177** (ambulans) of **112** van 'n selfoon. Rapporteer en teken elke besering aan.\n\n## Sekuriteit\n\n- **Gaste:** sleutelkaarte (wat vir elke nuwe gas herprogrammeer word), kluisies in die kamers, kringtelevisie (CCTV) en toegangsbeheer. **Moenie kamernommers hardop sê nie**, en gee nooit 'n kamernommer of sleutel aan iemand sonder bewys van identiteit nie.\n- **Personeel:** sluitkassies vir persoonlike besittings, 'n aparte personeelingang en ID-kaarte of naamkaartjies.\n- **Eiendom en voorraad:** gesluite stoorkamers, **sleutelbeheer** ('n sleutelregister en min sleutelhouers), gereelde **voorraadopname**, en aflewerings wat teen die faktuur nagegaan word.\n- **Kontant:** kluise, min kontant in die kasregister, en 'n **kontantopmaak** aan die einde van elke skof: **verwagte kontant = vlot + kontantverkope**. Vergelyk dit met die kontant wat getel is; die verskil is 'n tekort of 'n surplus.\n\n> **Wenk vir die eksamen:** As jy gevare in 'n beskrewe kombuis moet identifiseer, noem die gevaar én die voorkomingsmaatreël – albei kry gewoonlik 'n punt.","en":"## The Occupational Health and Safety Act (Act 85 of 1993)\n\nThis Act protects the health and safety of everyone at work. It places duties on both sides:\n\n| Employer (section 8) | Employee (section 14) |\n|---|---|\n| Provide and maintain a safe workplace and safe equipment | Take care of your own and others' safety and co-operate with the employer |\n| Train staff and give information about hazards | Follow all safety rules and procedures |\n| Provide an equipped first-aid kit and protective clothing where needed | Wear the protective clothing that is provided |\n| Identify hazards and take steps to reduce them | Report hazards, unsafe conditions and accidents immediately |\n\n## Accidents in the kitchen and restaurant – and how to prevent them\n\n| Hazard | Prevention |\n|---|---|\n| **Burns** (dry heat: oven, hot pans, flames) and **scalds** (steam and hot liquids such as boiling water) | Turn pot handles **inwards**; use **dry** oven gloves (wet gloves conduct heat); lift lids away from you; do not overfill pots |\n| **Cuts** | Keep knives **sharp** (blunt knives slip); use the **claw grip**; put a damp cloth under the cutting board; never leave knives in soapy water; do not try to catch a falling knife |\n| **Slips, trips and falls** | Wipe up spills **at once**; put out a “**wet floor**” sign; wear **non-slip shoes**; keep walkways clear |\n| **Electric shocks** | Work with **dry hands**; check cords and plugs; no water near plugs; switch appliances off before cleaning them |\n| **Strains** | Lift with **bent knees** and a **straight back**; keep the load close to your body; get help or use a trolley |\n\n**Broken glass or crockery:** do not pick it up with bare hands. Sweep it up with a brush and dustpan (small pieces with a damp paper towel), wrap it in newspaper and put it in a separate, marked container. If glass breaks in a sink, drain the water first. Throw away any food that was near the broken glass.\n\n## Fire safety\n\nThe **fire triangle**: a fire needs **heat**, **fuel** and **oxygen**. Remove one side and the fire goes out: cool it (remove heat), smother it (remove oxygen) or take away the fuel (e.g. switch off the gas).\n\n| Extinguisher | Use on |\n|---|---|\n| Water | wood, paper and fabric **only** |\n| Foam | flammable liquids (e.g. petrol) and solids |\n| CO₂ (carbon dioxide) | **electrical** fires and flammable liquids; does not conduct electricity and leaves no residue |\n| Dry chemical powder (DCP) | multipurpose: most fires, including electrical fires |\n| Wet chemical extinguisher and **fire blanket** | **cooking-oil and fat** fires |\n\n> **Remember!** **Never** throw **water** on an oil or fat fire. The water sinks below the oil, instantly turns into steam and throws the burning oil everywhere – a fireball. Switch off the heat (if it is safe), cover the pan with a lid or fire blanket and leave it covered until it has cooled down.\n\n**Evacuation:** raise the alarm; follow the evacuation plan; use the fire exits (never the lift); do not stop for belongings; go to the **assembly point**, where everyone is counted. Fire exits must be clearly marked, unlocked and free of obstructions.\n\n## First aid\n\n**First-aid kit:** blue plasters (easy to see if they fall into food), bandages, sterile gauze, disposable gloves, antiseptic, burn dressing and scissors. Check and restock it regularly.\n\n| Injury | What to do |\n|---|---|\n| Burn or scald | Cool under cool running water for **at least 10 minutes**; remove rings; do not burst blisters or apply butter; cover loosely with cling wrap or a clean dressing |\n| Cut | Put on gloves; press on the wound to stop the bleeding; clean it; blue plaster **plus** a glove if you work with food |\n| Nosebleed | Sit and **lean forward**; pinch the soft part of the nose for about **10 minutes** |\n| Choking | Back blows between the shoulder blades, then **abdominal thrusts** (the Heimlich manoeuvre) |\n| Electric shock | **Switch off the power first** before you touch the person |\n| Fainting | Let the person lie flat and **raise the legs** |\n\nGet medical help for serious injuries: call **10177** (ambulance) or **112** from a cellphone. Report and record every injury.\n\n## Security\n\n- **Guests:** key cards (reprogrammed for every new guest), room safes, CCTV and access control. **Do not say room numbers aloud**, and never give a room number or key to anyone without proof of identity.\n- **Staff:** lockers for personal belongings, a separate staff entrance and ID cards or name badges.\n- **Property and stock:** locked storerooms, **key control** (a key register and few key holders), regular **stocktaking**, and deliveries checked against the invoice.\n- **Cash:** safes, little cash in the till, and a **cash-up** at the end of every shift: **expected cash = float + cash sales**. Compare this with the cash counted; the difference is a shortage or a surplus.\n\n> **Exam tip:** When you have to identify hazards in a described kitchen, give the hazard and the prevention measure – each usually earns a mark."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Wet op Beroepsgesondheid en -veiligheid","en":"Occupational Health and Safety Act"},"def":{"af":"Wet 85 van 1993, wat die gesondheid en veiligheid van mense by die werk beskerm en pligte aan werkgewers en werknemers opdra.","en":"Act 85 of 1993, which protects the health and safety of people at work and places duties on employers and employees."}},{"term":{"af":"Gevaar","en":"Hazard"},"def":{"af":"Enigiets in die werkplek wat 'n besering of skade kan veroorsaak, bv. 'n nat vloer of 'n beskadigde koord.","en":"Anything in the workplace that can cause injury or damage, e.g. a wet floor or a damaged cord."}},{"term":{"af":"Skroeiwond","en":"Scald"},"def":{"af":"'n Brandwond wat deur stoom of 'n warm vloeistof soos kookwater veroorsaak word.","en":"A burn caused by steam or a hot liquid such as boiling water."}},{"term":{"af":"Vuurdriehoek","en":"Fire triangle"},"def":{"af":"Die drie dinge wat 'n vuur nodig het om te brand: hitte, brandstof en suurstof.","en":"The three things a fire needs to burn: heat, fuel and oxygen."}},{"term":{"af":"Brandkombers","en":"Fire blanket"},"def":{"af":"'n Kombers van brandbestande materiaal wat oor 'n klein vuur, soos 'n panbrand, gegooi word om die suurstof af te sny.","en":"A blanket of fire-resistant material that is placed over a small fire, such as a pan fire, to cut off the oxygen."}},{"term":{"af":"Versamelpunt","en":"Assembly point"},"def":{"af":"Die aangewese veilige plek buite die gebou waar almal ná 'n ontruiming bymekaarkom en getel word.","en":"The designated safe place outside the building where everyone gathers and is counted after an evacuation."}},{"term":{"af":"Noodhulp","en":"First aid"},"def":{"af":"Die eerste hulp wat aan 'n beseerde of siek persoon gegee word voordat mediese hulp opdaag.","en":"The first help given to an injured or ill person before medical help arrives."}},{"term":{"af":"Heimlich-maneuver","en":"Heimlich manoeuvre"},"def":{"af":"Buikstote wat gebruik word om 'n voorwerp uit die lugweg van 'n persoon wat verstik, te dwing.","en":"Abdominal thrusts used to force an object out of the airway of a person who is choking."}},{"term":{"af":"Sleutelbeheer","en":"Key control"},"def":{"af":"'n Stelsel, soos 'n sleutelregister, wat bepaal wie watter sleutels het en wanneer, om diefstal te voorkom.","en":"A system, such as a key register, that controls who has which keys and when, to prevent theft."}},{"term":{"af":"Kontantopmaak","en":"Cash-up"},"def":{"af":"Die prosedure aan die einde van 'n skof waar die kontant getel en met die verwagte bedrag (vlot + kontantverkope) vergelyk word.","en":"The procedure at the end of a shift in which the cash is counted and compared with the expected amount (float + cash sales)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: identifiseer gevare in 'n kombuis","en":"Source question: identify hazards in a kitchen"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die beskrywing van 'n restaurantkombuis in Hartbeespoort op 'n besige Saterdagaand: 'n Pot sop kook op die stoof met die handvatsel wat oor die rand van die stoof uitsteek. Daar is 'n plas olie op die vloer langs die diepvetbraaier. 'n Kok sny uie met 'n stomp mes. 'n Kelner prop die koffiemasjien met nat hande in. Leë bokse is voor die nooduitgang gestapel. Identifiseer vier gevare en sê hoe elkeen voorkom kan word.","en":"Read the description of a restaurant kitchen in Hartbeespoort on a busy Saturday evening: A pot of soup is boiling on the stove with its handle sticking out over the edge of the stove. There is a pool of oil on the floor next to the deep-fryer. A cook is cutting onions with a blunt knife. A waiter plugs in the coffee machine with wet hands. Empty boxes are stacked in front of the fire exit. Identify four hazards and say how each can be prevented."},"steps":[{"af":"Pothandvatsel steek uit → iemand kan daaraan stamp en die warm sop oor hom gooi (skroeiwond). Voorkoming: draai pothandvatsels na binne.","en":"Pot handle sticking out → someone can bump it and spill the hot soup over himself (scald). Prevention: turn pot handles inwards."},{"af":"Olie op die vloer → gly en val, en naby die diepvetbraaier selfs brandwonde. Voorkoming: vee dit dadelik op, plaas 'n “nat vloer”-teken en dra glyvaste skoene.","en":"Oil on the floor → slips and falls, and next to the deep-fryer even burns. Prevention: wipe it up at once, put out a “wet floor” sign and wear non-slip shoes."},{"af":"Stomp mes → die mes gly maklik en veroorsaak snywonde. Voorkoming: hou messe skerp en gebruik die klougreep op 'n stewige snyplank.","en":"Blunt knife → the knife slips easily and causes cuts. Prevention: keep knives sharp and use the claw grip on a stable cutting board."},{"af":"Nat hande by 'n prop → elektriese skok. Voorkoming: droog jou hande af voordat jy aan proppe en toestelle raak.","en":"Wet hands at a plug → electric shock. Prevention: dry your hands before you touch plugs and appliances."},{"af":"Bokse voor die nooduitgang → mense kan nie in 'n brand ontsnap nie. Voorkoming: hou nooduitgange altyd vry van hindernisse.","en":"Boxes in front of the fire exit → people cannot escape in a fire. Prevention: always keep fire exits free of obstructions."}],"answer":{"af":"Enige vier: pothandvatsel (draai na binne), olie op vloer (vee op + teken), stomp mes (slyp + klougreep), nat hande (droog af), geblokkeerde nooduitgang (hou oop).","en":"Any four: pot handle (turn inwards), oil on floor (wipe up + sign), blunt knife (sharpen + claw grip), wet hands (dry them), blocked fire exit (keep clear)."}},{"title":{"af":"'n Panbrand","en":"A pan fire"},"problem":{"af":"'n Pan met olie vat vlam op die stoof, en 'n junior personeellid gryp 'n beker water. (a) Verduidelik waarom water gevaarlik is. (b) Beskryf die korrekte stappe. (c) Gebruik die vuurdriehoek om te verduidelik hoekom jou metode werk.","en":"A pan of oil catches fire on the stove, and a junior staff member grabs a jug of water. (a) Explain why water is dangerous. (b) Describe the correct steps. (c) Use the fire triangle to explain why your method works."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Water is swaarder as olie en sak na die bodem. Daar verander dit onmiddellik in stoom, wat die brandende olie uit die pan skiet – 'n vuurbal wat mense ernstig kan brand en die vuur kan versprei.","en":"(a) Water is heavier than oil and sinks to the bottom. There it instantly turns into steam, which throws the burning oil out of the pan – a fireball that can badly burn people and spread the fire."},{"af":"(b) Keer die personeellid. Skakel die stoof af as dit veilig is. Bedek die pan met 'n deksel of 'n brandkombers (of gebruik 'n nat chemiese blusser). Moenie die pan dra nie, en laat dit toe totdat dit afgekoel het.","en":"(b) Stop the staff member. Switch off the stove if it is safe. Cover the pan with a lid or a fire blanket (or use a wet chemical extinguisher). Do not carry the pan, and leave it covered until it has cooled down."},{"af":"As die vuur versprei: lui die alarm, ontruim na die versamelpunt en skakel die brandweer of 112.","en":"If the fire spreads: raise the alarm, evacuate to the assembly point and call the fire brigade or 112."},{"af":"(c) Die deksel of brandkombers sny die suurstof af, en om die stoof af te skakel neem die hitte weg. Sonder al drie sye van die vuurdriehoek kan die vuur nie brand nie.","en":"(c) The lid or fire blanket cuts off the oxygen, and switching off the stove removes the heat. Without all three sides of the fire triangle the fire cannot burn."}],"answer":{"af":"Nooit water nie; skakel hitte af, bedek met deksel/brandkombers (of nat chemiese blusser) – dit verwyder suurstof en hitte.","en":"Never water; switch off the heat, cover with a lid/fire blanket (or wet chemical extinguisher) – this removes oxygen and heat."}},{"title":{"af":"Noodhulp vir 'n skroeiwond","en":"First aid for a scald"},"problem":{"af":"'n Commis-sjef stamp 'n pot kookwater om en die water spat oor haar onderarm. Beskryf die noodhulpstappe in die regte volgorde.","en":"A commis chef knocks over a pot of boiling water and the water splashes over her forearm. Describe the first-aid steps in the correct order."},"steps":[{"af":"Maak die area veilig: skakel die stoof af en hou ander mense weg van die warm water op die vloer.","en":"Make the area safe: switch off the stove and keep other people away from the hot water on the floor."},{"af":"Koel die arm onder koel lopende water vir minstens 10 minute. Dit stop die brandproses in die vel en verminder pyn.","en":"Cool the arm under cool running water for at least 10 minutes. This stops the burning process in the skin and reduces pain."},{"af":"Verwyder ringe, horlosies of nou klere naby die wond voordat dit swel (maar nie iets wat aan die vel vassit nie).","en":"Remove rings, watches or tight clothing near the wound before it swells (but not anything stuck to the skin)."},{"af":"Moenie blase oopbreek nie en moenie botter, olie of ys gebruik nie. Bedek die wond los met kleefplastiek of 'n skoon brandwondverband.","en":"Do not burst blisters and do not use butter, oil or ice. Cover the wound loosely with cling wrap or a clean burn dressing."},{"af":"Kry mediese hulp as die wond groot of diep is, en rapporteer en teken die besering aan soos die Wet vereis.","en":"Get medical help if the wound is large or deep, and report and record the injury as the Act requires."}],"answer":{"af":"Maak veilig → koel minstens 10 min onder lopende water → verwyder ringe → bedek los (geen botter/ys, moenie blase oopbreek nie) → mediese hulp en rapporteer.","en":"Make safe → cool for at least 10 min under running water → remove rings → cover loosely (no butter/ice, do not burst blisters) → medical help and report."}},{"title":{"af":"Kontantopmaak aan die einde van 'n skof","en":"Cash-up at the end of a shift"},"problem":{"af":"Aan die begin van die skof het die kasregister in 'n koffiewinkel in Brits 'n vlot van R500. Die kasregister se lesing wys kontantverkope van R3 845,50. Aan die einde van die skof tel die kassier R4 325,50 in die laai. (a) Bereken die verwagte kontant. (b) Is daar 'n tekort of 'n surplus, en hoeveel? (c) Noem twee maniere om kontant veilig te hou.","en":"At the start of the shift the till in a coffee shop in Brits has a float of R500. The till reading shows cash sales of R3 845.50. At the end of the shift the cashier counts R4 325.50 in the drawer. (a) Calculate the expected cash. (b) Is there a shortage or a surplus, and how much? (c) Name two ways to keep cash safe."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Verwagte kontant = vlot + kontantverkope = R500 + R3 845,50 = R4 345,50","en":"(a) Expected cash = float + cash sales = R500 + R3 845.50 = R4 345.50"},{"af":"(b) Verskil = getelde kontant – verwagte kontant = R4 325,50 – R4 345,50 = –R20,00","en":"(b) Difference = cash counted – expected cash = R4 325.50 – R4 345.50 = –R20.00"},{"af":"Die getelde bedrag is kleiner as die verwagte bedrag, dus is daar 'n tekort van R20,00. Dit moet aangeteken en aan die bestuurder gerapporteer word.","en":"The amount counted is less than the expected amount, so there is a shortage of R20.00. It must be recorded and reported to the manager."},{"af":"(c) Enige twee: hou min kontant in die kasregister; sit ekstra kontant in 'n kluis; laat twee mense die kontant tel; bank die kontant gereeld.","en":"(c) Any two: keep little cash in the till; put extra cash in a safe; let two people count the cash; bank the cash regularly."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) R4 345,50; (b) tekort van R20,00; (c) bv. min kontant in die kasregister en 'n kluis.","en":"(a) R4 345.50; (b) shortage of R20.00; (c) e.g. little cash in the till and a safe."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter drie elemente vorm die vuurdriehoek?","en":"Which three elements make up the fire triangle?"},"options":[{"af":"Hitte, water en suurstof","en":"Heat, water and oxygen"},{"af":"Vlamme, rook en hitte","en":"Flames, smoke and heat"},{"af":"Hitte, brandstof en suurstof","en":"Heat, fuel and oxygen"},{"af":"Brandstof, koolstofdioksied en hitte","en":"Fuel, carbon dioxide and heat"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Vuur het hitte, brandstof en suurstof nodig. Water en CO₂ word juis gebruik om vure te blus.","en":"A fire needs heat, fuel and oxygen. Water and CO₂ are in fact used to put fires out."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Wet op Beroepsgesondheid en -veiligheid is Wet ___ van 1993.","en":"The Occupational Health and Safety Act is Act ___ of 1993."},"answers":{"af":["85"],"en":["85"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is Wet 85 van 1993. Dit beskerm werkers en ander mense by die werkplek.","en":"It is Act 85 of 1993. It protects workers and other people at the workplace."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["58","75","93"],"en":["58","75","93"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Pleisters in 'n kombuis se noodhulpkissie is blou sodat hulle maklik raakgesien word as hulle in kos val.","en":"Plasters in a kitchen first-aid kit are blue so that they are easy to see if they fall into food."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Blou kom byna nooit natuurlik in kos voor nie, so 'n blou pleister val dadelik op.","en":"True. Blue almost never occurs naturally in food, so a blue plaster stands out immediately."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter brandblusser is SLEGS geskik vir brande in hout, papier en materiaal?","en":"Which fire extinguisher is suitable ONLY for fires in wood, paper and fabric?"},"options":[{"af":"Water","en":"Water"},{"af":"CO₂","en":"CO₂"},{"af":"Droë chemiese poeier","en":"Dry chemical powder"},{"af":"Nat chemiese blusser","en":"Wet chemical extinguisher"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Water mag slegs op hout, papier en materiaal gebruik word. Op olie veroorsaak dit 'n vuurbal en by elektrisiteit 'n skok.","en":"Water may only be used on wood, paper and fabric. On oil it causes a fireball and near electricity a shock."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"By 'n neusbloeding leun die persoon vorentoe en knyp die sagte deel van die neus vir ongeveer ___ minute.","en":"With a nosebleed, the person leans forward and pinches the soft part of the nose for about ___ minutes."},"answers":{"af":["10","tien"],"en":["10","ten"]},"explain":{"af":"Knyp ongeveer 10 minute lank. Leun vorentoe, nie agtertoe nie, sodat die bloed nie in die keel afloop nie.","en":"Pinch for about 10 minutes. Lean forward, not backward, so that the blood does not run down the throat."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","3","60"],"en":["1","3","60"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke gevaar by die beste voorkomingsmaatreël.","en":"Match each hazard to the best prevention measure."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Brandwonde","en":"Burns"},"r":{"af":"Draai pothandvatsels na binne en gebruik droë oondhandskoene","en":"Turn pot handles inwards and use dry oven gloves"}},{"l":{"af":"Snywonde","en":"Cuts"},"r":{"af":"Hou messe skerp en gebruik die klougreep","en":"Keep knives sharp and use the claw grip"}},{"l":{"af":"Gly en val","en":"Slips and falls"},"r":{"af":"Vee storting dadelik op en plaas 'n “nat vloer”-teken","en":"Wipe up spills at once and put out a “wet floor” sign"}},{"l":{"af":"Elektriese skok","en":"Electric shock"},"r":{"af":"Werk met droë hande en kontroleer koorde","en":"Work with dry hands and check cords"}},{"l":{"af":"Spierverrekking","en":"Strains"},"r":{"af":"Lig met gebuigde knieë en 'n reguit rug","en":"Lift with bent knees and a straight back"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke gevaar het sy eie voorkoming: hitte → handvatsels en droë handskoene; messe → skerp en klougreep; storting → opvee en teken; elektrisiteit → droë hande; swaar vragte → reg lig.","en":"Each hazard has its own prevention: heat → handles and dry gloves; knives → sharp and claw grip; spills → wipe up and sign; electricity → dry hands; heavy loads → lift correctly."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter EEN van die volgende is 'n plig van die WERKNEMER volgens die Wet op Beroepsgesondheid en -veiligheid?","en":"Which ONE of the following is a duty of the EMPLOYEE according to the Occupational Health and Safety Act?"},"options":[{"af":"Voorsien 'n toegeruste noodhulpkissie","en":"Provide an equipped first-aid kit"},{"af":"Rapporteer onveilige toestande en ongelukke aan die werkgewer","en":"Report unsafe conditions and accidents to the employer"},{"af":"Voorsien en onderhou veilige toerusting","en":"Provide and maintain safe equipment"},{"af":"Lei alle personeel in veiligheid op","en":"Train all staff in safety"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die werknemer moet gevare en ongelukke rapporteer, reëls volg en beskermende klere dra. Die ander drie is pligte van die werkgewer.","en":"The employee must report hazards and accidents, follow rules and wear protective clothing. The other three are duties of the employer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Brandwond wat deur stoom of kookwater veroorsaak word, word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A burn caused by steam or boiling water is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["skroeiwond","skroeiwonde"],"en":["scald","scalds"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Skroeiwond word deur nat hitte (stoom of warm vloeistof) veroorsaak; 'n brandwond deur droë hitte soos 'n warm oondrak.","en":"A scald is caused by wet heat (steam or hot liquid); a burn by dry heat such as a hot oven rack."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skaafwond","snywond","kneusplek"],"en":["graze","cut","bruise"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy moet botter op 'n brandwond smeer om die hitte uit te trek.","en":"You should put butter on a burn to draw out the heat."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Botter hou die hitte in die vel vas en kan infeksie veroorsaak. Koel die wond minstens 10 minute onder koel lopende water.","en":"False. Butter traps the heat in the skin and can cause infection. Cool the wound under cool running water for at least 10 minutes."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die Heimlich-maneuver?","en":"What is the Heimlich manoeuvre?"},"options":[{"af":"Mond-tot-mond-asemhaling","en":"Mouth-to-mouth breathing"},{"af":"Om die persoon water te laat drink","en":"Getting the person to drink water"},{"af":"Om die persoon plat te laat lê en die bene te lig","en":"Letting the person lie flat and raising the legs"},{"af":"Buikstote om 'n voorwerp uit die lugweg van 'n persoon wat verstik, te dwing","en":"Abdominal thrusts to force an object out of the airway of a person who is choking"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die Heimlich-maneuver is buikstote by verstikking. Om plat te lê met die bene gelig is die behandeling vir floutes.","en":"The Heimlich manoeuvre is abdominal thrusts for choking. Lying flat with the legs raised is the treatment for fainting."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Kasregister begin die skof met 'n vlot van R400. Die kontantverkope is R2 650. Die verwagte kontant in die laai is R___.","en":"A till starts the shift with a float of R400. The cash sales are R2 650. The expected cash in the drawer is R___."},"answers":{"af":["3050","3 050","R3 050","R3050","3050,00","3 050,00"],"en":["3050","3 050","R3 050","R3050","3050.00","3 050.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Verwagte kontant = vlot + kontantverkope = R400 + R2 650 = R3 050. Moenie die vlot aftrek of vergeet nie.","en":"Expected cash = float + cash sales = R400 + R2 650 = R3 050. Do not subtract or forget the float."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["2 650","2 250","3 450"],"en":["2 650","2 250","3 450"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Pan met kookolie vat vlam. Wat moet jy gebruik om dit te blus?","en":"A pan of cooking oil catches fire. What should you use to put it out?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Waterblusser","en":"A water extinguisher"},{"af":"'n Brandkombers of 'n nat chemiese blusser","en":"A fire blanket or a wet chemical extinguisher"},{"af":"'n Handvol meel","en":"A handful of flour"},{"af":"Dra die brandende pan vinnig na buite","en":"Carry the burning pan outside quickly"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Brandkombers sny die suurstof af; 'n nat chemiese blusser is vir olie- en vetbrande gemaak. Water veroorsaak 'n vuurbal, meel kan ontplof, en as jy die pan dra, kan jy die olie mors en die vuur versprei.","en":"A fire blanket cuts off the oxygen; a wet chemical extinguisher is made for oil and fat fires. Water causes a fireball, flour can explode, and carrying the pan can spill the oil and spread the fire."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou kollega kry 'n elektriese skok en hou nog die koord van die ketel vas. Wat doen jy EERSTE?","en":"Your colleague gets an electric shock and is still holding the kettle's cord. What do you do FIRST?"},"options":[{"af":"Skakel die krag by die muurprop of hoofskakelaar af","en":"Switch off the power at the wall plug or main switch"},{"af":"Trek hom met jou kaal hande weg","en":"Pull him away with your bare hands"},{"af":"Gooi water oor hom om hom af te koel","en":"Throw water over him to cool him down"},{"af":"Begin dadelik met mond-tot-mond-asemhaling","en":"Start mouth-to-mouth breathing immediately"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Skakel eers die krag af. As jy aan hom raak terwyl die stroom nog vloei, kry jy ook 'n skok, en water gelei elektrisiteit.","en":"Switch off the power first. If you touch him while the current is still flowing, you will also get a shock, and water conducts electricity."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"By die ontvangstoonbank van 'n besige hotel sê die ontvangsdame hardop: “Mnr. Dlamini, u kamer is nommer 214.” Waarom is dit 'n sekuriteitsrisiko?","en":"At the reception desk of a busy hotel the receptionist says aloud: “Mr Dlamini, your room is number 214.” Why is this a security risk?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit vertraag die inboekproses","en":"It slows down the check-in process"},{"af":"Dit is onbeleefd om die gas se van te gebruik","en":"It is rude to use the guest's surname"},{"af":"Die gas kan sy kamernommer vergeet","en":"The guest may forget his room number"},{"af":"Ander mense hoor die kamernommer en weet waar die gas en sy besittings is","en":"Other people hear the room number and know where the guest and his belongings are"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Kamernommers word nooit hardop gesê nie. 'n Dief of iemand met slegte bedoelings kan die gas of sy kamer teiken. Skryf die nommer eerder op die sleutelkaarthouer.","en":"Room numbers are never said aloud. A thief or someone with bad intentions can target the guest or his room. Rather write the number on the key-card holder."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir 'n brand in 'n elektriese toestel is 'n ___-blusser die beste keuse, omdat dit nie elektrisiteit gelei nie en geen residu laat nie.","en":"For a fire in an electrical appliance, a ___ extinguisher is the best choice, because it does not conduct electricity and leaves no residue."},"answers":{"af":["CO2","CO₂","koolstofdioksied","koolsuurgas","koolstofdioksiedblusser"],"en":["CO2","CO₂","carbon dioxide"]},"explain":{"af":"CO₂ verdryf die suurstof, gelei nie elektrisiteit nie en laat geen poeier op die toestel agter nie. Water en skuim gelei elektrisiteit.","en":"CO₂ displaces the oxygen, does not conduct electricity and leaves no powder on the appliance. Water and foam conduct electricity."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["water","skuim","nat chemiese"],"en":["water","foam","wet chemical"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Kelner brand haar hand aan 'n warm bord wat uit die oond kom. Watter reaksie is die BESTE?","en":"A waiter burns her hand on a hot plate that has come out of the oven. Which response is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"Druk ys op die brandwond en maak die blase oop","en":"Press ice on the burn and open the blisters"},{"af":"Smeer botter daaraan en draai dit styf toe","en":"Apply butter and wrap it tightly"},{"af":"Koel dit minstens 10 minute onder koel lopende water, verwyder ringe en bedek dit los met kleefplastiek","en":"Cool it under cool running water for at least 10 minutes, remove rings and cover it loosely with cling wrap"},{"af":"Hou dit 'n halwe minuut onder water en gaan dadelik voort met werk","en":"Hold it under water for half a minute and carry on working immediately"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Lank genoeg afkoel (minstens 10 minute) stop die skade, ringe moet af voordat die hand swel, en kleefplastiek hou die wond skoon. Ys, botter, oop blase en te kort afkoel maak dit erger.","en":"Cooling long enough (at least 10 minutes) stops the damage, rings must come off before the hand swells, and cling wrap keeps the wound clean. Ice, butter, open blisters and too little cooling make it worse."}}]},{"id":"gas10-t4-akkommodasie-departemente","title":{"af":"Akkommodasie-ondernemings, departemente en kliënteverhoudinge","en":"Accommodation establishments, departments and customer relations"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal tipes akkommodasie en hoteldepartemente met hul funksies kan beskryf, kan verduidelik hoe departemente saamwerk, en gaste met kulturele en spesiale behoeftes en klagtes professioneel kan hanteer.","en":"You will be able to describe types of accommodation and hotel departments with their functions, explain how departments work together, and professionally handle guests with cultural and special needs and complaints."},"summary":{"af":"## Tipes akkommodasie in Suid-Afrika\n\n| Tipe | Kenmerke, fasiliteite en dienste |\n|---|---|\n| Hotel | Volle diens: ontvangs dag en nag, restaurant, kroeg, kamerdiens, konferensielokale |\n| Oord | Akkommodasie plus baie ontspanningsfasiliteite, bv. swembaddens, gholf, 'n spa en aktiwiteite (bv. Sun City) |\n| Lodge | In 'n natuur- of wildgebied; maaltye en wildritte is dikwels ingesluit |\n| Gastehuis | Kleiner, met persoonlike diens; gewoonlik word ontbyt bedien |\n| Bed-en-ontbyt (B&B) | In 'n privaat huis waar die eienaar woon; bed en ontbyt |\n| Plattelandse herberg (country house) | Gastehuis op die platteland, dikwels met fyn etes |\n| Selfsorg-eenhede | Chalets, woonstelle of huisies met 'n toegeruste kombuis; gaste maak self kos |\n| Rugsakreisiger-akkommodasie (backpackers/hostels) | Goedkoop; slaapsale en gedeelde badkamers en kombuis |\n| Karavaan- en kampeerparke | Staanplekke, ablusieblokke en kragpunte |\n\nDie **TGCSA** (Tourism Grading Council of South Africa) ken **1–5 sterre** toe. Gradering is **vrywillig** en word **jaarliks** geassesseer.\n\n## Departemente in 'n hotel\n\n| Departement | Funksies (en personeel) |\n|---|---|\n| **Voorkantoor** | Besprekings, ontvangs (inboek en uitboek), gasterekeninge, conciërge (inligting, toere, taxi's, restaurantbesprekings), portiers (bagasie), skakelbord |\n| **Huishouding** | Kamers en openbare areas skoonmaak, linne en wassery, minikroeë aanvul, verlore eiendom (kamerbediendes, uitvoerende huishoudster) |\n| **Voedsel en drank** | Restaurante, kroeg, kamerdiens, bankette en konferensies (kelners, kroegman) |\n| **Kombuis** | Voedselproduksie deur die kombuisbrigade |\n| **Instandhouding (ingenieurswese)** | Herstel en onderhoud van geboue en toerusting, bv. lugversorgers, ligte, swembad |\n| **Menslike hulpbronne** | Werwing, aanstelling, opleiding en personeelsake |\n| **Finansies (rekeninge)** | Betalings, lone, begrotings, nagaan van gasterekeninge |\n| **Verkope en bemarking** | Advertensies, sosiale media, groep- en konferensieverkope |\n| **Sekuriteit** | Beskerm gaste, personeel en eiendom; toegangsbeheer, kameras en noodprosedures |\n\n### Die kombuisbrigade\n\n1. **Uitvoerende sjef** – hoof van die kombuis: spyskaarte, bestellings, koste en personeel.\n2. **Sous-sjef** – tweede in bevel; bestuur die kombuis daagliks en neem oor as die uitvoerende sjef afwesig is.\n3. **Chef de partie** – in beheer van een afdeling (seksie), bv. souse, groente of gebak.\n4. **Commis-sjef** – junior kok wat in 'n afdeling help en leer.\n\n### Hoe departemente saamwerk\n\n- **Huishouding** gee die **kamerstatus** (vuil, skoon, geïnspekteer of buite werking) aan die **voorkantoor**, sodat ontvangs weet watter kamers aan nuwe gaste gegee kan word.\n- Die voorkantoor laat huishouding weet van uitboekings en spesiale gaste (VIP's).\n- Huishouding meld foute (bv. 'n lekkende kraan) by **instandhouding** aan.\n- **Voedsel en drank** en die **kombuis** beplan saam vir bankette, en koste van kamerdiens word op die gas se rekening by die voorkantoor en **finansies** gesit.\n\n## Kliënteverhoudinge\n\n**Professionele gedrag en voorkoms:** 'n skoon uniform en naamplaatjie, netjiese hare, stiptelik, vriendelik en hulpvaardig.\n\n**Begroeting en kommunikasie:** groet die gas dadelik, glimlag, gebruik die gas se naam, luister aandagtig en praat duidelik en beleefd.\n\n### Kulturele sensitiwiteit\n\n| Groep | Wat om in gedagte te hou |\n|---|---|\n| Moslems (halaal) | Geen varkvleis of alkohol nie; vleis moet halaal wees |\n| Jode (kosher) | Geen varkvleis of skulpvis/skaaldiere nie; vleis en suiwel word apart gehou |\n| Baie Hindoes | Eet nie beesvleis nie; baie is vegetariërs |\n| Vegetariërs | Geen vleis, hoender of vis nie |\n| Veganiste | Geen diereprodukte nie – ook nie eiers, suiwel of heuning nie |\n\nGroete en lyftaal verskil tussen kulture (bv. oogkontak en handdruk), dus wees bedagsaam en respekvol.\n\n### Gaste met spesiale behoeftes\n\n- **Gestremdhede:** rolstoeltoeganklike kamers op die grondvloer of naby die hysbak, opritte, griprelings, wyer deure en 'n inloopstort.\n- **Bejaardes:** kamers naby die hysbak, hulp met bagasie en duidelike inligting.\n- **Kinders:** kinderstoele, 'n kinderspyskaart, babawiegies en veilige aktiwiteite.\n\n### Klagtes hanteer\n\n1. **Luister** aandagtig sonder om te onderbreek.\n2. **Vra om verskoning** en wys dat jy verstaan.\n3. **Los die probleem op** (of kry die regte persoon om dit te doen).\n4. **Bedank** die gas dat hy dit onder jou aandag gebring het.\n5. **Volg op** om seker te maak die gas is tevrede.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Moenie stry, 'n ander departement blameer of iets belowe wat jy nie kan nakom nie. 'n Klagte wat goed hanteer word, kan van 'n kwaai gas 'n lojale gas maak.","en":"## Types of accommodation in South Africa\n\n| Type | Features, facilities and services |\n|---|---|\n| Hotel | Full service: reception day and night, restaurant, bar, room service, conference venues |\n| Resort | Accommodation plus many leisure facilities, e.g. swimming pools, golf, a spa and activities (e.g. Sun City) |\n| Lodge | In a nature or game area; meals and game drives are often included |\n| Guest house | Smaller, with personal service; breakfast is usually served |\n| Bed and breakfast (B&B) | In a private home where the owner lives; bed and breakfast |\n| Country house | Guest house in the countryside, often with fine dining |\n| Self-catering units | Chalets, apartments or cottages with an equipped kitchen; guests cook for themselves |\n| Backpackers/hostels | Cheap; dormitories and shared bathrooms and kitchen |\n| Caravan and camping parks | Stands/sites, ablution blocks and power points |\n\nThe **TGCSA** (Tourism Grading Council of South Africa) awards **1–5 stars**. Grading is **voluntary** and is **assessed annually**.\n\n## Departments in a hotel\n\n| Department | Functions (and staff) |\n|---|---|\n| **Front office** | Reservations, reception (check-in and check-out), guest accounts, concierge (information, tours, taxis, restaurant bookings), porters (luggage), switchboard |\n| **Housekeeping** | Cleaning rooms and public areas, linen and laundry, restocking minibars, lost property (room attendants, executive housekeeper) |\n| **Food and beverage** | Restaurants, bar, room service, banqueting and conferences (waiters, barman) |\n| **Kitchen** | Food production by the kitchen brigade |\n| **Maintenance (engineering)** | Repair and upkeep of buildings and equipment, e.g. air conditioners, lights, pool |\n| **Human resources** | Recruitment, appointment, training and staff matters |\n| **Finance (accounts)** | Payments, wages, budgets, checking guest accounts |\n| **Sales and marketing** | Advertising, social media, group and conference sales |\n| **Security** | Protects guests, staff and property; access control, cameras and emergency procedures |\n\n### The kitchen brigade\n\n1. **Executive chef** – head of the kitchen: menus, ordering, costs and staff.\n2. **Sous chef** – second in command; runs the kitchen day to day and takes over when the executive chef is absent.\n3. **Chef de partie** – in charge of one section, e.g. sauces, vegetables or pastry.\n4. **Commis chef** – junior cook who helps and learns in a section.\n\n### How departments work together\n\n- **Housekeeping** reports the **room status** (dirty, clean, inspected or out of order) to the **front office**, so reception knows which rooms can be given to new guests.\n- The front office tells housekeeping about check-outs and special guests (VIPs).\n- Housekeeping reports faults (e.g. a leaking tap) to **maintenance**.\n- **Food and beverage** and the **kitchen** plan banquets together, and room-service charges go onto the guest's account at the front office and **finance**.\n\n## Customer relations\n\n**Professional behaviour and appearance:** a clean uniform and name badge, neat hair, punctual, friendly and helpful.\n\n**Greeting and communication:** greet the guest immediately, smile, use the guest's name, listen attentively and speak clearly and politely.\n\n### Cultural sensitivity\n\n| Group | What to keep in mind |\n|---|---|\n| Muslims (halaal) | No pork or alcohol; meat must be halaal |\n| Jews (kosher) | No pork or shellfish; meat and dairy are kept separate |\n| Many Hindus | Do not eat beef; many are vegetarian |\n| Vegetarians | No meat, chicken or fish |\n| Vegans | No animal products – also no eggs, dairy or honey |\n\nGreetings and body language differ between cultures (e.g. eye contact and handshakes), so be considerate and respectful.\n\n### Guests with special needs\n\n- **Disabilities:** wheelchair-accessible rooms on the ground floor or near the lift, ramps, grab rails, wider doors and a walk-in shower.\n- **The elderly:** rooms near the lift, help with luggage and clear information.\n- **Children:** high chairs, a children's menu, cots and safe activities.\n\n### Handling complaints\n\n1. **Listen** attentively without interrupting.\n2. **Apologise** and show that you understand.\n3. **Solve the problem** (or get the right person to do it).\n4. **Thank** the guest for bringing it to your attention.\n5. **Follow up** to make sure the guest is satisfied.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Don't argue, blame another department or promise something you cannot deliver. A complaint that is handled well can turn an angry guest into a loyal guest."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Voorkantoor","en":"Front office"},"def":{"af":"Die departement wat besprekings, ontvangs, inboek en uitboek, gasterekeninge en die conciërge hanteer; die gas se eerste kontakpunt.","en":"The department that handles reservations, reception, check-in and check-out, guest accounts and the concierge; the guest's first point of contact."}},{"term":{"af":"Huishouding","en":"Housekeeping"},"def":{"af":"Die departement wat kamers en openbare areas skoonmaak en vir linne, wassery, minikroeë en verlore eiendom sorg.","en":"The department that cleans rooms and public areas and looks after linen, laundry, minibars and lost property."}},{"term":{"af":"Kamerstatus","en":"Room status"},"def":{"af":"Die toestand van 'n kamer (vuil, skoon, geïnspekteer of buite werking) wat huishouding aan die voorkantoor rapporteer.","en":"The condition of a room (dirty, clean, inspected or out of order) that housekeeping reports to the front office."}},{"term":{"af":"Conciërge","en":"Concierge"},"def":{"af":"Die personeellid by die voorkantoor wat gaste met inligting, toere, vervoer en restaurantbesprekings help.","en":"The staff member at the front office who helps guests with information, tours, transport and restaurant bookings."}},{"term":{"af":"Kombuisbrigade","en":"Kitchen brigade"},"def":{"af":"Die rangorde van kombuispersoneel: uitvoerende sjef, sous-sjef, chef de partie en commis-sjef.","en":"The ranking of kitchen staff: executive chef, sous chef, chef de partie and commis chef."}},{"term":{"af":"Sous-sjef","en":"Sous chef"},"def":{"af":"Die tweede in bevel in die kombuis wat die kombuis daagliks bestuur en oorneem as die uitvoerende sjef afwesig is.","en":"The second in command in the kitchen who runs the kitchen day to day and takes over when the executive chef is absent."}},{"term":{"af":"Chef de partie","en":"Chef de partie"},"def":{"af":"Die kok in beheer van een afdeling van die kombuis, bv. souse, groente of gebak.","en":"The cook in charge of one section of the kitchen, e.g. sauces, vegetables or pastry."}},{"term":{"af":"Halaal","en":"Halaal"},"def":{"af":"Kos wat volgens Moslem-voorskrifte toelaatbaar is: geen varkvleis of alkohol nie, en vleis moet halaal geslag wees.","en":"Food that is permitted according to Muslim rules: no pork or alcohol, and meat must be slaughtered halaal."}},{"term":{"af":"Kosher","en":"Kosher"},"def":{"af":"Kos wat volgens Joodse voorskrifte toelaatbaar is: geen varkvleis of skulpvis nie, en vleis en suiwel word apart gehou.","en":"Food that is permitted according to Jewish rules: no pork or shellfish, and meat and dairy are kept separate."}},{"term":{"af":"Kliënteverhoudinge","en":"Customer relations"},"def":{"af":"Die manier waarop personeel met gaste omgaan – voorkoms, kommunikasie, kulturele sensitiwiteit en die hantering van klagtes.","en":"The way staff interact with guests – appearance, communication, cultural sensitivity and handling complaints."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kies akkommodasie vir 'n gasprofiel","en":"Choose accommodation for a guest profile"},"problem":{"af":"Beveel 'n tipe akkommodasie aan vir elke gas en gee 'n rede:\n\n(a) 'n Gesin van vyf op 'n klein begroting wat 'n week by Hartbeespoortdam wil bly en self wil kook.\n(b) 'n Sakevrou wat 'n driedaagse konferensie in Pretoria bywoon.\n(c) Twee jong rugsakreisigers uit Duitsland wat so goedkoop moontlik wil reis en ander reisigers wil ontmoet.","en":"Recommend a type of accommodation for each guest and give a reason:\n\n(a) A family of five on a small budget who want to stay at Hartbeespoort Dam for a week and cook for themselves.\n(b) A businesswoman attending a three-day conference in Pretoria.\n(c) Two young backpackers from Germany who want to travel as cheaply as possible and meet other travellers."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Selfsorg-eenheid** (bv. 'n chalet): daar is 'n toegeruste kombuis, so die gesin spaar geld op restaurante, en daar is plek vir vyf mense.","en":"(a) **Self-catering unit** (e.g. a chalet): there is an equipped kitchen, so the family saves money on restaurants, and there is room for five people."},{"af":"(b) **Hotel** met konferensiefasiliteite: sy kry volle diens (restaurant, kamerdiens, Wi-Fi) en die konferensie kan selfs in die hotel plaasvind.","en":"(b) **Hotel** with conference facilities: she gets full service (restaurant, room service, Wi-Fi) and the conference may even take place in the hotel."},{"af":"(c) **Rugsakreisiger-akkommodasie (backpackers)**: dit is die goedkoopste, en gedeelde slaapsale en kombuise maak dit maklik om ander reisigers te ontmoet.","en":"(c) **Backpackers/hostel**: it is the cheapest, and shared dormitories and kitchens make it easy to meet other travellers."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Selfsorg-eenheid  (b) Hotel met konferensiefasiliteite  (c) Backpackers","en":"(a) Self-catering unit  (b) Hotel with conference facilities  (c) Backpackers"}},{"title":{"af":"Departemente werk saam","en":"Departments work together"},"problem":{"af":"Mnr. Dlamini boek om 10:00 uit kamer 214 uit. Om 14:00 kom 'n nuwe gas aan wat dieselfde kamer bespreek het. Huishouding sien dat die lugversorger in die kamer nie werk nie. Verduidelik hoe die voorkantoor, huishouding, instandhouding en finansies saamwerk.","en":"Mr Dlamini checks out of room 214 at 10:00. At 14:00 a new guest arrives who has booked the same room. Housekeeping notices that the air conditioner in the room is not working. Explain how the front office, housekeeping, maintenance and finance work together."},"steps":[{"af":"**Voorkantoor:** boek mnr. Dlamini uit, lê sy rekening voor (kamer, maaltye, minikroeg) en laat huishouding weet dat kamer 214 nou vuil is.","en":"**Front office:** checks Mr Dlamini out, presents his account (room, meals, minibar) and tells housekeeping that room 214 is now dirty."},{"af":"**Finansies:** ontvang en kontroleer die betaling en maak seker al die koste (bv. van die restaurant) is op die rekening.","en":"**Finance:** receives and checks the payment and makes sure all charges (e.g. from the restaurant) are on the account."},{"af":"**Huishouding:** maak die kamer skoon, vul die minikroeg aan, meld die stukkende lugversorger by instandhouding aan en stel die kamerstatus intussen op \"buite werking\".","en":"**Housekeeping:** cleans the room, restocks the minibar, reports the broken air conditioner to maintenance and meanwhile sets the room status to \"out of order\"."},{"af":"**Instandhouding:** herstel die lugversorger en laat huishouding weet. Huishouding inspekteer die kamer en rapporteer dit as \"skoon en geïnspekteer\".","en":"**Maintenance:** repairs the air conditioner and informs housekeeping. Housekeeping inspects the room and reports it as \"clean and inspected\"."},{"af":"**Voorkantoor:** sien die nuwe status en boek die nuwe gas om 14:00 in kamer 214 in. As die herstelwerk nie betyds klaar is nie, gee ontvangs 'n ander kamer.","en":"**Front office:** sees the new status and checks the new guest into room 214 at 14:00. If the repair is not finished in time, reception gives another room."}],"answer":{"af":"Voorkantoor (uitboek, rekening) → finansies (betaling) → huishouding (skoonmaak, kamerstatus, meld fout aan) → instandhouding (herstel) → voorkantoor (inboek).","en":"Front office (check-out, account) → finance (payment) → housekeeping (cleaning, room status, reports fault) → maintenance (repair) → front office (check-in)."}},{"title":{"af":"Hanteer 'n klagte","en":"Handle a complaint"},"problem":{"af":"'n Gas kom kwaad by ontvangs aan: \"My kamer is nie vandag skoongemaak nie, en ek het 45 minute vir kamerdiens gewag!\" Gebruik die vyf stappe om die klagte te hanteer.","en":"A guest arrives angrily at reception: \"My room was not cleaned today, and I waited 45 minutes for room service!\" Use the five steps to handle the complaint."},"steps":[{"af":"**Luister:** laat die gas klaar praat sonder om te onderbreek, hou oogkontak en knik.","en":"**Listen:** let the guest finish speaking without interrupting, keep eye contact and nod."},{"af":"**Vra om verskoning:** \"Ek is baie jammer, meneer. Ek verstaan dit is frustrerend ná 'n lang dag.\"","en":"**Apologise:** \"I am very sorry, sir. I understand that it is frustrating after a long day.\""},{"af":"**Los op:** bel huishouding om die kamer dadelik skoon te maak, vra voedsel en drank wat met die bestelling gebeur het, en bied 'n gratis drankie in die kroeg aan terwyl hy wag.","en":"**Solve:** phone housekeeping to clean the room immediately, ask food and beverage what happened to the order, and offer a free drink in the bar while he waits."},{"af":"**Bedank:** \"Dankie dat u ons laat weet het – so kan ons ons diens verbeter.\"","en":"**Thank:** \"Thank you for letting us know – that is how we can improve our service.\""},{"af":"**Volg op:** bel die gas 'n uur later om seker te maak die kamer is reg en hy is tevrede, en skryf die voorval in die logboek.","en":"**Follow up:** phone the guest an hour later to make sure the room is in order and he is satisfied, and write the incident in the log book."}],"answer":{"af":"Luister → vra om verskoning → los op → bedank → volg op.","en":"Listen → apologise → solve → thank → follow up."}},{"title":{"af":"'n Kultureel sensitiewe spyskaart","en":"A culturally sensitive menu"},"problem":{"af":"'n Konferensie-middagete in 'n hotel in Brits word bygewoon deur Moslem-, Joodse en Hindoe-gaste en 'n veganis. Die voorgestelde geregte is: (A) varkribbetjies, (B) beesvleisbredie, (C) hoender in roomsous, (D) groentekerrie met rys (met olie gemaak, sonder room of botter) en (E) vars vrugteslaai. Watter geregte kan aan al die gaste bedien word? Verduidelik.","en":"A conference lunch at a hotel in Brits is attended by Muslim, Jewish and Hindu guests and a vegan. The suggested dishes are: (A) pork ribs, (B) beef stew, (C) chicken in cream sauce, (D) vegetable curry with rice (made with oil, without cream or butter) and (E) fresh fruit salad. Which dishes can be served to all the guests? Explain."},"steps":[{"af":"(A) Varkribbetjies: nie halaal of kosher nie, en nie vegan nie – uitgesluit.","en":"(A) Pork ribs: not halaal or kosher, and not vegan – excluded."},{"af":"(B) Beesvleisbredie: baie Hindoes eet nie beesvleis nie, en dit is nie vegan nie – uitgesluit.","en":"(B) Beef stew: many Hindus do not eat beef, and it is not vegan – excluded."},{"af":"(C) Hoender in roomsous: vleis en suiwel saam is nie kosher nie, en dit is nie vegan nie – uitgesluit.","en":"(C) Chicken in cream sauce: meat and dairy together is not kosher, and it is not vegan – excluded."},{"af":"(D) en (E): bevat geen vleis, alkohol of diereprodukte nie, dus pas dit by al die groepe.","en":"(D) and (E): contain no meat, alcohol or animal products, so they suit all the groups."},{"af":"Wenk: vra altyd vooraf na spesiale dieetbehoeftes en merk geregte duidelik. Streng kosher of halaal gaste verkies dikwels kos van 'n gesertifiseerde verskaffer.","en":"Tip: always ask about special dietary needs beforehand and label dishes clearly. Strictly kosher or halaal guests often prefer food from a certified supplier."}],"answer":{"af":"Gereg D (groentekerrie) en gereg E (vrugteslaai).","en":"Dish D (vegetable curry) and dish E (fruit salad)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter departement hanteer besprekings, inboek en uitboek?","en":"Which department handles reservations, check-in and check-out?"},"options":[{"af":"Huishouding","en":"Housekeeping"},{"af":"Voorkantoor","en":"Front office"},{"af":"Voedsel en drank","en":"Food and beverage"},{"af":"Finansies","en":"Finance"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die voorkantoor (ontvangs) is die gas se eerste kontakpunt: besprekings, inboek, uitboek en gasterekeninge.","en":"The front office (reception) is the guest's first point of contact: reservations, check-in, check-out and guest accounts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoof van die kombuisbrigade, wat die spyskaarte beplan en die kombuis bestuur, is die ___.","en":"The head of the kitchen brigade, who plans the menus and manages the kitchen, is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["uitvoerende sjef","uitvoerende kok","hoofsjef"],"en":["executive chef","head chef"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sous-sjef","commis-sjef","chef de partie"],"en":["sous chef","commis chef","chef de partie"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die uitvoerende sjef staan bo-aan. Die sous-sjef is tweede in bevel, die chef de partie beheer een afdeling en die commis-sjef is 'n junior kok.","en":"The executive chef is at the top. The sous chef is second in command, the chef de partie runs one section and the commis chef is a junior cook."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"TGCSA-sterregradering is verpligtend vir alle akkommodasie in Suid-Afrika.","en":"TGCSA star grading is compulsory for all accommodation in South Africa."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Gradering is vrywillig. Ondernemings doen aansoek omdat sterre gaste vertroue gee en help met bemarking. Die gradering word jaarliks geassesseer.","en":"False. Grading is voluntary. Businesses apply because stars give guests confidence and help with marketing. The grading is assessed annually."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter tipe akkommodasie is in 'n privaat huis waar die eienaar self woon en bied net 'n bed en ontbyt?","en":"Which type of accommodation is in a private home where the owner lives and offers only a bed and breakfast?"},"options":[{"af":"Oord","en":"Resort"},{"af":"Hotel","en":"Hotel"},{"af":"Bed-en-ontbyt (B&B)","en":"Bed and breakfast (B&B)"},{"af":"Rugsakreisiger-akkommodasie","en":"Backpackers"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n B&B is in die eienaar se eie huis, met bed en ontbyt. 'n Oord en 'n hotel bied volle diens, en backpackers het goedkoop slaapsale.","en":"A B&B is in the owner's own home, with bed and breakfast. A resort and a hotel offer full service, and backpackers have cheap dormitories."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kosher-kos: vleis en ___ word apart gehou en nie saam gekook of bedien nie.","en":"Kosher food: meat and ___ are kept separate and are not cooked or served together."},"answers":{"af":["suiwel","suiwelprodukte","melk","melkprodukte"],"en":["dairy","dairy products","milk","milk products"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["groente","brood","vrugte"],"en":["vegetables","bread","fruit"]}},"explain":{"af":"Volgens Joodse voedselreëls word vleis en suiwel apart gehou. Daarom is hoender in roomsous nie kosher nie.","en":"According to Jewish food rules, meat and dairy are kept separate. That is why chicken in cream sauce is not kosher."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wie in die kombuisbrigade is in beheer van een afdeling, soos souse of gebak?","en":"Who in the kitchen brigade is in charge of one section, such as sauces or pastry?"},"options":[{"af":"Chef de partie","en":"Chef de partie"},{"af":"Commis-sjef","en":"Commis chef"},{"af":"Uitvoerende sjef","en":"Executive chef"},{"af":"Sous-sjef","en":"Sous chef"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die chef de partie (afdelingsjef) lei een seksie. Die commis-sjef help hom, en die sous-sjef bestuur die hele kombuis daagliks.","en":"The chef de partie (section chef) leads one section. The commis chef helps him, and the sous chef runs the whole kitchen day to day."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Huishouding rapporteer die kamer___ (vuil, skoon, geïnspekteer of buite werking) aan die voorkantoor.","en":"Housekeeping reports the room ___ (dirty, clean, inspected or out of order) to the front office."},"answers":{"af":["status","kamerstatus"],"en":["status","room status"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sleutel","prys","nommer"],"en":["key","rate","number"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die kamerstatus vertel ontvangs watter kamers gereed is vir nuwe gaste. Dit is 'n kernvoorbeeld van hoe departemente saamwerk.","en":"The room status tells reception which rooms are ready for new guests. It is a key example of how departments work together."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ___ by die voorkantoor help gaste met inligting en bespreek toere, taxi's en restaurante vir hulle.","en":"The ___ at the front office helps guests with information and books tours, taxis and restaurants for them."},"answers":{"af":["conciërge","concierge"],"en":["concierge"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["portier","kassier","skakelbordoperateur"],"en":["porter","cashier","switchboard operator"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die conciërge is die gas se \"hulp vir alles\". Die portier dra bagasie en die skakelbordoperateur hanteer oproepe.","en":"The concierge is the guest's \"help with everything\". The porter carries luggage and the switchboard operator handles calls."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Baie Hindoes eet nie beesvleis nie.","en":"Many Hindus do not eat beef."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die koei is vir baie Hindoes heilig, en baie Hindoes is ook vegetariërs. Bied dus 'n alternatief vir beesvleis aan.","en":"True. The cow is sacred to many Hindus, and many Hindus are also vegetarian. So offer an alternative to beef."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke departement by sy funksie.","en":"Match each department to its function."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Huishouding","en":"Housekeeping"},"r":{"af":"Maak kamers skoon en sorg vir linne en verlore eiendom","en":"Cleans rooms and looks after linen and lost property"}},{"l":{"af":"Instandhouding","en":"Maintenance"},"r":{"af":"Herstel toerusting en geboue, bv. lugversorgers","en":"Repairs equipment and buildings, e.g. air conditioners"}},{"l":{"af":"Menslike hulpbronne","en":"Human resources"},"r":{"af":"Werf, stel aan en lei personeel op","en":"Recruits, appoints and trains staff"}},{"l":{"af":"Verkope en bemarking","en":"Sales and marketing"},"r":{"af":"Adverteer die hotel en verkoop konferensie- en groeppakkette","en":"Advertises the hotel and sells conference and group packages"}},{"l":{"af":"Sekuriteit","en":"Security"},"r":{"af":"Beskerm gaste, personeel en eiendom","en":"Protects guests, staff and property"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke departement het sy eie taak, maar hulle werk saam om die gas 'n goeie ervaring te gee.","en":"Each department has its own task, but they work together to give the guest a good experience."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Afgetrede egpaar wil 'n rustige naweek in die natuur naby Pilanesberg hê, met al hul maaltye en wildritte ingesluit. Watter akkommodasie pas die beste?","en":"A retired couple want a peaceful weekend in nature near Pilanesberg, with all their meals and game drives included. Which accommodation fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Rugsakreisiger-hostel in die dorp","en":"A backpackers' hostel in town"},{"af":"'n Karavaanpark","en":"A caravan park"},{"af":"'n Stadshotel naby die lughawe","en":"A city hotel near the airport"},{"af":"'n Wildlodge","en":"A game lodge"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Lodge is in 'n natuur- of wildgebied en sluit dikwels maaltye en wildritte in. 'n Karavaanpark en backpackers is selfdoen en goedkoop, en 'n stadshotel is nie in die natuur nie.","en":"A lodge is in a nature or game area and often includes meals and game drives. A caravan park and backpackers are do-it-yourself and cheap, and a city hotel is not in nature."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Stap 1 van klagtehantering: ___ aandagtig na die gas sonder om hom te onderbreek.","en":"Step 1 of handling a complaint: ___ attentively to the guest without interrupting him."},"answers":{"af":["luister"],"en":["listen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["praat","verduidelik","argumenteer"],"en":["talk","explain","argue"]}},"explain":{"af":"Eers luister, dan om verskoning vra, oplos, bedank en opvolg. As jy dadelik begin verduidelik, voel die gas dat jy hom nie hoor nie.","en":"First listen, then apologise, solve, thank and follow up. If you start explaining immediately, the guest feels that you are not hearing him."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gereg is geskik vir 'n Moslem-gas wat halaal eet?","en":"Which dish is suitable for a Muslim guest who eats halaal?"},"options":[{"af":"Halaal-hoenderkerrie met rys","en":"Halaal chicken curry with rice"},{"af":"Varkkotelette met appelsous","en":"Pork chops with apple sauce"},{"af":"Hoender in 'n witwynsous","en":"Chicken in a white-wine sauce"},{"af":"'n Spek-en-kaasburger","en":"A bacon-and-cheese burger"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Halaal beteken geen varkvleis (dus ook geen spek nie) en geen alkohol nie. Die wyn in die sous maak die hoendergereg ongeskik.","en":"Halaal means no pork (so also no bacon) and no alcohol. The wine in the sauce makes the chicken dish unsuitable."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gas kom om 14:00 aan, maar ontvangs kan hom nog nie 'n kamer gee nie, alhoewel verskeie gaste reeds uitgeboek het. Wat is die waarskynlikste rede?","en":"A guest arrives at 14:00, but reception cannot give him a room yet, although several guests have already checked out. What is the most likely reason?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kombuis het nog nie die middagete klaargemaak nie","en":"The kitchen has not finished lunch yet"},{"af":"Bemarking het die kamers nog nie geadverteer nie","en":"Marketing has not advertised the rooms yet"},{"af":"Huishouding het die kamers nog nie as skoon en geïnspekteer aan die voorkantoor gerapporteer nie","en":"Housekeeping has not yet reported the rooms as clean and inspected to the front office"},{"af":"Finansies moet eers die gas se salaris nagaan","en":"Finance must first check the guest's salary"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Ontvangs mag net kamers gee wat huishouding as skoon en geïnspekteer gerapporteer het. Die kamerstatus koppel die twee departemente.","en":"Reception may only give rooms that housekeeping has reported as clean and inspected. The room status links the two departments."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gas wat 'n rolstoel gebruik, bespreek 'n kamer. Wat is die beste reëling?","en":"A guest who uses a wheelchair books a room. What is the best arrangement?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Kamer op die boonste verdieping, want dit het die mooiste uitsig","en":"A room on the top floor, because it has the best view"},{"af":"'n Gewone kamer, en die portier help hom die trappe op","en":"An ordinary room, and the porter helps him up the stairs"},{"af":"'n Kamer met 'n diep bad sodat hy kan ontspan","en":"A room with a deep bath so that he can relax"},{"af":"'n Kamer op die grondvloer of naby die hysbak, met wyer deure, griprelings en 'n inloopstort","en":"A room on the ground floor or near the lift, with wider doors, grab rails and a walk-in shower"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gaste met gestremdhede het toeganklikheid nodig: geen trappe nie, wyer deure vir die rolstoel, griprelings en 'n stort sonder 'n rand. 'n Diep bad is moeilik om in en uit te klim.","en":"Guests with disabilities need accessibility: no stairs, wider doors for the wheelchair, grab rails and a shower without a step. A deep bath is hard to get in and out of."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Gas sê kwaad: \"Daar is hare in my bad en die lugversorger werk nie!\" Watter reaksie is die beste?","en":"A guest says angrily: \"There is hair in my bath and the air conditioner is not working!\" Which response is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Dis nie my departement nie; u moet met huishouding praat.\"","en":"\"That is not my department; you must speak to housekeeping.\""},{"af":"\"Ek is baie jammer, meneer. Ek stuur nou dadelik huishouding en instandhouding na u kamer, of ek kan u na 'n ander kamer skuif. Ek bel u oor 20 minute om seker te maak alles is reg. Dankie dat u ons laat weet het.\"","en":"\"I am very sorry, sir. I am sending housekeeping and maintenance to your room right away, or I can move you to another room. I will call you in 20 minutes to make sure everything is in order. Thank you for letting us know.\""},{"af":"\"Ons het die kamer vanoggend skoongemaak, so u moet seker verkeerd sien.\"","en":"\"We cleaned the room this morning, so you must be mistaken.\""},{"af":"\"Ek is jammer. Ek sal dit môre aan die bestuurder noem.\"","en":"\"I am sorry. I will mention it to the manager tomorrow.\""}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die beste reaksie volg al vyf stappe: dit vra om verskoning, los die probleem dadelik op (twee departemente en 'n ander kamer), volg op en bedank die gas. Die ander reaksies blameer, stry of stel uit.","en":"The best response follows all five steps: it apologises, solves the problem immediately (two departments and another room), follows up and thanks the guest. The other responses blame, argue or delay."}}]}]}]},"lewensorientering":{"id":"lewensorientering","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Lewensoriëntering","en":"Life Orientation"},"short":{"af":"LO","en":"LO"},"icon":"🌱","color":"#db2777","intro":{"af":"Lewensoriëntering in Graad 10 berei jou voor op die res van die hoërskool en daarna: selfbeeld en selfontwikkeling, gender en mag, vakkeuses en loopbaanvelde, diversiteit en menseregte, studievaardighede, sosiale en omgewingsverantwoordelikheid, lewensrolle, seksualiteit en leefstyl, die wêreld van werk, en godsdiens en sport. Die Novembereksamen is een skriftelike vraestel oor die hele jaar se werk; die Liggaamlike Opvoedingstaak (LOT) word apart as deel van die SBA geassesseer.","en":"Life Orientation in Grade 10 prepares you for the rest of high school and beyond: self-esteem and self-development, gender and power, subject choices and career fields, diversity and human rights, study skills, social and environmental responsibility, life roles, sexuality and lifestyle, the world of work, and religion and sport. The November exam is one written paper on the whole year's work; the Physical Education Task (PET) is assessed separately as part of SBA."},"examTips":[{"af":"Leer definisies presies (bv. selfbeeld, gender, diskriminasie, menseregteskending, volhoubare ontwikkeling) en gee altyd 'n voorbeeld.","en":"Learn definitions exactly (e.g. self-esteem, gender, discrimination, human rights violation, sustainable development) and always give an example."},{"af":"Lees die werkwoord in die vraag: \"noem\" vra feite, \"verduidelik\" vra 'n rede, \"evalueer\" of \"bespreek krities\" vra 'n mening met bewyse – een punt per geldige feit.","en":"Read the verb in the question: \"name\" asks for facts, \"explain\" asks for a reason, \"evaluate\" or \"critically discuss\" asks for an opinion with evidence – one mark per valid fact."},{"af":"By bron- en gevallestudievrae: gebruik die bron – verwys daarna of haal aan – en voeg jou eie kennis by waar die vraag dit vra.","en":"In source and case-study questions: use the source – refer to it or quote it – and add your own knowledge where the question asks for it."},{"af":"By die lang vrae in Afdeling C: skryf paragrawe met 'n duidelike stelling, 'n verduideliking en 'n voorbeeld, en gee soveel geldige punte as wat die vraag tel.","en":"In the long questions in Section C: write paragraphs with a clear statement, an explanation and an example, and give as many valid points as the question is worth."},{"af":"Gebruik die studieplan wat jy in Kwartaal 2 gemaak het: hersien elke onderwerp, maak opsommings en oefen met vorige vraestelle.","en":"Use the study plan you made in Term 2: revise every topic, make summaries and practise with past papers."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Departement van Basiese Onderwys (DBE)","en":"Department of Basic Education (DBE)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za","note":{"af":"CAPS-dokument vir Lewensoriëntering, eksamenriglyne en vorige NSS-vraestelle met memorandums – goed om die vraagstyl te leer ken.","en":"CAPS document for Life Orientation, exam guidelines and past NSC papers with memos – good for learning the question style."}},{"title":{"af":"Thutong-onderwysportaal","en":"Thutong Education Portal"},"url":"https://www.thutong.doe.gov.za","note":{"af":"Die DBE se gratis onderwysportaal met leer- en hersieningsmateriaal per vak en graad.","en":"The DBE's free education portal with learning and revision material by subject and grade."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Lewensoriëntering-eksamen Graad 10\n\n**Een skriftelike vraestel oor die hele jaar se werk – waarskynlik 80 punte, minstens 90 minute** (*skatting – bevestig met Hoërskool Brits se 2026-afbakening*). Die Liggaamlike Opvoedingstaak (LOT) is deel van die **SBA** en word nie in die vraestel getoets nie.\n\n| Afdeling | Soort vrae | ±Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Kort vrae: wat, waarom, lys, meervoudige keuse, waar/onwaar met 'n rede | 20 |\n| B | Kort oop vrae, scenario-, bron- en gevallestudievrae | 30 |\n| C | Uitgebreide skryfwerk: probleemoplossing, besluitneming, raad gee (bv. twee van drie vrae van 15 punte) | 30 |\n\n### Onderwerpe\n\n| Kwartaal | Onderwerpe |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Selfbeeld, gender en mag, selfkennis en vakkeuses, diversiteit en menseregte |\n| 2 | Studievaardighede, sosiale en omgewingsverantwoordelikheid |\n| 3 | Lewensrolle, seksualiteit en leefstyl, die wêreld van werk |\n| 4 | Godsdiens in 'n multigodsdienstige samelewing, sport en vooroordeel |\n\n### Wenke\n\n1. Verdeel jou tyd volgens die punte.\n2. Gee voorbeelde uit die Suid-Afrikaanse konteks.","en":"## Life Orientation exam Grade 10\n\n**One written paper on the whole year's work – probably 80 marks, at least 90 minutes** (*estimate – confirm with Hoërskool Brits's 2026 scope*). The Physical Education Task (PET) is part of **SBA** and is not tested in the paper.\n\n| Section | Type of questions | ±Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Short questions: what, why, list, multiple choice, true/false with a reason | 20 |\n| B | Short open questions, scenario, source and case-study questions | 30 |\n| C | Extended writing: problem-solving, decision-making, giving advice (e.g. two of three 15-mark questions) | 30 |\n\n### Topics\n\n| Term | Topics |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Self-esteem, gender and power, knowledge of self and subject choices, diversity and human rights |\n| 2 | Study skills, social and environmental responsibility |\n| 3 | Life roles, sexuality and lifestyle, the world of work |\n| 4 | Religion in a multi-religious society, sport and bias |\n\n### Tips\n\n1. Divide your time according to the marks.\n2. Give examples from the South African context."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Ontwikkeling van die self, loopbane en menseregte","en":"Development of the self, careers and human rights"},"topics":[{"id":"lo10-t1-selfbeeld","title":{"af":"Selfbewustheid, selfbeeld en selfontwikkeling","en":"Self-awareness, self-esteem and self-development"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die begrippe oor die self kan definieer, verduidelik wat jou selfagting beïnvloed en strategieë gee om selfvertroue in jouself en ander te bou.","en":"You will be able to define the concepts about the self, explain what influences your self-esteem and give strategies to build confidence in yourself and others."},"summary":{"af":"## Die LO-eksamen in Graad 10\n\nDie eindjaareksamen is een vraestel van **80 punte** (minstens 90 minute). Liggaamlike Opvoeding word nie in die vraestel geëksamineer nie.\n\n| Afdeling | Punte | Soort vrae |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | 20 | Kort vrae: wat, hoekom, noem, meervoudige keuse, waar/onwaar met rede |\n| B | 30 | Kort oop vrae, scenario's, bronne en gevallestudies |\n| C | 30 | Uitgebreide skryfwerk: probleemoplossing, besluitneming, raad gee (bv. twee uit drie vrae van 15 punte) |\n\n> **Wenk:** Die punte wys hoeveel feite jy moet gee. 'n Vraag van 4 punte vra gewoonlik vier duidelike punte.\n\n## Begrippe oor die self\n\n- **Selfbewustheid** – om jouself goed te ken: jou sterk punte, swak punte, waardes, gevoelens en persoonlikheid.\n- **Selfkonsep** – hoe jy jouself sien; die prentjie in jou kop van wie jy is (bv. \"Ek is 'n lojale vriend, maar sukkel met Wiskunde\").\n- **Selfbeeld** (beeld van jouself) – hoe jy jou voorkoms en jouself sien, insluitend jou **liggaamsbeeld**: hoe jy oor jou liggaam dink en voel.\n- **Selfagting** – hoeveel waarde jy aan jouself heg en hoe graag jy van jouself hou. Baie handboeke noem dit ook *selfbeeld*.\n- **Selfontwikkeling** – om doelbewus aan jouself te werk sodat jy groei: nuwe vaardighede, beter gewoontes en meer selfvertroue.\n\n## Faktore wat selfbewustheid en selfagting beïnvloed\n\n- **Gesin:** liefde, aanmoediging en grense bou selfagting; kritiek en verwaarlosing breek dit af.\n- **Vriende en die portuurgroep:** aanvaarding laat jou behoort; spot, uitsluiting en afknouery maak skade.\n- **Skool en onderwysers:** erkenning vir harde werk bou jou op; etikette soos \"lui\" of \"dom\" breek jou af.\n- **Kultuur en godsdiens:** gee waardes, verwagtinge en 'n gevoel van identiteit.\n- **Gemeenskap:** rolmodelle, veiligheid en geleenthede in jou omgewing.\n- **Prestasies en mislukkings:** sukses bou selfvertroue; hoe jy mislukking hanteer, bepaal of dit jou afbreek of laat groei.\n- **Voorkoms:** liggaamsbou, vel, hare en klere – veral in die tienerjare.\n- **Die media:** sosiale-media-filters en geredigeerde foto's, \"likes\" en volgers, onrealistiese liggaamsideale en advertensies wat sê jy is eers goed genoeg as jy 'n produk koop.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net \"die media\" neer te skryf. Verduidelik HOE: \"Filters wys 'n onrealistiese prentjie, sodat 'n tiener haar regte gesig met 'n geredigeerde een vergelyk en voel sy is nie goed genoeg nie.\"\n\n## Hoë teenoor lae selfagting\n\n| Hoë selfagting | Lae selfagting |\n|---|---|\n| Aanvaar jouself, met foute en al | Kritiseer jouself voortdurend |\n| Probeer nuwe dinge; sien foute as leerkanse | Vermy uitdagings uit vrees vir mislukking |\n| Kan \"nee\" sê en jou mening gee | Gee maklik toe aan portuurdruk |\n| Hanteer kritiek en aanvaar komplimente | Is baie sensitief vir kritiek; glo nie komplimente nie |\n| Respekteer ander en is bly oor hulle sukses | Is jaloers of knou ander af om self beter te voel |\n| Kies gesonde verhoudings | Bly in ongesonde verhoudings om aanvaar te word |\n\n## Strategieë om selfvertroue in jouself en ander te bou\n\n1. **Kommunikasie:** gebruik **ek-boodskappe** (\"Ek voel ... wanneer ... omdat ...\") en **aktiewe luister** (oogkontak, laat die ander persoon klaarpraat, som op wat jy gehoor het).\n2. **Voltooi take en projekte:** elke voltooide taak bewys vir jou \"ek kan\".\n3. **Neem deel aan gemeenskapslewe:** vrywilligerswerk, sport of 'n jeuggroep laat jou behoort en waarde toevoeg.\n4. **Neem goeie besluite:** dink aan die gevolge; goeie keuses bou selfrespek.\n5. **Bevestig ander:** prys moeite, nie net uitslae nie (\"Jy het regtig hard geoefen\").\n6. **Positiewe selfpraat:** vervang \"Ek is so dom\" met \"Ek het dit nog nie onder die knie nie\".\n7. **Realistiese SMART-doelwitte:** Spesifiek, Meetbaar, Haalbaar, Realisties en Tydgebonde – bv. \"Ek gaan drie weke lank elke dag 20 minute Wiskunde oefen om my volgende toetspunt met 10% te verbeter.\"\n8. **Persoonlike SWOT-ontleding:** sterk punte (*Strengths*) en swak punte (*Weaknesses*) is binne jou; geleenthede (*Opportunities*) en bedreigings (*Threats*) kom van buite.\n\n## Respek vir die uniekheid van jouself en ander\n\nElke mens is uniek. Mense verskil in **ras, gender en vermoë** (insluitend gestremdheid). Respek beteken jy waardeer verskille, gebruik nie neerhalende name nie en sluit niemand uit nie. Wanneer jy ander met respek behandel, bou jy ook hulle selfagting – en joune.\n\n> **Onthou!** In Afdeling C gee jy raad in paragraafvorm: noem die strategie, verduidelik hoe dit help en pas dit op die persoon in die scenario toe.","en":"## The LO exam in Grade 10\n\nThe end-of-year exam is one paper of **80 marks** (at least 90 minutes). Physical Education is not examined in the written paper.\n\n| Section | Marks | Type of questions |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | 20 | Short questions: what, why, list, multiple choice, true/false with a reason |\n| B | 30 | Short open questions, scenarios, sources and case studies |\n| C | 30 | Extended writing: problem-solving, decision-making, giving advice (e.g. two of three 15-mark questions) |\n\n> **Tip:** The marks show how many facts you must give. A 4-mark question usually asks for four clear points.\n\n## Concepts about the self\n\n- **Self-awareness** – knowing yourself well: your strengths, weaknesses, values, feelings and personality.\n- **Self-concept** – how you see yourself; the picture in your head of who you are (e.g. \"I am a loyal friend, but I struggle with Maths\").\n- **Self-image** – how you see your appearance and yourself, including your **body image**: how you think and feel about your body.\n- **Self-esteem** – how much you value yourself and how much you like yourself.\n- **Self-development** – deliberately working on yourself so that you grow: new skills, better habits and more self-confidence.\n\n## Factors that influence self-awareness and self-esteem\n\n- **Family:** love, encouragement and boundaries build self-esteem; criticism and neglect break it down.\n- **Friends and the peer group:** acceptance makes you belong; teasing, exclusion and bullying do damage.\n- **School and teachers:** recognition for hard work builds you up; labels such as \"lazy\" or \"stupid\" break you down.\n- **Culture and religion:** give values, expectations and a sense of identity.\n- **Community:** role models, safety and opportunities where you live.\n- **Achievements and failures:** success builds confidence; how you handle failure decides whether it breaks you down or helps you grow.\n- **Appearance:** build, skin, hair and clothes – especially in the teenage years.\n- **The media:** social-media filters and edited photos, likes and followers, unrealistic body ideals and adverts that say you are only good enough once you buy a product.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Writing only \"the media\". Explain HOW: \"Filters show an unrealistic picture, so a teen compares her real face with an edited one and feels she is not good enough.\"\n\n## High vs low self-esteem\n\n| High self-esteem | Low self-esteem |\n|---|---|\n| Accepts yourself, faults and all | Constantly criticises yourself |\n| Tries new things; sees mistakes as chances to learn | Avoids challenges for fear of failure |\n| Can say \"no\" and give your opinion | Gives in easily to peer pressure |\n| Handles criticism and accepts compliments | Is very sensitive to criticism; does not believe compliments |\n| Respects others and is glad about their success | Is jealous or bullies others to feel better |\n| Chooses healthy relationships | Stays in unhealthy relationships to be accepted |\n\n## Strategies to build confidence in self and others\n\n1. **Communication:** use **I-statements** (\"I feel ... when ... because ...\") and **active listening** (eye contact, let the other person finish, summarise what you heard).\n2. **Complete tasks and projects:** every finished task proves to you \"I can\".\n3. **Participate in community life:** volunteering, sport or a youth group make you belong and add value.\n4. **Make good decisions:** think about the consequences; good choices build self-respect.\n5. **Affirm others:** praise effort, not only results (\"You really practised hard\").\n6. **Positive self-talk:** replace \"I am so stupid\" with \"I haven't mastered this yet\".\n7. **Realistic SMART goals:** Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Realistic and Time-bound – e.g. \"For three weeks I will practise Maths for 20 minutes every day to improve my next test mark by 10%.\"\n8. **Personal SWOT analysis:** **S**trengths and **W**eaknesses (inside you); **O**pportunities and **T**hreats (outside you).\n\n## Respecting the uniqueness of self and others\n\nEvery person is unique. People differ in **race, gender and ability** (including disability). Respect means you value differences, don't use insulting names and don't exclude anyone. When you treat others with respect, you also build their self-esteem – and your own.\n\n> **Remember!** In Section C you give advice in paragraph form: name the strategy, explain how it helps and apply it to the person in the scenario."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Selfbewustheid","en":"Self-awareness"},"def":{"af":"Om jou eie sterk punte, swak punte, waardes, gevoelens en persoonlikheid te ken.","en":"Knowing your own strengths, weaknesses, values, feelings and personality."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfkonsep","en":"Self-concept"},"def":{"af":"Hoe jy jouself sien: die prentjie wat jy het van wie jy is.","en":"How you see yourself: the picture you have of who you are."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfbeeld","en":"Self-image"},"def":{"af":"Die beeld wat jy van jouself en jou voorkoms het, insluitend jou liggaamsbeeld.","en":"The image you have of yourself and your appearance, including your body image."}},{"term":{"af":"Liggaamsbeeld","en":"Body image"},"def":{"af":"Hoe jy oor jou liggaam dink en voel, en hoe jy glo ander dit sien.","en":"How you think and feel about your body, and how you believe others see it."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfagting","en":"Self-esteem"},"def":{"af":"Hoeveel waarde jy aan jouself heg en hoe graag jy van jouself hou.","en":"How much you value yourself and how much you like yourself."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfontwikkeling","en":"Self-development"},"def":{"af":"Om doelbewus aan jou vaardighede, gewoontes en selfvertroue te werk sodat jy groei.","en":"Deliberately working on your skills, habits and confidence so that you grow."}},{"term":{"af":"Portuurgroep","en":"Peer group"},"def":{"af":"Mense van jou eie ouderdom en status met wie jy meng en wat jou gedrag beïnvloed.","en":"People of your own age and status with whom you mix and who influence your behaviour."}},{"term":{"af":"Ek-boodskap","en":"I-statement"},"def":{"af":"'n Manier om gevoelens te deel sonder om te blameer: 'Ek voel ... wanneer ... omdat ...'.","en":"A way to share feelings without blaming: 'I feel ... when ... because ...'."}},{"term":{"af":"SMART-doelwit","en":"SMART goal"},"def":{"af":"'n Doelwit wat spesifiek, meetbaar, haalbaar, realisties en tydgebonde is.","en":"A goal that is specific, measurable, achievable, realistic and time-bound."}},{"term":{"af":"SWOT-ontleding","en":"SWOT analysis"},"def":{"af":"'n Selfondersoek van jou sterk punte, swak punte, geleenthede en bedreigings.","en":"A self-examination of your strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Onderskei tussen selfkonsep en selfagting (4)","en":"Distinguish between self-concept and self-esteem (4)"},"problem":{"af":"Afdeling A-vraag: Onderskei tussen *selfkonsep* en *selfagting*. Gee by elkeen 'n voorbeeld. (4)","en":"Section A question: Distinguish between *self-concept* and *self-esteem*. Give an example of each. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Definieer die eerste begrip (1): Selfkonsep is hoe jy jouself sien – die prentjie wat jy het van wie jy is.","en":"Define the first concept (1): Self-concept is how you see yourself – the picture you have of who you are."},{"af":"Voorbeeld (1): \"Ek is 'n rugbyspeler, 'n broer en ek hou van musiek.\"","en":"Example (1): \"I am a rugby player, a brother and I like music.\""},{"af":"Definieer die tweede begrip (1): Selfagting is hoeveel waarde jy aan jouself heg en hoe graag jy van jouself hou.","en":"Define the second concept (1): Self-esteem is how much you value yourself and how much you like yourself."},{"af":"Voorbeeld (1): \"Ek is trots op wie ek is, al het ek nie die span gehaal nie.\" Let op: selfkonsep beskryf, selfagting *waardeer*.","en":"Example (1): \"I am proud of who I am, even though I didn't make the team.\" Note: self-concept describes, self-esteem *values*."}],"answer":{"af":"Selfkonsep = hoe jy jouself sien (beskrywing); selfagting = hoeveel jy jouself waardeer (gevoel van waarde).","en":"Self-concept = how you see yourself (description); self-esteem = how much you value yourself (sense of worth)."}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: sosiale media en selfagting (6)","en":"Source question: social media and self-esteem (6)"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron: *Mia (15) van Brits plaas elke middag 'n selfie. As 'n foto minder as 50 \"likes\" kry, vee sy dit uit. Sy volg 'n beïnvloeder met 'n \"perfekte\" lyf en sê: \"Ek sal nooit so mooi wees nie.\"* (a) Noem TWEE faktore in die bron wat Mia se selfagting beïnvloed. (2) (b) Verduidelik hoe sosiale media 'n tiener soos Mia se selfagting kan benadeel. (4)","en":"Read the source: *Mia (15) from Brits posts a selfie every afternoon. If a photo gets fewer than 50 likes, she deletes it. She follows an influencer with a \"perfect\" body and says: \"I'll never be that pretty.\"* (a) Name TWO factors in the source that influence Mia's self-esteem. (2) (b) Explain how social media can harm the self-esteem of a teen like Mia. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Soek die faktore in die bron: \"likes\" op sosiale media (1) en die vergelyking met 'n beïnvloeder se liggaam / onrealistiese liggaamsideale (1).","en":"(a) Find the factors in the source: likes on social media (1) and comparing herself with an influencer's body / unrealistic body ideals (1)."},{"af":"(b) Punt 1: Sy meet haar waarde aan die aantal \"likes\", dus voel sy waardeloos wanneer 'n foto min aandag kry. (2)","en":"(b) Point 1: She measures her worth by the number of likes, so she feels worthless when a photo gets little attention. (2)"},{"af":"Punt 2: Beïnvloeders se foto's is dikwels gefiltreer en geredigeer; Mia vergelyk haar regte lyf met 'n onrealistiese ideaal en ontwikkel 'n negatiewe liggaamsbeeld. (2)","en":"Point 2: Influencers' photos are often filtered and edited; Mia compares her real body with an unrealistic ideal and develops a negative body image. (2)"},{"af":"Kontroleer: elke punt sê WAT gebeur en HOE dit haar selfagting skaad – dit is wat \"verduidelik\" vra.","en":"Check: each point says WHAT happens and HOW it harms her self-esteem – that is what \"explain\" asks for."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) \"Likes\"; vergelyking met 'n beïnvloeder. (b) Sy meet haar waarde aan \"likes\"; sy vergelyk haar met geredigeerde, onrealistiese beelde.","en":"(a) Likes; comparing herself with an influencer. (b) She measures her worth by likes; she compares herself with edited, unrealistic images."}},{"title":{"af":"Gee raad aan 'n vriend met lae selfagting (8)","en":"Advise a friend with low self-esteem (8)"},"problem":{"af":"Afdeling C-styl: Jou vriend Johan (Gr 10) het die eerste rugbyspan gemis. Hy sê nou hy is \"nutteloos\", wil nie meer oefen nie en sit pouses alleen. Skryf 'n paragraaf waarin jy vier strategieë aanbeveel om sy selfvertroue te bou. (8)","en":"Section C style: Your friend Johan (Gr 10) missed out on the first rugby team. He now says he is \"useless\", doesn't want to practise any more and sits alone at break. Write a paragraph recommending four strategies to build his confidence. (8)"},"steps":[{"af":"Beplan: kies vier CAPS-strategieë wat by Johan pas – positiewe selfpraat, 'n SMART-doelwit, deelname, en praat met iemand.","en":"Plan: choose four CAPS strategies that fit Johan – positive self-talk, a SMART goal, participation and talking to someone."},{"af":"Strategie 1 + verduideliking (2): \"Johan, vervang 'ek is nutteloos' met 'ek het nog nie die span gehaal nie'. Positiewe selfpraat help jou om nie op te gee nie.\"","en":"Strategy 1 + explanation (2): \"Johan, replace 'I'm useless' with 'I haven't made the team yet'. Positive self-talk helps you not to give up.\""},{"af":"Strategie 2 (2): \"Stel 'n SMART-doelwit, bv. drie keer per week ekstra fiksheidsoefening tot die volgende proewe in Februarie, sodat jy jou vordering kan sien.\"","en":"Strategy 2 (2): \"Set a SMART goal, e.g. extra fitness training three times a week until the next trials in February, so you can see your progress.\""},{"af":"Strategie 3 (2): \"Speel steeds vir die tweede span of help die o.14's afrig – om deel te neem en take te voltooi wys jou jy is waardevol.\"","en":"Strategy 3 (2): \"Keep playing for the second team or help coach the u/14s – taking part and completing tasks shows you that you are valuable.\""},{"af":"Strategie 4 (2): \"Praat met die afrigter oor wat jy kan verbeter, en met 'n vertroude volwassene oor hoe jy voel. Jou vriende sal jou ook bevestig en jou moeite raaksien.\"","en":"Strategy 4 (2): \"Talk to the coach about what you can improve, and to a trusted adult about how you feel. Your friends will also affirm you and notice your effort.\""}],"answer":{"af":"Vier strategieë, elkeen verduidelik en op Johan toegepas: positiewe selfpraat, SMART-doelwit, deelname/voltooi take, kommunikasie en bevestiging.","en":"Four strategies, each explained and applied to Johan: positive self-talk, a SMART goal, participation/completing tasks, communication and affirmation."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n SMART-doelwit","en":"Write a SMART goal"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato skryf: \"Ek wil fiks word.\" (a) Verduidelik waarom dit nie 'n SMART-doelwit is nie. (2) (b) Herskryf dit as 'n SMART-doelwit. (3)","en":"Lerato writes: \"I want to get fit.\" (a) Explain why this is not a SMART goal. (2) (b) Rewrite it as a SMART goal. (3)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit is nie spesifiek of meetbaar nie – wat beteken \"fiks\"? (1) Daar is ook geen tydsgrens nie, dus weet sy nie wanneer sy dit bereik het nie. (1)","en":"(a) It is not specific or measurable – what does \"fit\" mean? (1) There is also no time limit, so she won't know when she has achieved it. (1)"},{"af":"(b) Maak dit spesifiek en meetbaar: \"Ek gaan drie keer per week 3 km hardloop ...\"","en":"(b) Make it specific and measurable: \"I will run 3 km three times a week ...\""},{"af":"Maak dit haalbaar, realisties en tydgebonde: \"... vanaf Maandag vir agt weke, sodat ek die skool se 5 km-pretloop aan die einde van die kwartaal kan klaarmaak.\"","en":"Make it achievable, realistic and time-bound: \"... from Monday for eight weeks, so that I can finish the school's 5 km fun run at the end of the term.\""}],"answer":{"af":"\"Ek gaan vanaf Maandag vir agt weke drie keer per week 3 km hardloop sodat ek die skool se 5 km-pretloop aan die einde van die kwartaal kan klaarmaak.\"","en":"\"From Monday, for eight weeks, I will run 3 km three times a week so that I can finish the school's 5 km fun run at the end of the term.\""}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter begrip beskryf hoeveel waarde jy aan jouself heg en hoe graag jy van jouself hou?","en":"Which concept describes how much you value yourself and how much you like yourself?"},"options":[{"af":"Selfbewustheid","en":"Self-awareness"},{"af":"Selfagting","en":"Self-esteem"},{"af":"Selfkonsep","en":"Self-concept"},{"af":"Selfontwikkeling","en":"Self-development"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Selfagting gaan oor jou gevoel van waarde. Selfbewustheid is om jouself te ken; selfkonsep is hoe jy jouself sien.","en":"Self-esteem is about your sense of worth. Self-awareness is knowing yourself; self-concept is how you see yourself."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om jou eie sterk punte, swak punte, waardes en gevoelens te ken, word ___ genoem.","en":"Knowing your own strengths, weaknesses, values and feelings is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["selfbewustheid","self-bewustheid"],"en":["self-awareness","self awareness","selfawareness"]},"explain":{"af":"Selfbewustheid = jouself ken. Dit is die eerste stap: jy kan net aan jouself werk as jy weet waar jy staan.","en":"Self-awareness = knowing yourself. It is the first step: you can only work on yourself if you know where you stand."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selfagting","selfontwikkeling","selfvertroue"],"en":["self-esteem","self-development","self-confidence"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Liggaamlike Opvoeding word in die Graad 10 LO-eindjaarvraestel geëksamineer.","en":"Physical Education is examined in the Grade 10 LO end-of-year paper."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Liggaamlike Opvoeding word prakties geassesseer en is nie deel van die geskrewe vraestel van 80 punte nie.","en":"False. Physical Education is assessed practically and is not part of the 80-mark written paper."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel die Graad 10 LO-eindjaarvraestel altesaam?","en":"What is the total mark of the Grade 10 LO end-of-year paper?"},"options":[{"af":"100","en":"100"},{"af":"150","en":"150"},{"af":"80","en":"80"},{"af":"60","en":"60"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die vraestel is 80 punte: Afdeling A (20) + Afdeling B (30) + Afdeling C (30).","en":"The paper is 80 marks: Section A (20) + Section B (30) + Section C (30)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoe jy oor jou liggaam dink en voel, word jou ___ genoem.","en":"How you think and feel about your body is called your ___."},"answers":{"af":["liggaamsbeeld"],"en":["body image","bodyimage"]},"explain":{"af":"Liggaamsbeeld is deel van jou selfbeeld. Media met geredigeerde foto's kan dit maklik negatief beïnvloed.","en":"Body image is part of your self-image. Media with edited photos can easily affect it negatively."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selfkonsep","selfagting","persoonlikheid"],"en":["self-concept","self-esteem","personality"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gedrag is 'n teken van LAE selfagting?","en":"Which behaviour is a sign of LOW self-esteem?"},"options":[{"af":"Probeer nuwe dinge en sien foute as leerkanse","en":"Tries new things and sees mistakes as chances to learn"},{"af":"Is bly wanneer 'n vriend goed presteer","en":"Is glad when a friend does well"},{"af":"Aanvaar 'n kompliment met 'n dankie","en":"Accepts a compliment with a thank you"},{"af":"Gee maklik toe aan portuurdruk om aanvaar te word","en":"Gives in easily to peer pressure to be accepted"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Iemand met lae selfagting soek aanvaarding by ander en sê dus moeilik \"nee\". Die ander drie is tekens van hoë selfagting.","en":"Someone with low self-esteem seeks acceptance from others and therefore finds it hard to say \"no\". The other three are signs of high self-esteem."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van 'n SWOT-ontleding by die regte voorbeeld vir 'n Graad 10-leerder.","en":"Match each part of a SWOT analysis to the correct example for a Grade 10 learner."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sterk punt","en":"Strength"},"r":{"af":"Ek is geduldig en verduidelik goed vir ander","en":"I am patient and explain well to others"}},{"l":{"af":"Swak punt","en":"Weakness"},"r":{"af":"Ek stel my huiswerk uit tot laat in die aand","en":"I put off my homework until late at night"}},{"l":{"af":"Geleentheid","en":"Opportunity"},"r":{"af":"Die skool begin 'n gratis Wiskunde-hulpklas","en":"The school starts a free Maths help class"}},{"l":{"af":"Bedreiging","en":"Threat"},"r":{"af":"Vriende wat my druk om klas te stap","en":"Friends who pressure me to bunk class"}}],"explain":{"af":"Sterk en swak punte is BINNE jou (eienskappe, gewoontes). Geleenthede en bedreigings kom van BUITE (skool, vriende, gemeenskap).","en":"Strengths and weaknesses are INSIDE you (qualities, habits). Opportunities and threats come from OUTSIDE (school, friends, community)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is 'n goeie ek-boodskap?","en":"Which sentence is a good I-statement?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Jy luister nooit na my nie!\"","en":"\"You never listen to me!\""},{"af":"\"Almal weet jy is onbeskof.\"","en":"\"Everyone knows you are rude.\""},{"af":"\"Ek voel seergemaak wanneer jy my onderbreek, omdat dit lyk of my mening nie saak maak nie.\"","en":"\"I feel hurt when you interrupt me, because it seems my opinion doesn't matter.\""},{"af":"\"Hoekom is jy altyd so?\"","en":"\"Why are you always like this?\""}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Ek-boodskap volg die patroon \"Ek voel ... wanneer ... omdat ...\". Dit deel jou gevoel sonder om die ander te blameer, sodat hulle nie verdedigend raak nie.","en":"An I-statement follows the pattern \"I feel ... when ... because ...\". It shares your feeling without blaming the other person, so they don't become defensive."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n SMART-doelwit staan die T vir ___.","en":"In a SMART goal the T stands for ___."},"answers":{"af":["tydgebonde","tyd-gebonde","tydsgebonde"],"en":["time-bound","timebound","time bound","timely"]},"explain":{"af":"Tydgebonde beteken die doelwit het 'n sperdatum, bv. \"teen die einde van die kwartaal\". Sonder 'n datum stel 'n mens dit maklik uit.","en":"Time-bound means the goal has a deadline, e.g. \"by the end of the term\". Without a date it is easy to put it off."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["talentvol","toepaslik","teikengerig"],"en":["teamwork","truthful","thorough"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om iemand se moeite te prys (\"Jy het baie hard gewerk\") is 'n strategie om selfvertroue in ander te bou.","en":"Praising someone's effort (\"You worked very hard\") is a strategy to build confidence in others."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Om ander te bevestig is 'n CAPS-strategie. Moeite prys werk beter as net uitslae prys, want almal kan moeite doen.","en":"True. Affirming others is a CAPS strategy. Praising effort works better than praising only results, because everyone can make an effort."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo het sy eerste Wiskundetoets gedruip en sê: \"Ek is net dom.\" Watter sin is positiewe selfpraat?","en":"Thabo failed his first Maths test and says: \"I'm just stupid.\" Which sentence is positive self-talk?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Ek het dié werk nog nie onder die knie nie; ek gaan my onderwyser vra om my te help.\"","en":"\"I haven't mastered this work yet; I'm going to ask my teacher to help me.\""},{"af":"\"Ek sal nooit Wiskunde verstaan nie.\"","en":"\"I will never understand Maths.\""},{"af":"\"Die onderwyser het die toets te moeilik gemaak.\"","en":"\"The teacher made the test too difficult.\""},{"af":"\"Wiskunde is in elk geval nie belangrik nie.\"","en":"\"Maths isn't important anyway.\""}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Positiewe selfpraat is eerlik maar hoopvol en lei tot aksie. Om ander te blameer of die vak af te maak, los nie die probleem op nie.","en":"Positive self-talk is honest but hopeful and leads to action. Blaming others or dismissing the subject doesn't solve the problem."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die groep vriende van jou eie ouderdom wat jou gedrag beïnvloed, word jou ___ genoem.","en":"The group of friends of your own age who influence your behaviour is called your ___."},"answers":{"af":["portuurgroep","portuur-groep","portuurgroepe"],"en":["peer group","peergroup","peers"]},"explain":{"af":"Die portuurgroep is veral in die tienerjare 'n sterk faktor: aanvaarding bou selfagting, uitsluiting en spot breek dit af.","en":"The peer group is a strong factor especially in the teenage years: acceptance builds self-esteem, exclusion and teasing break it down."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gemeenskap","gesin","rolmodel"],"en":["community","family","role model"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lerato sê: \"Ek is goed met mense en ek kan mooi teken.\" In haar SWOT-ontleding is dit haar ___.","en":"Lerato says: \"I'm good with people and I can draw well.\" In her SWOT analysis these are her ___."},"answers":{"af":["sterk punte","sterkpunte","sterk punt","sterkpunt"],"en":["strengths","strength"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is eienskappe BINNE Lerato, en dit is positief – dus sterk punte. Geleenthede en bedreigings kom van buite.","en":"These are qualities INSIDE Lerato, and they are positive – so they are strengths. Opportunities and threats come from outside."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geleenthede","bedreigings","swak punte"],"en":["opportunities","threats","weaknesses"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter verduideliking wys die beste HOE sosiale media 'n tiener se selfagting kan benadeel?","en":"Which explanation best shows HOW social media can harm a teen's self-esteem?"},"options":[{"af":"Sosiale media is sleg vir tieners.","en":"Social media is bad for teens."},{"af":"Sosiale media kos baie data.","en":"Social media costs a lot of data."},{"af":"Beïnvloeders verdien baie geld met advertensies.","en":"Influencers earn a lot of money from adverts."},{"af":"Tieners vergelyk hulle regte lyf met gefiltreerde foto's en meet hulle waarde aan \"likes\", en voel dan hulle is nie goed genoeg nie.","en":"Teens compare their real bodies with filtered photos and measure their worth by likes, and then feel they are not good enough."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Verduideliking moet die oorsaak (filters, \"likes\", vergelyking) aan die gevolg (laer selfagting) koppel. \"Sosiale media is sleg\" is net 'n mening sonder verduideliking.","en":"An explanation must link the cause (filters, likes, comparison) to the effect (lower self-esteem). \"Social media is bad\" is only an opinion without explanation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter doelwit is 'n SMART-doelwit?","en":"Which goal is a SMART goal?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Ek wil beter doen op skool.\"","en":"\"I want to do better at school.\""},{"af":"\"Ek gaan vir ses weke elke weeksaand 45 minute studeer om 60% in my Geskiedenis-eksamen te kry.\"","en":"\"For six weeks I will study for 45 minutes every weeknight to get 60% in my History exam.\""},{"af":"\"Ek gaan volgende jaar die vinnigste atleet in Suid-Afrika wees.\"","en":"\"Next year I am going to be the fastest athlete in South Africa.\""},{"af":"\"Ek gaan fiks word.\"","en":"\"I am going to get fit.\""}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Net dié doelwit is spesifiek (45 minute studeer), meetbaar (60%), haalbaar, realisties en tydgebonde (ses weke). Die atleet-doelwit is nie realisties nie, en die ander is te vaag.","en":"Only this goal is specific (study 45 minutes), measurable (60%), achievable, realistic and time-bound (six weeks). The athlete goal is not realistic, and the others are too vague."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou vriendin Anika eet nie meer middagete nie, omdat sy soos 'n beïnvloeder wil lyk, en sy vee foto's met min \"likes\" uit. Watter raad is die BESTE?","en":"Your friend Anika has stopped eating lunch because she wants to look like an influencer, and she deletes photos with few likes. Which advice is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"Luister sonder om te oordeel, herinner haar dat beïnvloeders se foto's geredigeer word, help haar om op haar sterk punte te fokus en moedig haar aan om met 'n vertroude volwassene of die skoolberader te praat.","en":"Listen without judging, remind her that influencers' photos are edited, help her focus on her strengths and encourage her to talk to a trusted adult or the school counsellor."},{"af":"Sê vir haar sy moet ophou om so dramaties te wees.","en":"Tell her to stop being so dramatic."},{"af":"Moedig haar aan om meer filters te gebruik sodat haar foto's beter lyk.","en":"Encourage her to use more filters so her photos look better."},{"af":"Ignoreer dit – dit is net 'n fase.","en":"Ignore it – it's just a phase."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die beste raad kombineer verskeie strategieë: aktiewe luister, die media krities bevraagteken, op sterk punte fokus en hulp by 'n volwassene soek – want haar gesondheid kan in gevaar wees. Die ander opsies maak die probleem erger of ignoreer dit.","en":"The best advice combines several strategies: active listening, questioning the media critically, focusing on strengths and getting help from an adult – because her health may be at risk. The other options make the problem worse or ignore it."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t1-gender-mag","title":{"af":"Mag, magsverhoudinge, manlikheid, vroulikheid en gender","en":"Power, power relations, masculinity, femininity and gender"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal tussen geslag en gender kan onderskei, genderstereotipes en magsmisbruik kan herken en verduidelik hoe ongelyke mag tot GGG kan lei en waar hulp beskikbaar is.","en":"You will be able to distinguish between sex and gender, recognise gender stereotypes and abuse of power, and explain how unequal power can lead to GBV and where help is available."},"summary":{"af":"## Geslag en gender\n\n- **Geslag** is **biologies**: jy word daarmee gebore. Dit word bepaal deur chromosome (gewoonlik XX by vroue en XY by mans), voortplantingsorgane en hormone.\n- **Gender** is **sosiaal gekonstrueer**: die rolle, gedrag en verwagtinge wat 'n samelewing aan mans en vroue koppel. Gender word aangeleer (by die gesin, skool, media, kultuur en godsdiens) en kan oor tyd en tussen kulture verskil.\n- **Manlikheid** is die eienskappe en gedrag wat 'n samelewing as \"manlik\" beskou; **vroulikheid** is dié wat as \"vroulik\" beskou word.\n\n> **Onthou!** Geslag = biologie. Gender = samelewing (aangeleer en veranderbaar).\n\n### Verskille tussen mans en vroue\n\n- **In voortplanting** (geslagsverskille): net vroue kan swanger word, geboorte gee en borsvoed; mans produseer sperm.\n- **Rolle in die gemeenskap** (genderrolle): wie werk, wie kook, wie na die kinders kyk en wie lei – dit word deur die samelewing bepaal, nie deur biologie nie.\n\n## Genderstereotipes\n\n'n **Stereotipe** is 'n vaste, oorvereenvoudigde idee oor 'n hele groep mense. Voorbeelde:\n\n- \"Seuns huil nie\" – seuns leer om gevoelens weg te steek, wat tot opgekropte stres en woede kan lei.\n- Huiswerk en kinderversorging is \"vrouewerk\".\n- Loopbane word as manlik of vroulik geëtiketteer: \"Ingenieurs en mynwerkers is mans; verpleegkundiges is vroue.\"\n- \"Meisies is swak in Wiskunde\" en \"Die man moet die broodwinner wees.\"\n\nStereotipes beperk almal se keuses en lei tot ongelykheid.\n\n## Gender in fisieke aktiwiteit en sport\n\nMeisies hou dikwels vroeër as seuns op met sport. Redes:\n\n- **stereotipes** (\"sport is vir seuns\", \"rugby is nie vir meisies nie\");\n- **liggaamsbeeld** – skaamte oor hoe jy in sportklere lyk;\n- **veiligheid** – oefeninge wat laat eindig, onveilige vervoer of roetes;\n- swakker **fasiliteite** en minder spanne of afrigters vir meisies;\n- minder **media-dekking** en borgskap, dus minder vroulike rolmodelle.\n\n## Mag en magsverhoudinge\n\n**Mag** is die vermoë om ander mense of 'n situasie te beïnvloed of te beheer. **Magsverhoudinge** is die manier waarop mag tussen mense verdeel is.\n\n**Bronne van mag:** ouderdom, gender, geld, status, fisieke krag, posisie (bv. prefek, onderwyser, baas) en kennis.\n\n| Gebalanseerde mag | Ongebalanseerde mag |\n|---|---|\n| Albei se menings tel | Een persoon besluit alles |\n| Besluite word saam geneem | Die ander persoon is bang of afhanklik |\n| Respek en vertroue | Beheer, dreigemente en jaloesie |\n\n**Magsmisbruik** is wanneer iemand mag gebruik om ander te benadeel: **afknouery** (boeliegedrag), **dwang** (iemand forseer om iets te doen), **intimidasie** (dreig of bang maak) en beheer (bv. iemand se foon deursoek of vriendskappe verbied).\n\n## Gevolge van genderongelykheid\n\nWanneer een persoon in 'n verhouding baie meer mag het, kan dit die ander se welstand ernstig skaad:\n\n- **Seksuele misbruik** – iemand met meer mag dwing 'n ander tot seksuele kontak.\n- **Tienerswangerskap** – 'n meisie voel dalk sy kan nie \"nee\" sê of op 'n kondoom aandring nie.\n- **Geweld** – **gendergebaseerde geweld (GGG)** is geweld teen iemand weens hulle gender; **geweld deur 'n intieme maat** kom van 'n kêrel, meisie of eggenoot.\n- **SOI's, insluitend MIV en vigs** – 'n maat wat nie oor kondoomgebruik kan onderhandel nie, loop 'n groter risiko.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om net te skryf \"dit lei tot GGG\". Wys die skakel: ongelyke mag → een persoon glo hy of sy het die reg om te beheer → die ander kan nie weier of weggaan nie → misbruik en geweld.\n\n## Hoe om te reageer\n\n- **Daag stereotipes uit** – sê iets wanneer iemand sê \"dis vrouewerk\".\n- **Behandel almal gelyk** – deel take regverdig, kies spanne op grond van vermoë.\n- **Wees selfgeldend** – sê kalm en duidelik wat jy wil en nie wil nie.\n- **Rapporteer misbruik** by 'n vertroude volwassene, onderwyser, maatskaplike werker of die polisie.\n\n**Wette en instansies:**\n\n- **Wet op Gesinsgeweld 116 van 1998** – 'n slagoffer kan by die **landdroshof** aansoek doen om 'n **beskermingsbevel**.\n- **Kommissie vir Geslagsgelykheid** – 'n Hoofstuk 9-instelling wat gendergelykheid bevorder en klagtes ondersoek.\n- **16 Dae van Aktivisme** teen geweld teen vroue en kinders: **25 November tot 10 Desember**.\n\n**Hulp:** SAPD **10111** · GGG-bevelsentrum **0800 428 428** · Childline **116**.\n\n> **Wenk:** By 'n \"beveel aan\"-vraag gee jy strategieë wat die persoon self kan doen ÉN instansies of nommers waar hulp beskikbaar is.","en":"## Sex and gender\n\n- **Sex** is **biological**: you are born with it. It is determined by chromosomes (usually XX in females and XY in males), reproductive organs and hormones.\n- **Gender** is **socially constructed**: the roles, behaviour and expectations a society links to men and women. Gender is learnt (from family, school, media, culture and religion) and can differ over time and between cultures.\n- **Masculinity** is the qualities and behaviour a society regards as \"male\"; **femininity** is those regarded as \"female\".\n\n> **Remember!** Sex = biology. Gender = society (learnt and changeable).\n\n### Differences between men and women\n\n- **In reproduction** (sex differences): only women can fall pregnant, give birth and breastfeed; men produce sperm.\n- **Roles in the community** (gender roles): who works, who cooks, who looks after the children and who leads – decided by society, not by biology.\n\n## Gender stereotypes\n\nA **stereotype** is a fixed, oversimplified idea about a whole group of people. Examples:\n\n- \"Boys don't cry\" – boys learn to hide their feelings, which can lead to bottled-up stress and anger.\n- Housework and childcare are \"women's work\".\n- Careers are labelled male or female: \"Engineers and miners are men; nurses are women.\"\n- \"Girls are bad at Maths\" and \"The man must be the breadwinner.\"\n\nStereotypes limit everyone's choices and lead to inequality.\n\n## Gender in physical activity and sport\n\nGirls often drop out of sport earlier than boys. Reasons:\n\n- **stereotypes** (\"sport is for boys\", \"rugby is not for girls\");\n- **body image** – embarrassment about how you look in sports clothes;\n- **safety** – practices that end late, unsafe transport or routes;\n- poorer **facilities** and fewer teams or coaches for girls;\n- less **media coverage** and sponsorship, so fewer female role models.\n\n## Power and power relations\n\n**Power** is the ability to influence or control other people or a situation. **Power relations** are the way power is divided between people.\n\n**Sources of power:** age, gender, money, status, physical strength, position (e.g. prefect, teacher, boss) and knowledge.\n\n| Balanced power | Unbalanced power |\n|---|---|\n| Both opinions count | One person decides everything |\n| Decisions are made together | The other person is afraid or dependent |\n| Respect and trust | Control, threats and jealousy |\n\n**Abuse of power** is when someone uses power to harm others: **bullying**, **coercion** (forcing someone to do something), **intimidation** (threatening or frightening) and control (e.g. searching someone's phone or forbidding friendships).\n\n## Effects of gender inequality\n\nWhen one person in a relationship has much more power, it can seriously harm the other's well-being:\n\n- **Sexual abuse** – someone with more power forces another into sexual contact.\n- **Teenage pregnancy** – a girl may feel she cannot say \"no\" or insist on a condom.\n- **Violence** – **gender-based violence (GBV)** is violence against someone because of their gender; **intimate-partner violence** comes from a boyfriend, girlfriend or spouse.\n- **STIs, including HIV and AIDS** – a partner who cannot negotiate condom use is at greater risk.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Writing only \"it leads to GBV\". Show the link: unequal power → one person believes he or she has the right to control → the other cannot refuse or leave → abuse and violence.\n\n## How to respond\n\n- **Challenge stereotypes** – speak up when someone says \"that's women's work\".\n- **Treat everyone equally** – share tasks fairly, choose teams on ability.\n- **Be assertive** – say calmly and clearly what you want and don't want.\n- **Report abuse** to a trusted adult, teacher, social worker or the police.\n\n**Laws and institutions:**\n\n- **Domestic Violence Act 116 of 1998** – a victim can apply to the **magistrate's court** for a **protection order**.\n- **Commission for Gender Equality** – a Chapter 9 institution that promotes gender equality and investigates complaints.\n- **16 Days of Activism** for no violence against women and children: **25 November to 10 December**.\n\n**Help:** SAPS **10111** · GBV Command Centre **0800 428 428** · Childline **116**.\n\n> **Tip:** In a \"recommend\" question, give strategies the person can use themselves AND institutions or numbers where help is available."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Geslag","en":"Sex"},"def":{"af":"Die biologiese verskil tussen manlik en vroulik, bepaal deur chromosome, voortplantingsorgane en hormone.","en":"The biological difference between male and female, determined by chromosomes, reproductive organs and hormones."}},{"term":{"af":"Gender","en":"Gender"},"def":{"af":"Die sosiaal gekonstrueerde rolle, gedrag en verwagtinge wat 'n samelewing aan mans en vroue koppel.","en":"The socially constructed roles, behaviour and expectations that a society links to men and women."}},{"term":{"af":"Manlikheid","en":"Masculinity"},"def":{"af":"Eienskappe en gedrag wat 'n samelewing as tipies manlik beskou.","en":"Qualities and behaviour that a society regards as typically male."}},{"term":{"af":"Vroulikheid","en":"Femininity"},"def":{"af":"Eienskappe en gedrag wat 'n samelewing as tipies vroulik beskou.","en":"Qualities and behaviour that a society regards as typically female."}},{"term":{"af":"Genderstereotipe","en":"Gender stereotype"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste, oorvereenvoudigde idee oor hoe mans of vroue moet wees of wat hulle moet doen.","en":"A fixed, oversimplified idea about how men or women should be or what they should do."}},{"term":{"af":"Mag","en":"Power"},"def":{"af":"Die vermoë om ander mense of 'n situasie te beïnvloed of te beheer.","en":"The ability to influence or control other people or a situation."}},{"term":{"af":"Magsverhoudinge","en":"Power relations"},"def":{"af":"Die manier waarop mag tussen mense in 'n verhouding of groep verdeel is – gebalanseerd of ongebalanseerd.","en":"The way power is divided between people in a relationship or group – balanced or unbalanced."}},{"term":{"af":"Magsmisbruik","en":"Abuse of power"},"def":{"af":"Om mag te gebruik om ander te benadeel, bv. deur afknouery, dwang of intimidasie.","en":"Using power to harm others, e.g. through bullying, coercion or intimidation."}},{"term":{"af":"Gendergebaseerde geweld (GGG)","en":"Gender-based violence (GBV)"},"def":{"af":"Geweld teen 'n persoon weens hulle gender, bv. geweld teen vroue en meisies.","en":"Violence against a person because of their gender, e.g. violence against women and girls."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskermingsbevel","en":"Protection order"},"def":{"af":"'n Hofbevel (landdroshof, Wet op Gesinsgeweld 116 van 1998) wat 'n oortreder verbied om die slagoffer te mishandel of te kontak.","en":"A court order (magistrate's court, Domestic Violence Act 116 of 1998) that forbids an abuser from abusing or contacting the victim."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Onderskei tussen geslag en gender (4)","en":"Distinguish between sex and gender (4)"},"problem":{"af":"Onderskei tussen *geslag* en *gender*. Gee by elkeen 'n voorbeeld. (4)","en":"Distinguish between *sex* and *gender*. Give an example of each. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Definisie 1 (1): Geslag is biologies – dit word bepaal deur chromosome, voortplantingsorgane en hormone.","en":"Definition 1 (1): Sex is biological – it is determined by chromosomes, reproductive organs and hormones."},{"af":"Voorbeeld (1): Net vroue kan swanger word en borsvoed.","en":"Example (1): Only women can fall pregnant and breastfeed."},{"af":"Definisie 2 (1): Gender is sosiaal gekonstrueer – die rolle en verwagtinge wat die samelewing aan mans en vroue koppel; dit word aangeleer.","en":"Definition 2 (1): Gender is socially constructed – the roles and expectations society links to men and women; it is learnt."},{"af":"Voorbeeld (1): Die idee dat net mans die broodwinner of net vroue die kok moet wees. Toets: kan dit verander? Ja → gender. Nee → geslag.","en":"Example (1): The idea that only men should be the breadwinner or only women the cook. Test: can it change? Yes → gender. No → sex."}],"answer":{"af":"Geslag = biologies (bv. swangerskap); gender = sosiaal en aangeleer (bv. 'die man is die broodwinner').","en":"Sex = biological (e.g. pregnancy); gender = social and learnt (e.g. 'the man is the breadwinner')."}},{"title":{"af":"Drie genderstereotipes en hulle gevolge (6)","en":"Three gender stereotypes and their effects (6)"},"problem":{"af":"Noem DRIE genderstereotipes en verduidelik by elkeen hoe dit 'n tiener se keuses kan beperk. (6)","en":"Name THREE gender stereotypes and explain for each how it can limit a teen's choices. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"Stereotipe 1 (1) + gevolg (1): \"Seuns huil nie.\" → 'n Seun steek sy gevoelens weg en vra nie hulp nie, wat tot stres of woede kan lei.","en":"Stereotype 1 (1) + effect (1): \"Boys don't cry.\" → A boy hides his feelings and doesn't ask for help, which can lead to stress or anger."},{"af":"Stereotipe 2 (1) + gevolg (1): \"Ingenieurswese is 'n mansberoep.\" → 'n Meisie wat goed is in Wiskunde en Fisiese Wetenskappe kies dalk nie die vakke of loopbaan nie.","en":"Stereotype 2 (1) + effect (1): \"Engineering is a man's job.\" → A girl who is good at Maths and Physical Sciences may not choose those subjects or that career."},{"af":"Stereotipe 3 (1) + gevolg (1): \"Huiswerk is vrouewerk.\" → Meisies kry minder tyd vir studie en sport, en seuns leer nie om vir hulself te sorg nie.","en":"Stereotype 3 (1) + effect (1): \"Housework is women's work.\" → Girls get less time for study and sport, and boys don't learn to look after themselves."}],"answer":{"af":"Bv. \"Seuns huil nie\", \"Ingenieurswese is vir mans\", \"Huiswerk is vrouewerk\" – elkeen met 'n verduidelikte gevolg.","en":"E.g. \"Boys don't cry\", \"Engineering is for men\", \"Housework is women's work\" – each with an explained effect."}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: ongelyke mag in 'n verhouding (6)","en":"Source question: unequal power in a relationship (6)"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron: *Naledi (16) en Sipho (19) is ses maande lank saam. Sipho gaan haar foon elke dag deur, sê vir haar watter klere sy mag dra en raak kwaad as sy tyd saam met haar vriendinne deurbring. Naledi sê: \"Ek is bang om nee vir hom te sê.\"* (a) Identifiseer TWEE bronne van mag wat Sipho het. (2) (b) Verduidelik hoe hierdie ongelyke magsverhouding tot gendergebaseerde geweld kan lei. (4)","en":"Read the source: *Naledi (16) and Sipho (19) have been together for six months. Sipho checks her phone every day, tells her which clothes she may wear and gets angry when she spends time with her friends. Naledi says: \"I'm scared to say no to him.\"* (a) Identify TWO sources of power that Sipho has. (2) (b) Explain how this unequal power relationship can lead to gender-based violence. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ouderdom – hy is drie jaar ouer (1); gender/beheer – hy tree op asof hy as man die reg het om haar te beheer (1).","en":"(a) Age – he is three years older (1); gender/control – he acts as if he, as the man, has the right to control her (1)."},{"af":"(b) Stap 1 (1): Sipho beheer haar foon, klere en vriende – hy isoleer haar van mense wat haar kan help.","en":"(b) Step 1 (1): Sipho controls her phone, clothes and friends – he isolates her from people who could help her."},{"af":"Stap 2 (1): Naledi raak bang en afhanklik; sy kan nie meer \"nee\" sê of haar mening gee nie.","en":"Step 2 (1): Naledi becomes afraid and dependent; she can no longer say \"no\" or give her opinion."},{"af":"Stap 3 (2): Omdat hy glo hy het die reg om te beheer en sy nie kan weier nie, kan die emosionele misbruik oorgaan in dreigemente, fisieke geweld of seksuele dwang.","en":"Step 3 (2): Because he believes he has the right to control and she cannot refuse, the emotional abuse can turn into threats, physical violence or sexual coercion."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ouderdom; gender/beheer. (b) Beheer en isolasie → vrees en afhanklikheid → sy kan nie weier nie → risiko van emosionele, fisieke of seksuele geweld.","en":"(a) Age; gender/control. (b) Control and isolation → fear and dependence → she cannot refuse → risk of emotional, physical or sexual violence."}},{"title":{"af":"Beveel strategieë aan (8)","en":"Recommend strategies (8)"},"problem":{"af":"Afdeling C-styl: Beveel in 'n paragraaf VIER strategieë aan wat Naledi (uit die vorige bron) kan gebruik om haarself te beskerm. (8)","en":"Section C style: In a paragraph, recommend FOUR strategies that Naledi (from the previous source) can use to protect herself. (8)"},"steps":[{"af":"Strategie 1 (2): Wees selfgeldend – sê kalm en duidelik vir Sipho dat sy nie aanvaar dat hy haar foon deursoek of haar vriende verbied nie.","en":"Strategy 1 (2): Be assertive – tell Sipho calmly and clearly that she does not accept him searching her phone or forbidding her friends."},{"af":"Strategie 2 (2): Praat met 'n vertroude volwassene, haar ouers of die skoolberader, sodat sy nie alleen is nie en iemand haar kan help beplan.","en":"Strategy 2 (2): Talk to a trusted adult, her parents or the school counsellor, so that she is not alone and someone can help her plan."},{"af":"Strategie 3 (2): Bel die GGG-bevelsentrum (0800 428 428) of Childline (116) vir gratis, vertroulike raad; in nood die SAPD (10111).","en":"Strategy 3 (2): Call the GBV Command Centre (0800 428 428) or Childline (116) for free, confidential advice; in an emergency SAPS (10111)."},{"af":"Strategie 4 (2): As hy haar dreig of mishandel, kan sy by die landdroshof aansoek doen om 'n beskermingsbevel (Wet op Gesinsgeweld 116 van 1998) en die verhouding beëindig.","en":"Strategy 4 (2): If he threatens or abuses her, she can apply to the magistrate's court for a protection order (Domestic Violence Act 116 of 1998) and end the relationship."}],"answer":{"af":"Selfgelding; praat met 'n vertroude volwassene; hulplyne (0800 428 428, 116, 10111); beskermingsbevel en die verhouding beëindig.","en":"Assertiveness; talk to a trusted adult; helplines (0800 428 428, 116, 10111); protection order and ending the relationship."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een word biologies bepaal?","en":"Which one is biologically determined?"},"options":[{"af":"Genderrolle","en":"Gender roles"},{"af":"Genderstereotipes","en":"Gender stereotypes"},{"af":"Vroulikheid","en":"Femininity"},{"af":"Geslag","en":"Sex"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Geslag word deur chromosome, voortplantingsorgane en hormone bepaal. Genderrolle, stereotipes en vroulikheid word deur die samelewing gevorm en aangeleer.","en":"Sex is determined by chromosomes, reproductive organs and hormones. Gender roles, stereotypes and femininity are shaped by society and learnt."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die rolle, gedrag en verwagtinge wat 'n samelewing aan mans en vroue koppel, word ___ genoem.","en":"The roles, behaviour and expectations that a society links to men and women are called ___."},"answers":{"af":["gender"],"en":["gender"]},"explain":{"af":"Gender is sosiaal gekonstrueer en aangeleer. Geslag is die biologiese verskil.","en":"Gender is socially constructed and learnt. Sex is the biological difference."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geslag","mag","chromosome"],"en":["sex","power","chromosomes"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Gender word aangeleer en kan tussen kulture en oor tyd verskil.","en":"Gender is learnt and can differ between cultures and over time."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Wat as \"manlik\" of \"vroulik\" gesien word, verskil van kultuur tot kultuur en verander oor tyd – daarom is gender sosiaal gekonstrueer.","en":"True. What is seen as \"male\" or \"female\" differs from culture to culture and changes over time – that is why gender is socially constructed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer vind die 16 Dae van Aktivisme teen geweld teen vroue en kinders plaas?","en":"When do the 16 Days of Activism for no violence against women and children take place?"},"options":[{"af":"1–16 Desember","en":"1–16 December"},{"af":"25 November – 10 Desember","en":"25 November – 10 December"},{"af":"9–25 Augustus","en":"9–25 August"},{"af":"21 Maart – 6 April","en":"21 March – 6 April"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die veldtog loop van 25 November (Internasionale Dag vir die Uitskakeling van Geweld teen Vroue) tot 10 Desember (Internasionale Menseregtedag).","en":"The campaign runs from 25 November (International Day for the Elimination of Violence against Women) to 10 December (International Human Rights Day)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Vaste, oorvereenvoudigde idee oor 'n hele groep mense word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A fixed, oversimplified idea about a whole group of people is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["stereotipe","stereotiep"],"en":["stereotype"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Stereotipe plak een etiket op almal in 'n groep, bv. \"seuns huil nie\". Dit ignoreer dat elke mens uniek is.","en":"A stereotype sticks one label on everyone in a group, e.g. \"boys don't cry\". It ignores that every person is unique."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rolmodel","tradisie","statistiek"],"en":["role model","tradition","statistic"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is 'n voorbeeld van 'n genderstereotipe?","en":"Which statement is an example of a gender stereotype?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Net vroue kan swanger word.\"","en":"\"Only women can fall pregnant.\""},{"af":"\"Seuns huil nie.\"","en":"\"Boys don't cry.\""},{"af":"\"Mans produseer sperm.\"","en":"\"Men produce sperm.\""},{"af":"\"Vroue kan borsvoed.\"","en":"\"Women can breastfeed.\""}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die ander drie is biologiese feite (geslagsverskille in voortplanting). \"Seuns huil nie\" is 'n aangeleerde verwagting wat nie vir alle seuns waar is nie.","en":"The other three are biological facts (sex differences in reproduction). \"Boys don't cry\" is a learnt expectation that is not true for all boys."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke bron van mag by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each source of power to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ouderdom","en":"Age"},"r":{"af":"'n Matriekleerder beveel 'n Graad 8 om sy tas te dra","en":"A matric learner orders a Grade 8 to carry his bag"}},{"l":{"af":"Geld","en":"Money"},"r":{"af":"Iemand betaal vir almal se kos en verwag dat hulle sy besluite volg","en":"Someone pays for everyone's food and expects them to follow his decisions"}},{"l":{"af":"Posisie","en":"Position"},"r":{"af":"'n Prefek gee strafwerk","en":"A prefect gives detention work"}},{"l":{"af":"Fisieke krag","en":"Physical strength"},"r":{"af":"'n Groter seun dreig om 'n kleiner seun te slaan","en":"A bigger boy threatens to hit a smaller boy"}}],"explain":{"af":"Mag kan uit verskillende bronne kom. Dit is nie op sigself sleg nie – dit word misbruik wanneer dit gebruik word om ander te benadeel.","en":"Power can come from different sources. It is not bad in itself – it is abused when it is used to harm others."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kragtens watter wet kan 'n slagoffer van gesinsgeweld by die landdroshof aansoek doen om 'n beskermingsbevel?","en":"Under which Act can a victim of domestic violence apply to the magistrate's court for a protection order?"},"options":[{"af":"Gelykheidswet 4 van 2000","en":"Equality Act 4 of 2000"},{"af":"Kinderwet 38 van 2005","en":"Children's Act 38 of 2005"},{"af":"Wet op Gesinsgeweld 116 van 1998","en":"Domestic Violence Act 116 of 1998"},{"af":"Wet op Seksuele Misdrywe 32 van 2007","en":"Sexual Offences Act 32 of 2007"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Wet op Gesinsgeweld 116 van 1998 maak voorsiening vir beskermingsbevele. Die ander wette is ook bestaande wette, maar handel oor gelykheid, kinders en seksuele misdrywe.","en":"The Domestic Violence Act 116 of 1998 provides for protection orders. The other Acts also exist, but deal with equality, children and sexual offences."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Slagoffer van gesinsgeweld kan by die landdroshof aansoek doen om 'n ___.","en":"A victim of domestic violence can apply to the magistrate's court for a ___."},"answers":{"af":["beskermingsbevel","beskermingsbevele"],"en":["protection order","protectionorder"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Beskermingsbevel verbied die oortreder om die slagoffer te mishandel, te dreig of te kontak. As hy die bevel verbreek, kan hy gearresteer word.","en":"A protection order forbids the abuser from abusing, threatening or contacting the victim. If he breaks the order, he can be arrested."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dagvaarding","borgtog","skeibrief"],"en":["summons","bail","divorce order"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Om iemand te dwing om iets te doen deur hulle te dreig, is 'n voorbeeld van 'n gebalanseerde magsverhouding.","en":"Forcing someone to do something by threatening them is an example of a balanced power relationship."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is dwang en intimidasie – magsmisbruik. In 'n gebalanseerde verhouding tel albei se menings en word besluite saam geneem.","en":"False. That is coercion and intimidation – abuse of power. In a balanced relationship both opinions count and decisions are made together."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Baie meisies hou in die hoërskool op met sport. Watter rede hou verband met LIGGAAMSBEELD?","en":"Many girls stop playing sport in high school. Which reason is linked to BODY IMAGE?"},"options":[{"af":"Die skool het nie 'n netbalbaan nie.","en":"The school has no netball court."},{"af":"Oefening eindig eers na donker.","en":"Practice only ends after dark."},{"af":"Vrouesport kry min televisiedekking.","en":"Women's sport gets little television coverage."},{"af":"Sy skaam haar oor hoe sy in stywe sportklere lyk.","en":"She is embarrassed about how she looks in tight sports clothes."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Al vier is redes waarom meisies ophou, maar net die skaamte oor hoe sy lyk, gaan oor liggaamsbeeld. Die ander gaan oor fasiliteite, veiligheid en media-dekking.","en":"All four are reasons why girls drop out, but only the embarrassment about how she looks is about body image. The others are about facilities, safety and media coverage."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Geweld teen iemand weens hulle gender (bv. omdat sy 'n vrou is) word ___ geweld genoem.","en":"Violence against someone because of their gender (e.g. because she is a woman) is called ___ violence."},"answers":{"af":["gendergebaseerde","geslagsgebaseerde","gender-gebaseerde","GGG"],"en":["gender-based","gender based","GBV"]},"explain":{"af":"Gendergebaseerde geweld (GGG) word dikwels gedryf deur ongelyke mag en die idee dat een gender die ander mag beheer.","en":"Gender-based violence (GBV) is often driven by unequal power and the idea that one gender may control the other."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["xenofobiese","rassistiese","politieke"],"en":["xenophobic","racist","political"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die tolvrye nommer van die GGG-bevelsentrum is ___.","en":"The toll-free number of the GBV Command Centre is ___."},"answers":{"af":["0800 428 428","0800428428"],"en":["0800 428 428","0800428428"]},"explain":{"af":"0800 428 428 is die GGG-bevelsentrum (24 uur). 10111 is die SAPD, 116 is Childline en 10177 is vir ambulans en brandweer.","en":"0800 428 428 is the GBV Command Centre (24 hours). 10111 is SAPS, 116 is Childline and 10177 is for ambulance and fire services."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10111","116","10177"],"en":["10111","116","10177"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho gaan Naledi se foon elke dag deur en verbied haar om haar vriendinne te sien. Watter stelling verduidelik die beste hoe dit tot GGG kan lei?","en":"Sipho checks Naledi's phone every day and forbids her to see her friends. Which statement best explains how this can lead to GBV?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat hy haar beheer en isoleer, raak sy bang en afhanklik; sy kan nie meer weier of hulp vra nie, en die beheer kan oorgaan in emosionele en fisieke geweld.","en":"Because he controls and isolates her, she becomes afraid and dependent; she can no longer refuse or ask for help, and the control can turn into emotional and physical violence."},{"af":"Sipho is net jaloers omdat hy baie lief is vir haar.","en":"Sipho is just jealous because he loves her a lot."},{"af":"Naledi het meer mag in die verhouding omdat sy jonger is.","en":"Naledi has more power in the relationship because she is younger."},{"af":"Dit is 'n privaat saak tussen twee mense en het niks met geweld te doen nie.","en":"It is a private matter between two people and has nothing to do with violence."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die regte antwoord wys die skakel: beheer en isolasie → vrees en afhanklikheid → sy kan nie weier nie → geweld. Om beheer as \"liefde\" of 'n \"privaat saak\" af te maak, is juis hoe misbruik versteek word.","en":"The correct answer shows the link: control and isolation → fear and dependence → she cannot refuse → violence. Dismissing control as \"love\" or a \"private matter\" is exactly how abuse is hidden."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom verhoog genderongelykheid die risiko van MIV-infeksie?","en":"Why does gender inequality increase the risk of HIV infection?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat MIV net vroue aantas.","en":"Because HIV only affects women."},{"af":"Omdat mans immuun is teen MIV.","en":"Because men are immune to HIV."},{"af":"Omdat die maat met minder mag dalk nie op kondoomgebruik kan aandring of seks kan weier nie.","en":"Because the partner with less power may not be able to insist on condom use or refuse sex."},{"af":"Omdat kondome net by hospitale beskikbaar is.","en":"Because condoms are only available at hospitals."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"MIV tas almal aan en niemand is immuun nie. Die risiko styg wanneer een maat nie kan onderhandel oor veiliger seks nie – dit is 'n gevolg van ongelyke mag.","en":"HIV affects everyone and nobody is immune. The risk rises when one partner cannot negotiate safer sex – a result of unequal power."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thandi (15) vertel jou dat haar kêrel dreig om haar seer te maak as sy die verhouding beëindig. Watter raad is die BESTE?","en":"Thandi (15) tells you that her boyfriend threatens to hurt her if she ends the relationship. Which advice is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"Bly by hom sodat hy nie kwaad word nie.","en":"Stay with him so that he doesn't get angry."},{"af":"Vertel 'n vertroude volwassene of die skoolberader, bel die GGG-bevelsentrum (0800 428 428) of Childline (116), en doen by die landdroshof aansoek om 'n beskermingsbevel.","en":"Tell a trusted adult or the school counsellor, call the GBV Command Centre (0800 428 428) or Childline (116), and apply to the magistrate's court for a protection order."},{"af":"Konfronteer hom self in die skoolgang voor almal.","en":"Confront him yourself in the school corridor in front of everyone."},{"af":"Moenie vir enigiemand vertel nie – dit sal dit net erger maak.","en":"Don't tell anyone – it will only make it worse."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Dreigement is 'n vorm van misbruik. Die beste raad kombineer ondersteuning (vertroude volwassene), kundige hulp (hulplyne) en wetlike beskerming (beskermingsbevel). Stilbly of hom alleen konfronteer kan haar in groter gevaar plaas.","en":"A threat is a form of abuse. The best advice combines support (trusted adult), expert help (helplines) and legal protection (protection order). Keeping quiet or confronting him alone can put her in greater danger."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t1-selfkennis-vakkeuses","title":{"af":"Selfkennis, vakkeuses en loopbaanvelde","en":"Knowledge of self, subject choices and career fields"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal jou belangstellings en vermoëns aan loopbaanvelde kan koppel, die NSS-slaagvereistes kan toepas en 'n netto salaris kan bereken.","en":"You will be able to link your interests and abilities to career fields, apply the NSC pass requirements and calculate a net salary."},"summary":{"af":"## Ken jouself\n\nGoeie vak- en loopbaankeuses begin by **selfkennis**:\n\n- **Belangstellings** – wat jy graag doen (bv. rekenaars, diere, mense help).\n- **Vermoëns** – waarin jy reeds goed is (bv. Wiskunde, met jou hande werk).\n- **Talente** – natuurlike gawes (bv. sang, teken, sport).\n- **Sterk punte** – eienskappe soos geduld, deursettingsvermoë of leierskap.\n- **Waardes** – wat vir jou belangrik is (bv. om ander te help, sekuriteit, kreatiwiteit).\n- **Persoonlikheid** – bv. Holland se **RIASEC**-kodes:\n\n| Kode | Tipe | Hou van | Voorbeelde van beroepe |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R | Realisties | met die hande, masjiene, buitelug | elektrisiën, boer |\n| I | Ondersoekend | navorsing, probleme ontleed | wetenskaplike, dokter |\n| A | Artistiek | kreatiwiteit, selfuitdrukking | grafiese ontwerper, musikant |\n| S | Sosiaal | mense help en leer | onderwyser, verpleegkundige |\n| E | Ondernemend | lei, oorreed, verkoop | entrepreneur, bestuurder |\n| C | Konvensioneel | orde, syfers, reëls | rekenmeester, administrateur |\n\n## Vier begrippe wat jy moet kan onderskei\n\n| Begrip | Betekenis | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Loopbaanveld** | 'n Breë groep verwante beroepe | Gesondheidswetenskappe |\n| **Beroep** | 'n Spesifieke soort werk wat spesifieke vaardighede vra | Verpleegkundige |\n| **Loopbaan** | Die reeks werke/beroepe en jou vordering oor jou hele werkslewe | Verpleegkundige → senior verpleegkundige → kliniekbestuurder |\n| **Werk/pos** | 'n Spesifieke betaalde posisie by 'n werkgewer | Verpleegkundige by 'n kliniek in Brits |\n\n## Vakkeuses vir die NSS\n\nVir die Nasionale Senior Sertifikaat (NSS) neem jy **7 vakke**: Huistaal, Eerste Addisionele Taal, Wiskunde óf Wiskundige Geletterdheid, Lewensoriëntering en **3 keusevakke**.\n\nJou vakkeuse maak deure oop of toe. Ingenieurswese en geneeskunde vra byvoorbeeld **Wiskunde** (nie Wiskundige Geletterdheid nie) en **Fisiese Wetenskappe**. Kyk altyd na die toelatingsvereistes van die universiteit of kollege voordat jy kies.\n\n### NSS-slaagvlakke (einde van Graad 12)\n\n| Slaagvlak | Vereistes |\n|---|---|\n| Hoër Sertifikaat | 40% Huistaal, 40% in twee ander vakke, 30% in drie ander vakke |\n| Diploma | 40% Huistaal, 40% in vier ander hoëkrediet-vakke (nie LO nie), 30% in twee ander vakke |\n| Baccalaureus (graad) | 40% Huistaal, 50% in vier hoëkrediet-vakke (nie LO nie), 30% in twee ander vakke |\n\nVir 'n diploma- en baccalaureusslaag moet jy ook minstens **30% in die taal van leer en onderrig** behaal.\n\n### Bevordering in Graad 10 en 11\n\n40% in die Huistaal en in twee ander vakke, en 30% in drie ander vakke. Jy mag dus **een vak druip** en steeds bevorder word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** LO tel nie by die \"vier hoëkrediet-vakke\" vir 'n diploma of graad nie. Streep LO eers deur voordat jy tel.\n\n## Besluitneming\n\n1. Identifiseer die besluit.\n2. Versamel inligting.\n3. Lys die opsies.\n4. Weeg die gevolge op (voor- en nadele).\n5. Kies die beste opsie.\n6. Tree op (doen dit).\n7. Evalueer die besluit.\n\n## Lewensdomeine\n\n| Domein | Aspekte |\n|---|---|\n| **Wees** | fisies, psigologies, spiritueel – wie jy is |\n| **Behoort** | fisies (jou omgewing), sosiaal, gemeenskap – waar en by wie jy inpas |\n| **Word** | prakties, ontspanning, groei – wat jy doen om jou doelwitte te bereik |\n\n'n Goeie loopbaankeuse pas by al drie: dit pas by wie jy is, by jou gemeenskap en by hoe jy wil groei.\n\n## Sosio-ekonomiese faktore\n\n- **Gemeenskapsbehoeftes** – watter vaardighede is nodig (bv. verpleegkundiges, onderwysers, elektrisiëns en ingenieurs by die myne naby Brits)?\n- **Finansies en bekostigbaarheid** – klasgeld, verblyf, vervoer en boeke. Opsies: **beurse**, **NSFAS** (Nasionale Finansiële Hulpskema vir Studente), studielenings en **leerlingskappe** (werk en leer terselfdertyd).\n- **Stereotipering** – \"dis nie 'n werk vir 'n meisie/seun nie\".\n- **Toeganklikheid** – afstand na 'n kampus, internettoegang en gestremdheid.\n\n## Bruto en netto salaris\n\n**Netto salaris = bruto salaris − aftrekkings**\n\n- **LBS** (Lopende Betaalstelsel, *PAYE*) – inkomstebelasting wat die werkgewer namens SAID inhou.\n- **WVF** (Werkloosheidsversekeringsfonds, *UIF*) – **1%** van jou bruto salaris.\n- **Pensioen-** of voorsorgfondsbydrae.\n- **Mediese fonds**.\n\n> **Wenk:** 'n Pos wat R20 000 per maand adverteer, gee die *bruto* salaris. Wat jy in die hand kry, is minder. Bereken elke aftrekking apart, tel hulle op en trek die totaal van die bruto salaris af.","en":"## Know yourself\n\nGood subject and career choices start with **knowledge of self**:\n\n- **Interests** – what you like doing (e.g. computers, animals, helping people).\n- **Abilities** – what you are already good at (e.g. Maths, working with your hands).\n- **Talents** – natural gifts (e.g. singing, drawing, sport).\n- **Strengths** – qualities such as patience, perseverance or leadership.\n- **Values** – what is important to you (e.g. helping others, security, creativity).\n- **Personality** – e.g. Holland's **RIASEC** codes:\n\n| Code | Type | Likes | Examples of occupations |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R | Realistic | hands-on work, machines, outdoors | electrician, farmer |\n| I | Investigative | research, analysing problems | scientist, doctor |\n| A | Artistic | creativity, self-expression | graphic designer, musician |\n| S | Social | helping and teaching people | teacher, nurse |\n| E | Enterprising | leading, persuading, selling | entrepreneur, manager |\n| C | Conventional | order, numbers, rules | accountant, administrator |\n\n## Four concepts you must be able to distinguish\n\n| Concept | Meaning | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Career field** | A broad group of related occupations | Health sciences |\n| **Occupation** | A specific type of work that needs specific skills | Nurse |\n| **Career** | The series of jobs/occupations and your progress over your whole working life | Nurse → senior nurse → clinic manager |\n| **Job** | A specific paid position with an employer | Nurse at a clinic in Brits |\n\n## Subject choices for the NSC\n\nFor the National Senior Certificate (NSC) you take **7 subjects**: Home Language, First Additional Language, Mathematics or Mathematical Literacy, Life Orientation and **3 electives**.\n\nYour subject choice opens or closes doors. Engineering and medicine, for example, require **Mathematics** (not Mathematical Literacy) and **Physical Sciences**. Always check the admission requirements of the university or college before you choose.\n\n### NSC pass levels (end of Grade 12)\n\n| Pass level | Requirements |\n|---|---|\n| Higher Certificate | 40% Home Language, 40% in two other subjects, 30% in three other subjects |\n| Diploma | 40% Home Language, 40% in four other high-credit subjects (not LO), 30% in two other subjects |\n| Bachelor's (degree) | 40% Home Language, 50% in four high-credit subjects (not LO), 30% in two other subjects |\n\nFor a diploma or bachelor's pass you must also get at least **30% in the language of learning and teaching**.\n\n### Promotion in Grades 10 and 11\n\n40% in the Home Language and in two other subjects, and 30% in three other subjects. So you may **fail one subject** and still be promoted.\n\n> **Common mistake:** LO does not count towards the \"four high-credit subjects\" for a diploma or degree. Cross out LO first before you count.\n\n## Decision-making\n\n1. Identify the decision.\n2. Gather information.\n3. List the options.\n4. Weigh the consequences (pros and cons).\n5. Choose the best option.\n6. Act (do it).\n7. Evaluate the decision.\n\n## Life domains\n\n| Domain | Aspects |\n|---|---|\n| **Being** | physical, psychological, spiritual – who you are |\n| **Belonging** | physical (your environment), social, community – where and with whom you fit in |\n| **Becoming** | practical, leisure, growth – what you do to reach your goals |\n\nA good career choice fits all three: it suits who you are, your community and how you want to grow.\n\n## Socio-economic factors\n\n- **Community needs** – which skills are needed (e.g. nurses, teachers, electricians and engineers at the mines near Brits)?\n- **Finances and affordability** – fees, accommodation, transport and books. Options: **bursaries**, **NSFAS** (National Student Financial Aid Scheme), study loans and **learnerships** (work and learn at the same time).\n- **Stereotyping** – \"that's not a job for a girl/boy\".\n- **Accessibility** – distance to a campus, internet access and disability.\n\n## Gross and net salary\n\n**Net salary = gross salary − deductions**\n\n- **PAYE** (Pay As You Earn) – income tax that the employer withholds on behalf of SARS.\n- **UIF** (Unemployment Insurance Fund) – **1%** of your gross salary.\n- **Pension** or provident fund contribution.\n- **Medical aid**.\n\n> **Tip:** A job advertised at R20 000 per month gives the *gross* salary. What you take home is less. Calculate each deduction separately, add them up and subtract the total from the gross salary."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Loopbaanveld","en":"Career field"},"def":{"af":"'n Breë groep verwante beroepe, bv. gesondheidswetenskappe of ingenieurswese.","en":"A broad group of related occupations, e.g. health sciences or engineering."}},{"term":{"af":"Beroep","en":"Occupation"},"def":{"af":"'n Spesifieke soort werk wat spesifieke kennis en vaardighede vra, bv. verpleegkundige.","en":"A specific type of work that needs specific knowledge and skills, e.g. nurse."}},{"term":{"af":"Loopbaan","en":"Career"},"def":{"af":"Die reeks werke of beroepe en die vordering wat jy oor jou hele werkslewe maak.","en":"The series of jobs or occupations and the progress you make over your whole working life."}},{"term":{"af":"Werk/pos","en":"Job"},"def":{"af":"'n Spesifieke betaalde posisie by 'n werkgewer.","en":"A specific paid position with an employer."}},{"term":{"af":"Vermoë","en":"Ability"},"def":{"af":"Iets wat jy reeds goed kan doen, of die vaardigheid wat jy kan ontwikkel.","en":"Something you can already do well, or a skill you can develop."}},{"term":{"af":"Nasionale Senior Sertifikaat (NSS)","en":"National Senior Certificate (NSC)"},"def":{"af":"Die kwalifikasie wat jy aan die einde van Graad 12 ontvang as jy aan die slaagvereistes voldoen.","en":"The qualification you receive at the end of Grade 12 if you meet the pass requirements."}},{"term":{"af":"NSFAS","en":"NSFAS"},"def":{"af":"Die Nasionale Finansiële Hulpskema vir Studente wat studente uit gesinne met 'n lae inkomste help om naskoolse studie te betaal.","en":"The National Student Financial Aid Scheme, which helps students from low-income households pay for post-school study."}},{"term":{"af":"Leerlingskap","en":"Learnership"},"def":{"af":"'n Program waarin jy by 'n werkgewer werk en terselfdertyd vir 'n erkende kwalifikasie leer.","en":"A programme in which you work for an employer and at the same time study for a recognised qualification."}},{"term":{"af":"Bruto salaris","en":"Gross salary"},"def":{"af":"Jou totale salaris voordat enige aftrekkings gemaak word.","en":"Your total salary before any deductions are made."}},{"term":{"af":"Netto salaris","en":"Net salary"},"def":{"af":"Die bedrag wat jy in die hand kry nadat aftrekkings (LBS, WVF, pensioen, mediese fonds) afgetrek is.","en":"The take-home amount after deductions (PAYE, UIF, pension, medical aid) have been subtracted."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Onderskei die vier begrippe (4)","en":"Distinguish the four concepts (4)"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik die beroep *elektrisiën* om tussen 'n loopbaanveld, 'n beroep, 'n loopbaan en 'n werk/pos te onderskei. (4)","en":"Use the occupation *electrician* to distinguish between a career field, an occupation, a career and a job. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Loopbaanveld (1): ingenieurswese en tegnologie/ambagte – die breë groep waarin elektrisiëns val.","en":"Career field (1): engineering and technology/trades – the broad group into which electricians fall."},{"af":"Beroep (1): elektrisiën – 'n spesifieke soort werk wat spesifieke vaardighede vra (bedrading, foutsporing, veiligheidsreëls).","en":"Occupation (1): electrician – a specific type of work that needs specific skills (wiring, fault-finding, safety rules)."},{"af":"Loopbaan (1): leerling-elektrisiën → gekwalifiseerde elektrisiën → toesighouer → eie elektriese besigheid – die reeks en vordering oor jare.","en":"Career (1): apprentice electrician → qualified electrician → supervisor → own electrical business – the series and progress over years."},{"af":"Werk/pos (1): elektrisiën by 'n platinummyn naby Brits – een spesifieke betaalde posisie by een werkgewer.","en":"Job (1): electrician at a platinum mine near Brits – one specific paid position with one employer."}],"answer":{"af":"Veld = breë groep; beroep = soort werk; loopbaan = reeks en vordering oor jou werkslewe; pos = spesifieke betaalde posisie.","en":"Field = broad group; occupation = type of work; career = series and progress over your working life; job = specific paid position."}},{"title":{"af":"Pas die slaagvereistes toe","en":"Apply the pass requirements"},"problem":{"af":"Ruan se Graad 12-uitslae: Afrikaans HT 58%, English EAT 52%, Wiskunde 45%, LO 72%, Fisiese Wetenskappe 41%, Lewenswetenskappe 55%, Geografie 48%. Watter NSS-slaagvlak het hy behaal? Motiveer.","en":"Ruan's Grade 12 results: Afrikaans HL 58%, English FAL 52%, Mathematics 45%, LO 72%, Physical Sciences 41%, Life Sciences 55%, Geography 48%. Which NSC pass level did he achieve? Motivate."},"steps":[{"af":"Toets eers baccalaureus: hy het 50% nodig in vier hoëkrediet-vakke (nie LO nie). Net English (52%) en Lewenswetenskappe (55%) is 50% of meer – selfs saam met Afrikaans HT is dit net drie. Geen graadslaag nie.","en":"First test bachelor's: he needs 50% in four high-credit subjects (not LO). Only English (52%) and Life Sciences (55%) are 50% or more – even with Afrikaans HL it is only three. No degree pass."},{"af":"Toets diploma: Huistaal 58% ≥ 40% ✓. Vier ander vakke (nie LO nie) ≥ 40%: English 52, Wiskunde 45, Fisiese Wetenskappe 41, Lewenswetenskappe 55 (en Geografie 48) ✓.","en":"Test diploma: Home Language 58% ≥ 40% ✓. Four other subjects (not LO) ≥ 40%: English 52, Maths 45, Physical Sciences 41, Life Sciences 55 (and Geography 48) ✓."},{"af":"Twee ander vakke ≥ 30%: LO 72 en Geografie 48 ✓. Taal van leer en onderrig ≥ 30% ✓.","en":"Two other subjects ≥ 30%: LO 72 and Geography 48 ✓. Language of learning and teaching ≥ 30% ✓."},{"af":"Gevolgtrekking: hy voldoen aan al die diplomavereistes, maar nie aan die baccalaureusvereistes nie.","en":"Conclusion: he meets all the diploma requirements, but not the bachelor's requirements."}],"answer":{"af":"Diplomaslaag – hy het nie 50% in vier hoëkrediet-vakke vir 'n baccalaureusslaag nie.","en":"Diploma pass – he does not have 50% in four high-credit subjects for a bachelor's pass."}},{"title":{"af":"Bereken die netto salaris","en":"Calculate the net salary"},"problem":{"af":"Nomsa werk as administratiewe klerk. Haar bruto salaris is R16 500 per maand. Aftrekkings: LBS R1 850, WVF 1% van die bruto salaris, pensioen 7,5% van die bruto salaris en mediese fonds R1 400. Bereken haar netto salaris.","en":"Nomsa works as an administrative clerk. Her gross salary is R16 500 per month. Deductions: PAYE R1 850, UIF 1% of the gross salary, pension 7.5% of the gross salary and medical aid R1 400. Calculate her net salary."},"steps":[{"af":"WVF = 1% × R16 500 = 0,01 × 16 500 = R165,00","en":"UIF = 1% × R16 500 = 0.01 × 16 500 = R165.00"},{"af":"Pensioen = 7,5% × R16 500 = 0,075 × 16 500 = R1 237,50","en":"Pension = 7.5% × R16 500 = 0.075 × 16 500 = R1 237.50"},{"af":"Totale aftrekkings = R1 850 + R165 + R1 237,50 + R1 400 = R4 652,50","en":"Total deductions = R1 850 + R165 + R1 237.50 + R1 400 = R4 652.50"},{"af":"Netto salaris = bruto − aftrekkings = R16 500 − R4 652,50 = R11 847,50","en":"Net salary = gross − deductions = R16 500 − R4 652.50 = R11 847.50"}],"answer":{"af":"Netto salaris = R11 847,50 per maand","en":"Net salary = R11 847.50 per month"}},{"title":{"af":"Gee raad oor vakkeuse (8)","en":"Advise on subject choice (8)"},"problem":{"af":"Lindiwe (Gr 10) wil dokter word. Sy oorweeg dit om van Wiskunde na Wiskundige Geletterdheid oor te skakel, want haar vriendinne sê dit is makliker. Gebruik die stappe van besluitneming om haar raad te gee. (8)","en":"Lindiwe (Gr 10) wants to become a doctor. She is thinking of switching from Mathematics to Mathematical Literacy because her friends say it is easier. Use the steps of decision-making to advise her. (8)"},"steps":[{"af":"Identifiseer die besluit en versamel inligting (2): Moet sy Wiskunde hou? Kyk na universiteite se toelatingsvereistes vir MBChB – hulle vra Wiskunde en Fisiese Wetenskappe, nie Wiskundige Geletterdheid nie.","en":"Identify the decision and gather information (2): Should she keep Maths? Check universities' admission requirements for MBChB – they require Mathematics and Physical Sciences, not Mathematical Literacy."},{"af":"Lys die opsies (2): (a) skakel oor en verloor die geleentheid om medies te studeer; (b) hou Wiskunde en kry ekstra hulp; (c) ondersoek verwante beroepe in die gesondheidsveld.","en":"List the options (2): (a) switch and lose the chance to study medicine; (b) keep Maths and get extra help; (c) research related occupations in the health field."},{"af":"Weeg die gevolge op (2): Opsie (a) maak die deur na geneeskunde toe; opsie (b) vra harde werk, maar hou haar droom oop.","en":"Weigh the consequences (2): Option (a) closes the door to medicine; option (b) takes hard work, but keeps her dream open."},{"af":"Kies, tree op en evalueer (2): Hou Wiskunde, gaan na ekstra klasse of 'n studiegroep, gebruik gratis bronne soos Siyavula, en evalueer haar punte na elke kwartaal. Kies vakke op grond van jou loopbaan, nie jou vriende nie.","en":"Choose, act and evaluate (2): Keep Maths, attend extra classes or a study group, use free resources such as Siyavula, and evaluate her marks after each term. Choose subjects based on your career, not your friends."}],"answer":{"af":"Sy moet Wiskunde en Fisiese Wetenskappe hou, hulp kry en haar vordering evalueer – oorskakel sal geneeskunde as opsie uitskakel.","en":"She should keep Mathematics and Physical Sciences, get help and evaluate her progress – switching would rule out medicine as an option."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n loopbaanveld?","en":"Which one is a career field?"},"options":[{"af":"Verpleegkundige","en":"Nurse"},{"af":"Gesondheidswetenskappe","en":"Health sciences"},{"af":"'n Pos as verpleegkundige by 'n kliniek in Brits","en":"A position as a nurse at a clinic in Brits"},{"af":"Begin as verpleegkundige en word later kliniekbestuurder","en":"Start as a nurse and later become a clinic manager"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Loopbaanveld is 'n breë groep verwante beroepe. Verpleegkundige is 'n beroep, die pos by die kliniek is 'n werk/pos, en die vordering oor jare is 'n loopbaan.","en":"A career field is a broad group of related occupations. Nurse is an occupation, the position at the clinic is a job, and the progress over years is a career."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vir die NSS neem 'n leerder altesaam ___ vakke.","en":"For the NSC a learner takes ___ subjects in total."},"answers":{"af":["7","sewe"],"en":["7","seven"]},"explain":{"af":"Huistaal, Eerste Addisionele Taal, Wiskunde of Wiskundige Geletterdheid, LO en drie keusevakke = 7.","en":"Home Language, First Additional Language, Mathematics or Mathematical Literacy, LO and three electives = 7."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6","8","9"],"en":["6","8","9"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Wiskundige Geletterdheid is genoeg om vir 'n ingenieursgraad toegelaat te word.","en":"Mathematical Literacy is enough to be admitted to an engineering degree."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Ingenieurswese vereis Wiskunde (en Fisiese Wetenskappe). Daarom is vakkeuse in Graad 9 en 10 so belangrik.","en":"False. Engineering requires Mathematics (and Physical Sciences). That is why subject choice in Grades 9 and 10 is so important."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Volgens Holland se RIASEC-kodes is iemand wat graag mense help en leer, watter tipe?","en":"According to Holland's RIASEC codes, someone who likes helping and teaching people is which type?"},"options":[{"af":"Realisties","en":"Realistic"},{"af":"Konvensioneel","en":"Conventional"},{"af":"Sosiaal","en":"Social"},{"af":"Ondersoekend","en":"Investigative"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Sosiale tipe (S) hou daarvan om met mense te werk, bv. onderwysers en verpleegkundiges. Realisties = met die hande; konvensioneel = orde en syfers; ondersoekend = navorsing.","en":"The Social type (S) likes working with people, e.g. teachers and nurses. Realistic = hands-on; conventional = order and numbers; investigative = research."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die reeks werke en die vordering wat jy oor jou hele werkslewe maak, is jou ___.","en":"The series of jobs and the progress you make over your whole working life is your ___."},"answers":{"af":["loopbaan"],"en":["career"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Loopbaan strek oor baie jare en kan verskeie poste en selfs beroepe insluit.","en":"A career stretches over many years and can include several jobs and even occupations."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["beroep","loopbaanveld","pos"],"en":["occupation","career field","job"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Bruto salaris min aftrekkings is gelyk aan die ...","en":"Gross salary minus deductions is equal to the ..."},"options":[{"af":"netto salaris.","en":"net salary."},{"af":"bruto salaris.","en":"gross salary."},{"af":"inkomstebelasting.","en":"income tax."},{"af":"bonus.","en":"bonus."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die netto salaris is wat jy in die hand kry. Die bruto salaris is die bedrag vóór aftrekkings; inkomstebelasting (LBS) is een van die aftrekkings.","en":"The net salary is your take-home pay. The gross salary is the amount before deductions; income tax (PAYE) is one of the deductions."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"WVF (UIF) word teen ___% van die bruto salaris afgetrek.","en":"UIF is deducted at ___% of the gross salary."},"answers":{"af":["1","1%","een"],"en":["1","1%","one"]},"explain":{"af":"Die werknemer betaal 1% van sy bruto salaris aan die WVF (en die werkgewer dra nog 1% by).","en":"The employee pays 1% of his gross salary to the UIF (and the employer contributes another 1%)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","15","0,5"],"en":["10","15","0.5"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lewensdomein by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each life domain to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Wees","en":"Being"},"r":{"af":"Jou fisiese, psigologiese en spirituele self – wie jy is","en":"Your physical, psychological and spiritual self – who you are"}},{"l":{"af":"Behoort","en":"Belonging"},"r":{"af":"Jou verbintenis met jou omgewing, ander mense en die gemeenskap","en":"Your connection with your environment, other people and the community"}},{"l":{"af":"Word","en":"Becoming"},"r":{"af":"Praktiese aktiwiteite, ontspanning en groei om jou doelwitte te bereik","en":"Practical activities, leisure and growth to reach your goals"}}],"explain":{"af":"Wees = wie jy is; behoort = waar en by wie jy inpas; word = wat jy doen om te groei.","en":"Being = who you are; belonging = where and with whom you fit in; becoming = what you do to grow."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stap van besluitneming kom direk ná \"versamel inligting\"?","en":"Which step of decision-making comes directly after \"gather information\"?"},"options":[{"af":"Kies die beste opsie","en":"Choose the best option"},{"af":"Evalueer die besluit","en":"Evaluate the decision"},{"af":"Tree op","en":"Act"},{"af":"Lys die opsies","en":"List the options"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die volgorde is: identifiseer → versamel inligting → lys opsies → weeg gevolge op → kies → tree op → evalueer. Jy kan eers kies nadat jy die opsies gelys en opgeweeg het.","en":"The order is: identify → gather information → list options → weigh consequences → choose → act → evaluate. You can only choose after listing and weighing the options."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In Graad 10 en 11 kan 'n leerder een vak druip en steeds bevorder word, mits hy aan die ander bevorderingsvereistes voldoen.","en":"In Grades 10 and 11 a learner can fail one subject and still be promoted, provided he meets the other promotion requirements."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Hy het 40% in die Huistaal en twee ander vakke nodig en 30% in drie ander vakke – dit is ses van die sewe vakke.","en":"True. He needs 40% in the Home Language and two other subjects, and 30% in three other subjects – that is six of the seven subjects."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die skema van die regering wat studente uit gesinne met 'n lae inkomste help om naskoolse studie te betaal, is ___ (afkorting).","en":"The government scheme that helps students from low-income households pay for post-school study is ___ (abbreviation)."},"answers":{"af":["NSFAS"],"en":["NSFAS"]},"explain":{"af":"NSFAS = Nasionale Finansiële Hulpskema vir Studente. SAID is die belastingowerheid, SAKO is die kwalifikasie-owerheid en die WVF is vir werkloosheid.","en":"NSFAS = National Student Financial Aid Scheme. SARS is the tax authority, SAQA is the qualifications authority and UIF is for unemployment."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["SAID","SAKO","WVF"],"en":["SARS","SAQA","UIF"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter se Graad 11-punte: Afrikaans HT 45%, English EAT 38%, Wiskunde 35%, LO 60%, Geografie 42%, Lewenswetenskappe 41%, RTT 28%. Word hy bevorder?","en":"Pieter's Grade 11 marks: Afrikaans HL 45%, English FAL 38%, Maths 35%, LO 60%, Geography 42%, Life Sciences 41%, CAT 28%. Is he promoted?"},"options":[{"af":"Nee – hy het RTT gedruip.","en":"No – he failed CAT."},{"af":"Ja – Huistaal en twee ander vakke is bo 40%, drie ander is bo 30% en hy druip net een vak.","en":"Yes – Home Language and two other subjects are above 40%, three others are above 30% and he fails only one subject."},{"af":"Nee – hy het nie 50% in vier vakke nie.","en":"No – he does not have 50% in four subjects."},{"af":"Nee – sy Huistaal is onder 50%.","en":"No – his Home Language is below 50%."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Huistaal 45% ≥ 40% ✓; Geografie 42% en Lewenswetenskappe 41% ≥ 40% ✓; English 38%, Wiskunde 35% en LO 60% ≥ 30% ✓. Een vak (RTT) mag gedruip word. Die 50%-reël geld net vir 'n baccalaureusslaag in Graad 12.","en":"Home Language 45% ≥ 40% ✓; Geography 42% and Life Sciences 41% ≥ 40% ✓; English 38%, Maths 35% and LO 60% ≥ 30% ✓. One subject (CAT) may be failed. The 50% rule applies only to a bachelor's pass in Grade 12."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Werker se bruto salaris is R10 000 en sy totale aftrekkings is R2 350. Sy netto salaris is R___.","en":"A worker's gross salary is R10 000 and his total deductions are R2 350. His net salary is R___."},"answers":{"af":["7650","7 650","7650,00","7 650,00"],"en":["7650","7 650","7650.00","7 650.00"]},"explain":{"af":"Netto = bruto − aftrekkings = R10 000 − R2 350 = R7 650. Moenie die aftrekkings bytel nie (R12 350).","en":"Net = gross − deductions = R10 000 − R2 350 = R7 650. Don't add the deductions (R12 350)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["12 350","7 350","10 000"],"en":["12 350","7 350","10 000"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Aisha se Graad 12-uitslae: Afrikaans HT 62%, English EAT 55%, Wiskunde 51%, LO 80%, Fisiese Wetenskappe 53%, Lewenswetenskappe 57%, Geografie 39%. Watter slaagvlak het sy behaal?","en":"Aisha's Grade 12 results: Afrikaans HL 62%, English FAL 55%, Maths 51%, LO 80%, Physical Sciences 53%, Life Sciences 57%, Geography 39%. Which pass level did she achieve?"},"options":[{"af":"Hoër Sertifikaat","en":"Higher Certificate"},{"af":"Diploma, omdat Geografie onder 40% is","en":"Diploma, because Geography is below 40%"},{"af":"Gedruip, omdat een vak onder 40% is","en":"Failed, because one subject is below 40%"},{"af":"Baccalaureus (graad)","en":"Bachelor's (degree)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sonder LO en die Huistaal het sy vier vakke ≥ 50% (English 55, Wiskunde 51, Fisiese Wetenskappe 53, Lewenswetenskappe 57), Huistaal 62% ≥ 40%, en twee ander vakke ≥ 30% (LO 80, Geografie 39). Geografie hoef net 30% te wees.","en":"Without LO and the Home Language she has four subjects ≥ 50% (English 55, Maths 51, Physical Sciences 53, Life Sciences 57), Home Language 62% ≥ 40%, and two other subjects ≥ 30% (LO 80, Geography 39). Geography only needs 30%."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sizwe wil 'n elektrisiën word, maar die naaste TVET-kollege is 80 km van sy dorpie af en hy het nie internet by die huis nie. Watter sosio-ekonomiese faktor beïnvloed sy keuse die meeste?","en":"Sizwe wants to become an electrician, but the nearest TVET college is 80 km from his village and he has no internet at home. Which socio-economic factor influences his choice most?"},"options":[{"af":"Gemeenskapsbehoeftes","en":"Community needs"},{"af":"Toeganklikheid","en":"Accessibility"},{"af":"Stereotipering","en":"Stereotyping"},{"af":"Inkomstebelasting","en":"Income tax"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Afstand en gebrek aan internet maak dit moeilik om by die kollege uit te kom en aansoek te doen – dit is toeganklikheid. Niks in die scenario gaan oor stereotipes of belasting nie.","en":"Distance and a lack of internet make it hard to get to the college and to apply – that is accessibility. Nothing in the scenario is about stereotypes or tax."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lindiwe wil dokter word, maar wil Wiskunde vir Wiskundige Geletterdheid verruil omdat dit makliker is. Watter raad is die BESTE?","en":"Lindiwe wants to become a doctor, but wants to swap Maths for Mathematical Literacy because it is easier. Which advice is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"Ruil om – 'n hoër gemiddeld is belangriker as die vakke wat jy neem.","en":"Swap – a higher average is more important than the subjects you take."},{"af":"Kies dieselfde vakke as jou vriendinne sodat julle saam kan studeer.","en":"Choose the same subjects as your friends so you can study together."},{"af":"Hou Wiskunde en Fisiese Wetenskappe, kry ekstra hulp, kyk na die universiteit se toelatingsvereistes en ondersoek ook verwante gesondheidsberoepe.","en":"Keep Maths and Physical Sciences, get extra help, check the university's admission requirements and also research related health occupations."},{"af":"Los ook Fisiese Wetenskappe en neem makliker vakke.","en":"Drop Physical Sciences as well and take easier subjects."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Geneeskunde vereis Wiskunde en Fisiese Wetenskappe; om oor te skakel maak die deur toe. Die beste raad gebruik besluitneming: inligting, opsies, gevolge en 'n plan om haar punte te verbeter.","en":"Medicine requires Mathematics and Physical Sciences; switching closes the door. The best advice uses decision-making: information, options, consequences and a plan to improve her marks."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t1-diversiteit-menseregte","title":{"af":"Diversiteit, diskriminasie en menseregteskendings","en":"Diversity, discrimination and human rights violations"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal vooroordeel, stereotipes en diskriminasie kan herken, die geskende reg en artikel in 'n scenario kan identifiseer en weet waar om skendings aan te meld.","en":"You will be able to recognise prejudice, stereotypes and discrimination, identify the violated right and section in a scenario and know where to report violations."},"summary":{"af":"## Kernbegrippe\n\n- **Diversiteit** – die verskille tussen mense, bv. ras, kultuur, taal, godsdiens, gender, ouderdom, vermoë en of jy van die platteland of die stad kom.\n- **Stereotipe** – 'n vaste, oorvereenvoudigde idee oor 'n hele groep (\"Alle buitelanders is misdadigers\").\n- **Vooroordeel** – 'n negatiewe houding of oordeel oor iemand *voordat* jy hulle ken, net omdat hulle aan 'n sekere groep behoort.\n- **Partydigheid** – 'n eensydige voorkeur vir of teen 'n groep of standpunt, wat 'n regverdige oordeel verhinder.\n- **Diskriminasie** – om iemand onregverdig te *behandel* weens die groep waaraan hulle behoort. Vooroordeel is 'n *houding*; diskriminasie is 'n *daad*.\n  - **Direk:** openlik, bv. \"Ons verhuur nie aan buitelanders nie.\"\n  - **Indirek:** 'n reël wat neutraal lyk, maar 'n groep benadeel, bv. 'n reël wat alle kopbedekkings verbied en sekere gelowiges benadeel.\n  - **Onbillik:** diskriminasie op gronde soos ras, gender, swangerskap, ouderdom, gestremdheid, godsdiens, kultuur, taal of seksuele oriëntasie is verbode (a 9(3)).\n- **Menseregteskending** – wanneer iemand se regte, soos in die Grondwet beskryf, geskend of nie gerespekteer word nie.\n\n## Kontekste van diskriminasie\n\nRas, godsdiens, kultuur, taal, gender, ouderdom, plattelands of stedelik, gestremdheid, seksuele oriëntasie en **MIV- en vigs-status** (bv. iemand word afgedank omdat hy MIV-positief is).\n\n- **Xenofobie** – vrees vir of haat teenoor mense van ander lande. Gevolge vir **individue**: vrees, beserings, verlies van huise, besighede en inkomste. Gevolge vir die **samelewing**: geweld, verdeeldheid, skade aan die ekonomie en aan Suid-Afrika se beeld.\n- **Mensehandel** – mense word gewerf, vervoer en uitgebuit (bv. dwangarbeid of seksuele uitbuiting). Patroon: **werwing → vervoer → uitbuiting**. Lokvalle: vals werk- of modelaanbiedinge op sosiale media wat te goed is om waar te wees. Wet: **Wet op die Voorkoming en Bestryding van Handel in Persone 7 van 2013**.\n\n## Die Grondwet en die Handves van Regte\n\nDie **Grondwet** (Wet 108 van 1996) is die **hoogste wet** van Suid-Afrika. Nelson Mandela het dit op **10 Desember 1996** by **Sharpeville** onderteken. Die **Handves van Regte** (Handves van Menseregte) is **Hoofstuk 2**.\n\n| Artikel | Reg |\n|---|---|\n| 9 | Gelykheid |\n| 10 | Menswaardigheid |\n| 11 | Lewe |\n| 12 | Vryheid en sekerheid van die persoon |\n| 14 | Privaatheid |\n| 15 | Godsdiens-, geloofs- en meningsvryheid |\n| 16 | Vryheid van uitdrukking |\n| 24 | Omgewing |\n| 27 | Gesondheidsorg, voedsel, water en maatskaplike sekerheid |\n| 28 | Kinders |\n| 29 | Onderwys |\n| 30 | Taal en kultuur |\n\n- **Regte en verantwoordelikhede** gaan saam: jou reg op onderwys beteken jy moet ook ander se reg om te leer respekteer.\n- Regte kan **beperk** word (**artikel 36**) as dit redelik en regverdigbaar is in 'n oop en demokratiese samelewing.\n- **Vryheid van uitdrukking** sluit NIE in nie (**a 16(2)**): propaganda vir oorlog, aanhitsing tot dreigende geweld en haatspraak.\n\n## Internasionale dokumente\n\n- Universele Verklaring van Menseregte (VN, **1948**)\n- CEDAW – Konvensie oor die Uitskakeling van Alle Vorme van Diskriminasie teen Vroue (**1979**)\n- VN-Konvensie oor die Regte van die Kind (**1989**)\n- Afrika-handves oor die Regte en Welsyn van die Kind (**1990**)\n\n## Wie beskerm ons regte?\n\n- **Hoofstuk 9-instellings:** die Suid-Afrikaanse Menseregtekommissie (SAMRK), die Openbare Beskermer, die Kommissie vir Geslagsgelykheid en die CRL-regtekommissie (regte van kultuur-, godsdiens- en taalgemeenskappe).\n- Die **Gelykheidswet** (PEPUDA, Wet 4 van 2000) en die **Gelykheidshowe** – vir klagtes oor onbillike diskriminasie en haatspraak.\n- Die **SAPD** – vir misdade soos aanranding of mensehandel.\n- **NRO's** (nie-regeringsorganisasies) wat slagoffers ondersteun.\n\n## Die media en partydigheid\n\nNuus en sosiale media kan stereotipes **versterk** of **uitdaag**. Tekens van partydigheid:\n\n- **eensydig** – net een kant van die storie word vertel;\n- **emosionele woorde** – \"oorstroom\", \"indringers\", \"skandalig\";\n- **selektiewe feite** – feite wat nie in die storie pas nie, word weggelaat;\n- **veralgemenings** – \"almal\", \"hulle is altyd\".\n\n## Diskriminasie uitdaag\n\nPraat op, rapporteer dit (by die skool, die SAMRK, 'n Gelykheidshof of die SAPD), ondersteun veldtogte en help om 'n nasie te bou: **Menseregtedag (21 Maart)**, **Versoeningsdag (16 Desember)** en die Springbokke se Rugbywêreldbeker-oorwinnings (1995, 2007, 2019 en 2023), wat Suid-Afrikaners van alle agtergronde saamgebring het.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** In 'n scenario-vraag skryf leerders net \"sy regte is geskend\". Noem die **spesifieke reg en artikel**, bv. \"a 14 – privaatheid\", en verduidelik hoekom.","en":"## Key concepts\n\n- **Diversity** – the differences between people, e.g. race, culture, language, religion, gender, age, ability and whether you come from a rural or urban area.\n- **Stereotype** – a fixed, oversimplified idea about a whole group (\"All foreigners are criminals\").\n- **Prejudice** – a negative attitude or judgement about someone *before* you know them, only because they belong to a certain group.\n- **Bias** – a one-sided preference for or against a group or point of view, which prevents a fair judgement.\n- **Discrimination** – *treating* someone unfairly because of the group they belong to. Prejudice is an *attitude*; discrimination is an *action*.\n  - **Direct:** open, e.g. \"We don't rent to foreigners.\"\n  - **Indirect:** a rule that seems neutral but disadvantages a group, e.g. a rule that bans all head coverings and disadvantages certain believers.\n  - **Unfair:** discrimination on grounds such as race, gender, pregnancy, age, disability, religion, culture, language or sexual orientation is prohibited (s 9(3)).\n- **Human rights violation** – when someone's rights, as described in the Constitution, are violated or not respected.\n\n## Contexts of discrimination\n\nRace, religion, culture, language, gender, age, rural or urban, disability, sexual orientation and **HIV and AIDS status** (e.g. someone is dismissed because he is HIV-positive).\n\n- **Xenophobia** – fear or hatred of people from other countries. Effects on **individuals**: fear, injuries, loss of homes, businesses and income. Effects on **society**: violence, division, damage to the economy and to South Africa's image.\n- **Human trafficking** – people are recruited, transported and exploited (e.g. forced labour or sexual exploitation). Pattern: **recruitment → transport → exploitation**. Traps: fake job or modelling offers on social media that are too good to be true. Law: **Prevention and Combating of Trafficking in Persons Act 7 of 2013**.\n\n## The Constitution and the Bill of Rights\n\nThe **Constitution** (Act 108 of 1996) is the **supreme law** of South Africa. Nelson Mandela signed it on **10 December 1996** at **Sharpeville**. The **Bill of Rights** is **Chapter 2**.\n\n| Section | Right |\n|---|---|\n| 9 | Equality |\n| 10 | Human dignity |\n| 11 | Life |\n| 12 | Freedom and security of the person |\n| 14 | Privacy |\n| 15 | Freedom of religion, belief and opinion |\n| 16 | Freedom of expression |\n| 24 | Environment |\n| 27 | Health care, food, water and social security |\n| 28 | Children |\n| 29 | Education |\n| 30 | Language and culture |\n\n- **Rights and responsibilities** go together: your right to education means you must also respect others' right to learn.\n- Rights can be **limited** (**section 36**) if it is reasonable and justifiable in an open and democratic society.\n- **Freedom of expression** does NOT include (**s 16(2)**): propaganda for war, incitement of imminent violence and hate speech.\n\n## International instruments\n\n- Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UN, **1948**)\n- CEDAW – Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women (**1979**)\n- UN Convention on the Rights of the Child (**1989**)\n- African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child (**1990**)\n\n## Who protects our rights?\n\n- **Chapter 9 institutions:** the South African Human Rights Commission (SAHRC), the Public Protector, the Commission for Gender Equality and the CRL Rights Commission (rights of cultural, religious and linguistic communities).\n- The **Equality Act** (PEPUDA, Act 4 of 2000) and the **Equality Courts** – for complaints about unfair discrimination and hate speech.\n- **SAPS** – for crimes such as assault or human trafficking.\n- **NGOs** (non-governmental organisations) that support victims.\n\n## The media and bias\n\nNews and social media can **reinforce** or **challenge** stereotypes. Signs of bias:\n\n- **one-sided** – only one side of the story is told;\n- **emotive words** – \"flood\", \"invaders\", \"disgraceful\";\n- **selective facts** – facts that don't fit the story are left out;\n- **generalisations** – \"everyone\", \"they always\".\n\n## Challenging discrimination\n\nSpeak up, report it (to the school, the SAHRC, an Equality Court or SAPS), support campaigns and help build the nation: **Human Rights Day (21 March)**, **Day of Reconciliation (16 December)** and the Springboks' Rugby World Cup wins (1995, 2007, 2019 and 2023), which brought South Africans of all backgrounds together.\n\n> **Common mistake:** In a scenario question learners only write \"his rights were violated\". Name the **specific right and section**, e.g. \"s 14 – privacy\", and explain why."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Diversiteit","en":"Diversity"},"def":{"af":"Die verskille tussen mense, bv. ras, kultuur, taal, godsdiens, gender, ouderdom en vermoë.","en":"The differences between people, e.g. race, culture, language, religion, gender, age and ability."}},{"term":{"af":"Vooroordeel","en":"Prejudice"},"def":{"af":"'n Negatiewe houding of oordeel oor iemand voordat jy hulle ken, net omdat hulle aan 'n sekere groep behoort.","en":"A negative attitude or judgement about someone before you know them, only because they belong to a certain group."}},{"term":{"af":"Stereotipe","en":"Stereotype"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste, oorvereenvoudigde idee oor 'n hele groep mense.","en":"A fixed, oversimplified idea about a whole group of people."}},{"term":{"af":"Partydigheid","en":"Bias"},"def":{"af":"'n Eensydige voorkeur vir of teen 'n groep of standpunt, wat 'n regverdige oordeel verhinder.","en":"A one-sided preference for or against a group or point of view, which prevents a fair judgement."}},{"term":{"af":"Diskriminasie","en":"Discrimination"},"def":{"af":"Om iemand onregverdig te behandel weens die groep waaraan hulle behoort – direk of indirek.","en":"Treating someone unfairly because of the group they belong to – directly or indirectly."}},{"term":{"af":"Menseregteskending","en":"Human rights violation"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer iemand se regte in die Grondwet geskend of nie gerespekteer word nie.","en":"When someone's rights in the Constitution are violated or not respected."}},{"term":{"af":"Xenofobie","en":"Xenophobia"},"def":{"af":"Vrees vir of haat teenoor mense van ander lande.","en":"Fear or hatred of people from other countries."}},{"term":{"af":"Mensehandel","en":"Human trafficking"},"def":{"af":"Die werwing en vervoer van mense met die doel om hulle uit te buit, bv. vir dwangarbeid of seksuele uitbuiting.","en":"Recruiting and transporting people in order to exploit them, e.g. for forced labour or sexual exploitation."}},{"term":{"af":"Handves van Regte","en":"Bill of Rights"},"def":{"af":"Hoofstuk 2 van die Grondwet (Wet 108 van 1996), wat die regte van alle mense in Suid-Afrika beskerm.","en":"Chapter 2 of the Constitution (Act 108 of 1996), which protects the rights of all people in South Africa."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofstuk 9-instellings","en":"Chapter 9 institutions"},"def":{"af":"Onafhanklike instellings wat demokrasie en menseregte beskerm, bv. die SAMRK, die Openbare Beskermer en die Kommissie vir Geslagsgelykheid.","en":"Independent institutions that protect democracy and human rights, e.g. the SAHRC, the Public Protector and the Commission for Gender Equality."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die geskende reg (4)","en":"Identify the violated right (4)"},"problem":{"af":"Noem by elke scenario die reg (en artikel) wat geskend word: (a) 'n Fabriek naby Brits stort giftige afval in die Krokodilrivier. (b) 'n Onderwyser lees 'n leerder se privaat boodskappe hardop in die klas voor. (c) 'n Skool weier om 'n leerder toe te laat omdat sy MIV-positief is. (d) 'n Groep leerders spot 'n seun daagliks oor sy aksent en noem hom neerhalende name.","en":"For each scenario, name the right (and section) that is violated: (a) A factory near Brits dumps toxic waste into the Crocodile River. (b) A teacher reads a learner's private messages aloud in class. (c) A school refuses to admit a learner because she is HIV-positive. (d) A group of learners mock a boy every day about his accent and call him insulting names."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) a 24 – omgewing: almal het die reg op 'n omgewing wat nie skadelik vir hulle gesondheid is nie. (1)","en":"(a) s 24 – environment: everyone has the right to an environment that is not harmful to their health. (1)"},{"af":"(b) a 14 – privaatheid: niemand mag sonder rede jou kommunikasie openbaar maak nie. (1)","en":"(b) s 14 – privacy: no one may make your communications public without reason. (1)"},{"af":"(c) a 9 – gelykheid (onbillike diskriminasie weens MIV-status); ook a 29 – onderwys. (1)","en":"(c) s 9 – equality (unfair discrimination because of HIV status); also s 29 – education. (1)"},{"af":"(d) a 10 – menswaardigheid: neerhalende name en spot ondermyn sy waardigheid. (1)","en":"(d) s 10 – human dignity: insulting names and mockery undermine his dignity. (1)"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) a 24 omgewing (b) a 14 privaatheid (c) a 9 gelykheid / a 29 onderwys (d) a 10 menswaardigheid","en":"(a) s 24 environment (b) s 14 privacy (c) s 9 equality / s 29 education (d) s 10 human dignity"}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: die impak van xenofobie (6)","en":"Source question: the impact of xenophobia (6)"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die bron (eie voorbeeld): *Inwoners van 'n informele nedersetting het gisteraand winkels besit deur mense van ander lande geplunder. Mnr. Banda, wat al tien jaar 'n spazawinkel bedryf, het alles verloor. Sy kinders is te bang om skool toe te gaan.* Verduidelik die impak van xenofobie op (a) die individu (3) en (b) die samelewing (3).","en":"Read the source (own example): *Residents of an informal settlement last night looted shops owned by people from other countries. Mr Banda, who has run a spaza shop for ten years, lost everything. His children are too afraid to go to school.* Explain the impact of xenophobia on (a) the individual (3) and (b) society (3)."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ekonomies (1): Mnr. Banda verloor sy besigheid en inkomste en kan dalk nie sy gesin onderhou nie.","en":"(a) Economic (1): Mr Banda loses his business and income and may not be able to support his family."},{"af":"Emosioneel (1): vrees, trauma en onsekerheid. Regte (1): sy kinders se reg op onderwys (a 29) en die gesin se reg op veiligheid (a 12) word ingeperk.","en":"Emotional (1): fear, trauma and insecurity. Rights (1): his children's right to education (s 29) and the family's right to security (s 12) are restricted."},{"af":"(b) Die gemeenskap verloor 'n winkel en dienste (1); geweld en wantroue verdeel die samelewing (1).","en":"(b) The community loses a shop and services (1); violence and distrust divide society (1)."},{"af":"Suid-Afrika se beeld en ekonomie ly skade, bv. minder beleggers en toeriste (1).","en":"South Africa's image and economy are damaged, e.g. fewer investors and tourists (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"Individu: verlies van inkomste, vrees en trauma, geskende regte. Samelewing: verlies van dienste, verdeeldheid, skade aan ekonomie en beeld.","en":"Individual: loss of income, fear and trauma, violated rights. Society: loss of services, division, damage to the economy and image."}},{"title":{"af":"Raai 'n slagoffer waar om aan te meld (4)","en":"Advise a victim where to report (4)"},"problem":{"af":"Tumelo en sy vriende word by 'n restaurant in Hartbeespoort weggewys. Die bestuurder sê: \"Ons bedien nie julle soort nie.\" Raai hom oor wat hy kan doen en waar hy dit kan aanmeld. (4)","en":"Tumelo and his friends are turned away at a restaurant in Hartbeespoort. The manager says: \"We don't serve your kind.\" Advise him on what he can do and where he can report it. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"Herken die skending: dit is direkte, onbillike diskriminasie op grond van ras – a 9 (gelykheid) en a 10 (menswaardigheid).","en":"Recognise the violation: this is direct, unfair discrimination on the grounds of race – s 9 (equality) and s 10 (human dignity)."},{"af":"Versamel bewyse (1): skryf die datum, tyd en presiese woorde neer en kry die name en nommers van getuies.","en":"Gather evidence (1): write down the date, time and exact words and get the names and numbers of witnesses."},{"af":"Meld aan (2): lê 'n klag by die Suid-Afrikaanse Menseregtekommissie (SAMRK) of by 'n Gelykheidshof ingevolge die Gelykheidswet (Wet 4 van 2000).","en":"Report (2): lay a complaint with the South African Human Rights Commission (SAHRC) or at an Equality Court under the Equality Act (Act 4 of 2000)."},{"af":"Kry ondersteuning (1): praat met 'n vertroude volwassene en kontak 'n NRO wat slagoffers van diskriminasie help.","en":"Get support (1): talk to a trusted adult and contact an NGO that helps victims of discrimination."}],"answer":{"af":"Versamel bewyse en meld dit aan by die SAMRK of 'n Gelykheidshof (Gelykheidswet 4 van 2000); kry ondersteuning.","en":"Gather evidence and report it to the SAHRC or an Equality Court (Equality Act 4 of 2000); get support."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer 'n opskrif vir partydigheid (6)","en":"Evaluate a headline for bias (6)"},"problem":{"af":"'n Plaaslike nuuswebwerf plaas hierdie (versinde) opskrif: **\"Buitelanders oorstroom Madibeng – al ons werk is weg!\"** Evalueer die opskrif vir partydigheid en skryf 'n regverdiger weergawe. (6)","en":"A local news website posts this (made-up) headline: **\"Foreigners flood Madibeng – all our jobs are gone!\"** Evaluate the headline for bias and write a fairer version. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"Emosionele woorde (1): \"oorstroom\" laat mense soos 'n ramp klink en wek vrees.","en":"Emotive words (1): \"flood\" makes people sound like a disaster and stirs up fear."},{"af":"Veralgemening (1): \"al ons werk\" is oordrewe en word nie deur feite gesteun nie.","en":"Generalisation (1): \"all our jobs\" is exaggerated and not supported by facts."},{"af":"Eensydig en selektief (2): geen bronne, syfers of ander standpunte nie; dit ignoreer ander oorsake van werkloosheid. So 'n opskrif kan xenofobie aanblaas.","en":"One-sided and selective (2): no sources, figures or other views; it ignores other causes of unemployment. A headline like this can fuel xenophobia."},{"af":"Regverdige weergawe (2): \"Inwoners van Madibeng bespreek werkloosheid by gemeenskapsvergadering\" – neutraal, feitelik en sonder om 'n groep te blameer.","en":"Fairer version (2): \"Madibeng residents discuss unemployment at community meeting\" – neutral, factual and without blaming a group."}],"answer":{"af":"Partydig: emosionele woorde, veralgemening, eensydig, geen feite nie. Regverdiger: \"Inwoners van Madibeng bespreek werkloosheid by gemeenskapsvergadering.\"","en":"Biased: emotive words, generalisation, one-sided, no facts. Fairer: \"Madibeng residents discuss unemployment at community meeting.\""}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter hoofstuk van die Grondwet is die Handves van Regte?","en":"In which chapter of the Constitution is the Bill of Rights?"},"options":[{"af":"Hoofstuk 1","en":"Chapter 1"},{"af":"Hoofstuk 9","en":"Chapter 9"},{"af":"Hoofstuk 2","en":"Chapter 2"},{"af":"Hoofstuk 36","en":"Chapter 36"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die Handves van Regte is Hoofstuk 2. Hoofstuk 9 handel oor instellings wat demokrasie beskerm, en 36 is 'n artikel (beperking van regte), nie 'n hoofstuk nie.","en":"The Bill of Rights is Chapter 2. Chapter 9 deals with institutions that protect democracy, and 36 is a section (limitation of rights), not a chapter."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vrees vir of haat teenoor mense van ander lande word ___ genoem.","en":"Fear or hatred of people from other countries is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["xenofobie","xenofobia"],"en":["xenophobia"]},"explain":{"af":"Xenofobie is gerig op mense omdat hulle van 'n ander land kom. Rassisme gaan oor ras en seksisme oor gender.","en":"Xenophobia is aimed at people because they come from another country. Racism is about race and sexism is about gender."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rassisme","seksisme","mensehandel"],"en":["racism","sexism","human trafficking"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vooroordeel is 'n houding, terwyl diskriminasie 'n daad is.","en":"Prejudice is an attitude, while discrimination is an action."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Vooroordeel is wat jy dink of voel oor 'n groep; diskriminasie is wanneer jy iemand op grond daarvan onregverdig behandel.","en":"True. Prejudice is what you think or feel about a group; discrimination is when you treat someone unfairly because of it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Op watter datum vier Suid-Afrika Menseregtedag?","en":"On which date does South Africa celebrate Human Rights Day?"},"options":[{"af":"21 Maart","en":"21 March"},{"af":"16 Desember","en":"16 December"},{"af":"27 April","en":"27 April"},{"af":"16 Junie","en":"16 June"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Menseregtedag (21 Maart) herdenk die Sharpeville-slagting van 1960. 16 Desember is Versoeningsdag, 27 April Vryheidsdag en 16 Junie Jeugdag.","en":"Human Rights Day (21 March) commemorates the Sharpeville massacre of 1960. 16 December is Day of Reconciliation, 27 April Freedom Day and 16 June Youth Day."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Grondwet van Suid-Afrika is Wet ___ van 1996.","en":"The Constitution of South Africa is Act ___ of 1996."},"answers":{"af":["108"],"en":["108"]},"explain":{"af":"Die Grondwet is Wet 108 van 1996 en die hoogste wet van die land. Enige wet of optrede wat daarmee bots, is ongeldig.","en":"The Constitution is Act 108 of 1996 and the supreme law of the country. Any law or conduct that conflicts with it is invalid."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["116","200","32"],"en":["116","200","32"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter artikel van die Handves van Regte beskerm die reg op privaatheid?","en":"Which section of the Bill of Rights protects the right to privacy?"},"options":[{"af":"Artikel 9","en":"Section 9"},{"af":"Artikel 12","en":"Section 12"},{"af":"Artikel 16","en":"Section 16"},{"af":"Artikel 14","en":"Section 14"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"a 14 = privaatheid. a 9 = gelykheid, a 12 = vryheid en sekerheid van die persoon, a 16 = vryheid van uitdrukking.","en":"s 14 = privacy. s 9 = equality, s 12 = freedom and security of the person, s 16 = freedom of expression."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Volgens artikel ___ van die Grondwet kan regte beperk word as dit redelik en regverdigbaar is.","en":"According to section ___ of the Constitution, rights can be limited if it is reasonable and justifiable."},"answers":{"af":["36"],"en":["36"]},"explain":{"af":"Artikel 36 is die beperkingsklousule: geen reg is absoluut nie. Jou vryheid van uitdrukking word byvoorbeeld beperk sodat jy nie haatspraak mag versprei nie.","en":"Section 36 is the limitation clause: no right is absolute. Your freedom of expression, for example, is limited so that you may not spread hate speech."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["9","16","28"],"en":["9","16","28"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke internasionale dokument by die jaar waarin dit aanvaar is.","en":"Match each international instrument to the year it was adopted."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Universele Verklaring van Menseregte","en":"Universal Declaration of Human Rights"},"r":{"af":"1948","en":"1948"}},{"l":{"af":"CEDAW","en":"CEDAW"},"r":{"af":"1979","en":"1979"}},{"l":{"af":"VN-Konvensie oor die Regte van die Kind","en":"UN Convention on the Rights of the Child"},"r":{"af":"1989","en":"1989"}},{"l":{"af":"Afrika-handves oor die Regte en Welsyn van die Kind","en":"African Charter on the Rights and Welfare of the Child"},"r":{"af":"1990","en":"1990"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die Universele Verklaring (1948) kom eerste, ná die Tweede Wêreldoorlog. CEDAW (1979) beskerm vroue; die VN-konvensie (1989) en die Afrika-handves (1990) beskerm kinders.","en":"The Universal Declaration (1948) came first, after the Second World War. CEDAW (1979) protects women; the UN convention (1989) and the African Charter (1990) protect children."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Winkel plak 'n kennisgewing op: \"Geen buitelanders word hier aangestel nie.\" Watter soort diskriminasie is dit?","en":"A shop puts up a notice: \"No foreigners are employed here.\" What type of discrimination is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Indirekte diskriminasie","en":"Indirect discrimination"},{"af":"Direkte diskriminasie","en":"Direct discrimination"},{"af":"Billike diskriminasie","en":"Fair discrimination"},{"af":"Dit is nie diskriminasie nie","en":"It is not discrimination"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die reël sluit 'n groep openlik en doelbewus uit – dit is direkte diskriminasie. Indirekte diskriminasie is 'n reël wat neutraal lyk, maar 'n groep benadeel.","en":"The rule openly and deliberately excludes a group – that is direct discrimination. Indirect discrimination is a rule that seems neutral but disadvantages a group."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens artikel 16(2) beskerm vryheid van uitdrukking ook haatspraak wat aanhits om skade te doen.","en":"According to section 16(2), freedom of expression also protects hate speech that incites harm."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. a 16(2) sluit propaganda vir oorlog, aanhitsing tot dreigende geweld en haatspraak uit. Dit is 'n voorbeeld van hoe regte grense het.","en":"False. s 16(2) excludes propaganda for war, incitement of imminent violence and hate speech. This is an example of how rights have limits."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Fabriek naby Brits stort giftige afval in die Krokodilrivier waaruit mense water drink. Watter reg word die duidelikste geskend?","en":"A factory near Brits dumps toxic waste into the Crocodile River from which people drink water. Which right is most clearly violated?"},"options":[{"af":"a 14 – Privaatheid","en":"s 14 – Privacy"},{"af":"a 30 – Taal en kultuur","en":"s 30 – Language and culture"},{"af":"a 24 – Omgewing","en":"s 24 – Environment"},{"af":"a 15 – Godsdiensvryheid","en":"s 15 – Freedom of religion"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"a 24 gee almal die reg op 'n omgewing wat nie skadelik vir hulle gesondheid of welstand is nie. Die besoedeling hou ook verband met die reg op water (a 27).","en":"s 24 gives everyone the right to an environment that is not harmful to their health or well-being. The pollution is also linked to the right to water (s 27)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Mensehandel volg gewoonlik die patroon: werwing → vervoer → ___.","en":"Human trafficking usually follows the pattern: recruitment → transport → ___."},"answers":{"af":["uitbuiting"],"en":["exploitation"]},"explain":{"af":"Die doel van mensehandel is altyd uitbuiting – dwangarbeid, seksuele uitbuiting of ander misbruik. Die \"werk\" wat belowe is, bestaan nie.","en":"The aim of human trafficking is always exploitation – forced labour, sexual exploitation or other abuse. The promised \"job\" does not exist."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vrylating","opleiding","betaling"],"en":["release","training","payment"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter situasie is die waarskynlikste 'n lokval vir mensehandel?","en":"Which situation is most likely a human-trafficking trap?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Bekende maatskappy adverteer 'n pos op sy amptelike webwerf en hou onderhoude by sy kantoor.","en":"A well-known company advertises a post on its official website and holds interviews at its office."},{"af":"Jou skool hou 'n loopbaandag met plaaslike werkgewers.","en":"Your school holds a career day with local employers."},{"af":"'n Leerlingskap word geadverteer met 'n amptelike aansoekvorm en kontakbesonderhede.","en":"A learnership is advertised with an official application form and contact details."},{"af":"'n Onbekende persoon op Instagram bied jou 'n modelwerk in 'n ander stad aan met 'n hoë salaris en gratis vervoer, vra dat jy dit geheim hou en wil jou ID-dokument hê.","en":"A stranger on Instagram offers you a modelling job in another city with a high salary and free transport, asks you to keep it secret and wants your ID document."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Waarskuwingstekens: 'n onbekende persoon, 'n aanbod wat te goed is om waar te wees, gratis vervoer na 'n ander plek, geheimhouding en die vraag na jou identiteitsdokumente.","en":"Warning signs: a stranger, an offer that is too good to be true, free transport to another place, secrecy and a request for your identity documents."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Klagtes oor onbillike diskriminasie kan ingevolge die Gelykheidswet (Wet 4 van 2000) by 'n ___ aangehoor word.","en":"Complaints about unfair discrimination can be heard at an ___ under the Equality Act (Act 4 of 2000)."},"answers":{"af":["gelykheidshof","gelykheidshowe"],"en":["Equality Court","Equality Courts","equalitycourt"]},"explain":{"af":"Gelykheidshowe is spesiaal ingestel om sake oor onbillike diskriminasie, haatspraak en teistering te hanteer.","en":"Equality Courts were specially set up to deal with cases of unfair discrimination, hate speech and harassment."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kleineisehof","kinderhof","militêre hof"],"en":["Small Claims Court","Children's Court","military court"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Opskrif lui: \"Buitelanders oorstroom Madibeng – al ons werk is weg!\" Wat is die BESTE bewys dat dit partydig is?","en":"A headline reads: \"Foreigners flood Madibeng – all our jobs are gone!\" What is the BEST evidence that it is biased?"},"options":[{"af":"Die opskrif noem 'n spesifieke plek.","en":"The headline names a specific place."},{"af":"Die woord \"oorstroom\" is emosioneel en die opskrif veralgemeen sonder feite of bronne.","en":"The word \"flood\" is emotive and the headline generalises without facts or sources."},{"af":"Die opskrif is kort en kragtig.","en":"The headline is short and punchy."},{"af":"Die opskrif gebruik 'n uitroepteken, dus moet dit waar wees.","en":"The headline uses an exclamation mark, so it must be true."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Partydigheid word gewys deur emosionele woorde, veralgemenings, eensydigheid en 'n gebrek aan feite. 'n Plek noem of kort wees maak 'n opskrif nie partydig nie.","en":"Bias is shown by emotive words, generalisations, one-sidedness and a lack of facts. Naming a place or being short does not make a headline biased."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder van Zimbabwe word by jou skool afgeknou en \"gaan huis toe!\" genoem. Watter reaksie van die skool is die DOELTREFFENDSTE?","en":"A learner from Zimbabwe is bullied at your school and told to \"go home!\". Which response by the school is the MOST effective?"},"options":[{"af":"Ignoreer dit, sodat die situasie nie erger word nie.","en":"Ignore it so that the situation doesn't get worse."},{"af":"Laat die leerders dit self uitsorteer.","en":"Let the learners sort it out themselves."},{"af":"Ondersoek die saak en dissiplineer die oortreders volgens die gedragskode, gee die slagoffer berading en hou 'n bewusmakingsprogram oor diversiteit en menseregte.","en":"Investigate the matter and discipline the offenders according to the code of conduct, give the victim counselling and run an awareness programme on diversity and human rights."},{"af":"Plaas die slagoffer in 'n ander klas sodat hy uit die pad is.","en":"Move the victim to another class so that he is out of the way."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beste reaksie beskerm die slagoffer se regte (a 9 gelykheid, a 10 menswaardigheid), hou oortreders aanspreeklik en pak die oorsaak – vooroordeel – deur opvoeding aan. Om dit te ignoreer of die slagoffer te verskuif, straf eintlik die slagoffer.","en":"The best response protects the victim's rights (s 9 equality, s 10 human dignity), holds offenders accountable and tackles the cause – prejudice – through education. Ignoring it or moving the victim actually punishes the victim."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Studievaardighede; sosiale en omgewingsverantwoordelikheid","en":"Study skills; social and environmental responsibility"},"topics":[{"id":"lo10-t2-studievaardighede","title":{"af":"Studievaardighede, studieplan en eksamenskryf","en":"Study skills, study plan and exam writing"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal jou leerstyl ken, die regte studiemetodes kies, 'n studieplan opstel en slim in die eksamen werk.","en":"You will know your learning style, choose the right study methods, draw up a study plan and work smartly in the exam."},"summary":{"af":"## Studievaardighede\n\nGoed studeer is 'n vaardigheid wat jy kan aanleer. KABV noem sewe kernvaardighede:\n\n- **Luister:** gee aandag in die klas en maak notas van wat die onderwyser beklemtoon.\n- **Lees:** lees eers vinnig deur vir 'n oorsig, en dan noukeurig.\n- **Begrip:** kan jy dit wat jy gelees het in jou eie woorde verduidelik?\n- **Konsentrasie:** fokus sonder afleiding (foon weg, stil plek).\n- **Geheue:** stoor inligting sodat jy dit later kan herroep.\n- **Organisasie:** netjiese notas, lêers en 'n vaste werkplek.\n- **Tydsbestuur:** beplan jou tyd sodat alles betyds klaar is.\n\n## Leerstyle (VAK)\n\nJou **leerstyl** is die manier waarop jy die maklikste leer. Die meeste mense gebruik 'n mengsel, maar het een voorkeur.\n\n| Leerstyl | Leer die beste deur | Pas hierdie tegnieke |\n|---|---|---|\n| Visueel | te sien | breinkaarte, diagramme, kleurkodes, tabelle |\n| Ouditief | te hoor | hardop lees, opnames, groepbespreking, rympies |\n| Kinesteties | te doen en te beweeg | modelle bou, rondloop terwyl jy herhaal, flitskaarte sorteer |\n| Lees/skryf | woorde | opsommings, lyste, notas herskryf |\n\n## Studiemetodes\n\n- **Notas maak:** skryf net sleutelwoorde en hoofgedagtes neer, nie elke woord nie.\n- **Breinkaart:** die hoofonderwerp in die middel, met takke vir die subonderwerpe. Dit wys hoe idees verband hou.\n- **Sleutelbegrippe uitkies:** merk die belangrikste terme en definisies.\n- **Opsomming:** verkort 'n hoofstuk tot die kernfeite.\n- **Vergelyking:** gebruik 'n tabel of Venn-diagram vir ooreenkomste en verskille.\n- **Geheuehulpmiddels (mnemonika) en akronieme:** bv. VAK = visueel, ouditief, kinesteties.\n- **Flitskaarte:** term of vraag voor, antwoord agter.\n- **Selftoetsing en gespasieerde hersiening:** toets jouself en herhaal die werk oor 'n paar dae, eerder as om alles op die laaste aand in te prop.\n\n### Die SQ3R-metode\n\n1. **S – Survey (oorsig):** blaai deur die hoofstuk: opskrifte, prente, opsomming.\n2. **Q – Question (vra):** maak vrae van die opskrifte.\n3. **R – Read (lees):** lees aandagtig en soek die antwoorde.\n4. **R – Recite (opsê):** maak die boek toe en sê of skryf in jou eie woorde wat jy onthou.\n5. **R – Review (hersien):** gaan gereeld weer oor die werk.\n\n### 'n Werkopdrag of opstel saamstel\n\n'n **Inleiding** (waaroor dit gaan), 'n **liggaam** (een hoofgedagte per paragraaf, met voorbeelde), 'n **slot** (opsomming en eie gevolgtrekking) en 'n **bronnelys**. Om ander se werk as jou eie in te gee, is **plagiaat**.\n\n## Kritiese, kreatiewe en probleemoplossende denke\n\n1. Identifiseer die probleem.\n2. Versamel inligting.\n3. Dink aan moontlike oplossings (kreatief).\n4. Weeg die voor- en nadele op (krities).\n5. Kies die beste oplossing en voer dit uit.\n6. Evalueer die resultaat.\n\n## Die assesseringsproses\n\n- **Interne assessering:** die skool stel en merk die werk: die **SBA** (skoolgebaseerde assessering: toetse, take, projekte) en die **PAT** (praktiese assesseringstaak). Graad 10-eksamens word deur die skool of provinsie opgestel.\n- **Eksterne assessering:** die Graad 12-**NSS**-eksamen (Nasionale Senior Sertifikaat) word nasionaal opgestel en gemerk.\n- **Gewigte in Graad 10:** die meeste vakke: SBA 25% + eksamen 75%. Toerisme en Gasvryheidstudies: SBA 25% + PAT 25% + eksamen 50%. LO word intern geassesseer.\n\n## Jaarlikse studieplan en tydsbestuur\n\n1. Skryf al die toets-, taak- en eksamendatums op 'n **kwartaal- of jaarkalender**.\n2. Maak 'n **weeklikse rooster** met vaste tye vir skool, sport (bv. rugbyoefening), huiswerk, studie, ontspanning, familietyd en slaap.\n3. **Prioritiseer:** wat is eerste, wat tel die meeste, waar is jy die swakste?\n4. Werk in **kort, gefokusde sessies** (30–45 minute) met 'n kort ruskans tussenin.\n5. Beplan vir beurtkrag: laai jou foon en noodlig vooraf.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** **Uitstel** (werk vir later skuif) lei tot stres, haastige werk en swak punte. Breek 'n groot taak op in klein stappe en begin vandag met die eerste stap.\n\n## Eksamenskryf\n\n1. Lees die **hele vraestel** en al die **instruksies** eers deur.\n2. Beplan jou tyd: ongeveer **1 minuut per punt**.\n3. Beantwoord die makliker vrae eerste, maar nommer korrek.\n4. Ken die **opdragwerkwoorde**:\n\n| Werkwoord | Wat jy moet doen |\n|---|---|\n| Noem / lys | gee feite sonder verduideliking |\n| Definieer | gee die presiese betekenis |\n| Beskryf | sê in detail hoe iets lyk of werk |\n| Verduidelik | sê hoe of hoekom, met redes en voorbeelde |\n| Bespreek | kyk na verskillende kante van 'n saak |\n| Analiseer | breek dit op in dele en wys verbande |\n| Evalueer / beoordeel | weeg voor- en nadele op en gee 'n eie oordeel |\n| Bespreek krities | argumente vir en teen, met 'n gemotiveerde slot |\n| Beveel aan | stel praktiese oplossings voor |\n\n5. **Puntetoekenning = aantal punte (feite):** by \"noem\" is elke feit gewoonlik 1 punt werd.\n6. Gaan jou antwoorde aan die einde na.\n\n> **Eksamenstres:** slaap genoeg (8–10 uur), eet ontbyt, drink water, beweeg, haal diep en stadig asem as jy paniekerig voel, en moenie die aand voor die eksamen met nuwe werk begin nie.","en":"## Study skills\n\nStudying well is a skill you can learn. CAPS lists seven core skills:\n\n- **Listening:** pay attention in class and note what the teacher emphasises.\n- **Reading:** first read quickly for an overview, then carefully.\n- **Comprehension:** can you explain what you have read in your own words?\n- **Concentration:** focus without distractions (phone away, quiet place).\n- **Memory:** store information so that you can recall it later.\n- **Organisation:** neat notes, files and a fixed place to work.\n- **Time management:** plan your time so that everything is finished on time.\n\n## Learning styles (VAK)\n\nYour **learning style** is the way in which you learn most easily. Most people use a mix, but have one preference.\n\n| Learning style | Learns best by | Matching techniques |\n|---|---|---|\n| Visual | seeing | mind maps, diagrams, colour codes, tables |\n| Auditory | hearing | reading aloud, recordings, group discussion, rhymes |\n| Kinaesthetic | doing and moving | building models, walking while repeating, sorting flash cards |\n| Reading/writing | words | summaries, lists, rewriting notes |\n\n## Study methods\n\n- **Note-taking:** write down only key words and main ideas, not every word.\n- **Mind map:** the main topic in the centre with branches for the sub-topics. It shows how ideas are linked.\n- **Selecting key concepts:** mark the most important terms and definitions.\n- **Summary:** shorten a chapter to the core facts.\n- **Comparison:** use a table or Venn diagram for similarities and differences.\n- **Mnemonics and acronyms:** e.g. VAK = visual, auditory, kinaesthetic.\n- **Flash cards:** term or question on the front, answer on the back.\n- **Self-testing and spaced revision:** test yourself and repeat the work over a few days instead of cramming everything the night before.\n\n### The SQ3R method\n\n1. **S – Survey:** page through the chapter: headings, pictures, summary.\n2. **Q – Question:** turn the headings into questions.\n3. **R – Read:** read carefully and look for the answers.\n4. **R – Recite:** close the book and say or write in your own words what you remember.\n5. **R – Review:** go over the work again regularly.\n\n### Constructing an assignment or essay\n\nAn **introduction** (what it is about), a **body** (one main idea per paragraph, with examples), a **conclusion** (summary and your own conclusion) and a **list of sources**. Handing in someone else's work as your own is **plagiarism**.\n\n## Critical, creative and problem-solving thinking\n\n1. Identify the problem.\n2. Gather information.\n3. Think of possible solutions (creative).\n4. Weigh up the advantages and disadvantages (critical).\n5. Choose the best solution and carry it out.\n6. Evaluate the result.\n\n## The process of assessment\n\n- **Internal assessment:** the school sets and marks the work: the **SBA** (school-based assessment: tests, tasks, projects) and the **PAT** (practical assessment task). Grade 10 exams are set by the school or province.\n- **External assessment:** the Grade 12 **NSC** exam (National Senior Certificate) is set and marked nationally.\n- **Weightings in Grade 10:** most subjects: SBA 25% + exam 75%. Tourism and Hospitality Studies: SBA 25% + PAT 25% + exam 50%. LO is assessed internally.\n\n## Annual study plan and time management\n\n1. Write all test, task and exam dates on a **term or year calendar**.\n2. Make a **weekly timetable** with fixed times for school, sport (e.g. rugby practice), homework, study, relaxation, family time and sleep.\n3. **Prioritise:** what comes first, what counts most, where are you weakest?\n4. Work in **short, focused sessions** (30–45 minutes) with a short break in between.\n5. Plan for load-shedding: charge your phone and emergency light in advance.\n\n> **Common mistake:** **Procrastination** (putting work off until later) leads to stress, rushed work and poor marks. Break a big task into small steps and start the first step today.\n\n## Exam writing\n\n1. Read the **whole paper** and all the **instructions** first.\n2. Plan your time: about **1 minute per mark**.\n3. Answer the easier questions first, but number correctly.\n4. Know the **instruction verbs**:\n\n| Verb | What you must do |\n|---|---|\n| Name / list | give facts without explanation |\n| Define | give the exact meaning |\n| Describe | say in detail what something looks like or how it works |\n| Explain | say how or why, with reasons and examples |\n| Discuss | look at different sides of an issue |\n| Analyse | break it into parts and show the links |\n| Evaluate | weigh up advantages and disadvantages and give your own judgement |\n| Critically discuss | arguments for and against, with a motivated conclusion |\n| Recommend | suggest practical solutions |\n\n5. **Mark allocation = number of points (facts):** with \"name\", each fact is usually worth 1 mark.\n6. Check your answers at the end.\n\n> **Exam stress:** sleep enough (8–10 hours), eat breakfast, drink water, move, breathe deeply and slowly when you feel panicky, and do not start new work the night before the exam."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Leerstyl","en":"Learning style"},"def":{"af":"Die manier waarop 'n persoon die maklikste leer, bv. visueel, ouditief, kinesteties of lees/skryf.","en":"The way in which a person learns most easily, e.g. visual, auditory, kinaesthetic or reading/writing."}},{"term":{"af":"Studiemetode","en":"Study method"},"def":{"af":"'n Tegniek om leerwerk te verwerk en te onthou, bv. 'n breinkaart, opsomming of flitskaarte.","en":"A technique to process and remember learning material, e.g. a mind map, summary or flash cards."}},{"term":{"af":"Breinkaart","en":"Mind map"},"def":{"af":"'n Visuele opsomming met die hoofonderwerp in die middel en takke vir subonderwerpe en verbande.","en":"A visual summary with the main topic in the centre and branches for sub-topics and links."}},{"term":{"af":"SQ3R","en":"SQ3R"},"def":{"af":"'n Leesstudiemetode in vyf stappe: Survey (oorsig), Question (vra), Read (lees), Recite (opsê), Review (hersien).","en":"A five-step reading-study method: Survey, Question, Read, Recite, Review."}},{"term":{"af":"Geheuehulpmiddel (mnemonika)","en":"Mnemonic"},"def":{"af":"'n Truuk soos 'n akroniem, rympie of sin wat jou help om feite in volgorde te onthou.","en":"A trick such as an acronym, rhyme or sentence that helps you remember facts in order."}},{"term":{"af":"Skoolgebaseerde assessering (SBA)","en":"School-based assessment (SBA)"},"def":{"af":"Formele toetse, take en projekte deur die jaar wat deur die skool gestel en gemerk word; in die meeste Graad 10-vakke 25% van die jaarpunt.","en":"Formal tests, tasks and projects during the year, set and marked by the school; 25% of the year mark in most Grade 10 subjects."}},{"term":{"af":"Praktiese assesseringstaak (PAT)","en":"Practical assessment task (PAT)"},"def":{"af":"'n Praktiese taak in vakke soos Toerisme en Gasvryheidstudies wat 25% van die finale punt tel.","en":"A practical task in subjects such as Tourism and Hospitality Studies that counts 25% of the final mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitstel","en":"Procrastination"},"def":{"af":"Om take vir later te skuif al weet jy dit moet nou gedoen word.","en":"Putting tasks off until later even though you know they should be done now."}},{"term":{"af":"Opdragwerkwoord","en":"Instruction verb"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord in 'n vraag (bv. noem, verduidelik, evalueer) wat sê wat en hoeveel jy moet skryf.","en":"The verb in a question (e.g. name, explain, evaluate) that tells you what and how much to write."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Pas die studiemetode by die leerstyl","en":"Match the study method to the learning style"},"problem":{"af":"Drie Graad 10-leerders by Hoërskool Brits studeer vir die LO-eksamen. **Thandi** onthou die beste wat sy in prente en kleure sien. **Pieter** onthou die beste wat hy hoor en bespreek. **Kabelo** leer deur te doen en kan nie lank stilsit nie. Identifiseer elkeen se leerstyl en beveel twee studiemetodes vir elkeen aan. (9)","en":"Three Grade 10 learners at Hoërskool Brits are studying for the LO exam. **Thandi** remembers best what she sees in pictures and colours. **Pieter** remembers best what he hears and discusses. **Kabelo** learns by doing and cannot sit still for long. Identify each one's learning style and recommend two study methods for each. (9)"},"steps":[{"af":"Thandi leer deur te **sien**, dus is sy 'n **visuele** leerder. Sy kan breinkaarte met kleure maak en inligting in tabelle of diagramme opsom.","en":"Thandi learns by **seeing**, so she is a **visual** learner. She can make colourful mind maps and summarise information in tables or diagrams."},{"af":"Pieter leer deur te **hoor**, dus is hy 'n **ouditiewe** leerder. Hy kan sy notas hardop lees of opneem en daarna luister, of die werk in 'n studiegroep bespreek.","en":"Pieter learns by **hearing**, so he is an **auditory** learner. He can read his notes aloud or record them and listen afterwards, or discuss the work in a study group."},{"af":"Kabelo leer deur te **doen**, dus is hy 'n **kinestetiese** leerder. Hy kan rondloop terwyl hy definisies opsê en flitskaarte in groepe sorteer.","en":"Kabelo learns by **doing**, so he is a **kinaesthetic** learner. He can walk around while reciting definitions and sort flash cards into groups."},{"af":"Puntetoekenning: 1 punt vir elke leerstyl (3) + 1 punt vir elke gepaste metode (6) = 9.","en":"Mark allocation: 1 mark for each learning style (3) + 1 mark for each suitable method (6) = 9."}],"answer":{"af":"Thandi: visueel (breinkaarte, tabelle/diagramme); Pieter: ouditief (hardop lees/opnames, groepbespreking); Kabelo: kinesteties (beweeg terwyl hy herhaal, flitskaarte sorteer).","en":"Thandi: visual (mind maps, tables/diagrams); Pieter: auditory (reading aloud/recordings, group discussion); Kabelo: kinaesthetic (moving while repeating, sorting flash cards)."}},{"title":{"af":"Stel 'n studierooster op","en":"Draw up a study timetable"},"problem":{"af":"Dis Maandag. Jou LO-werkopdrag moet Donderdag ingehandig word, jy skryf Vrydag 'n Geskiedenistoets en volgende Dinsdag 'n Wiskundetoets. Jy het Maandae en Woensdae van 15:00 tot 17:00 rugbyoefening, en die gesin eet elke aand om 18:00. Stel 'n studieplan vir Maandag tot Donderdag op.","en":"It is Monday. Your LO assignment must be handed in on Thursday, you write a History test on Friday and a Mathematics test next Tuesday. You have rugby practice on Mondays and Wednesdays from 15:00 to 17:00, and the family eats every evening at 18:00. Draw up a study plan for Monday to Thursday."},"steps":[{"af":"**Stap 1 – Sperdatums in volgorde:** LO-taak (Do) → Geskiedenis (Vr) → Wiskunde (volgende Di). Die naaste sperdatum kry voorrang.","en":"**Step 1 – Deadlines in order:** LO task (Thu) → History (Fri) → Mathematics (next Tue). The nearest deadline gets priority."},{"af":"**Stap 2 – Blok die vaste tye:** rugby Ma en Wo 15:00–17:00; aandete elke dag 18:00–19:00.","en":"**Step 2 – Block the fixed times:** rugby Mon and Wed 15:00–17:00; dinner every day 18:00–19:00."},{"af":"**Stap 3 – Ma en Di:** Ma 17:15–18:00 LO-taak beplan en navorsing; 19:00–19:45 Geskiedenis afdeling 1 (breinkaart). Di 15:00–15:45 LO-taak skryf; ruskans; 16:00–16:45 Geskiedenis afdeling 2; 19:00–19:30 Wiskunde-oefeninge.","en":"**Step 3 – Mon and Tue:** Mon 17:15–18:00 plan and research the LO task; 19:00–19:45 History section 1 (mind map). Tue 15:00–15:45 write the LO task; break; 16:00–16:45 History section 2; 19:00–19:30 Maths exercises."},{"af":"**Stap 4 – Wo en Do:** Wo 17:15–18:00 LO-taak finaal nagaan en bronnelys; 19:00–19:45 Geskiedenis flitskaarte. Do: handig LO in; 15:00–15:45 Geskiedenis selftoets; ruskans; 16:00–16:45 Wiskunde. Die naweek: gespasieerde Wiskunde-hersiening.","en":"**Step 4 – Wed and Thu:** Wed 17:15–18:00 final check of the LO task and source list; 19:00–19:45 History flash cards. Thu: hand in LO; 15:00–15:45 History self-test; break; 16:00–16:45 Maths. Weekend: spaced Maths revision."},{"af":"**Stap 5 – Balans:** elke sessie is 30–45 minute met ruskanse, en ná 20:00 is daar tyd vir ontspanning en genoeg slaap.","en":"**Step 5 – Balance:** every session is 30–45 minutes with breaks, and after 20:00 there is time to relax and get enough sleep."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Rooster wat die naaste sperdatum eerste beplan, vaste tye respekteer, kort sessies met ruskanse gebruik en Wiskunde oor 'n paar dae versprei.","en":"A timetable that plans the nearest deadline first, respects fixed times, uses short sessions with breaks and spreads Maths over several days."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan jou tyd in die eksamen","en":"Plan your time in the exam"},"problem":{"af":"'n Vraestel tel 100 punte en jy het 2 uur (120 minute). Afdeling A tel 20 punte, Afdeling B 30 punte en Afdeling C 50 punte. Jy wil 10 minute gebruik om die vraestel deur te lees en 10 minute aan die einde om na te gaan. Hoeveel tyd moet jy aan elke afdeling bestee?","en":"A paper counts 100 marks and you have 2 hours (120 minutes). Section A counts 20 marks, Section B 30 marks and Section C 50 marks. You want to use 10 minutes to read through the paper and 10 minutes at the end to check. How much time should you spend on each section?"},"steps":[{"af":"Beskikbare skryftyd = 120 − 10 − 10 = 100 minute.","en":"Available writing time = 120 − 10 − 10 = 100 minutes."},{"af":"Tyd per punt = 100 minute ÷ 100 punte = 1 minuut per punt.","en":"Time per mark = 100 minutes ÷ 100 marks = 1 minute per mark."},{"af":"Afdeling A: 20 × 1 = 20 min; Afdeling B: 30 × 1 = 30 min; Afdeling C: 50 × 1 = 50 min. Kontrole: 20 + 30 + 50 = 100 min.","en":"Section A: 20 × 1 = 20 min; Section B: 30 × 1 = 30 min; Section C: 50 × 1 = 50 min. Check: 20 + 30 + 50 = 100 min."}],"answer":{"af":"A: 20 minute; B: 30 minute; C: 50 minute (plus 10 min lees en 10 min nagaan).","en":"A: 20 minutes; B: 30 minutes; C: 50 minutes (plus 10 min reading and 10 min checking)."}},{"title":{"af":"Bespreek krities: uitstel","en":"Critically discuss: procrastination"},"problem":{"af":"Bespreek krities hoe uitstel 'n Graad 10-leerder se studie en welstand beïnvloed. Skryf 'n paragraaf. (6)","en":"Critically discuss how procrastination affects a Grade 10 learner's studies and well-being. Write a paragraph. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Definieer** eers: uitstel is om take vir later te skuif al weet jy dit moet nou gedoen word (1).","en":"**Define** first: procrastination is putting tasks off until later even though you know they should be done now (1)."},{"af":"**Negatiewe gevolge:** werk word haastig en swak gedoen, sperdatums word gemis, en stres en angs neem toe namate die toets nader kom (2).","en":"**Negative effects:** work is done hastily and poorly, deadlines are missed, and stress and anxiety increase as the test gets closer (2)."},{"af":"**Die ander kant (krities):** sommige leerders sê hulle werk beter onder druk, maar laat-aand-inprop gee swakker langtermyngeheue en minder slaap, so die gehalte ly gewoonlik (1).","en":"**The other side (critical):** some learners say they work better under pressure, but late-night cramming gives weaker long-term memory and less sleep, so quality usually suffers (1)."},{"af":"**Oplossings en slot:** gebruik 'n studierooster, breek take in klein stappe op en sit die foon weg. Ek is van mening dat uitstel meer skade as voordeel inhou (2).","en":"**Solutions and conclusion:** use a study timetable, break tasks into small steps and put the phone away. In my opinion procrastination does more harm than good (2)."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Paragraaf met 'n definisie, negatiewe gevolge, 'n teenargument, oplossings en 'n gemotiveerde eie mening.","en":"A paragraph with a definition, negative effects, a counter-argument, solutions and a motivated personal opinion."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter leerstyl beskryf 'n leerder wat die beste leer deur prente, diagramme en kleure te sien?","en":"Which learning style describes a learner who learns best by seeing pictures, diagrams and colours?"},"options":[{"af":"Ouditief","en":"Auditory"},{"af":"Visueel","en":"Visual"},{"af":"Kinesteties","en":"Kinaesthetic"},{"af":"Lees/skryf","en":"Reading/writing"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Visuele leerder leer deur te sien. 'n Ouditiewe leerder leer deur te hoor en 'n kinestetiese leerder deur te doen.","en":"A visual learner learns by seeing. An auditory learner learns by hearing and a kinaesthetic learner by doing."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Visuele opsomming met die hoofonderwerp in die middel en takke na buite, word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A visual summary with the main topic in the centre and branches going outwards is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["breinkaart","mind map","mindmap","breinkaarte"],"en":["mind map","mindmap","mind-map","brain map"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Breinkaart wys hoe idees met die hoofonderwerp verband hou. 'n Venn-diagram vergelyk twee dinge met oorvleuelende sirkels.","en":"A mind map shows how ideas link to the main topic. A Venn diagram compares two things with overlapping circles."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Venn-diagram","flitskaart","opsomming"],"en":["Venn diagram","flash card","summary"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Graad 10-eindeksamens is eksterne nasionale eksamens wat deur die Departement van Basiese Onderwys opgestel en gemerk word.","en":"Grade 10 final exams are external national exams set and marked by the Department of Basic Education."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Graad 10-eksamens word deur die skool of provinsie opgestel (interne assessering). Net die Graad 12-NSS-eksamen is ekstern.","en":"False. Grade 10 exams are set by the school or province (internal assessment). Only the Grade 12 NSC exam is external."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy doen as 'n vraag met die opdragwerkwoord **noem** begin?","en":"What must you do when a question starts with the instruction verb **name**?"},"options":[{"af":"Gee 'n eie oordeel met redes","en":"Give your own judgement with reasons"},{"af":"Bespreek die voor- en nadele","en":"Discuss the advantages and disadvantages"},{"af":"Verduidelik hoekom iets gebeur","en":"Explain why something happens"},{"af":"Gee kort feite sonder verduideliking","en":"Give short facts without explanation"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'Noem' of 'lys' vra net feite. Moenie tyd mors op verduidelikings nie – dit is wat 'verduidelik' en 'bespreek' vra.","en":"'Name' or 'list' asks only for facts. Do not waste time on explanations – that is what 'explain' and 'discuss' ask for."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die meeste Graad 10-vakke tel die SBA ___% van die finale punt.","en":"In most Grade 10 subjects the SBA counts ___% of the final mark."},"answers":{"af":["25","25%","vyf-en-twintig"],"en":["25","25%","twenty-five"]},"explain":{"af":"In die meeste vakke: SBA 25% + eksamen 75%. Vakke met 'n PAT (Toerisme, Gasvryheid): SBA 25% + PAT 25% + eksamen 50%.","en":"In most subjects: SBA 25% + exam 75%. Subjects with a PAT (Tourism, Hospitality): SBA 25% + PAT 25% + exam 50%."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["75%","50%","40%"],"en":["75%","50%","40%"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter studietegniek pas die beste by 'n **kinestetiese** leerder?","en":"Which study technique suits a **kinaesthetic** learner best?"},"options":[{"af":"Rondloop en definisies opsê, of 'n model bou","en":"Walking around reciting definitions, or building a model"},{"af":"Na 'n opname van die notas luister","en":"Listening to a recording of the notes"},{"af":"'n Kleurvolle breinkaart teken","en":"Drawing a colourful mind map"},{"af":"Die notas woord vir woord herskryf","en":"Rewriting the notes word for word"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Kinestetiese leerders leer deur te doen en te beweeg. Opnames pas by ouditiewe leerders en breinkaarte by visuele leerders.","en":"Kinaesthetic learners learn by doing and moving. Recordings suit auditory learners and mind maps suit visual learners."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Om take vir later te skuif al weet jy dit moet nou gedoen word, word ___ genoem.","en":"Putting tasks off until later even though you know they should be done now is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["uitstel","uitstelgedrag","uitstellery"],"en":["procrastination","procrastinating"]},"explain":{"af":"Uitstel lei tot stres en haastige werk. Prioritisering en tydsbestuur is juis die oplossings daarvoor.","en":"Procrastination leads to stress and rushed work. Prioritising and time management are the solutions to it."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["prioritisering","tydsbestuur","konsentrasie"],"en":["prioritising","time management","concentration"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Kort, gefokusde studiesessies met ruskanse, oor 'n paar dae versprei, werk beter as een lang sessie die aand voor die toets.","en":"Short, focused study sessions with breaks, spread over a few days, work better than one long session the night before the test."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Gespasieerde hersiening help die brein om inligting in die langtermyngeheue te stoor. Laaste-aand-inprop vergeet jy gou.","en":"True. Spaced revision helps the brain store information in long-term memory. What you cram the night before is soon forgotten."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy maak die handboek toe en vertel jouself in jou eie woorde wat jy pas gelees het. By watter stap van SQ3R is jy?","en":"You close the textbook and tell yourself in your own words what you have just read. Which step of SQ3R are you at?"},"options":[{"af":"Survey (oorsig)","en":"Survey"},{"af":"Question (vra)","en":"Question"},{"af":"Recite (opsê)","en":"Recite"},{"af":"Review (hersien)","en":"Review"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Recite (opsê) beteken om sonder die boek in jou eie woorde te herhaal. Review (hersien) is om later weer oor al die werk te gaan.","en":"Recite means repeating in your own words without the book. Review is going over all the work again later."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Vraag lui: 'Noem vyf faktore wat konsentrasie benadeel. (5)' Jy moet ___ feite gee.","en":"A question reads: 'Name five factors that harm concentration. (5)' You must give ___ facts."},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five"]},"explain":{"af":"By 'noem' is elke feit gewoonlik 1 punt werd, dus 5 punte = 5 feite. Kyk altyd na die puntetoekenning.","en":"With 'name' each fact is usually worth 1 mark, so 5 marks = 5 facts. Always look at the mark allocation."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","2","10"],"en":["3","2","10"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke studiemetode by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each study method to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Flitskaarte","en":"Flash cards"},"r":{"af":"'n Term of vraag voor en die antwoord agter","en":"A term or question on the front and the answer on the back"}},{"l":{"af":"Venn-diagram","en":"Venn diagram"},"r":{"af":"Oorvleuelende sirkels wat ooreenkomste en verskille wys","en":"Overlapping circles that show similarities and differences"}},{"l":{"af":"Akroniem","en":"Acronym"},"r":{"af":"Die eerste letters van woorde vorm 'n nuwe woord, bv. VAK","en":"The first letters of words form a new word, e.g. VAK"}},{"l":{"af":"Opsomming","en":"Summary"},"r":{"af":"'n Hoofstuk verkort tot die kernfeite","en":"A chapter shortened to the core facts"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke metode verwerk die werk anders: flitskaarte vir selftoetsing, Venn-diagramme vir vergelykings, akronieme vir volgorde en opsommings vir die kernfeite.","en":"Each method processes the work differently: flash cards for self-testing, Venn diagrams for comparisons, acronyms for order and summaries for the core facts."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vraestel tel 80 punte en jy het 90 minute. Jy gebruik 10 minute om te lees en na te gaan, sodat 80 minute oorbly. Hoeveel tyd moet jy omtrent aan 'n vraag van 15 punte bestee?","en":"A paper counts 80 marks and you have 90 minutes. You use 10 minutes to read and check, so 80 minutes are left. About how much time should you spend on a 15-mark question?"},"options":[{"af":"10 minute","en":"10 minutes"},{"af":"15 minute","en":"15 minutes"},{"af":"17 minute","en":"17 minutes"},{"af":"30 minute","en":"30 minutes"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"80 minute vir 80 punte = 1 minuut per punt, dus 15 punte ≈ 15 minute. 17 minute kry jy as jy vergeet om die lees- en nagaantyd af te trek.","en":"80 minutes for 80 marks = 1 minute per mark, so 15 marks ≈ 15 minutes. You get 17 minutes if you forget to subtract the reading and checking time."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die opdragwerkwoord ___ vra dat jy die voor- en nadele afweeg en jou eie oordeel gee.","en":"The instruction verb ___ asks you to weigh up the advantages and disadvantages and give your own judgement."},"answers":{"af":["evalueer","beoordeel"],"en":["evaluate","assess"]},"explain":{"af":"Evalueer/beoordeel vra 'n oordeel. 'Noem' vra net feite, 'beskryf' vra detail en 'definieer' vra die presiese betekenis.","en":"Evaluate/assess asks for a judgement. 'Name' asks only for facts, 'describe' asks for detail and 'define' asks for the exact meaning."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["noem","beskryf","definieer"],"en":["name","describe","define"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato studeer altyd die aand voor 'n toets tot 01:00 terwyl sy op haar foon gesels, en haar punte is swak. Watter raad sal haar die meeste help?","en":"Lerato always studies until 01:00 the night before a test while chatting on her phone, and her marks are poor. Which advice will help her most?"},"options":[{"af":"Studeer nog langer die aand voor die toets","en":"Study even longer the night before the test"},{"af":"Lees die notas net weer en weer deur","en":"Just read the notes over and over"},{"af":"Maak 'n rooster met kort sessies oor 'n paar dae, sit die foon weg en toets jouself","en":"Make a timetable with short sessions over a few days, put the phone away and test yourself"},{"af":"Studeer met die TV aan sodat sy wakker bly","en":"Study with the TV on so that she stays awake"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Haar probleme is uitstel, afleiding en te min slaap. Gespasieerde hersiening, 'n foon-vrye werkplek en selftoetsing spreek al drie aan.","en":"Her problems are procrastination, distraction and too little sleep. Spaced revision, a phone-free workspace and self-testing address all three."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'Bespreek krities die impak van sosiale media op studie. (6)' Watter antwoord sal waarskynlik die meeste punte verdien?","en":"'Critically discuss the impact of social media on studying. (6)' Which answer is likely to earn the most marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Ses kort woorde in 'n lys, bv. 'afleiding, tyd, slaap'","en":"Six short words in a list, e.g. 'distraction, time, sleep'"},{"af":"'n Definisie van sosiale media en niks meer nie","en":"A definition of social media and nothing more"},{"af":"Een lang sin wat herhaal dat sosiale media sleg is","en":"One long sentence repeating that social media is bad"},{"af":"Argumente vir en teen, met voorbeelde, en 'n gemotiveerde eie slot","en":"Arguments for and against, with examples, and a motivated conclusion of your own"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'Bespreek krities' vra albei kante (bv. afleiding teenoor nuttige studievideo's en groepe) én 'n eie, gemotiveerde gevolgtrekking. 'n Lys woorde beantwoord 'noem', nie 'bespreek krities' nie.","en":"'Critically discuss' asks for both sides (e.g. distraction versus useful study videos and groups) and your own motivated conclusion. A list of words answers 'name', not 'critically discuss'."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dis die aand voor jou eerste eksamen en jy voel paniekerig. Watter plan is die beste?","en":"It is the night before your first exam and you feel panicky. Which plan is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Bly die hele nag wak met energiedrankies en leer nuwe werk","en":"Stay awake all night with energy drinks and learn new work"},{"af":"Gaan kortliks oor jou opsommings, haal diep asem, slaap 8–10 uur en eet ontbyt","en":"Briefly go over your summaries, breathe deeply, sleep 8–10 hours and eat breakfast"},{"af":"Slaan ontbyt oor sodat jy vroeër by die skool is","en":"Skip breakfast so that you get to school earlier"},{"af":"Vergelyk heelnag jou voorbereiding met vriende op WhatsApp","en":"Compare your preparation with friends on WhatsApp all night"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Slaap en kos help die brein om te konsentreer en te onthou; diep asemhaling kalmeer. Nuwe werk en energiedrankies die laaste aand verhoog net stres.","en":"Sleep and food help the brain to concentrate and remember; deep breathing calms you. New work and energy drinks the last night only increase stress."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t2-sosiale-omgewingsverantwoordelikheid","title":{"af":"Sosiale en omgewingsverantwoordelikheid","en":"Social and environmental responsibility"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sosiale en omgewingskwessies en hul gevolge vir gesondheid kan verduidelik en 'n gemeenskapsprojek kan beplan.","en":"You will be able to explain social and environmental issues and their effects on health, and plan a community project."},"summary":{"af":"## Kernbegrippe\n\n- **Sosiale geregtigheid:** die regverdige verdeling van hulpbronne, geleenthede en regte, sodat almal 'n regverdige kans in die lewe kry.\n- **Omgewingsgeregtigheid:** geen gemeenskap (veral nie 'n arm gemeenskap nie) mag 'n onregverdige deel van omgewingskade dra nie, bv. 'n stortingsterrein of besoedelende fabriek langs 'n informele nedersetting. **Artikel 24** van die Grondwet: elkeen het die reg op 'n omgewing wat nie skadelik vir hul gesondheid of welsyn is nie, en die omgewing moet vir huidige en toekomstige geslagte beskerm word.\n- **Voedselsekerheid:** wanneer alle mense te alle tye toegang het tot genoeg veilige, voedsame kos vir 'n gesonde, aktiewe lewe. By **voedselonsekerheid** slaan gesinne maaltye oor of eet hulle net goedkoop styselkos soos pap en brood.\n- **Voedselproduksie:** die verbouing en verwerking van kos, van kommersiële sitrusplase rondom Brits tot 'n groentetuin by die huis of skool. Meer plaaslike voedselproduksie verbeter voedselsekerheid.\n\n## Hedendaagse sosiale kwessies\n\nKABV noem: misdaad, armoede, voedselonsekerheid, geweld, MIV en vigs, veiligheid en sekuriteit, ongelyke toegang tot basiese hulpbronne, en 'n gebrek aan basiese dienste (skoon water, sanitasie, gesondheidsorg, elektrisiteit en beurtkrag).\n\n## Omgewingskwessies\n\n- **Besoedeling:** water (riool, chemikalieë), lug (rook van fabrieke en voertuie, brandende afval) en grond (gevaarlike afval).\n- **Onwettige storting en rommelstrooiery:** dit verstop stormwaterpype, lok rotte en vlieë en besoedel riviere.\n- **Waterskaarste:** droogtes, lekkende pype en vermorsing.\n- **Klimaatsverandering:** hoër temperature, meer droogtes en ernstiger oorstromings.\n\n### Plaaslike voorbeeld: Hartbeespoortdam\n\nDie dam word gevoed deur die Krokodilrivier (waarin die Jukskeirivier vloei), wat rioolwater van Gauteng se stede en kunsmisafloop van plase saambring. Die oormaat voedingstowwe (**fosfate en nitrate**) veroorsaak **eutrofikasie**: waterhiasint en blougroen alge groei te vinnig. Wanneer die plante en alge doodgaan en vrot, gebruik dit die suurstof in die water op, sodat visse vrek. Dit veroorsaak 'n slegte reuk, en sommige blougroen alge is giftig vir mense en diere. Toerisme, visvang en watersport ly daaronder, en dit raak werksgeleenthede in die gemeenskap. Dis 'n kwessie van omgewingsgeregtigheid: die mense rondom die dam dra die skade van besoedeling wat grotendeels stroomop veroorsaak word.\n\n## Skadelike gevolge vir persoonlike en gemeenskapsgesondheid\n\n| Kwessie | Gevolg vir gesondheid |\n|---|---|\n| Vuil water, geen sanitasie | siektes soos diarree en cholera |\n| Voedselonsekerheid | ondervoeding, groeiremming by kinders, 'n swak immuunstelsel, swak konsentrasie op skool |\n| Lugbesoedeling | asma en ander longprobleme |\n| Misdaad en geweld | beserings, trauma, stres en angs |\n| Armoede en werkloosheid | stres, depressie, swak toegang tot gesondheidsorg |\n| Beurtkrag | kos bederf in yskaste; paraffien en kerse kan brande veroorsaak |\n\n## Vaardighede vir burgerlike lewe\n\n- **Sosiale verantwoordelikheid:** jy gee om vir ander en die omgewing, en jy tree op.\n- **Kritiese denke:** vra wie geraak word, wat die oorsake is en of inligting betroubaar is.\n- **Konstruktiewe denke:** soek oplossings eerder as om net te kla.\n- **Ingeligte besluitneming:** versamel eers feite voordat jy besluit.\n\n## Jeugdiens en vrywilligerswerk\n\n**Vrywilligerswerk** is onbetaalde werk wat jy uit vrye wil vir die gemeenskap doen. Voorbeelde van jeug- en burgerlike organisasies: die **NYDA** (Nasionale Jeugontwikkelingsagentskap – help jongmense met vaardighede, werk en klein besighede), **loveLife** (jeuggesondheid en MIV-voorkoming), die **Padvinders** en kerkjeuggroepe.\n\n| Voordele vir die gemeenskap | Voordele vir die vrywilliger |\n|---|---|\n| dienste wat andersins nie sou bestaan nie | nuwe vaardighede en ervaring vir jou CV |\n| bespaar geld vir die gemeenskap | selfvertroue en 'n gevoel van doel |\n| bou eenheid en hoop | nuwe vriende en kontakte |\n| help kwesbare mense direk | empatie en begrip vir ander |\n\n**Evalueer 'n jeugdiens** met drie vrae:\n1. Wat is die **doel** daarvan?\n2. Wat is die **sterk punte**?\n3. Wat kan **verbeter** word (bv. meer vrywilligers, meer fondse, beter bemarking, langtermyn-opvolg)?\n\n## 'n Groepprojek oor 'n sosiale kwessie beplan\n\n1. **Identifiseer** die kwessie (bv. rommel by die taxistaanplek in Brits).\n2. **Doen navorsing:** hoe groot is die probleem, wie word geraak en wat is die oorsake?\n3. **Stel doelwitte** wat spesifiek, meetbaar en realisties is.\n4. **Beplan:** rolle (wie doen wat), 'n **begroting**, 'n tydlyn, toestemming en vennote (bv. die Madibeng-munisipaliteit).\n5. **Implementeer** die plan.\n6. **Evalueer en besin:** is die doelwitte bereik, en wat sal julle volgende keer anders doen?\n\n> **Wenk:** In 'n eksamenvraag oor 'n projek noem jy die stappe *in volgorde* en gee jy 'n konkrete plaaslike voorbeeld.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders verwar **sosiale** en **omgewings**kwessies. Misdaad en armoede raak mense se verhoudings en lewensomstandighede (sosiaal); besoedeling en storting raak die natuurlike omgewing (omgewing) – al raak albei uiteindelik ons gesondheid.","en":"## Key concepts\n\n- **Social justice:** the fair distribution of resources, opportunities and rights, so that everyone gets a fair chance in life.\n- **Environmental justice:** no community (especially not a poor community) should carry an unfair share of environmental harm, e.g. a dumping site or polluting factory next to an informal settlement. **Section 24** of the Constitution: everyone has the right to an environment that is not harmful to their health or well-being, and the environment must be protected for present and future generations.\n- **Food security:** when all people at all times have access to enough safe, nutritious food for a healthy, active life. With **food insecurity** families skip meals or eat only cheap starchy food such as pap and bread.\n- **Food production:** growing and processing food, from commercial citrus farms around Brits to a vegetable garden at home or school. More local food production improves food security.\n\n## Contemporary social issues\n\nCAPS lists: crime, poverty, food insecurity, violence, HIV and AIDS, safety and security, unequal access to basic resources, and a lack of basic services (clean water, sanitation, health care, electricity and load-shedding).\n\n## Environmental issues\n\n- **Pollution:** water (sewage, chemicals), air (smoke from factories and vehicles, burning waste) and land (hazardous waste).\n- **Illegal dumping and littering:** it blocks stormwater drains, attracts rats and flies and pollutes rivers.\n- **Water scarcity:** droughts, leaking pipes and waste.\n- **Climate change:** higher temperatures, more droughts and more severe floods.\n\n### Local example: Hartbeespoort Dam\n\nThe dam is fed by the Crocodile River (into which the Jukskei River flows), which carries sewage from Gauteng's cities and fertiliser run-off from farms. The excess nutrients (**phosphates and nitrates**) cause **eutrophication**: water hyacinth and blue-green algae grow too fast. When the plants and algae die and rot, they use up the oxygen in the water, so fish die. It causes a bad smell, and some blue-green algae are poisonous to people and animals. Tourism, fishing and water sport suffer, and this affects jobs in the community. It is an environmental-justice issue: the people around the dam carry the harm of pollution that is largely caused upstream.\n\n## Harmful effects on personal and community health\n\n| Issue | Effect on health |\n|---|---|\n| Dirty water, no sanitation | diseases such as diarrhoea and cholera |\n| Food insecurity | malnutrition, stunted growth in children, a weak immune system, poor concentration at school |\n| Air pollution | asthma and other lung problems |\n| Crime and violence | injuries, trauma, stress and anxiety |\n| Poverty and unemployment | stress, depression, poor access to health care |\n| Load-shedding | food spoils in fridges; paraffin and candles can cause fires |\n\n## Skills for civic life\n\n- **Social responsibility:** you care about others and the environment, and you act.\n- **Critical thinking:** ask who is affected, what the causes are and whether information is reliable.\n- **Constructive thinking:** look for solutions instead of only complaining.\n- **Informed decision-making:** gather facts first before you decide.\n\n## Youth service and volunteerism\n\n**Volunteerism** is unpaid work that you do of your own free will for the community. Examples of youth and civic organisations: the **NYDA** (National Youth Development Agency – helps young people with skills, jobs and small businesses), **loveLife** (youth health and HIV prevention), the **Scouts** and church youth groups.\n\n| Benefits for the community | Benefits for the volunteer |\n|---|---|\n| services that would otherwise not exist | new skills and experience for your CV |\n| saves the community money | confidence and a sense of purpose |\n| builds unity and hope | new friends and contacts |\n| helps vulnerable people directly | empathy and understanding for others |\n\n**Evaluate a youth service** with three questions:\n1. What is its **purpose**?\n2. What are its **strengths**?\n3. What can be **improved** (e.g. more volunteers, more funds, better marketing, long-term follow-up)?\n\n## Planning a group project on a social issue\n\n1. **Identify** the issue (e.g. litter at the taxi rank in Brits).\n2. **Do research:** how big is the problem, who is affected and what are the causes?\n3. **Set goals** that are specific, measurable and realistic.\n4. **Plan:** roles (who does what), a **budget**, a timeline, permission and partners (e.g. the Madibeng municipality).\n5. **Implement** the plan.\n6. **Evaluate and reflect:** were the goals achieved, and what will you do differently next time?\n\n> **Tip:** In an exam question about a project, give the steps *in order* and a concrete local example.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners confuse **social** and **environmental** issues. Crime and poverty affect people's relationships and living conditions (social); pollution and dumping affect the natural environment (environmental) – even though both eventually affect our health."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sosiale geregtigheid","en":"Social justice"},"def":{"af":"Die regverdige verdeling van hulpbronne, geleenthede en regte in 'n samelewing.","en":"The fair distribution of resources, opportunities and rights in a society."}},{"term":{"af":"Omgewingsgeregtigheid","en":"Environmental justice"},"def":{"af":"Die beginsel dat geen gemeenskap 'n onregverdige deel van omgewingskade mag dra nie en dat almal reg het op 'n gesonde omgewing (artikel 24).","en":"The principle that no community should carry an unfair share of environmental harm and that everyone has a right to a healthy environment (section 24)."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselsekerheid","en":"Food security"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer alle mense te alle tye toegang het tot genoeg veilige, voedsame kos vir 'n gesonde, aktiewe lewe.","en":"When all people at all times have access to enough safe, nutritious food for a healthy, active life."}},{"term":{"af":"Voedselproduksie","en":"Food production"},"def":{"af":"Die verbouing, oes en verwerking van kos, op plase of in huis- en gemeenskapstuine.","en":"Growing, harvesting and processing food, on farms or in home and community gardens."}},{"term":{"af":"Eutrofikasie","en":"Eutrophication"},"def":{"af":"Oormatige groei van alge en waterplante weens te veel voedingstowwe (fosfate en nitrate) in water, wat die suurstof verminder.","en":"Excessive growth of algae and water plants because of too many nutrients (phosphates and nitrates) in water, which reduces oxygen."}},{"term":{"af":"Onwettige storting","en":"Illegal dumping"},"def":{"af":"Om afval op 'n plek te los wat nie daarvoor bestem is nie, soos oop erwe of langs strome.","en":"Leaving waste in a place not meant for it, such as open plots or next to streams."}},{"term":{"af":"Vrywilligerswerk","en":"Volunteerism"},"def":{"af":"Onbetaalde werk wat iemand uit vrye wil doen om die gemeenskap te help.","en":"Unpaid work that someone does of their own free will to help the community."}},{"term":{"af":"Sosiale verantwoordelikheid","en":"Social responsibility"},"def":{"af":"Die plig om op te tree tot voordeel van die gemeenskap en die omgewing.","en":"The duty to act for the benefit of the community and the environment."}},{"term":{"af":"Ondervoeding","en":"Malnutrition"},"def":{"af":"'n Toestand wanneer die liggaam nie genoeg van die regte voedingstowwe kry nie, wat groei en immuniteit benadeel.","en":"A condition when the body does not get enough of the right nutrients, harming growth and immunity."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: voedselonsekerheid","en":"Source question: food insecurity"},"problem":{"af":"**Bron:** *Mnr. Mokoena van Letlhabile naby Brits het sy werk by 'n myn verloor. Die gesin van vyf leef nou van een kindertoelaag en eet meestal pap. Teen die einde van die maand slaan hulle aandete oor. Die jongste kind is dikwels siek en die oudste sukkel om op skool te konsentreer.*\n\n(a) Definieer voedselsekerheid. (2)\n(b) Verduidelik drie gevolge van hierdie situasie vir die gesin se gesondheid. (3)\n(c) Stel twee maniere voor waarop die gemeenskap kan help. (2)","en":"**Source:** *Mr Mokoena from Letlhabile near Brits lost his job at a mine. The family of five now lives on one child support grant and eats mostly pap. Towards the end of the month they skip supper. The youngest child is often ill and the eldest struggles to concentrate at school.*\n\n(a) Define food security. (2)\n(b) Explain three effects of this situation on the family's health. (3)\n(c) Suggest two ways in which the community can help. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Voedselsekerheid is wanneer alle mense te alle tye toegang het tot genoeg veilige, voedsame kos (1) vir 'n gesonde, aktiewe lewe (1).","en":"(a) Food security is when all people at all times have access to enough safe, nutritious food (1) for a healthy, active life (1)."},{"af":"(b) Pap alleen gee nie genoeg proteïene en vitamiene nie → **ondervoeding** en swakker groei by die kinders (1). 'n Swak immuunstelsel verklaar hoekom die jongste kind dikwels siek is (1). Honger veroorsaak swak konsentrasie en moegheid op skool (1).","en":"(b) Pap alone does not provide enough protein and vitamins → **malnutrition** and poorer growth in the children (1). A weak immune system explains why the youngest child is often ill (1). Hunger causes poor concentration and tiredness at school (1)."},{"af":"Ook aanvaarbaar: stres en angs by die ouers oor geld en kos.","en":"Also acceptable: stress and anxiety in the parents about money and food."},{"af":"(c) Enige twee: 'n gemeenskaps- of skoolgroentetuin begin (1); 'n sopkombuis of voedselpakkie-projek deur kerke (1); die skoolvoedingskema benut; die gesin help om by die NYDA vir vaardigheidsopleiding aan te meld.","en":"(c) Any two: start a community or school vegetable garden (1); a soup kitchen or food-parcel project run by churches (1); make use of the school nutrition programme; help the family register with the NYDA for skills training."}],"answer":{"af":"Definisie (2) + drie gesondheidsgevolge soos ondervoeding, swak immuniteit en swak konsentrasie (3) + twee gemeenskapsoplossings (2).","en":"Definition (2) + three health effects such as malnutrition, weak immunity and poor concentration (3) + two community solutions (2)."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan 'n groepprojek","en":"Plan a group project"},"problem":{"af":"Jou LO-groep wil iets doen aan die onwettige storting langs 'n stroom in julle woonbuurt in Brits. Beskryf die stappe van jul projekplan. (6)","en":"Your LO group wants to do something about the illegal dumping next to a stream in your neighbourhood in Brits. Describe the steps of your project plan. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**1. Identifiseer:** die kwessie is onwettige storting wat die stroom besoedel en rotte aanlok.","en":"**1. Identify:** the issue is illegal dumping that pollutes the stream and attracts rats."},{"af":"**2. Navorsing:** fotografeer die terrein, vra inwoners hoekom hulle daar stort (bv. vullis word nie gereeld verwyder nie) en vind uit wat die munisipaliteit se reëls is.","en":"**2. Research:** photograph the site, ask residents why they dump there (e.g. refuse is not collected regularly) and find out what the municipality's rules are."},{"af":"**3. Doelwit:** 'Ons ruim die stroomwal binne vier weke op en sit twee vullisdromme neer.'","en":"**3. Goal:** 'We will clean up the stream bank within four weeks and put down two refuse drums.'"},{"af":"**4. Beplan:** verdeel rolle (leier, bemarking, logistiek), maak 'n begroting (handskoene, sakke, plakkate) en kry toestemming en hulp van die Madibeng-munisipaliteit.","en":"**4. Plan:** divide roles (leader, marketing, logistics), draw up a budget (gloves, bags, posters) and get permission and help from the Madibeng municipality."},{"af":"**5. Implementeer en 6. Evalueer:** hou die opruimdag en 'n bewusmakingsveldtog; gaan ná 'n maand terug om te kyk of daar weer gestort word, en besin oor wat beter kan.","en":"**5. Implement and 6. Evaluate:** hold the clean-up day and an awareness campaign; go back after a month to see whether people are dumping again, and reflect on what can be done better."}],"answer":{"af":"Identifiseer → navorsing → doelwitte → beplan (rolle, begroting, tydlyn, vennote) → implementeer → evalueer en besin.","en":"Identify → research → goals → plan (roles, budget, timeline, partners) → implement → evaluate and reflect."}},{"title":{"af":"Hartbeespoortdam as omgewingsgeregtigheidskwessie","en":"Hartbeespoort Dam as an environmental-justice issue"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik hoe die waterhiasint- en algeprobleem by Hartbeespoortdam 'n kwessie van omgewingsgeregtigheid is. (4)","en":"Explain how the water-hyacinth and algae problem at Hartbeespoort Dam is an issue of environmental justice. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Oorsaak:** riool en kunsmisafloop van stede en plase stroomop vloei via die Krokodilrivier in die dam en veroorsaak eutrofikasie (1).","en":"**Cause:** sewage and fertiliser run-off from cities and farms upstream flow via the Crocodile River into the dam and cause eutrophication (1)."},{"af":"**Wie dra die skade:** die inwoners, vissers en mense wat in toerisme rondom die dam werk, ly onder giftige alge, slegte reuk en verlore inkomste (1).","en":"**Who carries the harm:** the residents, fishermen and people working in tourism around the dam suffer from toxic algae, bad smells and lost income (1)."},{"af":"**Onregverdig:** die mense wat die skade dra, is grotendeels nie dié wat die besoedeling veroorsaak nie (1).","en":"**Unfair:** the people who carry the harm are largely not the ones causing the pollution (1)."},{"af":"**Regte:** artikel 24 van die Grondwet gee almal die reg op 'n omgewing wat nie skadelik vir hul gesondheid of welsyn is nie (1).","en":"**Rights:** section 24 of the Constitution gives everyone the right to an environment that is not harmful to their health or well-being (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"Die besoedeling word stroomop veroorsaak, maar die gemeenskap by die dam dra die gesondheids- en ekonomiese skade, wat hul artikel 24-reg skend.","en":"The pollution is caused upstream, but the community at the dam carries the health and economic harm, which violates their section 24 right."}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer 'n jeugdiens","en":"Evaluate a youth service"},"problem":{"af":"'n Kerkjeuggroep in Brits bedien elke Saterdag sop en brood aan sowat 80 mense. Hulle het 12 vrywilligers, maar die kos raak soms op en hulle werk net op Saterdae. Evalueer hierdie diens deur na die doel, sterk punte en moontlike verbeterings te kyk. (6)","en":"A church youth group in Brits serves soup and bread to about 80 people every Saturday. They have 12 volunteers, but the food sometimes runs out and they only work on Saturdays. Evaluate this service by looking at its purpose, strengths and possible improvements. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Doel:** om honger te verlig en voedselonsekerheid in die gemeenskap te verminder (1).","en":"**Purpose:** to relieve hunger and reduce food insecurity in the community (1)."},{"af":"**Sterk punte:** dit is gereeld en betroubaar (elke Saterdag) (1); jongmense leer empatie en verantwoordelikheid (1).","en":"**Strengths:** it is regular and reliable (every Saturday) (1); young people learn empathy and responsibility (1)."},{"af":"**Verbeterings:** werf meer vrywilligers en skenkers sodat die kos nie opraak nie (1); begin 'n groentetuin om eie kos te produseer (1).","en":"**Improvements:** recruit more volunteers and donors so that the food does not run out (1); start a vegetable garden to produce their own food (1)."},{"af":"**Oordeel:** die diens is waardevol, maar dit verlig net simptome; om langtermyn-voedselsekerheid te bou, moet dit ook mense help om self kos te verbou of werk te kry (1).","en":"**Judgement:** the service is valuable, but it only relieves symptoms; to build long-term food security it should also help people to grow their own food or find work (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"Doel (1) + twee sterk punte (2) + twee verbeterings (2) + 'n gemotiveerde oordeel (1).","en":"Purpose (1) + two strengths (2) + two improvements (2) + a motivated judgement (1)."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken **voedselsekerheid**?","en":"What does **food security** mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Dat kos in 'n veilige pakhuis gestoor word","en":"That food is stored in a safe warehouse"},{"af":"Dat 'n land al sy kos uitvoer","en":"That a country exports all its food"},{"af":"Dat alle mense te alle tye toegang het tot genoeg veilige, voedsame kos","en":"That all people at all times have access to enough safe, nutritious food"},{"af":"Dat elke gesin een maaltyd per dag eet","en":"That every family eats one meal a day"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Voedselsekerheid gaan oor *toegang* vir *almal*, *te alle tye*, tot genoeg veilige en voedsame kos – nie net oor die berging van kos nie.","en":"Food security is about *access* for *everyone*, *at all times*, to enough safe and nutritious food – not just about storing food."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Onbetaalde werk wat jy uit vrye wil vir die gemeenskap doen, word ___ genoem.","en":"Unpaid work that you do of your own free will for the community is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["vrywilligerswerk","vrywillige werk","vrywilligheid"],"en":["volunteerism","volunteering","voluntary work","volunteer work"]},"explain":{"af":"Vrywilligerswerk is onbetaald en vrywillig. Deeltydse werk word betaal, en 'n toelaag is geld wat die staat aan mense betaal.","en":"Volunteerism is unpaid and voluntary. Part-time work is paid, and a grant is money the state pays to people."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["deeltydse werk","maatskaplike toelaag","regstellende aksie"],"en":["part-time work","social grant","affirmative action"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Artikel 24 van die Grondwet gee elkeen die reg op 'n omgewing wat nie skadelik vir hul gesondheid of welsyn is nie.","en":"Section 24 of the Constitution gives everyone the right to an environment that is not harmful to their health or well-being."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Artikel 24 is die omgewingsreg; dit vra ook dat die omgewing vir huidige en toekomstige geslagte beskerm word.","en":"True. Section 24 is the environmental right; it also requires the environment to be protected for present and future generations."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n **omgewingskwessie** eerder as 'n sosiale kwessie?","en":"Which one is an **environmental issue** rather than a social issue?"},"options":[{"af":"Misdaad","en":"Crime"},{"af":"Onwettige storting","en":"Illegal dumping"},{"af":"Werkloosheid","en":"Unemployment"},{"af":"Geweld","en":"Violence"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Onwettige storting besoedel die natuurlike omgewing (grond en water). Misdaad, werkloosheid en geweld is sosiale kwessies.","en":"Illegal dumping pollutes the natural environment (land and water). Crime, unemployment and violence are social issues."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die oormatige groei van alge en waterplante weens te veel voedingstowwe in die water, soos by Hartbeespoortdam, word ___ genoem.","en":"The excessive growth of algae and water plants because of too many nutrients in the water, as at Hartbeespoort Dam, is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["eutrofikasie","eutrofiering"],"en":["eutrophication"]},"explain":{"af":"Fosfate en nitrate uit riool en kunsmis 'voer' die alge en waterhiasint. Erosie is die wegspoel van grond, en ontbossing is die kap van woude.","en":"Phosphates and nitrates from sewage and fertiliser 'feed' the algae and water hyacinth. Erosion is soil washing away, and deforestation is cutting down forests."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["erosie","verwoestyning","ontbossing"],"en":["erosion","desertification","deforestation"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken **sosiale geregtigheid**?","en":"What does **social justice** mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Dat almal presies dieselfde inkomste verdien","en":"That everyone earns exactly the same income"},{"af":"Dat net die regering vir arm mense moet sorg","en":"That only the government must care for poor people"},{"af":"Dat oortreders altyd swaar gestraf word","en":"That offenders are always punished severely"},{"af":"Die regverdige verdeling van hulpbronne, geleenthede en regte","en":"The fair distribution of resources, opportunities and rights"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sosiale geregtigheid gaan oor *regverdigheid* en gelyke kanse, nie oor presies gelyke inkomste of oor strawwe nie.","en":"Social justice is about *fairness* and equal chances, not about exactly equal incomes or about punishment."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Tekort aan die regte voedingstowwe wat tot groeiremming en 'n swak immuunstelsel lei, word ___ genoem.","en":"A shortage of the right nutrients that leads to stunted growth and a weak immune system is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ondervoeding","wanvoeding"],"en":["malnutrition","undernutrition"]},"explain":{"af":"Ondervoeding is 'n gevolg van voedselonsekerheid. Dehidrasie is 'n tekort aan water, en voedselvergiftiging kom van besmette kos.","en":"Malnutrition is a result of food insecurity. Dehydration is a shortage of water, and food poisoning comes from contaminated food."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dehidrasie","allergie","voedselvergiftiging"],"en":["dehydration","allergy","food poisoning"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter gesondheidsprobleem word die meeste met vuil water en 'n gebrek aan sanitasie verbind?","en":"Which health problem is most linked to dirty water and a lack of sanitation?"},"options":[{"af":"Diarree en cholera","en":"Diarrhoea and cholera"},{"af":"Velkanker","en":"Skin cancer"},{"af":"Bysiendheid","en":"Short-sightedness"},{"af":"Hooikoors","en":"Hay fever"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Bakterieë in besmette water en swak sanitasie versprei siektes soos diarree en cholera, wat veral vir klein kinders gevaarlik is.","en":"Bacteria in contaminated water and poor sanitation spread diseases such as diarrhoea and cholera, which are especially dangerous for small children."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Vrywilligerswerk bevoordeel net die gemeenskap en nie die vrywilliger self nie.","en":"Volunteerism benefits only the community and not the volunteer."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die vrywilliger kry ook nuwe vaardighede, ervaring vir 'n CV, selfvertroue, kontakte en 'n gevoel van doel.","en":"False. The volunteer also gains new skills, experience for a CV, confidence, contacts and a sense of purpose."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou groep het die kwessie geïdentifiseer en navorsing gedoen. Wat is die **volgende** stap in die beplanning van 'n gemeenskapsprojek?","en":"Your group has identified the issue and done research. What is the **next** step in planning a community project?"},"options":[{"af":"Implementeer die projek dadelik","en":"Implement the project immediately"},{"af":"Stel doelwitte","en":"Set goals"},{"af":"Evalueer die resultate","en":"Evaluate the results"},{"af":"Skryf die eindverslag","en":"Write the final report"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die volgorde is: identifiseer → navorsing → doelwitte → beplan → implementeer → evalueer. Sonder doelwitte weet jy nie wat jy wil bereik nie.","en":"The order is: identify → research → goals → plan → implement → evaluate. Without goals you do not know what you want to achieve."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n projekplan wys die ___ hoeveel geld nodig is en waarvoor dit gebruik sal word.","en":"In a project plan the ___ shows how much money is needed and what it will be used for."},"answers":{"af":["begroting","budget"],"en":["budget"]},"explain":{"af":"Die begroting gaan oor geld. Die tydlyn wys wanneer elke taak gedoen word, en die doelwit sê wat julle wil bereik.","en":"The budget is about money. The timeline shows when each task is done, and the goal says what you want to achieve."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["tydlyn","doelwit","verslag"],"en":["timeline","goal","report"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke begrip by die beste voorbeeld.","en":"Match each concept to the best example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Voedselonsekerheid","en":"Food insecurity"},"r":{"af":"'n Gesin slaan teen die einde van die maand maaltye oor","en":"A family skips meals towards the end of the month"}},{"l":{"af":"Omgewingsongeregtigheid","en":"Environmental injustice"},"r":{"af":"'n Vullisterrein word langs 'n informele nedersetting aangelê","en":"A rubbish dump is placed next to an informal settlement"}},{"l":{"af":"Gebrek aan basiese dienste","en":"Lack of basic services"},"r":{"af":"'n Dorpie het geen lopende water of sanitasie nie","en":"A village has no running water or sanitation"}},{"l":{"af":"Vrywilligerswerk","en":"Volunteerism"},"r":{"af":"Leerders verf Saterdag sonder betaling 'n crèche","en":"Learners paint a crèche on Saturday without pay"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke voorbeeld wys die kern van die begrip: honger (voedselonsekerheid), onregverdige omgewingskade (omgewingsongeregtigheid), geen water (basiese dienste) en onbetaalde hulp (vrywilligerswerk).","en":"Each example shows the core of the concept: hunger (food insecurity), unfair environmental harm (environmental injustice), no water (basic services) and unpaid help (volunteerism)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die hoofoorsaak van die waterhiasint- en algeprobleem by Hartbeespoortdam?","en":"What is the main cause of the water-hyacinth and algae problem at Hartbeespoort Dam?"},"options":[{"af":"Te min reën in die Noordwes","en":"Too little rain in the North West"},{"af":"Toeriste wat te veel boot ry","en":"Tourists boating too much"},{"af":"Die dam se hoë ligging bo seespieël","en":"The dam's high altitude above sea level"},{"af":"Voedingstowwe uit riool en kunsmisafloop wat met die rivier saamkom","en":"Nutrients from sewage and fertiliser run-off carried in by the river"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Fosfate en nitrate uit riool en kunsmis veroorsaak eutrofikasie. Die ander opsies veroorsaak nie oormatige plant- en algegroei nie.","en":"Phosphates and nitrates from sewage and fertiliser cause eutrophication. The other options do not cause excessive plant and algae growth."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die laaste stap van 'n groepprojek, waar julle terugkyk na wat gewerk het en wat beter kan, is ___.","en":"The last step of a group project, where you look back at what worked and what can be done better, is ___."},"answers":{"af":["evaluering","evalueer","evaluasie","besinning","refleksie","evaluering en besinning"],"en":["evaluation","evaluate","reflection","reflect","evaluation and reflection"]},"explain":{"af":"Ná implementering evalueer en besin julle: is die doelwitte bereik, en wat sal julle volgende keer anders doen?","en":"After implementation you evaluate and reflect: were the goals achieved, and what will you do differently next time?"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["navorsing","implementering","beplanning"],"en":["research","implementation","planning"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag bederf die kos in die Mokoena-gesin se yskas, en hulle kan nie die vleis vervang nie. Wat is die beste verduideliking van hoe beurtkrag hier tot voedselonsekerheid bydra?","en":"During load-shedding the food in the Mokoena family's fridge spoils, and they cannot replace the meat. What is the best explanation of how load-shedding contributes to food insecurity here?"},"options":[{"af":"Beurtkrag laat kospryse altyd daal","en":"Load-shedding always makes food prices drop"},{"af":"Bederfde kos is verlore geld, sodat 'n arm gesin minder voedsame kos het om te eet","en":"Spoiled food is lost money, so a poor family has less nutritious food to eat"},{"af":"Beurtkrag raak net groot plase, nie gesinne nie","en":"Load-shedding only affects large farms, not families"},{"af":"Gesinne kan altyd met paraffien kook, so daar is geen effek nie","en":"Families can always cook with paraffin, so there is no effect"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die gesin kan nie bekostig om bederfde kos te vervang nie, so hul toegang tot genoeg voedsame kos daal. Paraffien is ook duur en 'n brandgevaar.","en":"The family cannot afford to replace spoiled food, so their access to enough nutritious food drops. Paraffin is also expensive and a fire hazard."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die LO-klas wil die rommelprobleem by die taxistaanplek in Brits aanspreek. Watter plan is die **beste**?","en":"The LO class wants to address the litter problem at the taxi rank in Brits. Which plan is **best**?"},"options":[{"af":"Een opruimdag sonder enige opvolg","en":"One clean-up day without any follow-up"},{"af":"Net 'n plasing op sosiale media wat mense blameer","en":"Only a social-media post blaming people"},{"af":"Navorsing, 'n opruimdag saam met die munisipaliteit, vullisdromme, 'n bewusmakingsveldtog en maandelikse evaluering","en":"Research, a clean-up day with the municipality, refuse drums, an awareness campaign and monthly evaluation"},{"af":"Taxibestuurders sonder waarskuwing beboet","en":"Fining taxi drivers without warning"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beste plan volg al die projekstappe, spreek die oorsaak aan (geen dromme, min bewustheid), werk met vennote saam en evalueer of dit volhoubaar is. Leerders het ook nie die mag om mense te beboet nie.","en":"The best plan follows all the project steps, addresses the cause (no drums, little awareness), works with partners and evaluates whether it is sustainable. Learners also do not have the power to fine people."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Lewensrolle, seksualiteit en die wêreld van werk","en":"Life roles, sexuality and the world of work"},"topics":[{"id":"lo10-t3-lewensrolle-volwassenheid","title":{"af":"Lewensrolle en veranderinge op pad na volwassenheid","en":"Life roles and changes towards adulthood"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal lewensrolle en rolkonflik kan verduidelik, die fisiese, emosionele en sosiale veranderinge van puberteit kan klassifiseer en verandering kan hanteer.","en":"You will be able to explain life roles and role conflict, classify the physical, emotional and social changes of puberty and cope with change."},"summary":{"af":"## Lewensrolle\n\n'n **Lewensrol** is 'n posisie wat jy in die lewe of samelewing inneem, met spesifieke verwagtinge en verantwoordelikhede. Jy speel baie rolle tegelyk: kind, leerder, gesinslid (broer of suster), vriend en spanmaat. Later word jy dalk 'n student, werknemer of werkgewer, lewensmaat, ouer (ma of pa), grootouer, broodwinner, leier of volgeling.\n\n| Rol | Verantwoordelikhede |\n|---|---|\n| Kind / gesinslid | respek, help by die huis, kommunikeer met ouers |\n| Leerder | klas bywoon, huiswerk doen, skoolreëls volg |\n| Werknemer | betyds wees, eerlik en betroubaar werk, werkplekreëls volg |\n| Werkgewer | regverdige lone betaal, 'n veilige werkplek voorsien |\n| Ouer | kinders versorg, beskerm, onderrig en onderhou |\n| Broodwinner | geld verdien om die gesin te onderhou |\n| Leier | rigting gee, ander motiveer, 'n goeie voorbeeld stel |\n| Volgeling | saamwerk, opdragte uitvoer, konstruktief bydra |\n\n### Hoe rolle verander\n\nRolle verander met ouderdom en omstandighede: 'n kind word 'n leerder, dan 'n student of werknemer, later 'n lewensmaat en ouer. 'n Tiener wat 'n deeltydse werk kry of na 'n jonger broer moet kyk, kry nuwe rolle en meer verantwoordelikheid.\n\n### Rolkonflik en verhoudings\n\n**Rolkonflik** ontstaan wanneer die eise van twee of meer rolle bots, bv. 'n leerder wat Saterdae by 'n winkel werk en daarom nie die rugbywedstryd of 'n familiefunksie kan bywoon nie. Rolle beïnvloed verhoudings: as jy minder tyd het, voel vriende of familie dalk verwaarloos, maar 'n nuwe rol kan ook respek en vertroue bou.\n\n### Invloed van die samelewing en kultuur\n\nDie samelewing en kultuur het verwagtinge oor rolle, bv. dat die oudste kind na die jonger kinders kyk, of die stereotipe dat net mans broodwinners is. Vandag word rolle al hoe meer gelykop gedeel.\n\n### Rolle doeltreffend hanteer\n\nPrioritiseer, gebruik 'n rooster, kommunikeer jou behoeftes, vra hulp, ken jou grense (leer om \"nee\" te sê) en maak tyd vir rus.\n\n## Veranderinge op pad na volwassenheid\n\n**Puberteit** is die tydperk waarin die liggaam geslagsryp word. Dit begin gewoonlik vroeër by meisies as by seuns, en elkeen ontwikkel teen sy of haar eie tempo. Dit is normaal.\n\n### 1. Liggaamlike (fisiese) veranderinge\n\nHormone beheer die veranderinge: **testosteroon** by seuns en **estrogeen** by meisies.\n\n- **Groeispurt:** 'n skielike, vinnige toename in lengte; die liggaamsverhoudings verander.\n- **Sekondêre geslagseienskappe by seuns:** 'n dieper stem, gesig- en lyfhare, breër skouers en meer spiere.\n- **Sekondêre geslagseienskappe by meisies:** borste ontwikkel en die heupe word wyer.\n- **By albei:** skaam- en okselhare.\n- **Primêre veranderinge:** meisies begin menstrueer en ovuleer; seuns begin sperms produseer.\n- **Vel en higiëne:** akne (puisies) weens meer olie in die vel, en liggaamsreuk omdat die sweetkliere aktiewer word. Stort daagliks en gebruik 'n reukweerder.\n\n### 2. Emosionele veranderinge\n\nGemoedskommelinge, sterker emosies en soms onsekerheid. Die persoonlikheid word meer volwasse en jy leer emosionele beheer. Jou behoeftes, belangstellings, oortuigings en waardes verander, en seksuele belangstelling ontwikkel – 'n normale deel van grootword.\n\n### 3. Sosiale veranderinge\n\nVerhoudings in die gesin verander en jy het 'n groter behoefte aan **onafhanklikheid**. Die **portuurgroep** word belangriker en die behoefte aan aanvaarding is sterk. Jy beweeg nader aan die werkswêreld (bv. 'n deeltydse werk) en kry meer verantwoordelikheid.\n\n### Portuurdruk\n\n**Portuurdruk** is die invloed wat mense van jou ouderdom op jou het om soos hulle te dink of op te tree.\n\n- **Positief:** vriende moedig jou aan om te studeer, by 'n sportspan aan te sluit of gesond te leef.\n- **Negatief:** druk om te stokkiesdraai, te rook, alkohol te drink of iemand te boelie.\n\n## Verandering hanteer\n\n- **Kommunikeer met ek-boodskappe:** \"Ek voel … wanneer … want … Ek sal graag wil hê …\". Jy beskryf jou gevoel sonder om die ander persoon te blameer.\n- **Luister aktief:** kyk die persoon aan, moenie onderbreek nie, vra vrae en som op wat jy gehoor het.\n- **Praat met 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou:** 'n ouer, onderwyser of die skoolberader.\n- **Maak en behou vriendskappe:** wees betroubaar, respekteer verskille en kies vriende wat jou opbou.\n- **Gesonde roetine:** genoeg slaap, gesonde kos en oefening.\n\n### Ontspanning en emosionele gesondheid\n\nSport en stokperdjies (bv. rugby, stap in die Magaliesberg, musiek) verminder stres, omdat oefening **endorfiene** vrystel wat jou beter laat voel. Dit bou ook selfvertroue en vriendskappe en gee jou 'n gesonde uitlaatklep vir emosies.\n\n> **Eksamenwenk:** As 'n vraag vra dat jy veranderinge noem, sorteer jou antwoord in **fisies, emosioneel en sosiaal**. Dit wys die nasiener dat jy die kategorieë ken.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders skryf net oor liggaamlike veranderinge. Die emosionele en sosiale veranderinge tel net soveel punte.","en":"## Life roles\n\nA **life role** is a position you take up in life or society, with specific expectations and responsibilities. You play many roles at once: child, learner, family member (brother or sister), friend and team-mate. Later you may become a student, employee or employer, life partner, parent (mother or father), grandparent, breadwinner, leader or follower.\n\n| Role | Responsibilities |\n|---|---|\n| Child / family member | respect, help at home, communicate with parents |\n| Learner | attend class, do homework, follow school rules |\n| Employee | be on time, work honestly and reliably, follow workplace rules |\n| Employer | pay fair wages, provide a safe workplace |\n| Parent | care for, protect, teach and support children |\n| Breadwinner | earn money to support the family |\n| Leader | give direction, motivate others, set a good example |\n| Follower | cooperate, carry out instructions, contribute constructively |\n\n### How roles change\n\nRoles change with age and circumstances: a child becomes a learner, then a student or employee, later a life partner and parent. A teenager who gets a part-time job or has to look after a younger brother takes on new roles and more responsibility.\n\n### Role conflict and relationships\n\n**Role conflict** happens when the demands of two or more roles clash, e.g. a learner who works at a shop on Saturdays and therefore cannot attend the rugby match or a family function. Roles affect relationships: if you have less time, friends or family may feel neglected, but a new role can also build respect and trust.\n\n### The influence of society and culture\n\nSociety and culture have expectations about roles, e.g. that the eldest child looks after the younger children, or the stereotype that only men are breadwinners. Today roles are increasingly shared equally.\n\n### Handling roles effectively\n\nPrioritise, use a timetable, communicate your needs, ask for help, know your limits (learn to say \"no\") and make time to rest.\n\n## Changes towards adulthood\n\n**Puberty** is the period in which the body becomes sexually mature. It usually starts earlier in girls than in boys, and everyone develops at his or her own pace. This is normal.\n\n### 1. Physical changes\n\nHormones control the changes: **testosterone** in boys and **oestrogen** in girls.\n\n- **Growth spurt:** a sudden, fast increase in height; body proportions change.\n- **Secondary sex characteristics in boys:** a deeper voice, facial and body hair, broader shoulders and more muscle.\n- **Secondary sex characteristics in girls:** breasts develop and the hips become wider.\n- **In both:** pubic and underarm hair.\n- **Primary changes:** girls start to menstruate and ovulate; boys start to produce sperm.\n- **Skin and hygiene:** acne (pimples) because of more oil in the skin, and body odour because the sweat glands become more active. Shower daily and use a deodorant.\n\n### 2. Emotional changes\n\nMood swings, stronger emotions and sometimes insecurity. The personality matures and you learn emotional control. Your needs, interests, beliefs and values change, and sexual interest develops – a normal part of growing up.\n\n### 3. Social changes\n\nFamily relationships change and you have a greater need for **independence**. The **peer group** becomes more important and the need for acceptance is strong. You move closer to the world of work (e.g. a part-time job) and get more responsibility.\n\n### Peer pressure\n\n**Peer pressure** is the influence that people of your own age have on you to think or act like them.\n\n- **Positive:** friends encourage you to study, join a sports team or live healthily.\n- **Negative:** pressure to bunk, smoke, drink alcohol or bully someone.\n\n## Coping with change\n\n- **Communicate with I-statements:** \"I feel … when … because … I would like …\". You describe your feeling without blaming the other person.\n- **Listen actively:** look at the person, do not interrupt, ask questions and summarise what you heard.\n- **Talk to an adult you trust:** a parent, teacher or the school counsellor.\n- **Make and keep friends:** be reliable, respect differences and choose friends who build you up.\n- **Healthy routine:** enough sleep, healthy food and exercise.\n\n### Recreation and emotional health\n\nSport and hobbies (e.g. rugby, hiking in the Magaliesberg, music) reduce stress, because exercise releases **endorphins** that make you feel better. They also build confidence and friendships and give you a healthy outlet for emotions.\n\n> **Exam tip:** When a question asks you to list changes, sort your answer into **physical, emotional and social**. It shows the marker that you know the categories.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners write only about physical changes. The emotional and social changes count just as many marks."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lewensrol","en":"Life role"},"def":{"af":"'n Posisie wat iemand in die lewe of samelewing inneem, met spesifieke verwagtinge en verantwoordelikhede.","en":"A position someone takes up in life or society, with specific expectations and responsibilities."}},{"term":{"af":"Rolkonflik","en":"Role conflict"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die eise van twee of meer lewensrolle met mekaar bots.","en":"When the demands of two or more life roles clash with each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Puberteit","en":"Puberty"},"def":{"af":"Die tydperk van liggaamlike en emosionele verandering waarin 'n kind geslagsryp word.","en":"The period of physical and emotional change in which a child becomes sexually mature."}},{"term":{"af":"Hormone","en":"Hormones"},"def":{"af":"Chemiese boodskappers in die bloed wat liggaamsveranderinge beheer, bv. testosteroon en estrogeen.","en":"Chemical messengers in the blood that control body changes, e.g. testosterone and oestrogen."}},{"term":{"af":"Sekondêre geslagseienskappe","en":"Secondary sex characteristics"},"def":{"af":"Liggaamlike kenmerke wat tydens puberteit ontwikkel, bv. 'n dieper stem by seuns en wyer heupe by meisies.","en":"Physical features that develop during puberty, e.g. a deeper voice in boys and wider hips in girls."}},{"term":{"af":"Groeispurt","en":"Growth spurt"},"def":{"af":"'n Skielike, vinnige toename in lengte tydens puberteit.","en":"A sudden, fast increase in height during puberty."}},{"term":{"af":"Portuurdruk","en":"Peer pressure"},"def":{"af":"Die invloed van mense van jou ouderdom om soos hulle te dink of op te tree; dit kan positief of negatief wees.","en":"The influence of people of your own age to think or act like them; it can be positive or negative."}},{"term":{"af":"Ek-boodskap","en":"I-statement"},"def":{"af":"'n Manier om jou gevoel uit te druk sonder om te blameer: 'Ek voel … wanneer … want …'.","en":"A way of expressing your feeling without blaming: 'I feel … when … because …'."}},{"term":{"af":"Aktiewe luister","en":"Active listening"},"def":{"af":"Om met volle aandag te luister, nie te onderbreek nie, vrae te vra en op te som wat jy gehoor het.","en":"Listening with full attention, not interrupting, asking questions and summarising what you heard."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Klassifiseer die veranderinge","en":"Classify the changes"},"problem":{"af":"Jaco (15) het die afgelope jaar 10 cm gegroei en sy stem het begin breek. Hy raak gou kwaad en voel die een oomblik bly en die volgende oomblik hartseer. Hy wil nie meer elke naweek saam met sy ouers gaan kuier nie en spandeer al sy tyd saam met sy vriende. Noem twee fisiese, twee emosionele en twee sosiale veranderinge in Jaco se lewe. (6)","en":"Jaco (15) has grown 10 cm in the past year and his voice has started to break. He gets angry quickly and feels happy one moment and sad the next. He no longer wants to go visiting with his parents every weekend and spends all his time with his friends. Name two physical, two emotional and two social changes in Jaco's life. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Fisies:** die groeispurt (10 cm gegroei) (1); 'n dieper stem wat breek – 'n sekondêre geslagseienskap (1).","en":"**Physical:** the growth spurt (grew 10 cm) (1); a deeper voice that breaks – a secondary sex characteristic (1)."},{"af":"**Emosioneel:** hy raak gou kwaad (1); gemoedskommelinge – bly en dan hartseer (1).","en":"**Emotional:** he gets angry quickly (1); mood swings – happy and then sad (1)."},{"af":"**Sosiaal:** 'n groter behoefte aan onafhanklikheid van sy ouers (1); die portuurgroep word belangriker (1).","en":"**Social:** a greater need for independence from his parents (1); the peer group becomes more important (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"Fisies: groeispurt, dieper stem. Emosioneel: gou kwaad, gemoedskommelinge. Sosiaal: behoefte aan onafhanklikheid, portuurgroep belangriker.","en":"Physical: growth spurt, deeper voice. Emotional: quick to anger, mood swings. Social: need for independence, peer group more important."}},{"title":{"af":"'n Rolverandering en verhoudings","en":"A role change and relationships"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato (16) kry 'n Saterdagwerk by 'n kafee by Hartbeespoortdam. Verduidelik hoe hierdie nuwe rol haar verhoudings kan beïnvloed, en stel twee maniere voor om rolkonflik te hanteer. (6)","en":"Lerato (16) gets a Saturday job at a café at Hartbeespoort Dam. Explain how this new role can affect her relationships, and suggest two ways to handle role conflict. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Nuwe rol:** sy is nou 'n *werknemer* bykomend tot 'n leerder, dogter en vriendin – met nuwe verantwoordelikhede (betyds wees, betroubaar werk).","en":"**New role:** she is now an *employee* in addition to being a learner, daughter and friend – with new responsibilities (being on time, working reliably)."},{"af":"**Negatiewe effek:** sy het minder tyd vir vriende en familie op Saterdae, sodat hulle verwaarloos kan voel (1); moegheid kan haar skoolwerk en humeur by die huis raak (1).","en":"**Negative effect:** she has less time for friends and family on Saturdays, so they may feel neglected (1); tiredness can affect her schoolwork and mood at home (1)."},{"af":"**Positiewe effek:** haar ouers vertrou haar met meer verantwoordelikheid (1), en sy verdien eie geld en bou nuwe verhoudings by die werk (1).","en":"**Positive effect:** her parents trust her with more responsibility (1), and she earns her own money and builds new relationships at work (1)."},{"af":"**Hanteer rolkonflik:** maak 'n weeklikse rooster sodat studie en familietyd vas ingeplan is (1); kommunikeer met 'n ek-boodskap met haar werkgewer as 'n belangrike skoolgeleentheid bots (1).","en":"**Handle role conflict:** make a weekly timetable so that study and family time are fixed (1); communicate with an I-statement to her employer when an important school event clashes (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"Die werk bring nuwe verantwoordelikhede en kan verhoudings onder druk plaas, maar ook vertroue bou; beplanning en kommunikasie help om rolkonflik te hanteer.","en":"The job brings new responsibilities and can put relationships under pressure, but can also build trust; planning and communication help to handle role conflict."}},{"title":{"af":"Gee raad aan 'n vriend","en":"Give advice to a friend"},"problem":{"af":"Jou vriend Thabo se ouers is pas geskei. Hy moet nou elke tweede naweek by sy pa in Pretoria bly, hy het opgehou rugby speel en hy raak baie stil. Skryf 'n paragraaf met raad aan Thabo oor hoe hy hierdie verandering kan hanteer. (6)","en":"Your friend Thabo's parents have just divorced. He now has to stay with his dad in Pretoria every second weekend, he has stopped playing rugby and he is becoming very quiet. Write a paragraph of advice to Thabo on how he can cope with this change. (6)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Erken sy gevoelens:** dit is normaal om hartseer, kwaad of onseker te voel wanneer jou gesin verander (1).","en":"**Acknowledge his feelings:** it is normal to feel sad, angry or unsure when your family changes (1)."},{"af":"**Kommunikeer:** praat met albei ouers met 'n ek-boodskap, bv. 'Ek voel uitgelaat wanneer ek nie my wedstryde kan speel nie, want rugby is vir my belangrik. Kan ons 'n plan maak?' (2)","en":"**Communicate:** talk to both parents with an I-statement, e.g. 'I feel left out when I cannot play my matches, because rugby is important to me. Can we make a plan?' (2)"},{"af":"**Kry ondersteuning:** praat met die skoolberader of 'n volwassene wat hy vertrou (1).","en":"**Get support:** talk to the school counsellor or an adult he trusts (1)."},{"af":"**Gesonde roetine en ontspanning:** gaan terug na rugby of 'n ander stokperdjie – oefening verminder stres – en bly naby sy vriende (2).","en":"**Healthy routine and recreation:** go back to rugby or another hobby – exercise reduces stress – and stay close to his friends (2)."}],"answer":{"af":"Erken die gevoelens, kommunikeer met ek-boodskappe, kry ondersteuning van 'n betroubare volwassene en hou 'n gesonde roetine met sport en vriende.","en":"Acknowledge the feelings, communicate with I-statements, get support from a trusted adult and keep a healthy routine with sport and friends."}},{"title":{"af":"Portuurdruk om in te pas","en":"Peer pressure to fit in"},"problem":{"af":"Mia (15) se nuwe vriendegroep wil hê sy moet die laaste periode stokkiesdraai om saam met hulle mall toe te gaan. Hulle sê: 'As jy nie saamkom nie, is jy nie regtig een van ons nie.' (a) Watter soort portuurdruk is dit? Motiveer. (2) (b) Hoe kan Mia reageer? (3)","en":"Mia's (15) new group of friends wants her to bunk the last period to go to the mall with them. They say: 'If you don't come, you're not really one of us.' (a) What kind of peer pressure is this? Motivate. (2) (b) How can Mia respond? (3)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Negatiewe portuurdruk** (1): hulle druk haar om skoolreëls te oortree en gebruik haar behoefte aan aanvaarding teen haar (1).","en":"(a) **Negative peer pressure** (1): they pressure her to break school rules and use her need for acceptance against her (1)."},{"af":"(b) Sê duidelik en kalm nee met 'n ek-boodskap: 'Ek wil nie in die moeilikheid kom nie, want my punte is vir my belangrik.' (1)","en":"(b) Say no clearly and calmly with an I-statement: 'I don't want to get into trouble, because my marks are important to me.' (1)"},{"af":"Stel 'n alternatief voor: 'Kom ons gaan Saterdag saam mall toe.' (1)","en":"Suggest an alternative: 'Let's go to the mall together on Saturday.' (1)"},{"af":"As hulle aanhou druk, besef sy dat ware vriende haar besluite respekteer, en soek sy vriende wat haar opbou (1).","en":"If they keep pushing, she realises that true friends respect her decisions, and she looks for friends who build her up (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Negatiewe portuurdruk. (b) Sê selfgeldend nee met 'n rede, stel 'n alternatief voor en kies vriende wat haar besluite respekteer.","en":"(a) Negative peer pressure. (b) Say no assertively with a reason, suggest an alternative and choose friends who respect her decisions."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter hormoon veroorsaak die meeste liggaamlike veranderinge by seuns tydens puberteit?","en":"Which hormone causes most of the physical changes in boys during puberty?"},"options":[{"af":"Estrogeen","en":"Oestrogen"},{"af":"Insulien","en":"Insulin"},{"af":"Testosteroon","en":"Testosterone"},{"af":"Adrenalien","en":"Adrenaline"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Testosteroon (uit die testes) veroorsaak by seuns 'n dieper stem, gesighare en breër skouers. Estrogeen is die hoofhormoon by meisies.","en":"Testosterone (from the testes) causes a deeper voice, facial hair and broader shoulders in boys. Oestrogen is the main hormone in girls."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die invloed van mense van jou eie ouderdom om soos hulle te dink of op te tree, word ___ genoem.","en":"The influence of people of your own age to think or act like them is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["portuurdruk","groepsdruk","portuurgroepdruk"],"en":["peer pressure"]},"explain":{"af":"Portuurdruk kom van jou portuurgroep (vriende van jou ouderdom). Dit kan positief of negatief wees.","en":"Peer pressure comes from your peer group (friends of your age). It can be positive or negative."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rolkonflik","selfbeeld","puberteit"],"en":["role conflict","self-esteem","puberty"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tydens puberteit kry sowel seuns as meisies skaam- en okselhare.","en":"During puberty both boys and girls get pubic and underarm hair."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Skaam- en okselhare ontwikkel by albei geslagte. Gesighare en 'n dieper stem is egter tipies by seuns.","en":"True. Pubic and underarm hair develop in both sexes. Facial hair and a deeper voice, however, are typical of boys."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n sekondêre geslagseienskap by **meisies**?","en":"Which one is a secondary sex characteristic in **girls**?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Dieper stem","en":"A deeper voice"},{"af":"Wyer heupe","en":"Wider hips"},{"af":"Breër skouers","en":"Broader shoulders"},{"af":"Gesighare","en":"Facial hair"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Wyer heupe en borste is sekondêre geslagseienskappe by meisies. 'n Dieper stem, breër skouers en gesighare is tipies by seuns.","en":"Wider hips and breasts are secondary sex characteristics in girls. A deeper voice, broader shoulders and facial hair are typical of boys."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hormoon ___ veroorsaak die meeste liggaamlike veranderinge by meisies tydens puberteit.","en":"The hormone ___ causes most of the physical changes in girls during puberty."},"answers":{"af":["estrogeen","oestrogeen","estrogen"],"en":["oestrogen","estrogen"]},"explain":{"af":"Estrogeen (uit die eierstokke) veroorsaak by meisies borsontwikkeling, wyer heupe en die begin van menstruasie.","en":"Oestrogen (from the ovaries) causes breast development, wider hips and the start of menstruation in girls."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["testosteroon","adrenalien","insulien"],"en":["testosterone","adrenaline","insulin"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter kategorie hoort **gemoedskommelinge**?","en":"In which category do **mood swings** belong?"},"options":[{"af":"Fisiese veranderinge","en":"Physical changes"},{"af":"Sosiale veranderinge","en":"Social changes"},{"af":"Primêre veranderinge","en":"Primary changes"},{"af":"Emosionele veranderinge","en":"Emotional changes"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Gemoedskommelinge gaan oor gevoelens, dus is dit 'n emosionele verandering – al word dit deels deur hormone veroorsaak.","en":"Mood swings are about feelings, so they are an emotional change – even though they are partly caused by hormones."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer die eise van twee lewensrolle bots, bv. 'n deeltydse werk en skoolwerk, noem ons dit ___.","en":"When the demands of two life roles clash, e.g. a part-time job and schoolwork, we call it ___."},"answers":{"af":["rolkonflik"],"en":["role conflict"]},"explain":{"af":"Rolkonflik ontstaan as jy nie aan die verwagtinge van al jou rolle tegelyk kan voldoen nie. 'n Rolmodel is iemand wat jy navolg.","en":"Role conflict happens when you cannot meet the expectations of all your roles at the same time. A role model is someone you look up to."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["portuurdruk","rolmodel","selfgelding"],"en":["peer pressure","role model","assertiveness"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorbeeld wys **positiewe** portuurdruk?","en":"Which example shows **positive** peer pressure?"},"options":[{"af":"Vriende moedig jou aan om by die atletiekspan aan te sluit","en":"Friends encourage you to join the athletics team"},{"af":"Vriende tart jou om 'n sigaret te probeer","en":"Friends dare you to try a cigarette"},{"af":"Vriende lag vir iemand se nuwe haarstyl en wil hê jy moet saamlag","en":"Friends laugh at someone's new hairstyle and want you to join in"},{"af":"Vriende vra jou om vir hulle te lieg teenoor 'n onderwyser","en":"Friends ask you to lie to a teacher for them"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Positiewe portuurdruk lei jou na gesonde, opbouende keuses soos sport. Die ander voorbeelde druk jou om skadelike of oneerlike dinge te doen.","en":"Positive peer pressure leads you towards healthy, constructive choices such as sport. The other examples push you to do harmful or dishonest things."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Persoon se lewensrolle bly dieselfde regdeur sy of haar lewe.","en":"A person's life roles stay the same throughout his or her life."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Rolle verander met ouderdom en omstandighede, bv. van kind en leerder na werknemer, lewensmaat, ouer en grootouer.","en":"False. Roles change with age and circumstances, e.g. from child and learner to employee, life partner, parent and grandparent."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is 'n goeie **ek-boodskap**?","en":"Which statement is a good **I-statement**?"},"options":[{"af":"'Jy is altyd so selfsugtig!'","en":"'You are always so selfish!'"},{"af":"'Ek voel seergemaak wanneer jy my boodskappe vir ander wys, want dit is privaat. Ek wil hê jy moet dit eers met my uitklaar.'","en":"'I feel hurt when you show my messages to others, because they are private. I want you to check with me first.'"},{"af":"'Ek dink jy is 'n slegte vriend.'","en":"'I think you are a bad friend.'"},{"af":"'Almal weet jy kan nie 'n geheim hou nie.'","en":"'Everyone knows you can't keep a secret.'"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Ek-boodskap beskryf jou gevoel, die situasie, die rede en wat jy wil hê – sonder om te blameer. 'Ek dink jy is …' begin met 'ek', maar is steeds 'n aanval.","en":"An I-statement describes your feeling, the situation, the reason and what you want – without blaming. 'I think you are …' starts with 'I' but is still an attack."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die skielike, vinnige toename in lengte tydens puberteit word die ___ genoem.","en":"The sudden, fast increase in height during puberty is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["groeispurt","groeisprong"],"en":["growth spurt"]},"explain":{"af":"Tydens die groeispurt groei jy vinnig en verander jou liggaamsverhoudings; daarom voel tieners soms lomp.","en":"During the growth spurt you grow fast and your body proportions change; that is why teenagers sometimes feel clumsy."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ovulasie","menstruasie","akne"],"en":["ovulation","menstruation","acne"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke lewensrol by die beste verantwoordelikheid.","en":"Match each life role to the best responsibility."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Leerder","en":"Learner"},"r":{"af":"Klas bywoon en huiswerk doen","en":"Attend class and do homework"}},{"l":{"af":"Broodwinner","en":"Breadwinner"},"r":{"af":"Geld verdien om die gesin te onderhou","en":"Earn money to support the family"}},{"l":{"af":"Werknemer","en":"Employee"},"r":{"af":"Betyds wees en die werkplekreëls volg","en":"Be on time and follow the workplace rules"}},{"l":{"af":"Leier","en":"Leader"},"r":{"af":"Rigting gee en ander motiveer","en":"Give direction and motivate others"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke rol bring sy eie verantwoordelikhede. Iemand kan verskeie rolle tegelyk hê, bv. 'n werknemer wat ook broodwinner is.","en":"Every role brings its own responsibilities. Someone can have several roles at once, e.g. an employee who is also a breadwinner."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Ruan (16) werk sedert 'n maand Saterdae by 'n hardewarewinkel in Brits. Hy mis rugbywedstryde en sy boetie se verjaarsdagpartytjie, en sy punte daal. Wat is die beste verduideliking?","en":"Ruan (16) has been working on Saturdays at a hardware store in Brits for a month. He misses rugby matches and his little brother's birthday party, and his marks are dropping. What is the best explanation?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy beleef negatiewe portuurdruk van sy spanmaats","en":"He is experiencing negative peer pressure from his team-mates"},{"af":"Hy is in 'n groeispurt en kort meer slaap","en":"He is in a growth spurt and needs more sleep"},{"af":"Hy is lui en nie lus vir skool nie","en":"He is lazy and not interested in school"},{"af":"Hy beleef rolkonflik tussen sy rolle as werknemer, leerder, spanmaat en broer","en":"He is experiencing role conflict between his roles as employee, learner, team-mate and brother"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sy nuwe rol as werknemer bots met sy ander rolle, wat sy verhoudings en skoolwerk raak. Niks in die scenario wys op portuurdruk nie.","en":"His new role as an employee clashes with his other roles, which affects his relationships and schoolwork. Nothing in the scenario points to peer pressure."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sport en oefening verbeter emosionele gesondheid omdat die liggaam ___ vrystel wat jou beter laat voel.","en":"Sport and exercise improve emotional health because the body releases ___ that make you feel better."},"answers":{"af":["endorfiene","endorfien","endorfine"],"en":["endorphins","endorphin"]},"explain":{"af":"Endorfiene is die liggaam se 'voel-goed'-stowwe. Gereelde oefening help ook om die stres-hormoon kortisol te verlaag.","en":"Endorphins are the body's 'feel-good' substances. Regular exercise also helps to lower the stress hormone cortisol."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["insulien","kortisol","histamien"],"en":["insulin","cortisol","histamine"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Anika (15) skaam haar vir haar akne en haar veranderende liggaam. Sy bly al hoe meer in haar kamer en vermy haar vriende. Watter raad is die **beste**?","en":"Anika (15) is embarrassed about her acne and her changing body. She stays in her room more and more and avoids her friends. Which advice is **best**?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy moet besef dit is normaal, met 'n vertroude volwassene praat, 'n gesonde roetine volg en aanhou sport doen en vriende sien","en":"She must realise it is normal, talk to a trusted adult, follow a healthy routine and keep doing sport and seeing friends"},{"af":"Sy moet duur velprodukte koop en wegbly tot haar vel skoon is","en":"She must buy expensive skin products and stay away until her skin is clear"},{"af":"Sy moet haarself met beïnvloeders aanlyn vergelyk vir wenke","en":"She must compare herself to influencers online for tips"},{"af":"Sy moet die gevoelens ignoreer; dit gaan vanself weg","en":"She must ignore the feelings; they will go away on their own"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die beste raad kombineer begrip (puberteit is normaal), ondersteuning, gesonde higiëne en roetine, en ontspanning saam met vriende. Onttrekking en vergelyking met beïnvloeders maak haar selfbeeld swakker.","en":"The best advice combines understanding (puberty is normal), support, healthy hygiene and routine, and recreation with friends. Withdrawing and comparing herself to influencers make her self-esteem weaker."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter se nuwe vriende spot hom omdat hy by die skaakklub is, en wil hê hy moet ophou om 'cool' te wees. Watter reaksie wys die **beste** hantering van hierdie portuurdruk?","en":"Pieter's new friends tease him because he is in the chess club and want him to quit to be 'cool'. Which response shows the **best** way of handling this peer pressure?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy hou op met skaak sodat hulle hom aanvaar","en":"He quits chess so that they accept him"},{"af":"Hy skree op hulle en slaan een van hulle","en":"He shouts at them and hits one of them"},{"af":"Hy gaan voort met skaak, sê kalm dat dit vir hom belangrik is, en bly by vriende wat sy keuses respekteer","en":"He carries on with chess, says calmly that it matters to him, and sticks with friends who respect his choices"},{"af":"Hy lieg dat sy ouers hom dwing om skaak te speel","en":"He lies that his parents force him to play chess"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Selfgeldende reaksie beskerm sy waardes en selfbeeld sonder aggressie of oneerlikheid. Toegee wys dat ander jou besluite neem, en aggressie skep nuwe probleme.","en":"An assertive response protects his values and self-esteem without aggression or dishonesty. Giving in shows that others make your decisions, and aggression creates new problems."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t3-seksualiteit-leefstyl","title":{"af":"Verantwoordelike besluite oor seksualiteit en leefstyl","en":"Responsible decisions about sexuality and lifestyle"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal riskante situasies kan herken, toestemming kan verduidelik, die gevolge van tienerswangerskap en SOI's kan bespreek, weierings- en besluitnemingsvaardighede kan toepas en weet waar om hulp te kry.","en":"You will be able to recognise risky situations, explain consent, discuss the consequences of teenage pregnancy and STIs, apply refusal and decision-making skills and know where to get help."},"summary":{"af":"## Gesonde verhoudings en riskante situasies\n\nIn 'n **gesonde verhouding** is daar respek, vertroue, eerlike kommunikasie en gelykheid, en albei voel veilig om \"nee\" te sê. Waarskuwingstekens van 'n ongesonde verhouding is druk, jaloesie, beheer (bv. om jou foon na te gaan) en dreigemente.\n\n**Gedrag wat tot seksuele omgang kan lei:**\n\n- om alleen met 'n maat op riskante plekke te wees (bv. 'n leë huis of 'n motor);\n- **alkohol en dwelms** – dit verswak jou oordeel, sodat dit moeiliker is om goeie besluite te neem;\n- **portuurdruk** – die mite dat \"almal dit doen\";\n- **sexting** – om seksuele boodskappe of foto's te stuur. Sodra jy dit stuur, het jy geen beheer meer daaroor nie. Seksuele foto's van iemand onder 18 word in die wet as kinderpornografie beskou – om dit te maak, te hê of aan te stuur, is 'n misdryf.\n\n## Toestemming\n\n**Toestemming** beteken dat 'n persoon vrywillig en duidelik \"ja\" sê, sonder druk, dreigemente of geweld.\n\n- Toestemming kan **enige tyd teruggetrek** word en moet elke keer gegee word.\n- Stilte, of om nie teë te stribbel nie, is **nie** toestemming nie.\n- Iemand wat **dronk**, onder die invloed van dwelms, **aan die slaap** of bewusteloos is, of wat **gedwing** word, kan nie toestem nie.\n- Die **ouderdom van toestemming is 16 jaar** (Wet op Seksuele Misdrywe 32 van 2007). 'n Kind **jonger as 12** kan glad nie toestem nie.\n\n**Seksuele mishandeling en verkragting** is ernstige misdade. Dit is **nooit** die slagoffer se skuld nie. Vertel 'n vertroude volwassene en kry dadelik hulp.\n\n## Tienerswangerskap: gevolge\n\n| Area | Gevolge |\n|---|---|\n| Gesondheid | 'n Jong liggaam het 'n groter risiko vir komplikasies; voorgeboortelike sorg is nodig |\n| Skoolwerk | Die leerder kan agter raak of uitsak (swanger leerders het wel die reg om in die skool te bly) |\n| Finansies | Doeke, kos en kliniekbesoeke kos geld; albei ouers is wetlik verantwoordelik vir onderhoud |\n| Emosies | Stres, vrees, skaamte en spanning in verhoudings en in die gesin |\n| Die baba | 'n Groter risiko van lae geboortegewig en minder ondersteuning |\n\n## SOI's en MIV\n\n**Seksueel oordraagbare infeksies (SOI's)**, bv. sifilis, gonorree, herpes en MIV, word deur seksuele kontak oorgedra. Baie het geen simptome nie – daarom is toetsing belangrik.\n\nMIV word oorgedra deur bloed, seksuele vloeistowwe en moedersmelk (bv. onbeskermde seks, gedeelde naalde, en van moeder na baba as sy nie behandeling kry nie), maar **nie** deur 'n drukkie, 'n gedeelde koppie of muskiete nie. MIV kan nie genees word nie, maar antiretrovirale behandeling (ARV's) help mense om lank en gesond te leef.\n\n**Voorkoming:**\n\n- **Onthouding** – om nie seks te hê nie; die enigste 100% veilige keuse.\n- **Uitstel van seksuele debuut** – wag totdat jy ouer en gereed is.\n- **Kondome** – korrek gebruik, elke keer.\n- **Toetsing** – MIV-berading en -toetsing (HCT), gratis by klinieke.\n- **PEP** (na-blootstellingsprofilakse) – medikasie wat binne **72 uur** ná moontlike blootstelling (bv. verkragting) begin moet word; hoe gouer, hoe beter.\n\n## Waardes en vaardighede\n\n**Waardes:** respek vir jouself en ander, onthouding, selfbeheersing, privaatheid, jouself beskerm, \"nee\" sê en verantwoordelikheid neem vir jou optrede.\n\n**Besluitnemingstappe:**\n\n1. Identifiseer die probleem of besluit.\n2. Versamel inligting.\n3. Lys jou keuses.\n4. Weeg die gevolge op (kort en lank termyn; jou waardes).\n5. Kies die beste keuse.\n6. Voer dit uit.\n7. Evalueer jou besluit.\n\n**Selfgelding** is om jou behoeftes eerlik en respekvol te stel:\n\n| Styl | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| Passief | \"Okay... as jy so sê.\" (jy gee toe) |\n| Aggressief | \"Los my uit, jou idioot!\" (jy val die ander persoon aan) |\n| Selfgeldend | \"Ek voel ongemaklik as jy my druk. Ek wil nie.\" (ek-boodskap) |\n\n**Weieringsvaardighede:** (1) sê duidelik **nee**, (2) gee 'n **rede**, (3) stel 'n **alternatief** voor, (4) **stap weg** as die druk aanhou.\n\nAnder vaardighede: selfbewustheid, kritiese denke, probleemoplossing, onderhandeling, kommunikasie, doelwitstelling en die insameling van inligting.\n\n## Riskante leefstylkeuses en beskermende faktore\n\n**Riskant:** alkohol, dwelms (bv. dagga en nyaope), partytjies sonder volwassenes (drankies kan gedokter word) en aanlyn risiko's (vreemdelinge wat jou vertroue wen om jou uit te buit).\n\n**Beskermende faktore:** 'n ondersteunende gesin, duidelike doelwitte, positiewe vriende, geloof en waardes, en betrokkenheid by sport of kultuur.\n\n> **Onthou:** 'n Goeie besluit beskerm jou toekoms. As jy onseker is, is die antwoord \"nee\" of \"nog nie\".\n\n## Waar om hulp te kry\n\nOuers, onderwysers, die skoolberader of maatskaplike werker, jeugvriendelike klinieke, **Childline 116**, **Thuthuzela-sorgsentrums** (mediese sorg, polisie, berading en PEP vir verkragtingsoorlewendes op een plek), die **SAPD 10111** en **loveLife**.","en":"## Healthy relationships and risky situations\n\nIn a **healthy relationship** there is respect, trust, honest communication and equality, and both people feel safe to say \"no\". Warning signs of an unhealthy relationship are pressure, jealousy, control (e.g. checking your phone) and threats.\n\n**Behaviour that can lead to sexual intercourse:**\n\n- being alone with a partner in risky places (e.g. an empty house or a car);\n- **alcohol and drugs** – they weaken your judgement, so it is harder to make good decisions;\n- **peer pressure** – the myth that \"everyone is doing it\";\n- **sexting** – sending sexual messages or photos. Once you send it, you no longer have any control over it. By law, sexual photos of anyone under 18 are regarded as child pornography – making, having or forwarding them is a crime.\n\n## Consent\n\n**Consent** means that a person freely and clearly says \"yes\", without pressure, threats or force.\n\n- Consent can be **withdrawn at any time** and must be given every time.\n- Silence, or not resisting, is **not** consent.\n- Someone who is **drunk**, under the influence of drugs, **asleep** or unconscious, or who is **forced**, cannot consent.\n- The **age of consent is 16 years** (Sexual Offences Act 32 of 2007). A child **under 12** cannot consent at all.\n\n**Sexual abuse and rape** are serious crimes. It is **never** the victim's fault. Tell a trusted adult and get help immediately.\n\n## Teenage pregnancy: consequences\n\n| Area | Consequences |\n|---|---|\n| Health | A young body has a higher risk of complications; antenatal care is needed |\n| Schooling | The learner may fall behind or drop out (pregnant learners do have the right to stay in school) |\n| Finances | Nappies, food and clinic visits cost money; both parents are legally responsible for maintenance |\n| Emotions | Stress, fear, shame and tension in relationships and in the family |\n| The baby | A higher risk of low birth weight and less support |\n\n## STIs and HIV\n\n**Sexually transmitted infections (STIs)**, e.g. syphilis, gonorrhoea, herpes and HIV, are passed on through sexual contact. Many have no symptoms – that is why testing is important.\n\nHIV is transmitted through blood, sexual fluids and breast milk (e.g. unprotected sex, shared needles, and from mother to baby if she does not get treatment), but **not** through a hug, a shared cup or mosquitoes. HIV cannot be cured, but antiretroviral treatment (ARVs) helps people live long and healthy lives.\n\n**Prevention:**\n\n- **Abstinence** – not having sex; the only 100% safe choice.\n- **Delaying sexual debut** – waiting until you are older and ready.\n- **Condoms** – used correctly, every time.\n- **Testing** – HIV counselling and testing (HCT), free at clinics.\n- **PEP** (post-exposure prophylaxis) – medication that must be started within **72 hours** after possible exposure (e.g. rape); the sooner, the better.\n\n## Values and skills\n\n**Values:** respect for yourself and others, abstinence, self-control, privacy, protecting yourself, saying \"no\" and taking responsibility for your actions.\n\n**Decision-making steps:**\n\n1. Identify the problem or decision.\n2. Gather information.\n3. List your options.\n4. Weigh up the consequences (short and long term; your values).\n5. Choose the best option.\n6. Carry it out.\n7. Evaluate your decision.\n\n**Assertiveness** means stating your needs honestly and respectfully:\n\n| Style | Example |\n|---|---|\n| Passive | \"Okay... if you say so.\" (you give in) |\n| Aggressive | \"Leave me alone, you idiot!\" (you attack the other person) |\n| Assertive | \"I feel uncomfortable when you pressure me. I don't want to.\" (I-statement) |\n\n**Refusal skills:** (1) say **no** clearly, (2) give a **reason**, (3) suggest an **alternative**, (4) **walk away** if the pressure continues.\n\nOther skills: self-awareness, critical thinking, problem-solving, negotiation, communication, goal-setting and gathering information.\n\n## Risky lifestyle choices and protective factors\n\n**Risky:** alcohol, drugs (e.g. dagga and nyaope), parties without adults (drinks can be spiked) and online risks (strangers who win your trust in order to exploit you).\n\n**Protective factors:** a supportive family, clear goals, positive friends, faith and values, and involvement in sport or culture.\n\n> **Remember:** A good decision protects your future. If you are unsure, the answer is \"no\" or \"not yet\".\n\n## Where to get help\n\nParents, teachers, the school counsellor or social worker, youth-friendly clinics, **Childline 116**, **Thuthuzela Care Centres** (medical care, police, counselling and PEP for rape survivors in one place), **SAPS 10111** and **loveLife**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Toestemming","en":"Consent"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n persoon vrywillig en duidelik \"ja\" sê, sonder druk, dreigemente of geweld; dit kan enige tyd teruggetrek word.","en":"When a person freely and clearly says \"yes\", without pressure, threats or force; it can be withdrawn at any time."}},{"term":{"af":"Ouderdom van toestemming","en":"Age of consent"},"def":{"af":"Die wettige ouderdom (16 jaar in Suid-Afrika) waarop 'n persoon tot seksuele aktiwiteit kan toestem.","en":"The legal age (16 years in South Africa) at which a person can consent to sexual activity."}},{"term":{"af":"Onthouding","en":"Abstinence"},"def":{"af":"Die keuse om nie seks te hê nie; die enigste 100% veilige manier om swangerskap en SOI's te voorkom.","en":"The choice not to have sex; the only 100% safe way to prevent pregnancy and STIs."}},{"term":{"af":"Uitstel van seksuele debuut","en":"Delaying sexual debut"},"def":{"af":"Om jou eerste seksuele ervaring uit te stel totdat jy ouer, ryp en gereed is.","en":"Postponing your first sexual experience until you are older, mature and ready."}},{"term":{"af":"Seksueel oordraagbare infeksie (SOI)","en":"Sexually transmitted infection (STI)"},"def":{"af":"'n Infeksie wat deur seksuele kontak oorgedra word, bv. sifilis, gonorree, herpes en MIV.","en":"An infection passed on through sexual contact, e.g. syphilis, gonorrhoea, herpes and HIV."}},{"term":{"af":"PEP (na-blootstellingsprofilakse)","en":"PEP (post-exposure prophylaxis)"},"def":{"af":"Medikasie wat MIV-infeksie help voorkom as dit binne 72 uur ná moontlike blootstelling begin word.","en":"Medication that helps prevent HIV infection if it is started within 72 hours after possible exposure."}},{"term":{"af":"Selfgelding","en":"Assertiveness"},"def":{"af":"Om jou gevoelens, behoeftes en grense eerlik en respekvol te stel, sonder om passief of aggressief te wees.","en":"Stating your feelings, needs and boundaries honestly and respectfully, without being passive or aggressive."}},{"term":{"af":"Weieringsvaardighede","en":"Refusal skills"},"def":{"af":"Vaardighede om druk te weerstaan: sê duidelik nee, gee 'n rede, stel 'n alternatief voor en stap weg.","en":"Skills to resist pressure: say no clearly, give a reason, suggest an alternative and walk away."}},{"term":{"af":"Portuurdruk","en":"Peer pressure"},"def":{"af":"Die invloed van mense van jou ouderdom om iets te doen wat jy nie self sou kies nie.","en":"The influence of people your age to do something you would not choose yourself."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskermende faktore","en":"Protective factors"},"def":{"af":"Dinge in jou lewe wat jou help om gesonde keuses te maak, bv. 'n ondersteunende gesin, doelwitte, positiewe vriende en waardes.","en":"Things in your life that help you make healthy choices, e.g. a supportive family, goals, positive friends and values."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Gebruik weieringsvaardighede","en":"Use refusal skills"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato (16) is by 'n partytjie in Brits. Haar kêrel, Ruan, wil hê sy moet saam met hom alleen na 'n leë kamer gaan en 'n bier drink. Sy wil nie. Wys hoe sy al vier weieringsvaardighede kan gebruik. (4)","en":"Lerato (16) is at a party in Brits. Her boyfriend, Ruan, wants her to go alone with him to an empty room and drink a beer. She does not want to. Show how she can use all four refusal skills. (4)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Sê duidelik nee:** met 'n vaste stem en oogkontak: \"Nee, Ruan, ek wil nie.\"","en":"**Say no clearly:** with a firm voice and eye contact: \"No, Ruan, I don't want to.\""},{"af":"**Gee 'n rede:** \"Ek is nie gereed nie, en ek drink nie.\" ('n Ek-boodskap wys selfgelding.)","en":"**Give a reason:** \"I am not ready, and I don't drink.\" (An I-statement shows assertiveness.)"},{"af":"**Stel 'n alternatief voor:** \"Kom ons gaan eerder terug na die ander en gaan dans.\"","en":"**Suggest an alternative:** \"Let's rather go back to the others and dance.\""},{"af":"**Stap weg:** as hy aanhou druk, gaan sy terug na haar vriende of bel haar ouers om haar te kom haal. 'n Maat wat jou \"nee\" nie respekteer nie, wys 'n ongesonde verhouding.","en":"**Walk away:** if he keeps pressuring her, she goes back to her friends or phones her parents to fetch her. A partner who does not respect your \"no\" shows an unhealthy relationship."}],"answer":{"af":"Nee sê → rede gee → alternatief voorstel → wegstap.","en":"Say no → give a reason → suggest an alternative → walk away."}},{"title":{"af":"Gevolge van tienerswangerskap","en":"Consequences of teenage pregnancy"},"problem":{"af":"Verduidelik VIER gevolge van tienerswangerskap vir 'n Graad 10-leerder. Noem telkens die area en verduidelik die gevolg. (8)","en":"Explain FOUR consequences of teenage pregnancy for a Grade 10 learner. Each time, name the area and explain the consequence. (8)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Gesondheid:** 'n jong liggaam is nog nie volgroei nie, so daar is 'n groter risiko vir komplikasies tydens die swangerskap en geboorte.","en":"**Health:** a young body is not yet fully grown, so there is a higher risk of complications during pregnancy and birth."},{"af":"**Skoolwerk:** kliniekbesoeke, siekte en die versorging van die baba lei tot afwesigheid, sodat die leerder agter kan raak of uitsak.","en":"**Schooling:** clinic visits, illness and caring for the baby lead to absence, so the learner may fall behind or drop out."},{"af":"**Finansies:** 'n baba het doeke, kos, klere en mediese sorg nodig. Die jong ouers het gewoonlik geen inkomste nie en is van hul gesinne afhanklik.","en":"**Finances:** a baby needs nappies, food, clothes and medical care. The young parents usually have no income and depend on their families."},{"af":"**Emosies:** stres, vrees, skaamte en spanning met die gesin en die maat; die tiener verloor ook vryheid en tyd saam met vriende.","en":"**Emotions:** stress, fear, shame and tension with the family and the partner; the teenager also loses freedom and time with friends."},{"af":"Wenk vir punte: noem die gevolg (1 punt) en verduidelik hoekom dit gebeur (1 punt).","en":"Tip for marks: state the consequence (1 mark) and explain why it happens (1 mark)."}],"answer":{"af":"Bv. gesondheidsrisiko's, skoolwerk ly, finansiële druk en emosionele stres.","en":"E.g. health risks, schooling suffers, financial pressure and emotional stress."}},{"title":{"af":"Feite en mites oor toestemming","en":"Facts and myths about consent"},"problem":{"af":"Sê of elke stelling 'n **feit** of 'n **mite** is en gee 'n rede:\n\n(a) \"As iemand nie nee sê nie, beteken dit ja.\"\n(b) \"'n Persoon mag van plan verander, selfs nadat hy of sy ja gesê het.\"\n(c) \"Iemand wat baie gedrink het, kan nie toestem nie.\"\n(d) \"As julle in 'n verhouding is, hoef jy nie te vra nie.\"","en":"Say whether each statement is a **fact** or a **myth** and give a reason:\n\n(a) \"If someone does not say no, it means yes.\"\n(b) \"A person may change his or her mind, even after saying yes.\"\n(c) \"Someone who has drunk a lot cannot consent.\"\n(d) \"If you are in a relationship, you don't have to ask.\""},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Mite.** Toestemming moet vrywillig en duidelik gegee word. Stilte of om nie teë te stribbel nie, is nie toestemming nie.","en":"(a) **Myth.** Consent must be given freely and clearly. Silence or not resisting is not consent."},{"af":"(b) **Feit.** Toestemming kan enige tyd teruggetrek word, en die ander persoon moet dit respekteer.","en":"(b) **Fact.** Consent can be withdrawn at any time, and the other person must respect that."},{"af":"(c) **Feit.** Alkohol en dwelms verswak 'n persoon se oordeel, so hy of sy kan nie vrywillig en bewustelik toestem nie.","en":"(c) **Fact.** Alcohol and drugs weaken a person's judgement, so he or she cannot consent freely and consciously."},{"af":"(d) **Mite.** Toestemming moet elke keer gegee word – ook in 'n verhouding. 'n Verhouding gee niemand die reg om die ander te dwing nie.","en":"(d) **Myth.** Consent must be given every time – also in a relationship. A relationship gives nobody the right to force the other."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Mite  (b) Feit  (c) Feit  (d) Mite","en":"(a) Myth  (b) Fact  (c) Fact  (d) Myth"}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer 'n besluit (sexting)","en":"Evaluate a decision (sexting)"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo (15) kry 'n intieme foto van 'n klasmaat op sy foon. Sy vriende druk hom om dit na die klasgroep aan te stuur. Gebruik die besluitnemingstappe om Thabo te help om 'n verantwoordelike besluit te neem.","en":"Thabo (15) receives an intimate photo of a classmate on his phone. His friends pressure him to forward it to the class group. Use the decision-making steps to help Thabo make a responsible decision."},"steps":[{"af":"**Identifiseer die probleem:** Thabo word gedruk om 'n privaat, intieme foto van 'n klasmaat verder te stuur.","en":"**Identify the problem:** Thabo is being pressured to forward a private, intimate photo of a classmate."},{"af":"**Versamel inligting:** seksuele foto's van iemand onder 18 word as kinderpornografie beskou – om dit te hê of aan te stuur, is 'n misdryf. Dit skend ook die meisie se privaatheid en waardigheid.","en":"**Gather information:** sexual photos of anyone under 18 are regarded as child pornography – having or forwarding them is a crime. It also violates the girl's privacy and dignity."},{"af":"**Lys keuses en weeg gevolge op:** (1) stuur dit aan – sy word seergemaak en hy oortree die wet; (2) ignoreer dit – die foto versprei dalk steeds; (3) stuur dit nie aan nie en vertel 'n vertroude volwassene – hy beskerm haar en homself.","en":"**List options and weigh consequences:** (1) forward it – she gets hurt and he breaks the law; (2) ignore it – the photo may still spread; (3) don't forward it and tell a trusted adult – he protects her and himself."},{"af":"**Kies en voer uit:** Thabo stuur dit nie aan nie, sê vir sy vriende \"Nee, dis onwettig en gemeen\" (weieringsvaardigheid) en vertel die skoolberader of 'n onderwyser.","en":"**Choose and carry out:** Thabo does not forward it, tells his friends \"No, it's illegal and cruel\" (refusal skill) and tells the school counsellor or a teacher."},{"af":"**Evalueer:** sy besluit wys respek, verantwoordelikheid en die moed om portuurdruk te weerstaan. Die meisie kan by die skoolberader of Childline (116) hulp kry.","en":"**Evaluate:** his decision shows respect, responsibility and the courage to resist peer pressure. The girl can get help from the school counsellor or Childline (116)."}],"answer":{"af":"Moenie die foto aanstuur nie; weier, en vertel 'n vertroude volwassene of die skoolberader.","en":"Don't forward the photo; refuse, and tell a trusted adult or the school counsellor."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die ouderdom van toestemming in Suid-Afrika?","en":"What is the age of consent in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"12 jaar","en":"12 years"},{"af":"18 jaar","en":"18 years"},{"af":"21 jaar","en":"21 years"},{"af":"16 jaar","en":"16 years"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Volgens die Wet op Seksuele Misdrywe (32 van 2007) is die ouderdom van toestemming 16. 'n Kind jonger as 12 kan glad nie toestem nie.","en":"According to the Sexual Offences Act (32 of 2007) the age of consent is 16. A child under 12 cannot consent at all."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die keuse om glad nie seks te hê nie, word ___ genoem.","en":"The choice not to have sex at all is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["onthouding"],"en":["abstinence"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["selfgelding","toestemming","selfagting"],"en":["assertiveness","consent","self-esteem"]}},"explain":{"af":"Onthouding is die enigste 100% veilige manier om swangerskap en SOI's te voorkom. Selfgelding is die vaardigheid om jou grense te stel.","en":"Abstinence is the only 100% safe way to prevent pregnancy and STIs. Assertiveness is the skill of stating your boundaries."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"As iemand vroeër ingestem het, mag hy of sy nie later van plan verander nie.","en":"If someone agreed earlier, he or she may not change their mind later."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Toestemming kan enige tyd teruggetrek word, en dit moet elke keer gegee word.","en":"False. Consent can be withdrawn at any time, and it must be given every time."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter situasie verhoog die risiko dat dinge verder gaan as wat jy wil?","en":"Which situation increases the risk that things go further than you want?"},"options":[{"af":"Saam met 'n groep vriende fliek toe gaan","en":"Going to the movies with a group of friends"},{"af":"Alleen met 'n maat in 'n leë huis wees nadat julle alkohol gedrink het","en":"Being alone with a partner in an empty house after you have drunk alcohol"},{"af":"'n Skoolfunksie bywoon waar onderwysers teenwoordig is","en":"Attending a school function where teachers are present"},{"af":"Met jou ouers oor verhoudings praat","en":"Talking to your parents about relationships"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Om alleen op 'n riskante plek te wees, plus alkohol wat jou oordeel verswak, maak dit baie moeiliker om 'n goeie besluit te neem.","en":"Being alone in a risky place, plus alcohol that weakens your judgement, makes it much harder to make a good decision."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die nasionale hulplyn vir kinders en tieners is Childline: ___.","en":"The national helpline for children and teenagers is Childline: ___."},"answers":{"af":["116"],"en":["116"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10111","10177","112"],"en":["10111","10177","112"]}},"explain":{"af":"Childline se nommer is 116 (gratis). 10111 is die SAPD se noodnommer en 10177 is vir 'n ambulans.","en":"Childline's number is 116 (free). 10111 is the SAPS emergency number and 10177 is for an ambulance."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe word MIV NIE oorgedra nie?","en":"How is HIV NOT transmitted?"},"options":[{"af":"Deur onbeskermde seks","en":"Through unprotected sex"},{"af":"Deur naalde te deel","en":"By sharing needles"},{"af":"Deur iemand te druk of 'n koppie te deel","en":"By hugging someone or sharing a cup"},{"af":"Van 'n moeder na haar baba as sy nie behandeling kry nie","en":"From a mother to her baby if she does not get treatment"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"MIV word deur bloed, seksuele vloeistowwe en moedersmelk oorgedra – nie deur gewone kontak soos 'n drukkie of 'n gedeelde koppie nie. Mense met MIV hoef nie vermy te word nie.","en":"HIV is transmitted through blood, sexual fluids and breast milk – not through ordinary contact such as a hug or a shared cup. People with HIV do not need to be avoided."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"PEP moet binne hoogstens ___ uur ná moontlike blootstelling aan MIV begin word.","en":"PEP must be started within at most ___ hours after possible exposure to HIV."},"answers":{"af":["72"],"en":["72"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["24","48","120"],"en":["24","48","120"]}},"explain":{"af":"PEP werk net as dit binne 72 uur begin word – en hoe gouer, hoe beter. Gaan dus dadelik na 'n kliniek of Thuthuzela-sorgsentrum.","en":"PEP only works if it is started within 72 hours – and the sooner, the better. So go to a clinic or Thuthuzela Care Centre immediately."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vriend druk jou om dagga te probeer. Watter antwoord is selfgeldend?","en":"A friend pressures you to try dagga. Which answer is assertive?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Nee dankie. Ek wil dit nie doen nie, want ek speel Saterdag rugby. Kom ons gaan eerder iets eet.\"","en":"\"No thanks. I don't want to, because I'm playing rugby on Saturday. Let's rather go and get something to eat.\""},{"af":"\"Okay... maar net 'n bietjie.\"","en":"\"Okay... but just a little.\""},{"af":"\"Is jy dom? Los my uit, jou loser!\"","en":"\"Are you stupid? Leave me alone, you loser!\""},{"af":"\"Ek weet nie... miskien later.\"","en":"\"I don't know... maybe later.\""}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die selfgeldende antwoord sê duidelik nee, gee 'n rede en stel 'n alternatief voor – sonder om die ander persoon aan te val. \"Okay\" en \"miskien later\" is passief, en die skel is aggressief.","en":"The assertive answer clearly says no, gives a reason and suggests an alternative – without attacking the other person. \"Okay\" and \"maybe later\" are passive, and the insult is aggressive."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Persoon wat dronk of aan die slaap is, kan nie toestemming gee nie.","en":"A person who is drunk or asleep cannot give consent."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Toestemming moet vrywillig en bewustelik gegee word. Iemand wat dronk, onder die invloed van dwelms, aan die slaap of bewusteloos is, kan dit nie doen nie.","en":"True. Consent must be given freely and consciously. Someone who is drunk, under the influence of drugs, asleep or unconscious cannot do that."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke weieringsvaardigheid by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each refusal skill to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Sê duidelik nee","en":"Say no clearly"},"r":{"af":"\"Nee, ek wil nie.\"","en":"\"No, I don't want to.\""}},{"l":{"af":"Gee 'n rede","en":"Give a reason"},"r":{"af":"\"Ek is nie gereed nie, en dit pas nie by my waardes nie.\"","en":"\"I'm not ready, and it doesn't fit my values.\""}},{"l":{"af":"Stel 'n alternatief voor","en":"Suggest an alternative"},"r":{"af":"\"Kom ons gaan eerder terug na die ander.\"","en":"\"Let's rather go back to the others.\""}},{"l":{"af":"Stap weg","en":"Walk away"},"r":{"af":"Jy gaan terug na jou vriende of bel jou ouers om jou te kom haal.","en":"You go back to your friends or phone your parents to fetch you."}}],"explain":{"af":"Die vier stappe werk saam: 'n duidelike nee, 'n rede, 'n alternatief, en as die druk aanhou, stap jy weg.","en":"The four steps work together: a clear no, a reason, an alternative, and if the pressure continues, you walk away."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n beskermende faktor?","en":"Which one is a protective factor?"},"options":[{"af":"Vriende wat elke naweek partytjie hou sonder volwassenes","en":"Friends who party every weekend without adults"},{"af":"Baie tyd alleen aanlyn met vreemdelinge","en":"Lots of time alone online with strangers"},{"af":"Om dagga te gebruik om stres te hanteer","en":"Using dagga to cope with stress"},{"af":"'n Ondersteunende gesin en duidelike doelwitte vir die toekoms","en":"A supportive family and clear goals for the future"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Beskermende faktore help jou om gesonde keuses te maak. Die ander opsies is risikofaktore wat jou kwesbaar maak.","en":"Protective factors help you make healthy choices. The other options are risk factors that make you vulnerable."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"By ___-sorgsentrums kan verkragtingsoorlewendes mediese sorg, polisiehulp, berading en PEP op een plek kry.","en":"At ___ Care Centres rape survivors can get medical care, police help, counselling and PEP in one place."},"answers":{"af":["Thuthuzela"],"en":["Thuthuzela"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["loveLife","Childline","LifeLine"],"en":["loveLife","Childline","LifeLine"]}},"explain":{"af":"Thuthuzela-sorgsentrums is spesiaal vir verkragtingsoorlewendes. loveLife is 'n jeugprogram oor gesonde leefstyle, en Childline is 'n telefoniese hulplyn.","en":"Thuthuzela Care Centres are specifically for rape survivors. loveLife is a youth programme about healthy lifestyles, and Childline is a telephone helpline."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die laaste stap van besluitneming is om jou besluit te ___ – kyk terug en leer daaruit.","en":"The last step of decision-making is to ___ your decision – look back and learn from it."},"answers":{"af":["evalueer"],"en":["evaluate","review"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["neem","ignoreer","herhaal"],"en":["make","ignore","repeat"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ná jy jou besluit uitgevoer het, evalueer jy dit: was dit 'n goeie besluit en wat sal jy volgende keer anders doen?","en":"After you have carried out your decision, you evaluate it: was it a good decision and what will you do differently next time?"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling oor tienerswangerskap is korrek?","en":"Which statement about teenage pregnancy is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Swanger leerder moet die skool verlaat","en":"A pregnant learner must leave school"},{"af":"Albei ouers is verantwoordelik vir die baba, en die pa moet volgens die wet onderhoud betaal","en":"Both parents are responsible for the baby, and by law the father must pay maintenance"},{"af":"Net die meisie se toekoms word geraak","en":"Only the girl's future is affected"},{"af":"'n Meisie kan nie die eerste keer swanger raak nie","en":"A girl cannot fall pregnant the first time"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Albei ouers het 'n wetlike plig om die kind te onderhou. Swanger leerders het die reg om in die skool te bly, en 'n meisie kán die eerste keer swanger raak – dit is 'n gevaarlike mite.","en":"Both parents have a legal duty to maintain the child. Pregnant learners have the right to stay in school, and a girl can fall pregnant the first time – that is a dangerous myth."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Pieter (15) kry 'n intieme foto van 'n klasmaat, en iemand vra hom om dit aan te stuur. Wat is die beste en wettig korrekte reaksie?","en":"Pieter (15) receives an intimate photo of a classmate, and someone asks him to forward it. What is the best and legally correct response?"},"options":[{"af":"Stuur dit net vir een goeie vriend aan","en":"Forward it to just one good friend"},{"af":"Hou dit op sy foon, maar wys dit vir niemand nie","en":"Keep it on his phone, but show it to nobody"},{"af":"Moenie dit aanstuur nie en vertel dadelik 'n vertroude volwassene of die skoolberader","en":"Don't forward it and immediately tell a trusted adult or the school counsellor"},{"af":"Plaas dit op 'n anonieme rekening sodat niemand weet wie dit was nie","en":"Post it on an anonymous account so nobody knows who it was"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Seksuele foto's van iemand onder 18 word as kinderpornografie beskou – om dit te hê of aan te stuur, is 'n misdryf, en dit skend die klasmaat se privaatheid. 'n Volwassene kan help om die verspreiding te keer.","en":"Sexual photos of anyone under 18 are regarded as child pornography – having or forwarding them is a crime, and it violates the classmate's privacy. An adult can help stop it from spreading."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Nomsa (16) los by 'n partytjie haar drankie onbewaak, en omdat haar foon pap is, klim sy saam met ouer seuns wat sy nie ken nie in 'n motor om huis toe te ry. Wat is die beste evaluering van haar besluite?","en":"At a party Nomsa (16) leaves her drink unattended, and because her phone battery is flat she gets into a car with older boys she does not know to get a lift home. What is the best evaluation of her decisions?"},"options":[{"af":"Riskant: haar drankie kon gedokter word en sy het by vreemdelinge ingeklim; sy moes haar drankie by haar gehou en 'n vertroude persoon se foon geleen het om haar ouers te bel","en":"Risky: her drink could have been spiked and she got into a car with strangers; she should have kept her drink with her and borrowed a trusted person's phone to call her parents"},{"af":"'n Goeie besluit – sy het veilig by die huis gekom, so daar was geen risiko nie","en":"A good decision – she got home safely, so there was no risk"},{"af":"Die enigste probleem was dat haar foon pap was","en":"The only problem was that her phone battery was flat"},{"af":"Dit was die seuns se verantwoordelikheid, so haar keuses maak nie saak nie","en":"It was the boys' responsibility, so her choices don't matter"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie evaluering kyk na die risiko's, nie net na die uitkoms nie. Haar keuses het haar kwesbaar gemaak; beplanning (drankie by jou hou, 'n veilige rit reël) beskerm jou. Dit sou nooit haar skuld wees as iemand haar skade aandoen nie, maar sy kan haar risiko verminder.","en":"A good evaluation looks at the risks, not only the outcome. Her choices made her vulnerable; planning (keeping your drink with you, arranging a safe lift) protects you. It would never be her fault if someone harmed her, but she can reduce her risk."}}]},{"id":"lo10-t3-werkwereld-tendense","title":{"af":"Diversiteit van werk, loopbaangeleenthede en tendense in die arbeidsmark","en":"Diversity of jobs, career opportunities and job-market trends"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal beroepe in ekonomiese sektore kan indeel, loopbaangeleenthede kan ondersoek, tendense in die arbeidsmark kan bespreek en die NKR-vlakke en lewenslange leer kan verduidelik.","en":"You will be able to classify jobs into economic sectors, investigate career opportunities, discuss job-market trends and explain the NQF levels and lifelong learning."},"summary":{"af":"## Diversiteit van werk: die drie ekonomiese sektore\n\nElke werk val in 'n **ekonomiese sektor**. Die sektor wys wat die werker met grondstowwe of mense doen.\n\n| Sektor | Wat gebeur? | Voorbeelde (ook naby Brits) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Primêre sektor** | Grondstowwe word uit die natuur **gewin** | mynbou (die platinummyne naby Brits en Rustenburg), boerdery (sitrusplase), visvang, bosbou |\n| **Sekondêre sektor** | Grondstowwe word **verwerk of vervaardig** tot produkte; **konstruksie** (bou) | 'n vrugtesapfabriek, 'n motorfabriek, 'n bouer, 'n platinumraffinadery |\n| **Tersiêre sektor** | **Dienste** en infrastruktuur word gelewer | toerisme by Hartbeespoortdam, bankwese, gesondheid, onderwys, vervoer (taxi's), kleinhandel |\n\n> **Wenk:** Vra: *Haal die werker iets uit die natuur (primêr), maak of bou hy iets (sekondêr), of lewer hy 'n diens (tersiêr)?* Een produk kan deur al drie sektore beweeg: 'n boer kweek lemoene → 'n fabriek maak sap → 'n winkel verkoop dit.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** 'n Bouer of messelaar is **nie** in die tersiêre sektor nie. Konstruksie is sekondêr.\n\n### Ander maniere om werk te beskryf\n- **Werksomgewing en -toestande:** binne of buite; kantoor, laboratorium, myn (ondergronds, skofwerk, veiligheidstoerusting), plaas; vaste ure of skofte; fisiek swaar of sittend.\n- **Aktiwiteite:** ontwerp, monteer (aanmekaarsit), kweek, herstel, verkoop, versorg, onderrig.\n- **Vaardighede en bevoegdhede:** inligting insamel en ontleed, instruksies gee en onderrig, kommunikasie, spanwerk, probleemoplossing, syfer- en rekenaarvaardighede.\n- **Fasette van die self:** kies werk wat by jou belangstellings, vermoëns, waardes en persoonlikheid pas. Iemand wat van mense hou en geduldig is, sal dalk in onderwys of verpleging gedy.\n\n## Loopbaangeleenthede\nOndersoek 'n loopbaan met **navorsingsvaardighede**: lees loopbaangidse en die webwerwe van universiteite en TVET-kolleges, besoek loopbaanuitstallings, voer 'n onderhoud met iemand in die beroep en doen **werkskaduwee** (job shadowing).\n\n**Ontspanning, fiksheid en sport** bied baie loopbane: biokinetikus, fisioterapeut, persoonlike afrigter, afrigter, sportbestuurder, skeidsregter, sportjoernalis en veldgids.\n\nWanneer jy 'n pos oorweeg, kyk na:\n- die **salarispakket** = basiese salaris + **byvoordele** (mediese fonds, pensioenfonds, bonus, toelaes soos 'n reis- of behuisingstoelae);\n- **bevorderingsgeleenthede** en geleenthede vir **verdere studie**;\n- **oordraagbare vaardighede** wat jy na 'n verwante bedryf kan saamneem, bv. 'n mynveiligheidsbeampte kan in konstruksie werk, en 'n kelner se kliëntediens help in kleinhandel.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders vergelyk net die basiese salaris. Twee poste met dieselfde salaris kan baie verskil as een ook mediese fonds en pensioen insluit.\n\n## Tendense en aanvraag in die arbeidsmark\n'n **Tendens** is 'n patroon of rigting van verandering oor tyd.\n\n- **Nuwe aanvraag:** IKT (inligtings- en kommunikasietegnologie), kunsmatige intelligensie (KI) en die **Vierde Nywerheidsrewolusie** (4NR: robotika, data, die internet van dinge); die **groen ekonomie** (sonpaneelinstalleerders, herwinning; tydens beurtkrag het baie huise na sonkrag oorgeskakel); **ambagslui** (elektrisiëns, loodgieters, sweisers); gesondheidsorg (verpleegkundiges).\n- **Veranderende loopbaanpatrone:** kontrak- en *gig*-werk (bv. aflewering via 'n app), mense wat **verskeie loopbane** in een leeftyd het, en **entrepreneurskap** (jou eie besigheid begin).\n- **Skaars vaardighede:** vaardighede waarvoor daar te **min** gekwalifiseerde mense is. Die Departement van Hoër Onderwys en Opleiding publiseer gereeld 'n lys van beroepe in hoë aanvraag.\n- **Groei en afname:** sommige beroepe groei (data-ontleders, sagteware-ontwikkelaars, soninstalleerders); ander krimp of verander weens outomatisering (kassiere by selfbedieningstoonbanke, tikkers, telefoniste).\n- **Lees die mark:** soek 'n **nis** – 'n behoefte wat nog nie gevul is nie, bv. 'n sonpaneel-skoonmaakdiens in Madibeng.\n\n## SAKO en die NKR\n**SAKO** (Suid-Afrikaanse Kwalifikasie-owerheid; SAQA) bestuur die **NKR** (Nasionale Kwalifikasieraamwerk; NQF). Die NKR het **10 vlakke** sodat kwalifikasies regoor die land vergelyk kan word.\n\n| NKR-vlak | Kwalifikasie |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Graad 9 |\n| 2–3 | Graad 10–11 (en TVET se NC(V)-vlakke 2–3) |\n| 4 | **NSS** (matriek) en NC(V)-vlak 4 |\n| 5 | Hoër sertifikaat |\n| 6 | Diploma |\n| 7 | Baccalaureusgraad of gevorderde diploma |\n| 8 | Honneursgraad of nagraadse diploma |\n| 9 | Meestersgraad |\n| 10 | Doktorsgraad |\n\n**Erkenning van vorige leer (EVL; RPL):** kennis en vaardighede wat jy deur werk en ervaring opgedoen het, word geassesseer en erken vir toelating of vir 'n deel van 'n kwalifikasie.\n\n## Lewenslange leer\n**Lewenslange leer** beteken om jou hele lewe lank aan te hou leer sodat jy kan verander, heroplei en buigsaam bly. Dit is belangrik omdat tegnologie werk vinnig verander, sommige poste verdwyn terwyl nuwes ontstaan, en werkgewers mense soek wat kan aanpas.\n\n| Tipe leer | Beskrywing | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Formeel** | georganiseer en **geakkrediteer**; lei tot 'n NKR-kwalifikasie | skool, universiteit, TVET-kollege |\n| **Nie-formeel** | georganiseer, maar **nie geakkrediteer** nie | 'n kort rekenaarkursus, 'n noodhulpkursus |\n| **Informeel** | alledaagse, ongeorganiseerde leer | by familie leer, aanlyn video's kyk |\n\n> **Onthou!** Eksamenvrae vra dat jy beroepe in sektore indeel, die NKR-vlak van 'n kwalifikasie gee, verduidelik waarom lewenslange leer saak maak, en 'n tendens **met voorbeelde** bespreek.","en":"## Diversity of jobs: the three economic sectors\n\nEvery job falls into an **economic sector**. The sector shows what the worker does with raw materials or people.\n\n| Sector | What happens? | Examples (also near Brits) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Primary sector** | Raw materials are **extracted** from nature | mining (the platinum mines near Brits and Rustenburg), farming (citrus farms), fishing, forestry |\n| **Secondary sector** | Raw materials are **processed or manufactured** into products; **construction** | a fruit-juice factory, a car factory, a builder, a platinum refinery |\n| **Tertiary sector** | **Services** and infrastructure are provided | tourism at Hartbeespoort Dam, banking, health, education, transport (taxis), retail |\n\n> **Tip:** Ask: *Does the worker take something from nature (primary), make or build something (secondary), or provide a service (tertiary)?* One product can move through all three sectors: a farmer grows oranges → a factory makes juice → a shop sells it.\n\n> **Common mistake:** A builder or bricklayer is **not** in the tertiary sector. Construction is secondary.\n\n### Other ways to describe work\n- **Work settings and conditions:** indoors or outdoors; office, laboratory, mine (underground, shift work, safety equipment), farm; fixed hours or shifts; physically hard or seated.\n- **Activities:** designing, assembling, growing, repairing, selling, caring, teaching.\n- **Skills and competencies:** gathering and analysing information, instructing and teaching, communication, teamwork, problem-solving, numeracy and computer skills.\n- **Facets of self:** choose work that fits your interests, abilities, values and personality. Someone who likes people and is patient may thrive in teaching or nursing.\n\n## Career opportunities\nInvestigate a career with **research skills**: read career guides and the websites of universities and TVET colleges, visit career expos, interview someone in the occupation and do **job shadowing**.\n\n**Recreation, fitness and sport** offer many careers: biokineticist, physiotherapist, personal trainer, coach, sport manager, referee, sport journalist and field guide.\n\nWhen you consider a post, look at:\n- the **salary package** = basic salary + **benefits** (medical aid, pension fund, bonus, allowances such as a travel or housing allowance);\n- **promotion prospects** and opportunities for **further study**;\n- **transferable skills** you can take to a related industry, e.g. a mine safety officer can work in construction, and a waiter's customer service helps in retail.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners compare only the basic salary. Two posts with the same salary can differ a lot if one also includes medical aid and a pension.\n\n## Trends and demands in the job market\nA **trend** is a pattern or direction of change over time.\n\n- **Emerging demands:** ICT (information and communication technology), artificial intelligence (AI) and the **Fourth Industrial Revolution** (4IR: robotics, data, the internet of things); the **green economy** (solar-panel installers, recycling; during load-shedding many homes switched to solar power); **artisans** (electricians, plumbers, welders); health care (nurses).\n- **Changing career patterns:** contract and *gig* work (e.g. deliveries through an app), people having **several careers** in one lifetime, and **entrepreneurship** (starting your own business).\n- **Scarce skills:** skills for which there are too **few** qualified people. The Department of Higher Education and Training regularly publishes a list of occupations in high demand.\n- **Growth and decline:** some occupations grow (data analysts, software developers, solar installers); others shrink or change because of automation (cashiers at self-service tills, typists, switchboard operators).\n- **Read the market:** look for a **niche** – a need that has not yet been met, e.g. a solar-panel cleaning service in Madibeng.\n\n## SAQA and the NQF\n**SAQA** (South African Qualifications Authority) oversees the **NQF** (National Qualifications Framework). The NQF has **10 levels** so that qualifications can be compared across the country.\n\n| NQF level | Qualification |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Grade 9 |\n| 2–3 | Grades 10–11 (and TVET NC(V) levels 2–3) |\n| 4 | **NSC** (matric) and NC(V) level 4 |\n| 5 | Higher certificate |\n| 6 | Diploma |\n| 7 | Bachelor's degree or advanced diploma |\n| 8 | Honours degree or postgraduate diploma |\n| 9 | Master's degree |\n| 10 | Doctorate |\n\n**Recognition of prior learning (RPL):** knowledge and skills you gained through work and experience are assessed and recognised for admission or for part of a qualification.\n\n## Lifelong learning\n**Lifelong learning** means continuing to learn throughout your life so that you can change, retrain and stay flexible. It matters because technology changes work quickly, some posts disappear while new ones appear, and employers look for people who can adapt.\n\n| Type of learning | Description | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Formal** | organised and **accredited**; leads to an NQF qualification | school, university, TVET college |\n| **Non-formal** | organised but **not accredited** | a short computer course, a first-aid course |\n| **Informal** | everyday, unorganised learning | learning from family, watching online videos |\n\n> **Remember!** Exam questions ask you to classify jobs into sectors, give the NQF level of a qualification, explain why lifelong learning matters, and discuss a trend **with examples**."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Primêre sektor","en":"Primary sector"},"def":{"af":"Die ekonomiese sektor wat grondstowwe uit die natuur win, bv. mynbou, boerdery, visvang en bosbou.","en":"The economic sector that extracts raw materials from nature, e.g. mining, farming, fishing and forestry."}},{"term":{"af":"Sekondêre sektor","en":"Secondary sector"},"def":{"af":"Die ekonomiese sektor wat grondstowwe verwerk of vervaardig tot produkte, insluitend konstruksie.","en":"The economic sector that processes or manufactures raw materials into products, including construction."}},{"term":{"af":"Tersiêre sektor","en":"Tertiary sector"},"def":{"af":"Die ekonomiese sektor wat dienste en infrastruktuur lewer, bv. toerisme, bankwese, gesondheid, onderwys en vervoer.","en":"The economic sector that provides services and infrastructure, e.g. tourism, banking, health, education and transport."}},{"term":{"af":"Salarispakket","en":"Salary package"},"def":{"af":"Die basiese salaris plus byvoordele soos mediese fonds, pensioen, bonus en toelaes.","en":"The basic salary plus benefits such as medical aid, pension, bonus and allowances."}},{"term":{"af":"Skaars vaardighede","en":"Scarce skills"},"def":{"af":"Vaardighede waarvoor daar te min gekwalifiseerde mense in die arbeidsmark is.","en":"Skills for which there are too few qualified people in the job market."}},{"term":{"af":"Oordraagbare vaardighede","en":"Transferable skills"},"def":{"af":"Vaardighede wat jy van een werk of bedryf na 'n ander, verwante bedryf kan saamneem.","en":"Skills you can take from one job or industry to another, related industry."}},{"term":{"af":"Vierde Nywerheidsrewolusie (4NR)","en":"Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR)"},"def":{"af":"Die huidige fase van tegnologiese verandering waarin KI, robotika, data en die internet van dinge werk verander.","en":"The current phase of technological change in which AI, robotics, data and the internet of things change work."}},{"term":{"af":"NKR (Nasionale Kwalifikasieraamwerk)","en":"NQF (National Qualifications Framework)"},"def":{"af":"'n Stelsel van 10 vlakke, bestuur deur SAKO, waarvolgens alle Suid-Afrikaanse kwalifikasies ingedeel en vergelyk word.","en":"A system of 10 levels, overseen by SAQA, by which all South African qualifications are classified and compared."}},{"term":{"af":"Erkenning van vorige leer (EVL)","en":"Recognition of prior learning (RPL)"},"def":{"af":"Die assessering en erkenning van kennis en vaardighede wat deur werk en ervaring opgedoen is.","en":"The assessment and recognition of knowledge and skills gained through work and experience."}},{"term":{"af":"Lewenslange leer","en":"Lifelong learning"},"def":{"af":"Om deur jou hele lewe aan te hou leer (formeel, nie-formeel en informeel) sodat jy kan aanpas en heroplei.","en":"Continuing to learn throughout your life (formally, non-formally and informally) so that you can adapt and retrain."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Deel werkers in ekonomiese sektore in","en":"Classify workers into economic sectors"},"problem":{"af":"Deel elke werker in Madibeng in die regte ekonomiese sektor in: (a) 'n rotsboorder by 'n platinummyn naby Brits, (b) 'n werker in 'n vrugtesapfabriek, (c) 'n gids by die Hartbeespoort-kabelkarbaan, (d) 'n sitrusplukker, (e) 'n messelaar wat 'n winkelsentrum bou, (f) 'n bankteller. (6 punte)","en":"Classify each worker in Madibeng into the correct economic sector: (a) a rock-drill operator at a platinum mine near Brits, (b) a worker in a fruit-juice factory, (c) a guide at the Hartbeespoort cableway, (d) a citrus picker, (e) a bricklayer building a shopping centre, (f) a bank teller. (6 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"Reël: primêr = haal grondstowwe uit die natuur; sekondêr = verwerk, vervaardig of bou; tersiêr = lewer 'n diens.","en":"Rule: primary = takes raw materials from nature; secondary = processes, manufactures or builds; tertiary = provides a service."},{"af":"(a) Die rotsboorder haal erts uit die aarde → primêr. (d) Die sitrusplukker oes vrugte op die plaas → primêr.","en":"(a) The rock-drill operator takes ore out of the earth → primary. (d) The citrus picker harvests fruit on the farm → primary."},{"af":"(b) Die fabriekswerker verwerk vrugte tot sap → sekondêr. (e) Die messelaar werk in konstruksie → sekondêr (nie 'n diens nie!).","en":"(b) The factory worker processes fruit into juice → secondary. (e) The bricklayer works in construction → secondary (not a service!)."},{"af":"(c) Die gids lewer 'n toerismediens → tersiêr. (f) Die bankteller lewer 'n finansiële diens → tersiêr.","en":"(c) The guide provides a tourism service → tertiary. (f) The bank teller provides a financial service → tertiary."}],"answer":{"af":"Primêr: (a), (d); Sekondêr: (b), (e); Tersiêr: (c), (f)","en":"Primary: (a), (d); Secondary: (b), (e); Tertiary: (c), (f)"}},{"title":{"af":"Gee die NKR-vlak","en":"Give the NQF level"},"problem":{"af":"Thandi wil in sportwetenskap studeer. Haar beplande studiepad is: NSS (matriek) → BSc in Sportwetenskap → Honneursgraad in Biokinetika. Haar broer beplan: Hoër Sertifikaat in Sportbestuur → Diploma in Sportbestuur. Gee die NKR-vlak van elke kwalifikasie en sê wie op die hoogste vlak eindig. (6 punte)","en":"Thandi wants to study sport science. Her planned study path is: NSC (matric) → BSc in Sport Science → Honours degree in Biokinetics. Her brother plans: Higher Certificate in Sport Management → Diploma in Sport Management. Give the NQF level of each qualification and say who ends at the highest level. (6 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"NSS (matriek) = NKR-vlak 4.","en":"NSC (matric) = NQF level 4."},{"af":"Thandi: BSc (baccalaureusgraad) = vlak 7; Honneursgraad = vlak 8.","en":"Thandi: BSc (bachelor's degree) = level 7; Honours degree = level 8."},{"af":"Broer: Hoër Sertifikaat = vlak 5; Diploma = vlak 6.","en":"Brother: Higher Certificate = level 5; Diploma = level 6."},{"af":"Vergelyk: 8 > 6, dus eindig Thandi hoër. Haar broer kan later verder studeer (bv. 'n gevorderde diploma op vlak 7) – dit is lewenslange leer.","en":"Compare: 8 > 6, so Thandi ends higher. Her brother can study further later (e.g. an advanced diploma at level 7) – that is lifelong learning."}],"answer":{"af":"NSS 4; BSc 7; Honneurs 8; Hoër Sertifikaat 5; Diploma 6. Thandi eindig op die hoogste vlak (8).","en":"NSC 4; BSc 7; Honours 8; Higher Certificate 5; Diploma 6. Thandi ends at the highest level (8)."}},{"title":{"af":"Vergelyk twee salarispakkette","en":"Compare two salary packages"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter kry twee werksaanbiedinge in Brits. Pos A (winkel): basiese salaris R12 000 per maand, geen byvoordele nie. Pos B (myn): basiese salaris R11 000 per maand, plus die werkgewer betaal R1 200 per maand vir mediese fonds en R800 per maand vir pensioen. Watter pos bied die beter pakket? Noem twee ander faktore wat hy moet oorweeg. (5 punte)","en":"Pieter gets two job offers in Brits. Post A (shop): basic salary R12 000 per month, no benefits. Post B (mine): basic salary R11 000 per month, plus the employer pays R1 200 per month towards medical aid and R800 per month towards a pension. Which post offers the better package? Name two other factors he should consider. (5 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"Pos A se pakket = R12 000 (net die basiese salaris).","en":"Post A's package = R12 000 (only the basic salary)."},{"af":"Pos B se pakket = R11 000 + R1 200 + R800 = R13 000 per maand.","en":"Post B's package = R11 000 + R1 200 + R800 = R13 000 per month."},{"af":"R13 000 − R12 000 = R1 000: Pos B se pakket is R1 000 per maand meer werd, al is die basiese salaris laer.","en":"R13 000 − R12 000 = R1 000: Post B's package is worth R1 000 more per month, even though the basic salary is lower."},{"af":"Ander faktore: werksomstandighede (ondergrondse skofwerk teenoor 'n winkel), bevorderingsgeleenthede, geleenthede vir verdere studie, en of die werk by sy belangstellings en waardes pas.","en":"Other factors: working conditions (underground shift work versus a shop), promotion prospects, opportunities for further study, and whether the work fits his interests and values."}],"answer":{"af":"Pos B (R13 000 teenoor R12 000). Oorweeg ook werksomstandighede en bevordering/verdere studie.","en":"Post B (R13 000 versus R12 000). Also consider working conditions and promotion/further study."}},{"title":{"af":"Lewenslange leer en oordraagbare vaardighede","en":"Lifelong learning and transferable skills"},"problem":{"af":"Sipho (45) werk al 20 jaar as elektrisiën by 'n myn naby Brits. Die myn sny poste. Verduidelik hoe lewenslange leer, oordraagbare vaardighede en 'n tendens in die arbeidsmark hom kan help om weer werk te kry. (6 punte)","en":"Sipho (45) has worked as an electrician at a mine near Brits for 20 years. The mine is cutting posts. Explain how lifelong learning, transferable skills and a job-market trend can help him find work again. (6 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"Lewenslange leer: hy moet bereid wees om aan te hou leer en heroplei, want werk verander en sommige poste verdwyn.","en":"Lifelong learning: he must be willing to keep learning and retraining, because work changes and some posts disappear."},{"af":"Oordraagbare vaardighede: sy kennis van bedrading, veiligheid en foutopsporing is ook in konstruksie, fabrieke en huise bruikbaar.","en":"Transferable skills: his knowledge of wiring, safety and fault-finding is also useful in construction, factories and homes."},{"af":"Tendens: die groen ekonomie groei – na beurtkrag wil baie mense sonkrag hê. 'n Kursus in soninstallasie bou op wat hy reeds kan.","en":"Trend: the green economy is growing – after load-shedding many people want solar power. A course in solar installation builds on what he can already do."},{"af":"Hy kan EVL gebruik sodat sy ervaring erken word, en hy kan entrepreneurskap oorweeg deur sy eie installasiebesigheid in Madibeng te begin.","en":"He can use RPL so that his experience is recognised, and he can consider entrepreneurship by starting his own installation business in Madibeng."}],"answer":{"af":"Hy moet heroplei (lewenslange leer), sy oordraagbare elektriese vaardighede gebruik en die groeiende vraag na soninstallasie benut, eers as werknemer of as entrepreneur.","en":"He should retrain (lifelong learning), use his transferable electrical skills and take advantage of the growing demand for solar installation, as an employee or as an entrepreneur."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter ekonomiese sektor werk 'n mynwerker by 'n platinummyn naby Brits?","en":"In which economic sector does a miner at a platinum mine near Brits work?"},"options":[{"af":"Tersiêre sektor","en":"Tertiary sector"},{"af":"Primêre sektor","en":"Primary sector"},{"af":"Sekondêre sektor","en":"Secondary sector"},{"af":"Openbare sektor","en":"Public sector"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Mynbou haal grondstowwe (platinumerts) uit die natuur, en dit is die primêre sektor. 'Openbare sektor' sê wie die werkgewer is (die regering), nie watter soort werk dit is nie.","en":"Mining extracts raw materials (platinum ore) from nature, so it is the primary sector. 'Public sector' tells you who the employer is (the government), not what kind of work it is."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die ___ sektor lewer dienste, soos bankwese, toerisme, gesondheid en onderwys.","en":"The ___ sector provides services, such as banking, tourism, health and education."},"answers":{"af":["tersiêre","tersiere","tersiêr","tersier","tertiary"],"en":["tertiary","tersiêre"]},"explain":{"af":"Die tersiêre sektor lewer dienste. Die primêre sektor win grondstowwe en die sekondêre sektor verwerk of vervaardig.","en":"The tertiary sector provides services. The primary sector extracts raw materials and the secondary sector processes or manufactures."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["primêre","sekondêre","informele"],"en":["primary","secondary","informal"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die NKR (Nasionale Kwalifikasieraamwerk) het 10 vlakke, en vlak 10 is 'n doktorsgraad.","en":"The NQF (National Qualifications Framework) has 10 levels, and level 10 is a doctorate."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die NKR strek van vlak 1 (Graad 9) tot vlak 10 ('n doktorsgraad). Die NSS (matriek) is op vlak 4.","en":"True. The NQF runs from level 1 (Grade 9) to level 10 (a doctorate). The NSC (matric) is at level 4."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter liggaam bestuur die NKR in Suid-Afrika?","en":"Which body oversees the NQF in South Africa?"},"options":[{"af":"SAKO (Suid-Afrikaanse Kwalifikasie-owerheid)","en":"SAQA (South African Qualifications Authority)"},{"af":"NSFAS (Nasionale Finansiële Hulpskema vir Studente)","en":"NSFAS (National Student Financial Aid Scheme)"},{"af":"SAID (Suid-Afrikaanse Inkomstediens)","en":"SARS (South African Revenue Service)"},{"af":"NYDA (Nasionale Jeugontwikkelingsagentskap)","en":"NYDA (National Youth Development Agency)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"SAKO (SAQA) bestuur die NKR en registreer kwalifikasies. NSFAS gee studiefinansiering, SAID vorder belasting in en die NYDA ondersteun jeugontwikkeling.","en":"SAQA oversees the NQF and registers qualifications. NSFAS provides study funding, SARS collects tax and the NYDA supports youth development."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Baccalaureusgraad (bv. 'n BCom of BSc) is op NKR-vlak ___.","en":"A bachelor's degree (e.g. a BCom or BSc) is at NQF level ___."},"answers":{"af":["7","sewe"],"en":["7","seven"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Baccalaureusgraad is op vlak 7. 'n Diploma is op vlak 6, 'n hoër sertifikaat op vlak 5 en 'n honneursgraad op vlak 8.","en":"A bachelor's degree is at level 7. A diploma is at level 6, a higher certificate at level 5 and an honours degree at level 8."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["6","8","5"],"en":["6","8","5"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n voorbeeld van nie-formele leer?","en":"Which one is an example of non-formal learning?"},"options":[{"af":"'n BSc-graad aan 'n universiteit","en":"A BSc degree at a university"},{"af":"Leer om vleis te braai deur jou oupa dop te hou","en":"Learning to braai meat by watching your grandfather"},{"af":"'n Kort noodhulpkursus by 'n sportklub wat nie tot 'n kwalifikasie lei nie","en":"A short first-aid course at a sports club that does not lead to a qualification"},{"af":"Graad 10 by Hoërskool Brits","en":"Grade 10 at Hoërskool Brits"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Nie-formele leer is georganiseer, maar nie geakkrediteer nie. Die graad en Graad 10 is formeel (geakkrediteer, op die NKR); om by jou oupa te leer, is informeel.","en":"Non-formal learning is organised but not accredited. The degree and Grade 10 are formal (accredited, on the NQF); learning from your grandfather is informal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bouer wat nuwe huise in Hartbeespoort oprig, werk in die ...","en":"A builder who puts up new houses in Hartbeespoort works in the ..."},"options":[{"af":"primêre sektor, want hy werk met stene en sand","en":"primary sector, because he works with bricks and sand"},{"af":"tersiêre sektor, want hy lewer 'n diens aan die huiseienaar","en":"tertiary sector, because he provides a service to the home owner"},{"af":"informele sektor, want hy werk buite","en":"informal sector, because he works outdoors"},{"af":"sekondêre sektor, want konstruksie val onder die sekondêre sektor","en":"secondary sector, because construction falls under the secondary sector"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Konstruksie is deel van die sekondêre sektor: materiale word verwerk tot iets nuuts ('n huis). Dit is 'n algemene fout om bou as 'n diens te sien. Om buite te werk, sê niks oor die sektor nie.","en":"Construction is part of the secondary sector: materials are processed into something new (a house). Seeing building as a service is a common mistake. Working outdoors says nothing about the sector."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Salarispakket bestaan uit die basiese salaris plus ___ soos mediese fonds, pensioen en toelaes.","en":"A salary package consists of the basic salary plus ___ such as medical aid, pension and allowances."},"answers":{"af":["byvoordele","voordele","benefits"],"en":["benefits","fringe benefits","byvoordele"]},"explain":{"af":"Byvoordele (mediese fonds, pensioen, bonus, toelaes) maak die pakket meer werd. Aftrekkings en belasting word juis van die bruto salaris afgetrek.","en":"Benefits (medical aid, pension, bonus, allowances) make the package worth more. Deductions and tax are taken off the gross salary."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aftrekkings","belasting","lenings"],"en":["deductions","tax","loans"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Skaars vaardighede is vaardighede waarvoor daar meer gekwalifiseerde mense is as wat werkgewers nodig het.","en":"Scarce skills are skills for which there are more qualified people than employers need."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is andersom: skaars vaardighede is vaardighede waarvoor daar te min gekwalifiseerde mense is, bv. sekere ambagte. Daarom bied hulle goeie werksgeleenthede.","en":"False. It is the other way round: scarce skills are skills for which there are too few qualified people, e.g. certain trades. That is why they offer good job opportunities."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke NKR-vlak by die regte kwalifikasie.","en":"Match each NQF level to the correct qualification."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Vlak 4","en":"Level 4"},"r":{"af":"NSS (matriek)","en":"NSC (matric)"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlak 5","en":"Level 5"},"r":{"af":"Hoër sertifikaat","en":"Higher certificate"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlak 6","en":"Level 6"},"r":{"af":"Diploma","en":"Diploma"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlak 8","en":"Level 8"},"r":{"af":"Honneursgraad","en":"Honours degree"}},{"l":{"af":"Vlak 10","en":"Level 10"},"r":{"af":"Doktorsgraad","en":"Doctorate"}}],"explain":{"af":"4 = NSS, 5 = hoër sertifikaat, 6 = diploma, 7 = baccalaureusgraad, 8 = honneursgraad, 9 = meestersgraad, 10 = doktorsgraad.","en":"4 = NSC, 5 = higher certificate, 6 = diploma, 7 = bachelor's degree, 8 = honours degree, 9 = master's degree, 10 = doctorate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato is mal oor rugby en netbal, skryf goeie opstelle en praat graag met mense. Sy wil in die media werk. Watter loopbaan in sport pas die beste by haar?","en":"Lerato loves rugby and netball, writes good essays and enjoys talking to people. She wants to work in the media. Which sport career suits her best?"},"options":[{"af":"Fisioterapeut","en":"Physiotherapist"},{"af":"Skeidsregter","en":"Referee"},{"af":"Biokinetikus","en":"Biokineticist"},{"af":"Sportjoernalis","en":"Sport journalist"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Sportjoernalis kombineer haar liefde vir sport met haar skryf- en kommunikasievaardighede en haar belangstelling in die media. Dit is hoe jy fasette van die self met die wêreld van werk integreer.","en":"A sport journalist combines her love of sport with her writing and communication skills and her interest in the media. This is how you integrate facets of self into the world of work."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vaardighede wat jy na 'n ander, verwante bedryf kan saamneem (bv. 'n kelner se kliëntediens wat in kleinhandel help), word ___ vaardighede genoem.","en":"Skills you can take to another, related industry (e.g. a waiter's customer service that helps in retail) are called ___ skills."},"answers":{"af":["oordraagbare","oordraagbaar","transferable"],"en":["transferable","oordraagbare"]},"explain":{"af":"Oordraagbare vaardighede (bv. kommunikasie, spanwerk, kliëntediens) maak dit makliker om van werk of bedryf te verander.","en":"Transferable skills (e.g. communication, teamwork, customer service) make it easier to change jobs or industries."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skaars","tegniese","basiese"],"en":["scarce","technical","basic"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter voorbeeld wys die beste 'n veranderende loopbaanpatroon in die arbeidsmark?","en":"Which example best shows a changing career pattern in the job market?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Grafiese ontwerper wat as vryskut via 'n app kontrakte vir verskillende kliënte doen","en":"A graphic designer who freelances on contracts for different clients through an app"},{"af":"'n Onderwyser wat 40 jaar lank by dieselfde skool werk","en":"A teacher who works at the same school for 40 years"},{"af":"'n Mynwerker wat elke week vaste skofte by dieselfde myn werk","en":"A miner who works fixed shifts at the same mine every week"},{"af":"'n Klerk wat elke oggend om 08:00 by dieselfde kantoor inklok","en":"A clerk who clocks in at the same office at 08:00 every morning"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Kontrak- en gig-werk (vryskut, via 'n app, vir verskillende kliënte) is 'n nuwe loopbaanpatroon. Die ander voorbeelde is die tradisionele patroon van een vaste pos by een werkgewer.","en":"Contract and gig work (freelance, through an app, for different clients) is a new career pattern. The other examples show the traditional pattern of one permanent post with one employer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Behoefte in die mark wat nog nie gevul is nie, en wat 'n entrepreneur kan benut, word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A need in the market that has not yet been met, and that an entrepreneur can use, is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["nis","nismark","niche"],"en":["niche","niche market","nis"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Nis is 'n gaping in die mark, bv. 'n sonpaneel-skoonmaakdiens. 'n Tendens is 'n patroon van verandering oor tyd – dit help jou om nisse raak te sien.","en":"A niche is a gap in the market, e.g. a solar-panel cleaning service. A trend is a pattern of change over time – it helps you spot niches."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["tendens","sektor","monopolie"],"en":["trend","sector","monopoly"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Tydens beurtkrag het baie huise en besighede in Brits sonpanele laat installeer. Watter tendens verduidelik die groter aanvraag na soninstalleerders die beste?","en":"During load-shedding many homes and businesses in Brits had solar panels installed. Which trend best explains the greater demand for solar installers?"},"options":[{"af":"Die afname van die tersiêre sektor","en":"The decline of the tertiary sector"},{"af":"Die verskuiwing van werk na die primêre sektor","en":"The shift of work to the primary sector"},{"af":"Die groei van die groen ekonomie en hernubare energie","en":"The growth of the green economy and renewable energy"},{"af":"Die oorvloed elektrisiëns in Suid-Afrika","en":"The oversupply of electricians in South Africa"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die groen ekonomie (hernubare energie soos sonkrag) skep nuwe werk. Elektrisiëns is juis ambagslui in aanvraag, nie 'n oorvloed nie, en die tersiêre sektor het nie afgeneem nie.","en":"The green economy (renewable energy such as solar power) creates new jobs. Electricians are artisans in demand, not an oversupply, and the tertiary sector has not declined."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo (Graad 10) sê: “Sodra ek my matriek het, hoef ek nooit weer te leer nie.” Watter evaluering van sy stelling is die beste?","en":"Thabo (Grade 10) says: “Once I have my matric, I never have to learn again.” Which evaluation of his statement is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is reg: die NSS is die hoogste vlak op die NKR","en":"He is right: the NSC is the highest level on the NQF"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: werk verander vinnig weens tegnologie, so hy sal moet aanhou leer en heroplei om in aanvraag te bly","en":"He is wrong: work changes quickly because of technology, so he will have to keep learning and retraining to stay in demand"},{"af":"Hy is reg: werkgewers kyk net na informele leer","en":"He is right: employers only look at informal learning"},{"af":"Hy is verkeerd: hy moet eers 'n doktorsgraad hê voordat hy mag werk","en":"He is wrong: he must first have a doctorate before he may work"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Lewenslange leer is nodig omdat die 4NR, KI en nuwe tendense werk voortdurend verander. Die NSS is net vlak 4 van 10, en jy het nie 'n doktorsgraad nodig om te werk nie.","en":"Lifelong learning is needed because the 4IR, AI and new trends keep changing work. The NSC is only level 4 of 10, and you do not need a doctorate to work."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Godsdiens, sport en menseregte","en":"Religion, sport and human rights"},"topics":[{"id":"lo10-t4-godsdiens-sport","title":{"af":"Lewe in 'n multigodsdienstige samelewing; sport en vooroordeel","en":"Living in a multi-religious society; sport and bias"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die etiese tradisies van die groot godsdienste in Suid-Afrika kan beskryf, verduidelik hoe gelowe harmonie bevorder, en vooroordeel en onregverdige praktyke in sport krities kan ontleed.","en":"You will be able to describe the ethical traditions of the major religions in South Africa, explain how faiths promote harmony, and critically analyse bias and unfair practices in sport."},"summary":{"af":"## Lewe in 'n multigodsdienstige samelewing\n\nSuid-Afrika is 'n **multigodsdienstige** land: mense van baie gelowe woon, werk en leer saam. Die Grondwet het **geen staatsgodsdiens** nie. **Artikel 15** waarborg vryheid van godsdiens, oortuiging en mening, en **artikel 31** beskerm die reg van kulturele, godsdienstige en taalgemeenskappe om hul kultuur en geloof te beoefen. Om oor ander gelowe te leer, beteken nie dat jy jou eie oortuiging prysgee nie. Dit gaan oor **kennis en respek**.\n\n### Etiese tradisies en godsdienstige wette\nDie volgorde hieronder volg die KABV-lys en sê niks oor belangrikheid nie.\n\n| Godsdiens | Heilige geskrif / bron | Etiese beginsels en wette |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Judaïsme** | Torah | Tien Gebooie; geregtigheid en liefdadigheid (*tzedakah*); Sabbat; kosher-voedselwette |\n| **Christendom** | Bybel | Tien Gebooie; “Heb jou naaste lief soos jouself”; die **Goue Reël**: “Doen aan ander wat jy wil hê hulle aan jou moet doen” |\n| **Islam** | Koran (Qur'an) | **Vyf Pilare**: geloofsbelydenis (*shahada*), gebed vyf keer per dag (*salah*), liefdadigheid (**zakaat**), vas in Ramadan (*sawm*), pelgrimstog na Mekka (*hajj*); **halaal** = toelaatbaar (bv. kos) |\n| **Hindoeïsme** | Vedas, Bhagavad Gita | **dharma** (jou plig, reg lewe), **karma** (elke handeling het gevolge), **ahimsa** (geweldloosheid) |\n| **Boeddhisme** | Leringe van die Boeddha | **Vier Edel Waarhede**, **Edele Agtvoudige Pad**, **Vyf Voorskrifte** |\n| **Bahá'í-geloof** | Geskrifte van Bahá'u'lláh | **eenheid van die mensdom**, **gelykheid van mans en vroue**, uitskakeling van vooroordeel |\n| **Afrika-godsdiens** | Mondelinge tradisie | 'n **Opperwese** (Skepper), die **voorouers** as tussengangers, **ubuntu**, deurgangsrites |\n\n- **Vier Edel Waarhede:** lyding is deel van die lewe; lyding word deur begeerte veroorsaak; lyding kan beëindig word (nirwana); die weg daarheen is die Edele Agtvoudige Pad (bv. regte spraak, regte optrede, regte lewensonderhoud).\n- **Vyf Voorskrifte:** moenie lewende wesens doodmaak nie, nie steel nie, nie seksuele wangedrag pleeg nie, nie lieg nie en nie bedwelmende middels gebruik nie.\n- **Ubuntu:** *umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu* – 'n persoon is 'n persoon deur ander mense.\n\n### Inheemse geloofstelsels in Suid-Afrika\n- **Oorsprong:** oorgedra deur **mondelinge tradisie**. Ouer mense vertel stories, liedere, idiome en geskiedenis aan jonger geslagte; daar is nie een geskrewe heilige boek nie. Die San se rotskuns hou verband met hul geestelike praktyke.\n- **Praktyke:** rituele en seremonies (bv. 'n dier word geslag om die voorouers te bedank of te raadpleeg), **inisiasie** (die oorgang van kind na volwassene) en rites by geboorte, huwelik en dood.\n- **Tradisionele genesers:** **sangomas** (*izangoma*, diviners) kommunikeer met die voorouers om die oorsaak van siekte of probleme te bepaal; **inyangas** (*izinyanga*, kruiegenesers) maak medisyne van plante, wortels en bas.\n\n### Gedeelde waardes en harmonie\nGodsdienste deel baie **waardes**: respek, eerlikheid, medelye, geregtigheid en sorg vir die armes. Hulle bevorder harmonie deur liefdadigheid en gemeenskapsprojekte (sopkombuise, hulp ná 'n vloed), **intergeloofsdialoog** (leiers van verskillende gelowe praat en werk saam), en deur lede te leer om vrede te maak en te vergewe.\n\n> **Wenk – respekvolle gedrag:** Moenie ander se geloof spot nie. Leer oor heilige dae (Sabbat, Kersfees, Ramadan en Eid, Diwali, Vesak, Naw-Rúz) en voedselwette (halaal, kosher, vegetaries), en beplan 'n klasbraai so dat almal kan eet.\n\n## Sport en vooroordeel\nSport kan 'n nasie verenig, soos die Springbokke se Wêreldbekeroorwinnings in 1995, 2007, 2019 en 2023. Daar is egter ook **vooroordeel** ('n onregverdige voorkeur vir of teen 'n groep) en onregverdige praktyke.\n\n- **Geslag:** vroue-atlete verdien dikwels minder (loongaping) en kry minder mediadekking, borgskappe en goeie fasiliteite.\n- **Ras:** tydens apartheid is sport volgens ras geskei, is swart sportlui uitgesluit en is Suid-Afrika internasionaal geboikot. Ná 1994 het **transformasie** (regverdige toegang en verteenwoordiging) 'n doelwit geword. In 2018 het Siya Kolisi die eerste swart toetskaptein van die Springbokke geword.\n- **Stereotipering in sportsoorte:** “rugby is vir seuns, netbal vir meisies”, of idees oor watter groep in watter posisie hoort.\n\n### Onregverdige praktyke\n| Praktyk | Wat dit is | Voorbeeld / reaksie |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Doping** | verbode prestasieverhogende middels gebruik (bv. anaboliese steroïede) | **SAIDS** (SA Instituut vir Dwelmvrye Sport) toets atlete, ook in skoolsport; oortreders word geskors |\n| **Wedstrydbeknoeiing** | geld aanneem om die uitslag of 'n deel van 'n wedstryd vooraf te bepaal | in 2000 het krieketkaptein Hansie Cronjé erken dat hy geld van boekmakers aangeneem het; hy is lewenslank geskors |\n| **Subjektiewe skeidsregterskap** | partydige of swak beslissings deur skeidsregters | tegnologie: **TMO** (rugby), **DRS** (krieket), **VAR** (sokker); neutrale skeidsregters |\n| **Wanadministrasie** | korrupsie, nepotisme, swak bestuur van fondse | onafhanklike oudits en deursigtigheid |\n\n### Maniere om dit reg te stel\n- **ontwikkelingsprogramme** in skole en gemeenskappe (afrigting, toerusting, fasiliteite);\n- **gelyke mediadekking** en borgskappe vir vroue- en gestremdesport;\n- **gedragskodes** vir spelers, afrigters en ouers;\n- **tegnologie** en **onafhanklike liggame** (SAIDS, anti-korrupsie-eenhede);\n- opvoeding oor doping en wedstrydbeknoeiing, met streng strawwe.\n\n## Proses van ontleding en kritiese evaluering\n1. **Identifiseer die kwessie** (wat is die probleem?).\n2. **Versamel bewyse** (feite uit die bron, nie net opinies nie).\n3. **Oorweeg verskillende standpunte** (spelers, aanhangers, borge, bestuur).\n4. **Weeg dit op** (wat werk, wat nie, en hoekom?).\n5. **Maak 'n gemotiveerde gevolgtrekking of aanbeveling.**\n\n> **Onthou!** In 'n 15-punt-antwoord oor maatreëls teen wedstrydbeknoeiing: noem elke maatreël, verduidelik hoe dit werk en **evalueer** of dit doeltreffend is. Sluit af met 'n gevolgtrekking.","en":"## Living in a multi-religious society\n\nSouth Africa is a **multi-religious** country: people of many faiths live, work and learn together. The Constitution has **no state religion**. **Section 15** guarantees freedom of religion, belief and opinion, and **section 31** protects the right of cultural, religious and linguistic communities to practise their culture and faith. Learning about other faiths does not mean giving up your own beliefs. It is about **knowledge and respect**.\n\n### Ethical traditions and religious laws\nThe order below follows the CAPS list and says nothing about importance.\n\n| Religion | Sacred text / source | Ethical principles and laws |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Judaism** | Torah | Ten Commandments; justice and charity (*tzedakah*); Sabbath; kosher dietary laws |\n| **Christianity** | Bible | Ten Commandments; “Love your neighbour as yourself”; the **Golden Rule**: “Do to others what you would have them do to you” |\n| **Islam** | Qur'an | **Five Pillars**: declaration of faith (*shahada*), prayer five times a day (*salah*), charity (**zakaat**), fasting in Ramadan (*sawm*), pilgrimage to Makkah (*hajj*); **halaal** = permitted (e.g. food) |\n| **Hinduism** | Vedas, Bhagavad Gita | **dharma** (your duty, right living), **karma** (every action has consequences), **ahimsa** (non-violence) |\n| **Buddhism** | Teachings of the Buddha | **Four Noble Truths**, **Noble Eightfold Path**, **Five Precepts** |\n| **Bahá'í Faith** | Writings of Bahá'u'lláh | **unity of humanity**, **equality of men and women**, elimination of prejudice |\n| **African Religion** | Oral tradition | a **Supreme Being** (Creator), the **ancestors** as intermediaries, **ubuntu**, rites of passage |\n\n- **Four Noble Truths:** suffering is part of life; suffering is caused by desire; suffering can end (nirvana); the way there is the Noble Eightfold Path (e.g. right speech, right action, right livelihood).\n- **Five Precepts:** do not kill living beings, steal, commit sexual misconduct, lie or use intoxicants.\n- **Ubuntu:** *umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu* – a person is a person through other people.\n\n### Indigenous belief systems in South Africa\n- **Origins:** passed on through **oral tradition**. Older people tell stories, songs, sayings and history to younger generations; there is no single written sacred book. San rock art is linked to their spiritual practices.\n- **Practices:** rituals and ceremonies (e.g. an animal is slaughtered to thank or consult the ancestors), **initiation** (the transition from child to adult) and rites at birth, marriage and death.\n- **Traditional healers:** **sangomas** (*izangoma*, diviners) communicate with the ancestors to find the cause of illness or problems; **inyangas** (*izinyanga*, herbalists) make medicine from plants, roots and bark.\n\n### Shared values and harmony\nReligions share many **values**: respect, honesty, compassion, justice and care for the poor. They promote harmony through charity and community projects (soup kitchens, help after a flood), **interfaith dialogue** (leaders of different faiths talk and work together), and by teaching members to make peace and to forgive.\n\n> **Tip – respectful behaviour:** Do not mock other people's faith. Learn about holy days (Sabbath, Christmas, Ramadan and Eid, Diwali, Vesak, Naw-Rúz) and dietary laws (halaal, kosher, vegetarian), and plan a class braai so that everyone can eat.\n\n## Sport and bias\nSport can unite a nation, like the Springboks' Rugby World Cup wins in 1995, 2007, 2019 and 2023. But there is also **bias** (an unfair preference for or against a group) and there are unfair practices.\n\n- **Gender:** women athletes often earn less (pay gap) and get less media coverage, sponsorship and good facilities.\n- **Race:** under apartheid sport was separated by race, black sportspeople were excluded and South Africa was boycotted internationally. After 1994 **transformation** (fair access and representation) became a goal. In 2018 Siya Kolisi became the first black Test captain of the Springboks.\n- **Stereotyping in sporting codes:** “rugby is for boys, netball for girls”, or ideas about which group belongs in which position.\n\n### Unfair practices\n| Practice | What it is | Example / response |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Doping** | using banned performance-enhancing substances (e.g. anabolic steroids) | **SAIDS** (SA Institute for Drug-Free Sport) tests athletes, also in school sport; offenders are banned |\n| **Match-fixing** | accepting money to decide the result or part of a match in advance | in 2000 cricket captain Hansie Cronjé admitted that he had accepted money from bookmakers; he was banned for life |\n| **Subjective umpiring/refereeing** | biased or poor decisions by referees and umpires | technology: **TMO** (rugby), **DRS** (cricket), **VAR** (football); neutral referees |\n| **Maladministration** | corruption, nepotism, mismanagement of funds | independent audits and transparency |\n\n### Ways to redress this\n- **development programmes** in schools and communities (coaching, equipment, facilities);\n- **equal media coverage** and sponsorship for women's and disability sport;\n- **codes of conduct** for players, coaches and parents;\n- **technology** and **independent bodies** (SAIDS, anti-corruption units);\n- education about doping and match-fixing, with strict penalties.\n\n## Process of analysis and critical evaluation\n1. **Identify the issue** (what is the problem?).\n2. **Gather evidence** (facts from the source, not just opinions).\n3. **Consider different viewpoints** (players, fans, sponsors, management).\n4. **Weigh them up** (what works, what does not, and why?).\n5. **Reach a motivated conclusion or recommendation.**\n\n> **Remember!** In a 15-mark answer on measures against match-fixing: name each measure, explain how it works and **evaluate** whether it is effective. End with a conclusion."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Multigodsdienstige samelewing","en":"Multi-religious society"},"def":{"af":"'n Samelewing waarin mense van baie verskillende gelowe saam woon en dieselfde regte het.","en":"A society in which people of many different faiths live together and have the same rights."}},{"term":{"af":"Godsdiensvryheid","en":"Freedom of religion"},"def":{"af":"Die reg (artikel 15 van die Grondwet) om jou eie godsdiens, oortuiging en mening te hê en te beoefen.","en":"The right (section 15 of the Constitution) to have and practise your own religion, belief and opinion."}},{"term":{"af":"Etiese tradisie","en":"Ethical tradition"},"def":{"af":"Die stel beginsels en reëls van 'n godsdiens wat sê wat reg en verkeerd is, bv. die Tien Gebooie of die Vyf Voorskrifte.","en":"A religion's set of principles and rules about right and wrong, e.g. the Ten Commandments or the Five Precepts."}},{"term":{"af":"Inheemse geloofstelsels","en":"Indigenous belief systems"},"def":{"af":"Geloofstelsels wat in Suid-Afrika ontstaan het en deur mondelinge tradisie oorgedra word, met rituele, seremonies en tradisionele genesers.","en":"Belief systems that originated in South Africa and are passed on through oral tradition, with rituals, ceremonies and traditional healers."}},{"term":{"af":"Ubuntu","en":"Ubuntu"},"def":{"af":"Die Afrika-waarde dat 'n persoon 'n persoon is deur ander mense; dit beklemtoon medemenslikheid en gemeenskap.","en":"The African value that a person is a person through other people; it stresses humanity and community."}},{"term":{"af":"Ahimsa","en":"Ahimsa"},"def":{"af":"Die beginsel van geweldloosheid teenoor alle lewende wesens, belangrik in Hindoeïsme (en ook in Boeddhisme).","en":"The principle of non-violence towards all living beings, important in Hinduism (and also in Buddhism)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vooroordeel (partydigheid) in sport","en":"Bias in sport"},"def":{"af":"'n Onregverdige voorkeur vir of teen 'n persoon of groep, bv. op grond van geslag of ras.","en":"An unfair preference for or against a person or group, e.g. based on gender or race."}},{"term":{"af":"Doping","en":"Doping"},"def":{"af":"Die gebruik van verbode prestasieverhogende middels om 'n onregverdige voordeel in sport te kry.","en":"The use of banned performance-enhancing substances to gain an unfair advantage in sport."}},{"term":{"af":"Wedstrydbeknoeiing","en":"Match-fixing"},"def":{"af":"Om geld of gunste aan te neem om die uitslag of 'n deel van 'n wedstryd vooraf te bepaal.","en":"Accepting money or favours to decide the result or part of a match in advance."}},{"term":{"af":"Wanadministrasie","en":"Maladministration"},"def":{"af":"Swak of oneerlike bestuur van 'n sportliggaam, bv. korrupsie, nepotisme en die misbruik van fondse.","en":"Poor or dishonest management of a sports body, e.g. corruption, nepotism and misuse of funds."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Pas godsdienste by etiese beginsels","en":"Match religions to ethical principles"},"problem":{"af":"Gee vir elk van die volgende godsdienste die heilige geskrif (of bron) en een etiese beginsel of wet: (a) Islam, (b) Boeddhisme, (c) Afrika-godsdiens. (6 punte)","en":"For each of the following religions give the sacred text (or source) and one ethical principle or law: (a) Islam, (b) Buddhism, (c) African Religion. (6 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Islam: die Koran (Qur'an). Beginsel: die Vyf Pilare, bv. zakaat – 'n deel van jou rykdom aan die armes gee.","en":"(a) Islam: the Qur'an. Principle: the Five Pillars, e.g. zakaat – giving part of your wealth to the poor."},{"af":"(b) Boeddhisme: die leringe van die Boeddha. Beginsel: die Vyf Voorskrifte, bv. moenie lewende wesens doodmaak nie.","en":"(b) Buddhism: the teachings of the Buddha. Principle: the Five Precepts, e.g. do not kill living beings."},{"af":"(c) Afrika-godsdiens: mondelinge tradisie (geen enkele geskrewe boek nie). Beginsel: ubuntu – 'n persoon is 'n persoon deur ander mense.","en":"(c) African Religion: oral tradition (no single written book). Principle: ubuntu – a person is a person through other people."},{"af":"Kontroleer: een punt vir die bron en een punt vir 'n korrekte beginsel per godsdiens.","en":"Check: one mark for the source and one mark for a correct principle per religion."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Koran; Vyf Pilare/zakaat (b) Leringe van die Boeddha; Vyf Voorskrifte (c) Mondelinge tradisie; ubuntu","en":"(a) Qur'an; Five Pillars/zakaat (b) Teachings of the Buddha; Five Precepts (c) Oral tradition; ubuntu"}},{"title":{"af":"Godsdienste en 'n harmonieuse samelewing","en":"Religions and a harmonious society"},"problem":{"af":"Scenario: In 'n dorp soos Brits begin 'n kerk, 'n moskee en 'n Hindoe-tempel saam 'n sopkombuis in die winter. Verduidelik hoe hierdie projek wys dat diverse godsdienste tot 'n harmonieuse samelewing kan bydra. (4 punte)","en":"Scenario: In a town like Brits a church, a mosque and a Hindu temple start a soup kitchen together in winter. Explain how this project shows that diverse religions can contribute to a harmonious society. (4 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"Gedeelde waardes: al drie gelowe leer medelye en sorg vir die armes, so hulle het 'n gemeenskaplike doel.","en":"Shared values: all three faiths teach compassion and care for the poor, so they have a common goal."},{"af":"Saamwerk bou verhoudings en vertroue: lede leer mekaar ken, en vooroordele en stereotipes verminder.","en":"Working together builds relationships and trust: members get to know one another, and prejudice and stereotypes decrease."},{"af":"Respek in die praktyk: 'n vegetariese sop kan deur almal geëet word en respekteer verskillende voedselwette (halaal, vegetaries).","en":"Respect in practice: a vegetarian soup can be eaten by everyone and respects different dietary laws (halaal, vegetarian)."},{"af":"Die gemeenskap sien 'n voorbeeld van vreedsame saambestaan, wat by die Grondwet se waardes pas (artikels 15 en 31).","en":"The community sees an example of peaceful coexistence, which fits the values of the Constitution (sections 15 and 31)."}],"answer":{"af":"Gedeelde waardes, saamwerk wat vertroue bou, respek vir voedselwette en 'n voorbeeld van vreedsame saambestaan.","en":"Shared values, cooperation that builds trust, respect for dietary laws and an example of peaceful coexistence."}},{"title":{"af":"Bronvraag: geslagsvooroordeel in sport","en":"Source question: gender bias in sport"},"problem":{"af":"Bron (fiktiewe skoolkoerantberig): “Ons meisies se krieketspan het die provinsiale skolekampioenskap gewen. Tog het die span geen eie kleedkamer nie, die borg gee net vir die seuns se span nuwe drag, en die plaaslike radiostasie het die eindstryd nie eers genoem nie.” (a) Identifiseer twee vorme van geslagsvooroordeel in die bron. (2) (b) Verduidelik hoe dit meisies se deelname aan sport kan raak. (2) (c) Stel twee maatreëls voor om dit reg te stel. (2)","en":"Source (fictional school-newspaper report): “Our girls' cricket team won the provincial schools championship. Yet the team has no change room of its own, the sponsor gives new kit only to the boys' team, and the local radio station did not even mention the final.” (a) Identify two forms of gender bias in the source. (2) (b) Explain how this can affect girls' participation in sport. (2) (c) Suggest two measures to redress it. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ongelyke fasiliteite (geen kleedkamer nie), ongelyke borgskap (net die seuns kry drag) en/of ongelyke mediadekking (die eindstryd is nie genoem nie). Enige twee.","en":"(a) Unequal facilities (no change room), unequal sponsorship (only the boys get kit) and/or unequal media coverage (the final was not mentioned). Any two."},{"af":"(b) Meisies voel hul prestasie is minder werd, verloor motivering en kan ophou speel; jonger meisies het minder rolmodelle om na op te kyk.","en":"(b) Girls feel their achievement is worth less, lose motivation and may stop playing; younger girls have fewer role models to look up to."},{"af":"(c) Die skool deel fasiliteite en borggeld regverdig tussen spanne; die media en die skoolkoerant gee gelyke dekking aan meisies- en seunsport.","en":"(c) The school shares facilities and sponsorship money fairly between teams; the media and the school newspaper give equal coverage to girls' and boys' sport."},{"af":"Wenk: haal bewyse uit die bron aan in (a), en gee in (c) maatreëls wat realisties en spesifiek is.","en":"Tip: quote evidence from the source in (a), and give realistic and specific measures in (c)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ongelyke fasiliteite, borgskap en mediadekking (enige twee) (b) Minder motivering en rolmodelle → meisies hou op (c) Regverdige verdeling van fasiliteite en borggeld; gelyke mediadekking","en":"(a) Unequal facilities, sponsorship and media coverage (any two) (b) Less motivation and fewer role models → girls drop out (c) Fair sharing of facilities and sponsorship; equal media coverage"}},{"title":{"af":"Evalueer maatreëls teen wedstrydbeknoeiing (15 punte)","en":"Evaluate measures against match-fixing (15 marks)"},"problem":{"af":"Evalueer krities die maatreëls wat sportliggame gebruik om wedstrydbeknoeiing te bekamp. Gebruik die proses van ontleding en kritiese evaluering, en sluit af met 'n aanbeveling. (15 punte)","en":"Critically evaluate the measures that sports bodies use to combat match-fixing. Use the process of analysis and critical evaluation, and end with a recommendation. (15 marks)"},"steps":[{"af":"Inleiding – identifiseer die kwessie: wedstrydbeknoeiing is om geld aan te neem om die uitslag of 'n deel van 'n wedstryd vooraf te bepaal. Voorbeeld: in 2000 het Hansie Cronjé erken dat hy geld van boekmakers aangeneem het; hy is lewenslank geskors. Dit vernietig aanhangers se vertroue.","en":"Introduction – identify the issue: match-fixing is accepting money to decide the result or part of a match in advance. Example: in 2000 Hansie Cronjé admitted that he had accepted money from bookmakers; he was banned for life. It destroys fans' trust."},{"af":"Maatreël 1 – gedragskodes en opleiding: spelers leer hoe boekmakers hulle nader en dat hulle elke benadering moet rapporteer. Evaluering: goed vir voorkoming, veral by jong spelers, maar dit keer nie iemand wat gierig is nie.","en":"Measure 1 – codes of conduct and education: players learn how bookmakers approach them and that they must report every approach. Evaluation: good for prevention, especially among young players, but it does not stop someone who is greedy."},{"af":"Maatreël 2 – onafhanklike anti-korrupsie-eenhede wat ondersoek instel en ongewone weddenskappatrone monitor. Evaluering: doeltreffend as hulle werklik onafhanklik is en genoeg geld en mag het.","en":"Measure 2 – independent anti-corruption units that investigate and monitor unusual betting patterns. Evaluation: effective if they are truly independent and have enough funding and power."},{"af":"Maatreël 3 – streng strawwe (lewenslange skorsings) en strafregtelike vervolging: in Suid-Afrika maak die Wet op die Voorkoming en Bestryding van Korrupte Bedrywighede (Wet 12 van 2004) korrupsie rondom sportbyeenkomste 'n misdryf. Evaluering: dit ontmoedig oortreders, maar werk net as mense gevang word.","en":"Measure 3 – strict penalties (lifetime bans) and criminal prosecution: in South Africa the Prevention and Combating of Corrupt Activities Act (Act 12 of 2004) makes corruption around sporting events a crime. Evaluation: it deters offenders, but only works if people are caught."},{"af":"Gevolgtrekking en aanbeveling: geen enkele maatreël is genoeg nie. 'n Kombinasie van opleiding, onafhanklike ondersoeke en streng strawwe, plus goeie salarisse sodat spelers minder kwesbaar is vir omkopery, werk die beste.","en":"Conclusion and recommendation: no single measure is enough. A combination of education, independent investigations and strict penalties, plus fair pay so that players are less vulnerable to bribery, works best."}],"answer":{"af":"Struktuur: inleiding (kwessie + voorbeeld) → 3 maatreëls, elk verduidelik én geëvalueer → gemotiveerde gevolgtrekking: 'n kombinasie van maatreëls is die doeltreffendste.","en":"Structure: introduction (issue + example) → 3 measures, each explained and evaluated → motivated conclusion: a combination of measures is most effective."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die heilige boek van Islam?","en":"What is the sacred book of Islam?"},"options":[{"af":"Die Torah","en":"The Torah"},{"af":"Die Bybel","en":"The Bible"},{"af":"Die Koran (Qur'an)","en":"The Qur'an"},{"af":"Die Bhagavad Gita","en":"The Bhagavad Gita"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Moslems volg die Koran (Qur'an). Die Torah is die heilige geskrif van Judaïsme, die Bybel van die Christendom en die Bhagavad Gita is 'n heilige geskrif van Hindoeïsme.","en":"Muslims follow the Qur'an. The Torah is the sacred text of Judaism, the Bible of Christianity, and the Bhagavad Gita is a sacred text of Hinduism."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die Afrika-waarde wat sê “'n persoon is 'n persoon deur ander mense” (umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu), word ___ genoem.","en":"The African value that says “a person is a person through other people” (umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu) is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["ubuntu"],"en":["ubuntu"]},"explain":{"af":"Ubuntu beklemtoon medemenslikheid en gemeenskap. Dharma en karma kom uit Hindoeïsme en tzedakah (liefdadigheid) uit Judaïsme.","en":"Ubuntu stresses humanity and community. Dharma and karma come from Hinduism and tzedakah (charity) from Judaism."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dharma","karma","tzedakah"],"en":["dharma","karma","tzedakah"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die Suid-Afrikaanse Grondwet maak een godsdiens die amptelike staatsgodsdiens.","en":"The South African Constitution makes one religion the official state religion."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Suid-Afrika het geen staatsgodsdiens nie. Artikel 15 waarborg vryheid van godsdiens, oortuiging en mening vir almal, en artikel 31 beskerm godsdienstige gemeenskappe.","en":"False. South Africa has no state religion. Section 15 guarantees freedom of religion, belief and opinion for everyone, and section 31 protects religious communities."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter organisasie toets Suid-Afrikaanse atlete vir verbode middels?","en":"Which organisation tests South African athletes for banned substances?"},"options":[{"af":"SAKO (Suid-Afrikaanse Kwalifikasie-owerheid)","en":"SAQA (South African Qualifications Authority)"},{"af":"Die Openbare Beskermer","en":"The Public Protector"},{"af":"Die Kommissie vir Geslagsgelykheid","en":"The Commission for Gender Equality"},{"af":"SAIDS (SA Instituut vir Dwelmvrye Sport)","en":"SAIDS (SA Institute for Drug-Free Sport)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"SAIDS toets atlete (ook in skoolsport) vir verbode prestasieverhogende middels. Die ander liggame het niks met dwelmtoetse in sport te doen nie.","en":"SAIDS tests athletes (also in school sport) for banned performance-enhancing substances. The other bodies have nothing to do with drug testing in sport."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Hindoeïsme is ___ die beginsel dat elke handeling gevolge het: goeie dade bring goeie gevolge en slegte dade slegte gevolge.","en":"In Hinduism ___ is the principle that every action has consequences: good deeds bring good results and bad deeds bad results."},"answers":{"af":["karma"],"en":["karma"]},"explain":{"af":"Karma gaan oor die gevolge van jou dade. Dharma is jou plig (reg lewe) en ahimsa is geweldloosheid. Zakaat is liefdadigheid in Islam.","en":"Karma is about the consequences of your actions. Dharma is your duty (right living) and ahimsa is non-violence. Zakaat is charity in Islam."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dharma","ahimsa","zakaat"],"en":["dharma","ahimsa","zakat"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter godsdiens volg die Vier Edel Waarhede en die Edele Agtvoudige Pad?","en":"Which religion follows the Four Noble Truths and the Noble Eightfold Path?"},"options":[{"af":"Judaïsme","en":"Judaism"},{"af":"Boeddhisme","en":"Buddhism"},{"af":"Bahá'í-geloof","en":"Bahá'í Faith"},{"af":"Hindoeïsme","en":"Hinduism"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die Vier Edel Waarhede en die Edele Agtvoudige Pad is die kern van die Boeddha se leringe, saam met die Vyf Voorskrifte.","en":"The Four Noble Truths and the Noble Eightfold Path are at the heart of the Buddha's teachings, together with the Five Precepts."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke godsdiens by 'n etiese beginsel uit sy tradisie.","en":"Match each religion to an ethical principle from its tradition."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Judaïsme","en":"Judaism"},"r":{"af":"Tzedakah: geregtigheid en liefdadigheid","en":"Tzedakah: justice and charity"}},{"l":{"af":"Christendom","en":"Christianity"},"r":{"af":"Die Goue Reël: doen aan ander wat jy wil hê hulle aan jou moet doen","en":"The Golden Rule: do to others what you would have them do to you"}},{"l":{"af":"Islam","en":"Islam"},"r":{"af":"Die Vyf Pilare, insluitend zakaat","en":"The Five Pillars, including zakaat"}},{"l":{"af":"Hindoeïsme","en":"Hinduism"},"r":{"af":"Ahimsa: geweldloosheid","en":"Ahimsa: non-violence"}},{"l":{"af":"Bahá'í-geloof","en":"Bahá'í Faith"},"r":{"af":"Eenheid van die mensdom en gelykheid van mans en vroue","en":"Unity of humanity and equality of men and women"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke godsdiens het sy eie etiese tradisie, maar baie gelowe het soortgelyke waardes, soos om ander te behandel soos jy self behandel wil word en om vir die armes te sorg.","en":"Each religion has its own ethical tradition, but many faiths share similar values, such as treating others as you want to be treated and caring for the poor."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Tradisionele geneser wat met die voorouers kommunikeer om die oorsaak van 'n siekte of probleem te bepaal, word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"A traditional healer who communicates with the ancestors to find the cause of an illness or problem is called a ___."},"answers":{"af":["sangoma","isangoma","izangoma","diviner"],"en":["sangoma","isangoma","izangoma","diviner"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Sangoma (diviner) werk met die voorouers. 'n Inyanga is 'n kruiegeneser wat medisyne van plante maak. 'n Imam lei gebede in 'n moskee en 'n rabbi is 'n Joodse geestelike leier.","en":"A sangoma (diviner) works with the ancestors. An inyanga is a herbalist who makes medicine from plants. An imam leads prayers in a mosque and a rabbi is a Jewish spiritual leader."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["inyanga","imam","rabbi"],"en":["inyanga","imam","rabbi"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken zakaat, een van die Vyf Pilare van Islam?","en":"What does zakaat, one of the Five Pillars of Islam, mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Om 'n deel van jou rykdom aan die armes te gee","en":"Giving part of your wealth to the poor"},{"af":"Om gedurende Ramadan van sonop tot sononder te vas","en":"Fasting from sunrise to sunset during Ramadan"},{"af":"Om een keer in jou lewe 'n pelgrimstog na Mekka te onderneem","en":"Making a pilgrimage to Makkah once in your life"},{"af":"Om vyf keer per dag te bid","en":"Praying five times a day"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Zakaat is liefdadigheid. Vas in Ramadan is sawm, die pelgrimstog is hajj en die daaglikse gebed is salah – almal ook Pilare, maar nie zakaat nie.","en":"Zakaat is charity. Fasting in Ramadan is sawm, the pilgrimage is hajj and daily prayer is salah – all of them Pillars too, but not zakaat."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Tegnologie soos die TMO in rugby, DRS in krieket en VAR in sokker help om foute en partydige beslissings van skeidsregters te verminder.","en":"Technology such as the TMO in rugby, DRS in cricket and VAR in football helps to reduce referees' mistakes and biased decisions."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Videotegnologie laat beslissings weer nagaan word, sodat subjektiewe of partydige skeidsregterskap minder invloed op die uitslag het.","en":"True. Video technology lets decisions be checked again, so subjective or biased refereeing has less influence on the result."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die Graad 10's hou 'n klasbraai. Aisha is Moslem en eet net halaal kos, en Priya is 'n Hindoe wat vegetariër is. Wat is die mees respekvolle plan?","en":"The Grade 10s are having a class braai. Aisha is Muslim and eats only halaal food, and Priya is a Hindu who is vegetarian. What is the most respectful plan?"},"options":[{"af":"Bedien net varkwors – hulle kan brood eet","en":"Serve only pork sausage – they can eat bread"},{"af":"Sê vir hulle om hul eie kos te bring en apart te sit","en":"Tell them to bring their own food and sit separately"},{"af":"Koop halaal vleis en vegetariese opsies, berei dit apart voor en merk die kos duidelik","en":"Buy halaal meat and vegetarian options, prepare them separately and label the food clearly"},{"af":"Maak grappies oor voedselwette sodat almal ontspan","en":"Make jokes about dietary laws so that everyone relaxes"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Respek beteken om voedselwette te ken en te akkommodeer sodat almal saam kan eet. Om mense uit te sluit of oor hul geloof te spot, is disrespekvol.","en":"Respect means knowing and accommodating dietary laws so that everyone can eat together. Excluding people or mocking their faith is disrespectful."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n speler geld van boekmakers aanneem om die uitslag (of 'n deel) van 'n wedstryd vooraf te bepaal, word dit ___ genoem.","en":"When a player accepts money from bookmakers to decide the result (or part) of a match in advance, it is called ___."},"answers":{"af":["wedstrydbeknoeiing","wedstryd-beknoeiing","match-fixing","matchfixing","wedstrydvervalsing"],"en":["match-fixing","match fixing","matchfixing","wedstrydbeknoeiing"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is wedstrydbeknoeiing, soos in die Hansie Cronjé-skandaal van 2000. Doping is verbode middels, en wanadministrasie is swak of korrupte bestuur.","en":"This is match-fixing, as in the Hansie Cronjé scandal of 2000. Doping is banned substances, and maladministration is poor or corrupt management."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["doping","wanadministrasie","stereotipering"],"en":["doping","maladministration","stereotyping"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die bron: “Die meisies se sokkerspan het die streekstoernooi gewen, maar die skoolkoerant gee hulle net een klein paragraaf. Die seuns se span, wat verloor het, kry die voorblad. Die meisies oefen boonop op die B-veld sonder ligte.” Watter vorm van vooroordeel word uitgebeeld?","en":"Read the source: “The girls' football team won the regional tournament, but the school newspaper gives them only one small paragraph. The boys' team, which lost, gets the front page. On top of that, the girls practise on the B-field without lights.” Which form of bias is shown?"},"options":[{"af":"Rasse-vooroordeel","en":"Racial bias"},{"af":"Wedstrydbeknoeiing","en":"Match-fixing"},{"af":"Subjektiewe skeidsregterskap","en":"Subjective refereeing"},{"af":"Geslagsvooroordeel: ongelyke mediadekking en fasiliteite","en":"Gender bias: unequal media coverage and facilities"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die bewyse (klein paragraaf teenoor die voorblad, die swakker veld) wys ongelyke behandeling op grond van geslag. Niks in die bron gaan oor ras, omkopery of skeidsregters nie.","en":"The evidence (a small paragraph versus the front page, the poorer field) shows unequal treatment based on gender. Nothing in the source is about race, bribery or referees."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Korrupsie, nepotisme en die swak bestuur van 'n sportfederasie se geld is voorbeelde van ___.","en":"Corruption, nepotism and the mismanagement of a sports federation's money are examples of ___."},"answers":{"af":["wanadministrasie","maladministrasie","wanbestuur","maladministration"],"en":["maladministration","mismanagement","wanadministrasie"]},"explain":{"af":"Wanadministrasie gaan oor hoe 'n sportliggaam bestuur word. Onafhanklike oudits en deursigtigheid help om dit reg te stel.","en":"Maladministration is about how a sports body is managed. Independent audits and transparency help to redress it."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["doping","wedstrydbeknoeiing","stereotipering"],"en":["doping","match-fixing","stereotyping"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling verduidelik die beste hoe diverse godsdienste tot 'n harmonieuse samelewing kan bydra?","en":"Which statement best explains how diverse religions can contribute to a harmonious society?"},"options":[{"af":"Gelowe deel waardes soos medelye en sorg vir die armes, en kan saamwerk aan projekte soos 'n sopkombuis","en":"Faiths share values such as compassion and care for the poor, and can work together on projects such as a soup kitchen"},{"af":"Elke geloofsgroep moet heeltemal apart bly om konflik te vermy","en":"Every faith group should stay completely separate to avoid conflict"},{"af":"Almal moet dieselfde godsdiens aanneem sodat daar geen verskille is nie","en":"Everyone should adopt the same religion so that there are no differences"},{"af":"Godsdiens moet uit die openbare lewe verban word","en":"Religion should be banned from public life"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Harmonie kom uit gedeelde waardes, samewerking en respek. Om mense te skei, almal te dwing om een geloof aan te neem of godsdiens te verban, sou artikels 15 en 31 van die Grondwet skend.","en":"Harmony comes from shared values, cooperation and respect. Separating people, forcing everyone into one faith or banning religion would violate sections 15 and 31 of the Constitution."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 2000 is Hansie Cronjé lewenslank uit krieket geskors nadat hy erken het dat hy geld van boekmakers aangeneem het. Watter kombinasie van maatreëls sal wedstrydbeknoeiing die doeltreffendste bekamp?","en":"In 2000 Hansie Cronjé was banned from cricket for life after admitting that he had accepted money from bookmakers. Which combination of measures will combat match-fixing most effectively?"},"options":[{"af":"Laat spelers toe om op hul eie wedstryde te wed, solank hul span wen","en":"Allow players to bet on their own matches, as long as their team wins"},{"af":"Gedragskodes en opleiding vir spelers, 'n onafhanklike anti-korrupsie-eenheid en streng strawwe soos skorsings","en":"Codes of conduct and education for players, an independent anti-corruption unit and strict penalties such as bans"},{"af":"Beboet net die kaptein, want hy neem die besluite","en":"Fine only the captain, because he makes the decisions"},{"af":"Speel alle wedstryde sonder toeskouers","en":"Play all matches without spectators"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Kombinasie werk die beste: opleiding voorkom, 'n onafhanklike eenheid ondersoek en streng strawwe ontmoedig. Wedstrydbeknoeiing kan enige speler betrek, en toeskouers is nie die oorsaak nie.","en":"A combination works best: education prevents, an independent unit investigates and strict penalties deter. Match-fixing can involve any player, and spectators are not the cause."}}]}]}]},"afrikaans":{"id":"afrikaans","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Afrikaans Huistaal","en":"Afrikaans Home Language"},"short":{"af":"Afr","en":"Afr"},"icon":"📖","color":"#0d9488","intro":{"af":"Afrikaans Huistaal in Graad 10 verdiep jou taal- en letterkundevaardighede: leesbegrip, woordsoorte, sinsbou en tye, die opsomming, die lydende vorm en indirekte rede, poësie, prosa, drama, visuele geletterdheid en kritiese taalbewustheid, en die opstel en transaksionele tekste. Die Novembereksamen toets die hele jaar se werk in drie vraestelle: V1 Taal (70), V2 Letterkunde (80) en V3 Skryfwerk (100).","en":"Afrikaans Home Language in Grade 10 deepens your language and literature skills: comprehension, parts of speech, sentence structure and tenses, the summary, the passive voice and reported speech, poetry, prose, drama, visual literacy and critical language awareness, and the essay and transactional texts. The November exam tests the whole year's work in three papers: P1 Language (70), P2 Literature (80) and P3 Writing (100)."},"examTips":[{"af":"V1: lees die vrae eers vlugtig, dan die teks; let op vraagwerkwoorde soos \"haal aan\" (presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens), \"verduidelik in eie woorde\" en \"motiveer\".","en":"P1: skim the questions first, then read the text; watch question verbs such as \"haal aan\" (exact words in quotation marks), \"verduidelik in eie woorde\" (explain in your own words) and \"motiveer\" (give a reason)."},{"af":"Opsomming: haal net die feite uit wat die opdrag vra, skryf elkeen in 'n volsin in jou eie woorde, en hou by die woordgrens.","en":"Summary: take out only the facts the instruction asks for, write each one as a full sentence in your own words, and keep to the word limit."},{"af":"Poësie: ken die terme (bv. metafoor, personifikasie, enjambement, rymskema) en noem altyd die effek – wat beteken dit en hoe beïnvloed dit die leser?","en":"Poetry: know the terms (e.g. metaphor, personification, enjambment, rhyme scheme) and always state the effect – what does it mean and how does it affect the reader?"},{"af":"Letterkunde: ken die intrige, karakters, konflik, ruimte en tema van elke voorgeskrewe teks, en staaf elke stelling met 'n voorbeeld of aanhaling.","en":"Literature: know the plot, characters, conflict, setting and theme of every prescribed text, and support every statement with an example or quotation."},{"af":"V3: beplan elke teks (breinkaart of raamwerk), hou by die formaat, register en woordtelling (opstel 300–350 woorde), en redigeer aan die einde vir spelling en leestekens.","en":"P3: plan every text (mind map or outline), stick to the format, register and word count (essay 300–350 words), and edit at the end for spelling and punctuation."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Departement van Basiese Onderwys (DBE)","en":"Department of Basic Education (DBE)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za","note":{"af":"CAPS-dokument vir Afrikaans Huistaal, eksamenriglyne en vorige NSS-vraestelle met memorandums – goed om die vraagstyl te leer ken.","en":"CAPS document for Afrikaans Home Language, exam guidelines and past NSC papers with memos – good for learning the question style."}},{"title":{"af":"Thutong-onderwysportaal","en":"Thutong Education Portal"},"url":"https://www.thutong.doe.gov.za","note":{"af":"Die DBE se gratis onderwysportaal met leer- en hersieningsmateriaal per vak en graad.","en":"The DBE's free education portal with learning and revision material by subject and grade."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Afrikaans Huistaal-eksamen Graad 10\n\n**Drie vraestelle, 250 punte** volgens die CAPS/DBE-patroon (*skatting – bevestig met Hoërskool Brits se 2026-afbakening*). Mondeling is deel van die SBA.\n\n| Vraestel | Afdelings | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| V1: Taal in konteks (2 uur) | A Leesbegrip 30, B Opsomming 10, C Taalstrukture en -konvensies 30 | 70 |\n| V2: Letterkunde | Poësie (voorgeskrewe en 'n ongesiene gedig), prosa en drama – volgens die keuses in die vraestel | 80 |\n| V3: Skryfwerk | A Opstel 50 (een opstel van 300–350 woorde), B twee transaksionele tekste (2 × 25) | 100 |\n\n### Wat om te verwag\n\n- **V1:** een of twee leesstukke, dikwels met 'n visuele teks; Afdeling C gebruik 'n advertensie, 'n spotprent of strokiesprent en 'n teks met taalvrae in konteks.\n- **V2:** kontekstuele vrae (1–3 punte elk) op uittreksels, plus paragraaf- of kort opstelvrae. Jy beantwoord net die gevraagde aantal vrae.\n- **V3:** verhalende, beskrywende, beredenerende of betogende opstelle; transaksionele tekste soos formele en informele briewe, toesprake, koerantberigte en resensies (180–200 woorde elk).\n\n### Wenke\n\n1. Lees die keuses in V2 en V3 eers deur voor jy begin.\n2. Verdeel jou tyd volgens die punte.","en":"## Afrikaans Home Language exam Grade 10\n\n**Three papers, 250 marks** following the CAPS/DBE pattern (*estimate – confirm with Hoërskool Brits's 2026 scope*). Orals are part of SBA.\n\n| Paper | Sections | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1: Language in context (2 hours) | A Comprehension 30, B Summary 10, C Language structures and conventions 30 | 70 |\n| P2: Literature | Poetry (prescribed and an unseen poem), prose and drama – according to the choices in the paper | 80 |\n| P3: Writing | A Essay 50 (one essay of 300–350 words), B two transactional texts (2 × 25) | 100 |\n\n### What to expect\n\n- **P1:** one or two passages, often with a visual text; Section C uses an advert, a cartoon or comic strip and a text with language questions in context.\n- **P2:** contextual questions (1–3 marks each) on extracts, plus paragraph or short essay questions. You answer only the required number of questions.\n- **P3:** narrative, descriptive, discursive or argumentative essays; transactional texts such as formal and informal letters, speeches, newspaper reports and reviews (180–200 words each).\n\n### Tips\n\n1. Read through the choices in P2 and P3 before you start.\n2. Divide your time according to the marks."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Leesbegrip, naamwoorde, poësie en die opstel","en":"Comprehension, nouns, poetry and the essay"},"topics":[{"id":"afr10-t1-leesbegrip","title":{"af":"Leesbegrip en leesstrategieë","en":"Reading comprehension and reading strategies"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n onbekende teks strategies kan lees, die eise van elke vraagwoord verstaan en antwoorde skryf wat al die punte verdien.","en":"You will be able to read an unseen text strategically, understand what each question word demands and write answers that earn all the marks."},"summary":{"af":"## Vraestel 1: Taal in konteks\n\nVraestel 1 tel **70 punte** en jy het **2 uur**.\n\n| Afdeling | Inhoud | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Leesbegrip | 30 |\n| B | Opsomming | 10 |\n| C | Taalstrukture en -konvensies | 30 |\n\nIn **Afdeling A** kry jy een of twee leestekste – byvoorbeeld 'n koerant- of tydskrifartikel, 'n rubriek of 'n onderhoud – en dikwels ook 'n kort **visuele teks**, soos 'n foto met 'n onderskrif, 'n grafiek of 'n spotprent. Die vrae toets of jy *die teks* verstaan, nie wat jy toevallig oor die onderwerp weet nie.\n\n## Leesstrategieë: só pak jy 'n onbekende teks aan\n\n1. **Voorlees:** Kyk na die titel, opskrifte, bron, foto's en onderskrifte en **voorspel** waaroor die teks gaan.\n2. **Vluglees:** Lees die hele teks vinnig deur om die **hoofgedagte** te kry. Die eerste sin van elke paragraaf help baie.\n3. **Lees die vrae.** Nou weet jy waarna jy soek wanneer jy weer lees.\n4. **Soeklees:** Soek vinnig na **spesifieke feite**, soos name, datums, syfers of 'n sekere woord.\n5. **Onderstreep sleutelwoorde** in die vraag (die vraagwoord en die paragraaf- of reëlnommer) en in die teks.\n6. **Lees noukeurig** die deel waaroor die vraag gaan, en antwoord dan.\n\n## Vraagwoorde: wat word van jou verwag?\n\n| Vraagwoord | Wat jy moet doen |\n|---|---|\n| **Noem / Gee** | Lys net die feite; geen verduideliking nie. |\n| **Haal aan** | Skryf die presiese woord, frase of sin uit die teks tussen **aanhalingstekens**. |\n| **Verduidelik in eie woorde** | Sê dit anders as die teks; moenie afskryf nie. |\n| **Motiveer / Staaf** | Gee 'n rede of bewys **uit die teks**. |\n| **Beskryf** | Gee besonderhede oor hoe iets lyk of gebeur. |\n| **Vergelyk** | Noem ooreenkomste **en** verskille. |\n| **Onderskei** | Wys duidelik wat die verskil tussen twee dinge is. |\n| **Is jy dit eens? Motiveer.** | Gee jou eie mening (*ja* of *nee*) **plus** 'n rede. |\n| **Waar of onwaar? Motiveer.** | Skryf *Waar* of *Onwaar* en haal 'n bewys uit die teks aan. |\n\n### Ander vraagsoorte\n\n- **Meervoudige keuse:** Lees al vier opsies voordat jy kies.\n- **Verwysingsvrae:** *Waarna verwys “dit” in reël 4?* Lees die sin(ne) **voor** die woord. Die antwoord is 'n naamwoord of 'n idee wat reeds genoem is.\n- **Woordbetekenis in konteks:** Gee die betekenis wat die woord **in hierdie sin** het. Vervang die woord met jou antwoord en kyk of die sin nog logies is.\n- **Toon en houding:** Die skrywer se toon kan byvoorbeeld sarkasties, bekommerd, optimisties, krities of humoristies wees. Noem die toon **en** haal 'n woord aan wat dit bewys.\n- **Doel van die teks:** Wil die skrywer **inlig**, **oorreed** of **vermaak**?\n- **Feit of mening:** 'n **Feit** kan bewys of nagegaan word (*Die skoonmaakdag was op Saterdag.*). 'n **Mening** is iemand se opinie (*Dit was die beste dag van die jaar.*). Woorde soos *ek dink*, *behoort*, *die beste* en *verskriklik* dui dikwels op 'n mening.\n- **Titelvrae:** Is die titel gepas? Verbind die titel met die **hoofgedagte** van die teks.\n- **Stylfigure:** Benoem die vergelyking, metafoor, hiperbool of retoriese vraag **en** verduidelik die effek daarvan op die leser.\n\n## Vlakke van vrae\n\n| Vlak | Wat dit vra | Tipiese vraag |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Letterlik** | Die antwoord staan net so in die teks. | *Noem twee ...* |\n| **Afleidend** | Lees tussen die reëls. | *Wat lei jy af oor ...?* |\n| **Evaluerend** | Oordeel oor die teks of die skrywer. | *Is die titel geslaagd? Motiveer.* |\n| **Waarderend** | Jou eie reaksie op die teks. | *Hoe sou jy gevoel het?* |\n\n## Punte en antwoordtegniek\n\n- **Die punt in hakies = die aantal feite.** (2) beteken twee feite, of 'n bewering plus 'n rede.\n- Antwoord in **volsinne**, behalwe by meervoudige keuse, aanhalings en eenwoordantwoorde.\n- Gebruik die woorde van die vraag in jou antwoord: *Die vrywilligers het die dam skoongemaak omdat ...*\n- Nommer jou antwoorde presies soos in die vraestel.\n- Verdeel jou tyd: 120 minute vir 70 punte is ongeveer 1,7 minute per punt, dus omtrent 50 minute vir Afdeling A.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy haal aan wanneer die vraag **eie woorde** vra. Dit kos jou die punt, al is die inhoud reg.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy gee net **een** rede vir 'n vraag van **2 punte**.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy haal uit die **verkeerde reël of paragraaf** aan, of jy skryf 'n hele sin af terwyl net een woord gevra word.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy antwoord uit jou **algemene kennis** in plaas van uit die teks.","en":"## Paper 1: Language in context\n\nPaper 1 counts **70 marks** and you have **2 hours**.\n\n| Section | Content | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Comprehension (Leesbegrip) | 30 |\n| B | Summary (Opsomming) | 10 |\n| C | Language structures and conventions | 30 |\n\nIn **Section A** you get one or two reading texts – for example a newspaper or magazine article, a column (rubriek) or an interview (onderhoud) – and often a short **visual text** as well, such as a photo with a caption, a graph or a cartoon. The questions test whether you understand *the text*, not what you happen to know about the topic.\n\n## Reading strategies: how to tackle an unseen text\n\n1. **Pre-reading (voorlees):** Look at the title, headings, source, photos and captions and **predict (voorspel)** what the text is about.\n2. **Skimming (vluglees):** Read the whole text quickly to get the **main idea**. The first sentence of each paragraph helps a lot.\n3. **Read the questions.** Now you know what you are looking for when you read again.\n4. **Scanning (soeklees):** Search quickly for **specific facts**, such as names, dates, figures or a particular word.\n5. **Underline key words** in the question (the question word and the paragraph or line number) and in the text.\n6. **Read carefully** the part the question is about, and then answer.\n\n## Question words: what is expected of you?\n\n| Question word | What you must do |\n|---|---|\n| **Noem / Gee** (name/give) | Only list the facts; no explanation. |\n| **Haal aan** (quote) | Write the exact word, phrase or sentence from the text in **quotation marks**. |\n| **Verduidelik in eie woorde** (explain in your own words) | Say it differently from the text; do not copy. |\n| **Motiveer / Staaf** (motivate/substantiate) | Give a reason or proof **from the text**. |\n| **Beskryf** (describe) | Give details of how something looks or happens. |\n| **Vergelyk** (compare) | Give similarities **and** differences. |\n| **Onderskei** (distinguish) | Show clearly what the difference between two things is. |\n| **Is jy dit eens? Motiveer.** (Do you agree?) | Give your own opinion (*yes* or *no*) **plus** a reason. |\n| **Waar of onwaar? Motiveer.** (True or false?) | Write *True* or *False* and quote proof from the text. |\n\n### Other question types\n\n- **Multiple choice:** Read all four options before you choose.\n- **Reference questions:** *What does “dit” in line 4 refer to?* Read the sentence(s) **before** the word. The answer is a noun or an idea that has already been mentioned.\n- **Word meaning in context:** Give the meaning the word has **in this sentence**. Replace the word with your answer and check that the sentence is still logical.\n- **Tone and attitude:** The writer's tone can be, for example, sarcastic, worried, optimistic, critical or humorous. Name the tone **and** quote a word that proves it.\n- **Purpose of the text:** Does the writer want to **inform (inlig)**, **persuade (oorreed)** or **entertain (vermaak)**?\n- **Fact or opinion:** A **fact (feit)** can be proved or checked (*The clean-up day was on Saturday.*). An **opinion (mening)** is someone's view (*It was the best day of the year.*). Words such as *ek dink* (I think), *behoort* (should), *die beste* (the best) and *verskriklik* (terrible) often signal an opinion.\n- **Title questions:** Is the title suitable? Link the title to the **main idea** of the text.\n- **Figures of speech:** Name the simile, metaphor, hyperbole or rhetorical question **and** explain its effect on the reader.\n\n## Levels of questions\n\n| Level | What it asks | Typical question |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Literal (letterlik)** | The answer is in the text as it stands. | *Name two ...* |\n| **Inferential (afleidend)** | Read between the lines. | *What do you infer about ...?* |\n| **Evaluative (evaluerend)** | Judge the text or the writer. | *Is the title successful? Motivate.* |\n| **Appreciative (waarderend)** | Your own response to the text. | *How would you have felt?* |\n\n## Marks and answering technique\n\n- **The mark in brackets = the number of facts.** (2) means two facts, or a statement plus a reason.\n- Answer in **full sentences**, except for multiple choice, quotations and one-word answers.\n- Use the words of the question in your answer: *Die vrywilligers het die dam skoongemaak omdat ...*\n- Number your answers exactly as in the question paper.\n- Divide your time: 120 minutes for 70 marks is about 1.7 minutes per mark, so roughly 50 minutes for Section A.\n\n> **Common mistake:** You quote when the question asks for **your own words**. It costs you the mark, even if the content is right.\n\n> **Common mistake:** You give only **one** reason for a **2-mark** question.\n\n> **Common mistake:** You quote from the **wrong line or paragraph**, or you copy a whole sentence when only one word is asked for.\n\n> **Common mistake:** You answer from your **general knowledge** instead of from the text."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Vluglees","en":"Skimming"},"def":{"af":"Om 'n teks vinnig deur te lees om die hoofgedagte te kry.","en":"Reading a text quickly to get the main idea."}},{"term":{"af":"Soeklees","en":"Scanning"},"def":{"af":"Om vinnig na spesifieke inligting soos name, datums of syfers in 'n teks te soek.","en":"Searching a text quickly for specific information such as names, dates or figures."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorspel","en":"Predict"},"def":{"af":"Om voor die lees uit die titel, opskrifte en prente te raai waaroor die teks gaan.","en":"Before reading, guessing from the title, headings and pictures what the text is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofgedagte","en":"Main idea"},"def":{"af":"Die belangrikste boodskap van 'n teks of 'n paragraaf.","en":"The most important message of a text or a paragraph."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhaling","en":"Quotation"},"def":{"af":"Die presiese woorde uit die teks, tussen aanhalingstekens geskryf.","en":"The exact words from the text, written in quotation marks."}},{"term":{"af":"Afleiding","en":"Inference"},"def":{"af":"'n Gevolgtrekking wat jy uit leidrade in die teks maak, al word dit nie direk gesê nie.","en":"A conclusion you draw from clues in the text, even though it is not said directly."}},{"term":{"af":"Toon","en":"Tone"},"def":{"af":"Die skrywer se houding teenoor die onderwerp, soos dit in sy of haar woordkeuse blyk (bv. sarkasties, bekommerd, optimisties).","en":"The writer's attitude towards the subject, as shown in the choice of words (e.g. sarcastic, worried, optimistic)."}},{"term":{"af":"Feit","en":"Fact"},"def":{"af":"'n Bewering wat bewys of nagegaan kan word.","en":"A statement that can be proved or checked."}},{"term":{"af":"Mening","en":"Opinion"},"def":{"af":"Iemand se persoonlike opinie of oordeel, wat nie bewys kan word nie.","en":"Someone's personal view or judgement, which cannot be proved."}},{"term":{"af":"Retoriese vraag","en":"Rhetorical question"},"def":{"af":"'n Vraag wat nie 'n antwoord verwag nie, maar die leser laat dink of klem lê.","en":"A question that expects no answer, but makes the reader think or adds emphasis."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Leesteks 1: artikel oor tieners en selfone","en":"Text 1: article on teenagers and cellphones"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die artikel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Is jou selfoon jou baas?**\n\n(1) Dit is kwart oor elf op 'n Dinsdagaand in Brits. Die huis is stil, maar onder Ruan (15) se kombers gloei 'n skerm. “Net nog een video,” belowe hy vir homself. 'n Uur later rol hy steeds. Die volgende oggend sit hy met swaar oë in die wiskundeklas en hoor nie een woord van die les nie.\n\n(2) Ruan is nie alleen nie. Baie tieners erken dat hulle hul fone saans moeilik neersit. Volgens sielkundiges is dit geen wonder nie: baie toepassings word doelbewus so ontwerp dat jy aanhou blaai. Elke nuwe “like” voel soos 'n klein beloning, en jou brein soek dadelik die volgende een.\n\n(3) Die gevolge is ernstig. Wie te min slaap, sukkel om te konsentreer, en wie snags rol, is bedags 'n wandelende spook. Sommige tieners voel boonop sleg oor hulself wanneer hulle hul gewone lewe met ander se “perfekte” foto's vergelyk.\n\n(4) Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie. Dieselfde toestel help jou om met jou klasmaats oor huiswerk te gesels, vir 'n toets te leer en met jou ouma in Polokwane te praat. Die probleem is nie die foon self nie, maar hoe ons dit gebruik.\n\n(5) Mev. Thandi Mokoena, 'n LO-onderwyseres in Madibeng, gee 'n eenvoudige raad: “Laai jou foon snags in die kombuis, nie langs jou bed nie.” Is dit regtig te veel gevra vir 'n goeie nag se rus?\n\n**Vrae**\n\n1.1 Noem die tyd en die dorp waar die teks begin. (2)\n1.2 Haal 'n frase uit paragraaf 1 aan wat wys dat Ruan die volgende oggend moeg is. (1)\n1.3 Verduidelik in jou eie woorde waarom dit volgens sielkundiges “geen wonder” is dat tieners hul fone moeilik neersit. (2)\n1.4 Benoem die stylfiguur in “wie snags rol, is bedags 'n wandelende spook” (paragraaf 3) en verduidelik wat dit beteken. (2)\n1.5 Waarna verwys “Dieselfde toestel” in paragraaf 4? (1)\n1.6 Waar of onwaar? Die skrywer meen dat selfone verbied moet word. Motiveer met 'n aanhaling. (2)\n1.7 Is die volgende stellings feite of menings? (a) Ruan is 15 jaar oud. (b) Die probleem is nie die foon self nie, maar hoe ons dit gebruik. (2)\n1.8 Benoem die stylfiguur in die laaste sin van die teks en sê wat die doel daarvan is. (2)\n1.9 Is die titel “Is jou selfoon jou baas?” gepas? Motiveer. (2)","en":"Read the article (in Afrikaans; translated here) and answer the questions.\n\n**Is your cellphone your boss?**\n\n(1) It is a quarter past eleven on a Tuesday night in Brits. The house is quiet, but under Ruan's (15) blanket a screen glows. “Just one more video,” he promises himself. An hour later he is still scrolling. The next morning he sits in the maths class with heavy eyes (“met swaar oë”) and does not hear a single word of the lesson.\n\n(2) Ruan is not alone. Many teenagers admit that they find it hard to put their phones down at night. According to psychologists this is no wonder (“geen wonder”): many apps are deliberately designed so that you keep scrolling. Every new “like” feels like a small reward, and your brain immediately looks for the next one.\n\n(3) The consequences are serious. Whoever sleeps too little struggles to concentrate, and whoever scrolls at night is a walking ghost by day (“'n wandelende spook”). Some teenagers also feel bad about themselves when they compare their ordinary lives with other people's “perfect” photos.\n\n(4) Yet the cellphone is not the enemy (“Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie”). The same device (“Dieselfde toestel”) helps you to chat to your classmates about homework, to study for a test and to talk to your gran in Polokwane. The problem is not the phone itself, but how we use it.\n\n(5) Mrs Thandi Mokoena, an LO teacher in Madibeng, gives simple advice: “Charge your phone in the kitchen at night, not next to your bed.” Is that really too much to ask for a good night's rest?\n\n**Questions**\n\n1.1 Name the time and the town where the text begins. (2)\n1.2 Quote a phrase from paragraph 1 that shows that Ruan is tired the next morning. (1)\n1.3 Explain in your own words why, according to psychologists, it is “no wonder” that teenagers struggle to put their phones down. (2)\n1.4 Name the figure of speech in “wie snags rol, is bedags 'n wandelende spook” (paragraph 3) and explain what it means. (2)\n1.5 What does “Dieselfde toestel” in paragraph 4 refer to? (1)\n1.6 True or false? The writer believes that cellphones should be banned. Motivate with a quotation. (2)\n1.7 Are the following statements facts or opinions? (a) Ruan is 15 years old. (b) The problem is not the phone itself, but how we use it. (2)\n1.8 Name the figure of speech in the last sentence of the text and say what its purpose is. (2)\n1.9 Is the title “Is jou selfoon jou baas?” suitable? Motivate. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**1.1** (2) Dit is kwart oor elf in die aand ✔ en die toneel speel in Brits af ✔. *Letterlike vraag: twee feite = twee punte.*","en":"**1.1** (2) It is a quarter past eleven at night ✔ and the scene is in Brits ✔. *Literal question: two facts = two marks.*"},{"af":"**1.2** (1) “met swaar oë” ✔. *Haal aan = presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens.*","en":"**1.2** (1) “met swaar oë” (with heavy eyes) ✔. *Quote = the exact words in quotation marks.*"},{"af":"**1.3** (2) Baie toepassings word met opset so gemaak dat 'n mens nie wil ophou nie ✔, en elke “like” gee jou 'n lekker gevoel wat jy weer wil hê ✔. *Eie woorde: moenie die sin afskryf nie.*","en":"**1.3** (2) Many apps are made on purpose so that you do not want to stop ✔, and every “like” gives you a good feeling that you want again ✔. *Own words: do not copy the sentence.*"},{"af":"**1.4** (2) Metafoor ✔. Die persoon is so moeg dat hy soos 'n spook rondloop: bleek, half wakker en nie regtig daar nie ✔.","en":"**1.4** (2) Metaphor ✔. The person is so tired that he walks around like a ghost: pale, half awake and not really there ✔."},{"af":"**1.5** (1) Na die selfoon ✔. *Lees die sin voor die verwysing: “Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie.”*","en":"**1.5** (1) To the cellphone ✔. *Read the sentence before the reference: “Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie.”*"},{"af":"**1.6** (2) Onwaar ✔. “Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie.” ✔ (Ook reg: “Die probleem is nie die foon self nie, maar hoe ons dit gebruik.”) *Sonder die aanhaling kry jy net 1 punt.*","en":"**1.6** (2) False ✔. “Tog is die selfoon nie die vyand nie.” ✔ (Also correct: “Die probleem is nie die foon self nie, maar hoe ons dit gebruik.”) *Without the quotation you get only 1 mark.*"},{"af":"**1.7** (2) (a) Feit ✔ – sy ouderdom kan nagegaan word. (b) Mening ✔ – dit is die skrywer se oordeel.","en":"**1.7** (2) (a) Fact ✔ – his age can be checked. (b) Opinion ✔ – it is the writer's judgement."},{"af":"**1.8** (2) Retoriese vraag ✔. Die skrywer laat die leser self besef dat die raad maklik is om te volg en oorreed hom so om dit te doen ✔.","en":"**1.8** (2) Rhetorical question ✔. The writer makes readers realise for themselves that the advice is easy to follow and so persuades them to do it ✔."},{"af":"**1.9** (2) Ja ✔. Die teks wys hoe die foon tieners se gedrag beheer, soos 'n baas: Ruan wil ophou, maar hy rol 'n uur langer ✔. *Evaluerende vraag: standpunt + bewys uit die teks.*","en":"**1.9** (2) Yes ✔. The text shows how the phone controls teenagers' behaviour, like a boss: Ruan wants to stop, but he scrolls for another hour ✔. *Evaluative question: standpoint + proof from the text.*"}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 16 punte. Let op hoe elke antwoord presies soveel feite gee as wat die punte vra.","en":"Total: 16 marks. Notice how every answer gives exactly as many facts as the marks ask for."}},{"title":{"af":"Leesteks 2: koerantberig oor die Hartbeespoortdam","en":"Text 2: newspaper report on the Hartbeespoort Dam"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die koerantberig en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Harties kry 'n nuwe kans**\n\n(1) Meer as driehonderd vrywilligers het Saterdag hul moue opgerol en die oewer van die Hartbeespoortdam skoongemaak. Leerders, vissermanne, kerkgroepe en sakemense het reeds om sewe-uur by die damwal bymekaargekom, gewapen met handskoene en swart vullissakke.\n\n(2) Die dam sukkel al jare lank met groen alge en met waterhiasint, 'n indringerplant wat soos 'n dik groen kombers oor die water versprei. Plastiekbottels, skyfiesakkies en ou visgerei maak die probleem nog erger.\n\n(3) “Ons kan nie net kla en wag dat iemand anders dit regmaak nie,” sê Lerato Molefe (16), 'n Graad 10-leerder van Brits wat die dag op sosiale media help reël het. “As elkeen een sak volmaak, maak ons saam 'n reuse verskil.”\n\n(4) Teen middagete was die munisipaliteit se bakkies propvol. Die vrywilligers het honderde sakke vullis opgetel, en een visserman het selfs 'n ou yskas uit die riete gesleep!\n\n(5) Die werk is egter nog lank nie klaar nie. Die organiseerders wil elke drie maande 'n skoonmaakdag hou, en hulle vra dat inwoners en besoekers hul vullis saam huis toe neem. Die dam is ons almal se erfenis – en dit is ons almal se verantwoordelikheid.\n\n**Vrae**\n\n2.1 Noem enige twee groepe mense wat aan die skoonmaakdag deelgeneem het. (2)\n2.2 Haal 'n vergelyking uit paragraaf 2 aan. (1)\n2.3 Verduidelik in jou eie woorde waarom die waterhiasint 'n probleem is. (2)\n2.4 Waarna verwys “dit” in Lerato se woorde “dat iemand anders dit regmaak”? (1)\n2.5 Wat lei jy uit paragraaf 3 af oor Lerato se karakter? Motiveer. (2)\n2.6 Waarom eindig paragraaf 4 met 'n uitroepteken? (1)\n2.7 Wat is die toon van die laaste sin? Haal een woord aan wat hierdie toon ondersteun. (2)\n2.8 Is die titel “Harties kry 'n nuwe kans” gepas? Motiveer. (2)","en":"Read the newspaper report (in Afrikaans; translated here) and answer the questions.\n\n**Harties gets a new chance**\n\n(1) More than three hundred volunteers rolled up their sleeves on Saturday and cleaned the shore of the Hartbeespoort Dam. Learners, anglers, church groups and business people had gathered at the dam wall by seven o'clock, armed with gloves and black refuse bags.\n\n(2) For years the dam has struggled with green algae and with water hyacinth, an invasive plant that spreads over the water like a thick green blanket (“soos 'n dik groen kombers”). Plastic bottles, chip packets and old fishing gear make the problem even worse.\n\n(3) “We cannot just complain and wait for someone else to fix it (“dit regmaak”),” says Lerato Molefe (16), a Grade 10 learner from Brits who helped to organise the day on social media. “If everyone fills one bag, together we make a huge difference.”\n\n(4) By lunchtime the municipality's bakkies were packed full. The volunteers picked up hundreds of bags of rubbish, and one angler even dragged an old fridge out of the reeds!\n\n(5) The work, however, is far from finished. The organisers want to hold a clean-up day every three months, and they ask residents and visitors to take their rubbish home with them. The dam is the heritage of all of us – and it is the responsibility (“verantwoordelikheid”) of all of us.\n\n**Questions**\n\n2.1 Name any two groups of people who took part in the clean-up day. (2)\n2.2 Quote a simile from paragraph 2. (1)\n2.3 Explain in your own words why the water hyacinth is a problem. (2)\n2.4 What does “dit” in Lerato's words “dat iemand anders dit regmaak” refer to? (1)\n2.5 What do you infer from paragraph 3 about Lerato's character? Motivate. (2)\n2.6 Why does paragraph 4 end with an exclamation mark? (1)\n2.7 What is the tone of the last sentence? Quote one word that supports this tone. (2)\n2.8 Is the title “Harties kry 'n nuwe kans” suitable? Motivate. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**2.1** (2) Leerders ✔ en vissermanne ✔ (ook reg: kerkgroepe, sakemense). *Noem = net die feite, geen verduideliking nie.*","en":"**2.1** (2) Learners ✔ and anglers ✔ (also correct: church groups, business people). *Name = only the facts, no explanation.*"},{"af":"**2.2** (1) “soos 'n dik groen kombers” ✔. *'n Vergelyking gebruik soos of as.*","en":"**2.2** (1) “soos 'n dik groen kombers” (like a thick green blanket) ✔. *A simile uses soos or as.*"},{"af":"**2.3** (2) Dit is 'n plant wat nie van nature hier hoort nie ✔ en wat die wateroppervlak heeltemal toemaak ✔.","en":"**2.3** (2) It is a plant that does not naturally belong here ✔ and that covers the surface of the water completely ✔."},{"af":"**2.4** (1) Na die besoedeling van die dam (die vuil toestand van die dam) ✔. *Die verwysing is 'n idee uit die vorige paragraaf, nie net een woord nie.*","en":"**2.4** (1) To the pollution of the dam (the dirty state of the dam) ✔. *The reference is an idea from the previous paragraph, not just one word.*"},{"af":"**2.5** (2) Sy is verantwoordelik en neem self die inisiatief ✔, want sy het gehelp om die skoonmaakdag te reël in plaas daarvan om net te kla ✔. *Afleidend: eienskap + bewys.*","en":"**2.5** (2) She is responsible and takes the initiative ✔, because she helped to organise the clean-up day instead of just complaining ✔. *Inferential: trait + proof.*"},{"af":"**2.6** (1) Om te wys hoe verbasend dit is dat iemand 'n hele yskas in die riete gekry het ✔.","en":"**2.6** (1) To show how surprising it is that someone found a whole fridge in the reeds ✔."},{"af":"**2.7** (2) Die toon is ernstig en oproepend ✔: “verantwoordelikheid” ✔ (ook reg: “ons almal”).","en":"**2.7** (2) The tone is serious and calls the reader to action ✔: “verantwoordelikheid” (responsibility) ✔ (also correct: “ons almal”)."},{"af":"**2.8** (2) Ja ✔. Die dam was vuil en besoedel, maar ná die skoonmaakdag en met die plan om elke drie maande weer skoon te maak, kry dit 'n kans om te herstel ✔.","en":"**2.8** (2) Yes ✔. The dam was dirty and polluted, but after the clean-up day and with the plan to clean it again every three months, it gets a chance to recover ✔."}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 13 punte. Die vrae beweeg van letterlik (2.1–2.2) na afleidend (2.3–2.6) en evaluerend (2.7–2.8).","en":"Total: 13 marks. The questions move from literal (2.1–2.2) to inferential (2.3–2.6) and evaluative (2.7–2.8)."}},{"title":{"af":"Leesteks 3: rubriek oor beurtkrag (toon en ironie)","en":"Text 3: column on load-shedding (tone and irony)"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die rubriek en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Kers, kopflits en ek**\n\n(1) Ek wil vandag dankie sê vir beurtkrag. Waar anders kry 'n mens die kans om jou huiswerk by kerslig te doen, soos 'n regte digter uit die negentiende eeu? Ag, wat 'n voorreg.\n\n(2) Om sesuur gaan die ligte dood – presies wanneer Ma die pasta wil kook en ek my Geskiedenisprojek moet tik. Ons sit soos uile in die donker en staar na mekaar. My boetie vra vir die honderdste keer: “Wanneer kom die krag terug?”\n\n(3) Ons gesin het intussen kenners geword. Ons ken die beurtkragskedule beter as ons eie verjaarsdae. Die gaskoker staan reg, die kragbank is gelaai en Pa het drie kopflitse, al kan hy nooit een kry wanneer hy dit nodig het nie.\n\n(4) Natuurlik is dit nie net snaaks nie. Klein besighede op Brits verloor geld, en leerders wat nie 'n kragopwekker of sonpanele het nie, sukkel om te leer. Dit is ernstige probleme wat ernstige oplossings verg.\n\n(5) Maar tot dan? Dan speel ons maar weer kaart by die kers. En weet jy wat? Verlede week het ek vir die eerste keer van Pa gewen.\n\n**Vrae**\n\n3.1 Noem twee dinge wat die gesin gereed hou vir beurtkrag. (2)\n3.2 Is die skrywer regtig dankbaar vir beurtkrag? Haal 'n sin uit paragraaf 1 aan om jou antwoord te bewys. (2)\n3.3 Haal 'n vergelyking uit paragraaf 2 aan. (1)\n3.4 Benoem die stylfiguur in “vir die honderdste keer” (paragraaf 2) en verduidelik die effek daarvan. (2)\n3.5 Verduidelik die ironie in die laaste sin van paragraaf 3. (2)\n3.6 Hoe verander die toon in paragraaf 4? Motiveer. (2)\n3.7 Gee 'n sinoniem vir “verg” soos dit in paragraaf 4 gebruik word. (1)\n3.8 Dink jy die slot van die rubriek is geslaagd? Motiveer. (2)","en":"Read the column (in Afrikaans; translated here) and answer the questions.\n\n**Candle, head torch and me**\n\n(1) Today I want to say thank you for load-shedding. Where else does a person get the chance to do homework by candlelight, like a real nineteenth-century poet? Oh, what a privilege (“Ag, wat 'n voorreg.”).\n\n(2) At six o'clock the lights go out – exactly when Mom wants to cook the pasta and I have to type my History project. We sit like owls (“soos uile”) in the dark and stare at each other. My little brother asks for the hundredth time (“vir die honderdste keer”): “When is the power coming back?”\n\n(3) Meanwhile our family has become experts. We know the load-shedding schedule better than our own birthdays. The gas cooker stands ready, the power bank is charged and Dad has three head torches, although he can never find one when he needs it.\n\n(4) Of course it is not only funny. Small businesses in Brits lose money, and learners who do not have a generator or solar panels struggle to study. These are serious problems that require (“verg”) serious solutions.\n\n(5) But until then? Then we just play cards by the candle again. And do you know what? Last week I beat Dad for the first time.\n\n**Questions**\n\n3.1 Name two things the family keeps ready for load-shedding. (2)\n3.2 Is the writer really grateful for load-shedding? Quote a sentence from paragraph 1 to prove your answer. (2)\n3.3 Quote a simile from paragraph 2. (1)\n3.4 Name the figure of speech in “vir die honderdste keer” (paragraph 2) and explain its effect. (2)\n3.5 Explain the irony in the last sentence of paragraph 3. (2)\n3.6 How does the tone change in paragraph 4? Motivate. (2)\n3.7 Give a synonym for “verg” as it is used in paragraph 4. (1)\n3.8 Do you think the ending of the column is successful? Motivate. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**3.1** (2) Die gaskoker ✔ en die gelaaide kragbank ✔ (ook reg: die kopflitse).","en":"**3.1** (2) The gas cooker ✔ and the charged power bank ✔ (also correct: the head torches)."},{"af":"**3.2** (2) Nee, die skrywer is sarkasties ✔. “Ag, wat 'n voorreg.” ✔ *Sarkasme: jy sê die teenoorgestelde van wat jy bedoel om te spot.*","en":"**3.2** (2) No, the writer is being sarcastic ✔. “Ag, wat 'n voorreg.” ✔ *Sarcasm: you say the opposite of what you mean in order to mock.*"},{"af":"**3.3** (1) “soos uile” ✔.","en":"**3.3** (1) “soos uile” (like owls) ✔."},{"af":"**3.4** (2) Hiperbool (oordrywing) ✔. Dit beklemtoon hoe dikwels en hoe ongeduldig die boetie vra ✔.","en":"**3.4** (2) Hyperbole (exaggeration) ✔. It emphasises how often and how impatiently the little brother asks ✔."},{"af":"**3.5** (2) Pa het meer as genoeg kopflitse ✔, maar hy kry nooit een nie – juis wanneer dit donker is en hy dit die nodigste het ✔.","en":"**3.5** (2) Dad has more than enough head torches ✔, but he never finds one – exactly when it is dark and he needs one most ✔."},{"af":"**3.6** (2) Die toon word ernstig ✔, want die skrywer noem die werklike skade: besighede verloor geld en leerders sukkel om te leer ✔.","en":"**3.6** (2) The tone becomes serious ✔, because the writer names the real damage: businesses lose money and learners struggle to study ✔."},{"af":"**3.7** (1) vereis ✔ (ook reg: vra, benodig). *Toets dit in die sin: “ernstige probleme wat ernstige oplossings vereis”.*","en":"**3.7** (1) vereis (require) ✔ (also correct: vra, benodig). *Test it in the sentence: “ernstige probleme wat ernstige oplossings vereis”.*"},{"af":"**3.8** (2) Ja ✔. Die slot keer terug na die ligte toon van die begin en eindig met 'n positiewe, snaakse wending, sodat die leser met 'n glimlag klaar lees ✔. *Evaluerend: oordeel + rede.*","en":"**3.8** (2) Yes ✔. The ending returns to the light tone of the beginning and ends with a positive, funny twist, so that the reader finishes with a smile ✔. *Evaluative: judgement + reason.*"}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 14 punte. By toonvrae noem jy die toon en gee jy bewys; by stylfigure benoem jy dit en verduidelik jy die effek.","en":"Total: 14 marks. For tone questions you name the tone and give proof; for figures of speech you name them and explain the effect."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel Afdeling A (Leesbegrip) in Vraestel 1?","en":"How many marks does Section A (Comprehension) count in Paper 1?"},"options":[{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"50","en":"50"},{"af":"70","en":"70"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Afdeling A tel 30 punte. Afdeling B (Opsomming) tel 10, Afdeling C (Taalstrukture) tel 30, en die hele vraestel tel 70.","en":"Section A counts 30 marks. Section B (Summary) counts 10, Section C (Language structures) counts 30, and the whole paper counts 70."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer jy 'n teks vinnig deurlees om net die hoofgedagte te kry, heet dit ___.","en":"When you read a text quickly just to get the main idea, it is called ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["vluglees"],"en":["vluglees","skimming","skim"]},"explain":{"af":"Vluglees = vinnig lees vir die hoofgedagte. Soeklees is wanneer jy na 'n spesifieke feit soek.","en":"Vluglees (skimming) = reading quickly for the main idea. Soeklees (scanning) is when you look for a specific fact."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["soeklees","voorspel","proeflees"],"en":["soeklees","scanning","proofreading"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wanneer jy vinnig na 'n spesifieke feit soos 'n datum of 'n naam in 'n teks soek, heet dit ___.","en":"When you search a text quickly for a specific fact such as a date or a name, it is called ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["soeklees"],"en":["soeklees","scanning","scan"]},"explain":{"af":"Soeklees = soek na spesifieke inligting. Jou oë hardloop oor die teks totdat jy die naam, datum of syfer kry.","en":"Soeklees (scanning) = searching for specific information. Your eyes run over the text until you find the name, date or figure."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vluglees","voorlees","opsom"],"en":["vluglees","skimming","summarising"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"By 'n vraag wat sê “Haal aan”, mag jy die antwoord in jou eie woorde skryf solank die betekenis reg is.","en":"In a question that says “Haal aan” (quote), you may write the answer in your own words as long as the meaning is right."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. “Haal aan” beteken jy skryf die presiese woorde uit die teks tussen aanhalingstekens. Eie woorde kry nie die punt nie.","en":"False. “Haal aan” means you write the exact words from the text in quotation marks. Your own words do not earn the mark."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Vraag tel (3) punte. Jy moet dus ___ feite in jou antwoord gee.","en":"A question counts (3) marks. You must therefore give ___ facts in your answer."},"answers":{"af":["3","drie"],"en":["3","three","drie"]},"explain":{"af":"Die punt in hakies dui die aantal feite aan: (3) = drie feite, of 'n bewering plus twee redes.","en":"The mark in brackets shows the number of facts: (3) = three facts, or a statement plus two reasons."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","2","4"],"en":["1","2","4"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke vraagwoord by wat dit van jou vereis.","en":"Match each question word to what it requires of you."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Noem","en":"Noem (name)"},"r":{"af":"Lys die feite sonder verduideliking","en":"List the facts without explanation"}},{"l":{"af":"Haal aan","en":"Haal aan (quote)"},"r":{"af":"Skryf die presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens","en":"Write the exact words in quotation marks"}},{"l":{"af":"Motiveer","en":"Motiveer (motivate)"},"r":{"af":"Gee 'n rede of bewys uit die teks","en":"Give a reason or proof from the text"}},{"l":{"af":"Vergelyk","en":"Vergelyk (compare)"},"r":{"af":"Noem ooreenkomste en verskille","en":"Give similarities and differences"}},{"l":{"af":"Is jy dit eens?","en":"Is jy dit eens? (Do you agree?)"},"r":{"af":"Gee jou eie mening plus 'n rede","en":"Give your own opinion plus a reason"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke vraagwoord vra iets anders. As jy die vraagwoord verkeerd lees, verloor jy punte al ken jy die inhoud.","en":"Every question word asks for something different. If you misread the question word, you lose marks even if you know the content."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vraag lui: “Noem twee redes waarom die vrywilligers die dam skoongemaak het. (2)” Wat verwag die nasiener?","en":"A question reads: “Name two reasons why the volunteers cleaned the dam. (2)” What does the marker expect?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Lang paragraaf oor besoedeling in Suid-Afrika","en":"A long paragraph about pollution in South Africa"},{"af":"Een goeie rede met baie besonderhede","en":"One good reason with lots of detail"},{"af":"Twee afsonderlike redes uit die teks, een punt elk","en":"Two separate reasons from the text, one mark each"},{"af":"'n Aanhaling van die hele paragraaf","en":"A quotation of the whole paragraph"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"(2) = twee feite. Een rede, hoe goed ook al, kry net een punt, en algemene kennis buite die teks tel nie.","en":"(2) = two facts. One reason, however good, earns only one mark, and general knowledge from outside the text does not count."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is 'n MENING?","en":"Which sentence is an OPINION?"},"options":[{"af":"Die skoonmaakdag het om sewe-uur begin.","en":"Die skoonmaakdag het om sewe-uur begin. (The clean-up day started at seven.)"},{"af":"Die munisipaliteit se bakkies het die vullis weggery.","en":"Die munisipaliteit se bakkies het die vullis weggery. (The municipality's bakkies took the rubbish away.)"},{"af":"Waterhiasint is 'n indringerplant.","en":"Waterhiasint is 'n indringerplant. (Water hyacinth is an invasive plant.)"},{"af":"Hartbeespoortdam is die mooiste plek in die Noordwes.","en":"Hartbeespoortdam is die mooiste plek in die Noordwes. (Hartbeespoort Dam is the most beautiful place in the North West.)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"“Die mooiste” is 'n persoonlike oordeel wat nie bewys kan word nie. Die ander drie sinne kan nagegaan word, dus is hulle feite.","en":"“The most beautiful” is a personal judgement that cannot be proved. The other three sentences can be checked, so they are facts."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die woorde “ek dink” in 'n sin dui gewoonlik daarop dat die skrywer 'n mening gee.","en":"The words “ek dink” (I think) in a sentence usually show that the writer is giving an opinion."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. “Ek dink”, “behoort”, “die beste” en “verskriklik” is tipiese leidrade vir 'n mening, want dit wys iemand se persoonlike oordeel.","en":"True. “Ek dink”, “behoort” (should), “die beste” (the best) and “verskriklik” (terrible) are typical clues for an opinion, because they show someone's personal judgement."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Teks eindig met: “Sluit Saterdag by ons aan – jou dam het jou nodig!” Die hoofdoel van hierdie slotsin is om die leser te ___.","en":"A text ends with: “Sluit Saterdag by ons aan – jou dam het jou nodig!” (Join us on Saturday – your dam needs you!) The main purpose of this closing sentence is to ___ the reader (Afrikaans or English)."},"answers":{"af":["oorreed","oortuig"],"en":["oorreed","oortuig","persuade","convince"]},"explain":{"af":"Die bevel (“Sluit aan”) en die emosionele beroep (“jou dam het jou nodig”) wil die leser oorreed om iets te doen.","en":"The command (“Sluit aan” – join) and the emotional appeal (“your dam needs you”) aim to persuade the reader to do something."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vermaak","inlig","beskryf"],"en":["entertain","inform","describe"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: “Ag, wonderlik, nog 'n aand sonder krag. Net wat ek nodig gehad het.” Wat is die toon?","en":"Read: “Ag, wonderlik, nog 'n aand sonder krag. Net wat ek nodig gehad het.” (Oh, wonderful, another evening without power. Just what I needed.) What is the tone?"},"options":[{"af":"Optimisties","en":"Optimistic"},{"af":"Sarkasties","en":"Sarcastic"},{"af":"Bekommerd","en":"Worried"},{"af":"Simpatiek","en":"Sympathetic"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker sê “wonderlik” maar bedoel die teenoorgestelde. Om die teenoorgestelde te sê om te spot, is sarkasme.","en":"The speaker says “wonderful” but means the opposite. Saying the opposite in order to mock is sarcasm."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In “Die verkeer op die N4 was 'n slak” word die verkeer direk, sonder “soos”, met 'n slak vergelyk. Hierdie stylfiguur is 'n ___.","en":"In “Die verkeer op die N4 was 'n slak” (The traffic on the N4 was a snail) the traffic is compared directly, without “soos” (like), with a snail. This figure of speech is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["metafoor"],"en":["metaphor","metafoor"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Metafoor sê iets IS iets anders. 'n Vergelyking sou gesê het: “Die verkeer was soos 'n slak.” Die effek: jy sien hoe stadig die verkeer beweeg.","en":"A metaphor says something IS something else. A simile would have said: “Die verkeer was soos 'n slak.” The effect: you see how slowly the traffic moves."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vergelyking","hiperbool","personifikasie"],"en":["simile","hyperbole","personification"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: “Die munisipaliteit het nuwe vullisdromme langs die dam opgesit, maar die bobbejane het hulle binne 'n week omgegooi. Dit het die inwoners baie kwaad gemaak.” Waarna verwys “Dit”?","en":"Read: “Die munisipaliteit het nuwe vullisdromme langs die dam opgesit, maar die bobbejane het hulle binne 'n week omgegooi. Dit het die inwoners baie kwaad gemaak.” (The municipality put up new bins next to the dam, but the baboons knocked them over within a week. This made the residents very angry.) What does “Dit” refer to?"},"options":[{"af":"Na die munisipaliteit","en":"To the municipality"},{"af":"Na die nuwe vullisdromme","en":"To the new bins"},{"af":"Na die feit dat die bobbejane die dromme omgegooi het","en":"To the fact that the baboons knocked over the bins"},{"af":"Na die dam","en":"To the dam"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"“Dit” verwys hier na 'n hele idee uit die vorige sin, nie na een naamwoord nie. Die inwoners is kwaad oor wat die bobbejane gedoen het.","en":"“Dit” here refers to a whole idea from the previous sentence, not to one noun. The residents are angry about what the baboons did."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter vraag is 'n AFLEIDENDE vraag?","en":"Which question is an INFERENTIAL question?"},"options":[{"af":"Wat lei jy uit Lerato se woorde af oor haar houding teenoor haar gemeenskap?","en":"Wat lei jy uit Lerato se woorde af oor haar houding teenoor haar gemeenskap? (What do you infer from Lerato's words about her attitude to her community?)"},{"af":"Noem die naam van die leerder wat die dag help reël het.","en":"Noem die naam van die leerder wat die dag help reël het. (Name the learner who helped organise the day.)"},{"af":"Hoe sou jy gevoel het as jy die yskas gevind het?","en":"Hoe sou jy gevoel het as jy die yskas gevind het? (How would you have felt if you had found the fridge?)"},{"af":"Is die titel 'n goeie keuse? Motiveer.","en":"Is die titel 'n goeie keuse? Motiveer. (Is the title a good choice? Motivate.)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By 'n afleidende vraag lees jy tussen die reëls: die antwoord staan nie net so in die teks nie. Die naam is letterlik, jou gevoel is waarderend en die titeloordeel is evaluerend.","en":"In an inferential question you read between the lines: the answer is not stated as such in the text. The name is literal, your feeling is appreciative and judging the title is evaluative."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Teks: “'n Uur later rol hy steeds. Die volgende oggend sit hy met swaar oë in die klas.” Vraag: “Verduidelik in jou eie woorde waarom Ruan moeg is. (2)” Watter antwoord kry 2 punte?","en":"Text: “'n Uur later rol hy steeds. Die volgende oggend sit hy met swaar oë in die klas.” Question: “Explain in your own words why Ruan is tired. (2)” Which answer earns 2 marks?"},"options":[{"af":"“'n Uur later rol hy steeds.”","en":"“'n Uur later rol hy steeds.” (a quotation)"},{"af":"Ruan is moeg.","en":"Ruan is moeg. (Ruan is tired.)"},{"af":"Ruan hou nie van wiskunde nie.","en":"Ruan hou nie van wiskunde nie. (Ruan does not like maths.)"},{"af":"Ruan het tot laat in die nag op sy foon gebly en daarom te min geslaap.","en":"Ruan het tot laat in die nag op sy foon gebly en daarom te min geslaap. (Ruan stayed on his phone until late at night and therefore slept too little.)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die regte antwoord gee twee feite (laat op die foon + te min slaap) in eie woorde. Die aanhaling ignoreer “eie woorde”, “Ruan is moeg” herhaal net die vraag, en die wiskunde-antwoord staan nie in die teks nie.","en":"The right answer gives two facts (late on the phone + too little sleep) in own words. The quotation ignores “own words”, “Ruan is tired” just repeats the question, and the maths answer is not in the text."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vraag: “Is jy dit eens dat skole selfone in die klas moet verbied? Motiveer. (2)” Watter antwoord verdien volpunte?","en":"Question: “Do you agree that schools should ban cellphones in class? Motivate. (2)” Which answer earns full marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Ja.","en":"Ja. (Yes.)"},{"af":"Nee, want 'n selfoon kan in die klas nuttig wees, byvoorbeeld om vinnig iets na te slaan.","en":"Nee, want 'n selfoon kan in die klas nuttig wees, byvoorbeeld om vinnig iets na te slaan. (No, because a cellphone can be useful in class, for example to look something up quickly.)"},{"af":"Ja, ek stem saam, want ek is dit eens.","en":"Ja, ek stem saam, want ek is dit eens. (Yes, I agree, because I agree.)"},{"af":"Die teks sê dat 'n selfoon jou kan help om vir 'n toets te leer.","en":"Die teks sê dat 'n selfoon jou kan help om vir 'n toets te leer. (The text says a cellphone can help you study for a test.)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Evalueringsvraag vra 'n duidelike standpunt (1) plus 'n geldige rede (1). “Ja.” het geen rede nie, die derde antwoord herhaal net die standpunt, en die vierde gee geen standpunt nie.","en":"An evaluation question asks for a clear standpoint (1) plus a valid reason (1). “Yes.” has no reason, the third answer only repeats the standpoint, and the fourth gives no standpoint."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t1-naamwoorde","title":{"af":"Woordsoorte 1: selfstandige naamwoorde, lidwoorde, voornaamwoorde en byvoeglike naamwoorde","en":"Parts of speech 1: nouns, articles, pronouns and adjectives"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal naamwoorde, lidwoorde, voornaamwoorde en byvoeglike naamwoorde in 'n teks kan herken en korrek kan vorm: meervoude, verkleinwoorde, vroulike vorme, verbuiging en trappe van vergelyking.","en":"You will be able to recognise nouns, articles, pronouns and adjectives in a text and form them correctly: plurals, diminutives, feminine forms, inflection and degrees of comparison."},"summary":{"af":"## Selfstandige naamwoorde (s.nw.)\n\n'n **Selfstandige naamwoord** is die naam van 'n persoon, dier, plek, ding, idee of gevoel.\n\n| Soort | Wat dit benoem | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Soortnaam** | enige lid van 'n groep | hond, skool, rivier |\n| **Eienaam** | 'n spesifieke persoon of plek; altyd 'n hoofletter | Thabo, Brits, Magaliesberg |\n| **Versamelnaam** | 'n groep as een geheel | 'n kudde skape, 'n swerm bye, 'n trop leeus |\n| **Stofnaam** | 'n stof of materiaal | goud, water, sand |\n| **Abstrakte s.nw.** | iets wat jy nie kan sien of aanraak nie | vreugde, liefde, vrees |\n| **Maatnaam** | 'n maat of eenheid | liter, kilogram, meter |\n\n### Meervoude\n\n| Uitgang | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **-e** | huis → huise, boek → boeke |\n| **-s** | tafel → tafels, bakker → bakkers, oom → ooms, koning → konings |\n| **-ers / -ere** | kind → kinders, lam → lammers, goed → goedere |\n| **Onreëlmatig** | skip → skepe, stad → stede, lid → lede, dag → dae, oog → oë |\n\n**Spelreëls by meervoude:**\n\n- **Kort klinker:** verdubbel die slotkonsonant: kat → katte, pen → penne, bus → busse.\n- **Lang klinker in 'n oop lettergreep** word enkel geskryf: maan → mane, boom → bome, muur → mure.\n- **f word w:** druif → druiwe, wolf → wolwe.\n- **g val weg** en 'n deelteken wys die nuwe lettergreep: ploeg → ploeë.\n- **Deelteken** wanneer die meervoud-e by 'n klinker aansluit: knie → knieë, see → seë.\n\n### Verkleinwoorde\n\n| Uitgang | Wanneer | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **-ie** | na meeste ander konsonante (p, k, f, s, g) | boek → boekie, huis → huisie, kop → koppie |\n| **-jie** | na d en t | hand → handjie, kat → katjie, hoed → hoedjie |\n| **-tjie** | na 'n lang klinker of tweeklank, alleen of met l, n of r | knie → knietjie, stoel → stoeltjie, seun → seuntjie |\n| **-pie** | na m | boom → boompie, arm → armpie, besem → besempie |\n| **-kie** | na -ing (die g val weg) | koning → koninkie, woning → woninkie |\n| **-etjie** | na 'n kort, beklemtoonde klinker + l, m, n, ng of r | pen → pennetjie, bal → balletjie, ring → ringetjie |\n\n> **Wenk:** Sê die woord hardop. Jou oor help jou om die regte uitgang te kies.\n\n### Vroulike vorme\n\n| Manlik | Vroulik |\n|---|---|\n| leeu, held, boer | leeuin, heldin, boerin |\n| onderwyser, prins | onderwyseres, prinses |\n| skrywer, werker | skryfster, werkster |\n| oom, hings | tante, merrie (ander woord) |\n\n## Lidwoorde\n\n- **Bepaalde lidwoord:** *die* – 'n spesifieke een: *Die hond by ons hek blaf.*\n- **Onbepaalde lidwoord:** *'n* – enige een: *'n Hond blaf.*\n\n> **Onthou!** Aan die begin van 'n sin kry *'n* nooit 'n hoofletter nie; die volgende woord kry dit: *'n Hond blaf.*\n\n## Voornaamwoorde (vnw.)\n\n'n **Voornaamwoord** staan in die plek van 'n naamwoord, sodat jy dit nie hoef te herhaal nie.\n\n| Soort | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| **Persoonlike** | ek/my, jy/jou, u, hy/hom, sy/haar, dit, ons, julle, hulle |\n| **Besitlike** | my, jou, sy, haar, ons, julle, hul; selfstandig: myne, joune, syne, hare, ons s'n, hulle s'n |\n| **Wederkerende** | Ek was **my**. Hy skeer **hom(self)**. |\n| **Wederkerige** | Die spelers groet **mekaar**. |\n| **Betreklike** | wat, wie, waarvan, waarmee, waarop, wie se |\n| **Vraende** | wie, wat, watter (ook die vraagwoorde waar en hoekom begin vrae) |\n| **Aanwysende** | hierdie, daardie, dié |\n| **Onbepaalde** | iemand, niemand, iets, niks, almal, elkeen |\n\nGebruik die regte vorm ná 'n voorsetsel: *Gee dit vir **my*** (nie *vir ek* nie); *Ons wag vir **hulle***.\n\n### Betreklike voornaamwoorde: die reëls\n\n- **wat** vir mense en dinge: *die seun **wat** wen; die bus **wat** laat is*.\n- **voorsetsel + wie** vir mense: *die vriend **met wie** ek praat; die tannie **vir wie** ons gehelp het*.\n- **waar + voorsetsel** vir dinge: *die pen **waarmee** ek skryf; die bank **waarop** ek sit; die boek **waarvan** ek hou* (met → waar**mee**, tot → waar**toe**).\n- **wie se** vir besit: *die meisie **wie se** fiets gesteel is*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *die man wat se hond* ✗ → *die man **wie se** hond* ✓; *die mes met wat ek sny* ✗ → *die mes **waarmee** ek sny* ✓.\n\n## Byvoeglike naamwoorde (b.nw.)\n\n'n **Byvoeglike naamwoord** beskryf 'n selfstandige naamwoord.\n\n- **Attributief:** staan **voor** die s.nw.: *die **rooi** motor*.\n- **Predikatief:** staan **ná** 'n koppelwerkwoord (is, word, lyk, bly): *Die motor is **rooi**.*\n\n### Verbuiging\n\nBaie b.nw. verander (kry 'n **-e**) as hulle attributief gebruik word. Predikatief verbuig hulle nie.\n\n| Predikatief | Attributief |\n|---|---|\n| Die boek is goed. | 'n **goeie** boek |\n| Die skoen is nuut. | 'n **nuwe** skoen |\n| Die berg is hoog. | 'n **hoë** berg |\n| Die kussing is sag. | 'n **sagte** kussing |\n| Die grond is droog. | **droë** grond |\n| Die pad is lank. | 'n **lang** pad (geen -e nie) |\n| Die man is oud. | 'n **ou** man |\n\nWoorde soos *groot*, *klein* en *mooi* verbuig nie: *'n groot huis, 'n mooi dag*.\n\n### Trappe van vergelyking\n\n| Stellende trap | Vergrotende trap | Oortreffende trap |\n|---|---|---|\n| groot | groter | grootste |\n| goed | beter | beste |\n| veel | meer | meeste |\n| min | minder | minste |\n| hoog | hoër | hoogste |\n| lank | langer | langste |\n\n- Die vergrotende trap vergelyk **twee**: *Thabo is **langer as** Pieter.*\n- Die oortreffende trap vergelyk **drie of meer**: *Hy is die **langste** in die span.*\n- Lang woorde gebruik dikwels **meer** en **mees**: *meer interessant, mees interessant*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *meer beter* ✗, *die mees mooiste* ✗, *goeder* ✗. Gebruik net **een** manier van vergelyk: *beter*, *die mooiste*.\n\n## Die naamwoordstuk: kern en bepaler\n\n'n **Naamwoordstuk** is 'n groep woorde rondom 'n s.nw. Die s.nw. is die **kern**; die ander woorde is **bepalers** wat die kern beskryf of bepaal.\n\n*'n baie mooi rooi motor* → kern = **motor**; bepalers = 'n, baie, mooi, rooi.\n\n> **Wenk:** Kyk altyd na die **funksie** van 'n woord in die sin. *Sy* in “*Sy* lees” is 'n persoonlike vnw., maar in “*sy* boek” is dit 'n besitlike vnw.","en":"## Nouns (selfstandige naamwoorde, s.nw.)\n\nA **noun** is the name of a person, animal, place, thing, idea or feeling.\n\n| Kind | What it names | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Common noun (soortnaam)** | any member of a group | hond, skool, rivier |\n| **Proper noun (eienaam)** | a specific person or place; always a capital letter | Thabo, Brits, Magaliesberg |\n| **Collective noun (versamelnaam)** | a group as one whole | 'n kudde skape, 'n swerm bye, 'n trop leeus |\n| **Material noun (stofnaam)** | a substance or material | goud, water, sand |\n| **Abstract noun (abstrakte s.nw.)** | something you cannot see or touch | vreugde, liefde, vrees |\n| **Unit noun (maatnaam)** | a measure or unit | liter, kilogram, meter |\n\n### Plurals (meervoude)\n\n| Ending | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **-e** | huis → huise, boek → boeke |\n| **-s** | tafel → tafels, bakker → bakkers, oom → ooms, koning → konings |\n| **-ers / -ere** | kind → kinders, lam → lammers, goed → goedere |\n| **Irregular** | skip → skepe, stad → stede, lid → lede, dag → dae, oog → oë |\n\n**Spelling rules for plurals:**\n\n- **Short vowel:** double the final consonant: kat → katte, pen → penne, bus → busse.\n- **A long vowel in an open syllable** is written single: maan → mane, boom → bome, muur → mure.\n- **f becomes w:** druif → druiwe, wolf → wolwe.\n- **g falls away** and a diaeresis (deelteken) shows the new syllable: ploeg → ploeë.\n- **Diaeresis** when the plural -e joins a vowel: knie → knieë, see → seë.\n\n### Diminutives (verkleinwoorde)\n\n| Ending | When | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **-ie** | after most other consonants (p, k, f, s, g) | boek → boekie, huis → huisie, kop → koppie |\n| **-jie** | after d and t | hand → handjie, kat → katjie, hoed → hoedjie |\n| **-tjie** | after a long vowel or diphthong, alone or with l, n or r | knie → knietjie, stoel → stoeltjie, seun → seuntjie |\n| **-pie** | after m | boom → boompie, arm → armpie, besem → besempie |\n| **-kie** | after -ing (the g falls away) | koning → koninkie, woning → woninkie |\n| **-etjie** | after a short, stressed vowel + l, m, n, ng or r | pen → pennetjie, bal → balletjie, ring → ringetjie |\n\n> **Tip:** Say the word aloud. Your ear helps you choose the right ending.\n\n### Feminine forms (vroulike vorme)\n\n| Masculine | Feminine |\n|---|---|\n| leeu, held, boer | leeuin, heldin, boerin |\n| onderwyser, prins | onderwyseres, prinses |\n| skrywer, werker | skryfster, werkster |\n| oom, hings | tante, merrie (a different word) |\n\n## Articles (lidwoorde)\n\n- **Definite article (bepaalde lidwoord):** *die* (the) – a specific one: *Die hond by ons hek blaf.*\n- **Indefinite article (onbepaalde lidwoord):** *'n* (a/an) – any one: *'n Hond blaf.*\n\n> **Remember!** At the start of a sentence *'n* never gets a capital letter; the next word gets it: *'n Hond blaf.*\n\n## Pronouns (voornaamwoorde, vnw.)\n\nA **pronoun** stands in the place of a noun, so that you do not have to repeat it.\n\n| Kind | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| **Personal (persoonlike)** | ek/my, jy/jou, u, hy/hom, sy/haar, dit, ons, julle, hulle |\n| **Possessive (besitlike)** | my, jou, sy, haar, ons, julle, hul; standing alone: myne, joune, syne, hare, ons s'n, hulle s'n |\n| **Reflexive (wederkerende)** | Ek was **my**. Hy skeer **hom(self)**. |\n| **Reciprocal (wederkerige)** | Die spelers groet **mekaar** (each other). |\n| **Relative (betreklike)** | wat, wie, waarvan, waarmee, waarop, wie se |\n| **Interrogative (vraende)** | wie, wat, watter (the question words waar and hoekom also start questions) |\n| **Demonstrative (aanwysende)** | hierdie, daardie, dié |\n| **Indefinite (onbepaalde)** | iemand, niemand, iets, niks, almal, elkeen |\n\nUse the right form after a preposition: *Gee dit vir **my*** (not *vir ek*); *Ons wag vir **hulle***.\n\n### Relative pronouns: the rules\n\n- **wat** for people and things: *die seun **wat** wen; die bus **wat** laat is*.\n- **preposition + wie** for people: *die vriend **met wie** ek praat; die tannie **vir wie** ons gehelp het*.\n- **waar + preposition** for things: *die pen **waarmee** ek skryf; die bank **waarop** ek sit; die boek **waarvan** ek hou* (met → waar**mee**, tot → waar**toe**).\n- **wie se** for possession (whose): *die meisie **wie se** fiets gesteel is*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *die man wat se hond* ✗ → *die man **wie se** hond* ✓; *die mes met wat ek sny* ✗ → *die mes **waarmee** ek sny* ✓.\n\n## Adjectives (byvoeglike naamwoorde, b.nw.)\n\nAn **adjective** describes a noun.\n\n- **Attributive (attributief):** stands **before** the noun: *die **rooi** motor*.\n- **Predicative (predikatief):** stands **after** a linking verb (is, word, lyk, bly): *Die motor is **rooi**.*\n\n### Inflection (verbuiging)\n\nMany adjectives change (get an **-e**) when they are used attributively. Predicatively they do not inflect.\n\n| Predicative | Attributive |\n|---|---|\n| Die boek is goed. | 'n **goeie** boek |\n| Die skoen is nuut. | 'n **nuwe** skoen |\n| Die berg is hoog. | 'n **hoë** berg |\n| Die kussing is sag. | 'n **sagte** kussing |\n| Die grond is droog. | **droë** grond |\n| Die pad is lank. | 'n **lang** pad (no -e) |\n| Die man is oud. | 'n **ou** man |\n\nWords such as *groot*, *klein* and *mooi* do not inflect: *'n groot huis, 'n mooi dag*.\n\n### Degrees of comparison (trappe van vergelyking)\n\n| Positive (stellende) | Comparative (vergrotende) | Superlative (oortreffende) |\n|---|---|---|\n| groot | groter | grootste |\n| goed | beter | beste |\n| veel | meer | meeste |\n| min | minder | minste |\n| hoog | hoër | hoogste |\n| lank | langer | langste |\n\n- The comparative compares **two**: *Thabo is **langer as** Pieter.*\n- The superlative compares **three or more**: *Hy is die **langste** in die span.*\n- Long words often use **meer** and **mees**: *meer interessant, mees interessant*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *meer beter* ✗, *die mees mooiste* ✗, *goeder* ✗. Use only **one** way of comparing: *beter*, *die mooiste*.\n\n## The noun phrase: head and modifier (kern en bepaler)\n\nA **noun phrase (naamwoordstuk)** is a group of words built around a noun. The noun is the **head (kern)**; the other words are **modifiers (bepalers)** that describe or limit the head.\n\n*'n baie mooi rooi motor* → head = **motor**; modifiers = 'n, baie, mooi, rooi.\n\n> **Tip:** Always look at the **function** of a word in the sentence. *Sy* in “*Sy* lees” (She reads) is a personal pronoun, but in “*sy* boek” (his book) it is a possessive pronoun."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Soortnaam","en":"Common noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Gewone naam vir enige lid van 'n groep mense, diere of dinge, bv. hond, skool.","en":"An ordinary name for any member of a group of people, animals or things, e.g. hond (dog), skool (school)."}},{"term":{"af":"Eienaam","en":"Proper noun"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van 'n spesifieke persoon, plek of ding; dit kry altyd 'n hoofletter, bv. Brits.","en":"The name of a specific person, place or thing; it always gets a capital letter, e.g. Brits."}},{"term":{"af":"Versamelnaam","en":"Collective noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Naam vir 'n groep as een geheel, bv. 'n swerm bye, 'n kudde skape.","en":"A name for a group as one whole, e.g. 'n swerm bye (a swarm of bees), 'n kudde skape (a flock of sheep)."}},{"term":{"af":"Abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord","en":"Abstract noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Naam vir 'n gevoel, idee of toestand wat jy nie kan sien of aanraak nie, bv. vreugde, liefde.","en":"A name for a feeling, idea or state that you cannot see or touch, e.g. vreugde (joy), liefde (love)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verkleinwoord","en":"Diminutive"},"def":{"af":"'n Vorm wat iets kleiner of liefliker maak met 'n uitgang soos -ie, -jie, -tjie, -pie, -kie of -etjie.","en":"A form that makes something smaller or more endearing with an ending such as -ie, -jie, -tjie, -pie, -kie or -etjie."}},{"term":{"af":"Betreklike voornaamwoord","en":"Relative pronoun"},"def":{"af":"'n Voornaamwoord wat 'n bysin aan 'n naamwoord koppel: wat, wie, waarmee, waarvan, wie se.","en":"A pronoun that links a clause to a noun: wat, wie, waarmee, waarvan, wie se."}},{"term":{"af":"Attributief en predikatief","en":"Attributive and predicative"},"def":{"af":"Attributief staan die b.nw. voor die s.nw. ('n goeie boek); predikatief staan dit ná 'n koppelwerkwoord (Die boek is goed).","en":"Attributive: the adjective stands before the noun ('n goeie boek); predicative: it stands after a linking verb (Die boek is goed)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbuiging","en":"Inflection"},"def":{"af":"Die verandering (gewoonlik 'n -e) wat 'n b.nw. kry wanneer dit attributief gebruik word, bv. nuut → 'n nuwe skoen.","en":"The change (usually an -e) an adjective gets when it is used attributively, e.g. nuut → 'n nuwe skoen."}},{"term":{"af":"Trappe van vergelyking","en":"Degrees of comparison"},"def":{"af":"Die stellende, vergrotende en oortreffende trap van 'n b.nw., bv. groot – groter – grootste.","en":"The positive, comparative and superlative degree of an adjective, e.g. groot – groter – grootste."}},{"term":{"af":"Kern van die naamwoordstuk","en":"Head of the noun phrase"},"def":{"af":"Die selfstandige naamwoord waarom die naamwoordstuk gebou is; die ander woorde is bepalers.","en":"The noun around which the noun phrase is built; the other words are modifiers."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Woordsoorte in 'n advertensie","en":"Parts of speech in an advert"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die advertensie en identifiseer die woordsoort van elke woord wat gelys word. Wees spesifiek (bv. *besitlike voornaamwoord*, nie net *voornaamwoord* nie).\n\n*Advertensie:* “Ons nuwe sitrussap is die varsste in Madibeng! Proe self die goue lemoene van Brits – elke bottel is vol vreugde.”\n\n(a) Ons  (b) nuwe  (c) varsste  (d) goue  (e) Brits  (f) vreugde","en":"Read the advert and identify the part of speech of each word listed. Be specific (e.g. *possessive pronoun*, not just *pronoun*).\n\n*Advert:* “Ons nuwe sitrussap is die varsste in Madibeng! Proe self die goue lemoene van Brits – elke bottel is vol vreugde.” (Our new citrus juice is the freshest in Madibeng! Taste for yourself the golden oranges of Brits – every bottle is full of joy.)\n\n(a) Ons  (b) nuwe  (c) varsste  (d) goue  (e) Brits  (f) vreugde"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Ons** = besitlike voornaamwoord: dit wys aan wie die sap behoort (*ons* sap).","en":"(a) **Ons** = possessive pronoun: it shows whom the juice belongs to (*our* juice)."},{"af":"(b) **nuwe** = byvoeglike naamwoord, attributief en verbuig (nuut → nuwe), want dit staan voor *sitrussap*.","en":"(b) **nuwe** = adjective, attributive and inflected (nuut → nuwe), because it stands before *sitrussap*."},{"af":"(c) **varsste** = byvoeglike naamwoord in die oortreffende trap (vars → varser → varsste): die sap word met al die ander vergelyk.","en":"(c) **varsste** = adjective in the superlative degree (vars → varser → varsste): the juice is compared with all the others."},{"af":"(d) **goue** = byvoeglike naamwoord (afgelei van die stofnaam *goud*), attributief gebruik.","en":"(d) **goue** = adjective (derived from the material noun *goud*, gold), used attributively."},{"af":"(e) **Brits** = eienaam (selfstandige naamwoord) – die naam van 'n spesifieke dorp, met 'n hoofletter. (f) **vreugde** = abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord – 'n gevoel wat jy nie kan aanraak nie.","en":"(e) **Brits** = proper noun – the name of a specific town, with a capital letter. (f) **vreugde** (joy) = abstract noun – a feeling you cannot touch."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) besitlike vnw. (b) b.nw., attributief verbuig (c) b.nw., oortreffende trap (d) b.nw. (e) eienaam (f) abstrakte s.nw.","en":"(a) possessive pronoun (b) adjective, attributive and inflected (c) adjective, superlative (d) adjective (e) proper noun (f) abstract noun"}},{"title":{"af":"Meervoude en verkleinwoorde","en":"Plurals and diminutives"},"problem":{"af":"Gee die meervoud en die verkleinwoord van elke woord: stad, maan, bal, koning, boom, knie.","en":"Give the plural and the diminutive of each word: stad (city), maan (moon), bal (ball), koning (king), boom (tree), knie (knee)."},"steps":[{"af":"**stad** → *stede* (onreëlmatige meervoud) en *stadjie* (na d kom -jie).","en":"**stad** → *stede* (irregular plural) and *stadjie* (after d comes -jie)."},{"af":"**maan** → *mane* (lang klinker in die oop lettergreep ma-ne word enkel geskryf) en *maantjie* (lang klinker + n → -tjie).","en":"**maan** → *mane* (a long vowel in the open syllable ma-ne is written single) and *maantjie* (long vowel + n → -tjie)."},{"af":"**bal** → *balle* (kort klinker: verdubbel die l) en *balletjie* (kort, beklemtoonde klinker + l → -etjie).","en":"**bal** → *balle* (short vowel: double the l) and *balletjie* (short, stressed vowel + l → -etjie)."},{"af":"**koning** → *konings* (woorde op -ing kry -s) en *koninkie* (-ing word -inkie).","en":"**koning** → *konings* (words ending in -ing get -s) and *koninkie* (-ing becomes -inkie)."},{"af":"**boom** → *bome* (oo word enkel in bo-me) en *boompie* (na m kom -pie).","en":"**boom** → *bome* (oo becomes single in bo-me) and *boompie* (after m comes -pie)."},{"af":"**knie** → *knieë* (die deelteken wys dat -ë 'n nuwe lettergreep begin) en *knietjie* (lang klinker → -tjie).","en":"**knie** → *knieë* (the diaeresis shows that -ë starts a new syllable) and *knietjie* (long vowel → -tjie)."}],"answer":{"af":"stede/stadjie; mane/maantjie; balle/balletjie; konings/koninkie; bome/boompie; knieë/knietjie","en":"stede/stadjie; mane/maantjie; balle/balletjie; konings/koninkie; bome/boompie; knieë/knietjie"}},{"title":{"af":"Kies die regte betreklike voornaamwoord","en":"Choose the correct relative pronoun"},"problem":{"af":"Vul die regte betreklike voornaamwoord in.\n\n(a) Die onderwyser ___ ons almal bewonder, gaan aan die einde van die jaar aftree.\n(b) Die vriend met ___ ek na die rugby gaan, woon op Hartbeespoort.\n(c) Die pen ___ ek skryf, is amper leeg.\n(d) Die meisie ___ selfoon gesteel is, het die polisie gebel.\n(e) Die bankie ___ ons sit, is pas geverf.","en":"Fill in the correct relative pronoun.\n\n(a) Die onderwyser ___ ons almal bewonder, gaan aan die einde van die jaar aftree. (The teacher whom we all admire is retiring at the end of the year.)\n(b) Die vriend met ___ ek na die rugby gaan, woon op Hartbeespoort. (The friend with whom I go to the rugby lives in Hartbeespoort.)\n(c) Die pen ___ ek skryf, is amper leeg. (The pen with which I write is almost empty.)\n(d) Die meisie ___ selfoon gesteel is, het die polisie gebel. (The girl whose phone was stolen called the police.)\n(e) Die bankie ___ ons sit, is pas geverf. (The bench on which we sit has just been painted.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **wat** – daar is geen voorsetsel nie, so *wat* werk vir mense en dinge.","en":"(a) **wat** – there is no preposition, so *wat* works for people and things."},{"af":"(b) **wie** – ná die voorsetsel *met* gebruik jy *wie* vir 'n persoon: *met wie*.","en":"(b) **wie** – after the preposition *met* you use *wie* for a person: *met wie*."},{"af":"(c) **waarmee** – 'n pen is 'n ding, so voorsetsel *met* word *waar + mee*. *Met wat* is fout.","en":"(c) **waarmee** – a pen is a thing, so the preposition *met* becomes *waar + mee*. *Met wat* is wrong."},{"af":"(d) **wie se** – dit wys besit (die meisie se selfoon). *Wat se* is 'n algemene fout.","en":"(d) **wie se** – it shows possession (the girl's phone). *Wat se* is a common mistake."},{"af":"(e) **waarop** – ons sit *op* die bankie ('n ding), dus *waar + op*.","en":"(e) **waarop** – we sit *on* the bench (a thing), so *waar + op*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) wat (b) wie (c) waarmee (d) wie se (e) waarop","en":"(a) wat (b) wie (c) waarmee (d) wie se (e) waarop"}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter verbuiging en trappe van vergelyking","en":"Correct inflection and degrees of comparison"},"problem":{"af":"Daar is vier foute met byvoeglike naamwoorde in die teks. Herskryf die teks korrek.\n\n“Dit was 'n baie goed wedstryd op Loftus. Die Bulle se nuut losskakel is die meer beter speler van die twee, en hy het die hoog skop van die dag geskop.”","en":"There are four errors with adjectives in the text. Rewrite the text correctly.\n\n“Dit was 'n baie goed wedstryd op Loftus. Die Bulle se nuut losskakel is die meer beter speler van die twee, en hy het die hoog skop van die dag geskop.” (It was a very good match at Loftus. The Bulls' new flyhalf is the better player of the two, and he kicked the highest kick of the day.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*'n baie goed wedstryd* → **'n baie goeie wedstryd**: *goed* staan attributief voor *wedstryd* en moet verbuig.","en":"*'n baie goed wedstryd* → **'n baie goeie wedstryd**: *goed* stands attributively before *wedstryd* and must inflect."},{"af":"*nuut losskakel* → **nuwe losskakel**: attributief, dus nuut → nuwe.","en":"*nuut losskakel* → **nuwe losskakel**: attributive, so nuut → nuwe."},{"af":"*die meer beter speler* → **die beter speler**: *beter* is reeds die vergrotende trap; *meer* is dubbel. Die vergrotende trap is reg, want net twee spelers word vergelyk.","en":"*die meer beter speler* → **die beter speler**: *beter* is already the comparative; *meer* doubles it. The comparative is right, because only two players are compared."},{"af":"*die hoog skop van die dag* → **die hoogste skop van die dag**: al die skoppe van die dag word vergelyk, dus die oortreffende trap.","en":"*die hoog skop van die dag* → **die hoogste skop van die dag**: all the kicks of the day are compared, so the superlative."}],"answer":{"af":"“Dit was 'n baie goeie wedstryd op Loftus. Die Bulle se nuwe losskakel is die beter speler van die twee, en hy het die hoogste skop van die dag geskop.”","en":"“Dit was 'n baie goeie wedstryd op Loftus. Die Bulle se nuwe losskakel is die beter speler van die twee, en hy het die hoogste skop van die dag geskop.”"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter soort selfstandige naamwoord is “kudde” in “'n kudde skape”?","en":"What kind of noun is “kudde” in “'n kudde skape” (a flock of sheep)?"},"options":[{"af":"Stofnaam","en":"Material noun (stofnaam)"},{"af":"Versamelnaam","en":"Collective noun (versamelnaam)"},{"af":"Abstrakte s.nw.","en":"Abstract noun"},{"af":"Maatnaam","en":"Unit noun (maatnaam)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Kudde is 'n groep diere wat as een geheel benoem word, dus 'n versamelnaam – soos swerm en trop.","en":"A kudde is a group of animals named as one whole, so a collective noun – like swerm and trop."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die meervoud van “lid” is ___.","en":"The plural of “lid” (member) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["lede"],"en":["lede"]},"explain":{"af":"Lid → lede is onreëlmatig, net soos skip → skepe en stad → stede.","en":"Lid → lede is irregular, just like skip → skepe and stad → stede."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["lids","liede","ledes"],"en":["lids","liede","ledes"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die sin “'n Hond blaf by die hek.” kry “Hond” die hoofletter en nie “'n” nie.","en":"In the sentence “'n Hond blaf by die hek.” “Hond” gets the capital letter and not “'n”."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die onbepaalde lidwoord 'n kry nooit 'n hoofletter nie; die woord daarna kry dit.","en":"True. The indefinite article 'n never gets a capital letter; the word after it gets it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verkleinwoord van “boom” is ___.","en":"The diminutive of “boom” (tree) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["boompie"],"en":["boompie"]},"explain":{"af":"Na m kom -pie: boom → boompie, arm → armpie.","en":"After m comes -pie: boom → boompie, arm → armpie."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["boomtjie","bomie","boometjie"],"en":["boomtjie","bomie","boometjie"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is 'n abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord?","en":"Which word is an abstract noun?"},"options":[{"af":"goud","en":"goud (gold)"},{"af":"swerm","en":"swerm (swarm)"},{"af":"liter","en":"liter"},{"af":"vreugde","en":"vreugde (joy)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vreugde is 'n gevoel wat jy nie kan sien of aanraak nie. Goud is 'n stofnaam, swerm 'n versamelnaam en liter 'n maatnaam.","en":"Vreugde (joy) is a feeling you cannot see or touch. Goud is a material noun, swerm a collective noun and liter a unit noun."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke soort voornaamwoord by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each kind of pronoun to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Persoonlike vnw.","en":"Personal pronoun"},"r":{"af":"hulle","en":"hulle (they)"}},{"l":{"af":"Besitlike vnw. (selfstandig)","en":"Possessive pronoun (standing alone)"},"r":{"af":"syne","en":"syne (his)"}},{"l":{"af":"Wederkerige vnw.","en":"Reciprocal pronoun"},"r":{"af":"mekaar","en":"mekaar (each other)"}},{"l":{"af":"Aanwysende vnw.","en":"Demonstrative pronoun"},"r":{"af":"daardie","en":"daardie (that)"}},{"l":{"af":"Onbepaalde vnw.","en":"Indefinite pronoun"},"r":{"af":"niemand","en":"niemand (nobody)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hulle staan vir mense (persoonlik); syne wys besit; mekaar wys 'n wedersydse handeling; daardie wys iets aan; niemand verwys na geen spesifieke persoon nie.","en":"Hulle stands for people (personal); syne shows possession; mekaar shows a mutual action; daardie points something out; niemand refers to no specific person."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die vroulike vorm van “onderwyser” is ___.","en":"The feminine form of “onderwyser” (teacher) is ___."},"answers":{"af":["onderwyseres"],"en":["onderwyseres"]},"explain":{"af":"Onderwyser kry -es: onderwyseres, net soos prins → prinses. -in gebruik jy by leeu → leeuin en held → heldin.","en":"Onderwyser takes -es: onderwyseres, just like prins → prinses. You use -in for leeu → leeuin and held → heldin."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["onderwyserin","onderwyster","onderwyseresse"],"en":["onderwyserin","onderwyster","onderwyseresse"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die korrekte meervoud van “druif”.","en":"Choose the correct plural of “druif” (grape)."},"options":[{"af":"druiwe","en":"druiwe"},{"af":"druifs","en":"druifs"},{"af":"druife","en":"druife"},{"af":"druiwers","en":"druiwers"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By die meervoud word die f 'n w: druif → druiwe, wolf → wolwe.","en":"In the plural the f becomes a w: druif → druiwe, wolf → wolwe."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voltooi: “Die boek ___ ek gister gepraat het, is uitverkoop.”","en":"Complete: “Die boek ___ ek gister gepraat het, is uitverkoop.” (The book I talked about yesterday is sold out.)"},"options":[{"af":"wat","en":"wat"},{"af":"oor wat","en":"oor wat"},{"af":"waaroor","en":"waaroor"},{"af":"wie","en":"wie"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Jy praat *oor* 'n boek ('n ding), dus waar + oor = waaroor. *Oor wat* is foutief, en *wie* is net vir mense.","en":"You talk *oor* (about) a book (a thing), so waar + oor = waaroor. *Oor wat* is incorrect, and *wie* is only for people."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die korrekte betreklike voornaamwoord: “Die seun ___ fiets gesteel is, het die polisie gebel.”","en":"Complete with the correct relative pronoun: “Die seun ___ fiets gesteel is, het die polisie gebel.” (The boy whose bicycle was stolen called the police.)"},"answers":{"af":["wie se"],"en":["wie se"]},"explain":{"af":"Besit by 'n persoon = wie se. *Wat se* is 'n baie algemene fout.","en":"Possession with a person = wie se (whose). *Wat se* is a very common mistake."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["wat se","wie","waarvan"],"en":["wat se","wie","waarvan"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die sin “Die motor is rooi.” word “rooi” attributief gebruik.","en":"In the sentence “Die motor is rooi.” (The car is red.) “rooi” is used attributively."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. “Rooi” staan ná die koppelwerkwoord “is”, dus predikatief. Attributief sou wees: “die rooi motor”.","en":"False. “Rooi” stands after the linking verb “is”, so it is predicative. Attributive would be: “die rooi motor”."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat die korrekte vorm van die byvoeglike naamwoord?","en":"Which sentence contains the correct form of the adjective?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy het 'n goed punt gekry.","en":"Sy het 'n goed punt gekry."},{"af":"Hy dra 'n nuwe baadjie.","en":"Hy dra 'n nuwe baadjie."},{"af":"Ons het 'n lank pad gery.","en":"Ons het 'n lank pad gery."},{"af":"Die droog grond kraak.","en":"Die droog grond kraak."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Attributief moet hulle verbuig: 'n goeie punt, 'n nuwe baadjie, 'n lang pad, die droë grond. Net *nuwe* is korrek.","en":"Attributively they must inflect: 'n goeie punt, 'n nuwe baadjie, 'n lang pad, die droë grond. Only *nuwe* is correct."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die oortreffende trap van “goed”: “Sy is die ___ leerder in die klas.”","en":"Give the superlative of “goed” (good): “Sy is die ___ leerder in die klas.” (She is the best learner in the class.)"},"answers":{"af":["beste"],"en":["beste"]},"explain":{"af":"Goed is onreëlmatig: goed – beter – beste. *Beter* is die vergrotende trap en vergelyk net twee.","en":"Goed is irregular: goed – beter – beste. *Beter* is the comparative and compares only two."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["goedste","beter","mees goeie"],"en":["goedste","beter","mees goeie"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die woord in HOOFLETTERS 'n besitlike voornaamwoord?","en":"In which sentence is the word in CAPITALS a possessive pronoun?"},"options":[{"af":"SY speel netbal vir die skool.","en":"SY speel netbal vir die skool. (She plays netball for the school.)"},{"af":"Ek het HAAR gister by die winkel gesien.","en":"Ek het HAAR gister by die winkel gesien. (I saw her at the shop yesterday.)"},{"af":"Hulle help MEKAAR met wiskunde.","en":"Hulle help MEKAAR met wiskunde. (They help each other with maths.)"},{"af":"Thabo het SY fiets by die hek gelos.","en":"Thabo het SY fiets by die hek gelos. (Thabo left his bicycle at the gate.)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In “SY fiets” wys sy besit (Thabo se fiets). In die eerste sin is Sy die onderwerp (persoonlik), HAAR is 'n persoonlike vnw. as voorwerp, en MEKAAR is wederkerig.","en":"In “SY fiets” (his bicycle) sy shows possession. In the first sentence Sy is the subject (personal), HAAR is a personal pronoun as object, and MEKAAR is reciprocal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die kern van die naamwoordstuk “die drie baie moeë rugbyspelers van Brits”?","en":"What is the head of the noun phrase “die drie baie moeë rugbyspelers van Brits” (the three very tired rugby players from Brits)?"},"options":[{"af":"drie","en":"drie"},{"af":"moeë","en":"moeë"},{"af":"rugbyspelers","en":"rugbyspelers"},{"af":"Brits","en":"Brits"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die kern is die selfstandige naamwoord waaroor dit gaan: rugbyspelers. Die, drie, baie, moeë en van Brits is almal bepalers wat die spelers beskryf.","en":"The head is the noun the phrase is about: rugbyspelers. Die, drie, baie, moeë and van Brits are all modifiers that describe the players."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat GEEN fout nie?","en":"Which sentence contains NO error?"},"options":[{"af":"Die twee vriende het mekaar voor die toets gehelp en is nou die gelukkigste leerders in die klas.","en":"Die twee vriende het mekaar voor die toets gehelp en is nou die gelukkigste leerders in die klas."},{"af":"Die man wat se hond so blaf, is ons buurman.","en":"Die man wat se hond so blaf, is ons buurman."},{"af":"Hierdie berg is meer hoër as daardie een.","en":"Hierdie berg is meer hoër as daardie een."},{"af":"Die pen met wat ek skryf, is myne.","en":"Die pen met wat ek skryf, is myne."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin is korrek. Die ander moet wees: “wie se hond”, “hoër” (sonder meer) en “waarmee ek skryf”.","en":"The first sentence is correct. The others must be: “wie se hond”, “hoër” (without meer) and “waarmee ek skryf”."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t1-poesie","title":{"af":"Poësie: terme en die ontleding van 'n gedig","en":"Poetry: terms and analysing a poem"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die belangrikste poësieterme kan toepas en 'n ongesiene gedig stap vir stap kan ontleed en kontekstuele vrae daaroor kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to apply the most important poetry terms and analyse an unseen poem step by step, answering contextual questions on it."},"summary":{"af":"## Poësie in Vraestel 2\n\nIn Vraestel 2 (Letterkunde) beantwoord jy **kontekstuele vrae** (1–3 punte elk) oor voorgeskrewe gedigte en 'n **ongesiene gedig**, en soms 'n **paragraaf- of opstelvraag** oor hoe die digter die tema uitbeeld. 'n Term alleen is net een punt; die **funksie** of **effek** verdien die res.\n\n## Wie praat met wie?\n\n- **Digter:** die persoon wat die gedig geskryf het.\n- **Spreker:** die stem (“ek”) in die gedig – nie noodwendig die digter nie.\n- **Aangesprokene:** die persoon of ding met wie die spreker praat (dikwels “jy”).\n- **Titel:** noem die onderwerp, skep verwagting, gee 'n leidraad tot die tema of is soms ironies.\n\n## Onderwerp, tema, toon en stemming\n\n- **Onderwerp:** waaroor die gedig gaan (bv. 'n oupa se boord).\n- **Tema:** die dieper boodskap of insig (bv. 'n erfenis leef voort in die volgende geslag).\n- **Toon:** die spreker se **houding** teenoor die onderwerp: ironies, nostalgies, bitter, spottend, liefdevol, berustend.\n- **Stemming/atmosfeer:** die **gevoel** wat die gedig by die leser skep: somber, rustig, dreigend.\n\n## Vorm en bou\n\n| Strofe | Reëls |\n|---|---|\n| Koeplet | 2 |\n| Tersine | 3 |\n| Kwatryn | 4 |\n| Kwintet | 5 |\n| Sekstet | 6 |\n| Septet | 7 |\n| Oktaaf | 8 |\n\n- **Versreël:** een reël van 'n gedig. **Strofe:** 'n groep versreëls.\n- **Enjambement:** die sin loop sonder 'n leesteken oor na die volgende reël. Dit skep vloei of spoed, of plaas klem op die eerste woord van die volgende reël.\n- **Vrye verse:** geen vaste rym, ritme of strofebou nie.\n- **Sonnet** (14 reëls):\n  - **Petrarca-sonnet:** oktaaf + sekstet; die **volta/wending** kom tussen reël 8 en 9.\n  - **Shakespeare-sonnet:** drie kwatryne + 'n koeplet; die wending kom in die koeplet.\n- **Ballade:** 'n verhalende gedig, dikwels met 'n **refrein** ('n herhaalde reël of strofe).\n\n## Rym en klank\n\n- **Eindrym:** die laaste woorde van versreëls rym. **Binnerym:** woorde binne een reël rym.\n- **Halfrym:** net die klinkers (*maan – kaal*) of net die konsonante (*hand – hond*) stem ooreen.\n- **Rymskema:** paarrym (aabb), kruisrym (abab), omarmende rym (abba). Gee elke nuwe rymklank 'n nuwe letter.\n- **Alliterasie:** herhaling van **konsonante**, veral aan die begin van woorde: *wilde wind waai*.\n- **Assonansie:** herhaling van **klinkers**: *die maan kom saam met die aand*.\n- **Onomatopee/klanknabootsing:** woorde wat 'n klank naboots: *kraak, sis, woef*.\n- **Ritme, herhaling en refrein:** lê klem en skep musikaliteit.\n\n## Beeldspraak en stylfigure\n\n| Stylfiguur | Wat dit is | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Vergelyking** | vergelyk met *soos* of *as* | Sy hardloop soos die wind. |\n| **Metafoor** | sê iets *is* iets anders | Die dam is 'n spieël. |\n| **Personifikasie** | iets nie-menslik kry menslike eienskappe | Die berg slaap onder die wolke. |\n| **Hiperbool** | doelbewuste oordrywing | Ek het jou 'n miljoen keer gebel. |\n| **Antitese/kontras** | teenoorgesteldes naas mekaar | Gister 'n held, vandag 'n nul. |\n| **Paradoks** | skynbaar teenstrydig, tog waar | Hoe meer ek leer, hoe minder weet ek. |\n| **Oksimoron** | twee teenoorgestelde woorde direk saam | 'n oorverdowende stilte |\n| **Ironie** | die teenoorgestelde van wat gesê of verwag word | “Pragtig!” as jou fiets breek |\n| **Simbool** | iets konkreets staan vir iets abstraks | 'n duif = vrede |\n| **Retoriese vraag** | vraag sonder verwagte antwoord | Wie sal ons dan help? |\n| **Eufemisme** | versagting van iets onaangenaams | Oupa het ontslaap. |\n| **Enumerasie** | opnoeming | brood, kerse, batterye |\n| **Klimaks / antiklimaks** | opbou na 'n hoogtepunt / skielike val ná die opbou | Hy loop, hardloop, vlieg! |\n\n> **Wenk:** Verduidelik 'n stylfiguur in drie stappe: (1) **benoem** dit, (2) sê **wat met wat** vergelyk word, (3) sê **waarom dit effektief is** – watter beeld of gevoel dit skep.\n\n## Tipografie\n\nTipografie is hoe die gedig op die bladsy lyk: **kursief** en **hoofletters** (klem), **inspringing**, **witruimte** (stilte, eensaamheid, 'n pouse), die **beletselteken** (... iets bly onvoltooid of 'n gedagte raak weg), die **aandagstreep** (– 'n pouse voor 'n verrassing of verduideliking) en die **dubbelpunt** (: 'n verduideliking of opsomming volg). 'n Woord alleen op 'n reël val op.\n\n## Stappe vir 'n ongesiene gedig\n\n1. Lees die **titel** en voorspel.\n2. Lees die gedig twee keer vir die **inhoud**.\n3. Bepaal **wie** praat, met **wie**, oor **wat**.\n4. Formuleer die **tema** in een sin.\n5. Soek die **beeldspraak**: wat word met wat vergelyk, en waarom is dit effektief?\n6. Kyk na **klank en vorm**: rym, alliterasie, enjambement, tipografie.\n7. Bepaal die **toon** en haal 'n woord aan as bewys.\n8. Soek die **wending**: waar verander die gedagte of gevoel, en hoe eindig die gedig?\n\n## Tipiese eksamenvrae\n\n- *Benoem die stylfiguur in r. 3 en verduidelik die funksie daarvan.* (2–3)\n- *Wat is die rymskema van strofe 2?* (1)\n- *Waarom gebruik die digter enjambement in r. 5–6?* (2)\n- *Haal 'n woord aan wat die toon aandui.* (1)\n- *Verduidelik die wending.* (2)\n- **Paragraafvraag** (6–10 punte): *Bespreek hoe die digter die tema uitbeeld.* Skryf een samehangende paragraaf: 'n inleidende sin met jou standpunt, drie of vier bewyse uit die gedig (met aanhalings en verduideliking) en 'n slotsin.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Jy verwar **toon** (die spreker se houding) met **stemming** (die leser se gevoel), of jy benoem 'n stylfiguur sonder om die effek te verduidelik.","en":"## Poetry in Paper 2\n\nIn Paper 2 (Literature) you answer **contextual questions** (1–3 marks each) on prescribed poems and an **unseen poem (ongesiene gedig)**, and sometimes a **paragraph or essay question** on how the poet portrays the theme. A term alone earns only one mark; the **function** or **effect** earns the rest.\n\n## Who speaks to whom?\n\n- **Poet (digter):** the person who wrote the poem.\n- **Speaker (spreker):** the voice (“I”) in the poem – not necessarily the poet.\n- **Person addressed (aangesprokene):** the person or thing the speaker talks to (often “you”).\n- **Title:** names the subject, creates expectation, gives a clue to the theme or is sometimes ironic.\n\n## Subject, theme, tone and mood\n\n- **Subject (onderwerp):** what the poem is about (e.g. a grandfather's orchard).\n- **Theme (tema):** the deeper message or insight (e.g. a heritage lives on in the next generation).\n- **Tone (toon):** the speaker's **attitude** towards the subject: ironic, nostalgic, bitter, mocking, loving, resigned.\n- **Mood/atmosphere (stemming/atmosfeer):** the **feeling** the poem creates in the reader: gloomy, peaceful, threatening.\n\n## Form and structure\n\n| Stanza | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| Couplet (koeplet) | 2 |\n| Tercet (tersine) | 3 |\n| Quatrain (kwatryn) | 4 |\n| Quintet (kwintet) | 5 |\n| Sestet (sekstet) | 6 |\n| Septet (septet) | 7 |\n| Octave (oktaaf) | 8 |\n\n- **Line (versreël):** one line of a poem. **Stanza (strofe):** a group of lines.\n- **Enjambment (enjambement):** the sentence runs on into the next line without punctuation. It creates flow or speed, or places emphasis on the first word of the next line.\n- **Free verse (vrye verse):** no fixed rhyme, rhythm or stanza pattern.\n- **Sonnet** (14 lines):\n  - **Petrarchan sonnet:** octave + sestet; the **volta/turn (wending)** comes between lines 8 and 9.\n  - **Shakespearean sonnet:** three quatrains + a couplet; the turn comes in the couplet.\n- **Ballad (ballade):** a narrative poem, often with a **refrain (refrein)** – a repeated line or stanza.\n\n## Rhyme and sound\n\n- **End rhyme (eindrym):** the last words of lines rhyme. **Internal rhyme (binnerym):** words within one line rhyme.\n- **Half-rhyme (halfrym):** only the vowels (*maan – kaal*) or only the consonants (*hand – hond*) match.\n- **Rhyme scheme (rymskema):** rhyming couplets/paarrym (aabb), alternate rhyme/kruisrym (abab), enclosed rhyme/omarmende rym (abba). Give every new rhyme sound a new letter.\n- **Alliteration (alliterasie):** repetition of **consonants**, especially at the start of words: *wilde wind waai*.\n- **Assonance (assonansie):** repetition of **vowels**: *die maan kom saam met die aand*.\n- **Onomatopoeia (onomatopee/klanknabootsing):** words that imitate a sound: *kraak, sis, woef*.\n- **Rhythm, repetition and refrain:** add emphasis and musicality.\n\n## Imagery and figures of speech (beeldspraak en stylfigure)\n\n| Figure of speech | What it is | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Simile (vergelyking)** | compares using *soos* or *as* (like/as) | Sy hardloop soos die wind. |\n| **Metaphor (metafoor)** | says something *is* something else | Die dam is 'n spieël. |\n| **Personification (personifikasie)** | something non-human gets human qualities | Die berg slaap onder die wolke. |\n| **Hyperbole (hiperbool)** | deliberate exaggeration | Ek het jou 'n miljoen keer gebel. |\n| **Antithesis/contrast (antitese)** | opposites side by side | Gister 'n held, vandag 'n nul. |\n| **Paradox (paradoks)** | seemingly contradictory, yet true | Hoe meer ek leer, hoe minder weet ek. |\n| **Oxymoron (oksimoron)** | two opposite words directly together | 'n oorverdowende stilte (a deafening silence) |\n| **Irony (ironie)** | the opposite of what is said or expected | “Pragtig!” when your bike breaks |\n| **Symbol (simbool)** | something concrete stands for something abstract | a dove = peace |\n| **Rhetorical question (retoriese vraag)** | a question with no expected answer | Wie sal ons dan help? |\n| **Euphemism (eufemisme)** | softening of something unpleasant | Oupa het ontslaap (passed away). |\n| **Enumeration (enumerasie)** | listing | brood, kerse, batterye |\n| **Climax / anticlimax** | build-up to a high point / sudden drop after the build-up | Hy loop, hardloop, vlieg! |\n\n> **Tip:** Explain a figure of speech in three steps: (1) **name** it, (2) say **what is compared with what**, (3) say **why it is effective** – which image or feeling it creates.\n\n## Typography (tipografie)\n\nTypography is how the poem looks on the page: **italics** and **capitals** (emphasis), **indentation**, **white space** (silence, loneliness, a pause), the **ellipsis** (... something stays unfinished or a thought fades), the **dash** (– a pause before a surprise or explanation) and the **colon** (: an explanation or summary follows). A word alone on a line stands out.\n\n## Steps for an unseen poem\n\n1. Read the **title** and predict.\n2. Read the poem twice for the **content**.\n3. Work out **who** speaks, to **whom**, about **what**.\n4. Formulate the **theme** in one sentence.\n5. Look for the **imagery**: what is compared with what, and why is it effective?\n6. Look at **sound and form**: rhyme, alliteration, enjambment, typography.\n7. Decide on the **tone** and quote a word as proof.\n8. Look for the **turn**: where does the thought or feeling change, and how does the poem end?\n\n## Typical exam questions\n\n- *Name the figure of speech in l. 3 and explain its function.* (2–3)\n- *What is the rhyme scheme of stanza 2?* (1)\n- *Why does the poet use enjambment in l. 5–6?* (2)\n- *Quote a word that indicates the tone.* (1)\n- *Explain the turn.* (2)\n- **Paragraph question** (6–10 marks): *Discuss how the poet portrays the theme.* Write one coherent paragraph: an opening sentence with your standpoint, three or four pieces of evidence from the poem (with quotations and explanation) and a closing sentence.\n\n> **Common mistake:** You confuse **tone** (the speaker's attitude) with **mood** (the reader's feeling), or you name a figure of speech without explaining its effect."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Spreker","en":"Speaker"},"def":{"af":"Die stem of “ek” wat in die gedig praat; nie noodwendig die digter self nie.","en":"The voice or “I” that speaks in the poem; not necessarily the poet himself or herself."}},{"term":{"af":"Tema","en":"Theme"},"def":{"af":"Die dieper boodskap of insig van die gedig, anders as die onderwerp (waaroor dit gaan).","en":"The deeper message or insight of the poem, as opposed to the subject (what it is about)."}},{"term":{"af":"Toon","en":"Tone"},"def":{"af":"Die spreker se houding teenoor die onderwerp, bv. ironies, nostalgies of bitter.","en":"The speaker's attitude towards the subject, e.g. ironic, nostalgic or bitter."}},{"term":{"af":"Stemming","en":"Mood"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoel of atmosfeer wat die gedig by die leser skep, bv. somber of rustig.","en":"The feeling or atmosphere the poem creates in the reader, e.g. gloomy or peaceful."}},{"term":{"af":"Enjambement","en":"Enjambment"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n sin sonder 'n leesteken van een versreël na die volgende oorloop.","en":"When a sentence runs on from one line to the next without a punctuation mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Rymskema","en":"Rhyme scheme"},"def":{"af":"Die patroon van eindrym, aangedui met letters, bv. abab (kruisrym) of abba (omarmende rym).","en":"The pattern of end rhyme, shown with letters, e.g. abab (alternate rhyme) or abba (enclosed rhyme)."}},{"term":{"af":"Alliterasie","en":"Alliteration"},"def":{"af":"Die herhaling van dieselfde konsonantklank, veral aan die begin van woorde.","en":"The repetition of the same consonant sound, especially at the start of words."}},{"term":{"af":"Assonansie","en":"Assonance"},"def":{"af":"Die herhaling van dieselfde klinkerklank in woorde naby mekaar.","en":"The repetition of the same vowel sound in words close to each other."}},{"term":{"af":"Personifikasie","en":"Personification"},"def":{"af":"'n Stylfiguur waarin iets nie-menslik menslike eienskappe of handelinge kry.","en":"A figure of speech in which something non-human is given human qualities or actions."}},{"term":{"af":"Volta (wending)","en":"Volta (turn)"},"def":{"af":"Die punt in 'n gedig, veral 'n sonnet, waar die gedagte of gevoel verander; in 'n Petrarca-sonnet tussen r. 8 en 9.","en":"The point in a poem, especially a sonnet, where the thought or feeling changes; in a Petrarchan sonnet between l. 8 and 9."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ongesiene gedig 1: beeldspraak, tipografie en enjambement","en":"Unseen poem 1: imagery, typography and enjambment"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die gedig en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Beurtkrag**\n\n1 Om sesuur\n2 sluk die donker\n3 ons hele straat in een hap.\n\n4 Die yskas hou sy asem op,\n5 die Wi-Fi-liggie knip een keer\n6 en sterf.\n7 My foon staar na my met 'n rooi oog:\n8 twee persent.\n\n9 Ma trek 'n vuurhoutjie.\n10 Ons gesigte word klein en goud,\n11 en vir 'n oomblik\n12 is die stilte\n13 ons s'n.\n\n**Vrae**\n\n1.1 Wat is die onderwerp van die gedig? (1)\n1.2 Benoem die stylfiguur in r. 2–3 en verduidelik die effek daarvan. (2)\n1.3 Waarom staan “twee persent.” alleen op 'n reël? (2)\n1.4 Haal die reëls aan waar enjambement in strofe 3 voorkom, en sê wat die effek is. (2)\n1.5 Hoe verander die toon van strofe 1–2 na strofe 3? (2)\n1.6 Formuleer die tema van die gedig in een sin. (2)","en":"Read the poem (in Afrikaans) and answer the questions.\n\n**Beurtkrag**\n\n1 Om sesuur\n2 sluk die donker\n3 ons hele straat in een hap.\n\n4 Die yskas hou sy asem op,\n5 die Wi-Fi-liggie knip een keer\n6 en sterf.\n7 My foon staar na my met 'n rooi oog:\n8 twee persent.\n\n9 Ma trek 'n vuurhoutjie.\n10 Ons gesigte word klein en goud,\n11 en vir 'n oomblik\n12 is die stilte\n13 ons s'n.\n\n(Translation for understanding: At six o'clock / the dark swallows / our whole street in one bite. // The fridge holds its breath, / the Wi-Fi light blinks once / and dies. / My phone stares at me with a red eye: / two percent. // Mom strikes a match. / Our faces become small and golden, / and for a moment / the silence / is ours.)\n\n**Questions**\n\n1.1 What is the subject of the poem? (1)\n1.2 Name the figure of speech in l. 2–3 and explain its effect. (2)\n1.3 Why does “twee persent.” stand alone on a line? (2)\n1.4 Quote the lines in stanza 3 where enjambment occurs, and say what the effect is. (2)\n1.5 How does the tone change from stanzas 1–2 to stanza 3? (2)\n1.6 Formulate the theme of the poem in one sentence. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**1.1** (1) 'n Aand van beurtkrag by 'n gesin se huis ✔.","en":"**1.1** (1) An evening of load-shedding at a family's home ✔."},{"af":"**1.2** (2) Personifikasie ✔ (metafoor word ook aanvaar): die donker *sluk* die straat soos 'n honger wese. Dit wys hoe skielik en volledig die ligte doodgaan ✔.","en":"**1.2** (2) Personification ✔ (metaphor is also accepted): the dark *swallows* the street like a hungry creature. It shows how suddenly and completely the lights go out ✔."},{"af":"**1.3** (2) Die witruimte rondom die woorde gee klem op die pap battery ✔ en skep spanning: die spreker se laaste kontak met die buitewêreld gaan nou ook verlore ✔.","en":"**1.3** (2) The white space around the words emphasises the flat battery ✔ and creates tension: the speaker's last contact with the outside world is now also being lost ✔."},{"af":"**1.4** (2) “en vir 'n oomblik / is die stilte / ons s'n” ✔. Die sin word reël vir reël stadig oopgevou, sodat die leser saam met die gesin stadiger word en die rustige oomblik beleef ✔.","en":"**1.4** (2) “en vir 'n oomblik / is die stilte / ons s'n” ✔. The sentence unfolds slowly, line by line, so that the reader slows down with the family and experiences the peaceful moment ✔."},{"af":"**1.5** (2) In strofe 1–2 is die toon gefrustreerd en effens dreigend (*sluk*, *sterf*, *staar*) ✔; in strofe 3 word dit rustig en teer (*goud*, *stilte*, *ons s'n*) ✔.","en":"**1.5** (2) In stanzas 1–2 the tone is frustrated and slightly threatening (*sluk*, *sterf*, *staar*) ✔; in stanza 3 it becomes peaceful and tender (*goud*, *stilte*, *ons s'n*) ✔."},{"af":"**1.6** (2) Selfs in 'n moeilike situasie soos beurtkrag ✔ kan 'n gesin nabyheid en vrede by mekaar vind ✔. *'n Tema is 'n insig, nie net die onderwerp nie.*","en":"**1.6** (2) Even in a difficult situation like load-shedding ✔ a family can find closeness and peace with each other ✔. *A theme is an insight, not just the subject.*"}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 11 punte. Elke stylfiguurvraag: benoem + verduidelik die effek.","en":"Total: 11 marks. Every figure-of-speech question: name it + explain the effect."}},{"title":{"af":"Ongesiene gedig 2: rymskema, vergelyking en kontras","en":"Unseen poem 2: rhyme scheme, simile and contrast"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die gedig en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Harties in die oggend**\n\n1 Die dam lê stil soos blink glas,\n2 die mis kruip sag oor riet en wal,\n3 'n visarend roep hoog bo die gras,\n4 en dou begin van elke blaar te val.\n\n5 Toe kom die bote met lawaai;\n6 die stilte breek soos porselein.\n7 Die skoonheid was te broos, te klein,\n8 en met die wind is dit weggewaai.\n\n**Vrae**\n\n2.1 Gee die rymskema van strofe 1 en strofe 2 en benoem elkeen. (2)\n2.2 Benoem die stylfiguur in r. 1 en verduidelik wat dit oor die dam sê. (2)\n2.3 Watter stylfiguur kom in “die mis kruip sag” (r. 2) voor? Verduidelik. (2)\n2.4 Verduidelik die kontras tussen die twee strofes. (2)\n2.5 Wat is die toon van r. 7–8? Haal 'n woord aan as bewys. (2)","en":"Read the poem (in Afrikaans) and answer the questions.\n\n**Harties in die oggend**\n\n1 Die dam lê stil soos blink glas,\n2 die mis kruip sag oor riet en wal,\n3 'n visarend roep hoog bo die gras,\n4 en dou begin van elke blaar te val.\n\n5 Toe kom die bote met lawaai;\n6 die stilte breek soos porselein.\n7 Die skoonheid was te broos, te klein,\n8 en met die wind is dit weggewaai.\n\n(Translation for understanding: The dam lies still like shiny glass, / the mist creeps softly over reed and bank, / a fish eagle calls high above the grass, / and dew begins to fall from every leaf. // Then the boats come with noise; / the silence breaks like porcelain. / The beauty was too fragile, too small, / and with the wind it was blown away.)\n\n**Questions**\n\n2.1 Give the rhyme scheme of stanza 1 and stanza 2 and name each. (2)\n2.2 Name the figure of speech in l. 1 and explain what it says about the dam. (2)\n2.3 Which figure of speech occurs in “die mis kruip sag” (l. 2)? Explain. (2)\n2.4 Explain the contrast between the two stanzas. (2)\n2.5 What is the tone of l. 7–8? Quote a word as proof. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**2.1** (2) Strofe 1: glas – wal – gras – val = **abab, kruisrym** ✔. Strofe 2: lawaai – porselein – klein – weggewaai = **cddc, omarmende rym** ✔. *Nuwe rymklanke kry nuwe letters.*","en":"**2.1** (2) Stanza 1: glas – wal – gras – val = **abab, alternate rhyme (kruisrym)** ✔. Stanza 2: lawaai – porselein – klein – weggewaai = **cddc, enclosed rhyme (omarmende rym)** ✔. *New rhyme sounds get new letters.*"},{"af":"**2.2** (2) Vergelyking (*soos*) ✔. Die water is so glad en stil dat dit soos glas blink; dit beklemtoon die volkome rus van die oggend ✔.","en":"**2.2** (2) Simile (*soos*) ✔. The water is so smooth and still that it shines like glass; it emphasises the complete calm of the morning ✔."},{"af":"**2.3** (2) Personifikasie ✔: die mis *kruip* soos 'n lewende wese – stadig, stil en versigtig – wat die rustige, geheimsinnige atmosfeer versterk ✔.","en":"**2.3** (2) Personification ✔: the mist *creeps* like a living being – slowly, quietly and carefully – which strengthens the peaceful, mysterious atmosphere ✔."},{"af":"**2.4** (2) Strofe 1 beskryf die stilte en skoonheid van die natuur ✔; in strofe 2 vernietig die lawaai van die bote dié stilte ✔. Die kontras wys hoe broos die natuur se rus is.","en":"**2.4** (2) Stanza 1 describes the silence and beauty of nature ✔; in stanza 2 the noise of the boats destroys that silence ✔. The contrast shows how fragile nature's peace is."},{"af":"**2.5** (2) Weemoedig/teleurgesteld ✔: “broos” (of “weggewaai”) ✔.","en":"**2.5** (2) Wistful/disappointed ✔: “broos” (fragile) (or “weggewaai”, blown away) ✔."}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 10 punte.","en":"Total: 10 marks."}},{"title":{"af":"Die Petrarca-sonnet en die wending","en":"The Petrarchan sonnet and the turn"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die sonnet en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Oupa se boord**\n\n1 Voor dagbreek, as die son nog skuil agter die rand,\n2 het Oupa deur sy boord gestap soos in 'n droom;\n3 hy het gesels met elke stam, met elke boom,\n4 asof die bome kinders was van sy eie land.\n5 Hy het die grond geken soos die palm van sy hand,\n6 die water deur die slote stadig laat stroom,\n7 en elke winter was sy oes die room,\n8 die trots van Brits se warm, vrugbare sand.\n9 Maar nou sit Oupa by die venster, stil en oud;\n10 sy hande bewe as hy na sy koppie gryp.\n11 Die boord is nou my werk, my erfenis, my plig.\n12 Ek stap voor dagbreek uit; die oggend is nog koud,\n13 en waar ek loop, voel ek hoe die lemoene ryp,\n14 en elke boom dra Oupa se glimlag, sy gesig.\n\n**Vrae**\n\n3.1 Watter soort sonnet is dit? Motiveer jou antwoord. (2)\n3.2 Verduidelik die wending in r. 9. (2)\n3.3 Benoem die stylfiguur in r. 7 en verduidelik dit. (2)\n3.4 Wat is die effek van die opnoeming in r. 11? (2)\n3.5 Verduidelik die beeld in r. 14 en sê hoe dit by die tema aansluit. (2)","en":"Read the sonnet (in Afrikaans) and answer the questions.\n\n**Oupa se boord**\n\n1 Voor dagbreek, as die son nog skuil agter die rand,\n2 het Oupa deur sy boord gestap soos in 'n droom;\n3 hy het gesels met elke stam, met elke boom,\n4 asof die bome kinders was van sy eie land.\n5 Hy het die grond geken soos die palm van sy hand,\n6 die water deur die slote stadig laat stroom,\n7 en elke winter was sy oes die room,\n8 die trots van Brits se warm, vrugbare sand.\n9 Maar nou sit Oupa by die venster, stil en oud;\n10 sy hande bewe as hy na sy koppie gryp.\n11 Die boord is nou my werk, my erfenis, my plig.\n12 Ek stap voor dagbreek uit; die oggend is nog koud,\n13 en waar ek loop, voel ek hoe die lemoene ryp,\n14 en elke boom dra Oupa se glimlag, sy gesig.\n\n(Translation for understanding: Before dawn, when the sun still hides behind the ridge, / Grandpa walked through his orchard as if in a dream; / he talked with every trunk, with every tree, / as if the trees were children of his own land. / He knew the soil like the palm of his hand, / let the water flow slowly through the furrows, / and every winter his harvest was the cream, / the pride of Brits's warm, fertile sand. / But now Grandpa sits by the window, quiet and old; / his hands tremble when he reaches for his cup. / The orchard is now my work, my heritage, my duty. / I walk out before dawn; the morning is still cold, / and where I walk, I feel how the oranges ripen, / and every tree bears Grandpa's smile, his face.)\n\n**Questions**\n\n3.1 What kind of sonnet is this? Motivate your answer. (2)\n3.2 Explain the turn in l. 9. (2)\n3.3 Name the figure of speech in l. 7 and explain it. (2)\n3.4 What is the effect of the enumeration in l. 11? (2)\n3.5 Explain the image in l. 14 and say how it links to the theme. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**3.1** (2) 'n Petrarca-sonnet ✔: dit bestaan uit 'n oktaaf (r. 1–8, rym abbaabba) en 'n sekstet (r. 9–14, rym cdecde) ✔.","en":"**3.1** (2) A Petrarchan sonnet ✔: it consists of an octave (l. 1–8, rhyme abbaabba) and a sestet (l. 9–14, rhyme cdecde) ✔."},{"af":"**3.2** (2) Die oktaaf beskryf Oupa in die verlede as sterk en bedrywig in sy boord ✔. Met “Maar nou” draai die gedig: Oupa is oud en swak, en die spreker neem die boord oor ✔.","en":"**3.2** (2) The octave describes Grandpa in the past as strong and busy in his orchard ✔. With “Maar nou” (But now) the poem turns: Grandpa is old and weak, and the speaker takes over the orchard ✔."},{"af":"**3.3** (2) Metafoor ✔: die oes word direk “die room” genoem – die beste deel van die melk. Sy oes was dus die heel beste ✔.","en":"**3.3** (2) Metaphor ✔: the harvest is called “die room” (the cream) directly – the best part of the milk. So his harvest was the very best ✔."},{"af":"**3.4** (2) Die opnoeming *werk, erfenis, plig* bou op na 'n klimaks ✔ en wys dat die spreker die boord met trots én as 'n ernstige verantwoordelikheid aanvaar ✔.","en":"**3.4** (2) The enumeration *werk, erfenis, plig* (work, heritage, duty) builds up to a climax ✔ and shows that the speaker accepts the orchard with pride and as a serious responsibility ✔."},{"af":"**3.5** (2) Die bome “dra” Oupa se glimlag soos vrugte (metafoor) ✔: Oupa se liefde en werk leef voort in die boord en in sy kleinkind, al word hy oud – die erfenis gaan na die volgende geslag oor ✔.","en":"**3.5** (2) The trees “bear” Grandpa's smile like fruit (metaphor) ✔: Grandpa's love and work live on in the orchard and in his grandchild, even though he grows old – the heritage passes to the next generation ✔."}],"answer":{"af":"Totaal: 10 punte. Onthou: in 'n Petrarca-sonnet soek jy die wending tussen r. 8 en 9.","en":"Total: 10 marks. Remember: in a Petrarchan sonnet you look for the turn between l. 8 and 9."}},{"title":{"af":"Die paragraafvraag (8 punte)","en":"The paragraph question (8 marks)"},"problem":{"af":"Lees weer die gedig “Beurtkrag”.\n\n**Beurtkrag**\n\n1 Om sesuur\n2 sluk die donker\n3 ons hele straat in een hap.\n\n4 Die yskas hou sy asem op,\n5 die Wi-Fi-liggie knip een keer\n6 en sterf.\n7 My foon staar na my met 'n rooi oog:\n8 twee persent.\n\n9 Ma trek 'n vuurhoutjie.\n10 Ons gesigte word klein en goud,\n11 en vir 'n oomblik\n12 is die stilte\n13 ons s'n.\n\n**Vraag:** Bespreek in 'n paragraaf van 120–150 woorde hoe die digter die tema van gesinsnabyheid uitbeeld. Verwys na beeldspraak, tipografie en toon. (8)","en":"Read the poem “Beurtkrag” again.\n\n**Beurtkrag**\n\n1 Om sesuur\n2 sluk die donker\n3 ons hele straat in een hap.\n\n4 Die yskas hou sy asem op,\n5 die Wi-Fi-liggie knip een keer\n6 en sterf.\n7 My foon staar na my met 'n rooi oog:\n8 twee persent.\n\n9 Ma trek 'n vuurhoutjie.\n10 Ons gesigte word klein en goud,\n11 en vir 'n oomblik\n12 is die stilte\n13 ons s'n.\n\n(Translation for understanding: At six o'clock / the dark swallows / our whole street in one bite. // The fridge holds its breath, / the Wi-Fi light blinks once / and dies. / My phone stares at me with a red eye: / two percent. // Mom strikes a match. / Our faces become small and golden, / and for a moment / the silence / is ours.)\n\n**Question:** Discuss in a paragraph of 120–150 words how the poet portrays the theme of family closeness. Refer to imagery, typography and tone. (8)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Beplan:** Skryf die tema in een sin neer en kies drie bewyse: (1) die personifikasie van die donker en die toestelle, (2) die tipografie van “twee persent.” en strofe 3, (3) die toonverandering.","en":"**Plan:** Write the theme down in one sentence and choose three pieces of evidence: (1) the personification of the dark and the devices, (2) the typography of “twee persent.” and stanza 3, (3) the change in tone."},{"af":"**Inleidende sin (standpunt):** *Die digter wys dat 'n gesin juis in die donker van beurtkrag nader aan mekaar kan kom.*","en":"**Opening sentence (standpoint):** *The poet shows that a family can come closer to each other precisely in the darkness of load-shedding.*"},{"af":"**Bewyse met verduideliking:** Die donker word gepersonifieer as 'n wese wat die straat “sluk”, en die toestelle “sterf” een vir een – die tegnologie wat die gesin skei, val weg. Die woorde “twee persent.” alleen op 'n reël beklemtoon dat die spreker se laaste kontak met die buitewêreld verdwyn. Dan trek Ma 'n vuurhoutjie: die gesigte word “klein en goud”, 'n warm beeld van saamwees.","en":"**Evidence with explanation:** The dark is personified as a creature that “swallows” the street, and the devices “die” one by one – the technology that separates the family falls away. The words “twee persent.” alone on a line emphasise that the speaker's last contact with the outside world disappears. Then Mom strikes a match: the faces become “small and golden”, a warm image of togetherness."},{"af":"**Toon en tipografie:** Die toon verander van gefrustreerd na rustig, en die enjambement in strofe 3 (“en vir 'n oomblik / is die stilte / ons s'n”) laat die leser stadiger lees, sodat hy die vrede saam met die gesin beleef.","en":"**Tone and typography:** The tone changes from frustrated to peaceful, and the enjambment in stanza 3 (“en vir 'n oomblik / is die stilte / ons s'n”) makes the reader read more slowly, so that he experiences the peace with the family."},{"af":"**Slotsin:** *So word die stilte, wat eers dreigend was, iets kosbaars wat net aan die gesin behoort.* Tel jou woorde en kyk dat elke bewys aan die tema gekoppel is.","en":"**Closing sentence:** *In this way the silence, which was threatening at first, becomes something precious that belongs only to the family.* Count your words and check that every piece of evidence is linked to the theme."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Samehangende paragraaf met 'n standpunt, drie of vier bewyse met aanhalings en verduideliking, en 'n slotsin wat na die tema terugkeer.","en":"A coherent paragraph with a standpoint, three or four pieces of evidence with quotations and explanation, and a closing sentence that returns to the theme."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Strofe van drie versreëls heet 'n ___.","en":"A stanza of three lines is called a ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["tersine"],"en":["tercet","tersine","triplet"]},"explain":{"af":"Drie reëls = tersine. Koeplet = 2, kwatryn = 4, kwintet = 5.","en":"Three lines = tersine (tercet). Koeplet = 2, kwatryn = 4, kwintet = 5."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["koeplet","kwatryn","kwintet"],"en":["couplet","quatrain","quintet"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stelling is 'n TEMA en nie bloot 'n onderwerp nie?","en":"Which statement is a THEME and not merely a subject?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Hond wat doodgaan.","en":"'n Hond wat doodgaan. (A dog that dies.)"},{"af":"Beurtkrag in Brits.","en":"Beurtkrag in Brits. (Load-shedding in Brits.)"},{"af":"Ware vriendskap word eers in moeilike tye getoets.","en":"Ware vriendskap word eers in moeilike tye getoets. (True friendship is only tested in difficult times.)"},{"af":"'n Oggend by die Hartbeespoortdam.","en":"'n Oggend by die Hartbeespoortdam. (A morning at the Hartbeespoort Dam.)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Tema is 'n insig of boodskap oor die lewe, gewoonlik as 'n volsin. Die ander drie noem net waaroor 'n gedig gaan – die onderwerp.","en":"A theme is an insight or message about life, usually as a full sentence. The other three only name what a poem is about – the subject."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Toon is die gevoel wat 'n gedig by die leser skep.","en":"Tone is the feeling a poem creates in the reader."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is stemming (atmosfeer). Toon is die spreker se houding teenoor die onderwerp.","en":"False. That is mood (atmosphere). Tone is the speaker's attitude towards the subject."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die rymskema abab heet ___.","en":"The rhyme scheme abab is called ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["kruisrym"],"en":["alternate rhyme","alternating rhyme","cross rhyme","kruisrym"]},"explain":{"af":"abab = kruisrym (die rym kruis oor). aabb = paarrym en abba = omarmende rym.","en":"abab = kruisrym/alternate rhyme (the rhymes cross over). aabb = paarrym and abba = omarmende rym."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["paarrym","omarmende rym","binnerym"],"en":["rhyming couplets","enclosed rhyme","internal rhyme"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stylfiguur by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each figure of speech to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Eufemisme","en":"Euphemism"},"r":{"af":"Oupa het ontslaap.","en":"Oupa het ontslaap. (Grandpa passed away.)"}},{"l":{"af":"Hiperbool","en":"Hyperbole"},"r":{"af":"Ek het jou al 'n miljoen keer gesê!","en":"Ek het jou al 'n miljoen keer gesê! (I've told you a million times!)"}},{"l":{"af":"Paradoks","en":"Paradox"},"r":{"af":"Hoe meer ek leer, hoe minder weet ek.","en":"Hoe meer ek leer, hoe minder weet ek. (The more I learn, the less I know.)"}},{"l":{"af":"Personifikasie","en":"Personification"},"r":{"af":"Die berg slaap onder die wolke.","en":"Die berg slaap onder die wolke. (The mountain sleeps under the clouds.)"}},{"l":{"af":"Simbool","en":"Symbol"},"r":{"af":"'n Wit duif as teken van vrede","en":"A white dove as a sign of peace"}}],"explain":{"af":"Eufemisme versag (dood → ontslaap); hiperbool oordryf; 'n paradoks klink teenstrydig maar is waar; personifikasie gee iets nie-menslik menslike handelinge; 'n simbool staan vir 'n abstrakte idee.","en":"Euphemism softens (death → ontslaap); hyperbole exaggerates; a paradox sounds contradictory but is true; personification gives something non-human human actions; a symbol stands for an abstract idea."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar kom die wending (volta) gewoonlik in 'n Petrarca-sonnet voor?","en":"Where does the turn (volta) usually occur in a Petrarchan sonnet?"},"options":[{"af":"Ná reël 4","en":"After line 4"},{"af":"Tussen reël 8 en 9","en":"Between lines 8 and 9"},{"af":"In die laaste koeplet","en":"In the final couplet"},{"af":"Tussen reël 12 en 13","en":"Between lines 12 and 13"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die Petrarca-sonnet het 'n oktaaf (8 reëls) en 'n sekstet (6 reëls); die wending kom waar die oktaaf in die sekstet oorgaan. Die wending in die koeplet is by die Shakespeare-sonnet.","en":"The Petrarchan sonnet has an octave (8 lines) and a sestet (6 lines); the turn comes where the octave becomes the sestet. The turn in the couplet belongs to the Shakespearean sonnet."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"“Die wilde wind waai woes oor die werf.” Die herhaling van die w-klank is ___.","en":"“Die wilde wind waai woes oor die werf.” The repetition of the w sound is ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["alliterasie"],"en":["alliteration","alliterasie"]},"explain":{"af":"Herhaalde konsonante (veral aan die begin van woorde) = alliterasie. Assonansie is herhaalde klinkers.","en":"Repeated consonants (especially at the start of words) = alliteration. Assonance is repeated vowels."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["assonansie","onomatopee","binnerym"],"en":["assonance","onomatopoeia","internal rhyme"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stylfiguur kom voor in “Die ou bakkie hoes en kug teen die bult uit”?","en":"Which figure of speech occurs in “Die ou bakkie hoes en kug teen die bult uit” (The old bakkie coughs and splutters up the hill)?"},"options":[{"af":"Vergelyking","en":"Simile"},{"af":"Antitese","en":"Antithesis"},{"af":"Personifikasie","en":"Personification"},{"af":"Eufemisme","en":"Euphemism"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die bakkie kry menslike handelinge (hoes, kug). Dit wys hoe oud en sukkelend die enjin is. Daar is geen *soos* nie, dus nie 'n vergelyking nie.","en":"The bakkie gets human actions (coughs, splutters). It shows how old and struggling the engine is. There is no *soos* (like), so it is not a simile."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Shakespeare-sonnet bestaan uit 'n oktaaf en 'n sekstet.","en":"A Shakespearean sonnet consists of an octave and a sestet."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die Shakespeare-sonnet het drie kwatryne en 'n koeplet (4 + 4 + 4 + 2). Oktaaf + sekstet is die Petrarca-sonnet.","en":"False. The Shakespearean sonnet has three quatrains and a couplet (4 + 4 + 4 + 2). Octave + sestet is the Petrarchan sonnet."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Twee teenoorgestelde woorde direk saam, soos in “'n oorverdowende stilte”, vorm 'n ___.","en":"Two opposite words directly together, as in “'n oorverdowende stilte” (a deafening silence), form an ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["oksimoron"],"en":["oxymoron","oksimoron"]},"explain":{"af":"Stilte kan nie letterlik oorverdowend wees nie: die twee woorde weerspreek mekaar direk. Dit beklemtoon hoe intens die stilte is.","en":"Silence cannot literally be deafening: the two words contradict each other directly. It emphasises how intense the silence is."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["eufemisme","hiperbool","personifikasie"],"en":["euphemism","hyperbole","personification"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die rymskema van hierdie strofe? “Die taxi stop met 'n gil, / die deure swaai wyd oop; / die mense klim en loop, / en dan is alles stil.”","en":"What is the rhyme scheme of this stanza? “Die taxi stop met 'n gil, / die deure swaai wyd oop; / die mense klim en loop, / en dan is alles stil.”"},"options":[{"af":"aabb (paarrym)","en":"aabb (rhyming couplets)"},{"af":"abab (kruisrym)","en":"abab (alternate rhyme)"},{"af":"abcb","en":"abcb"},{"af":"abba (omarmende rym)","en":"abba (enclosed rhyme)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"gil (a) – oop (b) – loop (b) – stil (a): die a-rym “omarm” die b-rym, dus omarmende rym.","en":"gil (a) – oop (b) – loop (b) – stil (a): the a-rhyme “embraces” the b-rhyme, so enclosed rhyme."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: “Ag ja, nog 'n pragtige Maandag: / die wekker skree, die geiser is koud.” Wat is die spreker se toon?","en":"Read: “Ag ja, nog 'n pragtige Maandag: / die wekker skree, die geiser is koud.” (Oh yes, another beautiful Monday: / the alarm screams, the geyser is cold.) What is the speaker's tone?"},"options":[{"af":"Ironies","en":"Ironic"},{"af":"Nostalgies","en":"Nostalgic"},{"af":"Vreedsaam","en":"Peaceful"},{"af":"Liefdevol","en":"Loving"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker noem die Maandag “pragtig”, maar die besonderhede (skreeuende wekker, koue geiser) wys hy bedoel die teenoorgestelde. Dit is ironie.","en":"The speaker calls Monday “beautiful”, but the details (screaming alarm, cold geyser) show he means the opposite. That is irony."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"“Kraak! Die tak breek, en die hond se woef-woef weerklink oor die werf.” Die woorde *kraak* en *woef-woef* is voorbeelde van ___.","en":"“Kraak! Die tak breek, en die hond se woef-woef weerklink oor die werf.” The words *kraak* (crack) and *woef-woef* (woof-woof) are examples of ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["onomatopee","klanknabootsing","onomatopeë"],"en":["onomatopoeia","onomatopee","klanknabootsing"]},"explain":{"af":"Woorde wat die klank naboots wat hulle beskryf, is onomatopee (klanknabootsing). Die leser hoor die geluide byna.","en":"Words that imitate the sound they describe are onomatopoeia (klanknabootsing). The reader almost hears the sounds."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["alliterasie","assonansie","personifikasie"],"en":["alliteration","assonance","personification"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die slot van 'n gedig: “Die klok slaan twaalf. / Die deur gaan oop. / En dan / niks.” Wat is die effek van die woord “niks.” alleen op die laaste reël?","en":"Read the end of a poem: “Die klok slaan twaalf. / Die deur gaan oop. / En dan / niks.” (The clock strikes twelve. / The door opens. / And then / nothing.) What is the effect of the word “niks.” alone on the last line?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit rym met die vorige reël en skep musikaliteit.","en":"It rhymes with the previous line and creates musicality."},{"af":"Die witruimte beklemtoon die leegte en skep 'n antiklimaks ná die spanning.","en":"The white space emphasises the emptiness and creates an anticlimax after the tension."},{"af":"Dit is 'n voorbeeld van alliterasie wat die klank beklemtoon.","en":"It is an example of alliteration that emphasises the sound."},{"af":"Dit wys dat die gedig 'n Petrarca-sonnet is.","en":"It shows that the poem is a Petrarchan sonnet."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die spanning bou op (twaalfuur, die deur gaan oop), en dan gebeur daar niks. Die woord alleen, met witruimte rondom, laat die leser die leegte en teleurstelling voel.","en":"The tension builds (midnight, the door opens), and then nothing happens. The word alone, with white space around it, makes the reader feel the emptiness and disappointment."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vraag: “Benoem die stylfiguur en verduidelik die funksie daarvan: ‘Ons straat is 'n slagveld ná die storm.’ (2)” Watter antwoord kry albei punte?","en":"Question: “Name the figure of speech and explain its function: ‘Ons straat is 'n slagveld ná die storm.’ (Our street is a battlefield after the storm.) (2)” Which answer earns both marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Metafoor.","en":"Metaphor."},{"af":"Vergelyking, want die straat lyk soos 'n slagveld.","en":"Simile, because the street looks like a battlefield."},{"af":"Hiperbool, want die storm was baie erg.","en":"Hyperbole, because the storm was very bad."},{"af":"Metafoor: die straat word direk 'n slagveld genoem, wat beklemtoon hoe verwoes en deurmekaar dit ná die storm is.","en":"Metaphor: the street is called a battlefield directly, which emphasises how devastated and chaotic it is after the storm."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Volpunte vra die regte term (1) plus die funksie (1). “Metafoor.” alleen kry net 1 punt; *vergelyking* is verkeerd, want daar is geen *soos* nie.","en":"Full marks need the right term (1) plus the function (1). “Metaphor.” alone earns only 1 mark; *simile* is wrong, because there is no *soos* (like)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy moet 'n paragraaf skryf: “Bespreek hoe die digter die tema van verlies uitbeeld.” Watter openingsin is die BESTE?","en":"You must write a paragraph: “Discuss how the poet portrays the theme of loss.” Which opening sentence is the BEST?"},"options":[{"af":"Die gedig is baie mooi en ek hou daarvan.","en":"Die gedig is baie mooi en ek hou daarvan. (The poem is very beautiful and I like it.)"},{"af":"Die digter gebruik kontras tussen die vrolike verlede en die leë hede, sterk beeldspraak en 'n berustende toon om te wys hoe verlies 'n mens se wêreld verander.","en":"Die digter gebruik kontras ... (The poet uses contrast between the happy past and the empty present, strong imagery and a resigned tone to show how loss changes a person's world.)"},{"af":"Die gedig het vier strofes en die rymskema is abab.","en":"Die gedig het vier strofes en die rymskema is abab. (The poem has four stanzas and the rhyme scheme is abab.)"},{"af":"Verlies is wanneer iemand doodgaan of weggaan.","en":"Verlies is wanneer iemand doodgaan of weggaan. (Loss is when someone dies or leaves.)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie openingsin gee 'n standpunt wat direk aan die tema gekoppel is en noem die tegnieke wat jy gaan bespreek. Die ander is 'n vae mening, net vorm, of 'n definisie wat niks oor die gedig sê nie.","en":"A good opening sentence gives a standpoint linked directly to the theme and names the techniques you will discuss. The others are a vague opinion, form only, or a definition that says nothing about the poem."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t1-opstel","title":{"af":"Opstelskryf: opstelsoorte en die skryfproses","en":"Essay writing: essay types and the writing process"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die opstelsoort wat 'n onderwerp vra kan herken, 'n opstel van 300–350 woorde stap vir stap kan beplan en skryf, en algemene taalfoute soos anglisismes kan vermy.","en":"You will be able to recognise the essay type a topic asks for, plan and write a 300–350-word essay step by step, and avoid common language errors such as anglicisms."},"summary":{"af":"## Vraestel 3: Skryfwerk\n\nVraestel 3 tel **100 punte**:\n\n| Afdeling | Wat jy skryf | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | **Een** opstel van **300–350 woorde** | 50 |\n| B | Twee transaksionele tekste | 2 × 25 = 50 |\n\n## Opstelsoorte\n\n| Soort | Doel | Kenmerke |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Verhalende** | vertel 'n storie | storielyn met begin, spanning, klimaks en einde; dialoog; gewoonlik in die verlede tyd |\n| **Beskrywende** | skilder 'n prent met woorde | al vyf sintuie; beeldspraak; *wys, moenie vertel nie* |\n| **Beredenerende** | bespreek 'n saak van alle kante | albei kante gebalanseerd; jou eie gevolgtrekking aan die einde |\n| **Betogende / argumenterende** | oortuig die leser | een duidelike standpunt; sterk argumente met voorbeelde; retoriese vrae |\n| **Bespiegelende / refleksiewe** | dink na oor 'n ervaring of idee | persoonlik; gevoelens, insigte en wat jy geleer het |\n\n*Wys, moenie vertel nie:* in plaas van *Ek was bang* skryf jy *My hande het gebewe en my mond was kurkdroog.*\n\n### Ander soorte onderwerpe\n\n- **Beeldmateriaal** ('n prent of foto): gee jou opstel 'n **eie titel** en sorg dat die verband met die prent duidelik is. Jy kies self die opstelsoort.\n- **'n Stelling of aanhaling** (bv. *Geld kan nie geluk koop nie*): jy kan beredeneer, betoog of bespiegel – maar bly by die stelling.\n\n> **Wenk:** Die sleutelwoorde in die onderwerp wys die opstelsoort: *Vertel* → verhalend; *Beskryf* → beskrywend; *Bespreek die voor- en nadele* → beredenerend; *Oortuig jou lesers* of *Is jy vir of teen ...?* → betogend; *Dink terug* of *Wat het jy geleer?* → bespiegelend.\n\n## Die skryfproses\n\n1. **Beplanning:** Maak 'n **breinkaart** of 'n lys **kernwoorde**, en besluit wat in elke paragraaf kom. Die beplanning moet duidelik op jou antwoordblad wees; trek dit daarna deur.\n2. **Konsep:** Skryf die eerste weergawe in paragrawe.\n3. **Redigering:** Verbeter die inhoud, volgorde, woordkeuse en sinsbou.\n4. **Proeflees:** Soek spel-, leesteken- en taalfoute.\n5. **Finale weergawe:** Skryf netjies oor (of maak die laaste verbeterings).\n\n- Die **titel** tel nie by die woordetal nie.\n- Skryf die **woordetal** aan die einde neer.\n- Beplan jou lengte: vyf paragrawe van 60–70 woorde is ongeveer 330 woorde.\n\n## Struktuur\n\n### Inleiding\n\nGryp die leser se aandag van die eerste sin af:\n\n- **Dialoog:** *“Hardloop!” skree Thabo.*\n- **'n Vraag:** *Het jy al ooit regtig niks gehoor nie?*\n- **In medias res** (begin midde-in die aksie): *Die tak kraak onder my voete.*\n\nVermy aankondigings soos *Ek gaan vir julle vertel van ...*\n\n### Middel\n\n- Elke paragraaf het **een hoofgedagte**, wat in die **kernsin** gestel word.\n- **Skakelwoorde** verbind jou sinne en paragrawe logies: *eerstens, daarbenewens, verder, nietemin, aan die ander kant, gevolglik, daarom, ten slotte*.\n\n### Slot\n\nBind die opstel af en **verwys terug** na die inleiding of die titel. Moenie 'n nuwe idee begin nie, en vermy *Toe word ek wakker – dit was alles 'n droom.*\n\n## Hoe word jy geassesseer? (HT-rubriek, 50 punte)\n\n| Kriterium | Punte |\n|---|---|\n| Inhoud en beplanning | 30 |\n| Taal, styl en redigering | 15 |\n| Struktuur | 5 |\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- **Te kort of te lank:** bly binne 300–350 woorde.\n- **Anglisismes** (Engelse uitdrukkings wat letterlik vertaal is):\n\n| Fout ✗ | Korrek ✓ |\n|---|---|\n| Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad. | Ek het dit geniet. / Ek het lekker gekuier. |\n| Ek het myself geniet. | Ek het dit geniet. |\n| Ons het die bus gemis. | Ons het die bus verpas. |\n| Hy het 'n besluit gemaak. | Hy het 'n besluit geneem. |\n| Aan die einde van die dag ... | Uiteindelik ... / Per slot van rekening ... |\n\n- **Wisseling van tye:** bly in een tyd – in 'n verhaal gewoonlik die verlede tyd.\n- **Sleng en kitsboodskaptaal** in 'n formele opstel (*cool*, *lol*, *ou* vir 'n man).\n- **Geen paragrawe nie**, of een lang blok teks.\n- 'n Opstel wat **nie by die onderwerp of die opstelsoort pas nie**.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die meeste punte (30) is vir inhoud en beplanning. 'n Oorspronklike, goed beplande opstel wat by die onderwerp bly, is die belangrikste.","en":"## Paper 3: Writing\n\nPaper 3 counts **100 marks**:\n\n| Section | What you write | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | **One** essay of **300–350 words** | 50 |\n| B | Two transactional texts | 2 × 25 = 50 |\n\n## Essay types (opstelsoorte)\n\n| Type | Purpose | Features |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Narrative (verhalende)** | tells a story | storyline with a beginning, suspense, climax and ending; dialogue; usually in the past tense |\n| **Descriptive (beskrywende)** | paints a picture with words | all five senses; imagery; *show, don't tell* |\n| **Discursive (beredenerende)** | discusses an issue from all sides | both sides balanced; your own conclusion at the end |\n| **Argumentative (betogende/argumenterende)** | convinces the reader | one clear standpoint; strong arguments with examples; rhetorical questions |\n| **Reflective (bespiegelende/refleksiewe)** | reflects on an experience or idea | personal; feelings, insights and what you learnt |\n\n*Show, don't tell:* instead of *Ek was bang* (I was scared) you write *My hande het gebewe en my mond was kurkdroog* (My hands shook and my mouth was bone-dry).\n\n### Other kinds of topics\n\n- **Visual material (beeldmateriaal)** (a picture or photo): give your essay **your own title** and make sure the link to the picture is clear. You choose the essay type yourself.\n- **A statement or quotation** (e.g. *Geld kan nie geluk koop nie* – money can't buy happiness): you may discuss, argue or reflect – but stay with the statement.\n\n> **Tip:** The key words in the topic show the essay type: *Vertel* (tell) → narrative; *Beskryf* (describe) → descriptive; *Bespreek die voor- en nadele* (discuss the pros and cons) → discursive; *Oortuig jou lesers* (convince your readers) or *Is jy vir of teen ...?* (are you for or against) → argumentative; *Dink terug* (think back) or *Wat het jy geleer?* (what did you learn) → reflective.\n\n## The writing process\n\n1. **Planning:** Make a **mind map (breinkaart)** or a list of **key words (kernwoorde)**, and decide what goes in each paragraph. The planning must be clearly visible on your answer sheet; cross it out afterwards.\n2. **Draft (konsep):** Write the first version in paragraphs.\n3. **Editing (redigering):** Improve the content, order, choice of words and sentence structure.\n4. **Proofreading (proeflees):** Look for spelling, punctuation and language errors.\n5. **Final version:** Write it out neatly (or make the final corrections).\n\n- The **title** does not count towards the word count.\n- Write the **word count (woordetal)** at the end.\n- Plan your length: five paragraphs of 60–70 words is about 330 words.\n\n## Structure\n\n### Introduction\n\nGrab the reader's attention from the first sentence:\n\n- **Dialogue:** *“Hardloop!” skree Thabo.* (“Run!” Thabo shouts.)\n- **A question:** *Het jy al ooit regtig niks gehoor nie?* (Have you ever truly heard nothing?)\n- **In medias res** (start in the middle of the action): *Die tak kraak onder my voete.* (The branch cracks under my feet.)\n\nAvoid announcements such as *Ek gaan vir julle vertel van ...* (I am going to tell you about ...)\n\n### Body\n\n- Every paragraph has **one main idea**, stated in the **topic sentence (kernsin)**.\n- **Linking words (skakelwoorde)** join your sentences and paragraphs logically: *eerstens* (firstly), *daarbenewens* (in addition), *verder* (further), *nietemin* (nevertheless), *aan die ander kant* (on the other hand), *gevolglik* (consequently), *daarom* (therefore), *ten slotte* (in conclusion).\n\n### Conclusion\n\nRound off the essay and **refer back** to the introduction or the title. Do not start a new idea, and avoid *Toe word ek wakker – dit was alles 'n droom* (Then I woke up – it was all a dream).\n\n## How are you assessed? (HL rubric, 50 marks)\n\n| Criterion | Marks |\n|---|---|\n| Content and planning | 30 |\n| Language, style and editing | 15 |\n| Structure | 5 |\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- **Too short or too long:** stay within 300–350 words.\n- **Anglicisms (anglisismes)** (English expressions translated literally):\n\n| Wrong ✗ | Correct ✓ |\n|---|---|\n| Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad. | Ek het dit geniet. / Ek het lekker gekuier. |\n| Ek het myself geniet. | Ek het dit geniet. |\n| Ons het die bus gemis. | Ons het die bus verpas. |\n| Hy het 'n besluit gemaak. | Hy het 'n besluit geneem. |\n| Aan die einde van die dag ... | Uiteindelik ... / Per slot van rekening ... |\n\n- **Switching tenses:** stay in one tense – in a story usually the past tense.\n- **Slang and text-message language** in a formal essay (*cool*, *lol*, *ou* for a man).\n- **No paragraphs**, or one long block of text.\n- An essay that **does not fit the topic or the essay type**.\n\n> **Remember!** Most of the marks (30) are for content and planning. An original, well-planned essay that stays with the topic matters most."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Verhalende opstel","en":"Narrative essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat 'n storie vertel, met 'n storielyn, spanning, 'n klimaks en 'n einde.","en":"An essay that tells a story, with a storyline, suspense, a climax and an ending."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskrywende opstel","en":"Descriptive essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat met die sintuie en beeldspraak 'n prent van 'n persoon, plek of gebeurtenis skilder.","en":"An essay that uses the senses and imagery to paint a picture of a person, place or event."}},{"term":{"af":"Beredenerende opstel","en":"Discursive essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat albei kante van 'n saak gebalanseerd bespreek en met 'n eie gevolgtrekking eindig.","en":"An essay that discusses both sides of an issue in a balanced way and ends with an own conclusion."}},{"term":{"af":"Betogende (argumenterende) opstel","en":"Argumentative essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat een standpunt inneem en die leser met sterk argumente probeer oortuig.","en":"An essay that takes one standpoint and tries to convince the reader with strong arguments."}},{"term":{"af":"Bespiegelende (refleksiewe) opstel","en":"Reflective essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Persoonlike opstel waarin jy oor 'n ervaring, gevoel of idee nadink en jou insigte deel.","en":"A personal essay in which you reflect on an experience, feeling or idea and share your insights."}},{"term":{"af":"Breinkaart","en":"Mind map"},"def":{"af":"'n Beplanningsdiagram met die onderwerp in die middel en kernwoorde wat daaruit vertak.","en":"A planning diagram with the topic in the middle and key words branching out from it."}},{"term":{"af":"Kernsin","en":"Topic sentence"},"def":{"af":"Die sin wat die hoofgedagte van 'n paragraaf stel.","en":"The sentence that states the main idea of a paragraph."}},{"term":{"af":"Skakelwoorde","en":"Linking words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde soos eerstens, daarbenewens, nietemin en gevolglik wat sinne en paragrawe logies verbind.","en":"Words such as eerstens, daarbenewens, nietemin and gevolglik that link sentences and paragraphs logically."}},{"term":{"af":"In medias res","en":"In medias res"},"def":{"af":"'n Inleiding wat midde-in die aksie begin, sonder agtergrond of aankondiging.","en":"An introduction that starts in the middle of the action, without background or announcement."}},{"term":{"af":"Anglisisme","en":"Anglicism"},"def":{"af":"'n Engelse woord of uitdrukking wat letterlik in Afrikaans vertaal is, bv. “Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad” in plaas van “Ek het dit geniet”.","en":"An English word or expression translated literally into Afrikaans, e.g. “Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad” instead of “Ek het dit geniet”."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Watter opstelsoort vra die onderwerp?","en":"Which essay type does the topic ask for?"},"problem":{"af":"Lees elke onderwerp en sê watter opstelsoort dit vra. Motiveer kortliks.\n\n(a) Vertel van die aand toe die ligte by die rugbyfinaal doodgegaan het.\n(b) Skole behoort selfone in die klas toe te laat. Oortuig jou lesers.\n(c) Beskryf die Magaliesberg op 'n somersoggend.\n(d) Sosiale media: vriend of vyand? Bespreek albei kante.\n(e) Die grootste les wat ek nog geleer het – dink terug en deel jou insigte.\n(f) *Prent:* 'n Ou man sit alleen op 'n bankie by 'n taxistaanplek; langs hom staan 'n leë stoel.","en":"Read each topic and say which essay type it asks for. Motivate briefly.\n\n(a) Vertel van die aand toe die ligte by die rugbyfinaal doodgegaan het. (Tell about the night the lights went out at the rugby final.)\n(b) Skole behoort selfone in die klas toe te laat. Oortuig jou lesers. (Schools should allow cellphones in class. Convince your readers.)\n(c) Beskryf die Magaliesberg op 'n somersoggend. (Describe the Magaliesberg on a summer morning.)\n(d) Sosiale media: vriend of vyand? Bespreek albei kante. (Social media: friend or foe? Discuss both sides.)\n(e) Die grootste les wat ek nog geleer het – dink terug en deel jou insigte. (The biggest lesson I have ever learnt – think back and share your insights.)\n(f) *Picture:* An old man sits alone on a bench at a taxi rank; next to him is an empty chair."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Verhalend** – *Vertel van die aand* vra 'n storie met 'n storielyn, spanning en 'n klimaks.","en":"(a) **Narrative** – *Vertel van die aand* (tell about the night) asks for a story with a storyline, suspense and a climax."},{"af":"(b) **Betogend** – *Oortuig jou lesers*: jy kies een kant en verdedig dit met sterk argumente.","en":"(b) **Argumentative** – *Oortuig jou lesers* (convince your readers): you choose one side and defend it with strong arguments."},{"af":"(c) **Beskrywend** – *Beskryf*: gebruik die sintuie en beeldspraak; daar hoef geen storielyn te wees nie.","en":"(c) **Descriptive** – *Beskryf* (describe): use the senses and imagery; there need not be a storyline."},{"af":"(d) **Beredenerend** – *Bespreek albei kante*: gee die voor- en nadele gebalanseerd en sluit af met jou eie gevolgtrekking.","en":"(d) **Discursive** – *Bespreek albei kante* (discuss both sides): give the pros and cons in a balanced way and end with your own conclusion."},{"af":"(e) **Bespiegelend** – *dink terug en deel jou insigte*: persoonlike nadenke oor 'n ervaring en wat jy daaruit geleer het. (f) **Beeldmateriaal** – jy kies self die soort (bv. verhalend oor die man wat op iemand wag), maar gee 'n eie titel en maak die verband met die prent duidelik.","en":"(e) **Reflective** – *dink terug en deel jou insigte* (think back and share your insights): personal reflection on an experience and what you learnt from it. (f) **Visual material** – you choose the type yourself (e.g. a narrative about the man who waits for someone), but give your own title and make the link to the picture clear."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) verhalend (b) betogend (c) beskrywend (d) beredenerend (e) bespiegelend (f) eie keuse, eie titel, duidelike verband met die prent","en":"(a) narrative (b) argumentative (c) descriptive (d) discursive (e) reflective (f) own choice, own title, clear link to the picture"}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan 'n verhalende opstel","en":"Plan a narrative essay"},"problem":{"af":"Beplan 'n opstel van 300–350 woorde oor die onderwerp: *'n Dag wat ek nooit sal vergeet nie.*","en":"Plan an essay of 300–350 words on the topic: *'n Dag wat ek nooit sal vergeet nie* (A day I will never forget)."},"steps":[{"af":"**Ontleed die onderwerp:** dit vra 'n verhalende opstel – 'n ek-verteller, die verlede tyd, 'n storielyn met spanning en 'n klimaks.","en":"**Analyse the topic:** it asks for a narrative essay – a first-person narrator, the past tense, a storyline with suspense and a climax."},{"af":"**Breinkaart (kernwoorde):** Hartbeespoortdam – kano – boetie – skielike wind – kano kantel – visserman – redding – les oor veiligheid.","en":"**Mind map (key words):** Hartbeespoort Dam – canoe – little brother – sudden wind – canoe capsizes – angler – rescue – lesson about safety."},{"af":"**Paragraafplan:** P1 inleiding *in medias res*: die kano kantel (±50 woorde). P2 terugflits: die rustige oggend op die dam (±70). P3 komplikasie: die wind kom op, die golwe groei (±80). P4 klimaks: ek gryp my boetie, 'n visserman roei nader (±80). P5 slot: terug na die koue water – wat ek geleer het (±50). Totaal ±330 woorde.","en":"**Paragraph plan:** P1 introduction *in medias res*: the canoe capsizes (±50 words). P2 flashback: the calm morning on the dam (±70). P3 complication: the wind picks up, the waves grow (±80). P4 climax: I grab my brother, an angler rows closer (±80). P5 conclusion: back to the cold water – what I learnt (±50). Total ±330 words."},{"af":"**Kies 'n titel** wat nuuskierig maak, bv. *Koue, groen water*. Die titel tel nie by die woordetal nie.","en":"**Choose a title** that creates curiosity, e.g. *Koue, groen water* (Cold, green water). The title does not count towards the word count."},{"af":"**Ná die skryf:** redigeer en proeflees, skryf die woordetal aan die einde en trek die beplanning deur (maar dit moet steeds sigbaar wees).","en":"**After writing:** edit and proofread, write the word count at the end and cross out the planning (but it must still be visible)."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Duidelike breinkaart, 'n vyfparagraafplan met 'n woordebegroting van ±330 woorde, 'n eie titel en die woordetal aan die einde.","en":"A clear mind map, a five-paragraph plan with a word budget of ±330 words, an own title and the word count at the end."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter 'n swak inleiding","en":"Improve a weak introduction"},"problem":{"af":"Hier is 'n swak inleiding vir die opstel *'n Dag wat ek nooit sal vergeet nie*. Noem die probleme en herskryf dit.\n\n“Ek gaan vir julle vertel van die dag toe ons by Harties was. Dit was baie lekker en ons het 'n goeie tyd gehad. Toe het iets gebeur.”","en":"Here is a weak introduction for the essay *'n Dag wat ek nooit sal vergeet nie*. Name the problems and rewrite it.\n\n“Ek gaan vir julle vertel van die dag toe ons by Harties was. Dit was baie lekker en ons het 'n goeie tyd gehad. Toe het iets gebeur.” (I am going to tell you about the day we were at Harties. It was very nice and we had a good time. Then something happened.)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Probleem 1:** *Ek gaan vir julle vertel* is 'n aankondiging. Dit verveel die leser en gryp nie sy aandag nie.","en":"**Problem 1:** *Ek gaan vir julle vertel* (I am going to tell you) is an announcement. It bores the reader and does not grab attention."},{"af":"**Probleem 2:** *ons het 'n goeie tyd gehad* is 'n anglisisme; skryf *ons het dit geniet* of *ons het lekker gekuier*.","en":"**Problem 2:** *ons het 'n goeie tyd gehad* is an anglicism; write *ons het dit geniet* or *ons het lekker gekuier*."},{"af":"**Probleem 3:** *baie lekker* en *iets het gebeur* is vaag: dit vertel, maar wys niks. Daar is geen sintuie of spanning nie.","en":"**Problem 3:** *baie lekker* (very nice) and *iets het gebeur* (something happened) are vague: they tell, but show nothing. There are no senses or suspense."},{"af":"**Herskryf in medias res:** “Die kano het gekantel. Koue, groen water het oor my kop geslaan, en al wat ek kon hoor, was my boetie se gil bo die wind. 'n Uur tevore was die Hartbeespoortdam nog 'n blink spieël ...”","en":"**Rewrite in medias res:** “Die kano het gekantel. Koue, groen water het oor my kop geslaan, en al wat ek kon hoor, was my boetie se gil bo die wind. 'n Uur tevore was die Hartbeespoortdam nog 'n blink spieël ...” (The canoe capsized. Cold, green water crashed over my head, and all I could hear was my brother's scream above the wind. An hour before, the Hartbeespoort Dam had still been a shiny mirror ...)"},{"af":"**Waarom dit beter is:** dit begin midde-in die aksie, gebruik die sintuie (koue, groen, gil) en 'n metafoor (spieël), en laat die leser wonder wat gebeur het. Die terugflits (*'n Uur tevore*) lei mooi na die volgende paragraaf, en die hele inleiding bly in die verlede tyd.","en":"**Why it is better:** it starts in the middle of the action, uses the senses (cold, green, scream) and a metaphor (mirror), and makes the reader wonder what happened. The flashback (*'n Uur tevore* – an hour before) leads neatly into the next paragraph, and the whole introduction stays in the past tense."}],"answer":{"af":"“Die kano het gekantel. Koue, groen water het oor my kop geslaan, en al wat ek kon hoor, was my boetie se gil bo die wind. 'n Uur tevore was die Hartbeespoortdam nog 'n blink spieël ...”","en":"“Die kano het gekantel. Koue, groen water het oor my kop geslaan, en al wat ek kon hoor, was my boetie se gil bo die wind. 'n Uur tevore was die Hartbeespoortdam nog 'n blink spieël ...”"}},{"title":{"af":"Korrigeer anglisismes en tydwisseling","en":"Correct anglicisms and tense switching"},"problem":{"af":"Die paragraaf bevat vier anglisismes en een fout met die tyd. Herskryf dit korrek.\n\n“Verlede Saterdag het ons by oom Koos gebraai. Ek het myself geniet, maar toe maak Pa 'n besluit: ons moet vroeg huis toe gaan. Ongelukkig het ons die laaste taxi gemis en moes ons stap. Aan die einde van die dag het ons nogtans 'n goeie tyd gehad.”","en":"The paragraph contains four anglicisms and one tense error. Rewrite it correctly.\n\n“Verlede Saterdag het ons by oom Koos gebraai. Ek het myself geniet, maar toe maak Pa 'n besluit: ons moet vroeg huis toe gaan. Ongelukkig het ons die laaste taxi gemis en moes ons stap. Aan die einde van die dag het ons nogtans 'n goeie tyd gehad.” (Last Saturday we had a braai at uncle Koos's. I enjoyed myself, but then Dad made a decision: we had to go home early. Unfortunately we missed the last taxi and had to walk. At the end of the day we still had a good time.)"},"steps":[{"af":"*Ek het myself geniet* → **Ek het dit geniet** (anglisisme van *I enjoyed myself*).","en":"*Ek het myself geniet* → **Ek het dit geniet** (anglicism of *I enjoyed myself*)."},{"af":"*toe maak Pa 'n besluit: ons moet* → **toe het Pa 'n besluit geneem: ons moes** – *'n besluit maak* is 'n anglisisme, en die verhaal moet in die verlede tyd bly.","en":"*toe maak Pa 'n besluit: ons moet* → **toe het Pa 'n besluit geneem: ons moes** – *'n besluit maak* is an anglicism, and the story must stay in the past tense."},{"af":"*die laaste taxi gemis* → **die laaste taxi verpas** (anglisisme van *missed the taxi*).","en":"*die laaste taxi gemis* → **die laaste taxi verpas** (anglicism of *missed the taxi*)."},{"af":"*Aan die einde van die dag ... 'n goeie tyd gehad* → **Uiteindelik het ons nogtans lekker gekuier** (twee anglisismes in een sin).","en":"*Aan die einde van die dag ... 'n goeie tyd gehad* → **Uiteindelik het ons nogtans lekker gekuier** (two anglicisms in one sentence)."}],"answer":{"af":"“Verlede Saterdag het ons by oom Koos gebraai. Ek het dit geniet, maar toe het Pa 'n besluit geneem: ons moes vroeg huis toe gaan. Ongelukkig het ons die laaste taxi verpas en moes ons stap. Uiteindelik het ons nogtans lekker gekuier.”","en":"“Verlede Saterdag het ons by oom Koos gebraai. Ek het dit geniet, maar toe het Pa 'n besluit geneem: ons moes vroeg huis toe gaan. Ongelukkig het ons die laaste taxi verpas en moes ons stap. Uiteindelik het ons nogtans lekker gekuier.”"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die HT-rubriek vir die opstel (50 punte), hoeveel punte tel inhoud en beplanning?","en":"In the HL rubric for the essay (50 marks), how many marks do content and planning count?"},"options":[{"af":"5","en":"5"},{"af":"15","en":"15"},{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"50","en":"50"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Inhoud en beplanning = 30, taal, styl en redigering = 15, struktuur = 5. Saam is dit 50.","en":"Content and planning = 30, language, style and editing = 15, structure = 5. Together that is 50."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Graad 10 Huistaal moet jou opstel tussen 300 en ___ woorde lank wees.","en":"In Grade 10 Home Language your essay must be between 300 and ___ words long."},"answers":{"af":["350"],"en":["350"]},"explain":{"af":"Die opstel is 300–350 woorde. Te kort of te lank kos jou punte.","en":"The essay is 300–350 words. Too short or too long costs you marks."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["250","400","500"],"en":["250","400","500"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die titel van jou opstel tel by die woordetal.","en":"The title of your essay counts towards the word count."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die titel tel nie. Skryf die woordetal aan die einde van die opstel neer.","en":"False. The title does not count. Write the word count at the end of the essay."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke opstelsoort by sy belangrikste kenmerk.","en":"Match each essay type to its main feature."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Verhalende","en":"Narrative"},"r":{"af":"'n Storielyn met spanning en 'n klimaks","en":"A storyline with suspense and a climax"}},{"l":{"af":"Beskrywende","en":"Descriptive"},"r":{"af":"Die sintuie skilder 'n prent met woorde","en":"The senses paint a picture with words"}},{"l":{"af":"Beredenerende","en":"Discursive"},"r":{"af":"Albei kante word gebalanseerd bespreek","en":"Both sides are discussed in a balanced way"}},{"l":{"af":"Betogende","en":"Argumentative"},"r":{"af":"Een standpunt word oortuigend verdedig","en":"One standpoint is defended convincingly"}},{"l":{"af":"Bespiegelende","en":"Reflective"},"r":{"af":"Persoonlike nadenke oor gevoelens en insigte","en":"Personal reflection on feelings and insights"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ken die verskil tussen beredenerend (albei kante) en betogend (een kant): dit is die mees algemene verwarring.","en":"Know the difference between discursive (both sides) and argumentative (one side): it is the most common confusion."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die sin wat die hoofgedagte van 'n paragraaf stel, heet die ___.","en":"The sentence that states the main idea of a paragraph is called the ___ (Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["kernsin"],"en":["topic sentence","kernsin","key sentence"]},"explain":{"af":"Die kernsin staan gewoonlik aan die begin van die paragraaf en sê waaroor die paragraaf gaan.","en":"The topic sentence usually stands at the start of the paragraph and says what the paragraph is about."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["slotsin","skakelwoord","inleiding"],"en":["concluding sentence","linking word","introduction"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die regte volgorde van die skryfproses?","en":"What is the correct order of the writing process?"},"options":[{"af":"Konsep → beplanning → proeflees → redigering → finale weergawe","en":"Draft → planning → proofreading → editing → final version"},{"af":"Beplanning → finale weergawe → konsep → redigering","en":"Planning → final version → draft → editing"},{"af":"Proeflees → beplanning → konsep → finale weergawe","en":"Proofreading → planning → draft → final version"},{"af":"Beplanning → konsep → redigering → proeflees → finale weergawe","en":"Planning → draft → editing → proofreading → final version"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Jy beplan eers, skryf dan 'n konsep, verbeter die inhoud en styl (redigering), soek die kleiner foute (proeflees) en lewer dan die finale weergawe.","en":"You plan first, then write a draft, improve the content and style (editing), look for the smaller errors (proofreading) and then hand in the final version."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Onderwerp: “Tieners behoort op 16 te mag stem. Oortuig jou lesers.” Watter opstelsoort word gevra?","en":"Topic: “Tieners behoort op 16 te mag stem. Oortuig jou lesers.” (Teenagers should be allowed to vote at 16. Convince your readers.) Which essay type is asked for?"},"options":[{"af":"Betogend","en":"Argumentative"},{"af":"Beredenerend","en":"Discursive"},{"af":"Beskrywend","en":"Descriptive"},{"af":"Verhalend","en":"Narrative"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Oortuig jou lesers* vra een standpunt met oortuigende argumente: 'n betogende opstel. Beredenerend sou albei kante bespreek.","en":"*Oortuig jou lesers* (convince your readers) asks for one standpoint with convincing arguments: an argumentative essay. Discursive would discuss both sides."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n beredenerende opstel gee jy net die argumente wat jou eie standpunt ondersteun.","en":"In a discursive essay you give only the arguments that support your own standpoint."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Beredenerende opstel bespreek albei kante gebalanseerd; jou eie mening kom eers in die gevolgtrekking. Net een kant is 'n betogende opstel.","en":"False. A discursive essay discusses both sides in a balanced way; your own opinion only comes in the conclusion. Only one side is an argumentative essay."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies 'n gepaste skakelwoord: “Die uitstappie na die Magaliesberg was duur. ___ was dit die moeite werd.”","en":"Choose a suitable linking word: “Die uitstappie na die Magaliesberg was duur. ___ was dit die moeite werd.” (The outing to the Magaliesberg was expensive. Nevertheless it was worth it.)"},"answers":{"af":["Nietemin","Tog","Nogtans"],"en":["Nietemin","Tog","Nogtans"]},"explain":{"af":"Die tweede sin stel 'n teenstelling (duur, maar die moeite werd), dus 'n kontrasskakelwoord: nietemin, tog of nogtans. Gevolglik en daarom wys 'n gevolg.","en":"The second sentence sets up a contrast (expensive, but worth it), so a contrast linking word: nietemin, tog or nogtans. Gevolglik and daarom show a consequence."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Gevolglik","Daarom","Eerstens"],"en":["Gevolglik","Daarom","Eerstens"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Korrigeer die anglisisme: “Ons het die bus gemis.” → “Ons het die bus ___.”","en":"Correct the anglicism: “Ons het die bus gemis.” (We missed the bus.) → “Ons het die bus ___.”"},"answers":{"af":["verpas"],"en":["verpas"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Bus, taxi of trein *verpas* jy. *Mis* in hierdie betekenis is 'n letterlike vertaling van die Engelse *miss*.","en":"You *verpas* a bus, taxi or train. *Mis* in this meaning is a literal translation of the English *miss*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gemis","verloor","vergeet"],"en":["gemis","verloor","vergeet"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inleiding begin IN MEDIAS RES?","en":"Which introduction starts IN MEDIAS RES?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek gaan vir julle vertel van my vakansie by die see.","en":"Ek gaan vir julle vertel van my vakansie by die see. (I am going to tell you about my holiday at the sea.)"},{"af":"Die tak kraak. Ek gryp na die tou, maar my hand gly ...","en":"Die tak kraak. Ek gryp na die tou, maar my hand gly ... (The branch cracks. I grab for the rope, but my hand slips ...)"},{"af":"Daar is baie soorte vakansies, en almal hou van vakansie.","en":"Daar is baie soorte vakansies, en almal hou van vakansie. (There are many kinds of holidays, and everyone likes holidays.)"},{"af":"Eendag, lank gelede, was daar 'n seun wat graag wou swem.","en":"Eendag, lank gelede, was daar 'n seun wat graag wou swem. (Once upon a time there was a boy who loved to swim.)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*In medias res* beteken jy begin midde-in die aksie. Die ander drie is 'n aankondiging, 'n vae algemene stelling en 'n kinderverhaal-cliché.","en":"*In medias res* means you start in the middle of the action. The other three are an announcement, a vague general statement and a children's-story cliché."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"“Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad.” is 'n voorbeeld van 'n ___ (letterlik uit Engels vertaal).","en":"“Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad.” is an example of an ___ (literally translated from English; Afrikaans term or English)."},"answers":{"af":["anglisisme"],"en":["anglicism","anglisisme"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit is 'n letterlike vertaling van *I had a good time*. Skryf eerder: *Ek het dit geniet* of *Ek het lekker gekuier*.","en":"It is a literal translation of *I had a good time*. Rather write: *Ek het dit geniet* or *Ek het lekker gekuier*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["idioom","eufemisme","spreekwoord"],"en":["idiom","euphemism","proverb"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin in 'n verhalende opstel bevat 'n FOUT met die tyd?","en":"Which sentence in a narrative essay contains a TENSE error?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek het die deur oopgemaak en die kamer binnegestap.","en":"Ek het die deur oopgemaak en die kamer binnegestap. (past + past)"},{"af":"Ek maak die deur oop en stap die kamer binne.","en":"Ek maak die deur oop en stap die kamer binne. (present + present)"},{"af":"Ek het die deur oopgemaak en ek stap die kamer binne.","en":"Ek het die deur oopgemaak en ek stap die kamer binne. (past + present)"},{"af":"Ons het gewag totdat die reën opgehou het.","en":"Ons het gewag totdat die reën opgehou het. (past + past)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die derde sin begin in die verlede tyd (*het oopgemaak*) en spring dan na die teenwoordige tyd (*stap*). Die ander sinne bly elk in een tyd.","en":"The third sentence starts in the past tense (*het oopgemaak*) and then jumps to the present (*stap*). The other sentences each stay in one tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die opstelonderwerp is 'n foto van 'n ou man wat alleen op 'n bankie by 'n bushalte sit. Wat is BELANGRIK?","en":"The essay topic is a photo of an old man sitting alone on a bench at a bus stop. What is IMPORTANT?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy moet die beskrywing van die foto as jou titel gebruik.","en":"You must use the description of the photo as your title."},{"af":"Jy moet 'n beskrywende opstel skryf.","en":"You must write a descriptive essay."},{"af":"Jy mag nie die man in die foto noem nie.","en":"You may not mention the man in the photo."},{"af":"Jy gee 'n eie titel, en die verband met die foto moet duidelik wees.","en":"You give your own title, and the link to the photo must be clear."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By beeldmateriaal kies jy self die opstelsoort en die titel, maar die nasiener moet die verband met die prent duidelik kan sien.","en":"With visual material you choose the essay type and the title yourself, but the marker must clearly see the link to the picture."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die inleiding: “Ek gaan vir julle vertel van die dag toe ons gaan visvang het. Dit was baie lekker.” Wat is die GROOTSTE probleem?","en":"Read the introduction: “Ek gaan vir julle vertel van die dag toe ons gaan visvang het. Dit was baie lekker.” (I am going to tell you about the day we went fishing. It was very nice.) What is the BIGGEST problem?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit kondig die onderwerp aan in plaas daarvan om die leser se aandag te gryp.","en":"It announces the topic instead of grabbing the reader's attention."},{"af":"Dit is te lank vir 'n inleiding.","en":"It is too long for an introduction."},{"af":"Dit is in die verlede tyd geskryf.","en":"It is written in the past tense."},{"af":"Dit bevat 'n retoriese vraag.","en":"It contains a rhetorical question."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Aankondiging (*Ek gaan vir julle vertel*) en 'n vae woord (*lekker*) maak die leser nie nuuskierig nie. Die verlede tyd is juis reg vir 'n verhaal, en daar is geen retoriese vraag nie.","en":"An announcement (*Ek gaan vir julle vertel*) and a vague word (*lekker*) do not make the reader curious. The past tense is in fact right for a story, and there is no rhetorical question."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter slot is die BESTE vir 'n verhaal wat begin het met “Die kano het gekantel”?","en":"Which ending is the BEST for a story that began with “Die kano het gekantel” (The canoe capsized)?"},"options":[{"af":"Toe word ek wakker en besef dit was alles 'n droom.","en":"Toe word ek wakker en besef dit was alles 'n droom. (Then I woke up and realised it was all a dream.)"},{"af":"Dit is die einde van my storie. Ek hoop julle het dit geniet.","en":"Dit is die einde van my storie. Ek hoop julle het dit geniet. (That is the end of my story. I hope you enjoyed it.)"},{"af":"Nou, elke keer as ek 'n kano op Harties sien, voel ek weer daardie koue water – en hou ek my boetie se hand 'n bietjie stywer vas.","en":"Nou, elke keer as ek 'n kano op Harties sien ... (Now, every time I see a canoe on Harties, I feel that cold water again – and I hold my brother's hand a little tighter.)"},{"af":"Daarna het ons huis toe gegaan en roomys geëet. Die volgende dag was Maandag.","en":"Daarna het ons huis toe gegaan en roomys geëet. Die volgende dag was Maandag. (Afterwards we went home and ate ice cream. The next day was Monday.)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beste slot verwys terug na die inleiding (die koue water) en wys wat die ervaring aan die verteller gedoen het. Die droom-einde is 'n cliché, die tweede is 'n aankondiging en die vierde eindig sonder enige betekenis of terugverwysing.","en":"The best ending refers back to the introduction (the cold water) and shows what the experience did to the narrator. The dream ending is a cliché, the second is an announcement and the fourth fizzles out without meaning."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Werkwoorde, sinsbou, opsomming, prosa en briewe","en":"Verbs, sentence structure, summary, prose and letters"},"topics":[{"id":"afr10-t2-werkwoorde","title":{"af":"Woordsoorte 2: werkwoorde, bywoorde, voorsetsels, voegwoorde, telwoorde en tussenwerpsels","en":"Parts of speech 2: verbs, adverbs, prepositions, conjunctions, numerals and interjections"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal werkwoorde, bywoorde, voorsetsels, voegwoorde, telwoorde en tussenwerpsels in 'n teks kan uitken en sinne met die regte woordorde kan verbind.","en":"You will be able to identify verbs, adverbs, prepositions, conjunctions, numerals and interjections in a text and join sentences with the correct word order."},"summary":{"af":"## Werkwoorde\n\n'n **Werkwoord** sê wat iemand doen, wat gebeur of in watter toestand iets is. Die **hoofwerkwoord** dra die betekenis; **hulpwerkwoorde** help die hoofwerkwoord.\n\n| Soort | Woorde | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hulpwerkwoord van tyd | het, sal | Ek **het** geëet. Ons **sal** wen. |\n| Modale hulpwerkwoord | kan, moet, wil, mag; verlede: kon, moes, wou, sou | Jy **moet** leer. Hy **kon** nie kom nie. |\n| Hulpwerkwoord van die lydende vorm | word (teenwoordig), is (verlede) | Die kos **word** gekook. Die venster **is** gebreek. |\n| Koppelwerkwoord | is, word, lyk, blyk, skyn, bly | Die kos **lyk** lekker. Sy **bly** kalm. |\n\n> **Wenk:** Volg daar 'n verlede deelwoord (ge-...) op *is* of *word*? Dan is dit 'n hulpwerkwoord van die lydende vorm (*Die venster is gebreek*). Volg daar 'n beskrywing? Dan is dit 'n koppelwerkwoord (*Hy is moeg*).\n\n- **Oorganklik** (neem 'n voorwerp): *Sy **lees** 'n boek.* **Onoorganklik** (geen voorwerp nie): *Die baba **slaap**.* Toets: vra *wat?* of *wie?* ná die werkwoord.\n- **Skeibare werkwoorde** skei in die sin: opstaan → *Ek staan vroeg op.* Verlede tyd: *Ek het vroeg op**ge**staan* (ge- in die middel). Infinitief: *om vroeg op te staan*. Die klem val op die eerste deel (OPstaan).\n- **Onskeibare werkwoorde** bly een woord: verstaan → *Ek verstaan dit. Ek het dit verstaan.*\n- **Infinitief:** ná *om ... te* en ná 'n modale hulpwerkwoord staan die hoofwerkwoord aan die einde: *Ek gaan Brits toe **om** skoene **te koop**. Ons **moet** vroeg **ry**.*\n- **Geen ge- nie:** werkwoorde met die onbeklemtoonde voorvoegsels **be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-** kry nie ge- in die verlede tyd nie: *besoek → het besoek, erken → het erken, gebruik → het gebruik, herhaal → het herhaal, ontmoet → het ontmoet, verstaan → het verstaan*.\n\n### Deelwoorde\n\n- **Teenwoordige (onvoltooide) deelwoord:** stam + *-ende*; die handeling is nog aan die gang: *'n lopende kraan, kokende water*.\n- **Verlede (voltooide) deelwoord:** *ge-* + stam + *-de/-te*; die handeling is klaar: *die gesteelde fiets, die gekookte eiers, die beplande uitstappie* (geen ge- nie, want be-).\n- **Sterk vorme** is ou vorme wat ons steeds as byvoeglike naamwoord gebruik: *'n gebroke hart, 'n gesonke skip, die verlore seun*. Let op: *'n gebreekte koppie* (letterlik) teenoor *'n gebroke hart* (figuurlik).\n\n## Bywoorde\n\n'n **Bywoord** sê meer oor die werkwoord (of oor 'n byvoeglike naamwoord of 'n ander bywoord).\n\n| Soort | Vraag | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tyd | Wanneer? | gister, môre, nou, altyd |\n| Plek | Waar? | hier, daar, buite |\n| Wyse | Hoe? | vinnig, stadig, hard |\n| Graad | Hoe erg? | baie, te, taamlik |\n| Modaliteit | Hoe seker? | miskien, beslis, waarskynlik |\n| Oorsaak/rede | Hoekom? | daarom, dus |\n\n> **Lokval:** *baie* is 'n bywoord van graad in *baie mooi*, maar 'n onbepaalde telwoord in *baie mense*. Kyk altyd na die funksie in die sin.\n\n## Voorsetsels en vaste verbindings\n\n'n **Voorsetsel** wys die verhouding tussen woorde (plek, tyd, rigting): *in, op, by, met, na, van, vir, aan, oor, onder, langs, sonder*. Sekere woorde vra 'n **vaste voorsetsel**, en dikwels nie die een wat Engels gebruik nie:\n\n| Afrikaans | Engels | Fout (anglisisme) |\n|---|---|---|\n| bang **vir** | afraid of | *bang van* |\n| trots **op** | proud of | *trots van* |\n| afhanklik **van** | dependent on | *afhanklik op* |\n| lief **vir** | fond of | *lief van* |\n| dink **aan** | think of | |\n| glo **in** | believe in | |\n| wag **vir** / wag **op** | wait for | |\n\n## Voegwoorde en woordorde\n\n| Groep | Voegwoorde | Woordorde | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | en, maar, of, want | geen verandering nie | Ek bly tuis, **want** ek **is** siek. |\n| 2 | dus, daarom, toe, anders | werkwoord kom direk ná die voegwoord | Ek is siek, **daarom bly** ek tuis. |\n| 3 (onderskikkend) | dat, omdat, as, toe, terwyl, hoewel, sodat, voordat, nadat, totdat, sodra, indien, of | werkwoord(e) na die einde van die bysin | Ek bly tuis **omdat** ek siek **is**. |\n\n- Begin die sin met die bysin, dan begin die hoofsin met die werkwoord: *Omdat ek siek is, **bly** ek tuis.*\n- In die verlede tyd staan *het* heel agter in die bysin: *... omdat ek laat **geslaap het**.*\n- *toe* in groep 2 beteken \"then\": *Ons het by die dam aangekom, toe begin dit reën.* *toe* in groep 3 beteken \"when\": *Toe ons by die dam aankom, het dit begin reën.*\n- *of* in groep 1 beteken \"or\"; *of* in groep 3 beteken \"whether\": *Ek wonder **of** hy kom.*\n\n## Telwoorde\n\n- **Hooftelwoorde** (hoeveel?): *een, twee, een-en-twintig* (met koppeltekens), *honderd*.\n- **Rangtelwoorde** (watter plek in 'n volgorde?): *eerste, tweede, derde, vierde, agtste, tiende, negentiende, twintigste, honderdste*. Tot negentien kry die meeste *-de*; vanaf twintig kry hulle *-ste*. Let op die uitsonderings *eerste, derde* en *agtste*.\n- **Onbepaalde telwoorde** (geen presiese getal nie): *baie, min, verskeie, enkele, sommige*.\n\n## Tussenwerpsels\n\nWoorde wat 'n gevoel of klank uitdruk, dikwels met 'n uitroepteken: *eina, sjoe, ag, hoera, foeitog, haai*. *Sjoe, dit was 'n spannende wedstryd!*\n\n> **Eksamenwenk:** Kyk by 'n onderstreepte woord wat dit in **daardie sin** doen. *bly* is 'n koppelwerkwoord in *Sy bly kalm*, maar 'n hoofwerkwoord in *Ons bly in Brits*.","en":"## Verbs\n\nA **verb** says what someone does, what happens or what state something is in. The **main verb** carries the meaning; **auxiliary verbs** help the main verb.\n\n| Kind | Words | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Auxiliary of tense | het, sal | Ek **het** geëet. Ons **sal** wen. |\n| Modal auxiliary | kan, moet, wil, mag; past: kon, moes, wou, sou | Jy **moet** leer. Hy **kon** nie kom nie. |\n| Auxiliary of the passive | word (present), is (past) | Die kos **word** gekook. Die venster **is** gebreek. |\n| Linking verb (copula) | is, word, lyk, blyk, skyn, bly | Die kos **lyk** lekker. Sy **bly** kalm. |\n\n> **Tip:** Is *is* or *word* followed by a past participle (ge-...)? Then it is an auxiliary of the passive (*Die venster is gebreek*). Is it followed by a description? Then it is a linking verb (*Hy is moeg*).\n\n- **Transitive** (takes an object): *Sy **lees** 'n boek.* **Intransitive** (no object): *Die baba **slaap**.* Test: ask *what?* or *whom?* after the verb.\n- **Separable verbs** split in the sentence: opstaan → *Ek staan vroeg op.* Past tense: *Ek het vroeg op**ge**staan* (ge- in the middle). Infinitive: *om vroeg op te staan*. The stress falls on the first part (OPstaan).\n- **Inseparable verbs** stay one word: verstaan → *Ek verstaan dit. Ek het dit verstaan.*\n- **Infinitive:** after *om ... te* and after a modal auxiliary the main verb goes to the end: *Ek gaan Brits toe **om** skoene **te koop**. Ons **moet** vroeg **ry**.*\n- **No ge-:** verbs with the unstressed prefixes **be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-** do not take ge- in the past tense: *besoek → het besoek, erken → het erken, gebruik → het gebruik, herhaal → het herhaal, ontmoet → het ontmoet, verstaan → het verstaan*.\n\n### Participles\n\n- **Present participle:** stem + *-ende*; the action is still going on: *'n lopende kraan, kokende water*.\n- **Past participle:** *ge-* + stem + *-de/-te*; the action is complete: *die gesteelde fiets, die gekookte eiers, die beplande uitstappie* (no ge-, because of be-).\n- **Strong forms** are old forms that we still use as adjectives: *'n gebroke hart, 'n gesonke skip, die verlore seun*. Note: *'n gebreekte koppie* (literal) versus *'n gebroke hart* (figurative).\n\n## Adverbs\n\nAn **adverb** tells us more about the verb (or about an adjective or another adverb).\n\n| Kind | Question | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| Time | When? | gister, môre, nou, altyd |\n| Place | Where? | hier, daar, buite |\n| Manner | How? | vinnig, stadig, hard |\n| Degree | To what extent? | baie, te, taamlik |\n| Modality | How certain? | miskien, beslis, waarskynlik |\n| Cause/reason | Why? | daarom, dus |\n\n> **Trap:** *baie* is an adverb of degree in *baie mooi*, but an indefinite numeral in *baie mense*. Always look at the function in the sentence.\n\n## Prepositions and fixed combinations\n\nA **preposition** shows the relationship between words (place, time, direction): *in, op, by, met, na, van, vir, aan, oor, onder, langs, sonder*. Some words take a **fixed preposition**, and often not the one English uses:\n\n| Afrikaans | English | Mistake (anglicism) |\n|---|---|---|\n| bang **vir** | afraid of | *bang van* |\n| trots **op** | proud of | *trots van* |\n| afhanklik **van** | dependent on | *afhanklik op* |\n| lief **vir** | fond of | *lief van* |\n| dink **aan** | think of | |\n| glo **in** | believe in | |\n| wag **vir** / wag **op** | wait for | |\n\n## Conjunctions and word order\n\n| Group | Conjunctions | Word order | Example |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | en, maar, of, want | no change | Ek bly tuis, **want** ek **is** siek. |\n| 2 | dus, daarom, toe, anders | the verb follows directly after the conjunction | Ek is siek, **daarom bly** ek tuis. |\n| 3 (subordinating) | dat, omdat, as, toe, terwyl, hoewel, sodat, voordat, nadat, totdat, sodra, indien, of | verb(s) move to the end of the subordinate clause | Ek bly tuis **omdat** ek siek **is**. |\n\n- If the sentence starts with the subordinate clause, the main clause starts with the verb: *Omdat ek siek is, **bly** ek tuis.*\n- In the past tense *het* goes right to the end of the subordinate clause: *... omdat ek laat **geslaap het**.*\n- *toe* in group 2 means \"then\": *Ons het by die dam aangekom, toe begin dit reën.* *toe* in group 3 means \"when\": *Toe ons by die dam aankom, het dit begin reën.*\n- *of* in group 1 means \"or\"; *of* in group 3 means \"whether\": *Ek wonder **of** hy kom.*\n\n## Numerals\n\n- **Cardinal numerals** (how many?): *een, twee, een-en-twintig* (with hyphens), *honderd*.\n- **Ordinal numerals** (which place in an order?): *eerste, tweede, derde, vierde, agtste, tiende, negentiende, twintigste, honderdste*. Up to nineteen most take *-de*; from twenty they take *-ste*. Note the exceptions *eerste, derde* and *agtste*.\n- **Indefinite numerals** (no exact number): *baie, min, verskeie, enkele, sommige*.\n\n## Interjections\n\nWords that express a feeling or a sound, often with an exclamation mark: *eina, sjoe, ag, hoera, foeitog, haai*. *Sjoe, dit was 'n spannende wedstryd!*\n\n> **Exam tip:** For an underlined word, look at what it does in **that sentence**. *bly* is a linking verb in *Sy bly kalm*, but a main verb in *Ons bly in Brits*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Hoofwerkwoord","en":"Main verb"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord wat die eintlike betekenis van die sin dra, bv. 'skoonmaak' in 'Hy sal sy kamer skoonmaak'.","en":"The verb that carries the actual meaning of the sentence, e.g. 'skoonmaak' in 'Hy sal sy kamer skoonmaak'."}},{"term":{"af":"Koppelwerkwoord","en":"Linking verb (copula)"},"def":{"af":"'n Werkwoord wat die onderwerp aan 'n beskrywing koppel: is, word, lyk, blyk, skyn, bly.","en":"A verb that links the subject to a description: is, word, lyk, blyk, skyn, bly."}},{"term":{"af":"Modale hulpwerkwoord","en":"Modal auxiliary verb"},"def":{"af":"'n Hulpwerkwoord wat moontlikheid, noodsaaklikheid, wil of toestemming uitdruk: kan, moet, wil, mag (verlede: kon, moes, wou, sou).","en":"An auxiliary that expresses possibility, necessity, will or permission: kan, moet, wil, mag (past: kon, moes, wou, sou)."}},{"term":{"af":"Skeibare werkwoord","en":"Separable verb"},"def":{"af":"'n Werkwoord wat in die sin skei, met die klem op die eerste deel: opstaan → Ek staan op; het opgestaan.","en":"A verb that splits in the sentence, with the stress on the first part: opstaan → Ek staan op; het opgestaan."}},{"term":{"af":"Verlede (voltooide) deelwoord","en":"Past participle"},"def":{"af":"Die ge-vorm van die werkwoord wat 'n voltooide handeling aandui en as byvoeglike naamwoord kan dien: die gesteelde fiets, 'n gesonke skip.","en":"The ge- form of the verb that shows a completed action and can act as an adjective: die gesteelde fiets, 'n gesonke skip."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord","en":"Adverb"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat meer sê oor die werkwoord: tyd, plek, wyse, graad, modaliteit of oorsaak.","en":"A word that says more about the verb: time, place, manner, degree, modality or cause."}},{"term":{"af":"Vaste verbinding","en":"Fixed combination (fixed preposition)"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat altyd 'n bepaalde voorsetsel neem, bv. trots op, bang vir, afhanklik van.","en":"A word that always takes a specific preposition, e.g. trots op, bang vir, afhanklik van."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderskikkende voegwoord","en":"Subordinating conjunction"},"def":{"af":"'n Voegwoord wat 'n bysin inlei en die werkwoord na die einde van die bysin stuur: omdat, dat, toe, terwyl, sodat.","en":"A conjunction that introduces a subordinate clause and sends the verb to the end of the clause: omdat, dat, toe, terwyl, sodat."}},{"term":{"af":"Rangtelwoord","en":"Ordinal numeral"},"def":{"af":"'n Telwoord wat 'n plek in 'n volgorde aandui: eerste, derde, agtste, twintigste.","en":"A numeral that indicates a place in an order: eerste, derde, agtste, twintigste."}},{"term":{"af":"Tussenwerpsel","en":"Interjection"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat 'n gevoel of klank uitdruk en los van die sin staan: eina, sjoe, ag, hoera.","en":"A word that expresses a feeling or sound and stands apart from the sentence: eina, sjoe, ag, hoera."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Woordsoorte in 'n advertensie","en":"Parts of speech in an advert"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die advertensie (eie teks) en benoem die woordsoort van elke vet woord.\n\n**Sjoe!** Jou **eerste** maand by FiksPlek Brits is gratis! Ons gimnasium is **langs** die taxi-staanplek. Oefen **terwyl** jy na jou gunstelingmusiek luister, en jy **sal** **beslis** fiks word. Sluit vandag aan!","en":"Read the advert (our own text) and name the part of speech of each bold word.\n\n**Sjoe!** Jou **eerste** maand by FiksPlek Brits is gratis! Ons gimnasium is **langs** die taxi-staanplek. Oefen **terwyl** jy na jou gunstelingmusiek luister, en jy **sal** **beslis** fiks word. Sluit vandag aan!\n\n(Translation: Wow! Your first month at FiksPlek Brits is free! Our gym is next to the taxi rank. Train while you listen to your favourite music, and you will definitely get fit. Join today!)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Sjoe** = tussenwerpsel. Dit druk verbasing uit, staan los van die sin en het 'n uitroepteken.","en":"**Sjoe** = interjection. It expresses surprise, stands apart from the sentence and has an exclamation mark."},{"af":"**eerste** = rangtelwoord. Dit sê watter plek in 'n volgorde (nie hoeveel nie). **langs** = voorsetsel. Dit wys die plekverhouding tussen die gimnasium en die taxi-staanplek.","en":"**eerste** = ordinal numeral. It says which place in an order (not how many). **langs** = preposition. It shows the place relationship between the gym and the taxi rank."},{"af":"**terwyl** = onderskikkende voegwoord. Bewys: die werkwoord *luister* staan aan die einde van die bysin.","en":"**terwyl** = subordinating conjunction. Proof: the verb *luister* is at the end of the subordinate clause."},{"af":"**sal** = hulpwerkwoord van tyd (toekomende tyd); dit help die koppelwerkwoord *word*. **beslis** = bywoord van modaliteit: dit sê hoe séker die skrywer is.","en":"**sal** = auxiliary of tense (future tense); it helps the linking verb *word*. **beslis** = adverb of modality: it says how certain the writer is."}],"answer":{"af":"Sjoe – tussenwerpsel; eerste – rangtelwoord; langs – voorsetsel; terwyl – onderskikkende voegwoord; sal – hulpwerkwoord van tyd; beslis – bywoord van modaliteit.","en":"Sjoe – interjection; eerste – ordinal numeral; langs – preposition; terwyl – subordinating conjunction; sal – auxiliary of tense; beslis – adverb of modality."}},{"title":{"af":"Sinne verbind met voegwoorde","en":"Joining sentences with conjunctions"},"problem":{"af":"Verbind die sinne met die voegwoord tussen hakies. Let op die woordorde.\n\n(a) Ek bly tuis. Ek is siek. (omdat)\n(b) Ek is siek. Ek bly tuis. (daarom)\n(c) Die krag het afgegaan. Ons het kerse aangesteek. (Begin met: Toe)\n(d) Ons ry vroeg. Ons kan die verkeer op die N4 vermy. (sodat)","en":"Join the sentences with the conjunction in brackets. Pay attention to the word order.\n\n(a) Ek bly tuis. Ek is siek. (omdat)\n(b) Ek is siek. Ek bly tuis. (daarom)\n(c) Die krag het afgegaan. Ons het kerse aangesteek. (Start with: Toe)\n(d) Ons ry vroeg. Ons kan die verkeer op die N4 vermy. (sodat)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *omdat* is onderskikkend (groep 3), dus skuif die werkwoord *is* na die einde: Ek bly tuis omdat ek siek **is**.","en":"(a) *omdat* is subordinating (group 3), so the verb *is* moves to the end: Ek bly tuis omdat ek siek **is**."},{"af":"(b) *daarom* is groep 2, dus kom die werkwoord direk daarna, voor die onderwerp: Ek is siek, daarom **bly ek** tuis.","en":"(b) *daarom* is group 2, so the verb comes directly after it, before the subject: Ek is siek, daarom **bly ek** tuis."},{"af":"(c) *toe* (wanneer) lei hier 'n bysin in: *het* skuif na die einde van die bysin, en die hoofsin begin met die werkwoord: Toe die krag afgegaan **het**, **het ons** kerse aangesteek.","en":"(c) *toe* (when) introduces a subordinate clause here: *het* moves to the end of the clause, and the main clause starts with the verb: Toe die krag afgegaan **het**, **het ons** kerse aangesteek."},{"af":"(d) *sodat* is onderskikkend: albei werkwoorde gaan na die einde, die modale werkwoord eerste: Ons ry vroeg sodat ons die verkeer op die N4 **kan vermy**.","en":"(d) *sodat* is subordinating: both verbs go to the end, the modal verb first: Ons ry vroeg sodat ons die verkeer op die N4 **kan vermy**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ek bly tuis omdat ek siek is. (b) Ek is siek, daarom bly ek tuis. (c) Toe die krag afgegaan het, het ons kerse aangesteek. (d) Ons ry vroeg sodat ons die verkeer op die N4 kan vermy.","en":"(a) Ek bly tuis omdat ek siek is. (b) Ek is siek, daarom bly ek tuis. (c) Toe die krag afgegaan het, het ons kerse aangesteek. (d) Ons ry vroeg sodat ons die verkeer op die N4 kan vermy."}},{"title":{"af":"Die regte voorsetsel","en":"The correct preposition"},"problem":{"af":"Vul die korrekte voorsetsel in.\n\n(a) Die sitrusboere is afhanklik ___ goeie reën.\n(b) Ons is trots ___ ons rugbyspan.\n(c) My boetie is bang ___ die donker tydens beurtkrag.\n(d) Ek dink gedurig ___ my ouma in Pretoria.","en":"Fill in the correct preposition.\n\n(a) Die sitrusboere is afhanklik ___ goeie reën. (The citrus farmers depend on good rain.)\n(b) Ons is trots ___ ons rugbyspan. (We are proud of our rugby team.)\n(c) My boetie is bang ___ die donker tydens beurtkrag. (My little brother is afraid of the dark during load-shedding.)\n(d) Ek dink gedurig ___ my ouma in Pretoria. (I keep thinking of my grandma in Pretoria.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) afhanklik **van**. Engels sê *dependent on*, maar 'afhanklik op' is 'n anglisisme.","en":"(a) afhanklik **van**. English says *dependent on*, but 'afhanklik op' is an anglicism."},{"af":"(b) trots **op**. Engels sê *proud of*, maar 'trots van' is verkeerd.","en":"(b) trots **op**. English says *proud of*, but 'trots van' is wrong."},{"af":"(c) bang **vir**. Moenie die Engelse *of* letterlik vertaal nie.","en":"(c) bang **vir**. Do not translate the English *of* literally."},{"af":"(d) dink **aan**: as jy aan iemand dink, sê jy *dink aan*.","en":"(d) dink **aan**: when you think of someone, you say *dink aan*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) van (b) op (c) vir (d) aan","en":"(a) van (b) op (c) vir (d) aan"}},{"title":{"af":"Deelwoorde en modale hulpwerkwoorde","en":"Participles and modal auxiliaries"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Gebruik die verlede deelwoord van *steel* as byvoeglike naamwoord: Die polisie het die ___ fiets naby die myn gevind.\n(b) Gebruik die teenwoordige deelwoord van *loop*: Hy het die ___ kraan toegedraai.\n(c) Gebruik die sterk vorm van die verlede deelwoord van *sink*: Duikers het die ___ skip ondersoek.\n(d) Herskryf met *moet* en daarna in die verlede tyd: Fietsryers dra 'n helm.","en":"(a) Use the past participle of *steel* (steal) as an adjective: Die polisie het die ___ fiets naby die myn gevind.\n(b) Use the present participle of *loop* (run): Hy het die ___ kraan toegedraai.\n(c) Use the strong form of the past participle of *sink*: Duikers het die ___ skip ondersoek.\n(d) Rewrite with *moet* and then in the past tense: Fietsryers dra 'n helm. (Cyclists wear a helmet.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die fiets is klaar gesteel, dus verlede deelwoord: ge- + steel + -de = **gesteelde**.","en":"(a) The bicycle has already been stolen, so past participle: ge- + steel + -de = **gesteelde**."},{"af":"(b) Die water loop nog, dus teenwoordige deelwoord: loop + -ende = **lopende**.","en":"(b) The water is still running, so present participle: loop + -ende = **lopende**."},{"af":"(c) Die sterk vorm van *gesink* is **gesonke**: 'n gesonke skip.","en":"(c) The strong form of *gesink* is **gesonke**: 'n gesonke skip."},{"af":"(d) Die modale werkwoord staan op plek 2 en die hoofwerkwoord skuif na die einde: Fietsryers **moet** 'n helm **dra**. Verlede tyd: moet → moes: Fietsryers **moes** 'n helm dra.","en":"(d) The modal verb stands in position 2 and the main verb moves to the end: Fietsryers **moet** 'n helm **dra**. Past tense: moet → moes: Fietsryers **moes** 'n helm dra."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) gesteelde (b) lopende (c) gesonke (d) Fietsryers moet 'n helm dra. / Fietsryers moes 'n helm dra.","en":"(a) gesteelde (b) lopende (c) gesonke (d) Fietsryers moet 'n helm dra. / Fietsryers moes 'n helm dra."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is 'n **koppelwerkwoord**?","en":"Which word is a **linking verb**?"},"options":[{"af":"loop","en":"loop"},{"af":"sal","en":"sal"},{"af":"lyk","en":"lyk"},{"af":"vinnig","en":"vinnig"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'lyk' koppel die onderwerp aan 'n beskrywing (Die kos lyk lekker). 'loop' is 'n hoofwerkwoord, 'sal' 'n hulpwerkwoord van tyd en 'vinnig' 'n bywoord van wyse.","en":"'lyk' links the subject to a description (Die kos lyk lekker). 'loop' is a main verb, 'sal' an auxiliary of tense and 'vinnig' an adverb of manner."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruik die rangtelwoord van *agt*: Ons huis is die ___ huis in die straat.","en":"Use the ordinal numeral of *agt* (eight): Ons huis is die ___ huis in die straat."},"answers":{"af":["agtste"],"en":["agtste"]},"explain":{"af":"agt → agtste. Dit is een van die uitsonderings: die meeste rangtelwoorde tot negentien kry -de (vierde, sewende), maar agt kry -ste.","en":"agt → agtste. It is one of the exceptions: most ordinals up to nineteen take -de (vierde, sewende), but agt takes -ste."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["agste","agtde","agtiende"],"en":["agste","agtde","agtiende"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke bywoord by die soort bywoord.","en":"Match each adverb to the kind of adverb."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"'gister' in: Ons het gister gespeel.","en":"'gister' in: Ons het gister gespeel."},"r":{"af":"Bywoord van tyd","en":"Adverb of time"}},{"l":{"af":"'hier' in: Wag hier vir my.","en":"'hier' in: Wag hier vir my."},"r":{"af":"Bywoord van plek","en":"Adverb of place"}},{"l":{"af":"'vinnig' in: Die taxi ry vinnig.","en":"'vinnig' in: Die taxi ry vinnig."},"r":{"af":"Bywoord van wyse","en":"Adverb of manner"}},{"l":{"af":"'te' in: Die toets was te moeilik.","en":"'te' in: Die toets was te moeilik."},"r":{"af":"Bywoord van graad","en":"Adverb of degree"}},{"l":{"af":"'miskien' in: Dit sal miskien reën.","en":"'miskien' in: Dit sal miskien reën."},"r":{"af":"Bywoord van modaliteit","en":"Adverb of modality"}}],"explain":{"af":"Vra die regte vraag: wanneer? (tyd), waar? (plek), hoe? (wyse), hoe erg? (graad), hoe seker? (modaliteit).","en":"Ask the right question: when? (time), where? (place), how? (manner), to what extent? (degree), how certain? (modality)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'Verstaan' is 'n onskeibare werkwoord: ons sê 'Ek verstaan die werk' en 'Ek het die werk verstaan'.","en":"'Verstaan' is an inseparable verb: we say 'Ek verstaan die werk' and 'Ek het die werk verstaan'."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die werkwoord skei nooit nie, en omdat dit met die onbeklemtoonde ver- begin, kry dit ook nie ge- in die verlede tyd nie.","en":"True. The verb never splits, and because it starts with the unstressed ver-, it also does not take ge- in the past tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die advertensie 'Jy sal ons nuwe pizza BESLIS geniet!' is die woord in hoofletters 'n ...","en":"In the advert 'Jy sal ons nuwe pizza BESLIS geniet!' the word in capitals is a(n) ..."},"options":[{"af":"byvoeglike naamwoord","en":"adjective"},{"af":"bywoord van modaliteit","en":"adverb of modality"},{"af":"voorsetsel","en":"preposition"},{"af":"hulpwerkwoord","en":"auxiliary verb"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'beslis' sê hoe séker die spreker is dat jy die pizza sal geniet. Dit beskryf die handeling (geniet), nie die pizza nie, dus is dit nie 'n byvoeglike naamwoord nie.","en":"'beslis' says how certain the speaker is that you will enjoy the pizza. It describes the action (geniet), not the pizza, so it is not an adjective."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die korrekte voorsetsel in: Ons is almal baie trots ___ ons rugbyspan.","en":"Fill in the correct preposition: Ons is almal baie trots ___ ons rugbyspan."},"answers":{"af":["op"],"en":["op"]},"explain":{"af":"Die vaste verbinding is *trots op*. 'trots van' is 'n anglisisme (Engels: proud of).","en":"The fixed combination is *trots op*. 'trots van' is an anglicism (English: proud of)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["van","met","aan"],"en":["van","met","aan"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die korrekte voorsetsel: Die sitrusboere rondom Brits is afhanklik ___ goeie reën.","en":"Choose the correct preposition: Die sitrusboere rondom Brits is afhanklik ___ goeie reën."},"options":[{"af":"op","en":"op"},{"af":"aan","en":"aan"},{"af":"met","en":"met"},{"af":"van","en":"van"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In Afrikaans is jy *afhanklik van* iets. 'afhanklik op' kom van die Engelse 'dependent on' en is 'n anglisisme.","en":"In Afrikaans you are *afhanklik van* something. 'afhanklik op' comes from the English 'dependent on' and is an anglicism."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: 'Ek trek my skoene aan.' → Ek het my skoene ___.","en":"Write in the past tense: 'Ek trek my skoene aan.' → Ek het my skoene ___."},"answers":{"af":["aangetrek"],"en":["aangetrek"]},"explain":{"af":"*aantrek* is skeibaar (AANtrek), dus kom ge- in die middel: aan-ge-trek. 'geaantrek' is 'n algemene fout.","en":"*aantrek* is separable (AANtrek), so ge- goes in the middle: aan-ge-trek. 'geaantrek' is a common mistake."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["geaantrek","aantrek","aangetrekte"],"en":["geaantrek","aantrek","aangetrekte"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Werkwoorde wat met ver- begin, kry ge- in die verlede tyd, dus is dit korrek: 'Hy het sy fiets geverkoop.'","en":"Verbs that start with ver- take ge- in the past tense, so this is correct: 'Hy het sy fiets geverkoop.'"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Werkwoorde met be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont- en ver- kry nie ge- nie: 'Hy het sy fiets verkoop.'","en":"False. Verbs with be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont- and ver- do not take ge-: 'Hy het sy fiets verkoop.'"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Verbind die sinne met *omdat*: 'Ek is moeg. Ek het laat geslaap.'","en":"Join the sentences with *omdat*: 'Ek is moeg. Ek het laat geslaap.'"},"options":[{"af":"Ek is moeg omdat ek laat geslaap het.","en":"Ek is moeg omdat ek laat geslaap het."},{"af":"Ek is moeg omdat ek het laat geslaap.","en":"Ek is moeg omdat ek het laat geslaap."},{"af":"Ek is moeg omdat het ek laat geslaap.","en":"Ek is moeg omdat het ek laat geslaap."},{"af":"Ek is moeg, omdat laat ek geslaap het.","en":"Ek is moeg, omdat laat ek geslaap het."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*omdat* is onderskikkend: die vervoegde werkwoord *het* skuif heel agter, ná die deelwoord: ... omdat ek laat geslaap het.","en":"*omdat* is subordinating: the finite verb *het* moves right to the end, after the participle: ... omdat ek laat geslaap het."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Verbind met *daarom*: 'Dit reën. Ons bly binne.' → Dit reën, daarom ___ binne.","en":"Join with *daarom*: 'Dit reën. Ons bly binne.' → Dit reën, daarom ___ binne."},"answers":{"af":["bly ons"],"en":["bly ons"]},"explain":{"af":"*daarom* is 'n groep 2-voegwoord: die werkwoord kom direk daarna en dan die onderwerp (inversie): daarom bly ons binne.","en":"*daarom* is a group 2 conjunction: the verb follows directly and then the subject (inversion): daarom bly ons binne."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ons bly","ons het gebly","is ons"],"en":["ons bly","ons het gebly","is ons"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruik die verlede deelwoord van *kook* as byvoeglike naamwoord: Ek eet graag ___ eiers vir ontbyt.","en":"Use the past participle of *kook* (boil) as an adjective: Ek eet graag ___ eiers vir ontbyt."},"answers":{"af":["gekookte"],"en":["gekookte"]},"explain":{"af":"ge- + kook + -te = gekookte. Voor 'n naamwoord kry die deelwoord die uitgang -te/-de. 'kokende' is die teenwoordige deelwoord (die eiers kook nog).","en":"ge- + kook + -te = gekookte. Before a noun the participle takes the ending -te/-de. 'kokende' is the present participle (the eggs are still boiling)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gekookde","gekook","kokende"],"en":["gekookde","gekook","kokende"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is *is* 'n hulpwerkwoord van die lydende vorm?","en":"In which sentence is *is* an auxiliary of the passive voice?"},"options":[{"af":"My broer is baie lank.","en":"My broer is baie lank."},{"af":"Die kos is koud.","en":"Die kos is koud."},{"af":"Ons is in Graad 10.","en":"Ons is in Graad 10."},{"af":"Die venster is gisteraand gebreek.","en":"Die venster is gisteraand gebreek."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Net in die laaste sin volg 'n verlede deelwoord (gebreek): iemand het die venster gebreek. In die ander sinne koppel *is* die onderwerp aan 'n beskrywing, dus is dit 'n koppelwerkwoord.","en":"Only in the last sentence is it followed by a past participle (gebreek): someone broke the window. In the other sentences *is* links the subject to a description, so it is a linking verb."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Herskryf met die modale hulpwerkwoord *moet*: 'Ons ry môre vroeg Pretoria toe.'","en":"Rewrite with the modal auxiliary *moet*: 'Ons ry môre vroeg Pretoria toe.'"},"options":[{"af":"Ons ry moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe.","en":"Ons ry moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe."},{"af":"Ons moet ry môre vroeg Pretoria toe.","en":"Ons moet ry môre vroeg Pretoria toe."},{"af":"Ons moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe ry.","en":"Ons moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe ry."},{"af":"Ons moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe gery.","en":"Ons moet môre vroeg Pretoria toe gery."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die modale werkwoord *moet* neem plek 2 in, en die hoofwerkwoord *ry* skuif as infinitief na die einde – sonder ge-.","en":"The modal verb *moet* takes position 2, and the main verb *ry* moves to the end as an infinitive – without ge-."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woordsoort is *toe* in: 'Toe die krag afgaan, het ons kerse aangesteek.'?","en":"Which part of speech is *toe* in: 'Toe die krag afgaan, het ons kerse aangesteek.'?"},"options":[{"af":"Onderskikkende voegwoord","en":"Subordinating conjunction"},{"af":"Voorsetsel","en":"Preposition"},{"af":"Bywoord van plek","en":"Adverb of place"},{"af":"Groep 1-voegwoord (geen inversie nie)","en":"Group 1 conjunction (no inversion)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*toe* beteken hier 'wanneer' en lei 'n bysin in: die werkwoord *afgaan* staan aan die einde van die bysin, en die hoofsin begin met die werkwoord *het*. Dit is die kenmerke van 'n onderskikkende voegwoord.","en":"*toe* means 'when' here and introduces a subordinate clause: the verb *afgaan* is at the end of the clause, and the main clause starts with the verb *het*. These are the features of a subordinating conjunction."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is heeltemal KORREK?","en":"Which sentence is completely CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek is bang van die donker, daarom ek slaap met 'n lig aan.","en":"Ek is bang van die donker, daarom ek slaap met 'n lig aan."},{"af":"Ek gaan nie die partytjie bywoon nie, want ek moet vir my eksamen leer.","en":"Ek gaan nie die partytjie bywoon nie, want ek moet vir my eksamen leer."},{"af":"Hy is afhanklik op sy ouers, want hy werk nog nie.","en":"Hy is afhanklik op sy ouers, want hy werk nog nie."},{"af":"Ek gaan nie die partytjie bywoon nie, omdat ek moet vir my eksamen leer.","en":"Ek gaan nie die partytjie bywoon nie, omdat ek moet vir my eksamen leer."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Na *want* (groep 1) bly die woordorde normaal. Die ander sinne het foute: 'bang van' (moet 'bang vir' wees) en 'daarom ek slaap' (moet 'daarom slaap ek' wees); 'afhanklik op' (moet 'afhanklik van' wees); ná *omdat* moet die werkwoorde na die einde skuif: '... omdat ek vir my eksamen moet leer'.","en":"After *want* (group 1) the word order stays normal. The other sentences have errors: 'bang van' (should be 'bang vir') and 'daarom ek slaap' (should be 'daarom slaap ek'); 'afhanklik op' (should be 'afhanklik van'); after *omdat* the verbs must move to the end: '... omdat ek vir my eksamen moet leer'."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t2-sinsbou-tye","title":{"af":"Sinsbou, woordorde, tye en ontkenning","en":"Sentence structure, word order, tenses and negation"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinsdele en sinsoorte kan benoem, die STOMPI-woordorde kan toepas en sinne korrek na 'n ander tyd of na die ontkennende vorm kan verander.","en":"You will be able to name sentence parts and sentence types, apply the STOMPI word order and correctly change sentences to another tense or to the negative form."},"summary":{"af":"## Sinsdele\n\n| Sinsdeel | Vraag | *Ma het my gister 'n nuwe selfoon gegee.* |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Onderwerp** | Wie of wat doen die handeling? | Ma |\n| **Gesegde** | Watter werkwoorde? (die werkwoordelike deel) | het ... gegee |\n| **Direkte voorwerp** | Wat of wie ondergaan die handeling? | 'n nuwe selfoon |\n| **Indirekte voorwerp** | Aan of vir wie? | my |\n| **Bepaling** | Wanneer, waar, hoe, hoekom? | gister (bepaling van tyd) |\n\n> **Wenk:** Die onderwerp is nie altyd die eerste woord nie. In *Gister het my broer 'n bal gekoop* is *my broer* die onderwerp. Vra: Wie het gekoop?\n\n## Sinsoorte\n\n- **Stelsin:** gee inligting en eindig met 'n punt: *Die taxi is laat.*\n- **Vraagsin:** vra iets en eindig met 'n vraagteken: *Is die taxi laat?*\n- **Bevelsin:** gee 'n opdrag; die werkwoord staan eerste: *Maak die deur toe.*\n- **Uitroepsin:** druk sterk gevoel uit, met 'n uitroepteken: *Wat 'n wedstryd!*\n\n'n **Enkelvoudige sin** het een hoofsin met een gesegde: *Ons speel Saterdag rugby.*\n\n'n **Saamgestelde sin** bestaan uit twee of meer sinne wat verbind is:\n\n- **Neweskikkend** (hoofsin + hoofsin; sommige boeke sê *veelvoudige sin*): met *en, maar, of, want, dus, daarom*: *Ek het hard geleer, maar die toets was moeilik.*\n- **Onderskikkend** (hoofsin + bysin; sommige boeke sê *komplekse sin*): met *omdat, dat, toe, as, terwyl, sodat* ens. Die werkwoord staan aan die einde van die bysin: *Ek is moeg omdat ek laat geslaap het.*\n\n## Woordorde: die STOMPI-reël\n\n| S (subjek) | W1 | T (tyd) | O (objek) | M (manier) | P (plek) | I (infinitief / W2) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ek | ry | môre | | met die taxi | na Brits | om skoene te koop |\n| Ons | sal | Saterdag | die vleis | stadig | by die dam | braai |\n\n- **Werkwoord 1** (die vervoegde werkwoord) staan in 'n stelsin altyd op die **tweede plek**.\n- **Werkwoord 2** (infinitief of deelwoord) staan heel agter: *Ons **sal** Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam **braai**.*\n- **Inversie:** begin die sin met iets anders as die onderwerp (tyd, plek of 'n bysin), dan kom werkwoord 1 tweede en die onderwerp direk daarna: *Môre **ry ek** met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.* *Omdat dit reën, **bly ons** binne.*\n- **Vraagsin:** met inversie (werkwoord eerste): *Gaan jy saam?* Of met 'n vraagwoord en dan inversie: *Waar gaan jy? Wanneer begin die eksamen?*\n\n## Tye\n\n| | Teenwoordige tyd | Verlede tyd | Toekomende tyd |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| gewone werkwoord | Hy eet. | Hy het geëet. | Hy sal eet. |\n| is | Sy is moeg. | Sy was moeg. | Sy sal moeg wees. |\n| het | Ek het 'n hond. | Ek het 'n hond gehad. | Ek sal 'n hond hê. |\n\n- **Verlede tyd:** *het* + *ge-* + stam; die deelwoord skuif na die einde: *Ons speel rugby → Ons het rugby gespeel.*\n- **Modale werkwoorde** het 'n eie verlede vorm: **kan → kon, moet → moes, wil → wou, sal → sou**. Nooit *het gekan* nie.\n- **Skeibare werkwoorde:** ge- in die middel: *Ek staan op → Ek het opgestaan.*\n- **Geen ge- nie** by be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-: *Ons besoek Ouma → Ons het Ouma besoek.*\n- **Twee werkwoorde ná *het*:** geen ge- nie: *Ek gaan swem → Ek het gaan swem.*\n- **In 'n bysin** staan *het* heel agter: *... omdat hy laat gekom **het**.*\n- **Toekomende tyd:** *sal* op plek 2 en die infinitief aan die einde: *Hy sal môre eet.*\n\n## Ontkenning\n\n- Afrikaans gebruik die **dubbele ontkenning**: die eerste *nie* kom ná die werkwoord en die tweede *nie* aan die einde van die sin: *Hy kom nie vandag nie.*\n- As die eerste *nie* reeds die laaste woord is, skryf jy net een *nie*: *Hy kom nie. Ek weet nie.*\n\n| Positief | Negatief |\n|---|---|\n| iemand | niemand ... nie |\n| iets | niks ... nie |\n| altyd | nooit ... nie |\n| êrens | nêrens ... nie |\n| 'n | geen ... nie (of nie 'n ... nie) |\n| al | nog nie ... nie |\n| nog | nie meer ... nie |\n| ook | ook nie ... nie |\n\n- *Iemand het gebel → Niemand het gebel nie.* *Sy het al geëet → Sy het nog nie geëet nie.* *Hy speel nog rugby → Hy speel nie meer rugby nie.*\n- **Bevelsin:** *Moenie ... nie!* Die skeibare werkwoord word weer een woord: *Skakel die TV af! → Moenie die TV afskakel nie!*\n\n> **Wenk:** *Jy moet kom* het twee ontkennings met verskillende betekenisse: *Jy moet nie kom nie* (dit is verbode) en *Jy hoef nie te kom nie* (dit is nie nodig nie).\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Geen inversie ná 'n tydsbepaling nie: *Môre ek gaan* (fout) → *Môre gaan ek.*\n- Die tweede *nie* vergeet.\n- *het* op die verkeerde plek in 'n bysin: *omdat hy het gekom* → *omdat hy gekom het*.\n- *het gekan, het gemoet* in plaas van *kon, moes*.","en":"## Parts of the sentence\n\n| Sentence part | Question | *Ma het my gister 'n nuwe selfoon gegee.* |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Subject** | Who or what does the action? | Ma |\n| **Predicate (verb part)** | Which verbs? | het ... gegee |\n| **Direct object** | What or who undergoes the action? | 'n nuwe selfoon |\n| **Indirect object** | To or for whom? | my |\n| **Adjunct** | When, where, how, why? | gister (adjunct of time) |\n\n> **Tip:** The subject is not always the first word. In *Gister het my broer 'n bal gekoop* the subject is *my broer*. Ask: Who bought?\n\n## Sentence types\n\n- **Statement:** gives information and ends with a full stop: *Die taxi is laat.*\n- **Question:** asks something and ends with a question mark: *Is die taxi laat?*\n- **Command:** gives an instruction; the verb comes first: *Maak die deur toe.*\n- **Exclamation:** expresses strong feeling, with an exclamation mark: *Wat 'n wedstryd!*\n\nA **simple sentence** has one main clause with one predicate: *Ons speel Saterdag rugby.*\n\nA **compound/complex sentence** (saamgestelde sin) consists of two or more joined clauses:\n\n- **Coordinate** (main clause + main clause; some books say *veelvoudige sin* – compound sentence): with *en, maar, of, want, dus, daarom*: *Ek het hard geleer, maar die toets was moeilik.*\n- **Subordinate** (main clause + subordinate clause; some books say *komplekse sin* – complex sentence): with *omdat, dat, toe, as, terwyl, sodat* etc. The verb goes to the end of the subordinate clause: *Ek is moeg omdat ek laat geslaap het.*\n\n## Word order: the STOMPI rule\n\n| S (subject) | V1 | T (time) | O (object) | M (manner) | P (place) | I (infinitive / V2) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ek | ry | môre | | met die taxi | na Brits | om skoene te koop |\n| Ons | sal | Saterdag | die vleis | stadig | by die dam | braai |\n\n- **Verb 1** (the finite verb) always stands in **second position** in a statement.\n- **Verb 2** (infinitive or participle) goes right to the end: *Ons **sal** Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam **braai**.*\n- **Inversion:** if the sentence starts with something other than the subject (time, place or a subordinate clause), verb 1 comes second and the subject directly after it: *Môre **ry ek** met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.* *Omdat dit reën, **bly ons** binne.*\n- **Questions:** with inversion (verb first): *Gaan jy saam?* Or with a question word followed by inversion: *Waar gaan jy? Wanneer begin die eksamen?*\n\n## Tenses\n\n| | Present | Past | Future |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ordinary verb | Hy eet. | Hy het geëet. | Hy sal eet. |\n| is | Sy is moeg. | Sy was moeg. | Sy sal moeg wees. |\n| het | Ek het 'n hond. | Ek het 'n hond gehad. | Ek sal 'n hond hê. |\n\n- **Past tense:** *het* + *ge-* + stem; the participle moves to the end: *Ons speel rugby → Ons het rugby gespeel.*\n- **Modal verbs** have their own past form: **kan → kon, moet → moes, wil → wou, sal → sou**. Never *het gekan*.\n- **Separable verbs:** ge- in the middle: *Ek staan op → Ek het opgestaan.*\n- **No ge-** with be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-, ver-: *Ons besoek Ouma → Ons het Ouma besoek.*\n- **Two verbs after *het*:** no ge-: *Ek gaan swem → Ek het gaan swem.*\n- **In a subordinate clause** *het* goes right to the end: *... omdat hy laat gekom **het**.*\n- **Future tense:** *sal* in position 2 and the infinitive at the end: *Hy sal môre eet.*\n\n## Negation\n\n- Afrikaans uses the **double negative**: the first *nie* comes after the verb and the second *nie* at the end of the sentence: *Hy kom nie vandag nie.*\n- If the first *nie* is already the last word, you write only one *nie*: *Hy kom nie. Ek weet nie.*\n\n| Positive | Negative |\n|---|---|\n| iemand (someone) | niemand ... nie |\n| iets (something) | niks ... nie |\n| altyd (always) | nooit ... nie |\n| êrens (somewhere) | nêrens ... nie |\n| 'n (a) | geen ... nie (or nie 'n ... nie) |\n| al (already) | nog nie ... nie |\n| nog (still) | nie meer ... nie |\n| ook (also) | ook nie ... nie |\n\n- *Iemand het gebel → Niemand het gebel nie.* *Sy het al geëet → Sy het nog nie geëet nie.* *Hy speel nog rugby → Hy speel nie meer rugby nie.*\n- **Commands:** *Moenie ... nie!* The separable verb becomes one word again: *Skakel die TV af! → Moenie die TV afskakel nie!*\n\n> **Tip:** *Jy moet kom* has two negatives with different meanings: *Jy moet nie kom nie* (it is forbidden) and *Jy hoef nie te kom nie* (it is not necessary).\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- No inversion after an adjunct of time: *Môre ek gaan* (wrong) → *Môre gaan ek.*\n- Forgetting the second *nie*.\n- *het* in the wrong place in a subordinate clause: *omdat hy het gekom* → *omdat hy gekom het*.\n- *het gekan, het gemoet* instead of *kon, moes*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp","en":"Subject"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling uitvoer; vra 'Wie of wat + werkwoord?'.","en":"The person or thing that performs the action; ask 'Who or what + verb?'."}},{"term":{"af":"Gesegde","en":"Predicate (verb part)"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoordelike deel van die sin: al die werkwoorde, bv. 'het ... gegee'.","en":"The verbal part of the sentence: all the verbs, e.g. 'het ... gegee'."}},{"term":{"af":"Direkte voorwerp","en":"Direct object"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling direk ondergaan; vra 'Wat?' of 'Wie?' ná die werkwoord.","en":"The person or thing that directly undergoes the action; ask 'What?' or 'Whom?' after the verb."}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte voorwerp","en":"Indirect object"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon aan of vir wie iets gegee of gedoen word, bv. 'my' in 'Ma het my 'n selfoon gegee'.","en":"The person to or for whom something is given or done, e.g. 'my' in 'Ma het my 'n selfoon gegee'."}},{"term":{"af":"Enkelvoudige sin","en":"Simple sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met een hoofsin en een gesegde.","en":"A sentence with one main clause and one predicate."}},{"term":{"af":"Saamgestelde sin","en":"Compound/complex sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met twee of meer sinne: neweskikkend (hoofsin + hoofsin) of onderskikkend (hoofsin + bysin).","en":"A sentence with two or more clauses: coordinate (main + main) or subordinate (main + subordinate clause)."}},{"term":{"af":"Bysin","en":"Subordinate clause"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin wat nie alleen kan staan nie, deur 'n onderskikkende voegwoord ingelei word en die werkwoord aan die einde het.","en":"A clause that cannot stand alone, is introduced by a subordinating conjunction and has the verb at the end."}},{"term":{"af":"Inversie","en":"Inversion"},"def":{"af":"Die omruil van onderwerp en werkwoord wanneer die sin met iets anders as die onderwerp begin: Môre gaan ek.","en":"Swapping the subject and the verb when the sentence starts with something other than the subject: Môre gaan ek."}},{"term":{"af":"STOMPI-reël","en":"STOMPI rule"},"def":{"af":"Die woordorde Subjek – Werkwoord 1 – Tyd – Objek – Manier – Plek – Infinitief/Werkwoord 2.","en":"The word order Subject – Verb 1 – Time – Object – Manner – Place – Infinitive/Verb 2."}},{"term":{"af":"Dubbele ontkenning","en":"Double negative"},"def":{"af":"Die Afrikaanse ontkenning met twee keer *nie* (of niemand/niks/nooit/nêrens/geen ... nie): Hy kom nie vandag nie.","en":"The Afrikaans negation with *nie* twice (or niemand/niks/nooit/nêrens/geen ... nie): Hy kom nie vandag nie."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"STOMPI en inversie","en":"STOMPI and inversion"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Rangskik die sinsdele in die korrekte volgorde: *na Brits / ek / om skoene te koop / môre / ry / met die taxi*\n(b) Herskryf jou sin en begin met *Môre*.\n(c) Verander jou sin in (a) in 'n vraagsin sonder 'n vraagwoord.","en":"(a) Arrange the sentence parts in the correct order: *na Brits / ek / om skoene te koop / môre / ry / met die taxi*\n(b) Rewrite your sentence starting with *Môre*.\n(c) Change your sentence in (a) into a question without a question word."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Volg STOMPI: S = Ek, W1 = ry, T = môre, M = met die taxi, P = na Brits, I = om skoene te koop.","en":"(a) Follow STOMPI: S = Ek, V1 = ry, T = môre, M = met die taxi, P = na Brits, I = om skoene te koop."},{"af":"Sin: *Ek ry môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.*","en":"Sentence: *Ek ry môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.*"},{"af":"(b) Die sin begin nou met die tydsbepaling, dus inversie: werkwoord 1 (*ry*) op plek 2, dan die onderwerp (*ek*): *Môre ry ek met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.*","en":"(b) The sentence now starts with the adjunct of time, so inversion: verb 1 (*ry*) in position 2, then the subject (*ek*): *Môre ry ek met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop.*"},{"af":"(c) 'n Ja/nee-vraag begin met die werkwoord: *Ry jy môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop?* (Ek → jy, want jy vra iemand anders.)","en":"(c) A yes/no question starts with the verb: *Ry jy môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop?* (Ek → jy, because you are asking someone else.)"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Ek ry môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop. (b) Môre ry ek met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop. (c) Ry jy môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop?","en":"(a) Ek ry môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop. (b) Môre ry ek met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop. (c) Ry jy môre met die taxi na Brits om skoene te koop?"}},{"title":{"af":"Verander die tyd","en":"Change the tense"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Skryf in die verlede en die toekomende tyd: *Thabo is moeg, want hy werk hard op die sitrusplaas.*\n(b) Skryf in die verlede tyd: *Ek kan nie kom nie, want ek moet my boetie oppas.*","en":"(a) Write in the past and the future tense: *Thabo is moeg, want hy werk hard op die sitrusplaas.* (Thabo is tired, because he works hard on the citrus farm.)\n(b) Write in the past tense: *Ek kan nie kom nie, want ek moet my boetie oppas.* (I can't come, because I must look after my little brother.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Verlede tyd: *is → was*; *werk → het ... gewerk* (deelwoord aan die einde): *Thabo was moeg, want hy het hard op die sitrusplaas gewerk.*","en":"(a) Past tense: *is → was*; *werk → het ... gewerk* (participle at the end): *Thabo was moeg, want hy het hard op die sitrusplaas gewerk.*"},{"af":"(a) Toekomende tyd: *sal* op plek 2 en die infinitief aan die einde; die infinitief van *is* is *wees*: *Thabo sal moeg wees, want hy sal hard op die sitrusplaas werk.*","en":"(a) Future tense: *sal* in position 2 and the infinitive at the end; the infinitive of *is* is *wees*: *Thabo sal moeg wees, want hy sal hard op die sitrusplaas werk.*"},{"af":"(b) Modale werkwoorde kry 'n eie verlede vorm: *kan → kon, moet → moes*. Die res van die sin bly dieselfde: *Ek kon nie kom nie, want ek moes my boetie oppas.*","en":"(b) Modal verbs take their own past form: *kan → kon, moet → moes*. The rest of the sentence stays the same: *Ek kon nie kom nie, want ek moes my boetie oppas.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Thabo was moeg, want hy het hard op die sitrusplaas gewerk. / Thabo sal moeg wees, want hy sal hard op die sitrusplaas werk. (b) Ek kon nie kom nie, want ek moes my boetie oppas.","en":"(a) Thabo was moeg, want hy het hard op die sitrusplaas gewerk. / Thabo sal moeg wees, want hy sal hard op die sitrusplaas werk. (b) Ek kon nie kom nie, want ek moes my boetie oppas."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontkenning","en":"Negation"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die sinne in die ontkennende vorm.\n\n(a) Iemand het die venster gebreek.\n(b) Sy het al geëet.\n(c) Ons speel nog elke Saterdag rugby.\n(d) Sit die lig aan!\n(e) Hy kom.","en":"Write the sentences in the negative form.\n\n(a) Iemand het die venster gebreek. (Someone broke the window.)\n(b) Sy het al geëet. (She has already eaten.)\n(c) Ons speel nog elke Saterdag rugby. (We still play rugby every Saturday.)\n(d) Sit die lig aan! (Switch the light on!)\n(e) Hy kom. (He is coming.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *iemand → niemand*, plus die tweede *nie* aan die einde: *Niemand het die venster gebreek nie.*","en":"(a) *iemand → niemand*, plus the second *nie* at the end: *Niemand het die venster gebreek nie.*"},{"af":"(b) *al → nog nie*: *Sy het nog nie geëet nie.* (c) *nog → nie meer*: *Ons speel nie meer elke Saterdag rugby nie.*","en":"(b) *al → nog nie*: *Sy het nog nie geëet nie.* (c) *nog → nie meer*: *Ons speel nie meer elke Saterdag rugby nie.*"},{"af":"(d) 'n Bevel word ontken met *Moenie ... nie!*, en die skeibare werkwoord *aansit* word weer een woord aan die einde: *Moenie die lig aansit nie!*","en":"(d) A command is negated with *Moenie ... nie!*, and the separable verb *aansit* becomes one word again at the end: *Moenie die lig aansit nie!*"},{"af":"(e) Die eerste *nie* is reeds die laaste woord, dus net een *nie*: *Hy kom nie.*","en":"(e) The first *nie* is already the last word, so only one *nie*: *Hy kom nie.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Niemand het die venster gebreek nie. (b) Sy het nog nie geëet nie. (c) Ons speel nie meer elke Saterdag rugby nie. (d) Moenie die lig aansit nie! (e) Hy kom nie.","en":"(a) Niemand het die venster gebreek nie. (b) Sy het nog nie geëet nie. (c) Ons speel nie meer elke Saterdag rugby nie. (d) Moenie die lig aansit nie! (e) Hy kom nie."}},{"title":{"af":"Sinsdele en sinsoorte","en":"Sentence parts and sentence types"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Benoem die onderwerp, gesegde, direkte voorwerp, indirekte voorwerp en die bepaling van tyd in: *Ma het my gister 'n nuwe selfoon gegee.*\n(b) Watter soort sin is dit, en waarom staan *het ons* in hierdie volgorde? *Omdat die krag af was, het ons by kerslig gestudeer.*","en":"(a) Name the subject, predicate, direct object, indirect object and the adjunct of time in: *Ma het my gister 'n nuwe selfoon gegee.* (Mom gave me a new cellphone yesterday.)\n(b) What kind of sentence is this, and why is *het ons* in this order? *Omdat die krag af was, het ons by kerslig gestudeer.* (Because the power was off, we studied by candlelight.)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Wie het gegee? **Ma** = onderwerp. Die werkwoorde **het ... gegee** = gesegde.","en":"(a) Who gave? **Ma** = subject. The verbs **het ... gegee** = predicate."},{"af":"Wat het sy gegee? **'n nuwe selfoon** = direkte voorwerp. Aan wie? **my** = indirekte voorwerp. Wanneer? **gister** = bepaling van tyd.","en":"What did she give? **'n nuwe selfoon** = direct object. To whom? **my** = indirect object. When? **gister** = adjunct of time."},{"af":"(b) Daar is 'n bysin (*Omdat die krag af was* – werkwoord *was* aan die einde) en 'n hoofsin, dus is dit 'n **saamgestelde sin – onderskikkend**.","en":"(b) There is a subordinate clause (*Omdat die krag af was* – verb *was* at the end) and a main clause, so it is a **complex sentence – subordinate**."},{"af":"Die sin begin met die bysin, dus is daar inversie in die hoofsin: die werkwoord *het* kom eerste en dan die onderwerp *ons*.","en":"The sentence starts with the subordinate clause, so there is inversion in the main clause: the verb *het* comes first and then the subject *ons*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Onderwerp: Ma; gesegde: het ... gegee; direkte voorwerp: 'n nuwe selfoon; indirekte voorwerp: my; bepaling van tyd: gister. (b) Saamgestelde sin (onderskikkend); inversie omdat die sin met die bysin begin.","en":"(a) Subject: Ma; predicate: het ... gegee; direct object: 'n nuwe selfoon; indirect object: my; adjunct of time: gister. (b) Complex sentence (subordinate); inversion because the sentence starts with the subordinate clause."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sinsoort is: 'Wat 'n pragtige sonsondergang oor die Magaliesberg!'?","en":"Which sentence type is: 'Wat 'n pragtige sonsondergang oor die Magaliesberg!'?"},"options":[{"af":"Stelsin","en":"Statement"},{"af":"Vraagsin","en":"Question"},{"af":"Bevelsin","en":"Command"},{"af":"Uitroepsin","en":"Exclamation"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die sin druk sterk gevoel (bewondering) uit en eindig met 'n uitroepteken. Al begin dit met 'Wat', vra dit niks nie, dus is dit nie 'n vraagsin nie.","en":"The sentence expresses strong feeling (admiration) and ends with an exclamation mark. Although it starts with 'Wat', it does not ask anything, so it is not a question."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verlede tyd van die modale werkwoord *kan* is ___.","en":"The past tense of the modal verb *kan* is ___."},"answers":{"af":["kon"],"en":["kon"]},"explain":{"af":"kan → kon. Modale werkwoorde kry 'n eie verlede vorm; 'het gekan' is verkeerd, en 'moes' is die verlede vorm van 'moet'.","en":"kan → kon. Modal verbs take their own past form; 'het gekan' is wrong, and 'moes' is the past form of 'moet'."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["het gekan","kun","moes"],"en":["het gekan","kun","moes"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Enkelvoudige sin bestaan uit een hoofsin met een gesegde.","en":"A simple sentence consists of one main clause with one predicate."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Sodra daar twee sinne (hoofsin + hoofsin of hoofsin + bysin) verbind word, is dit 'n saamgestelde sin.","en":"True. As soon as two clauses (main + main or main + subordinate) are joined, it is a compound/complex sentence."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord by sy ontkennende vorm.","en":"Match each word to its negative form."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"iemand","en":"iemand (someone)"},"r":{"af":"niemand ... nie","en":"niemand ... nie"}},{"l":{"af":"iets","en":"iets (something)"},"r":{"af":"niks ... nie","en":"niks ... nie"}},{"l":{"af":"altyd","en":"altyd (always)"},"r":{"af":"nooit ... nie","en":"nooit ... nie"}},{"l":{"af":"êrens","en":"êrens (somewhere)"},"r":{"af":"nêrens ... nie","en":"nêrens ... nie"}},{"l":{"af":"'n","en":"'n (a)"},"r":{"af":"geen ... nie","en":"geen ... nie"}}],"explain":{"af":"Onthou die dubbele ontkenning: die tweede *nie* kom steeds aan die einde, bv. 'Niemand het gebel nie.'","en":"Remember the double negative: the second *nie* still comes at the end, e.g. 'Niemand het gebel nie.'"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die **direkte voorwerp** in: 'Gister het my broer by die winkelsentrum 'n nuwe rugbybal gekoop.'?","en":"What is the **direct object** in: 'Gister het my broer by die winkelsentrum 'n nuwe rugbybal gekoop.'?"},"options":[{"af":"Gister","en":"Gister"},{"af":"my broer","en":"my broer"},{"af":"'n nuwe rugbybal","en":"'n nuwe rugbybal"},{"af":"by die winkelsentrum","en":"by die winkelsentrum"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vra: Wat het hy gekoop? 'n Nuwe rugbybal. 'my broer' is die onderwerp (wie het gekoop?), 'gister' 'n bepaling van tyd en 'by die winkelsentrum' 'n bepaling van plek.","en":"Ask: What did he buy? 'n Nuwe rugbybal. 'my broer' is the subject (who bought?), 'gister' an adjunct of time and 'by die winkelsentrum' an adjunct of place."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: 'Die wedstryd is baie spannend.' → Die wedstryd ___ baie spannend.","en":"Write in the past tense: 'Die wedstryd is baie spannend.' → Die wedstryd ___ baie spannend."},"answers":{"af":["was"],"en":["was"]},"explain":{"af":"is → was. 'is gewees' en 'het gewees' is nie Standaardafrikaans nie.","en":"is → was. 'is gewees' and 'het gewees' are not Standard Afrikaans."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is gewees","het gewees","wees"],"en":["is gewees","het gewees","wees"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vra 'n vraag met 'n vraagwoord oor die TYD: 'Ons gaan môre Pretoria toe.'","en":"Ask a question with a question word about the TIME: 'Ons gaan môre Pretoria toe.'"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer ons gaan Pretoria toe?","en":"Wanneer ons gaan Pretoria toe?"},{"af":"Wanneer gaan ons Pretoria toe?","en":"Wanneer gaan ons Pretoria toe?"},{"af":"Wanneer gaan ons môre Pretoria toe?","en":"Wanneer gaan ons môre Pretoria toe?"},{"af":"Ons gaan wanneer Pretoria toe?","en":"Ons gaan wanneer Pretoria toe?"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die vraagwoord *Wanneer* vervang die tydsbepaling *môre* (dus val *môre* weg), en daarna volg inversie: werkwoord (*gaan*) voor onderwerp (*ons*).","en":"The question word *Wanneer* replaces the adjunct of time *môre* (so *môre* falls away), and then inversion follows: verb (*gaan*) before subject (*ons*)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ontken: 'Sy het al geëet.' → Sy het ___ geëet nie.","en":"Negate: 'Sy het al geëet.' → Sy het ___ geëet nie."},"answers":{"af":["nog nie"],"en":["nog nie"]},"explain":{"af":"al → nog nie. 'Sy het nog nie geëet nie' beteken sy gaan nog eet. 'nie meer' is die ontkenning van 'nog'.","en":"al → nog nie. 'Sy het nog nie geëet nie' means she will still eat. 'nie meer' is the negation of 'nog'."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["nie al","nooit","nie meer"],"en":["nie al","nooit","nie meer"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die ontkenning van 'Ek weet.' is 'Ek weet nie nie.'","en":"The negation of 'Ek weet.' is 'Ek weet nie nie.'"},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. As die eerste *nie* reeds die laaste woord in die sin is, skryf jy net een *nie*: 'Ek weet nie.'","en":"False. If the first *nie* is already the last word in the sentence, you write only one *nie*: 'Ek weet nie.'"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die toekomende tyd: 'Hy is in Graad 11.' → Hy sal in Graad 11 ___.","en":"Write in the future tense: 'Hy is in Graad 11.' → Hy sal in Graad 11 ___."},"answers":{"af":["wees"],"en":["wees"]},"explain":{"af":"Ná *sal* volg die infinitief aan die einde, en die infinitief van *is* is *wees*: 'Hy sal in Graad 11 wees.'","en":"After *sal* the infinitive follows at the end, and the infinitive of *is* is *wees*: 'Hy sal in Graad 11 wees.'"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is","gewees","was"],"en":["is","gewees","was"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Begin die sin met *Môre*: 'Ek skryf môre my Afrikaans-eksamen.'","en":"Start the sentence with *Môre*: 'Ek skryf môre my Afrikaans-eksamen.'"},"options":[{"af":"Môre skryf ek my Afrikaans-eksamen.","en":"Môre skryf ek my Afrikaans-eksamen."},{"af":"Môre ek skryf my Afrikaans-eksamen.","en":"Môre ek skryf my Afrikaans-eksamen."},{"af":"Môre ek my Afrikaans-eksamen skryf.","en":"Môre ek my Afrikaans-eksamen skryf."},{"af":"Môre skryf my Afrikaans-eksamen ek.","en":"Môre skryf my Afrikaans-eksamen ek."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"As die sin met 'n tydsbepaling begin, is daar inversie: werkwoord 1 (*skryf*) bly op plek 2 en die onderwerp (*ek*) kom direk daarna.","en":"If the sentence starts with an adjunct of time, there is inversion: verb 1 (*skryf*) stays in position 2 and the subject (*ek*) comes directly after it."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ontken die bevel: 'Skakel die TV af!' → Moenie die TV ___ nie!","en":"Negate the command: 'Skakel die TV af!' → Moenie die TV ___ nie!"},"answers":{"af":["afskakel"],"en":["afskakel"]},"explain":{"af":"Ná *Moenie* staan die werkwoord as infinitief aan die einde, en die skeibare werkwoord word weer een woord: afskakel.","en":"After *Moenie* the verb stands at the end as an infinitive, and the separable verb becomes one word again: afskakel."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["skakel af","afgeskakel","af te skakel"],"en":["skakel af","afgeskakel","af te skakel"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die korrekte woordorde?","en":"Which sentence has the correct word order?"},"options":[{"af":"Ons sal braai Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam.","en":"Ons sal braai Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam."},{"af":"Saterdag ons sal die vleis stadig by die dam braai.","en":"Saterdag ons sal die vleis stadig by die dam braai."},{"af":"Ons Saterdag sal die vleis stadig by die dam braai.","en":"Ons Saterdag sal die vleis stadig by die dam braai."},{"af":"Ons sal Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam braai.","en":"Ons sal Saterdag die vleis stadig by die dam braai."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"STOMPI: Ons (S) sal (W1) Saterdag (T) die vleis (O) stadig (M) by die dam (P) braai (W2). Werkwoord 1 staan op plek 2 en werkwoord 2 heel agter; as die sin met 'Saterdag' begin, moet dit 'Saterdag sal ons' wees.","en":"STOMPI: Ons (S) sal (V1) Saterdag (T) die vleis (O) stadig (M) by die dam (P) braai (V2). Verb 1 stands in position 2 and verb 2 right at the end; if the sentence starts with 'Saterdag', it must be 'Saterdag sal ons'."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'Ek het hard geleer, maar die vraestel was steeds moeilik.' Watter soort sin is dit?","en":"'Ek het hard geleer, maar die vraestel was steeds moeilik.' What kind of sentence is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Enkelvoudige sin","en":"Simple sentence"},{"af":"Saamgestelde sin – onderskikkend (hoofsin + bysin)","en":"Complex sentence – subordinate (main + subordinate clause)"},{"af":"Saamgestelde sin – neweskikkend (hoofsin + hoofsin)","en":"Compound sentence – coordinate (main + main clause)"},{"af":"Bevelsin","en":"Command"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Daar is twee gesegdes (het geleer; was), verbind met *maar*. Albei dele kan alleen staan en die woordorde bly normaal, dus is dit neweskikkend.","en":"There are two predicates (het geleer; was), joined with *maar*. Both parts can stand alone and the word order stays normal, so it is coordinate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in die verlede tyd: 'Hy staan elke oggend vroeg op omdat hy die taxi moet haal.'","en":"Write in the past tense: 'Hy staan elke oggend vroeg op omdat hy die taxi moet haal.'"},"options":[{"af":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal.","en":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal."},{"af":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg geopstaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal.","en":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg geopstaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal."},{"af":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi het moet haal.","en":"Hy het elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi het moet haal."},{"af":"Hy staan elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal.","en":"Hy staan elke oggend vroeg opgestaan omdat hy die taxi moes haal."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*opstaan* is skeibaar: op-ge-staan. In die bysin word *moet* → *moes* (die modale werkwoord se eie verlede vorm), nie 'het moet' nie. In die hoofsin is *het* nodig.","en":"*opstaan* is separable: op-ge-staan. In the subordinate clause *moet* → *moes* (the modal verb's own past form), not 'het moet'. In the main clause *het* is needed."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is heeltemal KORREK?","en":"Which sentence is completely CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"Gister ons het nie by die dam geswem nie, want die water was te koud.","en":"Gister ons het nie by die dam geswem nie, want die water was te koud."},{"af":"Gister het ons nie by die dam geswem nie, want die water was te koud.","en":"Gister het ons nie by die dam geswem nie, want die water was te koud."},{"af":"Gister het ons nie by die dam geswem, want die water was te koud.","en":"Gister het ons nie by die dam geswem, want die water was te koud."},{"af":"Gister het ons nie by die dam swem nie, want die water was te koud.","en":"Gister het ons nie by die dam swem nie, want die water was te koud."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die korrekte sin het inversie ná 'Gister' (het ons), die tweede *nie* voor *want*, en die deelwoord *geswem*. Die ander sinne het elk een fout: geen inversie nie, geen tweede *nie* nie, of geen ge- nie.","en":"The correct sentence has inversion after 'Gister' (het ons), the second *nie* before *want*, and the participle *geswem*. The other sentences each have one error: no inversion, no second *nie*, or no ge-."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t2-opsomming","title":{"af":"Opsomming","en":"Summary"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n teks volgens 'n spesifieke opdrag kan opsom: die regte sewe feite kies, dit in eie woorde herskryf en binne die woordlimiet bly.","en":"You will be able to summarise a text according to a specific instruction: choose the right seven facts, rewrite them in your own words and stay within the word limit."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n opsomming?\n\n'n **Opsomming** is 'n kort weergawe van 'n teks wat **net die feite gee wat die opdrag vra**, waar moontlik in **jou eie woorde**. In Vraestel 1 (Taal in konteks) is dit **Afdeling B** en dit tel **10 punte**.\n\n## Die formaat\n\n| Wat | Vereiste |\n|---|---|\n| Aantal feite | gewoonlik **7** |\n| Vorm | **puntsgewys**: volsinne, genommer 1–7 onder mekaar; óf **een samehangende paragraaf** as die vraestel dit vra |\n| Lengte | gewoonlik **80–90 woorde**; volg altyd die limiet in die vraestel |\n| Woordetal | skryf dit aan die einde, bv. *(Woordetal: 82)* |\n| Taal | volsinne met 'n onderwerp en 'n werkwoord; eie woorde waar moontlik |\n\n## Hoe word dit nagesien? (10 punte)\n\n- **Inhoud: 7 punte** – een punt vir elke korrekte, relevante feit.\n- **Taal: 3 punte** – volgens die aantal taalkundig korrekte sinne:\n\n| Korrekte sinne | Taalpunt |\n|---|---|\n| 1–3 | 1 |\n| 4–5 | 2 |\n| 6–7 | 3 |\n\n- Die nasiener verdra gewoonlik tot **5 woorde** bo die limiet. Skryf jy nog meer, kan jy punte verloor.\n\n## Stap vir stap\n\n1. **Lees die opdrag twee keer.** Onderstreep die fokus (bv. *wenke om veilig aanlyn te bly*), die aantal feite, die vorm en die woordlimiet.\n2. **Vluglees** die teks om die hoofgedagte te kry.\n3. Lees noukeurig en **onderstreep net die feite wat die opdrag beantwoord**. Nommer hulle 1 tot 7 in die kantlyn.\n4. **Laat uit** alles wat nie 'n feit oor die fokus is nie (sien hieronder).\n5. **Herskryf elke feit as een kort volsin** in jou eie woorde.\n6. **Tel die woorde** en skryf die woordetal neer. Elke woord tel, ook *'n*, *die* en *nie*; die nommers 1–7 tel nie.\n7. **Proeflees:** spelling, leestekens, die dubbele ontkenning en die tye.\n\n## Wat laat jy uit?\n\n- **voorbeelde** (let op *byvoorbeeld, soos, onder andere*)\n- **stylfigure en beeldspraak**, bv. *'n mynveld vol gevare*\n- **herhaling**: dieselfde feit in ander woorde\n- **direkte rede** en aanhalings\n- **statistieke**, getalle en besonderhede wat nie die feit self is nie\n- die skrywer se **inleiding en slot**, en **jou eie mening**\n\n## Eie woorde – hoe?\n\n- Gebruik **sinonieme**: *dit is raadsaam om* → *jy moet*.\n- **Veralgemeen**: vervang 'n lys met een oorkoepelende woord: *appels, lemoene en piesangs* → *vrugte*.\n- **Verkort** lang frases: *op hierdie oomblik* → *nou*; *as gevolg van die feit dat* → *omdat*.\n- Verander die **sinsbou**: *Dit is belangrik dat jy jou profiel op privaat stel* → *Stel jou profiel op privaat.*\n- Vakterme en name (*wagwoord, profiel, Brits*) mag jy behou: daar is nie altyd 'n ander woord nie.\n\n## Puntsgewys of paragraaf?\n\n| Puntsgewys | Paragraaf |\n|---|---|\n| sewe genommerde volsinne onder mekaar | een samehangende paragraaf sonder nommers |\n| een feit per sin | een feit per sin, verbind met **verbindingswoorde**: *eerstens, verder, daarbenewens, ook, laastens* |\n| geen inleiding of slot nie | geen inleiding of slot nie |\n\n> **Onthou!** Verbindingswoorde tel ook as woorde. Gebruik net genoeg om die paragraaf vloeiend te maak.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- **Irrelevante feite** wat nie by die opdrag pas nie.\n- **Twee feite in een sin**: dit maak dit moeilik om punte toe te ken, en jy kan 'n punt verloor.\n- **Lang sinne afskryf** uit die teks.\n- **Geen woordetal nie**, of 'n woordetal wat nie klop nie.\n- **'n Inleiding skryf** (*In hierdie teks gaan ek ...*): dit mors woorde en kry geen punt nie.\n- **Onvolledige sinne** sonder 'n werkwoord: jy verloor taalpunte.\n\n> **Wenk:** Maak eers 'n vinnige konsep, tel die woorde, en skryf dan die finale weergawe netjies oor. So bly jy binne die limiet sonder om 'n feit te verloor.","en":"## What is a summary?\n\nA **summary** is a short version of a text that gives **only the facts the instruction asks for**, in **your own words** where possible. In Paper 1 (Language in context) it is **Section B** and it counts **10 marks**.\n\n## The format\n\n| What | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| Number of facts | usually **7** |\n| Form | **point form**: full sentences, numbered 1–7 below each other; or **one coherent paragraph** if the paper asks for it |\n| Length | usually **80–90 words**; always follow the limit in the paper |\n| Word count | write it at the end, e.g. *(Woordetal: 82)* |\n| Language | full sentences with a subject and a verb; own words where possible |\n\n## How is it marked? (10 marks)\n\n- **Content: 7 marks** – one mark for each correct, relevant fact.\n- **Language: 3 marks** – according to the number of linguistically correct sentences:\n\n| Correct sentences | Language mark |\n|---|---|\n| 1–3 | 1 |\n| 4–5 | 2 |\n| 6–7 | 3 |\n\n- The marker usually tolerates up to **5 words** over the limit. If you write even more, you can lose marks.\n\n## Step by step\n\n1. **Read the instruction twice.** Underline the focus (e.g. *tips for staying safe online*), the number of facts, the form and the word limit.\n2. **Skim** the text to get the main idea.\n3. Read carefully and **underline only the facts that answer the instruction**. Number them 1 to 7 in the margin.\n4. **Leave out** everything that is not a fact about the focus (see below).\n5. **Rewrite each fact as one short full sentence** in your own words.\n6. **Count the words** and write down the word count. Every word counts, including *'n*, *die* and *nie*; the numbers 1–7 do not count.\n7. **Proofread:** spelling, punctuation, the double negative and the tenses.\n\n## What do you leave out?\n\n- **examples** (look out for *byvoorbeeld, soos, onder andere*)\n- **figures of speech and imagery**, e.g. *'n mynveld vol gevare* (a minefield full of dangers)\n- **repetition**: the same fact in different words\n- **direct speech** and quotations\n- **statistics**, figures and details that are not the fact itself\n- the writer's **introduction and conclusion**, and **your own opinion**\n\n## Own words – how?\n\n- Use **synonyms**: *dit is raadsaam om* → *jy moet*.\n- **Generalise**: replace a list with one umbrella word: *appels, lemoene en piesangs* → *vrugte*.\n- **Shorten** long phrases: *op hierdie oomblik* → *nou*; *as gevolg van die feit dat* → *omdat*.\n- Change the **sentence structure**: *Dit is belangrik dat jy jou profiel op privaat stel* → *Stel jou profiel op privaat.*\n- You may keep technical terms and names (*wagwoord, profiel, Brits*): there is not always another word.\n\n## Point form or paragraph?\n\n| Point form | Paragraph |\n|---|---|\n| seven numbered full sentences below each other | one coherent paragraph without numbers |\n| one fact per sentence | one fact per sentence, joined with **linking words**: *eerstens, verder, daarbenewens, ook, laastens* |\n| no introduction or conclusion | no introduction or conclusion |\n\n> **Remember!** Linking words also count as words. Use just enough to make the paragraph flow.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- **Irrelevant facts** that do not fit the instruction.\n- **Two facts in one sentence**: this makes it hard to award marks, and you can lose a mark.\n- **Copying long sentences** from the text.\n- **No word count**, or a word count that does not add up.\n- **Writing an introduction** (*In hierdie teks gaan ek ...*): it wastes words and earns no mark.\n- **Incomplete sentences** without a verb: you lose language marks.\n\n> **Tip:** First make a quick draft, count the words, and then write the final version out neatly. That way you stay within the limit without losing a fact."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Opsomming","en":"Summary"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort weergawe van 'n teks wat net die feite gee wat die opdrag vra, waar moontlik in eie woorde.","en":"A short version of a text that gives only the facts the instruction asks for, in own words where possible."}},{"term":{"af":"Opdrag (fokus)","en":"Instruction (focus)"},"def":{"af":"Die vraag wat sê waaroor jy moet opsom, hoeveel feite, in watter vorm en hoeveel woorde.","en":"The question that says what you must summarise, how many facts, in which form and how many words."}},{"term":{"af":"Relevante feit","en":"Relevant fact"},"def":{"af":"'n Inligtingseenheid uit die teks wat die opdrag direk beantwoord; elke korrekte feit kry een inhoudspunt.","en":"A unit of information from the text that answers the instruction directly; each correct fact earns one content mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Puntsgewys","en":"Point form"},"def":{"af":"Die feite as genommerde volsinne onder mekaar, een feit per sin.","en":"The facts as numbered full sentences below each other, one fact per sentence."}},{"term":{"af":"Samehangende paragraaf","en":"Coherent paragraph"},"def":{"af":"Een paragraaf sonder nommers waarin die feite met verbindingswoorde aan mekaar gekoppel is.","en":"One paragraph without numbers in which the facts are linked with linking words."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordetal","en":"Word count"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal woorde wat jy gebruik het, aangedui aan die einde van die opsomming.","en":"The number of words you used, given at the end of the summary."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordlimiet","en":"Word limit"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal woorde wat die opdrag toelaat, gewoonlik 80–90 woorde in Graad 10.","en":"The number of words the instruction allows, usually 80–90 words in Grade 10."}},{"term":{"af":"Eie woorde (herformulering)","en":"Own words (rephrasing)"},"def":{"af":"Die feit in ander woorde of met 'n ander sinsbou weergee sonder om die teks af te skryf.","en":"Expressing the fact in other words or with a different sentence structure without copying the text."}},{"term":{"af":"Veralgemening","en":"Generalisation"},"def":{"af":"'n Lys besonderhede vervang met een oorkoepelende woord, bv. appels, lemoene en piesangs → vrugte.","en":"Replacing a list of details with one umbrella word, e.g. appels, lemoene en piesangs → vrugte."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbindingswoorde","en":"Linking words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat sinne in 'n paragraaf aan mekaar koppel: eerstens, verder, daarbenewens, ook, laastens.","en":"Words that link sentences in a paragraph: eerstens, verder, daarbenewens, ook, laastens."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Volledige opsomming: veilig aanlyn","en":"Complete summary: safe online"},"problem":{"af":"**Is jou aanlyn lewe 'n oop boek?** (eie teks)\n\n(1) Tieners in Brits, net soos tieners regoor die wêreld, spandeer elke dag ure op hul selfone om te klets, video's te kyk en speletjies te speel. Die internet is 'n wonderlike speelgrond, maar dit is ook 'n mynveld vol gevare. Hoe beskerm jy jouself?\n\n(2) Begin by jou wagwoord. Kies 'n sterk wagwoord wat uit letters, syfers en simbole bestaan. \"Moet nooit jou troeteldier se naam of jou verjaarsdag gebruik nie,\" waarsku mnr. Botha, die rekenaaronderwyser by 'n skool in die dorp. Deel ook nooit jou wagwoord met iemand nie – selfs nie met jou beste vriend nie.\n\n(3) Dink twee keer voordat jy 'n foto plaas. Wat eenmaal op die internet is, bly vir altyd daar, soos 'n tatoeëermerk wat nooit afwas nie. Stel boonop jou profiel op privaat sodat net mense wat jy ken, jou plasings kan sien.\n\n(4) Bedrieërs stuur dikwels boodskappe wat lyk asof dit van 'n bank of 'n winkel kom. Moenie op skakels in sulke vreemde boodskappe of e-posse druk nie. Een Graad 10-leerder het so R500 van sy sakgeld verloor.\n\n(5) Ontmoet nooit iemand wat jy net aanlyn leer ken het, sonder dat jou ouers daarvan weet nie. Mense is nie altyd wie hulle sê hulle is nie. Iemand wat beweer hy is vyftien, kan in werklikheid 'n volwasse man wees.\n\n(6) As iemand jou aanlyn boelie of dreig, moet jy dit nie vir jouself hou nie. Vertel dadelik 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou.\n\n(7) Onthou: jou wagwoord is soos jou tandeborsel – jy deel dit met niemand nie. Die internet is 'n goeie dienaar, maar 'n slegte meester.\n\n**Opdrag:** Som in puntsgewyse vorm SEWE wenke op wat die skrywer gee om veilig aanlyn te bly. Skryf volsinne en gebruik jou eie woorde waar moontlik. Jou opsomming moet tussen 80 en 90 woorde wees. Dui die woordetal aan.","en":"**Is jou aanlyn lewe 'n oop boek?** (eie teks)\n\n(1) Tieners in Brits, net soos tieners regoor die wêreld, spandeer elke dag ure op hul selfone om te klets, video's te kyk en speletjies te speel. Die internet is 'n wonderlike speelgrond, maar dit is ook 'n mynveld vol gevare. Hoe beskerm jy jouself?\n\n(2) Begin by jou wagwoord. Kies 'n sterk wagwoord wat uit letters, syfers en simbole bestaan. \"Moet nooit jou troeteldier se naam of jou verjaarsdag gebruik nie,\" waarsku mnr. Botha, die rekenaaronderwyser by 'n skool in die dorp. Deel ook nooit jou wagwoord met iemand nie – selfs nie met jou beste vriend nie.\n\n(3) Dink twee keer voordat jy 'n foto plaas. Wat eenmaal op die internet is, bly vir altyd daar, soos 'n tatoeëermerk wat nooit afwas nie. Stel boonop jou profiel op privaat sodat net mense wat jy ken, jou plasings kan sien.\n\n(4) Bedrieërs stuur dikwels boodskappe wat lyk asof dit van 'n bank of 'n winkel kom. Moenie op skakels in sulke vreemde boodskappe of e-posse druk nie. Een Graad 10-leerder het so R500 van sy sakgeld verloor.\n\n(5) Ontmoet nooit iemand wat jy net aanlyn leer ken het, sonder dat jou ouers daarvan weet nie. Mense is nie altyd wie hulle sê hulle is nie. Iemand wat beweer hy is vyftien, kan in werklikheid 'n volwasse man wees.\n\n(6) As iemand jou aanlyn boelie of dreig, moet jy dit nie vir jouself hou nie. Vertel dadelik 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou.\n\n(7) Onthou: jou wagwoord is soos jou tandeborsel – jy deel dit met niemand nie. Die internet is 'n goeie dienaar, maar 'n slegte meester.\n\n**Is your online life an open book?** (our own text, English translation)\n\n(1) Teenagers in Brits, just like teenagers around the world, spend hours on their cellphones every day to chat, watch videos and play games. The internet is a wonderful playground, but it is also a minefield full of dangers. How do you protect yourself?\n\n(2) Start with your password. Choose a strong password made up of letters, numbers and symbols. \"Never use your pet's name or your birthday,\" warns Mr Botha, the computer teacher at a school in town. Also never share your password with anyone – not even with your best friend.\n\n(3) Think twice before you post a photo. What is on the internet once, stays there forever, like a tattoo that never washes off. Also set your profile to private so that only people you know can see your posts.\n\n(4) Scammers often send messages that look as if they come from a bank or a shop. Do not click on links in such strange messages or e-mails. One Grade 10 learner lost R500 of his pocket money this way.\n\n(5) Never meet someone you only got to know online without your parents knowing about it. People are not always who they say they are. Someone who claims he is fifteen can in reality be an adult man.\n\n(6) If someone bullies or threatens you online, do not keep it to yourself. Immediately tell an adult you trust.\n\n(7) Remember: your password is like your toothbrush – you share it with no one. The internet is a good servant but a bad master.\n\n**Instruction:** Summarise in point form SEVEN tips the writer gives for staying safe online. Write full sentences and use your own words where possible. Your summary must be between 80 and 90 words. Give the word count."},"steps":[{"af":"Onderstreep die opdrag: *SEWE wenke*, *veilig aanlyn*, *puntsgewys*, *volsinne*, *80–90 woorde*, *woordetal*.","en":"Underline the instruction: *SEVEN tips*, *safe online*, *point form*, *full sentences*, *80–90 words*, *word count*."},{"af":"Die sewe feite wat jy onderstreep: (1) sterk wagwoord met letters, syfers en simbole – par. 2; (2) deel nooit jou wagwoord nie – par. 2; (3) dink twee keer voor jy 'n foto plaas – par. 3; (4) profiel op privaat – par. 3; (5) moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie – par. 4; (6) moenie aanlyn kennisse sonder jou ouers se medewete ontmoet nie – par. 5; (7) vertel 'n volwassene as jy geboelie word – par. 6.","en":"The seven facts you underline: (1) strong password with letters, numbers and symbols – para. 2; (2) never share your password – para. 2; (3) think twice before posting a photo – para. 3; (4) profile on private – para. 3; (5) do not click on links in strange messages – para. 4; (6) do not meet online acquaintances without your parents knowing – para. 5; (7) tell an adult if you are bullied – para. 6."},{"af":"Laat uit: die inleiding (par. 1, ook die voorbeelde 'klets, video's kyk, speletjies'), die metafoor 'mynveld' en die vergelyking 'soos 'n tatoeëermerk', mnr. Botha se aanhaling (direkte rede), die R500-voorbeeld, die voorbeeld van die 'vyftienjarige' en die herhaling plus spreekwoord in par. 7.","en":"Leave out: the introduction (para. 1, also the examples 'chat, watch videos, play games'), the metaphor 'minefield' and the simile 'like a tattoo', Mr Botha's quotation (direct speech), the R500 example, the example of the 'fifteen-year-old' and the repetition plus proverb in para. 7."},{"af":"Herskryf elke feit as een kort volsin in eie woorde, bv. 'Kies 'n sterk wagwoord wat uit letters, syfers en simbole bestaan' → 'Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat.' Kontroleer die dubbele ontkenning in elke negatiewe sin.","en":"Rewrite each fact as one short full sentence in own words, e.g. 'Kies 'n sterk wagwoord wat uit letters, syfers en simbole bestaan' → 'Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat.' Check the double negative in every negative sentence."},{"af":"Tel die woorde per sin: 10, 8, 12, 14, 10, 15, 13 = 82 woorde. Dit is binne 80–90, dus skryf jy *(Woordetal: 82)*.","en":"Count the words per sentence: 10, 8, 12, 14, 10, 15, 13 = 82 words. That is within 80–90, so you write *(Woordetal: 82)*."}],"answer":{"af":"1. Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat.\n2. Moet nooit jou wagwoord met iemand deel nie.\n3. Dink mooi voordat jy foto's aanlyn plaas, want hulle bly altyd daar.\n4. Stel jou profiel op privaat sodat net mense wat jy ken, jou plasings sien.\n5. Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe of e-posse druk nie.\n6. Moenie iemand wat jy aanlyn leer ken het, sonder jou ouers se medewete ontmoet nie.\n7. Vertel 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou as iemand jou aanlyn boelie of dreig.\n\n(Woordetal: 82)","en":"1. Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat.\n2. Moet nooit jou wagwoord met iemand deel nie.\n3. Dink mooi voordat jy foto's aanlyn plaas, want hulle bly altyd daar.\n4. Stel jou profiel op privaat sodat net mense wat jy ken, jou plasings sien.\n5. Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe of e-posse druk nie.\n6. Moenie iemand wat jy aanlyn leer ken het, sonder jou ouers se medewete ontmoet nie.\n7. Vertel 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou as iemand jou aanlyn boelie of dreig.\n\n(Woordetal: 82)"}},{"title":{"af":"Dieselfde opsomming as 'n paragraaf","en":"The same summary as a paragraph"},"problem":{"af":"Die vraestel vra nou: *Skryf die sewe wenke as een samehangende paragraaf van 80–90 woorde.* Gebruik die sewe feite uit die vorige voorbeeld.","en":"The paper now asks: *Write the seven tips as one coherent paragraph of 80–90 words.* (Skryf die sewe wenke as een samehangende paragraaf van 80–90 woorde.) Use the seven facts from the previous example."},"steps":[{"af":"Behou een feit per sin, maar laat die nommers weg.","en":"Keep one fact per sentence, but leave out the numbers."},{"af":"Koppel die sinne met verbindingswoorde: *Eerstens ... Verder ... ook ... Daarbenewens ... Laastens*. Gebruik nie by elke sin een nie – dit kos woorde.","en":"Link the sentences with linking words: *Eerstens ... Verder ... ook ... Daarbenewens ... Laastens*. Do not use one with every sentence – it costs words."},{"af":"Verkort waar nodig sodat die verbindingswoorde jou nie oor die limiet neem nie, bv. 'mense wat jy ken' → 'bekendes'.","en":"Shorten where necessary so that the linking words do not take you over the limit, e.g. 'mense wat jy ken' → 'bekendes'."},{"af":"Tel: 81 woorde – binne die limiet.","en":"Count: 81 words – within the limit."}],"answer":{"af":"Eerstens moet jy 'n sterk wagwoord gebruik wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat. Verder moet jy jou wagwoord met niemand deel nie. Dink ook mooi voordat jy foto's plaas, want hulle bly altyd aanlyn. Daarbenewens moet jy jou profiel op privaat stel sodat net bekendes jou plasings sien. Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie. Ontmoet ook nooit aanlyn kennisse sonder jou ouers se medewete nie. Laastens moet jy 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou, vertel as iemand jou aanlyn boelie.\n\n(Woordetal: 81)","en":"Eerstens moet jy 'n sterk wagwoord gebruik wat letters, syfers en simbole bevat. Verder moet jy jou wagwoord met niemand deel nie. Dink ook mooi voordat jy foto's plaas, want hulle bly altyd aanlyn. Daarbenewens moet jy jou profiel op privaat stel sodat net bekendes jou plasings sien. Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie. Ontmoet ook nooit aanlyn kennisse sonder jou ouers se medewete nie. Laastens moet jy 'n volwassene wat jy vertrou, vertel as iemand jou aanlyn boelie.\n\n(Woordetal: 81)"}},{"title":{"af":"Wat behou jy en wat laat jy uit?","en":"What do you keep and what do you leave out?"},"problem":{"af":"**Opdrag:** Watter sinne bevat feite oor hoe mense die dam kan help skoon hou? Herskryf daardie feite as kort volsinne.\n\n(1) Die Hartbeespoortdam is die trots van Madibeng, maar rommel en besoedeling bedreig die water. (2) \"Ons dam is ons lewensaar,\" sê 'n plaaslike visserman. (3) Besoekers moet hul rommel in sakke saamneem huis toe. (4) By die vorige skoonmaakdag het ons klas byvoorbeeld twintig sakke rommel langs die oewer opgetel. (5) Moenie olie, verf of chemikalieë in stormwaterdreine gooi nie, want dit loop in die dam in. (6) Die son het soos goud op die water geskitter. (7) Sluit aan by die maandelikse skoonmaakdag.","en":"**Instruction:** Which sentences contain facts about how people can help keep the dam clean? Rewrite those facts as short full sentences.\n\n(1) Die Hartbeespoortdam is die trots van Madibeng, maar rommel en besoedeling bedreig die water. (2) \"Ons dam is ons lewensaar,\" sê 'n plaaslike visserman. (3) Besoekers moet hul rommel in sakke saamneem huis toe. (4) By die vorige skoonmaakdag het ons klas byvoorbeeld twintig sakke rommel langs die oewer opgetel. (5) Moenie olie, verf of chemikalieë in stormwaterdreine gooi nie, want dit loop in die dam in. (6) Die son het soos goud op die water geskitter. (7) Sluit aan by die maandelikse skoonmaakdag.\n\n(Translation: (1) Hartbeespoort Dam is the pride of Madibeng, but litter and pollution threaten the water. (2) \"Our dam is our lifeline,\" says a local fisherman. (3) Visitors must take their litter home in bags. (4) At the previous clean-up day our class, for example, picked up twenty bags of litter along the shore. (5) Do not throw oil, paint or chemicals into stormwater drains, because it flows into the dam. (6) The sun sparkled like gold on the water. (7) Join the monthly clean-up day.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Toets elke sin teen die opdrag: sê dit wat iemand kan **doen** om die dam skoon te hou?","en":"Test every sentence against the instruction: does it say what someone can **do** to keep the dam clean?"},{"af":"Behou sin 3 (rommel saamneem), sin 5 (geen olie, verf of chemikalieë in dreine nie) en sin 7 (by die skoonmaakdag aansluit).","en":"Keep sentence 3 (take litter home), sentence 5 (no oil, paint or chemicals in drains) and sentence 7 (join the clean-up day)."},{"af":"Laat uit: sin 1 (inleiding – dit beskryf die probleem), sin 2 (direkte rede en 'n metafoor), sin 4 (voorbeeld met 'n getal – let op *byvoorbeeld*) en sin 6 (vergelyking en beskrywing).","en":"Leave out: sentence 1 (introduction – it describes the problem), sentence 2 (direct speech and a metaphor), sentence 4 (example with a number – note *byvoorbeeld*) and sentence 6 (simile and description)."},{"af":"Herskryf in eie woorde en veralgemeen die lys in sin 5: *olie, verf of chemikalieë* → *gevaarlike stowwe*.","en":"Rewrite in own words and generalise the list in sentence 5: *olie, verf of chemikalieë* → *gevaarlike stowwe* (dangerous substances)."}],"answer":{"af":"Feite: sinne 3, 5 en 7.\n1. Neem jou rommel saam huis toe.\n2. Moenie gevaarlike stowwe in stormwaterdreine gooi nie.\n3. Help elke maand met die skoonmaakdag.","en":"Facts: sentences 3, 5 and 7.\n1. Neem jou rommel saam huis toe.\n2. Moenie gevaarlike stowwe in stormwaterdreine gooi nie.\n3. Help elke maand met die skoonmaakdag."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter 'n swak opsomming","en":"Improve a weak summary"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder het die volgende opsomming vir die opdrag in die eerste voorbeeld geskryf. Identifiseer die foute en verduidelik hoe om dit reg te stel.\n\nIn hierdie artikel gee die skrywer wenke oor die internet.\n1. Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord en moenie dit met jou vriende deel nie.\n2. Een Graad 10-leerder het R500 verloor.\n3. Wat eenmaal op die internet is, bly vir altyd daar, soos 'n tatoeëermerk wat nooit afwas nie.\n4. Moenie op skakels druk.\n5. Stel jou profiel op privaat.","en":"A learner wrote the following summary for the instruction in the first example. Identify the mistakes and explain how to correct them.\n\nIn hierdie artikel gee die skrywer wenke oor die internet.\n1. Gebruik 'n sterk wagwoord en moenie dit met jou vriende deel nie.\n2. Een Graad 10-leerder het R500 verloor.\n3. Wat eenmaal op die internet is, bly vir altyd daar, soos 'n tatoeëermerk wat nooit afwas nie.\n4. Moenie op skakels druk.\n5. Stel jou profiel op privaat."},"steps":[{"af":"**Inleiding:** die eerste sin is nie 'n wenk nie. Dit mors woorde en kry geen punt nie – skrap dit.","en":"**Introduction:** the first sentence is not a tip. It wastes words and earns no mark – delete it."},{"af":"**Twee feite in een sin (punt 1)** en **'n voorbeeld (punt 2)**: verdeel punt 1 in twee sinne (sterk wagwoord; moenie dit deel nie) en skrap die R500-voorbeeld.","en":"**Two facts in one sentence (point 1)** and **an example (point 2)**: split point 1 into two sentences (strong password; do not share it) and delete the R500 example."},{"af":"**Afgeskryf met 'n vergelyking (punt 3):** dit is die rede, nie die wenk nie. Skryf: *Dink mooi voordat jy foto's aanlyn plaas.*","en":"**Copied, with a simile (point 3):** this is the reason, not the tip. Write: *Dink mooi voordat jy foto's aanlyn plaas.*"},{"af":"**Taalfout (punt 4):** die tweede *nie* ontbreek: *Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie.*","en":"**Language error (point 4):** the second *nie* is missing: *Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie.*"},{"af":"**Feite ontbreek en geen woordetal nie:** die wenke oor aanlyn kennisse ontmoet en 'n volwassene vertel ontbreek. Voeg dit by, tel die woorde en skryf die woordetal aan die einde.","en":"**Missing facts and no word count:** the tips about meeting online acquaintances and telling an adult are missing. Add them, count the words and write the word count at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"Foute: inleiding, twee feite in een sin, 'n voorbeeld, 'n afgeskryfde sin met 'n vergelyking, 'n ontbrekende tweede nie, ontbrekende feite en geen woordetal nie. Die verbeterde weergawe is die modelopsomming in die eerste voorbeeld.","en":"Mistakes: an introduction, two facts in one sentence, an example, a copied sentence with a simile, a missing second nie, missing facts and no word count. The corrected version is the model summary in the first example."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel die opsomming (Afdeling B) in Vraestel 1?","en":"How many marks does the summary (Section B) count in Paper 1?"},"options":[{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"70","en":"70"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die opsomming tel 10 punte: 7 vir inhoud en 3 vir taal. 30 is Afdeling A (leesbegrip) en 70 die hele vraestel.","en":"The summary counts 10 marks: 7 for content and 3 for language. 30 is Section A (comprehension) and 70 the whole paper."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die Graad 10-opsomming moet jy gewoonlik ___ feite gee.","en":"In the Grade 10 summary you usually have to give ___ facts."},"answers":{"af":["7","sewe"],"en":["7","seven","sewe"]},"explain":{"af":"Sewe feite, een inhoudspunt elk. Lees tog altyd die opdrag: as dit 'n ander getal vra, gee jy daardie getal.","en":"Seven facts, one content mark each. Always read the instruction, though: if it asks for a different number, you give that number."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["5","10","8"],"en":["5","10","8"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy moet die woordetal aan die einde van jou opsomming aandui.","en":"You must give the word count at the end of your summary."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die opdrag vra dit byna altyd, bv. '(Woordetal: 84)'. 'n Ontbrekende of vals woordetal is 'n algemene fout.","en":"True. The instruction almost always asks for it, e.g. '(Woordetal: 84)'. A missing or false word count is a common mistake."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel woorde moet 'n Graad 10-opsomming gewoonlik bevat (tensy die vraestel anders sê)?","en":"How many words should a Grade 10 summary usually contain (unless the paper says otherwise)?"},"options":[{"af":"50–60","en":"50–60"},{"af":"80–90","en":"80–90"},{"af":"120–150","en":"120–150"},{"af":"180–200","en":"180–200"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Gewoonlik 80–90 woorde vir sewe feite – ongeveer 12 woorde per sin. 180–200 woorde is die lengte van 'n transaksionele teks.","en":"Usually 80–90 words for seven facts – about 12 words per sentence. 180–200 words is the length of a transactional text."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Puntsgewys","en":"Point form"},"r":{"af":"Genommerde volsinne onder mekaar","en":"Numbered full sentences below each other"}},{"l":{"af":"Samehangende paragraaf","en":"Coherent paragraph"},"r":{"af":"Een paragraaf met verbindingswoorde","en":"One paragraph with linking words"}},{"l":{"af":"Woordetal","en":"Word count"},"r":{"af":"Die aantal woorde wat jy gebruik het","en":"The number of words you used"}},{"l":{"af":"Veralgemening","en":"Generalisation"},"r":{"af":"'n Lys vervang met een oorkoepelende woord","en":"Replacing a list with one umbrella word"}},{"l":{"af":"Eie woorde","en":"Own words"},"r":{"af":"Die feit herformuleer sonder om sinne af te skryf","en":"Rephrasing the fact without copying sentences"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie terme kom in die opdrag voor. As jy weet wat elkeen vra, verloor jy nie onnodig punte nie.","en":"These terms appear in the instruction. If you know what each one asks for, you do not lose marks unnecessarily."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een hoort NIE in 'n opsomming nie?","en":"Which one does NOT belong in a summary?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Relevante feit in jou eie woorde","en":"A relevant fact in your own words"},{"af":"'n Kort volsin wat die opdrag beantwoord","en":"A short full sentence that answers the instruction"},{"af":"Die woordetal aan die einde","en":"The word count at the end"},{"af":"'n Direkte aanhaling van wat iemand in die teks sê","en":"A direct quotation of what someone in the text says"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Direkte rede en aanhalings laat jy uit. Gee net die feit self, in jou eie woorde.","en":"You leave out direct speech and quotations. Give only the fact itself, in your own words."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As 6 of 7 van jou sinne taalkundig korrek is, kry jy ___ uit 3 vir taal.","en":"If 6 or 7 of your sentences are linguistically correct, you get ___ out of 3 for language."},"answers":{"af":["3","drie"],"en":["3","three","drie"]},"explain":{"af":"Taalpunte: 1–3 korrekte sinne = 1; 4–5 = 2; 6–7 = 3.","en":"Language marks: 1–3 correct sentences = 1; 4–5 = 2; 6–7 = 3."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["1","2","7"],"en":["1","2","7"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Jy mag twee feite in een sin skryf om woorde te spaar.","en":"You may write two facts in one sentence to save words."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Skryf een feit per sin. Twee feite in een sin maak dit moeilik om punte toe te ken, en jy kan 'n punt verloor.","en":"False. Write one fact per sentence. Two facts in one sentence make it hard to award marks, and you can lose a mark."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die nasiener verdra gewoonlik tot ___ woorde bo die woordlimiet.","en":"The marker usually tolerates up to ___ words over the word limit."},"answers":{"af":["5","vyf"],"en":["5","five","vyf"]},"explain":{"af":"Tot 5 woorde bo die limiet word gewoonlik verdra. Mik egter om binne die limiet te bly.","en":"Up to 5 words over the limit are usually tolerated. Aim to stay within the limit, though."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","2","20"],"en":["10","2","20"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder begin sy opsomming met: 'In hierdie artikel gaan ek die sewe wenke opsom.' Wat is die probleem?","en":"A learner starts his summary with: 'In hierdie artikel gaan ek die sewe wenke opsom.' What is the problem?"},"options":[{"af":"Die sin moet in die verlede tyd wees.","en":"The sentence must be in the past tense."},{"af":"Dit is 'n inleiding wat woorde mors en geen punt verdien nie.","en":"It is an introduction that wastes words and earns no mark."},{"af":"Die sin tel as een van die sewe feite, dus is daar nou te veel feite.","en":"The sentence counts as one of the seven facts, so there are now too many facts."},{"af":"Die sin moet tussen aanhalingstekens staan.","en":"The sentence must be in quotation marks."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Opsomming het geen inleiding of slot nie. Hierdie sin bevat geen feit nie, kry geen punt nie en tel tog by die woordetal.","en":"A summary has no introduction or conclusion. This sentence contains no fact, earns no mark and still counts towards the word count."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Veralgemeen die lys in een woord: 'Eet appels, lemoene, piesangs en druiwe.' → Eet ___.","en":"Generalise the list in one (Afrikaans) word: 'Eet appels, lemoene, piesangs en druiwe.' → Eet ___."},"answers":{"af":["vrugte"],"en":["vrugte","fruit"]},"explain":{"af":"Appels, lemoene, piesangs en druiwe is almal vrugte. Sitrus is te eng (net lemoene is sitrus), en groente is verkeerd.","en":"Apples, oranges, bananas and grapes are all fruit (vrugte). Citrus (sitrus) is too narrow (only oranges are citrus), and vegetables (groente) is wrong."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["groente","sitrus","vleis"],"en":["groente","sitrus","vleis"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Hoeveel woorde tel hierdie opsommingsin? 'Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie.'","en":"How many words does this summary sentence count? 'Moenie op skakels in vreemde boodskappe druk nie.'"},"answers":{"af":["8","agt"],"en":["8","eight","agt"]},"explain":{"af":"Moenie (1) op (2) skakels (3) in (4) vreemde (5) boodskappe (6) druk (7) nie (8). Elke woord tel, ook die kort woordjie 'nie'.","en":"Moenie (1) op (2) skakels (3) in (4) vreemde (5) boodskappe (6) druk (7) nie (8). Every word counts, including the short word 'nie'."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["7","9","6"],"en":["7","9","6"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Opdrag: Som op hoe gesinne water kan bespaar. Watter sin uit die teks bevat 'n RELEVANTE feit?","en":"Instruction: Summarise how families can save water. Which sentence from the text contains a RELEVANT fact?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dam het soos 'n spieël in die oggendson geblink.","en":"Die dam het soos 'n spieël in die oggendson geblink."},{"af":"'Water is lewe,' sê oom Koos.","en":"'Water is lewe,' sê oom Koos."},{"af":"Draai die kraan toe terwyl jy jou tande borsel.","en":"Draai die kraan toe terwyl jy jou tande borsel."},{"af":"Ons buurman het verlede jaar sy swembad volgemaak.","en":"Ons buurman het verlede jaar sy swembad volgemaak."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Net die derde sin sê wat 'n gesin kan doen om water te spaar. Die ander is 'n vergelyking, direkte rede en 'n irrelevante voorbeeld.","en":"Only the third sentence says what a family can do to save water (turn off the tap while brushing teeth). The others are a simile, direct speech and an irrelevant example."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die beste opsommingsin vir hierdie sin uit 'n teks? 'Wat jy ook al doen, en al lyk dit hoe eg, moet jy nooit op 'n skakel in 'n e-pos van 'n onbekende persoon druk nie, want dit kan jou duur te staan kom.'","en":"Which one is the best summary sentence for this sentence from a text? 'Wat jy ook al doen, en al lyk dit hoe eg, moet jy nooit op 'n skakel in 'n e-pos van 'n onbekende persoon druk nie, want dit kan jou duur te staan kom.'"},"options":[{"af":"Moenie op skakels in e-posse van onbekendes druk nie.","en":"Moenie op skakels in e-posse van onbekendes druk nie."},{"af":"Wat jy ook al doen, en al lyk dit hoe eg, moet jy nooit op 'n skakel druk nie.","en":"Wat jy ook al doen, en al lyk dit hoe eg, moet jy nooit op 'n skakel druk nie."},{"af":"Al lyk 'n e-pos hoe eg, kan dit jou duur te staan kom.","en":"Al lyk 'n e-pos hoe eg, kan dit jou duur te staan kom."},{"af":"E-posse van onbekendes is gevaarlik en duur.","en":"E-posse van onbekendes is gevaarlik en duur."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin behou die wenk (moenie op die skakel druk nie) en die belangrike detail (onbekende sender), en laat die klem en die rede weg. Die tweede skryf af, die derde verloor die wenk en die vierde verdraai dit.","en":"The first sentence keeps the tip (do not click the link) and the important detail (unknown sender), and leaves out the emphasis and the reason. The second copies, the third loses the tip and the fourth distorts it."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter weergawe van dieselfde feit sal die inhoudspunt kry EN as 'n taalkundig korrekte sin tel?","en":"Which version of the same fact will earn the content mark AND count as a linguistically correct sentence?"},"options":[{"af":"Skakels in onbekende boodskappe – nie druk nie.","en":"Skakels in onbekende boodskappe – nie druk nie."},{"af":"Moenie op skakels in onbekende boodskappe druk.","en":"Moenie op skakels in onbekende boodskappe druk."},{"af":"'n Leerder het R500 verloor toe hy op 'n skakel gedruk het.","en":"'n Leerder het R500 verloor toe hy op 'n skakel gedruk het."},{"af":"Moenie op skakels in onbekende boodskappe druk nie.","en":"Moenie op skakels in onbekende boodskappe druk nie."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die laaste sin is 'n volsin met die korrekte dubbele ontkenning. Die eerste is nie 'n volsin nie, die tweede het nie die tweede *nie* nie, en die derde is 'n voorbeeld, nie die wenk nie.","en":"The last sentence is a full sentence with the correct double negative. The first is not a full sentence, the second lacks the second *nie*, and the third is an example, not the tip."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jou opsomming het 97 woorde, maar die limiet is 80–90 woorde. Wat is die beste plan?","en":"Your summary has 97 words, but the limit is 80–90 words. What is the best plan?"},"options":[{"af":"Skrap onnodige woorde, voorbeelde en ekstra verbindingswoorde sonder om 'n feit te verloor.","en":"Delete unnecessary words, examples and extra linking words without losing a fact."},{"af":"Los dit so, want net die inhoud tel punte.","en":"Leave it as it is, because only the content earns marks."},{"af":"Skrap twee van die feite sodat dit korter is.","en":"Delete two of the facts so that it is shorter."},{"af":"Skryf 'n kleiner woordetal neer as die werklike getal.","en":"Write down a smaller word count than the real number."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"97 is meer as 5 woorde oor die limiet, dus moet jy sny – maar nie feite nie, want elke feit is 'n punt. Kyk na herhaling, voorbeelde, lang frases en verbindingswoorde. 'n Vals woordetal is oneerlik en die nasiener kan dit maklik kontroleer.","en":"97 is more than 5 words over the limit, so you must cut – but not facts, because every fact is a mark. Look at repetition, examples, long phrases and linking words. A false word count is dishonest and the marker can easily check it."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t2-roman-kortverhaal","title":{"af":"Prosa: roman en kortverhaal","en":"Prose: novel and short story"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n prosa-uittreksel kan ontleed: intrige, konflik, karakters, verteller, ruimte, tyd en tema, en kontekstuele vrae en 'n kort literêre opstel kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to analyse a prose extract: plot, conflict, characters, narrator, setting, time and theme, and answer contextual questions and a short literary essay."},"summary":{"af":"## Roman en kortverhaal\n\n| Kortverhaal | Roman |\n|---|---|\n| kort; jy kan dit in een sitting lees | lank, in hoofstukke |\n| min karakters | baie karakters en newekarakters |\n| een hoofgebeurtenis | verskeie gebeure en newe-intriges |\n| beperkte tyd en ruimte | dikwels 'n lang tydsverloop en verskillende plekke |\n| begin dikwels *in medias res* (midde-in die aksie) | begin dikwels met 'n uitgebreide eksposisie |\n| dikwels 'n onverwagte of oop einde | meer ruimte om karakters te laat ontwikkel |\n\n## Intrige en struktuur\n\nDie **gebeure** is alles wat in die verhaal gebeur. Die **intrige** (storielyn) is hoe die skrywer die gebeure rangskik en deur **oorsaak en gevolg** aan mekaar koppel.\n\n1. **Eksposisie:** die karakters, ruimte en situasie word bekendgestel.\n2. **Komplikasie / stygende aksie:** die konflik begin en die spanning neem toe.\n3. **Klimaks / hoogtepunt:** die spanning is die hoogste; dit is die keerpunt.\n4. **Afwikkeling:** die gevolge van die klimaks; die spanning neem af.\n5. **Ontknoping:** die finale uitkoms; die konflik word opgelos (of nie).\n\n## Konflik en spanning\n\n**Konflik** dryf die verhaal.\n\n- **Innerlike konflik:** 'n stryd binne 'n karakter (*Moet ek die waarheid praat?*).\n- **Uiterlike konflik:** karakter teen karakter; karakter teen die samelewing (reëls, vooroordeel, armoede); karakter teen die natuur (droogte, 'n storm, 'n veldbrand).\n\n**Spanning** is die onrus of nuuskierigheid wat die leser laat aanhou lees: wat gaan gebeur?\n\n## Karakters\n\n- **Protagonis / hoofkarakter:** die karakter om wie die verhaal draai.\n- **Antagonis / teenspeler:** die karakter (of mag) wat teen die protagonis werk.\n- **Newekarakters:** ondersteun die verhaal en die hoofkarakter.\n- **Ronde karakter:** veelkantig, met sterk en swak eienskappe. **Plat karakter:** net een of twee eienskappe.\n- **Dinamiese karakter:** verander of groei. **Statiese karakter:** bly dieselfde.\n\n### Karakterisering\n\n- **Direk:** die verteller sê self hoe die karakter is: *Wikus was 'n skaam seun.*\n- **Indirek:** jy lei dit af uit die karakter se **aksies**, **dialoog**, **gedagtes**, die **reaksies van ander**, sy **naam** en **voorkoms**.\n\n## Verteller en vertelperspektief\n\n| Verteller | Kenmerke |\n|---|---|\n| **Ek-verteller** (eerstepersoonsverteller) | 'n karakter vertel met *ek*; **subjektief**: ons ken net sy of haar gedagtes; kan **onbetroubaar** wees |\n| **Alwetende derdepersoonsverteller** | vertel met *hy/sy*; ken die gedagtes en gevoelens van **alle** karakters |\n| **Beperkte derdepersoonsverteller** | vertel met *hy/sy*, maar volg net **een** karakter se gedagtes |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die ek-verteller is nie die skrywer nie. Dit is 'n karakter in die verhaal.\n\n## Ruimte en tyd\n\n- **Fisiese ruimte:** die plek en tyd waar die verhaal afspeel (*'n sitrusplaas buite Brits, in die winter*).\n- **Sosiale ruimte:** die gemeenskap, verhoudings en omstandighede (*armoede, 'n streng skool*).\n- **Psigiese ruimte:** die innerlike wêreld van 'n karakter: sy gedagtes en gevoelens.\n- **Verteltyd:** hoe lank dit neem om die verhaal te lees (of hoeveel bladsye dit beslaan). **Vertelde tyd:** hoe lank die gebeure in die verhaal duur.\n- **Chronologies:** in die volgorde waarin dit gebeur het. **Terugflits:** 'n gebeurtenis uit die verlede word tussenin vertel. **Vooruitwysing:** 'n leidraad oor wat later gaan gebeur.\n\n## Tema, motief, simbool en ironie\n\n- **Onderwerp:** waaroor die verhaal gaan (*'n seun wat geboelie word*).\n- **Tema:** die dieper boodskap of insig (*Moed beteken om die waarheid te praat, al is dit moeilik*). Skryf 'n tema as 'n volsin.\n- **Motief:** 'n element (beeld, voorwerp of idee) wat herhaaldelik voorkom en die tema ondersteun.\n- **Simbool:** 'n konkrete ding wat vir iets anders staan (*'n toe hek = afsondering*).\n- **Verbale ironie:** jy sê die teenoorgestelde van wat jy bedoel. **Situasie-ironie:** die uitkoms is die teenoorgestelde van wat jy verwag.\n- **Atmosfeer:** die stemming wat die leser ervaar (*gespanne, onheilspellend, vrolik*).\n\n## Die einde\n\n**Geslote einde:** die konflik word opgelos. **Oop einde:** die leser moet self besluit wat gebeur. **Verrassingseinde:** 'n onverwagte wending aan die slot.\n\n## In die eksamen (Vraestel 2)\n\n- **Kontekstuele vrae** op 'n uittreksel: *Waar en wanneer speel dit af? Wat openbaar dit oor X se karakter? Haal 'n woord aan wat ... Verduidelik die ironie. Is X se optrede regverdigbaar? Motiveer.*\n- By *motiveer* gee jy 'n standpunt **en** bewys uit die teks. *Haal aan* beteken: skryf die presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens.\n- **Kort literêre opstel** (±250 woorde): 'n inleiding met 'n duidelike stelling, drie paragrawe met voorbeelde uit die teks, en 'n slot.\n\n> **Wenk:** Moenie in 'n opstel die storie net oorvertel nie. Elke paragraaf moet die vraag beantwoord en met bewys uit die teks gestaaf word.","en":"## Novel and short story\n\n| Short story | Novel |\n|---|---|\n| short; you can read it in one sitting | long, in chapters |\n| few characters | many characters and minor characters |\n| one main event | several events and subplots |\n| limited time and setting | often a long time span and different places |\n| often starts *in medias res* (in the middle of the action) | often starts with an extended exposition |\n| often an unexpected or open ending | more space to let characters develop |\n\n## Plot and structure\n\nThe **events** are everything that happens in the story. The **plot** (intrige/storielyn) is how the writer arranges the events and links them through **cause and effect**.\n\n1. **Exposition:** the characters, setting and situation are introduced.\n2. **Complication / rising action:** the conflict starts and the tension increases.\n3. **Climax:** the tension is at its highest; it is the turning point.\n4. **Falling action (afwikkeling):** the consequences of the climax; the tension decreases.\n5. **Resolution (ontknoping):** the final outcome; the conflict is resolved (or not).\n\n## Conflict and suspense\n\n**Conflict** drives the story.\n\n- **Internal conflict:** a struggle inside a character (*Should I tell the truth?*).\n- **External conflict:** character versus character; character versus society (rules, prejudice, poverty); character versus nature (drought, a storm, a veld fire).\n\n**Suspense** is the unease or curiosity that keeps the reader reading: what is going to happen?\n\n## Characters\n\n- **Protagonist / main character:** the character the story revolves around.\n- **Antagonist:** the character (or force) that works against the protagonist.\n- **Minor characters:** support the story and the main character.\n- **Round character:** many-sided, with strong and weak traits. **Flat character:** only one or two traits.\n- **Dynamic character:** changes or grows. **Static character:** stays the same.\n\n### Characterisation\n\n- **Direct:** the narrator says what the character is like: *Wikus was 'n skaam seun.*\n- **Indirect:** you deduce it from the character's **actions**, **dialogue**, **thoughts**, the **reactions of others**, his **name** and **appearance**.\n\n## Narrator and point of view\n\n| Narrator | Features |\n|---|---|\n| **First-person narrator** (ek-verteller) | a character narrates with *ek* (I); **subjective**: we know only his or her thoughts; can be **unreliable** |\n| **Omniscient third-person narrator** | narrates with *hy/sy* (he/she); knows the thoughts and feelings of **all** characters |\n| **Limited third-person narrator** | narrates with *hy/sy*, but follows only **one** character's thoughts |\n\n> **Common mistake:** The first-person narrator is not the author. He or she is a character in the story.\n\n## Setting and time\n\n- **Physical setting:** the place and time where the story takes place (*a citrus farm outside Brits, in winter*).\n- **Social setting:** the community, relationships and circumstances (*poverty, a strict school*).\n- **Psychological setting:** a character's inner world: his thoughts and feelings.\n- **Narrative time (verteltyd):** how long it takes to read the story (or how many pages it covers). **Narrated time (vertelde tyd):** how long the events in the story last.\n- **Chronological:** in the order in which it happened. **Flashback (terugflits):** an event from the past is told in between. **Foreshadowing (vooruitwysing):** a clue about what will happen later.\n\n## Theme, motif, symbol and irony\n\n- **Subject (onderwerp):** what the story is about (*a boy who is bullied*).\n- **Theme:** the deeper message or insight (*Courage means telling the truth, even when it is hard*). Write a theme as a full sentence.\n- **Motif:** an element (image, object or idea) that recurs and supports the theme.\n- **Symbol:** a concrete thing that stands for something else (*a closed gate = isolation*).\n- **Verbal irony:** you say the opposite of what you mean. **Situational irony:** the outcome is the opposite of what you expect.\n- **Atmosphere:** the mood the reader experiences (*tense, ominous, cheerful*).\n\n## The ending\n\n**Closed ending:** the conflict is resolved. **Open ending:** the reader must decide what happens. **Surprise ending:** an unexpected twist at the end.\n\n## In the exam (Paper 2)\n\n- **Contextual questions** on an extract: *Where and when is it set? What does it reveal about X's character? Quote a word that ... Explain the irony. Is X's behaviour justifiable? Motivate.*\n- With *motivate* you give a point of view **and** evidence from the text. *Quote* means: write the exact words in quotation marks.\n- **Short literary essay** (±250 words): an introduction with a clear statement, three paragraphs with examples from the text, and a conclusion.\n\n> **Tip:** In an essay, do not simply retell the story. Every paragraph must answer the question and be supported with evidence from the text."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Intrige (storielyn)","en":"Plot"},"def":{"af":"Die skrywer se rangskikking van die gebeure, wat deur oorsaak en gevolg aan mekaar gekoppel is.","en":"The writer's arrangement of the events, linked through cause and effect."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaks (hoogtepunt)","en":"Climax"},"def":{"af":"Die punt in die verhaal waar die spanning die hoogste is; die keerpunt van die konflik.","en":"The point in the story where the tension is at its highest; the turning point of the conflict."}},{"term":{"af":"Konflik","en":"Conflict"},"def":{"af":"Die stryd wat die verhaal dryf: innerlik (binne 'n karakter) of uiterlik (teen 'n ander karakter, die samelewing of die natuur).","en":"The struggle that drives the story: internal (inside a character) or external (against another character, society or nature)."}},{"term":{"af":"Protagonis","en":"Protagonist"},"def":{"af":"Die hoofkarakter om wie die verhaal draai.","en":"The main character the story revolves around."}},{"term":{"af":"Antagonis (teenspeler)","en":"Antagonist"},"def":{"af":"Die karakter of mag wat teen die protagonis werk.","en":"The character or force that works against the protagonist."}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte karakterisering","en":"Indirect characterisation"},"def":{"af":"Die leser lei 'n karakter se eienskappe af uit sy aksies, dialoog, gedagtes, voorkoms en die reaksies van ander.","en":"The reader deduces a character's traits from his actions, dialogue, thoughts, appearance and the reactions of others."}},{"term":{"af":"Ek-verteller","en":"First-person narrator"},"def":{"af":"'n Karakter wat die verhaal met 'ek' vertel; subjektief en soms onbetroubaar.","en":"A character who tells the story with 'ek' (I); subjective and sometimes unreliable."}},{"term":{"af":"Alwetende verteller","en":"Omniscient narrator"},"def":{"af":"'n Derdepersoonsverteller wat die gedagtes en gevoelens van al die karakters ken.","en":"A third-person narrator who knows the thoughts and feelings of all the characters."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruimte (fisies, sosiaal, psigies)","en":"Setting (physical, social, psychological)"},"def":{"af":"Die plek en tyd, die gemeenskap en omstandighede, en die innerlike wêreld van 'n karakter.","en":"The place and time, the community and circumstances, and a character's inner world."}},{"term":{"af":"Tema","en":"Theme"},"def":{"af":"Die dieper boodskap of insig van die verhaal, geskryf as 'n volsin; nie dieselfde as die onderwerp nie.","en":"The deeper message or insight of the story, written as a full sentence; not the same as the subject."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kontekstuele vrae op 'n uittreksel","en":"Contextual questions on an extract"},"problem":{"af":"**Die hek** (eie kortverhaal – uittreksel)\n\nDie hek kners toe Wikus dit agter hom toetrek. Dit is al donker, en die lemoenbome staan soos swart wagte in rye langs die grondpad. Iewers ver blaf 'n hond.\n\n\"Jy's laat,\" sê Pa. Hy sit op die stoep met sy kierie oor sy knieë. Sedert die ongeluk by die myn praat hy min.\n\n\"Rugbyoefening het uitgerek, Pa,\" lieg Wikus. Hy druk sy hande diep in sy sakke sodat Pa nie die skaafplekke op sy kneukels sien nie.\n\nPa kyk lank na hom. \"Jou ma het vir jou kos in die oond gelos.\"\n\nIn die kombuis staan Wikus by die venster. Hy dink aan Dewald en sy vriende wat hom elke middag by die taxi-staanplek voorlê. Hy dink aan die R200 vir Pa se medisyne wat Dewald vanmiddag uit sy hand geruk het. Môre, besluit hy. Môre sê hy vir iemand.\n\nBuite begin die hond weer blaf. Die hek kners.\n\n**Vrae:**\n(a) Beskryf die fisiese ruimte. (2)\n(b) Watter soort verteller word gebruik? Motiveer. (2)\n(c) Wat openbaar die woorde \"lieg Wikus\" en die hande in sy sakke oor sy karakter? (2)\n(d) Benoem TWEE soorte konflik in die uittreksel. (2)\n(e) Benoem die stylfiguur in \"die lemoenbome staan soos swart wagte\" en verduidelik watter atmosfeer dit skep. (2)\n(f) Verduidelik die funksie van die laaste twee sinne. (2)","en":"**Die hek** (eie kortverhaal – uittreksel)\n\nDie hek kners toe Wikus dit agter hom toetrek. Dit is al donker, en die lemoenbome staan soos swart wagte in rye langs die grondpad. Iewers ver blaf 'n hond.\n\n\"Jy's laat,\" sê Pa. Hy sit op die stoep met sy kierie oor sy knieë. Sedert die ongeluk by die myn praat hy min.\n\n\"Rugbyoefening het uitgerek, Pa,\" lieg Wikus. Hy druk sy hande diep in sy sakke sodat Pa nie die skaafplekke op sy kneukels sien nie.\n\nPa kyk lank na hom. \"Jou ma het vir jou kos in die oond gelos.\"\n\nIn die kombuis staan Wikus by die venster. Hy dink aan Dewald en sy vriende wat hom elke middag by die taxi-staanplek voorlê. Hy dink aan die R200 vir Pa se medisyne wat Dewald vanmiddag uit sy hand geruk het. Môre, besluit hy. Môre sê hy vir iemand.\n\nBuite begin die hond weer blaf. Die hek kners.\n\n**The gate** (our own short story – extract, English translation)\n\nThe gate creaks when Wikus pulls it shut behind him. It is already dark, and the orange trees stand like black guards in rows along the dirt road. Somewhere far away a dog barks.\n\n\"You're late,\" says Dad. He sits on the stoep with his walking stick across his knees. Since the accident at the mine he speaks little.\n\n\"Rugby practice ran late, Dad,\" Wikus lies. He pushes his hands deep into his pockets so that Dad does not see the grazes on his knuckles.\n\nDad looks at him for a long time. \"Your mom left food for you in the oven.\"\n\nIn the kitchen Wikus stands at the window. He thinks of Dewald and his friends who lie in wait for him every afternoon at the taxi rank. He thinks of the R200 for Dad's medicine that Dewald snatched out of his hand this afternoon. Tomorrow, he decides. Tomorrow he will tell someone.\n\nOutside the dog starts barking again. The gate creaks.\n\n**Questions:**\n(a) Describe the physical setting. (2)\n(b) What kind of narrator is used? Motivate. (2)\n(c) What do the words \"lieg Wikus\" (Wikus lies) and the hands in his pockets reveal about his character? (2)\n(d) Name TWO kinds of conflict in the extract. (2)\n(e) Name the figure of speech in \"die lemoenbome staan soos swart wagte\" and explain what atmosphere it creates. (2)\n(f) Explain the function of the last two sentences. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 'n Sitrusplaas met 'n lemoenboord en 'n grondpad ✔, in die aand / dit is donker ✔.","en":"(a) A citrus farm with an orange orchard and a dirt road ✔, in the evening / it is dark ✔."},{"af":"(b) 'n Beperkte derdepersoonsverteller ✔. Die verhaal word met 'hy' vertel, maar ons ken net Wikus se gedagtes, bv. 'Hy dink aan Dewald ...' ✔.","en":"(b) A limited third-person narrator ✔. The story is told with 'hy' (he), but we know only Wikus's thoughts, e.g. 'Hy dink aan Dewald ...' ✔."},{"af":"(c) Wikus wil sy beseerde pa beskerm en hom nie bekommer nie ✔; hy hou sy probleme vir homself / hy skaam hom ✔. (Indirekte karakterisering deur sy aksies.) (d) Uiterlike konflik: Wikus teen Dewald, karakter teen karakter ✔; innerlike konflik: moet hy iemand vertel of nie ✔.","en":"(c) Wikus wants to protect his injured father and not worry him ✔; he keeps his problems to himself / he is ashamed ✔. (Indirect characterisation through his actions.) (d) External conflict: Wikus versus Dewald, character versus character ✔; internal conflict: should he tell someone or not ✔."},{"af":"(e) 'n Vergelyking (soos) ✔. Die bome lyk dreigend, soos wagte wat hom in die donker dophou: dit skep 'n gespanne, onheilspellende atmosfeer ✔.","en":"(e) A simile (soos – like) ✔. The trees look threatening, like guards watching him in the dark: it creates a tense, ominous atmosphere ✔."},{"af":"(f) Die krakende hek herhaal die begin (motief) en wys dat iemand by die hek is: dit skep spanning ✔. Dit is 'n oop einde, want die leser weet nie wie daar is nie – Dewald of iemand anders ✔.","en":"(f) The creaking gate repeats the beginning (motif) and shows that someone is at the gate: it creates suspense ✔. It is an open ending, because the reader does not know who is there – Dewald or someone else ✔."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Sitrusplaas, in die donker. (b) Beperkte derdepersoonsverteller – net Wikus se gedagtes. (c) Beskermend teenoor sy pa; hou probleme vir homself. (d) Uiterlik (Wikus teen Dewald) en innerlik (vertel of nie). (e) Vergelyking; onheilspellende atmosfeer. (f) Spanning en 'n oop einde; die hek is 'n motief.","en":"(a) Citrus farm, in the dark. (b) Limited third-person narrator – only Wikus's thoughts. (c) Protective towards his father; keeps problems to himself. (d) External (Wikus versus Dewald) and internal (tell or not). (e) Simile; ominous atmosphere. (f) Suspense and an open ending; the gate is a motif."}},{"title":{"af":"Verteller en vertelperspektief","en":"Narrator and point of view"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die twee uittreksels (eie tekste) en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**A:** Ek het geweet Ma sou kwaad wees, maar ek het tog die bakkie se sleutels gevat. Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie.\n\n**B:** Lerato glimlag vir haar maats, maar binne-in is sy doodbang. Langs haar sit Johan en wonder of iemand sy nuwe skoene raaksien. Juffrou Nel, wat voor die klas staan, weet reeds wie die prys gaan wen.\n\n(a) Watter soort verteller word in elke uittreksel gebruik? Motiveer.\n(b) Waarom moet die leser versigtig wees om die verteller in A heeltemal te glo?","en":"Read the two extracts (our own texts) and answer the questions.\n\n**A:** Ek het geweet Ma sou kwaad wees, maar ek het tog die bakkie se sleutels gevat. Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie.\n(I knew Mom would be angry, but I took the bakkie's keys anyway. Nobody in this house understands me.)\n\n**B:** Lerato glimlag vir haar maats, maar binne-in is sy doodbang. Langs haar sit Johan en wonder of iemand sy nuwe skoene raaksien. Juffrou Nel, wat voor die klas staan, weet reeds wie die prys gaan wen.\n(Lerato smiles at her friends, but inside she is terrified. Next to her sits Johan, wondering whether anyone notices his new shoes. Miss Nel, who is standing in front of the class, already knows who will win the prize.)\n\n(a) What kind of narrator is used in each extract? Motivate.\n(b) Why should the reader be careful about fully believing the narrator in A?"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) A: 'n **Ek-verteller** (eerstepersoonsverteller) – die karakter vertel self met 'ek'.","en":"(a) A: a **first-person narrator** – the character narrates himself with 'ek' (I)."},{"af":"B: 'n **Alwetende derdepersoonsverteller** – die verhaal word met 'sy/hy' vertel, en die verteller ken die gedagtes van Lerato (doodbang), Johan (wonder oor sy skoene) én Juffrou Nel (weet wie gaan wen).","en":"B: an **omniscient third-person narrator** – the story is told with 'sy/hy' (she/he), and the narrator knows the thoughts of Lerato (terrified), Johan (wondering about his shoes) and Miss Nel (knows who will win)."},{"af":"(b) Die ek-verteller is **subjektief**: ons sien net sy kant. 'Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie' is sy mening, nie 'n feit nie – hy probeer dalk regverdig waarom hy die sleutels gevat het. Hy kan dus **onbetroubaar** wees.","en":"(b) The first-person narrator is **subjective**: we see only his side. 'Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie' (Nobody in this house understands me) is his opinion, not a fact – he may be trying to justify why he took the keys. He can therefore be **unreliable**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) A: ek-verteller; B: alwetende derdepersoonsverteller. (b) Die ek-verteller is subjektief en moontlik onbetroubaar: hy gee net sy eie kant.","en":"(a) A: first-person narrator; B: omniscient third-person narrator. (b) The first-person narrator is subjective and possibly unreliable: he gives only his own side."}},{"title":{"af":"Struktuur, ironie en die einde","en":"Structure, irony and the ending"},"problem":{"af":"**Die spykerskoene** (opsomming van 'n eie kortverhaal)\n\n(1) Thandi (15) woon by haar ouma in Brits. Sy is die vinnigste atleet in Graad 10.\n(2) Die afrigter sê wie vir die streekspan wil probeer, moet spykerskoene hê. Ouma het nie geld nie. Thandi begin smiddae in 'n winkel werk om te spaar, maar sy mis oefeninge en is gedurig moeg.\n(3) Op die dag van die proewe het sy steeds te min geld vir skoene. Sy hardloop kaalvoet – en wen die 400 m met een tree.\n(4) Die afrigter kies haar vir die span, en die skool skenk vir haar spykerskoene.\n(5) Daardie aand gee Thandi haar spaargeld vir Ouma om die kragrekening te betaal.\n\n**Vrae:** (a) Watter deel (1–5) pas by elke fase van die intrige? (b) Verduidelik die situasie-ironie. (c) Is die einde oop, geslote of 'n verrassingseinde? Motiveer.","en":"**Die spykerskoene** (The running spikes – summary of our own short story, English translation)\n\n(1) Thandi (15) lives with her grandmother in Brits. She is the fastest athlete in Grade 10.\n(2) The coach says whoever wants to try out for the regional team must have running spikes. Grandma has no money. Thandi starts working in a shop in the afternoons to save, but she misses practices and is constantly tired.\n(3) On the day of the trials she still has too little money for shoes. She runs barefoot – and wins the 400 m by one stride.\n(4) The coach chooses her for the team, and the school donates running spikes to her.\n(5) That evening Thandi gives her savings to Grandma to pay the electricity bill.\n\n**Questions:** (a) Which part (1–5) fits each phase of the plot? (b) Explain the situational irony. (c) Is the ending open, closed or a surprise ending? Motivate."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 1 = eksposisie (Thandi, Ouma en Brits word bekendgestel); 2 = komplikasie / stygende aksie (sy het skoene nodig en die spanning neem toe).","en":"(a) 1 = exposition (Thandi, Grandma and Brits are introduced); 2 = complication / rising action (she needs shoes and the tension increases)."},{"af":"3 = klimaks (die wedloop: die spanning is die hoogste); 4 = afwikkeling (die gevolge: sy word gekies en kry skoene); 5 = ontknoping (die finale uitkoms by die huis).","en":"3 = climax (the race: the tension is at its highest); 4 = falling action (the consequences: she is chosen and gets shoes); 5 = resolution (the final outcome at home)."},{"af":"(b) Situasie-ironie: Thandi werk so hard om skoene te koop dat sy oefeninge mis – en dan wen sy sonder skoene. Die uitkoms is die teenoorgestelde van wat ons verwag.","en":"(b) Situational irony: Thandi works so hard to buy shoes that she misses practices – and then she wins without shoes. The outcome is the opposite of what we expect."},{"af":"(c) 'n Geslote einde: die konflik (geen skoene nie) is opgelos. Die laaste gebeurtenis wys ook dat Thandi ontwikkel het: sy dink nou eerste aan Ouma (dinamiese karakter).","en":"(c) A closed ending: the conflict (no shoes) is resolved. The last event also shows that Thandi has developed: she now thinks of Grandma first (dynamic character)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) 1 eksposisie, 2 komplikasie, 3 klimaks, 4 afwikkeling, 5 ontknoping. (b) Sy werk vir skoene, maar wen kaalvoet. (c) Geslote einde – die konflik is opgelos.","en":"(a) 1 exposition, 2 complication, 3 climax, 4 falling action, 5 resolution. (b) She works for shoes, but wins barefoot. (c) Closed ending – the conflict is resolved."}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan 'n kort literêre opstel","en":"Plan a short literary essay"},"problem":{"af":"Beplan 'n literêre opstel van ±250 woorde oor die uittreksel *Die hek* in die eerste voorbeeld: **Bespreek hoe die ruimte die konflik in die verhaal versterk.**","en":"Plan a literary essay of ±250 words on the extract *Die hek* in the first example: **Discuss how the setting strengthens the conflict in the story.** (Bespreek hoe die ruimte die konflik in die verhaal versterk.)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Inleiding met 'n stelling:** *In 'Die hek' versterk die fisiese, sosiale en psigiese ruimte die konflik tussen Wikus en Dewald, en die stryd binne Wikus self.*","en":"**Introduction with a statement:** *In 'Die hek' versterk die fisiese, sosiale en psigiese ruimte die konflik tussen Wikus en Dewald, en die stryd binne Wikus self.* (In 'Die hek' the physical, social and psychological setting strengthen the conflict between Wikus and Dewald, and the struggle inside Wikus himself.)"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 1 – fisiese ruimte:** die donker plaas, die bome 'soos swart wagte' en die krakende hek skep 'n bedreigende atmosfeer; die gevaar van buite (Dewald) voel naby.","en":"**Paragraph 1 – physical setting:** the dark farm, the trees 'soos swart wagte' (like black guards) and the creaking gate create a threatening atmosphere; the danger from outside (Dewald) feels close."},{"af":"**Paragraaf 2 – sosiale ruimte:** Pa is ná die myn-ongeluk beseer en die geld is min. Daarom is die gesteelde R200 so ernstig, en daarom wil Wikus sy pa nie nog meer bekommer nie.","en":"**Paragraph 2 – social setting:** Dad is injured after the mine accident and money is short. That is why the stolen R200 is so serious, and why Wikus does not want to worry his father even more."},{"af":"**Paragraaf 3 – psigiese ruimte:** Wikus se skaamte en vrees (hy lieg, hy steek sy hande weg) wys sy innerlike konflik: moet hy iemand vertel?","en":"**Paragraph 3 – psychological setting:** Wikus's shame and fear (he lies, he hides his hands) show his internal conflict: should he tell someone?"},{"af":"**Slot:** koppel terug na die stelling: die ruimte maak die konflik meer intens, en die oop einde by die hek laat die spanning voortduur. Moenie die storie net oorvertel nie.","en":"**Conclusion:** link back to the statement: the setting makes the conflict more intense, and the open ending at the gate keeps the suspense going. Do not simply retell the story."}],"answer":{"af":"Inleiding (stelling) → fisiese ruimte → sosiale ruimte → psigiese ruimte → slot wat terugkoppel; elke paragraaf met bewys uit die teks.","en":"Introduction (statement) → physical setting → social setting → psychological setting → conclusion that links back; every paragraph with evidence from the text."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter kenmerk is tipies van 'n KORTVERHAAL?","en":"Which feature is typical of a SHORT STORY?"},"options":[{"af":"Baie karakters en verskeie newe-intriges","en":"Many characters and several subplots"},{"af":"Een hoofgebeurtenis met min karakters","en":"One main event with few characters"},{"af":"Dit strek altyd oor baie jare","en":"It always covers many years"},{"af":"Dit het altyd 'n gelukkige einde","en":"It always has a happy ending"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Kortverhaal is kort en gekonsentreerd: een hoofgebeurtenis, min karakters en beperkte tyd en ruimte. Baie karakters en newe-intriges pas by 'n roman.","en":"A short story is short and concentrated: one main event, few characters and limited time and setting. Many characters and subplots suit a novel."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die karakter wat teen die hoofkarakter werk, is die ___.","en":"The character who works against the main character is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["antagonis","teenspeler","die antagonis","die teenspeler"],"en":["antagonis","teenspeler","antagonist","the antagonist"]},"explain":{"af":"Die antagonis (teenspeler) werk teen die protagonis (hoofkarakter) en veroorsaak dikwels die uiterlike konflik.","en":"The antagonist (antagonis/teenspeler) works against the protagonist (main character) and often causes the external conflict."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["protagonis","newekarakter","verteller"],"en":["protagonist","minor character","narrator"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Ek-verteller ken die gedagtes van al die karakters in die verhaal.","en":"A first-person narrator knows the thoughts of all the characters in the story."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die ek-verteller is self 'n karakter en ken net sy eie gedagtes; daarom is hy subjektief. Die alwetende verteller ken almal se gedagtes.","en":"False. The first-person narrator is a character himself and knows only his own thoughts; that is why he is subjective. The omniscient narrator knows everyone's thoughts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die deel van die intrige waar die spanning die hoogste is, is die ___.","en":"The part of the plot where the tension is at its highest is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["klimaks","hoogtepunt","die klimaks","die hoogtepunt"],"en":["climax","the climax","klimaks","hoogtepunt"]},"explain":{"af":"Die klimaks (hoogtepunt) is die keerpunt. Daarna volg die afwikkeling en ontknoping; die eksposisie is aan die begin.","en":"The climax (klimaks/hoogtepunt) is the turning point. After it come the falling action and resolution; the exposition is at the beginning."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["eksposisie","afwikkeling","ontknoping"],"en":["exposition","falling action","resolution"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Terugflits","en":"Flashback"},"r":{"af":"'n Gebeurtenis uit die verlede word tussenin vertel","en":"An event from the past is told in between"}},{"l":{"af":"Vooruitwysing","en":"Foreshadowing"},"r":{"af":"'n Leidraad oor wat later gaan gebeur","en":"A clue about what will happen later"}},{"l":{"af":"In medias res","en":"In medias res"},"r":{"af":"Die verhaal begin midde-in die aksie","en":"The story starts in the middle of the action"}},{"l":{"af":"Verrassingseinde","en":"Surprise ending"},"r":{"af":"'n Onverwagte wending aan die slot","en":"An unexpected twist at the end"}},{"l":{"af":"Psigiese ruimte","en":"Psychological setting"},"r":{"af":"Die gedagtes en gevoelens binne 'n karakter","en":"The thoughts and feelings inside a character"}}],"explain":{"af":"Hierdie terme gaan oor tyd, struktuur en ruimte. In die eksamen moet jy die term kan benoem én verduidelik hoe dit in die uittreksel werk.","en":"These terms are about time, structure and setting. In the exam you must be able to name the term and explain how it works in the extract."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n TEMA eerder as 'n onderwerp?","en":"Which one is a THEME rather than a subject?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Seun wat geboelie word","en":"A boy who is bullied"},{"af":"Rugby by 'n skool in Brits","en":"Rugby at a school in Brits"},{"af":"'n Sitrusplaas in die winter","en":"A citrus farm in winter"},{"af":"Moed beteken om die waarheid te praat, al is dit moeilik","en":"Courage means telling the truth, even when it is hard"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Tema is die dieper boodskap, geskryf as 'n volsin. Die ander drie sê net waaroor die verhaal gaan of waar dit afspeel.","en":"A theme is the deeper message, written as a full sentence. The other three only say what the story is about or where it is set."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die tydsduur van die gebeure in die verhaal (bv. een hele somervakansie in 'n verhaal van vyf bladsye) noem ons die ___.","en":"The duration of the events in the story (e.g. a whole summer holiday in a five-page story) is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["vertelde tyd","die vertelde tyd"],"en":["narrated time","vertelde tyd"]},"explain":{"af":"Vertelde tyd = hoe lank die gebeure duur (die somervakansie). Verteltyd = hoe lank dit neem om te lees (vyf bladsye).","en":"Narrated time (vertelde tyd) = how long the events last (the summer holiday). Narrative time (verteltyd) = how long it takes to read (five pages)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verteltyd","terugflits","eksposisie"],"en":["narrative time","flashback","exposition"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is 'n voorbeeld van DIREKTE karakterisering?","en":"Which sentence is an example of DIRECT characterisation?"},"options":[{"af":"Wikus druk sy hande diep in sy sakke.","en":"Wikus druk sy hande diep in sy sakke. (Wikus pushes his hands deep into his pockets.)"},{"af":"'Jy's laat,' sê Pa.","en":"'Jy's laat,' sê Pa. ('You're late,' says Dad.)"},{"af":"Wikus was 'n skaam, bedagsame seun.","en":"Wikus was 'n skaam, bedagsame seun. (Wikus was a shy, thoughtful boy.)"},{"af":"Pa kyk lank na hom.","en":"Pa kyk lank na hom. (Dad looks at him for a long time.)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"By direkte karakterisering sê die verteller self hoe die karakter is (skaam, bedagsaam). Die ander sinne wys aksies en dialoog, waaruit die leser self moet aflei – dit is indirek.","en":"With direct characterisation the narrator says what the character is like (shy, thoughtful). The other sentences show actions and dialogue from which the reader must deduce – that is indirect."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Dinamiese karakter verander of groei in die loop van die verhaal.","en":"A dynamic character changes or grows in the course of the story."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n Statiese karakter bly dieselfde. Moenie dinamies/staties (verander of nie) met rond/plat (veelkantig of nie) verwar nie.","en":"True. A static character stays the same. Do not confuse dynamic/static (changes or not) with round/flat (many-sided or not)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Wikus worstel in sy binneste: moet hy iemand vertel of nie? Dit is ___ konflik.","en":"Wikus struggles inside himself: should he tell someone or not? This is ___ conflict."},"answers":{"af":["innerlike","innerlik","'n innerlike"],"en":["internal","innerlike","innerlik"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Stryd binne 'n karakter is innerlike konflik. Uiterlike konflik is teen 'n ander karakter, die samelewing of die natuur.","en":"A struggle inside a character is internal conflict. External conflict is against another character, society or nature."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["uiterlike","sosiale","fisiese"],"en":["external","social","physical"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'Ek het geweet Ma sou kwaad wees, maar ek het tog die bakkie se sleutels gevat. Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie.' Watter soort verteller is dit?","en":"'Ek het geweet Ma sou kwaad wees, maar ek het tog die bakkie se sleutels gevat. Niemand in hierdie huis verstaan my nie.' What kind of narrator is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Alwetende derdepersoonsverteller","en":"Omniscient third-person narrator"},{"af":"Ek-verteller (eerstepersoonsverteller)","en":"First-person narrator"},{"af":"Beperkte derdepersoonsverteller","en":"Limited third-person narrator"},{"af":"Die skrywer wat self met die leser praat","en":"The author speaking to the reader himself"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die karakter vertel self met 'ek'. Dit is nie die skrywer nie, maar 'n karakter in die verhaal – en omdat hy subjektief is, kan hy onbetroubaar wees.","en":"The character narrates himself with 'ek' (I). It is not the author but a character in the story – and because he is subjective, he can be unreliable."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Brandweerman se huis brand af terwyl hy elders 'n brand blus. Dit is 'n voorbeeld van ___.","en":"A firefighter's house burns down while he is putting out a fire elsewhere. This is an example of ___."},"answers":{"af":["situasie-ironie","situasieironie","ironie van situasie","situasionele ironie","situasie"],"en":["situational irony","situasie-ironie","situasieironie","irony of situation"]},"explain":{"af":"Die uitkoms is die teenoorgestelde van wat ons verwag: juis die man wat brande blus, se huis brand af. Verbale ironie is wanneer iemand die teenoorgestelde sê van wat hy bedoel.","en":"The outcome is the opposite of what we expect: the very man who puts out fires loses his house to fire. Verbal irony is when someone says the opposite of what he means."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verbale ironie","dramatiese ironie","vooruitwysing"],"en":["verbal irony","dramatic irony","foreshadowing"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n kortverhaal kners 'n plaashek telkens wanneer gevaar van buite af kom, en die hoofkarakter voel net binne die hek veilig. Wat simboliseer die hek waarskynlik?","en":"In a short story a farm gate creaks every time danger comes from outside, and the main character feels safe only inside the gate. What does the gate probably symbolise?"},"options":[{"af":"Die grens tussen die veilige huis en die bedreigende wêreld buite","en":"The boundary between the safe home and the threatening world outside"},{"af":"Die familie se rykdom","en":"The family's wealth"},{"af":"Die hoofkarakter se liefde vir die plaas se diere","en":"The main character's love for the farm's animals"},{"af":"Die weer op die plaas","en":"The weather on the farm"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Simbool is 'n konkrete ding wat vir iets abstraks staan. Omdat die hek elke keer kners wanneer gevaar kom, en veiligheid binne is, staan dit vir die grens tussen veiligheid en bedreiging. Die herhaling maak dit ook 'n motief.","en":"A symbol is a concrete thing that stands for something abstract. Because the gate creaks every time danger comes, and safety is inside, it stands for the boundary between safety and threat. The repetition also makes it a motif."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gebeure in 'n verhaal: Thandi spaar vir spykerskoene; sy mis oefeninge omdat sy werk; sy hardloop kaalvoet in die proewe en wen met een tree; sy word in die span gekies. Watter gebeurtenis is die KLIMAKS?","en":"Events in a story: Thandi saves for running spikes; she misses practices because she works; she runs barefoot in the trials and wins by one stride; she is chosen for the team. Which event is the CLIMAX?"},"options":[{"af":"Thandi spaar vir spykerskoene.","en":"Thandi saves for running spikes."},{"af":"Sy mis oefeninge omdat sy werk.","en":"She misses practices because she works."},{"af":"Sy hardloop kaalvoet in die proewe en wen met een tree.","en":"She runs barefoot in the trials and wins by one stride."},{"af":"Sy word in die span gekies.","en":"She is chosen for the team."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die wedloop is die keerpunt waar die spanning die hoogste is. Spaar en oefeninge mis is stygende aksie; gekies word is die afwikkeling.","en":"The race is the turning point where the tension is at its highest. Saving and missing practices are rising action; being chosen is the falling action."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'Die hek' lieg Wikus vir sy beseerde pa oor waar hy was, nadat 'n boelie Pa se medisyngeld van hom gesteel het. 'Is Wikus se leuen regverdigbaar? Motiveer.' Watter antwoord sal die meeste punte kry?","en":"In 'Die hek' Wikus lies to his injured father about where he was, after a bully stole Dad's medicine money from him. 'Is Wikus's lie justifiable? Motivate.' Which answer will earn the most marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Ja.","en":"Yes."},{"af":"Nee, want lieg is altyd verkeerd.","en":"No, because lying is always wrong."},{"af":"Wikus lieg omdat hy van rugby hou.","en":"Wikus lies because he likes rugby."},{"af":"Ja, want hy wil sy pa, wat ná die myn-ongeluk min praat, nie nog meer bekommer nie; tog bly hy alleen met die probleem, wat dit vir hom moeiliker maak.","en":"Yes, because he does not want to worry his father, who speaks little after the mine accident, even more; yet he stays alone with the problem, which makes it harder for him."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Motiveer-vraag vra 'n standpunt EN 'n rede uit die teks. Die laaste antwoord doen albei en weeg die gevolge op. 'Ja' alleen het geen rede nie, 'lieg is altyd verkeerd' verwys nie na die teks nie, en die rugby-antwoord verstaan die teks verkeerd.","en":"A motivate question asks for a point of view AND a reason from the text. The last answer does both and weighs up the consequences. 'Yes' alone has no reason, 'lying is always wrong' does not refer to the text, and the rugby answer misreads the text."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy moet 'n literêre opstel van ±250 woorde skryf: 'Bespreek hoe die ruimte die konflik versterk.' Watter beplanning is die beste?","en":"You must write a literary essay of ±250 words: 'Discuss how the setting strengthens the conflict.' Which plan is the best?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Inleiding met 'n duidelike stelling, drie paragrawe (fisiese, sosiale en psigiese ruimte) wat elk aan die konflik gekoppel is met bewys uit die teks, en 'n slot","en":"An introduction with a clear statement, three paragraphs (physical, social and psychological setting) each linked to the conflict with evidence from the text, and a conclusion"},{"af":"Vertel die hele storie van begin tot einde oor","en":"Retell the whole story from beginning to end"},{"af":"Skryf net oor die karakters van wie jy hou","en":"Write only about the characters you like"},{"af":"Maak 'n lys van al die stylfigure in die verhaal","en":"Make a list of all the figures of speech in the story"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Literêre opstel beantwoord die vraag met 'n argument: stelling, paragrawe met bewys en 'n slot. Oorvertel, eie voorkeure of 'n lys stylfigure beantwoord nie die vraag oor ruimte en konflik nie.","en":"A literary essay answers the question with an argument: statement, paragraphs with evidence and a conclusion. Retelling, personal preferences or a list of figures of speech do not answer the question about setting and conflict."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t2-briewe","title":{"af":"Transaksionele skryfwerk 1: formele en informele briewe, CV en aansoekbrief","en":"Transactional writing 1: formal and informal letters, CV and application letter"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal formele en vriendskaplike briewe, 'n CV en 'n aansoekbrief in die regte formaat en register kan skryf.","en":"You will be able to write formal and friendly letters, a CV and an application letter in the correct format and register."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat word in die eksamen gevra?\n\nIn **Vraestel 3 (Skryfwerk), Afdeling B** skryf jy **twee transaksionele tekste** van **180–200 woorde** elk (2 × 25 punte). 'n Transaksionele teks het 'n werklike doel en 'n werklike leser: jy wil iets vra, kla, bedank of reël. Daarom tel die **formaat** en die **register** net so swaar soos die inhoud.\n\n| Rubriek vir een transaksionele teks | Punte |\n|---|---|\n| Inhoud, beplanning en formaat | 15 |\n| Taal, styl en redigering | 10 |\n| **Totaal** | **25** |\n\n## Die formele brief\n\n- **Versoekbrief** – vra beleefd vir toestemming, inligting of hulp.\n- **Klagtebrief** – wys op 'n probleem en vra vir 'n oplossing.\n- **Dankiebrief** – bedank 'n persoon of organisasie.\n- **Aansoekbrief** – doen aansoek om 'n pos, beurs of plek (saam met 'n CV).\n- **Brief aan die pers (lesersbrief)** – lewer jou mening oor 'n saak in 'n koerant of tydskrif.\n\n### Formaat van die formele brief\n\n1. **Afsender se adres** regs bo. Gebruik 'n eie, versinde adres, bv. Posbus 1234, Brits, 0250. Skryf nie jou naam bo die adres nie.\n2. **Datum** onder jou adres, voluit: 21 Oktober 2026.\n3. **Ontvanger se adres** links, onder die datum, met die persoon se titel of pos: *Die Bestuurder, ...*\n4. **Aanhef**: *Geagte Meneer/Mevrou* of *Geagte mnr. Pretorius*.\n5. **Onderwerpreël** direk onder die aanhef, vetgedruk of onderstreep: **KLAGTE OOR GEBREKKIGE RUGBYSTEWELS** of *Insake: Aansoek om vakansiewerk*.\n6. **Liggaam** in paragrawe (sien hieronder).\n7. **Slot**: *Die uwe*\n8. **Handtekening**, met jou **voorletters en van** daaronder (P.J. Venter).\n\n### Die liggaam\n\n- **Paragraaf 1:** die rede vir die brief (*Ek rig hierdie brief aan u om ...*).\n- **Paragraaf 2–3:** die besonderhede: wat, wanneer, waar, watter bewyse.\n- **Laaste paragraaf:** jou versoek en 'n beleefde afsluiting (*Ek sien uit na u antwoord.*).\n\n### Formele register\n\n- Spreek die ontvanger met **u** aan, nooit met *jy* of *julle* nie.\n- Geen sleng, sametrekkings (*dis*, *jy's*), SMS-taal of emoji's nie.\n- Bly beleefd, selfs in 'n klagtebrief: gee feite, moenie beledig nie.\n- Nuttige frases: *Ek sal dit waardeer indien ...*; *By voorbaat dank.*\n\n## Die vriendskaplike (informele) brief\n\n- Net **jou adres en die datum** regs bo; geen ontvanger se adres nie.\n- Aanhef: *Liewe Ouma* of *Beste Jaco*.\n- **Geen onderwerpreël nie.**\n- Begin met 'n kort groet, maar kom gou by die hoofrede vir die brief.\n- Skryf in paragrawe, in informele maar **korrekte** taal (geen SMS-taal nie).\n- Slot: *Groete* of *Liefde*, dan *Jou kleinseun* of *Jou vriend* en net jou **voornaam** (Pieter).\n\n## Die CV (curriculum vitae)\n\n'n Kort, netjiese oorsig van wie jy is, onder duidelike opskrifte:\n\n| Afdeling | Wat daarin kom |\n|---|---|\n| Persoonlike besonderhede | naam, kontaknommer, e-posadres, tale – **geen ID-nommer nie** |\n| Opleiding | skool, graad, vakke, prestasies |\n| Vaardighede | bv. rekenaarvaardig, eerstehulp, leierskap |\n| Werkservaring | vakansiewerk, vrywillige werk |\n| Belangstellings | sport, stokperdjies |\n| Verwysings | twee mense wat nie familie is nie, met hul kontakbesonderhede |\n\n## Die aansoekbrief (begeleidende brief)\n\nDit is 'n **formele brief** wat saam met jou CV gestuur word. Noem die pos in die onderwerpreël, sê waar jy die advertensie gesien het, verduidelik kortliks waarom jy geskik is (verwys na die aangehegte CV) en sê wanneer jy vir 'n onderhoud beskikbaar is.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Die adresse aan die verkeerde kant, of 'n ontvanger se adres in 'n vriendskaplike brief.\n- *Liewe* in 'n formele brief, of *Geagte* in 'n brief aan jou neef.\n- 'n Formele brief wat met *Groete* of *Cheers* eindig.\n- Anglisismes: *Ek kyk uit vorentoe na u antwoord* → **Ek sien uit na u antwoord.**\n- Te kort of te lank: bly binne 180–200 woorde.\n\n> **Wenk:** Vra jouself voor jy begin: Wie skryf? Aan wie? Hoekom? Formeel of informeel? Skryf dan eers die formaat neer en vul daarna die inhoud in.","en":"## What is asked in the exam?\n\nIn **Paper 3 (Writing), Section B** you write **two transactional texts** of **180–200 words** each (2 × 25 marks). A transactional text has a real purpose and a real reader: you want to ask, complain, thank or arrange something. That is why **format** and **register** count just as much as content.\n\n| Rubric for one transactional text | Marks |\n|---|---|\n| Content, planning and format | 15 |\n| Language, style and editing | 10 |\n| **Total** | **25** |\n\n## The formal letter\n\n- **Letter of request (versoekbrief)** – politely asks for permission, information or help.\n- **Letter of complaint (klagtebrief)** – points out a problem and asks for a solution.\n- **Thank-you letter (dankiebrief)** – thanks a person or organisation.\n- **Application letter (aansoekbrief)** – applies for a job, bursary or place (with a CV).\n- **Letter to the press (lesersbrief)** – gives your opinion on an issue in a newspaper or magazine.\n\n### Format of the formal letter\n\n1. **Sender's address** top right. Use your own made-up address, e.g. Posbus 1234, Brits, 0250. Do not write your name above the address.\n2. **Date** below your address, in full: 21 Oktober 2026.\n3. **Receiver's address** on the left, below the date, with the person's title or position: *Die Bestuurder, ...*\n4. **Salutation (aanhef)**: *Geagte Meneer/Mevrou* or *Geagte mnr. Pretorius*.\n5. **Subject line (onderwerpreël)** directly below the salutation, in bold or underlined: **KLAGTE OOR GEBREKKIGE RUGBYSTEWELS** or *Insake: Aansoek om vakansiewerk*.\n6. **Body** in paragraphs (see below).\n7. **Closing (slot)**: *Die uwe*\n8. **Signature**, with your **initials and surname** below it (P.J. Venter).\n\n### The body\n\n- **Paragraph 1:** the reason for the letter (*Ek rig hierdie brief aan u om ...*).\n- **Paragraphs 2–3:** the details: what, when, where, what proof.\n- **Last paragraph:** your request and a polite ending (*Ek sien uit na u antwoord.*).\n\n### Formal register\n\n- Address the receiver as **u**, never as *jy* or *julle*.\n- No slang, contractions (*dis*, *jy's*), SMS language or emojis.\n- Stay polite, even in a complaint: give facts, do not insult.\n- Useful phrases: *Ek sal dit waardeer indien ...*; *By voorbaat dank.*\n\n## The friendly (informal) letter\n\n- Only **your address and the date** top right; no receiver's address.\n- Salutation: *Liewe Ouma* or *Beste Jaco*.\n- **No subject line.**\n- Start with a short greeting, but get to the main reason for the letter quickly.\n- Write in paragraphs, in informal but **correct** language (no SMS language).\n- Closing: *Groete* or *Liefde*, then *Jou kleinseun* or *Jou vriend* and only your **first name** (Pieter).\n\n## The CV (curriculum vitae)\n\nA short, neat overview of who you are, under clear headings:\n\n| Section | What goes in it |\n|---|---|\n| Personal details | name, contact number, e-mail address, languages – **no ID number** |\n| Education | school, grade, subjects, achievements |\n| Skills | e.g. computer literate, first aid, leadership |\n| Work experience | holiday jobs, volunteer work |\n| Interests | sport, hobbies |\n| References | two people who are not family, with their contact details |\n\n## The application letter (covering letter)\n\nThis is a **formal letter** sent with your CV. Name the post in the subject line, say where you saw the advertisement, explain briefly why you are suitable (refer to the attached CV) and say when you are available for an interview.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- The addresses on the wrong side, or a receiver's address in a friendly letter.\n- *Liewe* in a formal letter, or *Geagte* in a letter to your cousin.\n- A formal letter that ends with *Groete* or *Cheers*.\n- Anglicisms: *Ek kyk uit vorentoe na u antwoord* → **Ek sien uit na u antwoord.**\n- Too short or too long: stay within 180–200 words.\n\n> **Tip:** Before you start, ask: Who is writing? To whom? Why? Formal or informal? Then write the format down first and fill in the content afterwards."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Transaksionele teks","en":"Transactional text"},"def":{"af":"'n Funksionele teks met 'n werklike doel en 'n werklike leser, bv. 'n brief, e-pos of verslag.","en":"A functional text with a real purpose and a real reader, e.g. a letter, e-mail or report."}},{"term":{"af":"Formele brief","en":"Formal letter"},"def":{"af":"'n Brief aan 'n persoon of organisasie in formele register en met 'n vaste formaat (twee adresse, onderwerpreël, Die uwe).","en":"A letter to a person or organisation in formal register with a fixed format (two addresses, subject line, Die uwe)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vriendskaplike brief","en":"Friendly letter"},"def":{"af":"'n Informele brief aan familie of vriende, met net jou adres en die datum bo en geen onderwerpreël nie.","en":"An informal letter to family or friends, with only your address and the date at the top and no subject line."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhef","en":"Salutation"},"def":{"af":"Die groet aan die begin van die brief, bv. Geagte Meneer (formeel) of Liewe Ouma (informeel).","en":"The greeting at the start of the letter, e.g. Geagte Meneer (formal) or Liewe Ouma (informal)."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerpreël","en":"Subject line"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort reël direk onder die aanhef van 'n formele brief wat sê waaroor die brief gaan.","en":"A short line directly below the salutation of a formal letter that says what the letter is about."}},{"term":{"af":"Register","en":"Register"},"def":{"af":"Die vlak van formaliteit van die taal, aangepas by die leser en die doel van die teks.","en":"The level of formality of the language, adapted to the reader and the purpose of the text."}},{"term":{"af":"Curriculum vitae (CV)","en":"Curriculum vitae (CV)"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort, gestruktureerde oorsig van jou persoonlike besonderhede, opleiding, vaardighede, ervaring en verwysings.","en":"A short, structured overview of your personal details, education, skills, experience and references."}},{"term":{"af":"Begeleidende brief (aansoekbrief)","en":"Covering letter (application letter)"},"def":{"af":"'n Formele brief wat saam met 'n CV gestuur word om aansoek te doen om 'n pos.","en":"A formal letter sent with a CV to apply for a post."}},{"term":{"af":"Lesersbrief","en":"Letter to the press"},"def":{"af":"'n Brief aan die redakteur van 'n koerant of tydskrif waarin jy jou mening oor 'n saak gee.","en":"A letter to the editor of a newspaper or magazine in which you give your opinion on an issue."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Herskryf in formele register","en":"Rewrite in formal register"},"problem":{"af":"Jy skryf 'n klagtebrief aan 'n selfoonwinkel in Brits. Jou eerste konsep lui:\n\n*“Hey julle, die foon wat ek by julle gekoop het, is gemors. Dis net twee weke oud en dit werk nie meer nie. Sort dit asseblief uit, okay?”*\n\nHerskryf die paragraaf in die korrekte formele register.","en":"You are writing a letter of complaint to a cellphone shop in Brits. Your first draft reads:\n\n*“Hey julle, die foon wat ek by julle gekoop het, is gemors. Dis net twee weke oud en dit werk nie meer nie. Sort dit asseblief uit, okay?”*\n\nRewrite the paragraph in the correct formal register."},"steps":[{"af":"“Hey julle” is 'n informele groet. In 'n formele brief begin jy met *Geagte Meneer/Mevrou* en 'n onderwerpreël, nie met 'n groet in die liggaam nie.","en":"“Hey julle” is an informal greeting. A formal letter starts with *Geagte Meneer/Mevrou* and a subject line, not with a greeting in the body."},{"af":"Vervang *julle* met **u** en verwyder die sleng (*gemors*, *sort uit*, *okay*) en die sametrekking (*dis*).","en":"Replace *julle* with **u** and remove the slang (*gemors*, *sort uit*, *okay*) and the contraction (*dis*)."},{"af":"Gee feite in plaas van emosie: wanneer die foon gekoop is en presies wat fout is.","en":"Give facts instead of emotion: when the phone was bought and exactly what is wrong."},{"af":"Sluit af met 'n duidelike, beleefde versoek: *Ek sal dit waardeer indien ...*","en":"End with a clear, polite request: *Ek sal dit waardeer indien ...*"}],"answer":{"af":"Ek wil graag my ontevredenheid uitspreek oor 'n selfoon wat ek op 3 Oktober 2026 by u winkel gekoop het. Die toestel is slegs twee weke oud, maar dit skakel nie meer aan nie. Ek sal dit waardeer indien u die selfoon so gou moontlik kan herstel of vervang.","en":"Ek wil graag my ontevredenheid uitspreek oor 'n selfoon wat ek op 3 Oktober 2026 by u winkel gekoop het. Die toestel is slegs twee weke oud, maar dit skakel nie meer aan nie. Ek sal dit waardeer indien u die selfoon so gou moontlik kan herstel of vervang. (I would like to express my dissatisfaction with a cellphone I bought at your shop on 3 October 2026. The device is only two weeks old, but it no longer switches on. I would appreciate it if you could repair or replace the phone as soon as possible.)"}},{"title":{"af":"Vind die formaatfoute","en":"Find the format errors"},"problem":{"af":"Jaco skryf aan die voorsitter van 'n skaakklub om aansoek te doen om lidmaatskap. Sy brief se raamwerk lyk so:\n\n| Plek op die bladsy | Wat Jaco geskryf het |\n|---|---|\n| Links bo | Posbus 512, Brits, 0250 (sy eie adres) en 21 Oktober 2026 |\n| Regs, onder die datum | Die Voorsitter, Sonskyn-skaakklub, Posbus 77, Brits, 0250 |\n| Aanhef | Liewe mnr. Botha |\n| Onder die aanhef | (niks) |\n| Slot | Groete, Jaco |\n\nIdentifiseer en verbeter **vier** formaatfoute.","en":"Jaco writes to the chairperson of a chess club to apply for membership. The framework of his letter looks like this:\n\n| Place on the page | What Jaco wrote |\n|---|---|\n| Top left | Posbus 512, Brits, 0250 (his own address) and 21 Oktober 2026 |\n| Right, below the date | Die Voorsitter, Sonskyn-skaakklub, Posbus 77, Brits, 0250 |\n| Salutation | Liewe mnr. Botha |\n| Below the salutation | (nothing) |\n| Closing | Groete, Jaco |\n\nIdentify and correct **four** format errors."},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: Die adresse is omgeruil. Die **afsender** se adres en die datum hoort **regs bo**; die **ontvanger** se adres hoort **links**, onder die datum.","en":"Error 1: The addresses are swapped. The **sender's** address and the date belong **top right**; the **receiver's** address belongs on the **left**, below the date."},{"af":"Fout 2: *Liewe* is informeel. Die aanhef moet wees: **Geagte mnr. Botha**.","en":"Error 2: *Liewe* is informal. The salutation must be: **Geagte mnr. Botha**."},{"af":"Fout 3: Daar is geen onderwerpreël nie. Voeg direk onder die aanhef by: **AANSOEK OM LIDMAATSKAP**.","en":"Error 3: There is no subject line. Add directly below the salutation: **AANSOEK OM LIDMAATSKAP**."},{"af":"Fout 4: *Groete, Jaco* is 'n informele slot. Skryf **Die uwe**, dan die handtekening en daaronder voorletters en van, bv. **J. Fourie**.","en":"Error 4: *Groete, Jaco* is an informal closing. Write **Die uwe**, then the signature and below it initials and surname, e.g. **J. Fourie**."}],"answer":{"af":"Adresse omgeruil; Liewe → Geagte; onderwerpreël ontbreek; Groete, Jaco → Die uwe + handtekening + voorletters en van.","en":"Addresses swapped; Liewe → Geagte; subject line missing; Groete, Jaco → Die uwe + signature + initials and surname."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n klagtebrief","en":"Write a letter of complaint"},"problem":{"af":"Jy het op 10 Oktober 2026 by 'n sportwinkel in Brits rugbystewels vir R1 200 gekoop. Ná net een week se oefening het die sool van een stewel losgekom. Skryf 'n klagtebrief aan die bestuurder (180–200 woorde).","en":"On 10 October 2026 you bought rugby boots for R1 200 at a sports shop in Brits. After only one week of practice the sole of one boot came loose. Write a letter of complaint to the manager (180–200 words)."},"steps":[{"af":"**Bo-aan:** Regs bo jou adres en die datum (Posbus 1234, Brits, 0250 / 21 Oktober 2026). Links, onder die datum: Die Bestuurder, Doelskop-sportwinkel, Posbus 88, Brits, 0250.","en":"**At the top:** Top right your address and the date (Posbus 1234, Brits, 0250 / 21 Oktober 2026). On the left, below the date: Die Bestuurder, Doelskop-sportwinkel, Posbus 88, Brits, 0250."},{"af":"**Aanhef en onderwerpreël:** Geagte Meneer/Mevrou / **KLAGTE OOR GEBREKKIGE RUGBYSTEWELS**","en":"**Salutation and subject line:** Geagte Meneer/Mevrou / **KLAGTE OOR GEBREKKIGE RUGBYSTEWELS**"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 1 (rede):** Ek rig hierdie brief aan u om 'n klagte in te dien oor 'n paar rugbystewels wat ek op 10 Oktober 2026 by u winkel gekoop het.","en":"**Paragraph 1 (reason):** Ek rig hierdie brief aan u om 'n klagte in te dien oor 'n paar rugbystewels wat ek op 10 Oktober 2026 by u winkel gekoop het. (I am writing to complain about rugby boots I bought at your shop.)"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 2 (besonderhede):** Ek het R1 200 vir die stewels betaal. Ná slegs een week se oefening het die sool van die regterstewel heeltemal losgekom, hoewel ek die stewels volgens die instruksies gebruik en skoongemaak het. 'n Afskrif van my strokie is aangeheg.","en":"**Paragraph 2 (details):** Ek het R1 200 vir die stewels betaal. Ná slegs een week se oefening het die sool van die regterstewel heeltemal losgekom, hoewel ek die stewels volgens die instruksies gebruik en skoongemaak het. 'n Afskrif van my strokie is aangeheg. (Price, what went wrong, proof attached.)"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 3 (versoek) en slot:** Aangesien die rugbyseisoen binnekort begin, sal ek dit waardeer indien u die stewels kan vervang of my geld kan terugbetaal. Ek sien uit na u spoedige antwoord. / Die uwe / (handtekening) / P.J. Venter","en":"**Paragraph 3 (request) and closing:** Aangesien die rugbyseisoen binnekort begin, sal ek dit waardeer indien u die stewels kan vervang of my geld kan terugbetaal. Ek sien uit na u spoedige antwoord. / Die uwe / (signature) / P.J. Venter"}],"answer":{"af":"'n Formele klagtebrief met al agt formaatdele: afsender se adres en datum, ontvanger se adres, aanhef, onderwerpreël, liggaam in drie paragrawe, Die uwe, handtekening, voorletters en van. In die eksamen brei jy die paragrawe uit tot 180–200 woorde.","en":"A formal letter of complaint with all eight format parts: sender's address and date, receiver's address, salutation, subject line, body in three paragraphs, Die uwe, signature, initials and surname. In the exam you expand the paragraphs to 180–200 words."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n vriendskaplike brief","en":"Write a friendly letter"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 'n vriendskaplike brief aan jou ouma in Rustenburg. Bedank haar vir die horlosie wat sy vir jou verjaarsdag gestuur het en vertel haar van jou eerste wedstryd vir die o.16-rugbyspan.","en":"Write a friendly letter to your grandmother in Rustenburg. Thank her for the watch she sent for your birthday and tell her about your first match for the U16 rugby team."},"steps":[{"af":"**Bo-aan:** Net jou adres en die datum regs bo. Geen ontvanger se adres en geen onderwerpreël nie.","en":"**At the top:** Only your address and the date top right. No receiver's address and no subject line."},{"af":"**Aanhef:** Liewe Ouma","en":"**Salutation:** Liewe Ouma"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 1 (groet en dankie):** Baie dankie vir die pragtige horlosie wat Ouma vir my verjaarsdag gestuur het. Ek dra dit elke dag skool toe en almal wil weet waar ek dit gekry het!","en":"**Paragraph 1 (greeting and thanks):** Baie dankie vir die pragtige horlosie wat Ouma vir my verjaarsdag gestuur het. Ek dra dit elke dag skool toe en almal wil weet waar ek dit gekry het! (Thank you for the watch; I wear it every day.)"},{"af":"**Paragraaf 2 (die nuus):** Verlede Saterdag het ek my eerste wedstryd vir die o.16-span gespeel. Ek was so senuweeagtig dat my bene gebewe het, maar in die tweede helfte het ek 'n drie gedruk!","en":"**Paragraph 2 (the news):** Verlede Saterdag het ek my eerste wedstryd vir die o.16-span gespeel. Ek was so senuweeagtig dat my bene gebewe het, maar in die tweede helfte het ek 'n drie gedruk! (My first U16 match; I scored a try.)"},{"af":"**Slot:** Sê groete vir Oupa. / Liefde / Jou kleinseun / Pieter","en":"**Closing:** Sê groete vir Oupa. / Liefde / Jou kleinseun / Pieter"}],"answer":{"af":"'n Vriendskaplike brief met net die afsender se adres en datum, die aanhef Liewe Ouma, paragrawe in informele maar korrekte taal, en die slot Liefde, Jou kleinseun, Pieter.","en":"A friendly letter with only the sender's address and date, the salutation Liewe Ouma, paragraphs in informal but correct language, and the closing Liefde, Jou kleinseun, Pieter."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel woorde moet elke transaksionele teks in Graad 10 Huistaal (V3 Afdeling B) wees?","en":"How many words must each transactional text be in Grade 10 Home Language (P3 Section B)?"},"options":[{"af":"80–90 woorde","en":"80–90 woorde"},{"af":"180–200 woorde","en":"180–200 woorde"},{"af":"300–350 woorde","en":"300–350 woorde"},{"af":"400–450 woorde","en":"400–450 woorde"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Transaksionele tekste is 180–200 woorde elk. 80–90 woorde is die opsomming en 300–350 woorde is die opstel.","en":"Transactional texts are 180–200 words each. 80–90 words is the summary and 300–350 words is the essay."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die slot van 'n formele brief is: ___","en":"The closing of a formal letter (in Afrikaans) is: ___"},"answers":{"af":["Die uwe"],"en":["Die uwe"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Groete","Liefde","Jou vriend"],"en":["Groete","Liefde","Jou vriend"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Formele brief eindig met *Die uwe*, gevolg deur jou handtekening, voorletters en van. *Groete* en *Liefde* hoort in 'n vriendskaplike brief.","en":"A formal letter ends with *Die uwe*, followed by your signature, initials and surname. *Groete* and *Liefde* belong in a friendly letter."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n vriendskaplike brief skryf jy die ontvanger se adres links onder die datum.","en":"In a friendly letter you write the receiver's address on the left below the date."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Vriendskaplike brief het net jou eie adres en die datum regs bo. Die ontvanger se adres kom net in 'n formele brief.","en":"False. A friendly letter has only your own address and the date top right. The receiver's address appears only in a formal letter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter aanhef pas by 'n brief aan die hoof van jou skool?","en":"Which salutation suits a letter to the principal of your school?"},"options":[{"af":"Liewe Meneer","en":"Liewe Meneer"},{"af":"Beste Meneer","en":"Beste Meneer"},{"af":"Hallo Meneer","en":"Hallo Meneer"},{"af":"Geagte Meneer","en":"Geagte Meneer"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Geagte* is die formele aanhef. *Liewe* en *Beste* is vir familie en vriende, en *Hallo* is heeltemal te informeel.","en":"*Geagte* is the formal salutation. *Liewe* and *Beste* are for family and friends, and *Hallo* is far too informal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die kort reël direk onder die aanhef wat sê waaroor 'n formele brief gaan, is die ___.","en":"The short line directly below the salutation that says what a formal letter is about is the ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["onderwerpreël","onderwerpreel","onderwerp"],"en":["onderwerpreël","onderwerpreel","onderwerp","subject line"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aanhef","slot","inleiding"],"en":["aanhef","slot","inleiding"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die onderwerpreël (bv. KLAGTE OOR ...) staan onder die aanhef en is vetgedruk of onderstreep. Die aanhef is die groet self.","en":"The subject line (e.g. KLAGTE OOR ...) stands below the salutation and is in bold or underlined. The salutation is the greeting itself."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die korrekte formele register?","en":"Which sentence is in the correct formal register?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek wil net sê julle diens is regtig swak.","en":"Ek wil net sê julle diens is regtig swak."},{"af":"Julle het my lelik in die steek gelaat, ou.","en":"Julle het my lelik in die steek gelaat, ou."},{"af":"Ek wil graag my ontevredenheid oor u diens uitspreek.","en":"Ek wil graag my ontevredenheid oor u diens uitspreek."},{"af":"Jy moet asseblief gou maak met my bestelling.","en":"Jy moet asseblief gou maak met my bestelling."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die formele sin gebruik **u** en neutrale, beleefde woorde. Die ander gebruik *julle* of *jy*, en *regtig swak* en *ou* is informeel.","en":"The formal sentence uses **u** and neutral, polite words. The others use *julle* or *jy*, and *regtig swak* and *ou* are informal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat hoort NIE op 'n CV nie?","en":"What does NOT belong on a CV?"},"options":[{"af":"Jou ID-nommer","en":"Jou ID-nommer"},{"af":"Jou skoolprestasies","en":"Jou skoolprestasies"},{"af":"Twee verwysings","en":"Twee verwysings"},{"af":"Jou vaardighede","en":"Jou vaardighede"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Om veiligheidsredes skryf jy nie jou ID-nommer op 'n CV nie. Prestasies, vaardighede en verwysings is belangrike afdelings.","en":"For safety reasons you do not put your ID number on a CV. Achievements, skills and references are important sections."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die rubriek vir 'n transaksionele teks tel inhoud, beplanning en formaat ___ van die 25 punte.","en":"In the rubric for a transactional text, content, planning and format count ___ of the 25 marks."},"answers":{"af":["15","vyftien"],"en":["15","fifteen"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["10","20","5"],"en":["10","20","5"]}},"explain":{"af":"Inhoud, beplanning en formaat = 15; taal, styl en redigering = 10; totaal 25. 'n Verkeerde formaat kos jou dus uit die grootste blok punte.","en":"Content, planning and format = 15; language, style and editing = 10; total 25. A wrong format therefore costs you marks from the biggest block."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n formele brief spreek jy die ontvanger met *u* aan, nie met *jy* nie.","en":"In a formal letter you address the receiver as *u*, not as *jy*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *U* is die beleefde, formele aanspreekvorm. *Jy* en *julle* is informeel.","en":"True. *U* is the polite, formal form of address. *Jy* and *julle* are informal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy skryf aan die munisipaliteit oor 'n gevaarlike slaggat in jou straat in Brits. Watter onderwerpreël is die beste?","en":"You write to the municipality about a dangerous pothole in your street in Brits. Which subject line is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hallo, ek het 'n probleem","en":"Hallo, ek het 'n probleem"},{"af":"KLAGTE OOR 'N GEVAARLIKE SLAGGAT IN BOOMSTRAAT, BRITS","en":"KLAGTE OOR 'N GEVAARLIKE SLAGGAT IN BOOMSTRAAT, BRITS"},{"af":"Brief aan die munisipaliteit","en":"Brief aan die munisipaliteit"},{"af":"Slaggate is baie gevaarlik!","en":"Slaggate is baie gevaarlik!"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie onderwerpreël is kort en spesifiek: dit noem die soort brief (klagte), die saak (slaggat) en die plek. Die ander is vaag, informeel of 'n uitroep.","en":"A good subject line is short and specific: it names the type of letter (complaint), the issue (pothole) and the place. The others are vague, informal or an exclamation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Ek kyk uit vorentoe na u antwoord* is 'n anglisisme. Die korrekte Afrikaans is: *Ek sien ___ na u antwoord.*","en":"*Ek kyk uit vorentoe na u antwoord* is an anglicism. The correct Afrikaans is: *Ek sien ___ na u antwoord.*"},"answers":{"af":["uit"],"en":["uit"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vorentoe","op","terug"],"en":["vorentoe","op","terug"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die korrekte uitdrukking is *Ek sien uit na u antwoord.* *Kyk uit vorentoe* is 'n letterlike vertaling van die Engelse *look forward to*.","en":"The correct expression is *Ek sien uit na u antwoord.* *Kyk uit vorentoe* is a literal translation of the English *look forward to*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter slot pas by 'n vriendskaplike brief aan jou ouma?","en":"Which closing suits a friendly letter to your grandmother?"},"options":[{"af":"Liefde, jou kleinseun Pieter","en":"Liefde, jou kleinseun Pieter"},{"af":"Die uwe, P.J. Venter","en":"Die uwe, P.J. Venter"},{"af":"Hoogagtend, P.J. Venter","en":"Hoogagtend, P.J. Venter"},{"af":"Met vriendelike groete, mnr. P. Venter","en":"Met vriendelike groete, mnr. P. Venter"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In 'n vriendskaplike brief gebruik jy 'n warm slot en net jou voornaam. *Die uwe* en *Hoogagtend* met voorletters en van is formeel.","en":"In a friendly letter you use a warm closing and only your first name. *Die uwe* and *Hoogagtend* with initials and surname are formal."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke soort brief by sy doel.","en":"Match each type of letter to its purpose."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Versoekbrief","en":"Letter of request"},"r":{"af":"Vra beleefd vir toestemming, inligting of hulp","en":"Politely asks for permission, information or help"}},{"l":{"af":"Klagtebrief","en":"Letter of complaint"},"r":{"af":"Wys op 'n probleem en vra vir 'n oplossing","en":"Points out a problem and asks for a solution"}},{"l":{"af":"Dankiebrief","en":"Thank-you letter"},"r":{"af":"Bedank iemand vir hulp, 'n borgskap of 'n geskenk","en":"Thanks someone for help, a sponsorship or a gift"}},{"l":{"af":"Lesersbrief","en":"Letter to the press"},"r":{"af":"Lewer jou mening oor 'n saak in die koerant","en":"Gives your opinion on an issue in the newspaper"}},{"l":{"af":"Aansoekbrief","en":"Application letter"},"r":{"af":"Doen aansoek om 'n pos, saam met 'n CV","en":"Applies for a post, together with a CV"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die doel van die brief bepaal die inhoud van die onderwerpreël en die paragrawe, maar al vyf is formele briewe met dieselfde formaat.","en":"The purpose of the letter determines the subject line and the paragraphs, but all five are formal letters with the same format."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Herskryf in formele register: *Ons is gatvol vir die lawaai.* → *Ons is ___ oor die lawaai.*","en":"Rewrite in formal register: *Ons is gatvol vir die lawaai.* → *Ons is ___ oor die lawaai.*"},"answers":{"af":["ontevrede","baie ontevrede","uiters ontevrede","bekommerd","ontsteld"],"en":["ontevrede","baie ontevrede","uiters ontevrede","bekommerd","ontsteld"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gatvol","sat","flippen kwaad"],"en":["gatvol","sat","flippen kwaad"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Gatvol* en *sat* is informele spreektaal; *flippen* is sleng. *Ontevrede* sê dieselfde op 'n beleefde, formele manier.","en":"*Gatvol* and *sat* are informal speech; *flippen* is slang. *Ontevrede* says the same thing in a polite, formal way."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jaco skryf aan 'n sakeman wat sy rugbyspan se toer geborg het. Sy brief begin met *Liewe mnr. Botha* en eindig met *Groete, Jaco*. Wat is die grootste probleem?","en":"Jaco writes to a businessman who sponsored his rugby team's tour. His letter starts with *Liewe mnr. Botha* and ends with *Groete, Jaco*. What is the biggest problem?"},"options":[{"af":"*Mnr.* moet voluit as *Meneer* geskryf word.","en":"*Mnr.* moet voluit as *Meneer* geskryf word."},{"af":"'n Dankiebrief hoef nie 'n slot te hê nie.","en":"'n Dankiebrief hoef nie 'n slot te hê nie."},{"af":"Die onderwerpreël moet met *Hallo* begin.","en":"Die onderwerpreël moet met *Hallo* begin."},{"af":"Die aanhef en slot is informeel; dit moet *Geagte mnr. Botha* en *Die uwe* met voorletters en van wees.","en":"Die aanhef en slot is informeel; dit moet *Geagte mnr. Botha* en *Die uwe* met voorletters en van wees."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Dankiebrief aan 'n sakeman is 'n formele brief. Die register van die aanhef en slot moet formeel wees: *Geagte* en *Die uwe*, plus voorletters en van (J. Fourie).","en":"A thank-you letter to a businessman is a formal letter. The register of the salutation and closing must be formal: *Geagte* and *Die uwe*, plus initials and surname (J. Fourie)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy doen aansoek om vakansiewerk by 'n sitrusplaas naby Brits. Watter openingsparagraaf is die beste?","en":"You apply for holiday work at a citrus farm near Brits. Which opening paragraph is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Hallo! Ek is Pieter en ek is 16. Ek soek regtig werk, so gee my asseblief 'n kans.","en":"Hallo! Ek is Pieter en ek is 16. Ek soek regtig werk, so gee my asseblief 'n kans."},{"af":"Ek wil graag aansoek doen om die pos as vakansiewerker by u sitrusplaas, soos geadverteer op ons skool se kennisgewingbord. My CV is aangeheg.","en":"Ek wil graag aansoek doen om die pos as vakansiewerker by u sitrusplaas, soos geadverteer op ons skool se kennisgewingbord. My CV is aangeheg."},{"af":"Ek het u advertensie gesien. Ek is beskikbaar.","en":"Ek het u advertensie gesien. Ek is beskikbaar."},{"af":"Hoe gaan dit met u en u gesin? Ek hoop die lemoene groei mooi.","en":"Hoe gaan dit met u en u gesin? Ek hoop die lemoene groei mooi."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die beste opening is formeel, noem die pos en waar jy die advertensie gesien het, en verwys na die CV. *Hallo! Ek is Pieter ...* is te informeel, *Ek het u advertensie gesien. Ek is beskikbaar.* is te kort en vaag, en vrae oor die gesin en die lemoene hoort in 'n vriendskaplike brief.","en":"The best opening is formal, names the post and where you saw the advertisement, and refers to the CV. *Hallo! Ek is Pieter ...* is too informal, *Ek het u advertensie gesien. Ek is beskikbaar.* is too short and vague, and questions about the family and the oranges belong in a friendly letter."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Lydende vorm, visuele geletterdheid, drama en transaksionele tekste","en":"Passive voice, visual literacy, drama and transactional texts"},"topics":[{"id":"afr10-t3-lydende-indirekte-rede","title":{"af":"Lydende vorm en indirekte rede","en":"Passive voice and reported speech"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinne korrek van die bedrywende na die lydende vorm en van direkte na indirekte rede (en terug) kan omskakel.","en":"You will be able to change sentences correctly from active to passive voice and from direct to reported speech (and back)."},"summary":{"af":"## Die lydende vorm\n\nIn die **bedrywende vorm** doen die onderwerp die handeling: *Die kok berei die kos voor.* In die **lydende vorm** ondergaan die onderwerp die handeling: *Die kos word deur die kok voorberei.* Jy gebruik die lydende vorm wanneer die handeling of die voorwerp belangriker is as wie dit doen, bv. in koerantberigte en verslae.\n\n### Stappe: bedrywend → lydend\n\n1. Soek die **voorwerp** (wie of wat die handeling ondergaan). Dit word die nuwe **onderwerp**.\n2. Die oorspronklike onderwerp (die **doener**) skuif na **deur**: *deur die kok*.\n3. Verander die werkwoord volgens die **tyd** (sien die tabel).\n4. Pas die voornaamwoorde aan: *Hy het my gesien.* → *Ek is deur hom gesien.*\n\n| Tyd | Bedrywende vorm | Lydende vorm |\n|---|---|---|\n| Teenwoordig | Die kok berei die kos voor. | Die kos **word** deur die kok **voorberei**. |\n| Verlede | Die kok het die kos voorberei. | Die kos **is** deur die kok **voorberei**. |\n| Toekomend | Die kok sal die kos voorberei. | Die kos **sal** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n| Met *moet* | Die kok moet die kos voorberei. | Die kos **moet** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n| Met *moes* | Die kok moes die kos voorberei. | Die kos **moes** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n\n### Die verlede deelwoord\n\n- Die meeste werkwoorde kry **ge-**: was → gewas, bou → gebou, voer → gevoer.\n- Werkwoorde wat met **be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-** of **ver-** begin, kry nie *ge-* nie: besoek → besoek, verkoop → verkoop, herstel → herstel.\n- By **skeibare** werkwoorde kom *ge-* tussenin: opruim → opgeruim, skoonmaak → skoongemaak.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die gewone verlede tyd van die lydende vorm gebruik **is**, nie *was* nie: *Die skool is in 1950 gebou*, nie *Die skool was in 1950 gebou* nie.\n\n### Die doener mag wegval\n\nAs dit onbekend of onbelangrik is wie die handeling doen, laat jy die *deur*-deel weg: *Die venster is gebreek.* Gaan jy terug na die bedrywende vorm, moet jy 'n onderwerp invoeg: *Iemand het die venster gebreek.*\n\n## Direkte en indirekte rede\n\n**Direkte rede** gee iemand se presiese woorde tussen **aanhalingstekens**. Die aanhaling begin met 'n hoofletter en word voorafgegaan deur 'n dubbelpunt of gevolg deur 'n komma:\n\n- Pa sê: “Ons ry môre Hartbeespoort toe.”\n- “Ons ry môre Hartbeespoort toe,” sê Pa.\n\n**Indirekte rede** vertel wat iemand gesê het, sonder aanhalingstekens.\n\n### Reëls: direk → indirek\n\n1. Verwyder die **dubbelpunt** en die **aanhalingstekens**.\n2. **Stelling** → **dat**-sin; die werkwoord skuif na die einde: Thabo sê: “Ek is moeg.” → Thabo sê **dat** hy moeg **is**. (Sonder *dat* bly die gewone woordorde: *Thabo sê hy is moeg.* In die eksamen is die *dat*-vorm die veiligste.)\n3. **Ja/nee-vraag** → **of**: Sy vra: “Kom jy saam?” → Sy vra **of** ek **saamkom**.\n4. **Vraagwoordvraag** → die vraagwoord word die voegwoord: Hy vra: “Waar woon jy?” → Hy vra **waar** ek **woon**.\n5. **Bevel** → **moet**: Ma sê: “Ruim jou kamer op!” → Ma sê ek **moet** my kamer **opruim**. *Moenie ... nie* word *moet nie ... nie*.\n6. **Voornaamwoorde** verander volgens wie praat en met wie: ek → hy/sy, ons → hulle, jou → my.\n7. **Tyd- en plekwoorde** verander:\n\n| Direkte rede | Indirekte rede |\n|---|---|\n| vandag | daardie dag |\n| môre | die volgende dag |\n| gister | die vorige dag |\n| nou | toe |\n| hier | daar |\n| hierdie | daardie |\n\n8. Die **tyd bly dieselfde** as in die aanhaling: Hy het gesê: “Ek is moeg.” → Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In Engels skuif die tyd terug (*He said that he was tired*), maar nie in Afrikaans nie.\n9. Tussenwerpsels en aanspreekvorme val weg of word deel van die sin: “Sjoe, Lerato, jy is vinnig!” → Hy sê vir Lerato dat sy vinnig is.\n\n**Indirek → direk** werk andersom: voeg die dubbelpunt en aanhalingstekens in, gebruik die spreker se eie voornaamwoorde (ek, ons) en verander *die volgende dag* terug na *môre*.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** die werkwoord nie na die einde skuif nie (*dat hy is moeg*); *dat* by 'n vraag gebruik; *jy* en *môre* onveranderd laat staan; die tyd soos in Engels terugskuif.\n\n> **Wenk:** Lees jou indirekte sin hardop. Dit moet klink asof iemand anders vertel wat gesê is.","en":"## The passive voice\n\nIn the **active voice (bedrywende vorm)** the subject performs the action: *Die kok berei die kos voor.* In the **passive voice (lydende vorm)** the subject undergoes the action: *Die kos word deur die kok voorberei.* You use the passive when the action or the object is more important than who does it, e.g. in newspaper reports and reports.\n\n### Steps: active → passive\n\n1. Find the **object** (who or what undergoes the action). It becomes the new **subject**.\n2. The original subject (the **doer**) moves to **deur** (by): *deur die kok*.\n3. Change the verb according to the **tense** (see the table).\n4. Adjust the pronouns: *Hy het my gesien.* → *Ek is deur hom gesien.*\n\n| Tense | Active | Passive |\n|---|---|---|\n| Present | Die kok berei die kos voor. | Die kos **word** deur die kok **voorberei**. |\n| Past | Die kok het die kos voorberei. | Die kos **is** deur die kok **voorberei**. |\n| Future | Die kok sal die kos voorberei. | Die kos **sal** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n| With *moet* | Die kok moet die kos voorberei. | Die kos **moet** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n| With *moes* | Die kok moes die kos voorberei. | Die kos **moes** deur die kok **voorberei word**. |\n\n### The past participle\n\n- Most verbs take **ge-**: was → gewas, bou → gebou, voer → gevoer.\n- Verbs that start with **be-, er-, ge-, her-, ont-** or **ver-** do not take *ge-*: besoek → besoek, verkoop → verkoop, herstel → herstel.\n- With **separable** verbs *ge-* goes in the middle: opruim → opgeruim, skoonmaak → skoongemaak.\n\n> **Common mistake:** The ordinary past tense of the passive uses **is**, not *was*: *Die skool is in 1950 gebou*, not *Die skool was in 1950 gebou*.\n\n### The doer may be left out\n\nIf it is unknown or unimportant who performs the action, leave out the *deur* part: *Die venster is gebreek.* When you go back to the active voice, you must add a subject: *Iemand het die venster gebreek.*\n\n## Direct and reported speech\n\n**Direct speech (direkte rede)** gives someone's exact words in **quotation marks**. The quotation starts with a capital letter and is preceded by a colon or followed by a comma:\n\n- Pa sê: “Ons ry môre Hartbeespoort toe.”\n- “Ons ry môre Hartbeespoort toe,” sê Pa.\n\n**Reported speech (indirekte rede)** tells what someone said, without quotation marks.\n\n### Rules: direct → reported\n\n1. Remove the **colon** and the **quotation marks**.\n2. **Statement** → **dat** clause; the verb moves to the end: Thabo sê: “Ek is moeg.” → Thabo sê **dat** hy moeg **is**. (Without *dat* the normal word order stays: *Thabo sê hy is moeg.* In the exam the *dat* form is the safest.)\n3. **Yes/no question** → **of** (whether): Sy vra: “Kom jy saam?” → Sy vra **of** ek **saamkom**.\n4. **Question-word question** → the question word becomes the conjunction: Hy vra: “Waar woon jy?” → Hy vra **waar** ek **woon**.\n5. **Command** → **moet**: Ma sê: “Ruim jou kamer op!” → Ma sê ek **moet** my kamer **opruim**. *Moenie ... nie* becomes *moet nie ... nie*.\n6. **Pronouns** change according to who is speaking to whom: ek → hy/sy, ons → hulle, jou → my.\n7. **Time and place words** change:\n\n| Direct speech | Reported speech |\n|---|---|\n| vandag (today) | daardie dag (that day) |\n| môre (tomorrow) | die volgende dag (the next day) |\n| gister (yesterday) | die vorige dag (the previous day) |\n| nou (now) | toe (then) |\n| hier (here) | daar (there) |\n| hierdie (this) | daardie (that) |\n\n8. The **tense stays the same** as in the quotation: Hy het gesê: “Ek is moeg.” → Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In English the tense shifts back (*He said that he was tired*), but not in Afrikaans.\n9. Interjections and forms of address fall away or become part of the sentence: “Sjoe, Lerato, jy is vinnig!” → Hy sê vir Lerato dat sy vinnig is.\n\n**Reported → direct** works the other way round: add the colon and quotation marks, use the speaker's own pronouns (ek, ons) and change *die volgende dag* back to *môre*.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** not moving the verb to the end (*dat hy is moeg*); using *dat* with a question; leaving *jy* and *môre* unchanged; shifting the tense back as in English.\n\n> **Tip:** Read your reported sentence aloud. It must sound as if someone else is telling what was said."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bedrywende vorm","en":"Active voice"},"def":{"af":"Die sinsvorm waarin die onderwerp self die handeling uitvoer: Die kok berei die kos voor.","en":"The sentence form in which the subject itself performs the action: Die kok berei die kos voor."}},{"term":{"af":"Lydende vorm","en":"Passive voice"},"def":{"af":"Die sinsvorm waarin die onderwerp die handeling ondergaan; gevorm met word/is/sal ... word + verlede deelwoord.","en":"The sentence form in which the subject undergoes the action; formed with word/is/sal ... word + past participle."}},{"term":{"af":"Doener","en":"Doer (agent)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling uitvoer; in die lydende vorm ingelei deur *deur*.","en":"The person or thing that performs the action; in the passive introduced by *deur* (by)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verlede deelwoord","en":"Past participle"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoordvorm wat gewoonlik met ge- begin (gebou, opgeruim) en in die lydende vorm en verlede tyd gebruik word.","en":"The verb form that usually starts with ge- (gebou, opgeruim) and is used in the passive and the past tense."}},{"term":{"af":"Skeibare werkwoord","en":"Separable verb"},"def":{"af":"'n Werkwoord waarvan die deeltjie losgemaak kan word (opruim → Ek ruim op); ge- kom tussenin: opgeruim.","en":"A verb whose particle can be separated (opruim → Ek ruim op); ge- goes in the middle: opgeruim."}},{"term":{"af":"Direkte rede","en":"Direct speech"},"def":{"af":"Iemand se presiese woorde, tussen aanhalingstekens, met 'n dubbelpunt of komma.","en":"Someone's exact words, in quotation marks, with a colon or comma."}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte rede","en":"Reported speech"},"def":{"af":"'n Weergawe van wat iemand gesê het, sonder aanhalingstekens, met aangepaste voornaamwoorde, tyd- en plekwoorde.","en":"A version of what someone said, without quotation marks, with adjusted pronouns and time and place words."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhalingstekens","en":"Quotation marks"},"def":{"af":"Die leestekens (“ ”) wat die presiese woorde van 'n spreker in direkte rede insluit.","en":"The punctuation marks (“ ”) that enclose a speaker's exact words in direct speech."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bedrywend na lydend in drie tye","en":"Active to passive in three tenses"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die sin in die lydende vorm in (a) die teenwoordige, (b) die verlede en (c) die toekomende tyd:\n\n*Die leerders plant die bome by die skool.*","en":"Write the sentence in the passive voice in (a) the present, (b) the past and (c) the future tense:\n\n*Die leerders plant die bome by die skool.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Voorwerp = *die bome* → nuwe onderwerp. Doener = *die leerders* → *deur die leerders*. Verlede deelwoord van *plant* = *geplant*.","en":"Object = *die bome* → new subject. Doer = *die leerders* → *deur die leerders*. Past participle of *plant* = *geplant*."},{"af":"(a) Teenwoordig: **word** + deelwoord: *Die bome word deur die leerders by die skool geplant.*","en":"(a) Present: **word** + participle: *Die bome word deur die leerders by die skool geplant.*"},{"af":"(b) Verlede: **is** + deelwoord (nie *was* nie): *Die bome is deur die leerders by die skool geplant.*","en":"(b) Past: **is** + participle (not *was*): *Die bome is deur die leerders by die skool geplant.*"},{"af":"(c) Toekomend: **sal** ... deelwoord + **word**: *Die bome sal deur die leerders by die skool geplant word.*","en":"(c) Future: **sal** ... participle + **word**: *Die bome sal deur die leerders by die skool geplant word.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die bome word deur die leerders by die skool geplant. (b) Die bome is deur die leerders by die skool geplant. (c) Die bome sal deur die leerders by die skool geplant word.","en":"(a) Die bome word deur die leerders by die skool geplant. (b) Die bome is deur die leerders by die skool geplant. (c) Die bome sal deur die leerders by die skool geplant word."}},{"title":{"af":"Lydend na bedrywend","en":"Passive to active"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die bedrywende vorm:\n\n(a) *Die motor is gisteraand gesteel.*\n(b) *Die hek moet deur julle gesluit word.*\n(c) *Sy is deur hulle na die braai genooi.*","en":"Write in the active voice:\n\n(a) *Die motor is gisteraand gesteel.*\n(b) *Die hek moet deur julle gesluit word.*\n(c) *Sy is deur hulle na die braai genooi.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Daar is geen doener nie, so voeg 'n onderwerp in. *Is* + deelwoord = verlede tyd → *het ... gesteel*: **Iemand het die motor gisteraand gesteel.**","en":"(a) There is no doer, so add a subject. *Is* + participle = past tense → *het ... gesteel*: **Iemand het die motor gisteraand gesteel.**"},{"af":"(b) Doener = *julle* → onderwerp. *Moet ... gesluit word* → *moet ... sluit* (die infinitief, sonder ge-): **Julle moet die hek sluit.**","en":"(b) Doer = *julle* → subject. *Moet ... gesluit word* → *moet ... sluit* (the infinitive, without ge-): **Julle moet die hek sluit.**"},{"af":"(c) Doener = *hulle* → onderwerp; *sy* word voorwerp → *haar*. Verlede tyd: **Hulle het haar na die braai genooi.**","en":"(c) Doer = *hulle* → subject; *sy* becomes the object → *haar*. Past tense: **Hulle het haar na die braai genooi.**"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Iemand het die motor gisteraand gesteel. (b) Julle moet die hek sluit. (c) Hulle het haar na die braai genooi.","en":"(a) Iemand het die motor gisteraand gesteel. (b) Julle moet die hek sluit. (c) Hulle het haar na die braai genooi."}},{"title":{"af":"Direkte rede na indirekte rede: 'n stelling","en":"Direct to reported speech: a statement"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf in die indirekte rede:\n\n*Thabo het gesê: “Ek gaan môre saam met my pa na die myn naby Brits.”*","en":"Write in reported speech:\n\n*Thabo het gesê: “Ek gaan môre saam met my pa na die myn naby Brits.”*"},"steps":[{"af":"Verwyder die dubbelpunt en aanhalingstekens. Dit is 'n stelling, dus gebruik jy **dat**: *Thabo het gesê dat ...*","en":"Remove the colon and quotation marks. It is a statement, so you use **dat**: *Thabo het gesê dat ...*"},{"af":"Voornaamwoorde: Thabo praat oor homself, dus *ek* → **hy** en *my pa* → **sy pa**.","en":"Pronouns: Thabo is talking about himself, so *ek* → **hy** and *my pa* → **sy pa**."},{"af":"Tydwoord: *môre* → **die volgende dag**.","en":"Time word: *môre* → **die volgende dag**."},{"af":"Woordorde en tyd: ná *dat* skuif die werkwoord *gaan* na die einde, en die tyd bly teenwoordig (Afrikaans skuif nie die tyd terug nie).","en":"Word order and tense: after *dat* the verb *gaan* moves to the end, and the tense stays present (Afrikaans does not shift the tense back)."}],"answer":{"af":"Thabo het gesê dat hy die volgende dag saam met sy pa na die myn naby Brits gaan.","en":"Thabo het gesê dat hy die volgende dag saam met sy pa na die myn naby Brits gaan."}},{"title":{"af":"Vrae en 'n bevel in die indirekte rede","en":"Questions and a command in reported speech"},"problem":{"af":"'n Speler vertel wat die afrigter gesê het. Skryf elke sin in die indirekte rede:\n\n(a) *Die afrigter het gevra: “Het julle gister geoefen?”*\n(b) *Die afrigter het gevra: “Waarom is julle laat?”*\n(c) *Die afrigter het gesê: “Hardloop nou tien rondtes om die veld!”*","en":"A player reports what the coach said. Write each sentence in reported speech:\n\n(a) *Die afrigter het gevra: “Het julle gister geoefen?”*\n(b) *Die afrigter het gevra: “Waarom is julle laat?”*\n(c) *Die afrigter het gesê: “Hardloop nou tien rondtes om die veld!”*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ja/nee-vraag → **of**. *Julle* → **ons** (die speler was daar), *gister* → **die vorige dag**, werkwoorde na die einde: *Die afrigter het gevra of ons die vorige dag geoefen het.*","en":"(a) Yes/no question → **of**. *Julle* → **ons** (the player was there), *gister* → **die vorige dag**, verbs to the end: *Die afrigter het gevra of ons die vorige dag geoefen het.*"},{"af":"(b) Vraagwoordvraag → *waarom* word die voegwoord. *Julle* → **ons**, en *is* skuif na die einde maar bly in die teenwoordige tyd: *Die afrigter het gevra waarom ons laat is.*","en":"(b) Question-word question → *waarom* becomes the conjunction. *Julle* → **ons**, and *is* moves to the end but stays in the present tense: *Die afrigter het gevra waarom ons laat is.*"},{"af":"(c) Bevel → **moet**. *Nou* → **toe**, en die werkwoorde *moet hardloop* staan aan die einde van die *dat*-sin: *Die afrigter het gesê dat ons toe tien rondtes om die veld moet hardloop.*","en":"(c) Command → **moet**. *Nou* → **toe**, and the verbs *moet hardloop* stand at the end of the *dat* clause: *Die afrigter het gesê dat ons toe tien rondtes om die veld moet hardloop.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die afrigter het gevra of ons die vorige dag geoefen het. (b) Die afrigter het gevra waarom ons laat is. (c) Die afrigter het gesê dat ons toe tien rondtes om die veld moet hardloop.","en":"(a) Die afrigter het gevra of ons die vorige dag geoefen het. (b) Die afrigter het gevra waarom ons laat is. (c) Die afrigter het gesê dat ons toe tien rondtes om die veld moet hardloop."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Met watter woord word die doener in die lydende vorm ingelei?","en":"Which word introduces the doer in the passive voice?"},"options":[{"af":"deur","en":"deur"},{"af":"vir","en":"vir"},{"af":"met","en":"met"},{"af":"van","en":"van"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die doener kom ná *deur*: *Die kos word deur die kok voorberei.*","en":"The doer comes after *deur* (by): *Die kos word deur die kok voorberei.*"}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In die indirekte rede gebruik jy aanhalingstekens.","en":"In reported speech you use quotation marks."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Aanhalingstekens hoort by die direkte rede (die presiese woorde). In die indirekte rede verwyder jy hulle.","en":"False. Quotation marks belong to direct speech (the exact words). In reported speech you remove them."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Die seun voer die hond.* In die lydende vorm: *Die hond word deur die seun ___.*","en":"*Die seun voer die hond.* In the passive voice: *Die hond word deur die seun ___.*"},"answers":{"af":["gevoer"],"en":["gevoer"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["voer","gevoerde","voerde"],"en":["voer","gevoerde","voerde"]}},"explain":{"af":"Teenwoordige tyd lydend = *word* + verlede deelwoord. Die deelwoord van *voer* is *gevoer*.","en":"Present passive = *word* + past participle. The participle of *voer* is *gevoer*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die verlede tyd van die lydende vorm?","en":"Which sentence is in the past tense of the passive voice?"},"options":[{"af":"Die brief word deur Sanet geskryf.","en":"Die brief word deur Sanet geskryf."},{"af":"Die brief sal deur Sanet geskryf word.","en":"Die brief sal deur Sanet geskryf word."},{"af":"Die brief is deur Sanet geskryf.","en":"Die brief is deur Sanet geskryf."},{"af":"Sanet het die brief geskryf.","en":"Sanet het die brief geskryf."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Is* + verlede deelwoord = verlede tyd lydend. *Word* is teenwoordig, *sal ... word* is toekomend, en *Sanet het ... geskryf* is bedrywend.","en":"*Is* + past participle = past passive. *Word* is present, *sal ... word* is future, and *Sanet het ... geskryf* is active."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Ja/nee-vraag word in die indirekte rede ingelei met die voegwoord ___.","en":"A yes/no question is introduced in reported speech by the conjunction ___."},"answers":{"af":["of"],"en":["of"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dat","wat","want"],"en":["dat","wat","want"]}},"explain":{"af":"Sy vra: “Kom jy saam?” → Sy vra **of** ek saamkom. *Dat* gebruik jy net by stellings.","en":"Sy vra: “Kom jy saam?” → Sy vra **of** ek saamkom. You use *dat* only with statements."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Skryf in die lydende vorm: *Die munisipaliteit sal die pad herstel.*","en":"Write in the passive voice: *Die munisipaliteit sal die pad herstel.*"},"options":[{"af":"Die pad word deur die munisipaliteit herstel.","en":"Die pad word deur die munisipaliteit herstel."},{"af":"Die pad sal deur die munisipaliteit herstel word.","en":"Die pad sal deur die munisipaliteit herstel word."},{"af":"Die pad is deur die munisipaliteit herstel.","en":"Die pad is deur die munisipaliteit herstel."},{"af":"Die pad sal deur die munisipaliteit hersteld word.","en":"Die pad sal deur die munisipaliteit hersteld word."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Toekomende tyd: *sal* ... deelwoord + *word*. *Herstel* begin met *her-*, dus kry dit nie *ge-* nie, en *hersteld* is 'n byvoeglike naamwoord, nie die deelwoord nie.","en":"Future tense: *sal* ... participle + *word*. *Herstel* starts with *her-*, so it does not take *ge-*, and *hersteld* is an adjective, not the participle."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In Afrikaans bly die tyd van die aangehaalde woorde in die indirekte rede dieselfde, anders as in Engels.","en":"In Afrikaans the tense of the quoted words stays the same in reported speech, unlike in English."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Hy het gesê: “Ek is moeg.” → Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In Engels word dit *was*.","en":"True. Hy het gesê: “Ek is moeg.” → Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In English it becomes *was*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Ma het gesê: “Ek is vandag moeg.” → Ma het gesê dat sy ___ moeg is.","en":"Ma het gesê: “Ek is vandag moeg.” → Ma het gesê dat sy ___ moeg is."},"answers":{"af":["daardie dag","dié dag"],"en":["daardie dag","dié dag"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vandag","die vorige dag","die volgende dag"],"en":["vandag","die vorige dag","die volgende dag"]}},"explain":{"af":"In die indirekte rede word *vandag* → *daardie dag*. *Die vorige dag* vervang *gister* en *die volgende dag* vervang *môre*.","en":"In reported speech *vandag* (today) → *daardie dag* (that day). *Die vorige dag* replaces *gister* and *die volgende dag* replaces *môre*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter is die korrekte indirekte rede van: Die onderwyser vra: “Waar is jou huiswerk, Jaco?”","en":"Which is the correct reported speech of: Die onderwyser vra: “Waar is jou huiswerk, Jaco?”"},"options":[{"af":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco of waar sy huiswerk is.","en":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco of waar sy huiswerk is."},{"af":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco waar is sy huiswerk.","en":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco waar is sy huiswerk."},{"af":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco dat sy huiswerk waar is.","en":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco dat sy huiswerk waar is."},{"af":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco waar sy huiswerk is.","en":"Die onderwyser vra vir Jaco waar sy huiswerk is."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"By 'n vraagwoordvraag word *waar* die voegwoord en die werkwoord *is* skuif na die einde. *Jou* word *sy*, en die aanspreekvorm *Jaco* word deel van die sin.","en":"In a question-word question *waar* becomes the conjunction and the verb *is* moves to the end. *Jou* becomes *sy*, and the form of address *Jaco* becomes part of the sentence."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter is die korrekte indirekte rede van: Pa sê: “Moenie die hek oopmaak nie!”","en":"Which is the correct reported speech of: Pa sê: “Moenie die hek oopmaak nie!”"},"options":[{"af":"Pa sê dat ek die hek moenie oopmaak nie.","en":"Pa sê dat ek die hek moenie oopmaak nie."},{"af":"Pa sê ek moet nie die hek oopmaak nie.","en":"Pa sê ek moet nie die hek oopmaak nie."},{"af":"Pa sê ek moet die hek oopmaak.","en":"Pa sê ek moet die hek oopmaak."},{"af":"Pa sê of ek nie die hek oopmaak nie.","en":"Pa sê of ek nie die hek oopmaak nie."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Bevel word *moet*; *moenie ... nie* word *moet nie ... nie*. *Pa sê ek moet die hek oopmaak* verloor die ontkenning, *moenie* mag nie so in die *dat*-sin staan nie, en *of* hoort by vrae, nie by bevele nie.","en":"A command becomes *moet*; *moenie ... nie* becomes *moet nie ... nie*. *Pa sê ek moet die hek oopmaak* loses the negation, *moenie* cannot stand like that in the *dat* clause, and *of* belongs with questions, not commands."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter is die bedrywende vorm van: *Die rugbywedstryd is deur die Brits-span gewen.*","en":"Which is the active form of: *Die rugbywedstryd is deur die Brits-span gewen.*"},"options":[{"af":"Die Brits-span wen die rugbywedstryd.","en":"Die Brits-span wen die rugbywedstryd."},{"af":"Die Brits-span het die rugbywedstryd gewin.","en":"Die Brits-span het die rugbywedstryd gewin."},{"af":"Die Brits-span sal die rugbywedstryd wen.","en":"Die Brits-span sal die rugbywedstryd wen."},{"af":"Die Brits-span het die rugbywedstryd gewen.","en":"Die Brits-span het die rugbywedstryd gewen."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Is* + deelwoord = verlede tyd, dus *het ... gewen*. *Wen* alleen is teenwoordige tyd, *sal ... wen* is toekomend, en *gewin* is verkeerd gespel.","en":"*Is* + participle = past tense, so *het ... gewen*. *Wen* on its own is present tense, *sal ... wen* is future, and *gewin* is misspelt."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke woord in die direkte rede by sy vorm in die indirekte rede.","en":"Match each word in direct speech to its form in reported speech."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"môre","en":"môre (tomorrow)"},"r":{"af":"die volgende dag","en":"die volgende dag (the next day)"}},{"l":{"af":"gister","en":"gister (yesterday)"},"r":{"af":"die vorige dag","en":"die vorige dag (the previous day)"}},{"l":{"af":"nou","en":"nou (now)"},"r":{"af":"toe","en":"toe (then)"}},{"l":{"af":"hier","en":"hier (here)"},"r":{"af":"daar","en":"daar (there)"}},{"l":{"af":"hierdie","en":"hierdie (this)"},"r":{"af":"daardie","en":"daardie (that)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die tyd- en plekwoorde skuif weg van die oomblik en plek waar die woorde gesê is.","en":"The time and place words move away from the moment and place where the words were spoken."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lerato het gesê: “Ek het gister my selfoon verloor.” 'n Leerder skryf: *Lerato het gesê dat sy gister haar selfoon verloor het.* Wat is die fout?","en":"Lerato het gesê: “Ek het gister my selfoon verloor.” A learner writes: *Lerato het gesê dat sy gister haar selfoon verloor het.* What is the error?"},"options":[{"af":"*Gister* moet *die vorige dag* word.","en":"*Gister* moet *die vorige dag* word."},{"af":"*Verloor het* moet direk ná *dat* staan.","en":"*Verloor het* moet direk ná *dat* staan."},{"af":"*Sy* moet *ek* bly.","en":"*Sy* moet *ek* bly."},{"af":"Daar is geen fout nie.","en":"Daar is geen fout nie."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die voornaamwoorde (*sy*, *haar*) en die woordorde is reg, maar *gister* moet in die indirekte rede *die vorige dag* word.","en":"The pronouns (*sy*, *haar*) and the word order are correct, but *gister* must become *die vorige dag* in reported speech."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Die leerders moet die klas skoonmaak.* → *Die klas moet deur die leerders skoongemaak ___.*","en":"*Die leerders moet die klas skoonmaak.* → *Die klas moet deur die leerders skoongemaak ___.*"},"answers":{"af":["word"],"en":["word"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is","wees","het"],"en":["is","wees","het"]}},"explain":{"af":"Met *moet* kry die lydende vorm *moet* ... deelwoord + **word**. Let op die skeibare werkwoord: *skoonmaak* → *skoongemaak*.","en":"With *moet* the passive takes *moet* ... participle + **word**. Note the separable verb: *skoonmaak* → *skoongemaak*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Hy het my gister by die taxistaanplek gesien.* → *___ is gister deur hom by die taxistaanplek gesien.*","en":"*Hy het my gister by die taxistaanplek gesien.* → *___ is gister deur hom by die taxistaanplek gesien.*"},"answers":{"af":["Ek"],"en":["Ek"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["My","Hy","Myself"],"en":["My","Hy","Myself"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die voorwerp *my* word die onderwerp en kry die onderwerpsvorm **ek**. Die onderwerp *hy* word *deur hom*.","en":"The object *my* becomes the subject and takes the subject form **ek**. The subject *hy* becomes *deur hom*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Toeskouer vertel: Die kaptein het gesê: “Ons sal môre hier oefen as dit nie reën nie.” Watter indirekte weergawe is die beste?","en":"A spectator reports: Die kaptein het gesê: “Ons sal môre hier oefen as dit nie reën nie.” Which reported version is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Die kaptein het gesê dat ons môre hier sal oefen as dit nie reën nie.","en":"Die kaptein het gesê dat ons môre hier sal oefen as dit nie reën nie."},{"af":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar sou oefen as dit nie gereën het nie.","en":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar sou oefen as dit nie gereën het nie."},{"af":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar sal oefen as dit nie reën nie.","en":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar sal oefen as dit nie reën nie."},{"af":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar oefen sal as dit nie reën nie.","en":"Die kaptein het gesê dat hulle die volgende dag daar oefen sal as dit nie reën nie."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die toeskouer is nie in die span nie, dus *ons* → *hulle*; *môre* → *die volgende dag*; *hier* → *daar*; die tyd bly (*sal oefen*) en die werkwoorde staan aan die einde. Die weergawe met *sou oefen* en *gereën het* skuif die tyd terug soos in Engels.","en":"The spectator is not in the team, so *ons* → *hulle*; *môre* → *die volgende dag*; *hier* → *daar*; the tense stays (*sal oefen*) and the verbs stand at the end. The version with *sou oefen* and *gereën het* shifts the tense back as in English."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t3-visuele-geletterdheid","title":{"af":"Visuele geletterdheid en kritiese taalbewustheid: advertensies, spotprente en strokiesprente","en":"Visual literacy and critical language awareness: adverts, cartoons and comic strips"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal advertensies, spotprente en strokiesprente krities kan ontleed en vrae oor teikenmark, oorredingstegnieke, humor en bevooroordeelde taal kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to analyse adverts, cartoons and comic strips critically and answer questions on target market, persuasion techniques, humour and biased language."},"summary":{"af":"## Visuele tekste in die eksamen\n\nIn **Vraestel 1, Afdeling C** (Taalstrukture en -konvensies, 30 punte) kry jy gewoonlik 'n **advertensie**, 'n **spotprent of strokiesprent** en 'n teks, elk vir ongeveer 10 punte. Die vrae toets of jy die visuele teks verstaan én of jy taal in konteks kan hanteer: woordsoorte, meervoude, ontkenning, die lydende vorm. Hier word die visuele tekste in woorde beskryf; lees elke beskrywing so aandagtig soos jy na 'n prent sou kyk.\n\n## Advertensies\n\n| Deel | Wat dit is |\n|---|---|\n| Handelsnaam | die naam van die produk of maatskappy |\n| Logo | die simbool of embleem van die handelsnaam |\n| Slagspreuk | 'n kort, pakkende sin wat jy maklik onthou |\n| Kopskrif | die groot opskrif wat aandag trek |\n| Liggaam | die teks met inligting oor die produk of diens |\n| Kontakbesonderhede | telefoonnommer, webwerf, adres |\n| Kleinskrif by 'n sterretjie | die voorwaardes, bv. Aanbod geld tot 30 November |\n\n### Teikenmark\n\nDie **teikenmark** (teikengroep) is die mense vir wie die advertensie bedoel is. Motiveer altyd met 'n **visuele** leidraad (wie in die prent is, kleure, plek) én 'n **verbale** leidraad (woorde, register, sleng). 'n Skaatsplankryer en die woorde *Dis mal, bru!* wys op tieners; 'n groot lettertipe en *pensioenarisafslag* wys op ouer mense.\n\n### Oorredingstegnieke\n\n- Emosionele taal en hiperbool: *die heel beste in die land*\n- Gebiedende wys: *Koop nou!*\n- Retoriese vraag: *Moeg vir beurtkrag?*\n- Woordspeling: een woord met twee betekenisse\n- Alliterasie en rym: *Brits se beste braaivleis*\n- 'n Bekende persoon, bv. 'n rugbyster, wat die produk aanbeveel\n- *Gratis*, afslag en tydsdruk: *Net vandag!*\n- Direkte aanspreek met *jy* of *u*\n\n**Visuele elemente:** kleur (rooi trek aandag, groen dui op natuur of vars produkte), lettertipe en -grootte, die beeld, die uitleg en witruimte.\n\n**AIDA-model:** 'n Goeie advertensie trek **Aandag**, wek **Belangstelling**, skep **Begeerte** en lei tot **Aksie** (Engels: *Attention, Interest, Desire, Action*).\n\n## Spotprente en strokiesprente\n\n- **Spotprent:** een raam; lewer satiriese kommentaar op aktuele sake (politiek, beurtkrag, misdaad).\n- **Strokiesprent:** 'n reeks rame wat 'n kort storie vertel, gewoonlik met 'n humoristiese einde.\n\n| Element | Funksie |\n|---|---|\n| Spraakborrel | wat die karakter hardop sê |\n| Dinkborrel (wolkie) | wat die karakter dink, maar nie sê nie |\n| Skreeuborrel (gekartelde rand) | die karakter skree of is baie ontsteld |\n| Onomatopee | klanknabootsing: BOEM!, Kraak! |\n| Bewegingslyne | spoed of beweging |\n| Gesigsuitdrukking en lyftaal | gevoelens: gefronste wenkbroue = kwaad, hande in die lug = verbaas |\n| Vetdruk | klem op 'n woord |\n\n**Humor** ontstaan deur **ironie** (die teenoorgestelde van wat verwag word), **woordspeling**, **oordrywing** en 'n **onverwagte einde**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Vir *Waarom is die laaste raam snaaks?* noem jy (1) wat ons verwag het, (2) wat eintlik gebeur en (3) waarom die kontras humor skep.\n\n## Kritiese taalbewustheid\n\nKritiese taalbewustheid beteken jy lees nie net **wat** gesê word nie, maar ook **hoe** en **waarom**, en wie daardeur bevoordeel of benadeel word.\n\n- **Feit of mening:** 'n feit kan bewys word (*Die winkel maak om 08:00 oop*); 'n mening is 'n persoonlike oordeel (*Dit is die geselligste winkel in Brits*).\n- **Denotasie en konnotasie:** denotasie is die woordeboekbetekenis; konnotasie is die gevoelswaarde. *Goedkoop* klink negatief, *bekostigbaar* positief.\n- **Manipulerende en bevooroordeelde taal:** woorde wat die leser se gevoelens bespeel of net een kant van die saak gee.\n- **Stereotipering:** 'n hele groep word oor een kam geskeer: *Alle tieners is lui.*\n- **Seksisme in taal:** *Elke leerder moet sy boek bring* sluit meisies uit → *Leerders moet hul boeke bring.* *Brandweerman* → *brandbestryder*.\n- **Register:** formeel of informeel, na gelang van die leser.\n- **Taalvariëteite:** Standaardafrikaans, Kaaps en sleng. 'n Advertensie gebruik dikwels sleng om tieners te bereik.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders beskryf net die prent. Die vraag wil gewoonlik weet wat 'n element **beteken** of **bereik**, en die puntetoekenning sê hoeveel feite jy moet gee.","en":"## Visual texts in the exam\n\nIn **Paper 1, Section C** (Language structures and conventions, 30 marks) you usually get an **advertisement**, a **cartoon or comic strip** and a text, each worth about 10 marks. The questions test whether you understand the visual text and whether you can handle language in context: parts of speech, plurals, negation, the passive voice. Here the visual texts are described in words; read every description as carefully as you would look at a picture.\n\n## Advertisements\n\n| Part | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| Brand name (handelsnaam) | the name of the product or company |\n| Logo | the symbol or emblem of the brand |\n| Slogan (slagspreuk) | a short, catchy sentence that is easy to remember |\n| Headline (kopskrif) | the large heading that attracts attention |\n| Body (liggaam) | the text with information about the product or service |\n| Contact details | phone number, website, address |\n| Fine print at an asterisk | the conditions, e.g. Offer valid until 30 November |\n\n### Target market\n\nThe **target market (teikenmark)** is the people the advert is intended for. Always motivate with a **visual** clue (who is in the picture, colours, place) and a **verbal** clue (words, register, slang). A skateboarder and the words *Dis mal, bru!* point to teenagers; a large font and *pensioenarisafslag* (pensioner discount) point to older people.\n\n### Persuasion techniques (oorredingstegnieke)\n\n- Emotive language and hyperbole: *die heel beste in die land*\n- Imperative (gebiedende wys): *Koop nou!*\n- Rhetorical question: *Moeg vir beurtkrag?*\n- Pun (woordspeling): one word with two meanings\n- Alliteration and rhyme: *Brits se beste braaivleis*\n- A celebrity, e.g. a rugby star, who endorses the product\n- *Gratis* (free), discounts and time pressure: *Net vandag!*\n- Direct address with *jy* or *u*\n\n**Visual elements:** colour (red attracts attention, green suggests nature or fresh products), font type and size, the image, the layout and white space.\n\n**AIDA model:** A good advert grabs **Attention** (Aandag), creates **Interest** (Belangstelling), builds **Desire** (Begeerte) and leads to **Action** (Aksie).\n\n## Cartoons and comic strips\n\n- **Cartoon (spotprent):** one frame; gives satirical comment on current affairs (politics, load-shedding, crime).\n- **Comic strip (strokiesprent):** a series of frames that tells a short story, usually with a humorous ending.\n\n| Element | Function |\n|---|---|\n| Speech bubble (spraakborrel) | what the character says aloud |\n| Thought bubble (dinkborrel, wolkie) | what the character thinks but does not say |\n| Shout bubble (jagged edge) | the character shouts or is very upset |\n| Onomatopoeia | sound imitation: BOEM!, Kraak! |\n| Movement lines | speed or movement |\n| Facial expression and body language (lyftaal) | feelings: frowning eyebrows = angry, hands in the air = surprised |\n| Bold print | emphasis on a word |\n\n**Humour** comes from **irony** (the opposite of what is expected), **puns**, **exaggeration** and an **unexpected ending**.\n\n> **Tip:** For *Why is the last frame funny?* say (1) what we expected, (2) what actually happens and (3) why the contrast creates humour.\n\n## Critical language awareness (kritiese taalbewustheid)\n\nCritical language awareness means you read not only **what** is said, but also **how** and **why**, and who benefits or is disadvantaged by it.\n\n- **Fact or opinion (feit of mening):** a fact can be proved (*Die winkel maak om 08:00 oop*); an opinion is a personal judgement (*Dit is die geselligste winkel in Brits*).\n- **Denotation and connotation:** denotation is the dictionary meaning; connotation is the emotional value. *Goedkoop* (cheap) sounds negative, *bekostigbaar* (affordable) positive.\n- **Manipulative and biased language:** words that play on the reader's feelings or give only one side of the issue.\n- **Stereotyping (stereotipering):** a whole group is lumped together: *Alle tieners is lui.*\n- **Sexism in language:** *Elke leerder moet sy boek bring* excludes girls → *Leerders moet hul boeke bring.* *Brandweerman* (fireman) → *brandbestryder* (firefighter).\n- **Register:** formal or informal, depending on the reader.\n- **Language varieties:** Standard Afrikaans, Kaaps and slang. An advert often uses slang to reach teenagers.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners only describe the picture. The question usually wants to know what an element **means** or **achieves**, and the mark allocation tells you how many facts to give."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Teikenmark","en":"Target market"},"def":{"af":"Die groep mense vir wie 'n advertensie bedoel is, bv. tieners, ouers of pensioenarisse.","en":"The group of people an advert is intended for, e.g. teenagers, parents or pensioners."}},{"term":{"af":"Handelsnaam","en":"Brand name"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van die produk of maatskappy wat geadverteer word.","en":"The name of the product or company being advertised."}},{"term":{"af":"Slagspreuk","en":"Slogan"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort, pakkende sin wat by 'n handelsnaam hoort en maklik onthou word.","en":"A short, catchy sentence linked to a brand name that is easy to remember."}},{"term":{"af":"Oorredingstegniek","en":"Persuasion technique"},"def":{"af":"'n Taal- of visuele middel wat die leser oorreed om iets te koop of te doen, bv. 'n retoriese vraag of die gebiedende wys.","en":"A language or visual device that persuades the reader to buy or do something, e.g. a rhetorical question or the imperative."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordspeling","en":"Pun"},"def":{"af":"Die speelse gebruik van 'n woord of uitdrukking met twee betekenisse.","en":"The playful use of a word or expression with two meanings."}},{"term":{"af":"Spotprent","en":"Cartoon"},"def":{"af":"'n Tekening in een raam wat satiriese kommentaar op aktuele sake lewer.","en":"A drawing in one frame that gives satirical comment on current affairs."}},{"term":{"af":"Strokiesprent","en":"Comic strip"},"def":{"af":"'n Reeks rame met tekeninge en borrels wat 'n kort, gewoonlik humoristiese storie vertel.","en":"A series of frames with drawings and bubbles that tells a short, usually humorous story."}},{"term":{"af":"Konnotasie","en":"Connotation"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoelswaarde of bybetekenis van 'n woord, bo en behalwe die woordeboekbetekenis (denotasie).","en":"The emotional value or associated meaning of a word, over and above the dictionary meaning (denotation)."}},{"term":{"af":"Stereotipering","en":"Stereotyping"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n hele groep mense dieselfde (dikwels negatiewe) eienskap toegeskryf kry.","en":"When a whole group of people is given the same (often negative) characteristic."}},{"term":{"af":"Feit en mening","en":"Fact and opinion"},"def":{"af":"'n Feit kan bewys word; 'n mening is 'n persoonlike oordeel of gevoel.","en":"A fact can be proved; an opinion is a personal judgement or feeling."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ontleed 'n advertensie","en":"Analyse an advertisement"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die beskrywing van die advertensie en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Beskrywing:** Bo-aan staan die kopskrif in groot wit letters: MOEG VIR DIE STAD? Die foto wys 'n ontspanne jong paartjie met koffiebekers op 'n houtstoep. Agter hulle lê die Hartbeespoortdam en die Magaliesberg in die oranje lig van 'n sonsondergang. Regs onder is die logo, 'n klein geel son bo twee blou golwe, met die handelsnaam Damrus-gastehuis en die slagspreuk: “Kom bly by ons – jy sal bly wees!” Die liggaam lui: “Rustige kamers, 'n eie braaiplek en die mooiste sonsondergange in Noordwes. Boek nou en kry die derde nag GRATIS!” Agter GRATIS staan 'n sterretjie. Onderaan is 'n telefoonnommer en 'n webwerf, en in baie klein letters by die sterretjie: “Geld slegs van Sondag tot Donderdag.”\n\n(a) Wie is die teikenmark? Motiveer met een visuele en een verbale leidraad. (2)\n(b) Verduidelik die woordspeling in die slagspreuk. (2)\n(c) Noem twee oorredingstegnieke en gee 'n voorbeeld van elk. (2)\n(d) Waarom is die kleinskrif by die sterretjie belangrik vir die leser? (1)","en":"Read the description of the advertisement and answer the questions.\n\n**Description:** At the top is the headline in large white letters: MOEG VIR DIE STAD? (Tired of the city?) The photo shows a relaxed young couple with coffee mugs on a wooden deck. Behind them lie the Hartbeespoort Dam and the Magaliesberg in the orange light of a sunset. Bottom right is the logo, a small yellow sun above two blue waves, with the brand name Damrus-gastehuis and the slogan: “Kom bly by ons – jy sal bly wees!” The body reads: “Rustige kamers, 'n eie braaiplek en die mooiste sonsondergange in Noordwes. Boek nou en kry die derde nag GRATIS!” After GRATIS there is an asterisk. At the bottom is a phone number and a website, and in very small letters at the asterisk: “Geld slegs van Sondag tot Donderdag.” (Valid only from Sunday to Thursday.)\n\n(a) Who is the target market? Motivate with one visual and one verbal clue. (2)\n(b) Explain the pun in the slogan. (2)\n(c) Name two persuasion techniques and give an example of each. (2)\n(d) Why is the fine print at the asterisk important for the reader? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Teikenmark: stadsmense, bv. werkende volwassenes uit Pretoria of Johannesburg, wat 'n rustige wegbreek soek. Verbaal: die kopskrif *Moeg vir die stad?* praat met mense wat in die stad woon. Visueel: die ontspanne jong paartjie met koffie by die dam.","en":"(a) Target market: city people, e.g. working adults from Pretoria or Johannesburg, who want a quiet getaway. Verbal: the headline *Moeg vir die stad?* speaks to people who live in the city. Visual: the relaxed young couple with coffee at the dam."},{"af":"(b) Die eerste *bly* beteken om te **vertoef of oor te slaap**; die tweede *bly* beteken **gelukkig of tevrede**. Die advertensie belowe dus: as jy by ons oorbly, sal jy gelukkig wees.","en":"(b) The first *bly* means to **stay or sleep over**; the second *bly* means **happy or glad**. So the advert promises: if you stay with us, you will be happy."},{"af":"(c) Enige twee: retoriese vraag (*Moeg vir die stad?*); gebiedende wys (*Boek nou*); gratis-aanbod (*die derde nag GRATIS*); hiperbool (*die mooiste sonsondergange in Noordwes*).","en":"(c) Any two: rhetorical question (*Moeg vir die stad?*); imperative (*Boek nou*); free offer (*die derde nag GRATIS*); hyperbole (*die mooiste sonsondergange in Noordwes*)."},{"af":"(d) Die kleinskrif sê die gratis nag geld net van Sondag tot Donderdag, dus nie oor naweke nie. Die leser moet die voorwaardes lees voordat hy bespreek.","en":"(d) The fine print says the free night is valid only from Sunday to Thursday, so not over weekends. The reader must read the conditions before booking."}],"answer":{"af":"Teikenmark = stadsmense wat rus soek; woordspeling = bly (vertoef) en bly (gelukkig); tegnieke bv. retoriese vraag en gebiedende wys; die kleinskrif beperk die aanbod tot Sondag–Donderdag.","en":"Target market = city people looking for rest; pun = bly (stay) and bly (happy); techniques e.g. rhetorical question and imperative; the fine print limits the offer to Sunday–Thursday."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed 'n strokiesprent","en":"Analyse a comic strip"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die beskrywing van die strokiesprent en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Raam 1:** Ruan (16) sit by sy lessenaar met 'n stapel boeke en glimlag breed. Spraakborrel: “Ma, vanaand leer ek drie uur lank vir Afrikaans!” Sy ma staan in die deur, hande saamgevou, en glimlag trots.\n\n**Raam 2:** Die horlosie teen die muur wys 18:59. Ruan maak sy handboek oop en gaap groot. Sy selfoon lê langs die boek; die skerm gloei.\n\n**Raam 3:** Die hele raam is swart, behalwe Ruan se wit oë, 'n breë glimlag en die gloeiende selfoonskerm in sy hand. In 'n borrel met 'n gekartelde rand staan in vet letters: “AG NEE! BEURTKRAG! Nou kan ek ongelukkig nie leer nie ...” Uit die deur kom Ma se dinkborrel: “Ja-nee ... en die foon se battery is vol.”\n\n(a) Watter visuele leidraad in raam 3 wys dat Ruan eintlik nie ongelukkig is nie? (1)\n(b) Waarom het die borrel in raam 3 'n gekartelde rand? (1)\n(c) Waarom staan Ma se woorde in 'n dinkborrel en nie in 'n spraakborrel nie? (1)\n(d) Verduidelik waarom die laaste raam snaaks is. (2)\n(e) Benoem die woordsoort van *Ag* in raam 3. (1)","en":"Read the description of the comic strip and answer the questions.\n\n**Frame 1:** Ruan (16) sits at his desk with a pile of books, smiling broadly. Speech bubble: “Ma, vanaand leer ek drie uur lank vir Afrikaans!” (Mom, tonight I'm studying Afrikaans for three hours!) His mother stands in the doorway, hands folded, smiling proudly.\n\n**Frame 2:** The clock on the wall shows 18:59. Ruan opens his textbook and yawns widely. His cellphone lies next to the book; the screen glows.\n\n**Frame 3:** The whole frame is black, except Ruan's white eyes, a broad smile and the glowing phone screen in his hand. In a bubble with a jagged edge, in bold letters: “AG NEE! BEURTKRAG! Nou kan ek ongelukkig nie leer nie ...” (Oh no! Load-shedding! Now unfortunately I can't study ...) From the doorway comes Ma's thought bubble: “Ja-nee ... en die foon se battery is vol.” (Oh yes ... and the phone's battery is full.)\n\n(a) Which visual clue in frame 3 shows that Ruan is not really unhappy? (1)\n(b) Why does the bubble in frame 3 have a jagged edge? (1)\n(c) Why are Ma's words in a thought bubble and not in a speech bubble? (1)\n(d) Explain why the last frame is funny. (2)\n(e) Name the part of speech of *Ag* in frame 3. (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Sy **breë glimlag** (en wit oë wat blink) in die donker. Sy lyftaal weerspreek die woord *ongelukkig*.","en":"(a) His **broad smile** (and shining white eyes) in the dark. His body language contradicts the word *ongelukkig* (unfortunately)."},{"af":"(b) Die gekartelde rand wys dat Ruan **skree** of hard uitroep; sy reaksie is oordrewe en gespeel.","en":"(b) The jagged edge shows that Ruan **shouts** or exclaims loudly; his reaction is exaggerated and acted."},{"af":"(c) Ma sê dit nie hardop nie: dit is wat sy **dink**. Die leser weet dat sy hom nie glo nie, maar Ruan weet dit nie.","en":"(c) Ma does not say it aloud: it is what she **thinks**. The reader knows she does not believe him, but Ruan does not."},{"af":"(d) In raam 1 belowe Ruan om drie uur lank te leer, en ons verwag dat hy hard gaan werk. In raam 3 is hy **bly** oor beurtkrag, want dit gee hom 'n verskoning, al sê hy *ongelukkig*. Boonop het hy 'n foon met 'n vol battery, en die foon se lig sou hom kon help om te leer. Die kontras tussen sy belofte en sy optrede is ironies en snaaks.","en":"(d) In frame 1 Ruan promises to study for three hours, and we expect him to work hard. In frame 3 he is **glad** about load-shedding because it gives him an excuse, even though he says *ongelukkig*. On top of that he has a phone with a full battery, and its light could have helped him study. The contrast between his promise and his behaviour is ironic and funny."},{"af":"(e) *Ag* is 'n **tussenwerpsel**: dit druk 'n gevoel uit en staan los van die res van die sin.","en":"(e) *Ag* is an **interjection (tussenwerpsel)**: it expresses a feeling and stands apart from the rest of the sentence."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) breë glimlag; (b) hy skree; (c) Ma dink dit, sy sê dit nie; (d) ironie: hy belowe om te leer maar is bly oor die verskoning, terwyl die foon se lig hom kon help; (e) tussenwerpsel.","en":"(a) broad smile; (b) he shouts; (c) Ma thinks it, she does not say it; (d) irony: he promises to study but is glad about the excuse, while the phone's light could help him; (e) interjection (tussenwerpsel)."}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed 'n spotprent","en":"Analyse a cartoon"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die beskrywing van die spotprent en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Beskrywing (een raam):** Op die oewer van 'n dam staan 'n groot, blink bord: WELKOM BY ONS SKOON, PRAGTIGE DAM! Op die water dryf honderde plastiekbottels, skyfiesakkies en blikkies. 'n Visserman in 'n bootjie het sy stok opgetrek; aan die hoek hang 'n plastiekbottel. 'n Vis steek sy kop uit die rommel en sê in 'n spraakborrel: “Skoon? Ek het laas drie weke gelede water gesien!”\n\n(a) Verduidelik die ironie in die spotprent. (2)\n(b) Benoem die stylfiguur in die vis se woorde en verduidelik dit. (2)\n(c) Wat is die boodskap van die spotprent? (1)\n(d) Is die bord se bewering 'n feit of 'n mening? Motiveer. (2)","en":"Read the description of the cartoon and answer the questions.\n\n**Description (one frame):** On the bank of a dam stands a large, shiny sign: WELKOM BY ONS SKOON, PRAGTIGE DAM! (Welcome to our clean, beautiful dam!) Hundreds of plastic bottles, chip packets and cans float on the water. A fisherman in a small boat has pulled up his rod; a plastic bottle hangs from the hook. A fish sticks its head out of the rubbish and says in a speech bubble: “Skoon? Ek het laas drie weke gelede water gesien!” (Clean? The last time I saw water was three weeks ago!)\n\n(a) Explain the irony in the cartoon. (2)\n(b) Name the figure of speech in the fish's words and explain it. (2)\n(c) What is the message of the cartoon? (1)\n(d) Is the sign's claim a fact or an opinion? Motivate. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die bord beweer die dam is **skoon en pragtig**, maar die prent wys 'n dam vol rommel; die visserman vang selfs 'n bottel in plaas van 'n vis. Wat gesê word en wat ons sien, is die teenoorgestelde.","en":"(a) The sign claims the dam is **clean and beautiful**, but the picture shows a dam full of rubbish; the fisherman even catches a bottle instead of a fish. What is said and what we see are opposites."},{"af":"(b) **Hiperbool (oordrywing):** 'n vis leef in die water, maar beweer hy het lanklaas water gesien. Dit beklemtoon hoeveel rommel daar is. (*Personifikasie* is ook aanvaarbaar: die vis praat soos 'n mens.)","en":"(b) **Hyperbole (exaggeration):** a fish lives in water, yet claims it has not seen water for a long time. This stresses how much rubbish there is. (*Personification* is also acceptable: the fish talks like a person.)"},{"af":"(c) Mense besoedel ons damme; ons moet ophou rommel strooi en die water skoon hou, in plaas daarvan om net mooi borde op te sit.","en":"(c) People are polluting our dams; we must stop littering and keep the water clean, instead of just putting up nice signs."},{"af":"(d) **Mening:** *pragtig* is 'n persoonlike oordeel wat nie bewys kan word nie, en die prent wys boonop dat *skoon* nie waar is nie.","en":"(d) **Opinion:** *pragtig* (beautiful) is a personal judgement that cannot be proved, and the picture also shows that *skoon* (clean) is not true."}],"answer":{"af":"Ironie tussen die bord en die rommel; hiperbool (of personifikasie) in die vis se woorde; boodskap: hou ons damme skoon; die bord se bewering is 'n mening.","en":"Irony between the sign and the rubbish; hyperbole (or personification) in the fish's words; message: keep our dams clean; the sign's claim is an opinion."}},{"title":{"af":"Kritiese taalbewustheid","en":"Critical language awareness"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die sinne uit 'n skoolkoerant en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n1. Elke leerder moet sy toestemmingsbrief voor Vrydag inhandig.\n2. Alle tieners is lui en sit heeldag op hul selfone.\n3. A: Die snoepie verkoop nou bekostigbare middagetes. B: Die snoepie verkoop nou goedkoop middagetes.\n4. A: Die skoolsaal het 600 sitplekke. B: Die skoolsaal is die mooiste saal in Madibeng.\n\n(a) Watter soort bevooroordeelde taal kom in sin 1 voor? Herskryf die sin. (2)\n(b) Wat is verkeerd met sin 2? (1)\n(c) Verduidelik die verskil tussen 3A en 3B. (2)\n(d) Watter sin in 4 is 'n feit en watter een 'n mening? (2)","en":"Read the sentences from a school newspaper and answer the questions.\n\n1. Elke leerder moet sy toestemmingsbrief voor Vrydag inhandig. (Every learner must hand in his permission letter before Friday.)\n2. Alle tieners is lui en sit heeldag op hul selfone. (All teenagers are lazy and sit on their phones all day.)\n3. A: Die snoepie verkoop nou bekostigbare middagetes. B: Die snoepie verkoop nou goedkoop middagetes. (affordable vs cheap lunches)\n4. A: Die skoolsaal het 600 sitplekke. B: Die skoolsaal is die mooiste saal in Madibeng.\n\n(a) What kind of biased language occurs in sentence 1? Rewrite the sentence. (2)\n(b) What is wrong with sentence 2? (1)\n(c) Explain the difference between 3A and 3B. (2)\n(d) Which sentence in 4 is a fact and which one an opinion? (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Seksisme:** *sy* sluit meisies uit. Herskryf: *Leerders moet hul toestemmingsbriewe voor Vrydag inhandig.* (Of: *Elke leerder moet sy of haar toestemmingsbrief ...*)","en":"(a) **Sexism:** *sy* (his) excludes girls. Rewrite: *Leerders moet hul toestemmingsbriewe voor Vrydag inhandig.* (Or: *Elke leerder moet sy of haar toestemmingsbrief ...*)"},{"af":"(b) Dit is **stereotipering**: alle tieners word oor een kam geskeer, al is dit nie waar vir almal nie.","en":"(b) It is **stereotyping**: all teenagers are lumped together, even though it is not true for all of them."},{"af":"(c) Albei woorde het dieselfde **denotasie** (lae prys). *Bekostigbaar* het 'n **positiewe konnotasie** (goeie waarde), terwyl *goedkoop* 'n **negatiewe konnotasie** kan hê (swak gehalte).","en":"(c) Both words have the same **denotation** (low price). *Bekostigbaar* has a **positive connotation** (good value), while *goedkoop* can have a **negative connotation** (poor quality)."},{"af":"(d) 4A is 'n **feit**: die sitplekke kan getel word. 4B is 'n **mening**: *die mooiste* is 'n persoonlike oordeel.","en":"(d) 4A is a **fact**: the seats can be counted. 4B is an **opinion**: *die mooiste* (the most beautiful) is a personal judgement."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) seksisme, herskryf geslagsneutraal; (b) stereotipering; (c) dieselfde denotasie, verskillende konnotasie; (d) 4A feit, 4B mening.","en":"(a) sexism, rewrite gender-neutrally; (b) stereotyping; (c) same denotation, different connotation; (d) 4A fact, 4B opinion."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n slagspreuk?","en":"What is a slogan (slagspreuk)?"},"options":[{"af":"Die naam van die produk of maatskappy","en":"The name of the product or company"},{"af":"'n Kort, pakkende sin wat by die handelsnaam hoort en maklik onthou word","en":"A short, catchy sentence linked to the brand name that is easy to remember"},{"af":"Die klein skrif met die voorwaardes van 'n aanbod","en":"The small print with the conditions of an offer"},{"af":"Die simbool of embleem van die maatskappy","en":"The symbol or emblem of the company"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Slagspreuk is 'n kort, pakkende sin. Die naam is die handelsnaam, die simbool is die logo en die voorwaardes is die kleinskrif.","en":"A slogan is a short, catchy sentence. The name is the brand name, the symbol is the logo and the conditions are the fine print."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Strokiesprent bestaan altyd uit net een raam.","en":"A comic strip always consists of only one frame."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Spotprent het een raam; 'n strokiesprent is 'n reeks rame wat 'n storie vertel.","en":"False. A cartoon has one frame; a comic strip is a series of frames that tells a story."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die groep mense vir wie 'n advertensie bedoel is, is die ___.","en":"The group of people an advertisement is intended for is the ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["teikenmark","teikengroep","teikenpubliek"],"en":["teikenmark","teikengroep","teikenpubliek","target market"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["handelsnaam","slagspreuk","kopskrif"],"en":["handelsnaam","slagspreuk","kopskrif"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die teikenmark (teikengroep) is die mense op wie die advertensie gemik is. Motiveer dit altyd met visuele en verbale leidrade.","en":"The target market (teikenmark) is the people the advert is aimed at. Always motivate it with visual and verbal clues."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Bank se advertensie begin met: *Moeg vir lang toue?* Watter oorredingstegniek is dit?","en":"A bank's advert starts with: *Moeg vir lang toue?* (Tired of long queues?) Which persuasion technique is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Retoriese vraag","en":"Rhetorical question"},{"af":"Gebiedende wys","en":"Imperative"},{"af":"Alliterasie","en":"Alliteration"},{"af":"Bekende persoon","en":"Celebrity endorsement"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dit is 'n retoriese vraag: die advertensie verwag nie 'n antwoord nie, maar laat die leser aan sy eie frustrasie dink.","en":"It is a rhetorical question: the advert does not expect an answer, but makes the reader think of his own frustration."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Borrel met 'n gekartelde rand wys dat die karakter ___.","en":"A bubble with a jagged edge shows that the character ___ (answer in Afrikaans)."},"answers":{"af":["skree","skreeu","hard praat","uitroep"],"en":["skree","skreeu","hard praat","uitroep","shouts"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fluister","dink","slaap"],"en":["fluister","dink","slaap"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die gekartelde rand is 'n skreeuborrel: die karakter skree of is baie ontsteld. 'n Dinkborrel is wolkievormig.","en":"The jagged edge is a shout bubble: the character shouts or is very upset. A thought bubble is cloud-shaped."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stylfiguur kom in die slagspreuk *Brits se beste braaivleis* voor?","en":"Which figure of speech occurs in the slogan *Brits se beste braaivleis*?"},"options":[{"af":"Rym","en":"Rhyme"},{"af":"Personifikasie","en":"Personification"},{"af":"Alliterasie","en":"Alliteration"},{"af":"Retoriese vraag","en":"Rhetorical question"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Alliterasie is die herhaling van dieselfde beginklank: **B**rits, **b**este, **b**raaivleis. Dit maak die slagspreuk maklik om te onthou.","en":"Alliteration is the repetition of the same initial sound: **B**rits, **b**este, **b**raaivleis. It makes the slogan easy to remember."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *Seuns huil nie* is 'n voorbeeld van stereotipering.","en":"The sentence *Seuns huil nie* (Boys don't cry) is an example of stereotyping."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die sin skryf een eienskap aan alle seuns toe asof almal dieselfde is.","en":"True. The sentence gives one characteristic to all boys as if they were all the same."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Goedkoop* en *bekostigbaar* het dieselfde denotasie, maar *goedkoop* het 'n meer negatiewe ___.","en":"*Goedkoop* and *bekostigbaar* have the same denotation, but *goedkoop* has a more negative ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["konnotasie","bybetekenis","gevoelswaarde"],"en":["konnotasie","bybetekenis","gevoelswaarde","connotation"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["denotasie","slagspreuk","woordspeling"],"en":["denotasie","slagspreuk","woordspeling"]}},"explain":{"af":"Konnotasie is die gevoelswaarde van 'n woord. Die denotasie (woordeboekbetekenis) is dieselfde: 'n lae prys.","en":"Connotation is the emotional value of a word. The denotation (dictionary meaning) is the same: a low price."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie vir 'n nuwe selfoon wys 'n groep laggende tieners by 'n skoolkonsert. Die teks lui: *Moenie die oomblik mis nie – kiek dit, deel dit, vier dit!* Wie is die teikenmark?","en":"An advert for a new cellphone shows a group of laughing teenagers at a school concert. The text reads: *Moenie die oomblik mis nie – kiek dit, deel dit, vier dit!* Who is the target market?"},"options":[{"af":"Pensioenarisse wat 'n eenvoudige foon soek","en":"Pensioners looking for a simple phone"},{"af":"Sakemense wat baie e-posse stuur","en":"Business people who send lots of e-mails"},{"af":"Ouers van babas","en":"Parents of babies"},{"af":"Tieners en jong mense wat graag foto's deel","en":"Teenagers and young people who like sharing photos"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Visueel: laggende tieners by 'n skoolkonsert. Verbaal: die informele *kiek dit, deel dit* pas by jong mense wat foto's op sosiale media deel.","en":"Visual: laughing teenagers at a school concert. Verbal: the informal *kiek dit, deel dit* (snap it, share it) suits young people who share photos on social media."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom staan daar 'n asterisk (*) agter die woord GRATIS in 'n advertensie?","en":"Why is there an asterisk (*) after the word GRATIS (free) in an advert?"},"options":[{"af":"Om die leser se aandag op die logo te vestig","en":"To draw the reader's attention to the logo"},{"af":"Om te wys dat daar voorwaardes in die kleinskrif is","en":"To show that there are conditions in the fine print"},{"af":"Om aan te dui dat die hele produk gratis is","en":"To indicate that the whole product is free"},{"af":"Om die slagspreuk te beklemtoon","en":"To emphasise the slogan"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die sterretjie verwys na die kleinskrif onderaan, waar die voorwaardes staan. Dit is dikwels 'n beperking wat die aanbod minder aantreklik maak.","en":"The asterisk refers to the fine print at the bottom, where the conditions are. It is often a restriction that makes the offer less attractive."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke element van 'n strokiesprent by sy funksie.","en":"Match each element of a comic strip to its function."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Spraakborrel","en":"Speech bubble"},"r":{"af":"Die woorde wat die karakter hardop sê","en":"The words the character says aloud"}},{"l":{"af":"Dinkborrel","en":"Thought bubble"},"r":{"af":"Wat die karakter dink, maar nie sê nie","en":"What the character thinks but does not say"}},{"l":{"af":"Bewegingslyne","en":"Movement lines"},"r":{"af":"Wys spoed of beweging","en":"Show speed or movement"}},{"l":{"af":"Onomatopee","en":"Onomatopoeia"},"r":{"af":"'n Klanknabootsende woord soos BOEM!","en":"A sound-imitating word such as BOEM!"}},{"l":{"af":"Lyftaal","en":"Body language"},"r":{"af":"Houding en gebare wat gevoelens wys","en":"Posture and gestures that show feelings"}}],"explain":{"af":"Strokiesprente het min woorde, dus dra die visuele elemente baie van die betekenis en die humor.","en":"Comic strips have few words, so the visual elements carry much of the meaning and the humour."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak die sin geslagsneutraal: *Die brandweerman het die kat uit die boom gered.* → *Die ___ het die kat uit die boom gered.*","en":"Make the sentence gender-neutral: *Die brandweerman het die kat uit die boom gered.* → *Die ___ het die kat uit die boom gered.*"},"answers":{"af":["brandbestryder"],"en":["brandbestryder"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brandweerman","brandweervrou","brandweerkêrel"],"en":["brandweerman","brandweervrou","brandweerkêrel"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Brandweerman* sluit vroue uit en *brandweervrou* sluit mans uit. *Brandbestryder* is geslagsneutraal.","en":"*Brandweerman* (fireman) excludes women and *brandweervrou* excludes men. *Brandbestryder* (firefighter) is gender-neutral."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die slagspreuk *Ons verkoop vars lemoene* is *vars* 'n ___.","en":"In the slogan *Ons verkoop vars lemoene*, *vars* is a(n) ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["byvoeglike naamwoord","b.nw.","bnw","byvoeglike nw","adjektief"],"en":["byvoeglike naamwoord","b.nw.","bnw","byvoeglike nw","adjective"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["bywoord","selfstandige naamwoord","werkwoord"],"en":["bywoord","selfstandige naamwoord","werkwoord"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Vars* beskryf die selfstandige naamwoord *lemoene* en staan attributief voor dit, dus is dit 'n byvoeglike naamwoord.","en":"*Vars* (fresh) describes the noun *lemoene* (oranges) and stands attributively before it, so it is an adjective (byvoeglike naamwoord)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Potloodmaatskappy se slagspreuk is: *SkryfReg-potlode: skerp, net soos jy!* Verduidelik die woordspeling.","en":"A pencil company's slogan is: *SkryfReg-potlode: skerp, net soos jy!* Explain the pun."},"options":[{"af":"*Skerp* beteken die potlood het 'n fyn punt, maar ook dat die gebruiker slim is.","en":"*Skerp* means the pencil has a fine point, but also that the user is clever."},{"af":"*Skerp* is 'n retoriese vraag wat die leser laat nadink.","en":"*Skerp* is a rhetorical question that makes the reader think."},{"af":"*Skerp* is 'n hiperbool, want potlode kan nie sny nie.","en":"*Skerp* is hyperbole, because pencils cannot cut."},{"af":"*Skerp* is 'n stereotipe oor leerders wat potlode gebruik.","en":"*Skerp* is a stereotype about learners who use pencils."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Woordspeling gebruik twee betekenisse van een woord: *skerp* (met 'n fyn punt) en *skerp* (slim, vinnig van begrip). Die advertensie vlei die koper.","en":"A pun uses two meanings of one word: *skerp* (with a fine point) and *skerp* (clever, quick-witted). The advert flatters the buyer."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Strokiesprent: In raam 1 skree 'n afrigter vir sy span: “Julle moet harder werk! Geen pyn, geen glorie!” In raam 2 hardloop die spelers in die skroeiende son, met sweetdruppels wat afspat. In raam 3 lê die span uitgeput op die gras, terwyl die afrigter in die koelte sit met 'n koeldrank en 'n waaier en sê: “Sjoe, dis darem warm vandag.” Waarom is die laaste raam snaaks?","en":"Comic strip: In frame 1 a coach shouts at his team: “Julle moet harder werk! Geen pyn, geen glorie!” (You must work harder! No pain, no glory!) In frame 2 the players run in the scorching sun, with drops of sweat flying off. In frame 3 the team lies exhausted on the grass, while the coach sits in the shade with a cold drink and a fan and says: “Sjoe, dis darem warm vandag.” (Phew, it's really hot today.) Why is the last frame funny?"},"options":[{"af":"Die span wen die wedstryd in die laaste raam.","en":"The team wins the match in the last frame."},{"af":"Die afrigter gebruik 'n woordspeling met *glorie*.","en":"The coach uses a pun on *glorie*."},{"af":"Die spelers is kwaad vir mekaar.","en":"The players are angry with each other."},{"af":"Die afrigter eis harde werk, maar sit self gemaklik in die koelte en kla oor die hitte: dit is situasie-ironie.","en":"The coach demands hard work, but sits comfortably in the shade himself and complains about the heat: it is situational irony."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Ons verwag dat die afrigter self ook hard sal werk of ten minste met die span sal simpatiseer. In plaas daarvan kla hy oor die hitte terwyl hy niks doen nie. Die kontras skep die humor.","en":"We expect the coach to work hard too, or at least to sympathise with the team. Instead he complains about the heat while doing nothing. The contrast creates the humour."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie beweer: *Ons pille maak jou 10 jaar jonger!* Wat is die beste kritiese reaksie op hierdie bewering?","en":"An advert claims: *Ons pille maak jou 10 jaar jonger!* (Our pills make you 10 years younger!) What is the best critical response to this claim?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is 'n feit, want dit staan in 'n advertensie.","en":"It is a fact, because it is in an advert."},{"af":"Dit is 'n feit, want die getal 10 is presies.","en":"It is a fact, because the number 10 is exact."},{"af":"Dit is 'n onbewese, oordrewe bewering wat die leser manipuleer; 'n kritiese leser vra vir bewyse.","en":"It is an unproven, exaggerated claim that manipulates the reader; a critical reader asks for proof."},{"af":"Dit is 'n mening, want dit is in die gebiedende wys.","en":"It is an opinion, because it is in the imperative."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Niks word waar net omdat dit gedruk is of 'n presiese getal bevat nie. Die bewering is 'n hiperbool wat op mense se vrees vir ouderdom speel. Die sin is boonop 'n stelsin, nie die gebiedende wys nie.","en":"Nothing becomes true just because it is printed or contains an exact number. The claim is a hyperbole that plays on people's fear of ageing. The sentence is also a statement, not the imperative."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t3-drama","title":{"af":"Drama: terme en ontleding","en":"Drama: terms and analysis"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die dramaterme ken en kontekstuele vrae oor 'n drama-uittreksel kan beantwoord: neweteks, konflik, spanning, dramatiese ironie en karakterisering.","en":"You will know the drama terms and be able to answer contextual questions on a drama extract: stage directions, conflict, tension, dramatic irony and characterisation."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is drama?\n\n'n Drama is 'n **opvoerteks**: dit word geskryf om deur akteurs op 'n verhoog opgevoer te word. Daarom bestaan dit uit twee soorte teks:\n\n- **Hoofteks** – die **dialoog**: alles wat die karakters sê. Die karakter se naam staan links, gevolg deur 'n dubbelpunt.\n- **Neweteks** – die **toneelaanwysings**, in *kursief* of tussen hakies. Dit beskryf beweging, gebare, toon (*kwaad, fluisterend*), die dekor, beligting, klankeffekte en rekwisiete (voorwerpe op die verhoog).\n\nDie **rolverdeling** (karakterlys) aan die begin noem die karakters en soms hul ouderdom of verhouding. 'n Drama word in **bedrywe** verdeel, en 'n bedryf in **tonele**. 'n Nuwe toneel begin gewoonlik wanneer die tyd of plek verander.\n\n## Spreekvorme\n\n| Term | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| Dialoog | 'n gesprek tussen twee of meer karakters |\n| Monoloog | een karakter praat lank aan die woord terwyl ander karakters luister |\n| Alleenspraak | 'n karakter is alleen (of dink hy is alleen) en spreek sy gedagtes hardop uit; die gehoor kry insig in sy innerlike |\n\n## Struktuur: Freytag se piramide\n\n1. **Eksposisie** – die karakters, ruimte, tyd en agtergrond word bekendgestel.\n2. **Komplikasie / stygende aksie** – die konflik begin en die spanning bou op.\n3. **Klimaks / krisis** – die hoogtepunt van die konflik; die keerpunt.\n4. **Afwikkeling** – die gebeure ná die klimaks; die spanning neem af.\n5. **Ontknoping** – die finale uitkoms; die los drade word vasgeknoop.\n\n## Konflik en spanning\n\n- **Innerlike konflik** – 'n stryd binne die karakter: skuld, twyfel, 'n moeilike keuse.\n- **Uiterlike konflik** – karakter teen karakter, teen die samelewing of teen die natuur.\n\n**Spanning** laat die gehoor wonder wat gaan gebeur. Dit word geskep deur konflik, geheime, kort en skerp dialoog, onderbrekings en beletseltekens (...), stiltes en toneelaanwysings soos *(voetstappe kom nader)* of *(die ligte gaan af)*.\n\n## Dramatiese ironie\n\n**Dramatiese ironie** is wanneer die **gehoor meer weet as die karakter**. As ons weet die visstok lê stukkend onder die seil, maar die pa spog dat hy môre daarmee gaan wen, voel ons die spanning. Moenie dit met **verbale ironie** verwar nie: daar sê iemand die teenoorgestelde van wat hy bedoel.\n\n## Karakterisering\n\nIn 'n drama is daar gewoonlik nie 'n verteller wat die karakters beskryf nie. Ons leer hulle ken deur:\n\n- wat hulle **sê** (dialoog) en hoe hulle dit sê;\n- wat hulle **doen**;\n- die **toneelaanwysings** (gebare, toon, gesigsuitdrukking);\n- wat **ander karakters** oor hulle sê en hoe hulle op hulle reageer.\n\nDie **protagonis** is die hoofkarakter; die **antagonis** werk hom teen. 'n **Ronde** karakter het verskillende kante, 'n **plat** karakter net een. 'n **Dinamiese** karakter verander en ontwikkel; 'n **statiese** karakter bly dieselfde.\n\n## Ruimte, tema en toon\n\n- **Ruimte en tyd:** waar en wanneer die drama afspeel; die dekor en beligting wys dit.\n- **Tema:** die boodskap of insig oor die lewe (bv. *eerlikheid vra moed*). Die **onderwerp** is net waaroor dit gaan.\n- **Simbool en motief:** 'n simbool is 'n voorwerp met 'n dieper betekenis; 'n motief kom herhaaldelik voor.\n- **Toon en atmosfeer:** die karakter se houding (sarkasties, smekend) en die gevoel wat die toneel skep (gespanne, vrolik).\n\n## Komedie en tragedie\n\n'n **Komedie** gebruik humor en misverstande en eindig gewoonlik gelukkig. 'n **Tragedie** is ernstig: die hoofkarakter beleef verlies of ondergang, dikwels weens sy eie swakheid.\n\n## Kontekstuele vrae beantwoord\n\n- *Plaas die uittreksel in konteks:* wie, waar en wat het pas gebeur.\n- *Watter toneelaanwysing sou jy gee? Motiveer:* gee 'n konkrete aanwysing, bv. *(slaan met die vuis op die tafel)*, plus 'n rede uit die teks.\n- *Verduidelik die dramatiese ironie:* wat die gehoor weet + wat die karakter nie weet nie.\n- *Is X se reaksie geloofwaardig?* Ja/Nee + motivering met bewyse uit die teks.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders gee net hul mening sonder 'n aanhaling of verwysing na die teks. Elke punt moet bewys hê, en die puntetoekenning sê hoeveel punte jy moet maak.","en":"## What is drama?\n\nA drama is a **performance text (opvoerteks)**: it is written to be performed by actors on a stage. That is why it consists of two kinds of text:\n\n- **Main text (hoofteks)** – the **dialogue**: everything the characters say. The character's name stands on the left, followed by a colon.\n- **Side text (neweteks)** – the **stage directions (toneelaanwysings)**, in *italics* or in brackets. They describe movement, gestures, tone (*kwaad, fluisterend*), the set, lighting, sound effects and props (objects on stage).\n\nThe **cast list (rolverdeling)** at the start names the characters and sometimes their age or relationship. A drama is divided into **acts (bedrywe)**, and an act into **scenes (tonele)**. A new scene usually starts when the time or place changes.\n\n## Forms of speech\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Dialogue (dialoog) | a conversation between two or more characters |\n| Monologue (monoloog) | one character speaks at length while other characters listen |\n| Soliloquy (alleenspraak) | a character is alone (or thinks he is alone) and speaks his thoughts aloud; the audience gains insight into his inner self |\n\n## Structure: Freytag's pyramid\n\n1. **Exposition (eksposisie)** – the characters, setting, time and background are introduced.\n2. **Complication / rising action (komplikasie / stygende aksie)** – the conflict starts and the tension builds.\n3. **Climax / crisis (klimaks / krisis)** – the high point of the conflict; the turning point.\n4. **Falling action (afwikkeling)** – the events after the climax; the tension decreases.\n5. **Resolution (ontknoping)** – the final outcome; the loose ends are tied up.\n\n## Conflict and tension\n\n- **Internal conflict (innerlike konflik)** – a struggle inside the character: guilt, doubt, a difficult choice.\n- **External conflict (uiterlike konflik)** – character against character, against society or against nature.\n\n**Tension (spanning)** makes the audience wonder what will happen. It is created by conflict, secrets, short and sharp dialogue, interruptions and ellipses (...), silences and stage directions such as *(voetstappe kom nader)* (footsteps approach) or *(die ligte gaan af)* (the lights go out).\n\n## Dramatic irony\n\n**Dramatic irony (dramatiese ironie)** is when the **audience knows more than the character**. If we know the fishing rod lies broken under the cover, but the father boasts that he will win with it tomorrow, we feel the tension. Do not confuse it with **verbal irony**: there someone says the opposite of what he means.\n\n## Characterisation\n\nIn a drama there is usually no narrator who describes the characters. We get to know them through:\n\n- what they **say** (dialogue) and how they say it;\n- what they **do**;\n- the **stage directions** (gestures, tone, facial expression);\n- what **other characters** say about them and how they react to them.\n\nThe **protagonist** is the main character; the **antagonist** opposes him. A **round** character has different sides, a **flat** character only one. A **dynamic** character changes and develops; a **static** character stays the same.\n\n## Setting, theme and tone\n\n- **Setting and time (ruimte en tyd):** where and when the drama takes place; the set and lighting show it.\n- **Theme (tema):** the message or insight about life (e.g. *honesty takes courage*). The **subject (onderwerp)** is only what it is about.\n- **Symbol and motif:** a symbol is an object with a deeper meaning; a motif recurs.\n- **Tone and atmosphere:** the character's attitude (sarcastic, pleading) and the feeling the scene creates (tense, cheerful).\n\n## Comedy and tragedy\n\nA **comedy** uses humour and misunderstandings and usually ends happily. A **tragedy** is serious: the main character experiences loss or downfall, often because of his own weakness.\n\n## Answering contextual questions\n\n- *Plaas die uittreksel in konteks (Place the extract in context):* who, where and what has just happened.\n- *Watter toneelaanwysing sou jy gee? Motiveer:* give a concrete direction, e.g. *(slaan met die vuis op die tafel)*, plus a reason from the text.\n- *Verduidelik die dramatiese ironie:* what the audience knows + what the character does not know.\n- *Is X se reaksie geloofwaardig? (Is X's reaction credible?)* Yes/No + motivation with evidence from the text.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners give only their opinion without a quote or reference to the text. Every point needs evidence, and the mark allocation tells you how many points to make."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Opvoerteks","en":"Performance text"},"def":{"af":"'n Teks wat geskryf is om deur akteurs voor 'n gehoor opgevoer te word.","en":"A text written to be performed by actors in front of an audience."}},{"term":{"af":"Hoofteks","en":"Main text"},"def":{"af":"Die dialoog: die woorde wat die karakters sê.","en":"The dialogue: the words the characters speak."}},{"term":{"af":"Neweteks (toneelaanwysings)","en":"Side text (stage directions)"},"def":{"af":"Die aanwysings in kursief of tussen hakies oor beweging, toon, dekor, beligting, klank en rekwisiete.","en":"The directions in italics or brackets about movement, tone, set, lighting, sound and props."}},{"term":{"af":"Rolverdeling","en":"Cast list"},"def":{"af":"Die lys van karakters aan die begin van 'n drama.","en":"The list of characters at the start of a drama."}},{"term":{"af":"Bedryf en toneel","en":"Act and scene"},"def":{"af":"'n Bedryf is 'n groot deel van 'n drama; dit bestaan uit kleiner tonele, wat gewoonlik verander as die tyd of plek verander.","en":"An act is a large part of a drama; it consists of smaller scenes, which usually change when the time or place changes."}},{"term":{"af":"Alleenspraak","en":"Soliloquy"},"def":{"af":"'n Karakter wat alleen op die verhoog sy gedagtes en gevoelens hardop uitspreek.","en":"A character who, alone on stage, speaks his thoughts and feelings aloud."}},{"term":{"af":"Monoloog","en":"Monologue"},"def":{"af":"'n Lang toespraak deur een karakter terwyl ander karakters luister.","en":"A long speech by one character while other characters listen."}},{"term":{"af":"Dramatiese ironie","en":"Dramatic irony"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die gehoor iets weet wat 'n karakter nie weet nie.","en":"When the audience knows something that a character does not know."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaks","en":"Climax"},"def":{"af":"Die hoogtepunt en keerpunt van die konflik in 'n drama.","en":"The high point and turning point of the conflict in a drama."}},{"term":{"af":"Ontknoping","en":"Resolution"},"def":{"af":"Die finale uitkoms van die drama, waarin die los drade vasgeknoop word.","en":"The final outcome of the drama, in which the loose ends are tied up."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kontekstuele vrae op 'n uittreksel","en":"Contextual questions on an extract"},"problem":{"af":"*In die vorige toneel het die gehoor gesien hoe Zander per ongeluk sy pa se nuwe visstok breek en die stukke onder die bootseil wegsteek. Mia het hom gesien.*\n\n**ROLVERDELING:** ZANDER (16) · MIA (16, Zander se vriendin) · OOM GERT (Zander se pa)\n\n*(Saterdagaand by 'n huurhuisie langs die Hartbeespoortdam. Die vuur gloei. OOM GERT draai die tjops om. ZANDER en MIA sit op 'n bankie. Agter hulle staan die boot, met 'n seil oorgetrek.)*\n\nOOM GERT: *(tevrede, snuif die lug in)* Ruik jy dit, Zander? Dis die reuk van wen. Môre vang ons die grootste baber in die dam – met my nuwe stok.\n\nZANDER: *(sonder om op te kyk)* Ja, Pa ... môre.\n\nMIA: *(fluisterend, stamp hom met haar elmboog)* Sê vir hom.\n\nZANDER: *(fluister terug)* Bly stil!\n\nOOM GERT: Wat fluister julle twee daar? Gaan haal sommer die stok onder die seil, dan wys ek vir Mia hoe 'n regte visstok lyk.\n\nZANDER: *(spring op, te vinnig)* Nee! Ek bedoel ... Pa, dis donker. Die muskiete ...\n\nOOM GERT: *(lag)* Muskiete? Jy speel eerstespan-rugby, maar jy's bang vir 'n muskiet?\n\n*(MIA kyk na die grond. 'n Lang stilte. Net die vuur knetter.)*\n\nZANDER: *(sag)* Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê.\n\n*(Die ligte van die huisie flikker en gaan af. Beurtkrag. Net die vuur gloei nog.)*\n\nOOM GERT: *(in die donker)* Nou ja. Praat, my seun.\n\n(a) Plaas die uittreksel in konteks. (2)\n(b) Verduidelik die dramatiese ironie in Oom Gert se eerste spreekbeurt. (2)\n(c) Haal twee toneelaanwysings aan wat spanning skep en verduidelik hoe. (2)\n(d) Watter innerlike konflik beleef Zander? (2)","en":"*In the previous scene the audience saw Zander accidentally break his father's new fishing rod and hide the pieces under the boat cover. Mia saw him.*\n\n**CAST:** ZANDER (16) · MIA (16, Zander's friend) · OOM GERT (Zander's father)\n\n*(Saturday evening at a rented cottage beside the Hartbeespoort Dam. The fire glows. OOM GERT turns the chops. ZANDER and MIA sit on a bench. Behind them stands the boat, covered with a tarpaulin.)*\n\nOOM GERT: *(tevrede, snuif die lug in)* Ruik jy dit, Zander? Dis die reuk van wen. Môre vang ons die grootste baber in die dam – met my nuwe stok. (Smell that? It's the smell of winning. Tomorrow we catch the biggest barbel in the dam – with my new rod.)\n\nZANDER: *(sonder om op te kyk)* Ja, Pa ... môre.\n\nMIA: *(fluisterend, stamp hom met haar elmboog)* Sê vir hom. (Tell him.)\n\nZANDER: *(fluister terug)* Bly stil! (Be quiet!)\n\nOOM GERT: Wat fluister julle twee daar? Gaan haal sommer die stok onder die seil, dan wys ek vir Mia hoe 'n regte visstok lyk. (Go and fetch the rod under the cover.)\n\nZANDER: *(spring op, te vinnig)* Nee! Ek bedoel ... Pa, dis donker. Die muskiete ...\n\nOOM GERT: *(lag)* Muskiete? Jy speel eerstespan-rugby, maar jy's bang vir 'n muskiet?\n\n*(MIA kyk na die grond. 'n Lang stilte. Net die vuur knetter.)*\n\nZANDER: *(sag)* Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê. (Dad ... I have to tell you something.)\n\n*(Die ligte van die huisie flikker en gaan af. Beurtkrag. Net die vuur gloei nog.)*\n\nOOM GERT: *(in die donker)* Nou ja. Praat, my seun.\n\n(a) Place the extract in context. (2)\n(b) Explain the dramatic irony in Oom Gert's first speech. (2)\n(c) Quote two stage directions that create tension and explain how. (2)\n(d) What internal conflict does Zander experience? (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Dit is Saterdagaand by 'n huurhuisie langs die Hartbeespoortdam. Zander het pas sy pa se nuwe visstok per ongeluk gebreek en weggesteek; Mia weet daarvan, maar Oom Gert nie.","en":"(a) It is Saturday evening at a rented cottage beside the Hartbeespoort Dam. Zander has just accidentally broken and hidden his father's new fishing rod; Mia knows about it, but Oom Gert does not."},{"af":"(b) Oom Gert spog dat hulle môre die grootste baber **met sy nuwe stok** gaan vang. Die gehoor weet die stok lê stukkend onder die seil, maar hy weet dit nie. Sy selfvertroue maak die gehoor gespanne oor wat gaan gebeur as hy die waarheid uitvind.","en":"(b) Oom Gert boasts that tomorrow they will catch the biggest barbel **with his new rod**. The audience knows the rod lies broken under the cover, but he does not. His confidence makes the audience tense about what will happen when he finds out the truth."},{"af":"(c) Enige twee: *(spring op, te vinnig)* wys Zander se paniek, en die gehoor vrees dat hy homself gaan verraai; *('n Lang stilte. Net die vuur knetter.)* laat die gehoor wag op wat gaan gebeur; *(Die ligte ... gaan af.)* skep 'n onverwagte, donker atmosfeer net voor die bekentenis.","en":"(c) Any two: *(spring op, te vinnig)* shows Zander's panic, and the audience fears he will give himself away; *('n Lang stilte. Net die vuur knetter.)* makes the audience wait for what will happen; *(Die ligte ... gaan af.)* creates an unexpected, dark atmosphere just before the confession."},{"af":"(d) Zander twyfel of hy eerlik moet wees en die waarheid moet vertel, of moet stilbly om sy pa se teleurstelling en woede te vermy. Sy aarseling (*Ja, Pa ... môre.*; *Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê.*) wys die stryd.","en":"(d) Zander doubts whether he should be honest and tell the truth, or keep quiet to avoid his father's disappointment and anger. His hesitation (*Ja, Pa ... môre.*; *Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê.*) shows the struggle."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Braai by die dam; Zander het die stok gebreek en weggesteek. (b) Die gehoor weet die stok is stukkend, Oom Gert nie. (c) bv. spring op, te vinnig / lang stilte / ligte gaan af. (d) eerlikheid teenoor vrees vir sy pa se reaksie.","en":"(a) Braai at the dam; Zander broke and hid the rod. (b) The audience knows the rod is broken, Oom Gert does not. (c) e.g. jumps up too quickly / long silence / lights go out. (d) honesty versus fear of his father's reaction."}},{"title":{"af":"Herken en ontleed 'n alleenspraak","en":"Recognise and analyse a soliloquy"},"problem":{"af":"Later in dieselfde toneel stap Zander en sy pa na die boot. Mia bly agter.\n\nMIA: *(alleen by die vuur, kyk na die donker water)* Hoekom kon ek nie net my mond hou nie? As Zander nou alles vertel en hulle baklei, is dit my skuld. Maar as hy niks sê nie ... dan lieg ons albei. *(Sy gooi 'n stokkie hard in die vuur.)* Eerlikheid is maklik – solank dit nie jou eie pa is wat jy moet teleurstel nie.\n\n(a) Is dit 'n dialoog, monoloog of alleenspraak? Motiveer. (2)\n(b) Wat leer die gehoor hier oor Mia wat hulle nie uit die vorige dialoog kon aflei nie? (1)\n(c) Watter tema kom in die laaste sin na vore? (1)\n(d) Wat wys die toneelaanwysing *(Sy gooi 'n stokkie hard in die vuur.)* oor Mia se gevoelens? (1)","en":"Later in the same scene Zander and his father walk to the boat. Mia stays behind.\n\nMIA: *(alleen by die vuur, kyk na die donker water)* Hoekom kon ek nie net my mond hou nie? As Zander nou alles vertel en hulle baklei, is dit my skuld. Maar as hy niks sê nie ... dan lieg ons albei. *(Sy gooi 'n stokkie hard in die vuur.)* Eerlikheid is maklik – solank dit nie jou eie pa is wat jy moet teleurstel nie. (Why couldn't I just keep quiet? If Zander tells everything now and they fight, it's my fault. But if he says nothing ... then we are both lying. Honesty is easy – as long as it isn't your own father you have to disappoint.)\n\n(a) Is this a dialogue, monologue or soliloquy? Motivate. (2)\n(b) What does the audience learn about Mia here that they could not infer from the earlier dialogue? (1)\n(c) Which theme emerges in the last sentence? (1)\n(d) What does the stage direction *(Sy gooi 'n stokkie hard in die vuur.)* show about Mia's feelings? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) **Alleenspraak.** Mia is alleen op die verhoog (*alleen by die vuur*) en spreek haar gedagtes hardop uit; niemand anders hoor haar nie.","en":"(a) **Soliloquy (alleenspraak).** Mia is alone on stage (*alleen by die vuur*) and speaks her thoughts aloud; nobody else hears her."},{"af":"(b) Mia voel **skuldig en verskeur**: sy is bang dat sy die rusie veroorsaak het, maar sy wil ook nie lieg nie. Die alleenspraak wys haar innerlike konflik.","en":"(b) Mia feels **guilty and torn**: she is afraid that she caused the quarrel, but she also does not want to lie. The soliloquy shows her internal conflict."},{"af":"(c) **Eerlikheid vra moed**: dit is maklik om eerlik te wees as daar niks vir jou op die spel is nie.","en":"(c) **Honesty takes courage**: it is easy to be honest when nothing is at stake for you."},{"af":"(d) Die harde gooi wys haar **frustrasie en spanning**: sy is kwaad vir haarself en magteloos.","en":"(d) The hard throw shows her **frustration and tension**: she is angry with herself and powerless."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) alleenspraak – sy is alleen en dink hardop; (b) sy voel skuldig en verskeur; (c) eerlikheid vra moed; (d) frustrasie.","en":"(a) soliloquy – she is alone and thinks aloud; (b) she feels guilty and torn; (c) honesty takes courage; (d) frustration."}},{"title":{"af":"Freytag se piramide","en":"Freytag's pyramid"},"problem":{"af":"Hier is die gebeure van 'n eenbedryf-drama, *Die Eindronde*, deurmekaar gelys. Rangskik hulle volgens Freytag se piramide en benoem elke fase.\n\n- **A:** Op die oggend van die eindronde erken Lize voor haar onderwyser dat sy die antwoorde gesien het, en sy onttrek aan die kompetisie.\n- **B:** Lize, 'n Graad 10-leerder in Brits, oefen elke aand vir 'n provinsiale wiskundekompetisie terwyl haar ma lang skofte op 'n sitrusplaas werk.\n- **C:** Lize se vriend Kabelo wen die kompetisie. Lize besef sy is trotser op haar eerlikheid as wat sy op 'n medalje sou wees.\n- **D:** Lize kry per toeval die antwoorde in die hande en twyfel of sy dit moet gebruik; haar onderwyser begin agterdogtig raak.\n- **E:** Die hoof besluit dat 'n nuwe vraestel opgestel word, en Lize hoor sy mag volgende jaar weer deelneem.","en":"Here are the events of a one-act drama, *Die Eindronde* (The Final Round), listed out of order. Arrange them according to Freytag's pyramid and name each stage.\n\n- **A:** On the morning of the final round Lize admits to her teacher that she has seen the answers, and she withdraws from the competition.\n- **B:** Lize, a Grade 10 learner in Brits, practises every evening for a provincial maths competition while her mother works long shifts on a citrus farm.\n- **C:** Lize's friend Kabelo wins the competition. Lize realises she is prouder of her honesty than she would have been of a medal.\n- **D:** Lize gets hold of the answers by accident and doubts whether she should use them; her teacher starts to become suspicious.\n- **E:** The principal decides that a new paper will be set, and Lize hears she may take part again next year."},"steps":[{"af":"**Eksposisie = B:** ons leer Lize, haar ambisie en haar omstandighede ken.","en":"**Exposition = B:** we get to know Lize, her ambition and her circumstances."},{"af":"**Komplikasie / stygende aksie = D:** die konflik begin (die antwoorde, haar twyfel) en die spanning styg (die onderwyser raak agterdogtig).","en":"**Complication / rising action = D:** the conflict starts (the answers, her doubt) and the tension rises (the teacher becomes suspicious)."},{"af":"**Klimaks = A:** die keerpunt: sy kies eerlikheid en erken alles.","en":"**Climax = A:** the turning point: she chooses honesty and admits everything."},{"af":"**Afwikkeling = E:** die gevolge ná die klimaks word hanteer en die spanning neem af.","en":"**Falling action = E:** the consequences after the climax are dealt with and the tension decreases."},{"af":"**Ontknoping = C:** die finale uitkoms: Kabelo wen, en Lize se insig sluit die drama af.","en":"**Resolution = C:** the final outcome: Kabelo wins, and Lize's insight closes the drama."}],"answer":{"af":"B (eksposisie) → D (komplikasie) → A (klimaks) → E (afwikkeling) → C (ontknoping)","en":"B (exposition) → D (complication) → A (climax) → E (falling action) → C (resolution)"}},{"title":{"af":"Kort literêre paragraaf: karakterontwikkeling","en":"Short literary paragraph: character development"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys na die uittreksel in Voorbeeld 1. Skryf 'n paragraaf van ongeveer 120 woorde: **Bespreek hoe Zander se karakter in die uittreksel ontwikkel.**","en":"Refer to the extract in Example 1. Write a paragraph of about 120 words: **Discuss how Zander's character develops in the extract.**"},"steps":[{"af":"**Kernsin:** Zander ontwikkel van 'n ontwykende, bang seun tot iemand wat die moed het om eerlik te wees; hy is dus 'n dinamiese karakter.","en":"**Topic sentence:** Zander develops from an evasive, frightened boy into someone who has the courage to be honest; he is therefore a dynamic character."},{"af":"**Bewys 1:** Aan die begin vermy hy sy pa: hy antwoord *sonder om op te kyk* en sê net *Ja, Pa ... môre.* Die beletselteken wys sy aarseling.","en":"**Evidence 1:** At the start he avoids his father: he answers *sonder om op te kyk* (without looking up) and only says *Ja, Pa ... môre.* The ellipsis shows his hesitation."},{"af":"**Bewys 2:** Wanneer sy pa die stok wil sien, *spring* hy *op, te vinnig* en verskoon hom met die muskiete; sy paniek wys sy skuldgevoel.","en":"**Evidence 2:** When his father wants to see the rod, he *spring op, te vinnig* (jumps up too quickly) and makes the mosquitoes his excuse; his panic shows his guilt."},{"af":"**Bewys 3 en slot:** Ná die lang stilte sê hy *sag: Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê.* Hy kies eerlikheid bo sy vrees. Die ontwikkeling beklemtoon die tema dat eerlikheid moed vra.","en":"**Evidence 3 and conclusion:** After the long silence he says *sag: Pa ... ek moet vir Pa iets sê.* (softly: Dad ... I have to tell you something.) He chooses honesty over his fear. The development emphasises the theme that honesty takes courage."}],"answer":{"af":"'n Paragraaf met 'n duidelike kernsin, drie bewyse uit die hoofteks en neweteks, en 'n slot wat na die tema terugverwys.","en":"A paragraph with a clear topic sentence, three pieces of evidence from the main text and side text, and a conclusion that links back to the theme."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die neweteks in 'n drama?","en":"What is the side text (neweteks) in a drama?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dialoog wat die karakters sê","en":"The dialogue the characters speak"},{"af":"Die toneelaanwysings oor beweging, toon, dekor en beligting","en":"The stage directions about movement, tone, set and lighting"},{"af":"Die tema van die drama","en":"The theme of the drama"},{"af":"Die opsomming van die intrige op die agterblad","en":"The plot summary on the back cover"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die neweteks is die toneelaanwysings. Die dialoog is die hoofteks.","en":"The side text is the stage directions. The dialogue is the main text."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Toneelaanwysings word gewoonlik in kursief of tussen hakies geskryf.","en":"Stage directions are usually written in italics or in brackets."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die kursief of hakies skei die neweteks van die dialoog, sodat die akteurs weet wat hulle nie hardop moet sê nie.","en":"True. The italics or brackets separate the side text from the dialogue, so the actors know what not to say aloud."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die woorde wat die karakters sê, vorm die ___ van die drama.","en":"The words the characters speak form the ___ of the drama (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["hoofteks","dialoog"],"en":["hoofteks","dialoog","main text","dialogue"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["neweteks","rolverdeling","toneelaanwysing"],"en":["neweteks","rolverdeling","toneelaanwysing"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die hoofteks is die dialoog. Die neweteks (toneelaanwysings) word nie hardop gesê nie.","en":"The main text (hoofteks) is the dialogue. The side text (stage directions) is not spoken aloud."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Drama word in bedrywe verdeel, en elke bedryf bestaan uit een of meer ___.","en":"A drama is divided into acts (bedrywe), and each act consists of one or more ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["tonele","toneel"],"en":["tonele","toneel","scenes"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["strofes","hoofstukke","versreëls"],"en":["strofes","hoofstukke","versreëls"]}},"explain":{"af":"Bedrywe bestaan uit tonele. Strofes en versreëls hoort by poësie, hoofstukke by 'n roman.","en":"Acts consist of scenes (tonele). Stanzas and lines belong to poetry, chapters to a novel."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wanneer 'n karakter alleen op die verhoog sy gedagtes hardop uitspreek, is dit 'n ...","en":"When a character, alone on stage, speaks his thoughts aloud, it is a ..."},"options":[{"af":"dialoog","en":"dialogue (dialoog)"},{"af":"rolverdeling","en":"cast list (rolverdeling)"},{"af":"alleenspraak","en":"soliloquy (alleenspraak)"},{"af":"neweteks","en":"side text (neweteks)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In 'n alleenspraak is die karakter alleen en hoor net die gehoor sy gedagtes. 'n Dialoog het twee of meer sprekers.","en":"In a soliloquy the character is alone and only the audience hears his thoughts. A dialogue has two or more speakers."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die lys van karakters aan die begin van 'n drama is die ___.","en":"The list of characters at the start of a drama is the ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["rolverdeling","karakterlys"],"en":["rolverdeling","karakterlys","cast list"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["neweteks","eksposisie","toneel"],"en":["neweteks","eksposisie","toneel"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die rolverdeling (karakterlys) noem die karakters en soms hul ouderdom of verhouding tot mekaar.","en":"The cast list (rolverdeling) names the characters and sometimes their age or relationship to one another."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is dramatiese ironie?","en":"What is dramatic irony?"},"options":[{"af":"Wanneer die gehoor meer weet as die karakter","en":"When the audience knows more than the character"},{"af":"Wanneer 'n karakter die teenoorgestelde sê van wat hy bedoel","en":"When a character says the opposite of what he means"},{"af":"Wanneer die drama 'n gelukkige einde het","en":"When the drama has a happy ending"},{"af":"Wanneer twee karakters met mekaar stry","en":"When two characters argue with each other"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"By dramatiese ironie weet die gehoor iets wat die karakter nie weet nie. As 'n karakter die teenoorgestelde sê van wat hy bedoel, is dit verbale ironie.","en":"With dramatic irony the audience knows something the character does not know. When a character says the opposite of what he means, it is verbal irony."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die klimaks is die laaste deel van 'n drama, waarin al die los drade vasgeknoop word.","en":"The climax is the last part of a drama, in which all the loose ends are tied up."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die klimaks is die hoogtepunt en keerpunt van die konflik. Die ontknoping is die laaste deel waarin die los drade vasgeknoop word.","en":"False. The climax is the high point and turning point of the conflict. The resolution (ontknoping) is the last part in which the loose ends are tied up."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke fase van Freytag se piramide by die beskrywing.","en":"Match each stage of Freytag's pyramid to its description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Eksposisie","en":"Exposition"},"r":{"af":"Die karakters, ruimte en agtergrond word bekendgestel","en":"The characters, setting and background are introduced"}},{"l":{"af":"Komplikasie","en":"Complication"},"r":{"af":"Die konflik begin en die spanning bou op","en":"The conflict starts and the tension builds"}},{"l":{"af":"Klimaks","en":"Climax"},"r":{"af":"Die hoogtepunt en keerpunt van die konflik","en":"The high point and turning point of the conflict"}},{"l":{"af":"Afwikkeling","en":"Falling action"},"r":{"af":"Die gebeure ná die hoogtepunt; die spanning neem af","en":"The events after the high point; the tension decreases"}},{"l":{"af":"Ontknoping","en":"Resolution"},"r":{"af":"Die finale uitkoms van die drama","en":"The final outcome of the drama"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die spanning styg tot by die klimaks en daal daarna, soos die twee kante van 'n piramide.","en":"The tension rises up to the climax and falls afterwards, like the two sides of a pyramid."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Zander het sy pa se visstok gebreek en weggesteek. Sy pa vra hom om dit te gaan haal. ZANDER: *(spring op, te vinnig)* Nee! Ek bedoel ... Pa, dis donker. Wat wys die neweteks oor Zander?","en":"Zander has broken and hidden his father's fishing rod. His father asks him to fetch it. ZANDER: *(spring op, te vinnig)* Nee! Ek bedoel ... Pa, dis donker. What does the side text show about Zander?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is moeg en wil gaan slaap.","en":"He is tired and wants to go to sleep."},{"af":"Hy is opgewonde om te gaan visvang.","en":"He is excited to go fishing."},{"af":"Hy is kwaad vir sy pa.","en":"He is angry with his father."},{"af":"Hy is paniekerig en skuldig omdat hy iets wegsteek.","en":"He is panicky and guilty because he is hiding something."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Te vinnig* wys dat sy reaksie oordrewe is: hy skrik omdat sy pa die gebreekte stok sal ontdek. Die *Nee!* en die beletselteken bevestig sy paniek.","en":"*Te vinnig* (too quickly) shows that his reaction is exaggerated: he is alarmed because his father will discover the broken rod. The *Nee!* and the ellipsis confirm his panic."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Boer wat teen 'n droogte veg, beleef ___ konflik.","en":"A farmer fighting against a drought experiences ___ conflict (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["uiterlike","uiterlik"],"en":["uiterlike","uiterlik","external"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["innerlike","dramatiese","verbale"],"en":["innerlike","dramatiese","verbale"]}},"explain":{"af":"Karakter teen die natuur is uiterlike konflik. Innerlike konflik speel binne die karakter se gedagtes en gevoelens af.","en":"Character against nature is external (uiterlike) conflict. Internal conflict takes place inside the character's thoughts and feelings."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"LIZE: *(gaap, kyk op haar horlosie)* Nog 'n wonderlike, opwindende wiskundeles. Wat is Lize se toon?","en":"LIZE: *(gaap, kyk op haar horlosie)* Nog 'n wonderlike, opwindende wiskundeles. (Another wonderful, exciting maths lesson.) What is Lize's tone?"},"options":[{"af":"Sarkasties","en":"Sarcastic"},{"af":"Opgewonde","en":"Excited"},{"af":"Bang","en":"Afraid"},{"af":"Nostalgies","en":"Nostalgic"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die neweteks (sy gaap en kyk op haar horlosie) wys sy verveel haar, dus bedoel sy die teenoorgestelde van *wonderlik* en *opwindend*: sy is sarkasties.","en":"The side text (she yawns and looks at her watch) shows she is bored, so she means the opposite of *wonderlik* and *opwindend*: she is sarcastic."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Karakter wat in die loop van die drama verander en iets leer, is 'n ___ karakter.","en":"A character who changes and learns something during the drama is a ___ character (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["dinamiese","dinamies"],"en":["dinamiese","dinamies","dynamic"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["statiese","plat","ironiese"],"en":["statiese","plat","ironiese"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Dinamiese karakter ontwikkel; 'n statiese karakter bly dieselfde. *Plat* beskryf 'n karakter met net een kant.","en":"A dynamic (dinamiese) character develops; a static character stays the same. *Plat* (flat) describes a character with only one side."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die gehoor weet dat 'n inbreker agter die gordyn wegkruip. MAMA stap die donker kamer binne. Watter toneelaanwysing sal die spanning die meeste verhoog?","en":"The audience knows that a burglar is hiding behind the curtain. MAMA walks into the dark room. Which stage direction will increase the tension most?"},"options":[{"af":"*(Die gordyn sak en die toneel eindig.)*","en":"*(Die gordyn sak en die toneel eindig.)* (The curtain falls and the scene ends.)"},{"af":"*(Die inbreker stap uit en stel homself voor.)*","en":"*(Die inbreker stap uit en stel homself voor.)* (The burglar walks out and introduces himself.)"},{"af":"*(Die gordyn beweeg effens. Stilte. Net 'n horlosie tik.)*","en":"*(Die gordyn beweeg effens. Stilte. Net 'n horlosie tik.)* (The curtain moves slightly. Silence. Only a clock ticks.)"},{"af":"*(Die akteurs buig en groet die gehoor.)*","en":"*(Die akteurs buig en groet die gehoor.)* (The actors bow and greet the audience.)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die beweging van die gordyn, die stilte en die tik van die horlosie laat die gehoor wag en vrees, omdat hulle weet wat Mama nie weet nie. Die ander aanwysings beëindig of ontlont die spanning.","en":"The movement of the curtain, the silence and the ticking clock make the audience wait and fear, because they know what Mama does not know. The other directions end or defuse the tension."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste beskrywing van die verskil tussen 'n komedie en 'n tragedie?","en":"What is the best description of the difference between a comedy and a tragedy?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Komedie het geen konflik nie; 'n tragedie het baie konflik.","en":"A comedy has no conflict; a tragedy has a lot of conflict."},{"af":"'n Komedie het net een bedryf; 'n tragedie het altyd vyf.","en":"A comedy has only one act; a tragedy always has five."},{"af":"'n Komedie het geen neweteks nie; 'n tragedie het baie toneelaanwysings.","en":"A comedy has no side text; a tragedy has many stage directions."},{"af":"'n Komedie gebruik humor en eindig gewoonlik gelukkig; 'n tragedie is ernstig en eindig in verlies of ondergang.","en":"A comedy uses humour and usually ends happily; a tragedy is serious and ends in loss or downfall."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Albei soorte drama het konflik en toneelaanwysings, en die aantal bedrywe verskil van drama tot drama. Die verskil lê in die toon en die einde.","en":"Both kinds of drama have conflict and stage directions, and the number of acts differs from drama to drama. The difference lies in the tone and the ending."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"KARLA: *(glimlag breed, druk Suné styf vas)* Baie geluk met jou nuwe kêrel! Ek is so bly vir jou. *(Suné stap uit. Karla se glimlag verdwyn. Sy skeur 'n foto van Suné stukkend.)* Watter evaluering van Karla is die beste?","en":"KARLA: *(glimlag breed, druk Suné styf vas)* Baie geluk met jou nuwe kêrel! Ek is so bly vir jou. (Congratulations on your new boyfriend! I'm so happy for you.) *(Suné stap uit. Karla se glimlag verdwyn. Sy skeur 'n foto van Suné stukkend.)* Which evaluation of Karla is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Sy is 'n lojale vriendin, want sy sê sy is bly.","en":"She is a loyal friend, because she says she is glad."},{"af":"Sy is jaloers en vals: die hoofteks sê een ding, maar haar optrede in die neweteks wys die teenoorgestelde.","en":"She is jealous and false: the main text says one thing, but her actions in the side text show the opposite."},{"af":"Sy is 'n plat karakter omdat sy min praat.","en":"She is a flat character because she says little."},{"af":"Sy is die protagonis omdat sy eerste praat.","en":"She is the protagonist because she speaks first."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In drama wys die neweteks dikwels die waarheid agter die woorde. Karla se verdwynende glimlag en die stukkende foto bewys dat haar gelukwensing vals is.","en":"In drama the side text often shows the truth behind the words. Karla's disappearing smile and the torn photo prove that her congratulations are false."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t3-transaksionele-tekste","title":{"af":"Transaksionele skryfwerk 2: toespraak, dialoog, verslag, koerantberig, resensie en korter tekste","en":"Transactional writing 2: speech, dialogue, report, newspaper report, review and shorter texts"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die formaat en kenmerke van toesprake, dialoë, verslae, koerantberigte, resensies en korter tekste ken en elkeen in die regte register vir jou teikengroep kan skryf.","en":"You will know the format and features of speeches, dialogues, reports, newspaper reports, reviews and shorter texts, and be able to write each one in the right register for your audience."},"summary":{"af":"## Wat is 'n transaksionele teks?\n\n'n **Transaksionele teks** is 'n praktiese teks wat vir 'n bepaalde **teikengroep** (leser of gehoor) en met 'n duidelike **doel** geskryf word: om in te lig, te oorreed, te bedank, uit te nooi of te evalueer. In **Vraestel 3** skryf jy transaksionele tekste van **180–200 woorde** elk.\n\n| Rubriek (25 punte) | Punte |\n|---|---|\n| Inhoud, beplanning en formaat | 15 |\n| Taal, styl en redigering | 10 |\n\n> **Onthou!** Formaat tel deel van die 15 punte. 'n Goeie teks in die verkeerde formaat verloor maklik punte.\n\n### Stappe vir elke opdrag\n1. Onderstreep in die opdrag die **teksoort**, **teikengroep**, **doel** en **register**.\n2. Beplan met kernwoorde of 'n breinkaart.\n3. Skryf 'n konsep in die regte formaat.\n4. Redigeer (spelling, leestekens, register, woordtelling) en skryf die finale weergawe.\n\n## Register en toon\n- **Formeel:** *u*, *Meneer/Mevrou*, volsinne, geen sleng of sametrekkings (*dis*, *jy's*) nie, saaklik. Vir die skoolhoof, die pers of 'n amptelike verslag.\n- **Informeel:** *jy/julle*, gemaklik maar steeds korrekte taal. Vir vriende, 'n dagboek of 'n gesprek tussen tieners.\n- Die **toon** pas by die doel: entoesiasties, ernstig, simpatiek of humoristies.\n\n## Formaat en kenmerke\n\n### Toespraak\n- Begin met 'n **aanspreekvorm**: *Meneer die Voorsitter, geagte gaste, mede-leerders* (by 'n saalbyeenkoms: *Meneer die Hoof*).\n- 'n **Pakkende opening**: 'n retoriese vraag, 'n kort anekdote of 'n treffende stelling.\n- Praat **direk** met die gehoor (*julle/u*); gebruik retoriese vrae en herhaling.\n- **Slot:** som op, gee 'n oproep tot aksie en **bedank** die gehoor: *Baie dankie vir julle aandag.*\n\n### Dialoog\n- Die spreker se **naam staan links**, gevolg deur 'n **dubbelpunt**: *Thabo: Is jy gereed?*\n- **Toneelaanwysings** staan tussen **hakies**: *(kyk op sy horlosie)*.\n- **Geen aanhalingstekens** nie; elke spreker begin op 'n nuwe reël.\n- Die register pas by die karakters en klink natuurlik.\n\n### Onderhoud\nSoos 'n dialoog, maar tussen 'n **onderhoudvoerder** en 'n gas (*Onderhoudvoerder:* / *Me. Mokoena:*). Gebruik oop vrae (*Hoe het u begin ...?*) en 'n beleefde register.\n\n### Verslag\n- **Formeel:** titel, doel, metode, bevindinge, aanbevelings, naam en datum. Gebruik **subopskrifte**, saaklike taal en geen gevoelens nie.\n- **Informeel** (bv. oor 'n skooluitstappie vir die skoolkoerant): vertel in **chronologiese volgorde** wat gebeur het, met minder vaste opskrifte.\n\n### Koerantberig\n- **Opskrif:** kort en pakkend: *Veldbrand bedreig plase naby Brits*.\n- **Byreël** (byline): *Deur Lerato Mokoena*.\n- **Plek en datum**, bv. *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026*.\n- Die **eerste paragraaf** beantwoord **wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en hoe**.\n- **Derde persoon**, **verlede tyd**, objektief (feite, nie jou mening nie), met **aanhalings** van ooggetuies tussen aanhalingstekens. Kort paragrawe.\n\n### Resensie\nVan 'n film, boek of restaurant:\n- **Besonderhede:** titel, regisseur of skrywer, akteurs, genre (of die restaurant se naam, ligging en pryse).\n- 'n **Kort opsomming** van die storie, **sonder om die einde te verklap**.\n- **Evaluering:** sterk en swak punte, met redes.\n- **Aanbeveling** en 'n **gradering**, bv. ★★★★☆.\n\n### Ander langer tekste\n- **Huldeblyk:** eer iemand (bv. 'n onderwyser wat aftree of iemand wat oorlede is); eienskappe, prestasies en 'n anekdote in 'n respekvolle toon.\n- **Rubriek/tydskrifartikel:** opskrif, skrywer se naam, 'n persoonlike stem en mening; praat die leser direk aan.\n- **Dagboekinskrywing:** **datum** bo-aan, **eerste persoon** (*ek*), gevoelens en gedagtes, informele register.\n\n## Korter tekste\n- **Advertensie:** aandagtrekker, produk of diens, voordele, prys, kontakbesonderhede, oorredende taal.\n- **Uitnodiging:** wie nooi, wat (die geleentheid), waar, wanneer (datum **én** tyd), kleredrag en **RSVP** (antwoord asseblief) met 'n datum.\n- **Strooibiljet/plakkaat:** groot opskrif, min woorde, kolpunte en net die kernfeite.\n- **Aanwysings/instruksies:** die **gebiedende wys** (*Draai links by die robot.*), genommerde stappe, **landmerke** en afstande.\n- **E-pos:** *Aan*, *Onderwerp*, aanhef, kort liggaam, afsluiting en naam.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** aanhalingstekens in 'n dialoog; *ek* en eie menings in 'n koerantberig; 'n resensie wat die einde verklap; 'n uitnodiging sonder tyd of RSVP; sleng in 'n formele teks.\n\n> **Wenk:** Die eksamen vra ook korter vrae: herken die formaatfout, pas die teksoort by sy doel, of herskryf 'n sin in die regte register.","en":"## What is a transactional text?\n\nA **transactional text** is a functional text written for a specific **target audience** (reader or listeners) with a clear **purpose**: to inform, persuade, thank, invite or evaluate. In **Paper 3** you write transactional texts of **180–200 words** each.\n\n| Rubric (25 marks) | Marks |\n|---|---|\n| Content, planning and format | 15 |\n| Language, style and editing | 10 |\n\n> **Remember!** Format counts towards the 15 marks. A good text in the wrong format easily loses marks.\n\n### Steps for every task\n1. Underline the **text type**, **audience**, **purpose** and **register** in the instruction.\n2. Plan with key words or a mind map.\n3. Write a draft in the correct format.\n4. Edit (spelling, punctuation, register, word count) and write the final version.\n\n## Register and tone\n- **Formal:** *u*, *Meneer/Mevrou*, full sentences, no slang or contractions (*dis*, *jy's*), businesslike. For the principal, the press or an official report.\n- **Informal:** *jy/julle*, relaxed but still correct language. For friends, a diary or a conversation between teenagers.\n- The **tone** suits the purpose: enthusiastic, serious, sympathetic or humorous.\n\n## Format and features\n\n### Speech (toespraak)\n- Start with a **form of address** (*aanspreekvorm*): *Meneer die Voorsitter, geagte gaste, mede-leerders* (at assembly: *Meneer die Hoof*).\n- A **catchy opening**: a rhetorical question, a short anecdote or a striking statement.\n- Speak **directly** to the audience (*julle/u*); use rhetorical questions and repetition.\n- **Ending:** sum up, give a call to action and **thank** the audience: *Baie dankie vir julle aandag.*\n\n### Dialogue (dialoog)\n- The speaker's **name is on the left**, followed by a **colon**: *Thabo: Is jy gereed?*\n- **Stage directions** go in **brackets**: *(kyk op sy horlosie)*.\n- **No quotation marks**; each speaker starts on a new line.\n- The register suits the characters and sounds natural.\n\n### Interview (onderhoud)\nLike a dialogue, but between an **interviewer** (*onderhoudvoerder*) and a guest (*Onderhoudvoerder:* / *Me. Mokoena:*). Use open questions (*Hoe het u begin ...?*) and a polite register.\n\n### Report (verslag)\n- **Formal:** title, purpose, method, findings, recommendations, name and date. Use **subheadings**, businesslike language and no feelings.\n- **Informal** (e.g. about a school outing for the school newspaper): tell what happened in **chronological order**, with fewer fixed headings.\n\n### Newspaper report (koerantberig)\n- **Headline:** short and catchy: *Veldbrand bedreig plase naby Brits*.\n- **Byline** (*byreël*): *Deur Lerato Mokoena*.\n- **Place and date**, e.g. *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026*.\n- The **first paragraph** answers **who, what, where, when, why and how**.\n- **Third person**, **past tense**, objective (facts, not your opinion), with **quotes** from eyewitnesses in quotation marks. Short paragraphs.\n\n### Review (resensie)\nOf a film, book or restaurant:\n- **Details:** title, director or author, actors, genre (or the restaurant's name, location and prices).\n- A **short summary** of the story, **without giving away the ending**.\n- **Evaluation:** strong and weak points, with reasons.\n- **Recommendation** and a **rating**, e.g. ★★★★☆.\n\n### Other longer texts\n- **Tribute (huldeblyk):** honours someone (e.g. a retiring teacher or someone who has died); qualities, achievements and an anecdote in a respectful tone.\n- **Column/magazine article (rubriek):** headline, writer's name, a personal voice and opinion; speaks to the reader directly.\n- **Diary entry (dagboekinskrywing):** **date** at the top, **first person** (*ek*), feelings and thoughts, informal register.\n\n## Shorter texts\n- **Advertisement:** attention-grabber, product or service, benefits, price, contact details, persuasive language.\n- **Invitation (uitnodiging):** who is inviting, what (the event), where, when (date **and** time), dress code and **RSVP** (please reply) with a date.\n- **Flyer/poster (strooibiljet/plakkaat):** big heading, few words, bullet points and only the key facts.\n- **Directions/instructions (aanwysings/instruksies):** the **imperative** (*gebiedende wys*: *Draai links by die robot.*), numbered steps, **landmarks** and distances.\n- **E-mail:** *Aan* (To), *Onderwerp* (Subject), greeting, short body, closing and name.\n\n> **Common mistakes:** quotation marks in a dialogue; *ek* and own opinions in a newspaper report; a review that gives away the ending; an invitation without a time or RSVP; slang in a formal text.\n\n> **Tip:** The exam also asks shorter questions: spot the format error, match the text type to its purpose, or rewrite a sentence in the correct register."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Transaksionele teks","en":"Transactional text"},"def":{"af":"'n Praktiese teks met 'n bepaalde doel en teikengroep, bv. 'n toespraak, verslag of uitnodiging.","en":"A functional text with a specific purpose and audience, e.g. a speech, report or invitation."}},{"term":{"af":"Register","en":"Register"},"def":{"af":"Die vlak van formaliteit van die taal (formeel of informeel), gekies volgens die teikengroep en situasie.","en":"The level of formality of the language (formal or informal), chosen according to the audience and situation."}},{"term":{"af":"Teikengroep","en":"Target audience"},"def":{"af":"Die lesers of luisteraars vir wie die teks bedoel is.","en":"The readers or listeners the text is meant for."}},{"term":{"af":"Retoriese vraag","en":"Rhetorical question"},"def":{"af":"'n Vraag waarop jy nie 'n antwoord verwag nie; dit laat die gehoor dink en hou hulle aandag.","en":"A question that does not expect an answer; it makes the audience think and holds their attention."}},{"term":{"af":"Toneelaanwysings","en":"Stage directions"},"def":{"af":"Aanwysings tussen hakies in 'n dialoog wat wys hoe 'n karakter iets sê of wat hy doen.","en":"Directions in brackets in a dialogue that show how a character says something or what he does."}},{"term":{"af":"Byreël","en":"Byline"},"def":{"af":"Die naam van die joernalis wat die koerantberig geskryf het, onder die opskrif.","en":"The name of the journalist who wrote the newspaper report, under the headline."}},{"term":{"af":"Inleidende paragraaf (5 W's en H)","en":"Lead paragraph (5 Ws and H)"},"def":{"af":"Die eerste paragraaf van 'n koerantberig wat sê wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en hoe.","en":"The first paragraph of a newspaper report, which says who, what, where, when, why and how."}},{"term":{"af":"Resensie","en":"Review"},"def":{"af":"'n Teks wat 'n film, boek of restaurant beskryf, evalueer en aanbeveel of nie.","en":"A text that describes and evaluates a film, book or restaurant and recommends it or not."}},{"term":{"af":"RSVP","en":"RSVP"},"def":{"af":"Afkorting uit Frans (*répondez s'il vous plaît*): antwoord asseblief of jy die geleentheid gaan bywoon.","en":"Abbreviation from French (*répondez s'il vous plaît*): please reply whether you will attend the event."}},{"term":{"af":"Gebiedende wys","en":"Imperative"},"def":{"af":"Die bevelsvorm van die werkwoord (*Draai links.*), wat in aanwysings en instruksies gebruik word.","en":"The command form of the verb (*Draai links.*), used in directions and instructions."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Die begin van 'n koerantberig","en":"The opening of a newspaper report"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die opskrif, byreël, plek en datum en die inleidende paragraaf van 'n koerantberig vir die skoolkoerant. Feite: 120 leerders van 'n skool in Brits; skoonmaakaksie; 300 sakke rommel opgetel; oewer van Hartbeespoortdam; Saterdag 10 Oktober 2026; om aandag op plastiekbesoedeling te vestig; in groepe, met handskoene en sakke wat 'n plaaslike winkel geskenk het.","en":"Write the headline, byline, place and date and the lead paragraph of a newspaper report for the school newspaper. Facts: 120 learners from a school in Brits; clean-up campaign; 300 bags of litter picked up; banks of Hartbeespoort Dam; Saturday 10 October 2026; to draw attention to plastic pollution; in groups, with gloves and bags donated by a local shop."},"steps":[{"af":"Opskrif: kort en pakkend, in die derde persoon: *Leerders tel 300 sakke rommel by Hartbeespoortdam op*.","en":"Headline: short and catchy, in the third person: *Leerders tel 300 sakke rommel by Hartbeespoortdam op* (Learners pick up 300 bags of litter at Hartbeespoort Dam)."},{"af":"Byreël en plek/datum: *Deur Anja Venter* en *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026* (die berig verskyn ná die gebeurtenis).","en":"Byline and place/date: *Deur Anja Venter* and *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026* (the report appears after the event)."},{"af":"Sorteer die feite volgens die 5 W's en H: wie (120 leerders), wat (300 sakke rommel opgetel), waar (oewer van Hartbeespoortdam), wanneer (Saterdag), hoekom (plastiekbesoedeling), hoe (in groepe, met geskenkte handskoene en sakke).","en":"Sort the facts by the 5 Ws and H: who (120 learners), what (300 bags of litter picked up), where (banks of Hartbeespoort Dam), when (Saturday), why (plastic pollution), how (in groups, with donated gloves and bags)."},{"af":"Skryf die inleidende paragraaf in die verlede tyd, sonder eie mening: *Altesaam 120 leerders van 'n skool in Brits het Saterdag 300 sakke rommel langs die oewer van Hartbeespoortdam opgetel. Hulle het in groepe gewerk, met handskoene en sakke wat 'n plaaslike winkel geskenk het, om aandag op plastiekbesoedeling te vestig.*","en":"Write the lead paragraph in the past tense, without your own opinion: *Altesaam 120 leerders van 'n skool in Brits het Saterdag 300 sakke rommel langs die oewer van Hartbeespoortdam opgetel. Hulle het in groepe gewerk, met handskoene en sakke wat 'n plaaslike winkel geskenk het, om aandag op plastiekbesoedeling te vestig.*"},{"af":"Kontroleer: al ses vrae is beantwoord, dit is derde persoon en verlede tyd, en daar is geen *ek* of *ongelooflik* nie.","en":"Check: all six questions are answered, it is third person and past tense, and there is no *ek* (I) or *ongelooflik* (unbelievable)."}],"answer":{"af":"Opskrif + *Deur Anja Venter* + *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026* + 'n inleidende paragraaf wat wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en hoe objektief in die verlede tyd beantwoord.","en":"Headline + *Deur Anja Venter* + *Brits, 12 Oktober 2026* + a lead paragraph that answers who, what, where, when, why and how objectively in the past tense."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter die formaat van 'n dialoog","en":"Correct the format of a dialogue"},"problem":{"af":"'n Leerder het hierdie dialoog geskryf. Identifiseer en verbeter die drie formaatfoute.\n\n\"Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?\" vra Thabo.\nSipho: Net as jy die padkos dra! Hy glimlag breed.\nJaco – En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?","en":"A learner wrote this dialogue. Identify and correct the three format errors.\n\n\"Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?\" vra Thabo.\nSipho: Net as jy die padkos dra! Hy glimlag breed.\nJaco – En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?"},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: reël 1 is soos direkte rede in 'n storie geskryf (aanhalingstekens en *vra Thabo*). In 'n dialoog: *Thabo: Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?*","en":"Error 1: line 1 is written like direct speech in a story (quotation marks and *vra Thabo*). In a dialogue: *Thabo: Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?*"},{"af":"Fout 2: *Hy glimlag breed* is 'n toneelaanwysing en moet tussen hakies staan, voor die woorde wat hy sê: *Sipho: (glimlag breed) Net as jy die padkos dra!*","en":"Error 2: *Hy glimlag breed* (he smiles broadly) is a stage direction and must be in brackets, before the words he says: *Sipho: (glimlag breed) Net as jy die padkos dra!*"},{"af":"Fout 3: *Jaco –* gebruik 'n aandagstreep. Ná die naam kom 'n dubbelpunt: *Jaco: En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?*","en":"Error 3: *Jaco –* uses a dash. After the name comes a colon: *Jaco: En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?*"}],"answer":{"af":"Thabo: Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?\nSipho: (glimlag breed) Net as jy die padkos dra!\nJaco: En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?","en":"Thabo: Wil jy Saterdag saam Magaliesberg toe gaan stap?\nSipho: (glimlag breed) Net as jy die padkos dra!\nJaco: En ek? Mag ek ook saamkom?"}},{"title":{"af":"Die opening en slot van 'n toespraak","en":"The opening and ending of a speech"},"problem":{"af":"Jy is 'n lid van die VRL en moet by die saalbyeenkoms 'n toespraak lewer om leerders aan te moedig om aan die skool se herwinningsprojek deel te neem. Skryf die opening en die slot.","en":"You are a member of the RCL (VRL) and must give a speech at assembly to encourage learners to take part in the school's recycling project. Write the opening and the ending."},"steps":[{"af":"Bepaal die teikengroep en register: die hoof, personeel en leerders, dus formeel maar lewendig.","en":"Decide on the audience and register: the principal, staff and learners, so formal but lively."},{"af":"Aanspreekvorm: *Meneer die Hoof, geagte personeel, mede-leerders.*","en":"Form of address: *Meneer die Hoof, geagte personeel, mede-leerders.*"},{"af":"Pakkende opening met 'n retoriese vraag: *Kyk vanoggend om jou: hoeveel blikkies en plastiekbottels lê op ons skoolterrein?*","en":"Catchy opening with a rhetorical question: *Kyk vanoggend om jou: hoeveel blikkies en plastiekbottels lê op ons skoolterrein?* (Look around you this morning: how many cans and plastic bottles are lying on our school grounds?)"},{"af":"Slot met 'n oproep tot aksie en 'n bedanking: *Kom ons begin vandag: gooi jou blikkie in die groen houer. Baie dankie vir julle aandag.*","en":"Ending with a call to action and thanks: *Kom ons begin vandag: gooi jou blikkie in die groen houer. Baie dankie vir julle aandag.* (Let's start today: throw your can in the green bin. Thank you for your attention.)"}],"answer":{"af":"Opening: aanspreekvorm + retoriese vraag. Slot: oproep tot aksie + *Baie dankie vir julle aandag.*","en":"Opening: form of address + rhetorical question. Ending: call to action + *Baie dankie vir julle aandag.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Wat ontbreek in die uitnodiging?","en":"What is missing from the invitation?"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die uitnodiging en sê watter twee belangrike besonderhede ontbreek. Voeg dit dan by.\n\n*Kom vier saam met Lerato – sy word 16!*\n*Waar: Magnoliastraat 14, Brits*\n*Datum: Saterdag 7 November 2026*\n*Kleredrag: gemaklik (bring jou swemklere)*","en":"Read the invitation and say which two important details are missing. Then add them.\n\n*Kom vier saam met Lerato – sy word 16!*\n*Waar: Magnoliastraat 14, Brits*\n*Datum: Saterdag 7 November 2026*\n*Kleredrag: gemaklik (bring jou swemklere)*"},"steps":[{"af":"Kontroleer die lys vir 'n uitnodiging: wie nooi, wat, waar, wanneer (datum én tyd), kleredrag, RSVP.","en":"Check the list for an invitation: who is inviting, what, where, when (date and time), dress code, RSVP."},{"af":"Wie (Lerato), wat (16de verjaarsdag), waar (adres), datum en kleredrag is daar. Die **tyd** en die **RSVP** ontbreek.","en":"Who (Lerato), what (16th birthday), where (address), date and dress code are there. The **time** and the **RSVP** are missing."},{"af":"Voeg by: *Tyd: 12:00 tot 17:00* en *RSVP: WhatsApp vir Lerato voor 31 Oktober.*","en":"Add: *Tyd: 12:00 tot 17:00* and *RSVP: WhatsApp vir Lerato voor 31 Oktober.* (RSVP: WhatsApp Lerato before 31 October.)"}],"answer":{"af":"Die tyd en die RSVP ontbreek: *Tyd: 12:00 tot 17:00*; *RSVP: WhatsApp vir Lerato voor 31 Oktober.*","en":"The time and the RSVP are missing: *Tyd: 12:00 tot 17:00*; *RSVP: WhatsApp vir Lerato voor 31 Oktober.*"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe dui jy in 'n dialoog aan wie praat?","en":"How do you show who is speaking in a dialogue?"},"options":[{"af":"Die spreker se woorde staan tussen aanhalingstekens.","en":"The speaker's words are in quotation marks."},{"af":"Die spreker se naam staan links, gevolg deur 'n dubbelpunt.","en":"The speaker's name is on the left, followed by a colon."},{"af":"Die spreker se naam staan tussen hakies ná sy woorde.","en":"The speaker's name is in brackets after his words."},{"af":"Elke spreker se woorde word in 'n aparte paragraaf vertel.","en":"Each speaker's words are narrated in a separate paragraph."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"In 'n dialoog staan die naam links met 'n dubbelpunt (*Thabo: ...*). Aanhalingstekens hoort by direkte rede in 'n storie, nie in 'n dialoog nie.","en":"In a dialogue the name is on the left with a colon (*Thabo: ...*). Quotation marks belong to direct speech in a story, not in a dialogue."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die inleidende paragraaf van 'n koerantberig beantwoord die vrae wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en ___.","en":"The lead paragraph of a newspaper report answers the questions who, what, where, when, why and ___ (Afrikaans word)."},"answers":{"af":["hoe"],"en":["hoe","how"]},"explain":{"af":"Die 5 W's en H: wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en **hoe**. Die leser moet die kern van die nuus reeds in die eerste paragraaf kry.","en":"The 5 Ws and H: who, what, where, when, why and **how** (*hoe*). The reader must get the core of the news in the first paragraph."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hoeveel","hoe lank","waarheen"],"en":["hoeveel","hoe lank","waarheen"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Koerantberig word in die eerste persoon (*ek*) en met die joernalis se eie mening geskryf.","en":"A newspaper report is written in the first person (*ek*) and includes the journalist's own opinion."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Koerantberig is objektief: derde persoon, verlede tyd en feite. Menings verskyn net in aanhalings van ooggetuies of kenners.","en":"False. A newspaper report is objective: third person, past tense and facts. Opinions appear only in quotes from eyewitnesses or experts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Onderaan 'n uitnodiging skryf jy ___ (Frans vir 'antwoord asseblief') met 'n datum waarteen gaste moet laat weet of hulle kom.","en":"At the bottom of an invitation you write ___ (French for 'please reply') with a date by which guests must say whether they are coming."},"answers":{"af":["RSVP","R.S.V.P."],"en":["RSVP","R.S.V.P."]},"explain":{"af":"RSVP staan vir *répondez s'il vous plaît*: antwoord asseblief. NS is 'n naskrif onderaan 'n brief, en BTW is belasting.","en":"RSVP stands for *répondez s'il vous plaît*: please reply. NS (naskrif) is a postscript at the end of a letter, and BTW is VAT."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["NS","BTW","d.w.s."],"en":["NS","BTW","d.w.s."]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die naam van die joernalis onder die opskrif van 'n koerantberig (bv. *Deur Lerato Mokoena*) word die ___ genoem.","en":"The journalist's name under the headline of a newspaper report (e.g. *Deur Lerato Mokoena*) is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["byreël","byreel","byline"],"en":["byline","byreël","byreel"]},"explain":{"af":"Die byreël sê wie die berig geskryf het. Die opskrif is die titel bo-aan; 'n onderskrif staan onder 'n foto; 'n aanhef hoort in 'n brief.","en":"The byline (*byreël*) says who wrote the report. The headline is the title at the top; a caption is under a photo; a salutation belongs in a letter."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["onderskrif","opskrif","aanhef"],"en":["caption","headline","salutation"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n dialoog skryf jy toneelaanwysings tussen hakies, bv. *(kyk op sy horlosie)*.","en":"In a dialogue you write stage directions in brackets, e.g. *(kyk op sy horlosie)*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Toneelaanwysings wys hoe 'n karakter praat of wat hy doen. Die hakies skei dit van die woorde wat gesê word.","en":"True. Stage directions show how a character speaks or what he does. The brackets separate them from the words that are spoken."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die beste opskrif vir 'n koerantberig?","en":"Which one is the best headline for a newspaper report?"},"options":[{"af":"Ek het gister 'n groot brand naby Brits gesien","en":"Ek het gister 'n groot brand naby Brits gesien (I saw a big fire near Brits yesterday)"},{"af":"Was dit nie 'n verskriklike dag vir die boere nie?","en":"Was dit nie 'n verskriklike dag vir die boere nie? (Wasn't it a terrible day for the farmers?)"},{"af":"Veldbrand verwoes plaas naby Brits","en":"Veldbrand verwoes plaas naby Brits (Veld fire destroys farm near Brits)"},{"af":"'n Berig oor die brand wat Maandagmiddag op 'n plaas naby Brits uitgebreek en baie skade aangerig het","en":"'n Berig oor die brand wat Maandagmiddag op 'n plaas naby Brits uitgebreek en baie skade aangerig het (a report about the fire that broke out ... and caused a lot of damage)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Opskrif is kort, pakkend en saaklik, in die derde persoon. Die eerste opsie is in die eerste persoon, die tweede is 'n retoriese vraag en die laaste is veel te lank.","en":"A headline is short, catchy and factual, in the third person. The first option is in the first person, the second is a rhetorical question and the last is far too long."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy NIE in 'n resensie van 'n film doen nie?","en":"What must you NOT do in a film review?"},"options":[{"af":"Gee die titel, die regisseur en die hoofakteurs.","en":"Give the title, the director and the main actors."},{"af":"Evalueer die sterk en swak punte met redes.","en":"Evaluate the strong and weak points with reasons."},{"af":"Gee 'n sterre-gradering en 'n aanbeveling.","en":"Give a star rating and a recommendation."},{"af":"Vertel presies hoe die storie eindig.","en":"Tell exactly how the story ends."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Resensie gee 'n kort opsomming, maar verklap nie die einde nie; anders bederf jy die film vir die leser. Die ander drie is alles vereistes van 'n resensie.","en":"A review gives a short summary but does not give away the ending; otherwise you spoil the film for the reader. The other three are all requirements of a review."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter afdeling van 'n formele verslag stel jy voor hoe die probleem opgelos kan word?","en":"In which section of a formal report do you suggest how the problem can be solved?"},"options":[{"af":"Aanbevelings","en":"Recommendations (Aanbevelings)"},{"af":"Bevindinge","en":"Findings (Bevindinge)"},{"af":"Metode","en":"Method (Metode)"},{"af":"Doel","en":"Purpose (Doel)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Aanbevelings sê wat gedoen moet word. Bevindinge sê wat jy uitgevind het, die metode beskryf hoe jy die inligting ingesamel het, en die doel sê waarom die verslag geskryf is.","en":"Recommendations say what should be done. Findings say what you found out, the method describes how you gathered the information, and the purpose says why the report was written."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Aanwysings en instruksies gebruik die ___ wys van die werkwoord, bv. *Draai links by die robot.*","en":"Directions and instructions use the ___ mood of the verb (Afrikaans term), e.g. *Draai links by die robot.*"},"answers":{"af":["gebiedende"],"en":["gebiedende","imperative"]},"explain":{"af":"Die gebiedende wys is die bevelsvorm: die werkwoord staan voor (*Draai*, *Ry*, *Stop*). Die lydende en bedrywende vorm gaan oor wie die handeling doen, en die aantonende wys is 'n gewone stelsin.","en":"The imperative (*gebiedende wys*) is the command form: the verb comes first (*Draai*, *Ry*, *Stop*). The passive and active voice are about who performs the action, and the indicative (*aantonende wys*) is an ordinary statement."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["aantonende","lydende","bedrywende"],"en":["aantonende","lydende","bedrywende"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke teksoort by sy hoofdoel.","en":"Match each text type to its main purpose."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Resensie","en":"Review (resensie)"},"r":{"af":"Evalueer 'n film, boek of restaurant en beveel dit aan of nie","en":"Evaluates a film, book or restaurant and recommends it or not"}},{"l":{"af":"Huldeblyk","en":"Tribute (huldeblyk)"},"r":{"af":"Eer 'n persoon en sy of haar prestasies","en":"Honours a person and his or her achievements"}},{"l":{"af":"Aanwysings","en":"Directions (aanwysings)"},"r":{"af":"Verduidelik stap vir stap hoe om by 'n plek uit te kom","en":"Explains step by step how to get to a place"}},{"l":{"af":"Verslag","en":"Report (verslag)"},"r":{"af":"Gee bevindinge en aanbevelings oor 'n saak","en":"Gives findings and recommendations about a matter"}},{"l":{"af":"Dagboekinskrywing","en":"Diary entry (dagboekinskrywing)"},"r":{"af":"Teken jou eie gedagtes en gevoelens oor jou dag aan","en":"Records your own thoughts and feelings about your day"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke teksoort se doel bepaal sy formaat: 'n resensie evalueer, 'n huldeblyk eer, aanwysings lei stap vir stap, 'n verslag gee bevindinge en aanbevelings, en 'n dagboek is persoonlik.","en":"Each text type's purpose determines its format: a review evaluates, a tribute honours, directions guide step by step, a report gives findings and recommendations, and a diary is personal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy skryf 'n verslag vir die skoolhoof oor die kantien. Watter sin is in die regte register?","en":"You are writing a report for the principal about the tuck shop. Which sentence is in the correct register?"},"options":[{"af":"Ons ouens voel maar die kos is te duur, hoor.","en":"Ons ouens voel maar die kos is te duur, hoor. (slang: 'us guys feel the food is too pricey, hey')"},{"af":"Die meeste leerders het aangedui dat die kos in die kantien te duur is.","en":"Die meeste leerders het aangedui dat die kos in die kantien te duur is. (Most learners indicated that the food in the tuck shop is too expensive.)"},{"af":"Die kos is totaal oorduur en niemand koop dit nie!!","en":"Die kos is totaal oorduur en niemand koop dit nie!! (exaggerated, double exclamation marks)"},{"af":"Ek dink julle moet regtig iets aan die pryse doen, man.","en":"Ek dink julle moet regtig iets aan die pryse doen, man. (informal: 'I think you guys must really do something, man')"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Verslag is formeel en objektief. Die tweede sin is saaklik en gee 'n bevinding sonder sleng (*ouens*, *man*, *hoor*), oordrywing of uitroeptekens.","en":"A report is formal and objective. The second sentence is businesslike and gives a finding without slang (*ouens*, *man*, *hoor*), exaggeration or exclamation marks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak die sin formeel vir 'n brief aan die skoolhoof: *Kan jy asseblief die vorm teken?* → *Kan ___ asseblief die vorm teken?*","en":"Make the sentence formal for a letter to the principal: *Kan jy asseblief die vorm teken?* → *Kan ___ asseblief die vorm teken?*"},"answers":{"af":["u"],"en":["u"]},"explain":{"af":"*U* is die formele aanspreekvorm vir iemand met gesag of iemand wat jy nie goed ken nie. *Jou* is besitlik, *julle* is meervoud en *hulle* verwys na ander mense.","en":"*U* is the formal form of address for someone in authority or someone you don't know well. *Jou* is possessive, *julle* is plural and *hulle* refers to other people."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["julle","jou","hulle"],"en":["julle","jou","hulle"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees hierdie aanwysings: *Ry 'n entjie, dan gaan jy links, en dan is ons huis iewers daar.* Watter verbetering sal dit die meeste help?","en":"Read these directions: *Ry 'n entjie, dan gaan jy links, en dan is ons huis iewers daar.* (Drive a bit, then you go left, and then our house is somewhere there.) Which improvement will help most?"},"options":[{"af":"Voeg 'n aanhef (*Geagte Meneer*) en 'n slot (*Die uwe*) by.","en":"Add a salutation (*Geagte Meneer*) and a closing (*Die uwe*)."},{"af":"Skryf dit oor in die verlede tyd.","en":"Rewrite it in the past tense."},{"af":"Gebruik genommerde stappe in die gebiedende wys, met afstande en landmerke.","en":"Use numbered steps in the imperative, with distances and landmarks."},{"af":"Voeg retoriese vrae by om die leser se aandag te hou.","en":"Add rhetorical questions to hold the reader's attention."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Goeie aanwysings is presies: *1. Ry 2 km reguit. 2. Draai links by die vulstasie. 3. Ons huis is die derde huis regs, met die groen hek.* Die oorspronklike gee geen afstande of landmerke nie; 'n aanhef, verlede tyd of retoriese vrae help glad nie.","en":"Good directions are precise: *1. Ry 2 km reguit. 2. Draai links by die vulstasie. 3. Ons huis is die derde huis regs, met die groen hek.* The original gives no distances or landmarks; a salutation, past tense or rhetorical questions do not help at all."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die begin van 'n koerantberig: *Deur Thabo Nkosi. Brits – Ek was so bang toe ek die rook sien! Ek dink die brandweer was baie stadig.* Wat is die grootste fout?","en":"Read the opening of a newspaper report: *Deur Thabo Nkosi. Brits – Ek was so bang toe ek die rook sien! Ek dink die brandweer was baie stadig.* (I was so scared when I saw the smoke! I think the fire brigade was very slow.) What is the biggest mistake?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is in die eerste persoon met gevoelens en menings, in plaas van objektiewe feite (5 W's en H).","en":"It is in the first person with feelings and opinions, instead of objective facts (5 Ws and H)."},{"af":"Die byreël moet onderaan die berig staan.","en":"The byline must be at the bottom of the report."},{"af":"Die plek mag nie aan die begin genoem word nie.","en":"The place may not be mentioned at the beginning."},{"af":"'n Koerantberig moet in die toekomende tyd geskryf word.","en":"A newspaper report must be written in the future tense."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Koerantberig is objektief, in die derde persoon, en die eerste paragraaf gee die feite: wie, wat, waar, wanneer, hoekom en hoe. Die byreël en plek is reg geplaas, en 'n berig gebruik die verlede tyd.","en":"A newspaper report is objective, in the third person, and the first paragraph gives the facts: who, what, where, when, why and how. The byline and place are correctly placed, and a report uses the past tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy lewer 'n toespraak by die saalbyeenkoms oor afknouery. Watter opening is die doeltreffendste?","en":"You are giving a speech at assembly about bullying. Which opening is the most effective?"},"options":[{"af":"Liewe Dagboek, vandag wil ek oor afknouery praat.","en":"Liewe Dagboek, vandag wil ek oor afknouery praat. (Dear Diary, today I want to talk about bullying.)"},{"af":"Geagte Meneer, Insake: afknouery by die skool","en":"Geagte Meneer, Insake: afknouery by die skool (Dear Sir, Re: bullying at school)"},{"af":"Vandag gaan ek vir julle oor afknouery praat.","en":"Vandag gaan ek vir julle oor afknouery praat. (Today I am going to talk to you about bullying.)"},{"af":"Meneer die Hoof, geagte personeel, mede-leerders: het jy al ooit bang gevoel om skool toe te kom?","en":"Meneer die Hoof, geagte personeel, mede-leerders: het jy al ooit bang gevoel om skool toe te kom? (... have you ever been afraid to come to school?)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die laaste opsie het 'n korrekte aanspreekvorm én 'n retoriese vraag wat die gehoor dadelik betrek. Die eerste is dagboekformaat, die tweede is briefformaat, en die derde is 'n vervelige opening sonder aanspreekvorm.","en":"The last option has a correct form of address and a rhetorical question that involves the audience immediately. The first is diary format, the second is letter format, and the third is a dull opening without a form of address."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Woordeskat, woordvorming, spelling en leestekens","en":"Vocabulary, word formation, spelling and punctuation"},"topics":[{"id":"afr10-t4-woordvorming-woordeskat","title":{"af":"Woordvorming, woordeskat, idiome en spreekwoorde","en":"Word formation, vocabulary, idioms and proverbs"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal woorde met samestellings en affikse kan vorm, woordbetekenisse in konteks kan verduidelik en algemene idiome en spreekwoorde reg kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to form words with compounds and affixes, explain word meanings in context and use common idioms and proverbs correctly."},"summary":{"af":"## Woordvorming\n\n### Samestellings\n'n **Samestelling** bestaan uit twee of meer woorde wat elkeen alleen kan staan: *skool + sak = skoolsak*, *voet + bal + veld = voetbalveld*. 'n Samestelling word as **een woord** geskryf.\n\nSoms kom daar 'n **verbindingsklank** tussen die dele:\n- **-e-**: *hond-e-hok*, *boer-e-musiek*, *perd-e-by*\n- **-s-**: *regering-s-beleid*, *veiligheid-s-gordel*, *arbeid-s-mark*\n\n> **Lokval:** In *skoolsak* is die *s* deel van *sak*; dit is nie 'n verbindingsklank nie.\n\n### Afleidings\n'n **Afleiding** = 'n stam + 'n **affiks** ('n deel wat nie alleen kan staan nie). 'n Affiks voor die stam is 'n **voorvoegsel**; ná die stam is dit 'n **agtervoegsel**.\n\n| Voorvoegsel | Betekenis | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| on- | nie | ongelukkig, oneerlik |\n| be- | vorm 'n werkwoord | beloon, bedank |\n| ver- | verandering | verbeter, verklein |\n| ont- | weg, die teenoorgestelde | ontmoedig, ontwapen |\n| her- | weer | herskryf, herbou |\n| wan- | sleg, verkeerd | wanbegrip, wangedrag |\n| aarts- | die grootste, hoofste | aartsvyand, aartsbiskop |\n\n| Agtervoegsel | Vorm 'n ... | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| -heid | selfstandige naamwoord | vryheid, dapperheid |\n| -ing | selfstandige naamwoord | verbetering, opvoeding |\n| -skap | selfstandige naamwoord | vriendskap, kapteinskap |\n| -ery | selfstandige naamwoord (plek/bedryf) | bakkery, boerdery |\n| -lik | byvoeglike naamwoord | gevaarlik, lieflik |\n| -loos | byvoeglike naamwoord (sonder) | hopeloos, werkloos |\n| -baar | byvoeglike naamwoord (kan) | eetbaar, drinkbaar |\n| -agtig | byvoeglike naamwoord (soos) | kinderagtig, rooiagtig |\n\n### Die woordsoort verander\nMet affikse verander jy die **woordsoort**: *lief* (bnw) → *liefde* (sn) → *liefdevol* (bnw); *gevaar* (sn) → *gevaarlik* (bnw); *skryf* (ww) → *skrywer* (sn). Kyk na die sin om te besluit watter woordsoort nodig is: ná *die* of *haar* volg gewoonlik 'n selfstandige naamwoord.\n\n### Afkortings en letterwoorde\n- **Afkortings:** *bv.* (byvoorbeeld), *d.w.s.* (dit wil sê), *ens.* (ensovoorts), *mnr.* (meneer), *me.* (mevrou of mejuffrou), *dr.* (dokter).\n- **Letterwoorde** word uit die beginletters van woorde gevorm: *SAPD* (Suid-Afrikaanse Polisiediens), *SAUK* (Suid-Afrikaanse Uitsaaikorporasie). As jy dit soos 'n gewone woord uitspreek, bv. *NAVO*, is dit 'n **akroniem**.\n\n## Woordbetekenis\n- **Sinonieme** het dieselfde betekenis: *begin – aanvang*, *vinnig – gou*.\n- **Antonieme** (teenoorgesteldes) vorm jy met *on-* (*gelukkig → ongelukkig*) of met 'n ander woord (*vroeg → laat*). Die **konteks** bepaal die antoniem: *'n ou man → 'n jong man*, maar *'n ou motor → 'n nuwe motor*.\n- **Homonieme** het dieselfde spelling en klank, maar verskillende betekenisse: *bank* (om op te sit / vir jou geld), *blad* (van 'n boom / van 'n tafel).\n- **Homofone** klink dieselfde, maar het 'n ander spelling en betekenis: *lei* (die pad wys) / *ly* (pyn verduur), *wei* (gras eet) / *wy* (aan iets opdra), *reis / rys*, *hart / hard*.\n- **Paronieme** lyk en klink amper eenders, maar beteken iets anders: *kinderlik* (onskuldig soos 'n kind, positief) / *kinderagtig* (onvolwasse, negatief).\n- 'n **Eufemisme** is 'n sagter woord vir iets onaangenaams: *ontslaap* of *heengaan* vir *sterf*.\n- **Leenwoorde** kom uit ander tale: *piesang* (Maleis), *indaba* (isiZulu), *tjommie* (Engels).\n- **Anglisismes** is Engelse uitdrukkings wat letterlik vertaal is: *Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad* → *Ek het dit geniet*; *'n besluit maak* → *'n besluit neem*.\n\n## Idiome en spreekwoorde\n'n **Idioom** (uitdrukking) is 'n vaste groep woorde wat nie letterlik bedoel word nie en deel van 'n sin is. 'n **Spreekwoord** is 'n volledige sin met 'n lewensles.\n\n| Idioom | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| die kat uit die boom kyk | wag om te sien wat gebeur voordat jy iets doen |\n| met die deur in die huis val | dadelik en reguit sê wat jy wil sê |\n| agter die net vis | te laat wees en iets misloop |\n| iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai | iemand bedrieg of flous |\n| die bobbejaan agter die bult gaan haal | jou bekommer oor moeilikheid voordat dit kom |\n| op heterdaad betrap | betrap terwyl jy die oortreding pleeg |\n\n| Spreekwoord | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| Oefening baar kuns. | Hoe meer jy oefen, hoe beter word jy. |\n| Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie. | Kinders lyk na of doen soos hul ouers. |\n| Wie laaste lag, lag die lekkerste. | Wie aan die einde wen, het die meeste rede om bly te wees. |\n| Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie. | Moenie te gou seker wees van sukses nie. |\n| Haastige hond verbrand sy mond. | As jy te haastig is, maak jy foute. |\n\n> **Wenk:** Pas die werkwoord van die idioom by die sin aan (*Sy het met die deur in die huis geval.*), maar verander nooit die vaste woorde (*kat*, *boom*, *deur*) nie.\n\n> **Algemene foute:** samestellings as twee woorde skryf (*skool sak*); *ly* en *lei* verwar; 'n idioom letterlik verduidelik; 'n antoniem gee wat nie in die konteks pas nie.","en":"## Word formation (woordvorming)\n\n### Compounds (samestellings)\nA **compound** consists of two or more words that can each stand alone: *skool + sak = skoolsak*, *voet + bal + veld = voetbalveld*. A compound is written as **one word**.\n\nSometimes a **linking sound** (*verbindingsklank*) comes between the parts:\n- **-e-**: *hond-e-hok*, *boer-e-musiek*, *perd-e-by*\n- **-s-**: *regering-s-beleid*, *veiligheid-s-gordel*, *arbeid-s-mark*\n\n> **Trap:** In *skoolsak* the *s* belongs to *sak*; it is not a linking sound.\n\n### Derivations (afleidings)\nA **derivation** = a stem + an **affix** (a part that cannot stand alone). An affix before the stem is a **prefix** (*voorvoegsel*); after the stem it is a **suffix** (*agtervoegsel*).\n\n| Prefix | Meaning | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| on- | not | ongelukkig, oneerlik |\n| be- | forms a verb | beloon, bedank |\n| ver- | change | verbeter, verklein |\n| ont- | away, the opposite | ontmoedig, ontwapen |\n| her- | again | herskryf, herbou |\n| wan- | bad, wrong | wanbegrip, wangedrag |\n| aarts- | the greatest, chief | aartsvyand, aartsbiskop |\n\n| Suffix | Forms a ... | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| -heid | noun | vryheid, dapperheid |\n| -ing | noun | verbetering, opvoeding |\n| -skap | noun | vriendskap, kapteinskap |\n| -ery | noun (place/trade) | bakkery, boerdery |\n| -lik | adjective | gevaarlik, lieflik |\n| -loos | adjective (without) | hopeloos, werkloos |\n| -baar | adjective (can be) | eetbaar, drinkbaar |\n| -agtig | adjective (like) | kinderagtig, rooiagtig |\n\n### Changing the word class\nWith affixes you change the **word class**: *lief* (adj) → *liefde* (noun) → *liefdevol* (adj); *gevaar* (noun) → *gevaarlik* (adj); *skryf* (verb) → *skrywer* (noun). Look at the sentence to decide which word class is needed: after *die* or *haar* a noun usually follows.\n\n### Abbreviations and letter words\n- **Abbreviations (afkortings):** *bv.* (for example), *d.w.s.* (that is), *ens.* (etc.), *mnr.* (Mr), *me.* (Ms), *dr.* (Dr).\n- **Letter words (letterwoorde)** are formed from the first letters of words: *SAPD* (South African Police Service), *SAUK* (SABC). If you pronounce it like an ordinary word, e.g. *NAVO* (NATO), it is an **acronym** (*akroniem*).\n\n## Word meaning (woordbetekenis)\n- **Synonyms (sinonieme)** have the same meaning: *begin – aanvang*, *vinnig – gou*.\n- **Antonyms (antonieme/teenoorgesteldes)** are formed with *on-* (*gelukkig → ongelukkig*) or with a different word (*vroeg → laat*). The **context** decides the antonym: *'n ou man → 'n jong man*, but *'n ou motor → 'n nuwe motor*.\n- **Homonyms (homonieme)** have the same spelling and sound but different meanings: *bank* (to sit on / for your money), *blad* (of a tree / of a table).\n- **Homophones (homofone)** sound the same but have a different spelling and meaning: *lei* (lead) / *ly* (suffer), *wei* (graze) / *wy* (dedicate), *reis / rys* (journey / rice), *hart / hard* (heart / hard).\n- **Paronyms (paronieme)** look and sound almost the same but mean something different: *kinderlik* (innocent like a child, positive) / *kinderagtig* (immature, negative).\n- A **euphemism (eufemisme)** is a softer word for something unpleasant: *ontslaap* or *heengaan* for *sterf* (die).\n- **Loan words (leenwoorde)** come from other languages: *piesang* (Malay), *indaba* (isiZulu), *tjommie* (English).\n- **Anglicisms (anglisismes)** are English expressions translated literally: *Ek het 'n goeie tyd gehad* → *Ek het dit geniet*; *'n besluit maak* → *'n besluit neem*.\n\n## Idioms and proverbs (idiome en spreekwoorde)\nAn **idiom** (expression) is a fixed group of words that is not meant literally and forms part of a sentence. A **proverb** is a complete sentence with a life lesson.\n\n| Idiom | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| die kat uit die boom kyk | wait to see what happens before you act |\n| met die deur in die huis val | come straight to the point |\n| agter die net vis | be too late and miss out |\n| iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai | deceive someone |\n| die bobbejaan agter die bult gaan haal | worry about trouble before it comes |\n| op heterdaad betrap | catch red-handed |\n\n| Proverb | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Oefening baar kuns. | Practice makes perfect. |\n| Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie. | Children look like or behave like their parents. |\n| Wie laaste lag, lag die lekkerste. | He who laughs last laughs longest. |\n| Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie. | Don't count your chickens before they hatch. |\n| Haastige hond verbrand sy mond. | Haste makes waste: if you rush, you make mistakes. |\n\n> **Tip:** Adapt the verb of the idiom to the sentence (*Sy het met die deur in die huis geval.*), but never change the fixed words (*kat*, *boom*, *deur*).\n\n> **Common mistakes:** writing compounds as two words (*skool sak*); confusing *ly* and *lei*; explaining an idiom literally; giving an antonym that does not fit the context."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Samestelling","en":"Compound"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat uit twee of meer selfstandige woorde bestaan, bv. *skool + sak = skoolsak*.","en":"A word made up of two or more independent words, e.g. *skool + sak = skoolsak*."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbindingsklank","en":"Linking sound"},"def":{"af":"'n Klank (-e- of -s-) tussen die dele van 'n samestelling, bv. *hond-e-hok*, *regering-s-beleid*.","en":"A sound (-e- or -s-) between the parts of a compound, e.g. *hond-e-hok*, *regering-s-beleid*."}},{"term":{"af":"Afleiding","en":"Derivation"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat gevorm word deur 'n voorvoegsel of agtervoegsel by 'n stam te voeg, bv. *on + gelukkig*, *vriend + skap*.","en":"A word formed by adding a prefix or suffix to a stem, e.g. *on + gelukkig*, *vriend + skap*."}},{"term":{"af":"Sinoniem","en":"Synonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met dieselfde of amper dieselfde betekenis as 'n ander woord, bv. *begin – aanvang*.","en":"A word with the same or nearly the same meaning as another word, e.g. *begin – aanvang*."}},{"term":{"af":"Antoniem","en":"Antonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met die teenoorgestelde betekenis, bv. *vroeg – laat*, *gelukkig – ongelukkig*.","en":"A word with the opposite meaning, e.g. *vroeg – laat*, *gelukkig – ongelukkig*."}},{"term":{"af":"Homoniem","en":"Homonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met dieselfde spelling en uitspraak as 'n ander woord, maar 'n ander betekenis, bv. *bank*.","en":"A word with the same spelling and pronunciation as another word but a different meaning, e.g. *bank*."}},{"term":{"af":"Homofoon","en":"Homophone"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat dieselfde klink as 'n ander woord, maar anders gespel word en iets anders beteken, bv. *lei / ly*.","en":"A word that sounds the same as another word but is spelt differently and means something else, e.g. *lei / ly*."}},{"term":{"af":"Anglisisme","en":"Anglicism"},"def":{"af":"'n Engelse uitdrukking wat letterlik in Afrikaans vertaal is, bv. *'n besluit maak* in plaas van *'n besluit neem*.","en":"An English expression translated literally into Afrikaans, e.g. *'n besluit maak* instead of *'n besluit neem*."}},{"term":{"af":"Idioom","en":"Idiom"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste uitdrukking wat nie letterlik bedoel word nie, bv. *agter die net vis* (te laat wees).","en":"A fixed expression that is not meant literally, e.g. *agter die net vis* (to be too late)."}},{"term":{"af":"Spreekwoord","en":"Proverb"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste, volledige sin wat 'n lewensles of wysheid oordra, bv. *Oefening baar kuns.*","en":"A fixed, complete sentence that carries a life lesson or wisdom, e.g. *Oefening baar kuns.*"}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Vorm die regte woord met 'n agtervoegsel","en":"Form the correct word with a suffix"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die korrekte vorm van die woord tussen hakies.\n(a) Die leerders geniet die ___ van die vakansie. (vry)\n(b) Hierdie sampioene is nie ___ nie; moenie hulle pluk nie. (eet)\n(c) Ná die derde doel teen hulle het die spelers ___ gevoel. (hoop)","en":"Write the correct form of the word in brackets.\n(a) Die leerders geniet die ___ van die vakansie. (vry)\n(b) Hierdie sampioene is nie ___ nie; moenie hulle pluk nie. (eet)\n(c) Ná die derde doel teen hulle het die spelers ___ gevoel. (hoop)"},"steps":[{"af":"Bepaal eers watter woordsoort elke sin nodig het: (a) ná *die* → 'n selfstandige naamwoord; (b) en (c) beskryf iets → 'n byvoeglike naamwoord.","en":"First decide which word class each sentence needs: (a) after *die* → a noun; (b) and (c) describe something → an adjective."},{"af":"(a) vry + -heid = **vryheid**. Die agtervoegsel -heid vorm 'n selfstandige naamwoord.","en":"(a) vry + -heid = **vryheid** (freedom). The suffix -heid forms a noun."},{"af":"(b) eet + -baar = **eetbaar** ('kan geëet word').","en":"(b) eet + -baar = **eetbaar** (edible: 'can be eaten')."},{"af":"(c) hoop + -loos = **hopeloos** ('sonder hoop'). Let op die spelling: *ho-pe-loos* is 'n oop lettergreep, dus net een o.","en":"(c) hoop + -loos = **hopeloos** (hopeless: 'without hope'). Note the spelling: *ho-pe-loos* is an open syllable, so only one o."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) vryheid (b) eetbaar (c) hopeloos","en":"(a) vryheid (b) eetbaar (c) hopeloos"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontleed samestellings","en":"Analyse compounds"},"problem":{"af":"Verdeel die samestellings in hul dele en noem die verbindingsklank, as daar een is: (a) hondehok (b) veiligheidsgordel (c) voetbalveld","en":"Split the compounds into their parts and name the linking sound, if there is one: (a) hondehok (b) veiligheidsgordel (c) voetbalveld"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *hond + e + hok*: die verbindingsklank is **-e-**.","en":"(a) *hond + e + hok*: the linking sound is **-e-**."},{"af":"(b) *veiligheid + s + gordel*: die verbindingsklank is **-s-**.","en":"(b) *veiligheid + s + gordel*: the linking sound is **-s-**."},{"af":"(c) *voet + bal + veld*: drie woorde wat elkeen alleen kan staan, met **geen** verbindingsklank nie.","en":"(c) *voet + bal + veld*: three words that can each stand alone, with **no** linking sound."},{"af":"Onthou: al drie bly een woord. *Voetbal veld* sou verkeerd wees.","en":"Remember: all three stay one word. *Voetbal veld* would be wrong."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) hond-e-hok: -e- (b) veiligheid-s-gordel: -s- (c) voet-bal-veld: geen","en":"(a) hond-e-hok: -e- (b) veiligheid-s-gordel: -s- (c) voet-bal-veld: none"}},{"title":{"af":"Verduidelik en gebruik 'n idioom","en":"Explain and use an idiom"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Verduidelik die vetgedrukte idioom in eie woorde: Toe die polisie by die winkel in Brits opdaag, is die dief **op heterdaad betrap**.\n(b) Gebruik die idioom *met die deur in die huis val* in 'n sin van jou eie.","en":"(a) Explain the idiom in bold in your own words: Toe die polisie by die winkel in Brits opdaag, is die dief **op heterdaad betrap**.\n(b) Use the idiom *met die deur in die huis val* in a sentence of your own."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Lees die konteks: die polisie het opgedaag terwyl die dief nog in die winkel was.","en":"(a) Read the context: the police arrived while the thief was still in the shop."},{"af":"Betekenis: die dief is betrap **terwyl hy besig was om te steel**. Moenie die woord *heterdaad* net herhaal nie; verduidelik dit.","en":"Meaning: the thief was caught **while he was busy stealing** (caught red-handed). Do not just repeat the word *heterdaad*; explain it."},{"af":"(b) Kies 'n situasie waar iemand dadelik en reguit praat, en pas die werkwoord aan: *Ma het met die deur in die huis geval en gevra wie die venster gebreek het.*","en":"(b) Choose a situation where someone speaks immediately and directly, and adapt the verb: *Ma het met die deur in die huis geval en gevra wie die venster gebreek het.* (Mom came straight to the point and asked who broke the window.)"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Hy is betrap terwyl hy die misdaad gepleeg het. (b) Bv. *Ma het met die deur in die huis geval en gevra wie die venster gebreek het.*","en":"(a) He was caught while committing the crime. (b) E.g. *Ma het met die deur in die huis geval en gevra wie die venster gebreek het.*"}},{"title":{"af":"Homonieme, homofone en anglisismes","en":"Homonyms, homophones and anglicisms"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Wat beteken *bank* in elke sin? *Ek wag op die bank by die bushalte.* / *Ek deponeer my sakgeld by die bank.*\n(b) Kies die regte woord: *Oupa (lei / ly) aan rugpyn.*\n(c) Verbeter die anglisisme: *Ons het 'n goeie tyd by die braai gehad.*","en":"(a) What does *bank* mean in each sentence? *Ek wag op die bank by die bushalte.* / *Ek deponeer my sakgeld by die bank.*\n(b) Choose the correct word: *Oupa (lei / ly) aan rugpyn.*\n(c) Correct the anglicism: *Ons het 'n goeie tyd by die braai gehad.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *Bank* is 'n homoniem: in die eerste sin is dit 'n sitplek; in die tweede 'n finansiële instelling.","en":"(a) *Bank* is a homonym: in the first sentence it is a seat (bench); in the second a financial institution."},{"af":"(b) *Lei* en *ly* is homofone. *Ly* beteken pyn of swaarkry verduur, dus: *Oupa ly aan rugpyn.* (*Lei* beteken om die pad te wys.)","en":"(b) *Lei* and *ly* are homophones. *Ly* means to suffer pain or hardship, so: *Oupa ly aan rugpyn.* (*Lei* means to lead.)"},{"af":"(c) *'n Goeie tyd hê* is 'n letterlike vertaling van 'to have a good time'. Afrikaans: *Ons het die braai geniet* of *Ons het lekker by die braai gekuier.*","en":"(c) *'n Goeie tyd hê* is a literal translation of 'to have a good time'. Afrikaans: *Ons het die braai geniet* or *Ons het lekker by die braai gekuier.*"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) sitplek; finansiële instelling (b) ly (c) Ons het die braai geniet.","en":"(a) seat (bench); financial institution (b) ly (c) Ons het die braai geniet."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarvoor staan die afkorting *d.w.s.*?","en":"What does the abbreviation *d.w.s.* stand for?"},"options":[{"af":"deur wie saamgestel","en":"deur wie saamgestel (compiled by whom)"},{"af":"dit was so","en":"dit was so (it was so)"},{"af":"dit wil sê","en":"dit wil sê (that is to say)"},{"af":"die woord sê","en":"die woord sê (the word says)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*d.w.s.* = dit wil sê. Jy gebruik dit om iets te verduidelik: *Ons skryf V1, d.w.s. Taal in konteks.*","en":"*d.w.s.* = dit wil sê (that is / i.e.). You use it to explain something: *Ons skryf V1, d.w.s. Taal in konteks.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die voorvoegsel ___ maak van *gelukkig* sy antoniem.","en":"The prefix ___ turns *gelukkig* into its antonym."},"answers":{"af":["on","on-"],"en":["on","on-"]},"explain":{"af":"*on- + gelukkig = ongelukkig*. Die voorvoegsel on- beteken 'nie'. *Ont-* (ontmoedig) en *wan-* (wanbegrip) het ander betekenisse.","en":"*on- + gelukkig = ongelukkig*. The prefix on- means 'not'. *Ont-* (ontmoedig) and *wan-* (wanbegrip) have other meanings."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["ont","wan","ver"],"en":["ont","wan","ver"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Reis* en *rys* is homonieme, want hulle word op dieselfde manier gespel.","en":"*Reis* and *rys* are homonyms because they are spelt the same way."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Reis* (om te reis) en *rys* (die kos) klink dieselfde, maar word verskillend gespel: hulle is **homofone**. Homonieme het dieselfde spelling, soos *bank* (sitbank) en *bank* (geldbank).","en":"False. *Reis* (journey) and *rys* (rice) sound the same but are spelt differently: they are **homophones**. Homonyms have the same spelling, like *bank* (bench) and *bank* (money bank)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is 'n sinoniem van *begin*?","en":"Which word is a synonym of *begin*?"},"options":[{"af":"aanvang","en":"aanvang (commencement)"},{"af":"eindig","en":"eindig (end)"},{"af":"begrip","en":"begrip (understanding)"},{"af":"beweeg","en":"beweeg (move)"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Sinoniem het (amper) dieselfde betekenis: *begin = aanvang*. *Eindig* is 'n antoniem, en *begrip* lyk net soos *begin*.","en":"A synonym has (nearly) the same meaning: *begin = aanvang*. *Eindig* is an antonym, and *begrip* only looks like *begin*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die spreekwoord: *Oefening baar ___.*","en":"Complete the proverb: *Oefening baar ___.*"},"answers":{"af":["kuns"],"en":["kuns"]},"explain":{"af":"*Oefening baar kuns*: as jy aanhou oefen, word jy goed daarin, soos 'n skopper wat elke middag doelskoppe oefen. Die woorde van 'n spreekwoord is vas; jy mag hulle nie vervang nie.","en":"*Oefening baar kuns* (practice makes perfect): if you keep practising, you get good at it, like a kicker who practises goal kicks every afternoon. The words of a proverb are fixed; you may not replace them."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sukses","vrugte","kennis"],"en":["sukses","vrugte","kennis"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken die idioom *agter die net vis*?","en":"What does the idiom *agter die net vis* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"Iemand bedrieg of flous","en":"Deceive or fool someone"},{"af":"Te laat wees en iets misloop","en":"Be too late and miss out"},{"af":"Iets onwettigs doen sonder om betrap te word","en":"Do something illegal without being caught"},{"af":"Baie hard werk vir min beloning","en":"Work very hard for little reward"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"As jy agter die net vis, het die net die visse reeds gevang: jy is te laat. *Iemand bedrieg* is die betekenis van *iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai*.","en":"If you fish behind the net, the net has already caught the fish: you are too late. *Deceive someone* is the meaning of *iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Hy het ontslaap* is 'n eufemisme vir *Hy is dood*.","en":"*Hy het ontslaap* is a euphemism for *Hy is dood* (He died)."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n Eufemisme is 'n sagter of beleefder woord vir iets onaangenaams. *Ontslaap* klink minder hard as *dood* of *gesterf*.","en":"True. A euphemism is a softer or more polite word for something unpleasant. *Ontslaap* sounds less harsh than *dood* or *gesterf*."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke idioom by sy betekenis.","en":"Match each idiom to its meaning."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"die kat uit die boom kyk","en":"die kat uit die boom kyk"},"r":{"af":"wag om te sien wat gebeur voordat jy iets doen","en":"wait to see what happens before you act"}},{"l":{"af":"met die deur in die huis val","en":"met die deur in die huis val"},"r":{"af":"dadelik en reguit sê wat jy wil sê","en":"come straight to the point"}},{"l":{"af":"iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai","en":"iemand 'n rat voor die oë draai"},"r":{"af":"iemand bedrieg of flous","en":"deceive or fool someone"}},{"l":{"af":"die bobbejaan agter die bult gaan haal","en":"die bobbejaan agter die bult gaan haal"},"r":{"af":"jou bekommer oor moeilikheid voordat dit kom","en":"worry about trouble before it comes"}},{"l":{"af":"op heterdaad betrap","en":"op heterdaad betrap"},"r":{"af":"betrap terwyl jy die oortreding pleeg","en":"caught while committing the offence (red-handed)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Idiome word nie letterlik bedoel nie. Leer hulle saam met hul betekenis, en oefen om elkeen in 'n eie sin te gebruik.","en":"Idioms are not meant literally. Learn them together with their meaning, and practise using each one in a sentence of your own."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vorm 'n selfstandige naamwoord van *vriend* met die agtervoegsel -skap: ___","en":"Form a noun from *vriend* with the suffix -skap: ___"},"answers":{"af":["vriendskap"],"en":["vriendskap"]},"explain":{"af":"*vriend + -skap = vriendskap* ('n selfstandige naamwoord). *Vriendelik* en *vriendskaplik* is byvoeglike naamwoorde; *vriendin* is die vroulike vorm.","en":"*vriend + -skap = vriendskap* (friendship, a noun). *Vriendelik* and *vriendskaplik* are adjectives; *vriendin* is the feminine form."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["vriendelik","vriendskaplik","vriendin"],"en":["vriendelik","vriendskaplik","vriendin"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter samestelling is die *s* 'n verbindingsklank?","en":"In which compound is the *s* a linking sound?"},"options":[{"af":"skoolsak","en":"skoolsak"},{"af":"voetbalspan","en":"voetbalspan"},{"af":"hondehok","en":"hondehok"},{"af":"regeringsbeleid","en":"regeringsbeleid"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*regering + s + beleid*: die s is ingevoeg om die dele te verbind. In *skoolsak* en *voetbalspan* is die s die eerste letter van *sak* en *span*. In *hondehok* is die verbindingsklank -e-.","en":"*regering + s + beleid*: the s is inserted to link the parts. In *skoolsak* and *voetbalspan* the s is the first letter of *sak* and *span*. In *hondehok* the linking sound is -e-."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die antoniem van *ou* wat in die sin pas: *Pa het sy ou bakkie verkoop en 'n ___ een gekoop.*","en":"Choose the antonym of *ou* that fits the sentence: *Pa het sy ou bakkie verkoop en 'n ___ een gekoop.*"},"options":[{"af":"jong","en":"jong (young)"},{"af":"nuwe","en":"nuwe (new)"},{"af":"onou","en":"onou (not a real word)"},{"af":"ouer","en":"ouer (older)"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die konteks bepaal die antoniem: *'n ou man ↔ 'n jong man*, maar *'n ou bakkie ↔ 'n nuwe bakkie*. *Onou* bestaan nie, en *ouer* is 'n trap van vergelyking, nie 'n antoniem nie.","en":"The context decides the antonym: *'n ou man ↔ 'n jong man*, but *'n ou bakkie ↔ 'n nuwe bakkie*. *Onou* does not exist, and *ouer* is a degree of comparison, not an antonym."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies die regte homofoon: *Die skape ___ in die veld naby die Magaliesberg.* (wei / wy)","en":"Choose the correct homophone: *Die skape ___ in die veld naby die Magaliesberg.* (wei / wy)"},"answers":{"af":["wei"],"en":["wei"]},"explain":{"af":"*Wei* beteken om gras te eet: die skape wei. *Wy* beteken om iets aan iemand op te dra: *Sy wy haar lewe aan die kinders.*","en":"*Wei* means to graze: the sheep graze. *Wy* means to dedicate something to someone: *Sy wy haar lewe aan die kinders.*"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["wy","lei","ly"],"en":["wy","lei","ly"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Verbeter die anglisisme: *Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gemaak.*","en":"Correct the anglicism: *Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gemaak.*"},"options":[{"af":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit geneem.","en":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit geneem."},{"af":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gedoen.","en":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gedoen."},{"af":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gehad.","en":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gehad."},{"af":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gegee.","en":"Die komitee het gister 'n besluit gegee."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"In Afrikaans **neem** jy 'n besluit. *'n Besluit maak* is 'n letterlike vertaling van die Engelse 'make a decision'.","en":"In Afrikaans you **take** (*neem*) a decision. *'n Besluit maak* is a literal translation of the English 'make a decision'."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gebruik die woord tussen hakies in die regte vorm: *Haar ___ vir diere is duidelik.* (lief)","en":"Use the word in brackets in the correct form: *Haar ___ vir diere is duidelik.* (lief)"},"answers":{"af":["liefde"],"en":["liefde"]},"explain":{"af":"Ná *Haar* en voor *vir diere* het die sin 'n selfstandige naamwoord nodig: *lief* (bnw) → *liefde* (sn). *Liefdevol* en *lieflik* is byvoeglike naamwoorde, en *liewe* is die verbuigde vorm van *lief*.","en":"After *Haar* and before *vir diere* the sentence needs a noun: *lief* (adj) → *liefde* (noun, love). *Liefdevol* and *lieflik* are adjectives, and *liewe* is the inflected form of *lief*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["liefdevol","lieflik","liewe"],"en":["liefdevol","lieflik","liewe"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin word die idioom korrek gebruik?","en":"In which sentence is the idiom used correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Die dief is op heterdaad betrap toe hy die volgende week sy misdaad erken het.","en":"Die dief is op heterdaad betrap toe hy die volgende week sy misdaad erken het. (... when he confessed the next week)"},{"af":"Sy het die kat uit die boom gekyk en dadelik ingespring om te help.","en":"Sy het die kat uit die boom gekyk en dadelik ingespring om te help. (... and immediately jumped in to help)"},{"af":"Thabo het met die deur in die huis geval en sommer dadelik gevra of hy die motor kan leen.","en":"Thabo het met die deur in die huis geval en sommer dadelik gevra of hy die motor kan leen. (... and immediately asked if he could borrow the car)"},{"af":"Ons was agter die net vis, want ons het vroeg gekom en die beste plekke gekry.","en":"Ons was agter die net vis, want ons het vroeg gekom en die beste plekke gekry. (... because we came early and got the best seats)"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Met die deur in die huis val* beteken om reguit en dadelik te sê wat jy wil hê, en dit pas. In die ander sinne weerspreek die konteks die idioom: hy het later erken (nie op heterdaad nie), sy het nie gewag nie, en hulle was vroeg (nie te laat nie).","en":"*Met die deur in die huis val* means to say straight away what you want, and it fits. In the other sentences the context contradicts the idiom: he confessed later (not red-handed), she did not wait, and they were early (not too late)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sarel het die hele week gespog dat sy span die beker gaan wen. Hulle het toe in die halfeindronde verloor. Watter spreekwoord pas die beste?","en":"Sarel boasted all week that his team would win the cup. They then lost in the semi-final. Which proverb fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"Oefening baar kuns.","en":"Oefening baar kuns. (Practice makes perfect.)"},{"af":"Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie.","en":"Die appel val nie ver van die boom nie. (Like father, like son.)"},{"af":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond.","en":"Haastige hond verbrand sy mond. (Haste makes waste.)"},{"af":"Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie.","en":"Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie. (Don't count your chickens before they hatch.)"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sarel was te gou seker van sukses: *Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie.* *Haastige hond verbrand sy mond* gaan oor foute wat jy maak as jy iets te haastig doen, nie oor spoggery nie.","en":"Sarel was too sure of success too soon: *Moenie die dag voor die aand prys nie.* *Haastige hond verbrand sy mond* is about mistakes you make when you do something too hastily, not about boasting."}}]},{"id":"afr10-t4-spelling-leestekens","title":{"af":"Spelling, skryftekens en leestekens","en":"Spelling, diacritics and punctuation"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal hoofletters, skryftekens en leestekens korrek kan gebruik en 'n paragraaf met spel- en leestekenfoute kan redigeer.","en":"You will be able to use capital letters, diacritics and punctuation correctly and edit a paragraph with spelling and punctuation errors."},"summary":{"af":"## Hoofletters\n\nGebruik 'n **hoofletter**:\n- aan die begin van 'n sin;\n- vir **eiename**: *Thabo, Brits, Magaliesberg, Krokodilrivier*;\n- vir **tale** en woorde wat daarvan afgelei is: *Afrikaans, Setswana, Afrikaanse musiek*;\n- vir **dae en maande**: *Maandag, Januarie* (maar nie vir seisoene nie: *somer, winter*);\n- vir die eerste woord van 'n **titel**: *Die geheim van die ou myn*.\n\nAfkortings van titels voor 'n naam kry in die middel van 'n sin 'n kleinletter: *Ons het mnr. Botha en dr. Mokoena gesien.*\n\n> **Onthou!** *'n* kry nooit 'n hoofletter nie. Aan die begin van 'n sin kry die **volgende** woord die hoofletter: *'n Taxi het gestop.* Dieselfde geld vir *'s*: *'s Middags oefen ons.*\n\n## Skryftekens\n\n| Skryfteken | Wat dit doen | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Deelteken** (trema) ¨ | wys dat 'n **nuwe lettergreep** begin, sodat jy die klinkers nie saam lees nie | knieë (knie-ë), geïnteresseerd (ge-ïn-...), reünie (re-ü-nie), reën |\n| **Kappie** (sirkumfleks) ^ | dui 'n lang klank in sekere woorde aan | môre, wêreld, sê, brûe, wîe |\n| **Akuutteken** ´ | klem of onderskeid | dié (hierdie een), óf ... óf, én ... én |\n| **Gravis** ` | onderskei woorde of tussenwerpsels | hè, appèl (beroep) teenoor appel (vrug) |\n\n> **Wenk:** Die deelteken staan op die **eerste klinker van die nuwe lettergreep**: *be-ïn-druk → beïndruk*, *i-de-ë → ideë*.\n\n### Afkappingsteken (apostrof)\n- in *'n* en *'s* (*'s middags*);\n- in die meervoud van woorde wat op 'n **lang a, i, o of u** eindig: *ma's, pa's, foto's, radio's, taxi's*;\n- in die meervoud van letterwoorde: *SMS'e, cd's*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Afrikaans wys **besit** met *se*, nie met 's nie: *Pieter se boek* (NIE *Pieter's boek* nie).\n\n### Koppelteken (-)\n- in samestellings met eiename: *Suid-Afrika, Wes-Kaap*;\n- by *oud-* voor 'n titel: *oud-president, oud-leerder*;\n- by letters en syfers: *e-pos, SMS-boodskap, TV-program*;\n- in getalle met *en*: *een-en-twintig*;\n- om **verkeerde lees** te voorkom waar klinkers bots: *see-eend, na-aap*.\n\n## Klinkerverdubbeling en -vereenvoudiging\n- 'n **Lang klinker** in 'n **geslote lettergreep** (eindig op 'n medeklinker) skryf jy dubbel: *maan, boom, muur*. In 'n **oop lettergreep** (eindig op 'n klinker) skryf jy dit enkel: *ma-ne, bo-me, mu-re*.\n- 'n **Kort klinker** bly kort as jy die medeklinker **verdubbel**: *kat → kat-te, pot → pot-te, bus → bus-se*.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *maane* en *boome* is verkeerd, want *ma-* en *bo-* is reeds oop lettergrepe. *Pote* (met 'n lang o) is die meervoud van *poot*, nie van *pot* nie.\n\n## Leestekens\n\n| Leesteken | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Punt . | einde van 'n stelsin; ná sommige afkortings | Ons ry Pretoria toe. |\n| Komma , | in 'n lys (nie voor *en* nie); tussen bysin en hoofsin; om 'n aanspreekvorm | Ek koop brood, melk en eiers. Toe die klok lui, het ons gehardloop. Thabo, kom hier! |\n| Kommapunt ; | tussen twee hoofsinne wat nou verwant is | Dit reën; die wedstryd is uitgestel. |\n| Dubbelpunt : | voor 'n lys of direkte rede | Bring die volgende: 'n pen, 'n liniaal en 'n uitveër. |\n| Vraagteken ? | ná 'n direkte vraag | Wanneer begin die eksamen? |\n| Uitroepteken ! | ná 'n uitroep of bevel | Eina! Gaan sit! |\n| Aanhalingstekens \" \" | direkte rede, aanhalings en titels | Sy sê: \"Ek is moeg.\" |\n| Hakies ( ) | ekstra inligting | Die SAPD (Suid-Afrikaanse Polisiediens) het gehelp. |\n| Aandagstreep – | 'n verrassing, verduideliking of ingevoegde gedagte | Hy het gewen – niemand het dit verwag nie. |\n| Beletselteken ... | 'n onvoltooide sin, 'n pouse of spanning | En toe ... gaan die ligte af. |\n\n### Die leestekens van direkte rede\n- *Pa sê: \"Ons ry môre Hartbeespoortdam toe.\"* (dubbelpunt voor; hoofletter aan die begin van die aanhaling; punt binne die aanhalingstekens)\n- *\"Ons ry môre Hartbeespoortdam toe,\" sê Pa.* (komma binne die aanhalingstekens; *sê* met 'n kleinletter)\n- *\"Kom julle saam?\" vra Ma.* (vraagteken binne die aanhalingstekens)\n- *\"As dit reën,\" sê Pa, \"bly ons tuis.\"* (die tweede deel begin met 'n kleinletter)\n- 'n Nuwe spreker begin op 'n nuwe reël.\n\n## Getalle, datums en tyd\n- Datums: *3 Oktober 2026* (die maand met 'n hoofletter).\n- Tyd: *14:30* (24-uurstelsel).\n- 'n **Desimale komma**: *3,5 kg*, *R12,50*.\n- 'n **Spasie** tussen duisende: *1 000*, *R25 000*.\n\n## Redigering in die eksamen\n1. Lees die paragraaf sin vir sin.\n2. Kontroleer in dié volgorde: hoofletters → skryftekens → leestekens → spelling (meervoude, homofone soos *lei/ly*).\n3. Skryf elke verbetering duidelik neer. As die vraag vyf foute vra, soek presies vyf.","en":"## Capital letters (hoofletters)\n\nUse a **capital letter**:\n- at the start of a sentence;\n- for **proper names**: *Thabo, Brits, Magaliesberg, Krokodilrivier*;\n- for **languages** and words derived from them: *Afrikaans, Setswana, Afrikaanse musiek*;\n- for **days and months**: *Maandag, Januarie* (but not for seasons: *somer, winter*);\n- for the first word of a **title**: *Die geheim van die ou myn*.\n\nAbbreviated titles before a name take a small letter in the middle of a sentence: *Ons het mnr. Botha en dr. Mokoena gesien.*\n\n> **Remember!** *'n* never takes a capital letter. At the start of a sentence the **next** word gets the capital: *'n Taxi het gestop.* The same applies to *'s*: *'s Middags oefen ons.*\n\n## Diacritics (skryftekens)\n\n| Diacritic | What it does | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Diaeresis** (deelteken/trema) ¨ | shows that a **new syllable** starts, so you do not read the vowels together | knieë (knie-ë), geïnteresseerd (ge-ïn-...), reünie (re-ü-nie), reën |\n| **Circumflex** (kappie) ^ | marks a long sound in certain words | môre, wêreld, sê, brûe, wîe |\n| **Acute accent** (akuutteken) ´ | emphasis or distinction | dié (this one), óf ... óf (either ... or), én ... én (both ... and) |\n| **Grave accent** (gravis) ` | distinguishes words or interjections | hè, appèl (appeal) versus appel (apple) |\n\n> **Tip:** The diaeresis goes on the **first vowel of the new syllable**: *be-ïn-druk → beïndruk*, *i-de-ë → ideë*.\n\n### Apostrophe (afkappingsteken)\n- in *'n* and *'s* (*'s middags*);\n- in the plural of words ending in a **long a, i, o or u**: *ma's, pa's, foto's, radio's, taxi's*;\n- in the plural of letter words: *SMS'e, cd's*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Afrikaans shows **possession** with *se*, not with 's: *Pieter se boek* (NOT *Pieter's boek*).\n\n### Hyphen (koppelteken)\n- in compounds with proper names: *Suid-Afrika, Wes-Kaap*;\n- with *oud-* (former) before a title: *oud-president, oud-leerder*;\n- with letters and numerals: *e-pos, SMS-boodskap, TV-program*;\n- in numbers with *en*: *een-en-twintig*;\n- to prevent **misreading** where vowels clash: *see-eend, na-aap*.\n\n## Vowel doubling and simplification\n- A **long vowel** in a **closed syllable** (ending in a consonant) is written double: *maan, boom, muur*. In an **open syllable** (ending in a vowel) it is written single: *ma-ne, bo-me, mu-re*.\n- A **short vowel** stays short when you **double** the consonant: *kat → kat-te, pot → pot-te, bus → bus-se*.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *maane* and *boome* are wrong, because *ma-* and *bo-* are already open syllables. *Pote* (with a long o) is the plural of *poot* (paw), not of *pot*.\n\n## Punctuation (leestekens)\n\n| Punctuation mark | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full stop . | end of a statement; after some abbreviations | Ons ry Pretoria toe. |\n| Comma , | in a list (not before *en*); between subordinate and main clause; around a form of address | Ek koop brood, melk en eiers. Toe die klok lui, het ons gehardloop. Thabo, kom hier! |\n| Semicolon ; | between two closely related main clauses | Dit reën; die wedstryd is uitgestel. |\n| Colon : | before a list or direct speech | Bring die volgende: 'n pen, 'n liniaal en 'n uitveër. |\n| Question mark ? | after a direct question | Wanneer begin die eksamen? |\n| Exclamation mark ! | after an exclamation or command | Eina! Gaan sit! |\n| Quotation marks \" \" | direct speech, quotations and titles | Sy sê: \"Ek is moeg.\" |\n| Brackets ( ) | extra information | Die SAPD (Suid-Afrikaanse Polisiediens) het gehelp. |\n| Dash – | a surprise, explanation or inserted thought | Hy het gewen – niemand het dit verwag nie. |\n| Ellipsis ... | an unfinished sentence, a pause or suspense | En toe ... gaan die ligte af. |\n\n### Punctuating direct speech\n- *Pa sê: \"Ons ry môre Hartbeespoortdam toe.\"* (colon before; capital letter at the start of the quotation; full stop inside the quotation marks)\n- *\"Ons ry môre Hartbeespoortdam toe,\" sê Pa.* (comma inside the quotation marks; *sê* with a small letter)\n- *\"Kom julle saam?\" vra Ma.* (question mark inside the quotation marks)\n- *\"As dit reën,\" sê Pa, \"bly ons tuis.\"* (the second part starts with a small letter)\n- A new speaker starts on a new line.\n\n## Numbers, dates and time\n- Dates: *3 Oktober 2026* (the month with a capital letter).\n- Time: *14:30* (24-hour clock).\n- A **decimal comma**: *3,5 kg*, *R12,50*.\n- A **space** between thousands: *1 000*, *R25 000*.\n\n## Editing in the exam\n1. Read the paragraph sentence by sentence.\n2. Check in this order: capitals → diacritics → punctuation → spelling (plurals, homophones such as *lei/ly*).\n3. Write each correction clearly. If the question asks for five errors, look for exactly five."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Lettergreep","en":"Syllable"},"def":{"af":"'n Deel van 'n woord wat jy in een klankstoot uitspreek, bv. *re-ü-nie* het drie lettergrepe.","en":"A part of a word that you pronounce in one beat, e.g. *re-ü-nie* has three syllables."}},{"term":{"af":"Oop en geslote lettergreep","en":"Open and closed syllable"},"def":{"af":"'n Oop lettergreep eindig op 'n klinker (*ma-ne*); 'n geslote lettergreep eindig op 'n medeklinker (*maan*).","en":"An open syllable ends in a vowel (*ma-ne*); a closed syllable ends in a consonant (*maan*)."}},{"term":{"af":"Deelteken (trema)","en":"Diaeresis"},"def":{"af":"Twee kolletjies (¨) op 'n klinker wat wys dat 'n nuwe lettergreep begin, bv. *knieë*, *reünie*.","en":"Two dots (¨) on a vowel showing that a new syllable starts, e.g. *knieë*, *reünie*."}},{"term":{"af":"Kappie (sirkumfleks)","en":"Circumflex"},"def":{"af":"Die teken ^ op 'n klinker wat 'n lang klank in sekere woorde aandui, bv. *môre*, *wêreld*.","en":"The mark ^ on a vowel that marks a long sound in certain words, e.g. *môre*, *wêreld*."}},{"term":{"af":"Akuutteken","en":"Acute accent"},"def":{"af":"Die teken ´ wat klem of onderskeid aandui, bv. *dié*, *óf ... óf*.","en":"The mark ´ that shows emphasis or distinction, e.g. *dié*, *óf ... óf*."}},{"term":{"af":"Afkappingsteken (apostrof)","en":"Apostrophe"},"def":{"af":"Die teken ' in *'n*, *'s* en in meervoude soos *foto's* en *SMS'e*.","en":"The mark ' in *'n*, *'s* and in plurals such as *foto's* and *SMS'e*."}},{"term":{"af":"Koppelteken","en":"Hyphen"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort streep wat woorddele verbind, bv. *Suid-Afrika*, *e-pos*, *see-eend*.","en":"A short line that joins parts of words, e.g. *Suid-Afrika*, *e-pos*, *see-eend*."}},{"term":{"af":"Direkte rede","en":"Direct speech"},"def":{"af":"Die presiese woorde wat iemand sê, tussen aanhalingstekens.","en":"The exact words someone says, in quotation marks."}},{"term":{"af":"Aandagstreep","en":"Dash"},"def":{"af":"'n Lang streep (–) wat 'n verrassing, verduideliking of ingevoegde gedagte inlei.","en":"A long line (–) that introduces a surprise, explanation or inserted thought."}},{"term":{"af":"Beletselteken","en":"Ellipsis"},"def":{"af":"Drie puntjies (...) wat 'n onvoltooide sin, pouse of spanning aandui.","en":"Three dots (...) showing an unfinished sentence, a pause or suspense."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Redigering: verbeter vyf foute","en":"Editing: correct five errors"},"problem":{"af":"Die paragraaf bevat vyf spel- en skryftekenfoute. Identifiseer en verbeter dit.\n\nOp maandag het ons na die skool se reunie by Hartbeespoortdam gery. Pieter's pa het al die fotos geneem. Dit was die lekkerste dag in die wereld!","en":"The paragraph contains five spelling and diacritic errors. Identify and correct them.\n\nOp maandag het ons na die skool se reunie by Hartbeespoortdam gery. Pieter's pa het al die fotos geneem. Dit was die lekkerste dag in die wereld!"},"steps":[{"af":"Hoofletters: dae van die week kry 'n hoofletter, dus *maandag* → **Maandag**.","en":"Capitals: days of the week take a capital letter, so *maandag* → **Maandag**."},{"af":"Skryftekens: in *reunie* begin die u 'n nuwe lettergreep (re-ü-nie), dus **reünie**. *Wereld* kry 'n kappie: **wêreld**.","en":"Diacritics: in *reunie* the u starts a new syllable (re-ü-nie), so **reünie**. *Wereld* takes a circumflex: **wêreld**."},{"af":"Besit: Afrikaans gebruik *se*, nie 's nie: *Pieter's pa* → **Pieter se pa**.","en":"Possession: Afrikaans uses *se*, not 's: *Pieter's pa* → **Pieter se pa**."},{"af":"Meervoud: *foto* eindig op 'n lang o, dus kry die meervoud 'n afkappingsteken: **foto's**.","en":"Plural: *foto* ends in a long o, so the plural takes an apostrophe: **foto's**."}],"answer":{"af":"Op **Maandag** het ons na die skool se **reünie** by Hartbeespoortdam gery. **Pieter se** pa het al die **foto's** geneem. Dit was die lekkerste dag in die **wêreld**!","en":"Op **Maandag** het ons na die skool se **reünie** by Hartbeespoortdam gery. **Pieter se** pa het al die **foto's** geneem. Dit was die lekkerste dag in die **wêreld**!"}},{"title":{"af":"Punktueer direkte rede","en":"Punctuate direct speech"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die gesprek oor met die korrekte leestekens en hoofletters:\n\nhoe laat begin die wedstryd vra thabo dit begin om 14:30 antwoord sy pa","en":"Rewrite the conversation with the correct punctuation and capital letters:\n\nhoe laat begin die wedstryd vra thabo dit begin om 14:30 antwoord sy pa"},"steps":[{"af":"Vind die presiese woorde wat gesê word: *Hoe laat begin die wedstryd* ('n vraag) en *Dit begin om 14:30* ('n stelling).","en":"Find the exact words that are spoken: *Hoe laat begin die wedstryd* (a question) and *Dit begin om 14:30* (a statement)."},{"af":"Eerste spreker: hoofletter aan die begin, vraagteken binne die aanhalingstekens, *vra* met 'n kleinletter en *Thabo* met 'n hoofletter (eienaam): *\"Hoe laat begin die wedstryd?\" vra Thabo.*","en":"First speaker: capital at the start, question mark inside the quotation marks, *vra* with a small letter and *Thabo* with a capital (proper name): *\"Hoe laat begin die wedstryd?\" vra Thabo.*"},{"af":"Tweede spreker op 'n nuwe reël: die stelling eindig met 'n komma binne die aanhalingstekens omdat *antwoord sy pa* volg: *\"Dit begin om 14:30,\" antwoord sy pa.*","en":"Second speaker on a new line: the statement ends with a comma inside the quotation marks because *antwoord sy pa* follows: *\"Dit begin om 14:30,\" antwoord sy pa.*"}],"answer":{"af":"\"Hoe laat begin die wedstryd?\" vra Thabo.\n\"Dit begin om 14:30,\" antwoord sy pa.","en":"\"Hoe laat begin die wedstryd?\" vra Thabo.\n\"Dit begin om 14:30,\" antwoord sy pa."}},{"title":{"af":"Meervoude en skryftekens","en":"Plurals and diacritics"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van elke woord en verduidelik die reël: (a) knie (b) radio (c) maan (d) kat","en":"Write the plural of each word and explain the rule: (a) knie (b) radio (c) maan (d) kat"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *knie* + e → **knieë**. Die deelteken wys dat die ë 'n nuwe lettergreep begin: *knie-ë*.","en":"(a) *knie* + e → **knieë**. The diaeresis shows that the ë starts a new syllable: *knie-ë*."},{"af":"(b) *radio* eindig op 'n lang o → **radio's**. Sonder die afkappingsteken sou jy *ra-di-os* met 'n kort o lees.","en":"(b) *radio* ends in a long o → **radio's**. Without the apostrophe you would read *ra-di-os* with a short o."},{"af":"(c) *maan* → *ma-ne*: die eerste lettergreep is nou oop, dus net een a: **mane**.","en":"(c) *maan* → *ma-ne*: the first syllable is now open, so only one a: **mane**."},{"af":"(d) *kat* het 'n kort a. Verdubbel die t sodat die lettergreep geslote bly: *kat-te* → **katte**.","en":"(d) *kat* has a short a. Double the t so that the syllable stays closed: *kat-te* → **katte**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) knieë (b) radio's (c) mane (d) katte","en":"(a) knieë (b) radio's (c) mane (d) katte"}},{"title":{"af":"Getalle, datums en koppeltekens","en":"Numbers, dates and hyphens"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf elke sin korrek:\n(a) Die span het R1,250.75 ingesamel.\n(b) Die konsert is op 3 oktober om 2:30 nm.\n(c) Ek stuur vir jou 'n epos uit Suid Afrika.","en":"Rewrite each sentence correctly:\n(a) Die span het R1,250.75 ingesamel.\n(b) Die konsert is op 3 oktober om 2:30 nm.\n(c) Ek stuur vir jou 'n epos uit Suid Afrika."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Afrikaans gebruik 'n spasie tussen duisende en 'n desimale komma: **R1 250,75**.","en":"(a) Afrikaans uses a space between thousands and a decimal comma: **R1 250,75**."},{"af":"(b) Maande kry 'n hoofletter (**Oktober**), en 2:30 nm. in die 24-uurstelsel is **14:30**.","en":"(b) Months take a capital letter (**Oktober**), and 2:30 p.m. (nm.) on the 24-hour clock is **14:30**."},{"af":"(c) 'n Letter + woord kry 'n koppelteken (**e-pos**), en so ook die samestelling met 'n eienaam (**Suid-Afrika**).","en":"(c) A letter + word takes a hyphen (**e-pos**), and so does the compound with a proper name (**Suid-Afrika**)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Die span het R1 250,75 ingesamel. (b) Die konsert is op 3 Oktober om 14:30. (c) Ek stuur vir jou 'n e-pos uit Suid-Afrika.","en":"(a) Die span het R1 250,75 ingesamel. (b) Die konsert is op 3 Oktober om 14:30. (c) Ek stuur vir jou 'n e-pos uit Suid-Afrika."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die korrekte hoofletters?","en":"Which sentence has the correct capital letters?"},"options":[{"af":"Ons ry in die Somer Hartbeespoortdam toe.","en":"Ons ry in die Somer Hartbeespoortdam toe."},{"af":"Thabo praat vlot afrikaans en Setswana.","en":"Thabo praat vlot afrikaans en Setswana."},{"af":"Ons het Mnr. Botha in brits gesien.","en":"Ons het Mnr. Botha in brits gesien."},{"af":"'n Taxi het op Maandag voor die skool gestop.","en":"'n Taxi het op Maandag voor die skool gestop."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*'n* kry nooit 'n hoofletter nie, dus kry die volgende woord (*Taxi*) dit, en dae van die week kry 'n hoofletter (*Maandag*). Seisoene kry nie 'n hoofletter nie (*somer*), tale wel (*Afrikaans*), en in die middel van 'n sin skryf jy *mnr.* klein en *Brits* (eienaam) met 'n hoofletter.","en":"*'n* never takes a capital letter, so the next word (*Taxi*) gets it, and days of the week take a capital (*Maandag*). Seasons do not take a capital (*somer*), languages do (*Afrikaans*), and in the middle of a sentence you write *mnr.* small and *Brits* (a proper name) with a capital."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die tekentjie op die ï in *geïnteresseerd* word 'n ___ genoem.","en":"The mark on the ï in *geïnteresseerd* is called a ___ (Afrikaans term)."},"answers":{"af":["deelteken","trema"],"en":["deelteken","trema","diaeresis"]},"explain":{"af":"Die deelteken (trema) wys dat die ï 'n nuwe lettergreep begin: *ge-ïn-te-res-seerd*. Sonder dit sou jy die *ei* soos in *klein* lees.","en":"The diaeresis (*deelteken* or *trema*) shows that the ï starts a new syllable: *ge-ïn-te-res-seerd*. Without it you would read the *ei* as in *klein*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["kappie","akuutteken","afkappingsteken"],"en":["kappie","akuutteken","afkappingsteken"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In Afrikaans wys jy besit met *se* en nie met 's nie: *Pieter se boek*.","en":"In Afrikaans you show possession with *se* and not with 's: *Pieter se boek*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Pieter's boek* is 'n Engelse konstruksie. In Afrikaans skryf jy *Pieter se boek*, *die skool se span*.","en":"True. *Pieter's boek* is an English construction. In Afrikaans you write *Pieter se boek*, *die skool se span*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter sin is die komma korrek gebruik?","en":"In which sentence is the comma used correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo bring, asseblief jou boeke saam.","en":"Thabo bring, asseblief jou boeke saam."},{"af":"Thabo, bring asseblief jou boeke saam.","en":"Thabo, bring asseblief jou boeke saam."},{"af":"Toe die klok lui het, ons gehardloop.","en":"Toe die klok lui het, ons gehardloop."},{"af":"Ons het, gehardloop toe die klok lui.","en":"Ons het, gehardloop toe die klok lui."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Aanspreekvorm (die naam van die persoon met wie jy praat) word met 'n komma van die res van die sin geskei. In die derde sin moet die komma ná *lui* kom: *Toe die klok lui, het ons gehardloop.*","en":"A form of address (the name of the person you are speaking to) is separated from the rest of the sentence by a comma. In the third sentence the comma must come after *lui*: *Toe die klok lui, het ons gehardloop.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van *foto*: ___","en":"Write the plural of *foto*: ___"},"answers":{"af":["foto's","foto’s"],"en":["foto's","foto’s"]},"explain":{"af":"Woorde wat op 'n lang a, i, o of u eindig, kry 's in die meervoud: *foto's, radio's, ma's*. Sonder die afkappingsteken sou jy *fo-tos* met 'n kort o lees.","en":"Words ending in a long a, i, o or u take 's in the plural: *foto's, radio's, ma's*. Without the apostrophe you would read *fo-tos* with a short o."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["fotos","fotoë","fotose"],"en":["fotos","fotoë","fotose"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke skryfteken by die woord waarin dit voorkom.","en":"Match each diacritic or mark to the word in which it appears."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Deelteken","en":"Diaeresis (deelteken)"},"r":{"af":"reünie","en":"reünie"}},{"l":{"af":"Kappie","en":"Circumflex (kappie)"},"r":{"af":"wêreld","en":"wêreld"}},{"l":{"af":"Akuutteken","en":"Acute accent (akuutteken)"},"r":{"af":"dié","en":"dié"}},{"l":{"af":"Afkappingsteken","en":"Apostrophe (afkappingsteken)"},"r":{"af":"ma's","en":"ma's"}},{"l":{"af":"Koppelteken","en":"Hyphen (koppelteken)"},"r":{"af":"see-eend","en":"see-eend"}}],"explain":{"af":"Deelteken: nuwe lettergreep (re-ü-nie). Kappie: lang klank (wêreld). Akuutteken: klem (dié). Afkappingsteken: meervoud ná 'n lang klinker (ma's). Koppelteken: voorkom verkeerde lees (see-eend).","en":"Diaeresis: new syllable (re-ü-nie). Circumflex: long sound (wêreld). Acute accent: emphasis (dié). Apostrophe: plural after a long vowel (ma's). Hyphen: prevents misreading (see-eend)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die meervoud van *boom*?","en":"What is the plural of *boom* (tree)?"},"options":[{"af":"boome","en":"boome"},{"af":"bomme","en":"bomme"},{"af":"bome","en":"bome"},{"af":"booms","en":"booms"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"In *bo-me* eindig die eerste lettergreep op 'n klinker (oop lettergreep), dus word die lang o enkel geskryf. *Boome* is 'n algemene fout, en *bomme* is die meervoud van *bom*.","en":"In *bo-me* the first syllable ends in a vowel (open syllable), so the long o is written single. *Boome* is a common mistake, and *bomme* is the plural of *bom* (bomb)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *Ons het brood, melk, en eiers gekoop.* is korrek gepunktueer.","en":"The sentence *Ons het brood, melk, en eiers gekoop.* is correctly punctuated."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. In 'n lys kom daar nie 'n komma voor *en* nie: *Ons het brood, melk en eiers gekoop.*","en":"False. In a list there is no comma before *en* (and): *Ons het brood, melk en eiers gekoop.*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waarom kry *beïndruk* 'n deelteken?","en":"Why does *beïndruk* (impress) take a diaeresis?"},"options":[{"af":"Om te wys dat die ï 'n nuwe lettergreep begin (be-ïn-druk).","en":"To show that the ï starts a new syllable (be-ïn-druk)."},{"af":"Om die i-klank langer te maak.","en":"To make the i sound longer."},{"af":"Om klem op die woord te lê.","en":"To put emphasis on the word."},{"af":"Omdat dit 'n meervoudsvorm is.","en":"Because it is a plural form."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sonder die deelteken sou jy *bei-* soos in *beitel* lees. Die deelteken skei die klinkers sodat *be-* en *-ïn-* aparte lettergrepe is. 'n Lang klank word met 'n kappie aangedui, en klem met 'n akuutteken.","en":"Without the diaeresis you would read *bei-* as in *beitel*. The diaeresis separates the vowels so that *be-* and *-ïn-* are separate syllables. A long sound is marked with a circumflex, and emphasis with an acute accent."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die woord tussen hakies met die korrekte skryfteken: *Die wedstryd is ___ om 15:00.* (more)","en":"Write the word in brackets with the correct diacritic: *Die wedstryd is ___ om 15:00.* (more)"},"answers":{"af":["môre"],"en":["môre"]},"explain":{"af":"*Môre* (tomorrow) kry 'n kappie op die o. 'n Deelteken (*möre*) of gravis (*mòre*) is verkeerd.","en":"*Môre* (tomorrow) takes a circumflex on the o. A diaeresis (*möre*) or grave accent (*mòre*) is wrong."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["more","möre","mòre"],"en":["more","möre","mòre"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van *pot*: ___","en":"Write the plural of *pot*: ___"},"answers":{"af":["potte"],"en":["potte"]},"explain":{"af":"Die o in *pot* is kort. Om dit kort te hou, verdubbel jy die t: *pot-te*. *Pote* (met 'n lang o) is die meervoud van *poot*.","en":"The o in *pot* is short. To keep it short, you double the t: *pot-te*. *Pote* (with a long o) is the plural of *poot* (paw)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["pote","pots","potse"],"en":["pote","pots","potse"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is korrek geskryf?","en":"Which word is written correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"seeeend","en":"seeeend"},{"af":"see eend","en":"see eend"},{"af":"see-eend","en":"see-eend"},{"af":"seë-eend","en":"seë-eend"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die koppelteken skei die botsende klinkers sodat jy die woord nie verkeerd lees nie: *see-eend*. *Na-aap* werk op dieselfde manier. Dit is een woord, dus nie *see eend* nie.","en":"The hyphen separates the clashing vowels so that you do not misread the word: *see-eend* (sea duck). *Na-aap* works the same way. It is one word, so not *see eend*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi met die korrekte meervoud: *Ek het vandag drie ___ gestuur.* (SMS)","en":"Complete with the correct plural: *Ek het vandag drie ___ gestuur.* (SMS)"},"answers":{"af":["SMS'e","SMS’e"],"en":["SMS'e","SMS’e"]},"explain":{"af":"Letterwoorde kry 'n afkappingsteken voor die meervoudsuitgang. *SMS* eindig op 'n s-klank (es-em-es), dus kry dit -e: *SMS'e*. Vergelyk *cd's*.","en":"Letter words take an apostrophe before the plural ending. *SMS* ends in an s sound (es-em-es), so it takes -e: *SMS'e*. Compare *cd's*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["SMS's","SMSe","SMS'es"],"en":["SMS's","SMSe","SMS'es"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek volgens die Afrikaanse reëls vir getalle?","en":"Which sentence is correct according to the Afrikaans rules for numbers?"},"options":[{"af":"Die saal het plek vir 1,000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45,50.","en":"Die saal het plek vir 1,000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45,50."},{"af":"Die saal het plek vir 1 000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45,50.","en":"Die saal het plek vir 1 000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45,50."},{"af":"Die saal het plek vir 1 000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45.50.","en":"Die saal het plek vir 1 000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45.50."},{"af":"Die saal het plek vir 1.000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45.50.","en":"Die saal het plek vir 1.000 mense en 'n kaartjie kos R45.50."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Afrikaans gebruik 'n **spasie** tussen duisende (*1 000*) en 'n **desimale komma** (*R45,50*). *1,000* sou in Afrikaans 'een komma nul nul nul' beteken.","en":"Afrikaans uses a **space** between thousands (*1 000*) and a **decimal comma** (*R45,50*). *1,000* would mean 'one comma zero zero zero' in Afrikaans."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is heeltemal korrek?","en":"Which sentence is completely correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato sê die ouers is geinteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's.","en":"Lerato sê die ouers is geinteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's."},{"af":"Lerato se die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's.","en":"Lerato se die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's."},{"af":"Lerato sê die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool's nuwe kamera's.","en":"Lerato sê die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool's nuwe kamera's."},{"af":"Lerato sê die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's.","en":"Lerato sê die ouers is geïnteresseerd in die skool se nuwe kamera's."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die laaste sin is reg: *sê* (praat) kry 'n kappie, *geïnteresseerd* 'n deelteken, besit gebruik *se* (sonder kappie), en *kamera's* 'n afkappingsteken. Die ander sinne het elk een fout: *geinteresseerd*, *se* in plaas van *sê*, en *skool's*.","en":"The last sentence is correct: *sê* (says) takes a circumflex, *geïnteresseerd* a diaeresis, possession uses *se* (no circumflex), and *kamera's* an apostrophe. The other sentences each have one error: *geinteresseerd*, *se* instead of *sê*, and *skool's*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Redigeer die sin: *die wereld is so mooi vandag se thabo.* Watter weergawe is heeltemal korrek?","en":"Edit the sentence: *die wereld is so mooi vandag se thabo.* Which version is completely correct?"},"options":[{"af":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag,\" sê Thabo.","en":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag,\" sê Thabo."},{"af":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag,\" se Thabo.","en":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag,\" se Thabo."},{"af":"\"Die wereld is so mooi vandag,\" sê Thabo.","en":"\"Die wereld is so mooi vandag,\" sê Thabo."},{"af":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag.\" Sê Thabo.","en":"\"Die wêreld is so mooi vandag.\" Sê Thabo."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste weergawe is heeltemal reg: aanhalingstekens om die gesproke woorde, hoofletter *Die*, kappie op *wêreld*, komma binne die aanhalingstekens, *sê* met 'n kappie en kleinletter, en *Thabo* met 'n hoofletter. Die laaste opsie gebruik 'n punt en 'n hoofletter by *Sê*, wat verkeerd is.","en":"The first version is completely correct: quotation marks around the spoken words, capital *Die*, circumflex on *wêreld*, comma inside the quotation marks, *sê* with a circumflex and small letter, and *Thabo* with a capital. The last option uses a full stop and a capital on *Sê*, which is wrong."}}]}]}]},"english":{"id":"english","grade":10,"name":{"af":"Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal","en":"English First Additional Language"},"short":{"af":"Eng","en":"Eng"},"icon":"🗣️","color":"#dc2626","intro":{"af":"Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal in Graad 10 bou die Engels wat jy vir skool, studie en werk nodig het: leesbegrip, woordsoorte, tye en kongruensie, die opsomming, lydende vorm en indirekte rede, sinsbou en leestekens, woordeskat en kritiese taalbewustheid, visuele geletterdheid en letterkunde (roman en kortverhaal, poësie en drama). Jy skryf ook opstelle, briewe, 'n CV en ander transaksionele tekste. Die Novembereksamen dek die hele jaar in drie vraestelle: V1 Taal (80), V2 Letterkunde (70) en V3 Skryfwerk (100).","en":"English First Additional Language in Grade 10 builds the English you need for school, study and work: comprehension, parts of speech, tenses and concord, the summary, passive voice and reported speech, sentence structure and punctuation, vocabulary and critical language awareness, visual literacy and literature (novel and short story, poetry and drama). You also write essays, letters, a CV and other transactional texts. The November exam covers the whole year in three papers: P1 Language (80), P2 Literature (70) and P3 Writing (100)."},"examTips":[{"af":"V1: lees die vrae voor die leesstuk sodat jy weet waarna jy soek; haal aan as die vraag \"quote\" sê en gebruik jou eie woorde as dit \"explain\" sê.","en":"P1: read the questions before the passage so you know what to look for; quote when the question says \"quote\" and use your own words when it says \"explain\"."},{"af":"Opsomming: lys presies SEWE punte in volsinne, in jou eie woorde, genommer, en bly binne die woordgrens.","en":"Summary: list exactly SEVEN points in full sentences, in your own words, numbered, and stay within the word limit."},{"af":"Taalvrae: skryf die hele sin oor en kontroleer die tyd en kongruensie – in die lydende vorm bly die tyd dieselfde (\"She writes the letter\" → \"The letter is written by her\").","en":"Language questions: rewrite the whole sentence and check tense and concord – in the passive the tense stays the same (\"She writes the letter\" → \"The letter is written by her\")."},{"af":"V2: ken die intrige, karakters, konflik, ruimte en temas van jou voorgeskrewe werke, en staaf elke antwoord met bewyse uit die teks.","en":"P2: know the plot, characters, conflict, setting and themes of your set works, and support every answer with evidence from the text."},{"af":"V3: beplan voor jy skryf, gebruik die regte formaat vir elke transaksionele teks (adres, datum, aanhef, onderwerplyn) en hou by die woordtelling (opstel 150–200 woorde).","en":"P3: plan before you write, use the correct format for each transactional text (address, date, greeting, subject line) and keep to the word count (essay 150–200 words)."}],"resources":[{"title":{"af":"Departement van Basiese Onderwys (DBE)","en":"Department of Basic Education (DBE)"},"url":"https://www.education.gov.za","note":{"af":"CAPS-dokument vir Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal, eksamenriglyne en vorige NSS-vraestelle met memorandums – goed om die vraagstyl te leer ken.","en":"CAPS document for English First Additional Language, exam guidelines and past NSC papers with memos – good for learning the question style."}},{"title":{"af":"Thutong-onderwysportaal","en":"Thutong Education Portal"},"url":"https://www.thutong.doe.gov.za","note":{"af":"Die DBE se gratis onderwysportaal met leer- en hersieningsmateriaal per vak en graad.","en":"The DBE's free education portal with learning and revision material by subject and grade."}}],"examFormat":{"af":"## Engels Eerste Addisionele Taal-eksamen Graad 10\n\n**Drie vraestelle, 250 punte** volgens die CAPS/DBE-patroon (*skatting – bevestig met Hoërskool Brits se 2026-afbakening*). Mondeling is deel van die SBA.\n\n| Vraestel | Afdelings | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| V1: Taal in konteks (2 uur) | A Leesbegrip 30, B Opsomming 10, C Taalstrukture en -konvensies 40 | 80 |\n| V2: Letterkunde | Beantwoord TWEE van: roman, drama, kortverhale, poësie (35 punte elk) | 70 |\n| V3: Skryfwerk | A Opstel 50 (150–200 woorde), B langer transaksionele teks 30 (120–150 woorde), C korter teks 20 (80–100 woorde) | 100 |\n\n### Wat om te verwag\n\n- **V1:** 'n leesstuk van 400–600 woorde, dikwels met 'n grafiek of tabel; in Afdeling C 'n advertensie (±10), 'n spotprent of strokiesprent (±10) en taal in konteks (±20).\n- **V2:** kontekstuele vrae op uittreksels – feite, karakters, konflik, temas en jou eie mening met bewyse.\n- **V3:** verhalende, beskrywende, argumenterende of besprekende opstelle; briewe, 'n CV met dekbrief, verslae, toesprake, advertensies, dagboekinskrywings en uitnodigings.\n\n### Wenke\n\n1. Lees die keuses in V2 en V3 eers deur voor jy begin.\n2. Verdeel jou tyd volgens die punte.","en":"## English First Additional Language exam Grade 10\n\n**Three papers, 250 marks** following the CAPS/DBE pattern (*estimate – confirm with Hoërskool Brits's 2026 scope*). Orals are part of SBA.\n\n| Paper | Sections | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| P1: Language in context (2 hours) | A Comprehension 30, B Summary 10, C Language structures and conventions 40 | 80 |\n| P2: Literature | Answer TWO of: novel, drama, short stories, poetry (35 marks each) | 70 |\n| P3: Writing | A Essay 50 (150–200 words), B longer transactional text 30 (120–150 words), C shorter text 20 (80–100 words) | 100 |\n\n### What to expect\n\n- **P1:** a passage of 400–600 words, often with a graph or table; in Section C an advertisement (±10), a cartoon or comic strip (±10) and language in context (±20).\n- **P2:** contextual questions on extracts – facts, characters, conflict, themes and your own opinion with evidence.\n- **P3:** narrative, descriptive, argumentative or discursive essays; letters, a CV with covering letter, reports, speeches, adverts, diary entries and invitations.\n\n### Tips\n\n1. Read through the choices in P2 and P3 before you start.\n2. Divide your time according to the marks."},"terms":[{"term":1,"title":{"af":"Leesbegrip, woordsoorte, tye en die opstel","en":"Comprehension, parts of speech, tenses and the essay"},"topics":[{"id":"eng10-t1-comprehension","title":{"af":"Leesbegrip","en":"Reading comprehension"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n leesstuk en 'n visuele teks vinnig kan deurwerk en elke vraagtipe – van aanhalings tot toon en feit/mening – volgens die puntetoekenning kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to work through a passage and a visual text quickly and answer every question type – from quotations to tone and fact/opinion – according to the mark allocation."},"summary":{"af":"## Vraestel 1: Taal in konteks\n\nVraestel 1 (*Paper 1: Language in context*) tel **80 punte** en duur **2 uur**.\n\n| Afdeling | Inhoud | Punte |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Leesbegrip (*comprehension*) | 30 |\n| B | Opsomming (*summary*) | 10 |\n| C | Taalstrukture en -konvensies: advertensie (±10), spotprent of strokiesprent (±10), taal in konteks/redigering (±20) | 40 |\n\nIn Afdeling A kry jy 'n leesstuk van **400–600 woorde** – 'n artikel, onderhoud of blog – dikwels saam met 'n **visuele teks**: 'n grafiek, tabel, infografika of foto. Die vrae oor die visuele teks toets of jy dit kan lees **en** aan die leesstuk kan koppel.\n\n> **Wenk:** Verdeel jou tyd volgens die punte. Afdeling A is 30 van die 80 punte, dus ongeveer 45 van die 120 minute.\n\n## Leesstrategieë\n\n1. **Lees die vrae eerste.** Dan weet jy waarna jy soek terwyl jy lees.\n2. **Vluglees (*skimming*):** lees vinnig vir die hoofgedagte – titel, eerste en laaste paragraaf, eerste sin van elke paragraaf.\n3. **Soeklees (*scanning*):** soek 'n spesifieke feit, naam, getal of sleutelwoord uit die vraag.\n4. **Noukeurige lees:** lees die regte paragraaf stadig voordat jy antwoord.\n5. **Gebruik die puntetoekenning:** *(2)* beteken twee punte, dus twee feite, of 'n feit plus 'n rede.\n6. **Antwoord in volsinne**, behalwe as die vraag net een woord, 'n aanhaling of 'n letter vra.\n\n## Vraagtipes en hoe jy antwoord\n\n| Vraag | Wat jy doen |\n|---|---|\n| *List / Name / State* | Letterlik: gee die feite kort, soos dit in die teks staan. |\n| *Quote* | Skryf die presiese woorde in **aanhalingstekens**: \"…\". *Quote ONE word* = net een woord. |\n| *In your own words* | Verduidelik die betekenis sonder om die teks se woorde oor te skryf. |\n| *Give a reason / Why?* | Antwoord met *because …* |\n| *True or false? Quote to support* | Skryf *True/False* **en** die aanhaling. Sonder die aanhaling kry jy gewoonlik geen punt nie. |\n| *Multiple choice* | Skryf die letter en die antwoord: *C – to persuade*. |\n| *Reference* | *What does \"it\" in line 5 refer to?* Lees terug: die voornaamwoord verwys na 'n selfstandige naamwoord kort daarvoor. |\n| *Vocabulary in context* | Gee 'n sinoniem (dieselfde betekenis), antoniem (teenoorgestelde) of die betekenis – lees die sinne rondom die woord. |\n| *Figure of speech* | Benoem die stylfiguur (bv. *metaphor*), verduidelik die vergelyking **en** die effek. |\n\n### Toon, doel, feit en mening\n\n- **Toon** (*tone*) is die skrywer se houding, wat jy aan die woordkeuse herken: *sarcastic, concerned, admiring, critical, humorous, angry*. Gee een woord plus bewys uit die teks.\n- **Doel** (*purpose*): om in te lig (*to inform*), te oorreed (*to persuade*) of te vermaak (*to entertain*). Die gebiedende wys (*Join us!*) en *you* wys op oorreding.\n- **'n Feit** (*fact*) kan bewys of nagegaan word: *The clean-up started at 07:00.*\n- **'n Mening** (*opinion*) is 'n gevoel of oordeel: *It was the best event of the year.* Woorde soos *I think, best, should, amazing* dui gewoonlik op 'n mening.\n\n### Evaluerende vrae\n\n*Do you agree? Give a reason.* Kies **een** kant (*Yes* of *No*) en gee 'n oortuigende rede wat by die teks aansluit. *Yes* sonder 'n rede kry nul.\n\n*Is the title suitable?* of *How does the visual text support the passage?* Wys die **verband**: noem iets wat in albei voorkom.\n\n### 'n Grafiek of tabel lees\n\nLees die opskrif, die kolomopskrifte en die eenhede (persentasie of getal?) **voordat** jy antwoord. Vergelyk waardes versigtig: *most, fewest, more than half*. Antwoord net uit die gegewens – nie uit wat jy dink nie.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Om meer aan te haal as wat gevra word. *Quote a phrase* is 'n paar woorde, nie die hele sin nie. *Quote ONE word* is een woord.\n\n- Die teks oorskryf wanneer *own words* gevra word.\n- Uit algemene kennis antwoord in plaas van uit die teks.\n- Reëlnommers (*line numbers*) en paragraafnommers ignoreer en in die verkeerde deel soek.\n- Te min punte gee: 'n vraag van (3) wil drie punte hê.\n- 'n Waar/onwaar-vraag sonder aanhaling of rede beantwoord.\n\n> **Onthou!** Elke antwoord moet uit die **teks** kom en by die **puntetoekenning** pas. Lees die vraag twee keer: wat is die opdragwoord?","en":"## Paper 1: Language in context\n\nPaper 1 is worth **80 marks** and lasts **2 hours**.\n\n| Section | Content | Marks |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | Comprehension | 30 |\n| B | Summary | 10 |\n| C | Language structures and conventions: advertisement (±10), cartoon or comic strip (±10), language in context/editing (±20) | 40 |\n\nIn Section A you get a **400–600-word** passage – an article, interview or blog – often with a **visual text**: a graph, table, infographic or photo. The questions on the visual text test whether you can read it **and** link it to the passage.\n\n> **Tip:** Divide your time according to the marks. Section A is 30 of the 80 marks, so roughly 45 of the 120 minutes.\n\n## Reading strategies\n\n1. **Read the questions first.** Then you know what to look for while you read.\n2. **Skimming:** read quickly for the main idea – title, first and last paragraph, first sentence of each paragraph.\n3. **Scanning:** look for a specific fact, name, number or keyword from the question.\n4. **Close reading:** read the right paragraph slowly before you answer.\n5. **Use the mark allocation:** *(2)* means two marks, so two facts, or one fact plus a reason.\n6. **Answer in full sentences**, unless the question asks for only one word, a quotation or a letter.\n\n## Question types and how to answer\n\n| Question | What you do |\n|---|---|\n| *List / Name / State* | Literal: give the facts briefly, as they appear in the text. |\n| *Quote* | Write the exact words in **inverted commas**: \"…\". *Quote ONE word* = only one word. |\n| *In your own words* | Explain the meaning without copying the words of the text. |\n| *Give a reason / Why?* | Answer with *because …* |\n| *True or false? Quote to support* | Write *True/False* **and** the quotation. Without the quotation you usually get no mark. |\n| *Multiple choice* | Write the letter and the answer: *C – to persuade*. |\n| *Reference* | *What does \"it\" in line 5 refer to?* Read back: the pronoun refers to a noun shortly before it. |\n| *Vocabulary in context* | Give a synonym (same meaning), antonym (opposite) or the meaning – read the sentences around the word. |\n| *Figure of speech* | Name the figure of speech (e.g. *metaphor*), explain the comparison **and** the effect. |\n\n### Tone, purpose, fact and opinion\n\n- **Tone** is the writer's attitude, which you recognise from the word choice: *sarcastic, concerned, admiring, critical, humorous, angry*. Give one word plus proof from the text.\n- **Purpose**: to inform, to persuade or to entertain. The imperative (*Join us!*) and *you* point to persuasion.\n- **A fact** can be proved or checked: *The clean-up started at 07:00.*\n- **An opinion** is a feeling or judgement: *It was the best event of the year.* Words such as *I think, best, should, amazing* usually signal an opinion.\n\n### Evaluative questions\n\n*Do you agree? Give a reason.* Choose **one** side (*Yes* or *No*) and give a convincing reason that links to the text. *Yes* without a reason earns nothing.\n\n*Is the title suitable?* or *How does the visual text support the passage?* Show the **link**: mention something that appears in both.\n\n### Reading a graph or table\n\nRead the heading, the column headings and the units (percentage or number?) **before** you answer. Compare values carefully: *most, fewest, more than half*. Answer only from the data – not from what you think.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n> **Common mistake:** Quoting more than you are asked to. *Quote a phrase* is a few words, not the whole sentence. *Quote ONE word* is one word.\n\n- Copying the text when *own words* is asked.\n- Answering from general knowledge instead of from the text.\n- Ignoring line numbers and paragraph numbers and searching in the wrong part.\n- Giving too few points: a (3)-mark question wants three points.\n- Answering a true/false question without a quotation or reason.\n\n> **Remember!** Every answer must come from the **text** and fit the **mark allocation**. Read the question twice: what is the command word?"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Leesbegrip","en":"Comprehension"},"def":{"af":"Om 'n teks te lees, te verstaan en vrae daaroor te beantwoord – Afdeling A van Vraestel 1 (30 punte).","en":"Reading a text, understanding it and answering questions on it – Section A of Paper 1 (30 marks)."}},{"term":{"af":"Vluglees","en":"Skimming"},"def":{"af":"Vinnig deur 'n teks lees om die hoofgedagte te kry.","en":"Reading through a text quickly to get the main idea."}},{"term":{"af":"Soeklees","en":"Scanning"},"def":{"af":"'n Teks deursoek vir 'n spesifieke feit, naam, getal of sleutelwoord.","en":"Searching a text for a specific fact, name, number or keyword."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhaling","en":"Quotation"},"def":{"af":"Die presiese woorde uit die teks, tussen aanhalingstekens geskryf.","en":"The exact words from the text, written in inverted commas."}},{"term":{"af":"Eie woorde","en":"Own words"},"def":{"af":"Die betekenis van die teks verduidelik sonder om die skrywer se woorde oor te skryf.","en":"Explaining the meaning of the text without copying the writer's words."}},{"term":{"af":"Toon","en":"Tone"},"def":{"af":"Die skrywer se houding teenoor die onderwerp, wat uit sy of haar woordkeuse blyk, bv. sarkasties of besorg.","en":"The writer's attitude towards the subject, shown by word choice, e.g. sarcastic or concerned."}},{"term":{"af":"Doel van die teks","en":"Purpose of the text"},"def":{"af":"Waarom die teks geskryf is: om in te lig, te oorreed of te vermaak.","en":"Why the text was written: to inform, to persuade or to entertain."}},{"term":{"af":"Feit","en":"Fact"},"def":{"af":"'n Stelling wat bewys of nagegaan kan word.","en":"A statement that can be proved or checked."}},{"term":{"af":"Mening","en":"Opinion"},"def":{"af":"'n Persoonlike gevoel, oortuiging of oordeel wat nie bewys kan word nie.","en":"A personal feeling, belief or judgement that cannot be proved."}},{"term":{"af":"Visuele teks","en":"Visual text"},"def":{"af":"'n Teks wat inligting deur beelde, grafieke, tabelle of infografika oordra, dikwels saam met die leesstuk.","en":"A text that conveys information through images, graphs, tables or infographics, often with the passage."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Letterlike vrae, aanhaling, verwysing en eie woorde","en":"Literal questions, quotation, reference and own words"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die artikel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Hands for Harties*\n\n(1) At seven o'clock on Saturday morning, more than eighty volunteers gathered at the Hartbeespoort Dam wall. They came from schools, churches and local businesses, and each person was handed a pair of gloves and a stack of black bags.\n\n(2) The volunteers worked in teams along the shoreline. Plastic bottles, chip packets and fishing line were the most common items they found. \"Fishing line is the worst,\" said team leader Naledi Khumalo. \"Birds get tangled in it and cannot fly.\" By midday the teams had filled 300 bags. They loaded them onto a truck from a local recycling company.\n\n(3) Organiser Pieter Botha believes the morning was worth every minute. \"The water's edge looked spotless when we left. If every visitor took their rubbish home, we would not need to do this at all,\" he said.\n\n1.1 Name TWO groups of people that the volunteers came from. (2)\n1.2 Quote ONE word from paragraph 3 which shows that the shoreline was very clean. (1)\n1.3 What does \"them\" in paragraph 2 refer to? (1)\n1.4 Why does Naledi say that fishing line is \"the worst\"? Answer in your own words. (2)","en":"Read the article and answer the questions.\n\n*Hands for Harties*\n\n(1) At seven o'clock on Saturday morning, more than eighty volunteers gathered at the Hartbeespoort Dam wall. They came from schools, churches and local businesses, and each person was handed a pair of gloves and a stack of black bags.\n\n(2) The volunteers worked in teams along the shoreline. Plastic bottles, chip packets and fishing line were the most common items they found. \"Fishing line is the worst,\" said team leader Naledi Khumalo. \"Birds get tangled in it and cannot fly.\" By midday the teams had filled 300 bags. They loaded them onto a truck from a local recycling company.\n\n(3) Organiser Pieter Botha believes the morning was worth every minute. \"The water's edge looked spotless when we left. If every visitor took their rubbish home, we would not need to do this at all,\" he said.\n\n1.1 Name TWO groups of people that the volunteers came from. (2)\n1.2 Quote ONE word from paragraph 3 which shows that the shoreline was very clean. (1)\n1.3 What does \"them\" in paragraph 2 refer to? (1)\n1.4 Why does Naledi say that fishing line is \"the worst\"? Answer in your own words. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"1.1 (2 punte = twee feite.) Soeklees na *came from* in paragraaf 1. Die lys volg direk: *schools, churches and local businesses*. Enige TWEE: **They came from schools and churches.**","en":"1.1 (2 marks = two facts.) Scan for *came from* in paragraph 1. The list follows straight after: *schools, churches and local businesses*. Any TWO: **They came from schools and churches.**"},{"af":"1.2 *Quote ONE word* – net een woord, in aanhalingstekens, uit paragraaf 3: **\"spotless\"**. As jy *\"The water's edge looked spotless\"* skryf, verloor jy die punt omdat jy meer as een woord aangehaal het.","en":"1.2 *Quote ONE word* – only one word, in inverted commas, from paragraph 3: **\"spotless\"**. If you write *\"The water's edge looked spotless\"*, you lose the mark because you quoted more than one word."},{"af":"1.3 Verwysing: lees terug na die selfstandige naamwoord vóór *them*: *By midday the teams had filled 300 bags. They loaded them …* Die *volunteers* laai, so *them* is nie die mense nie. **\"Them\" refers to the 300 bags (of rubbish).**","en":"1.3 Reference: read back to the noun before *them*: *By midday the teams had filled 300 bags. They loaded them …* The *volunteers* do the loading, so *them* is not the people. **\"Them\" refers to the 300 bags (of rubbish).**"},{"af":"1.4 *Own words* – moenie *get tangled* en *cannot fly* oorskryf nie. Twee punte: wat gebeur (1) en die gevolg (1). **Birds become caught in the line, so they are unable to fly away.**","en":"1.4 *Own words* – do not copy *get tangled* and *cannot fly*. Two marks: what happens (1) and the result (1). **Birds become caught in the line, so they are unable to fly away.**"}],"answer":{"af":"1.1 Schools, churches (or local businesses) · 1.2 \"spotless\" · 1.3 the 300 bags of rubbish · 1.4 Birds get caught in it and are then unable to fly.","en":"1.1 Schools, churches (or local businesses) · 1.2 \"spotless\" · 1.3 the 300 bags of rubbish · 1.4 Birds get caught in it and are then unable to fly."}},{"title":{"af":"Stylfigure, feit/mening en toon","en":"Figures of speech, fact/opinion and tone"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die blog en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Blog: Confessions of a Scroll Addict* – Kea, 16, Brits\n\n(1) My phone is a black hole. I pick it up to check one message, and suddenly two hours have disappeared. Sound familiar?\n\n(2) Last month I tried an experiment: no social media for seven days. On day one, I checked my empty home screen about a thousand times. By day four, something strange happened – I finished a novel, helped my gran in her vegetable garden and actually slept before ten.\n\n(3) I am not saying social media is evil. It helps me chat to my cousins in Cape Town and find study notes. But I honestly think every teenager should try a week offline. You might be surprised at what you find when you look up.\n\n2.1 Identify the figure of speech in \"My phone is a black hole\" and explain what it means. (2)\n2.2 \"I checked my empty home screen about a thousand times.\" Name the figure of speech and say why the writer uses it. (2)\n2.3 \"I honestly think every teenager should try a week offline.\" Is this a fact or an opinion? Give a reason. (2)\n2.4 Describe the writer's tone in paragraph 3. Give a reason for your answer. (2)","en":"Read the blog and answer the questions.\n\n*Blog: Confessions of a Scroll Addict* – Kea, 16, Brits\n\n(1) My phone is a black hole. I pick it up to check one message, and suddenly two hours have disappeared. Sound familiar?\n\n(2) Last month I tried an experiment: no social media for seven days. On day one, I checked my empty home screen about a thousand times. By day four, something strange happened – I finished a novel, helped my gran in her vegetable garden and actually slept before ten.\n\n(3) I am not saying social media is evil. It helps me chat to my cousins in Cape Town and find study notes. But I honestly think every teenager should try a week offline. You might be surprised at what you find when you look up.\n\n2.1 Identify the figure of speech in \"My phone is a black hole\" and explain what it means. (2)\n2.2 \"I checked my empty home screen about a thousand times.\" Name the figure of speech and say why the writer uses it. (2)\n2.3 \"I honestly think every teenager should try a week offline.\" Is this a fact or an opinion? Give a reason. (2)\n2.4 Describe the writer's tone in paragraph 3. Give a reason for your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"2.1 Daar is geen *like* of *as* nie – die foon word direk 'n swart gat genoem, dus 'n **metafoor** (1). Verduidelik die vergelyking: 'n swart gat suig alles in. **Her phone \"swallows\" her time – she loses hours without noticing.** (1)","en":"2.1 There is no *like* or *as* – the phone is directly called a black hole, so it is a **metaphor** (1). Explain the comparison: a black hole sucks everything in. **Her phone \"swallows\" her time – she loses hours without noticing.** (1)"},{"af":"2.2 Niemand kyk letterlik 'n duisend keer nie, dus is dit **hiperbool** (*hyperbole*) (1). Effek: **The exaggeration shows how strong her habit or urge to check the phone was.** (1)","en":"2.2 Nobody literally looks a thousand times, so it is **hyperbole** (1). Effect: **The exaggeration shows how strong her habit or urge to check the phone was.** (1)"},{"af":"2.3 Seinwoorde *I honestly think* en *should* wys dat dit haar oortuiging is. **It is an opinion (1), because it is the writer's personal belief and cannot be proved (1).**","en":"2.3 The signal words *I honestly think* and *should* show that it is her belief. **It is an opinion (1), because it is the writer's personal belief and cannot be proved (1).**"},{"af":"2.4 Toon = houding, uit die woordkeuse. Sy erken die goeie kant (*I am not saying social media is evil*) maar moedig lesers aan (*You might be surprised*). **The tone is balanced and encouraging (1), because she admits the good side of social media but still urges teenagers to try a week offline (1).** Ook aanvaarbaar: *persuasive* of *hopeful*, met 'n rede.","en":"2.4 Tone = attitude, from the word choice. She admits the good side (*I am not saying social media is evil*) but encourages readers (*You might be surprised*). **The tone is balanced and encouraging (1), because she admits the good side of social media but still urges teenagers to try a week offline (1).** Also acceptable: *persuasive* or *hopeful*, with a reason."}],"answer":{"af":"2.1 Metaphor – the phone swallows her time · 2.2 Hyperbole – shows how strong the habit was · 2.3 Opinion – \"I honestly think\"/\"should\" is a belief · 2.4 Balanced/encouraging, with a reason","en":"2.1 Metaphor – the phone swallows her time · 2.2 Hyperbole – shows how strong the habit was · 2.3 Opinion – \"I honestly think\"/\"should\" is a belief · 2.4 Balanced/encouraging, with a reason"}},{"title":{"af":"'n Visuele teks: tabel en evaluering","en":"A visual text: table and evaluation"},"problem":{"af":"Bestudeer die tabel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Studying in the dark* – a made-up survey of one Grade 10 class (40 learners) at a school in Brits. The question was: “How do you study during load-shedding?”\n\n| Method | Number of learners |\n|---|---|\n| Rechargeable lamp or torch | 18 |\n| Study before the power goes off | 11 |\n| Phone torch | 7 |\n| Don't study | 4 |\n\nA sentence from the passage that goes with the table: “Load-shedding has made it impossible for teenagers to study.”\n\n3.1 Which method do most learners use? (1)\n3.2 How many learners use some kind of light to study in the dark? (1)\n3.3 Do you agree with the sentence from the passage? Use the table to support your answer. (2)","en":"Study the table and answer the questions.\n\n*Studying in the dark* – a made-up survey of one Grade 10 class (40 learners) at a school in Brits. The question was: “How do you study during load-shedding?”\n\n| Method | Number of learners |\n|---|---|\n| Rechargeable lamp or torch | 18 |\n| Study before the power goes off | 11 |\n| Phone torch | 7 |\n| Don't study | 4 |\n\nA sentence from the passage that goes with the table: “Load-shedding has made it impossible for teenagers to study.”\n\n3.1 Which method do most learners use? (1)\n3.2 How many learners use some kind of light to study in the dark? (1)\n3.3 Do you agree with the sentence from the passage? Use the table to support your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"3.1 Lees die kolom *Number of learners* en soek die grootste getal: 18. **Most learners use a rechargeable lamp or torch.**","en":"3.1 Read the column *Number of learners* and find the biggest number: 18. **Most learners use a rechargeable lamp or torch.**"},{"af":"3.2 *Some kind of light* = herlaaibare lamp of flits **plus** foonflits. *Study before the power goes off* gebruik nie lig in die donker nie. 18 + 7 = **25 learners.**","en":"3.2 *Some kind of light* = rechargeable lamp or torch **plus** phone torch. *Study before the power goes off* does not use light in the dark. 18 + 7 = **25 learners.**"},{"af":"3.3 Kies een kant en bewys dit met die tabel. Net 4 leerders studeer nie; 40 − 4 = 36 leerders studeer wel. **No, I disagree (1). The table shows that 36 of the 40 learners still find a way to study, so it is not impossible (1).**","en":"3.3 Choose one side and prove it with the table. Only 4 learners do not study; 40 − 4 = 36 learners do. **No, I disagree (1). The table shows that 36 of the 40 learners still find a way to study, so it is not impossible (1).**"}],"answer":{"af":"3.1 A rechargeable lamp or torch · 3.2 25 learners · 3.3 No – 36 of the 40 learners still study, so it is not impossible.","en":"3.1 A rechargeable lamp or torch · 3.2 25 learners · 3.3 No – 36 of the 40 learners still study, so it is not impossible."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel Afdeling A (leesbegrip) in Vraestel 1?","en":"How many marks is Section A (comprehension) worth in Paper 1?"},"options":[{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"40","en":"40"},{"af":"80","en":"80"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Afdeling A (leesbegrip) tel 30 punte. 10 is die opsomming, 40 is Afdeling C (taalstrukture) en 80 is die hele vraestel.","en":"Section A (comprehension) is worth 30 marks. 10 is the summary, 40 is Section C (language structures) and 80 is the whole paper."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Soeklees (*scanning*) beteken dat jy die teks vinnig lees om net die hoofgedagte te kry.","en":"Scanning means that you read the text quickly just to get the main idea."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is vluglees (*skimming*). Met soeklees (*scanning*) soek jy 'n spesifieke feit, naam of getal.","en":"False. That is skimming. With scanning you look for a specific fact, name or number."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke opdragwoord by wat jy moet doen.","en":"Match each command word to what you must do."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Quote","en":"Quote"},"r":{"af":"Skryf die presiese woorde in aanhalingstekens","en":"Write the exact words in inverted commas"}},{"l":{"af":"In your own words","en":"In your own words"},"r":{"af":"Verduidelik sonder om die teks oor te skryf","en":"Explain without copying the text"}},{"l":{"af":"Give a reason","en":"Give a reason"},"r":{"af":"Sê hoekom – gebruik *because*","en":"Say why – use *because*"}},{"l":{"af":"List","en":"List"},"r":{"af":"Noem die feite kort","en":"Name the facts briefly"}},{"l":{"af":"True or false? Quote to support","en":"True or false? Quote to support"},"r":{"af":"Gee jou keuse plus 'n aanhaling as bewys","en":"Give your choice plus a quotation as proof"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die opdragwoord sê presies wat die eksaminator wil hê. As jy *Quote* met eie woorde beantwoord (of andersom), verloor jy die punt.","en":"The command word tells you exactly what the examiner wants. If you answer *Quote* in your own words (or the other way round), you lose the mark."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Vraag lui: *Why did the volunteers start so early? (2)*. Wat sê die (2) vir jou?","en":"A question reads: *Why did the volunteers start so early? (2)*. What does the (2) tell you?"},"options":[{"af":"Jy moet die antwoord in twee sinne oorskryf","en":"You must copy the answer in two sentences"},{"af":"Jy moet twee woorde aanhaal","en":"You must quote two words"},{"af":"Jy moet twee minute aan die vraag spandeer","en":"You must spend two minutes on the question"},{"af":"Jy moet twee relevante punte gee","en":"You must give two relevant points"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die puntetoekenning wys hoeveel punte die eksaminator soek: (2) = twee relevante feite, of 'n feit plus 'n rede.","en":"The mark allocation shows how many points the examiner wants: (2) = two relevant facts, or a fact plus a reason."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi in Engels: 'n Stelling wat bewys of nagegaan kan word, is 'n ___.","en":"Complete: A statement that can be proved or checked is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["fact","a fact","feit","'n feit"],"en":["fact","a fact"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Feit (*fact*) kan bewys word, bv. *The clean-up started at 07:00.* 'n Mening (*opinion*) is 'n gevoel of oordeel wat nie bewys kan word nie.","en":"A fact can be proved, e.g. *The clean-up started at 07:00.* An opinion is a feeling or judgement that cannot be proved."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["opinion","theme","tone"],"en":["opinion","theme","tone"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *The volunteers collected 300 bags of rubbish. They loaded them onto a truck.* Waarna verwys *them*?","en":"Read: *The volunteers collected 300 bags of rubbish. They loaded them onto a truck.* What does *them* refer to?"},"options":[{"af":"the volunteers","en":"the volunteers"},{"af":"the bags of rubbish","en":"the bags of rubbish"},{"af":"the truck","en":"the truck"},{"af":"the rubbish truck drivers","en":"the rubbish truck drivers"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*They* (die vrywilligers) laai *them* (die sakke). Lees terug na die selfstandige naamwoord wat gelaai kan word: *300 bags of rubbish*.","en":"*They* (the volunteers) load *them* (the bags). Read back to the noun that can be loaded: *300 bags of rubbish*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lees: *Ten years ago the river was badly polluted. Today, thanks to the volunteers, its water is clean enough for fish.* Gee EEN woord uit die uittreksel wat die teenoorgestelde (antoniem) van *polluted* is: ___","en":"Read: *Ten years ago the river was badly polluted. Today, thanks to the volunteers, its water is clean enough for fish.* Give ONE word from the extract that is the opposite (antonym) of *polluted*: ___"},"answers":{"af":["clean"],"en":["clean"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Antoniem het die teenoorgestelde betekenis. *Polluted* (besoedel) se teenoorgestelde is *clean*. *Dirty* is 'n sinoniem, nie 'n antoniem nie.","en":"An antonym has the opposite meaning. The opposite of *polluted* is *clean*. *Dirty* is a synonym, not an antonym."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dirty","badly","enough"],"en":["dirty","badly","enough"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Lees: *Since January the club has planted 150 trees along the river. Members meet every second Saturday.* Stelling: *The club meets every Saturday.* Hierdie stelling is waar.","en":"Read: *Since January the club has planted 150 trees along the river. Members meet every second Saturday.* Statement: *The club meets every Saturday.* This statement is true."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die bewys is die aanhaling \"Members meet every second Saturday\" – dit is elke tweede Saterdag, nie elke Saterdag nie. In die eksamen moet jy die aanhaling saam met *False* gee.","en":"False. The proof is the quotation \"Members meet every second Saturday\" – that is every other Saturday, not every Saturday. In the exam you must give the quotation together with *False*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lees die plakkaat: *Don't sit at home complaining about the dirty dam. Grab your gloves, bring a friend and join us on Saturday – together we can make a difference!* Die hoofdoel van die teks is om te ___ (een Engelse woord).","en":"Read the poster: *Don't sit at home complaining about the dirty dam. Grab your gloves, bring a friend and join us on Saturday – together we can make a difference!* The main purpose of the text is to ___ (one word)."},"answers":{"af":["persuade","to persuade","oorreed"],"en":["persuade","to persuade"]},"explain":{"af":"Die gebiedende wys (*Grab, bring, join*) en die direkte aanspreek (*you, us*) wil die leser oorreed om iets te doen. Dit gee wel inligting (Saterdag), maar die hoofdoel is oorreding.","en":"The imperatives (*Grab, bring, join*) and direct address (*you, us*) want to persuade the reader to act. It does give information (Saturday), but the main purpose is persuasion."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["inform","entertain","describe"],"en":["inform","entertain","describe"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is 'n MENING?","en":"Which sentence is an OPINION?"},"options":[{"af":"Hartbeespoort Dam lies in the North West.","en":"Hartbeespoort Dam lies in the North West."},{"af":"The clean-up started at seven o'clock.","en":"The clean-up started at seven o'clock."},{"af":"Saturday's clean-up was the best community event of the year.","en":"Saturday's clean-up was the best community event of the year."},{"af":"The volunteers filled 300 bags with rubbish.","en":"The volunteers filled 300 bags with rubbish."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*The best … of the year* is 'n oordeel – iemand anders kan anders voel en dit kan nie bewys word nie. Die ander drie kan nagegaan word, dus is hulle feite.","en":"*The best … of the year* is a judgement – someone else may feel differently and it cannot be proved. The other three can be checked, so they are facts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Benoem die stylfiguur in Engels: *The wind whispered through the reeds at the edge of the dam.* ___","en":"Name the figure of speech: *The wind whispered through the reeds at the edge of the dam.* ___"},"answers":{"af":["personification","personifikasie"],"en":["personification"]},"explain":{"af":"Net mense kan fluister. Die wind kry 'n menslike eienskap, dus is dit **personifikasie** (*personification*). Daar is geen *like/as* nie, so dis nie 'n vergelyking (*simile*) nie.","en":"Only people can whisper. The wind is given a human quality, so it is **personification**. There is no *like/as*, so it is not a simile."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["simile","metaphor","alliteration"],"en":["simile","metaphor","alliteration"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *Oh wonderful, another four hours without power. I just love studying for exams by candlelight.* Wat is die spreker se toon?","en":"Read: *Oh wonderful, another four hours without power. I just love studying for exams by candlelight.* What is the speaker's tone?"},"options":[{"af":"sarcastic","en":"sarcastic"},{"af":"admiring","en":"admiring"},{"af":"grateful","en":"grateful"},{"af":"neutral","en":"neutral"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker sê die teenoorgestelde van wat sy bedoel: niemand vind vier uur sonder krag *wonderful* nie. Dit is sarkasme – die toon is **sarcastic**.","en":"The speaker says the opposite of what she means: nobody finds four hours without power *wonderful*. This is sarcasm – the tone is **sarcastic**."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Bestudeer die tabel ('n opgemaakte opname van 40 leerders in een klas):\n\n| App | Learners who use it daily |\n|---|---|\n| WhatsApp | 36 |\n| YouTube | 31 |\n| TikTok | 28 |\n| Instagram | 19 |\n\nWatter toep word daagliks deur die MINSTE leerders gebruik? ___","en":"Study the table (a made-up survey of 40 learners in one class):\n\n| App | Learners who use it daily |\n|---|---|\n| WhatsApp | 36 |\n| YouTube | 31 |\n| TikTok | 28 |\n| Instagram | 19 |\n\nWhich app is used daily by the FEWEST learners? ___"},"answers":{"af":["Instagram"],"en":["Instagram"]},"explain":{"af":"*Fewest* = die kleinste getal. Instagram het 19, die minste in die tabel. WhatsApp (36) het die meeste.","en":"*Fewest* = the smallest number. Instagram has 19, the lowest in the table. WhatsApp (36) has the most."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["WhatsApp","TikTok","YouTube"],"en":["WhatsApp","TikTok","YouTube"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees: *At six in the morning the Brits taxi rank was a beehive.* Watter antwoord verduidelik die stylfiguur en sy effek die beste?","en":"Read: *At six in the morning the Brits taxi rank was a beehive.* Which answer best explains the figure of speech and its effect?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is 'n vergelyking (*simile*) omdat die taxistaanplek met 'n byekorf vergelyk word.","en":"It is a simile because the taxi rank is compared to a beehive."},{"af":"Dit is 'n metafoor: die staanplek word 'n byekorf genoem om te wys hoe besig en raserig dit is, met mense wat oral rondbeweeg.","en":"It is a metaphor: the rank is called a beehive to show how busy and noisy it is, with people moving everywhere."},{"af":"Dit wys dat daar bye by die taxistaanplek woon.","en":"It shows that bees live at the taxi rank."},{"af":"Dit is personifikasie omdat die staanplek soos 'n mens optree.","en":"It is personification because the rank behaves like a person."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Daar is geen *like/as* nie, dus is dit 'n metafoor, nie 'n *simile* nie. 'n Volpunt-antwoord benoem die stylfiguur, verduidelik die vergelyking (besig, raserig, vol beweging) én die effek. Opsie C lees die sin letterlik.","en":"There is no *like/as*, so it is a metaphor, not a simile. A full-mark answer names the figure of speech, explains the comparison (busy, noisy, full of movement) and the effect. Option C reads the sentence literally."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Gebruik die tabel ('n opgemaakte opname van 40 leerders):\n\n| App | Learners who use it daily |\n|---|---|\n| WhatsApp | 36 |\n| YouTube | 31 |\n| TikTok | 28 |\n| Instagram | 19 |\n\nWatter gevolgtrekking word deur die tabel ondersteun?","en":"Use the table (a made-up survey of 40 learners):\n\n| App | Learners who use it daily |\n|---|---|\n| WhatsApp | 36 |\n| YouTube | 31 |\n| TikTok | 28 |\n| Instagram | 19 |\n\nWhich conclusion is supported by the table?"},"options":[{"af":"Every learner in the class uses WhatsApp daily.","en":"Every learner in the class uses WhatsApp daily."},{"af":"More learners use TikTok than YouTube daily.","en":"More learners use TikTok than YouTube daily."},{"af":"Instagram is the most popular app in the class.","en":"Instagram is the most popular app in the class."},{"af":"Fewer than half of the learners use Instagram daily.","en":"Fewer than half of the learners use Instagram daily."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die helfte van 40 is 20; Instagram het 19, dus minder as die helfte. WhatsApp het 36 (nie al 40 nie), YouTube (31) het meer as TikTok (28), en Instagram is die minste gewild.","en":"Half of 40 is 20; Instagram has 19, so fewer than half. WhatsApp has 36 (not all 40), YouTube (31) has more than TikTok (28), and Instagram is the least popular."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Blogskrywer sê: *Teenagers should be banned from social media until they turn 18, because it is addictive.* Vraag: *Do you agree? Give a reason. (2)* Watter antwoord sal waarskynlik albei punte kry?","en":"A blogger writes: *Teenagers should be banned from social media until they turn 18, because it is addictive.* Question: *Do you agree? Give a reason. (2)* Which answer would most likely earn both marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Yes.","en":"Yes."},{"af":"The writer thinks teenagers should be banned from social media.","en":"The writer thinks teenagers should be banned from social media."},{"af":"No. Although social media can be addictive, it also helps learners, for example in WhatsApp study groups, so a total ban goes too far.","en":"No. Although social media can be addictive, it also helps learners, for example in WhatsApp study groups, so a total ban goes too far."},{"af":"Maybe, because some people like it and some people don't.","en":"Maybe, because some people like it and some people don't."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Volpunt-antwoord kies duidelik een kant (*No*) en gee 'n oortuigende rede wat by die teks se argument aansluit. *Yes.* het geen rede nie, B herhaal net die skrywer, en D kies nie 'n kant nie.","en":"A full-mark answer clearly chooses one side (*No*) and gives a convincing reason that responds to the text's argument. *Yes.* has no reason, B only repeats the writer, and D does not choose a side."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t1-parts-of-speech","title":{"af":"Woordsoorte","en":"Parts of speech"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal elke woordsoort in 'n sin kan herken en meervoude, trappe van vergelyking, voornaamwoorde en voorsetsels foutloos kan gebruik.","en":"You will be able to recognise every part of speech in a sentence and use plurals, degrees of comparison, pronouns and prepositions without errors."},"summary":{"af":"## Selfstandige naamwoorde (*nouns*)\n\n| Soort | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Soortnaam (*common noun*) | *dam, taxi, teacher* |\n| Eienaam (*proper noun*) – altyd 'n hoofletter | *Brits, Sipho, October* |\n| Versamelnaam (*collective noun*) | *a herd of cattle, a swarm of bees, a pride of lions, a team of players* |\n| Abstrakte naamwoord (*abstract noun*) – kan nie gesien of aangeraak word nie | *happiness, fear, freedom* |\n\n**Telbaar en ontelbaar:** telbare naamwoorde (*bottles, people*) kry *many* en *fewer*; ontelbare naamwoorde (*water, time, money*) kry *much* en *less*: *many bottles, much water; fewer people, less time*.\n\n### Meervoude\n\n- Meeste woorde: + *s* (*books*)\n- Eindig op -s, -x, -ch, -sh: + *es* (*boxes, churches, buses*)\n- Medeklinker + y: y → *ies* (*baby – babies*); klinker + y: + *s* (*boys*)\n- -f/-fe word dikwels *-ves* (*leaf – leaves, knife – knives*)\n- -o: *potatoes, tomatoes*, maar *photos, pianos*\n- Onreëlmatig: *woman – women, child – children, mouse – mice, foot – feet, sheep – sheep*\n\n### Die besitlike apostrof\n\n- Enkelvoud: + *'s*: *the boy's bag* (een seun)\n- Meervoud wat op -s eindig: net *'*: *the boys' bags* (baie seuns)\n- Meervoud sonder -s: + *'s*: *the children's toys, the women's team*\n\n## Voornaamwoorde (*pronouns*)\n\n| Soort | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|\n| Persoonlik – onderwerp | *I, you, he, she, it, we, they* |\n| Persoonlik – voorwerp | *me, you, him, her, it, us, them* |\n| Besitlik | *my/mine, your/yours, our/ours, their/theirs* |\n| Wederkerend (*reflexive*) | *myself, himself, ourselves, themselves* |\n| Betreklik (*relative*) | *who, whom, whose, which, that* |\n| Aanwysend (*demonstrative*) | *this/these* (naby), *that/those* (ver) |\n| Vraend (*interrogative*) | *Who? What? Which? Whose?* |\n| Onbepaald (*indefinite*) | *everyone, nobody, someone, each* – **enkelvoudige werkwoord**: *Everyone **is** here.* |\n\n*Who* = mense (onderwerp); *whom* = mense (voorwerp, ook ná 'n voorsetsel: *to whom*); *whose* = besit; *which* = diere en dinge.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *Between you and I* ✘ → *Between you and **me*** ✔. Ná 'n voorsetsel en as voorwerp gebruik jy die voorwerpsvorm. Toets: haal die ander persoon weg – *The coach thanked (Sipho and) **me**.* As onderwerp: *Sipho and **I** went* – nie *Me and Sipho went* nie.\n\n## Lidwoorde en bepalers (*articles and determiners*)\n\n*A/an* is die onbepaalde lidwoord, *the* die bepaalde lidwoord. Die **klank**, nie die letter nie, besluit: *an hour, an honest man* (stil h), maar *a university, a uniform* (klink soos \"you\"). Ander bepalers: *this, my, some, every*.\n\n## Byvoeglike naamwoorde (*adjectives*)\n\nHulle beskryf 'n selfstandige naamwoord. **Trappe van vergelyking:**\n\n| Stellend | Vergrotend | Oortreffend |\n|---|---|---|\n| tall | taller | tallest |\n| big | bigger | biggest |\n| good | better | best |\n| bad | worse | worst |\n| many/much | more | most |\n| little | less | least |\n| beautiful | more beautiful | most beautiful |\n\nLang byvoeglike naamwoorde kry *more/most*. Moenie albei gebruik nie: *more taller* ✘.\n\n**Volgorde:** mening – grootte – ouderdom – vorm – kleur – oorsprong – materiaal: *a beautiful small old wooden table*.\n\n**Byvoeglike naamwoord of bywoord?** *She is a **good** player* (beskryf *player*) teenoor *She plays **well*** (beskryf *plays*).\n\n## Werkwoorde (*verbs*)\n\n- **Hoofwerkwoord:** die hoofaksie: *run, eat*\n- **Hulpwerkwoorde:** *be, have, do*: *She **is** running.*\n- **Modale hulpwerkwoorde:** *can, could, may, might, must, should, will, would*\n- **Infinitief:** *to* + werkwoord: *to swim*\n- **Gerundium (*gerund*):** 'n -ing-vorm wat as naamwoord werk: ***Swimming** is fun.*\n- **Deelwoorde (*participles*):** *running* (teenwoordig), *broken, played* (voltooid)\n- **Frasale werkwoorde (*phrasal verbs*):** werkwoord + partikel met 'n nuwe betekenis: *give up* (ophou), *look after* (oppas), *run out of* (opraak)\n\n## Bywoorde (*adverbs*)\n\nHulle sê **hoe, wanneer, waar, hoe dikwels** of **tot watter mate**: wyse (*quickly*), tyd (*yesterday*), plek (*outside*), frekwensie (*always, never*), graad (*very, too*). Baie eindig op *-ly*, maar nie almal nie: *fast, hard, well*.\n\n## Voorsetsels (*prepositions*)\n\n| | Tyd | Plek |\n|---|---|---|\n| *in* | maande, jare: *in October* | *in Brits, in the box* |\n| *on* | dae, datums: *on Monday* | *on the table* |\n| *at* | kloktye: *at 3 pm* | 'n spesifieke punt: *at the taxi rank* |\n\nVaste verbindings: *interested in, good at, afraid of, different from, proud of*.\n\n## Voegwoorde (*conjunctions*)\n\n- **Neweskikkend** (FANBOYS): *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so* – verbind twee gelyke dele.\n- **Onderskikkend:** *because, although, when, if, unless, while, since* – begin 'n bysin.\n\n## Tussenwerpsels (*interjections*)\n\nHulle druk 'n gevoel uit: *Wow! Ouch! Oh no!*\n\n> **Wenk:** Die woordsoort hang af van hoe die woord in die **sin** werk: *a **hard** test* (byvoeglike naamwoord) teenoor *He works **hard*** (bywoord). Vra: watter woord beskryf dit?\n\nIn die eksamen moet jy die woordsoort van 'n woord in konteks benoem, meervoude en trappe van vergelyking gee, voornaamwoordfoute regstel en die regte voorsetsel invul.","en":"## Nouns\n\n| Kind | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Common noun | *dam, taxi, teacher* |\n| Proper noun – always a capital letter | *Brits, Sipho, October* |\n| Collective noun | *a herd of cattle, a swarm of bees, a pride of lions, a team of players* |\n| Abstract noun – cannot be seen or touched | *happiness, fear, freedom* |\n\n**Countable and uncountable:** countable nouns (*bottles, people*) take *many* and *fewer*; uncountable nouns (*water, time, money*) take *much* and *less*: *many bottles, much water; fewer people, less time*.\n\n### Plurals\n\n- Most words: + *s* (*books*)\n- Ending in -s, -x, -ch, -sh: + *es* (*boxes, churches, buses*)\n- Consonant + y: y → *ies* (*baby – babies*); vowel + y: + *s* (*boys*)\n- -f/-fe often becomes *-ves* (*leaf – leaves, knife – knives*)\n- -o: *potatoes, tomatoes*, but *photos, pianos*\n- Irregular: *woman – women, child – children, mouse – mice, foot – feet, sheep – sheep*\n\n### The possessive apostrophe\n\n- Singular: + *'s*: *the boy's bag* (one boy)\n- Plural ending in -s: only *'*: *the boys' bags* (many boys)\n- Plural without -s: + *'s*: *the children's toys, the women's team*\n\n## Pronouns\n\n| Kind | Examples |\n|---|---|\n| Personal – subject | *I, you, he, she, it, we, they* |\n| Personal – object | *me, you, him, her, it, us, them* |\n| Possessive | *my/mine, your/yours, our/ours, their/theirs* |\n| Reflexive | *myself, himself, ourselves, themselves* |\n| Relative | *who, whom, whose, which, that* |\n| Demonstrative | *this/these* (near), *that/those* (far) |\n| Interrogative | *Who? What? Which? Whose?* |\n| Indefinite | *everyone, nobody, someone, each* – **singular verb**: *Everyone **is** here.* |\n\n*Who* = people (subject); *whom* = people (object, also after a preposition: *to whom*); *whose* = possession; *which* = animals and things.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *Between you and I* ✘ → *Between you and **me*** ✔. After a preposition and as an object you use the object form. Test: remove the other person – *The coach thanked (Sipho and) **me**.* As subject: *Sipho and **I** went* – not *Me and Sipho went*.\n\n## Articles and determiners\n\n*A/an* is the indefinite article, *the* the definite article. The **sound**, not the letter, decides: *an hour, an honest man* (silent h), but *a university, a uniform* (sounds like \"you\"). Other determiners: *this, my, some, every*.\n\n## Adjectives\n\nThey describe a noun. **Degrees of comparison:**\n\n| Positive | Comparative | Superlative |\n|---|---|---|\n| tall | taller | tallest |\n| big | bigger | biggest |\n| good | better | best |\n| bad | worse | worst |\n| many/much | more | most |\n| little | less | least |\n| beautiful | more beautiful | most beautiful |\n\nLong adjectives take *more/most*. Do not use both: *more taller* ✘.\n\n**Order:** opinion – size – age – shape – colour – origin – material: *a beautiful small old wooden table*.\n\n**Adjective or adverb?** *She is a **good** player* (describes *player*) versus *She plays **well*** (describes *plays*).\n\n## Verbs\n\n- **Main verb:** the main action: *run, eat*\n- **Auxiliary verbs:** *be, have, do*: *She **is** running.*\n- **Modal auxiliaries:** *can, could, may, might, must, should, will, would*\n- **Infinitive:** *to* + verb: *to swim*\n- **Gerund:** an -ing form that works as a noun: ***Swimming** is fun.*\n- **Participles:** *running* (present), *broken, played* (past)\n- **Phrasal verbs:** verb + particle with a new meaning: *give up* (stop), *look after* (care for), *run out of* (have none left)\n\n## Adverbs\n\nThey tell **how, when, where, how often** or **to what degree**: manner (*quickly*), time (*yesterday*), place (*outside*), frequency (*always, never*), degree (*very, too*). Many end in *-ly*, but not all: *fast, hard, well*.\n\n## Prepositions\n\n| | Time | Place |\n|---|---|---|\n| *in* | months, years: *in October* | *in Brits, in the box* |\n| *on* | days, dates: *on Monday* | *on the table* |\n| *at* | clock times: *at 3 pm* | a specific point: *at the taxi rank* |\n\nFixed combinations: *interested in, good at, afraid of, different from, proud of*.\n\n## Conjunctions\n\n- **Coordinating** (FANBOYS): *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so* – join two equal parts.\n- **Subordinating:** *because, although, when, if, unless, while, since* – begin a subordinate clause.\n\n## Interjections\n\nThey express a feeling: *Wow! Ouch! Oh no!*\n\n> **Tip:** The part of speech depends on how the word works in the **sentence**: *a **hard** test* (adjective) versus *He works **hard*** (adverb). Ask: which word does it describe?\n\nIn the exam you must name the part of speech of a word in context, give plurals and degrees of comparison, correct pronoun errors and fill in the correct preposition."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Selfstandige naamwoord","en":"Noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat 'n persoon, plek, ding of idee benoem, bv. *teacher, Brits, freedom*.","en":"A word that names a person, place, thing or idea, e.g. *teacher, Brits, freedom*."}},{"term":{"af":"Versamelnaam","en":"Collective noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Naamwoord vir 'n groep, bv. *a herd of cattle, a swarm of bees*.","en":"A noun for a group, e.g. *a herd of cattle, a swarm of bees*."}},{"term":{"af":"Abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord","en":"Abstract noun"},"def":{"af":"'n Naamwoord vir 'n gevoel, eienskap of idee wat jy nie kan sien of aanraak nie, bv. *happiness*.","en":"A noun for a feeling, quality or idea that you cannot see or touch, e.g. *happiness*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voornaamwoord","en":"Pronoun"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat die plek van 'n selfstandige naamwoord inneem, bv. *he, them, whose, myself*.","en":"A word that takes the place of a noun, e.g. *he, them, whose, myself*."}},{"term":{"af":"Byvoeglike naamwoord","en":"Adjective"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat 'n selfstandige naamwoord beskryf, bv. *a tired player*.","en":"A word that describes a noun, e.g. *a tired player*."}},{"term":{"af":"Trappe van vergelyking","en":"Degrees of comparison"},"def":{"af":"Die stellende, vergrotende en oortreffende trap van 'n byvoeglike naamwoord: *good – better – best*.","en":"The positive, comparative and superlative forms of an adjective: *good – better – best*."}},{"term":{"af":"Bywoord","en":"Adverb"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat 'n werkwoord, byvoeglike naamwoord of ander bywoord beskryf: hoe, wanneer, waar, hoe dikwels, tot watter mate.","en":"A word that describes a verb, adjective or another adverb: how, when, where, how often, to what degree."}},{"term":{"af":"Modale hulpwerkwoord","en":"Modal auxiliary verb"},"def":{"af":"'n Hulpwerkwoord wat vermoë, toestemming, moontlikheid of verpligting uitdruk: *can, may, might, must, should*.","en":"An auxiliary verb that expresses ability, permission, possibility or obligation: *can, may, might, must, should*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voorsetsel","en":"Preposition"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat die verhouding in tyd of plek tussen woorde aandui, bv. *in, on, at, under*.","en":"A word that shows the relationship in time or place between words, e.g. *in, on, at, under*."}},{"term":{"af":"Voegwoord","en":"Conjunction"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat woorde, frases of sinne verbind: neweskikkend (*and, but*) of onderskikkend (*because, although*).","en":"A word that joins words, phrases or sentences: coordinating (*and, but*) or subordinating (*because, although*)."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Benoem die woordsoort in konteks","en":"Identify the part of speech in context"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die sin en gee die woordsoort van elke woord: (a) *Wow* (b) *excited* (c) *quickly* (d) *into* (e) *because*\n\n*Wow! The excited learners from Brits quickly climbed into the old taxi because they were late.*","en":"Read the sentence and give the part of speech of each word: (a) *Wow* (b) *excited* (c) *quickly* (d) *into* (e) *because*\n\n*Wow! The excited learners from Brits quickly climbed into the old taxi because they were late.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *Wow!* druk 'n gevoel (verbasing) uit en staan los van die sin → **interjection** (tussenwerpsel).","en":"(a) *Wow!* expresses a feeling (surprise) and stands apart from the sentence → **interjection**."},{"af":"(b) *Excited* beskryf die selfstandige naamwoord *learners* → **adjective** (byvoeglike naamwoord).","en":"(b) *Excited* describes the noun *learners* → **adjective**."},{"af":"(c) *Quickly* sê **hoe** hulle geklim het – dit beskryf die werkwoord *climbed* → **adverb of manner** (bywoord van wyse).","en":"(c) *Quickly* tells **how** they climbed – it describes the verb *climbed* → **adverb of manner**."},{"af":"(d) *Into* wys die verhouding in plek tussen *climbed* en *the old taxi* → **preposition** (voorsetsel).","en":"(d) *Into* shows the relationship in place between *climbed* and *the old taxi* → **preposition**."},{"af":"(e) *Because* begin 'n bysin wat 'n rede gee → **subordinating conjunction** (onderskikkende voegwoord).","en":"(e) *Because* begins a subordinate clause that gives a reason → **subordinating conjunction**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) interjection (b) adjective (c) adverb (d) preposition (e) conjunction","en":"(a) interjection (b) adjective (c) adverb (d) preposition (e) conjunction"}},{"title":{"af":"Meervoude en trappe van vergelyking","en":"Plurals and degrees of comparison"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Gee die meervoud van: *leaf, potato, child, sheep*.\n(b) Vul die regte vorm van die woord tussen hakies in: *This is the ___ (bad) traffic jam I have ever seen on the N4.*\n(c) *The cableway at Hartbeespoort is ___ (exciting) than the bus trip.*","en":"(a) Give the plural of: *leaf, potato, child, sheep*.\n(b) Fill in the correct form of the word in brackets: *This is the ___ (bad) traffic jam I have ever seen on the N4.*\n(c) *The cableway at Hartbeespoort is ___ (exciting) than the bus trip.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *leaf* eindig op -f → **leaves**; *potato* is een van die -o-woorde wat -es kry → **potatoes**; *child* is onreëlmatig → **children**; *sheep* bly dieselfde → **sheep**.","en":"(a) *leaf* ends in -f → **leaves**; *potato* is one of the -o words that take -es → **potatoes**; *child* is irregular → **children**; *sheep* stays the same → **sheep**."},{"af":"(b) *the … I have ever seen* vergelyk met alles, dus die oortreffende trap. *Bad* is onreëlmatig: bad – worse – worst → **worst**. (*Baddest* bestaan nie.)","en":"(b) *the … I have ever seen* compares with everything, so the superlative. *Bad* is irregular: bad – worse – worst → **worst**. (*Baddest* does not exist.)"},{"af":"(c) *than* vergelyk twee dinge → vergrotende trap. *Exciting* is 'n lang woord, dus **more exciting** – nie *excitinger* nie.","en":"(c) *than* compares two things → comparative. *Exciting* is a long word, so **more exciting** – not *excitinger*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) leaves, potatoes, children, sheep (b) worst (c) more exciting","en":"(a) leaves, potatoes, children, sheep (b) worst (c) more exciting"}},{"title":{"af":"Stel die voornaamwoordfoute reg","en":"Correct the pronoun errors"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf elke sin korrek:\n(a) *Me and Thabo walked to the dam.*\n(b) *The teacher gave the books to Lerato and I.*\n(c) *This is the man who's car was stolen.*\n(d) *The players hurt theirselves during practice.*","en":"Rewrite each sentence correctly:\n(a) *Me and Thabo walked to the dam.*\n(b) *The teacher gave the books to Lerato and I.*\n(c) *This is the man who's car was stolen.*\n(d) *The players hurt theirselves during practice.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die voornaamwoord is deel van die **onderwerp**, dus die onderwerpsvorm *I*. Beleefdheid: noem jouself laaste. → ***Thabo and I walked to the dam.***","en":"(a) The pronoun is part of the **subject**, so the subject form *I*. Politeness: mention yourself last. → ***Thabo and I walked to the dam.***"},{"af":"(b) Ná die voorsetsel *to* kom die voorwerpsvorm. Toets: *gave the books to I* ✘ / *to me* ✔ → ***The teacher gave the books to Lerato and me.***","en":"(b) After the preposition *to* comes the object form. Test: *gave the books to I* ✘ / *to me* ✔ → ***The teacher gave the books to Lerato and me.***"},{"af":"(c) *Who's* = *who is*. Hier gaan dit oor besit (die man se motor), dus die betreklike voornaamwoord *whose* → ***This is the man whose car was stolen.***","en":"(c) *Who's* = *who is*. This is about possession (the man's car), so the relative pronoun *whose* → ***This is the man whose car was stolen.***"},{"af":"(d) *Theirselves* bestaan nie. Die wederkerende voornaamwoord vir *they* is *themselves* → ***The players hurt themselves during practice.***","en":"(d) *Theirselves* does not exist. The reflexive pronoun for *they* is *themselves* → ***The players hurt themselves during practice.***"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Thabo and I … (b) … to Lerato and me. (c) … whose car … (d) … themselves …","en":"(a) Thabo and I … (b) … to Lerato and me. (c) … whose car … (d) … themselves …"}},{"title":{"af":"Voorsetsels en voegwoorde","en":"Prepositions and conjunctions"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Vul die regte voorsetsels in: *The final starts ___ 3 pm ___ Saturday ___ October.*\n(b) *My little brother is afraid ___ the dark.*\n(c) Verbind die twee sinne met 'n onderskikkende voegwoord: *It was raining. We still played the match.*","en":"(a) Fill in the correct prepositions: *The final starts ___ 3 pm ___ Saturday ___ October.*\n(b) *My little brother is afraid ___ the dark.*\n(c) Join the two sentences with a subordinating conjunction: *It was raining. We still played the match.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Kloktyd → *at*; dag → *on*; maand → *in*: ***The final starts at 3 pm on Saturday in October.***","en":"(a) Clock time → *at*; day → *on*; month → *in*: ***The final starts at 3 pm on Saturday in October.***"},{"af":"(b) *Afraid* het 'n vaste voorsetsel: **afraid of** – nie *afraid for* nie (Afrikaans \"bang vir\" lei mense mis).","en":"(b) *Afraid* has a fixed preposition: **afraid of** – not *afraid for* (the Afrikaans \"bang vir\" misleads people)."},{"af":"(c) Die twee idees is in kontras (reën, tog gespeel) → *although*. Dit begin die bysin; sit 'n komma ná die bysin: ***Although it was raining, we still played the match.***","en":"(c) The two ideas contrast (rain, yet played) → *although*. It begins the subordinate clause; put a comma after the clause: ***Although it was raining, we still played the match.***"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) at, on, in (b) of (c) Although it was raining, we still played the match.","en":"(a) at, on, in (b) of (c) Although it was raining, we still played the match."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte versamelnaam: *a ___ of lions*","en":"Choose the correct collective noun: *a ___ of lions*"},"options":[{"af":"herd","en":"herd"},{"af":"swarm","en":"swarm"},{"af":"pride","en":"pride"},{"af":"flock","en":"flock"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Leeus vorm 'n *pride*. *A herd of cattle, a swarm of bees, a flock of sheep.*","en":"Lions form a *pride*. *A herd of cattle, a swarm of bees, a flock of sheep.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf die meervoud van *baby*: one baby, two ___","en":"Write the plural of *baby*: one baby, two ___"},"answers":{"af":["babies"],"en":["babies"]},"explain":{"af":"Medeklinker (b) + y: verander die y na *ies* → *babies*. Net ná 'n klinker voeg jy bloot -s by (*boys*).","en":"Consonant (b) + y: change the y to *ies* → *babies*. Only after a vowel do you simply add -s (*boys*)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["babys","babyes","babie"],"en":["babys","babyes","babie"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Happiness* is 'n abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord.","en":"*Happiness* is an abstract noun."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Jy kan geluk nie sien of aanraak nie – dit is 'n gevoel, dus 'n abstrakte selfstandige naamwoord.","en":"True. You cannot see or touch happiness – it is a feeling, so it is an abstract noun."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter frase is KORREK?","en":"Which phrase is CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"a hour","en":"a hour"},{"af":"an honest man","en":"an honest man"},{"af":"an university","en":"an university"},{"af":"a umbrella","en":"a umbrella"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die klank besluit: *honest* begin met 'n klinkerklank (stil h), dus *an*. *An hour* (stil h), *a university* (klink soos \"you\"), *an umbrella* (klinkerklank).","en":"The sound decides: *honest* begins with a vowel sound (silent h), so *an*. *An hour* (silent h), *a university* (sounds like \"you\"), *an umbrella* (vowel sound)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte trap van vergelyking in: *This is the ___ (bad) mark I have ever had.*","en":"Fill in the correct degree of comparison: *This is the ___ (bad) mark I have ever had.*"},"answers":{"af":["worst"],"en":["worst"]},"explain":{"af":"*The … I have ever had* vra die oortreffende trap. *Bad* is onreëlmatig: bad – worse – worst. *Worse* is die vergrotende trap.","en":"*The … I have ever had* needs the superlative. *Bad* is irregular: bad – worse – worst. *Worse* is the comparative."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["baddest","worse","most bad"],"en":["baddest","worse","most bad"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Volgens die reël gebruik ons *less* met telbare selfstandige naamwoorde, bv. *less people*.","en":"According to the rule, we use *less* with countable nouns, e.g. *less people*."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Fewer* gaan met telbare naamwoorde (*fewer people*); *less* met ontelbare naamwoorde (*less time, less water*).","en":"False. *Fewer* goes with countable nouns (*fewer people*); *less* with uncountable nouns (*less time, less water*)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die kleedkamer behoort aan al die seuns in die span. Kies die regte vorm: *The ___ change room was locked.*","en":"The change room belongs to all the boys in the team. Choose the correct form: *The ___ change room was locked.*"},"options":[{"af":"boys","en":"boys"},{"af":"boy's","en":"boy's"},{"af":"boys'","en":"boys'"},{"af":"boys's","en":"boys's"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Meervoud wat op -s eindig: sit net die apostrof ná die s → *boys'*. *Boy's* is net een seun; *boys's* is altyd verkeerd.","en":"A plural ending in -s: put only the apostrophe after the s → *boys'*. *Boy's* is only one boy; *boys's* is always wrong."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies die regte voornaamwoord: *Between you and ___, I think the test was easy.*","en":"Choose the correct pronoun: *Between you and ___, I think the test was easy.*"},"answers":{"af":["me"],"en":["me"]},"explain":{"af":"*Between* is 'n voorsetsel, dus volg die voorwerpsvorm *me*. *Between you and I* is 'n bekende fout.","en":"*Between* is a preposition, so the object form *me* follows. *Between you and I* is a well-known mistake."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["I","myself","mine"],"en":["I","myself","mine"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte voorsetsel in: *Thabo is very good ___ rugby.*","en":"Fill in the correct preposition: *Thabo is very good ___ rugby.*"},"answers":{"af":["at"],"en":["at"]},"explain":{"af":"*Good* het 'n vaste voorsetsel: *good at* (soos *interested in, afraid of, different from*).","en":"*Good* has a fixed preposition: *good at* (like *interested in, afraid of, different from*)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["in","on","with"],"en":["in","on","with"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Lees: *Ouch! The tired players walked slowly to the bus.* Pas elke woord by sy woordsoort.","en":"Read: *Ouch! The tired players walked slowly to the bus.* Match each word to its part of speech."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Ouch","en":"Ouch"},"r":{"af":"tussenwerpsel (interjection)","en":"interjection"}},{"l":{"af":"tired","en":"tired"},"r":{"af":"byvoeglike naamwoord (adjective)","en":"adjective"}},{"l":{"af":"slowly","en":"slowly"},"r":{"af":"bywoord (adverb)","en":"adverb"}},{"l":{"af":"to","en":"to"},"r":{"af":"voorsetsel (preposition)","en":"preposition"}},{"l":{"af":"bus","en":"bus"},"r":{"af":"selfstandige naamwoord (noun)","en":"noun"}}],"explain":{"af":"*Ouch* druk pyn uit; *tired* beskryf *players*; *slowly* sê hoe hulle geloop het; *to* wys rigting/plek; *bus* is 'n ding.","en":"*Ouch* expresses pain; *tired* describes *players*; *slowly* tells how they walked; *to* shows direction/place; *bus* is a thing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter frase het die byvoeglike naamwoorde in die regte volgorde?","en":"Which phrase has the adjectives in the correct order?"},"options":[{"af":"a wooden old beautiful small table","en":"a wooden old beautiful small table"},{"af":"a small beautiful wooden old table","en":"a small beautiful wooden old table"},{"af":"an old beautiful small wooden table","en":"an old beautiful small wooden table"},{"af":"a beautiful small old wooden table","en":"a beautiful small old wooden table"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Volgorde: mening (*beautiful*) – grootte (*small*) – ouderdom (*old*) – materiaal (*wooden*).","en":"Order: opinion (*beautiful*) – size (*small*) – age (*old*) – material (*wooden*)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte betreklike voornaamwoord in: *The learner ___ bag was stolen reported it to the principal.*","en":"Fill in the correct relative pronoun: *The learner ___ bag was stolen reported it to the principal.*"},"answers":{"af":["whose"],"en":["whose"]},"explain":{"af":"Dit gaan oor besit (die leerder se tas), dus *whose*. *Who's* beteken *who is* – *who is bag* maak nie sin nie.","en":"This is about possession (the learner's bag), so *whose*. *Who's* means *who is* – *who is bag* makes no sense."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["who's","who","whom"],"en":["who's","who","whom"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Although it rained, the match continued.* Watter woordsoort is *although*?","en":"*Although it rained, the match continued.* What part of speech is *although*?"},"options":[{"af":"neweskikkende voegwoord","en":"coordinating conjunction"},{"af":"onderskikkende voegwoord","en":"subordinating conjunction"},{"af":"voorsetsel","en":"preposition"},{"af":"bywoord van tyd","en":"adverb of time"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Although* begin 'n bysin (*although it rained*) wat nie alleen kan staan nie, dus 'n onderskikkende voegwoord. Die neweskikkende voegwoorde is net FANBOYS: *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so*.","en":"*Although* begins a subordinate clause (*although it rained*) that cannot stand alone, so it is a subordinating conjunction. The coordinating conjunctions are only FANBOYS: *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Sipho works hard every afternoon at the mine.* Watter woordsoort is *hard* in hierdie sin?","en":"*Sipho works hard every afternoon at the mine.* What part of speech is *hard* in this sentence?"},"options":[{"af":"byvoeglike naamwoord","en":"adjective"},{"af":"selfstandige naamwoord","en":"noun"},{"af":"bywoord","en":"adverb"},{"af":"voorsetsel","en":"preposition"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*Hard* sê **hoe** Sipho werk – dit beskryf die werkwoord *works*, dus 'n bywoord (sonder -ly). In *a hard test* beskryf dit 'n naamwoord en is dit 'n byvoeglike naamwoord. Pasop: *hardly* beteken \"skaars\".","en":"*Hard* tells **how** Sipho works – it describes the verb *works*, so it is an adverb (without -ly). In *a hard test* it describes a noun and is an adjective. Careful: *hardly* means \"barely\"."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Swimming in the Crocodile River is dangerous.* Wat is *Swimming* in hierdie sin?","en":"*Swimming in the Crocodile River is dangerous.* What is *Swimming* in this sentence?"},"options":[{"af":"'n gerundium – 'n werkwoordvorm wat as selfstandige naamwoord werk","en":"a gerund – a verb form that works as a noun"},{"af":"'n teenwoordige deelwoord in 'n deurlopende tyd","en":"a present participle in a continuous tense"},{"af":"'n byvoeglike naamwoord","en":"an adjective"},{"af":"'n bywoord van wyse","en":"an adverb of manner"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Swimming* is die onderwerp van die werkwoord *is* – dit werk soos 'n naamwoord, dus 'n gerundium. In *He is swimming* sou dit 'n deelwoord in 'n deurlopende tyd wees.","en":"*Swimming* is the subject of the verb *is* – it works like a noun, so it is a gerund. In *He is swimming* it would be a participle in a continuous tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is heeltemal KORREK?","en":"Which sentence is completely CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"Me and him went to the braai.","en":"Me and him went to the braai."},{"af":"The coach gave the medals to Sipho and I.","en":"The coach gave the medals to Sipho and I."},{"af":"Nobody have seen the keys.","en":"Nobody have seen the keys."},{"af":"She and I were chosen for the team.","en":"She and I were chosen for the team."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*She and I* is die onderwerp, dus onderwerpsvorms – reg. A moet *He and I* wees; B moet *to Sipho and me* wees (ná 'n voorsetsel); C moet *Nobody has* wees (onbepaalde voornaamwoord + enkelvoud).","en":"*She and I* is the subject, so subject forms – correct. A must be *He and I*; B must be *to Sipho and me* (after a preposition); C must be *Nobody has* (indefinite pronoun + singular)."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t1-tenses-concord","title":{"af":"Tye en kongruensie","en":"Tenses and concord"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinne in enige tyd kan herskryf, onreëlmatige werkwoorde korrek gebruik, kongruensiefoute regstel en vraagstertjies byvoeg.","en":"You will be able to rewrite sentences in any tense, use irregular verbs correctly, correct concord errors and add question tags."},"summary":{"af":"## Die tye (*tenses*)\n\nElke tyd het 'n **tydsvorm** (teenwoordig, verlede, toekomend) en 'n **aspek** (eenvoudig, deurlopend, voltooid).\n\n| | Teenwoordig (*present*) | Verlede (*past*) | Toekomend (*future*) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Eenvoudig (*simple*) | I **play** / she **plays** | I **played** | I **will play** |\n| Deurlopend (*continuous*) | I **am playing** | I **was playing** | I **will be playing** |\n| Voltooid (*perfect*) | I **have played** | I **had played** | I **will have played** |\n\n- **Eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd:** gewoontes en feite: *She plays netball every Friday.* Onthou die **-s** by *he/she/it*.\n- **Deurlopende tye:** 'n aksie wat op 'n sekere oomblik aan die gang is: *We were eating when the power went off.*\n- **Teenwoordige voltooide tyd:** 'n verlede aksie wat nou nog saak maak, sonder 'n vaste verlede tyd: *I have lost my key.*\n- **Verlede voltooide tyd:** 'n aksie wat klaar was **voor** 'n ander verlede aksie: *The taxi **had left** when we arrived.*\n- **Teenwoordige voltooid deurlopend** (*present perfect continuous*): het in die verlede begin en gaan nou nog aan: *I have been studying for two hours.*\n\n### Seinwoorde (*signal words*)\n\n| Seinwoord | Tyd |\n|---|---|\n| *yesterday, last week, ago, in 2020* | eenvoudige verlede: *I saw him yesterday.* |\n| *since, for, already, just, yet, ever, never* | voltooide tye: *We have lived here since 2019.* |\n| *now, at the moment, Look!, Listen!* | deurlopende tye: *He is studying now.* |\n| *every day, always, usually* | eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd |\n| *tomorrow, next week* | toekomende tyd |\n\n### Onreëlmatige werkwoorde (*irregular verbs*)\n\n| Infinitief | Verlede tyd | Voltooide deelwoord |\n|---|---|---|\n| go | went | gone |\n| write | wrote | written |\n| bring | brought | brought |\n| swim | swam | swum |\n| eat | ate | eaten |\n| begin | began | begun |\n| choose | chose | chosen |\n| lie (lê, rus) | lay | lain |\n| lay (neersit) | laid | laid |\n| lie (jok) | lied | lied |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *lie* en *lay* verwar. *I **lay** on the bed yesterday* (gelê) teenoor *She **laid** the books on the table* (neergesit). *Lay* het altyd 'n voorwerp: jy sit **iets** neer.\n\n### Tipiese foute van Afrikaanssprekendes\n\n| ✘ Fout | ✔ Reg | Hoekom |\n|---|---|---|\n| *I am staying in Brits.* | *I live in Brits.* | \"Bly\" beteken hier woon – iets permanents, dus die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd. |\n| *I have seen him yesterday.* | *I saw him yesterday.* | *Yesterday* = eenvoudige verlede; nooit saam met *have* nie. |\n| *Borrow me your pen.* | *Lend me your pen.* | *Lend* = vir 'n ruk gee; *borrow* = by iemand neem. |\n| *I am here since Monday.* | *I have been here since Monday.* | *Since* vra 'n voltooide tyd. |\n\n## Kongruensie (*concord*)\n\nDie werkwoord moet met sy **onderwerp** ooreenstem: enkelvoud by enkelvoud, meervoud by meervoud. In die teenwoordige tyd kry 'n enkelvoudige onderwerp die -s: *The boy **runs**; the boys **run**.*\n\n1. ***Each, every, everyone, everybody, nobody, someone*** → enkelvoud: *Everyone **has** a ticket. Each of the girls **is** ready.*\n2. ***One of the …*** → enkelvoud, want die onderwerp is *one*: *One of the boys **is** absent.*\n3. Woorde **tussen** die onderwerp en die werkwoord verander niks: *The box of apples **is** heavy. The captain, as well as his players, **is** here.*\n4. ***Neither … nor / either … or*** → die werkwoord stem ooreen met die **naaste** onderwerp: *Neither the coach nor the players **were** happy. Either the players or the coach **is** to blame.*\n5. ***The number of …*** → enkelvoud; ***a number of …*** (= baie) → meervoud: *The number of learners **is** growing. A number of learners **are** absent.*\n6. ***There is / there are*** → kyk na die naamwoord ná die werkwoord: *There **is** a taxi. There **are** two taxis.*\n7. **Versamelname** kry gewoonlik 'n enkelvoudige werkwoord: *The team **is** training.*\n8. Twee onderwerpe met ***and*** → meervoud: *Sipho and Lerato **are** friends.*\n\n## Vraagstertjies (*question tags*)\n\n'n Kort vraag aan die einde van 'n stelling wat bevestiging vra.\n\n- Positiewe stelling → negatiewe stertjie; negatiewe stelling → positiewe stertjie.\n- Gebruik dieselfde hulpwerkwoord plus 'n voornaamwoord: *He is tall, **isn't he?***\n- Geen hulpwerkwoord nie? Gebruik *do/does/did*: *She plays netball, **doesn't she?** They won, **didn't they?***\n- *You didn't go, **did you?***\n- *Never, nobody, hardly* is negatief: *He never cheats, **does he?***\n- Spesiale gevalle: *I am right, **aren't I?*** · *Let's go, **shall we?*** · *Close the door, **will you?***\n\n> **Wenk:** Om 'n kongruensiefout te vind, soek eers die **regte onderwerp** (wie of wat doen die aksie?) en ignoreer die woorde tussenin. Lees die sin dan sonder hulle.\n\nIn die eksamen moet jy 'n sin in 'n gegewe tyd herskryf, die regte werkwoordvorm kies, 'n kongruensiefout regstel, 'n vraagstertjie byvoeg en die voltooide deelwoord gee.","en":"## Tenses\n\nEvery tense has a **time** (present, past, future) and an **aspect** (simple, continuous, perfect).\n\n| | Present | Past | Future |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Simple | I **play** / she **plays** | I **played** | I **will play** |\n| Continuous | I **am playing** | I **was playing** | I **will be playing** |\n| Perfect | I **have played** | I **had played** | I **will have played** |\n\n- **Simple present:** habits and facts: *She plays netball every Friday.* Remember the **-s** with *he/she/it*.\n- **Continuous tenses:** an action in progress at a certain moment: *We were eating when the power went off.*\n- **Present perfect:** a past action that still matters now, without a fixed past time: *I have lost my key.*\n- **Past perfect:** an action that was finished **before** another past action: *The taxi **had left** when we arrived.*\n- **Present perfect continuous:** started in the past and is still going on: *I have been studying for two hours.*\n\n### Signal words\n\n| Signal word | Tense |\n|---|---|\n| *yesterday, last week, ago, in 2020* | simple past: *I saw him yesterday.* |\n| *since, for, already, just, yet, ever, never* | perfect tenses: *We have lived here since 2019.* |\n| *now, at the moment, Look!, Listen!* | continuous tenses: *He is studying now.* |\n| *every day, always, usually* | simple present |\n| *tomorrow, next week* | future |\n\n### Irregular verbs\n\n| Infinitive | Past tense | Past participle |\n|---|---|---|\n| go | went | gone |\n| write | wrote | written |\n| bring | brought | brought |\n| swim | swam | swum |\n| eat | ate | eaten |\n| begin | began | begun |\n| choose | chose | chosen |\n| lie (rest) | lay | lain |\n| lay (put down) | laid | laid |\n| lie (tell a lie) | lied | lied |\n\n> **Common mistake:** confusing *lie* and *lay*. *I **lay** on the bed yesterday* (rested) versus *She **laid** the books on the table* (put down). *Lay* always has an object: you put **something** down.\n\n### Typical errors of Afrikaans speakers\n\n| ✘ Error | ✔ Correct | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| *I am staying in Brits.* | *I live in Brits.* | The Afrikaans \"bly\" means \"live\" here – something permanent, so the simple present. |\n| *I have seen him yesterday.* | *I saw him yesterday.* | *Yesterday* = simple past; never with *have*. |\n| *Borrow me your pen.* | *Lend me your pen.* | *Lend* = give for a while; *borrow* = take from someone. |\n| *I am here since Monday.* | *I have been here since Monday.* | *Since* needs a perfect tense. |\n\n## Concord\n\nThe verb must agree with its **subject**: singular with singular, plural with plural. In the present tense a singular subject takes the -s: *The boy **runs**; the boys **run**.*\n\n1. ***Each, every, everyone, everybody, nobody, someone*** → singular: *Everyone **has** a ticket. Each of the girls **is** ready.*\n2. ***One of the …*** → singular, because the subject is *one*: *One of the boys **is** absent.*\n3. Words **between** the subject and the verb change nothing: *The box of apples **is** heavy. The captain, as well as his players, **is** here.*\n4. ***Neither … nor / either … or*** → the verb agrees with the **nearer** subject: *Neither the coach nor the players **were** happy. Either the players or the coach **is** to blame.*\n5. ***The number of …*** → singular; ***a number of …*** (= many) → plural: *The number of learners **is** growing. A number of learners **are** absent.*\n6. ***There is / there are*** → look at the noun after the verb: *There **is** a taxi. There **are** two taxis.*\n7. **Collective nouns** usually take a singular verb: *The team **is** training.*\n8. Two subjects joined by ***and*** → plural: *Sipho and Lerato **are** friends.*\n\n## Question tags\n\nA short question at the end of a statement that asks for confirmation.\n\n- Positive statement → negative tag; negative statement → positive tag.\n- Use the same auxiliary verb plus a pronoun: *He is tall, **isn't he?***\n- No auxiliary? Use *do/does/did*: *She plays netball, **doesn't she?** They won, **didn't they?***\n- *You didn't go, **did you?***\n- *Never, nobody, hardly* are negative: *He never cheats, **does he?***\n- Special cases: *I am right, **aren't I?*** · *Let's go, **shall we?*** · *Close the door, **will you?***\n\n> **Tip:** To find a concord error, first find the **real subject** (who or what does the action?) and ignore the words in between. Then read the sentence without them.\n\nIn the exam you must rewrite a sentence in a given tense, choose the correct verb form, correct a concord error, add a question tag and give the past participle."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Tyd","en":"Tense"},"def":{"af":"Die vorm van die werkwoord wat wys wanneer 'n aksie plaasvind: teenwoordig, verlede of toekomend.","en":"The form of the verb that shows when an action happens: present, past or future."}},{"term":{"af":"Eenvoudige verlede tyd","en":"Simple past tense"},"def":{"af":"'n Afgehandelde aksie op 'n bepaalde tyd in die verlede: *I saw him yesterday.*","en":"A completed action at a definite time in the past: *I saw him yesterday.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Deurlopende tyd","en":"Continuous tense"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd wat wys dat 'n aksie aan die gang is: *be* + -ing-vorm, bv. *She is reading.*","en":"The tense that shows an action in progress: *be* + -ing form, e.g. *She is reading.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Voltooide tyd","en":"Perfect tense"},"def":{"af":"*have/has/had* + voltooide deelwoord: *They have finished.*","en":"*have/has/had* + past participle: *They have finished.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Voltooide deelwoord","en":"Past participle"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoordvorm wat ná *have/has/had* (en in die lydende vorm) gebruik word, bv. *written, gone, swum*.","en":"The verb form used after *have/has/had* (and in the passive), e.g. *written, gone, swum*."}},{"term":{"af":"Onreëlmatige werkwoord","en":"Irregular verb"},"def":{"af":"'n Werkwoord wat nie -ed in die verlede tyd kry nie: *go – went – gone*.","en":"A verb that does not take -ed in the past tense: *go – went – gone*."}},{"term":{"af":"Seinwoord","en":"Signal word"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat aandui watter tyd nodig is, bv. *yesterday* (eenvoudige verlede) of *since* (voltooid).","en":"A word that shows which tense is needed, e.g. *yesterday* (simple past) or *since* (perfect)."}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerp","en":"Subject"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die aksie in die sin uitvoer; die werkwoord stem daarmee ooreen.","en":"The person or thing that performs the action in the sentence; the verb agrees with it."}},{"term":{"af":"Kongruensie","en":"Concord (subject–verb agreement)"},"def":{"af":"Die ooreenstemming tussen onderwerp en werkwoord in getal: *The dog barks / The dogs bark.*","en":"The agreement in number between subject and verb: *The dog barks / The dogs bark.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Vraagstertjie","en":"Question tag"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort vraag aan die einde van 'n stelling, bv. *…, isn't he?* of *…, did you?*","en":"A short question at the end of a statement, e.g. *…, isn't he?* or *…, did you?*"}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Herskryf in die gegewe tyd","en":"Rewrite in the given tense"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf *Lerato writes a letter to her gran.* in die (a) eenvoudige verlede tyd, (b) verlede deurlopende tyd, (c) teenwoordige voltooide tyd en (d) eenvoudige toekomende tyd.","en":"Rewrite *Lerato writes a letter to her gran.* in the (a) simple past, (b) past continuous, (c) present perfect and (d) simple future tense."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *Write* is onreëlmatig: write – **wrote** – written. ***Lerato wrote a letter to her gran.***","en":"(a) *Write* is irregular: write – **wrote** – written. ***Lerato wrote a letter to her gran.***"},{"af":"(b) Verlede deurlopend = *was/were* + -ing. *Lerato* is enkelvoud → *was*. ***Lerato was writing a letter to her gran.***","en":"(b) Past continuous = *was/were* + -ing. *Lerato* is singular → *was*. ***Lerato was writing a letter to her gran.***"},{"af":"(c) Teenwoordig voltooid = *has/have* + voltooide deelwoord. Enkelvoud → *has*; deelwoord → *written* (dubbel t). ***Lerato has written a letter to her gran.***","en":"(c) Present perfect = *has/have* + past participle. Singular → *has*; participle → *written* (double t). ***Lerato has written a letter to her gran.***"},{"af":"(d) Eenvoudige toekomend = *will* + infinitief (sonder -s). ***Lerato will write a letter to her gran.***","en":"(d) Simple future = *will* + infinitive (without -s). ***Lerato will write a letter to her gran.***"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) wrote (b) was writing (c) has written (d) will write","en":"(a) wrote (b) was writing (c) has written (d) will write"}},{"title":{"af":"Stel die kongruensiefoute reg","en":"Correct the concord errors"},"problem":{"af":"Elke sin het een kongruensiefout. Herskryf dit korrek.\n(a) *Each of the players have a new jersey.*\n(b) *Neither my brother nor my parents was at home.*\n(c) *There is many taxis at the Brits rank.*\n(d) *The number of learners who take the bus are growing.*","en":"Each sentence has one concord error. Rewrite it correctly.\n(a) *Each of the players have a new jersey.*\n(b) *Neither my brother nor my parents was at home.*\n(c) *There is many taxis at the Brits rank.*\n(d) *The number of learners who take the bus are growing.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die onderwerp is *each* (enkelvoud), nie *players* nie → ***Each of the players has a new jersey.***","en":"(a) The subject is *each* (singular), not *players* → ***Each of the players has a new jersey.***"},{"af":"(b) *Neither … nor*: die werkwoord stem ooreen met die naaste onderwerp, *parents* (meervoud) → ***Neither my brother nor my parents were at home.***","en":"(b) *Neither … nor*: the verb agrees with the nearer subject, *parents* (plural) → ***Neither my brother nor my parents were at home.***"},{"af":"(c) Kyk na die naamwoord ná die werkwoord: *many taxis* is meervoud → ***There are many taxis at the Brits rank.***","en":"(c) Look at the noun after the verb: *many taxis* is plural → ***There are many taxis at the Brits rank.***"},{"af":"(d) *The number of …* is enkelvoud; *who take the bus* is net tussenwoorde → ***The number of learners who take the bus is growing.***","en":"(d) *The number of …* is singular; *who take the bus* is only words in between → ***The number of learners who take the bus is growing.***"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) has (b) were (c) are (d) is","en":"(a) has (b) were (c) are (d) is"}},{"title":{"af":"Voeg vraagstertjies by","en":"Add question tags"},"problem":{"af":"Voeg die regte vraagstertjie by:\n(a) *Sipho is in Grade 10, ___?*\n(b) *They didn't finish the race, ___?*\n(c) *Your mother works at the mine, ___?*\n(d) *I am late again, ___?*","en":"Add the correct question tag:\n(a) *Sipho is in Grade 10, ___?*\n(b) *They didn't finish the race, ___?*\n(c) *Your mother works at the mine, ___?*\n(d) *I am late again, ___?*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Positiewe stelling met *is* → negatiewe stertjie met *is* + voornaamwoord: ***isn't he?***","en":"(a) Positive statement with *is* → negative tag with *is* + pronoun: ***isn't he?***"},{"af":"(b) Negatiewe stelling (*didn't*) → positiewe stertjie: ***did they?***","en":"(b) Negative statement (*didn't*) → positive tag: ***did they?***"},{"af":"(c) Geen hulpwerkwoord nie; *works* is eenvoudige teenwoordig, enkelvoud → *does*. Positief → negatief: ***doesn't she?***","en":"(c) No auxiliary; *works* is simple present, singular → *does*. Positive → negative: ***doesn't she?***"},{"af":"(d) Spesiale geval: *I am* → ***aren't I?*** (*amn't I* is nie standaard Engels nie).","en":"(d) Special case: *I am* → ***aren't I?*** (*amn't I* is not standard English)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) isn't he? (b) did they? (c) doesn't she? (d) aren't I?","en":"(a) isn't he? (b) did they? (c) doesn't she? (d) aren't I?"}},{"title":{"af":"Redigeer: tye en Afrikaanse foute","en":"Edit: tenses and Afrikaans-influenced errors"},"problem":{"af":"Stel die drie foute in hierdie paragraaf reg:\n\n*I am staying in Brits since 2015. Yesterday my friend has borrowed me his bike and we have rode to the dam.*","en":"Correct the three errors in this paragraph:\n\n*I am staying in Brits since 2015. Yesterday my friend has borrowed me his bike and we have rode to the dam.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1: *since 2015* vra 'n voltooide tyd, en *staying* is die Afrikaanse \"bly\" → ***I have lived in Brits since 2015.***","en":"Error 1: *since 2015* needs a perfect tense, and *staying* comes from the Afrikaans \"bly\" → ***I have lived in Brits since 2015.***"},{"af":"Fout 2: *Yesterday* vra die eenvoudige verlede tyd, en die vriend **gee** die fiets → *lend*, nie *borrow* nie: lend – **lent** → ***my friend lent me his bike***","en":"Error 2: *Yesterday* needs the simple past, and the friend **gives** the bike → *lend*, not *borrow*: lend – **lent** → ***my friend lent me his bike***"},{"af":"Fout 3: steeds *yesterday* → eenvoudige verlede. (*Have rode* is in elk geval verkeerd; die deelwoord is *ridden*.) ride – **rode** → ***we rode to the dam***","en":"Error 3: still *yesterday* → simple past. (*Have rode* is wrong anyway; the participle is *ridden*.) ride – **rode** → ***we rode to the dam***"}],"answer":{"af":"I have lived in Brits since 2015. Yesterday my friend lent me his bike and we rode to the dam.","en":"I have lived in Brits since 2015. Yesterday my friend lent me his bike and we rode to the dam."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die voltooide deelwoord (*past participle*) van *write*?","en":"What is the past participle of *write*?"},"options":[{"af":"wrote","en":"wrote"},{"af":"writed","en":"writed"},{"af":"written","en":"written"},{"af":"writen","en":"writen"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"write – wrote – **written** (met dubbel t). *Wrote* is die verlede tyd; *writed* en *writen* bestaan nie.","en":"write – wrote – **written** (with double t). *Wrote* is the past tense; *writed* and *writen* do not exist."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die verlede tyd van *bring*: *Yesterday Thabo ___ his guitar to school.*","en":"Give the past tense of *bring*: *Yesterday Thabo ___ his guitar to school.*"},"answers":{"af":["brought"],"en":["brought"]},"explain":{"af":"*Bring* is onreëlmatig: bring – brought – brought. Moenie dit met *sing – sang – sung* verwar nie.","en":"*Bring* is irregular: bring – brought – brought. Do not confuse it with *sing – sang – sung*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brang","bringed","brung"],"en":["brang","bringed","brung"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die seinwoord *yesterday* vra die eenvoudige verlede tyd.","en":"The signal word *yesterday* needs the simple past tense."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Yesterday* is 'n vaste tyd in die verlede, dus *I saw him yesterday* – nooit *I have seen him yesterday* nie.","en":"True. *Yesterday* is a fixed time in the past, so *I saw him yesterday* – never *I have seen him yesterday*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter tyd is hierdie sin? *They have finished their homework.*","en":"Which tense is this sentence in? *They have finished their homework.*"},"options":[{"af":"eenvoudige verlede tyd","en":"simple past tense"},{"af":"teenwoordige voltooide tyd","en":"present perfect tense"},{"af":"verlede voltooide tyd","en":"past perfect tense"},{"af":"teenwoordige deurlopende tyd","en":"present continuous tense"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Have* + voltooide deelwoord (*finished*) = teenwoordige voltooide tyd. Met *had finished* sou dit verlede voltooid wees.","en":"*Have* + past participle (*finished*) = present perfect. With *had finished* it would be the past perfect."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte vorm van *be* (verlede tyd) in: *Neither the coach nor the players ___ happy after the match.*","en":"Fill in the correct form of *be* (past tense): *Neither the coach nor the players ___ happy after the match.*"},"answers":{"af":["were"],"en":["were"]},"explain":{"af":"By *neither … nor* stem die werkwoord ooreen met die **naaste** onderwerp: *players* (meervoud) → *were*. *Are* is teenwoordige tyd.","en":"With *neither … nor* the verb agrees with the **nearer** subject: *players* (plural) → *were*. *Are* is present tense."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["was","are","been"],"en":["was","are","been"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte werkwoord: *One of the boys ___ absent today.*","en":"Choose the correct verb: *One of the boys ___ absent today.*"},"options":[{"af":"is","en":"is"},{"af":"are","en":"are"},{"af":"were","en":"were"},{"af":"be","en":"be"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die onderwerp is *one* (enkelvoud), nie *boys* nie. Daarom *is*.","en":"The subject is *one* (singular), not *boys*. Therefore *is*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voeg die regte vraagstertjie by: *You didn't go to the braai, ___?*","en":"Add the correct question tag: *You didn't go to the braai, ___?*"},"answers":{"af":["did you","did you?"],"en":["did you","did you?"]},"explain":{"af":"Negatiewe stelling (*didn't*) → positiewe stertjie met dieselfde hulpwerkwoord: *did you?*","en":"Negative statement (*didn't*) → positive tag with the same auxiliary: *did you?*"},"choices":{"d":{"af":["didn't you","do you","weren't you"],"en":["didn't you","do you","weren't you"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is KORREK?","en":"Which sentence is CORRECT?"},"options":[{"af":"I have seen him yesterday.","en":"I have seen him yesterday."},{"af":"I seen him yesterday.","en":"I seen him yesterday."},{"af":"I have saw him yesterday.","en":"I have saw him yesterday."},{"af":"I saw him yesterday.","en":"I saw him yesterday."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Yesterday* vra die eenvoudige verlede tyd: *saw*. Die voltooide tyd (*have seen*) gaan nie saam met 'n vaste verlede tyd nie – 'n tipiese Afrikaanse fout (\"Ek het hom gister gesien\").","en":"*Yesterday* needs the simple past: *saw*. The perfect tense (*have seen*) does not go with a fixed past time – a typical Afrikaans-influenced error (\"Ek het hom gister gesien\")."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In *The box of apples are heavy* is die werkwoord korrek, omdat *apples* meervoud is.","en":"In *The box of apples are heavy* the verb is correct, because *apples* is plural."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die onderwerp is *box* (enkelvoud); *of apples* staan net tussenin. Reg: *The box of apples **is** heavy.*","en":"False. The subject is *box* (singular); *of apples* only stands in between. Correct: *The box of apples **is** heavy.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Herskryf in die eenvoudige verlede tyd: *She swims in the river every Saturday.* → *She ___ in the river every Saturday.*","en":"Rewrite in the simple past tense: *She swims in the river every Saturday.* → *She ___ in the river every Saturday.*"},"answers":{"af":["swam"],"en":["swam"]},"explain":{"af":"swim – **swam** – swum. *Swum* is die voltooide deelwoord (ná *have*); *has swum* is die teenwoordige voltooide tyd, nie die eenvoudige verlede nie.","en":"swim – **swam** – swum. *Swum* is the past participle (after *have*); *has swum* is the present perfect, not the simple past."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["swum","swimmed","has swum"],"en":["swum","swimmed","has swum"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke sin by sy tyd.","en":"Match each sentence to its tense."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"I eat.","en":"I eat."},"r":{"af":"eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd","en":"simple present"}},{"l":{"af":"I am eating.","en":"I am eating."},"r":{"af":"teenwoordige deurlopende tyd","en":"present continuous"}},{"l":{"af":"I was eating.","en":"I was eating."},"r":{"af":"verlede deurlopende tyd","en":"past continuous"}},{"l":{"af":"I had eaten.","en":"I had eaten."},"r":{"af":"verlede voltooide tyd","en":"past perfect"}},{"l":{"af":"I will have eaten.","en":"I will have eaten."},"r":{"af":"toekomende voltooide tyd","en":"future perfect"}}],"explain":{"af":"Deurlopend = *be* + -ing; voltooid = *have/had* + voltooide deelwoord; toekomend = *will*.","en":"Continuous = *be* + -ing; perfect = *have/had* + past participle; future = *will*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Kies die regte werkwoord: *Yesterday the tired dog ___ in the shade all afternoon.*","en":"Choose the correct verb: *Yesterday the tired dog ___ in the shade all afternoon.*"},"options":[{"af":"laid","en":"laid"},{"af":"lied","en":"lied"},{"af":"lay","en":"lay"},{"af":"lain","en":"lain"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die hond het **gelê** (gerus) – geen voorwerp nie – dus *lie*, verlede tyd *lay*. *Laid* is van *lay* (iets neersit), *lied* is gejok en *lain* is die voltooide deelwoord.","en":"The dog **rested** – no object – so *lie*, past tense *lay*. *Laid* comes from *lay* (put something down), *lied* means told a lie and *lain* is the past participle."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte vorm van *be* (teenwoordige tyd) in: *A number of learners ___ absent today because of the taxi strike.*","en":"Fill in the correct form of *be* (present tense): *A number of learners ___ absent today because of the taxi strike.*"},"answers":{"af":["are"],"en":["are"]},"explain":{"af":"*A number of* beteken \"baie\" en is meervoud → *are*. Vergelyk: *The number of learners **is** growing* (enkelvoud).","en":"*A number of* means \"many\" and is plural → *are*. Compare: *The number of learners **is** growing* (singular)."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is","was","has"],"en":["is","was","has"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Voeg die regte vraagstertjie by: *Let's go to Hartbeespoort on Saturday, ___*","en":"Add the correct question tag: *Let's go to Hartbeespoort on Saturday, ___*"},"options":[{"af":"shall we?","en":"shall we?"},{"af":"will we?","en":"will we?"},{"af":"don't we?","en":"don't we?"},{"af":"aren't we?","en":"aren't we?"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ná *Let's* (*let us*) is die vaste vraagstertjie *shall we?*. Dit is 'n spesiale geval wat jy moet leer.","en":"After *Let's* (*let us*) the fixed question tag is *shall we?*. It is a special case that you must learn."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het die KORREKTE kongruensie?","en":"Which sentence has CORRECT concord?"},"options":[{"af":"Each of the players have a new jersey.","en":"Each of the players have a new jersey."},{"af":"The number of learners in our school is growing.","en":"The number of learners in our school is growing."},{"af":"Everybody in the class are ready.","en":"Everybody in the class are ready."},{"af":"There is many taxis at the rank.","en":"There is many taxis at the rank."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*The number of …* is enkelvoud → *is*. A moet *has* wees (*each* = enkelvoud), C *is* (*everybody* = enkelvoud) en D *There are* (*many taxis* = meervoud).","en":"*The number of …* is singular → *is*. A must be *has* (*each* = singular), C *is* (*everybody* = singular) and D *There are* (*many taxis* = plural)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin het GEEN fout nie?","en":"Which sentence has NO error?"},"options":[{"af":"Every one of the learners have passed.","en":"Every one of the learners have passed."},{"af":"We have went to Pretoria last week.","en":"We have went to Pretoria last week."},{"af":"My brother borrowed me his calculator.","en":"My brother borrowed me his calculator."},{"af":"I have been studying since six o'clock.","en":"I have been studying since six o'clock."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Since* vra 'n voltooide tyd, en *have been studying* is die teenwoordige voltooid deurlopende tyd – reg. A: *has passed* (*every one* = enkelvoud). B: *We went … last week* (vaste verlede tyd; *went* is ook nie 'n deelwoord nie). C: *lent me* (*lend* = gee).","en":"*Since* needs a perfect tense, and *have been studying* is the present perfect continuous – correct. A: *has passed* (*every one* = singular). B: *We went … last week* (fixed past time; *went* is not a participle either). C: *lent me* (*lend* = give)."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t1-essay","title":{"af":"Opstelskryf","en":"Essay writing"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die regte opstelsoort vir 'n onderwerp kan kies, dit beplan en 'n goed gestruktureerde opstel van 150–200 woorde skryf en redigeer.","en":"You will be able to choose the right type of essay for a topic, plan it, and write and edit a well-structured essay of 150–200 words."},"summary":{"af":"## Vraestel 3: Skryfwerk\n\nVraestel 3 (*Paper 3: Writing*) tel **100 punte**:\n\n| Afdeling | Wat jy skryf | Lengte (Gr 10) | Punte |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | **Een** opstel (*essay*) | 150–200 woorde | 50 |\n| B | Langer transaksionele teks | 120–150 woorde | 30 |\n| C | Korter teks | 80–100 woorde | 20 |\n\nIn Graad 12 (NSS) is die opstel 250–300 woorde, so die lengte groei elke jaar.\n\n## Opstelsoorte (*types of essays*)\n\n| Soort | Kenmerke |\n|---|---|\n| **Verhalend** (*narrative*) | Vertel 'n storie: begin → komplikasie → klimaks → oplossing. Gewoonlik in die **verlede tyd**; dialoog maak dit lewendig. |\n| **Beskrywend** (*descriptive*) | Skilder 'n prentjie met woorde: die **vyf sintuie**, sterk byvoeglike naamwoorde en beeldspraak. |\n| **Argumenterend** (*argumentative*) | Kies **een** kant en verdedig dit met sterk redes; eindig met 'n oortuigende slot. |\n| **Besprekend** (*discursive*) | Bespreek **albei** kante gebalanseerd, in 'n onpersoonlike toon; die slot weeg die argumente op. |\n| **Refleksief** (*reflective*) | Jou persoonlike gedagtes en gevoelens oor 'n ervaring of idee, en wat jy daaruit geleer het. |\n| **Prentopstel** (*picture-based*) | Gee jou eie titel; die opstel moet duidelik by die prent aansluit. |\n| **Verklarend** (*expository*) | Verduidelik 'n onderwerp of proses feitelik en logies. |\n\n> **Wenk:** Lees die onderwerp twee keer en onderstreep die sleutelwoorde. *Do you agree?* = argumenterend; *Discuss* of *advantages and disadvantages* = besprekend; *Describe* = beskrywend.\n\n### *Show, don't tell*\n\nMoenie net sê hoe iemand voel nie – **wys** dit deur aksies en besonderhede.\n- *Tell:* *I was scared.*\n- *Show:* *My knees shook and my mouth went dry.*\n\n## Die skryfproses\n\n1. **Beplanning:** maak 'n breinkaart (*mind map*) of 'n lys sleutelwoorde. Die beplanning **moet in jou antwoordboek wys**; trek 'n streep daardeur wanneer jy klaar is.\n2. **Eerste konsep** (*draft*).\n3. **Redigeer** (*edit*): verbeter inhoud, sinsbou, paragrawe en woordkeuse.\n4. **Proeflees** (*proofread*): spelling, leestekens, tye en kongruensie.\n5. **Finale weergawe** met 'n **titel**. Die titel tel nie by die woordtal nie. Skryf die **woordtal** aan die einde.\n\n## Paragrawe en verbindingswoorde\n\nElke paragraaf het **een hoofgedagte**, gestel in die **kernsin** (*topic sentence*) – gewoonlik die eerste sin. Die res van die paragraaf brei uit met besonderhede en voorbeelde.\n\nStruktuur: **inleiding** met 'n haak (*hook*) wat die leser se aandag trek → **middelparagrawe** → **slot**.\n\n| Funksie | Verbindingswoorde |\n|---|---|\n| Volgorde | *firstly, secondly, then, finally* |\n| Byvoeging | *furthermore, in addition, also* |\n| Kontras | *however, on the other hand, although* |\n| Gevolg | *as a result, therefore, consequently* |\n| Slot | *in conclusion, to sum up* |\n\n## Die rubriek (50 punte)\n\n| Kriterium | Punte |\n|---|---|\n| Inhoud en beplanning | 30 |\n| Taal, styl en redigering | 15 |\n| Struktuur | 5 |\n\nInhoud is die meeste werd: bly by die onderwerp, wees oorspronklik en hou die leser se aandag van die eerste tot die laaste sin.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- Te lank of te kort – hou by 150–200 woorde.\n- Tye wissel: *We walked … suddenly a dog **jumps** …* ✘ – bly in die verlede tyd.\n- Afrikaanse uitdrukkings letterlik vertaal: *close the light* ✘ → *switch off the light* ✔; *make a photo* ✘ → *take a photo* ✔; *learn me* ✘ → *teach me* ✔.\n- Geen paragrawe nie – een lang blok teks.\n- Sleng en SMS-taal (*lekker, bru, gonna, u r*) in 'n opstel.\n- Die verkeerde soort opstel, bv. albei kante in 'n argumenterende opstel.\n\n> **Onthou!** Die eksaminator soek 'n sigbare **beplanning**, die regte **soort** opstel, duidelike **paragrawe** en korrekte **taal**.\n\nIn die eksamen kan jy gevra word om die opstelsoort van 'n onderwerp te identifiseer, 'n opstel te beplan, 'n inleiding te skryf en 'n paragraaf met foute te redigeer.","en":"## Paper 3: Writing\n\nPaper 3 is worth **100 marks**:\n\n| Section | What you write | Length (Gr 10) | Marks |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | **One** essay | 150–200 words | 50 |\n| B | Longer transactional text | 120–150 words | 30 |\n| C | Shorter text | 80–100 words | 20 |\n\nIn Grade 12 (NSC) the essay is 250–300 words, so the length grows every year.\n\n## Types of essays\n\n| Type | Features |\n|---|---|\n| **Narrative** | Tells a story: beginning → complication → climax → resolution. Usually in the **past tense**; dialogue brings it to life. |\n| **Descriptive** | Paints a picture with words: the **five senses**, strong adjectives and figurative language. |\n| **Argumentative** | Chooses **one** side and defends it with strong reasons; ends with a persuasive conclusion. |\n| **Discursive** | Discusses **both** sides in a balanced way, in an impersonal tone; the conclusion weighs up the arguments. |\n| **Reflective** | Your personal thoughts and feelings about an experience or idea, and what you learnt from it. |\n| **Picture-based** | Give your own title; the essay must clearly link to the picture. |\n| **Expository** | Explains a topic or process factually and logically. |\n\n> **Tip:** Read the topic twice and underline the keywords. *Do you agree?* = argumentative; *Discuss* or *advantages and disadvantages* = discursive; *Describe* = descriptive.\n\n### Show, don't tell\n\nDo not just say how someone feels – **show** it through actions and details.\n- *Tell:* *I was scared.*\n- *Show:* *My knees shook and my mouth went dry.*\n\n## The writing process\n\n1. **Planning:** make a mind map or a list of keywords. The planning **must be visible in your answer book**; draw a line through it when you are done.\n2. **First draft.**\n3. **Edit:** improve content, sentence structure, paragraphs and word choice.\n4. **Proofread:** spelling, punctuation, tenses and concord.\n5. **Final version** with a **title**. The title is not counted in the word count. Write the **word count** at the end.\n\n## Paragraphs and linking words\n\nEach paragraph has **one main idea**, stated in the **topic sentence** – usually the first sentence. The rest of the paragraph develops it with details and examples.\n\nStructure: **introduction** with a hook that grabs the reader's attention → **body paragraphs** → **conclusion**.\n\n| Function | Linking words |\n|---|---|\n| Sequence | *firstly, secondly, then, finally* |\n| Addition | *furthermore, in addition, also* |\n| Contrast | *however, on the other hand, although* |\n| Result | *as a result, therefore, consequently* |\n| Conclusion | *in conclusion, to sum up* |\n\n## The rubric (50 marks)\n\n| Criterion | Marks |\n|---|---|\n| Content and planning | 30 |\n| Language, style and editing | 15 |\n| Structure | 5 |\n\nContent is worth the most: stick to the topic, be original and hold the reader's attention from the first to the last sentence.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- Too long or too short – keep to 150–200 words.\n- Switching tenses: *We walked … suddenly a dog **jumps** …* ✘ – stay in the past tense.\n- Afrikaans expressions translated literally: *close the light* ✘ → *switch off the light* ✔; *make a photo* ✘ → *take a photo* ✔; *learn me* ✘ → *teach me* ✔.\n- No paragraphs – one long block of text.\n- Slang and SMS language (*lekker, bru, gonna, u r*) in an essay.\n- The wrong type of essay, e.g. both sides in an argumentative essay.\n\n> **Remember!** The examiner looks for visible **planning**, the right **type** of essay, clear **paragraphs** and correct **language**.\n\nIn the exam you may be asked to identify the type of essay a topic asks for, plan an essay, write an introduction and edit a paragraph with errors."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Opstel","en":"Essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Langer kreatiewe of feitelike teks in paragrawe oor een onderwerp; in Gr 10 150–200 woorde (Vraestel 3, Afdeling A).","en":"A longer creative or factual text in paragraphs on one topic; 150–200 words in Gr 10 (Paper 3, Section A)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verhalende opstel","en":"Narrative essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat 'n storie vertel met 'n komplikasie, klimaks en oplossing.","en":"An essay that tells a story with a complication, climax and resolution."}},{"term":{"af":"Beskrywende opstel","en":"Descriptive essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat 'n persoon, plek of gebeurtenis met die vyf sintuie en beeldspraak beskryf.","en":"An essay that describes a person, place or event using the five senses and figurative language."}},{"term":{"af":"Argumenterende opstel","en":"Argumentative essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat een kant van 'n saak kies en dit met sterk redes verdedig.","en":"An essay that chooses one side of an issue and defends it with strong reasons."}},{"term":{"af":"Besprekende opstel","en":"Discursive essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat albei kante van 'n saak gebalanseerd en onpersoonlik bespreek.","en":"An essay that discusses both sides of an issue in a balanced, impersonal way."}},{"term":{"af":"Refleksiewe opstel","en":"Reflective essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel oor jou persoonlike gedagtes, gevoelens en lesse uit 'n ervaring.","en":"An essay about your personal thoughts, feelings and lessons from an experience."}},{"term":{"af":"Verklarende opstel","en":"Expository essay"},"def":{"af":"'n Opstel wat 'n onderwerp of proses feitelik en logies verduidelik.","en":"An essay that explains a topic or process factually and logically."}},{"term":{"af":"Kernsin","en":"Topic sentence"},"def":{"af":"Die sin (gewoonlik die eerste) wat die hoofgedagte van 'n paragraaf stel.","en":"The sentence (usually the first) that states the main idea of a paragraph."}},{"term":{"af":"Verbindingswoorde","en":"Linking words"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat sinne en paragrawe logies verbind, bv. *however, furthermore, as a result*.","en":"Words that connect sentences and paragraphs logically, e.g. *however, furthermore, as a result*."}},{"term":{"af":"Beplanning","en":"Planning"},"def":{"af":"Die breinkaart of lys sleutelwoorde wat jy voor die skryf maak; dit moet sigbaar wees en dan deurgetrek word.","en":"The mind map or list of keywords you make before writing; it must be visible and then crossed out."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die opstelsoort","en":"Identify the type of essay"},"problem":{"af":"Watter soort opstel vra elke onderwerp?\n(a) *The day I got lost in the Magaliesberg*\n(b) *Describe a summer thunderstorm over Hartbeespoort Dam.*\n(c) *Schools should start at nine o'clock. Do you agree?*\n(d) *The advantages and disadvantages of cellphones at school*","en":"Which type of essay does each topic ask for?\n(a) *The day I got lost in the Magaliesberg*\n(b) *Describe a summer thunderstorm over Hartbeespoort Dam.*\n(c) *Schools should start at nine o'clock. Do you agree?*\n(d) *The advantages and disadvantages of cellphones at school*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *The day I …* vra na 'n gebeurtenis met 'n begin, komplikasie (verdwaal) en oplossing → **narrative** (verhalend).","en":"(a) *The day I …* asks for an event with a beginning, complication (getting lost) and resolution → **narrative**."},{"af":"(b) Die opdragwoord *Describe* en 'n toneel wat jy kan sien, hoor en ruik → **descriptive** (beskrywend).","en":"(b) The command word *Describe* and a scene you can see, hear and smell → **descriptive**."},{"af":"(c) *Do you agree?* vra dat jy 'n kant kies en dit verdedig → **argumentative** (argumenterend).","en":"(c) *Do you agree?* asks you to choose a side and defend it → **argumentative**."},{"af":"(d) *Advantages and disadvantages* = albei kante gebalanseerd → **discursive** (besprekend).","en":"(d) *Advantages and disadvantages* = both sides in a balanced way → **discursive**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) narrative (b) descriptive (c) argumentative (d) discursive","en":"(a) narrative (b) descriptive (c) argumentative (d) discursive"}},{"title":{"af":"Beplan 'n argumenterende opstel","en":"Plan an argumentative essay"},"problem":{"af":"Beplan 'n opstel oor die onderwerp: *Every school should have a vegetable garden. Do you agree?*","en":"Plan an essay on the topic: *Every school should have a vegetable garden. Do you agree?*"},"steps":[{"af":"Stap 1: *Do you agree?* = argumenterend. Kies **een** kant en hou daarby: **Yes.**","en":"Step 1: *Do you agree?* = argumentative. Choose **one** side and stick to it: **Yes.**"},{"af":"Stap 2: Breinkaart met sleutelwoorde: *fresh vegetables – feeding scheme – saves money – learning by doing (Life Sciences) – teamwork – responsibility*.","en":"Step 2: Mind map with keywords: *fresh vegetables – feeding scheme – saves money – learning by doing (Life Sciences) – teamwork – responsibility*."},{"af":"Stap 3: Paragraafplan, een hoofgedagte per paragraaf: **Inleiding** (haak + standpunt) → **P1** gesonde kos vir die voedingskema → **P2** leer deur te doen → **P3** spanwerk en verantwoordelikheid → **Slot** (herhaal standpunt met 'n sterk laaste sin).","en":"Step 3: Paragraph plan, one main idea per paragraph: **Introduction** (hook + stand) → **P1** healthy food for the feeding scheme → **P2** learning by doing → **P3** teamwork and responsibility → **Conclusion** (restate the stand with a strong final line)."},{"af":"Stap 4: Skryf die opstel (150–200 woorde) en trek dan 'n streep deur die beplanning – dit moet sigbaar bly.","en":"Step 4: Write the essay (150–200 words) and then draw a line through the planning – it must stay visible."}],"answer":{"af":"Stand: Yes · Intro → healthy food → learning by doing → teamwork → strong conclusion","en":"Stand: Yes · Intro → healthy food → learning by doing → teamwork → strong conclusion"}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n inleiding vir 'n verhalende opstel","en":"Write an introduction for a narrative essay"},"problem":{"af":"Skryf 'n inleiding (40–60 woorde) vir die verhalende opstel: *The night the lights went out*.","en":"Write an introduction (40–60 words) for the narrative essay: *The night the lights went out*."},"steps":[{"af":"Stap 1: Begin met 'n **haak** – 'n klank, aksie of dialoog, nie *In this essay I will …* nie: *Click.*","en":"Step 1: Start with a **hook** – a sound, action or dialogue, not *In this essay I will …*: *Click.*"},{"af":"Stap 2: Stel die **toneel**: wanneer, waar, wie – in die **verlede tyd**: *The fridge stopped humming and our street in Brits disappeared into darkness.*","en":"Step 2: Set the **scene**: when, where, who – in the **past tense**: *The fridge stopped humming and our street in Brits disappeared into darkness.*"},{"af":"Stap 3: Voeg kort **dialoog** by om dit lewendig te maak: *\"Not again,\" Ma groaned.*","en":"Step 3: Add short **dialogue** to bring it to life: *\"Not again,\" Ma groaned.*"},{"af":"Stap 4: Sinspeel op die **komplikasie** sodat die leser wil aanhou lees: *I had no idea that, ten minutes later, I would come face to face with a stranger in our backyard.*","en":"Step 4: Hint at the **complication** so that the reader wants to keep reading: *I had no idea that, ten minutes later, I would come face to face with a stranger in our backyard.*"}],"answer":{"af":"Click. The fridge stopped humming and our street in Brits disappeared into darkness. \"Not again,\" Ma groaned. I grabbed my phone torch and headed for the kitchen. I had no idea that, ten minutes later, I would come face to face with a stranger in our backyard.","en":"Click. The fridge stopped humming and our street in Brits disappeared into darkness. \"Not again,\" Ma groaned. I grabbed my phone torch and headed for the kitchen. I had no idea that, ten minutes later, I would come face to face with a stranger in our backyard."}},{"title":{"af":"Redigeer 'n paragraaf met foute","en":"Edit a paragraph with errors"},"problem":{"af":"Hierdie paragraaf uit 'n verhalende opstel het vyf foute. Redigeer dit.\n\n*Last holiday me and my cousin goes to the dam. We make lots of photos and it was very lekker. Suddenly my cousin falls in the water!*","en":"This paragraph from a narrative essay has five errors. Edit it.\n\n*Last holiday me and my cousin goes to the dam. We make lots of photos and it was very lekker. Suddenly my cousin falls in the water!*"},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1 (voornaamwoord): *me and my cousin* is die onderwerp → ***my cousin and I***.","en":"Error 1 (pronoun): *me and my cousin* is the subject → ***my cousin and I***."},{"af":"Fout 2 (tyd): *Last holiday* is verlede tyd → *goes* word ***went***.","en":"Error 2 (tense): *Last holiday* is past tense → *goes* becomes ***went***."},{"af":"Fout 3 (letterlike vertaling + tyd): \"'n foto maak\" is in Engels *take a photo*, verlede tyd → ***We took lots of photos***.","en":"Error 3 (literal translation + tense): the Afrikaans \"'n foto maak\" is *take a photo* in English, past tense → ***We took lots of photos***."},{"af":"Fout 4 (sleng): *lekker* is Afrikaans/sleng en hoort nie in 'n opstel nie → ***and had a wonderful time***.","en":"Error 4 (slang): *lekker* is Afrikaans/slang and does not belong in an essay → ***and had a wonderful time***."},{"af":"Fout 5 (tyd wissel): bly in die verlede tyd → *falls* word ***fell***; *fell into the water* wys beweging.","en":"Error 5 (tense switch): stay in the past tense → *falls* becomes ***fell***; *fell into the water* shows movement."}],"answer":{"af":"Last holiday my cousin and I went to the dam. We took lots of photos and had a wonderful time. Suddenly my cousin fell into the water!","en":"Last holiday my cousin and I went to the dam. We took lots of photos and had a wonderful time. Suddenly my cousin fell into the water!"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel die opstel (Afdeling A) in Vraestel 3?","en":"How many marks is the essay (Section A) worth in Paper 3?"},"options":[{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"20","en":"20"},{"af":"50","en":"50"},{"af":"100","en":"100"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die opstel tel 50 van die 100 punte. Die langer transaksionele teks tel 30 en die korter teks 20.","en":"The essay is worth 50 of the 100 marks. The longer transactional text is worth 30 and the shorter text 20."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n beskrywende opstel spreek jy die leser se vyf ___ aan (sien, hoor, ruik, proe, voel).","en":"In a descriptive essay you appeal to the reader's five ___ (sight, hearing, smell, taste, touch)."},"answers":{"af":["senses","sintuie"],"en":["senses"]},"explain":{"af":"'n Beskrywende opstel skilder 'n prentjie deur die vyf sintuie: wat jy sien, hoor, ruik, proe en voel.","en":"A descriptive essay paints a picture through the five senses: what you see, hear, smell, taste and feel."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["paragraphs","characters","tenses"],"en":["paragraphs","characters","tenses"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die titel van die opstel tel by die woordtal.","en":"The title of the essay is counted in the word count."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die titel tel nie by die woordtal nie. Skryf die woordtal aan die einde van die opstel.","en":"False. The title is not counted in the word count. Write the word count at the end of the essay."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter soort opstel bespreek ALBEI kante van 'n saak gebalanseerd?","en":"Which type of essay discusses BOTH sides of an issue in a balanced way?"},"options":[{"af":"verhalend (narrative)","en":"narrative"},{"af":"argumenterend (argumentative)","en":"argumentative"},{"af":"refleksief (reflective)","en":"reflective"},{"af":"besprekend (discursive)","en":"discursive"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Besprekende opstel (*discursive*) weeg albei kante op. 'n Argumenterende opstel kies net een kant.","en":"A discursive essay weighs up both sides. An argumentative essay chooses only one side."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Graad 10 moet die opstel in Vraestel 3 ___ woorde lank wees.","en":"In Grade 10 the essay in Paper 3 must be ___ words long."},"answers":{"af":["150–200","150-200","150 to 200","150 tot 200"],"en":["150–200","150-200","150 to 200"]},"explain":{"af":"Gr 10: 150–200 woorde. 120–150 is die langer transaksionele teks, 80–100 die korter teks en 250–300 die Gr 12-opstel.","en":"Gr 10: 150–200 words. 120–150 is the longer transactional text, 80–100 the shorter text and 250–300 the Gr 12 essay."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["80–100","120–150","250–300"],"en":["80–100","120–150","250–300"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke opstelsoort by sy hoofkenmerk.","en":"Match each type of essay to its main feature."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"verhalend (narrative)","en":"narrative"},"r":{"af":"Vertel 'n storie met 'n komplikasie en klimaks","en":"Tells a story with a complication and climax"}},{"l":{"af":"beskrywend (descriptive)","en":"descriptive"},"r":{"af":"Skilder 'n prentjie met die vyf sintuie","en":"Paints a picture using the five senses"}},{"l":{"af":"argumenterend (argumentative)","en":"argumentative"},"r":{"af":"Verdedig EEN kant met sterk redes","en":"Defends ONE side with strong reasons"}},{"l":{"af":"refleksief (reflective)","en":"reflective"},"r":{"af":"Persoonlike gedagtes, gevoelens en lesse","en":"Personal thoughts, feelings and lessons learnt"}},{"l":{"af":"verklarend (expository)","en":"expository"},"r":{"af":"Verduidelik 'n onderwerp of proses","en":"Explains a topic or process"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ken elke soort se hoofkenmerk – as jy die verkeerde soort skryf, verloor jy punte vir inhoud.","en":"Know the main feature of each type – if you write the wrong type, you lose marks for content."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In die opstelrubriek (50 punte) tel inhoud en beplanning ___ punte.","en":"In the essay rubric (50 marks), content and planning count ___ marks."},"answers":{"af":["30"],"en":["30"]},"explain":{"af":"Inhoud en beplanning 30, taal, styl en redigering 15, struktuur 5: 30 + 15 + 5 = 50.","en":"Content and planning 30, language, style and editing 15, structure 5: 30 + 15 + 5 = 50."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["15","5","20"],"en":["15","5","20"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter soort opstel vra hierdie onderwerp? *Describe the sights, sounds and smells of the Brits taxi rank at rush hour.*","en":"Which type of essay does this topic ask for? *Describe the sights, sounds and smells of the Brits taxi rank at rush hour.*"},"options":[{"af":"verhalend (narrative)","en":"narrative"},{"af":"beskrywend (descriptive)","en":"descriptive"},{"af":"argumenterend (argumentative)","en":"argumentative"},{"af":"refleksief (reflective)","en":"reflective"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Describe* plus *sights, sounds and smells* (die sintuie) = 'n beskrywende opstel. Daar is geen storie of standpunt nie.","en":"*Describe* plus *sights, sounds and smells* (the senses) = a descriptive essay. There is no story or point of view to argue."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n argumenterende opstel gee jy albei kante ewe veel aandag en laat jy die leser self besluit.","en":"In an argumentative essay you give both sides equal attention and let the reader decide."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit beskryf 'n besprekende (*discursive*) opstel. In 'n argumenterende opstel kies jy een kant en probeer jy die leser oortuig.","en":"False. That describes a discursive essay. In an argumentative essay you choose one side and try to convince the reader."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul 'n verbindingswoord van kontras in: *Load-shedding is frustrating. ___, it has taught us to plan ahead.*","en":"Fill in a linking word of contrast: *Load-shedding is frustrating. ___, it has taught us to plan ahead.*"},"answers":{"af":["However","Nevertheless","Nonetheless","Even so","Still"],"en":["However","Nevertheless","Nonetheless","Even so","Still"]},"explain":{"af":"Die twee sinne kontrasteer ('n nadeel teenoor 'n voordeel), dus *However*. *Because* maak die sin onvolledig, *Similarly* wys ooreenkoms en *Firstly* wys volgorde.","en":"The two sentences contrast (a disadvantage versus an advantage), so *However*. *Because* makes the sentence incomplete, *Similarly* shows similarity and *Firstly* shows sequence."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Because","Similarly","Firstly"],"en":["Because","Similarly","Firstly"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Please close the light; I want to sleep.* Stel die letterlike vertaling reg: *Please ___ the light.*","en":"*Please close the light; I want to sleep.* Correct the literal translation: *Please ___ the light.*"},"answers":{"af":["switch off","turn off"],"en":["switch off","turn off"]},"explain":{"af":"\"Maak die lig toe\" word in Engels *switch off / turn off the light*. *Close the light* is 'n letterlike vertaling uit Afrikaans.","en":"In English you *switch off / turn off the light*. *Close the light* is a literal translation from Afrikaans (\"maak die lig toe\")."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["shut","open","lock"],"en":["shut","open","lock"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste opening vir die verhalende opstel *The day our school bus broke down*?","en":"Which sentence is the best opening for the narrative essay *The day our school bus broke down*?"},"options":[{"af":"With a loud bang and a cloud of black smoke, our old school bus shuddered to a stop on the road over the Magaliesberg.","en":"With a loud bang and a cloud of black smoke, our old school bus shuddered to a stop on the road over the Magaliesberg."},{"af":"In this essay I am going to write about the day our school bus broke down.","en":"In this essay I am going to write about the day our school bus broke down."},{"af":"A school bus is a large vehicle that carries learners to school.","en":"A school bus is a large vehicle that carries learners to school."},{"af":"Once upon a time there was a bus.","en":"Once upon a time there was a bus."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die eerste sin is 'n haak: aksie, klank (*bang*) en 'n toneel, in die verlede tyd. B kondig net aan, C is verklarend (nie 'n storie nie) en D is 'n cliché.","en":"The first sentence is a hook: action, sound (*bang*) and a scene, in the past tense. B only announces, C is expository (not a story) and D is a cliché."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*We walked along the dam wall. Suddenly a snake slides across the path and we freeze.* Watter herskrywing van die tweede sin is korrek?","en":"*We walked along the dam wall. Suddenly a snake slides across the path and we freeze.* Which rewrite of the second sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"Suddenly a snake slided across the path and we freezed.","en":"Suddenly a snake slided across the path and we freezed."},{"af":"Suddenly a snake slid across the path and we froze.","en":"Suddenly a snake slid across the path and we froze."},{"af":"Suddenly a snake has slid across the path and we have frozen.","en":"Suddenly a snake has slid across the path and we have frozen."},{"af":"Suddenly a snake slides across the path and we froze.","en":"Suddenly a snake slides across the path and we froze."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die opstel begin in die verlede tyd (*walked*), so bly daar: slide – **slid**, freeze – **froze** (albei onreëlmatig). C gebruik die teenwoordige voltooide tyd en D wissel steeds van tyd.","en":"The essay starts in the past tense (*walked*), so stay there: slide – **slid**, freeze – **froze** (both irregular). C uses the present perfect and D still switches tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin WYS (*show, don't tell*) dat Lerato senuweeagtig is?","en":"Which sentence SHOWS (*show, don't tell*) that Lerato is nervous?"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato was very nervous.","en":"Lerato was very nervous."},{"af":"Lerato felt nervous and scared.","en":"Lerato felt nervous and scared."},{"af":"Lerato's hands shook as she wiped them on her school skirt for the third time.","en":"Lerato's hands shook as she wiped them on her school skirt for the third time."},{"af":"Lerato is a nervous person.","en":"Lerato is a nervous person."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die derde sin wys die senuwees deur aksies (bewende hande, drie keer afvee). Die ander sinne **sê** net vir die leser hoe sy voel.","en":"The third sentence shows the nerves through actions (shaking hands, wiping them three times). The other sentences only **tell** the reader how she feels."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste keuse vir 'n beskrywende opstel?","en":"Which sentence is the best choice for a descriptive essay?"},"options":[{"af":"The braai was lekker and the vibe was hectic, bru.","en":"The braai was lekker and the vibe was hectic, bru."},{"af":"The braai was awesome, like, totally epic.","en":"The braai was awesome, like, totally epic."},{"af":"The braai was nice and it was nice to see everyone.","en":"The braai was nice and it was nice to see everyone."},{"af":"The smoky smell of boerewors on the coals drifted over the garden as laughter filled the warm evening air.","en":"The smoky smell of boerewors on the coals drifted over the garden as laughter filled the warm evening air."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die laaste sin gebruik die sintuie (reuk, gehoor, gevoel) en presiese woorde. A en B is sleng; C is swak omdat *nice* herhaal word en niks beskryf nie.","en":"The last sentence uses the senses (smell, hearing, touch) and precise words. A and B are slang; C is weak because *nice* is repeated and describes nothing."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Onderwerp: *Cellphones should be allowed in class. Do you agree?* Watter beplanning pas die beste by hierdie onderwerp?","en":"Topic: *Cellphones should be allowed in class. Do you agree?* Which plan suits this topic best?"},"options":[{"af":"Inleiding: haak + standpunt (Ja) → P1: navorsingsinstrument → P2: ouers kan leerders in noodgevalle bereik → P3: leerders leer verantwoordelikheid → Slot: herhaal die standpunt met 'n sterk laaste sin","en":"Introduction: hook + stand (Yes) → P1: research tool → P2: parents can reach learners in emergencies → P3: learners learn responsibility → Conclusion: restate the stand with a strong final line"},{"af":"Inleiding: albei kante het meriete → P1: redes vir → P2: redes teen → Slot: die leser moet self besluit","en":"Introduction: both sides have merit → P1: reasons for → P2: reasons against → Conclusion: the reader must decide"},{"af":"Inleiding: hoe ek my eerste foon gekry het → P1: my gunstelingtoeps → P2: my vriend se foon → Slot: Die einde","en":"Introduction: how I got my first phone → P1: my favourite apps → P2: my friend's phone → Conclusion: The end"},{"af":"Inleiding: 'n beskrywing van my foon → P1: sy kleur en vorm → P2: die klank van die luitoon → Slot: hoekom ek my foon liefhet","en":"Introduction: a description of my phone → P1: its colour and shape → P2: the sound of the ringtone → Conclusion: why I love my phone"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Do you agree?* vra 'n argumenterende opstel: een standpunt, sterk redes in aparte paragrawe en 'n oortuigende slot. B is besprekend, C verhalend en D beskrywend – almal die verkeerde soort.","en":"*Do you agree?* asks for an argumentative essay: one stand, strong reasons in separate paragraphs and a persuasive conclusion. B is discursive, C narrative and D descriptive – all the wrong type."}}]}]},{"term":2,"title":{"af":"Opsomming, prosa, lydende vorm en briewe","en":"Summary, prose, passive voice and letters"},"topics":[{"id":"eng10-t2-summary","title":{"af":"Opsomming","en":"Summary"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sewe relevante punte uit 'n Engelse teks kan kies en dit in volsinne, in jou eie woorde en binne die woordlimiet kan neerskryf.","en":"You will be able to select seven relevant points from an English text and write them in full sentences, in your own words and within the word limit."},"summary":{"af":"## Waar pas die opsomming in?\n\nDie opsomming is **Afdeling B van Vraestel 1** (*Language in context*, 80 punte, 2 uur) en tel **10 punte**. Jy kry 'n teks en 'n baie spesifieke opdrag, byvoorbeeld *\"List SEVEN ways in which learners can save water at school.\"*\n\nWat die vraestel van jou vra:\n\n- Kies **SEWE punte** uit die teks wat presies by die opdrag pas.\n- Skryf elke punt as 'n **volsin** (*full sentence*), nie as notas nie.\n- Nommer die sinne **1 tot 7** (puntsgewys, *point form*). Moenie 'n paragraaf skryf as puntsgewys gevra word nie.\n- Gebruik **nie meer as ongeveer 70 woorde nie**. Volg altyd die woordlimiet wat in die vraestel gedruk is.\n- Gebruik **jou eie woorde** waar moontlik.\n- Skryf die **woordetal** aan die einde, bv. *Word count: 58*.\n\n### Hoe word dit nagesien?\n\n| Deel | Punte |\n|---|---|\n| Inhoud: 7 relevante punte (1 punt elk) | 7 |\n| Taal: volsinne, eie woorde, korrekte taal | 3 |\n| **Totaal** | **10** |\n\nDie taalpunte hang af van hoeveel punte jy reg het en of jy in jou eie woorde geskryf het. Wie lang sinne net woord vir woord oorskryf, verloor taalpunte. As jy oor die woordlimiet gaan, hou die nasiener op lees by die laaste sin binne die limiet, en punte wat daarna kom, tel nie.\n\n## Die metode: stap vir stap\n\n1. **Lees die opdrag twee keer.** Onderstreep die sleutelwoorde: *wat* moet jy lys (voordele, stappe, redes of wenke?) en *hoeveel* woorde mag jy gebruik?\n2. **Vluglees** (*skim*) die teks om die hoofgedagte te kry.\n3. **Lees weer stadig** en onderstreep die **7 relevante feite**: net feite wat die opdrag beantwoord.\n4. **Laat weg:** voorbeelde, herhaling, beeldspraak, statistiek (syfers), aanhalings, persoonlike stories (anekdotes) en agtergrond.\n5. **Skryf een feit per sin** in jou eie woorde en nommer dit 1–7.\n6. **Tel die woorde** en skryf die woordetal aan die einde. Elke woord tel, ook *a*, *the* en *is*; die nommers 1–7 tel nie.\n\n> **Wenk:** As die opdrag *wenke*, *maniere* of *stappe* vra, begin elke sin met 'n werkwoord in die gebiedende wys (*imperative*): *Switch off… Use… Check…* Dit is kort, duidelik en steeds 'n volsin.\n\n### Wat is 'n \"punt\"?\n\n'n Punt is 'n **hoofgedagte** wat die opdrag beantwoord. Stel jou voor die opdrag is *\"List ways to save electricity at home\"*:\n\n| Sin uit die teks | Punt? | Hoekom? |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Unplug chargers when you are not using them.* | Ja | 'n Duidelike wenk wat die opdrag beantwoord |\n| *My cousin in Brits saved a lot of money this way.* | Nee | 'n Persoonlike voorbeeld (anekdote) |\n| *\"Every little bit helps,\" as the saying goes.* | Nee | 'n Aanhaling of spreekwoord |\n| *Load-shedding has been with us for years.* | Nee | Agtergrond, nie 'n wenk nie |\n\n### Hoe skryf jy in jou eie woorde?\n\n- Vervang moeilike woorde met **sinonieme**: *purchase → buy; assist → help; commence → start*.\n- **Verkort** die sin: los ekstra byvoeglike naamwoorde, voorbeelde en redes uit.\n- **Verander die woordorde of woordsoort**: *the installation of LED bulbs → install LED bulbs*.\n- Sleutelwoorde sonder 'n goeie sinoniem (bv. *geyser*, *LED*) mag bly.\n\n*Teks:* \"It is a very good idea to switch off the geyser at the distribution board for all the hours during which you do not really need any hot water.\" (28 woorde)\n\n*Punt:* **Switch off the geyser when you do not need hot water.** (11 woorde)\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- **Irrelevante punte** wat nie by die opdrag pas nie, bv. nadele as die opdrag voordele vra.\n- **Twee punte in een sin.** Jy kry net een punt daarvoor, en dan het jy net ses punte oor.\n- **Lang sinne oorskryf** in plaas daarvan om eie woorde te gebruik.\n- **Oor die woordlimiet** gaan.\n- **Geen woordetal** aan die einde nie.\n- **Notas sonder 'n werkwoord** (*LED bulbs.*) in plaas van volsinne.\n- Voorbeelde, syfers en aanhalings insluit.\n\n> **Onthou!** Sewe punte, sewe sinne, sewe nommers: een feit per sin, en die woordetal onderaan.","en":"## Where does the summary fit in?\n\nThe summary is **Section B of Paper 1** (*Language in context*, 80 marks, 2 hours) and counts **10 marks**. You get a text and a very specific instruction, for example *\"List SEVEN ways in which learners can save water at school.\"*\n\nWhat the paper asks of you:\n\n- Choose **SEVEN points** from the text that fit the instruction exactly.\n- Write each point as a **full sentence**, not as notes.\n- Number the sentences **1 to 7** (*point form*). Do not write a paragraph when point form is asked for.\n- Use **no more than about 70 words**. Always follow the word limit printed in the paper.\n- Use **your own words** where possible.\n- Give the **word count** at the end, e.g. *Word count: 58*.\n\n### How is it marked?\n\n| Part | Marks |\n|---|---|\n| Content: 7 relevant points (1 mark each) | 7 |\n| Language: full sentences, own words, correct language | 3 |\n| **Total** | **10** |\n\nThe language marks depend on how many points you got right and whether you wrote in your own words. If you simply copy long sentences word for word, you lose language marks. If you go over the word limit, the marker stops reading at the last sentence within the limit, and points after that do not count.\n\n## The method: step by step\n\n1. **Read the instruction twice.** Underline the key words: *what* must you list (advantages, steps, reasons or tips?) and *how many* words may you use?\n2. **Skim** the text to get the main idea.\n3. **Read it again slowly** and underline the **7 relevant facts**: only facts that answer the instruction.\n4. **Leave out:** examples, repetition, figurative language, statistics (figures), quotes, personal stories (anecdotes) and background.\n5. **Write one fact per sentence** in your own words and number them 1–7.\n6. **Count the words** and give the word count at the end. Every word counts, including *a*, *the* and *is*; the numbers 1–7 do not count.\n\n> **Tip:** If the instruction asks for *tips*, *ways* or *steps*, start each sentence with a verb in the imperative: *Switch off… Use… Check…* It is short, clear and still a full sentence.\n\n### What is a \"point\"?\n\nA point is a **main idea** that answers the instruction. Imagine the instruction is *\"List ways to save electricity at home\"*:\n\n| Sentence from the text | Point? | Why? |\n|---|---|---|\n| *Unplug chargers when you are not using them.* | Yes | A clear tip that answers the instruction |\n| *My cousin in Brits saved a lot of money this way.* | No | A personal example (anecdote) |\n| *\"Every little bit helps,\" as the saying goes.* | No | A quote or saying |\n| *Load-shedding has been with us for years.* | No | Background, not a tip |\n\n### How do you write in your own words?\n\n- Replace difficult words with **synonyms**: *purchase → buy; assist → help; commence → start*.\n- **Shorten** the sentence: leave out extra adjectives, examples and reasons.\n- **Change the word order or word class**: *the installation of LED bulbs → install LED bulbs*.\n- Key words without a good synonym (e.g. *geyser*, *LED*) may stay.\n\n*Text:* \"It is a very good idea to switch off the geyser at the distribution board for all the hours during which you do not really need any hot water.\" (28 words)\n\n*Point:* **Switch off the geyser when you do not need hot water.** (11 words)\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- **Irrelevant points** that do not fit the instruction, e.g. disadvantages when the instruction asks for advantages.\n- **Two points in one sentence.** You only get one mark for it, and then you have only six points left.\n- **Copying long sentences** instead of using your own words.\n- **Going over** the word limit.\n- **No word count** at the end.\n- **Notes without a verb** (*LED bulbs.*) instead of full sentences.\n- Including examples, figures and quotes.\n\n> **Remember!** Seven points, seven sentences, seven numbers: one fact per sentence, and the word count at the bottom."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Opsomming (summary)","en":"Summary"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort weergawe van slegs die hoofpunte van 'n teks, volgens 'n spesifieke opdrag.","en":"A short version of only the main points of a text, according to a specific instruction."}},{"term":{"af":"Puntsgewys (point form)","en":"Point form"},"def":{"af":"Die punte word as aparte, genommerde sinne (1–7) geskryf in plaas van as 'n paragraaf.","en":"The points are written as separate, numbered sentences (1–7) instead of as a paragraph."}},{"term":{"af":"Volsin (full sentence)","en":"Full sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met 'n onderwerp en 'n werkwoord wat 'n volledige gedagte uitdruk, bv. *Use LED light bulbs.*","en":"A sentence with a subject and a verb that expresses a complete thought, e.g. *Use LED light bulbs.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Woordlimiet (word limit)","en":"Word limit"},"def":{"af":"Die maksimum aantal woorde wat jy mag gebruik, soos in die vraestel gedruk (in Gr 10 ongeveer 70).","en":"The maximum number of words you may use, as printed in the paper (about 70 in Gr 10)."}},{"term":{"af":"Woordetal (word count)","en":"Word count"},"def":{"af":"Die aantal woorde in jou opsomming, wat jy aan die einde aandui, bv. *Word count: 58*.","en":"The number of words in your summary, which you give at the end, e.g. *Word count: 58*."}},{"term":{"af":"Eie woorde (own words)","en":"Own words"},"def":{"af":"Jy herskryf die feit met sinonieme, 'n korter sin of 'n ander woordorde in plaas daarvan om dit net oor te skryf.","en":"You rewrite the fact using synonyms, a shorter sentence or a different word order instead of simply copying it."}},{"term":{"af":"Relevante punt (relevant point)","en":"Relevant point"},"def":{"af":"'n Hoofgedagte uit die teks wat die opdrag direk beantwoord; nie 'n voorbeeld, aanhaling of agtergrond nie.","en":"A main idea from the text that answers the instruction directly; not an example, quote or background."}},{"term":{"af":"Vluglees en soeklees (skimming and scanning)","en":"Skimming and scanning"},"def":{"af":"Vluglees: vinnig lees vir die hoofgedagte. Soeklees: na spesifieke inligting soek, bv. die feite wat by die opdrag pas.","en":"Skimming: reading quickly for the main idea. Scanning: searching for specific information, e.g. the facts that fit the instruction."}},{"term":{"af":"Anekdote (anecdote)","en":"Anecdote"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort persoonlike storie of voorbeeld in die teks wat jy in 'n opsomming uitlaat.","en":"A short personal story or example in the text that you leave out of a summary."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Volledige opsomming: elektrisiteit spaar","en":"Full summary: saving electricity"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die teks en voer die opdrag uit.\n\nHOW TO SAVE ELECTRICITY DURING LOAD-SHEDDING\n\nLoad-shedding has become part of daily life in towns like Brits, but every household can help to take some pressure off the national grid. Here are a few simple ways to use less electricity at home.\n\nThe geyser is usually the biggest user of electricity in a home, so switch it off at the distribution board when you do not need hot water. It also helps to cover the geyser and its pipes with insulation so that the water stays hot for longer. My uncle in Hartbeespoort fitted a geyser blanket last winter, and he says his morning shower is still warm.\n\nReplace old light bulbs with LED bulbs, which use much less power. Do not leave TVs, computers and chargers on standby; unplug them at the wall instead, because appliances on standby still use electricity.\n\nIn the kitchen, put a lid on the pot so that the food cooks faster, and boil only as much water as you need in the kettle.\n\nFinally, when the power comes back on, wait a few minutes before you switch on big appliances such as the stove and the washing machine. As the old saying goes, every little bit helps!\n\n**Opdrag:** List SEVEN things a household can do to use less electricity. Write in full sentences, number them 1–7 and use no more than 70 words. Give your word count at the end.","en":"Read the text and carry out the instruction.\n\nHOW TO SAVE ELECTRICITY DURING LOAD-SHEDDING\n\nLoad-shedding has become part of daily life in towns like Brits, but every household can help to take some pressure off the national grid. Here are a few simple ways to use less electricity at home.\n\nThe geyser is usually the biggest user of electricity in a home, so switch it off at the distribution board when you do not need hot water. It also helps to cover the geyser and its pipes with insulation so that the water stays hot for longer. My uncle in Hartbeespoort fitted a geyser blanket last winter, and he says his morning shower is still warm.\n\nReplace old light bulbs with LED bulbs, which use much less power. Do not leave TVs, computers and chargers on standby; unplug them at the wall instead, because appliances on standby still use electricity.\n\nIn the kitchen, put a lid on the pot so that the food cooks faster, and boil only as much water as you need in the kettle.\n\nFinally, when the power comes back on, wait a few minutes before you switch on big appliances such as the stove and the washing machine. As the old saying goes, every little bit helps!\n\n**Instruction:** List SEVEN things a household can do to use less electricity. Write in full sentences, number them 1–7 and use no more than 70 words. Give your word count at the end."},"steps":[{"af":"Ontleed die opdrag: ons soek SEWE dinge wat 'n huishouding kan *doen* (aksies/wenke), in volsinne, genommer, hoogstens 70 woorde, met 'n woordetal.","en":"Analyse the instruction: we need SEVEN things a household can *do* (actions/tips), in full sentences, numbered, at most 70 words, with a word count."},{"af":"Onderstreep die 7 aksies: (1) switch off the geyser when you do not need hot water; (2) insulate the geyser and its pipes; (3) replace old bulbs with LED bulbs; (4) unplug appliances instead of leaving them on standby; (5) put a lid on the pot; (6) boil only as much water as you need; (7) wait a few minutes before switching on big appliances when the power returns.","en":"Underline the 7 actions: (1) switch off the geyser when you do not need hot water; (2) insulate the geyser and its pipes; (3) replace old bulbs with LED bulbs; (4) unplug appliances instead of leaving them on standby; (5) put a lid on the pot; (6) boil only as much water as you need; (7) wait a few minutes before switching on big appliances when the power returns."},{"af":"Laat weg: die inleiding oor beurtkrag (agtergrond), *the geyser is usually the biggest user* en *which use much less power* (redes), die oom in Hartbeespoort (anekdote), *such as the stove and the washing machine* (voorbeelde) en *every little bit helps* (spreekwoord).","en":"Leave out: the introduction about load-shedding (background), *the geyser is usually the biggest user* and *which use much less power* (reasons), the uncle in Hartbeespoort (anecdote), *such as the stove and the washing machine* (examples) and *every little bit helps* (saying)."},{"af":"Skryf elke aksie as 'n kort volsin in die gebiedende wys en in eie woorde waar moontlik, bv. *put a lid on the pot* → *Cover pots with lids while cooking.*","en":"Write each action as a short full sentence in the imperative and in your own words where possible, e.g. *put a lid on the pot* → *Cover pots with lids while cooking.*"},{"af":"Tel: 11 + 6 + 4 + 8 + 6 + 6 + 12 = 53 woorde. Dit is binne die limiet van 70, dus skryf *Word count: 53*.","en":"Count: 11 + 6 + 4 + 8 + 6 + 6 + 12 = 53 words. That is within the limit of 70, so write *Word count: 53*."}],"answer":{"af":"1. Switch the geyser off when you do not need hot water.\n2. Insulate the geyser and its pipes.\n3. Use LED light bulbs.\n4. Unplug appliances instead of leaving them on standby.\n5. Cover pots with lids while cooking.\n6. Boil only the water you need.\n7. Wait a while before switching on large appliances after the power returns.\nWord count: 53","en":"1. Switch the geyser off when you do not need hot water.\n2. Insulate the geyser and its pipes.\n3. Use LED light bulbs.\n4. Unplug appliances instead of leaving them on standby.\n5. Cover pots with lids while cooking.\n6. Boil only the water you need.\n7. Wait a while before switching on large appliances after the power returns.\nWord count: 53"}},{"title":{"af":"Punt of nie 'n punt nie?","en":"Point or not a point?"},"problem":{"af":"WHY TEENAGERS NEED ENOUGH SLEEP\n(A) Many Grade 10 learners stay up far too late, often scrolling on their phones. (B) Enough sleep helps you to concentrate in class. (C) It also improves your memory, so you remember more of what you studied. (D) Last term my friend Ruan fell asleep during a Maths test! (E) Sleep strengthens your immune system, so you get sick less often. (F) As my gran always says, \"Early to bed and early to rise.\"\n\n**Opdrag:** Watter sinne gee 'n punt vir die opdrag *\"List the benefits of enough sleep\"*? Skryf die punte in jou eie woorde.","en":"WHY TEENAGERS NEED ENOUGH SLEEP\n(A) Many Grade 10 learners stay up far too late, often scrolling on their phones. (B) Enough sleep helps you to concentrate in class. (C) It also improves your memory, so you remember more of what you studied. (D) Last term my friend Ruan fell asleep during a Maths test! (E) Sleep strengthens your immune system, so you get sick less often. (F) As my gran always says, \"Early to bed and early to rise.\"\n\n**Instruction:** Which sentences give a point for the instruction *\"List the benefits of enough sleep\"*? Write the points in your own words."},"steps":[{"af":"Die opdrag vra **voordele** van genoeg slaap, so ons soek net sinne wat sê wat slaap vir jou *doen*.","en":"The instruction asks for the **benefits** of enough sleep, so we only look for sentences that say what sleep *does* for you."},{"af":"(A) beskryf die probleem (agtergrond), nie 'n voordeel nie. (D) is 'n anekdote oor Ruan. (F) is 'n spreekwoord/aanhaling. Al drie val uit.","en":"(A) describes the problem (background), not a benefit. (D) is an anecdote about Ruan. (F) is a saying/quote. All three are left out."},{"af":"(B), (C) en (E) gee elkeen een voordeel. Die *so*-dele (*so you remember more…*, *so you get sick less often*) is verduidelikings wat ons kan weglaat.","en":"(B), (C) and (E) each give one benefit. The *so* parts (*so you remember more…*, *so you get sick less often*) are explanations that we can leave out."},{"af":"Herskryf kort: 1. Sleep improves your concentration in class. 2. It helps you to remember better. 3. It makes your body better at fighting illness.","en":"Rewrite briefly: 1. Sleep improves your concentration in class. 2. It helps you to remember better. 3. It makes your body better at fighting illness."}],"answer":{"af":"Punte: B, C en E. Nie punte nie: A (agtergrond), D (anekdote), F (aanhaling).","en":"Points: B, C and E. Not points: A (background), D (anecdote), F (quote)."}},{"title":{"af":"Verbeter 'n swak opsomming","en":"Improve a weak summary"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die leerder se antwoord en identifiseer die foute. Herskryf dan die punte korrek.\n\nInstruction: List SEVEN ways in which learners can stay safe when they walk home from school (no more than 70 words).\n\nA learner's first three points:\n1. Walk in a group and stay on busy roads.\n2. Learners should not use their cellphones while they are walking home, because it makes them easy targets for the thieves who are watching them.\n3. Last year a boy in our street lost his phone near the taxi rank.\n(The summary has no word count.)","en":"Read the learner's answer and identify the mistakes. Then rewrite the points correctly.\n\nInstruction: List SEVEN ways in which learners can stay safe when they walk home from school (no more than 70 words).\n\nA learner's first three points:\n1. Walk in a group and stay on busy roads.\n2. Learners should not use their cellphones while they are walking home, because it makes them easy targets for the thieves who are watching them.\n3. Last year a boy in our street lost his phone near the taxi rank.\n(The summary has no word count.)"},"steps":[{"af":"Punt 1 bevat **twee punte in een sin** (*walk in a group* + *stay on busy roads*). Die nasiener gee net 1 punt. Verdeel dit in twee genommerde sinne.","en":"Point 1 contains **two points in one sentence** (*walk in a group* + *stay on busy roads*). The marker gives only 1 mark. Split it into two numbered sentences."},{"af":"Punt 2 is **oorgeskryf en te lank** (24 woorde). Die rede (*because it makes them easy targets…*) val weg: *Do not use your cellphone while walking.* (7 woorde)","en":"Point 2 is **copied and too long** (24 words). The reason (*because it makes them easy targets…*) is left out: *Do not use your cellphone while walking.* (7 words)"},{"af":"Punt 3 is 'n **anekdote**, nie 'n veiligheidswenk nie. Dit gee geen punt nie en mors woorde, so dit moet uit.","en":"Point 3 is an **anecdote**, not a safety tip. It earns no mark and wastes words, so it must go."},{"af":"Daar is **geen woordetal** nie. Tel die woorde en skryf dit onderaan, bv. *Word count: …*","en":"There is **no word count**. Count the words and write it at the bottom, e.g. *Word count: …*"}],"answer":{"af":"1. Walk home in a group.\n2. Stay on busy roads.\n3. Do not use your cellphone while walking.\n(Anekdote weggelaat; woordetal aan die einde bygevoeg.)","en":"1. Walk home in a group.\n2. Stay on busy roads.\n3. Do not use your cellphone while walking.\n(Anecdote left out; word count added at the end.)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte tel die opsomming (Afdeling B) in Vraestel 1?","en":"How many marks is the summary (Section B) worth in Paper 1?"},"options":[{"af":"7","en":"7"},{"af":"10","en":"10"},{"af":"30","en":"30"},{"af":"40","en":"40"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die opsomming tel 10 punte: 7 vir inhoud en 3 vir taal. 30 is die leesbegrip en 40 die taalstrukture.","en":"The summary is worth 10 marks: 7 for content and 3 for language. 30 is the comprehension and 40 the language structures."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoeveel punte moet jy gewoonlik in die Gr 10-opsomming lys?","en":"How many points must you usually list in the Gr 10 summary?"},"options":[{"af":"Five","en":"Five"},{"af":"Six","en":"Six"},{"af":"Ten","en":"Ten"},{"af":"Seven","en":"Seven"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die opdrag vra SEWE punte, en elke relevante punt tel 1 punt (7 inhoudspunte).","en":"The instruction asks for SEVEN points, and each relevant point is worth 1 mark (7 content marks)."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? Jy moet die woordetal aan die einde van jou opsomming skryf.","en":"True or false? You must give the word count at the end of your summary."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die opdrag vra altyd die woordetal, bv. *Word count: 58*. As jy dit weglaat, verloor jy maklike punte.","en":"True. The instruction always asks for the word count, e.g. *Word count: 58*. If you leave it out, you lose easy marks."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die opsomming word uit 10 nagesien: ___ punte vir inhoud en 3 punte vir taal.","en":"The summary is marked out of 10: ___ marks for content and 3 marks for language."},"answers":{"af":["7","seven","sewe"],"en":["7","seven"]},"explain":{"af":"Sewe punte, een punt per relevante punt = 7. Die ander 3 is vir taal.","en":"Seven points, one mark per relevant point = 7. The other 3 are for language."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["3","5","10"],"en":["3","5","10"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n opsomming laat jy voorbeelde, herhaling, beeldspraak, statistiek en ___ (aanhalings) weg.","en":"In a summary you leave out examples, repetition, figures of speech, statistics and ___."},"answers":{"af":["quotes","quotations","aanhalings"],"en":["quotes","quotations"]},"explain":{"af":"Aanhalings (*quotes*) is iemand se presiese woorde en is nie hoofpunte nie. Feite en instruksies is juis wat jy wil hê.","en":"Quotes are someone's exact words and are not main points. Facts and instructions are exactly what you want."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["facts","verbs","instructions"],"en":["facts","verbs","instructions"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"As jy jou opsomming as genommerde, aparte sinne skryf, noem ons dit in Engels ___ form (puntsgewys).","en":"When you write your summary as numbered, separate sentences, it is called ___ form."},"answers":{"af":["point"],"en":["point"]},"explain":{"af":"*Point form* = puntsgewys, genommer 1–7. Dit is nie *note form* (notas sonder werkwoorde) nie, want elke punt moet 'n volsin wees.","en":"*Point form* = numbered 1–7. It is not *note form* (notes without verbs), because every point must be a full sentence."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["paragraph","note","essay"],"en":["paragraph","note","essay"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat moet jy in 'n opsomming UITLAAT?","en":"What must you LEAVE OUT of a summary?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Hoofgedagte wat die opdrag beantwoord","en":"A main idea that answers the instruction"},{"af":"'n Feit wat jy in jou eie woorde herskryf het","en":"A fact that you have rewritten in your own words"},{"af":"'n Voorbeeld wat 'n punt illustreer","en":"An example that illustrates a point"},{"af":"'n Kort sin met 'n werkwoord","en":"A short sentence with a verb"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Voorbeelde illustreer net 'n punt; hulle is nie self 'n punt nie. Hoofgedagtes in volsinne en eie woorde is presies wat jy wil hê.","en":"Examples only illustrate a point; they are not a point themselves. Main ideas in full sentences and own words are exactly what you want."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n VOLSIN wat as opsommingspunt aanvaar sal word?","en":"Which one is a FULL SENTENCE that will be accepted as a summary point?"},"options":[{"af":"LED bulbs.","en":"LED bulbs."},{"af":"Using LED bulbs.","en":"Using LED bulbs."},{"af":"LED bulbs instead of old ones.","en":"LED bulbs instead of old ones."},{"af":"Use LED light bulbs.","en":"Use LED light bulbs."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*Use LED light bulbs.* het 'n werkwoord in die gebiedende wys en is 'n volledige gedagte. Die ander is notas of sinsfragmente sonder 'n volledige werkwoord.","en":"*Use LED light bulbs.* has a verb in the imperative and is a complete thought. The others are notes or sentence fragments without a complete verb."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Tel die woorde in hierdie opsommingspunt: *Cover the pot with a lid while you cook.* Woordetal = ___","en":"Count the words in this summary point: *Cover the pot with a lid while you cook.* Word count = ___"},"answers":{"af":["9","nine","nege"],"en":["9","nine"]},"explain":{"af":"Cover (1) the (2) pot (3) with (4) a (5) lid (6) while (7) you (8) cook (9). Klein woordjies soos *the* en *a* tel ook.","en":"Cover (1) the (2) pot (3) with (4) a (5) lid (6) while (7) you (8) cook (9). Small words such as *the* and *a* also count."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["8","10","7"],"en":["8","10","7"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in eie woorde: *Purchase a geyser blanket.* → ___ a geyser blanket. (Gee een woord.)","en":"Write in your own words: *Purchase a geyser blanket.* → ___ a geyser blanket. (Give one word.)"},"answers":{"af":["buy","get"],"en":["buy","get"]},"explain":{"af":"*Purchase* beteken *buy* (koop). 'n Eenvoudige sinoniem wys dat jy jou eie woorde gebruik.","en":"*Purchase* means *buy*. A simple synonym shows that you are using your own words."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sell","borrow","return"],"en":["sell","borrow","return"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? As jy 85 woorde skryf en die limiet is 70, lees die nasiener steeds al jou punte en gee punte vir almal.","en":"True or false? If you write 85 words and the limit is 70, the marker still reads all your points and gives marks for all of them."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die nasiener hou op lees by die laaste sin binne die limiet. Punte wat daarna kom, tel nie.","en":"False. The marker stops reading at the last sentence within the limit. Points that come after that do not count."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die opdrag is: *\"List the advantages of cycling to school.\"* Watter sin uit die teks gee 'n relevante punt?","en":"The instruction is: *\"List the advantages of cycling to school.\"* Which sentence from the text gives a relevant point?"},"options":[{"af":"Cycling to school keeps you fit.","en":"Cycling to school keeps you fit."},{"af":"Bicycles were first built in the 1800s.","en":"Bicycles were first built in the 1800s."},{"af":"My friend Thabo cycles to school every day.","en":"My friend Thabo cycles to school every day."},{"af":"Many learners in Brits travel by taxi.","en":"Many learners in Brits travel by taxi."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Net *Cycling to school keeps you fit* is 'n voordeel. Die ander is agtergrond, 'n anekdote en 'n irrelevante feit.","en":"Only *Cycling to school keeps you fit* is an advantage. The others are background, an anecdote and an irrelevant fact."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke opsommingsfout by die beste regstelling.","en":"Match each summary mistake to the best correction."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Twee punte in een sin","en":"Two points in one sentence"},"r":{"af":"Verdeel dit in twee genommerde sinne","en":"Split it into two numbered sentences"}},{"l":{"af":"'n Lang sin is woord vir woord oorgeskryf","en":"A long sentence copied word for word"},"r":{"af":"Verkort dit en gebruik eie woorde","en":"Shorten it and use your own words"}},{"l":{"af":"Geen woordetal nie","en":"No word count"},"r":{"af":"Skryf *Word count: …* aan die einde","en":"Write *Word count: …* at the end"}},{"l":{"af":"Oor die woordlimiet","en":"Over the word limit"},"r":{"af":"Laat voorbeelde en ekstra besonderhede weg","en":"Leave out examples and extra detail"}}],"explain":{"af":"Elke fout kos punte: twee punte in een sin gee net 1 punt, oorskryf kos taalpunte, en woorde oor die limiet word nie gelees nie.","en":"Every mistake costs marks: two points in one sentence earn only 1 mark, copying costs language marks, and words over the limit are not read."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder skryf: *\"1. Switch off the geyser and use LED bulbs.\"* Wat is die grootste probleem?","en":"A learner writes: *\"1. Switch off the geyser and use LED bulbs.\"* What is the biggest problem?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is twee punte in een sin","en":"It is two points in one sentence"},{"af":"Dit is nie 'n volsin nie","en":"It is not a full sentence"},{"af":"Dit is te lank vir die limiet","en":"It is too long for the limit"},{"af":"Die woord *geyser* moes vervang word","en":"The word *geyser* should have been replaced"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die sin het twee aparte wenke (geyser + LED). Die nasiener gee net 1 punt. Dit IS 'n volsin, en *geyser* mag bly omdat dit 'n sleutelwoord is.","en":"The sentence has two separate tips (geyser + LED). The marker gives only 1 mark. It IS a full sentence, and *geyser* may stay because it is a key word."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die beste opsommingspunt vir hierdie sin? *\"It is a good idea for learners to avoid using their cellphones while they walk, because it makes them easy targets for thieves and they do not notice cars.\"*","en":"Which one is the best summary point for this sentence? *\"It is a good idea for learners to avoid using their cellphones while they walk, because it makes them easy targets for thieves and they do not notice cars.\"*"},"options":[{"af":"Thieves and cars are dangerous.","en":"Thieves and cars are dangerous."},{"af":"Do not use your cellphone while walking.","en":"Do not use your cellphone while walking."},{"af":"Cellphones while walking, thieves, cars.","en":"Cellphones while walking, thieves, cars."},{"af":"It is a good idea for learners to avoid using their cellphones while they walk.","en":"It is a good idea for learners to avoid using their cellphones while they walk."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Do not use your cellphone while walking.* behou die hoofgedagte, is kort, in eie woorde en 'n volsin. Die ander verloor die punt, is notas of is net oorgeskryf.","en":"*Do not use your cellphone while walking.* keeps the main idea, is short, in own words and a full sentence. The others lose the point, are notes or are simply copied."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Sipho se opsomming het 75 woorde, maar die limiet is 70. Al sewe sy punte is relevant. Wat is die BESTE manier om dit reg te stel?","en":"Sipho's summary has 75 words, but the limit is 70. All seven of his points are relevant. What is the BEST way to fix it?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy moet twee punte in een sin saamvoeg","en":"He must combine two points into one sentence"},{"af":"Hy moet die nommers 1–7 weglaat","en":"He must leave out the numbers 1–7"},{"af":"Hy moet net 70 as woordetal skryf","en":"He must simply write 70 as the word count"},{"af":"Hy moet voorbeelde en redes uit sy sinne verwyder","en":"He must remove examples and reasons from his sentences"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Om voorbeelde en redes te skrap verkort die sinne sonder om punte te verloor. Saamvoeg kos 'n punt, die nommers tel nie as woorde nie, en 'n vals woordetal is oneerlik en word raakgesien.","en":"Removing examples and reasons shortens the sentences without losing points. Combining costs a mark, the numbers do not count as words, and a false word count is dishonest and will be noticed."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t2-novel-short-story","title":{"af":"Roman en kortverhaal","en":"Novel and short story"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die letterkundige terme vir prosa ken en kontekstuele vrae oor 'n uittreksel uit 'n roman of kortverhaal met bewys uit die teks kan beantwoord.","en":"You will know the literary terms for prose and be able to answer contextual questions on an extract from a novel or short story, with evidence from the text."},"summary":{"af":"## Vraestel 2: Letterkunde\n\nVraestel 2 tel **70 punte**. Jy beantwoord vrae oor **TWEE** van die genres wat jy behandel het (roman, drama, kortverhale, poësie), **35 punte** elk. Die vrae is meestal **kontekstuele vrae** oor 'n uittreksel. Ons ken nie jou skool se voorgeskrewe boeke nie, daarom oefen ons hier die **vaardighede** met ons eie uittreksels. Leer die Engelse terme, want die vraestel is in Engels.\n\n## Intrige (*plot*) en struktuur\n\n| Fase | Wat gebeur? |\n|---|---|\n| **Exposition** (uiteensetting) | Ons leer die karakters, ruimte en agtergrond ken. |\n| **Rising action / complication** (komplikasie) | Die konflik begin en die spanning bou op. |\n| **Climax** (klimaks) | Die keerpunt: die spanning is op sy hoogste. |\n| **Falling action** (dalende aksie) | Die gevolge van die klimaks; die spanning neem af. |\n| **Resolution / denouement** (ontknoping) | Die konflik word opgelos of die verhaal kom tot 'n einde. |\n\n**Suspense** (spanning) laat jou wonder wat gaan gebeur, bv. kort sinne, 'n skielike geluid of 'n hoofstuk wat met 'n vraag eindig.\n\n## Konflik\n\n- **Internal conflict** (innerlike konflik): 'n stryd in 'n karakter se gedagtes, bv. skuldgevoel teenoor nood.\n- **External conflict** (uiterlike konflik): *character vs character*, *character vs society* (reëls, armoede, vooroordeel) of *character vs nature* (droogte, 'n storm, 'n vloed).\n\n## Karakters en karakterisering\n\n- **Protagonist** (hoofkarakter), **antagonist** (die persoon of krag teen die protagonis) en **minor characters** (byfigure).\n- **Round** (rond): kompleks, met baie kante. **Flat** (plat): net een of twee eienskappe.\n- **Dynamic** (dinamies): verander deur die verhaal. **Static** (staties): bly dieselfde.\n\n**Characterisation** is hoe die skrywer 'n karakter aan ons bekendstel:\n\n- **Direct** (direk): die verteller *sê* hoe die karakter is: *\"Mrs Naidoo was strict but fair.\"*\n- **Indirect** (indirek): jy lei dit self af uit **S**peech (wat hy sê), **T**houghts (gedagtes), **E**ffect on others (ander se reaksie), **A**ctions (dade) en **L**ooks (voorkoms). Onthou: **STEAL**.\n\n## Verteller en vertelperspektief\n\n| Perspektief | Kenmerk |\n|---|---|\n| **First person** (*I/we*) | Die verteller is 'n karakter; ons weet net wat hy weet, so dit kan subjektief wees. |\n| **Third person omniscient** (alwetend) | Die verteller weet alles, ook die gedagtes van *alle* karakters. |\n| **Third person limited** (beperk) | *He/she*, maar ons volg net *een* karakter se gedagtes. |\n\n## Ruimte (*setting*)\n\nSetting = **tyd** (tyd van die dag, seisoen, era), **plek** en die **sosiale/historiese** omstandighede. Die ruimte skep stemming, weerspieël 'n karakter se gevoelens of veroorsaak konflik.\n\n## Tema, simbool en motief\n\n- **Subject** (onderwerp): waaroor dit gaan, in 'n woord of frase: *poverty*.\n- **Theme** (tema): die boodskap oor die lewe, in 'n **volsin**: *Kindness can break down the barriers between people.*\n- **Symbol** (simbool): 'n voorwerp, kleur of persoon wat vir 'n groter idee staan, bv. 'n heining = skeiding.\n- **Motif** (motief): 'n beeld of idee wat herhaaldelik terugkom en die tema versterk.\n\n## Ironie en ander tegnieke\n\n- **Verbal irony** (verbale ironie): iemand sê die teenoorgestelde van wat hy bedoel.\n- **Situational irony** (situasie-ironie): die teenoorgestelde gebeur van wat verwag word.\n- **Dramatic irony** (dramatiese ironie): die leser weet iets wat 'n karakter nie weet nie.\n- **Foreshadowing** (vooruitwysing): 'n wenk oor iets wat later gaan gebeur.\n- **Flashback** (terugflits): 'n toneel uit die verlede wat die hede onderbreek.\n- **Tone** (toon): die verteller se houding. **Mood** (stemming): die gevoel wat by die leser geskep word.\n- **Open ending** (oop einde): jy moet self besluit. **Twist ending** (verrassingseinde): 'n onverwagte wending.\n\n## Kortverhaal teenoor roman\n\n| Kortverhaal | Roman |\n|---|---|\n| Een hoofgebeurtenis | Baie gebeure en newe-intriges (*subplots*) |\n| Min karakters | Baie karakters wat ontwikkel |\n| Kort tydsverloop | Lang tydsverloop |\n| Begin dikwels *in medias res* (in die middel van die aksie) | Meer ruimte vir agtergrond |\n| Dikwels 'n verrassingseinde | Uitgebreide ontknoping |\n\n## Kontekstuele vrae beantwoord\n\n- **\"Place the extract in context\"**: wat het net voor die uittreksel gebeur?\n- **\"Describe the setting\"**: tyd + plek, met bewys uit die teks.\n- **\"What does this reveal about X's character? Quote to support\"**: 'n **byvoeglike naamwoord** (*selfless*) + 'n **aanhaling** tussen aanhalingstekens.\n- **\"Explain the irony\"**: wat word **verwag** en wat gebeur **werklik**?\n- **\"Is X's behaviour justified? Discuss\"** (3 punte): jou standpunt + twee redes uit die teks.\n- **\"What is the theme and how does this extract convey it?\"**: die tema in 'n volsin + hoe die uittreksel dit wys.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders vertel die storie oor in plaas daarvan om die vraag te beantwoord. Kyk na die punte: 2 punte = twee aparte idees.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Toon en stemming word verwar, en die onderwerp word as die tema gegee. 'n Tema is altyd 'n volsin.","en":"## Paper 2: Literature\n\nPaper 2 is worth **70 marks**. You answer questions on **TWO** of the genres you studied (novel, drama, short stories, poetry), **35 marks** each. The questions are mostly **contextual questions** on an extract. We do not know your school's set works, so here we practise the **skills** with our own extracts. Learn the English terms, because the paper is in English.\n\n## Plot and structure\n\n| Stage | What happens? |\n|---|---|\n| **Exposition** | We meet the characters, the setting and the background. |\n| **Rising action / complication** | The conflict starts and the tension builds. |\n| **Climax** | The turning point: the tension is at its highest. |\n| **Falling action** | The results of the climax; the tension decreases. |\n| **Resolution / denouement** | The conflict is resolved or the story comes to an end. |\n\n**Suspense** makes you wonder what will happen, e.g. short sentences, a sudden sound or a chapter that ends with a question.\n\n## Conflict\n\n- **Internal conflict**: a struggle in a character's mind, e.g. guilt versus need.\n- **External conflict**: *character vs character*, *character vs society* (rules, poverty, prejudice) or *character vs nature* (drought, a storm, a flood).\n\n## Characters and characterisation\n\n- **Protagonist** (main character), **antagonist** (the person or force against the protagonist) and **minor characters**.\n- **Round**: complex, with many sides. **Flat**: only one or two traits.\n- **Dynamic**: changes during the story. **Static**: stays the same.\n\n**Characterisation** is how the writer presents a character to us:\n\n- **Direct**: the narrator *tells* us what the character is like: *\"Mrs Naidoo was strict but fair.\"*\n- **Indirect**: you work it out yourself from **S**peech, **T**houghts, **E**ffect on others, **A**ctions and **L**ooks. Remember: **STEAL**.\n\n## Narrator and point of view\n\n| Point of view | Feature |\n|---|---|\n| **First person** (*I/we*) | The narrator is a character; we only know what he knows, so it can be subjective. |\n| **Third person omniscient** | The narrator knows everything, including the thoughts of *all* the characters. |\n| **Third person limited** | *He/she*, but we follow the thoughts of only *one* character. |\n\n## Setting\n\nSetting = **time** (time of day, season, era), **place** and the **social/historical** circumstances. The setting creates mood, reflects a character's feelings or causes conflict.\n\n## Theme, symbol and motif\n\n- **Subject**: what it is about, in a word or phrase: *poverty*.\n- **Theme**: the message about life, in a **full sentence**: *Kindness can break down the barriers between people.*\n- **Symbol**: an object, colour or person that stands for a bigger idea, e.g. a fence = separation.\n- **Motif**: an image or idea that keeps coming back and strengthens the theme.\n\n## Irony and other techniques\n\n- **Verbal irony**: someone says the opposite of what he means.\n- **Situational irony**: the opposite of what is expected happens.\n- **Dramatic irony**: the reader knows something that a character does not know.\n- **Foreshadowing**: a hint of something that will happen later.\n- **Flashback**: a scene from the past that interrupts the present.\n- **Tone**: the narrator's attitude. **Mood**: the feeling created in the reader.\n- **Open ending**: you must decide for yourself. **Twist ending**: an unexpected turn.\n\n## Short story versus novel\n\n| Short story | Novel |\n|---|---|\n| One main incident | Many events and subplots |\n| Few characters | Many characters who develop |\n| Short time span | Long time span |\n| Often starts *in medias res* (in the middle of the action) | More room for background |\n| Often a surprise ending | Extended resolution |\n\n## Answering contextual questions\n\n- **\"Place the extract in context\"**: what happened just before the extract?\n- **\"Describe the setting\"**: time + place, with evidence from the text.\n- **\"What does this reveal about X's character? Quote to support\"**: an **adjective** (*selfless*) + a **quotation** in inverted commas.\n- **\"Explain the irony\"**: what is **expected** and what **actually** happens?\n- **\"Is X's behaviour justified? Discuss\"** (3 marks): your view + two reasons from the text.\n- **\"What is the theme and how does this extract convey it?\"**: the theme in a full sentence + how the extract shows it.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners retell the story instead of answering the question. Look at the marks: 2 marks = two separate ideas.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Tone and mood are confused, and the subject is given as the theme. A theme is always a full sentence."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Intrige (plot)","en":"Plot"},"def":{"af":"Die volgorde van gebeure in 'n verhaal: exposition, rising action, climax, falling action en resolution.","en":"The sequence of events in a story: exposition, rising action, climax, falling action and resolution."}},{"term":{"af":"Konflik (conflict)","en":"Conflict"},"def":{"af":"'n Stryd in 'n verhaal: innerlik (in die karakter se gedagtes) of uiterlik (teen 'n ander karakter, die samelewing of die natuur).","en":"A struggle in a story: internal (in the character's mind) or external (against another character, society or nature)."}},{"term":{"af":"Klimaks (climax)","en":"Climax"},"def":{"af":"Die keerpunt van die verhaal waar die spanning op sy hoogste is.","en":"The turning point of the story where the tension is at its highest."}},{"term":{"af":"Protagonis (protagonist)","en":"Protagonist"},"def":{"af":"Die hoofkarakter van die verhaal; die antagonis is die persoon of krag wat teen hom/haar werk.","en":"The main character of the story; the antagonist is the person or force working against him/her."}},{"term":{"af":"Karakterisering (characterisation)","en":"Characterisation"},"def":{"af":"Hoe 'n skrywer 'n karakter uitbeeld: direk (die verteller sê dit) of indirek (deur woorde, gedagtes, dade, ander se reaksies en voorkoms).","en":"How a writer portrays a character: directly (the narrator says it) or indirectly (through speech, thoughts, actions, others' reactions and looks)."}},{"term":{"af":"Verteller (narrator)","en":"Narrator"},"def":{"af":"Die stem wat die storie vertel: eerstepersoon (*I*) of derdepersoon (*he/she*), alwetend of beperk.","en":"The voice that tells the story: first person (*I*) or third person (*he/she*), omniscient or limited."}},{"term":{"af":"Ruimte (setting)","en":"Setting"},"def":{"af":"Die tyd, plek en sosiale/historiese omstandighede waarin die verhaal afspeel.","en":"The time, place and social/historical circumstances in which the story takes place."}},{"term":{"af":"Tema (theme)","en":"Theme"},"def":{"af":"Die boodskap of insig oor die lewe wat die verhaal oordra, in 'n volsin geskryf.","en":"The message or insight about life that the story conveys, written as a full sentence."}},{"term":{"af":"Ironie (irony)","en":"Irony"},"def":{"af":"'n Teenstelling tussen wat gesê of verwag word en wat werklik is of gebeur: verbaal, situasie of dramaties.","en":"A contrast between what is said or expected and what really is or happens: verbal, situational or dramatic."}},{"term":{"af":"Terugflits (flashback)","en":"Flashback"},"def":{"af":"'n Toneel uit die verlede wat die huidige gebeure onderbreek; vooruitwysing (*foreshadowing*) gee eerder 'n wenk oor die toekoms.","en":"A scene from the past that interrupts the present events; foreshadowing instead hints at the future."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Ruimte en karakter","en":"Setting and character"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die uittreksel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) Describe the setting of this extract. (2)\n(b) Refer to lines 3–4. What do Karabo's words reveal about his character? Quote to support your answer. (2)","en":"Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) Describe the setting of this extract. (2)\n(b) Refer to lines 3–4. What do Karabo's words reveal about his character? Quote to support your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) 2 punte = tyd + plek. Soek tydwoorde: *The sun was already sinking* (reël 1) → laatmiddag / sononder.","en":"(a) 2 marks = time + place. Look for time words: *The sun was already sinking* (line 1) → late afternoon / sunset."},{"af":"Soek plekwoorde: *Oom Gert's fence*, *orange trees*, *Magaliesberg* → Oom Gert se lemoenboord naby die Magaliesberg.","en":"Look for place words: *Oom Gert's fence*, *orange trees*, *Magaliesberg* → Oom Gert's orange orchard near the Magaliesberg."},{"af":"(b) Indirekte karakterisering deur sy woorde (*Speech*): hy steel om sy ma te voed, nie vir homself nie → hy is **omgee/onselfsugtig** (*caring/selfless*).","en":"(b) Indirect characterisation through his words (*Speech*): he steals to feed his mother, not himself → he is **caring/selfless**."},{"af":"Ondersteun met 'n kort aanhaling tussen aanhalingstekens: \"Mama won't go to bed hungry again tonight.\" Die woord *again* wys dat die armoede nie nuut is nie.","en":"Support with a short quotation in inverted commas: \"Mama won't go to bed hungry again tonight.\" The word *again* shows that the poverty is not new."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) It is late afternoon/sunset (\"The sun was already sinking\") on Oom Gert's orange farm near the Magaliesberg. (b) Karabo is caring and selfless: \"Mama won't go to bed hungry again tonight.\"","en":"(a) It is late afternoon/sunset (\"The sun was already sinking\") on Oom Gert's orange farm near the Magaliesberg. (b) Karabo is caring and selfless: \"Mama won't go to bed hungry again tonight.\""}},{"title":{"af":"Ironie en verteller","en":"Irony and narrator"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik dieselfde uittreksel.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) Explain the situational irony in lines 12–15. (2)\n(b) Identify the type of narrator in this extract and motivate your answer. (2)","en":"Use the same extract.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) Explain the situational irony in lines 12–15. (2)\n(b) Identify the type of narrator in this extract and motivate your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Wat word **verwag**? Karabo (en die leser) verwag straf: *the shout, the blow, the police van* (reël 12).","en":"(a) What is **expected**? Karabo (and the reader) expect punishment: *the shout, the blow, the police van* (line 12)."},{"af":"Wat gebeur **werklik**? Oom Gert is sag en nooi hom om volgende keer by die voorhek te kom vra. Die teenoorgestelde van die verwagting = situasie-ironie (en 'n verrassingseinde).","en":"What **actually** happens? Oom Gert is gentle and invites him to come and ask at the front gate next time. The opposite of what was expected = situational irony (and a twist ending)."},{"af":"(b) Die verteller gebruik *he* en *Karabo*, dus derdepersoon.","en":"(b) The narrator uses *he* and *Karabo*, so it is third person."},{"af":"Ons ken net Karabo se gedagtes (*he was sure the whole farm could hear it*), nie Oom Gert s'n nie → **third person limited**.","en":"We only know Karabo's thoughts (*he was sure the whole farm could hear it*), not Oom Gert's → **third person limited**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Karabo expects to be shouted at, hit or arrested, but instead the farmer treats him kindly and tells him to ask next time. (b) Third person limited: the narrator uses \"he\" and shows only Karabo's thoughts and feelings.","en":"(a) Karabo expects to be shouted at, hit or arrested, but instead the farmer treats him kindly and tells him to ask next time. (b) Third person limited: the narrator uses \"he\" and shows only Karabo's thoughts and feelings."}},{"title":{"af":"Tema en evaluering","en":"Theme and evaluation"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik dieselfde uittreksel.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) State ONE theme of this extract and explain how the extract conveys it. (2)\n(b) Is Karabo's behaviour justified? Discuss your view. (3)","en":"Use the same extract.\n\nTHE ORANGE THIEF (extract)\n\n1  The sun was already sinking behind the Magaliesberg when Karabo slipped through\n2  the gap in Oom Gert's fence. The orange trees stood in neat, silent rows.\n3  \"Just five,\" he whispered. \"Five oranges, and Mama won't go to bed hungry\n4  again tonight.\"\n5  Somewhere behind him a dog barked once – then silence. Karabo froze. His heart\n6  drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\n7  With shaking hands he filled his school bag. Then a torch beam caught him\n8  full in the face.\n9  \"So,\" said a slow, deep voice, \"you are the one who has been taking my\n10 oranges.\" Oom Gert stood between the trees, tall and broad, leaning on his\n11 heavy walking stick.\n12 Karabo could not speak. He waited for the shout, the blow, the police van.\n13 Instead, the old farmer sighed and pushed back his hat. \"Next time,\" he said\n14 quietly, \"come to the front gate and ask. A boy who carries a bag that heavy\n15 should not have to climb through a fence as well.\"\n\n(a) State ONE theme of this extract and explain how the extract conveys it. (2)\n(b) Is Karabo's behaviour justified? Discuss your view. (3)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Skryf die tema as 'n **volsin**, nie net *kindness* nie: *Kindness and understanding can overcome the barriers that poverty creates.*","en":"(a) Write the theme as a **full sentence**, not just *kindness*: *Kindness and understanding can overcome the barriers that poverty creates.*"},{"af":"Wys hoe: Oom Gert kies om Karabo te help eerder as om hom te straf; die *fence* (skeiding) word vervang deur die *front gate* ('n eerlike, oop pad na hulp).","en":"Show how: Oom Gert chooses to help Karabo instead of punishing him; the *fence* (separation) is replaced by the *front gate* (an honest, open way to get help)."},{"af":"(b) 3 punte = 'n duidelike **standpunt** + **twee redes** uit die teks. Albei standpunte kan punte kry as jy dit motiveer.","en":"(b) 3 marks = a clear **view** + **two reasons** from the text. Both views can earn marks if you motivate them."},{"af":"Voorbeeld: *Partly.* Steel is verkeerd, maar sy motief is om sy honger ma te voed (\"Mama won't go to bed hungry\") en hy neem net vyf lemoene. Tog kon hy gevra het, soos Oom Gert self aan die einde sê.","en":"Example: *Partly.* Stealing is wrong, but his motive is to feed his hungry mother (\"Mama won't go to bed hungry\") and he takes only five oranges. Still, he could have asked, as Oom Gert himself says at the end."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Kindness can overcome the barriers that poverty creates: the farmer helps instead of punishing, and offers the front gate instead of the fence. (b) Partly justified: his motive is to feed his hungry mother and he takes only five oranges, but stealing is still wrong and he could have asked.","en":"(a) Kindness can overcome the barriers that poverty creates: the farmer helps instead of punishing, and offers the front gate instead of the fence. (b) Partly justified: his motive is to feed his hungry mother and he takes only five oranges, but stealing is still wrong and he could have asked."}},{"title":{"af":"Eerstepersoon, terugflits en vooruitwysing","en":"First person, flashback and foreshadowing"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die begin van 'n ander kortverhaal.\n\n1  I still remember the morning the river came into our house. I was nine, and\n2  Ma had said the night before that the clouds over the dam looked angry. Now,\n3  twenty years later, I stand in the same kitchen, and I can still smell the\n4  mud on the walls.\n\n(a) Identify the narrative point of view. Give ONE reason. (2)\n(b) Which technique is used in lines 1–3? (1)\n(c) What do the \"angry\" clouds in line 2 foreshadow? (1)","en":"Read the opening of another short story.\n\n1  I still remember the morning the river came into our house. I was nine, and\n2  Ma had said the night before that the clouds over the dam looked angry. Now,\n3  twenty years later, I stand in the same kitchen, and I can still smell the\n4  mud on the walls.\n\n(a) Identify the narrative point of view. Give ONE reason. (2)\n(b) Which technique is used in lines 1–3? (1)\n(c) What do the \"angry\" clouds in line 2 foreshadow? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die verteller gebruik *I* en is self 'n karakter in die storie → **first-person narrator**.","en":"(a) The narrator uses *I* and is a character in the story → **first-person narrator**."},{"af":"(b) *I still remember* en *twenty years later*: die verteller kyk terug op iets wat lank gelede gebeur het → **flashback** (terugflits).","en":"(b) *I still remember* and *twenty years later*: the narrator looks back on something that happened long ago → **flashback**."},{"af":"(c) Die \"kwaai\" wolke is 'n wenk (en personifikasie) dat 'n storm gaan kom wat die rivier laat oorstroom en die huis inspoel.","en":"(c) The \"angry\" clouds are a hint (and personification) that a storm is coming which will make the river flood into the house."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) First person: the narrator uses \"I\"/is a character in the story. (b) Flashback. (c) The coming storm and the flood.","en":"(a) First person: the narrator uses \"I\"/is a character in the story. (b) Flashback. (c) The coming storm and the flood."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter deel van die intrige is die keerpunt waar die spanning op sy hoogste is?","en":"Which part of the plot is the turning point where the tension is at its highest?"},"options":[{"af":"Exposition","en":"Exposition"},{"af":"Climax","en":"Climax"},{"af":"Falling action","en":"Falling action"},{"af":"Resolution","en":"Resolution"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die *climax* is die keerpunt. Die *exposition* stel ons aan die karakters bekend, en die *falling action* en *resolution* kom ná die klimaks.","en":"The *climax* is the turning point. The *exposition* introduces the characters, and the *falling action* and *resolution* come after the climax."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die hoofkarakter van 'n verhaal word die ___ genoem.","en":"The main character of a story is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["protagonist","protagonis"],"en":["protagonist"]},"explain":{"af":"Die *protagonist* is die hoofkarakter. Die *antagonist* werk teen hom/haar, en die *narrator* is die stem wat die storie vertel.","en":"The *protagonist* is the main character. The *antagonist* works against him/her, and the *narrator* is the voice that tells the story."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["antagonist","narrator","minor character"],"en":["antagonist","narrator","minor character"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? 'n *Flat character* het baie kante en verander deur die verhaal.","en":"True or false? A *flat character* has many sides and changes during the story."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n *Flat character* het net een of twee eienskappe. Baie kante = *round*; iemand wat verander = *dynamic*.","en":"False. A *flat character* has only one or two traits. Many sides = *round*; someone who changes = *dynamic*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Toneel uit die verlede wat die huidige gebeure in 'n verhaal onderbreek, is 'n ___.","en":"A scene from the past that interrupts the present events in a story is a ___."},"answers":{"af":["flashback","terugflits","flash-back"],"en":["flashback","flash-back"]},"explain":{"af":"'n *Flashback* gaan terug na die verlede. *Foreshadowing* is die teenoorgestelde: 'n wenk oor die toekoms.","en":"A *flashback* goes back to the past. *Foreshadowing* is the opposite: a hint about the future."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["foreshadowing","climax","motif"],"en":["foreshadowing","climax","motif"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*\"I locked the door behind me and wondered whether I would ever see my brother again.\"* Watter vertelperspektief word gebruik?","en":"*\"I locked the door behind me and wondered whether I would ever see my brother again.\"* Which narrative point of view is used?"},"options":[{"af":"Third person omniscient","en":"Third person omniscient"},{"af":"Third person limited","en":"Third person limited"},{"af":"First person","en":"First person"},{"af":"Second person","en":"Second person"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die verteller gebruik *I* en vertel sy eie ervaring, dus is dit eerstepersoon (*first person*).","en":"The narrator uses *I* and tells his own experience, so it is *first person*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die atmosfeer of gevoel wat 'n verhaal by die leser skep, word die ___ genoem.","en":"The atmosphere or feeling that a story creates in the reader is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["mood","stemming"],"en":["mood"]},"explain":{"af":"*Mood* = die gevoel by die leser. *Tone* = die verteller of skrywer se houding. Dit is 'n algemene fout om die twee te verwar.","en":"*Mood* = the feeling in the reader. *Tone* = the narrator's or writer's attitude. Confusing the two is a common mistake."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["tone","theme","setting"],"en":["tone","theme","setting"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke term by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each term to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Verbal irony","en":"Verbal irony"},"r":{"af":"Iemand sê die teenoorgestelde van wat hy bedoel","en":"Someone says the opposite of what he means"}},{"l":{"af":"Situational irony","en":"Situational irony"},"r":{"af":"Die teenoorgestelde gebeur van wat verwag word","en":"The opposite of what is expected happens"}},{"l":{"af":"Dramatic irony","en":"Dramatic irony"},"r":{"af":"Die leser weet iets wat die karakter nie weet nie","en":"The reader knows something the character does not know"}},{"l":{"af":"Foreshadowing","en":"Foreshadowing"},"r":{"af":"'n Wenk oor iets wat later gaan gebeur","en":"A hint of something that will happen later"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die drie soorte ironie gaan almal oor 'n teenstelling: tussen woorde en bedoeling (verbaal), verwagting en uitkoms (situasie) of wat die leser en die karakter weet (dramaties).","en":"All three kinds of irony are about a contrast: between words and meaning (verbal), expectation and outcome (situational) or what the reader and the character know (dramatic)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is 'n TEMA en nie net 'n onderwerp nie?","en":"Which one is a THEME and not just a subject?"},"options":[{"af":"Poverty","en":"Poverty"},{"af":"A boy steals oranges","en":"A boy steals oranges"},{"af":"Kindness can break down the barriers between people.","en":"Kindness can break down the barriers between people."},{"af":"Friendship","en":"Friendship"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Tema is 'n boodskap oor die lewe in 'n volsin. *Poverty* en *Friendship* is onderwerpe, en *A boy steals oranges* is 'n gebeurtenis in die intrige.","en":"A theme is a message about life in a full sentence. *Poverty* and *Friendship* are subjects, and *A boy steals oranges* is an event in the plot."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? 'n Alwetende derdepersoonverteller (*third person omniscient*) kan die gedagtes van meer as een karakter aan die leser wys.","en":"True or false? A *third-person omniscient* narrator can show the reader the thoughts of more than one character."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. *Omniscient* beteken alwetend: die verteller ken almal se gedagtes. 'n *Limited* verteller volg net een karakter se gedagtes.","en":"True. *Omniscient* means all-knowing: the narrator knows everyone's thoughts. A *limited* narrator follows only one character's thoughts."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die verteller sê: *\"Mrs Naidoo was the strictest teacher in Brits.\"* Dit is ___ karakterisering.","en":"The narrator says: *\"Mrs Naidoo was the strictest teacher in Brits.\"* This is ___ characterisation."},"answers":{"af":["direct","direk"],"en":["direct"]},"explain":{"af":"Die verteller *sê* reguit hoe sy is, dus direkte karakterisering. Indirek sou wees as ons dit uit haar dade of woorde moes aflei.","en":"The narrator *tells* us directly what she is like, so it is direct characterisation. Indirect would be if we had to work it out from her actions or words."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["indirect","dynamic","flat"],"en":["indirect","dynamic","flat"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Sipho looked at the hail flattening his tomatoes. \"What perfect gardening weather,\" he muttered.* Dit is ___ irony.","en":"*Sipho looked at the hail flattening his tomatoes. \"What perfect gardening weather,\" he muttered.* This is ___ irony."},"answers":{"af":["verbal","verbale"],"en":["verbal"]},"explain":{"af":"Sipho *sê* die teenoorgestelde van wat hy bedoel (die hael is verskriklik), dus verbale ironie. Dit klink ook sarkasties.","en":"Sipho *says* the opposite of what he means (the hail is terrible), so it is verbal irony. It also sounds sarcastic."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["dramatic","situational","cosmic"],"en":["dramatic","situational","cosmic"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Karabo weet steel is verkeerd, maar hy wil sy honger ma help. Watter soort konflik is dit?","en":"Karabo knows that stealing is wrong, but he wants to help his hungry mother. What kind of conflict is this?"},"options":[{"af":"Character vs character","en":"Character vs character"},{"af":"Character vs nature","en":"Character vs nature"},{"af":"Character vs society","en":"Character vs society"},{"af":"Internal conflict","en":"Internal conflict"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die stryd vind in sy eie gedagtes plaas (gewete teenoor nood), dus innerlike konflik. Sy botsing met Oom Gert sou *character vs character* wees.","en":"The struggle takes place in his own mind (conscience versus need), so it is internal conflict. His clash with Oom Gert would be *character vs character*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*\"His heart drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\"* Wat is die hoofeffek van hierdie sin op die leser?","en":"*\"His heart drummed so loudly that he was sure the whole farm could hear it.\"* What is the main effect of this sentence on the reader?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit skep humor","en":"It creates humour"},{"af":"Dit skep spanning","en":"It creates suspense"},{"af":"Dit is 'n terugflits","en":"It is a flashback"},{"af":"Dit los die konflik op","en":"It resolves the conflict"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die oordrywing van sy hartklop wys sy vrees, en die leser wonder of hy gevang gaan word: dit bou spanning (*suspense*).","en":"The exaggeration of his heartbeat shows his fear, and the reader wonders whether he will be caught: it builds *suspense*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Oom Gert vang Karabo, sug en sê: *\"Next time, come to the front gate and ask.\"* Wat wys sy optrede oor sy karakter?","en":"Oom Gert catches Karabo, sighs and says: *\"Next time, come to the front gate and ask.\"* What do his actions reveal about his character?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is vergewensgesind en meelewend","en":"He is forgiving and compassionate"},{"af":"Hy is wreed en kwaad","en":"He is cruel and angry"},{"af":"Hy is lui en ongeërg","en":"He is lazy and indifferent"},{"af":"Hy is bang vir Karabo","en":"He is afraid of Karabo"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Hy straf nie, maar bied hulp aan: indirekte karakterisering deur sy dade en woorde wys dat hy vergewensgesind en meelewend is.","en":"He does not punish but offers help: indirect characterisation through his actions and words shows that he is forgiving and compassionate."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Karabo glip deur 'n gat in die heining, maar Oom Gert sê hy moet volgende keer by die *front gate* kom vra. Wat simboliseer die voorhek waarskynlik?","en":"Karabo slips through a gap in the fence, but Oom Gert says that next time he must come and ask at the *front gate*. What does the front gate most likely symbolise?"},"options":[{"af":"Die boer se rykdom","en":"The farmer's wealth"},{"af":"Gevaar en straf","en":"Danger and punishment"},{"af":"Oneerlikheid","en":"Dishonesty"},{"af":"'n Eerlike, oop manier om hulp te vra","en":"An honest, open way to ask for help"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die gat in die heining staan vir die geheime, oneerlike pad; die voorhek is die oop, eerlike pad waar Karabo welkom is om te vra.","en":"The gap in the fence stands for the secret, dishonest way; the front gate is the open, honest way where Karabo is welcome to ask."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*\"Is Karabo's behaviour justified? Discuss.\"* (3) Watter antwoord sal die volle 3 punte verdien?","en":"*\"Is Karabo's behaviour justified? Discuss.\"* (3) Which answer would earn the full 3 marks?"},"options":[{"af":"No, stealing is wrong.","en":"No, stealing is wrong."},{"af":"Karabo slips through the fence, fills his bag and is caught by Oom Gert.","en":"Karabo slips through the fence, fills his bag and is caught by Oom Gert."},{"af":"Partly. Stealing is wrong, but he only takes five oranges to feed his hungry mother (\"Mama won't go to bed hungry\"), so his motive is understandable.","en":"Partly. Stealing is wrong, but he only takes five oranges to feed his hungry mother (\"Mama won't go to bed hungry\"), so his motive is understandable."},{"af":"Yes, because Oom Gert is rich.","en":"Yes, because Oom Gert is rich."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vir 3 punte het jy 'n standpunt + redes + bewys uit die teks nodig. Die eerste antwoord het net een rede, die tweede vertel net die storie oor, en die laaste berus op 'n aanname wat nie in die teks staan nie.","en":"For 3 marks you need a view + reasons + evidence from the text. The first answer has only one reason, the second just retells the story, and the last rests on an assumption that is not in the text."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t2-voice-reported-speech","title":{"af":"Lydende vorm en indirekte rede","en":"Active and passive voice; direct and reported speech"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal Engelse sinne korrek van die bedrywende na die lydende vorm en van direkte na indirekte rede (en terug) kan omskakel.","en":"You will be able to change English sentences correctly from the active to the passive voice and from direct to reported speech (and back)."},"summary":{"af":"## Deel 1: Bedrywende en lydende vorm (*active and passive voice*)\n\nIn die **bedrywende vorm** (*active voice*) doen die onderwerp die handeling: *The chef cooks the meal.* In die **lydende vorm** (*passive voice*) verskuif die klem na die persoon of ding wat die handeling ondergaan: *The meal is cooked by the chef.*\n\n### Stappe: bedrywend → lydend\n\n1. Soek die **voorwerp** (*the meal*). Dit word die nuwe **onderwerp**.\n2. Bepaal die **tyd** van die werkwoord en kies die regte vorm van **to be** (*is, are, was, were, is being, has been, will be…*).\n3. Voeg die **voltooide deelwoord** (*past participle*) by: *cooked, written, eaten, built*.\n4. Voeg **by + doener** by (*by the chef*), of laat dit weg.\n5. Kontroleer die **kongruensie**: *The meal is…* maar *The meals are…*\n\n| Tyd | Bedrywend (*active*) | Lydend (*passive*) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Simple present | The chef cooks the meal. | The meal **is cooked** by the chef. |\n| Simple past | The chef cooked the meal. | The meal **was cooked** by the chef. |\n| Present continuous | The chef is cooking the meal. | The meal **is being cooked** by the chef. |\n| Past continuous | The chef was cooking the meal. | The meal **was being cooked** by the chef. |\n| Present perfect | The chef has cooked the meal. | The meal **has been cooked** by the chef. |\n| Past perfect | The chef had cooked the meal. | The meal **had been cooked** by the chef. |\n| Future | The chef will cook the meal. | The meal **will be cooked** by the chef. |\n| Modal | The chef must cook the meal. | The meal **must be cooked** by the chef. |\n\n- **Voornaamwoorde verander:** *They praised him.* → *He was praised by them.* (voorwerpsvorm *him* word onderwerpsvorm *he*; *they* word *them* ná *by*).\n- **Laat die doener weg** as hy onbekend, vanselfsprekend of onbelangrik is: *My phone was stolen.* *The thief was arrested.*\n- **Lydend → bedrywend:** die doener ná *by* word weer die onderwerp: *The match was won by our team.* → *Our team won the match.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Die verlede tyd in plaas van die voltooide deelwoord: ✗ *The letter was wrote* → ✓ *The letter was written*.\n\n> **Lokval vir Afrikaanssprekendes:** Die huis **word** gebou = The house **is being built / is built** (hede). Die huis **is** gebou = The house **was built / has been built** (verlede). Moenie Afrikaans se *is* outomaties as Engels *is* vertaal nie!\n\n## Deel 2: Direkte en indirekte rede (*direct and reported speech*)\n\n### Leestekens in direkte rede\n\n- Die presiese woorde staan tussen **aanhalingstekens**: *Thandi said, \"I am tired.\"*\n- 'n **Komma** (of **?** of **!**) kom vóór die sluitende aanhalingstekens: *\"I am tired,\" said Thandi.*\n- Die gesproke woorde begin met 'n **hoofletter**. 'n Nuwe spreker kry 'n nuwe paragraaf.\n\n### Stappe: direk → indirek\n\n1. Verwyder die aanhalingstekens en voeg **that** by (dit mag ook weggelaat word).\n2. Verander die **voornaamwoorde**: *I → he/she; we → they; my → his/her*.\n3. Skuif die **tyd een stap terug** as die rapporterende werkwoord in die verlede tyd is (*said, asked, told*).\n4. Verander **tyd- en plekwoorde**.\n\n| Direk | Indirek |\n|---|---|\n| am / is | was |\n| are | were |\n| simple present (*play*) | simple past (*played*) |\n| present continuous (*is playing*) | past continuous (*was playing*) |\n| simple past / present perfect (*played / has played*) | past perfect (*had played*) |\n| will / can / may / must | would / could / might / had to |\n\n| Direk | Indirek |\n|---|---|\n| today / tonight | that day / that night |\n| tomorrow | the next day / the following day |\n| yesterday | the previous day / the day before |\n| now / here | then / there |\n| this / these | that / those |\n| ago | before |\n\n### Vrae en bevele\n\n- **Ja/nee-vrae:** *asked + if/whether*: *\"Are you ready?\"* → *He asked if I was ready.*\n- **Vraagwoord-vrae:** behou die vraagwoord, maar gebruik **stellende woordorde** sonder *do/does/did* en sonder vraagteken: *\"Where do you live?\"* → *He asked where I lived.*\n- **Bevele en versoeke:** *told/asked/ordered + (not) to + infinitief*: *\"Close the door.\"* → *She told me to close the door.* *\"Don't shout!\"* → *She told me not to shout.* (let op: **not to**)\n\n> **Lokval:** In Afrikaans bly die tyd dieselfde: Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In Engels skuif dit terug: He said that he **was** tired.\n\n> **Wenk:** As die rapporterende werkwoord in die hede is (*He says…*), skuif die tyd nie: *He says that he is tired.*","en":"## Part 1: Active and passive voice\n\nIn the **active voice** the subject performs the action: *The chef cooks the meal.* In the **passive voice** the focus moves to the thing that undergoes the action: *The meal is cooked by the chef.*\n\n### Steps: active → passive\n\n1. Find the **object** (*the meal*). It becomes the new **subject**.\n2. Identify the **tense** of the verb and choose the correct form of **to be** (*is, are, was, were, is being, has been, will be…*).\n3. Add the **past participle**: *cooked, written, eaten, built*.\n4. Add **by + doer** (*by the chef*), or leave it out.\n5. Check the **concord**: *The meal is…* but *The meals are…*\n\n| Tense | Active | Passive |\n|---|---|---|\n| Simple present | The chef cooks the meal. | The meal **is cooked** by the chef. |\n| Simple past | The chef cooked the meal. | The meal **was cooked** by the chef. |\n| Present continuous | The chef is cooking the meal. | The meal **is being cooked** by the chef. |\n| Past continuous | The chef was cooking the meal. | The meal **was being cooked** by the chef. |\n| Present perfect | The chef has cooked the meal. | The meal **has been cooked** by the chef. |\n| Past perfect | The chef had cooked the meal. | The meal **had been cooked** by the chef. |\n| Future | The chef will cook the meal. | The meal **will be cooked** by the chef. |\n| Modal | The chef must cook the meal. | The meal **must be cooked** by the chef. |\n\n- **Pronouns change:** *They praised him.* → *He was praised by them.* (object form *him* becomes subject form *he*; *they* becomes *them* after *by*).\n- **Leave out the doer** when it is unknown, obvious or unimportant: *My phone was stolen.* *The thief was arrested.*\n- **Passive → active:** the doer after *by* becomes the subject again: *The match was won by our team.* → *Our team won the match.*\n\n> **Common mistake:** Using the simple past instead of the past participle: ✗ *The letter was wrote* → ✓ *The letter was written*.\n\n> **Trap for Afrikaans speakers:** Die huis **word** gebou = The house **is being built / is built** (present). Die huis **is** gebou = The house **was built / has been built** (past). Do not automatically translate Afrikaans *is* as English *is*!\n\n## Part 2: Direct and reported speech\n\n### Punctuating direct speech\n\n- The exact words go inside **inverted commas**: *Thandi said, \"I am tired.\"*\n- A **comma** (or **?** or **!**) comes before the closing inverted commas: *\"I am tired,\" said Thandi.*\n- The spoken words start with a **capital letter**. A new speaker gets a new paragraph.\n\n### Steps: direct → reported\n\n1. Remove the inverted commas and add **that** (it may also be left out).\n2. Change the **pronouns**: *I → he/she; we → they; my → his/her*.\n3. Shift the **tense one step back** if the reporting verb is in the past tense (*said, asked, told*).\n4. Change **time and place words**.\n\n| Direct | Reported |\n|---|---|\n| am / is | was |\n| are | were |\n| simple present (*play*) | simple past (*played*) |\n| present continuous (*is playing*) | past continuous (*was playing*) |\n| simple past / present perfect (*played / has played*) | past perfect (*had played*) |\n| will / can / may / must | would / could / might / had to |\n\n| Direct | Reported |\n|---|---|\n| today / tonight | that day / that night |\n| tomorrow | the next day / the following day |\n| yesterday | the previous day / the day before |\n| now / here | then / there |\n| this / these | that / those |\n| ago | before |\n\n### Questions and commands\n\n- **Yes/no questions:** *asked + if/whether*: *\"Are you ready?\"* → *He asked if I was ready.*\n- **Question-word questions:** keep the question word, but use **statement word order** without *do/does/did* and without a question mark: *\"Where do you live?\"* → *He asked where I lived.*\n- **Commands and requests:** *told/asked/ordered + (not) to + infinitive*: *\"Close the door.\"* → *She told me to close the door.* *\"Don't shout!\"* → *She told me not to shout.* (note: **not to**)\n\n> **Trap:** In Afrikaans the tense stays the same: Hy het gesê dat hy moeg **is**. In English it shifts back: He said that he **was** tired.\n\n> **Tip:** If the reporting verb is in the present tense (*He says…*), the tense does not shift: *He says that he is tired.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bedrywende vorm (active voice)","en":"Active voice"},"def":{"af":"Die onderwerp doen die handeling: *The dog chased the cat.*","en":"The subject performs the action: *The dog chased the cat.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Lydende vorm (passive voice)","en":"Passive voice"},"def":{"af":"Die voorwerp word die onderwerp; vorm van *to be* + voltooide deelwoord (+ *by* + doener): *The cat was chased by the dog.*","en":"The object becomes the subject; form of *to be* + past participle (+ *by* + doer): *The cat was chased by the dog.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Voltooide deelwoord (past participle)","en":"Past participle"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoordvorm ná *has/have/had* of in die lydende vorm: *written, eaten, built, stolen*.","en":"The verb form after *has/have/had* or in the passive: *written, eaten, built, stolen*."}},{"term":{"af":"Doener (doer/agent)","en":"Doer (agent)"},"def":{"af":"Die persoon of ding wat die handeling uitvoer; in die lydende vorm staan dit ná *by* of word weggelaat.","en":"The person or thing performing the action; in the passive it follows *by* or is left out."}},{"term":{"af":"Direkte rede (direct speech)","en":"Direct speech"},"def":{"af":"Iemand se presiese woorde tussen aanhalingstekens: *Lerato said, \"I am late.\"*","en":"Someone's exact words in inverted commas: *Lerato said, \"I am late.\"*"}},{"term":{"af":"Indirekte rede (reported speech)","en":"Reported (indirect) speech"},"def":{"af":"Jy vertel wat iemand gesê het sonder aanhalingstekens, met tyd-, voornaamwoord- en tydwoordveranderinge: *Lerato said that she was late.*","en":"You report what someone said without inverted commas, with tense, pronoun and time-word changes: *Lerato said that she was late.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Rapporterende werkwoord (reporting verb)","en":"Reporting verb"},"def":{"af":"Die werkwoord wat die rede inlei: *said, told, asked, ordered, replied*.","en":"The verb that introduces the speech: *said, told, asked, ordered, replied*."}},{"term":{"af":"Tydverskuiwing (backshift)","en":"Backshift (tense shift)"},"def":{"af":"In indirekte rede skuif die tyd een stap terug ná 'n rapporterende werkwoord in die verlede tyd: *is → was; will → would*.","en":"In reported speech the tense moves one step back after a reporting verb in the past tense: *is → was; will → would*."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhalingstekens (inverted commas)","en":"Inverted commas"},"def":{"af":"Die leestekens (\" \") wat die presiese gesproke woorde in direkte rede omsluit.","en":"The punctuation marks (\" \") that enclose the exact spoken words in direct speech."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Bedrywend na lydend in verskillende tye","en":"Active to passive in different tenses"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf in die lydende vorm:\n(a) The learners plant trees at the school.\n(b) The workers are repairing the bridge.\n(c) Someone has stolen my bicycle.","en":"Rewrite in the passive voice:\n(a) The learners plant trees at the school.\n(b) The workers are repairing the bridge.\n(c) Someone has stolen my bicycle."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Voorwerp *trees* word onderwerp. Tyd: simple present, meervoud → *are* + *planted*: Trees are planted at the school by the learners.","en":"(a) Object *trees* becomes the subject. Tense: simple present, plural → *are* + *planted*: Trees are planted at the school by the learners."},{"af":"(b) Voorwerp *the bridge*. Tyd: present continuous → *is being* + *repaired*: The bridge is being repaired by the workers.","en":"(b) Object *the bridge*. Tense: present continuous → *is being* + *repaired*: The bridge is being repaired by the workers."},{"af":"(c) Voorwerp *my bicycle*. Tyd: present perfect → *has been* + *stolen* (nie *stole* nie).","en":"(c) Object *my bicycle*. Tense: present perfect → *has been* + *stolen* (not *stole*)."},{"af":"Die doener *someone* is onbekend, so ons laat *by someone* weg: My bicycle has been stolen.","en":"The doer *someone* is unknown, so we leave out *by someone*: My bicycle has been stolen."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Trees are planted at the school by the learners. (b) The bridge is being repaired by the workers. (c) My bicycle has been stolen.","en":"(a) Trees are planted at the school by the learners. (b) The bridge is being repaired by the workers. (c) My bicycle has been stolen."}},{"title":{"af":"Lydend na bedrywend","en":"Passive to active"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf in die bedrywende vorm:\n(a) The final was won by Hoërskool Brits.\n(b) The new library will be opened by the mayor.\n(c) The windows must be cleaned by us.","en":"Rewrite in the active voice:\n(a) The final was won by Hoërskool Brits.\n(b) The new library will be opened by the mayor.\n(c) The windows must be cleaned by us."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Die doener ná *by* (*Hoërskool Brits*) word die onderwerp. *was won* = simple past → *won*: Hoërskool Brits won the final.","en":"(a) The doer after *by* (*Hoërskool Brits*) becomes the subject. *was won* = simple past → *won*: Hoërskool Brits won the final."},{"af":"(b) *will be opened* = future → *will open*: The mayor will open the new library.","en":"(b) *will be opened* = future → *will open*: The mayor will open the new library."},{"af":"(c) *by us* → onderwerp *We* (voorwerpsvorm *us* word onderwerpsvorm *we*). Modaal bly: *must clean*: We must clean the windows.","en":"(c) *by us* → subject *We* (object form *us* becomes subject form *we*). The modal stays: *must clean*: We must clean the windows."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Hoërskool Brits won the final. (b) The mayor will open the new library. (c) We must clean the windows.","en":"(a) Hoërskool Brits won the final. (b) The mayor will open the new library. (c) We must clean the windows."}},{"title":{"af":"Direkte na indirekte rede: 'n stelling","en":"Direct to reported speech: a statement"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf in indirekte rede:\nLerato said, \"I will visit my gran in Hartbeespoort tomorrow.\"","en":"Rewrite in reported speech:\nLerato said, \"I will visit my gran in Hartbeespoort tomorrow.\""},"steps":[{"af":"Verwyder die aanhalingstekens en die komma; voeg *that* by: *Lerato said that…*","en":"Remove the inverted commas and the comma; add *that*: *Lerato said that…*"},{"af":"Voornaamwoorde: *I → she*, *my → her*.","en":"Pronouns: *I → she*, *my → her*."},{"af":"Tyd: *said* is verlede tyd, dus *will → would*.","en":"Tense: *said* is past tense, so *will → would*."},{"af":"Tydwoord: *tomorrow → the next day* (of *the following day*).","en":"Time word: *tomorrow → the next day* (or *the following day*)."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato said that she would visit her gran in Hartbeespoort the next day.","en":"Lerato said that she would visit her gran in Hartbeespoort the next day."}},{"title":{"af":"Vrae en bevele in indirekte rede","en":"Questions and commands in reported speech"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf in indirekte rede:\n(a) The teacher asked, \"Have you finished your homework?\"\n(b) Coach Mokoena asked, \"Why are you late?\"\n(c) The coach shouted, \"Don't be late for practice again!\"","en":"Rewrite in reported speech:\n(a) The teacher asked, \"Have you finished your homework?\"\n(b) Coach Mokoena asked, \"Why are you late?\"\n(c) The coach shouted, \"Don't be late for practice again!\""},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Ja/nee-vraag → *asked if/whether*. *you → I*, *your → my*; present perfect *have finished* → past perfect *had finished*. Geen vraagteken nie.","en":"(a) Yes/no question → *asked if/whether*. *you → I*, *your → my*; present perfect *have finished* → past perfect *had finished*. No question mark."},{"af":"(b) Vraagwoord *why* bly. Stellende woordorde: onderwerp vóór werkwoord (*I was late*, nie *was I late* nie): Coach Mokoena asked why I was late.","en":"(b) The question word *why* stays. Statement word order: subject before verb (*I was late*, not *was I late*): Coach Mokoena asked why I was late."},{"af":"(c) Bevel → *told us + not to + infinitief*. Die uitroepteken val weg: The coach told us not to be late for practice again.","en":"(c) Command → *told us + not to + infinitive*. The exclamation mark falls away: The coach told us not to be late for practice again."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) The teacher asked if/whether I had finished my homework. (b) Coach Mokoena asked why I was late. (c) The coach told us not to be late for practice again.","en":"(a) The teacher asked if/whether I had finished my homework. (b) Coach Mokoena asked why I was late. (c) The coach told us not to be late for practice again."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is in die lydende vorm?","en":"Which sentence is in the passive voice?"},"options":[{"af":"The dog chased the cat.","en":"The dog chased the cat."},{"af":"The cat was chased by the dog.","en":"The cat was chased by the dog."},{"af":"The cat ran away from the dog.","en":"The cat ran away from the dog."},{"af":"The dog is chasing the cat.","en":"The dog is chasing the cat."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*was chased* = vorm van *to be* + voltooide deelwoord, met *by the dog* as doener. In die ander sinne doen die onderwerp self die handeling.","en":"*was chased* = form of *to be* + past participle, with *by the dog* as the doer. In the other sentences the subject itself performs the action."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? In die lydende vorm word die voorwerp van die bedrywende sin die onderwerp.","en":"True or false? In the passive voice, the object of the active sentence becomes the subject."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. The chef cooks **the meal**. → **The meal** is cooked by the chef.","en":"True. The chef cooks **the meal**. → **The meal** is cooked by the chef."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul die regte vorm van *write* in: *The letter was ___ by Sipho.*","en":"Fill in the correct form of *write*: *The letter was ___ by Sipho.*"},"answers":{"af":["written"],"en":["written"]},"explain":{"af":"Die lydende vorm gebruik die voltooide deelwoord: write – wrote – **written**. *was wrote* is 'n algemene fout.","en":"The passive uses the past participle: write – wrote – **written**. *was wrote* is a common mistake."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["wrote","writed","writing"],"en":["wrote","writed","writing"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke direkte vorm by die regte vorm in indirekte rede.","en":"Match each direct form to the correct form in reported speech."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"will","en":"will"},"r":{"af":"would","en":"would"}},{"l":{"af":"can","en":"can"},"r":{"af":"could","en":"could"}},{"l":{"af":"may","en":"may"},"r":{"af":"might","en":"might"}},{"l":{"af":"must","en":"must"},"r":{"af":"had to","en":"had to"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ná 'n rapporterende werkwoord in die verlede tyd skuif elke modale werkwoord een stap terug.","en":"After a reporting verb in the past tense, each modal verb moves one step back."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In indirekte rede word *tomorrow* → *the ___ day*.","en":"In reported speech, *tomorrow* becomes *the ___ day*."},"answers":{"af":["next","following"],"en":["next","following"]},"explain":{"af":"*tomorrow → the next day / the following day*. *the previous day* is die vorm vir *yesterday*.","en":"*tomorrow → the next day / the following day*. *the previous day* is the form for *yesterday*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["previous","same","other"],"en":["previous","same","other"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Herskryf in die lydende vorm: *The learners clean the classroom every Friday.*","en":"Rewrite in the passive voice: *The learners clean the classroom every Friday.*"},"options":[{"af":"The classroom was cleaned by the learners every Friday.","en":"The classroom was cleaned by the learners every Friday."},{"af":"The classroom is clean by the learners every Friday.","en":"The classroom is clean by the learners every Friday."},{"af":"The classroom is cleaned by the learners every Friday.","en":"The classroom is cleaned by the learners every Friday."},{"af":"The learners are cleaned by the classroom every Friday.","en":"The learners are cleaned by the classroom every Friday."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"*clean* is simple present → *is cleaned*. *was cleaned* verander die tyd, *is clean* het nie die voltooide deelwoord nie, en die laaste sin ruil die betekenis om.","en":"*clean* is simple present → *is cleaned*. *was cleaned* changes the tense, *is clean* lacks the past participle, and the last sentence swaps the meaning."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*The workers are repairing the road.* → *The road ___ repaired by the workers.*","en":"*The workers are repairing the road.* → *The road ___ repaired by the workers.*"},"answers":{"af":["is being"],"en":["is being"]},"explain":{"af":"Present continuous (*are repairing*) → *is being* + voltooide deelwoord. Enkelvoud *the road* → *is*.","en":"Present continuous (*are repairing*) → *is being* + past participle. Singular *the road* → *is*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["is","was being","has been"],"en":["is","was being","has been"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Thabo said, \"I am hungry.\"* Watter een is die korrekte indirekte rede?","en":"*Thabo said, \"I am hungry.\"* Which one is the correct reported speech?"},"options":[{"af":"Thabo said that he is hungry.","en":"Thabo said that he is hungry."},{"af":"Thabo said that he was hungry.","en":"Thabo said that he was hungry."},{"af":"Thabo said that I was hungry.","en":"Thabo said that I was hungry."},{"af":"Thabo said that he had been hungry.","en":"Thabo said that he had been hungry."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*am → was* en *I → he*. Om *is* te behou is die Afrikaanse lokval; *I* moet na *he* verander; *had been* skuif twee stappe terug.","en":"*am → was* and *I → he*. Keeping *is* is the Afrikaans trap; *I* must change to *he*; *had been* shifts two steps back."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? *She asked me where did I live.* is korrekte indirekte rede.","en":"True or false? *She asked me where did I live.* is correct reported speech."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Indirekte vrae gebruik stellende woordorde sonder *did*: *She asked me where I lived.*","en":"False. Reported questions use statement word order without *did*: *She asked me where I lived.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*Mom said, \"You must tidy your room.\"* → *Mom said that I ___ tidy my room.*","en":"*Mom said, \"You must tidy your room.\"* → *Mom said that I ___ tidy my room.*"},"answers":{"af":["had to"],"en":["had to"]},"explain":{"af":"In indirekte rede word *must → had to* ná 'n rapporterende werkwoord in die verlede tyd. *must have* verander die betekenis heeltemal.","en":"In reported speech *must → had to* after a reporting verb in the past tense. *must have* changes the meaning completely."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["has to","must have","will have to"],"en":["has to","must have","will have to"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Herskryf in die bedrywende vorm: *The new library was opened by the mayor.*","en":"Rewrite in the active voice: *The new library was opened by the mayor.*"},"options":[{"af":"The mayor opens the new library.","en":"The mayor opens the new library."},{"af":"The mayor has opened the new library.","en":"The mayor has opened the new library."},{"af":"The new library opened the mayor.","en":"The new library opened the mayor."},{"af":"The mayor opened the new library.","en":"The mayor opened the new library."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"*was opened* = simple past, dus *opened*. Die doener *the mayor* word die onderwerp. Behou altyd die oorspronklike tyd.","en":"*was opened* = simple past, so *opened*. The doer *the mayor* becomes the subject. Always keep the original tense."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*The teacher said to us, \"Don't talk during the test.\"* → *The teacher told us ___ talk during the test.* (twee woorde)","en":"*The teacher said to us, \"Don't talk during the test.\"* → *The teacher told us ___ talk during the test.* (two words)"},"answers":{"af":["not to"],"en":["not to"]},"explain":{"af":"Negatiewe bevele word *told + not to + infinitief*: *told us not to talk*.","en":"Negative commands become *told + not to + infinitive*: *told us not to talk*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["don't","didn't","that we don't"],"en":["don't","didn't","that we don't"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*The coach asked, \"Are you ready for the match?\"* Watter een is die korrekte indirekte rede?","en":"*The coach asked, \"Are you ready for the match?\"* Which one is the correct reported speech?"},"options":[{"af":"The coach asked if we were ready for the match.","en":"The coach asked if we were ready for the match."},{"af":"The coach asked are we ready for the match.","en":"The coach asked are we ready for the match."},{"af":"The coach asked that we were ready for the match?","en":"The coach asked that we were ready for the match?"},{"af":"The coach asked if we are ready for the match.","en":"The coach asked if we are ready for the match."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Ja/nee-vraag → *asked if/whether*, *are → were*, stellende woordorde en geen vraagteken nie. *that* word nie by vrae gebruik nie.","en":"Yes/no question → *asked if/whether*, *are → were*, statement word order and no question mark. *that* is not used with questions."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is fout in hierdie sin? *The cars was washed by the boys.*","en":"What is wrong in this sentence? *The cars was washed by the boys.*"},"options":[{"af":"Die kongruensie: *was* moet *were* wees","en":"The concord: *was* should be *were*"},{"af":"*washed* moet *washing* wees","en":"*washed* should be *washing*"},{"af":"*by the boys* moet weggelaat word","en":"*by the boys* must be left out"},{"af":"Niks; die sin is korrek","en":"Nothing; the sentence is correct"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*The cars* is meervoud, dus *were washed*. Kontroleer altyd die kongruensie met die nuwe onderwerp in die lydende vorm.","en":"*The cars* is plural, so *were washed*. Always check the concord with the new subject in the passive."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder wil *\"Die nuwe saal is verlede jaar gebou.\"* in Engels skryf. Watter sin is korrek?","en":"A learner wants to write *\"Die nuwe saal is verlede jaar gebou.\"* in English. Which sentence is correct?"},"options":[{"af":"The new hall is built last year.","en":"The new hall is built last year."},{"af":"The new hall was built last year.","en":"The new hall was built last year."},{"af":"The new hall is being built last year.","en":"The new hall is being built last year."},{"af":"The new hall has built last year.","en":"The new hall has built last year."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Afrikaans *is gebou* is verlede tyd lydend = *was built*. *last year* bevestig die verlede tyd. *is built* is die lokval van letterlike vertaling.","en":"Afrikaans *is gebou* is past passive = *was built*. *last year* confirms the past tense. *is built* is the trap of literal translation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*Lerato said, \"I saw this film yesterday.\"* Watter een is die korrekte indirekte rede?","en":"*Lerato said, \"I saw this film yesterday.\"* Which one is the correct reported speech?"},"options":[{"af":"Lerato said that she saw this film yesterday.","en":"Lerato said that she saw this film yesterday."},{"af":"Lerato said that I had seen that film the day before.","en":"Lerato said that I had seen that film the day before."},{"af":"Lerato said that she had seen this film yesterday.","en":"Lerato said that she had seen this film yesterday."},{"af":"Lerato said that she had seen that film the previous day.","en":"Lerato said that she had seen that film the previous day."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Al vier veranderinge is nodig: *I → she*, *saw → had seen*, *this → that*, *yesterday → the previous day*. Elke ander opsie het een of meer van hierdie veranderinge gemis.","en":"All four changes are needed: *I → she*, *saw → had seen*, *this → that*, *yesterday → the previous day*. Every other option misses one or more of these changes."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t2-letters-cv","title":{"af":"Briewe, CV en dekbrief","en":"Letters, CV and covering letter"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal formele en vriendskaplike briewe in die korrekte formaat en register kan skryf, en 'n CV met 'n dekbrief kan opstel.","en":"You will be able to write formal and friendly letters in the correct format and register, and draw up a CV with a covering letter."},"summary":{"af":"## Waar pas briewe in?\n\nBriewe is **langer transaksionele tekste** in **Vraestel 3, Afdeling B** (30 punte). Die **liggaam** van die brief moet **120–150 woorde** wees; die adresse, datum, aanhef en slot tel nie. Die nasiener kyk na inhoud, beplanning en **formaat**, en na taal, styl en redigering, so 'n korrekte uitleg gee maklike punte.\n\n## Soorte formele briewe\n\n- **Versoek** (*request*): jy vra inligting of toestemming.\n- **Klagte** (*complaint*): jy beskryf 'n probleem beleefd en vra vir 'n oplossing.\n- **Aansoek** (*application*): jy doen aansoek om 'n pos of beurs, saam met 'n **CV**.\n- **Brief aan die pers** (*letter to the press*): jy lewer kommentaar op 'n saak in 'n koerant.\n- **Bedankings- of sakebrief** (*thank-you/business letter*).\n\n## Formaat van 'n formele brief\n\n1. **Afsender se adres** regs bo. Gebruik 'n **versinde** adres, bv. *PO Box 512, Brits, 0250*.\n2. **Datum** reg onder die adres, met die maand in woorde: *21 October 2026*.\n3. **Ontvanger se titel en adres** links, onder die datum: *The Manager, …*\n4. **Aanhef** (*salutation*): *Dear Sir/Madam* (naam onbekend) of *Dear Mr Mokoena* (naam bekend).\n5. **Onderwerpreël** (*subject line*) direk ná die aanhef: *RE: Broken streetlights in Mimosa Street*, of 'n vetgedrukte/onderstreepte opskrif.\n6. **Liggaam** in paragrawe: **doel** (hoekom jy skryf) → **besonderhede** (feite, voorbeelde) → **versoek/aksie** (wat jy wil hê moet gebeur).\n7. **Slot** (*closing*) met 'n komma.\n8. **Handtekening**, en daaronder jou **voorletters en van**: *K. Molefe*.\n\n| Aanhef | Slot |\n|---|---|\n| Dear Sir/Madam | **Yours faithfully** |\n| Dear Mr Mokoena / Dear Ms Dlamini | **Yours sincerely** |\n| Dear Lerato (informeel) | Love, / Regards, / Your friend, + voornaam |\n\n> **Wenk:** *S*incerely gaan saam met 'n *S*pesifieke naam; *Faithfully* gaan saam met *Sir/Madam*. Net die *Y* van *Yours* kry 'n hoofletter.\n\n## Vriendskaplike (informele) brief\n\n- Net **jou eie adres en die datum** regs bo; **geen** ontvanger se adres nie.\n- Aanhef: *Dear Lerato,* (met 'n komma).\n- Kletserig en persoonlik, maar steeds **korrekte taal**: geen SMS-taal nie (*u, coz, thanx*).\n- Sluit af met *Love,* / *Regards,* / *Your friend,* + **net jou voornaam**.\n\n## CV (*curriculum vitae*) en dekbrief\n\n'n **CV** is 'n kort, netjiese opsomming van wie jy is. Gebruik **opskrifte** en puntsgewyse inligting:\n\n1. **Personal details**: naam, adres, selfoon, e-pos. **Moenie** jou ID-nommer insluit nie.\n2. **Education**: skool, graad, vakke.\n3. **Skills**: bv. tweetalig, rekenaarvaardig, goed met syfers.\n4. **Experience**: vorige werk of vrywillige werk.\n5. **Achievements**: bv. klasverteenwoordiger, sportspanne.\n6. **Interests**: stokperdjies.\n7. **References**: twee mense (bv. 'n onderwyser) met hul kontakbesonderhede, wat toestemming gegee het.\n\nDie **dekbrief** (*covering letter*) is 'n formele aansoekbrief wat saam met die CV gaan. Dit noem watter **pos** jy wil hê en **waar** jy die advertensie gesien het, **hoekom** jy geskik is, en dat jy beskikbaar is vir 'n **onderhoud**: *Please find my CV attached.*\n\n## Register\n\n| Informeel ✗ | Formeel ✓ |\n|---|---|\n| I'm / don't / can't | I am / do not / cannot |\n| Hey Sir | Dear Sir/Madam |\n| I wanna complain | I wish to complain |\n| super late | extremely late |\n| ASAP | as soon as possible |\n| Thanx a mil | Thank you very much |\n\n'n **Formele** brief is beleefd en saaklik: **geen** sametrekkings, slang, SMS-taal of uitroeptekens nie. 'n **Informele** brief mag sametrekkings gebruik en klink soos 'n gesprek.\n\n## Algemene foute\n\n- *Yours sincerely* ná *Dear Sir/Madam* (of andersom).\n- Die datum of onderwerpreël vergeet.\n- 'n Ontvanger se adres in 'n vriendskaplike brief.\n- Te lank of te kort: hou by **120–150** woorde vir die liggaam.\n- Sametrekkings en slang in 'n formele brief.\n- 'n Werklike ID-nommer in 'n CV.\n\n> **Onthou!** Formaat + register + duidelike paragrawe = die maklikste punte in Vraestel 3.","en":"## Where do letters fit in?\n\nLetters are **longer transactional texts** in **Paper 3, Section B** (30 marks). The **body** of the letter must be **120–150 words**; the addresses, date, salutation and closing are not counted. The marker looks at content, planning and **format**, and at language, style and editing, so a correct layout earns easy marks.\n\n## Kinds of formal letters\n\n- **Request**: you ask for information or permission.\n- **Complaint**: you describe a problem politely and ask for a solution.\n- **Application**: you apply for a post or bursary, together with a **CV**.\n- **Letter to the press**: you comment on an issue in a newspaper.\n- **Thank-you/business letter**.\n\n## Format of a formal letter\n\n1. **Sender's address** at the top right. Use a **made-up** address, e.g. *PO Box 512, Brits, 0250*.\n2. **Date** directly below the address, with the month in words: *21 October 2026*.\n3. **Recipient's title and address** on the left, below the date: *The Manager, …*\n4. **Salutation**: *Dear Sir/Madam* (name unknown) or *Dear Mr Mokoena* (name known).\n5. **Subject line** directly after the salutation: *RE: Broken streetlights in Mimosa Street*, or a bold/underlined heading.\n6. **Body** in paragraphs: **purpose** (why you are writing) → **details** (facts, examples) → **request/action** (what you want to happen).\n7. **Closing** with a comma.\n8. **Signature**, and below it your **initials and surname**: *K. Molefe*.\n\n| Salutation | Closing |\n|---|---|\n| Dear Sir/Madam | **Yours faithfully** |\n| Dear Mr Mokoena / Dear Ms Dlamini | **Yours sincerely** |\n| Dear Lerato (informal) | Love, / Regards, / Your friend, + first name |\n\n> **Tip:** *S*incerely goes with a *S*pecific name; *Faithfully* goes with *Sir/Madam*. Only the *Y* of *Yours* gets a capital letter.\n\n## Friendly (informal) letter\n\n- Only **your own address and the date** at the top right; **no** recipient's address.\n- Salutation: *Dear Lerato,* (with a comma).\n- Chatty and personal, but still **correct language**: no SMS language (*u, coz, thanx*).\n- End with *Love,* / *Regards,* / *Your friend,* + **only your first name**.\n\n## CV (curriculum vitae) and covering letter\n\nA **CV** is a short, neat summary of who you are. Use **headings** and information in point form:\n\n1. **Personal details**: name, address, cellphone, e-mail. **Do not** include your ID number.\n2. **Education**: school, grade, subjects.\n3. **Skills**: e.g. bilingual, computer literate, good with numbers.\n4. **Experience**: previous work or voluntary work.\n5. **Achievements**: e.g. class representative, sports teams.\n6. **Interests**: hobbies.\n7. **References**: two people (e.g. a teacher) with their contact details, who have given permission.\n\nThe **covering letter** is a formal letter of application that goes with the CV. It names the **post** you want and **where** you saw the advertisement, **why** you are suitable, and that you are available for an **interview**: *Please find my CV attached.*\n\n## Register\n\n| Informal ✗ | Formal ✓ |\n|---|---|\n| I'm / don't / can't | I am / do not / cannot |\n| Hey Sir | Dear Sir/Madam |\n| I wanna complain | I wish to complain |\n| super late | extremely late |\n| ASAP | as soon as possible |\n| Thanx a mil | Thank you very much |\n\nA **formal** letter is polite and businesslike: **no** contractions, slang, SMS language or exclamation marks. An **informal** letter may use contractions and sounds like a conversation.\n\n## Common mistakes\n\n- *Yours sincerely* after *Dear Sir/Madam* (or the other way round).\n- Forgetting the date or the subject line.\n- A recipient's address in a friendly letter.\n- Too long or too short: keep to **120–150** words for the body.\n- Contractions and slang in a formal letter.\n- A real ID number in a CV.\n\n> **Remember!** Format + register + clear paragraphs = the easiest marks in Paper 3."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Formele brief (formal letter)","en":"Formal letter"},"def":{"af":"'n Saaklike brief aan 'n onbekende persoon of organisasie, bv. 'n klagte, versoek of aansoek, met twee adresse en formele taal.","en":"A businesslike letter to an unknown person or organisation, e.g. a complaint, request or application, with two addresses and formal language."}},{"term":{"af":"Vriendskaplike/informele brief (friendly/informal letter)","en":"Friendly (informal) letter"},"def":{"af":"'n Persoonlike brief aan iemand wat jy ken, met net jou eie adres en die datum, en 'n kletserige maar korrekte styl.","en":"A personal letter to someone you know, with only your own address and the date, and a chatty but correct style."}},{"term":{"af":"Aanhef (salutation)","en":"Salutation"},"def":{"af":"Die groet aan die begin van die brief: *Dear Sir/Madam*, *Dear Mr Mokoena* of *Dear Lerato,*","en":"The greeting at the start of the letter: *Dear Sir/Madam*, *Dear Mr Mokoena* or *Dear Lerato,*"}},{"term":{"af":"Onderwerpreël (subject line)","en":"Subject line"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort opskrif ná die aanhef wat sê waaroor die brief gaan, bv. *RE: Application for the post of packer*.","en":"A short heading after the salutation that says what the letter is about, e.g. *RE: Application for the post of packer*."}},{"term":{"af":"Slot (closing)","en":"Closing"},"def":{"af":"Die afsluiting voor die handtekening: *Yours faithfully* (ná *Dear Sir/Madam*) of *Yours sincerely* (ná 'n naam).","en":"The ending before the signature: *Yours faithfully* (after *Dear Sir/Madam*) or *Yours sincerely* (after a name)."}},{"term":{"af":"Register","en":"Register"},"def":{"af":"Die vlak van formaliteit van jou taal, wat by die ontvanger en doel moet pas: formeel of informeel.","en":"The level of formality of your language, which must suit the recipient and purpose: formal or informal."}},{"term":{"af":"CV (curriculum vitae)","en":"CV (curriculum vitae)"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort opsomming van jou persoonlike besonderhede, opleiding, vaardighede, ervaring, prestasies, belangstellings en referente.","en":"A short summary of your personal details, education, skills, experience, achievements, interests and references."}},{"term":{"af":"Dekbrief (covering letter)","en":"Covering letter"},"def":{"af":"'n Formele aansoekbrief wat saam met jou CV gestuur word en die pos, jou geskiktheid en beskikbaarheid noem.","en":"A formal letter of application sent with your CV that names the post, your suitability and availability."}},{"term":{"af":"Referente (references/referees)","en":"References (referees)"},"def":{"af":"Mense, bv. 'n onderwyser, wat 'n werkgewer kan kontak om oor jou karakter en werk te getuig.","en":"People, e.g. a teacher, whom an employer can contact to vouch for your character and work."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"'n Formele klagtebrief","en":"A formal letter of complaint"},"problem":{"af":"Die straatligte en paaie naby jou skool in Brits is in 'n slegte toestand. Skryf 'n klagtebrief aan die Munisipale Bestuurder van die Madibeng Plaaslike Munisipaliteit. Die liggaam moet 120–150 woorde wees.","en":"The streetlights and roads near your school in Brits are in a bad condition. Write a letter of complaint to the Municipal Manager of the Madibeng Local Municipality. The body must be 120–150 words."},"steps":[{"af":"Formaat bo: jou versinde adres regs bo, die datum daaronder; dan links die ontvanger se titel en adres (*The Municipal Manager, Madibeng Local Municipality…*).","en":"Format at the top: your made-up address at the top right, the date below it; then on the left the recipient's title and address (*The Municipal Manager, Madibeng Local Municipality…*)."},{"af":"Naam onbekend → *Dear Sir/Madam*; onderwerpreël direk daarna: *RE: BROKEN STREETLIGHTS AND POTHOLES IN MIMOSA STREET*.","en":"Name unknown → *Dear Sir/Madam*; subject line directly after it: *RE: BROKEN STREETLIGHTS AND POTHOLES IN MIMOSA STREET*."},{"af":"Paragraaf 1 = doel (*I am writing to complain about…*). Paragraaf 2 = besonderhede (watter ligte, hoe lank, wat die gevaar is). Paragraaf 3 = versoek/aksie (*I would be grateful if…*).","en":"Paragraph 1 = purpose (*I am writing to complain about…*). Paragraph 2 = details (which lights, for how long, what the danger is). Paragraph 3 = request/action (*I would be grateful if…*)."},{"af":"Register: beleefd en formeel, geen sametrekkings nie (*I am*, nie *I'm* nie), geen uitroeptekens nie. Die liggaam hieronder is 126 woorde.","en":"Register: polite and formal, no contractions (*I am*, not *I'm*), no exclamation marks. The body below is 126 words."},{"af":"Slot: *Dear Sir/Madam* → *Yours faithfully*, dan handtekening en voorletters + van (*K. Molefe*).","en":"Closing: *Dear Sir/Madam* → *Yours faithfully*, then signature and initials + surname (*K. Molefe*)."}],"answer":{"af":"PO Box 512\nBrits\n0250\n21 October 2026\n\nThe Municipal Manager\nMadibeng Local Municipality\nBrits\n0250\n\nDear Sir/Madam\n\nRE: BROKEN STREETLIGHTS AND POTHOLES IN MIMOSA STREET\n\nI am writing to complain about the dangerous condition of Mimosa Street, the road that many learners use to walk to our school.\n\nFor the past two months, four of the streetlights in the street have not been working. As a result, learners who leave after evening study sessions have to walk home in the dark. In addition, the large potholes near the school gate have already damaged several cars, and taxis now swerve onto the pavement to avoid them. This puts pedestrians in serious danger.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if the municipality could repair the streetlights and fill the potholes as soon as possible. I am also willing to meet your officials to show them the problem areas. I look forward to your response.\n\nYours faithfully\n[signature]\nK. Molefe","en":"PO Box 512\nBrits\n0250\n21 October 2026\n\nThe Municipal Manager\nMadibeng Local Municipality\nBrits\n0250\n\nDear Sir/Madam\n\nRE: BROKEN STREETLIGHTS AND POTHOLES IN MIMOSA STREET\n\nI am writing to complain about the dangerous condition of Mimosa Street, the road that many learners use to walk to our school.\n\nFor the past two months, four of the streetlights in the street have not been working. As a result, learners who leave after evening study sessions have to walk home in the dark. In addition, the large potholes near the school gate have already damaged several cars, and taxis now swerve onto the pavement to avoid them. This puts pedestrians in serious danger.\n\nI would therefore be grateful if the municipality could repair the streetlights and fill the potholes as soon as possible. I am also willing to meet your officials to show them the problem areas. I look forward to your response.\n\nYours faithfully\n[signature]\nK. Molefe"}},{"title":{"af":"Herskryf in formele register","en":"Rewrite in formal register"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf hierdie sinne sodat hulle in 'n formele brief pas:\n(a) Hey Sir, I'm writing coz the taxi was super late again!!\n(b) Pls sort it out ASAP.\n(c) Thanx a mil for the awesome tour of the mine.","en":"Rewrite these sentences so that they fit in a formal letter:\n(a) Hey Sir, I'm writing coz the taxi was super late again!!\n(b) Pls sort it out ASAP.\n(c) Thanx a mil for the awesome tour of the mine."},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *Hey Sir* → *Dear Sir/Madam*; *I'm* → *I am*; *coz* → *because*; *super late* → *extremely late*; geen dubbele uitroepteken nie.","en":"(a) *Hey Sir* → *Dear Sir/Madam*; *I'm* → *I am*; *coz* → *because*; *super late* → *extremely late*; no double exclamation mark."},{"af":"(b) *Pls* → *Please*; *sort it out* (spreektaal) → *resolve the matter*; *ASAP* → *as soon as possible*.","en":"(b) *Pls* → *Please*; *sort it out* (colloquial) → *resolve the matter*; *ASAP* → *as soon as possible*."},{"af":"(c) *Thanx a mil* → *Thank you very much*; *awesome* (slang) → *excellent* of *informative*.","en":"(c) *Thanx a mil* → *Thank you very much*; *awesome* (slang) → *excellent* or *informative*."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing because the taxi was extremely late again. (b) Please resolve the matter as soon as possible. (c) Thank you very much for the excellent tour of the mine.","en":"(a) Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing because the taxi was extremely late again. (b) Please resolve the matter as soon as possible. (c) Thank you very much for the excellent tour of the mine."}},{"title":{"af":"Vind die formaatfoute","en":"Find the format errors"},"problem":{"af":"Thabo doen aansoek om 'n vakansiewerk by 'n supermark. Identifiseer VYF foute in sy brief.\n\nDear Mr Mokoena\n\nI want the job at your shop. I'm really good with people and I need the cash for the holidays!!\n\nYours faithfully\nThabo","en":"Thabo is applying for a holiday job at a supermarket. Identify FIVE errors in his letter.\n\nDear Mr Mokoena\n\nI want the job at your shop. I'm really good with people and I need the cash for the holidays!!\n\nYours faithfully\nThabo"},"steps":[{"af":"Bo-aan ontbreek **sy adres en die datum** (regs bo) en die **ontvanger se adres** (links).","en":"At the top, **his address and the date** (top right) and the **recipient's address** (left) are missing."},{"af":"Daar is **geen onderwerpreël** nie, bv. *RE: Application for the post of packer*.","en":"There is **no subject line**, e.g. *RE: Application for the post of packer*."},{"af":"Die **register** is te informeel: *I want the job*, *I'm*, *the cash* en *!!* → *I wish to apply for the post of packer…*, *I am*, geen uitroeptekens nie.","en":"The **register** is too informal: *I want the job*, *I'm*, *the cash* and *!!* → *I wish to apply for the post of packer…*, *I am*, no exclamation marks."},{"af":"Die aanhef het 'n naam (*Dear Mr Mokoena*), dus moet die slot **Yours sincerely** wees, nie *Yours faithfully* nie.","en":"The salutation has a name (*Dear Mr Mokoena*), so the closing must be **Yours sincerely**, not *Yours faithfully*."},{"af":"Hy teken net met sy voornaam; 'n formele brief eindig met handtekening + **voorletters en van** (bv. *T. Nkosi*). Die liggaam is ook veels te kort vir 120–150 woorde.","en":"He signs with his first name only; a formal letter ends with a signature + **initials and surname** (e.g. *T. Nkosi*). The body is also far too short for 120–150 words."}],"answer":{"af":"1. No sender's address/date and no recipient's address. 2. No subject line. 3. Informal register (I'm, the cash, !!). 4. \"Yours faithfully\" must be \"Yours sincerely\". 5. First name only instead of signature + initials and surname (and the body is too short).","en":"1. No sender's address/date and no recipient's address. 2. No subject line. 3. Informal register (I'm, the cash, !!). 4. \"Yours faithfully\" must be \"Yours sincerely\". 5. First name only instead of signature + initials and surname (and the body is too short)."}},{"title":{"af":"'n CV vir 'n vakansiewerk","en":"A CV for a holiday job"},"problem":{"af":"Pieter (Gr 10, Hoërskool Brits) wil aansoek doen om 'n vakansiewerk as pakker by 'n supermark in Brits. Stel sy CV op en noem wat in sy dekbrief moet staan.","en":"Pieter (Gr 10, Hoërskool Brits) wants to apply for a holiday job as a packer at a supermarket in Brits. Draw up his CV and say what must go into his covering letter."},"steps":[{"af":"Gebruik duidelike **opskrifte** in hierdie volgorde: Personal details → Education → Skills → Experience → Achievements → Interests → References.","en":"Use clear **headings** in this order: Personal details → Education → Skills → Experience → Achievements → Interests → References."},{"af":"Persoonlike besonderhede: naam, adres, selfoon en e-pos, maar **geen ID-nommer** nie (dit beskerm jou teen identiteitsdiefstal).","en":"Personal details: name, address, cellphone and e-mail, but **no ID number** (this protects you against identity theft)."},{"af":"Kies vaardighede en ervaring wat by die werk pas: tweetalig, goed met geld, vrywilliger by die snoepie.","en":"Choose skills and experience that suit the job: bilingual, good with money, volunteer at the tuck shop."},{"af":"Gee 'n referent (bv. sy klasonderwyser) met kontakbesonderhede, nadat hy toestemming gevra het.","en":"Give a referee (e.g. his class teacher) with contact details, after asking permission."},{"af":"Dekbrief (formele formaat): watter pos en waar hy die advertensie gesien het, hoekom hy geskik is, dat hy beskikbaar is vir 'n onderhoud, en *Please find my CV attached.*","en":"Covering letter (formal format): which post and where he saw the advertisement, why he is suitable, that he is available for an interview, and *Please find my CV attached.*"}],"answer":{"af":"CURRICULUM VITAE: PIETER NEL\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nName: Pieter Nel\nAddress: PO Box 512, Brits, 0250\nCellphone: 0XX XXX XXXX\nE-mail: pieter.nel@example.com\n\nEDUCATION\nHoërskool Brits, Grade 10 (2026)\nSubjects include English FAL, Afrikaans HL and Mathematics\n\nSKILLS\n- Bilingual (Afrikaans and English)\n- Good with numbers and money\n- Basic computer skills\n\nEXPERIENCE\nVolunteer at the school tuck shop (2025–2026)\n\nACHIEVEMENTS\nClass representative (2026)\n\nINTERESTS\nRugby, cycling, reading\n\nREFERENCES\nMrs A. Pretorius, Grade 10 class teacher, Hoërskool Brits, Tel: 0XX XXX XXXX","en":"CURRICULUM VITAE: PIETER NEL\n\nPERSONAL DETAILS\nName: Pieter Nel\nAddress: PO Box 512, Brits, 0250\nCellphone: 0XX XXX XXXX\nE-mail: pieter.nel@example.com\n\nEDUCATION\nHoërskool Brits, Grade 10 (2026)\nSubjects include English FAL, Afrikaans HL and Mathematics\n\nSKILLS\n- Bilingual (Afrikaans and English)\n- Good with numbers and money\n- Basic computer skills\n\nEXPERIENCE\nVolunteer at the school tuck shop (2025–2026)\n\nACHIEVEMENTS\nClass representative (2026)\n\nINTERESTS\nRugby, cycling, reading\n\nREFERENCES\nMrs A. Pretorius, Grade 10 class teacher, Hoërskool Brits, Tel: 0XX XXX XXXX"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Waar skryf jy die afsender se adres in 'n formele brief?","en":"Where do you write the sender's address in a formal letter?"},"options":[{"af":"Links bo","en":"Top left"},{"af":"Regs bo","en":"Top right"},{"af":"Regs onder, ná die slot","en":"Bottom right, after the closing"},{"af":"In die middel bo","en":"Top centre"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die afsender (jy) se adres staan regs bo, met die datum reg daaronder. Die ontvanger se adres staan links.","en":"The sender's (your) address goes at the top right, with the date directly below it. The recipient's address goes on the left."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Brief wat met *Dear Sir/Madam* begin, eindig met *Yours ___*.","en":"A letter that starts with *Dear Sir/Madam* ends with *Yours ___*."},"answers":{"af":["faithfully"],"en":["faithfully"]},"explain":{"af":"*Sir/Madam* → *faithfully*. *Sincerely* gebruik jy wanneer jy die persoon se naam in die aanhef skryf.","en":"*Sir/Madam* → *faithfully*. You use *sincerely* when you write the person's name in the salutation."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["sincerely","truly","lovingly"],"en":["sincerely","truly","lovingly"]}}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? 'n Vriendskaplike brief bevat die ontvanger se adres aan die linkerkant.","en":"True or false? A friendly letter includes the recipient's address on the left."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n Vriendskaplike brief het net jou eie adres en die datum regs bo. Twee adresse is vir formele briewe.","en":"False. A friendly letter has only your own address and the date at the top right. Two addresses are for formal letters."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die formele brief wat jy saam met jou CV stuur wanneer jy om 'n werk aansoek doen, is 'n ___ letter (dekbrief).","en":"The formal letter you send with your CV when you apply for a job is a ___ letter."},"answers":{"af":["covering","cover"],"en":["covering","cover"]},"explain":{"af":"Die *covering letter* (dekbrief) stel jou voor, noem die pos en verwys na die aangehegte CV.","en":"The *covering letter* introduces you, names the post and refers to the attached CV."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["thank-you","complaint","friendly"],"en":["thank-you","complaint","friendly"]}}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van 'n formele brief by sy regte posisie.","en":"Match each part of a formal letter to its correct position."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Afsender se adres","en":"Sender's address"},"r":{"af":"Regs bo","en":"Top right"}},{"l":{"af":"Datum","en":"Date"},"r":{"af":"Direk onder die afsender se adres","en":"Directly below the sender's address"}},{"l":{"af":"Ontvanger se adres","en":"Recipient's address"},"r":{"af":"Links, onder die datum","en":"On the left, below the date"}},{"l":{"af":"Onderwerpreël","en":"Subject line"},"r":{"af":"Direk ná die aanhef","en":"Directly after the salutation"}}],"explain":{"af":"Die uitleg van bo na onder: jou adres en datum regs, die ontvanger links, die aanhef, die onderwerpreël en dan die liggaam.","en":"The layout from top to bottom: your address and date on the right, the recipient on the left, the salutation, the subject line and then the body."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter slot is korrek vir 'n brief wat begin met *Dear Ms Dlamini*?","en":"Which closing is correct for a letter that starts with *Dear Ms Dlamini*?"},"options":[{"af":"Yours faithfully","en":"Yours faithfully"},{"af":"Lots of love","en":"Lots of love"},{"af":"Yours sincerely","en":"Yours sincerely"},{"af":"Yours lovingly","en":"Yours lovingly"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Spesifieke naam in die aanhef → *Yours sincerely*. *Yours faithfully* is vir *Dear Sir/Madam*, en die ander twee is informeel.","en":"A specific name in the salutation → *Yours sincerely*. *Yours faithfully* is for *Dear Sir/Madam*, and the other two are informal."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Waar of onwaar? In 'n formele brief moet jy sametrekkings soos *don't* en *I'm* vermy.","en":"True or false? In a formal letter you should avoid contractions such as *don't* and *I'm*."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Formele register gebruik die volle vorme: *do not*, *I am*.","en":"True. Formal register uses the full forms: *do not*, *I am*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die mees gepaste onderwerpreël vir 'n klagtebrief oor slaggate?","en":"Which one is the most suitable subject line for a letter of complaint about potholes?"},"options":[{"af":"RE: Letter","en":"RE: Letter"},{"af":"RE: I am very angry","en":"RE: I am very angry"},{"af":"Hi there, the roads!!","en":"Hi there, the roads!!"},{"af":"RE: Dangerous potholes in Mimosa Street","en":"RE: Dangerous potholes in Mimosa Street"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie onderwerpreël is kort, saaklik en spesifiek: dit sê presies waaroor die brief gaan. Die ander is vaag, emosioneel of informeel.","en":"A good subject line is short, businesslike and specific: it says exactly what the letter is about. The others are vague, emotional or informal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Herskryf formeel: *I'm writing to complain.* → *I ___ writing to complain.*","en":"Rewrite formally: *I'm writing to complain.* → *I ___ writing to complain.*"},"answers":{"af":["am"],"en":["am"]},"explain":{"af":"Die sametrekking *I'm* word in formele register *I am*.","en":"The contraction *I'm* becomes *I am* in formal register."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["are","is","was"],"en":["are","is","was"]}}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Herskryf formeel: *We need the documents ASAP.* → *We need the documents as soon as ___.*","en":"Rewrite formally: *We need the documents ASAP.* → *We need the documents as soon as ___.*"},"answers":{"af":["possible"],"en":["possible"]},"explain":{"af":"*ASAP* is 'n afkorting wat in formele briewe uitgeskryf word: *as soon as possible*.","en":"*ASAP* is an abbreviation that is written out in formal letters: *as soon as possible*."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["possibly","possibility","now"],"en":["possibly","possibility","now"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter inligting moet NIE in 'n CV wees nie?","en":"Which information should NOT be in a CV?"},"options":[{"af":"Jou ID-nommer","en":"Your ID number"},{"af":"Jou kontakbesonderhede","en":"Your contact details"},{"af":"Jou opleiding","en":"Your education"},{"af":"Referente","en":"References"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Jou ID-nommer is sensitiewe inligting wat misbruik kan word; dit hoort nie in 'n CV nie. Kontakbesonderhede, opleiding en referente is noodsaaklik.","en":"Your ID number is sensitive information that can be misused; it does not belong in a CV. Contact details, education and references are essential."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In 'n CV word mense wat vir jou kan instaan (bv. 'n onderwyser) onder die opskrif ___ gelys.","en":"In a CV, people who can vouch for you (e.g. a teacher) are listed under the heading ___."},"answers":{"af":["references","referees","referente"],"en":["references","referees"]},"explain":{"af":"*References* (referente) is mense wat 'n werkgewer kan skakel om oor jou te getuig. Vra altyd eers hul toestemming.","en":"*References* (referees) are people an employer can contact to vouch for you. Always ask their permission first."},"choices":{"d":{"af":["achievements","interests","skills"],"en":["achievements","interests","skills"]}}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin pas die beste in 'n aansoekbrief?","en":"Which sentence fits best in a letter of application?"},"options":[{"af":"I reckon I'd be awesome at this job.","en":"I reckon I'd be awesome at this job."},{"af":"I believe that my good communication skills make me suitable for this post.","en":"I believe that my good communication skills make me suitable for this post."},{"af":"Pls give me the job, I really need the money.","en":"Pls give me the job, I really need the money."},{"af":"Hire me or you will be sorry!","en":"Hire me or you will be sorry!"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die tweede sin is formeel, beleefd en noem 'n konkrete vaardigheid. Die ander gebruik slang, SMS-taal of 'n onbeleefde toon.","en":"The second sentence is formal, polite and names a concrete skill. The others use slang, SMS language or a rude tone."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Brief begin met *Dear Sir/Madam* en eindig met *Yours sincerely, T. Nkosi*. Wat is fout?","en":"A letter starts with *Dear Sir/Madam* and ends with *Yours sincerely, T. Nkosi*. What is wrong?"},"options":[{"af":"Die slot moet *Yours faithfully* wees","en":"The closing should be *Yours faithfully*"},{"af":"Hy moet net sy voornaam gebruik","en":"He should use only his first name"},{"af":"Die aanhef moet *Hi Sir* wees","en":"The salutation should be *Hi Sir*"},{"af":"Niks; dit is korrek","en":"Nothing; it is correct"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*Dear Sir/Madam* (geen naam) → *Yours faithfully*. Voorletters en van (*T. Nkosi*) is korrek vir 'n formele brief.","en":"*Dear Sir/Madam* (no name) → *Yours faithfully*. Initials and surname (*T. Nkosi*) are correct for a formal letter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die beste volgorde vir die liggaam van 'n klagtebrief?","en":"What is the best order for the body of a letter of complaint?"},"options":[{"af":"Versoek/aksie → besonderhede → doel","en":"Request/action → details → purpose"},{"af":"Besonderhede → doel → versoek/aksie","en":"Details → purpose → request/action"},{"af":"Doel → besonderhede → versoek/aksie","en":"Purpose → details → request/action"},{"af":"Doel → versoek/aksie → groete aan die familie","en":"Purpose → request/action → greetings to the family"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Sê eers hoekom jy skryf, gee dan die feite van die probleem, en sluit af met wat jy wil hê moet gebeur. Groete aan die familie hoort in 'n vriendskaplike brief.","en":"First say why you are writing, then give the facts of the problem, and end with what you want to happen. Greetings to the family belong in a friendly letter."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die straatligte voor jou skool in Brits werk al maande lank nie. Watter brief is die MEES geskik om die probleem opgelos te kry?","en":"The streetlights in front of your school in Brits have not worked for months. Which letter is the MOST suitable to get the problem solved?"},"options":[{"af":"'n Vriendskaplike brief aan jou neef in Pretoria","en":"A friendly letter to your cousin in Pretoria"},{"af":"'n Formele klagtebrief aan die Munisipale Bestuurder van Madibeng","en":"A formal letter of complaint to the Municipal Manager of Madibeng"},{"af":"'n Bedankingsbrief aan die redakteur van 'n koerant","en":"A thank-you letter to the editor of a newspaper"},{"af":"'n Informele brief vol slang aan die burgemeester","en":"An informal letter full of slang to the mayor"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Die munisipaliteit is verantwoordelik vir straatligte, dus is 'n formele klagtebrief aan die regte amptenaar die doeltreffendste. Die ander het die verkeerde ontvanger, doel of register.","en":"The municipality is responsible for streetlights, so a formal letter of complaint to the right official is the most effective. The others have the wrong recipient, purpose or register."}}]}]},{"term":3,"title":{"af":"Poësie, visuele geletterdheid, sinsbou en transaksionele tekste","en":"Poetry, visual literacy, sentence structure and transactional texts"},"topics":[{"id":"eng10-t3-poetry","title":{"af":"Poësie","en":"Poetry"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal 'n ongesiene gedig kan ontleed – spreker, tema, toon, struktuur, rym en stylfigure – en jou antwoorde met aanhalings kan staaf.","en":"You will be able to analyse an unseen poem – speaker, theme, tone, structure, rhyme and figures of speech – and support your answers with quotations."},"summary":{"af":"## Spreker, onderwerp en tema\n\n- Die **poet** (digter) skryf die gedig; die **speaker** (spreker) is die stem wat in die gedig praat. Hulle is nie noodwendig dieselfde persoon nie: 'n digter van 50 kan as 'n kind van 8 praat. Skryf dus *\"the speaker\"*, nie *\"the poet says\"* nie, as jy oor die *I* in die gedig praat.\n- Die **addressee** (aangesprokene) is die persoon of ding met wie die spreker praat (*you*, 'n ma, die maan).\n- Die **title** (titel) gee dikwels 'n leidraad oor die onderwerp, tema of 'n simbool. Lees dit altyd eerste.\n- Die **subject** (onderwerp) is *waaroor* die gedig gaan (bv. 'n oupa se hande). Die **theme** (tema) is die *boodskap of insig oor die lewe* (bv. *harde werk en liefde laat 'n blywende spoor, al word ons oud*). Skryf 'n tema altyd as 'n volsin.\n\n## Toon en stemming\n\n- **Tone** (toon) is die spreker se **houding** teenoor die onderwerp. Jy lei dit af uit woordkeuse en leestekens: *bitter, nostalgic* (terugverlangend), *sarcastic, hopeful, admiring, angry, sombre, mocking, reflective*.\n- **Mood** (stemming) is die **atmosfeer of gevoel wat by die leser** geskep word: *gloomy, peaceful, tense, joyful*.\n- Toon kan verander. Soek die **turning point** (wendingspunt), dikwels by *but, yet, now* of 'n nuwe strofe.\n\n> **Wenk:** Gee een woord vir die toon én 'n aanhaling wat dit bewys, bv. *The tone is bitter: \"they took everything and called it progress\".*\n\n## Struktuur en vorm\n\n| Strofe (stanza) | Reëls |\n|---|---|\n| couplet | 2 |\n| tercet | 3 |\n| quatrain | 4 |\n| sestet | 6 |\n| octave | 8 |\n\n- 'n **Line** (versreël) is een reël; 'n **stanza** (strofe) is 'n groep reëls.\n- **Free verse** (vrye vers): geen vaste rymskema of ritme nie; dit klink soos natuurlike spraak.\n- **Petrarchan sonnet:** 14 reëls = **octave** (8 reëls, *abbaabba*) + **sestet** (6 reëls, bv. *cdecde*). Die **volta** (wending) kom by reël 9: die probleem van die octave word in die sestet beantwoord of verander.\n- **Shakespearean sonnet:** 14 reëls = **drie quatrains + 'n rymende couplet** (*abab cdcd efef gg*). Die volta kom gewoonlik by reël 13; die couplet gee 'n slotsom of 'n verrassing.\n- **Ballad:** vertel 'n storie, gewoonlik in quatrains (dikwels *abcb*), met eenvoudige taal, dialoog en 'n **refrain**.\n\n## Rym, ritme en klank\n\n- **End rhyme** (eindrym): die eindwoorde rym. **Internal rhyme** (binnerym): rym binne een reël, bv. *the night was bright above the dam*.\n- **Rhyme scheme** (rymskema): elke nuwe eindklank kry 'n nuwe letter: **aabb** (paarrym), **abab** (kruisrym), **abba** (omarmende rym).\n- **Rhythm** (ritme): die patroon van beklemtoonde en onbeklemtoonde lettergrepe. 'n Vinnige ritme pas by opwinding, 'n stadige ritme by hartseer.\n- **Enjambment** (enjambement): die sin loop sonder 'n leesteken oor na die volgende reël. Effek: vloei, spoed of spanning, of dit boots die betekenis na (iets wat aanhou beweeg). 'n **End-stopped line** eindig met 'n leesteken en dwing 'n pouse af.\n- **Repetition** (herhaling) beklemtoon 'n idee; 'n **refrain** is 'n reël of strofe wat gereeld herhaal word, soos 'n koor.\n- **Alliteration** (alliterasie): herhaalde beginkonsonante, bv. *wheat and wind and wagons*. **Assonance** (assonansie): herhaalde klinkerklanke, bv. *I lie awake and hate the rain*. **Onomatopoeia** (klanknabootsing): *tap, hiss, crash*.\n\n## Stylfigure (figures of speech)\n\n| Term | Wat dit doen | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Simile | vergelyk met *like/as* | *rough as sandpaper* |\n| Metaphor | sê een ding IS 'n ander | *His hands are maps.* |\n| Personification | gee 'n ding menslike eienskappe | *The wind whispered.* |\n| Hyperbole | doelbewuste oordrywing | *I've told you a million times.* |\n| Antithesis/contrast | teenoorgestelde idees naas mekaar | *Some build walls; others build bridges.* |\n| Irony | die teenoorgestelde van wat verwag of bedoel word | 'n brandweerstasie wat afbrand |\n| Oxymoron | twee teenstrydige **woorde** saam | *deafening silence* |\n| Paradox | 'n **stelling** wat teenstrydig lyk, maar waar is | *The more I learn, the less I know.* |\n| Symbol | 'n ding wat 'n groter idee verteenwoordig | 'n kers = hoop |\n| Rhetorical question | 'n vraag vir effek; geen antwoord verwag nie | *Who will hold the light?* |\n| Euphemism | 'n sagte woord vir iets onaangenaams | *passed away* = died |\n\n**Imagery** (beelde): woorde wat 'n prentjie vir die sintuie skep: **visual** (sien), **auditory** (hoor), **tactile** (voel), en ook reuk en smaak.\n\n**Leestekens en tipografie:** 'n **dash** (aandagstreep) skep 'n skielike pouse of skuif; 'n **ellipsis** (…) wys iets wat wegraak, onuitgesê bly of tyd wat verbygaan; **capitals** (hoofletters) beklemtoon of wys skreeu; **italics** (kursief) beklemtoon of wys 'n ander stem.\n\n## Metode vir 'n ongesiene gedig\n\n1. Lees die gedig **twee keer**: een keer vir die gevoel, een keer stadig.\n2. Vra: **wie** praat, met **wie**, **waaroor**? Wat sê die titel?\n3. Formuleer die **tema** in een sin.\n4. Soek die stylfigure: noem dit, sê **wat met wat vergelyk word** en wat die **effek** is.\n5. Bepaal die **toon** en waar dit **verander**.\n6. Kyk na struktuur: strofes, rym, enjambement en leestekens.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *\"It is a metaphor.\"* kry net 1 uit 3 punte. Noem die term (1), verduidelik die vergelyking (1) en gee die effek of betekenis (1).\n\n> **Onthou!** As jy moet aanhaal, gee presies wat gevra word (een woord = een woord) in aanhalingstekens. Vir 'n paragraafvraag (4–6 punte): noem die tema, bespreek twee of drie tegnieke met aanhalings en wys hoe elkeen die tema oordra.","en":"## Speaker, subject and theme\n\n- The **poet** writes the poem; the **speaker** is the voice that speaks in the poem. They are not necessarily the same person: a poet of 50 can speak as a child of 8. So write *\"the speaker\"*, not *\"the poet says\"*, when you discuss the *I* in the poem.\n- The **addressee** is the person or thing the speaker is talking to (*you*, a mother, the moon).\n- The **title** often gives a clue about the subject, theme or a symbol. Always read it first.\n- The **subject** is *what* the poem is about (e.g. a grandfather's hands). The **theme** is the *message or insight about life* (e.g. *hard work and love leave a lasting mark, even when we grow old*). Always write a theme as a full sentence.\n\n## Tone and mood\n\n- **Tone** is the speaker's **attitude** towards the subject. You work it out from word choice and punctuation: *bitter, nostalgic, sarcastic, hopeful, admiring, angry, sombre, mocking, reflective*.\n- **Mood** is the **atmosphere or feeling created in the reader**: *gloomy, peaceful, tense, joyful*.\n- Tone can change. Look for the **turning point**, often at *but, yet, now* or a new stanza.\n\n> **Tip:** Give one word for the tone and a quotation that proves it, e.g. *The tone is bitter: \"they took everything and called it progress\".*\n\n## Structure and form\n\n| Stanza | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| couplet | 2 |\n| tercet | 3 |\n| quatrain | 4 |\n| sestet | 6 |\n| octave | 8 |\n\n- A **line** is one row of the poem; a **stanza** is a group of lines.\n- **Free verse:** no fixed rhyme scheme or rhythm; it sounds like natural speech.\n- **Petrarchan sonnet:** 14 lines = **octave** (8 lines, *abbaabba*) + **sestet** (6 lines, e.g. *cdecde*). The **volta** (turn) comes at line 9: the problem in the octave is answered or changed in the sestet.\n- **Shakespearean sonnet:** 14 lines = **three quatrains + a rhyming couplet** (*abab cdcd efef gg*). The volta usually comes at line 13; the couplet gives a conclusion or a surprise.\n- **Ballad:** tells a story, usually in quatrains (often *abcb*), with simple language, dialogue and a **refrain**.\n\n## Rhyme, rhythm and sound\n\n- **End rhyme:** the last words of lines rhyme. **Internal rhyme:** rhyme within one line, e.g. *the night was bright above the dam*.\n- **Rhyme scheme:** every new end sound gets a new letter: **aabb** (rhyming couplets), **abab** (alternate rhyme), **abba** (enclosed rhyme).\n- **Rhythm:** the pattern of stressed and unstressed syllables. A fast rhythm suits excitement, a slow rhythm suits sadness.\n- **Enjambment:** the sentence runs on to the next line without a punctuation mark. Effect: flow, speed or tension, or it imitates the meaning (something that keeps moving). An **end-stopped line** ends with a punctuation mark and forces a pause.\n- **Repetition** emphasises an idea; a **refrain** is a line or stanza repeated regularly, like a chorus.\n- **Alliteration:** repeated initial consonants, e.g. *wheat and wind and wagons*. **Assonance:** repeated vowel sounds, e.g. *I lie awake and hate the rain*. **Onomatopoeia:** *tap, hiss, crash*.\n\n## Figures of speech\n\n| Term | What it does | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Simile | compares using *like/as* | *rough as sandpaper* |\n| Metaphor | says one thing IS another | *His hands are maps.* |\n| Personification | gives a thing human qualities | *The wind whispered.* |\n| Hyperbole | deliberate exaggeration | *I've told you a million times.* |\n| Antithesis/contrast | opposite ideas placed side by side | *Some build walls; others build bridges.* |\n| Irony | the opposite of what is expected or meant | a fire station that burns down |\n| Oxymoron | two contradictory **words** together | *deafening silence* |\n| Paradox | a **statement** that seems contradictory but is true | *The more I learn, the less I know.* |\n| Symbol | a thing that stands for a bigger idea | a candle = hope |\n| Rhetorical question | a question for effect; no answer expected | *Who will hold the light?* |\n| Euphemism | a mild word for something unpleasant | *passed away* = died |\n\n**Imagery:** words that create a picture for the senses: **visual** (sight), **auditory** (sound), **tactile** (touch), as well as smell and taste.\n\n**Punctuation and typography:** a **dash** creates a sudden pause or shift; an **ellipsis** (…) shows something fading away, left unsaid or time passing; **capitals** emphasise or show shouting; **italics** emphasise or show a different voice.\n\n## Method for an unseen poem\n\n1. Read the poem **twice**: once for the feeling, once slowly.\n2. Ask: **who** is speaking, to **whom**, about **what**? What does the title say?\n3. Formulate the **theme** in one sentence.\n4. Find the figures of speech: name them, say **what is compared with what** and what the **effect** is.\n5. Decide on the **tone** and where it **changes**.\n6. Look at structure: stanzas, rhyme, enjambment and punctuation.\n\n> **Common mistake:** *\"It is a metaphor.\"* earns only 1 out of 3 marks. Name the term (1), explain the comparison (1) and give the effect or meaning (1).\n\n> **Remember!** When you must quote, give exactly what is asked (one word = one word) in inverted commas. For a paragraph question (4–6 marks): state the theme, discuss two or three techniques with quotations and show how each one conveys the theme."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Speaker (spreker)","en":"Speaker"},"def":{"af":"Die stem wat in die gedig praat; dit is nie noodwendig die digter self nie.","en":"The voice that speaks in the poem; it is not necessarily the poet."}},{"term":{"af":"Theme (tema)","en":"Theme"},"def":{"af":"Die boodskap of insig oor die lewe wat die gedig oordra – nie net die onderwerp nie.","en":"The message or insight about life that the poem conveys – not just the subject."}},{"term":{"af":"Tone (toon)","en":"Tone"},"def":{"af":"Die spreker se houding teenoor die onderwerp, bv. bitter, nostalgic of hopeful, wat uit die woordkeuse blyk.","en":"The speaker's attitude towards the subject, e.g. bitter, nostalgic or hopeful, shown by word choice."}},{"term":{"af":"Mood (stemming)","en":"Mood"},"def":{"af":"Die atmosfeer of gevoel wat die gedig by die leser skep.","en":"The atmosphere or feeling that the poem creates in the reader."}},{"term":{"af":"Rhyme scheme (rymskema)","en":"Rhyme scheme"},"def":{"af":"Die patroon van eindrym, aangedui met letters soos aabb, abab of abba.","en":"The pattern of end rhyme, shown with letters such as aabb, abab or abba."}},{"term":{"af":"Enjambment (enjambement)","en":"Enjambment"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n sin sonder 'n leesteken van een versreël na die volgende oorloop.","en":"When a sentence runs on from one line to the next without a punctuation mark."}},{"term":{"af":"Volta (wending)","en":"Volta (turn)"},"def":{"af":"Die punt in 'n sonnet waar die gedagte of toon verander: reël 9 in 'n Petrarchan-sonnet, gewoonlik reël 13 in 'n Shakespearean-sonnet.","en":"The point in a sonnet where the thought or tone changes: line 9 in a Petrarchan sonnet, usually line 13 in a Shakespearean sonnet."}},{"term":{"af":"Figure of speech (stylfiguur)","en":"Figure of speech"},"def":{"af":"Taal wat nie letterlik bedoel is nie en 'n spesiale effek skep, bv. simile, metaphor of personification.","en":"Language that is not meant literally and creates a special effect, e.g. simile, metaphor or personification."}},{"term":{"af":"Imagery (beelde)","en":"Imagery"},"def":{"af":"Beskrywende taal wat 'n beeld vir die sintuie skep: visueel, ouditief, tasbaar, reuk of smaak.","en":"Descriptive language that creates a picture for the senses: visual, auditory, tactile, smell or taste."}},{"term":{"af":"Free verse (vrye vers)","en":"Free verse"},"def":{"af":"Poësie sonder 'n vaste rymskema of gereelde ritme; dit klink soos natuurlike spraak.","en":"Poetry without a fixed rhyme scheme or regular rhythm; it sounds like natural speech."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Stylfigure identifiseer en verduidelik","en":"Identifying and explaining figures of speech"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die gedig en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Grandfather's Hands*\n\n1  His hands are maps of the mines near Brits,\n2  every scar a road he travelled underground,\n3  every crack a shift that started in the dark\n4  and ended in the dark.\n\n5  Those hands once lifted me above the orange trees\n6  so I could pick the sun itself;\n7  they were rough as sandpaper,\n8  gentle as rain on a tin roof.\n\n9  Now they tremble on the blanket,\n10  thin as paper, pale as dust –\n11  tap, tap, tap against the bed\n12  like a clock that is running down…\n\n13  Who will lift the children now?\n14  Who will hold the light?\n\n(a) Identify the figure of speech in line 1 and explain it. (3)\n(b) Name the sound device in line 11 and say why it is effective. (2)","en":"Read the poem and answer the questions.\n\n*Grandfather's Hands*\n\n1  His hands are maps of the mines near Brits,\n2  every scar a road he travelled underground,\n3  every crack a shift that started in the dark\n4  and ended in the dark.\n\n5  Those hands once lifted me above the orange trees\n6  so I could pick the sun itself;\n7  they were rough as sandpaper,\n8  gentle as rain on a tin roof.\n\n9  Now they tremble on the blanket,\n10  thin as paper, pale as dust –\n11  tap, tap, tap against the bed\n12  like a clock that is running down…\n\n13  Who will lift the children now?\n14  Who will hold the light?\n\n(a) Identify the figure of speech in line 1 and explain it. (3)\n(b) Name the sound device in line 11 and say why it is effective. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Reël 1: *\"His hands are maps of the mines near Brits\"*. Daar is geen *like* of *as* nie; die hande **is** kaarte. Dit is dus 'n **metaphor** (1 punt).","en":"(a) Line 1: *\"His hands are maps of the mines near Brits\"*. There is no *like* or *as*; the hands **are** maps. So it is a **metaphor** (1 mark)."},{"af":"Sê wat met wat vergelyk word: die letsels en lyne op oupa se hande word met die paaie op 'n kaart vergelyk (1 punt). Reël 2 bevestig dit: *\"every scar a road\"*.","en":"Say what is compared with what: the scars and lines on Grandfather's hands are compared to the roads on a map (1 mark). Line 2 confirms this: *\"every scar a road\"*."},{"af":"Gee die effek: soos 'n kaart 'n reis wys, wys sy hande die verhaal van sy lewe – jare van harde, gevaarlike werk ondergronds in die myne (1 punt).","en":"Give the effect: just as a map shows a journey, his hands show the story of his life – years of hard, dangerous work underground in the mines (1 mark)."},{"af":"(b) *\"tap, tap, tap\"* boots die geluid van sy bewende vingers teen die bed na: **onomatopoeia** (1 punt). Effek: ons *hoor* hoe swak en rusteloos hy is, en die herhaling klink soos 'n tikkende horlosie wat ons voorberei op reël 12 – sy tyd raak min (1 punt).","en":"(b) *\"tap, tap, tap\"* imitates the sound of his trembling fingers against the bed: **onomatopoeia** (1 mark). Effect: we *hear* how weak and restless he is, and the repetition sounds like a ticking clock, preparing us for line 12 – his time is running out (1 mark)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Metaphor: the scars and lines on his hands are compared to roads on a map; like a map, his hands record the story of his long, hard life in the mines. (b) Onomatopoeia: \"tap, tap, tap\" lets us hear his weak, trembling fingers, and it sounds like a ticking clock, suggesting that his life is running out.","en":"(a) Metaphor: the scars and lines on his hands are compared to roads on a map; like a map, his hands record the story of his long, hard life in the mines. (b) Onomatopoeia: \"tap, tap, tap\" lets us hear his weak, trembling fingers, and it sounds like a ticking clock, suggesting that his life is running out."}},{"title":{"af":"Enjambement, wendingspunt en vrye vers","en":"Enjambment, turning point and free verse"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys weer na *Grandfather's Hands* (voorbeeld 1).\n\n(a) Why is enjambment used in lines 3–4? (2)\n(b) Which word in stanza 3 marks the turning point? How does the tone change? (3)\n(c) Is the poem written in free verse? Give a reason. (2)","en":"Refer to *Grandfather's Hands* again (example 1).\n\n(a) Why is enjambment used in lines 3–4? (2)\n(b) Which word in stanza 3 marks the turning point? How does the tone change? (3)\n(c) Is the poem written in free verse? Give a reason. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Reël 3 eindig sonder 'n leesteken: *\"a shift that started in the dark / and ended in the dark.\"* Die sin loop oor, net soos die lang skof aanhou. Die kort reël 4 staan alleen en beklemtoon dat hy nooit daglig gesien het nie – sy werkure was baie lank (2 punte).","en":"(a) Line 3 ends without punctuation: *\"a shift that started in the dark / and ended in the dark.\"* The sentence runs on, just as the long shift keeps going. The short line 4 stands alone and emphasises that he never saw daylight – his working hours were very long (2 marks)."},{"af":"(b) Die woord **\"Now\"** (reël 9) is die wendingspunt (1 punt): strofes 1–2 praat oor die verlede, strofe 3 oor die hede.","en":"(b) The word **\"Now\"** (line 9) is the turning point (1 mark): stanzas 1–2 are about the past, stanza 3 is about the present."},{"af":"Die toon verander van **bewonderend/nostalgies** (*\"lifted me above the orange trees\"*) (1 punt) na **hartseer/somber** (*\"tremble\"*, *\"thin as paper\"*) (1 punt).","en":"The tone changes from **admiring/nostalgic** (*\"lifted me above the orange trees\"*) (1 mark) to **sad/sombre** (*\"tremble\"*, *\"thin as paper\"*) (1 mark)."},{"af":"(c) **Ja** (1 punt). Daar is geen gereelde rymskema nie (*Brits / underground / dark / dark* rym nie) en die reëls het nie 'n vaste lengte of ritme nie; dit klink soos natuurlike spraak (1 punt).","en":"(c) **Yes** (1 mark). There is no regular rhyme scheme (*Brits / underground / dark / dark* do not rhyme) and the lines have no fixed length or rhythm; it sounds like natural speech (1 mark)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) The run-on line imitates the long shift that keeps going, and the short line 4 emphasises that he worked in the dark from start to finish. (b) \"Now\" – the tone changes from admiring/nostalgic to sad/sombre. (c) Yes – there is no regular rhyme scheme or rhythm; it sounds like natural speech.","en":"(a) The run-on line imitates the long shift that keeps going, and the short line 4 emphasises that he worked in the dark from start to finish. (b) \"Now\" – the tone changes from admiring/nostalgic to sad/sombre. (c) Yes – there is no regular rhyme scheme or rhythm; it sounds like natural speech."}},{"title":{"af":"Die sonnet: soort, rymskema en volta","en":"The sonnet: type, rhyme scheme and volta"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die sonnet en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Hartbeespoort, Then and Now*\n\n1  When I was small, the water at the dam\n2  was blue as Ma's best Sunday-morning dress;\n3  we swam, we laughed, we ate our bread and jam\n4  and never thought of greed or carelessness.\n5  Now green hyacinth creeps from shore to shore,\n6  a thick, unwanted carpet on the tide;\n7  the boats lie still, the fishermen are poor,\n8  the dam that gave us life has slowly died.\n9  Who poisoned it? The factory, the drain,\n10  the plastic bags we tossed without a care;\n11  we blame the weeds, the government, the rain,\n12  but every one of us has had a share.\n13  Yet if we clean the mess that we have made,\n14  the blue may come again and never fade.\n\n(a) What type of sonnet is this? Give TWO reasons. (3)\n(b) Give the rhyme scheme of lines 1–4. (1)\n(c) Where does the volta occur, and how does the tone change? (2)\n(d) Identify the figure of speech in line 5. (1)","en":"Read the sonnet and answer the questions.\n\n*Hartbeespoort, Then and Now*\n\n1  When I was small, the water at the dam\n2  was blue as Ma's best Sunday-morning dress;\n3  we swam, we laughed, we ate our bread and jam\n4  and never thought of greed or carelessness.\n5  Now green hyacinth creeps from shore to shore,\n6  a thick, unwanted carpet on the tide;\n7  the boats lie still, the fishermen are poor,\n8  the dam that gave us life has slowly died.\n9  Who poisoned it? The factory, the drain,\n10  the plastic bags we tossed without a care;\n11  we blame the weeds, the government, the rain,\n12  but every one of us has had a share.\n13  Yet if we clean the mess that we have made,\n14  the blue may come again and never fade.\n\n(a) What type of sonnet is this? Give TWO reasons. (3)\n(b) Give the rhyme scheme of lines 1–4. (1)\n(c) Where does the volta occur, and how does the tone change? (2)\n(d) Identify the figure of speech in line 5. (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"Merk eers die eindwoorde: *dam (a), dress (b), jam (a), carelessness (b); shore (c), tide (d), poor (c), died (d); drain (e), care (f), rain (e), share (f); made (g), fade (g)*.","en":"First mark the end words: *dam (a), dress (b), jam (a), carelessness (b); shore (c), tide (d), poor (c), died (d); drain (e), care (f), rain (e), share (f); made (g), fade (g)*."},{"af":"(a) 'n **Shakespearean sonnet** (1): die rymskema is *abab cdcd efef gg* (1) en dit bestaan uit drie quatrains en 'n rymende couplet aan die einde (1).","en":"(a) A **Shakespearean sonnet** (1): the rhyme scheme is *abab cdcd efef gg* (1) and it consists of three quatrains and a rhyming couplet at the end (1)."},{"af":"(b) Reëls 1–4: **abab** (kruisrym).","en":"(b) Lines 1–4: **abab** (alternate rhyme)."},{"af":"(c) Die volta kom by **reël 13** met die woord *\"Yet\"* (1). Die toon verander van **verwytend/bitter** (*\"we blame\"*, *\"every one of us has had a share\"*) na **hoopvol** (*\"the blue may come again\"*) (1).","en":"(c) The volta comes at **line 13** with the word *\"Yet\"* (1). The tone changes from **accusing/bitter** (*\"we blame\"*, *\"every one of us has had a share\"*) to **hopeful** (*\"the blue may come again\"*) (1)."},{"af":"(d) *\"green hyacinth creeps\"*: die plant kruip soos 'n mens of dier – **personification** (1). Dit laat die waterhiasint dreigend en stadig maar onstuitbaar lyk.","en":"(d) *\"green hyacinth creeps\"*: the plant creeps like a person or animal – **personification** (1). It makes the water hyacinth seem threatening, slow but unstoppable."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Shakespearean sonnet: rhyme scheme abab cdcd efef gg; three quatrains and a rhyming couplet. (b) abab. (c) Line 13 (\"Yet\"): the tone changes from accusing/bitter to hopeful. (d) Personification.","en":"(a) Shakespearean sonnet: rhyme scheme abab cdcd efef gg; three quatrains and a rhyming couplet. (b) abab. (c) Line 13 (\"Yet\"): the tone changes from accusing/bitter to hopeful. (d) Personification."}},{"title":{"af":"Paragraafvraag: hoe word die tema oorgedra?","en":"Paragraph question: how is the theme conveyed?"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys na *Grandfather's Hands* (voorbeeld 1).\n\nDiscuss how the poet conveys the theme of the poem. Write a paragraph of about 80–100 words. (5)","en":"Refer to *Grandfather's Hands* (example 1).\n\nDiscuss how the poet conveys the theme of the poem. Write a paragraph of about 80–100 words. (5)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Stap 1 – stel die tema in 'n volsin** (1 punt): *The poem shows that a life of hard work and love deserves respect, but that time eventually weakens even the strongest person.*","en":"**Step 1 – state the theme in a full sentence** (1 mark): *The poem shows that a life of hard work and love deserves respect, but that time eventually weakens even the strongest person.*"},{"af":"**Stap 2 – kies twee of drie tegnieke met aanhalings:** die metafoor *\"His hands are maps\"*, die kontras *\"rough as sandpaper, / gentle as rain\"* en die simile *\"like a clock that is running down\"*.","en":"**Step 2 – choose two or three techniques with quotations:** the metaphor *\"His hands are maps\"*, the contrast *\"rough as sandpaper, / gentle as rain\"* and the simile *\"like a clock that is running down\"*."},{"af":"**Stap 3 – verbind elke tegniek met die tema** (3 punte): sê telkens *wat* dit wys, nie net *wat* dit is nie.","en":"**Step 3 – link each technique to the theme** (3 marks): each time say *what* it shows, not only *what* it is."},{"af":"**Stap 4 – sluit af** met die retoriese vrae aan die einde (1 punt) en tel jou woorde.","en":"**Step 4 – conclude** with the rhetorical questions at the end (1 mark) and count your words."}],"answer":{"af":"The poem shows that a life of hard work and love deserves respect, but that time weakens even the strongest person. The metaphor \"His hands are maps\" suggests that his scars record years of dangerous work in the mines. The contrast between \"rough as sandpaper\" and \"gentle as rain\" shows that he was physically tough but loving. After the turning point \"Now\", the simile \"like a clock that is running down\" shows that his life is ending. The rhetorical questions \"Who will hold the light?\" express the speaker's fear of losing him. (92 words)","en":"The poem shows that a life of hard work and love deserves respect, but that time weakens even the strongest person. The metaphor \"His hands are maps\" suggests that his scars record years of dangerous work in the mines. The contrast between \"rough as sandpaper\" and \"gentle as rain\" shows that he was physically tough but loving. After the turning point \"Now\", the simile \"like a clock that is running down\" shows that his life is ending. The rhetorical questions \"Who will hold the light?\" express the speaker's fear of losing him. (92 words)"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat noem ons 'n strofe van **agt** reëls?","en":"What do we call a stanza of **eight** lines?"},"options":[{"af":"sestet","en":"sestet"},{"af":"quatrain","en":"quatrain"},{"af":"octave","en":"octave"},{"af":"tercet","en":"tercet"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n *Octave* het 8 reëls. 'n *Sestet* het 6, 'n *quatrain* 4 en 'n *tercet* 3. In 'n Petrarchan-sonnet volg die sestet op die octave.","en":"An *octave* has 8 lines. A *sestet* has 6, a *quatrain* 4 and a *tercet* 3. In a Petrarchan sonnet the sestet follows the octave."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die spreker (*speaker*) in 'n gedig is altyd die digter self.","en":"The speaker in a poem is always the poet himself or herself."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Die spreker is die stem in die gedig; 'n digter kan as 'n kind, 'n dier of selfs 'n voorwerp praat. Skryf daarom *the speaker* in jou antwoorde.","en":"False. The speaker is the voice in the poem; a poet can speak as a child, an animal or even an object. That is why you write *the speaker* in your answers."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Shakespearean-sonnet eindig met 'n rymende ___. (Engelse term)","en":"A Shakespearean sonnet ends with a rhyming ___."},"answers":{"af":["couplet","koeplet"],"en":["couplet"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["quatrain","tercet","octave"],"en":["quatrain","tercet","octave"]}},"explain":{"af":"Drie quatrains (12 reëls) + 'n rymende couplet (2 reëls) = 14 reëls, met die rymskema *abab cdcd efef gg*.","en":"Three quatrains (12 lines) + a rhyming couplet (2 lines) = 14 lines, with the rhyme scheme *abab cdcd efef gg*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stylfiguur plaas twee teenstrydige woorde langs mekaar, soos *deafening silence* of *bitter-sweet*?","en":"Which figure of speech places two contradictory words side by side, as in *deafening silence* or *bitter-sweet*?"},"options":[{"af":"paradox","en":"paradox"},{"af":"oxymoron","en":"oxymoron"},{"af":"antithesis","en":"antithesis"},{"af":"euphemism","en":"euphemism"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n *Oxymoron* is twee teenstrydige **woorde** saam. 'n *Paradox* is 'n hele **stelling** wat teenstrydig lyk (*The more I learn, the less I know*). *Antithesis* stel teenoorgestelde idees in gebalanseerde frases teenoor mekaar.","en":"An *oxymoron* is two contradictory **words** together. A *paradox* is a whole **statement** that seems contradictory (*The more I learn, the less I know*). *Antithesis* sets opposite ideas against each other in balanced phrases."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die punt in 'n sonnet waar die gedagte of toon skielik verander, word die ___ genoem. (Engelse term)","en":"The point in a sonnet where the thought or tone suddenly changes is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["volta","the volta","turn","wending"],"en":["volta","the volta","turn"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["refrain","enjambment","stanza"],"en":["refrain","enjambment","stanza"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die *volta* (wending) kom by reël 9 in 'n Petrarchan-sonnet en gewoonlik by reël 13 (die couplet) in 'n Shakespearean-sonnet. 'n *Refrain* is 'n herhaalde reël.","en":"The *volta* (turn) comes at line 9 in a Petrarchan sonnet and usually at line 13 (the couplet) in a Shakespearean sonnet. A *refrain* is a repeated line."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Identifiseer die stylfiguur: *The wind sang lullabies to the sleeping Magaliesberg.*","en":"Identify the figure of speech: *The wind sang lullabies to the sleeping Magaliesberg.*"},"options":[{"af":"simile","en":"simile"},{"af":"hyperbole","en":"hyperbole"},{"af":"metaphor","en":"metaphor"},{"af":"personification","en":"personification"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Sing en slaap is menslike handelinge; die wind en die berg kry menslike eienskappe, dus *personification*. Daar is geen *like/as* nie (nie 'n simile nie) en niks word oordryf nie.","en":"Singing and sleeping are human actions; the wind and the mountain are given human qualities, so it is *personification*. There is no *like/as* (not a simile) and nothing is exaggerated."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die rymskema van hierdie strofe:\n\n*The rank is loud before the sun is high;*\n*the drivers whistle, hoot and shout and call;*\n*the queue grows long beside the station wall*\n*while sleepy workers shuffle, sigh by sigh.*\n\nRymskema: ___","en":"Give the rhyme scheme of this stanza:\n\n*The rank is loud before the sun is high;*\n*the drivers whistle, hoot and shout and call;*\n*the queue grows long beside the station wall*\n*while sleepy workers shuffle, sigh by sigh.*\n\nRhyme scheme: ___"},"answers":{"af":["abba"],"en":["abba"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["abab","aabb","abcb"],"en":["abab","aabb","abcb"]}},"explain":{"af":"*high* (a), *call* (b), *wall* (b), *sigh* (a): die buitenste reëls rym met mekaar en die middelste twee met mekaar – *abba*, omarmende rym.","en":"*high* (a), *call* (b), *wall* (b), *sigh* (a): the outer lines rhyme with each other and the middle two with each other – *abba*, enclosed rhyme."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Enjambement (*enjambment*) is wanneer 'n versreël met 'n punt eindig sodat die leser moet stilstaan.","en":"Enjambment is when a line ends with a full stop so that the reader has to pause."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit beskryf 'n *end-stopped line*. By enjambement loop die sin **sonder** 'n leesteken oor na die volgende reël.","en":"False. That describes an *end-stopped line*. With enjambment the sentence runs on to the next line **without** a punctuation mark."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord beskryf die toon van hierdie reëls die beste?\n\n*Oh, wonderful – another exam on my birthday.*\n*Just what I always wanted.*","en":"Which word best describes the tone of these lines?\n\n*Oh, wonderful – another exam on my birthday.*\n*Just what I always wanted.*"},"options":[{"af":"sarcastic","en":"sarcastic"},{"af":"hopeful","en":"hopeful"},{"af":"nostalgic","en":"nostalgic"},{"af":"admiring","en":"admiring"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die spreker sê die teenoorgestelde van wat hy bedoel: niemand wil 'n eksamen op sy verjaardag skryf nie. Dit is *sarcastic*. Woorde soos *wonderful* is dus nie letterlik nie.","en":"The speaker says the opposite of what he means: nobody wants to write an exam on his birthday. That is *sarcastic*. Words such as *wonderful* are therefore not literal."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Noem die klanktegniek (*sound device*) in hierdie reël: *I lie awake and hate the rain.* ___ (Engelse term)","en":"Name the sound device in this line: *I lie awake and hate the rain.* ___"},"answers":{"af":["assonance","assonansie"],"en":["assonance"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["alliteration","onomatopoeia","oxymoron"],"en":["alliteration","onomatopoeia","oxymoron"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die klinkerklank *a* (soos in *day*) word herhaal in *awake, hate, rain*: dit is *assonance*. *Alliteration* is herhaalde **beginkonsonante**, en geen woord boots 'n klank na nie.","en":"The vowel sound *a* (as in *day*) is repeated in *awake, hate, rain*: that is *assonance*. *Alliteration* is repeated **initial consonants**, and no word imitates a sound."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stylfiguur by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each figure of speech to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Simile","en":"Simile"},"r":{"af":"Her laugh rang out like a bell across the dam.","en":"Her laugh rang out like a bell across the dam."}},{"l":{"af":"Metaphor","en":"Metaphor"},"r":{"af":"After break, the classroom was a zoo.","en":"After break, the classroom was a zoo."}},{"l":{"af":"Hyperbole","en":"Hyperbole"},"r":{"af":"I've waited a hundred years for this taxi.","en":"I've waited a hundred years for this taxi."}},{"l":{"af":"Euphemism","en":"Euphemism"},"r":{"af":"Grandpa passed away last winter.","en":"Grandpa passed away last winter."}},{"l":{"af":"Paradox","en":"Paradox"},"r":{"af":"The more I learn, the less I know.","en":"The more I learn, the less I know."}}],"explain":{"af":"Simile gebruik *like/as*; metaphor sê die klas **is** 'n dieretuin; hyperbole oordryf (100 jaar); euphemism versag *died*; paradox klink teenstrydig maar bevat 'n waarheid.","en":"A simile uses *like/as*; the metaphor says the class **is** a zoo; hyperbole exaggerates (100 years); the euphemism softens *died*; the paradox sounds contradictory but contains a truth."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lees die reëls:\n\n*I slammed the gate. I hate this place,*\n*its dust, its noise, its endless queues.*\n\nHaal EEN woord uit reël 1 aan wat wys dat die spreker kwaad is: ___","en":"Read the lines:\n\n*I slammed the gate. I hate this place,*\n*its dust, its noise, its endless queues.*\n\nQuote ONE word from line 1 that shows that the speaker is angry: ___"},"answers":{"af":["slammed","hate","\"slammed\"","\"hate\""],"en":["slammed","hate","\"slammed\"","\"hate\""]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["gate","place","dust"],"en":["gate","place","dust"]}},"explain":{"af":"*slammed* (die hek hard toeklap) en *hate* wys albei woede. Gee presies EEN woord, uit die regte reël – *dust* kom uit reël 2 en wys nie self woede nie.","en":"*slammed* (shutting the gate violently) and *hate* both show anger. Give exactly ONE word, from the correct line – *dust* is from line 2 and does not show anger on its own."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom word enjambement in hierdie reëls gebruik?\n\n*The river runs and runs*\n*past farms and towns and never stops*\n*until it finds the sea.*","en":"Why is enjambment used in these lines?\n\n*The river runs and runs*\n*past farms and towns and never stops*\n*until it finds the sea.*"},"options":[{"af":"To imitate the continuous flow of the river – the lines run on just as the water does.","en":"To imitate the continuous flow of the river – the lines run on just as the water does."},{"af":"To create a regular rhyme scheme.","en":"To create a regular rhyme scheme."},{"af":"To force the reader to stop at the end of every line.","en":"To force the reader to stop at the end of every line."},{"af":"To show that the speaker is angry with the river.","en":"To show that the speaker is angry with the river."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die vorm boots die betekenis na: daar is geen leesteken aan die einde van reëls 1 en 2 nie, so die leser lees aan sonder om te stop – net soos die rivier. Die reëls rym nie, en enjambement verwyder juis pouses.","en":"The form imitates the meaning: there is no punctuation at the end of lines 1 and 2, so the reader reads on without stopping – just like the river. The lines do not rhyme, and enjambment actually removes pauses."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stylfiguur word hier gebruik? *A sign at the dam reads 'Keep our water clean!' – it floats among plastic bottles.*","en":"Which figure of speech is used here? *A sign at the dam reads 'Keep our water clean!' – it floats among plastic bottles.*"},"options":[{"af":"hyperbole","en":"hyperbole"},{"af":"euphemism","en":"euphemism"},{"af":"oxymoron","en":"oxymoron"},{"af":"irony","en":"irony"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Dit is situasie-ironie: die bord wat vra dat die water skoon gehou word, dryf self tussen die besoedeling – die teenoorgestelde van wat verwag word. Niks word oordryf of versag nie, en daar is nie twee teenstrydige woorde langs mekaar nie.","en":"This is situational irony: the sign asking people to keep the water clean is itself floating in the pollution – the opposite of what is expected. Nothing is exaggerated or softened, and there are no two contradictory words side by side."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Vraag (3 punte): *Identify the figure of speech in \"Hope is a candle in a load-shedding night\" and explain it.* Watter antwoord verdien al 3 punte?","en":"Question (3 marks): *Identify the figure of speech in \"Hope is a candle in a load-shedding night\" and explain it.* Which answer earns all 3 marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Metaphor.","en":"Metaphor."},{"af":"Simile – hope is like a candle that burns in the dark.","en":"Simile – hope is like a candle that burns in the dark."},{"af":"Metaphor – hope is compared to a candle: just as a small flame gives light in the dark, hope gives comfort and courage in difficult times.","en":"Metaphor – hope is compared to a candle: just as a small flame gives light in the dark, hope gives comfort and courage in difficult times."},{"af":"Personification – the candle is given the human quality of hope.","en":"Personification – the candle is given the human quality of hope."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die volledige antwoord gee die regte term (geen *like/as* nie, dus *metaphor*) (1), sê wat vergelyk word (hoop en 'n kers) (1) en verduidelik die effek (1). *Metaphor.* alleen kry 1 punt; *simile* en *personification* is die verkeerde terme.","en":"The full answer gives the correct term (no *like/as*, so *metaphor*) (1), says what is compared (hope and a candle) (1) and explains the effect (1). *Metaphor.* on its own earns 1 mark; *simile* and *personification* are the wrong terms."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder skryf oor die sonnet *Hartbeespoort, Then and Now*: *\"The theme of the poem is the dam.\"* Hoekom is dit 'n swak antwoord?","en":"A learner writes about the sonnet *Hartbeespoort, Then and Now*: *\"The theme of the poem is the dam.\"* Why is this a weak answer?"},"options":[{"af":"Omdat 'n tema altyd net een woord mag wees.","en":"Because a theme must always be only one word."},{"af":"Omdat dit die onderwerp (waaroor die gedig gaan) gee en nie die tema nie (die boodskap oor die lewe, bv. dat mense deur onverskilligheid vernietig wat hulle liefhet).","en":"Because it gives the subject (what the poem is about), not the theme (the message about life, e.g. that people destroy what they love through carelessness)."},{"af":"Omdat die tema van 'n gedig altyd in die titel staan.","en":"Because the theme of a poem is always stated in its title."},{"af":"Omdat 'n gedig oor die natuur nie 'n tema kan hê nie.","en":"Because a poem about nature cannot have a theme."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Die dam* is die **onderwerp**. Die **tema** is die insig wat die gedig oor die lewe gee, en jy skryf dit as 'n volsin: *People destroy what they love through carelessness, but it is not too late to repair the damage.*","en":"*The dam* is the **subject**. The **theme** is the insight the poem gives about life, and you write it as a full sentence: *People destroy what they love through carelessness, but it is not too late to repair the damage.*"}}]},{"id":"eng10-t3-visual-literacy","title":{"af":"Visuele geletterdheid: advertensies en spotprente","en":"Visual literacy: advertisements and cartoons"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal advertensies, spotprente en strokiesprente kan ontleed – teikenmark, oorredingstegnieke, visuele leidrade en humor – en taalvrae oor die teks kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to analyse advertisements, cartoons and comic strips – target market, persuasive techniques, visual clues and humour – and answer language questions on the text."},"summary":{"af":"## Visuele tekste in Vraestel 1, Afdeling C\n\n| Teks | Punte (ongeveer) |\n|---|---|\n| Advertensie | ±10 |\n| Spotprent of strokiesprent | ±10 |\n| Taal in konteks / redigering | ±20 |\n\nIn die eksamen is daar regte prente; hier beskryf ons elke visuele teks in woorde. Lees die **woorde én die prent**: baie vrae vra hoe die twee saamwerk. Daar kom ook taalvrae oor die teks self (woordsoort, tyd, lydende vorm, leestekens).\n\n## Advertensies\n\n### Dele van 'n advertensie\n\n| Deel | Wat dit is |\n|---|---|\n| Product/service (produk/diens) | wat verkoop word |\n| Brand name (handelsnaam) | die naam van die produk of maatskappy |\n| Logo | die simbool of ontwerp van die handelsmerk |\n| Headline (opskrif) | die groot opskrif wat eerste die aandag trek |\n| Body copy (hoofteks) | die inligting oor die produk |\n| Slogan/catchphrase (slagspreuk) | 'n kort, pakkende frase wat jy onthou |\n| Contact details | webwerf, telefoonnommer, adres |\n| Fine print / asterisk (*) | klein druk met bepalings en voorwaardes wat 'n bewering beperk |\n\n### Teikenmark (target market)\n\nDie **teikenmark** is die groep mense vir wie die advertensie bedoel is: ouderdom, geslag, belangstellings of inkomste. **Motiveer altyd** met 'n leidraad uit die advertensie, bv. *\"Teenagers, because the photo shows a teenager gaming and the advert says 'Everyone at school already has one'.\"* Net *\"teenagers\"* kry 1 uit 2.\n\n### Oorredingstegnieke (persuasive techniques)\n\n| Tegniek | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|\n| Emotive language (emosionele taal) | *Don't let your family suffer in the dark.* |\n| Exaggeration (oordrywing) | *The best pizza in the universe!* |\n| Imperatives (bevele) | *Buy now! Call today!* |\n| Rhetorical question | *Tired of cold showers?* |\n| Pun (woordspeling) | *We knead you!* (bakkery) |\n| Alliteration / rhyme | *Crunchy, crispy, crazy good!* / *Feel the heat – can't be beat!* |\n| Celebrity endorsement / testimonial | 'n bekende rugbyspeler of 'n \"tevrede klant\" beveel dit aan |\n| \"Free\" / discounts | *Buy one, get one FREE!* |\n| Bandwagon (meeloop-effek) | *Everyone is switching – don't be left out!* |\n| Direct address | *You deserve it.* |\n\n### Visuele tegnieke\n\n- **Colour** (kleur): rooi = opwinding of gevaar, groen = natuur of gesondheid, geel = energie of lig; sterk kontras trek die aandag.\n- **Font** (lettertipe): grootte en vet druk wys wat belangrik is; 'n speelse font pas by kinders, 'n deftige font by luukse produkte.\n- **Images** (beelde): mense wat gelukkig is met die produk, sodat die teikenmark homself daarin sien.\n- **Layout and white space** (uitleg en wit spasie): bepaal wat die oog eerste sien; leë spasie laat die produk uitstaan.\n\n### AIDA\n\n1. **Attention** – die opskrif, kleur of prent trek die aandag.\n2. **Interest** – die hoofteks maak jou nuuskierig.\n3. **Desire** – voordele en beloftes laat jou die produk wil hê.\n4. **Action** – 'n bevel en kontakbesonderhede sê wat jy moet doen.\n\n> **Feit of mening?** 'n **Feit** kan bewys word (*R399, 20 000 mAh*). 'n **Mening** is 'n oordeel (*the best, amazing, tastiest*). Advertensies vermom dikwels menings as feite.\n\n## Spotprente en strokiesprente\n\n- **Frame** (raam): elke blokkie in 'n strokiesprent; lees van links na regs.\n- **Speech bubble** (spraakborrel): woorde wat gesê word; die stertjie wys na die spreker.\n- **Thought bubble** (gedagteborrel): 'n wolkie met sirkeltjies – wat iemand dink.\n- **Shout bubble** (skreeuborrel): 'n getande, skerp rand – skree, woede of skok.\n- **Onomatopoeia**: klankwoorde soos *BANG!* of *BZZZ*.\n- **Movement lines** (beweginglyne): wys spoed of beweging.\n- **Facial expressions and body language**: oë, mond, wenkbroue en arms (gevoude arms = ongeduldig of ontevrede).\n- **Bold or capital letters**: beklemtoning of hard praat.\n\n### Hoe humor werk\n\n- **Irony**: die teenoorgestelde van wat verwag word, gebeur.\n- **Pun**: 'n woord met twee betekenisse.\n- **Exaggeration**: iets word belaglik groot of erg gemaak.\n- **Unexpected ending**: die laaste raam het 'n draai.\n\nSpotprente het dikwels 'n **boodskap**. **Satire** gebruik humor om mense, gewoontes of die samelewing te kritiseer.\n\n## Hoe om te antwoord\n\n1. Lees die opskrif en die beskrywing van elke raam.\n2. Lees die vrae en let op die punte (2 punte = antwoord + rede).\n3. Verwys na 'n **spesifieke** visuele leidraad (*his arms are folded*), nie net *\"his face\"* nie.\n4. Vir *\"Why is it funny?\"* verduidelik die **kontras** tussen wat verwag word en wat gebeur.\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders beskryf die prent, maar verduidelik nie die effek nie. Sê altyd *wat* jy sien én *wat dit wys*.","en":"## Visual texts in Paper 1, Section C\n\n| Text | Marks (approximately) |\n|---|---|\n| Advertisement | ±10 |\n| Cartoon or comic strip | ±10 |\n| Language in context / editing | ±20 |\n\nIn the exam there are real pictures; here we describe every visual text in words. Read **the words and the picture**: many questions ask how the two work together. There are also language questions on the text itself (part of speech, tense, passive voice, punctuation).\n\n## Advertisements\n\n### Parts of an advertisement\n\n| Part | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| Product/service | what is being sold |\n| Brand name | the name of the product or company |\n| Logo | the symbol or design of the brand |\n| Headline | the large heading that catches attention first |\n| Body copy | the information about the product |\n| Slogan/catchphrase | a short, catchy phrase that you remember |\n| Contact details | website, phone number, address |\n| Fine print / asterisk (*) | small print with terms and conditions that limit a claim |\n\n### Target market\n\nThe **target market** is the group of people the advert is meant for: age, gender, interests or income. **Always motivate** with a clue from the advert, e.g. *\"Teenagers, because the photo shows a teenager gaming and the advert says 'Everyone at school already has one'.\"* Only *\"teenagers\"* earns 1 out of 2.\n\n### Persuasive techniques\n\n| Technique | Example |\n|---|---|\n| Emotive language | *Don't let your family suffer in the dark.* |\n| Exaggeration | *The best pizza in the universe!* |\n| Imperatives (commands) | *Buy now! Call today!* |\n| Rhetorical question | *Tired of cold showers?* |\n| Pun | *We knead you!* (bakery) |\n| Alliteration / rhyme | *Crunchy, crispy, crazy good!* / *Feel the heat – can't be beat!* |\n| Celebrity endorsement / testimonial | a famous rugby player or a \"satisfied customer\" recommends it |\n| \"Free\" / discounts | *Buy one, get one FREE!* |\n| Bandwagon | *Everyone is switching – don't be left out!* |\n| Direct address | *You deserve it.* |\n\n### Visual techniques\n\n- **Colour:** red = excitement or danger, green = nature or health, yellow = energy or light; strong contrast attracts attention.\n- **Font:** size and bold print show what is important; a playful font suits children, an elegant font suits luxury products.\n- **Images:** people who are happy with the product, so that the target market sees itself in them.\n- **Layout and white space:** decide what the eye sees first; empty space makes the product stand out.\n\n### AIDA\n\n1. **Attention** – the headline, colour or picture grabs attention.\n2. **Interest** – the body copy makes you curious.\n3. **Desire** – benefits and promises make you want the product.\n4. **Action** – a command and contact details tell you what to do.\n\n> **Fact or opinion?** A **fact** can be proved (*R399, 20 000 mAh*). An **opinion** is a judgement (*the best, amazing, tastiest*). Adverts often disguise opinions as facts.\n\n## Cartoons and comic strips\n\n- **Frame:** each box in a comic strip; read from left to right.\n- **Speech bubble:** words that are spoken; the tail points to the speaker.\n- **Thought bubble:** a cloud with small circles – what someone thinks.\n- **Shout bubble:** a jagged, spiky edge – shouting, anger or shock.\n- **Onomatopoeia:** sound words such as *BANG!* or *BZZZ*.\n- **Movement lines:** show speed or movement.\n- **Facial expressions and body language:** eyes, mouth, eyebrows and arms (folded arms = impatient or displeased).\n- **Bold or capital letters:** emphasis or speaking loudly.\n\n### How humour works\n\n- **Irony:** the opposite of what is expected happens.\n- **Pun:** a word with two meanings.\n- **Exaggeration:** something is made ridiculously big or extreme.\n- **Unexpected ending:** the last frame has a twist.\n\nCartoons often have a **message**. **Satire** uses humour to criticise people, habits or society.\n\n## How to answer\n\n1. Read the heading and the description of each frame.\n2. Read the questions and note the marks (2 marks = answer + reason).\n3. Refer to a **specific** visual clue (*his arms are folded*), not just *\"his face\"*.\n4. For *\"Why is it funny?\"* explain the **contrast** between what is expected and what happens.\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners describe the picture but do not explain the effect. Always say *what* you see and *what it shows*."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Target market (teikenmark)","en":"Target market"},"def":{"af":"Die groep mense vir wie 'n advertensie bedoel is, bv. tieners, ouers of pensioenarisse.","en":"The group of people an advertisement is aimed at, e.g. teenagers, parents or pensioners."}},{"term":{"af":"Slogan (slagspreuk)","en":"Slogan"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort, pakkende frase wat mense onthou en met die handelsmerk verbind.","en":"A short, catchy phrase that people remember and link to the brand."}},{"term":{"af":"Persuasive techniques (oorredingstegnieke)","en":"Persuasive techniques"},"def":{"af":"Metodes wat 'n adverteerder gebruik om jou te oortuig om te koop, bv. emosionele taal, bevele en die meeloop-effek.","en":"Methods an advertiser uses to convince you to buy, e.g. emotive language, imperatives and bandwagon."}},{"term":{"af":"Body copy (hoofteks)","en":"Body copy"},"def":{"af":"Die hoofinligting in 'n advertensie wat die produk en sy voordele beskryf.","en":"The main information in an advertisement that describes the product and its benefits."}},{"term":{"af":"Fine print (fyn druk)","en":"Fine print"},"def":{"af":"Klein teks, dikwels by 'n asterisk (*), met die bepalings en voorwaardes wat 'n bewering beperk.","en":"Small text, often linked to an asterisk (*), with the terms and conditions that limit a claim."}},{"term":{"af":"AIDA","en":"AIDA"},"def":{"af":"Attention, Interest, Desire, Action: die vier stappe waarmee 'n advertensie die leser na 'n aankoop lei.","en":"Attention, Interest, Desire, Action: the four steps an advertisement uses to lead the reader to buy."}},{"term":{"af":"Speech bubble (spraakborrel)","en":"Speech bubble"},"def":{"af":"'n Borrel met 'n stertjie wat wys watter karakter die woorde sê; 'n getande borrel wys skree.","en":"A bubble with a tail that shows which character says the words; a jagged bubble shows shouting."}},{"term":{"af":"Thought bubble (gedagteborrel)","en":"Thought bubble"},"def":{"af":"'n Wolkvormige borrel met klein sirkeltjies wat wys wat 'n karakter dink, maar nie sê nie.","en":"A cloud-shaped bubble with small circles that shows what a character thinks but does not say."}},{"term":{"af":"Pun (woordspeling)","en":"Pun"},"def":{"af":"'n Speelse gebruik van 'n woord met twee betekenisse of van woorde wat dieselfde klink.","en":"A playful use of a word with two meanings, or of words that sound the same."}},{"term":{"af":"Satire (satire)","en":"Satire"},"def":{"af":"Humor, ironie of oordrywing wat gebruik word om mense, gewoontes of die samelewing te kritiseer.","en":"Humour, irony or exaggeration used to criticise people, habits or society."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Advertensie: teikenmark, woordspeling en AIDA","en":"Advertisement: target market, pun and AIDA"},"problem":{"af":"Bestudeer die advertensie en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Advertisement (described in words)**\n\n- **Top:** huge yellow capital letters on a black background: **DON'T LET LOAD-SHEDDING SHED YOUR FUN!**\n- **Picture:** a smiling teenage boy on a couch in a dark room, playing a game on his phone. The phone is plugged into a small black power bank. Only his face and the screen are lit.\n- **Brand name and logo:** the word **ZAPPA**; a yellow lightning bolt forms the letter Z.\n- **Body copy:** “Stage 6? No stress. The ZAPPA PowerBrick 20 000 mAh charges your phone up to five times.* It's light, tough and always ready when the grid isn't. Everyone at school already has one – why are you still sitting in the dark? Get yours today for only R399!”\n- **Slogan (bottom):** *ZAPPA – power that never pauses.*\n- **Contact details:** a website address and a WhatsApp number.\n- **Fine print:** “*Based on a fully charged PowerBrick and a phone with a 4 000 mAh battery. Terms and conditions apply.”\n\n(a) Who is the target market of this advertisement? Motivate your answer. (2)\n(b) Explain the pun in the headline. (2)\n(c) Which words in the body copy are the 'Action' step of AIDA? (1)","en":"Study the advertisement and answer the questions.\n\n**Advertisement (described in words)**\n\n- **Top:** huge yellow capital letters on a black background: **DON'T LET LOAD-SHEDDING SHED YOUR FUN!**\n- **Picture:** a smiling teenage boy on a couch in a dark room, playing a game on his phone. The phone is plugged into a small black power bank. Only his face and the screen are lit.\n- **Brand name and logo:** the word **ZAPPA**; a yellow lightning bolt forms the letter Z.\n- **Body copy:** “Stage 6? No stress. The ZAPPA PowerBrick 20 000 mAh charges your phone up to five times.* It's light, tough and always ready when the grid isn't. Everyone at school already has one – why are you still sitting in the dark? Get yours today for only R399!”\n- **Slogan (bottom):** *ZAPPA – power that never pauses.*\n- **Contact details:** a website address and a WhatsApp number.\n- **Fine print:** “*Based on a fully charged PowerBrick and a phone with a 4 000 mAh battery. Terms and conditions apply.”\n\n(a) Who is the target market of this advertisement? Motivate your answer. (2)\n(b) Explain the pun in the headline. (2)\n(c) Which words in the body copy are the 'Action' step of AIDA? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Soek leidrade: die prent wys 'n **tiener** wat op sy foon speel, en die hoofteks sê *\"Everyone at school\"*. Die teikenmark is dus tieners/skoolleerders met slimfone (1) – motivering uit die advertensie (1).","en":"(a) Look for clues: the picture shows a **teenager** gaming on his phone, and the body copy says *\"Everyone at school\"*. So the target market is teenagers/school learners with smartphones (1) – motivation from the advert (1)."},{"af":"(b) 'n Woordspeling gebruik een woord in twee betekenisse. *Load-shedding* is beurtkrag (die krag word afgesny); *shed* beteken ook om iets te verloor of af te gooi, soos 'n boom wat blare laat val (1).","en":"(b) A pun uses one word in two senses. *Load-shedding* is the planned power cut; *shed* also means to lose or drop something, like a tree that sheds its leaves (1)."},{"af":"Die boodskap: moenie dat die kragonderbreking jou pret laat \"afval\" nie – met ZAPPA hou jy aan speel (1).","en":"The message: don't let the power cut make you \"lose\" your fun – with ZAPPA you can keep playing (1)."},{"af":"(c) Die **Action**-stap sê vir die leser wat om te doen: *\"Get yours today for only R399!\"* – 'n bevel (imperatief) met die prys.","en":"(c) The **Action** step tells the reader what to do: *\"Get yours today for only R399!\"* – a command (imperative) with the price."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Teenagers/school learners with smartphones – the picture shows a teenage boy gaming on his phone and the advert says \"Everyone at school already has one\". (b) \"Load-shedding\" is a power cut, and \"shed\" also means to lose something: the advert says the power cut should not make you lose your fun. (c) \"Get yours today for only R399!\"","en":"(a) Teenagers/school learners with smartphones – the picture shows a teenage boy gaming on his phone and the advert says \"Everyone at school already has one\". (b) \"Load-shedding\" is a power cut, and \"shed\" also means to lose something: the advert says the power cut should not make you lose your fun. (c) \"Get yours today for only R399!\""}},{"title":{"af":"Oorredingstegnieke, feit/mening en die asterisk","en":"Persuasive techniques, fact/opinion and the asterisk"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys weer na die ZAPPA-advertensie (voorbeeld 1).\n\n(a) Identify TWO persuasive techniques in the body copy. Quote and explain each. (4)\n(b) \"It's light, tough and always ready.\" Is this a fact or an opinion? Give a reason. (2)\n(c) Why is there an asterisk after \"five times\"? (2)\n(d) How does the colour of the headline help to sell the product? (1)","en":"Refer to the ZAPPA advertisement again (example 1).\n\n(a) Identify TWO persuasive techniques in the body copy. Quote and explain each. (4)\n(b) \"It's light, tough and always ready.\" Is this a fact or an opinion? Give a reason. (2)\n(c) Why is there an asterisk after \"five times\"? (2)\n(d) How does the colour of the headline help to sell the product? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Tegniek 1: **bandwagon** – *\"Everyone at school already has one\"* (1). Die leser voel uitgesluit en wil inpas, so hy koop (1).","en":"(a) Technique 1: **bandwagon** – *\"Everyone at school already has one\"* (1). The reader feels left out and wants to fit in, so he buys (1)."},{"af":"Tegniek 2: **rhetorical question** – *\"why are you still sitting in the dark?\"* (1). Die vraag het 'n voor-die-hand-liggende antwoord: jy hoef nie, as jy 'n ZAPPA koop nie (1). (Ook aanvaarbaar: die bevel *\"Get yours today\"* of direkte aanspreek *\"you\"*.)","en":"Technique 2: **rhetorical question** – *\"why are you still sitting in the dark?\"* (1). The question has an obvious answer: you don't have to, if you buy a ZAPPA (1). (Also acceptable: the command *\"Get yours today\"* or direct address *\"you\"*.)"},{"af":"(b) **Opinion** (1): *light* en *tough* is die adverteerder se oordeel – geen massa of toetsresultate word gegee nie – en *always* is 'n oordrywing wat nie bewys kan word nie (1).","en":"(b) **Opinion** (1): *light* and *tough* are the advertiser's judgement – no mass or test results are given – and *always* is an exaggeration that cannot be proved (1)."},{"af":"(c) Die asterisk verwys na die **fyn druk** (1). Die bewering *\"up to five times\"* is net waar onder sekere voorwaardes – 'n vol gelaaide PowerBrick en 'n foon met 'n 4 000 mAh-battery; 'n groter foonbattery laai dus minder kere (1).","en":"(c) The asterisk refers to the **fine print** (1). The claim *\"up to five times\"* is only true under certain conditions – a fully charged PowerBrick and a phone with a 4 000 mAh battery; a bigger phone battery will charge fewer times (1)."},{"af":"(d) Geel op swart skep sterk kontras wat die aandag trek, en geel herinner aan lig en elektrisiteit – presies wat die produk verskaf (1).","en":"(d) Yellow on black creates strong contrast that attracts attention, and yellow suggests light and electricity – exactly what the product provides (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Bandwagon: \"Everyone at school already has one\" – makes the reader want to fit in. Rhetorical question: \"why are you still sitting in the dark?\" – the obvious answer is to buy a ZAPPA. (b) Opinion – \"light\" and \"tough\" are judgements without proof, and \"always\" is exaggerated. (c) It refers to the fine print: the claim is only true under certain conditions. (d) The high-contrast yellow attracts attention and suggests light/electricity.","en":"(a) Bandwagon: \"Everyone at school already has one\" – makes the reader want to fit in. Rhetorical question: \"why are you still sitting in the dark?\" – the obvious answer is to buy a ZAPPA. (b) Opinion – \"light\" and \"tough\" are judgements without proof, and \"always\" is exaggerated. (c) It refers to the fine print: the claim is only true under certain conditions. (d) The high-contrast yellow attracts attention and suggests light/electricity."}},{"title":{"af":"Strokiesprent: visuele leidrade, humor en boodskap","en":"Comic strip: visual clues, humour and message"},"problem":{"af":"Bestudeer die strokiesprent en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n**Comic strip (described in words)**\n\n- **Frame 1:** Dad sits on the couch and points a finger at his son, Sipho, who is staring at his phone. Dad's speech bubble: *You kids are **ALWAYS** on your phones! In my day we **TALKED** to each other!*\n- **Frame 2:** Sipho puts his phone down on the table and smiles. Speech bubble: *Okay, Dad. Let's talk.* Dad smiles proudly.\n- **Frame 3:** Dad's phone vibrates – the word *BZZZ* in jagged letters with little movement lines. Dad is now scrolling on his phone with a big grin. His thought bubble: *Ooh, 42 likes on my braai photo!* Sipho sits with his arms folded and one eyebrow raised.\n\n(a) Why are the words \"ALWAYS\" and \"TALKED\" in bold capital letters in frame 1? (1)\n(b) Which visual clue in frame 3 shows how Sipho feels? Explain. (2)\n(c) Why is the last frame funny? (2)\n(d) What message does the cartoonist want to convey? (1)","en":"Study the comic strip and answer the questions.\n\n**Comic strip (described in words)**\n\n- **Frame 1:** Dad sits on the couch and points a finger at his son, Sipho, who is staring at his phone. Dad's speech bubble: *You kids are **ALWAYS** on your phones! In my day we **TALKED** to each other!*\n- **Frame 2:** Sipho puts his phone down on the table and smiles. Speech bubble: *Okay, Dad. Let's talk.* Dad smiles proudly.\n- **Frame 3:** Dad's phone vibrates – the word *BZZZ* in jagged letters with little movement lines. Dad is now scrolling on his phone with a big grin. His thought bubble: *Ooh, 42 likes on my braai photo!* Sipho sits with his arms folded and one eyebrow raised.\n\n(a) Why are the words \"ALWAYS\" and \"TALKED\" in bold capital letters in frame 1? (1)\n(b) Which visual clue in frame 3 shows how Sipho feels? Explain. (2)\n(c) Why is the last frame funny? (2)\n(d) What message does the cartoonist want to convey? (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) Vet hoofletters wys **beklemtoning**: pa praat hard en geïrriteerd en beklemtoon hierdie woorde (1).","en":"(a) Bold capitals show **emphasis**: Dad speaks loudly and with irritation and stresses these words (1)."},{"af":"(b) Leidraad: Sipho se **gevoude arms en een opgetrekte wenkbrou** (1). Dit wys hy is onbeïndruk en ietwat sarkasties – hy sien raak dat pa doen waaroor hy self gekla het (1).","en":"(b) Clue: Sipho's **folded arms and one raised eyebrow** (1). This shows he is unimpressed and a bit sarcastic – he notices that Dad is doing what he complained about (1)."},{"af":"(c) Dit is **ironies** (1): pa kla dat kinders altyd op hul fone is, maar in die laaste raam is dit pa wat sy foon nie kan los nie en die gesprek vergeet; die rolle is omgeruil – 'n onverwagte einde (1).","en":"(c) It is **ironic** (1): Dad complains that kids are always on their phones, but in the last frame it is Dad who can't leave his phone and forgets the conversation; the roles are reversed – an unexpected ending (1)."},{"af":"(d) Die boodskap (satire): volwassenes is dikwels net so verslaaf aan hul fone as tieners – moenie ander kritiseer vir iets wat jy self doen nie (1).","en":"(d) The message (satire): adults are often just as addicted to their phones as teenagers – don't criticise others for something you do yourself (1)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) To show emphasis – Dad stresses the words because he is annoyed. (b) His folded arms and raised eyebrow show that he is unimpressed/disapproving of Dad's behaviour. (c) It is ironic: Dad criticised Sipho for using his phone, but Dad is the one who is glued to his phone in the end. (d) Adults are often as addicted to their phones as teenagers; people criticise others for what they do themselves.","en":"(a) To show emphasis – Dad stresses the words because he is annoyed. (b) His folded arms and raised eyebrow show that he is unimpressed/disapproving of Dad's behaviour. (c) It is ironic: Dad criticised Sipho for using his phone, but Dad is the one who is glued to his phone in the end. (d) Adults are often as addicted to their phones as teenagers; people criticise others for what they do themselves."}},{"title":{"af":"Taal in konteks oor die visuele tekste","en":"Language in context on the visual texts"},"problem":{"af":"Verwys na die advertensie (voorbeeld 1) en die strokiesprent (voorbeeld 3).\n\n(a) Give the part of speech of \"tough\" in \"It's light, tough and always ready\". (1)\n(b) Rewrite in the passive voice: \"The ZAPPA PowerBrick charges your phone.\" (1)\n(c) Write \"It's\" out in full. (1)\n(d) Rewrite in the past tense: \"Everyone at school already has one.\" (1)\n(e) Add a question tag to Sipho's words: \"Let's talk.\" (1)","en":"Refer to the advertisement (example 1) and the comic strip (example 3).\n\n(a) Give the part of speech of \"tough\" in \"It's light, tough and always ready\". (1)\n(b) Rewrite in the passive voice: \"The ZAPPA PowerBrick charges your phone.\" (1)\n(c) Write \"It's\" out in full. (1)\n(d) Rewrite in the past tense: \"Everyone at school already has one.\" (1)\n(e) Add a question tag to Sipho's words: \"Let's talk.\" (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *tough* beskryf die naamwoord (die PowerBrick, waarna *It* verwys): dit is 'n **adjective** (byvoeglike naamwoord).","en":"(a) *tough* describes the noun (the PowerBrick, which *It* refers to): it is an **adjective**."},{"af":"(b) Die voorwerp *your phone* word die onderwerp; teenwoordige tyd → *is* + voltooide deelwoord + *by*: **Your phone is charged by the ZAPPA PowerBrick.**","en":"(b) The object *your phone* becomes the subject; present tense → *is* + past participle + *by*: **Your phone is charged by the ZAPPA PowerBrick.**"},{"af":"(c) Die apostrof vervang die *i* van *is*: **It is**.","en":"(c) The apostrophe replaces the *i* of *is*: **It is**."},{"af":"(d) *Everyone* is enkelvoud, dus *has* → **had**: **Everyone at school already had one.**","en":"(d) *Everyone* is singular, so *has* → **had**: **Everyone at school already had one.**"},{"af":"(e) Ná *Let's* is die vraagstertjie altyd *shall we?*: **Let's talk, shall we?**","en":"(e) After *Let's* the question tag is always *shall we?*: **Let's talk, shall we?**"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Adjective. (b) Your phone is charged by the ZAPPA PowerBrick. (c) It is. (d) Everyone at school already had one. (e) Let's talk, shall we?","en":"(a) Adjective. (b) Your phone is charged by the ZAPPA PowerBrick. (c) It is. (d) Everyone at school already had one. (e) Let's talk, shall we?"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is 'n *slogan* (slagspreuk) in 'n advertensie?","en":"What is a *slogan* in an advertisement?"},"options":[{"af":"die klein druk met die bepalings en voorwaardes","en":"the small print with the terms and conditions"},{"af":"'n kort, pakkende frase wat mense onthou en met die handelsmerk verbind","en":"a short, catchy phrase that people remember and link to the brand"},{"af":"die hoofblok inligting oor die produk","en":"the main block of information about the product"},{"af":"die simbool of prentjie wat die maatskappy verteenwoordig","en":"the symbol or picture that represents the company"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Slagspreuk is kort en pakkend, bv. *ZAPPA – power that never pauses.* Die klein druk is die *fine print*, die hoofinligting is die *body copy* en die simbool is die *logo*.","en":"A slogan is short and catchy, e.g. *ZAPPA – power that never pauses.* The small print is the *fine print*, the main information is the *body copy* and the symbol is the *logo*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Gedagteborrel (*thought bubble*) word gewoonlik as 'n wolkie geteken met klein sirkeltjies wat na die karakter lei.","en":"A thought bubble is usually drawn as a cloud with small circles leading to the character."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Die sirkeltjies wys dat die woorde gedink en nie gesê word nie. 'n Spraakborrel het 'n stertjie wat na die spreker wys.","en":"True. The small circles show that the words are thought, not spoken. A speech bubble has a tail that points to the speaker."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die groep mense op wie 'n advertensie gemik is, word die ___ genoem. (Engelse term)","en":"The group of people an advertisement is aimed at is called the ___."},"answers":{"af":["target market","target audience","teikenmark","teikengehoor"],"en":["target market","target audience"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["brand name","slogan","body copy"],"en":["brand name","slogan","body copy"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die *target market* (teikenmark) kan volgens ouderdom, geslag, belangstellings of inkomste beskryf word. Motiveer dit altyd met 'n leidraad uit die advertensie.","en":"The *target market* can be described by age, gender, interests or income. Always motivate it with a clue from the advertisement."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In die AIDA-model staan die **D** vir ___.","en":"In the AIDA model, the **D** stands for ___."},"options":[{"af":"Discount","en":"Discount"},{"af":"Design","en":"Design"},{"af":"Desire","en":"Desire"},{"af":"Detail","en":"Detail"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"AIDA = Attention, Interest, **Desire**, Action. Die advertensie wek eers aandag en belangstelling, laat jou dan die produk **begeer** en sê laastens wat om te doen.","en":"AIDA = Attention, Interest, **Desire**, Action. The advert first grabs attention and interest, then makes you **want** the product and finally tells you what to do."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Spraakborrel met skerp, getande (*jagged*) kante wys dat die karakter ___. (Engelse woord op -ing)","en":"A speech bubble with sharp, jagged edges shows that the character is ___."},"answers":{"af":["shouting","screaming","yelling","skree","skreeu"],"en":["shouting","screaming","yelling"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["whispering","thinking","sleeping"],"en":["whispering","thinking","sleeping"]}},"explain":{"af":"Getande kante wys 'n harde stem: skree, woede of skok. Gedagtes word in 'n wolkie met sirkeltjies geskryf, en fluister word dikwels met 'n stippellyn-borrel of klein letters gewys.","en":"Jagged edges show a loud voice: shouting, anger or shock. Thoughts go in a cloud with small circles, and whispering is often shown with a dotted bubble or small letters."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter oorredingstegniek word hier gebruik? *Join the thousands of teens who already drink FIZZBANG every day!*","en":"Which persuasive technique is used here? *Join the thousands of teens who already drink FIZZBANG every day!*"},"options":[{"af":"pun","en":"pun"},{"af":"rhetorical question","en":"rhetorical question"},{"af":"celebrity endorsement","en":"celebrity endorsement"},{"af":"bandwagon","en":"bandwagon"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die advertensie sê *almal doen dit al* – jy wil nie uitgesluit wees nie: dit is die *bandwagon*-tegniek (meeloop-effek). Daar is geen vraag, woordspeling of bekende persoon nie.","en":"The advert says *everyone is already doing it* – you don't want to be left out: that is the *bandwagon* technique. There is no question, pun or famous person."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In raam 2 van 'n strokiesprent is die seun se oë wyd oop, sy mond is 'n groot O en sy hare staan regop. Wat wys dit?","en":"In frame 2 of a comic strip the boy's eyes are wide open, his mouth is a big O and his hair stands straight up. What does this show?"},"options":[{"af":"Hy is verveeld.","en":"He is bored."},{"af":"Hy is geskok of baie verbaas.","en":"He is shocked or very surprised."},{"af":"Hy is vaak.","en":"He is sleepy."},{"af":"Hy is trots.","en":"He is proud."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Wyd oop oë, 'n oop mond en regop hare is 'n tipiese tekenaar se manier om **skok** te wys. 'n Verveelde of vaak karakter sou halfoop oë hê.","en":"Wide eyes, an open mouth and hair standing up are a cartoonist's typical way of showing **shock**. A bored or sleepy character would have half-closed eyes."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die bewering *The tastiest burger in Pretoria!* is 'n feit (*fact*).","en":"The claim *The tastiest burger in Pretoria!* is a fact."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. *Tastiest* is 'n oordeel wat van persoon tot persoon verskil en nie bewys kan word nie – dit is 'n **mening** (*opinion*). 'n Feit sou bv. die prys of die gewig van die burger wees.","en":"False. *Tastiest* is a judgement that differs from person to person and cannot be proved – it is an **opinion**. A fact would be e.g. the price or weight of the burger."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Sinne soos *Buy now!* en *Call today!* is voorbeelde van watter oorredingstegniek? ___ (Engelse term)","en":"Sentences such as *Buy now!* and *Call today!* are examples of which persuasive technique? ___"},"answers":{"af":["imperative","imperatives","command","commands","imperatief","bevel","bevele"],"en":["imperative","imperatives","command","commands"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["rhetorical question","pun","bandwagon"],"en":["rhetorical question","pun","bandwagon"]}},"explain":{"af":"Dit is bevele (*imperatives*): die werkwoord staan voor en sê direk vir die leser wat om te doen – die *Action*-stap van AIDA.","en":"These are commands (*imperatives*): the verb comes first and tells the reader directly what to do – the *Action* step of AIDA."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke deel van 'n advertensie by die regte beskrywing.","en":"Match each part of an advertisement to the correct description."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Logo","en":"Logo"},"r":{"af":"die simbool of ontwerp wat die handelsmerk verteenwoordig","en":"the symbol or design that represents the brand"}},{"l":{"af":"Headline","en":"Headline"},"r":{"af":"die groot opskrif wat eerste die aandag trek","en":"the large heading that catches attention first"}},{"l":{"af":"Body copy","en":"Body copy"},"r":{"af":"die hoofteks met inligting oor die produk","en":"the main text with information about the product"}},{"l":{"af":"Fine print","en":"Fine print"},"r":{"af":"klein teks met bepalings en voorwaardes","en":"small text with terms and conditions"}},{"l":{"af":"Contact details","en":"Contact details"},"r":{"af":"webwerf, telefoonnommer of adres","en":"website, phone number or address"}}],"explain":{"af":"Ken die dele van 'n advertensie uit jou kop: die eksamen vra dikwels *\"Identify the slogan / logo / headline\"* of *\"Why is the fine print important?\"*","en":"Know the parts of an advertisement by heart: the exam often asks *\"Identify the slogan / logo / headline\"* or *\"Why is the fine print important?\"*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoekom staan daar 'n asterisk ná die bewering “Lose 5 kg in one week!*”?","en":"Why is there an asterisk after the claim “Lose 5 kg in one week!*”?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit verwys na die fyn druk, wat die bewering beperk of voorwaardes stel.","en":"It refers to the fine print, which limits the claim or sets conditions."},{"af":"Dit wys dat die bewering 'n bewese feit is.","en":"It shows that the claim is a proven fact."},{"af":"Dit is net 'n versiering om die advertensie mooier te maak.","en":"It is only a decoration to make the advert look nicer."},{"af":"Dit wys dat die produk gratis is.","en":"It shows that the product is free."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die asterisk lei die leser na die fyn druk onderaan, bv. “*Results vary. Only with a strict diet and daily exercise.” Die bewering is dus nie onvoorwaardelik waar nie – wees krities!","en":"The asterisk leads the reader to the fine print at the bottom, e.g. “*Results vary. Only with a strict diet and daily exercise.” So the claim is not true without conditions – be critical!"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie vir 'n aftree-oord in Hartbeespoort wys grys-hare egpare wat rolbal speel. Die opskrif lees: *Your golden years, your way.* Watter antwoord gee die teikenmark met die beste motivering?","en":"An advertisement for a retirement village in Hartbeespoort shows grey-haired couples playing bowls. The headline reads: *Your golden years, your way.* Which answer gives the target market with the best motivation?"},"options":[{"af":"Young families, because the advert shows a sports field.","en":"Young families, because the advert shows a sports field."},{"af":"Teenagers, because bowls is a fun sport.","en":"Teenagers, because bowls is a fun sport."},{"af":"Everyone, because all people like Hartbeespoort.","en":"Everyone, because all people like Hartbeespoort."},{"af":"Retired people (older than about 60), because the couples have grey hair and \"golden years\" refers to old age.","en":"Retired people (older than about 60), because the couples have grey hair and \"golden years\" refers to old age."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie antwoord noem 'n spesifieke groep **en** twee leidrade uit die advertensie (grys hare, *golden years*, 'n aftree-oord). *Everyone* is nooit 'n goeie teikenmark-antwoord nie.","en":"A good answer names a specific group **and** gives clues from the advert (grey hair, *golden years*, a retirement village). *Everyone* is never a good target-market answer."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Watter woord in hierdie slagspreuk is 'n woordspeling (*pun*)? *Brits Bakery – we knead you every day!* ___","en":"Which word in this slogan is a pun? *Brits Bakery – we knead you every day!* ___"},"answers":{"af":["knead"],"en":["knead"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Bakery","every","day"],"en":["Bakery","every","day"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Knead* (deeg knie) klink presies soos *need* (nodig hê): die bakkery knie elke dag deeg, en hulle het jou as klant nodig. Een klank, twee betekenisse – 'n woordspeling.","en":"*Knead* (to work dough) sounds exactly like *need*: the bakery kneads dough every day, and they need you as a customer. One sound, two meanings – a pun."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Skryf in die lydende vorm (*passive voice*): *Thousands of learners love our juice.* → *Our juice ___ by thousands of learners.*","en":"Rewrite in the passive voice: *Thousands of learners love our juice.* → *Our juice ___ by thousands of learners.*"},"answers":{"af":["is loved"],"en":["is loved"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["was loved","are loved","loves"],"en":["was loved","are loved","loves"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die oorspronklike sin is in die eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd, en die nuwe onderwerp *Our juice* is enkelvoud: *is* + voltooide deelwoord *loved*. *Was loved* verander die tyd; *are* pas nie by 'n enkelvoudige onderwerp nie.","en":"The original sentence is in the simple present tense, and the new subject *Our juice* is singular: *is* + past participle *loved*. *Was loved* changes the tense; *are* does not agree with a singular subject."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Strokiesprent: **Raam 1** – 'n bord by 'n gimnasium lees *Get fit! Exercise daily.* **Raam 2** – 'n man ry drie keer om die parkeerterrein om 'n plek reg langs die deur te kry. **Raam 3** – hy neem die roltrap na die gimnasium en sê: *Phew, I'm exhausted!* Hoekom is die laaste raam snaaks?","en":"Comic strip: **Frame 1** – a sign at a gym reads *Get fit! Exercise daily.* **Frame 2** – a man drives around the parking lot three times to find a spot right next to the door. **Frame 3** – he takes the escalator up to the gym and says: *Phew, I'm exhausted!* Why is the last frame funny?"},"options":[{"af":"Because the man's car is very big.","en":"Because the man's car is very big."},{"af":"Because the gym sign has a spelling mistake.","en":"Because the gym sign has a spelling mistake."},{"af":"It is ironic: he is going to the gym to exercise, yet he avoids every bit of walking and then says he is exhausted.","en":"It is ironic: he is going to the gym to exercise, yet he avoids every bit of walking and then says he is exhausted."},{"af":"Because the man is too old to go to the gym.","en":"Because the man is too old to go to the gym."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die humor kom uit **ironie**: die teenoorgestelde van wat verwag word. Iemand wat gaan oefen, behoort graag te loop, maar hy vermy elke tree – en is dan nog moeg ook. Verduidelik altyd die kontras tussen verwagting en werklikheid.","en":"The humour comes from **irony**: the opposite of what is expected. Someone going to exercise should be happy to walk, but he avoids every step – and is still tired. Always explain the contrast between expectation and reality."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie vir 'n energiedrankie sê: *Drink BLITZ and ace every exam! Top learners choose BLITZ.* Watter antwoord evalueer die bewering die beste?","en":"An advertisement for an energy drink says: *Drink BLITZ and ace every exam! Top learners choose BLITZ.* Which answer evaluates the claim best?"},"options":[{"af":"It is misleading: it is an unproven opinion that uses exaggeration (\"every exam\") and a bandwagon appeal (\"Top learners choose\"); a drink cannot replace studying.","en":"It is misleading: it is an unproven opinion that uses exaggeration (\"every exam\") and a bandwagon appeal (\"Top learners choose\"); a drink cannot replace studying."},{"af":"It is true, because it is printed in an advertisement.","en":"It is true, because it is printed in an advertisement."},{"af":"It is a fact, because top learners do exist.","en":"It is a fact, because top learners do exist."},{"af":"It is convincing, because it uses an imperative.","en":"It is convincing, because it uses an imperative."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Evalueringsvraag wil 'n oordeel **met redes** hê. Die beste antwoord noem die tegnieke (oordrywing, meeloop-effek), wys dat daar geen bewys is nie en verduidelik hoekom die bewering onrealisties is. 'n Imperatief maak 'n bewering nie waar nie.","en":"An evaluation question wants a judgement **with reasons**. The best answer names the techniques (exaggeration, bandwagon), shows that there is no proof and explains why the claim is unrealistic. An imperative does not make a claim true."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t3-sentences-punctuation","title":{"af":"Sinsbou, klousules, leestekens en spelling","en":"Sentence structure, clauses, punctuation and spelling"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinsoorte en bysinne kan identifiseer, sinne kan kombineer en voorwaardelik skryf, en leestekens en spelfoute in 'n redigeervraag kan regstel.","en":"You will be able to identify sentence types and clauses, combine sentences and write conditionals, and correct punctuation and spelling errors in an editing question."},"summary":{"af":"## Sinsoorte volgens doel\n\n| Soort | Doel | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Statement (stelling) | gee inligting | *The taxi is late.* |\n| Question (vraag) | vra iets | *Is the taxi late?* |\n| Command (bevel) | gee 'n opdrag | *Close the door.* |\n| Exclamation (uitroep) | wys sterk gevoel | *What a goal!* |\n\n## Sinsoorte volgens bou\n\n- **Simple sentence** (enkelvoudige sin): een hoofsin met een **finite verb** (persoonsvorm): *Thabo plays rugby.*\n- **Compound sentence** (saamgestelde sin, neweskikkend): twee hoofsinne verbind met 'n neweskikkende voegwoord (FANBOYS: *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so*): *Thabo plays rugby, but his sister plays netball.*\n- **Complex sentence** (saamgestelde sin, onderskikkend): 'n hoofsin + 'n bysin: *Thabo plays rugby **because he loves the game**.* Die bysin kan nie alleen staan nie.\n\nDie **subject** (onderwerp) is wie of wat die handeling doen; die **predicate** (gesegde) is die res van die sin, met die werkwoord: *[The old miner] [walked home slowly].* Die **object** (voorwerp) ontvang die handeling: *She kicked **the ball**.*\n\n'n **Phrase** (frase/woordgroep) het **geen** persoonsvorm nie (*after the match*); 'n **clause** (klousule) het 'n onderwerp en 'n persoonsvorm (*after we won the match*).\n\n### Bysinne (subordinate clauses)\n\n| Soort | Werk soos 'n … | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Noun clause | selfstandige naamwoord | *I know **that you are tired**.* |\n| Adjective/relative clause | byvoeglike naamwoord (beskryf 'n naamwoord) | *The boy **who scored** is my cousin.* |\n| Adverb clause | bywoord: tyd, rede, voorwaarde, kontras | ***when** the bell rang*, ***because** it rained*, ***if** you study*, ***although** he was tired* |\n\n**Who** = mense, **which** = diere en dinge, **that** = albei, **whose** = besit.\n\n**Sinne kombineer:** *My uncle works at the mine. He drives a huge truck.* → *My uncle, **who** works at the mine, drives a huge truck.* Of met 'n voegwoord: *It rained, **so** we stayed home.*\n\n### Voorwaardelike sinne (conditional sentences)\n\n- **Moontlik:** *If* + teenwoordige tyd, *will* + werkwoord: *If it rains, we **will** stay home.*\n- **Onwaarskynlik of denkbeeldig:** *If* + verlede tyd, *would* + werkwoord: *If I **had** money, I **would** buy a bakkie.*\n- **Onmoontlik (verlede, net bewustheid):** *If I had studied, I would have passed.*\n\n> **Algemene fout:** *If I will see him, I will tell him.* ✗ → *If I **see** him, I will tell him.* Moenie *will* in die *if*-deel gebruik nie.\n\n### Ontkenning en vrae\n\n- Engels gebruik net **een** ontkenning: *I don't know **anything**.* of *I know **nothing**.* Nie *I don't know nothing* ✗ nie – Afrikaans se dubbele *nie* bestaan nie in Engels. Ander ontkenningswoorde: *never, nobody, nowhere, none*.\n- Vrae en ontkennings in die eenvoudige teenwoordige en verlede tyd gebruik **do/does/did** + die stam: *She lives in Brits.* → *Where **does** she **live**?* *He went home.* → *Did he **go** home?* (nie *Did he went* ✗ nie).\n\n## Leestekens (punctuation)\n\n| Leesteken | Gebruik | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full stop . | einde van 'n stelling of bevel | *The match starts at three.* |\n| Comma , | lyste; ná 'n inleidende bysin; om die aanspreekvorm | *pap, wors and salad*; *When it rains, we stay inside.*; *Sipho, come here.* |\n| Apostrophe ' | samevoeging en besit | *don't*; *the boy's bag*, *the boys' bags* |\n| Colon : | voor 'n lys of verduideliking | *Bring three things: a pen, a ruler and water.* |\n| Semicolon ; | tussen twee verwante hoofsinne | *It was late; we went home.* |\n| Question mark ? / Exclamation mark ! | vraag / sterk gevoel of bevel | *Are you ready? Run!* |\n| Inverted commas \" \" | direkte rede, titels | *\"Let's go,\" said Thabo.* |\n| Hyphen - | saamgestelde woorde | *well-known, twenty-one* |\n| Dash – | skielike breek of byvoeging | *I opened the door – nobody.* |\n| Brackets ( ) | ekstra inligting | *NSFAS (the student aid scheme)* |\n\n**Hoofletters:** name, plekke, dae, maande, tale en titels: *Monday, October, Afrikaans, Dr Mokoena, Hartbeespoort Dam*. Seisoene kry nie hoofletters nie: *winter*.\n\n> **its of it's?** *it's* = *it is* of *it has*; *its* wys besit: *The dog wagged its tail.* Besitlike voornaamwoorde kry nooit 'n apostrof nie: *its, yours, theirs*.\n\n## Spelling\n\n| Woorde | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| their / there / they're | hulle s'n / daar / they are |\n| your / you're | jou / you are |\n| to / too / two | na, om te / ook, te (veel) / twee |\n| affect (v) / effect (n) | beïnvloed / die gevolg |\n| accept / except | aanvaar / behalwe |\n| lose / loose | verloor / los |\n| quiet / quite | stil / nogal, heeltemal |\n| advice (n) / advise (v) | raad / aanraai |\n| practice (n) / practise (v) | oefening / oefen |\n\n- **i before e except after c** (as dit soos *ee* klink): *believe, field, receive, ceiling*. Uitsonderings: *weird, seize*.\n- **Verdubbel die konsonant** ná 'n kort, beklemtoonde klinker: *run → running, stop → stopped, begin → beginning*; maar *rain → raining, open → opened*.\n- Suid-Afrika gebruik **Britse spelling**: *colour, centre, realise, travelled, programme* (nie *color, center, realize* nie).\n- **Afkortings:** *e.g.* (for example), *i.e.* (that is), *etc.* (and so on). **Akronieme** word uit beginletters gevorm: *SAPS* (South African Police Service), *NSFAS* (National Student Financial Aid Scheme).\n\n> **Redigeerwenk:** Soek in 'n redigeervraag elke keer na hoofletters, homofone (*their/there*), *its/it's*, kongruensie, die tyd, dubbele ontkennings en spelling. Herskryf net die fout, tensy die vraag vra dat jy die hele sin herskryf.","en":"## Sentence types by purpose\n\n| Type | Purpose | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Statement | gives information | *The taxi is late.* |\n| Question | asks something | *Is the taxi late?* |\n| Command | gives an instruction | *Close the door.* |\n| Exclamation | shows strong feeling | *What a goal!* |\n\n## Sentence types by structure\n\n- **Simple sentence:** one main clause with one **finite verb**: *Thabo plays rugby.*\n- **Compound sentence:** two main clauses joined by a coordinating conjunction (FANBOYS: *for, and, nor, but, or, yet, so*): *Thabo plays rugby, but his sister plays netball.*\n- **Complex sentence:** a main clause + a subordinate clause: *Thabo plays rugby **because he loves the game**.* The subordinate clause cannot stand on its own.\n\nThe **subject** is who or what does the action; the **predicate** is the rest of the sentence, with the verb: *[The old miner] [walked home slowly].* The **object** receives the action: *She kicked **the ball**.*\n\nA **phrase** has **no** finite verb (*after the match*); a **clause** has a subject and a finite verb (*after we won the match*).\n\n### Subordinate clauses\n\n| Type | Works like a … | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Noun clause | noun | *I know **that you are tired**.* |\n| Adjective/relative clause | adjective (describes a noun) | *The boy **who scored** is my cousin.* |\n| Adverb clause | adverb: time, reason, condition, contrast | ***when** the bell rang*, ***because** it rained*, ***if** you study*, ***although** he was tired* |\n\n**Who** = people, **which** = animals and things, **that** = both, **whose** = possession.\n\n**Combining sentences:** *My uncle works at the mine. He drives a huge truck.* → *My uncle, **who** works at the mine, drives a huge truck.* Or with a conjunction: *It rained, **so** we stayed home.*\n\n### Conditional sentences\n\n- **Possible:** *If* + present tense, *will* + verb: *If it rains, we **will** stay home.*\n- **Unlikely or imaginary:** *If* + past tense, *would* + verb: *If I **had** money, I **would** buy a bakkie.*\n- **Impossible (past, awareness only):** *If I had studied, I would have passed.*\n\n> **Common mistake:** *If I will see him, I will tell him.* ✗ → *If I **see** him, I will tell him.* Don't use *will* in the *if*-part.\n\n### Negation and questions\n\n- English uses only **one** negative: *I don't know **anything**.* or *I know **nothing**.* Not *I don't know nothing* ✗ – the Afrikaans double *nie* does not exist in English. Other negative words: *never, nobody, nowhere, none*.\n- Questions and negatives in the simple present and past tense use **do/does/did** + the base form: *She lives in Brits.* → *Where **does** she **live**?* *He went home.* → *Did he **go** home?* (not *Did he went* ✗).\n\n## Punctuation\n\n| Mark | Use | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full stop . | end of a statement or command | *The match starts at three.* |\n| Comma , | lists; after an introductory clause; around direct address | *pap, wors and salad*; *When it rains, we stay inside.*; *Sipho, come here.* |\n| Apostrophe ' | contraction and possession | *don't*; *the boy's bag*, *the boys' bags* |\n| Colon : | before a list or an explanation | *Bring three things: a pen, a ruler and water.* |\n| Semicolon ; | between two related main clauses | *It was late; we went home.* |\n| Question mark ? / Exclamation mark ! | question / strong feeling or command | *Are you ready? Run!* |\n| Inverted commas \" \" | direct speech, titles | *\"Let's go,\" said Thabo.* |\n| Hyphen - | compound words | *well-known, twenty-one* |\n| Dash – | sudden break or addition | *I opened the door – nobody.* |\n| Brackets ( ) | extra information | *NSFAS (the student aid scheme)* |\n\n**Capital letters:** names, places, days, months, languages and titles: *Monday, October, Afrikaans, Dr Mokoena, Hartbeespoort Dam*. Seasons do not take capitals: *winter*.\n\n> **its or it's?** *it's* = *it is* or *it has*; *its* shows possession: *The dog wagged its tail.* Possessive pronouns never take an apostrophe: *its, yours, theirs*.\n\n## Spelling\n\n| Words | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| their / there / they're | belonging to them / in that place / they are |\n| your / you're | belonging to you / you are |\n| to / too / two | towards, to (verb) / also, too much / 2 |\n| affect (v) / effect (n) | to influence / the result |\n| accept / except | to receive, agree / apart from |\n| lose / loose | to fail to keep / not tight |\n| quiet / quite | silent / fairly, completely |\n| advice (n) / advise (v) | a suggestion / to give a suggestion |\n| practice (n) / practise (v) | training / to train |\n\n- **i before e except after c** (when it sounds like *ee*): *believe, field, receive, ceiling*. Exceptions: *weird, seize*.\n- **Double the consonant** after a short, stressed vowel: *run → running, stop → stopped, begin → beginning*; but *rain → raining, open → opened*.\n- South Africa uses **British spelling**: *colour, centre, realise, travelled, programme* (not *color, center, realize*).\n- **Abbreviations:** *e.g.* (for example), *i.e.* (that is), *etc.* (and so on). **Acronyms** are formed from initial letters: *SAPS* (South African Police Service), *NSFAS* (National Student Financial Aid Scheme).\n\n> **Editing tip:** In an editing question always look for capital letters, homophones (*their/there*), *its/it's*, concord, tense, double negatives and spelling. Rewrite only the error, unless the question asks you to rewrite the whole sentence."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Simple sentence (enkelvoudige sin)","en":"Simple sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met net een hoofsin en een persoonsvorm (finite verb).","en":"A sentence with only one main clause and one finite verb."}},{"term":{"af":"Compound sentence (saamgestelde sin – neweskikkend)","en":"Compound sentence"},"def":{"af":"Twee of meer hoofsinne wat met 'n neweskikkende voegwoord (FANBOYS) verbind is.","en":"Two or more main clauses joined by a coordinating conjunction (FANBOYS)."}},{"term":{"af":"Complex sentence (saamgestelde sin – onderskikkend)","en":"Complex sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met 'n hoofsin en ten minste een bysin wat nie alleen kan staan nie.","en":"A sentence with a main clause and at least one subordinate clause that cannot stand on its own."}},{"term":{"af":"Clause (klousule)","en":"Clause"},"def":{"af":"'n Woordgroep met 'n onderwerp en 'n persoonsvorm, bv. *because it rained*.","en":"A group of words with a subject and a finite verb, e.g. *because it rained*."}},{"term":{"af":"Phrase (frase/woordgroep)","en":"Phrase"},"def":{"af":"'n Woordgroep sonder 'n persoonsvorm, bv. *after the match*.","en":"A group of words without a finite verb, e.g. *after the match*."}},{"term":{"af":"Subject and predicate (onderwerp en gesegde)","en":"Subject and predicate"},"def":{"af":"Die onderwerp is wie of wat die handeling doen; die gesegde is die res van die sin, insluitend die werkwoord.","en":"The subject is who or what does the action; the predicate is the rest of the sentence, including the verb."}},{"term":{"af":"Relative pronoun (betreklike voornaamwoord)","en":"Relative pronoun"},"def":{"af":"*Who, whom, whose, which, that* – begin 'n byvoeglike bysin en verbind twee sinne.","en":"*Who, whom, whose, which, that* – begins an adjective clause and joins two sentences."}},{"term":{"af":"Conditional sentence (voorwaardelike sin)","en":"Conditional sentence"},"def":{"af":"'n Sin met 'n *if*-deel wat 'n voorwaarde stel: *If it rains, we will stay home.*","en":"A sentence with an *if*-part that sets a condition: *If it rains, we will stay home.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Double negative (dubbele ontkenning)","en":"Double negative"},"def":{"af":"Twee ontkennings in een Engelse sin (*don't … nothing*); dit is foutief in Standaardengels.","en":"Two negatives in one English sentence (*don't … nothing*); it is incorrect in Standard English."}},{"term":{"af":"Homophones (homofone)","en":"Homophones"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat dieselfde klink maar verskillend gespel word en iets anders beteken, bv. *their/there/they're*.","en":"Words that sound the same but are spelt differently and mean different things, e.g. *their/there/they're*."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Identifiseer die sinsoort","en":"Identify the type of sentence"},"problem":{"af":"Is elke sin *simple*, *compound* of *complex*? Gee 'n rede.\n\n(a) Although the taxi was late, we arrived on time.\n(b) The power went off, so we lit a candle.\n(c) After the match the team ate boerewors rolls.","en":"Is each sentence *simple*, *compound* or *complex*? Give a reason.\n\n(a) Although the taxi was late, we arrived on time.\n(b) The power went off, so we lit a candle.\n(c) After the match the team ate boerewors rolls."},"steps":[{"af":"**Metode:** onderstreep elke persoonsvorm (finite verb) en kyk dan watter soort voegwoord die klousules verbind.","en":"**Method:** underline every finite verb, then check what kind of conjunction joins the clauses."},{"af":"(a) Twee persoonsvorme: *was*, *arrived*. *Although the taxi was late* kan nie alleen staan nie – dit is 'n bywoordelike bysin van kontras. Hoofsin + bysin = **complex**.","en":"(a) Two finite verbs: *was*, *arrived*. *Although the taxi was late* cannot stand alone – it is an adverb clause of contrast. Main clause + subordinate clause = **complex**."},{"af":"(b) Twee persoonsvorme: *went*, *lit*. Albei dele kan alleen staan, en *so* is 'n FANBOYS-voegwoord. Twee hoofsinne = **compound**.","en":"(b) Two finite verbs: *went*, *lit*. Both parts can stand alone, and *so* is a FANBOYS conjunction. Two main clauses = **compound**."},{"af":"(c) Net een persoonsvorm: *ate*. *After the match* het geen werkwoord nie – dit is 'n **frase**, nie 'n klousule nie. Een hoofsin = **simple**.","en":"(c) Only one finite verb: *ate*. *After the match* has no verb – it is a **phrase**, not a clause. One main clause = **simple**."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Complex – main clause + adverb clause of contrast (although …). (b) Compound – two main clauses joined by \"so\". (c) Simple – only one finite verb (\"ate\"); \"After the match\" is a phrase.","en":"(a) Complex – main clause + adverb clause of contrast (although …). (b) Compound – two main clauses joined by \"so\". (c) Simple – only one finite verb (\"ate\"); \"After the match\" is a phrase."}},{"title":{"af":"Sinne kombineer en 'n voorwaardelike sin skryf","en":"Combining sentences and writing a conditional"},"problem":{"af":"(a) Combine using a relative pronoun: *The girl won the debate. Her father is a teacher.*\n(b) Combine using \"although\": *It was cold. We swam in the dam.*\n(c) Rewrite as ONE conditional sentence: *I don't have a ticket. I can't go to the concert.*","en":"(a) Combine using a relative pronoun: *The girl won the debate. Her father is a teacher.*\n(b) Combine using \"although\": *It was cold. We swam in the dam.*\n(c) Rewrite as ONE conditional sentence: *I don't have a ticket. I can't go to the concert.*"},"steps":[{"af":"(a) *Her* wys besit, dus gebruik ons **whose**. Plaas die bysin reg ná die naamwoord wat dit beskryf (*The girl*): **The girl whose father is a teacher won the debate.**","en":"(a) *Her* shows possession, so we use **whose**. Place the clause right after the noun it describes (*The girl*): **The girl whose father is a teacher won the debate.**"},{"af":"(b) *Although* wys kontras en begin die bysin. As die bysin eerste staan, kom 'n komma daarna: **Although it was cold, we swam in the dam.**","en":"(b) *Although* shows contrast and starts the subordinate clause. When the clause comes first, a comma follows it: **Although it was cold, we swam in the dam.**"},{"af":"(c) Die situasie is nie waar nie (ek het nie 'n kaartjie nie), dus gebruik ons die **onwaarskynlike** voorwaarde: *If* + verlede tyd, *would/could* + werkwoord. Die ontkennings verdwyn: **If I had a ticket, I could go to the concert.**","en":"(c) The situation is not true (I don't have a ticket), so we use the **unlikely** conditional: *If* + past tense, *would/could* + verb. The negatives disappear: **If I had a ticket, I could go to the concert.**"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) The girl whose father is a teacher won the debate. (b) Although it was cold, we swam in the dam. (c) If I had a ticket, I could (would be able to) go to the concert.","en":"(a) The girl whose father is a teacher won the debate. (b) Although it was cold, we swam in the dam. (c) If I had a ticket, I could (would be able to) go to the concert."}},{"title":{"af":"Redigering: verbeter vyf foute","en":"Editing: correct five errors"},"problem":{"af":"Die paragraaf het **vyf** foute. Identifiseer en verbeter elkeen.\n\n*Last saturday my cousin and I took a taxi to Hartbeespoort. Their was so much traffic that we arrived late. My cousin's fishing rod lost it's hook in the reeds. We didn't catch nothing, but the sunset was to beautiful for us to complain.*","en":"The paragraph has **five** errors. Identify and correct each one.\n\n*Last saturday my cousin and I took a taxi to Hartbeespoort. Their was so much traffic that we arrived late. My cousin's fishing rod lost it's hook in the reeds. We didn't catch nothing, but the sunset was to beautiful for us to complain.*"},"steps":[{"af":"Fout 1 – **hoofletter**: dae van die week kry hoofletters: *saturday* → **Saturday**.","en":"Error 1 – **capital letter**: days of the week take capitals: *saturday* → **Saturday**."},{"af":"Fout 2 – **homofoon**: dit gaan oor 'n plek/bestaan, nie besit nie: *Their* → **There**.","en":"Error 2 – **homophone**: this is about existence/place, not possession: *Their* → **There**."},{"af":"Fout 3 – **its/it's**: die haak behoort aan die stok (besit), en *it is* maak nie sin nie: *it's* → **its**.","en":"Error 3 – **its/it's**: the hook belongs to the rod (possession), and *it is* makes no sense: *it's* → **its**."},{"af":"Fout 4 – **dubbele ontkenning**: *didn't catch nothing* → **didn't catch anything** (of *caught nothing*).","en":"Error 4 – **double negative**: *didn't catch nothing* → **didn't catch anything** (or *caught nothing*)."},{"af":"Fout 5 – **homofoon**: hier beteken dit *te* (te veel): *to beautiful* → **too beautiful**.","en":"Error 5 – **homophone**: here it means *excessively*: *to beautiful* → **too beautiful**."}],"answer":{"af":"1. saturday → Saturday  2. Their → There  3. it's → its  4. didn't catch nothing → didn't catch anything  5. to → too","en":"1. saturday → Saturday  2. Their → There  3. it's → its  4. didn't catch nothing → didn't catch anything  5. to → too"}},{"title":{"af":"Voeg die leestekens in","en":"Insert the punctuation"},"problem":{"af":"Herskryf die sin met die korrekte leestekens en hoofletters:\n\n*lets go said thabo bring your towel sunscreen and a hat sipho*","en":"Rewrite the sentence with the correct punctuation and capital letters:\n\n*lets go said thabo bring your towel sunscreen and a hat sipho*"},"steps":[{"af":"Soek die **direkte rede**: Thabo sê twee dinge – *Let's go* en *Bring your towel …*. Plaas elkeen tussen aanhalingstekens.","en":"Find the **direct speech**: Thabo says two things – *Let's go* and *Bring your towel …*. Put each in inverted commas."},{"af":"**Apostrof**: *lets* = *let us*, dus **Let's**. **Hoofletters**: die eerste woord van die aanhaling, en die name **Thabo** en **Sipho**.","en":"**Apostrophe**: *lets* = *let us*, so **Let's**. **Capital letters**: the first word of the quotation, and the names **Thabo** and **Sipho**."},{"af":"**Komma** binne die aanhalingstekens voor *said Thabo*; dan 'n **punt** ná *Thabo*, want 'n nuwe sin begin.","en":"**Comma** inside the inverted commas before *said Thabo*; then a **full stop** after *Thabo*, because a new sentence starts."},{"af":"**Lyskommas**: *towel, sunscreen and a hat* (geen komma voor *and* nie). **Aanspreekvorm**: 'n komma voor *Sipho*. Eindig met 'n punt binne die aanhalingstekens.","en":"**List commas**: *towel, sunscreen and a hat* (no comma before *and*). **Direct address**: a comma before *Sipho*. End with a full stop inside the inverted commas."}],"answer":{"af":"\"Let's go,\" said Thabo. \"Bring your towel, sunscreen and a hat, Sipho.\"","en":"\"Let's go,\" said Thabo. \"Bring your towel, sunscreen and a hat, Sipho.\""}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is 'n bevel (*command*)?","en":"Which sentence is a command?"},"options":[{"af":"The bus leaves at seven.","en":"The bus leaves at seven."},{"af":"Does the bus leave at seven?","en":"Does the bus leave at seven?"},{"af":"Be at the bus stop by seven.","en":"Be at the bus stop by seven."},{"af":"What a long trip it was!","en":"What a long trip it was!"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Bevel gee 'n opdrag en begin dikwels met die werkwoord (*Be …*). Die ander is 'n stelling, 'n vraag en 'n uitroep.","en":"A command gives an instruction and often starts with the verb (*Be …*). The others are a statement, a question and an exclamation."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"'n Frase (*phrase*) bevat altyd 'n onderwerp en 'n persoonsvorm (*finite verb*).","en":"A phrase always contains a subject and a finite verb."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. 'n **Klousule** het 'n onderwerp en 'n persoonsvorm (*after we won*); 'n **frase** het nie (*after the match*).","en":"False. A **clause** has a subject and a finite verb (*after we won*); a **phrase** does not (*after the match*)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Kies die regte woord (*their / there / they're*): ___ going to the braai on Saturday.","en":"Choose the correct word (*their / there / they're*): ___ going to the braai on Saturday."},"answers":{"af":["They're","They are"],"en":["They're","They are"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["Their","There","Thier"],"en":["Their","There","Thier"]}},"explain":{"af":"*They're* = *they are*: *They are going to the braai.* *Their* wys besit (*their car*) en *there* 'n plek (*over there*). *Thier* is 'n spelfout.","en":"*They're* = *they are*: *They are going to the braai.* *Their* shows possession (*their car*) and *there* a place (*over there*). *Thier* is a spelling mistake."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie woorde kry **nie** 'n hoofletter in 'n Engelse sin nie?","en":"Which one of these words does **not** take a capital letter in an English sentence?"},"options":[{"af":"monday","en":"monday"},{"af":"afrikaans","en":"afrikaans"},{"af":"october","en":"october"},{"af":"winter","en":"winter"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Seisoene (*winter, summer*) is gewone naamwoorde. Dae (*Monday*), maande (*October*) en tale (*Afrikaans*) kry in Engels altyd hoofletters – anders as in Afrikaans, waar *maandag* en *oktober* klein geskryf word.","en":"Seasons (*winter, summer*) are common nouns. Days (*Monday*), months (*October*) and languages (*Afrikaans*) always take capitals in English – unlike in Afrikaans, where *maandag* and *oktober* are written in lower case."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"*I wanted to swim, but the water was too cold.* Dit is 'n ___ sin. (*simple / compound / complex*)","en":"*I wanted to swim, but the water was too cold.* This is a ___ sentence. (*simple / compound / complex*)"},"answers":{"af":["compound","neweskikkende"],"en":["compound"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["simple","complex","conditional"],"en":["simple","complex","conditional"]}},"explain":{"af":"Twee hoofsinne (*I wanted to swim* / *the water was too cold*) wat albei alleen kan staan, verbind deur die FANBOYS-voegwoord *but*: 'n *compound sentence*.","en":"Two main clauses (*I wanted to swim* / *the water was too cold*) that can both stand alone, joined by the FANBOYS conjunction *but*: a *compound sentence*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat is die volledige onderwerp (*complete subject*) van hierdie sin? *The old man with the grey hat sells oranges at the taxi rank.*","en":"What is the complete subject of this sentence? *The old man with the grey hat sells oranges at the taxi rank.*"},"options":[{"af":"The old man","en":"The old man"},{"af":"The old man with the grey hat","en":"The old man with the grey hat"},{"af":"sells oranges at the taxi rank","en":"sells oranges at the taxi rank"},{"af":"oranges","en":"oranges"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Vra: *Wie verkoop lemoene?* – *The old man with the grey hat*. Die frase *with the grey hat* hoort by die onderwerp. *sells oranges at the taxi rank* is die gesegde, en *oranges* is die voorwerp.","en":"Ask: *Who sells oranges?* – *The old man with the grey hat*. The phrase *with the grey hat* belongs to the subject. *sells oranges at the taxi rank* is the predicate, and *oranges* is the object."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vul *its* of *it's* in: *The school changed ___ uniform this year.*","en":"Fill in *its* or *it's*: *The school changed ___ uniform this year.*"},"answers":{"af":["its"],"en":["its"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["it's","its'","it is"],"en":["it's","its'","it is"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die uniform behoort aan die skool – besit – dus *its* sonder 'n apostrof. Toets: *The school changed it is uniform* maak nie sin nie. *its'* bestaan nie.","en":"The uniform belongs to the school – possession – so *its* without an apostrophe. Test: *The school changed it is uniform* makes no sense. *its'* does not exist."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"*We stayed inside because it was raining.* Watter soort bysin is *because it was raining*?","en":"*We stayed inside because it was raining.* What type of clause is *because it was raining*?"},"options":[{"af":"adverb clause of reason","en":"adverb clause of reason"},{"af":"noun clause","en":"noun clause"},{"af":"adjective (relative) clause","en":"adjective (relative) clause"},{"af":"adverb clause of time","en":"adverb clause of time"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dit sê **hoekom** ons binne gebly het en begin met *because*: 'n bywoordelike bysin van rede. 'n Tydsbysin sou met *when/after/before* begin, en 'n byvoeglike bysin met *who/which/that*.","en":"It says **why** we stayed inside and starts with *because*: an adverb clause of reason. A clause of time would start with *when/after/before*, and an adjective clause with *who/which/that*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Die sin *I don't know nothing about the test.* is korrekte Standaardengels.","en":"The sentence *I don't know nothing about the test.* is correct Standard English."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar – dit is 'n dubbele ontkenning. Korrek: *I don't know anything about the test.* of *I know nothing about the test.*","en":"False – it is a double negative. Correct: *I don't know anything about the test.* or *I know nothing about the test.*"}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke leesteken by sy gebruik.","en":"Match each punctuation mark to its use."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Colon ( : )","en":"Colon ( : )"},"r":{"af":"lei 'n lys of verduideliking in","en":"introduces a list or an explanation"}},{"l":{"af":"Semicolon ( ; )","en":"Semicolon ( ; )"},"r":{"af":"verbind twee nou verwante hoofsinne","en":"joins two closely related main clauses"}},{"l":{"af":"Hyphen ( - )","en":"Hyphen ( - )"},"r":{"af":"verbind woorde tot 'n samestelling, bv. well-known","en":"joins words into a compound, e.g. well-known"}},{"l":{"af":"Apostrophe ( ' )","en":"Apostrophe ( ' )"},"r":{"af":"wys besit of 'n samevoeging","en":"shows possession or a contraction"}},{"l":{"af":"Brackets ( )","en":"Brackets ( )"},"r":{"af":"bevat ekstra inligting","en":"contain extra information"}}],"explain":{"af":"Onthou: die dubbelpunt *kondig aan*, die kommapunt *verbind*, die koppelteken *koppel woorde*, die apostrof wys *besit of weglating* en hakies bevat *bykomende inligting*.","en":"Remember: the colon *announces*, the semicolon *links*, the hyphen *joins words*, the apostrophe shows *possession or omission* and brackets hold *additional information*."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak 'n vraag van die sin: *She lives in Brits.* → *Where ___ she live?*","en":"Turn the sentence into a question: *She lives in Brits.* → *Where ___ she live?*"},"answers":{"af":["does"],"en":["does"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["do","is","has"],"en":["do","is","has"]}},"explain":{"af":"Eenvoudige teenwoordige tyd + derde persoon enkelvoud (*she*) → *does* + stam: *Where does she live?* Die *-s* van *lives* skuif na *does*.","en":"Simple present tense + third person singular (*she*) → *does* + base form: *Where does she live?* The *-s* of *lives* moves to *does*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Verbind die sinne met 'n betreklike voornaamwoord: *My uncle works at the mine. He drives a huge truck.*","en":"Combine the sentences using a relative pronoun: *My uncle works at the mine. He drives a huge truck.*"},"options":[{"af":"My uncle, which works at the mine, drives a huge truck.","en":"My uncle, which works at the mine, drives a huge truck."},{"af":"My uncle, whose works at the mine, drives a huge truck.","en":"My uncle, whose works at the mine, drives a huge truck."},{"af":"My uncle works at the mine, he drives a huge truck.","en":"My uncle works at the mine, he drives a huge truck."},{"af":"My uncle, who works at the mine, drives a huge truck.","en":"My uncle, who works at the mine, drives a huge truck."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Vir 'n persoon gebruik ons *who* (nie *which* nie). *Whose* wys besit. *My uncle works at the mine, he drives …* verbind twee hoofsinne net met 'n komma – dit is 'n fout (*comma splice*).","en":"For a person we use *who* (not *which*). *Whose* shows possession. *My uncle works at the mine, he drives …* joins two main clauses with only a comma – that is an error (*comma splice*)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voltooi die voorwaardelike sin: *If I ___ (have) more money, I would buy a new phone.*","en":"Complete the conditional sentence: *If I ___ (have) more money, I would buy a new phone.*"},"answers":{"af":["had"],"en":["had"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["have","has","will have"],"en":["have","has","will have"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Would* in die hoofsin wys 'n onwaarskynlike of denkbeeldige situasie, dus kom die *if*-deel in die verlede tyd: *If I had …, I would …*","en":"*Would* in the main clause shows an unlikely or imaginary situation, so the *if*-part is in the past tense: *If I had …, I would …*"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is korrek gespel?","en":"Which sentence is spelt correctly?"},"options":[{"af":"My coach gave me some good advise.","en":"My coach gave me some good advise."},{"af":"I must practise my speech tonight.","en":"I must practise my speech tonight."},{"af":"The noise did not effect my concentration.","en":"The noise did not effect my concentration."},{"af":"Everyone accept Sipho passed the test.","en":"Everyone accept Sipho passed the test."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Practise* is die werkwoord (Britse spelling). Die ander moet wees: *advice* (naamwoord), *affect* (werkwoord) en *except* (behalwe).","en":"*Practise* is the verb (British spelling). The others should be: *advice* (noun), *affect* (verb) and *except* (apart from)."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter is die korrekte weergawe van *Me and him has never been to the dam before.*?","en":"Which is the correct version of *Me and him has never been to the dam before.*?"},"options":[{"af":"Me and him have never been to the dam before.","en":"Me and him have never been to the dam before."},{"af":"He and I has never been to the dam before.","en":"He and I has never been to the dam before."},{"af":"He and I have never been to the dam before.","en":"He and I have never been to the dam before."},{"af":"Him and I have never been to the dam before.","en":"Him and I have never been to the dam before."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Daar is twee foute. (1) Die onderwerp vra onderwerpsvorme: *he* en *I* (nie *me/him* nie), en beleefdheidshalwe kom *I* laaste. (2) 'n Meervoudige onderwerp (*He and I*) kry *have*, nie *has* nie.","en":"There are two errors. (1) The subject needs subject forms: *he* and *I* (not *me/him*), and politely *I* comes last. (2) A plural subject (*He and I*) takes *have*, not *has*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een van hierdie sinne is 'n *complex sentence*?","en":"Which one of these sentences is a complex sentence?"},"options":[{"af":"The boy who won the race is my cousin.","en":"The boy who won the race is my cousin."},{"af":"I ran fast and I won the race.","en":"I ran fast and I won the race."},{"af":"After the race, we ate pap and wors.","en":"After the race, we ate pap and wors."},{"af":"Run faster!","en":"Run faster!"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*The boy who won the race is my cousin* het 'n hoofsin (*The boy is my cousin*) en 'n byvoeglike bysin (*who won the race*) – complex. *I ran fast and I won the race* is compound (twee hoofsinne + *and*). *After the race, we ate pap and wors* is simple: *After the race* is 'n frase sonder werkwoord. *Run faster!* is 'n eenvoudige bevel.","en":"*The boy who won the race is my cousin* has a main clause (*The boy is my cousin*) and an adjective clause (*who won the race*) – complex. *I ran fast and I won the race* is compound (two main clauses + *and*). *After the race, we ate pap and wors* is simple: *After the race* is a phrase without a verb. *Run faster!* is a simple command."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t3-transactional-texts","title":{"af":"Ander transaksionele tekste","en":"Other transactional texts"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal die formaat, register en toon van dialoë, toesprake, berigte, resensies, verslae, doodsberigte en korter tekste ken en dit uit 'n scenario kan skryf.","en":"You will know the format, register and tone of dialogues, speeches, reports, reviews, formal reports, obituaries and shorter texts, and be able to write them from a scenario."},"summary":{"af":"## Transaksionele tekste in Vraestel 3\n\n| Afdeling | Punte | Lengte (Gr 10) |\n|---|---|---|\n| B: langer transaksionele teks | 30 | 120–150 woorde (die liggaam) |\n| C: korter teks | 20 | 80–100 woorde |\n\n**Nasien:** eers **inhoud, beplanning en formaat** (die meeste punte), dan **taal, styl en redigering**. 'n Teks in die verkeerde formaat verloor dus baie punte, al is die taal goed. Lees die scenario noukeurig: **wie** skryf, **aan wie** en **hoekom**? Dit bepaal die **register** (formeel of informeel) en die **toon**.\n\n> **Wenk:** Beplan kortliks met sleutelwoorde, skryf die teks, lees dit oor en gee die woordetal as die vraag dit vra.\n\n## Langer tekste (Afdeling B)\n\n### Dialogue (dialoog)\n- Die spreker se naam staan **links**, gevolg deur 'n **dubbelpunt**: *Thabo: …*\n- **Geen aanhalingstekens** nie.\n- **Toneelaanwysings** staan tussen **hakies**, in die teenwoordige tyd: *(looks at his watch)*.\n- Elke spreker begin op 'n nuwe reël; die gesprek het 'n duidelike doel en 'n einde.\n\n### Interview (onderhoud)\nSoos 'n dialoog, maar die onderhoudvoerder stel vrae en die ander persoon antwoord volledig. Begin met 'n kort inleiding: wie, waar en hoekom.\n\n### Speech (toespraak)\n- **Groet die gehoor**: *Good morning, Principal, teachers and fellow learners.*\n- 'n **Hoek** (*hook*): 'n vraag, 'n treffende feit of 'n kort storie.\n- Twee of drie duidelike punte; **retoriese vrae** en **direkte aanspreek** (*you, we*) betrek die gehoor.\n- 'n Slot wat opsom of tot aksie oproep, en **bedank die gehoor**.\n\n### Newspaper report (koerantberig)\n- **Headline** (opskrif): kort en pakkend.\n- **Byline** (*By Thandi Mokoena*) en **plek en datum** (*BRITS, 19 October 2026 –*).\n- Die eerste paragraaf beantwoord die **5 W's + H**: *who, what, when, where, why, how*.\n- **Derde persoon, verlede tyd**, objektief (geen eie mening nie), met **aanhalings** van ooggetuies.\n\n### Magazine article (tydskrifartikel)\n'n Pakkende titel, dikwels met 'n subtitel; lewendiger en persoonliker as 'n berig; spreek die leser direk aan; paragrawe met subopskrifte.\n\n### Review (resensie)\n- Besonderhede: titel, skrywer/regisseur of restaurant, genre, plek of prys.\n- 'n Kort **opsomming sonder om die einde te verklap** (*no spoilers*).\n- **Evaluering**: sterk en swak punte, met redes.\n- 'n **Gradering** (*rating*), bv. 4/5 of ★★★★☆.\n\n### Report (formele verslag)\n**Titel**, **opdrag/doel** (*terms of reference*: wie het die verslag gevra en hoekom), **bevindinge** (*findings*), **aanbevelings** (*recommendations*), en **naam, pos en datum**. Formeel en objektief, met opskrifte of nommers.\n\n### Obituary (doodsberig)\n**Volle naam**, **geboorte- en sterfdatum**, die persoon se lewe en **prestasies**, die **familie** wat agterbly en die **begrafnis- of gedenkdiens** se besonderhede. Die toon is respekvol; eufemismes soos *passed away* is gepas.\n\n## Korter tekste (Afdeling C)\n\n| Teks | Formaat en kenmerke |\n|---|---|\n| Advertisement (advertensie) | opskrif, produk, voordele, prys, kontakbesonderhede, slagspreuk |\n| Diary entry (dagboekinskrywing) | datum (en tyd), *Dear Diary*, **eerste persoon**, gevoelens en nadenke, informeel |\n| Poster/flyer (plakkaat/strooibiljet) | net teks: groot opskrif, kort frases, wat/wanneer/waar, kontak |\n| Invitation (uitnodiging) | **wie** nooi, **wat**, **wanneer** (datum en tyd), **waar**, **RSVP** (antwoord asseblief – met 'n datum en nommer) |\n| Directions (aanwysings) | beginpunt, **volgorde**, **landmerke**, **afstande**, links/regs |\n| Instructions (instruksies) | titel, wat jy nodig het, **genommerde stappe** wat met 'n **imperatief** begin (*Mix …, Pour …*) |\n| Postcard (poskaart) | datum, groet, kort informele boodskap, ontvanger se adres regs |\n| E-mail (e-pos) | **To**, **Subject**, groet, kort paragrawe, afsluiting en naam |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Leerders skryf 'n koerantberig in die eerste persoon met hul eie gevoelens, of gebruik aanhalingstekens in 'n dialoog. Ken die formaat van elke teks uit jou kop.\n\n## Register en toon\n\n- **Formeel** (skoolhoof, maatskappy, koerant): volsinne, geen samevoegings nie (*do not*, nie *don't*), geen sleng of SMS-taal nie (*you*, nie *u*).\n- **Informeel** (vriend, dagboek, poskaart): gesellig en persoonlik; samevoegings mag, maar spelling en grammatika bly korrek.\n- Die toon pas by die doel: entoesiasties (plakkaat), respekvol (doodsberig), oortuigend (toespraak), objektief (verslag en berig).","en":"## Transactional texts in Paper 3\n\n| Section | Marks | Length (Gr 10) |\n|---|---|---|\n| B: longer transactional text | 30 | 120–150 words (the body) |\n| C: shorter text | 20 | 80–100 words |\n\n**Marking:** first **content, planning and format** (most of the marks), then **language, style and editing**. A text in the wrong format therefore loses many marks, even if the language is good. Read the scenario carefully: **who** is writing, **to whom** and **why**? This decides the **register** (formal or informal) and the **tone**.\n\n> **Tip:** Plan briefly with key words, write the text, read it over and give the word count if the question asks for it.\n\n## Longer texts (Section B)\n\n### Dialogue\n- The speaker's name is on the **left**, followed by a **colon**: *Thabo: …*\n- **No inverted commas.**\n- **Stage directions** go in **brackets**, in the present tense: *(looks at his watch)*.\n- Each speaker starts on a new line; the conversation has a clear purpose and an ending.\n\n### Interview\nLike a dialogue, but the interviewer asks questions and the other person answers fully. Start with a short introduction: who, where and why.\n\n### Speech\n- **Greet the audience**: *Good morning, Principal, teachers and fellow learners.*\n- A **hook**: a question, a striking fact or a short story.\n- Two or three clear points; **rhetorical questions** and **direct address** (*you, we*) involve the audience.\n- A conclusion that sums up or calls to action, and **thank the audience**.\n\n### Newspaper report\n- **Headline**: short and catchy.\n- **Byline** (*By Thandi Mokoena*) and **place and date** (*BRITS, 19 October 2026 –*).\n- The first paragraph answers the **5 Ws + H**: *who, what, when, where, why, how*.\n- **Third person, past tense**, objective (no personal opinion), with **quotations** from eyewitnesses.\n\n### Magazine article\nA catchy title, often with a subtitle; livelier and more personal than a report; addresses the reader directly; paragraphs with subheadings.\n\n### Review\n- Details: title, author/director or restaurant, genre, place or price.\n- A short **summary without giving away the ending** (*no spoilers*).\n- **Evaluation**: strengths and weaknesses, with reasons.\n- A **rating**, e.g. 4/5 or ★★★★☆.\n\n### Report (formal)\n**Title**, **terms of reference/purpose** (who asked for the report and why), **findings**, **recommendations**, and **name, position and date**. Formal and objective, with headings or numbers.\n\n### Obituary\n**Full name**, **dates of birth and death**, the person's life and **achievements**, the **family** left behind and the details of the **funeral or memorial service**. The tone is respectful; euphemisms such as *passed away* are appropriate.\n\n## Shorter texts (Section C)\n\n| Text | Format and features |\n|---|---|\n| Advertisement | headline, product, benefits, price, contact details, slogan |\n| Diary entry | date (and time), *Dear Diary*, **first person**, feelings and reflection, informal |\n| Poster/flyer | text only: big heading, short phrases, what/when/where, contact |\n| Invitation | **who** is inviting, **what**, **when** (date and time), **where**, **RSVP** (please reply – with a date and number) |\n| Directions | starting point, **sequence**, **landmarks**, **distances**, left/right |\n| Instructions | title, what you need, **numbered steps** that start with an **imperative** (*Mix …, Pour …*) |\n| Postcard | date, greeting, short informal message, recipient's address on the right |\n| E-mail | **To**, **Subject**, greeting, short paragraphs, closing and name |\n\n> **Common mistake:** Learners write a newspaper report in the first person with their own feelings, or use inverted commas in a dialogue. Know the format of every text by heart.\n\n## Register and tone\n\n- **Formal** (principal, company, newspaper): full sentences, no contractions (*do not*, not *don't*), no slang or SMS language (*you*, not *u*).\n- **Informal** (friend, diary, postcard): friendly and personal; contractions are allowed, but spelling and grammar stay correct.\n- The tone suits the purpose: enthusiastic (poster), respectful (obituary), persuasive (speech), objective (report and newspaper report)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Transactional text (transaksionele teks)","en":"Transactional text"},"def":{"af":"'n Funksionele teks met 'n praktiese doel en 'n vaste formaat, bv. 'n brief, berig, uitnodiging of e-pos.","en":"A functional text with a practical purpose and a fixed format, e.g. a letter, report, invitation or e-mail."}},{"term":{"af":"Format (formaat)","en":"Format"},"def":{"af":"Die vaste uitleg en kenmerke van 'n teks, bv. die opskrif en byline van 'n berig of die name en dubbelpunte van 'n dialoog.","en":"The fixed layout and features of a text, e.g. the headline and byline of a report or the names and colons of a dialogue."}},{"term":{"af":"Register (register)","en":"Register"},"def":{"af":"Die vlak van formaliteit van taal – formeel of informeel – wat by die leser en die doel pas.","en":"The level of formality of language – formal or informal – that suits the reader and the purpose."}},{"term":{"af":"Stage directions (toneelaanwysings)","en":"Stage directions"},"def":{"af":"Aanwysings tussen hakies in 'n dialoog wat wys hoe 'n karakter praat of beweeg, bv. *(sighs)*.","en":"Instructions in brackets in a dialogue that show how a character speaks or moves, e.g. *(sighs)*."}},{"term":{"af":"Byline (byline)","en":"Byline"},"def":{"af":"Die reël onder die opskrif van 'n koerantberig wat die joernalis se naam gee.","en":"The line under the headline of a newspaper report that gives the journalist's name."}},{"term":{"af":"5 Ws + H","en":"5 Ws + H"},"def":{"af":"*Who, what, when, where, why* en *how*: die inligting wat die eerste paragraaf van 'n koerantberig moet gee.","en":"*Who, what, when, where, why* and *how*: the information the first paragraph of a newspaper report must give."}},{"term":{"af":"Review (resensie)","en":"Review"},"def":{"af":"'n Teks wat 'n boek, film of restaurant beskryf en evalueer, met 'n gradering en sonder om die einde te verklap.","en":"A text that describes and evaluates a book, film or restaurant, with a rating and without giving away the ending."}},{"term":{"af":"Terms of reference (opdrag)","en":"Terms of reference"},"def":{"af":"Die deel van 'n formele verslag wat sê wie die verslag gevra het en wat ondersoek moes word.","en":"The part of a formal report that states who asked for the report and what had to be investigated."}},{"term":{"af":"RSVP","en":"RSVP"},"def":{"af":"Uit Frans *répondez s'il vous plaît* – \"antwoord asseblief\": laat die gasheer teen 'n sekere datum weet of jy kom.","en":"From French *répondez s'il vous plaît* – \"please reply\": let the host know by a certain date whether you are coming."}},{"term":{"af":"Obituary (doodsberig)","en":"Obituary"},"def":{"af":"'n Respekvolle teks wat iemand se dood aankondig en sy of haar lewe, prestasies, familie en begrafnisbesonderhede gee.","en":"A respectful text that announces someone's death and gives his or her life, achievements, family and funeral details."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n dialoog","en":"Write a dialogue"},"problem":{"af":"**Scenario:** You want your friend to join the hiking club on Saturday, but he would rather watch the rugby final on TV. Write the dialogue between the two of you. (120–150 words)","en":"**Scenario:** You want your friend to join the hiking club on Saturday, but he would rather watch the rugby final on TV. Write the dialogue between the two of you. (120–150 words)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Beplan:** wie praat (Lerato en Sipho), wat is die konflik (stap of rugby) en hoe eindig dit (Sipho stem in, want hy kan die finaal steeds kyk)?","en":"**Plan:** who speaks (Lerato and Sipho), what is the conflict (hiking or rugby) and how does it end (Sipho agrees, because he can still watch the final)?"},{"af":"**Formaat:** name links met 'n dubbelpunt, elke spreker op 'n nuwe reël, **geen aanhalingstekens** nie.","en":"**Format:** names on the left with a colon, each speaker on a new line, **no inverted commas**."},{"af":"**Toneelaanwysings** tussen hakies in die teenwoordige tyd wys toon en lyftaal: *(rolls her eyes)*, *(grinning)*.","en":"**Stage directions** in brackets in the present tense show tone and body language: *(rolls her eyes)*, *(grinning)*."},{"af":"**Taal:** natuurlike, informele spreektaal tussen vriende – samevoegings (*I can't*, *We'll*) is reg hier – maar korrekte spelling en leestekens. Tel die woorde (sonder die name): ±130.","en":"**Language:** natural, informal spoken language between friends – contractions (*I can't*, *We'll*) are fine here – but correct spelling and punctuation. Count the words (excluding the names): ±130."}],"answer":{"af":"Lerato: (excitedly) Sipho, the hiking club is climbing the Magaliesberg on Saturday. Are you coming?\nSipho: Saturday? The rugby final is on TV that afternoon, and I've been waiting all season for it. I can't miss it.\nLerato: (rolls her eyes) You can watch the highlights later. The view from the top is amazing, and the fresh air will do you good.\nSipho: But it's a four-hour hike. My legs will be finished before Monday's practice.\nLerato: We'll walk slowly, I promise. Besides, Coach said hiking builds stamina.\nSipho: (scratches his head) That's true. What time do we leave?\nLerato: The bus leaves school at six and we'll be back by one.\nSipho: (grinning) Then I can still watch the final at three. Fine, count me in!\nLerato: Great! Bring water, a hat and sunscreen – it gets hot up there.","en":"Lerato: (excitedly) Sipho, the hiking club is climbing the Magaliesberg on Saturday. Are you coming?\nSipho: Saturday? The rugby final is on TV that afternoon, and I've been waiting all season for it. I can't miss it.\nLerato: (rolls her eyes) You can watch the highlights later. The view from the top is amazing, and the fresh air will do you good.\nSipho: But it's a four-hour hike. My legs will be finished before Monday's practice.\nLerato: We'll walk slowly, I promise. Besides, Coach said hiking builds stamina.\nSipho: (scratches his head) That's true. What time do we leave?\nLerato: The bus leaves school at six and we'll be back by one.\nSipho: (grinning) Then I can still watch the final at three. Fine, count me in!\nLerato: Great! Bring water, a hat and sunscreen – it gets hot up there."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf 'n koerantberig","en":"Write a newspaper report"},"problem":{"af":"**Scenario:** On Saturday 17 October 2026, Grade 10 learners from your school cleaned up part of the Hartbeespoort Dam shore. Write a report for the local newspaper. (120–150 words)","en":"**Scenario:** On Saturday 17 October 2026, Grade 10 learners from your school cleaned up part of the Hartbeespoort Dam shore. Write a report for the local newspaper. (120–150 words)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Opskrif, byline, plek en datum:** 'n kort, pakkende opskrif; *By …*; dan *HARTBEESPOORT, 19 October 2026 –* (die dag van publikasie).","en":"**Headline, byline, place and date:** a short, catchy headline; *By …*; then *HARTBEESPOORT, 19 October 2026 –* (the day of publication)."},{"af":"**Eerste paragraaf = 5 W's + H:** *who* (40 Gr 10-leerders), *what* (vullis opgetel), *when* (Saterdagoggend), *where* (die oewer van die dam), *why* (bewusmaking oor besoedeling), *how* (met die hand).","en":"**First paragraph = 5 Ws + H:** *who* (40 Gr 10 learners), *what* (picked up rubbish), *when* (Saturday morning), *where* (the dam shore), *why* (to raise awareness about pollution), *how* (by hand)."},{"af":"**Liggaam:** meer besonderhede in die **derde persoon** en **verlede tyd**, met **aanhalings** van 'n leerder en die onderwyser. Geen eie mening nie (*I think it was great* ✗).","en":"**Body:** more details in the **third person** and **past tense**, with **quotations** from a learner and the teacher. No personal opinion (*I think it was great* ✗)."},{"af":"**Slot:** 'n kort laaste paragraaf oor wat volgende gebeur. Tel die woorde van die liggaam: ±130.","en":"**Ending:** a short last paragraph about what happens next. Count the words of the body: ±130."}],"answer":{"af":"**LEARNERS HAUL 300 BAGS OF RUBBISH FROM DAM SHORE**\n\nBy Thandi Mokoena\n\nHARTBEESPOORT, 19 October 2026 – Forty Grade 10 learners from a Brits high school spent Saturday morning picking up rubbish by hand along the shore of Hartbeespoort Dam to raise awareness about water pollution.\n\nWearing gloves and carrying refuse bags donated by a local hardware store, the learners filled more than 300 bags with plastic, bottles and fishing line in four hours.\n\n\"I could not believe how much plastic was hidden in the reeds,\" said Lebo Khumalo (15), one of the volunteers.\n\nTheir Life Orientation teacher, Mr Johan Venter, said the school planned to make the clean-up an annual event. \"Our learners have shown that young people can make a real difference,\" he said.\n\nThe learners sorted the rubbish into recyclables and general waste before it was collected.\n\nThe group hopes to return in March.","en":"**LEARNERS HAUL 300 BAGS OF RUBBISH FROM DAM SHORE**\n\nBy Thandi Mokoena\n\nHARTBEESPOORT, 19 October 2026 – Forty Grade 10 learners from a Brits high school spent Saturday morning picking up rubbish by hand along the shore of Hartbeespoort Dam to raise awareness about water pollution.\n\nWearing gloves and carrying refuse bags donated by a local hardware store, the learners filled more than 300 bags with plastic, bottles and fishing line in four hours.\n\n\"I could not believe how much plastic was hidden in the reeds,\" said Lebo Khumalo (15), one of the volunteers.\n\nTheir Life Orientation teacher, Mr Johan Venter, said the school planned to make the clean-up an annual event. \"Our learners have shown that young people can make a real difference,\" he said.\n\nThe learners sorted the rubbish into recyclables and general waste before it was collected.\n\nThe group hopes to return in March."}},{"title":{"af":"Skryf aanwysings (korter teks)","en":"Write directions (shorter text)"},"problem":{"af":"**Scenario:** Your friend Kabelo will arrive at the taxi rank and must walk to your house. The (imaginary) map shows: the taxi rank exit on Main Road; ±300 m to the right, traffic lights at a petrol station; Church Street to the left, with the library on the right; ±200 m further, a four-way stop and Acacia Avenue to the right; your house is number 12, the third on the left, with a green gate and a jacaranda tree. Write the directions. (80–100 words)","en":"**Scenario:** Your friend Kabelo will arrive at the taxi rank and must walk to your house. The (imaginary) map shows: the taxi rank exit on Main Road; ±300 m to the right, traffic lights at a petrol station; Church Street to the left, with the library on the right; ±200 m further, a four-way stop and Acacia Avenue to the right; your house is number 12, the third on the left, with a green gate and a jacaranda tree. Write the directions. (80–100 words)"},"steps":[{"af":"**Beginpunt:** sê presies waar hy begin (die hoofuitgang van die taxistaanplek).","en":"**Starting point:** say exactly where he starts (the main exit of the taxi rank)."},{"af":"**Volgorde:** genommerde stappe in die regte volgorde, elkeen met 'n **imperatief**: *Turn right …, Walk …, Pass …*","en":"**Sequence:** numbered steps in the right order, each with an **imperative**: *Turn right …, Walk …, Pass …*"},{"af":"**Landmerke en afstande:** die verkeersligte by die vulstasie, die biblioteek, die vierrigtingstop; *about 300 m*, *about 200 m*. Links/regs moet ooreenstem met die kaart.","en":"**Landmarks and distances:** the traffic lights at the petrol station, the library, the four-way stop; *about 300 m*, *about 200 m*. Left/right must match the map."},{"af":"**Bestemming:** beskryf die huis sodat hy dit herken (nommer, groen hek, jakarandaboom). Tel die woorde: ±95.","en":"**Destination:** describe the house so that he recognises it (number, green gate, jacaranda tree). Count the words: ±95."}],"answer":{"af":"Hi Kabelo\n\nHere is how to get to my house from the taxi rank:\n\n1. Leave the rank through the main exit on Main Road and turn right.\n2. Walk straight for about 300 m to the traffic lights at the petrol station.\n3. Turn left into Church Street and pass the library on your right.\n4. After about 200 m, at the four-way stop, turn right into Acacia Avenue.\n5. Our house, number 12, is the third house on the left. It has a green gate and a big jacaranda tree.\n\nPhone me if you get lost!\n\nThabo","en":"Hi Kabelo\n\nHere is how to get to my house from the taxi rank:\n\n1. Leave the rank through the main exit on Main Road and turn right.\n2. Walk straight for about 300 m to the traffic lights at the petrol station.\n3. Turn left into Church Street and pass the library on your right.\n4. After about 200 m, at the four-way stop, turn right into Acacia Avenue.\n5. Our house, number 12, is the third house on the left. It has a green gate and a big jacaranda tree.\n\nPhone me if you get lost!\n\nThabo"}},{"title":{"af":"Ontbrekende formaatkenmerke en register","en":"Missing format features and register"},"problem":{"af":"Lerato stuur hierdie e-pos aan haar skoolhoof, mnr. Nkosi:\n\nHi Sir\n\nI want to use the hall for our debating practice. We need it on a Wednesday afternoon. Can u let me know.\n\nLerato\n\n(a) Name THREE format features that are missing. (3)\n(b) Rewrite the greeting and the last sentence of the body in the correct register. (2)","en":"Lerato sends this e-mail to her principal, Mr Nkosi:\n\nHi Sir\n\nI want to use the hall for our debating practice. We need it on a Wednesday afternoon. Can u let me know.\n\nLerato\n\n(a) Name THREE format features that are missing. (3)\n(b) Rewrite the greeting and the last sentence of the body in the correct register. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"Vergelyk met die e-posformaat: **To**, **Subject**, groet, liggaam, afsluiting, volle naam.","en":"Compare with the e-mail format: **To**, **Subject**, greeting, body, closing, full name."},{"af":"(a) Ontbrekend: (1) die **To**-reël (mnr. Nkosi se e-posadres); (2) 'n **Subject**-reël, bv. *Request to use the school hall*; (3) 'n **afsluiting** (*Kind regards*) met haar **volle naam en klas**.","en":"(a) Missing: (1) the **To** line (Mr Nkosi's e-mail address); (2) a **Subject** line, e.g. *Request to use the school hall*; (3) a **closing** (*Kind regards*) with her **full name and class**."},{"af":"(b) Die ontvanger is die skoolhoof, dus **formele register**: *Hi Sir* → **Dear Mr Nkosi**.","en":"(b) The recipient is the principal, so **formal register**: *Hi Sir* → **Dear Mr Nkosi**."},{"af":"*Can u let me know.* bevat SMS-taal (*u*) en 'n vraag sonder vraagteken → **Could you please let me know whether the hall is available?**","en":"*Can u let me know.* contains SMS language (*u*) and a question without a question mark → **Could you please let me know whether the hall is available?**"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Any three: the \"To\" line (recipient's address), a subject line, a proper closing (e.g. Kind regards), her full name and class. (b) Dear Mr Nkosi … Could you please let me know whether the hall is available?","en":"(a) Any three: the \"To\" line (recipient's address), a subject line, a proper closing (e.g. Kind regards), her full name and class. (b) Dear Mr Nkosi … Could you please let me know whether the hall is available?"}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Hoe begin elke spreker se beurt in 'n dialoog?","en":"How does each speaker's turn begin in a dialogue?"},"options":[{"af":"With the words in inverted commas: \"Hello,\" said Thabo.","en":"With the words in inverted commas: \"Hello,\" said Thabo."},{"af":"With a dash: – Hello.","en":"With a dash: – Hello."},{"af":"With the name in brackets: (Thabo) Hello.","en":"With the name in brackets: (Thabo) Hello."},{"af":"With the name on the left, followed by a colon: Thabo: Hello.","en":"With the name on the left, followed by a colon: Thabo: Hello."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In 'n dialoog staan die spreker se naam links met 'n dubbelpunt, en daar is geen aanhalingstekens nie. Hakies word vir toneelaanwysings gebruik.","en":"In a dialogue the speaker's name is on the left with a colon, and there are no inverted commas. Brackets are used for stage directions."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n dialoog plaas jy aanhalingstekens om elke spreker se woorde.","en":"In a dialogue you put inverted commas around each speaker's words."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Aanhalingstekens hoort by direkte rede in 'n verhaal. 'n Dialoog gebruik *Naam:* en dan die woorde, sonder aanhalingstekens.","en":"False. Inverted commas belong to direct speech in a story. A dialogue uses *Name:* followed by the words, without inverted commas."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die reël onder 'n koerantberig se opskrif wat die joernalis se naam gee (*By Thandi Mokoena*), is die ___. (Engelse term)","en":"The line under a newspaper report's headline that gives the journalist's name (*By Thandi Mokoena*) is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["byline","by-line"],"en":["byline","by-line"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["headline","dateline","caption"],"en":["headline","dateline","caption"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die *byline* sê wie die berig geskryf het. Die *headline* is die opskrif, die *dateline* gee plek en datum, en 'n *caption* is die onderskrif by 'n foto.","en":"The *byline* says who wrote the report. The *headline* is the heading, the *dateline* gives place and date, and a *caption* is the text under a photo."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken *RSVP* op 'n uitnodiging?","en":"What does *RSVP* mean on an invitation?"},"options":[{"af":"Antwoord asseblief – laat weet of jy kom.","en":"Please reply – let the host know whether you are coming."},{"af":"Bring asseblief 'n geskenk.","en":"Please bring a present."},{"af":"Formele drag word verwag.","en":"Formal dress is expected."},{"af":"Die partytjie eindig om middernag.","en":"The party ends at midnight."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"*RSVP* kom van Frans *répondez s'il vous plaît* (antwoord asseblief). Gee altyd 'n datum en 'n kontaknommer by, bv. *RSVP to Lerato (072 …) by 1 November.*","en":"*RSVP* comes from French *répondez s'il vous plaît* (please reply). Always add a date and a contact number, e.g. *RSVP to Lerato (072 …) by 1 November.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die liggaam van 'n langer transaksionele teks in Graad 10 moet ___ woorde lank wees.","en":"The body of a longer transactional text in Grade 10 should be ___ words long."},"answers":{"af":["120–150","120-150","120 tot 150","120 to 150"],"en":["120–150","120-150","120 to 150"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["80–100","150–200","250–300"],"en":["80–100","150–200","250–300"]}},"explain":{"af":"Afdeling B (langer teks, 30 punte): 120–150 woorde. Afdeling C (korter teks, 20 punte): 80–100 woorde. Die opstel in Afdeling A is 150–200 woorde.","en":"Section B (longer text, 30 marks): 120–150 words. Section C (shorter text, 20 marks): 80–100 words. The essay in Section A is 150–200 words."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In watter persoon en tyd word 'n koerantberig meestal geskryf?","en":"In which person and tense is a newspaper report mostly written?"},"options":[{"af":"eerste persoon, teenwoordige tyd","en":"first person, present tense"},{"af":"tweede persoon, toekomende tyd","en":"second person, future tense"},{"af":"derde persoon, verlede tyd","en":"third person, past tense"},{"af":"eerste persoon, verlede tyd","en":"first person, past tense"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Berig vertel objektief wat reeds gebeur het: derde persoon (*the learners, he, she*) en verlede tyd (*collected, said*). Net die opskrif gebruik dikwels die teenwoordige tyd.","en":"A report tells objectively what has already happened: third person (*the learners, he, she*) and past tense (*collected, said*). Only the headline often uses the present tense."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter een is die beste begin van 'n dagboekinskrywing?","en":"Which one is the best start to a diary entry?"},"options":[{"af":"Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing to inform you about my day.","en":"Dear Sir/Madam, I am writing to inform you about my day."},{"af":"Friday, 16 October 2026, 21:45 – Dear Diary, I still can't believe what happened at practice today!","en":"Friday, 16 October 2026, 21:45 – Dear Diary, I still can't believe what happened at practice today!"},{"af":"BRITS – A learner had a bad day on Friday, a source said.","en":"BRITS – A learner had a bad day on Friday, a source said."},{"af":"1. Wake up. 2. Go to school. 3. Have a bad day.","en":"1. Wake up. 2. Go to school. 3. Have a bad day."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Dagboekinskrywing het 'n datum (en tyd), is in die eerste persoon en wys gevoelens. Die ander begin soos 'n formele brief, 'n koerantberig en instruksies.","en":"A diary entry has a date (and time), is in the first person and shows feelings. The others start like a formal letter, a newspaper report and instructions."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Instruksies is genommerde stappe wat gewoonlik met 'n werkwoord in die ___ begin, bv. *Mix the flour and water.* (Engelse term)","en":"Instructions are numbered steps that usually start with a verb in the ___, e.g. *Mix the flour and water.*"},"answers":{"af":["imperative","imperative form","command form","imperatief","gebiedende wys"],"en":["imperative","imperative form","command form"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["passive voice","past tense","future tense"],"en":["passive voice","past tense","future tense"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die imperatief (bevelsvorm) gee 'n direkte opdrag: *Mix …, Pour …, Bake …*. Dit maak instruksies kort en duidelik.","en":"The imperative (command form) gives a direct instruction: *Mix …, Pour …, Bake …*. It keeps instructions short and clear."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n toespraak kan 'n retoriese vraag gebruik word om die gehoor te betrek.","en":"In a speech a rhetorical question can be used to involve the audience."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. 'n Retoriese vraag (*Who wants to live without clean water?*) laat die gehoor dink en voel deel van die toespraak.","en":"True. A rhetorical question (*Who wants to live without clean water?*) makes the audience think and feel part of the speech."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke teks by sy belangrikste formaatkenmerk.","en":"Match each text to its most important format feature."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Newspaper report","en":"Newspaper report"},"r":{"af":"opskrif, byline en die 5 W's + H in die eerste paragraaf","en":"headline, byline and the 5 Ws + H in the first paragraph"}},{"l":{"af":"Review","en":"Review"},"r":{"af":"'n gradering, bv. 4/5 sterre","en":"a rating, e.g. 4/5 stars"}},{"l":{"af":"Formal report","en":"Formal report"},"r":{"af":"opdrag, bevindinge en aanbevelings","en":"terms of reference, findings and recommendations"}},{"l":{"af":"Obituary","en":"Obituary"},"r":{"af":"geboorte- en sterfdatum en begrafnisbesonderhede","en":"dates of birth and death and funeral details"}},{"l":{"af":"Invitation","en":"Invitation"},"r":{"af":"RSVP met 'n datum en kontaknommer","en":"RSVP with a date and contact number"}}],"explain":{"af":"Formaat tel baie punte. Leer vir elke teks die kenmerke wat die nasiener eerste soek.","en":"Format counts many marks. For each text, learn the features the marker looks for first."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die eerste paragraaf van 'n koerantberig beantwoord *who, what, when, where* en *why*. Die H staan vir ___.","en":"The first paragraph of a newspaper report answers *who, what, when, where* and *why*. The H stands for ___."},"answers":{"af":["how"],"en":["how"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["headline","history","help"],"en":["headline","history","help"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die 5 W's + H = *who, what, when, where, why* en ***how*** (hoe dit gebeur het). In die model-berig: *by hand*.","en":"The 5 Ws + H = *who, what, when, where, why* and ***how*** (how it happened). In the model report: *by hand*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Jy skryf 'n e-pos aan jou skoolhoof, mnr. Nkosi, om die saal te bespreek. Watter onderwerpreël en aanhef is die beste?","en":"You are writing an e-mail to your principal, Mr Nkosi, to book the hall. Which subject line and greeting are best?"},"options":[{"af":"Subject: hall!!! / Hey Mr N,","en":"Subject: hall!!! / Hey Mr N,"},{"af":"Subject: Hi / Dear friend,","en":"Subject: Hi / Dear friend,"},{"af":"Subject: Request to use the school hall on 4 November / Dear Mr Nkosi","en":"Subject: Request to use the school hall on 4 November / Dear Mr Nkosi"},{"af":"Subject: (none) / Yo Sir,","en":"Subject: (none) / Yo Sir,"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die onderwerpreël moet kort en spesifiek wees, en die aanhef formeel omdat die ontvanger die skoolhoof is. Uitroeptekens, *Hey* en *Yo* is te informeel.","en":"The subject line must be short and specific, and the greeting formal because the recipient is the principal. Exclamation marks, *Hey* and *Yo* are too informal."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter openingsin is die sterkste hoek (*hook*) vir 'n toespraak aan Graad 10's oor die bespaar van water?","en":"Which opening sentence is the strongest hook for a speech to Grade 10s about saving water?"},"options":[{"af":"Today I am going to talk to you about water.","en":"Today I am going to talk to you about water."},{"af":"Imagine turning on the tap tomorrow morning and hearing nothing but a dry cough of air.","en":"Imagine turning on the tap tomorrow morning and hearing nothing but a dry cough of air."},{"af":"Water is a liquid that is made of hydrogen and oxygen.","en":"Water is a liquid that is made of hydrogen and oxygen."},{"af":"Thank you for listening to my speech about water.","en":"Thank you for listening to my speech about water."}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n Goeie hoek gryp die gehoor dadelik: *Imagine …* spreek hulle direk aan en skep 'n lewendige beeld. *Today I am going to talk about …* is vervelig, die feit oor waterstof is irrelevant en *Thank you* hoort aan die einde.","en":"A good hook grabs the audience immediately: *Imagine …* addresses them directly and creates a vivid image. *Today I am going to talk about …* is dull, the fact about hydrogen is irrelevant and *Thank you* belongs at the end."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Watter belangrike inligting ontbreek in hierdie uitnodiging? *You're invited to Lerato's 16th birthday braai! Venue: 12 Acacia Avenue. Time: 14:00. RSVP to Lerato by 1 November.* ___","en":"Which important detail is missing from this invitation? *You're invited to Lerato's 16th birthday braai! Venue: 12 Acacia Avenue. Time: 14:00. RSVP to Lerato by 1 November.* ___"},"answers":{"af":["date","the date","datum","die datum","day","the day"],"en":["date","the date","day","the day"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["venue","time","RSVP"],"en":["venue","time","RSVP"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Who* (Lerato), *what* (16de verjaarsdagbraai), *where* (12 Acacia Avenue), die tyd en RSVP is daar – maar **op watter dag** is die braai? 'n Uitnodiging sonder 'n datum is nutteloos.","en":"*Who* (Lerato), *what* (16th birthday braai), *where* (12 Acacia Avenue), the time and RSVP are there – but **on which day** is the braai? An invitation without a date is useless."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die beste vir aanwysings (*directions*)?","en":"Which sentence is best for directions?"},"options":[{"af":"Go that way and turn somewhere near the shop.","en":"Go that way and turn somewhere near the shop."},{"af":"Turn left, then right, then left again.","en":"Turn left, then right, then left again."},{"af":"You will find it easily – everyone knows where it is.","en":"You will find it easily – everyone knows where it is."},{"af":"Walk straight for about 200 m to the four-way stop, then turn left at the library.","en":"Walk straight for about 200 m to the four-way stop, then turn left at the library."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Goeie aanwysings het 'n duidelike volgorde, **afstande** (*about 200 m*) en **landmerke** (*four-way stop, library*). *Turn left, then right* het geen landmerke nie, en die ander is vaag.","en":"Good directions have a clear sequence, **distances** (*about 200 m*) and **landmarks** (*four-way stop, library*). *Turn left, then right* has no landmarks, and the others are vague."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Leerder begin sy koerantberig so: *I was so scared when I saw the fire last night!!! It was the worst thing ever.* Watter evaluering is die beste?","en":"A learner starts his newspaper report like this: *I was so scared when I saw the fire last night!!! It was the worst thing ever.* Which evaluation is best?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit is swak: 'n berig is objektief, in die derde persoon en verlede tyd, en die eerste paragraaf moet die 5 W's + H gee – nie die skrywer se gevoelens met uitroeptekens nie.","en":"It is weak: a report is objective, in the third person and past tense, and the first paragraph must give the 5 Ws + H – not the writer's feelings with exclamation marks."},{"af":"Dit is goed, want dit trek die leser se aandag.","en":"It is good, because it grabs the reader's attention."},{"af":"Net die spelling moet reggemaak word.","en":"Only the spelling needs to be corrected."},{"af":"Dit moet in die teenwoordige tyd wees.","en":"It should be in the present tense."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Dit klink soos 'n dagboekinskrywing: eerste persoon (*I*), emosies, drie uitroeptekens en 'n mening (*the worst thing ever*). 'n Berig sou begin: *BRITS, 20 October – A fire destroyed …* met die 5 W's + H.","en":"It sounds like a diary entry: first person (*I*), emotions, three exclamation marks and an opinion (*the worst thing ever*). A report would begin: *BRITS, 20 October – A fire destroyed …* with the 5 Ws + H."}}]}]},{"term":4,"title":{"af":"Drama, woordeskat en kritiese taalbewustheid","en":"Drama, vocabulary and critical language awareness"},"topics":[{"id":"eng10-t4-drama","title":{"af":"Drama: terme en ontleding","en":"Drama: terms and analysis"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal dramaterme soos alleenspraak, tersyde en dramatiese ironie kan herken en kontekstuele vrae oor 'n drama-uittreksel volledig en met bewyse kan beantwoord.","en":"You will be able to identify drama terms such as soliloquy, aside and dramatic irony, and answer contextual questions on a drama extract fully and with evidence."},"summary":{"af":"## Drama in die eksamen\n\nDrama is een van die vier genres in **Vraestel 2: Letterkunde** (70 punte). Jy beantwoord vrae oor **twee** van die genres (roman, drama, kortverhale, poësie), elk 35 punte. Die vrae is **kontekstuele vrae** op 'n uittreksel van 10–20 reëls, met die punte tussen hakies.\n\n## Wat is 'n drama?\n\n'n **Drama** (toneelstuk) word geskryf om op 'n verhoog vir 'n **gehoor** (audience) **opgevoer** te word. Die teks is die **script**. Daar is **geen verteller** nie: alles wat ons weet, kom uit die **dialoog** en die **toneelaanwysings**.\n\n| Term | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| **Act** (bedryf) | 'n Hoofdeel van die drama |\n| **Scene** (toneel) | 'n Kleiner deel van 'n bedryf; 'n nuwe toneel beteken dikwels 'n nuwe plek of tyd |\n| **Cast list / dramatis personae** (rolverdeling) | Die lys karakters aan die begin, dikwels met 'n kort beskrywing |\n| **Dialogue** (dialoog) | Die gesprek tussen karakters – dit dryf die intrige vorentoe |\n| **Monologue** (monoloog) | 'n Lang toespraak deur een karakter **aan ander karakters** (of die gehoor) |\n| **Soliloquy** (alleenspraak) | Die karakter is **alleen** op die verhoog en dink hardop – ons hoor sy ware gedagtes en gevoelens |\n| **Aside** (tersyde) | 'n Kort opmerking aan die **gehoor** wat die ander karakters op die verhoog **nie hoor nie** |\n\n> **Wenk:** Monoloog = ander karakters luister. Alleenspraak = niemand anders is op die verhoog nie. Tersyde = kort, en net die gehoor hoor dit.\n\n## Toneelaanwysings (stage directions)\n\nToneelaanwysings staan in *kursief* en/of tussen hakies, en die akteurs sê dit **nie** hardop nie. Dit vertel ons:\n\n- **beweging en lyftaal:** *(enters slowly and folds her arms)*\n- **toon** – hoe 'n reël gesê word: *(sarcastically)*, *(in a whisper)*\n- **die toneel** (setting): plek en tyd, bv. *(A kitchen in Brits. Late at night.)*\n- **beligting, rekwisiete** (props) **en klankeffekte:** *(The lights dim. A dog barks.)*\n\n## Struktuur, konflik en spanning\n\nDie intrige volg dieselfde stadiums as 'n verhaal: **exposition** (uiteensetting) → **rising action** (stygende aksie/komplikasie) → **climax** (klimaks – die keerpunt, die spanning is die hoogste) → **falling action** (dalende aksie) → **resolution** (ontknoping).\n\n**Conflict** (konflik) is **internal** (innerlik – 'n stryd binne 'n karakter) of **external** (uiterlik – teen 'n ander karakter, die samelewing of die natuur). **Tension** (spanning) bou op wanneer die gehoor wonder wat gaan gebeur: kort, skerp reëls, stiltes, onderbrekings en klankeffekte help.\n\n## Karakterisering\n\nOmdat daar geen verteller is nie, leer ons 'n karakter ken deur:\n\n1. wat hy **sê** en **hoe** hy dit sê (dialoog en toon);\n2. wat hy **doen** (toneelaanwysings);\n3. wat **ander** karakters oor hom sê en hoe hulle op hom reageer.\n\n## Dramatiese ironie\n\n**Dramatic irony** (dramatiese ironie): die **gehoor weet meer as 'n karakter**. Bv. ons het in Toneel 1 gesien hoe Thabo die venster breek, maar in Toneel 2 blameer sy ma die hond. Dit bou spanning, want ons wil die karakter waarsku. Moenie dit verwar nie met **verbal irony** (verbale ironie – jy sê die teenoorgestelde van wat jy bedoel) en **situational irony** (situasie-ironie – die teenoorgestelde gebeur van wat verwag is).\n\n## Tema, simbool, toon en stemming\n\n- **Theme** (tema): die boodskap oor die lewe, bv. *Greed can destroy trust.* Die onderwerp (subject) is net waaroor dit gaan (hebsug).\n- **Symbol** (simbool): 'n voorwerp wat vir 'n groter idee staan, bv. 'n stukkende horlosie = die tyd staan stil ná 'n verlies.\n- **Tone** (toon): 'n karakter se houding – jy hoor dit in sy **stem** (bitter, sarkasties, smekend).\n- **Mood** (stemming): die **atmosfeer** wat die gehoor beleef (gespanne, vrolik, somber).\n\n## Komedie en tragedie\n\n- **Comedy** (komedie): lighartig, humor deur misverstande, woordspel en oordrywing; eindig gelukkig.\n- **Tragedy** (tragedie): ernstig; eindig met die hoofkarakter se **ondergang** (dikwels die dood), meestal weens 'n swakheid of 'n verkeerde keuse.\n\n## Die rol van die gehoor\n\n'n Drama is eers volledig wanneer dit **opgevoer** word. Die gehoor lag, skrik en simpatiseer, en weet soms meer as die karakters. Vra jouself: *Wat voel die gehoor op hierdie oomblik?*\n\n## Kontekstuele vrae – hoe om te antwoord\n\n| Vraag | Hoe om te antwoord |\n|---|---|\n| *Place the extract in context.* | Wat het **net voor** die uittreksel gebeur en wat gebeur nou? Moenie die hele storie oorvertel nie. |\n| *Give a stage direction for line X and motivate it.* | Gee lyftaal **of** toon **en** sê **hoekom**: *(shouting angrily) because he has just been called a liar.* |\n| *Explain the dramatic irony.* | Wat **weet die gehoor** + wat **weet die karakter nie**. |\n| *What does this reveal about X?* | Byvoeglike naamwoord + bewys uit die teks: *X is selfish: he …* |\n| *If you were the director, how would you …?* | Gee 'n konkrete instruksie (beweging, toon, beligting, klank) en motiveer met die teks. |\n| *Do you sympathise with X? Discuss.* | Neem 'n standpunt (*Yes/No*) en gee twee redes uit die teks. Albei kante kan volpunte kry as dit goed gemotiveer is. |\n\n> **Algemene foute:** die storie oorvertel in plaas daarvan om die vraag te beantwoord; 'n toneelaanwysing sonder motivering; *happy/sad* as toon (gebruik presiese woorde soos *bitter, desperate, mocking*); te veel aanhaal; die punte ignoreer (2 punte = twee feite).","en":"## Drama in the exam\n\nDrama is one of the four genres in **Paper 2: Literature** (70 marks). You answer questions on **two** of the genres (novel, drama, short stories, poetry), 35 marks each. The questions are **contextual questions** on an extract of 10–20 lines, with the marks in brackets.\n\n## What is a drama?\n\nA **drama** (play) is written to be **performed** on a stage in front of an **audience**. The text is the **script**. There is **no narrator**: everything we know comes from the **dialogue** and the **stage directions**.\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Act** | A main division of the play |\n| **Scene** | A smaller part of an act; a new scene often means a new place or time |\n| **Cast list / dramatis personae** | The list of characters at the start, often with a short description |\n| **Dialogue** | The conversation between characters – it drives the plot forward |\n| **Monologue** | A long speech by one character **to other characters** (or the audience) |\n| **Soliloquy** | The character is **alone** on stage and thinks aloud – we hear his true thoughts and feelings |\n| **Aside** | A short remark to the **audience** that the other characters on stage **do not hear** |\n\n> **Tip:** Monologue = other characters listen. Soliloquy = nobody else is on stage. Aside = short, and only the audience hears it.\n\n## Stage directions\n\nStage directions are in *italics* and/or brackets, and the actors do **not** say them aloud. They tell us about:\n\n- **movement and body language:** *(enters slowly and folds her arms)*\n- **tone** – how a line is said: *(sarcastically)*, *(in a whisper)*\n- **the setting:** place and time, e.g. *(A kitchen in Brits. Late at night.)*\n- **lighting, props and sound effects:** *(The lights dim. A dog barks.)*\n\n## Structure, conflict and tension\n\nThe plot follows the same stages as a story: **exposition** → **rising action/complication** → **climax** (the turning point, where tension is highest) → **falling action** → **resolution**.\n\n**Conflict** is **internal** (a struggle inside a character) or **external** (against another character, society or nature). **Tension** builds when the audience wonders what will happen: short, sharp lines, silences, interruptions and sound effects all help.\n\n## Characterisation\n\nBecause there is no narrator, we get to know a character through:\n\n1. what he **says** and **how** he says it (dialogue and tone);\n2. what he **does** (stage directions);\n3. what **other** characters say about him and how they react to him.\n\n## Dramatic irony\n\n**Dramatic irony**: the **audience knows more than a character**. E.g. in Scene 1 we saw Thabo break the window, but in Scene 2 his mother blames the dog. It builds tension because we want to warn the character. Don't confuse it with **verbal irony** (saying the opposite of what you mean) and **situational irony** (the opposite of what was expected happens).\n\n## Theme, symbol, tone and mood\n\n- **Theme:** the message about life, e.g. *Greed can destroy trust.* The subject is only what it is about (greed).\n- **Symbol:** an object that stands for a bigger idea, e.g. a broken clock = time stands still after a loss.\n- **Tone:** a character's attitude – you hear it in his **voice** (bitter, sarcastic, pleading).\n- **Mood:** the **atmosphere** the audience experiences (tense, cheerful, gloomy).\n\n## Comedy and tragedy\n\n- **Comedy:** light-hearted, humour through misunderstandings, wordplay and exaggeration; ends happily.\n- **Tragedy:** serious; ends with the main character's **downfall** (often death), usually because of a weakness or a wrong choice.\n\n## The role of the audience\n\nA drama is only complete when it is **performed**. The audience laughs, gets a fright and sympathises, and sometimes knows more than the characters. Ask yourself: *What does the audience feel at this moment?*\n\n## Contextual questions – how to answer\n\n| Question | How to answer |\n|---|---|\n| *Place the extract in context.* | What happened **just before** the extract and what is happening now? Don't retell the whole story. |\n| *Give a stage direction for line X and motivate it.* | Give body language **or** tone **and** say **why**: *(shouting angrily) because he has just been called a liar.* |\n| *Explain the dramatic irony.* | What **the audience knows** + what **the character does not know**. |\n| *What does this reveal about X?* | Adjective + evidence from the text: *X is selfish: he …* |\n| *If you were the director, how would you …?* | Give a concrete instruction (movement, tone, lighting, sound) and motivate it from the text. |\n| *Do you sympathise with X? Discuss.* | Take a stand (*Yes/No*) and give two reasons from the text. Either side can earn full marks if it is well motivated. |\n\n> **Common mistakes:** retelling the story instead of answering the question; a stage direction without a motivation; *happy/sad* as a tone (use precise words such as *bitter, desperate, mocking*); quoting too much; ignoring the marks (2 marks = two facts)."},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Bedryf en toneel (act and scene)","en":"Act and scene"},"def":{"af":"'n Bedryf (act) is 'n hoofdeel van 'n drama; elke bedryf bestaan uit kleiner tonele (scenes), dikwels elk op een plek en tyd.","en":"An act is a main division of a play; each act consists of smaller scenes, often each in one place and time."}},{"term":{"af":"Rolverdeling (cast list / dramatis personae)","en":"Cast list (dramatis personae)"},"def":{"af":"Die lys karakters aan die begin van 'n drama, dikwels met 'n kort beskrywing van elkeen.","en":"The list of characters at the beginning of a play, often with a short description of each."}},{"term":{"af":"Toneelaanwysings (stage directions)","en":"Stage directions"},"def":{"af":"Instruksies in kursief en/of tussen hakies oor beweging, toon, die toneel, beligting, rekwisiete en klank; dit word nie hardop gesê nie.","en":"Instructions in italics and/or brackets about movement, tone, setting, lighting, props and sound; they are not spoken aloud."}},{"term":{"af":"Monoloog (monologue)","en":"Monologue"},"def":{"af":"'n Lang toespraak deur een karakter aan ander karakters (of aan die gehoor).","en":"A long speech by one character to other characters (or to the audience)."}},{"term":{"af":"Alleenspraak (soliloquy)","en":"Soliloquy"},"def":{"af":"'n Toespraak wanneer 'n karakter alleen op die verhoog is en sy ware gedagtes en gevoelens hardop sê.","en":"A speech in which a character is alone on stage and speaks his true thoughts and feelings aloud."}},{"term":{"af":"Tersyde (aside)","en":"Aside"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort opmerking aan die gehoor wat die ander karakters op die verhoog nie hoor nie.","en":"A short remark to the audience that the other characters on stage do not hear."}},{"term":{"af":"Dramatiese ironie (dramatic irony)","en":"Dramatic irony"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer die gehoor meer weet as 'n karakter; dit bou spanning.","en":"When the audience knows more than a character; it builds tension."}},{"term":{"af":"Konflik en spanning (conflict and tension)","en":"Conflict and tension"},"def":{"af":"Konflik is die stryd wat die intrige dryf (innerlik of uiterlik); spanning is die onsekerheid en angs wat die gehoor voel oor wat gaan gebeur.","en":"Conflict is the struggle that drives the plot (internal or external); tension is the uncertainty and anxiety the audience feels about what will happen."}},{"term":{"af":"Toon en stemming (tone and mood)","en":"Tone and mood"},"def":{"af":"Toon is 'n karakter se houding soos dit in sy stem hoorbaar is; stemming is die atmosfeer wat die gehoor beleef.","en":"Tone is a character's attitude as you hear it in his voice; mood is the atmosphere the audience experiences."}},{"term":{"af":"Komedie en tragedie (comedy and tragedy)","en":"Comedy and tragedy"},"def":{"af":"'n Komedie is lighartig en eindig gelukkig; 'n tragedie is ernstig en eindig met die hoofkarakter se ondergang.","en":"A comedy is light-hearted and ends happily; a tragedy is serious and ends with the main character's downfall."}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Kontekstuele vrae: konteks, tersyde en dramatiese ironie","en":"Contextual questions: context, aside and dramatic irony"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die agtergrond en die drama-uittreksel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Background:* **Sour Oranges** (own example) is a one-act play set on a citrus farm near Brits. SIPHO (17) works in the packing shed every Saturday to save money for university, where he hopes to study with a bursary. In Scene 1, DIRK, the farmer's son, warns Sipho to \"stay out of his way\". In Scene 2 the audience sees DIRK secretly take R2 000 from the cash tin to pay back money he owes. The extract below is from Scene 3.\n\n*(The packing shed on Mr Venter's citrus farm near Brits. Late afternoon. Crates of oranges are stacked against the wall. A single bulb hangs from the roof. SIPHO is sweeping. MR VENTER enters, holding an empty cash tin. DIRK follows slowly, his hands in his pockets.)*\n\n[1] MR VENTER: *(holding up the tin)* Sipho. There was two thousand rand in this tin on Friday. Now it is empty.\n\n[2] SIPHO: *(stops sweeping)* Empty, Mr Venter? I … I don't understand.\n\n[3] DIRK: *(leaning against the crates)* He understands perfectly, Pa. He was the last one in the shed.\n\n[4] SIPHO: I locked the door at five and gave the key to Dirk. You were there, Dirk.\n\n[5] DIRK: *(laughing)* Listen to him! Now it's my fault?\n\n[6] MR VENTER: *(sharply)* Let him speak, Dirk.\n\n[7] SIPHO: *(quietly, looking straight at Mr Venter)* I have worked here every Saturday for two years. Have I ever taken even one orange without asking?\n\n[8] MR VENTER: *(sighs and puts the tin down on a crate)* No. No, you haven't.\n\n[9] DIRK: *(aside)* Two years of being the perfect worker. Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\n\n[10] MR VENTER: I'll call the police in the morning. They can sort this out.\n\n[11] SIPHO: The police? Mr Venter, with a criminal record I can forget about my bursary!\n\n[12] DIRK: *(smiling)* Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\n\n*(SIPHO drops the broom. The bulb flickers and goes out. Darkness.)*\n\n[13] MR VENTER: *(in the dark)* Load-shedding. Of course. Everybody out.\n\n(a) Place the extract in context. (2)\n\n(b) Refer to line 9. Name the dramatic device that DIRK uses and explain why the playwright uses it here. (2)\n\n(c) Explain the dramatic irony in lines 3–5. (2)\n\n(d) Give a suitable stage direction for SIPHO in line 4 and motivate your answer. (2)","en":"Read the background and the drama extract and answer the questions.\n\n*Background:* **Sour Oranges** (own example) is a one-act play set on a citrus farm near Brits. SIPHO (17) works in the packing shed every Saturday to save money for university, where he hopes to study with a bursary. In Scene 1, DIRK, the farmer's son, warns Sipho to \"stay out of his way\". In Scene 2 the audience sees DIRK secretly take R2 000 from the cash tin to pay back money he owes. The extract below is from Scene 3.\n\n*(The packing shed on Mr Venter's citrus farm near Brits. Late afternoon. Crates of oranges are stacked against the wall. A single bulb hangs from the roof. SIPHO is sweeping. MR VENTER enters, holding an empty cash tin. DIRK follows slowly, his hands in his pockets.)*\n\n[1] MR VENTER: *(holding up the tin)* Sipho. There was two thousand rand in this tin on Friday. Now it is empty.\n\n[2] SIPHO: *(stops sweeping)* Empty, Mr Venter? I … I don't understand.\n\n[3] DIRK: *(leaning against the crates)* He understands perfectly, Pa. He was the last one in the shed.\n\n[4] SIPHO: I locked the door at five and gave the key to Dirk. You were there, Dirk.\n\n[5] DIRK: *(laughing)* Listen to him! Now it's my fault?\n\n[6] MR VENTER: *(sharply)* Let him speak, Dirk.\n\n[7] SIPHO: *(quietly, looking straight at Mr Venter)* I have worked here every Saturday for two years. Have I ever taken even one orange without asking?\n\n[8] MR VENTER: *(sighs and puts the tin down on a crate)* No. No, you haven't.\n\n[9] DIRK: *(aside)* Two years of being the perfect worker. Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\n\n[10] MR VENTER: I'll call the police in the morning. They can sort this out.\n\n[11] SIPHO: The police? Mr Venter, with a criminal record I can forget about my bursary!\n\n[12] DIRK: *(smiling)* Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\n\n*(SIPHO drops the broom. The bulb flickers and goes out. Darkness.)*\n\n[13] MR VENTER: *(in the dark)* Load-shedding. Of course. Everybody out.\n\n(a) Place the extract in context. (2)\n\n(b) Refer to line 9. Name the dramatic device that DIRK uses and explain why the playwright uses it here. (2)\n\n(c) Explain the dramatic irony in lines 3–5. (2)\n\n(d) Give a suitable stage direction for SIPHO in line 4 and motivate your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a) Konteks:** Sê wat **net voor** die uittreksel gebeur het en wat **nou** gebeur – nie die hele storie nie. In Toneel 2 het die gehoor gesien hoe Dirk die geld vat. Nou ontdek mnr. Venter dat die geld weg is.\n\n*Model answer:* In Scene 2 Dirk secretly took the R2 000 from the cash tin to pay a debt. Now Mr Venter has discovered that the money is missing, and Sipho is being blamed for the theft. ✔✔","en":"**(a) Context:** Say what happened **just before** the extract and what is happening **now** – not the whole story. In Scene 2 the audience saw Dirk take the money. Now Mr Venter discovers that the money is gone.\n\n*Model answer:* In Scene 2 Dirk secretly took the R2 000 from the cash tin to pay a debt. Now Mr Venter has discovered that the money is missing, and Sipho is being blamed for the theft. ✔✔"},{"af":"**(b)** Die toneelaanwysing sê *(aside)*: Dirk praat met die **gehoor**, en Sipho en mnr. Venter hoor hom nie. Een punt vir die naam, een punt vir die doel.\n\n*Model answer:* It is an **aside**. ✔ It lets the audience hear Dirk's real, cruel intention – he wants Sipho to be punished – while the other characters on stage do not hear it. ✔","en":"**(b)** The stage direction says *(aside)*: Dirk speaks to the **audience**, and Sipho and Mr Venter do not hear him. One mark for the name, one mark for the purpose.\n\n*Model answer:* It is an **aside**. ✔ It lets the audience hear Dirk's real, cruel intention – he wants Sipho to be punished – while the other characters on stage do not hear it. ✔"},{"af":"**(c) Dramatiese ironie** = wat die **gehoor weet** + wat die **karakter nie weet nie**. In reël 3 blameer Dirk vir Sipho en in reël 5 lag hy vir Sipho se verduideliking.\n\n*Model answer:* The audience knows that Dirk stole the money himself (Scene 2), ✔ but Mr Venter does not know this and may believe Dirk when he blames Sipho. ✔","en":"**(c) Dramatic irony** = what **the audience knows** + what **the character does not know**. In line 3 Dirk blames Sipho and in line 5 he laughs at Sipho's explanation.\n\n*Model answer:* The audience knows that Dirk stole the money himself (Scene 2), ✔ but Mr Venter does not know this and may believe Dirk when he blames Sipho. ✔"},{"af":"**(d) Toneelaanwysing + motivering.** Gee lyftaal of toon (in hakies) en sê **hoekom** dit pas. 'n Aanwysing sonder rede kry net een punt.\n\n*Model answer:* *(turning to face Dirk, in a pleading voice)* ✔ – Sipho is desperate, because Dirk is the only person who can confirm that Sipho locked the shed and handed over the key. ✔","en":"**(d) Stage direction + motivation.** Give body language or tone (in brackets) and say **why** it fits. A direction without a reason earns only one mark.\n\n*Model answer:* *(turning to face Dirk, in a pleading voice)* ✔ – Sipho is desperate, because Dirk is the only person who can confirm that Sipho locked the shed and handed over the key. ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Dirk het in Toneel 2 die geld gesteel; nou word Sipho geblameer. (b) 'n Tersyde (aside) wat Dirk se ware bedoeling aan die gehoor wys. (c) Die gehoor weet Dirk is die dief; mnr. Venter weet dit nie. (d) Bv. *(turning to Dirk, pleading)* – net Dirk kan bevestig dat Sipho gesluit het.","en":"(a) Dirk stole the money in Scene 2; now Sipho is being blamed. (b) An aside that shows Dirk's real intention to the audience. (c) The audience knows Dirk is the thief; Mr Venter does not. (d) E.g. *(turning to Dirk, pleading)* – only Dirk can confirm that Sipho locked up."}},{"title":{"af":"Karakterisering, toneelaanwysings en die regisseur","en":"Characterisation, stage directions and the director"},"problem":{"af":"Gebruik weer die uittreksel uit *Sour Oranges* (Toneel 3) en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*(The packing shed on Mr Venter's citrus farm near Brits. Late afternoon. Crates of oranges are stacked against the wall. A single bulb hangs from the roof. SIPHO is sweeping. MR VENTER enters, holding an empty cash tin. DIRK follows slowly, his hands in his pockets.)*\n\n[1] MR VENTER: *(holding up the tin)* Sipho. There was two thousand rand in this tin on Friday. Now it is empty.\n\n[2] SIPHO: *(stops sweeping)* Empty, Mr Venter? I … I don't understand.\n\n[3] DIRK: *(leaning against the crates)* He understands perfectly, Pa. He was the last one in the shed.\n\n[4] SIPHO: I locked the door at five and gave the key to Dirk. You were there, Dirk.\n\n[5] DIRK: *(laughing)* Listen to him! Now it's my fault?\n\n[6] MR VENTER: *(sharply)* Let him speak, Dirk.\n\n[7] SIPHO: *(quietly, looking straight at Mr Venter)* I have worked here every Saturday for two years. Have I ever taken even one orange without asking?\n\n[8] MR VENTER: *(sighs and puts the tin down on a crate)* No. No, you haven't.\n\n[9] DIRK: *(aside)* Two years of being the perfect worker. Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\n\n[10] MR VENTER: I'll call the police in the morning. They can sort this out.\n\n[11] SIPHO: The police? Mr Venter, with a criminal record I can forget about my bursary!\n\n[12] DIRK: *(smiling)* Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\n\n*(SIPHO drops the broom. The bulb flickers and goes out. Darkness.)*\n\n[13] MR VENTER: *(in the dark)* Load-shedding. Of course. Everybody out.\n\n(a) What does the extract reveal about MR VENTER's character? Quote ONE phrase to support your answer. (2)\n\n(b) Explain how the stage directions after line 12 add to the mood of the scene. (2)\n\n(c) What could the darkness at the end of the extract symbolise? (2)\n\n(d) If you were the director, how would you instruct DIRK to say line 12? Motivate your answer. (2)","en":"Use the extract from *Sour Oranges* (Scene 3) again and answer the questions.\n\n*(The packing shed on Mr Venter's citrus farm near Brits. Late afternoon. Crates of oranges are stacked against the wall. A single bulb hangs from the roof. SIPHO is sweeping. MR VENTER enters, holding an empty cash tin. DIRK follows slowly, his hands in his pockets.)*\n\n[1] MR VENTER: *(holding up the tin)* Sipho. There was two thousand rand in this tin on Friday. Now it is empty.\n\n[2] SIPHO: *(stops sweeping)* Empty, Mr Venter? I … I don't understand.\n\n[3] DIRK: *(leaning against the crates)* He understands perfectly, Pa. He was the last one in the shed.\n\n[4] SIPHO: I locked the door at five and gave the key to Dirk. You were there, Dirk.\n\n[5] DIRK: *(laughing)* Listen to him! Now it's my fault?\n\n[6] MR VENTER: *(sharply)* Let him speak, Dirk.\n\n[7] SIPHO: *(quietly, looking straight at Mr Venter)* I have worked here every Saturday for two years. Have I ever taken even one orange without asking?\n\n[8] MR VENTER: *(sighs and puts the tin down on a crate)* No. No, you haven't.\n\n[9] DIRK: *(aside)* Two years of being the perfect worker. Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\n\n[10] MR VENTER: I'll call the police in the morning. They can sort this out.\n\n[11] SIPHO: The police? Mr Venter, with a criminal record I can forget about my bursary!\n\n[12] DIRK: *(smiling)* Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\n\n*(SIPHO drops the broom. The bulb flickers and goes out. Darkness.)*\n\n[13] MR VENTER: *(in the dark)* Load-shedding. Of course. Everybody out.\n\n(a) What does the extract reveal about MR VENTER's character? Quote ONE phrase to support your answer. (2)\n\n(b) Explain how the stage directions after line 12 add to the mood of the scene. (2)\n\n(c) What could the darkness at the end of the extract symbolise? (2)\n\n(d) If you were the director, how would you instruct DIRK to say line 12? Motivate your answer. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a) Karakter:** Gee 'n **byvoeglike naamwoord** + 'n **kort aanhaling** in aanhalingstekens. Mnr. Venter onderbreek Dirk en gee Sipho 'n kans om te praat, en hy erken dat Sipho nog nooit gesteel het nie.\n\n*Model answer:* He is fair-minded/just. ✔ He tells his son, \"Let him speak, Dirk.\" ✔ (Also accept: \"No, you haven't.\")","en":"**(a) Character:** Give an **adjective** + a **short quotation** in inverted commas. Mr Venter interrupts Dirk and gives Sipho a chance to speak, and he admits that Sipho has never stolen.\n\n*Model answer:* He is fair-minded/just. ✔ He tells his son, \"Let him speak, Dirk.\" ✔ (Also accept: \"No, you haven't.\")"},{"af":"**(b) Stemming:** Kyk wat die aanwysings **doen**: Sipho laat die besem val (skok, hopeloosheid) en die gloeilamp flikker en gaan dood (skielike donkerte).\n\n*Model answer:* Sipho dropping the broom shows his shock and despair, ✔ and the sudden darkness creates a tense, gloomy and threatening mood – the audience fears for Sipho's future. ✔","en":"**(b) Mood:** Look at what the directions **do**: Sipho drops the broom (shock, hopelessness) and the bulb flickers and goes out (sudden darkness).\n\n*Model answer:* Sipho dropping the broom shows his shock and despair, ✔ and the sudden darkness creates a tense, gloomy and threatening mood – the audience fears for Sipho's future. ✔"},{"af":"**(c) Simbool:** Dink wat donkerte in die konteks kan **voorstel** – 'n simbool staan vir 'n groter idee.\n\n*Model answer:* The darkness could symbolise Sipho's future, which suddenly looks hopeless, ✔ or the truth that is still hidden, because nobody except the audience can \"see\" that Dirk is guilty. ✔","en":"**(c) Symbol:** Think about what darkness could **stand for** in this context – a symbol represents a bigger idea.\n\n*Model answer:* The darkness could symbolise Sipho's future, which suddenly looks hopeless, ✔ or the truth that is still hidden, because nobody except the audience can \"see\" that Dirk is guilty. ✔"},{"af":"**(d) Regisseursvraag:** Gee 'n konkrete instruksie (toon + lyftaal) en motiveer uit die teks. Die aanwysing *(smiling)* en die woorde *shouldn't you?* wys dat Dirk Sipho spot.\n\n*Model answer:* I would tell Dirk to say it slowly in a mocking voice, with a cold smile, while looking Sipho straight in the eye. ✔ He enjoys watching Sipho suffer for a theft that he committed himself. ✔","en":"**(d) Director question:** Give a concrete instruction (tone + body language) and motivate it from the text. The direction *(smiling)* and the words *shouldn't you?* show that Dirk mocks Sipho.\n\n*Model answer:* I would tell Dirk to say it slowly in a mocking voice, with a cold smile, while looking Sipho straight in the eye. ✔ He enjoys watching Sipho suffer for a theft that he committed himself. ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Regverdig – \"Let him speak, Dirk.\" (b) Die laat val van die besem en die skielike donkerte skep 'n gespanne, somber stemming. (c) Sipho se hopelose toekoms of die verborge waarheid. (d) Stadig, spottend, met 'n koue glimlag – hy geniet Sipho se lyding.","en":"(a) Fair – \"Let him speak, Dirk.\" (b) The dropped broom and the sudden darkness create a tense, gloomy mood. (c) Sipho's hopeless future or the hidden truth. (d) Slowly, mockingly, with a cold smile – he enjoys Sipho's suffering."}},{"title":{"af":"Alleenspraak, innerlike konflik en 'n evalueringsvraag","en":"Soliloquy, internal conflict and an evaluation question"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die uittreksel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Background:* This extract comes from Scene 4 of **Sour Oranges** (own example), later that same night. Earlier, DIRK stole R2 000 from his father's cash tin and blamed SIPHO, a hard-working farm worker who now faces the police and could lose his bursary.\n\n*(The packing shed is dark except for the light of DIRK's cellphone torch. DIRK is alone. He sits on a crate, holding the empty cash tin.)*\n\n[1] DIRK: Sipho will lose his bursary. Pa will call the police. And me? I'll sleep in my warm bed tonight.\n\n*(He laughs, but the laugh dies quickly.)*\n\n[2] Why don't I feel better? I paid them back. Nobody is coming to look for me now.\n\n*(He stands up, walks to the broom that SIPHO dropped and picks it up.)*\n\n[3] Two years he swept this floor. Two years, and never one orange without asking. *(bitterly)* Pa trusts him more than he trusts me. Maybe Pa is right.\n\n*(He puts the tin down, takes out his phone and starts dialling – then stops.)*\n\n[4] If I tell the truth, I lose everything. If I keep quiet, Sipho loses everything.\n\n*(The lights fade slowly to black.)*\n\n(a) Is this speech a monologue or a soliloquy? Give a reason for your answer. (2)\n\n(b) Describe DIRK's internal conflict in this extract. Quote to support your answer. (2)\n\n(c) Describe DIRK's tone in line 3 and explain why he feels this way. (2)\n\n(d) Do you sympathise with DIRK? Discuss your view. (3)","en":"Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\n*Background:* This extract comes from Scene 4 of **Sour Oranges** (own example), later that same night. Earlier, DIRK stole R2 000 from his father's cash tin and blamed SIPHO, a hard-working farm worker who now faces the police and could lose his bursary.\n\n*(The packing shed is dark except for the light of DIRK's cellphone torch. DIRK is alone. He sits on a crate, holding the empty cash tin.)*\n\n[1] DIRK: Sipho will lose his bursary. Pa will call the police. And me? I'll sleep in my warm bed tonight.\n\n*(He laughs, but the laugh dies quickly.)*\n\n[2] Why don't I feel better? I paid them back. Nobody is coming to look for me now.\n\n*(He stands up, walks to the broom that SIPHO dropped and picks it up.)*\n\n[3] Two years he swept this floor. Two years, and never one orange without asking. *(bitterly)* Pa trusts him more than he trusts me. Maybe Pa is right.\n\n*(He puts the tin down, takes out his phone and starts dialling – then stops.)*\n\n[4] If I tell the truth, I lose everything. If I keep quiet, Sipho loses everything.\n\n*(The lights fade slowly to black.)*\n\n(a) Is this speech a monologue or a soliloquy? Give a reason for your answer. (2)\n\n(b) Describe DIRK's internal conflict in this extract. Quote to support your answer. (2)\n\n(c) Describe DIRK's tone in line 3 and explain why he feels this way. (2)\n\n(d) Do you sympathise with DIRK? Discuss your view. (3)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a)** Kyk na die toneelaanwysing: *DIRK is alone*. 'n Monoloog word aan ander karakters gerig; 'n alleenspraak word gesê wanneer die karakter **alleen** is.\n\n*Model answer:* It is a **soliloquy**, ✔ because Dirk is alone on stage and speaks his private thoughts aloud. ✔","en":"**(a)** Look at the stage direction: *DIRK is alone*. A monologue is directed at other characters; a soliloquy is spoken when the character is **alone**.\n\n*Model answer:* It is a **soliloquy**, ✔ because Dirk is alone on stage and speaks his private thoughts aloud. ✔"},{"af":"**(b) Innerlike konflik** = 'n stryd **binne** die karakter. Reël 4 gee die twee kante van sy keuse.\n\n*Model answer:* Dirk struggles between protecting himself and doing the right thing by telling the truth. ✔ \"If I tell the truth, I lose everything. If I keep quiet, Sipho loses everything.\" ✔","en":"**(b) Internal conflict** = a struggle **inside** the character. Line 4 gives the two sides of his choice.\n\n*Model answer:* Dirk struggles between protecting himself and doing the right thing by telling the truth. ✔ \"If I tell the truth, I lose everything. If I keep quiet, Sipho loses everything.\" ✔"},{"af":"**(c) Toon:** Die aanwysing *(bitterly)* gee die toon. Verduidelik dan die **rede** uit die teks.\n\n*Model answer:* His tone is bitter/jealous. ✔ He resents the fact that his father trusts a worker more than his own son – and he secretly knows that his father is right. ✔","en":"**(c) Tone:** The direction *(bitterly)* gives the tone. Then explain the **reason** from the text.\n\n*Model answer:* His tone is bitter/jealous. ✔ He resents the fact that his father trusts a worker more than his own son – and he secretly knows that his father is right. ✔"},{"af":"**(d) Evaluering (3 punte):** Neem 'n **standpunt** en gee **twee redes** uit die teks. Albei kante kan volpunte kry as jy dit motiveer.\n\n*Model answer (No):* No. ✔ Although Dirk feels guilty (\"Why don't I feel better?\") and was under pressure because of his debt, he chose to steal and then deliberately blamed an innocent worker. ✔ Even now he stops dialling, so he is still letting Sipho suffer for his crime. ✔\n\n*Model answer (Yes, partly):* Partly, because he is jealous of the trust Sipho gets, he is scared, and he starts to phone – a sign that his conscience is waking up.","en":"**(d) Evaluation (3 marks):** Take a **stand** and give **two reasons** from the text. Either side can earn full marks if you motivate it.\n\n*Model answer (No):* No. ✔ Although Dirk feels guilty (\"Why don't I feel better?\") and was under pressure because of his debt, he chose to steal and then deliberately blamed an innocent worker. ✔ Even now he stops dialling, so he is still letting Sipho suffer for his crime. ✔\n\n*Model answer (Yes, partly):* Partly, because he is jealous of the trust Sipho gets, he is scared, and he starts to phone – a sign that his conscience is waking up."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Alleenspraak – hy is alleen en dink hardop. (b) Homself beskerm teenoor die waarheid praat – \"If I tell the truth, I lose everything …\" (c) Bitter/jaloers – sy pa vertrou Sipho meer. (d) Standpunt + twee redes uit die teks, bv. Nee: hy het gesteel en 'n onskuldige geblameer.","en":"(a) Soliloquy – he is alone and thinks aloud. (b) Protecting himself versus telling the truth – \"If I tell the truth, I lose everything …\" (c) Bitter/jealous – his father trusts Sipho more. (d) A stand + two reasons from the text, e.g. No: he stole and blamed an innocent person."}},{"title":{"af":"Komedie, tersyde en situasie-ironie","en":"Comedy, aside and situational irony"},"problem":{"af":"Lees die uittreksel en beantwoord die vrae.\n\n*Background:* **The Braai** (own example) is a one-act play. TANNIE MARIE has invited the new neighbours, the Mokoenas, for a braai. Her husband, OOM SAREL, has promised to light the fire \"like a professional\".\n\n*(A back garden in Hartbeespoort. Sunday afternoon. Smoke everywhere. OOM SAREL is waving a piece of cardboard at a braai with no flames. TANNIE MARIE enters with a tray of raw meat.)*\n\n[1] TANNIE MARIE: *(sweetly)* How is the fire, my love?\n\n[2] OOM SAREL: *(coughing)* Perfect. It's … resting.\n\n[3] TANNIE MARIE: *(to the audience)* Resting. For two hours.\n\n*(MR MOKOENA enters with a bag of charcoal and a box of firelighters.)*\n\n[4] MR MOKOENA: I thought you might need these, neighbour.\n\n[5] OOM SAREL: *(proudly, throwing the cardboard away)* Never! A real man needs only wood and patience!\n\n*(A loud BANG from the braai. A cloud of black smoke. When it clears, OOM SAREL's face is black with soot.)*\n\n[6] OOM SAREL: *(calmly)* … Perhaps one firelighter.\n\n(a) Is this extract from a comedy or a tragedy? Give TWO reasons from the extract. (2)\n\n(b) Name the dramatic device in line 3 and explain what it adds to the scene. (2)\n\n(c) Explain the situational irony in lines 5–6 and how the stage directions make it funny. (2)","en":"Read the extract and answer the questions.\n\n*Background:* **The Braai** (own example) is a one-act play. TANNIE MARIE has invited the new neighbours, the Mokoenas, for a braai. Her husband, OOM SAREL, has promised to light the fire \"like a professional\".\n\n*(A back garden in Hartbeespoort. Sunday afternoon. Smoke everywhere. OOM SAREL is waving a piece of cardboard at a braai with no flames. TANNIE MARIE enters with a tray of raw meat.)*\n\n[1] TANNIE MARIE: *(sweetly)* How is the fire, my love?\n\n[2] OOM SAREL: *(coughing)* Perfect. It's … resting.\n\n[3] TANNIE MARIE: *(to the audience)* Resting. For two hours.\n\n*(MR MOKOENA enters with a bag of charcoal and a box of firelighters.)*\n\n[4] MR MOKOENA: I thought you might need these, neighbour.\n\n[5] OOM SAREL: *(proudly, throwing the cardboard away)* Never! A real man needs only wood and patience!\n\n*(A loud BANG from the braai. A cloud of black smoke. When it clears, OOM SAREL's face is black with soot.)*\n\n[6] OOM SAREL: *(calmly)* … Perhaps one firelighter.\n\n(a) Is this extract from a comedy or a tragedy? Give TWO reasons from the extract. (2)\n\n(b) Name the dramatic device in line 3 and explain what it adds to the scene. (2)\n\n(c) Explain the situational irony in lines 5–6 and how the stage directions make it funny. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a) Komedie of tragedie?** Soek kenmerke: humor, oordrywing, 'n lighartige situasie, geen ernstige gevolge nie.\n\n*Model answer:* It is a comedy. ✔ The situation is light-hearted and funny (a man who cannot light a braai but refuses help), and the ending is humorous rather than serious – he is only covered in soot. ✔","en":"**(a) Comedy or tragedy?** Look for features: humour, exaggeration, a light-hearted situation, no serious consequences.\n\n*Model answer:* It is a comedy. ✔ The situation is light-hearted and funny (a man who cannot light a braai but refuses help), and the ending is humorous rather than serious – he is only covered in soot. ✔"},{"af":"**(b)** Die aanwysing *(to the audience)* terwyl Oom Sarel op die verhoog is, wys dit is 'n **aside** (tersyde). Haar herhaling van sy woord *Resting* is sarkasties.\n\n*Model answer:* It is an **aside**. ✔ Tannie Marie shares her sarcastic disbelief with the audience – the fire has been \"resting\" for two hours, so we know Oom Sarel's excuse is nonsense, and we laugh with her. ✔","en":"**(b)** The direction *(to the audience)* while Oom Sarel is on stage shows that it is an **aside**. Her repetition of his word *Resting* is sarcastic.\n\n*Model answer:* It is an **aside**. ✔ Tannie Marie shares her sarcastic disbelief with the audience – the fire has been \"resting\" for two hours, so we know Oom Sarel's excuse is nonsense, and we laugh with her. ✔"},{"af":"**(c) Situasie-ironie** = die teenoorgestelde gebeur van wat verwag word. Oom Sarel spog dat 'n regte man net hout en geduld nodig het – en dadelik ontplof die vuur. Die aanwysings *(A loud BANG …)* en *(calmly)* skep die humor.\n\n*Model answer:* Oom Sarel boasts that \"A real man needs only wood and patience\", but immediately the braai explodes and covers his face in soot. ✔ The loud bang and his calm reply, \"Perhaps one firelighter\", are funny because his pride is suddenly punctured and he pretends nothing happened. ✔","en":"**(c) Situational irony** = the opposite of what is expected happens. Oom Sarel boasts that a real man needs only wood and patience – and immediately the fire explodes. The directions *(A loud BANG …)* and *(calmly)* create the humour.\n\n*Model answer:* Oom Sarel boasts that \"A real man needs only wood and patience\", but immediately the braai explodes and covers his face in soot. ✔ The loud bang and his calm reply, \"Perhaps one firelighter\", are funny because his pride is suddenly punctured and he pretends nothing happened. ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Komedie – lighartig en snaaks; geen ernstige gevolge nie. (b) 'n Tersyde (aside) – sy deel haar sarkasme met die gehoor. (c) Hy spog en dadelik ontplof die vuur; sy kalm \"Perhaps one firelighter\" maak dit snaaks.","en":"(a) Comedy – light-hearted and funny; no serious consequences. (b) An aside – she shares her sarcasm with the audience. (c) He boasts and the fire immediately explodes; his calm \"Perhaps one firelighter\" makes it funny."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat noem ons 'n toespraak waarin 'n karakter wat **alleen** op die verhoog is, sy gedagtes hardop sê?","en":"What do we call a speech in which a character who is **alone** on stage speaks his thoughts aloud?"},"options":[{"af":"monologue","en":"monologue"},{"af":"soliloquy","en":"soliloquy"},{"af":"aside","en":"aside"},{"af":"dialogue","en":"dialogue"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"'n **Soliloquy** (alleenspraak) word gesê wanneer die karakter alleen is. 'n Monoloog word aan ander karakters gerig, en 'n tersyde (aside) is 'n kort opmerking aan die gehoor terwyl ander op die verhoog is.","en":"A **soliloquy** is spoken when the character is alone. A monologue is directed at other characters, and an aside is a short remark to the audience while others are on stage."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"'n Drama word in *acts* (bedrywe) verdeel, en elke bedryf word in kleiner dele verdeel wat ___ genoem word.","en":"A play is divided into acts, and each act is divided into smaller parts called ___."},"answers":{"af":["scenes","scene","tonele","toneel"],"en":["scenes","scene"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["chapters","stanzas","paragraphs"],"en":["chapters","stanzas","paragraphs"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Drama het **acts and scenes** (bedrywe en tonele). 'n Roman het hoofstukke (chapters) en 'n gedig strofes (stanzas).","en":"A play has **acts and scenes**. A novel has chapters and a poem has stanzas."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"Toneelaanwysings (stage directions) word tydens 'n opvoering hardop deur die akteurs gesê.","en":"Stage directions are read aloud by the actors during a performance."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Toneelaanwysings staan in kursief of tussen hakies en word **nie** gesê nie – die akteurs **doen** dit (beweging, toon), en die regisseur gebruik dit vir beligting, rekwisiete en klank.","en":"False. Stage directions are in italics or brackets and are **not** spoken – the actors **act them out** (movement, tone), and the director uses them for lighting, props and sound."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Die persoon wat besluit hoe 'n drama op die verhoog aangebied word en vir die akteurs sê hoe om te beweeg en te praat, is die ___.","en":"The person who decides how a play is staged and tells the actors how to move and speak is the ___."},"answers":{"af":["director","the director","regisseur","die regisseur"],"en":["director","the director"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["playwright","narrator","audience"],"en":["playwright","narrator","audience"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die **director** (regisseur) lei die opvoering. Die **playwright** (dramaturg) het die teks geskryf, en 'n drama het geen verteller (narrator) nie.","en":"The **director** leads the performance. The **playwright** wrote the script, and a play has no narrator."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter stadium van die intrige is die keerpunt waar die spanning die hoogste is?","en":"Which stage of the plot is the turning point where the tension is at its highest?"},"options":[{"af":"exposition","en":"exposition"},{"af":"rising action","en":"rising action"},{"af":"climax","en":"climax"},{"af":"resolution","en":"resolution"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die **climax** (klimaks) is die keerpunt. In die rising action bou die spanning nog op, en in die resolution (ontknoping) word die konflik opgelos.","en":"The **climax** is the turning point. In the rising action the tension is still building, and in the resolution the conflict is resolved."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"In 'n **tragedy** (tragedie) eindig die hoofkarakter gewoonlik met sy ondergang of dood, dikwels weens 'n swakheid of 'n verkeerde keuse.","en":"In a **tragedy** the main character usually ends in downfall or death, often because of a weakness or a wrong choice."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Dit is die kenmerk van 'n tragedie. 'n Komedie (comedy) is lighartig en eindig gelukkig.","en":"True. That is the key feature of a tragedy. A comedy is light-hearted and ends happily."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke dramatiese tegniek by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each dramatic device to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Soliloquy (alleenspraak)","en":"Soliloquy"},"r":{"af":"(Alone on stage) NANDI: Should I tell them the truth, or keep quiet and save myself?","en":"(Alone on stage) NANDI: Should I tell them the truth, or keep quiet and save myself?"}},{"l":{"af":"Aside (tersyde)","en":"Aside"},"r":{"af":"(The others keep talking.) JOHAN: (to the audience) They have no idea that I failed the test.","en":"(The others keep talking.) JOHAN: (to the audience) They have no idea that I failed the test."}},{"l":{"af":"Stage direction (toneelaanwysing)","en":"Stage direction"},"r":{"af":"(The lights dim. Thunder rumbles in the distance.)","en":"(The lights dim. Thunder rumbles in the distance.)"}},{"l":{"af":"Monologue (monoloog)","en":"Monologue"},"r":{"af":"COACH: (to the whole team) Listen to me, all of you. Ten years ago I stood where you are standing now … (the speech continues for twenty lines)","en":"COACH: (to the whole team) Listen to me, all of you. Ten years ago I stood where you are standing now … (the speech continues for twenty lines)"}}],"explain":{"af":"Alleenspraak: Nandi is **alleen**. Tersyde: Johan praat **net met die gehoor** terwyl ander op die verhoog is. Toneelaanwysing: beligting en klank tussen hakies. Monoloog: 'n **lang** toespraak aan **ander karakters**.","en":"Soliloquy: Nandi is **alone**. Aside: Johan speaks **only to the audience** while others are on stage. Stage direction: lighting and sound in brackets. Monologue: a **long** speech to **other characters**."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Toneelaanwysings soos *(angrily)* of *(in a whisper)* wys hoe 'n reël gesê moet word. Hulle wys dus die karakter se ___ (sy houding soos ons dit in sy stem hoor).","en":"Stage directions such as *(angrily)* or *(in a whisper)* show how a line must be said. They therefore show the character's ___ (his attitude as we hear it in his voice)."},"answers":{"af":["tone","toon","tone of voice"],"en":["tone","tone of voice"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["mood","setting","plot"],"en":["mood","setting","plot"]}},"explain":{"af":"**Tone** (toon) is die karakter se houding in sy stem. Moenie dit met **mood** (stemming) verwar nie – dit is die atmosfeer wat die gehoor beleef.","en":"**Tone** is the character's attitude in his voice. Don't confuse it with **mood** – the atmosphere the audience experiences."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Daar is geen verteller in 'n drama nie. Hoe leer die gehoor die karakters **hoofsaaklik** ken?","en":"There is no narrator in a play. How does the audience **mainly** get to know the characters?"},"options":[{"af":"Uit die verteller se beskrywings van elke karakter","en":"From the narrator's descriptions of each character"},{"af":"Net uit die rolverdeling (cast list) aan die begin","en":"Only from the cast list at the beginning"},{"af":"Uit die titel van die drama","en":"From the title of the play"},{"af":"Deur wat die karakters sê en doen en hoe ander op hulle reageer","en":"Through what the characters say and do, and how others react to them"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"In 'n drama is karakterisering **indirek**: deur dialoog (wat en hoe iets gesê word), aksies in die toneelaanwysings en ander karakters se reaksies. Die rolverdeling gee hoogstens 'n kort beskrywing.","en":"In a play characterisation is **indirect**: through dialogue (what is said and how), actions in the stage directions and other characters' reactions. The cast list gives at most a short description."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lerato wil haar beste vriendin beskerm, maar sy weet sy moet die waarheid vir die hoof vertel. Hierdie stryd binne haar eie gemoed is ___ conflict.","en":"Lerato wants to protect her best friend, but she knows she must tell the principal the truth. This struggle inside her own mind is ___ conflict."},"answers":{"af":["internal","inner","innerlike","internal conflict"],"en":["internal","inner","internal conflict"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["external","social","physical"],"en":["external","social","physical"]}},"explain":{"af":"'n Stryd **binne** 'n karakter (lojaliteit teenoor eerlikheid) is **internal conflict** (innerlike konflik). External conflict is teen 'n ander karakter, die samelewing of die natuur.","en":"A struggle **inside** a character (loyalty versus honesty) is **internal conflict**. External conflict is against another character, society or nature."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die reël: *MRS NAIDOO: (looking up at the dark rain clouds) Oh, wonderful. Rain. Just what we needed for our picnic.* Wat is mev. Naidoo se toon?","en":"Read the line: *MRS NAIDOO: (looking up at the dark rain clouds) Oh, wonderful. Rain. Just what we needed for our picnic.* What is Mrs Naidoo's tone?"},"options":[{"af":"sarcastic","en":"sarcastic"},{"af":"grateful","en":"grateful"},{"af":"excited","en":"excited"},{"af":"nostalgic","en":"nostalgic"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Sy sê *wonderful*, maar reën bederf haar piekniek – sy bedoel die teenoorgestelde. Dit is 'n **sarcastic** (sarkastiese) toon. *Grateful* is die letterlike (verkeerde) lees.","en":"She says *wonderful*, but rain will spoil her picnic – she means the opposite. That is a **sarcastic** tone. *Grateful* is the literal (wrong) reading."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"In Toneel 1 sien die gehoor hoe Thabo die venster met sy rugbybal breek. In Toneel 2 blameer sy ma die buurman se seun. Omdat die gehoor meer weet as die ma, is dit ___ irony.","en":"In Scene 1 the audience sees Thabo break the window with his rugby ball. In Scene 2 his mother blames the neighbour's son. Because the audience knows more than the mother, this is ___ irony."},"answers":{"af":["dramatic","dramatic irony","dramatiese","dramatiese ironie"],"en":["dramatic","dramatic irony"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["verbal","situational","comic"],"en":["verbal","situational","comic"]}},"explain":{"af":"Wanneer die **gehoor meer weet as 'n karakter**, is dit **dramatic irony** (dramatiese ironie). Verbale ironie is om die teenoorgestelde te sê van wat jy bedoel; situasie-ironie is wanneer die teenoorgestelde gebeur van wat verwag is.","en":"When the **audience knows more than a character**, it is **dramatic irony**. Verbal irony is saying the opposite of what you mean; situational irony is when the opposite of what was expected happens."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die toneelaanwysing: *(A hospital waiting room. Midnight. ZANELE paces up and down. The clock on the wall ticks loudly. Every few seconds she looks at the closed door.)* Watter stemming skep hierdie aanwysing?","en":"Read the stage direction: *(A hospital waiting room. Midnight. ZANELE paces up and down. The clock on the wall ticks loudly. Every few seconds she looks at the closed door.)* What mood does this direction create?"},"options":[{"af":"ontspanne en vrolik","en":"relaxed and cheerful"},{"af":"gespanne en angstig","en":"tense and anxious"},{"af":"romanties","en":"romantic"},{"af":"humoristies","en":"humorous"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"Middernag in 'n hospitaal, 'n luide tikkende horlosie, Zanele wat op en af loop en na die toe deur kyk – alles wys wag en bekommernis. Die stemming is **gespanne en angstig** (tense and anxious).","en":"Midnight in a hospital, a loudly ticking clock, Zanele pacing and looking at the closed door – everything suggests waiting and worry. The mood is **tense and anxious**."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"In 'n drama probeer 'n pa telkens sy oorlede seun se ou radio regmaak, maar hy maak dit nooit klaar nie. Wat simboliseer die stukkende radio heel waarskynlik?","en":"In a play, a father keeps trying to fix his late son's old radio, but he never finishes the job. What does the broken radio most likely symbolise?"},"options":[{"af":"Die pa se liefde vir musiek","en":"The father's love of music"},{"af":"Die gesin se rykdom","en":"The family's wealth"},{"af":"Moderne tegnologie","en":"Modern technology"},{"af":"Die pa se rou en dat hy nie sy seun kan laat gaan nie","en":"The father's grief and his inability to let go of his son"}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Die radio behoort aan die **oorlede** seun, en die pa kan dit nooit **klaar** regmaak nie – net soos hy nie oor sy verlies kan kom nie. 'n Simbool staan vir 'n groter idee; die ander opsies het geen steun in die situasie nie.","en":"The radio belonged to the **late** son, and the father can never **finish** fixing it – just as he cannot get over his loss. A symbol stands for a bigger idea; the other options have no support in the situation."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Die gehoor weet dat Dirk die geld gesteel het. Terwyl Sipho geblameer word, sê Dirk *(smiling)*: \"Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\" Watter antwoord op *What does this line reveal about Dirk's character? (2)* kry **albei** punte?","en":"The audience knows that Dirk stole the money. While Sipho is blamed, Dirk says *(smiling)*: \"Should have thought of that before, shouldn't you?\" Which answer to *What does this line reveal about Dirk's character? (2)* earns **both** marks?"},"options":[{"af":"Dirk is smiling.","en":"Dirk is smiling."},{"af":"Dirk is a kind person who wants to help Sipho.","en":"Dirk is a kind person who wants to help Sipho."},{"af":"Dirk is cruel and dishonest: he smiles while Sipho is blamed for a theft that Dirk committed himself.","en":"Dirk is cruel and dishonest: he smiles while Sipho is blamed for a theft that Dirk committed himself."},{"af":"Dirk is cruel.","en":"Dirk is cruel."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Vir 2 punte gee jy 'n **eienskap** + **bewys/verduideliking** uit die teks. *Dirk is cruel* kry net 1 punt (geen bewys nie); *Dirk is smiling* herhaal net die toneelaanwysing; *kind* is verkeerd.","en":"For 2 marks you give a **quality** + **evidence/explanation** from the text. *Dirk is cruel* earns only 1 mark (no evidence); *Dirk is smiling* only repeats the stage direction; *kind* is wrong."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Dirk sê as 'n tersyde (aside): \"Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\" Sipho en mnr. Venter is ook op die verhoog. As jy die regisseur was, watter instruksie pas die beste by hierdie reël?","en":"Dirk says as an aside: \"Let's see how perfect he looks after tonight.\" Sipho and Mr Venter are also on stage. If you were the director, which instruction suits this line best?"},"options":[{"af":"Draai effens na die gehoor en sê dit sag met 'n koue glimlag, sodat die ander dit nie hoor nie.","en":"Turn slightly towards the audience and say it softly with a cold smile, so that the others do not hear it."},{"af":"Skree dit hard in Sipho se gesig sodat almal dit hoor.","en":"Shout it loudly in Sipho's face so that everyone hears it."},{"af":"Fluister dit in sy pa se oor.","en":"Whisper it into his father's ear."},{"af":"Sê dit terwyl hy huil, met sy rug na die gehoor.","en":"Say it while crying, with his back to the audience."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Tersyde is vir die **gehoor** bedoel en die ander karakters hoor dit nie – daarom draai hy na die gehoor en praat sag. Die *koue glimlag* pas by sy wrede bedoeling. Skree of fluister vir 'n ander karakter breek die tersyde, en huil pas nie by sy toon nie.","en":"An aside is meant for the **audience** and the other characters do not hear it – so he turns to the audience and speaks softly. The *cold smile* suits his cruel intention. Shouting or whispering to another character breaks the aside, and crying does not suit his tone."}}]},{"id":"eng10-t4-vocabulary-critical-language","title":{"af":"Woordeskat, beeldspraak en kritiese taalbewustheid","en":"Vocabulary, figurative language and critical language awareness"},"blurb":{"af":"Jy sal sinonieme, antonieme, woordvorms, idiome en stylfigure in konteks kan gebruik en verduidelik, en feite, menings, partydigheid en manipulerende taal in tekste kan raaksien.","en":"You will be able to use and explain synonyms, antonyms, word forms, idioms and figures of speech in context, and spot facts, opinions, bias and manipulative language in texts."},"summary":{"af":"## Woordeskat (vocabulary)\n\n### Sinonieme en antonieme\n- **Synonym** (sinoniem): dieselfde of byna dieselfde betekenis: *big – large, begin – commence, brave – courageous*.\n- **Antonym** (antoniem): die teenoorgestelde betekenis: *generous – mean, ancient – modern*.\n\nBaie antonieme word met 'n **prefix** (voorvoegsel) gevorm:\n\n| Prefix | Wanneer | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| un- | baie algemeen | unhappy, unfair |\n| in- | algemeen | incorrect, invisible |\n| im- | voor **m** en **p** | immature, impossible |\n| ir- | voor **r** | irresponsible, irregular |\n| il- | voor **l** | illegal, illogical |\n| dis- | nie / teenoorgestelde | dishonest, disagree |\n\n> **Wenk:** Jou sinoniem of antoniem moet **dieselfde woordsoort en tyd** hê as die woord in die sin: *He **purchased** a bike* → *bought* (nie *buy* nie).\n\n### Homonieme en homofone\n- **Homonyms** (homonieme): dieselfde spelling en uitspraak, verskillende betekenisse: *bat* (kolf/vlermuis), *bank* (geldbank/rivieroewer).\n- **Homophones** (homofone): klink dieselfde, maar spelling en betekenis verskil: *see/sea, weather/whether, peace/piece, brake/break*.\n\n### Voor- en agtervoegsels en woordfamilies\nPrefixes verander die **betekenis**: **dis-** (nie: *disconnect*), **mis-** (verkeerd: *misunderstand*), **re-** (weer: *rewrite*), **pre-** (vooraf: *prepaid*). Suffixes (agtervoegsels) verander dikwels die **woordsoort**:\n\n| Suffix | Maak 'n … | Voorbeelde |\n|---|---|---|\n| -ful / -less | b.nw. (vol van / sonder) | hopeful, careless |\n| -ness | s.nw. (toestand) | kindness, happiness |\n| -ment | s.nw. uit 'n werkwoord | payment, enjoyment |\n| -able | b.nw. (kan gedoen word) | washable, believable |\n| -ly | bywoord | quickly, happily |\n\nSpelling: *y* word *i* (*happy → happiness, beauty → beautiful*); die *e* val soms weg (*argue → argument, believe → believable*).\n\n'n **Word family** (woordfamilie) is woorde met dieselfde stam:\n\n| Werkwoord | S.nw. | B.nw. | Bywoord |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| decide | decision | decisive | decisively |\n| beautify | beauty | beautiful | beautifully |\n| succeed | success | successful | successfully |\n| create | creation | creative | creatively |\n\n> **Metode:** Kyk na die woorde om die oop spasie. Ná *a/the/her* volg 'n s.nw. (*her kindness*); voor 'n s.nw. kom 'n b.nw. (*a successful farmer*); 'n werkwoord word deur 'n bywoord beskryf (*she sang beautifully*).\n\n### Idiome en spreekwoorde\n'n **Idiom** (idioom) is 'n vaste uitdrukking wat **nie letterlik** bedoel word nie. 'n **Proverb** (spreekwoord) is 'n kort, bekende sin wat raad of 'n les gee.\n\n| Uitdrukking | Betekenis |\n|---|---|\n| a piece of cake | baie maklik |\n| break the ice | die eerste ongemak tussen mense breek |\n| let the cat out of the bag | 'n geheim per ongeluk verklap |\n| once in a blue moon | baie selde |\n| under the weather | effens siek |\n| Don't count your chickens before they hatch. | Moenie op iets reken voordat dit gebeur het nie. |\n| Every cloud has a silver lining. | Daar is iets goeds in elke slegte situasie. |\n| Look before you leap. | Dink voordat jy iets doen. |\n\n> **Algemene fout:** Afrikaanse idiome letterlik vertaal: *Ek het 'n appeltjie met jou te skil* = **I have a bone to pick with you**, nie \"an apple to peel\" nie.\n\n### Beeldspraak (figurative language)\n\n| Stylfiguur | Wat dit is | Voorbeeld |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Simile** (vergelyking) | vergelyk met *like/as* | as brave as a lion |\n| **Metaphor** (metafoor) | sê iets **is** iets anders | The classroom was a zoo. |\n| **Personification** (personifikasie) | menslike eienskappe vir iets nie-menslik | The sun smiled on the Magaliesberg. |\n| **Hyperbole** (hiperbool) | doelbewuste oordrywing | I've told you a million times! |\n| **Pun** (woordspeling) | speel met twee betekenisse of klanke | A bicycle can't stand on its own because it is two-tired. |\n| **Irony** (ironie) | die teenoorgestelde van wat bedoel of verwag word | A fire station burns down. |\n| **Sarcasm** (sarkasme) | spottende ironie wat seermaak | \"Great job!\" (when someone drops the cake) |\n| **Euphemism** (eufemisme) | sagte woord vir iets onaangenaams | passed away (= died) |\n| **Alliteration** (alliterasie) | herhaling van beginkonsonante | brave boys from Brits |\n| **Onomatopoeia** (klanknabootsing) | die woord boots 'n klank na | buzz, crash, hiss |\n| **Rhetorical question** (retoriese vraag) | vraag vir effek; geen antwoord word verwag nie | Who wants to live in a dirty town? |\n\n> **Eksamenformule:** noem die stylfiguur → verduidelik wat met wat vergelyk word → gee die effek.\n\n## Kritiese taalbewustheid (critical language awareness)\n\nJy ondersoek **hoe** taal gebruik word om jou te beïnvloed.\n\n- **Fact** (feit): kan **bewys of nagegaan** word: *Brits is in the North West.* **Opinion** (mening): 'n persoonlike oordeel: *Brits is the best town in South Africa.* Leidrade: *I think, best, worst, should, amazing*. Gee altyd 'n **rede**.\n- **Denotation** (denotasie): die woordeboekbetekenis. **Connotation** (konnotasie): die gevoelens wat 'n woord oproep: *slim* (positief) – *thin* (neutraal) – *skinny* (negatief); *curious* teenoor *nosy*; *affordable* teenoor *cheap*.\n- **Emotive language** (emotiewe taal) wek sterk gevoelens (*heartless, innocent, tragic*). **Manipulative language** (manipulerende taal) oorreed onregverdig: oordrywing, halwe waarhede, vrees, vleitaal, *everyone is doing it*.\n- **Bias** (partydigheid): net een kant word gewys of bevoordeel.\n- **Stereotyping** (stereotipering): almal in 'n groep word as dieselfde voorgestel: *Teenagers are lazy. Girls can't fix cars.*\n- **Sexist language** (seksistiese taal) – gebruik geslagsneutrale woorde: chairman → **chairperson**, policeman → **police officer**, fireman → **firefighter**, mankind → **humankind**; *Every learner must bring his book* → *All learners must bring their books*.\n- **Register** pas by die **gehoor** en doel: formeel vir 'n brief aan die munisipaliteit, informeel vir 'n vriend. **Slang** (sleng) is baie informele groepstaal (*eish, chilled*); **jargon** is vakwoorde (*bandwidth, offside*) – reg vir kenners, verwarrend vir ander.\n\n> **Neutraal herskryf:** haal emotiewe woorde en veralgemenings (*all, always, typical*) uit, vervang seksistiese woorde en hou by feite: *Typical lazy teenagers are always on their phones* → *Some teenagers spend many hours on their phones.*","en":"## Vocabulary\n\n### Synonyms and antonyms\n- **Synonym:** the same or almost the same meaning: *big – large, begin – commence, brave – courageous*.\n- **Antonym:** the opposite meaning: *generous – mean, ancient – modern*.\n\nMany antonyms are formed with a **prefix**:\n\n| Prefix | When | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| un- | very common | unhappy, unfair |\n| in- | common | incorrect, invisible |\n| im- | before **m** and **p** | immature, impossible |\n| ir- | before **r** | irresponsible, irregular |\n| il- | before **l** | illegal, illogical |\n| dis- | not / opposite | dishonest, disagree |\n\n> **Tip:** Your synonym or antonym must be the **same part of speech and tense** as the word in the sentence: *He **purchased** a bike* → *bought* (not *buy*).\n\n### Homonyms and homophones\n- **Homonyms:** same spelling and pronunciation, different meanings: *bat* (cricket bat/animal), *bank* (money/river bank).\n- **Homophones:** sound the same, but spelling and meaning differ: *see/sea, weather/whether, peace/piece, brake/break*.\n\n### Prefixes, suffixes and word families\nPrefixes change the **meaning**: **dis-** (not: *disconnect*), **mis-** (wrongly: *misunderstand*), **re-** (again: *rewrite*), **pre-** (before: *prepaid*). Suffixes often change the **part of speech**:\n\n| Suffix | Makes a … | Examples |\n|---|---|---|\n| -ful / -less | adjective (full of / without) | hopeful, careless |\n| -ness | noun (state) | kindness, happiness |\n| -ment | noun from a verb | payment, enjoyment |\n| -able | adjective (can be done) | washable, believable |\n| -ly | adverb | quickly, happily |\n\nSpelling: *y* changes to *i* (*happy → happiness, beauty → beautiful*); the *e* is sometimes dropped (*argue → argument, believe → believable*).\n\nA **word family** is a group of words with the same root:\n\n| Verb | Noun | Adjective | Adverb |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| decide | decision | decisive | decisively |\n| beautify | beauty | beautiful | beautifully |\n| succeed | success | successful | successfully |\n| create | creation | creative | creatively |\n\n> **Method:** Look at the words around the gap. After *a/the/her* comes a noun (*her kindness*); before a noun comes an adjective (*a successful farmer*); a verb is described by an adverb (*she sang beautifully*).\n\n### Idioms and proverbs\nAn **idiom** is a fixed expression that is **not meant literally**. A **proverb** is a short, well-known saying that gives advice or a lesson.\n\n| Expression | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| a piece of cake | very easy |\n| break the ice | ease the first awkwardness between people |\n| let the cat out of the bag | reveal a secret by accident |\n| once in a blue moon | very rarely |\n| under the weather | slightly ill |\n| Don't count your chickens before they hatch. | Don't rely on something before it has happened. |\n| Every cloud has a silver lining. | There is something good in every bad situation. |\n| Look before you leap. | Think before you act. |\n\n> **Common mistake:** translating Afrikaans idioms literally: *Ek het 'n appeltjie met jou te skil* = **I have a bone to pick with you**, not \"an apple to peel\".\n\n### Figurative language\n\n| Figure of speech | What it is | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Simile** | compares using *like/as* | as brave as a lion |\n| **Metaphor** | says something **is** something else | The classroom was a zoo. |\n| **Personification** | gives human qualities to something non-human | The sun smiled on the Magaliesberg. |\n| **Hyperbole** | deliberate exaggeration | I've told you a million times! |\n| **Pun** | plays on two meanings or sounds | A bicycle can't stand on its own because it is two-tired. |\n| **Irony** | the opposite of what is meant or expected | A fire station burns down. |\n| **Sarcasm** | mocking irony meant to hurt | \"Great job!\" (when someone drops the cake) |\n| **Euphemism** | a mild word for something unpleasant | passed away (= died) |\n| **Alliteration** | repetition of initial consonant sounds | brave boys from Brits |\n| **Onomatopoeia** | the word imitates a sound | buzz, crash, hiss |\n| **Rhetorical question** | a question for effect; no answer is expected | Who wants to live in a dirty town? |\n\n> **Exam formula:** name the figure of speech → explain what is compared to what → give the effect.\n\n## Critical language awareness\n\nYou examine **how** language is used to influence you.\n\n- **Fact:** can be **proved or checked**: *Brits is in the North West.* **Opinion:** a personal judgement: *Brits is the best town in South Africa.* Clues: *I think, best, worst, should, amazing*. Always give a **reason**.\n- **Denotation:** the dictionary meaning. **Connotation:** the feelings a word suggests: *slim* (positive) – *thin* (neutral) – *skinny* (negative); *curious* versus *nosy*; *affordable* versus *cheap*.\n- **Emotive language** stirs strong feelings (*heartless, innocent, tragic*). **Manipulative language** persuades unfairly: exaggeration, half-truths, fear, flattery, *everyone is doing it*.\n- **Bias:** only one side is shown or favoured.\n- **Stereotyping:** everyone in a group is presented as the same: *Teenagers are lazy. Girls can't fix cars.*\n- **Sexist language** – use gender-neutral words: chairman → **chairperson**, policeman → **police officer**, fireman → **firefighter**, mankind → **humankind**; *Every learner must bring his book* → *All learners must bring their books*.\n- **Register** suits the **audience** and purpose: formal for a letter to the municipality, informal for a friend. **Slang** is very informal group language (*eish, chilled*); **jargon** is specialist vocabulary (*bandwidth, offside*) – fine for experts, confusing for others.\n\n> **Rewriting neutrally:** remove emotive words and generalisations (*all, always, typical*), replace sexist words and stick to facts: *Typical lazy teenagers are always on their phones* → *Some teenagers spend many hours on their phones.*"},"keyTerms":[{"term":{"af":"Sinoniem (synonym)","en":"Synonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met dieselfde of byna dieselfde betekenis as 'n ander woord, bv. *brave – courageous*.","en":"A word with the same or almost the same meaning as another word, e.g. *brave – courageous*."}},{"term":{"af":"Antoniem (antonym)","en":"Antonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met die teenoorgestelde betekenis, dikwels met 'n voorvoegsel gevorm, bv. *legal – illegal*.","en":"A word with the opposite meaning, often formed with a prefix, e.g. *legal – illegal*."}},{"term":{"af":"Homofoon (homophone)","en":"Homophone"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord wat dieselfde klink as 'n ander woord, maar anders gespel word en iets anders beteken, bv. *weather/whether*.","en":"A word that sounds the same as another word but is spelt differently and means something different, e.g. *weather/whether*."}},{"term":{"af":"Homoniem (homonym)","en":"Homonym"},"def":{"af":"'n Woord met dieselfde spelling en uitspraak as 'n ander woord, maar 'n ander betekenis, bv. *bank* (geldbank/rivieroewer).","en":"A word with the same spelling and pronunciation as another word but a different meaning, e.g. *bank* (money/river bank)."}},{"term":{"af":"Idioom (idiom)","en":"Idiom"},"def":{"af":"'n Vaste uitdrukking waarvan die betekenis nie letterlik is nie, bv. *once in a blue moon* = baie selde.","en":"A fixed expression whose meaning is not literal, e.g. *once in a blue moon* = very rarely."}},{"term":{"af":"Spreekwoord (proverb)","en":"Proverb"},"def":{"af":"'n Kort, bekende sin wat raad of 'n lewensles gee, bv. *Look before you leap.*","en":"A short, well-known saying that gives advice or a life lesson, e.g. *Look before you leap.*"}},{"term":{"af":"Konnotasie (connotation)","en":"Connotation"},"def":{"af":"Die gevoelens of assosiasies wat 'n woord oproep, bo en behalwe die woordeboekbetekenis (denotasie), bv. *slim* (positief) teenoor *skinny* (negatief).","en":"The feelings or associations a word suggests beyond its dictionary meaning (denotation), e.g. *slim* (positive) versus *skinny* (negative)."}},{"term":{"af":"Emotiewe taal (emotive language)","en":"Emotive language"},"def":{"af":"Woorde wat doelbewus gekies word om sterk gevoelens by die leser te wek, bv. *heartless, innocent*.","en":"Words deliberately chosen to stir strong feelings in the reader, e.g. *heartless, innocent*."}},{"term":{"af":"Partydigheid (bias)","en":"Bias"},"def":{"af":"Wanneer 'n teks net een kant van 'n saak wys of een groep onregverdig bevoordeel.","en":"When a text shows only one side of an issue or unfairly favours one group."}},{"term":{"af":"Stereotipering (stereotyping)","en":"Stereotyping"},"def":{"af":"Om almal in 'n groep as dieselfde voor te stel, bv. *Teenagers are lazy.*","en":"Presenting everyone in a group as the same, e.g. *Teenagers are lazy.*"}}],"examples":[{"title":{"af":"Woordvorming in konteks","en":"Word formation in context"},"problem":{"af":"Give the correct form of the word in brackets. Write only the word. (4)\n\n(a) Her (kind) ___ to the new learner made him feel welcome.\n\n(b) After an hour the judges still could not reach a (decide) ___.\n\n(c) Driving without a licence is (legal) ___. (Give the antonym.)\n\n(d) My uncle is a (success) ___ citrus farmer near Brits.","en":"Give the correct form of the word in brackets. Write only the word. (4)\n\n(a) Her (kind) ___ to the new learner made him feel welcome.\n\n(b) After an hour the judges still could not reach a (decide) ___.\n\n(c) Driving without a licence is (legal) ___. (Give the antonym.)\n\n(d) My uncle is a (success) ___ citrus farmer near Brits."},"steps":[{"af":"**(a)** Ná *Her* (besitlike voornaamwoord) volg 'n **selfstandige naamwoord**. kind + **-ness** = **kindness**.","en":"**(a)** After *Her* (possessive pronoun) comes a **noun**. kind + **-ness** = **kindness**."},{"af":"**(b)** Ná *a* en aan die einde van die sin (die voorwerp) staan 'n **s.nw.** decide → **decision** (die *d* word *s* + *-ion*).","en":"**(b)** After *a* and at the end of the sentence (the object) we need a **noun**. decide → **decision** (the *d* becomes *s* + *-ion*)."},{"af":"**(c)** *Legal* begin met **l**, dus gebruik ons **il-**: **illegal** – onthou die dubbel-*l*.","en":"**(c)** *Legal* starts with **l**, so we use **il-**: **illegal** – remember the double *l*."},{"af":"**(d)** Voor die s.nw. *farmer* kom 'n **byvoeglike naamwoord**. success + **-ful** = **successful** (dubbel *c*, dubbel *s*, net een *l* aan die einde).","en":"**(d)** Before the noun *farmer* comes an **adjective**. success + **-ful** = **successful** (double *c*, double *s*, only one *l* at the end)."}],"answer":{"af":"(a) kindness (b) decision (c) illegal (d) successful","en":"(a) kindness (b) decision (c) illegal (d) successful"}},{"title":{"af":"Idiome en spreekwoorde verduidelik","en":"Explaining idioms and proverbs"},"problem":{"af":"Read the conversation and answer the questions.\n\nLERATO: How was the Maths test?\n\nSIPHO: A piece of cake! But I'm feeling a bit under the weather today.\n\nLERATO: Shame. And I have bad news – I let the cat out of the bag about Thandi's surprise party.\n\nSIPHO: Well, every cloud has a silver lining. Now she can at least choose what to wear!\n\n(a) What does Sipho mean when he says the test was \"a piece of cake\"? (1)\n\n(b) Explain \"under the weather\". (1)\n\n(c) What did Lerato do when she \"let the cat out of the bag\"? (1)\n\n(d) Explain the proverb Sipho uses and why it fits the situation. (2)","en":"Read the conversation and answer the questions.\n\nLERATO: How was the Maths test?\n\nSIPHO: A piece of cake! But I'm feeling a bit under the weather today.\n\nLERATO: Shame. And I have bad news – I let the cat out of the bag about Thandi's surprise party.\n\nSIPHO: Well, every cloud has a silver lining. Now she can at least choose what to wear!\n\n(a) What does Sipho mean when he says the test was \"a piece of cake\"? (1)\n\n(b) Explain \"under the weather\". (1)\n\n(c) What did Lerato do when she \"let the cat out of the bag\"? (1)\n\n(d) Explain the proverb Sipho uses and why it fits the situation. (2)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a)** 'n Idioom word nie letterlik bedoel nie – daar was geen koek nie. *A piece of cake* = **baie maklik**.\n\n*Model answer:* The test was very easy. ✔","en":"**(a)** An idiom is not meant literally – there was no cake. *A piece of cake* = **very easy**.\n\n*Model answer:* The test was very easy. ✔"},{"af":"**(b)** *Under the weather* = **effens siek / nie lekker nie**.\n\n*Model answer:* He is feeling slightly ill. ✔","en":"**(b)** *Under the weather* = **slightly ill / unwell**.\n\n*Model answer:* He is feeling slightly ill. ✔"},{"af":"**(c)** *Let the cat out of the bag* = **'n geheim per ongeluk verklap**.\n\n*Model answer:* She accidentally told Thandi (or someone) about the secret surprise party. ✔","en":"**(c)** *Let the cat out of the bag* = **reveal a secret by accident**.\n\n*Model answer:* She accidentally told Thandi (or someone) about the secret surprise party. ✔"},{"af":"**(d)** Gee die **betekenis** van die spreekwoord + **hoekom dit pas**.\n\n*Model answer:* \"Every cloud has a silver lining\" means there is something good in every bad situation. ✔ The surprise is spoilt (bad), but now Thandi can choose what to wear (good). ✔","en":"**(d)** Give the **meaning** of the proverb + **why it fits**.\n\n*Model answer:* \"Every cloud has a silver lining\" means there is something good in every bad situation. ✔ The surprise is spoilt (bad), but now Thandi can choose what to wear (good). ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Baie maklik. (b) Effens siek. (c) Sy het die geheim per ongeluk verklap. (d) Iets goeds in elke slegte situasie – die verrassing is bederf, maar Thandi kan nou kies wat om aan te trek.","en":"(a) Very easy. (b) Slightly ill. (c) She revealed the secret by accident. (d) Something good in every bad situation – the surprise is spoilt, but Thandi can now choose what to wear."}},{"title":{"af":"Stylfigure herken en verduidelik","en":"Identifying and explaining figures of speech"},"problem":{"af":"Read the paragraph and answer the questions.\n\n*At five o'clock the Brits taxi rank is a beehive. Hooters honk, engines roar and the old taxis groan up the hill like tired old men. \"Why do we put up with this every single day?\" asks a woman with three heavy shopping bags. The driver just laughs: \"Ma'am, I've been waiting here for a hundred years!\"*\n\n(a) Identify the figure of speech in \"the Brits taxi rank is a beehive\" and explain it. (2)\n\n(b) Quote ONE example of onomatopoeia. (1)\n\n(c) Identify the figure of speech in \"the old taxis groan up the hill like tired old men\" and explain its effect. (2)\n\n(d) Name the figure of speech in the woman's words and explain why she uses it. (2)\n\n(e) Identify the figure of speech in the driver's words. (1)","en":"Read the paragraph and answer the questions.\n\n*At five o'clock the Brits taxi rank is a beehive. Hooters honk, engines roar and the old taxis groan up the hill like tired old men. \"Why do we put up with this every single day?\" asks a woman with three heavy shopping bags. The driver just laughs: \"Ma'am, I've been waiting here for a hundred years!\"*\n\n(a) Identify the figure of speech in \"the Brits taxi rank is a beehive\" and explain it. (2)\n\n(b) Quote ONE example of onomatopoeia. (1)\n\n(c) Identify the figure of speech in \"the old taxis groan up the hill like tired old men\" and explain its effect. (2)\n\n(d) Name the figure of speech in the woman's words and explain why she uses it. (2)\n\n(e) Identify the figure of speech in the driver's words. (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a)** Geen *like/as* nie – die taxistaanplek **is** 'n byekorf: 'n **metafoor**. Verduidelik die vergelyking.\n\n*Model answer:* Metaphor. ✔ The taxi rank is compared to a beehive: it is very busy and noisy, with people moving in all directions like bees. ✔","en":"**(a)** No *like/as* – the taxi rank **is** a beehive: a **metaphor**. Explain the comparison.\n\n*Model answer:* Metaphor. ✔ The taxi rank is compared to a beehive: it is very busy and noisy, with people moving in all directions like bees. ✔"},{"af":"**(b)** Soek 'n woord wat die klank naboots: **\"honk\"** (ook aanvaar: \"roar\"). ✔","en":"**(b)** Look for a word that imitates the sound: **\"honk\"** (also accept: \"roar\"). ✔"},{"af":"**(c)** Die woord **like** wys dit is 'n **simile** (vergelyking). (*Groan* gee die taxi's ook menslike eienskappe – personifikasie.)\n\n*Model answer:* Simile. ✔ The taxis are compared to tired old men: they move slowly and noisily up the hill, which shows how old and worn out they are. ✔","en":"**(c)** The word **like** shows that it is a **simile**. (*Groan* also gives the taxis human qualities – personification.)\n\n*Model answer:* Simile. ✔ The taxis are compared to tired old men: they move slowly and noisily up the hill, which shows how old and worn out they are. ✔"},{"af":"**(d)** Sy verwag nie 'n antwoord nie: 'n **retoriese vraag**.\n\n*Model answer:* Rhetorical question. ✔ She uses it to show her frustration with the daily chaos, not to get an answer. ✔","en":"**(d)** She does not expect an answer: a **rhetorical question**.\n\n*Model answer:* Rhetorical question. ✔ She uses it to show her frustration with the daily chaos, not to get an answer. ✔"},{"af":"**(e)** Niemand wag 100 jaar nie – dit is doelbewuste oordrywing: **hyperbole** (hiperbool). ✔","en":"**(e)** Nobody waits 100 years – it is deliberate exaggeration: **hyperbole**. ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Metafoor – besig en raserig soos 'n byekorf. (b) \"honk\" (c) Simile – stadig en uitgeput soos ou mans. (d) Retoriese vraag – wys haar frustrasie. (e) Hiperbool (hyperbole).","en":"(a) Metaphor – busy and noisy like a beehive. (b) \"honk\" (c) Simile – slow and worn out like old men. (d) Rhetorical question – shows her frustration. (e) Hyperbole."}},{"title":{"af":"Kritiese taalbewustheid in 'n advertensie","en":"Critical language awareness in an advertisement"},"problem":{"af":"Read the advertisement (described in words) and answer the questions.\n\n*A bright yellow poster shows a smiling mother holding a plate of fried chicken. The text reads:*\n\n**SUNNY HEN CHICKEN** (own example)\n\n*Every smart mom in Brits buys Sunny Hen! Our chickens are raised on farms in the North West. Sunny Hen is the tastiest chicken in South Africa. Only a fool would buy cheap, tasteless chicken anywhere else. Hurry – our special price ends on Friday!*\n\n(a) Quote ONE fact and ONE opinion from the advert. Give a reason for each. (4)\n\n(b) Explain how the first sentence stereotypes women. (2)\n\n(c) Explain why the fourth sentence is manipulative. Refer to TWO words. (2)\n\n(d) Rewrite the first sentence so that it is gender-neutral and not manipulative. (1)","en":"Read the advertisement (described in words) and answer the questions.\n\n*A bright yellow poster shows a smiling mother holding a plate of fried chicken. The text reads:*\n\n**SUNNY HEN CHICKEN** (own example)\n\n*Every smart mom in Brits buys Sunny Hen! Our chickens are raised on farms in the North West. Sunny Hen is the tastiest chicken in South Africa. Only a fool would buy cheap, tasteless chicken anywhere else. Hurry – our special price ends on Friday!*\n\n(a) Quote ONE fact and ONE opinion from the advert. Give a reason for each. (4)\n\n(b) Explain how the first sentence stereotypes women. (2)\n\n(c) Explain why the fourth sentence is manipulative. Refer to TWO words. (2)\n\n(d) Rewrite the first sentence so that it is gender-neutral and not manipulative. (1)"},"steps":[{"af":"**(a) Feit:** \"Our chickens are raised on farms in the North West.\" ✔ – dit kan nagegaan word. ✔ **Mening:** \"Sunny Hen is the tastiest chicken in South Africa.\" ✔ – *tastiest* is 'n persoonlike oordeel wat nie bewys kan word nie. ✔ (Ook 'n feit: *our special price ends on Friday*.)","en":"**(a) Fact:** \"Our chickens are raised on farms in the North West.\" ✔ – it can be checked. ✔ **Opinion:** \"Sunny Hen is the tastiest chicken in South Africa.\" ✔ – *tastiest* is a personal judgement that cannot be proved. ✔ (Also a fact: *our special price ends on Friday*.)"},{"af":"**(b) Stereotipering:** Die sin sê net *moms*, asof net vroue kos koop en kook – mans word uitgesluit. ✔ Dit impliseer ook dat ma's wat nie Sunny Hen koop nie, nie slim is nie. ✔","en":"**(b) Stereotyping:** The sentence only mentions *moms*, as if only women buy and cook food – men are left out. ✔ It also implies that mothers who don't buy Sunny Hen are not smart. ✔"},{"af":"**(c) Manipulasie:** Die woord **fool** beledig lesers wat elders koop, sodat hulle skaam voel. ✔ **Cheap** en **tasteless** het 'n **negatiewe konnotasie** en maak ander handelaars se hoender sleg sonder enige bewys. ✔","en":"**(c) Manipulation:** The word **fool** insults readers who shop elsewhere, so that they feel ashamed. ✔ **Cheap** and **tasteless** have a **negative connotation** and make other shops' chicken sound bad without any proof. ✔"},{"af":"**(d) Neutraal:** haal *smart* en *mom* uit en moenie oordryf nie.\n\n*Model answer:* Many shoppers in Brits buy Sunny Hen chicken. ✔","en":"**(d) Neutral:** remove *smart* and *mom* and don't exaggerate.\n\n*Model answer:* Many shoppers in Brits buy Sunny Hen chicken. ✔"}],"answer":{"af":"(a) Feit: die hoenders word in Noordwes geteel (kan nagegaan word); mening: *the tastiest chicken* (persoonlike oordeel). (b) Net ma's word genoem – asof net vroue kos koop. (c) *Fool* beledig; *cheap, tasteless* is negatiewe konnotasie sonder bewys. (d) Many shoppers in Brits buy Sunny Hen chicken.","en":"(a) Fact: the chickens are raised in the North West (can be checked); opinion: *the tastiest chicken* (personal judgement). (b) Only moms are mentioned – as if only women buy food. (c) *Fool* insults; *cheap, tasteless* is negative connotation without proof. (d) Many shoppers in Brits buy Sunny Hen chicken."}}],"quiz":[{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter woord is 'n **sinoniem** vir *enormous*?","en":"Which word is a **synonym** of *enormous*?"},"options":[{"af":"tiny","en":"tiny"},{"af":"huge","en":"huge"},{"af":"ancient","en":"ancient"},{"af":"noisy","en":"noisy"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"*Enormous* beteken baie groot, dus is **huge** die sinoniem. *Tiny* is die antoniem (teenoorgestelde).","en":"*Enormous* means very big, so **huge** is the synonym. *Tiny* is the antonym (opposite)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Vorm die antoniem van *responsible* deur 'n voorvoegsel by te voeg: ___","en":"Form the antonym of *responsible* by adding a prefix: ___"},"answers":{"af":["irresponsible"],"en":["irresponsible"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["unresponsible","inresponsible","disresponsible"],"en":["unresponsible","inresponsible","disresponsible"]}},"explain":{"af":"Voor 'n woord wat met **r** begin, gebruik ons **ir-**: **irresponsible** (met dubbel *r*). Net so: *irregular, irrelevant*.","en":"Before a word that starts with **r** we use **ir-**: **irresponsible** (with a double *r*). Likewise: *irregular, irrelevant*."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Weather* en *whether* is homofone (homophones).","en":"*Weather* and *whether* are homophones."},"answer":true,"explain":{"af":"Waar. Hulle **klink dieselfde**, maar word anders gespel en beteken iets anders: *weather* = weer, *whether* = of.","en":"True. They **sound the same**, but are spelt differently and mean different things: *weather* = conditions outside, *whether* = if."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Wat beteken die idioom *once in a blue moon*?","en":"What does the idiom *once in a blue moon* mean?"},"options":[{"af":"elke maand","en":"every month"},{"af":"net in die nag","en":"only at night"},{"af":"baie selde","en":"very rarely"},{"af":"wanneer iemand hartseer is","en":"when someone is sad"}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"'n Idioom word nie letterlik bedoel nie. 'n \"Blou maan\" gebeur amper nooit, dus beteken dit **baie selde**: *My cousin visits us once in a blue moon.*","en":"An idiom is not meant literally. A \"blue moon\" almost never happens, so it means **very rarely**: *My cousin visits us once in a blue moon.*"}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Voeg 'n agtervoegsel by *hope* om 'n byvoeglike naamwoord te vorm wat \"sonder hoop\" beteken: ___","en":"Add a suffix to *hope* to form an adjective that means \"without hope\": ___"},"answers":{"af":["hopeless"],"en":["hopeless"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["hopeful","unhopeful","hopefulness"],"en":["hopeful","unhopeful","hopefulness"]}},"explain":{"af":"**-less** beteken *sonder*: hope + less = **hopeless**. **-ful** beteken *vol van* (*hopeful* = vol hoop), en *hopefulness* is 'n s.nw.","en":"**-less** means *without*: hope + less = **hopeless**. **-ful** means *full of* (*hopeful*), and *hopefulness* is a noun."}},{"type":"match","q":{"af":"Pas elke stylfiguur by die regte voorbeeld.","en":"Match each figure of speech to the correct example."},"pairs":[{"l":{"af":"Simile (vergelyking)","en":"Simile"},"r":{"af":"Her voice was as sweet as honey.","en":"Her voice was as sweet as honey."}},{"l":{"af":"Metaphor (metafoor)","en":"Metaphor"},"r":{"af":"My brother is a couch potato.","en":"My brother is a couch potato."}},{"l":{"af":"Personification (personifikasie)","en":"Personification"},"r":{"af":"The sun smiled down on the citrus farms.","en":"The sun smiled down on the citrus farms."}},{"l":{"af":"Hyperbole (hiperbool)","en":"Hyperbole"},"r":{"af":"I've told you a million times!","en":"I've told you a million times!"}},{"l":{"af":"Pun (woordspeling)","en":"Pun"},"r":{"af":"The baker stopped making doughnuts because he was tired of the hole business.","en":"The baker stopped making doughnuts because he was tired of the hole business."}}],"explain":{"af":"Simile gebruik *as/like*; 'n metafoor sê iets **is** iets anders; personifikasie gee 'n nie-menslike ding menslike eienskappe (die son *glimlag*); hiperbool is oordrywing; 'n woordspeling speel met *hole/whole*.","en":"A simile uses *as/like*; a metaphor says something **is** something else; personification gives a non-human thing human qualities (the sun *smiles*); hyperbole is exaggeration; a pun plays on *hole/whole*."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin bevat 'n **eufemisme** (euphemism)?","en":"Which sentence contains a **euphemism**?"},"options":[{"af":"Grandpa snored like a train last night.","en":"Grandpa snored like a train last night."},{"af":"Grandpa told the same joke a thousand times.","en":"Grandpa told the same joke a thousand times."},{"af":"Grandpa died in hospital last night.","en":"Grandpa died in hospital last night."},{"af":"Grandpa passed away last night.","en":"Grandpa passed away last night."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"'n Eufemisme is 'n **sagter** woord vir iets onaangenaams: *passed away* in plaas van *died*. *Snored like a train* is 'n simile en *a thousand times* is hiperbool; *died* is die direkte woord.","en":"A euphemism is a **milder** word for something unpleasant: *passed away* instead of *died*. *Snored like a train* is a simile and *a thousand times* is hyperbole; *died* is the direct word."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Gee die regte vorm van die woord tussen hakies: The (decide) ___ to cancel the rugby match was unpopular.","en":"Give the correct form of the word in brackets: The (decide) ___ to cancel the rugby match was unpopular."},"answers":{"af":["decision"],"en":["decision"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["decisive","decided","decisively"],"en":["decisive","decided","decisively"]}},"explain":{"af":"Ná *The* en as onderwerp van die sin is 'n **s.nw.** nodig: decide → **decision**. *Decisive* is 'n b.nw. en *decisively* 'n bywoord.","en":"After *The* and as the subject of the sentence we need a **noun**: decide → **decision**. *Decisive* is an adjective and *decisively* an adverb."}},{"type":"tf","q":{"af":"*Brits is the best town in the North West* is 'n feit, want Brits lê regtig in Noordwes.","en":"*Brits is the best town in the North West* is a fact, because Brits really is in the North West."},"answer":false,"explain":{"af":"Onwaar. Dit is 'n **mening**: *best* is 'n persoonlike oordeel waarmee ander kan verskil en wat nie bewys kan word nie. Net *Brits is in the North West* is 'n feit.","en":"False. It is an **opinion**: *best* is a personal judgement that others may disagree with and that cannot be proved. Only *Brits is in the North West* is a fact."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Al vier woorde beteken *nie vet nie*. Watter een het die mees **negatiewe konnotasie**?","en":"All four words mean *not fat*. Which one has the most **negative connotation**?"},"options":[{"af":"skinny","en":"skinny"},{"af":"slim","en":"slim"},{"af":"slender","en":"slender"},{"af":"thin","en":"thin"}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"Die **denotasie** is dieselfde, maar die gevoel verskil: *slim* en *slender* is positief (aantreklik), *thin* is neutraal en **skinny** klink negatief (te maer).","en":"The **denotation** is the same, but the feeling differs: *slim* and *slender* are positive (attractive), *thin* is neutral and **skinny** sounds negative (too thin)."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Maak die sin geslagsneutraal: *The firemen put out the veld fire near Hartbeespoort.* → *The ___ put out the veld fire near Hartbeespoort.*","en":"Make the sentence gender-neutral: *The firemen put out the veld fire near Hartbeespoort.* → *The ___ put out the veld fire near Hartbeespoort.*"},"answers":{"af":["firefighters","fire-fighters","firefighter"],"en":["firefighters","fire-fighters","firefighter"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["firemen","firewomen","firemans"],"en":["firemen","firewomen","firemans"]}},"explain":{"af":"*Firemen* sluit vroue uit – dit is **seksistiese taal**. Die geslagsneutrale woord is **firefighters**. *Firewomen* sluit weer mans uit.","en":"*Firemen* leaves women out – it is **sexist language**. The gender-neutral word is **firefighters**. *Firewomen* leaves men out instead."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Thabo het vir almal vertel hy het die kompetisie gewen en reeds beplan hoe om die prysgeld te spandeer – voordat die beoordelaars die wenner aangekondig het. Watter spreekwoord pas die beste?","en":"Thabo told everyone he had won the competition and was already planning how to spend the prize money – before the judges had announced the winner. Which proverb fits best?"},"options":[{"af":"Every cloud has a silver lining.","en":"Every cloud has a silver lining."},{"af":"Look before you leap.","en":"Look before you leap."},{"af":"Practice makes perfect.","en":"Practice makes perfect."},{"af":"Don't count your chickens before they hatch.","en":"Don't count your chickens before they hatch."}],"answer":3,"explain":{"af":"Thabo **reken op iets wat nog nie gebeur het nie** – presies wat *Don't count your chickens before they hatch* waarsku. *Look before you leap* gaan oor dink voordat jy iets riskants doen, en *Every cloud has a silver lining* oor iets goeds in 'n slegte situasie.","en":"Thabo is **relying on something that has not happened yet** – exactly what *Don't count your chickens before they hatch* warns against. *Look before you leap* is about thinking before doing something risky, and *Every cloud has a silver lining* is about something good in a bad situation."}},{"type":"fill","q":{"af":"Lees: *\"Oh, brilliant! You forgot the meat for the braai again.\"* Hierdie spottende opmerking, wat die teenoorgestelde bedoel van wat dit sê, is 'n voorbeeld van ___.","en":"Read: *\"Oh, brilliant! You forgot the meat for the braai again.\"* This mocking remark, which means the opposite of what it says, is an example of ___."},"answers":{"af":["sarcasm","sarkasme","sarcastic","verbal irony","irony","ironie"],"en":["sarcasm","sarcastic","verbal irony","irony"]},"choices":{"d":{"af":["euphemism","hyperbole","personification"],"en":["euphemism","hyperbole","personification"]}},"explain":{"af":"Die spreker sê *brilliant* maar bedoel *terrible*, en die doel is om te spot: dit is **sarcasm** (sarkasme), 'n skerp vorm van verbale ironie.","en":"The speaker says *brilliant* but means *terrible*, and the aim is to mock: this is **sarcasm**, a sharp form of verbal irony."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Lees die sin uit 'n brief aan 'n koerant: *\"Ruthless criminals are destroying our innocent town, and the useless council does nothing!\"* Watter woorde maak die sin emotief en partydig?","en":"Read the sentence from a letter to a newspaper: *\"Ruthless criminals are destroying our innocent town, and the useless council does nothing!\"* Which words make the sentence emotive and biased?"},"options":[{"af":"*criminals* en *town*","en":"*criminals* and *town*"},{"af":"*ruthless, destroying, innocent* en *useless*","en":"*ruthless, destroying, innocent* and *useless*"},{"af":"*our* en *does*","en":"*our* and *does*"},{"af":"*council* en *nothing*","en":"*council* and *nothing*"}],"answer":1,"explain":{"af":"**Ruthless, destroying, innocent** en **useless** is sterk, gelaaide woorde wat woede en jammerte wek en net een kant wys. *Criminals, town* en *council* is neutrale selfstandige naamwoorde.","en":"**Ruthless, destroying, innocent** and **useless** are strong, loaded words that stir anger and pity and show only one side. *Criminals, town* and *council* are neutral nouns."}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"Watter sin is die mees **neutrale** (onpartydige) weergawe van *\"Typical teenagers are lazy and always glued to their phones\"*?","en":"Which sentence is the most **neutral** (unbiased) version of *\"Typical teenagers are lazy and always glued to their phones\"*?"},"options":[{"af":"Some teenagers spend many hours a day on their phones.","en":"Some teenagers spend many hours a day on their phones."},{"af":"All teenagers are lazy phone addicts.","en":"All teenagers are lazy phone addicts."},{"af":"As usual, teenagers are wasting their lives on their phones.","en":"As usual, teenagers are wasting their lives on their phones."},{"af":"Lazy teenagers should have their phones taken away.","en":"Lazy teenagers should have their phones taken away."}],"answer":0,"explain":{"af":"'n Neutrale sin vermy **veralgemenings** (*all, typical, always*) en **emotiewe woorde** (*lazy, addicts, wasting*) en hou by iets wat waar en meetbaar is: **Some teenagers spend many hours a day on their phones.**","en":"A neutral sentence avoids **generalisations** (*all, typical, always*) and **emotive words** (*lazy, addicts, wasting*) and sticks to something true and measurable: **Some teenagers spend many hours a day on their phones.**"}},{"type":"mc","q":{"af":"'n Advertensie sê: *\"Every smart mom in Brits buys Sunny Hen chicken.\"* Wat is die **beste** kritiek op hierdie slagspreuk?","en":"An advert says: *\"Every smart mom in Brits buys Sunny Hen chicken.\"* What is the **best** criticism of this slogan?"},"options":[{"af":"Dit gebruik 'n woordspeling wat lesers sal verwar.","en":"It uses a pun that will confuse readers."},{"af":"Dit is 'n feit wat maklik nagegaan kan word.","en":"It is a fact that can easily be checked."},{"af":"Dit stereotipeer vroue as die enigstes wat kos koop, en manipuleer lesers deur te impliseer dat ma's wat dit nie koop nie, nie slim is nie.","en":"It stereotypes women as the only people who buy food, and manipulates readers by implying that moms who don't buy it are not smart."},{"af":"Dit gebruik jargon wat gewone lesers nie sal verstaan nie.","en":"It uses jargon that ordinary readers will not understand."}],"answer":2,"explain":{"af":"Die slagspreuk noem net *moms* (**stereotipering**/seksisme) en die woord *smart* **manipuleer**: as jy dit nie koop nie, is jy glo nie slim nie. Daar is geen woordspeling of jargon nie, en *every smart mom* is 'n mening, nie 'n feit nie.","en":"The slogan mentions only *moms* (**stereotyping**/sexism) and the word *smart* **manipulates**: if you don't buy it, you are supposedly not smart. There is no pun or jargon, and *every smart mom* is an opinion, not a fact."}}]}]}]}}};